
#bookname=borooah (en-sa)
#stripmethod=keep
#sametypesequence=h
#description=Data from https://www.sanskrit-lexicon.uni-koeln.de/ as on 2026-05-31

a
A or (before vowels) AN:<BR>I This article<BR>has no equiv. in Sanskrit and is expressed<BR>by the singular number alone:<BR>there is a<BR>large silk-cotton tree on the banks of the Godavari<BR>अस्ति गोदावरीतीरे विशालः शाल्मलीतरुः H. i.;<BR>there<BR>was a king named Cintamani<BR>अभूद्राजा चिन्तामणि-<BR>र्नाम Va.<BR>II But कश्चित् (काचित्, किञ्चित्)<BR>should be added when special attention<BR>is directed to the object: a (certain)<BR>Yaksha<BR>कश्चिद् यक्षः, Me. I 1.; A (certain)<BR>saint named Marichi<BR>कश्चिन्मरीचिर्नाभ भहर्षिः, D.<BR>iii.<BR>III When it means a species of, विशेषः,<BR> भेदः, etc. should be added: Asoka is a tree<BR>अशोको वृक्षविशेषः।<BR>IV When used distribu-<BR>-tively, (a) expr. by avy. comp. with प्रति,<BR>or, by the repetition of the word in proper<BR>agreement with the verb: give (me)<BR>500<BR>sovereign a day<BR>प्रत्यहं सुवर्णपञ्चशतानि देहि, H.<BR>iii; (b) the simple gen. may be used in<BR>connection with num. adverbs:<BR>dinner<BR>twice a day<BR>द्विरह्नो भोजनम्, V. In O. E. some-<BR>-times=on, in, for: q. v.:<BR>the world runs<BR>awheel<BR>*चक्रैर्जगद्धावति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abaft
ABAFT: पश्चाद्भागे (with gen.): abaft the mast<BR>*गुणवृक्षस्य पश्चाद्भागे।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abandon
ABANDON:<BR>(1) त्यजति, परि-, सं-, (त्यज्, c. l.);<BR>(2) जहाति, वि-, अप-, (हा, c. 3.);<BR>(3) उज्भ्कति,<BR> सम्-, प्र-, (उज्भ्क्, c. 6.);<BR>(4) उत्-सृजति, वि-,<BR>(सृज्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abandoned
ABANDONED:<BR>I Lit. त्यक्तः (क्ता, क्तं): v. To<BR>abandon.<BR>II Fig.: extremely wicked: q.<BR>v.<BR>(1) भ्रष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>(2) खण्डितवृत्तः (त्ता, त्तं)<BR>(=of a character).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abandonment
ABANDONMENT:<BR>(1) त्यागः;<BR>(2) परित्यागः;<BR>(3) उत्सर्गः; Ph: a. of wordly connexions:<BR>सन्न्यासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abase
ABASE:<BR>(1) अभि-भवति (भू, c. 1.);<BR>(2) नमयति<BR>(c. of नम्): v. To humble, to lower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abasement
