abettor
ABETTOR:<BR>(1) प्रोत्साहकः;<BR>(2) प्रवर्तकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abhor
ABHOR: जुगुप्प्तते: v. To hate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abhorrence
ABHORRENCE:<BR>(1) जुगुप्सा;<BR>(2) परमद्वेषः;<BR>N. B. Const. with loc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abhorrent
ABHORRENT: v. Repugnant, discordant,<BR>inconsistent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abide
ABIDE (v. i.):<BR>I To dwell: q. v.: वसति (वस्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II To stay: q. v.: अव-तिष्ठते (स्था,<BR>c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abide
ABIDE (v. t.):<BR>(1) To wait for: q. v.: प्रति-<BR>ईक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.).<BR>II To endure; q. v. सहते<BR>(सह् c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abide by
