aborigines
ABORIGINES: आदिमवासिनः (m. pl.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abortion
ABORTION:<BR>(1) गर्भस्रावः;<BR>(2) गर्भपातः;<BR>(3)<BR>गर्भपतनम्;<BR>(4) गर्भच्युतिः। To cause a.:<BR>(1) गर्भं<BR> पातयति (c. of पत्);<BR>(2) भ्रूणहत्यां करोति (कृ, c. 8.)<BR>One who causes a.:<BR>(1) भ्रूणहन् (f. घ्नी);<BR>(2)<BR>भ्रूणहत्याकारिन् (f. णी): Causing a.:<BR>(1) गर्भ-<BR>पातनम्;<BR>(2) भ्रूणहत्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abortive
ABORTIVE:<BR>I Producing abortion:<BR>(1) गर्भ-<BR>पातिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) गर्भस्राविन् (f. णी);<BR>(3)<BR>भ्रूणघ्न (f. घ्नी).<BR>II Born prematurely:<BR>(1)<BR>अकालप्रसूतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) अकालजातः (ता, तं).<BR>III<BR>Fruitless, unsuccessful: q. v.: निष्फल;<BR>(ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abortively
ABORTIVELY:<BR>(1) मुधा;<BR>(2) वृथा: v. In vain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abound
ABOUND (v. i.): No equiv: expr. by the<BR>corresp. adj s.:<BR>among those trees a. ing in<BR>good fruits<BR>भूयिष्ठसम्भाव्यफलेष्वमीषु पादपेषु, R. xiii.<BR>46; the country of Kimpurusha a. s in curiosities<BR>बहुकुतूहलः किम्पुरुषविषयः, K. : v. Abundant,<BR>full of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

about
ABOUT (Prep.):<BR>I Around: q. v.: परितः<BR>(with acc.). Sometimes sim. by the loc.:<BR>a.<BR>one's neck<BR>कण्ठे<BR>or<BR>कण्ठदेशे (not कण्ठं परितः).<BR>Ph.:<BR>a. these places<BR>इतस्ततः।<BR>II In atten-<BR>-dance on: सह (with ins.): v. With.<BR>III<BR>Respecting, concerning: प्रति (with acc.)<BR>(rare in this sense):<BR>you have spoken one<BR>thing good a. Śiva<BR>त्वयैकमीशं प्रति साधु भाषितम्,<BR>Ku. v. 81. N. B. Note the following exx.:<BR>is there any mistake a. it<BR>किमत्र काचिद्भ्रान्तिः,<BR>Vi. iii.;<BR>whether mere knowledge a. God<BR>leads to emancipation<BR>किमीश्वरविषयं ञ्जानमात्रं<BR> निर्वाणकारणम्, Ds.;<BR>conversing now a. his father,<BR>now a. his mother, now a. Sukanasa<BR>अन्तरा पितृ-<BR>सक्तमन्तरा मातृसम्बद्धध्मन्तरा शुकनासमयं कुर्वन्नालापम;<BR>K. ;<BR>I also want to ask something a. your<BR>friend<BR>वयमपि भवत्योः सखीगतं किमपि पृच्छामः,<BR>Sa. i.;<BR>we had some conversation a. the news<BR>of the country<BR>सङ्कया च देशवार्तानुविद्धा काचनावयोरभूत्;<BR>D. v.;<BR>a. the Lord of the Heavens<BR>दिवोधिनाथम-<BR>धिकृत्य;<BR>a. the friend of the god of Wind<BR>पवनस्य<BR> सखायं निर्दिश्य; a. the Lord of the (south)<BR>quarter<BR>दिक्पतिमुद्दिश्य;<BR>a. many Nalas<BR>अनेक-<BR>नलावलम्बां; N. xiii. 2. 9. 15. 26.<BR>IV Near (in<BR>time): v. About (adv.) (III) Ph.<BR>remain-<BR>ed for a. a moment<BR>मुहूर्तमिवासाञ्चक्रे, K. ;<BR>a.<BR>the same time<BR>तस्मिन्नेव क्षणान्तरे, D. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

about
ABOUT (adv.):<BR>I Around: q. v.: परितः।<BR>II<BR>Here and there<BR>इतस्ततः। To go, walk, wander<BR>a. परिक्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.).<BR>III Nearly.<BR>(1)<BR>by an altern. com.: we will reach (Patna) in<BR>a. a week (lit. in five or six days) पञ्चषैरहोभि-<BR>र्वयमेव तत्र गन्तारः, Mu. v.;<BR>(2) by bah. comp.<BR>with उप, आसन्न, अदूर<BR>etc: a. ten<BR>उपदशा: (m. pl.);<BR>a. four<BR>उपचतुराः;<BR>a. twenty<BR>आसन्नविंशाः; a. thirty<BR>अदूरत्रिंशाः;<BR>(3) by प्रायः (या, यं)<BR>or<BR>कल्पः (ल्पा,<BR> ल्पं) affixed:<BR>a. as high as the knee<BR>जानुदध्नकल्पः<BR>(ल्पा, ल्पं);<BR>(4) of age, by देशीयः (या, यं),<BR>affixed:<BR>a. 18 years of age<BR>अष्टादशवर्षदेशीयः<BR>(या, यं), D. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

about
ABOUT, BE: उद्यतः (ता, तं): v. Point of, on the;<BR>ready. Ph.:<BR>What is the king a. now<BR>अथ स<BR> राजा किमारम्भः सम्प्रति, U. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

above
ABOVE (adv.):<BR>I Overhead:<BR>(1) उपरि;<BR>(2)<BR>ऊर्द्ध्वम्;<BR>(3) उपरिष्टात्। From a.:<BR>(1) उपरिष्टात्;<BR>(2) ऊर्द्ध्वतः, Ku. xiv. 37.<BR>II Before:<BR>(1)<BR>पूर्वम्;<BR>(2) प्राक्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

above
ABOVE (adj.): पूर्वः (र्वा, र्वं),<BR>in the a. apho-<BR>rism<BR>पूर्वेण सूत्रेण, S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

above
ABOVE (Prep.):<BR>I In a higher place: उपरि<BR>(with gen.)<BR>Just a.:<BR>उपर्युपरि (with acc.),<BR>Just a. the village<BR>उपर्युपरि ग्रामम्।<BR>II In<BR>greater number:<BR>(1) by tat. comp. with अधिकः<BR>(का, कं):<BR>in a. half a moment<BR>अर्द्धाधिकमुहूर्तेन,<BR>Ram. ;<BR>(2) by bah. comp. with अधिक,<BR>a.<BR>forty<BR>अधिकचत्वारिंशः (m. pl.);<BR>(3)<BR>by comp.<BR>with<BR>परः, a. hundred (=hundreds) परःशतः<BR>(ता, तं); Ki. xiii. 26.<BR>III Beyond; v.<BR>Beyond (prep.) (III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

above
ABOVE, BE:<BR>(1) अतिवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.) Vi. iv.;<BR>(2) अधि<BR>or<BR>अति (with acc.) (rare):<BR>Kṛṣṇa<BR>is a. the gods<BR>अति देवान् कृष्णः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abrade
ABRADE: v. To rub, scrape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abreast
ABREAST: पार्श्वापार्शिव (indec.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abridge
ABRIDGE:<BR>(1) सङ् क्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.);<BR>(2)<BR>समा-हरति (हृ, c. 1.);<BR>(3) सम्-अस्यति (अस्, c. 4.);<BR>v. To lessen, shorten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abridgement
ABRIDGEMENT:<BR>(1) संक्षेपः;<BR>(2) प्रत्याहारः;<BR>(3)<BR>समाहारः;<BR>(4) समासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abroad
ABROAD (adv.):<BR>I In a foreign country:<BR>(1) विदेशे;<BR>(2) देशान्तरे।<BR>II To a foreign<BR>country:<BR>(1) विदेशं;<BR>(2) देशान्तरम्।<BR>III Not<BR>at home बहिस्।<BR>IV Widely: q. v.:<BR>spread-<BR>ing his rays far a.<BR>दूरप्रसारितकरः, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abroad
ABROAD, LIVE:<BR>(1) प्रवसति (वस्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) विदेशे वसति etc.<BR>One who is, or, is living<BR>a.<BR>प्रोषितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abrogate
ABROGATE, ABROGATION: v. To repeal, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abrupt
ABRUPT (adj.):<BR>I Steep, rugged: q. v.:<BR>विषमः (मा, मं).<BR>II Hasty, sudden: q. v.:<BR>(1) आकस्मिकः (की, कं);<BR>(2) अकाण्डः (ण्डा, ण्डं).<BR>III Of style: no equiv.: *भग्नः (भग्ना,<BR> भग्नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abruptly
ABRUPTLY: सहसा: v. Suddenly, hastily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abruptness
ABRUPTNESS:<BR>I Steepness: q. v. Haste,<BR>Suddenness: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abscess
ABSCESS: perh. विद्रधिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abscond
ABSCOND:<BR>(1) आत्मानं निगूहति (गुह्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To hide;<BR>(2) पलायते: v. To escape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absence
ABSENCE:<BR>I A not being present:<BR>(1)<BR>अनुपस्थितिः;<BR>(2) By the corresp. adj s v.<BR>ABSENT: Ph.<BR>how shall I live in his a.<BR>अहमेतस्य<BR> विरहे कथं जीविष्यामि, Vet.<BR>II A being abroad:<BR>(1) प्रवासः;<BR>(2) प्रवसनम्।<BR>III Non-existence:<BR>अभावः: first of all, the property goes to the<BR>brothers, in their a. to the mother, in mother's<BR>a. to the father, and in their a to the husband<BR>प्रथमं सोदराणां, तदभावे मातुः, मातुरभावे पितुः, एषां पुनरभावे<BR> तद्धनं भर्तुः, Da.<BR>IV Fig.: pl. a. of mind:<BR>(1) अन्यमनस्कता;<BR>(2) अमनोयोगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absent
ABSENT: (adj.)<BR>I Not present:<BR>(1) अनुपस्थितः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(2) अविद्यमानः (ना, नं);<BR>(3) अवर्तमानः<BR>(ना, नं).<BR>II Heedless: q. v.: अन्यमनस्कः<BR>(स्का, स्कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absent
ABSENT, BE: i. e. To be abroad: प्र-वसति (वस्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absent-minded
ABSENT-MINDED: शून्यहृदयः (या, यं), Sa.<BR>IV<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absentee
ABSENTEE:<BR>I One temporarily absent:<BR>अनुपस्थितः (ता, तं): v. Absent.<BR>II One being<BR>abroad:<BR>(1) प्रोषितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) प्रवासिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absolute
ABSOLUTE (adj.):<BR>I Perfect: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>नित्यः (त्या, त्यं) (=eternal, sometimes used<BR>with the same force):<BR>it is admitted by all<BR>assertors of final emancipation that it is a.<BR>नित्यश्च मोक्षः सर्वैर्मीक्षवादिभिरुपगम्यते, S. I. 4.;<BR>(2)<BR>परमः (मा, मं) (=excellent, q. v.).<BR>II<BR>Unconditional, uncontrolled: q. v.: Ph.:<BR>for fate has a. power<BR>सर्वथा प्रमवति हि मगवान्<BR> विधिः, K. iii. Not relative: केवलः (ला, लं)<BR>(?)<BR>the recent philosophy of a. the<BR>*आधुनिक-<BR>कैवल्यदर्शनम्<BR>or<BR>-विञ्जानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absolutely
ABSOLUTELY: i. e. Entirely:<BR>(1) सर्वथा;<BR>(2)<BR>एकान्ततस्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absolution
ABSOLUTION:<BR>I Acquittal: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Religious a.:<BR>(1) निस्तारः;<BR>(2) निष्कृतिः;<BR>(3) उद्धारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absolve
ABSOLVE:<BR>I To acquit, exonerate: q. v.:<BR>मोचयति (c. of मुच्).<BR>II In religious sense:<BR>(1) निष्-तारयति (c. of तॄ,);<BR>(2) उद्-धरति<BR>(धृ, c. i.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absorb
ABSORB (v. t.):<BR>I To imbibe, suck up:<BR>(1) चूषति (चूष्, c. i.);<BR>(2) शोषयति (c. of<BR>शुष्) (=dry up).<BR>II Fig.: To engross:<BR>(1) मज्जति, नि-, (मस्ज्, c. 6.),<BR>old men are a.<BR>ed. in thoughts and none clings to the supreme<BR>spirit<BR>वृद्धस्तावच्चिन्तामग्नः परमे ब्रह्मणि कोऽपि न लग्नः;<BR>(2) विशति, अभिनिविशते (विश्, c. 6.) (with acc.)<BR>[not so forcible as (1)]<BR>became a. ed in<BR>thought<BR>चिन्तां विवेश, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absorption
ABSORPTION:<BR>(1) चोषणम्;<BR>(2) चूषा;<BR>(3)<BR>निपानम्;<BR>(4) शोषणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstain
ABSTAIN (v. i.):<BR>(1) वि-रमति (रम्, c. 1.),<BR>a.<BR>from this dirty work<BR>विरम कर्मणोऽस्मान्मलीमसात्,<BR>D. iv.;<BR>(2) नि-वर्तयति (c. of वृत्) (with acc.),<BR>a. yourself from this unlucky affair<BR>निवर्त-<BR>यास्मादसदीप्सितान्मनः, Ku. v. 73.;<BR>(3) नि-वर्तते<BR>(वृत्, c. i.): निवृत्तमांसस्तु तत्रभवान् जनकः, U. IV.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstain
ABSTAIN from food: उप-वसति (वस्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstemious
ABSTEMIOUS:<BR>(1) मिताहारः (रा, रं);<BR>(2)<BR>मिताशनः (ना, नं);<BR>(3) मितभुज् (mfn);<BR>(4) लध्वाहारः (रा, रं);<BR>(5) लध्वाशिन् (f. नी);<BR>(6) यताहारः (रा,).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstemiously
ABSTEMIOUSLY:<BR>(1) मिताहारेण;<BR>(2) मिताशनेन;<BR>(3) लध्वाहारेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstemiousness
ABSTEMIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) मिताहारः;<BR>(2) मित-<BR>भोजनम;<BR>(3) मिताशनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstinence
ABSTINENCE:<BR>I In gen. sense, refraining<BR>from:<BR>(1) निवृत्तिः;<BR>(2) विरतिः;<BR>(3) क्षान्तिः।<BR>II From food:<BR>(1) उपवासः;<BR>(2) अनशनम्;<BR>v. Fasting.<BR>III From the gratification<BR>of animal propensities:<BR>(1) संयमनम;<BR>(2) यमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstinent
ABSTINENT:<BR>I From food:<BR>(1) यताहारः (रा, रं):<BR>v. Abstemious.<BR>II In a winder sense:<BR>संयमिन् (f. नी): v. Continent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstract
ABSTRACT (v. t.):<BR>I To separate: q. v.:<BR>वि-योजयति (c. of युज्).<BR>II To filch away,<BR>steal: q. v.: अप-हरति (हृ, c. 1.).<BR>III To<BR>abridge: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstract
ABSTRACT (subs): v. Abridgment, epitome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstract
ABSTRACT (adj.):<BR>I Separate: q. v.<BR>II As<BR>opposed to concrete: perh. सूक्षमः (क्ष्मा, क्ष्मं):<BR>v. Abstruse, refined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstraction
ABSTRACTION: Phil. t. t. *प्रणिधानम्; पदार्थानाम-<BR>परधर्माननादृत्यैकधर्मं प्रति प्रणिधानम्। In gen. sense,<BR>v. Stealing, separation, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstruse
