abundance
ABUNDANCE:<BR>(1) प्राचुर्यम्;<BR>(2) भूयस्त्वम्;<BR>(3)<BR>बाहुल्यम्;<BR>(4) प्रभूतत्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abundant
ABUNDANT:<BR>(1) प्रचुरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) प्रभूतः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(3) बहुलः (ला, लं);<BR>(4) भूयिष्ठः (ष्ठा,<BR> ष्ठं);<BR>(5) प्राज्यः (ज्या, ज्यं);<BR>(6) भूरि (mfn);<BR>(7) अदभ्रः (भ्रा, भ्रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abuse
ABUSE (v. t.):<BR>I To revile: q. v.: आ-<BR>क्षिपति, अधि-, (क्षिप्, c. 6.);<BR>(2) आ-क्रोशति (क्रूश्,<BR>c. 1.);<BR>(3) अप भाषते (भाष्, c. 1).<BR>II To make<BR>ill use of: Ph.<BR>a king who a. his rights goes<BR>to hell<BR>राजान्यायमाचरन्नरकं गच्छति;<BR>he a. s his<BR>time<BR>स कालं वृथा नयति, क्षिपति, हरति, etc.<BR>III<BR>To violate: q. v. प्रकुरुते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abuse
ABUSE (subs):<BR>I Ill-use:<BR>(1) कुव्यवहारः;<BR>(2) दुर्व्यवहारः;<BR>(3) कुप्रयोगः (of word);<BR>(4)<BR>वृथाहरणं (of time):<BR>II Contumely:<BR>(1)<BR>अधिक्षेपः;<BR>(2) तिरस्कारः;<BR>(3) आक्रोशः;<BR>(4)<BR>आक्षारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abusive
