acceptableness
ACCEPTABLENESS: v. Agreeableness, plea-<BR>-santness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acceptably
ACCEPTABLY: रुचिरम्: v. Agreeably, satis-<BR>-factorily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acceptance
ACCEPTANCE:<BR>(1) परिग्रहः;<BR>(2) प्रतिग्रहः;<BR>(3)<BR>स्वीकरणम्;<BR>(4) प्रतिपत्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acceptation
ACCEPTATION: अर्थः: v. Meaning. Ph.<BR>accor-<BR>ding to usual a. the word ‘inheritance’ conveys<BR>property over which ownership is created on the<BR>demise of the former owner<BR>पूर्वस्वाम्युपरमे यत्र द्रव्ये<BR> स्वत्वं तत्र निरूढो दायशब्दः: Da.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accepter
ACCEPTER:<BR>(1) ग्राहकः;<BR>(2) परिग्राहकः;<BR>(3) परिग्रहीता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

access
ACCESS:<BR>I Admission, interview: q. v. Ph.<BR>the asceties want to gain a. to the king<BR>तपस्विनो<BR> देवं द्रष्टुमिच्छन्ति, Sa. v.<BR>II The means of a.<BR>(1) आगमद्वारम्;<BR>(2) उपसर्पणमार्गः, etc.<BR>III<BR>Sexual intercourse: q. v. अभिगमनम्।<BR>IV<BR>Addition: v. Accession: v. A fit of<BR>disease: आगमः: v. Accession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accessible
ACCESSIBLE:<BR>I Of places:<BR>(1) गम्यः (म्या,<BR> म्यं);<BR>(2) सुगमः (मा, मं).<BR>II Of persons:<BR>(1) उपसर्पणीयः (या, यं).<BR>Surely kings are a. only<BR>at convenient times<BR>नन्ववसरोपसर्पणीया राजानः, Sa.<BR>vi.;<BR>(2) सुलभदर्शनः (ना, नं) (easily seen). Ph.:<BR>not a. to bribe or sexual gratification<BR>न धन-<BR>स्त्रीदानादिना भेद्यः: K. b.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accession
ACCESSION:<BR>I The act of joining:<BR>(1) योगः;<BR>(2) सङ्गमः।<BR>II A coming to power. Ph.<BR>on<BR>his a. to the throne<BR>राज्यमवाप्य etc.<BR>or<BR>सिंहासन-<BR>मारुह्य।<BR>III Increase: q. v. वृद्धिः, Ph.:<BR>a.<BR>of wealth<BR>धनागमः।<BR>IV Of disease:<BR>(1) आगमः;<BR>(2) आविर्भावः;<BR>(3) अवतारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accessory
