accidence
ACCIDENCE: उपक्रमणिका (?): v. Rudiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accident
ACCIDENT:<BR>I Chance, casualty: q. v. ph.<BR>seen by a.<BR>समापत्तिदृष्टाः, D. v.: v. Accidentally.<BR>II An unlucky event: दुर्घटनम् or sim.<BR>घटना (when the sense is clear).<BR>III A non-<BR>-essential property:<BR>(1) न प्रकृतिः;<BR>(2) असहजो<BR> धर्मः<BR>or<BR>गुणः (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accidental
ACCIDENTAL:<BR>I Casual, fortuitous: q. v.<BR>(1) दैविकः (की, कं)<BR>if a. there is no punish-<BR>ment<BR>दैविके नास्ति निग्रहः, M. viii. 409;<BR>(2)<BR>यादृच्छिकः (की, कं) not approving of a. union<BR>यादृच्छिकीं सम्पत्तिमनभिसमीक्ष्य, D. vi.;<BR>even a.<BR>union<BR>यदृच्छयापि योगः, Ki.,<BR>II Non-essential<BR>(1) असमवायिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) आहार्यः (र्या, र्यं);<BR>(3) असहजः (जा, जं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accidentally
ACCIDENTALLY:<BR>(1) दैवात्;<BR>(2) दैवयोगात्;<BR>(3) दैव-<BR>गत्या;<BR>(4) यदृच्छया;<BR>(5) विधिवशात्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acclamation
ACCLAMATION:<BR>(1) प्रशंसावाचः;<BR>with various<BR>a s of the spectators<BR>रङ्गगतस्य जनस्यौच्चावचाः<BR> प्रशंसावाचः, प्रतिगृह्णन्ती, D. vi.;<BR>(2) साधुवादः, Si.<BR>xiv. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acclimatize
ACCLIMATIZE: Ph.<BR>many foreigners become a. d<BR>to India<BR>*बहवो विदेशिनः कालेन भारतवर्षस्य जलवाय्वादि-<BR>सहिष्णवो भवन्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acclivity
ACCLIVITY: उत्सङ्गः: v. Slope, incline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accommodate
ACCOMMODATE (v. t.):<BR>I To adapt, con-<BR>-form: Ph. a yourself to the whims of nature<BR>विधिविलसितान्यनुवर्तस्व (?).<BR>II To reconcile,<BR>adjust: q. v.<BR>III To supply with conve-<BR>-niences: Ph.:<BR>a. me with lodgings<BR>*वासदानेन<BR> मामुपकुरु।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accommodation
ACCOMMODATION:<BR>I Adaptation: q. v.:<BR>उपयोगिता।<BR>II Reconciliation: q. v.<BR>III<BR>Conveniences: Ph.:<BR>we received every a.<BR>in the inn.<BR>सर्वोपकरणान्यस्माभिः पथिकाश्रमे समधिगतानि।<BR>IV A loan of money: Ph.<BR>a. bill<BR>*उपकरण-<BR>पत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accompanied by
ACCOMPANIED BY: Often expr. by any comp.<BR>with स-:<BR>as if a. by attendants<BR>ससचिव इव, Ki.<BR>x. 14. N. B. Note the fol. exx. a. by Sachi<BR>शचीसखः, R. viii. 32;<BR>a. by Rati<BR>रतिद्धितीयः<BR>Ku. iii. 35;<BR>a. by his mistress<BR>गृहिणीसहायः<BR>R. ii. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accompaniment
ACCOMPANIMENT: Ph. singing in a. with drums<BR>मृदङ्गानुगतसङ्गीतम्, Ra. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accompany
ACCOMPANY:<BR>I To go with:<BR>(1) अनु-गच्छति,<BR> अन्वेति, etc.: a. d by some of the chief Kiratas<BR>अन्वीतः स कतिपयैः किरातवर्यैः Ki. xii. 52: v. To<BR>go after, follow;<BR>(2) सहचरः (री, रं) भवति<BR>(भू, c. i.) (with gen.);<BR>(3) गच्छति, याति etc.<BR>with सह and ins.:<BR>I will a. you<BR>त्वया सह गमि-<BR>ष्यामि।<BR>II To play in accompaniment:<BR>(1)<BR>अनुगच्छति (गम्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) अनुसरति (सृ, c. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accomplice
ACCOMPLICE: सहायः: v. Accessory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accomplish
ACCOMPLISH (v. t.):<BR>I To complete: q. v.<BR>पूरयति (c. of पूर्).<BR>II To perform, execute:<BR>(1) साधयति (c. of सिध्);<BR>(2) निष्पादयति, सम्पा-<BR>दयति (c. of पद्);<BR>(3) निवर्तयति (c. of वृत्);<BR>(4) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">Page007</a>]<BR>समा-दधाति (धा, c. 3);<BR>(5) करोति (कृ, c. 8);<BR>(6) दिशति (दिश्, c. 9);<BR>(7) राधयति (c. of.<BR>राध्).<BR>III To furnish: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accomplished
ACCOMPLISHED (adj.):<BR>I Finished, performed:<BR>(1) सिद्धः (द्धा, द्धं);<BR>(2) निष्पन्नः (न्ना, न्नं);<BR>(3) निवृत्तः (त्ता, त्तं)<BR>II Clever, refined:<BR>(1) विशारदः (दा, दं);<BR>(2) विचक्षणः (णा, णं);<BR>(3) कृतिन् (f. नी):<BR>let the a. enjoy it with<BR>pleasure<BR>तत् सुप्रसन्नमनसः कृतिनो भजन्ताम्, Vi. i.<BR>N. B. The last word generally used absol.<BR>But see Ki. xiv. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accomplishment
ACCOMPLISHMENT:<BR>I The act of accom-<BR>-plishing:<BR>(1) सिद्धिः;<BR>(2) साधनम्;<BR>(3) सम्पा-<BR>दनम्;<BR>(4) निष्पत्तिः;<BR>(5) राद्धिः;<BR>(6) निवृत्तिः।<BR>II Attainment, acquirement, culture:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accord
ACCORD (subs.):<BR>I Agreement, concur-<BR>-rence: q. v.: Ph.<BR>let us all with one a. fly<BR>up with the net<BR>नर्वैरेकचित्तीभूय जालमादायीङ्ङीयताम्,<BR>H. i.,<BR>of one's own a.<BR>स्वेच्छातः।<BR>II Concord,<BR>harmony. q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accord
ACCORD (v.):<BR>I Trans: v. To grant.<BR>II<BR>Intrans: v. To harmonise, agree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accordance with in
ACCORDANCE WITH IN:<BR>(1) Comp with अनुसारेण;<BR>in a. with it<BR>तदनुसारेण;<BR>(2) Sometimes by the<BR>sim. abl. or ins: in a. with the king's command<BR>राजाञ्जया,<BR>in a. with my saying<BR>मद्वचनात्, Mr.:<BR>v. According to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

according to
ACCORDING TO:<BR>(1) By any. comp.<BR>with<BR>यथा,<BR>a. to rite<BR>यथाविधि; punishing a. to (the nature of)<BR>the offence (committed) यथापराधदण्डानां, R. i. 6.;<BR>(2) When indicating order or succession<BR>by अनुक्रमेण, क्रमेण, or by any comp. with अनु-,<BR>not a. to (the seniority of)<BR>the mother<BR>न मातृक्रमेण;<BR>K. b.;<BR>a. to regular order<BR>अनुपूर्वशः, M. : v.<BR>In accordance with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accordingly
ACCORDINGLY (adv.): तथैव: v. Agreeably,<BR>conformably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accordingly
ACCORDINGLY (conj.): Often understood or<BR>expr. by: circumlocution: Ph. ‘the princess<BR>is come, come to see her’, (saying this) she went<BR>and we<BR>a. followed her<BR>प्राप्तैवेयं भर्तृदारिका, आगच्छतां<BR> द्रष्ट मित्ययासीत् । तामन्वयाव चावां, D. vi.;<BR>he a.<BR>followed me<BR>तथोक्तः मामनुवव्राज: v. Consequ-<BR>-ently, therefore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accost
ACCOST (v. t.): आ-मन्त्रयति (मन्त्र्, c. 10): v.<BR>To address.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accouchement
ACCOUCHEMENT:<BR>(1) गर्भनिर्गमः;<BR>(2) प्रसवः:<BR>v. Delivery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accoucheur
ACCOUCHEUR:<BR>(1) कुमारभृत्याकुशलो भिषक्, R. iii.<BR>12.;<BR>(2) प्रजननकुशलः (पुरुषः), Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

account
ACCOUNT (subs):<BR>I Of money: गणना;<BR>a.<BR>book<BR>गणनापत्रिका, Raj.;<BR>Balancing an a.<BR>गण-<BR>नामेकीकृत्य, Raj.;<BR>render an a. for me<BR>मदर्थं गणनां<BR> कुरु।<BR>II Estimation: q. v. गणना।<BR>III Im-<BR>-portance, value, advantage: q. v.<BR>IV A<BR>narrative or description: q. v.<BR>(1) विवरणम्;<BR>(2) विवृत्तिः: v. Reason, consideration:<BR>q. v.: Ph.<BR>on this a.<BR>अतः,<BR>on what a.<BR>किमर्थम्<BR>or<BR>किन्निमित्तम्।<BR>or no a.<BR>न कथञ्चन; on all a. s<BR>सर्वथा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

account of
ACCOUNT OF, ON:<BR>(1) By the abl.:<BR>on a. of<BR>having no power<BR>अप्रभुत्वात्, D. ;<BR>(2) Sometimes<BR>by the ins especially if the word ends in ता,<BR>on a. of my childhood<BR>बालतया,;<BR>(3) By -निमित्तः<BR>(त्ता, त्तं),<BR>as we are reduced to this state on a.<BR>of the enemy<BR>द्विषन्निमित्ता यदियं दशा, Ki. i. 41.:<BR>v. For the sake of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

account
ACCOUNT (v. t.): गणयति (गण्, c. 10.): v.<BR>To consider, esteem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

account for
ACCOUNT FOR,:<BR>I To assign the cause of:<BR>कारणं दर्शयति, प्र-, (c. of दृश्) (with gen.):<BR>v. To explain.<BR>II To render an account:<BR>Ph.<BR>a. for the money received<BR>*यद्धनं प्राप्तं तस्य<BR> गणनां देहि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accountable
ACCOUNTABLE: Ph.<BR>I. apprehend you are a. for<BR>his death<BR>*त्वद्दोषात्तस्य मरणमाशङ्के;<BR>every one is a.<BR>to God for his conduct<BR>*सर्वैरीश्वरायात्मकार्याणां<BR> न्यायान्यायौ प्रदर्शयितव्यौ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accountant
ACCOUNTANT: perh. गणकः; chief a., a.-general<BR>गणनाध्यक्षः, RAJ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accoutre
ACCOUTRE (v. t.): सं-नह्यति (नह्, c. 4.): v.<BR>To equip, arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accoutrement
ACCOUTREMENT<BR>(1) सन्नाहः;<BR>(2) सज्जाः v.<BR>Arms, equipment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accredit
ACCREDIT (v.):<BR>I To trust: q. v.: वि-श्वसिति [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">Page008</a>]<BR>(श्वस्, c. 2).<BR>II To send with credentials:<BR>प्र-हिणोति (हि, c. 5): To send.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accretion
ACCRETION:<BR>(1) उपचयः;<BR>(2) वृद्धिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accure
ACCURE (v. 1.): v. To result; also to<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accumulate
ACCUMULATE (v. t.):<BR>(1) सं-चिनोति, समा-, प्र-<BR>(चि, c. 5);<BR>(2) सं-बिभर्ति (भृ, c. 3);<BR>(3)<BR>सं-गृह्वाति (ग्रह्, c. 9);<BR>(4) राशीकररोति, पूगीक-<BR>रोति etc. (=to amass).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accumulate
ACCUMULATE (v. i.):<BR>(1) उपचीयते (pass);<BR>(2)<BR>वर्धते (वृध्, c. i);<BR>(3) स्फीतः (ता, तं) भवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accumulation
ACCUMULATION:<BR>(1) सञ्चयः;<BR>(2) संग्रहः;<BR>(3)<BR>सम्भृतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accuracy
ACCURACY:<BR>(1) विशुद्धत्वम्;<BR>(2) विशुद्धिः: v.<BR>Correctness, nicety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accurate
ACCURATE: विशुद्धः (द्धा, द्धं): v. Correct,<BR>exact, careful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accurately
ACCURATELY: विशुद्धम्: v. Correctly, exactly<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accursed
ACCURSED:<BR>(1) -हतकः (का, कं), the a. moon.<BR>चन्द्रहतकः, K.;<BR>(2) दग्धः (ग्धा, ग्धं), the a. saint<BR>दग्धसिद्धः, D. vii.: v. Detestable, execrable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accusation
ACCUSATION:<BR>(1) अभियोगः;<BR>(2) अपवादः;<BR>made<BR>a false a. against her husband<BR>भर्तुर्मिथ्यापवाद-<BR>मभिहितवती, Ver;<BR>(3) अभिशापः (=false a.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accusative case
ACCUSATIVE CASE:<BR>(1) कर्मकारकम्;<BR>(2) कर्मन्<BR>(n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accusatory
ACCUSATORY (adj.): i. e. Containing an accu-<BR>-sation: अपवादगर्भः (र्भा, र्भं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accuse
ACCUSE (v. t.):<BR>(1) अभि-युनक्ति (युज्, c. 7),<BR>that I go like an a. d man<BR>अभियुक्त इव प्रयामि,<BR>Mr. ix.;<BR>(2) अप-वदति (वद्, c. 1.); v. To<BR>calumniate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accuser
ACCUSER:<BR>(1) अभियोक्तृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) अभियोगिन्<BR>(f. नी) (rare.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accustom
ACCUSTOM:<BR>(1) परिचयं करोति, a. ed himself in<BR>shooting moveable objects परिचयं चललक्ष्यनिपातने<BR>॥करोति, R. ix. 49;<BR>(2) अभ्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4)<BR>v. To practise. Ph.:<BR>he who is a. ed to good<BR>food<BR>*यः सर्वदा भोजनविशेषैराहारं करोति;<BR>a. ed to<BR>cheating<BR>वञ्चनापरः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ace
ACE: Of cards: *टेक्वा। Ph.:<BR>within an a. of<BR>piercing:<BR>*अल्पेन वेद्धुं न शशाक।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accerbity
ACCERBITY: कटुता (lit. and fig.): v. Sourness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ache
ACHE (subs):<BR>(1) पीडा;<BR>(2) वेदना;<BR>(3) व्यथा<BR>v. Head- a. etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ache
ACHE (v. i.):<BR>(1) व्यथते (व्यथ्, c. 1);<BR>(2)<BR>पीडयते (c. of पीड्). Ph.<BR>my head a. s<BR>शिरोवेदन<BR> मां बाधते। Mu. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

achieve
ACHIEVE (v. t.):<BR>(1) साधयति (c. of साध्)<BR>(2) निष्पादयति (c. of पद्): v. To accomplish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

achievement
ACHIEVEMENT:<BR>I Exploit: q. v.<BR>(1) अवदानम्<BR>measured by your a.<BR>अवदानसम्मितां, Sa. vii.<BR>(2) कर्मन् (n); v. Deed.<BR>II In heraldry<BR>v. Escutcheon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

achromatic
ACHROMATIC: *अवर्णः (र्णा, र्णं): a. telescope<BR>*अवर्णं दूरवीक्षणं येन तेजोविश्लेषेण रक्तपीताद्यादिमवणे<BR> न दृश्यते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acid
ACID:<BR>I adj. अम्ल: (म्ला, म्लं).<BR>II Subs.:<BR>अम्लः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acidity
ACIDITY:<BR>(1) अम्लता;<BR>(2) अम्लत्वभ्,<BR>a. of<BR>stomach<BR>अम्लपित्तः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aciduous
ACIDUOUS: ईषदम्लः (म्ला, म्लं) (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acknowledge
ACKNOWLEDGE (v. t.):<BR>(1) अभ्युप-एति (इ। c. 2)<BR>she a. defeat from me<BR>मत्तः पराजयोऽभ्युपेतः,<BR>D. ii.;<BR>(2) अभ्युप-गच्छति (गम्, c. 1):<BR>I a. I<BR>am just so<BR>अभ्युपगतं तावदस्माभिरेवंविधा एव वयम्, Sa.<BR>v.;<BR>(3) स्वीकरोति, D. s.;<BR>(4) अंगीकरोति,<BR>if<BR>one would not a. the authority of inference<BR>यदि<BR> कश्चित्प्रामाण्यमनुमानस्य नाङ्गीकुर्यात्, D. s.;<BR>(5) प्रति-<BR>पद्यते (पद्, c. 4.), M. viii. 183.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acknowledgement
ACKNOWLEDGEMENT:<BR>(1) स्वीकारः;<BR>(2) अभ्युप-<BR>गमः;<BR>(3) अभ्युपायः;<BR>(4) अङ्गीकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acme
ACME: परा कोटिः:<BR>the a. of joy<BR>परां कोटि-<BR>मानन्दस्य, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aconite
ACONITE: A poison: वत्सनाभः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acorn
ACORN: i. e. The fruit of the oak: v. Oak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acoustic
ACOUSTIC:<BR>(1) श्रौतः (ती, तं);<BR>(2) Comp. with<BR>श्रोत्र-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acoustics
ACOUSTICS: *शब्दविद्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquaint
ACQUAINT (v. t.):<BR>I To make familiar:<BR>परीचयं करोति (कृ, c. 8) आ-चरति (चर्, c. 1),<BR>making himself a. ed with all sciences<BR>सर्वविद्या-<BR>परिचयमाचरतः, K.<BR>II. To inform: q. v.<BR>बोधयति, अव-, (c. of बुध्),<BR>you should keep me a.<BR>ed with whatever happens there everyday<BR>प्रत्यहञ्च<BR> यद्यत्तत्र वृत्तान्तं जातं तदस्मि त्वयावबोध्यः, D. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquaintance
ACQUAINTANCE:<BR>I Familiar knowledge:<BR>(1)<BR>परिचयः,<BR>out of respect for his a. with all practical<BR>arts<BR>सकलकलाकलापपरिचयबहुमानेन, K. ;<BR>(2) संस्तवः<BR>(rare): v. Knowledge, intimacy.<BR>II A<BR>person known;<BR>(1) परिचितः (ता, तं),<BR>like old<BR>a. s<BR>चिरपरिचिताविव, D. iii.;<BR>(2) संस्तुतः (ता, तं)<BR>Ki. iii. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquainted with
ACQUAINTED WITH: अभिञ्जः (ञ्जा, ञ्जं) (with gen.),<BR>I am not a. with such affairs<BR>एवं विधानां वृत्तान्ताना-<BR>मनमिञ्जास्मि; K. : Ph.<BR>we are not a. with love<BR>affairs<BR>अनभ्यन्तरा खलु वयं मदनगतस्य वृत्तान्तस्य,<BR>Sa. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquiesce
ACQUIESCE: v. To assent, abide by, content<BR>with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquiescence
ACQUIESCENCE: सम्मतिः: v. Assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquire
ACQUIRE (v. t.):<BR>(1) अर्जति, उप-, (अर्ज्, c. 1)<BR>or commonly, उपार्जनं करोति (with gen.);<BR>(2) अधि-गच्छति (गम्, c. 1),<BR>to a. fame<BR>यशोधि-<BR>गन्तुम्, Ki. iii. 40. v. To gain, obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquirement
ACQUIREMENT:<BR>I The act of acquiring<BR>(1)<BR>अर्जनम्, उपार्जनम्, by the a. of knowledge<BR>विद्योपार्जनेन, P. i. p.;<BR>(2) अधिगमः;<BR>(3) लाभः;<BR>(4) अवाप्तिः।<BR>II Of knowledge: v. Attain-<BR>-ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquisition
ACQUISITION:<BR>I Acquirement: q. v.<BR>II The<BR>thing acquired लाभः v. Gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquit
ACQUIT (v. i.):<BR>(1) मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.);<BR>(2)<BR>मोचयति (c. of. मुच्);<BR>(3) निस्तारयति (c. of<BR>तॄ) (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquit oneself
ACQUIT ONESELF: आ-चरति (चर्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquittal
ACQUITTAL:<BR>(1) मुक्तिः;<BR>(2) मोचनम्;<BR>(3) मोक्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquittance
ACQUITTANCE:<BR>I Of debt:<BR>(1) परिशोधः;<BR>(2)<BR>निर्यातनम्।<BR>II A receipt: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acre
ACRE: भूमानविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acrid
ACRID (adj.): कटुः (ट्वी, टु): v. Pungent,<BR>sharp, acrimonious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acrimonious
ACRIMONIOUS:<BR>(1) कटुः (ट्वी, टु);<BR>(2) उग्रः<BR>(ग्रा, ग्रं);<BR>(3) प्रखरः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acrimoniousness
ACRIMONIOUSNESS, ACRIMONY:<BR>(1) कटुत्वम्;<BR>(2)<BR>प्राखर्यम्;<BR>(3) उग्रत्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

across
ACROSS (adv.):<BR>(1) व्यत्यस्तः (स्ता, स्तं);<BR>(2)<BR>कोणाकोणि (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

across
ACROSS (prep.): Ph.<BR>I will go a. the river.<BR>नदी-<BR>पारं गमिष्यामि;<BR>a bridge has been laid a. the<BR>Son<BR>*शोनस्योपरि सेतुर्बबन्धे।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acrostic
ACROSTIC: Nearest word चित्रकाव्यम्, Kav. i.<BR>8.; *आद्याक्षरबन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

act
ACT (v. t.):<BR>I To do, perform: q. v.<BR>II<BR>On the stage:<BR>(1) अभिनयति (नी, c. 1),<BR>Sa. 1.;<BR>(2) प्र-योजयति (युज्, c. 10),<BR>we should<BR>a. Malabikagnimitra in this spring festival<BR>मालविकाग्निमित्रमस्मिन् वसन्तोत्सवे प्रयोक्तव्यम्, Mal.;<BR>(3) नाटयति (नट्, c. 10.), Ma. i.: Ph.<BR>Urbashi a. ing the part of Lakshmi.<BR>लक्ष्मीभूमि-<BR>कायां वर्तमानोर्वशी, V. iii. N. B. The sense of a.<BR>ing is often expressed by nomi. v. s.:<BR>a.<BR>the nymph<BR>अप्सरायते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

act
ACT (v. i.):<BR>I To be in action: करोति (कृ,<BR>c. 8):<BR>this is not possible that one a. s and<BR>another enjoys<BR>न ह्ये तत् सम्भविष्यत्यन्यः करोत्यन्यः<BR> भुङ्क्त इति, D. s.<BR>II To conduct oneself:<BR>(1)<BR>आचरति (चर्, c. 1):<BR>the king has a. ed very<BR>ungentlemanly towards Sakuntala<BR>तेन राज्ञा शकु-<BR>न्तलायामनार्यमाचरितम्, Sa. iv. v. To behave;<BR>(2) by nominal verbs: to a. as. a step-mother<BR>सपत्नायते;<BR>to a. as a tutor<BR>गुरूयते;<BR>to a. like<BR>yourself<BR>त्वद्यते।<BR>III On the stage: अभिनयति<BR>(नी, c. 1) v. Act (v. t.) (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

act
ACT (subs):<BR>I A deed: q. v.:<BR>(1) कर्मन्<BR>(n);<BR>(2) क्रिया;<BR>(3) कृतम्।<BR>II A division of a<BR>play: अङ्क (mn.)<BR>III A law: *विधिः Ph.:<BR>the last act of life: (जीवनस्य) चरमदशा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

action
ACTION:<BR>I Agency: Often not expr:<BR>water<BR>boils by the a. of heat<BR>*वारि तपति तापेन। Ph.<BR>the<BR>a. of the senses<BR>इन्द्रियाणां वृत्तिः, Ku. iii. 72;<BR>the a. of love<BR>मदनस्य व्यापारः, Sa. i.<BR>II Deed,<BR>conduct: q. v.<BR>(1) चेष्टितम्;<BR>(2) विचेष्टितम्।<BR>III Gesticulation: q. v. चेष्टा, M. vii. 63.<BR>IV Law suit, cause: q. v. कार्यम्, Mr. xi.<BR>V. An engagement, battle: q. v.: युद्धम्।<BR>VI In plays etc.: *कार्यम्:<BR>there is much a.<BR>in the play<BR>*कार्यभुलं नाटकम्।:<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

actionable
ACTIONABLE:<BR>(1) व्यवहार्यः (र्या, र्यं),;<BR>(2) व्यवह-<BR>र्तव्यः (व्या, व्यं):<BR>a. subject<BR>व्यवहारपदं, M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

active
ACTIVE (adj.):<BR>I Agile, nimble:<BR>(1) उत्थान-<BR>शीलः [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">Page010</a>] (ला, लं);<BR>(2) उत्साहिन् (f. नी)<BR>(=zealous); (3, 4) क्षिप्रकारिन्, आशुकारिन्<BR>(f. णी) (=one who does quick);<BR>(5) तीक्ष्ण-<BR>कर्मन् (mfn) (sharp worker);<BR>(6) अतन्द्रितः<BR>(ता, तं) (=not slow).<BR>II Busy, industri-<BR>-ous; q. v.;<BR>(1) कर्मिष्ठः (ष्ठा, ष्ठं)<BR>(2) व्यवसायिन्<BR>(f. नी)<BR>III In gram.; Ph. a. verb<BR>स्कर्मकक्रिया;<BR>a. voice<BR>कर्तृवाच्यम्। —<BR>IV As<BR>opposed to passive: Ph.<BR>a. organs<BR>कर्मेन्द्रियाणि<BR>(n. pl.);<BR>entered into a. life<BR>संसारकार्ये व्यापृतः<BR>(ता, तं) (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

activity
ACTIVITY (subs.):<BR>I Agility,:<BR>(1) क्षिप्रकारिता;<BR>(2) उत्साहः v. Zeal.<BR>II Industry and<BR>energy:<BR>(1) उद्योगः;<BR>(2) व्यवसायः;<BR>(3)<BR>अव्यवसायः;<BR>(4) कर्माभिनिवेशः;<BR>(5) उत्थानशीलता।<BR>Ph.<BR>with great a.<BR>महता यत्नेन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

actor
ACTOR:<BR>I A doer: q. v.: कर्तृ (m).<BR>II A<BR>stage player:<BR>(1) नटः;<BR>(2) नर्तकः;<BR>(3)<BR>कुशीलवः;<BR>(4) चारणः;<BR>(5) शैलूषः;<BR>(6) अभिनेतृ<BR>(m);<BR>(7) रङ्गाजीवः;<BR>(8) शैलालिन् (m) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

actress
ACTRESS:<BR>(1) नटी;<BR>(2) नर्तकी;<BR>(3) अभिनेत्री।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

actual
ACTUAL:<BR>(1) यथार्थः (र्था, र्थं);<BR>(2) Comp.<BR>with परमार्थं: v. Real, true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

actuality
ACTUALITY:<BR>(1) यथार्थता;<BR>(2) तत्त्वम्: v.<BR>Realty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

actually
ACTUALLY:<BR>(1) परमार्थतः;<BR>(2) यथार्थतः: v.<BR>Really, truely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

actuary
ACTUARY: लेखकः (?) v. Clerk, Registrar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

actuate
ACTUATE: प्र-णुदति (नुद्, c. 6): v. To move,<BR>impel, influence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acumen
ACUMEN:<BR>(1) सूक्ष्मदर्शिता;<BR>(2) कुशाग्रबुद्धिः: v.<BR>Sagacity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acute
ACUTE (adj.):<BR>I In intellect:<BR>(1) सूक्ष्मदर्शिन<BR>(f. नी);<BR>(2) कुशाग्रबुद्धि (mfn.), R. v. 4.:<BR>v. Subtle, shrewd, keen.<BR>II Of the senses<BR>तिक्ष्णः (क्ष्णा, क्ष्णं): v. Sharp, penetrating.<BR>III Sharp, pointed: q. v.: Ph. a. angle:<BR>v. Angle:<BR>a. accent<BR>उदात्तः;<BR>a. pain<BR>तीव्रवेदना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acutely
ACUTELY: v. Sharply, kneely, subtly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acutness
ACUTNESS:<BR>I Of intellect: v. Acumen.<BR>II Of the senses:<BR>(1) तैक्ष्ण्यम्;<BR>(2) तेजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adage
ADAGE: वचनम् (when the sense is clear):<BR>v. Proverb, saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adamant
ADAMANT:<BR>I An imaginary stone: वज्रः<BR>(Lit. and Fig.).<BR>II Lode-stone q. v.<BR>अयस्कान्तः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adapt
ADAPT: v. To fit, suit. A. ed: v. Fit,<BR>suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adaptations
ADAPTATIONS: v. Fitness, suitability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

add
ADD:<BR>I To sum up:<BR>(1) योजयति, सं-, (युज,<BR>c. 10).;<BR>(2) सं-कलयति (कल्, c. 10).<BR>II To<BR>gain, unite: q. v.: योजयति।<BR>III To speak<BR>in addition अपरं च ब्रवीति (ब्रू, c. 2), अभिदधाति<BR>(धा, c. 3), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adder
ADDER: सर्पविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

addict
ADDICT:<BR>(1) आत्मानं आ-सज्जयति (with loc.);<BR>(2) आसज्जते (with loc.): v. To devote,<BR>give up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

addicted
ADDICTED:<BR>(1) आसक्तः, प्रसक्तः,<BR>or<BR>सक्तः (क्ता, क्तं);<BR>(2) निरतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

addition
ADDITION:<BR>I The process of adding<BR>(1)<BR>सङ्कलनम्;<BR>(2) सङ्कलितम्;<BR>a. of fractions<BR>भिन्न-<BR>सङ्कलितम्, Li.<BR>II The act of adding<BR>(1)<BR>योगः;<BR>(2) संयोगः;<BR>(3) समायोगः;<BR>(4) सङ्कनम्<BR>III Anything added योगः: v. Increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

additional
ADDITIONAL: Ph. on receiving the a. powers<BR>*अतिरिक्तक्ष्मतां प्राप्य;<BR>there are additional reasons<BR>for his departure<BR>*तस्य प्रस्थानस्यापराणि कारणानि<BR> सन्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

addle
ADDLE (adj.):<BR>(1) नष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं) (?);<BR>(2)<BR>दुष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं) (?) v. Putrid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

addle-headed
ADDLE-HEADED: v. Silly, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

address
ADDRESS (subs.):<BR>I A speaking to;<BR>(1)<BR>सम्बोधनम्;<BR>(2) अभिभाषणम्;<BR>(3) वचनम्।<BR>II A<BR>massage of respect: perh. अभिवादः।<BR>III<BR>Manner of speaking to another: Ph.<BR>of<BR>pleasing a.<BR>प्रियम्बदः (दा, दं)<BR>or<BR>मिष्टभाषिन् (f. णी)<BR>or<BR>मधुरालापिन् (f. नी).<BR>IV Tact, dexterity:<BR>q. v. दक्षता: V. In pl.: of courtship: Ph.<BR>his a. es were rejected<BR>*तस्यामन्त्रणं प्रत्यादिष्टम्।<BR>VI<BR>The superscription of a letter: बाह्यनामन् (n.)<BR>get this letter written by Sakatadasa without<BR>putting any a.:<BR>अदत्तबाह्यनामानं लेखं शकटदासेन<BR> लेखयित्वा Mu. i.<BR>VII The direction नामधमनी<BR>(n. du.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

address
ADDRESS (v. t.):<BR>I To discourse to:<BR>(1) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">Page011</a>]<BR>सम्बोधयति (बुध्, c. 10)<BR>or<BR>सम्बोधनं करोति;<BR>(2)<BR>अभि-भाषते, सभ्-, आ-, समा-, (भाष्, c. 1),<BR>he a.<BR>es me by my name<BR>नामग्रहणपूर्वकं मां सम्भाषते;<BR>(3)<BR>अभि-दधाति (धा, c. 3),<BR>a. me as you have been<BR>accustomed to do<BR>यथाभ्यस्तमभिधीयतां, U. i.: v.<BR>To speak to.<BR>II To superscribe (as a<BR>letter): q. v.: Ph. he a. ed a letter to me<BR>स मह्यं पत्रं प्राहिणोत्।<BR>III To court, woo: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adduce
ADDUCE (v. t.):<BR>(1) दिशति, उत्-, निर-, (दिश्,<BR>c. 6),<BR>if a man does not a. witness saying that<BR>he has got them<BR>साक्षिणो मम विद्यन्ते इत्युक्ता यो न<BR> निर्दिशति, K. b, M. viii. 56.;<BR>(2) उपन्यस्यति<BR>(अस्, c. 4)<BR>a. ing of witness<BR>साक्ष्युपन्यासः, K. b.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adept
ADEPT (adj.):<BR>(1) निपुणः (णा, णं);<BR>(2) कुशलः<BR>(ला, लं);<BR>(3) पटु (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adequacy
ADEQUACY: पर्याप्तिः v. Sufficiency. N. B. Better<BR>expr. by the adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adequate
ADEQUATE (adj.):<BR>I Sufficient: q. v. पर्याप्तः<BR>(प्ता, प्तं).<BR>II As applied to men:<BR>(1) उपयुक्तः<BR>(क्ता, क्तं);<BR>(2) समर्थः (र्था, र्थं). v. Compe-<BR>-tent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adequately
ADEQUATELY: Better expr. by the adj.: v.<BR>Sufficient, sufficiently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adhere
ADHERE (v. i.):<BR>(1) सज्जते (सज्ज्, c. 1),<BR>who<BR>a. s to my dress<BR>को नु निवसने मे सज्जते, Sa. iv.;<BR>(2) लगति, सं-, (लग्, c. 1)<BR>again a. d to the<BR>Sinsapa tree<BR>शिंशपावृक्षे पुनर्ललाग, etc. v. To<BR>stick, cling to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adherence
ADHERENCE: v. Adhesion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adherent
ADHERENT (subs.): अनुगामिन् (f. नी): v.<BR>Follower. Ph.<BR>Anantasira is an a. of Prahara-<BR>varma<BR>अनन्तसीरः प्रहारवर्मणः पक्षः, D. iii.: v.<BR>Partisan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adhesion
ADHESION (subs):<BR>I Lit.: Sticking to:<BR>(1)<BR>संलग्नत्वम्;<BR>(2) संसक्तिः<BR>II Fig. Attachment:<BR>q. v.: आसक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adhesion
ADHESION (adj.): Perh. श्यानः (ना, नं) v.<BR>Sticky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adieu
ADIEU (interj.): स्वस्ति with dat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adieu
ADIEU (subs):<BR>(1) आमन्त्रणम्;<BR>(2) आप्रच्छनम्। To<BR>bid a.<BR>(1) आमन्त्रयते (मन्त्र्, c. 10). R. vii.<BR>30.;<BR>(1) आ-पृच्छते, (प्रच्छ, c. 6). R. viii. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjacent
ADJACENT (adj.):<BR>(1) सन्निहितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2)<BR>सन्निकृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>(3) समीपवर्तिन् (f. नी);<BR>(4) निकटस्थः (स्था, स्थं);<BR>(5) आसन्नवर्तिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjective
ADJECTIVE:<BR>(1) विशेषणम्;<BR>(2) गुणवाचकः शब्दः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjoin
ADJOIN (v. t.):<BR>(1) लगति, सं-, (लग्, c. 1);<BR>(2) स्पृशति, (स्पृश्, c. 6).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjoining
ADJOINING (adj.): संलग्नः<BR>or<BR>लग्नः (ग्ना, ग्नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjourn
ADJOURN (v. t.): Perh. व्या-क्षिपति (क्षिप्,<BR>c. 6):<BR>a. ed the case till monday<BR>*सोमवारं<BR> यावत् कार्यं व्याचिक्षेप: v. To put off, postpone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjourn
ADJOURN (v. i.): Ph.<BR>the parliament a. ed for<BR>four days<BR>*चतुर्दिवसं महासभा त्यक्तकार्यासीत्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjournment
ADJOURNMENT: व्याक्षेपः (?) v. Postponment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjudge
ADJUDGE (v. t.): v. To award, to decree,<BR>to sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjudicate
ADJUDICATE: निर्णयति (नी, c. 1): v. To<BR>decide, judge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjudication
ADJUDICATION:<BR>(1) निर्णयः;<BR>(2) निर्णयनम्: v.<BR>Decision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjunct
ADJUNCT:<BR>(1) संयुक्तः (क्ता, क्तं);<BR>(2) सम्मिलितः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(3) अनुबद्धः (द्धा, द्धं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjuration
ADJURATION:<BR>I The act adjuring: शापनम्।<BR>II The form of oath: शपथः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjure
ADJURE: v. To entreat, beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjust
ADJUST:<BR>I To make extact, fit: q. v.<BR>II<BR>To Regulate: q. v. सन्निदधाति (धा, c. 3).<BR>III Of accounts: v. Account.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjustment
ADJUSTMENT: v. Regulation, settlement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjutancy
ADJUTANCY: *सहचरपदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adjutant
ADJUTANT (subs):<BR>I A military officer:<BR>*सहचरः।<BR>II The gigantic crane:<BR>(1) अस्थि-<BR>भक्षः;<BR>(2) लोहपृष्ठः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admeasurement
ADMEASUREMENT, ADMENSURATION: v.<BR>Measurement, mensuration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

administer
ADMINISTER (v. t.):<BR>I To manage, execute:<BR>q. v. निर्-वाहयति (c. of वह्): Ph. to a. justice<BR>धर्मविवेचनं करोति (कृ, c. 8.) M. viii. 21.<BR>II<BR>To give, afford: q. v. ददाति (दा, c. 3).<BR>III<BR>To tender an oath: शापयति (c. of शप).<BR>IV<BR>To manage an estate: *मृतकसम्पत्तेः रक्षणावेक्षणं<BR> करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

administration
ADMINISTRATION:<BR>I Execution, manage-<BR>-ment: q. v.: निर्वाहः। Ph. a. of Government<BR>शासनम्;<BR>a. of justice<BR>धर्मविवेचनम्; internal a. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">Page012</a>]<BR>प्रजासु वृत्तिः, Ki. i. I.<BR>II. The executive part<BR>of Government: सचिवाः (m. pl.).<BR>III<BR>Legal. t. t.: Ph.<BR>letters of a.<BR>*निर्वाहपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

administrative
ADMINISTRATIVE: Ph.<BR>his a. abilities are<BR>proverbial<BR>*तस्य शासनकार्यदाक्ष्यं सुप्रसिद्धम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

administrator
ADMINISTRATOR:<BR>I A manager: q. v.:<BR>निर्वाहकः।<BR>II Of an intestate's property:<BR>रक्षकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admirable
ADMIRABLE (adj.):<BR>(1) श्लाध्यः (ध्या, ध्यं);<BR>(2) प्रशस्तः (स्ता, स्तं);<BR>(3) अद्भुतः (ता, तं)<BR>(=wonderful, q. v.);<BR>(4) अनुपमः (मा, मं)<BR>(=incomparable, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admirable
ADMIRABLE (interj.): साधु, सुष्ठु।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admirably
ADMIRABLY:<BR>(1) साधु;<BR>(2) सुष्ठु;<BR>(3) In<BR>comp., by the words given under Admi-<BR>-rable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admiral
ADMIRAL:<BR>(1) नाविकनायकः, D. vi.;<BR>(2) *रण-<BR>पोतपतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admiralty
ADMIRALTY: The board of a.: *रणपोतसचिव-<BR>मण्डलो; सामुद्रिकसचिवसमाजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admiration
ADMIRATION:<BR>(1) श्लाघा;<BR>(2) प्रशंसा;<BR>(3) प्रशंसा-<BR>वाचः (acclamation, q. v.);<BR>(4) विस्मयः<BR>(=wonder, q. v.) Ki. xiii. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admire
ADMIRE (v. t.):<BR>(1) प्र-शंसति (शंस्, c. 1), Indra<BR>a. d the speed<BR>...<BR>बलस्य शत्रुः प्रशशंस शीघ्रताम्,<BR>Si. i. 52.;<BR>(2) श्लाघते (श्लाघ्, c. 1),<BR>a. d by<BR>the assembled gods<BR>श्लाषितो देवसङ्घैः, Ki. xviii.<BR>48;<BR>(3) स्तवीति (स्तु, c. 2) (some) a. deep sense<BR>स्तुवन्ति गुर्वीमभिघेयसम्पदम्, Ki. xiv. 5.: v. To<BR>praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admirer
ADMIRER:<BR>I Lit. प्रशंसकः।<BR>II A lover: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admiringly
ADMIRINGLY: Of gazing:<BR>(1) विस्मयविकसिताक्षः<BR>(क्षी, क्षं), D. ;<BR>(2) निश्चलनिबद्धलक्ष्येण, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admissible
ADMISSIBLE (adj.): ग्रह्यः (ह्या, ह्यं), M. viii.<BR>78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admission
ADMISSION (subs):<BR>I Acknowledgment:<BR>q. v.: स्वीकारः।<BR>II Admittance, entrance:<BR>(1) प्रवेशः;<BR>(2) प्रवेशनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admit
ADMIT (v. t.):<BR>I To allow to enter:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रवेशयति,<BR>a. them at once<BR>अविलम्बितं प्रवेशय तौ,<BR>Sa. ii.;<BR>(2) आ-वेशयति (c. of विश्), a. ing<BR>(me)<BR>to his hut<BR>स्वकुटिरमावेश्य, D. iii.<BR>II To<BR>acknowledge: q. v.:<BR>(1) अभ्युपैति (इ, c.<BR>2);<BR>(2) अभ्युपगच्छति, (गम्, c. 1).<BR>III To<BR>be capable of: Ph.<BR>it a. s of no other cons-<BR>truction<BR>*अत्रान्योऽन्वयो नलगति<BR>or<BR>नोपपद्यते;<BR>it a. s<BR>of no delay<BR>विलम्बं न सहते (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admittance
ADMITTANCE: v. Admission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admitting that
ADMITTING THAT: v. Granting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admixture
ADMIXTURE: मिश्रणम् v. Mixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admonish
ADMONISH (v. t.):<BR>(1) अनु-बोधयति (c. of<BR>बुध्): v. To remind;<BR>(2) उपदिशति (दिश्,<BR>c. 6): v. To advise;<BR>(3) उपा-लभते (लभ्,<BR>c. 1): v. To reprove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admonisher
ADMONISHER:<BR>(1) उपदेशकः v. Adviser;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रबोधकः (?): v. Monitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admonition
ADMONITION:<BR>(1) उपदेशः v. Advice;<BR>(2)<BR>उपालम्भः v. Reproof;<BR>(3) प्रत्यादेशः (?): v.<BR>Warning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

admonitory
ADMONITORY (adj.): उपदेशगर्भः (र्भा, र्भं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ado
ADO (subs): v. Trouble, difficulty, bustle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adolescence
ADOLESCENCE (subs):<BR>(1) यौवनम्;<BR>(2) तारु-<BR>ण्यम्: v. Youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adolescent
ADOLESCENT (adj.): युवन् (f. युवती<BR>or<BR>युनी):<BR>v. Young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adopt
ADOPT (v. t.):<BR>(1) गृह्वाति, परि-, प्रति-, (ग्रह्,<BR>c. 9) (Lit. and Fig.) he who a. s a son...<BR>यः पुत्रं परिगृह्वीयात्, M. ix. 171.;<BR>(2) करोति (=to<BR>make, applicable only to a. ing children),<BR>who should a. and what sort of children.<BR>केन कः<BR> क्रियतां सुतः, D. m.: Ph.<BR>to a. as a son<BR>पुत्री-<BR>करोति (nomi). D. m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adopter
ADOPTER: ग्रहीतृ, परिग्रहीतृ प्रतिग्रहीतृ (f. त्री) (Lit.<BR>and Fig.), D. m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adoption
ADOPTION:<BR>(1) परिग्रहः, प्रतिग्रहः (Lit and Fig.)<BR>D. m.;<BR>(2) पुत्रीकरणं (=a. as a child), D. m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adoptive
ADOPTIVE:<BR>I One who adopts: परिग्रहीतृ (f.<BR>त्री): v. Adopter.<BR>II One who is a. ed:<BR>(1) कृत्रिमः (मा, मं);<BR>(2) दत्तकः (a son given);<BR>(3) क्रीतः (a son bought). See M. ix. 168.<BR>169. 174. 177.: Ph.<BR>a. daughter<BR>अपत्यकृतिका,<BR>U. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adorable
ADORABLE:<BR>(1) आराधनीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) उपास्यः<BR>(स्या, स्यं);<BR>(3) पूज्यः (ज्या, ज्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adoration
ADORATION:<BR>(1) आराधना;<BR>(2) उपासना;<BR>(3) पूजा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adore
ADORE (v. t.):<BR>(1) उप-आस्ते (आस्, c. 2);<BR>(2) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">Page013</a>]<BR>उप-तिष्ठते (स्था, c. 1);<BR>(3) आराधयति (राध्,<BR>c. 10);<BR>(4) पूजयति (पूज्, c. 10).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adorer
ADORER:<BR>(1) आराधकः (का, कं);<BR>(2) उपासकः<BR>(का, कं);<BR>(3) पूजकः (का, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adorn
ADORN (v. t.):<BR>(1) अलं-करोति (कृ, c. 8);<BR>(2)<BR>भूषयति, वि-, (भूष् c. 10);<BR>(3) मण्डयति (मण्ड्,<BR>c. 10);<BR>(4) प्र-साधयति (c. of सिध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adorner
ADORNER:<BR>(1) अलङ्कर्तृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) प्रसाधकः<BR>(f. धिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adornment
ADORNMENT:<BR>I Adorning:<BR>(1) भूषा;<BR>(2)<BR>मण्डनम्;<BR>(3) अलंक्रिया।<BR>II Ornament: q. v.:<BR>(1) अलङ्कारः;<BR>(2) भूषणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adrift
ADRIFT: इतस्ततः प्लवमानः (ना, नं). To set a.:<BR>Perh. प्लावयति (c. of प्लु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adroit
ADROIT (adj.):<BR>(1) निपुणः (णा, णं);<BR>(2) हस्तवत्<BR>(f. ती): v. Clever, skilful, dexterous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adroitly
ADROITLY:<BR>(1) नैपुण्येन;<BR>(2) सपाटवम्;<BR>(3) हस्तवत्तया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adroitness
ADROITNESS:<BR>(1) दाक्ष्यम्;<BR>(2) नैपुण्यम्;<BR>(3) हस्त-<BR>वत्ता;<BR>(4) चातुरी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adulation
ADULATION:<BR>(1) चाटूक्तिः;<BR>(2) स्तवः (?);<BR>(3)<BR>by<BR>false a. s<BR>वितथैः स्तवैः, Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adulator
ADULATOR: चाटुकारः, v. Flatterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adulatory
ADULATORY:<BR>(1) चाटुपूर्णः (र्णा, र्णं) (?);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रशंसागर्भः (र्भा, र्भं);<BR>(3) श्लाघासूचकः (का, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adult
ADULT:<BR>(1) प्राप्तव्यवहारः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) युवन् (f. ती):<BR>v. Youthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adulterate
ADULTERATE (v. t.): अपद्रव्येण मिश्रयति (मिश्र्,<BR>c. 10.) or sim. मिश्रयति (when the sense is<BR>clear). Ph.<BR>a. d with water<BR>जलसंसृष्टः (ष्टा,<BR> ष्टं), M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adulterater
ADULTERATER:<BR>(1) मिश्रकः, M. xi. 50;<BR>(2)<BR>अपद्रव्येणमिश्रणकर्तृ (m), K. b.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adulteration
ADULTERATION: अपद्रव्यमिश्रणं, or sim. मिश्रणं (when<BR>the sense is clear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adulterer
ADULTERER:<BR>(1) पारदारिकः;<BR>(2) पारतल्पिकः;<BR>(3) परस्त्रीकामिन् (m).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adulteress
ADULTERESS:<BR>(1) व्यभिचारिणी;<BR>(2) परपुरुषसङ्गता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adulterous
ADULTEROUS:<BR>(1) व्यभिचारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2)<BR>Comp. with व्यभिचार।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adultery
ADULTERY:<BR>(1) व्यभिचारः;<BR>(2) पारदार्यम्;<BR>(3)<BR>परस्त्रीगमनम्;<BR>(4) परकलत्रलङ्घनम्;<BR>(5) पतिलङ्घनम्;<BR>(6) परपुरुषसङ्गमनम्। N. B. Note that 2, 3, and 4<BR>applicable to men only, and 5 and 6 to<BR>women only. Ph.: to commit a. with a man<BR>परपुरुषं संगच्छति (गम्, c. 1), with a woman<BR>परस्त्रीं भजते-ति (मज्, c. 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adumbrate
ADUMBRATE (v. t.): प्रतिच्छायां करोति (कृ,<BR>c. 8) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adumbration
ADUMBRATION: i. e. the sketch: प्रतिच्छाया (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adust
ADUST:<BR>(1) दग्धः (ग्धा, ग्धं);<BR>(2) शुष्कः (ष्का,<BR> ष्कं): v. Parched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advance
ADVANCE (v. i.):<BR>I To move forward:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रयाति,<BR>the chariot a. d towards Kṛṣṇa<BR>अभिशौरि<BR> रथः प्रययौ, Si. xx. 2.;<BR>(2) उच्चलति (चल्, c. 1),<BR>I a. d three or four steps<BR>त्रिचतुराणि पदान्युदचलम्,<BR>D. ii.;<BR>(3) अभि-याति (या, c, 2), अभ्या-गच्छति<BR>(गम्, c. 1), etc. (with acc.),<BR>at once a. d<BR>against the lords of the quarters<BR>सपदि ककुभामीशान-<BR>मभ्यागमत्, Ku. xvi. 50.;<BR>(4) अभिमुखं याति, व्रजति,<BR>etc.,<BR>should a. against the enemy<BR>द्विषतोऽभिमुखं<BR> व्रजेत्, Ka. xviii. 2. Ph.<BR>the day has a. d<BR>दूरमधि-<BR>रुढः सविता Sa. iv.<BR>II To make progress:<BR>q. v.: Ph. with his age, he a. d in knowledge<BR>वयसा सह ञ्जानमस्य ववृधे। Ph.: of a. d age:<BR>(1)<BR>गतवयस्, H. ;<BR>(2) गलितवयस्, R.;<BR>(3) परिणत-<BR>वयस्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advance
ADVANCE (v. t.):<BR>I To bring forward<BR>अभिमुखं चालयति (c. of चल्)<BR>or<BR>नयति (नी,<BR>c. 1.)<BR>II To promote, forward: q. v.:<BR>वर्द्धयति (c. of वृध्)<BR>III To offer or propose (as<BR>an opinion): q. v.<BR>IV To pay before-<BR>-hand: Ph.<BR>a. d 500 rupees for the bridge<BR>*सेतु-<BR>बन्धनार्थं पञ्चशतरूप्यमुद्राः प्रागेव दत्तवान्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advance
ADVANCE (subs):<BR>I Onward movement:<BR>(1) प्रयाणम्। v. Going;<BR>(2) आगमनम्। v. Coming.<BR>II Progress, improvement: q. v.: उन्नतिः।<BR>III Increase of price:. वृद्धिः।<BR>IV A<BR>paying beforehand: अग्रिमदानम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advanced-guard
ADVANCED-GUARD: नासीरचराः (m. pl.) (after<BR>Vi.) and sim. comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advancement
ADVANCEMENT:<BR>(1) उन्नतिः।<BR>(2) अभ्युदयः: v.<BR>Promotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advantage
ADVANTAGE (subs)<BR>I Benefit:<BR>(1) हितम् (=good<BR>q. v.),<BR>for whose a.<BR>कस्य हिताय;<BR>(2) लाभः<BR>(=profit, q. v.),<BR>what a. will you derive<BR>*तव<BR> को लाभो भविष्यति;<BR>(3) गुणः = merit, q. v.). they [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">Page014</a>]<BR>do not know the a. s of riding<BR>*अश्वारोहणतुणान्न<BR> जानन्ति।<BR>II Opportunity: q. v.: अवसरः।<BR>III<BR>Superiority: Ph.<BR>the enemy had the a. of<BR>us in number<BR>शत्रूणां संख्यास्मदधिकासीत्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advantage
ADVANTAGE (v. t.): उपकरोति (कृ, c. 8): v.<BR>To profit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advantageous
ADVANTAGEOUS:<BR>(1) हितकर: (री, रं): v.<BR>Beneficial;<BR>(2) लाभावहः (हा, हं) v. Profit-<BR>-able;<BR>(3) अर्थकरः (री, रं) (=enriching) To<BR>be a.: v. To advantage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advantageously
ADVANTAGEOUSLY:<BR>I Profitably: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Conveniently: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advent
ADVENT: आगमनम्: v. Arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adventitious
ADVENTITIOUS:<BR>(1) आहार्यः (र्या, र्यं);<BR>(2)<BR>आगन्तुकः (की, कं);<BR>(3) बाह्यः (ह्या, ह्यं)<BR>(=external: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adventure
ADVENTURE:<BR>I Risk, hazard: q. v.<BR>II A<BR>remarkable achievement:<BR>(1) अद्भुतं कर्म,<BR>although a boy, Rama is celebrated for his<BR>a. s<BR>रामः कर्मभिरद्भुतैः शिशुरपि ख्यातः, Vi. iii.;<BR>(2) चरितम्, (=the sum total of one's a. s)<BR>the a. s of the ten princes<BR>दशकुमारचरितम्।<BR>III<BR>Accident: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adventure
ADVENTURE: v. To venture, dare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adventurer
ADVENTURER: साहसिकः (की, कं). A military<BR>a.: v. Freebooter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adventurous
ADVENTUROUS: साहसिकः (की, कं): v. Bold,<BR>rash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adverb
ADVERB: क्रियाविशेषणम्। Ajal: *क्रियाविशेषकः<BR>(का, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adversary
ADVERSARY:<BR>(1) वैरिन् (m);<BR>(2) विपक्षः v.<BR>Opponent, enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adversative
ADVERSATIVE: *विरोधसूचकमव्ययम् यथा — ‘तु’, ‘तथाच’।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adverse
ADVERSE:<BR>(1) प्रतिकूलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) विपक्षः<BR>(क्षा, क्षं): v. Inimical, hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adversity
ADVERSITY:<BR>(1) विपद् (f);<BR>(2) आपद् (f): v.<BR>Calamity, misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advert to
ADVERT TO:<BR>(1) उदाहरति (हृ, c. 1.):<BR>if in<BR>course of conversation, people were to a. your<BR>name<BR>कथाप्रसङ्गे न जनैरुदाहृतात् तवाभिधानात्, Ki. i.<BR>24;<BR>(2) उत्-लिखति (लिख्, c. 6): v. To<BR>notice, allude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advertence
ADVERTENCE: अवधानम्: v. Attention, notice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advertise
ADVERTISE (v. t.):<BR>I To inform: q. v.: ञ्जपयति<BR>(c. of ञ्जा).<BR>II To publish a notice of:<BR>(1)<BR>*वि-ञ्जापयति (c. of ञ्जा);<BR>(2) *धोपयति (धुष्,<BR>c. 10): Ph.<BR>a. d a horse for sale in the Soma<BR>Prakasa<BR>*विक्रेयो घोटक इति सोमप्रकाशपत्रिकायां विञ्जा-<BR>पयामास।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advertisement
ADVERTISEMENT:<BR>I Information: q. v. A<BR>public notice:<BR>(1) *विज्ञापनम्;<BR>(2) घोषणा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advertiser
ADVERTISER: *घोषकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advice
ADVICE:<BR>I Counsel:<BR>(1) उपदेशः;<BR>(2) शासनम्;<BR>(3) अनुशासनम्। To give a. may be expr. by<BR>शास्ति etc.:<BR>what sort of friend is he who does<BR>not give good a. to his master<BR>स किंसखा साधु न<BR> शास्ति योऽधिपम्, Ki. i. 5: v. To advise.<BR>II<BR>Intelligence: q. v. संवादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advisable
ADVISABLE: युक्तः (क्ता, क्तं) B. xii. 15. v. Pru-<BR>-dent, expedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advisability
ADVISABILITY: औचित्यम्: v. Expediency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advise
ADVISE (v. t.)<BR>I To give advise:<BR>(1) उप-<BR>दिशति (दिश्, c. 6). there is nothing to a. you<BR>ते नाल्पमप्युपदेष्टव्यमस्ति, K. ;<BR>(2) शास्ति, अनु-,<BR>(शास्, c. 2),<BR>a. me what is to be done with<BR>this wealth<BR>किं विधेयमनयार्थसम्पदा, शाधि॥॥मां, Si.<BR>xiv. 11. N. B. These verbs may take two<BR>acc. s.<BR>II To inform: q. v.: ञ्जापयति (c. of ञ्जा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advisedly
ADVISEDLY: v. Designedly, purposely. Ph.<BR>a. cruel<BR>प्रतिपत्तिनिष्टुरः, R. viii. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adviser
ADVISER:<BR>(1) उपदेष्टृ (m);<BR>(2) उपदेशकः;<BR>(3)<BR>शासकः (rare in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advocacy
ADVOCACY: No equiv.: *अभिभाषणम्: v. Defence,<BR>vindication, recommendation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advocate
ADVOCATE (v.): *अभिभाषते (भाष्, c. 1): v. To<BR>plead, defend, vindicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advocate
ADVOCATE (subs):<BR>I A pleader: *अभिभाषकः;<BR> उकिलः:<BR>II. A. defender, vindicator: q. v.<BR>*अभिभाषकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advowee
ADVOWEE: *धर्मवृत्तिदः (दा, दं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advowson
ADVOWSON: *धर्मवृत्तिदानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adze
ADZE:<BR>(1) वासिः (m)<BR>or<BR>वासी (f);<BR>(2) तक्षणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aerial
AERIAL:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) वायवः (वी, वं);<BR>(2) वायु-<BR>सम्भवः (वा, वं) (=produced in the air);<BR>(3)<BR>वैहायसः (=through the air). Ph. a. flight:<BR>(1) नभोगतिः;<BR>(2) वियदुत्पतनं;<BR>a. spirit<BR>नभश्चरः [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">Page015</a>]<BR>(री, रं). —<BR>II Fig.: lofty: व्योमस्पृश् (mfn)<BR>and sim. comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aerie
AERIE:<BR>(1) कुलायः;<BR>(2) नीडः: v. Nest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aerolite
AEROLITE: Perh. गण्डशैलः; *वायूपलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aeromancy
AEROMANCY: *वायुगत्या भविष्यशुभाशुभकथनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aerometer
AEROMETER: *भारमापः; वाय्वादीनां भारमापकयन्त्र-<BR>विशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aeronaut
AERONAUT: विमानयातृ (f. त्री); नभश्चरः (री, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aesthetics
AESTHETICS: *रुचिविञ्जानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afar
AFAR: दूरात् (from a.)<BR>A. off<BR>दूरस्थः (स्था, स्थं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affability
AFFABILITY:<BR>(1) मधुरालापता;<BR>(2) मिष्टभाषिता;<BR>(3) सौजन्यम्;<BR>(4) प्रश्रयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affable
AFFABLE:<BR>(1) मधुरालापः (पा, पं);<BR>(2) मिष्टमाषिन्<BR>(f. णी): v. Courteous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affably
AFFABLY:<BR>(1) सौजन्येन;<BR>(2) प्रश्रयेण: v. Courte-<BR>-ously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affair
AFFAIR: कार्यम्,<BR>state a. s<BR>राजकार्याणिः v. Business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affect
AFFECT (v. t.):<BR>I To act upon, influence^1: Ph.<BR>I am a. ed with pain in the feet<BR>मम पादयोः पीडा<BR> सञ्जाता;<BR>as if a. ed with devil<BR>पिशाचोपहतमिव।<BR>II Of feeling Ph.<BR>a. ed with sorrow<BR>शोकामि-<BR>भूतः (ता, तं);<BR>a. ed with joy<BR>हर्षाकुलः (ला, लं);<BR>a. ed with those lamentations<BR>आहतस्तैः परिदेविताक्षरैः;<BR>his speech did not a. the audience<BR>*तस्योक्तिः श्रोतृ-<BR>वर्गहृदयानिन जग्राह<BR>or<BR>श्रोतृवर्गहृदयेष्ववकाशं न लेभे<BR>III<BR>To aspire to, aim at: q. v.<BR>IV To love:<BR>q. v. V. To concern: q. v.<BR>VI To make a<BR>mere show of. Ph.<BR>a. ing quarrel<BR>कृतककलहं कृत्वा,<BR>Mu. iii.;<BR>a. ing anger<BR>सकृतककोपं Sa. i.: v.<BR>To feign.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affected
AFFECTED:<BR>I Assumed:<BR>(1) कृतकः (का, कं),<BR>restraining his a. anger<BR>कृतकं कोपं संहृत्य, Mu. iii.;<BR>(2) कृत्रिमः (मा, मं),<BR>un-a. love<BR>अकृत्रिमं प्रेम, Ki.<BR>iii. 37.: v. False, feigned.<BR>II Moved<BR>(1) तरलः (ला, लं), I am a. by your manners<BR>तावकैरनुभावैस्तरलाः स्मः, N. v. 24;<BR>(2) गलितः<BR>(ता, तं) (=melted): v. To affect (II)<BR>III Unnatural and offensive: Perh. कृतकः<BR>(का, कं): v. Unnatural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affectedly
AFFECTEDLY:<BR>(1) By the adj: v. Affected;<BR>(2) साटोपं (=boastfully)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affecting
AFFECTING (adj.): करुणः (णा, णं) (=pathetic,<BR>q. v.): v. To affect (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affectingly
AFFECTINGLY: करुणम्<BR>spoke a.<BR>करुणमभिहितम्, K. x.<BR>58: v. Pathetically.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affection
AFFECTION:<BR>I Love:<BR>(1) स्नेहः;<BR>(2) अनुरागः;<BR>(3) प्रणयः (conjugal or friendly a.);<BR>(4)<BR>प्रेमन् (n) v. Love;<BR>(5) वात्सल्यम् (parental a.);<BR>(6) हार्दम् (rare). N. B. Note that these words<BR>agree with the loc.:<BR>I said I feel a. for this<BR>child as for my own<BR>औरस इवास्मिन् वत्से वत्सलतेति<BR> मया विज्ञापितः, D. iii.<BR>II An attribute or<BR>property: Ph.<BR>a. s of the mind<BR>मनोवृत्तयः;<BR>a. s<BR>of bodies<BR>शारीरधर्माः।<BR>III Disease: q. v.: Ph.<BR>remover of all rheumatic a. s<BR>सर्ववातविकारनुत्, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affectionate
AFFECTIONATE:<BR>(1) स्निग्धः (ग्धा, ग्धं);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रणयिन् (f. नी),<BR>a. heart<BR>प्रणयि हृदयम् Me. i. 10;<BR>(3) वत्सलः (ला, लं) (applied to parents);<BR>(4) भक्तिमत् (f. ती) (of dutiful affection<BR>towards parents and elder relatives);<BR>(5)<BR>प्रेमपरः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affectionately
AFFECTIONATELY:<BR>(1) स्निग्धभ्;<BR>(2) सानुरागम्;<BR>(3) प्रीत्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affectionateness
AFFECTIONATENESS: स्निग्धता: v. Affection<BR>(1)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affiance
AFFIANCE (subs):<BR>I Marriage contract:<BR>(1)<BR>विवाहसम्बन्धः;<BR>(2) वाग्दानं (only of the female<BR>by her guardian).<BR>II Trust, confidence:<BR>q. v. विश्वासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affiance
AFFIANCE (v. t.):<BR>I To betroth: q. v. प्रति-<BR>शृणोति (श्रु, c. 5),<BR>a. d to me<BR>मह्यं प्रतिश्रुता।<BR>II<BR>To trust, confide: q. v.: विश्वसिति (श्वस्,<BR>c. 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affidavit
AFFIDAVIT: *शपथपूर्वा विञ्जप्तिः: Ph.<BR>he made an a.<BR>that he is a bachelor<BR>*अकृतोद्वाहोऽस्मीति शपथपूर्वकं<BR> विज्ञापयामास।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affiliate
AFFILIATE:<BR>I To adopt: q. v.<BR>II.: To ally;<BR>q. v.<BR>III To receive into a society: Ph.<BR>a. d to the Calcutta University<BR>*कलिकाताविश्वविद्या-<BR>लयसंशिलष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affiliation
AFFILIATION:<BR>I Adoption: q. v.<BR>II Filia-<BR>-tion: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affinity
AFFINITY: सम्बन्धः (general and matrimonial):<BR>v. Relative, connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affirm
AFFIRM:<BR>I To assert positively: वदति (वद्,<BR>c. 1): v. To assert.<BR>II To confirm,<BR>establish: q. v.: द्रढयति (nomi).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affirmant
AFFIRMANT: वादिन् (f. नी): v. Asserter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affirmation
AFFIRMATION:<BR>I Assertion: q. v.: उक्तिः।<BR>II Confirmation, establishment: q. v.:<BR>Ph.<BR>on solemn a.<BR>प्रतिज्ञापूर्वकम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affirmative
AFFIRMATIVE (adj.):<BR>I Declaratory of what<BR>exists अस्तित्वसूचकः (का, कं)<BR>II Expressing<BR>assent स्वीकारसूचकः (का, कं)<BR>III Confirma-<BR>-tive: v. To confirm, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affirmative
AFFIRMATIVE (subs).: Ph.<BR>‘yes’ is an a.<BR>अथ किं<BR> स्वीकारे;<BR>one maintains the a., the other the<BR>negative<BR>एकोऽस्तित्वमपरो नास्तित्वं ब्रवीति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affix
AFFIX: प्रत्ययः:<BR>a. to verbs<BR>कृत्;<BR>a. to nouns<BR>तद्धितः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afflict
AFFLICT:<BR>(1) पीडयति (पीड्, c. 10);<BR>(2) क्लिश्नाति<BR>(क्लिश्, c. 9);<BR>(3) अर्दति (अर्द्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

