affluent
AFFLUENT: समृद्धः (द्धा, द्धं): v. Opulent, rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afflux
AFFLUX: प्रवाहः (?): v. Flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afford
AFFORD:<BR>I To give, yield, supply: q. v.:<BR>ददाति (दा, c. 3)<BR>II To be able to sell or<BR>expend without imprudence: Ph.<BR>he can a. to<BR>keep four servants<BR>*स चतुरो भृत्यान् रक्षितुं शक्नोति;<BR>he can a. to spend 500 Rs. a day<BR>*स प्रत्यहमक्लेशेन<BR> पञ्चशतरूप्यमुद्रा व्ययितुं समर्थः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affray
AFFRAY:<BR>(1) द्वन्द्वम्;<BR>(2) कलहः;<BR>(3) डिम्बः;<BR>(4) डमरः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affright
AFFRIGHT (v.):<BR>(1) मीषयते (c. of भी);<BR>(2)<BR>त्रासयति (c. of त्रस्): v. To frighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affright
AFFRIGHT (subs).:<BR>(1) त्रासः;<BR>(2) साध्वसम्: v.<BR>fear, terror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affront
AFFRONT (v. t.): अवमन्यते (मन्, c. 4): v. To<BR>insult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affront
AFFRONT (subs).:<BR>(1) अपमानम्:;<BR>(2) अवमाननाः<BR>v. Insult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affuse
AFFUSE (v. t.): सिञ्चति, नि-, (सिच्, c. 6):<BR>v. To pour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affusion
AFFUSION:<BR>(1) सेकः;<BR>(2) निषेकः;<BR>(3) अभिषेकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afloat
AFLOAT: प्लवमानः (ना, नं), or by the verb;<BR>I<BR>was a. for the day and the whole night<BR>तावदप्लोषि<BR> यावदपासरद्वासरः शर्वरी च सर्वा, D. vi. Fig.:<BR>the<BR>rumour is a.<BR>बहुलीभूतोऽयमर्थः, Sa. vi.: v. To<BR>get abroad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afoot
AFOOT (adv.):<BR>I Lit.: पद्भयाम्,<BR>did she go a. on<BR>in a carriage<BR>किमसौ पद्भयां गता उत प्रवहणेन ? Mr.<BR>ix.<BR>II FIG., in action: प्रारब्धः (ब्धा, ब्धं),<BR>good men do not abandon what is set a.<BR>प्रारब्घमु-<BR>त्तमगुणा न परित्यजन्ति, P: v. To begin, under-<BR>-take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aforegoing
AFOREGOING: v. Foregoing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aforementioned
AFOREMENTIONED, AFORENAMED, AFORESAID:<BR>(1) पूर्वोक्तः (क्ता, क्तं);<BR>(2) प्रागुक्तः (क्ता,<BR> क्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aforetime
AFORETIME:<BR>(1) पुरा;<BR>(2) पूर्वकाले v. Formerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afraid
AFRAID:<BR>(1) भीतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) शङ्कितः (ता, तं):<BR>v. Fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afraid
AFRAID, BE:<BR>(1) बिभेति (भी, c. 3) (with<BR>abl.): I am a. to allow girls to live publicly<BR>बिभेमि कन्यकानां प्रकाशावस्थानात्, D. iv.: v. To<BR>fear;<BR>(2) शङ्कते (with acc.): v. To appre-<BR>-hend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afresh
AFRESH:<BR>(1) पुनर्;<BR>(2) पुनरपि: v. Again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aft
AFT:<BR>I subs: *(नावः) पश्चाद्भागः<BR>II Adv.:<BR>v. Abaft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after
AFTER (prep.):<BR>I Behind: q. v.: अनु<BR>(with acc.):<BR>to go a.<BR>अनुगच्छति;<BR>to run a.<BR>अनु-<BR>द्रवति।<BR>II At a later time:<BR>(1) By abl.:<BR>seen<BR>a. a long time<BR>बहोर्दृष्टं कालात्, U. ii. N. B. This<BR>const. is very rare;<BR>(2) अनन्तरं (with abl. or<BR>crude base):<BR>a. his father<BR>पितुरनन्तरं, R. ix.<BR>1.;<BR>a. 16 years<BR>षोडशवर्षानन्तरं, D.;<BR>just a. his<BR>order<BR>वचनान्तरमेव, K.;<BR>(3) परं (with abl.):<BR>a.<BR>childhood<BR>बाल्यात् परं Ku. i. 31.;<BR>(4) ऊर्द्धम्<BR>(with abl.)<BR>a. childbirth<BR>ऊर्द्धं प्रसूतेः, R. xiv. 66;<BR>(5) अर्वाक् (with abl.) (rare);<BR>(6) When<BR>time is specified, by loc. or loc. absolute<BR>of words signifying motion:<BR>a. the rainy<BR>season<BR>अतीते वर्षुके काले, B. vii. 18.;<BR>a. a few<BR>days<BR>कतिपयदिवसावगमे, K.; ततो गतेषु कतिपयदिनेषु,<BR>D. (N. B. note that इतः (=from this time)<BR>and ततः (=from that time) are sometimes<BR>prefixed in such cases for the sake of<BR>precision);<BR>(7) Sometimes by part. s:<BR>a.<BR>bathing with the water of the cascade<BR>निर्भरजल-<BR>निवर्तितस्नानविधिः, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">Page017</a>] K.<BR>III. In an inferior<BR>degree to: अनु (with acc.):<BR>a. the acquisi-<BR>tion of friends<BR>मित्रलाभमनु, Ki. xiii. 53.<BR>IV In<BR>imitation of:<BR>(1) अनु (with acc.), every<BR>thing yours is a. me, but you do not feel the<BR>pain of separation from your beloved (wife) सर्वं<BR> मामनु ते प्रियाविरहजां त्वं तु व्यथां मानुभूः, V. iv.;<BR>(2) अनुरूपः (पा, पं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after
AFTER (adj.):<BR>I Subsequent, succeeding,<BR>later: q. v.<BR>II More aft.: Ph.<BR>the a.<BR>sails<BR>*पश्चाद्भागस्थानि वायुवसनानि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after
AFTER (adv.): of time: पश्चात्:<BR>soon a.<BR>किञ्चि-<BR>त्पश्चात्, Me. i. 10.;<BR>long a.<BR>चिरात्, Ra. iv.;<BR>how long a.<BR>कियच्चिरेण, Sa. vi. For phrases<BR>like many years a. (=a. many years):<BR>v. After (prep.) (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-ages
AFTER-AGES: आयतिः (?) v. Posterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-noon
AFTER-NOON (subs):<BR>(1) पराह्णः;<BR>(2) उपराह्णः;<BR>(3) वैकालः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-noon
AFTER-NOON (adj.):<BR>(1) अपराह्वतनः (नी, नं);<BR>(2) आपराह्विकः (की, कं);<BR>(3) वैकालिकः (की, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-pains
AFTER-PAINS: प्रसववेदना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-piece
AFTER-PIECE: *उपरूपकम्, *अनुनाटकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-thought
AFTER-THOUGHT:<BR>(1) अनुबोघः:<BR>(2) उत्तरचिन्ता (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afterwards
AFTERWARDS:<BR>(1) पश्चात्;<BR>(2) परेण (rare): v.<BR>After (adv.), then, thereupon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

again
AGAIN (adv.):<BR>I Once more;<BR>(1) पुनर्;<BR>(2)<BR>भूयस्;<BR>(3) पुनरपि। a. and a.:<BR>(1) पुनःपुनः;<BR>(2)<BR>भूयोभूयः;<BR>(3) वारंवारं;<BR>(4) असकृत्।<BR>II Moreover:<BR>q. v. अन्यच्च Ph.: sleeping never to wake a.<BR>अप्रतिबोघशायिन् (f. नी), R. viii. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

against
AGAINST:<BR>I Abreast of, facing:<BR>(1) प्रति-,<BR>a. the hostile army<BR>प्रत्यरिसैन्यं, R. vii. 55.;<BR>a. the wind<BR>प्रत्यनिलं, Ku. iii. 31.;<BR>(2) Comp.<BR>with अभि (rare),<BR>a. the enemy<BR>अभ्यमित्रं, Ki. xvi.<BR>5.;<BR>(3) अभिमुखं (in comp. or with gen.)<BR>should advance a. the enemy<BR>द्विषतोभिमुखं व्रजेत् Ka.<BR>xviii. 2.<BR>II In opposition to: Ph. (subjects)<BR>should not act a. their king<BR>राजन्यविरुद्धाभिर्वृत्तिभिर्व-<BR>तिंतव्यम् Mu. i.; I have never acted a. yours wishes<BR>प्रतिकूलं न च ते मया कृतम्; Ku. ii. 7.;<BR>if she, a.<BR>her caste.....<BR>यदियमतिक्रम्य स्वकुलघर्मम्, D. ii.<BR>III<BR>In provision for: Ph.<BR>a. misfortune<BR>आपदर्थे,<BR>H.<BR>IV. Upon: q. v.; v. also the verbs to<BR>which it is joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

agape
AGAPE: जृम्भमानः (ना, नं): v. Gaping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

agaric
AGARIC: v. Mushroom, touchwood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

agate
AGATE: शवलमणिविशेषः Perh. गोमेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

age
AGE:<BR>I Time of life:<BR>(1) वयस्,<BR>and what is his<BR>a.<BR>कियद्वा वयः, K. ;<BR>of the same a.<BR>सवयस्, (mfn.),<BR>R. v. 65.;<BR>of advanced a.<BR>गलितवयस् (mfn.)<BR>(poet.) R. iii. 70.; your majesty is still of a.<BR>वयःस्थ एव प्रभुः, Sa. vi.;<BR>(2) आयुस् (=the whole<BR>term of one's life):<BR>when the king passed the<BR>61st year of his a.<BR>एकषष्टिमतिक्रम्य वर्षान् भूपतिरायुषः,<BR>Raj.<BR>II An epoch: q. v. युगम् the golden a.<BR>(1) कृतयुगम्;<BR>(2) सत्ययुगम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

age
AGE, OF:<BR>(1) comp. with वर्ष, वत्सर, etc.:<BR>thir-<BR>teen years of a.<BR>त्रयोदशवर्षः (र्षा, र्षं) D. iii.;<BR>one who has completed twenty years<BR>पूर्णविंशतिवर्षः<BR>(र्षा, र्षं,) M. ii. 212.;<BR>(2) comp. with वर्षीयः<BR>(या, यं) etc.:<BR>twenty years of a.<BR>विंशतिवर्षींयः<BR>(या, यं), H. iv.;<BR>(3) comp. with वयस्कः<BR>(स्का, स्कं): v. Aged (II): Ph.<BR>about 18 years<BR>of a.<BR>अष्टादशवर्षदेशीयः (या, यं), D. vi.;<BR>below<BR>two years<BR>ऊनद्विवार्षिकः (की, कं), M. v. 68.:<BR>above 90 years of a.<BR>नवत्यधिकवयस् (mfn.), K. b.;<BR>who has not reached 25th. year of his a.<BR>अप्राप्त-<BR>पञ्चविंशतिम् Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

