anarchy
ANARCHY:<BR>(1) राज्यविप्लवः;<BR>(2) प्रजाविप्लवः, Vi. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anathema
ANATHEMA:<BR>(1) शापः (?);<BR>(2) अभिशापः (?) v.<BR>Curse, excommunication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anathematize
ANATHEMATIZE: शपति, अभि-, (शप्, c. 1): v.<BR>To curse, excommunicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anatomical
ANATOMICAL:<BR>(1) व्यवच्छेदविद्याविषयकः (का, कं);<BR>(2) by tat. comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anatomist
ANATOMIST: *व्यवच्छेदविद्याविशारदः<BR>or.<BR>-कुशलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anatomize
ANATOMIZE: व्यवच्छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7): v. To<BR>dissect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anatomy
ANATOMY: *व्यवच्छेदविद्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ancestor
ANCESTOR: पूर्वपुरुषः, In. pl.:<BR>(1) पूर्वपुरुषः;<BR>(2)<BR>पूर्वजाः;<BR>(3) पितरः;<BR>(4) पूर्वे,<BR>I have excelled<BR>my c. s<BR>पूर्वे तिरस्कारिताः, Vi. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ancestral
ANCESTRAL: पितृपैतामहः (ही, हं) P. v. Paternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ancestry
ANCESTRY:<BR>I Ancestors: q. v.<BR>II Birth, or<BR>honourable descent:<BR>(1) अन्वयः;<BR>(2) वंशः।<BR>Ph.: of good or noble a.:<BR>(1) अभिजातः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) अभिजनवत् (f. ती) Sa. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anchor
ANCHOR (subs): नौबन्धनलौहयन्त्रभेदः; *लङगरम्।<BR>Ph.<BR>the arms of an a.,<BR>*लङ्गरदन्ताः (m. pl.):<BR>the eye of an a.<BR>*लङ्गरच्छिद्रम;<BR>to cast a.<BR>*लङ्गरं<BR> प्रक्षिपति;<BR>to weigh a.<BR>लङ्गरम् उत्तोलयति (तुल्, c. 10.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anchor
ANCHOR (v.): लङ्गरं प्रक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.) (with<BR>gen.)<BR>a. ed off Benares<BR>*उपवाराणसि लङ्गरं प्रचिक्षेप,<BR>or<BR>लङ्गरेण नावं बबन्ध।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anchorage
ANCHORAGE:<BR>I The place: *लङ्गरस्थानम्।<BR>II The duty: *लङ्गरशुल्कम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anchorite
ANCHORITE:<BR>(1) यतिः;<BR>(2) सन्न्पासिन् (m). v.<BR>Hermit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anchovy
ANCHOVY: *हेरिंजातीयः क्षुद्रमत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ancient
ANCIENT (adj.):<BR>(1) पुराणः (णा, णं);<BR>(2) पुरातनः<BR>(नी, नं);<BR>(3) प्राचीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(4) चिरन्तनः (नी, नं);<BR>(5) प्राक्कालीनः (नी, नं);<BR>(6) पूर्वकालीनः (ना, नं):<BR>(7) प्राक्कालीनः (ना, नं): v. Old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ancient
ANCIENT (subs):<BR>I Flag: q. v.: पताका।<BR>II An ensign: q. v.: पताकिन् (f. नी)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anciently
ANCIENTLY:<BR>(1) पूर्वकाले;<BR>(2) पुरा। v. Formerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ancient
ANCIENT, THE:<BR>(1) वृद्धा (m. pl.), U. v.;<BR>(2)<BR>चिरन्तनाः (m. pl.), S. : v. Antiquity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ancillary
ANCILLARY: v. Supplemental.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

and
AND:<BR>I In case of subs. and adj. s: (a) by dva.<BR>comp.:<BR>summer a. spring<BR>ग्रीष्मवसन्तौ;<BR>father a.<BR>mother<BR>मातापितरौ; or, sim. पितरौ [so brother a.<BR>sister भ्राररौ;<BR>son a. daughter<BR>पुत्रौ;<BR>father-in-<BR>law a. mother-in-law<BR>श्वशुरौ];<BR>with his superior<BR>birth, asceticism, erudition, valour a. deeds<BR>अमिजन-<BR>तपोविद्याक्रियातिशयैर्निजैः, Vi. ii.; exhausted, tremu- [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=027" target="_blank">Page027</a>]<BR>-lous, and (therefore)<BR>pleasant<BR>अलसललितमुग्धानि,<BR>U. i.;<BR>(6) by च (enclitic):<BR>fresh youth, in-<BR>comparable beauty, a. superhuman prowess<BR>अभिनव-<BR>यौवनत्वमप्रतिमरूपत्वममानुषशक्तित्वं च, K.<BR>II. In<BR>case of numerals:<BR>(1) By a comp. with<BR>अधिकः (का, कं),<BR>or<BR>उत्तरः (रा, रं):<BR>one hundred a.<BR>two<BR>द्वधिकं शतं or sim., द्ववाधिकशतं:<BR>three thousand<BR>a. sixty-eight<BR>अष्टषष्टयु त्तरत्रिसहस्रं;<BR>(2) By a<BR>comp. with स-,:<BR>after a reign of 18 years a.<BR>thirteen days<BR>सोऽष्टादशाब्दान् क्षमां भुक्त्वा सत्रयोदश-<BR>वासरान्, Raj.;<BR>(3) by च (very rare), Vi.<BR>III<BR>In case of verbs, generally by participles:<BR>go a. speak this to the minister<BR>गत्वैवममात्यं ब्रू हि,<BR>Sa. vi.; then he alighted (from the horse)<BR>a.<BR>tied it up to a. branch of a tree, a. then approached<BR>a. saluted Śiva a. then again gazed on the same<BR>lady<BR>ततोऽवतीर्य तरुशाखायां बद्ध्वा तुरगमुपसृत्य प्रणम्य<BR> त्रिलोचनाय तामेव योषितं चक्षुषा पुनर्निरूपयामास, K. v.<BR>(iv).<BR>IV In connecting sentences:<BR>(1)<BR>By च (never at the beginning): (these remem-<BR>brances)<BR>burn my body a. rend my heart<BR>देहं<BR> दहन्ति हृदयं च विदारयन्ति; Ma. x.;<BR>(2) Some-<BR>-times च is omitted^1:<BR>behave so that you will not<BR>be laughed at by men, will not be censured by the<BR>good, will not be reviled by the seniors<BR>तथा<BR> प्रयतेथाः यथा नोपहस्यसे जनैः, न निन्दासे साधुभिः, न<BR> धिक्क्रियसे गुरूभिः, K.<BR>V. In Interrogation,<BR>generally by वा (enclitic):<BR>who is he,<BR>whose son, a. what is his name ?<BR>कोऽसौ, कस्य<BR> वापत्यं किमभिधानो वा? K. ;<BR>O. fair lady, who<BR>are you, whose spouse, a. what is your object for<BR>coming to me ?<BR>का त्वं शुभे कस्य परिग्रहो वा किं वा<BR> मदभ्यागमनकारणं ते, R. xiv. 8.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

and then
AND THEN: denoting immediate sequence:<BR>(1) तदनु<BR>in childhood a. then again in youth<BR>शैशवे<BR> तदनु, यौवने पुनः U. i.;<BR>(2) ततः,<BR>a. then allowed<BR>his son to go<BR>ततोऽनुज्ञे गमनं सुतस्य B. i. 23.;<BR>(3)<BR>तदनु च (very rare), Vi. ii. v. and (III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

and yet
AND YET: तथापि: v. YET.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

androgynal
ANDROGYNAL, ANDROGYNOUS (adj.): v.<BR>Hermaphrodite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anecdote
ANECDOTE:<BR>(1) कथा;<BR>(2) उपाख्यानम्: v. Story<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aneurism
ANEURISM: Perh. नाडीब्रणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anew
ANEW:<BR>(1) पुनर्;<BR>(2) पुनरपि: v. Again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

angel
ANGEL:<BR>I Lit.: देवदूतः; गन्धर्वः।<BR>II Fig:<BR>as a term of endearment:<BR>(1) प्रियतमा;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रेयसीः v. Love, darling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

angel
ANGEL, ANGELIC (adj.):<BR>I Belonging to<BR>angels: by tat. comp.<BR>II Resembling<BR>angels:<BR>(1) दिव्यः (व्या, व्यं);<BR>(2) अमानुषः<BR>(षी, सं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anger
ANGER (subs):<BR>(1) क्रोधः;<BR>(2) कोपः,<BR>to give<BR>way to a.<BR>कोपवशं गच्छति, V. iv.;<BR>restraining<BR>his a.<BR>कोपं निगृह्गन्, B. xii. 81.;<BR>(3) रोषः;<BR>(4) अमर्षः,<BR>void of a.<BR>अमर्षशून्यः (न्या, न्यं), Ki. i.<BR>33.;<BR>(5) मन्युः deep-rooted^1 a. possessed (him)<BR>मन्युरभजदवगादतरः, Si. xv. 2.;<BR>(6) संरम्भः;<BR>(7)<BR>रूष्, (f.);<BR>(8) क्रुध् (f.);<BR>(9) रूषा।<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anger
