ANODYNE:<BR>(1) शूलघ्नः (घ्नी, घ्नं);<BR>(2) पीडाशमकः<BR>(का, कं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anoint
ANOINT:<BR>I To besmear; q. v.:<BR>(1) लिम्पति<BR>(लिप्, c. 6.),<BR>as if a. ing, as if filling my sense<BR>of smell,<BR>अनुलिम्पन्तमिव पूरयन्तमिव घ्राणोन्द्रियम्, K. ;<BR>(2) अनक्ति, अभि-, (अञ्ज्, c. 7.), Sa. v.;<BR>(3)<BR>दिग्धे (दिह् c. 2.)<BR>a. ed with nectar as well as<BR>poison<BR>दिग्धोऽमृतेन च विषेण च, Ma. 1.;<BR>(4)<BR>समालभते (लभ्, c. 1.),<BR>I will prepare auspicious<BR>ointments<BR>मङ्गलसमालम्भं विरचयामि, Sa. iv.<BR>II<BR>To consecrate by unction: अभिषिञ्चति (सिच्,<BR>c. 6.), B. iii. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anointer
ANOINTER: विलेपकः: v. To anoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anointing
ANOINTING (subs):<BR>(1) विलेपनम्;<BR>(2) अभ्यञ्जनम्;<BR>(3) समालम्भः;<BR>(4) अभिषेकः (=consecration).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anomalous
ANOMALOUS:<BR>(1) विधिविरुद्धः (द्धा, द्धं) (?);<BR>(2)<BR>अनियमपरः (रा, रं) (?);<BR>(3) अविधि (mfn.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anomaly
ANOMALY:<BR>(1) विघिविरोधः;<BR>(2) अविधिः (?);<BR>(3) अनियमः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anon
ANON:<BR>I Quickly, soon: q. v.: सपदि।<BR>II<BR>Again: q. v. Ph.<BR>ever and a.<BR>यदा तदाः v.<BR>Often, frequently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anonymous
ANONYMOUS:<BR>(1) *अनिर्दिष्टलेखकाभिधानः (ना,<BR> नं)<BR>(2) अदत्तप्रणेतृसंज्ञः (झा, ञ्जं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anonymously
ANONYMOUSLY:<BR>(1) *अनिर्दिष्टलेखकाभिधानम्;<BR>(2) *अदत्तप्रणेतृसंज्ञम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

another
ANOTHER:<BR>(1) अन्यः (न्या, न्यत्),<BR>it is impossible<BR>that one acts and a. enjoys<BR>न ह्ये तत् सम्भविष्यत्यन्यः<BR> करोत्यन्यो भुंक्त इति, D. s.:<BR>a. day<BR>अन्येद्युः;<BR>(2)<BR>परः (रा, रं),<BR>a.'s wife<BR>परस्त्री,<BR>a.'s property<BR>परस्वम्;<BR>(3) अपरः (रा, रं), a. dearer to you than myself<BR>मत्तःप्रियतरस्तवापरो जनः, K. ;<BR>(4) in some case by<BR>अन्तर affixed,<BR>took her to a. king<BR>राजान्तरं निनाय,<BR>R. vi. 26.: v. Different. N. B. Note that पर<BR>is gen. confined to comp. and अपर is gen.<BR>used with a qualifying subs. Note also that<BR>अन्य and अपर do not gen. mean a.'s in<BR>comp.: v. Another's.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

another
ANOTHER, One (reciprocal): v. One<BR>another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anothers
ANOTHER'S:<BR>(1) अन्यदीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) परकीयः<BR>(या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

answer
ANSWER (v. t.):<BR>I To reply:<BR>(1) कथयति<BR>(कथ्, c. 10.), (first)<BR>a. my these four questions<BR>and then drink water<BR>ममैतान् चतुरो प्रश्नान् कथयित्वा<BR> जलं पिव, Mah.;<BR>(2) ब्रवीति (ब्रू, c. 2.), if you do<BR>not a. my questions,<BR>I will eat you<BR>न चेद्वूवीषि<BR> प्रश्नानश्नामि त्वां, D. vi.;<BR>(3) उत्तरं ददाति (दा,<BR>c. 3.) (with gen.);<BR>(4) प्रतिलिखति ( =to<BR>write back, q. v.). N. B.<BR>(1) and<BR>(2) are not<BR>applicable to writing.<BR>II To refute: q. v.<BR>III To correspond to, suit: q. v.<BR>IV<BR>To pay: q. v. Ph: this will a. my object<BR>अनेन सफलसमोहितो भवामि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

answer
ANSWER (v. i.):<BR>I To make a reply: उत्तरं<BR> ददाति।<BR>II To speak in reply:<BR>(1) प्रतिवक्ति<BR>(वच्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) प्रतिवदति (वद्, c. 1.);<BR>(3)<BR>प्रतिभाषते (भाष्, c. 1.).<BR>III To render an<BR>account to: expressed by circumlo.:<BR>you<BR>will have to a. to your master for the sums<BR>received<BR>*त्वया यद्धनं लब्धं तस्य विशेषवृत्तान्तः स्वामिने<BR> निवेदयितव्यः।<BR>IV To serve for.: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

answer
ANSWER (subs):<BR>(1) उत्तरं;<BR>(2) प्रतिवचनम्;<BR>(3)<BR>प्रत्युक्तिः;<BR>(4) प्रतिवाक्यम्। N. B. The last three<BR>words are applicable only to speaking in<BR>reply, while the first उत्तरं is applicable also<BR>to legal replies and solutions of problems.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

answerable
ANSWERABLE:<BR>I Refutable: खण्डनीयः (या, यं).<BR>II Responsible, accountable: q. v.<BR>III<BR>Correspondent, proportionate, suited: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ant
ANT:<BR>(1) पिपीलिका (the common small red a.);<BR>(2) पिपीलिकः (a large black a.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ant-eater
ANT-EATER: पिपीलिकाखादको जन्तुभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antagonism
ANTAGONISM:<BR>(1) विरोधः;<BR>(2) प्रतिद्वन्द्वम्;<BR>(3) पर्य-<BR>वस्थानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antagonist
ANTAGONIST:<BR>(1) विरोधिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) प्रतिद्व-<BR>न्द्विन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) पर्यवस्थातृ (f. त्री): v.<BR>Opponent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antagonistic
ANTAGONISTIC: विरोधिन् (f. नी): v. Opposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antarctic
ANTARCTIC: *दक्षिणकेन्द्रीयः (या, यं). A. pole<BR>*दक्षिणकेन्द्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antecedent
ANTECEDENT (adj.): v. Prior, previous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antecedent
ANTECEDENT (subs): Ph.<BR>whose a. s are not<BR>known<BR>*यस्य पूर्वचरितमविज्ञातम्।<BR>II In logic:<BR>पूर्वपक्षः।<BR>III In gram.: *पूर्वसंज्ञा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antechamber
ANTECHAMBER: Perh. प्राग्वंशः; *उपशाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antedate
ANTEDATE: Ph.:<BR>he a. d the letter<BR>*अग्रिमदिवसं<BR> पत्रे सन्निवेशयामास।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antedeluvian
ANTEDELUVIAN: प्रलयपूर्वकालीनः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antelope
ANTELOPE:<BR>(1) कृष्णसारः (the black spotted a.);<BR>(2) ऋष्यः (the painted a.);<BR>(3) मृगः (f. गी)<BR>(the general term for a. s, deer etc.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antenna
ANTENNA: Of insects: Perh. शुण्डम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anterior
ANTERIOR:<BR>I Preceding in time: v. Prior,<BR>previous.<BR>II Befor in place: अग्रः: (ग्रा,<BR> ग्रं), the a. part (as of a month): अग्रभागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anthem
ANTHEM:<BR>(1) सूक्तम्;<BR>(2) स्तोत्रम्: v. Hymn,<BR>song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anther
ANTHER: *परागकोषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anthology
ANTHOLOGY: कुसुमसंग्रहः (Lit. and Fig.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anthonys fire
ANTHONY'S FIRE: उदर्दः: v. Erysipelas.:<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antibilious
ANTIBILIOUS: पित्तघ्नः (घ्नी, घ्नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antichrist
ANTICHRIST: The great adversary of Christ:<BR>*प्रतिकृष्टः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anticipate
ANTICIPATE (v. t.):<BR>I To foresee: Ph.<BR>old<BR>men can a. what is coming<BR>वृद्धबुद्धिरनागतं पश्यति<BR>Vi.;<BR>even a. ing his death<BR>तस्य भाविमरणं जानन्नपि।<BR>II To be before in doing: Ph.<BR>I a. d his<BR>designs by removing to London<BR>*तस्याशयं निरूप्य<BR> लण्डनमहं जगाम;<BR>Scipio a. d Hannibal in cross-<BR>ing the Po.<BR>*हेनिबालस्याभिप्रायं ज्ञात्वा सिपियः प्रागेव<BR> पोनदीमुत्ततार।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anticipation
ANTICIPATION: Expr. by circumlo.: v. To<BR>anticipate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antidote
ANTIDOTE:<BR>I Any remedy: q. v.: प्रतिकारः।<BR>II For poison: विषघ्नौषधम् etc. A dealer in<BR>a. s:<BR>(1) विषवैद्यः;<BR>(2) जाङ्गलिकः,<BR>(3) नरेन्द्रः।<BR>III For fever: ज्वरघ्नौषधम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antimony
ANTIMONY:<BR>(1) स्रोतोञ्जनम्;<BR>(2) कापोतम्;<BR>(3)<BR>सौविरम्;<BR>(4) यामुनम्। These words properly<BR>mean sulphuret of a.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antipathy
ANTIPATHY: विद्वेषः: Hatred, aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antiphrasis
ANTIPHRASIS: Nearest word निहतार्थत्वम्, Sah.<BR>vii.; *विपरीतार्थत्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antipodes
ANTIPODES:<BR>I The opposite part of the globe:<BR>*प्रतिलोमम्; भूगोलस्याधोभागम्।<BR>II Those who<BR>inhabit it: *प्रतिलोभा। Ph.<BR>the a. and those who<BR>live in other parts of the globe, live just as com-<BR>fortably as we do here<BR>अनाकुलास्तिर्यगधः स्थिताश्च<BR> तिष्ठन्ति ते तत्र वयं यथात्र, S. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antiquarian
ANTIQUARIAN (adj.): Ph.<BR>a. knowledge<BR>प्राक्काली-<BR>नविषयविज्ञानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antiquarian
ANTIQUARIAN, ANTIQUARY (subs): *प्राक्कालीन-<BR>विषयेषु पण्डितः, अभिज्ञः, etc. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antiquated
ANTIQUATED (adj.): अप्रचलितः (ता, तं): v.<BR>Obsolete, old-fashioned^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antique
ANTIQUE (adj.): प्राचीनः (ना, नं): v. Ancient,<BR>old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antique
ANTIQUE (subs):<BR>(1) प्राचीनद्रव्यम् (?);<BR>(2) पुराण-<BR>द्रव्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antiquity
ANTIQUITY:<BR>I The ancients:<BR>(1) वृद्धाः (m.<BR>pl.);<BR>(2) पूर्वे (m. pl.);<BR>(3) चिरन्तनाः (m. pl.);<BR>(4) प्राचीनाः<BR>or<BR>प्राचीनलोकाः (m. pl.) etc.<BR>II<BR>The ancient time:<BR>(1) प्राक्कालः;<BR>(2) पूर्व-<BR>कालः।<BR>III Ancientness:<BR>(1) प्राचीनत्वम्;<BR>(2) पुराणत्वम्;<BR>(3) पुरातनत्वम्।<BR>IV The remains<BR>of a.:<BR>(1) प्राचीनद्रव्यम् (=an old thing);<BR>(2)<BR>प्राक्कालीनविषयः ( = antiquarian subject).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antithesis
ANTITHESIS: nearest word विरोधः, Sah. x.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antitype
ANTITYPE: आदर्शः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antler
ANTLER: हरिणशृङ्गम् (or simp. शृङ्गम् when the<BR>meaning is clear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antlered
ANTLERED: शृङ्गिन् (f. णी): v. Horned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

antonomasia
ANTONOMASIA: लक्षणा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anus
ANUS:<BR>(1) गुदम्;<BR>(2) गुह्यम्;<BR>(3) पायुः;<BR>(4) अपानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anvil
ANVIL:<BR>(1) शूर्मिः (m.);<BR>(2) सूर्मी (f.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anxiety
ANXIETY: उत्कण्ठा;<BR>(2) उद्वेगः (restless a.);<BR>(3) चिन्ता: v. Care;<BR>(4) व्याकुलता: v. Agi-<BR>-tation;<BR>(5) उत्कलिका;<BR>(6) रणरणकः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anxious
ANXIOUS:<BR>I Beset with anxiety:<BR>(1) उत्कण्ठितः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(2) उद्विग्नः (ग्ना, ग्नं);<BR>(3) व्याकुलः (ला, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">Page031</a>]<BR>लं);<BR>(4) चिन्तितः (ता, तं);<BR>II Solicitous,<BR>cager:<BR>(1) व्यग्रः (ग्रा, ग्रं);<BR>(2) उत्सुकः (का,<BR> कं).<BR>III Causing anxiety:<BR>(1) उद्वेगकरः<BR>(री, रं);<BR>(2) उत्कण्ठाप्रदः (दा, दं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anxious
ANXIOUS, TO BE: उन्मनायते (nomi.), a. to see<BR>दर्शनायोन्मनायमानः, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anxiously
ANXIOUSLY:<BR>I With anxiety:<BR>(1) सोत्कण्ठम्;<BR>(2) सोद्वेगम्;<BR>(3) by the adj. v. Anxious (I).<BR>II Eagerly: by the adj.: v. Anxious (II)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

any
ANY:<BR>(1) कश्चित् (काचित्, किञ्चित्),<BR>have you got<BR>a. one named Vimardaka<BR>किमस्ति कश्चिद्विमर्दको<BR> नामात्रभवतः; D. ii.: is there a. doubt about it<BR>किमत्र काचिद्भ्रान्तिः Vi.:<BR>I could not find a.<BR>thing in the house<BR>गृहं प्रविश्यन किञ्चिन्मया समासादि-<BR>तम्, Mr. iii.;<BR>(2) कोऽपि, (कापि, किमपि),<BR>a.<BR>one else<BR>अन्यः कोऽपि etc.;<BR>(3) कश्चन (काचन,<BR> किञ्चन) (rare). Ph.<BR>in the ab-sense of a. wit-<BR>ness<BR>साक्ष्यभावे;<BR>without a. wisdom<BR>ज्ञानं विना;<BR>what power has Dhanañjaya or a. body else even<BR>to take the name of your son<BR>का शक्तिरस्ति धनञ्जय-<BR>स्यान्यस्य वा नामापि ग्रहीतुं ते तनयस्य, Vi. ii. N. B.<BR>When a. means any one or anything whatever,<BR>it is expr.: (a) by यः कश्चित् etc.<BR>a. one could be<BR>a witness in a house or in a forest<BR>अन्तर्वेश्मन्यरण्ये<BR> वा यः कश्चित् साक्ष्यं कुर्यात्, M. viii. 69.; I want<BR>to give even the gold bracelet of my hand to a. one<BR>(I meet) स्वहस्तस्थमपि सुवर्णकङकणं यस्मैकस्मैचिद्दातु-<BR>मिच्छामि; (b) by यः॥॥॥ सः etc.,<BR>they can attack<BR>a. number of horsemen<BR>*यावानश्ववारानधिगच्छन्ति<BR> तावानेवामियोक्तुं शक्रुवन्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anyhow
ANYHOW:<BR>(1) येन केन प्रकारेण;<BR>(2) यथा तथा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

any longer
ANY LONGER, ANY MORE:<BR>(1) इतः परम् (=from<BR>this time);<BR>(2) ततः परम् ( =from that time).<BR>I will not think any more of other girls<BR>न<BR> चिन्तयेमितः परमितरनारीं, D. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

anywhere
ANYWHERE:<BR>(1) कुत्रापि,<BR>a. else<BR>अन्यत्र कुत्रापि;<BR>(2) क्वचिदपि, N. kiii. 55. Ph.<BR>go a. you<BR>like<BR>गच्छ यथेच्छम्, N. i. 143.; die a. you like<BR>यत्र तत्र वा प्राणत्यागं कुरु, Vi. vi.;<BR>I do not allow<BR>you to go a. ele from here<BR>इतोऽन्यतो न वो गन्तुमनु-<BR>मन्ये, Sa. iiii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aorist
AORIST: no equiv.: अनद्यतनभूतः (=indefinite<BR>past).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aorta
AORTA: हृदयस्य वामकोषनिर्गता रक्तवहा बृहन्नाडी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apace
APACE: सत्वरम्: v. Quickly, rapidly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apart
APART:<BR>I Separately: q. v.: पृथक्।<BR>II At<BR>a distance: दूरे।<BR>III Privately:<BR>(1) विजने;<BR>(2) निभृतम्। Ph.:<BR>a. from this, there is no other<BR>fault in the man.<BR>एतद्भिन्नस्तस्य दोषो नास्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apartment
APARTMENT: कोष्ठः: v. Room. The inner a. s<BR>अन्तःपुरम्।<BR>The attendants on the inner a. s<BR>अन्त-<BR>र्वंशिकाः पुरुषाः D. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apathetic
APATHETIC;<BR>I Void of passion:<BR>(1) वीतरागः<BR>(गा, गं);<BR>(2) वीतस्पृहः (हा, हं);<BR>(3) निस्पृहः<BR>(हा, हं);<BR>(4) उदासः (सा, सं);<BR>(5) विरागिन् (f.<BR>नी).<BR>II Indifferent: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apathy
APATHY:<BR>I Stoicism:<BR>(1) वेराग्यम्;<BR>(2)<BR>औदास्यम्।<BR>II Indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ape
APE (subs.): पुच्छहीनो वानरः; कपिभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ape
APE (v. t.): v. To imitate, copy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aperient
APERIENT:<BR>I Adj. रेचकः (की, कं).<BR>II Subs.:<BR>रेचकः: v. Purgative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aperture
APERTURE:<BR>(1) छिद्रम्;<BR>(2) रन्ध्रम्; v. Open-<BR>-ing, fissure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apex
APEX:<BR>(1) चूडा;<BR>(2) शिखरम्: v. Tip, point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aphorism
APHORISM:<BR>(1) सूत्रम्;<BR>(2) वचनम्: v. Maxim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aphoristic
APHORISTIC: Ph. the method of the book is a.<BR>*सूत्रैर्ग्रथितो ग्रन्थः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apiary
APIARY: *मधुमक्षिकाशाला: v. Bee-hive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apiece
APIECE: एकैकः (का, कं): v. Each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apish
APISH: v. Foolish, foppish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apocalypse
APOCALYPSE: प्रकाशनम्: v. Revelation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apocope
APOCOPE; *अन्त्याक्षरलोपः; *अन्त्याक्षरलोपालङ्कारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apocrypha
APOCRYPHA: कृष्टीयोपवेदः; *उपधर्मपुस्तकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apogee
APOGEE: उच्चः; चन्द्रकान्तिमण्डलस्य पृथिव्या दविष्ठ-<BR>पदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apologize
APOLOGIZE:<BR>(1) क्षमां प्रार्थयते<BR>or<BR>याचते;<BR>(2)<BR>मर्षयति (मृष्, c. 10.),<BR>a. to the king for what we<BR>said amongst ourselves against etiquette<BR>मर्षयत<BR> लोकपालं यदस्माभिर्विश्रब्धप्रलापिनीभिरूपचारातिक्रमेण<BR> भणितम्। Sa. iii.;<BR>(3) अनु-नयति (नी, c. 1.)<BR>( =to propitiate).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apologue
APOLOGUE: कथा: v. Fable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apology
APOLOGY:<BR>I An excuse for a fault: Ph.<BR>to make an a.<BR>क्षमाप्रार्थनां करोति; to accept an a.<BR>अनुनयवचनं परिगृह्वाति (after ge.): v. Excuse. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">Page032</a>]<BR>II An apologetic treatise; no equiv.:<BR>*प्रतिवादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apophthegm
APOPHTHEGM:<BR>(1) वचनम्:<BR>(2) वाक्यम्: v.<BR>Saying, maxim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apoplectic
APOPLECTIC:<BR>I subs.: सन्यासरोगिन् (f. णी).<BR>II Adj.: Expr. by tat. comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apoplexy
APOPLEXY: सन्यासरोगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apostasy
APOSTASY:<BR>(1) स्वघर्मत्यागः (=abandonment<BR>of one's religion);<BR>(2) स्वमतत्यागः ( = a. of<BR>one's principles);<BR>(3) परधर्माश्रयः (taking<BR>another religion): v. Desertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apostate
APOSTATE:<BR>(1) *स्वधर्मत्यागिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) यः<BR>(या, यत्) स्वधर्मं स्वमतं स्वपक्षं वा परित्यज्य परधर्मं,<BR> परमतं, परपक्षं वा अवलम्बते, आश्रयति, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apostatize
APOSTATIZE: स्वधर्मं, स्वमतं, स्वपक्षं वा त्यजति, परि-<BR>त्यजति; स्वधर्मात् स्वमतात् वा भ्रंसते (भ्रंस्, c. 1.),<BR>च्यवते (च्यु, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apostle
APOSTLE:<BR>(1) *ईश्वरदूतः;<BR>(2) महर्षिः। A. -Ship<BR>*ईश्वरदौत्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apostrophe
APOSTROPHE:<BR>I In Rhe.: सम्बोधनम्।<BR>II In<BR>gram.: *अमिनिधानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apostrophize
APOSTROPHIZE:<BR>(1) सम्बोधयति (c. of बुध्);<BR>(2) आह्वयति (ह्वे, c. 1.).: v. To address.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apothecary
APOTHECARY:<BR>(1) *औषधकारः;<BR>(2) भिषज् (m)<BR>( =physician, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apotheosis
APOTHEOSIS: v. Deification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appal
APPAL: वि-त्रासयति, सं-, (c. of त्रस्): v. To<BR>terrify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apparatus
APPARATUS: उपकरणम्: v. Tools, instruments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apparel
APPAREL (subs.): परिच्छदः: v. Dress, attire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apparel
APPAREL (v.): v. To dress, clothe, attire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apparent
APPARENT (adj.):<BR>I Visible: q. v. प्रादुर्भूत।<BR>(ता, तं).<BR>II Evident, clear: q. v.:<BR>(1) व्यक्तः<BR>(क्ता, क्तं);<BR>(2) स्फुटः (टा, टं);<BR>(3) स्पष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं).<BR>III Seeming (as opposed to real):<BR>(1)<BR>प्रकाशः (शा, शं);<BR>(2) प्रकटः (टा, टं);<BR>(3) बाह्यः<BR>(ह्या, ह्यं) ( =external, q. v.): v. Feigned,<BR>false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apparently
APPARENTLY:<BR>I Plainly, clearly: q. v.:<BR>व्यक्तम्।<BR>II Ostensibly, seemingly:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रकाशं;<BR>(2) प्रकटं, Si. xvi. 19.;<BR>(3) बहिः<BR>( =externally, q. v.),<BR>a. sweet, but really un-<BR>friendly<BR>मधुरं बहिरन्तरप्रियम्, Si. xvi. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apparition
APPARITION:<BR>I Appearance: q. v.:<BR>II A<BR>ghost, phantom: q. v.: छाया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apparitor
APPARITOR: no equiv.: दूतः; अनुचरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appeal
APPEAL (subs.):<BR>I Leg. t. t.: *पुनर्विचारप्रार्थना।<BR>A court of a.<BR>*ये प्राड्विवाकाः पुनर्विचारप्रार्थनां<BR> श्रोतुमर्हन्ति<BR>or<BR>शृण्वन्ति।<BR>II Reference to some<BR>one as an authority or witness: Ph. to<BR>make an a. to प्रमाणयति (nomi.).<BR>III Resort,<BR>recourse: q. v.<BR>IV An address of entreaty:<BR>प्रार्थना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appeal
APPEAL (v. i.):<BR>I Leg. t. t.: पुनर्विचारं प्रार्थयते<BR>(अर्थ्, c. 10.).<BR>II To refer to another as an<BR>authority: प्रमाणयति: Ph. I a. to gods about it<BR>अत्र विषये मम देवाः साक्षिणस्तिष्ठन्ति।<BR>III To<BR>implore, entreat: q. v.<BR>IV To excite,<BR>affect: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appear
APPEAR (v. i.):<BR>I To be visible:<BR>(1) आविर्भवति<BR>or<BR>प्रादुर्भवति,<BR>a herd of deer a. ed<BR>मृगाणां यूथमाविर्बभूव,<BR>R. ix. 55.;<BR>(2) प्रादुरस्ति (अस्, c. 1.) R. xi.<BR>63.;<BR>(3) दृश्यते, अथि-, प्रति-, (pass. of दृश्)<BR>(=to be seen) not restricted to real life as<BR>(1) and (2).;<BR>a swan a. ed in their dream<BR>तयोः<BR> स्वप्ने कश्चिज्जालपादः प्रत्यदृश्यत, D. i.<BR>II To<BR>show one's self: Ph.<BR>she does not a. before<BR>me<BR>सा मत्समक्षं नागच्छति (not दर्शनं ददाति, see<BR>R. xix. 7.).<BR>III To be out: निर्गच्छति,<BR>an<BR>article a. ed in the Induprakāsha about so and<BR>so<BR>*अमुकविषयकः प्रबन्ध इन्दुप्रकाशपत्रिकायां निर्गतः।<BR>IV Leg. t. t: to be present:<BR>(1) उपतिष्ठति<BR>(स्था, c. 1.);<BR>(2) Perh. दर्शनं ददाति। V. To<BR>seem: q. v. प्रतिभाति (भा, c. 2.).<BR>VI To be<BR>evident or clear: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appearance
APPEARANCE:<BR>I The act of becoming<BR>visible;<BR>(1) आविर्भावः (=actual a. especi-<BR>-ally of invisible spirits). who wants to make<BR>his a. (in this world) यश्चाविर्भावमिच्छति, Mah.;<BR>(2) by the verb: v. To appear (I);<BR>(3)<BR>प्रादुर्भावः (rare), Kuv.<BR>II Act of being<BR>present:<BR>(1) उपस्थितिः;<BR>(2) दर्शनम्,<BR>he who<BR>stands a security for one's a.<BR>यो यस्य प्रतिभूस्तिष्ठे-<BR>र्शनाय। M. viii. 58.<BR>III personal a.:<BR>(1) आकारः;<BR>(2) आकृतिः।<BR>of good a.:<BR>सुदृश्यः<BR>(श्या, श्यं).<BR>IV Semblance, mere show: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">Page033</a>]<BR>Ph.<BR>outward a.<BR>वाह्याकृतिः; has an a. of justice<BR>न्यायमिवावभासते, Ki. xiv. 7.: v. Apparently<BR>(II). V. A phenomenon: q. v.:<BR>VI Proba-<BR>-bility, likelihood: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appeasable
APPEASABLE: शमनीयः (या, यं): v. Placable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appease
APPEASE:<BR>(1) शमयति, प्र-, उप-, (c. of शम्);<BR>(2) सान्त्वयति, उप-, परि-, (सान्त्व, c. 10): v.<BR>Calm, propitiate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appeased
APPEASED, TO BE:<BR>(1) शाम्यति (शम्, c. 4.);<BR>(2)<BR>प्र-सीदति (सद्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appeaser
APPEASER: शमयिता; प्रशमयिता। v. To appease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appeasing
APPEASING (subs.):<BR>(1) शान्तिः;<BR>(2) प्रशान्तिः;<BR>(3) सान्त्वना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appellant
APPELLANT: *पुनर्विचारप्रार्थिन् (f. नी); निदेश-<BR>भङ्गार्थिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appellate
APPELLATE: Ph.<BR>a. jurisdiction<BR>*पुनर्विचाराधिकारः;<BR>a. court<BR>ये प्राड्विवाकाः पुनर्विचारप्रार्थनां श्रोतुमर्हन्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appellation
APPELLATION: नामधेयम्; v. Name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appellative
APPELLATIVE: i. e. common:<BR>(1) साधारणः (णा,<BR> णं);<BR>(2) सामान्यः (न्या, न्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

append
APPEND: अनुबध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appendage
APPENDAGE: Ph.<BR>a house with its a. s<BR>*सोपकरणं<BR> गृहं;<BR>virtue is an a. of belief in God<BR>*सदाचार<BR> आस्तिक्यबुद्धिमनुबध्नातिः, v. Concomitant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appendix
APPENDIX: परिशिष्टम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appertain
APPERTAIN: v. To belong. A. ing to: v.<BR>belonging to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appetence
APPETENCE: v. Appetite, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appetite
APPETITE:<BR>I Any mental desire:<BR>(1) कामः;<BR>(2) रागः; v. Desire, longing.<BR>II actual<BR>desire for food:<BR>(1) क्षुधा;<BR>(2) बुभुक्षा;<BR>(3)<BR>अशनाया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

applaud
APPLAUD:<BR>(1) प्रशंसति (शंस्, c. 1.) v. To praise;<BR>(2) गायति, उपगायति (गै, c. 1.) Ki. xvii. 47.;<BR>(3) वन्दते, परि-, (वन्द्, c. 1.),<BR>a. ed by the chiefs<BR>of the clans<BR>गणपतिभिः परिवन्दितेन, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

applause
APPLAUSE:<BR>I Acclamation: q. v.: प्रशंसावाचः<BR>(f. pl.).<BR>II Praise: q. v. प्रशंसा। N. B. Clap-<BR>-ping the hands is not a sign of a. in<BR>Sanskrit, but the reverse, Si. xv. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apple
APPLE:<BR>I A tree: *आतावृक्षः।<BR>II Its fruits:<BR>आताफलम्।<BR>III Of the eye: तारा: v.<BR>Pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appliance
APPLIANCE:<BR>I Application: q. v.<BR>II In pl.,<BR>instruments: q. v.: उपकरणानि। (n. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

applicability
APPLICABILITY: Expr. by circumlo.: v.<BR>Applicable, apply (v. i.) (1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

applicable
APPLICABLE: लगत् (f. न्ती), the fine-toothed<BR>(lady)<BR>hearing the whole speech equally a. to<BR>Indra and Nala<BR>आकर्ण्य तुल्यमखिलां सुदती लगन्ती-<BR>माखण्डलेऽपि च नलेऽपि च वाचमेतां, N. iii. 8. Ph.<BR>equa-<BR>lly a. to Yama and Nala<BR>शमननैषधयोः समानः N.<BR>iii. 20.;<BR>to be a.<BR>लगति (लग्, c. 1) (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

applicant
APPLICANT:<BR>(1) अर्थी;<BR>(2) प्रार्थयिता;<BR>(3) याचकः:<BR>v. Petitioner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

application
APPLICATION (subs).:<BR>I The act of putting to:<BR>प्रयोगः, सम्प्रयोगः,<BR>by the a. of fire or heat<BR>अग्न्यातप-<BR>संप्रयोगात्, R. v. 54.<BR>II The thing applied:<BR>प्रयोगः, should seize (them)<BR>by wet leather or by<BR>other a. s<BR>आर्द्र चर्मणान्यैर्वा प्रयोगैर्गृह्वीयात्, Sr.<BR>III<BR>Petition: q. v.:<BR>(1) प्रार्थना;<BR>(2) याच्ञा।<BR>IV<BR>attention, assiduity: q. v.:<BR>(1) अभिनिवेशः;<BR>(2) मनोयोगः। V. Use, employment; प्रयोगः Ki.<BR>VI Relation, reference: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apply
APPLY (v. i.):<BR>I Refer or relate to:<BR>(1)<BR>लगति (लग्, c. 1) (with loc.) N. xiii. 8.;<BR>(2)<BR>वर्तते (वृत्, c. 1) (only in certain cases),<BR>here<BR>the word ‘light’ a. s to God<BR>अत्र ज्योतिःशब्दः<BR> ब्रह्मणि वर्तते, S. iii. 40.<BR>II To solicit, have<BR>recourse to: q. v.: प्रार्थयते (अर्थ्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apply
APPLY (v. t.):<BR>I To lay or put on:<BR>(1) प्रयो-<BR>जयति<BR>or<BR>युनक्ति<BR>or<BR>यूंक्ते (युज्, c. 10. and 7.),<BR>do<BR>not a. liniment at night<BR>नालेपं रात्रौ प्रयुञ्जीत, Sr.;<BR>(2) नि-वेशयति (c. विश्),<BR>a. ing the shell to his<BR>lower lip<BR>अधरौष्ठे जलजं निवेश्य, R. vii. 63. Ph.:<BR>a. ing the bit to your mouth<BR>खलीनं मुखे प्रक्षिप्य, P.<BR>iv. 7.;<BR>he a. d his hand to my breast<BR>स ममोरसि<BR> हस्तं ददौ।<BR>II To use, refer: प्रयोजयति or<BR>युनक्ति,<BR>or<BR>युंक्ते, we a. the words like ‘sun’ to it<BR>तस्मिन्नादित्यादयः शब्दाः प्रयुज्यन्ते, S. iii. 32.<BR>III<BR>To use for a particular purpose, to devote:<BR>प्रयोजयति।<BR>IV To fix closely, incline: मनो<BR> यच्छति (दा, c. 1), ददाति (दा, c. 3), निदधाति<BR>(धा, c. 3),<BR>or<BR>युनक्ति (युज्, c. 7).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appoint
APPOINT (v. t.):<BR>I To make or nominate:<BR>(1) युनक्ति<BR>or<BR>यंक्ते, नि-, विनि-, (युज्, c. 7), as [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">Page034</a>]<BR>a king a. s officers over villages etc.<BR>यथा, राजा<BR> ग्रामादिष्वधिकृतान्विनियुंक्ते, Up.;<BR>(2) करोति (कृ,<BR>c. 8) v. To make;<BR>(3) निदधाति, सन्नि-, (धा,<BR>c. 3) Ki. i. 22. v. To place;<BR>(4) व्या-दिशति<BR>(दिश्, c. 6) Ku. iii. 13. v. To order.<BR>II<BR>To ordain, prescribe: q. v.: निर्दिशति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appointed
APPOINTED, WELL: i. e. well equipped:<BR>(1)<BR>सुसज्जितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) परिकल्पितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appointment
APPOINTMENT:<BR>I The act of appointing:<BR>(1) नियोगः;<BR>(2) विनियोगः।<BR>II Station, posi-<BR>-tion: पदम्।<BR>III Stipulation, agreement:<BR>q. v. समयः (rare in this sense).<BR>IV. A. com-<BR>-mand, decree: q. v.: नियोगः। v. Equipment:<BR>q. v. सज्जा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apportion
APPORTION: वि-भजति, प्रवि-, संवि-, (भज् c. 1):<BR>v. To distribute, allot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apportionment
APPORTIONMENT:<BR>(1) विभागः (=distribution,<BR>q. v.);<BR>(2) परिकल्पनम् (=assignment, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apposite
APPOSITE:<BR>(1) उपयुक्तः (क्ता, क्तं);<BR>(2) उपपन्नः<BR>(न्ना, न्नं);<BR>(3) सङ्गतः (ता, तं): v. Suitable,<BR>Fit, pertinent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appositely
APPOSITELY:<BR>(1) Expr. by the adj.;<BR>(2) स्थाने;<BR>(3) प्रस्तावसदृशम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appositeness
APPOSITENESS: Ph.<BR>your remark is characterized<BR>by a.<BR>सङ्गतं तव भाषितम्: v. Apposite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apposition
APPOSITION: एकान्वयः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appraise
APPRAISE (v. t.): भूल्यं निरूपयति (रूप्, c. 10),<BR>निर्धारयति (धृ, c. 10).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appraisement
APPRAISEMENT:<BR>(1) भूल्यनिरूपणम्;<BR>(2) मूल्यनिर्धारणम्:<BR>v. Valuation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appraiser
APPRAISER:<BR>(1) मूल्यनिरूपकः;<BR>(2) मूल्यनिर्धारकः:<BR>v. Valuer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appreciable
APPRECIABLE: उपलभ्यः (भ्या, भ्यं) (=percep-<BR>-tible, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appreciate
APPRECIATE:<BR>(1) मूल्यं<BR>or<BR>गुणागुणं जानाति (ज्ञा, c.<BR>9), अवगच्छति (गम्, c. 1);<BR>(2) बहुमन्यते (मन्,<BR>c. 4) (=to think much of).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appreciation
APPRECIATION:<BR>(1) मूल्यविञ्जानम् (?);<BR>(2) गुणा-<BR>गुणविज्ञानम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apprehend
APPREHEND:<BR>I To arrest: q. v.:<BR>(1) धरति<BR>(धृ, c. 1);<BR>(2) गृह्वाति (ग्रह्, c. 9).<BR>II To<BR>comprehend, conceive: q. v.:<BR>(1) उपलभते<BR>(लभ्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) अवगच्छति (गम्, c. 1.)<BR>III To believe, suppose: q. v.: शङ्कते<BR>(शङ्क, c. 1),<BR>I a. Bharata has come out to meet<BR>me<BR>शङके॥॥॥।प्रत्युद्गतो मां भरतः, R. xiii. 64.<BR>IV To fear शङ्कते, आ-, वि-, परि-,<BR>a. ing defeat<BR>from you<BR>विशङ्कमानो भवतः पराभवं, Ki. i. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apprehnsion
APPREHNSION:<BR>I The act of seizing:<BR>(1)<BR>ग्रहणम्;<BR>(2) धृतिः (rare).<BR>II Arrest: q. v.:<BR>आसोधः।<BR>III Conception, comprehension,<BR>understanding: q. v.: Ph.<BR>a man of quick<BR>a.<BR>तीक्ष्णबुद्धिः,<BR>a man of dull a.<BR>स्थूलबुद्विः।<BR>IV<BR>Opinion, notion: q. v.: मतम्। V. Fear of<BR>future evil:<BR>(1) शङ्क्ला;<BR>(2) आशङ्का।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apprehensive
APPREHENSIVE:<BR>(1) शङ्कितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) शङ्कान्वितः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR>to be a.<BR>शङ्कते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apprentice
APPRENTICE (subs): no equiv.: अन्तेवासिन्<BR>(f. नी) (=disciple) may be used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apprentice
APPRENTICE (v): Ph.<BR>he was a. d to me for<BR>five years<BR>*पञ्चवर्षपर्यन्तं स मम नियमबद्धोऽन्तेवास्यासीत्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apprenticeship
APPRENTICESHIP: अन्तेवासित्वम्। (?); नियमबद्धा-<BR>न्तेवासित्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apprise of
APPRISE OF: वि-ञ्जापयति (c. of ञ्जा): v. To<BR>inform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

approach
APPROACH (v.):<BR>I To come or go near:<BR>(1) उप-सर्पति (सृप्, c. 1);<BR>(2) उप-सरति, समुप-,<BR>(सृ, c. 1);<BR>(3) उप-सीदति, उपा-, (सद्, c. 1);<BR>(4) समीपं, निकटं, etc. गच्छति (गम्, c. 1), याति<BR>(या, c. 2), etc.: v. Go near;<BR>(5) उप-<BR>गच्छति, समुप-। N. B. Observe that समीपं etc. are<BR>cons. with the gen., all the other verbs<BR>take the acc.<BR>II To approximate,<BR>resemble: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

approach
APPROACH (subs):<BR>I The act of approa-<BR>-ching:<BR>(1) आसन्नता (=the act of being<BR>near);<BR>(2) उपागमः;<BR>(3) आगमः (=arrival).<BR>II A means of a. ing:<BR>(1) उपसर्पणमार्गः (?);<BR>(2) उपागमद्वारम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

approachable
APPROACHABLE: उपसर्पणीयः (या, यं): v. Acc-<BR>-essible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

approaching
APPROACHING (part. adj.):<BR>(1) आसन्नः (न्ना, न्नं),<BR>whose death was a.<BR>आसन्नशरीरपातः, Ku. iii. 44;<BR>(2) अभ्यर्णः (र्णा, र्णं),<BR>a. separation,<BR>अभ्यर्णविरह-,<BR>K.;<BR>(3) उपोढः (ढा, ढं), Ki. xvii. 54.;<BR>(4) सन्निकृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

approbation
APPROBATION:<BR>I Acclamation:<BR>(1) धन्यवादः;<BR>(2) साधुवादः,<BR>you will receive a. throughout the<BR>world<BR>यावत् संसारमण्डलमवाप्नुहि साधुवादम्, Si. xiv.<BR>87.<BR>II Assent, approval: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appropriate
APPROPRIATE (v. t.):<BR>I To set apart for a<BR>particular purpose:<BR>(1) नि-योजयति, विनि-,<BR> प्र-, (युज्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) उप-कल्पयति (कॢप्, c. 10.).<BR>II To take to one's self:<BR>(1) आत्मसात्<BR> करोति (कृ, c. 8.),<BR>what princes strive to a. even<BR>by misdeeds<BR>दुरितैरपि कर्तुमात्मसात् प्रयतन्ते नृपसूनवो हि<BR> यत्, R. viii. 2;<BR>(2) स्वायत्तः (त्ता, त्तं)<BR>or<BR>स्वाधीनः<BR>(ना, नं) (agreeing with the object) करोति, M.<BR>n. (not very common).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appropriate
APPROPRIATE (adj.):<BR>I Apposite, suitable:<BR>q. v.: उपपन्नः (न्ना, न्नं),<BR>this epithet is very a.<BR>for the breeze<BR>उपपन्नं विशेषणमस्य वायोः V. ii.<BR>II<BR>Peculiar: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appropriately
APPROPRIATELY:<BR>(1) उपपन्नम्;<BR>(2) युक्तम्: v.<BR>Fitly, suitably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appropriateness
APPROPRIATENESS: Fitness: suitableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appropriation
APPROPRIATION:<BR>(1) प्रयोगः;<BR>(2) विनियोगः;<BR>(3) उपकल्पनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

approval
APPROVAL:<BR>(1) अनुमोदनम् (rare);<BR>(2) सम्मतिः<BR>(=assent);<BR>(3) by the verb,<BR>you have received<BR>my a.<BR>मयानुमोदितोऽसि: v. Also approba-<BR>-tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

approve
APPROVE:<BR>I To be pleased with:<BR>(1) अनु-<BR>मोदते (मुद्, c. 1) (gen. with the acc. of the<BR>person whose measures etc. are a. d), none<BR>of his brothers could oppose or a. (his determi-<BR>-nation) न कश्चन भ्रातृषु तेषु शक्तो निषेद्धु मासीदनुमोदितुं<BR> वा। R. xiv. 43;<BR>without obtaining a. al of<BR>my mother<BR>मात्राननुमोदिता; K.;<BR>(2) रोचते, अभि-,<BR>(रुच्, c. 1) (with dat. of the person who a.<BR>s), if you ask me,<BR>I do not a. even of their<BR>quarrel<BR>यदि मां पृच्छसि तदैतेषां विवाद एव न मे रोचते,<BR>Mal. i.;<BR>(3) अनु-मन्यते (मन्, c. 4) (rare in<BR>this sense), D. iv.:<BR>II To prove: q. v.<BR>III To commend: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

approved
APPROVED:<BR>(1) परीक्षितः (ता, तं) (=tried);<BR>(2) अभिमतः (ता, तं) (=accepted).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

approver
APPROVER. leg.t. t.: यः स्वयं दोषं प्रतिपद्य सहायान-<BR>प्यभियुनक्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

approximate
APPROXIMATE (adj.): आसन्नः (न्ना, न्नं): v.<BR>Near, next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

approximate
APPROXIMATE (v.):<BR>I To approach: q. v.<BR>II<BR>To resemble: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

approximation
APPROXIMATION: Ph. this is only an a. to truth<BR>*एतन्ने दिष्ठमेव सत्यस्यः v. Near, next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apricot
APRICOT: सुस्वादुः फलविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

april
APRIL: उत्तरचैत्रपूर्ववैशाखानुवादीयुरुपीयवत्सरस्य चतुर्थो<BR> मासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apron
APRON:<BR>I An article of dress: युतकम्। (?)<BR>II A covering for the legs: *चर्ममयः जङ्घा-<BR>प्रच्छदः, जङ्धात्राणम्।<BR>III A piece of lead to<BR>cover the vent of a cannon: no equiv.<BR>पिधानम् (=covering) may be used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apropos
APROPOS: स्थाने: v. Opportunely, seasonably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apsis
APSIS: मन्दोच्चः (मन्दः =the lower a., उच्चः<BR>=the higher a.) The line of apsides:<BR>मन्दोच्चरेखा (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

apt
APT:<BR>I Fit, suitable: q. v.: उपयुक्तः (क्ता,<BR> क्तं).<BR>II Inclined, prone:<BR>(1) by शीलः<BR>(ला, लं) in comp.,<BR>a. to forget<BR>विस्मरणशीलः (ला,<BR> लं);<BR>(2) in some cases by a deriv: a. to break<BR>भङ्गुरः (रा, रं);<BR>a. to fall<BR>पातुकः (का, कं),<BR>not<BR>a. to perish<BR>अविनश्वरः (रा, रं).<BR>III Ready,<BR>prompt: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aptitude
APTITUDE:<BR>I Tendency, propensity: expr.<BR>by शीलता or by deriv.:<BR>a. to break<BR>भङ्गुरता: v.<BR>Apt (ii).<BR>II Fitness, Suitableness: q. v.<BR>उपयोगिता।<BR>III Readiness in learning:<BR>of<BR>remarkable a.<BR>तीक्ष्णबुद्धि। (mfn.): v. Sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aptly
APTLY:<BR>(1) यथोचितम्;<BR>(2) यथोपपन्नम्: v. Fitly,<BR>suitably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aptness
APTNESS: v. Aptitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aqua-fortis
AQUA-FORTIS: (nitric acid): *तीक्ष्णरसः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aquarius
AQUARIUS: कुम्भराशिः, or simply, कुम्भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aquatic
AQUATIC:<BR>I Pertaining to water: जल (in<BR>comp.): a. animal:<BR>(1) जलजन्तुः;<BR>(2) यादस<BR>(n).<BR>II Pertaining to water: जलचरः or<BR>जलेचरः (री, रं).<BR>III Born in water:<BR>(1)<BR>जलजः (जा, जं);<BR>(2) वारिजः (जा, जं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aqueduct
AQUEDUCT:<BR>(1) जलप्रणाली;<BR>(2) जलवाहिनी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aqueous
AQUEOUS:<BR>(1) जलमयः (यी, यं);<BR>(2) अभ्मयः<BR>(यी, यं): v. Watery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aquiline
AQUILINE: Ph.<BR>one who has a. nose<BR>शुकनासः (सा,<BR> सं); तुङ्गघोणः (णा, णं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arabesque
ARABESQUE: *गृहभित्त्यादावुत्कीर्णकुसुमाद्यलङ्कारविशेषः,<BR> आरवालङ्कारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arable
ARABLE:<BR>(1) कृषियोग्यः (ग्या, ग्यं);<BR>(2) हल्यः (ल्या,<BR> ल्यं). A. land: हल्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arbiter
ARBITER:<BR>I An arbitrator: q. v. मध्यस्थः।<BR>II A lord, master: ईशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arbitrarily
ARBITRARILY:<BR>(1) स्वेच्छया;<BR>(2) स्वेच्छातः;<BR>(3)<BR>स्वकामतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arbitrary
ARBITRARY:<BR>I Depending on mere will: Ph.<BR>an a. decision<BR>*इच्छानुरूपो निर्णयः; a. conduct<BR>स्वेच्छाचारिता<BR>or<BR>कामचारिता;<BR>it was a. on your<BR>part to arrest me<BR>*त्वं स्वेच्छया मां धृतवान्।<BR>II<BR>Absolute, despotic:<BR>(1) स्वेच्छाचारिन् (f. णी):<BR>(2) कामचारिन्। (f. णी);<BR>(3) उद्दामः (मा, मं)<BR>(without any control).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arbitrate
ARBITRATE: निर्णयति (नी, c. 1): v. To decide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arbitration
ARBITRATION: निर्णयः (=decision: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arbitrator
ARBITRATOR: मध्यस्थः: v. Umpire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arbour
ARBOUR:<BR>(1) कुञ्जः;<BR>(2) निकुञ्जः: v. Bower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arc
ARC: वृत्तखण्डम् (a. of a circle): v. Arch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arcade
ARCADE: Perh. तोरणगृहम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arch
ARCH (subs.) तोरण (mn) (properly=an arched<BR>gateway, but may, by analogy, be applied<BR>to other arches).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arch
ARCH (v):<BR>I To cover with an arch: तोरणं<BR> न्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4) (after Mu.)<BR>or<BR>तोरणेन प्रच्छा-<BR>दयति (छद् c. 10).<BR>II To bend, curve: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arch
ARCH (adj.): चतुरः (रा, रं): v. Cunning, sly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archaeologist
ARCHAEOLOGIST: *पुराणसाहित्यविद्; प्राक्कालीन-<BR>साहित्यादिविषयेषु पण्डितः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archaeology
ARCHAEOLOGY: *पुराणसाहित्यम्; प्राक्कालीनसाहि-<BR>त्यादिविषयका विद्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archaism
ARCHAISM: *प्राचीनप्रयोगः: A. s occurring in the<BR>Mahābhārata, Rāmāyana, Manu, etc. are<BR>called आर्षप्रयोगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archangel
ARCHANGEL: *ईश्वरस्य प्रधानदूतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archbishop
ARCHBISHOP: *कृष्टीयसम्प्रदायेषु सर्वप्रधानाचार्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archbishopric
ARCHBISHOPRIC: *कृष्टीयसम्प्रदायेषु यः सर्वप्रधानाचार्यः,<BR> तस्याधिकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archdeacon
ARCHDEACON: *ईलण्डदेशे विशपस्य निम्नस्थो धर्मो-<BR>पासकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archdeaconry
ARCHDEACONRY:<BR>I The office of an arch-<BR>-deacon: *आर्चडिकनपदम्।<BR>II His residence:<BR>*आर्चडिकनावासः।<BR>III His jurisdiction *आर्चडि-<BR>कनस्याधिकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archduchy
ARCHDUCHY: Ph.<BR>a. of Baden<BR>वादेनराज्यम्: v.<BR>Kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archduke
ARCHDUKE (m.), Archduches (f.): उपाधिविशेषः;<BR> *उपराजः (m), उपराञ्जी (f.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arched
ARCHED:<BR>I Covered with an arch: न्यस्ततोरणः<BR>(णा, णं) (?),<BR>an a. gateway<BR>तोरणम्।<BR>II In the<BR>form of an arch, curved:<BR>(1) भुग्नः (ग्ना, ग्नं);<BR>(2) कुञ्चितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archer
ARCHER:<BR>I A bowman: q. v.: धानुष्कः।<BR>II<BR>The constellation: धनुस् (n.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archery
ARCHERY:<BR>(1) धनुर्विद्या (the art);<BR>(2) शराभ्यासः (the<BR>practice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archetype
ARCHETYPE: आदर्शः: v. Pattern, model.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archiepiscopal
ARCHIEPISCOPAL: i. e. belonging to an arch-<BR>-bishop: expr. by tat. comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archipelago
ARCHIPELAGO: द्वीपसमूहः; द्वीपसङ्घातः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

architect
ARCHITECT:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) वास्तुविद्योपजीविन् (m),<BR>K. b.;<BR>(2) स्थपतिः, P. i. 1.;<BR>(3) शिल्पिन् (n.)<BR>(=artisan, but may be appropriately used<BR>when the sense is clear), R.<BR>II. Fig.: a<BR>maker: q. v.: कर्ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

architectural
ARCHITECTURAL: expr. by comp., a. skill<BR>निर्माणकौशलम।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

architecture
ARCHITECTURE:<BR>(1) वास्तुविद्या;<BR>(2) गृहनिर्माणशिल्पम्<BR>(?);<BR>(3) शिल्पम् (when the sense is clear). Si.<BR>iii. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

architrave
ARCHITRAVE: no equiv.: *उपस्तम्भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archives
ARCHIVES:<BR>I Records: *प्राचीनपत्रसञ्चयः।<BR>II<BR>The place where they are kept: *प्राचीन-<BR>पत्रागारम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archly
ARCHLY:<BR>(1) चतुरम्;<BR>(2) विदग्धम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

archness
ARCHNESS:<BR>(1) चातुर्यम्;<BR>(2) चातुरी;<BR>(3) वैदग्धम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arctic
ARCTIC: *उत्तरकेन्द्रीयः (या, यं):<BR>the a. pole<BR>उत्तर-<BR>केन्द्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ardency
ARDENCY: v. Ardour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ardent
ARDENT:<BR>I Fiery, hot: q. v.: प्रचण्डः (ण्डा, ण्डं).<BR>II Eager: Ph. a. eyes (of a lover) सतृष्णनयने।<BR>III Warm, affectionate: अत्यन्तः (न्ता, न्तं)<BR>or<BR>निरतिशयः (या, यं) (=excessive), a. love [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">Page037</a>]<BR>निरतिशयानुरागः: Ph. a. vows (of a lover) शपथाः<BR>(m. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ardently
ARDENTLY: सतृष्णं (as in gazing);<BR>(2) अत्यन्तं<BR>(=excessively).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ardour
ARDOUR:<BR>I Heat: q. v. उत्तापः।<BR>II Warmth,<BR>eagerness: उत्साहः;<BR>with a.<BR>सोत्साहं। Ph.<BR>the<BR>a. of his love<BR>तस्य निरतिशयानुरागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arduous
ARDUOUS:<BR>I Lofty: q. v.<BR>II Difficult: q. v.<BR>दुष्करः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arduousness
ARDUOUSNESS: v. Difficulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

area
AREA<BR>I Outer a.: अङ्गनम्: v. Yard.<BR>II<BR>Inner<BR>a.<BR>प्रकोष्ठः।<BR>III In geo. फलम्, a. of a circle<BR>वृत्तक्षेत्रफलम्;<BR>a. of a triangle<BR>त्रिभुजफलम्, Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arena
ARENA:<BR>(1) रङ्गः;<BR>(2) रङ्गभूमिः;<BR>(3) अक्षवाटः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

argillaceous
ARGILLACEOUS: v. Clayey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

argonautic
ARGONAUTIC: Ph.<BR>a. expedition<BR>*कनकोर्णान्वेष-<BR>णाय जेसनस्य कल्विसं प्रति यात्रा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

argosy
ARGOSY: बृहन्नौविशेषः: v. Merchantman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

argue
ARGUE (v. i.):<BR>I To reason: तर्कयति, वि-,<BR>(तर्क्, c. 10)<BR>or<BR>तर्कं करोति<BR>II To infer: q. v.:<BR>(1) तर्कयति; ऊहते (ऊह्, c. 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

argue
ARGUE (v. t.):<BR>I To discuss: Ph.<BR>he a. d the<BR>cause very ably<BR>*स युक्तिं प्रदश्र्य सुनिपुणं तर्कयामास।<BR>II To prove or evince: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

argument
ARGUMENT:<BR>I A process of reasoning:<BR>(1)<BR>तर्कः;<BR>(2) वितर्कः।<BR>II Any reason alleged:<BR>(1) युक्तिः,<BR>when all a. s fail<BR>युक्तिष्वप्यवसन्नासु;<BR>(2) उप्पत्तिः Ki. ii. 23.<BR>III A debate, dis-<BR>-cussion: q. v.: वादानुवादः।<BR>IV The subject of<BR>a discourse, etc.: Ph. I will give the a. (of<BR>the play) संक्षेपत इतिवृत्तमभिधीयते, Tārānāth: v.<BR>Subect. v. An abstract summary: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

argumentation
ARGUMENTATION: तर्कः: v. Reasoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

argumentative
ARGUMENTATIVE: तार्किकः (की, कं): Ph.<BR>it is<BR>a. of almighty power in the creator<BR>एतदीश्वरस्य<BR> सर्वशक्तित्वं प्रदर्शयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arid
ARID:<BR>(1) शुष्कः (ष्का, ष्कं);<BR>(2) परिशुष्कः (ष्का, ष्कं):<BR>v. Dry, parched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aridity
ARIDITY: शुष्कता।: v. Dryness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aries
ARIES: a constellation: मेषः; मेषराशिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aright
ARIGHT:<BR>(1) युक्तम्,<BR>(2) यथोचितम्;<BR>(3) सम्यक्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arise
ARISE:<BR>(1) उदेति (इ, c. 2);<BR>(2) उद्गच्छति (गम्,<BR>c. 1): v. To rise, produce (iv). N. B.<BR>These two verbs are used in all the senses<BR>the English verb:<BR>a. ing from the seat<BR>आस-<BR>नादुद्वन्, Ki. ii. 57.;<BR>the moon arose<BR>उदगात् सुधा-<BR>सूतिः, K.; does (not)<BR>your fear a., maiden<BR>उदेति<BR> ते भीरपि किन्नु बाले, N. iii. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arising from
ARISING FROM (as adj.):<BR>(1) जः (जा, जं) or<BR>जनितः (ता, तं) (in comp.),<BR>the infamy a. from<BR>the assassination of Parvateśvara<BR>पर्वतेश्वरविनाश-<BR>जनितस्यायशसः, Mu. iii.;<BR>(2) भवः, उद्भवः, प्रभवः<BR>(वा, वं) (in comp.),<BR>the darkness a. from youth<BR>is very impervious<BR>अतिगहनं तमो यौवनप्रभवभ, K.;<BR>(3) उत्थः, समुत्थः (त्था, त्थं),<BR>bodily pains are<BR>those a. from diseases etc.<BR>तत्र शारीरं व्याध्याद्यु त्थम्,<BR>S.p. b.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aristocracy
ARISTOCRACY:<BR>I A form of Government:<BR>*कुलीनशासनम्<BR>or<BR>कुलीनप्रभुत्वम्।<BR>II The persons<BR>of whom it is composed *कुलीनसम्प्रदायः or<BR>राज्यशासककुलीनवर्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aristocrat
ARISTOCRAT:<BR>I A member of an aristo-<BR>-cracy: *कुलीनः।<BR>II One who supports<BR>aristocracy: *कुलीनशासनसमर्थकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aristocratic
ARISTOCRATIC: Ph.<BR>a. government<BR>*कुलीनशास-<BR>नम्;<BR>a. pride<BR>कुलाभिमानः;<BR>of a. family<BR>कुलीनः<BR>(ना, नं)<BR>or<BR>अभिजातः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arithmetic
ARITHMETIC:<BR>(1) अङ्कविद्या;<BR>(2) पाटीगणितम्।<BR>The<BR>eight rules of a.<BR>परिकर्माष्टकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arithmetical
ARITHMETICAL:<BR>(1) अङ्कविद्याविषयकः (का, कं)<BR>(relating to a.);<BR>(2) अङ्कविद्यानुसारेण (according<BR>to the rules of a.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arithmetician
ARITHMETICIAN: अङ्कविद्याविशारदः (दा, दं) and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ark
ARK:<BR>I A vessel: q. v.:<BR>(1) नौः;<BR>(2) तरणी।<BR>II. A. chest:<BR>(1) पेटिका;<BR>(2) आधारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arm
ARM (subs.):<BR>I Of the human body:<BR>(1)<BR>भुजः;<BR>(2) बाहुः;<BR>(3) दोस्; (m);<BR>(4) प्रवेष्टः।<BR>A.<BR>The fore a.<BR>प्रकोष्ठः।<BR>The upper a.<BR>प्रगण्डः।<BR>II<BR>any object analogous to an arm: (a) of a<BR>tree शाखा। v. Bough. (b) of a chair: *बाहुः।<BR>(c) of the sea or of a river:<BR>(1) वङ्कः;<BR>(2)<BR>वक्रम्। (d) of the polypi: v. Feelers.<BR>III<BR>A weapon: v. Arms.<BR>IV A branch of the<BR>military service: अङ्गम्। v. Power: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arm
ARM (v. i.):<BR>I To take arms:<BR>(1) संनह्यति (नह्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">Page038</a>]<BR>c. 4) (=to accoutre),<BR>ordered the generals to<BR>a.<BR>सेनापतीन् संनहनार्थमादिशत्, Ku. xv. 5.;<BR>(2)<BR>अस्त्रं गृह्वाति (ग्रह्, c. 9);<BR>(3) सायुधः (धा, धं)<BR>भवति।<BR>II To prepare for war युद्धाय सज्जी-<BR>भवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arm
ARM (v. t.):<BR>(1) सन्नाहयति (c. of नह);<BR>(2)<BR>सायुधः (धा, धं) करोति;<BR>(3) सज्जीकरोति (=to<BR>equip).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

armada
ARMADA: पोतावलिः। v. Fleet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

armadillo
ARMADILLO: विलेशयः क्षुद्रजन्तुविशेषः; *वर्मधरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

armament
ARMAMENT:<BR>I A body of forces equipped<BR>for war: बलम्: v. Army, fleet.<BR>II The guns<BR>and ammunitions of a man-of-war: युद्धो-<BR>पकरणानि (n. pl.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

armed
ARMED (adj.):<BR>(1) सायुधः (धा, धं);<BR>(2) संनद्धः<BR>(द्धा, द्धं)<BR>(3) सज्जः (ज्जा, ज्जं) (=equipped).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

armhole
ARMHOLE:<BR>(1) कक्षः;<BR>(2) बाहुमूलम्;<BR>(3) भुजकोटरः;<BR>(4) कक्षालयः, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

armistice
ARMISTICE:<BR>(1) अयुद्धम्;<BR>(2) युद्धविरतिः; and sim.<BR>comp. s. Ph.<BR>from filial affection, asked for<BR>two day's a.<BR>ययाचे पुत्रवात्सल्यादयुद्धं दिवसद्वयम्; Raj.<BR>v. Truce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

armless
ARMLESS:<BR>I Without an arm:<BR>(1) अभुजः (जा,<BR> जं);<BR>(2) भुजहीनः (ना, नं); etc.<BR>II Without<BR>weapons:<BR>(1) अशस्त्रः (स्त्रा, स्त्रं);<BR>(2) अनायुधः<BR>(धा, धं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

armlet
ARMLET: वलयः v. Bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

armour
ARMOUR:<BR>(1) वर्मन् (n).;<BR>(2) कवच (mn.);<BR>(3)<BR>वारबाणः;<BR>(4) संनाहः;<BR>(5) कञ्चुकः;<BR>(6) तनुत्रम्।<BR>Chain a.<BR>जालिका (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

armourer
ARMOURER: शस्त्रकारः; Perh. असिधारकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

armoury
ARMOURY:<BR>(1) आयुधागारम्;<BR>(2) शस्त्रगृहम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arm-pit
ARM-PIT: कक्षः; v. Arm-hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arms
ARMS:<BR>I Weapons:<BR>(1) शस्त्रम्;<BR>(2) अस्त्रम्;<BR>(3) आयुधः;<BR>(4) हेतिः;<BR>(5) प्रहरणम्।<BR>II War,<BR>hostility: q. v.<BR>III Armorial bearings:<BR>*कुलचिह्रानि (n. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

army
ARMY:<BR>(1) सैन्यम्;<BR>(2) बलम्;<BR>(3) दण्डचक्रम्;<BR>(4)<BR>पताकिनी;<BR>(5) चमूः;<BR>(6) व्यूहः (an a. in battle<BR>array);<BR>(7) चतुरङ्गबलम् (an a. comprising the<BR>four complements, elephants, cars, horse<BR>and foot). N. B. सैन्यम् and बलम् are also used<BR>in the plural in the ‘singular’ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aroma
AROMA:<BR>(1) गन्धः;<BR>(2) सौरभम्;<BR>(3) आमोदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aromatic
AROMATIC:<BR>(1) सुगन्धि (mfn.);<BR>(2) सुगन्धः<BR>(न्धा, न्धं);<BR>(3) सुरभि (mfn.): v. Fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

around
AROUND (prep.): परितः (with acc.), a. the altar<BR>वेदीं परितः, B. i. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

around
AROUND (adv.):<BR>(1) परितः;<BR>(2) सर्वतः,<BR>looking<BR>a.<BR>सर्वतो विलोक्य, U.;<BR>(3) समन्ततः, समन्तात्, K.;<BR>(4) विष्वक्,<BR>with sparks scattered all a.<BR>विष्वग्वि-<BR>सृतस्फुलिङगः, Ki. xvi. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arouse
AROUSE:<BR>I From sleep: प्रबोधयति: v. To<BR>awake.<BR>II From inaction<BR>(1) उत्तेजयति<BR>(तिज्, c. 10),<BR>will go to the island of Mahendra<BR>to a. Jāmadagnya<BR>जामदग्न्यमुत्तेजयितुं महेन्द्रद्वीपमेव<BR> गच्छावः Vi. ii.;<BR>(2) उत्थापयति (c. of स्था),<BR>and<BR>a. ing his natural enemies<BR>उत्थाप्य सहजांश्च द्विषः<BR>D. iv.;<BR>(3) प्रबोधयति (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrack
ARRACK:<BR>(1) ताली;<BR>(2) ताडिः<BR>or<BR>ताडी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arraign
ARRAIGN: अमियुनक्ति<BR>or<BR>योजयति (युज्, c. 7 and<BR>10): v. To accuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arraignment
ARRAIGNMENT: अभियोगः: v. Accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrange
ARRANGE:<BR>I To put in order:<BR>(1) रचयति, वि-,<BR>(रच्, c. 1),<BR>a. ing the division of the forest<BR>विर-<BR>चय्य काननविभागम्, Ki. xii. 44.;<BR>(2) विन्यस्यति<BR>(अस्, c. 4),<BR>merely by a. ing sentences<BR>पदविन्यास-<BR>मात्रेण;<BR>(3) यथाक्रमं स्थापयति (c. of स्था).<BR>II<BR>To adjust, settle, determine: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrangement
ARRANGEMENT:<BR>I Orderly disposition:<BR>(1)<BR>रचना;<BR>(2) विन्यासः;<BR>(3) संविधानम्।<BR>II Settle-<BR>-ment, adjustment, agreement: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrant
ARRANT: पामरः (री, रं): v. Infamous, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arras
ARRAS: v. Tapestry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

array
ARRAY (subs.):<BR>I Battle-array: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Arrangement, order: q. v.<BR>III Dress,<BR>clothing: q. v.: परिच्छदः।<BR>IV Of jurymen<BR>*न्यायप्रतिभूगणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

array
ARRAY (v. t.):<BR>I To arrange, draw up: q. v.<BR>रचयति, वि-, (रच्, c. 10).<BR>II To dress, deck:<BR>q. v. भूषयति।<BR>III To select jurymen *न्याय-<BR>प्रतिभुवो निरूपयति (रूप्, c. 10).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrear
ARREAR, ARREARS: *अवशिष्टदेयम्, pay up your a. s<BR>*अवशिष्टदेयं परिशोधय;<BR>I owe large a. s<BR>*मया<BR> बहु परिशोधनीयम्;<BR>a. of rent<BR>*करशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrest
ARREST (v. t.):<BR>I To obstruct, stop: q. v.: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">Page039</a>]<BR>रूणद्धि (रुध्, c. 7).<BR>II To apprehend legally:<BR>(1) आसेधति (सिध, c. 1);<BR>(2) धरति<BR>or<BR>धारयति<BR>(धृ, c. 1 and 10):<BR>(3) गृह्वाति (ग्रह्, c. 9).<BR>III To fix, engage: Ph. (it) a. s my eyes<BR>बध्नाति मे चक्षुः; R.;<BR>it a. s my attention<BR>मामनन्य-<BR>मनस्कं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrest
ARREST (subs.):<BR>(1) आसेधः;<BR>(2) धृतिः (?). Ph.<BR>a. of judgment<BR>*निर्णयरोधः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrival
ARRIVAL:<BR>(1) आगमनम्;<BR>(2) आगमः;<BR>(3) उपया-<BR>नम् (rare), Ku. vii. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrive
ARRIVE (v. i.):<BR>(1) प्र-आप्नोति, अव-, सम्प्र-, अनुप्र-,<BR>(आप्, c. 5), a. d at the hermitage af the saint<BR>महर्षेः प्रापदाश्रमम्; R. i. 48.;<BR>(2) आ-सीदति, समा-,<BR>(सद्, c. 1),<BR>Kusha a. ing at the banks of the<BR>Sarayū<BR>कूलं समासाद्य कुशः सरय्वाः, R. xvi. 35.;<BR>(3) प्र-पद्यते (पद्, c. 4),<BR>a. ed at the hermitage<BR>of Atri<BR>अत्रेस्तपोवनं प्रपेदे, B. iv. 19.;<BR>after child-<BR>hood, she a. ed at youth<BR>बाल्यात् परं साथ वयः प्रपेदे,<BR>Ku. i. 31. N. B. Observe that all these<BR>verbs take an acc. Ph.:<BR>a. ed at no conclu-<BR>sion<BR>निर्णयं नाससाद;<BR>the news a. ed of the ass-<BR>assination of his father<BR>पितृवधवार्ता समागता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrogance
ARROGANCE:<BR>(1) औद्धत्यम्;<BR>(2) प्रागल्भ्यम्;<BR>(3)<BR>उत्सेकः;<BR>(4) अवलेपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrogant
ARROGANT:<BR>(1) उद्धतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) प्रगल्भः<BR>(ल्भा, ल्भं);<BR>(3) उत्सिक्तः (क्ता, क्तं);<BR>(4) अव-<BR>लिप्तः (प्ता, प्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrogantly
ARROGANTLY:<BR>(1) उद्धतम्;<BR>(2) प्रगल्भम्;<BR>(3) साव-<BR>लेपम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrogate
ARROGATE: *अन्यायतः गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9) or<BR>स्वीकरोति (कृ, c. 8), अन्यायेन स्वस्वत्वं ख्यापयति<BR>(c. of ख्या)<BR>or<BR>प्रकटयति (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrogation
ARROGATION: *न्याय्यग्रहणम्; अन्याय्यस्वीकारः;<BR> अन्यायेन स्वस्वत्वख्यापनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrow
ARROW:<BR>(1) शरः;<BR>(2) बाणः;<BR>(3) इषुः;<BR>(4)<BR>सायकः<BR>or<BR>शायकः;<BR>(5) मार्गणः;<BR>(6) शिलीमुखः;<BR>(7) आशुगः;<BR>(8) पत्री;<BR>(9) पृषत्कः;<BR>(10) विशिखः<BR>A shower of a. s<BR>शरवर्षः। To discharge, shoot a. s<BR>शरं निरस्यति (अस्, c. 4), क्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6),<BR>Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrow-head
ARROW-HEAD:<BR>(1) फलम्,<BR>(2) शल्यम्;<BR>(3) बाणाग्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrow-headed
ARROW-HEADED: *फलाकारः (रा, रं), a. characters,<BR>*फलाकारावर्णाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrow-root
ARROW-ROOT: खाद्योपयोगी द्रव्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arrowy
ARROWY:<BR>I Of arrows: शर- (in comp.)<BR>a. shower<BR>शरवर्षः।<BR>II Crooked like an arrow:<BR>कुटिलः (ला, लं): v. Crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arsenal
ARSENAL:<BR>(1) आयुधागारम्;<BR>(2) शस्त्रगृहम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arsenic
ARSENIC: मनःशिला (=red a.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arson
ARSON:<BR>(1) आगारदाहः;<BR>(2) गृहदाहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

art
ART:<BR>I As opposed to nature: शिल्पम्।<BR>II<BR>As opposed to science: कला,<BR>in the a. s of<BR>dancing, singing, playing, and acting<BR>नृत्यगीत-<BR>वाद्यनाट्यकलासु, D. ii. Ph. the industrial a. s<BR>शिल्पविद्या;<BR>the fine a. s<BR>सङ्गीतादि-कला (?) or<BR>*श्रेष्ठकलाः (f. pl.).<BR>III Skill, dexterity:<BR>q. v.: कौशलम्।<BR>IV Cunning, artifice: q. v.<BR>छलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

arterial
ARTERIAL; expr. by the gen. of words given<BR>under artery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

artery
ARTERY:<BR>(1) रक्तवाहिनी नाडिः;<BR>(2) रक्तवहा शिरा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

artful
ARTFUL: चतुरः (रा, रं), Ku. iv. 20.: v. Cunn-<BR>-ing, crafty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

artfully
ARTFULLY:<BR>(1) निपुणम्;<BR>(2) कौशलेन। v. Cunn-<BR>-ingly, ingeniously, craftily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

artfulness
ARTFULNESS:<BR>(1) चातुर्यम्;<BR>(2) चातुरी: v.<BR>Cunning, ingenuity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

artichoke
ARTICHOKE: शाकविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

article
ARTICLE (subs.):<BR>I A part of speech:<BR>विशेष्यस्वभावनिरूपकाव्ययशब्दः।<BR>II A commodity<BR>or substance: q. v. द्रव्यम्।<BR>III A Clause<BR>in a contract etc.: प्रकरणम् (?). Ph.<BR>we<BR>enter into this a. to remove this doubt<BR>एतामाशङ्कां<BR> निवर्तयितुमिदमधिकरणमारभ्यते, S. iii. 34.;<BR>the a.<BR>about Harisha Chandra was very good,<BR>*हरीशचन्द्र-<BR>विषयकः प्रबन्धोऽत्युत्तम आसीत्; the a. s of war<BR>*सैनिकनियमावलिः।<BR>IV A distinct part:<BR>(1) अंशः (=part);<BR>(2) विषयः (= subject). V.<BR>Moment:<BR>(1) क्षणः;<BR>(2) समयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

article
ARTICLE (v. t.): *नियमपत्रेण बध्नाति (बध्न्, c. 9.),<BR>an a. d clerk<BR>*नियमबद्धः लेखकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

articular
ARTICULAR: सन्धिगतः (ता, तं),<BR>a. disease<BR>सन्धिगत-<BR>रोगः, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

articulate
ARTICULATE (adj.):<BR>(1) स्पष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>(2)<BR>स्फुटः (टा, टं): v. Distinct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

articulate
ARTICULATE (v. t.)<BR>I To utter distinctly: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=040" target="_blank">Page040</a>]<BR>स्फुटं<BR>or<BR>स्पष्टम् उच्चारयति (c. of चर्), उदीरयति (ईर्,<BR>c. 10.), etc.<BR>II To joint: संदधाति (धा,<BR>c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

articulation
ARTICULATION:<BR>I Of words: Ph. distinct a.<BR>स्पष्टता वर्णोच्चारणे K.<BR>II Of bones: सन्धिः: v.<BR>Joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

artifice
ARTIFICE:<BR>(1) उपायः:<BR>(2) छलं;<BR>(3) उपाधिः,<BR>women are originators of all a. s<BR>स्त्रियश्चोपाधीना-<BR>मुद्भवक्षेत्रम्, D. N. B.<BR>(2) and<BR>(3) always in the<BR>bad sense: v. Stratagem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

artificer
ARTIFICER:<BR>I An artisan: q. v. शिल्पी।<BR>II<BR>A maker, contriver: q. v.: कर्ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

artificial
ARTIFICIAL:<BR>I Made by art: कृत्रिमः (मा, मं),<BR>herds of a. young elephants<BR>कृत्रिमकरिकलभयूथानि,<BR>K. Ph.<BR>sometimes over a. hills<BR>कदाचित्<BR> क्रीडापर्वतेषु, K.<BR>a. lake<BR>केलिपल्वलम्, N. ;<BR>a.<BR>clouds<BR>मायामेघमालाः, K.<BR>II. Feigned, fictitious:<BR>q. v.: कृत्रिमः (मा, मं).<BR>III Ingenious.<BR>skilful: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

artillery
ARTILLERY:<BR>I Weapons in general: अस्त्राणि<BR>(n. pl.).<BR>II Cannon with all that apper-<BR>-tains to them: *कामानानि or (when the<BR>meaning is not clear) सोपकरणकामानानि<BR>(n. pl.).<BR>III The troops who manage can-<BR>-non etc.: *कामानबलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

artisan
ARTISAN:<BR>(1) शिल्पिन् (m.);<BR>(2) शिल्पकारः;<BR>(3)<BR>कारुः<BR>or<BR>कारुकः;<BR>(4) कर्मकारः।<BR>The workshop of<BR>an a.<BR>शिल्पशाला<BR>or<BR>शिल्पिशाला।<BR>The business of<BR>an a.<BR>शिल्पकर्मन् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

artist
ARTIST:<BR>I An artisan: q. v.<BR>II A painter:<BR>q. v. चित्रकरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

artistic
ARTISTIC: विचित्रः (त्रा, त्रं) (?): v. Ingenious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

artless
ARTLESS:<BR>I Simple, frank, guileless: q. v.;<BR>(1) अमायः (या, यं);<BR>(2) ऋजु (mfn.).<BR>II<BR>Contrived without art:<BR>(1) नीरसः (सा, सं)<BR>(=devoid of taste);<BR>(2) अलङ्कारहीनः (ना,<BR> नं) (=unadorned).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

artlessly
ARTLESSLY: i. e. Simply, frankly: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>मायां विना;<BR>(2) अकपटेन;<BR>(3) आर्जवेन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

artlessness
ARTLESSNESS:<BR>(1) अमायिता;<BR>(2) सरलता;<BR>(3)<BR>आर्जवम्: v. Simplicity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

as
AS:<BR>I As a particle of comparison:<BR>(1)<BR>वत् affixed, (he who looks on) other's wives as<BR>mothers, on other's things as clods<BR>मातृवत् परदारेषु<BR> परद्रव्येषु लोष्ट्रवत्, H. i.;<BR>as before<BR>पूर्ववत्;<BR>(2) यथा<BR>(either in comp. to expr. sim. comparison,<BR>or with तथा<BR>or<BR>एवं to expr. as......so......<BR>also to introduce illustrations): as ordered<BR>यथानिदेशं;<BR>as prescribed<BR>यथाविधि; as before<BR>यथापुरा, Sa. vi.;<BR>as eating is inferred from<BR>nourishment or country from its language, so is<BR>knowable inferred from knowledge,<BR>यथा पुष्टया<BR> भोजनमनुमीयते यथा च भाषया देशः तथा ज्ञानाकारेण<BR> ज्ञेयमनुमेयम्। D. s. (see also R. iii. 23 and<BR>notice the repetition of यथा in such cases);<BR>as animals attempt to fly away when they see<BR>men with sticks, so....<BR>यथा पश्वादयः दण्डोद्यतकरं<BR> पुरूषमभिमुखमुपलभ्य पलायितुमारभन्ते एवं॥ S. i. p.;<BR>as for instance, fire is inferred from smoke<BR>यथा<BR> धूमेनाग्निरिति, N. d. As for instance: sometimes<BR>expr. by तथाहिः<BR>he, as a rule, enjoyed the pleasures<BR>of youth as for instance, sometimes roamed over<BR>artificial mountains, sometimes walked through<BR>summer houses<BR>स प्रायशो यौवनसुखमनुबभूव, तथाहि<BR> कदाचित् क्रीडापर्वतेषु विचचार कदाचिल्लतागृहेषु बभ्राम,<BR>K.<BR>II. While: expr. by the pres. part:<BR>as he went, he thought<BR>व्रजंश्च समर्थयामास, K.<BR>III. Since, in as much as: q. v.:<BR>(1) by the<BR>abl. and when the subs. ends in ता<BR>or<BR>आ by<BR>the ins.: as the motion of the vessels (at sea)<BR>depends on wind<BR>वाताधीनपोतगमनत्वात्, K. b.;<BR>as there was much political work<BR>राजकार्यस्य<BR> बहुलतया Sa. vi.;<BR>(2) यतः॥।ततः॥ Miscell:<BR>as long as one lives<BR>यावज्जीवं; as far as the ocean<BR>आ समुद्रात्;<BR>as high as the knee<BR>जानुदघ्नः (घ्ना, घ्नं);<BR>as yet<BR>अद्यापि। N. B. as, when it connects two<BR>subs. s in apposition is expr. by भूत्वा<BR>or<BR>कृत्वा:<BR>I will remain as your queen<BR>तव महिषी भूत्वा तिष्ठामि;<BR>sent me to you as his agent<BR>मां प्रतिनिधिं कृत्वा<BR> त्वत्सकाशं प्रेरयामास।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

as being
AS BEING: Expr. By the ins. of subs. s in ता or<BR>by the abl. in other cases:<BR>a. few<BR>अल्पतया;<BR>a.<BR>a child<BR>बालतया;<BR>a. weak<BR>दौर्बल्यात्;<BR>a. wonder-<BR>ful<BR>अद्भुतत्वात्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

as if
AS IF: इव (always after the word it governs):<BR>passed the night as if in a moment<BR>क्षणादिव क्षणदां [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">Page041</a>]<BR>क्षपितवती, K.;<BR>as if painted, as if engraved, as<BR>if paralyzed<BR>लिखितमिवोत्कीर्णमिव स्तम्भितमिव, K.;<BR>as if from hell to heaven<BR>नरकादिव स्वर्गम्, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

as follows
AS FOLLOWS: इति (at the end of the quota-<BR>-tion, which is placed first in Sanskrit).<BR>see R. iii. 47., Ku. iv. 43. Ph.:<BR>began to<BR>speak as follows<BR>वक्तुमित्थमुपचक्रमे वचः, K. xiii.<BR>36.;<BR>Bachaspati spoke a.<BR>वाचस्पतिरवाचेदं, Ku.<BR>ii. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

as for
AS FOR, AS TO: विषयः (या, यं)<BR>or<BR>विषयकः (का, कं)<BR>in comp.:<BR>as for his valour, I will not say a<BR>word<BR>तस्य शौर्यविषयं न किञ्चिद् वदामि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

as soon as
AS SOON AS:<BR>(1) by a comp. adj. with मात्रः (त्रा,<BR> त्रं),<BR>he who does not put down an enemy or a<BR>disease a. it appears<BR>जातमात्रं न यः शत्रुं रोगं च<BR> प्रशमं नयेत्, P. i. 8.;<BR>(2) यदा॥।तदैव। Ph.:<BR>a. I spoke<BR>मद्वचनान्तरमेव, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

as well as
AS WELL AS: च॥॥॥चः<BR>anointed with nectar<BR>a. poison<BR>दिग्धोऽमृतेन च विषेण च, Ma. i.;<BR>as a<BR>mother a. as a father<BR>माता च पिता च भूत्वा D. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

asafoetida
ASAFŒTIDA:<BR>(1) हिङ्गु (n.);<BR>(2) जतुकम्, A.;<BR>(3) वाह्लीकम्, A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ascarides
ASCARIDES: A disease: कृमिरोगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ascend
ASCEND (v. i.): आरोहति (with acc.): v. To<BR>mount, rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ascend
ASCEND (v. t.): आ-रोहति, अधि-, (रुह, c. 1.): v.<BR>To mount.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ascendant
ASCENDANT: प्रभुत्वम्: v. Superiority.<BR>To be<BR>in the a.:<BR>जयति (जि, c. 1.) (=to flourish)<BR>(only when it conveys the idea of flourish-<BR>-ing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ascendancy
ASCENDANCY: प्रभुत्वम्: v. Authority, influence.<BR>Ph:<BR>Chandrapālita, by various amusements,<BR>gained complete a. over Bihārabhadra<BR>चन्द्रपालितो<BR> विविघाभिः क्रीडाभिर्विहारभद्रमात्मसादकरोत्, D. viii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ascension
ASCENSION: v. Ascent. A. -day: *कृष्टस्य<BR> स्वर्गारोहणपर्वन् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ascent
ASCENT:<BR>I The act of ascending:<BR>(1) आरोहः;<BR>(2) आरोहणम्;<BR>(3) अधिरोहणम्।<BR>II The way<BR>of ascending:<BR>(1) आरोहमार्गः;<BR>(2) आरोहणपथः।<BR>III Inclination, slope:<BR>the road has an a.<BR>of one foot per hundred.<BR>*प्रतिशतपादमेकपादोन्नतो<BR> मार्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ascertain
ASCERTAIN:<BR>I To find out:<BR>(1) जानाति, परि-,<BR>(ज्ञा, c. 9),<BR>a. what is the time now<BR>ज्ञायतां का<BR> वेला वर्तत इति, Mu. v.;<BR>(2) निरूपयति (रूप्, c.<BR>10.),<BR>I will follow him and a. what it is<BR>तदनु<BR> गत्वा किमेतदिति निरूपयामि, H. iii.;<BR>(3) निश्चिनोति<BR>(चि, c. 5.).<BR>a. ing that the remaining one was<BR>the king<BR>निश्चित्य शेषं तमसौ नरेशं, N. xiv. 14.:<BR>(4) निर्णयति (नी, c. 1.),<BR>to a. this, we begin the<BR>second and the third part<BR>तन्निर्णयाय द्वितीयतृतीयौ<BR> पादावारभ्येते, S. ii. p.;<BR>(5) निर्धारयति (c. of धृ),<BR>when a thing is a. ed by letter<BR>निर्धारितेऽर्थे लेखेन,<BR>Si. ii. 70.<BR>II To make certain: स्थिरीकरोति:<BR>v. Certain.<BR>III To assure: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ascertainable
ASCERTAINABLE:<BR>(1) निर्णेयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) निरू-<BR>पणीयः (या, यं);<BR>(3) निर्धार्यः (र्या, र्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ascertainment
ASCERTAINMENT:<BR>(1) निरूपणम्;<BR>(2) निर्णयः;<BR>(3) निर्धारणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ascetic
ASCETIC:<BR>(1) यतिः;<BR>(2) योगी;<BR>(3) वैरागी;<BR>(4) संन्यासी;<BR>(5) तपस्वी;<BR>(6) तापसः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

asceticism
ASCETICISM:<BR>(1) वैराग्यम्;<BR>(2) संन्यासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ascites
ASCITES: i. e. Dropsy of the peritoneum: उदरी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ascribable
ASCRIBABLE:<BR>(1) आरोपणीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) अध्या-<BR>रोपणीयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ascribe
ASCRIBE:<BR>I To refer to as an attribute:<BR>आ-रोपयति, अध्या-, (c. of रुह्),<BR>to whom divine<BR>nature has been falsely a. d<BR>अध्यारोपितवितथदेवतानु-<BR>भावः, D. i.;<BR>II To refer to, as an effect:<BR>expr. by circumlo.:<BR>common people a. every<BR>thing to fate<BR>दैवायत्तं सर्वमिति प्राकृता वदन्ति;<BR>the<BR>citizens a. ed his cure to the power of the charm<BR>*मन्त्रबलेनासावारोग्यं लेभ इति पौरैरधिगतम्। N. B. When<BR>the cause is<BR>a person,<BR>आरोपयति may be used:<BR>they a. ed to me the success of the day<BR>तद्दिवसस्य<BR> जयं मय्यारोपयामासुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ascription
ASCRIPTION:<BR>(1) आरोपणम्;<BR>(2) अध्यारोपणम्;<BR>(3) better by verb: v. To ascribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ash
ASH: a tree: वन्यवृक्षविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ash-white
ASH-WHITE:<BR>(1) भस्मधवलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) भूतिसितः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ashamed
ASHAMED:<BR>(1) लज्जितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) ह्वीतः (ता,<BR> तं);<BR>(3) व्रीडितः (ता, तं);<BR>(4) त्रपायुक्तः (क्ता, क्तं);<BR>(5) ह्रीणः (णा, णं).<BR>To make a.<BR>ह्रेपयति (c. of<BR>ह्री), v. To shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ashamed
ASHAMED, FEEL:<BR>(1) लज्जते (लज्ज्, c. 6.);<BR>(2)<BR>जिह्रेति (ह्री, c. 3.);<BR>(3) व्रीडाम् एति (इ, c. 2.). Si.<BR>xiv. 2.;<BR>(4) त्रपते (त्रप्, c. 1.) (rare);<BR>(5)<BR>ह्रिणीयते (rare) B. iii. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ashes
ASHES:<BR>(1) भस्मन् (n.), reduced Madana to a.<BR>भस्मावशेषं मदनं चकार, Ku. iii. 72.<BR>To reduce<BR>to a.<BR>भस्मीकरोति, भस्मसात् करोति।<BR>To be reduced<BR>to a.<BR>भस्मीभवति;<BR>(2) भूतिः, वि-, A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ashore
ASHORE:<BR>I On to the shore: तीरं; तटम्।<BR>II On the shore: तीरे; तटे; उत्तीरस्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ash-wednesday
ASH-WEDNESDAY: कृष्टीयपर्वभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ashy
ASHY: भास्मनः (नी, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aside
ASIDE: v. Apart. (to speak), a. (to any one):<BR>(1) अपवार्य;<BR>(2) जनान्तिकम्;<BR>(3) विजने।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

asinine
ASININE:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) गर्दमीयः (या, यं):<BR>v. Also stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ask
ASK:<BR>I To interrogate, enquire:<BR>(1) पृच्छति,<BR> परि-, सं-, (प्रच्छ्, c. 6.) (with double acc.),<BR>a.<BR>ed her attendants why she was weeping<BR>बाष्पहेतु-<BR>मस्याः परिजनमपृच्छत्, K. ;<BR>(2) अनु-युनक्ति (युज्,<BR>c. 7.),<BR>the king a. ed the priest<BR>अन्वयुंक्त गुरुमीश्वरः<BR> क्षितेः, R. xi. 62.;<BR>(3) जिज्ञासते। v. To enquire.<BR>N. B. The sense of this verb is often expr.<BR>by वदति, अभिदधाति, etc. (=to speak):<BR>the king<BR>a. ed her why she was weeping and why she was<BR>not bedecked<BR>भूमिपालस्तामवादीत् देवि किमर्थ रुद्यते<BR> किमर्थं च नालङ्कृ तासि, K. Ph.<BR>may I a. who you<BR>are<BR>कां पुनरत्रभवतीमवगच्छामि, U. ii.<BR>II To<BR>request, beg:<BR>(1) याचति, -ते (याच्, c. 1),<BR>a. ed her for drink (ताम्) अयाचत च पानीयम्, D.<BR>vi.;<BR>(2) अर्थयते, प्र-, अभि-, (अर्थ्, c. 10),<BR>let<BR>me a. this stag for news about my darling<BR>इमं<BR> तावत् प्रियाप्रवृत्तये सारङ्गमासीनमम्यर्थये, V. iv.;<BR>(3)<BR>वृणोति (वृ, c. 5.), a. ed for Rāma's banishment<BR>ववार रामस्य वनप्रयाणम्, B. iii. 6.;<BR>(4) नाथति,<BR> -ते (नाथ् c. 1.) (rare),<BR>why don't you a. the<BR>mountain king<BR>नाथसे किमु पतिं न भूभृतः, Ki. xiii.<BR>59. N. B. All these take two acc. s, one of<BR>person and one of object a. ed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

askance
ASKANCE:<BR>(1) साचि;<BR>(2) तिर्यक्;<BR>(3)<BR>तिरश्चीनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

asker
ASKER:<BR>I An enquirer: प्रष्टा।<BR>II A petitioner;<BR>(1) याचकः;<BR>(2) प्रार्थकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aslant
ASLANT:<BR>(1) तिर्यक्;<BR>(2) तिरश्चीनम्: v. Obli-<BR>-quely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

asleep
ASLEEP:<BR>(1) सुप्तः (प्ता, प्तं):<BR>fast a.<BR>प्रसुप्तः (प्ता, प्तं)<BR>whether apparently or really a.<BR>किं लक्ष्यसुप्तमुत<BR> परमार्थसुप्तम्, Mr. iii.;<BR>(2) निद्रितः (ता, तं);<BR>(3)<BR>शयितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

