attach
ATTACH:<BR>I To fasten, lit. and fig.:<BR>(1)<BR>आसञ्जयति (c. of सञ्ज्);<BR>(2) संश्लेषयति (c. of श्लिष्);<BR>(3) लगयति (c. of लग्) ?.<BR>II<BR>To a. one's<BR>property<BR>*क्रोकं करोति। (with gen.): v. Also<BR>to arrest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attached
ATTACHED: आसक्तः (क्ता, क्तं).<BR>To be a.<BR>आसज्यते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attachment
ATTACHMENT (subs.):<BR>I Connexion, con-<BR>-tact: q. v.<BR>II Affection, devotion:<BR>(1)<BR>आसक्तिः;<BR>(2) प्रसक्तिः;<BR>(3) सङ्गः;<BR>(4) आसङ्गः।<BR>N. B. All these words cons. with the loc.<BR>III In law:<BR>a. of property<BR>*क्रोकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attack
ATTACK (subs):<BR>(1) आक्रमः;<BR>(2) आक्रमणम्;<BR>(3)<BR>अभिक्रमः;<BR>(4) अभियोगः;<BR>(5) अभिग्रहः;<BR>(6)<BR>अवस्कन्दः<BR>or<BR>अवस्कन्दनम् (=storming).<BR>A. of any<BR>disease:<BR>आक्रमः, -णम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attack
ATTACK (v. t.);<BR>I Of physical force:<BR>(1)<BR>आ-क्रामति<BR>or<BR>क्राम्यति, अभि-, (क्रम्, c. 1. and 4.);<BR>(2) अभियुनक्ति<BR>or<BR>योजयति (युज् c. 7. and 10.),<BR>Anantavarmā raised an army to a. him<BR>अनन्तवर्मा<BR> तममियोक्तुं बलसमुत्थानमकरोत्, D. viii.;<BR>(3)<BR>अव-स्कन्दति (स्कन्द्, c. 1.) (=to fall upon),<BR>Mādhavasena coming to me was, in the way,<BR>a. ed and seized by your Antapāla<BR>माधवसेनो ममो-<BR>पान्तिकमुपसर्पन्नन्तरा त्वदीयेनान्तपालेनावस्कन्द्य गृहीतः,<BR>Mal. i. To a. in defence:<BR>(1) प्रत्यमियुनक्ति;<BR>(2) प्रतिगृह्वाति (ग्रह c. 9.), a. ed the opposite army<BR>प्रतिबलं प्रतिजग्राह, D. i.;<BR>(3) प्रतियुध्यते (युध्, c.<BR>4.). v. To fight.<BR>II To assail with words:<BR>(1) आक्रामति;<BR>(2) अवस्कन्दयति (स्कन्द् c. 10.),<BR>Vi. iii.;<BR>(3) आ-हन्ति, अभि-, परा-, (हन्, c. 2.),<BR>a. ed by his haughty words<BR>वचौभिरुद्धतैः पराहतः, Ki.<BR>xiv. 1.<BR>III To a. an opinion etc.:<BR>(1)<BR>परामर्षति (मृष्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) प्रत्यवतिष्ठते (स्था, c. 1.)<BR>(with loc.) (=to stand up against).<BR>IV<BR>Of disease:<BR>(1) आक्रामति, a. ed with fever<BR>ज्वराक्रान्तः (न्ता, न्तं);<BR>(2) चरति (चर्, c. 1.),<BR>O<BR>fever, listen to me how you would a. men<BR>शृणुष्व<BR> ज्वर सन्देशं यथा लोके चरिष्यसि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attain
ATTAIN (v. t.):<BR>(1) अधि-गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.),<BR>even<BR>after a. ing knowledge<BR>श्रुतमप्यधिगम्य, Ki. ii.<BR>41.;<BR>(2) आ-सीदति (सद्, c. 1.),<BR>the king will a.<BR>divine form by means of charms<BR>राजा किल मन्त्रबलेन<BR> देवयोग्यं वपुरासादयिष्यति, D. iii.;<BR>(3) प्राप्नोति: v.<BR>To obtain;<BR>(4) स्पृशति (स्पृश्, c. 6.) (=to<BR>touch), by this time would have a. ed your age<BR>इयता कालेन तवेमां वयोवस्थामस्प्रक्ष्येतां, D. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attain
ATTAIN (v. i.):<BR>(1) अधिगच्छति (with acc.);<BR>(2) आसीदति (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attainable
ATTAINABLE:<BR>(1) लभ्यः (भ्या, भ्यं);<BR>(2) सुलभः<BR>(भा, भं);<BR>(3) प्राप्यः (प्या, प्यं)<BR>(4) अधिगम्यः (म्या,<BR> म्यं);<BR>(5) आसादनीयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attainder
ATTAINDER: v. Stain. Ph.: a bill of a.<BR>*अभियोगपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attainment
ATTAINMENT:<BR>I The act of attaining:<BR>(1)<BR>अधिगमः;<BR>(2) लाभः;<BR>(3) प्राप्तिः;<BR>(4) अवाप्तिः। By<BR>the a. of: expr. by the part. of the verb ‘to<BR>attain’. For the a. of: expr. by the inf. of<BR>the verb ‘to attain’.<BR>II Of knowledge:<BR>(1) व्युत्पत्तिः;<BR>(2) पारदर्शिता,<BR>of great mathe-<BR>matical a. s<BR>गणितशास्त्रस्य पारदर्शी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attaint
ATTAINT:<BR>I To stain: q. v.<BR>II Leg t. t.:<BR>a. ed of high treason<BR>राजद्रोहदूषितः (ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attemper
ATTEMPER: v. To temper, mitigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attempt
ATTEMPT (subs.):<BR>(1) उद्यमः,<BR>I have resolved on<BR>an a. on his life<BR>बद्धो वधायोद्यमः, Vi. v.;<BR>(2)<BR>यत्नः, प्रयत्नः (=effort),<BR>I fancy the a. of Dāru-<BR>varmā has been unsuccessful<BR>अफलं दारुवर्मणः प्रयत्न-<BR>मवगच्छामि, Mu. iii.;<BR>(3) आरम्भः (=beginn-<BR>-ing),<BR>with success proportionate to a. s<BR>आरम्भ-<BR>सदृशोदयः, R. i. 15;<BR>(4) चेष्टा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attempt
ATTEMPT (v. t.):<BR>I To endeavour:<BR>(1) यतते,<BR> प्र-, (यत्, c. 1.),<BR>which princes a. to appropriate<BR>even by misdeeds<BR>दुरितैरपि कर्तुमात्मसात् प्रयतन्ते नृप-<BR>सूनवो हि यत्, R. viii. 2.;<BR>(2) यसति<BR>or<BR>यस्यति,<BR> प्र- (यस्, c. 1 and 4). repeatedly a. ed to fly up<BR>पुनः पुनः प्रायसदुत्प्लवाय सः, N. i. 125;<BR>(3) चेष्टते,<BR>(चेष्ट्, c. 1.) Mu. v.;<BR>(4) आ-रभते, प्र-, (रभ्, c.<BR>1.) (=to begin),<BR>low people do not a. at all<BR>from fear of obstacles<BR>प्रारभ्यते न खलु विघ्नभयेन नीचैः,<BR>Mu. iii.;<BR>(5) घटते (घट्, c. 1.) (rare) B. xii.<BR>26.<BR>II To attack: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attend
ATTEND (v. t.)<BR>I To attend on or upon: q. v.<BR>II To await, stay for: q. v. प्रतीक्षते (ईक्ष्, c.<BR>1.)<BR>III To be present at:<BR>(1) उप-तिष्ठति<BR>(स्था, c. 1.) (see Ki. vi. 29);<BR>(2) संनि-दधाति<BR>or धत्ते (धा, c. 3.)<BR>I a. ed it with my friend<BR>Dhanamitra<BR>अहं च सह सख्या धनमित्रेण तत्र सन्नयधिषि,<BR>D. ii.;<BR>(3) better by गच्छति, सङ्गच्छति or<BR>आगच्छति, समागच्छति, according as it means<BR>going or coming.<BR>IV To attend to: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attend on or upon
ATTEND ON OR UPON:<BR>(1) उप-तिष्ठते, पर्युप- (स्था,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>returning after a. ing on the sun<BR>सूर्योपस्थान-<BR>सन्निवृत्तं, V. i.;<BR>(2) उप-चरति, परि-, (चर्, c. 1.),<BR>a. on her with care<BR>यत्नादुपचर्यंतां, Sa. iii.;<BR>(3)<BR>उप-आस्ते (आस्, c. 2.), N. xxii. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attend to
ATTEND TO:<BR>(1) शृणोति (श्रु, c. 5.) (=to listen:<BR>q. v.), a. to that (message) शृणु॥।तां, R. viii.<BR>77.;<BR>a. to me<BR>मम वचनं शृणु;<BR>(2) अव-दधाति or<BR>धत्ते (धा, c. 3.),<BR>let the superintendents also a.<BR>each to his own work<BR>स्वे स्वे कर्मण्यथ समवधत्ताप्यधि-<BR>कृताः, Vi. vii.;<BR>(3) मनो यच्छति<BR>or<BR>ददाति (दा, c.<BR>1. and 3.)<BR>or<BR>निदधाति (धा, c. 3.),<BR>or<BR>युनक्ति (युज्,<BR>c. 7.) (=to apply the mind; fix one's<BR>attention on);<BR>(4) अवेक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.) (=to<BR>look after: q. v.),<BR>I have a. ed to only one<BR>civil action<BR>एकमेव मया पौरकार्यमवेक्षितम्, Sa. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attendance
ATTENDANCE:<BR>I The act of waiting on or<BR>serving:<BR>(1) उपचारः;<BR>(2) उपस्थानम् (rare);<BR>(3) शुश्रूषा (=reception of a guest).<BR>II<BR>Presence: q. v. उपस्थितिः। Ph.<BR>there was a<BR>good a. in the meeting<BR>समायां बहवः समागमन्।<BR>III A train, a retinue: q. v.: अनुयायिवर्गः।<BR>IV Attention: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attendant
ATTENDANT (subs.):<BR>(1) अनुचरः;<BR>(2) अनुयायिन्<BR>(m.);<BR>(3) परिचरः: v. Companion, servant,<BR>follower. Ph. a train of a. s:<BR>(1) अनुयायिवर्गः;<BR>(2) परिबर्हः;<BR>(3) परिच्छदः: v. Also conco-<BR>-mitant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attendant
ATTENDANT (adj.):<BR>(1) आनुषङ्गिकः (की, कं);<BR>(2)<BR>अनुगामिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attended by
ATTENDED BY: v. Accompanied by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attention
ATTENTION:<BR>I The act or state of attending:<BR>(1) अवधानम्, please lend me your a. for a moment<BR>मां मुहूर्तमवधानदानेनानुगृह्वन्तु, Ma. ix.;<BR>(2) मनोयोगः;<BR>(3) अप्रमादः<BR>or<BR>अप्रमत्तता (=carefulness);<BR>(4)<BR>अभिनिवेशः (=application, study);<BR>(5) अवेक्षा<BR>(=looking after). Ph.:<BR>his whole a. being<BR>devoted to it<BR>अनन्यहृदयतया, K.; it engages my a.<BR>मनो मे बध्नाति, (after R. xiii. 47.);<BR>to draw<BR>the a. of the king<BR>नरपतिप्रबोधनार्थम्, K.<BR>II.<BR>Politeness, courtesy: q. v. आदरः<BR>or<BR>समादरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attention
ATTENTION, PAY:<BR>(1) अवधानं ददाति (दा, c. 3.),<BR>paying a. to the buzzing of bees<BR>दत्तावधानं मधुलेहि-<BR>गीतौ B. ii. 7.;<BR>(2) आद्रियते (दृ, c. 6.) (=to<BR>respect), the king without paying any a. (to<BR>what he said) राजा अनादृत्य, Sa. vi.:<BR>(3)<BR>आसज्यते (=to devote to: q. v.): v. Attend<BR>to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attentive
ATTENTIVE:<BR>I Heedful, observant:<BR>(1)<BR>अवहितः (ता, तं); दत्तावधानः<BR>or<BR>कृतावधानः (ना, नं)<BR>(=paying attention);<BR>(3) सावधानः (ना, नं)<BR>(4) समाहितः (ता, तं);<BR>(5) अप्रमत्तः (त्ता, त्तं).<BR>II<BR>Attentive to a guest etc.:<BR>(1) दर्शितादरः (रा,<BR> रं), K.;<BR>(1) दक्षिणः (णा, णं) (as a lover ?)<BR>V. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attentively
ATTENTIVELY:<BR>(1) अवहितम्;<BR>(2) सावधानम्;<BR>(3)<BR>अप्रमत्तम्;<BR>(4) मनोयोगेन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attenuant
ATTENUANT (adj. and subs.): विद्रावकः or<BR>विलायकः (का, कं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attenuate
ATTENUATE:<BR>(1) कृशीकरोति;<BR>(2) तनूकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attenuated
ATTENUATED:<BR>(1) कृशः (शा, शं);<BR>(2) क्षीणः (णा,<BR> णं);<BR>(3) अपचितः (ता, तं): v. Thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attest
ATTEST:<BR>I To a deed: *पत्रस्य विशुद्धिप्रदर्शनाय<BR> साक्षी भवति<BR>or<BR>स्वनाम पत्रे लिखति: Ph.<BR>the will is<BR>a. ed by three witnesses<BR>*अस्येच्छापत्रस्य विशुद्धिप्रदर्शका-<BR>स्त्रयः साक्षिणः सन्ति।<BR>II To manifest: q. v.:<BR>(1) प्रकटीकरोति;<BR>(2) व्यनक्ति (अञ्ज्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attestation
ATTESTATION:<BR>I Verbal: साक्ष्यम्।<BR>II Written:<BR>Ph.<BR>the a. s of the will are all forged<BR>*इच्छापत्रे<BR> येषां साक्षिणां नामानि लिखितानि तत् सर्वं कृत्रिमम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attic
ATTIC (adj.): *एथिनीयः (या, यं); यवनः (नी, नं)<BR>(with less precision).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attic
ATTIC (subs.): Perh. अट्टः; शिरोगृहम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attire
ATTIRE (v. t.):<BR>(1) वस्ते (वस्, c. 2.) (=to put<BR>on, dress: q. v.);<BR>(2) भूषयति (=to adorn:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attire
ATTIRE (subs.):<BR>(1) वेशः;<BR>(2) परिबर्हः, in rich a.<BR>स्फीतपरिबर्हः (र्हा, र्हं), D. ii.: v. Dress, closses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attitude
ATTITUDE: v. Posture, position. Ph.<BR>Russia<BR>has assumed a threatening a. towards Persia<BR>*पारस्यराज्यं प्रति रुसियैर्विरुद्धवृत्तिः कक्षीकृता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attorney
ATTORNEY: *व्यवहारप्रतिनिधिः; मोक्तारः।<BR>A power<BR>of a.<BR>*व्यवहारप्रतिनिधिपत्रम्।<BR>A general<BR>*व्यवहार-<BR>सचिवः, विचारादिकार्येषु राजपक्षसमर्थको राजकीय-<BR>प्रधानोपदेष्टा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attract
ATTRACT: आकर्षति, समा-, (कृष्, c. 1.) (Lit. and<BR>Fig.): v. To draw, allure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attraction
ATTRACTION:<BR>I The power of a.: आकर्षणशक्तिः।<BR>II The act of attracting.:<BR>(1) आकर्षणम्;<BR>(2) आकृष्टिः;<BR>(3) समाकर्षणम्।<BR>III Allurement,<BR>enticements: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attractive
ATTRACTIVE:<BR>I Lit.: Ph. the a. force (of<BR>bodies): आकर्षणशक्तिः।<BR>II Fig.; alluring,<BR>charming: q. v.: हारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attractiveness
ATTRACTIVENESS: मनोहारित्वम्: v. Charm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attributable
ATTRIBUTABLE:<BR>(1) आरोपणीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2)<BR>अध्यारोपणीयः (या, यं). Ph.:<BR>it was a. to you<BR>that we did not take the fort<BR>*त्वन्निमित्तं दुर्गं न<BR> गृहीतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attribute
ATTRIBUTE (v. t.): आरोषयति (c. of रूप): v.<BR>To ascribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attribute
ATTRIBUTE (subs.):<BR>(1) धर्मः,<BR>and on the contra-<BR>-ry, the imputation of the subject and its a. s on<BR>the object<BR>तद्विपर्ययेण विषयिणस्तद्धर्माणां च विषयेऽध्यासः,<BR>S. i. p.;<BR>(2) गुणः,<BR>possessed of the eight a. s,<BR>minuteness etc.<BR>अणिमाद्यष्टगुणोपेतस्य।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attributive
ATTRIBUTIVE (subs.): विशेषणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attrition
ATTRITION: घर्षणम्: v. Friction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

attune
ATTUNE: Ph.<BR>a. your voice to the lyre.<BR>*वीणानु-<BR>गतं स्वरं कुरु।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

auburn
AUBURN:<BR>(1) पिशङ्गः (ङ्गा, ङ्गं): v. Tawny;<BR>(2) श्यावः (वा, वं): v. Brown;<BR>(3) गौरः<BR>(री, रं): v. Yellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

auction
AUCTION: *आह्वानविक्रयः; सर्वोच्चमूल्यदात्रे प्रकाश-<BR>विक्रयः,<BR>A. room<BR>*आह्वानविक्रयगृहं; आह्वानविक्रयशाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

auctioneer
AUCTIONEER: *आह्वानविक्रोतृ (f. त्री); यः (f. या)<BR>सर्वजनसमक्षं सर्वोच्चमूल्यदात्रे विक्रीणीते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

audacious
AUDACIOUS:<BR>(1) प्रगल्भः (ल्भा, ल्भं);<BR>(2) धृष्टः<BR>(ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>(3) प्रतिभान्वितः (ता, तं);<BR>(4) प्रति-<BR>भानवत् (f. ती): v. Bold, impudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

audaciousness
AUDACIOUSNESS, AUDACITY:<BR>(1) प्रगल्भता;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रागल्भ्यम्;<BR>(3) प्रतिभा<BR>or<BR>प्रतिभानम्;<BR>(4) धाष्टयम्;<BR>(5) साहसम् (=boldness);<BR>(6) निर्लज्जता<BR>(=impudence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

audible
AUDIBLE: स्फुटः (टा, टं) (=distinct: q. v.). Ph.:<BR>he speaks in an a. voice<BR>*स तथा गिरमुदीरयति<BR> यथा श्रोतृवर्गाणां कर्णगोचरीभवति<BR>or<BR>यथा श्रोतारो ग्रहीतुं<BR> शक्रुवन्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

audibly
AUDIBLY: स्फुटम् (=distinctly: q. v.): v.<BR>Audible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

audience
AUDIENCE:<BR>I A hearing: Ph.<BR>to give a.<BR>कर्णं<BR> ददाति (दा, c. 3);<BR>to gain a.<BR>श्रोतारं लभते (लभ्,<BR>c. 1).<BR>II Admittance to a hearing: दर्शनम्,<BR>to give a.<BR>दर्शनं ददाति, R.;<BR>to get an a. to the<BR>king<BR>राजदर्शनार्थम्।<BR>III A body of hearers:<BR>(1) श्रोतारः (m. pl.);<BR>(2) श्रोतृवर्गः;<BR>(3) प्रेक्षकाः<BR>(m. pl.) (=spectators).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

audit
AUDIT (subs.):<BR>I In gen.: परीक्षा।<BR>II Of<BR>accounts: *गणनापरीक्षा, गणनाशोधनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

audit
AUDIT (v. t.): परि-ईक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1);<BR>(2) शोध-<BR> यति (c. of शुध्) (?), have you a. ed the account<BR>*अपि गणना परिशोधिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

auditor
AUDITOR:<BR>I A hearer: q. v.: श्रोता।<BR>II Of<BR>accounts: *गणनाशोधकः; परीक्षकः<BR>or<BR>शोधकः<BR>(when the meaning is clear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

auditory
AUDITORY (subs.): an assembly of hearers:<BR>v. Audience (III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

auditory
AUDITORY (adj.): Ph.<BR>a. passages<BR>श्रवणमार्गाः<BR>(m. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

auger
AUGER:<BR>(1) आस्फोटनी:<BR>(2) वेधनिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

augment
AUGMENT (v. i.): वर्धते (वृध् c. 1): v. To in-<BR>-crease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

augment
AUGMENT (v. t.): वर्धयति (c. of वृध्): v. To<BR>increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

augment
AUGMENT (subs.): वृद्धिः v. Augmentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

augmentation
AUGMENTATION:<BR>(1) वृद्धिः;<BR>(2) वर्धनम्: v. In-<BR>-crease, enlargement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

augmentative
AUGMENTATIVE:<BR>(1) वर्धिष्णु (mfn.);<BR>(2) वर्ध-<BR>मानः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

augur
AUGUR (subs.):<BR>(1) शकुनज्ञः<BR>or<BR>शकुनज्ञानविद् (m.)<BR>(from birds),<BR>I heard from the a. that I would<BR>meet you just after 30 days<BR>शकुनज्ञात्तस्मात्त्रिंश<BR> द्रिवसावसानन्तरमेव भवत्सङ्गः सम्भविष्यतीत्यशृणवम्, D.;<BR>(2) निमित्तज्ञः। (from any omen) K.: v.<BR>Soothsayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

augur
AUGUR (v. t.):<BR>I To betoken, predict: q. v.:<BR>सूचयति (सूच्, c. 10).<BR>II To infer, conjec-<BR>-ture: q. v.: शङ्कते। A. ed (by birds): शकुन-<BR>निर्दिष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं), D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

augury
AUGURY:<BR>I From birds: शकुनज्ञानम्<BR>or<BR>शकुनि-<BR>रूतिज्ञानम्, K.<BR>II From any phenomena:<BR>निमित्तज्ञानम्: Ph.<BR>to practise a.<BR>*निमित्तैः शुमाशुभं<BR> कथयति।<BR>III An omen: q. v.<BR>(1) शकुनम्;<BR>(2)<BR>निमित्तम्,<BR>a bad a.<BR>अनिमित्तम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

august
AUGUST (adj.):<BR>(1) महामहिमन् (mfn.);<BR>(2) पृथु-<BR>धामन् (mfn.): v. Majestic, grand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

august
AUGUST (subs.): उत्तरश्रावणपूर्वभाद्रसंवादीयुरुपीयवत्सर-<BR>स्याष्टमो मासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aunt
AUNT:<BR>(1) पितृस्वसा (father's sister):<BR>(2) मातृ-<BR>स्वसा (mother's sister);<BR>(3) पितृव्या (father's<BR>brother's wife).;<BR>(4) मातुली, मातुलानी<BR>(mother's brother's wife).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

auricle
AURICLE:<BR>I The external ear: शष्कुली<BR>or<BR>कर्ण-<BR>शष्कुली।<BR>II A cavity of the heart: *हृदयशष्कुली,<BR> हृदयस्य रक्ताशयस्योध्र्वस्थकोषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

auricular
AURICULAR: श्रौतः (ती, तं) Ph. a. confession<BR>निभृतस्वीकारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aurochs
AUROCHS: पोलण्डदेशस्य वन्यगोविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aurora
AURORA:<BR>(1) अरुणः;<BR>(2) उषस् (n.);<BR>(3) दिन-<BR>मुखम्;<BR>(4) अहर्मुखम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aurora borealis
AURORA BOREALIS: विद्युदुद्भवो रात्रिदृश्यो महोज्ज्वलः<BR> प्रकाशविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

auspice
AUSPICE:<BR>I An omen: q. v.: शकुनम्।<BR>II Pro-<BR>-tection, patronage: q. v. आश्रयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

auspicious
AUSPICIOUS:<BR>I Lucky, propitious: q. v.:<BR>(1) शुभः (भा, भं);<BR>(2) कल्याणः (णा, णं);<BR>(3)<BR>मङ्गलः (ला, लं)<BR>II Fortunate, prosperous:<BR>q. v. ऋद्धिमत् (f. ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

auspiciously
AUSPICIOUSLY: शुभलग्ने (=at an a. moment):<BR>v. Propitiously, favourably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

austere
AUSTERE:<BR>I Severe, stern, harsh: q. v.;<BR>कठोरः (रा, रं).<BR>II Harsh, rough (to the<BR>taste): q. v.: शुक्तः (क्ता, क्तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

austere
AUSTERE:<BR>(1) कठोरभ्;<BR>(2) उग्रम्;<BR>(3) निष्ठुरम्:<BR>v. Severely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

austerity
AUSTERITY:<BR>(1) कार्कश्यम्;<BR>(2) कठोरता: v.<BR>Severity, sternness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

authentic
AUTHENTIC:<BR>I Genuine, true:<BR>(1) तथ्यः (थ्या,<BR> थ्यं);<BR>(2) सत्यः (त्या, त्यं);<BR>(3) अकृत्रिमः (मा, मं)<BR>(=not forged, as an a. register).<BR>II Of<BR>approved authority, reliable: q. v. प्रामा-<BR>णिकः (की, कं),<BR>an a. writer<BR>प्रामाणिकलेखकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

authentically
AUTHENTICALLY:<BR>(1) प्रमाणतः;<BR>(2) तत्त्वतः;<BR>(3)<BR>सारतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

authenticate
AUTHENTICATE:<BR>I To render authentic:<BR>प्रामाण्यं करोति (कृ, c. 8)<BR>II To prove authen-<BR>-tic: प्रमाणयति (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

authentication
AUTHENTICATION: Ph.<BR>for a.<BR>प्रामाण्यं कर्तुम्: v.<BR>Confirmation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

authenticity
AUTHENTICITY:<BR>(1) प्रामाण्यं;<BR>(2) सत्यता;<BR>(3)<BR>अकृत्रिमता (=the quality of not being for-<BR>-ged).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

author
AUTHOR:<BR>I The writer of a book:<BR>(1) कारः<BR>or<BR>कृत् (in comp.),<BR>a. of the commentary<BR>भाष्य-<BR>कारः;<BR>the a. of the Mitākṣarā<BR>मिताक्षराकृत्, Da.<BR>com.;<BR>(2) ग्रन्थकारः<BR>or<BR>-कर्ता<BR>or<BR>-कृत् (=a. of a<BR>book and hence to be used when a. is used<BR>abs.);<BR>(3) लेखकः;<BR>(4) रचकः<BR>or<BR>रचयिता;<BR>(5)<BR>प्रणेता;<BR>(6) निबन्धृ (m.) (rare);<BR>(7) कृतिन् (m.)<BR>(very rare). N. B. 3, 4, 5, and 6. are gen.<BR>used with some defining word.<BR>II A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">Page050</a>]<BR>maker, contriver, originator: q. v.: कर्ता,<BR>a. of great wonders<BR>कर्ता महाश्चर्याणाम्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

authoress
AUTHORESS:<BR>(1) कृत् (in comp.);<BR>(2) ग्रन्थकर्त्री;<BR> प्रणेत्री;<BR>(4) रचयित्री।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

authoritative
AUTHORITATIVE:<BR>I Determinative:<BR>(1) सप्र-<BR>माणः (णा, णं) (=with proof).<BR>(2) दृढः (ढा, ढं)<BR>(=firm).<BR>II Dictatorial, overbearing:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

authoritatively
AUTHORITATIVELY:<BR>(1) सप्रमाणम्;<BR>(2) दृढम्<BR>(=firmly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

authority
AUTHORITY:<BR>I Lawful power:<BR>(1) प्रभुत्वम्;<BR>(2) क्षमता;<BR>(3) शक्तिः।<BR>II Influence, might:<BR>q. v.: गौरवम्।<BR>III Permission, order: q. v.:<BR>अनुज्ञा।<BR>IV Testimony: प्रमाणं,<BR>the Vedas are<BR>our a. for this<BR>अत्र वेदाः प्रमाणम् (note the sing.<BR>numb.). V. Credibility: प्रामाण्यं,<BR>its a. is<BR>disputed<BR>अस्य प्रामाण्यं सन्दिग्धम्।<BR>VI In pl.,<BR>government: Perh. प्रमवः (m. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

authorize
AUTHORIZE:<BR>I To empower:<BR>(1) क्षमतां ददाति<BR>(दा, c. 3) (rare);<BR>(2) अनुमन्यते (मन्, c. 4)<BR>(=to allow);<BR>(3) नियोजयति (युज्, c. 10)<BR>(to appoint).<BR>II To legalize: q. v.<BR>III<BR>To authenticate: q. v. Ph.: a. ed by usage<BR>व्यवहारसिद्धः (द्धा, द्धं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

authorship
AUTHORSHIP: ग्रन्थकर्तृत्वं or sim. कर्तृत्वम्: Ph.<BR>its a. is disputed<BR>*न निश्चीयते कोऽस्य लेखकः v.<BR>Author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

autobiographer
AUTOBIOGRAPHER: *स्वचरितलेखकः; आत्मजीवन-<BR>चरितप्रणेता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

autobiography
AUTOBIOGRAPHY: *आत्मचरितम्, स्वकीयजीवन-<BR>चरितम्; स्वजीवनवृत्तान्तः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

autocrat
AUTOCRAT: ईश्वरः: v. Despot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

autograph
AUTOGRAPH (adj.): स्वहस्तलिखितः (ता, तं):<BR>a.<BR>letter<BR>स्वहस्तलेख्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

autograph
AUTOGRAPH (subs.):<BR>(1) स्वहस्तलेखः;<BR>(2) स्वहस्ता-<BR>क्षरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

automation
AUTOMATION: *स्वयञ्चलयन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

autumn
AUTUMN:<BR>(1) शरद्, (f.);<BR>(2) शरत्कालः;<BR>(3)<BR>घनान्तः (poetical).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

autumnal
AUTUMNAL:<BR>(1) शारदः (दी, दं);<BR>(2) शारदीयः<BR>(या, यं);<BR>(3) शरत्कालीनः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

auxiliary
AUXILIARY (adj.):<BR>(1) सहकारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2)<BR>उत्तरसाधकः (का, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

auxiliary
AUXILIARY (subs.): सहायः। Ph. a. s i. e.<BR>a.<BR>troops:<BR>आसारः (rare), Si. ii. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avail
AVAIL (v.):<BR>I To make use of: Ph.<BR>I will<BR>a. myself of your advice<BR>*तवोपदेशं ग्रहीष्यामि;<BR>he<BR>a. ed himself of this opportunity to carry out his<BR>design<BR>*अस्मिन्नवसरे स्वार्थसम्पादनपरो बभूव।<BR>II To<BR>serve, be of use: q. v.: all these did not a.<BR>(सर्वमेतत्) नार्थवद् बभूव, Ki.: v. Avail (subs.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avail
AVAIL (subs):<BR>(1) गुणः,<BR>of what a. is a loyal,<BR>but unwise and timid servant<BR>अप्राज्ञेन च कातरेण च<BR> गुणः स्यात् सानुरागेण कः, Mu. i.;<BR>the study of<BR>religious books has been of no a.<BR>निर्गुणो धर्मशास्त्रा-<BR>भ्यासः K.;<BR>(2) अर्थः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

available
AVAILABLE:<BR>I Profitable: q. v.<BR>II Obtain-<BR>-able: not a.<BR>(1) दुर्लभः (भा, भं);<BR>(2) दुष्प्राप्यः<BR>(प्या, प्यं);<BR>(3) दुष्प्रापः (पा, पं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avalanche
AVALANCHE: हिमनिस्यन्दः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avarice
AVARICE:<BR>(1) लोभः (covetousness);<BR>(2) अर्थ-<BR>कामः;<BR>(3) धनलोभः;<BR>(4) वित्तेहा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avaricious
AVARICIOUS:<BR>I Covetous: q. v.: लोभिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR>II Desirous of wealth:<BR>(1) अर्थ-<BR>लुब्धः (ब्धा, ब्धं);<BR>(2) अर्थरुचि (mfn.);<BR>(3)<BR>धनलुब्धः (ब्धा, ब्धं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avariciously
AVARICIOUSLY:<BR>(1) अर्थलोमात्;<BR>(2) धनलोभेन:<BR>v. Covetously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avaunt
AVAUNT: अपेहि (2nd pers. sin. imper. of इ):<BR>v. Get away, begone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avenge
AVENGE (v. t.):<BR>(1) प्रति-करोति (कृ, c. 8), (I)<BR>have a. d it now by taking away their clothes<BR>तत् साभ्प्रतं प्रतिकृतं हरतांशुकानि, Dh.;<BR>(2) प्रतिकार<BR>or<BR>प्रतीकारं करोति (with gen.);<BR>(3) वैरानृण्यमुपग-<BR> च्छति (गम्, c. 1), (with loc. of the wrong<BR>doer), Vi.;<BR>(4) परिशोधं गृह्वाति (ग्रह्, c. 9)<BR>(with gen.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avenger
AVENGER: प्रतिकर्ता<BR>or<BR>प्रतीकारकर्ता (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avenue
AVENUE:<BR>I Passage, approach: q. v.: द्वार<BR>II An alley: वीथिः:<BR>a. of mango trees<BR>चूत-<BR>वीथिः, D. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aver
AVER (v. t.): प्रतिजानीते: v. To affirm, assert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

average
AVERAGE (adj.): Ph. all her parts are of a.<BR>dimensions<BR>अस्याः सर्व एवावयवाः नातिस्थूला नातिकृ<BR>D. vi.;<BR>there was a. amount of rainfall this<BR>year<BR>*अस्मिन् वर्षे नात्यधिका नात्यल्पा वृष्टिः पपात; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">Page051</a>]<BR>is a man af a. stamp<BR>*तस्य बुद्धिर्नातिप्रखरा नाति-<BR>स्थूला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

average
AVERAGE (subs.): no equiv.: मध्यम may be<BR>used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

averment
AVERMENT:<BR>(1) प्रतिञ्जा;<BR>(2) दृढवाक्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

averse
AVERSE:<BR>I Disliking, unwilling:<BR>(1) विरक्तः<BR>(क्ता, क्तं);<BR>(2) पराङ्नु खः (खी, खं);<BR>(3) विमतः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR>II Unfavourable: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aversion
AVERSION:<BR>(1) विरागः;<BR>(2) विरक्तिः;<BR>(3) विमतिः<BR>(rare);<BR>(4) द्वेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avert
AVERT:<BR>(1) नि-वर्तयति, विनि-, व्या-, अप-, (c. of<BR>वृत्);<BR>(2) निवारयति (c. of वृ) (=to prevent:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aviary
AVIARY (subs.):<BR>(1) पक्षिशाला;<BR>(2) कुलायिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avidity
AVIDITY: v. Eagerness, greediness; with a.:<BR>v. Eagerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avocation
AVOCATION:<BR>(1) कार्यम्;<BR>(2) कर्मन् (n.);<BR>(3) व्या-<BR>पारः: v. Business, occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avoid
AVOID<BR>(1) परि-हरति (हृ, c. 1), a. ing his sight<BR>दृष्टिप्रपातं परिहृत्य तस्य Ku. iii. 43.;<BR>(2) वर्जयति<BR>(वर्ज्, c. 10) v. Shun, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avoidable
AVOIDABLE:<BR>(1) परिहर्तव्यः (व्या, व्यं);<BR>(2) परि-<BR>हरणीयः (या, यं);<BR>(3) वर्जनीयः (या, यं);<BR>(4)<BR>हेयः (या, यं);<BR>(5) त्याज्यः (ज्या, ज्यं);<BR>(6) परि-<BR>हार्यः (र्या, र्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avoidance
AVOIDANCE:<BR>(1) वर्जनम्;<BR>(2) परिहरणम्। (rare):<BR>v. Abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avouch
AVOUCH: प्रति-जानीते (ञ्जा, c. 9): v. To main-<BR>-tain, assert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avow
AVOW: स्वीकरोति (कृ, c. 8): v. To confess,<BR>acknowledge, declare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avowal
AVOWAL: स्वीकारः: v. Confession, acknow-<BR>-ledgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avowed
AVOWED (part. adj.): स्पष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं) (open,<BR>plain, evident: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avowedly
AVOWEDLY:<BR>(1) स्पष्टम्; (प्रकाशम्;)<BR>(3) प्रकटम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

await
AWAIT (v. t.):<BR>I To wait for: q. v.<BR>(1) प्रतीक्षते<BR>(ईक्ष् c. 1);<BR>(2) प्रतिपालयति (पाल्, c. 10).<BR>II To be in store for: आ-सीदति, प्रत्या-, (सद्,<BR>c. 1) (to be nigh),<BR>salvation a. s thee<BR>प्रत्या-<BR>सीदति मुक्तिस्त्वां, Ki. xi. 36. Ph.<BR>death a. s every<BR>one<BR>मरणं प्रकृतिः शरीरिणाम्, R.; what a. s me next<BR>*किमतः परं मे सम्भविष्यति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awake
AWAKE (v. i.):<BR>(1) बुध्यते, वि-, प्र-, प्रति-, (बुध् c.<BR>4);<BR>(2) उत्तिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1) (=to get up);<BR>(3) निद्रां त्यजति, जहाति etc.; विनिद्रः (द्रा, द्रं)<BR>भवति etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awake
AWAKE (v. t.):<BR>I From sleep:<BR>(1) बोधयति,<BR> प्र-, वि-, प्रति-, विप्र-, (c. of बुध्);<BR>(2) जागरयति<BR>(c. of जागृ);<BR>(3) निद्रां भनक्ति (भन्ज्, c. 7)<BR>(with gen.).<BR>II From inattention, or inac-<BR>-tion: v. To arouse, rouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awake
AWAKE (adj.):<BR>(1) जाग्रत् (f. ती);<BR>(2) जागरः<BR>(रा, रं);<BR>(3) उन्निद्रः (द्रा, द्रं) (without<BR>sleep);<BR>(4) प्रबुद्धः (द्धा, द्धं): v. To be awake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awake
AWAKE, BE: जागर्ति, प्र-, (जागृ, c. 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awaken
AWAKEN: v. To awake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awakening
AWAKENING (subs):<BR>(1) प्रबोधः, प्रबोधनम्;<BR>(2)<BR>बोधः;<BR>(3) विबोधनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

award
AWARD (v. t.):<BR>(1) ददाति (दा, c. 3);<BR>(2) वि-<BR>तरति (तॄ, c. 1);<BR>(3) दापयति (c. of दा) (in<BR>the legal sense, when a judge a. s damages<BR>etc.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

award
AWARD (subs.): निर्णयः: v. Judgment, sen-<BR>-tence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aware
AWARE, BE:<BR>(1) जानाति (ञ्जा, c. 9);<BR>(2) अव-<BR>गच्छति (गम्, c. 1): v. To know.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aware
AWARE, MADE:<BR>(1) बोधितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) विबो-<BR>धितः (ता, तं);<BR>(3) अवबोधितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

away
AWAY: v. the several verbs with which it is<BR>used. Ph.:<BR>a. with begging<BR>कृतमेव याच्ञया, Ki.<BR>xiv. 20;<BR>a. with shame<BR>अलं ह्रिया, R. v. 58;<BR>a. (=begone; q. v.) अन्तरमन्तरम्, Mr. ii.;<BR>she is a. (=absent, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awe
AWE (subs.):<BR>(1) भयम्;<BR>(2) त्रासः;<BR>(3) साध्वसम्;<BR>(4) आदरः। N. B. There is no exact equiv.<BR>of awe: 1, 2 and 3 mean fear, 4 means<BR>respect. To stand in a. of: बिभेति (भी, c. 3)<BR>(with abl.). Ph.: he is known to me and not<BR>disagreeable, still<BR>I approach him with a<BR>न च<BR> न परिचितो न चाप्यरम्यश्चकितमुपैमि तथापि पार्श्वमस्य,<BR>Mal. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awe
AWE (v. t.): v. To frighten, terrify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awe struck
AWE STRUCK:<BR>(1) भयविप्लुतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) साध्वस-<BR>परीतः (ता, तं);<BR>(3) त्रासाकुलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awful
AWFUL:<BR>I Awe-inspiring:<BR>(1) घोरः (रा, रं) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">Page052</a>]<BR>(=terrific: q. v.: not applicable to men);<BR>(2) अतितेजस्विन् (f. नी)<BR>or<BR>महातेजस् (mfn.)<BR>(full of that which inspires awe: appli-<BR>-cable to men only and their appearance).<BR>Ph.:<BR>Oh how a. is royal majesty<BR>अहो ! दुरासदो<BR> राजमहिमा, Mal. i.;<BR>wild mountain scenery, grand<BR>and a.<BR>प्रशान्तगम्मीरनीलविपुलश्रीररण्यगिरिभूमिः, Vi.<BR>v.<BR>II Awestruck: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awfully
AWFULLY:<BR>I Fearfully q. v.<BR>II Exceedingly:<BR>q. v. अत्यन्तम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awfulness
AWFULNESS:<BR>(1) तेजः (of men etc.);<BR>(2) प्रशान्त-<BR>गम्भीरता (=calm solemnity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awhile
AWHILE: कियत्कालम्;<BR>(2) कञ्चित्कालम्;<BR>(3) मुहू-<BR>र्तम् (=for a moment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awkward
AWKWARD:<BR>I Unskilful: q. v.: अदक्षः (क्षा,<BR> क्षं).<BR>II Inelegant, clumsy: q. v.:<BR>(1) अप-<BR>रूपः (पा, पं);<BR>(2) ग्राम्यः (म्या, म्यं) (=rustic),<BR>(applicable to manners etc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awkwardly
AWKWARDLY: v. Clumsily, inelegantly, un-<BR>-skilfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awkwardness
AWKWARDNESS:<BR>I Unskilfulness: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Inelegance: q. v.: ग्राम्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awl
AWL:<BR>(1) आरा;<BR>(2) चर्मप्रभेदिका (shoemaker's<BR>a.);<BR>(3) वेधनिका। v. Gimlet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awn
AWN:<BR>(1) किंशारुः;<BR>(2) शस्यशूकम्;<BR>(3) शुङ्गः;<BR>(4) शूकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awning
AWNING:<BR>(1) वितानम्;<BR>(2) उल्लोचः: v. Veil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awry
AWRY:<BR>(1) तिर्यक्;<BR>(2) तिरश्चीनम्;<BR>(9) साचि;<BR>(4) कुटिलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

axe
AXE:<BR>(1) कुठारः;<BR>(2) परशुः;<BR>(3) परश्वधः।<BR>A<BR>small a.<BR>कुठारिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

axiom
AXIOM: *अप्रमेयतत्वम्, स्वतःसिद्धवस्तु, K. d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

axis
AXIS: *अक्षरेखा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

axle
AXLE, AXLE-TREE:<BR>(1) चक्रदण्डः (?);<BR>(2) अक्षाग्रम्<BR>(?);<BR>(3) अनुकर्षः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aye
AYE:<BR>I Yes: q. v.<BR>II For aye: v. Always.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

azure
AZURE: नीलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

babble
BABBLE (v. i.):<BR>(1) जल्पति (जल्प्, c. 1.);<BR>(2)<BR>प्र-लपति (लप्, c. 1.);<BR>(3) वावद्ये, वावद्मि,<BR>or<BR>वावदीमि<BR>(freq. of वद्);<BR>(4) वावच्ये, वावच्मि (freq. of वच्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

babble
BABBLE, BABBLING (subs.):<BR>(1) जल्पः;<BR>(2)<BR>जल्पनम्;<BR>(3) जल्पितम्;<BR>(4) प्रलपितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

babbler
BABBLER:<BR>(1) (जल्पकः (का, कं);<BR>(2) जल्पाकः<BR>(की, कं);<BR>(3) वाचाटः (टा, टं);<BR>(4) वावदूकः (का, कं);<BR>(5) प्रलापिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

babbling
BABBLING (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: Babbler.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>v. Murmuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baboon
BABOON: हनुमत् (m.) (?); वानरविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baby
BABY, BABE: दारकः, m. (दारिका, f.): v. Infant,<BR>suckling, child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

babyhood
BABYHOOD: शैशवम् (childhood: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

babyish
BABYISH: बालिशः (शा, शं): v. Childish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bacchanal
BACCHANAL, BACCHANALIAN: तान्त्रिकः (की, कं)<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bachelor
BACHELOR:<BR>(1) अकृतदारः<BR>or<BR>अकृतोद्वाहः: v. Un-<BR>-married;<BR>(2) वण्टः<BR>or<BR>वण्ठः (very rare). Ph.:<BR>a b. of arts<BR>*‘वि ए’ उपाधिधारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

back
BACK (subs.):<BR>I Of an animal: पृष्ठम्,<BR>whose<BR>b. s the enemy has seen<BR>दृष्टपृष्ठानरातिना, Ki. xv.<BR>19.: Ph. behind one's b.:<BR>(1) पृष्ठतः;<BR>(2)<BR>परोक्षे (in one's absence).<BR>II As opposed to<BR>front:<BR>(1) पृष्ठम्,<BR>on the b. of a writing<BR>लेखस्य पृष्ठे,<BR>Y.;<BR>(2) पृष्ठदेशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

back
BACK (adv.): v. Backwards. It is generally<BR>expr. by the prefix प्रति:<BR>to come back<BR>प्रत्या-<BR>गच्छति;<BR>to give back<BR>प्रति-ददाति etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

back
BACK (v. i.): प्रत्या-वर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.): v. To go<BR>back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

back
BACK (v. t.):<BR>I To mount: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>support, second: q. v.<BR>III To drive back-<BR>-ward: प्रतीपं नुदति (नुद्, c. 6.)<BR>or<BR>चालयति (c.<BR>of चल्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backbite
BACKBITE:<BR>(1) परोक्षे परि-वदति (वद्, c. 1.), असूयति<BR>(nomi.), etc. v. To slander;<BR>(2) पृष्ठमांसम् अत्ति<BR>(अद्, c. 2.) खादति (खाद्, c. 1.) (with gen) (not<BR>very common).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backbiter
BACKBITER:<BR>(1) पृष्ठमांसादः;<BR>(2) यः परोक्षे परिवदति<BR>etc.;<BR>(3) पिशुनः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backbiting
BACKBITING:<BR>(1) पृष्ठमांसादनम्;<BR>(2) पिशुनवाक्यम्:<BR>v. Slander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backbone
BACKBONE:<BR>(1) पृष्ठवंशः;<BR>(2) कशेरुः;<BR>(3) कशेरुका;<BR>(4) रीटकः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backdoor
BACKDOOR:<BR>(1) पक्षद्वारम्;<BR>(2) पक्षकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

back-gammon
BACK-GAMMON: क्रीडाविशेषः। b.-board:<BR>(1) अष्टा-<BR>पदम् (?);<BR>(2) चर्मपट्टिका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

background
BACKGROUND: *पश्चाद्भूमिः (in ana. with अग्र-<BR>भूमिः) or expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

back-side
BACK-SIDE:<BR>(1) पृष्ठभागः;<BR>(2) पृष्ठदेशः v. Also<BR>buttocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

back-slide
BACK-SLIDE: स्वधर्माद् भ्रश्यति (भ्रंश्, c. 4.), च्यवते<BR>(च्यु, c. 1.): v. To go astray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

back-slider
BACK-SLIDER:<BR>(1) घर्मभ्रष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>(2) घर्मच्युतः<BR>(ता, तं): v. Apostate<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

back-stairs
BACK-STAIRS:<BR>(1) *पक्षसोपानम्;<BR>(2) *अन्तःसोपानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backwards
BACKWARDS:<BR>I Towards the back: पृष्ठभागे<BR>or<BR>पृष्ठदेशे।<BR>II On the back:<BR>to fall b.<BR>अवमूर्ध-<BR>पातं पतति।<BR>III In a reversed direction:<BR>प्रतीपम्। Ph. to go b. (fig.) क्रमशोऽवनतिं गच्छति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backward
BACKWARD (adj.):<BR>I Reluctant, averse:<BR>q. v. पराङ्मु खः (खी, खं).<BR>II Slow, dull: q. v.<BR>कुण्ठितः (ता, तं).<BR>III Late: q. v.<BR>IV<BR>Reversed: q. v.: प्रतीपः (पा, पं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backwardness
BACKWARDNESS: पराङ्मू खता: v. Reluctance,<BR>aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bacon
BACON: *लावणशुष्कशूकरमांसम्; Perh. वल्लुरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bad
BAD: Gen. expr. by the prefixes दुर्, कु, अप<BR>etc. and sometimes by the affix क: a b. man<BR>दुर्जनः;<BR>b. weather<BR>दुर्दिनम्;<BR>b. luck<BR>दुर्दैवम्;<BR>not a<BR>b. speaker<BR>अकद्वदः;<BR>a b. road<BR>कदध्वन् (m.);<BR>b.<BR>food<BR>कदन्नम्;<BR>b. design<BR>कुमतिः;<BR>b. policy<BR>अपनयः;<BR>b.<BR>reputation<BR>अपयशः;<BR>a b. horse<BR>अश्वकः: v. Wicked,<BR>injurious, unfavourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

badge
BADGE (subs.):<BR>(1) चिह्नम्;<BR>(2) लक्षणम्;<BR>(3) लिङ्गम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

badger
BADGER (subs.): भल्लूकजातीयजन्तुविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

badinage
BADINAGE (subs.) नर्मभाषितम्: v. Joke, raillery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

badly
BADLY: Ph.<BR>I am b. off for servants<BR>भृत्याभावात्<BR> क्लिश्यामि;<BR>you have behaved b. towards her<BR>तस्यां<BR> त्वयानार्यमाचरितम्;<BR>he is b. bitten by the dog<BR>स<BR> कुक्कु रेण तीव्रं<BR>or<BR>बलवत् दष्टः,<BR>b. governed<BR>कुशासितः<BR>(ता, तं):<BR>b. formed<BR>कदाकारः (रा, रं);<BR>smell-<BR>ing b.<BR>दुर्गन्धः (न्धा, न्धं): v. Wrongly,<BR>wickedly, unfortunately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

badness
BADNESS:<BR>(1) by the adj.: b. of character<BR>दुराचारः;<BR>the b. of this soil is proverbial<BR>*अस्य<BR> प्रदेशस्य कुमृत्तिका प्रसिद्धा;<BR>(2) दुष्टटा (=wicked-<BR>-ness);<BR>(3) निर्गुणता (=worthlessness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baffle
BAFFLE (v. t.):<BR>(1) व्यर्थीकरोति;<BR>(2) मोघीकरोति:<BR>v. Frustrate, elude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bag
BAG (subs.):<BR>(1) Perh. पुटम्;<BR>canvas b.<BR>*शाण-<BR>पुटम्;<BR>(2) भस्त्रा;<BR>leather b.<BR>चर्ममस्त्रिका D. ii.;<BR>(3) गोणी (=sack. q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bagatelle
BAGATELLE:<BR>I a trifle: q. v.<BR>II A game:<BR>कन्दुकक्रीडाविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baggage
BAGGAGE:<BR>I Of an army:<BR>(1) साधनम्;<BR>the<BR>bugle sounding and the b. being ready<BR>आहतायां<BR> प्रयाणभेर्यां सज्जीक्रियमाणे साधने, K.;<BR>(2) वीवधः<BR>(provisions), Si. ii. 64.<BR>II A strumpet:<BR>q. v. बन्धकी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bagnio
BAGNIO:<BR>I A bath: q. v. स्नानागारम्;<BR>II A<BR>brothel: q. v. वेश्यालयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bag-pipe
BAG-PIPE: सुषिरवाद्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bail
BAIL (subs.):<BR>I The person who gives b.:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रतिभूः,<BR>he who stands a b. to produce a man<BR>यो<BR> यस्य प्रतिभूस्तिष्ठेद्दर्शनायेह मानवः, M. viii. 158;<BR>(2) लग्नकः।<BR>II Security: प्रातिभाव्यम्, on b.<BR>प्रातिभाव्यन। D. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bail
BAIL (v. t.):<BR>I As applied to securities: Ph.<BR>I will b. you<BR>तवाहं प्रतिभूर्मवामि (भू, c. 1.) or<BR>तिष्ठामि (स्था, c. 1.)<BR>II as applied to magis-<BR>-trates: प्रतिभाव्येन मुञ्चति (मुञ्च्, c. 6.)<BR>or<BR>मोचयति<BR>(मुच् c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bailable
BAILABLE: Ph.<BR>this offence is b.<BR>*ग्राह्यलग्नकोऽपराघः<BR>or<BR>अस्मिन्नपराघे प्रतिभूर्गृह्यते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bail-bond
BAIL-BOND: *प्रातिभाव्यपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bailiff
BAILIFF: *आसेधादिकर्मणि नियुक्तः शेरिफस्य प्रतिनिधिः;<BR> *यष्टिधरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bait
BAIT (subs.): आमिषम् (Lit. and Fig.), Ka.<BR>i. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bait
BAIT (v. t.):<BR>I To apply a bait:<BR>(1) सामिषं<BR> करोति (?);<BR>(2) आमिषं वडिशे निदधाति (धा, c. 3.)<BR>II To furnish animals with food on a<BR>journey: यवसादिना भोजयति (c. of भुज्) (?):<BR>Ph.<BR>b. ing his horse<BR>एनं तावदागृहीतकतिपयदूर्वा-<BR>प्रबालकवलं कृत्वा, K.<BR>III. To attack an animal<BR>with dogs: Ph.<BR>to b. a bear<BR>भल्लूकबाधनाय<BR> कुक्कु रान् प्रणुदति (नुद्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bake
BAKE (v. t.):<BR>(1) पचति (पच्, c. 1.) (prop. to<BR>cook: q. v.),<BR>b. d brick<BR>पक्वेष्टका, Mr.;<BR>(2)<BR>भृज्जति, ते (भ्रस्ज्, c. 6.) (=to fry, q. v.), the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">Page054</a>]<BR>word lāja (also)<BR>means b. d grain<BR>लाजं भृष्टघान्ये<BR>Ph. b. d in an iron pan or oven (as bread,<BR>cakes etc.) कान्दवः (वी, वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bake-house
BAKE-HOUSE, BAKERY:<BR>(1) पूपशाला (?);<BR>(2)<BR>पाकशाला (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baker
BAKER:<BR>(1) आपूपिकः;<BR>(2) कान्दविकः;<BR>(3) पिष्टक-<BR>पाचकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

balance
BALANCE (subs.):<BR>I A pair of scales:<BR>(1)<BR>तुला;<BR>(2) मापनः (?).<BR>The beam of a b.<BR>तुलादण्डः;<BR>the string by which it is suspended<BR>प्रग्रहः or<BR>प्रग्राहः;<BR>the cup of a b.<BR>घटः;<BR>assay b.<BR>नाराची।<BR>II Of an account:<BR>(1) शेषः (=remainder:<BR>q. v.),<BR>he asked for the b. of money<BR>गृहीतशेषं दातुं<BR> स धनं प्रार्थयताथ तं, Raj.;<BR>(2) अन्तरम् (differ-<BR>-ence: q. v.),<BR>gives the whole b.<BR>दीयतां सकलान्तरम्,<BR>Raj.<BR>III Counterpoise: q. v.<BR>IV Com-<BR>-parison, estimate: q. v. तुलना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

balance
BALANCE (v. t.):<BR>I To bring to an equipoise;<BR>तुलयति (तुल्, c. 10) (Lit. and Fig.): Ph.<BR>their<BR>equipment is not b. d<BR>न तुलाधृतस्तावदनयोः परिकरः,<BR>Vi. vi.<BR>II To counterpoise: q. v.<BR>III Of<BR>accounts:<BR>(1) समीकरोति (कृ, c. 8.);<BR>(2) एकीक-<BR>रोति (?),<BR>b. ing the account<BR>गणनामेकीकृत्य, Raj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

balance
BALANCE (v. i.):<BR>I To be in equipoise:<BR>समीभवति (भू, c. 1.) (?).<BR>II To fluctuate,<BR>hesitate: q. v.: दोलायते (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

balcony
BALCONY:<BR>(1) प्रग्रीवः (?);<BR>(2) वितर्द्धिः (?);<BR>(3) इन्द्रकोषः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bald
BALD (adj.):<BR>I Hairless: q. v.:<BR>(1) अकेशः<BR>(शा, शं);<BR>(2) खलति (mfn.) (by disease).<BR>II<BR>Without natural covering: अनावृतः (ता, तं).<BR>III Unadorned, inelegant: q. v.: असंस्कृतः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

balderdash
BALDERDASH: v. Jargon, nonsense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baldness
BALDNESS:<BR>I Want of hair: अकेशता and sim.<BR>comp. morbid b.:<BR>(1) इन्द्रलुप्तम्;<BR>(2) खालित्यं<BR>Bha.<BR>II Of style: v. Inelegance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baldric
BALDRIC: प्रालम्बम् (?): v. Belt, girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bale
BALE (subs.): पोट्टली: v. Bundle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bale
BALE (v.): To b. out the bilge-water (नावः)<BR>जलं सिञ्चति (सिच्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baleful
BALEFUL:<BR>I Fatal, destructive: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Woeful, sad: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

balk
BALK (subs.):<BR>I Of a field:<BR>(1) आलिः;<BR>(2)<BR>आली (f.).<BR>II A beam, rafter: q. v.<BR>III<BR>Disappointment: q. v.: आशाभङ्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

balk
BALK (v. t.): खण्डयति (खण्ड्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>frustrate, disappoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ball
BALL (subs.):<BR>I A playing-ball: alternately<BR>striking with her left and right hands, sent (th<BR>b.)<BR>up<BR>वामदक्षिणाभ्यां करायां पर्यायेणाभिघ्नत्युदस्थापयत्<BR>D. vi.<BR>II A round mass:<BR>(1) गोल (mn.)<BR>(2) वर्तुलः।<BR>a small b.<BR>गुलिका;<BR>the eye b.<BR>तारा<BR>a b. of thread<BR>सूत्रकोषम् (?)<BR>III A meeting for<BR>dancing:<BR>(1) नृत्यम्;<BR>(2) नर्तनम् (=dancing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ballad
BALLAD: गाथा। b. singer;<BR>(1) गाथिकः;<BR>(2)<BR>गाथाकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ballast
BALLAST *निलमः; पोतस्थैर्यार्थं तदघोमागनिविष्टं प्रस्तर-<BR> -लोहादिद्रव्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ballet
BALLET: no equiv.: यात्रा would do. b. girl:<BR>(<BR>I) नर्तकी;<BR>(2) नटी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

balloon
BALLOON:<BR>(1) विमानम्;<BR>(2) व्योमयानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ballot
BALLOT (subs.):<BR>I A ball or ticket used in<BR>voting: *गुटिका।<BR>II Voting. by b.: *गुटिका;<BR> निभृतगुटिकापातेन मतामतप्रकाशनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ballot
BALLOT (v. i.): गुटिकापातेन मतामतं प्रकाशयति (c. of.<BR>काश्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ball-room
BALL-ROOM (subs.): *नृत्यशाला; नर्तनकोष्ठः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

balm
BALM:<BR>I The sap of a shrub: निर्यासविशेषः।<BR>II Solace, comfort: q. v. सुघालेपः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

balmy
BALMY:<BR>I Odoriferous, aromatic: q. v.<BR>सुगन्धि (mfn.).<BR>II Assuaging, soothing<BR>(1)<BR>तापहरः (री, रं);<BR>(2) शान्तिदः (दा, दं). Ph.<BR>the b. tree<BR>*वामवृक्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

balsam
BALSAM: v. Balm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

balsamic
BALSAMIC: v. Balmy, soft, unctuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

balustrade
BALUSTRADE: प्रग्रीवः (m. n.) (?); वृत्तिविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bamboo
BAMBOO:<BR>(1) वेणुः;<BR>(2) वंशः;<BR>(3) कीचकः (when<BR>rattling).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bamboozle
BAMBOOZLE: (v. t.): वञ्चयते (वञ्च्, c. 10.): v.<BR>Fool, to make a; to deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ban
BAN:<BR>I A proclamation: q. v.<BR>II Of<BR>marriage: Ph.<BR>have you published the b. s of<BR>marriage<BR>*अपि विवाहघोषणा प्रकाशिता।<BR>III Inter-<BR>-diction, proscription: q. v.: Ph.<BR>under b. to<BR>touch<BR>निषिद्धस्पर्शः (र्शा, र्शं).<BR>IV Curse: शापः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ban
BAN (v. t.): v. To curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

banana
BANANA:<BR>I The tree:<BR>(1) कदली;<BR>(2) रम्भा।<BR>II The fruit:<BR>(1) कदलीफलम्;<BR>(2) चम्पकम्<BR>(a species of it).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

band
BAND (subs.):<BR>I That which binds:<BR>(1)<BR>बन्घः:<BR>b. of hope<BR>आशाबन्घः, Me. i. 10;<BR>(2)<BR>बन्घनम्;<BR>(3) बन्घनी।<BR>II A company of<BR>persons:<BR>(1) दलम्;<BR>(2) गुल्मः (b. of troops).<BR>III Musical instruments:<BR>(1) वाद्यभाण्डम्।<BR>(?);<BR>(2) तूर्यैघः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

band together
BAND TOGETHER (v.): संहतः (ता, तं) (भवति) (भू,<BR>c. 1.) v. To combine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bandage
BANDAGE (subs.):<BR>(1) बन्धः, Śr.;<BR>(2) पट्टः<BR>(cloth) (only when the sense is clear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bandage
BANDAGE (v. t.): बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.),<BR>b. with a<BR>soft cloth<BR>मृदुपट्टं निवेश्य बध्नीयात्, Śr. Ph.<BR>things<BR>used in b. ing sores<BR>व्रणबन्घनद्रव्याणि, Śr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

band-box
BAND-BOX: पेटिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bandit
BANDIT: परिपन्थिन् (m); दस्युः v. Robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bandy
BANDY (v. t.):<BR>I to exchange: q. v.: विनिमयते<BR>(मे, c. 1.).<BR>II to agitate: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bandy-legged
BANDY-LEGGED:<BR>(1) प्रञ्जु (mfn.);<BR>(2) प्रगतजानु<BR>(mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bane
BANE:<BR>I Poison: q. v. विषम्।<BR>II Any fatal<BR>cause of mischief: Ph.<BR>he became the b. of<BR>India<BR>*भारतवर्षस्य कालरूपो<BR>or<BR>कालो बभूव;<BR>prosti-<BR>tution is the b. of society<BR>*वेश्यावृत्तिः समाजस्यानर्थ-<BR>मूलम्।<BR>III Ruin, destruction: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baneful
BANEFUL (v.): v. Pernicious, injurious, des-<BR>-tructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bang
BANG (v.): v. To beat, strike. Ph.<BR>the door<BR>b. s<BR>विरौति कपाटः Mr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bang
BANG (subs.): Ph. opened the door with a b.<BR>महाशब्दपूर्वकं कपाटमपावृतवान्: v. Explosion; v.<BR>Also blow, stroke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

banian-tree
BANIAN-TREE:<BR>(1) वटः;<BR>(2) न्यग्रोधः, its berry:<BR>नैयग्रोधम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

banish
BANISH (v. t.):<BR>I To condemn to exile:<BR>(1)<BR>निर्-वासयति (c. of वस्),<BR>first of all, Fivasiddhi<BR>was b. ed from the city<BR>आदावेव जीवसिधिर्नगरान्नि-<BR>र्वासितः Mu. ii.;<BR>(2) वि-वासयति (c. of वस्)<BR>M. viii. 123;<BR>(3) निर्-अस्यति (अस्, c. 4.)<BR>b. ed Fānaki from his house, but not from his<BR>mind<BR>गृहान्निरस्ता न तेन वैदेहसुता मनस्तः, R. xiv. 84.<BR>v. To drive away.<BR>(4) प्र-व्राजयति (c. of व्रज्)<BR>(rare) M.<BR>II Fig. To drive away, remove:<BR>q. v. shame was b. ed (from their minds) त्रपा<BR> निरस्ता, Ki. x. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

banishment
BANISHMENT:<BR>(1) निर्वासनम्;<BR>(2) विवासनम्;<BR>(3)<BR>प्रवासनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

banister
BANISTER: *सोपानस्तम्भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bank
BANK (subs.):<BR>I For dealing in money:<BR>*धनागारम्, the affairs of the b. were wound up<BR>*धनागारकार्याणि संहृतानि;<BR>the b. failed<BR>*धनागारमव-<BR>ससाद<BR>or<BR>क्षयं जगाम।<BR>II Of a river etc.:<BR>(1)<BR>तीरम्;<BR>(2) तटम्;<BR>(3) कूलम्;<BR>(4) प्रतीरम्;<BR>(5)<BR>रोघस् (n.);<BR>(6) कच्छः (rare). The opposite b.<BR>पारम्।<BR>The near b.<BR>अपारम्।<BR>A sand b.<BR>सैकतम्।<BR>B.<BR>of a hill<BR>वप्रम्।<BR>III A mound: q. v.<BR>(1) चयः;<BR>(2) वप्र (mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bank
