baptize
BAPTIZE (v. t.):<BR>(1) *अभिषिञ्चति (सिच्, c. 6.);<BR>(2) *कृष्टघर्मं ग्राहयति (c. of. ग्रह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bar
BAR (subs.):<BR>I Of a door: अर्गलम्।<BR>II Of a<BR>cage etc.: शलाका। v. Pole, beam.<BR>III A<BR>hindrance or obstruction: q. v.: प्रत्यूहः।<BR>IV A bank at the mouth of a river or<BR>harbour: बन्घः (?). V. For prisoners in a<BR>court of justice, or an inn.: *वृतिः।<BR>VI<BR>Any tribunal: q. v.: Ph.<BR>at the b. of public<BR>opinion<BR>*साधारणमतस्याग्रे।<BR>VII The entire<BR>body of advocates: *अभिभाषकवर्गः, उत्तरवादिनः<BR>(m. pl.).<BR>VIII In music: लम्बः (?).<BR>IX<BR>An ingot or wedge of metal: Perh. पिण्डः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bar
BAR (v. t.):<BR>I To bolt: q. v.<BR>II To hinder,<BR>prevent: q. v.:<BR>(1) नि-रुणद्धि (रुध्, c. 7.);<BR>(2) प्रति-षेधति (सिध्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barb
BARB (subs.):<BR>I A. horse: q. v.: वाजिः।<BR>II<BR>Of an arrow: कर्णः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barbican
BARBICAN: उपदुर्गम्, प्रवेशनिरोघनार्थं नगरोपान्तनिर्मितो<BR> दुर्गविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barbarian
BARBARIAN (adj.): v. Barbarous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barbarian
BARBARIAN (subs.):<BR>I An uncivilized person:<BR>(1) असभ्यः (भ्या, भ्यं);<BR>(2) म्लेच्छः (properly<BR>one who is not a Hindu, but may be used<BR>in the sense of b.).<BR>II A cruel man:<BR>पिशाचः (?). v. Cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barbaric
BARBARIC: i. e. foreign: q. v.: विदेशीयः (या, यं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barbarism
BARBARISM:<BR>I Incorrect language: म्लेच्छितम्<BR>(?), gentlemen do not use b. s in their speech<BR>नार्याम्लेच्छन्ति भाषामिः, Mah.<BR>II An uncivilized<BR>condition: असभ्यता<BR>III Barbarity: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barbarity
BARBARITY (subs.):<BR>(1) निष्ठुरता;<BR>(2) क्रौर्यम्:<BR>v. Ferocity, cruelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barbarize
BARBARIZE (v. t.): *म्लेच्छीकरोति (कृ, c. 8.): v.<BR>To brutalize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barbarous
BARBAROUS (adj.):<BR>I Uncivilized: q. v.:<BR>असभ्यः (भ्या, भ्यं).<BR>II Cruel, ferocious:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) निष्ठुरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) नृशंसः (सा, सं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barbarously
BARBAROUSLY:<BR>I Without refinement:<BR>(1)<BR>असभ्यम् (?);<BR>(2) अश्लीलम् (- coarsely, in-<BR>-decently).<BR>II Cruelly: q. v.: निर्दयम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barbarousness
BARBAROUSNESS: क्रौर्यम्: v. Barbarity, bar-<BR>-barism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barbed
BARBED (adj.): कर्णिन् (f. नी) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barbel
BARBEL: नादेयमत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barber
BARBER:<BR>(1) नापितः;<BR>(2) क्षुरिन् (m.);<BR>(3)<BR>क्षौरिकः;<BR>(4) मुण्डिन् (m.)<BR>A b. 's shop<BR>नापितशाला;<BR>b.'s business<BR>नापित्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barberry
BARBERRY: गुल्मविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bard
BARD:<BR>I<BR>(1) मागधः;<BR>(2) वैतालिकः;<BR>(3) वन्दिन्<BR>(m.);<BR>(4) मघुकः।<BR>II A poet: q. v.:<BR>कविः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bare
BARE (adj.):<BR>I Uncoverd:<BR>(1) अनावृतः (ता,<BR> तं);<BR>(2) शून्यः (न्या, न्यं);<BR>(3) केवलः (ला, लं)<BR>(only of places and things), on the b. ground<BR>स्थण्डिल एव केवले, Ku. v. 12.<BR>II Destitute:<BR>q. v.: दीनः (ना, नं).<BR>III Simple, unadorned:<BR>q. v.<BR>IV Mere, alone: q. v. V. Thread-<BR>-bare: जीर्णः (र्णा, र्णं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bare
BARE (v. t.): विवस्त्रयति: v. To uncover, divest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bare-faced
BARE-FACED (adj.): निर्लज्जः (ज्जा, ज्जं): v. Im-<BR>-pudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bare-facedly
BARE-FACEDLY (adv.): निर्लज्जम्: v. Impu-<BR>-dently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bare-facedness
BARE-FACEDNESS: निर्लज्जता: v. Impudence,<BR>effrontery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bare-foot
BARE-FOOT, BARE-FOOTED: शून्यपादः (दा, दं);<BR>(2) अनावृतपादः (दा, दं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bare-headed
BARE-HEADED:<BR>(1) अनावृतशिरस् (mfn.);<BR>(2)<BR>शून्यमस्तकः (का, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barely
BARELY:<BR>I Only: q. v. केवलम्।<BR>II Scarcely:<BR>q. v. कर्थञ्चित्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bareness
BARENESS:<BR>I Nakedness: अनावृतत्वम्।<BR>II<BR>Indigence: q. v.: दैन्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bargain
BARGAIN (subs.):<BR>I An agreement or stipu-<BR>-lation: q. v.<BR>(1) समयः;<BR>(2) संविद् (f.).<BR>II.<BR>A gainful or satisfactory transaction: Ph.<BR>buy the house, it is a good b.<BR>*अल्पमूल्येन लभ्यं<BR> गृहं क्रीणीहि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bargain
BARGAIN (v. i.); पणते (पण्, c. 1.) (?): v. To<BR>agree, stipulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barge
BARGE:<BR>I A pleasure-boat: केलिनौका (?).<BR>II A large boat for the conveyance of<BR>passengers or goods:<BR>(1) तरालुः;<BR>(2) तरान्धुः;<BR>(3) वहित्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bargeman
BARGEMAN:<BR>(1) नाविकः;<BR>(2) पोतवाहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bark
BARK (subs.):<BR>I Of trees:<BR>(1) वल्कल (mn.);<BR>(2) वल्कम्;<BR>(3) त्वच् (f.);<BR>(4) छल्लिः (f.) (rare).<BR>II Of dogs: बुक्कनम्।<BR>III A small vessel<BR>(1) नौः;<BR>(2) तरी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bark
BARK (v. t.):<BR>(1) वल्कलं निर्हरति (हृ, c. 10.),<BR>अपनयति (नी, c. 1.) etc;<BR>(2) त्वचयति (nomi.);<BR>(3) त्वक्षति (त्वक्ष्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bark
BARK (v. i.):<BR>(1) बुक्कयति, ते (बुक्क्, c. 1.),<BR>b. ed at<BR>by dogs<BR>कुक्कुरैर्बुक्क्यमानः Mr. i:<BR>(2) भषति (भष्,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>human dogs always b. thus<BR>भषन्ति हैवं<BR> श्वनराः सदैव, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barking
BARKING: Of dogs:<BR>(1) बुक्कनम्;<BR>(2) भषितम्:<BR>v. Noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barley
BARLEY: यवः।<BR>Fit for producing b.<BR>यवक्यः (क्या,<BR> क्यं).<BR>made of b.<BR>यवमयः (यी, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barley-corn
BARLEY-CORN: यवः।<BR>Fried b.<BR>धाना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barley-sugar
BARLEY-SUGAR: सिताखण्डः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barley-water
BARLEY-WATER:<BR>(1) उदमन्थः;<BR>(2) यवोदकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barm
BARM: मण्डः or (more fully) सुरामण्डः: v.<BR>Yeast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barmaid
BARMAID: *मण्डपरक्षिणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barn
BARN:<BR>(1) कुशूलः;<BR>(2) घान्यकोष्ठम्,<BR>(3) घान्या-<BR>गारम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barnacle
BARNACLE:<BR>I A mollusc: शम्बूकविशेषः।<BR>II A<BR>kind of goose हंसविशेषः।<BR>III In farriery:<BR>यन्त्रविशेषः; *नस्तग्रहा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barometer
BAROMETER: *वायुमापः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baron
BARON (subs.): *इंलण्डीयकौलीनोपाधिभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baronage
BARONAGE:<BR>I The whole body of barons:<BR>*बेरणवर्गः।<BR>II The rank of a baron *बेरणपदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baroness
BARONESS: बेरणवधूः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baronet
BARONET: उपाघिविशेषः: *उपबेरणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baronial
BARONIAL (adj.): *बेरणीयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barony
BARONY: *बेरणस्याघिपत्यम्; बैरण्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barque
BARQUE: नौविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barrack
BARRACK: (nearest word) निवेशः; v. Camp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barrack-master
BARRACK-MASTER: *निवेशाध्यक्षः, निवेशाघिकारिन्<BR>(m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barrel
BARREL (subs.):<BR>I A kind of cask: भाण्डम्<BR>(any vessel).<BR>II A cylinder or tube, as<BR>of a gun or watch: नाला<BR>or<BR>नाली (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barrel
BARREL (v.): भाण्डे निवेशयति (c. of विश्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barren
BARREN:<BR>(1) बन्ध्यः (न्ध्या, न्ध्यं) (Lit. and Fig.),<BR>a. b. woman<BR>बन्ध्या K. b. whose anger is not b.<BR>अबन्ध्यकोपः (पा, पं), Ki. i. 33.;<BR>(2) निष्फलः (ला,<BR> लं) (not applied to females: v. unfruitful).<BR>Ph.<BR>b. soil<BR>अनुर्वरा<BR>or<BR>अशस्यप्रदा भूमिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barrenness
BARRENNESS:<BR>(1) बन्ध्यता;<BR>(2) बन्धात्वम् (of<BR>females), Śr;<BR>(3) निष्फलता (fruitlessness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barricade
BARRICADE (subs.): वृक्षादिनिर्मितप्राकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barricade
BARRICADE (v. t.): वृक्षादिना प्रवेशमागर्दीन् अवरुणद्धि<BR>(रुध्, c. 7.) v. To obstruct, block up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barrier
BARRIER:<BR>I Fence, enclosure: q. v. वृतिः।<BR>II An obstacle: q. v.<BR>(1) प्रतिबन्धः;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रत्यूहः।<BR>III A boundary: q. v.: सीमा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barrister
BARRISTER: *अभिभाषकविशेषः; व्यवहारपण्डितः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barrow
BARROW:<BR>I A vehicle: हस्तचालितयानविशेषः।<BR>II A castrated hog: उत्पाटितवृषणः शूकरः (?).<BR>III A mound or hillock: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barter
BARTER (subs.):<BR>(1) विनिमयः;<BR>(2) निमेयः<BR>(rare);<BR>(3) नैमेयः (rare): v. Exchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barter
BARTER: (v. t.):<BR>(1) नि-मयते, विनि- (मे, c. 1.);<BR>(2) परि-वर्तयति (c. of वृत्) Ph.:<BR>he b. ed a<BR>book for a cloth<BR>*स पुस्तकं दत्वा वस्त्रं जग्राह।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

barter
BARTER (v. i.): द्रव्याणि विनिमयते न विक्रिणीते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

basalt
BASALT: प्रस्तरविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

base
BASE (adj.):<BR>I Of mean parentage:<BR>(1)<BR>अनभिजातः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) अकुलीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(3)<BR>दुष्कुलीनः (ना, नं). A b. man:<BR>(1) प्राकृतः;<BR>(2)<BR>पृथग्जनः, Ki.<BR>II A bastard: विजन्मन् (mfn.).<BR>III Mean, disingenuous:<BR>(1) निकृष्टः (ष्टा,<BR> ष्टं);<BR>(2) अपकृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>(3) कदर्यः (र्या,<BR> र्यं);<BR>(4) जघन्यः (न्या, न्यं);<BR>(5) पामरः (रा,<BR> रं).<BR>IV Of musical tones: गम्भीरः (रा,<BR> रं): v. Grave, deep. V. Of metals:<BR>निकृष्टः<BR>or<BR>अपकृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं). Ph.<BR>b. metal<BR>कुप्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

base
BASE (subs.):<BR>I The bottom of any thing:<BR>अधोभागः: v. Foot, foundation.<BR>II In geo.:<BR>भूः<BR>or<BR>भूमिः, Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

based on
BASED ON (as adj.): मूलः (ला, लं) (in comp.),<BR>b. on knowledge<BR>ज्ञानमूलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baseless
BASELESS: अमूलकः (का, कं): v. Groundless,<BR>imaginary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

basely
BASELY: expr. by the adj.: v. Meanly,<BR>disgracefully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

basement
BASEMENT:<BR>(1) मित्तिमूलम्;<BR>(2) वास्तु (n.):<BR>(3)<BR>पोटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baseness
BASENESS:<BR>I Meanness: q. v.:<BR>(1) निकृष्टता;<BR>(2) कदर्यता;<BR>(3) अनार्यता।<BR>II Of birth:<BR>दुष्कुलीनता।<BR>III Bastardy: विजन्मता।<BR>IV Of<BR>sounds: गाम्मीर्यम्। V. Of metal:<BR>(1)<BR>निकृष्टता;<BR>(2) अपकृष्टता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bashful
BASHFUL (adj.):<BR>(1) लज्जाशीलः (ला, लं) (applied<BR>only to persons);<BR>(2) लज्जालु (mfn.);<BR>(3)<BR>लज्जावत् (f. ती): v. Modest, shamefaced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bashfully
BASHFULLY:<BR>(1) सलज्जम्;<BR>(2) सव्रीडम्;<BR>(3)<BR>सत्रपम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bashfulness
BASHFULNESS:<BR>(1) लज्जाशीलता;<BR>(2) शालीनता:<BR>v. Modesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

basil
BASIL: तुलसी (the holy b.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

basilica
BASILICA: घर्मशाला (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

basilisk
BASILISK: सर्पभेदः; *तक्षकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

basin
BASIN:<BR>I A vessel for washing etc.:<BR>(1)<BR>द्रोणी;<BR>(2) भाण्डम् (any vessel)<BR>in a. b. of<BR>indigo<BR>नीलीभाण्डे, H. iii.<BR>II A reservoir:<BR>(1)<BR>जलाशयः;<BR>(2) तडागः;<BR>(3) कासारः।<BR>III A b.<BR>round the root of a tree: आलवालम्।<BR>IV<BR>dock: q. v. V. Geog. t. t.: *जलाघारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

basis
BASIS (subs.): मूलम्: v. Base, foundation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bask
BASK: आतपं सेवते, आ-, नि-, (सेव्, c. 1.),<BR>is b. ing<BR>in the morning sun<BR>बालातपं सेवते, v. t.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

basket
BASKET:<BR>(1) पेटकः<BR>or<BR>मञ्जूषा (=a large b. or<BR>box for keeping clothes etc.);<BR>(2) करण्डः<BR>(a small b. for gathering flowers etc.);<BR>(3) डल्लकम् (=a moderate sized portable b.);<BR>(4) विदलम्<BR>or<BR>वैदलम् (any b. work).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

basking
