bath
BATH:<BR>I A receptacle for bathing: *स्नान-<BR> पात्रम्,<BR>is the b. ready<BR>*अपि प्रस्तुतं स्नानपात्रम्।<BR>II<BR>Public b. s: स्नानशाला। Ph.:<BR>to take a cold<BR>shower b.<BR>*शीतलासारोदकैः स्नाति (स्ना, c. 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bathe
BATHE (v. i.):<BR>(1) स्नाति (स्ना, c. 2.);<BR>(2) अभिषेकं<BR> करोति (by pouring water);<BR>(3) मज्जति, नि-,<BR>(मज्ज्, c. 6.) (by plunging);<BR>(4) अवगाह<BR>(गाह्, c. 1.) (by immersing, diving) (with<BR>acc.),<BR>to b. in the waters<BR>पयोवगाढुम्, Ki. viii.<BR>27.;<BR>(5) आ-प्लवते (प्ल, c. 1.) (Perh. by<BR>swimming).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bathe
