bay-window
BAY-WINDOW: *प्रलम्बवातायनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bazar
BAZAR (subs.):<BR>(1) पण्यवीथिका;<BR>(2) आपणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bdellium
BDELLIUM:<BR>(1) गुग्गुलः;<BR>(2) उलूखलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

be
BE:<BR>I As a logical copula:<BR>(1) भवति (भू,<BR>c. 1),<BR>it is long-necked<BR>दीर्धग्रीवः स भवति, U.<BR>iv.;<BR>the hearts of good men are always com-<BR>passionate<BR>करुणार्द्राणि सतां खलु भवन्ति सदा चेतांसि,<BR>K. N. B. It is often understood:<BR>the end of<BR>aims is beyond comprehension<BR>दुरघिगमा हि गतिः<BR> प्रयोजनानाम्, Ki. x. 40.<BR>II Denoting existence,<BR>presence: अस्ति,<BR>there was formerly a king<BR>named Śudraka<BR>आसीद्राजा शूद्रको नाम, K.;<BR>and<BR>there are heaps of gems<BR>सन्ति रत्ननिचयाश्च भूरिशः,<BR>Ki. xiii. 55. N. B. Note (a) that this verb is<BR>exclusively used for there is-, there was-,<BR>etc.; (b) that in this sense, it is gen.<BR>placed at the beginning of the sentence;<BR>and (c) that this verb is defective and its<BR>non-conjugational tenses are supplied by<BR>those of भू and hence we meet with phrases<BR>like अभून्नृपः (-there was a king), B. i. 1.;<BR>(2) वर्तते, सं-, (वृत्, c. 1),<BR>in a moment you will<BR>be in your realm<BR>क्षणात् स्वाघिकारभूमौ वर्तिष्यते, Sa.<BR>vii.: v. To be present. Ph.:<BR>here are<BR>we<BR>इमे स्मः, Sa. iv.;<BR>be it so<BR>एवमस्तु, मवतु।<BR>III<BR>To become: q. v.: भवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

be over
BE OVER: Ph.<BR>let the rain be over<BR>भवतु वृष्ठेरुपशमः,<BR>H. iii.: v. To cease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beach
BEACH:<BR>(1) रोघस् (n.);<BR>(2) कूलम्: v. Shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beacon
BEACON: *आकाशदीपः, शत्रोरागमनसूचनाय समुद्रयायिनां<BR> च पथदर्शनायोन्नतभूभागस्थापिता महोल्का।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bead
BEAD (subs.):<BR>(1) गुली;<BR>(2) गुलिका;<BR>(3) गुटी;<BR>(4) गुटिका।<BR>A string of b. s<BR>माला; a rosary of<BR>b. s:<BR>(1) अक्षमाला;<BR>(2) जपमाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beadle
BEADLE: Perh. शोधनकः, Mr. ix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beagle
BEAGLE: आखेटिकः कुक्कुरप्रभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beak
BEAK:<BR>I Of birds:<BR>(1) चञ्चुः;<BR>(2) चञ्चूः;<BR>(3)<BR>त्रोटिः;<BR>(4) मुखम्;<BR>(5) तुण्डः।<BR>II Of ships:<BR>*चञ्चवाकारं पोतमुखम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beaked
BEAKED (adj.):<BR>(1) चञ्चुमत् (f. ती);<BR>(2) चञ्चु-<BR>विशिष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beaker
BEAKER (subs.): चषकः: v. Cup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beam
BEAM (subs.): Of a house: तुला, Si. iii. 50.<BR>II Of a balance:<BR>(1) तुलादण्डः;<BR>(2) तुलाधारः.<BR>III Of a loom:<BR>(1) वेमन् (n.);<BR>(2) वापदण्डः;<BR>(3) वायदण्डः।<BR>IV Of a carriage: धुर् (f.):<BR>v. Pole.<BR>V A ray of light: (अंशुः;<BR>(2)<BR>किरणः: v. Ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beam
BEAM (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.: भासते (भास्, c. 1): To<BR>gleam, glitter.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) लसति, उत्-, प्रोत्-,<BR>(लस्, c. 1);<BR>(2) स्फुरति (स्फुर्, c. 6).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bean
BEAN:<BR>(1) शिम्बा;<BR>(2) शिम्बिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bear
BEAR (v. t.):<BR>I To carry: q. v.: वहति (वह्,<BR>c. 1)<BR>II To sustain, support:<BR>(1) वहति,<BR>bore the bent down head with difficulty<BR>उवाह<BR> दुःखेन भृशानतं शिरः, Si. i. 57.<BR>(2) बिभर्ति (भृ, c. 3),<BR>easily bore the great burden of state<BR>महान्तं तं राज्य-<BR>भारमनायासेनैव बभार, K.<BR>III. To suffer, endure:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) वहति, उत्- (rare in this sense),<BR>surely distress...is very difficult to be borne<BR>दुःखानि नूनमतिमात्रदुरुद्वहांनि, Sa. iv.;<BR>(2) सहते, प्र-,<BR> वि-, (सह्, c. 1), could not b. the respect (paid<BR>to Kṛṣṇa) मानमसहत न, Si. xv. 1.;<BR>the faculty<BR>of b. ing cold, heat and wind<BR>शीतोष्णवातप्रसहि-<BR>ष्णुता, Ka. xv. 37.<BR>IV To bring forth,<BR>produce: q. v.:<BR>(1) वहति (very rare);<BR>(2)<BR>सूते (सू, c. 2),<BR>immediately^1 the Aśoka tree bore<BR>flowers<BR>असूत सद्यः कुसुमान्यशोकः, Ku. iii. 26.;<BR>(3) बिभर्ति (rare), Ki. viii. 4. V. To cherish,<BR>q. v. Ph.;<BR>I. b. no hatred towards you<BR>त्वयि मम<BR> द्वेषो नास्ति<BR>or<BR>न विद्यते etc.<BR>VI To behave:<BR>q. v.<BR>VII To admit: q. v. Ph.:<BR>to be. wit-<BR>ness<BR>साक्ष्यं ददाति (दा, c. 3); to b company<BR>सहचरः (री, रं) भवति (भू, c. 1) (with gen.);<BR>to b. a hand<BR>हस्तं ददाति (?);<BR>to b. a name<BR>नाम<BR> बिभर्ति M. ii. 157.;<BR>your good policy has borne<BR>fruit<BR>फलिता तव सुनीतिः। D. ii.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bear against
BEAR AGAINST: अभि-वर्तते (वृत्, c. 1), Ki. xii. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bear back
BEAR BACK: परा-वर्तते (वृत्, c. 1): v. To retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bear down
BEAR DOWN (v. i.): सन्निपतति (पत्, c. 1): v.<BR>To hasten, approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bear off
BEAR OFF:<BR>V To carry away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bear on
BEAR ON, or UPON: I To press, affect:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) पीडयति (पीड्, c. 10);<BR>(2) बाधते<BR>(बाध्, c. 1)<BR>II To have reference to:<BR>q. v.: लगति (लग्, c. 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bear out
BEAR OUT:<BR>I To carry out: q. v.<BR>II Fig.<BR>to support: q. v.: द्रढयति (nomi).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bear up
BEAR UP:<BR>I Trans: v. To support.<BR>II<BR>Intrans.:<BR>(1) उद्वहति, (with acc.);<BR>could not<BR>b. under the weight<BR>धुरमुद्वोढुं न शशाक;<BR>(2) सहते<BR>(with acc.): v. To resist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bear with
BEAR WITH: सहते (सह्, c. 1): v. To endure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bear
BEAR (subs.):<BR>I An animal:<BR>(1) भल्लः;<BR>(2)<BR>भल्लु (ल्लू) कः;<BR>(3) ऋक्षः;<BR>(4) अच्छभल्लः;<BR>(5)<BR>भाल्लूकः।<BR>II A constellation: Ph.:<BR>the little<BR>b.<BR>शिशुमारः (?) V. p. The seven stars of the<BR>Great Bear:<BR>(1) सप्तर्षिमण्डलम्; चित्रशिखण्डिनः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beard
BEARD (subs.):<BR>I Of men etc.:<BR>(1) श्मश्रु (n.);<BR>(2) कूर्चम्;<BR>(3) मुखरोमन् (n.)<BR>II Of corn:<BR>(1)<BR>शूकम्;<BR>(2) शुङ्गः;<BR>(3) किंशारुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beard
BEARD (v. t.)<BR>I To seize by the beard: श्मश्रुणा<BR>or<BR>श्मश्रुणि गृह्णाति (ग्रह c. 9).<BR>II To defy<BR>openly; न्यक्करोति (?): v. To insult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bearded
BEARDED (adj.)<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) श्मश्रुलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) कूर्चघरः (रा, रं),<BR>even by long-b. goats<BR>प्रलम्ब-<BR>कूर्चधरैश्छागैरपि, K. Ph.<BR>a b. woman<BR>पोटा (rare)<BR>II As corn:<BR>(1) by comp.<BR>b. corn<BR>शुकघान्यम्;<BR>(2) शुङ्गिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) शुकवत् (f. ती).<BR>III<BR>Bearded: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beardless
BEARDLESS:<BR>(1) श्मश्रुहीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) अनुद्भिन्न-<BR>श्मश्रु (mfn.);<BR>(3) अजातश्मश्रु (mfn.). N. B.<BR>(2)<BR>and<BR>(3) mean one whose beard has not come<BR>out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bearer
BEARER: i. e. porter, carrier: q. v.:<BR>(1) वाहकः;<BR>(2) वाहः; (at the end of a comp.). Letter b.<BR>पत्रवाहः; corpse b.;<BR>(1) शववाहः;<BR>(2) प्रेतनिहरिकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bearing
BEARING (subs.):<BR>I Gesture, mien: q. v.:<BR>चेष्टा;<BR>his b. is not as before<BR>अस्य चेष्टा नामायथापूर्वम्<BR>D. viii.<BR>II Relation, reference: q. v. Ph.<BR>what b. has your argument on this subject<BR>*अस्य-<BR>विषयस्य तवोपपत्तेश्च कः सम्बन्घः।<BR>III Relative [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">Page061</a>]<BR>situation: Ph. the b. of the cape is n. w.<BR>*अस्मात् पश्चिमोत्तरस्थमन्तरीपम्;<BR>ascertain the b. s of<BR>the lighthouse<BR>कतमस्मिन्दिग्भागे दीपगृहमिति ज्ञायताम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bearish
BEARISH: v. Rude, surly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beast
BEAST:<BR>I An irrational animal:<BR>(1) पशुः;<BR>(2) तिर्यच् (n.) (rare),<BR>a b. of prey:<BR>श्वापदः;<BR>a<BR>b. burden<BR>धुर्यः: v. Animal.<BR>II A brutal<BR>man: पशुः, Ve.: v. Brute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beastliness
BEASTLINESS: जघन्यता: v. Filthiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beastly
BEASTLY: जघन्यः (न्या, न्यं): V. Filthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beat
BEAT (v. t.):<BR>I To strike: q. v.:<BR>(1) ताडयति<BR>(तड्, c. 10),<BR>b. ing her breast<BR>सोरस्ताडम्, Vi.<BR>vi.;<BR>to b. in return<BR>प्रतीपं ताडयति, Mr. xi.;<BR>(2) हन्ति आ-, अभि-, नि-, (हन्, c. 2),<BR>of un-b.<BR>en drums<BR>अनाहतस्य दुन्दुभेः, Ki. xviii. 17.<BR>II<BR>To defeat: q. v.:<BR>(1) भनक्ति (मञ्ज्, c. 7),<BR>b.<BR>the king's troops in the battle<BR>राजानीकं बभञ्जाजौ,<BR>Raj.;<BR>(2) खण्डयति, परि, (खण्ड्, c. 10), B.<BR>xii. 17.;<BR>being b. en by the enemy<BR>खण्डनां प्राप्य<BR> परात्, Ki. xvii. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beat
BEAT (v. i.):<BR>I To strike, knock; q. v.; ताडयति<BR>(तड्, c. 10) (with acc.)<BR>II To palpitate:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) कम्पते (कम्प्, c. l); वेपते (वेप्, c. 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beat back or off
BEAT BACK or OFF: वि-द्रावयति (c. of द्रु): v.<BR>To drive back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beat down
BEAT DOWN:<BR>I To break, crush, or press<BR>down: q. v.<BR>II Of price: लघयति (nomi.):<BR>v. To lessen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beat-out
BEAT-OUT: Of metals: Perh. आहन्ति (हन्,<BR>c. 2): v. To forge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beat-up
BEAT-UP:<BR>I To attack suddenly: अलक्षितम्<BR> आक्रामति: v. To attack.<BR>II As eggs: Perh<BR>मृद्नाति (मृद्, c. 9)<BR>or<BR>घर्षति (धृष्, c. 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beat upon
BEAT UPON: Ph.<BR>the foam of big waves b. ing<BR>upon the rocks<BR>उपलाहतोद्धततरङ्गधृतं फेनमपाम्, Ki.<BR>vi. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beaten
BEATEN (adj.):<BR>(1) क्षुण्णः (ण्णा, ण्णं)<BR>from the b.<BR>track<BR>क्षुण्णाद्वर्त्मनः, R. i. 17.;<BR>(2) प्रहतः (ता, तं)<BR>M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beatific
BEATIFIC: निःश्रेयसकरः (री, रं), Ki. xi. 19:<BR>Blessed, blissful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beatification
BEATIFICATION: *दिव्यजनत्वारोपणम्; सिद्धिलाभ-<BR>प्रख्यापनम्: v. Next art.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beatify
BEATIFY:<BR>I To bless, make happy: q. v.:<BR>सुखयति।<BR>II t. t. in the Romish church *दिवं-<BR>गतः (ता, तं) इति प्रख्यापयति; दिव्यजनत्वम् आरोप-<BR>यति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beating
BEATING (subs.):<BR>I The act of striking:<BR>(1)<BR>ताडना;<BR>(2) ताडनभ्।<BR>II Of the heart: कम्पः।<BR>Ph. b. time (in music): तालः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beatitude
BEATITUDE:<BR>(1) मोक्षः;<BR>(2) मुक्तिः;<BR>(3) अपवर्गः;<BR>(4) निःश्रेयसम्;<BR>(5) सिद्धिः;<BR>(6) निर्वाणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beau
BEAU:<BR>(1) सुवेशिन् (m.);<BR>(2) सुभगम्मन्यः;<BR>(3)<BR>सुभगमानिन् (m.): v. Fop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beauteous
BEAUTEOUS:<BR>(1) सुन्दरः (री, रं);<BR>(2) रभ्यः (म्या,<BR> म्यं); v. Beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beautifier
BEAUTIFIER: i. e. a lady's maid:<BR>(1) प्रसाधिका;<BR>(2) ञ्लङ्कर्त्री।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beautiful
BEAUTIFUL:<BR>(1) सुन्दरः (री, रं);<BR>(2) रमणीयः (या,<BR> यं);<BR>(3) कमनीयः (या, यं);<BR>(4) शोभनः (ना, नं);<BR>(5) चारु (f. र्वी);<BR>(6) कान्तः (न्ता, न्तं);<BR>(7) पेशलः<BR>(ला, लं);<BR>(8) मञ्जुलः (ला, लं);<BR>(9) अभिरामः (मा, मं);<BR>(10) मनोज्ञः (ज्ञा, ज्ञं);<BR>(11) by सु in comp.;<BR>a<BR>girl with a b. face<BR>सुमुखी; Ph.:<BR>oh, what a b.<BR>morning<BR>अहो रमणीयता प्रभातस्य, Dh.;<BR>oh, what a<BR>b. place<BR>अहो रामणीयकमस्य, Na. I.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beautifully
BEAUTIFULLY:<BR>(1) सुन्दरम्;<BR>(2) चारु;<BR>(3) शोभनम्;<BR>(4) by the adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beautify
BEAUTIFY:<BR>(1) भूषयति (भूष्, c. 10);<BR>(2) प्रसाध-<BR>यति (c. of साघ्): v. To adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beauty
BEAUTY:<BR>(1) सौन्दर्यम्;<BR>(2) चारुता (=loveliness);<BR>(3) रमणीयता (=pleasantness);<BR>(4) शोभा<BR>(splendour);<BR>(5) रूपम् (=b. of person);<BR>(6) लावण्यम् (=prettiness);<BR>(7) अभिख्या (rare).<BR>Ph.: a. b. (=beautiful girl) सुन्दरी;<BR>the b.<BR>s of poem.<BR>काव्यस्य मधूनि (?);<BR>enchanted with<BR>the b. s of nature<BR>प्राकृतिकशोभयाहृतचित्तः (त्ता, त्तं);<BR>attained the b. of a bed<BR>शयनीयलक्ष्मीं बभार, Ki.<BR>viii. 57.;<BR>vying with the b. of the ocean<BR>पयोधि-<BR>लक्ष्मीमुषि, N. i. 117.: N. B. In the same sense<BR>श्री, which is more common in comps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beaver
BEAVER:<BR>I Aṇ animal: *विवरः, विवरेशयश्चतु-<BR>ष्पादजन्तुभेदः।<BR>II A b. hat: *विवरलोमनिर्मितमियु-<BR>रूपीयजनभृतशिरस्कम्।<BR>III Of a helmet: *शिर-<BR>स्कस्यप चिवुकप्रच्छादकभागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

becafico
BECAFICO: द्राक्षादिफलभक्षको क्षुद्रपक्षिमेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

becalm
BECALM (v. t.): शमयति, प्र-, उप-, (c. of शम्):<BR>v. To appease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

because
BECAUSE (conj.):<BR>(1) इति;<BR>poems are not good b.<BR>old, nor faultly b. new<BR>पुराणमित्येव न साधु सर्वं न<BR> चापि काव्यं नवमित्यवद्यम्, Mal. I. N. B. Note the<BR>position of इति;<BR>(2) हि (never at the begin-<BR>-ning of a sentence), b. you see that a rich<BR>man feels pain at the loss of his wealth (you<BR>cannot conclude that)<BR>he will have the same pain<BR>when he assumes mendicancy<BR>न हि धनिनो धनापहा-<BR>रनिमित्तं दुःखं दृष्टमिति तस्यैव प्रव्रजितस्य तदेव दुःखं भवति,<BR>S. i. 4.: v. For. N. B. Observe that न हि is<BR>the best way of expressing because...not.<BR>(3) कुतः<BR>or<BR>कस्मात् (=why) with abl.:<BR>here<BR>the word<BR>आयतन<BR>means something else, b. we hear<BR>that it is the bridge of ambrosia<BR>तत्रार्थान्तरं किम-<BR>प्यायतनं स्यादिति प्राप्तम्, कस्मात्? अमृतस्यैष सेतुरिति<BR> श्रवणात्, S. iii. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

because of
BECAUSE OF (prep.): By ins. or abl. etc.: v.<BR>Account of, on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beck
BECK (subs.):<BR>(1) सङ्केतः;<BR>(2) संज्ञा;<BR>(3) इङ्गितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beckon
BECKON (v. i.): संज्ञां, सङ्केतं<BR>or<BR>इङ्गितं ददाति (दा,<BR>c. 3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beckon
BECKON (v. t.): इङ्गितेन<BR>or<BR>संज्ञया आह्वयति, समा-,<BR>(ह्वे, c. 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

become
BECOME (v. i.): भवति (भू, c. 1), what in the<BR>forest became of the deer-eyed (damsel) किममवत्<BR> विपिने हरिणीदृशः, U. iii.<BR>(2) सम्पद्यते (पद्, c. 4).<BR>(rare) Me. i. 16. N.B. This verb in conne-<BR>-xion with adj. s, is (a) often expr. by verbs<BR>of motion with corres. sub. s.:<BR>became very<BR>sorry<BR>परं विषादमगमत्। P. i. 2.;<BR>b. s an object<BR>of hatred to the people<BR>द्वेष्यतां याति लोके, P. i. 3.;<BR>b. s of no use<BR>व्रजति व्यर्थकताम्, Si. xvi. 43. (b)<BR>and by verbs meaning to produce:<BR>b. ing<BR>very sorry<BR>समुपजातशोका, K. (his)<BR>face became<BR>terrible<BR>आननं क्रूरमजनि, Si. xv. 8. (c) and<BR>sometimes by verbs meaning to obtain:<BR>became surprised<BR>विस्मयमापेदे, K. (d) by incep-<BR>-tive verbs:<BR>to b. congealed<BR>घनीभवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

become
BECOME (v. t.):<BR>(1) युज्यते (pass. of युज्) (with)<BR>gen.);<BR>(2) उप-पद्यते (पद्, c. 4) (with gen.).<BR>Better by the adj. s अनुरूपः (पा, पं), सदृशः<BR>(शी, शं); उपपन्नः (न्ना, न्नं); युक्तः (क्ता, क्तं),<BR>etc. (with gen. or in comp.):<BR>we are going<BR>to act in a way, b. ing our prowess<BR>गच्छामो वयं<BR> विक्रमानुरूपमाचरितुम्, Ve. i.;<BR>and what b. s such<BR>love<BR>ईदृशस्य चानुरागस्य सदृशम्, R.;<BR>this does not b.<BR>men like you<BR>अनुपपन्नमिदं भवद्विधानां, Ve. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

becoming
BECOMING (adj.):<BR>(1) उचितः, समुचितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) उपयुक्तः, युक्तः (क्ता, क्तं): v. Suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

becoming
BECOMING, IT IS: साम्प्रतं, is not b. (for me)<BR>to<BR>speak now<BR>सम्प्रत्यसाम्प्रतं वक्तुम्, Si. ii. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

becomingness
BECOMINGNESS:<BR>(1) औचित्यम्;<BR>(2) योग्यता;<BR>(3)<BR>सामञ्जस्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bed
BED (subs.):<BR>I For sleeping:<BR>(1) शय्या, (best<BR>equiv.)<BR>a soft feather b.<BR>हंसतूलगर्भकोमलशय्या, D.<BR>ii.;<BR>making his bed<BR>उपरचय्य शय्याम्, D. v.;<BR>leave your b.<BR>मुञ्च शय्याम्, R. v. 66.;<BR>confined<BR>to b.<BR>शय्यागतः (ता, तं)<BR>or<BR>शय्याग्रस्तः (स्ता, स्तं);<BR>(2) शयनीयम्;<BR>(3) तल्पम्;<BR>(4) संस्तरः;<BR>(5) शयनम्,<BR>got out of b.<BR>शयनान्तादुत्थितः (ता, तं) Si. xi.<BR>7. (more commonly) सुप्तोत्थितः (ता, तं) Sa.;<BR>(6) औशीरम् (rare). Ph.<BR>defiler of a preceptor's<BR>b.<BR>गुरुतल्पगः;<BR>defiler of other's beds<BR>पारतल्पिकः,<BR>D.;<BR>to go to b.<BR>शेते (शी, c. 2): v. To sleep.<BR>II Marriage: q. v.: विवाहः।<BR>III Stratum,<BR>layer: q. v.: भित्तिः (?),<BR>in gold b. ed sum-<BR>mits<BR>काञ्चनभित्तिषु सानुषु, Ki. v. 8.<BR>IV Bottom<BR>of a stream:<BR>(1) तलम्;<BR>(2) अधोभागः V. Gar-<BR>-den-bed: प्रस्तरः<BR>or<BR>संस्तरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bedable
BEDABLE (v. t.):<BR>(1) सिञ्चति (सिच्, c. 6);<BR>(2)<BR>उक्षति (उक्ष्, c. 1) v. To sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bedaub
BEDAUB (v. t.): लिम्पति, वि-, (लिम्प्, c. 6): v.<BR>To besmear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bed-chamber
BED-CHAMBER:<BR>(1) शयनागारम्;<BR>(2) शयनगृहम्;<BR>(3) वासगृहम। (properly speaking, these words<BR>mean houses, as the Hindus had and even<BR>still gen. have separate houses for sleep-<BR>-ing: शयनकोष्ठः would be exact equiv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bed-clothes
BED-CLOTHES, BEDDING:<BR>(1) शय्योपस्कराः (m.<BR>pl.);<BR>(2) शय्योपकरणानि (n. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bedeck
BEDECK (v. t.):<BR>(1) विभूषयति (भूष्, c. 10);<BR>(2)<BR>मण्डयति (मण्ड्, c. 10) v. To adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bedew
BEDEW (v. t.) v. To moisten. Ph.<BR>her breast b. ed<BR>with drops of tear<BR>अश्रुबिन्दुतारकितपयोघरा, D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bed-hangings
BED-HANGINGS: वितानम्: v. Curtains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bedim
BEDIM (v. t.): To dim, obscure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bedizen
BEDIZEN (v. t.): no exact equiv.: मण्डयति (मण्ड्,<BR>c. 10): v. To adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bedlam
BEDLAM (subs.): *वातुलाश्रमः: v. Madhouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bedlamite
BEDLAMITE:<BR>(1) वातुलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) उन्मत्तः<BR>(त्ता, त्तं): v. mad man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bedrench
BEDRENCH: v. To drench.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bed-rid
BED-RID, BED-RIDDEN:<BR>(1) शय्यागतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) शय्याग्रस्तः (स्ता, स्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bed-room
BED-ROOM: शयनागारम्: v. Bed-chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bed-sheet
BED-SHEET:<BR>(1) शय्योत्तरच्छदः;<BR>(2) आस्तरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bed-stead
BED-STEAD:<BR>(1) पर्यङ्कः;<BR>(2) खट्वा, a small b.<BR>खट्विका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bed time
BED TIME:<BR>(1) शयनकालः;<BR>(2) शय्यागमनसमयः (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bee
BEE:<BR>(1) क्षुद्रा;<BR>(2) सरघा;<BR>(2) मधुमक्षिका;<BR>as b. s<BR>follow their queen<BR>यथा मधुकरराजं मघुमक्षिका अनु-<BR>वर्तन्ते, D. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bee-eater
BEE-EATER: *सरघाभुज् (m.); मधुमक्षिकाशिन् (m.);<BR>पक्षिविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bee-hive
BEE-HIVE:<BR>(1) छत्त्रकः;<BR>(2) करण्डः;<BR>(3) मधुकोषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beech
BEECH: वृक्षविशेषः;<BR>B. -nut<BR>*बीच्फलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beef
BEEF. गोमांसम्।<BR>Roast b.<BR>*शूल्यगोमांसम्, Salt b.<BR>*लावणगोमांसम्।<BR>A b. -steak<BR>भृष्टगोमांसखण्डम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beer
BEER: यवसुरम्; मदिराविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beet
BEET: पालङ्कः (a species of the b.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beetle
BEETLE:<BR>I An insect: गोमयोत्था।<BR>II A ram-<BR>-mer: मुद्गरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beetle
BEETLE (v.) प्रलम्बते (लम्ब्, c. 1): v. To pro-<BR>-ject, overhang.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beetle-browed
BEETLE-BROWED (adj.): उन्नतभ्रू (n. भ्रु) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beeves
BEEVES:<BR>(1) गावः (m. pl.);<BR>(2) गवां कदम्बकम्<BR>and sim. expressions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

befall
BEFALL (v.): नि-पतति, सम्-, आ-, (पत्, c. l)<BR>v. To happen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

befit
BEFIT (v. t.):<BR>(1) युज्यते;<BR>(2) उपपद्यते: v. To<BR>become, suit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

befitting
BEFITTING (adj.):<BR>(1) यथोचितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2)<BR>यथायोग्यः (ग्या, ग्यं): v. Fitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

befool
BEFOOL (v.): मोहयति, वि-, (c. of मुह्): v. To<BR>delude, deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

before
BEFORE (prep.):<BR>I In front of:<BR>(1) पुरस्,<BR>b.<BR>him<BR>पुरोऽस्य, Si. i. 12.;<BR>(2) पुरतः, b. the army<BR>सैन्यस्य पुरतः, Vi. vii.;<BR>(3) अग्रे,<BR>I will quit my<BR>life b. you<BR>तवाग्रे प्राणमोक्षणं करोमि, P. ii. p.;<BR>(4) अग्रतः, Ku. iv. 26.;<BR>(5) अभितः, Ki. ii.<BR>59.; N.B. Note that the first four are const.<BR>with gen., but<BR>(5) with the acc. Ph.:<BR>b. the<BR>wind<BR>अनुवातम्।<BR>II Before the eyes of: समक्षम्<BR>(with gen., or in comp. or absol). b. Umā<BR>उमासमक्षम्;<BR>b. her two friends<BR>सख्योः समक्षम्,<BR>b.<BR>her own eyes<BR>समक्षम्, Ku. iii. 64., 75.; v. I.<BR>III Of time, succession, etc.:<BR>(1) प्राक<BR>(with abl.),<BR>b. Chandragupta's entry<BR>प्राक् चन्द्र-<BR>गुप्तप्रवेशात्, Mu. ii.;<BR>(2) पूर्वम् (with abl.),<BR>after daughter's son, but b. the mother<BR>दौहित्रात्प-<BR>रतो मातृतश्च पूर्वम्, Da.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

before
BEFORE (adv.):<BR>I Of space:<BR>(1) पुरस्, from b.<BR>पुरस्तात्, K.:<BR>(2) पुरतः;<BR>(3) अग्रतः;<BR>(4) अग्रे।<BR>II<BR>Of time:<BR>(1) पुरा (=formerly: q. v.):<BR>(2) पूर्वम्<BR>not seen or known or felt b.<BR>अपूर्वः (र्वा,<BR> र्वं);<BR>not heard b.<BR>अश्रुतपूर्वः (र्वा, र्वं). N.B. Ob-<BR>-serve the cons. of यावत् न॥।तावत्॥ b. the<BR>Demons laughed in this way, his (step)<BR>found<BR>measure in the sky<BR>यावदित्थमहसन्न दानवास्तावदस्य न<BR> ममौ नभस्तले, Si. xiv. 75.; see also B. xii. 4.,<BR>Si. i. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

before-hand
BEFORE-HAND:<BR>(1) प्रागेव;<BR>(2) पूर्वमेव;<BR>(3) प्रथम-<BR>मेव;<BR>(4) आदावेव।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

before-mentioned
BEFORE-MENTIONED: पूर्वोक्तः (क्ता, क्तं);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रागुक्तः (क्ता, क्तं);<BR>(3) पूर्वोदितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

befoul
BEFOUL:<BR>(1) मलिनयति;<BR>(2) कलूषयति;<BR>(3) दूष-<BR>यति: v. To soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

befriend
BEFRIEND (v. t.): अनुकूलयति (nomi.): v. To<BR>aid, favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beg
BEG (v. i.):<BR>(1) भिक्षते (भिक्ष्, c. 1);<BR>(2) भिक्षां<BR> याचते (याच्, c. 1) etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beg
BEG (v. t.):<BR>(1) अञ्जलिं बद्ध्वा (=joining the palms)<BR>or<BR>जानुभ्यां स्थित्वा (=kneeling)<BR>or<BR>पादयोः पतित्वा<BR>(=falling on one's feet) निवेदयति, विज्ञापयति<BR>etc. (to inform, q. v.);<BR>(2) याचते: v.<BR>To ask. Ph.<BR>to b. the question<BR>प्रमेयं प्रमितं<BR> परिगृह्वाति (ग्रह्, c. 9) etc. (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beget
BEGET (v. t.):<BR>(1) जनयति, उप-, प्र-, वि-, (c. of<BR>जन्) (Lit. and Fig.) b. ting. a child by her<BR>जनयित्वा सुतं तस्याम्, M. iii. 17.;<BR>(2) उत्पादयति, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">Page064</a>]<BR>समुत्-, (c. of पद्),<BR>the child that a Brahmin<BR>lustfully b. s by a Śudra woman<BR>यं ब्राह्मणस्तु<BR> शूद्रायां कामादुत्पादयेत् सुतम्, M.: v. To bring forth,<BR>produce, cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begetter
BEGETTER:<BR>(1) जनयितृ (m.);<BR>(2) जनकः;<BR>(3)<BR>उत्पादकः: v. Father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begetting
BEGETTING (subs.):<BR>(1) जननम्;<BR>(2) प्रजननम्;<BR>(3) उत्पादनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beggar
BEGGAR (subs.):<BR>I A mendicant:<BR>(1) भिक्षुः;<BR>(2) भिक्षुकः (की, f.).<BR>II A very poor person:<BR>(1) दरिद्रः (द्रा, द्रं);<BR>(2) अकिञ्चनः (ना, नं): v.<BR>Indigent.<BR>III One who begs:<BR>(1) याचकः;<BR>(2) वनीयकः: v. Solicitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beggar
BEGGAR (v. t.): दरिद्रः (द्रा, द्रं)<BR>or<BR>निःस्वः (स्वा,<BR> स्वं) करोति (कृ, c. 8)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beggarly
BEGGARLY (adj.) कृपणः (णा, णं) (?): v. Mean,<BR>contemptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beggary
BEGGARY: दारिद्र्यम्: v. Poverty, indigence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begging
BEGGING (subs.):<BR>(1) भिक्षा;<BR>(2) भिक्षणम्;<BR>(3)<BR>भिक्षाटनम् (going about b.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begin
BEGIN (v.):<BR>(1) आरभते, प्रा-, समा-, (रम, c. l)<BR>the low people do not b. from fear of obstacles<BR>प्रारभ्यते न खलु विध्नभयेन नीचैः, Mu. ii.;<BR>(2) प्रवर्तते<BR>(वृत्, c. l) (with. inf. or loc.), began to weep<BR>रोदितुं प्रवृत्ता, Sa. v.;<BR>the singing is begun<BR>प्रवृत्तं<BR> सङ्गीतकम्, Mal. i.<BR>(3) उप-, क्रमते, प्र-, (क्रम्, c. l)<BR>(gen. with inf.),<BR>began thus to speak<BR>वक्तुमित्थमु-<BR>पचक्रमे वचः, Ki. xiii. 36;<BR>(4) प्र-स्तौति (स्तु, c. 2)<BR>(rare),<BR>b. the holy ceremony<BR>प्रस्तुतं कर्म धर्म्यम्, B.<BR>ii. 28;<BR>(5) प्र-कुरुते (कृ, c. 8) (rare),<BR>began<BR>to speak<BR>उदीरयितुं प्रचक्रे, N. xiii. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beginner
BEGINNER:<BR>I One who begins:<BR>(1) आरब्धृ<BR>(f. ब्घ्री);<BR>(2) उपक्रन्तृ (f. न्त्री).<BR>II A novice:<BR>q. v.: नवच्छात्रः (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beginning
BEGINNING (subs.):<BR>I Commencement:<BR>(1)<BR>आरम्भः;<BR>(2) प्रारम्भः;<BR>(3) समारम्मः।<BR>II The<BR>first cause: आदिः,<BR>you are the b. of the world<BR>but you yourself have no b., you are the end of<BR>the world, but you yourself have no end<BR>जगदादि-<BR>रनादिस्त्वं जगदन्तो निरन्तकः, Ku. ii. 9.: v.<BR>Cause, origin.<BR>III The first state: आदिः,<BR>in the b. (God)<BR>created water<BR>अप एव ससर्जादौ,<BR>M. i. 8.;<BR>I want to hear from the b.<BR>आदितः<BR>श्रोतुमिच्छामि, Mu. ii.; from the b. to the end<BR>आद्यन्तः (न्ता, न्तं).<BR>IV Rudiments: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begird
BEGIRD (v. t.):<BR>I To gird: q. v,<BR>II To en-<BR>-compass: q. v.: परिवेष्टते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begone
BEGONE (interj.): अपेहि अपसर, etc. (imper.<BR>dual sing.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begrimed
BEGRIMED (adj.): कलुषितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) दूषितः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR>B. with dust<BR>धूलिधूसरितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begrude
BEGRUDE: v. To grudge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beguile
BEGUILE (v. t.):<BR>I To cheat, deceive: q. v.<BR>वि-प्रलभते (लभ्, c. l).<BR>II Of time: Ph.<BR>b. d<BR>the day with various anecdotes<BR>कथाभिर्विनोद्यमानस्तं<BR> दिवसमवाहयत्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beguiler
BEGUILER: वञ्चकः: v. Deceiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behalf of
BEHALF OF, IN OR ON:<BR>(1) अर्थम्,<BR>on my b.<BR>मद-<BR>र्थम्;<BR>(2) कृते (with gen.) on b. of the Śudra<BR>वृषलस्य कृते: v. For, on account of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behave
BEHAVE (v. t.):<BR>(1) आचरति (चर्, c. l),<BR>the<BR>king b. d very ungentlemanly towards Śakuntalā<BR>तेन राज्ञा शकुन्तलायामनार्यमाचरितम्, Sa. iv.;<BR>(2)<BR>वर्तते (वृत्, c. l) (with loc.)<BR>b. politely towards<BR>him<BR>अस्मिन् विनयेन वर्तताम्, U. vi.;<BR>b. towards the<BR>other wives as dear friends<BR>कुरु प्रियसखीवृत्तिं सपत्नीजने<BR>Sa. iv.;<BR>(3) व्यवहरति (हृ, c. l), what (he) b.<BR>s towards me by (asking for)<BR>an interchange of<BR>acts<BR>कथं कार्यविनिमयेन मयि व्यवहरति, Mal. i.;<BR>(4)<BR>यतते, प्र-, (यत्, c. l) (to b. persistently),<BR>you should b. in such a way that she will be<BR>soon your worthy attendant<BR>तथा प्रयतितव्यं यथेय-<BR>मतिचिरमुचिता परिचारिका ते भवतीति, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behaviour
BEHAVIOUR:<BR>(1) वृत्तिः;<BR>(2) आचारः;<BR>(3) व्यव-<BR>हारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behead
BEHEAD (v. t.): शिरः<BR>or<BR>मूर्धानं<BR>or<BR>शीर्षं छिनत्ति<BR>(छिद्, c. 7)<BR>or<BR>कृन्तति (कृत्, or c. 7) or<BR>लुनाति (लु, c. 5) (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beheading
BEHEADING (subs.):<BR>(1) शिरश्छेदः;<BR>(2) शीर्ष-<BR>श्छेदः;<BR>(3) भूर्धच्छेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behest
BEHEST (subs.):<BR>(1) आज्ञा;<BR>(2) निदेशः: v.<BR>Command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behind
BEHIND (prep.):<BR>I At the back of:<BR>(1)<BR>पृष्ठतः (with gen.);<BR>(2) अनु (with acc.);<BR>(3)<BR>पश्चात् (with gen.),<BR>b. them<BR>तासां पश्चात्, Ku.<BR>Ph.<BR>from b. the bushes<BR>लताव्यवहितः (ता, तं), [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">Page065</a>]<BR>Sa. iii.<BR>II In a state of inferiority to:<BR>(1)<BR>नीचः (चा, चं):<BR>(2) अधःस्थः (स्था, स्थं): v.<BR>Inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behind
BEHIND (adv.):<BR>(1) पृष्ठतः (=on or from the<BR>back),<BR>shuts the king's eyes from b.<BR>पृष्ठेनागत्य<BR> राज्ञो लोचने संवृणोति, V. iii.;<BR>(2) पश्चात्,<BR>from<BR>b.<BR>पश्चादेत्य। V. iii.;<BR>putting b.<BR>पश्चात्क्रिया,<BR>Ki. xviii. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behold
BEHOLD (v. t.):<BR>(1) पश्यति (दृश्, c. l);<BR>(2)<BR>अव-लोकयति, वि-, (लोक्, c. 10); v. To see,<BR>look at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behold
BEHOLD (interj.) पश्य<BR>or<BR>पश्य पश्य (imper. dual<BR>sing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beholden
BEHOLDEN (part. adj.): v. Obliged, indebted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beholder
BEHOLDER:<BR>(1) प्रेक्षकः;<BR>(2) दर्शकः;<BR>(3) द्रष्ट्ट (m.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behoof
BEHOOF (subs.) लाभः: v. Advantage, benefit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behove
BEHOVE (v. impers.): Expr. by the future<BR>pass. part: it b. s you to forgive this fault<BR>अयमपराधो भवता मर्षयितव्यः, Sa. iv.: v. Ought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

being
BEING (subs.):<BR>I Existence:<BR>(1) अस्तित्वम्;<BR>(2) सद्भावः;<BR>(3) सत्वम्,<BR>(4) सत्ता,<BR>endowed with b.<BR>by birth<BR>जन्मना लब्धसत्ताकस्य, S. i. 2.<BR>II That<BR>with exists:<BR>(1) भूतम्,<BR>of mortal and immortal<BR>b. s<BR>मर्त्यामर्त्यस्य भूतग्रामस्य, U. vii.;<BR>(2) सत्वः;<BR>(3) विवेकिन् (m.) (=rational b.);<BR>(4) चेतनः<BR>(=sentient b.); (प्राणिन्, प्राणभृत् (m.) (=one<BR>endowed with life);<BR>(6) शरीरिन्, देहिन् (m.)<BR>(=corporeal b.) Ph. the Supreme B.<BR>परमेश्वरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

being
BEING (part.): When=from the fact of being<BR>., expr. by the abl.: v. From, since,<BR>in as much as.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belabour
BELABOUR: ताडयति (तड्, c. 10): V. To beat,<BR>cudgel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belay
BELAY:<BR>I To block up: q. v.<BR>II To fasten:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belch
BELCH (v.):<BR>(1) उत्-वमति (वम्, c. l); उत्-गिरति<BR>(गॄ, c. 6).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belch
BELCH, BELCHING (subs.):<BR>(1) (उद्वमः;<BR>(2)<BR>उद्वमनम्;<BR>(3) उद्गारः;<BR>(4) उद्गिरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beldam
BELDAM: वृद्धा: v. Old woman, hag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beleaguer
BELEAGUER (v. t.): रुणद्धि, अव-, उप, (रुध्, c. 7):<BR>v. To besiege, blockade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belfry
BELFRY: *घण्टाशृङ्गम्; यस्मिन् प्रासादशृङ्गे वादनाय घण्टा<BR> स्थाप्यते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belie
BELIE (v. t.):<BR>I To show to be false: expr.<BR>by<BR>(1) व्यनक्ति (व्यञ्ज्, c. 7);<BR>(2) वि-वृणोति (वृ,<BR>c. 5);<BR>(3) प्रकाशयति (nomi.) etc. (=to show:<BR>q. v.) the (wanton sword of)<BR>language of bad<BR>men b. s their heart<BR>हृदयं निगूहतः स्फुरन्नसाधोर्विवृणोति<BR> वागसिः, Ki. xiv. 12.<BR>II To calumniate,<BR>misrepresent: q. v.: अप-वदति (वद्, c. l).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belief
BELIEF (subs.):<BR>I Credence:<BR>(1) विश्वासः,<BR>worthy of b.<BR>विश्वासयोग्यः (ग्या, ग्यं): v. Credi-<BR>-ble;<BR>(2) प्रत्ययः।<BR>II Religious faith:<BR>(1) श्रद्धा;<BR>(2) विश्वासः;<BR>(3) आस्तिक्यम्;<BR>(4) आस्तिक्यबुद्धिः<BR>III Doctrine, opinion: q. v. मतम्।<BR>IV The<BR>object of belief: expr. by the verb:<BR>ghosts<BR>are the belief of fools<BR>*मूर्खा भूतेषु विश्वसन्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

believe
BELIEVE (v. i.):<BR>I To have faith in:<BR>(1)<BR>विश्वसिति (श्वस्, c. 2.) (with loc.)<BR>when does a<BR>virgin b. in man<BR>पुंसि विश्वसिति कुत्र कुमारी, N. v.<BR>100.<BR>(2) प्रत्येति (इ, c. 2.) (with acc.)<BR>every<BR>body b. s in the existence of his self<BR>सर्वो<BR> ह्यात्मास्तित्वं प्रत्येति, S.<BR>II To think, suppose:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) सम्भावयति;<BR>(2) मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

believe
BELIEVE (v. t.):<BR>(1) प्रत्येति, if you don't b. me<BR>यदि मम वचने न प्रत्येषि, Ra.;<BR>(2) विश्वसिति,<BR>so<BR>that his Highness would b. me<BR>यथा मां विश्वसेद् विभुः,<BR>A. r.;<BR>(3) श्रद्दधाति<BR>or<BR>श्रद्धत्ते (धा, c. 3)<BR>who will<BR>b. the real fact<BR>कः श्रद्धास्यति भूतार्थम्, Mr. iii.;<BR>(4) सम्भावयति (c. of भूः =to think possible),<BR>who will b. that the Maurya king sold the<BR>ornament<BR>मौर्ये भूषणविक्रयं नरपतौ को नाम सम्भावयेत्,<BR>Mr. v. Ph.<BR>I dont b. this<BR>अत्र मेऽप्रत्ययः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

believer
BELIEVER (subs.):<BR>(1) श्रद्धालुः;<BR>(2) विश्वासिन्<BR>(m.);<BR>(3) आस्तिकः (a religious b.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bell
BELL: घण्टा,<BR>to ring a b.<BR>घण्टां वादयति (c. of वद्);<BR>small tinkling b. s<BR>किङ्किणी, B. man: v. Bell-<BR>-ringer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bell-founder
BELL-FOUNDER: *घण्टाकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bell-foundry
BELL-FOUNDRY: *घण्टासन्धानशाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bell-metal
BELL-METAL: *घोषः; ताम्रत्रपुमिश्रितोपधातुभेदः, कांस्यम्<BR>(properly an alloy of copper and zinc).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bell-ringer
BELL-RINGER:<BR>(1) घण्टावादकः;<BR>(2) घण्टाताडः;<BR>(3) घाण्टिकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belle
BELLE:<BR>(1) सुन्दरी;<BR>(2) मत्तकाशिनी;<BR>(3) वरवर्णिनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belles-letters
BELLES-LETTERS: अलङ्कारादिशास्त्रम्: v. Litera-<BR>-ture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belligerent
BELLIGERENT:<BR>(1) युध्यमानः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) रणाभि-<BR>युक्तः (क्ता, क्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bellow
BELLOW (v. i.); नर्दति (नर्द्, c. l.): v. To<BR>roar, sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bellowing
BELLOWING (subs.):<BR>(1) नर्दितम्;<BR>(2) नर्दनम्;<BR>(3) गर्जनम्: v. Roaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bellows
BELLOWS:<BR>(1) भस्त्रा,<BR>a black-smith's b.<BR>कर्मकार-<BR>भस्त्रा, H.;<BR>(2) दृतिः;<BR>(3) चर्मप्रसेविका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belly
BELLY (subs.):<BR>I. Of an animal:<BR>(1) उदरम्;<BR>(2) कुक्षिः;<BR>(3) तुन्दम्, A.;<BR>(4) पिचिण्डः, A.<BR>one who has a big b.<BR>तुण्डिलः<BR>or<BR>पिचिण्डिलः<BR> (ला, लं).<BR>II The womb: q. v.: कुक्षिः।<BR>III The stomach: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belly
BELLY, BELLY OUT (v. i.): v. Swell out, pro-<BR>-ject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belly-ache
BELLY-ACHE: उदरशूलम्, Śr.; उदरवेदना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belly-band
BELLY-BAND: उदरत्राणम्: v. Girth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belly-ful
BELLY-FUL (adv.): आकण्ठम् (=up to the neck),<BR>they ate b.<BR>अमीभिराकण्ठमभोजि, N. xvi. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belong
BELONG (v. i.):<BR>I To be the property of:<BR>expr. by the gen. with भू gen. understood:<BR>it is said that a field b. s to him who clears the<BR>jungle<BR>स्थानुच्छेदकस्य केदारमाहुः, M. ix. 44: v.<BR>Belonging to, have.<BR>II To relate to, con-<BR>-cern: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belonging to
BELONGING TO (as adj.):<BR>(1) by- ईय deriv.<BR>b. to another<BR>अन्यदीयः (या, यं): b. to a king<BR>राजकीयः;<BR>(2) by- अ der.: b. to the season<BR>आर्तवः (वी, वं);<BR>b. the next world<BR>पारलौकिकः<BR>(की, कं);<BR>(3) by- य der.: b. to one's father<BR>पित्र्यः (त्र्या, त्र्यं);<BR>b. to a cow<BR>गव्यः (व्या, व्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beloved
BELOVED (adj.):<BR>(1) प्रियः (या, यं), o, my b.<BR>अयि प्रिये, N.;<BR>(2) इष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>(3) वल्लभः<BR>(भा, भं);<BR>(4) दयितः (ता, तं); v. Dear (II)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

below
BELOW (prep.):<BR>I Of place:<BR>(1) अधः or<BR>अधस्तात् (with gen.);<BR>(2) तले (with gen.),<BR>b.<BR>the bed<BR>पर्यङ्कतले, H.: v. Beneath, under.<BR>II Less than: Ph.:<BR>b. two years<BR>ऊनद्वि-<BR>वार्षिकः, M. v. 68.; v. Under.<BR>III Of rank<BR>or dignity: अनु (with acc.): v. Beneath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

below
BELOW (adv.):<BR>I Of place:<BR>(1) अधस्;<BR>(2)<BR>अधस्तात् (from b.)<BR>(3) अघोभागे (not of motion);<BR>(4) नीचैः: v. Down.<BR>II In the regions of<BR>the dead:<BR>(1) अधोलोके;<BR>(2) अधोभुवने।<BR>III<BR>To those regions: अधोलोकम् etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belt
BELT (subs.): मेखला (also=sword-belt): v.<BR>Girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belt
BELT (v. t.): v. To encompass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bemoan
BEMOAN (v. t.):<BR>(1) वि- लपति (लप्, c. l.),<BR>b. s.<BR>the loss of his son<BR>पुत्रशोकेन विलपति;<BR>b. s. the<BR>death of his brother<BR>भ्रातृमरणात् विलपति<BR>or<BR>भातृ-<BR>मरणशोकेन विलपति;<BR>(2) अनुशोचति (शुच्, c. l.)<BR>(rare)<BR>I b. my fate<BR>भाग्यमनुशोचामि;<BR>(3) परिदेवयति<BR>(देव्, c. 10.) (rare) v. To lament, bewail. N.B.<BR>Observe that only<BR>(2) takes a direct object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bench
BENCH<BR>I A seat: no equiv.: पीठः; पट्टः; फलकः,<BR>etc. may be used.<BR>II The seat of justice:<BR>(1) धर्मासनम् (the personal seat);<BR>(2) अधिकरण-<BR>मण्डपः, Mr. ix.;<BR>(3) व्यवहारमण्डपः, Mr. ix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bencher
BENCHER (of an inn of law): *सभासद्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bend
BEND (v. t.);<BR>I To inflect:<BR>(1) नमयति, आ-,<BR> -अव-, (c. of नम्),<BR>a bow not bent before<BR>धनुरनमित-<BR>पूर्वम्, R. xi. 72.;<BR>(2) आवर्जयति (वृज, c. 10),<BR>b. ing the boughs<BR>आवर्ज्य शाखाः, R. xvi. 19.;<BR>(3) वक्रीकरोति (कृ, c. 8) (=to curve);<BR>(4)<BR>भुजति, आ-, वि-, (भुज्, c. 6.),<BR>b. ing his neck<BR>विभुज्य<BR> कण्ठं, N. xi. 12.;<BR>(5) जिह्मयति (nomi.) (rare),<BR>Ph. (a bow that has been)<BR>bent:<BR>चक्रीकृतम्,<BR>Ku.; मण्डलीकृतम्<BR>or<BR>आविर्मण्डलम्, Ki. (धनुः).<BR>II Fig.: To subdue: q. v.:<BR>(1) नमयति,<BR>R.;<BR>(2) आवर्जयति, D.<BR>III To apply or<BR>exert: q. v. Ph.<BR>to b. one's mind<BR>मनो ददाति<BR>(दा, c. 3.);<BR>to b. the brow<BR>भ्रूभङ्गं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bend
BEND (v. i.)<BR>I To crook or be curving:<BR>(1)<BR>नमति, अव-, आ-, (नम्, c. l.)(2) by भवति and<BR>any one of the adj.s given under crooked,<BR>curved.<BR>II To bow: q. v.: नमति।<BR>III<BR>To be closely directed. Ph. bent on revenge<BR>प्रतिचिकीर्षु (mfn);<BR>bent on mischief<BR>जिघांसु<BR>(mfn.)<BR>or<BR>हिंसापरायणः (णा, णं); bent on religion<BR>धर्मपरायणः (णा, णं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bend down
BEND DOWN:<BR>I Trans.: अव-नमयति, आ-, (c. l.<BR>of नम्).<BR>II Intrans.: अव-नमति आ-, (नम्, c. 1.); [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">Page067</a>]<BR>head much bent down with sorrow<BR>दुःखेन भृशानतं<BR> शिरः, Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bend
BEND (subs): of a river:<BR>(1) वक्रम्;<BR>(2) वङ्कः;<BR>(3) पुटभेदः (वक्रीकरणम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bending
BENDING (subs):<BR>(1) नतिः;<BR>(2) नमनम्; अव-,<BR> आ-,;<BR>(3) आवर्जनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bending
BENDING (adj.): i. e. overhanging: प्रलम्बः<BR>(म्बा, म्बं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beneath
BENEATH (prep):<BR>I Under:<BR>(1) अधः<BR>or<BR>अधस्तात्<BR>(with gen.) or by the adj. अधस्थः (स्था, स्थं),<BR>b. the banyan tree<BR>न्यग्रोधस्याधस्तात्, P. iii. 4.;<BR>(2) तले in comp.,<BR>b. the bed<BR>पर्यङ्कतले, H. Ph.<BR>b. a. tree<BR>वृक्षमूले, V. s.<BR>II Fig.: Ph,<BR>our country<BR>sinks b. his yoke<BR>*तस्य पीडनेनाधोगच्छत्यस्मद्देशः।<BR>III Lower in rank etc.: अनु (with acc.)<BR>the gods are b. Viṣṇu<BR>अनुहरिं सुराः, S. k.: v.<BR>Low, inferior.<BR>IV Unbecoming, unworthy<BR>of: expr. circum.:<BR>he thinks it b. his dignity<BR>to converse with me<BR>*स मां सम्भाषणस्यायोग्यं<BR> मन्यते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beneath
BENEATH (adv.):<BR>(1) अधः;<BR>(2) अधस्तात्: v.<BR>Below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benediction
BENEDICTION:<BR>(1) आशिस् (f.);<BR>(2) आशीर्वादः:<BR>v. Blessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benefaction
BENEFACTION: v. Benefit, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benefactor
BENEFACTOR:<BR>(1) उपकर्तृ (m.);<BR>(2) उपकारकः;<BR>(3) उपकारिन् (m.);<BR>(4) हितकारिन् (m.);<BR>(5)<BR>प्रियकृत्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benefactress
BENEFACTRESS:<BR>(1) उपकर्त्री;<BR>(2) उपकारिणी;<BR>(3)<BR>हितकारिणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benefice
BENEFICE: वृत्तिः।<BR>A b. d. clergy man:<BR>वृत्तिभुक्<BR> पुरोहितः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beneficence
BENEFICENCE:<BR>(1) परोपकारिता;<BR>(2) दानशोलता<BR>(=magnificence: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beneficent
BENEFICENT:<BR>I As applied to men:<BR>(1)<BR>परोपकारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) परोपकारकः (का, कं);<BR>(3) दानशीलः (ला, लं) (munificent: q. v.).<BR>II As applied to acts etc.:<BR>(1) हितकरः (री,<BR> रं);<BR>(2) हितकारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beneficently
BENEFICENTLY: v. Benevolently, kindly,<BR>liberally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beneficial
BENEFICIAL: Ph.<BR>b. results<BR>शुभफलानि;<BR>b. exer-<BR>tions<BR>हितचेष्टितानि: v. Profitable, useful. To<BR>be b. to or for:<BR>हिताय (with gen.):<BR>agri-<BR>culture is b. for the whole human race<BR>कृषिः सर्व-<BR>लोकहिताय: v. Good (subs.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beneficially
BENEFICIALLY: v. Profitably, usefully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beneficiary
BENEFICIARY:<BR>(1) वृत्तिभुज् (mfn.) (?);<BR>(2)<BR>वृत्तिभोगिन् (f. नी) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benefit
BENEFIT (subs.)<BR>I An act of kindness, a<BR>favour conferred: उपकारः,<BR>like b. s. conferred<BR>on bad men<BR>उपकार इवासति प्रयुक्तः, Ki. xiii. 33.<BR>II Advantage, profit: q. v.:<BR>(1) उपकारः;<BR>(2) हितम्,<BR>for public b.<BR>प्रकृतिहिताय, Sa. vii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benefit
BENEFIT (v. t.): उपकरोति (कृ, c. 8.): v. To<BR>profit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benefit
BENEFIT (v. i.): v. To profit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benevolence
BENEVOLENCE:<BR>(1) हितैषिता;<BR>(2) परोपकारिता:<BR>v. Generosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benevolent
BENEVOLENT:<BR>I As applied to persons:<BR>(1)<BR>हितैषिन् (f. णी); परोपकारिन् (f. णी): v. Gener-<BR>-ous.<BR>II As applied to acts, institutions,<BR>etc.<BR>(1) हितकरः (री, रं);<BR>(2) हितकारिन् (f. णी।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benevolently
BENEVOLENTLY:<BR>(1) हितेच्छया;<BR>(2) कृपया (=<BR>kindly: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benighted
BENIGHTED:<BR>I Lit: Ph.<BR>we were b. in the<BR>wood<BR>वन एवास्माकं निशा जगाम।<BR>II Fig., of mind<BR>etc.<BR>(1) तिमिरावृतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) तमोवृतः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benign
BENIGN, BENIGNANT: दयालु (mfn.): v. Kind,<BR>generous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benignity
BENIGNITY:<BR>I Kindness: q. v. दयालुता।<BR>II<BR>Salubrity: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benignly
BENIGNLY:<BR>(1) सदयम् (=kindly: q. v.);<BR>(2)<BR>सौजन्येन (=graciously).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benison
BENISON: आशिस् (f.): v. Blessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bent
BENT (subs.):<BR>I Flexure, curvity:<BR>(1) नतिः;<BR>(2) जिह्मता;<BR>(3) वक्रता।<BR>II Slope, declivity:<BR>q. v.<BR>III Inclination, disposition: q. v.:<BR>भावः।<BR>IV Particular direction or tendency<BR>q. v. v. Bent grass: दूर्वा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benumb
BENUMB:<BR>(1) जडीकरोति<BR>or<BR>जडयति (nomi.);<BR>(2) स्तभ्नाति (स्तम्भ्, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

benzoin
BENZOIN:<BR>(1) कपितैलम्;<BR>(2) अश्मपुष्पम्;<BR>(3) शैलेयम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bequeath
BEQUEATH:<BR>(1) ददाति<BR>or<BR>यच्छति, प्र- (दा, c. 3<BR>or 1.);<BR>(2) प्रतिपादयति (c. of पद्);<BR>(3) समर्पयति [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">Page068</a>]<BR>(c. of कृ). N. B. These words simply mean<BR>to give: when precision is wanted, some<BR>qualifying words must be added:<BR>b. ed<BR>all his personal property to me<BR>*सर्वा अस्थावर-<BR>सम्पत्तीर्मामिच्छापत्रेण प्रदत्तवान्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bequest
BEQUEST: दानम् (gift: q. v.); (or precisely)<BR>*इच्छापत्रेण दानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bereave
BEREAVE (v. t.):<BR>(1) (वियोजयति (युज्, c. 10.),<BR>you<BR>will be bereft of your dear wife<BR>वियोक्ष्यसे वल्लभया,<BR>N. i. 138.;<BR>(2) विश्लेषयति (c. of शिलष्). v.<BR>To deprive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bereavement
BEREAVEMENT:<BR>(1) वियोगः;<BR>(2) विप्रयोगः: v.<BR>Deprivation, separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bereaver
BEREAVER:<BR>(1) वियोजकः;<BR>(2) विप्रयोजकः;<BR>(3)<BR>वियोक्ता;<BR>(4) विश्लेषकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bergamot
BERGAMOT: जम्बीरजातीयवृक्षविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

berry
BERRY: no equiv.: *सारफलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

berth
BERTH:<BR>I Anchorage: q. v.<BR>II Cabin: q. v.:<BR>कोष्ठः (?).<BR>III A place, situation: q. v.: पदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beryl
BERYL: मणिविशेषः; गोमेदः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beseech
BESEECH: प्रार्थयते (अर्थ, c. 10.): v. To beg,<BR>entreat, implore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beseem
BESEEM: युज्यते: v. To become (v. t.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beset
BESET:<BR>I To besiege, block up: q. v.:<BR>रुणद्धि (रुध्, c. 7.).<BR>II To harass, perplex:<BR>q. v.: बाधते (बाध्, c. l.).<BR>III To encom-<BR>-pass: q. v. वेष्टते, परि-, (वेष्ट्, c. l.).<BR>VI To set<BR>on or in: q. v.: छुरति, (छुर्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beshrew
BESHREW: v. To curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beside
BESIDE (prep.):<BR>I Near, by the side of:<BR>q. v.: पार्श्वे (with gen.)<BR>b. her father<BR>पितुः पार्श्वे,<BR>Ku. vi. 84.<BR>II Over and above: v.<BR>Besides.<BR>III Not belonging to: बहिः (with<BR>abl.),<BR>b. my theme<BR>प्रबन्धाद्वहिः<BR>or<BR>प्रबन्धस्य बहिर्भूतः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beside ones self
BESIDE ONE'S SELF:<BR>(1) हतज्ञानः (ना, नं);<BR>(2)<BR>विगतचेतनः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

besides
BESIDES (prep.):<BR>(1) by a comp. with भिन्नः<BR>(न्ना, न्नं)<BR>or<BR>व्यतिरिक्तः (क्ता, क्तं)<BR>b. this, another<BR>misfortune has befallen us<BR>एतद्भिन्नं<BR>or<BR>एतद्-<BR>व्यतिरिक्तं व्यसनमपरमस्माकमापतितम्;<BR>(2) विहाय,<BR> अपहाय, etc. (with acc.),<BR>I have no other friend<BR>b. you<BR>त्वामपहाय ममापरो बन्धुर्नास्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

besides
BESIDES (adv.): expr. by अन्यः (न्या, न्यत्) or<BR>अपरः (रा, रं) or by the prep.:<BR>are there any<BR>here b.<BR>किमत्रापरे सन्ति,<BR>I give you a horse b.<BR>एतद्व्यतिरिक्तं घोटकं तुभ्यं ददामि v. Also, more-<BR>-over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

besiege
BESIEGE (v. t.): रुणद्धि, उप-, अव-, (रुध्, c. 7.),<BR>b. d Champā<BR>रुरोध चम्पाम्, D. ii.; let (the<BR>Yadavas)<BR>b. Māhiṣmati<BR>माहिष्मन्तीमुपरुन्धन्तु,<BR>Si. ii. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

besieger
BESIEGER:<BR>(1) अवरोधकः;<BR>(2) अवरोद्धृ (m.) (?);<BR>(3) रोधिन् (m.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

besieging
BESIEGING (subs.):<BR>(1) रोधः;<BR>(2) अवरोधः;<BR>(3) उपरोधः;<BR>(4) रोधनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

besmear
BESMEAR (v. t.): लिम्पति, वि-, आ-, समा-, उप-,<BR> अनु-, (लिप्, c. 6.): v. To anoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

besom
BESOM (subs.): सम्मार्जनी: v. Broom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

besot
BESOT (v. t.): मोहयति (c. of मुह्): v. To<BR>stupefy, infatuate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bespatter
BESPATTER (v. t.):<BR>(1) अभ्युक्षति (उक्ष्, c. l.);<BR>(2) अभिषिञ्चति (सिच्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bespeak
BESPEAK (v. t.):<BR>I To order before hand:<BR>Ph. I bespoke a vessel to carry me to London<BR>*पूर्वमेव मयादेशि यानं यानाय लण्डने: v. To engage^1,<BR>hire.<BR>II To be taken: q. v.:<BR>(1) कथयति<BR>Śr.;<BR>(2) वदति (वद् c. 1.), (these signs)<BR>b.<BR>this death<BR>तं वदन्ति गतायुषम्, Śr.;<BR>(3) आवेदयति<BR>(c. of विद्), K.<BR>III. To address: q. v. भाषते<BR>(माष्।, c. l.)<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bespread
BESPREAD: v. To spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

besprinkle
BESPRINKLE (v. t.):<BR>(1) अभिषिञ्चति;<BR>(2)<BR>अभ्युक्षति: v. To sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

best
BEST (adj.): Super. of good: q. v. Ph.:<BR>to<BR>the b. of one's ability<BR>यावच्छक्तितः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

best
BEST (adv.): v. Well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bestial
BESTIAL (adj.): v. Beastly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bestiality
BESTIALITY: i. e. unnatural connection with<BR>a beast:<BR>(1) पशुगमनम्;<BR>(2) पशुषु मैथुनाचरणम्, V. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bestir oneself
BESTIR ONESELF:<BR>(1) यतते, प्र-, (यत्, c. l.);<BR>(2) घटते (घट्, c. l.): v. To exert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bestow
BESTOW (v. t.):<BR>I To give, grant: q. v.:<BR>ददाति (दा, c. 3.).<BR>II To give in marriage:<BR>ददाति, प्र-:<BR>she should be. b. ed on him whom she<BR>fancies<BR>यं चाभिलषेत् सामुष्मै देया, D. vi.<BR>III To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">Page069</a>]<BR>apply, use: q. v.: प्र-युनक्ति (युज्, c. 7.).<BR>IV<BR>To deposit, store: q. v.: नि-दधाति (धा,<BR>c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bestowal
BESTOWAL:<BR>(1) दानम्;<BR>(2) प्रदानम्;<BR>(3) प्रति-<BR>पादनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bestower
BESTOWER:<BR>(1) दातृ<BR>or<BR>प्रदातृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) द or<BR>प्रद (f. दा), in comp.;<BR>b. of money<BR>धनदः<BR>(दा, दं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bestrew
BESTREW (v. t.): स्तृणोति (स्तृ, c. 5.): v. To<BR>strew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bestride
BESTRIDE (v. t.): Ph.<BR>to b. a horse<BR>अश्वमारोहति<BR>(रुह्, c. l.): v. To stride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bet
BET (sub.):<BR>(1) पणः;<BR>(2) ग्लहः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bet
BET (v. t.) पणं करोति (कृ, c. 8.);<BR>(2) पणतां नयति<BR>(नी, c. l.), Ki. xi. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

betake
BETAKE (v. i.):<BR>(1) आ-श्रयति, सभा-, उपा-, (श्रि,<BR>c. l.),<BR>b. n to Malayaketu<BR>मलयकेतुमाश्रितः (ता,<BR> तं), Mu. iii.<BR>(2) मजति, -ते, (भज्, c. l.),<BR>shall<BR>I b. to quiet<BR>शान्तिं भजामि, Ma. n.<BR>IV 50.:<BR>v. Recourse to, have.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

betel
BETEL (subs.):<BR>(1) ताम्बूली;<BR>(2) नागवल्ली;<BR>(3)<BR>नागलता;<BR>(4) कुहली।<BR>The prepared b.<BR>ताम्बूलम्।<BR>B. -seller<BR>ताम्बूलिकः।<BR>B. -box = -bearer<BR>ताम्बूल-<BR>करङ्कवाहिनी, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

betel-nut
BETEL-NUT:<BR>(1) पूगम्;<BR>(2) गुवाकम्;<BR>(3) ताम्बूलम्।<BR>B. tree:<BR>(1) पूगः;<BR>(2) क्रमुः;<BR>(3) गुवाकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bethink oneself
BETHINK ONESELF: संचिन्तयति (चिन्त्, c. 10):<BR>v. To remember, reflect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

betide
BETIDE (v. t.): v, To happen, befall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

betimes
BETIMES (adv.):<BR>I Seasonably: q. v.: समये।<BR>II Soon: q. v.: शीघ्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

betaken
BETAKEN (v. t.): सूचयति, आ-वि-, (सूच्, c. 10.):<BR>v. To forebode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

betray
BETRAY (v. t.):<BR>I To give up treacherously:<BR>Ph.<BR>b. ed the fleet to the pirates<BR>*सविश्रम्म्भघातं<BR> पोतावलीं दस्युहस्ते समर्पयामास (c. of ऋ);<BR>do not<BR>b. your trust<BR>मा विश्वासं वधीः (हन्, c. 2.)<BR>or<BR>भांक्षीः<BR>(भञ्ज्, c. 7.).<BR>II To disclose: q. v.: भिनत्ति<BR>(भिद्, c. 7.),<BR>b. ed the secret<BR>रहस्यं बिभेद।<BR>III<BR>To mislead, expose, or indicate: q. v.<BR>IV<BR>To deceive: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

betrayal
BETRAYAL: Ph.<BR>the b. of a city<BR>शत्रुहस्ते नगर-<BR>समर्पणम्: v. To betray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

betrayer
BETRAYER:<BR>(1) विश्वासघातकः (=traitor);<BR>(2)<BR>वञ्चकः (=deceiver). Ph.<BR>where is the b. of<BR>the city<BR>क्व स विश्वासधातकः, यो नगरं शत्रुहस्ते समर्पया-<BR>मास। N.B. Note that in such cases<BR>(1) or<BR>(2) simply will not do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

betroth
BETROTH (v. t.):<BR>(1) ददाति (दा, c. 3.) (only of<BR>b. al by the father or guardian of the<BR>girl),<BR>I apprehend she is already b. ed<BR>दत्तपूर्वेत्या-<BR>शंक्यते, Ma.;<BR>(2) प्रतिपादयति (c. of पद्), Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

betrothal
BETROTHAL:<BR>(1) वागदानम् (=verbal b. of a<BR>girl by her father or guardian);<BR>(2) विवाह-<BR>सम्बन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

betrothed
BETROTHED (adj.):<BR>(1) दत्ता<BR>or<BR>वाग्दत्ता (a girl<BR>b. by her father or guardian) Da. com.;<BR>(2) प्रतिपादिता,<BR>b. ed wife<BR>प्रतिपादिता वधूः, Si.<BR>xvi. 49.<BR>(3) प्रतिश्रुतः (ता, तं) (=engaged,<BR>promised). N.B. The person to whom one<BR>is b. is put in the dat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

better
BETTER (adj.):<BR>I Comparative of good:<BR>q. v.<BR>II Preferable; Ph. b. (to have)<BR>a<BR>learned enemy than a stupid friend^1<BR>पण्डितोऽपि<BR> वरं शत्रुर्न मूर्खो हितकारकः, P. i. 21.;<BR>b. to die<BR>than to mix with low people<BR>वरं प्राणत्यागो<BR> न पुनरधमानामुपगमः, H. i.;<BR>b. to keep silence<BR>than to utter a lie<BR>वरं मौनं कार्यं न च वचनमुक्तं<BR> यदनृनम्; H.<BR>III. In improved health: Ph.:<BR>are you b.? Oh, yes, a little b.<BR>अपि ते लघु-<BR>सन्तापान्यङ्गानि? अहो अस्ति विशेषः, Sa. iii.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

better off
BETTER OFF, BE: v. Well off, be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

better
BETTER (subs.):<BR>I Advantage or victory:<BR>q. v.: Ph.<BR>to get the b. of an enemy<BR>शत्रूमभिभवति<BR>(भू, c. l.).<BR>II Improvement: q. v.<BR>III<BR>In pl. superiors गुरवः (m. pl.): Ph.<BR>your<BR>b. s in knowledge<BR>त्वदधिकज्ञानसम्पन्नाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

better
BETTER (v.): To mend, improve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

better
BETTER (adv.): v. Well. Ph.:<BR>I love you b.<BR>than self<BR>*त्वय्यहं प्राणेम्योऽधिकमनुरक्तः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

between
BETWEEN, BETWIXT<BR>(1) by the gen. (not of<BR>time),<BR>the distance b. the Hemakūta and the<BR>Vindhyas is very great<BR>विप्रकृष्टमन्तरं हेमकूटविन्ध्या-<BR>चलयोः, K.;<BR>the space b. the divine rivers<BR>Sarasvati and Drishadvati<BR>सरस्वतीदृषद्वत्योर्देव-<BR>नद्योर्यदन्तरम्, M. ii. 17.;<BR>enmity b. us<BR>तस्य च [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=070" target="_blank">Page070</a>]<BR>मम च वैरम्, D. ii.;<BR>the conflict b. the two im-<BR>portant duties<BR>विप्रतिषेधं तं गुरुणोरथ कार्ययोः, Si. ii.<BR>6.;<BR>(2) मध्ये<BR>or<BR>अन्तरे (with gen.) (of time<BR>and occasionally of other relations):<BR>middle age is b. sixteen and seventy years<BR>षोडश-<BR>सप्तत्योरन्तरे मध्यं वयः। Śr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beverage
BEVERAGE: पानीयम्: v. Drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bevy
BEVY:<BR>I Of ladies etc.: गणः।<BR>II Of birds:<BR>कुलम्: v. Flock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bewail
BEWAIL (v.): वि-लपति (लप्, c. l.),<BR>what are you<BR>b. ing for<BR>किमर्थं विलपसि: v. To lament,<BR>weep, grieve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bewailing
BEWAILING (subs).:<BR>(1) विलापः;<BR>(2) परिदेवनम्;<BR>(3) क्रन्दनम्: v. Lamentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beware
BEWARE: no exact equiv.:<BR>b. of him<BR>तस्मिन्<BR> बद्धविश्वासो मा भव;<BR>b. of your servants that they<BR>may not deceive you<BR>तथा प्रयतेथाः यथा न वञ्च्यसे<BR> सेवकैः;<BR>b. of your steps<BR>सावधानं परिक्राम: v.<BR>Care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bewilder
BEWILDER:<BR>(1) सं-मोहयति (c. of मुह्);<BR>(2) जडी-<BR>करोति (कृ, c. 8.)<BR>or<BR>जडयति (nomi.);<BR>(3) सं-<BR>भ्रमयति (c. of. भ्रम्);<BR>(4) विक्लवीकरोति (कृ, c. 8.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bewildered
BEWILDERED:<BR>(1) सम्भ्रान्तः (न्ता, न्तं);<BR>(2)<BR>विक्लवः (वा, वं);<BR>(3) किंकर्तव्यतामूढः (ढा, ढं)<BR>(=not to know what to do);<BR>(4) संमुग्धः<BR>(ग्धा, ग्धं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bewilderment
BEWILDERMENT:<BR>(1) सम्भ्रमः;<BR>(2) वैक्लव्यम्;<BR>(3)<BR>सम्मोहः: v. Perplexity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bewitch
BEWITCH:<BR>I To charm or fascinate:<BR>(1)<BR>मोहयति, परि-, वि-, सं-, (c. of मुह्,),<BR>let not Cupid<BR>b. you<BR>मा मूमुहत् खलु भवन्तमनन्यजन्मा, Ma. i.;<BR>(2) मदयति (c. 10. मद्),<BR>which b. the heart<BR>मनो<BR> मदयन्ति ये, Ma. i.<BR>II To fascinate by<BR>magic:<BR>(1) मोहयति;<BR>(2) मन्त्रेण वशीकरोति<BR>(कृ, c. 8.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bewitcher
BEWITCHER: v. Enchanter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bewitching
BEWITCHING (adj.): मोहनः (नी<BR>or<BR>ना, नं): v.<BR>Charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beyond
BEYOND (prep.):<BR>I On the further side of:<BR>Ph:<BR>b. it a desolate forest and b. that the<BR>mount Kailāsa<BR>ततः परतो निर्मानुषमरण्यं, तच्चातिक्रम्य<BR> कैलासगिरिः, K.; b. the range of speech and mind<BR>अतीत्य वाचां मनसां च गोचरम्, Ki. xviii. 41.<BR>II Further than, past: Ph. this is b. us<BR>इदमस्माकमसाध्यम्; it was even b. my expectations<BR>मनोरथानामप्यभूमिः, Sa. vii.;<BR>b. measure<BR>अतीव;<BR>who is b. our senses<BR>अतीन्द्रियाय, M. n.;<BR>naturally b. any one's comprehension<BR>निसर्गदुर्बोधः<BR>(धा, धं) Ki. Ph.: b. the seas: i. e. out of the<BR>country: द्वीपान्तरे (not समुद्रपारे, which = on<BR>the coast of the sea).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beyond
BEYOND (adv.): i. e. yonder: q. v.: दूरे,<BR>from<BR>b.<BR>दूरात्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beyond
