BIESTINGS (subs.):<BR>(1) पीयूष (mn.);<BR>(2) पेयूष<BR>(mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bifurcation
BIFURCATION: Ph.<BR>near the b. of the river<BR>यत्र<BR> नदी दूयोः प्रवाहयोः प्रविभक्ता तस्य समीपे।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

big
BIG (adj.):<BR>I Large, huge: q. v.:<BR>(1) बृहत्<BR>(f. ती) (not applicable to men);<BR>(2) बृहत्-<BR>कायः<BR>or<BR>महाकायः (या, यं) (=large-bodied);<BR>(3) महाप्रमाणः<BR>or<BR>अतिप्रमाणः (णा, णं) (=of large<BR>height),<BR>a b. man<BR>महाप्रमाणः पुरुषः K., saw the<BR>b. (horse)<BR>Indrāyudha<BR>अतिप्रमाणमिन्द्रायुधमद्राक्षीत्,<BR>K.<BR>II. Pregnant (Lit. and Fig.): q. v.:<BR>III<BR>Boastful: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bigamist
BIGAMIST:<BR>I The man:<BR>(1) द्विभार्यः;<BR>(2)<BR>द्विपत्नीकः।<BR>II The woman *द्विभर्तृका; वर्तमाने<BR> पत्यौ या स्त्री पुनर्विवाहं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bigamy
BIGAMY:<BR>(1) *द्विस्त्रीकरणम् (of men;<BR>(2) *द्विपती-<BR>करणम् (of women).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bight
BIGHT: v. Bay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bigness
BIGNESS: v. Bulk, size.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bigot
BIGOT: *धर्मनिर्बद्धः (द्धा, द्धं); यः (या, यं) अविचारेणान्य-<BR>मतानि प्रत्याख्याय स्वमतमनुवर्तते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bigoted
BIGOTED (adj.): v. Bigot. Ph.<BR>this is a b.<BR>country<BR>*अत्र पुरुषाः अविचारेण स्वमतासक्ताः<BR>or<BR>परधर्म-<BR>विद्वेषिणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bigotry
BIGOTRY: *धर्मनिर्बन्धः; स्वमताग्रहः; अविचारेण<BR> स्वमतासक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bile
BILE: पित्तम्। To stir one's b. (Fig.) वायुं प्रकोपयति<BR>(c. of कुप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bilge-water
BILGE-WATER: नौकातलजलम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

biliary
BILIARY (adj.):<BR>the b. duct<BR>पित्तवाहिनी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bilious
BILIOUS (adj.): पैत्तिकः (की, कं):<BR>b. fever<BR>पित्त-<BR>ज्वरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bilk
BILK (v. t.): वञ्चयते (वञ्च, c. 10.): v. To cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bill
BILL (sub.):<BR>I A declaration in writing लेखः,<BR>a b. of indictment<BR>अभियोगलेखः।<BR>II A bill of<BR>exchange: *हुण्डिः,<BR>a b. payable at sight<BR>*दर्शन-<BR>देयो हुण्डिः।<BR>III Proposed law: *पाण्डुलिपिः,<BR>the House of Commons rejected the b. by a great<BR>majority<BR>*बहुसभ्यानामैकमत्येन साधारणसभा पाण्डुलिपिं<BR> प्रत्यादिदेश।<BR>IV A written or printed notice:<BR>घोषणापत्रम्: v. Advertisement, placard. V. An<BR>account (rendered) of money due: *देयपत्रम्,<BR>make out a b. for me.<BR>मया यत्तुभ्यं देयं तस्य गणनां<BR> कुरु। Miscell.:<BR>a. b. of sale<BR>विक्रयपत्रम्;<BR>a b. of<BR>lading<BR>*प्रेरणपत्रम्।<BR>VI The beak of a bird:<BR>(1) चञ्चुः;<BR>(2) चञ्चुपुटः।<BR>VII A mattock, a<BR>hatchet: q. v.: दात्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bill
BILL (v. i.): Ph. the pigeons are b. ing and cooing<BR>अन्योन्यस्य चञ्चुं संघट्य कपोताः कुजन्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

billet
BILLET (subs.):<BR>I A note: q. v.: पत्रम्।<BR>II<BR>A ticket: q. v. निदर्शनपत्रम्।<BR>III A log of<BR>wood: काष्ठम्: v. Log, stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

billet
BILLET (v. t.); i. e. to quarter as soldiers:<BR>निवेशयति (c. of विश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bill-hook
BILL-HOOK: फणिमुखः; D.: v. Hatchet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

billiard
BILLIARD (adj.): Ph.<BR>a b. ball<BR>*अण्डम्;<BR>b.<BR>room<BR>*अण्डागारम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

billiards
BILLIARDS: *अण्डक्रीडा।<BR>To play at b.<BR>*अण्डैः<BR> क्रीडति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

billion
BILLION: खर्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

billow
BILLOW:<BR>(1) महोर्मिः;<BR>(2) कल्लोलः;<BR>(3) उल्लोलः;<BR>(4) लहरिः: v. Wave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

billowy
BILLOWY:<BR>(1) तरङ्गितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) ऊर्मिमालिन्<BR>(f. नी);<BR>(3) कल्लोलमालाकुलः (ला, लं);<BR>(4)<BR>उद्वेलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bin
BIN (subs.): Ph.<BR>corn-b.<BR>धान्यकोष्ठः; wine-b.<BR>मदिराकोष्ठः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

binary
BINARY (adj.): Ph.<BR>a b. compound<BR>*द्विभूतजं<BR> द्रव्यम्;<BR>b. scale<BR>*द्विकमूला गणनापद्धतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bind
BIND (v. t):<BR>I Lit., to tie: q. v.:<BR>(1) बध्नाति,<BR> नि-, (बन्ध्, c. 9.)<BR>b. ing firmly to a post<BR>स्थूणया<BR> सह दृढबन्धनेन बद्ध्वा, P. i. 4.;<BR>(2) सं-यच्छति (यम्,<BR>c. l.) (=to restrain: q. v.),<BR>as if bound by<BR>chains<BR>निगडैरिव सं-यताम्, K.<BR>II. Fig., to<BR>restrain, hold in check: बध्नाति, नि-, (बन्ध, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">Page072</a>]<BR>c. 9.),<BR>bound by affection<BR>स्नेहनिबद्धः (द्धा, द्धं), Ki.<BR>ii. 44.,<BR>b. s my sight<BR>बध्नाति मे चक्षुः, R. xiii.<BR>47.;<BR>(2) नियन्त्रयति (यन्त्र्, c. 10),<BR>laws do not b.<BR>him<BR>*विधयस्तं न नियन्त्रयन्ति। Ph.<BR>b. him by an<BR>oath<BR>शपथेन तमाबद्धं कुरु<BR>III To render costive:<BR>(1) बध्नाति, नि-,<BR>b. ing of the bowels<BR>बद्धविट्कता,<BR>Śr.;<BR>(2) आनह्यति (नह्, c. 4.)<BR>IV To bind<BR>books: (चर्मादिना) बध्नाति (?). V. To protect<BR>with a border: बध्नाति (?): V. To border,<BR>fringe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bind over
BIND OVER: आबध्नाति<BR>or<BR>आबद्धः (द्धा, द्धं) करोति (?).<BR>Ph.<BR>b. him over in 100 Rs. recognizance to keep<BR>the peace<BR>*शान्तिरक्षार्थं शतरूप्यमुद्रादानप्रतिज्ञया<BR> तमाबद्धं कुरु।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bind up
BIND UP: बध्नाति, नि-, (बन्ध्, c. 9.):<BR>the snakes<BR>as if b. ing up the wounds of the branches<BR>शाखानां<BR> व्रणमिव निबध्नन्ति फणिनः, Mu. vi. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bind up in or with
BIND UP IN or WITH: only in pass.: Ph.<BR>my<BR>love for you is bound up with my nature<BR>त्वयि मे<BR> भावनिबन्धना रतिः, R. viii. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

binder
BINDER: i. e. book- b.:<BR>(1) *पुस्तकबन्धनकारी;<BR>(2) *पुस्तकपिधाता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

binding
BINDING (subs.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) बन्धः;<BR>(2)<BR>बन्धनम्।<BR>II Of a book: Perh पिधानम्: v.<BR>Covering.<BR>III Of a dress: v. Border,<BR>fringe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

binding
BINDING (adj.): Of medicines: ग्राहिन् or<BR>संग्राहिन् (f. णी), Śr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bind-weed
BIND-WEED: क्षीरविदारी (a species of convolvu-<BR>-lus).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

binocular
BINOCULAR (adj.):<BR>(1) द्विनयनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2)<BR>द्विनेत्रः (त्रा, त्रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

binomial
BINOMIAL: *द्विपदः (दा, दं).<BR>B. theorem<BR>*द्विपद-<BR>वृद्धितत्त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

biographer
BIOGRAPHER:<BR>(1) *चरितलेखकः;<BR>(2) जीवन-<BR>चरितरचकः;<BR>(3) *जीवनचरितकृत् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

biographical
BIOGRAPHICAL: Ph. b. writer: v. Biographer;<BR>b. work: v. Biography.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

biography
BIOGRAPHY:<BR>(1) चरितम्,<BR>b. of Śriharṣa<BR>श्रीहर्ष-<BR>चरितम्, C.;<BR>(2) जीवनचरितम्;<BR>(3) जीवनवृत्तान्तः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bipartite
BIPARTITE (adj.): Perh. द्वैधः (धी, धं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

biped
BIPED (adj.):<BR>(1) द्विपदः<BR>or<BR>द्विपादः (दा, दं);<BR>(2)<BR>द्विपाद् (m.), पती (f.) पत्, (n.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

birch or birch-tree
BIRCH or BIRCH-TREE: भूर्जः भूर्जपत्रः or (a species<BR>of b.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

birchen
BIRCHEN (adj.):<BR>(1) by tat. comp.;<BR>(2) भूर्ज-<BR>मयः (यी, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bird
BIRD:<BR>(1) विहगः;<BR>(2) विहङ्गः;<BR>(3) विहङ्गमः;<BR>(4) पक्षिन् (m.);<BR>(5) पतत्रिन् (m.);<BR>(6) पतगः;<BR>(7) खगः;<BR>(8) शकुन्तः;<BR>(9) शकुनः;<BR>(10) विष्किरः;<BR>(11) गरुत्मत् (m.);<BR>(12) द्विजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bird-cage
BIRD-CAGE: पिञ्जरम्<BR>or<BR>पञ्जरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bird-call
BIRD-CALL: पक्षिरुतानुकारिणी वंशी यया प्रलोभ्य पक्षिणो<BR> बध्यन्ते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bird-catcher
BIRD-CATCHER:<BR>(1) शाकुनिकः;<BR>(2) पाक्षिकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bird-keeper
BIRD-KEEPER:<BR>(1) विहगपालः;<BR>(2) पक्षिपालः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bird-lime
BIRD-LIME: पक्षिबन्धनार्थं श्यानोदपेषम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

birth
BIRTH (subs):<BR>I Coming into life:<BR>(1) जन्मन्<BR>(n.) (the best equiv.),<BR>blind from b.<BR>जन्मान्धः<BR>(न्धा, न्धं);<BR>(2) जन्यम्;<BR>(3) जननम्;<BR>(4) जनिः;<BR>(5) उद्भवः;<BR>(6) उत्पत्तिः;<BR>(7) भवः;<BR>(8) सम्भवः;<BR>(9) सूतिः; Ph.<BR>lordship from b.<BR>गर्भेश्वरत्वम्, K.<BR>II Lineage, descent^1: q. v.:<BR>(1) कुलम्,<BR>(2)<BR>अन्वयः; Ph.<BR>proud of one's b.<BR>कुलाभिमानिन् (f.<BR>नी), Ki.;<BR>of high b.<BR>अभिजनवत् (f. ती), Sa iii.<BR>The act of giving birth:<BR>(1) प्रसवः;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रजननम्।<BR>IV That which is born: v.<BR>Creature.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

birth
BIRTH, TO GIVE:<BR>(1) सूते (सू, c. 2.);<BR>(2) जनयति<BR>(c. of जन्): v. To bring forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

birth-day
BIRTH-DAY:<BR>(1) जन्मदिनम्;<BR>(2) जनिदिवसम्, Vi.<BR>vi.; and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

birth-place
BIRTH-PLACE:<BR>(1) जन्मभूमिः;<BR>(2) जन्मस्थानम्;<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

birth-right
BIRTH-RIGHT:<BR>(1) जन्मनः स्वत्वम्<BR>or<BR>अधिकारः;<BR>(2)<BR>by circumlo., sold his b. for a morsel of bread<BR>*अपूपखण्डार्थं पितृसम्पत्त्यादौ सर्वं स्वत्वं व्यक्रीणीत।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

biscuit
BISCUIT: इयुरुपीयपिष्टकविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bisect
BISECT:<BR>(1) द्वैधीकरोति<BR>or<BR>द्विधाकरोति (कृ, c. 8.);<BR>(2) समांशद्वयेन विभजति (भज्, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bisection
BISECTION:<BR>(1) द्विधाकरणम्;<BR>(2) द्वैधीकरणम्;<BR>(3)<BR>समांशद्वयेन विभागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bishop
BISHOP: *कृष्टीयसम्प्रदायेषु प्रधानाचार्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bishopric
BISHOPRIC:<BR>I A bishop's office: प्रधानाचार्य-<BR>पदम्।<BR>II Bishop's district *प्रधानाचार्यस्याधिकारः;<BR>b. of London<BR>*लण्डनस्य प्रधानाचार्यस्याधिकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bismuth
BISMUTH: आलोहितशुक्लधातुप्रभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bison
BISON: एमेरीकादेशीयो महिषाकारोऽरण्यजन्तुविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bissextile
BISSEXTILE: वैषुववत्सरेणैक्यार्थं पाश्चात्यपाण्डिताश्चतुर्थे<BR> चतुर्थे वर्षे फेव्रुवारीमासमेकाधिकदिवसमूनत्रिंशद्दिवसात्मक-<BR>मिति परिगणयन्ति । स च एकाधिकदिवसो वर्षस्तैर<BR>“विसेकष्टाइल्”, “लिप इयार” चाभिधीयते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bit
BIT (subs.):<BR>I Of the bridle:<BR>(1) खलीन<BR>(mn.);<BR>(2) कविकः<BR>or<BR>कविका;<BR>(3) वल्गा।<BR>II<BR>A small piece:<BR>(1) खण्डः;<BR>(2) ग्रासः (=a<BR>mouthful).<BR>Not a b.<BR>न मनागपि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bit
BIT (v. t.);<BR>To b. a horse<BR>अश्वस्य मुखे खलीनं ददाति,<BR>Mu.<BR>or<BR>खलीमं प्रक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.), P. iv. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bitch
BITCH:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) कुक्कुरी;<BR>(2) शुनी;<BR>(3)<BR>सरमा।<BR>II As a term of reproach: बन्धकी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bite
BITE (v. t.):<BR>I With teeth etc.: दशति, वि-,<BR> सं-, (दन्श्, c. l.): Ph.<BR>one should not b. off<BR>one's nails<BR>दन्तैर्नोत्पाटयेन् (c. of पट्) नखान्, M. iv.<BR>69.;<BR>one who b. s his nails<BR>नखखादी, M.;<BR>to<BR>b. the lips<BR>ओष्ठौ दशति<BR>or<BR>खण्डति, वि-, (खण्ड् c. l.),<BR>Si. xvii. 2.,<BR>or<BR>निर्विभुनक्ति (भुज्, c. 7.) (poet)<BR>II To produce a keen, pungent sensation:<BR>ज्वलयति (c. of ज्वल्,)<BR>III To adhere to: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bite
BITE (subs.):<BR>I The act of biting: दंशः;<BR>poisonous b.<BR>सविषो दंशः, U.<BR>II. The wound<BR>made by biting: दंशः।<BR>III A cheat or<BR>one who cheats q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

biting
BITING (adj.): i. e. sharp, severe, sarcastic:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bitter
BITTER (adj.):<BR>I Of the taste: तिक्तः (क्ता, क्तं).<BR>II Harsh, stern:<BR>(1) कटु। (mfn.)<BR>even by<BR>the b. words of Śiśupāla<BR>कटुनापि चैद्यवचनेन। Si.<BR>xv. 40.;<BR>(2) मर्माविध् (mfn.) (Lit. piercing<BR>the vital parts);<BR>(3) निष्ठुरः (रा, रं) (prop=<BR>cruel.),<BR>we are very b. ly reviled<BR>अति निष्ठुरमुपा-<BR>लब्धाः स्मः, U. iv.<BR>III Painful, severe:<BR>q. v.: उद्वेजनकरः (री, रं): Ph.<BR>b. cold<BR>अत्यन्तशीतम्।<BR>IV Mournful, distressing, pitiable: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bitterly
BITTERLY:<BR>I Severly, cruelly: q. v.: निष्ठुरम्।<BR>II Sorrowfully, piteously: q. v.: Ph.<BR>wept<BR>b.<BR>भृशं<BR>or<BR>अत्यन्तं रुरोद।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bittern
BITTERN: क्रौञ्चजातीयपक्षिभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bitterness
BITTERNESS:<BR>I Of taste:<BR>(1) तिक्तता;<BR>(2)<BR>तिक्तत्वम्।<BR>II Keenness of reproach, sarcasm:<BR>(1) कटुता;<BR>(2) निष्ठुरता।<BR>III Deep distress<BR>of mind: दुःखम्।<BR>IV Impious feeling: पाषण्ड-<BR>बुद्धिः। v. Malice, hatred: q. v.: विद्वेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bitumen
BITUMEN:<BR>(1) शिलाजतु (n.);<BR>(2) गिरिपुष्पकम्;<BR>(3)<BR>शिलादद्रुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bituminous
BITUMINOUS: शिलाजतुशालिन् (f. नी) (?) (=con-<BR>-taining bitumen).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bivouac
BIVOUAC (sub.); v. Watch, guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bivouac
BIVOUAC (v.): Ph. “determined to b. there for<BR>the night” अप्रमत्तास्तत्रैव यामिनीं यापयितुं कृतसंकल्पाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blab
BLAB, BLABBER: वावदूकः: v. Babbler, tell-tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blab
BLAB (v. t.): भिनत्ति (भिद्, c. 7.): v. To<BR>divulge: v. Also, to babble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

black
BLACK (adj.):<BR>I Of colour:<BR>(1) कृष्णः (ष्णा,<BR> ष्णं);<BR>(2) कृष्णवर्णः (र्णा, र्णं);<BR>(3) श्यामः (मा,<BR> मं)<BR>or<BR>श्यामलः (ला, लं) (=dark blue);<BR>(4)<BR>नीलः (ला, लं) (prop. = blue);<BR>(5) कालः (ला,<BR> लं);<BR>(6) मेचकः (का, कं);<BR>(7) मलिनः (ना, नं);<BR>your heart must be very b. like your exterior<BR>बहिरिव मलिनतरं तव मनोऽपि भविष्यति नूनम्, Gi.<BR>viii. 7.<BR>II Fig., dismal, gloomy, calami-<BR>-tious, horrible, wicked: q. v. B. and blue:<BR>v. Livid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

black
BLACK (subs.):<BR>I The colour:<BR>(1) कृष्णः;<BR>(2) कृष्णवर्णः।<BR>III Black dress:<BR>(1) कृष्णवस्त्रम्,<BR>(2) कृष्णवसनम्।<BR>III A black man:<BR>(1)<BR>कृष्णकायः (या, यं);<BR>(2) श्यामाङ्गः (ङ्गी, ङ्गं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

black-art
BLACK-ART:<BR>(1) इन्द्रजालम्;<BR>(2) कार्मणम्: v.<BR>Magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

black-ball
BLACK-BALL (subs.): (प्रत्याख्यानप्रदर्शनी) कृष्ण-<BR>गुटिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

black-ball
BLACK-BALL (v. t.): प्रत्याख्याति (ख्या, c. 2.): v.<BR>To reject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

black-berry
BLACK-BERRY: फलविशेषः। In India, some-<BR>-times applied to जम्बु (n.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

black-bird
BLACK-BIRD: पक्षिभेदः। In India, the term is<BR>applied to कोकिलः। (=Cuckoo).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

black-cattle
BLACK-CATTLE: मांसार्थं पालिता गावः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blacken
BLACKEN:<BR>I To make black:<BR>(1) कालीकरोति,<BR>b. s his face<BR>मुखं कालीकरोति, Na. iii.;<BR>(2)<BR>कृष्णीकरोति (rare);<BR>(3) श्यामीकरोति (=to make<BR>dark blue).<BR>II To darken: q. v.<BR>III To<BR>sully: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blackguard
BLACKGUARD:<BR>(1) दुर्वृत्तः (त्ता, त्तं);<BR>(2) दुराचारः<BR>(रा, रं): v. Rake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blacking
BLACKING (subs.): काली (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blackish
BLACKISH:<BR>(1) ईषत्कृष्णः (ष्णा, ष्णं). ईषत्कालः<BR>(ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

black-lead
BLACK-LEAD: लोहभेदः; *अङ्गारलोहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blackness
BLACKNESS:<BR>(1) कालिमन् (m.);<BR>(2) कृष्णत्वम्;<BR>(3) कृष्णिमन् (m.): v. Also, darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blacksmith
BLACKSMITH:<BR>(1) कर्मकारः;<BR>(2) कर्मारः;<BR>(3)<BR>लोहकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bladder
BLADDER:<BR>(1) क्लोमन् (m.);<BR>(2) मूत्राशयः;<BR>(3)<BR>तिलकम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blade
BLADE:<BR>I The cutting part of a knife etc.;<BR>धारा।<BR>II Of grass:<BR>(1) दल (mn.);<BR>(2) काण्डम्<BR>(?).<BR>III A rake: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blade-bone
BLADE-BONE: v. Shoulder-bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blamable or blameable
BLAMABLE or BLAMEABLE:<BR>(1) निन्दनीयः (या,<BR> यं);<BR>(2) निन्द्यः (न्द्या, न्द्यं);<BR>(3) निन्दार्हः (र्हा,<BR> र्हं): v. Faulty, culpable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blamableness
BLAMABLENESS or BLAMEABLENESS: निन्द्यताः<BR>v. Culpability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blame
BLAME (subs.):<BR>I Censure, reprehension:<BR>q. v.: निन्दा।<BR>II Fault, crime दोषः,<BR>he lays<BR>the b. on another's shoulders<BR>अन्यस्मिन्<BR>or<BR>अन्यस्य<BR> स्कन्धे स दोषं न्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.). Without b. =<BR>blameless: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blame
BLAME (v. t.): निन्दति, वि-, (निन्द्, c. l.): v.<BR>To censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blameless
BLAMELESS:<BR>(1) अनिन्द्यः (न्द्या, न्द्यं);<BR>(2) अनिन्दनीयः<BR>(या, यं);<BR>(3) निर्दोषः (षा, षं) (=faultless:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(4) निष्कलङ्कः (ङ्का, ङ्कं) (=spotless:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(5) विशुद्धः (द्धा, द्धं) (pure: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blamelessly
BLAMELESSLY: v. Innocently, faultlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blamelessness
BLAMELESSNESS:<BR>(1) अनिन्द्यता;<BR>(2) निर्दोषता<BR>(=faultlessness);<BR>(3) विशुद्धता (= purity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blameworthy
BLAMEWORTHY:<BR>(1) निन्दार्हः (र्हा, र्हं);<BR>(2)<BR>निन्दनीयः (या, यं): v. Censurable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blamer
BLAMER: निन्दकः: v. Censurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blanch
BLANCH (v.);<BR>I To whiten: q. v.: धवलयति<BR>(nomi.).<BR>II To peel: q. v. त्वचयति (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bland
BLAND: मृदु (द्वी, दु): Mild, gentle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blandishment
BLANDISHMENT:<BR>I Of love:<BR>(1) हावः;<BR>(2)<BR>विलासः;<BR>(3) विभ्रमः। N. B. Applied only to<BR>women.<BR>II Sweet words:<BR>(1) प्रियवाक्यम्;<BR>(2) मधुरभाषितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blank
BLANK (adj.):<BR>I Not filled or written on:<BR>शुद्धः (द्धा, द्धं) (?).<BR>II White pale or dis-<BR>-mayed: q. v.: Ph.<BR>b. verse:<BR>अमित्राक्षरछन्दः;<BR>b. cartridge<BR>*केवलचूर्णकोषः;<BR>b. endorsement<BR>लेखक।<BR> -नामविरहितं हुण्ड्यादौ पृष्ठलिखनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blank
BLANK (subs.):<BR>I A void space: Ph.<BR>don't<BR>leave so much b.<BR>एतावदलिखितं<BR>or<BR>शुद्धं (?) मा<BR> रक्षीः:<BR>II A b. ticket *शुद्धनिदर्शनी।<BR>III A<BR>b. ballot *शुद्धगुटिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blanket
BLANKET:<BR>(1) कम्बलः;<BR>(2) रल्लकः;<BR>(3) ऊर्णायुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blaspheme
BLASPHEME: निन्दति (निन्द्, c. l.): v. To<BR>revile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blasphemer
BLASPHEMER:<BR>(1) ईश्वरनिन्दकः;<BR>(2) पाषण्डः<BR>(=heretic).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blasphemous
BLASPHEMOUS:<BR>(1) ईश्वरनिन्दकः (का, कं);<BR>(2)<BR>comp. with पाषण्ड-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blasphemously
BLASPHEMOUSLY:<BR>(1) अभवत्या (=irreligiously);<BR>(2) अवज्ञया (=contemptuously).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blasphemy
BLASPHEMY:<BR>(1) ईश्वरनिन्दा;<BR>(2) पाषण्डता<BR>(=heresy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blast
BLAST (subs.):<BR>I A gust of wind:<BR>(1) वात्या;<BR>(2) जवानिलः: v. Gale.<BR>II The blowing of<BR>a wind instrument: v. Blowing.<BR>III A<BR>blight: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blast
BLAST (v. t.):<BR>I To blight: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>destroy, frustrate: q. v. उन्मूलयति (मूल्, c. 10.).<BR>III To rend open by explosion; विदारयति<BR>(c. of द) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blaze
BLAZE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्रभा;<BR>(2) अर्चिस<BR>(m.): v. Flame, light.<BR>II Fig.: Ph.:<BR>“b. of fame” यशःप्रभा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blaze
BLAZE (v. i.):<BR>(1) (ज्वलति, प्र-, सम्प्र-, (ज्वल्, c. l.),<BR>b. ing powers<BR>ज्वलत्प्रतापावलिः; N. i. 2.;<BR>(2)<BR>दीप्यते, प्र-, सं-, (दीप्, c. 4.)<BR>the Raghu-chief b. ed<BR>with rage<BR>कुद्धोऽदीपि रघुव्याघ्रः, B. vi. 32.: v.<BR>To kindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blazon
BLAZON (v. t.):<BR>I To display: q. v.: प्रथयति<BR>(c. of प्रथ्).<BR>III To deck, embellish: q. v.:<BR>मण्डयति<BR>III To explain coat of arms<BR>व्याख्याति (ख्या, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blazon
BLAZON, BLAZONRY (subs.):<BR>I A coat of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">Page075</a>]<BR>arms: q. v.<BR>II Publication, display:<BR>q. v.: आडम्भरः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bleach
BLEACH:<BR>I To whiten: q. v.: धवलयति (nomi.)<BR>II To make pale: विवर्णयति (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bleaching-powder
BLEACHING-POWDER: *विरञ्जकचूर्णम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bleak
BLEAK (adj.):<BR>I Bold, frigid: q. v.: अतिशीतः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR>II Exposed to cold: expr. by<BR>circum.:<BR>these wastes are so b.<BR>*एषु खिलप्रदेशेषु<BR> हिमस्येदृक् प्रादुर्भावः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bleak
BLEAK (subs.): नादेयः शुक्लवर्णः क्षुद्रमत्स्यभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bleakness
BLEAKNESS:<BR>I Exposure to the wind: by<BR>circum.: v. Bleak (II).<BR>II Coldness:<BR>q. v.: शीतता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blearedness
BLEAREDNESS:<BR>(1) क्लिन्नाक्षता;<BR>(2) चुल्लता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blear-eyed
BLEAR-EYED:<BR>(1) क्लिन्नाक्षः (क्षी, क्षं);<BR>(2) चुल्लः<BR>or<BR>चिल्लः (ल्ला, ल्लं);<BR>(3) पिल्लः, (ल्ला, ल्लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bleat
BLEAT (v. i.): रेभते (रेभ्, c. l): v. To make<BR>noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bleat
BLEAT, BLEATING (subs.):<BR>(1) रावः<BR>or<BR>रेमणम्:<BR>v. Noise.<BR>(2) मेषरुतम् (the cry of a<BR>sheep).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bleed
BLEED (v. t.): रक्तं<BR>or<BR>रुधिरं<BR>or<BR>शौणितं स्रावयति, वि-,<BR> आ-, परि-, (c. of स्त्र);<BR>or<BR>मोक्षयति (मुक्ष्,<BR>c. 10);<BR>or<BR>मोचयति (c. of मुच्)<BR>or<BR>अवसेचयति (c. of<BR>सिच्). N. B. These verbs are cons. with gen.<BR>of the person who is bled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bleed
BLEED (v. i.): रक्तं<BR>or<BR>रुधिरं<BR>or<BR>शोणितं स्रवति (स्रु,<BR>c. l);<BR>or<BR>च्यवते (च्यु, c. l), Ki.;<BR>or<BR>क्षरति<BR>(क्षर्, c. l). M. n.;<BR>or<BR>गच्छति (गम्, c. l)<BR>(rare),<BR>when it stops itself after sufficient b.<BR>ing<BR>सम्यग् गत्वा यदा रक्तं स्वयमेवावतिष्ठते, Śr.; or<BR>प्रवर्तते (वृत्, c. l) (rare),<BR>if it does not b.<BR>अप्र-<BR>वर्तमाने रक्ते। N. B. These verbs are cons.<BR>with gen. of the person and abl. of the<BR>part which b. s:<BR>his hand b. s<BR>तस्य हस्तात्<BR> शोणितं स्रवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bleeding
BLEEDING (subs.):<BR>I Letting of blood;<BR>(1)<BR>रक्तस्रावः, -णं;<BR>(2) रक्तमोक्षणम्;<BR>(3) रक्तावसेचनम्,<BR>etc.<BR>II Flowing of blood:<BR>(1) रक्तस्रु तिः;<BR>(2) रक्तच्युतिः;<BR>(3) रक्तक्षरणम् etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blemish
BLEMISH (v. t.):<BR>(1) मलिनयति (nomi.);<BR>(2)<BR>दूषयति (c. of दुष्): v. To stain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blemish
BLEMISH (subs.): दोषः: v. Stain, defect, fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blend
BLEND, BLENDING: v. To mingle, mingling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bless
BLESS (v. t.):<BR>I To pronounce a blessing<BR>on:<BR>(1) often by sim. आशीर्लिङ्<BR>or<BR>लोट् when<BR>any particular blessing is specified,<BR>I b.<BR>you that you may have a son like yourself,<BR>पुत्रं लभस्वात्मगुणानुरूपम्, R. v. 34.;<BR>(2) आषिशं<BR> ददाति (दा, c. 3)<BR>or<BR>प्रयुनक्ति (युज्, c. 7) (with<BR>dat.), R. v. 35.<BR>(3) आशास्ते (शास्, c. 2),<BR>I b. you by the Rig Veda<BR>ऋक्छन्दसाशासे, Sa.<BR>iv.;<BR>(4) आशंसते (शंस्, c. l) (rare), M. n.:<BR>Ph.<BR>God b. you<BR>ईशस्ते कल्याणं<BR>or<BR>शुभं वितरतु।<BR>II<BR>To glorify or praise: q. v.: Ph.<BR>b. the<BR>Lord, b. his holy name<BR>*ईशो गीयतां, तस्य पवित्रं<BR> नाम गीयताम्।<BR>III To consecrate: q. v.<BR>IV<BR>To favour, endow liberally: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blessed
BLESSED:<BR>I Happy, highly favoured:<BR>(1)<BR>धन्यः (न्या, न्यं), Si. xiv. 87.;<BR>(2) महा-<BR>भाग्यवत् (f. ती), Vi.<BR>II Enjoying heavenly<BR>felicity: लब्धमोक्षः (क्षा, क्षं);<BR>(3) सिद्धः (द्धा, द्धं).<BR>Ph.<BR>b. foot<BR>श्रीचरणकमलम्;<BR>b. shore<BR>श्रीमत्कूलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blessedness
BLESSEDNESS: v. Happiness, felicity. “In<BR>single b.” अनुद्वाहसुखेन (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blessing
BLESSING:<BR>I A benediction:<BR>(1) आशिस् (f.);<BR>(2) आशीर्वादः;<BR>(3) आशीर्वचनम्।<BR>II A gift,<BR>benefit, or advantage: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blight
BLIGHT (v. t.):<BR>(1) उत्सादयति (c. of सद्) (=to<BR>destroy);<BR>(2) वृद्धिं स्तभ्नाति (स्तम्भ्। c. 9)<BR>(=stop the growth) (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blight
BLIGHT (subs.):<BR>(1) उपद्रवः (?);<BR>(2) व्याघातः (?);<BR>(3) क्षयः (=decay).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blind
BLIND (adj.): अन्धः, (न्धा, न्धं),<BR>born b.<BR>जन्मान्धः<BR>(न्धा, न्धं)<BR>or<BR>जात्यन्धः (न्धा, न्धं) (rare)<BR>M.;<BR>(2) अन्धदृश् (mfn.) and sim. comp. s.,<BR>naturally b. to their own improprieties<BR>सहजान्ध-<BR>दृशः स्वदुर्नये, Si. xvi. 29. Ph b. of one eye<BR>काणः (णा, णं);<BR>b. at night<BR>रात्र्यन्धः (न्धा, न्धं);<BR>a b. well<BR>अन्धकूपः, Va.;<BR>love is b.<BR>*प्रेम भद्रं न<BR> पश्यति<BR>or<BR>गणयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blind
BLIND (v.): अन्धयति (nomi.)<BR>or<BR>अन्धीकरोति (कृ<BR>c. 8),<BR>b. ed by sensual pleasures<BR>विषयान्धीकृतेक्षणः,<BR>Ka. Ph.<BR>b. ed by passion<BR>कामान्धः (न्धा, न्धं)<BR>b. ed by rage<BR>क्रोन्धान्धः (न्धा, न्धं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blind
BLIND (subs.): तिरस्करिणीः v. Screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blindfold
BLINDFOLD (v. t.): नेत्रे<BR>or<BR>लोचने<BR>or<BR>दृशौ बध्नाति<BR>(बन्ध्, c. 9)<BR>or<BR>अभिनह्यति (नह्, c. 4).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blindfolded
BLINDFOLDED (adj.):<BR>(1) बद्धचक्षुस् (mfn.),<BR>S. c.;<BR>(2) अभिनद्धाक्षः (f. क्षी). Up. Fig.<BR>“fate's b. reign” *देवस्य तिमिरावृतमाधिपत्यम्: v.<BR>Also blindly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blindly
BLINDLY:<BR>(1) अन्धवत्;<BR>(2) असमीक्ष्य (=inconsi-<BR>-derately);<BR>(3) सहसा (=suddenly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blindmans buff
BLINDMAN'S BUFF: नेत्रबन्धः, -क्रीडा, B. p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blindness
BLINDNESS:<BR>I Lit.<BR>(1) अन्धता;<BR>(2) अन्धत्बम्<BR>II<BR>Fig.: मोहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bilnk
BILNK: v. To wink, twinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bliss
BLISS: परमसुखम् v. Happiness, felicity, beati-<BR>-tude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blissful
BLISSFUL: आनन्दमयः (यी, यं): v. Happy,<BR>blessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blister
BLISTER (subs.):<BR>I A watery tumour: जल-<BR>पूर्णं व्रणम् (?).<BR>A b. on the foot:<BR>विपादिका।<BR>II A<BR>plaster for raising b. s: *दाहालेपः, जलपूर्ण-<BR>व्रणोत्पादकालेपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blister
BLISTER (v. t.):<BR>I To apply a blister: *दाहा-<BR>लेपं प्रयुनक्ति (युज्, c. 7.).<BR>II To raise blisters:<BR>जलपूर्णानि व्रणानि उत्थापयति (c. of स्था) (?).<BR>III<BR>Fig. v. To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blister
BLISTER (v. i.): Ph, “let my tongue b.” *मम<BR> जिह्वायां जलपूर्णनि व्रणानि भवन्तु।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blithe
BLITHE, BLITHESOME: v. Cheerful, gay,<BR>merry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blithely
BLITHELY:<BR>(1) सहर्षम्;<BR>(2) सोल्लासम्: v. Cheerfully,<BR>merrily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blitheness
BLITHENESS:<BR>(1) स्फूर्तिः;<BR>(2) उल्लासः: v. Cheerful-<BR>-ness, sprightliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bloat
BLOAT: v. To swell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bloated
BLOATED (adj.):<BR>(1) स्फीतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) शूनः<BR>(ना, नं);<BR>(3) स्फातः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

block
BLOCK (subs.):<BR>I Of wood: काष्ठम्।<BR>II Of<BR>stone: शिला।<BR>III For beheading criminals:<BR>वध्यकाष्ठम् (after वध्यशिला, of Na.). Ph.<BR>whose<BR>heads were brought to the b.<BR>येषां शिरांसि वध्यकाष्ठं<BR> स्पर्शितानि or sim. छिन्नानि।<BR>IV Any mass:<BR>पिण्ड (mn.). V. A row: q. v.: श्रेणी।<BR>VI<BR>Any obstruction or hindrance: q. v.<BR>VII<BR>A blockhead: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

block up
BLOCK UP:<BR>(1) रुणद्धि, अव-, नि-, सं-, उप-, प्रति-,<BR>(रुध्, c. 7.)<BR>b. ing up the path<BR>मार्गमवरुध्य Mah.;<BR>(2) आवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.), b. ing up the road<BR>आवृत्य पन्थानम्, R. vii. 31.<BR>(3) आच्छादयति<BR>(c. of छद्) (rare),<BR>b. ing up the way of the<BR>chariot<BR>आच्छाद्य रथपन्थानम्, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blockade
BLOCKADE (subs.):<BR>(1) रोधः;<BR>(2) अवरोधः;<BR>(3)<BR>उपरोधः;<BR>(4) संरोधः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blockade
BLOCKADE (v. t.):<BR>(1) रुणद्धि, अव-, उप-, (रुध्,<BR>c. 7.);<BR>(2) परिवेष्टते (बेष्ट्, c. l.) (=to surround:<BR>q. v.) (to be used only when the context<BR>determines the meaning).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blockader
BLOCKADER: अवरोद्धा: v. Besieger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blockhead
BLOCKHEAD:<BR>(1) स्थूलबुद्धिः;<BR>(2) वर्वरः: v. Fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blood
BLOOD:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) रक्तम्;<BR>(2) रुधिरम्;<BR>(3)<BR>शोणितम्;<BR>(4) असृज् (n.);<BR>(5) अस्रम्;<BR>(6) क्षतजम्<BR>(rare),<BR>the cascade of fresh b;<BR>प्रत्यग्रक्षतजभरी,<BR>Vi. vii.<BR>(7) कीलालम् (rare),<BR>quenched by b.<BR>flowing<BR>सरत्कीलालनिर्वापित, Vi. iii. Ph.:<BR>to lose<BR>b.<BR>रक्तं मुञ्चति (भुच्, c. 6.);<BR>to take one's b.<BR>हन्ति<BR>(हन्, c. 2.) v. To murder.<BR>II Kindred, line-<BR>-age: q. v.: Ph.<BR>related by b.<BR>सनाभि (mfn.);<BR>of<BR>whole b.<BR>सोदरः (रा, रं); half-b. q. v.<BR>III Blood-<BR>-shed: q. v.<BR>IV Temper of mind, passion:<BR>Ph.<BR>their b. was up for revenge<BR>*प्रतीकारार्थं तेषां<BR> क्रोधाग्निरुद्दिदीपे;<BR>do not rouse my b.<BR>मा मां प्रकोपय;<BR>murdered the child in cold b.<BR>*शान्तो बालं जघान।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blood
BLOOD (v. t.):<BR>I To bleed: q. v.<BR>II To stain<BR>with blood: रुधिरेण लिम्पति (v. To. annoint)<BR>or<BR>कलुषयति (v. To stain): Ph.<BR>b. ed scimi-<BR>tars<BR>खङ्गाः शोणितसन्दिग्धाः, Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blood-hound
BLOOD-HOUND: कुक्कुरभेदः: v. Hound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bloodiness
BLOODINESS: जिघांसा: v. Cruelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bloodless
BLOODLESS:<BR>I Without blood:<BR>(1) रक्तहीनः<BR>(ना, नं) (?);<BR>(2) गतासु (mfn.) (=dead).<BR>II<BR>Without shedding of blood: रक्तपातं विना<BR>Ph. by which the discharger obtains a b. victory<BR>यतः प्रयोक्तुर्न चारिहिंसा विजयश्च हस्ते, R. v. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blood-let
BLOOD-LET: (v.): v. To bleed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blood-red
BLOOD-RED: रक्तः (क्ता, क्तं): v. Red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blood-shed
BLOOD-SHED: रक्तपातः: v. Slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blood-shot
BLOOD-SHOT:<BR>(1) अतिरक्तः (क्ता, क्तं) (=very<BR>red);<BR>(2) रक्ताभिष्यन्दिन् (f. नी) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blood-stained
BLOOD-STAINED:<BR>(1) रक्ताक्तः (क्ता, क्तं);<BR>(2) रुधिर-<BR>संलिप्तः (प्ता, प्तं);<BR>(3) शोणितसन्दिग्धः (ग्धा, ग्धं);<BR>(4) अस्रदिग्धः (ग्धा, ग्धं), R.; and sim. comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blood-sucker
BLOOD-SUCKER:<BR>(1) रक्तपायिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>अस्रपः (पा, पं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blood-thirsty
BLOOD-THIRSTY:<BR>(1) रुधिरप्रियः (या, यं);<BR>(2)<BR>जिघांसु (mfn.): v. Sanguinary, murderous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blood-vessel
BLOOD-VESSEL रक्तवाहिनी<BR>or<BR>असृग्वहा नाडी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bloody
BLOODY:<BR>I Blood-stained: q. v.<BR>II Sangui-<BR>-nary, murderous: q. v.<BR>III Attended with<BR>blood-shed: Ph.<BR>it was a b. battle<BR>अस्मिन् युद्धे<BR> बहु रक्तं पपात (?);<BR>that day was most b. for the<BR>Romans<BR>*तस्मिन् दिवसे रुमीयाणां बंहिष्ठं रक्तं पपात।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bloom
BLOOM (subs.):<BR>I Blossom: q. v.<BR>II Fig.,<BR>the b. of youth<BR>नवयौवनम्; the b. (of a maiden's)<BR>cheek<BR>कपोलरागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bloom
BLOOM (v. i.): v. To blossom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blooming
BLOOMING, BLOSSOMING (adj.):<BR>(1) प्रफुल्लः (ल्ला,<BR> ल्लं),<BR>b. face<BR>प्रफुल्लवदनम्;<BR>(2) विकसत् (f. न्ती);<BR>(3) स्फुटत् (f. न्ती);<BR>(4) कुसुमितः (ता, तं);<BR>(5)<BR>पुष्पितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blossom
BLOSSOM (v. i.):<BR>(1) स्फुटति (स्फुट्, c. 6);<BR>(2)<BR>फुल्लति (फुल्ल्, c. l);<BR>(3) विकसति (कस्, c. l);<BR>(4) पुष्पति (पुष्प्, c. 4) (rare): v. To flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blossom
BLOSSOM (subs.):<BR>(1) पुष्पम् (=flower: q. v.);<BR>(2)<BR>मुकुल (mn.) (=an opening bud.);<BR>(3) प्रसवः<BR>(rare),<BR>mango b. s<BR>चूतप्रसवः, Ku.;<BR>(4) प्रवालः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blot
BLOT (subs.): कलङ्कः: v. Spot. stain, tarnish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blot out
BLOT OUT: v. To erase, efface, obliterate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blotch
BLOTCH:<BR>(1) किलासम् (?);<BR>(2) कच्छपिका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blotting-paper
BLOTTING-PAPER: *मसीशोषकं कागजम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blow
BLOW (subs.):<BR>I With the fist:<BR>(1) मुष्टि-<BR>प्रहारः,<BR>gives a b. on the nose<BR>धोणायां मुष्टिप्रहारं<BR> ददाति, Mr. ii.<BR>(2) मुष्टिघातः;<BR>(3) भुजाहतिः, Ki.<BR>To strike a b.:<BR>मुष्टिना हन्ति (हन्, c. 2.) or<BR>ताडयति (तड्, c. 10.).<BR>II. B. in general: प्रहारः:<BR>v. Stroke.<BR>III Fig. Infliction of evil: Ph.<BR>“gave a death-b. to the constitution” *शासनप्रणाल्या<BR> विनाशं कल्पयामास; “fortune's b. s” दैवनिर्धातः, U.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blow
BLOW (v. i.):<BR>I To blossom: q. v.: स्फुटति,<BR> प्र-, (स्फुट्, c. 6.).<BR>II As air:<BR>(1) वाति, प्र-<BR>(वा, c. 2.);<BR>(2) वहति, प्र-, (वह्, c. l.), Ku.<BR>xvii. 26.<BR>III To breathe hard or quick.:<BR>v. To breathe, to part.<BR>IV To sound as a<BR>wind instrument: Ph.<BR>horns blew<BR>पूर्णाः पेराश्च<BR> सस्वनुः: B.: v. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blow
BLOW (v. t.):<BR>I To b. the fire: धमति, सभा-,<BR> प्र-, उप-, (ध्मा, c. l.) M. iv. 53.<BR>II To drive,<BR>to impel: q. v.: Ph.<BR>the tempest blew the<BR>ship ashore<BR>*वात्या पोतं विचिक्षेप (क्षिप्, c. 6.)<BR>तटे;<BR>dust b. n by the wind<BR>अनिलोद्धतं (धू, c. 9.)<BR>or<BR>अनिलोत्थापितं (c. of स्था) रजः।<BR>III To<BR>sound a wind instrument:<BR>(1) धमति, सभा-,<BR>blew the shell<BR>जलजं दध्मौ R.;<BR>(2) पूरयति or<BR>मुखमारुतेन पूरयति (पूर्, c. 10.),<BR>blew horns<BR>काहलाः<BR> पूरयाञ्चक्रुः, B. xiv. 3.<BR>IV To spread, pub-<BR>-lish: q. v.: Ph.:<BR>to b. the nose<BR>नासिकां धमति;<BR>one who does so<BR>नासिकन्धमः।<BR>To b. hot and<BR>cold:<BR>अनुग्रहनिग्रहौ प्रकटयति (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blow away
BLOW AWAY: वि-धूनोति<BR>or<BR>धूनयति<BR>or<BR>धूनाति (धू,<BR>c. 5., 10. &. 9.): v. To drive away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blow into
BLOW INTO: फूत्करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blow out
BLOW OUT: निर्वापयति (c. of वा): Ph.<BR>if you<BR>allow me, I will b. the dust from your eye<BR>यद्यनु-<BR>मन्यसे तदहमेनां वदनमारुतेन विशदां करवाणि, Sa. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blow over
BLOW OVER: शाम्यति, प्र-, उप-, (शम्, c. 4): v.<BR>To cease, pass away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blow up
BLOW UP:<BR>I To swell, inflate: q. v.<BR>II By<BR>explosion: no equiv.: उद्धूनयति (धू, c. 10)<BR>may be used.<BR>III To destroy: उन्मूलयति<BR>(मूल्, c. 10).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blow upon
BLOW UPON: v. To destroy, to taint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blower
BLOWER:<BR>(1) धमकः;<BR>(2) ध्माता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blowing
BLOWING (subs.):<BR>I Of a wind instrument:<BR>(1) ध्मातम् (rare):<BR>(2) नादः: v. sound:<BR>II<BR>Of a flower, etc.:<BR>(1) विकाशः;<BR>(2) फुल्लिः।<BR>In other senses, v. To blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blow-pipe
BLOW-PIPE: धमनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blubber
BLUBBER (subs.): तिम्यादियादसां मेदस् (n.): v.<BR>Fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blubber
BLUBBER (v. i.): v. To weep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bludgeon
BLUDGEON: लगुडः: v. Club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blue
BLUE (adj.):<BR>(1) नीलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) श्यामः<BR>(मा, मं) (=dark b.); असितः (ता, तं) (poet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blue
BLUE (subs.):<BR>(1) नीलः;<BR>(2) नीलवर्णः। B. s.;<BR>i. e. low spirits: v. Melancholy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blue-bird
BLUE-BIRD: *नीलपक्षी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blue-bottle
BLUE-BOTTLE: लताभेदः; मक्षिकाभेदश्च।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blue-eyed
BLUE-EYED: नीलाक्षः (क्षी, क्षं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bluff
BLUFF (adj.): v. Uncouth, steep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bluish
BLUISH:<BR>(1) आनीलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) ईषन्नीलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blunder
BLUNDER (v. i.): प्रमाद्यति (मद्, c. 4): v. To<BR>err, mistake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blunder
BLUNDER (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रमादः;<BR>(2) स्खलितम्;<BR>(3)<BR>भ्रमः: v. Mistake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blunderbuss
BLUNDERBUSS: *आयतच्छिद्रविशिष्टः क्षुद्रबन्दुकविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blunderer
BLUNDERER:<BR>(1) प्रमादिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) प्रमत्तः<BR>(त्ता, त्तं);<BR>(3) भ्रान्तचित्तः (त्ता, त्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blundering
BLUNDERING (adj.):<BR>(1) प्रमत्तः (त्ता, त्तं);<BR>(2)<BR>भ्रान्तः (न्ता, न्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blunderingly
BLUNDERINGLY:<BR>(1) प्रमादेन<BR>(2) by the adj.<BR>he<BR>talks b.<BR>प्रमत्तः प्रलपति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blunt
BLUNT (adj.):<BR>I Not sharp:<BR>(1) निस्तेजस्<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(2) कुण्ठः (ष्ठा, ण्ठं);<BR>(3) कुण्ठितः (ता,<BR> तं);<BR>(4) प्रखरः (रा, रं).<BR>To become b.:<BR>कुण्ठी-<BR>भवति।<BR>II Fig. Of understanding, etc.:<BR>(1)<BR>स्थूलः (ला, लं)<BR>(2) निस्तेजस् (mfn.).<BR>III Plain<BR>but unceremonious: सरलः (ला, लं) or<BR>अजिह्मः (ह्मा, ह्मं), (किन्तु) अविनीतः (ता, तं)<BR>or<BR>अशिष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं):<BR>by his b. remarks<BR>*तस्य<BR> सरलाभिरविनीनाभिरुक्तिमिः;<BR>be frank not b.<BR>सरलो<BR> भव नाविनीतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blunt
BLUNT (v. t.):<BR>(1) कुण्ठीकरोति (कृ, c. 8);<BR>(2)<BR>निस्तेजयति (तिज्, c. 10);<BR>(3) तैक्ष्ण्यं<BR>or<BR>प्राखर्यं<BR> नाशयति (c. of नश्)<BR>or<BR>लुम्पति (लुप्, c. 6) (with<BR>gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bluntly
BLUNTLY: Frankly, rudely, plainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bluntness
BLUNTNESS: Of manners: सहजाविनीतता (?);<BR>ग्राम्यता (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blur
BLUR (subs.): v. Smear, blot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blur
BLUR (v.): v. To smear, stain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blush
BLUSH (v. i.):<BR>(1) लज्जां नाटयति (नट्, c. 10),<BR>Mālavikā b. s<BR>मालविका लज्जां नाटयति, Mal. iii.<BR>(2) जिह्रे ति (ह्री, c. 3)<BR>putting the sun to b. in<BR>splendour<BR>ह्रेपयन्नहिमतेजसं त्विषा, Ki xiii. 41.<BR>N. B. Redness of the face is not used to<BR>indicate b. ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blush
BLUSH (subs.):<BR>I A rosy tint: रक्तिमन् (m.)<BR>II A red colour suffusing the cheeks or<BR>face: expr. by<BR>(1) लज्जा,<BR>(2) व्रीडा or<BR>(3) ह्रीः<BR>(=shame):<BR>a b. came upon her face<BR>तस्यानन-<BR>मालोहितं बभूव or, as gen. represented in<BR>Sanskrit व्रीडयाधोमुखी बभूव।<BR>III Glance, view:<BR>q. v. Ph.<BR>at the first b.<BR>प्रथमदर्शने।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blushing
BLUSHING (adj.): प्रफुल्लः (ल्ला, ल्लं): v. Ruddy,<BR>also blushful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blushful
BLUSHFUL:<BR>(1) लज्जावनम्रः (म्रा, म्रं);<BR>(2) ह्रीपरि-<BR>गतः (ता, तं);<BR>(3) व्रीडावनतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bluster
BLUSTER (v. i.): To be boisterous: व्थाक्रोशति<BR>(क्रुश्, c. l.).<BR>II To brag: q. v.<BR>III To<BR>bully: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bluster
BLUSTER (subs.): v. Noise, tumult, boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

blusterer
BLUSTERER: v. Boaster, swaggerer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boa-constrictor
BOA-CONSTRICTOR (a serpent):<BR>(1) अजगरः;<BR>(2) वाहसः;<BR>(3) शयुः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boar
BOAR:<BR>(1) वराहः;<BR>(2) शूकरः;<BR>(3) कोलः;<BR>(4)<BR>पोत्री, A.;<BR>(5) धृष्टिः, A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

board
BOARD (subs.):<BR>I A plank: फलक (mn.).<BR>II<BR>A table for food: भोजनफलकः।<BR>III Food,<BR>diet: q. v.: आहारः: Ph.<BR>but b. and clothing<BR>should be given<BR>ग्रासाच्छादनन्तु देयमेव, K. b.<BR>IV<BR>For playing games:<BR>(1) अष्टापदम्,<BR>(2) शारिफलम्।<BR>V. A council: सभा। A member of it: सभ्यः<BR>or<BR>सभासद् (m.) Ph.<BR>to get on b. a vessel<BR>नाव-<BR>मारोहति (रुह्, c. l.), Raj.; to leap over b. v.<BR>Overboard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

board
BOARD (v. t.):<BR>I To cover with b. s: फलकैः<BR> आच्छादयति (c. of छद्,)<BR>or<BR>आवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.).<BR>II To enter a ship by force: बलात् (नावं)<BR>आरोहति (रुह्, c. l).<BR>III To furnish with<BR>food: अर्थं गृहीत्वा) भोजयति (c. of भुज्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

board
BOARD (v. i.): (अर्थं दत्वा) (परगृहे) अत्ति (अद्, c.<BR>2.)<BR>or<BR>अभ्यवहरति (हृ, c. l.):<BR>I<BR>b. here with<BR>my master<BR>*अत्रोपाध्यायेन सह भोजनं करोमि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boarder
BOARDER: expr. by the verb: v. Board<BR>(v. i.) and (v. t.) (III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boarding-school
BOARDING-SCHOOL: यस्मिन् विद्यालये छात्रा वासं<BR> भोजनञ्चाधिगच्छन्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boast
BOAST (v. i.):<BR>(1) कत्यते, वि-, (कत्थ्, c. l.),<BR>you<BR>b. for nothing<BR>त्वं कत्थसे मूधा, A. r.:<BR>(2) दृप्यति<BR>(दृप्, c. 4.),<BR>he does not b. himself<BR>स नात्मना<BR> दृप्यति, U. vi.:<BR>(3) आत्मानं (one's self) or [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">Page079</a>]<BR>आत्मचरितं<BR>or<BR>आत्मकर्म (one's acts) श्लाघते<BR>(श्लाघ्, c. l), why are you so b. ing of your acts<BR>किमेवमात्मकर्म श्लाघसे, Ve. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boast
BOAST (subs.): v. Boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boaster
BOASTER:<BR>(1) आत्मश्लाघिन् (m.);<BR>(2) विकत्थिन्<BR>(m.): v. Proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boastful
BOASTFUL, BOASTING (adj.):<BR>(1) विकत्थनः (ना,<BR> नं)<BR>or<BR>विकत्थिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) आत्मश्लाघिन् (f.<BR>नी);<BR>(3) दृप्तः (प्ता, प्तं);<BR>(4) गर्वितः (ता, तं);<BR>(5) by comp. with अहङ्कार।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boasting
BOASTING (subs.):<BR>(1) आत्मश्लाघा;<BR>(2) विकत्थनम्,<BR> -ना,<BR>what b. about it<BR>का तत्र विकत्थना, Vi.;<BR>(3)<BR>गर्वः: v. Pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boastingly
BOASTINGLY:<BR>(1) सगर्वम्;<BR>(2) सदर्पम्;<BR>(3)<BR>साभिमानम्;<BR>(4) विकत्थनया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boat
BOAT:<BR>(1) नौः;<BR>(2) नौका;<BR>(3) तरी;<BR>(4) तरणिः<BR> -णी;<BR>(5) पोतः (=a big boat, a ship).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boatable
BOATABLE (adj.): नौतार्यः (र्या, र्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boat-man
BOAT-MAN:<BR>(1) नाविकः;<BR>(2) पोतवाहः;<BR>(3) दाशः<BR>(a class of boat-men). M. viii. 408.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boat-swain
BOAT-SWAIN: *नौपालः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bobbin
BOBBIN: v. Reel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bode
BODE: v. To forbode, portend. presage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bodice
BODICE:<BR>(1) कूर्पासक।;<BR>(2) चोलः;<BR>(3) कञ्चु लिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bodiless
BODILESS:<BR>(1) अशरीरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) अविग्रहः<BR>(हा, हं);<BR>(3) अनङ्गः (ङ्गा, ङ्गं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bodily
BODILY (adj.):<BR>(1) शारीरिकः (की, कं);<BR>(2)<BR>कायिकः (की, कं);<BR>(3) दैहिकः (की, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bodily
BODILY (adv.):<BR>I Corporeally: सशरीरम्।<BR>II<BR>Entirely: q. v. साकल्येन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bodkin
BODKIN:<BR>I For piercing: आविधः।<BR>II For<BR>the hair: केशकीलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

body
BODY:<BR>I The frame of an animal:<BR>(1) शरीरम्;<BR>(2) गात्रम्;<BR>(3) कायः;<BR>(4) देहः (mn.);<BR>(5) वपुः;<BR>(6) तनुः (f.);<BR>(7) कलेवरम्;<BR>(8) मूर्तिः;<BR>(9) विग्रहः<BR>(rare);<BR>(10) वर्ष्मन् (n.) (rare).<BR>II A person:<BR>v. No body, some body, etc.<BR>III Any<BR>substance: पदार्थः, by collision of two b. s<BR>पदार्थद्वयस्य संघट्टात्।<BR>IV An assembly: q. v. सभा।<BR>V. A collection: q. v. समवायः, a b. of men<BR>जनसमवायः।<BR>VI The main or central part:<BR>Ph.<BR>the b. of a carriage<BR>यानमध्यम् (?);<BR>the b. of<BR>a tree<BR>प्रकाण्डः;<BR>the b. of an army<BR>बलसमुदायः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

body-guard
BODY-GUARD: शरीररक्षाधिकारनियुक्तः पुरुषः, K.:<BR>v. Guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bog
BOG: अनूपः: v. Fen, marsh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boggle
BOGGLE: v. To hesitate, shuffle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boggy
BOGGY: अनूपः (पा, पं): v. Fenny, marshy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boil
BOIL (subs.):<BR>(1) स्फोटः;<BR>(2) विस्फोटः;<BR>(3)<BR>गण्डः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boil
BOIL (v. t.):<BR>(1) क्वाथयति (c. of क्वथ्),<BR>to b. in<BR>oil<BR>तैलमध्ये क्वाथयति, V. p.<BR>(2) पचति (पच्, c.<BR>1) (=to cook),<BR>much b. ed milk<BR>अतिपक्वं<BR> दुग्धम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boil
BOIL (v. i.):<BR>I Of liquids:<BR>(1) क्वथ्यते (pass.<BR>of क्वथ्),<BR>b. ing water<BR>आपः क्वथ्यमानाः; V. d.<BR>II Fig., क्वथ्यते: v. To burn.<BR>III To be<BR>cooked in liquid: सिद्ध; (द्धा, द्धं) मवति (भू,<BR>c. l).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boiled
BOILED (in a boiler):<BR>(1) उख्यः (ख्या ख्यं,);<BR>(2) स्थालीपक्व; (क्वा, क्वं);<BR>(3) पैठर; (री, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boiler
BOILER:<BR>(1) स्थाली;<BR>(2) कटाहः;<BR>(3) पिठरः;<BR>(4)<BR>उखा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boisterous
BOISTEROUS:<BR>I Violent, rough:<BR>(1) उच्चै रसितृ<BR>(f. त्री),<BR>the b. ocean<BR>उच्चैरसितापगानां पतिः Si.<BR>iii. 72: v. Noisy;<BR>(2) उत्कटः (टा, टं)<BR>(=furious: q. v.);<BR>(3) प्रचण्डः (ण्डा, ण्डं)<BR>(=violent, strong),<BR>II Turbulent, tumul-<BR>-tous: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boisterously
BOISTEROUSLY: v. Violently, furiously, tumul-<BR>-tously;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bold
BOLD<BR>I Daring, intrepid;<BR>(1) साहसिकः (की,<BR> कं);<BR>(2) साहसिन् (f. नी)<BR>II Impudent,<BR>rude: q. v.:<BR>III Of expression etc. प्रगल्भः<BR>(ल्भा, ल्भं),<BR>a b. speaker<BR>प्रगल्भवाच् (mfn.), D.<BR>Ph.<BR>it is a mere b. assertion that there is no<BR>part of the Vedas treating of existing things.<BR>भूतवस्तुपरो वेदभागो नास्तीति वचनं साहसमात्रम्, S. i.<BR>4.<BR>IV Conspicuous, prominent: q. v. V.<BR>Steep: q. v. To make b. (to say): निर्भयं or<BR>प्रगल्भं<BR>or<BR>साहसेन (वदति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bold-faced
BOLD-FACED: v. Impudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boldly
BOLDLY:<BR>I Courageously:<BR>(1) साहसेन;<BR>(2)<BR>निर्भयम्<BR>II Impudently: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boldness
BOLDNESS:<BR>I Courage:<BR>(1) साहसं,<BR>pleased with<BR>the b. of the weaver<BR>कौलिकसाहसानुरञ्जितमनसा, P. i. 5; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">Page080</a>]<BR>(2) निर्भीकता (=intrepidity);<BR>(3) शौर्यम् (=<BR>valour).<BR>II Of language: साहसम्।<BR>III Im-<BR>-pudence: q. v. साहसं,<BR>it is b. to be in front<BR>of a master<BR>पत्युः पुरः साहसमासितव्यम्, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bole
BOLE: v. Trunk, stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boll
BOLL: v. Pod, follicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bolster
BOLSTER (subs.): उपधानम् (=pillow: q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bolster up
BOLSTER UP (v.): v. To support, prop up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bolt
BOLT (subs.):<BR>I A missile, a dart: q. v.<BR>II<BR>For securing doors:<BR>(1) अर्गलम्;<BR>(2) विष्कम्भः<BR>(rare).<BR>III Thunder-bolt: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bolt
BOLT (v. t.):<BR>I To secure with a bolt:<BR>(1)<BR>अर्गलेन पिदधाति (धा, c. 3.)<BR>or<BR>रुणद्धि (रुध्, c. 7.)<BR>or<BR>बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9);<BR>(2) अर्गलं ददाति (दा c.<BR>3.) (with gen.).<BR>II To fasten, restrain:<BR>q. v.<BR>III To sift: q. v.<BR>IV To examine:<BR>q. v. V. To exhibit: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bolt
BOLT (v. i.): निष्पतति (पत् c. l.), M. viii. 55.:<BR>v. To depart. Also=to start abruptly:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bolter
BOLTER, BOLTING-SIEVE:<BR>(1) चालनी;<BR>(2) तितौः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bolus
BOLUS: *गुलीः v. Pill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bomb
BOMB: आग्नेयगुली, प्रज्वलितप्रक्षिप्तः खण्डशः पतित्वा<BR> शत्रुविमर्दनकारी स्वयंविदीर्यमानपदार्थपरिपूर्णायोगुली-<BR>विशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bombard
BOMBARD: *आग्नेयगुलीभिर्मृद्राति (मृद्, c. 9.):<BR>v. To batter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bombardment
BOMBARDMENT: *आग्नेयगुलीभिर्मर्दनं<BR>or<BR>विमर्दनं or<BR>मन्थनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bombast
BOMBAST:<BR>(1) अप्रतीतशब्दप्रयोगः;<BR>(2) उच्चशब्दप्रयोगः;<BR>(3) उच्चशब्दाः (=big words)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bombastic
BOMBASTIC:<BR>(1) अप्रतीतः (ता, तं), Kav.;<BR>(2)<BR>उच्चः (च्चा, च्चं);<BR>(3) ध्वनिसारः (रा, रं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bond
BOND (subs.):<BR>I A band, a ligament: q. v.:<BR>बन्धः।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) पाशः,<BR>b. of affection<BR>प्रणय-<BR>पाशः;<BR>(2) बन्धः (rare),<BR>b. of hope<BR>आशाबन्धः।<BR>Me. iii. In. pl., imprisonment, captivity:<BR>q. v.: बन्धनम्।<BR>IV A legal document:<BR>प्रतिज्ञापत्रम्: Ph.<BR>bail b.<BR>प्रातिभाव्यपत्रम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bond
BOND (adj.): v. Captive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bondage
BONDAGE:<BR>(1) दासत्वम् (=slavery: q. v.);<BR>(2)<BR>वन्दित्वम् (=captivity; q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bonded
BONDED (adj.): Ph.<BR>b. goods<BR>*प्रतिज्ञातशुल्कदानानि<BR>द्रव्याणि (n. pl.):<BR>b. warehouse<BR>*प्रतिज्ञातशुल्कदान-<BR>द्रव्यशाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bond-maid
BOND-MAID, BOND-WOMAN:<BR>(1) दासी;<BR>(2) चेटी;<BR>(3) किङ्करी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bond-man
BOND-MAN, BOND-SERVANT:<BR>(1) दासः;<BR>(2)<BR>किङ्करः;<BR>(3) चेटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bone
BONE (subs.):<BR>(1) अस्थि (n.);<BR>(2) कीकसम् (rare);<BR>(3) कुल्यम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bone
BONE, OF BONE (adj.): अस्थि (in comp.),<BR>b-<BR>ache<BR>अस्थितोदः;<BR>b. necklace<BR>अस्थिमाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bone
BONE (v. t.):<BR>(1) निरस्थीकरोति (कृ, c. 8.);<BR>(2)<BR>अस्थीनि निर्हरति (हृ, c. l.).<BR>or<BR>निष्कर्षति (कृष्, c.<BR>1) (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boneless
BONELESS<BR>(1) अस्थिहीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) अस्थिरहितः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boneset
BONESET: सन्धिमुक्तं काण्डभग्नं वास्थि समादधाति (धा, c.<BR>3.)<BR>or<BR>स्थापयति (c. of स्था).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bone-setter
BONE-SETTER: यः सन्धिमुक्तं भग्नं चास्थि समादधाति;<BR> भग्नास्थिचिकित्सकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bonfire
BONFIRE: उत्सवाग्निः (?) उत्सवधूपः (?) (see B.<BR>iii. 5).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bonmot
BONMOT: नर्मभाषितम्: v. Witticism, jest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bonnet
BONNET: (स्त्रीलोकभृतं) शिरस्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bonny
BONNY (adj.): सुन्दरः (री, रं): v. Handsome,<BR>pretty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bony
BONY:<BR>(1) अस्थिमत्<BR>or<BR>अस्थिवत् (f. ती) (=having<BR>bones);<BR>(2) अस्थिमयः (यी, यं) (=made of<BR>or full of bones): v. Also robust, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

booby
BOOBY: स्थूलबुद्धिः: v. Blockhead, fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

book
BOOK (subs.):<BR>I Any literary work:<BR>(1)<BR>पुस्तकम्,<BR>a printed b.<BR>*मुद्रितपुस्तकम्;<BR>(2) ग्रन्थः (=<BR>work: q. v.)<BR>II A division of a literary<BR>work:<BR>(1) अध्यायः, S.:<BR>(2) पर्वन्, (n.) (sp. of<BR>the b. s of the Mahābhārata):<BR>(3) काण्डः<BR>(sp. of the b. s of the Rāmāyaṇa;<BR>(4)<BR>सर्गः (=canto), N. Ph.:<BR>account-b.<BR>गणनापत्रिका,<BR>Raj.; “I was so much in his b. s” तस्याहमेतादृश-<BR>मनुग्रहभाजनमासम्; without b. (=without autho-<BR>-rity) प्रमाणं विना; without b. (=by memory<BR>q. v.): पुस्तकव्यतिरेकेण (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

book
BOOK (v. t.): पत्रिकायां सन्निवेशयति (c. of विश्) or<BR>आरोपयति (c. of रुह्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bookbinder
BOOKBINDER: *पुस्तकबन्धनकारीः v. Binder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bookbinding
BOOKBINDING: पुस्तकबन्धनशिल्पम्; or sim. पुस्तक-<BR>बन्धनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

book-case
BOOK-CASE: *पुस्तकरक्षिणी; पुस्तकाधारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bookish
BOOKISH:<BR>(1) ग्रन्थप्रियः (या, यं) (?);<BR>(2) पुस्तकासक्तः<BR>(क्ता, क्तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

book-keeper
BOOK-KEEPER: गणनापत्रिकापालः (?): v. Accoun-<BR>-tant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

book-keeping
BOOK-KEEPING: गणनापत्रिकाविद्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

book-seller
BOOK-SELLER:<BR>(1) पुस्तकविक्रेतृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) पुस्तक<BR> विक्रयिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

book-worm
BOOK-WORM:<BR>I A person extremely fond of<BR>books: पुस्तकचुञ्चुः<BR>II A worm that eats b. s:<BR>धुणः; पुस्तकखादककीटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boom
BOOM (v. i.): प्रध्वनति (ध्वन्, c. l): v. To echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boom
BOOM (subs.):<BR>I For extending the bottom<BR>of sails: *वातवसनप्रसारणदण्डः<BR>II A chain or<BR>line of spars to obstruct navigation etc.:<BR>बन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boon
BOON (adj.):<BR>I Gay, merry: q. v.<BR>II Kind,<BR>bountiful: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boon
BOON (subs.):<BR>I Favour, gift: q. v. अनुग्रहः।<BR>II A prayer, petition: q. v.: प्रार्थना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boor
BOOR:<BR>I A peasant, a rustic: q. v.<BR>II A<BR>rude man: अविनीतः<BR>or<BR>निर्मर्यादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boorish
BOORISH:<BR>(1) ग्राम्यः (म्या, म्यं);<BR>(2) अशिष्ट;<BR>(ष्टा, ष्टं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boorishly
BOORISHLY: ग्राम्यजनवत्: v. Also coarsely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boorishness
BOORISHNESS:<BR>(1) ग्राम्यता (=rusticity);<BR>(2)<BR>अशिष्टता (=coarseness: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boot
BOOT (v. t.): v. To benefit, profit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boot
BOOT, TO: i. e. in addition: exp by the adj.<BR>अतिरिक्तः (क्ता, क्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boot
BOOT (subs.):<BR>(1) पादुका (=shoe: q. v.);<BR>(2)<BR>उन्नतपादुका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

booth
BOOTH:<BR>(1) पर्णशाला (=hut);<BR>(2) दूष्यम् (=tent):<BR>(3) उपकार्या (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bootjack
BOOTJACK: *उन्नतपादुकानिःसारिणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bootless
BOOTLESS: निष्फलः (ला, लं): v. Fruitless, un-<BR>-availing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bootlessly
BOOTLESSLY: निरर्थकम्: v. In vain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boot-tree
BOOT-TREE: पादुकानां चर्मशिथिलीकरणाय जंघाकृतिकाष्ठ-<BR>यन्त्रम्; काष्ठपादुका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

booty
BOOTY: लुण्ठितम्<BR>or<BR>लुण्ठितानि (n. pl.): v. Plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

borax
BORAX:<BR>(1) टङ्कनम्;<BR>(2) धातुद्रावकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

border
BORDER (subs.):<BR>(1) पर्यन्तः,<BR>whose b. s were<BR>carved with flowers<BR>कुसुमलवच्छुरितपर्यन्तः (न्ता, न्तं)<BR>D. ii.; from the b. of the disk of the sun<BR>पर्यन्तादहिममयूखमण्डलस्य; Ki. vii. 9.;<BR>(2) प्रान्तः,<BR>Ku. iii. 43.;<BR>(3) उपान्तः,<BR>on whose b.<BR>यस्यो-<BR>पान्ते, Me. ii. 14.;<BR>(4) अन्तः,<BR>on the b. of a<BR>forest<BR>वनान्ते। B. of a garment:<BR>(1) अञ्चलः;<BR>(2) दशा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

border
BORDER (v. t.): पर्यन्तं<BR>or<BR>प्रान्तं विदधाति (धा, c.<BR>2)<BR>or<BR>निर्माति (मा, c. 2) (with gen.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

border on or upon
BORDER ON or UPON:<BR>I Lit., expr. by the<BR>subs.:<BR>lands b. ing on the Kailāsa<BR>कैलासपर्यन्त-<BR>भूमयः<BR>or<BR>कैलासपरिसराः;<BR>Bengal, on the south b. s<BR>on the sea<BR>वङ्गानां दक्षिणसीमा सागरः: v. To<BR>adjoin.<BR>II Fig.: To resemble closely:<BR>vanity b. s on insolence<BR>गर्वो धाष्ठर्यान्नातिदूरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bore
BORE (subs.):<BR>I That which bores:<BR>(1)<BR>वेधनी;<BR>(2) वेधनिका;<BR>(3) आविधः।<BR>II A hole<BR>made by boring:<BR>(1) छिद्रम्;<BR>(2) रन्ध्रम्।<BR>III<BR>Calibre: q. v.<BR>IV A high tide: वानम्। v. A<BR>troublesome fellow: उद्वेजकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bore
BORE (v. t.):<BR>I To perforate:<BR>(1) विध्यति, आ-,<BR>(व्यध्, c. 4);<BR>(2) स्फोटयति (स्फुट, c. 10);<BR>(3) छिद्रयति (छिद्र्, c. 10).<BR>II To vex, worry,<BR>harass: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

borer
BORER:<BR>I One who bores:<BR>II That which<BR>bores: v. Bore (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boring
BORING:<BR>(1) वेधः, b. of the ears (a religious<BR>ceremony), कर्णवेधः;<BR>(2) स्फोटनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

born
BORN:<BR>(1) जातः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) प्रसूतः (ता, तं);<BR>(3)<BR>उद्भूतः (ता, तं);<BR>(4) जः (जा, जं), in. comp.,<BR>b. of a different father<BR>अन्यपितृजः (जा, जं), K. b.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

born
BORN, BE:<BR>(1) जायते (जन्, c. 4),<BR>b. of the race<BR>of Manu<BR>मनोः कुले जातम्, Si. i. 67;<BR>(2) उद्भवति<BR>(भू, c. l)<BR>the child was b. of me<BR>बालो मय्युदभूत्,<BR>D. iv.;<BR>(3) सूयते, प्र, (pass. of सू);<BR>(1) उत्पद्यते<BR>(पद्, c. 4) (with loc.). Ph.<BR>the son b. of a<BR>Śudra by a slave girl<BR>यः शूद्रस्य सुतो दास्यां भवेत्,<BR>M. ix. 179.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boron
BORON: *वोरणः; धातुविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

borough
BOROUGH: नगरम् (=town); *ब्रिटनीयमहासभायां<BR> प्रतिनिधिप्रेरणाधिकारि नगरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

borrow
BORROW:<BR>I To b. money, etc.:<BR>(1) ऋणं करोति<BR>(कृ, c. 8), should eat ghee (even)<BR>by b. ing<BR>ऋणं<BR> कृत्वा घृतं पिबेत्, D. s.;<BR>(2) ऋणं गृह्वाति (ग्रह्, c. 9) or<BR>आदत्ते (दा, c. 3);<BR>(3) धारं करोति (?).<BR>II To<BR>take from another: Ph.<BR>this sentence is b. ed<BR>from Kālidāsa<BR>*वचनमिदं कालिदासाद् गृहीतम्।<BR>III<BR>Assume, imitate: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

borrower
BORROWER:<BR>(1) ऋणकर्ता;<BR>(2) ऋणग्रहीता;<BR>(3)<BR>ऋणग्राही;<BR>(4) खादकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

borrowing
BORROWING (subs.):<BR>(1) ऋणग्रहः, -णम्;<BR>(2) ऋणकरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bosky
BOSKY: v. Woody, bushy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bosom
BOSOM (subs.):<BR>I The breast:<BR>(1) वक्षस् (n.),<BR>pressed (him)<BR>to his bosom<BR>निष्पिपेष परिरभ्य वक्षसा।<BR>Ki. xviii. 13;<BR>(2) उरम् (n.),<BR>and beat her<BR>b.<BR>उरो जघान च, Ku. iv. 26;<BR>(3) वक्षःस्थलम्;<BR>(4) भुजान्तरम् (poet).<BR>II Fig.: The heart:<BR>q. v. हृदयम्,<BR>b. friend<BR>हृदयङ्गमः सखा Ku. iv.<BR>24.<BR>III The interior: गर्भः,<BR>the b. of the<BR>earth<BR>भूगर्भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bosom
BOSOM (v. t.):<BR>I To take to heart: हृदि धारयति<BR>(धृ, c. l)<BR>or<BR>निदधाति (धा, c. 3).<BR>II To<BR>conceal: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boss
BOSS: गण्डः (?): v. Stud, knob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

botanic
BOTANIC, -AL: उद्भिद्विद्याविषयकः (का, कं); B.<BR>garden<BR>*उद्भिदुद्यानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

botanist
BOTANIST: *उद्भिद्विद् (mfn.); उद्भिद्विद्याविशारदः<BR>(दा, दं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

botanize
BOTANIZE: *परीक्षायै तरुलतादीन् गवेषयति (गवेष्,<BR>c. 10).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

botany
BOTANY: उद्भिद्विद्या; तरुलतादिविषया विद्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

botch
BOTCH (subs.):<BR>I A blotch: q. v.<BR>II A potch<BR>q. v.: कन्था।<BR>III A clumsy performance:<BR>v. Clumsy and performance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

botch
BOTCH (v. t.):<BR>I To potch: q. v.<BR>II To do<BR>any thing clumsily: कौशलं विना<BR>or<BR>अपटु कार्यं<BR> करोति (?):<BR>you have b. ed this<BR>त्वयेदं नष्टम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

botcher
BOTCHER: अदक्षसूचिकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

both
BOTH (adj.):<BR>(1) उभौ (m. du.), उभे (f. n. du.),<BR>b. of them bowing were not (distinctly) seen by<BR>b. (the mothers) उभावुभाभ्यां प्रणतौ न दृष्टौ, R.<BR>xiv. 2.;<BR>(2) उभयः (या, यं) (gen. in comp.)<BR>on b. sides<BR>उभयतः;<BR>in b. ways<BR>उभयथा;<BR>in b.<BR>places<BR>उभयत्र;<BR>b. days<BR>उभयेद्युः;<BR>(3) Often<BR>sim. by the dual:<BR>b. the parents<BR>पितरौ,<BR>R. i. 1.;<BR>with b. the hands<BR>दोर्भ्याम्, Ku.<BR>iii. 76.;<BR>(4) द्वयम् affixed, to b. the seniors<BR>गुरुद्वयाय, Si. ii. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

both
BOTH (conj.): च॥।च,<BR>where b. fate and cupid<BR>are assailants<BR>यस्मिन् विधिश्च मदनश्च कृताभियोगः,<BR>Ma. i.;<BR>does b. good and bad<BR>शुभञ्चाशुभञ्च विद-<BR>धाति, Ma. i.;<BR>b. to see the country and to learn<BR>its customs<BR>*देशदर्शनायाचारव्यवहारपरिज्ञानाय च।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bother
BOTHER (v.): v. To tease, annoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bots
BOTS: कृमिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bottle
BOTTLE (v. t.): Ph.: to b. wine from a cask<BR>भाण्डान्मद्यं गृहीत्वा बोतलेषु, निवेशयति (c. of विश्)<BR>or<BR>बोतलान् पूरयति (पूर्, c. 10).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bottle
BOTTLE (subs.): *बोतलः; काचादिनिर्मितपात्रविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bottom
BOTTOM (subs.):<BR>I The lowest part:<BR>(1)<BR>तल्लम्,<BR>whose b. cannot be touched<BR>अतलस्पर्शः (र्शा,<BR> र्शं);<BR>who were sitting at the b. of the tree<BR>तरु-<BR>तलेऽवस्थितान्, H. ii.;<BR>(2) अधोभागः;<BR>(3) पादः<BR>(of a hill: v. Foot).<BR>II Fig.: Ph.<BR>one who<BR>has dived to the b. of Philosophy<BR>दर्शनपारदर्शी;<BR>one who has gone to the b. of all śāstras<BR>सकल-<BR>शास्त्रपारङ्गमः, P. i. 10;<BR>you should examine it to<BR>the b.<BR>त्वयेदमामूलं परीक्षितव्यम्;<BR>you are at the b.<BR>of this mischief<BR>त्वमस्यानर्थस्य भूलं<BR>or<BR>निदानम्।<BR>III<BR>A valley: q. v.; निम्नभूमिः।<BR>IV A ship:<BR>q. v.: पोतः। V. Stamina: q. v.<BR>VI Dregs:<BR>q. v.: मलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bottom
BOTTOM (v. t.):<BR>I To found or build upon<BR>q. v. B. ed: v. Based.<BR>II To furnish with<BR>a bottom: तलं विदधाति (धा, c. 3) (with<BR>gen.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bottomless
BOTTOMLESS:<BR>(1) अगाधः (धा, धं);<BR>(2) अतलस्पर्श<BR>(र्शा, र्शं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bottomry
BOTTOMRY: पोतबन्धकः: v. Hypothecation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bough
BOUGH:<BR>(1) शाखा;<BR>(2) विटपः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bougie
BOUGIE: मूत्रमार्गादेर्मलशोधनाय यन्त्रविशेषः; *प्रवेशिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boulder
BOULDER: गण्डशैलः (?), Ki. vii. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boulevard
BOULEVARD: राजपथः: v. Street.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bounce
BOUNCE:<BR>I To spring: q. v.: आस्कन्दी<BR>(स्कन्द्, c. 1).<BR>II To boast: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bouncing
BOUNCING: v. Stout, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bound
BOUND (subs.):<BR>I A leap, spring: q. v. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">Page083</a>]<BR>लम्फः।<BR>II Limit, confine, boundary: q. v.:<BR>Ph. without b. v. Boundless;<BR>to keep within<BR>b. s<BR>सीमां न व्यत्येति (इ, c. 2);<BR>to transgress the<BR>b. s of decorum<BR>मर्यादां भिनत्ति (भिद्, c. 7).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bound
BOUND (v. t.): Ph.:<BR>b. ed on the north by the<BR>Himālayas<BR>यस्योत्तरसीमा हिमालयः; b. ed on the<BR>all sides (i. e. encircled) by the river Vetravatī<BR>वेत्रवत्या परिगतः (ता, तं);<BR>b. this field<BR>अस्य क्षेत्रस्य<BR> सीमां निर्धारय (धृ, c. 10).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bound
BOUND (v. i.): v. To leap, spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bound
BOUND (adj.)<BR>I Confine: बद्धः (द्धा, द्धं): v.<BR>To bind.<BR>II Destined: Ph. b. for Puri<BR>पुरीयात्रिन् (f. णी);<BR>where are you b. to<BR>क्व गच्छसि।<BR>III Equiv. to must: q. v.:<BR>you are b. to do<BR>this<BR>त्वयेदमवश्यं कर्तव्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boundary
BOUNDARY: सीमा (f.)<BR>or<BR>सीमन् (m.):<BR>a dispute<BR>about b. s<BR>सीमाविवादः;<BR>on the b. lines<BR>सीमा-<BR>सन्धिषु;<BR>b. marks<BR>सीमालिङ्गानि, M. viii. 6.<BR>248. 249.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bounden
BOUNDEN (adj.):<BR>(1) अवश्यकर्तव्यः (व्या, व्यं);<BR>(2) अवश्यकरणीयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boundless
BOUNDLESS:<BR>(1) असीमः (मा, मं);<BR>(2) निरवधि<BR>(mfn.) (rare),<BR>b. ditch<BR>निरवधिपरिखा, Vi. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boundlessness
BOUNDLESSNESS:<BR>(1) असीमता;<BR>(2) अनन्तता;<BR>(3)<BR>अमेयता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bounteous bounteously
BOUNTEOUS BOUNTEOUSLY: v. Bountiful,<BR>bountifully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bountiful
BOUNTIFUL:<BR>(1) वदान्यः (न्या, न्यं): v. Muni-<BR>-ficent;<BR>(2) उदारः (रा, रं): v. Liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bountifully
BOUNTIFULLY:<BR>to give b.<BR>मुक्तहस्तं ददाति: v.<BR>Liberally, largely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bountifulness
BOUNTIFULNESS:<BR>(1) वदान्यता;<BR>(2) औदार्यम्: v.<BR>Liberality, generosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bounty
BOUNTY:<BR>I Munificence: q. v.: वदान्यता।<BR>II Gift: q. v. दानम्।<BR>III A premium or<BR>reward: q. v.: पारितोषिकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bouquet
BOUQUET:<BR>I Of flowers: v. Nosegay.<BR>II<BR>Of wine: आमोदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bourgeon
BOURGEON: स्फुटति (स्फुट्, c. 6): v. To bud,<BR>sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bourn
BOURN: v. Bound, limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bout
BOUT:<BR>I A conflict, contest: q. v.<BR>II A<BR>turn: q. v. वारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bovine
BOVINE:<BR>(1) comp. with गो-,<BR>b. genus<BR>गोजातिः;<BR>(2) गव्यः (व्या, व्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bow
BOW (v. i.): नमति, प्र-, (नम्, c. l),<BR>b. s to you<BR>all<BR>नमति वः सर्वान्, Ku. vi. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bow
BOW (v. t.): नमयति, अव-, आ-, वि-, प्र-, अभि-,<BR>(c. of नम्):<BR>b. ing the head<BR>शिरो नमयित्वा (not<BR>शिरसा प्रणम्य which means a dif. kind of salu-<BR>-tation): v. To bend, incline, subdue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bow
BOW (subs.):<BR>I Salutation: q. v.:<BR>(1) प्रणामः<BR>(the most common word, though the form<BR>of salutation dif. from a b.);<BR>(2) मूर्घ्नः कम्पः,<BR>Ku. vii. 43.<BR>II The stem or prow of a<BR>ship: q. v.: पोताग्रम्।<BR>III A knot: q. v.:<BR>पाशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bow
BOW (subs.):<BR>I For discharging arrows:<BR>(1)<BR>धनुः;<BR>(2) चाप (mn.);<BR>(3) कार्मुकम्;<BR>(4) शरासनम्।<BR>B. of Arjuna<BR>गाण्डीवः;<BR>b. of Śiva<BR>पिनाकः;<BR>the<BR>notched^1 extremity of a b.<BR>अटनी;<BR>to bend the b.<BR>against deer<BR>धनुरिदं मृगेषु नमयितुम्, Sa. ii.<BR>II A<BR>musician's b.<BR>(1) कोणः;<BR>(2) परिवादः;<BR>(3)<BR>शारिका (rare).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bow-bent
BOW-BENT:<BR>(1) वक्रः (क्रा, क्रं);<BR>(2) कुटिलः (ला,<BR> लं): v. Crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bow-legged
BOW-LEGGED:<BR>(1) प्रज्ञु (mfn.);<BR>(2) प्रगतजानु<BR>(mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bow-man
BOW-MAN:<BR>(1) धन्वी;<BR>(2) धानुष्कः;<BR>(3) धनुर्धरः;<BR>(4) धनुर्भृत्;<BR>(5) निषङ्गी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bow-string
BOW-STRING:<BR>(1) ज्या;<BR>(2) धनुर्गुणः;<BR>(3) मौर्वी;<BR>(4) जीवा (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bowels
BOWELS:<BR>I The intestines: अन्त्राणि (n. pl.).<BR>II The interior of any thing, गर्भः।<BR>III<BR>Fig., compassion, pity: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bower
BOWER:<BR>(1) कुञ्जः;<BR>(2) निकुञ्जः;<BR>(3) लतामण्डपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bowl
BOWL (subs.):<BR>I A vessel: पुटः (?): v. Cup.<BR>II The hollow of a vessel<BR>(1) पुटः;<BR>(2) गर्भः<BR>III A ball: q. v. गुलिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bowl
BOWL (v. t.):<BR>I To roll: q. v.<BR>II To pelt:<BR>q. v. B. out: v. Knock down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bowl
BOWL (v. i.): गुलिकाभिः क्रीडति (क्रीड्, c. l).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bowler
BOWLER: expr. by verb: v. To bowl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bowling-green
BOWLING-GREEN: गुलिकाक्रीडार्थं समीकृतो भूभागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bowsprit
BOWSPRIT: पोताग्रप्रलम्बी वातवसनप्रसारणदण्डः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

box
BOX (subs.):<BR>I A chest, etc.:<BR>(1) पेटिका;<BR>(2) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">Page084</a>]<BR>समुद्गः, -कः;<BR>(3) सम्पुटः, -कः।<BR>II An enclosed<BR>space with seats in a theatre: *कोष्ठः or<BR>निभृतकोष्ठः।<BR>III The driver's seat on a<BR>carriage; सूतासनम् (?).<BR>IV A tree; वृक्षविशेषः।<BR>v. A blow: q. v.: मुष्टिप्रहारः।<BR>VI A present:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

box
BOX (v. i.):<BR>(1) मल्लयुद्धं करोति;<BR>(2) मुष्टीमुष्टि प्रहरति<BR>(हृ, c. l)<BR>or<BR>युव्यते (युध्, c. 4).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

box
BOX (v. t.): मुष्टिना प्रहरति (हृ, c. l)<BR>or<BR>हन्ति (हन्,<BR>c. 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boxer
BOXER:<BR>(1) मल्लयोद्धा;<BR>(2) मल्लः;<BR>(3) भल्लः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boxing
BOXING (subs.): मल्लयुद्धम् (also = b. match.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boxing-day
BOXING-DAY; *कृष्टस्य जन्मोत्तरदिनं यदा पारितोषि-<BR>काणींलण्डनदेशे प्रदीयन्ते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boy
BOY:<BR>(1) बालः;<BR>(2) बालकः;<BR>(3) शिशुः;<BR>(4) कुमारः;<BR>(5) दारकः (=an infant);<BR>(6) माणवकः (spe. in<BR>contempt.).<BR>From a boy<BR>बाल्यात् प्रभृति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boyhood
BOYHOOD:<BR>(1) बाल्यम्;<BR>(2) शैशवम्;<BR>(3) कौमारम्;<BR>(4) शिशुत्वम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boyish
BOYISH: बालिशः (शा, शं): v. Childish.<BR>b.<BR>nature:<BR>बालभावः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brace
BRACE (subs.):<BR>I A support: *आलम्ब।<BR>II A<BR>cincture or bandage: q. v.<BR>III In print-<BR>-ing: “}” ‘इत्याकारः संयोगचिह्नविशेष:<BR>IV A pair,<BR>a couple; q. v. V. A strap, girth; q. v.:<BR>चर्मबन्धः (?). VI. A rope: वायुवसनदण्डचालनरज्जुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brace
BRACE (v. t.):<BR>I To prop, support: q. v.<BR>II To tighten, strengthen: q. v.<BR>III To<BR>turn the yards of a ship:<BR>(1) सञ्चालयति (c.<BR>of चल्);<BR>(2) परावर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bracelet
BRACELET:<BR>(1) अङ्गदम्;<BR>(2) कङ्कणम्;<BR>(3) केयूरम्;<BR>(4) वलय (mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bracket
BRACKET (subs.):<BR>I A support:<BR>(1) निर्यूहः;<BR>(2) नागदन्तः।<BR>II A mark in printing: *अर्ध-<BR>चन्द्रद्वयम्, चिह्नविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bracket
BRACKET (v. t.): *अर्धचन्द्रद्वयेन चिह्रयति (चिह्न्,<BR>c. 10).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brackish
BRACKISH:<BR>(1) ईषल्लवणः (णा, णं);<BR>(2) comp.<BR>with क्षार-,<BR>b. water<BR>क्षारजलम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brad
BRAD: कीलविशेषः। B. -awl वेधनिकाः v. Gimlet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brag
BRAG; विकत्थते (कत्य्, c. l): To boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

braggart
BRAGGART, BRAGGADOCIO: विकत्थीः v. Boaster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bragging
BRAGGING (adj.): विकत्थिन् (f. नी): v. Boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bragging
BRAGGING (subs.): विकत्थनम्: v. Boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

braggingly
BRAGGINGLY:<BR>(1) साहङ्कारम्;<BR>(2) सविकत्थम्: v.<BR>Boastingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brahmin
BRAHMIN:<BR>(1) ब्राह्मणः;<BR>(2) विप्रः;<BR>(3) द्विजः। a<BR>false B.:<BR>(1) ब्राह्मणब्रुवः;<BR>(2) ब्रह्मबन्धुः। The B. s<BR>add शर्मन् (m.) after their names.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

braid
BRAID (v. t.).<BR>I Of hair:<BR>(1) कवरीं<BR>or<BR>केशपाशं<BR> बव्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9);<BR>(2) केशान् संग्रथनाति (ग्रन्थ,<BR>c. 9).<BR>II To weave, entwine: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

braid
BRAID (subs.):<BR>I Of hair:<BR>(1) कवरी;<BR>(2)<BR>धम्मिल्लः (b. ed and ornamented hair;<BR>(3)<BR>वेणी (unornamented b. ed hair, as worn by<BR>widows, etc.)<BR>II A knot: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brain
BRAIN:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मस्तिष्कम्;<BR>(2) मस्तुलुङ्गम्;<BR>(3) गोर्दम् (rare).<BR>II Intellect, sense: q. v.:<BR>बुद्धिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brain
BRAIN (v. t.):<BR>I मस्तकं चूर्णयति, etc.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>To ruin, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brainless
BRAINLESS: निर्बुद्धि (mfn.): Senseless, stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brake
BRAKE:<BR>I For railway cars.: *गतिस्तम्भयन्त्रम्।<BR>II A cart for breaking in horses: *अश्व-<BR>दमनयानम्।<BR>III A snaffle: q. v.<BR>IV A<BR>thicket: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bramble
BRAMBLE: कण्टकिगुल्मः, K. b.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brambly
BRAMBLY:<BR>(1) कण्टकिगुल्मावृतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2)<BR>कण्टकिन् (f. नी) (=thorn).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bran
BRAN:<BR>(1) तुषः;<BR>(2) बुषम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

branch
BRANCH (subs.): शाखा (in all the senses of<BR>the English word). B. of a b.<BR>(1) प्रशाखा;<BR>(2) प्रतिशाखा, V. p.;<BR>(3) अवान्तरशाखा,<BR>V p.<BR>com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

branch
BRANCH (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.: शाखां निर्मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.).<BR>II To divide into parts: q. v.:<BR>the race<BR>b. ed into eight parts<BR>भिन्नोऽष्टधा वंशः। R. xvi. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

branch off
BRANCH OFF: Ph.<BR>there again b. es off<BR>*तत्रास्यापरा<BR> शाखा निर्गता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

branch out
BRANCH OUT: Ph. b. ed out into a long discourse<BR>सविस्तरं वक्तुमारेभे।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

branching
BRANCHING, BRANCHY adj.):<BR>(1) शाखिन् (f.)<BR>नी) (=having branches);<BR>(2) शाखामयः (यी,<BR> यं) (=full of b. es.);<BR>(3) शाख्यः (ख्या, ख्यं)<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brand
BRAND (subj.):<BR>I Fire-brand: q. v.: अलातम्। [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">Page085</a>]<BR>II A mark of infamy:<BR>(1) अङ्कः;<BR>(2) चिह्नम्।<BR>III A sword: q. v.<BR>IV Kind, quality:<BR>q. v.: Ph.<BR>ale of so and so b.<BR>*अमुकचिह्रविशिष्टं<BR> यवसुरम।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brand
BRAND (v. t.):<BR>I With a hot iron: (तप्तलोहेन)<BR>चिह्नयति (चिह्र, c. 10.)<BR>or<BR>अङ्कयति (अङ्क्, c. 10.).<BR>II To stigmatize: q. v.: Ph.<BR>b. ed with<BR>infamy,<BR>अयशसाङ्कितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brandish
BRANDISH:<BR>(1) लासयति (c. of लस);<BR>(2) भ्रमयति<BR>(c. of भ्रम्),<BR>b. ed the pikes<BR>शूलानि भ्रमयांचक्रुः। B.<BR>xiv. 9. Ph.<BR>b. ed their bows<BR>धनूंष्यास्फालितानि<BR>(after Śi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brandy
BRANDY: मदिराविशेषः; वारुणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brangle
BRANGLE: v. Wrangle, squabble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brash
BRASH (adj.): अधीरः (रा, रं): v. Impetuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brasier
BRASIER: A pan for coals:<BR>(1) अङ्गारशकटी;<BR>(2) अङ्गारधानिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brass
BRASS:<BR>(1) पित्तलम्;<BR>(2) आरकूटम् (rare).<BR>Oxide of<BR>b.<BR>रीतिपुष्पम्। A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brassy
BRASSY: comp. with पित्तल-।: v. Brazen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brat
BRAT: अर्मकः: v. Child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bravado
BRAVADO: v. Boast, defiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brave
BRAVE (v. t.): v. To face, disregard, defy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brave
BRAVE (adj.):<BR>I Courageous:<BR>(1) साहसिकः<BR>(की, कं) (=bold, daring);<BR>(2) विक्रान्तः (न्ता,<BR> न्तं) (=valorous);<BR>(3) निर्भयः (या, यं) (=fear-<BR>-less);<BR>(4) तेजस्विन् (f. नी) (=spirited). Ab.<BR>man: i. e. a hero:<BR>(1) वीरः;<BR>(2) शूरः Ph.:<BR>fortune favours the b.<BR>साहसे श्रीः प्रतिवसति। Mr.<BR>iv.<BR>II Excellent, noble, grand: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bravely
BRAVELY:<BR>(1) निर्भयम् v. Fearlessly;<BR>(2) कृत-<BR>सत्त्ववेगः (गा, गं), Ki. xvii. 15.;<BR>(3) सधैर्यम्<BR>(=with fortitude).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bravery
BRAVERY:<BR>I Courage:<BR>(1) शौर्यम्;<BR>(2) साहसम्<BR>(=boldness);<BR>(3) विक्रमः (=valour)<BR>(4)<BR>निर्भीकता (fearlessness^1).<BR>II Splendour,<BR>magnificence: q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bravo
BRAVO:<BR>I Interjec.: साधु।<BR>or<BR>साधु साधु।<BR>II<BR>Subs.: v. Assassin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brawl
BRAWL (v. i.): व्याक्रोशति (क्रुश्, c. l.): v. To<BR>wrangle, quarrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brawl
BRAWL, BRAWLING (subs.): व्याक्रोशः। v.<BR>Wrangling, quarrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brawling
BRAWLING (adj.): कलहप्रियः (या, यं): Quarrel-<BR>-some, noisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brawn
BRAWN:<BR>I The flesh of a boar:<BR>(1) शूकर-<BR>मांसम्;<BR>(2) वल्लूरम्।<BR>II Muscle, strength: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brawny
BRAWNY: मांसलः (ला, लं): v. Muscular,<BR>strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bray
BRAY (v.):<BR>I To pound: q. v.: पिनष्टि (पिष्,<BR>c. 7.).<BR>II To utter a harsh cry:<BR>(1)<BR>चित्कारं करोति (कृ, c. 8.);<BR>(2) विरौति (रु, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bray
BRAY, BRAYING (subs.):<BR>(1) चित्कारः;<BR>(2)<BR>खरनादः (=b. of an ass): v. Noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

braying
BRAYING (subs.): i. e. pounding; q. v.: पेषणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brazen
BRAZEN:<BR>I Made of brass:<BR>(1) पित्तलमयः (यी,<BR> यं);<BR>(2) by comp.,<BR>b. vessel<BR>पित्तलपात्रम्।<BR>II<BR>Shameless, impudent; q. v. निर्लज्जः (ज्जा, ज्जं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brazen-browed
BRAZEN-BROWED, BRAZEN-FACED: v. Shame-<BR>-less, impudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brazier
BRAZIER: कांस्यकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brazil-nut
BRAZIL-NUT: फलविशेषः:<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brazil-wood
BRAZIL-WOOD: रङ्गदो रक्तवर्णकाष्ठविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breach
BREACH:<BR>I Fracture: q. v.<BR>II A gap made<BR>by breaking:<BR>(1) छिद्रम्;<BR>(2) रन्ध्रम्<BR>III Vio-<BR>-lation: q. v.: Ph.<BR>b. of peace<BR>शान्तिभङ्गः (?);<BR>b. of promise<BR>प्रतिज्ञाभङ्गः;<BR>b. of agreement<BR>समय-<BR>भेदः;<BR>b. of faith<BR>विश्वासघातः।<BR>IV. B. of union:<BR>भेदः;<BR>a b. between friends<BR>सुहृद्भेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breach
BREACH (v. t.): i. e. to make a breach: v.<BR>Breach (subs.) (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bread
BREAD:<BR>I Lit.: रोटी, Bha. Unleavened b.<BR>अपूपः।<BR>II Sustenance, living: q. v.: अन्नं<BR>or<BR>अन्नजलम् (=b. and water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bread-corn
BREAD-CORN: रोटीकरणोपयोगिगोधूमादिशस्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bread-fruit
BREAD-FRUIT:<BR>(1) कण्ट-<BR>or<BR>कण्टक-<BR>or<BR>कण्टकिफलम्;<BR>(2) पनसं<BR>or<BR>पनसफलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bread-fruit-tree
BREAD-FRUIT-TREE:<BR>(1) पनसः;<BR>(2) कण्टकि (की)-<BR>-फलः;<BR>(3) कण्टकफलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bread-root
BREAD-ROOT: पालङ्गाकारः शाकभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breadth
BREADTH:<BR>I Width:<BR>(1) विस्तारः;<BR>(2) परिसरः;<BR>(3) प्रस्थः;<BR>(4) आयामः (rare);<BR>(5) परिणाहः;<BR>(6) विष्कम्भः (rare). Ph.: two fingers in b.<BR>द्व्यङ्गुलः (ला, लं); (the doors)<BR>should be made<BR>two cubits in b.<BR>तानि द्विहस्तविस्तृतानि कार्याणि।<BR>II<BR>In painting:<BR>b. of effect:<BR>विस्तारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break
BREAK (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) भनक्ति (भञ्ज्, c. 7.),<BR>the flag-staff is broken<BR>भग्नः स्यन्दनकेतुः, Ve. ii.;<BR>(2) चूर्णयति, सं-, (चूर्ण्, c. 10.) (=reduce to<BR>powder),<BR>shall I not b. Suyodhana's thighs with<BR>my mace<BR>संचूर्णयामि गदया न सुयोधनोरू, Ve. ii. To<BR>weaken or subdue: q. v.: भनक्ति।<BR>III To<BR>make bankrupt: अवसादयति (c. of सद्) (?).<BR>Miscell.:<BR>but do not b. my meditation<BR>मा पुनः<BR> समाधिं भंक्ष्यसि, V. ii.;<BR>b. ing his silence<BR>मौनभङ्गं<BR> विधायास्य, Vet.;<BR>to b. one's sleep<BR>निद्राभङ्ग<BR> करोति, Si.;<BR>to b. an agreement<BR>समयं भिनत्ति (भिद्,<BR>c. 7.), M. v. To violate; I will b. all order<BR>भनज्मि सर्वमर्यादाः, B. vi. 38.; to “b. one's<BR>mind” हृदयं विवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.), Ki. v. To<BR>open; to b. horse etc.: v. To break<BR>in;<BR>to b. wind<BR>पर्दते (पर्द्, c. l.);<BR>I will<BR>b. their union<BR>तान् विघटयामि (घट्, c. 10.) (the<BR>time) has come (for) b. ing my fast by (sucking)<BR>blood<BR>उपस्थिता शोणितपारणा मे, R. ii. 39.;<BR>to b.<BR>ground<BR>मृत्तिकाम् उत्तोलयति (तुल्, c. 10.) (?);<BR>to b.<BR>one's heart<BR>हृदयं विदारयति (c. of दृ), U.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break
BREAK (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) भज्यते (pass. of<BR>भञ्ज्) or more commonly भग्नः (ग्ना, ग्नं) भवति<BR>(भू, c. l.);<BR>(2) त्रुट्यति (त्रुट्, c. 4.). Fig.<BR>my<BR>heart is b. ing<BR>स्फुटति हृदयम्, U.; v. To rend.<BR>II To become bankrupt: अवसीदति (सद्,<BR>c. l.) (?).<BR>III To dawn: Ph.<BR>the day has<BR>nearly broken<BR>प्रभातप्राया रजनी, Sa. iv.<BR>IV To<BR>decline in health; Ph.<BR>you are b. ing every<BR>day<BR>अनुदिवसं परिहीयसेऽङ्गेषु, Sa. iii. V. To<BR>burst: q. v.<BR>VI To fall out: Ph.<BR>their<BR>union broke<BR>भेदस्तेषामजनि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break away
BREAK AWAY: i. e. to become dispersed, as<BR>clouds: विप्रकीर्णः (र्णा, र्णं) भवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break down
BREAK DOWN (v. t.): चूर्णयति (चूर्ण्, c. 10.): v.<BR>To crush, demolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break down
BREAK DOWN (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.: भग्नः (ग्ना, ग्नं)<BR>भवति।<BR>II Fig. To fail: अवसीदति (सद्, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break forth
BREAK FORTH: v. To break out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break in
BREAK IN:<BR>I Lit.: प्रसह्य प्रविशति (विश्, c. 6.).<BR>II To train horses, etc.<BR>(1) दमयति (c. of<BR>दम्);<BR>(2) विनयति (नी, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break into
BREAK INTO:<BR>(1) अपजिहीर्षया प्रविशति (विश्, c. 6.)<BR>(?);<BR>(2) सन्धिं कृत्वा प्रविशति (=by making a<BR>hole under the walls of a house;<BR>(3) कुड्य<BR> कृत्वा प्रविशति (by making a passage in a<BR>wall).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break in or into pieces
BREAK IN or INTO PIECES:<BR>I Trans: खण्डं खण्डं<BR> करोति (कृ, c. 8.);<BR>(2) चूर्णयति;<BR>II Intrans:<BR>(1) खण्डं खण्डं भवति (भू, c. l.),<BR>the fruit fell<BR>from the king's hand and broke in p.<BR>फलं राज्ञः<BR> करकमलान्निपत्य भग्नं खण्डं बभूव, Vet.;<BR>(2) चूर्णितः<BR>(ता, तं) (भवति), H. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break loose
BREAK LOOSE:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by circumlo:<BR>it broke loose and got into the high street<BR>स<BR> आलानस्तम्भं भंक्त्वाराजमार्गमवतीर्णः Mr. ii.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>of anger, etc.:<BR>(1) उद्दीष्यते (दीप्, c. 4.);<BR>(2)<BR>स्फूर्जति (स्फुर्ज्, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break off
BREAK OFF (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: भनक्ति।<BR>II To put<BR>and end to: Ph. b. his journey for three nights<BR>त्रिरात्रं प्रयानभङ्गमकरोत्, P. i. p.; to b. a marriage<BR>विवाहभङ्गं करोति (?) (comp. the Bengali<BR>idiom).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break off
BREAK OFF (v. i.): विरमति (रम्, c. l.) (=to<BR>cease: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break open
BREAK OPEN:<BR>(1) भनक्ति;<BR>(2) त्रोटयति (c. of त्रुट्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break out
BREAK OUT:<BR>I To escape from restraint:<BR>v. To escape.<BR>II To arise suddenly:<BR>(1)<BR>आविर्भवति<BR>or<BR>प्रादुर्भवति (भू, c. l.);<BR>(2) उदेति (इ,<BR>c. 2.):<BR>(3) उद्गच्छति (गम्, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break up
BREAK UP (v. t.): To break into pieces: q. v.<BR>II To abolish: q. v.<BR>to b. an assembly<BR>सभाभङ्गं<BR> करोति<BR>or<BR>सभां भनक्ति, C.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break up
BREAK UP (v. i.):<BR>I To break into pieces:<BR>q. v.<BR>II To be dissolved: Ph. let us b. now<BR>स्वं स्वं स्थानमिदानीं गच्छामः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break upon
BREAK UPON: Ph.<BR>the waves b. the rocks<BR>उप-<BR>लाहतास्तरङ्गा विभेदं<BR>or<BR>विलयं गच्छन्ति (after Ki.<BR>and Si.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break with
BREAK WITH: विवदते (वद्, c. l.): v. To quarrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break
BREAK (subs.):<BR>I An interruption:<BR>(1)<BR>विच्छेदः;<BR>(2) छेदः।<BR>II An opening made by<BR>fracture: भङ्गः।<BR>III. B. of day: v. Dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breakage
BREAKAGE: i. e. an allowance for breaking:<BR>Perh. simp. भङ्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breaker
BREAKER:<BR>I One who breaks: भञ्जकः: v. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">Page087</a>]<BR>To break for the different senses.<BR>II A<BR>wave breaking upon a sand-bank, etc.:<BR>भङ्गः<BR>or<BR>भङ्गिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breakfast
BREAKFAST (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रातराशः;<BR>(2) प्रात-<BR>र्भोजनम्;<BR>(3) कल्यवर्तः, Mr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breakfast
BREAKFAST (v. i.): प्रातराशं<BR>or<BR>प्रातर्भोजनं करोति<BR>(कृ, c. 8.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breaking
BREAKING (subs.): भङ्गः (in almost all the<BR>English senses). B. in (of horses etc.) दमनम्।<BR>B. out (of disease, etc.):<BR>(1) उद्भवः;<BR>(2)<BR>आविर्भावः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

break-water
BREAK-WATER: *जलवेगरोधकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bream
BREAM: मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breast
BREAST (subs.):<BR>I The bosom: q. v.<BR>(1)<BR>वक्षस्;<BR>(2) उरस् (n.)<BR>II The organ that<BR>secretes milk:<BR>(1) स्तनः;<BR>(2) कुचः (of human<BR>b. only);<BR>(3) पयोधरः।<BR>III The heart:<BR>q. v. हृदयम्।<BR>B. -bone<BR>वक्षोऽस्थि (n.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breast
BREAST (v. t.): सम्मुखयति (nomi.): v. To face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breast-plate
BREAST-PLATE: उरस्त्राणम्: v. Corslet, cuirass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breast-work
BREAST-WORK: प्रगण्डी, Mah.: v. Rampart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breath
BREATH:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) श्वासः,<BR>to take b.<BR>श्वसिति;<BR>(2) निःश्वासः (=air exhaled),<BR>to hold b.<BR>निःश्वासं<BR> रुणद्धि;<BR>(3) प्राणः (=air inhaled), restraint of<BR>b. (a religious exercise) प्राणायामः;<BR>or<BR>प्राण-<BR>संयमः<BR>(4) श्वसितम्,<BR>out of b.<BR>मुहुर्मुहुरत्युल्वणं निःश्वसिति,<BR>K.<BR>II. Life: प्राणाः (m. pl.).<BR>III Respite,<BR>pause: q. v. विरामः।<BR>IV An instant: निमेषः,<BR>in a b.<BR>निमेषेण। V. Breeze: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breathe
BREATHE (v. i.):<BR>I To respire: श्वसिति (श्वस्,<BR>c. l.).<BR>to b. the last<BR>प्राणान् जहाति (हा, c. 3.):<BR>v. To die.<BR>II To live: q. v.: श्वसिति (I)<BR>who b.<BR>यः श्वसिमि N. v. 109.<BR>III Pause, rest:<BR>q. v.<BR>to b. hard<BR>विनिःश्वसिति N. xii. 2.;<BR>to<BR>b. freely<BR>उच्छ्वसिति, Ki. ix. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breathe
BREATHE (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>we b. the air<BR>*वायुं<BR> गृह्णीमः (ग्रह्, c. 9.): n. b. पिबति (पा, c. l.) is<BR>used, but not in the exact sense.<BR>II To<BR>exhale: उद्गिरति (ग, c. 6.). b. ing the smell of<BR>परिमलोद्गारिभिः, Me. i. 26.<BR>III To<BR>express, manifest: q. v.<BR>IV To whisper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breathe in or into
BREATHE IN or INTO: v. To infuse.<BR>B. life<BR>into:<BR>जीवं संचारयति (c. of चर्) P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breathe out
BREATHE OUT:<BR>(1) उद्गिरति (गॄ, c. 6.);<BR>(2)<BR>उद्वमति (वम्, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breathing
BREATHING (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) श्वासः;<BR>(2)<BR>श्वासनम्।<BR>II Inspiration: q. v.<BR>III Aspi-<BR>-ration: q. v.<BR>IV In gram.: Ph. rough b.<BR>महाप्राणचिह्नम्; soft b. अभिनिष्टानचिह्नम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breathing hole
BREATHING HOLE: गवाक्षम्: v. Vent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baeathing-time
BAEATHING-TIME: Ph.<BR>give me b.<BR>श्वसितुमवकाश<BR> देहि: v. Pause, respite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breathless
BREATHLESS:<BR>I Out of breath: v. Breath.<BR>II Lifeless: q. v.: निरुच्छ्वासः (सा, सं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bred
BRED: v. To breed,<BR>well-b.:<BR>विनीतः (ता, तं).<BR>Ill-b.:<BR>दुर्विनीतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breech
BREECH:<BR>(1) कटिदेशः<BR>(2) नितम्बः। B. of a gun:<BR>*पश्चाद्भागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breeches
BREECHES: जङ्घावारः। Sometimes = Trousers: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breed
BREED (v. t.):<BR>I To beget (Lit and Fig):<BR>q. v.: जनयति (c. of जन्).<BR>II To bring up:<BR>(1) पुष्णाति<BR>or<BR>पुष्यति (पुष्, c. 9. and 4.):<BR>(2)<BR>वर्धयति (c. of वृध्).<BR>III To educate, instruct:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breed
BREED (v. i.):<BR>I To conceive:<BR>(1) गर्मं धारयति<BR>or<BR>धरति (धृ, c. 10. and 1.),<BR>(2) गर्भवती<BR>or<BR>गर्भिणी<BR> भवति (भू, c. l.).<BR>II To be produced: जायते<BR>(जन्, c. 4.): v. To produce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breed
BREED (subs.):<BR>I Race, kind: जातिः,<BR>a cock<BR>of the Balākā b.<BR>बलाकाजातिस्ताम्रचूडः, D. v.<BR>Of<BR>a good b.:<BR>उत्तमजातीयः (या, यं).<BR>II Progeny,<BR>offspring: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breeder
BREEDER:<BR>I The female that produces:<BR>(1)<BR>जनयित्री;<BR>(2) जननी;<BR>(3) प्रसूतिः;<BR>(4) उत्पादिका।<BR>II A b. of animals:<BR>(1) पोषकः;<BR>(2) पोष्ट्ट (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breeding
BREEDING (subs.):<BR>I Nurture, education,<BR>instruction: q. v.<BR>II Manners, deport-<BR>-ment: q. v.: Ph.<BR>good b.<BR>विनयः of good b.<BR>विनीतः (ता, तं): v. Politeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breeze
BREEZE:<BR>(1) मन्दानिलः;<BR>(2) मृदुपवनः;<BR>(3)<BR>समीरणः v. Wind, Ph.:<BR>the b. is blowing<BR>मन्दं<BR> मन्दं वहति पवनः<BR>morning b.<BR>विभातवायुः R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breezy
BREEZY: सुप्रवातः (ता, तं): v. Windy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

breviary
BREVIARY:<BR>I An epitome: q. v.<BR>II of<BR>prayers: *स्तोत्रसंग्रहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brevity
BREVITY: संक्षेपः: v. Conciseness, shortness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brew
BREW (v. t.):<BR>I To make beer: पचति (पच्,<BR>c. l.) (?).<BR>II To mix: q. v.<BR>III To.<BR>contrive, plot, hatch: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brew
BREW (v. i.): यवसुरं पचति (पच्, c. l.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brewer
BREWER: *यवसुरपाचकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brewhouse or brewery
BREWHOUSE or BREWERY: *यवसुरपाचकस्थली;<BR> यवसुरपाकशाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brewing
BREWING (subs.): *यवसुरपाकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

briar
BRIAR: v. Brier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bribe
BRIBE (subs.): उत्कोचः,<BR>taking b. s even from the<BR>ministers<BR>सचिवमण्डलादप्युत्कोचग्राही, D.;<BR>not<BR>corruptible by b. etc.<BR>धनदानादिनाभेद्यः, K. b. one<BR>who receives b.<BR>(1) उत्कोचकः (rare);<BR>(2)<BR>उत्कोचग्राहकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bribe
BRIBE (v. t.): उत्कोचं ददाति (दा, c. 3.) Ph.<BR>the<BR>judge has been b. d<BR>उत्कोचदानेन वशीकृतो विचारकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

briber
BRIBER: उत्कोचदाता (=one who gives bribe).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bribery
BRIBERY:<BR>(1) उत्कोचदानम् (giving bribe):<BR>(2)<BR>उत्कोचग्रहणम् (taking b.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brick
BRICK (subs.): इष्टका,<BR>baked b.<BR>पक्वेष्टका;<BR>unbaked<BR>b.<BR>आभेष्टका, Mr.<BR>A b. house<BR>इष्टकागृहम्;<BR>a pile<BR>of b. s<BR>इष्टकाराशिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brickbat
BRICKBAT:<BR>(1) इष्टकाखण्डम् (?);<BR>(2) इष्टका-<BR>शकलम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brick-kiln
BRICK-KILN: इष्टकापाकः (?): v. Kiln.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bricklayer
BRICKLAYER:<BR>(1) लेपकः;<BR>(2) पलगण्डः: v.<BR>Mason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brickmaker
BRICKMAKER:<BR>(1) इष्टकापाचकः (?);<BR>(2) इष्टका-<BR>कारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brick-work
BRICK-WORK: इष्टकाभिर्निर्मितः (ता, तं);<BR>these are<BR>b. s<BR>एतानीष्टकाभिर्निर्मितानि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bridal
BRIDAL (subs.): विवाहोत्सवः: v. Marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bridal
BRIDAL (adj.): वैवाहिकः (की, कं). B. procession<BR>(of the bridegroom) वरयात्रा N. xvi. 4.;<BR>b. string<BR>कौतुकम्;<BR>b. chamber<BR>कौतुकागारम्। Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bride
BRIDE:<BR>(1) वधूः;<BR>the b. and the bridegroom<BR>वधूवरम्,<BR>Ku. vii. 78.;<BR>(2) नववधः;<BR>(3) नवोढा (=just<BR>married);<BR>(4) आसन्नपाणिग्रहणा (=about to<BR>marry). A young b.:<BR>(1) कन्या;<BR>(2) कुमारी,<BR>R. vii. 22. A b. who chooses her own husband:<BR>स्वयंवरा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bridegroom
BRIDEGROOM: वरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bride-maid
BRIDE-MAID: जन्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bridesman
BRIDESMAN: जन्यः; वरस्य वध्वाश्च सहचरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bridewell
BRIDEWELL: कारागारम्: v. Prison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bridge
BRIDGE (subs.):<BR>(1) सेतुः,<BR>stone b.<BR>पापाणसेतुः,<BR>Raj.;<BR>to make a b.<BR>सेतुं बध्नाति R.<BR>or<BR>करोति,<BR>Mah.<BR>or<BR>निर्माति, Vi,<BR>or<BR>विदधाति, Ma. n. (with<BR>loc. or gen. and उपरि);<BR>(2) सङ्क्रमः (=foot<BR>-b.);<BR>(3) संवरः (rare).<BR>B. of the nose<BR>नासावंशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bridge
BRIDGE (v. t.): सेतुना बध्नाति, नि-, (बन्ध्, c. 9.),<BR>Mah.;<BR>b. d the Padmā, with boats:<BR>नौभिः<BR> पद्मां बबन्ध।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bridle
BRIDLE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: वल्गा: v. Bit, reins.<BR>II Fig.: v. Restraint, check.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bridle
BRIDLE (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: Perh. वल्गितः (ता, तं)<BR>करोति v. To bit, rein.<BR>II Fig.: To restrain,<BR>check: q. v.: नियन्त्रयति (यन्त्र्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brief
BRIEF (adj.):<BR>I Compressed, terse: v.:<BR>संक्षिप्तः (प्ता, प्तं). To be b. (when=b. ly): किं<BR> बहुना।<BR>II Lasting but little time: क्षणिकः<BR>(का, कं),<BR>b. enjoyment<BR>क्षणिका प्रीतिः H.;<BR>(2)<BR>अचिरस्थायिन् (f. नी): v. Temporary.<BR>III<BR>Short: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brief
BRIEF (subs.):<BR>I An epitome: q. v.<BR>II A<BR>dispatch: q. v.<BR>III An abridgment of a<BR>client's case: *विवादतत्त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

briefless
BRIEFLESS: Ph.<BR>he is a b. barrister<BR>*तं व्यवहार-<BR>पण्डितं कार्योपदेशार्थमर्थिप्रत्यर्थिनो नाश्रयन्ते; विवादतत्र्व-<BR>हीनो व्यवहारपण्डितः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

briefly
BRIEFLY:<BR>(1) संक्षेपेण;<BR>(2) संक्षेपतः;<BR>(3) समासतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

briefness
BRIEFNESS: v. Brevity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brier or briar
BRIER or BRIAR: कण्टकिगुल्मविशेषः; also = कण्टकि-<BR>गुल्मः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brig
BRIG: सामुद्रपोतभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brigade
BRIGADE: *पृतना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brigadier
BRIGADIER, BRIGADIER-GENERAL: *पृतनापतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brigand
BRIGAND:<BR>(1) परिपन्थी;<BR>(2) दस्युः: v. Robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brigandage
BRIGANDAGE: दस्युता: v. Robbery, plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brigantine
BRIGANTINE: Perh. वहित्रम्, D. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bright
BRIGHT:<BR>I Shining, lustrous:<BR>(1) उज्ज्वलः (ला,<BR> लं);<BR>(2) भासुरः (रा, रं);<BR>(3) दीप्रः (प्रा, प्रं);<BR>(4)<BR>द्योतनः (ना, नं);<BR>(5) रोचिष्णु (mfn.).<BR>II Clear,<BR>transparent: q. v.: उज्ज्वलः (ला, लं).<BR>III<BR>Sparkling with wit, clever: Perh. उज्ज्वल<BR>(ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brighten
BRIGHTEN (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: To make bright:<BR>(1) द्योतयति, उत्-, प्र-, (c. of द्युत्);<BR>(2) उज्ज्वलयति<BR>(c. of ज्वल्);<BR>(3) उद्भासयति (c. of भास्);<BR>(4)<BR>दीपयति (c. of दीप्), b. ing the skies with its rays<BR>दीपयन्नथ नभः किरणौघैः, Ki., ix. 23.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1)<BR>उज्ज्वलयति;<BR>(2) उद्भासयति।<BR>III To improve:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brighten
BRIGHTEN (v. i.): i. e. to be or become bright:<BR>expr. by the adj. s under bright. Ph.<BR>the sky<BR>did not quite b.<BR>न प्रसादमुचितं गमिता द्यौः, Ki.<BR>ix. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brightly
BRIGHTLY:<BR>(1) उज्ज्वलम्;<BR>(2) विमलम् (=clearly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brightness
BRIGHTNESS:<BR>I Splendour, brilliancy:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रभा;<BR>(2) तेजस्;<BR>(3) द्युतिः;<BR>(4) औज्ज्वल्यम्।<BR>II<BR>Acuteness, sharpness: q. v.: Perh. औज्ज्वल्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brill
BRILL: सुखाद्यमत्स्यविशेषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brilliancy
BRILLIANCY:<BR>(1) प्रभा;<BR>(2) उज्ज्वलता;<BR>(3) दीप्तिः;<BR>(4) रोचिष्णुता;<BR>(5) भ्राजथुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brilliant
BRILLIANT:<BR>(1) महोज्ज्वलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) प्रद्योतनः<BR>(ना, नं);<BR>(3) भासुरः (रा, रं); रोचिष्णु (mfn.);<BR>(5) भ्राजिष्णु (mfn.);<BR>(6) प्रदीप्तः (प्ता, प्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brilliantly
BRILLIANTLY: expr. by circumlo: v. Brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brim
BRIM:<BR>I Rim, border: q. v.: प्रान्तः।<BR>II Of<BR>any vessel: मुखम्,<BR>to the b.<BR>आमुखम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brimful
BRIMFUL: परिपूर्णः (र्णा, र्णं)<BR>or<BR>एकान्तं पूर्णं (र्णा, र्णं),<BR>“B. of glory” तेजोमयः (यी, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brimstone
BRIMSTONE: गन्धकः: v. Sulphur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brinded
BRINDED, BRINDLED:<BR>(1) शवलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2)<BR>कर्बू (र्बु) रः (रा, रं);<BR>(3) किर्मीरः (रा, रं);<BR>(4)<BR>चित्रः (त्रा, त्रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brine
BRINE:<BR>I Water saturated with salt:<BR>(1)<BR>लवणोदम्;<BR>(2) लवणजलम्।<BR>II The ocean:<BR>(1)<BR>लवणोदः;<BR>(2) लवणोदधिः;<BR>(3) लवणाम्बुराशिः;<BR>(4)<BR>लवणाब्धिः।<BR>III Tears: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bring
BRING:<BR>I To fetch^1 or cause to come:<BR>(1)<BR>आनयति (नी, c. l.),<BR>b. my darling here<BR>दयित-<BR>मिहानय, Ki. x. 47.;<BR>(2) आहरति, उप-, (हृ, c.<BR>1.),<BR>b. two dishes<BR>उभे शरावे चाहर, D. vi. Ph.<BR>winter b. s cold<BR>हेमन्तेन सह शीतमागच्छति।<BR>II To<BR>cause the obtaining of:<BR>(1) by verbs of<BR>motion or verbs signifying to obtain and<BR>the ins. or abl. of the cause:<BR>poverty b. s<BR>shame<BR>दारिद्र्याद्ध्रियमेति, Mr. i.; disgrace b. s<BR>despondency<BR>परिभवान्निर्वेदमापद्यते, Mr. i.;<BR>(2) ददाति<BR>(=to give: q. v.);<BR>(3) विकर्षति (कृष्, c. l.),<BR>b. s fortune<BR>श्रियं विकर्षति, Ki. iii. 7.<BR>III To<BR>induce, prevail on: q. v. Ph.:<BR>to b. an<BR>action<BR>अभियोगं करोति (?):<BR>b. to an end<BR>समापयति<BR>(c. of आप्); b. to pass: v. Bring about.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bring about
BRING ABOUT: घटयति (c. of घट्): v. To effect,<BR>accomplish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bring back
BRING BACK:<BR>(1) प्रत्यानयति (नी, c. l.),<BR>will b.<BR>the fortune of victory<BR>जयश्रियं प्रत्यानेष्यति, Ku. ii.<BR>52.;<BR>(2) प्रत्याहरति (हृ, c. l.), M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bring down
BRING DOWN:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) आनयति,<BR>brought<BR>them down to the earth<BR>क्षितिमानिन्युः, Ki. vii.<BR>19.;<BR>(2) अवतारयति (c. of तॄ) (=cause to<BR>descend) V. i.<BR>II To humble, abuse: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bring forth
BRING FORTH:<BR>I To beget: q. v.: सूते, प्र-,<BR>(सू, c. l.),<BR>Sumitrā brought f. twins<BR>सुमित्रा सुषुवे<BR> यमौ, R. x. 71.<BR>II To yield: q. v.: सूते,<BR>the aśoka tree at once brought f. flowers<BR>असूत सद्यः<BR> कुसुमान्यशोकः, Ku. iii. 26.<BR>III To b. forward:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bring forward
BRING FORWARD:<BR>(1) आनयति;<BR>(2) उपन्यस्यति<BR>(अस्, c. 4.);<BR>(3) उदाहरति (हृ, c. l.),<BR>argu-<BR>ments have been forcibly brought f.<BR>उपपत्तिरुदाहृता<BR> बलात्, Ki. ii. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bring in
BRING IN:<BR>I To admit: q. v.<BR>II To yield,<BR>produce: q. v.<BR>III To collect: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bring off
BRING OFF:<BR>(1) अपनयति (नी, c. l.);<BR>(2) अप-<BR>हरति (हृ, c. l.), Ve. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bring on
BRING ON: आवहति (वह्, c. l.): v. To<BR>produce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bring out
BRING OUT: बहिष्करोति,<BR>b. ing his son out<BR>तत्पुत्रं<BR> बहिष्कृत्य, H. ii.: v. To publish, expose, or<BR>detect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bring over
BRING OVER:<BR>I To bear across: आनयति (with<BR>double acc.), I brought him over to London<BR>*तमहं लण्डनमानीतवान्।<BR>II To draw to a new<BR>party or opinion: Ph.<BR>b. ing the Brahmins<BR>over by gold<BR>द्विजान् स्वीकृत्य स्वर्णेन, Raj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bring to
BRING TO: v. To resuscitate. Ph.<BR>I have<BR>brought troubles to my husband<BR>क्लेशावहा भर्तुः, R.<BR>xiv. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bring together
BRING TOGETHER:<BR>(1) समानयति (नी, c. l.); [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">Page090</a>]<BR>(2) समाहरति (हृ, c. l.): v. To collect,<BR>assemble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bring under
BRING UNDER:<BR>(1) नमयति (c. of नम्), R. xiii.<BR>9.;<BR>(2) आवर्जयति (वृज्, c. 10.), D. ii.<BR>To b.<BR>one's power<BR>वशं नयति<BR>or<BR>आनयतिः v. To subdue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bring up
BRING UP:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) आनयति;<BR>(2) उपानयति;<BR>(3) आहरति।<BR>II To train up, rear: q. v.:<BR>वर्धयति (c. of वृध्), (the child)<BR>was brought up<BR>by Vinayavati<BR>अवर्धत विनयवत्या, D. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brink
BRINK: v. Edge, margin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

briny
BRINY: लावणः (णी, णं): v. Salty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brisk
BRISK: चपलः (ला, लं) (of movements, etc.);<BR>(2) चतुरः (रा, रं) (=clever, sharp): v.<BR>Lively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brisket
BRISKET: Ph.<BR>b. of beef<BR>*गोवक्षोमांसम्;<BR>b. of<BR>mutton<BR>मेषवक्षोमांसम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

briskly
BRISKLY: त्वरितम् (=quickly): v. Vigorously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

briskness
BRISKNESS: v. Vivacity, quickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bristle
BRISTLE (subs.): सटा, Ki. viii. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bristle
BRISTLE (v. t.): Ph.<BR>b. ing of the hairs<BR>बद्ध-<BR>सटोन्नतिः, Ki. xiii. 2.<BR>or<BR>उद्भृ तसटाः (m. pl.),<BR>R. ix. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bristle
BRISTLE (v. i.):<BR>(1) स्तब्धः (ब्धा, ब्धं)<BR>or<BR>उन्नतः<BR>(ता, तं) भवति;<BR>(2) हृष्यति (हृष्, c. 4.) or<BR>पुलकितः (ता, तं) भवति (only of man in joy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bristly
BRISTLY: कण्टकितः (ता, तं),<BR>their skins b. with<BR>joy<BR>प्रीतिकण्टकितत्वचः, Ku. vi. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brittle
BRITTLE:<BR>(1) भङ्गुरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) सुभङ्गः (ङ्गा,<BR> ङ्गं);<BR>(3) भङ्गभाज् (mfn.) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brittleness
BRITTLENESS:<BR>(1) भङ्गुरता;<BR>(2) सुभङ्गता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

broach
BROACH (subs.): v. Spit; v. Also, brooch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

broach
BROACH (v. t.):<BR>I To spit: q. v.: शूलाकरोति।<BR>II To tap, pierce: q. v.<BR>III To put forth,<BR>publish first: q. v.: प्रचारयति (c. of चर्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

broad
BROAD:<BR>I Wide (in measurement): q. v.:<BR>(1) विस्तृतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) expr. by a comp.<BR>with the words given under breadth (I) or<BR>by adj. formed with any of those words<BR>and the affix वत्:<BR>seven cubits long and one<BR>cubit b.<BR>सप्तहस्तदीर्घा एकहस्तविस्ताराः: Ph.:<BR>a b.<BR>road<BR>सुविस्तारवान्मार्गः (?) (not विशालमार्गः):<BR>one<BR>who has a b. chest<BR>विशालवक्षस् (mfn.), R.;<BR>a<BR>breast beautiful and b. as the leaf of a door<BR>कपाट-<BR>-विस्तीर्णमनोरमोरः, Si. iii. 13.<BR>II Extensive,<BR>vast: q. v.: विस्तीर्णः (र्णा, र्णं). Ph.: b. jokes<BR>ग्राम्यपरिहासाः (m. pl.);<BR>b. nonsense<BR>*स्पष्टनिरर्थक-<BR>भाषितम्;<BR>thefts are not rare here even in b. day-<BR>light<BR>*देदीप्यमाने सूर्योऽप्यत्र चौर्याणि न विरलानि; it<BR>is as b. as long, i. e. (it makes no difference)<BR>अत्र को विशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

broad cloth
BROAD CLOTH: *बनातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

broadly
BROADLY: v. Widely. Ph.<BR>b. these are the<BR>species<BR>इत्येता जातयः स्थौल्यात्, Śr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

broadside
BROADSIDE:<BR>to fire a b.<BR>रणपोतस्यैकपार्श्वस्थां बन्दुक-<BR>श्रेणिं समं विसर्जयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

broadsword
BROADSWORD: खङ्गविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brocade
BROCADE: कार्मिकवस्त्रम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brocket
BROCKET: द्विवर्षीणो हरिणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brocoli
BROCOLI: शाकभेदः; फुल्लकबिसदृशः कबिभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brogue
BROGUE: पादुकाविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

broil
BROIL (subs.): कलहः: v. Quarrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

broil
BROIL (v. t.):<BR>(1) अङ्गारे पचति, Bha.;<BR>(2)<BR>भर्जयति (c. of भृज्) (upon a gridiron): v. To<BR>fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

broil
BROIL (v. i.): भृज्जति, -ते (भ्रज्ज्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

broken
BROKEN: v. Break. Ph.<BR>b. number<BR>भग्नांशः;<BR>b. -<BR>winded<BR>अल्पश्वासः (सा, सं);<BR>b.-hearted<BR>भग्नाशः<BR>(शा, शं)<BR>or<BR>भग्नमानसः (सा, सं), Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

broker
BROKER: *दल्लालः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brokerage
BROKERAGE: *दल्लालिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bromine
BROMINE: *पूयम्; ब्रोमिणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bronze
BRONZE: Perh. आरम् (comp. Lat. aes, aeris.)<BR>or<BR>आरकूटम्: v. Brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brooch
BROOCH: *वक्षोभूषणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brood
BROOD (v. i.): सेवते (सेव्, c. l.) (?) (used in<BR>this sense in Hindi),<BR>b. ing on eggs<BR>अण्डानि<BR> सेवमानः (ना, नं) (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brood over or on
BROOD OVER or ON: ध्यायति (ध्यै, c. l.) (with<BR>acc.): v. Contemplate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brood
BROOD (subs.):<BR>I Offspring, progeny: q. v.<BR>II A hatch: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brood
BROOD (adj.): Ph.<BR>b. mare<BR>बालप्रसवार्थं रक्षिता<BR> घोटकी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brooding
BROODING (subs.): Ph.<BR>b. on eggs<BR>अण्डसेवा (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brook
BROOK (subs.):<BR>(1) सरित्<BR>or<BR>कुसरित्;<BR>(2) क्षुद्र-<BR>नदी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brook
BROOK (v. t.): मर्षयति (मृष्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>endure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

broom
BROOM:<BR>I A brush:<BR>(1) सम्मार्जनी;<BR>(2) शोधनी।<BR>II A shrub: लताविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

