caldron
CALDRON:<BR>(1) कटाहः;<BR>(2) पिठरः: v. Boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calendar
CALENDAR:<BR>I An almanac: पञ्जिका।<BR>II A<BR>list: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calendar
CALENDAR (subs.): *चक्रयन्त्रम्, Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calender
CALENDER (v. t.): *चक्रयन्त्रेण श्लक्ष्णीकरोति (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calends
CALENDS: रोमकीयमासस्य प्रथमदिवसम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calenture
CALENTURE: व्यामोहः (Lit. and Fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calf
CALF:<BR>I The young of the cow:<BR>(1) वत्सः<BR>(2) गोवत्सः<BR>or<BR>धेनुवत्सः;<BR>(3) तणिकः (=a newly<BR>born c.), A.<BR>A she-c. two years old<BR>द्विहायनी.<BR>II A dolt, blockhead: q. v.<BR>III The c.<BR>of the leg: जङ्घाया मांसलः पश्चाद्भागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calibre
CALIBRE: Ph.: the c. (of a tube, etc.)<BR>मुखस्य<BR>or<BR>छिद्रस्य परिमाणम्;<BR>of small c.<BR>क्षुद्रमुखविशि<BR>(?);<BR>a man of small c.<BR>क्षुद्रबुद्धिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calico
CALICO: कार्पासभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

caligraphy
CALIGRAPHY: v. Penmanship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calk
CALK (v. t.): जलप्रवेशनिरोधाय नौकायाः फलकसनि<BR> च्छिद्राणि जीर्णवस्त्रखण्डैः पूरयति (c. of पॄ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calker
CALKER: जीर्णवस्त्रखण्डैर्नौकायाः फलकस न्धिच्छिद्रपूरक।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

call
CALL (v. t.):<BR>I To summon:<BR>(1) ह्वयति, आ -<BR>(ह्वे, c. l.), I will c. and ask my mistra<BR>गृहिणीमाहूय पृच्छामि, Mr. i.;<BR>(2) शब्दायते (nom)<BR>(=c. aloud),<BR>c. Maitreya<BR>मैत्रेयं तावत् शब्दाय<BR>Mr. iv.;<BR>(3) आकारयति (c. of कृ) (rare)<BR>(4) निमन्त्रयति (मन्त्र्, c. 10.) (=invite: q. v.)<BR>II To address by a particular name<BR>(1) आह्वयति, c. ed her by the name Pārvati<BR>पार्वतीति नाम्ना जुहाव, Ku. i. 26.;<BR>(2) नाम्ना<BR> संज्ञया<BR>or<BR>आख्यया अभिदधाति (धा, c. 3.): “c. a spade<BR>a spade” यो यद्रूपस्तं तद्रूपमभिधेहि।<BR>III To name<BR>designate:<BR>(1) वक्ति (वच्, c. 2.), भाषते (भाष्<BR>c. l.), etc. (=to speak: q. v.), you are c.ed<BR>‘mountainlifter’ तुलितभूभृदुच्यसे Si. xv. 30.;<BR>उदाहरति (हृ, c. l.),<BR>c. ed Dasharatha<BR>दशरथ<BR>इत्युदाहृतः, B. i. 1.;<BR>(3) अप-दिशति, व्यप-, (दिश्,<BR>c. l.), Si. xv. 28. Ph.<BR>c. to mind<BR>मनसि<BR>करोति;<BR>c. ed Rik, Yajus and Sāman<BR>ऋग्यजुःसाम-<BR>संज्ञकाः, S. p.;<BR>c. ed Tāraka<BR>तारकसंज्ञितः, Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

call back
CALL BACK: v. To recall, revoke, retract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

call for
CALL FOR: To demand, require.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

call forth
CALL FORTH: आह्वयति (ह्वे, c. l.) (Lit. and fig)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

call in
CALL IN:<BR>I To collect, as debts: v. to<BR>collect.<BR>II To invite, as friends आह्वयति,<BR> सम्-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

call off
CALL OFF: i. e. to divert: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

call out
CALL OUT: v. To recite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

call on
CALL ON or UPON:<BR>I To implore: q. v.<BR>To invoke: q. v.<BR>III To pay a short [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">Page099</a>]<BR>c. ed on me<BR>मां द्रष्टुमाजगाम (after Mu.);<BR>c. on<BR>him<BR>तं द्रष्टुं गच्छ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

call to
CALL TO: शब्दायते: v. Call (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

call
CALL (subs.):<BR>I A vocal address: आह्वानम्।<BR>Ph. “c. of the house” *सभासदां नामपाठः।<BR>II<BR>Demand, requisition: q. v.<BR>III A pipe or<BR>whistle: q. v. To make or give or pay a c.:<BR>v. Call on (III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calling
CALLING:<BR>I Lit.: आह्वानम्।<BR>II Vocation:<BR>q. v.: वृत्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

callosity
CALLOSITY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) किणः;<BR>(2) कदरः (?).<BR>II Fig.: hard-heartedness, insensibility:<BR>(1) काठिन्यम्;<BR>(2) कठोरता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

callous
CALLOUS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मृतः (ता, तं) (?);<BR>(2) कठिनः<BR>(ना, नं) (=hard: q. v.).<BR>II Fig.: hard-<BR>-hearted: q. v.: कठिनः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

callousness
CALLOUSNESS:<BR>(1) काठिन्यम्;<BR>(2) कठोरता: v.<BR>Insensibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

callow
CALLOW:<BR>(1) पक्षहीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) वीतपक्षः<BR>(क्षा, क्षं); and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calm
CALM (adj.):<BR>(1) शान्तः, प्र-, (न्ता, न्तं),<BR>O, what<BR>a c. and beautiful morning<BR>अहो प्रशान्तरमणीयता<BR> प्रभातस्य;<BR>c. and solemn place<BR>प्रशान्तगम्भीरभूमिः,<BR>Vi.;<BR>c. countenance<BR>शान्ताकारः, Ma.;<BR>(2)<BR>निष्कम्पः (म्पा, म्पं), निश्चलः (ला, लं) etc. (with-<BR>-out motion: as a sea),<BR>like the c. ocean on<BR>a c. day<BR>निवातनिष्कम्पमिवापगापतिम्, Ki.;<BR>the sea<BR>became very c. with unruffled water<BR>निभृतोऽभवदत्यर्थं<BR> समुद्रः स्तिमितोदकः। V. p.;<BR>(3) निर्वातः (ता, तं),<BR>etc. (=without wind: as a c. place), V. ;<BR>(4) अनुत्तरङ्गः (f. ङ्गा) etc. (=not wavy: as a<BR>river);<BR>(5) अक्षुब्धः (f. ब्धा), etc. (=not agi-<BR>-tated),<BR>To be c.:<BR>शाम्यति, प्र-, (शम्, c. 4.), Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calm
CALM (subs.):<BR>I As opposed to storm:<BR>निवातः<BR>or<BR>निर्वातः।<BR>II Calmness, tranquillity:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calm
CALM (v. t.):<BR>(1) शमयति, प्र-, (c. of शम्),<BR>to c.<BR>a tempest<BR>चण्डवातं शमयति;<BR>(2) शान्त्वयति or<BR>सान्त्वयति, अभि-, उप-, परि-, (शान्त्व्<BR>or<BR>सान्त्व् c.<BR>10.), to c. the son of wind (Bhima) मरुतः सुतमुप-<BR>सान्त्वयितुम्, Ki. ii. 25: v. To quiet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calmly
CALMLY:<BR>I Gently: q. v.<BR>II Quietly,<BR>patiently: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calmness
CALMNESS:<BR>(1) शान्तिः<BR>or<BR>शमः;<BR>(2) प्रशान्तिः or<BR>प्रशमः;<BR>(3) अक्षोभः and sim. comp. s<BR>(=absence of agitation);<BR>(4) better by<BR>adj. c. of mind:<BR>(1) धैर्यम्, Ki. xiv. 1<BR>(2)<BR>निर्विकारचित्तत्वम्, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calomel
CALOMEL: *पीतहरितपारदः; शुद्धपारदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

caloric
CALORIC: तापः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calorific
CALORIFIC: तापनः (नी, नं)<BR>or<BR>तापकः (का, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

caltrop
CALTROP:<BR>I A thistle: गोक्षुरः।<BR>II A mili-<BR>-tary instrument: *चतुःशूलम्; अश्वारोहाणां गति-<BR>निरोधाय युद्धयन्त्रविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calumniate
CALUMNIATE: परिवदति (वद्, c. l.), c. s in my<BR>presence (my)<BR>friend the king of Anga<BR>परिवदति<BR> समक्षं मित्रमङ्गाधिराजम्, Ve. v.: v. To slander,<BR>detract, revile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calumniation
CALUMNIATION: परिवादः: v. Calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calumniator
CALUMNIATOR: परिवादकः<BR>or<BR>परिवादीः v. Slan-<BR>-derer, reviler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calumnious
CALUMNIOUS: परिवादिन् (f. नी): v. Slanderous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calumniously
CALUMNIOUSLY:<BR>(1) गुणापवादेन;<BR>(2) अभूतमासज्य<BR>(=falsely);<BR>(3) असूयया (=detractingly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calumny
CALUMNY:<BR>(1) परिवादः,<BR>not before acquainted<BR>with c. s<BR>परिवादगोचरमयातपूर्वः (र्वा, वं), Ki.;<BR>(2)<BR>परिभाषणम् (rare);<BR>(3) पिशुनवाक्यम् (=evil<BR>speech): v. Slander, detraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calve
CALVE: वत्सं सूते, प्र-, (सू, c. 2.): v. To beget.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calvinism
CALVINISM: *केल्विनमतं<BR>or<BR>केल्विनस्य मतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calvinist
CALVINIST: *केल्विनमतावलम्बिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

calyx
CALYX: *दलकोषः; पुष्पदलावरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cambric
CAMBRIC: *किम्बृकम्; सूक्ष्मपटविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

camel
CAMEL:<BR>(1) उष्ट्रः;<BR>(2) क्रमेलकः;<BR>(3) द्विककुद्<BR>(m.) (rare).<BR>A young c.:<BR>करभः, A she-c.:<BR>उष्ट्री।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

camelopard
CAMELOPARD: दीर्घग्रीवः (?); उष्ट्रजातीयश्चित्रितो<BR> जन्तुविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cameo
CAMEO: *कामोपलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

camera obscura
CAMERA OBSCURA: *प्रतिविम्बग्राहको यन्त्रविशेषः,<BR> प्रतिविम्बग्राहिणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

camp
CAMP (subs.):<BR>(1) शिविरम्;<BR>(2) कटकः,<BR>To pitch<BR>a c.:<BR>स्कन्धावारं निवेशयति (c. of विश्), Ka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

camp
CAMP (v.): v. To encamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

campaign
CAMPAIGN:<BR>I An open tract:<BR>(1) समभूमिः;<BR>(2) केदारव्रततिश्वत्रवृक्षगुल्मादिवर्जिता भूमिः, Ka.<BR>II [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=100" target="_blank">Page100</a>]<BR>The time that an army keeps the field:<BR>विग्रहकालः (?) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

camphor
CAMPHOR:<BR>(1) कर्पर (mn.);<BR>(2) सिताभ्रः, A.;<BR>(3) हिमवालुका, A.<BR>(4) धनसारः, A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

camphorated
CAMPHORATED: कर्पूरवासितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

can
CAN (subs.):<BR>(1) चषक (mn.);<BR>(2) कंस (mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

can
CAN (v.);<BR>(1) शक्नोति (शक्, c. 5.), Menā could<BR>not restrain (her)<BR>from the undertaking<BR>शशाक मेना<BR> न नियन्तुमुद्यमात्, Ku. v. 5.;<BR>c. not be made to<BR>accept the ministry of Chandragupta<BR>वृषलस्य<BR> साचिव्यं ग्राहयितुं न शक्यते, Mu.;<BR>(2) प्रभवति (भू,<BR>c. l.),<BR>an enemy c. not conquer then<BR>प्रभवति न<BR> तदा परो विजेतुम्, Ki. x. 35.;<BR>(3) ईष्टे (ईश्, c. 2.),<BR>who c. move a good man<BR>सुजनं जनाश्चलयितुं क ईशते,<BR>Si. xv. 40.;<BR>(4) पारयति (पृ, c. 10.),<BR>nor c.<BR>we say that it is our friend's fault<BR>सखिगामी दोष<BR> इति व्यवसाययितुमपि न पारयामः, Sa. iv.;<BR>(5) क्षमते<BR>(क्षम्, c. l.), N. xiv. 16.;<BR>(6) समर्थः (र्था, र्थं)<BR>or<BR>शक्तः (क्ता, क्तं)<BR>or<BR>क्षमः (मा, मं) भवति (often<BR>understood). N. B. (a) Do not use 2 and 3<BR>in the pass.; (b) could can also be idiomati-<BR>-cally expressed by विधिलिङ्:<BR>I. c. deprive<BR>even Śiva of his fortitude<BR>कुर्यां हरस्यापि पिनाक-<BR>पाणेर्धैर्यच्युतिम्, Ku. iii. 10.; (c) cannot be — is<BR>best expressed by part. adj. s- तव्य, अनीय<BR>and य; what cannot be accomplished or cured<BR>असाध्यः (ध्या, ध्यं); what cannot be measured<BR>अपरिमेयः (या, यं); (d) cannot but- is expressed<BR>by अवश्यं or circumlo.: I cannot but remark<BR>मयावश्यं वक्तव्यम्;<BR>I cannot but weep<BR>रोदनं निवारयितुं<BR> न शक्नोमि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

canal
CANAL:<BR>(1) कुल्या;<BR>(2) प्रणाली;<BR>(3) उपकुल्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

canary bird
CANARY BIRD: पीतवर्णः पक्षिविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cancel
CANCEL:<BR>I To erase, obliterate: कुण्डलनां<BR> तनोति (तन्, c. 8.) (with gen.) (properly by<BR>the circular mark prevalent among<BR>Hindus), N.<BR>II. To annul=destroy; लुम्पति,<BR> अव-, वि-, (लुप्, c. 6.) (?).<BR>III To strike out<BR>common factors: अपवर्तयति (c. of वृत्), Li.<BR>IV To enclose: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cancellation
CANCELLATION:<BR>I Erasing: कुण्डलनाक्रिया।<BR>II<BR>Annulment: अवलोपः (?).<BR>III Striking out<BR>common factors: अपवर्तनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cancer
CANCER:<BR>I One of the signs of the zodiac:<BR>(1) कर्कटः;<BR>(2) ककः (rare).<BR>II A disease:<BR>कर्कटरोगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cancerous
