catch
CATCH (v. t.):<BR>I To seize:<BR>(1) धारयति<BR>or<BR>धरति<BR>(धृ, c. 10. and 1.), for which you were caught<BR>धृतोऽसि यदर्थम्, N. i. 143;<BR>for c. ing fish<BR>मत्स्य-<BR>धारणार्थम्, Tārānāth;<BR>(2) दधाति, धत्ते (धा, c. 3),<BR>the king caught the bird with his hand<BR>नृपः पतङ्गं<BR> तमधत्त पाणिना, N. i. 124;<BR>(3) गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9),<BR>caught the descending (ball) in the air<BR>अवपतन्तमाकाश एवाग्रहीत्, D. vi.;<BR>I was caught<BR>stealing<BR>चोरयित्वा ग्राहितः, D. iv.;<BR>(4) बध्नाति<BR>(बन्ध्, c. 9.) (=c. in a trap, etc.),<BR>c. ing of<BR>elephants<BR>कुञ्जरबन्धनम्, Nil.<BR>II Of fire: उप-<BR>गच्छति (गम्, c. l.)<BR>or<BR>उपैति (इ, c. 2.),<BR>all of<BR>them caught fire and died<BR>सर्व एव ज्वलनमुपगता<BR> उपरताश्च, Mu. ii.<BR>III Of disease:<BR>to c. a<BR>disease<BR>व्याधिमधिगच्छति (गम्, c. l.), अवाप्नोति<BR>(आप्, c. 5.), etc., Śr.<BR>IV To ensnare:<BR>Perh. धरति। V. To charm: q. v.<BR>VI To<BR>overtake: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

catch
CATCH (v. i.): लगति (लग्, c. l):<BR>my garland<BR>has caught in the branch<BR>विटपे वैजयन्तिका मे लग्ना,<BR>Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

catch
