caterwauling
CATERWAULING: मेमेयितम् (?): विडालरुतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cates
CATES: v. Dainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

catgut
CATGUT: v. String, rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cathertic
CATHERTIC: v. Purgative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cathedral
CATHEDRAL: प्रधानधर्ममन्दिरम् (?): v. Church.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

catheter
CATHETER: *मूत्राकर्षिणी; मूत्रनिष्कर्षकयन्त्रविशेषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

catholic
CATHOLIC (adj.):<BR>I Universal: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Liberal: q. v.<BR>III Belonging to Roman<BR>c. s: expr. by gen. or comp.:<BR>c. emancipa-<BR>tion<BR>*रोमकधर्मिणां मोक्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

catholic
CATHOLIC (subs.): i. e. Roman-c.: *रोमक-<BR>धर्मिन् (f. णी)<BR>or<BR>रोमकधर्मावलम्बिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

catholicism
CATHOLICISM:<BR>I Liberality: q. v.<BR>II Roman<BR>-c.: *रोभकधर्मः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

catkin
CATKIN: *विडालपुच्छम्; विडालपुच्छाकारं प्रसूनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

catonian
CATONIAN:<BR>I Lit.: *कैटवः (वी, वं).<BR>II Grave,<BR>severe: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cats-eye
CAT'S-EYE: A stone: वैदुर्यम्, Si. iii. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cattle
CATTLE:<BR>I The bovine species: गावः (m. pl.),<BR>c. range<BR>गोचरः, Ki.;<BR>herd af c.<BR>गोकुलम्, V. p.;<BR>c.-<BR>keeper<BR>गोपः, Ki.;<BR>c. -path<BR>गोवाटः, Ga.<BR>II In a<BR>wider sense, including sheep, etc.:<BR>(1)<BR>पशवः (m. pl.),<BR>breeding of c.<BR>पाशुपाल्यम्, M.;<BR>to graze c.<BR>पशून् चारयति, B. p.;<BR>(2) गोमेषादयः<BR>(m. pl.),<BR>c. show<BR>*गोमेषादिमेला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

caudle
CAUDLE (subs.): अण्डादिमिश्रितमद्यमयः पानीयभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

caul
CAUL:<BR>I A veil: q. v.: अवगुण्ठनम्।<BR>II The<BR>omentum: q. v. मेदोधरा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cauliflower
CAULIFLOWER:<BR>I The plant: कबिपुष्पः;<BR>शाकभेदः।<BR>II The flower: *कबिपुष्पम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

causal
CAUSAL:<BR>(1) हेत्वर्थकः (का, कं) (as a c. con-<BR>junction);<BR>(2) हेतुमत् (f. ती) (of c. verbs),<BR>Paṇini;<BR>(3) णिजन्तः (न्त, न्ता) (=ending in<BR>णिच्: of Sanskrit c. verbs.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

causality
CAUSALITY: (कारणस्य) कार्योत्पादिका शक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

causation
CAUSATION:<BR>I Causality: expr. by कारणम्<BR>II The act of causing: V. Cause, pro-<BR>-duction, creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

causative
CAUSATIVE:<BR>I Causal: q. v.<BR>II Causing<BR>जनयितृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cause
CAUSE (subs.):<BR>I That which produces<BR>effect: कारणं,<BR>you are the c. of all element<BR>c. s<BR>त्वं कारणं कारणकारणानाम्, Ki. Primary c.:<BR>आदिकारणम्;<BR>(2) निदानम्, R. iii.<BR>I Material<BR>समवायिकारणम्,<BR>Efficient c.<BR>निमित्तम्<BR>or<BR>निमित्तकार<BR>II That which is the occasion of<BR>action: कारणम्,<BR>without any c.<BR>अकारणम्:<BR>Reason, ground.<BR>III A lawsuit: q. v.:<BR>कार्यम्, tell (us)<BR>that c.<BR>तत्कार्यं कथय। Mr. ix.<BR>IV Object, side: q. v. कार्यम्,<BR>our c. is all but<BR>undertaken by you<BR>कार्यं त्वया नः प्रतिपन्नकल्पम्, Ku.<BR>iii. 14; in the Śudra's (Chandragupta's c.<BR>वृषलस्य कृते, Mu.: v. For the sake of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cause
CAUSE (v. t.):<BR>(1) Often by a causal verb:<BR>to cause pain<BR>व्यथयति (c. of व्यथ्); to c.<BR>आनन्दयति (c. of नन्द्);<BR>to c. to fall<BR>पातयति<BR>of पत्);<BR>(2) जनयति (c. of जन्) (=produce,<BR>create). even an iota of master's favour<BR>arrogance among unsteady (people) जनयति<BR> प्रभुप्रसादलवोऽपि प्रागल्भ्यमधीरप्रकृतेः, K.;<BR>(3)<BR>circumlo.:<BR>this will c. his death<BR>अनेन तस्य<BR> भविष्यति;<BR>ascertaining that the dropping of<BR>arched gateway will c. his own destruction<BR>तो<BR> पातमात्मविनाशफलमवधार्य, Mu. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

causeless
CAUSELESS:<BR>I Uncaused:<BR>(1) expr.<BR>circumlo.,<BR>you are c.<BR>न ते किञ्चित् कारणम<BR>M. n.;<BR>(2) अकारणः (f. णा) (rare), M.<BR>(3) अयोनि (mfn.),<BR>you are the cause of<BR>world, but yourself c.<BR>जगद्योनिरयोनिस्त्वम्,<BR>I [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">Page109</a>]<BR>ii. 9.<BR>II Groundless: q. v.: निष्कारणः<BR>(णा, णं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

causelessly
CAUSELESSLY:<BR>(1) अकारणम्;<BR>(2) निष्कारणम्;<BR>(3) निर्निमित्तम्;<BR>(4) अहेतुकम्;<BR>(5) निष्प्रयोजनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

causer
CAUSER:<BR>(1) कर्तृ (f. त्री):<BR>(2) विधातृ (f. त्री);<BR>(3) सम्पादयितृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

causeway
CAUSEWAY:<BR>(1) सेतुः;<BR>(2) आलिः (f.);<BR>(3)<BR>पिण्डिलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

caustic
CAUSTIC (subs.):<BR>I<BR>Lunar c.:<BR>*अपानाम्ल-<BR>संश्लिष्टरजतम्, कष्टिकम्।<BR>II In the wider sense:<BR>दाहकपदार्धः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

caustic
CAUSTIC (adj.):<BR>I Burning, corrosive: विदा-<BR>हिन् (f. नी).<BR>II Severe, sarcastic: q. v.:<BR>मर्मच्छिद् (mfn.), Ki. xi. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cauterization
CAUTERIZATION:<BR>(1) दाहः;<BR>(2) दहनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cauterize
CAUTERIZE: (तप्तलोहादिना व्याधितमांसादि) दहति<BR>(दह्, c. l).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cautery
CAUTERY: दाहः<BR>or<BR>दहनम्।<BR>Actual c.<BR>*यथार्थदाहः;<BR>potential c.<BR>*तेजोदाहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

caution
CAUTION (subs.):<BR>I Wariness:<BR>(1) समीक्षा<BR>(circumspection),<BR>to use c. in any work<BR>समीक्ष्य<BR> कार्यं करोति;<BR>(2) अप्रमादः (=care);<BR>(3) साव-<BR>धानता। (=attention).<BR>II Guarantee, secu-<BR>-rity: q. v.<BR>III Warning: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

caution
CAUTION (v.) v. To warn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cautious
CAUTIOUS (adj.):<BR>(1) सावधानः (ना, नं);<BR>(2)<BR>अप्रमत्तः (त्ता, त्तं): v. Circumspect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cautiously
CAUTIOUSLY:<BR>(1) सावधानम्;<BR>(2) अप्रमत्तम्;<BR>(3)<BR>समीक्ष्य (=circumspectly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cautiousness
CAUTIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) सावधानता;<BR>(2) अप्रमत्तता;<BR>(3) समीक्ष्यकारिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cavalcade
CAVALCADE: अश्वारोहिणः (m. pl.) (=horse-<BR>-men): v. Also procession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cavalier
CAVALIER:<BR>I A horseman: q. v.: अश्वारोहिन्<BR>(m.).<BR>II Of Charles I.: नागरः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cavalierly
CAVALIERLY: सगर्वम्: v. Haughtily, disdain-<BR>-fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cavalry
CAVALRY:<BR>(1) वाजिसैन्यम्, M. n., तुरगबलम्, K.<BR>and sim. comp. s;<BR>(2) अश्वारोहिणः (m. pl.)<BR>and sim. terms (=horse-soldiers);<BR>(3)<BR>अश्वारोहिसैन्यम् and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cave
CAVE, CAVERN:<BR>I Natural:<BR>(1) गुहा,<BR>entered<BR>the great c.<BR>प्रविवेश महागुहाम्, V. p.;<BR>(2) गह्वरम्;<BR>(3) कन्दरः (री, रं);<BR>(4) दरी<BR>or<BR>दरिः।<BR>II Den,<BR>c a y: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

caveat
CAVEAT: A notice: *विज्ञापनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

caverned
CAVERNED;<BR>I Cavernous: q. v.<BR>II Living<BR>in a cavern: गुहाशयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cavernous
CAVERNOUS: बहुगुहः (हा, हं) and sim comp. s<BR>c: v. Cavern, full of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

caviar
CAVIAR, CAVIARE: लावणमत्स्याण्डम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cavil
CAVIL (v.):<BR>(1) मिथ्यादोषमारोपयति (c. of रुड्);<BR>(2) अवक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6): v. To censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cavil
CAVIL (subs.): मिथ्यादोषारोपणम्: v. Censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

caviller
CAVILLER: मिथ्यादोषारोपकः: v. Censurer,<BR>carper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cavity
CAVITY:<BR>(1) छिद्रम्;<BR>(2) रन्ध्रम्;<BR>(3) गर्तः<BR>(=hole).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

caw
CAW (v.):<BR>(1) काकायते (nomi.), Mr. v.;<BR>(2) कायति (के, c. l) (=to make noise: q. v.).<BR>C. ing:<BR>(1) काकरुतम्;<BR>(2) काकायितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cease
CEASE (v. i.):<BR>(1) विरमति (रम्, c. l) (with<BR>abl.),<BR>c. ing to weep<BR>विलापाद् विरता, R. xiv.<BR>71;<BR>when the lion c. d<BR>विरते मृगेन्द्रे, R. ii. 57;<BR>(2) शाम्यति, प्र-, उप-, (शम्, c. 4) (=to be<BR>over),<BR>when the rain c. d,<BR>शान्ते पानीयवर्षे, H.<BR>iii.; saying this, (he)<BR>c. d<BR>एतावदभिधायोपशशाम,<BR>K.;<BR>(3) विश्राम्यति (श्रम्, c. 4) (=to c. for a<BR>time),<BR>whose flowers have c. d to come out<BR>विश्रा-<BR>न्तपुष्पोद्गमा, V. iv.;<BR>(4) जहाति (हा, c. 3)<BR>(=to leave off, abandon: q. v.),<BR>c. to thirst<BR>after money<BR>जहीहि धनागमतृष्णाम्, J.;<BR>(5) by the<BR>use of the negative,<BR>c. to grieve<BR>मा व्यथिष्ठाः,<BR>R. xiv. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cease
CEASE (v. t.): v. To stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ceaseless
CEASELESS: अनवरतः (ता, तं): v. Perpetual,<BR>constant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ceaselessly
CEASELESSLY: अनवरतम्: v. Incessantly, per-<BR>-petually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cedar
CEDAR: वृक्षविशेषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cede
CEDE: उत्सृजति (सृज्, c. 6): v. To give up,<BR>yield, surrender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ceiling
CEILING: अन्तःपटलः, Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

celandine
CELANDINE: अर्कवृक्षः: v. Swallow-wort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

celebrate
CELEBRATE (v. t.):<BR>I To extol:<BR>(1) कीर्तयति,<BR>(कीर्त्, c. 10),<BR>to c. one's adventures<BR>चरितानि कीर्त- [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">Page110</a>]<BR>यति, Ki.;<BR>(2) गायति, उप-, (गै, c. 1) (in verse or<BR>song),<BR>may your fame be c. d by distinguished<BR>men<BR>श्लोकः प्रशस्तचरितैरुपगीयतां ते, Vi. vii.;<BR>(3) प्रथयति: v. Known, to make.<BR>II To<BR>solemnize:<BR>(1) अमिनन्दयति (नन्द्, c. l),<BR>c d<BR>my birth with a festival<BR>महोत्सवेन मम जन्माभि-<BR>नन्दितवान्, K.;<BR>(2) अनुतिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1) (=to<BR>perform: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

celebrated
CELEBRATED:<BR>(1) प्रथितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) ख्यातः,<BR> वि-, (ता, तं);<BR>(3) विश्रुतः (ता, तं): v. Famous,<BR>renowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

celebration
CELEBRATION:<BR>I A praising: कीर्तनम्: v. To<BR>celebrate, praise.<BR>II Solemnization<BR>(1)<BR>अभिनन्दनम्;<BR>(2) अनुष्ठानम् (=performance:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

celebrity
CELEBRITY;<BR>I Fame, renown: q. v. Ph.:<BR>of<BR>c.<BR>विख्यातः (ता, तं).<BR>II A man of c.:<BR>विख्यातलोकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

celerity
CELERITY:<BR>(1) वेगः;<BR>(2) जवः: v. Speed,<BR>quickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

celery
CELERY: शाकप्रभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

celestial
CELESTIAL: दिव्यः (व्या, व्यं): v. Heavenly,<BR>divine. Ph.:<BR>c. sphere:<BR>खगोलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

celebacy
CELEBACY: अनुद्वाहः; and sim. comp. s: v.<BR>Marriage.<BR>Living in c.<BR>अकृतदारपरिग्रहः; and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cell
CELL:<BR>I A small cavity: q. v.: गर्तः।<BR>II A<BR>small apartment:<BR>(1) क्षुद्रकक्षः;<BR>(2) गुप्तिः<BR>(of prisoners), Mr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cellar
CELLAR:<BR>(1) गुप्तिः;<BR>(2) भूमिगृहम्, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cellarer
CELLARER, CELLARIST: गुप्तिपालः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cellular
CELLULAR: *छिद्रमयः (यी, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cement
CEMENT (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: लेपः: v. Mortar,<BR>glue.<BR>II Fig.: बन्धनम्: v. Bond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cement
CEMENT (v.): घटयति (घट्। c. 10): v. To glue,<BR>to unite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cemetery
CEMETERY:<BR>(1) परेतावासः;<BR>(2) प्रेतवनम्;<BR>(3)<BR>पितृकाननम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cenobite
CENOBITE: विहारवासिन् (f. नी): v. Monk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cenotaph
CENOTAPH: *स्मरणस्तम्भः; (fully) अनिहितप्रेतः<BR> स्मरणस्तम्भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cense
CENSE (v.): वासयति (c. of वस्): v. To per-<BR>-fume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

censer
CENSER:<BR>I For burning incense: धूषाधारः (?).<BR>II A bottle: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

censor
CENSOR:<BR>I A Roman magistrate: *करनिधातृ<BR>(m.).<BR>II A captious critic: Perh. परीक्षकः.<BR>III A public officer to examine manus-<BR>-cripts: *ग्रन्थपरीक्षकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

censorious
CENSORIOUS:<BR>(1) दोषदर्शिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) दोषैव<BR> दृश् (mfn.);<BR>(3) पुरोभागिन् (f. नी);<BR>(4) निन्द<BR> व्रतिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

censoriousness
CENSORIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) दोषदर्शिता;<BR>(2) पुरोभागिता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

censorship
CENSORSHIP:<BR>I Of the Roman censors :<BR>*करनिधातृपदम्।<BR>II Of the examiners of<BR>manuscripts: *ग्रन्यपरीक्षकपदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

censurable
CENSURABLE: निन्द्यः (f. न्द्या), निन्दनीयः (या, यं)<BR>or<BR>निन्दार्हः (f. र्हा): v. Faulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

censurably
CENSURABLY: expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

censure
CENSURE (subs.):<BR>(1) निन्दा (=blame):<BR>(2)<BR>उपालम्भः (=reproach),<BR>I have received this c.<BR>from Your Highness<BR>मया कुमारादयमुपालम्भोऽधिगत<BR>Mu. v.;<BR>(3) भर्त्सना (reproof);<BR>(4) तिर<BR> स्कारः (=abuse, rebuke);<BR>(5) गर्हा (rare in<BR>this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

censure
CENSURE (v. t.):<BR>(1) निन्दति, वि-, प्र-, (निन्द्, c. l.)<BR>(=to blame),<BR>c. d her figure<BR>निनिन्द तस्या रूपम्<BR>Ku. v. 10;<BR>(2) उपालभते (लभ्, c. l.) (=to re<BR>proach),<BR>do not c. me for faults already commi-<BR>tted<BR>मोपालब्धाः कृतैर्दोषैः, B. xv. 20.;<BR>(3) भर्त्स<BR> यति, -ते, निर्-, (भर्त्स्, c. 10) (=to reprove)<BR>c. this wicked (cupid) निर्भत्स्य तामयं दुराचारः, Ki.<BR>(4) धिक्करोति (कृ, c. 8) (=to say “shame”)<BR>act in a way that you will not be blamed by good<BR>men or c. d by your elders<BR>तथा प्रयतेथा यथा न निन्द्यसे<BR> साधुमिः न धिक्क्रियसे गुरुमिः, K.;<BR>(5) तिरस्करोति<BR>(=to abuse);<BR>why have I been c. d without<BR>any fault<BR>किमित्यदोषेण तिरस्कृता वयम्, Ki. xiv<BR>11.;<BR>(6) गर्हयति (गर्ह्, c. 10) (censure mixed<BR>with abhorrence), N. i. 131;<BR>(7) जुगुप्सते<BR>(from गुप्) (6), B. xv. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

censurer
CENSURER:<BR>(1) निन्दकः;<BR>(2) उपालब्धृ (m.);<BR>(3)<BR>भर्त्सनाकारिन् (m.);<BR>(4) better expr. by the<BR>verb: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

census
CENSUS:<BR>(1) प्रजासंख्यानिरूपणम् (?);<BR>(2) लोकसंख्या-<BR>निर्धारणम् (?).<BR>To take a c.<BR>प्रजानां संख्यां [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=111" target="_blank">Page111</a>]<BR>निरूपयति (रूप्, c. 10)<BR>or<BR>निर्धारयति (धृ, c.<BR>10) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cent
CENT: Ph.<BR>Interest at two, three, four, five per c.<BR>per annum<BR>द्विकं, त्रिकं, चतुष्कं, पञ्चकं शतं वार्षिकी वृद्धिः or<BR>वर्धे वर्षे द्वित्रिचतुःपञ्चकं शतं वृद्धिः, M.;<BR>our profits are<BR>100 per c.<BR>द्विगुणा नो लाभाः, (after M. n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

centaur
CENTAUR: *नराश्वः (after नरसिंहः);<BR>or<BR>*अश्व-<BR>शरीरः (after अश्वमुखः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

centaury
CENTAURY: ओषधिविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

centenarian
