CHIVALROUSLY: v. Boldly, gallantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

chivalry
CHIVALRY:<BR>I A body of knights: सादिनः<BR>(m. pl.): v. Knight.<BR>II Knighthood:<BR>q. v.<BR>III Valour, etc.: शौर्यदाक्षिण्यादिगुणाः<BR>(m. pl.) (?): v. Valour, gallantry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

chive
CHIVE:<BR>I A kind of onion: q. v.<BR>II Stamen:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

chlorate
CHLORATE: *पीतहरिताम्लसंश्लिष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

