civilly
CIVILLY: v. Politely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

clad in
CLAD IN:<BR>(1) वसानः (ना, नं) (with acc.);<BR>(2) परिदधत् (f. ती) (with acc);<BR>(3) बिभ्रत् (f. ती)<BR>(with acc.);<BR>(4) by a comp. with वीत,<BR> संवीत, etc. (=covered),<BR>c. clean bark:<BR>शुचि-<BR>वल्कवीतवपुस् (mfn.), Ki. vi. 31.: v. To<BR>clothe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

claim
CLAIM (v. t.): expr. by circum.:<BR>who c. s.<BR>anything:<BR>ममेदमिति यो ब्रूयात्, M. viii. 31.;<BR>the owners of the two mares went up to the king,<BR>both claiming (the colt): मदीयोऽयं मदीयोऽयमिति<BR>(ब्रुवाणौ) वडवाधिपती राजान्तिकमगच्छताम्, Raj.;<BR>c. s. a bow from him:<BR>ममानेन धनुर्देयमिति<BR> निर्दिशति, K. b.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

claim
CLAIM (subs.):<BR>(1) expr. by verb;<BR>(2) उक्तम्<BR>(when the context fixes the meaning),<BR>to<BR>establish one's c.:<BR>उक्तं प्रतिपादयति, K. b.;<BR>(3)<BR>अभियोगः (legal c.): v. Demand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

claimant
CLAIMANT, CLAIMER:<BR>(1) अर्थिन् (m.) (=plain-<BR>-tiff);<BR>(2) by circum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

clamber
CLAMBER: v. To climb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

clamminess
CLAMMINESS, CLAMMY: v. Viscidity, viscous;<BR>glutinousness, glutinous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

clamorous
CLAMOROUS: Noisy, Turbulent. Ph.<BR>c. for<BR>his banishment:<BR>तस्य निर्वासनार्थमुत्क्रोशन्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

clamour
CLAMOUR (subs.): उत्क्रोशः: v. Noise, cry (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

clamour
CLAMOUR (v.) उत्क्रोशति (क्रुश्, c. l.): v. To<BR>shout, make noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

clamp
CLAMP (subs.): कीलः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

clamp
