cornet
CORNET:<BR>I A wind instrument: काहलः<BR>II<BR>A cavalry officer: वैजयन्तिकः (=standard<BR>bearer: q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cornice
CORNICE: चूडा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cornucopia
CORNUCOPIA: *श्रीशृङ्गम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corny
CORNY:<BR>I Lit.: धान्यमयः (यी, यं).<BR>II Horny:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corolla
COROLLA: गर्मदलम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corollary
COROLLARY: अनुमानम्, K. d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

coronation
CORONATION: अभिषेकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

coroner
CORONER: शवपरीक्षकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

coronet
CORONET: An inferior crown: v. Crown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corporal
CORPORAL (subs.): An officer in the army:<BR>*अधियोधः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corporal
CORPORAL (adj.):<BR>(1) कायिकः (की, कं);<BR>(2)<BR>शारीरिकः (की, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corporate
CORPORATE: Ph.: c. body: v. Corporation;<BR>c. town: v. Municipality;<BR>c. property<BR>*सम-<BR>वायस्य सम्पत्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corporation
CORPORATION: समवायः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corporeal
CORPOREAL:<BR>I Having a body:<BR>(1) देहिन्<BR>(f. नी);<BR>(2) शरीरिन् (f. णी);<BR>(3) शरीरभाज्<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(4) वपुष्मत् (f. ती);<BR>(5) विग्रहवत्<BR>(f. ती) (rare).<BR>II Material: q. v. Ph.: c.<BR>frame: v. Body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corps
CORPS: दलम् (?): v. Company (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corpse
CORPSE:<BR>(1) शव (mn.);<BR>(2) कुणप (mn.) (rare):<BR>v. Dead and body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corpulence
CORPULENCE:<BR>(1) पीनता;<BR>(2) स्थूलताः v. Fat-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corpulent
CORPULENT:<BR>(1) पीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) स्थूलः (ला,<BR> लं): v. Fat, stout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corpuscle
CORPUSCLE: परमाणुः: v. Atom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corpuscular
CORPUSCULAR: expr. by comp.,<BR>c. theory:<BR>पर-<BR>माणुवादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

correct
CORRECT (adj.):<BR>(1) शुद्धः (द्धा, द्धं), वि-, परि-;<BR>(2) अभ्रान्तः (न्ता, न्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

correct
CORRECT (v.):<BR>I To amend: शोधयति, परि-,<BR> सं-, (c. of शुध्),<BR>c. ing Śudras:<BR>वृषलान् संशोधयित्वा,<BR>Mat.<BR>II To remove: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

correction
CORRECTION: शोधनं<BR>or<BR>शुद्धिः, वि-, परि-, सं-, its c.<BR>तस्य विशुद्धिः, Tārānātha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corrective
CORRECTIVE:<BR>(1) शोधकः (धिका, धिकं);<BR>(2)<BR>शोधनः (नी, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

correctly
CORRECTLY:<BR>(1) शुद्धम्;<BR>(2) अभ्रान्तम्;<BR>(3) अञ्जसा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

correctness
CORRECTNESS: शुद्धता, वि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corrector
CORRECTOR: शोधकः, वि-, परि-, सं-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

correlation
CORRELATION: परस्परसम्बन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

correlative
CORRELATIVE: परस्परसम्बद्धः (द्धा, द्धं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

correspond
CORRESPOND:<BR>I To fit.: expr. by adj. s:<BR>अनुरूपः (पा, पं)<BR>or<BR>सदृशः (शी, शं).<BR>II To<BR>agree: q. v. संवदति (वद्, c. l.).<BR>III By<BR>letter: *पत्रेण संवादं करोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

correspondence
CORRESPONDENCE:<BR>I Fitness, congruity:<BR>q. v.: अनुरूपता।<BR>II By letter: पत्रसंवादः।<BR>III<BR>Letters: पत्राणि (n. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

correspondent
CORRESPONDENT:<BR>I Subs.: पत्रप्रेरकः or by<BR>circum.,<BR>he has many London c. s:<BR>*लण्डनाद्-<BR>बहवस्तं पत्राणि लिखन्ति<BR>or<BR>प्रेरयन्ति।<BR>II Adj.: v.<BR>Corresponding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corresponding
CORRESPONDING (adj.):<BR>I Agreement: संवादिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR>II By letter: पत्रसंवादिन् (f. नी)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corridor
CORRIDOR: v. Gallery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corrigible
CORRIGIBLE: शोधनीयः (या, यं), वि-, परि-, सं-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corroborate
CORROBORATE: द्रढयति (nomi.): v. To con-<BR>-firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corroboration
CORROBORATION: i. e. the act of corrobora-<BR>-ting or that which c. s: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corroborative
CORROBORATIVE: expr. by verb,<BR>this is c. of<BR>his guilt:<BR>एतत्तस्यापराधं द्रढयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corrode
CORRODE: क्षिणोति (क्षि, c. 5.) (?); खादति<BR>(खाद्, c. l.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corrosive
CORROSIVE: क्षयकरः (री, रं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corrupt
CORRUPT (v. i.): i. e., to rot: पूतीभवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corrupt
CORRUPT (v. t.):<BR>I To putrefy: पूतीकरोति (कृ,<BR>c. 8.).<BR>II To vitiate:<BR>(1) दूषयति (c. of दुष्),<BR>to<BR>c. a virgin:<BR>कन्यां दूषयति, M.;<BR>(2) नाशयति (c. of<BR>नश्) (=to destroy),<BR>great addiction to sensual<BR>pleasures c. s men:<BR>नाशयति पुरुषमत्यासङ्गो विषयेषु,<BR>K.;<BR>(3) पातयति (c. of पत्) (to cause to fall<BR>from), for c. ing the character of noble ladies:<BR>कुलवधूनां शीलपातने, D.;<BR>(4) विकरोति (कृ, c. 8.),<BR>whose minds are not c. ed in presence of c. ing<BR>agencies:<BR>विकारहेतौ सति विक्रियन्ते येपांन चेतांसि, Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corrupt
CORRUPT (adj.):<BR>I Rotten: पूति (mfn.).<BR>II Spoiled, depraved: नष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं).<BR>III<BR>Incorrect: भ्रान्तः (न्ता, न्तं).<BR>IV Impure:<BR>अशुचि (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corrupter
CORRUPTER:<BR>(1) दूषकः;<BR>(2) नाशकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corruptible
CORRUPTIBLE:<BR>I Subject to decay:<BR>(1)<BR>नश्वरः, वि-, (रा, रं);<BR>(2) नाशिन् (f. नी), वि-;<BR>(2) ध्वंसिन् (f. नी), वि-।<BR>II Capable of being<BR>vitiated: expr. by verb. Ph.: c. by money:<BR>धनदानेन भेद्यः (द्या, द्यं), K. b.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corruption
CORRUPTION:<BR>I Putrescence: q. v.<BR>II Pus:<BR>q. v.<BR>III Vitiating:<BR>(1) दूषणम्;<BR>(2) नाशनम्;<BR>(3) पातनम्।<BR>IV Depravity, impurity: q. v.<BR>Ph.:<BR>“c. of blood”:<BR>अधिकारलोपः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corruptly
CORRUPTLY: expr. by adj. or circum.,<BR>to<BR>decree and dismiss c.:<BR>*नष्टः<BR>or<BR>धनेन भिन्नः<BR> जयपराजयौ विदधाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corruptness
CORRUPTNESS:<BR>I The state: नष्टता।<BR>II De-<BR>-pravity, impurity: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corsair
CORSAIR:<BR>I A pirate: q. v.<BR>II A piratical<BR>vessel: दस्युपोतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corse
CORSE: शवः: v. Corpse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corselet
CORSELET:<BR>(1) कवचः;<BR>(2) उरश्छदः;<BR>(3) उर-<BR>स्त्राणम्;<BR>(4) चोलकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corset
CORSET:<BR>(1) चोलः;<BR>(2) कूर्पासकः: v. Bodice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cortege
CORTEGE:<BR>(1) परिजनाः (m. pl.);<BR>(2) परिवर्हः:<BR>v. Retinue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

coruscation
CORUSCATION:<BR>(1) छटा;<BR>(2) स्फुरितम्: v.<BR>Flash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

corvette
CORVETTE:<BR>(1) रणपोतविशेषः;<BR>(2) वहित्रम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cosmetic
COSMETIC:<BR>(1) कान्तिदः (दा, दं);<BR>(2) कान्ति-<BR>वर्धकः (का, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cosmogony
COSMOGONY: *जगदुद्भवतत्त्वम्, and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cosmography
COSMOGRAPHY:<BR>(1) *विश्वविवरणम्;<BR>(2) *जगद्-<BR> -वर्णनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cosmopolite
COSMOPOLITE: यः (या, यं) समभावेन सर्वदेशवासिनः<BR> पश्यति; *वैश्वानरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cost
COST (subs.):<BR>I Price: q. v.: सूल्यम्।<BR>Expense: q. v.: व्ययः,<BR>even at the c. of one<BR>life:<BR>प्राणव्ययेनापि, H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cost
COST (v. t.):<BR>I Of price: Ph.:<BR>what did the<BR>book c. you:<BR>कियता मूल्येन त्वया पुस्तको गृहीतः,<BR>II Of expense: Ph.:<BR>it c. him much to repair<BR>the town:<BR>बहुधनव्ययेन नवीकृता नगरी। Ph.:<BR>though<BR>it c. me ten nights' watchings:<BR>दशरात्रिजागरणेनापि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

costermonger
COSTERMONGER: फलविक्रोताः v. Fruiterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

costive
COSTIVE:<BR>I Of medicines:<BR>(1) ग्राहिन् (f. णी<BR>सं-, Sr.;<BR>(2) विष्टम्मिन् (f. नी), Sr.<BR>II Of<BR>bowels, constipated: v. To constipate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

costiveness
COSTIVENESS:<BR>(1) आनाहः;<BR>(2) विड्बद्धताः<BR>Constipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

costliness
COSTLINESS:<BR>(1) बहुमूल्यता;<BR>(2) महार्घता;<BR>(3) महा-<BR> र्हता;<BR>(4) दुर्मूल्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

costly
COSTLY:<BR>(1) बहुमूल्यः (ल्या, ल्यं);<BR>(2) महार्घः र्घा,<BR>र्घं);<BR>(3) महार्हः (र्हा, र्हं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

costume
COSTUME: वेशः<BR>or<BR>वेषः,<BR>riding costume:<BR>तुरङ्गाधि-<BR> -रोहणोचितो वेशः, K.: v. Dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cot
COT:<BR>I A cottage: q. v.: कुटीरः।<BR>II A small<BR>bed: खट्टा<BR>or<BR>खट्टिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cotemporary
COTEMPORARY: v. Contemporary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cottage
COTTAGE:<BR>(1) कुटीरः;<BR>(2) उटजः;<BR>(3) पर्णशाला ;<BR>(4) तृणकुटी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cottager
COTTAGER: कुटीरवासिन् (m.): v. Peasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cotton
COTTON:<BR>I The plant: कार्पासी।<BR>II Its<BR>down-like substance:<BR>(1) कार्पासम्;<BR>(2) तूल<BR>(mn.);<BR>(3) पिचुलः।<BR>III Cloth made of<BR>cotton: कार्पासवस्त्रम्। Ph.: made of c.:<BR>(1)<BR>कार्पासः (सी, सं);<BR>(2) फालः (ली, लं). C. mill<BR>*कार्पासचक्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

couch
COUCH (subs.):<BR>(1) शय्या;<BR>(2) प्रस्तरः: v. Bed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

couch
COUCH (v. i.):<BR>I To lie down: q. v.: शेते<BR>(शी, c. 2.).<BR>II To hide: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

couch
COUCH (v. t.):<BR>I To lay down, place: q. v.<BR>II To express: ग्रथ्नाति (ग्रन्थ्, c. 9).<BR>III.<BR>To level a lance; v. To aim.<BR>IV To c. a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">Page157</a>]<BR>cataract:<BR>दृष्टिमण्डलजकफहरणाय शुक्लभागौ विध्यति<BR>(व्यध्, c. 4.), Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cough
COUGH (subs.): कासः<BR>or<BR>काशः,<BR>dry c.:<BR>शुष्ककासः<BR>(after Sr.);<BR>suffering from c.:<BR>काशिन् (f. नी),<BR>Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cough
COUGH (v. i.): कासते (कास्, c. l). C. up:<BR>उत्कासते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

coulter
COULTER:<BR>(1) फालः;<BR>(2) कुशी;<BR>(3) पोत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

council
COUNCIL<BR>(1) सभा (best equiv.),<BR>to hold a c.:<BR>समां<BR> करोति<BR>or<BR>कारयति (if held through another's<BR>instrumentality), H.;<BR>to break up a c.:<BR>सभा-<BR>भङ्गं करोति, H.;<BR>secret c.:<BR>गूढसभा; august c.:<BR>महासभा;<BR>(2) संसद्, (f.);<BR>(3) सदस् (n.);<BR>(4)<BR>समितिः,<BR>addressed the c.:<BR>समितिं बभाषे, B. C.<BR>chamber, C. room:<BR>(1) by the above words,<BR>arrived at the c.:<BR>आसदत्सदः। Si.;<BR>(2) सभागृहम्,<BR>and sim. comp.;<BR>(3) इन्द्रकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

council-board
COUNCIL-BOARD:<BR>I Lit.: सभापीठम् (?).<BR>II<BR>Fig., = council: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

councillor
COUNCILLOR: Ph.:<BR>town-c.:<BR>पोरसभासद् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counsel
COUNSEL (subs.):<BR>I Consultation: q. v.:<BR>भन्त्रणा।<BR>II Deliberation, prudence: q. v.:<BR>विचारः।<BR>III Advice: q. v.: उपदेशः।<BR>IV<BR>Scheme, policy: उपायः। V. An advocate:<BR>q. v.: *धर्मोपदेष्ट्ट (f. ष्ट्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counsel
COUNSEL (v.): उपदिशति: v. To advise, con-<BR>-sult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counsellor
COUNSELLOR:<BR>I An adviser: q. v.<BR>II A<BR>councillor: मन्त्रिन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

count
COUNT (subs.):<BR>I A title: पदवीविशेषः; *कान्तः।<BR>II Counting: q. v.<BR>III Esteem: q. v.<BR>IV<BR>In law, *पादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

count
COUNT (v.):<BR>I Trans: गणयति, वि-, परि-, प्र-,<BR>(गण्, c. 10.) (lit. and fig.), c. ed lotus-leaves:<BR>कमलपत्राणि गणयामास Ku.: v. To reckon.<BR>II<BR>Intrans: गण्यते (pass. of गण्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

count on or upon
COUNT ON or UPON: गणयति, वि-, परि-,<BR>c. ing on<BR>success:<BR>फलनिष्पत्तिं विगणय्य, Ki. ii. 35.: v. To<BR>rely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

count out
COUNT OUT: संख्याति (ख्या, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

countenance
COUNTENANCE (subs.):<BR>I Face: q. v.: आननम्,<BR>“out of c.”: नताननः (ना, नं) (?).<BR>II Look,<BR>appearance:<BR>(1) आकारः;<BR>(2) आकृतिः।<BR>III<BR>Favour, encouragement: q. v.:<BR>To give c.<BR>to:<BR>अनुकूलयति (nomi.).<BR>IV Show, pretence:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

countenance
COUNTENANCE (v. t.): v. To favour, encour-<BR>-age, support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counter
COUNTER (subs.):<BR>I A piece of metal etc.<BR>used in reckoning: गुटिका (properly a small<BR>ball), Da.<BR>II A shop-c.: गणनाफलकम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counter
COUNTER (adj.): v. Contrary, opposite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counter to
COUNTER TO: v. Against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counteract
COUNTERACT:<BR>(1) निवारयति (वृ, c. 10) (=to<BR>prevent: q. v.);<BR>(2) मोधीकरोति (=frustrate:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counteraction
COUNTERACTION: प्रतिक्रिया (?): v. Hindrance,<BR>resistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counterbalance
COUNTERBALANCE (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: Ph.:<BR>when<BR>the weight c. s the man:<BR>प्रतिमानपुरुषौ समधृतौ,<BR>V. s.;<BR>being c. d:<BR>प्रतिमानसमीभूतः, Y.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>शमयति (c. of शम्) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counterchange
COUNTERCHANGE: v. Exchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counterfeit
COUNTERFEIT (adj.)):<BR>(1) कपट- in comp.,<BR>c.<BR>seal:<BR>कपटमुद्रा, Mu. v.;<BR>(2) कूट- in comp.,<BR>c.<BR>order:<BR>कूटशासनम्, M. ix. 232.;<BR>(3) कृत्रिमः (मा,<BR> मं)<BR>or<BR>कृतकः (का, कं) (=fabricated, forged),<BR>c. letter:<BR>कृतको लेखः, Mu. vi.: v. False, spuri-<BR>-ous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counterfeit
COUNTERFEIT (subs.):<BR>I In bad sense: expr.<BR>by the adj.: these c. s are well-fabricated:<BR>*सुकृतान्येतानि कपटद्रव्याणि।<BR>II Likeness, coun-<BR>-terpart: q. v.<BR>III A cheat, an impostor:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counterfeiter
COUNTERFEITER: A forger: कूटकर्मकर्तृ (m.),<BR>V. s.;<BR>c. of letters:<BR>कूटलेखकारः,<BR>V s.<BR>II An<BR>impostor: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

countermand
COUNTERMAND (v.): प्रत्यादिशति (दिश्, c. 6.):<BR>v. To revoke, contradict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

countermand
COUNTERMAND (subs.): प्रत्यादेशः: v. Revoca-<BR>-tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

countermarch
COUNTERMARCH (v.): प्रत्यावर्तते (वृत्, c. l.):<BR>v. To return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

countermark
COUNTERMARK (subs.): *प्रतिचिह्नम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

countermine
COUNTERMINE (subs.): प्रतिसुरङ्गम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

countermine
COUNTERMINE (v. t.): मोधीकरोति: v. Frustrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counternatural
COUNTERNATURAL: प्रकृतिविरुद्धः (द्धा, द्धं), and<BR>sim. comp. s: v. Natural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counterpane
COUNTERPANE: कुथः, K.: v. Coverlet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counterpart
COUNTERPART: प्रतिरूपम्: v. Duplicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counterplot
COUNTERPLOT (subs.): प्रतीपमन्त्रणा (?), and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counterpoise
COUNTERPOISE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: प्रतिमानं भवति<BR>(with gen.) (?).<BR>II Fig.: शमयति (c. of<BR>शम्) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counterpoise
COUNTERPOISE (subs.). प्रतिमानम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counterscarp
COUNTERSCARP (f.): परिखापर्यन्तः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

countersign
COUNTERSIGN (v. t.): *प्रति-लिखति (लिख्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

countersignature
COUNTERSIGNATURE: *प्रतिलेखः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counter-tenor
COUNTER-TENOR: तारस्वरः (?), Mr. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

countervail
COUNTERVAIL (v.): v. To equal, balance,<BR>compensate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

countess
COUNTESS: पदवीविशेषः; *कान्ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

counting
COUNTING (subs.): गणना।<BR>C. -house:<BR>गणना-<BR>गृहम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

countless
COUNTLESS: असङ्ग्य (f. ङ्गया): v. Innumerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

country
COUNTRY (subs.):<BR>I A tract of land:<BR>(1)<BR>देशः,<BR>one's own c.:<BR>स्वदेशः; I will leave this c.:<BR>देशमिमं जिहासामि, D. ii.;<BR>(2) राष्ट्रम्,<BR>among the<BR>c. s you have seen:<BR>भवदृष्टेषु राष्ट्रेषु, D. vi.;<BR>(3) विषयः;<BR>(4) जनपदः।<BR>II As opposed to<BR>town: ग्रामः (=village) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

country
COUNTRY (adj.):<BR>I As opposed to city:<BR>ग्राम्यः (म्या, म्यं),<BR>c. mouse:<BR>ग्राम्यभूषिकः; c. town:<BR>*ग्राम्यपत्तनम्<BR>or<BR>खर्वटम्;<BR>c. -house:<BR>*ग्राम्यभवनम्;<BR>to lead a c. life:<BR>ग्रामेषु जीवनमतिवाहयति (?).<BR>II<BR>Rude: q. v.: ग्राम्यः (म्या, म्यं).<BR>III Of a c.:<BR>देशीयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

country-folk
COUNTRY-FOLK:<BR>(1) ग्राम्यजनाः (m. pl.);<BR>(2)<BR>ग्राम्याः (m. pl.): v. Rustic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

countryman
COUNTRYMAN:<BR>I A rustic: q. v.<BR>II An<BR>inhabitant of a country: देशीयः (या, यं) or<BR>देशवासिन् (f. नी),<BR>one's own c.:<BR>स्वदेशीयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

county
COUNTY: प्रदेशः (?),<BR>c. town:<BR>पत्तनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

coup-de-main
COUP-DE-MAIN: Ph.:<BR>by c.:<BR>अतर्कितं द्रुततर-<BR>मवस्कन्द्य (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

coup-detat
COUP-D'ETAT: *आकस्मिकनीतिकौशलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

couple
COUPLE (subs.):<BR>I A pair: q. v.: युग्मम्।<BR>II<BR>Of animals:<BR>(1) मिथुनम्, c. s of the ruddy<BR>goose:<BR>मिथुनानि रथाङ्गनाम्नाम्, Ki.;<BR>(2) द्वन्द्वम्,<BR>in c.<BR>s:<BR>द्वन्द्वीभूय, A. r.;<BR>(3) दम्पती (m. dual) (man<BR>and wife);<BR>(4) वधूवरम् (a newly married<BR>c.), Ku.<BR>III A bond or leash: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

couple
COUPLE (v. i.): संयोजयति (युज्, c. 10): v. To<BR>join.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

couple
COUPLE (v. i.): To copulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

couplet
COUPLET: पंक्तिद्वयम् (?).<BR>C. of two slokas:<BR>युग्मकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

courage
COURAGE:<BR>(1) शौर्यम् (=valour);<BR>(2) निर्भीकता<BR>(=intrepidity);<BR>(3) साहसम् (= boldness).<BR>To lose c.:<BR>सत्वात् परिभ्रश्यते, Mr.<BR>To inspire<BR>with c.:<BR>उत्साहयति (c. of सह्), Ku. xv. 51.<BR>To take c.:<BR>सम्-आश्वसिति (श्वस्, c. 2), Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

courageous
COURAGEOUS: v. Brave, valiant, intrepid,<BR>spirited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

courageously
COURAGEOUSLY: v. Bravely, valiantly, fear-<BR>-lessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

courier
COURIER:<BR>(1) जङ्घाकरिकः<BR>or<BR>जङ्घालः;<BR>(2) वार्तावहः<BR>(=any message-bearer);<BR>(3) लेखहारः (= letter<BR>carrier).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

course
COURSE (subs.):<BR>I Motion: q. v.:<BR>(1) गतिः,<BR>the c. of his chariot was not interrupted:<BR>गतिर्विजघ्न<BR> नहि तद्रथस्य। R. v. 27.;<BR>(2) प्रवाहः (=flowing<BR>c., as of rivers): Ph.:<BR>look, so the balloon bends<BR>its c.:<BR>प्रवर्तते पश्य तथा विमानम्, R.;<BR>directed the c.<BR>of the car towards the capital:<BR>राजधानीं रथस्यदस्य<BR> लक्ष्यीचकार, N.<BR>II Track, way: q. v.: मार्गः,<BR>c. of an arrow:<BR>मार्गणस्य मार्गः, Ki.<BR>III Race-<BR>-course: q. v.<BR>IV Method of procedure:<BR>गतिः,<BR>there being no other c.:<BR>गत्यन्तरामावात्, D.<BR>ii.;<BR>one who has no c. left:<BR>अगतिकः (का, कं), K.<BR>Ph.<BR>take to a sacred c.:<BR>पूतं भजस्व पन्थानम्, Vi.<BR>V Of lectures etc.: Ph.: a c. of lecture:<BR>*क्रमिकपाठाः।<BR>VI Of dishes: भोजनप्रकारः (or<BR>strictly) *भोजनक्रमः।<BR>VII The menstrual c.:<BR>ऋतुः।<BR>A woman in her c.:<BR>रजस्वला। Ph.:<BR>as a<BR>matter of c.:<BR>प्रकृत्या, U.: v. Naturally;<BR>he<BR>would of c. give his assent:<BR>स नियतमनुज्ञास्यति, Da.<BR>v. Indeed, certainly, undoubtedly; in the<BR>c. of, expr. by मध्ये or by loc. absol.;<BR>in the<BR>c. of conversation:<BR>कथाप्रसङ्गेन, K. i. 24<BR>or<BR>कथानु-<BR>कथनेन, N. v. 13;<BR>in the c. of time:<BR>गच्छति काले,<BR>K.<BR>or<BR>कालक्रमेण, Ku.;<BR>in due c.:<BR>क्रमेण, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

course
COURSE (v.):<BR>I To hunt, pursue: q. v.<BR>II<BR>To run: q. v.: धावति, प्र-, (धाव्, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

courser
COURSER:<BR>I A hunter: q. v.: जवनवाजिन् (m.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

court
COURT (subs.):<BR>I An enclosed space:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रकोष्ठः,<BR>a dwelling with eight c. s<BR>अष्टप्रकोष्ठकं भवनम्,<BR>Mr.;<BR>(2) चत्वरम् (a front c.): v. Yard.<BR>II A palace: q. v.: राजकुलम्,<BR>we will go and<BR>represent in the c.<BR>राजकुलं गत्वा निवेदयावः, Mr.<BR>II<BR>C. dress<BR>राजदर्शनोचितो वेशः, and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR>III The men about a king: राज-<BR>सन्निधिलोकाः (m. pl.), P.<BR>IV Their assembly:<BR>सभा,<BR>to hold a c.<BR>सभां करोति, Mah. V. Atten-<BR>-tion, civility: q. v.<BR>VI A c. of justice:<BR>(1) विचारालयः;<BR>(2) अधिकरणम्, Mr.;<BR>(3) व्यवहार-<BR>मण्डपः, Mr.;<BR>(4) धर्माधिकरणस्थानम्, P.<BR>VII A<BR>judge or judges:<BR>(1) अधिकरणिकः,<BR>this is to<BR>be asked by men, not by the c.:<BR>जनस्य प्रच्छनीयो-<BR>ऽयमर्थः, न पुनरधिकरणिकस्य, Mr.;<BR>(2) धर्माधिकारिन्<BR>(m),<BR>the c. said to him:<BR>धर्माधिकारिणस्तमूचुः, P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

court
COURT (v. t.):<BR>I To pay c. to: आराधयति (c.<BR>of राध्),<BR>c. ing the people:<BR>आराधनाय लोकानाम्,<BR>U.<BR>II To solicit, seek: q. v.<BR>III To<BR>woo: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

court-day
COURT-DAY: *व्यवहारदिनम्; अधिवेशनदिवसः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

court-martial
COURT-MARTIAL: *युद्धाधिकरणम्; योधविचारसभा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

courteous
COURTEOUS:<BR>(1) दक्षिणः (णा, णं) (=complai-<BR>-sant);<BR>(2) विनीतः (ता, तं) (=polite);<BR>(3)<BR>प्रियंवदः (दा, दं) (=affable);<BR>(4) सुजनः<BR>(=civil).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

courteously
COURTEOUSLY:<BR>(1) सविनयम्;<BR>(2) सप्रश्रयम्;<BR>(3)<BR>सौजन्येन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

courteousness
COURTEOUSNESS: v. Courtesy (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

courtesan
COURTESAN:<BR>(1) गणिका;<BR>(2) वाराङ्गना, and sim.<BR>comp. s;<BR>(3) वारविलासिनी।<BR>A chief c.<BR>वारमुख्या,<BR>Me. ii. 10: v. Prostitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

courtesy
COURTESY:<BR>I Courteousness:<BR>(1) दाक्षिण्यम्,<BR>by<BR>her politeness^1, c., and affability:<BR>तस्या विनयेन<BR> दाक्षिण्येन मधुरालापितया। K.;<BR>(2) विनयः;<BR>(3)<BR>प्रश्रयः,<BR>accepted with c.:<BR>सप्रश्रयं प्रतिजग्राह, K.;<BR>(4) सौजन्यम्। c., agreeable as free from arrogance:<BR>अपगताभिमानमधुरा सुजनता। K.<BR>II An act of c.:<BR>उपचारः,<BR>by c. s to the invited ladies:<BR>उपचारेण<BR> निमन्त्रितस्त्रीषु, C.<BR>III A bow: प्रणामः, R. vi. 25.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

courtier
COURTIER:<BR>I A member of a princely<BR>court:<BR>(1) राजसन्निधिलोकः;<BR>(2) राजवल्लभः;<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR>II A flatterer: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

courtly
COURTLY:<BR>I Relating to a court: expr. by<BR>comp.<BR>II Well-bred: q. v.<BR>III Obsequi-<BR>-ous: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

courtship
COURTSHIP: no equiv.: expr. by प्रणयः or<BR>आसक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

courtyard
COURTYARD:<BR>(1) अङ्गनम्;<BR>(2) प्राङ्गणम्;<BR>(3)<BR>चत्वरम्;<BR>(4) अजिरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cousin
COUSIN:<BR>(1) पितृव्यपुत्रः (f. त्री) (=father's bro-<BR>-ther's child);<BR>(2) पितृस्वस्त्रीयः (f. या) (=f.<BR>sister's c.);<BR>(3) मातृस्वस्त्रीयः (f. या) (=mother's<BR>s. c.);<BR>(4) मातुलपुत्रः (f. त्री) (=m. bro-<BR>-ther's c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cove
COVE: वङ्कः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

covenant
COVENANT (subs.): संविद् (f.): v. Agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

covenant
COVENANT (v.): संविदं करोति: v. To agree,<BR>bargain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cover
COVER (v. t.):<BR>I To overspread:<BR>(1) छादयति,<BR> आ-, समा-, प्र-, (छद्, c. 10.),<BR>c. him with this<BR>wrapper:<BR>अनेन प्रावारकेण छादयैनम्, Mr.; i.<BR>(2) आ-<BR>वृणोति, समा-, (rarely प्रा-, सं-, नि-,) (वृ, c. 5.),<BR>c. ed with darkness:<BR>तिमिरावृतः (ता, तं), M. n.;<BR>c. ed face:<BR>संवृतमुखम्, K.;<BR>(3) अपि-दधाति, पि-,<BR>(धा, c. 3.)<BR>c. ing his head with a wing:<BR>शिरः<BR> पिधाय पक्षेण, N.;<BR>(4) स्तृणाति<BR>or<BR>स्तृणोति (स्तृ<BR>or<BR>स्त्दृ,<BR>c. 9. and 5.) (rare),<BR>c. ed the ground with their<BR>hands:<BR>शिरोभिर्महीं तस्तार, R. iv. 63.;<BR>(5) आचिनोति,<BR> समा-, (चि, c. 5.) (rare),<BR>c. ed with bunches of<BR>flowers:<BR>कुसुमस्तवकाचितः (ता, तं);<BR>(6) उर्णौति, प्र-,<BR>(उर्णु, c. 2.) (rare), B.;<BR>(7) स्थगयति (स्थग्, c.<BR>10) (rare). Ph.:<BR>c. ed with wounds:<BR>क्षतविक्षतः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR>II To conceal: q. v.<BR>(1) आच्छायति,<BR> प्र-,<BR>by what means shall I c. this failing:<BR>केनोपायेन<BR> स्खलितमिदं प्रच्छादयमि, K.;<BR>(2) आ-वृणोति, सं-,<BR>M. n.;<BR>(3) पिदधाति, Si.<BR>C. ed way:<BR>छन्नपथः or<BR>गूढमार्गः।<BR>III To protect: q. v.: रक्षति (रक्ष,<BR>c. l.),<BR>to c. the rear:<BR>पृष्ठदेशं रक्षितुम्, M. n.<BR>IV<BR>To brood: आवृणोति (?). V. To be sufficient<BR>for: v. Sufficient.<BR>VI To include: q. v.<BR>VII To copulate with: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cover
COVER (subs.):<BR>I C. ing, lid: q. v. C. (of a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">Page160</a>]<BR>book) वेष्टनम्, C.<BR>II Fig., screen:<BR>(1) आवरणम्;<BR>(2) आच्छादनम्;<BR>(3) पिधानम्।<BR>III Shelter, pro-<BR>-tection: q. v.: expr. by verb, (women are)<BR>under c. of their father during their childhood:<BR>पिता रक्षति कौमारे, M. Ph.:<BR>under c. of the<BR>night:<BR>रात्रियोगेन।<BR>IV Pretext: q. v. V. For<BR>game: no equiv.: वनम्: v. Wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

covering
COVERING (subs.):<BR>(1) आवरणम्, c. of the body:<BR>देहावरणानि, Ki.;<BR>(2) आच्छादनम्,<BR>give me also<BR>your under-garment and c.:<BR>परिधानाच्छादनवस्त्रमपि<BR> समर्पय, P.;<BR>(3) पिधानम् (not used of clothes):<BR>v. Clothing, cloak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

coverlet
COVERLET:<BR>(1) उत्तरच्छदः;<BR>(2) प्रच्छदपटः;<BR>(3)<BR>उपर्यास्तरणवस्त्रम्, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

covert
COVERT (adj.):<BR>I Secret: q. v.: प्रच्छन्नः (न्ना,<BR> न्नं).<BR>II Protected, as a fence c.: रक्षितः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

covert
COVERT (subs.):<BR>I A shelter: q. v.<BR>II A<BR>thicket: q. v.<BR>III Of wings of birds:<BR>perh.: पक्षतिः, N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

covertly
COVERTLY: छन्नम्, D.: v. Secretly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

covet
COVET:<BR>(1) लुभ्यति, -ते (लुभ्, c. 4.) (with dat.)<BR>(in bad sense),<BR>yet Rama c. ed the stag:<BR>तथापि<BR> रामो लुलुभे मृगाय, H.;<BR>(2) स्पृहयति (स्पृह्, c. 10.)<BR>(=to long for, desire: q. v.). I c. this (child)<BR>स्फृहयाम्यस्मै। Sa. vii.;<BR>(3) गृध्यति (गृध्, c. l.)<BR>(rare),<BR>he who would c. me:<BR>यो मां गृध्येत Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

covetable
COVETABLE: स्पृहनीयः (या, यं): v. Desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

covetous
COVETOUS:<BR>I In bad sense:<BR>(1) लुब्ध (f. ब्धा),<BR>c. of riches:<BR>धनलुब्धः (f. ब्धा), H.; a c. man:<BR>लुब्धकः, P.;<BR>(2) लोभिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) लोभवत् (f.<BR>ती);<BR>(4) गृध्नु (mfn) (rare). Ph.:<BR>your mind<BR>is c.:<BR>तृष्णातरलं भवन्मनः, N. Very c.:<BR>(1)<BR>लोलुभः (भा, भं);<BR>(2) लोलुपः (पा, पं).<BR>II In<BR>good sense, = desirous: q. v.: लिप्सु (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

covetously
COVETOUSLY:<BR>(1) लोभात्;<BR>(2) लोभेन;<BR>(3)<BR>expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

covetousness
COVETOUSNESS: लोभः,<BR>c. creates thirst:<BR>लोभो<BR> जनयते तृषाम्, H.: v. Desire, avarice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

covey
COVEY: कुलम्: v. Flock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cow
COW (subs.): गो (mf.)<BR>c.' s milk:<BR>गोदुग्धम्;<BR>killing<BR>a c.:<BR>गोहत्या;<BR>milch c.:<BR>धेनुः। C. -dung:<BR>(1)<BR>गोमय (mn.);<BR>(2) गोविष् (f.).<BR>Dry c.:<BR>करीर (mn.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cow
COW (v.): v. To stupefy, terrify. C. ed down:<BR>(1) जडीभूतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) सन्त्रस्तः (स्ता, स्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cow herd
COW HERD:<BR>(1) गोपः;<BR>(2) वल्लवः;<BR>(3) आभीरः;<BR>(4) गोपालः। A station of c. s:<BR>(1) घोषः;<BR>(2)<BR>आभीरपल्लिः। C. ess:<BR>(1) गोपी;<BR>(2) वल्लवी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cow hide
COW HIDE:<BR>I Lit.: गोचर्मन् (n.).<BR>II A whip:<BR>गोचर्मनिर्मिता कशा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cow-house
COW-HOUSE, COW-PEN:<BR>(1) व्रजः;<BR>(2) गोष्ठम्;<BR>(3) गोशाला;<BR>(4) गोकुलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

coward
COWARD:<BR>(1) कापुरुषः H.;<BR>(2) भीरुः,<BR>whether<BR>he was a c. or a hero:<BR>स भीरुः शूरो वा, Ve iii.:<BR>v. Timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cowardice
COWARDICE:<BR>(1) भीरुता,<BR>from c.<BR>भीरुत्या, Mr.;<BR>(2) कातर्यम् (=timidity), simple policy is c.:<BR>कातर्यं केवला नीति।, R.;<BR>(3) कुविक्रमः (towards<BR>the weak),<BR>your c. to a poor bird:<BR>कुविक्रमं ते कृपणे<BR> पतत्रिणि, N.;<BR>(4) अपौरुषम् (=unmanliness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cowardly
COWARDLY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) भीरु (mfn.) v.<BR>Timid;<BR>(2) निर्वीर्यः (र्या, र्यं);<BR>(3) अपौरुषः<BR>(षा, षं): v. Unmanly.<BR>II Mean, base:<BR>q. v.: कृपणः (f. णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cower
COWER (v. i.): भयावनम्रशरीरः (रा, रं); भयावनतः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cowl
COWL: शिरस्कविशेषः: v. Head-dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cowship
COWSHIP: ओषधिभेदः; *गोकन्दः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

coxcomb
COXCOMB:<BR>I A fop: q. v.: दाम्भिकः (?).<BR>II<BR>A plant: मयूरचूडा<BR>or<BR>मयूरकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

coxcombry
COXCOMBRY:<BR>(1) नागरिकता (?);<BR>(2) दम्भः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

coy
COY: अप्रगल्भः (ल्भा, ल्भं): v. Modest, reserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

coyly
COYLY:<BR>(1) अविश्रम्भम् (=without confidence);<BR>(2) सव्रीडम् (=bashfully, modestly: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

coyness
COYNESS:<BR>(1) अविश्रम्भता (want of confidence),<BR>K.;<BR>(2) व्रीडा (=bashfulness, modesty:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cozen
COZEN: छलयति (छल्, c. 10.): v. To cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cozenage
COZENAGE: छलना: v. Cheating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cozily
COZILY: आरामेण<BR>or<BR>सारामम् (?): v. Comfortably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cozy
COZY: आराम-,<BR>c. seat:<BR>आरामासनम् (?): v.<BR>Comfortable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crab
CRAB:<BR>(1) कर्कटः;<BR>(2) कुलीरः। C., i. e. c. -apple:<BR>कपित्थः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crabbed
CRABBED<BR>I Harsh, cross: q. v.<BR>II Difficult,<BR>perplexing: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crabbedly
CRABBEDLY: v. Peevishly; with difficulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crabbedness
CRABBEDNESS: v. Peevishness; roughness;<BR>perplexity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crack
CRACK (v. i.):<BR>I To break into pieces: q. v:<BR>त्रुटति (त्रुट्, c. 6.).<BR>II To rattle: q. v.: विरैति<BR>(रु, c. 2.).<BR>III To boast: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crack
CRACK (v. t.):<BR>I To break, burst: q. v.:<BR>त्रोटयति (c. of त्रुट्).<BR>II To snap: q. v.:<BR>स्फोटयति, आ-, (c. of स्फुट्).<BR>III To puff:<BR>q. v. Ph.:<BR>to c. a joke:<BR>परिहासं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crack
CRACK (subs.):<BR>I Chink: छिद्रम्, c. in a wall:<BR>भित्तिच्छिद्रम्, Mu. ii.<BR>II A sound: q. v.:<BR>विरावः।<BR>III A crazy person: v. C.-brained.<BR>IV A boaster: q. v.: विकत्थिन् (m).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crack-brained
CRACK-BRAINED: हतज्ञानः (ना, नं): v. Mad,<BR>foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cracker
CRACKER: a firework: *स्फोटकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crackle
CRACKLE (v. i.): चटचटायते (nomi.),<BR>continuously<BR>c. ing sesamum, white mustard seed, etc.:<BR>निरन्तरचटचटायितान् तिलसिद्धार्थकादीन्, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crackling
CRACKLING (subs.):<BR>I A rattle: q. v.: चट-<BR>चटायितम्।<BR>II The rind of roast pork: शूल्य-<BR>शूकरमांसस्य त्वक्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cracknel
CRACKNEL: a kind of biscuit: *मुडमुडी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cradle
CRADLE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: no equiv.: शिशूनां<BR> दोला: v. Swing. Ph.: from one's c.:<BR>आ शैशवात्: v. Childhood;<BR>an infant in the<BR>c.:<BR>क्रोडस्थः<BR>or<BR>स्तनन्धयः शिशुः<BR>II Fig., abode:<BR>q. v.: आवासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cradle
CRADLE (v. t.): लालयति (c. of लल्): v. To<BR>nurse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

craft
CRAFT:<BR>I Art, occupation: q. v.: कला,<BR>I<BR>learnt it as a c., but it is my livelihood now:<BR>कलेति शिक्षिता जोविकेदानीं संवृत्ता, Mr. ii.<BR>II Cun-<BR>-ning, artifice: q. v.: कौशलम्।<BR>III A small<BR>vessel:<BR>(1) नौः;<BR>(2) तरी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

craftily
CRAFTILY: चतुरम्: v. Cunningly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

craftiness
CRAFTINESS:<BR>(1) वैदग्ध्यम्;<BR>(2) चातुर्यम्: v.<BR>Cunning, artifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

craftsman
CRAFTSMAN: कारुः: v. Artisan, mechanic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crafty
CRAFTY:<BR>(1) विदग्धः (f. ग्धा);<BR>(2) चतुरः (रा, रं):<BR>v. Cunning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crag
CRAG:<BR>I Rock, cliff: q. v.: कूटः।<BR>II Neck: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cragged
CRAGGED, CRAGGY:<BR>I Rugged, rough: q. v.<BR>II Rocky: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cram
CRAM (v. t.):<BR>I To fill to excess:<BR>c. med<BR>with houses:<BR>गृहसंबाधः (धा, धं), V. p.;<BR>the forest<BR>was c. med with the attendants of Śiva:<BR>वनं<BR> गणैरविच्छेदनिरुद्धम्, K.;<BR>c. ming the belly with<BR>sweetmeats:<BR>मोदकैः कुक्षिं पूरयित्वा, Mal.: v. To<BR>fill, stuff.<BR>II Of special instruction:<BR>*विशेषशिक्षां ददाति (दा, c. 3.) (?),<BR>c. mer<BR>*विशेष-<BR>शिक्षादातृ (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cram
CRAM (v. i.): *विशेषशिक्षां गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cramp
CRAMP (subs.): A restriction: q. v.<BR>II C.<BR>-iron: वक्रलौहः (?).<BR>III Spasm: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cramp
CRAMP (v.):<BR>I To check: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>fasten: q. v.<BR>III To afflict with c.: संकोचति<BR>(कुच्, c. l.) (?). C. ed: v. Crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crane
CRANE:<BR>I The bird:<BR>(1) सारसः (the Indian<BR>c.);<BR>(2) कर्करेटुः (the Numidian c.).<BR>II A<BR>Machine for hoisting: *उत्तोलनयन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crank
CRANK:<BR>I An iron elbow: वक्रभागः (?).<BR>II<BR>Bend, turning: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crannied
CRANNIED: छिद्रपूर्णः (र्णा, र्णं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cranny
CRANNY: छिद्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crape
CRAPE: वस्त्रविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crapulence
CRAPULENCE: महातङ्कः (?); अतिपानजनिता वमनेच्छा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crapulent
CRAPULENT, CRAPULOUS: भदविह्वलः (ला, लं)<BR>(=drunk: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crash
CRASH (subs.): महाशब्दः: v. Sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crash
CRASH (v. t.): चूर्णयति (चूर्ण, c. 10.): v. To<BR>break, crush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crash
CRASH (v. i.): महाशब्देन भज्यते (pass. of भञ्ज्): v.<BR>To clatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crasis
CRASIS: in grammar: *संयोगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crass
CRASS: v. Gross, thick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crate
CRATE: v. Basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crater
CRATER: of a volcano: मुखम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

craunch
CRAUNCH: दन्तैः निष्पीडयति (पीड्, c. 10.), B.:<BR>v. To crush, chew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cravat
CRAVAT: v. Neckcloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crave
CRAVE:<BR>I To beg, implore: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>long for: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

craven
CRAVEN: कापुरुषः: v. Coward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

craving
CRAVING (subs.): लालसा: v. Longing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

craw
CRAW: v. Crop. (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crawfish
CRAWFISH, CRAYFISH: चिङ्गेटः (?); मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crawl
CRAWL (v.):<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) रिङ्गति (रिङ्ग्,<BR>c. l.), they then used to c. about in the cowpen:<BR>रिङ्गितौ तौ तदा व्रजे, V. p.;<BR>(2) जानुभ्यां रंहति<BR>(रंह्, c. l.), S.;<BR>(3) जानुभ्यां कराभ्यां च भुवं संघृष्य<BR> सञ्चरति (चर्, c. l.), V. p. com.<BR>II Of<BR>animals: सर्पति, प्र-, (सृप्, c. l.). C. up to:<BR>उपसर्पति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crawl
CRAWL,-ING (subs.):<BR>(1) रिङ्गनम् (of boys etc.);<BR>(2) सर्पणम् (of reptiles).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crawler
CRAWLER: i. e. a crawling animal: सरीसृपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crayon
CRAYON: वर्तिका (=pencil); कठिनी (=chalk.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

craze
CRAZE (v.):<BR>I To crush, grind: q. v.<BR>II<BR>To confuse: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crazed
CRAZED, CRAZY:<BR>I Decrepit, feeble: q. v.<BR>II Mad: q. v.: क्षिप्तः (प्ता, प्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

craziness
CRAZINESS:<BR>I Feebleness: q. v.<BR>II Mad-<BR>-ness: q. v.: क्षिप्तता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

creak
CREAK (v.): कडकडायते (nomi.) (?); विरौति (रु,<BR>c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

creak
CREAK, -ING (subs.): कडकडायितम् (?); विरावः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cream
CREAM:<BR>I Lit.: सरः (?).<BR>II Fig: सारः:<BR>v. Essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cream-coloured
CREAM-COLOURED: i. e. light yellow: आपीतः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crease
CREASE (subs.):<BR>(1) मङ्गिः;<BR>(2) ऊर्मो।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crease
CREASE (v.): भङ्गिं करोति (?): v. To fold,<BR>wrinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

create
CREATE:<BR>I To call into being: सृजति (सृज्,<BR>c. 6.),<BR>c. d water first:<BR>अप एव ससर्जादौ, M. i. 8.;<BR>to c. pain:<BR>व्यथां सृजति, N. iv. II.: v. To<BR>cause.<BR>II To conceive by the mind:<BR>(1)<BR>सृजति,<BR>by whom this story is c. d:<BR>येनेयं कथा सृष्टा,<BR>K.;<BR>(2) निर्-मिमीते (मा, c. 3.), poet's c. -ion:<BR>कवेर्निर्मितिः, Kav.<BR>III To make, appoint:<BR>q. v.: करोति। Tungabala was c. d. a governor:<BR>तुङ्गबलो भोगपतिः कृतः, H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

creation
CREATION:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) सृष्टिः;<BR>(2) सर्गः,<BR>the<BR>sole cause of the c. continuation and destruction<BR>of the world:<BR>विश्वस्य सर्गस्थितिप्रलयानामेकं कारणम्;<BR>(3) सृजनम्।<BR>II Fig., as of a poet:<BR>(1) सृष्टिः;<BR>(2) निर्माणम्<BR>or<BR>निर्मितिः।<BR>III A thing created:<BR>सृष्टिः, as if the first c. of God as regards women:<BR>युवतिविषये सृष्टिराद्ये व धातुः, Me. ii. 21.<BR>IV<BR>Appointment: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

creative
CREATIVE: Ph.:<BR>c. power:<BR>सृजनशक्तिः; निर्माण-<BR>शक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

creator
CREATOR:<BR>I Lit.: स्रष्ट्ट (f. ष्ट्री);<BR>(2) सृज्। in<BR>comp.,<BR>c. of the world:<BR>विश्वसृज् (mfn.), R.<BR>II<BR>The Supreme Being:<BR>(1) विधातृ (m.);<BR>(2)<BR>विश्वसृज्, विश्वकृत्, and sim. comp. s<BR>III Maker,<BR>originator: q. v.:<BR>(1) कर्तृ (f. र्त्री);<BR>(2) विधातृ<BR>(f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

creature
CREATURE;<BR>I A created being: सृष्टपदार्थः।<BR>Living c.:<BR>प्राणिन् (m.).: v. Animal.<BR>II A<BR>term of contempt: जन्तुः।<BR>III A term of<BR>endearment: जातः (ता, तं), D.<BR>IV A tool,<BR>dependant: q. v.: आश्रितः (ता, तं). Ph.:<BR>being my c.:<BR>मत्तो लब्धोदयः (या, यं), M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

credence
CREDENCE: विश्वासः: v. Belief. To give c. to:<BR>विश्वासं करोति: v. To believe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

credentials
CREDENTIALS: *विश्वासोत्पादिका; श्रद्धाजननपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

credibility
CREDIBILITY:<BR>(1) विश्वास्यता।<BR>from the c. of the<BR>great sage:<BR>विश्वास्यतया महर्षेः, Ki. iii. 34.;<BR>(2)<BR>विश्वसनीयता;<BR>(3) विश्वासयोग्यता;<BR>(4) श्रद्धेयता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

credible
CREDIBLE:<BR>(1) विश्वास्यः (स्या, स्यं);<BR>(2) विश्वसनीयः<BR>(या, यं);<BR>(3) विश्वासयोग्यः (ग्या, ग्यं);<BR>(4) श्रद्धेयः<BR>(या, यं),<BR>this is not c.:<BR>अश्रद्धेयमेतत्, Sa. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

credit
CREDIT (subs.):<BR>I Belief: q. v.: विश्वासः।<BR>II<BR>Esteem, reputation: q. v.: प्रतिष्ठा। Ph.:<BR>it reflects c. on you:<BR>एतत्ते दाक्ष्यं दर्शयति<BR>or<BR>त्वां<BR> प्रतिष्ठापयति (?).<BR>III Authority: प्रामाण्यम्।<BR>IV<BR>In a commercial sense: *विश्वासः,<BR>to sell on<BR>c.:<BR>*विश्वासेन विक्रीणीते। Ph.: c. side (of an<BR>account) *प्राप्तधनभागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

credit
CREDIT (v.):<BR>I To believe: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>enter upon the c. side: *प्राप्तधनभागे लिखति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

creditable
CREDITABLE: श्लाध्यः (ध्या, ध्यं): v. Honour-<BR>-able. Ph.:<BR>c. to you:<BR>तव गौरवकरः (री, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

creditably
CREDITABLY: v. Honourably, well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

creditor
CREDITOR:<BR>(1) उत्तमर्णः;<BR>(2) ऋणदातृ (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

credulity
CREDULITY:<BR>(1) विश्वासशीलता;<BR>(2) विश्रम्भप्रवणता;<BR>(3) श्रद्धालुता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

credulous
CREDULOUS:<BR>(1) विश्वासशीलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2)<BR>विश्रम्भप्रवणः (णा, णं);<BR>(3) श्रद्धालु (mfn.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

credulously
CREDULOUSLY: expr. by adj. or by ins. of<BR>subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

creed
CREED: धर्मः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

creek
CREEK:<BR>(1) वङ्कः;<BR>(2) खातम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

creep
CREEP:<BR>I To crawl: q. v.<BR>II To move<BR>slowly: मन्दं मन्दं सर्पति (सृप्, c. l.).<BR>III Of<BR>plants:<BR>(1) विसर्पति;<BR>(2) चरति (चर्, c. l.),<BR>c. ing on the ground:<BR>भूचरः, Nil.<BR>IV To fawn:<BR>q. v. Ph.:<BR>to c. into the mind:<BR>मनसि आविर्भवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

creeper
CREEPER:<BR>(1) लता (gen. term.);<BR>(2) वीरुध्<BR>(f.);<BR>(3) वल्ली;<BR>(4) व्रतती<BR>or<BR>ति (f).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cremation
CREMATION:<BR>(1) दाहः;<BR>(2) दहनम्;<BR>(3) (fully)<BR>शवदाहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crepuscle
CREPUSCLE, CREPUSCULAR: v. Twilight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crescent
CRESCENT (adj.):<BR>(1) वर्धिष्णु (mfn.);<BR>(2)<BR>वर्धमानः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crescent
CRESCENT (subs.):<BR>I Of the moon:<BR>(1) अर्ध-<BR>चन्द्रः (=half moon);<BR>(2) वर्धमाना चान्द्रमसी<BR> लेखा, Ku. or sim. शशाङ्कलेखा, and sim. comp. s.<BR>II The Turkish flag: अर्धचन्द्रकेतनम्।<BR>III<BR>The Turkish power: अर्धचन्द्रकेतनास्तुरस्काः<BR>(m. pl.).<BR>IV Anything c. -shaped: अर्ध-<BR>चन्द्रः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crescentic
CRESCENTIC, CRESCENT-SHAPED: अर्धचन्द्राकारः<BR>(रा, रं). and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cress
CRESS: शाकप्रभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cresset
CRESSET: आकाशदीपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crest
CREST:<BR>I Of animals:<BR>(1) चूडा;<BR>(2) शिखा।<BR>II<BR>Of a helmet:<BR>(1) शिखा;<BR>(2) चूडा;<BR>(3) शेखरः।<BR>III Of a mountain:<BR>(1) चूडा;<BR>(2) शिखरः:<BR>v. Summit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crested
CRESTED;<BR>(1) शिखिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) शिखाधरः (रा,<BR> रं);<BR>(3) चूडावत् (f. ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crest-fallen
CREST-FALLEN:<BR>(1) भग्नचूडः (डा, डं);<BR>(2)<BR>हतौजस् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cretin
CRETIN: गडुकण्ठः (ण्ठा, ण्ठं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crevice
CREVICE: छिद्रम्,<BR>c. of a rock:<BR>ग्रावच्छिद्रम्, D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crew
CREW:<BR>I A throng: q. v.: गणः।<BR>II A ship's<BR>c.:<BR>(1) नाविकाः (m. pl.);<BR>(2) पोतवाहाः (m. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crib
CRIB:<BR>I A manger: q. v.: द्रोणी।<BR>II A stall<BR>for cattle: गोष्ठम्: v. Cow-house.<BR>III A<BR>child's bed: शिशुशय्या: v. Bed.<BR>IV A hut:<BR>q. v.: कुटीरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cribble
CRIBBLE: चालनी: v. Sieve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crick
CRICK: a kind of sprain: v. Sprain, strain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cricket
CRICKET:<BR>I The insect:<BR>(1) भिल्ली,<BR>chirping<BR>of the c.:<BR>भिल्लीभ्कङ्कारः, A. r.<BR>(2) भृङ्गारी;<BR>(3)<BR>चीरी।<BR>II The game: *कन्दुकनोदनक्रीडा। N. B.<BR>कन्दुकक्रीडा is a quite dif. game.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crier
CRIER:<BR>(1) धोषकः;<BR>(2) उद्घोषकः;<BR>(3) घोषणाकारः,<BR> -कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crime
CRIME:<BR>(1) पापम् (=offence=sin.),<BR>to commit<BR>a c. deliberately:<BR>कामतः पापं करोति, M.;<BR>c. s<BR>cannot be checked without punishment:<BR>दण्डादृते<BR> पापविनिग्रहः कर्तु न शक्यः, M.;<BR>(2) अपराधः: v.<BR>Offence;<BR>(3) दोषः: v. Fault;<BR>(4) साहसम्<BR>(=daring c.), M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

criminal
CRIMINAL:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) अपराधिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) पातकित् (f. नी): v. Guilty.<BR>II Of acts:<BR>(1) सापराधः (धा, धं);<BR>(2) सपापः (पा, पं);<BR>(3)<BR>by comp.,<BR>c. act:<BR>पापक्रिया, K. b. Ph.: c. law:<BR>*अपराधविधिः; “c. conversation”: परस्य पत्न्या रहः<BR> सम्माषा, M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

criminality
CRIMINALITY: सापराधता: v. Guiltiness, wicked-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

criminally
CRIMINALLY:<BR>I Wickedly: सापराधम्।<BR>II Accor-<BR>-ding to criminal law: *अपराधविध्यनुसारेण।<BR>Ph.:<BR>to proceed c.:<BR>दण्डनायकं निवेदयति (c. of<BR>विद्) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

criminate
CRIMINATE:<BR>I To accuse: q. v.: अभियुनक्ति<BR>(युज्, c. 7.).<BR>II To implicate: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crimination
CRIMINATION: अभियोगः: v. Accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

criminatory
CRIMINATORY:<BR>(1) अपवादगर्भः (र्भा, र्भं);<BR>(2)<BR>अभियोगलिप्तः (प्ता, प्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crimp
CRIMP (adj.):<BR>I Brittle: q. v.<BR>II Inconsist-<BR>-ent: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crimp
CRIMP (v.):<BR>I To decoy: q. v.<BR>II To curl:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crimp
CRIMP (subs.): प्रतारकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crimple
CRIMPLE: v. To contract; to curl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crimson
CRIMSON: शोणः (णा, णं): v. Red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cringe
CRINGE: Ph.:<BR>who is always c. ing:<BR>योऽहर्निशमु-<BR>परचिताञ्जलिः स्तौति, K.; c. before Lakṣmaṇa:<BR>सौमित्रेश्चरणौ भज, Vi.<BR>C. ing:<BR>आपादपद्मप्रणतः (ता,<BR> तं), R.: v. To Bend, bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cringingly
CRINGINGLY: पादयोः पतित्वा; अञ्जलिं बद्धा; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crinoline
CRINOLINE: i. c. a lady's skirt expanded:<BR>*सरी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cripple
CRIPPLE (subs. or adj.): पङ्गु (mfn.) (=lame:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(2) विकलः (ला, लं) (=wanting any<BR>limb),<BR>carrying the c. on his shoulders:<BR>तं विकलं<BR> स्कन्धेनोदुह्य, D. vi.;<BR>(3) विकलाङ्गः (f. ङ्गी) (=<BR>विकल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cripple
CRIPPLE (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: विकलीकरोति,<BR>who has<BR>c. d my husband:<BR>येन मे पतिर्विकलीकृतः, D.: v.<BR>To lame, disable.<BR>II To impair, weaken:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crippling
CRIPPLING: i. e. a spar for support: उप-<BR>स्तभ्मः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crisis
CRISIS: सङ्कटम्,<BR>c. of an affair:<BR>कार्यसङ्कटकम्, K.<BR>Ph.:<BR>at this c.:<BR>तस्मिन् क्षणे<BR>or<BR>अत्रान्तरे, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crisp
CRISP, CRISPY (adj.): भङ्गुरः (रा, रं): v. Cur-<BR>-ly, brittle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crisp
CRISP (v.): To curl; to interweave. “C. ed<BR>(brook)” तरङ्गितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crispness
CRISPNESS: मङ्गुरता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

criss-cross-row
CRISS-CROSS-ROW:<BR>(1) मातृका;<BR>(2) सिद्धिफला:<BR>v. Alphabet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

criterion
CRITERION: लक्षणम्: v. Sign, mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

critic
CRITIC:<BR>I One who criticizes: गुणदोषविचारकः।<BR>(?).<BR>II One skilled in criticism: गुणदोष-<BR>कोविदः; गुणदोषविचारपण्डितः; etc.<BR>III A carper:<BR>दोषैकदृश् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

critical
CRITICAL:<BR>I Relating to criticism: expr.<BR>by comp.,<BR>c. dissertation:<BR>गुणदोषविचारप्रबन्ध।:<BR>II<BR>Possessing skill to criticize: गुणदोपविचारकुशलः<BR>(ला, लं), and sim. comp. s (?). C. power:<BR>गुणदोषविचारशक्तिः (?).<BR>III Captious, fastidious:<BR>q. v.<BR>IV Belonging to a crisis: Ph:<BR>c.<BR>position:<BR>सङ्कटम्;<BR>whose intellect does not fail in c.<BR>circumstances:<BR>कार्यसङ्कटेष्वविषण्णधीः, K.;<BR>c. philoso-<BR>phy:<BR>*कण्ठदर्शनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

critically
CRITICALLY:<BR>I In a critical manner: गुण-<BR>दोषान् विचार्य; सूक्ष्मम् (=minutely, carefully).<BR>II At a crisis: सङ्कटे।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

criticise
CRITICISE, CRITICIZE:<BR>I To examine as a<BR>critic: गुणदोषान् विचारयति (चर्, c. 10.)<BR>II<BR>To pass criticism on: समालोचयति (लोच्, c.<BR>10.) (?).<BR>III To censure: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

criticism
CRITICISM:<BR>I The art: गुणदोषविचारः (?).<BR>II.<BR>Review: *समालोचनम्; गुणागुणवादः।<BR>III Cen-<BR>-sure: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

critique
CRITIQUE: गुणदोषविचारप्रबन्धः (?), and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

croak
CROAK (v.):<BR>I As frogs or crows:<BR>(1) रटति<BR>(रट्, c. l.), the crow is much c. ing gratingly:<BR>काकः कटूच्चैः खलु रारटीति, Ch.;<BR>(2) मकमकायते<BR>(nomi.) (of frogs), J.;<BR>(3) शब्दं करोति (=to<BR>make any sound),<BR>when I will c.:<BR>यदाहं<BR> शब्दं करोमि, H.: v. To cry.<BR>II To grumble :<BR>मकमकायते (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

croak
CROAK, -ING (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: भेकनादः (of<BR>frog.);<BR>(2) काकशब्दः (of crows): v. Cry.<BR>II.<BR>Fig.: मकमकायितम् (?): v. Complaint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

croaker
CROAKER: i. e. grumbler: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crock
CROCK:<BR>I A pot: q. v.: “c. of gold”:<BR>हिरण्मयपात्रम्।<BR>II Soot: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crockery
CROCKERY: मृन्मयपात्राणि (n. pl.): v. Earthern-<BR>-ware.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crocodile
CROCODILE:<BR>(1) कुम्भीरः;<BR>(2) नक्रः। Ph.: “c.<BR>tears”: कृत्रिमाश्रूणि (n. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crocus
CROCUS: कुङ्कुमलता (a species of c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

croft
CROFT: वृतिः: v. Enclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crone
CRONE:<BR>(1) वृद्धा;<BR>(2) जरती।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crony
CRONY: सुहृद्: v. Friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crook
CROOK (subs.):<BR>I A bend or turn: q. v.<BR>II<BR>A shepherd's staff: दण्डः Ph.:<BR>by hook or<BR>by c.:<BR>येन केन प्रकारेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crook
CROOK (v.): वक्रीकरोति (कृ, c. 8): v. To<BR>bend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crook-back
CROOK-BACK:<BR>(1) कुब्ज (f. ब्जा);<BR>(2) न्युब्ज (f.<BR>ब्जा);<BR>(3) गडुरः (रा, रं);<BR>(4) वक्र (f. क्रा),<BR>V. p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crooked
CROOKED (adj.):<BR>I Not straight:<BR>(1) वक्र<BR>(f. क्रा);<BR>(2) कुटिलः (ला, लं);<BR>(3) वक्रिमः (मा,<BR> मं);<BR>(4) अरालः (ला, लं);<BR>(5) जिह्य, वि-, (f.<BR>ह्मा);<BR>(6) वृजिनः (ना, नं).<BR>II In moral<BR>sense:<BR>(1) वक्र (f. क्रा) (rare),<BR>c. nature<BR>वक्र-<BR>भावः, N.;<BR>(2) कुटिलः (ला, लं),<BR>c. minded<BR>कुटिल-<BR>मति (mfn.), Mu.;<BR>(3) जिह्म (f. ह्मा), yet than<BR>c. (man.): तथापि जिह्मः सः, Ki.;<BR>(4) अनृजु<BR>(mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crookedly
CROOKEDLY:<BR>(1) वक्रम्;<BR>(2) कुटिलम्;<BR>(3) जिह्मम्:<BR>v. Awry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crookedness
CROOKEDNESS:<BR>(1) वक्रता;<BR>(2) वक्रिमन् (m.);<BR>(3) कौटिल्यम्;<BR>(4) विजिह्मता;<BR>(5) कुटिलता;<BR>(6)<BR>जैह्म्यम्;<BR>(7) अनृजुता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crop
CROP (subs.):<BR>I The produce of fields:<BR>(1)<BR>शस्यम्,<BR>yielding all c. s:<BR>सर्वशस्यप्रदः (दा, दं), Nil.;<BR>devastation of c. s:<BR>शस्यघातः, D.;<BR>(2) not expr.<BR>when any particular c. is meant, rice c.:<BR>धान्यम्।<BR>II Of birds: कण्ठम् (=throat).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crop
CROP (v.):<BR>I To cut short: कल्पति (कॢप्, c.<BR>1).<BR>II To reap: q. v.: लुनाति (लु, c. 9).<BR>III To nibble: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crop out
CROP OUT: आविर्भवति (भू, c. l.). v. To<BR>appear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crop-eared
CROP-EARED: छिन्नकर्णाग्र (f. ग्रा), and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crosier
CROSIER: *क्रुशदण्ड, or sim. दण्डः (when no<BR>ambiguity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cross
CROSS (adj.):<BR>I Transverse:<BR>(1) व्यत्यस्तः (स्ता,<BR> स्तं);<BR>(2) तिरश्चीनः (ना, नं) (=sideways).<BR>II Adverse, contrary: q. v.: प्रतीपः (पा, पं).<BR>Ph.:<BR>oh! how c. is fate:<BR>अहो वामता भागधेयानाम्।<BR>Vi.<BR>III Ill-tempered, peevish: q. v. प्रतीपः<BR>(पा, पं),<BR>don't get c. with your husband:<BR>भर्तुः<BR> प्रतीपं मास्म गमः, Sa.<BR>A c. charge:<BR>प्रत्यभि-योगः, Y.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cross
CROSS (v. t):<BR>I To pass over:<BR>(1) तरति (तृ,<BR>c. l.),<BR>c. ed the Ganges:<BR>गङ्गां ततार, R. xvi.<BR>52.;<BR>I want to c. the ocean on a raft:<BR>उडुपेन<BR> सागरं तितीर्षुरस्मि, R.;<BR>(2) लङ्घते<BR>or<BR>लङ्घयति, वि,-<BR>उत्-, (लङ्घ्, c. l. and 10.), c. ed the Vindhya:<BR>विन्ध्यं व्यलङ्घयत्, R. xvi. 32.<BR>II Of the<BR>mind, to occur to: q. v.<BR>III To thwart,<BR>obstruct: q. v.<BR>IV To mix breeds: perh.<BR>संमिश्रयति (मिश्र्, c. 10.). V. To conceal:<BR>q. v.<BR>VI To put across, expr. by circumlo.,<BR>to c. arms.:<BR>एकस्मिन् भुजे भुजान्तरं विन्यस्यति or<BR>विदधाति।<BR>VII To draw line across: रेखया<BR> अङ्कयति (अङ्क्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cross
CROSS (v. i.):<BR>to c. over to Ceylon:<BR>समुद्रमुल्लङ्घ्या सिंहलं<BR> गच्छति: v. To cross (I) and go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cross
CROSS (subs.):<BR>I An instrument^1: शूलम् (=<BR>stake: q. v.); *क्रुशम्।<BR>II The symbol: *क्रुशम्;<BR>व्यत्यस्तरेखाद्वयम्।<BR>III The gospel: q. v.<BR>IV<BR>Money: नाणकम्। V. Affliction, trouble: q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cross-bill
CROSS-BILL: पक्षिविशेषः; *व्यत्यस्तपुटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cross-bow
CROSS-BOW: *वक्रचापः।<BR>C. -man:<BR>*वक्रचापभृत्<BR>(mfn.)<BR>or<BR>-धरः (री, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cross-breed
CROSS-BREED: खच्चरः (री, रं) (in modern dia-<BR>-lects).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cross-examination
CROSS-EXAMINATION: *प्रतीपपरीक्षा; कूटपरीक्षा (in<BR>modern Bengali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cross-examine
CROSS-EXAMINE: *प्रतीपं परीक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. l.);<BR>कूटपरीक्षां करोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cross-grained
CROSS-GRAINED: प्रतीपः (पा, पं): v. Morose,<BR>perverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crossing
CROSSING:<BR>I Lit.: तरः, -णम्: v. Passage. Fare<BR>for c.:<BR>(1) तारिकम्, M.;<BR>(2) तार्यम्, M.<BR>II<BR>Where roads cross:<BR>(1) चतुष्पथम् (of four<BR>roads);<BR>(2) शृङ्गाटकम् (=1);<BR>(3) त्रिपथम् (of<BR>three roads);<BR>(4) तरः (very rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cross-legged
CROSS-LEGGED: व्यत्यस्तपादः (दा, दं), and sim.<BR>comp. s. Sitting c. (i. e. placing the feet on<BR>the thighs) वीरासनस्थः (स्था, स्थं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cross-question
CROSS-QUESTION: v. To cross-examine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cross-road
CROSS-ROAD: i. e. an obscure road:<BR>(1)<BR>उत्पथः;<BR>(2) उन्मार्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cross-row
CROSS-ROW: i. e. the alphabet: q. v.: मातृका,<BR>M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crosswise
CROSSWISE:<BR>(1) व्यत्यस्तम् (?);<BR>(2) तिरश्चीनम्:<BR>v. Sideways, athwart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crossly
CROSSLY:<BR>I Peevishly: q. v.<BR>II Adversely:<BR>प्रतीपम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crotchet
CROTCHET:<BR>I A whim, fancy: q. v.<BR>II In<BR>music: *शृणिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crotchety
CROTCHETY: i. e. full of whims: v. Whim,<BR>whimsical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crouch
CROUCH:<BR>I To stoop low: q. v.: नमयति<BR>(c. of नम्).<BR>II To cringe: q. v.: पादयोः<BR> पतति (पत्, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

croup
CROUP:<BR>I Of a horse, etc.: जघनभागः, K.<BR>II<BR>A disease: काशरोगविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crow
CROW (subs.):<BR>I The bird:<BR>(1) काकः;<BR>(2)<BR>वायसः।<BR>Carrion c.:<BR>दग्धकाकः (?).<BR>II A bar:<BR>लोहदण्डः।<BR>III Of the cock: रवः: v. Cry.<BR>Ph.:<BR>at cock-c.<BR>प्रत्यूषे: v. Morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crow
CROW (v.):<BR>I Of the cock: रौति, वि-, (रु c.<BR>2.): v. To cry.<BR>II To boast: q. v. विकत्थते<BR>(कत्थ्, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crowfoot
CROWFOOT: a plant: *काकपादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crowd
CROWD (subs.):<BR>I Of people:<BR>(1) जनसमूहः,<BR>Mr.;<BR>(2) जनसंमर्दः (=men pressed together<BR>without order),<BR>a great c.:<BR>महान् जनसंमर्दः,<BR>Mr. x.;<BR>(3) सङ्कुलम् (=जनसंमर्दः), D. iv.;<BR>(4)<BR>जनौघः, and sim. comp. s<BR>II Populace:<BR>q. v.<BR>III Any c.: v. Throng, multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crowd
CROWD (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: Ph.:<BR>the place was<BR>very c. ed:<BR>तत्र महान् जनसंमर्द आसीत्;<BR>c. ed with<BR>cars and horses:<BR>रथाश्वसङ्कुलः (ला, लं), Ki. i. 16.,<BR>a. c. ed house:<BR>जनाकीर्णं गृहम् (i. e. full of men),<BR>Sa.:<BR>the theatre is c. ed today:<BR>अद्य प्रेक्षकपूर्णा रङ्ग-<BR>शाला (?).<BR>II To urge: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crowd
CROWD (v. i.): expr. as above: v. To<BR>flock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crowder
CROWDER: v. Fiddler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crown
CROWN (subs.):<BR>I The ornament:<BR>(1) किरीट<BR>(mn.);<BR>(2) मुकुटम्;<BR>(3) मौलिः<BR>II Fig., royal<BR>power:<BR>got the c. of Italy:<BR>इतालिराज्यमवाप;<BR>placed the c. on his son:<BR>तदात्मसम्मवं राज्ये समादधुः,<BR>R. xvii. 8.<BR>III Fig., sovereign: q. v. Ph.:<BR>servant of the c.:<BR>राजसेवकः।<BR>IV Any garland:<BR>q. v.: माला। V. Of the head: चूडा।<BR>VI<BR>Summit: q. v.: चूडा।<BR>VII A coin: इंलण्डीय-<BR>रूप्यमुद्राविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crown
CROWN (v. t.):<BR>I To invest with royal power:<BR>(1) (राज्ये) अभिसिञ्चति (सिच् c. 6) (accord-<BR>-ing to the Hindu style), R.;<BR>(2) राज्ये समा-<BR>दधति (धा, c. 3.), R.<BR>(3) मौलिं ग्राहयति (c. of<BR>ग्रह्) (?).<BR>II To adorn: q. v.: भूषयति (भूष्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR>III To consummate: q. v. Ph.:<BR>c. ing success<BR>सिद्धेः परा कोटिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crown-jewels
CROWN-JEWELS: राजरत्नानि (n. pl.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crown-prince
CROWN-PRINCE: युवराजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crucial
CRUCIAL: perh. मर्मभेदिन् (f. णी): v. Severe,<BR>strict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crucible
CRUCIBLE:<BR>(1) सूषः (षी, षं);<BR>(2) आवर्तनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crucifix
CRUCIFIX: *क्रुशारोपितस्य कृष्टस्य प्रतिमा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crucifixion
CRUCIFIXION: *क्रुशारोपणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cruciform
CRUCIFORM: *क्रुशाकारः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crucify
CRUCIFY:<BR>I Lit.: *क्रुशम् आरोपयति (c. of रुह्)<BR>II Fig.:<BR>to c. the flesh:<BR>इन्द्रियाणि जयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crude
CRUDE: अपक्व (f. क्वा) (lit. and fig.): v. Unripe,<BR>immature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crudely
CRUDELY: v. Imperfectly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crudeness
CRUDENESS, CRUDITY: अपक्वता: v. Unripeness,<BR>immaturity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cruel
CRUEL:<BR>(1) निष्ठुरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) क्रुरः (रा, रं)<BR>(3) नृशंसः (सा, सं);<BR>(4) निष्करुणः (णा, णं) (=un-<BR>merciful: q. v.);<BR>(5) कठिनः (ना, नं) (=hard-<BR>hearted: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cruelly
CRUELLY:<BR>(1) निष्ठुरम्;<BR>(2) क्रुद्धम्;<BR>(3) निष्करुणम्<BR>v. Unmerciful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cruelty
CRUELTY: नैष्ठुर्यम्<BR>or<BR>निष्ठुरता;<BR>(2) क्रौर्यम्<BR>or<BR>क्रुरता<BR>(3) नृशंसता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cruet
CRUET: *कूपकः।<BR>C. -stand:<BR>*कूपकाधारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cruise
CRUISE (subs.):<BR>I A jug: q. v.<BR>II of a<BR>ship: v. Voyage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cruise
CRUISE (v. i.): (समुद्रेण<BR>or<BR>पोतेन) परिभ्रमति (भ्र<BR>c. l.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cruiser
CRUISER: *परिभ्रमणपोतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crumb
CRUMB:<BR>I A morsel: q. v.<BR>II The soft part<BR>of bread: मध्यमागः<BR>or<BR>कोमलभागः (?). Ph. :<BR>to a c.:<BR>निरवशेषम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crumble
CRUMBLE (v. t.): चूर्णयति (चूर्ण्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>bruise.<BR>To be c. d into dust:<BR>धलीमवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crumble
CRUMBLE (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.: चूर्णीमवति।<BR>II Fig. :<BR>विनश्यति (नश्, c. 4.): v. To perish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crump
CRUMP:<BR>I Crooked: q. v.: कुब्जः (f. -ब्जा).<BR>II.<BR>Hard: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crumple
CRUMPLE: v. To rumple, wrinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crupper
CRUPPER: पुच्छबन्धः, Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crusade
CRUSADE: *क्रुशेदम्; कृष्टीयानां पुण्यभूमिलाभाय<BR>महम्मदीयान् प्रत्यभियोगः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crush
CRUSH (v. t.);<BR>(1) मृद्राति<BR>or<BR>मर्दयति, -ते, आ-, परि-,<BR>वि-, सं-, (मृद्, c. 9. or 10.), c. ed the forces of<BR>his enemies:<BR>परेषां बलान्यमृद्रात्, R.;<BR>(2) दलति<BR>or<BR>दलयति (दल्, c. l. and 10.), c. ing forts<BR>दलयन्दुर्गाणि, K.;<BR>(3) मथ्नाति, प्र-, (मन्थ्, c. 9.),<BR>shall I not c. the hundred Kauravas:<BR>मथ्नामि<BR>कौरवशतं न, Ve.: v. To grind, overwhelm,<BR>put down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crush
CRUSH, CRUSHING (subs.):<BR>I The act: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">Page167</a>]<BR>(1) मर्दनम्, वि-;<BR>(2) दलनम्।<BR>II Of a crowd:<BR>जनसंमर्दः, Mr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crushing
CRUSHING (adj.): प्रमाथिन् (f. नी),<BR>of c. cala-<BR>mities:<BR>प्रमाथिनीनां विपदाम्, Ki. iii. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crush
CRUSH (v.):<BR>I Trans.: v. To encrush.<BR>II<BR>Intrans: उपरि संहन्ति (हन्, c. 2.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crust
CRUST (subs.): कठिनभागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crustacean
CRUSTACEAN, CRUSTACEOUS: *वर्मधरः (री, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crustily
CRUSTILY: v. Peevishly, angrily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crustiness
CRUSTINESS:<BR>I Hardness: q. v.<BR>II Peevish-<BR>-ness: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crusty
CRUSTY:<BR>I Hard: q. v.: कठिनः (ना, नं).<BR>II<BR>Peevish, surly: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crutch
CRUTCH: यष्टिः,<BR>leaning on a c.:<BR>यष्ट्यावलम्बितः,<BR>Ki.: v. Stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cry
CRY (subs.):<BR>I Of lower animals: रवः or<BR>विरावः,<BR>very loud cries were also uttered by the<BR>elephants:<BR>मुक्तो विरावः सुमहान् कुञ्जरैरपि, Mah.:<BR>v. Noise, sound.<BR>II Clamour: उत्क्रोशः or<BR>आक्रोशः,<BR>by the c. s of the disputants:<BR>विवदमानानां<BR> प्रजानामाक्रोशैः, D.: v. Noise.<BR>III Of distress:<BR>(1) आर्तनादः, आर्तरवः, and sim. comp.<BR>s, by the<BR>piteous cries of the attendants:<BR>परिजनानां करुण-<BR>स्वनेन, M. n.;<BR>(2) क्रन्दनम्<BR>or<BR>आक्रन्दितम्<BR>or<BR>आक्रन्दः<BR>(=loud c. of grief);<BR>(3) रुदितम्: v. Weep-<BR>-ing.<BR>IV Of crier: perh. आक्रोशः: v. Pro-<BR>-clamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cry
CRY (v. t.):<BR>I To utter: q. v.<BR>II To pro-<BR>-claim: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cry
CRY (v. i.):<BR>I To c. out: q. v.<BR>II To weep:<BR>(1) क्रन्दति<BR>or<BR>क्रन्दयति, आ-, (क्रन्द्, c. l. and 10.),<BR>cried aloud:<BR>मुक्तकण्ठं चक्रन्द, R. xiv. 68;<BR>(2)<BR>रोदिति, प्र-, (रुद्, c. 2.),<BR>cried aloud:<BR>उच्चैररोदीत्,<BR>K.; क्रोशति, वि-, आ-, (क्रुश्, c. l.) (rare), B.<BR>iii. 22.<BR>III To utter sounds:<BR>(1) रौति,<BR> वि-, (रु, c. 2.), this vulture is c. ing not once:<BR>नैकशः शकुनिरयं विरौति, Mr.;<BR>(2) वाशति<BR>or<BR>वाश्यते<BR>(वाश्, c. l. and 4.), this crow is c. ing gratingly:<BR>रुक्षस्वरं वाशति वायसोऽयम्, Mr.: v. Noise, to<BR>make.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cry down
CRY DOWN: अव-क्रोशति, उप-, अप-,: v. To<BR>detract, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cry out
CRY OUT:<BR>(1) क्रोशति, आ, वि-, उत्,<BR>C.:<BR>आक्रोश,<BR>विक्रोश, लपाधिचण्डम्, Mr.;<BR>(2) शब्दायते (=to<BR>call out).<BR>To c. for protection:<BR>शरणं क्रन्दति,<BR>V. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cry up
CRY UP: v. To extol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crying
CRYING (adj.): v. Notorious, heinous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crystal
CRYSTAL:<BR>I Subs.: स्फटिकः।<BR>II Adj.:<BR>(1)<BR>स्फटिक-,<BR>c. palace:<BR>स्फटिकहर्म्यम्, Ku. vi. 42.;<BR>स्फटिकाभः (भा, भं) (=like c.): v. Transparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crystalline
CRYSTALLINE: v. Crystal (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crystallization
CRYSTALLIZATION: *स्फाटिकीभावः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

crystallize
CRYSTALLIZE:<BR>I Trans.: *स्फाटिकीकरोति।<BR>II<BR>Intrans: *स्फाटिकीभवति (भू, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cub
CUB (subs.): शावः, -कः: v. Young (subs.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cub
CUB (v.): सते (सू, c. 2.): v. To bring forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cube
CUBE (subs.):<BR>I In arith.: घनः,<BR>c. root:<BR>घन-<BR>मूलम्, Li.<BR>II In geo.: समकोणसमचतुर्भुजघन-<BR>क्षेत्रम्, K. d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cubic
CUBIC, CUBICAL: expr. by comp., c. hand:<BR>घनहस्तः, Li.;<BR>c. equation<BR>*घनसमीकरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cubit
CUBIT:<BR>(1) हस्तः,<BR>five c. s in length:<BR>पञ्चहस्तदीर्घ (f.<BR>र्घा);<BR>(2) किष्कुः, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cuckold
CUCKOLD: expr^1. by circumlo,<BR>he is a c.:<BR>तस्य<BR> भार्या पुंश्चली<BR>or<BR>बन्धकी।<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cuckoo
CUCKOO:<BR>(1) कोकिलः;<BR>(2) पिकः;<BR>(3) परभृतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cucumber
CUCUMBER:<BR>I The plant: त्रपुषी।<BR>II fruit:<BR>त्रपुषम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cud
CUD:<BR>I Lit.: पशुविशेषैः पुनश्चर्वणाय मुखनीतं भुक्तम्।<BR>Ph.:<BR>to chew the c.:<BR>रोमन्थमभ्यस्यति, Sa. ii.;<BR>chewing the c.:<BR>रोमन्थः।<BR>II Where it is<BR>chewed: perh. रोमन्थभागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cudgel
CUDGEL (subs.):<BR>(1) लगुडः;<BR>(2) यष्टिः;<BR>(3) दण्डः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cudgel
CUDGEL (v.): लगुडेन<BR>or<BR>यष्ट्या प्रहरति (हृ, c. l.) or<BR>ताडयति (तड्, c. l.)<BR>or<BR>आहन्ति (हन्, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cudgelling
CUDGELLING (subs.):<BR>(1) यष्ट्याघातः;<BR>(2) लगुड-<BR>प्रहारः, giving (them)<BR>a very good c.:<BR>लगुडप्रहारै-<BR>र्जर्जरीकृत्य, P. i. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cue
CUE:<BR>I The end of a thing: अन्तः: v. End.<BR>II A hint: q. v.: संज्ञा,<BR>to give a c.:<BR>संज्ञां<BR> ददाति, Mr.<BR>III Humour, disposition: q. v.<BR>IV For billiards: *दीर्घदण्डः<BR>or<BR>दण्डः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cuff
CUFF (v. t.): करतलेन<BR>or<BR>तलेन<BR>or<BR>चपेटेन ताडयति (तड्,<BR>c. 10.), आहन्ति (हन्, c. 2.),<BR>or<BR>प्रहरति (हृ, c. l.),<BR>c. ed him on the breast:<BR>तलेनोरस्यताडयत्, V. p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cuff
CUFF (subs.):<BR>I A blow, slap: q. v.: तल-<BR>प्रहारः। Ph.:<BR>to be at fisti -c. s:<BR>मुष्टीमुष्टि युध्यते।<BR>II Of a sleeve: *कफम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cuirass
CUIRASS:<BR>(1) कवच (mn.);<BR>(2) वर्मन् (n.);<BR>(3)<BR>वारवाणः;<BR>(4) कङ्कटः, -कः;<BR>(5) तनुत्रम्;<BR>(6) उरश्छदः;<BR>(7) दंशनम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cuirassler
CUIRASSLER:<BR>(1) कवचिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) वर्मितः (ता,<BR> तं);<BR>(3) व्यूढकङ्कटः (टा, टं), and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

culinary
CULINARY: पाक- in comp.,<BR>c. utensil:<BR>पाकपात्रम्;<BR>the c. art:<BR>पाककला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cull
CULL: आहरति (हृ, c. l.): v. To pluck, gather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

culm
CULM: स्तम्बः: v. Stalk<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

culminate
CULMINATE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>the sun has c. d:<BR>मध्य-<BR>मलङ्करोति भानुः, K.<BR>II Fig.: परां कोटिम अधि-<BR>गच्छति (गम्, c. l.), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

culminating
CULMINATING (adj.): Ph.:<BR>c. point:<BR>परा कोटिः;<BR> परा काष्ठा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

culpability
CULPABILITY:<BR>(1) सदोषता;<BR>(2) सापराधता;<BR>(3)<BR>निन्दार्हता (=blamableness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

culpable
CULPABLE:<BR>(1) सदोषः (षा, षं);<BR>(2) सापराधः (धा,<BR> धं);<BR>(3) निन्दार्ह (f. र्हा) (=blamable: q. v.).<BR>C. homicide:<BR>ज्ञानकृता नृहत्या (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

culprit
CULPRIT:<BR>I An accused person: अभियुक्तः<BR>(क्ता, क्तं).<BR>II A criminal: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cultivate
CULTIVATE:<BR>I To till:<BR>(1) क्षेत्रं करोति,<BR>to have<BR>land c. d:<BR>क्षेत्रं कारयति, Y.;<BR>(2) कर्षति (कृष्, c. l.)<BR>(=to plough).<BR>II To devote, to foster:<BR>(1) शीलयति, अनु-, (शील्, c. 10.),<BR>sages c. good<BR>conduct:<BR>शीलयन्ति मुनयः सुशीलताम्, Ki.;<BR>(2) उ प-<BR>चिनोति, प्र-, (चि, c. 5.),<BR>c. friendship:<BR>प्रचिनु<BR> मैत्रीम्, Vi. iii.;<BR>(3) सेवते, नि-, (सेव्, c. l.): v.<BR>To devote.<BR>III To civilize: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cultivation
CULTIVATION:<BR>I Tillage:<BR>(1) कर्षणम्;<BR>(2)<BR>कृष्टिः (rare).<BR>II Fostering care: अनुशीलनम्।<BR>III Culture: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cultivator
CULTIVATOR: क्षेत्रिकः: v. Husbandman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

culture
CULTURE:<BR>I v. Cultivation.<BR>II Refine-<BR>-ment: q. v.: शिक्षा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

culvert
CULVERT: *आवृतनाली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cumber
CUMBER: v. To encumber, embarrass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cumbersome
CUMBERSOME, CUMBROUS:<BR>I Burdensome:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) भारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) दुर्मरः (रा, रं).<BR>II<BR>Vexatious: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cumbrance
CUMBRANCE: v. Encumbrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cumbrousness
CUMBROUSNESS: भारिता: v. Cumbrous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cummin
CUMMIN:<BR>(1) जीरः;<BR>(2) जीरकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cumulative
CUMULATIVE:<BR>(1) उपचयिन् (f. नी) (?);<BR>(2)<BR>निचयिन् (f. नी) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cuneiform
CUNEIFORM: कीलाकारः (रा, रं). “C. scholar”<BR>*कौलवर्णविद् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cunning
CUNNING (adj.):<BR>I Skilful: q. v.<BR>II Artful:<BR>(1) चतुरः (रा, रं) (best equiv.);<BR>(2) विदग्ध<BR>(f. ग्धा);<BR>(3) छलनापरः (रा, रं) (=wily).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cunning
CUNNING (subs.):<BR>I Skill, dexterity: q. v.<BR>II Art, deceit:<BR>(1) चातुर्यम्;<BR>(2) चातुरी;<BR>(3)<BR>वैदग्ध्यम्;<BR>(4) छलम् (=stratagem).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cunningly
CUNNINGLY:<BR>(1) चातुर्येण;<BR>(2) छलेन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cup
CUP (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पानपात्रम्;<BR>(2) पान-<BR>भाजनम्;<BR>(3) चषक (mn.).<BR>II Drinking:<BR>q. v.:<BR>“fond of the c.”<BR>पानप्रियः (या, यं).<BR>III<BR>Lot, portion: q. v. Ph.<BR>“to taste of the<BR>sorrow's c.”<BR>दुःखं रसयति।<BR>IV A flower -c.:<BR>पुष्पकोषः।<BR>A c. made of leaves:<BR>पत्रपुटः, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cup
CUP (v.): रक्तं स्रावयति (c. of स्रु)<BR>or<BR>मोक्षयति (मोक्ष्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cup-bearer
CUP-BEARER: पानपात्रवाहिन् (m.) (?); चषकवाहकः<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cupboard
CUPBOARD: अन्नकोष्ठः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cupid
CUPID:<BR>(1) कामः;<BR>(2) कन्दर्पः;<BR>(3) मदनः;<BR>(4)<BR>मन्मथः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cupidity
CUPIDITY:<BR>I Covetousness: q. v.: लोमः।<BR>II<BR>Lust: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cupola
CUPOLA: तोरणशीर्षम्<BR>or<BR>तोरणशृङ्गम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cupping-glass
CUPPING-GLASS: शरारीमुखम् (a kind of c.), Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cur
CUR: शुनकः: v. Dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curable
CURABLE:<BR>(1) चिकित्स्य (f. स्या);<BR>(2) साध्य (f.<BR>ध्या),<BR>easily c.:<BR>सुखसाव्य (f. ध्या) Sr.;<BR>(3)<BR>प्रतीकार्य (f. र्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curacy
CURACY: *आचार्यकपदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curate
CURATE: *आचार्यकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curative
CURATIVE:<BR>(1) रोगघ्न (f. घ्नी);<BR>(2) रोगहरः<BR>(री, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curator
CURATOR: अध्यक्षः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curb
CURB (subs.):<BR>I For a horse: अश्वमुखशृझला<BR>(?): v. Bit.<BR>II Fig.: v. Check, restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curb
CURB (v.): नियन्त्रयति (यन्त्र्, c. 10.), whose [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">Page169</a>]<BR>mouth is not c. ed:<BR>अनियन्त्रितमुखः, D.: v. To<BR>restrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curb-stone
CURB-STONE: निरोधोपलः, and sim. comp. s (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curd
CURD: दधि (n.),<BR>skim of c. s:<BR>दध्नः सरः, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curdle
CURDLE (v.):<BR>I Trans: घनीकरोति (कृ, c. 8.).<BR>II Intrans: घनीभवति (भू, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cure
CURE (subs.):<BR>I Curacy: q. v.<BR>II Of<BR>diseases:<BR>(1) शान्तिः;<BR>(2) उपशमः;<BR>(3) सिद्धिः;<BR>(4) प्रतीकारः: v. Treatment (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cure
CURE (v. t.):<BR>I Of diseases:<BR>(1) चिकित्सति<BR>(कित्, c. l.) (gen. to treat),<BR>not a sick man<BR>returned without his disease c. d:<BR>नाचिकित्सितगदेन<BR> रोगिणा प्रत्यगामि। Si. xiv. 49.;<BR>(2) शमयति, प्र-,<BR> उप-, (c. of शम्),<BR>for c. ing diseases:<BR>रोगोपशमार्थम्,<BR>Sr.;<BR>(3) साधयति (c. of सिध्) (such),<BR>ulcers get<BR>c. d with difficulty:<BR>व्रणाः कृच्छ्रेण सिध्यन्ति, Sr.;<BR>(4) प्रतिक्ररोति, Sr.<BR>II Of persons:<BR>(1) by<BR>the above verbs with the gen. of the<BR>person c. d,<BR>I will c. the child:<BR>बालस्य रोगं<BR> साधयामि;<BR>(2) सुस्थं (f. स्थां), नीरोगं (f. गां) करोति<BR>with abl. of the disease.<BR>III To pre-<BR>-serve: लवणयति (nomi.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curfew-bell
CURFEW-BELL: प्रदोषधण्टा, and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curiosity
CURIOSITY:<BR>I Inquisitiveness:<BR>(1) कुतूहलम् or<BR>कौतूहलम्,<BR>satisfy your c.:<BR>पूरयतु कुतूहलम्, U. iv.;<BR>excited his excessive c.:<BR>अतुलं विदधे कुतूहलम्, N. ii.<BR>7.;<BR>from c.:<BR>कुतूहलवशात्, K.;<BR>(2) कौतुकम्,<BR>since seeing you I have very great c. about it.:<BR>अतिमहत् खलु भवद्दर्शनात् प्रभृति मे कौतुकमस्मिन् विषये,<BR>K. (note the loc.);<BR>(3) दिदृक्षा (c. to see),<BR>my heart filled with c.:<BR>दिदृक्षाक्रान्तहृदयः, D.;<BR>(4) शुश्रूषा<BR>or<BR>श्रोतुमिच्छा (c. to hear), Ki.<BR>II<BR>An object of c.: कुतूहलम्<BR>or<BR>कौतूहलम्<BR>or<BR>कौतुकम्<BR>(rare), by telling about many c. s seen by travel:<BR>पर्यटनदृष्टानेककौतूहलप्रकथनेन। P. iii. 2.;<BR>(2) अपूर्व-<BR>वस्तु (n.)<BR>or<BR>अपूर्वदृश्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curious
CURIOUS:<BR>I Inquisitive:<BR>(1) कुतूहलिन् (f. नी),<BR>c. to see:<BR>दर्शनकुतूहलिन् (f. नी) K.;<BR>(2)<BR>कुतृहलाक्रान्तमनस् (mfn.);<BR>(3) कौतुकाविष्टचेतस्<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(4) दिदृक्षु (mfn.) (=c. to see);<BR>(5) शुश्रूषु (mfn.) (=c. to hear) (rare);<BR>(6)<BR>जिझासु (mfn.) (=c. to know).<BR>II Singular,<BR>wonderful:<BR>(1) कुतूहलः (ला, लं) (rare);<BR>(2) अपूर्वः (र्वा, र्वं).<BR>III Nice, scrupulous:<BR>q. v.<BR>IV Careful, studious: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curiously
CURIOUSLY:<BR>I Inquisitively: सकौतुकम्।<BR>II<BR>Carefully: q. v.<BR>III Wonderfully: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curl
CURL (subs.):<BR>I Of hair:<BR>(1) अलकः;<BR>(2)<BR>चूर्णकुन्तलः।<BR>II Any undulation: भङ्गिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curl
CURL (v. t.):<BR>I To crisp: भङ्गुरीकरोति (?):<BR>v. Curly.<BR>II To coil: q. v.: मण्डलीकरोति,<BR>c. ing up the trunk:<BR>मण्डलितहस्तकाण्डः, D.<BR>III To<BR>ripple: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curl
CURL (v. i.): expr. by adj.: v. Curled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curled
CURLED, CURLY:<BR>(1) कुटिलः (ला, लं), Mah.;<BR>(2) भङ्गुरः (रा, रं), D. vi.;<BR>(3) अरालः (ला, लं),<BR>c. haired:<BR>अरालकेशः (शी, शं), N. xiii. 40.;<BR>(4)<BR>कुञ्चितः (ता, तं),<BR>c. -haired:<BR>कुञ्चितकेशः (शी, शं),<BR>H. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curlew
CURLEW: a. bird: क्रौञ्चः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curliness
CURLINESS:<BR>(1) कुटिलता;<BR>(2) भङ्गुरता;<BR>(3) अरालता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curling-iron
CURLING-IRON: *अलकलौहम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curmudgeon
CURMUDGEON: v. Miser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

currant
CURRANT:<BR>I The tree: *करण्टः।<BR>II Its fruit:<BR>करण्टम्<BR>or<BR>करण्टफलम्।<BR>III A kind of dried<BR>grape: perh. शुष्कद्राक्षा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

currency
CURRENCY:<BR>I Circulation: q. v. Ph.: to<BR>gain c. (i. e. to be current) प्रचलितः (ता, तं)<BR>भवति।<BR>II Estimation: q. v.<BR>III The<BR>current coin: प्रचलित मुद्रा (?),<BR>we have a paper<BR>c. here:<BR>*अत्र कागजमुद्रा प्रचलिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

current
CURRENT (adj.):<BR>(1) प्रचलितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रचलः (ला, लं). Ph.:<BR>c. year:<BR>वर्तमानवत्सरः;<BR>c. report:<BR>जनप्रवादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

current
CURRENT (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) स्रोतस् (n.) (of<BR>water),<BR>against the c.:<BR>प्रतिस्रोतस्;<BR>(2) प्रवाहः,<BR>c. of electricity:<BR>*विद्यु त्प्रवाहः;<BR>(3) रयः<BR>or<BR>वेगः<BR>(speed) (when the sense is clear),<BR>the c.<BR>of river is its cause:<BR>नदीवेगस्तत्र कारणम्, Sa.<BR>II<BR>Fig.:<BR>c. of time:<BR>कालगतिः (?);<BR>the c. of opinion<BR>is in your favour:<BR>*तवानुकूलं साधारणानां मतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

currently
CURRENTLY: v. Generally, commonly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curricle
CURRICLE: रथः (?): v. Chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

currier
CURRIER: *चर्मशोधकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

currish
CURRISH:<BR>I Churlish, quarrelsome: q. v.<BR>II Brutal: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curry
CURRY (subs.): व्यञ्जनम् (applied to all c. s),<BR>N. xvi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curry
CURRY (v. t.):<BR>I To dress leather: शोधयति<BR>(c. of शुध्) (?).<BR>II To beat, drub: q. v.<BR>Ph.:<BR>to c. a horse:<BR>अश्वदेहं मार्ष्टि (मृज्, c. 2.);<BR>to c. favour with the people:<BR>लोकानाराधयति, U. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curry-comb
CURRY-COMB: *अश्वदेहमार्जनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curse
CURSE (v.) शपति, -ते, अभि-, (शप्, c. l.),<BR>c. d him<BR>“become a moral”:<BR>तमशपत् एहि मर्त्यत्वमिति, D. iii.;<BR>Kṛṣṇa gave no reply when the Chedi king was<BR>c. ing:<BR>प्रतिवाचमदत्त केशवः शपमानाय नचेदि भूभुजे, Si.<BR>xvi. 25. Ph.:<BR>I will c. and reduce your father to<BR>ashes:<BR>शापं दत्त्वा पितरं ते भस्मसात् करिष्यामि, P. i. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curse
CURSE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: शापः, अभिशापः।<BR>II<BR>Bane, pest: q. v.:<BR>c. of the nation:<BR>कुलाङ्गारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cursed
CURSED (adj.): expr. by -हत or -हतक affixed<BR>or<BR>दग्ध prefixed,<BR>c. son of Madri:<BR>माद्रीसुतहतकः,<BR>Ve.: v. Accursed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cursorily
CURSORILY: क्षिप्रम्: v. Hastily, slightly,<BR>summarily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cursory
CURSORY: क्षिप्रः (प्रा, प्रं): v. Superficial,<BR>slight, hasty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curst
CURST (adj.): संक्षिप्तः (प्ता, प्तं): v. Peevish,<BR>malignant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curt
CURT (adj.): संक्षिप्तः (प्ता, प्तं): v. Brief, concise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curtness
CURTNESS: संक्षेपः (पा, पं): v. Conciseness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curtail
CURTAIL (v.): To diminish, shorten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curtain
CURTAIN:<BR>(1) तिरस्करिणी;<BR>(2) जवनिका;<BR>(3)<BR>मशहरी (mosquito-c.). Ph.:<BR>the c. falls:<BR>जवनिका<BR> पतति (?); the c. rises: जवनिका उत्पतति (?);<BR>behind the c., (a) in theatrical language नेपथ्ये<BR>(loc.), (b) in gen. sense परोक्षे।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curtained
CURTAINED: अवगुण्ठितः (ता, तं): v. To veil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curtain-lecture
CURTAIN-LECTURE: *शय्यानुशासनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curtly
CURTLY: संक्षेपेण: v. Briefly, concisely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curule
CURULE: Ph.:<BR>c. chair:<BR>सिंहासनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curvature
CURVATURE: वक्रिमन् (m.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curve
CURVE (v.): वक्रीकरोति: v. To bend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curve
CURVE (subs.):<BR>I A bending: q. v.<BR>II A<BR>c. line: *वक्ररेखा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curved
CURVED:<BR>(1) वक्रः (क्रा, क्रं);<BR>(2) जिह्मितः (ता,<BR> तं): v. Crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curvet
CURVET (v.): v. To leap, bound, frisk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curvet
CURVET (subs.):<BR>I Of horses: वल्गितम्।<BR>II<BR>A prank, frolic: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curvilinear
CURVILINEAR: *वक्ररेखामयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cushion
CUSHION:<BR>(1) उपधानम्;<BR>(2) उपबर्हः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cushiony
CUSHIONY: v. Soft, pliable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cusp
CUSP: चुडा: v. Also point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

custard
CUSTARD: *दुग्धाण्डमिष्टम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

custard-apple
CUSTARD-APPLE:<BR>I The tree: आतृप्यः।<BR>II<BR>The fruit: आतृप्यम्<BR>or<BR>फलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

custodian
CUSTODIAN: रक्षकः: v. Keeper, superin-<BR>-tendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

custody
CUSTODY:<BR>I Charge, guarding: q. v. रक्षा।<BR>II Confinement: q. v.: निरोधः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

custom
CUSTOM:<BR>I Usage: आचारः, immemorial c.:<BR>शाश्वत आचारः, M.;<BR>deviating from c.:<BR>आचारा-<BR>द्विच्युतः, M.<BR>II. Business: q. v. Ph.:<BR>he has<BR>a great deal of c.:<BR>तस्यानेका ग्राहकाः।<BR>III A c.<BR>duty: शुल्क (mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

custom-house
CUSTOM-HOUSE: शुल्कशाला।<BR>C. officer:<BR>शुल्काधिकृतः;<BR> शुल्कोपजीवी, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

customary
CUSTOMARY:<BR>(1) आचार in comp.,<BR>c. taking of<BR>smoke:<BR>आचारधूमग्रहणम्, K. Ph.:<BR>it is c.:<BR>एष<BR> आचारः;<BR>(2) नित्यः (त्या, त्यं) (what should be<BR>observed daily), B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

customer
CUSTOMER: ग्राहकः,<BR>a known c.:<BR>परिचितग्राहकः,<BR>P. i. l.: v. Buyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cut
CUT (subs.):<BR>I A wound:<BR>(1) छिन्नम्, Sr.;<BR>(2) क्षतम् (=hurt, wound: q. v.)<BR>II A blow:<BR>(1) प्रहारः;<BR>(2) आघातः।<BR>III Portion cut<BR>off: छेदः।<BR>IV A slight. Ph.:<BR>this was an un-<BR>kind cut:<BR>*एष परिहारो निर्दय आसीत्।<BR>V A<BR>groove: q. v.: खातम्।<BR>VI An engraving:<BR>q. v.<BR>VII Shape: आकारः।<BR>VIII Of cards:<BR>*विभागः। Ph.:<BR>whose c. is it:<BR>*कस्य विभागावसरः।<BR>IX A horse: अश्वः। Ph.:<BR>a short c.:<BR>सरलमार्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cut
CUT (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 5.)<BR>(best equiv.),<BR>to c. the Śami tree:<BR>शमीलतां छेत्तुम्,<BR>Sa.;<BR>to c. nails:<BR>नखानि छिनत्ति, M. iv. 69.;<BR>c. ing the heart:<BR>भर्मच्छिद् (mfn.), Ki. xi. 49.;<BR>(2) लुनाति (लू, c. 9.),<BR>with hair c.:<BR>लूनकेशः,<BR>K. b.;<BR>c. ting of corn:<BR>व्रीहिलवनम्, S. c.;<BR>(3)<BR>कृन्तति (कृत्, c. 6.) नि-, to cut one's own throat:<BR>स्वस्य कण्ठं निकृन्तति, Mah.;<BR>(4) वृश्चति (व्रश्च, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">Page171</a>]<BR>c. l.) (rare),<BR>c. one another:<BR>परस्परं वव्रश्चुः,<BR>B. ;<BR>(5) द्यति (दो, c. 4.) (rare). Ph.:<BR>the dart<BR>was c. into three pieces:<BR>त्रिधा कृता शक्तिः, Ve. iv.<BR>II To carve: q. v.<BR>III To intersect:<BR>q. v.<BR>IV To castrate: q. v. Ph.:<BR>(1)<BR>to c.<BR>cards:<BR>*तासं कृन्तति;<BR>(2)<BR>to c. a figure:<BR>प्रतिष्ठां<BR> प्राप्नोति;<BR>(3)<BR>to c. a person:<BR>परिहरति;<BR>(4)<BR>to c.<BR>capers:<BR>उपहासं करोति;<BR>(5) to c. the teeth. V.<BR>To put forth;<BR>(6)<BR>c. -glass:<BR>*संस्कृतकाचः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cut
CUT (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.: v. Above.<BR>II To inter-<BR>-fere (as a horse): q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cut down
CUT DOWN:<BR>I To fell: छित्त्वा<BR>or<BR>लूत्त्वा or<BR>कर्तित्वा पातयति (c. of पत्); अवकृन्तति; अवद्यति,<BR>Ki.<BR>II To abash: q. v.: ह्रेपयति (c. of ह्री).<BR>III To reduce, diminish: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cutin
CUTIN or INTO: i. e. to interrupt: q. v. विच्छिनत्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cut off
CUT OFF:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) छिनत्ति, (their)<BR>heads<BR>were c. off:<BR>मूर्धनौ चिच्छिदाते, Vi. vi.;<BR>(2)<BR>कृन्तति, नि-,<BR>c. off his arms:<BR>भुजौ चकृततुस्तस्य,<BR>B. vi. 45.;<BR>(3) लुनाति,<BR>c. ting off the head of<BR>this boy:<BR>एतस्य शिशोः शिरो लूत्वा, Vi. iii.<BR>II<BR>To destroy: q. v.: to be c. off by disease:<BR>रोगेण क्षयं गच्छति, एति।<BR>III To interrupt:<BR>नि-रुणद्धि (रुध्, c. 5.),<BR>c. off supplies:<BR>वीवधं<BR> निरुणद्धि, Si. ii. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cut out
CUT OUT:<BR>I Lit.: उत्कृन्तति।<BR>II To con-<BR>-trive, adapt: q. v.<BR>III To supersede:<BR>q. v.: उच्छिनत्ति।<BR>IV To carry off: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cut short
CUT SHORT:<BR>I To abridge: संक्षिपति (क्षिप्,<BR>c. 6.). Ph.:<BR>to c. the matter short:<BR>किं बहुना।<BR>II To interrupt: Ph.: c. ing him short:<BR>अस्य वचनम् आक्षिप्य (क्षिप्, c. 6.), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cut to
CUT TO or IN PIECES:<BR>(1) खण्डखण्डं करोति;<BR>(2)<BR>खण्डशः<BR>or<BR>लवशः<BR>or<BR>सहस्रशः etc. छिनत्ति, कृन्तति,<BR>etc.;<BR>(3) शकलयति, वि-, (nomi.), Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cut under
CUT UNDER: v. To undersell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cut up
CUT UP:<BR>I To cut to pieces: q. v.: निकृन्तति,<BR>which c. s. up enemies’ army:<BR>परसेनानिकर्तनम्,<BR>Mah.<BR>II Fig.: to wound, assail:<BR>(1)<BR>गुरुभिर्दोषैर्मर्मसु निस्तुदति (तुद्, c. 6.). Ki. xvii. 43.;<BR>(2) खण्डयति (खण्ड्, c. 10.), B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cutaneous
CUTANEOUS: expr. by comp.,<BR>c. disease:<BR>त्वग्रोगः;<BR>c. eruption:<BR>दद्रुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cuticle
CUTICLE: अवभासिनी, Wilson: v. Skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cutlass
CUTLASS: कर्तरिका: v. Sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cutler
CUTLER: *छुरिकाकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cutlery
CUTLERY:<BR>I The business of a cutler:<BR>छुरिकाकारव्यवसायः।<BR>II Cutting instruments:<BR>*छुरिकादीनि (n. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cutlet
CUTLET: *भृष्टफालिका,<BR>veal c.:<BR>*भृष्टा वत्समांस-<BR>फालिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cutpurse
CUTPURSE: ग्रन्थिभेदः, -कः, M. ix. 277; v.<BR>Thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cutter
CUTTER:<BR>I One who cuts:<BR>(1) छेदकः;<BR>(2)<BR>छेत्तृ (m.);<BR>(3) छिद् in comp.,<BR>wood -c:<BR>वनछिद्;<BR>(4) लवनकर्तृ (m.),<BR>rice -c.:<BR>धान्यलवनकर्ता, K. b.<BR>II A cutting instrument: कर्तरिका।<BR>III A<BR>front teeth: v. Incisor.<BR>IV A small ship:<BR>perh. मद्गुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cut-throat
CUT-THROAT:<BR>I Subs.: कण्च्छेदकः: v. Mur-<BR>-derer.<BR>II Adj.: v. Murderous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cutting
CUTTING (adj.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) छित्वरः (री, रं);<BR>(2) व्रश्चनः (ना, नं).<BR>II Of wind or cold:<BR>perh. उद्वेगकारिन् (f. णी).<BR>III Biting, severe:<BR>q. v.: मर्मच्छिद् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

cutting
