DANDLE: v. To fondle, caress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dandriff
DANDRIFF, DANDRUFF: दारुणम्<BR>or<BR>दारुणकम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dandy
DANDY: दाम्भिकः (?): v. Fop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

danger
DANGER (subs.):<BR>(1) भयम् (fear: q. v.),<BR>the<BR>d. from the demon is passed:<BR>गतं सुरारिसम्भवं<BR> भयम्, V. ;<BR>(2) संशयः (=doubt: q. v.),<BR>we are<BR>all put in d. of our lives:<BR>सर्वे वयं जीवितसंशय-<BR>मारोपिताः, Ve. vii.;<BR>(3) विपद्, -त्तिः (cala-<BR>-mity: q. v.),<BR>you do not see my d.:<BR>न हि पश्यसि मे<BR> विपत्तिम्, Mr. ix.;<BR>(4) कण्टकम्, शल्यम् etc. (=any-<BR>-thing causing mischief or annoyance),<BR>clearing d. s of roads:<BR>स्थलपथशल्यशोधनम्, D. viii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dangerous
DANGEROUS:<BR>I Beset with danger:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रत्यवायमूयिष्ठः (ष्ठा, ष्ठं);<BR>(2) संकटः (टा, टं);<BR>(3)<BR>सम्बाधः (धा, धं), in a place not d. and pleasant:<BR>असम्बाधशिवे देशे, Ki.<BR>II Causing danger:<BR>भयावहः (हा, हं): v. Dreadful, danger. Ph.:<BR>d. illness:<BR>सांघातिकरोगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dangerously
DANGEROUSLY: expr. by circumlo., d. ill:<BR>सांघातिकरोगाक्रान्तः (न्ता, न्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dangle
DANGLE (v.): लोलति, वि- (लुल्, c. l.): v. To<BR>hang.<BR>D. about or after:<BR>अनुसरति (सृ, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dangler
DANGLER: कालक्षेपिन् (m.)<BR>or<BR>कालक्षेपकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dangling
DANGLING (adj.):<BR>(1) लोलः (ला, लं) वि-, व्या-;<BR>(2) चञ्चत् (f. न्ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dapper
DAPPER: Lively, smart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dapple
DAPPLE:<BR>I Adj.: विचित्रबिन्दुयुक्तः (क्ता, क्तं),<BR>A. r.: v. Spotted, variegated.<BR>II Subs.:<BR>बिन्दुः: v. Spot.<BR>III Verb.: चित्रवति (चित्र्,<BR>c. 10.): v. To variegate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dare
DARE (v. t.):<BR>I To venture: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>challenge: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dare
DARE (v. i.): Ph.:<BR>who d. s assail me:<BR>को मां<BR> धर्षयितुं शक्तः, A. r.;<BR>did not d. to enter:<BR>प्रवेष्टुं न<BR> विषेहिरे, Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

daring
DARING (subs.): साहसम् (=boldness and also<BR>bold act.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

daring
DARING (adj.):<BR>(1) साहसिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>निर्विशङ्कः (ङ्का, ङ्कं): v. Intrepid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

daringly
DARINGLY: साहसेन: v. Boldly, fearlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

daringness
DARINGNESS: साहसिकता: v. Boldness,<BR>courage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dark
DARK (subs.):<BR>I Darkness: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Secrecy: q. v. Ph.:<BR>in d.:<BR>गूढम्: v. Secretly.<BR>III Ignorance: q. v.:<BR>in the d.:<BR>अनभिज्ञः<BR>(ज्ञा, ज्ञं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dark
DARK (adj.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) by comp.,<BR>a d.<BR>place:<BR>अन्धकारभूमिः, Kar.; in a very d. night:<BR>घोरान्धकारे रात्रौ, Vet.;<BR>(2) तिमिरावृतः (ता, तं),<BR>तमसाभिभूतः (ता, तं). तिमिरनिरुद्धः (द्धा, द्धं);<BR>(3) तामसः (सी, सं);<BR>(4) निरालोकः (का, कं)<BR>and sim. comp. s. (=destitute of light).<BR>II<BR>Black: q. v.: कालः (ली, लं).<BR>III Obscure:<BR>q. v.: तमसावृतः (ता, तं), and sim. comp. s.<BR>IV Vile, wicked: q. v. V. Gloomy: q. v.<BR>VI Blind: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

darken
DARKEN (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अन्धकारीकरोति<BR>V. p.:<BR>(2) अन्धकारतां नयति, K.,<BR>d. ed by the<BR>shadows of:<BR>छायान्धकारितः (ता, तं), Vi. vii.<BR>II Fig.: to obscure, sully: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

darken
DARKEN (v. i.): i. e. to become dark: v.<BR>Dark and to become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

darkly
DARKLY: v. Dimly, obscurely, blindly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

darkness
DARKNESS:<BR>I Physical or moral:<BR>(1)<BR>अन्धकार (mn.),<BR>d. came on the plain:<BR>अन्धकार-<BR>मुदवाप समानि, Ki. ix. 11.;<BR>(2) तमस् (n.),<BR>d.<BR>dispelling:<BR>तमोपहः (हा, हं), D. ;<BR>(3) तिमिरम्,<BR>enveloped in d.:<BR>तिमिरावगुण्ठितः (ता, तं), Ku.;<BR>(4)<BR>तमसम् (in. comp. s),<BR>thick d.:<BR>धनसन्तमसम्, Si.;<BR>blinding d.:<BR>अन्धतमसम्, Vi.;<BR>(5) तमिस्रा (=ex-<BR>-tensive d.);<BR>(6) Ph.: ध्वान्तम्: to enter the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">Page174</a>]<BR>land of d.: दीर्घतरं तमः प्रविशति, Ki. xiii. 30.<BR>II<BR>Secrecy: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

darksome
DARKSOME: तामसः (सी, सं); v. Dark, obs-<BR>-cure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

darling
DARLING:<BR>(1) प्रियः (या, यं);<BR>(2) प्रियतमः (मा,<BR> मं): v. Dear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

darn
DARN (subs.): सूचिसंहितम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

darn
DARN (v.): सूच्या सं-दधाति<BR>or<BR>धत्ते (धा, c. 3.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

darnel
DARNEL: तृणविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dart
DART (subs.):<BR>(1) अस्त्रम् (=any missile);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रासः (any d. specially a lance). Species of d.:<BR>शल्यम्; शक्तिः; परिघः; मुशलः; पट्टिशः; कर्पणः;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dart
DART (v. t.): मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.),<BR>d. ed an iron<BR>spear at the demon:<BR>शक्तिं मुमोच दितिजं प्रति,<BR>Mat.; her companions d. ed glances at me:<BR>मामवलोक्य तस्याः सखीजनेन कटाक्षा मुक्ता, Ma. i.: v.<BR>To hurl; to emit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dart
DART (v. i.): Ph.: an arrow d. ed from the<BR>Pinaka (bow of Śiva): निपपात जवादिषुः पिनाकात्,<BR>Ki. xiii. 20.: v. To start, run.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dash
DASH (subs.):<BR>I Collision:<BR>(1) सङ्घट्टः;<BR>(2)<BR>समाघातः।<BR>II A check: q. v.<BR>III An<BR>admixture: Ph.: wine with a d. of water;<BR>जलसिक्तं मद्यम् (?);<BR>with a d. of white:<BR>ईषद्धवलाभः<BR>(भा, भं).<BR>IV An onset, a blow: q. v. V.<BR>Capacity for bold movements: प्रागल्भ्यम्।<BR>VI A line: रेखा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dash
DASH (v. t.):<BR>I To throw with violence:<BR>q. v. प्रसभं क्षिपति।<BR>II To shatter: q. v.:<BR>चूर्णीकरोति।<BR>To be d. ed:<BR>चूर्णीभवति।<BR>III To<BR>abash: q. v.<BR>IV To overspread partially:<BR>स्पर्शयति (c. of स्पृश्) (?): v. To mix.<BR>Comp. s: (a) d. off: i. e. to execute ra-<BR>-pidly: शीघ्रं करोति; (b.) d. out, i. e. to<BR>obliterate: q. v. व्या-मार्ष्टि<BR>or<BR>मार्जयति (मृज्, c. 2.<BR>and 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dash
DASH (v. i.): धावति (धाव्, c. l.): v. To rush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dastard
DASTARD:<BR>(1) कापुरुषः;<BR>(2) भीरुः: v. Coward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dastard
DASTARD, DASTARDLY (adj.): Ph.: d. conduct:<BR>कापुरुषत्वम्: v. Timid, base.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dastardy
DASTARDY: कापुरुषत्वम्: v. Cowardliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

data
DATA: स्वीकृतानि (n. pl.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

date
DATE (subs.):<BR>I A fruit: खर्जुरम्, -री।<BR>II<BR>Epoch:<BR>(1) कालः,<BR>the d. of Harsha Deva's<BR>accession:<BR>हर्षदेवराज्यारम्भकालः, Mahesha;<BR>(2)<BR>समयः।<BR>III Of letters, etc.: Ph.:<BR>it bears<BR>no d.:<BR>*लिखनदिनमत्र न वर्तते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

date
DATE (v. t.): *लिखनदिनम् आरोपयति (c. of रुह) or<BR>चिह्नयति (चिह्न्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

date
DATE (v. i.):<BR>I To begin: q. v.<BR>II To have<BR>a d.:<BR>d. d London, the 1st. June:<BR>*लण्डने जुनस्य<BR> प्रथमदिवसे लिखितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

date-tree
DATE-TREE: खर्जुरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dative case
DATIVE CASE:<BR>(1) सम्प्रदानम्;<BR>(2) सम्प्रदानकारकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

datura
DATURA: धुस्तू(स्तु)रः; धुत्तुरा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

daub
DAUB (v.): लिम्पति (लिप्, c. 6.): v. To bes-<BR>-mear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

daub
DAUB (subs.): लेपः: v. Smear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dauber
DAUBER:<BR>I Lit.: लेपकः, वि-, प्र-,।<BR>II A<BR>flatterer: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

daughter
DAUGHTER:<BR>(1) दुहितृ (f.);<BR>(2) तनया;<BR>(3)<BR>सुता;<BR>(4) पुत्री;<BR>(5) नन्दिनी;<BR>(6) in the case<BR>of proper names, also by patronymic,<BR>d. of<BR>Fanaka:<BR>जानकी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

daughter-in-law
DAUGHTER-IN-LAW:<BR>(1) स्नुषा;<BR>(2) पुत्रवधूः;<BR>(3) वधूः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

daunt
DAUNT: त्रासयति (c. of त्रस्): v. To terrify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dauntless
DAUNTLESS: निर्भयः (या, यं): v. Fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dauntlessness
DAUNTLESSNESS: निर्भीकता: v. Fearlessness,<BR>daring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dauphin
DAUPHIN: फरासीयराज्ञो ज्येष्ठपुत्रः; युवराजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dauphine
DAUPHINE, DAUPHINESS: i. e. wife of the<BR>Dauphin: फरासीययुवराजस्त्री।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

daw
DAW: काकजातीयपक्षिभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dawdle
DAWDLE: कालं क्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.): v. To<BR>trifle, loiter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dawdler
DAWDLER: v. Loiterer, idler<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dawn
DAWN (subs.):<BR>(1) अरुणोदयः;<BR>(2) उषस् (n.);<BR>(3)<BR>प्रत्यु (त्यू) षः;<BR>(4) प्रभातम्;<BR>(5) विभातम्:<BR>(6) दिन-<BR>मुखम्;<BR>(7) दिनादिः;<BR>(8) निशान्तः;<BR>(9) निशावसानम्।<BR>v. Morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dawn
DAWN (v. i.): Ph.:<BR>before the day d. ed:<BR>अप्रभातायां<BR> रजन्याम्, Mu. i.;<BR>when it was d. ing:<BR>प्रत्धुन्मि-<BR>षत्यरुणार्चिषि, D. ii. Fig.: as of genius:<BR>(1)<BR>उन्मिषति (मिष्, c. 6.);<BR>(2) उद्भिनत्ति (भिद्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

day
DAY:<BR>(1) दिनम्<BR>(2) दिवस (mn);<BR>(3) वासरम्;<BR>(4) अहन् (n.).<BR>A d. of the week:<BR>वारः।<BR>A lunar<BR>d.:<BR>तिथिः।<BR>D. to d.<BR>दिने दिने: v. Daily (adv).<BR>D. and night (adv.):<BR>(1) अहर्निशम्;<BR>(2) दिवा-<BR>निशम्;<BR>(3) दिवरात्रम्;<BR>(4) रात्रिन्दिवम्। A whole d.<BR>i. e. a d. and night: अहोरात्रः। The d. before:<BR>पूर्वेद्युः। The next d.: परेद्यः।<BR>Another d.:<BR>अन्येद्युः।<BR>Both d. s:<BR>उभयेद्युः।<BR>By d.:<BR>दिवा। Late in the d.:<BR>वैकाले।<BR>Even to this d.:<BR>अद्यापि। Every other d.:<BR>द्वितीये द्वितीये दिवसे।<BR>A d. 's hire:<BR>दैनिकी।<BR>In his<BR>d.:<BR>तत्काले: v. Time.<BR>The last of a Hindu<BR>month:<BR>संक्रान्तिः।<BR>Gained the d.:<BR>विजयं लेभे (लभ्,<BR>c. l): v. Victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

day-book
DAY-BOOK: दैनिकपुस्तकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

day-break
DAY-BREAK:<BR>(1) दिनमुखम्, Ki.;<BR>(2) निशान्तः;<BR>(3) प्रत्युषः: v. Dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

day-dream
DAY-DREAM: दिवास्वप्नः (?): v. Dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

day-labour
DAY-LABOUR, DAY-WORK: दिनकर्मन् (n.), and<BR>sim. comp s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

day-labourer
DAY-LABOURER: दिनकर्मकरः and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

day-light
DAY-LIGHT: दिवालोकः and sim. comp. s,<BR>yet it<BR>was like d. day and night:<BR>तथापि दिवसाकारं<BR> प्रकाशं तदहर्निशम्, Mat. Ph.:<BR>in the d.:<BR>तपति तपने;<BR>before d.:<BR>अनुदिते भास्करे।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

day-sight
DAY-SIGHT: रात्र्यन्धता,<BR>affected with d.:<BR>रात्र्यन्धः<BR>(न्धा, न्धं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

day-star
DAY-STAR:<BR>I The morning-star: q. v.<BR>II<BR>The sun: दिनमणिः, Go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

day-time
DAY-TIME: दिवाभागः,<BR>in the d.<BR>दिवा: v. Day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dazzle
DAZZLE (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>to d. the eye:<BR>चक्षुष-<BR>स्तेजांसि प्रतिहन्ति (हन्, c. 2.) K. ; d. d by it.:<BR>(1) तेन प्रतिहतेक्षणा, B. p.<BR>II Fig.: मोहयति (c.<BR>of मुह्): v. To charm, blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dazzling
DAZZLING (adj.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) लोचनानि प्रति-<BR>ध्नत् (f.), Ki.<BR>or<BR>प्रतिबध्नत् (f. ती), M. n. etc.;<BR>(2) (better) दुष्प्रेक्ष्यः (क्ष्या, क्ष्यं), दुर्दर्शः (र्शा,<BR> र्शं) etc.: v. Brilliant.<BR>II Fig.: v. Wonder-<BR>-ful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deacon
DEACON: *याजकः।<BR>D. ess:<BR>*याजिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deaconhood
DEACONHOOD, DEACONRY, DEACONSHIP: याजक-<BR>त्वम्; याजकपदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dead
DEAD (subs.):<BR>in the d. of night:<BR>विगाढायां<BR> शर्वर्याम्, C.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dead
DEAD (adj.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मृतः (ता, तं (best<BR>equiv.),<BR>naturally d.:<BR>स्वयं मृतः, H. ; half d.:<BR>मृतकल्पः (f. ल्पा), D. iv.;<BR>d. body:<BR>मृतकम्, D.<BR>vi.;<BR>(2) परासु (mfn.),<BR>fell d.:<BR>परासुरपतत्, Ku.<BR>xvii. 53.;<BR>(3) गतासु (mfn.), and sim. comp. s<BR>(=whose life is past),<BR>just d.:<BR>तत्क्षणविगत-<BR>जीवितः (ता, तं), K. ;<BR>(4) उपरतः (ता, तं); (a<BR>milder term deceased), Da. (rarely);<BR>(5)<BR>प्रेतः (ता, तं);<BR>(6) संस्थितः (ता, तं);<BR>(7) प्रमीतः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(8) परेतः (ता, तं);<BR>II Of civil<BR>death: perh. मृतकल्पः (ल्पा, ल्पं); निरंशकः<BR>(का, कं) (=entitled to no share of ances-<BR>-tral property), Y.<BR>III. Fig.: d. language:<BR>अप्रचलितभाषा (?);<BR>d. sleep:<BR>घोरनिद्रा; d. darkness:<BR>घोरान्धकारः;<BR>d. drunk:<BR>मदमूढः (ढा, ढं); d. letter<BR>(i. e. obsolete): लुप्तः (प्ता, प्तं); d. letter (i. e.<BR>unclaimed letter): *अगृहीतपत्रम्; d. lock: v.<BR>Stoppage.<BR>IV Without motion as a d.<BR>weight: निश्चलः (ला, लं).<BR>V. Unproductive:<BR>निष्फलः (ला, लं).<BR>VI Dull, monotonous:<BR>q. v.<BR>VII Fixed: q. v.<BR>VIII Vapid: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dead
DEAD, BE: म्रियते: v. To die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deaden
DEADEN (v. t.):<BR>I To blunt, impair: q. v.:<BR>कुण्ठीकरोति।<BR>II To retard: q. v.<BR>III To make<BR>vapid: विरसीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deaden
DEADEN (v. i.): कुण्ठीभवति: v. To blunt, de-<BR>-cay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deadliness
DEADLINESS:<BR>(1) प्राणहरत्वम्;<BR>(2) प्राणनाशकत्वम्;<BR>(3) better by adj.: v. Deadly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deadly
DEADLY (adj.):<BR>I Destructive:<BR>(1) प्राणहरः<BR>(री, रं),<BR>d. poison:<BR>प्राणहरं विषम्, Ni.;<BR>(2)<BR>प्राणान्तिकः (का, कं):<BR>(3) प्राणनाशकः (शिका,<BR> शकं);<BR>(4) जीवितापहः (हा, हं) and sim. comp. s.<BR>II Fig.: implacable: q. v.: d. enmity:<BR>आमरणान्तिकं वैरम्, Mr. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deadly
DEADLY (adv.):<BR>I Mortally: q. v.:<BR>II Like<BR>death: expr. by comp.,<BR>d. pale:<BR>शवश्यावः (वा,<BR> वं).<BR>II Exceedingly: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deadness
DEADNESS:<BR>I Numbness: q. v.: स्तब्धता।<BR>II<BR>Languor: q. v.: ग्लानिः।<BR>III Inactivity:<BR>q. v.: शैथिल्यम्।<BR>IV Vapidness: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dead-wind
DEAD-WIND: प्रतीपवायुः, प्रतीपगा मरुतः, R.; and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deaf
DEAF:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) बधिरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) एडः (डा,<BR> डं) (rare),<BR>d. mute:<BR>एडमूकः (का, कं);<BR>(3) कल्लः,<BR>(ल्ला, ल्लं) (rare);<BR>(4) विकलश्रोत्रः (त्रा, त्रं), and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR>II Fig.: unwilling to hear:<BR>कर्णं न ददाति<BR>or<BR>न कर्णे करोति, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deafen
DEAFEN:<BR>(1) बधिरयति (nomi.);<BR>(2) बधिरीकरोति,<BR>Si. xiii. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deafening
DEAFENING (adj.):<BR>(1) कर्णविदारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) श्रोत्रभिद् (mfn.), Ki. xiii. 21.; and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deafness
DEAFNESS:<BR>(1) बधिरता;<BR>(2) बाधिर्यम्, Viv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deal
DEAL (subs.):<BR>I A quantity: expr. by बहु<BR>(mfn.),<BR>a great d. of time:<BR>बहुसमयः: v. Much,<BR>a good d.:<BR>अत्यन्तम्: v. Exceedingly.<BR>II In<BR>cards: वण्टनम्।<BR>III D. wood: देवदारु (n.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deal
DEAL (v. t.):<BR>I To d. out: वण्टयति (वण्ट्, c. 10.):<BR>v. To distribute.<BR>II Of cards: *वण्टयति।<BR>III Of blows, etc.: ददाति (दा, c. 3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deal
DEAL (v. i.):<BR>I To traffic: q. v.: क्रयविक्रयं<BR> करोति।<BR>II To act, behave: q. v. D. with:<BR>(a) to treat, handle: q. v.; (b) to con-<BR>-tend: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dealer
DEALER:<BR>I A Trader, merchant: q. v.:<BR>विक्रेतृ (m.),<BR>horse d.:<BR>अश्वविक्रेता।<BR>II Of cards:<BR>*वण्टकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dealing
DEALING:<BR>I Traffic, trade: q. v.: क्रयविक्रयः।<BR>II Intercourse, connexion: q. v. संसर्गः।<BR>III Treatment: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dean
DEAN:<BR>I Under a bishop: *आचार्यः,<BR>d. and<BR>chapter:<BR>*धर्मसमाजः।<BR>II The president of a<BR>faculty: सभापतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deanery
DEANERY: i. e. a dean's house: *आचार्यावासः<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dear
DEAR (adj.):<BR>I High-priced:<BR>(1) दुर्मूल्यः<BR>(f. ल्या):<BR>(2) बहुमूल्यः (ल्या, ल्यं),<BR>sell cheap<BR>things at a d. price:<BR>अल्पमूल्यं बहुमूल्येन विक्रीणते, Viv.<BR>(3) गुरुमूल्यः (ल्या, ल्यं), Viv.: v. Costly.<BR>II Highly valued:<BR>(1) प्रियः (या, यं) (=be-<BR>-loved: q. v.),<BR>d. er than myself:<BR>मत्तः प्रियतरः,<BR>K.;<BR>(2) अभिमतः (ता, तं),<BR>with his d. friend<BR>spring:<BR>माधवेनाभिमतेन सख्या, Ku.;<BR>(3) हृदय-<BR>ङ्गमः (मा, मं) (=reaching the heart), d. friend:<BR>हृदयङ्गमः सखा, Ku. iv. 24. Ph.:<BR>d. as one's<BR>life:<BR>प्राणसमः (मा, मं), K. ;<BR>to an old man, a young<BR>wife is d. er than his life:<BR>वृद्धस्य तरुणी भार्या<BR> प्राणेभ्योऽपि गरीयसी, H. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dear
DEAR, DEARLY (adv.):<BR>I At a high rate:<BR>(1) बहुमूल्येन;<BR>(2) महार्घेण।<BR>II Greatly: q. v.:<BR>अत्यन्तम्, “d. loved”: अतिप्रियः (या, यं).<BR>III Affec-<BR>-tionately: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dearness
DEARNESS:<BR>I High price:<BR>(1) दुर्मूल्यता;<BR>(2)<BR>महार्घता<BR>(3) दुर्लभता (scarcity).<BR>II Tender-<BR>-ness: प्रियत्वम्, -ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

death
DEATH:<BR>(1) मृत्युः,<BR>unnatural d.:<BR>अपमृत्युः, P. ;<BR>premature d.:<BR>अकालमृत्युः, U.;<BR>violent d.:<BR>अपघातभृत्युः;<BR>under the grasp of d.:<BR>मृत्युहस्तवर्तिन् (f. नी),<BR>D. ;<BR>who have met d. for you:<BR>तवार्थे मृत्युमीयुषां,<BR>Mah.;<BR>(2) मरणम्,<BR>did not meet d.:<BR>मरणं नाभ्यपद्यत,<BR>Mah.;<BR>the swing of birth and d.:<BR>जननमरणदोला,<BR>J.<BR>(3) प्राणवियोगः and sim. comp. s (=extinc-<BR>-tion of life);<BR>(4) प्राणपरित्यागः and sim.<BR>comp. s (=quitting life: only of volun-<BR>-tary d.)<BR>(5) वधः (=killing: q. v.), to seek d.:<BR>वधं मृगयते, Ka. Ph.:<BR>pelted to d.:<BR>लोष्ट्राघातं हतः,<BR>Mu. ii.;<BR>longing for d.:<BR>मृत्युकामः (मा, मं),<BR>V. p.;<BR>sentence of d.:<BR>प्राणदण्डः,<BR>will pass sentence<BR>of d. on this man with forfeiture of all property:<BR>अस्य सर्वस्वप्राणहरणं दण्डमाज्ञापयिष्यति, Mu. i.;<BR>angel<BR>of d.:<BR>यमदूतः, V. p.;<BR>after d.:<BR>प्रेत्य (rare), D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

death
DEATH, PUT TO:<BR>(1) हन्ति (हन्, c. 2.),<BR>put him<BR>to d. at once,<BR>हन्यतामविलम्बितम्: V. p.;<BR>(2) व्यापाद-<BR>यति (c. of पद्),<BR>no, he has not been put to d.,<BR>but thrown into prison:<BR>न खलु व्यापादितः परन्तु बन्ध-<BR>नागारे निक्षिप्तः, Mu. ii.;<BR>(3) by वधः,<BR>the king<BR>ordered him to be put to d.:<BR>राज्ञा (तस्य) वध<BR> आदिष्टः, P. ; one who should not be put to d.:<BR>अवध्यः (ध्या, ध्यं): v. To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

death-bed
DEATH-BED: मृत्युशय्या।<BR>On one's d.:<BR>मृत्यकाले or<BR>मरणसमये, Vet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deathless
DEATHLESS: अमरः (रा, रं): v. Immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

death-like
DEATH-LIKE: v. Cadaverous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deaths head
DEATH'S HEAD: a moth: *कापालिकः; कपाल-<BR>चिह्रितपक्षः पतङ्गभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

death-warrant
DEATH-WARRANT: वधादेशलेखः, and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

death-watch
DEATH-WATCH: गोमयोत्थाप्रभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debar
DEBAR (v.): प्रतिषेधति (सिध्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>prevent, exclude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debark
DEBARK: अवतरति (तृ, c. 1.): v. To disem-<BR>-bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debase
DEBASE:<BR>(1) अपकर्षति (c. of कृष्);<BR>(2) अवनमयति<BR>(c. of नम्);<BR>(3) by adj.: v. Base.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debasement
DEBASEMENT:<BR>(1) अपकर्षः;<BR>(2) अवमानना (=dis-<BR>-grace: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debatable
DEBATABLE:<BR>(1) विवदनीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) सन्दिग्धः<BR>(ग्धा, ग्धं) (=doubtful).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debate
DEBATE (subs.):<BR>(1) विवादः,<BR>and there were d. s<BR>amongst themselves.<BR>अन्योन्यस्य विवादाश्च प्रादुरभूवन्,<BR>C. ;<BR>(2) वादः: v. Controversy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debate
DEBATE (v.):<BR>(1) विवदते (विद्, c. l.): v. To<BR>dispute;<BR>(2) विचारयति (c. of चर्): v. To<BR>discuss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debater
DEBATER:<BR>(1) वादिन् (m.);<BR>(2) वक्तृ (m.) (strictly<BR>=speaker), Ki.;<BR>(3) तर्किन् (m.) (=argu-<BR>-mentator).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debauch
DEBAUCH (v.): नाशयति (c. of नश्),<BR>great attach-<BR>ment to sensual pleasures d. es a man:<BR>नाशयति<BR> पुरुषमत्यासङ्गो विषयेषु, K. ;<BR>to d. a girl:<BR>बालां नाश-<BR>यति, D. ii.: v. To corrupt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debauch
DEBAUCH (subs.):<BR>I Debauchery: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Revel: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debauchee
DEBAUCHEE:<BR>(1) लम्पटः: v. Lewd;<BR>(2) काम-<BR>वृत्तः: v. Libertine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debaucher
DEBAUCHER:<BR>(1) नाशकः;<BR>(2) दूषकः;<BR>(3) दूष-<BR>यितृ (m.):<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debauchery
DEBAUCHERY:<BR>I Corruption: q. v.: नाशः।<BR>II Lewdness, libertinism: q. v.: लाम्पट्यम्<BR>III Intemperance: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debenture
DEBENTURE: *देयलेखः; देयस्वीकारपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debilitate
DEBILITATE: क्षिणोति (क्षि, c. 5.): v. To<BR>weaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debility
DEBILITY: दर्बलता: v. Feebleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debit
DEBIT (v.): *देयधनभागे लिखति (लिख, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debit
DEBIT (subs.): Ph.:<BR>d. side:<BR>देयधनभागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debonair
DEBONAIR: विनीतः (ता, तं): v. Gentle, affa-<BR>-ble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debt
DEBT: ऋणम् (lit. and fig.):<BR>to discharge a d.:<BR>ऋणं<BR> शोधयति, K. b.;<BR>to contract a d.:<BR>ऋणं करोति,<BR>D. s.;<BR>involved in d.:<BR>ऋणग्रस्तः (स्ता, स्तं), At.;<BR>recovery of a d.:<BR>ऋणादानम्, M.; as I may get out<BR>of this (d.): तस्मान्मुच्ये यथा, R. i. 72.;<BR>one who<BR>is unable to pay d.:<BR>ऋणं दातुमशक्तो यः, M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debtor
DEBTOR:<BR>(1) ऋणिन् (m.)<BR>or<BR>ऋणिकः (lit. and<BR>fig.);<BR>(2) अधमर्णः (lit.);<BR>(3) ऋणग्रहीतृ (m.), K.<BR>b.;<BR>(4) खादकः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

debut
DEBUT:<BR>I A beginning: प्रारम्भः।<BR>II A first<BR>appearance: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decade
DECADE: i. e. ten of any thing: d. (of years):<BR>दशवर्षम्: v. Ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decadence
DECADENCE, DECADENCY: अवसादः: v. Decay,<BR>decline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decagon
DECAGON: दशकोणः (णा, णं); दशभुजः (जा, जं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decalogue
DECALOGUE: *निदेशदशकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decamp
DECAMP:<BR>I To break up a camp: कटकं<BR> भनक्ति (भञ्ज्, c. 7.)<BR>or<BR>स्थानान्तरं नयति (नी, c.<BR>1.).<BR>II To go away, flee: q. v.: अपसर्पति<BR>(सृप्, c. l.),<BR>d. ed from the battle:<BR>रणादपससर्प,<BR>Mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decampment
DECAMPMENT:<BR>I Lit.: कटकभञ्जनम् (?).<BR>II Fli-<BR>-ght: q. v.: अपसर्पणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decant
DECANT: स्रावयति (c. of स्रु) (?): v. To pour<BR>gently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decanter
DECANTER: a glass vessel: भरी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decapitate
DECAPITATE: शिरः छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7.) (with<BR>gen.): v. To behead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decapitation
DECAPITATION: शिरश्छेद: v. Beheading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decay
DECAY (v. i.):<BR>(1) क्षीयते, परि-, (pass. of क्षि)<BR>or<BR>क्षयं गच्छति, याति, etc.; of un-d. ed loyalty:<BR>अक्षीणभक्तिः, Mu.;<BR>when the night d. ed:<BR>क्षीणायां<BR> क्षपायाम्, K. ;<BR>(2) शीर्यते, वि-, (pass. of शॄ) (=<BR>go to ruin),<BR>doors of income d. ed:<BR>आयद्वाराणि<BR> व्यशीर्यन्त, D. ;<BR>d. ed leaf:<BR>शीर्णपर्णः, Me.;<BR>(3)<BR>जीर्यति<BR>or<BR>जरति (जॄ, c. 4. and 1.) (from age):<BR>the teeth of a d. ing man d.:<BR>दन्ता जीर्यन्ति जीर्यतः,<BR>P. v. 10.;<BR>d. ed bark:<BR>जीर्णवल्कलम्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decay
DECAY (subs.):<BR>(1) क्षयः, परि-,<BR>d. of fame:<BR>यशः-<BR>क्षयः, Ki.;<BR>(2) विशीर्णता (going to ruin: as a<BR>building);<BR>(3) जीर्णता (from age);<BR>(4) अव-<BR>सादः (=failing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decaying
DECAYING (adj.):<BR>(1) क्षयिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2)<BR>क्षयिष्णु (mfn.);<BR>(3) क्षीयमाण (f. णा), परि-;<BR>(4) विशीर्यमाण (f. णा);<BR>(5) जीर्यत् (f. न्ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decease
DECEASE:<BR>I Subs.: उपरमः: v. Demise.<BR>II<BR>Verb: v. To die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deceased
DECEASED: उपरतः (ता, तं): v. Dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deceit
DECEIT:<BR>I Deception: q. v.: प्रतारणा।<BR>II<BR>Artifice, strategem:<BR>(1) छलम्,<BR>d. is not admit-<BR>ted here:<BR>छलमत्र न गृह्यते, Mr.;<BR>(2) कपट (mfn.),<BR>able to follow out d.:<BR>कपटानुसारकुशलः, Mr.;<BR>(3)<BR>छह्मन् (n.) (strictly = disguise),<BR>by d.:<BR>छह्मना,<BR>Viv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deceitful
DECEITFUL:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्रतारणापरायण (f. णा);<BR>(2) वञ्चनाशीलः (ला, लं);<BR>(3) छलनापरः (रा, रं);<BR>(4) कपटप्रवण (f. णा).<BR>II Fig.: false: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deceitfully
DECEITFULLY:<BR>(1) छलेन;<BR>(2) सकपटम्;<BR>(3)<BR>छद्मना;<BR>(4) सव्याजम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deceitfulness
DECEITFULNESS:<BR>(1) प्रतारणापरायणता;<BR>(2) वञ्चन-<BR>शीलता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deceitless
DECEITLESS:<BR>(1) निष्कपटः (टा, टं);<BR>(2) निर्व्याजः<BR>(जा, जं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deceive
DECEIVE:<BR>(1) प्रतारयति (c. of तॄ),<BR>was d. d and<BR>drawn away to the bush:<BR>प्रतार्य तेनाचकृषे लतासु, N.;<BR>(2) वञ्चयते (वञ्च्, c. 10.),<BR>d. ing me:<BR>मां वञ्चयित्वा,<BR>P. ;<BR>(3) छलयति (छल्, c. 10),<BR>to the d. r of<BR>Bali:<BR>बलिं छलयते, Gi.;<BR>(4) विप्रलभते (लभ्, c. 1.);<BR>(5) अभिसन्धत्ते (धा, c. 3.), Sa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deceiver
DECEIVER:<BR>(1) प्रतारकः;<BR>(2) वञ्चकः;<BR>(3) विप्रलम्भकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

december
DECEMBER: उत्तराग्रहायणपूर्वपौषसंवादीयुरुपीयवत्सरस्य<BR> द्वादशो मासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decemvir
DECEMVIR: दशानाम् एकः।<BR>D. i.:<BR>*दश; प्राचीनरोमकस्य<BR> दशशासकाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decemviral
DECEMVIRAL: *दशानाम्,<BR>d. government:<BR>दशानां<BR> शासनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decemvirate
DECEMVIRATE: दशाधिपत्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decency
DECENCY:<BR>(1) शालीनता (=modesty);<BR>(2) विनयः:<BR>v. Decorum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decennial
DECENNIAL:<BR>(1) दशवार्षिकः (की, कं):<BR>(2) दशा-<BR>ब्दिकः (की, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decent
DECENT:<BR>I Decorous:<BR>(1) विनीतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) विनयोपेतः (ता, तं).<BR>II Not obscene: साधु-<BR>सम्मतः (ता, तं).<BR>III Sufficient: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decently
DECENTLY:<BR>(1) शालीनतया (modestly);<BR>(2)<BR>समुचितम् (=suitably).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deception
DECEPTION:<BR>(1) प्रतारणा, -णम्,<BR>well up in d.:<BR>प्रतारण-<BR>कुशलः (ला, लं), K. ;<BR>(2) वञ्चना, प्र-, even d. is a<BR>gain:<BR>वञ्चनापि लाभाय, M. n.;<BR>(3) छलना,<BR>addicted<BR>to d.:<BR>छलनापरः, Si.;<BR>(4) विप्रलम्भः, means of d.:<BR>विप्रलम्भोपायः, D.<BR>(5) अभिसन्धानम्, Sa. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deceptive
DECEPTIVE: भ्रान्तिजनकः (का, कं), and sim.<BR>comp. s: v. False.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deceptiveness
DECEPTIVENESS: भ्रान्तिजनकत्वम्: v. Falsity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decide
DECIDE (v. t.):<BR>(1) निर्णयति (नी, c. l.),<BR>we are<BR>to d., the rest rests with the king:<BR>निर्णये वयं प्रमाणं,<BR> शेषे तु राजा, Mr. ix.;<BR>(2) निश्चिनोति, (चि, c. 5.),<BR>he d. d that the r had been altered into s by the<BR>merchant:<BR>रेफे सकारं वणिजा कारितं निश्चिकायसः, Raj.<BR>(3) स्थिरीकरोति (=to fix.),<BR>to d. the meaning of<BR>the plaint:<BR>भाषार्थस्थिरीकरणाय, K. b. Ph.:<BR>d. ing<BR>for and against according to pleasure:<BR>स्वेच्छया<BR> जयपराजयौ विदधानाः (m. pl.), D. viii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decided
DECIDED (adj.):<BR>(1) निश्चितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) स्थिरः<BR>(रा, रं) (=firm);<BR>(3) असन्दिग्धः (ग्धा, ग्धं)<BR>(=undoubted: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decidedly
DECIDEDLY:<BR>(1) निश्चितम्;<BR>(2) असंशयम्: v. Un-<BR>-doubtedly, certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decider
DECIDER: निर्णेतृ (m.): v. Judge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deciduous
DECIDUOUS: पतनशीलः (ला, लं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decimal
DECIMAL: *दशकः (का, कं),<BR>d. fraction:<BR>*दशक-<BR>भिन्नम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decimate
DECIMATE:<BR>I Lit.: दशाशं गृह्वाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.).<BR>II To punish every tenth man of: दशम-<BR>भागस्य प्राणदण्डं करोति (with gen.).<BR>III To<BR>devastate: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decimation
DECIMATION: दशमभागस्य वधः<BR>or<BR>प्राणदण्डः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decipher
DECIPHER: निर्वाचयति (c. of वच्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decipherer
DECIPHERER: निर्वाचकः।<BR>Decipheress:<BR>निर्वाचिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decision
DECISION:<BR>I Adjudication: निर्णयः,<BR>d. of a<BR>case:<BR>व्यवहारनिर्णयः, K. b.<BR>II Firmness: q. v.:<BR>स्थैर्यम्।<BR>A man of d.:<BR>स्थिरधीः, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decisive
DECISIVE: निश्चायकः (का, कं) (?); संशयच्छिद्<BR>(mfn.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decisively
DECISIVELY: v. Decidedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deck
DECK (subs.): *छदः; नौपृष्ठभ्।<BR>Four d. ed:<BR>*चतु-<BR>श्छदः (दा, दं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deck
DECK (v.):<BR>I To adorn: q. v.: भूषयति (भूष्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR>II To furnish with a deck: छदेन<BR> योजयति (युज्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

declaim
DECLAIM (v.):<BR>(1) माषते (भाष्, c. 1.): v. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">Page179</a>]<BR>speak;<BR>(2) गिरामूर्मीः निर्मिमीते (मा, c. 3)<BR>(poet), N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

declaimer
DECLAIMER, DECLAIMANT: वक्त (m.): v.<BR>Speaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

declamation
DECLAMATION:<BR>I Speech: q. v.: गिर् (f.)<BR>(often in the pl.).<BR>II Rhetorical display:<BR>वागाडम्बरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

declamatory
DECLAMATORY:<BR>I Lit.: वाङ्मयः (यी, यं).<BR>II<BR>Fig.: v. Bombastic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

declaration
DECLARATION:<BR>I Assertion, statement: q. v.<BR>उक्तिः।<BR>II Announcement, proclamation:<BR>q. v.: ख्यापनम् Ph.: the D. of Independence:<BR>*स्वाधीनताख्यापनम्, -पत्रम्।<BR>IV In law: भाषा, K.<BR>b.; भाषापदम्, Mi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

declarative
DECLARATIVE, DECLARATORY: v. Expres-<BR>-sive, explanatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

declare
DECLARE (v. t.):<BR>I To clear: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>assert: q. v.: ब्रवीति<BR>or<BR>ब्रूते (ब्रू, c. 2.).<BR>III<BR>To make known, manifest: q. v.: ब्रवीति or<BR>ब्रूते,<BR>for good men d. their use by results:<BR>ब्रुवते हि<BR> फलेन साधवो निजोपयोगिताम्, N.<BR>IV. To proclaim:<BR>q. v.: घोषयति (c. of घष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

declare
DECLARE (v. i.): ब्रवीति v. To say. To d. for:<BR>अवलम्बते।<BR>To d. against:<BR>प्रतिपक्षम् अवलम्बते (लम्ब्,<BR>c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

declension
DECLENSION:<BR>I Decline: q. v.<BR>II In gram.<BR>शब्दरूपाखयानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

declinable
DECLINABLE: नैकरूपः (पा, पं) (i. e. having<BR>more than one form).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

declination
DECLINATION:<BR>I Obliquity: q. v.<BR>II In<BR>astr: अपमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decline
DECLINE (v. i.):<BR>I To bend over: लम्बते, अव-,<BR>(लम्ब्, c. l.).<BR>II To decay, diminish: q. v.:<BR>हासमुपैति (इ, c. 2.).<BR>III Of day, etc.:<BR>(1)<BR>परिणमति (नम् c. l.), by this time the day d. d.:<BR>अनेन समयेन परिणतो दिवसः, K. ;<BR>(2) गलति (गल्,<BR>c. l.),<BR>the third watch d. ing:<BR>गलति तृतीये यामे,<BR>C. ;<BR>(3) क्षीयते,<BR>when the night d. d.:<BR>क्षीणायां<BR> क्षपायाम्, K.<BR>IV. To deviate: q. v.<BR>V. To<BR>refuse: q. v. प्रत्याख्याति (ख्या, c. 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decline
DECLINE (v. t.):<BR>I To refuse, reject: q. v.:<BR>प्रत्याख्याति।<BR>II To inflect: Ph.:<BR>d.<BR>पतिः *पते<BR> रूपाण्याख्याहि (ख्या, c. 2.).<BR>III To bend: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decline
DECLINE (subs.):<BR>(1) ह्रासः (=decrease),<BR>by the<BR>rise and d. of prices:<BR>अर्घस्य वृद्धिह्रासेन, Vy.;<BR>(2)<BR>क्षयः (=decay),<BR>d. of fame:<BR>यशःक्षयः, Ki.;<BR>(3) परिणामः,<BR>or<BR>परिणतिः, (lit., bending: of<BR>life or time),<BR>d. of life:<BR>वयःपरिणामः, K. ;<BR>d. of<BR>night:<BR>रात्रेः परिणतिः, Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

declining
DECLINING (subs.): प्रत्याख्यानम्: v. Refusal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

declivity
DECLIVITY:<BR>(1) अवसर्पिणी भूमिः;<BR>(2) नतभूः: v.<BR>Slope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decoction
DECOCTION: क्वाथः (both of decocting and of<BR>the extract).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decollate
DECOLLATE: v. To behead. “D. d head”: छिन्न-<BR>शिरस् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decompose
DECOMPOSE (v. i.):<BR>I To dissolve: विलीयते<BR>(ली, c. 4.).<BR>II To decay: पूयते (पूय्, c. l.) (?).<BR>v. Decomposition (III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decompose
DECOMPOSE (v. t.):<BR>I To analyze: q. v.<BR>II<BR>To dissolve: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decomposition
DECOMPOSITION:<BR>I Analysis: *विश्लेषः।<BR>II<BR>Dissolution:<BR>(1) विलयः;<BR>(2) परिक्षयः।<BR>III<BR>Corruption: पूतिः, that there might be no d.:<BR>माभूत् पूतिरिति, B. com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decorate
DECORATE:<BR>(1) प्रसाधयति (c. of साध्);<BR>(2)<BR>आकल्पयति (कल्प्, c. 10.): v. To adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decoration
DECORATION:<BR>(1) प्रसाधनम्, Ka. vii. 30;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रतिकर्मन्<BR>or<BR>परिकर्मन् (n.). Ku. vii. 6.;<BR>(3)<BR>आकल्पः: v. Ornament; adornment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decorator
DECORATOR:<BR>(1) प्रसाधकः (f. धिका);<BR>(2) अल-<BR>ङ्कर्तृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decorous
DECOROUS: विनीतः (ता, तं),<BR>in a d. dress:<BR>विनीत-<BR>वेषेण, Sa.: v. Becoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decorously
DECOROUSLY:<BR>(1) सविनयम्;<BR>(2) विनयेन;<BR>(3)<BR>यथोचितम् (=suitably).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decorum
DECORUM:<BR>(1) विनयः, seeing his ripeness in d.:<BR>वीक्ष्य तस्य विनये परिपाकम्, N. ;<BR>(1) मर्यादा,<BR>trans-<BR>gressor of d.:<BR>मर्यादालङ्घिन् (f. नी), M. n.;<BR>(3)<BR>स्थितिः,<BR>breaker of d.:<BR>स्थितिभिद् (mfn.), R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decoy
DECOY (v. t.): आकर्षति (c. of कृष्): v. To<BR>entrap, allure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decoy
DECOY (subs.): i. e. a d. -bird: आकर्षकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decrease
DECREASE (subs.):<BR>(1) ह्रासः, from gradual d.:<BR>अल्पाल्पह्रासात्, V. p.;<BR>(2) क्षयः (=gen. decay),<BR>d. and increase:<BR>क्षयवृद्धी, Su.;<BR>(2) अपक्षयः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decrease
DECREASE (v. t.): v. To diminish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decrease
DECREASE (v. i.):<BR>(1) ह्रासमुपैति, अधिगच्छति, etc.,<BR>spirit d. s:<BR>सत्वं ह्रासमुपैति, Mr.;<BR>(2) क्षीयते,<BR> परि-, (pass. of क्षि),<BR>the nights d. when the sun<BR>is on the north of the equator:<BR>क्षीयन्ते खलूत्तरायणे<BR> रात्रयः M. n.;<BR>(3) हीयते, परि-, प्र-, (pass. of हा),<BR>every day you are d. ing in your body:<BR>अनुदिवसं<BR> खलु परिहीयसेऽङ्गेषु, Sa.;<BR>(4) अपचीयते (pass. of<BR>चि) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decree
DECREE (subs.):<BR>(1) आज्ञा;<BR>(2) आदेशः: v.<BR>Order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decree
DECREE (v.):<BR>I To order: q. v.:<BR>(1) आदिशति<BR>(दिश्, c. 6.);<BR>(2) दापयति (c. of दा) (=cause<BR>to give),<BR>should d. the debt to the creditor:<BR>धनिने<BR> धनं दापयेत्, Y.<BR>II. To decide: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decrement
DECREMENT: ह्रासः: v. Decrease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decrepit
DECREPIT:<BR>(1) जरातुरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) जराजीर्णेन्द्रियः<BR>(या, यं);<BR>(3) जरत् (f. ती) d. son of Ganga:<BR>जरद्गाङ्गेयः, Ve.: v. Infirm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decrepitude
DECREPITUDE: जरा,<BR>d. and deformity:<BR>जरा वैरूप्य-<BR>मेव च, V. p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decretal
DECRETAL (adj:): expr. by comp., d. epistle:<BR>आदेशपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decretal
DECRETAL (subs.): a collection of decrees:<BR>आदेशसंग्रहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decrial
DECRIAL: अपक्रोश: v. Calumny, abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decry
DECRY: परिवदति (वद्, c. l.): v. To disparage,<BR>censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decurion
DECURION: दशाध्यक्षः, and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decussation
DECUSSATION: तिर्यक्पातः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dedicate
DEDICATE:<BR>I To consecrate: q. v.: उत्सृजति<BR>(सृज्, c. l.).<BR>II To devote: q. v.<BR>III To<BR>d. books, etc.: समर्पयति (c. of ऋ) (?);<BR>उत्सृजति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dedication
DEDICATION:<BR>I Consecration, appropriation:<BR>उत्सर्गः।<BR>II Of a book: मुखबन्धः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dedicatory
DEDICATORY: Ph.:<BR>d. epistle:<BR>मुखबन्धः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deduce
DEDUCE:<BR>I To derive or draw: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>infer: q. v.:<BR>(1) निर्णयति (नी c. l.);<BR>(2)<BR>लभते (लभ्, c. l.) (to get).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deducible
DEDUCIBLE:<BR>(1) अनुमेयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) लभ्यः<BR>(भ्या, भ्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deduct
DEDUCT v. t.: वियोजयति (युज्, c. 10.) Ph.: capital<BR>d. ed from amount is interest:<BR>मूलं मिश्राच्च्युतं<BR> कलान्तरम्, Li.: v. To subtract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deduction
DEDUCTION:<BR>I Conclusion, inference: q. v.:<BR>निगमनम्।<BR>II Subtraction:<BR>(1) वियोजनम्;<BR>(2)<BR>व्यवकलनम्,<BR>To make d. s:<BR>वियोजयति, Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deductive
DEDUCTIVE: नैगमिकः (की, कं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deed
DEED:<BR>I An act: q. v.:<BR>(1) कर्मन् (n.);<BR>(2)<BR>अवदानम् (=a noble d.), Sa.<BR>II A legal ins-<BR>-trument: पत्रम्,<BR>d. of sale:<BR>विक्रयपत्रम्, Raj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deem
DEEM: मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.): v. To think.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deep
DEEP (adj.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) गभीरः<BR>or<BR>गम्भीरः (रा,<BR> रं); अगाधः (धा, धं) (=very d., bottomless):<BR>Ph.:<BR>thigh-d.:<BR>उरुदघ्नः (घ्ना घ्नं), K.;<BR>in thumb-d.<BR>water:<BR>अङ्गुष्ठोदकमात्रेण, J.<BR>II, Of sounds:<BR>(1)<BR>गभीरः<BR>or<BR>गम्भीरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) मन्द्रः (f. न्द्रा);<BR>v. Grave.<BR>III Of colours:<BR>(1) घन, in comp.,<BR>d. red:<BR>घनारुण (f. णा);<BR>(2) नितान्त- in comp.:<BR>v. Exceedingly.<BR>IV In various senses:<BR>d.<BR>sense:<BR>गभीरार्थः, Ki.;<BR>in a very d. king:<BR>अतिगम्भीरे<BR> भूपे, C. ;<BR>very d. wounds:<BR>दूरावगाढा व्रणाः, Sr.;<BR>in<BR>a d. mind:<BR>अवगाढे हृदि, N. ;<BR>d. sleep:<BR>गाढनिद्रा or<BR>घोरनिद्रा, K. ;<BR>d. sigh:<BR>दीर्घनिश्वासः; very d. anger:<BR>गम्भीरतरः कोपः, Pri.;<BR>with d. passion:<BR>विगाढभावेन,<BR>B. p.;<BR>soldiers nine files d.:<BR>नवपंक्तयो योधाः (?);<BR>d.-rooted:<BR>स्थिरबद्धमूलः (ला, लं), B.; d. darkness:<BR>घोरान्धकारः, Vet.;<BR>d. distress:<BR>घोरदुःखम्: v.<BR>Cunning, artful: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deep
DEEP (subs.): expr. by the adj.,<BR>in the d. of<BR>night:<BR>गाढायां रजन्याम्, K. ; moving about in the d.<BR>अगाधसलिले चरन्, Ka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deepen
DEEPEN (v. i.): गभीरीभवति: v. Also to thicken,<BR>increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deepen
DEEPEN (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) गभीरीकरोति;<BR>(2)<BR>by the adj.: v. Deep, to make.<BR>II To<BR>increase: q. v.: वर्द्धयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deeply
DEEPLY:<BR>(1) गाढम्, (her)<BR>glances are d. impress-<BR>ed on my heart:<BR>गाढं निखात इव मे हृदये कटाक्षः, Ma.<BR>i.;<BR>(2) प्रगाढम् (=very d.);<BR>(3) अत्यन्तम् (=ex-<BR>-cessively: q. v.). Ph.:<BR>sighing d.:<BR>दीर्घं निश्वस्य,<BR>K. ; wounded d. in (her)<BR>heart:<BR>हृदि व्यायतपात-<BR>मक्षिणोत्, Ku. v. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deepness
DEEPNESS: v. Depth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deer
DEER:<BR>(1) मृगः;<BR>(2) हरिणः:<BR>(3) कुरङ्गः, -मः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deface
DEFACE:<BR>I To disfigure: q. v. विरुपीकरोति।<BR>II To spoil: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defacemfnt
DEFACEMFNT:<BR>I Disfigurement: विरूपीकरणम्।<BR>II Obliteration: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defalcation
DEFALCATION:<BR>I A deficit: q. v.<BR>II Embez-<BR>-zlement: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defamation
DEFAMATION: परिवादः: v. Calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defamatory
DEFAMATORY: परिवादगर्भः (र्भा, र्भं): v. Slan-<BR>-derous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defame
DEFAME:<BR>(1) परिवदति (वद्, c. l.), is d. ing in<BR>(my)<BR>presence my friend, the king of Anga:<BR>परि-<BR>वदति समक्षं मित्रमङ्गाधिराजम्, Ve.;<BR>(2) अपभाषते<BR>(भाष्, c. l.),<BR>who d. s great men:<BR>यो महतोऽप-<BR>भाषते, Ku.;<BR>(3) आक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. l.) (=to<BR>asperse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defamer
DEFAMER: परिवादिन्: (f. नी): v. Slanderer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

default
DEFAULT (v.):<BR>I To offend: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>be absent: अनुपस्थितः (ता, तम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

default
DEFAULT (subs.):<BR>I Negligence: शैथिल्यम्।<BR>II<BR>Fault: q. v.: देषः।<BR>III Absence:<BR>in d. of the<BR>plaintiff:<BR>अनुपस्थिते वादिनि;<BR>in d. of fine:<BR>अदत्तेदण्डे;<BR>in d. of fishes:<BR>मत्स्याभावे।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defaulter
DEFAULTER:<BR>I In law: अनुपर्थितः (ता, तं).<BR>II A delinquent: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defeat
DEFEAT (v. t):<BR>I To overthrow: पराजयते (जि,<BR>c. l.),<BR>the Yavanas were d. ed:<BR>पराजयिषत यवनाः,<BR>D. vi.: v. To conquer, bear.<BR>II To frus-<BR>-trate in battle: q. v.: हन्ति, नि-, व्या-, (हन्, c.<BR>2.),<BR>would d. my object:<BR>निहन्यान्मे मनोरथम्,<BR>D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defeat
DEFEAT (subs.):<BR>I Discomfiture:<BR>(1) पराजयः,<BR>who has admitted d. from me:<BR>यया मत्तः पराजयोऽ-<BR>भ्युपेतः, D. ii.;<BR>(2) पराभवः; d. of Paraśurāma:<BR>परशुरामस्य पराभवः, Vi.;<BR>to get a d.:<BR>पराभवं प्राप्नोति,<BR>Ki.;<BR>(3) भङ्गः (rout).<BR>II Frustration:<BR>q. v.: विघातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defecate
DEFECATE:<BR>I Trans: v. To clarify, refine.<BR>II Intrans: मलोत्सर्गं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defecate
DEFECATE (adj.); DEFECATION: v. Refined,<BR>Purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defect
DEFECT:<BR>I Want: q. v.<BR>II Fault, blemish:<BR>q. v.: दोषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defection
DEFECTION: Ph.: d. from one's own religion:<BR>स्वधर्मत्यागः;<BR>“d. to Popery”<BR>रोमकधर्मपरिग्रहः;<BR>“d. of a realm” *राष्ट्रविघटनम्।: v. Revolt,<BR>apostacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defective
DEFECTIVE: असम्पूर्णः (र्णा, र्णं): v. Imperfect,<BR>maimed, faulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defectiveness
DEFECTIVENESS:<BR>(1) असम्पूर्णता;<BR>(2) सदोषता,<BR>(faultiness);<BR>(3) वैकल्यम् (of limbs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defence
DEFENCE:<BR>I Protection: q. v.:<BR>(1) रक्षा;<BR>(2)<BR>गुप्तिः,<BR>for the d. of cities:<BR>नगरगुप्त्यर्थम्, Mah.;<BR>(3) better by circumlo: v. To defend.<BR>II<BR>Art of d.: prob. रक्षा।<BR>III That which<BR>defends: गुप्तिः,<BR>and the d. s are quite impass-<BR>able:<BR>अलङ्घयतमा च गुप्तिः, D.: v. Also defender.<BR>IV. In law: उत्तरम्,<BR>witnesses for the d.:<BR>उत्तर-<BR>वादिनः साक्षिणः, Y. V. Apology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defenceless
DEFENCELESS:<BR>(1) अगुप्तः (प्ता, प्तं);<BR>(2) अनायुधः<BR>(धा, धं) (=unarmed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defend
DEFEND:<BR>I To protect: q. v. रक्षति (रक्ष, c. l.),<BR>d. him from Bhima:<BR>रक्षैनं भीमात्। Ve. iii. N. B.<BR>Exact sense expr. by circumlo.,<BR>Karṇa cannot<BR>d. the Kaurava army from Bhīma and Arjuna:<BR>कैरवबलमालोडयन्तौ भीमार्जुनौ राधेयेन न शक्येते<BR> निवारयितुम्, Ve.<BR>II In law, to contest: उत्तरं<BR> ददाति, (दा, c. 3.).<BR>III To repel: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defendant
DEFENDANT:<BR>(1) प्रत्यर्थिन् (f. नी), Mr. ix.;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रतिवादिन् (f. नी), Si. xx. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defender
DEFENDER:<BR>(1) रक्षकः;<BR>(2) गोप्त्ट (m.),<BR>d. of the<BR>faith:<BR>धर्मस्य गोप्ता, Vi. v.: v. Protector,<BR>guardian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defensive
DEFENSIVE: Ph.:<BR>on the d.:<BR>आत्मरक्षार्थम्;<BR>d.<BR>and offensive weapons:<BR>आक्रमणनिवारण-, परप्रहरणा-<BR>युधाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defer
DEFER (v. t.):<BR>I To put off, delay: q. v.:<BR>व्याक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 9.).<BR>II To refer: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defer
DEFER (v. i.):<BR>I To yield, submit: q. v.:<BR>अनुपालयति (पाल्, c. 10.).<BR>II To delay, put<BR>off: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deference
DEFERENCE:<BR>(1) बहुमानः (=regard),<BR>out of d.<BR>to a good thing:<BR>सद्वस्तुबहुमानात्, V.;<BR>(2) अनुरोधः<BR>(=complaisance),<BR>is this d. to the sayings of<BR>superiors:<BR>किमयं गुरुजनवचनानुरोधः, K. To treat<BR>with d.:<BR>(1) बहु मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.), Sa.;<BR>(2)<BR>अनुरुध्यते, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deferential
DEFERENTIAL: v. Respectful, obliging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deferentially
DEFERENTIALLY:<BR>(1) सबहुमानम्;<BR>(2) सप्रश्रयम्<BR>(=courteously).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defiance
DEFIANCE:<BR>(1) अवज्ञा (=contempt: q. v.);<BR>(2) आह्वानम् (=challenge: q. v.). Ph.:<BR>he, in<BR>d. of us:<BR>अस्मानयमतिक्रम्य, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deflant
DEFLANT: उद्धतः (ता, तं): v. Haughty, in-<BR>-solent, fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defiantly
DEFIANTLY: अद्धतम्, (you)<BR>act d. even towards<BR>Kṛṣṇa:<BR>हरावप्युद्धतं चेष्टसे, Ve.: v. Haughtily,<BR>insolently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deficiency
DEFICIENCY:<BR>(1) अभावः (=want: q. v.);<BR>(2) न्यूनता (=state of being less);<BR>(3) वैकल्यम्<BR>(=incompleteness),<BR>d. of strength:<BR>शाक्ति-<BR>वैकल्यम्, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deficient
DEFICIENT:<BR>(1) हीनः (ना, नं) (=wanting:<BR>q. v.),<BR>d. in limbs:<BR>हीनाङ्गः (f. ङ्गी), Pa.;<BR>(2)<BR>न्यूनः<BR>or<BR>ऊनः (ना, नं) (=less)<BR>or<BR>अल्पः (ल्पा, ल्पं)<BR>(=little):<BR>not of d. fortune:<BR>अननर्द्धि (mfn.),<BR>R.;<BR>d. in wisdom:<BR>अल्पप्रज्ञः (ज्ञा, ज्ञं), V. p.;<BR>(3)<BR>विकलः (ला, लं) (=incomplete),<BR>even when<BR>the clouds are d.:<BR>विकलेऽपि हि पर्जन्ये, H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deficit
DEFICIT:<BR>there will be a d. in revenue:<BR>राजस्वं<BR> न्यूनं भवति: v. Wanting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defier
DEFIER: अवमन्तृ (m.) (=despiser); अतिक्रमकारिन्<BR>(m.) (=transgressor).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defile
DEFILE: (v. t.): दूषयति (c. of दूष्), to d. a virgin:<BR>कन्यां दूषयति, M. viii. 364: v. To corrupt,<BR>pollute^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defile
DEFILE (v. i.); दण्डव्यूहेन यात्रां करोति<BR>or<BR>याति (या,<BR>c. 2.), M. vii. 187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defile
DEFILE (subs.): सम्बाध; (?): v. Pass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defilement
DEFILEMENT: दूषणभ्: v. Pollution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defiler
DEFILER: दूषकः,<BR>d. of virgin's apartments:<BR>कन्या-<BR>पुरदूषकः, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

definable
DEFINABLE:<BR>(1) निर्वचनीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) व्याख्येयः<BR>(या, यं) (what can be explained);<BR>(3)<BR>निरूपणीयः (या, यं) (what can be determined).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

define
DEFINE:<BR>I To end: q. v.<BR>II To determine:<BR>q. v.: निरूपयति (रूप्, c. 10.).<BR>III To explain:<BR>q. v.<BR>(1) व्याख्याति (ख्या, c. 2.), perception is d. d:<BR>व्याखयातं प्रत्यक्षम्, N. d.;<BR>(2) स्वरूपं<BR>or<BR>लक्षणं कथयति<BR>(=to say: q. v.)<BR>or<BR>निरूपयति (=to determine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

definite
DEFINITE:<BR>(1) निश्चितः (ता, तं): v. Certain;<BR>(2) स्थिथरः (रा, रं): v. Fixed. Ph.:<BR>the d.<BR>article:<BR>*विशेष्यनिर्द्धारकमव्ययम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

definitely
DEFINITELY:<BR>(1) निशिचितभ्: v. Certainly: (a)<BR>स्पष्टम्: v. Clearly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

definiteness
DEFINITENESS, DEFINITUDE:<BR>(1) निश्चयः;<BR>(2)<BR>निर्णयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

definition
DEFINITION:<BR>(1) लक्षणवचनम्, N. d.;<BR>(2) निर्वचनम्<BR>(-etymological d.), Sr.;<BR>(3) व्याख्या (=ex-<BR>-planation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

definitive
DEFINITIVE:<BR>I Definite: q. v.<BR>II Deter-<BR>-mining: निश्चायकः (का, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

definitivly
DEFINITIVLY: v. Definitely, positively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deflect
DEFLECT:<BR>I Trans: विचालयति (c. of चल्)<BR>(?).<BR>II Intrans: v. To deviate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deflection
DEFLECTION: v. Deviation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defloration
DEFLORATION: दूषणम्,<BR>d. of a girl:<BR>कन्यादूषणम्,<BR>D.: v. Seduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deflower
DEFLOWER (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: पुष्पहीनं (नां) करोति।<BR>II To deprive: हरति (हृ, c. l.).<BR>III To<BR>defile: q. v.: नाशयति (c. of नश्),<BR>will seduce<BR>and d. this girl:<BR>एनां बालां विलोभ्य नाशयिष्यति,<BR>D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deflowerer
DEFLOWERER: दूषकः, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deform
DEFORM (v. t.): विरूपयति (रूप्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>disfigure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deformed
DEFORMED (part. adj.):<BR>(1) विरूपः (पा, पं),<BR>d.<BR>and eightfold crooked:<BR>विरूपं वक्रमष्टधा, V. p.;<BR>(2) अनमिरूपः (पा, पं);<BR>(3) विकृतः (ता, तं),<BR>of<BR>d. figure:<BR>विकृताकृति (mfn.), Vi.;<BR>(4) विकलः<BR>(ला, लं) (wanting a limb or limbs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deformity
DEFORMITY: वैरूप्यम्, on account of my d.:<BR>वैरूप्यान्मम, D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defraud
DEFRAUD: वञ्चयते (वञ्च्, c. 10.): v. To cheat,<BR>deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defrauder
DEFRAUDER:<BR>(1) वञ्चकः, प्र-;<BR>(2) प्रतारकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defray
DEFRAY: ददाति (दा, c. 3.) (=to pay: q. v.):<BR>v. Also to supply, assist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defrayment
DEFRAYMENT: दानम् (=payment: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deft
DEFT: वामः (मा, मं): v. Neat, dexterous.<BR>D. ly:<BR>वामम्, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defunct
DEFUNCT: संस्थितः (ता, तं): v. Dead, deceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

defy
DEFY:<BR>(1) आह्वयते: v. To challenge;<BR>(2) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">Page183</a>]<BR>तृणीकरोति (=to care a straw for),<BR>and d. ing<BR>those who have assembled:<BR>तृणीकृत्य च सङ्गतान्,<BR>Mah.;<BR>(3) अतिक्रामति (क्रम् c. l.) (=to trans-<BR>-gress),<BR>d. ing the duties of her caste:<BR>अतिक्रम्य<BR> स्वकुलधर्मम्, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

degeneracy
DEGENERACY, DEGENERATENESS:<BR>(1) क्षयः<BR>(=decay: q. v.);<BR>(2) हानिः (=loss: q. v.);<BR>(3) भ्रंशः (fall: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

degenerate
DEGENERATE (adj.): Ph.:<BR>d. in time:<BR>काल-<BR>विभ्रष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं), Kal.;<BR>d. Kshatriyas:<BR>क्षत्रिया-<BR>पसदाः, Ve.;<BR>d. Brahmin:<BR>ब्रह्मबन्धुः, Ana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

degenerate
DEGENERATE (v.): क्षीयते (pass. of क्षि): v. To<BR>decay:<BR>(2) हियते (pass. of हा): v. Inferior,<BR>be-;<BR>(3) च्यवते (च्यु, c. l.): v. To fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deglutition
DEGLUTITION:<BR>(1) गिलनम्;<BR>(2) ग्रसनम्;<BR>(3) गीर्णिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

degradation
DEGRADATION:<BR>I Lit.: *निम्नपदारोपणम्, or<BR>-लम्भनम्।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) क्षयः (=decay);<BR>(2)<BR>अवमानना (=disgrace).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

degrade
DEGRADE:<BR>I Lit.: *निम्नपदे क्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.)<BR>or<BR>निम्नपदं लम्भयति (c. of लम्भ्).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>लघूकरोति<BR>or<BR>लघयति (nomi.),<BR>shame on me d. d. by<BR>life:<BR>मां धिग जीवितलघूकृताम्, B. To become d. d.:<BR>(1) लघूमवति;<BR>(2) हीयते (pass. of हा), H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

degree
DEGREE:<BR>I Academical: उपाधिः।<BR>II Posi-<BR>-tion, rank: q. v.: पदम्।<BR>III Grade: q. v.<BR>Ph.:<BR>by d. s:<BR>क्रमशः: v. Gradually; ‘in the<BR>highest d.’, ‘to ad.’: निरतिशयम्: v. Exceedingly;<BR>in some d.: v. Somewhat; in the same d.<BR>as: v. Equally.<BR>IV Of latitude or longi-<BR>-tude: *कला। V. In genealogy: पुरुषः,<BR>a<BR>relation in the third d.:<BR>*त्रिपुरुषान्तरो बन्धुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deification
DEIFICATION:<BR>(1) देवीकरणम् (rare);<BR>(2) देवत्वा-<BR>रोपणम् (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deified
DEIFIED, TO BE:<BR>(1) देवत्वम् एति;<BR>(2) देवीभवति;<BR>(3) त्रिदशिभवति, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deify
DEIFY:<BR>(1) देवत्वम् आरोपयति (c. of रुह्) (with<BR>loc.);<BR>(2) देवीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deign
DEIGN: अर्हति (अर्ह, c. l.),<BR>d. to excuse this:<BR>इदं<BR> विषोढुमर्हति, Sa. iii.: v. To condescend, please.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deism
DEISM: ईश्वरवादः (?); ईश्वरवादित्वम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deist
DEIST: ईश्वरवादिन् (f. नी) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deistical
DEISTICAL: Ph.:<BR>d. writer:<BR>*ईश्वरवादी लेखकः;<BR>d. work:<BR>ईश्वरवादविषयको ग्रन्थः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deity
DEITY:<BR>I Divinity: q. v.<BR>II A god or<BR>goddess: q. v.: देवता।<BR>III The Supreme<BR>Being:<BR>(1) ईश्वरः;<BR>(2) देवदेवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deject
DEJECT (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: to cast down: अवक्षिपति<BR>(क्षिप्, c. 6.).<BR>II Fig.: to dispirit: विषण्णी-<BR>करोति<BR>or<BR>विषादं जनयति (c. of जन्): v. Dejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dejected
DEJECTED: विषण्णः (ण्णा, ण्णं).<BR>To be d.:<BR>विषीदति<BR>(सद्, c. l.),<BR>do not be d.:<BR>मा विषीद, Ch.;<BR>d. ly<BR>said this:<BR>विषीदन्निदमब्रवीत्, G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dejectedly
DEJECTEDLY:<BR>(1) सविषादम्;<BR>(2) विषण्णः (ण्णा, ण्णं);<BR>(3) विषीदत् (f. न्ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dejectedness
DEJECTEDNESS, DEJECTION:<BR>(1) विषाद:<BR>or<BR>विषण्णता,<BR>the demolisher seeing (his)<BR>forces in d.:<BR>विषाद-<BR>वक्तव्यबलः प्रमाथी, Ki.;<BR>(2) वैमनस्यम्, Sa.;<BR>(3)<BR>परितापः (=anguish), N. xiii. 54;<BR>(4) निर्वेदः<BR>(=despondency).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delate
DELATE:<BR>I To carry: q. v.<BR>II To spread:<BR>q. v.<BR>III To cause: q. v. IV. To manage:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delay
DELAY (v. t.):<BR>I To retard: विलम्बयति (c. of<BR>लम्ब्), with wishes, whose fruits were d. ed:<BR>विलम्बितफलैर्मनोरथैः, R.<BR>II To put off, pro-<BR>-long: q. v. विलम्बेन करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delay
DELAY (v. i.):<BR>(1) विलम्बते (लम्ब्, c. l);<BR>(2)<BR>चिरयति<BR>or<BR>चिरायते (nomi.),<BR>why my men are d.<BR>ing:<BR>किमिति चिरायते मे जनः, P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delay
DELAY (subs.):<BR>(1) विलम्बः,<BR>whether there will be<BR>d. in their way:<BR>अन्तरा वा गच्छतां विलम्ब उत्पत्स्यते<BR> न वा, K. ;<BR>without d.:<BR>अविलम्बम्<BR>or<BR>अविलम्बेन<BR>or<BR>अविलम्बितम्, Sa.;<BR>(2) व्याक्षेपः (putting<BR>off), R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delayer
DELAYER:<BR>(1) विलम्बकारिन् (f. णी) (of another);<BR>(2) विलम्बिन् (f. नी) (lingerer: q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delectable
DELECTABLE: रम्यः (म्या, म्यं): v. Delightful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delectation
DELECTATION: v. Delight, gratification,<BR>amusement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delegate
DELEGATE (v. t.):<BR>I To depute: q. v.<BR>II<BR>To assign, commit: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delegate
DELEGATE (subs.): प्रतिनिधिः: v. Representa-<BR>-tive commissioner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delegation
DELEGATION:<BR>I Deputing: नियोगः<BR>II Assign-<BR>-ing: अर्पणम्।<BR>III A body of delegates:<BR>प्रतिनिधिवर्गः।<BR>IV In law: प्रतिभूः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delete
DELETE (v.):<BR>(1) अप-मार्ष्टि<BR>or<BR>मार्जयति, निर्-, व्या-,<BR>(मृज्, c. 2. and 10.);<BR>(2) लुम्पति, वि-, अव-,<BR>(लुप्, c. 6.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deleterious
DELETERIOUS:<BR>(1) प्राणहरः (री, रं);<BR>(2) प्राण-<BR>नाशिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) जीवितापहः (हा, हं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delf
DELF:<BR>I Mine: q. v.<BR>II Earthenware:<BR>मृद्भाण्डम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deliberate
DELIBERATE (v.): वि-मृशति, परा-, (म्टश्, c. 6.):<BR>v. Consider;<BR>(2) मन्त्रयति, सं-, (मन्त्र्, c. 10.):<BR>v. To consult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deliberate
DELIBERATE (adj.):<BR>I Circumspect: q. v.:<BR>धीरः (रा, रं). D-ly resolved:<BR>(1) निश्चितः (ता,<BR> तं): v. Certain;<BR>(2) स्थिरः (रा, रं): v. Con-<BR>-stant. Ph.:<BR>of d. intention:<BR>ध्रु वेच्छः (च्छा, च्छं),<BR>Ku.;<BR>to commit d. crimes:<BR>कामतः पापानि करोति,<BR>Pa.<BR>III Slow: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deliberately
DELIBERATELY:<BR>I Circumspectly:<BR>(1) समीक्ष्य;<BR>(2) विमृश्य।<BR>II Intentionally: कामत: Ph.:<BR>d. cruel:<BR>प्रतिपत्तिनिष्ठुरः, R.<BR>III. Slowly: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deliberateness
DELIBERATENESS:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) धीरता;<BR>(2)<BR>समीक्ष्यकारिता।<BR>II Of acts: expr. by circumlo:<BR>v. Deliberate (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deliberation
DELIBERATION:<BR>(1) मन्त्रणा<BR>or<BR>मन्त्रः, णम्-,<BR>but wisdom<BR>and not valour is required in d.:<BR>प्रज्ञा तु मन्त्रेऽधिकृता<BR> न शौर्यम्, B. ;<BR>(2) विमर्शः: v. Consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deliberative
DELIBERATIVE: Ph.:<BR>“the d. body”:<BR>मन्त्रिमण्डलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delicacy
DELICACY:<BR>I Of flavour, odour, etc.:<BR>(1)<BR>माधुर्यम्।<BR>II Fineness: सौकुमार्यम्,<BR>from great<BR>d.:<BR>अतिसौकुमार्यत्, M. n.<BR>III Elegance:<BR>लालित्यम्।<BR>IV Of manners: अत्यादरः। V. Of<BR>character: मार्दवम्।<BR>VI Luxury; self-in-<BR>-dulgence: q. v.<BR>VII A dainty: विशिष्ट-<BR>भोजनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delicate
DELICATE:<BR>I Delightful: q. v.: ललितः (ता,<BR> तं).<BR>II Pleasing to the senses: मधुरः (रा,<BR> रं),<BR>d. meat:<BR>मधुरं मांसम्, Bha.<BR>III Fine, soft,<BR>feeble:<BR>(1) सुकुमारः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) कोमलः (ला,<BR> लं),<BR>with d. limbs:<BR>कोमलैरङ्गैः, S.<BR>IV Refined,<BR>polite: q. v.<BR>V Luxurious: q. v.<BR>VI<BR>Of subjects, difficult: विषमः (मा, मं).<BR>VII Nice, critical: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delicately
DELICATELY: v. Softly, nicely, delightfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delicateness
DELICATENESS: v. Delicacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delicious
DELICIOUS:<BR>(1) स्वादु (mfn.) (to the taste),<BR>fruits d. as the nectar:<BR>अमृतरसस्वादुनि फलानि, K. ;<BR>(2) ललितः (ता, तं) (tender, fine),<BR>very d.<BR>flesh:<BR>सुललितं मांसम्, H. ;<BR>(3) मधुरः (रा, रं): v.<BR>Sweet, pleasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deliciously
DELICIOUSLY: v. Delightfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deliciousness
DELICIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) सुस्वादुता;<BR>(2) लालित्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delight
DELIGHT (subs.):<BR>I Pleasure: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>आह्वादः;<BR>(2) प्रमोदः।<BR>II That which gives<BR>d.:<BR>(1) आह्वादनम्;<BR>(2) आनन्दनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delight
DELIGHT (v. i.), DELIGHTED, TO BE:<BR>(1) हृष्यति,<BR> सं-, प्र-, (हृष्, c. 4.),<BR>with a d. ed face:<BR>प्रहृष्ट-<BR>वदनः (ना, नं), K. ;<BR>(2) तुष्यति, परि-, सं-, (तुष्,<BR>c. 4.),<BR>was d. ed to see the beauty of the rice<BR>crop:<BR>कलमस्य रामणीयकं पश्यन् तुतोष, Ki.;<BR>(3)<BR>मोदते, प्र-, (मुद्, c. 4.), Kāmandakī (always)<BR>d. s<BR>in Mālatī:<BR>भालति मालतीति मोदते कामन्दकी, Ma.;<BR>(4) ह्लादते, सं-, प्र-, आ-, (ह्लाद्, c. l. (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delight
DELIGHT (v. t.):<BR>(1) आ-ह्लादयति, प्र-, सं-, (c. of<BR>ह्लाद्),<BR>d. s the tongue:<BR>रसनामाह्लादयति, K.;<BR>(2)<BR>रमयति, अभि-, (c. of रम्),<BR>whom does not a<BR>woman d.:<BR>कं न नारी रमयति, Ka.: v. To<BR>please.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delghtful
DELGHTFUL:<BR>(1) रम्यः (म्या, म्यं)<BR>or<BR>रमणीयः<BR>(या, यं),<BR>whichever country may be d.:<BR>रम्यो<BR> यो देशः, Mah.;<BR>(2) आ-ह्लादनः, प्र-, (नी, नं),<BR>d. to the eye:<BR>आह्लादनं दृष्टेः, K. ;<BR>(3) संह्लादिन<BR>(f. नी),<BR>even the name of women is d.:<BR>नामापि<BR> स्त्रीति संह्लादि, K.;<BR>(4) प्रमोदिन् (f. नी): v.<BR>Charming, pleasing, sweet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delightfully
DELIGHTFULLY: expr. by circumlo., d. cool:<BR>सुशीतलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delightfulness
DELIGHTFULNESS:<BR>(1) रम्यता;<BR>(2) रमणीयता:<BR>v. Pleasantness, sweetness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delineate
DELINEATE:<BR>I To sketch, draw: q. v.:<BR>लिखति (लिख्, c. 6.).<BR>II To describe: q. v.:<BR>वर्णयति (वर्ण् c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delineation
DELINEATION:<BR>I A drawing: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Description: q. v. वर्णना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delinquency
DELINQUENCY:<BR>(1) दोषः: v. Fault, offence;<BR>(2) व्यतिक्रमः: v. Transgression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delinquent
DELINQUENT: अपराधिन् (f. नी): v. Offender,<BR>guilty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delirious
DELIRIOUS: भ्रान्तः (न्ता, न्तं)<BR>or<BR>भ्रान्ताचित्तः (त्ता,<BR> त्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delirium
DELIRIUM: भ्रमः<BR>or<BR>मनसः सम्भ्रमः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deliver
DELIVER:<BR>I To release, rescue: q. v.:<BR>मोचयति (c. of मुच्)<BR>or<BR>मोक्षयति (मोक्ष्, c. 10.),<BR>to d. my friend:<BR>सुहृदः परिमोक्षणाय, Mr. iv.<BR>II<BR>To make over: अर्पयति, सम्-, (c. of ऋ),<BR>d. ed<BR>two letters:<BR>लेखद्वितयमर्पयाम्बभूव, K. ;<BR>d. ing<BR>Patralekhā to Meghanāda:<BR>पत्रलेखां मेघनादाय<BR> समर्प्य, K. : v. To give. Ph.: d. (this) back<BR>to him: [इदं] तस्मै प्रतिनिर्यातय, Mr. iv.: v. To<BR>give back.<BR>III To utter, pronounce:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) उदीरयति (ईर्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) कथयति<BR>(कथ्, c. 10.) (to tell),<BR>d. Kādambari's<BR>message:<BR>कथय कादम्बर्याः सन्देशम्, K.;<BR>(3)<BR>आवेदयति, नि-, (c. of विद्) (=to d. respect-<BR>-fully),<BR>d. ed the return message:<BR>प्रतिसन्देश-<BR>मावेदयत्, D. i.<BR>IV To discharge (of missi-<BR>-les): q. v.: मुञ्चति (मुच् c. 6.).<BR>V In child-<BR>-birth: गर्भं मोचयति, P.<BR>A woman who has<BR>recently d. ed:<BR>नवप्रसूता: v. To bring forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deliverance
DELIVERANCE:<BR>(1) मोचनम्;<BR>(2) उद्धारः;<BR>(3)<BR>मोक्षः, -णम्;<BR>(4) परिमोक्षणम्;<BR>(5) निस्तारः;<BR>(6)<BR>मुक्तिः: v. Release, rescue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deliverer
DELIVERER:<BR>I Rescuer:<BR>(1) मोचकः;<BR>(2)<BR>मोक्षकः, परि-;<BR>(3) निस्तारकः;<BR>(4) उद्धर्तृ (m.).<BR>II Announcer:<BR>(1) विज्ञापकः;<BR>(2) आवेदकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delivery
DELIVERY:<BR>I Deliverance: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Making over:<BR>(1) अर्पणम्;<BR>(2) समर्पणम्;<BR>(3) निर्यातनम् (of trusts, etc.).<BR>III Child-<BR>-birth: q. v.: गर्भमोचनम्।<BR>House of d.:<BR>सूतिका-<BR>गृहभ्।<BR>IV Utterance: q. v.:<BR>(1) व्याहारः;<BR>(2) विज्ञप्तिः (of message).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dell
DELL: दरी: v. Dale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delta
DELTA: त्रिभुजाकारभूभिः; *त्रिमुखम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delude
DELUDE:<BR>I To deceive: q. v.: सम्मोहयति<BR>(c. of मुह्).<BR>II To frustrate: q. v. D. ing:<BR>v. Delusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deluder
DELUDER: v. Deceiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deluge
DELUGE (subs.):<BR>I<BR>Universal d.:<BR>प्रलयाप्लावः,<BR>Si.; आभूतसंप्लवः, Mat.<BR>II Inundation,<BR>flood: q. v.:<BR>(1) आप्लावः;<BR>(2) संप्लवः।<BR>III<BR>Fig.: perh. संप्लवः, “fiery d.”: अग्निसंप्लवः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deluge
DELUGE (v. t.): प्लावयति, आ-, वि-, अभि-, (c. of<BR>प्ल) (lit. and fig.),<BR>d. ed Dwārakā:<BR>द्वारकां<BR> प्लावयामास, V. p.: v. To drown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delusion
DELUSION:<BR>I Illusion: q. v.: मोहः।<BR>II<BR>Deception: q. v.: वञ्चना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delusive
DELUSIVE: मिथ्या (=false: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

delve
DELVE (v.):<BR>I To dig: q. v.<BR>II To fathom:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demagogue
DEMAGOGUE: *प्राकृतनायकः; इतरलोकशासकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demand
DEMAND (v.):<BR>I To ask: q. v.:<BR>(1) याचते<BR>(याच्, c. l.);<BR>(2) by circumlo.,<BR>d. ed the<BR>balance from the merchant:<BR>श्रेष्ठिनमुवाच दीयतां मे<BR> तुलेति, P. i. 21.<BR>II To call for: Ph.:<BR>it d. s<BR>careful enquiry:<BR>निपुणमिदमनुसन्धेयम्;<BR>the case d. s<BR>your special attention:<BR>अस्मिन्विषये त्वया विशेषेणा-<BR>वधानं देयम्<BR>or<BR>विशेषेणावहितेन भवितव्यम्।<BR>III To<BR>summon: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demand
DEMAND (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अनुयोगः;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रार्थना (=asking). Ph.:<BR>a debt should be paid<BR>on d.:<BR>ऋणं याचमानाय दातव्यम्, Vri.<BR>II Query:<BR>अनुयोगः।<BR>III Want: *ईप्सा,<BR>horses are in<BR>great d. now:<BR>*इदानीमश्वेप्सा प्रबला।<BR>IV That<BR>which may be d. ed: प्राप्यम् (?), arrear d.:<BR>अवशिष्टप्राप्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demarkation
DEMARKATION: Ph.:<BR>a line of d.:<BR>प्रतिभागसीमा:<BR>v. Boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demean
DEMEAN (v.):<BR>I To behave: q. v.<BR>II<BR>To debase: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demeanour
DEMEANOUR: चेष्टा: v. Behaviour, mien.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demented
DEMENTED, DEMENTATE (adj.): उन्मत्तः (त्ता,<BR> त्तं): v. Mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demerit
DEMERIT: दोषः: v. Fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demesne
DEMESNE: भूमीश्वराणां स्वहस्तस्था भूमिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demigod
DEMIGOD:<BR>(1) उपदेवः;<BR>(2) देवयोनिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demigoddess
DEMIGODDESS:<BR>(1) उपदेवी;<BR>(2) देवयोनि: (f.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demise
DEMISE (v.):<BR>I To bequeath: q. v.: समर्पयति<BR>(c. of ऋ).<BR>II To lease: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demise
DEMISE (subs.):<BR>I Death: उपरमः,<BR>on the d.<BR>of the owner:<BR>स्वाम्योपरमे, Da.<BR>On the d. of the<BR>king:<BR>ऊर्द्धं<BR>or<BR>दिवं गते (=gone to heaven) राज्ञि,<BR>Kal.<BR>II Transference: q. v.: समर्पणम् (?);<BR>हस्तान्तरीकरणम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

democracy
DEMOCRACY: प्रजातन्त्रम् (?); प्रजाशासनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

democrat
DEMOCRAT: *प्रजातन्त्रिन् (f. णी). प्रजातन्त्रवादिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

democratical
DEMOCRATICAL: *प्रजातन्त्रीयः (या, यं). Ph.:<BR>d. people:<BR>*प्रजातन्त्रवादिनः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

democratically
DEMOCRATICALLY: *प्रजातन्त्रानुसारेण, and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demolish
DEMOLISH: ध्वंसयति वि-, प्र-, (c. of ध्वंस्): v.<BR>To destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demolisher
DEMOLISHER: विध्वंसकः: v. Destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demolition
DEMOLITION: ध्वंसः, वि-, प्र-: v. Destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demon
DEMON:<BR>(1) दैत्यः<BR>or<BR>दानवः (=titan);<BR>(2)<BR>राक्षसः (=goblin?);<BR>(3) पिशाचः (=fiend);<BR>(4) भूतः (=ghost).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demoniac
DEMONIAC (subs.):<BR>(1) आविष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं), K. ;<BR>(2) भूताधिष्ठितः (ता, तं), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demoniac
DEMONIAC,-AL (adj.):<BR>(1) पैशाचः (ची, चं);<BR>(2) राक्षसः (सी, सं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demonstrable
DEMONSTRABLE:<BR>(1) साध्यः (ध्या, ध्यं);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रतिपादनीयः (या, यं);<BR>(3) उपपाद्यः (द्या, द्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demonstrably
DEMONSTRABLY: expr. by adj., this is d. false:<BR>*अस्यालीकता साध्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demonstrate
DEMONSTRATE:<BR>I To exhibit: प्रदर्शयति (c. of<BR>दृश्), S.<BR>II. To establish, prove q. v.:<BR>साधयति (c. of साध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demonstration
DEMONSTRATION:<BR>I Proof: q. v.: साधनम्।<BR>II Exhibiton: प्रदर्शनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demonstrative
DEMONSTRATIVE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) साधकः (f. धिका);<BR>(2) प्रदर्शकः (f. र्शिका).<BR>II Frank: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demonstratively
DEMONSTRATIVELY: v. Clearly, certainly,<BR>openly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demoralization
DEMORALIZATION:<BR>I Corruption: धर्मभ्रष्टता।<BR>II Of discipline: शासनातिक्रमः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demoralize
DEMORALIZE: विकरोति (कृ, c. 8.): v. To<BR>corrupt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demulcent
DEMULCENT: दाहघ्नः (घ्नी, घ्नं)<BR>or<BR>दाहनुद् (mfn.),<BR>Bha.: v. Soothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demur
DEMUR (v.):<BR>I To delay, pause: q. v.<BR>II<BR>In law: *प्रतीपवादं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demur
DEMUR (subs.):<BR>(1) विलम्बः: v. Delay;<BR>(2)<BR>विरामः: v. Pause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demure
DEMURE: शान्तः (न्ता, न्तं): v. Grave, modest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demurely
DEMURELY:<BR>(1) शान्तम्;<BR>(2) प्रशान्तम्: v.<BR>Gravely, modestly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demureness
DEMURENESS: प्रशान्तिः, K. : v. Gravity,<BR>modesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demurrage
DEMURRAGE:<BR>I Detention of a vessel beyond<BR>the prescribed time (?):<BR>II Payment for it:<BR>*विलम्बदेयम्ः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

demurrer
DEMURRER: in law; *प्रतीपवादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

den
DEN:<BR>I Lit:<BR>(1) विवरम्;<BR>(2) बिलम्, bear's d.:<BR>ऋक्षबिलम्, V. p.: v. Cave.<BR>II Fig.: haunt:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denary
DENARY (adj.):<BR>(1) दशकः (का, कं);<BR>(2) दशिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deniable
DENIABLE:<BR>(1) प्रत्याख्येयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) अस्वीकार्यः<BR>(र्या, र्यं): v. To deny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denial
DENIAL:<BR>(1) अस्वीकारः;<BR>(2) अपह्नवः;<BR>(3) अपह्नु तिः;<BR>(4) अपलापः;<BR>(5) प्रत्याख्यानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denier
DENIER:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अस्वीकर्तृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2)<BR>अपह्रोतृ (f. त्री);<BR>(3) अपलापिन् (f. नी).<BR>II A<BR>small coin: वराटिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denizen
DENIZEN:<BR>I A naturalized citizen: *कृतपौरः।<BR>II A dweller: q. v.: निवासिन् (m.) Ph.:<BR>d. of heaven:<BR>दिवौकस् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denominate
DENOMINATE: अभिदधाति (धा, c. 3.): v. To<BR>name, designate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denomination
DENOMINATION:<BR>I Name, epithet: q. v.:<BR>अभिधेयम्।<BR>II Sect: q. v.: गणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denominator
DENOMINATOR:<BR>I Lit.: नामकृत्।<BR>II In arith.:<BR>छेदः,<BR>having the same d.:<BR>समच्छेदः (दा, दं),<BR>Li.;<BR>reduction to a common d.:<BR>सवर्णम्, Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denotation
DENOTATION; निर्देशः (=pointing out); अर्थः<BR>(=meaning).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denote
DENOTE:<BR>I To mark, point: q. v.: निर्दिशाति<BR>(दिश्, c. 6.).<BR>II To mean, signify: q. v.:<BR>expr. by अर्थ,<BR>here the word<BR>अर्थ d. s. succession:<BR>अत्रार्थशब्द आनन्तर्यार्थः, S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denouement
DENOUEMENT:<BR>I Of a drama:<BR>(1) निष्ठा;<BR>(2) निर्वहणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denounce
DENOUNCE:<BR>I To announce: q. v.:<BR>II To<BR>stigmatize, accuse:<BR>(1) अभिशंसति (शंस्,<BR>c. l.);<BR>(2) अधिक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denouncement
DENOUNCEMENT:<BR>I Announcement: q. v.<BR>II Accusation: अभिशंसनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denouncer
DENOUNCER:<BR>(1) अभिशंसकः;<BR>(2) अधिक्षेपकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dense
DENSE:<BR>(1) घनः (ना, नं),<BR>d. dews:<BR>घननीहारः, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">Page187</a>]<BR>Ki.;<BR>(2) निविडः (डा, डं),<BR>d. union:<BR>निविडसंयोगः,<BR>J.;<BR>(3) सान्द्रः (न्द्रा, न्द्रं),<BR>to make d.:<BR>सान्द्री-<BR>करोति, R.;<BR>(4) अविरलः (ला, लं) (=close);<BR>(5) निरन्तरः (रा, रं)<BR>or<BR>निरन्तरालः (ला, लं);<BR>(=without any intervening space).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

densely
DENSELY:<BR>(1) धनम्;<BR>(2) निविडम्;<BR>(3) सान्द्रम्;<BR>(4) अविरलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

density
DENSITY:<BR>(1) घनत्वम्;<BR>(2) निविडता;<BR>(3) सान्द्रता,<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dental
DENTAL:<BR>I Adj.: दन्त्यः (न्त्या, न्त्यं).<BR>II<BR>Subs.: दन्त्यम्, दन्त्यवर्णः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dentate
DENTATE:<BR>(1) दन्तिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) दन्तुरः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denticulated
DENTICULATED: सूक्ष्मदन्तिन् (f. नी) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dentifrice
DENTIFRICE:<BR>(1) दन्तशोधनचूर्णम् (=tooth<BR>powder);<BR>(2) दन्तपावनम्, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dentist
DENTIST: *दन्तवैद्यः, दान्तिकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dentistry
DENTISTRY: *दन्तचिकित्सा; दान्तिकविद्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dentition
DENTITION:<BR>(1) दन्तोद्भेदः;<BR>(2) दन्तनिर्गमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denudate
DENUDATE, DENUDE: नग्नीकरोति: v. To strip,<BR>uncover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denudation
DENUDATION:<BR>(1) नग्नीकरणम्;<BR>(2) शून्यीकरणम्<BR>(=emptying).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

denunciation
DENUNCIATION:<BR>(1) अभिशंसनम्;<BR>(2) अधिक्षेपः,<BR> अभिशापः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deny
DENY (v. t.):<BR>I To gainsay, disown:<BR>(1)<BR>न स्वीकरोति, etc. (=not acknowledge: q. v.),<BR>if any one were to d. the authority of inference:<BR>यदि कश्चित् प्रामाण्यमनुमानस्य नाङ्गीकुर्यात्, D. s.;<BR>(2)<BR>अप- ह्नुते, नि-, (ह्नु, c. 2.), and who (first) speci-<BR>fies and (then)<BR>d. s:<BR>निर्दिश्यापह्नु ते च यः, M.;<BR>(3) प्रत्याख्व्याति (ख्या, c. 2.),<BR>it cannot be d. ed<BR>that by devotion one can get divinity:<BR>योग<BR> ऐश्वर्यप्राप्तिफलको न शक्यते प्रत्याख्यातुम्, S.<BR>II To<BR>refuse, withhold: q. v. Ph.: to d. one's self:<BR>आत्मानं संयव्च्छति (यम्, c. l.): v. Self-denial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deodand
DEODAND: *देवदेयम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depart
DEPART (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्रतिष्ठते, सम्-, (स्था,<BR>c. l.) (on a journey), d. ed for Hariprastha:<BR>हरिप्रस्थं प्रतस्थे, Si. iii. 1.;<BR>(2) अपक्रामति (क्रम्,<BR>c. l.) (=to go away: q. v.),<BR>d. ed from the<BR>city:<BR>नगरादपक्रान्तः, Mu. i. Ph.:<BR>my parents have<BR>d. ed me for the hermitage:<BR>मां परित्यज्य तपोवनं<BR> यातौ पितरौ, Na. i.: v. To leave, one whose<BR>life is d. ed:<BR>विगतजीवितः (ता, तं), K. ; to d. this<BR>life (=to die: q. v.): परलोकं गच्छति।<BR>II<BR>Ph.: did not d. a line from the beaten track:<BR>क्षुण्णाद्वर्त्मनो रेखामात्रमपि नव्यतीयुः, R.;<BR>d. ed from<BR>virtue:<BR>धर्मभ्रष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं).<BR>III To pass away,<BR>vanish, set: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

departed
DEPARTED (adj.): i. e. dead: q. v.<BR>(1) दिवं<BR> गतः (ता, तं) (i. e. gone to heaven; of great<BR>men), Raj.;<BR>(2) परलोकगतः (ता, तं), Mu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

department
DEPARTMENT: विभागः (in all senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

departure
DEPARTURE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्रस्थानम्;<BR>(2) प्रयाणम्।<BR>II Death: q. v. परलोकगमनम्।<BR>III Deviation:<BR>q. v.: व्यतिक्रमः।<BR>IV Desertion: q. v.: त्यागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depend
DEPEND:<BR>I To hang: q. v.:<BR>II To be<BR>dependant on:<BR>(1) अधीनः (ना, नं) (in<BR>comp. or with loc.),<BR>for what have stoics to<BR>d. on us:<BR>अस्मास्वधीनं किमु निस्पृहाणाम्, Ki. iii.<BR>9.;<BR>pleasure d. s. on you:<BR>त्वदधीनं सुखम्, Ku.;<BR>(2) आयत्तः (त्ता, त्तं) (in comp. or with<BR>loc.), as the fruits of agriculture d. on you:<BR>त्वय्यायत्तं कृषिफलमिति, Me. i. 16.;<BR>whose life d. s<BR>entirely on water:<BR>जलैकायत्तजीवितः (ता, तं),<BR>M. n.;<BR>(3) निघ्नः (घ्ना, घ्नं) (with loc.) (rare),<BR>(4) -तन्त्र in comp. (rare), as it d. s. on (the<BR>will of)<BR>man:<BR>पुरुषतन्त्रत्वात्, S. i. 4.<BR>III To<BR>rely on: q. v.: विश्वसिति (श्वस्, c. 2.) (with<BR>loc.). Ph.:<BR>d. upon it:<BR>ध्रुवमेतदवेहि, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dependence
DEPENDENCE:<BR>I Suspension: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Connexion: q. v.: सम्बन्धः।<BR>III Reliance:<BR>q. v.: विश्वास।<BR>IV A state of subjection:<BR>(1) अधीनता;<BR>(2) आयत्तता;<BR>(3) निघ्नता (rare).<BR>V. That on which one depends:<BR>(1) आश्रयः;<BR>(2) अवलम्बनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dependency
DEPENDENCY:<BR>I Dependence: q. v.<BR>II A<BR>dependant state: अधीनराष्ट्रम्;<BR>England's<BR>d. s:<BR>इंलण्डाधीनराष्ट्राणि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dependent or dependant
DEPENDENT or DEPENDANT (adj.):<BR>I Hang-<BR>-ing down: प्रलम्बः (म्बा, म्बं).<BR>II Subject to:<BR>(1) अधीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) आयत्तः (त्ता, त्तं): v.<BR>To depend (II). D. on another:<BR>(1) पराधीनः<BR>(ना, नं);<BR>(2) परायत्तः (त्ता, त्तं);<BR>(3) परवशः<BR>(शा, शं);<BR>(4) प्रतन्त्रः (न्त्रा, न्त्रं);<BR>(5) परवत्<BR>(f. ती), N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dependent
DEPENDENT (subs.):<BR>(1) अनुजीविन् (f. ना),<BR>d. s<BR>of Suyodhana:<BR>सुयोधनानुजीविनः, Ve.<BR>(2) आश्रितः<BR>(ता, तं),<BR>my d. s:<BR>ममाश्रितान्, H. : v. Also<BR>servant, attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depict
DEPICT:<BR>I To paint: q. v.: चित्रयति (चित्र्<BR>c. 10.).<BR>II To describe: q. v.: वर्णयति (वर्ण्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depilate
DEPILATE: अपलोमं (मां,) करोति,<BR>skinned and<BR>d. d:<BR>अपलोमत्वच् (mfn.), D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depilation
DEPILATION:<BR>(1) लोमापनयनम्, etc.:<BR>(2) केशलुञ्चनम्<BR>(of the hair on the head), D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depilatory
DEPILATORY: लोमापहः (हा, हं): केशहरः (री,<BR> रं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deplete
DEPLETE:<BR>I To empty: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>exhaust: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deplorable
DEPLORABLE: शोचनीयः (या, यं): v. Lament-<BR>-able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deplorableness
DEPLORABLENESS: शोचनीयता: v. Misery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deplorably
DEPLORABLY: v. Miserably, exceedingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deplore
DEPLORE: शोचति, अनु-, (शुच्, c. l.): v. To<BR>lament, bewail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deploy
DEPLOY: विस्तारयति (c. of स्तृ): v. To extend,<BR>display.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deponent
DEPONENT:<BR>I A witness: q. v.: साक्षिन् (f.<BR>णी).<BR>II A verb: expr. by आत्मनेपदम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depopulate
DEPOPULATE:<BR>(1) निर्जनीकरोति;<BR>(2) निर्मानुषी-<BR>करोति;<BR>(3) शून्यीकरोति (=empty), d. the town:<BR>नगरं शून्यं कुरु, Vet.: v. To desolate, ravage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depopulation
DEPOPULATION:<BR>(1) निर्जनीकरणम्;<BR>(2) निर्मानुषी-<BR>करणम्: v. Desolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depopulator
DEPOPULATOR: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deport
DEPORT v.:<BR>I To transport, banish: q. v.:<BR>निर्वासयति (c. of वस्).<BR>II To behave: q. v.:<BR>व्यवहरति (हृ, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deportation
DEPORTATION: निर्वासनम्: v. Banishment,<BR>transportation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deportment
DEPORTMENT: व्यवहारः: v. Behaviour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depose
DEPOSE (v.):<BR>I To dethrone: राज्यात्<BR>or<BR>राष्ट्राद्<BR> अवरोपयति (c. of रुह्)<BR>or<BR>पातयति (c. of पत्),<BR>Khāṇḍikya was d. d by Keshidhwaja:<BR>केशिध्वजेन<BR> खाण्डिक्यः स्वराष्ट्रादवरोपितः, V. p.<BR>II To dismiss:<BR>q. v.<BR>III To bear testimony:<BR>(1) साक्ष्यं<BR> ददाति (=give evidence);<BR>(2) वदति, वक्ति,<BR>etc. (=to say: when the meaning is<BR>clear),<BR>d. falsely:<BR>अनृतं वदति, V. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deposit
DEPOSIT (v.): निक्षिपति (क्षिप् c. l.): v. To<BR>lay down, entrust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deposit
DEPOSIT (subs.):<BR>I Pledge: q. v.: निक्षेपः।<BR>II Sediment: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depositary
DEPOSITARY:<BR>(1) निक्षेपग्राहकः;<BR>(2) न्यासग्रहीतृ<BR>(m.): v. Trustee, pledgee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deposition
DEPOSITION:<BR>I The act of dethroning:<BR>राज्यात्पातनम्<BR>or<BR>अवरोपणम्।<BR>II The state of<BR>being dethroned: राज्यभ्रंशः, राज्यच्युतिः।<BR>III<BR>Dismissal: q. v.<BR>IV Testimony:<BR>(1) उक्तिः<BR>(=saying);<BR>(2) साक्ष्यम् (=evidence). V.<BR>Depositing:<BR>(1) निक्षेपः, -णम्;<BR>(2) न्यासः or<BR>न्यसनम्।<BR>VI Presentation: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depositor
DEPOSITOR:<BR>(1) निक्षेप्तृ (f. प्त्री);<BR>(2) न्यासकर्तृ<BR>(f. र्त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depository
DEPOSITORY:<BR>(1) आशयः;<BR>(2) आधारः (=recep-<BR>-tacle);<BR>(3) निधिः (only in fig. sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depot
DEPOT:<BR>I A warehouse: q. v.<BR>II A military<BR>d.: सैन्यनिवेशः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depravation
DEPRAVATION: दूषणम्: v. Corruption, per-<BR>-version.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deprave
DEPRAVE:<BR>I To corrupt: q. v.: दूषयति।<BR>II<BR>To defame: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depraved
DEPRAVED: of men:<BR>(1) पामरः (री, रं);<BR>(2)<BR>खण्डितवृत्तः (त्ता, त्तं);<BR>(3) दुराचारः (रा, रं);<BR>(4) दुरात्मन् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depravity
DEPRAVITY:<BR>(1) दुराचारता;<BR>(2) दौर्जन्यम्;<BR>(3)<BR>दौरात्म्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deprecate
DEPRECATE:<BR>I Lit.: शान्तये<BR>or<BR>शान्तिमधिकृत्य<BR> ईश्वरम् उपच्छन्दयति (छन्द्, c. 10.).<BR>II To<BR>regret: q. v.: अनुशोचयति (शुच्, c. l.).<BR>III<BR>To censure: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deprecation
DEPRECATION:<BR>I Prayer: स्तवः।<BR>II Begging<BR>pardon: क्षमाप्रार्थना।<BR>III Curse: शापः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deprecatory
DEPRECATORY: शान्तिमधिकृत्य, R.;<BR>to perform d.<BR>rites:<BR>शान्तिं करोति, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depreciate
DEPRECIATE:<BR>(1) अपवदति (वद्, c. 1.);<BR>(2)<BR>अवक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depreciation
DEPRECIATION:<BR>(1) अपवादः;<BR>(2) अवक्षेपः: v.<BR>Disparagement, detraction. D. (i. e. fall in<BR>price): अर्घस्य ह्रासः, Vy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depredate
DEPREDATE:<BR>(1) उप-द्रवति, अभि-, (द्रु, c. l.),<BR>d. d Prāgjyotiṣa (Gauhati) प्राग्ज्योतिषमुपाद्रवत्,<BR>Mah.;<BR>the gods d. d by Rāvaṇa:<BR>पौलस्त्योपद्रुता<BR> देवाः, R.<BR>(2) उपप्लवते (प्लु, c. l.),: v. Also to<BR>plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depredation
DEPREDATION:<BR>(1) उपद्रवः;<BR>(2) उपप्लवः,<BR>for<BR>committing d. s on people:<BR>लोकानामुपप्लवाय, Ku.:<BR>v. Also to plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depredator
DEPREDATOR:<BR>(1) उपद्रवकारिन् (m.);<BR>(2) उप-<BR>प्लवकारिन् (m.);<BR>(3) विप्रकर्तृ (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depress
DEPRESS (v.):<BR>I Lit.: to press down:<BR>पातयति (c. of पत्).<BR>II To humble: लघूकरोति।<BR>III To deject, discourage:<BR>(1) विषादं or<BR>वैमनस्यं जनयति;<BR>(2) खेदयति (c. of खिद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depression
DEPRESSION:<BR>I Lit.: पातनम्।<BR>II A cavity:<BR>बिलम्,<BR>the face is coverd with d. s.:<BR>वलिभिर्मुखमा-<BR>क्रान्तम्, J.<BR>III Humiliation: q. v.<BR>IV Of<BR>spirits: सत्त्वभ्रंशः, Vi.: v. Defection, despon-<BR>-dency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deprivation
DEPRIVATION:<BR>(1) हरणम्;<BR>(2) वियोगः: v. To<BR>deprive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deprive
DEPRIVE (v.):<BR>(1) हरति, अप-, (हृ, c. l.) (=to<BR>take away: q. v.),<BR>say what has not been<BR>taken away by death by d. ing me of you:<BR>मृत्युना हरता त्वां वद किं न मे हृतम्, R.;<BR>(2) वियोजयति<BR>or -युंक्ते (युज्, c. 10 and 7.) (=to disunite,<BR>separate),<BR>d. d of his life:<BR>प्राणैर्वियोजितः (ता,<BR> तं), D. ;<BR>(3) विनाकरोति (=2), d. d of Cupid:<BR>मदनेन विनाकृता, Ku.;<BR>(4) हापयति (c. of हा)<BR>(=cause to leave),<BR>or will be soon d. d of his<BR>life:<BR>प्राणैर्वा हाप्यतेऽचिरात्, A. r.: v. Also<BR>devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depth
DEPTH: Lit.:<BR>(1) गभीरता;<BR>(2) गाम्भीर्यम्, (we)<BR>get the d. of water:<BR>लब्धं जलगाम्भीर्यम्, Li.<BR>II<BR>Fig.:<BR>(1) गभीरता;<BR>(2) गाम्भीर्यम्: v. Deep.<BR>III A deep: q. v.: Ph.: in the d. of night:<BR>विगाढायां शर्वर्याम्, C.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deputation
DEPUTATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) प्रेरणम् (=send-<BR>-ing);<BR>(2) नियोगः (=employing).<BR>II The<BR>person or persons deputed:<BR>(1) प्रतिनिधिः,<BR>I am sent as his d.:<BR>स्वप्रतिनिधिः प्रेषितोऽस्मि, B. r.;<BR>(2) दूतः (=ambassador), (the king)<BR>Bhoja<BR>sent a d. to Raghu:<BR>भोजेन दूतो रघवे विसृष्टः, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

depute
DEPUTE:<BR>(1) प्रेरयति (ईर, c. 1.): v. To send;<BR>(2) नियुंक्ते (युज्, c. 7.): v. To employ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deputy
DEPUTY:<BR>(1) प्रतिनिधिः;<BR>(2) प्रतिहस्तः -कः।<BR>D.<BR>collector:<BR>*प्रतिनिधिकरनायकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

derange
DERANGE: क्षोभयति, वि-, (c. of क्षुम्): v. To<BR>disturb, confuse. D. d (in mind) उन्मत्तः (त्ता,<BR> त्तं): v. Insane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

derangement
DERANGEMENT:<BR>I Confusion: q. v.: विक्षोभः।<BR>II Insanity: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dereliction
DERELICTION: त्यागः: v. Abandonment,<BR>neglect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deride
DERIDE: अवहसति, उप-, अप-, (हस्, c. l.): v.<BR>To laugh at, ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

derider
DERIDER:<BR>(1) उपहासकः;<BR>(2) अवहासकः;<BR>(3)<BR>अपहासकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deriding
DERIDING, DERIDINGLY: v. Derisive, deri-<BR>-sively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

derision
DERISION:<BR>(1) उपहासः;<BR>(2) अवहासः: v. Ridi-<BR>-cule, mockery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

derisive
DERISIVE:<BR>(1) सोपहासः (सा, सं);<BR>(2) सावहासः<BR>(सा, सं);<BR>(3) अपहासगर्भः (र्भा, र्भं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

derisively
DERISIVELY:<BR>(1) सोपहासम्;<BR>(2) सावहासम्;<BR>(3)<BR>सापहासम। Ph.:<BR>d. and contemptuously:<BR>अव-<BR>हस्यावमन्य च, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

derivation
DERIVATION:<BR>I Lit.: of words, etc.: व्युत्पत्तिः।<BR>II That which is derived: शाखा, “artificial<BR>d.”: कृत्रिमशाखा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

derivative
DERIVATIVE (subs.): व्युत्पन्नशब्दः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

derive
DERIVE v.:<BR>I To draw from: Ph.:<BR>the race d. d<BR>from the sun:<BR>सूर्यप्रभवो वंशः, R.;<BR>one who is d. d<BR>from Virasena:<BR>वोरसेनोद्भूतिः, N.: v. Origin,<BR>arising from. II. Of words: व्युत्पत्तिं वदति<BR>(वद्, c. l.): v. To say.<BR>To be d. d:<BR>व्युत्प-<BR>द्यते (पद्, c. 4),<BR>as being d. d in the passive<BR>sense:<BR>कर्मव्युत्पन्नतया, Da. com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

derogate
DEROGATE:<BR>I To detract, disparage: q. v.<BR>II To restrict: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

derogation
DEROGATION: अवमानना: v. Detraction, insult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

derogatory
DEROGATORY: expr. by subs.,<BR>this is d. to<BR>God:<BR>*इदमीश्वरस्यावमानना: v. Detraction,<BR>insult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dervise
DERVISE: *महम्मदीययतिः<BR>or<BR>संन्यासिन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

descant
DESCANT (v.):<BR>I To sing: q. v.<BR>II To com-<BR>-ment: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">Page190</a>] विस्तरेण वदति (वद्, c. l.), वक्ति (वच्,<BR>c. 2.), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

descant
DESCANT (subs.)<BR>I To songs: q. v.: गीतम्।<BR>II A discourse:<BR>(1) वाग्जालम्, Si. ii. 27.;<BR>(2) वागाडम्बरः, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

decend
DECEND:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अवतरति (तॄ, c. l) (=to<BR>d. wilfully),<BR>d. ed from the sky:<BR>ज्योतिष्पथादव-<BR>ततार, R. xii. 68.;<BR>(2) अवरोहति (रुह्, c. l.)<BR>(=अवतरति),<BR>as if d. ing from the summits of<BR>mountains:<BR>शैलानामवरोहतीव शिखरात्, Sa. vii. 8.;<BR>(3) अवपतति (पत्, c. l.) (=to d. irrespective<BR>of one's own will), caught the d. ing (ball)<BR>in<BR>the air:<BR>अवपतन्तमाकाश एवाग्रहीत्, D. vi.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>अवतरति,<BR>then why d. ing into the considera-<BR>tion of..<BR>तत्र कुतो॥।चिन्तावतारः, S.<BR>III To<BR>make an attack: v. Descent (II).<BR>IV To<BR>come down: आगच्छति (गम्, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

descendant
DESCENDANT: सन्ततिः: v. Offspring. D. s:<BR>पुत्रपौत्राः (pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

descended
DESCENDED: i. e. derived:<BR>(1) by a deriv.,<BR>d.<BR>from Yadu:<BR>यादवः;<BR>d. from Puru:<BR>पौरवः;<BR>(2)<BR>जातः (ता, तं) (=born: q. v.);<BR>(3) उद्भूतः (ता,<BR> तं) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

descending
DESCENDING (adj.): Ph.:<BR>d. scale:<BR>*अवरोहपद्धतिः;<BR>d. node:<BR>पातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

descent
DESCENT:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अवतरणम्<BR>or<BR>अवतारः,<BR>as if<BR>to tell the news of Minerva's d.:<BR>सरस्वत्यवतरण-<BR>वार्त्तमिव कथयितुम्, C.;<BR>(2) अवरोहः, -णम्;<BR>(3)<BR>अवपातः (falling);<BR>(4) अधोगतिः (=going<BR>downwards).<BR>II Attack: q. v.:<BR>we made<BR>a d. on Vindhyaketu:<BR>विन्ध्यकेतोरुपरि निपतिताः स्म,<BR>Pri.<BR>III. Lineage, birth: q. v.:<BR>princes of<BR>noble d.:<BR>कुलजाः कुमाराः, N.<BR>IV Issue: सन्ततिः।<BR>V. A declivity, slope: अवसर्पिणी (भूमिः), Mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

describe
DESCRIBE (v. t.):<BR>I To draw: लिखति (लिख्,<BR>c. 6.),<BR>to d. a circle:<BR>मण्डलं लिखति, Su.<BR>II<BR>To give a description of:<BR>(1) वर्णयति, उप-,<BR> अनु-, सं-, (वर्ण्, c. 10.), she has d. d her dream:<BR>स्वप्नदर्शनमनया वर्णितम्, Ve. ii.;<BR>d. s Himālaya<BR>in sixteen verses:<BR>षोडशम्भिः श्लोकैर्हिमाद्रिं वर्णयति,<BR>M. n.;<BR>(2) व्या-ख्याति (ख्या, c. 2.) (to d.<BR>and explain), At.;<BR>(3) आ-ख्याति: v. To<BR>narrate, say.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

describer
DESCRIBER: वर्णयितृ (f. त्री), उप-, अनु-, सं-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

description
DESCRIPTION: वर्णना, -नम्, उप-, सं-,<BR>d. of Shan-<BR>karavarman:<BR>शङ्करवर्मणो वर्णनम्, B. r.: v. Also<BR>narration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

descry
DESCRY: पश्यति (दृश्, c. l.): To see, dis-<BR>-cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desecrate
DESECRATE:<BR>(1) अपवित्रीकरोति;<BR>(2) दूषयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desecration
DESECRATION:<BR>(1) अपवित्रीकरणम्;<BR>(2) दूषणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desert
DESERT (adj.):<BR>(1) विजनः (ना, नं): v. Soli-<BR>-tary;<BR>(2) खिलः (ला, लं): v. Waste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desert
DESERT (subs.):<BR>I A waste place:<BR>(1) मरु-<BR>भूमिः;<BR>(2) धन्वन् (m.) (rare). Ph.: a sandy d.:<BR>वालुकार्णवः, Mah.<BR>II Merit: q. v.: गुणः,<BR>d.<BR>and not acquaintance:<BR>गुणा न संस्तवः, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desert
DESERT (v.): त्यजति, परि-, सं-, (त्यज्, c. l.),<BR>servants d. a master when his fortune is gone:<BR>भृत्यास्त्यजन्ति प्रचलितविभवं स्वामिनम्, Mu.;<BR>(2)<BR>जहाति, वि-, अप-, (हा, c. 3.); d. ing a dear wife:<BR>अपहाय प्रियां भार्याम्, Mah.;<BR>(3) उत्सृजति (सृज्, c.<BR>6.), d. ing a sleeping (woman) in the forest:<BR>उत्सृज्य विपिने सुप्ताम्, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deserter
DESERTER:<BR>I Lit.: त्यागिन् (m.).<BR>II A soldier<BR>or seaman: *नियोगत्यागिन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desertion
DESERTION:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) त्यागः, परि-;<BR>(2)<BR>उत्सर्गः।<BR>II Military: *नियोगत्यागः, नियोगाद-<BR>पसरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deserve
DESERVE (v.): अर्हति (अर्ह्, c. l.), d. s death:<BR>वधमर्हति, M.;<BR>d. s snakebite:<BR>अर्हति सर्पदंशनम्,<BR>Mal.: v. Deserving, deserving of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deservedly
DESERVEDLY:<BR>(1) योग्यतया;<BR>(2) अर्हतया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deserving
DESERVING (adj.):<BR>(1) योग्यः (ग्या, ग्यं),<BR>to the<BR>most d.:<BR>योग्यतमाय, Ki. iv. 26.;<BR>(2) उपयुक्तः<BR>(क्ता, क्तं);<BR>(3) अर्हः (र्हा, र्हं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deserving of
DESERVING OF:<BR>(1) often by a part. in य,<BR>d. of<BR>compassion<BR>अनुकम्प्यः (म्प्या, म्प्यं) R.;<BR>d. of<BR>death:<BR>वध्यः (ध्या, ध्यं), R.;<BR>(2) by words given<BR>above:<BR>d. of death:<BR>वधार्हः (र्हा, र्हं), M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deservingly
DESERVINGLY:<BR>(1) योग्यतया;<BR>(2) अर्हतया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deshabille
DESHABILLE:<BR>in d.:<BR>एकवस्त्रः (f. स्त्रा), Mah.:<BR>v. Undress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desiccate
DESICCATE:<BR>I To dry: q. v.: शोषयति (c. of<BR>शुष्).<BR>II To become dry: (शुष्यति (शुष्,<BR>c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desiccation
DESICCATION: शोषणम्: v. Drying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desiderate
DESIDERATE: v. To want, need.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desiderative
DESIDERATIVE:<BR>(1) इच्छार्थकः (का, कं);<BR>(2)<BR>सनन्तः (न्ता, तं) (of Sanskrit d. s).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desideratum
DESIDERATUM: अभावः (=want).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

design
DESIGN (v. t.):<BR>I To draw, delineate: q. v.<BR>II To indicate: q. v.<BR>III To project:<BR>q. v.: कल्पयति, परि-, सं-, (कऌप, c. 10.).<BR>IV<BR>To intend, purpose: q. v.: कल्पयति, परि-,<BR> सं-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

design
DESIGN (subs.):<BR>I A sketch: q. v.: सूत्रपातः।<BR>II Device, plot: q. v.: मन्त्रणा।<BR>III Inten-<BR>-tion, purpose: q. v.: आशयः,<BR>my d.:<BR>मदाशयः,<BR>Mu.<BR>IV Of medals etc.: गठनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

designate
DESIGNATE:<BR>I To name: q. v.: आख्याति<BR>(ख्या, c. 2).<BR>II To nominate, elect:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

designation
DESIGNATION:<BR>I Name: q. v.: आख्या,<BR>got<BR>the d. of Aparṇā<BR>अपर्णाख्यामवाप, S. p.<BR>II<BR>Appointment, selection: q. v.: नियोगः।<BR>III<BR>Signification: q. v.: अर्थः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

designedly
DESIGNEDLY:<BR>(1) कामतः (=intentionally);<BR>(2)<BR>ज्ञानतः (=knowingly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

designer
DESIGNER:<BR>I In good sense: *रूपोद्भावकः;<BR> गठनकल्पकः।<BR>II A schemer, plotter: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

designing
DESIGNING:<BR>(1) चतुरः (रा, रं) (=artful);<BR>(2)<BR>उपजापिन् (f. नी) (=intriguing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desirable
DESIRABLE:<BR>(1) अभिलषणीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2)<BR>वाञ्छनीयः (या, यं);<BR>(3) आकाङ्क्षणीयः (या, यं);<BR>(4) एषणीयः (या, यं) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desirability
DESIRABILITY, DESIRABLENESS:<BR>(1) वाञ्छणीयता;<BR>(2) better by adj.: v. Desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desire
DESIRE (subs.):<BR>(1) इच्छा,<BR>although I have not<BR>satisfied your d.:<BR>अनिच्छापूरकोऽपि, Sa. iii.;<BR>(2)<BR>अभिलाषः,<BR>d. for Tilottamā:<BR>तिलोत्तमायामभिलाषः,<BR>D. ii.;<BR>(2) वाञ्छा,<BR>d. rises from it:<BR>ततो वाञ्छा<BR> प्रवर्तते, H. ;<BR>(4) मनोरथ: (wish: q. v.);<BR>(5)<BR>कामना (=wish);<BR>(6) स्पृहा (=longing: q. v.);<BR>(7) कामः (often =lust);<BR>(8) by desi. noun,<BR>d.<BR>to see:<BR>दिदृक्षा;<BR>(9) इष्टम् (=object of d.),<BR>be<BR>united with your d.:<BR>इष्टेन युज्यस्व, Sa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desire
DESIRE (v. t.):<BR>I To wish, long for: q. v.:<BR>(1) इच्छति (इष, c. 6.);<BR>(2) by desi. verb,<BR>d. to go:<BR>जिगमिषति, K.<BR>II. To ask: q. v.:<BR>याचते (याच्, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desirous
DESIROUS:<BR>(1) इच्छु (mfn.);<BR>(2) इच्छुकः (का,<BR> कं);<BR>(3) अभिलषिन् (f. णी);<BR>(4) अभिलाषुकः<BR>(का, कं);<BR>(5) वाञ्छिन् (f. नी);<BR>(6) by desi.<BR>adj.,<BR>I am d. of hearing you:<BR>तव गिरः शुश्रूषुरहम्,<BR>Si.;<BR>d. of seeing Indra:<BR>इन्द्रं दिदृक्षुः, N.;<BR>d. of again saying something:<BR>किमपि पुनर्विवक्षुः,<BR>Ku.: v. Eager; to wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desist
DESIST: विरमति (रम्, c. l.), d. from this work:<BR>विरम कर्मणोऽस्मात्, D.: v. To cease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desk
DESK: *देश्कम्: v. Bench.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desolate
DESOLATE (adj.):<BR>I Uninhabited:<BR>(1)<BR>निर्मानुषः (षा, षं), and sim. comp. s, a d. forest:<BR>निर्मानुषमरण्यम्, K. ;<BR>(2) खिलः (ला, लं), (=empty),<BR>the road being d.:<BR>खिलीभूते पथि, Ku. ii. 45.<BR>II Decayed: जीर्णः (र्णा, र्णं), a d. garden:<BR>जीर्णोद्यानम्, Mu.<BR>III Lonely: असहायः (या,<BR> यं), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desolate
DESOLATE (v.): उच्छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7.): v.<BR>To devastate, ravage,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desolateness
DESOLATENESS:<BR>I Uninhabitedness: निर्मानु-<BR>षत्वम्, and sim. comp. s.<BR>II Decayed state:<BR>जीर्णता।<BR>III Loneliness: असहायता, -त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desolation
DESOLATION: उच्छेदः: v. Devastation, ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despair
DESPAIR (subs.): नौराशयम्<BR>or<BR>निराशता। In d. (as<BR>adj.): निराशः (शा, शं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despair
DESPAIR (v. i.): निराशः (शा, शं) भवति,<BR>d. ed as to<BR>his life:<BR>निराशो जीवितेऽभवत्, Raj.;<BR>(2) नैराशयं<BR> व्रजति, निराशतां गच्छति, etc., d. ing of flying:<BR>उड्डयने निराशतां गतः, N. i. 125.;<BR>(3) आशां जहाति,<BR>etc. (=to abandon hope: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despairingly
DESPAIRINGLY:<BR>(1) निराशः (शा, शं);<BR>(2)<BR>नौराश्यात्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despatch
DESPATCH (v. t.):<BR>I To send, depute: q. v.:<BR>प्रेरयति (ईर्, c. 10.).<BR>II To kill: q. v.:<BR>(शमनसदनं) प्रेरयति, (the son of Śiva)<BR>having<BR>thus d. ed the demon-king:<BR>इति (हरतनयेन)<BR>प्रेरिते दानवेन्द्रे, Ku. xvii. 56.<BR>III To perform.<BR>execute: q. v.: समादधाति<BR>or<BR>त्वरितं समादधाति<BR>or<BR>धत्ते (धा, c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despatch
DESPATCH (subs.):<BR>I The act of sending:<BR>(1) प्रेरणम्;<BR>(2) प्रेषणम्।<BR>II Dismissal: विसर्जनम्। [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">Page192</a>]<BR>III Hasty execution: q. v.:<BR>with d.:<BR>त्वरितम्<BR>or<BR>क्षिप्रम्।<BR>IV A message:<BR>(1) पत्रम् (=letter);<BR>(2) सन्देशः।<BR>D. -box:<BR>सन्देशपे टिका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desperado
DESPERADO:<BR>(1) साहसिकः (=daring);<BR>(2)<BR>उन्मत्तः (=mad).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desperate
DESPERATE:<BR>I Hopeless: q. v.: निराशः (शा,<BR> शं).<BR>II Beyond hope: आशातीतः। Ph.:<BR>the<BR>case is d.:<BR>अतिभूमिमयं गतः (lit. gone to the<BR>extreme), K.;<BR>a d. disease:<BR>वैद्ययत्नपरिभावी गदः,<BR>R. : v. Incurable.<BR>III Excessive: q. v.:<BR>IV Daring: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desperately
DESPERATELY:<BR>I Furiously: q. v.: उन्मत्तः<BR>(त्ता, त्तं) इव।<BR>II Exclusively: q. v.: निरति-<BR>शयम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desperation
DESPERATION: नौराश्यम्: v. Despair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despicable
DESPICABLE: जघन्यः (न्या, न्यं): v. Mean,<BR>worthless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despise
DESPISE:<BR>(1) अवजानाति (ज्ञा, c. l.),<BR>d. ed in<BR>mind:<BR>मनसावज्ञातवान्, D. ;<BR>(2) अवमन्यते (मन्,<BR>c. 4.),<BR>I will not d. high Brahmins:<BR>नावमंस्ये<BR> ब्राह्मणर्षभान्, Mah.;<BR>(3) जुगुप्सते (=to hate:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(4) तुच्छयति (nomi.):<BR>(5) तृणीकरोति;<BR>(6) न गणयति (गण्, c. 10.): v. To care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despisingly
DESPISINGLY:<BR>(1) अवज्ञया;<BR>(2) सावमानम्;<BR>(3)<BR>अनादरेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despite
DESPITE (subs.):<BR>I Hatred, malice: q. v.:<BR>जुगुप्सा।<BR>II Defiance, contempt:<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despite
DESPITE (prep.):<BR>(1) अवमन्य;<BR>(2) अवगणय्य;<BR>etc.: v. To despise^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despiteful
DESPITEFUL, DESPITEFULLY: v. Malicious,<BR>maliciously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despoil
DESPOIL: हरति (हृ, c. l.): v: To deprive,<BR>divert, rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despoliation
DESPOLIATION: हरणम्: v. Deprivation, divest-<BR>-ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despond
DESPOND (v.): निर्वेदं गच्छति (गम्, c. l.),<BR>आपद्यते (पद्, c. 4.), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despondency
DESPONDENCY:<BR>(1) निर्वेदः;<BR>(2) विषादः (=de-<BR>-jection).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despondent
DESPONDENT:<BR>(1) निर्विण्णः (ण्णा, ण्णं);<BR>(2) विषण्णः<BR>(ण्णा, ण्णं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despondingly
DESPONDINGLY:<BR>(1) सनिर्वेदम्;<BR>(2) विषण्णम्;<BR>(3)<BR>नौराशयात्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despot
DESPOT:<BR>I A lord: q. v.<BR>II A tyrant: q. v.:<BR>घूमकेतुः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despotical
DESPOTICAL: स्वेच्छाचारिन् (f. णी): v. Also<BR>tyrannically.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despotically
DESPOTICALLY: स्वेच्छाचारेण: v. Also tyranni-<BR>-cally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despotism
DESPOTISM: स्वेच्छाचारित्वम्: v. Also tyranny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despumate
DESPUMATE: फेनायते (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

despumation
DESPUMATION: निष्फेनीकरणम्, (?): v. Clarifi-<BR>-cation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dessert
DESSERT: फलमिष्टादीनि (n. pl.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

destination
DESTINATION:<BR>I Intention, purpose: q. v.:<BR>अभिप्रायः।<BR>II End of a journey: ईप्सितं<BR> स्थानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

destine
DESTINE:<BR>(1) स्थिरीकरोति (=to fix: q. v.);<BR>(2) better by circumlo,<BR>I am ‘d. d to eternal<BR>woe’:<BR>*अविरतदुःखं कपाले मे लिखितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

destiny
DESTINY: भवितव्यता,<BR>following d.:<BR>भवितव्यतानु-<BR>विधायिन् (f. नी), V.: v. Fate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

destitute
DESTITUTE: दीनः (ना, नं): v. Needy, indi-<BR>-gent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

destitue of
DESTITUE OF: हीनः (ना, नं): v. Devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

destitution
DESTITUTION:<BR>I Indigence, poverty: q. v.:<BR>दैन्यम्।<BR>II The state of being destitute of:<BR>हीनता, वि-, परि-, in tat. comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

destroy
DESTROY:<BR>(1) नाशयति, वि-, प्र-, (c. of नश्),<BR>why has he d. ed the whole park:<BR>वनं किमर्थं सकलं<BR> विनाशितम्, A. r.; d. (our)<BR>ignorance:<BR>अज्ञानं<BR> विनाशय, B. p.;<BR>(2) ध्वंसयति, वि-, प्र-, (c. of ध्वंस्)<BR>(=demolish),<BR>Hanumān who has d. ed the,<BR>whole city:<BR>विध्वंसिताशेषपुरो हनुमान्, B. xii. 23.;<BR>(3) क्षयं नयति (नी, c. l.) (=to annihilate),<BR>d. ed Rākṣasas:<BR>अनौषीद्राक्षसान् क्षयम्, B. xv. 10.;<BR>(4) हन्ति (हन्, c. 2.) (prop. =to kill).<BR>if this<BR>garland d. s life:<BR>स्रगियं यदि जीवितापहा, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

destroyed
DESTROYED, BE or GET:<BR>(1) नश्यति, वि-, (नश्,<BR>c. 4.):<BR>(2) नाशम्<BR>or<BR>विनाशमेति (इ, c. 2.), अवा-<BR>प्नोति (आप्, c. 5.) etc., everything else gets d.:<BR>नाशं सर्वमन्यद्धि गच्छति, M.;<BR>(3) ध्वंसं<BR>or<BR>प्रध्वंसं or<BR>विध्वंसम् एति etc., Ki.;<BR>(4) ध्वंसते, वि-, प्र-,<BR>(ध्वंस्, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

destroyer
DESTROYER:<BR>(1) नाशकः, वि-, d. of Tāraka:<BR>तारकस्य विनाशकः, Mat.;<BR>(2) नाशयितृ, वि-, (m.) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">Page193</a>]<BR>Ch.;<BR>(3) नाशः, -नः in bah. comp.,<BR>d. of<BR>sins.:<BR>पापनाशः, J.;<BR>(4) हन्ता (=slayer: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

destroying
DESTROYING (adj.): नाशिन्, प्र-, (f. नी) in<BR>comp.,<BR>sin-d.:<BR>पापप्रणाशिन् (f. नी), Mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

destructibility
DESTRUCTIBILITY: नश्वरता, वि-,: v. Frailty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

destructible
DESTRUCTIBLE:<BR>(1) नश्वरः (री, रं), वि-,<BR>in d.<BR>wealth:<BR>नश्वरवित्ते, J. ;<BR>(2) ध्वंसिन् (f. नी), वि-,<BR>body is d. in a moment:<BR>शरीरं क्षणविध्वंसि, H.:<BR>v. Frail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

destruction
DESTRUCTION:<BR>(1) नाशः, वि-, for one's own d.:<BR>स्वनाशाय, A. r.;<BR>(2) ध्वंसः, वि-, प्र-, (strictly=<BR>demolition),<BR>from the d. of the seed of igno-<BR>rance:<BR>अविद्याबीजविध्वंसात्, Ana.;<BR>(3) क्षयः<BR>(gradual complete d.),<BR>I have avenged the d.<BR>of my race:<BR>साधितं मया कुलक्षयजं वैरम्, P. Ph.: to<BR>come to or meet d.: v. Destroyed, get.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

destructive
DESTRUCTIVE:<BR>(1) नाशिन्, वि-, प्र-, (f. नी) in<BR>comp.;<BR>(2) अपहः (हा, हं)<BR>or<BR>घ्नः (घ्नी, घ्नं) in<BR>comp.:<BR>(3) प्राणहरः (री, रं) (d. of life), Bha.;<BR>(4) क्षयावह (हा, हं)<BR>d. of monkeys:<BR>वानराणां क्षया-<BR>वहः, P. v. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

destructively
DESTRUCTIVELY: नाशम्<BR>or<BR>क्षयम् परिकल्प्य (with<BR>gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

destructiveness
DESTRUCTIVENESS:<BR>(1) नाशकत्वम्;<BR>(2) क्षयावहता;<BR>(3) better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desuetude
DESUETUDE: अव्यवहारः: v. Disuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

desultory
DESULTORY:<BR>(1) अधीरः (रा, रं) (=hasty);<BR>(2) उच्छ्टङ्खलः (ला, लं) (=without order);<BR>(3)<BR>भ्रान्तः (न्ता, न्तं) (=roving).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detach
DETACH:<BR>I To separate, disunite: q. v.:<BR>विशलेषयति (c. of शिलष्).<BR>II To send: q. v.:<BR>प्रेषयति (c. of इष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detachment
DETACHMENT:<BR>I Separation: q. v.: विशलेषः।<BR>II A body of troops: दलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detail
DETAIL (v. t.): विस्तरेण<BR>or<BR>विस्तरतः<BR>or<BR>कार्त्स्येन कथयति<BR>(कथ्, c. 10.) (=to tell: q. v.)<BR>or<BR>वर्णयति<BR>(=to describe), d. to us the birth of Kārtika:<BR>अस्माकं गुहजन्म कात्स्येन ब्रूहि, Mat.;<BR>I want to<BR>hear a d. ed account of it:<BR>विस्तरेण श्रोतुमिच्छामि,<BR>Mu. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detail
DETAIL (subs.): विस्तरः<BR>or<BR>विस्तारः,<BR>d. s of the<BR>army of the gods also:<BR>सुराणामपि सैन्यानां विस्तरः,<BR>Mat.<BR>In d.:<BR>विस्तरेण<BR>or<BR>विस्तरतः<BR>or<BR>सविस्तरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detain
DETAIN (v.):<BR>I To with-hold: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>restrain from proceeding: Ph.<BR>we were d. ed<BR>by the rain:<BR>*वृष्ट्या नो विलम्बो जनितः: v. Delay.<BR>III To hold in custody: रक्षति (रक्ष्, c.<BR>1.): v. To keep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detainer
DETAINER: a writ: *रक्षापत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detect
DETECT:<BR>(1) प्रकाशयति (c. of काश्);<BR>(2)<BR>बहिष्करोति (कृ, c. 8.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detection
DETECTION:<BR>(1) प्रकाशः, -नम्;<BR>(2) बहिष्कारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detective
DETECTIVE: Ph.: d. officer:<BR>(1) चरः<BR>or<BR>चारः<BR>(=spy), Ve. vi.; सुनिपुणसञ्चारालापादिभिस्तस्करा-<BR>दिप्रकाशकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detention
DETENTION:<BR>I Confinement, restraint: q. v.:<BR>निरोधः।<BR>II Delay: q. v.: विलम्बः।<BR>III With-<BR>-holding: v. To withhold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deter
DETER: निवर्तयति (c. of वृत्): v. To prevent,<BR>hinder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deterge
DETERGE: शोधयति, वि-, (c. of शुध्): v. To<BR>cleanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detergent
DETERGENT:<BR>I Adj.: शोधनः (नी, नं).<BR>II<BR>Subs.: शोधनम्, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deteriorate
DETERIORATE (v.):<BR>I Intrans:<BR>(1) हीयते (pass.<BR>of हा);<BR>(2) क्षयं गच्छति (गम्, c. l.).<BR>II<BR>Trans.:<BR>(1) हीनीकरोति;<BR>(2) क्षयं नयति (नी,<BR>c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deterioration
DETERIORATION: क्षयः: v. Degeneracy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

determent
DETERMENT: निवर्तनम्: v. Prevention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

determinate
DETERMINATE: स्थिरः (रा, रं): v. Fixed, de-<BR>-finite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

determination
DETERMINATION:<BR>I The act of determining:<BR>निर्णयः, वि-,<BR>d. of boundaries:<BR>सीमाविनिर्णयः, M.<BR>II Resolution: q. v.: निश्चयः, is this your d.:<BR>एष ते निश्चयः, Mu.<BR>III.: Purpose: q. v.: प्रति-<BR>पत्तिः,<BR>what is your d.:<BR>का ते प्रतिपत्तिः, D.<BR>IV<BR>Direction or tendency: गतिः।<BR>V Termina-<BR>-tion: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

determine
DETERMINE:<BR>I To limit: q. v.<BR>II To settle,<BR>decide: q. v.: निरूपयति (रूप्, c. 10.).<BR>(2)<BR>निर्णयति (नी, c. l.).<BR>III To resolve: q. v.:<BR>निश्चयं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

determinedly
DETERMINEDLY:<BR>(1) निश्चितम्;<BR>(2) स्थिरम्: v.<BR>Firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detersive
DETERSIVE: शोधनः (नी, नं): v. Detergent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detest
DETEST: जुगुप्सते (जुगुप्स्, c. l.): v. To hate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detestable
DETESTABLE:<BR>(1) गर्हितः (ता, तं), the very d.<BR>Chārvāka (philosophy): चार्वाकमतिगर्हितम्, P. p.;<BR>घृणितः (ता, तं);<BR>(3) जुगुप्सितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detestably
DETESTABLY:<BR>I Lit.: जुगुप्सया।<BR>II Excessively:<BR>q. v.: अत्यन्तम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detestation
DETESTATION: जुगुप्सा: v. Hatred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detester
DETESTER: expr. by verb or subs.: v. Also<BR>hater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dethrone
DETHRONE: सिंहासनात् पातयति (c. of पत्), Mu.<BR>i.: v. To depose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dethronement
DETHRONEMENT: छत्रभङ्गः: v. Deposition (I)<BR>and (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detonate
DETONATE (v.):<BR>I Intrans: स्तनति (स्तन्, c. l.)<BR>(?).<BR>II Trans.: स्तनयति (c. of स्तन्) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detonation
DETONATION: स्तननम् (?): v. Explosion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detour
DETOUR: भ्रमिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detort
DETORT: विकरोति (कृ, c. 8.): v. To pervert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detract
DETRACT:<BR>I To take away: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>defame, censure: q. v.:<BR>(1) अपवदति (वद्,<BR>c. l.),<BR>by d. ing merit:<BR>गुणापवादेन, Ki.;<BR>(2)<BR>असूयति (with dat.) (=to d. men.),<BR>d. s<BR>Viṣṇu:<BR>हरयेऽसूयति, S. k.;<BR>(3) अधि-क्षिपति, आ-,<BR>(=to asperse), while the King (Śiśupāla)<BR>was d. ing Kṛṣṇa:<BR>नृपतावधिक्षिपति शौरिम्, Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detraction
DETRACTION:<BR>(1) अपवादः;<BR>(2) असूया;<BR>(3)<BR>अधिक्षेपः<BR>or<BR>आक्षेपः v. To detract; calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detractor
DETRACTOR:<BR>(1) अपवादिन् (m.);<BR>(2) असूयकः;<BR>(3) अधि-क्षेपकः, आ-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detriment
DETRIMENT: हानिः: v. Loss, harm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detrimental
DETRIMENTAL: हानिकरः (री, रं) or better by<BR>subs.: v. Injurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detrition
DETRITION: क्षयः: v. To wear off, rub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detruncate
DETRUNCATE: v. To cut off, lop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

detruncation
DETRUNCATION:<BR>(1) अवच्छेदः;<BR>(2) कर्तनम्, अव-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deuce
DEUCE:<BR>I In dice: कटः, Mr.<BR>II A devil: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deuteronomy
DEUTERONOMY: *द्वितीयविधिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devastate
DEVASTATE:<BR>(1) उच्छिनत्ति, सम्-, (छिद्, c. 7.);<BR>(2) उत्सादयति (c. of सद्);<BR>(3) अव-मृद्राति, अधि-,<BR> आ-, (मृद्, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devastation
DEVASTATION:<BR>(1) उच्छेदः, सम्-,<BR>(2) उत्सादनम्;<BR>(3) अवमर्दः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

develop
DEVELOP:<BR>I To disclose, expound: q. v.:<BR>विवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.).<BR>II To rear, mature:<BR>q. v.<BR>III To grow, increase: q. v. D. ed.:<BR>of buds: सन्नद्ध: (द्धा, द्धं), Sa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

development
DEVELOPMENT:<BR>I Disclosure, exposition:<BR>विवृतिः।<BR>II Growth, increase: q. v.<BR>III<BR>Issue, ripeness: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deviate
DEVIATE (v.): अति-एति, व्येति-, (इ, c. 2.)<BR>(=transgress, pass by: q. v.),<BR>did not d. a<BR>line from the path:<BR>वर्त्मनः परं रेखामात्रमपि न<BR> व्यतीयुः, R. i. 17.;<BR>(2) चलति, वि-, (चल्, c. l.)<BR>(=to swerve: q. v.), (his)<BR>mind does not<BR>d. from virtue:<BR>न धर्माच्चलते बुद्धिः, Mah.;<BR>(3)<BR>च्यवते (च्यु, c. l.) (=to fall: q. v.), in<BR>the assembly d. d from the (right)<BR>course:<BR>पथ-<BR>शच्युतायां समितौ, Ki.: v. Also to wander,<BR>stray, err.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deviation
DEVIATION:<BR>(1) अतिक्रमः (=transgression);<BR>(2) विचलनम् (=swerving);<BR>(3) च्युतिः (=fall-<BR>-ing);<BR>(4) उन्मार्गगमनम् (=going by a wrong<BR>path);<BR>(5) भ्रमः (=error).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

device
DEVICE:<BR>I A contrivance:<BR>(1) उपायः;<BR>(2)<BR>छलम्: v. Stratagem.<BR>II Invention: q. v.:<BR>निर्माणम्।<BR>III An emblem: चिह्नम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devil
DEVIL: भूतः: v. Demon. Ph.: printer's d.:<BR>*बालमुद्रकः;<BR>to play the d. with:<BR>*उत्पीडयति<BR>(पीड्, c. 10.): v. To molest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devilish
DEVILISH:<BR>(1) पैशाचः (ची, चं);<BR>(2) राक्षसः<BR>(सी, सं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devilry
DEVILRY: पैशाचत्वम्; पैशाचाचारः, and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devious
DEVIOUS:<BR>I Lit.: वक्रः (क्रा, क्रं),<BR>although this<BR>route is d. to you:<BR>वक्रः पन्था यदपि भवतः, Me.:<BR>v. Crooked.<BR>II Erring, wandering: q. v.<BR>उद्भ्रान्तः (न्ता, न्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devise
DEVISE (v.):<BR>I To contrive: q. v.: कल्पयति<BR>(क्लऋप, c. 10.).<BR>II To bequeath: q. v.:<BR>*इच्छापत्रेण ददाति (दा, c. 3.) or sim ददाति<BR>when the meaning is clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devise
DEVISE (subs.): *इच्छापत्रेण स्थावरसम्पत्तिदानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devisee
DEVISEE: *इच्छापत्रेण यस्मै स्थावरसम्पत्तिर्दीयते;<BR> दानाधिकारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

deviser
DEVISER: कल्पयितृ (f. त्री): v. Inventor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devisor
DEVISOR: *इच्छापत्रेण स्थावरसम्पत्तिदातृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devoid of
DEVOID OF:<BR>(1) हीनः (ना, नं), वि-, परि-,<BR>d. of<BR>spirits:<BR>तेजोविहीनः (ना, नं), Ki;<BR>(2) रहितः<BR>(ता, तं), वि-,<BR>d. of wealth:<BR>धनैर्विरहितः (ता,),<BR>Mr.;<BR>(3) शून्यः (न्या, न्यं),<BR>d. of the power of<BR>combustion:<BR>दाहशक्तिशून्यः (न्या, न्यं), S. p. b.;<BR>(4) वर्जितः (ता, तं), वि-, परि-,<BR>d. of covetousness<BR>and anger:<BR>लोभक्रोधविवर्जितः (ता, तं), Mah.;<BR>(5) वीत-, विगत-, etc. in comp. (=gone: of<BR>what was once possessed), d. of care:<BR>वीतचिन्तः (न्ता, न्तं), Sa.;<BR>(6) often by a neg.<BR>comp.,<BR>d. of hands and feet:<BR>अपाणिपादः (दा, दं),<BR>S.;<BR>d. of flies:<BR>निर्मक्षिकः (का, कं), V. ;<BR>d. of<BR>clouds:<BR>व्यभ्रः (भ्रा, भ्रं), V. p. N. B.<BR>(1) to<BR>(4)<BR>are used as second member of a comp. or<BR>with ins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devolve
DEVOLVE (v. t.):<BR>I To roll on: पातयति (पत्,<BR>c. 6.).<BR>II To commit, entrust: q. v.:<BR>निक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.) (with loc.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devolve
DEVOLVE (v. i.): expr. by circumlo.,<BR>on the<BR>demise of a King the crown d. s on his eldest son:<BR>उपरते राज्ञि ज्येष्ठपुत्रो राज्यभाक्: v. Also to come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devote
DEVOTE:<BR>I To consecrate: उत्सृजति (सृज्, c. 6.),<BR>d. d animals:<BR>उत्सृष्टपशवः, Y.<BR>II To doom: q. v.<BR>III To give up:<BR>(1) योजयति, आ-, अभि-,<BR>(युज्, c. 10.) (=to apply), (you)<BR>have d. d.<BR>yourself to great penances:<BR>आयोजितस्तपसि महत्यात्मा,<BR>K.;<BR>(2) आ-वेशयति, नि-, अभिनि-, (c. of विश्)<BR>(=to put), of (those)<BR>who have d. d themselves<BR>to you:<BR>त्वय्यावेशितचित्तानाम्, R.;<BR>(3) expr. by<BR>आ-सक्तः (क्ता, क्तं), *प्र-, व्या-,<BR>the fools are d. d<BR>to them:<BR>आसक्तास्ताष्वमी मूढाः, Ki.;<BR>d. ed to<BR>gambling:<BR>द्यूतप्रसक्तः (क्ता, क्तं), Mr.; or<BR>(4)<BR>रक्तः (क्ता, क्तं), अनु-, (fondly),<BR>young men are d. d<BR>to young women:<BR>तरुणस्तावत्तरुणीरक्तः, J.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devotedly
DEVOTEDLY: एकाग्रचित्तेन: v. Earnestly, zea-<BR>-lously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devotedness
DEVOTEDNESS: v. Devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devotee
DEVOTEE:<BR>(1) तापसः (f. सी);<BR>(2) योगिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) धर्मनिरतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devotion
DEVOTION:<BR>I Consecration: उत्सर्गः।<BR>II<BR>Addiction:<BR>(1) आसक्तिः;<BR>(2) निरतिः, Ki.<BR>III<BR>Religious or respectful: भक्तिः,<BR>d. to your<BR>preceptor:<BR>गुरौ भक्तिः, R.<BR>IV A. gift: दानम।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devotional
DEVOTIONAL:<BR>I Devout:<BR>(1) धर्मपरायणः (f. णा);<BR>(2) धर्मनिष्ठः (ष्ठा, ष्ठं).<BR>II Relating to devo-<BR>-tion: expr. by धर्म- in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devour
DEVOUR: भक्षयति (भक्ष, c. 10.), will d. us all:<BR>भक्षयिष्यति नः सर्वान्, A. r., the world-d. ing time:<BR>कालो जगद्भक्षकः, J.: v. To eat, swallow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

devourer
