DON: भर्तृ (m.) (in addressing): v. Grandee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

donation
DONATION: दानम्: v. Gift, grant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

donative
DONATIVE: दानम्: Gift, present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

donjon
DONJON: गुप्तिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

donkey
DONKEY: खरः: v. Ass, male.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

donor
DONOR: दातृ (f. त्री): v. Giver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dooly
DOOLY: दोला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doom
DOOM (subs.):<BR>I Sentence: दण्डाज्ञा।<BR>II Lit.:<BR>परिणामः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doom
DOOM (v.):<BR>I To condemn: दण्डयति (दण्ड्, c.<BR>10.).<BR>II To destine: Ph.:<BR>only d. ed to dis-<BR>tress:<BR>केवलदुःखभाजनम्, K.: v. Fated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doomsday
DOOMSDAY: महाविचारदिनम्, and sim. comp.s (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doomsday-book
DOOMSDAY-BOOK: *ईंलण्डीयभूमिपत्रिका “विजय”-<BR>राजाज्ञया संगृहीता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

door
DOOR:<BR>(1) द्वारम् (lit. and fig.),<BR>near the d.:<BR>द्वारो-<BR>पान्ते, Me.;<BR>to open a d.:<BR>द्वारं विवृणोति, Ku.;<BR>shut the back d.:<BR>पिधेहि पक्षद्वारकम्, Mr. ii.;<BR>d. s<BR>of income broke down:<BR>आयद्वाराणि व्यशीर्यन्त, D.<BR>viii.;<BR>death's d.:<BR>मृत्युद्वारम्, H.;<BR>(2) द्वार् (f.)<BR>(rare, except in the loc.), who is at the d.:<BR>कोऽयं द्वारि तिष्ठति, Mu. ii.;<BR>(3) कपा(वा)ट (mn)<BR>(the leaf of a d.). Ph.:<BR>from d. to d.:<BR>गृहाद्-<BR>गृहम्, D.; (b)<BR>indoors:<BR>गेहे, U.; (c) out of d. s:<BR>बहिः; next d. to (i. e. bordering on): अनन्तरः<BR>(रा, रं);<BR>“the fault lies at my d.:<BR>*द्वारे मे<BR> वर्तते दोषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

door-keeper
DOOR-KEEPER:<BR>(1) द्वारपालः;<BR>(2) द्वारिन् (m.):<BR>(3) द्वाररक्षकः;<BR>(4) दौवारिकः, B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

door-post
DOOR-POST: द्वारस्तम्मः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

door-sill
DOOR-SILL:<BR>(1) द्वारपिण्डी;<BR>(2) देहलिः, -ली (f.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doorway
DOORWAY: द्वारम्: v. Door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dorian
DORIAN, DORIC: *डौरः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dormant
DORMANT:<BR>I Lit.: सुप्तः (प्ता, प्तं).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>v. Obsolete, hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dormitory
DORMITORY:<BR>(1) शय्यागृहम्;<BR>(2) शयनगृहम्; and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dormouse
DORMOUSE: *वृक्षमूषिकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dorsal
DORSAL:<BR>(1) पृष्ठ- in comp.,<BR>d. bone:<BR>पृष्ठवंशः;<BR>(2)<BR>पृष्ठ्यः (ष्ठ्या, ष्ठ्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dose
DOSE (subs.): expr. by circumlo.,<BR>should give<BR>this medicine in d. s of three rattis:<BR>रसमिमं रत्तिका-<BR>त्रयमितं दद्यात्, Bha.;<BR>should increase the d.<BR>everyday by one ratti:<BR>प्रतिदिनं तस्यैकैकां रत्तिकां<BR> वर्द्धयेत्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dose
DOSE (v.): i. e. to prepare or give d. s:<BR>expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dot
DOT (subs.): बिन्दुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dot
DOT (v.):<BR>I Lit.: बिन्दुना चिह्नयति (चिह्न्, c.<BR>10.).<BR>II To diversify: “d. ed with cottages”<BR>इतस्ततः कुटीरैः समलङ्कृतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dotage
DOTAGE: जराजीर्णेन्द्रियता: जरा (= decrepitude).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dotard
DOTARD: जराजीर्णेन्द्रियः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dote upon
DOTE UPON (v.): अत्यन्तानुरागवत् (f. ती) (with<BR>loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dotingly
DOTINGLY:<BR>I Fondly: अत्यन्तानुरागेण।<BR>II Foo-<BR>-lishly: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

double
DOUBLE (adj.):<BR>I Two-fold:<BR>(1) द्वि- in<BR>comp.;<BR>(2) द्विकः (का, कं).<BR>II As much<BR>again: द्विगुणः (णा, णं),<BR>d. pay:<BR>द्विगुणवेतनम्।<BR>III<BR>In pairs: द्वन्द्वीभूय।<BR>IV Deceitful, ambiguous;<BR>q. v.: perh. द्वि- in comp., having a d. meaning:<BR>द्व्यर्थः (र्था, र्थं), Va.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

double
DOUBLE (subs.):<BR>I Twice as much: द्विगुणम्।<BR>II A trick: q. v.<BR>III Companion: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

double
DOUBLE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: द्विगुणीकरोति।<BR>II To be<BR>d. of: द्विगुणः (णा, णं).<BR>III To double up:<BR>द्विभङ्गिं करोति (?). Ph.:<BR>to d. a cape:<BR>*प्रलम्बं लङ्घयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

double
DOUBLE (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.: द्विगुणीभवति।<BR>II To<BR>return: परावर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.).<BR>III To play<BR>false: छलनां करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

double-barrelled
DOUBLE-BARRELLED: *द्विनालः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

double-dealer
DOUBLE-DEALER, DOUBLE-DEALING: v. Deceit-<BR>-ful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

double-dealing
DOUBLE-DEALING (subs.): v. Deceit, artifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

double-entendre
DOUBLE-ENTENDRE: द्व्यर्थः (र्था, र्थं), Ve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

double-faced
DOUBLE-FACED: prob. द्विमुखः (खा, खं): v.<BR>Deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

double-headed
DOUBLE-HEADED: द्विशिरस् (mfn.) and sim.<BR>comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

double-lock
DOUBLE-LOCK (v.): *तालकद्वयेन पिदधाति (धा,<BR>c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

double-tongued
DOUBLE-TONGUED: द्विजिह्व (f. ह्वा) (lit. and<BR>fig.), Si. i. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doublet
DOUBLET:<BR>I A pair: q. v.: युग्मम्।<BR>II A<BR>vest: चोलः, -कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doubly
DOUBLY:<BR>(1) द्विः;<BR>(2) द्विगुणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doubt
DOUBT (v.):<BR>(1) संशेते (शी, c. 2.),<BR>was d. ingly<BR>received by the king:<BR>संशय्य नृपैः प्रपन्नः, Ki.;<BR>(2)<BR>संदिग्घे (दिह्, c. 1.),<BR>a man alone d. s in things<BR>to be done:<BR>एकः सन्दिग्घे कार्यवस्तुनि, Si.;<BR>(3)<BR>शङ्कते, आ-, वि-, (शङ्क, c. 1.) (= to apprehend),<BR>from whom (you)<BR>d. disgrace:<BR>यतोऽवधीरणां<BR> विशङ्कसे, Sa.;<BR>(4) न प्रत्येति (इ, c. 2.) (= not to<BR>believe: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doubt
DOUBT (subs.):<BR>(1) संशयः,<BR>without d.:<BR>असंशयम्,<BR>Sa.;<BR>I have only one d. about (his) form:<BR>रूपे मे<BR> संशयस्त्वेकः, Mah.;<BR>(2) सन्देहः, he is in d. even of<BR>our marriage: [आर्यस्य] परिणय एव सन्देहः, Sa.<BR>v.;<BR>(3) शङ्का, आशङ्का (apprehension),<BR>I will<BR>remove your d.:<BR>तवाशङ्कामपनेष्यामि, Sa. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doubter
DOUBTER:<BR>(1) संशयितृ (m.);<BR>(2) सन्देग्धृ (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doubtful
DOUBTFUL:<BR>(1) सन्दिग्धः (ग्धा, ग्धं), d. as (in<BR>this verse): सन्दिग्धं यथा, Kav.;<BR>(2) सांशयिकः (की,<BR> कं);<BR>(3) सन्देहयुक्तः (क्ता, क्तं);<BR>(4) संशयापन्नः<BR> न्ना, न्नं);<BR>(5) शङ्कनीय: (या, यं). To be d.: i. e.<BR>to have doubts: v. Doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doubtfully
DOUBTFULLY:<BR>(1) ससन्देहम्;<BR>(2) ससंशयम्;<BR>(3)<BR>सन्दिग्धम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doubtingly
DOUBTINGLY:<BR>(1) संशय्य;<BR>(2) सन्दिह्य;<BR>(3)<BR>साशङ्कम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doubtless
DOUBTLESS: निःसन्देहः (हा, हं): v. Undoubted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doubtlessly
DOUBTLESSLY: निःसन्देहम्: v. Undoubtedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

douceur
DOUCEUR: पारितोषिकम्: v. Present, gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dough
DOUGH: पिष्टगोधूमचूर्णपिण्डः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doughty
DOUGHTY: विक्रान्तः (न्ता, न्तं): v. Valiant,<BR>illustrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dove
DOVE:<BR>I Lit.: कपोतः।<BR>II Fig.: v. Darling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dove-cot
DOVE-COT:<BR>(1) कपोतपालिका;<BR>(2) विटङ्कः (rare),<BR>Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dove-tail
DOVE-TAIL (subs.): *कपोतपुच्छबन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dove-tail
DOVE-TAIL (v.): v. To unite; fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dowager
DOWAGER: विधवा (= widow: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dower
DOWER (subs.):<BR>I Any gift: दानम्।<BR>II<BR>Woman's: यौत(तु)कम्;<BR>mother's d.:<BR>मातुर्यौतकम्,<BR>M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dowered
DOWERED: यौत(तु)कवती, and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dowerless
DOWERLESS: यौतुकहीना (a d. woman); निर्धनः<BR>(ना, नं) (= poor).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

down
DOWN (subs.): i. e. soft hair: कोमलरोमन् (n.)<BR>(?).<BR>Eider-d.<BR>हंसतूलम् (?), D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

down
DOWN (subs.):<BR>I A bank: स्थलम्।<BR>II Low<BR>ground: निम्नं<BR>or<BR>निम्नप्रदेशः, ups and d. s:<BR>निम्नोन्नतानि, H.; on the road having ups and d. s:<BR>मार्गे नतोन्नतभूमिमागे, Sa.<BR>III Fig., d. fall: पातः,<BR>ups and d. s of men:<BR>पातोत्पाता मनुष्याणाम्, H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

down
DOWN (prep.):<BR>I Below: expr. by adv.<BR>II<BR>D. the same line: gen. not expr.:<BR>d. the<BR>stream:<BR>अनुस्रोतस्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

down
DOWN (adv.):<BR>(1) अधः,<BR>for which it does not go<BR>d.:<BR>येन नेयमियादधः, Go.;<BR>looking d.:<BR>अधोऽवलोक्य,<BR>Ana.;<BR>(2) नीचैः,<BR>goes up and d.:<BR>नीचैर्गच्छत्युपरि<BR> च, Me. Ph.:<BR>“d. with the palace”.:<BR>अधः<BR> पातय प्रासादम्;<BR>d. to the present time:<BR>अद्य यावत्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

down
DOWN (adj.): of trains, etc.: निम्नगामिन्, (f.<BR>नी) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

downcast
DOWNCAST:<BR>(1) अधोमुखः (खी, खं), and sim.<BR>comp. s,<BR>Karṇa d. from dejection:<BR>कर्णो दैन्याद-<BR>धोमुखः, Mah.;<BR>(2) विषण्ण (f. ण्णा) (= dejected)).<BR>Ph.:<BR>with d. eyes:<BR>अधोदृष्टि (mfn.), and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

downfall
DOWNFALL:<BR>(1) विनिपातः;<BR>(2) अवपातः;<BR>(3) पतनम्;<BR>(4) क्षयः: v. Ruin. destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

downhearted
DOWNHEARTED: दीनमनस् (mfn.), Mah.; and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

downhill
DOWNHILL (adj.): पातुकः (का, कं): v. Slop-<BR>-ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

downright
DOWNRIGHT (adj.):<BR>I Plain, artless: q. v.:<BR>स्पष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं),<BR>II Open, absolute. स्पष्टः<BR>(ष्टा, ष्टं),<BR>d. nonsense:<BR>स्पष्टनिरर्थकमाषितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

downright
DOWNRIGHT (adv.):<BR>I Lit.: नीचैः।<BR>II Plainly:<BR>q. v.: स्पष्टम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

downward
DOWNWARD (adj.):<BR>(1) अधोगामिन् (f. नी):<BR>(2)<BR>पातुकः (का, कं) (= sloping).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

downwards
DOWNWARDS (adv.):<BR>I Lit.: अधः: v. Down.<BR>II From a remote time: पूर्वेभ्यः (abl. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

downy
DOWNY:<BR>I Lit.: कोमललोममयः (यी, यं) (?).<BR>II Fig., soft, calm: कोमलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dowry
DOWRY: यौतुकम्: v. Dower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doxy
DOXY:<BR>I In good sense: दयिता।<BR>II In bad<BR>sense: बन्धकी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doze
DOZE: निद्रायते (nomi.), Mal.: v. To sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dozen
DOZEN: द्वादशन् (mfn.): v. Twelve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

doziness
DOZINESS: निद्राशीलता (?): v. Sleepiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dozing
DOZING, DOZY: निद्राशीलः (ला, लं) (?): v.<BR>Sleepy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drab
DRAB (adj.): पिङ्गलः (ला, लं): v. Brown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drab
DRAB (subs.):<BR>I A slut: बन्धकी।<BR>II A wool-<BR>-len cloth: *द्रावम्ः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drachm
DRACHM, DRACHMA: रूप्यमुद्राविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draff
DRAFF: उच्छिष्टम्: v. Refuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draft
DRAFT:<BR>I Draught: q. v.<BR>II A bill of<BR>exchange: *निष्कर्षपत्रम्।: v. Bill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drag
DRAG (subs.):<BR>I Of an Indian boat: गुणः।<BR>II A d. -net: आकर्षजालम्।<BR>III A hook:<BR>आकर्षणी।<BR>IV A carriage: क्षिप्रयानम् (?)<BR>V A<BR>harrow: q. v.<BR>VI A break: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drag
DRAG (v. t.):<BR>I To draw: q. v.: कर्वति, आ-,<BR>(कृष, c. 1.),<BR>to d. hounds:<BR>कौलेयकानाकर्षति,<BR>K.<BR>II To earn: q. v. Ph.: to d. on life:<BR>जीवनं वाहयति, (c. of वह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drag
DRAG (v. i.): i. e. to hang to the ground:<BR>लुठति (लुठ्, c. 6.), H. Ph.:<BR>the matter d. ed on<BR>for a year:<BR>*एकवर्षं चचालार्थः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draggle
DRAGGLE: v. To drag. D. -tailed: v. Un-<BR>-tidy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drag-net
DRAG-NET: आकर्षजालम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dragoman
DRAGOMAN: व्याख्यातृ (m.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dragon
DRAGON: *नागसिंहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dragoon
DRAGOON (subs.): अश्वारोहः (= horseman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dragoon
DRAGOON (v.):<BR>I Lit.: अश्वारोहैः वशीकरोति (कृ,<BR>c. 8.).<BR>II Fig., to harass: सम्पीडयति (पीड्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drain
DRAIN (subs.):<BR>(1) *मलप्रणाली (= sewer);<BR>(2)<BR>जलप्रणाली (= water-course).<BR>(3) जलनिर्गमः (for<BR>the exit of water);<BR>(4) भ्रमः (= 3), Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drain
DRAIN (v. t.):<BR>I To draw off water:<BR>to d. a<BR>marsh:<BR>अनूपप्रदेशस्य जलम् अपकर्षति (कृष्, c. 1.) or<BR>अपवाहयति (c. of वह्)<BR>or<BR>निर्गमयति (c. of गम्).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) क्षपयति (c. of क्षि): v. To<BR>exhaust.<BR>(2) रिक्तीकरोति। v. To empty.<BR>III<BR>To filter: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drainage
DRAINAGE: *जलनिर्गमप्रणाली, and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drake
DRAKE: कादम्बः: v. Duck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dram
DRAM:<BR>I Lit.: मानविशेषः<BR>II Drinking: पानम्।<BR>D. -drinker:<BR>मद्यपः: v. Drunkard. D. -shop:<BR>शौण्डिकालयः, शुण्डापानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drama
DRAMA:<BR>I A play: नाटकम्।<BR>II<BR>The d.:<BR>दृश्य-<BR>काव्यं<BR>or<BR>दृश्यं काव्यम्, Sah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dramatic
DRAMATIC, -AL: expr. by comp., d. genius:<BR>*दृश्यकाव्यशक्तिः;<BR>d. composition<BR>दृश्यकाव्यं or<BR>प्रबन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dramatically
DRAMATICALLY:<BR>(1) नाट्येन (by representa-<BR>-tion);<BR>(2) दृश्यकाव्यानुसारेण (according to<BR>drama).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dramatist
DRAMATIST:<BR>(1) कविः (= poet: q. v.);<BR>(2) नाटक-<BR>प्रणेतृ (m.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dramatize
DRAMATIZE: नाटकयति (nomi.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drape
DRAPE: वस्त्रैर्भूषयति, वि-, (भूष्, c. 10.)<BR>or<BR>मण्डयति<BR>(मण्ड्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draper
DRAPER: लोमशवस्त्रविक्रेतृ (m.)<BR>or<BR>विक्रयिन् (m.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drapery
DRAPERY:<BR>I Cloth: लोमशवस्त्रम् (?).<BR>II<BR>D.<BR>selling:<BR>लोमशवस्त्रविक्रयः (?).<BR>III For statues,<BR>etc.: परिच्छदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draught
DRAUGHT:<BR>I Drawing: आकर्षः, -णम्।<BR>II Load<BR>carrying: धुर्वहनम्।<BR>D. -cattle:<BR>धुर्यः<BR>or<BR>धुर्वहः।<BR>III Drinking: q. v.: पानम्।<BR>IV Delinea-<BR>-tion: लेखनम्।<BR>V That which is drawn: expr.<BR>by circumlo.,<BR>“which brought him a great<BR>d.”:<BR>*येन बह्वाकृष्टमासीत्।<BR>VI A potion: q. v.<BR>VII A detachment: q. v.<BR>VIII A sketch:<BR>q. v.<BR>IX A draft: *निष्कर्षपत्रम्।<BR>X Current<BR>of air ओघः: v. Current.<BR>XI A drain:<BR>मलनिर्गमः।<BR>XII Of ships: Ph.:<BR>“a ship of 12ft.<BR>d.”<BR>*अष्टहस्तजलगामिपोतः।<BR>XIII In pl., a game:<BR>अष्टापदक्रीडा (??),<BR>d, -board:<BR>अष्टापदम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draughtsman
DRAUGHTSMAN:<BR>I A drawer:<BR>(1) लेखकः;<BR>(2)<BR>चित्रकरः (= painter).<BR>II A tippler: मद्यपः।<BR>III For playing draughts: शारिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draw
DRAW (v. t.):<BR>I To pull: कर्षति, आ-, (कृष्, c.<BR>1.),<BR>d. s a snake out of the basket:<BR>भुजङ्गमाकर्षति<BR> पेटिकायाः, V. t.;<BR>d. ing his sword:<BR>खङ्गमाकृष्य,<BR>Ve. iii.;<BR>d. n up to the ear:<BR>आकर्णकृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं),<BR>R. ix. 57.;<BR>d. ing the sheet rolled up under his<BR>arm-pit:<BR>कक्षतललुण्ठीकृतं पटमाकृष्य, Mr. ii.;<BR>to d.<BR>a curtain:<BR>जवनिकाम् आकर्षति (?) (there were<BR>no sliding curtains among the Hindus).<BR>Fig.;<BR>d. n. by fame:<BR>यशसाकृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं): v.<BR>To allure.<BR>II To extract: q. v.: निष्कर्षति,<BR>intend to d. money from Kuvera:<BR>निष्क्रष्टुमर्थं चकमे<BR> कुवेरात्, R. v. 26.<BR>III To lift: q. v.: उदञ्चयति<BR>(अञ्च्, c. 10.), d. ing water to quench thirst:<BR>पिपासां प्रतिकर्तुमुदकमुदञ्चयन्, D.<BR>IV To delineate:<BR>लिखति, अभि-, आ-, (लिख्, c. 6.),<BR>the person d. n<BR>on the canvas:<BR>पटे लिखितं पुरुषम्, D. iv. V. To<BR>write: लिखति, अभि-।<BR>VI To deduce: q. v.<BR>VII To require a depth of: Ph.:<BR>it d. s six<BR>feet of water:<BR>*चतुर्हस्तजले गच्छति।<BR>VIII To<BR>gain: q. v.: Misc:<BR>to d. the breast:<BR>स्तनम्<BR> आकर्षति (?)<BR>or<BR>पिबति, B. p.; to d. an animal:<BR>पशोः क्लोमादीन्यपोहति, (after D.); serpents d. air:<BR>सर्पाः पिबन्ति पवनम्, P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draw
DRAW (v. i.):<BR>I To pull: आकर्षति।<BR>II To be [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">Page220</a>]<BR>d. n: आकृष्यते (pass. of कृष्).<BR>III To con-<BR>-tract: q. v.<BR>IV To sketch: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draw away
DRAW AWAY: अपकर्षति, वि-,<BR>Chandragupta has<BR>been d. n a. from Chāṇakya:<BR>अपकृष्टश्चाणक्याच्चन्द्रगुप्तः,<BR>Mu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draw back
DRAW BACK:<BR>I Trans.: प्रति-कर्षति, प्रत्या-।<BR>II<BR>Intrans: परावर्तते, प्रत्या-, प्रतिनि-, (वृत्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draw in
DRAW IN:<BR>I To bring in: कर्षति, आ-, वि-,<BR>d. s<BR>in fortune:<BR>श्रियं विकर्षति, Ki.<BR>II To entice:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draw near or nigh
DRAW NEAR or NIGH:<BR>(1) सन्निकर्षति, D. i.;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रत्यासीदति (सद्, c. 1.),<BR>time for going home d.<BR>s n.:<BR>प्रत्यासीदति गृहगमनकालः, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draw off
DRAW OFF:<BR>I Lit.: अप-कर्षति, आ-, अपा-,<BR>d. ing<BR>off the eyes from the king:<BR>अवनिपालमुखादाकृष्य<BR> चक्षुः, K.<BR>II To withdraw, retire: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draw on
DRAW ON:<BR>I To draw in: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>draw near: q. v.<BR>III<BR>To make a draft to d.<BR>on the Bank of Bengal:<BR>*वङ्गधनागारात् निष्कर्षति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draw out
DRAW OUT:<BR>I To draw: v. Draw (I).<BR>II<BR>To extract: v. Draw (II).<BR>III To stretch,<BR>extend: q. v.<BR>IV To prolong: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draw over
DRAW OVER: prob. समाकर्षति: v. To bring<BR>over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draw together
DRAW TOGETHER: समाकर्षति: v. To bring<BR>together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

draw up
DRAW UP:<BR>I Lit.: उत्कर्षति, R.<BR>II To com-<BR>-pose: लिखति (लिख्, c. 6.).<BR>III To arrange<BR>troops:<BR>(1) विन्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.);<BR>(2)<BR>विरचयति (रच्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drawback
DRAWBACK:<BR>(1) हानिः (= loss);<BR>(2) प्रत्यूहः<BR>(obstacle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drawbridge
DRAWBRIDGE: *आकर्षसेतुः; यन्त्रोपेतसंक्रमः, Ram.<BR>To close (it): हरति (हृ, c. 1.), Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drawee
DRAWEE: of a cheque: *आदिष्टनिष्कर्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drawer
DRAWER:<BR>I Lit.: कर्षकः, आ-,।<BR>II A painter:<BR>लेखकः।<BR>III Of a cheque: *निष्कर्षकः।<BR>IV<BR>A sliding box: *निष्कर्षणी।<BR>V In pl., a<BR>garment: जङ्घावारः। Ph.:<BR>a chest of d. s:<BR>*निष्कर्ष-<BR>पेटिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drawing
DRAWING (subs.):<BR>I The act: आकर्षः, -णम्।<BR>II Delineation: चित्रकर्मन् (n.).<BR>III A<BR>picture: q. v.:<BR>whose d. is it:<BR>केनेदं लिखितम्।<BR>IV In lotteries: निःसारणम्, (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drawing-master
DRAWING-MASTER: चित्रशिक्षकः (?), and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drawing-room
DRAWING-ROOM: सभाजनकोष्ठः (?). Ph.:<BR>to hold<BR>a d.<BR>*सभाजनकोष्ठं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drawl
DRAWL (v.): मन्दं मन्दम् उदीरयति (ईर्, c. 10.):<BR>v. To utter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dray
DRAY, DRAY-DART: शकटः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drayman
DRAYMAN: शकटवाहकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dread
DREAD (subs.): त्रासः, वि-,<BR>d. inspiring:<BR>त्रासजननः<BR>(नी, नं), Ki.: v. Fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dread
DREAD (adj.): v. Dreadful, terrible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dread
DREAD (v.): त्रस्यति, वि-, (त्रस्, c. 4.) (with<BR>abl.): v. To Fear. Ph.: d. ing me:<BR>मत्त्रासात्, Ve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dreaded
DREADED (adj.): घोरः (रा, रं): v. Formid-<BR>-able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dreadful
DREADFUL:<BR>(1) भीषण (f. णा);<BR>(2) दारुण, नि-,<BR>(f. णा);<BR>(3) घोरः (रा, रं);<BR>(4) त्रासावहः<BR>(हा, हं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dreadfully
DREADFULLY:<BR>(1) धोरम्;<BR>(2) दारुणम्;<BR>(3) भीषणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dreadfulness
DREADFULNESS:<BR>(1) भीषणत्वम्;<BR>(2) दारुणत्वम्;<BR>(3)<BR>घोरता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dreadless
DREADLESS: निर्भयः (या, यं): v. Fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dream
DREAM (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) स्वप्नः,<BR>to have a<BR>bad d.:<BR>दुःस्वप्नं पश्यति, D. viii.;<BR>(2) सुप्तिः or<BR>सुप्तिका,<BR>pleasant d.:<BR>सुखसुप्तिका, Sa. iv. Ph.:<BR>to speak in d.:<BR>उत्स्वग्नायते (nomi.), U.<BR>II<BR>Fig. Ph.:<BR>pleasures are but d. s:<BR>कामाः स्वप्नोपमाः,<BR>Ki. xi. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dream
DREAM (v.): Lit.:<BR>(1) स्वप्ने पश्यति (दृश्, c. 1.)<BR>(= to d. of something.),<BR>d. t that the moon<BR>had entered into the mouth of Vilāsavatī:<BR>स्वप्ने<BR> विलासवत्या आनने शशिनं प्रविशन्तमपश्यत्, K.;<BR>(2)<BR>स्वप्नं पश्यति (= to have a d.).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>ध्यायति (ध्यै, c. 1.) (= to meditate). To d.<BR>away or out: of time: मिथ्याचिन्तया कालं क्षिपति,<BR>(क्षिप्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dreamer
DREAMER:<BR>I Lit.: स्वप्नदर्शिन् (f. नी)<BR>II Fig.:<BR>उन्मत्तः (त्ता, त्तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dreamless
DREAMLESS:<BR>(1) वीतस्वप्नः (प्ना, प्नं);<BR>(2) स्वप्न-<BR>शून्यः (न्या, न्यं), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dreamy
DREAMY i. e. dreamlike: स्वप्नोपमः (मा, मं), and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drear
DREAR: v. Dreary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drearily
DREARILY:<BR>(1) घोरम्;<BR>(2) निरानन्दम् (= cheer-<BR>-lessly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dreariness
DREARINESS: घोरता: v. Desolation, cheer-<BR>-lessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dreary
DREARY: घोरः (रा, रं): v. Desolate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dredge
DREDGE: आकर्षणी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dregs
DREGS:<BR>I Lit.: मलम्।<BR>II Fig.: उच्छिष्टम्: v.<BR>Refuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drench
DRENCH (subs.): पानम्: v. Drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drench
DRENCH (v.):<BR>I To make to drink: पाययति<BR>(c. of पा).<BR>II To moisten, wet: q. v.:<BR>क्लेदयति (c. of क्लिद्). Ph.:<BR>although I was d.<BR>ed with sweat:<BR>स्वेदसलिलस्नातापि, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dress
DRESS (subs.): वेषः<BR>or<BR>वेशः,<BR>take away the hunt-<BR>ing d.:<BR>मृगयावेशमपनयन्तु, Sa.;<BR>(2) नेपथ्यम् (rare),<BR>with marriage d.:<BR>वैवाहिकेन नेपथ्येन, Ma. vi.: v.<BR>Clothes, garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dress
DRESS (v. t.):<BR>I To clothe: q. v.:<BR>(1) वेषयति<BR>(c. of विष्) (= to d. another),<BR>d. ing Sāmba<BR>with female d.:<BR>साम्बं स्त्रीवेषैर्वेषयित्वा, B. p.;<BR>(2)<BR>वेषं विदधाति (धा, c. 3.) M. n.;<BR>or<BR>विरचयति (रच्,<BR>c. 10.),<BR>d. ed:<BR>विरचितवेषः, R. v. 76.;<BR>(3) वेषं<BR> विभर्ति (भृ, c. 3.), (= to d. one's self), R. Ph.:<BR>d. ed as Vāsavadattā:<BR>वासवदत्तावेशधारिणी, Ra.<BR>iii.<BR>II Of the hair:<BR>(1) रचयति, वि-,<BR>d. the<BR>hair:<BR>केशरचनां कुर्वन्त, Ri. iv. 15.;<BR>(2) कल्पयति,<BR> आ-, (कॢप्, c. 10.), here (they are)<BR>d. ing the<BR>mane of horses:<BR>इतो इतोऽश्वानां केशकल्पना क्रियते,<BR>Mr. iv.;<BR>(3) संस्करोति (कृ, c. 8.).<BR>III Of food,<BR>etc.; संस्करोति, I also know how to d. food:<BR>अन्नसंस्कारमपि जानामि, Mah.<BR>IV Of wounds:<BR>शोधयति (c. of शुध्) Bha.: v. To bind up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dresser
DRESSER:<BR>I One who dresses: प्रसाधक (f.<BR>धिका).<BR>II A table.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dressing
DRESSING (subs.):<BR>I Dress: q. v.<BR>II For a<BR>wound: लेपः, प्र-, वि-,।<BR>III Of food: संस्कारः<BR>(?).<BR>IV Belabouring: v. To belabour,<BR>thrash. Comp.s. (a)<BR>d. -gown<BR>*प्राक्प्रसाधनवेषः;<BR>(b)<BR>d.- room<BR>प्रसाधनकोष्ठः, (?); (c) d. table:<BR>*प्रसाधनमेजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dribble
DRIBBLE: क्षरति (क्षर्, c. 1.): v. To trickle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dribblet
DRIBBLET: कणः,<BR>in d.s.:<BR>कणशः: v. Drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drift
DRIFT (subs.):<BR>I That which is driven:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रवाहः;<BR>(2) राशिः (= heap: q. v.) Ph.: under<BR>the d. of = impelled by: v. To impel.<BR>II<BR>Course: q. v.<BR>III Purport: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>भावः;<BR>(2) तात्पर्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drift
DRIFT (v. t.): नुदति, (नुद्, c. 6.): v. To drive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drift
DRIFT (v. i.): नुद्यते (pass. of नुद्); उह्यते (pass.<BR>of वह्), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drill
DRILL (subs.):<BR>I For boring: वेधनी: v.<BR>Gimlet.<BR>II Of soldiers: सैन्यव्यायामः, Ka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drill
DRILL (v. t.):<BR>I To bore: q. v.: विध्यति (व्यध्,<BR>c. 4.).<BR>II To train and exercise^1 troops:<BR>Ph.:<BR>should d. the soldiers every d.:<BR>अन्वहं सैन्य-<BR>व्यायामं कारयेत् (c. of कृ), Ka. xvi. 18.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drilling
DRILLING (subs.): स्थूलकार्पासपटविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drink
DRINK (v.): पिबति (पा, c. 1.),<BR>while they were d.<BR>ing there:<BR>पिबतां तत्र वै तेषाम्, V. p.;<BR>d. ing<BR>maireya liquor:<BR>मैरेयं मधु पीत्वा, B. p. Ph.: he<BR>d. s (= a drunkard: q. v.) स पानं करोति;<BR>we d.<BR>to your health:<BR>*तव स्वास्थ्याय पिबामः।, D. off or<BR>up:<BR>(1) नि-पबति;<BR>(2) उत्-चुलुम्पति, Vi. v. D.<BR>in: v. To imbibe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drink
DRINK (subs.):<BR>(1) पानीयम्;<BR>(2) पेयम्;<BR>(3)<BR>पानम्,<BR>bring me d. quick:<BR>पानमाहर मे क्षिप्रम्,<BR>Mah.<BR>D. -money:<BR>सुरामूल्यम्, Sa. vi.<BR>To take<BR>to d.<BR>आसवम् आसेवते, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drinkable
DRINKABLE:<BR>(1) पेयः (या, यं);<BR>(1) पानीयः<BR>(या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drinker
DRINKER: यः (या, यत्) पानं करोति: v. Drunkard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drinking
DRINKING: पानम्,<BR>excessive d.:<BR>अतिपानम्, Ki.;<BR>great d. began:<BR>प्रावर्तत महापानम्, Mah.<BR>D.<BR>vessel:<BR>पानपात्रम् and sim. comp.s. D. assembly:<BR>पानगोष्ठी, D.<BR>D. -place<BR>प्रपा, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drip
DRIP (subs.):<BR>I Dropping: पातः।<BR>II Eaves:<BR>स्यन्दनिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drip
DRIP (v. t.): गालयति (c. of गल्),<BR>I will d. this<BR>cloth on her:<BR>एतच्चीवरमस्या उपरि गालयिष्यामि, Mr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drip
DRIP (v. i.):<BR>(1) क्षरति (क्षर्, c. 1.):<BR>(2) गलति<BR>(गल्, c. 1.); v. To ooze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dripping
DRIPPING (subs.): रसः,<BR>d. -pan:<BR>*रसधारिणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drive
DRIVE (v. t.):<BR>I To impel:<BR>(1) प्रेरयति (ईर्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">Page222</a>]<BR>c. 10.),<BR>d. n by contrary wind:<BR>प्रतिवातप्रेरितः (ता,<BR> तं), D. vi.;<BR>d. the horses fast towards the N.<BR>E.:<BR>ऐशानीं दिशं प्रति प्रेरयाश्वानाशुगमनाय, V. i.;<BR>(2) नूदति<BR>or<BR>नोदयति (नुद्, c. 6. and 10.),<BR>d. n<BR>by fate:<BR>नियत्या नोदिताश्वः, Si. xx. 2.;<BR>d. n by the<BR>charioteer:<BR>सारथिसम्प्रणुन्नः, Ku. xvii. 10.;<BR>(3)<BR>चोदयति, प्र-, सं-, (चुद्, c. 10.),<BR>drove the horses on<BR>level ground:<BR>समे देशे हयान् प्राचोदयत्, Mah.;<BR>(4) वाहयति (c. of वह्),<BR>don't d. the car:<BR>मा तावत्<BR> प्रवहणं वाहय, Mr. vi.;<BR>(5) चालयति, परि-, (c. of<BR>चल्) (= cause to move), in d. ing chariots:<BR>रथस्य परिचालने, Nil. Ph.:<BR>I will d. you to your<BR>house:<BR>रथेन त्वां गृहं नयामि<BR>or<BR>प्रापयामि;<BR>to d.<BR>a nail:<BR>कीलं प्रवेशयति (c. of विश्).<BR>II To hunt:<BR>q. v.<BR>III To follow, carry on: q. v.<BR>IV<BR>To force: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drive
DRIVE (v. i.):<BR>I To be impelled: expr. by<BR>the pass. of verbs given under drive (v. t.)<BR>(I.)<BR>II To rush: q. v.: निष्पतति (पत्, c. 1.).<BR>III To go by a carriage: रथेन गच्छति,<BR> चलति: v. To go, move.<BR>IV To d. at:<BR>अभिसन्दधाति (घा, c. 3.): v. To aim, strive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drive away
DRIVE AWAY:<BR>(1) निर्-अस्यति, अप-, (अस्, c. 4.)<BR>(= cast away);<BR>(2) निर्-सारयति, अप-, (c. of<BR>सृ);<BR>(3) निर्-धूनोति, अव-, वि-, (धू, c. 5.)<BR>(= shake off).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drive off
DRIVE OFF: निःसारयति: v. Drive away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drive out
DRIVE OUT:<BR>(1) निर्वासयति (c. of वस): v. To<BR>banish;<BR>(2) निःसारयति (c. of सृ),<BR>drove the<BR>son out of the country:<BR>देशान्निःसारयामास सुतम्,<BR>B.p.;<BR>(3) निरस्यति (अस्, c. 4.): v. To dispel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drive
DRIVE (subs.):<BR>I The exercise: expr. by<BR>verb:<BR>gone out to take a d.:<BR>वायुसेवनार्थं रथेन-<BR>निर्गतः।<BR>II A place for d.: रथ्या (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drivel
DRIVEL (subs.):<BR>I Slaver: लाला।<BR>II Non-<BR>-sense: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drivel
DRIVEL (v.):<BR>I To slaver: लालायते (nomi.).<BR>II To dote:<BR>d. ing:<BR>लालायितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

driveller
DRIVELLER:<BR>I Lit.: लालास्रवः।<BR>II Fig.: v.<BR>Idiot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

driver
DRIVER:<BR>(1) वाहकः,<BR>d. of a carriage:<BR>प्रवहणवाहकः,<BR>Mr.;<BR>(2) यन्तृ (m.) (= moderator: of<BR>animals),<BR>elephant -d.:<BR>यन्ता गजस्य, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drizzle
DRIZZLE:<BR>when it was d. ing:<BR>मन्दं मन्दं प्रवर्षति<BR> पर्जन्ये, P.; v. To rain gently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drizzly
DRIZZLY: d. weather: i. e. raining: expr.<BR>by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

droll
DROLL (adj.): हास-<BR>or<BR>हास्यकरः (री, रं) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

droll
DROLL (subs.):<BR>(1) वैहासिकः;<BR>(2) मण्डः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drollery
DROLLERY: परिहासः: v. Fun, humour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dromedary
DROMEDARY: एकककुदुष्ट्रः; आरविकोष्ट्रः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drone
DRONE (v.):<BR>I To idle, loiter: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>hum: हुङ्करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drone
DRONE (subs.):<BR>I A non-working bee:<BR>मधुकरः।<BR>II An idler: q. v.<BR>III A noise: डुङ्कुतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dronish
DRONISH: अलसः (सा, सं): v. Idle, lazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

droop
DROOP (v.):<BR>I To hang down: q. v.:<BR>अवनमति (नम्, c. 1.),<BR>d. ing of lotus:<BR>पङ्कजावनतिः,<BR>M. n.<BR>II To fade, decline: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>सीदति, अव-, वि-, (सद्, c. 1.),<BR>my limbs are d.<BR>ing:<BR>सीदन्ति मम गात्राणि, G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

droopingly
DROOPINGLY: i. e. dejectedly: विषण्णः (ण्णा, ण्णं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drop
DROP (subs.):<BR>I A liquid globule:<BR>(1)<BR>बिन्दुः,<BR>two or three d. s of water:<BR>द्वित्राः पयोबिन्दवः,<BR>J.;<BR>(2) पृषत् (n.)<BR>or<BR>पृषतः (rare).<BR>II The<BR>smallest portion of a fluid;<BR>(1) कणः;<BR>(2)<BR>शीकरः,<BR>the breast coverd with d. s of blood:<BR>शोणित-<BR>शीकरस्थगितभूजान्तरः, Ki.<BR>III An ear-ring:<BR>q.v.: कुण्डलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drop
DROP (v. t.):<BR>I To let fall in d. s:<BR>(1) क्षरति<BR>(क्षर्, c. 1.),<BR>d. ping the rutting juice:<BR>मदं<BR> क्षरन्तः, Ki.;<BR>(2) by subs., nectar-d. ping:<BR>अमृतबिन्दुनिःस्यन्दिन् (f. नी), K.<BR>II To let fall:<BR>पातयति, नि-, अव-, (c. of पत्),<BR>to d. on Vairo-<BR>dhaka:<BR>वैरोधकस्योपरि निपातनाय, Mu.<BR>III To<BR>leave off: q. v.: संहरति, उप-, (हृ, c. 1.), d. it:<BR>संह्नियतामियम्, K.<BR>IV To communicate: q. v.<BR>V To send: q. v. Ph.:<BR>“d. ped” deer:<BR>बिन्दु-<BR>भिर्युक्तो मृगः, A. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drop
DROP (v. i.):<BR>I To fall in d. s: expr. by<BR>subs,<BR>by the d. ping of water:<BR>जलबिन्दुनिपातेन, H.<BR>II To fall: पतति, नि-, (पत्, c. 1.),<BR>Nakula<BR>has d.’d down on the ground:<BR>नकुलः पतितो मुवि,<BR>Mah.<BR>III Fig.: to come out: q. v.:<BR>निर् -एति (इ, c. 2.).<BR>IV To cease: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drop-scene
DROP-SCENE: *उपसंहारजवनिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dropsical
DROPSICAL: वातश्वयथुपीडितः (ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dropsy
DROPSY: वातश्वयथुः (?); उदरी (= ascites).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dross
DROSS:<BR>I Of metals: मण्ड (mn.).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>उच्छिष्टम्: v. Refuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drossy
DROSSY: समलः (ला, लं) (?): v. Impure,<BR>worthless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drought
DROUGHT:<BR>I Aridity:<BR>(1) अनावृष्टिः;<BR>(2)<BR>अवग्रहः।<BR>II Thirst: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

droughty
DROUGHTY: शुष्कः (ष्का, ष्कं): v. Dry, parched,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drove
DROVE: यूथम्: v. Herd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drover
DROVER: पशुपालः: v. Herdsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drown
DROWN (v. t.):<BR>I To deluge: q. v.: प्लावयति<BR>(c. of प्लु).<BR>II To kill by immersion:<BR>(1)<BR>जले निमज्जयति, -ते (c. of मस्ज्) (= to plunge:<BR>when the sense is clear),<BR>will d. you soon like<BR>a vessel of stone:<BR>पाषाणनौरिव निमज्जयते पुरा त्वाम्,<BR>Ku. xvii. 15.;<BR>(2) जले मज्जयित्वा व्यापादयति<BR>(c. of पद्): v. To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drowned
DROWNED, TO BE:<BR>I To perish in water:<BR>(1) निमज्जति (मस्ज्, c. 1.) (when the sense is<BR>clear),<BR>I don't know whether Ratnodbhava was<BR>d. there or reached the coast.:<BR>रत्नोद्भवस्तत्र निमग्नो वा<BR> तीरमगमद्वा न जानामि, D.;<BR>(2) by circumlo.<BR>II<BR>Fig.: निमज्जति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drowsily
DROWSILY:<BR>(1) निद्रालसः (सा, सं): v. Sleepily;<BR>(2) आलस्येन; v. Slothfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drowsiness
DROWSINESS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) निद्रा (= sleep),<BR>overcome with d.:<BR>निद्रयाभिभूतः;<BR>(2) सुषुप्सा: v.<BR>Sleepiness.<BR>II Slothfulness: q. v.: आलस्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drowsy
DROWSY:<BR>I Sleepy: q. v.: निद्रालु (mn.).<BR>II<BR>Soporific: निद्रादः (दा, दं) (?).<BR>III Dull,<BR>stupid: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drub
DRUB (v.): लगुडेन ताडयति (तड्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>beat, cudgel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drub
DRUB (subs.):<BR>(1) यष्ट्यघातः:<BR>(2) लगुडप्रहारः;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drudge
DRUDGE (subs.): निकृष्टकर्मकरः (?), and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drudge
DRUDGE (v.): निकृष्टकर्मसु आत्मानम् आयासयति (c.<BR>of यस्) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drudgery
DRUDGERY: निकृष्टकर्माणि (?), and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drug
DRUG (subs.):<BR>(1) औषधम् (= medicine: q. v.);<BR>(2) औषधिः (= plants used in their compo-<BR>-sition).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drug
DRUG (v.):<BR>I Intrans: औषधं ददाति।<BR>II<BR>Trans: मिश्रयति (पिश्र्, c. 1.): v. To mix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drugget
DRUGGET: स्थूलप्रावारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

druggist
DRUGGIST:<BR>(1) औषधविक्रेतृ (m.) (?);<BR>(2) औषधीय-<BR>द्रव्यविक्रेतृ, (m.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

druid
DRUID: *द्रुतः।<BR>D. -ism:<BR>*द्रुतत्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drum
DRUM (subs.):<BR>(1) मृदङ्गः;<BR>(2) पटहः;<BR>(3)<BR>दुन्दुभिः;<BR>(4) डिण्डिमः (a small d.), beat the d.:<BR>आहत डिण्डिमम्, Mr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drum
DRUM (v.):<BR>I Lit.: मृदङ्गं नादयति (c. of नद्),<BR>ताडयति (तड्, c. 10.), etc.<BR>II To throb: कम्पते<BR>(कम्प्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drum out
DRUM OUT: सपटहताडं निर्वासयति (c. of वस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drummer
DRUMMER:<BR>(1) मार्दङ्गिकः;<BR>(2) पटहताडकः, and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drumstick
DRUMSTICK: दण्डः (= stick).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drunk
DRUNK:<BR>(1) मत्तः (त्ता, त्तं),<BR>half d.:<BR>मध्येन मदेन<BR> मत्तः, Ni.; in the fourth stage (a man)<BR>d. is<BR>worse than dead:<BR>चतुर्थे तु मदे मूढो मृतादप्यपरो मृतः,<BR>Ni.;<BR>(2) मदोन्मत्तः (त्ता, त्तं);<BR>(3) क्षीवः (वा,<BR> वं), परि-, d. with the blood of Duḥśāsana:<BR>क्षीवो दुःशासनासृजा, Ve. Ph.:<BR>I got d.:<BR>मदेनास्पृश्ये;<BR>being d.:<BR>उपोढमदः, D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drunkard
DRUNKARD:<BR>(1) सुरापः;<BR>(2) मद्यपः;<BR>(3) पानपः,<BR>Mah.;<BR>(4) पानशौण्डः, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drunken
DRUNKEN: मत्तः (त्ता, त्तं),<BR>the d. fell:<BR>मत्ताः परि-<BR>पतन्ति स्म, Mah.: v. Drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

drunkenness
DRUNKENNESS:<BR>(1) मत्तता;<BR>(2) मदोन्मत्तता;<BR>(3)<BR>भदः;<BR>(4) क्षैव्यं<BR>or<BR>क्षीवता (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dry
DRY (adj.):<BR>(1) शुष्कः (ष्का, ष्कं) (in all the<BR>senses of the English word),<BR>a heap of d.<BR>leaves:<BR>शुष्कपत्रसञ्चयः, Mr.; when it becomes d.:<BR>अस्मिन् शुष्के, V.;<BR>d. grinding:<BR>शुष्कपेषः, B.;<BR>d.<BR>altercation:<BR>शुष्कविग्रहः, B. p.;<BR>(2) परि-शुष्कः,<BR> सम्-, उत्-, वि-, (ष्का, ष्कं). Ph.:<BR>d. land:<BR>स्थलम्;<BR>d. measure:<BR>*शुष्कमानम्;<BR>d. wine:<BR>*शुष्कासवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dry
DRY (v. t.):<BR>(1) शुष्कं (f. ष्कां) करोति, where shall<BR>I spread and d. (this cloth): कुत्र प्रसार्य शुष्कं<BR> करिष्यामि, Mr. viii.:<BR>(2) शोषयति (c. of शुष्),<BR>should d. the body with penances:<BR>तपसा शरीरं<BR> शोषयेत्, V.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dry
DRY (v. i.): शोषमेति (इ, c. 2.), याति (या, c. 2.).<BR>व्रजति (व्रज्, c. 1.), गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.),<BR>and the<BR>ponds dried:<BR>ययुः शोषं सरांसि च, V.p.: v.<BR>To dry up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dry up
DRY UP (v. i.): शुष्यति (शुष्, c. 4.),<BR>that branch<BR>dries up:<BR>सा शाखा शुष्यति, S.c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dry up
DRY UP (v. t.): शोषयति, वि-, परि-, उत्-, सं-, (c.<BR>of शुष्),<BR>is like d. ing up the ocean:<BR>समुद्रस्येव<BR> शोषणम्, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dryad
DRYAD: वनदेवता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dry-eyed
DRY-EYED: prob. शुष्कनेत्रः (त्रा, त्रं): v. Tear-<BR>-less.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dryness
DRYNESS: शुष्कता, परि-, वि-, सं-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dry-nurse
DRY-NURSE: अस्तन्यपायिनी धात्री।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dry-point
DRY-POINT: सूचिविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dry-shod
DRY-SHOD: शुष्कपादः (दा, दं), and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dual
DUAL: but why (you have used) the d. number:<BR>द्विवचनन्तु कथम्, U. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

duality
DUALITY:<BR>(1) द्वित्वम्;<BR>(2) द्वैतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dub
DUB (v.):<BR>(1) करोति (= to make);<BR>(2)<BR>कीर्तयति (= to glorify).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dubious
DUBIOUS: संदिग्धः (ग्धा, ग्धं): v. Doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dubiously
DUBIOUSLY: ससंदेहम्: v. Doubtfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dubiousness
DUBIOUSNESS: संदिग्धता: v. Doubtfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ducal
DUCAL: *डिउकीयः (या, यं); उपराजकीयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ducat
DUCAT: *डिउकीयमुद्रा; उपराजमुद्रा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

duchess
DUCHESS: *डिउकी; उपराज्ञी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

duchy
DUCHY: *उपराज्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

duck
DUCK (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) कादम्बः;<BR>(2)<BR>कलहंसः।<BR>II A darling: जातकः (f. का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

duck
DUCK (v.): v. To plunge, nod.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ducker
DUCKER:<BR>I A plunger, diver: q. v.<BR>II A<BR>fawner: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

duckling
DUCKLING: कादम्बशावः: v. Duck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

duct
DUCT: नाडिः: v. Also passage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ductile
DUCTILE: विनेयः (या, यं): v. Docile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ductility
DUCTILITY: विनेयता: Docility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dudgeon
DUDGEON: मन्युः,<BR>in d.:<BR>समन्यु (mfn.): v. Anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

due
DUE (adv.): सरलम्,<BR>d. east:<BR>सरलपूर्वः (र्वा, र्वं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

due
DUE (adj.):<BR>I Owed:<BR>(1) देयः (या, यं) (= to<BR>be given);<BR>(2) प्राप्यः (प्या, प्यं) (= to be<BR>received.)<BR>II Proper, fit: q. v.: उपयुक्तः (क्ता,<BR> क्तं).<BR>III Owing:<BR>the fall of rain is d. to its<BR>heaviness:<BR>अपां पतनं तद्गुरुत्वकारणकम्, V. d.: v.<BR>Accout of, on-. Ph.:<BR>the mail is d. now:<BR>अद्य<BR> पत्राणि समागन्तव्यानि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

due
DUE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) देयम्;<BR>(2) ऋणम् (= debt).<BR>Ph.:<BR>respect. is d. to elders:<BR>पूज्या गुरवः: v.<BR>Ought.<BR>II Right: q. v.<BR>III In pl., taxes:<BR>शुल्कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

duel
DUEL:<BR>I Subs.: द्वन्द्वयुद्धम्।<BR>II Verbs: द्वन्द्वयुद्धं<BR> करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

duelist
DUELIST: द्वन्द्वयुद्धकारिन् (f. णी); द्वन्द्वयोद्धृ (f. द्धी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dug
DUG (subs.): स्तनः: v. Nipple, teat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dugong
DUGONG: *द्विजङ्घः; स्तनन्धयमत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

duke
DUKE: *अधिनायकः; उपराजः; द्युकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dukedom
DUKEDOM: *अधिनायकत्वम्; उपराज्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dulcet
DULCET: मधुरः (रा, रं): v. Sweet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dulcimer
DULCIMER: तन्त्री (?); वाद्ययन्त्रविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dull
DULL (adj.):<BR>I Of intellect:<BR>(1) मन्दः (न्दा,<BR> न्दं);<BR>(2) मूढ (ढा, ढं) (= stupid).<BR>II Of<BR>colours, etc.:<BR>(1) मन्दः (न्दा, न्दं); when the<BR>d. -lighted (moon)<BR>was about to set:<BR>अथास्तमासेदुषि<BR> मन्दकान्तौ, B.;<BR>(2) मलिनः (ना, नं) (= dark).<BR>III Blunt: q. v.: निस्तेजस् (mfn.).<BR>IV Sad,<BR>melancholy: q. v.: विषण्ण (f. ण्णा).<BR>V Flat,<BR>insipid: q. v.: अरसः (सा, सं).<BR>VI Heavy,<BR>insensible: q. v.<BR>VII Cloudy, dark: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dull
DULL (v.):<BR>I To stupify: जडीकरोति।<BR>II To<BR>blunt: कुण्ठीकरोति।<BR>III To obscure: मलिनी-<BR>करोति।<BR>IV To depress: म्लानीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dullard
DULLARD: मूढः: v. Fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dull-brained
DULL-BRAINED, DULL-HEADED:<BR>(1) मन्दधी (n.<BR>धि), Ve.;<BR>(2) मन्दमति (mfn.), Pra.;<BR>(3) स्थूल-<BR>बुद्धि (mfn.), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dully
DULLY:<BR>(1) मन्दम् (= slowly);<BR>(2) नीरसम् (= insi-<BR>-pidly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dulliness
DULLINESS:<BR>(1) मान्द्यम् (= slowness, dimness);<BR>(2) जाड्यम् (= stupidity);<BR>(3) निस्तेजस्कता<BR>(= bluntness, drowsiness);<BR>(4) नीरसता<BR>(= insipidity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

duly
DULY:<BR>I Fitly.: q. v.: यथायथम्।<BR>II In proper<BR>time: यथासमये।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dumb
DUMB:<BR>(1) मूकः (का, कं) (the best equiv.),<BR>deaf and d.:<BR>एडमूकः (का, कं);<BR>(2) जडः (डा, डं):<BR>v. Speechless.<BR>To strike d.:<BR>जडीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dumb-bell
DUMB-BELL: prob. अयोदण्डः, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dumbly
