dynastic
DYNASTIC:<BR>(1) वंश्यः (श्या, श्यं);<BR>(2) by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dynasty
DYNASTY: वंशः,<BR>the solar d.:<BR>सूर्यवंशः;<BR>of the<BR>solar d.:<BR>सूर्यवंश्य (f. श्या), R. xvi. 10.;<BR>that d.<BR>will become extinct with Kshemaka:<BR>क्षेमकं प्राप्य<BR> स वंशः संस्थां प्राप्स्यते, V. p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dysentery
DYSENTERY:<BR>(1) ग्रहणी;<BR>(2) आमरक्तः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dyspepsia
DYSPEPSIA: आमयावित्त्वम्: v. Indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dyspeptic
DYSPEPTIC: आमयाविन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

dysury
DYSURY: मूत्रकृच्छ्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

each
EACH: v. Every. Ph.: went e. to his own house:<BR>स्वं स्वं धाम जग्मतुः, B. p.;<BR>e. of these:<BR>एषामेकैकम्,<BR>K.;<BR>gave one code to e.:<BR>एकैकां संहितामेकैकस्मै ददौ,<BR>B. p.: v. Everybody;<BR>we are ashamed of e.<BR>other:<BR>अन्योन्यस्य जिह्नीमः, Ki. v.: One another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eager
EAGER:<BR>I Desirous:<BR>(1) लालसः (सा, सं)<BR>(best equiv.),<BR>e. to see Śiva:<BR>ईशानसंदर्शनलालसः<BR>(सा, सं), Ku.;<BR>(2) लोलुपः (पा, पं),<BR>e. for an<BR>embrace:<BR>आश्लेषलोलुपः (पा, पं), Si.<BR>II Impe-<BR>-tuous, fervent:<BR>(1) व्यग्रः (ग्रा, ग्रं);<BR>(2) उत्सुकः<BR>(का, कं),<BR>the spring is very e.:<BR>पर्युत्सुक एष माधवः,<BR>Ku.<BR>III Brittle: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eagerly
EAGERLY:<BR>(1) सस्पृहम् (= longingly);<BR>(2) सतृष्णम्<BR>(= thirstily);<BR>(3) सोत्साहम् (= zealously);<BR>(4) व्यग्रम् (= impetuously).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eagerness
EAGERNESS:<BR>I Eager desire:<BR>(1) लालसा;<BR>(2)<BR>तृष्णा (= thirst).<BR>II Impetuosity: व्यग्रता।<BR>III Zeal: उत्साहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eagle
EAGLE: prob. खट्वाङ्गः of Mat.; पक्षिविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eagle-eyed
EAGLE-EYED: गृध्रदृश् (mfn.)<BR>or<BR>-दृष्टि (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eagle-stone
EAGLE-STONE: उपलौहविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eaglet
EAGLET: खट्वाङ्गशावकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ear
EAR (subs.):<BR>I Of animals:<BR>(1) कर्णः,<BR>to come<BR>to one's e.s:<BR>कर्णपथम् आयाति, Sa.; to shut the e.:<BR>कर्णौ पिदधाति, M.;<BR>to lend an e.:<BR>कर्णं ददाति,<BR>Sa.;<BR>to whisper into one's e:<BR>कर्णे कथयति, Mu.;<BR>the boring of the e. s (a religious ceremony)<BR>कर्णवेधः;<BR>the root of an e.:<BR>कर्णमूलम्, R.,<BR>or<BR>कर्णान्तः।<BR>R.,<BR>or<BR>कर्णजाहम्, B.;<BR>the middle e. or drum of the<BR>e.:<BR>कर्णकूपः, N.;<BR>(2) श्रोत्रम्,<BR>e. -enchanting:<BR>श्रोत्र-<BR>हारिन् (f. णी), K.;<BR>(3) श्रुतिः,<BR>being of the same<BR>name to the e.:<BR>श्रुतेः सनाम्नः, Mu. Ph.:<BR>the tip<BR>of an e.:<BR>पालिः;<BR>the outer e.:<BR>शष्कुली, C. s. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">Page227</a>]<BR>II Of other objects: perh. कर्णः।<BR>III Of<BR>corn:<BR>(1) कणिश (mn.);<BR>(2) शस्यमञ्जरी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ear
EAR (v.):<BR>I To plough: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>put forth ears of corn: v. To put<BR>forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ear-ache
EAR-ACHE: कर्णशूलम्, Sr., creates a bad man's e.:<BR>उपजनयति श्रवणस्थितं शूलमभव्यस्य, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eared
EARED:<BR>I Having ears:<BR>(1) कर्णिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) कर्णवत् (f. ती);<BR>(3) कर्णिलः (ला, लं).<BR>II<BR>Spiked: मञ्जरितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eardrop
EARDROP: कर्णपूरः (?): v. Ear-ring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ear lap
EAR LAP: कर्णपालिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ear-less
EAR-LESS:<BR>(1) अकर्णः (र्णा, र्णं);<BR>(2) कर्णहीनः<BR>(ना, नं); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ear-mark
EAR-MARK:<BR>I Lit.: कर्णचिह्नम्।<BR>II Any mark:<BR>चिह्नम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ear-ring
EAR-RING:<BR>(1) कुण्डलम्,<BR>gold e.:<BR>काञ्चनकुण्डलम्,<BR>Si.;<BR>(2) कर्णपाली;<BR>(3) कर्णिका;<BR>(4) कर्णभूषणम्;<BR>(5) कर्णवेष्टनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ear-shot
EAR-SHOT: कर्णविषयः; कर्णगोचरः; and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ear-trumpet
EAR-TRUMPET: *कर्णनादिनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ear-wax
EAR-WAX:<BR>(1) कर्णमलः;<BR>(2) कर्णगूथम्;<BR>(3) तोक्मम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ear-wig
EAR-WIG: कर्णकीटी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earl
EARL: उपाधिविशेषः; *उपनायकः।<BR>E. dom:<BR>*उपनाय-<BR>कत्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earliness
EARLINESS: expr. by adj.: v. Early.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

early
EARLY (adj.):<BR>I Commencing: Ph.:<BR>e.<BR>drops of rain:<BR>वर्षाग्रबिन्दवः, Me.;<BR>in the e. part<BR>of the day:<BR>दिवसस्याद्यभागे, Dak.; e. twilight:<BR>अग्रसन्ध्या, Sa.;<BR>e. youth:<BR>प्रथमं वयः।<BR>II Ancient:<BR>q. v.:<BR>in e. times:<BR>पूर्वकाले।<BR>III Forward:<BR>the<BR>winter is e. this year:<BR>*अस्मिन् वर्षे शीघ्रं समागतं<BR> शीतम्;<BR>e. death:<BR>अकालमृत्युः।<BR>IV In the morn-<BR>-ing: प्रगेतनः (नी, नं): v. Morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

early
EARLY (adv.):<BR>I In the morning:<BR>(1) प्रातर्;<BR>(2) प्रत्यूषसि: v. Morning. Ph.:<BR>very e. in the<BR>morning:<BR>अतिप्रत्यूषे<BR>or<BR>महति प्रत्यूषे, Sa.<BR>II Soon:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) शीध्रम्;<BR>(2) अचिरेण।<BR>III First:<BR>q. v.: पूर्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earn
EARN (v.):<BR>(1) अर्जयति, उप-, (अर्ज्, c. 10.),<BR>e.<BR>ing fleeting fortune:<BR>अर्जयन् गत्वरीः श्रियः, Ki,;<BR>(2) अर्जनं<BR>or<BR>उपार्जनं करोति,<BR>after e. ing three<BR>hundred sovereigns:<BR>सुवर्णशतत्रयोपार्जनं कृत्वा, P.: v.<BR>To acquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earnest
EARNEST (adj.):<BR>I Eager, zealous: q. v.:<BR>(1) व्यग्रः (ग्रा, ग्रं);<BR>(2) सोत्साहः (हा, हं). Ph.:<BR>e. wish:<BR>एकान्तकामना।<BR>II Intent:<BR>(1) एकाग्रः<BR>(ग्रा, ग्रं);<BR>(2) निविष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं).<BR>III Seri-<BR>-ous: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earnest
EARNEST (subs.):<BR>I Reality: सत्यम्। Ph.:<BR>I am<BR>in e.:<BR>न परिहसामि।<BR>II Eagerness, intentness:<BR>q. v.<BR>III Part-payment:<BR>(1) सत्यापनम्;<BR>(2)<BR>सत्यङ्कारः,<BR>to give e.:<BR>सत्यङ्कारं ददाति, Vy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earnestly
EARNESTLY:<BR>I With fixed attention:<BR>(1)<BR>एकाग्रचित्तेन;<BR>(2) निविष्टमनसा।<BR>II Eagerly:<BR>q. v.: सोत्साहम्।<BR>III Seriously: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earnestness
EARNESTNESS:<BR>I Eagerness: व्यग्रता।<BR>II<BR>Intentness: एकाग्रता।<BR>III Seriousness:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earning
EARNING (subs.): अर्जितम्, उप-, one's own e. s:<BR>स्वयमर्जितम्, Ga.;<BR>e. s of valour:<BR>शौर्यार्जितम्, Da.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earth
EARTH (subs.):<BR>I The globe:<BR>(1) पृथिवी;<BR>(2) पृथ्वी;<BR>(3) वसुधा;<BR>(4) वसुमती;<BR>(5) वसुन्धरा;<BR>(6) अवनि: (f.);<BR>(7) मेदिनी;<BR>(8) मही;<BR>(9)<BR>धरित्री;<BR>(10) भूः;<BR>(11) भूमिः;<BR>(12) धरा;<BR>(13)<BR>क्षितिः;<BR>(14) धरणी।<BR>II The dry land: स्थलम्।<BR>III Clay:<BR>(1) मृत्तिका;<BR>(2) मृद् (f.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earth
EARTH (v.):<BR>I Trans: भूमौ निदधाति (धा, c.<BR>3.).<BR>II Intrans: [भूमौ] वसति (वस्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earth-born
EARTH-BORN:<BR>(1) भूमिजः (जा, जं), and sim.<BR>comp.s;<BR>(2) भौमः (मी, मं),<BR>when you went to<BR>conquer the e.:<BR>त्वयि भौमं गते जेतुम्, Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earthen
EARTHEN:<BR>(1) मृन्मयः (यी, यं),<BR>e. vessel:<BR>मृन्मयं<BR> पात्रम्, R.;<BR>(2) मार्तिकः (की, कं) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earthen-ware
EARTHEN-WARE:<BR>(1) मृद्भाण्डम्;<BR>(2) मृन्मयं भाण्डम्;<BR>(3) मार्तिकम्;<BR>(4) कौलालकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earthling
EARTHLING:<BR>(1) भौभः;<BR>(2) मर्त्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earthly
EARTHLY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पार्थिवः (वी, वं),<BR>e. for-<BR>tune:<BR>पार्थिवश्रीः, R.;<BR>(2) भौमः (मी, मं), e. forms:<BR>भौमा उपाधयः, Vi.; सांसारिकः (की, कं) (= worldly<BR>q. v.).<BR>II Conceivable: खलु; what e. pleasure:<BR>किं खलु सुखम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earthquake
EARTHQUAKE:<BR>(1) भूमिकम्पः, Raj.;<BR>(2) क्षिति-<BR>कम्पः,<BR>V m.;<BR>(3) अवनिप्रकम्पनम्, Ku. and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earth-worm
EARTH-WORM:<BR>I Lit.: पीलुः।<BR>II Fig.: कीटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earthwork
EARTHWORK:<BR>I Lit.: मृदुत्तोलनम् (?).<BR>II A<BR>mound: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

earthy
EARTHY: v. Earthen, earthly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ease
Ease (subs.):<BR>I Comfort: सुखम्,<BR>at e.:<BR>सुखेन or<BR>निरुद्वेगेन।<BR>II Peace, tranquillity:<BR>(1) निर्वृत्तिः,<BR>how could he have e.<BR>कधं स्यात्तस्य निर्वृतिः, P.;<BR>(2) स्वास्थ्यम्,<BR>I am now at e.:<BR>लब्धमिदानीं स्वास्थ्यम्,<BR>Sa.<BR>III Facility: अनायासः, with e.: v.<BR>Easily.<BR>IV Of style, etc.: स्वाच्छन्द्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ease
EASE (v.):<BR>I To comfort: स्वस्थयति (nomi.).<BR>II<BR>To alleviate: लघयति (nomi.)<BR>III To move<BR>gently: ईषच्चालयति (c. of चल्).<BR>IV To<BR>dung: अशौचं करोति, V. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

easel
EASEL: *चित्राधारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

easement
EASEMENT:<BR>I Assistance: q. v.<BR>II In law:<BR>परभूमावधिकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

easily
EASILY:<BR>I With facility:<BR>(1) सुखेन,<BR>or<BR>सुखम्, or<BR>सुख in comp.,<BR>e. to be got:<BR>सुखेन लभ्य (f. भ्या),<BR>Ki. i. 17.;<BR>digests e.:<BR>सुखं जीर्यति, Sr.;<BR>(2) अना-<BR>यासेन<BR>or<BR>निरायासेन (= without exertion),<BR>to<BR>sustain e.:<BR>अनायासेन बिभर्ति, K.<BR>(3) अक्लेशेन<BR>(= without trouble).<BR>II Without anxiety:<BR>(1) निरुद्वेगेन;<BR>(2) निश्चिन्तम्।<BR>III Gently,<BR>gracefully: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

easiness
EASINESS:<BR>I Comfort: सुखम्।<BR>II Good-<BR>-nature: सौजन्यम्।<BR>III Credulity: q. v.<BR>IV<BR>Of style, etc.: स्त्राच्छन्द्यम् (?).<BR>V Facility:<BR>सौकर्यम्; better expr. by adj.: v. Easy (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

east
EAST (adj.):<BR>(1) पूर्वः (र्वा, र्वं),<BR>on the e.:<BR>पूर्वतः,<BR>A. p.;<BR>(2) प्राच् (f. ची), e. of Vinashana:<BR>प्राग्विनशनात्, M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

east
EAST (subs.):<BR>(1) पूर्वदिश् (f.), and sim. comp.s,<BR>flow towards the e.:<BR>पूर्वां दिशं प्रति स्रवन्ति, S. c.;<BR>(2) प्राची,<BR>he first went to the e.:<BR>स ययौ प्रथमं प्राचीं,<BR>R.;<BR>(3) ऐन्द्री दिक् and sim. comp.s, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

easter
EASTER: *कृष्टस्य पुनरुत्थानपर्वन् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

easterly
EASTERLY:<BR>I Adj.: v. Eastern.<BR>II Adv.:<BR>expr. by loc.:<BR>(1) पूर्वस्यां दिशि;<BR>(2) प्राच्याम्;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eastern
EASTERN:<BR>(1) पूर्वः (र्वा, र्वं),<BR>the e. and western<BR>oceans:<BR>पूर्वापरौ तोयनिधी, Ku.;<BR>(2) प्राच्यः (च्या,<BR> च्यं),<BR>e. gate:<BR>प्राच्यं द्वारम्, B.;<BR>the e. s:<BR>प्राच्याः,<BR>Mah.;<BR>(3) पौरस्त्य (f. स्त्या),<BR>e. regions:<BR>पौर-<BR>स्त्या जनपदाः, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eastward
EASTWARD: expr. by ins.:<BR>(1) पूर्वेण;<BR>(2)<BR>प्राच्या<BR>or<BR>प्राचा,<BR>passing a little e.:<BR>प्राचा किञ्चिदन्तर-<BR>मतिक्रम्य, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

easy
EASY:<BR>I Not difficult:<BR>(1) सुकरः (रा, रं),<BR>अयत्नसाध्यः (ध्या, ध्यं), etc. (= e. to do),<BR>it is<BR>not e. to break great men's contemplation:<BR>न हि<BR> महतां सुकरः समाधिमङ्गः, Ki.;<BR>(2) सुगमः (मा, मं)<BR>(= e. to go or understand), the rest is e.:<BR>शेषं सुगमम्, Go.;<BR>(3) सु in comp.,<BR>fortune is not<BR>e. to keep:<BR>असुरक्षाः श्रियः, Ki.;<BR>Indra is e. to<BR>worship:<BR>स्वाराध्यो मरुत्वान्, Ki.<BR>II Quiet, calm:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) निर्वृतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) सुस्थः (स्था, स्थं).<BR>III Of style, etc.: स्वच्छन्दः (न्दा, न्दं) (?).<BR>IV Causing ease: उत्तमः (मा, मं) (= good).<BR>V Compliant: अनुरोधिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eat
EAT (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) खादति (खाद्, c. 1.),<BR>should not e. fishes:<BR>मत्स्यान्न खादेत्, K. b.;<BR>(2) अत्ति (अद्, c. 2.),<BR>we e. Brahmins:<BR>अह्मो<BR> द्विजान्, B.;<BR>(3) अश्नाति (अश्, c. 9.),<BR>and nobody<BR>returned without e. ing who wanted to e.:<BR>इच्छता-<BR>शितुमनाशुषा न च प्रत्यगामि, Si.;<BR>(4) भक्षति or<BR>भक्षयति (भक्ष्, c. 1. and 10.), will e. us all:<BR>भक्षयिष्यति नः सर्वान्, A. r.;<BR>(5) भुंक्ते (भुज्, c. 7.),<BR>they ate belly-ful:<BR>अमीभिराकण्ठममोजि, N.;<BR>(6) जक्षिति (जक्ष्, c. 2.) (rare);<BR>(7) घसति<BR>(घस्, c. 1.) (rare);<BR>(8) प्साति (प्सा, c. 2.)<BR>(rare).<BR>II To corrode: खादति: Ph.:<BR>to e.<BR>one's own words:<BR>स्ववचनं वितथं करोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eat
EAT (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.: v. Eat (I).<BR>II To<BR>taste: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eat away
EAT AWAY, EAT OUT: खादति, सं-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eat up
EAT UP:<BR>(1) भक्षति<BR>or<BR>भक्षयति;<BR>(2) जक्षिति (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eatable
EATABLE (Subs.):<BR>(1) खाद्यम्;<BR>(2) भोज्यम्;<BR>(3) मक्ष्यम्;<BR>(4) भोजनीयम्;<BR>(5) अशितव्यम्;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eater
EATER:<BR>(1) खादकः;<BR>(2) भक्षकः;<BR>(3) भोक्तृ<BR>(m.);<BR>(4) भोजिन् (m.),<BR>man -e.:<BR>मानुषभोजिन्,<BR>A. r.;<BR>(5) -आशिन्, e. of one's own race:<BR>स्वकुलाशिन्, N.;<BR>(6) -अदः,<BR>a fish-e. is e. of all<BR>flesh:<BR>मत्स्यादः सर्वमांसादः, M.;<BR>(7) -भुज् (m.),<BR>man -e.:<BR>नृभुज्, B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eating
EATING (subs.):<BR>(1) भोजनम्;<BR>(2) भक्षणम्;<BR>(3)<BR>अशनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eaves
EAVES:<BR>(1) नीध्रम्;<BR>(2) वलिकः;<BR>(3) स्यन्दनिका;<BR>(4) पटलप्रान्तः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eavesdropper
EAVESDROPPER: श्रवणकामुकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ebb
EBB (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) क्षीयमाणा वेला;<BR>(2)<BR>वेलाह्नासः।<BR>II Fig.: v. Decline, decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ebb
EBB (v.):<BR>(1) क्षीयते (pass. of क्षि);<BR>(3) ह्नासं<BR> गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ebony
EBONY: कोविदारः,<BR>a banner of e.:<BR>कोविदारकेतुः, U.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ebriety
EBRIETY: मत्तता,<BR>in a state of e.:<BR>मत्तः (त्ता, त्तं):<BR>v. Drunkenness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ebullition
EBULLITION:<BR>I Lit.: बुद्वुदायितम् (?).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>उद्रेकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eccentric
ECCENTRIC:<BR>I Deviating from a centre:<BR>*केन्द्रभ्रष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं).<BR>II Not having the same<BR>e.: *विषमकेन्द्रः (न्द्रा, न्द्रं).<BR>III Irregular,<BR>odd.: perh. विषमः (मा, मं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eccentricity
ECCENTRICITY: वैषम्यम्। (?): v. Oddity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ecclesiastic
ECCLESIASTIC, -AL (adj.):<BR>(1) धर्म- in comp.;<BR>(2) याजकीयः (या, यं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ecclesiastic
ECCLESIASTIC (subs.): याजकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

echinus
ECHINUS: v. Hedgehog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

echo
ECHO (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रतिशब्दः, -कः,<BR>men follow royal<BR>sayings like e. s:<BR>प्रतिशब्दक इव राजवचनमनुगच्छति<BR> जनः, K.;<BR>(2) प्रतिध्वनिः;<BR>(3) प्रतिस्वनः,<BR>by its<BR>e. in the cave:<BR>प्रतिस्वनेनास्य गुहागतेन, R.;<BR>(4)<BR>प्रतिनादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

echo
ECHO (v. i.):<BR>(1) प्रतिध्वनति (ध्वन्, c. 1.);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रतिस्वनति (स्वन्, c. 1.);<BR>(3) प्रतिनदति (नद्, c.<BR>1.),<BR>the noise e. ed in the caves:<BR>ध्वनिर्दरीषु<BR> प्रतिननाद, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

echo
ECHO (v. t.):<BR>I To cause to e.:<BR>(1) प्रतिध्वानयति<BR>(c. of ध्वन्),<BR>e. ing the cave:<BR>कन्दरभुवः कुर्वन्<BR> प्रतिध्वानिताः, Na.;<BR>(2) प्रतिनादयति, (c. of नद्).<BR>II To echo: q. v.: अनु-नदति, etc.<BR>III<BR>Fig., to adopt: expr. by these verbs: v.<BR>Echo (subs.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eclat
ECLAT:<BR>I Splendour: q. v.: प्रशंसा।<BR>II<BR>Applause: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eclectic
ECLECTIC: *समाहारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eclipse
ECLIPSE (subs.):<BR>(1) ग्रहणम् (the best equiv.),<BR>total e.:<BR>सम्पूर्णग्रहणम्, Su. com.,<BR>or<BR>सर्वग्रहणम्,<BR>Gan.;<BR>(2) ग्रासः,<BR>partial e.:<BR>आंशिकग्रासः, Su.<BR>com.;<BR>magnitude of an e.:<BR>ग्रासप्रमाणम्, Gan.;<BR>(3) उपरागः,<BR>lunar e.:<BR>चन्द्रोपरागः, Mu. i.;<BR>(4)<BR>ग्रहः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eclipse
ECLIPSE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: छादयति, प्र-, आ-, सं-,<BR>(छद्, c. 10.), in the solar e. the moon e. s the sun:<BR>रविग्रहणे रविं विधुश्छादयति, Gan.<BR>II Fig.: to<BR>obscure, darken:<BR>(1) छादयति, प्र-,<BR>e. ing<BR>their fame:<BR>कीर्तिं प्रच्छाद्य तेषां वै, Mah.;<BR>(2)<BR>तिरस्करोति (कृ, c. 8.),<BR>so long as your title of<BR>prince is not e. d by the title of emperor:<BR>अधिराजशब्देनातिरस्कृते कुमारशब्दे, Mu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ecliptic
ECLIPTIC:<BR>(1) क्रान्तिवृत्तम्;<BR>(2) क्रान्तिमण्डलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eclogue
ECLOGUE: *गोपकाव्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

economic
ECONOMIC, -AL:<BR>I Domestic: q. v.<BR>II Fru-<BR>-gal: q. v.<BR>III Prudent, careful: q. v.:<BR>अप्रमत्तः (त्ता, त्तं).<BR>IV Relating to economy:<BR>expr. by comp. Ph.:<BR>e. museum:<BR>*साधारण-<BR>कौतुकागारम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

economically
ECONOMICALLY: v. Frugally, prudently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

economics
ECONOMICS: अर्थशास्त्रम्: v. Economy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

economist
ECONOMIST:<BR>I Lit.: विवेकव्ययिन् (f. नी) (?).<BR>II<BR>Political e.:<BR>अर्थशास्त्रविद् (mfn.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

economize
ECONOMIZE: विवेकेन व्ययते (व्यय्, c. 1.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

economy
ECONOMY:<BR>I Lit.: विवेकव्ययः (?).<BR>II Orderly<BR>system: नियमावलिः (?).<BR>Political e.:<BR>अर्थशास्त्रम्<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ecstacy
ECSTACY:<BR>I Rapture: हर्षोन्मादः,<BR>in e.:<BR>सहर्षो-<BR>न्मादम्, Vi.<BR>II Madness, frenzy: q. v.:<BR>उन्मादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ecstatic
ECSTATIC:<BR>I Entrancing: उन्मादिन् (f. नी),<BR>as if in e. mind:<BR>उन्मादिनेव मनसेव, N.<BR>II Rap-<BR>-turous: उन्मादिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ecumenic
ECUMENIC, -AL:<BR>(1) सार्वलौकिकः (की, कं);<BR>(2)<BR>विश्वजनीनः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eddy
EDDY (subs.):<BR>(1) आवर्तः;<BR>(2) भ्रमिः: v.<BR>Whirlpool.<BR>E. of wind:<BR>चक्रवात्या: v. Whirl-<BR>-wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eddy
EDDY (v.):<BR>I Lit.: भ्रमीभवति (?).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>आवर्तवद् भ्राम्यति (भ्रम्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

edge
EDGE (subs.):<BR>I Of a cutting instrument:<BR>धारा,<BR>the sharp e. of the axe of Rāma:<BR>धारां शितां<BR> रामपरश्वधस्य, R.<BR>II Border, end: q. v.: धारा। [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">Page230</a>]<BR>III Sharpness, severity: तेजस् (n.).<BR>IV<BR>Commencement: प्रारम्भः। Ph.:<BR>“to set the<BR>teeth on e.”:<BR>दन्तहर्षं जनयति (जन्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

edge
EDGE (v. t.):<BR>I To whet: q. v.:<BR>(1) prob.<BR>धारयति;<BR>(2) शाणयति (nomi.).<BR>II To<BR>embitter: q. v.: तेजयति, उत्-, Vi.<BR>III To<BR>border: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

edge
EDGE (v. i.): i. e. to e. along: प्रसर्पति (सृप्, c.<BR>1.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

edged
EDGED:<BR>(1) सधारः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) धारोज्ज्वलः (ला,<BR> लं) (poet), Pra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

edging
EDGING (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रान्तः: v. Border;<BR>(2)<BR>दशा (of a garment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

edible
EDIBLE: खाद्यः (द्या, द्यं): v. Eatable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

edict
EDICT: शासनम्: v. Order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

edification
EDIFICATION: शिक्षा (?): v. Instruction,<BR>improvement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

edifice
EDIFICE:<BR>(1) प्रासादः;<BR>(2) सौधम्;<BR>(3) हर्म्यम्;<BR>(4) अट्टालिका,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

edify
EDIFY:<BR>(1) उत्कर्षति (कृष्, c. 1.) (= to ennoble);<BR>(2) शिक्षयति (शिक्ष्, c. 10.) (= to teach).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

edifying
EDIFYING (adj.):<BR>(1) ज्ञानदः (दा, दं);<BR>(2)<BR>मोहध्वंसिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

edit
EDIT:<BR>(1) प्रकाशयति (काश्, c. 10.) (= to publish);<BR>(2) संस्करोति (कृ, c. 8.) (?);<BR>(3) मुद्रयति (मुद्र्,<BR>c. 10.) (= to print).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

edition
EDITION: *संस्करणम्,<BR>first e.:<BR>प्रथमसंस्करणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

editor
EDITOR: *संस्कर्तृ (f. र्त्री);<BR>(2) प्रकाशक (f. शिका)<BR>(= publisher).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

educate
EDUCATE:<BR>(1) विनयति (नी, c. 1.), e. d him:<BR>विनिन्युरेनम्, R. iii. 29.;<BR>(2) शिक्षयति (शिक्ष्,<BR>c. 1.) (= to instruct);<BR>(3) संस्करोति (कृ, c. 8.)<BR>(= to dress up).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

educated
EDUCATED: of men:<BR>(1) कृतविद्यः (द्या, द्यं);<BR>(2) सुशिक्षितः (ता, तं): v. Learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

education
EDUCATION:<BR>(1) संस्कारः,<BR>e. has been given by<BR>(your) father with great care:<BR>पित्रा महता प्रयत्नेन<BR> समारोपितसंस्कारः, K.;<BR>(2) विनयः (rare),<BR>by<BR>giving e.:<BR>विनयाधानात्, R.;<BR>(3) शिक्षा (= ins-<BR>-truction).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

educational
EDUCATIONAL: Ph.:<BR>for e. purposes:<BR>*प्रजा-<BR>शिक्षार्थम्;<BR>e. series<BR>*शिक्षापुस्तकावलिः;<BR>e. depart-<BR>ment:<BR>*शिक्षाविभागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

educator
EDUCATOR:<BR>(1) विनेतृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) संस्कृर्तृ (f. र्त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

educe
EDUCE<BR>(1) उन्नयति (नी, c. 1.);<BR>(2) उत्-हरति, -ते<BR> हृ, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eel
EEL: कुञ्चिका (?); वर्मिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

efface
EFFACE: मार्ष्टि<BR>or<BR>मार्जयति, अप-, उत्-, निर्-, प्र-,<BR> व्या-, (मृज्, c. 2. and 10.),<BR>to e. the mud of<BR>infamy:<BR>प्रमार्ष्टुमयशःपङ्कम्, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effacement
EFFACEMENT: मार्जना, -नम्, अप-, प्र-, निर्-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effect
EFFECT (subs.):<BR>I As opposed to cause:<BR>कार्यम्, there is no e. in the absence of a cause:<BR>कारणाभावात् कार्याभावः, V. d.<BR>II Consequence,<BR>result: q. v.: फलम्,<BR>of no e.:<BR>निष्फलः (ला, लं).<BR>III Force, importance: Ph.:<BR>he always speaks<BR>with e.:<BR>हृदयग्राहीणि सदा खलु तस्य वचांसि;<BR>“the e.<BR>was heightened by the lonely nature of the place”:<BR>*स्थानविविक्तता रौद्रतां वर्धयामास: (the real e.<BR>should be expr. in such cases).<BR>IV<BR>Purpose: q. v.: अभिप्रायः,<BR>to this e.:<BR>एतदभिप्रायः<BR>(या, यं).<BR>V Fact: q. v.:<BR>in e.:<BR>फलतः, S.<BR>VI<BR>In pl., goods: q. v. सम्पत्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effect
EFFECT (v.): निष्पादयति (c. of पद्): v. To<BR>accomplish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effectible
EFFECTIBLE:<BR>(1) साध्यः (ध्या, ध्यं);<BR>(2) निष्पाद्यः<BR>(द्या, द्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effection
EFFECTION:<BR>(1) निष्पादनम्;<BR>(2) उपपादनम्;<BR>(3)<BR>साधनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effective
EFFECTIVE:<BR>I Producing effects: कार्योत्पादक<BR>(f. दिका).<BR>II Effectual: फलवत् (f. ती).<BR>III<BR>Telling, impressive: हृदयग्राहिन् (f. णी).<BR>IV<BR>Serviceable: कार्यक्षमः (मा, मं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effectiveness
EFFECTIVENESS: of speech: हृदयग्राहित्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effectless
EFFECTLESS: निष्फलः (ला, लं): v. Ineffectual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effector
EFFECTOR: निष्पादकः: v. Doer, author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effectual
EFFECTUAL:<BR>(1) फलवत् (f. ती);<BR>(2) सफलः (ला,<BR> लं);<BR>(3) बलवत् (f. ती) (= forcible).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effectually
EFFECTUALLY:<BR>(1) सफलम्;<BR>(2) बलवत् (= for-<BR>-cibly);<BR>(3) अमोघम् (without failure).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effectuate
EFFECTUATE: सम्पादयति (c. of पद्): v. To<BR>accomplish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effeminacy
EFFEMINACY:<BR>(1) कापुरुषत्वम् (= cowardice);<BR>(2) क्लैव्यम्;<BR>(3) मार्दवम् (= mildness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effeminate
EFFEMINATE:<BR>I Womanish:<BR>(1) क्लीवः (वा, वं):<BR>v. Unmanly, coward;<BR>(2) सुकुमारः (रा, रं); [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">Page231</a>]<BR>v. Delicate.<BR>II Womanly: स्त्रैण (f. णी),<BR>by e. lightness:<BR>स्त्रैणेन लघिम्ना, B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effeminately
EFFEMINATELY: स्त्रीवत्, to shed eye-drops e.:<BR>स्त्रीवन्नयनसलिलं परित्यजति, Ve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effeminateness
EFFEMINATENESS: v. Effeminacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effervesce
EFFERVESCE: बुद्वुदायते (nomi.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effervescence
EFFERVESCENCE:<BR>I Lit.: बुद्वुदायितम् (?).<BR>II<BR>Fig., excitement: तापः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effete
EFFETE:<BR>(1) बन्ध्यः (न्ध्या, न्ध्यं): v. Barren;<BR>(2) जीर्णः (र्णा, र्णं) (= worn-out).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

efficacious
EFFICACIOUS:<BR>(1) गुणवत् (f. ती);<BR>(2) फलवत् (f. ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

efficaciously
EFFICACIOUSLY: सफलम्: v. Effectually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

efficaciousness
EFFICACIOUSNESS, EFFICACY:<BR>(1) गुणवत्ता;<BR>(2)<BR>साफल्यम्;<BR>(3) प्रभावः (= power).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

efficiency
EFFICIENCY:<BR>I Effectual agency: कार्योत्पादिका<BR> शक्तिः।<BR>II Competent energy:<BR>(1) तेजस्<BR>(n.);<BR>(2) प्रभावः।<BR>III Ability: दाक्ष्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

efficient
EFFICIENT:<BR>(1) कार्यक्षमः (मा, मं);<BR>(2) दक्षः<BR>(क्षा, क्षं) (= able).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

efficiently
EFFICIENTLY:<BR>(1) दाक्ष्येण (= ably);<BR>(2)<BR>अतन्द्रितम् (= actively).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effigy
EFFIGY: प्रतिमा: v. Image, likeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

efflorescence
EFFLORESCENCE:<BR>I Lit.: पुष्पोदूगमः।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>आविर्भावः: v. Appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effluence
EFFLUENCE: निर्गमः: v. Issue, flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effluvium
EFFLUVIUM: perh. उद्गारः: v. Exhalation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

efflux
EFFLUX: स्रावः: v. Flow, effusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effort
EFFORT: यत्नः, प्र-, with the utmost possible e.:<BR>सर्वप्रयत्नेन, R.: v. Endeavour, attempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effortless
EFFORTLESS: निर्यत्नः (त्ना, त्नं), V. p.; and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effrontery
EFFRONTERY: धार्ष्ट्य म्: v. Impudence, bold-<BR>-ness, shamelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effulgence
EFFULGENCE: उज्ज्वलता: v. Splendour, bright-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effulgent
EFFULGENT: उज्ज्वलः (ला, लं): v. Bright,<BR>splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

effusion
EFFUSION: स्रावः,<BR>e. of blood:<BR>रक्तस्रावः: v. Flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eft
EFT: तृणगोधा (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

egg
EGG (subs.):<BR>(1) अण्डम् (the best equiv.),<BR>hen's<BR>e.:<BR>कुक्कुटाण्डम्, Ya.; I will lay e. s there:<BR>तत्राहमण्डकविमोक्षणं करोमि, P. i. 12. (rarely);<BR>(2) डिम्बः;<BR>(3) कोषः;<BR>(4) पेशी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

egg on
EGG ON (v.): प्रोत्साहयति (c. of सह्): v. To<BR>instigate, impel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

egg-plant
EGG-PLANT:<BR>(1) वार्ताकुः;<BR>(2) वङ्गनः;<BR>(3)<BR>हिण्डीरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

egg-spoon
EGG-SPOON: *अण्डखादनचमसः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eglantine
EGLANTINE: वन्यसेवती (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

egoism
EGOISM:<BR>I Philo: अहंवादः।<BR>II Egotism: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

egotism
EGOTISM: आत्मश्लाघा: v. Vanity, pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

egotist
EGOTIST: आत्मश्लाघिन् (f. नी): v. Vain, proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

egotistic
EGOTISTIC, -AL: आत्मश्लाघामयाः (यी, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

egotistically
EGOTISTICALLY:<BR>(1) आत्मश्लाघया; आत्मश्लाघापूर्वकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

egregious
EGREGIOUS: असाधारणः (णी, णं) (= uncommon),<BR>e. mistake:<BR>असाधारणभ्रमः। Ph.:<BR>e. fool:<BR>अत्यन्त-<BR>मूर्खः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

egregiously
EGREGIOUSLY: अत्यन्तम्: v. Exceedingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

egress
EGRESS:<BR>(1) निर्गमः, -णम्;<BR>(2) निर्याणम्;<BR>(3)<BR>निष्क्रमः, -णम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eider-down
EIDER-DOWN: perh. हंसतूलः, D. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eight
EIGHT: अष्टन् (mfn.), in e. ways or parts:<BR>अष्टधा;<BR>e. times:<BR>अष्टकृत्वः<BR>or<BR>अष्टवारान्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eighteen
EIGHTEEN: अष्टादशन् (mfn.).<BR>E. th:<BR>अष्टादशः<BR>(शी, शं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eightfold
EIGHTFOLD: अष्टगुणः (णा, णं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eighth
EIGHTH (adj.): अष्टमः (मी, मं), in the e. place:<BR>अष्टमतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eighth
EIGHTH (subs.):<BR>(1) अष्टमांशः<BR>or<BR>अष्टांशः;<BR>(2)<BR>अष्टमभागः<BR>or<BR>अष्टभागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eightieth
EIGHTIETH:<BR>(1) अशीतितमः (मी, मं);<BR>(2) अशीतः<BR>(ती, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eightly
EIGHTLY:<BR>(1) अष्टमतः;<BR>(2) अष्टमम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eighty
EIGHTY: अशीतिः,<BR>e. times:<BR>अशीतिकृत्वः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

either
EITHER (conj.):<BR>(1) वा ॥॥॥॥॥वा (never at<BR>the beginning of a clause),<BR>e. I dissolve on the<BR>summit of this mountain:<BR>नगमूर्द्धनि विलीये वा,<BR>Ki.;<BR>(2) ॥॥॥॥।किंवा,<BR>will touch e. his nails<BR>or his arrow-heads:<BR>तन्नखं किंवा तदिषुमुखं स्प्रष्टारः,<BR>Vi.: v. Or.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

either
EITHER (pro.): Ph.:<BR>e. of two:<BR>अन्यतरः (रा, रत्);<BR>e. of three:<BR>अन्यतमः (मा, मत्); “on e. cheek”:<BR>कपोलयोः;<BR>“on e. side”:<BR>उभयतः: v. Both; not e.<BR>v. Neither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ejaculate
EJACULATE: उद्गिरति (गॄ, c. 6.), to e. greatness:<BR>माहात्म्यम् उद्गिरति, Vi.: v. To utter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ejaculation
EJACULATION: उद्गारः, N.: v. Cry (subs.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ejaculatory
EJACULATORY: perh. उदीर्यमाणः (णा, णं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eject
EJECT: निरस्यति (अस, c. 4.): v. To throw<BR>out, drive away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ejection
EJECTION, EJECTMENT: निःसारणम्, निरसनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eke
EKE (adv.): अपि: v. Also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eke
EKE (v.):<BR>I To increase: q. v.: वर्धयति।<BR>II<BR>To extend: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elaborate
ELABORATE:<BR>(1) बहुश्रमेण करोति (= to produce<BR>with labour);<BR>(2) संस्करोति (= to refine:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elaborate
ELABORATE (adj.):<BR>(1) संस्कृतः (ता, तं) (= re-<BR>-fined);<BR>(2) बहुश्रमसिद्ध (f. द्धा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elaborately
ELABORATELY:<BR>(1) बहुश्रमेण (= with great<BR>labour: q. v.);<BR>(2) ससंस्कारम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elaboration
ELABORATION:<BR>I Refinement: संस्कारः।<BR>II<BR>Of style, etc.: *संस्कारः,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elapse
ELAPSE:<BR>(1) अत्येति, सम्-, (इ, c. 2.),<BR>12 years<BR>have e. d:<BR>द्वादशसमाः समतीयुः, D. iv.;<BR>(2)<BR>अतिक्रामति<BR>or<BR>क्राम्यति, सम्-, (क्रम्, c. 1. and 4.),<BR>when the sixth night watching had e. d:<BR>अतिक्रान्ते<BR> षष्ठीजागरे, K.: v. To pass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elastic
ELASTIC:<BR>I Lit.: स्थितिस्थापकः (का, कं).<BR>II<BR>Fig.: v. Cheerful, brisk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elasticity
ELASTICITY: स्थितिस्थापकः, Par.; स्थितिस्थापकता, -त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elate
ELATE (v.): उत्सेचयति (c. of सिच्): v. To<BR>puff up, inflate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elate
ELATE or ELATED, TO BE: उत्सिञ्चति (सिच्, c.<BR>6.), (yet)<BR>his mind was not e.:<BR>न तस्योत्सिषिचे<BR> मनः, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elation
ELATION: उत्सेकः: v. Pride; to elate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elbow
ELBOW:<BR>(1) अरत्निः;<BR>(2) कफोणिः;<BR>(3) कूर्परः।<BR>Ph.:<BR>saw her leaning on her left e.:<BR>वामकरतल-<BR>विनिहितमुखकमलां ददर्श, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elbow-room
ELBOW-ROOM: i. e. room for motion: अवकाशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elder
ELDER (adj.):<BR>(1) ज्येष्ठः (f. ष्ठा);<BR>(2) ज्यायस्<BR>(f. सी) (rare);<BR>(3) वयोधिकः (का, कं).<BR>E.<BR>brother:<BR>अग्रजः;<BR>e. sister:<BR>अग्रजा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elder
ELDER (subs.):<BR>I A tree: वृक्षविशेषः।<BR>II An<BR>e. person:<BR>(1) वृद्धः, e. s in knowledge, and merit:<BR>जन्मविद्यागुणज्येष्ठः, Vri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elderly
ELDERLY: अधिधकवयस् (mfn.): प्रवयस् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eldership
ELDERSHIP:<BR>(1) ज्येष्ठता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2) ज्यैष्ठम्, Da.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eldest
ELDEST: ज्येष्ठः (ष्ठा, ष्ठं), the e. or his next,<BR>ज्येष्ठोऽनन्तरो वा, L. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elect
ELECT (v.):<BR>I To choose: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>select by vote: no equiv.: निर्वाचयति (c. of<BR>वच्) (?); मनोनीतं (f. तां) करोति (in Bengali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elect
ELECT (adj.): निर्वाचितः (ता, तं) (?); स्थिरीकृतः<BR>(ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

election
ELECTION:<BR>I Choice: q. v.<BR>II For an<BR>office: निर्वाचनम् (?).<BR>III The e. s: *निर्वाचन-<BR>कार्याणि (n. pl.).<BR>IV Free will: इच्छा।<BR>V<BR>Discernment: विवेकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

electioneering
ELECTIONEERING:<BR>I Subs.: *निर्वाचननिर्वाहः।<BR>II Adj.: expr. by comp.,<BR>e. agent:<BR>*निर्वाचन-<BR>निर्वाहकर्मकरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elective
ELECTIVE: Ph.:<BR>e. franchise:<BR>*निर्वाचनाधिकारः;<BR>e. office<BR>*निर्वाचनीयपदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elector
ELECTOR: *निर्वाचकः; निर्वाचनाधिकारिन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

electoral
ELECTORAL: expr. by comp., the e. body:<BR>*निर्वाचकसम्प्रदायः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

electric
ELECTRIC, ELECTRICAL:<BR>(1) वैद्यतः (ती, तं), e. fire:<BR>वैद्युतः कृशानुः; Ki.;<BR>(2) by comp., e. current:<BR>*तडित्प्रवाहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

electricity
ELECTRICITY:<BR>(1) तडित् (f.), the science of e.:<BR>*तडिद्विज्ञानम्;<BR>(2) विद्युत् (f.), atmospheric e.:<BR>*वायवविद्युत्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

electrify
ELECTRIFY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>to e. a jar:<BR>*घटं तडित्वन्तं<BR> करोति।<BR>II Fig., to surprise: परं विस्मयं जनयति<BR>(c. of जन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

electuary
ELECTUARY: अवलेहः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eleemosynary
ELEEMOSYNARY: i. e. relating to or founded<BR>or supported by charity: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elegance
ELEGANCE:<BR>(1) चारुता: v. Beauty;<BR>(2) माधुर्यम्<BR>(of style, etc.), Kav.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elegant
ELEGANT:<BR>(1) चारु (f. र्वी): v. Beautiful;<BR>(2)<BR>मधुरः (रा, रं) (of style, manners, etc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elegantly
ELEGANTLY:<BR>(1) चारु;<BR>(2) मधुरम्;<BR>(3) सुललितम्<BR>(of movements, etc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elegiac
ELEGIAC: करुणार्थग्रथितः (ता, तं), and sim.<BR>comp.s. E. metre (in Sanskrit): वियोगिनी-<BR>वृत्तम्, M.n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elegy
ELEGY: करुणार्थग्रथितं काव्यम् (= poem)<BR>or<BR>गीतम्<BR>(= song).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

element
ELEMENT:<BR>I An e. ary substance:<BR>(1) भूतम्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">Page233</a>]<BR>sky, etc. are the five e.s:<BR>पञ्चभूतानि वियदादीनि,<BR>D. s.;<BR>the sixth of the great e. s:<BR>भूतानां महतां षष्ठः,<BR>R.;<BR>(2) मूलपदार्थः।<BR>II Rudiments: q. v.:<BR>e. s of grammer:<BR>व्याकरणसारः<BR>or<BR>लघुव्याकरणम्।<BR>III<BR>The proper sphere: Ph.: he is out of his e.:<BR>*न स्वभूमौ वर्तते सः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elementary
ELEMENTARY: Ph.:<BR>e. substance:<BR>मूलपदार्थः;<BR>e.<BR>instruction:<BR>वार्तामात्रावबोधनम्, D.; e. treatise:<BR>लघुप्रबन्धः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elephant
ELEPHANT:<BR>(1) गजः,<BR>e. -catcher:<BR>गजबन्धः, Vet.;<BR>a<BR>wild e.:<BR>वनगजः;<BR>(2) हस्तिन् (m.);<BR>(3) करिन्<BR>(m.);<BR>(4) मातङ्गः;<BR>(5) कुञ्जरः;<BR>(6) नागः;<BR>(7)<BR>वारणः;<BR>a rutting e.:<BR>मत्तवारणः;<BR>(8) दन्तिन् (m.);<BR>(9) द्विपः,<BR>a newly caught e.:<BR>नवग्रहो द्विपः, D.<BR>ii.;<BR>a musk -e.:<BR>गन्धद्विपः। A she -e.:<BR>(1)<BR>करिणी;<BR>(2) हस्तिनी;<BR>(3) गजवशा;<BR>(4) करेणु<BR>(f.).<BR>A young e.:<BR>कर(ल)भः। The leader of a<BR>(wild) herd (of e.s): यूथनाथः<BR>or<BR>यूथपः। A large<BR>fine e.:<BR>(1) गजेन्द्रः;<BR>(2) गजपुङ्गवः;<BR>(3) करेणुवर्यः।<BR>The roaring of an e.:<BR>बृंहितम्। Its trunk:<BR>(1) करः;<BR>(2) शुण्डः;<BR>(3) हस्तः (rare).<BR>Its<BR>frontal globes:<BR>कुम्भौ (m. dual). Its temple:<BR>(1) गण्डः;<BR>(2) कटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elephant-apple
ELEPHANT-APPLE:<BR>(1) कपित्थः;<BR>(2) दधित्थः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elephant-driver
ELEPHANT-DRIVER:<BR>(1) आधोरणः;<BR>(2) हस्तिपकः;<BR>(3) महामात्रः, Mr.;<BR>(4) गजस्य यन्ता<BR>or<BR>नियन्ता, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elephantiasis
ELEPHANTIASIS: a disease of the leg: श्लीपदम् or<BR>शिलीपदम्,<BR>one effected with e.<BR>श्लीपदिन् (f. नी), M.<BR>iii. 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elephantine
ELEPHANTINE: expr. by comp., e. epoch:<BR>*हस्तियुगम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elevate
ELEVATE:<BR>I To raise: q. v.: उन्नमयति (c. of<BR>नम्).<BR>II To exalt: q. v.: उन्नमयति। E. d.:<BR>i. e. lofty: q. v.: उन्नतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elevation
ELEVATION:<BR>I Rising:<BR>(1) उन्नमनम्;<BR>(2)<BR>उत्तोलनम्।<BR>II Loftiness: q. v.: उन्नतत्वम्, K.<BR>III Of ground: उन्नतभूमिः: v. Height.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eleven
ELEVEN: एकादशन् (mfn.).<BR>E. times:<BR>एकादशवारान्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eleventh
ELEVENTH:<BR>I Adj.; एकादशः (शी, शं).<BR>II<BR>Subs.: एकादशभागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elf
ELF: डाकिनी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elfin
ELFIN, ELFISH:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by comp.<BR>II<BR>Fig.: v. Mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elf-lock
ELF-LOCK: जटा,<BR>e.s:<BR>जटाजूटः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elicit
ELICIT:<BR>(1) निर्हरति, (हृ, c. 1.) (= bring out);<BR>(2) निष्कर्षति (कृष्, c. 1.) (= draw out).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elide
ELIDE: लुम्पति (लुप्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eligibility
ELIGIBILITY:<BR>I Lit.: *निर्वाच्याधिकारः।<BR>II<BR>Worthiness: q. v.: योग्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eligible
ELIGIBLE:<BR>I Lit.: निर्वाच्याधिकारिन् (f. णी).<BR>II<BR>Worthy: q. v.: योग्य (f. ग्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eliminate
ELIMINATE: निष्कासयति (c. of कस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elimination
ELIMINATION: निष्कासनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elision
ELISION: लोपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elite
ELITE: मुख्याः (m. pl.); रत्नानि (n. pl.)<BR>(= gems.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elixir
ELIXIR:<BR>I Lit.: रसायनम्।<BR>II Fig.: सारः,<BR>the<BR>e. of wives:<BR>दारसारः, N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elk
ELK: ऋष्यः (?); हरिणविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ell
ELL: मानविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ellipse
ELLIPSE: *अण्डवृत्तम्<BR>or<BR>उपवृत्तम्<BR>or<BR>उपमण्डलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ellipsis
ELLIPSIS: न्यूनपदम्, Kav.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ellipsoid
ELLIPSOID: *अण्डवृत्तस्थूलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elliptic
ELLIPTIC, -AL:<BR>I Rhet: न्यूनपदः (दा, दं).<BR>II Geo.: expr. by comp.,<BR>e. motion:<BR>*उप-<BR>वृत्तगतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elliptically
ELLIPTICALLY: expr. by circumlo: v. Want-<BR>-ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elm
ELM: वन्यपादपविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elocution
ELOCUTION:<BR>I The power of speech:<BR>वाक्शक्तिः।<BR>II Delivery: व्याहारः।<BR>III Elo-<BR>-quence: वाग्मिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elongate
ELONGATE: दीर्घीकरोति: v. To lengthen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elongation
ELONGATION:<BR>I Extension: विततिः।<BR>II<BR>Distance: q. v.: विप्रकर्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elope
ELOPE: पलायते (पलाय्, c. 1.): v. To run<BR>away. Ph.:<BR>she e. d with him:<BR>तेन सह देशान्तरं<BR> जगाम (after D.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elopement
ELOPEMENT: पलायनम्: v. Flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eloquence
ELOQUENCE:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) वाग्मिता;<BR>(2)<BR>वाक्पाटवम्।<BR>II Of address, etc.: perh.<BR>प्रौढत्वम, Ma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eloquent
ELOQUENT:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) वाग्मिन् (f. नी),<BR>at<BR>the head of the e.:<BR>वाग्मिनां धुरि, Ki.;<BR>(2) वाक्य-<BR>कोविदः (दा, दं), M. n.; and sim. comp. s.<BR>II Of speeches, etc.: perh. प्रौढः (ढा, ढं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eloquently
ELOQUENTLY:<BR>(1) प्रौढम् (?);<BR>(2) सपाटवम्<BR>(= skilfully);<BR>(3) वाग्विलासेन (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

else
ELSE (conj.):<BR>(1) अन्यथा;<BR>(2) इतरथा: v.<BR>Otherwise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

else
ELSE (adj.): Ph.:<BR>who e.:<BR>कोऽन्यः<BR>or<BR>कोऽपरः, K.;<BR>what e.:<BR>किमन्यत्<BR>or<BR>किमपरम्, Ma.<BR>or<BR>किमितः परम्,<BR>Ra.;<BR>something e.:<BR>अन्यत् किञ्चित्, Ana;<BR>some-<BR>where e.:<BR>अन्यत्र कुत्रापि, N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elsewhere
ELSEWHERE:<BR>(1) अन्यत्र;<BR>(2) अन्यतः, R. v. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elucidate
ELUCIDATE:<BR>(1) उद्भासयति (c. of मास्);<BR>(2)<BR>विशदीकरोति (कृ, c. 8.): v. To explain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elucidation
ELUCIDATION:<BR>(1) उद्भासनम्;<BR>(2) विशदीकरणम्:<BR>v. Explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elucidator
ELUCIDATOR: उद्भासकः,: v. Interpreter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elude
ELUDE:<BR>(1) कौशलेन परिहरति (हृ, c. 1.);<BR>(2)<BR>मोघीकरोति (= to frustrate: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elysian
ELYSIAN: स्वर्गीयः (या, यं) (= heavenly: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

elysium
ELYSIUM: स्वर्गः (= heaven); वैकुण्ठम् (of Viṣṇu).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emaciate
EMACIATE:<BR>I To make lean:<BR>(1) कर्शयति,<BR> परि-, (c. of कृश्)<BR>or<BR>कृशीकरोति,<BR>e. d. by disfigure-<BR>ment:<BR>वैरूप्यकर्शितः (ता, तं), Ram.;<BR>(2)<BR>क्षिणोति, परि-, (क्षि, c. 5.), the disease e.d him:<BR>आमयस्तमक्षिणोत्, R.<BR>II To become lean:<BR>(1)<BR>कृशीमवति<BR>or<BR>कृश्यति, परि-, (कृश्, c. 4.);<BR>(2)<BR>क्षीयते (pass. of क्षि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emaciate
EMACIATE (adj.): परिकृशः (शा, शं): v. Lean,<BR>thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emaciation
EMACIATION:<BR>(1) कृशता;<BR>(2) कार्श्यम्;<BR>(3) क्षामता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emanate
EMANATE:<BR>I To flow from: q. v.: उद्गच्छति<BR>(गम्, c. 1.).<BR>II To arise, originate: q. v.:<BR>उद्गच्छति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emanation
EMANATION:<BR>I The act: उद्गमः; निर्गमः।<BR>II<BR>That which comes out: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emancipate
EMANCIPATE: मोचयति<BR>or<BR>मोक्षयति, वि-, (मुच् or<BR>मोक्ष् c. 10.),<BR>you will be e. d from the bond of<BR>the world:<BR>भवबन्घाद्विमोक्ष्यसे, V. c.;<BR>they should<BR>be e. d by the king:<BR>राज्ञा मोचयितव्यास्ते, M. p.:<BR>v. To liberate, free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emancipation
EMANCIPATION: मोक्षः;<BR>e. of slaves:<BR>दासस्य मोक्षः,<BR>Viv.: v. Liberation, release.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emancipator
EMANCIPATOR: मोचयितृ (f. त्री): v. Libera-<BR>-tor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emasculate
EMASCULATE:<BR>I Lit., to castrate: पुंस्त्वं हन्ति,<BR> उप-, प्रति-, (हन्, c. 2.), V. s.<BR>II Fig.: v.<BR>To Weaken, Enervate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emasculate-d
EMASCULATE-D (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: हतपुंस्त्वः।<BR>II<BR>Fig.: हतवीर्य (f. र्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emasculator
EMASCULATOR:<BR>(1) पुंस्त्वस्य प्रतिघातकृत्, Y., and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embalm
EMBALM:<BR>(1) रक्षति (रक्ष्, c. 1.),<BR>therefore (they)<BR>e. the king:<BR>ततो रक्षन्ति भूमिपम्, Ram.;<BR>(2)<BR>तैले निक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.) (to e. in oil), B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embalmer
EMBALMER: expr. by verb: v. Above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embank
EMBANK: वप्रेण बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embankment
EMBANKMENT: वप्रबन्धः (?): v. Mound, bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embargo
EMBARGO: निषेधः<BR>or<BR>प्रस्थाननिषेधः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embark
EMBARK (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) नौकायाम् आरोपयति<BR>(c. of रुह्)<BR>or<BR>निदधाति (धा, c. 3.) (= put on<BR>board),<BR>e. ing them all:<BR>अस्यां निधाय सर्वास्तान्,<BR>Mat.;<BR>(2) नौकया प्रस्थापयति (c. of स्था) (= to<BR>send by boat).<BR>II To engage: व्यापारयति<BR>(c. of पृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embark
EMBARK (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) नावं<BR>or<BR>पोतम् आ-<BR>रोहति, अधि-, (रुह्, c. 1.) etc.,<BR>without e. ing<BR>on a vessel:<BR>पोताधिरोहेण विनैव, Tar.;<BR>(2) नौकया<BR> प्रतिष्ठते (स्था, c. 1.) (= to depart).<BR>II To<BR>engage: व्याप्रियते (पृ, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embarkation
EMBARKATION: नौकारोहणम् (going)<BR>or<BR>नोकारोपणम्<BR>(putting on board); प्रस्थानम् (= departure).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embarrass
EMBARRASS:<BR>(1) आकुलयति (= to perplex),<BR>affection e. es Śatānanda:<BR>स्नेहः शतानन्दमाकुलयति,<BR>An.;<BR>(2) मोहयति, वि-, प्र-, व्या-, (c. of मुह्)<BR>(= to confound), I. am e. ed seeing (this) evil:<BR>अनर्थमुत्प्रेक्ष्य प्रमुग्धोऽस्मि, An.<BR>(3) बाधते (= to<BR>hinder, annoy), Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embarrassment
EMBARRASSMENT:<BR>(1) व्याकुलता;<BR>(2) प्रमोहः;<BR>(3) बाधा;<BR>(4) विषमम् (= difficulty: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embassador
EMBASSADOR: v. Ambassador.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embassy
EMBASSY:<BR>I Lit.: दौत्यम्<BR>or<BR>दूत्यम्।<BR>II The<BR>dwelling of an ambassador: दूतावासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embattled
EMBATTLED:<BR>(1) विन्यस्तः (स्ता, स्तं);<BR>(2) विर-<BR>चितः (ता, तं). Ph.:<BR>e. field:<BR>युद्धक्षेत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embedded
EMBEDDED:<BR>(1) निहितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) न्यस्त (f.<BR>स्ता);<BR>(3) निविष्ट (f. ष्टा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embellish
EMBELLISH: विभूषयति (भूष्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embellishment
EMBELLISHMENT: विभूषणम्: v. Adornment,<BR>ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embers
EMBERS: मस्मन् (n.): v. Ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ember-day
EMBER-DAY; उपवासदिवसः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embezzle
EMBEZZLE: छन्नम् आत्मसात्करोति (कृ, c. 8.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embezzlement
EMBEZZLEMENT: छन्नमात्मसात्करणम्; स्तेयम् (= theft).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embezzler
EMBEZZLER: छन्नमात्मसात्कर्तृ (f. र्त्री): v. Also<BR>thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embitter
EMBITTER:<BR>I Lit.: तिक्तायते (nomi.).<BR>II To<BR>distress: क्लिश्नाति (क्लिश्, c. 9.).<BR>III To<BR>exasperate: उत्कोपयति (c. of कुप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emblazon
EMBLAZON:<BR>(1) मण्डयति (मण्ड्, c. 10.);<BR>(2)<BR>विभूषयति (भूष्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emblazonry
EMBLAZONRY: पताकादिभिः मण्डनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emblem
EMBLEM:<BR>(1) लक्षणम्;<BR>(2) लाञ्छनम्;<BR>(3) लिङ्गम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emblematic
EMBLEMATIC.-AL: expr. by emblem: v.<BR>Symbolic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emblematically
EMBLEMATICALLY: लक्षणेन (?): v. Also figura-<BR>-tively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embodiment
EMBODIMENT:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by verb.<BR>II<BR>Representation: Ph.:<BR>e. of virtue:<BR>सशरीरो<BR> धर्मः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embody
EMBODY: Lit.: देहेन<BR>or<BR>शरीरेण युनक्ति (युज्, c. 7.).<BR>II To collect: q. v.: समाहरति (हृ, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embolden
EMBOLDEN: साहसं जनयति (जन्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>encourage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emboss
EMBOSS: उच्चरेखादिना तक्षति। (तक्ष्, c. 1.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embowel
EMBOWEL:<BR>I To eviscerate: अन्त्राणि अपनयति<BR>(नी, c. 1.): v. To remove.<BR>II To em-<BR>-balm: q. v.<BR>III To busy: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embowered
EMBOWERED: कुञ्जितः (ता, तं), नि-,।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embrace
EMBRACE (v.):<BR>I To clasp:<BR>(1) आ-लिङ्गति,<BR> समा-, (लिङ्ग्, c. 1.),<BR>the father e. d him with<BR>open arms:<BR>प्रसारितभुजयुगलस्तं पितालिलिङ्ग, K.<BR>(2)<BR>आश्लिष्यति, समा-, सं-, उप-, (श्लिष्, c. 4.),<BR>e. d<BR>the pillar for a moment:<BR>क्षणं स्तम्भमाश्लिषत्, Si.;<BR>(3) स्वजते, परि-, (स्वञ्ज्, c. 1.), e. ing her firmly:<BR>तां दृढं परिष्वज्य, D.;<BR>(4) उपगूहति (गुह्, c. 1.),<BR>as<BR>if e. ing me with cool breezes:<BR>शिशिरानिलैर्मामुप-<BR>गूहतीव, R.;<BR>(5) परिरभते (रभ, c. 1.),<BR>was (it)<BR>e. d with the eyes:<BR>परिरेभे नु विलोचनाभ्याम्, Ki.<BR>II<BR>To comprise: q. v.: क्रोडीकरोति,<BR>from (its) e.<BR>ing also another sense:<BR>अर्थान्तरस्यापि क्रोडीकरणात्,<BR>Kuv.<BR>III To accept: q. v.: परिगृह्नाति (ग्रह्,<BR>c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embrace
EMBRACE (subs.):<BR>(1) आलिङ्गनम्;<BR>(2) आश्लेषः;<BR>(3) परिरम्भः;<BR>(4) परिष्वङ्गः;<BR>(5) उपगूहनम्;<BR>(6)<BR>आलिङ्गितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embrasure
EMBRASURE: छिद्रम् (= any aperture).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embrocate
EMBROCATE:<BR>(1) मृद्राति (मृद्, c. 9.);<BR>(2) संवा-<BR>हयति (c. of वह्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embrocation
EMBROCATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) मर्दनम्, सं-;<BR>(2) संवाहनम्।<BR>II A lotion for e.: expr. by<BR>comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embroider
EMBROIDER: Ph.:<BR>e. ed cloth:<BR>कार्मिकवस्त्रम्;<BR>he<BR>knows how to e. cloth:<BR>वस्त्रोपरि कर्म कर्तुं जानाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embroiderer
EMBROIDERER: कार्मिकवस्त्रकारः, and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embroidery
EMBROIDERY:<BR>I Variegated needle-work:<BR>Ph.:<BR>this is gold e.:<BR>*स्वर्णकर्मैतत्: v. To<BR>embroider.<BR>II Fig., decoration: अलङ्कारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embroil
EMBROIL: आकुलीकरोति: v. To confound,<BR>perplex.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embroilment
EMBROILMENT: संक्षोभः: v. Confusion, perple-<BR>-xity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embryo
EMBRYO:<BR>I Lit.: गर्भः<BR>or<BR>अपरिणतगर्भः।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>this work is in e.:<BR>अपरिणतेयं कृतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

embryonic
EMBRYONIC, EMBRYOTIC: अपरिणतः (ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emend
EMEND: शोधयति (c. of शुध्): v. To correct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emendation
EMENDATION: शुद्धिः: v. Correction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emendator
EMENDATOR: शोधकः, सं-, वि-, परि-,।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emerald
EMERALD (subs.):<BR>(1) मरकतः;<BR>(2) हरिण्मणिः;<BR>(3) गारुत्मतम् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emerald
EMERALD (adj.):<BR>(1) expr. by tat.;<BR>(2) भार-<BR>कतः (ती, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emerge
EMERGE: उन्मज्जति (मस्ज्, c. 6.),<BR>e. ing from the<BR>river of arrows:<BR>बाणनद्या उन्मज्जन्, Ki.;<BR>slowly<BR>e. d from the eastern ocean:<BR>पूर्वपयोधेः शनकैरुन्ममज्ज,<BR>Ki.: v. To rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emergence
EMERGENCE: उन्मज्जनम्: v. Rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emergency
EMERGENCY:<BR>I Crisis, occasion: q. v.: सङ्कटम्।<BR>II Exigency: q. v.: प्रयोजनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emergent
EMERGENT:<BR>I Lit.: उन्मज्जत् (f. ती).<BR>II<BR>Critical: Ph.:<BR>e. business:<BR>आत्ययिकं कार्यम्, H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emersion
EMERSION:<BR>I Lit.: उन्मज्जनम्।<BR>II Astro.:<BR>मोक्षः, Su.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emery
EMERY: अश्मसारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emetic
EMETIC: वान्तिकरः (री, रं), and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emigrant
EMIGRANT: *निर्वासिन् (f. नी); स्वदेशत्यागिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emigrate
EMIGRATE: *निर्वसति (वस्, c. 1.),<BR>e. d to<BR>America:<BR>आमेरिकां निरूषुः; वासर्थं देशान्तरं गच्छति,<BR> व्रजति, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emigration
EMIGRATION: *निर्वासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eminence
EMINENCE:<BR>I A height: q. v.: उन्नतभूमिः।<BR>II<BR>Exaltation: q. v.:<BR>(1) उत्कर्षः<BR>or<BR>प्रकर्षः;<BR>(2)<BR>उन्नतिः, सम्-।<BR>III As a title: भगवत् (f. ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eminent
EMINENT:<BR>(1) उत्कृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं): v. Excellent;<BR>(2) विश्रुतः (ता, तं): v. Celebrated;<BR>(3)<BR>असाधारण (f. णी): v. Uncommon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eminently
EMINENTLY:<BR>(1) अति- in comp.: v. Exceed-<BR>-ingly;<BR>(2) विशिष्टम्: v. Especially;<BR>(3)<BR>शोभनम्: v. Well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emissary
EMISSARY:<BR>(1) चरः;<BR>(2) चारः;<BR>(3) प्रणिधिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emission
EMISSION:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मोक्षः;<BR>(2) विसर्जनम्;<BR>(3) निर्गम्ः<BR>or<BR>निष्क्रमः (= coming out);<BR>(4)<BR>उद्गारः (= throwing up);<BR>(5) स्रावः (=flow).<BR>II Animal: रेतस्खलनम्, रेतःस्रुतिः; रेतःक्षरणम्;<BR> वीर्यनिषेकः; etc. Ph.:<BR>he had e.:<BR>अस्य रेतः<BR> चस्कन्द<BR>or<BR>सुस्राव, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emit
EMIT (v.):<BR>(1) मुञ्चति निर्-, वि-, प्र-, (मुच्, c. 6.),<BR>e. ted steam:<BR>उष्माणममुञ्चत्, Ku.; to e. water:<BR>अपो मुञ्चति, Ki.;<BR>(2) विसृजति (सृज्, c. 6.),<BR>to<BR>e. fire:<BR>अग्निं विसृजति, Sa.: v. To send forth,<BR>throw out, vomit. To be e. ted.: i. e. to<BR>come out: q. v.: निः- सरति, प्र-, (सृ, c. 1.),<BR>from the bow arrows were e. ted:<BR>धनुषः शराः<BR> प्रसस्रुः, Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emmet
EMMET: पिपीलिका: v. Ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emollient
EMOLLIENT:<BR>I Adj.: स्नेहनः (नी, नं).<BR>II<BR>Subs.: स्नेहनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emolument
EMOLUMENT: लाभः: v. Gain, salary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emotion
EMOTION:<BR>I Feeling: q. v.: रसः, the tender e.:<BR>करुणरसः, U.<BR>II Excitement: q. v.:<BR>(1) विकारः,<BR> विकृतिः,<BR>or<BR>विक्रिया, seeing the e. s (of Nala)<BR>of holy fame:<BR>पुण्यश्लोकस्य विकारं दृष्ट्वा, Mah.;<BR>(2) अपकृतिः (rare), unable to control her e. s:<BR>अपकृतीर्विनियन्तुमक्षमा, Ki. i. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

empale
EMPALE:<BR>I To enclose: q. v.<BR>II To put to<BR>death: शूलं<BR>or<BR>शूले<BR>or<BR>शूलायाम् आरोपयति (c. of<BR>रुह्), P.; शूले निवेशयति (c. of विश्), Viv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emperor
EMPEROR:<BR>(1) सम्राज् (m.);<BR>(2) महाराजः;<BR>(3)<BR>अधिराजः;<BR>(4) राजराजः;<BR>(5) राजाधिराजः;<BR>(6)<BR>राजेन्द्रः;<BR>(7) अधीश्वरः;<BR>(8) सार्वभौमः (rare),<BR>e. of<BR>the gods:<BR>देवतासार्वभौमः, Kuv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emphasis
EMPHASIS: शक्त्युत्कर्षद्योतकोक्तिः, (after Tārā-<BR>-nāth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emphasise
EMPHASISE: शक्त्युत्कर्षद्योतनाय द्रढयति (nomi.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emphatic
EMPHATIC:<BR>(1) दृढः (ढा, ढं) (= firm);<BR>(2)<BR>निश्चितः (ता, तं) (= certain);<BR>(3) सबलः (ला,<BR> लं) (= forcible).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emphatically
EMPHATICALLY:<BR>(1) दृढम् (= firmly);<BR>(2) निश्चितम्<BR>(= certainly):<BR>(3) बलात् (=forcibly);<BR>(4)<BR>सगौरवम् (= gravely).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

empire
EMPIRE:<BR>(1) साम्राज्यम्;<BR>(2) अधिराज्यम् (rare):<BR>v. Kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

empiric
EMPIRIC (subs.):<BR>I A quack: कुवैद्यः।<BR>II An<BR>examiner: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

empirical
EMPIRICAL:<BR>I In good sense: दर्शनसिद्ध (f.<BR>द्धा).<BR>II In bad s.: असिद्धः (द्धा, द्धं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

empirically
EMPIRICALLY:<BR>I In good sense: बहुदर्शनेन।<BR>II In bad s.: अविद्यया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

empiricism
EMPIRICISM: i. e. quackery: अशास्त्रचिकित्सा (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

employ
EMPLOY (subs.): v. Employment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

employ
EMPLOY (v. t.):<BR>I To use: q. v.: प्रयुंक्ते।<BR>II<BR>To commission:<BR>(1) नियुंक्ते<BR>or<BR>योजयति (युज्, c.<BR>7. and 10.), e. (me)<BR>without any hesitation in<BR>what are to be done:<BR>कर्तव्येष्वविशङ्कितया नियुज्यताम्,<BR>K.;<BR>(2) व्यापारयति (c. of पृ),<BR>e. ed to break<BR>their confederacy:<BR>तत्संहतिभेदाय व्यापारिताः, Mu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

employee
EMPLOYEE:<BR>(1) अधिकृतः;<BR>(2) नियोज्यः, Sa.:<BR>v. Officer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

employer
EMPLOYER:<BR>(1) नियोजकः;<BR>(2) प्रयोजकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

employment
EMPLOYMENT:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्रयोगः;<BR>(2) नियोगः।<BR>II Occupation: कर्मन् (n.),<BR>to dismiss from<BR>an e.:<BR>कर्मणोऽपकर्षति, Mah.: v. Service,<BR>livelihood, office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emporium
EMPORIUM: वाणिज्यस्थानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

empower
EMPOWER: क्षमतां ददाति (दा, c. 3.): v. To<BR>authorize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

empress
EMPRESS:<BR>(1) अधिराज्ञी;<BR>(2) महाराज्ञी;<BR>(3) राज-<BR>राजेश्वरी;<BR>(4) राजाधिराज्ञी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emptiness
EMPTINESS:<BR>I Lit.: शून्यता;<BR>(2) रिक्तता।<BR>II<BR>Fig.: असारता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

empty
EMPTY (adj.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) शून्यः (न्या, न्यं),<BR>परि-,<BR>the street is e.:<BR>शून्यो राजमार्गः, Mr. i.;<BR>today my bed is e.:<BR>परिशून्यं शयनीयमद्य मे, R.;<BR>(2) रिक्तः (क्ता, क्तं) (rare),<BR>in the e. mouth of<BR>the quiver:<BR>रिक्ते निषङ्गवक्त्रे, Ki.<BR>II Fig.: असारः<BR>(रा, रं),<BR>in this e. world:<BR>असारे संसारे, Va.: v.<BR>Vain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

empty
EMPTY (v. t.):<BR>(1) शून्यीकरोति;<BR>(2) रिक्तीकरोति,<BR>e. ing tanks:<BR>रिक्तीकुर्वन् सरांसि, K.<BR>(3) रिणक्ति<BR>(रिच्, c. 7.) (rare), B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

empty
EMPTY (v. i.): शून्यीभवति, D. Ph.:<BR>the rivers quick-<BR>ly e. themselves in the ocean:<BR>प्रयान्ति नद्यस्त्वरितं<BR> पयोनिधिम्, Ri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

empty-handed
EMPTY-HANDED:<BR>(1) शून्यहस्तः (स्ता, स्तं);<BR>(2)<BR>रिक्तहस्तः (स्ता, स्तं), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

empty-headed
EMPTY-HEADED: शून्यमस्तिष्कः (ष्का, ष्कं), and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

empyreal
EMPYREAL: तेजोमयः (यी, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

empyrean
EMPYREAN: वैकुण्ठम् (?); तेजोलोकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emulate
EMULATE: स्पर्धते (स्पर्ध्, c. 1.),<BR>the accused Rāk-<BR>ṣasa is e. ing me:<BR>मया सह स्पर्धते राक्षसहतकः, Mu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emulation
EMULATION: स्पर्धा,<BR>as if in e. of the waters of the<BR>celestial rivers:<BR>दिव्यसरिदम्बुपद्धतिस्पर्धयेव, Si.: v.<BR>Also rivalry, contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emulative
EMULATIVE, EMULATORY: v. Emulous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emulator
EMULATOR: स्पर्धिन् (f. नी), प्रति-,: v. Rival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emulous
EMULOUS: स्पर्धिन् (f. नी),<BR>E. of:<BR>स्पर्धया: v.<BR>Emulation. To be e. of: v. To emulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

emulously
EMULOUSLY: स्पर्धया, स्पर्धापूर्वकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enable
ENABLE: शक्तिं, सामर्थ्यं<BR>or<BR>क्षमतां ददाति (दा, c. 3.),<BR>better by circumlo.; it will e. you to decamp:<BR>अनेन तवापसर्पणं शक्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enact
ENACT:<BR>I To decree: करोति,<BR>to e. laws:<BR>*विधीन्<BR> करोति।<BR>II To do, perform: q. v.: करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enactment
ENACTMENT:<BR>I The act: करणम्; निष्पादनम्।<BR>II A law: कृतिः (?); विधिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enactor
ENACTOR: कर्तृ (f. त्री): v. Doer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enamel
ENAMEL (subs.): *अनामिलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enamel
ENAMEL (v.): *अनामिलयति (nomi.); अनामिलेन<BR> रञ्जयति (रञ्ज्, c. 10.).<BR>E. ’d.:<BR>*अनामिलितः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enamour
ENAMOUR: Ph.:<BR>he is e. ed of her:<BR>अयमस्यामासक्त-<BR>भावः, D.;<BR>I am e. ed of these books:<BR>*एतेषु पुस्त-<BR>केषु बद्धभावोऽस्मि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encage
ENCAGE: पञ्जरे रुणद्धि, नि-, अव-, सं-, (रुध्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encamp
ENCAMP (v. i.): निविशते (विश्, c. 1.),<BR>preparing<BR>to e.:<BR>निवेष्टुमुद्यच्छमाना, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encamp
ENCAMP (v. t.): निवेशयति (c. of विश्),<BR>e. ed the<BR>forces:<BR>बलानि निवेशयामास, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encampment
ENCAMPMENT: निवेशः, R. v. 49.: v. Camp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enceinte
ENCEINTE: गर्भवती: v. Pregnant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enchain
ENCHAIN (v.): निगडैर्बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.)<BR>or<BR>संय-<BR>च्छति (यम्, c. 1.) (lit.), K. ;<BR>(2) निगडयति<BR>(nomi.), D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enchant
ENCHANT:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) वशीकरोति, Kuv.;<BR>(2)<BR>साधयति (c. of सिध्), D.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>to e. the<BR>hearers:<BR>शृण्वतां मनो हर्तुम्, R. xv. 64.: v. To<BR>charm, delight. E. ing: v. Charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enchanter
ENCHANTER:<BR>I A magician:<BR>(1) मायाविन्<BR>(m.);<BR>(2) मायाकारः।<BR>II A charmer: मोहनः<BR>or<BR>-कः, वि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enchantment
ENCHANTMENT:<BR>I The act: वशीकरणम्, K.<BR>II<BR>The practice: वश्यकर्मन् (n.), D. s.<BR>III Any<BR>thing enchanting: v. Charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enchantress
ENCHANTRESS:<BR>(1) मोहिनी;<BR>(2) मायाविनी (in<BR>bad sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encircle
ENCIRCLE:<BR>(1) परि-वेष्टयति (वेष्ट्, c. 10.),<BR>e.<BR>whatever be on the side:<BR>यत्पार्श्वतो भवति तत्परि-<BR>वेष्टयन्ति, P.;<BR>to e. in the arms:<BR>भुजाभ्यां परि-<BR>वेष्टयन्ति, D.;<BR>(2) परिगच्छति (गम्, c. 2.) (= to<BR>go round),<BR>e. d by the Vetravatī:<BR>वेत्रवत्या परिगता,<BR>K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enclose
ENCLOSE (v.):<BR>I To surround: q. v.: परि-<BR>वृणोति<BR>or<BR>वारयति (वृ, c. 5. or 10.).<BR>e. d. me with<BR>showers of arrows:<BR>शरवर्षैर्मां पर्यवारयन्, Mah.<BR>II To fence: q. v.: परिवृणोति।<BR>III To shut<BR>up, confine: q. v.<BR>IV To put in a case:<BR>सह प्रेरयति (ईर्, c. 10.) (= to send with).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enclosure
ENCLOSURE:<BR>I Fence: वृतिः, परि-,<BR>e. s of<BR>parks:<BR>उपवनवृतयः, Me.;<BR>over the e. s:<BR>वृतीनामुपरि,<BR>Si.<BR>II That which is enclosed:<BR>there was<BR>no e. s with letter:<BR>*पत्रेण सहितं न किञ्चित् प्रेरितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encomiast
ENCOMIAST: v. Eulogist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encomiastic
ENCOMIASTIC, -AL: v. Eulogistic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encomium
ENCOMIUM: स्तवः: v. Eulogy, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encompass
ENCOMPASS: परिवेष्टयति (वेष्ट्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>encircle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encore
ENCORE:<BR>I Adv.: पुनरभिनीयताम् (?).<BR>II Verb.:<BR>पुनरभिनीयतामिति वदति (वद्, c. 1.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encounter
ENCOUNTER (v. i.): संगच्छते (गम्, c. 1.),<BR>the<BR>two seas of armies e. ed:<BR>सेनाम्भोघी सञ्जग्माते,<BR>Si.: v. To meet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encounter
ENCOUNTER (v. t.):<BR>I To meet in opposition:<BR>(1) अभि- एति, आ-, (इ, c. 2.),<BR>footmen e. ed<BR>footmen:<BR>पत्तिः पत्तिमभीयाय रणाय, Ku.;<BR>horse e.<BR>ed horse:<BR>वाहमेयाय वाजी, Si.;<BR>(2) अभ्या-पतति<BR>(पत्, c. 1.), R. ;<BR>of the two armies coming up<BR>to e. each other:<BR>संग्रामाय सन्निपततः सैन्ययुगस्य,<BR>Ku.;<BR>(3) वि-गृह्वाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.) (= to fight),<BR>for<BR>whom we have e. ed enemies:<BR>यत्कृतेऽरीन् व्यगृह्वीम,<BR>B.<BR>II To struggle with: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encounter
ENCOUNTER (subs.):<BR>I A meeting: अभ्यागमः।<BR>II Conflict, battle: संयुगः।<BR>“for fierce e. s<BR>fit”:<BR>सांयुगीनः (ना, नं), V.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encourage
ENCOURAGE:<BR>(1) साहसं जनयति (जन्, c. 10.)<BR>(with gen.) (= to embolden);<BR>(2) आश्वासयति<BR>(c. of श्वस्) (= to cheer);<BR>(3) प्रोत्साहयति (c.<BR>of सह्) (= to incite).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encouragement
ENCOURAGEMENT:<BR>(1) आश्वासः, -नम्,<BR>it found no<BR>e. from the public:<BR>*साधारण्यादाश्वासं न लेभे;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रोत्साहः, -नम्,:<BR>“with good e.”<BR>सुप्रोत्साहनेन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encourager
ENCOURAGER:<BR>(1) आश्वासकः;<BR>(2) प्रोत्साहकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encouraging
ENCOURAGING:<BR>(1) आश्वासनः (नी, नं);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रोत्साहनः (नी, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encroach
ENCROACH:<BR>(1) गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.) (= to seize),<BR>your house has been e. ed upon by another croco-<BR>dile:<BR>त्वदीयं गृहमपरेण मकरेण गृहीतम्, D.;<BR>(2) हरति<BR>(हृ, c. 1.) (= to take);<BR>(3) अन्यायेन प्रविशति<BR>(विश्, c. 6.) (= to enter unlawfully);<BR>(4)<BR>न्यूनीकरोति (= to lessen).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encroachment
ENCROACHMENT:<BR>(1) ग्रहणम् (= seizing);<BR>(2)<BR>अन्यायप्रवेशः (= unlawful entry). Ph.:<BR>e. of a<BR>river:<BR>नदीसञ्चारः, Viv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encrust
ENCRUST: v. To incrust^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encumber
ENCUMBER:<BR>thus e. ed by you on all sides:<BR>आर्येणैवं<BR> सर्वतो निरुद्धचेष्टाप्रसरस्य, Mu.;<BR>e. ed estate:<BR>ऋणग्रस्ता<BR> सम्पत्तिः: v. To burden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encumbrance
ENCUMBRANCE: प्रतिबन्धः: v. Impediment,<BR>burden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encyclical
ENCYCLICAL: v. Circular,<BR>e. letter:<BR>*चक्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encyclopaedia
ENCYCLOPÆDIA: विद्याकोषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

encyclopaedic
ENCYCLOPÆDIC, -AL: Ph.:<BR>of learning:<BR>विद्या-<BR>सागरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

end
END (subs.):<BR>I Extreme point: अन्तः, (rarely<BR>पर्यन्तः, प्रान्तः, उपान्तः) at the e. of the journey:<BR>अध्वनोऽन्ते, R. xvi. 35.; e. of a martle:<BR>अंशुकान्तः, J.<BR>II Termination:<BR>(1) अन्तः or<BR>पर्यन्तः,<BR>at the e. of the year:<BR>संवत्सरान्ते, Mat.;<BR>distressing in the e.:<BR>पर्यन्तपरितापिन् (f. नी), Ki.;<BR>(2) अवसानम्,<BR>at the e. of the day:<BR>दिनावसाने,<BR>Sa.;<BR>(3) परिणामः<BR>or<BR>परिणतिः, pleasing in the e.:<BR>परिणामसुखः (खा, खं), Ki.<BR>III Conclusion:<BR>(1) अन्तः,<BR>at the e. of the sacrifice:<BR>सत्रान्ते, R.;<BR>(2) अवसानम्,<BR>at the beginning, middle or e.:<BR>आदौ<BR> मध्येऽवसाने वा, N.s. Ph.:<BR>put an e. to:<BR>समापयति<BR>(c. of आप्), Vi.<BR>IV Death, destruction:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) अन्तः,<BR>will surely meet his e.:<BR>अन्त-<BR>मवाप्स्यति ध्रुवम्, Ku. xv. 42.;<BR>(2) अवसानम्,<BR>at<BR>the e. of the head-man:<BR>मूलपुरुषावसाने, Sa.<BR>V<BR>Aim, object: q. v.: आशयः। Ph.: to no e.:<BR>निरर्थकम्;<BR>to the e. that<BR>॥॥॥॥एतदभिप्रायकः (का,<BR> कं).<BR>VI Remnant: अन्तः,<BR>in the morning, giving<BR>its e. s to the servants:<BR>प्रत्यूषे तदन्तं कर्मकरान् दत्त्वा, P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

end
END (v. t.):<BR>(1) अन्तं करोति (rare),<BR>the e. er of<BR>Kshatriyas:<BR>क्षत्रियान्तकरः, Vi.<BR>(2) समापयति (c.<BR>of आप्): v. To finish, complete. Ph.: e. er<BR>of the e. er (= death): अन्तकस्यान्तकः, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

end
END (v. i.):<BR>(1) expr. by subs.,<BR>this dynasty<BR>will e. in Sumitra:<BR>अयं वंशः सुमित्रान्तो भविष्यति,<BR>V. p.; (words)<BR>e. ing in the affix<BR>ई<BR>are femi-<BR>nine:<BR>ईप्रत्ययान्तः स्त्री स्यात्, S. k.;<BR>whether it will<BR>e. auspiciously or otherwise:<BR>कल्याणी परिणतिरस्तु<BR> वान्यथा वा, Vi.;<BR>(2) अवसीयते (pass. of सो)<BR>(rare),<BR>it will e. so:<BR>एवं किलावसीयते, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endanger
ENDANGER: i. e. to bring into danger: expr.<BR>by subs,<BR>it e. s my life:<BR>मम जीवितमनेन संशयमा-<BR>रोपितम्: v. Danger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endear
ENDEAR: i. e. to make dear: v. Dear and<BR>make.<BR>E. ing:<BR>प्रीतिकरः (री, रं); मधुरः (रा,<BR> रं) (= sweet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endearment
ENDEARMENT: i. e. blandishment:<BR>(1) हावः;<BR>(2) विलासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endeavour
ENDEAVOUR (v.):<BR>(1) यतते (यत्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>attempt;<BR>(2) उद्यच्छति, -ते (यम्, c. 1.),<BR>e. ing<BR>to go:<BR>उद्यच्छमाना गमनाय, R.;<BR>(3) व्यवस्यति (सो,<BR>c. 4.),<BR>who would e. to separate her:<BR>कस्तां पृथक्-<BR>कर्तुं व्यवस्येत्, Mu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endeavour
ENDEAVOUR (subs.):<BR>(1) उद्यमः;<BR>(2) व्यवसायः:<BR>v. Attempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ending
ENDING (subs.): अन्तः: v. End; to end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endive
ENDIVE: शाकप्रभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endless
ENDLESS:<BR>I Without end: अनन्तः (न्ता, न्तं),<BR>of e. prowess:<BR>अनन्तवीर्यः (र्या, र्यं), Ku.<BR>II<BR>Without an object: निरर्थकः (का, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endlessly
ENDLESSLY:<BR>(1) अनन्तम्: v. Incessantly;<BR>(2)<BR>निरर्थकम्: v. In vain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endorse
ENDORSE:<BR>I In gen. sense: पृष्ठे लिखति, अभि-,<BR>(लिख्, c. 6.),<BR>a debtor should e. payments on the<BR>bond:<BR>लेखस्य पृष्ठेऽभिलिखेद्दत्वा दत्त्वा धनं ऋणी, Y.<BR>II Fig.: of opinion, etc.: कक्षीकरोति, D.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endorsement
ENDORSEMENT: पृष्ठलिखितम्, this is my e.:<BR>*ममैतत् पृष्ठलिखितम्<BR>or<BR>मयैतत् पृष्ठे लिखितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endow
ENDOW:<BR>I Lit.: वृत्तिं ददाति (दा, c. 3.).<BR>II<BR>To furnish with: योजयति (युज्, c. 10.). E.<BR>ed with:<BR>(1) अन्वितः (ता, तं), सम्-,<BR>e. with<BR>reason:<BR>विवेकसमन्वितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) उपेतः (ता,<BR> तं);<BR>(3) युक्तः (क्ता, क्तं): v. To possess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endowment
ENDOWMENT:<BR>I The act: वृत्तिदानम्।<BR>II A<BR>settlement: वृत्तिः।<BR>III Talent, gift: शक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endue
ENDUE: v. Endow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endurable
ENDURABLE: सह्यः (ह्या, ह्यं): v. Tolerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endurance
ENDURANCE:<BR>I The habit of enduring:<BR>सहिष्णुता, प्र-,<BR>e. of troubles:<BR>क्लेशसहिष्णुता, Ka.<BR>II The act of e.:<BR>(1) सहनम्;<BR>(2) मर्षः, णम्-।<BR>III Lastingness: स्थायित्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endure
ENDURE (v. t.):<BR>(1) सहते, वि-, प्र-, all-e. ing:<BR>सर्वंसहः (हा, हं),<BR>I cannot e. the slur:<BR>अहमवर्णं<BR> सोढुन्नेशे, R.;<BR>e. s to live:<BR>जीवितुं विषहते, Ve.;<BR>(2)<BR>मर्षयति<BR>or<BR>मर्षति, -ते (मृष्, c. 10. 4. and<BR>1.),<BR>did not e. the horns:<BR>शृङ्गं न ममृषे, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

endure
ENDURE (v. i.): तिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.): v. To last,<BR>remain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enduring
ENDURING: i. e. lasting: स्थायिन् (f. नी), चिर-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enemy
ENEMY:<BR>(1) शत्रुः,<BR>who never made an e.:<BR>अजात-<BR>शत्रुः, Ve.;<BR>a prostrate e.:<BR>चरणनिपतितः शत्रः,<BR>Mr.;<BR>(2) रिपुः,<BR>attack on the e. s' side:<BR>रिपु-<BR>पक्षाभियोगः, Vi.;<BR>(3) वैरिन् (m.), great e.:<BR>वैरिवरः, Ku.;<BR>(4) अरिः, to the e. of Namuchi<BR>(i.e. Indra): नमुचेररये, R.;<BR>(5) अरातिः,<BR>victory over the e. s:<BR>अरातिषु जयः, Ki.;<BR>(6) द्विष्,<BR> विद्विष्,<BR>or<BR>द्विषत् (n.),<BR>e. s of gods:<BR>देवद्विषः, Ku.;<BR>(7) परः (an ambiguous term),<BR>by stronger<BR>e. s:<BR>बलवत्तरैः परैः, Ku.;<BR>(8) परिपन्थिन् (m.)<BR>(rare);<BR>(9) शात्रवः (rare): v. Opponent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

energetic
ENERGETIC:<BR>(1) वीर्यवत् (f. ती) (= strong,<BR>powerful);<BR>(2) तेजस्विन् (f. नी) (= spirited):<BR>v. Active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

energetically
ENERGETICALLY: सोत्साहम् (= eagerly);<BR>(2)<BR>सहतेजसा (= spiritedly);<BR>(3) वीर्यं समाश्रित्य<BR>(= vigorously);<BR>(4) अतन्द्रितम् (= actively).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

energy
ENERGY:<BR>(1) तेजः: v. Spirit;<BR>(2) वीर्यम्: v.<BR>Vigour, strength;<BR>(3) उद्योगः: v. Activity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enervate
ENERVATE (v.):<BR>(1) दुर्बलीकरोति;<BR>(2) वीर्यं हरति<BR>(हृ, c. 1.): v. To weaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enervate
ENERVATE, -D (adj.): हतवीर्य (f. र्या): v. Weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enervation
ENERVATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) दुर्बलीकरणम्;<BR>(2) वीर्यक्षयः।<BR>II The state:<BR>(1) हतवीर्यता;<BR>(2) निर्वीर्यता;<BR>(3) क्लैव्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enfeeble
ENFEEBLE: दुर्बलीकरोति, e. (the ministers)<BR>one by<BR>one:<BR>एकैकं दुर्बलीकुरु, Mah.: v. Feeble, to<BR>weaken, emaciate, break down.<BR>To be-<BR>come e. d:<BR>दुर्बलीभवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enfeeblement
ENFEEBLEMENT:<BR>I The act: दुर्बलीकरणम्।<BR>II<BR>Weakness: q. v.: दुर्बलता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enfeoff
ENFEOFF: Ph.:<BR>e. ed this estate to me:<BR>*भाटकेन<BR> भूमिमिमां मां सम्पूर्णमोगाय ददौ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enfeoffment
ENFEOFFMENT: expr. as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enforce
ENFORCE (v.):<BR>I To compel: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>force: q. v.<BR>III To give force to: प्रबलयति<BR>(nomi.); प्रबलं (f. लां) करोति।<BR>IV To carry<BR>out: अनुतिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.).<BR>V To confirm,<BR>support: q. v.: द्रढयति, (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enforcement
ENFORCEMENT: expr. by verb.: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enfranchise
ENFRANCHISE (v.):<BR>I To release: q. v.:<BR>मोक्षयति (मोक्ष, c. 10.).<BR>II To naturalize: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">Page240</a>]<BR>(1) पौराधिकारं ददाति (दा, c. 3.) (?);<BR>(2) पौरत्वं<BR> लम्मयति (c. of लभ्) (?).<BR>E. d:<BR>दत्तपौराधिकारः<BR>(रा, रं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enfranchisement
ENFRANCHISEMENT:<BR>I Release: q. v.: मोक्षः।<BR>II Admission to the freedom of a corpo-<BR>-ration: पौराधिकारदानम् (?); पौरत्वप्रतिपादनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engage
ENGAGE (v. t.):<BR>I To bind, pledge: q. v.:<BR>बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 7.).<BR>II To enlist: perh.<BR>भाटयति (= to hire); उत्थापयति (c. of स्था)<BR>(= raise).<BR>III To attract: q.v.: आकर्षति<BR>(कृष्, c. 1.).<BR>IV To occupy, employ: q. v.:<BR>व्यापारयति (c. of पृ).<BR>To be e. d:<BR>व्याप्रियते (पृ,<BR>c. 6.).<BR>E. d:<BR>व्यापृतः (ता, तं); सव्यापारः (रा,<BR> रं),<BR>in the daytime while e.:<BR>सव्यापारामहनि, Me.<BR>V. To encounter: q. v.: अभ्येति (इ, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engage
ENGAGE (v. i.):<BR>I To promise, undertake:<BR>q. v.: प्रतिशृणोति (श्रु, c. 8.). Ph.:<BR>she is e. d to<BR>me:<BR>मह्यं प्रतिश्रुता सा।<BR>II To enter in:<BR>when<BR>the ascetic e. d in fighting:<BR>मुनौ रणमुपेयुषि, Ki.;<BR>e. d in meditation;<BR>ध्याननिविष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>while<BR>they were e. d in the controversy:<BR>प्रवृत्ते च तयोर्वादे।:<BR>v. To Begin, enter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engagement
ENGAGEMENT:<BR>I A battle: q. v.: युद्धम्।<BR>II<BR>A promise to visit: Ph.:<BR>I have an e. today<BR>at his:<BR>*अद्य तद्गृहगमनं मया प्रतिश्रुतम्;<BR>I could<BR>not keep my e.:<BR>*नाहं प्रतिश्रुतं रक्षितुमशक्नोम्।<BR>III<BR>Betrothal: प्रतिश्रुतसम्बन्धः।<BR>IV Business: q. v.:<BR>(1) व्यापारः;<BR>(2) कार्यम्;<BR>(3) कृत्यम्।<BR>V Pledge:<BR>q. v.<BR>VI An obligation: q. v.<BR>VII The<BR>act of engaging: v. To engage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engaging
ENGAGING:<BR>(1) हृदयहारिन् (f. णी): v. Charming;<BR>(2) रम्यः (म्या, म्यं): v. Pleasant, delightful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engagingly
ENGAGINGLY: expr. by adj. or verb: v. To<BR>charm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engender
ENGENDER: जनयति: v. To beget, produce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engine
ENGINE: यन्त्रम्,<BR>military e.:<BR>युद्धयन्त्रम्; e. -driver<BR>*यन्त्रवाहकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engineer
ENGINEER: वास्तुविद्याविशारदः (?): v. E. ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engineering
ENGINEERING: वास्तुविद्या (?):<BR>Civil e.:<BR>पथ-<BR>प्रणाल्यादिनिर्माणविद्या (?).<BR>Military e.:<BR>वप्रपरिखादि-<BR>निर्माणविद्या (?).<BR>Mechanical e.:<BR>यन्त्रविद्या (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

english
ENGLISH: ईलण्डीयः (या, यं); इंरेजः (जा, जं),<BR>knows e.:<BR>*इंरेजीं जानाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

englishman
ENGLISHMAN: *इंलण्डदेशीयः, इंरेजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engraft
ENGRAFT: v. To ingraft, graft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engrained
ENGRAINED: v. Ingrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engrave
ENGRAVE:<BR>(1) मुद्रयति (मुद्र्, c. 10.),<BR>with my<BR>name e. d on it:<BR>मन्नामाक्षरमुद्रितः (ता, तं), A. r.;<BR>(2) उत्किरति (कृ, c. 6.),<BR>with name e. d. on the<BR>bezel:<BR>मणिबन्धनोत्कीर्णनामघेयः (या, यं), Sa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engraver
ENGRAVER: नामादिमुद्राकारिन् (f. णी) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engraving
ENGRAVING:<BR>I The art: नामादिमुद्राकर्मन् (n.)<BR>or<BR>-कला (?).<BR>II A print: expr. by मुद्रितः<BR>(ता, तं); उत्कीर्ण (f. र्णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engross
ENGROSS:<BR>I To thicken: q. v.<BR>II To copy<BR>in a large fair hand: स्पष्टाक्षरैः लिखति (लिख्,<BR>c. 6.) (?).<BR>III To absorb: q. v.: Ph.:<BR>it<BR>e. es my mind:<BR>अत्रासक्तं मे मनः।<BR>IV To buy up:<BR>परिक्रीणीते (क्री, c. 9.).<BR>V To assume: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engrosser
ENGROSSER:<BR>I A copyist: स्पष्टाक्षरलेखकः।<BR>II<BR>A fore-staller:<BR>(1) परिक्रयिन् (f. णी) (?);<BR>(2)<BR>पूर्वक्रेतृ (f. त्री) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

engulf
ENGULF:<BR>(1) ग्रसते (ग्रस्, c. 1.) (= to swallow);<BR>(2) प्लावयति (c. of प्लु) (= to drown).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enhance
ENHANCE: वर्द्धयति (c. of वृध्): v. To increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enhancement
ENHANCEMENT: v. Increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enharmonic
ENHARMONIC: एकतानिकः (की, कं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enigma
ENIGMA: प्रहेलिका: v. Riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enigmatic
ENIGMATIC, -AL: वक्रः (क्रा, क्रं): v. Obscure,<BR>ambiguous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enigmatically
ENIGMATICALLY: वक्रम्: v. Ambiguously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enjoin
ENJOIN:<BR>I To order: q. v.: शास्ति (शास्, c.<BR>2.).<BR>II To prohibit or restrain: q. v.:<BR>निषेधति (सिध्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enjoy
ENJOY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) भुनक्ति<BR>or<BR>भुंक्ते, उप-, परि-,<BR> अनु-, अधि-, (भुज्, c. 7.),<BR>e. my milk:<BR>पयो<BR> मदीयमुपभुंक्ष्व, R. ; e. s the kingdom of heaven:<BR>भुनक्ति स्वाराज्यम्, N;<BR>(2) अनुभवति (भू, c. 1.) (prop.<BR>to feel),<BR>e. ing all pleasures:<BR>सर्वसुखान्यनुभवन्तः,<BR>K.;<BR>(3) निर्विशति (विश्, c. 6.),<BR>e. the beauties<BR>of youth:<BR>यौवनश्रीर्निर्विश्यताम्, R.<BR>II Carnally:<BR>भुनक्ति, उप-, P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enjoyment
ENJOYMENT: भोगः, उप-, सं-, परि-,<BR>the desire of e.<BR>is over:<BR>निवृत्ता भोगेच्छा, J.;<BR>what an e. in those<BR>places:<BR>स सम्भोगो यस्तादृशेषु प्रदेशेषु, V.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enkindle
ENKINDLE: संधुक्षयति (धुक्ष्, c. 10.): v. Kindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enlarge
ENLARGE (v. t.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) वर्धयति (c. of<BR>वृध्): v. To increase;<BR>(2) विस्तारयति (c. of<BR>स्तृ): v. To extend.<BR>II To release: q. v.:<BR>मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enlarge
ENLARGE (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.: वर्धते (वृध्, c. 1.),<BR>the<BR>fish e. d there:<BR>स तत्र ववृधे मत्स्यः, Mah.: v. To<BR>increase, extend.<BR>II<BR>To e. upon:<BR>प्रपञ्चयति<BR>(पञ्च्, c. 10.),<BR>now we will e. on its different<BR>states:<BR>इदानी तस्यैवावस्थाभेदः प्रपञ्चयते, S.: v. To<BR>detail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enlargement
ENLARGEMENT<BR>I Extension, expansion:<BR>q. v.: वृद्धिः, वि-, R.<BR>II Release: q. v.: मोक्षः।<BR>III Expatiation: विस्तारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enlighten
ENLIGHTEN:<BR>I To lighten: q. v.: दीपयति (c.<BR>of दीप्).<BR>II To instruct: ज्ञानं ददाति (दा, c.<BR>3.) (= to give knowledge);<BR>(2) चक्षुरुन्मीलयति<BR>(c. of मील्) (= to open the eyes);<BR>(3)<BR>उद्भासयति (c. of भास्) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enlightened
ENLIGHTENED: perh. उद्भासितः (ता, तं): v.<BR>Educated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enlightenment
ENLIGHTENMENT: perh. संविद्, the Lord of e.:<BR>संविदामीशः, Ki.: v. Refinement, civilization.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enlist
ENLIST (v. t.):<BR>I To enroll: q. v.:<BR>(1) गृह्णाति<BR>(ग्रह्, c. 9.) (= to take);<BR>(2) उत्थापयति (c. of<BR>स्था) (= to raise).<BR>II To gain over: perh.<BR>निवेशयति (c. of विश्)<BR>or<BR>ग्राहयति (c. of ग्रह्),<BR>I<BR>will e. them in the cause of trust:<BR>*तान् सत्यार्थे<BR> निवेशयामि<BR>or<BR>सत्यपथं ग्राहयामि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enlist
ENLIST (v. i.):<BR>I To engage in: विशति, प्र-,<BR>(विश्, c. 6.).<BR>II To enter heartily in a<BR>cause: निविशते, अभि-, (विश्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enlistment
ENLISTMENT:<BR>I The act: v. To enlist.<BR>II<BR>A writing: *प्रवेशपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enliven
ENLIVEN:<BR>(1) उत्तेजयति (c. of तिज्) (= to excite:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(2) हर्षयति (c. of हृष्) (= to gladden:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enlivening
ENLIVENING: हर्षजननः (नी, नं): v. Joyful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enmity
ENMITY:<BR>(1) वैरम्,<BR>should not make e. with any<BR>one:<BR>न॥॥।वैरं कुर्वीत केनचित्, B. p.;<BR>e. to-<BR>wards Udāraka:<BR>उदारके वैरम्, D. ii.;<BR>(2) शत्रुता;<BR>(3) विद्वेषः;<BR>(4) शात्रवम्;<BR>(5) दौहृद्यम् (rare);<BR>(6)<BR>विरोधः (= feud).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ennoble
ENNOBLE:<BR>I To dignify:<BR>(1) उन्नमयति (c. of<BR>नम्);<BR>(2) उत्-कर्षति, प्र-, (कृष्, c. 1.);<BR>(3) उत्-<BR>श्राययति (c. of श्रि).<BR>II To raise to the nobi-<BR>-lity: *अनुराजं<BR>or<BR>अध्यार्यं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ennui
ENNUI: स्वेदः: v. Weariness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enormity
ENORMITY:<BR>I Greatness: घोरता।<BR>II An<BR>atrocious crime: q. v.: घोरपातकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enormous
ENORMOUS:<BR>I Inordinate: असाधारण (f. णी).<BR>II Great:<BR>(1) महाप्रमाण<BR>or<BR>बृहत्प्रमाण<BR>or<BR>अति-<BR>प्रमाण (f. णा) (= of e. size);<BR>(2) विशालः (ला,<BR> लं) (= large: q. v.)<BR>III Atrocious: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enormously
ENORMOUSLY: अत्यन्त- in comp.: v. Exceed-<BR>-ingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enough
ENOUGH:<BR>(1) अलम्; all this is not e. for one:<BR>सर्वं तन्नालमेकस्य, Mah.;<BR>e. of this story:<BR>अलमनया<BR> कथया, K.;<BR>(2) पर्याप्तः (प्ता, प्तं).<BR>I am e. for all<BR>the Rākṣasas in battle:<BR>सर्वेषामेव पर्याप्तो राक्षसाना-<BR>महं युधि, Ram.;<BR>and so much fuel is e. for cook-<BR>ing so much food:<BR>इयतश्चौदनस्य पाकायैतावदिन्धनं<BR> पर्याप्तम्, D.;<BR>(3) प्रचुरः (रा, रं) (= abundant).<BR>Ph.: and I have not had e. of (lit. not satiated<BR>with)<BR>youth:<BR>न च तृप्तोऽस्मि यौवने, Mat.;<BR>more<BR>than e. for hundred years' consumption:<BR>व्रर्षशतो-<BR>पभोगेऽप्यक्षय्यम्, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enquire
ENQUIRE:<BR>I To ask: q. v.: अनुयुंक्ते (युज्, c. 7.),<BR>e. d of him what was to be given and how much:<BR>किं प्रदेयं कियद्वेति तमन्वयुंक्त, R.<BR>II To seek to<BR>know: जिज्ञासते,<BR>we will now e. into the nature<BR>of spirit:<BR>प्राणः किंस्वरूप इतीदानीं जिज्ञास्यते, S.<BR>III To examine, consider: q. v.: अनुसन्द-<BR>धाति<BR>or<BR>धत्ते (धा, c. 3.),<BR>personally e. d into dis-<BR>putes:<BR>विवादान् स्वयमनुसन्दधौ, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enquiry
ENQUIRY:<BR>I Asking: अनुयोगः,<BR>whoever I may<BR>be (you) should make no e.:<BR>यास्मि सास्म्यानुयोगो<BR> मे न कर्तव्यः, Mah.<BR>II Seeking to know:<BR>जिज्ञासा,<BR>e. after duties:<BR>धर्मजिज्ञासा, M. d.;<BR>a<BR>subject of e.:<BR>जिज्ञास्यम्, S.<BR>III Examination,<BR>consideration: q. v.: अनुसन्धानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enrage
ENRAGE:<BR>(1) कोपयति, प्र-, सं-, (c. of कुप्),<BR>I will<BR>e. him:<BR>कोपयाम्येनम्, B. r.<BR>(2) क्रोधयति (c. of<BR>क्रुध्);<BR>(3) रोषयति (c. of रुष्);<BR>(4) कोपं जनयति<BR>(c. of जन्);<BR>(5) क्रोधं उत्पादयति (c. of पद्),<BR>K.;<BR>(6) संरम्भं नयति (नी, c. 1.), R.; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enraged
ENRAGED:<BR>(1) क्रुद्धः (द्धा, द्धं);<BR>(2) कुपितः (ता, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">Page242</a>]<BR>तं);<BR>(3) रुष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>(4) संरब्ध (f. ब्धा);<BR>(5) जातामर्षः (र्षा, र्षं);<BR>(6) आगतमन्यु (mfn.);<BR>etc. To be e.:<BR>(1) कुप्यति (कुप्, c. 4.): v.<BR>Angry, to be-;<BR>(2) क्रोधम् एति (इ, c. 2.);<BR>(3)<BR>मन्युं प्राप्नोति (आप्, c. 5.), Vi.; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enrapture
ENRAPTURE, ENRAVISH: प्रहर्षयति (c. of हृष्):<BR>v. To charm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enravishingly
ENRAVISHINGLY: प्रहर्षं जनयत् (f. न्ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enrich
ENRICH:<BR>I Lit.: धनिनं (f. नीं)<BR>or<BR>धनशालिनं (f.<BR>नीं) करोति: v. Rich, to make.<BR>II To adorn:<BR>q. v.: मण्डयति (c. of मण्ड्).<BR>III To fertilize:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enrichment
ENRICHMENT: expr. by circumlo.: v. To<BR>enrich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enroll
ENROLL (v.):<BR>I To enlist: *निवेशपत्रिकायां नाम<BR> निवेशयति (c. of विश्).<BR>II To record: q. v.<BR>III To envelop: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enrollment
ENROLLMENT:<BR>I The act: *नामनिवेशनम्।<BR>II<BR>A register: *निवेशपत्रिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enrooted
ENROOTED:<BR>(1) बद्धमूलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) रूढमूलः<BR>(ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ensample
ENSAMPLE: निदर्शनम्: v. Example.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ensanguined
ENSANGUINED: रुधिरसंलिप्तः (प्ता, प्तं);<BR>(2) शोणिताक्त<BR>(f. क्ता);<BR>(3) अस्रदिग्ध: (f. ग्धा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ensconce
ENSCONCE: लीयते (ली, c. 4.): v. To hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enshrine
ENSHRINE:<BR>I Lit.: v. Shrine; to enclose.<BR>II To cherish: रक्षति (रक्ष्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ensign
ENSIGN:<BR>I A banner: q. v.: पताका।<BR>II A.<BR>standard-bearer:<BR>(1) पताकिन् (m);<BR>(2)<BR>वैजयन्तिकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enslave
ENSLAVE: दासौकरोति,<BR>one who has e. d the whole<BR>of the three worlds:<BR>दासौकृताशेषजगत्त्रयः (या, यं),<BR>Ku.;<BR>there is none whom the good qualities of<BR>Kādambarī do not e.:<BR>कादम्बर्या गुणा न कञ्चिन्न<BR> दासीकुर्वन्ति, K.<BR>To become e. d:<BR>दासीभवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enslavement
ENSLAVEMENT:<BR>I The act: दासीकरणम्।<BR>II<BR>The state: दास्यम्: v. Slavery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ensnare
ENSNARE: पाशेन बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.)<BR>or<BR>पाशे पातयति<BR>(c. of पत्) (lit and fig.).<BR>To be e. d:<BR>पाशे पतति<BR>(पत्, c. 1.) (lit and fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ensue
ENSUE: अनुवर्तते: v. To follow. E. ing: v.<BR>Following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ensure
ENSURE, ENSURER: v. Insure, insurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entablature
ENTABLATURE, ENTABLEMENT: *स्तम्भशिरःशाखा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entail
ENTAIL (subs.):<BR>I An estate: *अनुच्छेद्यसम्पत्तिः।<BR>II Its rule: *अनुच्छेदनियमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entail
ENTAIL (v.):<BR>I Lit.: to settle unalienably:<BR>*अनुच्छेदनियमेन बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>to bring on: आवहति (वह्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entangle
ENTANGLE:<BR>I Lit.: ज(फ्क)टयति (c. of जट)<BR>(used in Bengali).<BR>To be e. d:<BR>ज(फ्क)टयति (जट or<BR>भ्कट्, c. 1.). Ph.: e. d in the bracelets of creepers:<BR>व्रततिवलयासङ्गसञ्जातपाश्ः, Sa.<BR>II To embarrass,<BR>puzzle: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entanglement
ENTANGLEMENT:<BR>I Lit.: v. To entangle.<BR>II Embarrassment: q.v.: प्रमुग्धता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enter
ENTER (v.):<BR>I In gen.: विशति, प्र-, (rarely<BR>आ-, समा-,) (with acc.)<BR>or<BR>निविशते (with loc.)<BR>(rare) (विश्, c. 6.),<BR>e. ed the house of Vasanta-<BR>senā:<BR>वसन्तसेनागृहं प्रविष्टः, Mr. ii.;<BR>if a Śuka<BR>thorn e. s the foot:<BR>निविशते यदि शुकशिखा पदे, N.<BR>iv.<BR>II.;<BR>e. d the hearts of the ascetics:<BR>तपोभृतां<BR> हृदयानि समाविवेश, Ki.; you e. (on your story):<BR>अत्रभवान् प्रविशतु, D. v.: v. To begin; you have<BR>e. ed into the sixth year (of your school life):<BR>प्रविष्टोऽसि षष्ठं वर्षम्, K. v. To attain;<BR>e. ed<BR>into reflection:<BR>चिन्तां विवेश, K.:;<BR>e. ed into com-<BR>bat:<BR>प्राविशातां रणे, B. p. v. To engage in.<BR>Ph.:<BR>to e. into an alliance:<BR>सन्धिं करोति, Ve.<BR>II To make an entry of: निवेशयति, सं-, (c.<BR>of विश्),<BR>should e. (his) name with (his) own<BR>hand:<BR>नाम स्वहस्तेन निवेशयेत्, Y.;<BR>(2) (= to<BR>write: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enterprise
ENTERPRISE (subs.):<BR>I A (bold) undertaking:<BR>(1) उद्यमः: v. Attempt.;<BR>(2) अवदानम् (= achi-<BR>-evement);<BR>(3) साहसम् (often in bad sense).<BR>II Energy: q. v.: उद्यमः a man of great e.:<BR>महोद्यमः पुरुषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enterprise
ENTERPRISE (v.): आरभते (रभ्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>begin, undertake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enterprising
ENTERPRISING (adj.):<BR>(1) उद्योगिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>अध्यवसायिन् (f. नी): v. Active, bold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entertain
ENTERTAIN (v.):<BR>I To maintain: q. v.<BR>II<BR>To receive guests: शुश्रूषते (desi. of श्रु);<BR>(2)<BR>पूजयति (पूज्, c. 10.) (= to honour: q. v.). Ph.:<BR>then we are ready to e. you:<BR>ततः सज्जातिथेया वयम्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">Page243</a>]<BR>Vi.<BR>II To amuse: q. v.: जुषते (जुष्, c. 6.),<BR>e. us:<BR>जुषस्व नः, Vi.<BR>IV To accept: q. v.:<BR>परिगृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.).<BR>V To cherish: करोति,<BR>to c. a hope:<BR>आशां करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entertainer
ENTERTAINER:<BR>I A host: q. v.: शुश्रूषाकारिन्<BR>(f. णी).<BR>II An amuser: q. v.: विनोदकः।<BR>III<BR>A cherisher: expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entertaining
ENTERTAINING (adj.):<BR>(1) विनोदिन् (f. नी)<BR>(= amusing);<BR>(2) हास्यकरः (री, रं) (= excit-<BR>-ing laughter).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entertainingly
ENTERTAININGLY:<BR>(1) विनोदं विदधत् (f. ती);<BR>(2)<BR>हास्यं जनयत् (f. न्ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entertainment
ENTERTAINMENT:<BR>I Hospitality: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>शुश्रूषा;<BR>(2) पूजा।<BR>II A feast उत्सवः।<BR>III<BR>Amusement: q. v.: विनोदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enthrall
ENTHRALL: दासीकरोति: v. To enslave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enthrone
ENTHRONE:<BR>(1) अभिषिञ्चति (सिच्, c. 6.);<BR>(2)<BR>सिंहासने निवेशयति (c. of विश्) (only of kings):<BR>v. To place, throne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enthronement
ENTHRONEMENT:<BR>(1) अभिषेकः;<BR>(2) सिंहासन-<BR>निवेशनम् (only of kings).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enthusiasm
ENTHUSIASM:<BR>I Frenzy, fanaticism: धर्मोन्मादः<BR>(?).<BR>II Warmth, zeal: q. v.: अत्युत्साहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enthusiast
ENTHUSIAST:<BR>I A fanatic: धर्मोन्मत्तः (त्ता, त्तं)<BR>(?).<BR>II In gen. sense: perh. उन्मत्तः (त्ता,<BR> त्तं),<BR>e. s about war:<BR>युद्धोन्मत्ताः; अत्युत्साहवत् (f.<BR>ती): v. Zealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enthusiastic
ENTHUSIASTIC, -AL:<BR>(1) व्यग्रः (ग्रा, ग्रं) (= eager,<BR>zealous);<BR>(2) उन्मत्तः (त्ता, त्तं) (= mad);<BR>(3)<BR>प्रचण्ड (f. ण्डा) (= impetuous). Ph.: e. devotion:<BR>निरतिशयभक्तिः: v. Extreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enthusiastically
ENTHUSIASTICALLY:<BR>(1) निरतिशयम् (= extreme-<BR>-ly);<BR>(2) सोत्साहम् (= eagerly);<BR>(3) सोन्मादम्<BR>(= madly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enthymeme
ENTHYMEME: उपनयान्निगमनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entice
ENTICE (v.):<BR>(1) हरति (हृ, c. 1.) (= to allure:<BR>q. v.),<BR>not e.d by other temptations:<BR>अहृतस्य<BR> विलोभनान्तरैः, R.;<BR>(2) प्र-, लोभयति, वि-, (c. of लुभ्)<BR>(= to tempt: q. v.),<BR>if any one e. s and defiles<BR>this girl:<BR>यदि कश्चिदेनां बालां विलोभ्य नाशयिष्यति, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enticement
ENTICEMENT:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) हरणम्;<BR>(2)<BR>प्र-लोभनम्, वि-।<BR>II Alluring object: प्र-लोभनम्,<BR> वि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enticer
ENTICER: प्रलोभकः: v. Tempter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enticing
ENTICING: v. Alluring; charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enticingly
ENTICINGLY:<BR>(1) प्रलोभ्य, वि-;<BR>(2) मनो हृत्वा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entire
ENTIRE:<BR>I Complete, whole: q. v.:<BR>(1) कृत्स्न<BR>(f. त्स्ना);<BR>(2) समग्रः (ग्रा, ग्रं);<BR>(3) अखण्डः (ण्डा,<BR> ण्डं);<BR>(4) अविकलः (ला, लं);<BR>(5) निखिलः (ला,<BR> लं);<BR>(6) अखिलः (ला, लं);<BR>(7) समस्तः (स्ता,<BR> स्तं).<BR>II Not gelded: q. v.: prob. अविकलः<BR>(ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entirely
ENTIRELY:<BR>I Completely: q. v.:<BR>(1) कार्त्स्न्येन;<BR>(2) साकल्येनः;<BR>(3) समग्रम्;<BR>(4) अखण्डम्;<BR>(5)<BR>सर्वथा (= altogether);<BR>(6) by adj.<BR>II Solely:<BR>comp. with एक, whose life depends e. on water:<BR>जलैकायतजीवितः (ता, तं). M. n.;<BR>of e. peaceful<BR>character:<BR>शमैकवृत्ति (mfn.), Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entireness
ENTIRENESS, ENTIRETY:<BR>(1) कार्त्स्न्यम्;<BR>(2)<BR>साकल्यम्;<BR>(3) समग्रता;<BR>(4) सम्पूर्णता: v. Entire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entitle
ENTITLE (v.):<BR>I To call, name:<BR>(1) अभिदधाति<BR>(धा, c. 3.);<BR>(2) उदाहरति (हृ, c. 1.)<BR>II To<BR>give a claim to: expr. by अधिकारः<BR>or<BR>अर्हति<BR>(अर्ह्, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>-भाज् (mfn.) in comp.,<BR>who<BR>are not e. d to share:<BR>विभागानधिकारिणः, Mit.;<BR>how is the youngest e. d to the kingdom in pre-<BR>ference to the eldest:<BR>कथं ज्येष्ठमतिक्रम्य कनीयान्<BR> राज्यमर्हति, Mat.;<BR>in the absence of the former, the<BR>latter is e. d to property:<BR>पूर्वस्याभावे धनभागुत्तरः, Y.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entity
ENTITY:<BR>(1) सत्, G.;<BR>(2) भावः, G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entomb
ENTOMB: निदधाति (धा, c. 3.) (= to bury).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entombment
ENTOMBMENT: i. e. burial in a tomb: v.<BR>Burial, tomb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entomologist
ENTOMOLOGIST: *कीटविज्ञानविद् (mfn.), -विशारदः<BR>(दा, दं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entomology
ENTOMOLOGY: *कीटविज्ञानम्; कीटविद्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entozoon
ENTOZOON (pl. -zoa): *अन्तर्जीवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entrail
ENTRAIL:<BR>(1) अन्त्रम्;<BR>(2) पुरीतत् (n.) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entrance
ENTRANCE (subs.):<BR>I The act or right of<BR>entering: प्रवेशः, -नम्,<BR>for our e.:<BR>अस्माकं प्रवेशाय,<BR>V. p.;<BR>give me e.:<BR>देहि भे प्रवेशम्, Mu.; e. -fee:<BR>*प्रवेशनशुल्कम्।<BR>II A place for e.: प्रवेशः,<BR>at the<BR>e. of a certain town:<BR>कस्यचिन्नगरस्य प्रवेशे, P. iv.<BR>6.: v. Door, passage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entrance
ENTRANCE (v.):<BR>I To put in a trance: मोहं<BR> जनयति (जन्, c. 10.), उत्पादयति (c. of पद्), etc. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">Page244</a>]<BR>E. d:<BR>मोहाविष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं), मोहाधिष्ठितः (ता, तं).<BR>II To enrapture: प्रहर्षयति (c. of हृष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entrap
ENTRAP:<BR>(1) बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.) (when the<BR>meaning is clear)<BR>by means of nets, hooks, and<BR>other devices for e. ping fish:<BR>जालवडिशप्रभृतिभिर्मत्स्य-<BR>बन्धनोपायैः, Sa v.;<BR>(2) पाशे पातयति (c. of पत्):<BR>v. To ensnare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entreat
ENTREAT: उपच्छन्दयति (छन्द्, c. 10.), R. v. 58:<BR>v. To beg, implore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entreaty
ENTREATY:<BR>(1) अभ्यर्थना<BR>or<BR>प्रार्थना,<BR>by e. s, by<BR>advice:<BR>अभ्यर्थनाभिश्चोपदेशैश्च, K.<BR>(2) याच्ञा: v.<BR>Request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entrepot
ENTREPOT: वाणिज्यस्थानम् (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entrust
ENTRUST (v. t.): निक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.),<BR>should e.<BR>all work to him:<BR>तस्मिन् सर्वकार्याणि निक्षिपेत्, M.<BR>vii. 59;<BR>is the secret you were entrusted with<BR>kept:<BR>रक्ष्यते भवता रहस्यनिक्षेपः, V. ii.;<BR>(2) न्यस्यति,<BR> वि-, (अस्, c. 4.)<BR>or<BR>न्यासीकरोति (with sim.<BR>cons.),<BR>e. ing wife to sons:<BR>सुतविन्यस्तपत्नीकः, Y.;<BR>(3) नि-दधाति<BR>or<BR>धत्ते (धा, c. 3.) (with sim cons.),<BR>K. b.;<BR>(4) निवेशयति (c. of विश्) (rare),<BR>all work<BR>was e. ed to you:<BR>त्वयि निवेशितसर्वकार्यः, Mu. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entry
ENTRY:<BR>I The act of entering: प्रवेशः, -नम्,<BR>on<BR>(your) e.:<BR>प्रवेशे, R. vi. 24:<BR>getting an e. with<BR>difficulty^1:<BR>कथमपि लब्धप्रवेशः, Va.<BR>II A passage<BR>for entering: प्रवेशः: v. Entrance (III),<BR>passage.<BR>III That which is entered:<BR>expr. by verb: this is an erroneous e.:<BR>*इदम्भ्रमान्निवेशितम्; to make an e. of: v. Enter<BR>(II).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

entwine
ENTWINE (v.): परि-वेष्टयति (वेष्ट्, c. 10.) (= to<BR>encircle, surround: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enumerate
ENUMERATE:<BR>I To count: संख्याति (ख्या, c.<BR>2.).<BR>II To recount, mention: q. v. आख्याति<BR>(ख्या, c. 2.),<BR>e. the kings of England:<BR>*इंलण्डे-<BR>श्वराणां नामानि कथय।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enumeration
ENUMERATION: आख्यानम्। v. Mention, recital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enunciate
ENUNCIATE:<BR>I To predicate: लक्षणं<BR>or<BR>रूपं<BR> कथयति (कथ्, c. 10.).<BR>II To pronounce:<BR>q. v.: उच्चारयति (c. of चर्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enunciation
ENUNCIATION:<BR>I Predication: लक्षण-<BR>or<BR>रूप-<BR>कथनम्।<BR>II Mode of utterance: उच्चारणम्।<BR>III<BR>A declaration: उक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

envelop
ENVELOP (v.):<BR>(1) गुण्ठयति, अव-, (गुण्ठ्, c. 10.)<BR>(= to veil),<BR>e. ed in nocturnal darkness:<BR>रजनी-<BR>तिमिरावगुण्ठितः (ता, तं), Ku.;<BR>(2) परि-वृणोति<BR>or<BR>वारयति (वृ, c. 5. and 10.) (= to enclose),<BR>e. ing the whole Lankā:<BR>लङ्कां समस्तां परिवार्य,<BR>Ram.: v. Also to encircle, conceal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

envelop
ENVELOP (subs.): *पत्रवेष्टनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

envenom
ENVENOM (v.):<BR>I Lit.: विषेण लिम्पति (लिप्, c.<BR>6.)<BR>or<BR>देग्धि (दिह्, c. 2.)<BR>or<BR>अनक्ति (ञ्ज्, c. 2.).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>e. ed glance:<BR>विषेण दिग्धः कटाक्षः,<BR>Ma.;<BR>“e. ed tongue of calumny”:<BR>विषाक्ता<BR> पिशुनजिह्वा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enviable
ENVIABLE: स्पृहणीयः (या, यं), of e. prowess:<BR>स्पृहणीयवीर्यः, Ku. iii. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

envier
ENVIER:<BR>(1) ईर्ष्यिन् (m.);<BR>(2) असूयकः:<BR>(3)<BR>मत्सरिन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

envious
ENVIOUS:<BR>(1) ईर्ष्यिन् (f. णी),<BR>e., hateful, discon-<BR>tented:<BR>ईर्ष्यी घृण्यसन्तुष्टः, H.;<BR>(2) मत्सरिन् (f. णी),<BR>e. of others' rise:<BR>परवृद्धिमत्सरिन् (f. णी), Si.;<BR>साभ्यसूयः (या, यं);<BR>(4) ईर्ष्यालु (mfn.);<BR>(5)<BR>असूयापरीतः (ता, तं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enviously
ENVIOUSLY:<BR>(1) सेर्ष्यम्;<BR>(2) साभ्यसूयम्;<BR>(3)<BR>समत्सरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

enviousness
ENVIOUSNESS: v. Envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

environ
ENVIRON (v.): परिवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.): v. En-<BR>-compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

environs
ENVIRONS: परिसराः<BR>or<BR>परिसरविषयाः (m. pl.):<BR>v. Suburbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

envoy
ENVOY: दूतः: v. Ambassador.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

envy
ENVY (subs.):<BR>(1) ईर्ष्या: v. Jealousy;<BR>(2)<BR>अभि-असूया,<BR>who has created yours e.:<BR>केनाभ्यसूया ते<BR> जनिता, Ku.;<BR>(3) मात्सर्यम्,<BR>whose minds are<BR>vitiated with the feeling of e.:<BR>मात्सर्यरागोपहतात्मन्<BR>(mfn.), Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

envy
ENVY (v.):<BR>I In bad sense:<BR>(1) असूयति, अभि-,<BR>(nomi.) (with dat.);<BR>(2) ईर्ष्यति, (ईर्ष्य, c. 1.)<BR>(rare: with dat.);<BR>(3) better by subs.<BR>II<BR>In good sense; स्पृहयति, -ते (स्पृह्, c. 10.)<BR>(with dat.),<BR>I e. the king Daśaratha:<BR>स्पृहयामि<BR> राज्ञे दशरथाय, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epact
EPACT:<BR>annual e.:<BR>सूर्यचन्द्रवत्सरान्तरम्; monthly e.:<BR>अर्कचन्द्रमासान्तरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epaulet
EPAULET: स्कन्धाभरणम्, and sim. comp. s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ephemeral
EPHEMERAL:<BR>I Diurnal: q. v.<BR>II Short-<BR>-lived: क्षणभङ्गुरः (रा, रं): v. Transient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ephod
EPHOD: परिकरः (?) v. Girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ephor
EPHOR: *परिदर्शकः।<BR>E. -alty:<BR>*परिदर्शकत्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epic
EPIC: Ph.:<BR>e. poem:<BR>महाकाव्यम्;<BR>e. poet:<BR>महाकाव्य-<BR>लेखकः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epicene
EPICENE: स्त्रीपुंलिङ्गः (ङ्गा, ङ्गं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epicure
EPICURE: भोजनचञ्चुः, Vet.: विषयासक्तचेतस् (mfn.)<BR>(= sensualist: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epicurian
EPICURIAN:<BR>I Lit.: *एपिकौरीयः (या, यं).<BR>II<BR>Luxurious: विशिष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं).<BR>III Given to<BR>indulgence:<BR>(1) इन्द्रियसुखनिरतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) विषयासक्तः (क्ता, क्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epidemic
EPIDEMIC:<BR>I Adj.: व्यापक (f. पिका).<BR>II<BR>Subs.: व्यापकव्याधिः; मारिः (= pestilence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epiglottis
EPIGLOTTIS: उपजिह्वा; प्रतिजिह्वा, अलिजिह्वा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epigram
EPIGRAM: क्षुद्रकविता (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epigrammatic
EPIGRAMMATIC, -AL:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by comp.<BR>II Concise, pointed: q. v.; लघु (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epigrammatist
EPIGRAMMATIST: क्षुद्रकवितालेखकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epilepsy
EPILEPSY:<BR>(1) अपस्मारः;<BR>(2) भ्रामरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epileptic
EPILEPTIC:<BR>(1) अपस्मारिन् (f. णी), Si.;<BR>(2)<BR>भ्रामरिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epilogue
EPILOGUE: उपसंहारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epiphany
EPIPHANY:<BR>I Lit.: आविर्भावः: v. Appearance.<BR>II A festival: *आविर्भावपर्वन् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

episcopal
EPISCOPAL: expr. by comp., e. jurisdiction:<BR>*प्रधानाचार्याधिकारः;<BR>e. church:<BR>आचार्यधर्म-<BR>मन्दिरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

episcopally
EPISCOPALLY: *प्रधानाचार्यैः (ins. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

episcopate
EPISCOPATE:<BR>I A bishopric: q. v.<BR>II The<BR>body of bishops: *प्रधानाचार्यवर्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

episode
EPISODE: उपाख्यानम्; उपकथा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epistle
EPISTLE: पत्रम्: v. Letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epistolary
EPISTOLARY: expr. by पत्रम्,<BR>e. style:<BR>*पत्ररीतिः,<BR>e. correspondence:<BR>*पत्रसंवादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epitaph
EPITAPH: *स्मरणमण्डनम्: v. Inscription.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epithalamium
EPITHALAMIUM:<BR>(1) मङ्गलगीतम्;<BR>(2) विवाहगीतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epithet
EPITHET: विशेषणम्, V.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epitome
EPITOME:<BR>(1) सारसंग्रहः;<BR>(2) संक्षेपः (=abrid-<BR>-ment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epitomist
EPITOMIST: सारसंग्रहकरः; संक्षेप्तृ (m.) (=abrid-<BR>-ger).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epitomize
EPITOMIZE:<BR>(1) सारसंग्रहं करोति;<BR>(2) संक्षिपति<BR>(क्षिप्, c. 6.) (= to abridge);<BR>(3) समस्यति<BR>(अस्, c. 4.) (= 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epoch
EPOCH:<BR>(1) कालः (= time);<BR>(2) युगम् (=age).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epode
EPODE: काव्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

epoper
EPOPER: v. Epic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equability
EQUABILITY: समता: v. Evenness, equanimity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equable
EQUABLE: समः (मा, मं),<BR>e. -tempered:<BR>समवृत्तिः,<BR>Ki.: v. Even, uniform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equably
EQUABLY: समम्: v. Evenly, uniformly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equal
EQUAL (adj.):<BR>I A like:<BR>(1) समः (मा, मं),<BR>I<BR>do not see any one greater than or e. to Rāma:<BR>पश्यामि रामादधिकं समं वा नान्यम्, B.; e. share:<BR>समभागः, Da.;<BR>(2) समानः (ना, नं),<BR>e. in caste<BR>and number:<BR>समाना जातिसंख्यया, Da.; to (men)<BR>of e. valour, lineage, and manliness:<BR>समानवीर्यान्वय-<BR>पौरुषेषु, Ki.;<BR>(3) तुल्यः (ल्या, ल्यं) (= match-<BR>-ing, like),<BR>of e. strength:<BR>तुल्यश्क्ति (mfn.),<BR>M. n.;<BR>(4) सदृशः (शी, शं) (= तुल्य),<BR>with those,<BR>who are not his e. s:<BR>अनात्मसदृशेषु, Mu.<BR>II<BR>Adequate:<BR>(1) समः (मा, मं);<BR>(2) पर्याप्तः (प्ता,<BR> प्तं) (= enough: q. v.).<BR>III Equitable:<BR>समः (मा, मं).<BR>IV Indifferent: समः (मा,<BR> मं)<BR>or<BR>समानः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equal
EQUAL (subs.):<BR>(1) expr. by adj.: समः (मा,<BR> मं)<BR>or<BR>समानः (ना, नं),<BR>with e. s:<BR>समैः, H.;<BR>two<BR>e. s:<BR>समानौ, B.;<BR>(2) समानजनः,<BR>before e. s:<BR>समान-<BR>जनसमक्षम्, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equal
EQUAL (v. t.):<BR>I To be e. to: expr. by adj.,<BR>but does not e. me in penances:<BR>न तु तपसा मे समः,<BR>Vi.<BR>II To make e. to:<BR>(1) expr. by adj.;<BR>(2) समीकरोति<BR>or<BR>समानीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equality
EQUALITY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) साभ्यम्,<BR>bearing e. with<BR>the thunder of Jupiter:<BR>अशनिना मघोनः साम्यं गतः,<BR>Ki.;<BR>(2) समानता;<BR>(3) तुल्यता।<BR>II Evenness:<BR>तुल्यता।<BR>III Uniformity: समता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equalization
EQUALIZATION:<BR>(1) समीकरणम्;<BR>(2) समानीकरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equalize
EQUALIZE:<BR>(1) समीकरोति;<BR>(2) समानीकरोति;<BR>(3) by adj. v. Equal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equally
EQUALLY:<BR>(1) समं<BR>or<BR>समानम्,<BR>treats his servants<BR>e.:<BR>समं भृत्येषु वर्तते, P.;<BR>(2) तुल्यम्;<BR>(3) सदृशम्;<BR>(4) by adj.,<BR>the battle was e. matched:<BR>तुल्य-<BR>प्रतिद्वन्द्वि बभूव युद्धम्, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equanimity
EQUANIMITY:<BR>(1) समता,<BR>by e.:<BR>समतया, R. ix.<BR>6.;<BR>(2) समवृत्तिता;<BR>(3) समभावः;<BR>(4) समचित्तता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equation
EQUATION: समीकरणम्,<BR>quadratic e.:<BR>वर्गसमीकरणम्,<BR>Vij.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equator
EQUATOR:<BR>I Terrestrial:<BR>(1) भूपरिधिः;<BR>(2)<BR>भूकक्षा।<BR>II Celestial:<BR>(1) व्योमकक्षा and sim.<BR>comp.s.;<BR>(2) आकाशपरिधिः, Gan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equatorial
EQUATORIAL: Ph.:<BR>e. region:<BR>निरक्षदेशः, Go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equerry
EQUERRY, EQUERY:<BR>I A stable:<BR>(1) मन्दुरा;<BR>(2) वाजिशाला;<BR>(3) अश्वशाला।<BR>II An officer:<BR>मन्दुरापालः, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equestrian
EQUESTRIAN (subs.): अश्ववारः: v. Horseman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equestrian
EQUESTRIAN (adj.):<BR>I Pertaining to horse:<BR>(1) अश्वीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) आश्व (f. श्वा);<BR>(3)<BR>आश्विकः (की, कं).<BR>II Pertaining to horse-<BR>-men: expr. by tat. comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equiangular
EQUIANGULAR:<BR>(1) समकोणः (णा, णं);<BR>(2)<BR>समानास्र (f. स्रा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equidistant
EQUIDISTANT:<BR>(1) समदूरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) समानान्तरः<BR>(रा, रं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equilateral
EQUILATERAL: समभुजः (जा, जं). E. triangle:<BR>समत्रिभुजः;<BR>e. pentagon:<BR>समपञ्चभुजः; and so on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equilibrium
EQUILIBRIUM: समधृतिः (?); V. s. To be in e.:<BR>(1) समधृतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) तुलाधृतः (ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equinoctial
EQUINOCTIAL: विषुवीयः (या, यं). The e. line:<BR>(1) विषुवरेखा;<BR>(2) विषुवचक्रम्;<BR>(3) विषुवद्वृत्तम्, Su.<BR>The e. sun:<BR>विषुवस्थो दिवाकरः, Su. E. point:<BR>अयनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equinox
EQUINOX:<BR>(1) विषुवम्;<BR>(2) विषुवत् (n.).<BR>Vernal<BR>e.:<BR>महाविषुवम्,<BR>Autumnal e.:<BR>जलविषुवम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equip
EQUIP (v.):<BR>(1) सज्जीकरोति,<BR>well e. ped:<BR>सुसज्जितः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(2) आ-कल्पयति, उप-, (क्ल्ट्प्, c. 10.): v.<BR>Also to adorn, accoutre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equipage
EQUIPAGE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) सज्जा;<BR>(2) आकल्पः।<BR>Ph.:<BR>personal e.:<BR>शरीरोपकरणानि, K.<BR>II Re-<BR>-tinue: q. v.: परिवर्हः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equipment
EQUIPMENT:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) सज्जीकरणम्;<BR>(2)<BR>आकल्पनम्, उप-,।<BR>II Equipage: q. v.: सज्जा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equipoise
EQUIPOISE: समधृतिः: v. Equilibrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equitable
EQUITABLE:<BR>I Of men: न्यायपरायण (f. णा).<BR>II Of acts: न्यायसंगतः (ता, तं): v. Just.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equitably
EQUITABLY: न्यायेन<BR>or<BR>न्यायतः: v. Justly, fairly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equity
EQUITY: न्यायः:<BR>e. governs in the conflict of two<BR>codes of law:<BR>स्मृत्योर्विरोधे न्यायो बलवान्, Y.: v.<BR>Justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equivalent
EQUIVALENT (adj.):<BR>(1) तुल्यः (ल्या, ल्यं) v.<BR>Equal;<BR>(2) तुल्यार्थकः (का, कं) (in meaning);<BR>(3) तुल्यबलः (ला, लं) (in force);<BR>(4) तुल्यमूल्यं<BR>(ल्या, ल्यं) (in value).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equivalent
EQUIVALENT (subs.):<BR>I An e. thing: expr.<BR>by adj.<BR>II In chemistry: *तुल्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equivocal
EQUIVOCAL: वक्रः (क्रा, क्रं): v. Ambiguous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equivocally
EQUIVOCALLY: वक्रम्: v. Ambiguously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equivocate
EQUIVOCATE (v.):<BR>(1) वक्रोक्तिं करोति;<BR>(2) भङ्गिं<BR> करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

equivocation
EQUIVOCATION:<BR>(1) वक्रोक्तिः:<BR>(2) स्फुटभिन्नार्थं वचः,<BR>Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

era
ERA:<BR>(1) कालः: v. Time;<BR>(2) शकः<BR>or<BR>शाकः<BR>(sp. of. Śālivāhana);<BR>(3) संवत् (of Vikra-<BR>-māditya).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eradicate
ERADICATE:<BR>(1) उन्मूलयति, सम्-, (मूल्, c. 10.),<BR>an enemy can be easily e. d:<BR>रिपुरुन्मूलयितुं सुकरः,<BR>Ki. ii. 50;<BR>(2) उद्धरति (हृ, c. 1.),<BR>I will e.<BR>the enemy today:<BR>शत्रुमद्योद्धरिष्यामि, Ram.;<BR>(3)<BR>उच्छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eradication
ERADICATION:<BR>(1) उन्मूलनम्;<BR>(2) उद्धरणम्<BR>or<BR>उद्धारः;<BR>(3) उच्छेदः,<BR>e. of birth:<BR>उच्छेदो जन्मनः, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erase
ERASE:<BR>I To efface: q. v.: प्र-मार्ष्टि (मृज्, c.<BR>2.).<BR>II To destroy: q.v.: कषति (कष, c.<BR>1.),<BR>all-e. ing fate:<BR>सर्वंकषा भवितव्यता, Ma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erasure
ERASURE: लोपः। (?): v. Obliteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ere
ERE: पूर्वम्,<BR>e. this:<BR>इतः पूर्वम्: v. Before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ere long
ERE LONG:<BR>(1) अचिरेण;<BR>(2) अचिरात्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erect
ERECT (adj.):<BR>I Of posture: perh. उन्नतः (ता,<BR> तं).<BR>II Raised, uplifted: q. v.: उन्नतः (ता,<BR> तं),<BR>with eyebrows e.:<BR>उन्नतभ्रू (n. भ्रु). Ph.: his<BR>hair became e. (from joy): पुलकितो बभूव।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erect
ERECT (v.):<BR>I To set up, plant: q. v.:<BR>स्थापयति (c. of स्था).<BR>II To build: q. v.:<BR>(1) निर्मिमीते (मा, c. 3.);<BR>(2) करोति (= to<BR>make).<BR>III To exalt: q. v.: उन्नमयति (c. of<BR>नम्).<BR>IV To establish, found: q.v.:<BR>स्थापयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erection
ERECTION:<BR>I Planting:<BR>(1) स्थापनम्, सं-,<BR>(2)<BR>प्रतिष्ठापनम्।<BR>II Building: निर्माणम्।<BR>III Exal-<BR>-tation: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erectly
ERECTLY: prob. उन्नतकायेन<BR>or<BR>उन्नतो (f. ता) भूत्वा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erectness
ERECTNESS: उन्नतता, -त्वम्: v. Erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erewhile
EREWHILE: किञ्चित्पूर्वम्: v. Sometime, before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eremite
EREMITE: अरण्यवासी, Vi.;<BR>(2) आरण्यकः, Vi.: v.<BR>Hermit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ermine
ERMINE:<BR>I An animal: नकुलजातीयजन्तुविशेषः।<BR>II Its fur: *ऊर्मीणलोमन् (n.).<BR>III The<BR>dignity of judges: ऊर्मीणलोमधराः (m. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erotic
EROTIC: v. Amatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

err
ERR (v.):<BR>(1) भ्रमति, वि-, (भ्रम्, c. 1.),<BR>that you<BR>may not e. again:<BR>मा भूयो विभ्रमेरिति, Mah.;<BR>(2) पथः<BR>or<BR>मार्गात् च्यवते (च्यु, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>भ्रश्यति,<BR> -ते (भ्रंश्, c. 4.) (= to wander from the right<BR>way), Ki.;<BR>(3) उत्पथेन<BR>or<BR>उन्मार्गेण गच्छति (गम्,<BR>c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>धावति (धाव्, c. 1.) (in moral sense),<BR>U.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

errand
ERRAND: सन्देशः: v. Message.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

errant
ERRANT:<BR>I Wandering: q. v.: परिभ्रमिन् (f.<BR>णी).<BR>II Wild: q. v.: उद्वृत्तः (त्ता, त्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erring
ERRING (adj.):<BR>(1) भ्रान्तः (न्ता, न्तं), e. -minded:<BR>भ्रान्तबुद्धि (mfn.), M. n.;<BR>(2) व्यभिचारिन् (f. णी),<BR>un-e. knowledge:<BR>ज्ञानमव्यभिचारि, N. d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erroneous
ERRONEOUS:<BR>(1) भ्रममूलकः (का, कं),<BR>this reading<BR>is e.:<BR>इति पाठस्तु म्रममूलकः, Va. com.;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रामादिकः (की, कं), e. interchange of things:<BR>प्रामादिकी वस्तुपरिवृत्तिः, M. n.;<BR>(3) मिथ्या (= false)<BR>in comp.,<BR>an e. inference:<BR>मिथ्यानुमानम्, N. d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erroneously
ERRONEOUSLY:<BR>(1) भ्रमात्;<BR>(2) प्रमादेन;<BR>(3)<BR>भ्रान्तितः, Go.;<BR>(4) मिथ्या (= falsely: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erroneousness
ERRONEOUSNESS:<BR>(1) भ्रममूलत्वम्;<BR>(2) प्रामादिक-<BR>त्वम्: v. Falsity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

error
ERROR:<BR>I A mistake: q. v.: भ्रमः।<BR>II An<BR>inaccuracy: अशुद्धम्।<BR>III Deviation: उन्मार्ग-<BR>गमनम्।<BR>IV Fault, sin.: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erst
ERST: पुरा: v. Formerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eruct
ERUCT, ERUCTATION: v. Belch, belching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erudite
ERUDITE:<BR>I As applied to men: पण्डितः (ता,<BR> तं): v. Learned.<BR>II As applied to any<BR>science, etc.: v. Abstruse, profound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erudition
ERUDITION:<BR>(1) पाण्डित्यम्;<BR>(2) वैदुष्यम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eruption
ERUPTION:<BR>I A bursting forth:<BR>(1) निःसरणम्;<BR>(2) निर्गमः।<BR>II Of the skin: what are these e.s:<BR>*किं निर्गतमङ्गे: v. Pimple, itch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eruptive
ERUPTIVE: expr. by verb: निर्गच्छति (गम्, c.<BR>1.)<BR>or<BR>निःसरति (सृ, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

erysipelas
ERYSIPELAS:<BR>(1) उदर्दः;<BR>(2) दद्रुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

escalade
ESCALADE:<BR>I Subs: prob. अवस्कन्दः, -नम्।<BR>II<BR>Verb: अवस्कन्दति (स्कन्द्, c. 1.) (?); लङ्घयति<BR>(लङ्घ्, c. 10.) (= to scale).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

escapade
ESCAPADE: स्खलितम्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

escape
ESCAPE (v. t.):<BR>I To get out of:<BR>(1) मुच्यते,<BR> वि-, परि-, (pass. of मुच्) (with abl.),<BR>who e. s<BR>the great snare:<BR>यो महापाशाद्विमुक्तः, V. c.;<BR>(2)<BR>तरति, उत्- निर्-, सम्-, अभि, (तॄ, c. 1.) (= to<BR>cross, overcome), without e. ing an accusation:<BR>अभियोगमनिस्तीर्य, Y.;<BR>to e. death:<BR>मृत्युं तरति,<BR>Vi.<BR>II To avoid: q. v.: परिहरति (हृ, c. 1.),<BR>infamy has been e. d:<BR>परिहृतमयशः, Mu.<BR>III<BR>Of observation, etc.:<BR>e. d the notice of the<BR>guards:<BR>न लक्षितो रक्षिभटैः, N.;<BR>it e. d his<BR>notice:<BR>स एतन्नालक्षयत् (लक्ष्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

escape
ESCAPE (v. i.): i. e. to flee:<BR>(1) अप-क्रामति or<BR>क्राम्यति, निर-, समप-, (क्रम्, c. 1. and 4.),<BR>why<BR>was he allowed to e.:<BR>स कस्मादपक्रामन्नु पेक्षितः, Mu.<BR>iii.;<BR>(2) अप-सरति, निर्-, (सृ, c. 1.);<BR>(3) अपस-<BR>र्पति, (सृप्, c. 1.);<BR>(4) निर्-गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.).<BR>To e. from: v. Escape (v. t.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

escape
ESCAPE (subs.):<BR>I E. ing from:<BR>(1) निस्तारः,<BR>I<BR>see no e.:<BR>निस्तारं न पश्यामि;<BR>(2) by verb,<BR>it<BR>was a narrow e.:<BR>कथं कथमपि तस्माद्विमुक्तः।<BR>II<BR>Fleeing:<BR>(1) निष्क्रमः;<BR>(2) अपसर्पणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

escarpment
ESCARPMENT: [पर्वतस्य] पातुकपार्श्वः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

escheat
ESCHEAT (v. i.):<BR>I To the crown:<BR>(1) राजस्वताम्<BR> आपद्यते (पद्, c. 4.), Sa. vi.;<BR>(2) राजसात्<BR> गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.),<BR>all these accumulated silver,<BR>base metal, etc. e. ed to the crown:<BR>सञ्चितं रौप्य-<BR>कुप्यादि सर्वं तद्राजसादगात्, Raj.<BR>II To a lord:<BR>by ana: स्वामिसात् गच्छति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

escheat
ESCHEAT (subs.): expr. by circumlo.: v. To<BR>escheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eschew
ESCHEW: वर्जयति (वृज्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>avoid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

escort
ESCORT (subs.):<BR>(1) expr. by circumlo.<BR>attended<BR>by a large e.:<BR>महता बलेन रक्षितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2)<BR>रक्षाधिकृतपुरुषः;<BR>(3) परिचरः: v. Retinue, guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

escort
ESCORT (v.): अनुगच्छति (गम्, c. 1.), I myself [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">Page248</a>]<BR>will e. her:<BR>स्वयमेवानुगच्छामि तत्रभवतीम्, Mr.: v.<BR>To accompany; guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

esculent
ESCULENT: खाद्यः (द्या, द्यं): v. Eatable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

escutcheon
ESCUTCHEON: *कुलचिह्नपत्रम्, Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

esoteric
ESOTERIC: विशिष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

espalier
ESPALIER: लतागुञ्जः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

especial
ESPECIAL: विशेष in com.: v. Principal, parti-<BR>-cular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

especially
ESPECIALLY:<BR>(1) विशेषेण;<BR>(2) विशेषम्:<BR>(3)<BR>प्राधान्येन (= principally: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

espionage
ESPIONAGE:<BR>I The practice of spies: गूढ-<BR>प्रचारः, and sim. comp. s.<BR>II Their employ-<BR>-ment: चारप्रयोगः, and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

esplanade
ESPLANADE: विरामभूमिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

espousal
ESPOUSAL:<BR>I Betrothal: दानम्, प्र-।<BR>II Marri-<BR>-age: q. v.: विवाहः।<BR>III Fig., adoption:<BR>परिग्रहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

espouse
ESPOUSE:<BR>I To betroth: ददाति, प्र-, (दा, c.<BR>3.).<BR>II To marry: q. v.: परिगृह्णाति (ग्रह्,<BR>c. 9.).<BR>III To accept: परिगृह्णाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

espy
ESPY: निर्वर्णयति (वर्ण्, c. 10.): v. To see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

esquire
ESQUIRE:<BR>I An attendant: सहचरः।<BR>II A<BR>title: श्रीमत् (m.) prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

essay
ESSAY (subs.):<BR>I To Attempt: व्यवस्यति (सो,<BR>c. 4.). q. v.:<BR>II To Assay: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

essay
ESSAY (subs.):<BR>I Attempt: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Assay: q. v.<BR>III Composition:<BR>(1) प्रबन्धः;<BR>(2) निबन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

essayist
ESSAYIST: प्रबन्धलेखकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

essence
ESSENCE:<BR>I In gen. sense: सारः, e. of beauty:<BR>सौन्दर्यसारः; Ma.;<BR>in e. and in character:<BR>सारतः<BR> शीलतश्च, D.<BR>II Perfume: गन्धसारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

essential
ESSENTIAL:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by comp., e. thing:<BR>सारवस्तु।<BR>II Containing essence:<BR>(1) ससार:<BR>(रा, रं);<BR>(2) सारवत् (f. ती).<BR>III Indispens-<BR>-able, necessary: q. v.:<BR>the study of the Vedas<BR>is e. for an enquiry about duties:<BR>धर्मजिज्ञासा<BR> वेदाध्ययनं नियमेनापेक्षते, S. Ph.:<BR>e. oil:<BR>*सारतैलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

essentially
ESSENTIALLY: सारतः: v. Essential, really.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

establish
ESTABLISH:<BR>I To found, settle: q. v.: स्थाप-<BR>यति, सं-, प्रति-, (c. of स्था),<BR>will e. Kaivartas<BR>in his kingdom:<BR>कैवर्तान् राज्ये स्थापयिष्यति, V. p.<BR>Ph:<BR>the e. ed church:<BR>*प्रतिष्ठापितधर्मः।<BR>II To<BR>confirm: q. v.: स्थिरीकरोति।<BR>III To prove:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) प्रति-पादयति, उप-, (c. of पद,),<BR>does<BR>not e. his claim by evidence:<BR>उक्तं प्रमाणेन न<BR> प्रतिपादयति, K. b.;<BR>(2) भावयति, वि-, (c. of भू)<BR>(rare),<BR>a case e. ed by witness:<BR>साक्षिभिर्भावितं<BR> कार्यम्, Kat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

establisher
ESTABLISHER:<BR>I A founder: स्थापकः, सं-,<BR> प्रति-।<BR>II Prover: प्रतिपादकः, or by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

establishment
ESTABLISHMENT:<BR>I Settlement: स्थापनम्, सं-।<BR>II Confirmation: स्थिरीकरणम्।<BR>III Prov-<BR>-ing: प्रतिपादनम्।<BR>IV System, government:<BR>स्थितिः। v. Domestic: expr. by circumlo.:<BR>he keeps a large e.:<BR>बहूनि भृत्यादीनि रक्षति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

estate
ESTATE:<BR>I State: q. v.: अवस्था।<BR>II Property:<BR>q. v.: सम्पत्तिः।<BR>III An order or class: वर्गः (?),<BR>the third e. (i. e. the commonalty): *तृतीयवर्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

esteem
ESTEEM (v.):<BR>I To think, reckon: q. v.:<BR>गणयति (गण्, c. 10.).<BR>II To respect, love:<BR>q. v.: बहु मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

esteem
ESTEEM (subs.): expr. by verb,<BR>he is held in<BR>high e. by the people:<BR>प्रजास्तं बहु मन्यन्ते: v.<BR>Regard, reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

estimable
ESTIMABLE:<BR>I Praiseworthy: q. v.: श्लाध्यः<BR>(ध्या, ध्यं).<BR>II What can be estimated:<BR>q. v.: निरूप्यः (प्या, प्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

estimate
ESTIMATE (subs.):<BR>I Of money, etc.: गणना (?).<BR>II Judgement, appreciation: q. v.: गणना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

estimate
ESTIMATE: निरूपयति (रूप्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>count, compute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

estimation
ESTIMATION:<BR>I Lit.: निरूपणम्: v. Computa-<BR>-tion.<BR>II Opinion: q. v.: मतम्।<BR>III Esteem:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

estop
ESTOP: *प्रतिबध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.),<BR>e. d by his<BR>own deed:<BR>*स्वपत्रेण प्रतिबद्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

estopple
ESTOPPLE: *प्रतिबन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

estrange
ESTRANGE: विश्लेषयति (c. of श्लिष्): v. To<BR>alienate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

estrangement
ESTRANGEMENT: विच्छेदः: v. Alienation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

estuary
ESTUARY: पुटभेदः (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

et cetera
ET CETERA:<BR>(1) आदि (mfn.), animals, etc.:<BR>पश्वादयः, S.;<BR>(2) प्रभृति (mfn.),<BR>citizen, villagers,<BR>etc.:<BR>पौरजानपदप्रभृतयः, Ana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

etch
ETCH: लिखति (लिख्, c. 6.) (= to draw: q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eternal
ETERNAL:<BR>(1) नित्यः (त्या, त्यं), to the e. God.:<BR>नित्याय देवाय, Vi.;<BR>(2) शाश्वतः (ती, तं),<BR>in e.<BR>course:<BR>शाश्वते पथि, Ka.;<BR>(3) अनन्तः (न्ता, न्तं)<BR>(=endless);<BR>(4) सनातनः (नी, नं) (= ever-<BR>-existing);<BR>(5) सन्ततः (ता, तं) (= incessant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eternally
ETERNALLY:<BR>(1) नित्यम्;<BR>(2) शाश्वतम्;<BR>(3)<BR>अनन्तम्;<BR>(4) सनातनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eternity
ETERNITY:<BR>(1) नित्यता;<BR>(2) better by adj.:<BR>v. Eternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

etesian
ETESIAN: वार्षिकः (की, कं): v. Annual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ether
ETHER:<BR>I A medium: *तेजोवहः।<BR>II A fluid:<BR>*हिमद्रवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ethereal
ETHEREAL:<BR>I Celestial: q. v.:<BR>e. regions:<BR>नभस्:<BR>v. Sky.<BR>II Spirit-like: तैजसः (सी, सं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ethic
ETHIC, ETHICAL: expr. by धर्म- in com.,<BR>“e.<BR>meaning”:<BR>*धर्मार्थः; authors of e. systems:<BR>धर्मशास्त्रप्रयोजकाः, Y.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ethics
ETHICS: धर्मशास्त्रम् (applied also to jurispru-<BR>-dence); धर्मतत्त्वम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

etiquette
ETIQUETTE: आचारः<BR>or<BR>सदाचारः: v. Custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

etymological
ETYMOLOGICAL: व्युत्पत्तिविषयकः (का, कं), and<BR>sim. expr. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

etymologist
ETYMOLOGIST: व्युत्पत्तिविद् (mfn.) (?); व्युत्पत्ति-<BR>विद्याविशारदः (दा, दं) (?), and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

etymology
ETYMOLOGY:<BR>I In gram.: शब्दादीनां रूपप्रकरणम्।<BR>II Derivation: व्युत्पत्तिः।<BR>III The science:<BR>व्युत्पत्तिः, -विद्या (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eucharist
EUCHARIST: *कृष्टश्राद्धम्।<BR>E. -ic.:<BR>*कृष्टश्राद्धीयः (या,<BR> यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eulogist
EULOGIST:<BR>(1) प्रशंसकः;<BR>(2) स्तुतिपाठकः (who<BR>sings eulogies).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eulogize
EULOGIZE: स्तौति<BR>or<BR>स्तवीति (स्तु, c. 2.): v. To<BR>praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eulogy
EULOGY: स्तुतिः<BR>or<BR>स्तवः,<BR>others are pleased with<BR>false e. s:<BR>तोषमेति वितथैः स्तवैः परः, Si.: v.<BR>Praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eunuch
EUNUCH:<BR>(1) वर्षवरः;<BR>(2) षण्डः;<BR>(3) क्लीवः;<BR>(4)<BR>नपुंसकः। N. B.<BR>(3) and<BR>(4) are usually terms of<BR>contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

euphemism
EUPHEMISM: *मङ्गलभाषितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

euphemistic
EUPHEMISTIC: Ph.:<BR>e. expression:<BR>*मङ्गलभाषितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

euphonic
EUPHONIC, -AL, EUPHONIOUS:<BR>(1) सुस्वरः (रा,<BR> रं);<BR>(2) सुस्वरसंश्लिष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

euphoniously
EUPHONIOUSLY:<BR>(1) सुस्वरेण (?);<BR>(2) सुस्वर-<BR>संश्लिष्टम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

euphnony
EUPHNONY: सुस्वरः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

euphorbia
EUPHORBIA: बहुदुग्धिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

euphuism
EUPHUISM: वाग्विलासः (?); *औफिम्मम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evacuate
EVACUATE (v.):<BR>I To empty: q. v.: शून्यी-<BR>करोति।<BR>II To void: q. v.: उत्सृजति, (सृज्,<BR>c. 6.).<BR>III To desert, quit: q. v.: त्यजति,<BR> परि-, (त्यज्, c. 1.),<BR>e. ing Dwārakā:<BR>द्वारकां<BR> परित्यज्य, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evacuation
EVACUATION:<BR>I Of the bowels: मलोत्सर्गः। E. s.:<BR>उच्चारः।<BR>II Of a town or fort मोक्षः,<BR>the<BR>siege and e. by Śālva:<BR>रोधं मोक्षञ्च शाल्वेन,<BR>Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evade
EVADE (v.): परिहरति (हृ, c. 1.),<BR>to e. a sum-<BR>mons:<BR>*आह्वानं परिहरति, Ph.: to e. observation:<BR>v. To escape (v. t.) (III); e. ing these points:<BR>अमू विमुच्यैव, N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evanescent
EVANESCENT: क्षणभङ्गुरः (रा, रं): v. Transient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evangelic
EVANGELIC, -AL: Ph.:<BR>e. preacher:<BR>*मङ्गलप्रवक्ता;<BR>*e. history:<BR>मङ्गलपुरावृत्तम्;<BR>e. truth:<BR>*बाईबलानुगतं<BR> सत्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evangelically
EVANGELICALLY: *बाईबलानुसारेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evangelist
EVANGELIST:<BR>I A writer: मङ्गललेखकः।<BR>II A<BR>preacher: *मङ्गलप्रवक्तृ (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evangelize
EVANGELIZE:<BR>to e. the world<BR>*लोकेभ्यो मङ्गलं<BR> प्रवक्ति (वच्, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evaporate
EVAPORATE (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: *बाष्पीकरोति (?):<BR>v. Vapour; to dissipate.<BR>II To dry up:<BR>q. v.: आचामति (चम्, c. 1.), R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evaporate
EVAPORATE (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.: बाष्पो भूत्वा गच्छति<BR>(गम्, c. 1.) (?).<BR>II Fig.: to be wasted: नश्यति<BR>(नश्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evaporation
EVAPORATION:<BR>I Lit.: बाष्पीकरणम् (?) (turning<BR>into vapour); बाष्पीभावः (?) (passing off in<BR>v.).<BR>II Fig.: क्षयः: v. Decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evasion
EVASION:<BR>(1) expr. by verb: v. To evade:<BR>(2) छलम् (= trick).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evasive
EVASIVE: वक्रः (क्रा, क्रं) (?): v. Ambiguous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evasively
EVASIVELY:<BR>(1) प्रस्तुतं परिहृत्य (?);<BR>(2) वक्रोत्तया:<BR>v. Ambiguously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eve
EVE, EVEN (subs.):<BR>I Evening: q. v.:<BR>II<BR>The evening preceding a feast: पूर्वप्रदोषः (?). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">Page250</a>]<BR>III Fig.:<BR>we are on the eve of war:<BR>प्रत्यासीदति<BR>(सीद्, c. 1.) नो युद्धम्: v. To approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

even
EVEN (adj.):<BR>I Level, smooth: q. v.: समः<BR>(मा, मं),<BR>it (the earth) looks e. to him:<BR>सा समा तस्य<BR> प्रतिभाति, Go.<BR>II Equable: समः (मा, मं),<BR>e.<BR>tempered:<BR>समवृत्ति (mfn), Ki.<BR>III Not odd:<BR>समः (मा, मं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

even
EVEN (adj.): अपि (placed after the word em-<BR>-phasized),<BR>where e. the trees, e. the animals are<BR>my friends:<BR>यत्र द्रुमा अपि मृगा अपि बन्धवो मे, U. iii.;<BR>very difficult to be shunned e. when leaving:<BR>सुदु-<BR>स्त्यजास्त्यजन्तोऽपि, Ki.;<BR>e. now:<BR>अद्यापि, J.; e. if:<BR>v. If;<BR>not e. he:<BR>सोऽपि॥॥॥।न। Ph.:<BR>e. so:<BR>एम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

even-handed
EVEN-HANDED:<BR>(1) समः (मा, मं);<BR>(2) समदर्शिन्<BR>(f. नी);<BR>(3) तुल्यवृत्ति (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evening
EVENING (subs.):<BR>(1) सायंकालः;<BR>(2) प्रदोषः;<BR>(3)<BR>सन्ध्या;<BR>(4) विकालः;<BR>(5) दिनान्तः (poet);<BR>(6)<BR>रजनीमुखम् (poet).<BR>In the e.:<BR>सायम्;<BR>e. and morn-<BR>ing:<BR>सायं प्रातश्च, Sha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evening
EVENING (adj.):<BR>(1) सायन्तनः (नी, नं);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रादोषिकः (की, कं);<BR>(3) सायंकालीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(4) सान्ध्यः (f. न्ध्या);<BR>(5) वैकालिकः (की, कं);<BR>(6) by tat. comp.<BR>The e. star:<BR>*प्रदोषतारा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evenly
EVENLY:<BR>(1) समम्;<BR>(2) समानम्;<BR>(3) तुल्यम्:<BR>v. Equally, uniformly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evenness
EVENNESS:<BR>I Lit.: समता।<BR>II Of temper:<BR>समता, by e., by discharging showers of wealth:<BR>समतया वसुवृष्टिविसर्जनैः, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

event
EVENT:<BR>I An occurrence:<BR>(1) घटना;<BR>(2)<BR>वृत्तम्। Ph.:<BR>at all e. s:<BR>अन्ततः;<BR>in the e. of:<BR>यदि:<BR>v. If.<BR>II Issue, end: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eventful
EVENTFUL: घटनाकुलः (ला, लं) (?): v. Memo-<BR>-rable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

even-tide
EVEN-TIDE: सायंकालः: v. Evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eventual
EVENTUAL: अन्तिमः (मा, मं): v. Final, ulti-<BR>-mate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eventually
EVENTUALLY: अवशेषे: v. Finally, ultimately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ever
EVER:<BR>I At any time: कदाचित्<BR>or<BR>कदापि,<BR>if<BR>these e. deserve union:<BR>कदाचिदेते यदि योगमर्हतः, Ku.;<BR>“nobody e. yet hated his own flesh”:<BR>*अद्यापि न<BR> कोऽपि स्वमांसं दिद्वेष। Ph.:<BR>e. and anon:<BR>यदा तदा।<BR>II Always: q. v.:<BR>(1) सततम्,<BR>e. think of the<BR>truth:<BR>तत्त्वं चिन्तय सततम्, J.;<BR>(2) नित्यम्, D.:<BR>Ph.:<BR>gone for e.:<BR>अपुनरागमनाय गतः; lost for e.:<BR>एकान्तनष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं) E. so (= in whatever<BR>degree): v. However.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

everblooming
EVERBLOOMING: नित्यपुष्पः (ष्पा, ष्पं), and sim.<BR>comps.,<BR>where trees are e.:<BR>यत्र पादपा नित्यपुष्पाः,<BR>Me.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evergreen
EVERGREEN:<BR>(1) सततहरितः (ता, तं); (?);<BR>(2) नित्यपर्ण (f. र्णा) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

everlasting
EVERLASTING: नित्यस्थायिन् (f. नी): v. Eternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

everlastingly
EVERLASTINGLY: v. Eternally, continually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evermore
EVERMORE:<BR>I For e.: सततम्।<BR>II At all<BR>times: सदा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

every
EVERY:<BR>(1) by doubling the word,<BR>at e.<BR>place:<BR>स्थाने स्थाने, J.;<BR>in e. house:<BR>गृहे गृहे, Ku.;<BR>e. six months:<BR>षण्मासे षण्मासे, P. iii. 6.;<BR>(2) by<BR>comp. with प्रति,<BR>in e. direction:<BR>प्रतिदिशम्, Ki.;<BR>e. day:<BR>प्रत्यहम्, H.;<BR>(3) by comp. with अनु<BR>(of rapid succession),<BR>e. moment, e. now and<BR>then:<BR>अनुक्षणम्;<BR>(4) सर्वः (र्वा, र्वं) (when e.=<BR>all);<BR>e. poem:<BR>सर्वं काव्यम्, Mal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

everybody
EVERYBODY, EVERYONE:<BR>(1) सर्वः,<BR>e. is after<BR>his own interest:<BR>सर्वः स्वार्थे समीहते, Si. ii. 65.;<BR>(2) सर्वंजनः, सकलो जनः, etc.,<BR>e. will say:<BR>सर्वो<BR> जनो वदिष्यति, P.;<BR>e. hates the minister:<BR>सकलो<BR> जनोऽमात्यं जुगुप्सते, Ma. ii. Ph.:<BR>delighted e. one<BR>of the citizens:<BR>पौरान् प्रत्येकं ह्लादयाञ्चक्रे, R.;<BR>looking<BR>at e. one:<BR>प्रत्येकमवलोक्य, Ana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

everyday
EVERYDAY (adj.):<BR>(1) प्रात्यहिकः (की, कं),<BR>e.<BR>hunger:<BR>प्रात्यहिकक्षुत्, S. d.;<BR>(2) नित्यः (त्या, त्यं)<BR>(= regular),<BR>e. present:<BR>नित्यदक्षिणा, Mal.: v.<BR>Daily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

everything
EVERYTHING: सर्वम्, everybody does not know e.<BR>न सर्वः सर्वं जानाति, Mu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

every-time
EVERY-TIME: यदा यदा: v. Whenever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

every-way
EVERY-WAY, IN:<BR>(1) सर्वथा;<BR>(2) सर्वप्रकारेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

everywhere
EVERYWHERE:<BR>(1) सर्वत्र;<BR>(2) सर्वतः, you go e.:<BR>त्वं सर्वतोगामि, Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evict
EVICT: निःसारयति (c. of सृ) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eviction
EVICTION: निःसारणम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evidence
EVIDENCE (subs.):<BR>(1) साक्ष्यम् (of witnesses),<BR>to give e.:<BR>साक्ष्यं ददाति, Y.;<BR>e. may be direct and<BR>also hearsay:<BR>समक्षदर्शनात् साक्ष्यं श्रवणाच्चैव सिध्यति,<BR>M.;<BR>(2) प्रमाणम् (= any proof), does not estab- [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">Page251</a>]<BR>lish his claim by e.: उक्तं प्रमाणेन न प्रतिपादयति,<BR>K. b.; document (=written) possession (= real)<BR>and witnesses (=oral)<BR>are e.:<BR>प्रमाणं लिखितं भुक्तिः<BR> साक्षिणश्च, Y.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evidence
EVIDENCE (v.): प्रमाणयति (nomi.): v. To<BR>evince, prove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evident
EVIDENT:<BR>(1) स्पष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं), वि-,<BR>although e. the<BR>lustre of his body was not e.:<BR>स्पष्टोऽप्यविस्पष्टवपुः-<BR>प्रकाशः, Ki.;<BR>(2) व्यक्तः (क्ता, क्तं), अभि-,<BR>very e.<BR>from the long wet footsteps:<BR>सुव्यक्तमार्द्रपदपंक्तिभिरा-<BR>यताभिः, R.;<BR>(3) स्फुटः (टा, टं), परि-, to become e.<BR>स्फुटीभवति, Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evident
EVIDENT, TO BE:<BR>(1) प्रकाशते (काश्, c. 1.), M. n.;<BR>(2) विकश(स)ति (कश्<BR>or<BR>कस्, c. 1.),<BR>your untruth-<BR>fulness is e. from your act:<BR>तव कर्मणैव विकशत्य-<BR>सत्यता, Si. xv. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evident
EVIDENT, TO MAKE:<BR>(1) प्रकाशयति (c of काश्),<BR>who have made your intellect and character e.:<BR>प्रकाशितत्वन्मतिशीलसाराः, Ki.;<BR>(2) विकाश(स)यति<BR>(c. of कश्<BR>or<BR>कस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evidently
EVIDENTLY:<BR>(1) व्यक्तम्, e. I have been deceived:<BR>व्यक्तमस्मि विप्रलब्धा, D.;<BR>(2) स्पष्टम्, वि-,;<BR>(3)<BR>(3) स्फुटम्, परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evil
EVIL (adj,):<BR>I Having bad qualities:<BR>(1)<BR>दुष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं),<BR>quieting the e. ones:<BR>दुष्टप्रशान्तिः,<BR>Vi.;<BR>e. sleep:<BR>दुष्टनिद्रा, K.<BR>(2) by दुर् prefixed,<BR>e. doings:<BR>दुष्कर्माणि (n. pl.);<BR>e. speaking:<BR>दुर्वाक्यम्।<BR>II Not good: by कु- pref, at an e. moment:<BR>कुक्षणे;<BR>e. course:<BR>कुमार्गः;<BR>e. eye:<BR>कुदृष्टिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evil
EVIL (subs.):<BR>I Mischief, calamity: q. v.:<BR>अनिष्टम्।<BR>II Wickedness: q. v.: दुष्टता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evil
EVIL (adv.): v. Badly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evil-minded
EVIL-MINDED:<BR>(1) कुमति (mfn.);<BR>(2) दुराचारः<BR>(रा, रं);<BR>(3) दुष्प्रकृति (mfn.): v. Wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evince
EVINCE: दर्शयति (c. of दृश्): v. To show,<BR>manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eviscerate
EVISCERATE: अन्त्राणि अपनयति (नी, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>अपोहति<BR>(ऊह्, c. 1.) (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evoke
EVOKE:<BR>(1) आह्वयति (ह्वे, c. 1.) (= to call);<BR>(2)<BR>निष्कर्षति (कृष्, c. 1.) (= to draw out)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evolution
EVOLUTION:<BR>I Development: उद्भेदः,<BR>e. of<BR>affection:<BR>अनुरागस्योद्भेदः, Ma.<BR>II A series:<BR>परम्परा।<BR>III In arith: मूललाभः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evolve
EVOLVE (v.):<BR>I To disclose: q. v.: विवृणोति<BR>(वृ, c. 5.).<BR>II To emit: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

evulsion
EVULSION:<BR>(1) लुञ्चनम्, अव-, उत्-;<BR>(2) पाटनम्,<BR> उत्-, वि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ewe
EWE:<BR>(1) मेषी;<BR>(2) भेडी;<BR>(3) उरणी;<BR>(4) एडका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ewer
EWER: कमण्डलुः: v. Pitcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exact
EXACT (adj.):<BR>I Precise: q. v.: यथार्थः (र्था,<BR> र्थं).<BR>II Accurate, punctual: q. v.: स्ववहितः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exact
EXACT (v.): निष्कर्षति (कृष्, c. 1.): v. To extort<BR>take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exaction
EXACTION:<BR>I Extortion: q. v.: निष्कर्षः, -णम्।<BR>II That which is exacted: perh निष्कर्षः,<BR> -णम् (after उत्पीडनम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exactly
EXACTLY:<BR>I Precisely, accurately: q. v.:<BR>यथार्थतः।<BR>II Nicely: सूक्ष्मम्, Ph.:<BR>these are e.<BR>alike:<BR>नास्ति कश्चिदनयोर्विशेषः;<BR>e. so:<BR>एवमेव: v.<BR>Just (adv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exactness
EXACTNESS:<BR>I Accuracy: q. v.: शुद्धता।<BR>II<BR>Nicety: q. v.: सूक्ष्मता।<BR>III Carefulness:<BR>q.v.: अवहितता।<BR>IV Regularity: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exaggerate
EXAGGERATE (v.): perh. वर्धयति (c. of वृध्)<BR>or<BR>अधिकं कथयति (कथ्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exaggeration
EXAGGERATION:<BR>(1) अत्युक्तिः<BR>or<BR>अतिशयोक्तिः<BR>(= hyperbole).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exalt
EXALT:<BR>I Lit.: उन्नमयति (c. of नम्),<BR>e. ed by<BR>the echoes:<BR>प्रतिस्वनैरुन्नमितः (ता, तं), Ki.: v.<BR>To lift.<BR>II Fig., to elevate:<BR>(1) उन्नमयति,<BR> सम्-<BR>or<BR>उन्नतिं<BR>or<BR>समुन्नतिं नयति (नी, c. 1.), प्रापयति<BR>(c. of आप्) etc.,<BR>e. s some:<BR>कांश्चिन्नयत्युन्नतिम्, Mr.;<BR>(2) उच्छ्राययति, सम्-, (c. of श्रि), e. ing (his)<BR>prowess by arms:<BR>अस्त्रैर्वीर्यमुच्छ्राययिष्यन्, Vi.<BR>III<BR>To elate: उल्लासयति (c. of लस्), e. s Daśaratha:<BR>दशरथमुल्लासयति, An.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exaltation
EXALTATION:<BR>I The act: उन्नमनम्।<BR>II The<BR>state:<BR>(1) उन्नतिः, सम्-,।<BR>(2) उच्छ्रायः, सम्-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exalted
EXALTED:<BR>(1) उन्नतः (ता, तं), सम्-,<BR>bending the<BR>e.:<BR>उन्नतान्नमयन्, K.<BR>(2) उच्छ्रितः (ता, तं), सम्-,<BR>in a very e. minister:<BR>अत्युच्छ्रिते मन्त्रिणि, Mu.;<BR>(3) उच्चैः (= high),<BR>a more e. place:<BR>उच्चैस्तरं<BR> पदम्, Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exalted
EXALTED, TO BE: उन्नमति (नम्, c. 1.),<BR>as if the<BR>sky was e.:<BR>द्यौरुन्ननामेव, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

examination
EXAMINATION: परीक्षा,<BR>e. of gems:<BR>रत्नपरीक्षा,<BR>Mal.;<BR>e. -in-chief:<BR>*पूर्वपरीक्षा;<BR>post mortem<BR>e.:<BR>*प्रेतपरीक्षा;<BR>e. of urine:<BR>मूत्रपरीक्षा, Bha.;<BR>after e. (of a book): परीक्ष्य, Mal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

examine
EXAMINE (v.): परीक्षते, सं-, (ईक्ष्, c. 1.),<BR>one<BR>should e. and then form association:<BR>सङ्गतं परीक्ष्य<BR> कर्तव्यम्, Sa.;<BR>shall e. a sick man by look, touch<BR>and question:<BR>दर्शनस्पर्शनप्रश्नै रोगिणं परीक्षेत, Bha.;<BR>shall not e. witnesses in all cases of violence:<BR>साहसेसु च सर्वेषु न परीक्षेत साक्षिणः, N. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

examiner
EXAMINER:<BR>(1) परीक्षकः<BR>or<BR>परीक्षिन् (m.),<BR>e. of<BR>coins:<BR>नाणकपरीक्षी, Y.;<BR>(2) प्राश्निकः (by ques-<BR>-tions), your Reverence should take the post of e.:<BR>भगवत्या प्राश्निकपदमध्यासितव्यम्, Mal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

example
EXAMPLE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) उदाहरणम्,<BR>I am an e. of<BR>it:<BR>तस्याहमस्म्युदाहरणभूता, D. vi.;<BR>(2) निदर्शनम्,<BR>with e. s:<BR>सनिदर्शनः (ना, नं), K.;<BR>(3) दृष्टान्तः,<BR>an e. of the weak:<BR>दुर्बलानां दृष्टान्तः, M. n.: v.<BR>Also instance.<BR>II Fig., =way: q. v.<BR>“to<BR>give e.”:<BR>पन्थानं दर्श्यति (c. of दृश्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exanimate
EXANIMATE:<BR>I Dead: q. v.: गतजीवितः (ता,<BR> तं).<BR>II Spiritless, dejected: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exasperate
EXASPERATE:<BR>I To enrage: q. v.:<BR>(1) उत्-<BR>कोपयति (c. of कुप्);<BR>(2) संक्षोभयति (c.<BR>of क्षुभ्).<BR>II To aggravate: वर्धयति (c.<BR>of वृध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exasperation
EXASPERATION:<BR>I Irritation: उत्कोपनम्।<BR>II<BR>Increase: वृद्धिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excavate
EXCAVATE:<BR>(1) खनति: v. To dig.:<BR>(2) विदारयति<BR>(c. of दॄ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excavation
EXCAVATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) खननम्;<BR>(2)<BR>विदारणम्।<BR>II A cavity or hollow q. v.: खातम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excavator
EXCAVATOR:<BR>I A digger: q. v.<BR>II A<BR>machine: *विदारिणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exceed
EXCEED (v.):<BR>(1) अतिक्रामति<BR>or<BR>क्राम्यति (क्रम्, c.<BR>1. and 4.);<BR>(2) अत्येति (इ, c. 2.), Ki.: v.<BR>Surpass, excel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exceeding
EXCEEDING (= prep.):<BR>(1) expr. by verb;<BR>(2) by अति- in comp. (rare),<BR>e. human spirit<BR>and prowess:<BR>अतिमानुषप्राणबलः (ला, लं), D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exceeding
EXCEEDING, EXCEEDINGLY (adv.):<BR>(1) अति,<BR>you are e. arrogant:<BR>अति हि नामावलिप्यसे, Vi.;<BR>(2) अत्यन्तम्,<BR>e. proud:<BR>अत्यन्तमानिन् (f. नी), Mu.;<BR>(3) अतिमात्रम्;<BR>(4) अतीव: v. Also extremely,<BR>excessively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excel
EXCEL (v. t.):<BR>(1) प्रकृष्यते<BR>or<BR>उत्- (pass. of कृष्)<BR>(= to be drawn up) (with abl.),<BR>no body e.s<BR>Viśvāmitra in greatness:<BR>न खलु विश्वामित्रान्महत्वेन<BR> कश्चिदपरः प्रकृष्यते, Vi. i.;<BR>(2) अतिवर्तते (वृत्, c.<BR>1.) (= to be beyond),<BR>what is eulogy to you<BR>whose dignity e.s the range of eulogy:<BR>का ते स्तुतिः<BR> स्तुतिपथादतिवृत्तधाम्नः, Vi.;<BR>(3) अतिशेते (शी, c. 2.)<BR>(= to lie beyond),<BR>in this your Excellency e. s<BR>your ancestors:<BR>पूर्वान् महाभागतयातिशेषे, R. v. 14;<BR>(4) अतिरिच्यते (pass. of रिच्) (to be more)<BR>(with abl.);<BR>truth e. s even thousand horse-<BR>sacrifices:<BR>अश्वमेधसहस्राद्धि सत्यमेवातिरिच्यते, H.<BR>iv.;<BR>(5) अधरयति (nomi.) (= put down:<BR>q. v.),<BR>e. ling the sages in his pure acts:<BR>चरितै-<BR>र्मुनीनधरयन् शुचिभिः, Ki. vi. 24.;<BR>(6) तिरस्करोति<BR>(= to eclipse: q. v.), M. n;<BR>(7) अभिभवति (भू,<BR>c. 1.) (= to humble: q. v.),<BR>e. ling the frag-<BR>rance of other flowers:<BR>अभिभूतान्यकुसुमपरिमलम्, K.;<BR>(8) जयति (जि, c. 1.) (= to conquer: q. v.),<BR>Si. i. 19.;<BR>(9) हेपयति (c. of ही) (= to put to<BR>shame), Ki. xiii. 41.;<BR>(10) निन्दति (निन्द्, c.<BR>1.) (= to censure: q. v.), Gi. ii. 6.: v. To<BR>surpass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excellence
EXCELLENCE:<BR>I Superiority:<BR>(1) उत्कर्षः or<BR>प्रकर्षः;<BR>(2) उत्कृष्टता;<BR>(3) विशिष्टता: v. Also<BR>greatness, loftiness.<BR>II Any good quality:<BR>गुणः<BR>or<BR>महद्गुणः<BR>or<BR>विशिष्टगुणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excellency
EXCELLENCY:<BR>I Excellence: q. v.<BR>II A<BR>title: देवः (f. वी) (applied to kings and<BR>ministers); महाभागः (गा, गं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excellent
EXCELLENT:<BR>I Admirable, eminent: q. v.:<BR>(1) उत्कृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>(2) विशिष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>(3) प्रकृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं), the bird parrot is of e. form:<BR>शुकपक्षी प्रकृष्टरूपः, S. p. b.<BR>II Extremes: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excellently
EXCELLENTLY: expr. by adj.: v. Also<BR>admirably, well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

except
EXCEPT (v.):<BR>I Trans.: to leave out:<BR>(1)<BR>वर्जयति, वि-, (वृज्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) अपास्यति (अस्,<BR>c. 4.).<BR>II Intrans, to object: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

except
EXCEPT (conj.): यदि न: v. Unless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

except
EXCEPT, EXCEPTING (prep.):<BR>(1) by part.s [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">Page253</a>]<BR>वर्जयित्वा, विहाय, अपहाय, मुक्त्वा, etc. (with acc.),<BR>e. your acceptance of Sitā:<BR>सीतायाः स्वीकारं वर्जयित्वा,<BR>M. n.;<BR>e. Damayantī:<BR>विहाय भैमीम्, N. i. 13;<BR>(2) ऋते (with acc. or abl.),<BR>e. the sun:<BR>ऋते रवेः,<BR>Si. i. 33.: v. Also but, without.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exception
EXCEPTION (subs.):<BR>I Excluding: वर्जनम्,<BR> वि-, Ph.:<BR>with the e. of:<BR>वर्जयित्वा (with acc.):<BR>v. Except (prep.).<BR>II To rules, etc.: अपवादः,<BR>e. to theft:<BR>चौर्यापवादः, Viv.; like precepts by e. s:<BR>अपवादैरिवोत्सर्गाः, Ku. ii. 27.<BR>III Objection:<BR>q. v.: आपत्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exceptionable
EXCEPTIONABLE: v. Objectionable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exceptional
EXCEPTIONAL: i. e. uncommon: असाधारण (f.<BR>णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excerpt
EXCERPT:<BR>I उद्धरति (हृ, c. 1.).<BR>II Subs.:<BR>expr. by उद्धृतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excerption
EXCERPTION:<BR>I The act: उद्धरणम्।<BR>II Except:<BR>expr. by उद्धृतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excess
EXCESS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) आधिक्यम्;<BR>(2) अतिरेकः<BR>M. n.;<BR>(3) often by adj.: अधिकः (का, कं)<BR>or<BR>अतिरिक्तः (क्ता, क्तं), when there is e. of bile:<BR>पित्तेऽधिके, Bha.;<BR>e. population:<BR>अतिरिक्तजनः,<BR>M. n.<BR>To be in e. of:<BR>अतिरिच्यते (pass. of रिच्)<BR>(with abl.).<BR>II Intemperance, dissipation:<BR>q. v.: perh. अतिभोगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excessive
EXCESSIVE:<BR>(1) अति- in comp.,<BR>e. rain:<BR>अतिवृष्टिः;<BR>e. drinking:<BR>अतिपानम्;<BR>(2) अतिशय- in comp.,<BR>e.<BR>devotion:<BR>अतिशयभक्तिः;<BR>(3) अत्यन्तः (न्ता, न्तं)<BR>e. crying<BR>अन्यन्तं रुदितम्, R.;<BR>(4) नितान्तः (न्ता,<BR> न्तं);<BR>(5) सातिशयः (या, यं): v. Abundant,<BR>much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excessively
EXCESSIVELY:<BR>(1) अतीव,<BR>e. agitated:<BR>अतीव व्याकुलित-<BR>चित्तः, P.;<BR>(2) नितान्तम्,<BR>e. fond:<BR>नितान्तवत्सलः,<BR>R.;<BR>(3) सातिशयम्: v. Exceedingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exchange
EXCHANGE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: विनिमयः,<BR>how many<BR>pomegranates are to be got in e.:<BR>कति दाडिमानि<BR> लभ्यानि तद्विनिमयेन भवन्ति, Li.; e. of qualities:<BR>गुणानां विनिमयः, Ki.: v. Also change, inter-<BR>-change. Ph.:<BR>take my life in e. of hers:<BR>विहाय<BR> जीवितं तस्या गृहाण मम जीवितम्;<BR>bill of e.:<BR>*विनिमय-<BR>पत्रम्;<BR>e. is in favour of London:<BR>*लण्डनानुकूलो<BR> विनिमयः।<BR>II E. place: श्रेष्ठिचत्वरम् (?); *विनिमय-<BR>गृहम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exchange
EXCHANGE (v.):<BR>(1) मयते, नि-, (gen.) विनि-,<BR>(मे, c. 1.);<BR>(2) परिवर्तयति (c. of वृत्) (= change:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(3) by circumlo., e. these for fuel:<BR>इमान्दत्त्वा काष्ठान्याहर, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exchangeable
EXCHANGEABLE: विनिमेयः (या, यं); विनिमययोग्यः<BR>(ग्या, ग्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exchequer
EXCHEQUER:<BR>I Treasury: q. v.: कोषः,<BR>lord<BR>of the e.:<BR>कोषपतिः।<BR>II A court: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excisable
EXCISABLE (adj.): *उपशुल्कार्ह (f. र्हा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excise
EXCISE (subs.): i. e.<BR>e. duty:<BR>*उपशुल्कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exciseman
EXCISEMAN: *उपशुल्कग्राहकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excision
EXCISION: उच्छेदः: v. Extirpation destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excitable
EXCITABLE<BR>(1) उत्तेजनीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) कोपनः<BR>(ना, नं) (= irritable).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excitant
EXCITANT: दीपनः (नी, नं), Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excitation
EXCITATION:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) उत्तेजनम्, सम्-;<BR>(2)<BR>उत्कोपनम्;<BR>(3) उद्दीपनम् (= kindling).<BR>II Caus-<BR>-ing: जननम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excite
EXCITE:<BR>I To stir up:<BR>(1) उत्तेजयति, सम्-, (c.<BR>of तिज्),<BR>I will e. the king's servants to release<BR>my friend:<BR>सुहृदः परिमोक्षणाय नरेन्द्रभृत्यानुत्तेजयामि,<BR>Mr.;<BR>speech e. ing an enemy:<BR>शत्रोरुत्तेजनकरी वाक्,<BR>Sah.;<BR>(2) उत्कोपयति (c. of कुप्) (a stronger<BR>term),<BR>to e. head-ache:<BR>शिरःशूलमुत्कोपयति, Vi.;<BR>(3) उद्दीपयति (c. of दीप्) (= to kindle: q. v.).<BR>II To produce, cause: q. v.: जनयति (c. of<BR>जन्),<BR>to e. envy:<BR>ईष्यां जनयति, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excitement
EXCITEMENT:<BR>I Exciting: उत्तेजनम्।<BR>II Agita-<BR>-tion, emotion: q. v.: संक्षोभः।<BR>III That<BR>which excites: उत्तेजनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exciter
EXCITER (adj.):<BR>(1) उत्तेजक (f. जिका);<BR>(2)<BR>उत्कोपयितृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exciting
EXCITING (adj.): उत्तेजक (f. जिका);<BR>(2) उत्तेजनकरः<BR>(री, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exclaim
EXCLAIM: गदति (गद्, c. 1.): v. To speak, cry<BR>out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exclaimer
EXCLAIMER: वक्तृ (f. क्त्री): v. Speaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exclamation
EXCLAMATION: आक्रोशः: v. Clamour, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exclamation
EXCLAMATION:<BR>I Expressing exclamation:<BR>आक्रोशव्यञ्जक (mn.) (?).<BR>II Using excla-<BR>-mation: आक्रोशिन् (f. नी) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exclude
EXCLUDE (v.):<BR>I To turn out, eject:<BR>(1)<BR>बहिष्करोति;<BR>(2) निःसारयति (c. of सृ).<BR>II To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">Page254</a>]<BR>hinder: q. v.: निषेधति (सिध्, c. 1.).<BR>III To<BR>except: वर्जयति (वृज्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exclusion
EXCLUSION:<BR>I Turning out:<BR>(1) बहिष्करणम्;<BR>(2) निःसारणम्।<BR>II Exception: बर्जनम्, वि-,<BR> परि-।<BR>III Rejection: प्रत्याख्यानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exclusive
EXCLUSIVE: Lit.: निवारक (f. रिका).<BR>II Not<BR>shared by others: अनन्यसाधारण (f. णी) or<BR>अनन्यसामान्य (f. न्या). Ph.:<BR>e. of horse:<BR>अश्वारोहा-<BR>तिरेकेण<BR>or<BR>अश्वारोहातिरिक्तः (क्ता, क्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exclusively
EXCLUSIVELY: अनन्यसाधारणम्; अनन्यसामान्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exclusiveness
EXCLUSIVENESS: अनन्यसाधारणता, अनन्यसामान्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excogitate
EXCOGITATE:<BR>(1) उद्भावयति (c. of भू);<BR>(2) परि-<BR>कल्पयति (c. of कॢप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excogitation
EXCOGITATION:<BR>(1) उद्भावनम्, सम्-;<BR>(2) परि-<BR>कल्पनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excommunicate
EXCOMMUNICATE:<BR>I Lit.: समाजाद् बहिष्करोति।<BR>E. d:<BR>समाजवहिष्कृतः (ता, तं); अपपात्रितः (ता, तं),<BR>Viv.<BR>II To forbid: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excommunication
EXCOMMUNICATION: समाजाद्बहिष्करणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excoriate
EXCORIATE: चर्म पीडयति (पीड्, c. 10.) (with<BR>gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excoriation
EXCORIATION:<BR>I Lit.: चर्मपीडनम्।<BR>II Spolia-<BR>-tion: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excrement
EXCREMENT:<BR>(1) उच्चारः;<BR>(2) अव(प)स्करः: v.<BR>Dung, ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excremental
EXCREMENTAL:<BR>(1) उच्चरितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2)<BR>अव(प)स्कृतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excrescence
EXCRESCENCE: आविर्भावः: v. Also encumb-<BR>-rance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excrete
EXCRETE:<BR>(1) उत्सृजति (सृज्, c. 6.);<BR>(2) निः-<BR>सारयति (c. of सृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excretion
EXCRETION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) उत्सर्गः;<BR>(2)<BR>निःसारणम्।<BR>II Excrement: q. v.: उच्चारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excretory
EXCRETORY (subs.): *मलवाहिनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excruciate
EXCRUCIATE (v.): अत्यन्तं व्यथयति (c. of व्यथ्):<BR>v. To pain, exceedingly. Ph.: e. ing pain:<BR>मर्मच्छेदिनी<BR>or<BR>अरुन्तुदा वेदना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exculpate
EXCULPATE:<BR>(1) शोधयति, वि-, परि-, (c. of शुध्)<BR>if he does not e. himself:<BR>नात्मानं चेद्विशोधयेत्, Y.;<BR>(2) मोचयति (मुच्, c. 10.) (= free) (when the<BR>meaning is clear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exculpation
EXCULPATION:<BR>(1) शोधनम्, वि-, परि-;<BR>(2) मोचनम्<BR>(= freeing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exculpatory
EXCULPATORY: expr. by comp., e. evidence:<BR>शोधनप्रमाणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excursion
EXCURSION:<BR>I Expedition: अभिद्रवः।<BR>To make<BR>an e.:<BR>अभिद्रवति (द्रु, c. 1.), Mah.<BR>II A strip:<BR>q. v.:<BR>to make an e. into Cashmere:<BR>काश्मीरान्द्रष्टुं<BR> गच्छति।<BR>III Deviation, digression: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excursive
EXCURSIVE:<BR>I Lit.: पर्यटनशीलः (ला, लं).<BR>II<BR>Fig.: सर्वतोधाविन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excusable
EXCUSABLE:<BR>(1) मर्षणीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) क्षन्तव्यः<BR>(व्या, व्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excuse
EXCUSE (v.):<BR>I To absolve: मोचयति (मुच्, c.<BR>10.).<BR>II To forgive, pardon: q. v.: मर्षयति<BR>(c. of मृष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excuse
EXCUSE (subs.):<BR>I Release: मोचनम्।<BR>II For-<BR>-giving: मर्षणम्,<BR>“in e. for it”:<BR>तन्मर्षणाय।<BR>III<BR>Plea, apology: उत्तरम् (= reply).<BR>IV That<BR>which e. s: expr. by verb:<BR>“it hath the e. of<BR>youth”:<BR>शैशवाद्धेतोरिदं मर्षयितव्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

excuseless
EXCUSELESS:<BR>(1) अमर्षणीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) अक्षमार्ह<BR>(f. र्हा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

execrable
EXECRABLE: अतिगर्हितः (ता, तं): v. Abomin-<BR>-able, detestable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

execrate
EXECRATE:<BR>I To curse: q. v.: शपति (शप्, c.<BR>1.).<BR>II To detest, hate: q. v.: जुगुप्सते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

execration
EXECRATION:<BR>I Curse: q. v.: शापः; अभिशापः।<BR>II Anything detested: जुगुप्सितः (ता, तं);<BR>अतिगर्हितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

execute
EXECUTE:<BR>I To accomplish, carry out:<BR>q. v.: अनुतिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.), to e. an order:<BR>शासनमनुतिष्ठति, R.<BR>II Of deeds: करोति।<BR>III<BR>To put to death: q. v.: व्यापादयति (c. of पद्).<BR>Ph.:<BR>about to be e. d:<BR>वध्यमानः (ना, नं),<BR>Mu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

execution
EXECUTION:<BR>I Accomplishment:<BR>(1)<BR>अनुष्ठानम्;<BR>(2) निष्पादनम्;<BR>(3) निर्वाहः।<BR>II Of<BR>deeds: करणम्।<BR>III Putting to death:<BR>व्यापादनम्। Ph.:<BR>place of e.:<BR>वध्यभूमिः, Mu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

executioner
EXECUTIONER: घातकः; वधाधिकृतः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

executive
EXECUTIVE (adj.):<BR>I Pertaining to execu-<BR>-tion: expr. by comp.,<BR>e. duty:<BR>अनुष्ठाननियोगः,<BR>e. power:<BR>*अनुष्ठानक्षमता।<BR>II Fitted for execution:<BR>(1) कार्यक्षमः (मा, मं);<BR>(2) कार्यकुशलः (ला, लं),<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

executive
EXECUTIVE (subs.): *अनुष्ठानाधिकृताः (m. pl.);<BR>व्यक्तिक्रमशासकाः (m. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

executor
EXECUTOR (m.), EXECUTRIX (f.):<BR>I Doer:<BR>q. v.: निष्पादयितृ (f. त्री).<BR>II Of a will:<BR>*इच्छापत्रानुशासकः (f. सिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

executory
EXECUTORY:<BR>I Executive: q. v.<BR>II In law:<BR>*अनुष्ठेयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exegesis
EXEGESIS: विवृतिः: v. Explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exegete
EXEGETE, EXEGETIST: व्याख्यातृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2)<BR>व्याकर्तृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exemplar
EXEMPLAR: आदर्शः: v. Model.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exemplary
EXEMPLARY:<BR>(1) expr. by आदर्शः;<BR>(2) प्रशस्यः<BR>(स्या, स्यं) (= commendable).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exemplification
EXEMPLIFICATION: expr. by verb: v. Below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exemplify
EXEMPLIFY:<BR>(1) उदाहरणेन<BR>or<BR>दृष्टान्तेन<BR>or<BR>सनिदर्शनं<BR> स्पष्टीकरोति<BR>or<BR>स्फुटीकरोति;<BR>(2) उदाहरति (हृ, c. 1.),<BR>these have been e. ed in order:<BR>तत्क्रमेणोदाहृतम्,<BR>Kuv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exempt
EXEMPT (v.): मोचयति (मुच्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>free, release.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exempt
EXEMPT (adj.): expr. by निर्<BR>or<BR>वीत pref. d,<BR>e. from birth and decrepitude:<BR>वीतजन्मजरस् (mfn.),<BR>Ki. v. 22.: v. Free from, devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exemption
EXEMPTION:<BR>(1) मुक्तिः: v. Feedom;<BR>(2) by<BR>deriv.,<BR>e. from anxiety:<BR>निश्चिन्तता, बीतचिन्तता,<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exequial
EXEQUIAL:<BR>(1) और्द्धदेहिकः (की, कं);<BR>(2) अन्त्येष्टि-<BR>in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exequies
EXEQUIES (pl.):<BR>(1) और्द्धदेहिकम्;<BR>(2) अन्त्येष्टि-<BR>क्रिया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exercise
EXERCISE (subs.):<BR>I Application, employ-<BR>-ment: q. v.: प्रयोगः।<BR>II Performance, prac-<BR>-tice: अनुष्ठानम्।<BR>III Exertion:<BR>(1) व्यायामः,<BR>place of e.:<BR>व्यायामभूमिः, Ka.;<BR>(2) श्रमः, परि-,<BR>took e. with iron maces:<BR>अयोदण्डेन श्रममकरोत्, K.;<BR>tired with e.:<BR>परिश्रमक्लान्तः (न्ता, न्तं), Ki.<BR>IV<BR>A disquisition^1, task: q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exercise
EXERCISE (v. t.):<BR>(1) व्यायामं करोति:<BR>(2) श्रमं<BR> करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exercise
EXERCISE (v. i.):<BR>I To use: q. v.: प्रयुंक्ते (युज्,<BR>c. 7.).<BR>II To practise: q. v.: अभ्यस्यति<BR>(अस्, c. 4.).<BR>III To discipline: शिक्षयति<BR>(c. of शिक्ष्).<BR>IV To cause to e.: व्यायामं<BR> कारयति (c. of कृ), Ka.<BR>V To afflict: आया-<BR>सयति (c. of यस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exert
EXERT (v.):<BR>I To e oneself: यत्नं करोति: v.<BR>To endeavour, attempt.<BR>II To employ,<BR>apply: q. v.: प्रयुंक्ते (युज्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exertion
EXERTION: आयासः,<BR>from e.:<BR>आयासात्, Si.: v.<BR>Effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exfoliate
EXFOLIATE: परिपुटति (पुट्, c. 6.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exfoliation
EXFOLIATION: परिपुटनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhalation
EXHALATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) उद्गारः;<BR>(2)<BR>उत्क्षेपः।<BR>II That which is exhaled: perh.<BR>उद्गारः, N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhale
EXHALE:<BR>(1) उद्गिरति (गॄ, c. 6.), to e. a smell:<BR>परिमलम् उद्गिरति, Me.;<BR>(2) उत्क्षिपति (क्षिप्,<BR>c. 6.) (= to throw up): v. To emit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhaust
EXHAUST (v.):<BR>I To empty: q. v.: शून्यी-<BR>करोति।<BR>II To dry up: q. v.: शोषयति (c. of<BR>शुष्).<BR>III To consume: क्षयं<BR>or<BR>परिक्षयं करोति।<BR>IV To weary: खेदयति (c. of खिद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhaustion
EXHAUSTION:<BR>I Emptying:<BR>(1) शून्यीकरणम्;<BR>(2) रिक्तीकरणम्।<BR>II Drying up: शोषणम्, वि-,<BR> उत्-।<BR>III Consumption: क्षयः, परि-।<BR>IV<BR>Fatigue: q. v.: खेदः। v. Dejection: अव-<BR>सादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhaustive
EXHAUSTIVE: क्षयिन् (f. णी), परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhaustless
EXHAUSTLESS: अक्षयः (या, यं): v. Inexhausti-<BR>-ble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhibit
EXHIBIT:<BR>(1) दर्शयति, प्र-, उत्-, (c. of दृश्): v.<BR>To shew;<BR>(2) प्रकटयति (nomi.)<BR>or<BR>प्रकटीकरोति,<BR>discharged the magician who had e. ed skill:<BR>प्रकटीकृतपाटवं विद्येश्वरं विससर्ज, D.;<BR>(3) व्यञ्जयति<BR>(c. of अञ्ज्),<BR>e. ing your good fortune:<BR>सौमाग्यं<BR> ते व्यञ्जयन्ती, Me.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhibit
EXHIBIT (subs.): निदर्शनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhibition
EXHIBITION:<BR>I Display:<BR>(1) दर्शनम्, प्र-,<BR>(2)<BR>प्रकटीकरणम्।<BR>II A show: प्रदर्शनी (?).<BR>III A<BR>scholarship: वृत्तिः, (or fully) छात्रवृत्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhibitioner
EXHIBITIONER:<BR>(1) वृत्तिभुज् (mfn.);<BR>(2) छात्रवृत्ति-<BR>भोगिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhilarate
EXHILARATE: उल्लासयति (c. of लस्): v. To<BR>cheer, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhilarating
EXHILARATING (adj.):<BR>(1) उल्लासिन् (f. नी), सम्-;<BR>(2) उल्लासकरः (री, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhilaration
EXHILARATION: उल्लासः: v. Cheerfulness, de-<BR>-light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhort
EXHORT (v.): प्रोत्साहयति (c. of सह्): v. To<BR>incite, advise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhortation
EXHORTATION: प्रोत्साहः, -नम्: v. Incitement,<BR>advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhortative
EXHORTATIVE, EXHORTATORY:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) प्रोत्साहक (f. हिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhorter
EXHORTER: प्रोत्साहकः: v. Inciter, adviser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhumation
EXHUMATION: उत्खननम्: e. of a corpse:<BR>शवोत्खननम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exhume
EXHUME (v.): उत्खनति, प्र-, (खन्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exigence
EXIGENCE, EXIGENCY:<BR>e. of business:<BR>कार्यगौरवम्;<BR>“in the present e. of affairs:”<BR>वर्तमाने कार्यसंकटे;<BR>in<BR>this e.:<BR>अस्मिन् कृच्छे: v. Urgency, import-<BR>-ance, crisis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exigent
EXIGENT (adj.): गुरुतरः (रा, रं) (= very impor-<BR>-tant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exile
EXILE (subs.):<BR>I Banishment: q. v.: निर्वासनम्।<BR>II The person e. d: निर्वासितः<BR>or<BR>विवासितः<BR>or<BR>प्रव्राजितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exile
EXILE (v.): निर्वासयति (c. of वस्): v. To banish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exist
EXIST:<BR>I To be: q. v.: अस्ति (अस्, c. 2.),<BR>everybody would believe that he does not e.:<BR>सर्वो<BR> लोको नायमस्तीति प्रतीयात्, S.;<BR>(2) वर्तते (वृत्, c.<BR>1.), H.<BR>II To live, remain: q. v.: तिष्ठति,<BR> अव-, (स्था, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

existence
EXISTENCE:<BR>(1) अस्तित्वम् (as opposed to non-e.),<BR>e. of God:<BR>ब्रह्मास्तित्वम्, S.;<BR>(2) अवस्थानम्<BR>or<BR>स्थितिः<BR>(= continuance),<BR>birth, e. and destruction:<BR>जन्म-<BR>स्थितिनाशाः, S.;<BR>(3) जीवनम् (= life: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

existent
EXISTENT: वर्तमानः (ना, नं). To be e.: v. To<BR>exist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exit
EXIT:<BR>(1) निष्क्रमः;<BR>(2) निर्गमः;<BR>(3) निर्याणम्।<BR>E. (in drama) निष्क्रान्तः (न्ता, न्तं). Exeunt<BR>(pl.) or<BR>e. omnes:<BR>निष्क्रान्ताः सर्वे, Y.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exodus
EXODUS:<BR>(1) निर्याणम्,<BR>e. of the Jews:<BR>*इहुदीनां<BR> निर्याणम्;<BR>(2) निर्गमः, -णम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exonerate
EXONERATE: शोधयति (c. of शुध्): v. To ex-<BR>-culpate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exorable
EXORABLE:<BR>(1) अनुनेयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) प्रसादनीयः<BR>(या, यं);<BR>(3) or by circumlo.,<BR>he is e.:<BR>स<BR> अनुनयं गृह्णाति<BR>or<BR>प्रसादयितुं शक्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exorbitance
EXORBITANCE, EXORBITANCY: v. Excess,<BR>enormity, extravagance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exorbitant
EXORBITANT: अत्यधिकः (का, कं): v. Excessive,<BR>extravagant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exorbitantly
EXORBITANTLY: अत्यधिकम्: v. Excessively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exorcise
EXORCISE:<BR>(1) भूतं दूरीकरोति;<BR>(2) भूतावेशात् मोच-<BR>यति (मुच्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exorcism
EXORCISM: भूतापसारणम्; भूतप्रतिषेधः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exordium
EXORDIUM: मुखबन्धः: v. Preface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exoteric
EXOTERIC: साधारणः (णी, णं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exotic
EXOTIC: विदेशीयः (या, यं) (= foreign: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expand
EXPAND (v. t.): प्रसारयति (c. of सृ): v. To<BR>spread, extend, open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expand
EXPAND (v. i.): प्रसरति (सृ, c. 1.): v. To spread,<BR>extend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expanse
EXPANSE: प्रसरः: v. Extent. Ph.:<BR>in the e. of<BR>heaven:<BR>विततनमसि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expansion
EXPANSION: प्रसारः<BR>or<BR>प्रसरः: v. Extension,<BR>space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expansive
EXPANSIVE:<BR>(1) प्रसारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) प्रसर्पिन्<BR>(f. णी): v. Also diffusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expatiate
EXPATIATE:<BR>I To rove: q. v.<BR>II To enlarge:<BR>q.v.: प्रपञ्चयति (पञ्च्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expatriate
EXPATRIATE: स्वराष्ट्राद्विप्रवासयति (c. of वस्), Y.:<BR>v. To banish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expatriation
EXPATRIATION: स्वराष्ट्राद्विप्रवासनम्: v. Banish-<BR>-ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expect
EXPECT:<BR>(1) उत्पश्यति (दृश्, c. 1.) (= to look<BR>forward),<BR>e. ing the fierce fall of the lion:<BR>उत्पश्यतः<BR> सिंहनिपातमुग्रम्, R.;<BR>(2) उत्प्रेक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1)<BR>(= 1), M. n.;<BR>(3) तर्कयति (तर्क्, c. 10.) (=to<BR>fancy: q. v.);<BR>(4) सम्भावयति (c. of भू) (= to<BR>believe: q. v.);<BR>(5) प्रतीक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.) (= to<BR>wait for: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expectable
EXPECTABLE: उत्प्रेक्ष्य (f. क्ष्या)<BR>or<BR>उत्प्रेक्षणीयः<BR>(या, यं): v. To expect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expectance
EXPECTANCE, EXPECTANCY:<BR>I Expectation:<BR>q. v.<BR>II Hope: आशा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expectant
EXPECTANT: उत्प्रेक्षकः: v. Candidate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expectation
EXPECTATION:<BR>I The act: expr. by verb,<BR>I<BR>was in e. of it:<BR>तदहमुदपश्यम्।<BR>II Hope: q. v.:<BR>आशा,<BR>it is beyond our e.s:<BR>आशातीतमेतत्।<BR>III<BR>Promise: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expectorate
EXPECTORATE: उद्गिरति (गॄ, c. 6.): v. To spit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expectoration
EXPECTORATION: उद्गारः: v. Spittle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expediency
EXPEDIENCY:<BR>I Fitness: q. v.: युक्तता।<BR>II Self-<BR>-interest: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expedient
EXPEDIENT (adj.): उचितः (ता, तं): v. Fit,<BR>proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expedient
EXPEDIENT (subs.): उपायः: v. Means, shift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expedite
EXPEDITE:<BR>I To hasten: q. v.: त्वरयति (c.<BR>of त्वर्).<BR>II To despatch: q. v.: विसृजति<BR>(सृज्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expedition
EXPEDITION:<BR>I Haste: q. v.: त्वरा।<BR>II De-<BR>-parture: q. v.: यात्रा।: v. Attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expeditious
EXPEDITIOUS: त्वरान्वितः (ता, तं): v. Quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expeditiously
EXPEDITIOUSLY: त्वरितम्: v. Speedily, hastily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expel
EXPEL: निरस्यति (अस्, c. 4.): v. To banish,<BR>drive away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expened
EXPENED: व्ययते (व्यय्, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>व्ययं करोति: v.<BR>To spend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expenditure
EXPENDITURE: व्ययः,<BR>heads of e. increased:<BR>व्यय-<BR>मुखान्यवर्द्धन्त, D. viii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expense
EXPENSE: व्ययः, परि-,<BR>e. s connected with commo-<BR>dities:<BR>व्ययः पण्यसमुद्भवः, Y.;<BR>and who have e. s<BR>and no income:<BR>निराया व्ययवन्तश्च, Y.;<BR>at the e. of<BR>food:<BR>भक्तव्ययेन, K. b.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expenseless
EXPENSELESS:<BR>(1) व्ययरहितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) व्यय-<BR>शून्यः (न्या, न्यं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expensive
EXPENSIVE:<BR>I Dear: q. v.: बहुमूल्यः (ल्या, ल्यं).<BR>II Requiring expense: expr. by circumlo,<BR>living here is e.:<BR>अत्र जीवनं बहुव्ययसाध्यम्।<BR>III<BR>Lavish: बहुव्ययिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expensively
EXPENSIVELY:<BR>(1) बहुव्ययेन;<BR>(2) महता व्ययेन:<BR>v. Dearly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expensiveness
EXPENSIVENESS:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by circumlo:<BR>v. Expensive (II).<BR>II Costliness: q. v.:<BR>बहुमूल्यता।<BR>III Extravagance: बहुव्ययिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

experience
EXPERIENCE (subs.):<BR>I Knowledge: q. v.:<BR>अनुभवः।<BR>II Practical wisdom: बहुदर्शिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

experience
EXPERIENCE (v.).<BR>I Lit.: अनुभवति (भू, c. 1.),<BR>to e. pain:<BR>वेदनामनुभवति, Ki.<BR>II To exercise:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

experienced
EXPERIENCED (adj.): i. e. wise:<BR>(1) बहुदर्शिन्<BR>(f. नी);<BR>(2) बहुदृश्वन् (mfn.)<BR>(3) परिदृष्टकार्यः<BR>(र्या, र्यं) (in work), B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

experiment
EXPERIMENT (subs.): *संपरीक्षा (?): v. Trial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

experiment
EXPERIMENT (v.): संपरीक्षते (ईक्ष, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

experimental
EXPERIMENTAL:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by comp. or<BR>adv.<BR>II Experimented: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

experimentally
EXPERIMENTALLY: संपरीक्ष्य; बहुदर्शनेन (= by<BR>experiment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expert
EXPERT:<BR>(1) दक्षः (क्षा, क्षं);<BR>(2) प्रवीणः (णा,<BR> णं);<BR>(3) कृतिन् (f. नी): v. Able, skilful,<BR>dexterous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expertly
EXPERTLY: प्रावीण्येन: v. Skilfully, dexterously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expertness
EXPERTNESS:<BR>(1) दाक्ष्यम्;<BR>(2) प्रावीण्यम्: v.<BR>Skill, dexterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expiable
EXPIABLE: मार्जनीयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expiate
EXPIATE:<BR>(1) शोधयति (c. of शुध्) (= to clear:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(2) मार्जयति (मृज्, c. 10.); (= to<BR>efface: q. v.);<BR>(3) पुनाति (पू, c. 9.) (= to<BR>purify), Brahmins' sins are e. d by sacrifices:<BR>होमैर्द्विजातयः पापेभ्य: पूयन्ते, V. s.;<BR>(4) प्रायश्चित्तं<BR> करोति, चरति (चर्, c. 1.), etc. (= to perform<BR>expiation),<BR>I will e. your transgression:<BR>व्यति-<BR>क्रमाद्वः प्रायश्चित्तं चरिष्यामि, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expiation
EXPIATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) शोधनम्;<BR>(2) मार्ज-<BR>नम्;<BR>(3) पाबनम्,; At.<BR>II The means:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रायश्चित्तम्;<BR>(1) प्रायश्चेतनम्, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expiatory
EXPIATORY: पावनः (नी, नं),<BR>e. rite:<BR>पावनो विधिः,<BR>Pa. Ph.:<BR>e. ceremony:<BR>प्रायश्चित्तम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expiration
EXPIRATION:<BR>I Death, end: q. v.: उपरमः।<BR>II Cessation: q. v.: उपरमः।<BR>III Emission:<BR>q. v.: उद्गारः।<BR>IV Breathing out: निःश्वसनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expire
EXPIRE (v. i.): उपरमति (रम्, c. 1.): v. To die,<BR>cease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expire
EXPIRE (v. t.):<BR>I To breathe out: निःश्वसिति<BR>(श्वस्, c. 2.).<BR>II To emit: q. v.: उद्गिरति<BR>(गॄ, c. 6.).<BR>III To finish: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expiring
EXPIRING:<BR>I Dying: म्रियमाण (f. णा).<BR>II<BR>Pertaining to e. time:<BR>(1) मरणकालीनः (ना,<BR> नं);<BR>(2) expr. by अन्तकाले<BR>or<BR>अवसानसमये।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expiry
EXPIRY: v. Expiration. Ph.:<BR>on the e. of the<BR>lease:<BR>*अतीते भाटकसमये।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

explain
EXPLAIN (v. t.):<BR>(1) व्याख्याति (ख्या, c. 2.) (best<BR>equiv.), I will briefly e. these mantras: [एतान्]<BR>मन्त्रान् संक्षेपतो व्याख्यास्यामः, Up.;<BR>(2) विवृणोति,<BR>(वृ, c. 5.),<BR>the meaning e. d by sages:<BR>मुनिभि- [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">Page258</a>]<BR> -र्विवृतमर्थम्, K. b.;<BR>(3) स्फुटीकरोति (to make<BR>clear), (I)<BR>have already e. d its meaning:<BR>अस्यार्थः<BR> प्रागेव स्फुटीकृतः, Sah.;<BR>(4) स्पष्टीकरोति (3),<BR>this has been e. ed in another Smriti:<BR>स्पष्टीकृत-<BR>श्चायमर्थः स्मृत्यन्तरे, Mit.;<BR>(5) विशदीकरोति (= 3):<BR>let me e. the aphorisms:<BR>कारिकावलीं विशदीकरवाणि,<BR>Par.;<BR>(6) व्याकरोति<BR>or<BR>कुरुते (कृ, c. 8.),<BR>shew<BR>the bow, the gentle Rāma will e.:<BR>कार्मुकं दर्शय,<BR> रामभद्र एव व्याकरोतु, An.;<BR>(7) व्याचष्टे (चक्ष, c.<BR>2.),<BR>e. s the three poems:<BR>काव्यत्रयं व्याचष्टे, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

explainable
EXPLAINABLE:<BR>(1) व्याखयेयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) स्फुटी-<BR>करणीयः (या, यं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

explainer
EXPLAINER:<BR>(1) व्याख्यातृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) स्फुटीकर्तृ<BR>(f. र्त्री), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

explanation
EXPLANATION:<BR>(1) व्याख्या, -नम्;<BR>from the various<BR>e. s of former writers:<BR>बहुविधपूर्वनिबन्धृव्याख्यातः,<BR>Da.;<BR>(2) विवृतिः (= exposition),<BR>in the e. of<BR>Manu's sayings:<BR>मनूक्तविवृतौ, K. b.: v. To<BR>explain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

explanatory
EXPLANATORY: Ph.:<BR>e. notes:<BR>व्याख्यान-<BR>or<BR>अर्थ-<BR>व्यञ्जकटीका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expletive
EXPLETIVE (subs.): i. e.<BR>e. word:<BR>पादपूरकशब्दः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

explicable
EXPLICABLE:<BR>(1) expr. by verb;<BR>(2) व्याखयेयः<BR>(या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

explicate
EXPLICATE (v.):<BR>(1) विवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.);<BR>(2)<BR>व्यञ्जयति (c. of व्यञ्ज्), Gan.: v. To explain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

explication
EXPLICATION: विवृतिः: v. Explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

explicit
EXPLICIT:<BR>(1) स्पष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>(2) स्फुटः (टा, टं):<BR>v. Clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

explicitly
EXPLICITLY:<BR>(1) स्पष्टम्, वि-;<BR>(2) स्फुटम्, परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

explicitness
EXPLICITNESS:<BR>(1) स्पष्टता, वि-;<BR>(2) स्फुटता,<BR> परि-, Ki. iii. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

explode
EXPLODE (v. i.): महाशब्देन विदीर्यते (pass. of दॄ)<BR>or<BR>स्फुटति (स्फुट्, c. 6.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exploded
EXPLODED (adj.): i. e. rejected:<BR>(1) निरस्त (f.<BR>स्ता);<BR>(2) दूरीकृतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exploit
EXPLOIT:<BR>(1) अवदानम्;<BR>(2) अद्भुतं कर्मन् (n.), Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exploration
EXPLORATION: गवेषणा: v. Search.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

explore
EXPLORE: गवेषयति (गवेष्, c. 10.): v. To search.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

explorer
EXPLORER: गवेषकः: v. Searcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

explosion
EXPLOSION:<BR>(1) सशब्दस्फोटनम् (?);<BR>(2) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

explosive
EXPLOSIVE: स्वयं विदी(शी)र्यमाण (f. णा) (?); स्वयं<BR> स्फुटत् (f. ती) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

export
EXPORT (v. t.):<BR>(1) विदेशम्<BR>or<BR>देशान्तरम् नयति (नी,<BR>c. 1.) (= to take),<BR>grain should not be e. ed<BR>during famine:<BR>दुर्भिक्षे धान्यं देशान्तरं न नेयम्,<BR>K. b.;<BR>(2) विदेशे<BR>or<BR>देशान्तरे प्रेरयति (ईर्, c. 10.)<BR>(= to send);<BR>(3) निर्हरति (हृ, c. 1.) (rare), to<BR>e. contraband (articles): प्रतिषिद्धानि निर्हरति, M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exportation
EXPORTATION:<BR>(1) विदेशनयनम्;<BR>(2) विदेशे नयनम्;<BR>(3) निर्गमः, M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exports
EXPORTS (subs.): देशान्तरनीतानि द्रव्याणि; निर्हृत-<BR>द्रव्याणि (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expose
EXPOSE (v.):<BR>I To lay out, disclose: विवृणोति<BR>(वृ, c. 5.), you have e. d your heart from rapture:<BR>त्वयातिहर्षाद्विवृतोऽन्तरात्मा, B.<BR>II To explain:<BR>q. v.: विवृणोति।<BR>III To shew: q. v.: दर्शयति<BR>(c. of दृश्).<BR>IV To put: q. v.: ददाति (दा, c.<BR>3.). v. To e. a child: अपविध्यति (व्यध्, c. 4.)<BR>D. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exposition
EXPOSITION:<BR>(1) विवृति:<BR>(2) व्याख्या (= expla-<BR>-nation: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expositor
EXPOSITOR: विवृतिकारः: v. Explainer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expository
EXPOSITORY: Ph.:<BR>e. index:<BR>सूचिपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expostulate
EXPOSTULATE: तर्कयति (तर्क्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>remonstrate, reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expostulation
EXPOSTULATION: विरुद्धतर्कः: v. Remonstrance,<BR>dissuasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expostulatory
EXPOSTULATORY: विरुद्धतर्कमयः (यी, यं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exposure
EXPOSURE:<BR>I Disclosure: विवृतिः।<BR>II Shew-<BR>-ing: प्रदर्शनम्। Ph.:<BR>e. in the sun:<BR>आतपलङ्घनम्,<BR>Sa.:<BR>northern e.:<BR>उत्तराभिमुखता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expound
EXPOUND (v.): विवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.),<BR>it has been e.<BR>ed in Tatvakaumudi:<BR>विवृतं तत्त्वकौमुद्याम्, D. s.:<BR>v. To explain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expounder
EXPOUNDER: विवृतिकारः: v. Explainer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

express
EXPRESS (v. t.):<BR>I To press out of:<BR>(1) निष्कर्षति<BR>(कृष्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) निष्पीड्य गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.).<BR>II To indicate, exhibit: q. v.: व्यनक्ति (अञ्ज्,<BR>c. 7.),<BR>your interview e. es worthiness:<BR>भवदीय-<BR>दर्शनं योग्यतां व्यनक्ति, Si.;<BR>or it e. es “you are<BR>saying false”:<BR>अथवा मिथ्या वदसीति व्यज्यते, Kav.<BR>III To denote: q. v.: वक्ति (वच्, c. 2.),<BR>here the word beast is intended to e. illiberal:<BR>अत्र जन्तुपदमदातर्यर्थे विवक्षितम्, Kav.<BR>IV To<BR>declare, speak: q. v.: वक्ति, what he was [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">Page259</a>]<BR>about to e.:<BR>विवक्षितां गिरम्, Si.<BR>V To send: q. v.:<BR>विसृजति (सृज्, c. 6.).<BR>VI To represent: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

express
EXPRESS (adj.):<BR>I Explict, plain: q. v.: स्पष्टः<BR>(ष्टा, ष्टं).<BR>II Special: विशिष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं),<BR>e.<BR>messenger:<BR>विशिष्टवार्तावाहकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

express
EXPRESS (subs.):<BR>I A courier: जङ्घाकरिकः।<BR>II<BR>An e. train: *विशिष्टयानावलिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expressible
EXPRESSIBLE:<BR>I What can be declared:<BR>(1)<BR>कथनीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) आख्येयः (या, यं).<BR>II<BR>What can be squeezed: निष्कर्षणीयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expression
EXPRESSION:<BR>I Pressing out:<BR>(1) निष्कर्षणम्;<BR>(2) निष्पीड्य ग्रहणम्।<BR>II Declaration:<BR>(1) कथनम्;<BR>(2) स्थापनम्।<BR>III Significance: indication:<BR>व्यञ्जनम्।<BR>IV Look: q. v.<BR>V Phrase: वाक्यम्,<BR>here the fault is of e.:<BR>अत्र वाक्यस्यैव दोषः, Kav.<BR>VI In arith: राशिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expressive
EXPRESSIVE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) व्यञ्जकः (f. ञ्जिका)<BR>(= indicative),<BR>e. of shame:<BR>व्रीडाव्यञ्जकः, Kav.;<BR>(2) वाचकः (f. चिका) (= denoting),<BR>day is not e.<BR>of light:<BR>दिनमिति प्रकाशमयमित्थर्थेऽवाचकम्, Kav.<BR>II Significant: q. v. अर्थवत् (f. ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expressiveness
EXPRESSIVENESS:<BR>(1) व्यञ्जकता;<BR>(2) वाचकत्वम्;<BR>(3) अर्थवत्ता: v. Above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expressly
EXPRESSLY:<BR>(1) स्पष्टम्;<BR>(2) भिन्नार्थम्: v. Expli-<BR>-citly, plainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expugn
EXPUGN: विजयते (जि, c. 1.): v. To conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expugner
EXPUGNER: जेतृ (f. त्री) वि-: v. Conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expulsion
EXPULSION:<BR>(1) निरसनम्;<BR>(2) निःसारणम्;<BR>(3)<BR>निर्वासनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expulsive
EXPULSIVE:<BR>(1) निःसारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) by comp.,<BR>e. power:<BR>निरसनशक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expunge
EXPUNGE: उन्मार्ष्टि<BR>or<BR>मार्जयति (मृज्, c. 2. and<BR>10.): v. To blot out, erase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expurgate
EXPURGATE: पुनाति (पू, c. 9.): v. To purge,<BR>purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

expurgatory
EXPURGATORY: पावनः (नी, नं). Ph.: e. index:<BR>*निषिद्धपुस्तकनामावलिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exquisite
EXQUISITE (adj.):<BR>I Excellent: अत्युत्तमः (मा,<BR> मं).<BR>II Most delightful: अतिरम्यः (म्या, म्यं);<BR>मनोहारिन् (f. णी): v. Delightful, charming.<BR>III Extreme: q. v.: परमः (मा, मं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exquisitely
EXQUISITELY: expr. by adj.: v. Also extreme-<BR>-ly; well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exquisiteness
EXQUISITENESS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अत्युत्तमता;<BR>(2)<BR>अतिरमणीयता; etc.<BR>II Extremity: expr. by<BR>परमः (मा, मं).<BR>III Sharpness: तीव्रता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exsiccate
EXSICCATE: शोषयति (c. of शुष्): v. To dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exsiccation
EXSICCATION: शोषः<BR>or<BR>शोषणम्, उत्-, वि-, परि-, सं-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exsiccative
EXSICCATIVE:<BR>(1) शोषिन् (f. णी), वि-, परि-;<BR>(2)<BR>विशोषण (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extant
EXTANT:<BR>I Protruded: बहिर्गतः (ता, तं).<BR>II<BR>Not lost: विद्यमानः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extasy
EXTASY, EXTATIC: v. Ecstasy, ecstatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extemporaneous
EXTEMPORANEOUS, EXTEMPORARY:<BR>(1) तत्क्षण-<BR>कल्पितः (ता, तं) (?);<BR>(2) तत्क्षणविहितः (ता, तं)<BR>(?);<BR>(3) तत्कालकृतः (ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extempore
EXTEMPORE (adv.): expr. by adj.,<BR>delivered an<BR>address e.:<BR>*तत्क्षणविहितां वक्तृतामुदीरयामास।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extend
EXTEND (v. t.):<BR>(1) विस्तारयति (स्तॄ, c. 10.),<BR>amass-<BR>ing fame, e. ing excellencies:<BR>उपचिन्वन् यशः,<BR> विस्तारयन् गुणान्, K.;<BR>(2) तनोति, वि-, प्र-, (तन्,<BR>c. 8.),<BR>to e. fame:<BR>यशस्तनोति, Ki.;<BR>(3) प्रसारयति<BR>(c. of सृ) (= to stretch),<BR>who would e. (his)<BR>hand:<BR>कः करं प्रसारयेत्, Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extend
EXTEND (v. i.):<BR>(1) विस्तीर्यते (pass. of स्तॄ);<BR>(2)<BR>वितन्यते (pass. of तन्);<BR>(3) विस्तृतः<BR>or<BR>विततः<BR>(ता, तं) भवति: v. To spread, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extendible
EXTENDIBLE, EXTENSIBLE, EXTENSILE:<BR>(1)<BR>विस्तारणीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) विस्तारक्षमः (मा, मं);<BR>(3) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extension
EXTENSION:<BR>(1) विस्तारः (best equiv.);<BR>(2)<BR>विस्तीर्णता;<BR>(3) विस्तृतिः;<BR>(4) विततिः;<BR>(5) प्रततिः;<BR>(6) विस्तरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extensive
EXTENSIVE: विस्तीर्ण (f. र्णा),<BR>the sea-garmented<BR>(earth) is e.:<BR>विस्तीर्णेयमर्णवाम्बरा, D.;<BR>news of<BR>Kusumapura is e.:<BR>विस्तीर्णः कुसुमपुरवृत्तान्तः, Ku: v.<BR>Large, wide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extensively
EXTENSIVELY:<BR>(1) विस्तीर्णम्;<BR>(2) विस्तरेण;<BR>(3)<BR>विस्तरशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extensiveness
EXTENSIVENESS: विस्तीर्णता: v. Largeness, wide-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extent
EXTENT: विस्तारः,<BR>a Yojana in e.:<BR>योजनविस्तारः<BR>(रा, रं). Ph.:<BR>to a great e.:<BR>अतिमात्रम्: v. Exceed-<BR>-ingly;<BR>to such an e.:<BR>एतावत्: v. Much, so;<BR>to<BR>a slight e.:<BR>ईषत्: v. Little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extenuate
EXTENUATE (v. t.):<BR>I To thin: q. v.: कर्शयति [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">Page260</a>]<BR>(c. of कृश्).<BR>II To palliate, to degrade:<BR>q. v.: लघयति (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extenuation
EXTENUATION: लघूकरणम्: v. Palliation, miti-<BR>-gation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exterior
EXTERIOR (adj.): बहिः in comp.: v. External,<BR>outer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exterior
EXTERIOR (subs.):<BR>(1) बहिर् (ind.),<BR>like (your)<BR>e.:<BR>बहिरिव, Gi. viii. 7; charming only in the e.:<BR>बहिरेव मनोहराः, H.;<BR>(2) बहिर्भागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exterminate
EXTERMINATE: उच्छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7.): v. To<BR>extirpate, eradicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extermination
EXTERMINATION: उच्छेदः, सम्-: v. Extirpation,<BR>eradication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exterminator
EXTERMINATOR:<BR>(1) उच्छेदक (f. दिका), सम्-;<BR>(2)<BR>उन्मूलयितृ (f. त्री) सम्-;<BR>(3) उद्धतृ (f. त्री), सम्;<BR>(4) विध्वंसिन् (f. नी);<BR>(5) अन्तकृत् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

external
EXTERNAL (adj.):<BR>(1) बहिः (in comp.),<BR>remove-<BR>ing e. and internal dirt:<BR>बहिरन्तर्मलमुष् (mfn.),<BR>An.;<BR>(2) बाह्यः (ह्या, ह्यं),<BR>e. objects:<BR>बाह्यविषयाः<BR>S. p. b.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

externally
EXTERNALLY:<BR>(1) बहिः,<BR>e. sweet, but internally<BR>disagreeable:<BR>मधुरं बहिरन्तरप्रियम्, Si.;<BR>not only<BR>internally but also e.:<BR>न केवलमन्तर्बहिरपि, K.;<BR>(2) बाह्यतः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extinct
EXTINCT (adj.):<BR>I At an end:<BR>(1) उच्छिन्नः<BR>(न्ना, न्नं);<BR>(2) संस्थितः (ता, तं),<BR>to be e.:<BR>संस्थां<BR> प्राप्नोति, V. p.: v. Also end.<BR>II Extin-<BR>-guished:<BR>(1) शान्तः (न्ता, न्तं);<BR>(2) निर्वातः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extinction
EXTINCTION:<BR>I Putting out: निर्वाणम्।<BR>II<BR>Destruction: q. v.: उच्छेदः, e. of Kshatriyas:<BR>क्षत्रियोच्छेदः,<BR>VI iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extinguish
EXTINGUISH:<BR>I To put out: q. v.: निर्वापयति<BR>(c. of वा),<BR>I will e. the fire of bereavement by<BR>quitting life:<BR>देहमुत्सृज्य विरहाग्निं निर्वापयामि, Va.<BR>II To destroy: q. v.: उच्छिनक्ति (छिद्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extinguished
EXTINGUISHED, BE: I. To go out: q. v.: निर्वाति<BR>(वा, c. 2.),<BR>these fires are not yet e.:<BR>निर्वान्त्य-<BR>द्यापि नैते हव्यवाहाः, Mu.<BR>II To be destroyed:<BR>q. v.: expr. by उच्छिन्नः (न्ना, न्नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extinguishable
EXTINGUISHABLE:<BR>I Of lights: निर्वाप्य (f. प्या).<BR>II Fig.: उच्छेद्य (f. द्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extinguisher
EXTINGUISHER: of a lamp: *दीपनिर्वापकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extinguishment
EXTINGUISHMENT: v. Extinction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extirpate
EXTIRPATE:<BR>(1) उन्मूलयति, सम्- (मूल्, c. 10.),<BR>and<BR>all the Nandas have been e. d:<BR>नन्दाश्चोन्मूलिताः<BR> सर्वे, Mu.;<BR>(2) उच्छिनत्ति, सम्-, (छिद्, c. 7.),<BR>to<BR>e. enemies:<BR>रिपूनुच्छिनत्ति, R.;<BR>(3) उत्सादयति (c.<BR>of सद्),<BR>e. ing thorns:<BR>उत्सादयन् कण्टकान्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extirpation
EXTIRPATION:<BR>(1) उन्मूलनम्;<BR>(2) उच्छेदः, सम्-;<BR>(3) उत्सादनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extol
EXTOL (v.):<BR>I To raise up: उन्नमयति (c. of<BR>नम्).<BR>II To praise: q. v.: कीर्तयति (कॄत्, c.<BR>10.),<BR>especially to those who^1 e. d the excellencies<BR>of Damayantī:<BR>विशिष्य भैमीगुणकीर्तनकृताम्, N.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extort
EXTORT (v. t.): निष्कर्षति (कृष्, c. 1.),<BR>to e. a con-<BR>fession:<BR>*प्रतिपत्तिं निष्कर्षति;<BR>to e. money:<BR>अर्थं<BR> निष्कर्षति, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extortion
EXTORTION: निष्कर्षः, -णम्<BR>e. of money:<BR>*अर्थनिष्कर्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extorter
EXTORTER, EXTORTIONER: निष्कर्षक (f. षिका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extra
EXTRA:<BR>I Adj.: अतिरिक्तः (क्ता, क्तं).<BR>II Subs.:<BR>अतिरिक्तम्।<BR>III Prep.: v. Beyond, exceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extract
EXTRACT (v.):<BR>(1) निर्-कर्षति, उत्-, (कृष्, c. 1.),<BR>to e. an oil:<BR>तैलं निष्कर्षति;<BR>(2) निर्-हरति, -ते,<BR> उत्-; (हृ, c. 1.), will e. the thorn of infamy:<BR>अयशःशल्यमुद्धरे, Ki. To e. a root (in arith.): मूलं<BR> निर्धारयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extract
EXTRACT (subs.):<BR>I That which is e. ed: expr.<BR>by verb.<BR>II Essence:<BR>(1) रसः;<BR>(2) निर्यासः;<BR>(3) निर्यूहः।<BR>III A citation, quotation: expr.<BR>by उद्धृतः (ता, तं).<BR>IV Descent: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extraction
EXTRACTION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) निष्कर्षः<BR>or<BR>उत्कर्षः,<BR> -णम्;<BR>(2) निर्हारः<BR>or<BR>निर्हरणम्;<BR>(3) उद्धरणम्।<BR>II<BR>Lineage, descent: q. v.: Ph.: e. of roots (in<BR>arith.): मूलनिर्द्धारणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extraforaneous
EXTRAFORANEOUS: perh. simply बहिः in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extrajudicial
EXTRAJUDICIAL: व्यवहारबहिर्भूतः (ता, तं) (?);<BR>व्यवहारबाह्य (f. ह्या) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extramundane
EXTRAMUNDANE: अलौकिकः (की कं); अपार्थिवः<BR>(वी, वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extramural
EXTRAMURAL: भित्तिबहिर्भूतः (ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extraneous
EXTRANEOUS: बाह्य (f. ह्या): v. External,<BR>foreign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extraordinarily
EXTRAORDINARILY:<BR>(1) असाधारण्येन;<BR>(2) अपूर्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extraordinariness
EXTRAORDINARINESS:<BR>(1) असाधारण्यम्;<BR>(2) असा-<BR>मान्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extraordinary
EXTRAORDINARY:<BR>(1) असाधारण (f. णी);<BR>(2)<BR>असामान्य (f. न्या);<BR>(3) अलोकसामान्य (f. न्या), Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extravagance
EXTRAVAGANCE:<BR>I In expenditure: अतिव्ययः<BR>or<BR>महान् व्ययः,<BR>began to enjoy with e.:<BR>महताव्ययेनोप-<BR>भोक्तुमारब्धवान्, Mu.<BR>II Of expression:<BR>अतिशयोक्तिः, Kav.<BR>III Excess: q.v.<BR>IV<BR>Wandering beyond proper limits: व्यभिचारः<BR>(lit. and fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extravagant
EXTRAVAGANT:<BR>I Prodigal: q.v.: अतिव्ययिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR>II: Unrestrained: Ph.: e. conduct:<BR>व्यभिचारः,<BR>e. language:<BR>अतिशयोक्तिः।<BR>III Err-<BR>-ing: व्यभिचारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extravagantly
EXTRAVAGANTLY:<BR>I Prodigally:<BR>(1) अतिव्ययेन;<BR>(2) महता व्ययेन।<BR>II Wildly, excessively: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extravaganza
EXTRAVAGANZA: उद्भ्रान्तगीतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extravasated
EXTRAVASATED: नाडिनिर्गतः (ता, तं), and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extravasation
EXTRAVASATION: Ph.:<BR>e. of blood:<BR>रक्तनिर्गमः: v.<BR>Effusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extreme
EXTREME (adj.):<BR>I Greatest:<BR>(1) परः (रा,<BR> रं),<BR>possessed of e. faith:<BR>श्रद्धया परयोपेतः, G.;<BR>(2)<BR>परमः (मा, यं),<BR>e. gain:<BR>परमो लाभः, Ki.;<BR>(3)<BR>निरतिशयः (या, यं),<BR>e. joy:<BR>निरतिशयानन्दः, D.s.;<BR>(4) एकान्तः (न्ता, न्तं),<BR>e. coldness:<BR>एकान्तशैत्यम्,<BR>Ku.<BR>II Outermost: परः (रा, रं), e. limit<BR>परा काष्ठा, Ku.<BR>III Last: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extreme
EXTREME (subs.): परा कोटिः: v. Acme, end.<BR>Ph.:<BR>gone to the e.:<BR>अतिभूमिं गतः, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extremely
EXTREMELY:<BR>(1) परम्,<BR>was e. pleased:<BR>परमहृष्यत्,<BR>D.;<BR>(2) परमम्;<BR>(3) निरतिशयम्;<BR>(4) एकान्तम् or<BR>एकान्ततः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extremity
EXTREMITY:<BR>I Highest degree: परा कोटिः:<BR>v. Acme.<BR>II End: q.v.: अन्तः, e. of nail:<BR>नखान्तः, At.<BR>III Utmost limit: अवधिः,<BR>e. of<BR>the delightful:<BR>आह्लादनीयानामवधिः, K.<BR>IV<BR>Greatest need: अतिकृच्छ्रम्<BR>or<BR>महत् कृच्छ्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extricable
EXTRICABLE:<BR>(1) उद्धरणीयः (या, यं), सम्-;<BR>(2)<BR>मोच्य (f. च्या), वि-, परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extricate
EXTRICATE:<BR>(1) उद्धरति, सम्-, to e. one's self:<BR>आत्मानमुद्धरति, V. c.;<BR>(2) मोचयति (मुच्, c. 10.)<BR>(= to free: q.v.); तारयति (c. of तॄ) (=to<BR>save: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extrication
EXTRICATION:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) उद्धारः, सम्-;<BR>(2)<BR>उद्धरणम्, सम्-;<BR>(3) मोक्षः, -णम्: v. Deliverance.<BR>II Emission: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extrinsic
EXTRINSIC, -AL: बाह्यः (ह्या, ह्यं): v. External.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

extrude
EXTRUDE: निःसारयति (c. of सृ): v. To expel,<BR>thrust out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exuberance
EXUBERANCE: प्राचुर्यम्: v. Abundance, excess.<BR>Ph.:<BR>in e. of joy:<BR>हर्षनिर्भरः (रा, रं), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exuberant
EXUBERANT: प्रचुरः (रा, रं): v. Abundant,<BR>excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exuberantly
EXUBERANTLY: प्रचुरम्: v. Abundantly, excess-<BR>-ively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exudation
EXUDATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) उद्गारः;<BR>(2)<BR>निष्ठीवनम्।<BR>II Flow: q.v.<BR>III What is<BR>exuded:<BR>(1) निर्यासः;<BR>(2) निर्यूहः;<BR>(3) रसः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exude
EXUDE (v.):<BR>I Trans.:<BR>(1) उद्गिरति (गॄ, c. 6.);<BR>(2) निरस्यति (अस्, c. 4.);<BR>(3) निष्ठीवति (ष्ठीव्,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>some e.d lac.:<BR>केनचिल्लाक्षारसो निष्ठ्यूतः,<BR>Sa.<BR>II Intrans.: स्रवति (स्रु, c. 1.): v. To<BR>flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exult
EXULT (v.):<BR>(1) उत्सिञ्चति, -ते (सिञ्च्, c. 6.)<BR>(often in bad sense),<BR>his mind did not e.:<BR>न<BR> तस्योत्सिषिचे मनः, R.;<BR>(2) प्रमोदते (मुद्, c. 1.),<BR>we<BR>eagerly e.:<BR>व्यं व्यग्राः प्रमोदामहे, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exultant
EXULTANT:<BR>(1) उत्सिक्तः (क्ता, क्तं), of the e. ascetic:<BR>उत्सिक्तस्य तपोनिधेः, Vi.<BR>(2) प्रमुदितः (ता, तं),<BR>the e. party of the bridegroom:<BR>प्रमुदितवरपक्षः, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exultation
EXULTATION:<BR>(1) उत्सेकः;<BR>(2) प्रमोदः: v.<BR>Rapture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exultingly
EXULTINGLY:<BR>(1) सोत्सेकम्;<BR>(2) सोल्लासम्;<BR>(3)<BR>प्रमोदनिर्मरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

exustion
EXUSTION:<BR>(1) निर्दाहः;<BR>(2) निर्दहनम्: v. To<BR>burn up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eye
EYE (subs.):<BR>(1) चक्षुः,<BR>have divine e.s in seeing<BR>others' fault:<BR>परदोषेक्षणदिव्यचक्षुषः, Si.;<BR>where a<BR>king places his e.:<BR>यस्मिन् पार्थिवश्चक्षुरारोपयति, P.;<BR>(2) लोचनम्, वि-, shut the e.s never to open again<BR>(i.e. died): अपुनरुन्मीलनाय निमिमील लोचने, C.;<BR>pass with e.s shut:<BR>लोचने मीलयित्वा गमय, Me.;<BR>(3) नेत्रम्,<BR>the observed of hundreds of e.s:<BR>नेत्रशतैक-<BR>लक्ष्यः (क्ष्या, क्ष्यं), R.;<BR>(4) नयनम्,<BR>his e. fell on<BR>her e.s:<BR>अस्य तस्या नयनयुगले निपपात चक्षुः, K.;<BR>(5) अक्षि (n.), the thousand-e.d. (Indra): सहस्राक्षः;<BR>the external coat of the e.:<BR>अक्ष्णयोर्बाह्य पटलम्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">Page262</a>]<BR>Bha.;<BR>(6) दृश् (f), all the fine -e.d (companions)<BR>drunk him with (their)<BR>e.s:<BR>अमुं दृशा पपुस्ताः सुदृशः<BR> समस्ताः, N.<BR>Blind of one e.:<BR>काणः (णा, णं).<BR>The outer corner of the e.:<BR>(1) अपाङ्गः;<BR>(2)<BR>नयनोपान्तः। Before the e.s of:<BR>(1) समक्षं<BR>or<BR>प्रत्यक्षम्<BR>(with gen. or absol.), before the e.s of kings:<BR>प्रत्यक्षं क्ष्मापतीनाम्, Ve.;<BR>(2) by gen. or loc. of<BR>पश्यत् (f. न्ती)<BR>before my e.s:<BR>पश्यतो मे<BR>or<BR>पश्यति मयि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eye
EYE (v.): निरीक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.): v. To see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eye-ball
EYE-BALL:<BR>(1) तारा<BR>or<BR>तारका;<BR>(2) कनीनिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eye-brow
EYE-BROW: भ्रूः<BR>or<BR>भ्रूलता। A girl with beautiful e.:<BR>सुभ्रूः।<BR>A face with black, smooth, gracefully arched<BR>e.s:<BR>अनुवक्रनीलस्निग्धभ्रूलतमाननम्, D. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eye-drop
EYE-DROP:<BR>(1) नयनजलबिन्दुः, K.;<BR>(2) नयन-<BR>सलिलम्, Me.;<BR>(3) नयनाम्बु (n.), Ki.;<BR>(4)<BR>अश्रुबिन्दुः, D.: v. Tear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eye-glass
EYE-GLASS: उपनेत्रम्; उपलोचनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eye-lash
EYE-LASH: पक्ष्मन् (n.),<BR>eyes with raised e.s:<BR>उत्पक्ष्म-<BR>राजीनि विलोचनानि, R. xiii. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eyelet
EYELET, EYELET-HOLE: छिद्रम्: v. Aperture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eyelid
EYELID:<BR>(1) नेत्रच्छदः;<BR>(2) नयनच्छदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eye-piece
EYE-PIECE: *नेत्रखण्डम्: v. Lens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eye-salve
EYE-SALVE: अञ्जनम्, नेत्राञ्जनम्; etc.: v. Oint-<BR>-ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eye-service
EYE-SERVICE: प्रत्यक्षसेवा; प्रत्यक्षशुश्रूषा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eye-shot
EYE-SHOT, EYE-REACH: चक्षुर्विषयः, and sim.<BR>comp.s,<BR>when they were out of e.:<BR>चक्षुर्विषयमति-<BR>क्रान्तेषु तेषु, H.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eye-sight
EYE-SIGHT: दृष्टिः,<BR>my e. cannot decipher these<BR>letters:<BR>नात्र मे वर्णविभावनसहा दृष्टिः, V.: v. Sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eye-sore
EYE-SORE:<BR>(1) चक्षुःशूलम्;<BR>(2) अक्षिगतः (ता, तं),<BR>I am his e.:<BR>अक्षिगतोऽहमस्य, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eye-witness
EYE-WITNESS:<BR>(1) प्रत्यक्षसाक्षिन् (f. णी) (after<BR>M.);<BR>(2) प्रत्यक्षद्रष्टृ (f. ष्ट्री), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eyre
EYRE: परिभ्रमणम्: v. Circuit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

eyrie
EYRIE, EYRY: कुलायः: v. Nest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fabian
FABIAN (adj.): *फाबीयः (या, यं); दीर्घसूत्रः (त्रा,<BR> त्रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fable
FABLE:<BR>II Lit.: कथा: v. Story.<BR>II False-<BR>-hood: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fabric
FABRIC:<BR>I Texture: q.v.<BR>II Edifice:<BR>q.v.: भवनम्।<BR>III Cloth: q.v.: पट्टः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fabricate
FABRICATE:<BR>I To build, produce: q.v.:<BR>रचयति (रच्, c. 10.).<BR>II To invent: सृजति<BR>(सृज्, c. 6.): v. Counterfeit; false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fabrication
FABRICATION:<BR>I Construction, manufacture:<BR>q.v.: रचना, वि-।<BR>II Falsehood:<BR>this is a<BR>f.:<BR>अलीकमेतत्: v. False, counterfeit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fabricator
FABRICATOR: रचयितृ (m.): v. Maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fabulist
FABULIST:<BR>(1) कथाकारः (?);<BR>(2) आख्यानकानां<BR> कर्ता, K.;<BR>(3) आख्यायिकाकारः, C.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fabulous
FABULOUS:<BR>I Fictitious: q.v.<BR>II Related<BR>in fable: कथानिबद्धः (द्धा, द्धं); आख्यानकीर्तितः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

facade
FACADE: मुखम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

face
FACE (subs.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) मुखम्,<BR>struck<BR>Yudhisṭhira on the f.:<BR>युधिष्ठिरं मुखेऽहनम्, Mah.:<BR>with a f. beautiful as the moon:<BR>इन्दुसुन्दरमुखी,<BR>Ma.;<BR>how (we) will shew our f. to men:<BR>कथं<BR> लोकस्य मुखं द्रक्ष्यामः, Ana.;<BR>makes thousands of<BR>f. s:<BR>मुखभङ्गिसहस्राणि कुरुते, K.;<BR>is it proper for a<BR>king to turn his f. from duty:<BR>किं धर्मं प्रति विमुख-<BR>तोचिता राझः, Sa.; you have come before my f.<BR>(= eyes: v. Eye): मत्सम्मुखभागतोऽसि, Ve.;<BR>the<BR>f.s of the quarters:<BR>दिशां मुखानि, N.;<BR>(2)<BR>आननम्;<BR>(3) वदनम्;<BR>(4) वक्त्रम्;<BR>(5) आस्यम्।<BR>Ph.:<BR>in the f. of the Vedāntas:<BR>वेदान्तोषु जागरुकेषु,<BR>D.s.<BR>II In Geo.: पाश्र्वः, K. d.: *मुखम्,<BR>hav-<BR>ing six f. s:<BR>षण्मुखः (खी, खं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

face
FACE (v.):<BR>I To confront:<BR>(1) सम्मुखयति<BR>(nomi.);<BR>(2) अभिमुखयति (nomi.);<BR>(3) सम्मुखी-<BR>or<BR>अभिमुखीभवति (with gen.),<BR>made it f. me with<BR>difficulty:<BR>कथमपि मदभिमुखमकरोत्, D.: v. To meet.<BR>II To front upon: expr. by मुख-<BR>or<BR>अभिमुख-<BR>in comp.,<BR>f. ing the east:<BR>पूर्वमुख (f. खी);<BR>f.<BR>the north:<BR>उत्तरमुख (f. खी); f. ing Lakṣmaṇa:<BR>लक्षणाभिमुखः, Ram.<BR>III To cover the f. of: v.<BR>To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

facet
FACET.: as of a diamond: मुखम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

facetious
FACETIOUS:<BR>I Merry, jocular: परिहासशीलः<BR>(ला, लं).<BR>II Exciting laughter:<BR>f. conver-<BR>sation:<BR>नर्मभाषितम्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

facetiously
FACETIOUSLY: परिहासपूर्वकम्: v. Merrily, gaily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

facile
FACILE:<BR>I Easy:<BR>(1) सुकरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) अयत्न-<BR>साध्यः (ध्या, ध्यं);<BR>(3) अनायासनिष्पाद्यः (द्या, द्यं).<BR>II Easy to pass: सुगमः (मा, मं).<BR>III Mild,<BR>affable: q.v.: मृदु (f. द्वी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

facilitate
FACILITATE: expr. by adj.,<BR>it will f. their<BR>union:<BR>अनेन समागमस्तयोरयत्नसाध्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

facility
FACILITY:<BR>I Ease: q.v.: सौकर्यम्।<BR>II Dexteri-<BR>-ty: q.v.: लाघवम्, shewing the f. of his hand:<BR>दर्शयन् पाणिलाघवम्, Ram.<BR>III Mildness, affa-<BR>-bility: मार्दवम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

facing
FACING (subs.): *मुखच्छदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fac-simile
FAC-SIMILE: प्रतिरूपम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fact
FACT (subs.):<BR>I Reality, truth: q.v.: भूतार्थः,<BR>it was speaking the f.:<BR>भूतार्थव्याहृतिः सा हि, R.;<BR>why don't you represent the f.:<BR>किमर्थं भूतार्थो न<BR> निवेद्यते, Mr. ix.<BR>II An act, event: q.v.: वृत्तम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fact
FACT, IN:<BR>(1) वस्तुतः,<BR>but in f.:<BR>वस्तुतस्तु, Da. com.;<BR>(2) प्रत्युत,<BR>it is in f. (your) abuse:<BR>प्रत्युत सा<BR> तिरस्क्रिया, Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faction
FACTION:<BR>I A body of combatants: दलम्।<BR>II<BR>A party: q.v.: दलम्।<BR>III Discord: q.v.: भेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

factious
FACTIOUS:<BR>I Given to faction:<BR>(1) कलहप्रियः<BR>(या, यं) (= quarrelsome),<BR>(2) उपजापिन् (f. नी)<BR>(=intriguing).<BR>II Belonging to a f.: expr.<BR>by comp. or gen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

factiousness
FACTIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) कलहप्रियता;<BR>(2) उपजापिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

factitious
FACTITIOUS: कृत्रिमः (मा, मं): v. Artificial,<BR>unnatural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

factitive
FACTITIVE: Ph.:<BR>f. object:<BR>गौणं कर्मन् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

factor
FACTOR:<BR>I A manager, agent: q.v.<BR>II<BR>In arith: expr. by circumlo:<BR>two is a f. of<BR>ten:<BR>दश द्वाभ्यां भाज्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

factorage
FACTORAGE: पारितोषिकम् (= reward): v. Also<BR>commission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

factory
FACTORY: *कर्मस्थानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faculty
FACULTY:<BR>I Power: q.v.: शक्तिः।<BR>II Autho-<BR>-rity: क्षमता।<BR>III A body of men: समाजः,<BR>f. of<BR>medicine:<BR>*चिकित्सासमाजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fade
FADE (v.i.):<BR>I To decay, droop: q.v.: अव-<BR>सीदति (सद्, c. 1.).<BR>II To lose freshness:<BR>(1) म्लायति, परि-, (म्लै, c. 1.),<BR>with f. d beauty<BR>of faces:<BR>परिम्लानमुखश्रियाम्, Ku.;<BR>(2) मलिनीभवति,<BR>the f. ing garland:<BR>मालां मलिनीभवन्तीम्, N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fade
FADE (v. t.):<BR>(1) म्लापयति, परि- (c. of म्लै),<BR>fad-<BR>ing the chaplet:<BR>वनमालां म्लापयन्, Si.;<BR>(2)<BR>मलिनयति (nomi.)<BR>or<BR>मलिनीकरोति, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faeces
FÆCES: अवस्करः: v. Excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fag
FAG (subs.): चेटः: v. Servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fag
FAG (v. i.):<BR>I To drudge^1: कर्म करोति।<BR>II To<BR>tire: खिद्यते (खिद्, c. 4.).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fag
FAG (v. t.):<BR>(1) आयासयति (c. of यस्);<BR>(2)<BR>खेदयति (c. of खिद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fag-end
FAG-END: पर्यन्तः: v. End, refuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fagot
FAGOT: काष्ठानि (n. pl.): v. Fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fail
FAIL (v.i.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) सीदति, अव-, वि-,<BR>(सद्, c. 1.),<BR>of f. ed eyesight:<BR>अवसन्नदृश् (mfn.),<BR>R.: v. To depart, go; my limbs are f. ing:<BR>सीदन्ति मम गात्राणि, G.: v. To sink, decay;<BR>with intellect not f. ing in exigencies:<BR>कार्यसङ्कटेष्व-<BR>विषण्णधीः, K.: v. To break, become frustrated;<BR>(2) अवस्यति (सो, c. 4.), my strength f. s:<BR>शक्तिर्ममावस्यति, Ki.<BR>II To be deficient: v.<BR>Deficient.<BR>F. of:<BR>हीनः (ना, नं), in comp.:<BR>v. Wanting, fall off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fail
FAIL (v.t.): v. To desert, disappoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fail
FAIL (subs.): v. Failure.<BR>without f.:<BR>नियतम्:<BR>Certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

failing
FAILING (subs.):<BR>I Fault: q.v.: दोषः।<BR>II In<BR>money-matters: अवसादः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

failure
FAILURE:<BR>I Want, deficiency: q.v.:<BR>f. of<BR>rain:<BR>वृष्ट्यभावः;<BR>f. of crops:<BR>शस्यविपत्तिः, V. m.<BR>II Non-performance, miscarriage: भङ्गः,<BR>f.<BR>of a vow:<BR>व्रतभङ्गः, K.; which was the first f.:<BR>तत्पूर्वभङ्गः (ङ्गा, ङ्गं), R.<BR>III Decay, destruc-<BR>-tion: q.v.:<BR>(1) अवसादः;<BR>(2) लोपः,<BR>f. of<BR>memory:<BR>स्मृतिलोपः, Sa.,<BR>IV In business:<BR>(1)<BR>अवसादः;<BR>(2) परिक्षीणता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fain
FAIN (adj.): स्पृहयालु (mfn.): v. Glad, apt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fain
FAIN (adv.): सोल्लासम्: v. Gladly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faint
FAINT (adj.):<BR>I Languid: अवसन्नः (न्ना, न्नं).<BR>II Cowardly, dejected: q.v.: दीनः (ना, नं).<BR>III Feeble: q.v.: दुर्बलः (ला, लं).<BR>IV Not<BR>distinct अस्फुटः (ता, तं): v. Also little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faint
FAINT (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मूर्छति (मूर्छ्, c.<BR>1.), f. ed away from the sudden fall of distress:<BR>सहसा दुःख्रोपनिपातान्मुमूर्च्छ, M. n.;<BR>(2) मूर्छां [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">Page264</a>]<BR>गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.), मोहम् एति (इ, c. 2.), etc.<BR>II To vanish: q.v.: नश्यति (नश्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faint-hearted
FAINT-HEARTED: दीनमनस् (mfn.): v. Dejected,<BR>coward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faint-heartedness
FAINT-HEARTEDNESS: दीनमनस्कता: v. Dejec-<BR>-tion, cowardice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fainting
FAINTING (subs.):<BR>(1) मूर्च्छा;<BR>(2) मोहः (ambi-<BR>-guous),<BR>given to f.:<BR>मोहपरायणा, Ku.;<BR>(3) प्रलयः<BR>(rare),<BR>the end of f.:<BR>प्रलयान्तः, Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faintly
FAINTLY:<BR>(1) ईषत् (= little: q.v.);<BR>(2) दुर्बलम्:<BR>(= feebly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faintness
FAINTNESS:<BR>I Dejection, inactivity: q.v.:<BR>अवसादः।<BR>II Feeblness: q.v.: दौर्बल्यम्।<BR>III<BR>Dulness: मान्द्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fair
FAIR (adj.):<BR>I Clear: q.v.: विमलः (ला, लं).<BR>II Beautiful: q.v.: सुन्दरः (री, रं). Ph.:<BR>the f. or f. sex:<BR>सुन्दर्यः (f. pl.).<BR>III Frank,<BR>upright: q.v.: ॠजु (mfn.).<BR>IV Of comple-<BR>-xion: गौरः (री, रं)<BR>or<BR>गौरवर्ण (f. र्णा). V.<BR>Favourable: q.v.<BR>VI Proper: q.v.: युक्तः<BR>(क्ता, क्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fair
FAIR (adv.):<BR>I Clearly: स्पष्टम्।<BR>II Frankly:<BR>ऋजु। Ph.: to bid f.: v. To promise: f. and<BR>square: v. Justly, honesly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fair
FAIR (subs.): मेला,<BR>Fancy f.:<BR>*रुचिरमेला: v.<BR>Market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fairing
FAIRING (subs.): मेलामूल्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fairly
FAIRLY:<BR>I Expressly: q.v.: स्पष्टम्।<BR>II Just-<BR>-ly: q.v.: न्यायेन।<BR>III Properly: q.v.:<BR>यथार्हम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fairness
FAIRNESS:<BR>I Clearness: q.v.: वैमल्यम् (?).<BR>II Beauty: q.v.: सौन्दर्यम्।<BR>III Honesty:<BR>q.v.: आर्जवम्।<BR>IV Distinctness: स्पष्टता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fair-spoken
FAIR-SPOKEN: प्रियंवदः (दा, दं): v. Affable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fairy
FAIRY:<BR>I Illusion: माया।<BR>II A female<BR>spirit:<BR>(1) अप्सरस् (f.),<BR>“f. ring”<BR>*अप्सरीमण्डलम्;<BR>(2) सुरकामिनी।: v. Also elf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faith
FAITH (subs.): श्रद्धा,<BR>being full of f. saluted the<BR>gods:<BR>श्रद्धामयीभूय सुपर्वणस्तान् ननाम, N.: v. Belief.<BR>To have f. in:<BR>श्रद्दधाति<BR>or<BR>धत्ते (धा, c. 3.) (with<BR>loc.),<BR>having f. in gods:<BR>सुरेषु श्रद्दधत् (f. ती),<BR>N.;<BR>he had f. in Rāma's prowess:<BR>स पौरुषं<BR> राघवे श्रद्दधे, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faith
FAITH (interj.): सत्यम्: v. Verily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faithful
FAITHFUL:<BR>I Full of faith:<BR>(1) श्रद्धालु (mfn.);<BR>(2) श्रद्धामयः (यी, यं).<BR>II Loyal: भक्तः (क्ता,<BR> क्तं). Ph.:<BR>a f. wife:<BR>पतिव्रता नारी; a f. husband:<BR>पत्नीरतः पुमान् (?).<BR>III Not breaking promises:<BR>सत्यसन्धः (न्धा, न्धं); सत्यप्रतिझः (झा, झं), etc.<BR>IV Worthy of belief: विश्वसनीयः (या, यं)<BR>or<BR>विश्वास्य (f. स्या).<BR>V True: यथार्थः (र्था, र्थं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faithfulness
FAITHFULNESS:<BR>I Lit.: श्रद्धालुता।<BR>II Loyalty:<BR>भक्तिः।<BR>III Constancy: अव्यभिचारिता।<BR>IV<BR>Truth: यथार्थता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faithless
FAITHLESS:<BR>I Lit.: अश्रद्दधानः (ना, नं);<BR>(2)<BR>श्रद्धाहीनः (ना, नं).<BR>II Treacherous: विश्वास-<BR>घातिन् (f. नी).<BR>III Disloyal: भक्तिहीनः (ना, नं).<BR>IV Inconstant: व्यमिचारिन् (f. णी). v.<BR>Delusive: अयथार्थः (र्था, र्थं).<BR>VI In promises:<BR>असत्यसन्ध (f. न्धा); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faithlessly
FAITHLESSLY: expr. by acc. sing. of adj. or<BR>ins. sing. of subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faithlessness
FAITHLESSNESS:<BR>I Lit.: अश्रद्धा।<BR>II Treachery:<BR>विश्वासघातः।<BR>III Disloyalty: अभक्तिः।<BR>IV In-<BR>-constancy: व्यभिचारिता।<BR>V Delusiveness:<BR>अयथार्थता।<BR>VI In promises:<BR>(1) असत्यसन्धता;<BR>(2) प्रतिझाभङ्गः, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

falcate
FALCATE, FALCATED: अनुवक्रः (क्रा, क्रं), D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

falchion
FALCHION: खङ्गविशेषः v. Sword, scimitar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

falcon
FALCON: श्येनः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

falconer
FALCONER: श्येनजीविन् (f. नी), M. iii. 169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fall
FALL (v.i.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) पतति, नि-, (rarely<BR>प्र-, परि-, विनि-, आ-, सं-,) (पत्, c. l.,)<BR>Putanā<BR>fell on the ground:<BR>पपात पूतना भूमौ, v. p.;<BR>with<BR>the dress fell into the water:<BR>सवासाः प्रापतज्जले,<BR>Mah.;<BR>to fall on the knees:<BR>जानुभ्यां (ins.)<BR>पतति, Mah.;<BR>the glittering scimitar fell from<BR>his hand:<BR>ज्वलन्नसिस्तस्य पपात पाणेः; Ki. xvii. 58.;<BR>rivers f. ing into the ocean:<BR>अभ्बुराशिं पतन्तीर्नदीः,<BR>Si. iii. 75. (This use of पत् is rare. Gen.<BR>expr. by प्रविशति, M. n.<BR>or<BR>उपैति, Mah. or<BR>प्रयाति, Ri., etc.); flower-rain fell from the sky:<BR>वियतः पुष्पवर्षं पपात, Vi.: v. Rain;<BR>we suddenly<BR>fell on Vindhyaketu:<BR>अतर्किता एव विन्ध्यकेतोरुपरि<BR> निपतिताः स्म, Pri.: v. To assail, some rise and [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">Page265</a>]<BR>f.: कोऽप्युत्थितः पतति, Mr.: v. To decline,<BR>the<BR>refuge of the f. en:<BR>पतितशरण्या, J.;<BR>something else<BR>has f. en there:<BR>अन्यत् किमप्यर्थान्तरं तत्र पतितम्, Ana.<BR>iv. v.: To happen;<BR>this kingdom had f. en<BR>into the hands of Vasantabhānu:<BR>वसन्तभानोर्हस्ते<BR> राज्यमिदं पतितम्, D.;<BR>(2) भ्रश्यति, -ते<BR>or<BR>भ्रंशते, परि-,<BR>(भ्रंश्, c. 4. and 1.) (gen. in fig. senses),<BR>f.<BR>en on the ground:<BR>उर्व्यां भ्रष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं), R.;<BR>did<BR>not f. from truth:<BR>सत्यान्नाभ्रश्यत, R.;<BR>(3) च्यवते,<BR> वि-, प्र-, परि-, (च्यु, c. 1.) (gen. fig.),<BR>has<BR>f. en from the top of the tree:<BR>तरुशिखरादस्मात्परि-<BR>च्युतः, K.;<BR>f. en from the path:<BR>पथश्च्युतः (ता,<BR> तं), Ki.<BR>II To cease: q.v.: शाम्यति (शम्,<BR>c. 4.),<BR>when the wind fell:<BR>वाते शमतां गते, Mah.<BR>III To decrease: q.v.: ह्नासमुपैति (इ, c. 2.).<BR>Ph.: to f. asleep: v. Asleep; to fall calm, i.e.<BR>to become calm.: v. Calm; to f. foul: v. To<BR>attack;<BR>to f. short:<BR>न्यूनीभवतिः v. Deficient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fall away
FALL AWAY:<BR>I To pine: अङ्गेषु परिहीयते (pass.<BR>of हा), Sa.<BR>II To sink into wickedness:<BR>पततिः v. To fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fall back
FALL BACK:<BR>I To recede: q.v.<BR>II Not to<BR>fulfil: q.v.:<BR>(1) भ्रश्यति;<BR>(2) च्यवते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fall down
FALL DOWN:<BR>I Lit.: पतति, नि-, अव-, as if the<BR>hot-rayed (sun)<BR>had f. en d. on the earth:<BR>निपतन्त-<BR>मिवोष्णरशिममुर्व्याम्, Ki.<BR>II To prostrate: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fall in
FALL IN:<BR>I To agree: q.v.<BR>II To comply:<BR>q.v.<BR>III To enter: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fall in with
FALL IN WITH: आसादयति, सम्-, (c. of सद्): v.<BR>To meet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fall off
FALL OFF:<BR>(1) भ्रश्यति,<BR>does not f. off or decay:<BR>न<BR> भ्रश्यति नजीर्यति, Vi.;<BR>spirit f.s off:<BR>तेजः प्रभ्रंशमेति,<BR>Ki.;<BR>(2) च्यवते;<BR>(3) पततिः v. To fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fall out
FALL OUT:<BR>I To quarrel: q.v.<BR>II To<BR>happen: पतति, आ-, नि-, सं-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fall over
FALL OVER:<BR>I Lit.: v. To fall.<BR>II To<BR>revolt: q.v.:<BR>the people of Tirhut have f. en<BR>o. Prahārvarman:<BR>प्रहारवर्मण्यधि विदेहा जाताः, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fall to
FALL TO:<BR>I To begin: q.v.: प्रस्तौति (स्तु, c.<BR>2.).<BR>II To apply: निविशते, अभि-, (विश्, c. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fall under
FALL UNDER:<BR>I To come under:<BR>to f. u.<BR>one's power:<BR>वशमेति, H.; v. To come.<BR>II<BR>To come within: expr. by अन्तर्गतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fall
FALL (subs.):<BR>I The act of f. ing:<BR>(1) पातः,<BR> नि-,<BR>f. of a mountain:<BR>गिरिपातः, V. p.;<BR>(2)<BR>पतनम्, नि-, प्र-,<BR>f. from a mountain:<BR>गिरेः पतनम्,<BR>H. i.;<BR>(3) अवपतनं<BR>or<BR>अवपातः (= f. ing down);<BR>(4) भ्रंशः, प्र-, (rare);<BR>(5) च्युतिः, परि-, वि-,<BR>(rare). Ph.: coming out had a f. in front:<BR>निष्क्रम्याग्रे पपात ह, Mah.: v. To fall.<BR>II<BR>Death, destruction: q.v.: पातः<BR>or<BR>पतनम्,<BR> नि-, विनि-,<BR>how will Rāvaṇa brook the repeated<BR>f. of his men:<BR>कथमिव दशमुखः भूयोभूयः स्वजनविनि-<BR>पातं सहेत, Vi.<BR>III Downfall, degradation:<BR>पातः<BR>or<BR>पतनम्, अव-, नि-, विनि-,<BR>rise and f. of<BR>men:<BR>पातोत्पाता मनुष्याणाम्, H.;<BR>even f.....is<BR>equivalent to rise:<BR>विनिपातोऽपि समं समुन्नतेः, Ki.<BR>IV Decrease: q.v.: ह्रासः,<BR>rise and f. of<BR>prices:<BR>अर्घस्य वृद्धिह्रासः, Vy. V. Cadence: q.v.:<BR>पातः।<BR>VI Declivity, slope: q.v. पातः।<BR>VII<BR>Waterfall: प्रपातः, the f. s of the great Koshi:<BR>महाकोशीप्रपातः, Ku.<BR>VIII A falling: पातः,<BR>heavy f. of hail:<BR>तुमुलकरकावृष्टिपातः, Me.<BR>IX<BR>Felling: पातः, -नम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fallacious
FALLACIOUS:<BR>(1) भ्रमजननः (नी, नं);<BR>(2) मिथ्या in<BR>comp. (= false: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fallaciously
FALLACIOUSLY:<BR>(1) भ्रमं जनयत् (f. न्ती);<BR>(2)<BR>वञ्चनार्थम् (= to deceive).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fallacy
FALLACY:<BR>I Deception: q.v.: वञ्चना।<BR>II<BR>Mistake: q.v.: भ्रमः।<BR>III Logical:<BR>(1)<BR>हेत्वाभासः, N. d.;<BR>(2) भ्रान्ततर्कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fallibility
FALLIBILITY:<BR>(1) पतनशीलता;<BR>(2) भ्रान्तिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fallible
FALLIBLE:<BR>(1) पतनशीलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) भ्रान्तः<BR>(न्ता, न्तं) (= erring).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

falling-sickness
FALLING-SICKNESS: अपस्मारः: v. Epilepsy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fallow
FALLOW (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: पतितः (ता, तं) (land<BR>which lies) f. for three years is waste (land):<BR>त्रिवर्षपतितं खिलम्, Viv.: v. Untilled.<BR>II Pale<BR>red: पाटलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fallow
FALLOW (subs.): पतितभूमिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fallow
FALLOW (v.):<BR>(1) पातयति (c. of पत्),<BR>f. ing<BR>land:<BR>क्षेत्रं पातयित्वा, Viv.;<BR>(2) वाहयति (c. of<BR>वह्),<BR>to f. low land:<BR>निम्नां भूमिं वाहयति, Pa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fallow-deer
FALLOW-DEER: हरिणविशेषः: v. Deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

false
FALSE (subs.):<BR>I Not true, not real:<BR>(1)<BR>मिथ्या। in comp.,<BR>f. reply:<BR>मिथ्योत्तरम्; to speak f.: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">Page266</a>]<BR>मिथ्या वदति, M.;<BR>(2) अलीकः (का, कं),<BR>f. pro-<BR>wess<BR>अलीकविक्रमः, Pr. i.;<BR>f. Nala:<BR>अलीकनलः,<BR>N.;<BR>(3) वितथः (था, थं), this proverb is f.:<BR>अयं लोकवादो वितथः, Ve.;<BR>(4) मृषा in comp.,<BR>f. assertion:<BR>मृषावादः, K. b.;<BR>(5) अनृतः (ता, तं),<BR>f. accusation:<BR>अनृताभियोगः, Si.;<BR>(6) असत्यः (त्या,<BR> त्यं).<BR>II Uttering falsehood: मिथ्यावादिन् (f.<BR>नी);<BR>(2) अनृतगिर् (mfn.); and sim. comp.s.<BR>III Fictitious, counterfeit: q.v.: कूट in<BR>comp.,<BR>f. measures of weight:<BR>कूटतुलामानम्, P.;<BR>f. evidence:<BR>कूटसाक्ष्यम्, M.<BR>IV. Treacherous,<BR>unfaithful: q.v.: असत्यसन्धः (न्धा, न्धं), Sa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

false
FALSE (adv.): v. Falsely.<BR>F. -hearted:<BR>कपट-<BR>हृदयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

falsehood
FALSEHOOD:<BR>I Want of truth:<BR>(1) असत्यता;<BR>(2) अलीकता;<BR>(3) वैतथ्यम्,<BR>how could f. take a<BR>footing in their speech:<BR>कथं तादृशानां गिरि<BR> वैतथ्यमास्पदं कुर्यात्, K.<BR>II A lie: q.v.: अनृतम्।<BR>III Deceit: q.v.: कैतवम्,<BR>unaquainted with<BR>f.:<BR>अनभिझः कैतवस्य, Sa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

falsely
FALSELY:<BR>I Not truly:<BR>(1) मिथ्या;<BR>(2) मृषा,<BR>deposing f.:<BR>साक्ष्यं मृषा ब्रुवन्ः, Mit.;<BR>(3) by adj.<BR>v. False.<BR>II Deceitfully: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

falseness
FALSENESS:<BR>I Lit.: अलीकता: v. Falsehood (I).<BR>II Fictitiousness: कृत्रिमता।<BR>III Perfidy,<BR>deceitfulness: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

falsification
FALSIFICATION:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मिथ्याकरणम्;<BR>(2)<BR>वितथीकरणम्, etc.<BR>II Counterfeiting,<BR>f. of<BR>coins:<BR>कृत्रिममुद्राकरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

falsifier
FALSIFIER:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by verb.<BR>II<BR>Counterfeiter: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

falsify
FALSIFY (v.t.):<BR>I To counterfeit^1; forge.<BR>II<BR>To prove^2 to be false:<BR>(1) मिथ्याकरोति,<BR> वितथीकरोति, etc., if you f. your own saying:<BR>मिथ्याकरोषि चेत् स्वीयं भाषितम्, A. r.;<BR>(2) अनृतं<BR>(f. तां) करोति;<BR>you should not f. it:<BR>तत्त्वया<BR> नानृतं कार्यम्, V. p.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

falsify
FALSIFY (v.i.):<BR>(1) मिथ्या वदति;<BR>(2) मृषा ब्रवीति,<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

falsity
FALSITY: v. Falseness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

falter
FALTER:<BR>I Of speech:<BR>making them f. at<BR>every step:<BR>वचनानि स्खलयन् पदे पदे, Ku.;<BR>f. ing<BR>with tears:<BR>साश्रुद्गदम्, D. ii.<BR>II To tremble:<BR>Ph.:<BR>with steps f. ing:<BR>स्खलिताभिर्गतिभिः, Si.<BR>ix. 78.<BR>III To fail: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faltering
FALTERING, FALTERINGLY:<BR>(1) स्खलद्गिरा;<BR>(2)<BR>गद्गदवाचा;<BR>(3) गद्गदगलोद्गच्छद्विलीनाक्षरः, J.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fame
FAME:<BR>I Rumour: q.v.: किंवदन्ती।<BR>II Glory,<BR>renown:<BR>(1) यशस् (n.),<BR>to acquire f.:<BR>यशोऽधि-<BR>गन्तुम्, Ki;<BR>(2) कीर्ति,<BR>of endless f.:<BR>अनन्तकीर्ति<BR>(mfn.), R.: v. Renown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

famed
FAMED: Celebrated, famous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

familiar
FAMILIAR (adj.):<BR>I Domestic: q.v.:<BR>II<BR>Acquainted with: q.v.:<BR>(1) परिचितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) अभिझः (झा, झं).<BR>III Easy, accessible:<BR>घनिष्ठः (ष्ठा, ष्ठं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

familiar
FAMILIAR (subs.): चिरपरिचितः, D.: Friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

familiarity
FAMILIARITY:<BR>I Acquaintance: परिचयः।<BR>II<BR>Intimacy: घनिष्ठता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

familiarize
FAMILIARIZE:<BR>(1) परिचयं करोति;<BR>(2) अभ्यस्यति<BR>(अस्, c. 4.): v. To accustom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

familiarly
FAMILIARLY:<BR>(1) विस्रब्धम्;<BR>(2) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

family
FAMILY: कुलम्,<BR>this girl is the life of the f.:<BR>कन्येयं<BR> कुलजीवितम्, Ku.;<BR>of good f.:<BR>कुलजः (जा, जं),<BR>N.: v. Race, lineage, descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

famine
FAMINE: दुर्भिक्षम्,<BR>in a f. stricken country:<BR>दुर्भिक्ष-<BR>पीडिते देशे, P. iv. 4.: f. would enter a country:<BR>दुर्भिक्षमाविशेद्राष्ट्रम्, Mah.: v. To starve, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

famish
FAMISH (v.t.): क्षुधया पीडयति (पीड्, c. 10.) or<BR>अवसादयति (c. of सद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

famish
FAMISH (v. i.): क्षुधया अवसीदति (सद्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To starve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

famous
FAMOUS:<BR>(1) ख्यातः (ता, तं), वि-, प्र-;<BR>(2) विश्रुतः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(3) प्रथितः (ता, तं): v. Renowned,<BR>illustrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fan
FAN (subs.):<BR>(1) व्यजनम्;<BR>(2) तालवृन्तः (of palm<BR>leaves). Winnowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fan
FAN (v.t.):<BR>I वीजयति, उप-, उत्-, (वीज्, c. 10.),<BR>are my friends. f. ing me:<BR>किं वीजयतो मां सख्यौ,<BR>Sa.<BR>II To kindle: q.v.: सन्धुक्षयति।<BR>III To<BR>winnow: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fanatic
FANATIC (subs.): धर्मोन्मत्तः (त्ता, त्तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fanatic
FANATIC, FANATICAL:<BR>(1) उग्रः (ग्रा, ग्रं);<BR>(2)<BR>उन्मत्तः (त्ता, त्तं) (= mad).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fanatically
FANATICALLY:<BR>(1) उन्मत्तवत् (= madly);<BR>(2)<BR>उग्रम् (= sharply).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fanaticism
FANATICISM: धर्मोन्मादः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fancier
FANCIER:<BR>I Lit.: भावकः।<BR>II A breeder: पोषकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fanciful
FANCIFUL:<BR>I Dictated by fancy:<BR>(1) भावितः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(2) कल्पितः (ता, तं).<BR>II Whim-<BR>-sical: q.v.: भावनापरायण (f. ना) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fancifully
FANCIFULLY: भावनया: v. Wildly, whimsically.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fancy
FANCY (subs.):<BR>I Imagination: q.v.: भावः,<BR> -ना,<BR>my f. -got likeness:<BR>भावगम्यं मत्सादृश्यम्, Me.<BR>II Conception, idea: q.v.: भावः, -ना।<BR>III<BR>Inclination: भावः,<BR>my mind rests on him with<BR>entire f.:<BR>ममात्र भावैकरसं मनः स्थितम्, Ku.; “f-free”<BR>भावमुक्तः (क्ता, क्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fancy
FANCY (v.i.): मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.),<BR>one who f. s.<BR>himself to be a learned man:<BR>पण्डितम्मन्यः, B.:<BR>v. To think, believe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fancy
FANCY (v. t.):<BR>I To imagine, guess: q. v.:<BR>तर्कयति (तर्क्, c. 10.); which do you f. (to be<BR>Śakuntalā): त्वं तावत् कतमां तर्कयसि, Sa.<BR>II To<BR>have a f. for: रोचते (रुच्, c. 1.). (with dat.<BR>of the person): v. To like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fancy
FANCY (adj.):<BR>F. goads:<BR>रुचिरद्रव्याणि; f. ball:<BR>*रुचिरनृत्यम्;<BR>f. price<BR>*कल्पितमूल्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fancy-sick
FANCY-SICK: दुष्टबुद्धि (mfn.) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fane
FANE: सिद्धायतनम्: v. Temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fang
FANG: दंष्ट्रा,<BR>with the rays of the f. s.:<BR>दंष्ट्रामयूखैः,<BR>R. Ph.: having poison in the f. (i. e. a<BR>serpent): आशीविषः, Ve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fanged
FANGED: दंष्ट्रिन् (f. णी), Ki. xiii. 50<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fangless
FANGLESS: दंष्ट्राहीनः (ना, नं) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fanner
FANNER, FANNING-MACHINE: व्यजनयन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fantasm
FANTASM: v. Phantom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fantastic
FANTASTIC, -AL:<BR>I Not real: कल्पितः (ता, तं)<BR>II Capricious: चपलः (ला, लं).<BR>III Irregular,<BR>wild: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fantasy
FANTASY: v. Fancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

far
FAR (adj.):<BR>I Not near:<BR>(1) द्रः (रा, रं),<BR>(with abl. or gen.),<BR>f. from the village:<BR>दूरं<BR> ग्रामस्य ग्रामाद्वा, S. k.;<BR>not very f. from here:<BR>इतो<BR> नातिदूरे, K.;<BR>(2) विप्रकृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं) (rare),<BR>even<BR>now (his) time of awaking is very f.:<BR>अद्यापि<BR> विप्रकृष्टः प्रबोधकालः, Vi.<BR>II. Remote from pur-<BR>-pose: f. be it from me to justify cruelty:<BR>*दूरतस्तावत् क्रौर्यशोधनप्रस्तावः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

far
FAR (Adv.)<BR>I To a great distance: दूरम्,<BR>with<BR>f. different results:<BR>दूरभिन्नफलयोः, Si.;<BR>f. -risen<BR>hope:<BR>दूरारोहिणी आशा, Sa.<BR>II At a great d.:<BR>दूरे, Mu. Ph.: from f.:<BR>(1) दूरात्;<BR>(2) दूरादेव,<BR>K.;<BR>(3) दूरतः, P.;<BR>(4) दूरत एव, K. How f.:<BR>(a)=to what distance: कियद्दूरं,<BR>h. f. are you<BR>coming:<BR>कियद्यावदुपैषि दूरम्, N.;<BR>(2) कियत्,<BR>h. f. did<BR>he come following us:<BR>कियदनुसरन्नस्मानसावागतः, K.<BR>(b)=at what distance:<BR>(1) कियद्दूरे;<BR>(2)<BR>कियत्यध्वनि, what sort of a place is Ujjayanī and<BR>how f. is it (from here): कीदृश्युज्जयिनी कियत्यध्वनि<BR> सा च, K. Far off:<BR>(1) दूरं<BR>or<BR>दूरेः v. Far.<BR>(2)<BR>दूरस्थः (स्था, स्थं) (= situated f.),<BR>nearing what<BR>was f. o.:<BR>नेदयन् दूरसंस्थम्, B. So far (i. e. such a<BR>distance): एतावतीं भूमिम्, K. So far as: v. So.<BR>As far as: (a)=up to: पर्यन्तं in comp.,<BR>as f.<BR>as the park:<BR>वनान्तपर्यन्तम्, N.; (b)=so far as:<BR>v. So.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farf-famed
FARF-FAMED:<BR>(1) दूरयशस् (mfn.) (?);<BR>(2) प्रथित-<BR>यशस् (mfn.);<BR>(3) उरुकीर्ति। (mfn.), R.; and<BR>sim. comp s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farce
FARCE:<BR>I A comedy: प्रहसनम्:<BR>II Empty<BR>show: perh. दर्शनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farcical
FARCICAL: v. Ludicrous, deceptive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farcin
FARCIN, FARCY: जन्तूनां चर्मरोगविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fare
FARE (subs.):<BR>I Food: q. v.: अन्नम्।<BR>II Passage<BR>money: (f.) तारिकं<BR>or<BR>तार्यम् (for crossing);<BR>(2)<BR>वाहिकम् (?) (for conveying).<BR>III News; वार्त्ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fare
FARE (v.i.):<BR>I To go, pass: q.v.: व्रजति (व्रज्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II To be in any state:<BR>how does<BR>Sāgarikā f.:<BR>सागरिकायाः किं वर्तते, Ra,;<BR>he f. s.<BR>well, ill:<BR>तस्य प्रियं, अप्रियं वर्तते: v. To happen.<BR>III To feed: q.v.: भोजनं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farewell
FAREWELL: v. Adieu. Bid your companion f.:<BR>आमन्त्रयस्व सहचरम्, Sa.; I have done, f. to you:<BR>साधयाम्यहमविघ्नमस्तु ते, R.;<BR>“f.:”<BR>शिवमस्तु।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farina
FARINA:<BR>I Flour: q.v.:<BR>II Pollen:<BR>(1)<BR>परागः;<BR>(2) पुष्परेणुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farinaceous
FARINACEOUS:<BR>I Made of flour: चूर्णमयः (यी,<BR> यं) (?).<BR>II Yielding f.: चूर्णदः (दा, दं) (?).<BR>III<BR>Mealy: चूर्ण- in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farm
FARM (subs.):<BR>I Lit. क्षेत्रम्,<BR>owner of a f.:<BR>क्षेत्र-<BR>पतिः, H.<BR>II Lease: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farm
FARM (v.):<BR>I To let: q.v.: भाटेन<BR>or<BR>भाटकेन<BR> ददाति (दा, c. 8.).<BR>II To hire: भाटयति (c. of<BR>भट्)<BR>or<BR>भाटकेन गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.), Viv.<BR>III<BR>To cultivate: q.v.: क्षेत्रं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farmer
FARMER:<BR>I A cultivator:<BR>(1) क्षेत्रपतिः;<BR>(2)<BR>क्षेत्रस्वामिन् (m);<BR>(3) क्षेत्रिकः।<BR>II A lease-<BR>-holder: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farm-yard
FARM-YARD: कुशूलचत्वरम; कुशूलाङ्गनम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farming
FARMING (subs.):<BR>(1) कृषिकर्मन् (n.);<BR>(2) क्षेत्र-<BR>कर्मन् (n.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farrago
FARRAGO (subs.): घोलम् (?): v. Medley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farrier
FARRIER:<BR>(1) अश्ववैद्यः;<BR>(2) अश्वचिकित्सकः;<BR>(3)<BR>अश्वलाक्षणिकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farriery
FARRIERY: अश्वचिकित्सा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farrow
FARROW: v. To bring forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farther
FARTHER: v. Further (adj. and adv.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

farthing
FARTHING: ताम्रमुद्राविशेषः; *पेनिपादम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fasces
FASCES: दण्डपरशुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fasciation
FASCIATION: बन्धः: v. Bondage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fascicular
FASCICULAR: पुञ्जितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fascinate
FASCINATE (v.): मोहयति, वि- (c. of मुह्),<BR>what<BR>man you may not f.:<BR>पुमांसं कं न मोहयेः, Mah.:<BR>v. To bewitch, charm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fascinating
FASCINATING (adj.):<BR>(1) मोहनः (नी, नं);<BR>(2)<BR>विमोहिन् (f. नी),<BR>world-f. Sitā:<BR>सीता लोक-<BR>विमोहिनी, A.r.: v. Charming. Ph:<BR>a woman<BR>with f. eyes:<BR>मदिराक्षी, R.; मुग्धाक्षी, Mal.; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fascination
FASCINATION:<BR>I The art: मोहनम्, वि-; better<BR>by verb.<BR>II The power: मोहनी शक्तिः, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fash
FASH:<BR>I Verb: v. To vex, tease.<BR>II Subs.:<BR>v. Anxiety, care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fashion
FASHION (subs.):<BR>I Shape, make: q.v.:<BR>गठनम्।<BR>II Prevailing custom: रीतिः (?),<BR>this<BR>is the new f.:<BR>*इयममिनवा रीतिः।<BR>III Manner,<BR>way: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fashion
FASHION (v.):<BR>I To form: q.v.: गठति (गठ्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II To fit, adopt: q.v.:<BR>“laws<BR>ought to be f. ed to the manners of the people”:<BR>*लोकाचारानुरूपिणो विधयो विधेयाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fashionable
FASHIONABLE:<BR>I Approved.: लोकसम्मतः (ता, तं):<BR>v. Good.<BR>II Current: q.v.: प्रचलितः (ता,<BR> तं).<BR>III Observing fashions: no equiv.:<BR>*रीत्यनुयायिन् (f. नी).<BR>IV Gentle, good: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fashionably
FASHIONABLY: *रीत्यनुसारेण; यथारीति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fashion-monger
FASHION-MONGER: *रीत्यैकदृश् (mfn.): v. Fop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fast
FAST (adj.):<BR>I Firm: q.v.: दृढः (ढा, ढं). Ph.:<BR>f. sleep:<BR>गाढनिद्रा;<BR>very f. friend:<BR>घनिष्ठमित्रम्।<BR>II<BR>Swift: q.v.: शीघ्रगामिन् (f. नी).<BR>III Rash:<BR>q.v.: प्रमत्तः (त्ता, त्तं).<BR>A f. girl:<BR>प्रगल्भवनिता, K.;<BR>f.-handed:<BR>बद्धमुष्टि (mfn.), N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fast
FAST (adv.):<BR>I Firmly: q.v.: दृढम्।<BR>II<BR>Swiftly: q.v.:<BR>(1) शीघ्नम्;<BR>(2) आशु,<BR>f. er than<BR>the mind itself:<BR>मनसोऽप्याशुतरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fast
FAST (subs.):<BR>I F. ing:<BR>(1) उपवासः;<BR>(2)<BR>अनशनम्, निराहारः (= not taking food);<BR>(3) प्रायः<BR>(rare), R.<BR>II F. ing time: उपवासकालः,<BR>f.<BR>day:<BR>उपवासदिनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fast
FAST (v.i.):<BR>(1) उपवसति (वस्, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>उपवासं<BR> करोति<BR>or<BR>कुरुते, but (they) all f. ed that day:<BR>तस्मिंस्तु दिवसे सर्वे उपवासं प्रचक्रिरे, A r.;<BR>(2) न<BR> अश्नाति (अश्, c. 9.), etc.: v. To eat, not.<BR>To<BR>f. to death:<BR>अनशनेन उपरमते (रम्, c. 1.), D. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fasten
FASTEN (v.): बध्नाति, नि-, आ-, सं-, (बन्ध्, c. 9),<BR>f. ing a chain to the feet:<BR>शृङ्नलया चरणयोर्निबध्य,<BR>V.t.;<BR>did not f. her affection on him:<BR>तस्मिन्<BR> भावं न बबन्ध, R. vi. 36.;<BR>she took off (her)<BR>necklace and f. ed on a bark:<BR>सा हारं विमुच्य वल्कलं<BR> बबन्ध, Ku. v. 8;<BR>f. ed. (secured) by the glances<BR>of beauties:<BR>सुन्दरीणां कटाक्षैर्बद्धः, Ku. iii. 5.: v.<BR>To bind, tie. Ph.:<BR>to f. a door:<BR>द्वारं ददाति, Vi.<BR>or<BR>कपाटं ददाति, Va.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fastener
FASTENER: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fastening
FASTENING (subs.):<BR>I The act: बन्धनम्।<BR>II<BR>That which binds: बन्धः, -नः, -नी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faster
FASTER:<BR>(1) उपवासकारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) कृतोपवासः<BR>(सा, सं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fastidious
FASTIDIOUS:<BR>(1) दोषदृश् (mfn.) (= fault-find-<BR>-ing);<BR>(2) असन्तुष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं) (=discontented);<BR>(3) कष्टप्रीतः (ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fastidiously
FASTIDIOUSLY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fastidiousness
FASTIDIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) दोषदर्शिता;<BR>(2) असन्तुष्टता:<BR>v. Fastidious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fasting
FASTING (subs.): v. Fast (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fastly
FASTLY: दृढम्: v. Firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fastness
FASTNESS:<BR>I Firmness; q. v.: दृढता।<BR>II<BR>A fort: दुर्गम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fat
FAT (adj.):<BR>I Corpulent:<BR>(1) पीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) पीवरः (रा, रं);<BR>(3) मेदस्विन् (f. नी), f. men:<BR>मेदस्विनः, Bha.;<BR>(4) पुष्टाङ्ग (f. ङ्गी) (in body),<BR>H.<BR>II Oily, rich:<BR>(1) घृतसंसृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं) (in<BR>ghee);<BR>(2) मेदस्विन् (f. नी) (?) (in fat).<BR>III<BR>Dull, stupid: q.v.<BR>IV Productive, rich:<BR>स्फीतः (ता, तं),<BR>of f. capital:<BR>स्फीतसारधनः (ना, नं),<BR>D.;<BR>the country became f.:<BR>स्फीतो जनपदोऽभवत्,<BR>Mah. ii. 33. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fat
FAT (subs.):<BR>(1) मेदस् (n.);<BR>(2) वसा;<BR>(3) वपा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatal
FATAL:<BR>I Inevitable: q.v.<BR>II Deadly,<BR>mortal:<BR>(1) प्राणहरः (री, रं);<BR>(2) सांघातिकः<BR>(की, कं);<BR>(3) आत्ययिकः (की, कं);<BR>(4) दुरन्तः<BR>(न्ता, न्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatalism
FATALISM: दैष्टिकता, Si. ii. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatalist
FATALIST:<BR>(1) दैष्टिकः;<BR>(2) दैवप्रमाणकः, M.n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatality
FATALITY:<BR>I Inevitable necessity: दैवनिर्बन्धः।<BR>II Mortality:<BR>(1) प्राणहरत्वम्;<BR>(2) साङ्घातिकता;<BR>(3) better by adj.<BR>III Fate: q.v.: भवितव्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatally
FATALLY:<BR>I Inevitably दैवनिर्बन्धेन।<BR>II<BR>Mortally: expr. by adj.: to wound f.:<BR>प्राणहरव्रणं करोति;<BR>f. deceived:<BR>आत्ययिकवञ्चनागतः<BR>(ता, तं) (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fate
FATE:<BR>I In abstract sense:<BR>(1) दैवम्,<BR>f. can-<BR>not be altered:<BR>न शक्यं दैवमन्यथा कर्तुम्, K.;<BR>(2)<BR>नियतिः,<BR>f. is the cause in the world:<BR>नियतिः कारणं<BR> लोके, Ram.;<BR>(3) भवितव्यता, following^1 f.:<BR>भवितव्यतानुविधायिन् (f. नी), V.;<BR>(4) विधिः,<BR>f.<BR>dominates:<BR>प्रभवति विधिः, K.;<BR>(5) दिष्टम्;<BR>(6)<BR>अदृष्टम्।<BR>II Appointed lot: दिष्टम्,<BR>has met end<BR>of f.:<BR>दिष्टान्तं समनुप्राप्तः, Ram. ii. 74. 25.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fated
FATED:<BR>(1) दैवविहितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) विधिकृतः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(3) दिष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

father
FATHER: (subs.):<BR>(1) पितृ (m.),<BR>he was the f.,<BR>their f. s were only begetters:<BR>स पिता पितरस्तासां<BR> केवलं जन्महेतवः, R. i. 24.;<BR>you are the f. of<BR>f.s:<BR>त्वं पितॄणामसि पिता, Ku. ii. 14.;<BR>(2) जनकः;<BR>(3) जनयितृ (m.);<BR>(4) तातः (= papa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

father
FATHER (v.):<BR>I To beget: q.v.<BR>II To<BR>adopt: q.v.<BR>III To f. on or upon: v. To<BR>ascribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatherhood
FATHERHOOD: पितृत्वम्: v.: Paternity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

father-land
FATHER-LAND:<BR>(1) पैतृकभूमिः;<BR>(2) पितृभूमिः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

father-in-law
FATHER-IN-LAW: श्वशुरः,<BR>your f. is my friend:<BR>तव<BR> श्वशुरो मे सखा, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatherless
FATHERLESS:<BR>(1) पितृहीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) अपितृकः<BR>(का, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatherliness
FATHERLINESS:<BR>(1) expr. by adj.;<BR>(2) वात्सल्यम्<BR>(= fatherly affection).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatherly
FATHERLY (adj.):<BR>(1) पितृसन्निभः (भा, भं) and<BR>sim. comp. s.;<BR>(2) by adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatherly
FATHERLY (adv.)<BR>(1) पितृवत्;<BR>(2) पितेव।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fathom
FATHOM:<BR>I Subs.: व्यामः<BR>or<BR>व्यायामः।<BR>II Verb:<BR>मापयति (c. of मा): v. To measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fathomless
FATHOMLESS:<BR>(1) अगाधः (धा, धं);<BR>(2) अतलस्पर्शः<BR>(र्शा, र्शं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatigue
FATIGUE (subs.):<BR>(1) आयासाः, Ki. vii. 3.;<BR>(2)<BR>खेदः (= exhaustion), Si. vii. 75.;<BR>(3) क्लान्तिः<BR>or<BR>क्लमः (= weariness), Ki. ix. 75.;<BR>(4) श्रमः or<BR>परिश्रमः (= by exertion), R. ix. 49. Ph.:<BR>inured to f.:<BR>जितश्रमः (मा, मं), Ka.;<BR>able to bear<BR>f.:<BR>आयाससहः (हा, हं), V. p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatigue
FATIGUE (v.):<BR>(1) आयासयति (c. of यस्);<BR>(2)<BR>खेदयति (c. of खिद्);<BR>(3) क्लमयति, परि-, (c. of<BR>क्लम्);<BR>(4) श्रमं जनयति (c. of जन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatigued
FATIGUED:<BR>(1) श्रान्तः<BR>or<BR>परिश्रान्तः (न्ता, न्तं),<BR>f.<BR>by watering the trees:<BR>वृक्षसेचनात् परिश्रान्ता, Sa.;<BR>(2) क्लान्तः<BR>or<BR>परिक्लान्तः (न्ता, न्तं);<BR>(3) खिन्नः<BR>(न्ना, न्नं);<BR>(4) आयासितः (ता, तं). To be f.:<BR>(1)<BR>श्राम्यति, परि-, (श्रम्, c. 4.);<BR>(2) क्लाम्यति (क्लम्,<BR>c. 4.);<BR>(3) खिद्यते (खिद्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatiguing
FATIGUING (adj.):<BR>(1) श्रमकरः (री, रं);<BR>(2)<BR>आयासकरः (री, रं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatness
FATNESS:<BR>(1) मेदस्विता;<BR>(2) पीनता;<BR>(3) पीवरता;<BR>(4) पुष्टाङ्गता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatten
FATTEN (v.t.):<BR>(1) प्याययति, आ-, (c. of प्यै);<BR>(2) पीवरीकरोति;<BR>(3) बृंहयति (c. of बृंह्);<BR>(4)<BR>by (adj.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatten
FATTEN (v.i.):<BR>(1) प्यायते, आ-, (प्यै, c. 1.);<BR>(2)<BR>by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fattening
FATTENING:<BR>(1) पौष्टिकः (की, कं) (= nourishing);<BR>(2) बृंहण (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatty
FATTY: मेदस्विन् (f. नी).<BR>F. tissue:<BR>*मेदोजालम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatuitous
FATUITOUS, FATUOUS:<BR>I Foolish, weak: q.v.:<BR>दुर्बुद्धि (mfn.).<BR>II Illusory: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fatuity
FATUITY: मूर्खता: v. Foolishness, weakness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faucet
FAUCET: for drawing liquors: *निष्काशकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fault
FAULT:<BR>(1) दोषः,<BR>this is not your f.:<BR>न ते दोषोऽयम्,<BR>P. i. 16.;<BR>will not find f. with it:<BR>दोषं न ग्रहीष्यति,<BR>Sa.;<BR>these are f.s of language:<BR>वाक्येऽपि दोषाः<BR> सन्त्येते, Kav.;<BR>(2) अपराधः (not physical),<BR>how<BR>can a slave be without f.:<BR>कथं नु दासो निरपराधः,<BR>V. ii.;<BR>it is not the f. of a stump if a blind man<BR>does not see it:<BR>नैष स्थाणोरपराधो यदेनमन्धो न पश्यति,<BR>Say. To find f. with: दूषयति (c. of दुष्),<BR>bad<BR>men in a moment find f. with the excellencies of<BR>good men:<BR>दुर्जनो दूषयत्येव सतां गुणगणं क्षणात्, J.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fault-finder
FAULT-FINDER: दोषदृश् (mfn.),<BR>a mere f.:<BR>दोषैक-<BR>दृश् (mfn.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faultily
FAULTILY:<BR>(1) सदोषम्;<BR>(2) साधपराधम;<BR>(3) दोषेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faultiness
FAULTINESS:<BR>(1) सदोषता;<BR>(2) दुष्टता;<BR>(3)<BR>सापराधता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faultless
FAULTLESS:<BR>(1) निर्दोषः (षा, षं);<BR>(2) दोषहीनः<BR>(ना, नं); दोषशून्यः (न्या, न्यं), etc.: v. Devoid<BR>of;<BR>(3) अदोषः (षा, षं): v. Also blameless,<BR>innocent, correct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faultlessness
FAULTLESSNESS:<BR>(1) निर्दोषता;<BR>(2) दोषशून्यता; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

faulty
FAULTY:<BR>(1) दोषवत् (f. ती),<BR>f. girl:<BR>दोषवती कन्या,<BR>M. ix. 73.;<BR>(2) दोषिन् (f. णी);<BR>(3) सदोषः<BR>(षा, षं);<BR>(3) दुष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं) (often=vicious),<BR>afterwards found to be f.:<BR>*दुष्टं पश्चाद्विभावितम्,<BR>Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fauna
FAUNA: जन्तवः (m. pl.),<BR>fossil f.:<BR>*शिलीभूत-<BR>जन्तवः: v. Animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

favour
FAVOUR (subs.):<BR>(1) अनुग्रहः,<BR>f. proceeding from<BR>remembrance:<BR>संस्मरणप्रवृत्तोऽनुग्रहः, Ku. iii. 3;<BR>with your f.:<BR>तवानुग्रहात्;<BR>even this my chastise-<BR>ment has been made a f. by you:<BR>मम त्वया<BR> निग्रहोऽप्ययमनुग्रहीकृतः, R. xi. 90.;<BR>disposer of f. s<BR>and dis-f.s:<BR>अनुग्रहावग्रहयोर्विधाता, Si. i. 71.;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रसादः (= a f.), do the f. (to excuse me),<BR>Sir:<BR>तत्<BR> प्रसादं करोतु स्वामी, P. i. 3.;<BR>who eagerly longs<BR>for your f.:<BR>प्रसादमाकांक्षति यस्तोवोत्सुकः, V. III.<BR>Ph. in f. with i. e. f. ed: v. F. ite; in f.<BR>of i.e. on the side of: पक्षे (with gen.). v.<BR>Side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

favour
FAVOUR (v.t.):<BR>(1) अनुगृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.),<BR>just<BR>favour with a look:<BR>विलोकनेनानुगृहाण तावत्, N.<BR>xxii. 3;<BR>(2) अनुकूलयति (nomi.) (= to be<BR>friend),<BR>even Indra f. s him with ornaments of<BR>the Kalpa tree:<BR>तमनुकूलयतीन्द्रोऽपि कल्पद्रुमविभूषणैः,<BR>Ku. ii. 39.;<BR>(3) by subs.,<BR>the king ceased to<BR>f. Dantila:<BR>स राजा दन्तिलस्य प्रसादपराङ्मुखः सञ्जातः,<BR>P. i. 3.;<BR>(4) अभ्युपपद्यते (पद्, c. 4.), Ku. v. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

favourable
FAVOURABLE:<BR>(1) अनुकूलः (ला, लं),<BR>considering<BR>what was f. to him:<BR>अस्यानुकूलं विचिन्त्य, Ki. xii.<BR>43.;<BR>f. wind:<BR>अनुकूलवातः;<BR>(2) प्रसन्नः (न्ना, न्नं)<BR>(= cheerful);<BR>f. look:<BR>प्रसन्नदृष्टिः;<BR>(3) शुमः<BR>(भा, भं) (= auspicious: of time): v. Also<BR>conducive, good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

favourableness
FAVOURABLENESS:<BR>(1) अनुकूलता;<BR>(2) प्रसन्नता: v.<BR>FAVOURABLE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

favourer
FAVOURER:<BR>(1) अनुग्रहकारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) better<BR>by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

favourite
FAVOURITE (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रियपात्रम्, प्रियमाजनम्, and<BR>sim. comp.s,<BR>I was her greatest f.:<BR>तस्याः परं<BR> प्रसादपात्रमासम्, D. ii.;<BR>(2) वल्लभ (f. मा),<BR>and to<BR>the f.s of a king:<BR>वल्लभेभ्यश्च भूपतेः, Ka. v. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

favourite
FAVOURITE (adj.): प्रियः (या, यं): v. Dear,<BR>favourite (subs.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

favouritism
FAVOURITISM:<BR>(1) वल्लभप्रियता (?);<BR>(2) पक्षपातिता<BR>(= partiality).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fawn
FAWN (subs.):<BR>(1) मृगशावः, -कः;<BR>(2) मृगपोतः;<BR>(3) हरिणशिशुः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fawn
FAWN (v.):<BR>I To bring forth a f.: प्रसूते (सू,<BR>c. 2.),<BR>f. ing of deer:<BR>मृगीणां प्रसूतिः, R.<BR>II To<BR>flatter: q.v.: चाटुशतं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fawningly
FAWNINGLY:<BR>(1) चाटुशतैः, H.;<BR>(2) स्तुतीः कृत्वा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fay
FAY:<BR>I Subs., a fairy: q.v.: विद्याधरी।<BR>II<BR>verb., to fit, suit: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fealty
FEALTY: प्रभुभक्तिः (?): v. Also loyalty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fear
FEAR (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मयम्,<BR>out of f.:<BR>भयात्,<BR>Sa.;<BR>or, through f. of the ascetic:<BR>भयेन वा मुनेः,<BR>Ki.;<BR>(2) भीतिः (rare);<BR>(3) त्रासः, सम्-, परि-,<BR>(= terror, q.v.).<BR>II Source of (1).: मयम्,<BR>the f. from the titan is over:<BR>सुरारिसम्भवं भयं गतम्,<BR>V. i.;<BR>you have no f. from me:<BR>न मत्तोऽस्ति भयं तव,<BR>Mah., ii. 43. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fear
FEAR (v.t.):<BR>(1) बिभेति (मी, c. 3.) (with abl.),<BR>f. s. thieves:<BR>चौराद्विभेति, S. k.;<BR>f. s in the<BR>forest:<BR>अरण्ये बिभेति, S.k.:<BR>(2) त्रस्यति, सं-, वि-,<BR> परि-, (त्रस, c. 4.) (with abl.): stronger [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">Page271</a>]<BR>than f.,<BR>if he did not f. the god Śiva:<BR>यदि तेन<BR> देवाद्भवानीपतेर्न त्रस्तम्, Vi. ii. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fear
FEAR (v.i.):<BR>I Lit.: बिभेति।<BR>II To appre-<BR>-hend: q.v.: शङ्कते, आ-, (शङ्क्, c. 1.),<BR>affection<BR>f. s of evil:<BR>स्नेहः पापशङ्की, Sa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fearful
FEARFUL (adj.):<BR>I Inspiring fear:<BR>(1) भयङ्करः<BR>(री, रं);<BR>(2) भयावहः (हा, हं);<BR>(3) भयदः (दा,<BR> दं);<BR>(4) भयदायिन्<BR>or<BR>-विधायिन् (f. नी);<BR>(5)<BR>भयानकः (का, कं);<BR>(6) भीषणः (णा, णं): v.<BR>Dreadful, terrible.<BR>II Full of fear:<BR>(1)<BR>भीतः (ता, तं) (with abl. of the source of<BR>fear): v. Afraid;<BR>(2) सभयः (या, यं) (= possess-<BR>-ed of fear);<BR>(3) भयातुरः (रा, रं) (= habi-<BR>-tually);<BR>(4) त्रस्नु (mfn.): v. Timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fearfully
FEARFULLY:<BR>I Timidly:<BR>(1) सभयम्;<BR>(2)<BR>ससाध्वसम्;<BR>(3) सत्रासम्, Y.<BR>II Frightfully,<BR>terribly: q.v.: मीषणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fearfulness
FEARFULNESS:<BR>I Timidity:<BR>(1) भीतिः (with<BR>abl.): v. Fear;<BR>(2) भीरुता (habitual).<BR>II<BR>Dreadfulness: q.v.: भीषणत्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fearless
FEARLESS:<BR>(1) निर्भयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) निर्भीकः (का,<BR> कं);<BR>(3) अकुतोभयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fearlessly
FEARLESSLY:<BR>(1) निर्भयम्;<BR>(2) by the adj.s:<BR>अपभयः (या, यं), अपभी, गतभी, विगतभी (n. भि)<BR>etc. R. iii. 51.; xi. 70.;<BR>(3) निःशङ्कम् (with-<BR>-out any apprehension).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fearlessness
FEARLESSNESS:<BR>(1) निर्भीकता;<BR>(2) निर्भयता;<BR>(3)<BR>अभीतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feasibility
FEASIBILITY:<BR>(1) साध्यता;<BR>(2) उपादेयता (com-<BR>-bining utility).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feasible
FEASIBLE:<BR>(1) साध्य (f. ध्या);<BR>(2) उपादेयः (या,<BR> यं) (f. and useful).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feast
FEAST (subs.):<BR>I Festival: q.v.: उत्सवः<BR>“moveable f.”:<BR>अस्थिरोत्सवः (?).<BR>II Banquct:<BR>सम्भोजनम् (?).<BR>III Fig.: उत्सवः, f. to the eye:<BR>नयनोत्सवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feast
FEAST (v.i.):<BR>I Lit.: विशिष्टभोजनं करोति (?).<BR>II Fig.: मोदते, प्र-, (मुद्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feast
FEAST (v.t.):<BR>I Lit: विशिष्टभोजनं ददाति (दा, c.<BR>3.) (?).<BR>II Fig.: to delight: q.v.: मोदयति,<BR> प्र- (c. of मुद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feat
FEAT (subs.): अवदानम्,<BR>whose f.s are seen:<BR>दृष्टावदानः<BR>(ना, नं), K. xviii. 16.: v. Deed, exploit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feather
FEATHER (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पत्रम्,<BR>I am throw-<BR>ing away this one f.:<BR>एतत्पत्रं त्यजाम्येकम्, Mah. i.<BR>30. 21.; f. -bed: (*पतग-) पत्रसंस्तरः;<BR>to win a f.<BR>in the cap:<BR>सुभगपताकां हरति, D.;<BR>(2) पर्णः,<BR>good<BR>f. ed:<BR>सुपर्णः, Mah.<BR>II Of an arrow:<BR>(1) पत्रम्,<BR>heron- f. ed (arrows): कङ्कपत्राः, U.;<BR>(2) पक्षः,<BR>of f. supported arrows:<BR>पक्षाश्रयिणां शिलीमुखानाम्,<BR>Si. xx. 9.<BR>III A species: q.v.: जातिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

featly
FEATLY: वामम्: v. Cleverly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feature
FEATURE:<BR>I Form: q.v.: रूपम्,<BR>the same digni-<BR>fied f.s.:<BR>रूपं तदोजस्वि, R.; what sort of f.s he has:<BR>कीदृशं तस्य रूपम्, K.<BR>II The face: q.v.: मुखम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

febrifuge
FEBRIFUGE: जवरघ्न (f. घ्नी) and sim. comp.s.,<BR>a f.;<BR>ज्वरघ्नभौषधम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

febrile
FEBRILE: expr. by comp. or gen.,<BR>f. symp-<BR>toms:<BR>ज्वरस्य लक्षणम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

february
FEBRUARY: उत्तरमाघपूर्वफाल्गुनसंवादीयुरूपीयवर्षस्य<BR> द्वितीयो मासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fecal
FECAL: expr. by comp.,<BR>f. ditch:<BR>अमेध्यखातम्;<BR>f. matter:<BR>मलम्: v. Dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feculence
FECULENCE: पङ्किलता: v. Muddiness, foul-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feculent
FECULENT: अमेध्य (f. ध्या): v. Foul, muddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fecundate
FECUNDATE:<BR>I Lit.: बहुप्रजं (f. जां) करोति (?).<BR>II To impregnate.: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fecundity
FECUNDITY:<BR>I Of seeds or plants:<BR>(1) फल-<BR>वत्ता;<BR>(2) better by adj. फलदः (दा, दं).<BR>II<BR>Of females:बहुप्रजात्वम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

federal
FEDERAL: *संहतः (ता, तं),<BR>f. constitution:<BR>*संहत-<BR>तन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

federal
FEDERAL, FEDERALIST: *संहतिध्वजः (जा, जं);<BR>संहतिवादिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

federalism
FEDERALISM: *संहतिवादः; संहतिध्वजानां मतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fee
FEE (subs.):<BR>I Property, possession: q.v.<BR>II Charge, pay: शुल्क (mn.),<BR>even a Śūdra<BR>should not take f., giving away a daughter:<BR>आददीत न शूद्रोऽपि शुल्कं दुहितरं ददत्, M. ix. 98.;<BR>f. giver:<BR>शुल्कदः, M. iii.<BR>F. -simple:<BR>चिरस्थायिनी<BR> भूमिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fee
FEE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: शुल्कं ददाति (दा, c. 3.).<BR>II<BR>To bribe: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feeble
FEEBLE: दुर्बलः (ला, लं),<BR>the king is the strength<BR>of the f.:<BR>दुर्बलस्य बलं राजा, J.; having f. hope [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">Page272</a>]<BR>for the fulfilment of his object:<BR>स्वार्थोपपत्तिं प्रति<BR> दुर्वलाशः, R. v. 12.: v. Weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feebleness
FEEBLENESS:<BR>(1) दौबल्यम्;<BR>(2) दुर्बलता: v.<BR>Weakness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feebly
FEEBLY:<BR>(1) by adj.;<BR>(2) दुर्बलतया<BR>or<BR>बलक्षयात्<BR>मन्दं मन्दम् (= slowly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feed
FEED (subs.):<BR>I Food: q.v.: भोजनम्,<BR>she is<BR>my f.:<BR>सा भोजनं मे, M.n.<BR>II Pasture-land:<BR>प्रचारभूमिः।<BR>III Of a boiler. *पोषकम्; जलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feed
FEED (v.t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) भोजयति (c. of भुज्),<BR>should f. hundred Brahmins:<BR>शतं द्विजान् भोजयेत्,<BR>Shat.; employed Duḥśāsana about f. ing people:<BR>भक्ष्यभोज्याधिकारेषु दुःशासनमायोजयत्, Ma. n.;<BR>(2)<BR>आशयति, प्र-, (c. of अश्) (rare).<BR>II To graze:<BR>q.v.: चारयति (c. of चर्).<BR>III To fill the<BR>wants of: पूरयति (पूर्, c. 10.).<BR>IV To<BR>supply: ददाति (दा, c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feed
FEED (v.i.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) भोजनं करोति;<BR>(2) अत्ति<BR>(अद्, c. 2.): v. To eat.<BR>II To graze: q.v.<BR>III Fig., to grow fat: स्फीतः (ता, तं) भवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feeder
FEEDER:<BR>I An eater: q.v.<BR>II One who<BR>gives food:<BR>(1) भोजयितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) आशयितृ<BR>(f. त्री), Si.<BR>III An encourager: उत्साहदातृ<BR>(f. त्री).<BR>IV A breeder: पोषक (f. षिका).<BR>V<BR>Of roads and canals:<BR>f. road:<BR>*अङ्गपथः,<BR> पोषकपथः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feeding
FEEDING (subs.):<BR>I The act: expr. by verb.<BR>II Food: q.v.: भोजनम्।<BR>III Pasture-land:<BR>प्रचारभूमिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feel
FEEL (v.t.):<BR>I To perceive:<BR>(1) अनुभवति (भू,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>much more, Mahāśvetā who has felt the<BR>ways of love:<BR>किमुतानुभूतमदनवृत्तान्ता महाश्वेता, K.,<BR>as if f. ing the pain of those who ask:<BR>वेदना-<BR>मनुमवन्निवार्थिनाम् Ki. xiii. 60.;<BR>(2) उपलभते (लभ्,<BR>c. 1.) (= to receive), then Śiva f. ing pleasure:<BR>उपलब्धसुखस्तदा हरः, Ku. iv. 42.:<BR>(3) वेत्ति, सं-<BR>(विद्, c. 2.) (= to know),<BR>which one f.s but<BR>cannot express:<BR>अनाख्येयः (या, यं), संवेद्यः (द्या, द्यं),<BR>K.<BR>II To be conscious of: जानाति (झा, c.<BR>9.),<BR>the two sons of Daśaratha were not seen but<BR>felt:<BR>झातावुभौ दाशरथी न दृष्टौ, R.: v. To know.<BR>III To touch: q.v.: स्पृशति (स्पृश्, c. 6.).<BR>IV To examine by touching: स्पृशति,<BR>should<BR>carefully f. the pulse:<BR>नाडीमवहितः स्पृशेत्, Bha.:<BR>v. Also to examine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feel
FEEL (v.i.).<BR>I To appear to the touch:<BR>expr. by स्पर्शः।<BR>II In other senses: v. Feel<BR>(trans.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feel
FEEL (subs.):<BR>I F. ing: q.v.<BR>II Touch:<BR>q.v.: स्पर्शः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feeler
FEELER:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by verb.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>expr. by circumlo,<BR>it is a f.:<BR>*मतझानायेदं प्रयुक्तम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feeling
FEELING (subs.):<BR>I The sense: स्पर्शः।<BR>II<BR>Perception:<BR>(1) अनुभवः, (rarely) अनुभूतिः;<BR> उपलब्धिः; (rarely),<BR>(2) उपलम्मः। (actual f.),<BR>from<BR>the f. of pleasure:<BR>सुखोपलम्भात्, R.;<BR>(3) संवेदः, -नम्<BR>(= knowledge),<BR>only for f. pain:<BR>दुःखसंवेदनायैव,<BR>U. i. 47.<BR>III Susceptibility to emotions:<BR>expr. by हृदयम् (= heart),<BR>a man of f.:<BR>सहृदयः<BR>(या, यं),<BR>destitute of f.:<BR>निष्करुण (f. णा): v.<BR>Hard.<BR>IV Any state of mind:<BR>(1) भावः;<BR>(2) वृत्तिः। Ph.:<BR>f. of pride:<BR>अभिमानिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feelingly
FEELINGLY: सहृदयतया (?): v. Affectingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feign
FEIGN (v.): expr. by f. ed,<BR>f. ing quarrel:<BR>कृतक-<BR>कलहं कृत्वा, Mu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feigned
FEIGNED (adj.):<BR>(1) कपट in comp.,<BR>with f.<BR>cloak of virtue:<BR>कपटधर्मकञ्चुकः, Da. i.: v. Coun-<BR>-terfeit;<BR>(2) कृतकः (का, कं),<BR>f. anger:<BR>कृतककोपः,<BR>Sa. v.: v. Affected;<BR>(3) अलीकः (का, कं),<BR>f. Nala:<BR>अलीकनलः, N.: v. False.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feignedly
FEIGNEDLY:<BR>(1) सकपटम्;<BR>(2) सव्याजम्;<BR>(3) मिथ्या:<BR>v. Falsely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feigner
FEIGNER: expr. by adj.,<BR>f. of anger:<BR>कृतककोपकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feint
FEINT: छलम्: v. Pretence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

felicitate
FELICITATE (v.):<BR>I To delight: q.v.<BR>II To<BR>congratulate: expr. by दिष्ट्या वर्धते (वृध्, c. 1.),<BR>I f. you on your recovery:<BR>दिष्ट्या वर्धसे रोगोत्यानेन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

felicitous
FELICITOUS.<BR>(1) श्रेयसः (सी, सं);<BR>(2) श्रेयस्करः<BR>(री, रं): v. Happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

felicity
FELICITY: श्रेयस् (n.),<BR>of you who have received<BR>every f.:<BR>श्रेयांसि सर्वाण्यधिजग्मुषस्ते, R. v. 34.: v.<BR>Happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feline
FELINE: i.e. pertaining to or like a cat: v.<BR>Cat, etc.<BR>The f. species:<BR>मार्जारजातिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fell
FELL (subs.):<BR>I A mountain: q.v.<BR>II Hide,<BR>skin: q.v.: चर्मन् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fell
FELL (adj.): निष्ठुरः (रा, रं): v. Cruel, fierce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fell
FELL (v.t.):<BR>(1) पातयति, अव-, नि-, (c. of पत्);<BR>(2) छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7.) (= to cut: q.v. as of<BR>timber).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fell-monger
FELL-MONGER: *चर्माजीवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fellness
FELLNESS: निष्ठुरता: v. Cruelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

felloe
FELLOE: of a wheel:<BR>(1) नेमिः;<BR>(2) प्रधिः;<BR>(3) नीध्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fellow
FELLOW: A companion: q.v.: सहायः।<BR>II<BR>A person: q.v.: जनः,<BR>this f. is very audaci-<BR>ous:<BR>अतिप्रगल्भोऽयं जनः।<BR>III A mate: सहचरः<BR>(f. री), Me. ii. 22.<BR>IV An equal: q.v.<BR>V<BR>Holder of a f.-ship: वृत्तिभुज् (mfn.).<BR>VI<BR>Of a society or corporation: सभ्यः।<BR>VII<BR>As a prefix: सह-<BR>or<BR>स- in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fellow-commoner
FELLOW-COMMONER: एकपाकभोजिन् (f. नी), Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fellow-creature
FELLOW-CREATURE:<BR>(1) सहजन्मन् (mfn.);<BR>(2)<BR>by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fellow-feeling
FELLOW-FEELING: सहानुभूतिः: v. Sympathy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fellow-passenger
FELLOW-PASSENGER: सहयात्रिन् (f. णी): v. F.<BR>traveller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fellowship
FELLOWSHIP:<BR>I Association: q.v.: सङ्गः।<BR>II<BR>Company: q.v.: सङ्गः।<BR>III Partnership as<BR>in pain: सहानुभूतिः।<BR>IV A band: दलम्।<BR>V<BR>Scholarship: वृत्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fellow-student
FELLOW-STUDENT:<BR>(1) सहाध्यायः,<BR>Nichula, f. of<BR>Kālidāsa:<BR>निचुलः कालिदासस्य सहाध्यायः, M.n.;<BR>(2)<BR>सहाध्यायिन् (f. नी), Mu. i.;<BR>(3) सतीर्थ (f. र्था)<BR>(rare), Ma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fellow-traveller
FELLOW-TRAVELLER:<BR>(1) सहगामिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>सहयात्रिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) सहप्रस्थायिन् (f. नी), K.s.<BR>i. 10. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

felly
FELLY:<BR>I Adv.: निष्ठुरम्: v. Cruelly.<BR>II<BR>Subs. v. Felloe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

felo-de-se
FELO-DE-SE:<BR>(1) आत्मघातिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) आत्महन्<BR>(mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

felon
FELON: आततायिन् (f. नी): v. Criminal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

felonious
FELONIOUS: By comp.,<BR>f. act:<BR>पापक्रिया: v.<BR>Criminal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

felony
FELONY: पापम्: v. Crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

felt
FELT (subs.): ऊर्णा,<BR>f. hat:<BR>*ऊर्णामयं शिरस्त्रम्: v.<BR>Wool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

female
FEMALE (subs.): स्त्री: v. Woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

female
FEMALE (adj.): Not male:<BR>(1) by a feminine<BR>termination आ<BR>or<BR>ई:<BR>f. preceptor:<BR>उपाध्याया;<BR>a f. monkey:<BR>वानरी;<BR>a f. dove:<BR>कपोतिका,;<BR>(2) by वधू affixed (denoting the f. of a<BR>couple),<BR>the f. Chakra:<BR>चक्रवाकवधूः, M.n.<BR>II<BR>Belonging to a woman: expr. by comp.:<BR>f. form:<BR>स्त्रीरूपम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feminine
FEMININE:<BR>I As opposed to manly: स्त्रैण (f.<BR>णी), hesitates from f. (consideration): स्त्रैणेन<BR> विचिकित्सति, Vi. i. 37.: v. Also effeminate.<BR>II In gram.: स्त्री,<BR>f. gender:<BR>स्त्रीलिङ्गम् (the<BR>word); इषुधि<BR>is also f.:<BR>इषुधिः स्त्री च, S.k.;<BR>the<BR>five words<BR>अप् etc. are f. and (used in the)<BR>plural:<BR>अबादीनां पञ्चानां स्रीत्वं बहुत्वं च, S.k.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fen
FEN:<BR>(1) अनूपः;<BR>(2) कच्छभूः: v. Marsh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fence
FENCE (subs.):<BR>I Enclosure: q.v.: वृतिः।<BR>II<BR>F. ing: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fence
FENCE (v.):<BR>I To defend: q.v.: रक्षति (रक्ष्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II To enclose: वृतिना आ-वृणोति, परि-,<BR>(वृ, c. 5.)<BR>or<BR>वेष्टयति, परि-, (वेष्ट्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fencer
FENCER:<BR>(1) असियोधः (with sword);<BR>(2)<BR>दण्डयोधः (with stick);<BR>(3) भ्कल्लः (= 2), Nil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fencing
FENCING (subs.):<BR>(1) असिचर्या (with sword),<BR>Mah.;<BR>(2) दण्डयुधम् (with stick);<BR>(3) गदायुद्धम्<BR>(= 2), Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fend
FEND: निवारयति (वृ, c. 10.): v. To prevent,<BR>ward off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fender
FENDER:<BR>I For coals of fire: *अङ्गारगुप्तिः।<BR>II<BR>Of a car:<BR>(1) वरूथः;<BR>(2) रथगुप्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fennel
FENNEL:<BR>(1) शतपुष्पा (a species of f.);<BR>(2)<BR>मिशी (another species).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fenny
FENNY:<BR>(1) अनूपः (पा, पं),<BR>f. land:<BR>अनूपभूमिः;<BR>(2) पङ्किलः (ला, लं) (= muddy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feoff
FEOFF (v.): ददाति (दा, c. 3.): v. To enfeoff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ferine
FERINE:<BR>(1) हिंस्रः (स्रा, स्रं);<BR>(2) वन्यः (न्या,<BR> न्यं) (= wild).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ferment
FERMENT (subs.)<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) किण्व (mn.);<BR>(2)<BR>मण्ड (mn.).<BR>II Heat, agitation: q.v.: क्षोभः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ferment
FERMENT (v.t.): क्षोभयति (c. of क्षुभ्): v. To<BR>agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ferment
FERMENT (v.i.):<BR>I To effervesce: q.v.:<BR>फेनायते (nomi.) (?).<BR>II To be agitated:<BR>क्षुभ्यति (क्षुभ्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fermentation
FERMENTATION:<BR>(1) सन्धानम् (?);<BR>(2) स्फूर्तिः (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fermentative
FERMENTATIVE:<BR>(1) स्फूर्तिकरः (री, रं) (?);<BR>(2)<BR>मण्डजननः (नी, नं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fern
FERN: लताजातिविशेषः; *पत्रप्रसूः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ferocious
FEROCIOUS:<BR>(1) रौद्रः (द्री, द्रं);<BR>(2) उग्रः (ग्रा,<BR> ग्रं): v. Dreadful, cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ferociously
FEROCIOUSLY:<BR>(1) दारुणम् (= dreadfully);<BR>(2)<BR>क्रूरम् (= cruelly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ferociousness
FEROCIOUSNESS, FEROCITY:<BR>(1) रौद्रता;<BR>(2)<BR>उग्रता;<BR>(3) क्रौर्यम् (=cruelty);<BR>(4) दारुणता<BR>(= dreadfulness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ferrule
FERRULE: लोहवलयः, Monier Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ferry
FERRY (v.):<BR>I Intran: तरति (तॄ, c. 1.).<BR>II<BR>Trans.: तारयति (c. of तॄ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ferry
FERRY (subs.): तरः,<BR>should employ confidential men<BR>in charge of mines, customs, and f.s:<BR>आकरशुल्क-<BR>तरेष्वाप्तान्नियुञ्जीत, V.s.;<BR>f. boat:<BR>तरनौः, तरणनौका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ferryman
FERRYMAN:<BR>(1) घट्टजीविन् (m.);<BR>(2) तरनायकः। (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fertile
FERTILE:<BR>I Fruitful: q.v.:<BR>(1) शस्यप्रदः (दा,<BR> दं);<BR>(2) उ(ऊ)र्वरा (of soil),<BR>f. land:<BR>उर्वरा भूमिः।<BR>II Fig., rich, inventive: निर्माणकुशलः (ला,<BR> लं) and sim. comp.s,<BR>he has f. mind:<BR>*तस्य<BR> निर्माणदक्षं मनः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fertileness
FERTILENESS, FERTILITY:<BR>I Fruitfulness:<BR>(1) फलवत्ता;<BR>(2) by adj.<BR>II Inventiveness:<BR>निर्माणदक्षता (?) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fertilize
FERTILIZE<BR>(1) फलवन्तं (तीं, त्) करोति;<BR>(2)<BR>फलदीकरोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fertilization
FERTILIZATION<BR>(1) expr. by verb;<BR>(2) फलदी-<BR>करणम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ferule
FERULE: दण्डकाष्ठम् (?); वेत्रम् (= cane).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fervency
FERVENCY:<BR>(1) औत्सुक्यम्;<BR>(2) उत्साहः: v. Zeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fervent
FERVENT:<BR>I Hot: q.v.<BR>II Eager, earnest:<BR>q.v.: उत्सुकः (का, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fervently
FERVENTLY: सोत्साहम्: v. Eagerly, zealously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fervid
FERVID:<BR>I Very hot: प्रचण्डः (ण्डा, ण्डं),<BR>when<BR>the sun is f.:<BR>प्रचण्डसूर्यः,<BR>f. heat:<BR>प्रचण्डतापः, Rit.<BR>II Vehement: q.v.: प्रचण्ड (f. ण्डा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fervour
FERVOUR:<BR>I Heat: q.v.: प्रचण्डता।<BR>II<BR>Ardour: प्रचण्डता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

festal
FESTAL: expr. by comp.,<BR>f. day:<BR>उत्सवदिनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fester
FESTER (v.):<BR>I Intrans.: v. To corrupt.<BR>II Trans.: v. To nurse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

festival
FESTIVAL:<BR>(1) उत्सवः,<BR>the great f. of the birth<BR>of the prince increased every moment:<BR>प्रतिक्षणमवर्धत<BR> राजसूनोर्जन्मनो महोत्सवः, K.;<BR>(2) अभ्युदयः (rare),<BR>even in f.s:<BR>अभ्युदयेष्वपि, M. ix. 84.;<BR>(3) महः<BR>or<BR>महस् (n.) (rare),<BR>the f. of cupid:<BR>मदनमहः, Ra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

festive
FESTIVE:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) पार्वणः (f. णी)<BR>(= relating to पर्व=holiday),<BR>the chief citi-<BR>zens take to desired f. work:<BR>भजन्ते विधिमभिलषितं<BR> पार्वणं पौरमुखयाः, Mu. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

festivity
FESTIVITY:<BR>I Festival: q.v.<BR>II Joy: q.v.:<BR>प्रमोदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

festoon
FESTOON:<BR>adorned with f.s:<BR>दामभिर्वरमाल्यानां प्रालम्बैः<BR> समलङ्कृतम्, Ram. ii. 12. 31.: v. Wreath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fetal
FETAL: expr. by comp.; v. Fetus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fetch
FETCH (v.):<BR>I To bring: q.v.: आहरति (हृ, c.<BR>1.),<BR>went to Kichaka's house to f. wine:<BR>प्रातिष्ठत<BR> सुराहारी कीचकस्य निवेशनम्, Mah. iii. 16. 17.<BR>II<BR>To sell for, expr. by लभते (लभ्, c. 1.),<BR>friend,<BR>what price will fourteen f.:<BR>चतुर्द श सखे मूल्यं लभन्ते<BR> कियत्, Li.<BR>III To arrive at: q.v.: प्राप्नोति<BR>(आप्, c. 5.).<BR>IV To fell: q.v.: पातयति। (c.<BR>of पत्). V. To make, do: q.v.: करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fetch
FETCH (subs.): छलम्: v. Trick, artifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fetcher
FETCHER:<BR>(1) आहर्तृ (f. त्री); सम्-;<BR>(2) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fete
FETE:<BR>I Subs.: पर्वन् (n.): v. Festival.<BR>II<BR>Verb, to feast: तर्पयति, सं-, (c. of तृप्),<BR>f.d<BR>the great Brahmins:<BR>तर्पयामास विप्रेन्द्रान्, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fetid
FETID (adj.):<BR>(1) दुर्गन्धः (न्धा, न्धं);<BR>(2) दुर्गन्धि<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(3) पूतिगन्धिः (mfn.);<BR>(4) पूति<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(5) उग्रगन्धि (mfn.) (= strong-smell-<BR>-ing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fetidness
FETIDNESS:<BR>(1) दुर्गन्ध(न्धि)ता;<BR>(2) पूतिगन्धिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fetish
FETISH, FETICH: भूतम् (?).<BR>F. ism:<BR>भूतभक्तिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fetor
FETOR:<BR>(1) पूतिगन्धः;<BR>(2) दुर्गन्धः: v. Fetid-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fetter
FETTER (subs.): शृङ्खलः, (-ला, -लं): v. Chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fetter
FETTER: (v.): निगडयति (nomi.): v. To en-<BR>-chain, confine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fetus
FETUS: गर्भः,<BR>dead f.:<BR>मूढगर्भः, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feud
FEUD:<BR>I Quarrel: q.v.: कलहम्,<BR>II An<BR>estate: कर्मणोपभोग्या भूमिः (?). *कर्मोत्तरभूमिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feudal
FEUDAL:<BR>the f. system:<BR>*कर्मोत्तरभूमिप्रणाली;<BR>f.<BR>rights<BR>*कर्मोत्तरभूम्यधिकाराः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feudatory
FEUDATORY:<BR>f. chiefs:<BR>कर्मकारिणो भूपालाः: v.<BR>Also tributary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fever
FEVER:<BR>I Lit. ज्वरः, acute (lit. new)<BR>f.:<BR>नव-<BR>ज्वरः; chronic (lit. old)<BR>f.:<BR>जीर्णज्वरः, Bha.;<BR>inflammatory f.:<BR>दाहज्वरः;<BR>cold f.:<BR>शीतज्वरः;<BR>typhoid f.:<BR>सन्निपातज्वरः (?); he will have f. again:<BR>अस्य पुनरेव भवेज्ज्वरः; Sr.;<BR>recovered from f.:<BR>जरो-<BR>त्सृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं), Sr,<BR>or<BR>ज्वरमुक्तः (क्ता, क्तं), Bha.<BR>II Fig.: ज्वरः,<BR>speak it without f.:<BR>तद्ब्रूत विगत-<BR>ज्वराः, Mat.: v. Excitement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feverish
FEVERISH:<BR>I Affected with fever:<BR>(1) ज्वरितः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(2) ज्वरिन् (f. णी);<BR>(3) जरार्त<BR>(f. र्ता);<BR>(4) ज्वरग्रस्त (f. स्ता); and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Indicating fever: expr. by ज्वरभावः।<BR>III Hot.: q.v.<BR>IV Fickle: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

feverishness
FEVERISHNESS:<BR>(1) ज्वरितता (=actual f.);<BR>(2)<BR>ज्वरभावः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

few
FEW:<BR>(1) अल्पः (ल्पा, ल्पं), in a very f. days:<BR>स्वल्पीयोभिरेव दिवसैः, C.;<BR>in f.:<BR>अल्पेन;<BR>(2) कतिपयः<BR>(या, यं)<BR>or<BR>कतिचित् (= a small number),<BR>a<BR>f. nights:<BR>कतिचित् शर्वरीः, R. xi. 93. v. Also<BR>some, small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fewness
FEWNESS: अल्पता: v. Also smallness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fiat
FIAT: शासनम्: v. Decree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fib
FIB (subs.):<BR>(1) अनृतम्;<BR>(2) असत्यम्;<BR>(3) अलीकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fibre
FIBRE:<BR>I Thread: q.v.: तन्तुः।<BR>II Of animals<BR>or plants: शिरा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fibril
FIBRIL: सूक्ष्मतन्तुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fibrous
FIBROUS:<BR>(1) तन्तुमयः (यी, यं) (?);<BR>(2) तन्तुघटितः<BR>(ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fickle
FICKLE:<BR>(1) चञ्चलः (ला, लं),<BR>fortune is f.:<BR>चञ्चलं<BR> वसु, Ki.;<BR>(2) चपलः (ला, लं);<BR>this Brahmin<BR>youth is f.:<BR>चपलोऽयं ब्राह्वणवटुः, Sa. ii.;<BR>(3) अस्थिरः<BR>(रा, रं) (= inconstant);<BR>(4) अनवस्थितः (ता,<BR> तं) (= 3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fickleness
FICKLENESS:<BR>(1) चञ्चलता;<BR>(2) चपलता;<BR>(3) अस्थि-<BR>रता;<BR>(4) चाञ्चल्यम्;<BR>(5) चापल्यम्<BR>(6) अस्थैर्यम्;<BR>(7)<BR>चलचित्तता (= f. of mind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fickly
FICKLY:<BR>(1) अस्थिरम्;<BR>(2) चापल्येन;<BR>(3) चञ्चलतया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fiction
FICTION: कल्पना, this is a f. of his own creation:<BR>तस्य मनःकल्पितमलीकमेतत्: v. Invention, untruth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fictitious
FICTITIOUS:<BR>(1) कृत्रिमः (मा, मं);<BR>(2) अलीकः।<BR>v. False;<BR>(3) काल्पनिकः (की, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fiddle
FIDDLE (subs.): शा(सा)रङ्गी। Ph.: to play the<BR>second f. to: perh. प्रतिध्वनिं करोति, K.; f. -stick:<BR>कोणः (gen. term), B. xiv. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fiddle
FIDDLE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: शारङ्गीं वादयति (c. of वद्).<BR>II To tweedle: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fiddle-faddle
FIDDLE-FADDLE: निरर्थककथा, यत्तत्<BR>or<BR>यत्किञ्चित्, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fiddler
FIDDLER:<BR>I Lit.: शारङ्गीवादः, -कः।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>यत्किञ्चनकारी, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fidelity
FIDELITY:<BR>I Loyalty: भक्तिः, with (your)<BR>f. to (your)<BR>preceptor:<BR>भत्तया गुरौ, R. ii. 63.<BR>Honesty, निष्कपटता।<BR>III Attachment:<BR>(1)<BR>आसक्तिः;<BR>(2) सङ्गः (rare), गणिकायाश्च गम्यं प्रति<BR> सज्जतैव न सङ्गः, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fidgety
FIDGETY: चपलः (ला, लं) (?): v. Restless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fiduciary
FIDUCIARY:<BR>I Adj.: expr. by विश्वासं समालम्ब्य,<BR>Mr.: v. Also confident, firm.<BR>II Subs.:<BR>v. Trustee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fie
FIE (interj.): धिक् (with acc.): v. Shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fief
FIEF: *कर्मोत्तरभूमिः; योधभूमिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

field
FIELD:<BR>I Agricultural:<BR>(1) क्षेत्रम्,<BR>the boundaries<BR>of a f.:<BR>क्षेत्रसीमा, M.;<BR>the owner of a f.:<BR>क्षेत्रस्वामी,<BR>K. b.;<BR>high f.:<BR>मालं क्षेत्रम्, Me.;<BR>good f.:<BR>सत्क्षेत्रम्,<BR>Mu. i. 3.<BR>(2) केदारः (rare).<BR>II Battle-f.:<BR>q.v. समरभूमिः,<BR>to leave the f.:<BR>समरभूमिं<BR>or<BR>समरं<BR> त्यजति, Ve.<BR>III Battle: q.v.: युद्धम्,<BR>they lost<BR>the f.:<BR>पराजिता बभूवुः।<BR>IV Scope, range: perh<BR>क्षेत्रम्,<BR>f. of knowledge.:<BR>झानक्षेत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

field-day
FIELD-DAY: सैन्यव्यायामदिनं<BR>or<BR>दिवसम् (after Ka.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

field-fare
FIELD-FARE: पक्षिभेदः; *क्षेत्रचारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

field-marshal
FIELD-MARSHAL: बलाध्यक्षः: v. General.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

field-mouse
FIELD-MOUSE: क्षेत्रमूषिकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

field-piece
FIELD-PIECE: *लधुकामानम्; युद्धयन्त्रविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

field-sport
FIELD-SPORT: मृगयाविहारः, M. n.: v. Hunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fiend
FIEND:<BR>(1) पिशाचः;<BR>(2) राक्षसः (= ghoul);<BR>(3)<BR>यातुधानः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fiendish
FIENDISH:<BR>(1) पैशाचः (ची, चं);<BR>(2) राक्षसः (सी,<BR> सं): v. Malignant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fierce
FIERCE:<BR>(1) घोरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) क्रूरः (रा, रं)<BR>(= cruel, savage),<BR>his face became f. with<BR>frowns:<BR>क्रूरमजनि कुटिलभ्रू तस्याननम्, Si. xv. 8.;<BR>(3)<BR>दारुणः (णा, णं), नि- (= terrible), of f. form:<BR>दारुणाकृतिः, Mah. i. 150. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fiercely
FIERCELY:<BR>(1) घोरम्;<BR>(2) क्रूरम्;<BR>(3) दारुणम्, नि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fierceness
FIERCENESS:<BR>(1) घोरता;<BR>(2) क्रूरता;<BR>(3) दारुणता,<BR> नि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fieriness
FIERINESS:<BR>(1) तेजस्विता;<BR>(2) चण्डता, प्र- (of<BR>temper).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fiery
FIERY:<BR>I Lit.: आग्नेयः (यी, यं).<BR>II Full of<BR>heat: तेजस्विन् (f. नी) (lit. and fig.: applied<BR>to a f. horse, K.), among f. (things): तेजस्वि-<BR>मध्ये, Si. ii. 52.<BR>III Vehement, passionate:<BR>चण्ड (f. ण्डा), प्र-,<BR>f. (and) collected wrath:<BR>प्रचण्ड-<BR>परिपिण्डितो मन्युः, Vi. v. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fiery-footed
FIERY-FOOTED:<BR>(1) अनिलोपमः (मा, मं), Mah.;<BR>(2) वातरंहस् (mfn.) and sim. comp.s, Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fife
FIFE: वेणुः: v. Flute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fifer
FIFER:<BR>(1) वेणुध्मः;<BR>(2) वेणुवादः, -कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fifteen
FIFTEEN: पञ्चदशन् (mfn.)<BR>F. -th:<BR>पञ्चदशः (शी, शं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fifth
FIFTH:<BR>I Adj.: पञ्चमः (मी, मं), in the f. place:<BR>पञ्चमतः।<BR>II Subs.:<BR>(1) पञ्चभागः; पञ्चांशः or<BR>पञ्चलवः;<BR>(2) पञ्चमांशः<BR>or<BR>पञ्चमभागः। The f. note (in<BR>music): मध्यमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fifthly
FIFTHLY:<BR>(1) पञ्चमतः;<BR>(2) पञ्चभम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fiftieth
FIFTIETH:<BR>(1) पञ्चाशत्तम; (मी, मं);<BR>(2) पञ्चाशः<BR>(शी, शं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fifty
FIFTY: पञ्चाशत् (f.)<BR>Hundred and f.:<BR>सार्द्धशतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fig
FIG:<BR>I The tree:<BR>(1) अञ्जीरः (ficus carica);<BR>(2) उडुम्बरः (ficus glomirata);<BR>(3) न्यग्रोधः<BR>or<BR>वटः (f. Indica);<BR>(4) अश्वत्थः<BR>or<BR>पिप्पलः<BR>(f. religiosa);<BR>(5) प्लक्षः<BR>or<BR>पर्कटी (f. Infectiosa).<BR>II The fruit: अञ्चीरम् (the common f.);<BR>उडुम्बरम्, न्यैयग्रोधम्, आश्वत्थम्, प्लाक्षम् of the other<BR>species named. Ph.:<BR>not to care a f. for<BR>anything:<BR>न तृणाय मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fight
FIGHT (v.i.):<BR>(1) युध्यते, नि- (युध्, c. 4.),<BR>where women could f.:<BR>स्त्रियोऽपियत्र युध्येयुः, V.p.;<BR>with whom you are eager to f.:<BR>केन ते योद्धमुत्सहते<BR> मनः, Mah. ii. 23. 2.;<BR>(2) योधयति (c. of युध्)<BR>(= to f. with),<BR>Indra went out to f. with<BR>Kṛṣṇa for the sake of the Pārijāta:<BR>प्रययौ पारि-<BR>जातार्थमिन्द्रो योधयितुं हरिम्, V. p.;<BR>(3) युद्धं करोति,<BR> कुरुते,<BR>I wish to f. a duel with Arjuna:<BR>अहं पार्थेन<BR> द्वन्द्वयुद्धं कर्तुमिच्छामि, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fight
FIGHT (v.t.):<BR>I Lit.: योधयति।<BR>II Fig., to<BR>carry on:<BR>to f. one's way:<BR>पथं मोचयति (मुच्, c.<BR>10.);<BR>to f. a cause:<BR>कार्यार्थं वदति (वद्, c. 1.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fight
FIGHT, FIGHTING: (subs.):<BR>(1) युद्धम्,<BR>who did<BR>not wish f. with him:<BR>योऽनेन युद्धं नेयेष, Mah.;<BR>(2) रणम् (prop.=battle), I defy you, come to f.:<BR>आह्वये त्वां रणं गच्छ, Mah. ii. 45. 2.;<BR>(3) नियुद्धम्<BR>(= close f., foot-f.),<BR>very strong on elephant, on<BR>horse-back, and in foot-f.:<BR>गजपृष्ठेऽश्वपृष्ठे च नियुद्धे<BR> च महाबलाः, Mah. i. 132. 29.;<BR>(4) आयोधनम्<BR>(rare),<BR>if both fall in the f.:<BR>आयोघेने चेदुमयो-<BR>र्निघातः, Vi. ii. 12.;<BR>(5) युध् (f.) (rare), Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fighter
FIGHTER:<BR>(1) योद्धृ (m.);<BR>(2) योधिन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

figment
FIGMENT: कल्पना: v. Fiction, invention, un-<BR>-truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

figurate
FIGURATE:<BR>I Lit.: आकारवत् (f. ती).<BR>II Dis-<BR>-cordant: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

figurative
FIGURATIVE:<BR>(1) गौण (f. णी) (= not literal);<BR>(2) सालङ्कारः (रा, रं) (= flowery);<BR>(3) लाक्षणिकः<BR>(की, कं) (= significant);<BR>(4) व्यञ्जकः (का, कं)<BR>=indicatory); for dif. v. Kav. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

figuratively
FIGURATIVELY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

figure
FIGURE (subs.):<BR>I Form: q.v.: मूर्तिः।<BR>II<BR>An image: q.v.: मूर्तिः।<BR>III A design: मूर्तिः।<BR>IV A numeral: अङ्कः।<BR>V Price: मूल्यम्।<BR>VI<BR>A f. of speech: अलङ्कारः।<BR>VII In dancing:<BR>प्रचारः, undulating f.: (?) गोमूत्रिकाप्रचारः, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

figure
FIGURE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: v. To form.<BR>II To<BR>depict: q.v.: रूपयति (रूप्, c. 10.).<BR>III To<BR>calculate: q.v.: गणयति (गण्, c. 10.).<BR>IV<BR>To indicate: q.v.: सूचयति (सूच्, c. 10.).<BR>V To image: कल्पयति (कॢप्, c. 10.). F.d.:<BR>i.e. adorned with f. s: चित्रः (त्रा, त्रं). F. out:<BR>गणयति।<BR>F. up:<BR>संकलयति (कल्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>add.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filaceous
FILACEOUS:<BR>(1) सत्रमयः (यी, यं);<BR>(2) तन्तुमयः<BR>(यी, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filament
FILAMENT:<BR>(1) केश(स)रः;<BR>(2) किञ्जलकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filbert
FILBERT: फलविशेषः; *कुच्चफलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filch
FILCH: मुष्णाति (मुष्, c. 9.): v. To steal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filcher
FILCHER: मोषकः: v. Thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filchingly
FILCHINGLY;<BR>(1) मोषेण;<BR>(2) चौरिकया;<BR>(3)<BR>चौर्येण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

file
FILE (subs.)<BR>I Of soldiers: perh. दण्डपंक्तिः।<BR>II An orderly collection: perh. समष्टिः।<BR>III A line or wire on which letters are [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">Page277</a>]<BR>kept: perh. गुणः<BR>IV A list: perh. नामावलिः।<BR>V. A steel instrument: perh. रेत्री (comp.<BR>vern. रेति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

file
FILE (v.i.): दण्डव्यूहेन याति (या, c. 2.)<BR>or<BR>यात्रां<BR> करोति, M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

file
FILE (v.t.):<BR>I To smooth: q.v.<BR>II To<BR>arrange: *गुणीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filial
FILIAL: expr. by comp.,<BR>f. duty:<BR>पुत्रधर्मः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filially
FILIALLY:<BR>(1) पुत्रवत्;<BR>(2) पुत्रैति and sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filiation
FILIATION:<BR>I Lit.: पुत्रत्वम्।<BR>II Af-f.: जनक-<BR>त्वारोपणम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filigree
FILIGREE: *जालकर्मन्,<BR>f. busket:<BR>जालकर्मपेटिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filing
FILING: चूर्णम् (= powder),<BR>iron-f.<BR>लौहचूर्णम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fill
FILL (v.t.);<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पूरयति, प्र-, परि-, सं-,<BR> आ-, प्रति-, (पूर्, c. 10.),<BR>f. -ing the pot with<BR>water:<BR>वारिणा कमण्डलुमापूर्य, K.;<BR>(2) बिभर्ति (भृ,<BR>c. 1.) (rare), I (will) f. my prison with them:<BR>तैर्भिभर्मि स्वकाराम्, Vi.<BR>II To cause to abound:<BR>पूरयति, प्र-, परि-, सं-, being f. ed with ascetics:<BR>पूर्यमाणं तपस्विभिः, R. i. 49.<BR>III To satisfy;<BR>q.v.: पूरयति।<BR>IV Of office etc.: perh.<BR>पूरयति,<BR>to f. the throne:<BR>सिंहासनस्य प्रतिपूरणाय,<BR>R. xviii. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fill
FILL (v.i.): पूर्यते, प्र-, परि-, सं-, आ-, प्रति-, (pass.<BR>of पूर्),<BR>the begging pot f. ed with fruits dropped<BR>naturally:<BR>स्वयंपतितैः फलैरपूर्यत भिक्षाभाजनम्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fill in
FILL IN: पूरयति (with loc.): v. To fill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fill up
FILL UP:<BR>I Trans: परि-पूरयति, सं-, आ-,<BR>is the<BR>earth f. ed up in the uneven parts:<BR>पूरिता नु विषमेषु<BR> धरित्री, Ki. ix. 15.; one who f. s up a ditch:<BR>परिखापूरकः, M.<BR>II Intrans: परि-पूर्यते, सं-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fill
FILL (subs.): gen. in pl. ‘my f.’, ‘your f.’ best<BR>expr. by यथेच्छम्, U.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filler
FILLER:<BR>(1) पूरक (f. रिका), परि-, सं-;<BR>(2) पूरयितृ<BR>(f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fillet
FILLET (subs.):<BR>I A band: पट्टः।<BR>II Of meat:<BR>खण्डः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fillet
FILLET (v.): पट्टेन बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.); v. To<BR>bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filling
FILLING (subs.):<BR>I The act; पूरणम्।<BR>II That<BR>which fills: perh. पूरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fillip
FILLIP:<BR>I Verb: perh. स्फोटयति (c. of स्फुट्).<BR>II Subs. perh. स्फोटनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

film
FILM:<BR>I A covering: पटलम्।<BR>II A slender<BR>thread: सूक्ष्मतन्तुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filmy
FILMY: सूक्ष्मतन्तुघटितः (ता, तं), V. d. and sim.<BR>comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filter
FILTER (subs.): *पावकी,<BR>carbon f.:<BR>*अङ्गारपावकी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filter
FILTER (v.t.): पुनाति (पू, c. 9.): v. To purify,<BR>clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filth
FILTH (subs.): मलम् (lit. and fig.): v. Dirt, foul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filthily
FILTHILY: सममल: v. Dirtily, foully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filthiness
FILTHINESS: समलता: v. Dirtiness, foulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filthy
FILTHY: समलः (ला, लं): v. Dirty, foul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filtrate
FILTRATE, FILTRATED:<BR>(1) पूतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2)<BR>शोधितः (ता, तं), वि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

filtration
FILTRATION:<BR>(1) पावनम्;<BR>(2) शोधनम्, वि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fin
FIN: perh. हिल्लः (comp. Bengali इल्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finable
FINABLE: अर्थदण्डार्ह (f. र्हा) or (when the sense<BR>is clear) दण्डार्ह (f. र्हा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

final
FINAL:<BR>(1) परमः (मा, मं);<BR>(2) अन्तिमः (मा,<BR> मं);<BR>(3) अन्त्य (f. न्त्या);<BR>(4) पश्चिमः (मा, मं),<BR>remembering the f. order:<BR>स्मरन्तः पश्चिमामाझाम्,<BR>R. xvii. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finally
FINALLY: चरमम्: v. Lastly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finality
FINALITY:<BR>I Lastness: चरमता।<BR>II Conclu-<BR>-siveness: अखण्ड्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finance
FINANCE: आयः, your f. s superintended by loyal<BR>(men): आयस्तव भक्तैरनु(धि ?)ष्ठितः, Mah. ii. 5. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

financial
FINANCIAL: आयव्ययसम्बन्धिन् (f. नी). Ph.:<BR>to<BR>improve the f. condition:<BR>कोषवृद्धिं करोति, Nil.;<BR>his<BR>f. condition is bad:<BR>न स्फीतस्तस्यायः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

financier
FINANCIER:<BR>I An officer: आयव्ययाध्यक्षः;<BR> अर्थनायकः (?).<BR>II One skilled in finance:<BR>आयव्ययकुशलः; अर्थविद्याविशारदः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finch
FINCH: सुस्वरः पक्षिविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

find
FIND:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) उपलभते (लभ्, c. 1.),<BR>after careful search did not f. him:<BR>निपुणमन्विष्य<BR> नोपलब्धवान्, D. ii.;<BR>(2) प्राप्नोति (आप्, c. 5.)<BR>(= to get: q.v.),<BR>whoever is found there at<BR>night with other woman:<BR>यो नरः प्राप्यते तत्र रात्रौ<BR> सह परस्त्रिया, K. s.<BR>II To furnish:<BR>(1) ददाति<BR>(दा, c. 3.) (= to give: q.v.);<BR>(2) योजयति<BR> प्र-, नि-, (युज्, c. 10.) (= to cause to join),<BR>Ku. iv. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

find out
FIND OUT:<BR>I Lit.: उपलभते: v. To find.<BR>II [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">Page278</a>]<BR>To discover: जानाति (ज्ञा, c. 9. =to know:<BR>q.v.),<BR>f. out the cause of his anxiety:<BR>जानीहि<BR> तस्योत्कण्ठाकारणम्, V. ii.<BR>III To solve: expr.<BR>by वदति (वद्, c. 1.), ब्रवीति (ब्रू, c. 2.), etc.<BR>(= to say), f. out. the amount of their money:<BR>तयोर्वद धने मम किंप्रमाणे, Vij.;<BR>f. out how many<BR>pearls this necklace is made of:<BR>कथय कतिपयैर्मौक्ति-<BR>कैरेष हारः, Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finder
FINDER:<BR>(1) उपलब्धृ (f. ब्ध्री);<BR>(2) आसादयितृ (f.<BR>त्री);<BR>(3) better by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finding
FINDING (subs.): in law:<BR>(1) निर्णयः;<BR>(2)<BR>perh. उपलम्भः (ब्धिः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fine
FINE (adj.):<BR>I Not coarse or heavy: सूक्ष्म<BR>(f. क्ष्मा),<BR>coarse and f.:<BR>स्थूलः सूक्ष्मः, Ku. ii. 11.;<BR>f. thread:<BR>सूक्ष्मतन्तुः V. d.;<BR>of f. intellect:<BR>सूक्ष्मबुद्धि<BR>(mfn.) M. n.<BR>II Excellent, good: q. v.<BR>(1)<BR>उत्कृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>(2) सु- in comp.,<BR>having f.<BR>teeth:<BR>सुदत् (f. ती), N.<BR>III Beautiful, ele-<BR>-gant: शोभनः (ना, नं),<BR>f. language:<BR>शोभनोक्तिः;<BR>oh. f. lady:<BR>शोभने, Mah.<BR>IV Artful: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fine
FINE (subs.): अर्थदण्डः or sim. दण्डः (when the<BR>sense is clear),<BR>unable to pay the f.:<BR>दण्डं दातुम-<BR>शक्नु वन्, M.; is liable to a fine of 100 (panas):<BR>शतं दण्डमर्हति, M.;<BR>is to be punished with a f. of<BR>fifty panas:<BR>पञ्चाशत् पणान् दण्डयः, K. b.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fine
FINE (v.t.):<BR>I To refine: q.v.<BR>II To<BR>decorate: q.v.<BR>III To impose a f.:<BR>(1)<BR>अर्थदण्डं करोति;<BR>(2) दण्डयति (दण्ड्, c. 10.) (= to<BR>punish when the sense is clear);<BR>(3) दण्डं<BR>or<BR>दमं दापयति (c. of दा=to cause to give),<BR>should f. him double:<BR>तं दापयेद् द्विगुणं दमम्, Y. iii.<BR>309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fine-draw
FINE-DRAW: सूक्ष्मं सीव्यति (सिव्, c. 4.): v.<BR>To sew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fine-fingered
FINE-FINGERED: सूक्ष्मकर्मनिपुण (f. णा); लघुहस्त<BR>(f. स्ता) (dexterous: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finely
FINELY:<BR>I Minutely: सूक्ष्मम्।<BR>II Elegantly:<BR>शोभनम्; better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fineness
FINENESS:<BR>(1) सूक्ष्मता (= minuteness, delicacy);<BR>(2) उत्कृष्टता (= excellence);<BR>(3) शोभा<BR>(= beauty);<BR>(4) निर्मलता (=clearness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finery
FINERY: अलङ्कारः: v. Decoration, ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finesse
FINESSE: छलम्: v. Artifice, stratagem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finger
FINGER (subs.): अङ्गुलिः (ली),<BR>the fore f.:<BR>तर्जनी;<BR>the<BR>middle f.:<BR>मध्यमा;<BR>a ring for the middle f.:<BR>मध्यमो-<BR>पलः; Ki. ix. 2.;<BR>the third or ring f.:<BR>अनामिका;<BR>the little f.:<BR>कनिष्ठा। Measuring two f. s in breadth:<BR>द्व्यङ्गुलः (ला, लं). To snap or crack the f. s:<BR>अङ्गुलिस्फोटनं<BR>or<BR>-मोटनं करोति, M.<BR>Five-f. ed<BR>wood:<BR>पञ्चाङ्गुलं दारु, S. k.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finger
FINGER (v.t.):<BR>I Lit.: अङ्गुल्या स्पृशति (स्पृश्, c.<BR>1.).<BR>II To pilfer: perh. अङ्गुलिं चालयति (c.<BR>of चल्) (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finger-glass
FINGER-GLASS: *अङ्गुलिधावनपात्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finger-post
FINGER-POST: v. Signpost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finical
FINICAL: एकान्तसूक्ष्म (f. क्ष्मा) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fining
FINING (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: v. To fine.<BR>II<BR>Clarification: q.v.: पावनम्।<BR>III That which<BR>refines: पावनद्रव्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finish
FINISH (v.t.):<BR>I To put an end to: समापयति<BR>(c. of आप्), and f. (your)<BR>axe:<BR>समापयतु परशुं<BR> च, Vi. iii.: v. End.<BR>II To complete:<BR>q.v.: समापयति,<BR>f. ing the work proper for morn-<BR>ing:<BR>प्रातःकालोचितमनुष्ठानं समाप्य, M. n.<BR>III To<BR>polish: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finish
FINISH (subs.):<BR>(1) समाप्तिः;<BR>(2) अन्तः (= end:<BR>q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finisher
FINISHER:<BR>(1) समापक (f. पिका);<BR>(2) समापयितृ<BR>(f. त्री);<BR>(3) अन्तकः (= ender).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finite
FINITE:<BR>(1) परिच्छेद्य (f. द्या);<BR>(2) प्रमेयः (या,<BR> यं) (-measurable);<BR>(3) निरूपणीयः (या, यं)<BR>(what can be ascertained).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finiteness
FINITENESS:<BR>(1) परिच्छेद्यता;<BR>(2) प्रमेयता (=<BR>measurableness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finless
FINLESS: हिल्लहीनः (ना, नं) (?) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

finnikin
FINNIKIN: पारावतविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fir
FIR: वृक्षविशेषः; देवदारुः, Monier Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire
FIRE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अग्निः,<BR>who threw f.<BR>on our fort:<BR>केनास्मद्दुर्गे निक्षिप्तोऽग्निः, H.;<BR>to throw<BR>oneself into f.:<BR>अग्निं विशति (विश्, c. 6.),;<BR>(2)<BR>वह्निः,<BR>the f. spread according to the turning<BR>of the wind:<BR>ततान वह्निः पवनानुवृत्त्या, Ki. xvi. 52;<BR>(3) अनलः,<BR>burning f.:<BR>ज्वलितानलः, Si.; forest f.:<BR>दावानलः, Ki.<BR>(4) ज्वलनः,<BR>the weapon of f.:<BR>ज्वलन-<BR>स्यास्त्रम्, Ki.;<BR>(5) पावकः,<BR>a good f.<BR>सुसन्दीप्तः पावकः,<BR>P.;<BR>(6) दहनः।<BR>II Fig.: तेजस् (n.), that is [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">Page279</a>]<BR>ever-rising f. (of horses): तत्तेजःसततोत्थितम्, M. n.<BR>III Of fire-arms: अग्निः: v. (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire
FIRE (v.t.):<BR>I To set on f.: q.v.<BR>II To<BR>inflame, animate: q.v.: उत्तेजयति (तिज्, c.<BR>10.).<BR>III To f. up.: दीपयति (c. of दीप्):<BR>v. Light (I).<BR>IV To discharge, as a gun:<BR>मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire
FIRE (v.i.):<BR>I To kindle: q.v.: दीप्यते (दीप्,<BR>c. 4.).<BR>II Of f. arms: आग्नेयास्त्रं मुञ्चति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire
FIRE, ON:<BR>(1) अग्निपरीतः (ता, तं), and sim.<BR>comp.s.,<BR>the inner apartment of the princess as<BR>if on f.:<BR>राजकन्यान्तःपुरमग्निपरीतमिव, D. i.;<BR>(2)<BR>अग्निनाभिभूतः (ता, तं) and sim., comp.s., Ku.<BR>xvii. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire
FIRE, TO SET ON:<BR>(1) दाहयति (c. of दह्) (=<BR>cause to burn),<BR>set the house on f.:<BR>दाहितं गृहम्,<BR>Mu. ii.;<BR>(2) दीपयति, आ-, (c. of दीप्) (= to<BR>light: q.v.) Ram.;<BR>(3) by circumlo,<BR>set the<BR>house of Rāvaṇa on f.:<BR>ज्वलदग्नि रावणगृहं कृतवान्,<BR>B. x. 2.;<BR>(4) अग्निं मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.), विसृजति<BR>(सृज्, c. 6.) (= to put f.),<BR>and setting the<BR>houses of Rākṣasas on f.:<BR>विसृज्य रक्षोभवनेषु<BR> चाग्निम्, Ram. v. 50. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire
FIRE, TO TAKE:<BR>(1) अग्निं प्राप्नोति (आप्, c. 5.),<BR>वह्निं समागच्छति (गम्, c. 1.), etc., P. x. 11.;<BR>(2) ज्वलति (ज्वल्, c. 1.) (= to burn: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire-arm
FIRE-ARM: आग्नेयास्त्रम् (?); आग्न्यस्त्रम् (?); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire-ball
FIRE-BALL:<BR>I Lit: अग्निगोलः (?).<BR>II Heavenly:<BR>उल्का।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire-brand
FIRE-BRAND:<BR>I Lit.: ज्वलदलातम्; उल्का; उल्मुकम्,<BR>Mah.<BR>II Fig: अग्निदः (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire-engine
FIRE-ENGINE: *अग्निनिर्वापणयन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire-escape
FIRE-ESCAPE: *अग्नित्राणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire fly
FIRE FLY: प्रभाकीटः: v. Glow-worm<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire-guard
FIRE-GUARD: *अग्न्यावरणम्; अग्निनिरोधः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire-man
FIRE-MAN:<BR>I Of an engine: *अग्निदर्शकः।<BR>II<BR>To extinguish fire: अग्निनिर्वापकः (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire-pan
FIRE-PAN:<BR>(1) अग्न्याधारः;<BR>(2) अङ्गारधानिका;<BR>(3)<BR>अङ्गारिणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fireplace
FIREPLACE: अग्निस्थानम् (?) (not चुल्ली=cooking<BR>place).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fireproof
FIREPROOF: अनग्निधृष्य (f. ष्या) (?): v. In-<BR>-combustible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire-ship
FIRE-SHIP: *अग्निपोतः; शत्रुपोतेषु वह्निसंयोजनगपोतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire-side
FIRE-SIDE: expr. by अग्निः<BR>or<BR>गृहम् (= house)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire-stone
FIRE-STONE: अग्न्युपलः (?); आग्नेयाश्मन् (m.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire-ward
FIRE-WARD,-EN: *अग्निनिर्वापकाध्यक्षः, and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

firewood
FIREWOOD: इन्धनम्: v. Fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fireworks
FIREWORKS:<BR>I The play:<BR>(1) अग्निक्रीडा;<BR>(2)<BR>वह्निक्रीडनम्, Raj.: and sim. comp. s<BR>II The<BR>preparations: *अग्निक्रीडनद्रव्याणि (n. pl.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fire-worship
FIRE-WORSHIP: अग्न्युपासना, San. F. -er:<BR>(1)<BR>अग्न्युपासकः (का, कं);<BR>(2) अग्निदेवः (वा, वं);<BR>(3)<BR>अग्निमतानुवर्तिन् (f. नी), San.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

firing
FIRING:<BR>I The act.: आग्नेयास्त्रमोचनम् (?).<BR>II<BR>Application of fire: अग्निप्रयोगः।<BR>III Fuel:<BR>q.v.: दाह्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

firkin
FIRKIN: मानविशेषः; द्रोणार्द्धम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

firm
FIRM: (adj.):<BR>(1) दृढः (डा, डं),<BR>made a bridge f.<BR>er than the friendship of Sugriva:<BR>सुग्रीवसख्यादपि<BR> दृढं सेतुमकरोत्।, Ma. n. vi. 30.;<BR>seeing the attack<BR>was very f.:<BR>दृढतरमभियोगं वीक्ष्य, Vi. vi. 27;<BR>to<BR>make it more f.:<BR>दृढतरीकर्तुम्, D. iii.;<BR>(2) स्थिरः<BR>(रा, रं) (= constant: q.v.),<BR>f. -minded:<BR>स्थिरधीः,<BR>R. viii. 88.;<BR>of f. instruction^1:<BR>स्थिरोपदेशः (शा,<BR> शं), Ku. i. 30.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

firm
FIRM (v.): v. To confirm, firm (adj.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

firm
FIRM (subs.): समवायः (?).: v. Also partnership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

firmament
FIRMAMENT: नभस्तलम्: v. Sky, heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

firmamental
FIRMAMENTAL:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) आकाशीयः<BR>(या, यं);<BR>(3) वैहायसः (सी, सं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

firmly
FIRMLY:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) दृढम्;<BR>(3) स्थिरम्<BR>(= constantly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

firmness
FIRMNESS:<BR>(1) दृढता;<BR>(2) दार्ढ्यम्;<BR>(3) द्रढिमन्<BR>(m.);<BR>(4) स्थैर्यं<BR>or<BR>स्थिरता (= constancy);<BR>(5)<BR>संहतिः (= compactness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

first
FIRST (adj.):<BR>(1) प्रथमः (मा, मं) (of time, place,<BR>or rank),<BR>on the f. day. of Aṣāḍha:<BR>आषढस्य<BR> प्रथमदिवसे, Me. i. 1.;<BR>in the f. court:<BR>प्रथमे प्रकोष्ठे,<BR>Mr. iv.; f. of those, who share in sacrifices:<BR>मखांशभाजां प्रथमः, R. iii. 44.: v. Also chief;<BR>(2) आदि- in comp. or आद्यः (द्या, द्यं)<BR>or<BR>आदिमः<BR>(मा, मं) (= the beginning),<BR>the f. poet:<BR>आदिकविः;<BR>on the f. day of separation:<BR>आद्ये विरहदिवसे, Me.<BR>ii. 31.;<BR>(3) पूर्व-, in comp. (when there is [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">Page280</a>]<BR>comparison),<BR>the f. half:<BR>पूर्वार्द्धम्, R.;<BR>the f.<BR>part of the day:<BR>पूर्वाह्णः;<BR>(4) अग्य्रः (ग्य्रा, ग्य्रं) or<BR>अग्रिमः (मा, मं)<BR>or<BR>अग्रणी (n. णी) (= foremost),<BR>you are the f. to eat:<BR>भोक्तुं भवानग्रणीः, Ma. n.<BR>ix. 86. Ph.: for the f. time:<BR>(1) तत्प्रथमम्, Si<BR>xv. 42.;<BR>(2) तत्पूर्वम्, Ki. vii. 11.;<BR>the f. of<BR>archers:<BR>चापभृतां पुरोगः, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

first
FIRST (adv.):<BR>(1) प्रथमम्,<BR>f. of all, this is itself<BR>a great wonder:<BR>प्रथमं तावदिदमेव महदाश्चर्यम्, K.;<BR>(2) पूर्वंम्,<BR>f. of all, I am a fool:<BR>पूर्वं तावदहं मूर्खः, P.<BR>iii. 13;<BR>the king f. reflected in this way;<BR>इत्थं नृपः<BR> पूर्वमवालुलोचे, B. i. 23.;<BR>(3) प्राक्, f. (took her)<BR>to the king of Magadha:<BR>प्राक् सन्निकर्षं मगधेश्वरस्य,<BR>R. vi. 20.;<BR>(4) पुरा,<BR>f. ascertained to be an<BR>assemblage of light:<BR>चयस्त्विषामित्यवधारितं पुरा, Si.<BR>i. 3.;<BR>(5) आदौ (= in the beginning),<BR>at f.<BR>Jivasiddhi was banished from the city:<BR>आदावेव-<BR>जीवसिद्धिर्नगरान्निर्वासितः, Mu. ii.;<BR>(6) अग्रे (=<BR>before anything else), D. vi. N.B.<BR>(3) and<BR>(4) with ref. to time only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

first-begotten
FIRST-BEGOTTEN, FIRST-BORN (adj.):<BR>(1) अग्रजः<BR>(जा, जं);<BR>(2) अग्रजन्मन् (mfn.);<BR>(3) पूर्वंजः<BR>(जा, जं);<BR>(4) पूर्वप्रसूतः, (ता, तं) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

first-fruit
FIRST-FRUIT: प्रथमफलानि (n. pl.) (?) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

firstling
FIRSTLING: expr. by adj.: v. First-begotten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

firstly
FIRSTLY:<BR>(1) प्रथमतः;<BR>(2) प्रथमम्;<BR>(3) पूर्वम्;<BR>(4)<BR>आदौ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fisc
FISC: v. Treasury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fiscal
FISCAL: कोषः in comp.<BR>or<BR>कोषस्य (gen): v.<BR>Also financial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fish
FISH (subs.):<BR>(1) मत्स्यः,<BR>caught f. es with<BR>various traps:<BR>बबन्धुर्विविधैर्योगैर्मत्स्यान्, Mah.:<BR>f. es<BR>with one bone:<BR>एककण्टका मत्स्याः, Ram.;<BR>(2)<BR>मीनः,<BR>raw-f.-eaters:<BR>आममीनाशनाः, Ram.;<BR>(3)<BR>भ्कषः (rare). F. basket.<BR>(1) मत्स्यधानी;<BR>(2)<BR>कुवेणी;<BR>(3) मत्स्यकरण्डिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fish
FISH (v.):<BR>I Lit.: मत्स्यान् बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.)<BR>or<BR>गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.)<BR>or<BR>धारयति (धृ, c. 10.).<BR>II<BR>Fig.: v. To search.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fish-bone
FISH-BONE:<BR>(1) कण्टक (nm.) (= small f.);<BR>(2)<BR>अस्थि (n.) (= large bone).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fisher
FISHER, FISHERMAN:<BR>(1) धीवरः;<BR>(2) कैवर्तः;<BR>(3) जालु(लि)कः<BR>(4) मात्स्यिकः;<BR>(5) आनायी, R.<BR>xvi. 55.;<BR>(6) मत्स्यबन्धः, मत्स्योपजीविन् (m.), etc.<BR>Mah;<BR>(7) दासः। N.B.<BR>(2) and<BR>(7) are f.-<BR>castes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fishery
FISHERY:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) मत्स्यबन्धनम्;<BR>(2)<BR>मत्स्यधारणम्।<BR>II The place: prob. मत्स्यबन्धः;<BR> मत्स्यस्थानम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fishful
FISHFUL: प्रभूतमत्स्य (f. त्स्या), Mah.; and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fish-hook
FISH-HOOK<BR>(1) वडिशम्;<BR>(2) मत्स्यवेधनम्, -नी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fish-tying-rope
FISH-TYING-ROPE:<BR>(1) उद्यानम्, Mah. s. 137.<BR>115.;<BR>(2) ग्रथनसूत्रम्, Nil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fishing
FISHING:<BR>(1) मत्स्यधारणम्, Tārānāth;<BR>(2) मत्स्य-<BR>बन्धनम्, Sa. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fishing-boat
FISHING-BOAT: जालिकनौः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fishing-frog
FISHING-FROG: मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fishing line
FISHING LINE: वडिशसूत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fishing-net
FISHING-NET:<BR>(1) जालः;<BR>(2) आनायः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fishing-tackle
FISHING-TACKLE: मत्स्यबन्धनोपकरणम् (gen. term).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fishmonger
FISHMONGER:<BR>(1) मत्स्यविक्रेतृ (m.);<BR>(2) मत्स्य-<BR>विक्रयिन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fishy
FISHY:<BR>I Fishful: q.v.<BR>II Extravagant:<BR>prob. जालिक- in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fissure
FISSURE:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) छिद्रम्;<BR>(2) रन्ध्रम्।<BR>II<BR>Verb: v. To divide, leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fist
FIST: मुष्टिः।<BR>struck back with the f.:<BR>मुष्टिभिः प्रति-<BR>जघान, Ki. xviii. l.;<BR>a blow with the f.:<BR>मुष्टिघातः,<BR>M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fisticuffs
FISTICUFFS: मुष्टीमुष्टिप्रहरणम्, Vi.; मुष्टियुद्धम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fistula
FISTULA:<BR>I A disease: भगन्दरः (anal f.).<BR>II<BR>A pipe: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fistulous
FISTULOUS: Ph.:<BR>f. sore:<BR>नाडि<BR>or<BR>नाडी, -व्रणम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fit
FIT (subs.):<BR>I A convulsion: मूर्च्छा,<BR>then<BR>men get f. s:<BR>तदा मूर्च्छन्ति मानवाः, Bha.<BR>II An<BR>attack: q.v.:<BR>in a f. of rage:<BR>क्रोधमूर्च्छितः (ता,<BR> तं), Ram.;<BR>in a f. of madness:<BR>वायुग्रस्तः (स्ता,<BR> स्तं).<BR>III A vicissitude: विलासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fit
FIT (adj.):<BR>(1) योग्यः (ग्या, ग्यं),<BR>f. for sending<BR>to Lankā:<BR>लङ्काप्रस्थापनयोग्यः (ग्या, ग्यं), Ma. n.;<BR>I am f. (to hold the weapon),<BR>you are not f.,<BR>how is this:<BR>योग्योऽहमयोग्यो भवानिति कथमेतत्, Mu.<BR>vii.;<BR>(2) उचितः (ता, तं),<BR>f. for riding:<BR>तुरङ्गा-<BR>धिरोहणोचितः (ता, तं), K.;<BR>(3) क्षमः (मा, मं) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">Page281</a>]<BR>(= able, adequate),<BR>dress f. for going to<BR>hunting fields:<BR>मृगवनोपगमक्षमवेषः, R. ix. 50.: v.<BR>Also proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fit
FIT (v.):<BR>I To make f.: expr. by adj.<BR>II<BR>Of tailors, etc.: perh. समानीकरोति।<BR>III To<BR>besuitable to: perh. समानीभवति (with gen.).<BR>Comp.: (a)<BR>f. out:<BR>सज्जीकरोति; (b) f. up:<BR>अलङ्करोति,<BR>Dwārakā was f. ed to honour the son<BR>of Pāṇḍu:<BR>कुन्तीपुत्रस्य पूजार्थं द्वारकालङ्कृता बभूव, Mah.<BR>i. 216. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fitch
FITCH:<BR>I A chick-pea: चणकः।<BR>II A fur:<BR>q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fitful
FITFUL:<BR>(1) चञ्चलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) चपलः (ला,<BR> लं);<BR>(3) लोलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fitly
FITLY:<BR>(1) युक्तम्;<BR>(2) उचितम्;<BR>(3) better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fitness
FITNESS:<BR>(1) योग्यता;<BR>(2) औचित्यम्;<BR>(3) क्षमता।<BR>For dif.: v. Fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fitting
FITTING:<BR>I The act: v. To fit.<BR>II Anything<BR>used in f. up: सज्जा (?); उपकरणम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

five
FIVE: पञ्चन् (mfn.).<BR>F. or six:<BR>पञ्चष (f. षा) (only<BR>in pl.), Vi.<BR>F. times:<BR>पञ्चकृत्व;<BR>or<BR>पञ्चवारान्।<BR>In f.<BR>ways or parts:<BR>पञ्चधा।<BR>F. hundred:<BR>पञ्चशत्म्।<BR>F.<BR>fold:<BR>पञ्चगुणः (णा, णं). Having f. claws:<BR>पञ्चनख (f. खी), M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

five-finger
FIVE-FINGER, FIVE-LEAF: a plant *पञ्चदलः<BR>(पञ्चाङ्गुलः is another p.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fives
FIVES: a play: पञ्चकक्रीडा (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fix
FIX (subs.) Ph.:<BR>Kṛṣṇa thought himself to be<BR>on a f.:<BR>कृष्ण आत्मानं चक्रान्तरस्थितमिव मेने, V. p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fix
FIX (v.t.):<BR>I To set, establish: स्थापयति (c.<BR>of स्था),<BR>f. ing (them) as two trophies:<BR>कीर्तिस्तम्भ-<BR>द्वयमिव स्थापयित्वा, R. xv. 103.<BR>II To fasten:<BR>q.v.: बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.).<BR>III To implant:<BR>q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fix
FIX (v.i.):<BR>I To rest: q.v.: तिष्ठति, अव-, (स्था,<BR>c. 2.),<BR>not f. ed on darlings:<BR>दयितास्वनवस्थितम्, Ku.<BR>iv. 28.<BR>II To f. on: स्थिरीकरोतिः v. To<BR>resolve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fixed
FIXED (adj.):<BR>I Firm: q.v.: स्थिरः (रा, रं),<BR>II Fastened: बद्धः (f. द्धा), नि-,<BR>with eyes<BR>whose aim is immovably f.:<BR>निश्चलनिबद्धलक्ष्येण<BR> चक्षुषा, K.<BR>III Of mind:<BR>(1) एकाग्रः (ग्रा,<BR> ग्रं);<BR>(2) अनन्य- in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fixedly
FIXEDLY:<BR>(1) स्थिरम्;<BR>(2) दृढम् (= firmly);<BR>(3) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fixedness
FIXEDNESS:<BR>I Firmness: q.v.: स्थैर्यं<BR>or<BR>स्थिरता।<BR>II Of mind: एकाग्रता; अनन्यमनस्कता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fixture
FIXTURE:<BR>I As of a house: no equiv.: expr.<BR>by सङ्गीयः (या, यं).<BR>II Firmness: q.v. दृढता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flabbiness
FLABBINESS:<BR>(1) शिथिलता;<BR>(2) शैथिल्यम्: v. Also<BR>softness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flabby
FLABBY: शिथिलः (ला, लं): v. Also soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flaccid
FLACCID: श्लथः (था, थं), प्र-: v. Flabby, soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flaccidity
FLACCIDITY: श्लथता: Flabbiness, softness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flag
FLAG (subs.):<BR>I A banner: q.v.:<BR>(1) ध्वजा;<BR>(2) पताका।<BR>II F. stone: समशिला (?).<BR>III<BR>A plant: गोलोभी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flag
FLAG (v.i.): म्लायति (म्लै, c. 1.): v. To droop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flag
FLAG (v.t.):<BR>I To droop: q.v.<BR>II To lay<BR>with f. stone: आ-स्तॄणाति (स्तॄ, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flag-staff
FLAG-STAFF:<BR>(1) ध्वजदण्डः;<BR>(2) केतुयष्टिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flageolet
FLAGEOLET: वंशः (gen. name: v. Flute).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flagginfss
FLAGGINFSS:<BR>(1) शिथिलता: v. Weakness;<BR>(2) नीरसता: v. Insipidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flagging
FLAGGING:<BR>I A pavement: समशिला भूमिः (?).<BR>II Flags: समशिला (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flaggy
FLAGGY:<BR>I Weak, flexible: q.v.: शिथिलः (ला,<BR> लं).<BR>II Insipid: q.v.: नीरसः (सा, सं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flagitious
FLAGITIOUS:<BR>I Of acts: महापाप- in comp.<BR>II Of men: घोरपातकिन् (f. नी): v. Also<BR>atrocious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flagitiously
FLAGITIOUSLY: expr. by adj. “so f. unjust”:<BR>एतादृशं घोरमन्याय्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flagon
FLAGON: पुटग्रीवः (?): v. Vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flagrancy
FLAGRANCY:<BR>I Enormous:<BR>(1) घोरता;<BR>(2)<BR>दारुणता, -त्वम् घोरः (रा, रं);<BR>(3) दारुण (f. णा).<BR>II Glowing, raging: दीप्यमानः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flail
FLAIL: कण्डनयष्टिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flake
FLAKE: perh. पिण्ड (mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flaky
FLAKY: पिण्डमयः (यी, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flambeau
FLAMBEAU: उल्का,<BR>then they went about at the<BR>head of the battle with f. s in their hands:<BR>उल्काहस्तौ तदा रात्रौ रणमूर्ध्नि विचेरतुः, Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flame
FLAME (subs.): शिखा, as if coming out in f. s:<BR>शिखाभिर्विनिश्चरन्, Vi. v. 26.;<BR>(2) ज्वाला,<BR>with<BR>hairy f.s.:<BR>ज्वालासटैः, Ki. xvi. 50.;<BR>(3) अर्चिस [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">Page282</a>]<BR>(f.),<BR>with circles of fiery f. s.:<BR>अरुणैरर्चिषां चक्रवालैः,<BR>Vi. vi. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flame
FLAME (v.):<BR>I Intrans: ज्वलति (ज्वल्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To burn.<BR>II Trans.: v. To inflame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flamingo
FLAMINGO: पक्षिविशेषः; *शोणच्छदः, मरालः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flamy
FLAMY:<BR>(1) शिखावत् (f. ती);<BR>(2) शिखिन् (f.<BR>नी);<BR>(3) ज्वालामयः (यी, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flank
FLANK (subs.): पाश्र्व (mn.)<BR>or<BR>पार्श्वदेशः,<BR>in front,<BR>on the rear, and on the f. s.:<BR>अग्रे पृष्ठे च पार्श्वयोः,<BR>A. r.; (the horse) as if painted on the f. s:<BR>उल्लिखितमिव पार्श्वयोः, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flank
FLANK (v.):<BR>I To border, touch: q.v.<BR>II<BR>To attack the f.: पार्श्वं हन्ति, अभि-, (हन्, c.<BR>2.), Ka.<BR>III To guard the f.: पार्श्वे or<BR>पार्श्वयोः रक्षति (रक्ष्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flannel
FLANNEL: *प्राणलम्,<BR>F. led:<BR>*प्राणलवस्त्रावृतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flap
FLAP (subs.):<BR>I Anything that hangs loose:<BR>प्रालम्बः (?).<BR>II F. -ping;<BR>(1) धूननम्, वि-;<BR>(2)<BR>आस्फालनम्।<BR>III In pl. अश्वानामोष्ठरोगभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flap
FLAP (v.t.):<BR>I To strike: q.v.: ताडयति (तड्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR>II To shake:<BR>(1) धूनाति<BR>or<BR>धूनीते<BR>(धू, c. 9.);<BR>(2) आस्फालयति (c. of<BR>स्फल्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flare
FLARE (subs.):<BR>(1) लोलशिखा;<BR>(2) चाञ्चल्यप्रभा,<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flare
FLARE (v.): expr. by subs.: v. Also to glare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flaringly
FLARINGLY:<BR>(1) लोलम्;<BR>(2) चञ्चलम्;<BR>(3) by adj.<BR>न स्तिमितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flash
FLASH (subs.):<BR>(1) स्फुरितम्,<BR>terrified with f. es of<BR>wreathy lightning:<BR>विद्युद्दामस्फुरितचकितः (ता, तं),<BR>Me. i. 28.;<BR>(2) स्फुरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flash
FLASH (v.i.): स्फुरति (स्फुर्, c. 6.) (lit. and fig.),<BR>they are f. ing with rage:<BR>स्फुरितमनयोः क्रोधेन, U. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flashy
FLASHY:<BR>I Lit.: क्षणप्रभ (f. भा) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Insipid: नीरसः (सा, सं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flask
FLASK:<BR>(1) भाण्डम् (gen. term.);<BR>(2) महाकूपी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flasket
FLASKET:<BR>I For viands: अन्नपात्रम् (?).<BR>II A<BR>basket: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flat
FLAT (adj.):<BR>I Plain, level: समः (मा, मं),<BR>to<BR>lay f.:<BR>समीकरोति, Ku. or fig. पातयति (c. of<BR>पत्) (= to fell), V. p.<BR>II Dull, insipid:<BR>नीरसः (सा, सं).<BR>III Positive, clear: स्फुटः<BR>(टा, टं),<BR>“that is f.”:<BR>स्फुटमेतत्।<BR>IV Of<BR>letters: घोषवत् (f. ती), T. p. i. 14. V. Of<BR>nose, etc.: स्थूलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flat
FLAT (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: समभूमिः।<BR>II A shallow:<BR>q.v.<BR>III A boat:<BR>(1) तरालु;<BR>(2) तरान्धु।<BR>IV<BR>A car: यानविशेषः।<BR>V A dull fellow: स्थूल-<BR>बुद्धि (mfn.), K.<BR>VI Story: q.v.<BR>VII A f.<BR>part: perh. पृष्ठम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flat
FLAT (v.):<BR>I Lit.: समीकरोति।<BR>II To depress:<BR>q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flatly
FLATLY<BR>I Evenly: समम्।<BR>II Openly: स्फुटम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flatness
FLATNESS:<BR>I Lit.: समता।<BR>II Of nose, etc.:<BR>स्थूलता।<BR>III Dejection: q.v.: विषादः।<BR>IV<BR>Insipidity: नीरसता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flatten
FLATTEN:<BR>I Lit.: समीकरोति।<BR>II To fell:<BR>q.v.: पातयति (c. of पत्).<BR>III To deject,<BR>depress: q.v.<BR>IV To make vapid:<BR>नीरसीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flatter
FLATTER:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) स्तौति, सं-, अभि-, परि-,<BR>(स्तु, c. 2.), who day and night f. s (him)<BR>as<BR>super-divine:<BR>योऽहर्निशमधिदैवतमिव स्तौति, K.: v.<BR>To praise;<BR>(2) by subs., to f. one's vanity:<BR>चाटूक्तिभिर्मानं वर्धयति (c. of वृध्).<BR>II To gra-<BR>-tify, please: q.v.: सं-तोषयति (c. of तुष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flatterer
FLATTERER:<BR>(1) स्तोतृ (m.), सं-।: v. Praiser.;<BR>(2) चाटुकारः;<BR>(3) संस्तववक्तृ (m.), Mah. ii. 44. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flattering
FLATTERING (adj.):<BR>(1) प्रीतिवर्द्धनः (नी, नं)<BR>(= gratifying);<BR>(2) शोभनः (ना, नं) (=fine);<BR>(3) by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flattery
FLATTERY:<BR>(1) स्तवः, सं- (= praise: q.v.),<BR>with<BR>false f.:<BR>वितथैः स्तवैः, Si. xiv. 3.;<BR>(2) चाटुः or<BR>चाटूक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flatting
FLATTING:<BR>I The act.: समीकरणम्।<BR>II A mode<BR>of painting: समीकरणम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flatulence
FLATULENCE, FLATULENCY:<BR>(1) अजीर्णम् (= indi-<BR>-gestion);<BR>(2) वातात्मकोऽरोचकः (?), Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flatulent
FLATULENT:<BR>(1) वाताधिकः (का, कं) (!);<BR>(2)<BR>(2) अजीर्णरोगिन् (f. णी) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flaunt
FLAUNT:<BR>I Intrans: सगर्वं चलति (चल्, c. 1.)<BR>(?).<BR>II Trans.: v. To show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flavour
FLAVOUR (subs.):<BR>(1) आस्वादः: v. Relish;<BR>(2) आमोदः: v. Fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flavour
FLAVOUR (v.):<BR>f. ing essences:<BR>सुस्वादकरसाः (?);<BR>highly-f. ed wine:<BR>उग्रस्वादं मद्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flavourless
FLAVOURLESS: स्वादहीनः (ना, नं): v. Taste-<BR>-less.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flaw
FLAW (subs.):<BR>I In gen.: छिद्रम्,<BR>evils multiply<BR>in f. s.:<BR>छिद्रेष्वनर्था बहुलीभवन्ति, H.: v. Defect,<BR>fault.<BR>II A quarrel: q.v. कलिः।<BR>III Of<BR>mind:. चण्डवातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flaw
FLAW: (v.t.): छिद्रयति (छिद्र्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>break, crack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flawless
FLAWLESS:<BR>(1) अच्छिद्र (f. द्रा),<BR>f. should see the<BR>flaws of others:<BR>अच्छिद्रश्छिद्रदर्शी स्यात्, Mah.;<BR>(2)<BR>निर्दोषः (षा, षं);<BR>(3) निष्कलङ्क (f. ङ्का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flax
FLAX:<BR>I The plant:<BR>(1) क्षुमा;<BR>(2) अतसी।<BR>II<BR>The skin: क्षुमा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flax-comb
FLAX-COMB: क्षुमामार्जनी (?) and sim comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flax-dresser
FLAX-DRESSER: क्षुमाशोधकः (?) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flaxen
FLAXEN: क्षौमः (मी, मं),<BR>f. -haired.:<BR>क्षौमकेश (f.<BR>शी) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flay
FLAY (v.):<BR>(1) त्वचयति (nomi.);<BR>(2) चर्म<BR> अपनयति (नी, c. 1.), निर्हरति (हृ, c. 1.),<BR>निष्कर्षति (कृष्, c. 1.), etc.;<BR>(3) अपत्वचं<BR>(n. क्) करोति, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flayer
FLAYER: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flea
FLEA: दंशः (?),<BR>f.-bite:<BR>दंशदंशः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleak
FLEAK (subs.): बिन्दुः, A. r.: v. Spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleck
FLECK (v.t.): चित्रयति (चित्र्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>variegate, spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fledge
FLEDGE: exp. by subs.,<BR>“not yet f. d”:<BR>असञ्जात-<BR>पक्षपुटः (टा, टं), K.;<BR>but when sufficiently f. d to<BR>go in the air:<BR>उद्भिन्नपक्षतिस्तु गगनतलसञ्चरणसमर्थः, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flee
FLEE (v.i.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पलायते, प्र-, वि-, (पलाय्,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>does not f. from battle:<BR>नाहवात्पलायते, Ki.;<BR>(2) द्रवति, वि-, सं-, प्र-, (द्रु, c. I.), Mat.: v.<BR>Also to go away.<BR>II To avoid: q.v.:<BR>पलायते,<BR>piety f.s from there:<BR>तस्माद्धर्मः पलायते, S.p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleece
FLEECE (subs.): मेषलोमन् (n.) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleece
FLEECE (v.t.):<BR>I Lit.: अपलो(रो)मं or<BR>विलो(रो)मं (f. मां) करोति।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) लुण्ठति<BR>(लुठ्, c. 1.): v. To plunder;<BR>(2) निष्कर्षति<BR>(कृष्, c. 1.): v. To extort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleecy
FLEECY:<BR>(1) लो(रो)मशः (शा, शं);<BR>(2) बहु-<BR>लोमन् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleer
FLEER (subs.):<BR>I A flier: पलायितः (ता, तं).<BR>II Derision: अवहासः। (हस्, c. 1.): v. To mock,<BR>ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleet
FLEET (subs.):<BR>I In gen.: पोतावलिः (?).<BR>II<BR>Military: रणपोतावलिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleet
FLEET (adj.):<BR>(1) प्रजविन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) वेगिन्<BR>(f. नी);<BR>(3) वेगवत् (f. ती);<BR>(4) जवनः (नी, नं),<BR>f. charger:<BR>जवनवाजी, R.: v. Swift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleet
FLEET (v.):<BR>I To fly swiftly: जवेन<BR>or<BR>द्रुतं प्रसर्पति<BR>(सृप्, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>चलति (चल्, c. 1.) etc.<BR>II To<BR>skim: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleeting
FLEETING (adj.):<BR>(1) चञ्चलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2)<BR>चपलः (ला, लं);<BR>(3) चलः (ला, लं);<BR>(4) गत्वरः<BR>(री, रं) (rare), Ki.;<BR>(5) अचिरस्थयिन् (f. नी);<BR>(6) क्षणभङ्गुरः (रा, रं): v. Transient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleetly
FLEETLY: द्रुतम्: v. Swiftly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleetness
FLEETNESS:<BR>(1) जवः;<BR>(2) वेगः: v. Speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flesh
FLESH (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मांसम्,<BR>abstaining<BR>from f. and wine:<BR>निवृत्तः मांसमद्ययोः, Pa.;<BR>horse<BR>f. is sweet (and) light:<BR>अश्वमांसं मधुरं लधुरं लघु, Bha.;<BR>(2) आमिषम्,<BR>the f. of buffalo is sweet:<BR>महिषस्यामिषं<BR> स्वादु, Mah.;<BR>(3) पिशितम् (rare),<BR>f.-eater:<BR>पिशिता-<BR>शिन् (f. नी), R.<BR>II Body: q.v.: मांसम्।<BR>III<BR>Mankind: q.v.<BR>IV Kindness: q.v.:<BR>perh. मांसम्। v. Carnality: कामः।<BR>VI<BR>Kindred: सनाभि (mfn.):<BR>VII Of fruit: वीजम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flesh
FLESH (v.):<BR>I Lit.: मांसेन भोजयति (c. of भुज्).<BR>II To glut, satiate: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flesh-broth
FLESH-BROTH:<BR>(1) मांसरसः;<BR>(2) सिद्धमांसरसः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flesher
FLESHER:<BR>(1) मांसिकः;<BR>(2) मांसविक्रेतृ (m.);<BR>(3)<BR>मांसविक्रयिन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flefh-hook
FLEFH-HOOK: *मांसकर्षणी: v. Hook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleshiness
FLESHINESS: मांसलता: v. Plumpness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleshless
FLESHLESS: निर्मांसः (सा, सं) and sim. comp.s,<BR>from f. ness:<BR>निर्मांसतया, K.: v. Lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleshliness
FLESHLINESS: विषयासक्तिः: v. Carnality, sen-<BR>-suality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleshly
FLESHLY:<BR>I Corporeal: q.v. शारीरिकः (की,<BR> कं).<BR>II Animal: मांस- in comp. Ph.:<BR>f.<BR>minded:<BR>विषयासक्त (f. क्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flesh-meat
FLESH-MEAT:<BR>to take f.:<BR>मांसाहारं<BR>or<BR>आमिषभोजनं<BR> करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fleshy
FLESHY: मांसलः (ला, लं),<BR>f. not tendinous:<BR>मांसला-<BR>वशिरालौ, D.: v. Plum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flex
FLEX:<BR>(1) नमयति (c. of नम्): v. To bend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flexibility
FLEXIBILITY:<BR>(1) नम्यता, अव-, आ-;<BR>(2) कुञ्चनीयता,<BR> आ-, अव-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flexible
FLEXIBLE:<BR>(1) नम्य (f. म्या)<BR>or<BR>नमनीयः (या, यं),<BR>आ-, अव-;<BR>(2) कुञ्चनीयः (या, यं), आ-, अव-: V.<BR>Also soft, elastic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flexion
FLEXION:<BR>(1) नमनम्, आ-;<BR>(2) कुञ्चनम्, आ-, अव-,<BR>their use is seen in unfolding and f.:<BR>प्रसारणाकुञ्च-<BR>नयोर्दृष्टं तासां प्रयोजनम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flexure
FLEXURE:<BR>I Flexion: q.v.<BR>II A turn,<BR>bend: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flicker
FLICKER:<BR>I To flutter: q.v.<BR>II Of flames<BR>etc.: expr. by adj. चञ्चलः (ला,; लं), अस्थिरः<BR>(रा, रं), अस्तिमित। (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flier
FLIER:<BR>I Lit.: पलायकः।<BR>II Of a spindle:<BR>बादुः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flight
FLIGHT (subs.):<BR>I Fleeing: पलायनम्, taken to f.:<BR>पलायनपरायण (f. णा).<BR>To put to f.:<BR>विद्रावयति (c.<BR>of द्रु).<BR>II Of birds:<BR>(1) डयनम्, upward f.:<BR>उड्डयनम्;<BR>(2) गतिः (= motion), of “lazy f.”:<BR>मन्दगतिः, H.<BR>III Fig., soaring, wandering:<BR>ऊर्ध्वगतिः (?).<BR>IV A flock: q.v.<BR>V Of<BR>stairs: निःश्रेणि, -णी, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flight-shot
FLIGHT-SHOT: बाणक्षेपः and sim. comp.s.<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flighty
FLIGHTY: चञ्चलः (ला, लं): v. Fleeting, fickle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flimsiness
FLIMSINESS:<BR>(1) असारता;<BR>(2) निःसारता;<BR>(3)<BR>दुर्बलता (= weakness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flimsy
FLIMSY:<BR>(1) असारः<BR>or<BR>निःसारः (रा, रं);<BR>(2)<BR>दुर्बलः (ला, लं) (= weak).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flinch
FLINCH (v.):<BR>(1) पराङ्मुखीमवति;<BR>(2) विमुखीभवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flincher
FLINCHER: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flinder-mouse
FLINDER-MOUSE, FLITTER-MOUSE: चर्मचटी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fling
FLING (v.): क्षिपति, नि-, (क्षिप्, c. 6.): v. To<BR>throw, cast, emit. Comp.s.:<BR>f. away:<BR>अवक्षिपति;<BR>f. down:<BR>अधःक्षिपति;<BR>f. in, f. off:<BR>अवक्षिपति; f. open:<BR>बलात् अपावृणोति (वृ, c. 5.) (?). v. Also to break<BR>open;<BR>f. out:<BR>उद्गिरति (गॄ, c. 6.);<BR>f. up:<BR>अव-<BR>क्षिपति, त्यजति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fling
FLING (subs.):<BR>I A throw: क्षेपः, नि-, प्र-।<BR>II<BR>A gibe:<BR>(1) आक्षेपः;<BR>(2) अवक्षेपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flint
FLINT:<BR>(1) अग्निप्रस्तरः;<BR>(2) अरणिः। F. glass:<BR>*अरणिकाचः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flinty
FLINTY:<BR>I Lit: by comp.<BR>II Cruel: वज्य-<BR>in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flip
FLIP: पानीयविशेषः; *प्लवः।<BR>F. -dog:<BR>*प्लवलौहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flippancy
FLIPPANCY:<BR>I Of speech: वाचालता।<BR>II Of<BR>conduct: चापल्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flippant
FLIPPANT:<BR>I In speech: वाचालः (ला, लं).<BR>II<BR>Empty, pert: q.v.: चपलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flirt
FLIRT (v.):<BR>I To throw: q.v.<BR>II To toss<BR>about: सञ्चालयति (c. of चल्).<BR>III To co-<BR>-quet: प्रेमालापं करोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flirt
FLIRT (subs.):<BR>I A jerk: q.v.<BR>II A co-<BR>-quette: प्रेमालापनिपुणा (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flirtation
FLIRTATION: प्रेमालापः (?) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flit
FLIT:<BR>I To fly: q.v.<BR>II To flutter: q.v.<BR>III To migrate: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flitter
FLITTER: चीरम्: v. Rag, tatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

float
FLOAT (subs.):<BR>I A raft:<BR>(1) प्लवः;<BR>(2)<BR>कोलः;<BR>(3) उडुपः।<BR>II Of the fishing line:<BR>तरण्ड (mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

float
FLOAT (v.i.): प्लवते (प्ल, c. l,),<BR>pumpkins sinking<BR>in water and stones f. ing:<BR>अम्चुनि मज्जन्त्यलाबूनि<BR> ग्रावाणः प्लवन्त इति, Vi. i.;<BR>a body of horse f. ing<BR>in that cloud of dust:<BR>तस्मिन्ने व महति रजसि प्लवमान-<BR>मश्ववृन्दम्, C.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

float
FLOAT (v.t.):<BR>I To cause to f.: expr. by<BR>प्लवते।<BR>II To deluge: q.v.: प्लावयति (c. of प्लु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flock
FLOCK (subs.):<BR>(1) यूथम्;<BR>(2) सङ्घः;<BR>(3) कुलम्;<BR>(4) वृन्दम्;<BR>(5) कदम्बकम्;<BR>(6) गणः;<BR>(7) ओघः;<BR>(8) व्रातः;<BR>(9) व्रजः;<BR>(10) समूहः;<BR>(11) by<BR>deriv.,<BR>a. f. of pigeons:<BR>कापोतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flock
FLOCK (v.): एकत्र<BR>or<BR>एकस्थ (f. स्था) भवति: v.<BR>Gather, crowd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flog
FLOG (v.):<BR>(1) कशया (whip)<BR>or<BR>वेत्रेण (rattan)<BR>प्रहरति (हृ, c. 1.): v. To beat;<BR>(2) कशाघातं<BR>or<BR>वेत्राघातं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flogging
FLOGGING:<BR>(1) कशाघातः;<BR>(2) वेत्राघातः।<BR>Deser-<BR>ving f:.<BR>कश्य (f. श्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flood
FLOOD (subs.):<BR>I A flow,<BR>f. of water:<BR>जलौघः,<BR>Ki.<BR>or<BR>जलसंघातः, Ku.<BR>II Deluge:<BR>(1) आप्लाव;<BR>(2) संप्लवः,<BR>universal f.:<BR>आभूतसंप्लवः, Mat.;<BR>(3)<BR>वन्या<BR>or<BR>वानम् (= high f.). Ph.:<BR>all was a f. of<BR>water:<BR>सर्वमाम्भसमेवासीत्, Mah.<BR>or<BR>एतदेकार्णवं सर्वम्,<BR>Mat.<BR>III Of tide: v. Tide.<BR>IV Abun- [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">Page285</a>]<BR>-dance: q.v.: प्राचुर्यम्। V. A stream: प्रवाहः,<BR>f. of tears:<BR>अश्रुप्रवाहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flood
FLOOD (v.) प्लावयति (c. of प्लु): v. To deluge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flood-gate
FLOOD-GATE:<BR>I Lit.: निर्गमनमार्गः, K. and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR>II Any passage: मार्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flook
FLOOK: v. Fluke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

floor
FLOOR (subs.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) तलम्;<BR>(2)<BR>भूतलम्: v. Ground.<BR>II Story: q.v.<BR>(1)<BR>भूमिः,<BR>in the seventh f.:<BR>सप्तमभूमिमागे, N. xxii. 1.;<BR>(2) perh. तलम् (comp. Bengali दोताला, तेताला,<BR>etc.).<BR>III A platform: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

floor
FLOOR (v.t.):<BR>I To furnish with a f.: expr.<BR>by subs.<BR>II To throw on the ground:<BR>भूमौ पातयति (c. of पत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

floor-cloth
FLOOR-CLOTH: भूम्यास्तरणम् (?) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flooring
FLOORING:<BR>I Pavement: q.v.<BR>II Mate-<BR>-rials for floor: *तलास्तरः, भूमिस्रस्तरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flora
FLORA:<BR>I The goddess of flowers: नन्दन-<BR>वनदेवता (?), K.<BR>II A list of plants:<BR>f. of<BR>Bengal:<BR>वङ्गानां पुष्पावलिः<BR>or<BR>लताकोषः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

floral
FLORAL:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) पौष्प (f. ष्पी);<BR>(3) कौसुम (f. मी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

florid
FLORID:<BR>I Red: q.v.: रक्त (f. क्ता).<BR>II<BR>Ornate: perh. पुष्पितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) अलङ्कृतः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(3) विचित्रः (त्रा, त्रं);<BR>(4) उज्ज्वलः<BR>(ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

floridity
FLORIDITY: FLORIDNESS:<BR>I Redness: रक्तता।<BR>II Of style:<BR>(1) औज्ज्वल्यम्;<BR>(2) अलङ्कारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

florin
FLORIN: मुद्राविशेषः, *पुष्पकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

florist
FLORIST:<BR>I Lit.: पुष्पोपजीविन् (f. नी), Ram.<BR>II Writer of a flora: *पुष्पावलि-<BR>or<BR>लताकोष-<BR>रचयितृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flota
FLOTA: पोतावलिः।<BR>Flotilla:<BR>क्षुद्रपोतावलिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flotation
FLOTATION:<BR>I The act: प्लवनम्।<BR>II The<BR>science: प्लवनम्, -झानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flounce
FLOUNCE (v.): अङ्गानि विक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.) or<BR>संचालयति (c. of चल्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flounce
FLOUNCE (subs.): अङ्गविक्षेपः (?); अङ्गचालनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flounder
FLOUNDER:<BR>I Verb: v. To flounce.<BR>II<BR>Subs.: मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flour
FLOUR:<BR>I Of wheat:<BR>(1) गोधूमचूर्णम्;<BR>(2)<BR>गोधूमपिष्टम्, Raj.<BR>II Of other grains: by चूर्णं<BR>or<BR>पिष्टम्,<BR>barley^1 f.:<BR>यवचूर्णम्।<BR>Fried-grain-f.:<BR>शक्तुः।<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flourish
FLOURISH (subs.):<BR>I Show: आडम्बरः,<BR>with<BR>great f.:<BR>बह्वाडम्बरपूर्वकम्।<BR>II Of language: अति-<BR>शयोक्तिः।<BR>III Brandishing: आस्फालनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flourish
FLOURISH (v.i.):<BR>I To thrive: वर्धते (c. of<BR>वृध्).<BR>II To decorate: q.v.: अतिशयोक्तिं<BR> करोति।<BR>III To brandish: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flourish
FLOURISH (v.t.):<BR>I To thrive: वर्धयति (c. of<BR>वृध्).<BR>II To decorate: q.v.: अलङ्करोति।<BR>III<BR>To brandish: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flourishing
FLOURISHING (adj.):<BR>(1) समृद्ध (f. द्धा) (= affl-<BR>-uent);<BR>(2) उत्कृष्ट (f. ष्टा) (= excellent).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flout
FLOUT:<BR>I Verb: अवहसति (हस्, c. 1.) (with<BR>acc.)<BR>II Subs.; अवहासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flow
FLOW (subs.):<BR>I A pouring:<BR>(1) स्रवः, स्रवणम् or<BR>स्रुतिः, परि-,<BR>f. of eye-drops:<BR>अश्रुबिन्दुस्रुतिः, N. ix.<BR>104;<BR>(2) स्यन्दः, -नम्, नि-, अभि-,<BR>emission of the<BR>f. of heaven:<BR>स्वर्गाभिष्यन्दवमनम्, Ku. vi. 37.;<BR>(3)<BR>प्रवाहः (= stream): q.v.).<BR>II Of tide: वर्धमाना<BR> वेला: v. Tide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flow
FLOW (v.i.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) स्रवति, प्र-, परि-,<BR>(स्रु, c. 1.) (best equiv.),<BR>rivers like the Ganges<BR>f. towards the east:<BR>नद्यो गङ्गाद्याः पूर्वां दिशं प्रति<BR> स्रवन्ति, S.c.;<BR>honey- f. ing:<BR>मधुस्रवः (वा, वं), N.;<BR>(2) स्यन्दति, प्र-, अभि-, नि-, (स्यन्द्, c. 1.),<BR>as if<BR>the place from which the quarters f.:<BR>निष्यन्दमिव<BR> दिशाम्, K.;<BR>(3) प्रवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.) (= to pro-<BR>-ceed: of language), Ki.<BR>II Of the tide:<BR>v. Tide.<BR>III To melt: q.v.<BR>IV To hang<BR>loose: लम्बते, प्र-, (लम्ब्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flower
FLOWER (subs.):<BR>I In gen. sense:<BR>(1) पुष्पम्,<BR>the stars, the f.s of heaven:<BR>ताराः खपुष्पाणि, N.;<BR>(2) कुसुमम्,<BR>f. -bed:<BR>कुसुमास्तरणम्, Ku.;<BR>(3) प्रसूनं or<BR>प्रसवः (rare),<BR>coming out of f.s:<BR>प्रसूनस्यागमः, U.<BR>In f.:<BR>कुसुमितः (ता, तं)<BR>or<BR>पुष्पितः (ता, तं), Mah.<BR>II Best part: सारमागः।<BR>F. of life:<BR>प्रौढयौवनम्<BR>(?).<BR>III Menstrual discharge: पुष्पम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flower
FLOWER (v.): expr. by subs.,<BR>ever f. ing:<BR>नित्य-<BR>पुष्प (f. ष्पा), Me. v. Also to blossom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

floweret
FLOWERET: क्षुद्रपुष्पम्; प्रसूनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flowerless
FLOWERLESS:<BR>(1) अपुष्प (f. ष्पा);<BR>(2) कुसुमहीनः<BR>(ना, नं); and sim. comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flower-stalk
FLOWER-STALK:<BR>(1) मञ्जरी;<BR>(2) पुष्पवृन्तम्;<BR>(3)<BR>प्रसवबन्धनम् (poet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flowery
FLOWERY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पुष्पमयः (यी यं);<BR>(2)<BR>कुसुममयः (यी, यं);<BR>(3) पुष्पबहुलः (ला, लं);<BR>etc.<BR>II Florid: q.v.: पुष्पितः (ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flowingly
FLOWINGLY:<BR>(1) द्रुतम्;<BR>(2) अनर्गलम् (without<BR>restraint).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fluctuate
FLUCTUATE (v.):<BR>(1) दोलायते (nomi.): v. To<BR>waver;<BR>(2) विचिकित्सते (= to hesitate: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fluctuation
FLUCTUATION:<BR>I The act: expr. by verb.<BR>II Unsteadiness: q.v.: चाञ्चल्यम्।<BR>II In<BR>pl., ups and downs: पातोत्पाताः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flue
FLUE: *वायुस्रोतस् (n.); धूममार्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fluency
FLUENCY:<BR>(1) वाक्शक्तिः;<BR>(2) वाक्पाटवम्: v.<BR>Eloquence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fluent
FLUENT:<BR>(1) वश्यवाच् (mfn.), Vi.;<BR>(2) अनर्गलवाच्<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(3) वचस्विन् (f. नी), Si. xvii. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fluently
FLUENTLY:<BR>(1) अनर्गलम् (= without stop);<BR>(2)<BR>अविश्रान्तम् (= continuously).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fluid
FLUID:<BR>I Adj.: द्रवः (वा, वं).<BR>II Subs.:<BR>द्रवः, -द्रव्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fluidity
FLUIDITY, FLUIDNESS: द्रवता, -त्वम्, Par.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fluke
FLUKE: (*लङ्गर-) दन्ताग्रं<BR>or<BR>दन्तमुखम् (दन्त being the<BR>whole arm).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flumery
FLUMERY:<BR>I A pap: q.v.<BR>II Flattery:<BR>मिथ्याप्रशंसा; वितथस्तवः, Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flunkey
FLUNKEY: पीठमर्दः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flurry
FLURRY (subs.):<BR>(1) व्याकुलताः v. Confusion;<BR>(2) त्वरा: v. Hurry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flurry
FLURRY (v.):<BR>(1) क्षोभयति (c. of क्षुभ्): v. To<BR>agitate;<BR>(2) उद्वेजयति (c. of विज्): v. To<BR>alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flush
FLUSH (subs.):<BR>I A rush: q.v.:<BR>II A<BR>blush: q.v. रक्तिमन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flush
FLUSH (adj.):<BR>I Lively: q.v.: प्रफुल्लः (ल्ला,<BR> ल्लं).<BR>II Affluent: q.v.<BR>III Liberal:<BR>q.v.: त्यागिन् (f. नी).<BR>IV Level: समः (मा,<BR> मं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flush
FLUSH (v.t.):<BR>I To redden: q.v.:<BR>“faintly<BR>f. ed”:<BR>ईषदरुणितः (ता, तं).<BR>II To elate:<BR>उत्सेचयति (c. of सिच्.<BR>III To agitate:<BR>क्षोमयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flush
FLUSH (v.i.):<BR>I To rush: q.v.<BR>II To<BR>redden: q.v.: अरुणीभवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flute
FLUTE (subs.):<BR>I A pipe:<BR>(1) वेणुः,<BR>a lute is<BR>played on, a f. is blown:<BR>वीणा वाद्यते वेणुः पूर्यते,<BR>N.d.;<BR>(2) वंशः, -शी;<BR>(3) मुरली,<BR>enchanted with<BR>the music of the f.:<BR>मुरलीनादमोहितः (ता, तं).<BR>II<BR>A channel, groove: रेखा (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flute
FLUTE (v.):<BR>I Intrans: वेणुं पूरयति (पूर्, c. 10.)<BR>etc.<BR>II Trans: गायति (गै, c. 1.): v. To<BR>sing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fluter
FLUTER, FLUTIST:<BR>(1) वेणुध्मः;<BR>(2) वांशिकः;<BR>(3) वंशीधरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flutter
FLUTTER (v.):<BR>I Lit.: पक्षौ धूनति<BR>or<BR>धूनुते or<BR>धूनयति, -ते (धू, c. 5. and 10)., N.<BR>II To<BR>fluctuate: दोलायते (nomi.).<BR>III To agitate:<BR>q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flutter
FLUTTER (subs.):<BR>I Vibration, motion:<BR>q.v.<BR>II Agitation: क्षोभः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fluvial
FLUVIAL, FLUVIATIC: नादेयः (यी, यं) or by<BR>comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flux
FLUX (subs.):<BR>I Flow: q.v.<BR>II Concourse:<BR>q.v. संमर्दः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fluxible
FLUXIBLE: विलयनीयः (या, यं): v. Fusible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fluxion
FLUXION:<BR>I Flow: स्रुतिः।<BR>II Decoration:<BR>उद्वर्तनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fly
FLY (subs.):<BR>(1) मक्षिका;<BR>(2) माचिका (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fly
FLY (v.i.):<BR>I As birds:<BR>(1) डीयते<BR>or<BR>डयते (डी<BR>c. 4. and 1.);<BR>(2) उत्पतति: v. To f. up;<BR>(3) गच्छति: v. To go.<BR>II To move rapid-<BR>-ly:<BR>(1) क्षिप्रं गच्छति and sim. ph.s,<BR>f.ing<BR>more quickly than the mind:<BR>मनसोऽप्याशुतरं यतः,<BR>Ki. xiii. 22.: v. Go and rapidly;<BR>(2) धावति<BR>(धाव्, c. 1.), f. ing through the firmament:<BR>गीर्वाणवर्त्मना धावन्, K.<BR>III To flee: q.v.:<BR>पलायते (पलाय्, c. 1.)<BR>IV To burst open:<BR>q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fly
FLY (v.t.):<BR>I To avoid: q.v.: परिहरति (हृ,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II To cause to start: चालयति (c. of<BR>चल्), Ki.<BR>III As a kite: उड्डीनं (f. नां) करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fly down
FLY DOWN: अवडीयते: v. To alight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fly round
FLY ROUND: परिडीयते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fly together
FLY TOGETHER: as birds: संडीयते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fly up
FLY UP:<BR>(1) उड्डीयते;<BR>(2) उत्पतति (= to go up:<BR>q.v.),<BR>flew up to the sky:<BR>वियदुत्पपात, H. ii. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flyblow
FLYBLOW: मक्षिकाण्डम्।<BR>Fly-blown:<BR>मक्षिकाण्ड-<BR>दूषितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flyboat
FLYBOAT: द्रुतनौका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flycatcher
FLYCATCHER: a bird: *मक्षिकाग्राहकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

flying
FLYING: डयनम्,<BR>f. up:<BR>उड्डयनम्;<BR>f. together:<BR>संडीनम्:<BR>v. To fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fly-leaf
FLY-LEAF: *शुद्धपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fly-trap
FLY-TRAP: a plant: *कीटग्रहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foal
FOAL (v.): अश्वशावः (of a horse): v. Colt, filly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foal
FOAL (v.): सूते, प्र-, (सू, c. 2.): v. To bring<BR>forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foam
FOAM (subs.):<BR>(1) फेनः;<BR>(2) हिण्डीरः (= sea -f.)<BR>(rare): v. Froth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foam
FOAM (v.i.): फेनायते (nomi.): v. To froth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foamy
FOAMY: फेनिलः (ला, लं), R. xiii. 2.: v.<BR>Frothy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fob
FOB:<BR>I A little pocket: आधारः।<BR>II To<BR>cheat: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

focus
FOCUS:<BR>I Subs.: केन्द्रम् (?).<BR>II Verb: एकत्री-<BR>करोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fodder
FODDER (subs.):<BR>(1) घासः,<BR>and f. for horses is<BR>easily procurable:<BR>अश्वघासश्च सुग्रहः, K.s. xv. 124.;<BR>(2) यवसः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foe
FOE: शत्रुः, even-handed to both friends and foes:<BR>समः शत्रौ च मित्रे च, G.: v. Enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fog
FOG:<BR>(1) कुज्भ्कटिका;<BR>(2) धुमि(पि)का:<BR>(3) कुहा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fogginess
FOGGINESS:<BR>(1) कुज्भ्कटिकाच्छन्नता;<BR>(2) कुहावृतता;<BR>(3) धूमलता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foggy
FOGGY:<BR>(1) कुज्भ्कटिकाच्छन्नः (न्ना, न्नं);<BR>(2) कुहावृतः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(3) धूमलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foh
FOH: आः; धिक् (= fie).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foible
FOIBLE:<BR>(1) छिद्रम्;<BR>(2) दोषः: v. Fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foil
FOIL (v.): मोघीकरोतिः v. To frustrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foil
FOIL (subs.):<BR>I Defeat: q.v.: भङ्गः।<BR>II A<BR>blunt sword: मिथ्याखङ्गः (?).<BR>III A leaf of<BR>metal: पत्रम्।<BR>IV Fig.: विभूषणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foist
FOIST (v.): संक्रामयति (c. of क्रम्)., Mr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foister
FOISTER:<BR>(1) संक्रामकः;<BR>(2) संक्रामयितृ (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fold
FOLD (v.):<BR>I To double: पुटीकरोति, सं-, (?).<BR>II To confine: q.v.: निरुणद्धि (रुध्, c. 7.).<BR>III Of doors: पिदधाति (धा, c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fold
FOLD (subs.):<BR>I F. ing: भङ्गिः<BR>or<BR>भङ्गः (?).<BR>II<BR>Embrace: q.v.<BR>III Sheep-pen: अवरोधः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

folding-door
FOLDING-DOOR: मङ्गप्रवणं द्वारम् (?), द्विपक्षद्वारम्, Mah.<BR>i. 205. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foliage
FOLIAGE:<BR>(1) पत्राणि (n. pl.);<BR>(2) पल्लवः (fresh<BR>f.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foliation
FOLIATION: पत्रीकरणम् (?);<BR>(2) तनूकरणम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

folio
FOLIO: विशालपत्रम् (?) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

folk
FOLK: लोकः: v. Man, people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

follow
FOLLOW (v.t.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) अनुगच्छति<BR>(गम्, c. 1.),<BR>f. ed her like a shadow:<BR>छायेव<BR> तामन्वगच्छत्, R. ii. 6.;<BR>f. s heroic conduct:<BR>अनु-<BR>गच्छति वीरवृत्तम्, U. v. 24.;<BR>(2) अनुयाति (या, c.<BR>2.),<BR>if I f. you:<BR>त्वामनुयामि यद्यपि, Ku. iv. 21.;<BR>(3) अनुसरति (सृ, c. 1.),<BR>how far did he come f.<BR>ing us:<BR>कियदनुसरन्नस्मानसावागत इति, Ri.;<BR>f. ing<BR>the way of policy:<BR>नीतिमार्गानुसारिन् (f. णी), M.<BR>n.;<BR>(4) अनुव्रजति (व्रज्, c. 1.) (lit.),<BR>f. ed up to<BR>the door:<BR>आद्वारमनुवव्राज, Ram.;<BR>(5) अनुधावति<BR>(धाव्, c. 1.) (= to run after: q.v.);<BR>(6)<BR>अनुवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.) (fig.),<BR>for men f. their<BR>master's mind:<BR>प्रभुचित्तमेव हि जनोऽनुवर्तते, Si.;<BR>(7)<BR>अनुविदधाति<BR>or<BR>विधत्ते (धा, c. 3.) (= to do after),<BR>f. ing destiny:<BR>भवितव्यतानुविधायिन् (f. नी), V.;<BR>(8) अनुवदति (वद्, c. 1.) (= to speak after,<BR>repeat),<BR>is f. ing our speech:<BR>अनुवदति गिरं नः, R.<BR>v. 74.<BR>II As a result, consequence: expr.<BR>by लभते (लभ्, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>प्राप्नोति (आप्, c. 5.)<BR>(= to get)<BR>or<BR>सिध्यति (सिध्, c. 4.) (=to suc-<BR>-ceed) or not expr.,<BR>it f. s from this that God is<BR>the source of all Śāstras:<BR>तस्मात् प्राप्तं लब्धं or<BR>सिद्धं ब्रह्मणः सर्वशास्त्रयोनित्वम्;<BR>because one man lives<BR>hundred years, it does not follow that every man<BR>will live hundred years:<BR>न हि शतायुः पुरुषो दृष्ट इति<BR> सर्वे शतायुषो भवन्ति (after S.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

follower
FOLLOWER:<BR>(1) अनुगामिन् (f. नी),<BR>women follow<BR>the way of their husbands:<BR>स्त्रियः पतिमार्गानुगामिन्यः,<BR>M.n.;<BR>(2) अनुयायिन् (f. नी),<BR>a body of f.s:<BR>अनुयायि-<BR>वर्गः, R. ii. 4.;<BR>(3) अनुसारिन् (f. णी),<BR>f.s of the<BR>doctrines of Jaimini:<BR>जैमिनिमतानुसारिणः, Va.;<BR>(4)<BR>अनुगः (गा, गं);<BR>(5) अनुसर (f. री) (= atten-<BR>-dant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

following
FOLLOWING (subs.):<BR>(1) अनुगमनम् (gen. lit.);<BR>(2) अनुसरणम्;<BR>(3) अनुवृत्तिः (fig.),<BR>f. of royal<BR>duties:<BR>राजधर्मानुवृत्तिः, Mu.;<BR>(4) अनुयानम् (rare):<BR>v. To follow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

following
FOLLOWING (adj.); i.e. next: q.v.: परः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

folly
FOLLY:<BR>(1) मूर्खता,<BR>oh, what sort of f. I<BR>have been:<BR>अहो मे मूर्खतायाः प्रकारः, K.;<BR>(2)<BR>मौर्ख्यम् (rare);<BR>(3) निर्बुद्धिता;<BR>(4) बुद्धिहीनता: v.<BR>Foolishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foment
FOMENT (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) उत्तापयति (c. of तप्)<BR>(?);<BR>(2) सेकं ददाति (दा, c. 3.)<BR>or<BR>दापयति (c. of<BR>दा),<BR>then girding it with a bandage, should f.<BR>with ghee:<BR>ततः पट्टेनसंवेष्ट्य घृतसेकं प्रदापयेत्, S. N.B.<BR>सिञ्चति<BR>or<BR>सेचयति, परि-, सं-, (सिच्, c. 2. and c.<BR>of सिच्), of Bha. as in उष्णैःसंसेचयेच्छोथम्, do not<BR>mean f. ing but sprinkling.<BR>II To encourage:<BR>q.v.: प्रोत्साहयति (c. of सह्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fomentation
FOMENTATION:<BR>I The act.:<BR>(1) उत्तापनम् (?);<BR>(2) सेकदानम्<BR>or<BR>सेकप्रदानम्।<BR>II The lotion: सेकः<BR>or<BR>परिषेकः।<BR>III Exertion: प्रोत्साहनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fomenter
FOMENTER:<BR>(1) प्रोत्साहकः;<BR>(2) उत्तेजकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fond
FOND:<BR>I Foolish: q.v.<BR>II Doting:<BR>(1)<BR>अनुरागवत् (f. ती),<BR>the old husband was very f. of<BR>her:<BR>स वृद्धपतिस्तस्यामतीवानुरागवान्, H.;<BR>(2) expr.<BR>by आसक्तः (क्ता, क्तं), रक्तः (क्ता, क्तं), etc., boys<BR>are f. of (lit. attached to)<BR>sports, young men<BR>of young women:<BR>बालस्तावत् क्रीडासक्तस्तरुणस्तावत्तरुणी-<BR>रक्तः, J.;<BR>(3) वत्सलः (ला, लं) (as a parent).<BR>III Liking: प्रियः (या, यं) in comp.s.,<BR>f. of<BR>wine:<BR>मद्यप्रियः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fondle
FONDLE (v.t.): लालयति (c. of लल्), should f.<BR>(a son for the first)<BR>five years:<BR>लालयेत् पञ्च-<BR>वर्षाणि, J.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fondling
FONDLING (subs.):<BR>I The act: लालनम्।<BR>II<BR>The object: प्रेमपात्रम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fondly
FONDLY:<BR>I Affectionately: सानुरागम्।<BR>II<BR>Foolishly: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fondness
FONDNESS:<BR>I Affection:<BR>(1) अनुरागः;<BR>(2)<BR>अनुरक्तिः;<BR>(3) रागः (rare), D.<BR>II Likeness:<BR>प्रियता in comp.,<BR>f. of wine:<BR>मद्यप्रियता।<BR>III<BR>Foolishness: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

font
FONT:<BR>I A fountain: q.v.<BR>II A basin:<BR>कुण्डम् (?).<BR>III Of types: *मुद्राक्षरमाला; मुद्राक्षर-<BR>जातम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

food
FOOD:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) आहारः (best equiv.),<BR>in<BR>giving me: f.:<BR>ममाहारदाने, H.;<BR>to take f.:<BR>आहारं<BR> करोति, Va.;<BR>we have to eat f. consisting chiefly<BR>of roasted meat:<BR>शूल्यमांसभूयिष्ठ आहारोऽश्यते, K.;<BR>(2) अन्नम् (used absol.),<BR>bad f.:<BR>कदन्नम्;<BR>the ways<BR>of preparing f.:<BR>अन्ननां साधनप्रकारः, Bha.;<BR>(3)<BR>आमिषम् (= animal f.): v. Meat;<BR>(4) भोजनम्<BR>(often=feeding), M.n.;<BR>(5) खाद्यम्: v. Eat-<BR>-able. Ph.:<BR>without taking f.:<BR>अनाहारेण or<BR>अनशनेन, K.;<BR>f.: and raiment:<BR>ग्रासाच्छादनम्, K.b.;<BR>forbidden f.:<BR>अभक्ष्यम्, V.s.<BR>II Fig.: आमिषम्,<BR>became the f. of the enemies:<BR>द्विषामामिषतां ययौ,<BR>R. xii. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fool
FOOL (subs.):<BR>(1) मूर्खः,<BR>there is no medicine for<BR>a f.:<BR>मूर्खस्य नास्त्यौषधम्, J.;<BR>(2) निर्बुद्धिः<BR>or<BR>अबुद्धिः,<BR>what has been done by me a f.:<BR>किं मया कृतमबुद्धिना,<BR>Mah.;<BR>(3) अविद्वान्,<BR>f. s bow down to fate:<BR>दैवम-<BR>विद्वांसः प्रमाणयन्ति, Mu. Ph.: to make a f. of:<BR>अवहासास्पदं करोति;<BR>to play the f.:<BR>मूर्खवद् व्यवहरति<BR>(हृ, c. 1.);<BR>f.'s errand:<BR>मूर्खचेष्टितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fool
FOOL (v.t.): मोहयति, वि-, व्या-, (c. of मुह्): v.<BR>To delude, deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foolery
FOOLERY: मूर्खता (of the behaviour and of<BR>acts of folly), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fool-hardiness
FOOL-HARDINESS:<BR>(1) अतिसाहसिकत्वम्;<BR>(2) व्यामोहः<BR>(= madness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fool-hardy
FOOL-HARDY: अतिसाहसिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) प्रमत्तः<BR>(त्ता, त्तं) (= mad).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foolish
FOOLISH:<BR>I Silly: मूढः (ढा, ढं),<BR>f. (men) are<BR>troubled with passion:<BR>मूढो मदनेनायास्यते, K.: v.<BR>Also unwise.<BR>II Of acts, etc.:<BR>(1) वालिशः<BR>(शा, शं) (=children), attachment to f. acts:<BR>वालिशचरितेष्वासक्तिः, K.;<BR>(2) निरर्थकः (का, कं)<BR>(= useless: q.v.).<BR>III Ridiculous: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foolishly
FOOLISHLY:<BR>(1) मूढतया<BR>or<BR>मौढ्यात् (rare), V.p.<BR>v. 30. 4.;<BR>(2) दुर्बुद्धिक्रमेण;<BR>(3) अझानतः (= not<BR>knowing);<BR>(4) निरर्थकम् (=uselessly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foolishness
FOOLISHNESS:<BR>(1) मूढता;<BR>(2) वालिशता;<BR>(3)<BR>दुर्बुद्धिता: v. Foolly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foolscap
FOOLSCAP: *पुरस्कम्, पुरस्कपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foot
FOOT (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पादः,<BR>without hand<BR>and f.:<BR>अपाणिपादः (दा, दं). S.; to go on f.:<BR>पद्भ्यां (or पादचारेण A.r.) गच्छतिः Mr.;<BR>water<BR>for cleaning the feet:<BR>पाद्यम्;<BR>water in which feet<BR>have been washed:<BR>पादोदकम्;<BR>(2) चरण (mn.);<BR>(3) पदम्;<BR>(4) अंघ्निः।<BR>II Fig.: पादः,<BR>from its<BR>f. rises the lake named Hill-water:<BR>तस्य पादात् [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">Page289</a>]<BR>प्रभवति शैलोदं नाम तत्सरः, Mat.: v. Bottom.<BR>III<BR>Of a stool etc.: पादः<BR>or<BR>पदम्।<BR>IV Metrical<BR>f.:<BR>(1) चरण (mn.),<BR>a Gāyatri f. consists of six<BR>syllables:<BR>षडक्षरो गायत्रीचरणः, Li.;<BR>(2) पादः;<BR>(3) पदम्। V. A measure: expr. by हस्तः<BR>(= cubit),<BR>three f. in length:<BR>त्रिहस्तदीर्घः (र्घा,<BR> र्घं).<BR>VI Infantry:<BR>(1) पत्तिः;<BR>(2) पदातिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foot
FOOT (v.):<BR>I To tread: q.v.<BR>II To kick:<BR>q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foot
FOOT, SET ON: प्रवर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foot-ball
FOOT-BALL पादाहतकण्डुकक्रीडा; पादकण्डुकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foot-bath
FOOT-BATH:<BR>I The act: पादमज्जनम्।<BR>II The<BR>vessel: पादद्रोणी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foot-board
FOOT-BOARD: पादफलकम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foot-boy
FOOT-BOY: चेटः: v. Menial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foot-bridge
FOOT-BRIDGE: सङ्क्रमः, all the f.s were broken:<BR>सङ्क्रमा भेदिताः सर्वे, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

footed
FOOTED (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: expr. by comp.,<BR>two-f.:<BR>द्विपदः (दा, दं);<BR>f. like the goat:<BR>अजपादः<BR>(दा, दं).<BR>II Established: बद्धमूलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foot-fall
FOOT-FALL:<BR>I Foot-step: q.v.<BR>II A trip:<BR>स्खलनम्, पाद-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foot-fight
FOOT-FIGHT:<BR>(1) पादचारयुद्धम् (after U.);<BR>(2)<BR>नियुद्धम् (gen. f.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foot-guards
FOOT-GUARDS: रक्षाधिकृताः पदातयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foothold
FOOTHOLD: v. Footing (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

footing
FOOTING:<BR>I Ground: q.v.: स्थानम्।<BR>II Firm<BR>position:<BR>(1) स्थितिः;<BR>(2) better by adj.:<BR>बद्धमूलः (ला, लं).<BR>III Condition: q.v.:<BR>वृत्तिः।<BR>IV Footstep: q.v.<BR>V Sum: फलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

footless
FOOTLESS:<BR>(1) निष्पादः (दा, दं);<BR>(2) चरणहीनः<BR>(ना, नं); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foot-licker
FOOT-LICKER:<BR>(1) चरणसेविन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) पादलिह्<BR>(mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

footman
FOOTMAN:<BR>I A soldier: पदातिः।<BR>II A<BR>menial: चेटः।<BR>III A runner: जङ्घाकरिकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

footmark
FOOTMARK, FOOT-PRINT:<BR>(1) पदवी, Ki. v.<BR>40.;<BR>(2) पद्धतिः, H. ii.;<BR>(3) पादचिह्नम् and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

footpath
FOOTPATH:<BR>(1) संसरणम्, Vri.;<BR>(2) गोवाटः<BR>(= cattle-path).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foot-soldier
FOOT-SOLDIER:<BR>(1) पदातिः;<BR>(2) पत्तिः, Ku.<BR>xvi. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

footstep
FOOTSTEP:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पदविक्षेपः;<BR>(2) पादन्यासः;<BR>(3) चरणपातः; and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Foot-<BR>-print: q.v.: पदम्,<BR>by rows of wet f.s.:<BR>आर्द्रपद-<BR>पंक्तिभिः, R. ix. 59.<BR>III Token, mark: q.v.:<BR>लक्षणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

footstool
FOOTSTOOL: पादपीठम्, Ku. iii. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fop
FOP: सुभगमानिन् (m.); सुन्दरम्मन्यः; वेषाभिमानिन्<BR>(m.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foppery
FOPPERY:<BR>I Lit.: सुभगमानिता; वेषाभिमानः (?).<BR>II Folly: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foppish
FOPPISH, FOPPISHNESS: v. Fop, foppery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

for
FOR (prep.):<BR>I Denoting cause or occasion:<BR>(1) by abl.,<BR>f. want of combustibles:<BR>दाह्याभावात्,<BR>Mu. i. 11.; tied for hundred (rupees): शताद्बद्धः,<BR>S.k.;<BR>(2) by ins,<BR>is any one respected simply<BR>f. his caste:<BR>किं जातिमात्रेण कश्चित्पूज्यते, H. i.;<BR>f.<BR>what reason:<BR>केन हेतुना: v. Why. N.B. Use<BR>the ins. when the Sanskrit subs., which f.<BR>governs, is feminine.<BR>II Denoting object<BR>or end:<BR>(1) by dat.,<BR>f. appeasing the fears<BR>of the distressed:<BR>आर्तभयोपशान्तये, R. viii. 31.;<BR>(2) अर्थं<BR>or<BR>अर्थे in comp.,<BR>f. amusing you:<BR>त्बद्विनोद-<BR>नार्थभ्, U. i.;<BR>(3) by loc. (only in some cases),<BR>kill elephants f. their tusks:<BR>दन्तयोर्हन्ति कुञ्जरम्,<BR>S.k.<BR>III For the sake of:<BR>(1) by अर्थं or<BR>अर्थे in comp.,<BR>f. me:<BR>मदर्थम्, N. i. 137.;<BR>(2)<BR>कृते (with gen.), f. the Śūdra (Chandragupta):<BR>वृषलस्य कृते, Mu. i.;<BR>(3) अपेक्ष्य (with acc.) or<BR>अपेक्षया in comp.,<BR>f. me he should be released<BR>with his wife and brothers:<BR>मदपेक्षया सकलत्रसोदर्यो<BR> मोचयितव्यः, Mal. i.<BR>IV=towards: प्रति (with<BR>acc.),<BR>“for China”:<BR>चीनं प्रति।<BR>V =as for:<BR>q.v. =in spite of:<BR>f. all of them:<BR>तिष्ठत्सु तेषु<BR>or<BR>ताननादृत्य।<BR>VII In the character for:<BR>do<BR>not take him f. a friend:<BR>मा तं बन्धुरिति परिगृहाण or<BR>बन्धुमवगच्छ।<BR>VIII Instead of: q.v. प्रति<BR>(with abl.) (?),<BR>give dal for sesame:<BR>तिलेभ्यः प्रति-<BR>यच्छति माषान्, S.k.<BR>IX Of time through<BR>which an action extends by acc.,<BR>for ten<BR>days:<BR>दशाहम्, Vas.;<BR>f. one or two nights:<BR>एकरात्रं<BR> द्विरात्रं वा;<BR>f. twelve months:<BR>द्वादशमासान्, Vat.;<BR>f. so many years:<BR>तावन्ति वर्षाणि, Sam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

for
FOR (conj.):<BR>(1) हि (never at the beginning [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">Page290</a>]<BR>of a sentence),<BR>f. you know the internal (senti-<BR>ments) of animals:<BR>अन्तर्गतं प्राणभृतां हि वेद, R. ii.<BR>43.; f. it is not easy to break the meditations of<BR>great (men): न हि महतां सुकरः समाधिभङ्गः, Ki. x.<BR>23. N.B. Note the cons. of न हि (= f......<BR>not;<BR>(2) यतः<BR>or<BR>यस्मात्,<BR>f. association of good<BR>men......<BR>यतः सतां सङ्गतं॥॥, Ku. v. 39.: v.<BR>Because. Ph.:<BR>f. why:<BR>कस्मात्, किंनिमित्तम्,<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forage
FORAGE (subs.):<BR>I Search for food: धान्याद्या-<BR>हरणम्।<BR>II Fodder: यवसः,<BR>in a place where<BR>water and f. are easily procurable:<BR>सुलभपयोयवसे<BR> प्रदेशे, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forage
FORAGE (v.): prob. प्रसारं करोति, Si. ii. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forager
FORAGER: प्रसारकारिन् (m.) (?); धान्याद्याहर्तृ (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foraging
FORAGING (subs.): प्रसारः (?); धान्याद्याहरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forasmuch
FORASMUCH:<BR>(1) यतः;<BR>(2) यस्मात्: v. Since.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forbear
FORBEAR:<BR>I To desist, abstain from: q.v.:<BR>निवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.)<BR>II To bear with:<BR>(1)<BR>सहते (सह्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) क्षमते, (क्षम्, c. 1.).<BR>III To refuse: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forbearance
FORBEARANCE:<BR>(1) क्षमा;<BR>(2) तितिक्षा,<BR>there is<BR>no instrument like f.:<BR>न तितिक्षासममस्ति साधनम, Ki.<BR>ii. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forbid
FORBID: निषेधति, प्रति-, (सिध्, c. 1.),<BR>even the<BR>remaining followers were f. den:<BR>न्यषेधि शेषोऽप्यनु-<BR>यायिवर्गः, R. ii. 4.;<BR>f. den commodities:<BR>प्रतिषिद्धानि<BR> भाण्डानि, M.;<BR>to whom even residence in the<BR>country has been f. den:<BR>यस्य देशेऽप्यवस्थानं निषिद्धम्,<BR>Cha. Ph.:<BR>God f. that I should be the king<BR>while you are alive:<BR>अहं क्षितीन्द्रस्त्वयि स्थिते स्यामिति<BR> शान्तमेतत्, B. iii. 55.;<BR>God f. such an evil:<BR>शान्तं<BR> पापं प्रतिहतमङ्गलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forbidding
FORBIDDING (p. adj.): v. Disagreeable, odi-<BR>-ous, repulsive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

force
FORCE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) बलम्,<BR>the mount<BR>Kailāsa (knows my) f.:<BR>बलं कैलासाद्रिः, Vi.:<BR>every act done by f.<BR>सर्वान् बलकृतानर्थान्, M.;<BR>then<BR>tell (their) f. and weakness:<BR>तदाख्यात बलाबले, N.<BR>xvii. 44.;<BR>(2) शक्तिः,<BR>weakness of f.:<BR>शक्तिवैकल्यम्,<BR>Ku.;<BR>(3) सामर्थ्यम्,<BR>f. of language:<BR>गिरां सामर्थ्यम्,<BR>Ki. ii. 27.: v. Strength.<BR>To be in f.:<BR>बलवत्।<BR>(f. ती) भवति।<BR>II Military: बलम्, f. s heroic:<BR>बलानि शूराणि, Si. i. 45.; that unmeasurable f.:<BR>तदपरिमितं बलम्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

force
FORCE (v.):<BR>I To compel: q.v.: बलात् or<BR>बलेन कारयति (c. of कृ).<BR>II To ravish: बलात्<BR> करोति।<BR>III<BR>To take by f., storm:<BR>बलात् गृह्णाति,<BR>(ग्रह्, c. 9.).<BR>IV To garrison: q.v. Ph.:<BR>to f. a passage:<BR>मार्गं साधयति (c. of सिध्), Vi.<BR>vi.; f. d (fruit, wine, etc.): *त्वरितकारितः (ता,<BR> तं), Comp.s:<BR>f. down:<BR>अधः प्रेरयति (c. of ईर्)<BR>etc.:<BR>f. from or out:<BR>निष्कर्षति (कृष्): v. To<BR>extort:<BR>f. on or upon:<BR>बलात् कारयति<BR>or<BR>योजयति<BR>(c. of युज्);<BR>f. up:<BR>प्रचोदयति (c. of चुद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forced
FORCED (adj.):<BR>I Artificial: q.v.: कृत्रिमः<BR>(मा, मं).<BR>II Effected by labour: यत्नसाधितः<BR>(ता, तं). For other senses: v. Force. (V.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

force-meat
FORCE-MEAT: अवच्छिन्नमांसम्, and sim. comp.s.<BR>(?.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forceps
FORCEPS:<BR>(1) संदंशः;<BR>(2) कङ्कमुखः;<BR>(3) खण्डधारा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forcible
FORCIBLE:<BR>I In gen.<BR>(1) बलवत् (f. ती);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रबलः (ला, लं);<BR>(3) सबलः (ला, लं);<BR>(4)<BR>शक्तिमत् (f. ती);<BR>(5) समर्थः (र्था, र्थं);<BR>(6)<BR>वीर्यवत् (f. तां): v. Also strong, weighty.<BR>II<BR>Effected by force: बलकृतः (ता, तं), M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forcibly
FORCIBLY:<BR>(1) बलात्;<BR>(2) प्रसमम्, Ki. ii. 28.;<BR>(3) प्रसह्य, R. ii. 27.;<BR>(4) हठात्, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ford
FORD (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: सुप्रतरस्थलम्।<BR>II A<BR>current: स्रोतस् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ford
FORD (v.t.): पद्भ्यां तरति (तॄ, c. 1.),<BR>to f. on<BR>horseback:<BR>हयेन तरति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fordable
FORDABLE:<BR>(1) सुतरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) सुप्रतरः (रा,<BR> रं), R. iv. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore
FORE (adj.):<BR>(1) अग्रः (ग्रा, ग्रं),<BR>f. part:<BR>अग्रभागः;<BR>(2) पूर्वः (र्वा, र्वं) (= upper).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore
FORE (adv.): अग्रतः,<BR>f. and aft.:<BR>अग्रपश्चात्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore-arm
FORE-ARM (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रकोष्ठः;<BR>(2) अग्रबाहुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore-arm
FORE-ARM (v.):<BR>(1) पूर्वमेव<BR>or<BR>प्रागेव सन्नह्यति (नह्,<BR>c. 4.): v. To arm;<BR>(2) सज्जीमवति (=to<BR>prepare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forebode
FOREBODE:<BR>(1) सूचयति, वि-, आ-, (सूच्, c. 10.)<BR>(= to indicate),<BR>this omen is good-f. ing:<BR>कल्याण-<BR>सूचकमिदं निमित्तम्, Sa. i.;<BR>(2) कथयति (= to tell),<BR>f. s terrible death:<BR>कथयति महाघोरं मृत्युम्, Mr. ix.:<BR>v. To bespeak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foreboding
FOREBODING (subs.): by verb: v. Also augury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forecast
FORECAST (v.):<BR>I To project: कल्पयति (कॢप्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR>II To foresee: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forecast
FORECAST (subs.):<BR>I Contrivance: कल्पना।<BR>II Prevision: समीक्षा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forecastle
FORECASTLE: *अग्रकोष्ठः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foreclosure
FORECLOSURE: बन्ध (-क) मोक्षप्रतिषेधः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore-deck
FORE-DECK: *अग्रच्छदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore-end
FORE-END:<BR>(1) पूर्वान्तः (?);<BR>(2) अग्रोपान्तः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore-fathers
FORE-FATHERS:<BR>(1) पूर्वजाः (m. pl.);<BR>(2) पूर्व-<BR>पुरुषाः;<BR>(3) पूर्वा, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forefend
FOREFEND: निवारयति (वृ, c. 10.): v. To forbid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore-finger
FORE-FINGER:<BR>(1) तर्जनी;<BR>(2) प्रदेशिनी। N.B. With<BR>or without अङ्गुली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore-foot
FORE-FOOT:<BR>(1) अग्रपादः;<BR>(2) पूर्वचरणम्, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forego
FOREGO: जहाति (हा, c. 3.): v. To relin-<BR>-quish, renounce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foregoing
FOREGOING: i.e. preceding: अतिक्रान्तः (न्ता,<BR> न्तं), S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foregone
FOREGONE: Ph.:<BR>f. conclusion:<BR>पूर्वकल्पितनिगमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foreground
FOREGROUND: अग्रभूमिः, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forehead
FOREHEAD:<BR>(1) ललाटम्,<BR>whatever is written by<BR>God on one's f.:<BR>यस्येश्वरेण यदलेखि ललाटपट्टे, N.;<BR>(2) भालम् (rare). Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foreign
FOREIGN:<BR>I Of another country:<BR>(1) by<BR>comp.,<BR>f. commodities:<BR>परदेशपण्याः, V. s.;<BR>(2)<BR>विदेशीयः (या, यं);<BR>(3) वैदेशिकः (की, कं),<BR>f.<BR>merchant:<BR>वैदेशिकवणिक्, D. i.;<BR>(4) देशान्तरीयः<BR>(या, यं), K. b.;<BR>(5) विदेशजः (जा, जं), etc.<BR>(= produced in a f. country);<BR>(6) परदेश्यः<BR>(f. श्या) (rare), Y. Ph.: f. country:<BR>(1) विदेशः;<BR>(2) देशान्तरम्;<BR>(3) परदेशः।<BR>II Extraneous,<BR>irrelevant: बाह्य (f. ह्या),<BR>f. matters:<BR>बाह्य-<BR>वस्तूनि (?);<BR>it is f. to my purpose......<BR>मदभि-<BR>प्रेतबाह्य (f. ह्या) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foreigner
FOREIGNER:<BR>(1) वैदेशिकः (की, कं), as I am a f.:<BR>वैदेशिकोऽस्मीति, U. i.;<BR>(2) विदेशिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) पारदेशिकः (की, कं) (rare): v. Stranger,<BR>new comer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore-know
FORE-KNOW: प्रगेव जानातिः v. To know,<BR>beforehand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore-knowledge
FORE-KNOWLEDGE: अग्रझानम् (?); भविष्यद्विझानम्;<BR> अनागतझानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foreland
FORELAND: *प्रलम्बम्: v. Promontory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forelock
FORELOCK:<BR>(1) अग्रकेशाः (m. pl.);<BR>(2) अग्रशिखा।<BR>Ph.:<BR>to take time or occasion by the f.:<BR>*विनाति-<BR>पातं कालं<BR>or<BR>अवसरं गृह्णाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foreman
FOREMAN:<BR>(1) प्रधानः,<BR>f. of a fury:<BR>सभ्यप्रधानः।<BR>v. Chief;<BR>(2) नायकः (= leader).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foremast
FOREMAST:<BR>(1) अग्रकूपकः;<BR>(2) अग्रस्थो गुणवृक्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foremost
FOREMOST:<BR>I Chief: q.v.:<BR>(1) मुख्य (f. ख्या);<BR>(2) प्रधानतमः (मा, मं).<BR>II First: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore-noon
FORE-NOON (subs.):<BR>(1) पूर्वाह्लः;<BR>(2) प्राह्णः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore-noon
FORE-NOON (adj.):<BR>(1) पूर्वाह्णेतनः (नी, नं);<BR>(2)<BR>प्राह्णेतनः (नी, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forensical
FORENSICAL: expr. by comp., f. medicine:<BR>व्यवहारचिकित्सा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore-ordain
FORE-ORDAIN: पूर्वं निर्दिशति (दिश्, c. 6.): v.<BR>To ordain, beforehand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forepart
FOREPART:<BR>(1) अग्रभागः;<BR>(2) अग्रिमभागः;<BR>(3)<BR>पूर्वभागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore-quarter
FORE-QUARTER of an animal: अग्रपादः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore-runner
FORE-RUNNER:<BR>(1) पूरोगः, -गामिन् (m.);<BR>(2)<BR>पुरःसरः;<BR>(3) अग्रेसरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foresee
FORESEE:<BR>(1) पश्यति, प्र-, (दृश्, c. 1.) (when<BR>the sense is clear),<BR>old man's intellect f.s the<BR>future:<BR>वृद्धबुद्धिरनागतं पश्यति, Vi. vi.: v. To see;<BR>(2) expr. with words meaning future,<BR>I<BR>f. death:<BR>मम भावि मरणं पश्यामि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fore-seeing
FORE-SEEING (adj.): भविष्यद्दर्शिन् (f. नी); भविष्यत्-<BR>प्रेक्षिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foreshadow
FORESHADOW: पूर्वम्<BR>or<BR>प्राक्<BR>or<BR>अग्रे रूपयति (रूप्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foreshorten
FORESHORTEN:<BR>I Lit.: अग्रं संहरति (हृ, c. 1.)<BR>(??).<BR>II Fig.: संहरति (हृ, c. 1.). v. To<BR>shorten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foreshortening
FORESHORTENING (subs.): अग्रसंहारः, वक्रचित्रितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foreshow
FORESHOW:<BR>(1) सूचयति (सूच्, c. 10.) (= to<BR>indicate);<BR>(2) कथयति (कथ्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>bespeak;<BR>(3) प्रदर्शयति (c. of दृश्): v. To<BR>show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foresight
FORESIGHT:<BR>I Lit.: भविष्यद्दर्शनम् (?).<BR>II In<BR>gen.;<BR>(1) दूरदर्शिता, (?), दीर्घदर्शिता, Ka. viii. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foreskin
FORESKIN: (पुरुषाङ्गस्य) उपरिगतचर्मन् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forest
FOREST:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) वनम् (also=a park);<BR>(2)<BR>अरण्यम्;<BR>(3) विपिनम्;<BR>(4) काननम्;<BR>(5) अटवी;<BR>(6) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">Page292</a>]<BR>गहनम् (= thicket).<BR>II Adj.:<BR>(1) expr. by<BR>tat. comp.:<BR>a f. tree:<BR>वनपादपः;<BR>(2) वन्यः (न्या,<BR> न्यं);<BR>(3) आरण्यक (f. का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forestall
FORESTALL:<BR>I To anticipate: q.v.<BR>II To<BR>obstruct: q.v.<BR>III To f. a market: मूल्य-<BR>वर्धनाय द्रव्याणि पूर्वं क्रीणाति (क्री, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forestaller
FORESTALLER: मूल्यवर्धनाय पूर्वक्रेतृ (m.); *पण्यरोधकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forester
FORESTER:<BR>I Inhabitant of a forest:<BR>(1)<BR>वनेचरः;<BR>(2) वनेसद्- (m.);<BR>(3) वनवासिन् (m.);<BR>(4) आरण्यकः;<BR>(5) आटविकः, H.; and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Keeper of a forest: बनपालः, N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foretaste
FORETASTE:<BR>I Subs.: पूर्वस्वादः: v. Taste.<BR>II<BR>Verb: पूर्वम्<BR>or<BR>प्राक् स्वादयति (c. of स्वद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foretell
FORETELL: अनागतं वदति (वद्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>predict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foreteller
FORETELLER: भविष्यद्वक्तृ (m.): v. Prophet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forethought
FORETHOUGHT:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by verb,<BR>having<BR>f. of his own end:<BR>भाविनमन्तमात्मनो जानन्नपि, Si.<BR>II Prudence: समीक्षा, प्र-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foretoken
FORETOKEN: सूचयति (सूच्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>forebode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foretop-mast
FORETOP-MAST: *अग्रमञ्चकूपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forewarn
FOREWARN, FOREWARNING: v. Warn; warn-<BR>-ing, beforehand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forewoman
FOREWOMAN:<BR>(1) प्रधाना;<BR>(2) नायिका: v. Fore-<BR>-man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forfeit
FORFEIT (subs.): दण्डः: v. Penalty, fine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forfeit
FORFEIT (v.):<BR>(1) दण्डम् अधिगच्छति (गम्, c. 1.)<BR>v. Punishment;<BR>(2) हारयति (c. of हृ) v. To<BR>lose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forfeited
FORFEITED (adj.): no exact equiv.: दण्डितः<BR>(ता, तं) (= punished, fined): v. Also to<BR>escheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forfeiture
FORFEITURE:<BR>I The act: expr. by दण्डः or<BR>हानिः (= loss).<BR>II Anything forfeited:<BR>प्रमादाद्देयो दण्डः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forge
FORGE (subs.):<BR>(1) कुटिलिका, Wilson;<BR>(2)<BR>उद्ध्मानम् (gen. term).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forge
FORGE (v.t.):<BR>I To form, effect: q.v.:<BR>घटयति (c. of घट्).<BR>II To fabricate, expr.<BR>with कपट<BR>or<BR>कूट,<BR>to f. a grant:<BR>कूटशासनं करोति;<BR>to<BR>use a f.d letter:<BR>कपटलेखं प्रयुंक्ते: v. Counterfeit,<BR>false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forger
FORGER: कूटकारः, -कः; कूटकृत् (m.); कपटलेखादिकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forgery
FORGERY:<BR>I The crime: कूटकरणम् (?),<BR>f. of a<BR>document:<BR>कपटलेखकरणम्।<BR>II Anything forged:<BR>expr. by कौटः (टी, टं)<BR>or<BR>कौटिकः (की, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forget
FORGET:<BR>(1) विस्मरति (स्मृ, c. 1.), who f. s wrongs:<BR>योऽपकृतं विस्मरति, Mr. ii.;<BR>(2) न स्मरति,<BR>who f.s<BR>his mother land:<BR>केन जन्मभूमिर्न स्मर्यते, V.p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forgetful
FORGETFUL:<BR>(1) विस्मरणशीलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2)<BR>स्वल्पस्मृति (mfn.), Mr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forgetfulness
FORGETFULNESS:<BR>(1) विस्मृतिः;<BR>(2) विस्मरणम्;<BR>(3)<BR>अस्मरणम्;<BR>(4) स्मृतिलोपः, Sa. and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forgive
FORGIVE:<BR>(1) क्षमते<BR>or<BR>क्षाम्यति (क्षम्, c. l. and 4.),<BR>Śātānanda will not so easily f.:<BR>न त्वेवं शतनन्दः<BR> क्षमिष्यते, Vi. iii.;<BR>(2) तितिक्षते (तितिक्ष्, c. 1.),<BR>please f. my misbehaviour:<BR>तितिक्षतुं दुश्चरितं त्वमर्हसि,<BR>Ki. xviii. 42.;<BR>(3) मर्षयति<BR>or<BR>मृष्यति (मृष्, c. 10.<BR>and 4.),<BR>you should f. this fault:<BR>अयमपराधो भवता<BR> मर्षयितव्यः, Sa. iv.;<BR>(4) सहते (सह्, c. 1.),<BR>I<BR>will then f. this fault:<BR>अपराधिममं ततः सहिष्ये, Sa.<BR>iii. N.B. Only क्षम् can take an acc. of the<BR>person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forgiveness
FORGIVENESS:<BR>(1) क्षमा;<BR>(2) तितिक्षा;<BR>(3) सहिष्णुता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forgiving
FORGIVING (adj.):<BR>(1) क्षमिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) क्षमावत्<BR>(f. ती);<BR>(3) तितिक्षु (mfn.);<BR>(4) सहिष्णु (mfn.)<BR>(= bearing up);<BR>(5) कृपालु (mfn.) (=merci-<BR>-ful).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fork
FORK (subs): *कण्टकः,<BR>three pronged f.:<BR>*त्रिमुख-<BR>कण्टकः; चतुर्दन्तकण्टकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forked
FORKED (adj.): द्विमुखः (खा, खं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forlorn
FORLORN:<BR>I Deserted: त्यक्तः (क्ता, क्तं).<BR>II<BR>Miserable, helpless:<BR>(1) दीनः (ना, नं)<BR>(= wretched);<BR>(1) हतः (ता, तं) (=done for),<BR>in this f. life:<BR>हतजीवितेऽस्मिन्, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

form
FORM (subs.):<BR>I Shape:<BR>(1) रूपम्,<BR>assuming a<BR>f. at pleasure:<BR>कामरूपिन् (f. णी), Ram;<BR>like in<BR>f. and quality:<BR>रूपस्य गुणस्य च सदृशः (शी, शं), Mr.<BR>ix. 33.;<BR>(2) आकारः<BR>or<BR>आकृतिः (gen.=features),<BR>external f.:<BR>बहिराकारः, M.n.;<BR>(3) मूर्तिः (= entire<BR>f.),<BR>assuming dwarfish f. to deceive:<BR>विधाय मूर्तिं<BR> कपटेन वामनीम्, N.: v. Body.<BR>II Shapeliness,<BR>beauty: रूपम्।<BR>III Appearance: आकारः। Ph.<BR>in due f.:<BR>यथाविधि;<BR>f. of prayer:<BR>स्तोत्रसूत्रम् (?).<BR>IV<BR>system, kind: q.v.:<BR>f. of Government:<BR>राजतन्त्रम्। [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">Page293</a>]<BR>V. A bench: q.v.<BR>VI A hare's seat:<BR>निलयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

form
FORM (v.t.):<BR>I To construct:<BR>(1) निर्मिमीते<BR>(मा, c. 3.),<BR>to f. this charming f.:<BR>मनोहरमिदं रूपं<BR> निर्मातुम्, V.i.;<BR>(2) घटयति (घट्, c. 10.)<BR>f. ed of<BR>thread:<BR>तन्तुघटितः (ता, तं). V. d.;<BR>(3) विदधाति<BR>(धा, c. 3.), Ki. vi. 42.: v. To make.<BR>II<BR>To enter upon:<BR>(1) घटयति,<BR>better not to f.<BR>affection:<BR>स्नेहो हि वरमघटितः, Bho.;<BR>(2) विदधाति,<BR>f. ing friendship:<BR>विधाय मैत्रीम्, Si.<BR>III To con-<BR>-ceive: q.v.: कल्पयति (कॢप्, c. 10.).<BR>IV To<BR>train: संस्करोति,<BR>f. ed mind:<BR>संस्कृतमनस्।<BR>V To<BR>constitute: मवति,<BR>they f. ed the majority:<BR>*ते<BR> बहवो बभूवुः।<BR>VI To derive: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

formal
FORMAL:<BR>I Essential: सार- in comp.<BR>II<BR>Done in due from: expr. with adv.s: यथा-<BR>विधि<BR>or<BR>आचारानुसारेण।<BR>III Of men: आचारानुगतः<BR>(ता, तं) (?).<BR>IV Not real: बाह्यिकः (की, कं),<BR>बाह्याचारतः।<BR>V Of form: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

formalist
FORMALIST: कपटधर्मकञ्चुकः, D. i.; बाह्यधर्मसेविन् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

formality
FORMALITY:<BR>I A formal ceremony: आचारः<BR>or<BR>उपचारः।<BR>II Of manners:<BR>(1) अत्यादरः,<BR>leave off this f.:<BR>विमुच्यतामयमत्यादरः, K.;<BR>(2)<BR>उपचारः, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

formally
FORMALLY:<BR>I With due ceremony: यथोपचारम्।<BR>II Of behaviour: अत्यादरेण; सोपचारम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

formation
FORMATION:<BR>(1) घटना;<BR>(2) निर्माणम्;<BR>(3) कल्पना;<BR>(4) विधानम्; for dif. of meaning: v. To form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

former
FORMER (adj.):<BR>(1) पूर्वः (र्वा, र्वं),<BR>and by the f.<BR>kings:<BR>पूर्वराजैश्च, D. iv.;<BR>(2) प्राक्तनः (नी, नं);<BR>v. Ancient. F......latter:<BR>(1) पूर्वः (र्वा,<BR> र्वं), उत्तरः (रा, रं),<BR>the f. course was avoided as<BR>what favour would please (them); the latter was<BR>also avoided as by severe punishment we would<BR>lose the confidence of the subjects.....<BR>कीदृशो-<BR>ऽनुग्रहः प्रीतिं जनयिष्यतीति परिहृतः पूर्वः पक्षः उत्तरो-<BR>प्युग्रेण दण्डेन प्रकृतीनामविश्वास्या मवाम इति परिहृत<BR> एव, Mu. iii.;<BR>(2) प्रथमः (मा, मं) (= first)....<BR>अपरः (रा, रं) (= after), R. viii. 28.;<BR>(3)<BR>आद्यः (द्या, द्यं) (= first)...... द्वितीयः (या, यं)<BR>(= second), D.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

formerly
FORMERLY:<BR>(1) पुरा, where we f. lived long:<BR>यस्मिन्नभूम चिरमेव पुरा वसन्तः,<BR>V i. 22.;<BR>(2) पूर्वम्,<BR>f. seen:<BR>पूर्वदृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>(3) पूर्वकाले;<BR>(4)<BR>प्राक्काले।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

formidable
FORMIDABLE:<BR>(1) महत् (f. ती) (= great);<BR>(2)<BR>भयावहः (हा, हं): v. Fearful;<BR>(3) उद्वेगकरः (री,<BR> रं) (= alarming);<BR>(4) दारूण (f. णा) (=terrible),<BR>f. enemy:<BR>दारुणः शत्रुः, Ka. viii. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

formidableness
FORMIDABLENESS:<BR>(1) भीषणत्वम्;<BR>(2) उद्वेगकरत्वम्;<BR>(3) better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

formidably
FORMIDABLY:<BR>(1) भीषणम्;<BR>(2) दारुणम्;<BR>(3) भयं<BR> जनयत् (f. न्ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

formless
FORMLESS:<BR>(1) अरूपः (पा, पं);<BR>(2) निराकारः<BR>(रा, रं);<BR>(3) नीरूपः (पा, पं) etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

formula
FORMULA: सूत्रम्; पाठः,<BR>“f. of will”:<BR>*इच्छापत्रपाठः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

formulary
FORMULARY: a book of form: *सूत्रग्रन्थः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fornicate
FORNICATE: व्यभिचरति (चर्, c. 2.); व्यभिचारं<BR> करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fornication
FORNICATION: व्यभिचारः: v. Debauchery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fornicatory
FORNICATORY: व्यभिचारिन् (m.): v. Debau-<BR>-chee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forsake
FORSAKE: त्यजति, परि-, सं-, (त्यज्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forsaking
FORSAKING (subs.): त्यागः, परि-। v. Abandon-<BR>-ment, desertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forsooth
FORSOOTH: v. Indeed, truly, of course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forswear
FORSWEAR:<BR>I To abjure: q.v.<BR>II Perjure:<BR>q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fort
FORT:<BR>(1) दुर्गम्,<BR>governor of a f.:<BR>दुर्गाधिकारिन्, H.;<BR>mountainous f.:<BR>गिरिदुर्गम्, N.;<BR>(2) कोटः<BR>or<BR>कोट्टः<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forte
FORTE: बलम् (= force).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forth
FORTH:<BR>I Of time: Ph.: from this day f.:<BR>अद्यप्रभृति;<BR>from that time f.:<BR>तदाप्रभृति।<BR>II Of<BR>place: बहिः v. Out and the verbs to<BR>which f. is joined,<BR>III Of succession: Ph.:<BR>and so f.:<BR>इत्यादि (mfn.) (always agreeing<BR>with a subs. gen. expressed and sometimes<BR>understood: see U. iii. 26).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forthcoming
FORTHCOMING: आसन्नप्रकाशः (शा, शं): v. Also<BR>coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forthwith
FORTHWITH:<BR>(1) सपदि;<BR>(2) भ्कटिति;<BR>(3) द्राक्:<BR>v. Immediately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fortieth
FORTIETH:<BR>(1) चत्वारिंशः (शा, शं);<BR>(2) चत्वारिं-<BR>शत्तमः (मी, मं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fortification
FORTIFICATION:<BR>I The works:<BR>(1) गुप्तिः<BR>(= defences), the f.s are most inaccessible:<BR>अलङ्घ्यतमा गुप्तिः, D.;<BR>(2) दुर्गम् (= fort),<BR>f. s naturally<BR>strong:<BR>प्रकृत्या विषमं दुर्गम्, Mah.;<BR>(3) प्राकारपरिखादि<BR>(n.).<BR>II The operation: गुप्तिः; दुर्गकर्मन् (n.),<BR>Mah. s. 86. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fortifier
FORTIFIER: expr. by verb,<BR>f. of a town:<BR>नगर-<BR>गुप्तिकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fortify
FORTIFY (v.):<BR>I In gen.: v. To strengthen,<BR>confirm.<BR>II To render defensible:<BR>(1)<BR>सुगुप्त (f. प्तां)<BR>or<BR>सुरक्षितं (f. तां) करोति, to f. strongly:<BR>परमां गुप्तिं करोति, Ka.;<BR>(2) by circumlo.: “पुरी<BR> समन्ताद्विहिता सपताका सतोरणा । सचक्रा सहुडा चैव<BR> सयन्त्रखनका तथा ॥.......संक्रमा भेदिताः सर्वे नावश्च<BR> प्रतिषेधिताः । परिखाश्चापि कौख्य कीलैः सुनिचिताः<BR> कृताः ॥ उदपानाः कुरुश्रेष्ठ तथैवाप्यम्बरीषकाः । समन्तात्<BR> कोशमात्रञ्च कारिता विषमा च भूः ॥”, Mah. iii. 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fortitude
FORTITUDE:<BR>(1) धैर्यम्;<BR>(2) धृतिः (rare), R.<BR>viii. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fortnight
FORTNIGHT:<BR>(1) पक्षः,<BR>in three f.s:<BR>पक्षत्रये, L.s.;<BR>the dark f.:<BR>कृष्णपक्षः;<BR>the light f.:<BR>शुक्लपक्षः;<BR>(2)<BR>मासार्द्धम् (= half a month).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fortress
FORTRESS:<BR>I A fort: q.v.: दुर्गम्।<BR>II A town:<BR>सुगुप्तं नगरम् and sim. expr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fortuitous
FORTUITOUS:<BR>(1) आकसिमकः (की, कं);<BR>(2)<BR>समापत्ति- in comp.: v. Accidental.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fortuitously
FORTUITOUSLY: दैवयोगेनः v. Accidentally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fortunate
FORTUNATE:<BR>(1) भाग्यवत् (f. ती),<BR>considered him-<BR>self more f. than even Indra:<BR>मघवतोऽपि भाग्यवन्त-<BR>मात्मानमजीगणत्, D. iv.;<BR>(2) सुभाग्य (f. ग्या),<BR>ah! I<BR>am very f.:<BR>अहोऽतीव सुभाग्याऽहम्, Mah.;<BR>(3) सुभगः<BR>(गा, गं),<BR>vain of being. f. thinks himself beauti-<BR>ful:<BR>सुभगमानी सुन्दरम्मन्यः, D. ii.;<BR>(4) धन्यः (न्या, न्यं)<BR>(= happy),<BR>f. are you:<BR>धन्योऽसि, Si;<BR>(5) मङ्गल्य<BR>(f. ल्या) (= auspicious: q.v.: of time etc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fortunately
FORTUNATELY:<BR>(1) भाग्यात्<BR>or<BR>भाग्येन, सौ-;<BR>(2)<BR>दिष्ट्या, U.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fortune
FORTUNE:<BR>I The goddess:<BR>(1) श्रीः;<BR>(2)<BR>लक्ष्मीः,<BR>at home she is f.:<BR>इयं गेहे लक्ष्मीः, U.<BR>II<BR>Chance, luck:<BR>(1) भाग्यम्,<BR>to conceal your good<BR>f.:<BR>आत्मनः सौभाग्यं निगुहितुम्, V. ii.; (every thing)<BR>else depends on f.:<BR>भाग्याधीनमतःपरम्, Sa. iv.;<BR>(2)<BR>दैवम्: v. Fate.<BR>III Wealth; possessions:<BR>(1) ऋद्धिः;<BR>(2) समृद्धिः;<BR>(3) ऐश्वर्यम्। Ph.:<BR>to tell<BR>f. s:<BR>शुभाशुभं वदति, कथयति, etc.: v. To tell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fortune-hunter
FORTUNE-HUNTER: ऐश्वर्यलिप्सु (mfn.) and sim<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fortune-teller
FORTUNE-TELLER:<BR>(1) दैवझ (f. झा);<BR>(2)<BR>विप्रश्निका (= female f.);<BR>(3) कार्तान्तिकः (rare),<BR>D.: v. Also soothsayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fortune-telling
FORTUNE-TELLING: शुभाशुभकथनम् and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forty
FORTY: चत्वारिंशत् (f.),<BR>f. times:<BR>चत्वारिंशद्वारान्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forum
FORUM: अधिकरणम्, -मण्डपः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forward
FORWARD (adj.):<BR>I In place:<BR>(1) अग्रिमः<BR>(मा, मं);<BR>(2) अग्रस्थः (स्था, स्थं).<BR>II Early:<BR>(1) शीघ्रपक्व (f. क्वा) (= precocious);<BR>(2)<BR>आकालिकः (की, कं) (= untimely), a f. spring:<BR>आकालिकी मधुप्रवृत्तिः, Ku. iii. 34.<BR>III Bold,<BR>confident: q.v.: प्रगल्भ (f. ल्भा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forward
FORWARD (v.):<BR>I To send on: q.v.: प्रेरयति<BR>(ईर्, c. 10.).<BR>II To hasten: q.v.: त्वरयति (c.<BR>of त्वर्).<BR>III To promote: वर्धयति (c. of वृध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forward
FORWARD, FORWARDS (adv.):<BR>(1) अग्रतः;<BR>(2)<BR>पुरतः।<BR>To go f.:<BR>पुरः सरति; to go backwards and f.:<BR>परिक्रामति;<BR>from this day f.:<BR>अद्यारभ्य, अद्यप्रभृति; f.:<BR>पुरो भब, Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

forwardness
FORWARDNESS:<BR>I Promptness, eagerness:<BR>q.v.: उत्साहः।<BR>II Boldness, impudence:<BR>q.v.: प्रगल्भता।<BR>III Precociousness: शीघ्रपाकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fosse
FOSSE: खातम्: v. Dich, moat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fossil
FOSSIL:<BR>I Dug out: उत्खातः (ता, तं).<BR>II<BR>Petrified: शिलीभूतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foster
FOSTER: पुष्णाति<BR>or<BR>पोषयति (पुष्, c. 9. and 10.):<BR>v. To nourish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foster-brother
FOSTER-BROTHER:<BR>(1) धात्रेयः;<BR>(2) धात्रीपुत्रः and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foster-child
FOSTER-CHILD:<BR>(1) पोष्यपुत्रः (f. त्री);<BR>(2)<BR>परिष्क(स्क)न्द(न्न) (f. न्दा<BR>or<BR>न्ना) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fosterer
FOSTERER:<BR>(1) पोषकः, परि-;<BR>(2) पालयितृ (m);<BR>(3) धातृ (m.) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foster-father
FOSTER-FATHER: पालकपितृ (m.); धातृ (m.) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foster-mother
FOSTER-MOTHER:<BR>(1) मातृका;<BR>(2) उपमातृ: v.<BR>Nurse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foster-sister
FOSTER-SISTER: धात्रेयी, by Mālatī's f. Lavangikā:<BR>मालतीधात्रेय्या लवङ्गिकया, Ma. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foster-son
FOSTER-SON:<BR>(1) पोष्यपुत्रः;<BR>(2) पालितसुतः and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fostering
FOSTERING (adj.):<BR>(1) पोषकः (f. षिका) (?);<BR>पा(ला)लकः (f. लिका) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foul
FOUL (v.t.): कलुषयति (nomi.): v. To befoul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foul
FOUL (adj.):<BR>I Dirty: q.v.:<BR>(1) मलपूर्ण (f.<BR>र्णा) (= full of dirt);<BR>(2) अशुचि (mfn.), अमेध्य<BR>(f. ध्या), etc. (= impure), in a ditch full of f.<BR>(matter): अशुचिसंपूर्णे खातके, K.s. xiii. 148.<BR>II<BR>Obscene, abusive: q.v.: अश्लीलः (ला, लं).<BR>III Abominable, detestable: q.v.: मलिनः<BR>(ना, नं), K.<BR>IV Unfair, fraudulent: q.v.:<BR>कूट- in comp.,<BR>f. play:<BR>कूटव्यवहारः।<BR>V Unfavour-<BR>-able: q.v. Ph.:<BR>f. weather:<BR>दुर्दिनम्; fall f. of:<BR>उपरि पतति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foully
FOULLY:<BR>(1) मलिनम (= dirtily);<BR>(2) अश्लीलम्<BR>(= obscenely);<BR>(3) गर्हितम्। (=abominably);<BR>better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foul-mouthed
FOUL-MOUTHED:<BR>(1) वागदुष्ट (f. ष्टा);<BR>(2) अश्लील-<BR>वादिन् (f. नी), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foulness
FOULNESS:<BR>(1) मलिनता;<BR>(2) अश्लीलता (= obs-<BR>-cenity);<BR>(3) अमेध्यता (= impurity, dis-<BR>-honesty): v. Also foul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

found
FOUND (v.t.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) स्थापयति, प्रति-,<BR>(c. of स्था) (= to establish: q.v.);<BR>(2)<BR>निर्मिमीते (मा, c. 3.) (= to build: q.v.);<BR>(3)<BR>मूल (= root) in comp.,<BR>f. ed on love:<BR>प्रेममूलः<BR>(ला, लं).<BR>II To cast: सं-दधाति (धा, c. 3.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foundation
FOUNDATION:<BR>I Groundwork:<BR>(1) भित्तिमूलम्<BR>(lit. and fig.), lay the f. stone of a college:<BR>*विद्यालयस्य मित्तिमूलप्रस्तरं न्यस्यति;<BR>(2) भूमिः (=<BR>ground).<BR>II Endowment: वृत्तिः, f. scholarship:<BR>*मूलवृत्तिः।<BR>III Establishment: स्थापनम्, प्रति-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

founder
FOUNDER (subs.):<BR>I In gen.;<BR>(1) स्थापकः,<BR> प्रति- (= establisher):<BR>(2) निर्मातृ (m.) (=buil-<BR>-der);<BR>(3) कारः (= author);<BR>(4) मूलम्; (=root).<BR>II Caster: संधातृ (m.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

founder
FOUNDER (v.):<BR>I Lit.: जलाविष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं)<BR>नश्यति (नश्, c. 4.): v. Also to sink.<BR>II To<BR>fail, miscarry: नश्यति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foundery
FOUNDERY, FOUNDRY:<BR>(1) सन्धानी;<BR>(2) कुप्यशाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foundling
FOUNDLING: अपविद्धबालः (f. ला),<BR>f. hospital:<BR>*अनाथ-<BR>बालाश्रमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foundress
FOUNDRESS:<BR>(1) स्थापयित्री, प्रति-;<BR>(2) स्थापिका,<BR> प्रति-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fount
FOUNT, FOUNTAIN:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्रस्रवणम्;<BR>(2)<BR>निर्भ्करः;<BR>(3) उत्सः<BR>II Source:<BR>(1) मूलम्;<BR>(2)<BR>योनिः;<BR>(3) प्रसूः<BR>or<BR>प्रसूतिः (= mother), Ki.<BR>III Of types: v. Font.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

four
FOUR: चतुर् (mfn.),<BR>f. times:<BR>चतुः; of f. kinds:<BR>चतुर्विधः (धा, धं),<BR>aggregate of f.:<BR>चतुष्टयम्;<BR>in f.<BR>ways:<BR>चतुर्धा;<BR>f. hundred:<BR>चतुःशतम्; the f. objects<BR>of human pursuit (virtue, wealth, love, and sal-<BR>vation): चतुर्वर्गः;<BR>an army complete in its four<BR>parts-horse, foot, car and elephants:<BR>चतुरङ्गबलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

four-cornered
FOUR-CORNERED:<BR>(1) चतुरस्र (f. स्रा);<BR>(2)<BR>चतुष्कोण (f. णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fourfold
FOURFOLD:<BR>(1) चतुर्गुणः (णा, णं);<BR>(2) by adv.:<BR>चतुर्वारान्;<BR>(3) चतुर्धा (in f. ways).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

four-footed
FOUR-FOOTED:<BR>(1) चतुष्पदः (दी, दं);<BR>(2)<BR>चतुष्पाद् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fourscore
FOURSCORE: अशीतिः: v. Eighty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

foursquare
FOURSQUARE: समचतुरस्र (f. स्रा): v. Square.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

four-wheeled
FOUR-WHEELED: चतुश्चक्रः (क्रा, क्रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fourteen
FOURTEEN: चतुर्दशन् (mfn.)<BR>F. th:<BR>चतुर्दशः (शी, शं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fourth
FOURTH (adj.):<BR>(1) चतुर्थः (र्था, र्थं);<BR>(2) तुरीयः<BR>(या, यं);<BR>(3) तुर्यः (र्या, र्यं). In the f. place:<BR>चतुर्थतः;<BR>for the f. time:<BR>चतुर्थवारम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fourth
FOURTH (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) चतुर्भागः;<BR>(2)<BR>पादः,<BR>three f. s:<BR>पादत्रयम्, Li.: v. Quarter.<BR>II<BR>The f. note in music: षड्जः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fourthly
FOURTHLY:<BR>(1) चतुर्थतः;<BR>(2) तुरीयतः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fowl
FOWL (subs.):<BR>I A bird: q.v.<BR>II A cock<BR>or hen: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fowl
FOWL (v.i.): पक्षिणो हन्ति (हन्, c. 2.), etc.;<BR>always<BR>f. ing in the forest:<BR>द्विजान् हत्वा वने सदा, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fowler
FOWLER:<BR>(1) शाकुनिकः;<BR>(2) शकुनिलुब्धकः, P.<BR>iii. 7.;<BR>(3) विहङ्गहन् (m.), Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fowling
FOWLING: पक्षिघातः।<BR>F. -piece:<BR>*पक्षिघातयन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fox
FOX:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) खिखिः<BR>or<BR>किखिः;<BR>(2) खिङ्गिरः।<BR>II Fig.: a sly rogue: धूर्तः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fox-glove
FOX-GLOVE: औषधिभेदः; *खिखिपादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fox-hound
FOX-HOUND: v. Hound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fraction
FRACTION:<BR>I In arith: भिन्नम्, -राशिः,<BR>multipli-<BR>cation of f.s:<BR>भिन्नगुणनम्, Li.<BR>II A portion,<BR>fragment: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fractious
FRACTIOUS: v. Peevish, irritable, ill-tempered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fracture
FRACTURE (subs.):<BR>(1) भङ्गः, f. of the bones:<BR>अस्थ्नां भङ्गः, Sr.;<BR>(2) भग्नम्,<BR>a f. heals with diffi-<BR>culty:<BR>भग्नं कृच्छ्रे ण सिध्यति, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fracture
FRACTURE (v.t.): भनक्ति (भञ्ज्, c. 7.): v. To<BR>break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fragile
FRAGILE:<BR>(1) भङ्गुरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) सुभङ्ग (f. ङ्गा)<BR>(3) भङ्गशीलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fragility
FRAGILITY:<BR>(1) भङ्गुरता;<BR>(2) भङ्गशीलता;<BR>(3)<BR>सुभङ्गता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fragment
FRAGMENT:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) खण्ड (mn.), in f.s:<BR>खण्डशः;<BR>(2) शवल (mn.) (rare).<BR>II Of a<BR>work: perh. खण्ड (mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fragmentary
FRAGMENTARY: खण्डितः (ता, तं), “व्यक्तिविवेक-<BR>लोचनग्रन्थावत्र खण्डितावेव स्त इति न तौ सम्पूर्णं दृष्टौ”,<BR>Mahesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fragrance
FRAGRANCE, FRAGRANCY:<BR>(1) सौरभम्<BR>or<BR>सौरम्यम्;<BR>(2) परिमलः;<BR>(3) आमोदः;<BR>(4) सुगन्धिः, सुगन्धः<BR>or<BR>सौगन्ध्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fragrant
FRAGRANT:<BR>(1) सुगन्धः (न्धा, न्धं);<BR>(2) सुगन्धि<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(3) सुरभि (mfn.);<BR>(4) आमोदिन् (f.<BR>नी);<BR>(5) परिमलवत् (f. ती);<BR>(6) सामोदः (दा,<BR> दं) (rare), Ki. viii. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fragrantly
FRAGRANTLY:<BR>(1) सौरभेन;<BR>(2) सुगन्धम्;<BR>(3)<BR>सामोदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frail
FRAIL (subs.): पेटिका: v. Basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frail
FRAIL (adj.):<BR>I Fragile: q.v.<BR>II Weak,<BR>infirm: दुर्ब्बलः (ला, लं).<BR>III Easily des-<BR>-troyed:<BR>(1) क्षणभङ्गुरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) विनश्वरः<BR>(री, रं).<BR>IV Of infirm virtue: इन्द्रियपरवशः<BR>(शा, शं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frailness
FRAILNESS, FRAILTY:<BR>I Fragility: भङ्गुरता।<BR>II<BR>Weakness; दुर्बलता।<BR>III Fickleness: अनित्यता।<BR>IV Fault, foible: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frame
FRAME (subs.):<BR>I A fabric: निर्माणम्।<BR>II A<BR>case: आधारः,<BR>door -f.:<BR>द्वारस्याधारदारु, M.n.<BR>III<BR>Body: q.v.: वपुः,<BR>surely (her) f. was made<BR>of golden lotuses:<BR>ध्रुवं वपुः काञ्चनपद्मनिर्मितम्, Ku.<BR>IV Humour: भावः; oftenn ot expr.,<BR>in a<BR>happy f. of mind:<BR>निर्वृतमनस् (mfn.).<BR>V System:<BR>प्रकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frame
FRAME (v.t.):<BR>I To form, make: q.v.:<BR>निर्मिमीते (मा, c. 3.), with which the earth has<BR>been f.d:<BR>वसुधा येन निर्मिता, Ram.<BR>II To plan:<BR>q.v.: कल्पयति (कॢप्, c. 10.).<BR>III To provide<BR>with a f.: साधारं (f. रां) करोति।<BR>IV To draw<BR>up: निबध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

framer
FRAMER: रचयितृ (f. त्री),<BR>f. of the world:<BR>विश्व-<BR>रचयिता;<BR>f. of a law:<BR>विधिरचयिता (?);<BR>f. of<BR>the Vedas:<BR>वेदस्य कर्तारः, D.s.: v. Maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

framework
FRAMEWORK: आधारः: v. Frame (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

franchise
FRANCHISE (subs.):<BR>I Freedom: मोक्षः।<BR>II<BR>In gen.: अधिकारः,<BR>f. of a citizen:<BR>पौराधिकारः;<BR>“crowning f.”<BR>प्रधानतमाधिकारः;<BR>monasteries in<BR>Spain are f.s for criminals”:<BR>*हिस्पानीयविहारा<BR> दुष्टानामधिकाराः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

franchise
FRANCHISE (v.): मोक्षयति (मोक्ष्, c. 10.); मोक्षं<BR> ददाति (दा, c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frank
FRANK (adj.):<BR>(1) सरलः (ला, लं) (= straight-<BR>-forward);<BR>(2) निष्कपटः (टा, टं), अमायः (या, यं)<BR>etc. (= sincere);<BR>(3) स्फुटमाषिन् (f. णी), स्फुट-<BR>वादिन् (f. नी), etc. (= open: of men only);<BR>(4) असंवृतः (ता, तं) (= unreserved).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frank
FRANK (v.): of letters: राजकार्यतो विना मूल्येन<BR> वाहार्थं पत्रोपरि प्रेरकस्य नाम लिखति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frankincense
FRANKINCENSE:<BR>(1) कुन्दुरुः;<BR>(2) कुन्दुः;<BR>(3)<BR>रसालम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frankly
FRANKLY:<BR>(1) स्फुटम् (= openly),<BR>makes enmity<BR>when talked to f.:<BR>करोति बैरं स्फुटमुच्यमानः, B. xii.<BR>83.;<BR>(2) निष्कपटम्: v. Sincerely;<BR>(3) असंवृतम्<BR>(= unreservedly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frankness
FRANKNESS:<BR>(1) सरलता<BR>or<BR>सारल्यम्;<BR>(2) निष्कपटता;<BR>(3) अमायता;<BR>(4) असंवृतिः;<BR>(5) स्फुटभाषित्वम्;<BR>(6) स्फुटवादिता; for dif.: v. Frank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frantic
FRANTIC: ऊन्मत्तः (त्ता, त्तं),<BR>f. with rage:<BR>क्रोधोन्मत्तः<BR>(त्ता, त्तं): v. Mad, maddened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

franticly
FRANTICLY: उन्मत्तवत्: v. Madly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fraternal
FRATERNAL: भ्रात्रीयः (या, यं): v. Brotherly (adj.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fraternally
FRATERNALLY:<BR>(1) भ्रातृवत्;<BR>(2) भ्रातृसन्निभम्;<BR>(3)<BR>सोदरवत्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fraternity
FRATERNITY:<BR>I Brother-hood: भ्रातृत्वम्,<BR>good<BR>f.:<BR>सौम्रात्रम्, R.<BR>II Association: q.v.: समाजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fraternize
FRATERNIZE: म्रातृवत् मिलितः<BR>or<BR>संहतः (ता, तं)<BR> मवति (भू, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fratricidal
FRATRICIDAL: expr. by comp.,<BR>f. crime:<BR>म्रातृ-<BR>वधपातकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fratricide
FRATRICIDE:<BR>I The murderer: भ्रातृधातिन्<BR>(f. नी), Mah.; भ्रातृहन् (mfn.) भ्रातृघातकः (m.);<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR>II The crime: भ्रातृहत्या;<BR> भ्रातृवधः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fraud
FRAUD: च्छलम्,<BR>without force or f.:<BR>बलच्छले विहाय,<BR>Viv.: v. Deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fraudulent
FRAUDULENT: expr. by छलेन, to make a f. sale:<BR>छलेन विक्रयं करोति; f. (man): छलप्रियः (या, यं),<BR> छलनापरः (रा, रं): v. Deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fraudulently
FRAUDULENTLY: छलेनः v. Deceitfully, dis-<BR>-honestly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fray
FRAY:<BR>I Subs.: कलिः: v. Affray.<BR>II Verb.<BR>f. ed:<BR>भीतः (ता, तं): v. To frighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freak
FREAK (subs.): कामाचारः: v. Caprice. Ph.:<BR>in<BR>a f., by a mere f.:<BR>असमीक्ष्य।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freak
FREAK (v.): चित्रयति (चित्र्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>variegate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freakish
FREAKISH: चपलः (ला, लं): v. Capricious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freakishly
FREAKISHLY:<BR>(1) चापल्यात् (inconstantly);<BR>(2)<BR>असमीक्ष्य (inconsiderately);<BR>(3) कामचारेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freakishness
FREAKISHNESS:<BR>(1) कामचारिता;<BR>(2) चापल्यम्;<BR>(3) मनोलौल्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freckle
FRECKLE:<BR>(1) तिलः, -कः;<BR>(2) कालकः;<BR>(3) जटुलः<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freckled
FRECKLED, FRECKLY:<BR>(1) तिलकिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>कालकिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

free
FREE (adj.):<BR>I At liberty:<BR>(1) स्वाधीनः (ना,<BR> नं),<BR>he is f.:<BR>स्वाधीनोऽयम्, K.,<BR>“f. town”:<BR>*स्वाधीन-<BR>नगरम्;<BR>(2) स्वतन्त्र (f. न्त्रा),<BR>who being f. sells<BR>himself:<BR>विक्रीणीते स्वतन्त्रः सन्नात्मानं यः, N.s.;<BR>“f.<BR>country”.<BR>स्वतन्त्रराज्यम्। Ph.:<BR>according to one's f.<BR>will:<BR>स्वेच्छया;<BR>she should be made f.:<BR>सादासी कर्तव्या,<BR>Kat.: v. Slave;<BR>f. agency,<BR>स्वच्छन्दता।<BR>II<BR>Liberated: मुक्तः (क्ता, क्तं), वि-, निर्-; मोक्षितः<BR>(ता, तं), वि-।<BR>III Unrestrained: निर्यन्त्रण<BR>(f. णा); अयन्त्रितः (ता, तं).<BR>IV मुक्तहस्तः (स्ता,<BR> स्तं).<BR>V Not obstructed, open: मुक्तः (क्ता, क्तं).<BR>VI Gratuitous: expr. by विना मुल्येन।<BR>VII<BR>Unreserved: असंवृतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

free from
FREE FROM:<BR>(1) by निर्<BR>or<BR>अ pref., f. f. all care:<BR>निश्चिन्तः (न्ता, न्तं),<BR>f. f. debt:<BR>अनृणः (णा, णं);<BR>(2) गतः, विगतः, वीतः, etc. pref.,<BR>f. f. desire:<BR>गत-<BR>स्पृहः (हा, हं), Si.;<BR>(3) वर्जितः (ता, तं), वि-, f.<BR>f. the possession of pride:<BR>स्मयावेशविवर्जितः (ता, तं),<BR>R.: v. Also devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

free
FREE (v.t.):<BR>I To set free:<BR>(1) मोक्षयति, वि-,<BR>(मोक्ष्, c. 10.),<BR>how to f. a slave:<BR>कथं दासस्य<BR> मोक्षः, Viv.;<BR>f. s from danger of life:<BR>मोक्षयेत्<BR> प्राणसंशयात्, M. p.;<BR>(2) मुञ्चति<BR>or<BR>मोचयति, वि-,<BR> परि-, निर्-, (मुच्, c. 6. and 10.),<BR>a debtor is f. d<BR>from slavery.....<BR>ऋणी दास्याद्विमुच्यते, Viv.;<BR>f. d<BR>him thus bewailing:<BR>इत्थममं विलपन्तममुञ्चत्, N.<BR>II<BR>To clear: q.v.: मोचयति, वि-, निर्-,<BR>one who<BR>f. s others from all doubts:<BR>सर्बसंशयनिर्मोक्ता, Mah.<BR>ii. 39. 8.<BR>III To f. a lock: उन्मोचयति or<BR>उन्मुञ्चति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

free with
FREE WITH, MAKE: असङ्कोचेन व्यवहरति (हृ, c. 1.)<BR>(with ins.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freebooter
FREEBOOTER:<BR>(1) लुब्धकः;<BR>(2) दस्युः: v. Rob-<BR>-ber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freebooting
FREEBOOTING (subs.); दस्युवृत्तिः: v. Robbery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freeborn
FREEBORN:<BR>(1) जातस्वाधीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2)<BR>जातस्वतन्त्र (f. न्त्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freedman
FREEDMAN:<BR>(1) लब्धमोक्षो दासः;<BR>(2) अदासीकृतो<BR> जनः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freedom
FREEDOM:<BR>I Liberty:<BR>(1) स्वाधीनता;<BR>(2)<BR>स्वतन्त्रता।<BR>II Release:<BR>(1) मोक्षः, वि-, परि-;<BR>(2) मुक्तिः, निर्-, वि-।<BR>III Licence: q.v.<BR>IV<BR>Liberality: मुक्तहस्तता।<BR>V Frankness: q.v.:<BR>असङ्कोचव्यवहारः।<BR>VI Unrestrainedness: निर्य-<BR>न्त्रणता, -त्वम्।<BR>VII Exemption, f. from disease:<BR>नीरोगता: v. Free from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freedwoman
FREEDWOMAN:<BR>(1) लब्धमोक्षा दासी;<BR>(2) अदासीकृता<BR> दासी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freehold
FREEHOLD (subs.):<BR>f. property:<BR>निष्करभूमिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freeholder
FREEHOLDER: निष्करभूस्वामिन् (m.); निष्करभूमिपतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freely
FREELY:<BR>I Of one's own will:<BR>(1) स्वेच्छया:<BR>(2) स्वच्छन्दतः;<BR>(4) स्वैरम्,<BR>as moving f.:<BR>यथा स्वैरं<BR> भ्राम्यन्, Vi.<BR>II Gratuitously: विनामूल्येन।<BR>III<BR>Liberally, amply: मुक्तहस्तम्।<BR>IV Without<BR>restraint:<BR>(1) निर्यन्त्रणम्;<BR>(2) अनियन्त्रितम्;<BR>(3) यथेच्छम्, this wood is f. enjoyable by you:<BR>यथेच्छं भोग्यं वो वनमिदम्, U. i.<BR>V Without<BR>scruple: असङ्गोचेन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freeman
FREEMAN:<BR>(1) सवाधीनः;<BR>(2) स्वतन्त्रः;<BR>(3) अप-<BR>राधीनः;<BR>(4) अदासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freemason
FREEMASON: *समवायधर्मिन् (m.); संसर्गध्वजिन्<BR>(m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freemasonry
FREEMASONRY: *समवायधर्मः; संसर्गध्वजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freeminded
FREEMINDED:<BR>I Lit.: स्वाधीनमनम् (mfn.)<BR>II<BR>Careless: निश्चिन्तमनस् (mfn.) etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freeness
FREENESS: v. Freedom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

free-spoken
FREE-SPOKEN:<BR>(1) स्फुटभाषिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) स्पष्ट-<BR>वादिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

free-stone
FREE-STONE: सुखच्छेद्यप्रस्तरविशेषः; *विघटोपलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

free-thinker
FREE-THINKER: *यथेच्छभावुकः (की, कं): v.<BR>Also atheist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

free-thinking
FREE-THINKING: यथेच्छभावना: v. Scepticism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

free-will
FREE-WILL:<BR>I In gen.: यथेच्छा।<BR>II Phil. t.<BR>t.: v. Will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freeze
FREEZE (v.i.):<BR>I Lit.: शिलीभवति,<BR>where even<BR>on roads where snow has frozen:<BR>मार्गे शिलीभूत-<BR>हिमेऽपियत्र, Ku. i. 11.; घनीभवति। (= to congeal).<BR>II Fig.: जडीभवति (nomi.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freeze
FREEZE (v.i.):<BR>I Lit.: शिलीकरोति, घनीकरोति।<BR>II Fig: जडीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freight
FREIGHT (subs.):<BR>I Cargo: q.v.: expr. by<BR>द्रव्यम्<BR>or<BR>भाण्डम्,<BR>f. to go to Mathura:<BR>मथुरागामीनि<BR> भाण्डानि, P.<BR>II Fare:<BR>(1) तरः (gen. term).<BR>M. viii. 406.;<BR>(2) वाहिकम् (after तारिकम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freight
FREIGHT (v.): माण्डानि निवेशयति (c. of विश्)<BR>(with loc.): v. To load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

french
FRENCH: *फरासीयः (या, यं). Ph.:<BR>to take f.<BR>leave:<BR>*चौरप्रस्थानं करोति।<BR>F. -bean:<BR>क्षुद्रशिम्बिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frenzied
FRENZIED: उन्मत्तः (त्ता, त्तं): v. Mad. F. ly:<BR>v. Madly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frenzy
FRENZY: उन्मादः: v. Madness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frequency
FREQUENCY:<BR>(1) पौनःपुन्यम्;<BR>(2) अभीक्ष्णता or<BR>आभीक्ष्ण्यम्;<BR>(3) समभिहारः,<BR>by f. of acts:<BR>क्रियासमभि-<BR>हारेण, Si. ii. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frequent
FREQUENT (adj.): expr. by adv.,<BR>his visit to me<BR>are f.:<BR>समामभीक्ष्णं पश्यति: v. F. ly, continually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frequent
FREQUENT (v.): नियतं गच्छतिः v. To go, visit;<BR>f. ly, continually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frequentative
FREQUENTATIVE:<BR>(1) समभिहारार्थकः (का, कं)<BR>(after Pāṇini);<BR>(2) यङ्न्तः (न्ता, न्तं) (= end-<BR>-ing in यङ्: of Sanskrit verbs only).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frequented
FREQUENTED, MUCH (adj.): जनाकीर्ण (f. र्णा)<BR>(= crowded: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frequently
FREQUENTLY:<BR>(1) पुनःपुनः;<BR>(2) मुहुर्मुहुः;<BR>(3)<BR>भूयोभूयः;<BR>(4) असकृत्;<BR>(5) अभीक्ष्णम्;<BR>(6) समभि-<BR>हारेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fresco
FRESCO:<BR>I Coolness: q.v.<BR>II In painting:<BR>मण्डोदकेन भित्तौ चित्रकरणम्।<BR>Painting in f.:<BR>मण्डोदक-<BR>चित्रम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fresh
FRESH:<BR>I New: q.v.:<BR>(1) अभिनवः (वा, वं),<BR>f. blood:<BR>अभिनवशोणितम्, Sa. vi. 32.; f. youth:<BR>अभिनवयौवनम्, K.;<BR>(2) प्रत्यग्रः (ग्रा, ग्रं),<BR>with f.<BR>flowers:<BR>प्रत्यग्रैः कुसुमैः, Me.;<BR>(3) sometimes by<BR>सद्यः,<BR>f. meat:<BR>सद्योमांसम्, J.<BR>II Not saline:<BR>(1)<BR>निर्दोषः (षा, षं);<BR>(2) पेयः (या, यं) (= drink-<BR>-able). Ph.:<BR>having f. water:<BR>शुद्धोदः (दा, दं),<BR>D. s.; आस्वाद्यतोयः (या, यं), H.<BR>III Unprac-<BR>-tised: नवः (वा, वं),<BR>f. men:<BR>नवाः; प्रथमवर्षच्छात्राः।<BR>IV Of wind:<BR>f. air:<BR>शिवा मरुतः, Ki. vi. 33.;<BR>सुखा वाताः, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freshen
FRESHEN (v.t.):<BR>I To refresh: q.v.<BR>II To<BR>take saltness from: निर्दोषीकरोति (?); विलवणी-<BR>करोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freshen
FRESHEN (v.i.): v. Fresh, to become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freshly
FRESHLY:<BR>I Newly: q.v.: अभिनवम्।<BR>II Coo-<BR>-lly: सुखम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

freshness
FRESHNESS:<BR>I Newness: नवीनता।<BR>II Liveli-<BR>-ness: उल्लासः।<BR>III Pleasantness: सुखता।<BR>IV<BR>Not salted-ness; निर्दोषता। Better by adj.: v.<BR>FRESH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fresh-water
FRESH-WATER (adj.): expr. by comp.,<BR>f.<BR>fishes:<BR>पेयजलमत्स्याः<BR>or<BR>नादेयमत्स्याः (= river-f.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fret
FRET (subs.): क्षोमः: v. Agitation, vexation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fret
FRET (v.t.):<BR>I To rub: q.v.: घर्षति (घृष्, c.<BR>1.).<BR>II To impair: q.v.: दापयति (c. of<BR>दो).<BR>III To variegate: q.v.<BR>IV To vex:<BR>q.v.: क्लिश्नाति (क्लिश्, c. 9.). v. To agitate:<BR>q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fret
FRET (v.i.):<BR>I To be agitated: q.v.: क्षुभ्यति<BR>(क्षुभ्, c. 4.).<BR>II To be vexed: क्षुभ्यति;<BR> सन्तप्यते (pass. of तप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fretful
FRETFUL:<BR>(1) चण्ड (f. ण्डा) (= irritable);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रतीपः (पा, पं) (= cross);<BR>(3) शीध्रक्षुब्ध (f. ब्धा),<BR>आशुसन्तप्त (f. प्ता), etc. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fretfully
FRETFULLY:<BR>(1) सक्रोधम् (= angrily);<BR>(2) क्षोभेण;<BR>(3) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fretfulness
FRETFULNESS:<BR>(1) शीघ्रक्षुब्धता;<BR>(2) आशुसन्तापिता;<BR>(3) प्रतीपता (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fretwork
FRETWORK: कर्णरेखाकर्मन् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

friability
FRIABILITY:<BR>(1) भङ्गुरता: v. Fragility;<BR>(2)<BR>by circumlo.: v. Friable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

friable
FRIABLE: मङ्गुरः (रा, रं): v. Fragile. यः (या,<BR> यत्) सुखेन चूर्णीमवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

friar
FRIAR: ब्रह्मचारिन् (m.) (?): v. Monk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fricasse
FRICASSE (subs.): तलितमांसम् (?), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

friction
FRICTION:<BR>(1) घर्षणम्;<BR>(2) घर्षः, नि-, सं-, उत्-,<BR>fire<BR>rising from the f. of the roots of branches:<BR>शाखान्त-<BR>निघर्षजोऽनलः, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

friday
FRIDAY:<BR>(1) शुक्रवारः;<BR>(2) शुक्रवासरः;<BR>(3) भृगु-<BR>वारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

friend
FRIEND:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) सखि (m.) (f. खी),<BR>bosom f.:<BR>हृदयङ्गमः सखा, Ku.<BR>(2) मित्रम्,<BR>greatest<BR>f.:<BR>परं मित्रम्, K.;<BR>old f.:<BR>चिरमित्रम्, H.;<BR>(3)<BR>सुहृद् (m.),<BR>dear old f.:<BR>चिरन्तनप्रियसुहृद्, U. vi.;<BR>first shewing leniency as a f.:<BR>सुहृदिव प्रथममनुकूलतां<BR> प्रकटय्य, Ma. iv. 7.;<BR>(7) बन्धुः,<BR>who else is f. to<BR>me like you:<BR>कोऽपरः त्वत्समो मे बन्धुः, K.;<BR>(5)<BR>वयस्य (f. स्या = of the same age).<BR>II An<BR>advocate:<BR>(1) मित्रम्;<BR>(2) बन्धुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

friendless
FRIENDLESS:<BR>(1) बन्धुहीनः (ना, नं),<BR>I live in this<BR>wood f. as dead:<BR>अत्रारण्ये बन्धुहीनो मृतवन्निवसामि, H.;<BR>(2) मित्रहीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(3) असहायः (या, यं)<BR>(= without a helper).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

friendliness
FRIENDLINESS:<BR>(1) स्नेहः: v. Affection, love;<BR>(2) अनुकूलता (favourableness);<BR>(3) दया<BR>(= kindness):<BR>(4) मित्रवद्व्यवहारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

friendly
FRIENDLY (adj.):<BR>(1) स्निग्ध (f. ग्धा) (affec-<BR>-tionate);<BR>(2) अनुकूलः (ला, लं) (= favour-<BR>-able);<BR>(3) सदयः (या, यं) (= kind). Ph.:<BR>should have f. feeling towards those who have<BR>enjoyments:<BR>सम्भोगापन्ने षु मैत्रीं भावयेत्, P. d.;<BR>the<BR>one next to an enemy is a f. power:<BR>अरेरनन्तरं मित्रम्,<BR>M. vii. 158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

friendly
FRIENDLY (adv.):<BR>(1) मित्रवत्;<BR>(2) सुहृदिव;<BR>(3)<BR>बन्धुवत्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

friendship
FRIENDSHIP:<BR>(1) सख्यम्,<BR>among the good, f. (is<BR>produced) in seven words:<BR>सतां साप्तपदं सख्यम्, Mah.;<BR>(2) मित्रता<BR>or<BR>मैत्री,<BR>to make f.:<BR>मैत्रीं करोति, Ki.;<BR>it is not proper (to form) f. with a stranger:<BR>आगन्तुना सह मैत्री न युक्ता, H.;<BR>(3) सौहार्दम्<BR>or<BR>सौहृदम्<BR>out of f. or from compassion towards me:<BR>सौहार्दाद्वा<BR> मय्यनुक्रोशबुद्ध्या वा, Me.;<BR>(4) बन्धुता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frieze
FRIEZE:<BR>I Coarse cloth: स्थूलपट्टम्।<BR>II In<BR>architecture: *अवचूडा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frigate
FRIGATE: मद्गुः (?). D. vi.: v. Ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fright
FRIGHT (subs.): त्रासः: v. Fear, terror.<BR>To<BR>take f.:<BR>त्रस्यति (त्रस्, c. 4.) (with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frighten
FRIGHTEN (v.):<BR>(1) भीषयति, वि-, (c. of भी),<BR>I<BR>can never be f. ed with mere words:<BR>नाहं भीषयितुं<BR> शक्यो वाङ्मात्रेण कथञ्चन, Mah.<BR>(2) त्रासयति, वि-,<BR>(c. of त्रस्), on the pretence of f. ing pigeons:<BR>पारावतत्रासनापदेशात्, D.<BR>To be f. ed:<BR>बिभेति,<BR> भी, c. 2.),<BR>do not get f. ed:<BR>मा भैषीः,<BR>I therefore<BR>stand f. ed before you:<BR>अत एव भीतस्तिष्ठामि तेऽग्रतः,<BR>Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frightful
FRIGHTFUL:<BR>(1) भैरवः (वी, वं);<BR>(2) भीषण (f.<BR>णा);<BR>(3) भीमः (मा, मं);<BR>(4) करालः (ला, लं);<BR>(5) विकटः (टा, टं): v. Also dreadful, fear-<BR>-ful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frightfully
FRIGHTFULLY:<BR>(1) भैरवम्;<BR>(2) भीषणम्;<BR>(3) भीमम्;<BR>(4) करालम्;<BR>(5) विकटम्, Vi.: v. Also dread-<BR>-fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frightfulness
FRIGHTFULNESS:<BR>(1) भैरवता;<BR>(2) भीषणता;<BR>(3)<BR>दारुणता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frigid
FRIGID:<BR>I Cold: q.v.: शीतः (ता, तं).<BR>II Un-<BR>-feeling: q.v.: नीरसः (सा, सं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frigidity
FRIGIDITY:<BR>I Coldness: q.v.: शीतता।<BR>II<BR>Fig.: नीरसता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frigidly
FRIGIDLY:<BR>I Lit.: शीतलम्।<BR>II Fig.: नीरसम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frill
FRILL: *फुल्लितदशा (after Assamese).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fringe
FRINGE:<BR>(1) दशा;<BR>(2) अञ्चलः;<BR>(3) तरी<BR>or<BR>तरिः<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fringed
FRINGED:<BR>(1) दशायुक्तः (क्ता, क्तं);<BR>(2) अञ्चलान्वितः<BR>(ता, तं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frippery
FRIPPERY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) जीर्णवस्त्रम्;<BR>(2) उच्छिष्ट-<BR>वस्त्रम्।<BR>II Fig.: secondhand finery: दृष्टि-<BR>शोभनः (ना, नं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frisk
FRISK (v.) खेलति (खेल्, c. 1.), U.: v. To play,<BR>leap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frith
FRITH: मुखम् (= mouth); सङ्गमः (= confluence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fritter
FRITTER (subs.): खण्डः (mn.): v. Fragment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fritter
FRITTER (v.):<BR>I To cut: खण्डशः कृन्तति (कृत्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">Page300</a>]<BR>c. 6.).<BR>II To break into pieces: शकलयति<BR>(nomi.)<BR>F. away:<BR>क्षपयति (c. of क्षै). v. To<BR>waste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frivolity
FRIVOLITY:<BR>(1) लाघवम्;<BR>(2) लघुता;<BR>(3) लघुवृत्तिता;<BR>(4) चापल्यं<BR>or<BR>चपलता। (fickleness);<BR>(5) यत्किञ्चन-<BR>कारिता, Ki. N.B.<BR>(3) to<BR>(5) only of conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frivolous
FRIVOLOUS:<BR>I Of little weight, slight: लघु<BR>(mfn.).<BR>II Given to trifling<BR>(1) लघु (mfn.);<BR>(2) यत्किञ्चनकारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(3) चपलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frivolously
FRIVOLOUSLY:<BR>(1) लघुतया;<BR>(2) लाघवेन;<BR>(3)<BR>चापल्येन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

friz
FRIZ, FRIZE, FRIZZLE (v.): कुञ्चितम् (f. तां) करोतिः<BR>v. Curly, to make.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frizzled
FRIZZLED, FRIZZLY:<BR>(1) कुटिलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2)<BR>भङ्गुरः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fro
FRO: Ph.: to and f.:<BR>(1) इतस्ततः;<BR>(2) इतश्चेतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frock
FROCK:<BR>I For females: शाटी (?):<BR>II For<BR>males: आप्रपदीनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frog
FROG:<BR>(1) भेकः;<BR>(2) मण्डूकः;<BR>(3) दर्दुरः;<BR>(4)<BR>वर्षाभूः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frog-fish
FROG-FISH: मत्स्यविशेषः; *भेकमुखः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frolic
FROLIC (v. i): खेलति (खेल, c. 1.): v. To play,<BR>sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frolic
FROLIC (subs.): खेला: v. Play, sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frolicsome
FROLICSOME:<BR>(1) विलासप्रियः (या, यं);<BR>(2) विनोदिन्<BR>(f. नी): v. Also playful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frolicsomeness
FROLICSOMENESS:<BR>(1) विलासप्रियता;<BR>(2) विनोदिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

from
FROM:<BR>I Of place: (a) by abl. f. its top:<BR>तस्याग्रभागात्, Sa.;<BR>rose f. the seat:<BR>पीठादुदत्तिष्ठत्,<BR>Si. i. 12.; (b) sometimes by tat. comp.,<BR>fallen f. the mouth of a hawk:<BR>श्येनमुखपरिभ्रष्टः (ष्टा,<BR> ष्टं), K.<BR>II Of distance: by abl.:<BR>the<BR>village is a Yojana f. the forest:<BR>वनाद्ग्रामो योजनम्,<BR>S. k.;<BR>not far f. here:<BR>इतो नातिदूरे, K.<BR>III Of<BR>time; (a) by abl. and प्रभृति<BR>or<BR>आरभ्य,<BR>f. the<BR>time of seeing:<BR>दर्शनात् प्रभृति, K.;<BR>f. today:<BR>अद्य-<BR>प्रभृति, Ki.; (b) by comp. with -अवधि<BR>or<BR>आ,<BR>f. today:<BR>अद्यावधि;<BR>f. birth:<BR>आजन्मनः, Sa. v.<BR>IV<BR>Of source, origin: (a) by abl.,<BR>the Ganges<BR>rises f. the Himalayas:<BR>हिमवतो गङ्गा प्रभवति;<BR>men<BR>are sprung f. God:<BR>त्रह्मणः प्रजाः प्रजायन्ते, S. k.<BR>V<BR>Denoting cause, occasion, etc.: (a) by abl.<BR>not f. exhaustion:<BR>न खेदात्, Mu. i.;<BR>and f. non-<BR>perception of others:<BR>इतरेषाञ्चानुपलब्धेः, S.; (b) by<BR>ins. in the case of feminine nouns,<BR>f. a<BR>desire^1 to see:<BR>दिदृक्षया, Ki.:<BR>f. fragrance:<BR>सुरभितया,<BR>K.<BR>VI Of material: v. Of.<BR>VII Of<BR>persons: expr. by सकाशात् and gen., f. Raghu:<BR>रोघोः सकाशात्, R. v. 24. Miscell: f. day to day.<BR>दिने दिने, Ku. i. 25.:<BR>f. country: to country:<BR>देशात्<BR> देशम्<BR>or<BR>देशान्तरम्, D. vi.;<BR>wandered f. house to<BR>house:<BR>गृहाद्गृहं प्रविश्याभ्रमत्, D.; f. the beginning:<BR>आमूलात्<BR>or<BR>आदितः, Mu. ii.;<BR>f. a boy:<BR>बाल एव or<BR>बाल्यात् प्रभृतिः, Vi.;<BR>f. behind:<BR>पृष्ठेनागत्य<BR>or<BR>पश्चा-<BR>देत्य,<BR>V iii.;<BR>f. humanity to corporeal beings<BR>ending in God:<BR>मनुष्यत्वादारभ्य ब्रह्मान्तेषु देहवत्सु, S.;<BR>f. God to columns:<BR>आब्रह्मस्तम्भपर्यन्तम्, S. p. b.;<BR>speaking of the difference of happiness f. humanity<BR>upwards, speaks of it among the lower (beings):<BR>मनुष्यत्वादूर्ध्वगतेषु सुखस्य तारतम्यमुक्तवाऽधोगतेषु, तदाह,<BR>S. com.; told (her) all f. the conquest:<BR>विजयादारभ्य सर्वमाचचक्षे, K.; f. me (=for me):<BR>मद्वचनात्, Sa.;<BR>the sixth king f. Nimi:<BR>निमेः षष्ठो<BR> महीपतिः, Ram. i. 68. 8.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

front
FRONT (subs.):<BR>I Face, brow: q.v.<BR>II In<BR>gen.:<BR>(1) अग्रम्,<BR>in f. of:<BR>अग्रतः (with gen.), Ku.:<BR>v. Before.;<BR>(2) अग्रभागः (= f. part);<BR>(3)<BR>अग्रभूमिः (= f. place), Ki.;<BR>(4) शिरस् (n.)<BR>(= head; q.v.),<BR>in f. of battle:<BR>रणशिरसि, Sa.<BR>From the f. as if dragged by the heart, on the<BR>back as if driven by Cupid:<BR>पुरस्तादाकृष्यमाणेव हृदयेन<BR> पृष्ठतः प्रेर्यमाणेव पुष्पधन्वना, K.;<BR>the leader should go<BR>in f.:<BR>नायकः पुरतो यायात्, Ka.; to place in f.:<BR>पुरस्करोति, Ka.;<BR>goer in f.:<BR>पुरोगः (गा, गं), etc,<BR>Ku.<BR>in f...... on the rear:<BR>पुरः, पूर्वतः॥॥।<BR> पश्चात्, Ka. xviii. 56. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

front
FRONT (adj.):<BR>(1) अग्र (f. ग्रा) (= fore);<BR>(2) सम्मुखीनः (ना, नं),<BR>f. window.:<BR>सम्मुखीनं<BR> वातायनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

front
FRONT (v.):<BR>(1) सम्मुखयति;<BR>(2) अभिमुखयति:<BR>v. To face, con-f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frontage
FRONTAGE: सम्मुखभागः, सम्मुखम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frontier
FRONTIER:<BR>I Subs: border: q.v.: प्रान्तः।<BR>II<BR>Adj.: सामन्तः (न्ता, न्तं),<BR>f. king:<BR>सामन्तः।<BR>VI<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frontispiece
FRONTISPIECE:<BR>I Of a book: प्रथमचित्रम् (?).<BR>II Of a building: सम्मुखम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frontlet
FRONTLET:<BR>I Lit.: ललाटिका।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>भ्रु(भ्रू)कुटिः; भ्रूभङ्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frost
FROST: no exact equiv.:<BR>(1) तुषारः;<BR>(2) प्रालेयः;<BR>(3) अवश्यायः would do. F.-bitten:<BR>(1) तुषारक्षतः<BR>(ता, तं), Ku.;<BR>(2) प्रालेयावततिम्लानः (ना, नं), Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frosty
FROSTY: अतिहिमः (म, मं),<BR>F. weather:<BR>तुषारकालः,<BR>Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

froth
FROTH (subs.):<BR>(1) फेनः (णः);<BR>(2) मण्डः (in<BR>boiling),<BR>removed the f.:<BR>मण्डमगालयत्, D. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

froth
FROTH (v.):<BR>(1) फेना(णा)यते (nomi.),<BR>f. ing<BR>ocean:<BR>फेनायमानं पतिमापगानाम्, Si. iii. 72.;<BR>(2)<BR>मण्डायते (in boiling);<BR>(3) फेनम् उद्गिरति (गॄ, c.<BR>6.) (as of horse), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frothiness
FROTHINESS:<BR>I Lit.: फेनिलता।<BR>II Emptiness:<BR>निःसारता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frothy
FROTHY:<BR>I Lit.: फेनि(णि)लः, (ला, लं); फेनलः<BR>(ला, लं).<BR>II Fig., empty: निःसारः (रा, रं);<BR>फेनोपमः (मा, मं),<BR>f. life:<BR>फेनोपमं जीवितम्, H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frouzy
FROUZY: पूतिगन्धः (न्धा, न्धं): v. Fetid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

froward
FROWARD: प्रतीपः (पा, पं): v. Perverse, ob-<BR>-stinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frowardly
FROWARDLY: प्रतीपम्: v. Perversely, obsti-<BR>-nately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frowardness
FROWARDNESS: प्रतीपता: v. Obstinacy, per-<BR>-verseness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frown
FROWN (subs.):<BR>(1) भ्रूभङ्गः,<BR>making a f.:<BR>भ्रूभङ्गमा-<BR>धाय, B. -आबध्य, com.;<BR>(2) भ्र(भ्रु)कुटिः, -टी,<BR>face<BR>bent with f.:<BR>भ्रूकुटिकुटिलं मुखम्, V. p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frown
FROWN (v.): भ्रूभङ्गं करोति; भ्रुकुटिं बघ्नाति (बन्ध्, c.<BR>9). etc.,<BR>you are f. ing at me:<BR>मय्येव भ्रूकुटिधरः<BR> संवृत्तः, Vi. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frowningly
FROWNINGLY:<BR>(1) भ्रूभङ्गं बद् ध्वा;<BR>(2) भ्रूकुटिं कृत्वा;<BR>(3) भ्रूमङ्गमाधाय।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frozen
FROZEN:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) शिलीभूतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2)<BR>घनः (ना, नं) (= thick),<BR>f. dew:<BR>घननीहारः, Ki.:<BR>v. To freeze.<BR>II Chilly;<BR>(1) नितान्तशीतः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(2) हिमप्रधानः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fructification
FRUCTIFICATION:<BR>I Lit.: फलदीकरणम्; better<BR>by verb.<BR>II The reproductive parts of a<BR>plant: प्रसूनम्; फलपुष्पम्।<BR>III The process:<BR>प्रसूनकॢप्तिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fructify
FRUCTIFY: फलवन्तम् (तीं, -त्) करोति; फलदीकरोति<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frugal
FRUGAL:<BR>(1) मितव्ययिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) परिमित-<BR>व्ययः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frugality
FRUGALITY:<BR>(1) मितव्ययिता;<BR>(2) परिमितव्ययः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frugally
FRUGALLY:<BR>I With frugality: मितव्ययेन,<BR> परि-,<BR>II Moderately, sparingly: मितम्, परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fruit
FRUIT:<BR>(1) (lit. and fig.),<BR>raw, ripe, dry, juicy,<BR>insect-contaminated f.:<BR>आमं, पक्वं, शुष्कं, सरसं,<BR> कीटद्गषितं फलम्, Bha.;<BR>and to enjoy the sweet f. s<BR>of the life-tree:<BR>भोक्तुं, स्वादु फलञ्च जीविततरोः, B. i.;<BR>you will get (its)<BR>f. also:<BR>फलमपि प्राप्स्यसि, Mr.<BR>ii.;<BR>considering very important production of<BR>f. s:<BR>गरीयसीं फलनिष्पत्तिं विगणय्य, Ki. ii. 35.;<BR>(2) प्रसवः (of trees, of animals), about f. s:<BR>प्रसवं प्रति, M. ix. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fruit
FRUIT, TO BEAR: फलति (फल्, c. 1.),<BR>b. s f.<BR>among the good:<BR>फलति साधुषु, Ma. n.;<BR>your<BR>wishes have borne f.:<BR>तव कामाः फलिताः, R.;<BR>about<BR>to b. f.:<BR>फलोन्मुखः (खा, खं), Vi.; b. f. in time:<BR>काले फलं बध्नन्ति, R. xii. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fruit-bearing
FRUIT-BEARING:<BR>(1) फलिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) फलभृत्<BR>(mfn.): v. Fruitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fruiterer
FRUITERER:<BR>(1) फलविक्रोतृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) फलविक्रयिन्<BR>(f. नी);<BR>(3) फलजीविन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fruitery
FRUITERY:<BR>I Fruits: फलानि (n. pl.).<BR>II A<BR>fruit-loft: फलागारम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fruitful
FRUITFUL:<BR>(1) फलवत् (f. ती);<BR>(2) फलिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) फलशालिन् (f. नी),<BR>f. action:<BR>फलशालिनी क्रिया,<BR>Ki. ii. 36.;<BR>(4) फलदः (दा, दं), फलदायिन् (f. नी),<BR>etc. (= fruit-producing),<BR>as a germ would<BR>become f. in time:<BR>यथाङ्कुरः काले फलप्रदो मवेत्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fruitefully
FRUITEFULLY:<BR>(1) फलवत्;<BR>(2) सफलम्;<BR>(3) प्रचुरम्<BR>(= copiously).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fruitfulness
FRUITFULNESS:<BR>(1) फलवत्ता;<BR>(2) फलशालिता;<BR>(3) फलप्रदत्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fruit-garden
FRUIT-GARDEN:<BR>(1) फलवाटिका;<BR>(2) फलोद्यानम्,<BR>Raj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fruition
FRUITION: सम्भोगः: v. Enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fruitless
FRUITLESS<BR>(1) निष्फलः (ला, लं), by all means<BR>(your)<BR>wisdom is f.:<BR>सर्वथा निष्फला प्रज्ञा, K.;<BR>(2) विफलः (ला, लं);<BR>(3) अफलः (ला, लं);<BR>(4) फलहीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(5) फलशून्यः (न्या, न्यं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fruitlessly
FRUITLESSLY:<BR>(1) निष्फलम्;<BR>(2) विफलम्;<BR>(3)<BR>व्यर्थम् (= in vain: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fruit-tree
FRUIT-TREE:<BR>(1) फलवान् वृक्षः, etc.;<BR>(2) वनस्पतिः<BR>(large f.), B. ii. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frustrate
FRUSTRATE:<BR>(1) विफलीकरोति,<BR>whose efforts were<BR>f. d:<BR>विफलीकृतयत्न (f. त्ना) Ki. xv. 46.;<BR>(2) व्यर्थी-<BR>करोति,<BR>finding her undertaking f. d:<BR>अस्या व्यवसायं<BR> व्यर्थीकृतमवसाय, N. iii. 6.;<BR>(3) मोघीकरोति;<BR>(4) निष्फलीकरोति;<BR>(5) विफलं (f. लां), मोघं (f.<BR>घां), etc. करोति, वितनोति (तन्, c. 8.)<BR>or<BR>विदधाति<BR>(धा, c. 3.).<BR>To be f. d:<BR>विफलीभवति, etc., K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frustration
FRUSTRATION:<BR>(1) by verb;<BR>(2) भङ्गः;<BR>(3)<BR>षिघातः<BR>or<BR>व्याघातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fry
FRY (subs.):<BR>I Of fishes:<BR>(1) क्षुद्रमत्स्यसंघातः;<BR>(2) पोताधानम् (= small f.), A.<BR>II Of men:<BR>“even the smaller f.”:<BR>क्षुद्रा अपि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fry
FRY (v. t.): भर्जयति, सं-, नि-, (c. of भृज्),<BR>to f. with<BR>oil:<BR>तैले भर्जयति, Bha.<BR>F. ed meat:<BR>मृष्टं मांसम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

frying-pan
FRYING-PAN:<BR>(1) भ्राष्टम्;<BR>(2) भ्रज्जनम्;<BR>(3)<BR>अम्बरीषम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fuddled
FUDDLED: मदेन<BR>or<BR>मधुना हृतचेतनः (ना, नं), K. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fudge
FUDGE: an exclamation:<BR>(1) हलम्;<BR>(2) कम्;<BR>(3) फस् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fuel
FUEL:<BR>(1) इन्धनम्;<BR>(2) समिध् (f.);<BR>(3) एधस् (n.);<BR>(4) इध्मम्। Ph.:<BR>to add. f. to the flames:<BR>क्षारं<BR> क्षते प्रक्षिपति, Mr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fugitive
FUGITIVE (adj.);<BR>I Fleeting: q.v.:<BR>(1)<BR>चञ्चलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) अचिरस्थायिन् (f. नी).<BR>II<BR>Running away: पलायितः (ता, तं); कृतपलायनः<BR>(ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fugitive
FUGITIVE (subs.): कृतपलायणः (ना, नं); पलायन-<BR>कारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fulcrum
FULCRUM: *आलम्बः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fulfil
FULFIL:<BR>I To fill up: q.v.<BR>II To carry<BR>into effect:<BR>(1) पूरयति (पूर्, c. 10.), f. ing<BR>(his)<BR>promise:<BR>पूरयित्वा प्रतिज्ञाम्, Ve. iv.;<BR>(2)<BR>सफलीकरोति,-कृरुते (कृ, c. 8.),<BR>f. our wishes:<BR>मनोरथान्नः<BR> सफलीकुरुष्व, Ki. iii. 54.;<BR>(3) निर्वाहयति (c. of<BR>वह) (to accomplish: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fulfiller
FULFILLER:<BR>(1) पूरकः, सम्-, परि-;<BR>(2) पूरयितृ (m.),<BR>परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fulfilment
FULFILMENT:<BR>(1) पूरणम्, परि-;<BR>(2) साधनम् (= ac-<BR>-complishment: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fulgency
FULGENCY: रोचिष्णुता।: v. Brightness, splend-<BR>-our.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fulgent
FULGENT: रोचिष्णु (mfn.): v. Bright, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

full
FULL (adj.):<BR>I Full of, abounding in:<BR>(1)<BR>पूर्ण (f. र्णा), परि-, सं-,<BR>a pot f. of Chātu:<BR>शक्तुपूर्ण-<BR>शरावः, H.; is seen every morning f. of gold:<BR>प्रातः प्रातः सुवर्ण पूर्णो घ्श्यते, D.;<BR>f. of water:<BR>सलिल-<BR>संपूर्ण (f. र्णा), Ve.;<BR>(2) -मयः (यी, यं) (fig.),<BR>f. of<BR>joy:<BR>आनन्दमयः (यी, यं), S.;<BR>(3) भृतः (ता, तं), सम्-,<BR>(rare), Vi.;<BR>(4) -वलः (ला, लं) (only in some<BR>cases)<BR>f. of reeds:<BR>नड्वलः (ला, लं), R.<BR>II Ample,<BR>copious: q.v.: पूर्ण (f. र्णा), सम्-, परि-।<BR>III<BR>Complete, entire: q.v.: पूर्ण (f. र्णा), सं-, परि-,<BR>f. youth:<BR>पूर्णयौवनम्;<BR>a f. year:<BR>पूर्णवर्षम् (adv.);<BR>f. speed:<BR>पूर्णवेगः M.n.<BR>IV Mature: q.v.:<BR>परिणतः (ता, तं). V. Of colour: घोरः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

full
FULL (adv.): पूर्णम्, सं-, परि-,<BR>f. blown:<BR>पूर्णविकासिन्<BR>(f. नी);<BR>f. -bodied wine:<BR>*पुष्टं मद्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

full
FULL (v.):<BR>I Intrans: पूर्ण (f. र्णा) भवति।<BR>II<BR>Trans:<BR>(1) श्लक्ष्णयति (nomi.), to f. cloth:<BR>श्लक्ष्णयति वस्त्रम्, S.k.;<BR>(2) श्लक्ष्णीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

full-grown
FULL-GROWN:<BR>I Lit.: पूर्णयौवनः (ना, नं).<BR>II<BR>Fig., mature: पक्वः (क्वा, क्वं), परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

full-length
FULL-LENGTH (adj.): Ph.:<BR>f. portrait:<BR>देहदीर्ध-<BR>चित्रम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

full-moon
FULL-MOON:<BR>(1) पूर्णचन्द्रः and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(2) सकलेन्दुः, V.;<BR>(3) कठोरताराधिपः (rare), Si.<BR>The lunar day of f.:<BR>(1) पूर्णिमा;<BR>(2) पौर्ण-<BR>मासी;<BR>(3) राका। (rare), Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fuller
FULLER: रजकः (= washerman),<BR>f.'s earth:<BR>रजक-<BR>मृत्तिका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fullness
FULLNESS, FULNESS:<BR>I The state of being<BR>full:<BR>(1) पूर्णता, सं-;<BR>(2) पूर्तिः, परि-, (rare).<BR>II<BR>Abundance, sufficiency: q.v.:<BR>(1) पूर्णता;<BR>(2) बाहुल्यम्।<BR>III Completeness:<BR>(1) पूर्णता;<BR> परिपाकः (= maturity).<BR>IV Of colour: घोरता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fully
FULLY:<BR>I Completely, altogether:<BR>(1)<BR>सम्पूर्णम्;<BR>(2) अशेषेण।<BR>II At length:<BR>(1) विस्तरेण;<BR>(2) सुविस्तरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fulminate
FULMINATE (v.):<BR>I Lit., to thunder: स्फूर्जति<BR>(स्फूर्ज्, c. 1.).<BR>II Fig., to send out: स्फूर्जयति<BR>(c. of स्फूर्ज्) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fulmination
FULMINATION: स्फूर्जितम्, with f.s of thunder:<BR>स्फूर्जथुस्फूर्जितैः, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fulsome
FULSOME:<BR>I Nauseous, disgusting: कुत्सितः [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">Page303</a>]<BR>(ता, तं).<BR>II Coarse, obscene: गर्हितः (ता, तं),<BR>f. flattery:<BR>गर्हितस्तवः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fulsomely
FULSOMELY:<BR>(1) गर्हितम्;<BR>(2) कुत्सितम्;<BR>(3)<BR>बीभत्सम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fulsomeness
FULSOMENESS:<BR>(1) गर्हितता;<BR>(2) बीभत्सता;<BR>(3)<BR>कुत्सितता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fumble
FUMBLE: सम्भ्रान्तः (न्ता, न्तं) परामृशति (मृश्,<BR>c. 6.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fumbler
FUMBLER: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fumblingly
FUMBLINGLY:<BR>(1) सम्भ्रान्तः (न्ता, न्तं) (= con-<BR>-fused);<BR>(2) अपरूपम् (= awkwardly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fume
FUME (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: धूमः (पः),<BR>“f. s. of<BR>wine”<BR>*मद्यधूपाः।<BR>II Of rage: संरम्भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fume
FUME (v.i.):<BR>I Lit.: धूमा(पा)यते (nomi.).<BR>II<BR>Fig.: to rage: संरब्ध (f. ब्धा) भवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fumid
FUMID:<BR>(1) सधूमः (मा, मं);<BR>(2) धूमान्वितः (ता, तं);<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fumigate
FUMIGATE: (v.t.):<BR>(1) धूपायति (nomi.);<BR>(2)<BR>वासयति (वास्, c. 10.) (= to perfume).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fumigation
FUMIGATION:<BR>(1) expr. by verb:<BR>(2) वासनम्,<BR> अधि-, अनु-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fuming
FUMING: संरब्धः (ब्धा, ब्धं): v. Enraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fuminer
FUMINER, FUMITORY: *कुधूमः; दुर्गन्धौषधिभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fun
FUN: परिहासः (= jest: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

function
FUNCTION:<BR>I Work: q.v.: व्यापारः।<BR>II<BR>Action: q.v.: वृत्तिः,<BR>f. of the heart:<BR>हृदयवृत्तिः।<BR>III Math. t.t.: वृत्तिः,<BR>f. of x:<BR>*शस्य वृत्तिः;(श)वृं।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

functionary
FUNCTIONARY: अधिकृतः v. Officer, employee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fund
FUND (subs.):<BR>I Stock, capital: q.v.: सार-<BR>धनम्।<BR>II A store, supply: कोषः,<BR>“an inex-<BR>haustible f. of stories”:<BR>अक्षय्यकथाकोपः।<BR>III In pl.,<BR>public f. s:<BR>*राजर्णम्; राष्ट्रर्णम्। Ph.: sinking f.:<BR>*शोधनमूलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fundament
FUNDAMENT:<BR>(1) गुदम्;<BR>(2) गुह्यम्;<BR>(3) अपानम्;<BR>(4) पायुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fundamental
FUNDAMENTAL: मूल-, in comp.,<BR>f. bodies:<BR>मूल-<BR>पदार्थाः;<BR>f. cause:<BR>मूलकारणम्;<BR>f. sound:<BR>मूलध्वनिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fundamentally
FUNDAMENTALLY:<BR>(1) मूलतः;<BR>(2) सारतः;<BR>(3)<BR>तत्त्वतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fund-holder
FUND-HOLDER: *राजर्णदातृ (f. त्री); राष्ट्रर्णदातृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

funeral
FUNERAL (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अन्त्येष्टः, -क्रिया;<BR>(2) और्ध्वदेहिकम्, -क्रिया;<BR>(3) प्रेतकार्यम्।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>f. procession:<BR>प्रेतयात्रा (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

funeral
FUNERAL (adj.): और्ध्वदेहिकः (की, कं). Ph.:<BR>f.<BR>ceremony:<BR>श्राद्धम्;<BR>f. fire:<BR>चिताग्निः; f. procession:<BR>प्रेतयात्रा; f. hymn (in burning): प्रेतदाहमन्त्रः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

funereal
FUNEREAL: शोकविप्लुतः (ता, तं): v. Sorrowful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fungous
FUNGOUS: छत्रोपमः (मा, मं); छत्रसन्निभः (भा, भं), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fungus
FUNGUS:<BR>(1) छत्रम्, -त्रा;<BR>(2) छत्र(त्रा)कम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

funnel
FUNNEL: चुङ्गी (in modern vernaculars),<BR>f.<BR>form, f. -shaped<BR>*चुङ्ग्याकारः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

funny
FUNNY:<BR>(1) हास्यकरः (री, रं);<BR>(2) हास्यजननः<BR>(नी, नं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fur
FUR (subs.):<BR>I Fine hair: सूक्ष्मलो(रो)मन्<BR>(n.).<BR>II Skin with f.: सूक्ष्भलोमचर्मन् (n.) (?).<BR>III Of the tongue: कुल(ल्व)कम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furbelow
FURBELOW: a flounce: प्रम्बालम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furbish
FURBISH:<BR>(1) प्रमाजर्यति<BR>or<BR>मार्ष्टि (मृज्, c. 10.<BR>and 2.);<BR>(2) धावति (धाव्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furbisher
FURBISHER:<BR>(1) प्रमार्जकः;<BR>(2) धावकः<BR>F. of<BR>weapons:<BR>अस्त्रमार्जः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furious
FURIOUS:<BR>I Mad, violent: मत्तः (त्ता, त्तं),<BR>f.<BR>elephant:<BR>मत्तगजः।<BR>II Strong, turbulent: q.v.:<BR>चण्डः (ण्डा, ण्डां),<BR>f. wind:<BR>चण्डवातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furiously
FURIOUSLY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furiousness
FURIOUSNESS: v. Fury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furl
FURL (v.): पिण्डीकरोति, Mr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furlong
FURLONG: नल्वः; क्रोशस्य षोडशभागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furlough
FURLOUGH: *कर्म्मावसरः; विदायः (= leave).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furnace
FURNACE:<BR>(1) उध्मानम्;<BR>(2) अग्निकुण्डम्। A port-<BR>able f.:<BR>(1) अङ्गारधानिका;<BR>(2) अङ्गारशकटी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furnish
FURNISH:<BR>I In gen.: no equiv.<BR>(1) योजयति,<BR> सं-, (युज्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) सं-बिभर्ति (भृ, c. 3.);<BR>(3) उपपादयति (c. of पद्).<BR>II To offer:<BR>(1)<BR>ददाति (दा, c. 3.);<BR>(2) प्रतिपादयति (c. of पद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furnished
FURNISHED: Ph.:<BR>f. house:<BR>परिवर्हवन्ति वेश्मानि (?),<BR>R. xiv. 15.; सोपकरणानि गृहाणि (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furniture
FURNITURE: उपकरणानि (n. pl.) (?); परिवर्हः (?), R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furred
FURRED, FURRY:<BR>I Lit.: सूक्ष्मलोमशः (शा, शं);<BR>सूक्ष्मरोमान्वितः (ता, तं).<BR>II Of the tongue:<BR>कुलु(ल्व)किन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furrier
FURRIER: पशुलोमजीविन् (m.) (?); सूक्ष्मलोमविक्रेतृ<BR>(m.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furrow
FURROW (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) सीता;<BR>(2)<BR>लाङ्गलपद्धतिः।<BR>II A groove: रेखा।<BR>III Wrinkle:<BR>q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furrow
FURROW (v.): दारयति, वि- (द्ध, c. 10.), R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furrowed
FURROWED (adj.): i.e. wrinkled: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

further
FURTHER (v.):<BR>(1) अनुकूलयति (nomi.) (= to be<BR>friend);<BR>(2) वर्धयति (c. of वृध्) (= to advance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

further
FURTHER (adj.):<BR>I More distant:<BR>(1)<BR>दूरतरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) दवीयस् (f. सी).<BR>II As<BR>opposed to nearer:<BR>(1) दूरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2)<BR>दूरस्थः (स्था, स्थं।)<BR>III Additional:<BR>(1) अधिकः<BR>(का, कं);<BR>(2) अपरः (रा, रं) (= other).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

further
FURTHER (adv.):<BR>I Of distance:<BR>(1) दूरतरभ्;<BR>(2) दवीयस्।<BR>II In. addition: अधिकम्।<BR>III<BR>Moreover: अपरञ्च।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furtherance
FURTHERANCE: expr. by verb: v. Further.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furtherer
FURTHERER:<BR>(1) सहायः (= helper);<BR>(2) better<BR>by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furthermore
FURTHERMORE: अपरञ्च: v. Moreover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furtive
FURTIVE: v. Stolen, secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furtively
FURTIVELY: v. Stealth (by), secretly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fury
FURY:<BR>I Madness: मत्तता,<BR>in f.:<BR>मत्तः (त्ता, त्तं).<BR>II Violence: चण्डता, प्र-, उत्-,<BR>III Violent<BR>rage: संरम्भः।<BR>IV A deity:<BR>(1) चण्डा;<BR>(2) भैरवी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

furze
FURZE: वीतपुष्पः सदापर्णो गुल्मभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fuse
FUSE (v.):<BR>I Trans.: विलाययति (c. of ली): v.<BR>To melt.<BR>II Intrans: विलीयते (ली, c. 4.). v.:<BR>Melt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fusee
FUSEE:<BR>I Of a watch: *शङ्कुचक्रम्।<BR>II A light<BR>musket: *लधुबन्दुकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fusible
FUSIBLE:<BR>(1) विलयनीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) गलनीयः<BR>(या, यं);<BR>(3) द्राव्य (f. व्या)<BR>or<BR>द्रवणीयः (या, यं), वि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fusibility
FUSIBILITY:<BR>(1) विलयनीयता;<BR>(2) गलनीयता;<BR>(3)<BR>द्राव्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fusion
FUSION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) विलयनम्;<BR>(2) गलनम्;<BR>(3) विद्रावणम्।<BR>II Union: q.v.: संयोगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fuss
FUSS (subs.):<BR>(1) आडम्बरः (= show);<BR>(2) सम्भ्रमः<BR>(= bustle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fussy
FUSSY:<BR>(1) आडम्बरप्रियः (या, यं);<BR>(2) सम्भ्रमशीलः<BR>(ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fustian
FUSTIAN:<BR>I Coarse cloth: स्थूलपट्टम्।<BR>II Of<BR>language: अतिशयोक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fustigation
FUSTIGATION: वेत्राघातः: v. Flogging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fustiness
FUSTINESS:<BR>I Lit.: दुर्गन्धता।<BR>II Dryness: शुष्कता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

fusty
FUSTY:<BR>I Rank: दुर्गन्धः (न्धा, न्धं).<BR>II Dry:<BR>शुष्कः (ष्का, ष्कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

futile
FUTILE: निरर्थकः (का, कं): v. Useless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

futility
FUTILITY:<BR>(1) निरर्थकता;<BR>(2) निष्फलता: v.<BR>Uselessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

future
FUTURE (adj.):<BR>(1) भविष्यत् (f. न्ती)<BR>or<BR>मविष्यः<BR>(ष्या, ष्यं),<BR>of the f. husband:<BR>मविष्यतः पत्युः, Ku.<BR>iii. 58.;<BR>f. kings:<BR>भविष्याः पार्थवाः, V.p.;<BR>(2)<BR>भाविन् (f. नी), the past, the present and the f.:<BR>समतीतञ्च भवच्च भावि च, R viii. 78.;<BR>(3) अनागतः<BR>(ता, तं) (= what is not present), sees the f.:<BR>अनागतं पश्यति, Vi.;<BR>(4) भव्य (f. व्या) (rare), Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

future
FUTURE (subs.): v. Future (adj.) and futurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

futurity
FUTURITY:<BR>(1) आयतिः;<BR>(2) उदर्कः;<BR>(3) उत्तर-<BR>कालः and sim comp.s. F. (as opposed to this<BR>world): परकालः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gabardine
GABARDINE: स्थूलमाप्रपदीनम् (?); *गोवर्धनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gabble
GABBLE: जल्पति (जल्प्, c. 1.): v. To Babble,<BR>chatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gabbler
GABBLER: जल्पाकः (की, कं): v. Babbler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gabion
GABION: *गोपकः; शत्रोरग्नेर्गोपको मृद्गर्भः करण्डविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gable
GABLE: त्रिकोणशिरस् (n.) (?).<BR>G. window:<BR>त्रिकोण-<BR>वातायनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gad
GAD (subs.):<BR>I Of a weapon: अग्रम्,<BR>g. of<BR>an arrow:<BR>बाणाग्रम्।<BR>II A spike or wedge:<BR>कीलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gad
GAD (v.i.): अटति (अट्, c. 1.): v. To roam,<BR>wander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gadder
GADDER: वृथाभ्रमणकारिन् (f. णी): v. Rambler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gadfly
GADFLY:<BR>(1) दंशः, -शी;<BR>(2) दंशकः;<BR>(3)<BR>गोमक्षिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gag
GAG (subs.):<BR>(1) मुखबन्धनी;<BR>(2) मुखरोधनम् (?),<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gag
GAG (v.): मुखं बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.), रुणद्धि। नि-,<BR>(रुध्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gage
GAGE (subs.):<BR>I Pledge: q.v.: बन्धकः।<BR>II<BR>A challenge to combat.: perh. क्षेपः,<BR>“there I<BR>throw my g.”:<BR>अत्राहं क्षेपं क्षिपामि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gage
GAGE (v.):<BR>I To bind: q.v.<BR>II To gauge:<BR>q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gaggling
GAGGLING: Of geese:<BR>(1) हंसनादः; हंसनिस्वनः,<BR>Ki.;<BR>(2) मरालकूजितम्, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gaiety
GAIETY:<BR>(1) आमोदः;<BR>(2) प्रमोदः: v. Mirth,<BR>cheerfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gaily
GAILY:<BR>I Cheerfully: सोल्लासम्।<BR>II Beauti-<BR>-fully: सुन्दरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gain
GAIN (subs.):<BR>(1) लाभः,<BR>are the g. s of your<BR>business thriving:<BR>अपि प्रचीयन्ते संव्य्वहाराणां लाभा वः,<BR>Mu. i.;<BR>participating good g. s:<BR>उत्तमलाभभाज्<BR>(min.), Si. iii. 76.;<BR>(2) वृद्धिः (= increase),<BR>considering g. and loss:<BR>वृद्धिक्षयौ विचार्य, M.<BR>viii. 401.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gain
GAIN (v.t.):<BR>I To obtain, acquire: q.v.:<BR>लभते (लभ्, c. 1.),<BR>g. ed by knowledge:<BR>विद्यया लब्ध<BR>(f. ब्धा), Y.;<BR>if you again g. your place:<BR>यदि लब्धं<BR> पुनरात्मनः पदम्, Ki.<BR>II To be successful in:<BR>जयति (जि, c. 1.),<BR>to g. a battle:<BR>युद्धं जयति<BR>or<BR>युद्धे<BR> जयं लभते;<BR>one who g.s a case:<BR>जयिन् (f. नी), Mit.<BR>III To arrive at: q.v.: प्राप्नोति (आप्, c. 5.).<BR>IV Of time:<BR>it g. s an hour a day:<BR>*प्रत्यह-<BR>मस्येका घटिका वर्धते (वृध्, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>उपचीयते (pass.<BR>of चि). Ph:<BR>to g. ground:<BR>उप-चीयते, प्र-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gain on or upon
GAIN ON or UPON: “g. ed u. the Venetains”<BR>*वैनसिकेभ्यः वृद्धिं प्रापुः;<BR>“so far g. ed on the<BR>emperor”:<BR>*अधिराजमीदृगनुकूलीचकार।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gain over
GAIN OVER: धनदानादिना आत्मीयं (f. यां) करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gainer
GAINER: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gainful
GAINFUL: लामकरः (री, रं): v. Profitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gainless
GAINLESS: अलाभः (भा, भं): v. Unprofitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gainsay
GAINSAY: प्रत्याख्याति (ख्या, c. 2.): v. To con-<BR>-tradict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gait
GAIT:<BR>(1) गतिः;<BR>(2) चलनम्;<BR>(3) गमनम् as in<BR>गजगमनः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gaiter
GAITER: गुल्फत्राणम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gala-day
GALA-DAY:<BR>(1) उत्सवदिनम्;<BR>(2) प्रमोददिवसः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

galaxy
GALAXY:<BR>I The milky-way: सुरनदी।<BR>II A<BR>splendid^1 assemblage<BR>“of g. poets”:<BR>महाकवीनां<BR> समागमः।<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

galban
GALBAN, GALBANUM: *गाल्वनम्; निर्यासविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gale
GALE: वातः,<BR>hard g.:<BR>चण्डवातः: v. Wind, breeze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gall
GALL (subs.):<BR>I The bile: पित्तम्, g.-bladder:<BR>पित्ताशयः।<BR>II Spite, malignity: q.v.: विषम्<BR>(= poison). Ph.:<BR>to add g. to bitterness:<BR>क्षते<BR> क्षारं क्षिपति, P.<BR>III A sore by rubbing: क्षतम्<BR>(gen. term),<BR>IV Of a tree: मलम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gall
GALL (v.t.):<BR>I To chafe: घर्षणेन क्षिणोति<BR>(क्षि, c. 5.).<BR>II To tease, vex: q.v.: बाधते<BR>(बाध्, c. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gall-fly
GALL-FLY: लतामक्षिका (after गोमक्षिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gall-stone
GALL-STONE: पित्ताशयशर्करा: v. Stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gallant
GALLANT (adj.):<BR>I Handsome, showy: q.v.:<BR>शोभनः (ना, नं).<BR>II Brave, courageous: q.v.;<BR>शूरः (रा, रं).<BR>III Chivalrous: दक्षिण (f. णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gallant
GALLANT (subs.):<BR>I Lover: वल्लभः।<BR>II Para-<BR>-mour: जारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gallantly
GALLANTLY:<BR>I Bravely: ससाहसम्।<BR>II Poli-<BR>-tely:<BR>(1) दक्षिणम्;<BR>(2) दाक्षिण्येन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gallantry
GALLANTRY:<BR>I Courage, bravery: q.v.:<BR>शौर्यम्।<BR>II Politeness: दाक्षिण्यम्।<BR>III Amour:<BR>प्रणयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

galleon
GALLEON: महापोतः: v. Ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gallery
GALLERY:<BR>I A room: कोष्ठः,<BR>picture g.:<BR>*चित्र-<BR>कीष्ठः।<BR>II A raised structure: मञ्चाः (m. pl.),<BR>R. vi. 1.,<BR>ladies' g.:<BR>योषितां मञ्चाः, V.p. v. 20.<BR>26.<BR>III A covered passage: छन्नपथः and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR>IV Underground: कुल्या<BR>(= mine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

galley
GALLEY:<BR>I A long boat: नोः।<BR>II The cook-<BR>-room of a man-of-war: पाकस्थली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

galley-slave
GALLEY-SLAVE: नौदासः (?); पोतदासः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gallic
GALLIC, -AN: *फरासीयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gallicism
GALLICISM: *फरासीयनीतिः; फरासीयभाषरीतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gallinule
GALLINULE: जलकुक्कुटः (f. टी); जलरङ्कुः, Wilson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

galling
GALLING (adj.):<BR>(1) कटु (mfn.) (= bitter);<BR>(2) मर्माविध् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gallipot
GALLIPOT: घटी (?): v. Pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gallon
GALLON: द्रवमानविशेषः; अर्द्धप्रस्थः, Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gallop
GALLOP (v.):<BR>I Of the animal:<BR>(1) प्लवते (प्लु,<BR>c. 1.);<BR>(2) वल्गति (वल्ग्, c. 1.).<BR>II Of<BR>the rider: perh प्लुतगत्या चलति (चल्, c. 1.);<BR>पुलायितेन गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gallop
GALLOP (subs.):<BR>(1) प्लुतम्;<BR>(2) पुलायितम्;<BR>(3)<BR>वल्गितम्।<BR>Full g:<BR>पूर्णवेगा गतिः, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gallows
GALLOWS: बद्धकाष्ठम् (?); बद्धदारु (n.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

galvanic
GALVANIC: *गल्वनीयः (या, यं); गाल्वनं (नी, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

galvanize
GALVANIZE: *गाल्वनीकरोति,<BR>g. d iron:<BR>*गाल्वनी-<BR>कृतलोहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gamble
GAMBLE:<BR>(1) दीव्यति (दिव्, c. 4.), g. s. on [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=306" target="_blank">Page306</a>]<BR>hundred: शतस्य दीव्यति, S. k.;<BR>(2) द्युतं करोति or<BR>सेवते, नि- (सेव्, c. 1.), M. ix. 228.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gambler
GAMBLER:<BR>(1) द्यूत करः<BR>or<BR>-कारः;<BR>(2) देवितृ (m.),<BR>Mah.;<BR>(3) दुरोदरः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gambling
GAMBLING:<BR>(1) द्यूतम्;<BR>(2) देवनम्, M.;<BR>(3) दुरोदरम्<BR>(rare);<BR>(4) कैतवम् (rare).<BR>G. -assembly:<BR>द्यूत-<BR>सभा<BR>or<BR>द्यूतसमाजम्।<BR>Its president:<BR>सभिकः। G. -house:<BR>द्यूतशाला।<BR>G. -table, g. -board:<BR>द्यूतफलकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gambol
GAMBOL (subs.): नृत्यम् (= dance);<BR>(2) क्रीडा<BR>(= sport).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gambol
GAMBOL (v.):<BR>(1) नृत्यति (नृत्, c. 4.) (= to<BR>dance);<BR>(2) क्रीडति (= to play).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

game
GAME:<BR>I Sport:<BR>(1) क्रीडा,<BR>shewed other good<BR>g. s with a ball:<BR>क्रीडान्तराणि दर्शनीयानि कन्दुकेनाद-<BR>र्शयत्, D.;<BR>(2) खेला, let us have a g. at chess:<BR>*चतुरङ्गखेलां करवाव, Ph.:<BR>you are making a g. of<BR>me:<BR>मया सह क्रीडां<BR>or<BR>खेलां करोषि।<BR>II In hunting:<BR>जाङ्गलः, almost all g. is light and strengthening:<BR>जाङ्गलाः प्रायशः सर्वे लघवो बलवर्धनाः, Bha.<BR>III<BR>Project, scheme: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

game-cock
GAME-COCK:<BR>(1) योधकुक्कुटः;<BR>(2) चरणायुधः (poet),<BR>कथमुपक्रान्तएव क्रूरधारचरणशस्त्रयो श्चरणायुधयोः कलहः, V. t.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

game-egg
GAME-EGG: योधकुक्कु टगर्भमण्डम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

game-keeper
GAME-KEEPER: जाङ्गलपालः (after वनपालः of N.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gamesome
GAMESOME:<BR>(1) क्रीडाप्रियः (या, यं);<BR>(2) खेला-<BR>प्रियः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gamester
GAMESTER: द्यूतकरः: v. Gambler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gaming
GAMING: v. Gambling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gammon
GAMMON:<BR>I Smoked ham: धूपितवल्ल रम् (?).<BR>II<BR>A game: v. Back-g.<BR>III An imposition:<BR>(1) छलम्;<BR>(2) कपटम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gamut
