gauge
GAUGE (v.): मापयति (c. of मा): v. To mea-<BR>-sure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gauge
GAUGE (subs.): मापः,<BR>rain-g.:<BR>*वृष्टिमापः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gauger
GAUGER: मापकः, परि-; मापयितृ (m.) परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gaunt
GAUNT: कृशः (शा, शं), परि-: v. Lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gauntlet
GAUNTLET: हस्तत्राणम्; गोधा (?), Mah. Ph.:<BR>to<BR>throw down, take up the g.:<BR>युद्धाय आह्वानं करोति,<BR> परिगृह्णाति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gauze
GAUZE: गजम् (in vernacular); सूक्ष्मांशुकविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gauzy
GAUZY: गजसन्निभः (भा, भं); सूक्ष्म (f. क्ष्मा)<BR>(= thin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gay
GAY:<BR>I Merry:<BR>(1) आमोदिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रमोदिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) प्रफुल्लः (ल्ला, ल्लं) (= cheer-<BR>-ful).<BR>II Gaudy: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gaze
GAZE (v.):<BR>(1) बद्धलक्ष्येण<BR>or<BR>स्थिरदृष्ट्या निरीक्षते [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">Page308</a>]<BR>(ईक्ष्, c. 1.), अवलोकयति (लोक्, c. 10.), etc.<BR>v. To see, look;<BR>(2) निर्वर्णयति (वर्ण्, c. 10.)<BR>(= to look with attention),<BR>g. ing by turn at<BR>me and the painted man:<BR>लिखितं पुरुषं माञ्च पर्यायेण<BR> निर्वर्णयन्ती, D. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gaze
GAZE (subs.):<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) स्थिदृष्टिः;<BR>(2)<BR>बद्धदृष्टिः, नि-।<BR>II The object: स्थिर-<BR>or<BR>बद्धलक्ष्यम्,<BR>K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gazelle
GAZELLE: prob. एणः: v. Deer. G.-eyed:<BR>एणाक्ष (f. क्षी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gazette
GAZETTE (subs.): *वार्तावहः,<BR>the Assam g.:<BR>*असम-<BR>वार्तावहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gazetteer
GAZETTEER:<BR>I A gazetter-writer: *वार्तावह-<BR>लेखकः।<BR>II Of places: *स्थानकोषः, g. of India<BR>*भारतवर्षस्थानकोषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gazing-stock
GAZING-STOCK: दर्शनपात्रम् (?); परिहासभूमिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gear
GEAR: उपकरणम्। Ph.:<BR>in, out of g.:<BR>संलग्न (f. ग्ना),<BR>विलग्न (f. ग्ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gelatine
GELATINE: घनसारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gelatinous
GELATINOUS: *घनसारसदृशः (शी, शं): v. Viscus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

geld
GELD:<BR>I Subs.: v. Money.<BR>II Verb: v.<BR>To castrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gelder
GELDER:<BR>(1) वृषणोत्पाटकः (?);<BR>(2) मुष्कच्छेदकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gelding
GELDING:<BR>I Castration: q.v. मुष्कच्छेदः।<BR>II<BR>A. gelded horse: छिन्नमुष्कोऽश्वः (?) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gem
GEM (subs.):<BR>(1) रत्नम् (lit. and fig.),<BR>a g. does<BR>not seek, but it is sought:<BR>न रत्नमन्विव्यति मृग्यते हि<BR> तत्, Ku.; the nine g.s (of the Court of Vikramā-<BR>ditya); नवरत्नानि;<BR>a necklace of g. s:<BR>रत्नमाला;<BR>(2) मणिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gem
GEM (v.t.): v. To stud, adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gemini
GEMINI: मिथुनः, -राशिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gemmed
GEMMED:<BR>(1) मणिमयः (यी, यं);<BR>(2) रत्नखचितः<BR>(ता, तं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gender
GENDER: लिङ्गम्,<BR>of masculine g.:<BR>पुंलिङ्गः;<BR>of feminine<BR>g.:<BR>स्त्रीलिङ्गा;<BR>of neuter g.:<BR>क्लीवलिङ्गम्; of two g. s:<BR>द्विलिङ्ग (ङ्गा, ङ्गं),<BR>of three g.s:<BR>त्रिलिङ्गः (ङ्गा, ङ्गं);<BR>a predicative noun of invariable g.:<BR>अजहल्लिङ्गः;<BR>these (words)<BR>are of masculine g.:<BR>एतानि पुंसि स्युः;<BR>the (words) अर्चिः<BR>is of feminine and neuter g.:<BR>अर्चिः<BR> सित्रयान्नपुंसके च स्यात्, S. k.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genealogical
GENEALOGICAL: expr. by comp., g. writer:<BR>वंशावलिलेखकः;<BR>g. tree:<BR>वंशवृक्षः; g. table:<BR>वंशक्रमः (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genealogically
GENEALOGICALLY:<BR>(1) वंशावलिक्रमेण;<BR>(2) वंशानु-<BR>सारेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genealogist
GENEALOGIST:<BR>(1) वंशक्रमज्ञः;<BR>(2) वंशज्ञः;<BR>(3)<BR>अनवयज्ञः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genealogy
GENEALOGY:<BR>(1) बंशावलिः, -ली;<BR>(2) often by<BR>sim. वंशः (= dynasty),<BR>I. will tell you the g. of<BR>Yadu:<BR>यदोर्वंशमहं कथयामि, V.p.;<BR>who had heard<BR>of the g. of kings:<BR>नृपाणां श्रुतवृत्तवंशा, R. vi. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

general
GENERAL (adj.): साधारणः (णी, णं): v. Com-<BR>-mon, usual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

general
GENERAL, IN:<BR>(1) साधारण्येन;<BR>(2) प्रायेण (=<BR>usually).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

general
GENERAL (subs.):<BR>I Commander of an army:<BR>(1) सेनापतिः;<BR>(2) सेनानी;<BR>(3) बलाध्यक्षः;<BR>(4)<BR>सेनानायकः;<BR>(5) चमूपतिः (= g. of a division);<BR>(6)<BR>*पृतनापतिः (= brigadier-g.).<BR>II A master of<BR>the military art:<BR>(1) रणपण्डितः;<BR>(2) युद्धामिज्ञ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

generalissimo
GENERALISSIMO:<BR>(1) मुख्यसेनापतिः;<BR>(2) बलाध्यक्षः:<BR>v. General.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

generality
GENERALITY:<BR>I The bulk: expr. by प्रायेण,<BR>g. of mankind:<BR>प्रायेण सर्वे मनुष्याः।<BR>II A general<BR>statement: साधारणवाक्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

generalization
GENERALIZATION: सामान्यप्रत्यक्षम् (?); बहुषु साधारण-<BR>धर्मोपलब्धिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

generalize
GENERALIZE:<BR>I In gen.: साधारणधर्मं प्रदर्शयति<BR>(दृश्, c. 10.) (= to shew)<BR>or<BR>उपलभते (लम्, c.<BR>1.) (to perceive) (?),<BR>Newton g. d the motions<BR>of planets,<BR>*नूटनो ग्रहगतीनां साधारणधर्मं प्रदर्शयामास,<BR>v.<BR>V d. ii. 2.<BR>II To derive, collect: संगृह्बाति<BR>(ग्रह्, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

generally
GENERALLY:<BR>I In general:<BR>(1) साधारण्येन;<BR>(2) सामान्यतः;<BR>(3) साधारणतः।<BR>II Mostly:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रायेण;<BR>(2) प्रायशः;<BR>(3) प्रायः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

generalship
GENERALSHIP:<BR>I The office:<BR>(1) सैनापत्यम्;<BR>(2) सेनापतित्वम्; etc.: v. General.<BR>II A<BR>general's skill:<BR>(1) रणपाण्डित्यम्;<BR>(2) युद्धनैपुण्यम्;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

generate
GENERATE: जनयति (c. of जन्): v. To beget,<BR>produce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

generation
GENERATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) जननम्, प्र-;<BR>(2)<BR>उत्पादनम्;<BR>(3) प्रसवः।<BR>II Formation:<BR>(1) by [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">Page309</a>]<BR>verb;<BR>(2) उत्पत्तिः।<BR>III Offspring: q.v.:<BR>प्रसवः, प्रसूतिः।<BR>IV Race: q.v.: वंशः। V. A<BR>rank in genealogy: पुरुषाः,<BR>seven g.s:<BR>सप्त पुरुषाः।<BR>VI People living at one period: expr. by<BR>circumlo.;<BR>he survived his g.:<BR>*स समकालीनपुरुषेम्यो<BR> दीर्धं जिजीव; saw three g. s of men pass away:<BR>*त्रिकालीनपुरूषाणामत्यन्यं ददर्श।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

generative
GENERATIVE: जननः (नी, नं),<BR>g. power:<BR>प्रजननशक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

generator
GENERATOR: जनयितृ (f. त्री): v. Parent,<BR>begetter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

generic
GENERIC: जातिगतः (ता, तं) (?), g. difference:<BR>जातिगतप्रभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

generically
GENERICALLY: जातितः (?); जात्या (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

generosity
GENEROSITY: औदार्यम्: v. Kindness, liberality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

generous
GENEROUS:<BR>(1) उदारः (रा, रं): v. Liberal;<BR>(2)<BR>दयालुः (mfn.): v. Kind;<BR>(3) त्यागशीलः (ला,<BR> लं): v. Munificent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genesis
GENESIS:<BR>I Birth: q.v.: जन्मन् (n.).<BR>II Of<BR>the Bible: आदिकाण्डाः (after Ram.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genial
GENIAL:<BR>I Generative: q.v.<BR>II Cheering:<BR>(1) सुखदः (दा, दं);<BR>(2) रुचिरः (रा, रं).<BR>III<BR>In disposition: उदारः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

geniality
GENIALITY:<BR>(1) प्रफुल्लता;<BR>(2) उदारता (= liberality).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genially
GENIALLY:<BR>(1) प्रफुल्लम्;<BR>(2) प्रसन्नचित्तेन;<BR>(3)<BR>सोल्लासम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genital
GENITAL: v. Generative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genitals
GENITALS: जननाङ्गानि (n. pl.) (?); गुप्ताङ्गानि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genitive
GENITIVE: षष्ठी,<BR>subjective, objective g.:<BR>कर्तरि,<BR> कर्मणि षष्ठी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genius
GENIUS:<BR>I Mental power: शक्तिः, g., skill:<BR>श्क्तिर्निपुणता, Kav. i. 3.;<BR>these are surely dis-<BR>plays of poetic g.:<BR>कवित्वशक्तेः खलु ते विलासाः, N.<BR>xiv. 14.<BR>II A man of genius: धीशक्तिसम्पन्नः<BR>(न्ना, न्नं), and sim. comp.s.,<BR>Shakespeare was a<BR>rare g.:<BR>*साक्ष्यप्रियोऽसाधारणो धीशक्तिसम्पन्न आसीत्।<BR>III Peculiar constitution: perh.: प्रकृतिः।<BR>IV<BR>A being<BR>(1) देवता (= good g.; god);<BR>(2)<BR>भूतः (= spirit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genteel
GENTEEL: विनीतः (ता, तं): v. Polite, elegant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genteelly
GENTEELLY:<BR>(1) विनीतम्;<BR>(2) विनयेनः v. Poli-<BR>-tely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gentian
GENTIAN:<BR>(1) भूनिम्बः;<BR>(2) किराततिक्तः;<BR>(3)<BR>चिरतिक्तः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gentile
GENTILE:<BR>I Belonging to a gens: जातीयः<BR>(या, यं).<BR>II As opposed to Christian:<BR>विजातीयः (या, यं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gentility
GENTILITY:<BR>(1) विनीतता;<BR>(2) विनयः: v. Polite-<BR>-ness, refinement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gentle
GENTLE:<BR>I Well-born, refined: भद्रः (द्रा, द्रं),<BR>of g. nature:<BR>भद्रप्रकृतिः (mfn.); g. behaviour:<BR>भद्रव्यवहारः;<BR>g. address:<BR>भद्रसम्भाषणम्।<BR>II Mild,<BR>soft: q.v.:<BR>(1) मृदु (f. द्वी),<BR>with g. fire:<BR>मृदुना<BR> वह्रिना, Bha.;<BR>with g. foams:<BR>मृदुभिः फेनैः, B. xii.<BR>48.;<BR>(2) शान्तः (न्ता, न्तं) (= calm, quiet).<BR>III Of inclinations: अलक्षितः (ता, तं)<BR>(= unperceived) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gentleman
GENTLEMAN:<BR>(1) साधुः, -जनः;<BR>(2) भद्रः,<BR>to act<BR>like a g.:<BR>भद्रवद् व्यवहरति;<BR>(3) आर्यः, (stronger<BR>term)<BR>g.'s living:<BR>आर्यवृत्तिः D. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gentlemanly
GENTLEMANLY: expr. by comp., g. behaviour:<BR>साधुवृत्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gentleness
GENTLENESS:<BR>(1) भद्रता (= gentlemanliness);<BR>(2) मार्दवम् (= mildness);<BR>(3) विनीतता (=gen-<BR>-tility);<BR>(4) शान्तिः, प्र- (= calmness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gentlewoman
GENTLEWOMAN:<BR>(1) भद्रा;<BR>(2) साध्वी;<BR>(3)<BR>आर्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gently
GENTLY:<BR>I Softly:<BR>(1) सादयम् (= kindly),<BR>en-<BR>joyed g.:<BR>सदयं बुभूजे, R.<BR>(2) मृदु (= mildly);<BR>(3)<BR>शान्तम् (= calmly);<BR>(4) मन्दं मन्दम् (=slowly).<BR>II Gradually:<BR>(1) क्रमशः;<BR>(2) अलक्षितम्<BR>(= unperceived).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gentry
GENTRY:<BR>(1) भद्राः<BR>or<BR>भद्रजनाः;<BR>(2) साधवः;<BR>(3)<BR>आर्याः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genuine
GENUINE:<BR>(1) अकृत्रिमः (मा, मं) (= not arti-<BR>-ficial),<BR>g. love:<BR>अकृत्रिमप्रेम, Ki.;<BR>(2) निष्कपटः (टा,<BR> टं) (= without deception);<BR>(3) सत्यः (त्या,<BR> त्यं) (= real: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genuinely
GENUINELY:<BR>(1) अकृत्रिमम्;<BR>(2) निष्कपटम्;<BR>(3)<BR>(3) सत्यम्: v. Genuine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genuineness
GENUINENESS:<BR>(1) अकृत्रिमता;<BR>(2) निष्कपटता;<BR> सत्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

genus
GENUS: जातिः, ‘समानप्रसवात्मिका जातिः’, N. d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

geographer
GEOGRAPHER: *भूमण्डलविद् (mfn.); भूगोलज्ञ (f. ज्ञा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

geographical
GEOGRAPHICAL: *भूमण्डलविषयकः (का, कं) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

geography
GEOGRAPHY: भूमण्डलविवरणम् and sim, comp.s. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">Page310</a>]<BR>Outlines of g.:<BR>भूमण्डलस्य संक्षिप्तविवरणम् (after<BR>V. p.);<BR>g. of India:<BR>*भारतभूमिविवरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

geological
GEOLOGICAL: *भूतत्त्वविषयकः (का, कं) and sim,<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

geologically
GEOLOGICALLY: *भूतत्त्वविद्यानुसारेण; भूतत्त्वानुसारेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

geologist
GEOLOGIST: *भूतत्त्वविद् (mfn.); भूतत्त्वविद्याविशारदः<BR>(दा, दं); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

geology
GEOLOGY: *भूतत्त्वं<BR>or<BR>भूतत्त्वविद्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

geometer
GEOMETER: v. Geometrician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

geometrical
GEOMETRICAL, GEOMETRIC: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

geometrically
GEOMETRICALLY: रेखागणितानुसारेण; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

geometrician
GEOMETRICIAN: *ज्यामितिज्ञः, रेखागणितपण्डितः;<BR>and sim comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

geometry
GEOMETRY:<BR>(1) ज्यामितिः,<BR>plane, solid g.<BR>*सम-,:<BR> स्थूल-ज्यामितिः;<BR>(2) रेखागणितम्;<BR>plane g.:<BR>*सम-<BR>भूरेखागणितम्। K. d. has क्षेत्रतत्त्वम्, but it means<BR>mensuration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

georgic
GEORGIC:<BR>the G. s of Virgil:<BR>*वीरकीलस्य कृषिकाव्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

germ
GERM: अङ्कुरः (or अङ्कूरः) (lit. and fig.),<BR>generation<BR>of g.s in seeds:<BR>वीजेऽङ्कुरजननम्, D.s; the journey<BR>of (his)<BR>sister to deceive them is the g.:<BR>अङ्कुरः<BR> स्वसुर्यात्रा तौ परिवञ्चितुम्, Vi. vi. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

german
GERMAN:<BR>I Kindred: सनाभि (mfn.).<BR>Cousin<BR>g.:<BR>एकपितामहः (हा, हं).<BR>II Belonging to<BR>G. y: *शार्मणः (णी, णं).<BR>III G. language:<BR>*शार्मणभाषा। Ph.: G. silver: *उपरूप्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

germane
GERMANE:<BR>I Allied: q.v.<BR>II Relevant:<BR>q.v.: expr. by सम्पर्कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

germinate
GERMINATE: expr. by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

germination
GERMINATION:<BR>(1) अङ्कुरोद्गमः;<BR>(2) अङ्कुरोद्भेदः;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gerund
GERUND: *वाहकक्रिया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gestation
GESTATION: गर्भधारणम्: v. Pregnancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gesticulate
GESTICULATE: अङ्गभङ्गिं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gesticulation
GESTICULATION: अङ्गभङ्गिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gesticulatory
GESTICULATORY: expr. by comp. or ins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gesture
GESTURE: चेष्टा, M.; इङ्गितम् (= sign).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get
GET (v.t.):<BR>I To obtain:<BR>(1) लभते (लभ्, c.<BR>1.),<BR>man g. s what he is to g.:<BR>प्राप्तव्यमर्थं लभते मनुष्यः,<BR>P. ii. 4.;<BR>to g. sleep:<BR>निद्रां लभते, A.r.; divid-<BR>ing (we) g. 72.: भक्ता लब्धम् 72, Li.;<BR>or he might<BR>g. three fortnights:<BR>लभोतासौ त्रिपक्षं वा, Kat.;<BR>(2)<BR>आप्नोति, अव-, प्र-, सम्प्र-, समव-, (आप्, c. 5.),<BR>got<BR>a son by Kusha:<BR>काकुस्थात् पुत्रमाप, R.;<BR>to g. one's<BR>wishes:<BR>कामान्प्राप्नोति, Mat.;<BR>(3) आ-सादयति,<BR> समा-, (c. of सद्), where did you g. this ring:<BR>कुत्र त्वयैतदङ्गुरीयकं समासादितम्, Sa.;<BR>(4) प्रपद्यते, अमि-,<BR> समभि-, (पद्, c. 4.),<BR>one who wishes to g. beati-<BR>tude:<BR>मुक्तिं प्रपित्सुः, Ki.;<BR>(5) अधिगच्छति (गम्, c.<BR>1.),<BR>to g. a saviour:<BR>त्रातारम् अधिगच्छति, A.r.<BR>II<BR>To come into possession of:<BR>(1) जायते, सं-,<BR>(जन्, c. 4.) (with gen. of the person g.<BR>ting), I have got headache with this exercise:<BR>व्यायामेन ममाऽनेन जाता शिरसि वेदना, Mah. iii.<BR>29:. 3.;<BR>(2) उत्पद्यते, सम्-, (पद्, c. 4.) (same<BR>cons.), Ra.<BR>III To induce: expr. by<BR>causal v.,<BR>to g. food cooked:<BR>भक्तानि पाचयति,<BR>Mah.;<BR>to g. work done:<BR>कर्म कारयति, M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get
GET (v.i.):<BR>I To become: q.v.: to g. angry:<BR>कोपं गच्छति;<BR>to g. disunited:<BR>विश्लेषम् एति, Ki.;<BR>to g. red:<BR>लोहितायते (nomi.), to g. cloudy:<BR>दुर्दिनायते;<BR>to g. clear:<BR>सुदिनायते, S.k.<BR>II To<BR>arrive: q.v.: प्राप्नोति (with acc.),<BR>got to the<BR>town:<BR>नगरं प्रापुः, K.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get abroad
GET ABROAD:<BR>(1) प्रसरति (सृ, c. 1.), D. iii.;<BR>(2) प्रसर्पति (सृप्, c. 1.),<BR>the rumour got abroad<BR>on all sides:<BR>प्रतिदिशं लोकवादः प्रासर्पत्, D. viii.;<BR>(3) बहुलीमवति (भू, c. 1.), Sa. vi.;<BR>(4) प्रथते<BR>(प्रथ्, c. 1.) (= to be known),<BR>the fame of<BR>Dhanamitra got abroad:<BR>धनमित्रस्य कीर्तिरप्रथत, D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get across
GET ACROSS: पारं गच्छति (to go)<BR>or<BR>नयति (to<BR>take).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get ahead
GET AHEAD: अग्रे भवति<BR>or<BR>अग्रसहीभवति (with<BR>gen.): v. Also to advance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get along
GET ALONG: v. To proceed.<BR>G. a.!:<BR>अन्तर-<BR>मन्तरम्, Mr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get among
GET AMONG: मध्ये भवति,<BR>g. ing among them un-<BR>perceived:<BR>तत्रैव जनानुलीनः, D. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get at
GET AT: प्राप्नोति (आप्, c. 5.) (with acc.): v.<BR>To reach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get away
GET AWAY: अपसरति (सृ, c. 1.): v. To go<BR>away, escape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get back
GET BACK:<BR>I Intrans.: पुनः प्राप्नोति, Ku.: v.<BR>To return.<BR>II Trans.:<BR>(1) पुनर्लंभते, Ki.;<BR>(2) by sim. get: q.v.: he got back youth:<BR>यौवनं प्रतिपेदे सः, Mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get the better of
GET THE BETTER OF:<BR>(1) परिभवतिः v. To over-<BR>-come;<BR>(2) आवर्जयति।: v. To bend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get beyond
GET BEYOND: अतिक्राम्यति (क्रम्, c. 4.): v. To<BR>go beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get clear of
GET CLEAR OF:<BR>(1) निर्मोचयति (मुच, c. 10.) v.<BR>To release;<BR>(2) उन्मज्जति (मस्ज्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>emerge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get down
GET DOWN:<BR>I Intrans:<BR>(1) अवतरति (तॄ, c.<BR>1.);<BR>(2) अवरोहति (रुह्, c. 1.).<BR>II Trans.:<BR>(1) अवतारयति (c. of तॄ), V. i.;<BR>(2) अवरोहयति<BR>(c. of रुह्), R. i. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get hold of
GET HOLD OF: प्राप्नोति (= to get: q.v.): v.<BR>Also to seize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get in
GET IN (v.):<BR>I To enter: q.v.: प्रविशति (विश्,<BR>c. 6.): v. Also to get into.<BR>II To collect:<BR>q.v.: समाहरति (हृ, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get into
GET INTO: Ph.:<BR>to g. into a carriage:<BR>प्रवहणम्<BR> आरोहति<BR>or<BR>अधिरोहति (रुह्, c. 1.), Mr.<BR>or<BR>अध्यास्ते<BR>(आस्, c. 1.), R. vi. 10.;<BR>he himself helped<BR>Damayantī in g.ting into the car:<BR>रथे स भैमीं<BR> स्वयमध्यरूरुहत्, N. xvi. 114.;<BR>to g. into debt:<BR>ऋण-<BR>ग्रस्तः (स्ता, स्तं) भवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get off
GET OFF:<BR>I Trans.: v. To extricate.<BR>II<BR>Intrans: (a) to escape: q.v.: अपसरति; (b)<BR>to be acquitted: perh. निःसरति; मुक्तः (क्ता,<BR> क्तं) भवति।<BR>II To alight: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get on
GET ON: expr. by वर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get out
GET OUT:<BR>I To go out: अपैति (इ, c. 2.).<BR>II<BR>To leave: मुञ्चति (मुच्। c. 6.), त्यजति (त्यज्, c.<BR>1.), etc.,<BR>g. o. of bed:<BR>शय्यां मुञ्च, R.;<BR>g. ting out<BR>of temper:<BR>विहाय धैर्यम्, B. xii. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get ready
GET READY: सज्जीकरोति, -कुरुते: v. To prepare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get rid of
GET RID OF:<BR>(1) आत्मानं मोचयति (मुच्, c. 10.)<BR>(with abl.) (to disengage oneself);<BR>(2)<BR>दूरीकरोति (= to remove.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get through
GET THROUGH:<BR>I To complete: q.v.: समापयति<BR>(c. of आप्).<BR>II To traverse, arrive:<BR>q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get together
GET TOGETHER: समाहरतिः v. To assemble,<BR>bring together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get up
GET UP:<BR>I From a seat: उत्-तिष्ठति, अम्युत्-,<BR>(स्था, c. 1.),<BR>got up from the seat:<BR>पीठादुदतिष्ठत्, Si.<BR>II From bed: उत्तिष्ठनि,<BR>g. g. a thief is gone<BR>out:<BR>उत्तिष्ठ, उत्तिष्ठ, चौरो निष्क्रान्तः, Mr. iii.<BR>III<BR>To prepare (as an oration): सज्जीकरोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

get upon
GET UPON: आरोहति (रुह्, c. 1.): v. To mount.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gewgaw
GEWGAW: perh. अकिञ्चनः; अकिञ्चित्करः (री, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

geyser
GEYSER: सीतोत्सः (after सीताकुण्डः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ghastliness
GHASTLINESS:<BR>I Lit.: भूतसरूपता।<BR>II Pale-<BR>-ness: विवर्णता।<BR>III Dreadfulness:<BR>(1)<BR>करालता;<BR>(2) विकटता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ghastly
GHASTLY:<BR>I Lit.: भूतसरूपः (पा, पं); शवस्येव<BR>(= as of a corpse), Mah.<BR>II Pale, dismal:<BR>विवर्ण (f. र्णा), these (ghosts) with long g. bodies:<BR>एते विवर्णदिर्घदेहाः, Ma. v. 15.<BR>III Horrible,<BR>dreadful:<BR>(1) करालः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) विकटः<BR>(टा, टं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ghaut
GHAUT, GHAT:<BR>(1) तीरसोपानपथः, R. xvi. 56.;<BR>(2) घट्टः (specially ferry-g.);<BR>(3) सोपानमार्गः<BR>and sim. comp.s. (where the sense is clear),<BR>Me. ii. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ghost
GHOST:<BR>I The soul: q.v.: आत्मन् (m.). Ph.:<BR>the Holy G.:<BR>पुरुषोत्तमः:<BR>to give up the g.:<BR>देहं<BR> त्यजति। v. To die.<BR>II An apparition: भूतः,<BR>a g. lives in this tree:<BR>एतस्मिन् पादपे कोऽपि भूतः<BR> प्रतिवसति, Ra. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ghostly
GHOSTLY:<BR>I Spiritual: q.v.<BR>II Pertaining<BR>to ghosts: भूत- in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ghoul
GHOUL: राक्षस (f. सी),<BR>Brahmin -g.:<BR>ब्रह्मराक्षसः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

giant
GIANT:<BR>I A great man: महापुरुषः,<BR>“a g.'s<BR>strength”:<BR>अतिमानुषं बलम्।<BR>II Atitan:<BR>(1) दैत्यः;<BR>(2) दानवः।<BR>G.'s causeway:<BR>*दानवबन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

giant
GIANT (adj.): वृहत्कायः (या, यं): v. Also<BR>gigantic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

giantess
GIANTESS: दानवी (may be applied also to g.<BR>females).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gibber
GIBBER: अस्पष्टं जल्पति (जल्प्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>chatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gibberish
GIBBERISH:<BR>(1) अस्पष्टजल्पितम्;<BR>(2) किलकिलायितम्<BR>(like monkey's)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gibbet
GIBBET (subs.): उद्वन्धनकाष्ठम् (?); वध्यकाष्ठम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gibbet
GIBBET (v.):<BR>I Lit.: वध्यकाष्ठं बध्नाति (बन्ध्,<BR>c. 9.) (?).<BR>II Fig., to brand: अङ्कयति।<BR>To g. a<BR>name:<BR>दुर्नाम प्रकाशयति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gibbous
GIBBOUS:<BR>I Crooked: q.v.: वक्रः (क्रा, क्रं).<BR>II Hunched: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gibe
GIBE (subs.): गालिः, J.: v. Abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gibe
GIBE (v.): गालिं ददाति (दा, c. 3.). J.: v. To<BR>abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

giblets
GIBLETS: खगानां हृद्यकृदादि; खण्डमांसम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

giddily
GIDDILY: i.e. thoughtlessly:<BR>(1) चापल्येन;<BR>(2) चञ्चलतया; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

giddiness
GIDDINESS:<BR>I Lit.: शिरोहर्षः (?), Bha.<BR>II<BR>Fig.: thoughtlessness:<BR>(1) चापल्यम्;<BR>(2)<BR>चाञ्चल्यम्;<BR>(3) चलचित्तता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

giddy
GIDDY:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by भ्रमति<BR>or<BR>भ्राम्यति (भ्रम्,<BR>c. 1. and 4),<BR>I feel g.:<BR>शिरो मे भ्रमति।<BR>II Fig.;<BR>fickle:<BR>(1) चञ्चलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) चपलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gift
GIFT (subs.):<BR>I A present: q.v.:<BR>(1) दानम्,<BR>great g.:<BR>महादानम्, He.;<BR>(2) दत्तम्, g.s from brothers:<BR>भ्रातृदत्तम्, N.s.;<BR>(3) दायः (rare), g. of love:<BR>प्रीतिदायः, Ram.<BR>II An endowment:<BR>you<BR>have all the g.s of nature:<BR>*सर्वाणि ते स्वामाविका-<BR>न्यभिलषणीयानि सन्ति; शक्तिः (= faculty,<BR>power).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gifted
GIFTED:<BR>I Endowed: q.v.: अन्वितः (ता, तं);<BR>सम्पन्नः (न्ना, न्नं).<BR>II Endowed with natural<BR>g.s: शक्तिसम्पन्नः (न्ना, न्नं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gig
GIG: लघुयानविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gigantic
GIGANTIC:<BR>(1) अतिमानुषः (षी, षं) (= super-<BR>-human);<BR>(2) दानवः (वी, वं) (?). Comp.<BR>दैत्यमल्लः of V.p. v. 20. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

giggle
GIGGLE (v.): प्रहसति (हस्, c. 1.) (?): v. To<BR>laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gild
GILD (v.): स्वर्णलं<BR>or<BR>हेमलं (f. लां) करोति (??);<BR>स्वर्णेन रञ्जयति (रञ्ज्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gilded
GILDED, GILT: स्वर्णलः<BR>or<BR>हेमलः (ला, लं) (??);<BR>स्वर्णरञ्जितः (ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gilder
GILDER: expr. by verb, स्वर्णरञ्जकः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gilding
GILDING:<BR>I The art: स्वर्णरञ्जनम् (?); स्वर्णकर्मन्<BR>(n.).<BR>II The gold surface: स्वर्णच्छदः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gill
GILL: i.e. quarter of a pint: पादः: v. Pint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gills
GILLS: of a fish: नासारन्ध्रे (n. dual) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gimlet
GIMLET:<BR>(1) वेधनिका;<BR>(2) आवेधः;<BR>(3) आस्फोटनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gin
GIN (subs.):<BR>I A spirit:<BR>शीधुः (?).<BR>II A<BR>snare: q.v.: जालम्।<BR>III A machine: यन्त्रम्,<BR>cotton -g.:<BR>*कार्पासयन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gin
GIN (v.) शोधयति (c. of शुध्): v. To clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ginger
GINGER:<BR>(1) आर्द्रकम्;<BR>(2) शृङ्गवेरम्, A. Dry g.:<BR>शुण्ठिः।<BR>G.-bread:<BR>आर्द्रकरसवासितपिष्टकविशेषः।<BR>G.<BR>beer, pop, or wine:<BR>*आर्द्रकासवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gingerly
GINGERLY: v. Cautiously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gipsy
GIPSY: *याक्ष (f. क्षी); हाप्सिः (f. प्सी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

giraffe
GIRAFFE: *दीर्धग्रीवः; चित्रोष्ट्रः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gird
GIRD (v.t.):<BR>(1) वेष्टयति, आधि- (वेष्ट्, c. 10.) (= to<BR>encircle: q.v.), g. ed by the mountain......<BR>भूमिभृताधिवेष्टितः (ता, तं), Ki. xii. 22.;<BR>(2)<BR>नह्यति, अपि-, (नह्, c. 4.) (= to fasten),<BR>the<BR>matted hair g. ed upon with snakes:<BR>भुजङ्गमोन्नद्ध-<BR>जटाकलापः (पा, पं), Ku. iii. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

girder
GIRDER: आधारदारु (n.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

girdle
GIRDLE:<BR>(1) मेखला;<BR>(2) रस(श)ना;<BR>(3) काञ्ची;<BR>(4)<BR>कक्ष्या;<BR>(5) सारसनम्;<BR>(6) परिकरः (any g.),<BR>with<BR>tied g.:<BR>वद्धपरिकरः, D.;<BR>(7) शृङली (= man's g.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

girl
GIRL:<BR>(1) बाला;<BR>(2) बालिका;<BR>(3) कन्या (= un-<BR>-married g. and gen. with ref. to the<BR>parents);<BR>(4) कृमारी (= a virgin);<BR>(5) वासू<BR>(only in addressing g.s.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

girlhood
GIRLHOOD:<BR>(1) बाल्यम् (= childhood: q.v.);<BR>(2) बालिकावस्था;<BR>(3) बालभावः, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

girlish
GIRLISH:<BR>I Pertaining to a girl: expr. by<BR>comp.<BR>II Like a girl: expr. by circumlo,<BR>g. taste:<BR>बालानामिव रुचिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

girlishly
GIRLISHLY:<BR>(1) बालेव;<BR>(2) कृमारीवः v. Girl, like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

girth
GIRTH:<BR>I Of a horse:<BR>(1) वरत्रा;<BR>(2) वर्द्ध्रम्।<BR>II The middle: मध्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gist
GIST:<BR>(1) फलितार्थः;<BR>(2) फलार्थः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gittern
GITTERN: v. Guitar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

give
GIVE (v.t.):<BR>I To bestow:<BR>(1) ददाति, दत्ते or<BR>यच्छति, प्र-, सम्प्र-, सं-, (दा, c. 3. and 1),<BR>the king<BR>g.s him his daughter and lieutenancy:<BR>तस्मै राजा<BR> ददाति तनयां च यौवराज्यं च, K.s. xxiv. 53.;<BR>to g.<BR>knowledge:<BR>विद्यां दातुम्, Ki. iii. 23.;<BR>(2) वितरति<BR>(तॄ, c. 1.) (= to g. freely), I will g. you eyes:<BR>चक्षुस्ते वितराम्यहम्, Mah.;<BR>(3) वि-सर्जयति, अति-<BR>(सृज्, c. 10.) (= to g. lavishly),<BR>for taking is<BR>to g.:<BR>आदानं हि विसर्गाय, R. iv. 86.;<BR>(4) प्रति-<BR>पादयति (c. of पद्) (rare) (= to make over),<BR>g. ing of things with faith:<BR>अर्थानां श्रद्धया प्रतिपादनम्,<BR>H.s.;<BR>(5) स्पर्शयति (c. of स्पृश्) (rare) (= to<BR>cause to reach),<BR>g. ing millions of kine:<BR>गाः<BR> कोटिशः स्पर्शयत, R. iii. 49.<BR>II To deliver: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">Page313</a>]<BR>(1) ददाति there are six ways of g. ing and taking:<BR>षड्विधो दानादानविधिः, N.s.;<BR>(2) अर्पयति, सम्-,<BR>gave (the child)<BR>to the queen to bring up:<BR>देव्यै<BR> वर्धयेति समर्पितवान्, D.<BR>III To produce: जायते<BR> सं-, (जन्, c. 4.), striking off twenty, it g.s interest:<BR>..... विंशत्यापवर्त्य जातं कलान्तरम्, Li.<BR>IV To<BR>admit: q.v.: परिगृह्वाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.). V. To<BR>devote: q.v.: आत्मानं ददाति<BR>or<BR>समर्पयति,<BR>Miscel.,<BR>to g. ear:<BR>कर्णं ददाति, Sa. i.; to g. advice:<BR>उपदेशं ददाति, P.; to g. way (in the street, etc.):<BR>वर्त्म ददाति, Ki. xiv. 14.<BR>or<BR>अन्तरं ददाति, Mr.<BR>x.;<BR>to g. order:<BR>आज्ञां ददाति, V.p.; to give time:<BR>कालं ददाति, Mat.;<BR>to g. thanks:<BR>धन्यवादं करोति (?),<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

give
GIVE (v. i.): v. To yield, give way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

give away
GIVE AWAY: प्रददाति v. To give (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

give back
GIVE BACK:<BR>(1) प्रत्यर्पयति;<BR>(2) प्रतिददाति: v.<BR>To return (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

give chase
GIVE CHASE: अनुधावति (धाव्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>pursue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

give forth
GIVE FORTH: v. To give way (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

give in
GIVE IN (v.t.): ददाति, प्र-: v. Also to declare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

give in to
GIVE IN TO: i.e. to adopt: परिगृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

give off
GIVE OFF:<BR>(1) त्यजति, परि-, (त्यज्, c. 1.);<BR>(2)<BR>जहाति, वि-, (हा, c. 3.); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

give out
GIVE OUT: 1. To announce: Ph.:<BR>g. ing out<BR>that the queen was burnt:<BR>देवी दग्वेति वार्तामुत्पाद्य,<BR>Ra. iv.;<BR>should not g. out master's secret acts<BR>and counsel:<BR>गुह्यं कर्म च मन्त्रं च न मर्तुः सम्प्रकाशयेत्,<BR>Ka. v. 31.: v. To disclose, reveal.<BR>II To<BR>emit: q.v.<BR>III To yield: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

give up
GIVE UP:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) ददाति;<BR>(2) समर्पयति:<BR>v. To give (II and V).<BR>II To despair:<BR>आशां जहाति, त्यजति, etc. (with loc.).<BR>III To<BR>cease: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

give way
GIVE WAY:<BR>I To yield to force:<BR>(1) अवसीदति<BR>(सद्, c. 1.) (?);<BR>(2) भज्यते, (pass. of भञ्ज्)<BR>(= to break).<BR>II Fig.: वशं गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.),<BR>you should not g. way to sorrow:<BR>शुचो वशं गन्तुं<BR> नार्हसि, R. viii. 90.<BR>III To comply with:<BR>अनुमन्यते (मन्, c. 4.) (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

given
GIVEN: in math.: expr. by यदि ॥॥। स्यात्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

giver
GIVER (subs.):<BR>(1) दातृ, प्र-, (f. त्री,) a g. unasked:<BR>अयाचितप्रदाता, Ga.;<BR>(2) -दः<BR>or<BR>-प्रदः (दा, दं) or<BR>दायिन् (f. नी) in comp.,<BR>money-g.:<BR>धनदः;<BR>g. s<BR>of fire and water:<BR>अग्न्युदकदायिनः, Kat.;<BR>(3)<BR>त्यागशालिन् (f. नी) (= a lavish g.), Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

giving
GIVING (subs.):<BR>(1) दानम् (best equiv.);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रदानम्, सं-;<BR>(3) प्रतिपादनम्;<BR>(4) वितरणम्;<BR>(5)<BR>विसर्जनम्<BR>(6) विश्राणनम् (rare): v. To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

giving
GIVING (adj.):<BR>(1) -दः<BR>or<BR>-प्रदः (दा, दं), life-g.:<BR>प्राणप्रदः (दा, दं);<BR>strength g:<BR>बलदः (दा, दं), Bha.;<BR>(2) -दायिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gizzard
GIZZARD: of birds: जठरः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glacial
GLACIAL: expr. by comp.: v. Glacier, icy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glacier
GLACIER: *संहतहिमक्षेत्रम्; शिलीभूतहिभूमिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glacis
GLACIS: *बहिःप्रवणः; बहिःप्रवणा भूमिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glad
GLAD (adj.):<BR>(1) हृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं), प्र-, सं-, (best<BR>equiv.);<BR>(2) आनन्दितः (ता, तं);<BR>(3) सानन्दः<BR>(न्दा, न्दं);<BR>(4) आह्लादितः (ता, तं). To become g.:<BR>हृष्यति (हृष्, c. 4.): v. Delighted, to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gladden
GLADDEN: हर्षयति, प्र-, सं-, (c. of हृष्): v. To<BR>delight, please.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glade
GLADE: वनमार्गः or sim. मार्गः (when the sense<BR>is clear)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gladiator
GLADIATOR: असियोधः (?); असिमल्लः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gladiatorial
GLADIATORIAL expr. by comp., g. fight:<BR>असियोधयुद्धम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gladly
GLADLY:<BR>(1) सहर्षम्;<BR>(2) साह्लादम्;<BR>(3) सानन्दम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gladness
GLADNESS:<BR>(1) हर्षः, प्र-;<BR>(2) आह्लादः;<BR>(3) आनन्दः;<BR>(4) हृष्टिः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gladsome
GLADSOME:<BR>I Glad: q.v.<BR>II Clearing:<BR>expr. by comp.,<BR>g. way:<BR>आनन्ददानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glance
GLANCE (subs.):<BR>(1) दृष्टिपातः;<BR>(2) कटाक्षः<BR>(= sidelong g.),<BR>a g. containing nectar as well<BR>as poison:<BR>दिग्धोऽमृतेन च विषेण च कटाक्षः, Ma.<BR>i. 30;<BR>(3) अपाङ्गनिक्षेपः (= 2);<BR>(4) साचि विलोकितम्<BR>and sim. comp.s (= 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glance
GLANCE (v.):<BR>I To cast the eyes rapidly:<BR>(1) दृष्टिं क्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.);<BR>(2) कटाक्षपातं<BR> करोति।<BR>II To graze: घर्षति (घृष्, c. 1.).<BR>III<BR>To allude: कटाक्षेण वदति (वद्, c. 1.), वक्ति<BR>(वच्, c. 1.), etc. Tārānāth.<BR>IV To move<BR>quickly: स्फुरति (स्फुर्, c. 6.). V. To dart<BR>aside: जवात् निष्पतति (पत्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gland
GLAND: शिरा, (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glanders
GLANDERS: prob. क्षयथुः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glandular
GLANDULAR: expr. by comp. or by gen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glare
GLARE (subs.): perh. तेजस्, I cannot bear the g.:<BR>आतपतेजः सोढुं न शक्नोमिः v. Also brightness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glare
GLARE (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) संदीप्यते (दीप्, c. 4.);<BR>(2) वि-द्योतते (द्युत्, c. 1.);<BR>(3) रोचते (रुच्, c. 1.).<BR>II Fig.: expr. by adj., where the eye g.s on:<BR>यत्र संदीप्तचक्षुः पतति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glaring
GLARING:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) सं-दीप्तः (प्ता, प्तं), प्र-;<BR>(2)<BR>द्योतनः (नी, नं), वि-;<BR>(3) रोचिष्णु (mfn.).<BR>II<BR>Very clear: q.v.: सुस्पष्ट (ष्टा, ष्टं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glaringly
GLARINGLY:<BR>(1) सुस्पष्टम्;<BR>(2) परिस्फुटम्: v. Clearly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glass
GLASS (subs.):<BR>I The material:<BR>(1) काचः;<BR>(2) स्फटिकः (= crystal).<BR>II A mirror: q.v.:<BR>दर्पणः।<BR>III A g. instrument: perh. काचयन्त्रम्ः<BR>v. Telescope, microscope, etc.<BR>IV A drink-<BR>-ing. g.: चषक (mn.) (= cup);<BR>wine-g.:<BR>*काच-<BR>निर्मितं भद्यपानपात्रम्। V. Glassware: *काचपात्राणि<BR>(n. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glass
GLASS (adj.):<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>g.-bottle:<BR>काचकूपी;<BR>(2) स्फाटिकः (की, कं) (= crystal ?), g.-door:<BR>स्फाटिकं द्वारम्, Mah. ii. 47. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glass
GLASS (v.):<BR>I To see: q.v.: निरीक्षते (ईक्ष्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II To reflect: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glass-blower
GLASS-BLOWER: *काचन्धमः; काचधमकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glass-cutting
GLASS-CUTTING: *काचपरिष्कारः; काचतक्षणभ्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glassful
GLASSFUL (subs.): expr. by glass,<BR>two g. s:<BR>द्वे<BR> चषके।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glass-work
GLASS-WORK:<BR>I The work: काचकर्मन् (n.) (?).<BR>II The place: *काचागारम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glassy
GLASSY:<BR>I Lit.: v. Glass (adj.).<BR>II Resembl-<BR>-ing g.: स्फाटिकः (की, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glaze
GLAZE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: *काचयति (nomi).<BR>II<BR>To render smooth: श्लक्ष्णीकरोति।<BR>III To<BR>furnish with glass: expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glazier
GLAZIER: *काचकारः (= glass-maker): काच-<BR>संघातृ (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gleam
GLEAM (v.):<BR>(1) स्फुरति, वि-, परि-, (स्फुर्, c. 6.);<BR>(2) लसति, उत्-, वि-, (लस्, c. 1.);<BR>(3) दीप्यते<BR>(दीप्, c. 4.): v. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gleam
GLEAM (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: स्फुरितम्, स्फुरणम्।<BR>II<BR>Brightness, splendour: q.v.: प्रभा।<BR>III<BR>Fig., of hope, joy, etc.: not expr.,<BR>there is<BR>no g. of hope:<BR>आशालेशोऽपि नास्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gleaming
GLEAMING (adj.):<BR>(1) स्फुरत् (f. न्ती), वि-, प्र-,<BR> परि-,<BR>g. rays:<BR>स्फुरन्मरीवि-, Ku.;<BR>(2) लसत् (f. न्ती),<BR>उत्-, वि-,<BR>g. lightning:<BR>लसत्तडित्, Ki. xvi. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glean
GLEAN (v.):<BR>(1) संकलयति (कल्, c. 10.);<BR>(2)<BR>सं-गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gleaner
GLEANER:<BR>(1) संकलयितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) संग्रहीतृ<BR>(f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gleaning
GLEANING:<BR>I Lit.: उच्चः (rare), M. iv. 5.<BR>II<BR>In gen.:<BR>(1) संकलनम्;<BR>(2) संग्रहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glebe
GLEBE: मृत्तिका: v. Ground, soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gleby
GLEBY:<BR>(1) लोष्टमयः (यी, यं) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glede
GLEDE: चिल्लः v. Kite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glee
GLEE: हर्षः: v. Joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gleeful
GLEEFUL: प्रहृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं): v. Joyful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glen
GLEN: उपत्यका: v. Valley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glib
GLIB:<BR>I Slippery: पिच्छिलः (ला, लं).<BR>II<BR>Voluble: चपलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glibly
GLIBLY: द्रुतम्<BR>or<BR>क्षिप्रम् (= quickly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glibness
GLIBNESS:<BR>I Slipperiness: पिच्छिलता।<BR>II<BR>Volubility: चपलता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glide
GLIDE:<BR>I Of time: याति (या, c. 2.): v. To<BR>go.<BR>II Of rivers: स्रवति (स्रु, c. 1.): v. To<BR>flow.<BR>III To move on: प्रचलति (चल्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glide
GLIDE, GLIDING (subs.):<BR>(1) गतिः (= motion);<BR>(2) प्रसर्पणम् (as of serpent);<BR>(3) स्रुतिः (= flow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glimmer
GLIMMER (v.): मन्दं मन्दं ज्वलति (ज्वल्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glimmer
GLIMMER (subs.):<BR>(1) मन्दतेजस् (n.);<BR>(2) मन्द-<BR>प्रभा;<BR>(3) better by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glimmering
GLIMMERING (adj.): मन्दं मन्दं ज्वलत् (f. न्ती);<BR>मन्दप्रभः (भा, भं) (with faint light), B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glimpse
GLIMPSE:<BR>(1) क्षणदृष्टिः (?);<BR>(2) मुहूर्तदर्शनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glisten
GLISTEN, GLISTER: द्योतते (द्युत्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>gleam, shine. G. ing: v. Bright, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glitter
GLITTER (v.):<BR>(1) द्योतते, वि-, (द्युत्, c. 1.);<BR>(2)<BR>राजते, वि-, (राज्, c. 1.);<BR>(3) भासते, उत्-, (भास्,<BR>c. 1.);<BR>(4) भाति, वि- (भा, c. 2.). Ph.:<BR>“all that<BR>g. s is not gold”:<BR>शैले शैले न माणिक्यम् (?). J.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glitter
GLITTER (subs.):<BR>(1) औज्ज्वलयम्, Ma;<BR>(2) द्युतिः;<BR>(3) प्रभा;<BR>(4) तेजस् (n.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glittering
GLITTERING: ज्वलत् (न्ती), प्र-,<BR>g. energy:<BR>ज्वलत्प्रतापः,<BR>N.: v. Bright, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gloat
GLOAT (v.): तृप्यति, सं-, परि-, (तृप्, c. 4.) (= to<BR>be satiate).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

globe
GLOBE:<BR>I A sphere: रोलः,<BR>terrestrial g.:<BR>पृठिवी-<BR>गोलः, Su. xiii. 3.<BR>II The earth: q.v.:<BR>भूगोलः,<BR>the Meru is in the center of the g.:<BR>भूगोल-<BR>मव्यगो मेरुः, Su.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

globular
GLOBULAR:<BR>(1) गोलाकारः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) गोलकाकृति<BR>(mfn.), Su.; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

globule
GLOBULE: गुली, -काः v. Ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gloom
GLOOM:<BR>I Lit.: तिमिरम्: v. Darkness.<BR>II<BR>Fig., cloudiness of mind: निष्प्रभता; better<BR>by adj., निष्प्रभः (भा, भं).<BR>III Sadness, cala-<BR>-mity: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gloomily
GLOOMILY:<BR>I Dimly: निष्प्रभम्।<BR>II Sadly:<BR>सविषादम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gloominess
GLOOMINESS: निष्प्रभता: v. Gloom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gloomy
GLOOMY:<BR>(1) तामसः (सी, सं): v. Dark;<BR>(2)<BR>निष्प्रभः (भा, भं): v. Dim;<BR>(3) विषण्ण (f. ण्णा): v.<BR>Dejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glorification
GLORIFICATION:<BR>(1) कीर्तनम्, सं-, परि-;<BR>(2) आरा-<BR>धनम्;<BR>(3) सत्कारः। For dif.: v. Glorify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glorify
GLORIFY:<BR>(1) कीर्तयति, सं-, परि- (कीर्त्, c. 10.),<BR>g. ed in heaven:<BR>लोकान्तरगीतकीर्ति (mfn.), R. vi.<BR>45.: v. To celebrate;<BR>(2) आराधयति (राध्,<BR>c. 10.): v. To adore;<BR>(3) सत्करोति: v. To<BR>honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glorious
GLORIOUS:<BR>I Illustrious, famous: q.v.:<BR>(1)<BR>महायशस् (mfn.);<BR>(2) उदग्रकीर्ति (mfn.).<BR>II<BR>Conferring glory:<BR>(1) यशस्य (f. स्या);<BR>(2)<BR>यशस्करः (री, रं).<BR>III Excellent, great: q.v.:<BR>महत् (f. ती).<BR>IV Splendid: q.v.: महोज्जवलः<BR>(ला, लं), he was a g. collection of greatness:<BR>राशिरासीन्महसां महोज्ज्वलः, N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gloriously
GLORIOUSLY:<BR>(1) महोज्ज्वलम् (= splendidly);<BR>(2) विशिष्टम् (= excellently).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glory
GLORY (subs.):<BR>I Renown: q.v.:<BR>(1) कीर्तिः;<BR>(2) यशस् (n.). Ph.: the g. of your fame:<BR>सौभाग्यमात्मयशसः, Sa. vii.<BR>II Honour: q.v.:<BR>गौरवम्।<BR>III Splendour: q.v.:<BR>(1) तेजस् (n.);<BR>(2) प्रतापः।<BR>IV Pride: q.v.: अभिमानः।<BR>V<BR>Praise: expr. by कीर्तयति।<BR>VI An orna-<BR>-ment:<BR>(1) अलङ्कारः;<BR>(2) रत्नम् (= gem.);<BR>(3)<BR>तिलकः (rare),<BR>the g. of the race of Raghu:<BR>रधुकुल-<BR>तिलकः, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glory
GLORY (v.):<BR>I To rejoice: q.v.: मोदते, प्र-,<BR>(मुद्, c. 1.).<BR>II To boast: q.v.: दृप्यति<BR>(दृप्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gloss
GLOSS (subs.):<BR>I Comment, interpretation:<BR>(1) टीका;<BR>(2) टीप्यनी;<BR>(3) व्याखया,<BR>in the g.<BR>of the Mīmānsā styled “light of the glorious<BR>commentary”:<BR>मीमांसकव्याख्यायां भाष्यरन्तप्रभायाम्।<BR>II<BR>A specious appearance: बाह्यशोभा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gloss
GLOSS (v.): टीकां करोति (with gen.): v. To<BR>explain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glossary
GLOSSARY: निघण्टुः,<BR>medical g.:<BR>वैद्यकनिघण्टुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glossiness
GLOSSINESS:<BR>(1) स्निग्धता;<BR>(2) चिक्कणता;<BR>(3)<BR>बाह्यशोभा (in bad sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glossy
GLOSSY:<BR>I Polished:<BR>(1) स्निग्ध (f. ग्धा),<BR>g. black<BR>hair:<BR>स्निग्धनीलो मूर्धजकलापः, D.;<BR>(2) चिक्कणः (णा, णं).<BR>II In bad sense: बाह्यप्रभः (भा, भं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glove
GLOVE (subs.): *हस्तुका; करछदः। To throw<BR>the g. (fig): नियुद्धाय आह्वयते (ह्वे, c. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glove
GLOVE (v.t.):<BR>(1) *हस्तुकया<BR>or<BR>करच्छदेन आवृणोति<BR>(वृ, c. 5.);<BR>(2) हस्तुकां परिदधाति (धा, c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glover
GLOVER: *हस्तुकाकारः; करच्छदनिर्मातृ (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glow
GLOW (subs.):<BR>I Heat: q.v.: उत्तापः।<BR>II<BR>Redness: रक्तता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glow
GLOW (v.):<BR>(1) दीप्यते (दीप्, c. 4.) (= to be<BR>lighted, inflamed),<BR>g. ed with rage:<BR>क्रुद्धोऽदीपि,<BR>B. vi. 32.;<BR>(2) ज्वलति (ज्वल्, c. 1.) (= to<BR>burn: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glowing
GLOWING (adj.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्रदीप्तः (प्ता, प्तं);<BR>(2) ज्वलितः (ता, तं).<BR>II With passion, etc.:<BR>प्रदीप्त (f. प्ता).<BR>III Red.: रक्तः (क्ता, क्तं).<BR>IV<BR>Brilliant: उज्ज्वलः (ला, लं),<BR>in g. colours:<BR>उज्ज्वल-<BR>वर्णैः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glowingly
GLOWINGLY: i.e. in glowing terms: perh.<BR>दीप्ताक्षरैः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glow-worm
GLOW-WORM:<BR>(1) खद्योतः;<BR>(2) ज्योतिरिङ्गः, -णः;<BR>(3) प्रभाकीटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gloze
GLOZE:<BR>I Verb: v. To flatter, fawn.<BR>II<BR>Subs.: v. Flattery, adulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glue
GLUE (subs.):<BR>(1) क्षारम्, -कम् Mah. s. 147. I.;<BR>(2) लाक्षा (?) (comp. vernacular लाच्छा);<BR>(3)<BR>संश्लेषार्थं चिक्कणद्रव्यम्, Nil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glue
GLUE (v.): क्षारेण<BR>or<BR>लाक्षया संश्लेषयति (c. of श्लिष्) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glue-boiler
GLUE-BOILER:<BR>(1) क्षारकारः। (?);<BR>(2) लाक्षाकारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gluey
GLUEY: v. Glutinous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glut
GLUT (v.t.):<BR>I To swallow: q.v.: ग्रसते (ग्रस्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II To satiate: q.v.: सं-तर्पयति (c. of<BR>तृप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glut
GLUT (subs.):<BR>I That which is swallowed,<BR>ग्रासः।<BR>II Abundance: q.v.: प्राचुर्यम्।<BR>III<BR>Satiety: q.v.: सौहित्यम्, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glutinous
GLUTINOUS:<BR>(1) चिक्कणः (णा, णं) (?);<BR>(2) संलग्नशीलः<BR>(ला, लं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glutinousness
GLUTINOUSNESS:<BR>(1) चिक्कणता (?);<BR>(2) संलग्न-<BR>शीलता (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

glutton
GLUTTON:<BR>(1) औदरिकः;<BR>(2) उदरम्भरिः;<BR>(3)<BR>आद्यूनः, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gluttonous
GLUTTONOUS:<BR>(1) औदरिकः (का, कं);<BR>(2) धस्मरः<BR>(रा, रं);<BR>(3) अत्याहारप्रियः (या, यं);<BR>(4) गृध्रः<BR>(घ्रा, ध्रं) (= covetous).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gluttony
GLUTTONY:<BR>(1) औदरिकता;<BR>(2) घस्मरता;<BR>(3)<BR>अत्याहारप्रियता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gnarled
GNARLED: ग्रन्थिलः (ला, लं): v. Knotty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gnash
GNASH:<BR>to g. the teeth:<BR>दन्तैर्दन्तान् निष्पीडयति (पीड्,<BR>c. 10.)<BR>or<BR>दशति, वि-, सं-, (दंश्, c. 1.), Mah. ii.<BR>43. 12.; क्ष्वेडति (क्ष्वेड्, c. 1.), M. iv. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gnashing
GNASHING: क्ष्वेडनम्। K.b.; better by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gnat
GNAT:<BR>(1) मशकः (= mosquito);<BR>(2) दंशः (a fly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gnaw
GNAW: दशति (दंश्, c. 1.): v. To bite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gnawing
GNAWING (subs.): दंशः: v. Bite, sting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gnome
GNOME:<BR>I A fairy: भूतधात्री (?).<BR>II A goblin:<BR>भूतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gnomic
GNOMIC,-AL: i.e. sententious: लघु (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gnomon
GNOMON:<BR>I Of a dial:<BR>(1) अङ्कुः;<BR>(2) कीलः;<BR>(3) मयूखः।<BR>II In geo.: *स्वरूपच्छेदः; कीलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gnomonics
GNOMONICS: घटीविद्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gnostic
GNOSTIC: *पण्डिताभिमानिन् (f. नी); नोस्तिकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gnosticism
GNOSTICISM: *नोस्तिकमतम्; नोस्तिकदर्शनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gnu
GNU: कृष्णसारजातीयोऽश्वकारो द्विशृङ्गो जन्तुविशेषः;<BR>prob. न्यङ्कुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go
GO:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.),<BR>when<BR>Keyūraka had gone:<BR>गते च केयूरके, K.; true and<BR>going to (i.e. reaching)<BR>the heart:<BR>यथार्था हृदयङ्गमा,<BR>Ku.;<BR>the danger is gone:<BR>गतं भयम्,<BR>V i. 5.;<BR>is<BR>gone, will not return:<BR>गत एव न निवर्तते, Ku. iv.<BR>30.;<BR>a road going to the Golden City:<BR>सुवर्णपुरगाभी<BR> पन्थाः, K.;<BR>that they should go the way of their<BR>husbands:<BR>यद्भर्तुर्गतिर्गन्तव्येति, P. iv.; in her<BR>absence, (it)<BR>goes to the daughter:<BR>तदभावे दुहितृगामि,<BR>V s.;<BR>(2) याति (या, c. 2.), and you go to<BR>another (man): अपरञ्च यासि, Mr. iv.;<BR>the man<BR>will go one month:<BR>मासमेकं नरो याति, H.; moon-<BR>light goes (away)<BR>with the moon:<BR>शशिना सह याति<BR> कौमुदी, Ku.;<BR>(3) एति (इ, c. 2.),<BR>come, come,<BR>let us go:<BR>एह्ये हि वामः; U.;<BR>(4) व्रजति (व्रज्, c.<BR>1.),<BR>go and conquer the enemies:<BR>भ्रज जय रिपुलोकम्,<BR>Ki.<BR>II To sell: expr. by लभते (लम्, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>प्राप्नोति (आप्, c. 5.), eight go for hundred:<BR>अष्टौ लभन्ते शतम्, Li.<BR>III To fare, turn out:<BR>q.v. Ph.:<BR>go in:<BR>अभ्यन्तरं प्रविश, Mr. i.;<BR>he has<BR>gone too far:<BR>अतिभूमिमयं गतः, K.; he is going<BR>(lit. wishes)<BR>to say something:<BR>किमप्ययं विवक्षुः,<BR>Ku.;<BR>or<BR>वक्तुकामः, Sa.; (I am)<BR>going to ask<BR>something:<BR>किञ्चित् प्रष्टुमनाः, Ku.; as the story goes:<BR>किल (enclitic);<BR>to go for nothing:<BR>विफलीभवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go about
GO ABOUT:<BR>I To round: q.v.<BR>II To endea-<BR>-vour: q.v.: perh. गच्छति, याति, यतते (यत्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go after
GO AFTER: अनुगच्छति (with acc.): v. To<BR>follow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go astray
GO ASTRAY:<BR>(1) अपन्थानं गच्छति, etc., Ana.;<BR>(2)<BR>उन्मार्गेण गच्छति, याति, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go away
GO AWAY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अपैति (इ);<BR>(2) अप-<BR>सरति;<BR>(3) अप-क्रामति;<BR>(4) अप-गच्छति;<BR>(5) अप-<BR>याति;<BR>(6) अप-सर्पति।<BR>II To vanish<BR>(1) गच्छति;<BR>(2) याति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go back
GO BACK:<BR>(1) प्रति-गच्छति,<BR>you should go back<BR>from here after communicating your message to us:<BR>अत्र नः सन्दिश्य प्रतिगन्तुमर्हसि, Sa. iv.;<BR>(2) प्रतियाति,<BR>D. ii.: v. To return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go before
GO BEFORE: पुरो गच्छति, याति,<BR>or<BR>सरति (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go by
GO BY:<BR>I Lit.: v. To pass by.<BR>II Fig., to<BR>follow: अनुगच्छति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go down
GO DOWN: अधो गच्छति: v. To descend; to<BR>sink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go forth
GO FORTH: निक्रामति: v. To go out (I.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go near
GO NEAR: उपगच्छति<BR>or<BR>उपयाति (with acc.): v.<BR>To approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go off
GO OFF:<BR>I To go away: q.v.<BR>II To turn out:<BR>q.v.<BR>III To discharge, as a gun: perh.<BR>मुच्यते, निर्- (pass. of मुच्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go on
GO ON:<BR>I In gen.: याति, प्र-,<BR>go on:<BR>याहीति, R.<BR>vi. 30.;<BR>go on, cattle:<BR>यातं गावौ यातम्, Mr. vi.<BR>II<BR>To take place: वर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go out
GO OUT:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) निष्क्रामति;<BR>(2) निर्ग-<BR>च्छति;<BR>(3) निर्याति;<BR>(4) निःसरति;<BR>(5) निरेति।<BR>II Of light:<BR>(1) निर्वाति (वा, c. 2.), Sa. v.;<BR>(2) शाम्यति, उप-, (शम्, c. 4.), Mu. Ph.:<BR>my<BR>life is g. ing out:<BR>प्रचलन्ति हि मे प्राणाः, Vi. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go out to meet
GO OUT TO MEET or RECEIVE:<BR>(1) प्रत्युद्गच्छति (गम्),<BR>Ku. vii. 52.;<BR>(2) प्रत्युदेति (इ), Ku. v. 31.;<BR>(3) प्रत्युद्याति (या), Vi. vii.;<BR>(4) प्रत्युद्व्रजति (व्रज्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go over
GO OVER:<BR>I To read: q.v.: वाचयति (c. of<BR>वच्).<BR>II To examine: q.v. परीक्षते (ईक्ष्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>III To change sides: expr. by श्रयति,<BR> आ-, सं-, (श्रि, c. 1.),<BR>people being alarmed go o.<BR>enemies:<BR>भूतानि उद्विजमानानि द्विषतां यान्ति संश्रयम्;,<BR>Ka. xiv. 13.<BR>IV To revolt: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go round
GO ROUND:<BR>(1) परिगच्छति;<BR>(2) पर्येति (इ);<BR>(3)<BR>चङ्क् भ्यते (freq. of क्रम्) N. i. 144.;<BR>(4) प्रदक्षिणं<BR> करोति<BR>or<BR>प्रदक्षिणीकरोति (= to g. r. a sacred<BR>fire etc. as a sort of reverential salutation),<BR>Sa. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go through
GO THROUGH:<BR>I To accomplish, finish: q.v.:<BR>समापयति (c. of आप्).<BR>II To suffer, under-<BR>-go: q.v.: अनुमवति (भू, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go to
GO TO:<BR>go to war:<BR>रणं गच्छति, B. p.; v. To<BR>go (I.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go to and fro
GO TO AND FRO: परि-क्रामति<BR>or<BR>क्राम्यति (क्रम्, c.<BR>1. and 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go towards
GO TOWARDS: अभिमुखं (with gen.)<BR>or<BR>-प्रति (with<BR>acc.) गच्छति, व्रजति, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go under
GO UNDER:<BR>I Lit.: अधो गच्छति, याति, etc.<BR>II<BR>To be known: q.v.: expr. by प्रथितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go up to
GO UP TO:<BR>(1) अभिगच्छति;<BR>(2) अभियाति;<BR>(3)<BR>अभ्येति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goad
GOAD (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रतोहः;<BR>(2) अङ्कुशः (for ele-<BR>-phants);<BR>(3) प्राजनम्;<BR>(4) शृणिः (= 2);<BR>(5)<BR>(rarely) तोत्रं<BR>or<BR>तोदनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goad
GOAD (v.):<BR>I Lit.: तुदति<BR>or<BR>तोदयति, प्र-, (तुद्,<BR>c. 6. or c. of तुद्),<BR>g. ing speech:<BR>वाकप्रतोदः,<BR>Ram.<BR>II Fig.: perh.<BR>(1) प्रतोदयति;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रणो(चो)दयति (c. of नुद्<BR>or<BR>चुद्): v. To<BR>drive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goal
GOAL:<BR>I Lit.: अग्रभूमिः।<BR>II Fig.: अन्तः: v.<BR>End.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goat
GOAT:<BR>(1) अजः;<BR>(2) छागः;<BR>(3) छागलः। She-g.:<BR>(1) अजा;<BR>(2) छागी।<BR>A flock of g.s:<BR>आजकम्। G.<BR>herd:<BR>(1) अजाजीवः;<BR>(2) जाबालः;<BR>(3) छागपालः।<BR>G.'s flesh:<BR>छागमांसम्।<BR>G.'s milk:<BR>छागीदुग्धम्<BR>or<BR>छागं<BR> दुग्धम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goatish
GOATISH: expr. by tat. comp.: v. Also lust-<BR>-ful, rank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goatishly
GOATISHLY:<BR>(1) छागवत्;<BR>(2) अजवत्: v. Also<BR>lustfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goat-sucker
GOAT-SUCKER: पक्षिविशेषः; *मिथ्योलूकः; छागचूषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go-between
GO-BETWEEN:<BR>(1) मध्यस्थः;<BR>(2) मध्यवर्तिन् (m.).<BR>Female g.: v. Procuress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gobbet
GOBBET: ग्रासः: v. Mouthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gobble
GOBBLE: उत्-ग्रसते (ग्रस्, c. 1.): v. To swallow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goblet
GOBLET:<BR>(1) चषक (mn.): v. Cup;<BR>(2)<BR>कांस्यम् (of Kānsa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goblin
GOBLIN:<BR>(1) भूतः,<BR>possessed by g.s:<BR>भूताविष्टः (ष्टा,<BR> ष्टं);<BR>(2) प्रेतः;<BR>(3) पिशाचः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

god
GOD:<BR>I A g.:<BR>(1) देवः (you are) ṭhe G. of g. s:<BR>देवानामपि देवता, Ku.: the earthly g.s (Brahmins):<BR>भूमिदेवाः, Ma.;<BR>(2) देवता (= deity), town g.:<BR>नगरदेवता, D. ii.;<BR>(3) सुरः (as opposed to असुरः<BR>Titan),<BR>having faith in g. s:<BR>सुरेषु श्रद्दधत् (f. ती),<BR>N.;<BR>(4) अमरः (= immortal);<BR>(5) विबुधः<BR>(=wise);<BR>(6) दिवौकस् (m.) (= residing in<BR>heaven);<BR>(7) lokapAlaH (of the quarters),<BR>human g.s (kings): नरलोकपालाः, R.<BR>II The G.:<BR>ईश्वरः, परम-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

godchild
GODCHILD: धर्मपुत्रः (f. त्री): धर्मसुतः (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goddess
GODDESS:<BR>(1) देवी;<BR>(2) भगवती (gen. restricted<BR>to दुर्गा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

godfather
GODFATHER: धर्मपितृ (m.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

godhead
GODHEAD:<BR>I Divinity: q.v.: देवत्वम्, -ता।<BR>II<BR>A god: देवता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

godless
GODLESS: निरीश्वरः (रा, रं), P. p.: v. Impious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

godlike
GODLIKE: दिव्य (f. व्या): v. Divine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

godliness
GODLINESS:<BR>(1) धार्मिकता;<BR>(2) धर्मिष्ठताः: v.<BR>Piety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

godly
GODLY:<BR>(1) धार्मिकः (की, कं);<BR>(2) धर्मिष्ठ (f. ष्ठा):<BR>v. Pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

godmother
GODMOTHER; धर्ममातृ (m.); धर्मजननी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

godsend
GODSEND:<BR>(1) expr. by देवदत्तः (त्ता, त्तं);<BR>(2)<BR>सौभाग्यम् (= good fortune).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

godson
GODSON: धर्मपुत्रः and sim. comp.s,<BR>g. of Viś-<BR>vāmitra:<BR>विश्वामित्रधर्मपुत्रः, B. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goer
GOER:<BR>(1) गन्तृ (f. न्त्री);<BR>(2) गामिन्<BR>or<BR>यायिन्<BR>(f. नी)<BR>or<BR>सरः (री, रं)<BR>or<BR>गः (गा, गं) in comp.,<BR>front g.:<BR>पुरोगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goggle-eyed
GOGGLE-EYED: लोलनेत्रः (त्रा, त्रं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

going
GOING (subs.):<BR>(1) गमनम्,<BR>g. back:<BR>प्रतिगमनम्; g. out:<BR>निर्गमः-नम्;<BR>g. round:<BR>परि-गमनम्;<BR>g. up to:<BR>अभिगमनम्;<BR>(2) यानम्,<BR>g. forth:<BR>निर्याणम्;<BR>g. away:<BR>अपयानम्;<BR>g.<BR>and coming:<BR>यातायातम्: v. The several verbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goitre
GOITRE:<BR>(1) गलगण्डः;<BR>(2) गण्डिः;<BR>(3) गडुः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goitred
GOITRED, GOITROUS: गलगण्डिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gold
GOLD (subs.):<BR>(1) स्वर्णम्;<BR>(2) सुवर्णम्;<BR>(3) कनकम्;<BR>(4) काञ्चनम्;<BR>(5) हेमन्;<BR>(6) हिरण्यम्; (rarely);<BR>(7) चामीकरम्;<BR>(8) जाम्बून्दम्;<BR>(9) रुक्मम्;<BR>(10)<BR>महारजतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gold
GOLD, OF GOLD (adj.): v. Golden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gold-beater
GOLD-BEATER: स्वर्णपत्रकारः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gold-dust
GOLD-DUST:<BR>(1) काञ्चनरेणुः;<BR>(2) कनकपरागः;<BR>(3) चामीकरचूर्णम्, K. and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

golden
GOLDEN:<BR>(1) by tat. comp.,<BR>g. ornament:<BR>कनक-<BR>भूषणम्;<BR>(2) काञ्चनः (नी, नं);<BR>(3) सौवर्ण (f. र्णी);<BR>(4) हिरण्मयः (यी, यं);<BR>(5) स्वर्णमयः (यी, यं);<BR>(6) हैमः (मी, मं);<BR>(7) कनकभयः (यी, यं). Ph.:<BR>the g. age:<BR>सत्ययुगम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goldfinch
GOLDFINCH: सुवर्णसवर्णपक्षः पक्षिविशेषः; *स्वर्णपतत्रः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goldfish
GOLDFISH: *स्वर्णवर्णः चीनदेशीयमत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goldleaf
GOLDLEAF:<BR>(1) स्वर्णपत्रम्;<BR>(2) सुवर्णपत्रम्;<BR>(3)<BR>कनकपत्रम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gold-refiner
GOLD-REFINER: स्वर्णशोधकः and sim. comp.s.:<BR>v. To refine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goldsmith
GOLDSMITH:<BR>(1) स्वर्णकारः;<BR>(2) सुवर्णकारः (rare);<BR>(3) हेमकारः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gold-thread
GOLD-THREAD or WIRE:<BR>(1) कनकसूत्रम्;<BR>(2) सुवर्ण-<BR>सूत्रम्;<BR>(3) सुवर्णतन्तुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gondola
GONDOLA: इटालिदेशीयकेलिनौविशेषः; गण्डः, -नौः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gondolier
GONDOLIER: गण्डवाहकः: v. Boatman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gong
GONG:<BR>(1) कांस्यम्;<BR>(2) घनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gonorrhoea
GONORRHOEA: मूत्राघातः (gen. term), Bha.:<BR>मूत्रशूक्रम् (?), Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good
GOOD:<BR>I In ordinary sense:<BR>(1) उत्तमः (मा,<BR> मं),<BR>the g. things of Camphor island:<BR>कर्पूरद्विपस्योत्त-<BR>मानि वस्तूनि, H. iv.;<BR>his best painter:<BR>निजश्चित्र-<BR>करोत्तमः, K.s. 57. 123.; the best of men (God):<BR>पुरुषोत्तमः,<BR>(2) उत्कृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं) (= excellent),<BR>g., bad, and middling:<BR>उत्कृष्टापकृष्टमव्यमः, K. b.;<BR>(3) विशिष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं) (= very g.), very g. cloth:<BR>विशिष्टवस्त्रम्, P. iii. 9.;<BR>(4) सु<BR>or<BR>सत् prefixed:<BR>a g. poet:<BR>सुकविः, Bha.;<BR>a. g. physician:<BR>सुचिकि-<BR>त्सकः;<BR>a g. judge:<BR>सद्विचारकः;<BR>g. man:<BR>सज्जनः or<BR>sim. सत्, U.;<BR>of g. appearance:<BR>सुरूपः (पा, पं);<BR>(5) गुणवत् (f. ती) (having g. qualities),<BR>g.<BR>soil:<BR>गुणवती भूमिः, Ka.;<BR>g. wife:<BR>गुणवती भार्या;<BR>(6) दर्शनीयः (या, यं)<BR>or<BR>दृश्य (f. श्या) (g. to see),<BR>other g. games:<BR>क्रीडान्तराणि दर्शनौयानि, D.<BR>II<BR>Suited, adopted: हितः (ता, तं), g. for cattle:<BR>गोहितः (ता, तं), Ka. iv. 51.;<BR>sour gruel is not<BR>g. in fever:<BR>यवागूर्न हिता ज्वरे, Bha.<BR>III Proper:<BR>right: q.v.: श्स्तः (स्ता, स्तं), N. iii. 9.<BR>IV<BR>Considerable: सु-,<BR>for a g: while:<BR>सुचिरम्, K.;<BR>g.<BR>many days:<BR>सुबहून्दिवसान्, C. viii.;<BR>a g. number<BR>of:<BR>सुबहु (mfn.).<BR>V Auspicious: q.v.: शुभः<BR>(भा, भं). Ph.:<BR>g. fellow:<BR>भद्रः<BR>or<BR>भद्रमुखः;<BR>g.-for-<BR>nothing:<BR>अकर्मण्य (f. ण्या) or sometimes by अ- in<BR>comp.,<BR>a field g.-for-nothing:<BR>अक्षेत्रम्, M.; a. g.<BR>deal: (adv.): विशेषेण; be so g. as, be g. enough:<BR>अनुग्रहपुर्वकम्;<BR>this is a g. day to me:<BR>अयं मे सुदिवसः,<BR>U. ii. 1. [N.B. Note सुदिवसः, सुप्रभातम् etc. are<BR>not used in the English sense for which use<BR>कुशलं ते, कुशलं भवतः, etc.<BR>or<BR>स्वागतम् to a visitor];<BR>as g. as (i.e. in effect): वस्तुतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good
GOOD (subs.):<BR>I Advantage:<BR>(1) उपकारः (=<BR>benefit),<BR>I. will do g. to this man:<BR>उपकारं करोम्यस्य,<BR>Ka. ix. 11.;<BR>(2) हितम् (= welfare),<BR>for the g.<BR>of the people:<BR>प्रकृतिहिताय; Sa. vii. For the g. of<BR>may be expr. by अर्थम्<BR>or<BR>अर्थे in comp.: v.<BR>For the sake of.<BR>II As opposed to evil:<BR>(1) शुभम्,<BR>this is g., this is not g.:<BR>शुभमिदमशुभमिदम्,<BR>K.;<BR>(2) कल्याणम्;<BR>(3) कुशलम्;<BR>(4) मङ्गलम्;<BR>(5)<BR>श्रेयस् (= well-being);<BR>(6) क्षेमम् (=5),<BR>ing.-con-<BR>ferring work:<BR>क्षेमङ्करेऽर्थे, B. xii. 6.<BR>III In pl.,<BR>=property: q.v.: सम्पत्तिः। Ph.: for g. expr.<BR>by circumlo.<BR>slept for g.:<BR>अप्रबोधाय सुष्वाप, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good
GOOD (as interj.):<BR>(1) वाढम् (as an assent): v.<BR>Yes;<BR>(2) साधु (= very g.; admirable).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good
GOOD, TO DO:<BR>(1) उपकरोति<BR>or<BR>-कुरुते (कृ, c. 8.)<BR>(with gen.), Ki. vii. 28.;<BR>(2) प्रियं करोति<BR>(with gen.), V. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good
GOOD, TO MAKE: v. To make good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good-breeding
GOOD-BREEDING:<BR>(1) भद्रता;<BR>(2) साधुता (= gentle-<BR>-manliness), D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good-fellowship
GOOD-FELLOWSHIP:<BR>I Lit.: सत्सङ्गः।<BR>II Pleasant<BR>company: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good-friday
GOOD-FRIDAY: सुशुक्रवारः<BR>or<BR>-वासरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good humour
GOOD HUMOUR:<BR>(1) प्रफुल्लचित्तता;<BR>(2) प्रसन्नमनस्कता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good-humoured
GOOD-HUMOURED:<BR>(1) प्रफुल्लचित्तः (त्ता, त्तं);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रफुल्लमनस्कः (स्का, स्कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good-humouredly
GOOD-HUMOUREDLY:<BR>(1) प्रफुल्लचित्तेन;<BR>(2) प्रसन्नमनसा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good-looking
GOOD-LOOKING:<BR>(1) प्रियदर्शनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) सुदृश्यः<BR>(श्या, श्यं);<BR>(3) सुदर्शनः (ना, नं);<BR>(4) दर्शनीयः<BR>(या, यं)<BR>or<BR>दृश्य (f. श्या),<BR>very g.:<BR>विशेषदृश्यः (श्या,<BR> श्यं), R., vi. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goodly
GOODLY: v. Handsome, pleasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goodman
GOODMAN:<BR>I In gen.: भद्रः।<BR>II Husband:<BR>आर्यपुत्रः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good-nature
GOOD-NATURE:<BR>(1) सौजन्यम्<BR>or<BR>सुजनता, त्वम्,<BR>this<BR>your g.:<BR>सौजन्यमेतद्धि वोः, Vi. v. 62.;<BR>(2) सद्भावः<BR>(rare), but then by that additional (act) which<BR>shewed (her)<BR>g.:<BR>तदानीन्तु तेनापरेण दर्शितसद्भावेन, K.;<BR>(3) भद्रता (= good-breeding).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good-natured
GOOD-NATURED:<BR>(1) सौजन्यवत् (f. ती);<BR>(2)<BR>सद्भावशालिन् (f. नी): v. Also gentlemanly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good-naturedly
GOOD-NATUREDLY:<BR>(1) सौजन्येन;<BR>(2) सद्भावतः:<BR>v. Also kindly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goodness
GOODNESS:<BR>I Excellence:<BR>(1) उत्तमता। (rare);<BR>(2) उत्कृष्टता;<BR>(3) विशिष्टता;<BR>(4) गुणवत्ता: v.<BR>Good-nature: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good-tempered
GOOD-TEMPERED:<BR>(1) अचण्डप्रकृति (mfn).;<BR>(2)<BR>मृदुप्रकृति (mfn.) (= mild).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

good-will
GOOD-WILL:<BR>I Benevolence:<BR>(1) दया (= kind-<BR>-ness);<BR>(2) अनुग्रहः (= favour).<BR>II Of any<BR>business: प्रतिष्ठा (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goods
GOODS: v. Good (subs.): (III). G.-wagon:<BR>भाण्डयानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goose
GOOSE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) हंसः (f. सी);<BR>(2) राजहंसः<BR>(f. सी);<BR>(3) चक्राङ्गः (f. ङ्गी) (rare). G.-quill:<BR>हंसपत्रम् (??).<BR>The ruddy g.:<BR>चक्रवाकः<BR>The striped<BR>g.:<BR>धार्तराष्ट्रः।<BR>II Fig.: v. Fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gooseberry
GOOSEBERRY: फलविशेषः; *तेपारि। G.-fool:<BR>*तैपारीयक्षीरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

go-out
GO-OUT: निर्गमः; जलनिर्गमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gordian
GORDIAN: Ph.:<BR>g. knot;<BR>अमोच्यबन्धः; to cut it:<BR>अमोच्यबन्धं छिनत्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gore
GORE (subs.):<BR>I Blood: q.v.: रक्तपिण्डः; रक्त-<BR>गुल्मः।<BR>II A piece of cloth: योजितपटखण्डः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gore
GORE (v.t.): विध्यति (व्यध्, c. 4.): v. To stab,<BR>pierce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gorge
GORGE (subs.):<BR>I The throat: q.v.: कण्ठः।<BR>II A defile, pass: the Krauncha g.:<BR>क्रौञ्चरन्घ्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gorge
GORGE (v.):<BR>I To swallow: उद्रग्रसते (ग्रस्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II To satiate, fill: q.v.: (कुक्षिं)<BR>पूरयति, परि-, (पूर्, c. 10).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gorgeous
GORGEOUS:<BR>(1) विचित्रः (त्रा, त्रं), with a g. canopy:<BR>वितानेन विचित्रेण, Mah. i. 183. 17.;<BR>(2) उज्ज्वलः<BR>(ला, लं),<BR>wearing a g. dress:<BR>उज्ज्वलवेशधारिन् (f. णी),<BR>Mr. ix;<BR>(3) शोभनः (ना, नं) (= beautiful).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gorgeously
GORGEOUSLY: expr. by adj.,<BR>g. dressed.:<BR>उज्ज्वल-<BR>वेशभृत् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gorgeousness
GORGEOUSNESS:<BR>(1) विचित्रता;<BR>(2) औज्ज्वल्यम्;<BR>(3) शोभा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gorget
GORGET: गलत्राणम्, कण्ठकञ्चुकः, and sim. comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gorgon
GORGON:<BR>I Subs.: गार्गी (?).<BR>II Adj.: राक्षसः<BR>(सी, सं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gormandize
GORMANDIZE: कुक्षिं परिपूर्य खादति (खाद्, c. 1.);<BR>अत्याहारं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gormandizer
GORMANDIZER, GORMAND: v. Gourmand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gorse
GORSE: पीतपुष्पः कण्टकिगुल्मविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gory
GORY:<BR>I Blood-stained: q.v.: रक्ताक्त (f. क्ता).<BR>II Murderous: रक्तप्रियः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goshawk
GOSHAWK: श्येनभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gosling
GOSLING:<BR>(1) हंसशावः, -कः<BR>(2) हंसशिशुः,<BR>as your<BR>g. s will be dead:<BR>यतस्ते शिशवः परासवः, N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gospel
GOSPEL: *सुवृत्तम्।<BR>To preach the g.:<BR>*कृष्टधर्मं प्रवक्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gossamer
GOSSAMER: वृद्धासूत्रम् (after Assamese).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gossip
GOSSIP (subs.):<BR>I A talkative person:<BR>(1)<BR>जल्पाकः;<BR>(2) वावदूकः;<BR>(3) प्रलापिन् (m.).<BR>II<BR>Idle talk:<BR>(1) जल्पितम्;<BR>(2) प्रलापः: v. Also<BR>rumour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gossip
GOSSIP (v.):<BR>(1) जल्पति (जल्प्, c. 1.) (?);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रलपति (लप्, c. 1.) (?): v. Also to converse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gossiping
GOSSIPING (adj.): जल्पाकः (की, कं): v. Babbling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

goth
GOTH: *गोथः<BR>G. ic.:<BR>*गोथीयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gouge
GOUGE (v.): उत्पातयति (c. of पत्); उद्धरति (हृ,<BR>c. 1.), D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gourd
GOURD: no gen. term:<BR>(1) रक्तकुष्माण्डः (= pum-<BR>-kin g.);<BR>(2) लाबुः, अ- (= bottle g.);<BR>(3)<BR>श्वेतकुष्माण्डः (= chāl kumrā); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gourmand
GOURMAND:<BR>(1) औदरिकः;<BR>(2) उदरम्भरिः;<BR>(3)<BR>आद्यूनः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gout
GOUT: सन्घिगतो वातः, Bha., g. in the stomach:<BR>पक्वाशयगतो वातः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gouty
GOUTY: वातरोगिन् (f. णी) (gen. term); सन्धि-<BR>वातकिन् (f. नी) (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

govern
GOVERN:<BR>I As a country:<BR>(1) शास्ति, प्र-,<BR> अनु- (शास्, c. 2.),<BR>g. the world:<BR>शाधि पृथ्वीम्, B. iii.<BR>53.;<BR>(2) पालयति, परि। (पाल्, c. 10.) (= to<BR>protect; not to regulate),<BR>let kings g. the<BR>earth always standing by virtue:<BR>राजानः परिपालयन्तु<BR> वसुधां धर्मे स्थिताः सर्वदा, Ma. x.;<BR>(3) by subs.<BR>प्रमुः, ईश्वरः, etc.: v. Lord, master.<BR>II To<BR>control: q.v.: नियच्छति (यम्, c. 1.).<BR>III In<BR>gram.: expr. by संबध्यते (pass. of बन्ध्) or<BR>अन्वीयते (pass of इ) (= to agree: with ins.),<BR>Da.; or by कर्मन् (n.) (= accusative).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

governance
GOVERNANCE: शासनम्: v. Government (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

governess
GOVERNESS:<BR>I Lit.: शासित्री।<BR>II An instruc-<BR>-tress; q.v.: perh. शासित्री, -अनु।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

government
GOVERNMENT: The act:<BR>(1) शासनम्, प्र-, अनु-,<BR>good g.:<BR>सुशासनम्;<BR>(2) परिपालनम् (= protection),<BR>g. of people:<BR>प्रजानां परिपालनम्, M.<BR>II Supreme<BR>power:<BR>(1) राज्यम्; v. Kingdom;<BR>(2) प्रभुत्वम्;<BR>v. Supremacy.<BR>III Form of g.: तन्त्रम्<BR>(?).<BR>IV The ruling power:<BR>(1) राजन्<BR>(= monarch: q.v.):<BR>(2) प्रभवः (m. pl.)<BR>(= masters.) V. A state: राष्ट्रम्,<BR>hearing that<BR>the g. was thoroughly occupied by the sons of<BR>Samhāravarman:<BR>संहारवर्मणः सुतैर्व्याप्तं राष्ट्रमाकर्ण्य,<BR>D. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

governor
GOVERNOR:<BR>I Ruler:<BR>(1) शासकः;<BR>(2) शासितृ<BR>(m.);<BR>(3) प्रभुः: v. Master, lord.<BR>II Of a<BR>province: अघिपतिः;<BR>(2) भोगपतिः,<BR>was made<BR>g. of. the town called Virapur<BR>वीरपुरनाम्नि नगरे<BR> भोगपतिः कृतः, H.;<BR>(3) देशाद्यक्षः,<BR>V s.<BR>III<BR>An instructor: q.v.: शासकः<BR>or<BR>शासितृ (m.),<BR>the god Śiva is my g.:<BR>भगवानीशो हि मे शासिता,<BR>Vi. ii. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

governorship
GOVERNORSHIP: आधिपत्यम्;<BR>(2) मोगपतित्वम्;<BR>(3)<BR>देशाध्यक्षता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gown
GOWN:<BR>I For women: शाटी (?).<BR>II Of scholars<BR>etc.: *गौणम्।<BR>III A dressing-g.: q.v.:<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gownsman
GOWNSMAN: *गौणभृत् (m.), गौणधारिन् (m.), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grace
GRACE (subs.):<BR>I Favour: q.v.: प्रसादः,<BR>she obtaining the g. of the gods:<BR>प्रसादमासाद्य सुरैः<BR> कृतं सा, N. xiv. 8.<BR>II Beauty: q.v.: लावण्यम्।<BR>III Good quality: गुणः।<BR>IV Ornament:<BR>q.v.: भूषणम्, these various (actions)<BR>become their<BR>g.s.:<BR>इति विविधमियाय तासु भूषाम्, Ki. x. 59.<BR>V As<BR>a title: देवः (for dukes), भगवत् (m.) (for<BR>archbishops).<BR>VI A goddess: अप्सरस् (f.).<BR>VII A prayer before or after meal:<BR>to<BR>say g.:<BR>*ईश्वरस्य प्रसादं कीर्तयति<BR>or<BR>प्रसादनाम् आद्रियते<BR>(दृ, c. 4.), N. xiv. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grace
GRACE (v.):<BR>I To adorn, decorate: q.v.:<BR>भूषयति,<BR>chaste knowledge graces flesh:<BR>शुचि भूषयति<BR> श्रुतं वपुः, Ki. ii. 32.<BR>II To honour: q.v.:<BR>सम्मानयति (c. of मन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graceful
GRACEFUL:<BR>(1) लावण्यवत् (f. ती) (= pretty);<BR>(2) शोभनः (ना, नं) (= fine);<BR>(3) रमणीयः (या, यं)<BR>(= lovely, pleasant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gracefully
GRACEFULLY:<BR>(1) शोभनम्: v. Beautifully,;<BR>(2)<BR>मधुरम्: v. Sweetly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gracefulness
GRACEFULNESS:<BR>(1) चारुता: v. Beauty,<BR>(2)<BR>माधुर्य्यम्: v. Sweetness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graceless
GRACELESS: नष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं): v. Depraved, corrupt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gracious
GRACIOUS:<BR>I Merciful: q.v.:<BR>(1) प्रसन्नः<BR>(न्ना, न्नं);<BR>(2) दयामयः (यी, यं),<BR>To be g.:<BR>प्रसीदति<BR>(सद्, c. 1.).<BR>II Excellent: q.v.: विशिष्टः<BR>(ष्टा, ष्टां).<BR>III Beautiful: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graciously
GRACIOUSLY:<BR>(1) सानुग्रहम् (= favourable);<BR>(2)<BR>सदयम्: v. Kindly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graciousness
GRACIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) प्रसन्नता;<BR>(2) दया: v. Kind-<BR>-ness,<BR>(3) औदार्यम्: v. Liberality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gradation
GRADATION: v. Grade, degree. In music:<BR>आरोहावरोहः। (?). M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grade
GRADE:<BR>(1) श्रेणिः (= class);<BR>(2) प्रकारः (=kind);<BR>(3) पदम् (= position). Ph.;<BR>g. d. service<BR>*श्रेणि-<BR>बद्धा वृत्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gradient
GRADIENT:<BR>I Moving: चलत् (f. न्ती).<BR>II<BR>Inclined: प्रणतः (ता, तं) (?),<BR>a g.:<BR>प्रणतभूमिः (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gradual
GRADUAL:<BR>(1) क्रिमिकः (की, कं), आनु-;<BR>(2) अल्पाल्प-<BR>in comp.,<BR>g. decrease:<BR>अल्पाल्पह्रासः, V.p.;<BR>(3)<BR>by adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gradually
GRADUALLY:<BR>(1) क्रमशः,<BR>a pot is g. filled:<BR>क्रमशः<BR> पूर्यते घटः, H.;<BR>(2) क्रमे क्रमे;<BR>(3) अनुक्रमेणः;<BR>(4)<BR>अल्पाल्पशः (little by lit.);<BR>(5) शनैः शनैः<BR>(= slowly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graduate
GRADUATE (subs.): उपाधिधारिन् (f. णी): उपाधि-<BR>ग्राहक (f. हिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graduate
GRADUATE (v.):<BR>to g. in a university:<BR>*विश्च-<BR>विद्यालयस्थोपाधिं गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.); g. scale:<BR>*अङ्कितपादा पद्धतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graduation
GRADUATION: expr. by verb: v. To graduate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graft
GRAFT (subs.): भिन्नवृक्षे निधानाय वृक्षपल्लवः<BR>or<BR>कलमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graft
GRAFT (v.):<BR>I Lit.: निदधति (धा, c. 3.) (?).<BR>II Fig.: निदधाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grafter
GRAFTER: सङ्करफलोत्पादकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grain
GRAIN (subs.):<BR>I Corn.: धान्यम्, small g.<BR>(= millet: q.v.): क्षुद्रधान्यम्।<BR>II Seed: q.v.:<BR>वीजम्।<BR>III A small particle: कणः।<BR>IV Of<BR>the veins of wood:<BR>against the g.:<BR>प्रतिलोमम्: v.<BR>A weight: expr. by रक्तिका (= 1¾ g.) Ph.:<BR>in. g. i.e. deeply seated: अस्थिगतः (ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grain
GRAIN (v.):<BR>I To dye: दृढं रञ्जयति (c. of रञ्ज).<BR>II To form into g s: कणमयं (f. यीं) करोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grainy
GRAINY: धान्यमयः (यी, यं) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graminivorous
GRAMINIVOROUS:<BR>(1) तृणजम्भ (f. म्भा);<BR>(2) शष्प-<BR>भोजिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) घासादः (f. दा, दं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grammar
GRAMMAR:<BR>(1) व्याकरणम्;<BR>(2) शब्दविद्या (rare), D.<BR>A master of the rules of g.:<BR>शब्दशासनविद् (mfn.)<BR>Si. xiv. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grammarian
GRAMMARIAN:<BR>(1) वैयाकरणः,<BR>a mere g.<BR>केवल-<BR>वैयाकरणः, S.k.;<BR>(2) शब्दशास्त्रज्ञः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grammatical
GRAMMATICAL:<BR>I Lit.: by comp.<BR>II Accor-<BR>-ding to the rules of grammar: not g.:<BR>व्याकरणलक्षणहीनः (ना, नं), Kav.<BR>or<BR>च्युतसंस्कारः<BR>(रा, रं), Sah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grammatically
GRAMMATICALLY:<BR>(1) व्याकरणानुसारेण;<BR>(2) by<BR>adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grampus
GRAMPUS: मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

granary
GRANARY:<BR>(1) कुशूलः;<BR>(2) धान्यकोष्ठः, -कः;<BR>(3) मरारः<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grand
GRAND:<BR>I Great: q.v.: महत् (f. ती).<BR>II<BR>Chief: q.v.: प्रधानः (ना, नं).<BR>III Lofty,<BR>dignified: q.v.: तेजस्विन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grandchild
GRANDCHILD: v. Grandson, granddaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

granddaughter
GRANDDAUGHTER:<BR>(1) पौत्री (= son's d.);<BR>(2) दौहित्री (= daughter's d.);<BR>(3) नप्त्री<BR>Great -g.:<BR>प्रपौत्री, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grandee
GRANDEE: महाजनः (?): v. Noble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grandeur
GRANDEUR:<BR>I Greatness: q.v.: महत्वम्।<BR>II<BR>Nobleness, majesty: q.v.: माहात्म्यम्।<BR>III<BR>Loftiness, impressiveness: q.v.: तेजस्विता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grandfather
GRANDFATHER:<BR>(1) पितामहः (= paternal);<BR>(2) मातामहः (maternal).<BR>Great g.:<BR>प्रपितामहः<BR>(p.); प्रमातामहः (m.).<BR>Great great g.:<BR>वृद्धप्रपिता-<BR>महः, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grandiloquence
GRANDILOQUENCE:<BR>(1) अतिशयोक्तिः;<BR>(2) उच्च-<BR>वादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grandiloquent
GRANDILOQUENT, GRANDILOQUOUS:<BR>(1) उच्च-<BR>वादिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) ध्वनिसारः (र, रं) (in bad<BR>sense), Si.;<BR>(2) वाक्शूरः, M.n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grandly
GRANDLY:<BR>(1) उज्ज्वलम् (= splendidly);<BR>(2)<BR>विशिष्टम् (= excellently);<BR>(3) better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grandmother
GRANDMOTHER:<BR>(1) पितामही (= paternal);<BR>(2) मातामही (= maternal).<BR>Great g.:<BR>प्रपितामही,<BR>etc.<BR>Great g.g.:<BR>वृद्धप्रपितामही, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grandson
GRANDSON:<BR>(1) पौत्रः (son's son);<BR>(2) दौहित्रः<BR>(daughter's s.);<BR>(3) नप्तृ (m.). Great -g.:<BR>प्रपौत्रः, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grange
GRANGE:<BR>I Granary: q.v.<BR>II Farm: क्षेत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

granite
GRANITE: *ग्रन्थिकः,<BR>red. g.:<BR>*रक्तग्रन्थिकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

granivorous
GRANIVOROUS: धान्यभूज् (mfn.); धान्यादः (दा, दं);<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grant
GRANT (subs.):<BR>(1) दानम्, प्र-, g. of a village:<BR>ग्रामदानम्, He.;<BR>(2) शासनम् (= edict: of royal<BR>g.), with g.s attested with his own signature:<BR>स्वहस्तकृतचिह्नशासनः, Si. xiv. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grant
GRANT (v.t.):<BR>I To give: q.v.:<BR>(1) ददाति or<BR>दत्ते (दा, c. 3.), what does not God g. (when) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">Page322</a>]<BR>gracious:<BR>किं न ददाति भगवान् प्रसन्नः, Ve.;<BR>(2)<BR>वितरति (तॄ, c. 1.), God, g. me whatever is good:<BR>तन्मे भद्रं भद्रं वितर भगवन्, Ma. i. 4.;<BR>to whom<BR>excessive powers had been g. ed:<BR>वितीर्णवीर्यातिशयान्,<BR>Si. i. 71. Ph.:<BR>to g. a request:<BR>प्रर्थितं<BR>or<BR>कामं<BR> ददाति, v. p.<BR>or<BR>अभिलाषं पूरयति।<BR>II To con-<BR>-cede:<BR>(1) स्वीकरोति (= to admit: q.v.);<BR>(2) by अथ<BR>or<BR>अथो (= g. ed),<BR>g. ed the arrow<BR>was discharged by him for me:<BR>अथो शरस्तेन मदर्थ-<BR>मुज्भ्कितः, Ki. xiv. 17.;<BR>(3) by imper.,<BR>I g. he<BR>is wholly so:<BR>तथाविधस्तावदशेषमस्तु सः, Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grantee
GRANTEE:<BR>(1) दानग्रहीतृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) प्रतिग्रहीतृ<BR>(f. त्री), He.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grantor
GRANTOR:<BR>(1) दानकर्तृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) दातृ (f. त्री):<BR>v. Giver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

granular
GRANULAR:<BR>(1) कणमयः (यी, यं) (?);<BR>(2)<BR>कणपूर्ण (f. र्णा) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grape
GRAPE: द्राक्षा,<BR>mountain- g.:<BR>वर्वतजा द्राक्षा;<BR>g. with-<BR>out stone or seedless g.:<BR>अवीजा द्राक्षा; large g.:<BR>गोस्तनी द्राक्षा, Bha. N.B. These words are<BR>often applied to raisins, Bha.: for distinc-<BR>-tion, add आमा<BR>or<BR>पक्वा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graphic
GRAPHIC, -AL:<BR>(1) विचित्रः (त्रा, त्रं) (= pictures-<BR>-que);<BR>(2) सुस्पष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं) (= very clear);<BR>(3) अर्थवत् (f. ती) (= significant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graphically
GRAPHICALLY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grapnel
GRAPNEL:<BR>I Properly: क्षुद्रलङ्गरः।<BR>II In gen:<BR>आक्रर्षणी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grapple
GRAPPLE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.),<BR>g.<BR>ed the arms of Śiva:<BR>शिवस्य भुजद्वयं जग्राह्, M.n.:<BR>v. To seize.<BR>II To comprehend: q.v.:<BR>गृह्णाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grapple
GRAPPLE, GRAPPLING (subs.):<BR>I Seizure:<BR>q.v.: ग्रहणम्।<BR>II A hook: आकर्षणी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grappling-irons
GRAPPLING-IRONS: लौहाकर्षणी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grapy
GRAPY:<BR>I Lit.: by comp.<BR>II Like grape:<BR>द्राक्षाभः (भा, भं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grasp
GRASP (v.):<BR>I To catch: q.v.: गृह्णाति (ग्रह्,<BR>c. 9.).<BR>II To comprehend: q.v.: गृह्णाति।<BR>G. at.: i.e. aspire to: q.v.: ईप्सति (desi.<BR>of आप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grasp
GRASP (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: ग्रहः, -णम,<BR>he has fallen<BR>in my g.:<BR>सोऽयं मद्भुजपञ्जरे निपतितः, Ve. iii.;<BR>embraced with a firm g.:<BR>निष्पपेष परिरभ्य वक्षसा,<BR>Ki. xviii. 13.: by their g. ing of each^1 other:<BR>तयोर्भूजविनिष्पेषात्, Mah. iii. 39. 60.<BR>II Men-<BR>-tal: v. Capacity, comprehension.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grasping
GRASPING (adj.): गृध्नु (mfn.): v. Covetous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graspingly
GRASPINGLY: expr. by adj.,<BR>un -g.:<BR>अगृध्नुः, R.:<BR>v. Also covetously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graspingness
GRASPINGNESS: गृध्नूता: v. Covetousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grass
GRASS: तृणम्। young g.:<BR>(1) बालतृणम्;<BR>(2) शष्पम्;<BR>(3) शादः। Meadow g.:<BR>(1) घासः;<BR>(2) यवसः।<BR>The ‘Sacrificial g.’:<BR>(1) कुश (mn.);<BR>(2) दर्भः।<BR>The Dūrvā g.:<BR>दूर्वा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grass-green
GRASS-GREEN:<BR>(1) शाद्वलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) शाद-<BR>हरितः (ता, तं);<BR>(3) नवतृण (f. णा), Ki. x. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grasshopper
GRASSHOPPER:<BR>(1) शलभः;<BR>(2) पतङ्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grassy
GRASSY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) बहुतृण (f. णा);<BR>(2)<BR>तृणावृतः (ता, तं); and sim. comp.s.<BR>II<BR>Green: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grate
GRATE (subs.): no equiv.: *लौहयोगः। लौहचुल्ली<BR>might be used for g. =fireplace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grate
GRATE (v.):<BR>I To furnish with g.s: *लौह-<BR>योगान्वितं (f. तां) करोति; लौहदण्डैः दृढीकरोति।<BR>II<BR>To rub: q.v.: घर्षति (घृष्, c. 1.).<BR>III To<BR>vex, irritate: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grateful
GRATEFUL:<BR>I Pleasant: q.v.: रम्य (f. म्या).<BR>II Thankful:<BR>(1) कृतज्ञ (f. ज्ञा);<BR>(2) कृतवेदिन्<BR>(f. नी),<BR>and who is not g.:<BR>यश्च कृतं न<BR> वेत्ति, H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gratefully
GRATEFULLY:<BR>I Pleasantly: q.v.<BR>II Thank-<BR>-fully: कृतज्ञतया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gratefulness
GRATEFULNESS:<BR>I Gratitude: q.v.<BR>II<BR>Pleasantness: q.v.: रभ्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grater
GRATER: घर्षणी (?), घर्षणयन्त्रम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gratification
GRATIFICATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) तोषणम्, सं-,<BR> परि-;<BR>(2) तर्पणम्, परि-, (rare).<BR>II Pleasure,<BR>delight: q.v.:<BR>(1) सन्तोषः;<BR>(2) परितोषः;<BR>(3) तुष्टिः;<BR>receiving g. at night:<BR>तुष्टिमुपेयुषां निशि,<BR>N. xvi. iii.<BR>III Reward: q.v.: पारितोषिकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gratify
GRATIFY: तोषयति, सं-, परि-, (c. of तुष्),<BR>you will<BR>g. him and return quick:<BR>तं सन्तोष्य सत्वरमागमिष्यसि,<BR>H.;<BR>the killer of Vritra was g. ed with his<BR>excessive strength:<BR>तुतोष वीर्यातिशयेन वृत्रहा, R. iii.<BR>62: v. To please, satisfy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grating
GRATING (adj.); कर्कशः (शा, शं), g. to the ear:<BR>कर्णकर्कशः (शा, शं), N. xvii. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grating
GRATING (subs.):<BR>I Rubbing: संघर्षणम्,<BR>g. of<BR>teeth:<BR>दन्तसम्।<BR>II Grate: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gratingly
GRATINGLY: कर्कशम्; v. Harshly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gratis
GRATIS: विना मूल्येन; स्वतः (= naturally).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gratitude
GRATITUDE:<BR>(1) कृतज्ञता;<BR>(2) कृतवेदिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gratuitous
GRATUITOUS:<BR>I Given without recompense:<BR>expr. by adv.<BR>II Without good ground:<BR>अमूलकः (का, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gratuitously
GRATUITOUSLY:<BR>(1) विना मूल्येन;<BR>(2) स्वतः<BR>(= naturally: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gratuity
GRATUITY: दानम्: v. Present, gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gratulate
GRATULATE, GRATULATION, GRATULATORY:<BR>v. Congratulate, congratulation, congratu-<BR>-latory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grave
GRAVE (adj.):<BR>I Heavy: q.v.: गुरु (f. र्वी).<BR>II Important: q.v.: गुरु (f. र्वी).<BR>III<BR>Solemn:<BR>(1) गम्भी(भी)रः (रा, रं) (= deep);<BR>(2) धीरः (रा, रं) (= steady).<BR>IV Of sound:<BR>(1) गम्भि(भी)रः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) मन्द्र (f. न्द्रा);<BR>(3)<BR>धीरः (रा, रं);<BR>(4) घनः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grave
GRAVE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: शवखातम् (?).<BR>II Tomb:<BR>q.v.: समाधिः।<BR>III Death, end: q.v.: अन्तः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grave
GRAVE (v.): मुद्रयति (मुद्र्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>engrave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grave-clothe
GRAVE-CLOTHE: प्रेतवासस् (n.),<BR>covering the<BR>emperor with g.:<BR>महाराजं वाससा समाच्छाद्य, Ram.<BR>ii. 83. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grave-digger
GRAVE-DIGGER: शवखातखनकः। (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grave-stone
GRAVE-STONE: निधानोपलः (?); निधानप्रस्तरः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graveyard
GRAVEYARD: प्रेतवनम्: v. Cemetery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gravel
GRAVEL (subs.): शर्करा (= both the earth and<BR>the disease).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gravel
GRAVEL (v.):<BR>I Lit.: शर्करावृतं (f. तां) or<BR>शर्कराच्छन्नं (f. न्नां) करोति।<BR>II Fig.: v. To<BR>entangle, embarrass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gravelly
GRAVELLY:<BR>(1) श्र्करावत् (f. ती);<BR>(2) शार्करिकः<BR>(की, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gravely
GRAVELY:<BR>(1) गम्भीरम्;<BR>(2) धीरम्: v. Grave<BR>(adj.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graveness
GRAVENESS: v. Gravity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gravitate
GRAVITATE: आकृष्यते (pass of कृष्), g.s. (lit. is<BR>drawn) towards it according to the law of g. ion<BR>(lit. by its force): आकृष्यते स्वाभिमुखं स्वशक्त्या,<BR>Go. iii. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gravitation
GRAVITATION: आकर्षणम्।<BR>Law of g.:<BR>आकर्षणशक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gravity
GRAVITY:<BR>I Heaviness: गुरुत्वम्, specific g.:<BR>विशेषगुरुत्वम्।<BR>II Weight, importance: q.v.:<BR>गुरुत्वम्।<BR>III Solemnity:<BR>(1) गाम्भीर्यम्;<BR>(2) धैर्य्भ्<BR>(= steadiness).<BR>IV Of sound:<BR>(1) गाम्मीर्यम्;<BR>(2) मन्द्रता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gravy
GRAVY: सिद्धमांसरसः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gray
GRAY (adj.):<BR>(1) पाण्डु (mfn.) (= pale white),<BR>covered with ash-g. hair:<BR>भस्मपाण्डुरोमाश्लिष्टः (ष्टा,<BR> ष्टं), K.;<BR>(2) धवलः (ला, लं) (= white: q.v.)<BR>g. old age:<BR>धवला जरा, K.;<BR>(3) धूम्र (f. म्रा)<BR>(= smoky: q.v.),<BR>g. eyed:<BR>धूम्राक्ष (f. क्षी), Ram.;<BR>(4) पलितः (ता, तं) (of the head and of old<BR>men),<BR>a man is not old because his head is g.:<BR>न<BR> तेन स्थविरो भवति येनास्य पलितं शिरः, Mah.;<BR>gray<BR>for nothing:<BR>वृथा पलितः, Si.; not by g. (hairs): न<BR> पलितैः, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gray
GRAY (subs.):<BR>I The colour: v. Gray<BR>(adj.).<BR>II A g. animal: expr. by white,<BR>g. horse:<BR>शुक्लाश्वः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grayish
GRAYISH:<BR>(1) पाण्डु (mfn.) (?);<BR>(2) पाण्डुरः<BR>(रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grayness
GRAYNESS: पलितम्: v. Gray (4).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

graze
GRAZE (v.):<BR>I To feed on: चरति (चर्, c. 1.),<BR>for g. ing at a distance:<BR>दूरे चरणाय, Pa.;<BR>g.<BR>grass:<BR>तृणं चरन्ति, Pa.<BR>II To feed: चारयति,<BR> सं-, प्र-, (c. of चर्),<BR>to g. calves:<BR>वत्सांश्चारयति।<BR>V.p.<BR>III To touch slightly: घर्षति, (घृष्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grazer
GRAZER: तृणचारिन् (f. णी), Pa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grazier
GRAZIER: चारकः, N.s.<BR>Cattle-g.:<BR>गोचारकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grazing
GRAZING (subs.):<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) चरणम्;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रचारः।<BR>II G. land:<BR>(1) प्रचारभूमिः, V.p.<BR>com.;<BR>(2) गोचरः (for king), Ki.<BR>III Rubb-<BR>-ing: आ-घर्षणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grease
GREASE (subs.):<BR>(1) वसा;<BR>(2) वपा;<BR>(3) मेदस्<BR>(n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grease
GREASE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: वसया श्लक्ष्णीकरोति: v. Also<BR>to smear.<BR>II To bribe: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greasily
GREASILY:<BR>I Lit. चिक्कणम्।<BR>II Grossly: अश्लीलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greasy
GREASY:<BR>I Oily: वसाप्लुतः (ता, तं) (after घृत-<BR>प्लुतः of N.).<BR>II Smooth: q.v.: चिक्कणः (णा, णं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

great
GREAT:<BR>(1) महत् (f. ती): in most senses: (a)<BR>of size:<BR>a g. forest:<BR>महावनम्, Mu.: v. Large.<BR>(b) of quantity:<BR>g. collection:<BR>महान्निचयः, Ki.;<BR>a g. crowd:<BR>महाजनसमूहः, Ku. (c) of weight:<BR>g. news:<BR>महती वार्त्ता, H.;<BR>for g. result:<BR>महते फलाय,<BR>Ki.: v. Important. (d) eminent, noble:<BR>of the g.:<BR>महताम्, Ki.;<BR>g. man:<BR>महाजनः, Mah.;<BR>g. -minded:<BR>महात्मन् (mfn.), K.: v. Principal,<BR>chief. (e) of degree, etc.:<BR>a g. while:<BR>महान्<BR> कालः, K.;<BR>g. effort:<BR>महान् यन्टः, R.; g. sinner:<BR>महापातकिन्, Vi.;<BR>of g. price:<BR>महार्ह (f. र्हा), Ku.;<BR>g. interval:<BR>महन्दतरम्। P.;<BR>(2) सु (= good) or<BR>अति (= very) prefixed (to intensify the<BR>meaning),<BR>to a g. distance:<BR>सुटूरम्, K.; g. many:<BR>सुबहु (mfn.), K.;<BR>to a g. degree:<BR>अत्यर्थम्, Ki.;<BR>(3) अधिकः (का, कं) (when there is compari-<BR>-son),<BR>the g. animals did not harass the little:<BR>ऊनं<BR> न सत्त्वेष्वधिको बबाधे, R. ii. 14.; g. er devotion:<BR>अधिका भक्तिः, K.: v. More.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

great-coat
GREAT-COAT: not equiv.: *महाचोलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

great-grandfather
GREAT-GRANDFATHER etc.: v. Grandfather<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greatest
GREATEST: in degree: परमः (मा, मं): v.<BR>Extreme.<BR>In the g. degree:<BR>परम्: v. Extremely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greatly
GREATLY:<BR>I Much, exceedingly: q.v.:<BR>(1) अति-<BR>or<BR>सु- in comp.;<BR>(2) अतिशयम्;<BR>(3)<BR>भृशम्।<BR>Very g.:<BR>सुतराम्, नितराम्,<BR>or<BR>अतितराम्,<BR>his love<BR>was very g. implanted:<BR>सुतरामारोपितप्रीतिरभवत्, K.<BR>II Nobly: q.v.: by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greatness
GREATNESS:<BR>(1) महत्त्वम्,<BR>for accession of g.:<BR>महत्त्व-<BR>योगाय, Ki. iii. 23.;<BR>(2) महिमन् (m.),<BR>the chief<BR>of devotees domineers with her g.:<BR>प्रभवति हि महिम्ना<BR> स्वेन योगेश्वरीयम्, Ma. x. 8.: v. Eminence,<BR>grandeur;<BR>(3) गुरुत्वम् (= importance: q.v.);<BR>(4) उदारता (= magnanimity: q.v.);<BR>(5)<BR>विपुलता (= largeness: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greaves
GREAVES: जङ्घात्राणम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grecian
GRECIAN:<BR>I Adj.:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2)<BR>*आग्रिकः (की, कं).<BR>II Subs; (a) a Greek:<BR>*अग्रिकः (b.) one versed in Greek: *अग्रिक-<BR>भाषाज्ञः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grecism
GRECISM: *अग्रिकभाषाणुसारिणी वाक्पद्धतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greedily
GREEDILY: expr. by adj.: v. Also covet-<BR>-ously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greediness
GREEDINESS, GREED:<BR>I Covetousness: q.v.:<BR>गृध्नुता।<BR>II Voracity:<BR>(1) घस्मरता<BR>or<BR>अह्मरता;<BR>(2) जिघत्सा,: v. Hunger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greedy
GREEDY:<BR>I Covetous: q.v.: गृध्नु (mfn.).<BR>II Of food:<BR>(1) अह्मरः<BR>or<BR>घस्मरः (रा, रं)<BR>(= voracious),<BR>the g. destructive Rudra:<BR>घस्मर-<BR>कलरुद्रः। vi. iii. 48.;<BR>(2) जिघत्सु (mfn.) (= wish-<BR>-ing to eat): v. Hungry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greek
GREEK: i.e.<BR>G. language:<BR>*अग्रिकभाषा। For<BR>other senses: v. Grecian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

green
GREEN (adj.):<BR>I Of colour:<BR>(1) हरितः (ता,<BR> तां)<BR>or<BR>हरित् (mfn.),<BR>about g. paddy:<BR>हरिते धान्ये,<BR>M. viii. 330.;<BR>(2) पलाशः (शा, शं) (rare),<BR>a<BR>wood g. like new leaves:<BR>नवपलाशपलाशवनम्, Si. vi.<BR>2.<BR>II Fresh: q.v.:<BR>g. manhood:<BR>नववयस्;<BR>g.<BR>crop:<BR>नवश्स्यम्।<BR>III Raw, immature: q.v.:<BR>अपरिणतः (ता, तं).<BR>IV Not dry, as of g.<BR>wood: आर्द्र. (f. र्द्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

green
GREEN (subs.):<BR>I The colour:<BR>(1) हरितः;<BR>(2)<BR>हरिद्वर्णः;<BR>(3) पलाशः (rare).<BR>II A grassy<BR>plain: शाद्वलस्थली: v. Also grassy.<BR>III In<BR>pl., vegetables: शाकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

green
GREEN, TO BE or BECOME: हरितायते (nomi.)<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greenfinch
GREENFINCH: पक्षिभेदः; हारीतः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greengage
GREENGAGE: no equiv.: *पलाशफलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greengrocer
GREENGROCER: फलादिविक्रेतृ (f. त्री); फलोप-<BR>जीविन् (f. नी), Ram. ii. 90. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greenhorn
GREENHORN:<BR>(1) अपरिणतबुद्धि (mfn.);<BR>(2)<BR>अपक्वधी (n. धि); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greenhouse
GREENHOUSE: *आतपत्राणम्; हरितगृहम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greensih
GREENSIH:<BR>(1) ईषद्धरितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) हरिदाभः<BR>(भा, भं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greenness
GREENNESS:<BR>I Lit.: हरितता, -त्वम्।<BR>II Fresh-<BR>-ness: नवता।<BR>III Immaturity: अपक्रता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greensward
GREENSWARD: तृणावृता भूमिः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greenwood
GREENWOOD (adj.): by comp.,<BR>g. shade:<BR>हरित-<BR>वनद्धाया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greet
GREET (v.): सभाजयति (सभाज्, c. 10.), coming<BR>to g. (his daughter)<BR>out of affection:<BR>स्नेहात्सभा- [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">Page325</a>]<BR> -जयितुमेत्य, U. i. 7.; uses the right arm to g. me:<BR>सभाजने मे सव्येतरं भुजं प्रयुंक्ते, Ram. xiii. 43.: v.<BR>Also salute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greeter
GREETER:<BR>(1) सभजयितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) better<BR>by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greeting
GREETING:<BR>(1) सभाजनम्;<BR>(2) अभिनन्दनम् (= con-<BR>-gratulation): v. Also salutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gregarious
GREGARIOUS:<BR>(1) यूयचारिन् (f. णी) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (= moving in company: as of<BR>elephants):<BR>(2) सङ्घप्रियः (या, यं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gregariously
GREGARIOUSLY:<BR>(1) by adj.;<BR>(2) सङ्घशः (in<BR>flock).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grenade
GRENADE: *अवपोथिका (used in a like sense in<BR>Mah).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grenadier
GRENADIER: *दक्षिणरक्षिन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grey
GREY: v. Gray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

greyhound
GREYHOUND: श्वन् (m.),<BR>and presented many tiger-<BR>like g.s:<BR>व्याघ्रसंहननद्युतीन्॥॥॥।शुनश्चोपानयद्वहून्,<BR>Ram. ii. 72. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grice
GRICE: शूकरशावः, -कः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gridiron
GRIDIRON: अम्बरीषम् (?); भ्राष्टम् (= frying pan).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grief
GRIEF:<BR>(1) शोकः,<BR>broken-hearted from g. on<BR>account of me:<BR>ममैव शोकेन विदीर्णवक्षसा, N. i.<BR>140.;<BR>(2) दुःखम् (= pain),<BR>g. at a son's loss<BR>dries up the heart, body and mind:<BR>हृच्छरीरमनःशोषि<BR> दुःखं पुत्रवियोगजम्, Ram. ii. 76. 28.: v. Also<BR>sorrow, distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grievance
GRIEVANCE:<BR>I Injury:<BR>(1) दुःखम्;<BR>(2) कष्टम्;<BR>(3) क्लेशः।<BR>II Grief: सन्तापः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grieve
GRIEVE (v.i.):<BR>(1) शोचति,<BR>why she will not g.<BR>in distress:<BR>कथं शोचेन्न दुःखिता, Ram.;<BR>(2) by<BR>adj.: v. Sorry.<BR>To g. at or for:<BR>अनुशोचति,<BR>Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grieve
GRIEVE (v.t.):<BR>I To afflict:<BR>(1) दुःखयति<BR>(nomi.),<BR>this g.s. me:<BR>अदो दुःखाकरोति मां, Si. ii.<BR>11.;<BR>(2) तापयति, सं-, (c. of तप्) (stronger),<BR>g. d by widowhood:<BR>वैधव्यतापिता, Si. xi. 67.;<BR>(3)<BR>दुनोति (दु, c. 5),<BR>I am not g.d:<BR>न दुये, Si.<BR>II To<BR>mourn: शोचति,<BR>I g. you:<BR>भवन्तं शोचामि, Mr. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grievingly
GRIEVINGLY: शोचमानः (ना, नं): v. Sorrow-<BR>-fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grievous
GRIEVOUS:<BR>I Heinous, aggravated: घोरः<BR>(रा, रं). Ph.:<BR>g. hurt:<BR>घोरक्षतम्।<BR>II Full of<BR>grief: शोकाकुलः (ला, लं).<BR>III painful:<BR>(1) दुःखाकरः (री, रं);<BR>(2) दुःखजननः (नी, नं), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grievously
GRIEVOUSLY:<BR>(1) घोरम्;<BR>(2) बलवत्;<BR>(3) सशोकम्<BR>(= sorrowfully): v. Also exceedingly^1, pain-<BR>-fully.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grievousness
GRIEVOUSNESS:<BR>(1) घोरता: v. Fierceness;<BR>(2)<BR>शोकाकृलता (= sorrowfulness);<BR>(3) शोच्यता<BR>(= sadness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

griffin
GRIFFIN, GRIFFON: *श्येनसिंहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grig
GRIG:<BR>I An eel: कुञ्चिकाभेदः।<BR>II Health:<BR>q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grill
GRILL: भृज्जति (भ्रस्ज्, c. 6.): v. To fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grim
GRIM: घोरः (रा, रं): v. Frightful, horrible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grimace
GRIMACE: मुखभङ्गिः, K.; and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grimly
GRIMLY: घोरम्: v. Fiercely, sternly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grimness
GRIMNESS: घोरत: v. Fierceness, frightful-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grimy
GRIMY: मलिनः (ना, नं): v. Dirty, foul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grin
GRIN (v.): दन्तान् दर्शयति (c. of दृश्),<BR>then the<BR>fool g.ned and laughed loudly:<BR>ततो जहास स्वनव-<BR>न्मूढो दन्तान् दर्शयन्, V. p. v. 28. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grin
GRIN (subs.):<BR>(1) विकृतस्मितम् (?);<BR>(2) better<BR>as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grind
GRIND (v.t.):<BR>I Lit.: पिनष्टि, निस्-, उत्-, विनिस्-<BR> प्रति-, (पिष्, c. 7.),<BR>say whether we shall g. the<BR>sun on the ground:<BR>किं ब्रूहि भूमौ पिनषाम भानुम्, B.<BR>xii. 18.: v. Also to pound.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>पिनष्टि, निस्-, विनिस-, g. ed (his) teeth from rage:<BR>रोषाद्दन्तान् दन्तैर्निष्पिपेष, Mah. iv. 16. 14.;<BR>it<BR>ground that powder:<BR>तदेष पिपेष पिष्टम्, N. xiii. 19.;<BR>g. ing the world:<BR>पिष्टा ब्रह्माण्डम्, Vi. vi. 10.;<BR>ground down by taxes:<BR>करनिष्पिष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं): v.<BR>To oppress.<BR>III To rub: घर्षति (घृष्, c.<BR>1.): v. To gnash, whet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grind
GRIND (v.i.):<BR>I To do g. ing: पेषणं करोति।<BR>II<BR>To become ground: पेष्यते, निस्, विनिस् (pass.<BR>of पिष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grinder
GRINDER:<BR>I Lit.: पेषकः, निस्-।<BR>II A molar:<BR>चर्वणदन्तः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grindingly
GRINDINGLY:<BR>(1) निष्पिष्य, वि-;<BR>(2) निष्पीड्य।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grindstone
GRINDSTONE:<BR>I Whet-stone: q.v.: शाणम्।<BR>II Grinding-s.: पेषणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grinningly
GRINNINGLY: दन्तान् दर्शयत् (f. न्ती), प्र-, V. p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grip
GRIP:<BR>I Subs.: expr. by हस्तभ्: v. Grasp.<BR>II Verb: गृह्राति (ग्रह्, c. 9.): v. To catch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gripe
GRIPE (subs.):<BR>I Grasp: q.v.: expr. by<BR>हस्तम्।<BR>II Handle: हस्तम्।<BR>III In pl. pain in<BR>the intestines: उदरशूलम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gripe
GRIPE (v.):<BR>I To grasp: q.v.<BR>II To cause<BR>pain to the bowels: expr. by उदरशूलम् (?).<BR>III To distress: सन्तापयति (c. of तप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

griper
GRIPER:<BR>I Lit.: ग्राहकः।<BR>II Oppressor:<BR>पेषकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grisly
GRISLY: भीषण (f. णा): v. Terrible, horrible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grist
GRIST:<BR>I Corn for grinding: पेष्यम्।<BR>II<BR>Ground-corn: पिष्टम्।<BR>III Supply, provi-<BR>-sion: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gristle
GRISTLE: तरुणास्थि (n.), Sr. (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gristly
GRISTLY: तरुणास्थिमयः (यी, यं), Monier<BR>Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grit
GRIT:<BR>I Sand, gravel: q.v.: शर्करा।<BR>II In<BR>pl. oats or wheat coarsely ground: स्थूल-<BR>पिष्टम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gritty
GRITTY: शर्करामयः (यी, यं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grizzel
GRIZZEL: पाण्डुरः (रा, रं): v. Gray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grizzly
GRIZZLY: धूम्रः (म्रा, म्रं),<BR>g. bear:<BR>धूम्रभल्लः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

groan
GROAN (v.): रटति (रट्, c. 1.): v. To cry,<BR>sigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

groan
GROAN (subs.): रटितम्,<BR>very sad g. s:<BR>अतिकातरं<BR> रटितम्, D.: v. Also cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

groat
GROAT: प्राचीनमुद्राविशेषः; *चतुष्पाणिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grocer
GROCER: गन्धवणिज् (m.) (?) सितादिविक्रेतृ (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grocery
GROCERY सितादिपण्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

groin
GROIN:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) वंक्षणः;<BR>(2) वाटः।<BR>II In<BR>architecture: *वाटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

groom
GROOM (subs.):<BR>(1) अश्वपालः, -कः;<BR>(2) तुरग-<BR>परिचारकः, K. and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

groom
GROOM (v.): परिचर्यां करोति (= with gen.);<BR>परिचरति (चर्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

groove
GROOVE:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) रेखा (= line);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रणाली (= canal).<BR>II Verb: रेखां<BR>or<BR>प्रणालीं<BR> करोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grope
GROPE (v.): परामृश्यति (मृश्, c. 6.): v. To<BR>search, feel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gropingly
GROPINGLY: अन्धकारे परामृशत् (f. ती) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gross
GROSS:<BR>I Bulky: स्थूलः (ला, लं).<BR>II Coarse:<BR>स्थूलः (ला, लं)<BR>III Stupid: स्थूलः (ला, लं).<BR>IV Obscene: q.v.<BR>V Great, as g. injus-<BR>-tice: महत् (f. ती).<BR>VI Whole, total: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grossly
GROSSLY:<BR>I Greatly: भृशम्।<BR>II Indecently:<BR>अश्लीलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grossness
GROSSNESS:<BR>I Thickness, coarseness: स्थौल्यम्<BR>or<BR>स्थूलता।<BR>II Enormity, greatness: महत्त्वम्<BR>III Indecency: अश्लीलता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grot
GROT, GROTTO:<BR>(1) कन्दरा;<BR>(2) दरी: v. Cave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grotesque
GROTESQUE:<BR>I Adj.: अपरूपः (पा, पं) (?).<BR>II<BR>Subs.: अपरूपम् (?) or by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grotesquely
GROTESQUELY: अपरूपम् (?): v. Also ridi-<BR>-culously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grotesqueness
GROTESQUENESS: अपरूपता (?): v. Also ridi-<BR>-culousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ground
GROUND (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) भूमिः<BR>or<BR>भूः,<BR>good<BR>g.:<BR>गुणवती भूमिः, Ka.;<BR>in another's g.:<BR>परुभूमौ,<BR>Vi.;<BR>seeing him fallen on the g.:<BR>तंदृष्ट्वा पतितंभूमौ,<BR>Ram. vi. 92. 63.;<BR>gone to the g.:<BR>गतो भुवि,<BR>Ku. xvi. 41.;<BR>(2) क्षितिः (= earth), fruitful^1 g.:<BR>फलवती क्षितिः, R.;<BR>(3) स्थलं, -ली, सं-, (= high<BR>g.), let us stand from here on high (fighting) g.:<BR>तदितः स्थलीमधितिष्ठाव, Vi. v.;<BR>lying on g. full of<BR>Dūrvā grass<BR>अदभ्रदर्भामधिशय्य संस्थलीम्, Ki. i. 58;<BR>(4) स्थण्डिलम् (= cleared g.) (rare),<BR>on the bare<BR>g.:<BR>स्थण्डिल एव केवले, Ku. v. 12.;<BR>(5) रणम्<BR>(= battle: q.v.: poet. for battle g.), Ram;<BR>(6) भूतलं<BR>or<BR>भहीतलम् (= surface of earth), V. p.<BR>II Basis;<BR>(1) मूलम्: v. Root;<BR>(2) कारणम्: v.<BR>Cause:<BR>(3) प्रयोजनम्: v. Object.<BR>III In<BR>painting: भित्तिः,<BR>although the g. is plain:<BR>मित्तौ<BR> समायामपि, Sa. vi. 16.<BR>IV In pl., dregs:<BR>मलम्। Ph.: (a)<BR>to gain g.:<BR>उपचीयते (pass. of चि):<BR>v. To advance; (b)<BR>to lose g.:<BR>अवचीयते: v.<BR>To decline; (c) to give g.: v. To recede.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ground
GROUND (v. i.): भूमिं<BR>or<BR>क्षिंतिं स्पृशति (स्पृश्, c. 6.)<BR>(?)<BR>or<BR>भूमौ<BR>or<BR>क्षितौ लगति (लग्, c. 1.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ground
GROUND (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: भूमौ लगयति (c. of<BR>लग्) (?)<BR>II To establish: q.v.: expr.<BR>by मूलः (ला, लं),<BR>g. ed in love:<BR>प्रेममूलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ground-floor
GROUND-FLOOR: प्रथमो भूभागः (after N.); sim.<BR>भूमिः<BR>or<BR>क्षितिः (when the sense is clear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ground-ivy
GROUND-IVY: लताविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

groundless
GROUNDLESS: अमूलः<BR>or<BR>निर्मूलः (ला, लं), -कः (का,<BR> कं): v. Also false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

groundlessly
GROUNDLESSLY:<BR>(1) अमूलम्;<BR>(2) निष्कारणम्: v.<BR>Also falsely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

groundlessness
GROUNDLESSNESS:<BR>(1) अमूलता;<BR>(2) असारता<BR>(= emptiness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ground-nut
GROUND-NUT: चीनवादामः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ground-rent
GROUND-RENT: भूमिकरः (?); स्तोमः, N. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

groundsel
GROUNDSEL: ओषधिभेदः; भूमिवर्धनः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

groundwork
GROUNDWORK:<BR>I Lit.: मित्तिमूलम्।<BR>II First<BR>cause: निदानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

group
GROUP (subs.):<BR>(1) सङ्घः,<BR>in g.:<BR>सङ्घशः;<BR>(2)<BR>समवायः;<BR>(3) समूहः;<BR>(4) गणः;<BR>(5) ओघः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

group
GROUP (v. t.): गणीकरोति (?): v. To arrange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grouse
GROUSE: वन्यपक्षिभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grove
GROVE:<BR>(1) वृक्षवाटिका;<BR>(2) उपवनम्;<BR>(3) आरामः।<BR>A g. near a house:<BR>(1) गृहारामः;<BR>(2) निष्कृटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grovel
GROVEL: रिङ्गति (रिङ्ग्, c. 1): v. To crawl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grovelling
GROVELLING (adj.): कृपण (f. णा): v. Mean,<BR>base.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grow
GROW (v. i.):<BR>I To increase: वर्धते (वृध्, c.<BR>1.),<BR>the fish grew there:<BR>स तत्र ववृधे मत्स्यः, Mah.<BR>iii. 187. 12.: v. To grow up.<BR>II To be<BR>produced: जायते (जन्, c. 4.)<BR>or<BR>भवति (भू, c.<BR>1.),<BR>barley g. s here:<BR>यवोऽत्र जायते<BR>or<BR>भवति। Ph.:<BR>land where all crops g.:<BR>सर्वशस्यप्रदा भूमिः, K. b.<BR>III To become: q.v.: जायते<BR>or<BR>भवति,<BR>grew<BR>fierce:<BR>क्रूरमजनि, Si.<BR>IV To arise from: q.v.:<BR>जायते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grow
GROW (v. t.): i.e. to raise: करोति (कृ, c. 8.)<BR>N. B. रोपयति, सं-, (c. of रुह्) is gen. restricted<BR>to planting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grow up
GROW UP:<BR>(1) वर्धते, परि-, सं-, (वृध्, c. 1.),<BR>Rājavāhana grew up with the minister's sons:<BR>राजवाहनो मन्त्रिपुत्रैः सहावर्धत, D.;<BR>(2) एधते (एध्,<BR>c. 1.) (rare),<BR>g. n up with young deer:<BR>मृगशाबैः<BR> सममेधितः (ता, तं), Sa. ii.;<BR>(3) रोहति (रुह्,<BR>c. 1.) (of trees etc.),<BR>as seeds g.:<BR>यथा वीजानि<BR> रोहन्ति, Vri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grower
GROWER:<BR>(1) रोपयितृ (m.);<BR>(2) रोपकः, आ-,<BR>g. of trees:<BR>वृक्षारोपकः, M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

growl
GROWL (v.): चित्कारं करोति: v. Also to roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

growl
GROWL (subs.): चित्कारः: v. Also roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grown up
GROWN UP (adj.): i.e. adult: प्रौढः (ढा, ढं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

growth
GROWTH:<BR>I Increase: q.v.: वृद्धिः। Ph.:<BR>of<BR>one year's g.:<BR>एकवर्षीण (f. णा);<BR>full g.:<BR>परिणामः<BR>: v. Maturity.<BR>II Product.: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grub
GRUB (subs.):<BR>I A larva: अण्डः (?).<BR>II<BR>Dwarf: वामनः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grub
GRUB (v.):<BR>I To dig: खनति (खन्, c. 1.).<BR>G. up:<BR>उन्मूलयति, विदलति (दल्, c. 1.), Ram.<BR>II To beg.: q.v.: भिक्षते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grubber
GRUBBER:<BR>I A digger: खनकः।<BR>II A ins-<BR>-trument: खनित्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grub-street
GRUB-STREET (adj.): perh. ग्राम्य (f. म्या) (lit.<BR>village).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grudge
GRUDGE (v.):<BR>(1) दूयते (pass. of दु) (= to be<BR>grieved);<BR>(2) by साभ्यसूयः (या, यं) (= envi-<BR>-ous);<BR>(3) by वदति (= to day).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grudge
GRUDGE (subs.):<BR>(1) रागः: v. Enmity;<BR>(2)<BR>अभ्धसूया (= envy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grudgingly
GRUDGINGLY:<BR>(1) अनिच्छया (= unwillingly);<BR>(2) दुःखेन (with difficulty).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gruel
GRUEL:<BR>(1) यवागूः;<BR>(2) काञ्चीकम्;<BR>(3) आरनालम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gruff
GRUFF: कर्कशः (शा, शं): v. Rough, harsh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gruffly
GRUFFLY: कर्कशम्; v. Roughly, harshly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gruffness
GRUFFNESS: कार्कश्यम्: v. Roughness, harsh-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grumble
GRUMBLE:<BR>I To complain:<BR>(1) न तुष्यति<BR>(तुष्, c. 4.);<BR>(2) खिद्यते (खिद्, c. 4.) (= to<BR>be distressed).<BR>II To roar: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grumbler
GRUMBLER: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grumblingly
GRUMBLINGLY:<BR>(1) असन्तुष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं) (= dis-<BR>-contented);<BR>(2) सखेदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grunt
GRUNT (v.):<BR>g. ed loud:<BR>जगर्ज परिघर्घरम्, V. p. i.<BR>4. 25.;<BR>where do not fierce g. ing boars g.:<BR>कः<BR> कः कुत्र न घुर्घुरायितघुरो घोरो घुरेच्छूकरः, Kav.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

grunt
GRUNT (subs.): घर्घरनादः and sim. comp.s.:<BR>v. Cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gruntling
GRUNTLING: शूकरशावः, -कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guano
GUANO: सामुद्रिकपक्षिमलम्; *गवनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guarantee
GUARANTEE (subs.):<BR>I The person: प्रत्यय-<BR>प्रतिभूः, Mit.<BR>II An engagement: प्रत्ययः,<BR>on<BR>my g., give him goods:<BR>मत्प्रत्ययेनास्य द्रव्यं देहि,<BR>Mit.: v. Security.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guarantee
GUARANTEE (v.): expr. by प्रत्ययः;<BR>(2) प्रतिभु-<BR>र्भवति (= to become surety).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guard
GUARD (v. t.):<BR>(1) रक्षति, परि-, सं-, अभि-, प्रति-,<BR>(रक्ष्, c. 1.), and the gods of quarters g. ing (your)<BR>strength as to penances:<BR>रक्षन्तस्तपसि बलञ्च लोकपालाः,<BR>Ki. v. 50.;<BR>was well-g. ed and well-protected<BR>like the edifice of Indra:<BR>सुरक्षितं सुगुप्तञ्च यथेन्द्रभवनं<BR> तथा, Mah.;<BR>(2) गोपायति, अभि-, सं-, अनु-,<BR>(गुप्, c. 1.),<BR>g. ed himself undaunted:<BR>जुगोपात्मा-<BR>नमत्रस्तः, R. i. 21.: v. Also to protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guard against
GUARD AGAINST: अप्रमत्तः (त्ता, त्तं) भवतिः v.<BR>Careful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guard
GUARD (subs.):<BR>I G. ing: रक्षा<BR>or<BR>रक्षणम्: v.<BR>Protection. Ph.:<BR>off the g.:<BR>प्रभत्तः (त्ता, त्तं):<BR>v. Careless;<BR>be on your g.:<BR>सावधानो भव, U. v.:<BR>v. Careful;<BR>to mount g.:<BR>रक्षम् अधितिष्ठति (स्था,<BR>c. 1.) (?)<BR>II One who g. s.:<BR>(1) रक्षिन्<BR>(m.);<BR>(2) रक्षकः;<BR>(3) रक्षाधिकृतः। N. B. Use<BR>pl. when it conveys many,<BR>life-g.:<BR>अङ्गरक्षकाः,<BR>Bha.<BR>G. -master:<BR>गुल्मस्थानाधिपः, Mu. v.<BR>III<BR>In a vessel, a fence: आवरणम् (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guarded
GUARDED (adj.):<BR>(1) अप्रमत्तः (त्ता, त्तं);<BR>(2)<BR>अवहितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guardedly
GUARDEDLY:<BR>(1) by adj.;<BR>(2) सावधानम्;<BR>(3)<BR>विमृश्य।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guardian
GUARDIAN:<BR>I Protector: q.v.:<BR>(1) रक्षकः;<BR>(2) रक्षितृ (m.);<BR>(3) गोप्तृ (m.);<BR>(4) गोपायकः,<BR>of the g. s of the three worlds:<BR>गोपायकानां भुवनत्रयस्य,<BR>Ki.<BR>II Of a minor or female: रक्षकः, the<BR>husband is the g. of a married woman (lit. in<BR>youth): भर्ता रक्षति यौवने, H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guardianless
GUARDIANLESS: अनाथः (था, थं); अरक्षकः (का,<BR> कं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guardianship
GUARDIANSHIP:<BR>I Care, defence: रक्षा।<BR>II<BR>The office: रक्षकपदम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guava
GUAVA:<BR>(1) अञ्जीरम्;<BR>(2) आत्रलम् (?) (comp. H.<BR>आमरुल्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gudgeon
GUDGEON: क्षुद्रमत्स्यभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guerdon
GUERDON: फलभ्: v. Reward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guess
GUESS (subs.):<BR>(1) ऊहः: v. Conjecture;<BR>(2)<BR>शङ्का (= apprehension).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guess
GUESS (v.):<BR>(1) शङ्कते, आ-, (शङ्क्, c. 1.) (= to<BR>apprehend: q.v.);<BR>(2) तर्कयति, वि-, (तर्क्,<BR>c. 10.): v. To conjecture;<BR>(2) अनुमिमीते,<BR>(मा, c. 3.) (= to infer: q.v.);<BR>(4) ऊहते<BR>(ऊह्, c. 1.), B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guest
GUEST:<BR>(1) अतिथिः (= one who comes un-<BR>-asked), make (him) the g. of the abode of Death:<BR>विधेहि कीनाशनिकेतनातिथिभ्, Si.;<BR>(2) निमन्त्रितः (ता,<BR> तं) (= invited), C.;<BR>(3) अभ्यागतः (ता, तं)<BR>(= visitor);<BR>(4) प्राघूर्णिकः (=1. rare);<BR>(5)<BR>प्रेक्षकः (= spectator), U. vii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guidance
GUIDANCE: expr. by उपदेशः<BR>or<BR>शासनम्: v. Advice,<BR>counsel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guide
GUIDE (subs.):<BR>I To a place:<BR>(1) अध्वदर्शिन्<BR>(f. नी) and sim. comp.s.<BR>I myself would be<BR>your g.:<BR>अहभेव भवेयमध्वदर्शी, D. vi.;<BR>(2) पथोपदेशकः,<BR>Ra. iv.<BR>II Adviser, leader: q.v.: उपदेष्ट्ट<BR>(f. ष्ट्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guide
GUIDE (v. t.):<BR>I To lead: q.v.:<BR>(1) नयति<BR>(नी, c. 1.);<BR>(2) पथं दर्शयति (c. of दृश्) or<BR>उपदिशति (दिश्, c. 1.).<BR>II To direct:<BR>(1)<BR>उपदिशति;<BR>(2) शास्ति, अनु-, (शास्, c. 2.): v.<BR>Also to control.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guide-post
GUIDE-POST: पथदर्शककाष्ठम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guider
GUIDER: v. Guide (subs.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guild
GUILD: श्रेणी, (?) वणिकसमाजः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guildhall
GUILDHALL: पौरशाला; श्रेष्ठिसङ्गमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guile
GUILE:<BR>(1) माया;<BR>(2) कपटम्: v. Deceit, cunning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guileful
GUILEFUL:<BR>(1) मायिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) कापटिकः<BR>(की, कं): v. Deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guileless
GUILELESS:<BR>(1) अमायः (या, यं);<BR>(2) निष्कपटः<BR>(टा, टं): v. Simple, honest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guilelessly
GUILELESSLY<BR>(1) निष्कपटम्;<BR>(2) मायां विना: v.<BR>Sincerely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guilelessness
GUILELESSNESS:<BR>(1) निष्कपटता;<BR>(2) अमायताः<BR>(3)<BR>अजिह्मता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guillotine
GUILLOTINE: गलकृन्तनम्; शिरश्छेदयन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guilt
GUILT:<BR>I Crime: q.v.:<BR>(1) अपराधः;<BR>(2) पापम्।<BR>II Criminality.: expr. by crime:<BR>my g.<BR>has fallen on another's shoulders:<BR>मया कृतं पाप-<BR>मन्यस्य मस्तके निपतितम्, Mr. ix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guiltily
GUILTILY:<BR>(1) सापराधम्;<BR>(2) सपापम्: v.<BR>Wickedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guiltiness
GUILTINESS:<BR>(1) अपराधिता;<BR>(2) कृतापराधता;<BR>(3)<BR>by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guiltless
GUILTLESS:<BR>(1) निष्पापः (पा, पं), g. livelihood:<BR>निष्पापा वृत्तिः, Raj.;<BR>(2) अपापः (पा, पं),<BR>thousands<BR>of g. men:<BR>अपापानां सहस्राणि, Mr. ix.;<BR>(3) निर-<BR>पराधः (धा, धं): v. Innocent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guiltlessness
GUILTLESSNESS:<BR>(1) निष्पापता;<BR>(2) निरपराधता।:<BR>v. Innocence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guilty
GUILTY:<BR>(1) पापिन् (f. नी),<BR>the love of the g.<BR>couple:<BR>पापिनोः प्रेम तत्तयोः, Raj.;<BR>(2) पातकिन् (f.<BR>नी),<BR>this g. Brahmin:<BR>अयं हि पातकी विप्रः, Mr.<BR>ix.;<BR>g. of heinous offences:<BR>महापातकिन्, V. s.;<BR>(3)<BR>अपराधिन्, (f. नी),<BR>I am surely g.:<BR>अपराधी नूनमहम्,<BR>V. ii.;<BR>(4) कृतापरधः (धा, धं);<BR>(5) लभापराधः<BR>(धा, धं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guinea
GUINEA: स्वर्णमुद्राविशेषः; *प्राचीनमुद्राविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guinea-fowl
GUINEA-FOWL: *चित्रकुक्कूटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guinea-pig
GUINEA-PIG: *बिन्दुशूकरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guise
GUISE:<BR>(1) वेषः: v. Dress;<BR>(2) छह्मन् (n.): v.<BR>Disguise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guitar
GUITAR: *षड्तन्त्री; हिस्पानपरिवादिनी: v. Lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gulf
GULF:<BR>I An abyss: q.v.: खातम्।<BR>II A bay:<BR>(1) महाखातम् (?);<BR>(2) उपसागरः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gulfy
GULFY: घूर्णिमयः (यी, यं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gull
GULL (subs.):<BR>(1) गङ्गाचिल्ली;<BR>(2) जलकुक्कूटी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gull
GULL (v.): v. To delude, cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gullet
GULLET: गलः,<BR>does not go below the g.:<BR>विशत्यधो-<BR>गलान्न। K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gullibility
GULLIBILITY: expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gullible
GULLIBLE: यत् शृणोति तत् श्रद्दधति: v. Credul-<BR>-ous, silly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gully
GULLY: प्रणली: v. Channel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gully-hole
GULLY-HOLE: प्रणालीमुखम् (?) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gulp
GULP (v.):<BR>g. down:<BR>ग्रसते (ग्रस्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To swallow.<BR>G. up:<BR>उद्गिरति (तॄ, c. 6.): v.<BR>To disgorge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gulp
GULP (subs.):<BR>I A swallow: ग्रास।<BR>II G. ing<BR>up.: उद्गिरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gum
GUM (subs.):<BR>I Of the mouth:<BR>(1) दन्तवेष्टः,<BR>whose g. s suddenly bleed:<BR>शोणितं दन्तवेष्टेभ्यो यस्या-<BR>कस्मात् प्रवर्तते, Bha.;<BR>(2) दन्तमांसम्।<BR>II Of trees:<BR>निर्यासः (?).<BR>III For gumming: *गोमम्।<BR>G.<BR>boil:<BR>दन्तपुप्पुटः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gum
GUM (v. t.): *गोमयति (nomi.): v. To glue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gummy
GUMMY: v. Viscous, adhesive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gun
GUN: 1. Cannon: *कामानम्,<BR>g. carriage:<BR>*कामान-<BR>यानम्।<BR>II Musket: *बन्दुकम्। N.B. Under Mah.<BR>iii. 15. 5., Nil identifies महायन्त्रम् with great<BR>and क्षुद्रयन्त्रम् with small g. s., but without<BR>authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gun-barrel
GUN-BARREL: *कामाननाली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gun-cotton
GUN-COTTON: *स्फोटकयन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gunner
GUNNER: *काभानिकः; कामानाधिकृतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gunnery
GUNNERY: *कामानविज्ञानम्; आग्नेयास्त्रविद्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gunpowder
GUNPOWDER: आग्नेयचूर्णम्। Nil. uses आग्नेयौषधम्<BR>probably in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gunshot
GUNSHOT:<BR>I Subs.: कामानविषयः।<BR>II Adj.:<BR>कामानकृतः (त, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gunsmith
GUNSMITH: बन्दुककारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gunwale
GUNWALE, GUNNEL: *कामानदर्शनम्; उच्चधारा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gurgle
GURGLE (v.): घर्घरायते (nomi.),<BR>g. stream:<BR>घर्घरवा<BR> सरित्, Mah. v. 19. अथाहं पूर्यमाणस्य जलकुभ्मस्य<BR> निःस्वनम् । अचक्षुविषयेऽश्रौषं वारणस्येव बृंहितम्,<BR>Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gurgle
GURGLE, GURGLING (subs.): घर्घरायितम्, घर्घरशब्दः<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gurnard
GURNARD, GURNET: समुद्रमत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gush
GUSH (subs.): प्रवाहः: v. Flow, rush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gush
GUSH (v.): प्रपतति (पत्, c. 1.): v. To Flow,<BR>rush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gushing
GUSHING (adj.): i.e. soft-hearted: कोमलहृदयः<BR>(या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gust
GUST:<BR>I Of wind: चण्डवातः and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Enjoyment: सम्भोगः।<BR>III Relish:<BR>स्वादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gusto
GUSTO: रुचिः: v. Taste, relish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gusty
GUSTY: v. Stormy, tempestuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gut
GUT (subs.): अन्त्राणि (n. pl.): v. Intestines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gut
GUT (v.):<BR>I Lit.: अन्त्राणि अपनयति (नी, c. 1.),<BR>निर्हरति (हृ, c. 1.), etc.<BR>II To plunder:<BR>लुण्ठति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gutter
GUTTER:<BR>I Of a house: स्यन्दनिका, Mit.<BR>II<BR>A channel: प्रणाली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gutteral
GUTTERAL: कण्ठ्य (f. ण्ठ्या),<BR>g. letter:<BR>कण्ठ्यवर्णः।<BR>G. sound:<BR>कण्ठकुहरम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guzzle
GUZZLE (v.): अतिपानं करोति: v. To drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

guzzle
GUZZLE, GUZZLER: अतिपायिन् (f. नी): v.<BR>Drunkard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gymnasium
GYMNASIUM: व्यायामशाला,<BR>school of g.:<BR>व्यायाम-<BR>शिक्षाशाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gymnastic
GYMNASTIC (adj.): by comp., g. exercises:<BR>व्यायामः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gymnastics
GYMNASTICS: धावनलक्ष्याभिहरणादिक्रीडाः; व्यायामः<BR>(= exercise): v. Also wrestling, fencing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gymnosophist
GYMNOSOPHIST: योगिन् (f. नी): v. Ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gypsum
GYPSUM: प्रस्तरविशेषः; *याक्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gypsy
GYPSY: *याक्ष (f. क्षी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gyration
GYRATION: घूर्णीः: v. Rotation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gyve
GYVE: निगडः: v. Fetter, chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ha
HA: आ: v. Oh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

habeas-corpus
HABEAS-CORPUS: *दर्शशासनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haberdasher
HABERDASHER: सूच्यादिक्षुद्रपण्यविक्रेतृ (m.) or<BR>विक्रयिन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

habiliment
HABILIMENT: वसनम्: v. Garment, dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

habit
HABIT:<BR>I Dress: q.v.: वेशः।<BR>II Condition,<BR>temperament: q.v.: अवस्था।<BR>III Practice,<BR>custom:<BR>(1) अभ्यासः (?);<BR>(2) शीलम् (?),<BR>of bad<BR>h. s:<BR>अशीलः (ला, लं), Ki. To be in the h. of:<BR>शीलः (ला, लं) in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

habit
HABIT (v.): v. To dress, clothe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

habitable
HABITABLE: वासयोग्यः (ग्या, ग्यं): v. Inhabi-<BR>-table.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

habitant
HABITANT: निवासिन् (f. नी): v. Inhabi-<BR>-tant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

habitation
HABITATION:<BR>(1) वसतिः,<BR>the h. of serpents:<BR>भुजङ्ग-<BR>मानां वसतिः, R.;<BR>(2) धामन् (n.), the h. of gods:<BR>त्रिदशधाम, N.: v. Residence, house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

habitual
HABITUAL:<BR>(1) नित्य (f. त्या) (= every day);<BR>(2) अभ्यासजः (जा, जं) (formed by habit) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

habitually
HABITUALLY:<BR>(1) नित्यम्;<BR>(2) सततम् (= const-<BR>-antly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

habitude
HABITUDE:<BR>I Familiarity: q.v.<BR>II Mode:<BR>प्रकारः (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

habituate
HABITUATE: अभ्यासं करोति: v. To accustom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hack
HACK (subs.):<BR>I A cut: q.v.:<BR>II A procuress:<BR>q.v.<BR>III A horse for hire: भाटकघोटकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hack
HACK (v.): व्यव-छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7.): v. Cut<BR>to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hackney-coach
HACKNEY-COACH: भाटकयानम् (?); gen. simp.<BR>यानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hackneyed
HACKNEYED (adj.):<BR>(1) साधारण (f. णी) (= com-<BR>-mon);<BR>(2) जीर्ण (f. र्णा) (= worn out);<BR>(3)<BR>बहुभिः प्रणीतः (ता, तं) (of subjects), Ana;<BR>(4) बहुप्रयुक्तः (क्ता, क्तं) (of words, etc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haddock
HADDOCK: समुद्रमत्स्यविशेषः; *हाडकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haft
HAFT: मुष्टिः v. Handle, hilt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hag
HAG:<BR>(1) जरती;<BR>(2) राक्षसी (in contempt).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haggard
HAGGARD:<BR>I Emaciate, lean: q.v.: परिकृशः<BR>(शा, शं).<BR>II Wild, rough: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haggle
HAGGLE (v.): perh. कलहं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hah
HAH: आः: v. Oh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hail
HAIL (interj.): नमः (with dat.) “शिखिनेऽनेक-<BR>शिखाय ते नमः”, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hail
HAIL (subs.):<BR>(1) शिलावृष्टिः;<BR>(2) करकावृष्टिः,<BR>heavy<BR>h.:<BR>तुमुलकरकावृष्टिः, Me. i. 55.<BR>H. water:<BR>करका-<BR>जलम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hail
HAIL (v.):<BR>I To salute: q.v.: वन्दते (वन्द्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II Of h.: expr. by subs. or वर्षति,<BR>it h. ed heavily burning firebrands:<BR>ज्वलद्भिरङ्गार-<BR>चयैर्नभस्तलं ववर्ष गाढम्, Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hailstone
HAILSTONE:<BR>(1) करका;<BR>(2) वर्षोपलः and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haily
HAILY: expr. by comp.,<BR>h. shower:<BR>करकावृष्टिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hair
HAIR:<BR>I Of the head:<BR>(1) केशः,<BR>seizing by the<BR>h.:<BR>केशैर्गृहीत्वा, P.;<BR>here they are dressing the h. of<BR>horses:<BR>इतोऽश्वानां केशकल्पना क्रियते, Mr. iv.;<BR>the<BR>Śakas with short h, the Pāradas with flowing h.:<BR>अर्द्धमुण्डान् शकान्, प्रलम्बकेशान् पारदान्, V.p. iv.<BR>3.;<BR>arranging the h. in the folds of a peacock's<BR>tail:<BR>मयूरबर्हिभङ्ग्या केश्पाशं विधाय, D.;<BR>(2) कचः;<BR>(3) कुन्तलः;<BR>(4) चिकृरः;<BR>(5) शिरोरुहः, मूर्द्धजः, etc.<BR>(poet). The entire h. of the head:<BR>(1) केशपाशः;<BR>(2) केशकलापः;<BR>(3) कचौघः, N.;<BR>(4) चिकुरप्रकरः।<BR>N.; etc., (her)<BR>h. not very curly, thick, long and<BR>every one of them naturally equal, smooth,<BR>and black:<BR>अनतिभङ्गुरो बहुल आयामवानेकैकनिसर्गसम-<BR>स्निग्धनीलो मूर्द्धजकलापः, D. vi.<BR>Matted or clotted<BR>h.:<BR>जटा, -जुटः; Curly h.:<BR>(1) अलकः;<BR>(2) चूर्णकुन्तलः।<BR>H.;<BR>twisted together into a single braid:<BR>वेणिः<BR>(णी);<BR>to do so:<BR>वेणीं<BR>or<BR>शिखां बध्नाति, Me.<BR>A braid<BR>of h.:<BR>कवरी।<BR>Ornamental h.:<BR>धम्भिल्लः (rare.) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">Page331</a>]<BR>II Of the body:<BR>(1) रि(लो)मन् (n.),<BR>with<BR>gladdened h.:<BR>हृष्टरोमन् (mfn.), Ram.;<BR>(2) बालः<BR>(specially of an animal's tail), Ki.;<BR>(3)<BR>तनु(नू)रुहम् (poet).<BR>III Of plants: केश(स)रः,<BR>Ph.:<BR>a h.'s breadth:<BR>रेखामात्रमपि, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haircloth
HAIRCLOTH: लो(रो)मपटः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hairdresser
HAIRDRESSER: केशकल्पकः: v. Barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hairiness
HAIRINESS: लो(रो)मशता, -त्वम्: v. Hairy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hairless
HAIRLESS:<BR>I Of the head:<BR>(1) अकेशः (शा, शं);<BR>(2) केशहीनः (ना, नं) and sim. comp.<BR>s, like a<BR>crest on a h. head:<BR>शिरसीव कङ्कणमपेतमूर्द्धजे, Si. xv.<BR>33.<BR>II Of the body: निर्लोमन् (mfn.) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hair-powder
HAIR-POWDER: केशचूर्णम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hair-spring
HAIR-SPRING: *केशाग्रतारः; सूक्ष्मतारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hairy
HAIRY:<BR>(1) लो(रो)मशः (शा, शं);<BR>(2) लोमावृतः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

halberd
HALBERD: शूलविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

halcyon
HALCYON:<BR>I Subs.: मत्स्यरङ्गः: v. Kingfisher.<BR>II Adj.: v. Peaceful, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hale
HALE (adj.): सुस्थः (स्था, स्थं): v. Healthy,<BR>robust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hale
HALE (v. t.): आकर्षति (कृष्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>pull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half
HALF (subs.):<BR>(1) अर्द्धम्,<BR>h. the day is over:<BR>अर्द्धं गतं<BR> दिवसस्य, V.;<BR>will take the other h.:<BR>अपरमर्द्धं<BR> गृह्णीयुः, Da.;<BR>and its h. in width:<BR>तदर्धेन तु विस्तृता,<BR>A. p.;<BR>(2) अर्द्धभगः<BR>or<BR>अर्धांशः,<BR>with h. of it:<BR>तदर्द्ध-<BR>भागेन, Ku. Ph.: in h., i.e. in two: द्विधा;<BR>each<BR>of them went halves with her:<BR>अर्द्धार्द्धभागाभ्यां<BR> तामयोजयतामुभे, R. x. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hale
HALE (adj.): अर्द्ध (f. र्द्धा),<BR>h.-moon:<BR>अर्द्धचन्द्रः:<BR>v. Half(subs.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-afraid
HALF-AFRAID: भीतभीतः (ता, तं), Ki. xiv. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-binding
HALF-BINDING: अर्द्धचर्मबन्धनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-blood
HALF-BLOOD: v. Half-brother, half-sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-boot
HALF-BOOT: *आगुल्फपादुका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-bred
HALF-BRED: अर्द्धशिक्षितः (ता, तं) (?) (used in<BR>Bengali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-brother
HALF-BROTHER:<BR>I By the same father:<BR>(1)<BR>वैमात्रेयभ्राता;<BR>(2) सापत्नः (rare);<BR>(3) अन्योदर्यो<BR> भ्राता, Mit.<BR>II By the same mother;<BR>(1)<BR>मातृजो भ्राता, Mah.;<BR>(2) अन्यपितृजो भ्राता, K. b.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-burnt
HALF-BURNT:<BR>(1) अर्द्धदग्ध (f. ग्धा) and sim.<BR>comp.s.;<BR>(2) दग्धादग्ध (f. ग्धा), D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-caste
HALF-CASTE: सङ्कीर्णयोनि (mfn.), M. x. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-cooked
HALF-COOKED: अर्द्धसिद्धः (द्धा, द्धं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-dead
HALF-DEAD:<BR>(1) अर्द्धमृतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) मृतकल्पः<BR>(ल्पा, ल्पं);<BR>(3) मृतप्रायः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-dozenth
HALF-DOZENTH: षष्ठ (f. ष्ठी): v. Sixth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-eaten
HALF-EATEN: अर्द्धोपभुक्तः (क्ता, क्तं), Ku. and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-hearted
HALF-HEARTED: निहृदयः (या, यं) (= without<BR>any heart).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-holiday
HALF-HOLIDAY: in schools; perh. अर्द्धानध्यायः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-learned
HALF-LEARNED: v. Half-bred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-open
HALF-OPEN:<BR>(1) अर्द्धाविवृतः (ता, तं) and sim.<BR>comp.s;<BR>(2) स्फुटास्फुटः (टा, टं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-penny
HALF-PENNY: ताम्रमुद्राविशेषः; *अर्द्धपाणिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-seas-over
HALF-SEAS-OVER:<BR>(1) अर्द्धमत्तः (त्ता, तं);<BR>(2)<BR>मध्येन मदेन मत्तः (त्ता, त्तं), Ni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-sister
HALF-SISTER:<BR>I By the same father: वैमात्रेय-<BR>भगिनी।<BR>II By the same mother: अन्यपितृजा<BR>or<BR>मातृजा भगिनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-way
HALF-WAY (adv.): अर्द्धपथे, V. =i. and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-year
HALF-YEAR:<BR>(1) षण्मासः;<BR>(2) अर्द्धवर्षः and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

half-yearly
HALF-YEARLY:<BR>I Adj.:<BR>(1) षाण्मासिकः (की,<BR> कं);<BR>(2) अर्द्धवार्षिकः (की, कं);<BR>II Adv.:<BR>षण्मासे षण्मासे, M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

halibut
HALIBUT: समुद्रमत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hall
HALL:<BR>(1) शाला;<BR>(2) सभा (= public h.),<BR>the h.<BR>of Brahmā is not supported by columns:<BR>ब्राह्मी सभा<BR> स्तम्मैर्न धृता, Mah.;<BR>(3) चैत्यम्, -कम् (= religious<BR>h. of Buddhists), Mah. ii. 21. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hallelujah
HALLELUJAH: ईश्वरगीतम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

halloo
HALLOO (interj.):<BR>(1) मोः<BR>or<BR>भो<BR>or<BR>भो भो;<BR>(2)<BR>हंहो।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

halloo
HALLOO (v.): उच्चैः शब्दायते (nomi.); v. To<BR>call.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hallow
HALLOW (v.): पुनाति (पू, c. 9.), मन्त्रपूतः (ता,<BR> तं), K.: v. To sanctify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hallucination
HALLUCINATION: मतिविभ्रमः: v. Delusion,<BR>dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

halm
HALM or HAUL: काण्डः: v. Stalk, straw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

halo
HALO: तेजस् (n.), K.: v. Also glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

halt
HALT (v.):<BR>I To stop:<BR>(1) अवतिष्ठते (स्था, c.<BR>1.) (= to stay);<BR>(2) विश्राम्यति (श्रम्, c. 4.)<BR>(= to rest). H. ing place (for troops): निवेशः<BR>(= encampment), R. xvi. 29.<BR>II To hesi-<BR>-tate: विचिकित्सति।<BR>III To limp: q.v.: लङ्गति<BR>(लङ्ग्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

halt
HALT (subs.):<BR>I Stay, rest: अवस्थितिः।<BR>II<BR>Lame:<BR>लङ्गुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

halt
HALT, HALTING (adj.): पङ्गु (mfn.): v. Lame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

halter
HALTER (subs.):<BR>I Rope, noose: q.v.: रज्जूः।<BR>II For the neck: कण्ठपाशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

halter
HALTER (v.): कण्ठपाशेन बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.) (?):<BR>v. To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

halve
HALVE (v.): अर्द्धार्द्धं करोति।<BR>H. ing it with the<BR>gambling-master:<BR>तदर्द्धं सभिकाय दत्त्वार्द्धं स्वीकृत्य,<BR>D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

halved
HALVED (adj.): in botany: *अर्द्धच्छिन्नः (न्ना, न्नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

halves
HALVES:<BR>to cry h.:<BR>अर्द्धं ममेति वदति (वद्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ham
HAM:<BR>I The back of the knee: मन्दिरः।<BR>II<BR>The thigh: ऊरुः।<BR>III Of hog: *लावण-<BR>शूकरोरुः; शौकरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hamlet
HAMLET: पल्लिः, -ग्रामः: v. Village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hammer
HAMMER (subs.):<BR>(1) मुद्गरः;<BR>(2) अयोधनः।<BR>(= forge-h.), R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hammer
