HAPLY:<BR>(1) दैवात्: v. Accidentally;<BR>(2) अपि<BR> नाम (= would it......).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

happen
HAPPEN:<BR>(1) वर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.) (= to occur),<BR>we do not know what has h. ed to her:<BR>न विह्मः<BR> किं तस्या वृत्तमिति, K.;<BR>(2) by भवति (भू, c. 1.)<BR>(= to be),<BR>what is to h. will h.:<BR>भवितव्यं भवत्येव, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">Page334</a>]<BR>D. b.;<BR>(3) पतति, नि-, सं-, आ-, (पत्, c. 1.)<BR>(= to befall),<BR>alas! very bad has h. ed:<BR>अहो<BR> कष्टतरमापतितम्, K. N. B. when it h. ed to be=when<BR>it was is expr. by sim. loc.: v. When.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

happily
HAPPILY:<BR>I Luckily:<BR>(1) सौभाग्येन;<BR>(2) दिष्ट्या।<BR>II In a happy manner:<BR>(1) सुखेन;<BR>(2)<BR>सुखान्यनुभवत् (f. न्ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

happiness
HAPPINESS:<BR>(1) सुखम् (= pleasure),<BR>I seek neither<BR>h. nor wealth:<BR>न सुखं प्रार्थये नार्थम्, Ki. xi. 66.;<BR>(2)<BR>श्रेयस् (m.) (= bless);<BR>(3) सन्तोषः (=content-<BR>-ment);<BR>(4) सौभाग्यम् (= good fortune);<BR>(5)<BR>श्रीः (fortune).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

happy
HAPPY:<BR>I Fortunate; q.v.: धन्यः (न्या, न्यं).<BR>II Good: q.v.:<BR>(1) प्रशस्तः (स्ता, स्तं)<BR>(= commendable);<BR>(2) श्रेयम् (f. सी) (rare),<BR>of this speech although h.:<BR>श्रेयसोऽप्यस्थ वचसः, Ki.<BR>xi. 44.<BR>III Delighted: q.v.:<BR>(1) सुखिन्<BR>(f. नी),<BR>be delightedly h.:<BR>मोदमानः सुखी भव,<BR>Mah.;<BR>(2) सन्तुष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं) (= content).<BR>IV<BR>Able: q.v.: पटु (f. also ट्वी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harangue
HARANGUE (subs.): उच्चवचस् (n.) (?): v.<BR>Speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harangue
HARANGUE (v.):<BR>h. d the populace:<BR>प्रजाभ्यो भारतीं<BR> व्याहरति (हृ, c. 1.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haranguer
HARANGUER: expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harass
HARASS (v.):<BR>I To fatigue: q.v.: खेदयति<BR>(c. of खिद्).<BR>II To annoy:<BR>(1) बाधते, प्र-,<BR> परि-, (बाध्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) अर्दति<BR>or<BR>अर्दयति, -ते (अर्द्,<BR>c. 1. and 10.), D. vii.: v. To trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harassing
HARASSING (adj.):<BR>(1) खेदजननः (नी, नं): v.<BR>Fatiguing;<BR>(2) क्लेशकरः (री, रं): v. Trouble-<BR>-some.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harbinger
HARBINGER:<BR>(1) अग्रेसरः;<BR>(2) दूतः (= envoy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harbour
HARBOUR (subs.):<BR>I Refuge: शरणम्।<BR>II A<BR>port: *क्रोडः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harbour
HARBOUR (v.):<BR>I To shelter, protect: q.v.<BR>II To take shelter: वसति (वस्, c. 1.),<BR>I.<BR>will h. here one night:<BR>अत्रैकां रजनीं वसामि, K. s.<BR>18. 225.: v. To stay, reside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harbourage
HARBOURAGE: आश्रयः।: v. Shelter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harbour-master
HARBOUR-MASTER: *क्रोडनायकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hard
HARD (adj.):<BR>I To the touch:<BR>(1) कठिनः<BR>(ना, नं) (best equiv.),<BR>with h. limbs:<BR>कठिनैः<BR> शरीरैः;<BR>(2) कठोरः,<BR>h. er than adamant:<BR>वज्रादपि<BR> कठोराणि, U.<BR>II Fig.: hard-hearted: q.v.:<BR>कठिनः (ना, नं).<BR>III Difficult: q.v.:<BR>(1)<BR>कठिनः (ना, नं),<BR>sometimes they are ambiguous<BR>and h.:<BR>क्वचिद्वक्रता कठिनता च, Pra.;<BR>(2) कठोरः (रा, रं),<BR>with h. argumentative discourses:<BR>कठोरतार्किकालापैः।<BR>IV Trying, distressing:<BR>(1) कठिनः (ना, नं),<BR>very h. pain:<BR>नितान्तकठिनां रुजम्,<BR>V ii.;<BR>(2) दीनः<BR>(ना, नं): v. Pitiable, wretched.<BR>V =exces-<BR>-sive: q.v.<BR>VI Of wines: perh. कर्कशः<BR>(शा, शं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hard
HARD (adj.):<BR>I Diligently: q.v.: आयासेन।<BR>H.-fought battle:<BR>भीषणं<BR>or<BR>घोरं युद्धम्।<BR>II With<BR>difficulty: q.v.: कष्टेन। He is h. up for money:<BR>धनाभावेन क्लिश्यति।<BR>III Excessively: q.v.:<BR>नितान्तम्।<BR>To drink h.:<BR>अतिपानं करोति;<BR>h. by:<BR>अति-<BR>सन्निहितः (ता, तं).<BR>IV Rapidly: q.v.: शीघ्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harden
HARDEN:<BR>I Trans:<BR>(1) कठिनीकरोति, Ki. i.<BR>36.;<BR>(2) कठिनं (f. नां) करोति।<BR>II Intrans:<BR>(1) कठिनीभवति;<BR>(2) कठिनः (ना, नं) भवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hard-hearted
HARD-HEARTED:<BR>(1) कठिनहृदयः (या, यं), K.;<BR>(2) कठिनचेतस् (mfn), Ve. vi. and sim.<BR>comp.s.;<BR>(3) कठिनः (ना, नं),<BR>women are<BR>surely h.:<BR>कठिनाः खलु स्त्रियः, Ku. iv. 5.;<BR>(4)<BR>कठोरः (रा, रं),<BR>o, h.:<BR>अयि कठोर, U. iii. 27.;<BR>(5) निष्ठुरः (रा, रं): v. Cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hard-heartedness
HARD-HEARTEDNESS:<BR>(1) कठिनहृदयता and sim.<BR>comp.s.;<BR>(2) काठिन्यम्;<BR>(3) नैष्ठुर्यम्: v.<BR>Cruelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hardihood
HARDIHOOD: साहसम्: v. Boldness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hardly
HARDLY:<BR>I With difficulty: q.v.: कथमपि।<BR>II Scarcely: कष्टेन।<BR>III Harshly: q.v.:<BR>(1) कठिनम्;<BR>(2) कठोरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hard-mouthed
HARD-MOUTHED: कठिनमुखः (खा, खं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hardness
HARDNESS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) कठिनता<BR>or<BR>काठिन्यम्;<BR>(2) कठोरता (rare).<BR>II Harshness, insensi-<BR>-bility:<BR>(1) कठिनता,<BR>leave off h.:<BR>जहिहि कठिनताम्।<BR>Ki. x. 51.;<BR>(2) कठोरता (rare).<BR>III Difficulty<BR>of comprehension or accomplishment:<BR>कठिनता।<BR>IV Hardship: q.v.:<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hardship
HARDSHIP:<BR>(1) कष्टम्,<BR>I got this h.:<BR>इदं कष्टमुपागमम्,<BR>K.s.;<BR>(2) क्लेशः (= trouble: q.v.), do not [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">Page335</a>]<BR>think of this h.: इमं परिक्ले शं हृदि मा कृथाः, Mah.;<BR>(3) दुःखम् (= pain), putting (you) into such h.:<BR>ईदृशं दुःखमानीय, Mah.; the h. s met in the<BR>(forest)<BR>Daṇḍaka:<BR>दण्डकायां प्राप्तानि दुःखानि, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hardware
HARDWARE: लोहभाण्डानि (n. pl.).<BR>H. manu-<BR>facturer:<BR>लोहमाण्डकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hard-working
HARD-WORKING (adj.): परिश्रमिन् (f. णी): v.<BR>Industrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hardy
HARDY:<BR>I Bold, confident: q.v.: साहसिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR>II Strong, inured to fatigue:<BR>q.v.: कठिनः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hare
HARE: शशः, -कः, h.'s horn (any improbability):<BR>शशविषाणम्; h.-spotted (the moon): शशाङ्कः; h. (i.e.<BR>h.'s flesh)<BR>is cool, light, sweet:<BR>शशः शीतो लघुः<BR> स्वदुः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harebell
HAREBELL: नीलमसीरसो लताविशेषः, *क्षीरवल्ली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hare-brained
HARE-BRAINED: चपलः (ला, लं): v. Rash,<BR>giddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hare-lip
HARE-LIP: शशोष्ठः (?); छिन्नोष्टः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harem
HAREM:<BR>I The place:<BR>(1) अवरोधः;<BR>(2) शुद्धान्तः;<BR>(3) अन्तःपुरम्।<BR>II The female:<BR>(1) अवरोधः,<BR>although his h. was large:<BR>अवरोधे महत्यपि, R. i.<BR>32,;<BR>(2) अवरोधवध्वः (f. pl.), Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hark
HARK:<BR>(1) शृणु;<BR>(2) आकर्णय;<BR>(3) निशामय।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harlequin
HARLEQUIN: भण्डः: v. Jester, buffoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harlot
HARLOT:<BR>(1) वेश्या;<BR>(2) पण्यस्त्री: v. Prostitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harlotry
HARLOTRY:<BR>I Of women: वेश्यावृत्तिः।<BR>II Of<BR>men: वेशवधूपभोगः, and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harm
HARM (subs.): अपकारः,: v. Damage, injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harm
HARM (v.): अपकरोतिः v. To damage, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harmful
HARMFUL: हिंस्र (f. स्रा): v. Hurtful, injurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harmless
HARMLESS:<BR>I Innocent: q.v.: निरपराधः (धा, धं).<BR>II Unhurt: अक्षतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harmlessly
HARMLESSLY:<BR>(1) निरपराधम्: v. Innocently;<BR>(2)<BR>अक्षतम् (= unhurt).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harmlessness
HARMLESSNESS: मिरपराधता (not अहिंसा which<BR>is active virtue).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harmonic
HARMONIC, -AL:<BR>(1) रक्तः (क्ता, क्तं);<BR>(2) श्लिष्टः<BR>(ष्टा, ष्टं),<BR>and the h. sound of lute:<BR>श्लिष्टञ्च तन्त्रीस्वनम्,<BR>Mr. iii. 5.;<BR>(3) एकतालः (ला, लं)<BR>or<BR>एकतानः<BR>(ना, नं) (= in unison).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harmonically
HARMONICALLY: रक्तम्,<BR>h. and sweetly:<BR>रक्तञ्च मधुरञ्च,<BR>Mr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harmonics
HARMONICS: रागाः (m. pl.),<BR>to know h.:<BR>रागान्<BR> जानातिः v. Music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harmonious
HARMONIOUS:<BR>I HARMONIC: q.v.<BR>II Sweet,<BR>melodious: q.v.: मधुरः (रा, रं).<BR>III Sym-<BR>-metrical: सर्वङ्गसंवादिन् (f. नी) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harmoniously
HARMONIOUSLY:<BR>I Of sounds:<BR>(1) रक्तम्;<BR>(2)<BR>मधुरम्: v. Sweetly.<BR>II Symmetrically: expr.<BR>by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harmonium
HARMONIUM: a musical instrument *हर्म्योनः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harmonize
HARMONIZE: expr. by adj.,<BR>the tones h.:<BR>श्लिष्टाः<BR> स्वराः;<BR>the arguments h.:<BR>संवसन्ति तर्काः: v. To<BR>agree;<BR>h. the sound:<BR>नादं रक्तं कुरु (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harmony
HARMONY:<BR>I Of sounds:<BR>(1) रक्तम्, “रक्तं नाम<BR> वेणुवीणादिस्वराणामेकीभावः”, Narada;<BR>(2) एकतालः<BR>(नः) (= unison: q.v.).<BR>II Melody, sweet-<BR>-ness: q.v.: माधुर्यम्।<BR>III Agreement, sym-<BR>-metry: सर्वाङ्गसंवदिता। (?).<BR>IV Peace, friend-<BR>-ship: ऐक्यम्: v. A literary work: *ऐक्यदर्शनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harness
HARNESS (subs.): (अश्व-) सज्जा and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harness
HARNESS (v.):<BR>I To equip.: सज्जीकरोति।<BR>II<BR>To yoke: रथं युनक्ति<BR>or<BR>योजयति (यृज्, c. 7. and<BR>10.),<BR>h. ed chariot:<BR>युक्तो रथः, Ram. ii. 13. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harp
HARP (subs.): *त्रिभुजवीणाः v. Lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harp
HARP (v.):<BR>I Lit.: वादयति (c. of वद्): v.<BR>To play.<BR>II Fig.: to dwell tediously on<BR>the same theme: भूयोभूयो गायति (गै, c. 1.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harper
HARPER, HARPIST: त्रिभुजवीणावादकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harpoon
HARPOON:<BR>I Subs.: perh. शूलम्।<BR>II Verb:<BR>शूलोन गृह्वाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harpooneer
HARPOONEER, HARPOONER: शूलवेधकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harpy
HARPY:<BR>I A fabulous monster: क्षुधा (??).<BR>II An extortioner, plunderer: q.v.:<BR>निष्कर्षकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harridan
HARRIDAN:<BR>(1) वृद्धवेशया;<BR>(2) वृद्धकुट्टिनी, K. s.<BR>xii. 79.: v. Prostitute, old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harrier
HARRIER: शशश्वन् (m.): v. Hound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harrow
HARROW (subs.):<BR>(1) कोटि(टी)शः;<BR>(2) जित्यः<BR>(rare);<BR>(3) लोष्टभेदनः, A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harrow
HARROW (v.):<BR>I Lit.: कोटिशं चालयति (c. of<BR>चल्) (with loc.)<BR>II To rend, grind: पिनष्टि,<BR> निस्- (पिष्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harrower
HARROWER:<BR>I Properly: कोटिशचालकः<BR>II<BR>=harrier: q.v.:<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harrowing
HARROWING (adj.): अरुन्तुदः (दा, दं): v. Heart-<BR>-rending, horrible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harsh
HARSH:<BR>(1) कर्कशः (शा, शं),<BR>h. like the lotus<BR>stalk:<BR>अभ्भोजनालकर्कशः, Vi.; this man is h. (in<BR>appearance): कर्कशोऽयं पुरुषः, D. iv.;<BR>h. to the<BR>ear:<BR>कर्णकर्कशः (शा, शं), N.;<BR>this is the h. end of<BR>my peacefulness:<BR>एष भे प्रशमस्य कर्कशः परिणामः, Vi.<BR>ii.;<BR>(2) रूक्षः (क्षा, क्षं) (= rough), lotus-film is<BR>sweet (but) h. (in taste): भृणालं मधुरं रूक्षभ्, Bha;<BR>in a h. tone:<BR>रूक्षेण स्वरेण, Mah.;<BR>of exceedingly<BR>h. resolution towards the daughter of Janaka:<BR>जनकात्मजायां नितान्तरूक्षामिनिवेशः (शा, शं) R. xiv.<BR>43;<BR>(3) परुषः (षा, षं) (of words), h. language:<BR>परुषं वाक्यम्, Ram.: v. Also hard, cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harshly
HARSHLY:<BR>(1) कर्कशम्;<BR>(2) रूक्षम्;<BR>(3) परुषम्,<BR>Mah.<BR>or<BR>परुषाक्षरम्, R. (in harsh words): v.<BR>Also cruelly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harshness
HARSHNESS:<BR>(1) कर्कशता, -त्वम्<BR>or<BR>कार्कश्यम्, R.;<BR>(2)<BR>रूक्ष्ता<BR>or<BR>रौक्ष्यम्,<BR>forgive my h.:<BR>रौक्ष्यं मे क्षमस्व, R.<BR>xiv. 56.;<BR>(3) परुषता<BR>or<BR>पारुष्यम् (of language),<BR>h. is not good:<BR>परुषता न साध्वी, Ki. ix. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hart
HART:<BR>(1) मृगः;<BR>(2) हरिणः;<BR>(3) कुरङ्गः, -मः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harvest
HARVEST (subs.):<BR>I The season: लवः,<BR>h. is<BR>the reaping time:<BR>लवः शस्यच्छेदनकालः, Nil.<BR>II<BR>The crops: शस्यानि (n. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harvest
HARVEST (v.): लुनाति (लू, c. 9.),<BR>in sowing, in<BR>h. ing:<BR>वपने लवने, Pa: v. To reap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harvester
HARVESTER:<BR>(1) लावकः, N. d.;<BR>(2) लवनकर्तृ<BR>(f. त्री), K. b.: v. Reaper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

harvest-home
HARVEST-HOME: नवान्नम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hash
HASH (subs.): कुट्टितं सिद्धमांसम् (?); वेसवारः, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hash
HASH (v.): कुट्टयति (कुट्ट्, c. 10.): v. To chop,<BR>mince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hasp
HASP: कुडुपः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hassock
HASSOCK:<BR>(1) कटः;<BR>(2) कुशासनम् (used by<BR>Brahmins).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haste
HASTE (subs.): त्वरा, of doubled speed from h.:<BR>त्वराद्विगुणरंहस् (mfn.), Ku. ii. 68.; to make h.:<BR>v. To haste; in h.: v. Hastily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haste
HASTE, HASTEN (v.):<BR>I Intrans: त्वरते<BR>(त्वर्, c. 1.),<BR>h., h. the sages are calling:<BR>त्वरस्व,<BR> त्वरस्व ऋषयः शब्दायन्ते, Sa.: v. Also to fly, run.<BR>II Trans:<BR>(1) त्वरयति (c. of त्वर्),<BR>who h. s<BR>crowds in the way:<BR>वृन्दानि त्वरयति पथि, Me.;<BR>h. his dinner:<BR>त्वरयास्य भोजनम्, v. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hastily
HASTILY:<BR>(1) त्वरितम्;<BR>(2) सत्वरम्;<BR>(3) त्वरान्वितः<BR>(ता, तं) and sim. comp.s, Ram. ii. 13. 20.;<BR>(4) क्षिप्रम्: v. Quickly. Ph.:<BR>should not do a<BR>thing h.:<BR>सहसा विदधीत न क्रियाम्, Ki. ii. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hastiness
HASTINESS:<BR>I Haste: त्वरा।<BR>II Rashness:<BR>q.v.: असमीक्ष्य-<BR>or<BR>आविमृष्यकारिता।<BR>III Irrita-<BR>-bility: शीघ्रागिता, and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hasty
HASTY:<BR>I Quick: q.v.: त्वरितः (ता, तं).<BR>II<BR>Rash: q.v.: असमीक्ष्य-<BR>or<BR>अविमृष्य-कारिन् (f. णी),<BR>III Of words: अविमृष्य (f. ष्या)<BR>or<BR>अन्याय-,<BR>in comp. (= unjust).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hat
HAT: पाश्चात्यशिरस्कम्: v. Cap, turban.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hatch
HATCH (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: बिभर्ति (भृ, c. 3.),<BR>ants<BR>h. but do not break their eggs:<BR>अण्डानि बिभ्रति स्वानि<BR> न भिन्दन्ति पिपीलिकाः, Mah.<BR>II Fig.: to con-<BR>-trive, form: q.v.: सं-कल्पयति (कॢप्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hatch
HATCH (subs.): in a deck: *प्रवेशपिधनम्। To be<BR>under the h. s: (lit.) अवरुद्धः (द्धा, द्धं); (fig.)<BR>अवसन्नः (न्ना, न्नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hatchet
HATCHET: टङ्कः,<BR>cut with axes, and h. s and with<BR>bills.:<BR>कृठारैष्टङ्कैश्च दात्रैश्चैव प्रचिच्छिदुः, Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hate
HATE (subs.): v. Harted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hate
HATE (v.):<BR>(1) द्वेष्टि, वि-, (द्विष्, c. 2.), h. s<BR>beautiful (things): रम्यं द्वेष्टि, Sa.;<BR>bad men h. the<BR>doings of the great:<BR>द्विषन्ति मन्दाश्चरितं महात्मनाम्,<BR>Ku.;<BR>(2) जुगुप्सते (जुगुप्स्, c. 1.) (stronger<BR>than h. ing);<BR>(3) घृणां करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hateful
HATEFUL (adj.):<BR>I Malignant: q.v.:<BR>with<BR>h. eyes:<BR>विदेषचक्षुषा।<BR>II Hated, odious:<BR>(1)<BR>घृणितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) घृणार्ह (f. र्हा);<BR>(3) गर्हितः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(4) निर्घृण (f. णा),<BR>where all practices<BR>are more h. than the hearts of people:<BR>लोकहृदयेभ्यो<BR> निर्घृणतरसर्वसंव्यवहारम्, K. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hatefully
HATEFULLY:<BR>I With hate:<BR>(1) सद्वेषम्;<BR>(2) द्वेष-<BR>भावेन;<BR>II Odiously:<BR>(1) घृणितम्;<BR>(2) गर्हितम्;<BR>(3) जुगुप्सितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hatefulness
HATEFULNESS:<BR>I Lit.: द्वेषिता, वि-,<BR>II Hated-<BR>-ness:<BR>(1) घृणितता;<BR>(2) गर्हितता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hatred
HATRED:<BR>(1) द्वेषः, वि-,<BR>one who does good to a<BR>king becomes the object of h. with the people<BR>नरपतिहितकर्ता द्वेष्यतां याति लोके, P. i. 3.<BR>(2) घृणा, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">Page337</a>]<BR>and expressed h. for the sound of the lute:<BR>घृणाञ्च<BR> वीणाक्वणितं वितेने, N. iii. 60.;<BR>(3) जुगुप्सा<BR>(= abhorrence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haughtily
HAUGHTILY:<BR>(1) उद्धतम्;<BR>(2) सावलेपम्;<BR>(3)<BR>साटोपम्।: v. Also proudly, insolently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haughtiness
HAUGHTINESS:<BR>(1) औद्धत्यम्;<BR>(2) अवलेपः (= arro-<BR>-gance);<BR>(3) उत्सेकः (= inflatedness);<BR>(4)<BR>मानिता, अभि-, (= pride).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haughty
HAUGHTY:<BR>(1) उद्धतः (ता, तं),<BR>struck with the<BR>h. words of the Kirāta:<BR>किरातस्य वचोभिरुद्धतैः<BR> पराहतः, Ki. xiv. i.;<BR>(2) उत्सिक्तः (क्ता, क्तं),<BR>on<BR>the one hand, from the arrival of the h. mine of<BR>penances and powers:<BR>उत्सिक्तस्य तपःपराक्रमनिधेरभ्या-<BR>गमादेकतः, Vi. ii. 22: v. Also arrogant,<BR>proud, insolent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haul
HAUL (v.): आकर्षति (कृष्, c. 1.): v. To pull.<BR>Ph.:<BR>to h. the wind:<BR>वाताभिमुखीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haul
HAUL (subs.):<BR>I A pull: q.v.<BR>II Of nets:<BR>क्षेपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haulm
HAULM: काण्डः: v. Stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haunch
HAUNCH (subs.):<BR>(1) जघनम्,<BR>I will eat the h. of<BR>the dog:<BR>भक्षयिष्ये श्वजाघनीम्, Mah. s. 141. 71.;<BR>(2) नितभ्बः;<BR>(3) उत्सङ्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haunt
HAUNT (v.): सेवते, नि-, (सेव्, c. 1.),<BR>h. ed by<BR>ghosts:<BR>भूतसेवितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haunt
HAUNT (subs.): expr. by verb: v. Also refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

have
HAVE:<BR>I To possess:<BR>(1) अस्ति (with gen.<BR>of the person h. ing: often understood),<BR>I h. no other friend like you:<BR>न त्वत्समोऽन्योऽस्ति मम<BR> सुहृद्, P. ii. 1.;<BR>I h. something more to ask:<BR>अस्ति<BR> नोऽन्यदपि प्रष्टव्यम्, Sa.;<BR>I h. no doubts as to her<BR>divinity:<BR>न हि मे संशीतिरस्य दिव्यतां प्रति, K.;<BR>(2)<BR>वर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.) or<BR>(3) विद्यते (विद्, c. 4.) (with<BR>sim. comps.: not so common), for even<BR>good (men)<BR>h. fear from the mischievous:<BR>विद्यते हि<BR> नृशंसेभ्यो भयं गुणवतामपि, H.;<BR>you h. manliness:<BR>विद्यते<BR> पौरुषं तव, K. s. 10. I.;<BR>(4) by bah.:<BR>bad men<BR>h. divine eyes to see others' faults:<BR>उसाधवः पर-<BR>दोषेक्षणदिव्यचक्षुषः, Si.; you h. no beginning, no end:<BR>त्वमनादिर्निरन्तकः, Ku.<BR>II To accept, obtain:<BR>q.v.: लभते,<BR>“wilt thou h.” him:<BR>स किं लप्स्यते,<BR>D. iii.<BR>III To be under necessity: expr.<BR>by fut. pass. part.,<BR>I h. to go there:<BR>मया तत्र<BR> गन्तव्यम्;<BR>I. h. to ask this:<BR>प्रष्टव्यमेतन्मया।<BR>IV To<BR>cause, procure: expr. by causal: v. To<BR>get. (III).<BR>H. on:<BR>दधति<BR>or<BR>धत्ते (धा, c. 3.): v.<BR>To wear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haven
HAVEN:<BR>(1) क्रोडः (?);<BR>(2) कोलः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haversack
HAVERSACK: भस्त्रा: v. Bag, sack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

having
HAVING:<BR>(1) by bah.:<BR>h. four arms:<BR>चतुर्भुजः<BR>(जा, जं);<BR>h. great wealth:<BR>बहुधनः (ना, नं);<BR>h. rags on:<BR>चिरवासस् (mfn.); affixes वत्<BR>or<BR>मत्<BR>(f. ती), इन् (f. नी), or rarely विन्<BR>or<BR>मिन्<BR>(f. नी) (v. s. k. for their use),<BR>h. good<BR>qualities:<BR>गुणवत् (f. ती);<BR>h. a hump:<BR>ककुह्मत्<BR>(f. ती);<BR>h. sons:<BR>पुत्रिन् (f. णी);<BR>h. good<BR>memory:<BR>मेधाविन् (f. नी);<BR>h. cattle:<BR>गोमिन्<BR>(f. नी): v. Also endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

havoc
HAVOC: ध्वंसः, वि-: v. Destruction, waste,<BR>slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haw
HAW;<BR>I A hedge: वृतिः।<BR>II A fruit: -फलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hawk
HAWK (subs.):<BR>I The bird: शयेनः (= falcon);<BR>शशघातकः, Bha.<BR>II A board: फलकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hawk
HAWK (v.):<BR>I To catch with h.: शयेनं मुक्त्वा<BR> पक्षिणो गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.).<BR>II To sell by h.<BR>ing: मार्गेषु घोषयन् विक्रीणीते (क्री, c. 9.).<BR>III<BR>To force up: उत्कासयति (c. of कास्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hawker
HAWKER: उद्घोषविक्रयिन् (f. णी) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hawk-eyed
HAWK-EYED: सूक्ष्मदर्शिन (f. नी): v. Keen-<BR>-sighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hawser
HAWSER: दृढवरत्रा, Mah.: v. Cable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hawthorn
HAWTHORN: a tree: हगकण्टकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hay
HAY: शुष्कतृणम्,<BR>h.-cock:<BR>तृणराशिः<BR>or<BR>-चितिः;<BR>h.-<BR>loft:<BR>तृणकोष्ठः;<BR>h.-maker:<BR>तृणशोषकः (?);<BR>h.-<BR>market:<BR>घासापणः (?);<BR>h.-rick, h.-stock:<BR>तृण-<BR>राशिः: v. Also grass, fodder. Ph.:<BR>make h.<BR>while the sun shines:.<BR>यथावसरं कार्यसिद्धिं कूरु (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hazard
HAZARD (subs.):<BR>I Danger: सङ्कटम्।<BR>II<BR>Chance: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hazard
HAZARD (v.):<BR>I To risk:<BR>(1) सङ्गटे क्षिपति (क्षिप्,<BR>c. 6.).<BR>(2) संशयस्थं (f. स्थां) करोति।<BR>II To<BR>venture: साहसं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hazardous
HAZARDOUS:<BR>I सङ्कटः (टा, टं);<BR>(2) सन्दिग्धः<BR>(ग्धा, ग्धं) (= doubtful): v. Also dangerous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hazardously
HAZARDOUSLY:<BR>(1) ससङ्कटम्;<BR>(2) ससाहसम्<BR>(= boldly);<BR>(3) ससंशयम् (=doubtfully).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

haze
HAZE:<BR>I Lit: कुज्भ्कटिका: v. Fog.<BR>II Dim-<BR>-ness: q.v.:<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hazel
HAZEL (subs.): a plant:<BR>h.-nut:<BR>*कोरलबादामः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hazel
HAZEL (adj.): कपिशः (शा, शं): v. Tawny,<BR>brown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hazy
HAZY: सधूमः (मा, मं) (= smoky: lit. and fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

he
HE:<BR>I Pron.:<BR>(1) तद् (= that),<BR>I am he:<BR>एषोऽस्मि<BR> सः, Mu. vii. 4.;<BR>here is he:<BR>अयं सः, Sa.;<BR>he<BR>also:<BR>सोऽपि, D.;<BR>(2) अदस्, which of them is he:<BR>कतमोऽसौ, D.; what he would have done to you:<BR>त्वय्यसौ यदकरिष्यत्, K.<BR>(3) इदम् (= this),<BR>is he a<BR>new-comer:<BR>किमयमागन्तुकः, Mu.;<BR>(4) एतद्,<BR>(= this: q.v.);<BR>(5) not expr. when the<BR>meaning is clear,<BR>moreover he is cruel:<BR>अपरञ्च<BR> क्रूरः, P. Ph.:<BR>things he is a Śudra:<BR>शूद्रोऽहमिति<BR> मन्यते, G. p.: v. That.<BR>II He who, he<BR>that: यद्॥॥तद्: v. Who.<BR>III A male:<BR>q.v.: expr. by m. gender:<BR>he-goat:<BR>छागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

head
HEAD (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) शिरस् (n.),<BR>the h.<BR>aches:<BR>शिरो रुजति, Sr.; with a shake of the h.:<BR>सशिरःकम्पम्, Ve.;<BR>(2) मूर्द्धन् (m.), three-h. ed:<BR>त्रिमूर्द्धन् (mfn.), Vi.;<BR>(3) मस्तकम्,<BR>I will hash<BR>your h.:<BR>मस्तकं ते कुट्टयिष्यामि, Mr.;<BR>(4) शीर्षम्,<BR>with<BR>the frightful h. s. cut off:<BR>छिन्नैः शीर्षैर्भयङ्करैः, A. r.;<BR>(5) मुण्डम् (in contempt),<BR>shaving the h.:<BR>मुण्डं<BR> मुण्डयित्वा, Mu.;<BR>(6) तुण्डम् (rare), the h. is grey:<BR>पलितं तुण्डम्, J.<BR>II Chief, leader: q.v.: अग्रणी।<BR>Ph.:<BR>the h. of the atheists:<BR>नास्तिकशिरोमणिः, Da.<BR>III Of things: अग्रम्। Ph.:<BR>at the h. of a<BR>battle:<BR>रणशिरसि, रणमूर्द्धनि, etc.; h. of a mount:<BR>गिरिमूर्द्धा;<BR>h. of a wound:<BR>व्रणमुखम्, Ki.<BR>IV<BR>Source: q.v.<BR>V A topic of discourse:<BR>विषयः।<BR>VI Intellect: q.v.:<BR>VII An indi-<BR>-vidual: q.v.:<BR>VIII Force, strength: q.v.<BR>Ph.: to come to a h. (of wounds): पाकं व्रजति;<BR>h. or tail:<BR>एष पार्श्वोऽन्यो वा (?).; neither h. nor tail:<BR>न किञ्चिदपि;<BR>to one's h.:<BR>समक्षम्; to make h.: v.<BR>To advance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

head
HEAD (adj.): only in comp.s.: मुख्यः (ख्या, ख्यं):<BR>v. Chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

head
HEAD (v.):<BR>I To lead, command: expr. by<BR>comp.s.,<BR>an army h. ed by Atikāya:<BR>अतिकायमुखं<BR> बलम्, A.r.: v. Leader.<BR>II To behead:<BR>q.v.<BR>III To go in front of: पुरः<BR>or<BR>अग्रतः<BR> गच्छति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

headache
HEADACHE:<BR>(1) शिरोवेदना, शिरःपीडा, and sim.<BR>comp.s.,<BR>violent h.:<BR>प्रबला शिरोवेदना, K.;<BR>I have<BR>got h. by looking into this picture:<BR>मभेदं चित्रं<BR> पश्यन्त्याः शीर्षवेदना समुत्पन्ना, Ra. ii.;<BR>(2) शिरःशूलम्,<BR>(rare), D.;<BR>(3) शिरोरोगः (= any disease of<BR>the head).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

headband
HEADBAND:<BR>(1) शिरोवेष्टः, -नम्;<BR>(2) शिरोबन्धनम्,<BR> -नी; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

head-dress
HEAD-DRESS: शिरोभूषणम्: v. Also veil, turban,<BR>crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

head-foremost
HEAD-FOREMOST:<BR>to fall h.:<BR>अवमूर्द्धपातं पतति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

headland
HEADLAND: perh. टङ्कः (comp. टेंक in Bengali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

headless
HEADLESS: अशिरस् (mfn.) and sim. comp.<BR>s. H.<BR>trunk:<BR>कबन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

headlong
HEADLONG (adv.): Headforemost: q.v.:<BR>अवाक्शिरस् (mfn.) and sim. comp.s. (= with<BR>the head down).<BR>II Rashly, hastily: q.v.:<BR>सहसा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

headlong
HEADLONG (adj.):<BR>I Rash, reckless: q.v.<BR>II Precipitous: अवसर्पिन् (f. णी), Mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

headman
HEADMAN:<BR>(1) मुख्यः;<BR>(2) मण्डलः (of many<BR>Indian villages).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

headquarters
HEADQUARTERS: मुख्यनिवेशः and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

headship
HEADSHIP:<BR>(1) प्राधान्यम्;<BR>(2) प्रभुत्वम् (= mastery).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

headstrong
HEADSTRONG: अग्रचित्तः (त्ता, त्तं) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

head-wind
HEAD-WIND: सभ्मुखवातः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heady
HEADY:<BR>I Rash, violent: q.v.<BR>II Of wines:<BR>उग्रः (ग्रा, ग्रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heal
HEAL (v.t.):<BR>I Lit.: v. To cure.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>मार्ष्टि<BR>or<BR>मार्जयति, प्र-, (मृज्, c. 2. and 10): v.<BR>To reconcile, clean, wash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heal
HEAL (v. i.):<BR>(1) शाम्यति, प्र-, उप-, (शम्, c. 4.)<BR>(of wounds only),<BR>wounds of aged people<BR>quickly h.:<BR>वयःस्थनामाशु व्रणा रोहन्ति, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

healer
HEALER:<BR>I Physician: q.v.<BR>II That which<BR>heals:<BR>(1) -घ्न (f. घ्नी) in comp. (= killing);<BR>(2) -हर (f. री) (= removing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

healing
HEALING (subs.):<BR>(1) शमः<BR>or<BR>शान्तिः<BR>or<BR>उपशामः;<BR>(2) प्रति(ती)कारः<BR>or<BR>प्रतिक्रिया (= remedying), for [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">Page339</a>]<BR>h. disease: प्रतीकाराय रोगाणाम्, Bha.;<BR>(3) नाशः<BR>etc. (= destruction), जनव्याधिविध्वंसनाय, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

healing
HEALING (adj.):<BR>(1) शान्तिकरः (री, रं);<BR>(2)<BR>शान्तिदः (दा, दं);<BR>(3) शीतः (ता, तं) (= cool).<BR>Ph.:<BR>the h. art:<BR>आमयानां शमोपायः, Bha.: v.<BR>Medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

health
HEALTH:<BR>(1) आरोग्यम् (best equiv.) (also<BR>अरोगिता<BR>or<BR>अरोगता),<BR>strength, h.:<BR>शक्तिरागोग्यम्,<BR>Ph.:<BR>to recover h.:<BR>आरोग्यं प्राप्नोति; to wish h.:<BR>आरोग्यमिच्छति, Kat.;<BR>(2) स्वास्थ्यम्, to keep h.:<BR>स्वास्थ्यं रक्षति, Sr.;<BR>(3) अनामयम् (rare),<BR>says this,<BR>wishing you h.:<BR>अनामयप्रश्नपूर्वकमिदमाह, Sa. v.<BR>To<BR>be in good, bad h.:<BR>सुस्थः (स्था, स्थं), अ-: v.<BR>Well, ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

healthful
HEALTHFUL:<BR>I Healthy: q.v.<BR>II Whole-<BR>-some: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

health-giving
HEALTH-GIVING: स्वास्थ्यकरः (री, रं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

healthily
HEALTHILY, HEALTHFULLY:<BR>(1) सुस्थम्;<BR>(2) निरा-<BR>मयम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

healthiness
HEALTHINESS:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) स्वास्थ्यम्;<BR>(2)<BR>अरोगिता and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Of places:<BR>expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

health-officer
HEALTH-OFFICER: स्वास्थ्याधिकृतः (?) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

healthy
HEALTHY:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) सुस्थः (स्था, स्थं);<BR>(2) अरोगः (गा, गं), निरामयः (या, यं) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (= without disease);<BR>(3) कुशलिन्<BR>(f. नी) (= well: q.v.).<BR>II Of places:<BR>(1)<BR>क्षेम्य (f. म्या), M. vii. 212.;<BR>(2) अनामयक्षमः<BR>(मा, मं), K. b. and sim. comp.s.<BR>III Of<BR>food:<BR>(1) हितः (ता, तं) (= good: q.v.):<BR>(2)<BR>पथ्य (f. थ्या), Sr.: v. Wholesome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heap
HEAP (subs.):<BR>(1) राशिः,<BR>h. s. of jewels:<BR>रत्नराशीन्,<BR>Si.;<BR>(2) चयः, नि-, सं-,<BR>h. of ashes:<BR>भस्मनां चयः,<BR>Ki.;<BR>(3) पुञ्जः;<BR>(4) पूगः;<BR>(5) स्तोमः: v. Also<BR>pile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heap
HEAP (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) राशीकरोति, पूगीकरोति,<BR>etc.;<BR>(2) चिनोति, सं-, नि-, आ-, प्र-, समा-,<BR>(चि, c. 5.): v. Also to collect.<BR>II Of<BR>favours etc.: वर्षति (वृष्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>shower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hear
HEAR:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) शृणोत्ति (श्रु, c. 5.),<BR>he h. s.<BR>without ears:<BR>शृणोत्यकर्णः, S.;<BR>we h. he will go to<BR>hermitage:<BR>तपोवनं गमिष्यतीति श्रूयते, Mu. iv.;<BR>I<BR>will h. their confidential talk:<BR>शृणोमि विश्वस्त-<BR>कथितान्यासाम्, Sa. iii.;<BR>(2) आकर्णयति, सम्-, (कर्ण,<BR>c. 10.) (= perceive by the ear),<BR>h. ing the<BR>noise of geese:<BR>हंसनादानाकर्णयन्, B. ii. 7;<BR>(3)<BR>निशामयति (शम्, c. 10.) (rare),<BR>h. ing of the<BR>succes of enemies:<BR>निशम्य सिद्धिं द्विषताम्, Ki. i. 27.<BR>II To listen to: शृणोति, [princes]<BR>h. him<BR>who flatters day and night:<BR>तस्य वचनं शृण्वन्ति<BR> योऽहर्निशं स्तौति, K.;<BR>a king after rising is to h.<BR>about all receipts and disbursements:<BR>उत्थितेन राज्ञा<BR> कृत्स्नमायव्ययजातं श्रोतव्यम्, D. viii.<BR>III In law:<BR>पश्यति (दृश्, c. 1.) (= to see),<BR>he personally h. d<BR>complaints:<BR>स स्वयं व्यवहारान् ददर्श, R. xvii. 39.<BR>IV To receive letters:<BR>I have not h. d from<BR>him for a long time:<BR>*बहोः कालात् तस्य पत्राणि न<BR> मयाधिगतानि; distressed at not h. ing (of him)<BR>for good many days:<BR>बहुदिवसापगमे च वार्तया<BR> विनोत्ताम्यन्ती, K. ii.: v. Also to learn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hearer
HEARER<BR>(1) श्रोतृ (f. त्री), you will get a h.:<BR>लप्स्यसे श्रोतारम्, Mu. l.;<BR>(2) श्रावक (f. विका),<BR>all those h. s:<BR>सर्वानेव तान् श्रावकान्, K.;<BR>(3)<BR>शृण्वत् (f. ती) (= actually hearing),<BR>to draw<BR>the hearts of the h. s:<BR>शृण्वतां मनो हर्तुम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hearing
HEARING (subs.):<BR>I The act: श्रवणम्,<BR>from<BR>first h.:<BR>प्रथमश्रवाणात्, M. n.: v. To hear.<BR>II The<BR>faculty;<BR>(1) श्रवणशक्तिः;<BR>(2) श्रुतिः।<BR>III An<BR>audience: q.v.: दर्शनम्।<BR>IV Judicial: दर्शनम्,<BR>of not h. or of h. improperly:<BR>अदर्शनान्यथादर्शनयोः,<BR>Mit.<BR>V Reach of the ear.: श्रवणविषयः। Ph.:<BR>within h.:<BR>श्रवणगोचरः (रा, रं);<BR>out of h.:<BR>असंश्रवः<BR>(वा, वं); going beyond the h. of a cow's lowing:<BR>गोरुतान्तरमतिक्रम्य, D.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hearken
HEARKEN: आकर्णयति (कर्ण्, c. 10.): v. Listen,<BR>hear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hearsay
HEARSAY: जनश्रुतिः: v. Rumour, Ph.:<BR>h. evi-<BR>dence:<BR>श्रुतसाक्ष्यम् (?), Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hearse
HEARSE:<BR>(1) शवयानम्;<BR>(2) प्रेतशकटम्, Say.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heart
HEART:<BR>I Lit.: हृदयम्<BR>or<BR>हृद् (n.),<BR>has any body<BR>two h. s:<BR>किं कस्यचिद्धृदयद्वयं भवति,। P. iv. 1.<BR>II<BR>Fig.:<BR>(1) हृदयम्,<BR>touching the h.:<BR>हृदयग्राहिन् (f. णी),<BR>Ki.;<BR>(2) चेतः,<BR>the unsteady h. runs behind:<BR>धावति [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">Page340</a>]<BR> पश्चादसंस्थितं चेतः, Sa.;<BR>(3) मनस्। (n.), even at h.:<BR>मनसापि, R.: v. Mind.<BR>III The interior of<BR>anything: उदरम्,<BR>the h. of the city:<BR>पुरोदरम्, B.<BR>xiv. 10.<BR>IV Courage, spirit: q.v.: सत्त्वभ्,<BR>Ph.:<BR>take h.:<BR>प्रफुल्लमना भव।<BR>V Real intention:<BR>अभिप्रायः, Ph.:<BR>to get by h.:<BR>कण्ठस्थं (f. स्थां)<BR>करोति;<BR>to have in h.:<BR>हृदये करोति;<BR>he has set his<BR>whole h. on it:<BR>स सर्वात्मनैवास्मिन्निमग्नः;<BR>he took it<BR>to h.:<BR>*इदं तस्य हृदयं पस्पर्श<BR>or<BR>मनो खेदयामास;<BR>I<BR>“find in the h.” that he is a friend:<BR>*स मित्रमिति<BR> हृदयं मां कथयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heartache
HEARTACHE: मनस्तापः, हृदयसन्तापः, and sim.<BR>comp.s.,<BR>yet his advancement gives wicked men<BR>h.:<BR>तथापि तदुन्नतिरसतां हृद्रोगकरी, Si. xvi. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heart-breaking
HEART-BREAKING: हृदयभेदिन् (f. नी): v. Heart-<BR>-rending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heart-broken
HEART-BROKEN:<BR>(1) मग्नहृदयः (या, यं);<BR>(2)<BR>भग्नमानसः (सा, सं), Mah.; and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heartburn
HEARTBURN:<BR>(1) हृदयज्वाला;<BR>(2) हृद्दाहः;<BR>(3) मनःसन्तापः (?), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heartburning
HEARTBURNING:<BR>I Subs: v. Heartburn.<BR>II Adj.: सन्तापकरः (री, रं) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heart-felt
HEART-FELT: हृदयङ्गमः (मा, मं): v. Sincere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heart-pea
HEART-PEA:<BR>(1) ज्योतिष्मती;<BR>(2) पारावतांघ्री;<BR>(3) पारावतपदी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heart-rending
HEART-RENDING:<BR>(1) हृदयविदारणः (णा, णं),<BR>Mu.;<BR>(2) हृदयच्छिद्। (mfn), Ram.;<BR>(3) हृदय-<BR>मर्मच्छिद् (mfn.), U.; and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heart-whole
HEART-WHOLE: अक्षतहृदयः (या, यं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hearten
HEARTEN: आश्वासयति (c. of श्वस्): v. To cheer,<BR>encourage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hearth
HEARTH:<BR>(1) अग्निकुण्डम्;<BR>(2) चुल्लिः (ल्ली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heartily
HEARTILY:<BR>I Freely, at pleasure:<BR>(1) कामम्,<BR> प्र-, नि-;<BR>(2) यथेच्छम्।<BR>II Vigorously: प्रयत्नेन।<BR>III<BR>Sincerely: q.v.<BR>IV Cordially: स्नेहनिर्भरम्<BR>(= affectionately), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heartiness
HEARTINESS: मनोयोगः: v. Zeal, devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heartless
HEARTLESS: निर्हृदयः (या, यं): v. Hard-<BR>-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heartlessly
HEARTLESSLY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heartlessness
HEARTLESSNESS: निर्हृदयताः v. Hard-hearted-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hearts ease
HEART'S EASE: a plant: ओषधिभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hearty
HEARTY:<BR>I Sincere: q.v.: अकृत्रिमः (मा, मं).<BR>II Cordial:<BR>(1) हृद्य (f. द्या);<BR>(2) स्नेहनिर्भरः।<BR>(रा, रं) (= affectionate).<BR>III Rich, abun-<BR>-dant: q.v.: by adv.,<BR>h. sleep.:<BR>प्रकामशयितव्यम्,<BR>Sa.<BR>IV Sound, firm: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heat
HEAT (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) तपः, उत्-, सं-, अभि-,<BR> परि-, प्र-,<BR>able to remove h.:<BR>तापापनोदक्षमः (मा, मं),<BR>R.;<BR>from the h. of the sun:<BR>दिनकरपरितापात्,<BR>Ri.; the breeze cooled the h. of the ladies:<BR>कान्तानां सन्तापं विरमयति स्म मातरिश्वा, Ki.;<BR>(2)<BR>उष्णः (ष्मः),<BR>do not care for cold or h.:<BR>गणयन्ति<BR> न शीतोष्णम्, Mr.;<BR>overpowered with h.:<BR>उष्णालु<BR>(mfn.), V.;<BR>(3) ग्रीष्मः,<BR>pleasing in h.:<BR>ग्रीष्मसुखः<BR>(खा, खं), R.;<BR>(4) घर्मः,<BR>eruptions from h.:<BR>घर्म-<BR>विचर्चिका;<BR>(5) निदाघः (rare), the mine of h.<BR>(sun): निदाघधामन् (m.), Si.<BR>II Fig.,<BR>vehemence, excitement: उत्तापः।<BR>III A<BR>course: चर्या।<BR>IV As of youth.: मदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heat
HEAT (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: तापयति<BR>or<BR>तपति, सं-, उत्-,<BR> प्र-, अभि-, परि-, (तप्, c. 10. and 1.),<BR>the earth<BR>is h. ed with the rays of the sun:<BR>सूर्यातपतापिता मही,<BR>Ri.;<BR>the h. ed water:<BR>तप्तं वारि, V.<BR>II. Fig.:<BR>उत्तपति<BR>or<BR>-तापयति: v. To inflame, excite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heated
HEATED: of animals: मत्तः (त्ता, त्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heath
HEATH:<BR>I A plant: *हीरकः।<BR>II A desert: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heathcock
HEATHCOCK: a bird: काष्ठकुक्कुटः। (?), Mat.<BR>117. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heathen
HEATHEN (subs.): म्लेच्छः (used by Hindus to<BR>other nations).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heathen
HEATHEN (adj.): म्लेच्छ- in comp., h. nations:<BR>म्लेच्छजातयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heathenish
HEATHENISH:<BR>I Heathen: q.v.<BR>II Cruel,<BR>savage: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heathenism
HEATHENISM: म्लेच्छव्यवहारः: v. Also idolatry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heathy
HEATHY: *हीरकाच्छन्नः (न्ना, न्नं); जाङ्गलः (ला, लं)<BR>(= jungly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heating
HEATING (adj.): i.e. stimulating: दीपनः (नी, नं),<BR>Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heave
HEAVE (v. t.):<BR>I To raise: q.v.: उन्नमयति<BR>(c. of नम्).<BR>II To cast: q.v.: क्षिपति (क्षिप्,<BR>c. 6.). H. up: (a)<BR>to vomit:<BR>उद्गिरति (गॄ, c. 6.);<BR>(b)<BR>to raise:<BR>उत्तोलयति (तुल्, c. 10.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heave
HEAVE (v. i.):<BR>I To go up: उन्नमति (नम्, c. 1.)<BR>II To palpitate: स्पन्दते (स्पन्द्, c. 1.).<BR>III<BR>To pant: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heaven
HEAVEN:<BR>I The sky: q.v.: द्यौः।<BR>II The<BR>blessed region:<BR>(1) स्वर्गः (best equiv.),<BR>as if<BR>from hell to h.:<BR>नरकादिव स्वर्गम्, D.;<BR>(2) द्यौः,<BR>if you<BR>seek h.:<BR>दिवं यदि प्रार्थयसे, Ku.; the road to h.:<BR>दिवंगमो मार्गः, Mah.;<BR>(3) त्रिदिव (mn.),<BR>a ladder<BR>to h.:<BR>त्रिदिवनिःश्रेणिः, R.;<BR>(4) स्वर् in comp.s.,<BR>the master of h.:<BR>स्वर्पतिः, N.;<BR>(5) नाकः, N.;<BR>(6)<BR>वैकुण्ठम् (= h. of Viṣṇu).<BR>III God: q.v.:<BR>bestowed by h.:<BR>देवदत्तः (त्ता, त्तं), Ma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heaven-born
HEAVEN-BORN: दिविजः (जा, जं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heavenly
HEAVENLY:<BR>(1) स्वर्गीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) दिव्यः (व्या,<BR> व्यं);<BR>(3) अपार्थिवः (वा, वं), with h. flowers:<BR>कुसुमैरपार्थिवैः, R.;<BR>h. body:<BR>नक्षत्रम्: v. Star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heavenwards
HEAVENWARDS:<BR>(1) स्वर्गाभिमुखम्;<BR>(2) दिवं प्रति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heavily
HEAVILY:<BR>I Lit.: गुरु;<BR>(2) by adj.<BR>II<BR>Slowly: q.v.: मन्दं मन्दम्।<BR>III.: sorrowfully:<BR>q.v.: खिन्नः (न्ना, न्नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heaviness
HEAVINESS:<BR>I Weight: गुरुत्वभ्, -ता।<BR>II Sadness:<BR>विषादः।<BR>III Sluggishness: मान्द्यम्।<BR>IV Oppres-<BR>-sion: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heavy
HEAVY:<BR>I In gen.: गुरु (f. र्वी),<BR>h. clothes:<BR>गुरूणि<BR> वासांसि, Ri.;<BR>the h. er falls quicker:<BR>गुरुतरं शीघ्रं<BR> पतति, Go.;<BR>very h. clouds:<BR>गुरुतरा घनाः, Ku.<BR>xiv. 50.;<BR>Sitā h. with child:<BR>गर्भगुर्वी सीता, Sah.;<BR>beef is h.:<BR>गोमासं गुरु, Bha.<BR>II Of rain, snow,<BR>etc.: महत् (f. ती),<BR>h. rain:<BR>महती वृष्टिः, A.<BR>III<BR>Sad, oppressed: q.v.: स्तिमितः (ता, तं),<BR>h.<BR>with care:<BR>चिन्तास्तिमितः (ता, तं) K.<BR>IV Slow:<BR>q.v.: मन्दः (न्दा, न्दं). Ph.:<BR>h. price:<BR>गुरुमूल्यम्<BR>(D. has लघीयसा मूल्येन); h. (sea): ऊर्मिसभाकुलः<BR>(ला, लं): v. Ruffled;<BR>h. sigh:<BR>दीर्घनिःश्वासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heavy-headed
HEAVY-HEADED:<BR>(1) स्थूलबुद्धि (mfn.);<BR>(2) मन्दधी<BR>(n. धि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

headomadal
HEADOMADAL: साप्ताहिकः (की, कं): v. Weekly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hebraiism
HEBRAIISM: *हिब्रुभाषानुसारिणी वाकपद्धतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hebraist
HEBRAIST: *हिब्रुभाषाज्ञः (ज्ञा, ज्ञं), -विशारदः (दा, दं),<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hebrew
HEBREW:<BR>I A jew: q.v.: *हिब्रुः<BR>II The<BR>language: हिब्रुभाषा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hecatomb
HECATOMB:<BR>I Lit.: *शतगोमेधः।<BR>II Victim:<BR>q.v.: बलिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hectic
HECTIC: v. Habitual.<BR>H. fever:<BR>तापज्वरः। (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hector
HECTOR (v.):<BR>I To boast: q.v.<BR>II To<BR>vex: बाधते (बाध्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hector
HECTOR (subs.): पिण्डीशूरः (?): v. Bully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hedge
HEDGE (subs.): कण्टकवृतिः: v. Fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hedge
HEDGE (v.): आ-वृणोति (वृ, c. 5.): v. To<BR>fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hedgehog
HEDGEHOG: शस्यमूषिकः; Perh. शस्यकः,<BR> “श्वाविच्छस्यक-”, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hedge-sparrow
HEDGE-SPARROW: कलविङ्कः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heed
HEED (subs.):<BR>(1) अवधानम्;<BR>(2) सावधानताः v.<BR>Care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heed
HEED (v.): गणयति (गण्, c. 10.): v. To care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heedful
HEEDFUL: अप्रमत्तः (त्ता, त्तं): v. Careful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heedless
HEEDLESS: प्रमत्तः (त्ता, त्तं): v. Careless, rash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heedlessly
HEEDLESSLY: प्रमत्तम्: v. Carelessly, rashly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heedlessness
HEEDLESSNESS: प्रमत्तताः v. Carelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heel
HEEL (subs.): पार्ष्णिः,<BR>to be at one's h. s.:<BR>पार्ष्णि<BR> गृह्लाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.).<BR>H. of a shoe:<BR>तलम् (?).<BR>To<BR>show or take to the h. s.:<BR>पलायते: v. To flee.<BR>Neck and h. s.:<BR>आपादमस्तकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heel
HEEL (v.): Of ships; to incline: expr. by<BR>वर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heel
HEEL:<BR>I Effort: q.v.: यत्नः।<BR>II Handle:<BR>मुष्टिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hegira
HEGIRA:<BR>I Lit.: महम्मदीयशकः।<BR>II Flight,<BR>departure: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heifer
HEIFER: वत्सतरः (f. री), U. (H) two years old:<BR>द्विहायनी, A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heigh-ho
HEIGH-HO: हंहो: v. O.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

height
HEIGHT (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) उच्छायः (or<BR>rarely उच्छ्रितिः),<BR>of great h.:<BR>महोच्छ्रायः (या, यं);<BR>and whose h. is three cubits:<BR>त्रिकरोच्छ्रितिश्च, Li.;<BR>(2) उत्सेधः, M. n.;<BR>(3) उच्चता<BR>or rarely<BR>औच्च्यम्,<BR>Li.;<BR>(4) तुङ्गता।: v. Also loftiness, tallness.<BR>II<BR>Fig.: expr. by the above words: v. Lofti-<BR>-ness.<BR>III An elevated place:<BR>(1) उच्चस्थली;<BR>(2) उन्नतभूमागः; etc.: v. Also summit.<BR>IV<BR>Utmost degree: expr. by adj.:<BR>in the h. of<BR>fever:<BR>प्रबले ज्वरे;<BR>the h. of wisdom:<BR>परमं ज्ञानम्: v.<BR>Extreme, acme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heighten
HEIGHTEN (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) उच्चीकरोति, etc.;<BR>(2) by adj.: v. High.<BR>II To increase:<BR>q.v.: वर्धयति (c. of वृध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heinous
HEINOUS:<BR>(1) घोरः (रा, रं),<BR>h. sin:<BR>घोरपातकभ्;<BR>(2) दारुणः (णा, णं),<BR>on account of committing a<BR>h. offence:<BR>दारुणापराधित्वेन, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heinously
HEINOUSLY:<BR>(1) घोरम्;<BR>(2) दारुणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heinousness
HEINOUSNESS:<BR>(1) घोरता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2) दारुणता, -त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heir
HEIR, HEIRESS:<BR>(1) उत्तरधिकारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2)<BR>ऋक्थिन् (f. नी)<BR>or<BR>ऋक्थहरः (री, रं),<BR>sons are<BR>father's h. s:<BR>पुत्रा ऋक्थहराः पितुः, M. ix. 185.;<BR>(3)<BR>दायादः (दा, दं) (applied also to all relatives);<BR>(4) धनाधिकारिन् (f. णी), धनमाज् (mfn.), etc.,<BR>sole h.:<BR>समग्रधनभाक्;<BR>h. to one half:<BR>अर्द्धहरः, Da.:<BR>v. Also sharer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heir-apparent
HEIR-APPARENT: राज्यभाज् (mfn.),<BR>h. to the<BR>crown of England:<BR>इंलण्डराज्यभाक्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heirless
HEIRLESS:<BR>(1) अदायकः (का, कं), Devala;<BR>(2)<BR>दायादशून्यः (न्या, न्यं), Viv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heirloom
HEIRLOOM: expr. by कुलक्रमागतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heirship
HEIRSHIP:<BR>(1) उत्तराधिकारित्वम्, -ता;<BR>(2) धनाधि-<BR>कारित्वम्, ता,<BR>Sole h. to mother's property:<BR>सकल-<BR>मातृधनाधिकारित्वम्, Da.; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hell
HELL:<BR>(1) नरकः,<BR>resident of the h.:<BR>नरकवासिन्, K.;<BR>(2) निरयः,<BR>leading to h.:<BR>निरयफलः (ला, लं),<BR>D. ii.;<BR>(6) पातालम्,<BR>the heart of h.:<BR>पातालोदरम्,<BR>U. v. 14.;<BR>(4) रसातलम्,<BR>let caste go to h.:<BR>जातिर्यातु<BR> रसातलम्, J. N. B. (1),<BR>(2) = place of punish-<BR>-ment; (3), (4)=lower world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hellebore
HELLEBORE: औषधीयवृक्षविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hellenic
HELLENIC: *ऐलेनीयः (या, यं); अग्रिक- (Gre-<BR>-cian) in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hellenism
HELLENISM: *ऐलेनरीतिः,<BR>this is a h.:<BR>*इद्रमैलेन-<BR>भाषानुवर्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hellenist
HELLENIST: *ऐलेनवादिन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hellhound
HELLHOUND:<BR>I Lit.: नरकश्वन् (m.) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR>II Fig.: आक्रोशकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hellism
HELLISM: नारकः (की, कं): v. Infernal, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

helm
HELM:<BR>I Of a vessel:<BR>(1) अरित्रम् (= properly<BR>rudder: q.v.);<BR>(2) केनिपातः;<BR>(3) कर्णः,<BR>one<BR>who holds the h.:<BR>कर्णधारः, H.<BR>II H. -et: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

helmet
HELMET:<BR>(1) शिरस्त्रम्<BR>or<BR>शिरस्त्राणम्;<BR>(2) शिरस्कम्;<BR>(3) शीर्षण्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

helot
HELOT: दासः (= slave: may be used lit. and<BR>fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

help
HELP (subs.): साहाप्यम्: v. Assistance. H. h.:<BR>त्राहि, त्राहि, V. p.<BR>or<BR>परित्रायस्व, परित्रायस्व, Sa. vi.;<BR>there is no h. for it:<BR>अस्य प्रतिक्रिया नास्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

help
HELP (v.):<BR>I To assist: साहाय्यं (कं) करोति,<BR>I<BR>will h. you:<BR>साहाय्यं वः करिष्यामि,<BR>V p. v. 11. 5.;<BR>the spring will of course h. you:<BR>मधुस्ते सहाय एव,<BR>Ku. iii. 21. Ph.: ‘so h. me God’ (in oaths):<BR>perh. प्रसीद भगवन्।<BR>II To avoid, prevent: q.v.:<BR>I cant's h. saying:<BR>मयावश्य वक्तव्यम्: v. Must;<BR>what<BR>can I h.:<BR>किं करोमि, K.; this evil cannot be h. ed<BR>(lit. has no remedy): निष्प्रतीकारेयमापत्, K.<BR>III<BR>At table: परिवेषयति (विष्, c. 10.) (= to<BR>serve); perh. ददाति (दा, c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

helper
HELPER:<BR>(1) सहायः;<BR>(2) साहाय्यकारिन् (m.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

helpful
HELPFUL: उपयोगिन् (f. नी): v. Useful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

helping
HELPING (adj.):<BR>to lend a h. hand:<BR>साहाय्याय हस्तं<BR> ददाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

helpless
HELPLESS:<BR>I Needing help:<BR>(1) निराश्रयः (या,<BR> यं);<BR>(2) अनाथः (था, थं);<BR>(3) अगतिकः (का,<BR> कं).<BR>II Beyond help: अप्रतिकार्य (f. र्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

helplessly
HELPLESSLY: expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

helplessness
HELPLESSNESS:<BR>(1) निराश्रयता;<BR>(2) अनाथता; etc.:<BR>v. Helpless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

helpmate
HELPMATE, HELPMEET:<BR>(1) सहधर्मिणी;<BR>(2)<BR>सहधर्मचारिणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

helter-skelter
HELTER-SKELTER: यथा तथा: v. Also rashly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hem
HEM (subs.): दशा: v. Border, margin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hem
HEM (v.):<BR>I To sew the border: दशां सीव्यति<BR>(सिब्, c. 4.).<BR>II To h. in: निरुणद्धि (रुध्,<BR>c. 7.): v. To confine.<BR>III In speaking:<BR>उत्कासते (कास्, c. 1.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hem
HEM (interj.): हुं, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hemiplegia
HEMIPLEGIA:<BR>(1) पक्षाघातः;<BR>(2) पक्षवधः;<BR>(3)<BR>अर्द्धाङ्गवातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hemisphere
HEMISPHERE:<BR>(1) अर्द्धगोलः, -कः;<BR>(2) कपालः, Su.<BR>v. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hemispherical
HEMISPHERICAL: अर्द्धगोलाकारः (रा, रं), and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hemistich
HEMISTICH:<BR>(1) अर्द्धश्लोकः;<BR>(2) श्लोकार्द्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hemlock
HEMLOCK: prob. शक्तुकः, Bha.; विषभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hemorrhage
HEMORRHAGE: रक्तस्रावः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hemorrhoids
HEMORRHOIDS अर्शस् (n.): v. Piles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hemp
HEMP:<BR>I The plant. शणः; शणपुष्पी (another<BR>variety).<BR>II The rind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hempen
HEMPEN: शाण (f. णी),<BR>H. cord:<BR>शणसूत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hen
HEN: 1. In gen.: कुक्कुटी।<BR>II =she, female:<BR>q.v.: -वधूः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

henbane
HENBANE: विषभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hence
HENCE (interj.): अपेहिः v. Away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hence
HENCE:<BR>I Of place: इतः,<BR>will go from h.:<BR>इतो<BR> गमिष्यामि, Ku.<BR>II Of time इतः<BR>or<BR>अतः,<BR>five<BR>days h.:<BR>इतः पञ्चदिनानाभपगमे;<BR>a year h.:<BR>अद्य प्रभृति<BR> संवत्सरेण (lit. in a year from today), Mah.<BR>III Of reason: अतः, h. relatives wish a woman<BR>(to be)<BR>near her husband:<BR>अतः समीपे परिणेतुरिष्यते॥।<BR> प्रमदा स्वबन्धुमिः, Sa. v.<BR>IV Of source: अतः or<BR>इतः,<BR>the demon h. receiving his fortune:<BR>इतः स<BR> दैत्यः प्राप्तश्रीः, Ku. ii. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

henceforth
HENCEFORTH, HENCEFORWARD:<BR>(1) इतः परम्;<BR>(2) अतः परम्;<BR>(3) अद्य प्रभृति (= from now).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hen-coop
HEN-COOP: कुक्कुटपालिका (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hendecasyllabic
HENDECASYLLABIC: एकादशाक्षरः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

henpecked
HENPECKED:<BR>(1) स्त्रीवश्य (f. श्या),<BR>you are also<BR>h. like Nanda and Vararuchi:<BR>त्वमपि नन्दवररुचिवत्<BR> स्त्रीवश्यः, P. iv. 7.;<BR>(2) स्त्रीजितः (ता, तं);<BR>(3)<BR>स्त्रीविधेयः (या, यं), Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hen-roost
HEN-ROOST: कुक्कुटनिलयः (?) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hepatic
HEPATIC: यकृत्- in comp.: v. Liver, belong-<BR>-ing to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heptagon
HEPTAGON: सप्तभुजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hlptagonal
HLPTAGONAL:<BR>(1) सप्तभुजः (जा, जं);<BR>(2) सप्तास्र<BR>(f. स्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heptarchy
HEPTARCHY: *सप्तशासनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

her
HER: v. She, his, he.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

herald
HERALD (subs.):<BR>(1) कञ्चुकिन् (= royal h.),<BR>Mu. iv.;<BR>(2) घोषकः, (= proclaimer).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

herald
HERALD (v.): घोषयति (घुष्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>announce, proclaim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heraldic
HERALDIC:<BR>h. distinctions:<BR>*कुलचिह्नानि;<BR>h. deline-<BR>ation:<BR>*कृलचिह्नरचना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heraldry
HERALDRY: *कृलचिह्नविद्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

herb
HERB:<BR>(1) ओषधिः;<BR>(2) शाकम् (= vegetable).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

herbaceous
HERBACEOUS: expr. by comp.s. or gen.,<BR>h.<BR>plant:<BR>ओषधिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

herbage
HERBAGE:<BR>I Grass: q.v.: grazed tender h.<BR>नवशस्यं चेरुः, V. p.<BR>II In law: चारणाधिकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

herbal
HERBAL: ओषधीनां विज्ञानम्, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

herbalist
HERBALIST: ओषधिज्ञः (ज्ञा, ज्ञं) (?);<BR>(2) ओषधि<BR> विज्ञानविद् (mfn.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

herbarium
HERBARIUM: *ओषधिशाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

herbivourous
HERBIVOUROUS: शाकजम्भ (f. म्भा): v. Gramini-<BR>-vorous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

herd
HERD (subs.):<BR>I Flock: q.v.:<BR>(1) यूथम्;<BR>(2)<BR>वृन्दम्;<BR>(3) कदम्बकम्।<BR>II Crowd: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

herd
HERD (v.): यूथेन<BR>or<BR>सङ्घशः चरति, सं-, (चर्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

herdsman
HERDSMAN: रक्षकः: v. Cowherd, shepherd,<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

here
HERE:<BR>I In this place:<BR>(1) अत्र,<BR>(2) इह। Ph.:<BR>who is h.:<BR>कः कोऽत्र भोः। Sa.; look h. is the queen:<BR>पश्येयं देवी, Ra.;<BR>h. are we:<BR>इभे स्मः, Sa.<BR>II In<BR>this world:<BR>(1) इह;<BR>(2) इहलोके। Ph.:<BR>h.<BR>and hereafter:<BR>उभयत्र, Ki.<BR>or<BR>परत्रोह च, R.<BR>or<BR>इहा-<BR>मुत्र च, S. p. H.....there:<BR>(1) इतः॥॥॥।इतः,<BR>h.<BR>a flock of deer, there a herd of wild elephants:<BR>इतो मृगकदम्बकं, इतो वनगज्यूथम्, K.;<BR>(2) क्वचित्॥।<BR> क्वचित्, R. H. and there:<BR>(1) इतस्ततः, sang h.:<BR>इतस्ततो जगतुः, R.;<BR>(2) अन्तरान्तरा (at intervals),<BR>K.;<BR>(3) क्वचित् क्वचित्, N. (= 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hereabout
HEREABOUT,-S:<BR>(1) इतो नातिदूरे;<BR>(2) अत्रोपान्ते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hereafter
HEREAFTER:<BR>I Of time: अतः<BR>or<BR>इतः परम्<BR>or<BR>ऊर्द्ध्वम्।<BR>II By and by:<BR>(1) अग्रे, Go.;<BR>(2) ऊर्द्ध्वम, S.;<BR>(3) उपरिष्टात्, P. d.<BR>III In the next world:<BR>(1) परत्र;<BR>(2) अमुत्र।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hereafter
HEREAFTER (subs.):<BR>(1) परकालः;<BR>(2) by परलोकः<BR>(= next world).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hereat
HEREAT:<BR>(1) अत्र;<BR>(2) इह: v. Also hereupon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hereby
HEREBY: अनेन; अनेन योगेन। (with this acce-<BR>-ssion), Ki.; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hereditament
HEREDITAMENT:<BR>(1) ऋक्थम्;<BR>(2) दायः: v.<BR>Property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hereditarily
HEREDITARILY:<BR>(1) वंशक्रमेण;<BR>(2) कृलक्रमेण;<BR>(3) पितृपितामहक्रमेण; K. b.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hereditary
HEREDITARY:<BR>(1) कुलक्रमागतः (ता, तं),<BR>h. minis-<BR>ter:<BR>कुलक्रमागतः सचिवः, P.<BR>(2) पितृपैतामहः (ही, हं),<BR>h. kingdom:<BR>पितृपैतामहं राज्यम्, Ram. ii. 50. 8.<BR>(3) मौलः (ली, लं), M. vii. 54.;<BR>(4) मूलागतः<BR>(ता, तं), M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

herein
HEREIN:<BR>(1) अत्र, Vi.;<BR>(2) इह, Mu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heresiarch
HERESIARCH: पाषण्डशिरोमणिः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heresy
HERESY: पाषण्डमार्गः, and sim. comp.s.,<BR>my<BR>conversion to h.:<BR>मम पाषण्डपथावतारः, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heretic
HERETIC: पाषण्डः,<BR>unprecedented h.:<BR>अपूर्वपाषण्डः,<BR>Vi. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heretical
HERETICAL: expr. by comp.: v. Also false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heretically
HERETICALLY:<BR>(1) पाषण्डबुद्धि (mfn.):<BR>(2) by<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heretofore
HERETOFORE:<BR>(1) अद्यावधि (= up to now);<BR>(2) इतः पूर्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hereupon
HEREUPON: ततः (= then), B vii. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

herewith
HEREWITH: expr. by ins. of this, अनेन, एतेन,<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heriot
HERIOT: ऋक्थभोगशुल्कः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heritage
HERITAGE:<BR>I Lit.: v. Inheritance.<BR>II<BR>Fig.: भोगः (= enjoyment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hermaphrodite
HERMAPHRODITE: अर्द्धनारीनरः (after अर्द्धनारीशः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hermeneutics
HERMENEUTICS: *बाइबलव्याख्यानम्, -विवृतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hermetic
HERMETIC: v. Chemical. H. Philosophy:<BR>*त्रिभूतदर्शनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hermetically
HERMETICALLY: निरुद्धवातप्रवेशम् (?); by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hermit
HERMIT:<BR>(1) तापसः (f. सी);<BR>(2) तपस्विन् (f.<BR>नी);<BR>(3) यतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hermitage
HERMITAGE: आश्रमः,<BR>H. of Kanva:<BR>कण्वस्याश्रमः,<BR>Sa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hern
HERN: बकः: v. Heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hernla
HERNLA:<BR>(1) अन्त्रवृद्धिः (inguinal h.);<BR>(2) नाभि-<BR>वर्धनम् (umbilical h.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hero
HERO:<BR>I Lit.: वीरः,<BR>mother of a h.:<BR>वीरसूः, R.;<BR>to whom even the son of Bhrigu (fāmadagnya)<BR>is not a h.:<BR>यस्य भृगुनन्दनोऽपि न वीरः, U. v. 34.<BR>II Of a play: नायकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heroic
HEROIC, -AL:<BR>I Lit.: by comp., h. age:<BR>*वीरयुगम्।<BR>II Epic: q.v.<BR>III Bold, brave:<BR>q.v.:<BR>h. action:<BR>वीरत्वम्;<BR>h. enterprise:<BR>वीरचरितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heroically
HEROICALLY: वीरवत्: v. Bravely, boldly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heroine
HEROINE:<BR>I Lit.: वीराङ्गना, and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Of a play: नायिका, Sah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heroism
HEROISM: वीरत्वम्: v. Bravery, courage, valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heron
HERON:<BR>(1) बकः;<BR>(2) बलाका (a smaller variety).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

herring
HERRING: मत्स्यविशेषः; हेरङ्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hers
HERS: तदीयः (या, यं) or by gen.: v. He.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

herself
HERSELF:<BR>I As nom.: स्वयम्: v. Self.<BR>II<BR>As acc.: आत्मानम्।<BR>III Sane: स्वस्थ (f. स्था)<BR>Ph.:<BR>by h.:<BR>एकाकिनीः v. Alone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hesitancy
HESITANCY: विचिकित्साः v. Hesitation, doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hesitate
HESITATE:<BR>I To be in suspense:<BR>(1) विचि-<BR>कित्सते (चिकित्सा, c. 1.),<BR>my mind h. s to kill<BR>this woman:<BR>वनितामेनां हन्तुं मनो विचिकित्सते, An.<BR>ii. 62.;<BR>(2) दोलायते: v. To vacillate: v.<BR>Also to doubt.<BR>II To stammer, falter:<BR>q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hesitatingly
HESITATINGLY:<BR>(1) दोलायितमनसा;<BR>(2) संशय्य<BR>(= doubtingly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hesitation
HESITATION:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) विचिकित्सा;<BR>(2)<BR>विकल्पः: v. Doubt.<BR>II In speaking: स्खलित<BR>(mfn.): v. To falter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hesperian
HESPERIAN: पाश्चात्यः (त्या, त्यं): v. Western.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hest
HEST: शासनम्: v. Command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heteroclite
HETEROCLITE: *उद्दामरूपः (पा, पं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heterodox
HETERODOX: *भिन्नमतः (ता, तं), h. opinion:<BR>धर्मविरुद्धं मतम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heterodoxy
HETERODOXY: *भिन्नमतम्; धर्मविरुद्धताः v. Also<BR>heresy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heterogeneal
HETEROGENEAL, HETEROGENEOUS:<BR>(1) भिन्नः<BR>(न्ना, न्नं) (= different);<BR>(2) पृथग्विघः (धा, धं)<BR>(= various).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hew
HEW: छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7.): v. To cut. H. out:<BR>कृन्तति: v. To form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hewer
HEWER: छेदक (f. दिका): v. Cutter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hexagon
HEXAGON:<BR>(1) षड्भुजः;<BR>(2) षडस्रः;<BR>(3) षट्कोणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hexagonal
HEXAGONAL:<BR>(1) षड्भुजः (जा, जं);<BR>(2) षट्कोण<BR>(f. णा), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hexameter
HEXAMETER: पाश्चात्यं षट्पदवृत्तम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hey
HEY: ही ही, V. v.: v. O.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

heyday
HEYDAY: उल्लासः।<BR>H. of youth:<BR>प्रौढयौवनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hiatus
HIATUS:<BR>I Lit.: विच्छेदः।<BR>II In gram.:<BR>सन्धिभङ्गः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hibernal
HIBERNAL:<BR>(1) हैमन्त (f. न्ती);<BR>(2) हैमन (f.<BR>नी);<BR>(3) हैमन्तिक (f. की).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hibernate
HIBERNATE: हेमन्तं<BR>or<BR>शीतं कालं गमयति (c. of गम्),<BR>नयति (नी, c. 1.) etc.: v. To pass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hiccough
HICCOUGH, HICCUP:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) हिक्का or<BR>हेक्का;<BR>(2) हल्लासः।<BR>II Verb.: हिक्कति, -ते (= हिक्क्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hidden
HIDDEN:<BR>(1) गूढ (f. ढा), नि-;<BR>(2) प्रच्छन्न (f.<BR>ना): v. Secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hide
HIDE (subs.): चर्मन् (n.): v. Skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hide
HIDE (v. t.): प्रच्छादयति (छद्, c. 10.), I will h. (the<BR>body)<BR>with these leaves:<BR>शुष्कपर्णपुटेन प्रच्छादयामि,<BR>Mr. viii.; and who h. them (thieves): ये च<BR> प्रच्छादयन्ति तान्, Mat.: v. Also to conceal.<BR>Ph.:<BR>he hid himself under the bed:<BR>पर्यङ्कतले निभृतं<BR> स्थितः, H. iii.; h. ing among the amaranths:<BR>कुरवकैरपवारितशरीरः (रा, रं), Sa. iii.;<BR>it was<BR>not known where he hid himself:<BR>न ज्ञायते कापि<BR> प्रलीनः सः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hide and seek
HIDE AND SEEK: a play: लुक्कायितमार्गणम् (?)<BR>(comp. लुकाचुरि); पलायितान्वेषणम् (?) (comp.<BR>पलापलि); अस्पृश्यम् (?), B. p. x. 18. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hideous
HIDEOUS:<BR>(1) विकृतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) विकृताकारः<BR>(रा, रं) and sim. comp.s.; h. face and body:<BR>वक्त्र वपुश्च विकृताकृति, Vi. v. 29.;<BR>(3) बीभत्सदर्शनः<BR>(ना, नं): v. Also horrible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hideously
HIDEOUSLY:<BR>(1) विकृतम्ः;<BR>(2) घोरम् (= fright-<BR>-fully, horribly: q.v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hideousness
HIDEOUSNESS:<BR>(1) विकृतता;<BR>(2) विकृताकारता;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hider
HIDER: गोप्तृ (f. त्री): v. Concealer, to<BR>hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hiding
HIDING (subs.):<BR>I Concealment: q.v.<BR>II<BR>Passive: प्रच्छन्नावस्थानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hiding-place
HIDING-PLACE: expr. by circumlo: v. To<BR>hide, place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hie
HIE (v.): त्वरते (त्वर्, c. 1.): v. To hasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hierarch
HIERARCH: धर्मनायकः (?); धर्माधीशः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hierarchical
HIERARCHICAL: expr. by comp.: v. Also<BR>priestly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hierarchy
HIERARCHY:<BR>I The body: धर्माधीशाः (m. pl.)<BR>(?) etc.<BR>II The government: *धर्माधीशतन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hieroglyphic
HIEROGLYPHIC: *चित्राक्षरम्; चित्रवर्णः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hieroglyphical
HIEROGLYPHICAL: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hierophant
HIEROPHANT: आचार्यः: v. Priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

higgle
HIGGLE: v. To haggle. H. dy-piggledy:<BR>अस्तव्यस्त (f. स्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

high
HIGH (adj.):<BR>(1) उच्चः (च्चा, च्चं)<BR>or<BR>उच्चैः (indec.).<BR>h. places:<BR>उच्चैः स्थानानि, D.; but now a h. er<BR>(place)<BR>than that on account of your favour of<BR>remembrance:<BR>अद्य तूच्चै स्तरं ताभ्यां स्मरणानुग्रहात्तव,<BR>Ku. vi. 19.; much more one so h. (i.e. noble:<BR>q.v.) किं पुनर्यस्तथोच्चैः, Me. 1. 17.; h. -minded:<BR>उच्चमनस्कः (स्का, स्कं); of a h. family, h.-born:<BR>उच्चवंशजः (जा, जं);<BR>at a h. price:<BR>उच्चमूल्येन;<BR>h.<BR>talk:<BR>उच्चप्रलापः, D.: v. Haughty; h. education:<BR>उच्चशिक्षा (after Bengali);<BR>(2) उन्नतः (ता, तं),<BR>सम्- (= lofty),<BR>h. summit:<BR>उन्नतं शैलाग्रम्, M. n.;<BR>connected with that h. (personage): उन्नतेन तेन<BR> योजितसम्बन्धः (न्धा, न्धं), Ku. vi. 30.;<BR>(3) उच्छ्रितः<BR>(ता, तं), सम्-, (lit. =h.; fig. =lofty: rare),<BR>h. umbrella:<BR>उच्छ्रितं च्छत्रम्, R. xvii. 33.;<BR>six feet<BR>h.:<BR>चतुर्हस्तोच्छ्रितः (ता, तं);<BR>h. sound:<BR>समुच्छ्रितो रवः,<BR>Ku.;<BR>(4) तुङ्ग (f. ङ्गा), उद्-, (= 3: rare),<BR>even a h. mountain is accessible:<BR>गम्यस्तुङ्गोऽपि भूघरः,<BR>Ki. xi. 63,;<BR>(5) प्रांशु (mfn.) (= tall: q.v.);<BR>(6) महत् (f. ती) (when h. =great),<BR>h. plea-<BR>sure:<BR>महासुखम्;<BR>h. admiral:<BR>*महानाविकनायकः;<BR>h.<BR>priest:<BR>*महान् पुरोहितः: v. Also chief. Ph.:<BR>h.<BR>note:<BR>उदात्तस्वरः;<BR>h. wind:<BR>गुरुसमीरः, Ku.;<BR>it is<BR>h. noon:<BR>मध्यमलङ्करोति भानुः;<BR>h. time:<BR>समुचितकालः;<BR>h. water:<BR>प्रवृद्धा वेला;<BR>h. meat:<BR>उग्रमांसम्;<BR>h. anti-<BR>quity:<BR>अतिपूर्वकालः;<BR>h. sauce:<BR>उग्रोपस्करः;<BR>h. er<BR>and h. er:<BR>अधिकाधिकम् (= more and more); h.<BR>est: i.e. extreme: q.v.: परः (रा, रं);<BR>h.<BR>treason:<BR>राजद्रोहः, -अपराधः;<BR>he has h. opinion of<BR>you:<BR>स त्वामुच्चैर्मन्यते;<BR>on h.<BR>ऊर्द्धम्; from on h.:<BR>उपरिष्टात्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

high
HIGH (adv.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) उच्चैः;<BR>(2) उच्चकैः;<BR>(3) उच्चम्।<BR>II Fig.: expr. by adj.: h. -aimed:<BR>उच्चाभिलाषिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

high-blown
HIGH-BLOWN: उत्सिक्तः (क्ता, क्तं): v. Inflated,<BR>proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

high-bred
HIGH-BRED:<BR>(1) अभिजातः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) सुजातः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

high-climbing
HIGH-CLIMBING:<BR>(1) उच्चः (च्चा, च्चं);<BR>(2) तुङ्ग<BR>(f. ङ्गा): v. High.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

high-coloured
HIGH-COLOURED:<BR>I Lit.: अतिरञ्जितः (ता, तं).<BR>II Fig.: विचित्र (f. त्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

high-day
HIGH-DAY: पर्वन् (n.): v. Festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

high-flown
HIGH-FLOWN: स्फीतः (ता, तं) (lit. and fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

high-handed
HIGH-HANDED: उत्-पीडक (f. डिका): v.<BR>Oppressive, violent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

high-heeled
HIGH-HEELED: उच्चतलः (ला, लं) (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

highland
HIGHLAND: पार्वतीयदेशः (?),<BR>h. dress:<BR>पार्वतीयवेषः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

highlander
HIGHLANDER:<BR>I Lit.: पार्वतीयः (या, यं) (?).<BR>II A Scot: *स्कुदः (दा, दं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

highly
HIGHLY:<BR>I =high: q.v.<BR>II Greatly: q.v.:<BR>भृशम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

high-mettled
HIGH-METTLED:<BR>(1) महासत्त्व (f. त्त्वा);<BR>(2)<BR>महातेजस् (mfn.);<BR>(3) अतितेजस्विन् (f. नी), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

highness
HIGHNESS:<BR>I Lit.: v. Height.<BR>II As title:<BR>देव (f. वी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

high-priestship
HIGH-PRIESTSHIP, HIGH-PRIESTHOOD: महा-<BR>पौरोहित्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

high-road
HIGH-ROAD:<BR>(1) रथ्या;<BR>(2) राजमार्गः: v. Street.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

high-seasoned
HIGH-SEASONED: सुसंस्कृतः (ता, तं) (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

high-spirited
HIGH-SPIRITED:<BR>I = high-mettled: q.v.<BR>II<BR>Irascible: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

highway
HIGHWAY: राजमार्गः,<BR>shall not obstruct h.:<BR>राजमार्गान्न<BR> रोधयेत्, N. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

highwayman
HIGHWAYMAN: perh. पान्थमुष् (mfn.), Mit.<BR>वाटपाटच्चरः, Viv.: v. Also robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hilarity
HILARITY: उल्लासः, सम्-: v. Mirth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hill
HILL: पर्वतः (properly=mount); क्षुद्रपर्वतः:<BR>v. Mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hillock
HILLOCK:<BR>(1) स्थली;<BR>(2) वप्र (mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hilly
HILLY: पर्वतमयः (यी, यं) (= mountainous:<BR>q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hilt
HILT: त्सरुः,<BR>from the h.:<BR>त्सरुप्रदेशात्, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

himself
HIMSELF:<BR>I As nomi.: स्वयम्<BR>or<BR>स्वयमेव<BR>(emphatic),<BR>killing h.:<BR>स्वयं मारयित्वा, Mr. ix.:<BR>v. Self.<BR>II As acc.: आत्मानम्, he who kills h.:<BR>य आत्मानं व्यापादयति।<BR>By h.:<BR>एकाकी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hind
HIND (subs.):<BR>I The female of the stag:<BR>(1) मृगी;<BR>(2) मृगवधूः; etc.: v. Deer.<BR>II<BR>A peasant: q.v.: ग्राम्यजनः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hind
HIND, HINDER (adj.):<BR>(1) पश्चिमः (मा, मं);<BR>(2) जघन्यः (न्या, न्यं).<BR>H. part:<BR>पश्चाद्भागः, पश्चाहेशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hinder
HINDER (v.):<BR>(1) वारयति, नि-, विनि-, प्रति-,<BR>with<BR>h. ed twinkling.:<BR>निवारितनिमेषः (षा, षं), Sa.;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रतिषेधति (सिध्, c. 1.),<BR>h. ing the entry of all<BR>attendants.:<BR>प्रतिषिद्धाशेषपरिजनप्रवेशा, K.: v. To<BR>prevent, obstruct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hindermost
HINDERMOST, HINDMOST: सर्वपश्चिमः (मा, मं);<BR>(2) परमः (मा, मं) (= final).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hindoo
HINDOO:<BR>I As subs.: आर्यः।<BR>II As adj.:<BR>by comp. or gen.,<BR>for H. student:<BR>छात्राणामार्य-<BR>देशयानाम्, Raj. vi. 8. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hindoostani
HINDOOSTANI: सिन्धुस्थानी, -भाषा, उर्दुः, -वाक्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hindrance
HINDRANCE:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) वरणम्, नि-;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रतिषेधः।<BR>II Obstacle: q.v.: विघ्नः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hinge
HINGE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: *केन्द्रयति (nomi.)<BR>II<BR>Fig.: v. To enter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hingle
HINGLE (subs.): *केन्द्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hint
HINT (subs.):<BR>(1) इङ्गितम्;<BR>(2) सङ्केतः;<BR>(2) आकुतम्।<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hint
HINT (v.): इङ्गितं ददाति (दा, c. 3.)<BR>or<BR>करोति (कृ,<BR>c. 8.).<BR>II To suggest, allude: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hip
HIP:<BR>I Hanuch: q.v.: कटिः। Ph.:<BR>I have<BR>him on my h.:<BR>मम हस्तगतः सः।<BR>II A fruit:<BR>*हिबम्, -कम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hippocamp
HIPPOCAMP, HIPPOCAMPUS: *अश्वकृञ्चिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hippodrome
HIPPODROME: रथचर्या, -स्थानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hippogriff
HIPPOGRIFF: *श्येनघोटकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hippopotamus
HIPPOPOTAMUS: *जलहस्तिन् (f. नी); जलशूकरः<BR>(f. री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hire
HIRE (v. t.): भाटयति (c. of भट्), h. ing a cart:<BR>भाटयित्वा शकटम्, Viv. Ph.:<BR>a h. d labourer:<BR>भृतः,<BR> -कः, Viv.;<BR>to h. labourers:<BR>भृतकान् गृह्वाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hire
HIRE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: भाटः<BR>or<BR>भाटकः, to pay h.:<BR>भाटं ददाति, Viv.;<BR>to take on h.:<BR>भाटकेन गृह्वाति,<BR>N.s.<BR>II Wages: q.v.: मूल्यम्, Mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hireling
HIRELING (adj.): perh. गृह्यः, D. ii.: v.<BR>Venal, mercenary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hireling
HIRELING (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) भृतकः;<BR>(2)<BR>वैतनिकः।<BR>II A mercenary: q.v.<BR>III A<BR>prostitute: पण्यस्त्री।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hirer
HIRER:<BR>(1) माटयितृ (f. त्री) (of things);<BR>(2)<BR>स्वामिन् (f. नी) (= master) (of men), V.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hirsute
HIRSUTE:<BR>(1) लो(रो)मशः (शा, शं);<BR>(2) बहुलो(रो)मन्<BR>(mfn.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

his
HIS:<BR>(1) तदीयः (या, यं) (of that);<BR>(2) पतदीयः<BR>(या, यं) (of this);<BR>(3) by gen. N.B.<BR>When not emphatic, it is not expr. when<BR>the sense is clear and when emphatic,<BR>it is expr. by those words given under own.<BR>Confining with h. family:<BR>एनं सपुत्रकलत्रं नियम्य,<BR>Mu.; as this (man)<BR>quits h. life:<BR>यथायं प्राणान् [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">Page347</a>]<BR> त्यजति, Mu. 1;<BR>with h. fortitude:<BR>निजेन धैर्यगुणेन,<BR>Ki. xiv. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hiss
HISS (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) फू(फु)त्करोति;<BR>(2)<BR>फूत्कारम् उद्गिरति (गॄ, c. 6.), V. t.<BR>II To h.<BR>off: निष्कासयति (c. of कस्) (= to drive out);<BR>धिक्करोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hiss
HISS, HISSING (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: फू(फु)त्कारः।<BR>II<BR>Of content: perh. घिक्कारः<BR>or<BR>धिक्कृतम्, D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hist
HIST (interj.): तूष्णीम् (indec.): v. Silent, be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

historian
HISTORIAN:<BR>(1) इतिहासप्रणेतृ (m.) and sim.<BR>comp.s.: v. Author:<BR>(2) आख्यानविद् (m.),<BR>Vi. (=annalist).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

historic
HISTORIC, -AL:<BR>(1) ऐतिहासिकः (की, कं);<BR>(2)<BR>by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

historically
HISTORICALLY: इतिहासानुक्रमेण, आख्यानक्रमेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

historiographer
HISTORIOGRAPHER: *इतिहासलेखकः; आख्यानाधिकृतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

history
HISTORY:<BR>(1) इतिहासः, knows h. and mythology:<BR>इतिहासपुराणज्ञः, Mah.;<BR>(2) पुरावृत्तम् (= ancient h.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

histrionic
HISTRIONIC, -AL: नाटकोयः (या, यं): v. Thea-<BR>-trical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hit
HIT (subs.):<BR>I Blow: q.v.: प्रहारः।<BR>II<BR>throw: क्षेपः। Ph.: a good h.: prob. सुप्रहारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hit
HIT (v.):<BR>I To strike: प्रहरति (हृ, c. 1.),<BR>look, you are to h. this mark now:<BR>त्वयेदानीं प्रहर्तव्य-<BR>मेतल्लक्ष्यं विलोक्यताम्, Mah. i. 131. I.<BR>II. To h.<BR>on or upon, i.e. to come by chance: expr.<BR>by लभते (लभ्, c. 1.): v. To get.<BR>III To<BR>h. off, i.e. to describe with h. s: perh.<BR>विवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.) (= to expose).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hitch
HITCH (subs.): बाधः (?), there is a h. in it:<BR>*सबाधभेतत्: v. Obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hither
HITHER (adv.): इतः: v. Here. H. and thither:<BR>(1) इतस्ततः;<BR>(2) इतशचेतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hither
HITHER (adj.): expr. by this, on the h. side:<BR>अस्मिन् पार्श्वे।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hitherto
HITHERTO:<BR>I Of time:<BR>(1) अद्यावधि;<BR>(2)<BR>अद्य यावत्।<BR>II Of place: एतत्पर्यन्तम्।: v. Up to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hitherward
HITHERWARD:<BR>(1) इत इतः;<BR>(2) एतदभिमुखम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hive
HIVE:<BR>(1) मधुकोषः;<BR>(2) करण्डः;<BR>(3) छत्रकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ho
HO, HOA (interj.): हंहोः v. O.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoar
HOAR: धवलः (ला, लं): v. Hoary, gray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoard
HOARD (subs.): पूगः: v. Heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoard
HOARD (v.): पूगीकरोति: v. To heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoar-frost
HOAR-FROST:<BR>(1) घननीहारः, Ki. xiii. 24.;<BR>(2)<BR>सान्द्रतुहिनम्, M.n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoariness
HOARINESS:<BR>(1) धवलता;<BR>(2) शुक्लताः v. Gray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoarse
HOARSE: रूक्षः (क्षा, क्षं) (= harsh, rough:<BR>q.v.): v. H. ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoarsely
HOARSELY: रूक्षस्वरम्<BR>or<BR>रूक्षेण स्वरेण (= harshly,<BR>roughly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoarseness
HOARSENESS:<BR>(1) रूक्षता;<BR>(2) रूक्षस्वरता। H. of<BR>voice (from cold):<BR>(1) स्वरभङ्गः;<BR>(2) स्वरोपधातः,<BR>Sr.: v. Harshness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoary
HOARY: expr. by words given under white,<BR>become h. with age:<BR>जराधवलितः (ता, तं), K.;<BR>with h. hair:<BR>सितैः केशैः, Ki. xi. 3.; h. brows:<BR>विशदभ्रूयुगम्, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoax
HOAX (subs.): विप्रलम्भः: v. Trick, deception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoax
HOAX (v.): विप्रलभते (लभ्, c. 1.),<BR>h. ed by the<BR>boys:<BR>विप्रलब्धाः कुमारकैः, V.p. v. 37. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hob
HOB: ग्राम्यजनः: v. Rustic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hobble
HOBBLE (v.): लङ्गति (लङ्ग्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>limp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hobby
HOBBY, -HORSE:<BR>I Lit.: घोटकविशेषः।<BR>II A<BR>play-horse: क्रीडाघोटकः।<BR>III A favourite<BR>theme: चिरकाम्यम् (?),<BR>to ride one's h.:<BR>*चिरकाम्यं<BR> कीर्तयति<BR>or<BR>स्तौति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hobgoblin
HOBGOBLIN: भूतः: v. Goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hobnail
HOBNAIL: स्थूलकीलः and sim. comp.s. (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hobnob
HOBNOB: expr. by पानगोष्ठी: v. To drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hobsons choice
HOBSON'S CHOICE: ॥॥॥भृत्याभिरुचिः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hock
HOCK: मदिरविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hocus-pocus
HOCUS-POCUS:<BR>I Juggler: q.v.: मायाकारः।<BR>II His trick: माया। Ph.:<BR>by h.:<BR>तन्त्रमन्त्रैः, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hod
HOD: लेपफलकम् (?) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hodgepodge
HODGEPODGE: सप्तमिश्रम् (?); सन्निपातः (?),<BR>Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoe
HOE (subs.): कुद्दालः,<BR>others tore up grass stumps<BR>with h. s.:<BR>अपरे वीरणस्तम्बान् कृद्दालैः विदलन्ति स्म,<BR>Ram. ii. 7. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoe
HOE (v.): कुद्दालेन तृणानि विदलति (दल्, c. 1.),<BR>उन्मूलयति (मूल्, c. 10.), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoeing
HOEING, HOER: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hog
HOG:<BR>(1) शू(सू)करः,<BR>h.-keeper:<BR>शौकरिकः, Ram. ii.<BR>90. 17.;<BR>(2) वराहः, with h.'s flesh and venison:<BR>मांसैर्वाराहहारिणैः, Mah. ii. 4. 2.;<BR>(3) कोलः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoggish
HOGGISH<BR>(1) शूकरसन्निभः (भा, भं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.;<BR>(2) by adv., शूकरवत्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hog-plum
HOG-PLUM:<BR>I The tree: आम्रातः, -कः।<BR>II<BR>The fruit: आम्रातम्, -कम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hogshead
HOGSHEAD:<BR>I A measure: भानविशेषः।<BR>II A<BR>cask: कुण्डम्,<BR>drank eight h.s:<BR>अष्टौ कृण्डान्यपिबत्,<BR>Mah. i. 126. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hogsty
HOGSTY:<BR>(1) शूकरशाला;<BR>(2) शूकरशरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoiden
HOIDEN: v. Hoyden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoist
HOIST (v.): उन्नमयति (c. of नम्): v. To raise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoist
HOIST (subs.):<BR>I A machine: *उन्नमनयन्त्रम्।<BR>II H. ing:<BR>(1) उन्नमनम्;<BR>(2) उत्थापतम्, Bharata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hold
HOLD (subs.):<BR>I Grasp: q.v.: Ph.:<BR>to take<BR>or lay h.:<BR>गृह्वाति, परि-, (ग्रह्, c. 9.); to keep h.:<BR>धारयति।<BR>II Support: q.v.: आलम्बः, -नम्,<BR>without any h.:<BR>निरालम्बनः, D.<BR>III Authority,<BR>claim: q.v.: अधिकारः।<BR>IV Influence,<BR>ascendancy: q.v.<BR>V Prison: q.v.: चारकम्।<BR>VI Strong-h. दुर्गम्।<BR>VII Of a ship: perh.<BR>क्रोडः (comp. Bengali कोल्),<BR>fore h.:<BR>अग्रः क्रोडः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hold
HOLD (v. t.):<BR>I To keep h. of: धारयति, -ते<BR>or (rarely) धरति, वि-, सं-, परि-, (धृ, c., 10. and<BR>1.),<BR>h. me uncle:<BR>मातुल धारयस्व भाम्, Vi. iv.<BR>Can-<BR>not h. his neck:<BR>न शक्रोति शिरोधरां धरयितुम्, R.<BR>II<BR>To restrain: धरयति॥॥॥<BR>I cannot h. my<BR>tongue:<BR>न शक्नोभ्यात्मनो जिह्वां धारयितुम्,<BR>V ii.;<BR>and h. ing the horse asked from a distance:<BR>धृततुरङ्गमश्च दूरादेवापृच्छत्, K.<BR>III. To possess:<BR>धारयति<BR>or<BR>धरति, (which was)<BR>long held by kings<BR>of your race:<BR>चिरंधृता भूपतिभिः स्ववंशजैः, Ki. i. 29.;<BR>burden held by himself:<BR>आत्मना धृतां धुरम्, R. iii.<BR>35.<BR>IV To contain: धारयति<BR>or<BR>धरति,<BR>the<BR>celestial river will h. the seed:<BR>सुरापगा बीजं<BR> धारयिष्यति, Ku. x. 25.<BR>V To keep, defend,<BR>q.v.: रक्षति (रक्ष्, c. 1.).<BR>VI To maintain:<BR>q.v.: धारयति<BR>or<BR>धरति;<BR>h. ing thoughts for<BR>victory:<BR>धृतजयधृति (mfn.), Ki. xii. 2.<BR>VII To<BR>esteem, think: q.v.: मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.).<BR>VIII To do, bring about: करोति,<BR>to h.<BR>counsel:<BR>मन्त्रणां करोति;<BR>to h. a council:<BR>सभां<BR> करोति;<BR>to h. a wager:<BR>पणं करोति। Ph.: to h.<BR>one's own: perh. नापचीयते (pass. of चि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hold
HOLD (v. i.):<BR>I To stand, stop: q.v.: निष्ठति<BR>(स्था, c. 1.).<BR>II To last, remain: q.v.:<BR>तिष्ठति।<BR>II To apply: q.v.: लगति (लग्, c.<BR>1.).<BR>IV To think: q.v.: मन्यते।<BR>V To<BR>refrain, desist: q.v.: निवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.).<BR>VI To defend, derive: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hold back
HOLD BACK:<BR>I Intrans: perh. विचिकित्सते<BR>(= to hesitate).<BR>II Trnas.: v. To with-<BR>-hold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hold forth
HOLD FORTH, HOLD OUT:<BR>I To stretch out:<BR>q.v.: प्रसारयति (c. of सृ).<BR>II To exhibit,<BR>offer: q.v.: धारयति।<BR>III To endure:<BR>q.v.: सहते (सह्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hold in
HOLD IN:<BR>I Trans:<BR>(1) धारयति;<BR>(2) नियच्छति<BR>(यम्, c. 1.) (= to restrain: q.v.).<BR>II<BR>Intrans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hold off
HOLD OFF: परिहरति (हृ, c. 1.): v. To avoid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hold on
HOLD ON:<BR>I To continue: तिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.).<BR>II To proceed in: न विरमति (रम्, c. 1.), Ki.<BR>v. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hold to
HOLD TO: धारयति: v. Also to maintain,<BR>cling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hold up
HOLD UP:<BR>I To raise: q.v.: उन्नमयति (c.<BR>of नम्).<BR>II To support one's self: आत्मानं<BR> संधारयति।<BR>III To cease raining:<BR>let the<BR>weather h. up:<BR>भवतु वृष्टेरुपशमः, H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hold-back
HOLD-BACK: अन्तरायः: v. Obstacle, restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

holder
HOLDER:<BR>I Lit.: धारकः, धारयितृ (m.); etc.<BR>II A thing for holding, expr. by verb,<BR>this is its h.:<BR>अनेनैतद्धर्यते: v. Handle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

holder-forth
HOLDER-FORTH: प्रवक्तृ (f. क्ती): v. Speaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hold-fast
HOLD-FAST: *दृढाग्रहः: v. Catch, hook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

holding
HOLDING (subs.): i.e. tenure; क्षेत्रम् (= field),<BR>according to the nature of the h.:<BR>क्षेत्रस्थित्यनुसारेण,<BR>Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hole
HOLE:<BR>I A pierce:<BR>(1) गर्तः (spec. of h.s<BR>in earth: not fig.);<BR>(2) छिद्रम्,<BR>making a h.<BR>on a side:<BR>पार्श्वे छिद्रं विधाय, Bha.;<BR>(3) रन्घरम्,<BR>dexterous in picking h. s:<BR>रन्घ्रान्वेषणदक्षः, R.;<BR>(4)<BR>विवरम् (rare),<BR>in other's h. s.:<BR>परस्य विवरे, Ki.<BR>II A cave, den: q.v.: विवरम्।<BR>III A<BR>hovel: perh. विवरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

holiday
HOLIDAY:<BR>(1) पर्वन् (n.) (= religious day);<BR>(2) अनध्यायः (= school h.), because to day is a h.: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">Page349</a>]<BR>अद्यानध्याय इति,<BR>V iv.;<BR>(2) *बन्धः, -दिनम्,<BR>(= court h.): v. Also festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

holily
HOLILY: v. Piously, sacredly, holy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

holiness
HOLINESS:<BR>I Sanctity, sacredness: q.v.:<BR>पवित्रता।<BR>II In address: भगवत् (f. ती), if<BR>(your) revered h. gives (me)<BR>no harbour:<BR>यति<BR> भगवत्पादमूलमशरणम्, D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

holla
HOLLA, HOLLO, HOLLOA: हला (in Prakrit):<BR>v. O.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hollow
HOLLOW (subs.):<BR>(1) कोटरः (of trees),<BR>in the<BR>centres of h. s:<BR>कोटरोदरेषु, K.;<BR>(2) (कर-) पुटः<BR>(of the hand);<BR>(3) (कर्ण-) कूपः (of the ear);<BR>(4) (नाभि-) आवर्तः (of the nave);<BR>(5) गर्तः<BR>(= hole: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hollow
HOLLOW (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: शून्यगर्भ (f. र्भा);<BR>(2) मध्यशुषिरः (रा, रं) (rare), B. com.<BR>II<BR>Fig.: शून्यगर्भ (f. र्भा): v. Empty, vain.<BR>III Of sounds, deep: धीरः (रा, रं) or perh.<BR>धीरगभीरः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hollow
HOLLOW (v.):<BR>(1) तक्षति (तक्ष्, c. 1.) (?);<BR>(2) खनति (खन्, c. 1.) (= to dig);<BR>(3)<BR>better by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hollowness
HOLLOWNESS:<BR>I Lit. and fig.: शून्यगर्भता: v.<BR>Emptiness.<BR>II Of sounds: धीरता or perh.<BR>धीरगभीरता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

holly
HOLLY: *हालिः; सदाहरितो गुल्मभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hollyhock
HOLLYHOCK: a plant: *चित्रमेवती।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

holly-oak
HOLLY-OAK, HOLM-OAK: सिन्दूरभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

holocaust
HOLOCAUST:<BR>(1) होमः;<BR>(2) हुतम्;<BR>(3) हव्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

holy
HOLY: पुण्घ (f. ण्या),<BR>h. person:<BR>पुण्यजनः, Ki. iii.<BR>31.;<BR>h. prayer:<BR>पुण्या स्तुतिः, K.;<BR>h. rivers:<BR>सरितः<BR> पुण्याः, Ram. ii. 12. 5.; h. place of pilgrimage:<BR>पुण्यतीर्थः, Ram.;<BR>h. land:<BR>पूण्यभूमिः: v. Also<BR>pure, sacred. Ph.:<BR>h. father, mother:<BR>भगवत्<BR>(f. ती);<BR>“h. alliance”:<BR>धर्मसन्धिः; h. -day: v.<BR>Holiday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homage
HOMAGE (subs.):<BR>I In gen.<BR>(1) नमस्कारः;<BR>(2) नमस्या, N.: v. Also respect.<BR>To do,<BR>pay h.:<BR>नमति, प्र-, (नम्, c. 1.),<BR>men do not pay<BR>h. to a man until he pays h. to you:<BR>न नमन्ति पुरुषं<BR> पुरुषास्तव यावदीश न नतिः क्रियते, Ki.<BR>II Feudal:<BR>to do h. (to a lord): perh. प्रभुत्वं स्वीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

home
HOME (subs.):<BR>(1) गृहम् (= house: q.v.),<BR>gone<BR>h.:<BR>गृहं गतः, Mr. ix.;<BR>(2) जन्मभूमिः (= birth-<BR>-place),<BR>where is your h., sir? Madam, Patna<BR>is my h.:<BR>कुत आर्यः? आर्ये पाटलिपुत्रं मे जन्मभूमिः,<BR>Mr. ii.;<BR>(3) आलयः (= abode: q.v.). Ph.:<BR>at h.:<BR>गृहे<BR>or<BR>गेहे, U. i. 57. 8.;<BR>he is making<BR>himself at h. there:<BR>तत्रा परिचित इव व्यवहरति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

home
HOME (adv.):<BR>I Lit.: गृहम्।<BR>II Fig: expr.<BR>by मर्मन् (n.),<BR>to come h.:<BR>मर्म स्पृशति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

home
HOME (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: ग्र्ह- in comp.<BR>II Of<BR>one's country:<BR>“h. department”.<BR>*स्वदेशविभागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

home-bound
HOME-BOUND:<BR>(1) गृहगामिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) स्वदेश-<BR>गामिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

home-bred
HOME-BRED:<BR>I Lit.: गृहजः (जा, जं)<BR>or<BR>जातः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR>II Rude: ग्राम्य (f. म्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homeless
HOMELESS: अगृहः (हा, हं), Mah. iii. 27. 16.;<BR>निराश्रयः (या, यं) and sim. comp.s.: v. Also<BR>exile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homliness
HOMLINESS: ग्राम्यता: v. Homely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homely
HOMELY:<BR>I Domestic: q.v.: गृह्य (f. ह्या).<BR>II Plain, unpolished: ग्राम्य (f. म्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

home-made
HOME-MADE:<BR>I Made at home: गृह- in<BR>comp.,<BR>h. butter:<BR>गृहनवनीतम्।<BR>II Made in one's<BR>own country: स्वदेश- in comp.: v. Also<BR>made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homer
HOMER:<BR>I The poet: *होमरः।<BR>II A measure:<BR>मानविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homesick
HOMESICK: गृहविरहातुरः (रा, रं); गृहविरहार्त (f.<BR>र्ता), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homespun
HOMESPUN:<BR>I Adj.: गृहोतः (ता, तं) (?).<BR>II<BR>Subs.: गृहोतम् (?); गृहनिर्मितवस्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homestall
HOMESTALL, HOMESTEAD:<BR>(1) वास्तु (mn.);<BR>(2) गृहवास्तु (n.), Kat;<BR>(3) वेश्मन् (n.) (rare)<BR>Kat.;<BR>(4) वासभूमिः, Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homeward
HOMEWARD: स्वदेशाभिमुखम्,<BR>“H. -bound”.<BR>स्वदेशाभि-<BR>मुखः (खा, खं): v. Also home-bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homicidal
HOMICIDAL: expr. by tat. comp.: v. next<BR>art; belonging to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homicide
HOMICIDE:<BR>I The deed: नृहत्या and sim.<BR>comp.s.: v. Murder.<BR>II The slayer:<BR>(1) नरहत्याकारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) मनुष्यघातिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homily
HOMILY: धर्मप्रबन्धः (?): v. Sermon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homoepathic
HOMOEPATHIC: expr. by comp., h. doctor:<BR>*समव्यवस्थाविद्वैद्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homoepathy
HOMOEPATHY: *समव्यवस्था, समव्यवस्थाशास्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homogeneal
HOMOGENEAL, HOMOGENEOUS: *सजातीयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homologous
HOMOLOGOUS: *समस्थिति (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

homonymous
HOMONYMOUS: बह्वर्थकः (का, कं): v. Also<BR>equivocal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hone
HONE: शाणः(नः): v. Whetstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

honest
HONEST:<BR>I Decent, good: q.v.<BR>II Upright,<BR>just:<BR>(1) शुचि (mfn.) (= pure), M.;<BR>(2)<BR>अर्थशौचयुक्त (f. क्ता), K. b.;<BR>(3) सरलः (ला,<BR> लं) (= simple);<BR>(4) निष्कपटः (टा, टं) (=guile-<BR>-less).<BR>III Frank, sincere: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

honestly
HONESTLY:<BR>(1) छलं विहाय;<BR>(2) निष्कपटम्: v.<BR>Also simply, sincerely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

honesty
HONESTY:<BR>(1) अर्थशौचभ् or sim. शौचम्<BR>or<BR>शुचिता,<BR> त्वम् (when the sense is clear);<BR>(2) निष्कपटता<BR>(= guilelessness);<BR>(3) सारल्यम् (=simplicity);<BR>(4) आर्जवम् (= uprightness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

honey
HONEY: मधु (n.),<BR>h. -bees make h. by gathering<BR>the juice of divers trees:<BR>भधुकरमक्षिका नानाजातीनां<BR> वृक्षाणां रसान् समाहृत्य मधु निष्पादयन्ति, S. c.; old<BR>(h.)<BR>is binding and astringent:<BR>पुराणं ग्राहकं रूक्षं,<BR>Bha; of this (king)<BR>who is h. in mouth and<BR>poison at heart:<BR>अस्य मुखमधोर्हृ दयविषस्य, Sa. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

honey-bee
HONEY-BEE: मधुमक्षिका: v. Bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

honeycomb
HONEYCOMB:<BR>(1) मधुकोषः;<BR>(2) मधुचक्रम्;<BR>(3)<BR>छत्रकम्;<BR>(4) मधुजालकम्, Si. xii. 54;<BR>(5) क्षौद्रपटलम्<BR>(rare), R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

honeydew
HONEYDEW: दालं मधु, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

honeyed
HONEYED: मधुमयः (यी, यं) (lit. and fig.) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

honey-harvest
HONEY-HARVEST: मधुसंग्रहः (?) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

honeysuckle
HONEYSUCKLE: *मधुगर्भा; सुपुष्पलताभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

honey-tongued
HONEY-TONGUED:<BR>(1) मुखमधु (mfn.), Sa. and<BR>sim. comp.s.;<BR>(2) perh. मधुजिह्व (f. ह्ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

honorary
HONORARY: no equiv. *साभ्मानिकः (की, कं)<BR>or by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

honour
HONOUR (subs.):<BR>I A nice sense of what is<BR>right: मानः, सम्-,<BR>who has from age lost all<BR>sense of h.:<BR>जरावलुप्तमानावमानचित्तः, D. ii.<BR>II<BR>Nobility, chastity: मानः, सम-,<BR>rich in h.:<BR>मान-<BR>धनः (ना, नं), Ki. ii. 19.;<BR>devoid of h.:<BR>मानहीनः<BR>(ना, नं), Ki. xi. 59.<BR>III Respect, reverence:<BR>q.v.<BR>(1) मानः, सम-, P.;<BR>(2) आदरः (= atten-<BR>-tion):<BR>IV A mark of respect:<BR>(1) मानः,<BR> सम्-,<BR>for this h.:<BR>अस्य सभ्मानस्य कृते, P. i. 3.;<BR>(2) गौरवम्,<BR>master's h.s on dependents are as a<BR>rule moving with the object to be accomplished:<BR>प्रयोजनापेक्षितया प्रभूणां प्रायश्चलं गौरवमाश्रितेषु, Ku.<BR>iii. 1.;<BR>(3) प्रसादः (= favour: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

honour
HONOUR (v.):<BR>(1) मानयति, सं-, (rarely) प्रति-,<BR>(c. of मन्),<BR>yet your Highness will be pleased<BR>to h. my request:<BR>तथापि मद्विज्ञापनां मानयितुमर्हत्यार्यः,<BR>Mu. ii.;<BR>(2) पूजयति, सम्-, अभि-, प्र-, (प्वज्,<BR>c. 10.) (= to respect: q.v.)<BR>he, although<BR>destitute of h. will be everywhere h. ed:<BR>सम्मान-<BR>हीनोऽपि स सर्वत्र प्रपूज्यते, P. i. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

honourable
HONOURABLE:<BR>I Possessing a high mind:<BR>मानिन् (f. नी).<BR>II Illustrious, respected:<BR>(1) मान्य (f. न्या)<BR>or<BR>माननीयः (या, यं), सम्-;<BR>(2) पूज्य (f. ज्या)<BR>or<BR>पूजनीयः (या, यं), I have<BR>been commanded by h. sir (you): पूज्येनाहमादिष्टः,<BR>Mah.: v. Respectable.<BR>III Conferring<BR>honour: सम्मानकरः (री, रं) and sim. comp.s.:<BR>v. Also famous.<BR>IV Good, noble: q.v.:<BR>शुद्ध (f. द्धा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

honourably
HONOURABLY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hood
HOOD:<BR>I For women: शिरस्कम् (?)<BR>II Of a<BR>carriage: शिरस् (n.) (??).<BR>III Of a serpent:<BR>फणा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoodwink
HOODWINK:<BR>I Lit.: v. To blind.<BR>II To<BR>deceive: q.v.: perh. छलयति (छल् c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoof
HOOF:<BR>(1) खुरः,<BR>right h.:<BR>दक्षिणखुरः, K.;<BR>(2)<BR>शफ (mn.) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoofed
HOOFED:<BR>(1) खुरिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) खुरान्वितः<BR>(ता, तं); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hook
HOOK (v.):<BR>I Of fishes: वडिशयति (nomi.).<BR>II To entrap: पाशे पातयति, (c. of पत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hook
HOOK (subs.):<BR>I Fish-h.: q.v.: वडिशम्।<BR>II<BR>To goad elephants: अङ्कुश (mn.).<BR>III In<BR>gen.: आकर्षणी (?).<BR>IV A sickle: दात्रम्।<BR>V<BR>Fig.: पाशः: v. Snare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hooked
HOOKED (adj.): वक्र (f. क्रा): v. Crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hook-nosed
HOOK-NOSED: शुकनासः (सा, सं); तुङ्गनासः (सा,<BR> सं) [not वक्रनासः].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoop
HOOP (subs.): चक्रम् (= anything circular).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoop
HOOP (v.):<BR>(1) चित्कारं करोति;<BR>(2) उच्चैः शब्दायते<BR>(nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hooping-cough
HOOPING-COUGH: perh. ऊर्ध्वश्वासः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoopoe
HOOPOE: a bird: काष्ठकूटः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoot
HOOT, HOOTING (subs.):<BR>I In gen.: धिक्कारः<BR>(?) or by circumlo.<BR>II Of an owl: घूत्कारः, U.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoot
HOOT (v.):<BR>I In gen.: गर्हयति (गर्ह्, c.<BR>10.) (?).<BR>II Of an owl: घूत्करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hop
HOP (subs.):<BR>I A leap: q.v.: एकपादलम्फः।<BR>II A plant: लताविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hop
HOP (v.): एकपादेन प्लवते (प्लु, c. 1.): v. To<BR>leap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hope
HOPE (subs.):<BR>I Expectation: आशा, प्रति-,<BR>what is not done from h.:<BR>आशया किमिव न क्रियते,<BR>K.;<BR>I have no h. of life:<BR>निराशोऽस्मि जीविते, Sa.<BR>vi.; the girl entertained h.s of remeeting<BR>(her)<BR>master:<BR>बभुवाशावती बाला पुनर्भर्तृसमागमे,<BR>Mah.;<BR>false h.:<BR>दुराशा K.: v. Also wish.<BR>II That which gives h.:<BR>(1) आशा;<BR>(2)<BR>आश्वासः, for you are the h. of the distressed:<BR>त्वं ह्यार्तानां समाश्वासः, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hope
HOPE (v.):<BR>(1) आशां करोति;<BR>(2) आशंसते (शंस्,<BR>c. 1.) (= to apprehend). N.B. In questions,<BR>“I h.” may be expr. by the interro. parti-<BR>-cles अपि, कच्चित्, अथ,<BR>we h. the breeze of these<BR>lotus-leaves pleases you:<BR>अपि सुखायते ते नलिनी-<BR>पत्रवातः, Sa. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hopeful
HOPEFUL:<BR>I Entertaining hope:<BR>(1) आशावत्<BR>(f. ती);<BR>(2) आशान्वितः (ता, तं); and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Giving hope:<BR>(1) आशाजननः<BR>(नी, नं);<BR>(2) आशावर्धन (f. नी) (= very h.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hopefully
HOPEFULLY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hopefulness
HOPEFULNESS:<BR>(1) आशावत्ता;<BR>(2) आशाजननता।<BR>For dif. v. Hopeful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hopeless
HOPELESS:<BR>I Without hope:<BR>(1) निराशः<BR>(शा, शं);<BR>(2) हताशः (शा, शं); etc.<BR>II<BR>Beyond hope: आशातीतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hopelessly
HOPELESSLY: expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hopelessness
HOPELESSNESS:<BR>(1) नैराश्यम्;<BR>(2) निराशता;<BR>(3)<BR>हताशता; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hopper
HOPPER: in a mill: शस्याधारः, Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horde
HORDE: सङ्घः (= crowd, flock: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horizon
HORIZON:<BR>(1) हरिजम्, as a sign comes to the h.:<BR>यद्वद्राशिर्व्रजति हरिजम्, Ja. v. 17.;<BR>(2) क्षितिजम्,<BR>that point is then on the h.:<BR>तल्लग्नं क्षितिजे तदा, Su.<BR>iii. 48. N.B. Colloquially दिङ्मण्डलः and sim.<BR>comp.s. would do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horizontal
HORIZONTAL: समः (मा, मं) (= level: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horizontally
HORIZONTALLY: perh. समभूमौ (= on a level).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horn
HORN:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) शृङ्गम्,<BR>the root of a h.:<BR>शृङ्ग-<BR>मूलम्;<BR>the tip of a h.:<BR>शृङ्गाग्रम्, Pa.; sharp-h. ed:<BR>तीक्ष्णशृङ्गः, Ram.;<BR>(2) विषाणम्, struck with h. s.:<BR>विषाणैराहतः (ता, तं), M.n.<BR>II A wind-instru-<BR>-ment: काहला,<BR>blew h.s:<BR>काहलाः पूरयाञ्चक्रुः, B.<BR>xiv. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hornbill
HORNBILL: perh. खट्वाङ्गः, “खट्वाङ्गान् लुब्धकांस्तथा”,<BR>Mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hornbook
HORNBOOK: प्रथमपाठः (?): v. Primer, hand-<BR>-book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horned
HORNED: शृङ्गिन् (f. णी).<BR>H. moon:<BR>सिनीवाली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hornet
HORNET:<BR>(1) वरटा;<BR>(2) विषशृङ्गिन् (m.)<BR>or<BR>विष-<BR>शूकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hornless
HORNLESS: शृङ्गहीनः (ना, नं) and sim. comp.s.<BR>H. deer:<BR>मुण्डिन् (m.). Bha.<BR>H. Bull:<BR>तूवरः<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horny
HORNY:<BR>I Lit.: शार्ङ्ग (f. ङ्गी).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>कठिनः (ना, नं): v. Hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horologe
HOROLOGE: कालसाधनयन्त्रम्, Su. iii. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horology
HOROLOGY: कालज्ञानम्, Su. xiii. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horoscope
HOROSCOPE:<BR>(1) जन्मपत्रिका (the table);<BR>(2)<BR>जन्मनक्षत्रम् (the sign).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horoscopy
HOROSCOPY:<BR>(1) होराशास्त्रम्, V.m.;<BR>(2) होरा-<BR>तन्त्रम्, Ja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horrible
HORRIBLE:<BR>I Dreadful: q.v.:<BR>(1) घोरः (रा,<BR> रं);<BR>(2) करालः (ला, लं).<BR>II Abominable:<BR>बीभत्स (f. त्सा), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horribly
HORRIBLY:<BR>(1) घोरम्;<BR>(2) करालम्: v. Dread-<BR>-fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horrid
HORRID:<BR>I Rough: q.v.<BR>II Hideous:<BR>q.v.<BR>III Disagreeable: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horridly
HORRIDLY: घोरम्: v. Dreadfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horridness
HORRIDNESS: घोरता: v. Also hideousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horrific
HORRIFIC: भैरवः (वी, वं): v. Terrific.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horrification
HORRIFICATION: रो(लो)महर्षः, -णम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horrify
HORRIFY: वि-त्रासयति (c. of त्रम्): v. To ter-<BR>-rify, horror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horror
HORROR:<BR>I A shaking: कम्पः, Sa.<BR>II The<BR>feelings: त्रासः, सं-, (= terror).<BR>III Dreari-<BR>-ness:<BR>(1) घोरता:<BR>(2) रौद्रता,<BR>the great h. of the<BR>funeral yard:<BR>महती श्मशानवाटस्यं रौद्रता, Ma. v.;<BR>(3) बीमत्सम्, बीभत्समेवाग्रे वर्तते, Ma. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horse
HORSE:<BR>I The animal:<BR>(1) अश्वः, h. -flesh:<BR>अश्वमांसम्, Bha.;<BR>one who knows the peculiarities<BR>of h. s:<BR>अश्वलाक्षणिकः, S., k.;<BR>the ceremony h.<BR>sacrifice:<BR>क्रतुरश्वमेधः, U. ii.; h. s of good breed:<BR>आजानेया अश्वाः, Mah. ii. 49. 9.;<BR>I am well up<BR>in breaking as well as in treating h. s:<BR>कृशलोऽ-<BR>स्म्यश्वशिक्षायां तथा चाश्वचिकित्सिते, Mah. iv. 3. 4.;<BR>(2) तुरगः,<BR>mounted on another h.:<BR>अन्यतुरगारूढः, K.;<BR>(3) तुरङ्गः, -मः,<BR>eight-h. d chariot:<BR>युक्ताष्टतुरङ्गो रथः,<BR>Ram. vi. 75. 27.;<BR>turned the h., moving the<BR>reins by the left hand:<BR>वामकरतलवलितरश्मिपाश-<BR>स्तुरङ्गमं व्यावर्तयामास, K.;<BR>a h. moving about with-<BR>out any control:<BR>उद्दामप्रचारी तुरङ्गमः, K. ii.<BR>(4) हयः,<BR>Sind h. of great speed:<BR>महारयः सिन्धुजो हयः, N. i.<BR>64. 6.;<BR>(5) वाहः, Arabian (?)<BR>h. s:<BR>वनायुदेशया<BR> वाहाः, R. v. 73.;<BR>(6) वाजिन् (m.), swift h.:<BR>जवनवाजी, R. ix. 56.;<BR>(7) घोटकः। Ph.:<BR>a white<BR>h.:<BR>कर्कः, A.;<BR>h. -neck:<BR>निगालः, A.<BR>II Cavalry:<BR>q.v.: अश्वाः<BR>or<BR>अश्व in comp.,<BR>these are the duties<BR>of h. and of infantry.:<BR>इत्यश्वकर्म पत्तेश्च, Ka. xix.<BR>5. Ph.:<BR>clothes -h.:<BR>*वस्त्रधारिणी; towel-h.:<BR>*गात्रमार्जनपटधरिणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

horseback
HORSEBACK: अश्वपृष्ठम्। Ph.:<BR>goes on h.:<BR>अश्वेन<BR> गच्छति, S.;<BR>seated on h.:<BR>तुरङ्गसादी, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

