HOSIERY: *पादावरणानि (n. pl.); पादावरणविक्रयः<BR>(the business).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hospitable
HOSPITABLE: आतिथेयः (या, यं),<BR>h. regard:<BR>आतिथे-<BR>यापचितिः, Ki. xi. 9.;<BR>the h. Pārvati:<BR>आतिथेयी<BR> पार्वती, Ku. v. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hospitably
HOSPITABLY: सादरम्, बहुमानपूर्वम्, etc. (= with<BR>attention).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hospital
HOSPITAL:<BR>(1) आरोग्यशाला, Raj.;<BR>(2) चिकित्सालयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hospitality
HOSPITALITY:<BR>(1) आतिथ्यम्<BR>or<BR>आतिथेयम्,<BR>then our h.<BR>is ready:<BR>ततः सज्जातिथेया वयम्, Vi. ii. 50.;<BR>did not<BR>cease to do h.:<BR>आतिथेयं कर्तु नाश्रमत्, Si. xiv. 35.;<BR>(2) अतिथिसत्कारः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

host
HOST:<BR>I An entertainer: no equiv.: expr.<BR>by गृहिन् (f. णी) (when the sense is clear);<BR>निमन्त्रयितृ (f. त्री) (= inviter); भोजनदातृ (f.<BR>त्री) (one who gives food).<BR>II A multitude:<BR>q.v.: सङ्घ।<BR>III The consecrated water<BR>वलिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

