HOUND ON: उत्तेजयति (तिज्, c. 10.): v. Excite,<BR>urge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hour
HOUR: होरा (very rare), Su. xii. 79.; gen.<BR>expr. by दण्डः<BR>or<BR>घटी<BR>or<BR>घटिका (= 24 minutes),<BR>Ph.: at all h. s.: i.e. always:<BR>(1) सदा;<BR>(2)<BR>सर्वदा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hour-angle
HOUR-ANGLE: नतम्, Su. iii. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hour-glass
HOUR-GLASS: घटीयन्त्रम्<BR>or<BR>घटिका, Gan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

houri
HOURI:<BR>(1) दिव्यङ्गना;<BR>(2) अप्सरस् (f.);<BR>(3)<BR>विद्याधरी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hourly
HOURLY (adj.): expr. by adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hourly
HOURLY (adv.):<BR>I Lit.: प्रतिदण्डम्।<BR>II Conti-<BR>-nually: q.v.: सदा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

house
HOUSE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) गृहम् (best equiv.:<BR>गृहाः in pl.=h. with its surroundings or<BR>inmates), to the h. of the chief of Vidarbha:<BR>गृहान् विदर्भाधिपतेः, N. xvi. 1.;<BR>where h. s shone as<BR>if with edges of thatches:<BR>गृहाणि निध्रैरिव यत्र रेजुः,<BR>Si. iii. 49.;<BR>(2) गेहम्,<BR>she is fortune in h.<BR>इयं गेहे<BR> लक्ष्मीः, U. i. 38.;<BR>the mistress of my h.:<BR>मद्रगेहिनी,<BR>Me. ii. 16.;<BR>(3) आ(अ)गरम्,<BR>our h.:<BR>अस्मदीयागारम्,<BR>Ma.;<BR>(4) कुलम् (rare),<BR>h. of god:<BR>देवकुलम्, Mr. ii.;<BR>(5) शरणम् (rare: prop=protection), h. of fire:<BR>अग्निशरणम्, Sa. iv.;<BR>(6) भवनम् (= building): v.<BR>Edifice;<BR>(7) निकेतनम् (= abode: q.v.);<BR>(8)<BR>आयतनम्: v. Temple.<BR>II Family, race: q.v.:<BR>गृहम्,<BR>is this becoming your h.:<BR>युक्तमेतद्वो गृहस्य, Vi.<BR>iv.<BR>III A firm: गृहम् (after Bengali).<BR>IV In<BR>chess: गृहम्।<BR>V A legislative body: समा,<BR>“to bring down the whole h.”:<BR>समग्रसभागृहम् (or<BR>श्रावकान्) आवर्जयति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

house
HOUSE (adj.): by comp.,<BR>h.-dog:<BR>गृहकुक्कुरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

house
HOUSE (v.):<BR>I To harbour: वासं ददाति [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">Page354</a>]<BR>(दा, c. 3.).<BR>II To shelter, store: गेहे रक्षति<BR>(रक्ष्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

house-breaker
HOUSE-BREAKER: कुड्यच्छेदिन् (f. नी): v.<BR>Burglar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

house-breaking
HOUSE-BREAKING: कुड्यच्छेदः: v. Burglary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

household
HOUSEHOLD (subs.):<BR>I Family:<BR>(1) परिजनः;<BR>(2) परिवारः।<BR>II Family life: expr. by गृहम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

house
HOUSE (adj.): expr. by comp.<BR>h. god:<BR>गृहदेवता;<BR>to perform h. affairs:<BR>गृहकार्याणि अनुतिष्ठति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

householder
HOUSEHOLDER:<BR>(1) गृहस्थः, H.;<BR>(2) गृहिन् (m.);<BR>(3) गृहपतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

housekeeper
HOUSEKEEPER:<BR>I Lit.: गृहिन् (f. णी).<BR>II A<BR>female servant: गृहजनाधिष्ठात्री (?), गृहरक्षिका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

housekeeping
HOUSEKEEPING: गृहरक्षा (??); गृहावेक्षणम् (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

house-leek
HOUSE-LEEK: कुतृणम्, Wilson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

houseless
HOUSELESS:<BR>(1) गृहहीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) अशरण<BR>(f. णा);<BR>(3) निराश्रयः (या, यं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

housemaid
HOUSEMAID: चेटी (= maid-servant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

house-pigeon
HOUSE-PIGEON: गृहकपोतः (f. ती, -तिका), U.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

house-rent
HOUSE-RENT: गृहभाटः, -कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

house-tax
HOUSE-TAX: गृहकरः (??); गृहशुल्कम् (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

house-warming
HOUSE-WARMING: गृहप्रवेशोत्सवः (?); वास्तूपशमनम्<BR>(a similar ceremony).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

housewife
HOUSEWIFE: गृहिणी,<BR>look up to hs.:<BR>गृहिणीनेत्राः,<BR>Ku. vi. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

housewifery
HOUSEWIFERY: गृहकार्यानुष्ठानम् (after D.); and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

housing
HOUSING:<BR>(1) आस्तरः, -णम्;<BR>(2) पृष्ठपटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hovel
HOVEL:<BR>(1) पर्णशाला;<BR>(2) कुटी, -रः;<BR>(3) उटजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hover
HOVER:<BR>I Lit.: perh. परिडीयते (डी, c. 4.).<BR>II Fig., to hang about: परितो विसर्पति<BR>(सृप्, c. 1.) (?); पर्यवेक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.) (= to<BR>look about).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoveringly
HOVERINGLY: expr. by pres. part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

how
HOW (adv.):<BR>I In what way:<BR>(1) कथम्,<BR>h. can a<BR>servant be without fault:<BR>कथं नु दासो निरपराधः,<BR>V.; h. (you) fell into the hands of the Chandal:<BR>कथं चण्डालहस्तगमनम्, K.;<BR>(2) केन प्रकारेण,<BR>teach me<BR>h. to make prostration:<BR>केन प्रकारेण दण्डप्रणामः<BR> कर्तव्यस्तन्मां शिक्षय, V.t. N.B.<BR>(1) In the last<BR>sense, h. is often not expr., you know (h.) to<BR>make (one)<BR>take:<BR>जानासि ग्राहयितुम्, K.;<BR>(2)<BR>sometimes expr. by किम् (= what), h. is<BR>(= what has happened to) Sāgarikā:<BR>सागरिकायाः किं वर्तते, Ra. iv.<BR>II To what<BR>degree: कियत्। N.B. For h. many, h. long, etc.:<BR>v. Many, long, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

howbeit
HOWBEIT: तथापि।: v. Nevertheless, yet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

howdah
HOWDAH: वरण्डः, -कः, Wilson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

however
HOWEVER (adv.):<BR>I In whatever way:<BR>(1)<BR>यथा यथा;<BR>(2) येन येन प्रकारेण<BR>II To whatever<BR>degree: expr. by super. and अपि, h. poor:<BR>अत्यन्तदरिद्रोऽपि (f. द्रापि);<BR>h. learned:<BR>पण्डित-<BR>वरिष्ठोऽपि;<BR>h. often:<BR>यावतो यावतो वारान्।<BR>III At<BR>least: अन्ततः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

however
HOWEVER (conj.):<BR>(1) परन्तु: v. But.;<BR>(2)<BR>तथापिः v. Yet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

howl
HOWL (subs.):<BR>(1) ची(चि)त्कृतम्;<BR>(2) आक्रन्दितम्;<BR>(3) चीत्कारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

howl
HOWL (v.):<BR>(1) ची(चि)त्कारं करोति;<BR>(2) आक्रन्दति<BR>(क्रन्द्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

howling
HOWLING (adj.):<BR>“h. wilderness”:<BR>निर्मानुषमरण्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

howsoever
HOWSOEVER: v. However.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoy
HOY: पोतः: v. Ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hoyden
HOYDEN: ग्राम्य (f. म्या): v. Rude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hubble-bubble
HUBBLE-BUBBLE: गुर्गुरिः (in Bengali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hubbus
HUBBUS: कोलाहलः: v. Tumult, uproar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

huckster
HUCKSTER (subs.): क्षुद्रपण्यविक्रयिकः, -विक्रेतृ (m.)<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

huckster
HUCKSTER (v.): क्षुद्रपण्यानि विक्रीणीते (क्री, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

huddle
HUDDLE (subs.): जनसंमर्दः (of person); सङ्करः<BR>(of thing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

huddle
HUDDLE (v.): i.e. h. together: perh. पिण्डी-<BR>करोति: v. Also to crowd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hue
HUE (subs.):<BR>I Colour: q.v.: रङ्गः।<BR>II A<BR>shouting,<BR>so when a h. and cry is raised after<BR>a thief, those who hear and do not run after him<BR>also share in his guilt:<BR>उत्क्रोशतां जनानान्तु ह्रियमाणे<BR> धने तथा । श्रुत्वा ये नाभिधावन्ति तेऽपि तद्दोषभागिनः॥,<BR>N.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

huff
HUFF (subs.):<BR>I Rage: q.v.: मन्युः।<BR>II A<BR>boaster: उत्सिक्तः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

huff
HUFF (v.): v. To swell, bully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hug
HUG (subs.): परिष्वङ्गः: v. Embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hug
HUG (v.): परिष्वजते (स्वञ्ज्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

huge
HUGE:<BR>(1) विशालः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) विपुलः (ला, लं);<BR>(3) महाप्रमाण (f. णा): v. Large, immense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hugely
HUGELY:<BR>(1) विशालम्;<BR>(2) विपुलम्: v. Largely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hugeness
HUGENESS:<BR>(1) विशालता;<BR>(2) विपुलता: v. Large-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hulk
HULK: जीर्णनौका। Ph.: to condemn to the h. s.:<BR>*पोतनिरोधम् आदिशति (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hull
HULL:<BR>I Of fruits: पुटः।<BR>II Of grain: तुषः।<BR>III Of a ship: expr. by पोतः<BR>or<BR>नौः or<BR>नौका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hum
HUM (subs.):<BR>I Buzz: q.v.: हुङ्कृ तम्,<BR>with the<BR>h. of bees:<BR>मधुलिहां हुङ्कृ तेन, K.<BR>II Of men:<BR>कलकलः।<BR>III A low murmur: हुङ्कारः, Sa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hum
HUM (v.):<BR>(1) हुङ्करोति;<BR>(2) गुञ्जति (जुञ्ज, c. 1.)<BR>(= to buzz).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hum
HUM (interj.): हुम्, हुं राक्षसः, Vi. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

human
HUMAN:<BR>(1) by comp.,<BR>in h. tongue:<BR>मनुष्यवाचा,<BR>R.;<BR>h. nature:<BR>मानुषता, K.: v. Man;<BR>(2)<BR>मानुषः (षी, षं),<BR>h. body:<BR>मानुषी तनुः, R. xvi. 22.;<BR>(3) मानवः (वी, वं)<BR>or-<BR>वीयः (या, यं), h. form:<BR>मानवं रूपम्, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humane
HUMANE: दयालु (mfn.): v. Kind, benevolent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humanely
HUMANELY: सदयम्: v. Kindly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humanity
HUMANITY:<BR>I Human nature:<BR>(1) मनुष्यता,<BR> -त्वम्;<BR>(2) मानुष्यम्।<BR>II Mankind: q.v.: मनुष्याः<BR>(m. pl.).<BR>III Humane feeling: दया: v.<BR>Kindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humanize
HUMANIZE: विनयति (नि, c. 1.): v. To civilize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humanly
HUMANLY: मनुष्यवत्,<BR>“H. speaking”:<BR>मनुष्यबुद्ध्पा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humble
HUMBLE (adj.):<BR>I Low, mean: q.v.: नीचः<BR>(चा, चं).<BR>II Small, modest: क्षुद्र (f. द्रा).<BR>Ph.: and where (my)<BR>h. intellect:<BR>क्व चाल्पविषया<BR> मतिः, R. i. 2.<BR>III Meek, not proud:<BR>(1)<BR>नम्र (f. म्रा), अव-;<BR>(2) निरभिमानः (ना, नं) and<BR>sim. comp.s.: v. Proud, not. Ph.: to eat h.<BR>pie (fig.:) अपमानं पुरस्करोति, मानं पृष्ठे करोति, J.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humble
HUMBLE (v.):<BR>(1) नमयति, अव-, (c. of नम्),<BR>h. s. his head to the foe of Namuchi:<BR>नमयति<BR> नमुचेररये शिरः, R.;<BR>h. ing the lofty:<BR>उन्नतान् नमयन्,<BR>K.;<BR>(2) नमस्करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humble-bee
HUMBLE-BEE:<BR>(1) भ्रमरः,<BR>honey of h. s.:<BR>भ्रामरं भधु;<BR>(2) भृङ्गः;<BR>(3) अलिः;<BR>(4) द्विरेफः;<BR>(5) शिलीमुखः<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humbleness
HUMBLENESS:<BR>I Lowness, meanness: q.v.:<BR>नीचता।<BR>II Humility: q.v.: नम्रता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humbling
HUMBLING (adj.): दर्पहरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) दर्पहः<BR>(हा, हं); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humbly
HUMBLY:<BR>(1) नम्रम्, अव-;<BR>(2) नीचैः (rare),<BR>R. v. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humbug
HUMBUG (subs.): प्रतारणा (= deception:<BR>q.v.) (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humbug
HUMBUG (v.): प्रतारयति (c. of तॄ): v. To<BR>deceive, fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humdrum
HUMDRUM: जडः (डा, डं): v. Dull, slow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humid
HUMID: सार्द्र (f. र्द्रा): v. Moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humidity
HUMIDITY: आर्द्रता: v. Moisture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humiliate
HUMILIATE: गर्व मनक्ति (मञ्ज, c. 7.), हरति (हृ,<BR>c. 1.), हन्ति (हन्, c. 2.) etc. (with gen.):<BR>v. Also to humble. H. ing (adj.): v.<BR>Humbling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humiliation
HUMILIATION:<BR>(1) अवमानना: v. Disgrace;<BR>(2)<BR>दर्पभङ्गः and sim. comp.s. (= breaking of<BR>pride).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humility
HUMILITY:<BR>(1) नम्रता, अव-, वि-;<BR>(2) निरभिमानता<BR>and sim. comp.s. (= want of pride);<BR>(3)<BR>विनयः (good breeding).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humming-bird
HUMMING-BIRD: मधुप्रियः (?) (comp. Assamese<BR>name).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humorous
HUMOROUS: Perh. सरसः (सा, सं); हासकरः<BR>(री, रं) (= laughable).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humorously
HUMOROUSLY: perh. सरसम्: v. Also jestingly,<BR>sportively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humour
HUMOUR (subs.):<BR>I Wit, h. ousness: रसिकता<BR>(?)<BR>II Disposition, temper:<BR>(1) मवः;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रकृतिः Ph.:<BR>he is in a bad h.:<BR>न प्रकृतिस्थः सः (?)<BR>III Whim: छन्दस् (n.).<BR>IV Fluid: रसः।<BR>Disorder (of the h.s of the body): दोषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humour
HUMOUR (v.):<BR>I To comply with the h. of: I<BR>will h. (our)<BR>master:<BR>अहं स्वामिनः चित्तवृत्तिमनुवर्तिष्ये<BR>(वृत् c. 1.), Sa. ii.;<BR>a fool by h. ing:<BR>मूर्ख<BR> छन्दोऽनुवृत्तेन, H. iv. 104.<BR>II To favour: q.v.:<BR>अभ्युपपद्यते (पद्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humourist
HUMOURIST: वैहासिकः (?); परिहासवेत्तृ (m.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

humoursome
HUMOURSOME: v. Capricious, whimsical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hump
HUMP:<BR>(1) गङुः;<BR>(2) ककुद् (f.) (of a bull).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hump-backed
HUMP-BACKED, HUMPED:<BR>(1) कृब्ज (f. ब्जा); [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">Page356</a>]<BR>(2) गडुरः (रा, रं)<BR>or<BR>गडुलः (ला, लं). H. bull:<BR>ककुह्मत् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hunch
HUNCH, HUNCHBACKED: v. Hump, hump-<BR>-backed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hundred
HUNDRED:<BR>I The numeral: शतम्,<BR>I will give<BR>you h. villages<BR>शतंः ग्रामान् प्रदास्यामि, A. r.;<BR>three<BR>h. years:<BR>अब्दशतानि त्रीणि,<BR>V p. iv. 24. 15.;<BR>h.<BR>times:<BR>शतवारान्;<BR>in a h. ways:<BR>शत्धा;<BR>by<BR>hundreds:<BR>शतशः;<BR>a h. thousand:<BR>लक्षम्।<BR>II A<BR>district: मण्डलम्। N.B.<BR>V s. has शताध्यक्षः =<BR>chief of h. (villages).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hundredth
HUNDREDTH (adj.): शततमः (मी, मं), h. part:<BR>शततमी कला, D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hundredth
HUNDREDTH (subs.):<BR>(1) शतांशः<BR>(2) शतभागः;<BR>(3) शततमो भागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hundredweight
HUNDREDWEIGHT: expr. by मणम् (= 2/3 of a<BR>cwt.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hunger
HUNGER (subs.):<BR>(1) क्षुधा,<BR>to allay h.:<BR>क्षुधाशान्तये,<BR>H.; (our)<BR>master is suffering from h.:<BR>स्वामी क्षुधया<BR> परिपीड्यते, P. i. 16.;<BR>(2) बुभुक्षा, I will eat this<BR>in (my)<BR>first h.:<BR>प्रथमबुभुक्षायामिदं खादामि, H.<BR>(3)<BR>क्षुध् (gen. in comp.),<BR>and in a moment h. and<BR>thirst of all went off.<BR>क्षुत्पिपासे च सर्वेषां क्षणेन व्यप-<BR>गच्छताम्, Mah. iii. 314.;<BR>(4) अशनाया (rare);<BR>(5) जिघसा (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hunger
HUNGER (v.):<BR>I Lit.: क्षुध्यति (क्षुध्, c. 4.),<BR>better by adj.<BR>II Fig.: क्षुध्यति (क्षुध्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hungry
HUNGRY, HUNGERED:<BR>(1) क्षुधितः (ता, तं),<BR>I am<BR>h., my life is going out:<BR>क्षुधितोऽहं गतप्राणः, Mah.;<BR>(2) बुमुक्षितः (ता, तं),<BR>the h. monkey:<BR>बुभुक्षितः<BR> कपिः, A.r.;<BR>(3) क्षुधार्त (f. र्ता), क्षुधाविष्ट (f. ष्टा),<BR>क्षुधापीडितः (ता, तं), etc.;<BR>you are h.:<BR>क्षुधलुर्भवान्,<BR>P. i. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hunt
HUNT (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: मृगयते (मृग्, c. 10.) or<BR>मृगयां करोति<BR>or<BR>चरति (चर्, c. 1.), Ram.<BR>II<BR>Fig.: मृगयते, a gem does not seek, but it is h. ed:<BR>न रत्नमन्विष्यति मृग्यते हि तत्, Sa.: v. To<BR>search.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hunt
HUNT, HUNTING (subs.):<BR>(1) मृगया,<BR>there is<BR>nothing so beneficial as h.<BR>यथा मृगया ह्यौपकारिकी न<BR> तथान्यत्, D. viii.; to go out (for)<BR>h.:<BR>मृगयां याति,<BR>Mah.;<BR>devoted to h.:<BR>मृगयाशीलः (ला, लं), Sa.<BR>ii.;<BR>(2) आखेटः, -कः,<BR>deer. h.:<BR>हरिणाखेट्कः, K. s.<BR>ix. 74.;<BR>(3) मृगव्यम् (rare),<BR>h.-forest:<BR>मृगव्यसत्रम्,<BR>Ki. xiii. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hunter
HUNTER:<BR>I One who hunts:<BR>(1) व्याधः<BR>(= professional h.);<BR>(2) मृगयुः (rare:) of<BR>more gen. application).<BR>II A hunting<BR>horse: वाजिन् (m.), R. ix. 56. (?): v. Horse.<BR>III A hound: मृगयाकुक्कुरः; आखेटिकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hunting-box
HUNTING-BOX, HUNTING-SEAT: मृगयास्थली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

huntsman
HUNTSMAN:<BR>I A hunter: q.v.<BR>II A<BR>servant: मृगयापुरुषः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurdle
HURDLE: *काष्ठबन्धः<BR>or<BR>काष्ठरोघः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurl
HURL (v.):<BR>(1) क्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.): v. To cast,<BR>throw;<BR>(2) पातयति (c. of पत्) (= to cause<BR>to fall).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurl
HURL (subs.):<BR>I A cast: q.v.: क्षेपः।<BR>II<BR>Tumult: q.v.: तुमुलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurling
HURLING (subs.): a game: perh. कन्दुकक्षेपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurly-burly
HURLY-BURLY: तुमुलम्: v. Tumult, confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurra
HURRA, HURRAH: जयध्वनिः। and sim, comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurricane
HURRICANE:<BR>(1) भ्कष्भ्का,-निलः। and sim. comp.s.,<BR>a violent h. blew:<BR>महाबलो भष्क्भ्कावातो ववौ, Mah.<BR>i. 149. 2.;<BR>(2) प्रभञ्जनः, H.;<BR>(3) चण्डवातः,<BR> जवानिलः, etc. (any strong gale).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurried
HURRIED (adj.):<BR>(1) त्वरितः (ता, तं) (= hasty:<BR>q.v.);<BR>(2) त्वराविभ्रान्त (f. न्ता) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurriedly
HURRIEDLY:<BR>(1) त्वरितम्: v. Hastily;<BR>(2)<BR>ससम्भ्रमम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurry
HURRY (v. i.): त्वरते (त्वर्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>hasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurry
HURRY (v. t.): त्वरयति (c. of त्वर्): v. To<BR>Hasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurry
HURRY (subs.):<BR>I Haste: q.v.: त्वरा।<BR>II<BR>Bustle: सम्भ्रमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurry-skurry
HURRY-SKURRY (adv.):<BR>(1) अस्तव्यस्तम्;<BR>(2)<BR>ससम्भ्रमम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurrying
HURRYING (subs.): “there was h. to and fro”:<BR>जना धावन्तोऽतस्ततः: v. Also haste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurt
HURT (subs.):<BR>(1) क्षतम्,<BR>causing of h.<BR>क्षतदर्शन,<BR>N.s.; व्रणम् (= wound: q.v.);<BR>(2) दुःखम्<BR>(= pain: q.v.),<BR>to cause h. without drawing<BR>blood:<BR>शोणितेन विना दुःखमुत्पादयति, V. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurt
HURT (v. t.):<BR>(1) पीडयति (पीड्, c. 10.): v. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=357" target="_blank">Page357</a>]<BR>pain;<BR>(2) क्षिणोति (क्षि, c. 5.): v. To injure;<BR>(3) तुदति (तुद्, c. 6.), then the enemy h. (him)<BR>with sharp words:<BR>वाक्सायकैरथ तुतोद तदा विपक्षः,<BR>Si. xx. 77.;<BR>(4) by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurtful
HURTFUL:<BR>(1) पीडाकरः (री, रं),<BR>h. thing:<BR>पीडाकरं<BR> द्रव्यम्, V. s.;<BR>(2) हिंस्र (f. स्ना) (not of things):<BR>v. Injurious, mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurtfully
HURTFULLY: v. Injuriously, mischievously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurtfulness
HURTFULNESS:<BR>(1) पीडाकरता;<BR>(2) हिंस्रता;<BR>(3)<BR>better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hurtle
HURTLE: संघट्टते (घट्ट्, c. 1.): v. To clash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

husband
HUSBAND (subs.):<BR>(1) पतिः,<BR>get a h. who will<BR>not take to others:<BR>अनन्यभाजं पतिमाप्नुहि, Ku.<BR>iii. 63.;<BR>who had h. s and children:<BR>याः पतिपुत्रवत्यः,<BR>Ku. viii. 6.;<BR>(2) भर्तृ (m.),<BR>will choose a<BR>second h.:<BR>भर्तारं द्वितीयं वरयिष्यति, Mah.;<BR>(3)<BR>स्वामिन् (m.), but you (are my)<BR>h.:<BR>किन्तु स्वामी त्वम्,<BR>H.;<BR>(4) परिणेतृ (m.), Sa;<BR>(5) उपयन्तृ (m.), R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

husband
HUSBAND (v.): वाहयति (c. of वहृ): v. To use,<BR>till.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

husbandman
