HYPOTHESIS: अनुभवः (??); अनुमानम् (= inference).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hypothetic
HYPOTHETIC, -AL: अनुमवसिद्ध (f. द्धा)<BR>or<BR>-गृहीतः<BR>(ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hypothetically
HYPOTHETICALLY: अनुभवेन<BR>or<BR>अनुभवपूर्वकम् (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hyssop
HYSSOP: *हिशोकः; ओषधिभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hysteria
HYSTERIA, HYSTERICS: हर्षमूर्च्छा (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

hysteric
HYSTERIC, -AL; हर्षभूर्च्छालः (ला, लं) (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

i
I: अहम्। N.B. Not expr. when the meaning is<BR>clear,<BR>I am coming:<BR>अयमागतोऽस्मि, Mr. ix.;<BR>I<BR>do not know:<BR>न जाने, H.; I am going now:<BR>गम्यतेऽधुना, U.,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

iambic
IAMBIC, LAMBUS:<BR>(1) आदिलधुर्द्विकः;<BR>(2) ध्वजम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ibex
IBEX: पार्वतीयो छागः<BR>or<BR>अजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ibis
IBIS: पक्षिभेदः; क्रौञ्चः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ice
ICE (subs.):<BR>(1) हिमघनः;<BR>(2) तुषारसङ्घातः, Ku.<BR>v. 35.; and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ice
ICE (v.): no equiv.: हिमीकरोति (?); तुषारी-<BR>करोति (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

iceberg
ICEBERG: *हिमघनसंहतिः; हिमसंघातक्षेत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ice-cold
ICE-COLD:<BR>(1) हिमशुतलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) तुषार-<BR>शिशिरः (रा, रं), K.;<BR>(3) निहारनिभः (भा, भं),<BR>N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ice-house
ICE-HOUSE: हिमगृहभ् may do; *हिमघनकोष्ठः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ichneumon
ICHNEUMON:<BR>(1) नकुलः:<BR>(2) बभ्रुः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ichor
ICHOR: of elephants:<BR>(1) भदः;<BR>(2) दानम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

icicle
ICICLE: *हिमघनकणः, -णिका। N.B. Not तुषारकणः<BR>=dew-drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

iconoclast
ICONOCLAST: प्रतिमापोथकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

icy
ICY:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by comp. or<BR>II Ice-cold:<BR>q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idea
IDEA:<BR>I Conception: बुद्धिः,<BR>under the i. of a<BR>tiger:<BR>व्याघ्रबुद्ध्पा।<BR>To have an i.:<BR>सम्भावयति (c. of<BR>भू).<BR>II Opinion: q.v.: मतम्।<BR>III A<BR>thought: मावः, -ना।<BR>IV Platonic: perh.<BR>कल्पना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ideal
IDEAL:<BR>I Mental: q.v.: मानसिकः (की, कं).<BR>II Conceived in the mind, visionary:<BR>काल्पनिकः (की, कं).<BR>III Perfect, best: expr.<BR>by परमः (मा, मं),<BR>i. form of virtue:<BR>परमधर्म-<BR>लक्षणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idealism
IDEALISM: perh. बाह्यशून्यम्, -वादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idealist
IDEALIST: बाह्यशून्यवादिन् (f. नी) (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ideally
IDEALLY: मनसा (= in mind): v. Ideal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

identical
IDENTICAL:<BR>he is the i. person:<BR>स एवैषः: v.<BR>Same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

identification
IDENTIFICATION: v. To identify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

identify
IDENTIFY:<BR>I To make to be the the same:<BR>मिथुनीकरोति (= to couple), S.; and sim.<BR>verbs.<BR>II To prove to be same: expr. by<BR>circumlo.,<BR>to i. stolen property:<BR>लोप्त्रमेवैतदिति<BR> प्रदर्शयति (c. of दृश्,)<BR>or<BR>प्रतिपादयति (c. of पद्):<BR>v. Also to recognize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

identity
IDENTITY:<BR>I Sameness: q.v.: ऐक्यम्।<BR>II<BR>The condition of being identical: expr. by<BR>adj.,<BR>to prove the i. of an offender:<BR>सोऽपराध्येव एष<BR> इति प्रतिपादयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ides
IDES: in Roman calendar: *मध्यदिनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idiocy
IDIOCY: जडता<BR>or<BR>जाड्यम्: v. Also foolishness,<BR>insanity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idiom
IDIOM: *वाकपद्धतिः, रीतिः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idiomatic
IDIOMATIC: expr. by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idiomatically
IDIOMATICALLY: *वाक्पद्धत्यनुसारेण, रीतिक्रमेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idiosyncrasy
IDIOSYNCRASY: व्यक्तिगतो भावः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idiot
IDIOT: जडः (डा, डं): v. Also foolish, mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idiotcy
IDIOTCY: जडता<BR>or<BR>जाड्यम्: v. Also foolishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idiotic
IDIOTIC: expr. by comp. or gen.: v. Also<BR>foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idle
IDLE (adj.):<BR>I Vain, useless: q.v.: निरर्थकः<BR>(का, कं).<BR>II Lazy, inactive: q.v.: अलसः<BR>(सा, सं) like the action of an i. (man): अलसस्य<BR> यथा कार्यम्। Vi. vi. 2.<BR>III Unemployed: q.v.<BR>अव्यापृतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idle
IDLE (v.): i.e. i. away: क्षपयति (c. of क्षै):<BR>v. To waste, spend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idleness
IDLENESS:<BR>I Laziness, inactivity:<BR>(1) आलस्यम्;<BR>(2) अलसता।<BR>II Uselessness: q.v.: निरर्थक्रता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idler
IDLER: अलसः: v. Also lazy, sluggard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idly
IDLY:<BR>I Vain: q.v.: निरर्थकम्।<BR>II Lazily:<BR>आलस्येन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idol
IDOL:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्रतिमा,<BR>oh. a wooden i.; no, no,<BR>of stone:<BR>कथं काष्ठप्रतिमा, न न शैलप्रतिमा, Mr. ii.;<BR>i. of the goddes (Durgā): देवीप्रतिमा, A. p.;<BR>(2) मूर्तिः (= form; when the sense is clear);<BR>(3) विग्रहः (rare);<BR>(4) शालग्रामः (of Viṣṇu),<BR>A. p.;<BR>(5) लिङ्गम् (of Śiva).<BR>II Fig.: perh.<BR>देवता; better by आराधयति (c. of राध्) (= to<BR>worship).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idolater
IDOLATER:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) देवपूजकः;<BR>(2) प्रतिमा-<BR>पूजकः (?).<BR>II Fig.: आराधयितृ (m.): v.<BR>Adorer, worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idolatrous
IDOLATROUS:<BR>I Lit.: by comp. i. worship:<BR>प्रतिमापूजा।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>i. veneration:<BR>परममक्तिः:<BR>v. Excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idolatry
IDOLATRY:<BR>(1) प्रतिमापूजा (?);<BR>(2) देवोपासना (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idolize
IDOLIZE: देववत् पूजयति (पूज्, c. 10.), आराधयति<BR>(c. of राध्), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

idyl
IDYL, IDYLL: गीतकाव्यम् (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

if
IF:<BR>(1) यदि,<BR>if you are not delighted with the<BR>tremulous glances.......:<BR>लोलापाङ्गैर्यदि न रमसे, Me.;<BR>if so, I am fortunate:<BR>यद्येवं दद्धन्योऽहम्, P.;<BR>or if you<BR>again get your place:<BR>त्वयाथवा यदि लब्धं पुनरात्मनः<BR> पदम्, Ki.;<BR>even if his union was doubtful:<BR>सन्दि-<BR>ग्धोऽप्यस्य समागमो यदि स्यात्, K.; if (he)<BR>had not<BR>wagered:<BR>यदि पणं नाकरिष्यत्, V.; then again if<BR>.....: पुनरपरं यदि, K.;<BR>(2) चेत् (never at the<BR>beginning of a sentence),<BR>if not:<BR>नो चेत्, H.<BR>v. Otherwise;<BR>if on the other hand, you are<BR>waiting for time:<BR>अथ चेदवधिः प्रतीक्ष्यते, Ki.;<BR>but<BR>if I could not find out some means here:<BR>अपि तु न<BR> चेदिह कमप्युपायमुद्भावयितुं शक्नुयाम्, D. N.B. Note<BR>the use of विधिलिङ् when the sentence implies<BR>that something may or might happen and of ऌङ्<BR>when it implies that something would have happe-<BR>ned.<BR>लट्, लुट् and ऌट् are used when it deals<BR>with facts actual or assumed, the first with<BR>present and the last two with future facts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

igneous
IGNEOUS:<BR>(1) आग्ने यः (यी, यं);<BR>(2) वह्रिमयः (यी,<BR> यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ignis-fatuus
IGNIS-FATUUS: भूतदीपिका (?); भूतालोकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ignite
IGNITE:<BR>I Trans: ज्वलयति (c. of ज्वल्): v.<BR>To kindle.<BR>II Intrans:<BR>(1) ज्वलति (ज्वल्,<BR>c. 1.);<BR>(2) समिध्यते (pass. of इन्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ignition
IGNITION:<BR>(1) ज्वलनम्;<BR>(2) इन्धनम्, सम्-;<BR>(3)<BR>दीपनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ignoble
IGNOBLE: नीचः (चा, चं): v. Mean, base,<BR>low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ignobly
IGNOBLY: expr. by adj.: v. Also meanly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ignominious
IGNOMINIOUS: यशोघ्न (f. घ्नी): v. Infamous,<BR>shameful, base.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ignominy
IGNOMINY:<BR>(1) निकृतिः,<BR>did not bear the i. of<BR>being removed from the front seat:<BR>साग्रासनापनयजा<BR> निकृतिर्न सोढा, Mu. iv. ii.;<BR>(2) न्यक्कारः, Vi. v.<BR>22.: v. Disgrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ignoramus
IGNORAMUS:<BR>(1) अज्ञः;<BR>(1) निर्बोधः: v. Fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ignorance
IGNORANCE:<BR>I Absol.: अज्ञानम्।<BR>II In special<BR>subjects: अनमिञ्जता,<BR>i. of algebra:<BR>बीजानभिञ्जता।<BR>Ph.:<BR>I will keep her in i. of it:<BR>न तामेतदभिञ्जां<BR> करोमि: v. Also to conceal; to be in i. of:<BR>अनभिञ्ज (f. ञ्जा) (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ignorant
IGNORANT (adj.):<BR>I Destitute of knowledge:<BR>(1) अञ्ज (f. ञ्जा);<BR>(2) अबोध (f. धा);<BR>(3) ञ्जानहीनः<BR>(ना, नं), विद्याविहीनः (ना, नं), and sim. comp.s;<BR>(4) अपण्डित (f. ता), अविद्वस् (f. दुषी), etc.<BR>(= not learned).<BR>II Unacquainted:<BR>(1) अनभिञ्ज (f. ञ्जा) or occ. अञ्ज (f. ञ्ज);<BR>(2)<BR>by verb: v. Know, not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ignorantly
IGNORANTLY:<BR>(1) अञ्जानतः;<BR>(2) अञ्जानात्;<BR>(3)<BR>अञ्जानेन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ignore
IGNORE (v): न स्वीकरोति: v. To admit, not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

iguana
IGUANA:<BR>(1) गोधा<BR>or<BR>गोधिका;<BR>(2) गौधेयः (रः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

iliac
ILIAC:<BR>i. passion:<BR>उदावर्तः, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill
ILL:<BR>I Bad: q.v.: expr. by दुर्-<BR>or<BR>अ- in<BR>comp.,<BR>i. health:<BR>असुस्थता।<BR>II In ill health:<BR>(1) असुस्थशरीरः (रा, रं), Kādambari, who is very i.:<BR>बलवदसुस्थशरीरा कादभ्बरी, K.;<BR>(2) असुस्थ<BR>or<BR>अस्वस्थ<BR>(f. स्था);<BR>(3) पीडितः,<BR>i. with fever:<BR>ज्वरपीडितः<BR>(ता, तं): v. Also sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill
ILL (subs.):<BR>(1) अनिष्टम्;<BR>(2) अशुभभ्, अमङ्गलम्,<BR>etc.,<BR>crying i. of the boy:<BR>वत्सस्य मङ्गलविरुद्धं रटन्,<BR>Vi. iii. 31.;<BR>(3) पापम्,<BR>to wish i.:<BR>पापं वाञ्छति,<BR>Vi. ii. 50.: v. Also calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill
ILL (adv.): expr. by adj. or subs: v. Also<BR>badly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill- advised
ILL- ADVISED (adj.): expr. by न सम्यगालोच्य or<BR>विविच्य,<BR>i. action:<BR>अविवेककर्मन्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-affected
ILL-AFFECTED:<BR>I Disaffected: q.v.: विरक्तः<BR>(क्ता, क्तं).<BR>II III-disposed: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illative
ILLATIVE:<BR>(1) आनुमानिकः (की, कं);<BR>(2) आनुष-<BR>ङ्गिकः (की, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-behaved
ILL-BEHAVED:<BR>(1) दुःशीलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) दुराचारः<BR>(रा, रं);<BR>(3) दुर्वृत्त (f. त्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-blood
ILL-BLOOD: द्वेषः, वि-,: v. Enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-bred
ILL-BRED:<BR>(1) दुर्विनीतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) अविनीतः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(3) अशिष्ट (f. ष्टा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-breeding
ILL-BREEDING:<BR>(1) अविनयः;<BR>(2) अशिष्टता;<BR>(3)<BR>अभद्रता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-disposed
ILL-DISPOSED:<BR>(1) दुष्टबुद्धि (mfn.);<BR>(2) पापबुद्धि<BR>(mfn.,) etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illegal
ILLEGAL: *अवैधः (धी, धं); विधिविरुद्ध्व (f. द्धा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illegally
ILLEGALLY: *विधीन् अतिर्क्रम्य, प्रमथ्य, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illegibility
ILLEGIBILITY:<BR>(1) expr. by adj.:<BR>(2) दुर्वाच्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illegible
ILLEGIBLE:<BR>(1) न सुपठः (ठा, ठं);<BR>(2) दुर्वाच्य<BR>(f. च्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illegibly
ILLEGIBLY:<BR>(1) by adj.;<BR>(2) अस्पष्टाक्षरैः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illegitimate
ILLEGITIMATE:<BR>I Illegal: q.v.:<BR>II Illogical:<BR>अन्याय्य (f. य्या).<BR>III Bastard: q.v.: विजन्मन्<BR>(mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illegitimately
ILLEGITIMATELY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-fated
ILL-FATED: अभागः (गा, गं): v. Unlucky, un-<BR>-happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-favoured
ILL-FAVOURED: कदाकारः (रा, रं): v. Ugly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-gotten
ILL-GOTTEN:<BR>(1) अन्यायार्जितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2)<BR>अन्यायलब्ध (f. ब्धा), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illiberal
ILLIBERAL:<BR>(1) अनुदारः (रा, रं) (rare);<BR>(2)<BR>कृपण (f. णा): v. Niggardly, mean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illiberality
ILLIBERALITY:<BR>(1) अनौदार्यम् (rare);<BR>(2) कृपणता<BR>or<BR>कार्पव्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illiberally
ILLIBERALLY:<BR>(1) expr. by adj.:<BR>(2) कार्पण्येन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illicit
ILLICIT: निषिद्ध<BR>or<BR>प्रतिषिद्ध (f. द्धा) (= forbidden),<BR>V. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illicitly
ILLICITLY: expr. by adj.: v. Also illegally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illimitable
ILLIMITABLE, ILLIMITED:<BR>(1) निरवधि (mfn.);<BR>(2) असीमः (मा, मं): v. Also endless, infinite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illiterate
ILLITERATE: अशिक्षितः (ता, तं): v. Ignorant (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-matched
ILL-MATCHED: न तुलाधृतः (ता, तं), Vi. vi.: v.<BR>Unequal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-natured
ILL-NATURED:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) दुष्प्रकृति (mfn.);<BR>(2) वक्रस्वभावः (वा, वं).<BR>II Mischievous: दुष्टः<BR>(ष्टा, ष्टं).<BR>III Of land: दोषवत् (f. ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-naturedly
ILL-NATUREDLY:<BR>(1) दुष्प्रकृत्या;<BR>(2) वक्रस्वमावतया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illness
ILLNESS:<BR>(1) असुस्थता (gen. i.);<BR>(2) पीडा: v.<BR>Discease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illogical
ILLOGICAL:<BR>(1) अन्याय्य (f. य्या);<BR>(2) न्याय-<BR>विरुद्ध (f. द्धा);<BR>(3) अयुक्तिसिद्ध (f. द्धा); etc.<BR>Ph.;<BR>i. conclusion:<BR>अपसिद्धान्तः, N. d. v. 2. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illogically
ILLOGICALLY: न न्यायानुसारेण<BR>or<BR>न्यायक्रमेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-omened
ILL-OMENED: अशुभः (भा, भं): v. Mischievous,<BR>omen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-starred
ILL-STARRED:<BR>(1) दुर्दैवः (वा, वं);<BR>(2) दैवोपहतः<BR>(ता, तं), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-temper
ILL-TEMPER:<BR>(1) कोपनता;<BR>(2) क्रोधशीलता;<BR>(3)<BR>चण्डस्वभावः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-tempered
ILL-TEMPERED:<BR>(1) कोपनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) क्रोध-<BR>शीलः (ला, लं);<BR>(3) चण्ड (f. ण्डा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-timed
ILL-TIMED: अकाल-कल्पितः (ता, तं) (= planned),<BR>विहितः (ता, तं) (= done), -उदितः (ता, तं)<BR>(= said), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-trained
ILL-TRAINED:<BR>(1) अशिक्षितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) अप-<BR>शिक्षितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ill-treat
ILL-TREAT: खलीकरोति: v. To maltreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illude
ILLUDE: विप्रलभेते (लभ्, c. 1.): v. To deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illume
ILLUME, ILLUMINE:<BR>(1) द्योतयति, उत्-, (c. of<BR>द्युत्);<BR>(2) भासयति (c. of भास्): v. To<BR>light (III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illuminate
ILLUMINATE:<BR>I To illumine: q.v.<BR>II To<BR>adorn with lights: दीर्पैः उद्भासयति (c. of<BR>mas).<BR>III of manuscripts: रञ्जयति (c. of<BR>रञ्ज्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illumination
ILLUMINATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) द्योतनम्, प्र-;<BR>(2) उद्भासनम्;<BR>(3) दीपनम्।<BR>II Festive decora-<BR>-tion: दीपालिः (the i. festival).<BR>III Decoration<BR>of manuscripts: पत्रञ्जनम्।<BR>IV Brightness,<BR>splendour: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illuminator
ILLUMINATOR: of manuscripts: पत्ररञ्जकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illusion
ILLUSION: माया,<BR>is this an i. or is it delusion of<BR>my mind:<BR>माया स्विदेषा मतिविम्रमो वा, Ki. xvi. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illusive
ILLUSIVE, ILLUSORY:<BR>(1) मिथ्या in comp.: v.<BR>False;<BR>(2) असारः (रा, रं) (= unsubstantial).<BR>Ph.:<BR>i. show:<BR>माया,<BR>i. clouds:<BR>मायामेघमाला, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illustrate
ILLUSTRATE:<BR>(1) स्फुटीकरोति;<BR>(2) उदाहरति (हृ,<BR>c. 1.): v. To exemplify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illustration
ILLUSTRATION:<BR>I The act.: expr. by verb:<BR>v. Also elucidation, explanation.<BR>II<BR>Example: q.v.: उदाहरणम्, here in the first i.:<BR>अत्राद्योदाहरणे,, KUV.;<BR>i. s in order:<BR>क्रमेणोदाहरणम्,<BR>Kav.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illustrative
ILLUSTRATIVE: expr. by verb or subs.,<BR>it is i.<BR>of this:<BR>तदेतत् स्फुटीकरोति<BR>or<BR>तस्योदाहरणमेतत्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illustrious
ILLUSTRIOUS:<BR>(1) महायशस् (mfn.); पुण्यश्लोकः<BR>(का, कं); v. Famous, renowned, celebra-<BR>-ted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

illustriously
ILLUSTRIOUSLY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

image
IMAGE (subs.):<BR>I Likeness: q.v.: Ph.: this<BR>boy is the very i. (of Rāma): [रामस्य] सम्पूण प्रति-<BR>विम्बितैव निखिलास्मिन् शिशावाकृतिः, U. iv. 21.<BR>II<BR>An idol: q.v.:<BR>(1) प्रतिमा,<BR>i. -worship:<BR>प्रतिमा-<BR>पूजा;<BR>(2) मूर्तिः,<BR>how many varieties of i. s.:<BR>कति<BR> मूर्तिभेदाः, Li. 241.<BR>III Reflected i.:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रतिबिम्बम्;<BR>(2) छाया (= shadow).<BR>IV Show,<BR>appearance: q.v.<BR>V Mental: कल्पना।<BR>VI<BR>Rhetorical: perh. चित्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

image
IMAGE (v.):<BR>I To reflect: q.v.<BR>II Mentally:<BR>कल्पयति (c. of कॢप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imagery
IMAGERY:<BR>I Images: चित्राणि (n. pl.)<BR>II<BR>Appearance: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imaginable
IMAGINABLE: सं-भाव्य (f. व्या)<BR>or<BR>मावनीयाः (या,<BR> यं): v. To imagine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imaginary
IMAGINARY: काल्पनिकः (की, कं); v. Also false.<BR>Ph.:<BR>i. quantity:<BR>काल्पनिकराशिः (?); करणी<BR>(= Surd).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imagination
IMAGINATION:<BR>(1) मावना, सं-, or rarely भावः,<BR>what can be sketched by i.:<BR>सम्मावनयोत्प्रेक्ष्य (f.<BR>क्ष्या), M. n.;<BR>(2) कल्पना (= mental creation);<BR>(3) चिन्ता (= thought),<BR>like a poet's mind<BR>agitated with many hundreds of self-created i. s:<BR>स्वयमुत्पादितानेकचिन्ताशताकुला कविमतिरिव, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imaginative
IMAGINATIVE: expr. by comp.s.; i. power:<BR>कल्पनाशक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imagine
IMAGINE:<BR>I To conceive: q.v.: सं-भावयति<BR>(c. of भू).<BR>II To think: q.v.: भावयति,<BR> वि-।<BR>III To contrive: q.v.: कल्पयति (कॢप्,)<BR>c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imbalm
IMBALM, IMBANK, etc.: v. Embalm, embank,<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imbecile
IMBECILE:<BR>I Weak: q.v.: दुर्बलः (ला, लं).<BR>Idiotic: जडमति (mfn.): v. Also foolish,<BR>childish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imbecility
IMBECILITY:<BR>I Weakness: q.v.: दौर्बल्यम्।<BR>II<BR>II Of mind:<BR>(1) बुद्धिमान्द्यम्;<BR>(2) बालिश्यम्<BR>(= childishness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imbibe
IMBIBE:<BR>I To drink in, absorb: q.v.: नि-<BR>पिवति (पा, c. 1.).<BR>II To contract, acquire:<BR>q.v.: अधिगच्छति (गम्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imbitter
IMBITTER, IMBLAZON, IMBODY, IMBOLDEN: V.<BR>Embitter, emblazon, embody, embolden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imbosom
IMBOSOM: क्रोडीकरोति<BR>or<BR>क्रोडे करोतिः v. Also to<BR>embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imbrue
IMBRUE:<BR>(1) आर्द्रोकरोतिः v. Wet;<BR>(2) लिम्पति<BR>(लिप्, c. 6.): v. Anoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imbue
IMBUE: रञ्जयति, अमि-, (रञ्ज्,) c. 10.) (lit. and<BR>fig.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imitable
IMITABLE: अनुकरणीयः (या, यं)<BR>or<BR>अनुकार्य (f. र्या);<BR>better by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imitate
IMITATE:<BR>(1) अनुकरोति<BR>or<BR>कुरुते (कृ, c. 8.),<BR>men<BR>i. the sound of peacock:<BR>पुरुषो मयूरवासितमनुकरोति,<BR>N. d.;<BR>for artists i. work after seeing:<BR>दृष्ट्वा<BR> क्रियामनुकरोति शिल्पिवर्गः, Mr. ix. 33.;<BR>(2) अनु-<BR>विदधाति<BR>or<BR>धत्ते (धा, c. 3.), Ki. ix. 10.;<BR>(3)<BR>अनुवदति (वद्, c. 1.) (in speaking): v. To<BR>follow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imitation
IMITATION: अनुकरणम्<BR>or<BR>अनुक्रिया (both of the act<BR>and of the thing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imitative
IMITATIVE:<BR>I Inclined to imitate:<BR>(1) अनु-<BR>करणशीलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) अनुकरणप्रियः (या, यं);<BR>etc.<BR>II Formed after a model: expr. by<BR>अनुकरणम्,<BR>“was i. of the first”:<BR>प्रथमस्यानुकरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imitator
IMITATOR:<BR>(1) अनुकारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) अनुकारक<BR>(f. रिका) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immaculate
IMMACULATE:<BR>(1) निष्कलङ्क (f. ङ्का);<BR>(2) निर्मलः<BR>(ला, लं); v. Pure, unstained, unblemi-<BR>-shed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immaculately
IMMACULATELY:<BR>(1) निष्कलङ्कम्;<BR>(2) निर्मलम्;<BR>(3) शुद्धम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immaterial
IMMATERIAL:<BR>I Incorporeal: q.v.: अमूर्त (f.<BR>र्ता).<BR>II Unmimporatant: q.v.:<BR>(1) अकिञ्चित्करः<BR>(री, रं);<BR>(2) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immateriality
IMMATERIALITY:<BR>(1) अमूर्तता;<BR>(2) अदेहवत्ता;<BR>(3)<BR>अशरीरता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immaterially
IMMATERIALLY: निरर्थकम्; v. (In) vain; (for)<BR>nothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immature
IMMATURE:<BR>(1) अपक (f. क्वा);<BR>(2) अपरिपक्व<BR>(f. क्वा);<BR>(3) अपरिणत (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immaturity
IMMATURITY:<BR>(1) अपक्वता;<BR>(2) अपरिपाकः;<BR>(3)<BR>अपरिणामः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immeasurable
IMMEASURABLE:<BR>(1) अर्मयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) अपरि-<BR>मेयः (या, यं);<BR>(3) अप्रमेयः (या, यं);<BR>(4) अपरि-<BR>मितः (ता, तं), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immeasurably
IMMEASURABLY:<BR>(1) निरतिशयम् (= exceedingly);<BR>(2) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immediate
IMMEDIATE:<BR>I Proximate, close:<BR>(1) अनन्तरः<BR>(रा, रं);<BR>(2) अव्यवहितः (ता, तं).<BR>II Instant:<BR>expr. by adv.<BR>III Acting or cognized<BR>directly: perh अव्यवहितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immediately
IMMEDIATELY:<BR>I Proximately:<BR>(1) अनन्तरम्;<BR>(2) अव्यवहितम्।<BR>II Instantly: q.v.<BR>(1) सद्यः;<BR>(2) सपदि। Ph.:<BR>i. after or on:<BR>अनन्तरमेव; i. on<BR>(his)<BR>saying:<BR>वचनान्तरमेव, K.: v. Also as<BR>soon as.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immedicable
IMMEDICABLE: अचिकित्स्य (f. त्स्या): v. Incura-<BR>-ble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immemorial
IMMEMORIAL:<BR>i. time:<BR>अस्मार्तकालः, Mi.;<BR>i.<BR>custom:<BR>शश्वतः (or पारम्पर्यागतः, K. b.) आचारः। M.<BR>i. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immense
IMMENSE<BR>I Excessive: q.v.: अत्यन्त (f. अन्ता).<BR>II Vast, infinite: q.v.: अनन्तः (न्ता,<BR> न्तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immensely
IMMENSELY:<BR>(1) अत्यन्तम्: v. Exceedingly;<BR>(2)<BR>अनन्तम्: v. Endlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immensity
IMMENSITY:<BR>I Infinity: अनन्तता।<BR>II Vast-<BR>-ness: विशालता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immerge
IMMERGE, IMMERSE:<BR>I Trans: निमज्जयति (c.<BR>of मस्ज्): v. To plunge, dip in.<BR>II In-<BR>-trans: मज्जति, नि-, (मस्ज्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immersion
IMMERSION: मज्जनम्, नि-, (lit. and fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immesh
IMMESH: पाशे बध्यते, नि-, (pass. of बन्ध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immigrant
IMMIGRANT: *अधिप्रवासिन् (f. नी); or by<BR>circumlo,<BR>they are i. s:<BR>ते स्वदेशं परित्यज्यात्र<BR> निवसन्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immigrate
IMMIGRATE: *अधिप्रवसति (वस्, c. 1.); or by<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immigration
IMMIGRATION: अधिप्रवासः; परदेशनिवासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imminence
IMMINENCE:<BR>I Nearness: सन्निकर्षः।<BR>II Impen-<BR>-ding evil: अत्ययिकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imminent
IMMINENT:<BR>I Impending:<BR>(1) आसन्नतरः (रा,<BR> रं);<BR>(2) सन्निकृष्ट (f. ष्टा).<BR>II Perilous: आत्य-<BR>यिकः (की, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immobile
IMMOBILE: अचलः (ला, लं): v. Immovable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immobility
IMMOBILITY:<BR>(1) अचलता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2) निश्चलता, -त्वम्;<BR>(3) स्थैर्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immoderate
IMMODERATE: अपरिमितः (ता, तं): v. Also<BR>excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immoderately
IMMODERATELY: अपरिमितम्: v. Also excessively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immoderateness
IMMODERATENESS: expr. by adj.: v. Im-<BR>-moderate, excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immodest
IMMODEST:<BR>I Shameless: q.v.: निर्लज्जः (ज्जा,<BR> ज्जं).<BR>II Low, unchaste: q.v.: perh. निर्लज्ज<BR>(f. ज्जा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immodestly
IMMODESTLY: निर्लज्जम्: v. Shamelessly, un-<BR>-chastely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immodesty
IMMODESTY: निर्लज्जताः v. Shamelessness, un-<BR>-chastity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immolate
IMMOLATE: बलिं ददाति (दा, c. 3.): v. To<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immolation
IMMOLATION:<BR>(1) बलिः: v. Sacrifice;<BR>(2)<BR>बलिदानम् (the act.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immolator
IMMOLATOR: बलिदातृ (f. त्री); v. Sacrificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immoral
IMMORAL:<BR>(1) असत् (f. ती);<BR>(2) असाधु (f. ध्वी);<BR>v. Also vicious, corrupt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immorality
IMMORALITY: विधर्मः, -ता (?): v. Vice, profli-<BR>-gacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immorally
IMMORALLY: धर्ममतिक्रम्य (?): v. Viciously,<BR>wrongly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immortal
IMMORTAL:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अमरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2)<BR>अविनश्वर (f. री) (= imperishable).<BR>II Eter-<BR>-nal: q.v.: शाश्वत (f. ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immortality
IMMORTALITY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अमरत्वम्, -ता;<BR>(2)<BR>अविनश्वरता (= imperishableness).<BR>II Perpe-<BR>-tuity:<BR>(1) नित्यता;<BR>(2) चिरस्थायिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immortalize
IMMORTALIZE: expr. by adj., it well i. him:<BR>एतत्तममरं करिव्यति,<BR>or<BR>तस्यानन्तकीर्ति स्थापयिष्यतिः v.<BR>Also to perpetuate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immoveable
IMMOVEABLE:<BR>(1) अचलः<BR>or<BR>निश्चलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2)<BR>निष्कम्पः (म्पा, म्पं) (not shaking or swerving),<BR>but good men's minds are i.:<BR>निष्कम्पं तु सतां मनः,<BR>K. s. xx. 120.: v. Moveable; firm.<BR>I<BR>(property): स्थावरम्, Ya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immoveably
IMMOVEABLY: expr. by adj.,<BR>i. fixed:<BR>निश्चल-<BR>निबद्धः, K.: v. Firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immunity
IMMUNITY:<BR>I Privilege: q.v.<BR>II form: v.<BR>Exemption, freedom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immutability
IMMUTABILITY:<BR>(1) निर्विकारता;<BR>(2) अविकारिता;<BR>(3) अविकार्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immutable
IMMUTABLE:<BR>(1) निर्विकारः (रा, रं):<BR>(2) अवि-<BR>कारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(3) अविकार्य (f. र्या);<BR>(4)<BR>अविकारः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

immutably
IMMUTABLY:<BR>(1) निर्विकारम्;<BR>(2) by adj. or<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imp
IMP:<BR>I A. scion, offspring: q.v.<BR>II A<BR>goblin: भूतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impact
IMPACT: संघट्टः, “वायुद्वयसंघट्टः।” V. d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impair
IMPAIR: क्षीणीकरोति: v. To enfeeble, weaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impale
IMPALE: v. To empale.<BR>I. ment:<BR>शूलारोपणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impalpabile
IMPALPABILE:<BR>(1) दुर्ग्रहः (हा, हं);<BR>(2) दुरमिग्रह<BR>(f. हा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impannel
IMPANNEL:<BR>to i. a jury:<BR>*सम्यानां नामानि निवेशयति<BR>(c. of विश्)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impart
IMPART (v.):<BR>(1) वि-तरति (तृ c. 1.),<BR>to i.<BR>knowledge:<BR>विद्यां विररति, U. ii. 4.;<BR>(2) ददाति<BR>(दा, c. 3.): v. To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impatial
IMPATIAL:<BR>(1) अपक्षपातः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) विपक्ष-<BR>पातः (ता, तं);<BR>(3) अपक्षपातिन् (f. नी);<BR>(4)<BR>पक्षपातरहितः (ता, तं);<BR>(5) पक्षपातहीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(6) समः (मा, मं) (= evenhanded: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impartiality
IMPARTIALITY:<BR>(1) अपक्षपातिता, -त्वम्<BR>or<BR>अपक्षपातः,<BR>i. to suitors:<BR>अर्थिष्वपक्षपातः, At.;<BR>(2) समवृत्तिः<BR>(= evenhandedness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impartially
IMPARTIALLY:<BR>(1) अपक्षपातेन;<BR>(2) समम् (= even-<BR>-ly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impartible
IMPARTIBLE:<BR>I Indivisible: अविमाज्य (f. ज्या).<BR>II Capable of being imparted; वितरणीयः<BR>(या, यं); देयः (या, यं), प्र-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impassable
IMPASSABLE:<BR>(1) अगम्य (f. म्या) (= inacces-<BR>-sible);<BR>(2) कलङ्घ्य (f. ङ्घया);<BR>(3) दुस्तरः (रा,<BR> रं);<BR>(4) अनतिक्रमणीयः (या, यं), M. n.;<BR>(5)<BR>अनतिशयनीयः (या, यं) (rare), Ki. vi. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impassableness
IMPASSABLENESS:<BR>(1) अगम्यता;<BR>(2) अलङ्घ्यता;<BR>(3) दुस्तरता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impassible
IMPASSIBLE:<BR>(1) अमेद्य (f. द्या) (what cannot<BR>be penetrated);<BR>(2) अस्पृश्य (f. श्या) (what<BR>cannot be touched).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impassioned
IMPASSIONED: तेजस्विन् (f. नी (fiery, spirited).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impassive
IMPASSIVE: v. Impassible, insensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impatience
IMPATIENCE:<BR>I Inability to endure:<BR>(1)<BR>अक्षमा;<BR>(2) असहिष्णुता।<BR>II Of passion:<BR>(1)<BR>अक्षमा;<BR>(2) अमर्षः,<BR>devoid of i.:<BR>अमर्षशून्य (f. न्या),<BR>Ki. i. 33.<BR>III Eagerness: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impatient
IMPATIENT:<BR>I Not tolerant:<BR>(1) असहनः (ना,<BR> नं);<BR>(2) असहिष्णु, (mfn.).<BR>II Passionate:<BR>(1) अक्षमिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) अमर्षण (f. णा);<BR>(3)<BR>अक्षमापरीतः (ता, तं); and sim. comp.s.<BR>III<BR>Very eager: व्यग्र (f. ग्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impatiently
IMPATIENTLY: expr. by adj.,<BR>i. met the hostile<BR>army:<BR>अक्षमापरीतः प्रतिबलं प्रतिजग्राह, D. ii. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impeach
IMPEACH:<BR>(1) धर्षति (धृष्, c. 1.) (= to assail)<BR>(?);<BR>(2) अमिशंसति (शंस्, c. 1.) (= to accuse:<BR>q.v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impeachment
IMPEACHMENT: धर्षणा (?),<BR>i. of Hastings:<BR>*हस्तिं-<BR>सस्य प्रधर्षणाः v. Also accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impeccability
IMPECCABILITY:<BR>(1) निष्पापता;<BR>(2) अनघता;<BR>(3) often by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impeccable
IMPECCABLE:<BR>(1) निष्पापः (पा, पं);<BR>(2) अनघः<BR>(घा, घं);<BR>(3) अनेनस् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impede
IMPEDE: स्तम्नाति (स्तम्भ्,) c. 9.): v. To stop,<BR>hinder, retard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impediment
IMPEDIMENT:<BR>(1) व्याघातः;<BR>(2) प्रतिबन्धः;<BR>(3)<BR>प्रत्यहः;<BR>(4) बाधा;<BR>(5) प्रतिष्टम्भः: v. Also<BR>obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impel
IMPEL:<BR>I To drive: q.v.: प्रणे (चो) दयति (नुद्,<BR>or<BR>चुद्, c. 10.).<BR>II To urge on: q.v.:<BR>(1) प्रणो (चो) दयति;<BR>(2) नि-योजयति, प्र-, (-युज्,) c.<BR>10.) (= to employ),<BR>i. s. me to ask:<BR>बलान्मां<BR> प्रश्नकर्मणि नियोजयति, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impend
IMPEND:<BR>I To hang over: expr. by उपरि<BR>(= above).<BR>II To be imminent:<BR>(1) प्रत्या-<BR>सीदति (सद्, c. 1.) (= approach);<BR>(2) पतति,<BR> सं-, आ-, (पत्, c. 1.) (= to befall).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impendent
IMPENDENT, IMPENDING:<BR>(1) प्रत्यासन्न (f. न्ना);<BR>(2) सन्निकृष्ट (f. ष्टा);<BR>(3) उपनतः (ता, तं)<BR>(= arrived).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impenetrability
IMPENETRABILITY: अभेद्यता etc.: v. Impene-<BR>-trable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impenetrable
IMPENETRABLE:<BR>(1) अभेद्य (f. द्या), i. to the sun:<BR>अभानुभेद्य (f. द्या), K.;<BR>(2) by circumlo,<BR>his<BR>mind is i. to advice:<BR>तस्य मनसि न विशन्त्युपदेशाः;<BR>(3) दुष्प्रवेशः (शा, शं) (what cannot be enter-<BR>-ed);<BR>(4) गहनः (ना, नं) (= thick).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impenitence
IMPENITENCE: काठिन्यम् (= hardness): v. Also<BR>repentance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impenitent
IMPENITENT:<BR>(1) expr. by न अनुतप्यते (तप्, c.<BR>4.): v. Repent;<BR>(2) कठिनः (ना, नं) (= hard).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperative
IMPERATIVE:<BR>I Absolute, obligatory: अखण्ड्य<BR>(f. ण्ड्या).<BR>II In gram. विञ्यर्थकः (का, कं),<BR>“लोट्प्रत्ययो भवति धातोर्विध्यादिष्वर्थेषु”, Kāśikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperceptible
IMPERCEPTIBLE:<BR>(1) दुर्ग्रहः (हा, हं);<BR>(2) दुर्लक्ष्य<BR>(f. क्ष्या): v. To perceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperceptibly
IMPERCEPTIBLY:<BR>(1) by adj.;<BR>(2) अल्पाल्पम्<BR>(= little by little).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperfect
IMPERFECT:<BR>I Not complete: q.v.: असम्पूर्ण<BR>(f. र्णा).<BR>II Defective, faulty: q.v.: विकलः<BR>(ला, लं).<BR>III In gram. भुतः; लङ् (in Sans-<BR>-krit gram. only).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperfection
IMPERFECTION:<BR>I Deficiency: q.v.: असम्पूर्णता।<BR>II Fault, want: q.v.: दोषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperfecitly
IMPERFECITLY: expr. by adj.: v. Incomple-<BR>-tely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperfectness
IMPERFECTNESS:<BR>(1) असम्पूर्णता;<BR>(2) वैकल्यम्;<BR>(3)<BR>अपूर्णता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperial
IMPERIAL:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by comp., i. title:<BR>अधिराजशब्दः, Mr. iv.;<BR>i. fortune:<BR>साम्राज्यश्रीः, Si.<BR>xiv. 88.: v. Emperor, empire.<BR>II Superior:<BR>q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperialist
IMPERIALIST: *सार्वमवादिन् (f. नी); अधिराज-<BR>पक्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperially
IMPERIALLY: perh. अधिराजवत्: v. Royally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperil
IMPERIL: संशयस्थं (f. स्थां) करोतिः v. Danger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperious
IMPERIOUS: उद्धतः (ता, तं): v. Haughty, arro-<BR>-gant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperiously
IMPERIOUSLY: अद्धतम्ः v. Haughtily, arrogantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperiousness
IMPERIOUSNESS: औद्धत्यम्ः v. Haughtiness,<BR>arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperishable
IMPERISHABLE:<BR>(1) अविनश्वरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2)<BR>अविनाशिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) अक्षयः (या, यं) (= un-<BR>-decaying).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperishably
IMPERISHABLY: expr. by adj.,<BR>“i. pure”<BR>नित्य-<BR>शुद्ध (f. द्धा), S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impermeable
IMPERMEABLE:<BR>it is i. to water:<BR>अत्र जलं न प्रविशतिः<BR>v. To enter, impenetrable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impersonal
IMPERSONAL: in gram.: *प्रथमपुरुषः (षा, षं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impersonally
IMPERSONALLY: *प्रथमपुरुषे (loc. sing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impersonate
IMPERSONATE: v. To personate, personify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impertinence
IMPERTINENCE:<BR>I Irrelevancy: q.v.<BR>II<BR>Impudence, insolence: q.v.: धाष्ट्य<BR>or<BR>धृष्टता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impertinent
IMPERTINENT:<BR>I Irrelevant: q.v.: असम्पर्क<BR>(f. र्का).<BR>II Impudent, insolent: q.v.: धृष्टः<BR>(ष्टा, ष्टं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impertinently
IMPERTINENTLY:<BR>I Insolently: q.v.: धार्ष्ट्येन।<BR>II Irrelevantly: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperturbable
IMPERTURBABLE:<BR>(1) अक्षोम्य (f. भ्या);<BR>(2)<BR>निष्कम्प (f. म्पा): v. Calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperturbability
IMPERTURBABILITY:<BR>(1) अक्षोम्याता;<BR>(2) अप्रकम्प्यता<BR>(rare), Ki.: v. Calmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impervious
IMPERVIOUS: दुष्प्रवेशः (शा, शं): v. Impenetr-<BR>-able, impassable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imperviously
IMPERVIOUSLY:<BR>(1) दुष्प्रवेशम्;<BR>(2) better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impetuosity
IMPETUOSITY:<BR>(1) वेगः v. Rush;<BR>(2) चण्डता:<BR>v. Fury;<BR>(3) संरम्भः: v. Race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impetuous
IMPETUOUS:<BR>(1) चण्ड (f. ण्डा), प्र-, उत्-, i. wind:<BR>चण्डो मरुत्, K. xvii. 44.;<BR>(2) खरः (रा, रं), प्र-, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">Page365</a>]<BR>(= sharp: q.v.);<BR>(3) घोरः (रा, रं) (=fierce:<BR>q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impetuously
IMPETUOUSLY:<BR>(1) चण्डम्, प्र-;<BR>(2) महावेगेन<BR>(= swiftly: only of motion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impetuousness
IMPETUOUSNESS: v. Impetuosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impetus
IMPETUS: वेगः, सं-, आ-,<BR>I cannot hold the i. of<BR>sorrow:<BR>न शक्नोम्यहं दुःखावेगं धारयितुम्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impiety
IMPIETY:<BR>I The quality: पाषण्डबुद्धिः v.<BR>Also piety, wickedness, irreligiousness.<BR>II<BR>Sin, guilt: q.v.: पापम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impinge
IMPINGE: अभिहन्ति (हन्, c. 2.): v. To clash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impious
IMPIOUS:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) पाषण्डिन् (f. नी)<BR>(= heretic);<BR>(2) अधार्मिकः (कीम्, कं) (= irreli-<BR>-gious);<BR>(3) पापिष्ठ (f. ष्ठा) (= sinful);<BR>(4)<BR>भक्तिहीनः (ना, नं): (= wanting in faith).<BR>II Of acts, etc. पाप-<BR>or<BR>पाषण्ड- in comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impiously
IMPIOUSLY:<BR>(1) पाषण्डबुध्द्या;<BR>(2) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

implacable
IMPLACABLE:<BR>I In gen.: अहार्य (f. र्या)<BR>(= what cannot be taken away),<BR>of i. reso-<BR>lution:<BR>अहार्यनिश्चया, Mu. Ph.: i. enmity:<BR>आमरणान्तिकं वैरम्, Mr.<BR>II In enmity: बद्धवैरः<BR>(रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

implacably
IMPLACABLY: by adj. or by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

implant
IMPLANT: निदधाति (धा, c. 3.),<BR>as you, i. ed in<BR>her heart, will not be removed even by Indra:<BR>हृदये<BR> निहितस्तया भवानपि नेन्द्रेण यथापनीयते, N. ii. 47.;<BR>it is true you have i. ed these excellences [among<BR>these things]: निहिताः सत्यममी गुणस्तया, R. viii.<BR>60.: v. Also to put, keep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

implead
IMPLEAD: आवेदयति (c. of विद्): v. Also to<BR>accuse, plead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

implement
IMPLEMENT: उपकरणम्,<BR>i. of exercise:<BR>व्यायामोप-<BR>करणम्, R.;<BR>whatever is one's i.:<BR>यद्यस्योपकरणम्,<BR>Mit.: v. Tool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

implicate
IMPLICATE:<BR>(1) सम्बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.) (?);<BR>(2) संक्रामयति (c. of क्रम्) (falsely),<BR>might i. me<BR>in this crime:<BR>इदमकार्यं मयि संक्रामयेत्, Mr.<BR>viii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

implication
IMPLICATION:<BR>I Connection: सम्बन्धः।<BR>II<BR>An implying: ध्वनिः, M. n. Ph.: by i.:<BR>भङ्ग्या, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

implicit
IMPLICIT:<BR>I Implied: कार्यतः (by action) or<BR>अर्थतः (by meaning).<BR>II Absolute, uncon-<BR>ditional:<BR>(1) परमः (मा। मं);<BR>(2) निरतिशयः<BR>(या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

implicitly
IMPLICITLY:<BR>I Impliedly: कार्यतः<BR>or<BR>अर्थतः।<BR>II Absolutely:<BR>(1) परमम्;<BR>(2) निरतिशयम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

implore
IMPLORE: अम्यर्थयते (अर्थ्, c. 10.): v. To beg,<BR>ask (II.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imploringly
IMPLORINGLY:<BR>(1) कृताञ्जलि (mfn.)<BR>or<BR>अञ्जलिं<BR> बद्धा (= with joined palms);<BR>(2) पादयोः<BR> पतित्वा (= falling at one's foot);<BR>(3) जानुम्यां<BR> महीं गत्वा (= kneeling).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imply
IMPLY: सूचयति (सूच्, c. 10.) (= to indicate:<BR>q.v.): v. Also to involve, implicit (I).<BR>Ph.:<BR>it also i. ies.:<BR>इदमप्यर्थान्तरं ध्वनयति, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impolicy
IMPOLICY:<BR>(1) दुर्नयः;<BR>(2) दुर्नीतिः;<BR>(3) कुरीतिः;<BR>(4) अपनयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impolite
IMPOLITE:<BR>(1) अशिष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>(2) असम्यः<BR>(भ्या, भ्यं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impolitely
IMPOLITELY:<BR>(1) शिष्टाचारम् अतिक्रम्य;<BR>(2) असभ्य-<BR>तया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impoliteness
IMPOLITENESS:<BR>(1) असम्यता;<BR>(2) विनयापराधः;<BR>(3) शिष्टाचारस्यातिक्रमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impolitic
IMPOLITIC:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) नयभेदिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) नौत्यां नाद्द्यः (ता, तं), D.;<BR>(3) प्रनष्टनीति<BR>(mfn.), B.; and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Of acts,<BR>etc.: comp.,<BR>i. act.:<BR>दुर्नयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imponderable
IMPONDERABLE:<BR>(1) मारहीनः (ना, नं) (?);<BR>(2) अमरः (रा, रं) (?); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

import
IMPORT (v.):<BR>I Of goods: विदेशात्<BR>or<BR>देशान्तरात्<BR> आनयनि (नी, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>आहरति (हृ, c. 1.). I.<BR>ed from may be expr. also by: आगतः (ता, तं)<BR>(= come),<BR>i. from China:<BR>चीनागतः (ता, तं).<BR>II To imply, mean: expr. by अर्थ<BR>(= meaning)<BR>or<BR>अमिप्रायः (= purport).<BR>III<BR>To concern:<BR>(1) अवलम्बते (लम्ब्,) c. 1.);<BR>(2)<BR>by gen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

import
IMPORT (subs.):<BR>I In. pl. imported goods:<BR>विदेशीयपण्यानि; विदेशागतद्रव्याणि। and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Purport, meaning: q.v.:<BR>भावः।<BR>III Importance: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

importance
IMPORTANCE: गौरवम् (of persons)<BR>or<BR>गुरुत्वम्, -ता<BR>(of things),<BR>why do you raise into i. this attack<BR>by men:<BR>नरामियोगं॥।किं नयसे गुरुत्वम्, B. xii. 17.;<BR>lightening mountains in i.:<BR>गौरवेन लघयन्महीभृतः, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">Page366</a>]<BR>Ki. xiii. 33.: v. Also distinction, weight.<BR>Ph.: (a)<BR>of no i.:<BR>अकिञ्चित्करः (री, रं)<BR>or<BR>निरर्थकः<BR>(का, कं); (b) of great, much i., etc.; बहुफलः<BR>(ला, लं), महाप्रयोजनः (ना, नं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

important
IMPORTANT:<BR>(1) गुरु (f. र्वी) (mostly of things),<BR>the i. object begun has not been finished:<BR>गुर्वर्थः<BR> प्रारब्धो न परिसमाप्तः, K.;<BR>(2) महत् (f. ती) (=<BR>great: q.v.). Ph.: for it is i. it is not i.,<BR>etc.; = it is of i. ance, it is of no i. ance,<BR>etc.: v. Of i. ance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

importation
IMPORTATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) देशन्तराद्भाण्डा-<BR>नयनम्, P.;<BR>(2) पण्यानामागमः, M. viii. 401.;<BR>and sim. expr.<BR>II = import: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

importer
IMPORTER: विदेशपण्याहर्तृ (f. त्री), better by<BR>verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

importunate
IMPORTUNATE: expr. by verb or subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

importune
IMPORTUNE: अनुरुणद्धि (रुध्, c. 7.),<BR>thus men i.<BR>d with improper demands:<BR>एवं नामानुरुध्यमानाः<BR> पुमांसः, Vi. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

importunity
IMPORTUNITY:<BR>(1) अनुरोधः;<BR>(2) ग्रहः (= per-<BR>-tinacity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impose
IMPOSE: न्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.), all burden (of<BR>state)<BR>is i. d. on a worthy minister:<BR>योग्यसचिवे न्यस्तः<BR> समस्तो मरः, Ra. i. 10.: v. To put, employ.<BR>I. on or upon:<BR>विप्रलमते (लभ्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imposing
IMPOSING (adj.):<BR>(1) प्रकाण्ड- in comp.: v.<BR>Also wonderful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imposition
IMPOSITION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) न्यासः;<BR>(2)<BR>नियोगः (= employment).<BR>II Burden, tax:<BR>q.v.: करः।<BR>III Deception: q.v.: विप्रलम्भः,<BR>even i. is for good:<BR>विप्रलम्भोऽपि लामाय, Ki. xi.<BR>270.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impossibility
IMPOSSIBILITY:<BR>I The quality:<BR>(1) असाध्यता;<BR>(2) अशक्यता।<BR>II An impossible thing: असाध्यम्:<BR>sv. Impossible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impossible
IMPOSSIBLE:<BR>(1) असम्भवः (वा, वं) (= impro-<BR>-bable: q.v.);<BR>(2) असाध्यः (ध्या, ध्यं) (what<BR>cannot be accomplished),<BR>there is nothing i. in<BR>this world:<BR>असाध्यं नास्ति लोकेऽत्र, P.;<BR>(3) अशक्यः<BR>(क्या, क्यं) (what cannot be done),<BR>i. either<BR>to acquire or to avoid:<BR>अशक्यार्जनवर्जनः (ना, नं),<BR>N. xvii. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impost
IMPOST: करः: v. Tax, duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impostor
IMPOSTOR:<BR>(1) धूर्तः (= rogue),<BR>buffoons, i. s,<BR>and goblins are the authors of Vedas:<BR>वेदस्य कर्तारो<BR> भण्डधूर्तनिशाचराः, D. s.;<BR>(2) लोकदम्भकः, M. iv.<BR>195.: v. Also deceiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imposture
IMPOSTURE:<BR>(1) छलनाः v. Deception;<BR>(2)<BR>छद्मन् (n.) (= disguise).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impotence
IMPOTENCE, IMPOTENCY:<BR>I Weakness: q.v.:<BR>(1) वैकल्यम्;<BR>(2) दुर्बलता।<BR>II Inability to<BR>beget:<BR>(1) क्लैव्यम्;<BR>i. from birth:<BR>सहजं क्लैव्यम्,<BR>Bha.;<BR>(2) ध्वजमङ्गः (the usual from of i.)<BR>Bh.<BR>III Ungovernable passion: उद्दामता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impotent
IMPOTENT:<BR>I Weak, feeble: q.v.: अशक्तः<BR>(क्ता, क्तं).<BR>II Without generative power.<BR>सुरताशक्तः, Bha.; क्लीवः।<BR>III Violent: q.v.:<BR>“i. of tongue”:<BR>अनियन्त्रितजिह्व (f. ह्वा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impotently
IMPOTENTLY: दुर्बलम् (= weakly: q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impound
IMPOUND (v.): निरुणद्धि (रुध्, c. 7.): v. To<BR>confine, shut up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impoverish
IMPOVERISH (v.):<BR>I Lit.: दरिद्रीकरोतिः v.<BR>Poor, make.<BR>II To exhaust the strength<BR>of: क्षीणीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impoverished
IMPOVERISHED (adj.): नष्टघनः (ना, नं), गतविभवः<BR>(वा, वं), and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impoverishment
IMPOVERISHMENT:<BR>(1) धननाशः, धनक्षयः, etc.;<BR>(2) दारिद्राम् (= poverty).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impraciticability
IMPRACITICABILITY:<BR>(1) दुःसाध्यता;<BR>(2) अहार्यता;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impracticable
IMPRACTICABLE:<BR>I Impossible: दृःसाध्य (f.<BR>ध्या).<BR>II Intractable: दुर्दमः (मा, मं).<BR>III<BR>Impassable: दुर्गमः (मा, मं).<BR>IV Inexor-<BR>-able: अनिवार्य (f. र्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imprecate
IMPRECATE:<BR>(1) स्तौति<BR>or<BR>स्तवीति (स्तु, c. 1.)<BR>(= to pray);<BR>(2) शपति-ते (शप्, c. 1.) (= to<BR>curse: q.v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imprecation
IMPRECATION: अभिचारः, like the sharp i. s of the<BR>Atharva (Veda): अथर्वणस्तीव्र इवाभिचारः, Vi. i.<BR>62.: v. Also curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imprecatory
IMPRECATORY: आभिचारिकः (की, कं), i. action:<BR>आभिचारिकी क्रिया, Ki. iii. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impregnable
IMPREGNABLE:<BR>(1) अलङ्घ्य (f. ङ्घ्या),<BR>the defences<BR>are most i.:<BR>अलङ्घ्यतमा गुप्तिः, D.;<BR>(2) अजेयः (या,<BR> यं) (= inevitable).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impregnate
IMPREGNATE (v.):<BR>I To make pregnant:<BR>गर्भवतीं करोतिः v. Pregant.<BR>II To fertilize:<BR>q.v.<BR>III To infuse: perh. निवेशयति (c. of.<BR>विश्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impregnate
IMPREGNATE (adj.):<BR>“i. with disease”:<BR>रोगगर्भ<BR>(f. र्भा) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impregnation
IMPREGNATION:<BR>I Lit.: गर्भाधानम्।<BR>II Infusion:<BR>सम्मिश्रणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impress
IMPRESS (v.):<BR>I To press: अङ्कयति (अङ्क्, c.<BR>10.).<BR>II To implant: q.v.: निदधाति (धा,<BR>c. 3.).<BR>III To produce an effect on: हरति<BR>(हृ, c. l.) (to allure).<BR>IV To take by<BR>force for public service:<BR>(1) धरति (धृ, c. 1.)<BR>(in Assamese);<BR>(2) बलाद् गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impress
IMPRESS (subs.):<BR>I Mark: q.v.: चिह्नम्।<BR>II<BR>Seal: q.v.: मुद्रा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impressible
IMPRESSIBLE: expr. by verb: v. To impress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impression
IMPRESSION:<BR>I Marking: अङ्कनम्।<BR>II Mark:<BR>q.v.: चिह्नम्।<BR>III Mental: Ph.:<BR>it made no i.<BR>on him.<BR>तस्य हृदयं न जग्राह<BR>or<BR>जहार<BR>or<BR>तस्य हृदये<BR> स्थानं न लेभे।<BR>IV Idea: अनुमवः।<BR>V An edi-<BR>-tion, copy: *अनुलिपिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impressive
IMPRESSIVE:<BR>(1) हृदयग्राहिन् (f. णी), Ki.;<BR>(2)<BR>हृदयहारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(3) हृदयस्पृश् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impressively
IMPRESSIVELY: expr. by adj.<BR>he speaks i.:<BR>तस्य<BR> भारती हृदयग्राहिणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impressiveness
IMPRESSIVENESS:<BR>(1) हृदयग्राहिता;<BR>(2) हृदयहारिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imprint
IMPRINT: v. Impress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imprison
IMPRISON: (v.):<BR>I Lit.: कारायां निरुणद्धि (रुध्, c.<BR>7.): v. Jail, to confine.<BR>II To restrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imprisonament
IMPRISONAMENT:<BR>(1) कारावासः;<BR>(2) कारागारनिषे-<BR>वणम्, Bha, and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(3) निरोधनम्।<BR>(= confinement), M. viii. 310.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

improbability
IMPROBABILITY:<BR>I The quality:<BR>(1) असम्भ-<BR>वता;<BR>(2) असम्माव्यता।<BR>II Anything improb-<BR>-able: असम्मवम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

improbable
IMPROBABLE:<BR>(1) असम्मवः (वा, वं),<BR>birth of a<BR>golden deer is i.:<BR>असम्भवं हेममृगस्य जन्म, H.;<BR>(2)<BR>असम्मावनीयः (या, यं)<BR>or<BR>असम्भाव्य (f. व्या), this<BR>is i. even in Bhīṣma or in (our) preceptor Droṇa:<BR>भीष्भेऽप्यसम्भाव्यमिदं गुरौ वा, Ki. xvi. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

improbably
IMPROBABLY: expr. by adj.,<BR>to talk i.:<BR>असम्मवं<BR> वक्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

improbity
IMPROBITY: अशुचिता: v. Dishonesty, Probity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impromptu
IMPROMPTU: v. Extempore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

improper
IMPROPER:<BR>(1) अनुचितः (ता, तं), i. language:<BR>अनुचितं वचः, K. s. xi. 2;<BR>(2) अयुक्तः (क्ता, क्तं),<BR>etc.: v. Proper, not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

improperly
IMPROPERLY:<BR>(1) अनुचितम्;<BR>(2) अयुक्तम्;<BR>(3) often<BR>by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impropriate
IMPROPRIATE: (ग्राभ्यजन-) हस्ते निदधाति (धा, c. 3.)<BR>(??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impropriety
IMPROPRIETY: अनुचितव्यवहारः, etc.: v. Un-<BR>-becoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

improve
IMPROVE (v. t.):<BR>I To make better:<BR>(1) expr.<BR>by adj.: v. Good;<BR>(2) वर्धयति (c. of वृध्)<BR>(to increase: q.v.);<BR>(3) उत्-कर्षति, प्र-,<BR>(कृष्, c. 1.) (rare).<BR>II To employ<BR>to good purpose: सद्रव्यवहारं करोति (with<BR>gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

improve
IMPROVE (v. i.): i.e. to become better:<BR>(1)<BR>by adj.;<BR>(2) वर्धते (वृध्, c. 1.): v. To in-<BR>-crease;<BR>(3) उत्-कृष्यते, प्र-, (pass. of कृष्) (rare).<BR>Ph.: I. See (she is) almost i. ing on Irāvati:<BR>अतिक्रामन्तीमिवेरावतीं प्रेक्षे, Mal. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

improvement
IMPROVEMENT:<BR>(1) उत्कर्षः (= excellence);<BR>(2)<BR>उन्नतिः (= advancement);<BR>(3) वृद्धिः (= in-<BR>-crease).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

improvidence
IMPROVIDENCE:<BR>(1) असमीक्ष्यकारिता;<BR>(2) प्रमत्तता<BR>(= carelessness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

improvident
IMPROVIDENT:<BR>(1) असमीक्ष्यकारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रमत्तः (त्ता, त्तं) (= carelessness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

improvidently
IMPROVIDENTLY:<BR>(1) असमीक्ष्य;<BR>(2) सप्रमादम्<BR>(= carelessly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imprudence
IMPRUDENCE:<BR>(1) अविवेकः,<BR>i. is the great seat of<BR>evils:<BR>अविवेकः परमापदां पदम, Ki. ii. 30.;<BR>(2)<BR>अविवेकिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imprudent
IMPRUDENT:<BR>(1) अविवेकिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) विवेक-<BR>हीनः (ना, नं), B. and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imprudently
IMPRUDENTLY: अविवेकेन<BR>or<BR>निर्विवेकेनः v. Also<BR>rashly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impudence
IMPUDENCE:<BR>(1) धार्ष्ट्यम;<BR>(2) निर्लज्जताः v. Shame-<BR>-lessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impudent
IMPUDENT:<BR>(1) निर्लज्जः (ज्जा, ज्जं); v. Shame-<BR>-less;<BR>(2) धृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं): v. Confident;<BR>(3)<BR>दुर्विनीतः (ता, तं) (= III-bred).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impudently
IMPUDENTLY:<BR>(1) निर्लज्जम्: v. Shamelessly;<BR>(2)<BR>धार्ष्टेयनः v. confidently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impugn
IMPUGN:<BR>(1) प्रत्याख्याति (ख्या, c. 2.): v. To<BR>deny, contradict;<BR>(2) धर्षति (धृष्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To assail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impugner
IMPUGNER: प्रतिवादिन् (f. नी) (?); better by<BR>verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impulse
IMPULSE, IMPULSION:<BR>I The act: प्रणो (चो) दनम्।<BR>II Force communicated: expr. by प्रतिघातः<BR>or<BR>संघट्टः (= clash): v. Also speed.<BR>III<BR>Mental:<BR>(1) भावगतिः (?);<BR>(2) by verb<BR>प्रणो (चो) दयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impulsive
IMPULSIVE: of persons: यो मावगत्या कार्याण्यविचार्य<BR> करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impulsively
IMPULSIVELY: expr. as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impunity
IMPUNITY: दण्डमोक्षः (?).<BR>with i.:<BR>निर्बाघम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impure
IMPURE: अशुद्ध (f. द्धा);<BR>(2) अशुचि (mfn.);<BR>etc.: v. Pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impurely
IMPURELY:<BR>(1) अशुद्धम्, etc.: v. Purely;<BR>(2)<BR>समलम्: v. Foully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impurity
IMPURITY:<BR>I The condition:<BR>(1) अशुद्धिः;<BR>(2) अशौचम्;<BR>(3) अमेध्यता।<BR>II Anything im-<BR>-pure: expr. by n. or adj. अशुचि, अमेध्यम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imputable
IMPUTABLE: आरोपणीयः (या, यं), सम्-, अधि-;<BR>better by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

imputation
IMPUTATION:<BR>I The act.: आरोपणम्।<BR>II<BR>Accusation, blame: q.v.: अपवादः।<BR>III Hint,<BR>notice: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

impute
IMPUTE:<BR>I To attribute: q.v.: अरोपयति<BR>(c. of रुह्), सम्-।<BR>II To accuse: q.v.: अप-<BR>वदति (वद्, c. 1.).<BR>III To reckon, regard:<BR>q.v.: विगणयति (गण्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

in
IN:<BR>I Denoting where: by loc.,<BR>in the house<BR>of Vasudeva:<BR>वसुदेवसद्मनि, Si.; in (the work)<BR>Yogapradipa:<BR>योगप्रदीपे,<BR>V p. com.;<BR>in the first<BR>chapter:<BR>प्रथमेपादे, S. Ph.:<BR>in one place:<BR>एकत्र, Vi.;<BR>in my presence:<BR>पश्यतो मे;<BR>in the hearing of<BR>Sugriva:<BR>शृण्वतः सुग्रीवस्य, Ram.<BR>II Denoting<BR>when: by loc.,<BR>in childhood:<BR>शैशवे, R.;<BR>in the<BR>first or the third year:<BR>प्रथमेऽब्दे तृतीये वा, M.<BR>III<BR>Denoting by what time: by ins., (he)<BR>stu-<BR>died Anuvāka in a day:<BR>अह्नानुवाकोऽधीतः, S. K.;<BR>in twenty years:<BR>विंश्त्या वत्सरैः, Raj. Ph.: in a<BR>short time:<BR>अचिरेण, K.<BR>IV Denoting how: by<BR>ins.,<BR>passing in a balloon:<BR>विमानेन विगाहमानः, R.;<BR>resolving in his mind:<BR>मनसा निश्चित्य, K.;<BR>in<BR>Anuṣṭubh metre:<BR>आनुष्टुभेन छन्दसा, U.;<BR>in the<BR>style of butterflies:<BR>शालभेन विधिना, Mu.;<BR>in what<BR>manner:<BR>केन प्रकारेण। Vet.:<BR>in rage:<BR>क्रुधा, Si. Ph.:<BR>in short:<BR>किं बहुना, K. V., of direction:<BR>(1) by<BR>ins.,<BR>16 miles in breadth:<BR>विस्तारेण योजनद्वयम्,<BR>Mat.;<BR>(2) better by comp.: v. Length,<BR>breadth.<BR>VI To denote other circumstances:<BR>by loc.,<BR>in deciding:<BR>निर्णये, Mr.<BR>VII The<BR>interior: अभ्यन्तरम्,<BR>took him in:<BR>तमभ्यन्तरं निन्ये,<BR>C.;<BR>go or come in:<BR>अभ्यन्तरं प्रविश, Vi., Mr.<BR>Ph.:<BR>in most cases:<BR>बहुशः; in all likelihood:<BR>प्रायेण, Sa.; “not in man” i.e. not the nature of<BR>man: v. Nature; in that: v. Because;<BR>in consequence of: v. On account of; in the<BR>name of (i.e. on behalf of): -अर्थे<BR>or<BR>-वचनात्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

inability
INABILITY:<BR>(1) असामर्थ्यम्;<BR>(2) अशक्तिः;<BR>(3) अक्षमता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

inaccessibility
INACCESSIBILITY:<BR>I Of places:<BR>(1) अगम्यता;<BR>(2) दुरासदत्वम्।<BR>II Of documents, etc.:<BR>(1)<BR>दुर्लमता;<BR>(2) दुष्प्राप्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

inaccessible
INACCESSIBLE:<BR>I Of places:<BR>(1) दुर्गमः (मा, मं);<BR>(2) अगम्यः (म्या, म्यं);<BR>(3) दुरासदः (दा, दं).<BR>II<BR>Unattainable: q.v.: दुर्लभः (भा, भं)<BR>III Of<BR>persons: दुर्लभदर्शनः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

inaccuracy
INACCURACY:<BR>(1) अशुद्धता;<BR>(2) अशुद्धिः: v. Mis-<BR>-take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

inaccurate
INACCURATE: अशुद्धः (द्धा, द्धं): v. Erroneous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

inaccurately
INACCURATELY: अशुद्धम: v. Also erroneously,<BR>falsely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

inaction
INACTION:<BR>(1) by विना कर्मणा<BR>or<BR>कार्येण;<BR>(2)<BR>औदासीन्यम् (= indifference); विश्रामः (= rest).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

inactive
INACTIVE:<BR>I Inert: जडः (डा, डं).<BR>II Not<BR>active:<BR>(1) निष्कर्मन् (mfn.);<BR>(2) मन्दकर्मन्<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(3) अलसः (सा, सं) (idle);<BR>(4)<BR>निरुद्योगः (गा, गं) (= not diligent).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

inactivity
INACTIVITY:<BR>I Inertness: जाड्यम्।<BR>II Idleness:<BR>q.v.:<BR>(1) निष्कर्मता;<BR>(2) निरुद्योगः;<BR>(3) कार्यद्वेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

inadequacy
INADEQUACY:<BR>(1) अप्राचुर्यम्;<BR>(2) अक्षमता (= in-<BR>-ability).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

inadequate
INADEQUATE:<BR>(1) अप्रचुरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) अक्षमः<BR>(मा, मं) (= incapable).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

inadequately
INADEQUATELY:<BR>(1) अप्रचुरम्;<BR>(2) न पर्याप्तम्;<BR>(3) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

inadmissible
INADMISSIBLE:<BR>(1) अग्राह्य (f. ह्या);<BR>(2) अग्रहणीयः<BR>(या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

inadvertence
INADVERTENCE, INADVERTENCY: अनवधानम्: v.<BR>Inattention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

inadvertent
INADVERTENT: अनवहितः (ता, तं): v. Inattentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

inadvertently
