marline-spike
MARLINE-SPIKE: कीलविशेषः (?); *विषाणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

marmalade
MARMALADE: *मधुकषायः; मिष्टविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

marmot
MARMOT: गिरिमूषिकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

maroon
MAROON (adj.):<BR>(1) पाण्डुशोण (f. णा) (?);<BR>घनारुण (f. णा) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

marlot
MARLOT:<BR>(1) मन्त्रविघातकः (?);<BR>(2) कार्यविघातकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

marque
MARQUE: Ph.:<BR>letters of m.:<BR>*उपद्रवशासनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

marquee
MARQUEE: उपकार्या: v. Tent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

marquis
MARQUIS, MARQUESS: *नायकः; मार्क्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

marquisate
MARQUISATE: *नायकत्वम्; मार्क्षता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

marriage
MARRIAGE:<BR>(1) विवाहः,<BR>m. dress:<BR>विवाहवेषः, R.<BR>vi. 10.;<BR>bad m.:<BR>कुविवाहः, M. iii. 63.;<BR>after<BR>celebrating the m. of his after-born sister:<BR>अनुष्ठितानन्तरजाविवाहः, R. ;<BR>and making him the<BR>m. witness:<BR>तमेव चाधाय विवाहसाक्ष्ये, R. ;<BR>(2)<BR>उद्वाहः,<BR>m. time:<BR>उद्वाहकालः, Vas.; m.-gift:<BR>औद्वाहिकम्, M. ;<BR>(3) परिणयः,<BR>recent m.:<BR>नव-<BR>परिणयः, Ku. vii. 95.;<BR>seeing this m.:<BR>अनयोः<BR> परिणयमवलोक्य, N. xvi. 130.;<BR>(4) उपय(या)मः<BR>(rare);<BR>(5) पाणिग्रहः, -णम्, दारपरिग्रहः, etc.<BR>(= taking a wife).<BR>M.-chamber:<BR>कौतुकागारम्,<BR>Ku. M.-string:<BR>(1) मङ्गलसूत्रम्;<BR>(2) कौतुकम्, R. ;<BR>(3) कङ्कणम्, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

marriageable
MARRIAGEABLE: विवाहयोग्य (f. ग्या), and sim.<BR>comp.s,<BR>of m. age:<BR>विवाहयोग्यवयस् (mfn.),<BR>M. n.; and that his son was of m. condition:<BR>दारक्रियायोग्यदशञ्च पुत्रम्, R. v. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

married
MARRIED (adj.): विवाहितः (ता, तं). Of men:<BR>कृतोद्वाहः and sim. expr.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

marrow
MARROW: मज्जा,<BR>m. -place:<BR>मज्जास्थानम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

marrow-bone
MARROW-BONE: मज्जाबहुलमस्थि (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

marrowy
MARROWY: मज्जाबहुलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

marry
MARRY (v.):<BR>I To take a wife:<BR>(1) उत्-<BR>वहति, वि-, समुत्- (वह्, c. l.),<BR>who m. ies such a<BR>girl:<BR>यस्तां समुद्वहेत् कन्याम्, Ph.:<BR>(2) परिणयति,<BR>(नी, c. l.), when (Śiva) will m. Pārvatī:<BR>परिणेष्यति पार्वतीं यदा, Ku.;<BR>(3) उपयच्छते (यम्,<BR>c. l.),<BR>m. ed according to rite and took the<BR>girl:<BR>विधिवदुपयम्य कन्यां निन्ये, D. ;<BR>(4) पाणिं<BR> गृह्नाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.), (with gen.);<BR>(5) by<BR>subs., at the time of m. ing another woman:<BR>स्त्र्यन्तरविवाहकाले, Mit.<BR>II To take a<BR>husband:<BR>(1) पाणिं ग्राहयति (c. of ग्रह्),<BR>with-<BR>out considering this how could I m.:<BR>अविगणय्यैतत्<BR> कथं पाणिं ग्राहयिष्यामि, K. ;<BR>(2) पतिं गृह्णाति, परि-,<BR> प्रति-, (ग्रह्, c. 9.)<BR>or<BR>याति, उप-, (या, c. 2.), or<BR>भर्तारं सम्भावयति (c. of भू), R. etc.;<BR>(3) वृणीते<BR>or<BR>वरयति (वृ, c. 9. and 10 (to select).<BR>III To cause to m.<BR>(1) योजयति, सं- (युज्,<BR>c. 10.), m. ed Rājavāhana with Avantisundarī:<BR>राजवाहनेनावन्तिसुन्दरीं संयोजयामास, D. ;<BR>(2) पाणि-<BR>ग्रहणं सम्पादयति (c. of पद्) (with gen.), R. ;<BR>(3) विवाहं कारयति (c. of कृ) (with gen.),<BR>M. n.; etc.<BR>IV To give away in [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=437" target="_blank">Page437</a>]<BR>marriage:<BR>(1) ददाति<BR>or<BR>यच्छति, प्र-, (दा, c.<BR>3. and l.): v. To give;<BR>(2) ग्राहयति (c.<BR>of ग्रह्),<BR>could not m. his daughter to the god of<BR>gods:<BR>देवदेवं सुतां ग्राहयितुं न शशाक, Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

marry
MARRY (interj.): सत्यम्: v. Indeed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mars
MARS:<BR>I The planet:<BR>(1) मङ्गलः;<BR>(2) कुजः।<BR>II The god of war:<BR>(1) कुमारः;<BR>(2) कार्त्तिकेयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

marsh
MARSH:<BR>(1) कच्छः, -भूः;<BR>(2) अनूपभूमिः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

