mercilessness
MERCILESSNESS:<BR>(1) कृपाशून्यता;<BR>(2) निर्दयता;<BR>(3) निष्कारुण्यम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mercurial
MERCURIAL: i. e., fickle: q. v.: चञ्चलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mercury
MERCURY:<BR>I The metal: पारदः, calx of m.:<BR>रसभस्मन् (n.).<BR>Sulphuret of m.:<BR>कज्जली।<BR>II The<BR>planet: बुधः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mercy
MERCY:<BR>(1) कृपा,<BR>do not talk of m.:<BR>कृपेति चेदस्तु,<BR>Ki. xiv. 16.;<BR>(2) करुणा (= pity),<BR>m. does not<BR>check you:<BR>त्वां करुणा रुणद्धि न, N. i. 135;<BR>(3)<BR>दया (= kindness),<BR>to have m.:<BR>दयां करोति, K. :<BR>(4) अनुकम्पा (= compassion);<BR>(5) दयालुता;<BR>(7) घृणा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mercy-seat
MERCY-SEAT: कृपास्थानम्, and sim. comp.s<BR>(?. comp. कृपासिन्धुः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mere
MERE (subs.):<BR>I A lake: q. v.: सरस् (n.).<BR>II A boundary: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mere
MERE (adj.):<BR>(1) केवलः (ला, लं) (= bare),<BR>m.<BR>policy is cowardice:<BR>कातर्यं केवला नीतिः, R.<BR>xvii. 47.;<BR>not of m. milk:<BR>न केवलानां पयसाम्,<BR>R. ii. 63.;<BR>(2) with एव (to emphasize<BR>= absolute),<BR>with your m. look:<BR>विलोकनेनैव<BR> तव, Si. i. 29.;<BR>(3) शुद्धः (द्धा, द्धं) (= pure,<BR>unmixed),<BR>from a m. bath:<BR>शुद्धस्नानात्, Me.<BR>ii. 30.;<BR>(4) मात्र, in comp. (= simply),<BR>on<BR>account of m. caste:<BR>जातिमात्रेण, H. i. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

merely
MERELY:<BR>(1) by adj.;<BR>(2) केवलम् (= only,<BR>barely).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

meretricious
MERETRICIOUS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) वैशिकः (की, कं);<BR>(2) by comp.: v. Harlot.<BR>II Fig.: वैशिकः<BR>(की, कं): v. Showy, gaudy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

meretriciously
MERETRICIOUSLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo:<BR>v. Also gaudily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

meretriciousness
MERETRICIOUSNESS: वैशिकम्, -ता: v. Also<BR>gaudiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

merge
MERGE:<BR>I Trans.: मज्जयति, नि-, (c. of मस्ज्):<BR>v. To immerse.<BR>II Intrans.: मज्जति, नि-,<BR>(मस्ज्, c. 1.), Ku. i. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

meridian
MERIDIAN (subs.):<BR>I Mid-day: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Climax: q. v.<BR>III In astro.: (ऊर्द्धं) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">Page445</a>]<BR>याम्योत्तरवृत्तम् (the circle). Ph.:<BR>when the sun<BR>is on the m.:<BR>समारूढे मध्यमह्णः सवितरि, K. ; मध्यगतो<BR> भानुः, B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

meridian
MERIDIAN (adj.):<BR>I Mid-day: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Highest: expr. by परा कोटिः (with gen.):<BR>v. Acme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

meridional
MERIDIONAL: याम्य (f. म्या): v. Southern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

merit
MERIT (subs.):<BR>(1) गुणः,<BR>not to enumerate your<BR>m.s:<BR>न गुणानामियत्तया, R. x. 32.; according to<BR>(our)<BR>m.s:<BR>गुणदोषतः, Mal.;<BR>(2) उत्कर्षः (= ex-<BR>-cellence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

merit
MERIT (v.): अर्हति (अर्ह्, c. l.): v. To<BR>deserve, earn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

merited
MERITED (adj.): उपयुक्त (f. क्ता): v. Proper,<BR>fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

meritorious
MERITORIOUS: प्रशस्त (f. स्ता): v. Praiseworthy,<BR>good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

meritoriously
MERITORIOUSLY:<BR>(1) प्रशस्तम्;<BR>(2) शोभनम्: v.<BR>Well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

merl
MERL, MERLE (subs.): कृष्णवर्णः पक्षिभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mermaid
MERMAID:<BR>(1) मत्स्यकुमारी (?);<BR>(2) मत्स्यकन्या<BR>(?);<BR>(3) जलनारी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

merman
MERMAN: *मत्स्यपुरुषः; जलनरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

merrily
MERRILY:<BR>(1) सहर्षम्;<BR>(2) सानन्दम्;<BR>(3) सोल्लासम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

merry
MERRY:<BR>I Cheerful, joyful:<BR>(1) हृष्ट (f. ष्टा),<BR>प्र-;<BR>(2) सानन्द (f. न्दा);<BR>(3) हृष्टमनस् (mfn.);<BR>(4) उल्लसः (सा, सं).<BR>II Causing mirth:<BR>हासकरः<BR>or<BR>हास्यकरः (री, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

merry-andrew
MERRY-ANDREW: पीठमर्दः (?): v. Buffoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

merry-making
MERRY-MAKING, MERRY-MEETING: आनन्दोत्सवः,<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

merry-thought
MERRY-THOUGHT: कुक्कुटस्य द्विशूलमुरोऽस्थि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

meseems
MESEEMS: मन्ये: v. To think.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mesenteric
MESENTERIC: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mesentery
MESENTERY: अन्त्रपेशी (?); अन्त्रकोषः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mesh
MESH:<BR>I Net: पाशः।<BR>II Its interstice:<BR>छिद्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

meshy
MESHY: जालाकारः (रा, रं), and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mesmerize
MESMERIZE: *मस्मरयति (nomi.); हस्तचालनादिना<BR> विवशीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mess
MESS (v.): सह<BR>or<BR>एकत्र भोजनम्<BR>or<BR>आहारं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mess
MESS (subs.):<BR>I A dish or quantity of food:<BR>not expr.<BR>II Of persons: expr. with,<BR>एकपाकभोजिन् (m.), Mit.<BR>III A medley: सङ्करः,<BR>Mah. 69. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

message
MESSAGE: सन्देशः,<BR>represented the return m. of<BR>Darpasāra:<BR>दर्पसारस्य प्रतिसन्देशमावेदयत्, D.;<BR>convey this m.:<BR>सन्देशं मे हर, Me.: v. News.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

messenger
MESSENGER:<BR>(1) सन्देशहरः;<BR>(2) वार्त्तावहः;<BR>(3)<BR>वैवधिकः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

messiah
MESSIAH: *त्राणाभिषिक्तः।<BR>M.-ship:<BR>*त्राणाभिषिक्तता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

messmate
MESSMATE:<BR>(1) एकपाकभोजिन् (m.):<BR>(2) एकस्थाली,<BR>Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metal
METAL (subs.):<BR>(1) धातुः;<BR>(2) लोहः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metallic
METALLIC: expr. by comp., m. property:<BR>घातुगुणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metalliferous
METALLIFEROUS: धातुगर्भ (f. र्भा) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metallurgy
METALLURGY: *धातुनिष्कर्षः, धातुशोधनादिकला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metamorphose
METAMORPHOSE:<BR>m. d:<BR>परिवृत्तशरीरः (रा, रं):<BR>v. To change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metamorphosis
METAMORPHOSIS: शरीरपरिवृत्तिः and sim. comp.s.<BR>(??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metaphor
METAPHOR: रूपकम्, Kav. x. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metaphorical
METAPHORICAL: रूपक- in comp.: v. Figu-<BR>-rative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metaphorically
METAPHORICALLY: लक्षणया (?): v. Figura-<BR>-tively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metaphysical
METAPHYSICAL: आन्वीक्षिकीविषयकः (का, कं)<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metaphysics
METAPHYSICS: आन्वीक्षिकी; समयविद्या (rare), D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mete
METE (v.): मापयति (c. of मा): v. To<BR>measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metempsychosis
METEMPSYCHOSIS: expr. with पुनर्जन्मन् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

meteor
METEOR: उल्का,<BR>fall of m.:<BR>उल्कापातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

meteoric
METEORIC: by comp. or circumlo, m. -stone:<BR>*उल्कास्थप्रस्तरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

meteorological
METEOROLOGICAL: आकाशीयः (या, यं) (??);<BR>or by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

meteorology
METEOROLOGY: *वायुविद्या; नभोविद्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

methinks
METHINKS: मन्ये; तर्कयामि, etc.: v. To think,<BR>fancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

method
METHOD:<BR>(1) प्रणाली;<BR>(2) रीतिः: v. Way,<BR>manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

methodical
METHODICAL:<BR>(1) प्रणालीसङ्गतः (ता, तं) (?);<BR>(2) रीत्यनुगतः (ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

methodically
METHODICALLY:<BR>(1) सुप्रणाल्या;<BR>(2) रीतिक्रमेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

methodist
METHODIST: of a Christian sect: *रीतिध्वजः<BR>(जा, जं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

methodize
METHODIZE: to dispose methodically: q. v.:<BR>expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metonymy
METONYMY: लक्षणा, Kav.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metope
METOPE: *मितोपः; विवृतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metre
METRE:<BR>(1) छन्दस् (n.), sung in various m.s:<BR>छन्दोभिर्विविधैर्गोतम्, G. ;<BR>(2) वृत्तम्,<BR>in this canto<BR>the m. is mostly<BR>उपजातिः अस्मिन् सर्गे प्रायेण वृत्तमुप-<BR>जातिः, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metrical
METRICAL: expr. by the above words:<BR>m.<BR>composition is poetry:<BR>छन्दोबद्धपदं पद्यम्, Sah.;<BR>what is not m. is prose:<BR>वृत्तबन्धोज्भितं गद्यम्,<BR>Sah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metrically
METRICALLY: वृत्तबन्धेन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metropolis
METROPOLIS: राजधानी: v. Capital (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metropolitan
METROPOLITAN (adj.):<BR>(1) पौरः (री, रं);<BR>(2)<BR>राजधानी in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

metropolitan
METROPOLITAN (subs.): *पौराचार्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mettle
METTLE (subs.): तेजस् (n.),<BR>of great m.:<BR>महा-<BR>तेजस्विन् (f. नी): v. Spirit, vigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mettlesome
METTLESOME: तेजस्विन् (f. नी): v. Spirited,<BR>strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mettlesomeness
METTLESOMENESS: तेजस्विता: v. Mettle, spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mew
MEW (subs.):<BR>I A cage: q. v.<BR>II A fowl:<BR>समुद्रपक्षिभेदः।<BR>III Cat's cry: मेरावः and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mew
MEW (v.):<BR>I To moult: q. v.<BR>II To shut<BR>up, enclose: q. v.: बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.).<BR>III To cry as a cat: मे मे रौति (रु, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mews
MEWS: मन्दुरा: v. Stable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miasma
MIASMA: *दुष्टोद्गारः; दूषकाणवः (m. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mica
MICA: अभ्रम्, -कम्, Monier Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

michaelmas
MICHAELMAS: *मेखलपर्वन् (n.) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

microscope
MICROSCOPE: *अणुवीक्षणम्, -यन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

microscopic
MICROSCOPIC: Ph.<BR>m. insects:<BR>*अणुवीक्षणदृश्याः<BR> कीटाः;<BR>m. observation:<BR>*अणुवीक्षणपरीक्षा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mid
MID (adj.): मध्यः (ध्या, ध्यं): v. Middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mid-day
MID-DAY (subs.):<BR>(1) मध्याह्नः: v. Noon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mid-day
MID-DAY (adj.):<BR>(1) माध्याह्रिकः (की, कं);<BR>(2)<BR>माध्यन्दिनः (नी, नं);<BR>(3) better by comp.,<BR>m. meal:<BR>मध्याह्रभोजनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

middle
MIDDLE (adj.):<BR>(1) मध्यः (ध्या, ध्यं),<BR>the m.<BR>men leave off, beset with obstacles:<BR>विघ्ननिहता<BR> विरमन्ति मध्याः, Mu.;<BR>(2) मध्यमः (मा, मं),<BR>following a m. course:<BR>पुरस्कृतमध्यमक्रमः, R. ;<BR>the m. world (i. e. the earth): मध्यमलोकः, Vi.;<BR>(3) मध्यस्थः (स्था, स्थं) (= on the m.);<BR>(4)<BR>मध्यमीयः (या, यं) (rare).<BR>The m. age:<BR>*मध्य-<BR>युगम्<BR>or<BR>मध्यकालः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

middle
MIDDLE (subs.):<BR>(1) मध्यम्, the m. of the sky:<BR>व्योममध्यम्, V. ;<BR>in the m. of the ocean:<BR>मध्ये-<BR>समुद्रम्, Si.;<BR>in the m. of the army:<BR>सैन्यस्य मध्ये,<BR>K. ; making the m. (= waist)<BR>slender:<BR>मध्यं<BR> तनूकृत्य, N. vii. 81.;<BR>(2) मध्यभागः,<BR>and there<BR>in the m.:<BR>तत्र च मध्यमागे, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

middle-age
MIDDLE-AGE: मध्यं वयस्<BR>or<BR>मध्यवयस् (n.) or<BR>वयोमध्यम्;<BR>m., decay and death:<BR>वयोमध्यं जरा<BR> मृत्युः, B. p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

middle-aged
MIDDLE-AGED (adj.): मध्यवयस् (mfn.), Bha.;<BR>मध्यवयस्कः (स्का, स्कं); अर्द्धवयस्कः (स्का, स्कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

middling
MIDDLING: मध्यमः (मा, मं),<BR>men good, bad and<BR>m.:<BR>पुरुषानुत्तमाधममध्यमान्, Mah. ii. 5. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

midge
MIDGE: मशकः (= gnat, mosquito).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

midland
MIDLAND (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: मध्यदेशीयः (या, यं).<BR>II In gen.: अभ्यन्तरवर्तिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

midnight
MIDNIGHT:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) अर्द्धरात्रः, R. ;<BR>(2)<BR>मध्यरात्रम्;<BR>(3) मध्यनिशा, P. v. ii.;<BR>(4) निशीथः,<BR>in the calm m.:<BR>स्तिमिते निशीथे, C.<BR>II. Adj.<BR>expr. by comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

midriff
MIDRIFF: i. e. diaphragm: उदरवक्षःपेशी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

midst
MIDST: मध्यम्: v. Middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

midsummer
MIDSUMMER: उत्तरायणम् (= summer solstice);<BR>मध्यनिदाघः and sim. comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

midway
MIDWAY (adv.): अर्द्धपथे,<BR>V and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

midwife
MIDWIFE: प्रजननकुशला स्त्री, Sr. (for men,<BR>use m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

midwifery
MIDWIFERY:<BR>(1) सूतिकर्मन् and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(2) कृमारभृत्या, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

midwinter
MIDWINTER: दक्षिणायनम् (= winter solstice);<BR>मध्यहेमन्तः and sim. comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mien
MIEN (subs.): आकारः: v. Look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

might
MIGHT (v.): v. May.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

might
MIGHT (subs.): शक्तिः: v. Power, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mightily
MIGHTILY:<BR>(1) तेजसा;<BR>(2) भृशम् (= exceedingly:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mighty
MIGHTY:<BR>I Powerful, strong: q. v.: शक्तिमत्<BR>(f. ती).<BR>II Great, important: q. v.: महत्<BR>(f. ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mignonette
MIGNONETTE: सुगन्धिलताविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

migrate
MIGRATE:<BR>(1) निर्गच्छति (गम्, c. l (= go<BR>out: q. v.);<BR>(2) देशान्तरं, स्थानान्तरं, etc.<BR>गच्छति: v. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

migration
MIGRATION: expr. as above: *निर्वासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

migratory
MIGRATORY: अनवस्थितवासः (सा, सं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

milch
MILCH:<BR>(1) दुग्धवती;<BR>(2) क्षीरिणी;<BR>(3) पयस्विनी;<BR>(4) दोग्ध्री, Mah. v. 35. 13.<BR>M.-cow:<BR>धेनुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mild
MILD: मृदु (f. द्वी),<BR>was neither harsh nor very<BR>m.:<BR>न खरो न च भूयसा मृदुः। R. viii. 9.:<BR>m.<BR>things:<BR>मृदु वस्तु;<BR>m. air:<BR>मृदुपवनः, V. ;<BR>m. speech:<BR>मृद्वी वाक्, N. iii. 60.; m. action:<BR>मृदुक्रिया, Sr.: v. Also soft, gentle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mildew
MILDEW: (subs.): prob.: छत्रकम्; श्वे तरजस् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mildew
MILDEW (v.):<BR>I Trans.: छत्रकितं (f. तां)<BR>करोति।<BR>II Intrans.: *छत्रकितः (ता, तं) भवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mildly
MILDLY: मृदु: v. Gently, softly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mildness
MILDNESS:<BR>(1) मृदुता;<BR>(2) मार्दवम्;<BR>(3) म्रदिमन्<BR>(m.): v. Also gentleness, softness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mile
MILE: अर्द्धक्रोशः (क्रोशः = 4000 cubits).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mileage
MILEAGE:<BR>to draw m.:<BR>*क्रोशानुसारेण भ्रमणव्ययं<BR> निष्कर्षति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mile-post
MILE-POST: *अर्द्धक्रोशफलकः (after सीमावृक्षः of m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

milfoil
MILFOIL: सहस्रपत्रः (?); लताविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

militant
MILITANT: युद्धे प्रवृत्तः (त्ता, त्तं) and sim. expr.s:<BR>v. War.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

military
MILITARY (adj.):<BR>I Pertaining to war:<BR>युद्ध-, etc. in comp.: v. War.<BR>II Belonging<BR>to a soldier: सैनिक-, etc. in comp.: v.<BR>Soldier. Ph.:<BR>m. man:<BR>योधः<BR>or<BR>भटः;<BR>a man<BR>of m. caste:<BR>क्षत्रियः or (rarely) क्षत्रम्; m. duty:<BR>क्षत्रधर्मः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

military
MILITARY (subs.): expr. by pl. of soldiers,<BR>योधाः, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

militate
MILITATE: expr. with विरोधिन् (f. नी)<BR>(= opposed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

militia
MILITIA: *रक्षाबलम्; सामयिकसैन्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

milk
MILK (subs.):<BR>(1) दुग्धम् (best equiv.),<BR>buffalo-<BR>m.:<BR>महिषीदुग्धम्<BR>or<BR>माहिषं दुग्धम्; camel's m.:<BR>उष्ट्रीदुग्धम्<BR>or<BR>औष्ट्रं दुग्धम्, Bha.:<BR>(2) क्षीरम् (also<BR>of plant):<BR>doe's m.:<BR>मृगक्षीरम्, S.k.;<BR>m. -yield-<BR>ing trees:<BR>क्षीरिणः पादपा, M. viii. 246.;<BR>(3)<BR>पयस् (n (rare),<BR>m. ing my m. in a vessel of<BR>leaves:<BR>दुग्व्वा पयः पत्रपुटे मदीयम्, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

milk
MILK (v.): दोग्धि (दुह्, c. 2.),<BR>m. ed gems from<BR>the earth:<BR>धरित्रीं रत्नानि दुदुहुः, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

milker
MILKER:<BR>(1) दोग्धृ (f. ग्ध्री);<BR>(2) दोहकः (f.<BR>हिका);<BR>(3) दोहिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

milkiness
MILKINESS: expr. with दुग्धवत् (= like milk):<BR>v. Also softness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

milking
MILKING (subs.): दोहः, -नम्। M. pail:<BR>(1) दोहन-<BR>पात्रम्;<BR>(2) दोहिनी;<BR>(3) दोहः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

milkmaid
MILKMAID:<BR>(1) गोपी;<BR>(2) गोपिका;<BR>(3) गोपिनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

milk-white
MILK-WHITE: दुग्धधवलः (ला, लं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

milky
MILKY:<BR>I Yielding milk: v. Milch.<BR>II<BR>Relating to or made of m.: expr. by<BR>comp.:<BR>m. cake:<BR>दुग्धकूपा, Bha.<BR>III Soft,<BR>mild: q. v. Ph.:<BR>m. juice:<BR>क्षीरम्; m. trees:<BR>क्षीरिणो महीरुहाः, Mah. s. 86. 15.; m. way:<BR>(1) मन्दाकिनी;<BR>(2) स्वर्नदी;<BR>(3) आकाशगङ्गा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mill
MILL (subs.): चक्रम्;<BR>oil m.:<BR>लैचक्रम्;<BR>cotton<BR>m.:<BR>*कार्पासचक्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mill
MILL (v.):<BR>I To grind: q. v.: चूर्णीकरोति।<BR>II To cut fine grooves: *दन्तुरीकरोति।<BR>III<BR>To beat: निष्पिनष्टि (पिष्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mill-dam
MILL-DAM: *चक्रबन्धः; चक्रचालनोपयोगी बन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mill-race
MILL-RACE: *चक्रपयःस्रोतस् (n.) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mill-stone
MILL-STONE:<BR>(1) पेषणी(णिः);<BR>(2) शिलापट्टः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

milled
MILLED (adj.): as a coin: दन्तुरितः (ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

millenarian
MILLENARIAN: *सहस्रवर्षवादिन् (f. नी); कृष्टस्य<BR> सहस्रवर्षाधिपत्यवादिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

millennial
MILLENNIAL: सहस्रवर्षीयः (या, यं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.: v. Year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

millennium
MILLENNIUM:<BR>(1) सहस्रवर्षम्;<BR>(2) वर्षसहस्रम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miller
MILLER: चाक्रिकः (?); चक्राजीवः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

millet
MILLET: क्षुद्रधान्यम्।<BR>Italian m.:<BR>प्रियङ्गुः;<BR>Indian<BR>m.:<BR>चीनाकः;<BR>little m.:<BR>श्यामाकः; spiked m.:<BR>कङ्गुः;<BR>kodo m.:<BR>कोद्रवः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

milliner
MILLINER: परिच्छदोपजीविन् (f. नी), and sim.<BR>expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

millinery
MILLINERY:<BR>(1) परिच्छदः;<BR>(2) वस्त्रम् (= cloth:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

million
MILLION: नियुतम्<BR>or<BR>प्रयुतम्।<BR>Ten m. s:<BR>कोटिः।<BR>By<BR>m. s:<BR>कोटिशः।<BR>M.-th:<BR>नियुततमः (मी, मं) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

millionaire
MILLIONAIRE:<BR>(1) कुवेरः;<BR>(2) लक्षपतिः;<BR>(3)<BR>लक्षेशः, J.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

milt
MILT:<BR>I Spleen: q. v.: प्लीहन् (m.).<BR>II<BR>Roe: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mime
MIME:<BR>I A farce: perh. भाणः।<BR>II A<BR>player: भण्डः; कुशीलवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mimic
MIMIC (adj.):<BR>I Imitative: q. v.:<BR>II Imi-<BR>-tated: अनुकृतः (ता, तं), better by circumlo.<BR>III Ludicrous: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mimic
MIMIC (subs.): भण्डः: v. Buffoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mimic
MIMIC (v.): विडम्बयति: v. To mock, imitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mimicry
MIMICRY: भाण्डम्: v. Buffoonery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minaret
MINARET: *दीपनम्; भासशृङ्गम्; मीनारकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mince
MINCE (v.): सूक्ष्मखण्डशः छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7.)<BR>(= to cut). Ph.:<BR>not to m. matters:<BR>स्पष्टं<BR> सम्पूर्णं प्रकाशयति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mince-meat
MINCE-MEAT: विशकलितं मांसम्; सूक्ष्मं खण्डीकृतं<BR> मांसम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mincingly
MINCINGLY: Fig.:<BR>(1) असम्पूर्णम्;<BR>(2) खण्डितम्;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mind
MIND (subs.):<BR>(1) मनस् (n.),<BR>m. whose action<BR>through the nine passages was prevented:<BR>मनो<BR> नवद्वारनिषिद्धवृत्ति, Ku. iii. 50.;<BR>as his m. is<BR>entirely turned to you:<BR>एतन्मनो यद्भवदेकवृत्ति, N.<BR>iii. 105.;<BR>this person has a m. to ask you some-<BR>thing:<BR>अयं जनः किञ्चिद्भवतीं प्रष्टुमनाः, Ku. v.<BR>40.;<BR>say now what is in your m.:<BR>वदेदानों<BR> यत्ते मनसि वर्तते, Mal. ii.;<BR>to cross the m.:<BR>मनसि<BR> उदेति, N.;<BR>to call to m.:<BR>मनसि करोति;<BR>out of<BR>m.:<BR>शून्यमनस्कः (स्का, स्कं);<BR>(2) चित्तम् (not<BR>used in the sense of memory),<BR>knowing of<BR>one's m.:<BR>चित्तज्ञानम्, D.;<BR>by all being of one<BR>m.:<BR>सर्वैरेकचित्तीभूय, H. ;<BR>(3) चेतः (= 2),<BR>my<BR>unsteady m. is running behind:<BR>मम धावति पश्चाद-<BR>संस्थितं चेतः, Sa.;<BR>not little-m.ed:<BR>अनल्पचेतस्<BR>(mfn.), Ki.;<BR>(4) हृदयम् (= heart: q. v.);<BR>(5) अन्तःकरणम् (lit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mind
MIND (v.): आद्रियते (दृ, c. 6.): v. To attend,<BR>care, look, remember.<BR>Never m. the rest:<BR>मा<BR> शेषाणि विलोकय।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mindful
MINDFUL:<BR>(1) अवहितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) आहितमनस्<BR>(mfn.): v. Attentive. Ph.: to be m. of:<BR>स्मरति (स्मृ, c. l (= to remember: q. v.),<BR>R. xvii. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mine
MINE (adj.):<BR>(1) मदीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) मामकीनः<BR>(ना, नं)<BR>or<BR>मामकः (की, कं) (very rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mine
MINE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) आकरः (= any<BR>source),<BR>in a m. of rubies:<BR>आकरे पद्मरागाणाम्,<BR>H. ;<BR>(2) खनिः<BR>or<BR>खनी, खनिभिः सुषुवे रत्नम्, R.;<BR>(3) भूमिः, etc. (= earth),<BR>as he digs the place<BR>there is copper-m.;<BR>यावत्तं प्रदेशं खनति तावत्ताभ्रमयी<BR> भूमिः, P. v. 3.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) आकरः,<BR>the m. of<BR>mercy:<BR>आकरः करुणायाः, C. iii.;<BR>(2) निधिः: v.<BR>Abode.<BR>III Military:<BR>(1) कुल्या,<BR>over-<BR>charged m.:<BR>*अधिचूर्णकुल्या;<BR>(2) सुरङ्गः, Nil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mine
MINE (v.): खनति (खन्, c. l (in both senses):<BR>v. To dig.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mine
MINE (subs.): खनक (in both senses),<BR>so with<BR>machines and m. s:<BR>सयन्त्रखनकास्तथा, Mah.<BR>iii. 15. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mineral
MINERAL: धातुः (= metal). M. product:<BR>आकरजं द्रव्यम्,<BR>should appropriate all m. sub-<BR>stances:<BR>आकरेभ्यः सर्वमादद्यात्, V.s.; m. water:<BR>*धातुजलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mineralist
MINERALIST, MINERALOGIST: *धातुविद्याविशारदः<BR>(दा, दं) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mineralogy
MINERALOGY: *धातुविद्या; आकरद्रव्यविज्ञानम्, and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mingle
MINGLE (v.):<BR>I Trans.:<BR>(1) मिश्रयति, वि-, सं-,<BR>(मिश्र्, c. l.);<BR>(2) मिश्रीकरोतिः v. To mix.<BR>II Intrans.: मिलति, सं-, (मिल्, c. 6.); ऐक्यं<BR> गच्छति, Si. xvii. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mingling
MINGLING (subs.): मिश्रणम्: v. Mixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miniature
MINIATURE: expr. with: ह्रस्व (f. स्वा) (= short)<BR>or<BR>सूक्ष्म (f. क्ष्मा) (= minute, fine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minim
MINIM: in music: अर्द्धस्वरः (??); दीर्धस्वरः,<BR>Wilson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minimum
MINIMUM: expr. with सर्वाल्पः (ल्पा, ल्पं) or<BR>लघिष्ठ (f. ष्ठा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mining
MINING (subs.): खनिकर्मन् (n.) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minion
MINION: वल्लभः: v. Favourite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minister
MINISTER (subs.):<BR>I Helper, servant: q. v.:<BR>सचिवः;<BR>mistress, minister, private friend:<BR>गृहिणी<BR> सचिवः सखी मिथः, R.<BR>II. Of state:<BR>(1) सचिवः,<BR>and then entrusting to m.s:<BR>सन्निवेश्य सचिवेष्वतः<BR> परम्, R. xix. 4.;<BR>m.s should be of good descent,<BR>pure, valorous...<BR>कृलीनाः शुचयः शूराः सचिवाः<BR> स्युर्महीपतेः, Ka.;<BR>(2) मन्त्रिन् (m (= counsellor),<BR>placing the burden of state on another m.:<BR>राजकार्यधृरामन्यत्र मन्त्रिणि समासज्य, Mu. iv.;<BR>principal m.:<BR>मुख्यमन्त्री, P.;<BR>(3) अमात्यः,<BR>m.'s<BR>failing:<BR>अमात्यव्यसनम्, Mu.<BR>III A preacher,<BR>pastor; perh. आचार्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minister
MINISTER (v. t.):<BR>I To serve: q. v.: सेवते<BR>(सेव्, c. l.).<BR>II To attend to: q. v.:<BR>उपचरति (चर्, c. 1.)<BR>III To conduce:<BR>q. v.: कल्पते, उप-, (कॢप्, c. l.), Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ministerial
MINISTERIAL: expr. by comp.: m. duties:<BR>सचिवकार्याणि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ministration
MINISTRATION: उपचारः: v. Also ministry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ministry
MINISTRY:<BR>I Ministration, agency: q. v.<BR>II Office of a minister:<BR>(1) साचिव्यम्;<BR>(2)<BR>मन्त्रित्वम्, etc.<BR>III Ministers jointly: सचिव-<BR>मण्डलम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minium
MINIUM:<BR>(1) सिन्दूरम्;<BR>(2) नागजम् (very<BR>rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minnow
MINNOW: in gen.: क्षुद्रमत्स्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minor
MINOR (adj.): उप- in comp.,<BR>m. division:<BR>उप-<BR>विभागः;<BR>m. deity:<BR>उपदेवता, etc.: v. Also<BR>premiss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minor
MINOR (subs.): अप्राप्तवयस्क (f. स्का)<BR>or<BR>अप्राप्त-<BR>व्यवहार (f. रा), बाल (f. ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minority
MINORITY:<BR>I Under age: expr. by subs.,<BR>the king is (the guardian) of children during m.:<BR>राजा बालानामप्राप्तव्यवहाराणाम्, Vas.: v. Infancy.<BR>II Smaller number: expr. by अल्पः (ल्पा,<BR> ल्पं),<BR>they were in the m.:<BR>*तेऽल्पा आसन्;<BR>the<BR>m. was large:<BR>*अल्पानां संख्या महत्यासीत्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minotaur
MINOTAUR: *नरवृषभः and sim. comp.s. (after<BR>नरसिंहः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minster
MINSTER: सिद्धायतनम्: v. Monastery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minstrel
MINSTREL: मागधः (prop. a class of m. s.), Si.<BR>Celestial m.:<BR>गन्धर्वः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minstrelsy
MINSTRELSY: गान्धर्वम्: v. Music.<BR>‘M. of<BR>heaven’:<BR>गन्धर्वाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mint
MINT (subs.):<BR>I A plant: *पदिना (in<BR>Bengali).<BR>II For coining: टङ्कशाला,<BR>m.<BR>master:<BR>टङ्कशालाध्यक्षः।<BR>III Fig. = mine:<BR>खनिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mint
MINT (v.): मुद्रयति (nomi.): v. To coin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minuet
MINUET: मन्दगत्या नृत्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minus
MINUS: v. Devoid of. 10000 m. these:<BR>एतानयुतवियुतान्, Li.; 100<BR>m. five:<BR>पञ्चवर्जितशतम्,<BR>Li.;<BR>the square of 3 and of — 3:<BR>त्रितयस्य क्षयस्य<BR> च वर्गः; — 2x: या 2, Vij.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minute
MINUTE (subs.):<BR>I Of time:<BR>(1) क्षणः: v.<BR>Moment:<BR>(2) more precisely by पलम्<BR>(= 2/5 of a m.), Gan.<BR>II In geo.: कला,<BR>sixty seconds make a m.:<BR>विकलानां कला षष्ट्या,<BR>Su. i. 28.<BR>III Of proceedings: सारलेखः,<BR>m. -book:<BR>सारलेखपत्रिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minute
MINUTE (v.): सारं लिखति (लिख्, c. 6 (with<BR>gen (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minute
MINUTE (adj.): सूक्ष्म (f. क्ष्मा),<BR>animals of m.<BR>source:<BR>सूक्ष्मयोनीनि भूतानि, Mah. s. 15. 26.:<BR>सूक्ष्मकार्यार्थदर्शिन् (f. नी), R. iv. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minute-hand
MINUTE-HAND: *क्षणदर्शकहस्तःम्; क्षणप्रदर्शिनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minutely
MINUTELY:<BR>I Nicely:<BR>(1) सूक्ष्मम्;<BR>(2) पुंखानु-<BR>पुंखम्।<BR>II Every minute: प्रतिक्षणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minuteness
MINUTENESS:<BR>(1) सूक्ष्मता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2) सौक्ष्म्यम्<BR>(rare): v. Also fineness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minutiae
MINUTIÆ (pl.): सूक्ष्माणि (n. pl.); सूक्ष्मतत्त्वानि<BR>(n. pl.); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

minx
MINX: perh. रण्डा (used in contempt).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miracle
MIRACLE:<BR>(1) अलौकिकं कर्मन् (n.) and sim.<BR>comp.s.;<BR>(2) अद्भुतम् (= wonder).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miraculous
MIRACULOUS:<BR>(1) अलौकिकः (की, कं): v. Super-<BR>-human:<BR>(2) अद्भुतः (ता, तं): v. Wonderful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miraculously
MIRACULOUSLY:<BR>(1) अलौकिकशक्त्या and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mirage
MIRAGE:<BR>(1) मृगतृष्णा, -ष्णिका,<BR>I am tired of<BR>dissuading dear friend from this m.:<BR>परिश्रान्तो-<BR>ऽस्या मृगतृष्णायाः प्रियवयस्यं निवर्तयितुम्,<BR>V ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mire
MIRE: पङ्कः: v. Mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miriness
MIRINESS:<BR>(1) पङ्किलता;<BR>(2) सपङ्कताः<BR>Muddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mirror
MIRROR (subs.):<BR>(1) दर्पणः,<BR>but on the clean<BR>surface of a m.;<BR>शुद्धे तु दर्पणतले, Sa.;<BR>(2) आदर्शः,<BR>on the m.-like sky:<BR>आदर्शनिभे नभस्तले, N.;<BR>(3)<BR>मुकुरः, Go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mirror
MIRROR (v.): विम्बति, प्रति-,: v. To reflect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mirth
MIRTH:<BR>(1) हर्षः, प्र-;<BR>(2) आनन्दः;<BR>(3) उल्लासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mirthful
MIRTHFUL: हर्षाकुलः (ला, लं) and sim. comp.s.:<BR>v. Also glad, cheerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mirthfully
MIRTHFULLY:<BR>(1) प्रहृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>(2) सहर्षम्;<BR>(3) सोल्लासम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mirthfulness
MIRTHFULNESS:<BR>(1) प्रहृष्टता;<BR>(2) सोल्लासताः<BR>v. Mirth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miry
MIRY: पङ्किलः (ला, लं): v. Muddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misadventure
MISADVENTURE: दुर्घटना: v. Also misfortune,<BR>calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misalliance
MISALLIANCE: in marriage:<BR>(1) कुसम्बन्धः;<BR>(2) कुविवाहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misanthrope
MISANTHROPE, MISANTHROPIST: *नरद्वेषिन् (m.)<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misanthropic
MISANTHROPIC, -AL: *नरद्वेषिन् (f. णी); by<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misanthropy
MISANTHROPY: *नरद्वेषः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misapplication
MISAPPLICATION: अस्थानप्रयोगः; असत्प्रयोगः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misapply
MISAPPLY: v. To apply and wrongly, im-<BR>-properly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misapprehend
MISAPPREHEND: अन्यथा गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.):<BR>v. To apprehend, wrongly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misapprehension
MISAPPREHENSION: v. Misunderstanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misbecome
MISBECOME, MISBECOMINGNESS: v. To become,<BR>etc., not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misbegot
MISBEGOT, -TEN:<BR>(1) विजन्मन् (mfn.);<BR>(2) विजातः<BR>(ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misbehave
MISBEHAVE: v. To behave improperly.<BR>M. ing:<BR>दुराचारः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misbehaviour
MISBEHAVIOUR:<BR>(1) दुश्चेष्टितम्;<BR>(2) दुर्वृत्तिः;<BR>(3)<BR>अविनयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miscalculate
MISCALCULATE: वि-गणयति (गण्, c. 10.): v.<BR>Also to err.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miscalculation
MISCALCULATION: भ्रान्तगणना (?); भ्रमः (= error).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miscall
MISCALL: v. To call, improperly. M. ed:<BR>मिथ्याभिहितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miscarriage
MISCARRIAGE:<BR>I Abortion: q. v.: गर्भपातः।<BR>II Failure: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miscarry
MISCARRY:<BR>I To have a miscarriage: गर्मः<BR> स्रवति (स्रु, c. l.), पतति (पत्, c. l.), etc. (with<BR>gen.).<BR>II Not to succeed: न सिध्यति (सिध्,<BR>c. 4.).<BR>II Of letters, etc.: म्रियते (मृ, c. 6.)<BR>(used in Bengali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miscellaneous
MISCELLANEOUS: प्रकीर्ण (f. र्णा), -कः (का, कं),<BR>R.: v. Also promiscuous, various, mix(ed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miscellaneously
MISCELLANEOUSLY:<BR>(1) प्रकीर्णम्;<BR>(2) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miscellaneousness
MISCELLANEOUSNESS:<BR>(1) प्रकीर्णता;<BR>(2) मिश्रितता<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miscellany
MISCELLANY:<BR>(1) expr. by adj.;<BR>(2) संकरः<BR>(= medley).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mischance
MISCHANCE: दुर्घटना: v. Misfortune, calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mischief
MISCHIEF:<BR>I Harm, injury:<BR>(1) अपकारः;<BR>(2) हिंसा (in old writers):<BR>if cattle commit m.<BR>to crops:<BR>धान्यं विहिंस्युः पशवो यदि, M. Ph.:<BR>m. to (lit. destruction of) crops by cattle, etc.:<BR>शस्यघातो गवादिमिः, N.s.<BR>II Damage, loss:<BR>q. v.: हानिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mischief-maker
MISCHIEF-MAKER: expr. by circumlo. with:<BR>भेदः (= separation), विवादः (= dispute) or<BR>अनर्थः (= evil),<BR>he was the m.:<BR>*स भेदं जनयामास।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mischief-making
MISCHIEF-MAKING: (adj. or subs.): expr.<BR>by circumlo. as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mischievous
MISCHIEVOUS:<BR>(1) हिंस्र (f. स्रा);<BR>(2) घातुकः<BR>(का, कं) (= murderous);<BR>(3) दुष्टबुद्धि (mfn.)<BR>(= malicious);<BR>(4) पाप- in comp. (= wic-<BR>-ked).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mischievously
MISCHIEVOUSLY:<BR>(1) हिंसापूर्वम्;<BR>(2) दुष्टबद्ध्या<BR>(= maliciously).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mischievousness
MISCHIEVOUSNESS: हिंस्रता, etc.: v. Mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misconceive
MISCONCEIVE, MISCONCEPTION: v. Misun-<BR>-derstand, -ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misconduct
MISCONDUCT (subs.):<BR>(1) दुश्चरितम्;<BR>(2) दुश्चे-<BR>ष्टितम्;<BR>(3) दुर्नयः: v. Also misdeed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misconduct
MISCONDUCT (v.): दुश्चरति (चर्, c. l (?);<BR>दुष्टं चरति; न सम्यक् व्यवहरति (हृ, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misconstruction
MISCONSTRUCTION: असङ्गतव्याख्या; अयथार्थव्याख्या<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misconstrue
MISCONSTRUE: न सम्यक् परिगृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.),<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miscreant
MISCREANT:<BR>(1) खण्डितवृत्तः (त्ता, त्तं);<BR>(2) पापा-<BR>चारः (रा, रं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misdate
MISDATE (v.): *लिखनदिनभ्रमं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misdeed
MISDEED:<BR>(1) कुकर्मन् (n.), etc.;<BR>(2) अकार्यम्;<BR>of all m.s:<BR>सर्वेषामकार्याणाम्, Mah. s. 35. 36.:<BR>v. Also crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misdemeanour
MISDEMEANOUR: दुश्चरितम्: v. Misconduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misdirect
MISDIRECT: expr. by circumlo.,<BR>he m.ed the<BR>letter to Jāhānābād in Gayā instead of to<BR>Jāhānābād in Burdwan:<BR>*पत्रं वर्धमानान्तर्गतं<BR> जाहानाबादमप्रेष्य गयायां जाहानाबादं निर्दिदेश।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miser
MISER:<BR>(1) कृपणः, -जनः, H. ;<BR>(2) मितंपचः (cook-<BR>-ing little) (rare), H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miserable
MISERABLE:<BR>(1) कृपण (f. णा) (= mean), yet<BR>m. (men) bear distress at the door of the rich:<BR>सहन्ते सन्तापं तदपि धनिनां द्वारि कृपणाः, J.;<BR>(2)<BR>दीनः (ना, नं) (= wretched), very m. condition:<BR>सुदीना दशा, Ku.;<BR>(3) दुःखितः (ता, तं) (= un-<BR>-happy), surely the poor fellow is m. like me:<BR>नूनमहमिव दुःखितस्तपस्वी, Mu. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miserably
MISERABLY:<BR>(1) कार्पण्येन;<BR>(2) दीनम्: v.<BR>Meanly, wretchedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miserableness
MISERABLENESS:<BR>(1) कार्पण्यम्;<BR>(2) कदर्यता;<BR>(3)<BR>लुब्धता (= covetousness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miserly
MISERLY:<BR>(1) कृपण (f. णा);<BR>(2) कदर्य (f. र्या):<BR>v. Also mean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misery
MISERY:<BR>(1) दुःखम् (gen. term = distress, trou-<BR>-ble), the same becomes the seed of the tree of m.:<BR>तदेष दुःखवृक्षस्य बीजत्वमुपगच्छति,<BR>V p.;<BR>even m.ies<BR>met in the Daṇḍakā:<BR>प्राप्तानि दुःखान्यपि दण्डकायाम्,<BR>R. xiv. 25.;<BR>(2) दैन्यम् (the state),<BR>full of m.<BR>and thievishness:<BR>दैन्यस्तैन्यमयाः, N. xvii. 25.;<BR>(3) व्यसनम् (= calamity). fellow-disciple of m.:<BR>व्यसनसब्रह्मचारिन्, Mu. vi.;<BR>(4) कार्पण्यम् (rare),<BR>D. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misfortune
MISFORTUNE:<BR>(1) दुर्भाग्यम् (both of ill-luck<BR>and of disasters);<BR>(2) दुर्दैवम् (rarely of<BR>disasters),<BR>this is my m.:<BR>मम दुर्दैवमेतत्, H. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misgive
MISGIVE:<BR>my heart m.s me:<BR>उदेति मनसि शङ्का or<BR>अनिष्टं शङ्कते मे हृदयम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misgiving
MISGIVING (subs.): शङ्का: v. Apprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misgotten
MISGOTTEN (adj.): अन्यायोपार्जितः (ता, तं) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misgovern
MISGOVERN: न सम्यक् शास्ति (शास्, c. 2); better<BR>by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misgovernment
MISGOVERNMENT:<BR>(1) कुशासनम्;<BR>(2) दुष्टशासनम्;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misguide
MISGUIDE: अपथे पातयति (c. of पत्) and sim.<BR>expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misguided
MISGUIDED (adj.): विमार्गधावितः (ता, तं) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mishap
MISHAP: दुर्घटना: v. Calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misinform
MISINFORM: न सम्यक् निवदयति (c. of विद्) etc.:<BR>v. To inform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misinterpret
MISINTERPRET: न यथार्थं व्याख्याति (ख्या, c. 2.)<BR>or<BR>व्याचप्टे (चक्ष्, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misinterpretation
MISINTERPRETATION: असङ्गता<BR>or<BR>अयथार्था व्याख्या,<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misjudge
MISJUDGE: v. To judge wrongly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mislay
MISLAY:<BR>the letter is m.id:<BR>*अस्थाते निहितं पत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mislead
MISLEAD:<BR>(1) अपथे पातयति (c. of पत्);<BR>(2)<BR>वञ्चयते (वञ्च्, c. 10.): v. To deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misleading
MISLEADING (adj.): as of statement: भ्रमोत्पा-<BR>दक (f. दिका) and sim. comps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mismanage
MISMANAGE: expr. by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mismanagement
MISMANAGEMENT:<BR>through his m. the estate<BR>went to ruin:<BR>*तस्य कार्यनिर्वाहदोषान्नाशमगमत् सम्पत्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misname
MISNAME:<BR>I Lit.: नामान्तरेण अभिदधाति (धा, c.<BR>3.), etc.<BR>II To name improperly: expr.<BR>with मिथ्या (= falsely).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misnomer
MISNOMER:<BR>(1) मिथ्यामिधानम्;<BR>(2) मिथ्यानामन्<BR>(n.), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misogamist
MISOGAMIST: विवाहद्वेषिन् (m.); उद्वाहद्वेषिन् (m.);<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misogynist
MISOGYNIST: स्त्रीद्वेषिन् (m.) and sim. comp.s.:<BR>v. Woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misplace
MISPLACE: expr. with: अस्थानम्: v. Place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misprint
MISPRINT: *मुद्राक्षरदोषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misprision
MISPRISION:<BR>m. of treason:<BR>*राजद्रोहनिगूहनम्<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mispronounce
MISPRONOUNCE: अशुद्धम् उच्चारयति (c. of चर्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misquote
MISQUOTE: न सम्यक् उदाहरति (हृ, c. 1.): v.<BR>To quote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misrepresent
MISREPRESENT: मिथ्या<BR>or<BR>मृषा<BR>or<BR>अन्यथा वर्णयति<BR>(वर्ण्, c. 10.): v. To represent, describe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misrepresentation
MISREPRESENTATION: मिथ्याव्याहारः and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misrule
MISRULE (subs.): कुशासनम्; दुर्नयः (= impolicy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miss
MISS (subs.):<BR>I In writing: श्रीमती-।<BR>II In<BR>addressing: भर्तृदारिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miss
MISS (subs.):<BR>I Loss.: q. v.<BR>II Error:<BR>q. v.<BR>III Opposed to hit: भङ्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miss
MISS (v.):<BR>I Not to hit:<BR>(1) मोघीभवति (= be<BR>frustrated: q. v.);<BR>(2) with न पतति (पत्, c.<BR>1 (= not to fall).<BR>II Not to attain:<BR>q. v.: न लभते (लभ्, c. 1.).<BR>III To omit, pass<BR>by: expr. with जहाति (हा, c. 2.); etc. (= to<BR>abandon),<BR>to m. an opportunity:<BR>अवसरं जहाति<BR>or<BR>क्षिपति (= throw away).<BR>IV To lose:<BR>q. v.<BR>V To feel the want of: expr. by<BR>circumlo.,<BR>I m. him very much:<BR>*तस्य विप्रयोग-<BR>दुःखं नितरामनुभवामिः v. Also anxious.<BR>VI<BR>To err: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

missal
MISSAL: रोमकधर्मस्तोत्रसंहिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

missend
MISSEND: प्रमादात्<BR>or<BR>भ्रमवशात् प्रेरयति (ईर्, c. 10.),<BR>etc.: v. To send.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misshapen
MISSHAPEN:<BR>(1) विरूपः (पा, पं);<BR>(2) विकृताकृति<BR>(mfn.); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

missile
MISSILE: क्षेपणीयः (या, यं) (rare), R. iv. 77.<BR>M. weapon:<BR>अस्त्रम्: v. Dart, weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

missing
MISSING (part. adj.):<BR>I Lost: नष्ट (f. ष्टा),<BR>प्र-,<BR>m. property:<BR>प्रनष्टं द्रव्यम्, M.<BR>II. Wanting:<BR>(1) हीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) न्यूनः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mission
MISSION:<BR>I Sending, delegation:<BR>(1) by<BR>circumlo.;<BR>(2) gen. expr. by दौत्यम् (= em-<BR>-bassy, commission).<BR>II Christian:<BR>(1)<BR>*कृष्टधर्मप्रचारकाः (m. pl (of the men);<BR>(2)<BR>कृष्टधर्मप्रचारणा (of the preaching).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

missionary
MISSIONARY: *कृष्टधर्मप्रचारकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

missive
MISSIVE:<BR>I Adj.: सन्दिष्ट (f. ष्टा).<BR>II Subs.:<BR>सन्देशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mis-spell
MIS-SPELL: *वर्णविन्यासव्यत्ययं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mis-spend
MIS-SPEND: अपव्ययं करोति (with gen.); क्षिपति<BR>(क्षिप्, c. 1 (= to throw).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mis-state
MIS-STATE: न याथातथ्येन कथयति (कथ्, c. 10.):<BR>v. To state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mis-statement
MIS-STATEMENT:<BR>(1) अयथाकथनम् and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?);<BR>(2) with adv. अयथातथम्: v.<BR>Also falsehood, false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mist
MIST:<BR>(1) कूहा;<BR>(2) कुहेलि(डिका);<BR>(3) कुज्भटिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mistake
MISTAKE (subs.):<BR>(1) भ्रमः, by m. of name:<BR>नामभ्रमात्, N. xvii. 106.;<BR>(2) भ्रान्तिः, by m.:<BR>भ्रान्तितः, Go.;<BR>(3) दोषः (= fault);<BR>(4) अशुद्धिः<BR>(= incorrection);<BR>(5) प्रमादः (= careless-<BR>-ness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mistake
MISTAKE (v.):<BR>I Intrans.: expr. by subs.:<BR>v. To err.<BR>II Trans.: expr. with मन्यते<BR>(मन्, c. 4 (= to think) or with subs. बुद्धिः,<BR> धीः, etc.:<BR>m. ing for milk:<BR>दुग्धधिया, Sah. x.<BR>or<BR>पय इति [मत्वा], Kav. x. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mistaken
MISTAKEN:<BR>I In error: expr. by subs.,<BR>you<BR>are much m.:<BR>महान्ते भ्रमः; m. beauty (of langu-<BR>age): भ्रान्तिमानलङ्कारः, Kav.<BR>II Wrong, false:<BR>q. v.: भ्रान्त (f. न्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mistakenly
MISTAKENLY:<BR>(1) भ्रमात्;<BR>(2) भ्रान्तितः;<BR>(3)<BR>भ्रमेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misteach
MISTEACH: अन्यथा शिक्षयति (c. of शिक्ष्): v.<BR>To teach, wrongly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mistempered
MISTEMPERED: v. Disorderly (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mister
MISTER: v. Master (VI).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mistiness
MISTINESS:<BR>I Lit.: कूहाच्छन्नता।<BR>II Fig.: v.<BR>Dimness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mistletoe
MISTLETOE: a parasite: *पुक्कसम् (Lat. viscus;<BR>Gr. Fizos).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mistranslate
MISTRANSLATE: expr. by circumlo.,<BR>he has m.d<BR>the verses:<BR>*न तेनाञ्जसा (or याथातथ्येन) भाषान्तरी-<BR>कृताः श्लोकाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mistranslation
MISTRANSLATION: expr. as above: v. Trans-<BR>-lation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mistress
MISTRESS (subs.):<BR>I Of a house:<BR>(1) गृहिणी<BR>(also गेहिनी),<BR>I will call and ask the m. of the<BR>house:<BR>गृहिणीमाहूय पृच्छामि, Mr. i.;<BR>(2) स्वामिनी,<BR>the m. of the whole seraglio:<BR>निखिलान्तःपुर-<BR>स्वामिनी, K. ;<BR>(3) भट्टिनी (with ref. to servants);<BR>(4) कुटुम्बिनी (matron);<BR>(5) ईश्वरी (= lady),<BR>m. of life:<BR>जीवितेश्वरी, Sa. iv.<BR>II A kept<BR>woman:<BR>(1) उपपत्नी;<BR>(2) बन्धकी,<BR>gamblers<BR>have m.es in their house:<BR>भवन्ति गेहे बन्धक्यः<BR> कितवानाम्, Mah.;<BR>(3) अवरोधः (when the<BR>sense is clear), कामपि गणिकामवरोधमकरोत्, D.<BR>III. A sweetheart: प्रिया<BR>or<BR>प्रियतमा: v.<BR>Darling, woman.<BR>IV A teacher: q. v.:<BR>शिक्षयित्री।<BR>V Skilled: q. v.: कुशला, प्रवीणा,<BR>etc.<BR>VI As title: श्रीमती।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mistrust
MISTRUST (subs.): अविश्वासः: v. Distrust,<BR>suspicion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mistrust
MISTRUST (v.): न विश्वसिति (श्वस, c. 2.): v.<BR>To distrust, suspect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mistrustful
MISTRUSTFUL; अविश्वासिन् (f. नी): v. Dis-<BR>-trustful, suspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misty
MISTY:<BR>I Lit.: कूहाच्छन्न (f. न्ना) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Fig.: गहनः (ना, नं): v. Ob-<BR>-scure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misunderstand
MISUNDERSTAND: अन्यथा परिगृह्वाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.):<BR>v. To understand wrong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

misunderstanding
MISUNDERSTANDING:<BR>I Mistake: q. v.: अन्य-<BR>थाग्रहणम्<BR>or<BR>-बोधः।<BR>II Dis-agreement, differ-<BR>-ence: वैमत्यम्; मनोभेदः (?) (comp. Bengali<BR>मनान्तर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

missuse
MISSUSE: v. Abuse, misspend, maltreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mite
MITE:<BR>I Of money:<BR>(1) कपर्दकः (?);<BR>(2)<BR>वराटकः (?).<BR>II An insect: अणुकः।<BR>II A<BR>particle: लवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mitigate
MITIGATE:<BR>(1) लघयति<BR>or<BR>लघ्करोति: v. To<BR>lighten;<BR>(2) शमयति (c. of शम्) (= to quiet<BR>down, soothe).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mitigating
MITIGATING (adj.);<BR>there were no m. circum-<BR>stances:<BR>*नासीत् किमप्यपराधलाघवकारि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mitigation
MITIGATION: gen. expr. with लाघवम् (= light-<BR>-ness)<BR>or<BR>शान्तिः (= quieting down): v. To<BR>mitigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mitre
MITRE: शिरस्कम्; किरीटः; *धर्मकिरीटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mitred
MITRED: किरीटिन् (f. नी); शिरस्कभृत् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mitten
MITTEN: *हस्तत्राणम् (after अङ्गुलित्राणम् of Mah.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mix
MIX (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मिश्रयति (मिश्र्, c. 10.)<BR>सं-, वि-, व्या-;<BR>(2) by verbs meaning<BR>to unite:<BR>m.ed with pepper;<BR>मरिचसंयुतः (ता, तं), Sr.<BR>II Fig.: मिश्रयति, although (she)<BR>does not m.<BR>words with my words:<BR>वाचं न मिश्रयति यद्यपि<BR> मद्वचोभिः, Sa. i. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mix
MIX (v. i.):<BR>(1) मिश्रीभवति,<BR>m.ed with the jing-<BR>ling of the wires of a lute:<BR>वीणातन्त्रीभङ्कारमिश्र (f.<BR>श्रा), K. ;<BR>(2) मिलति (मिल्, c. 6.) (fig.): v.<BR>To unite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mixedly
MIXEDLY: सम्मिश्रेण: v. Promiscuously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mixen
MIXEN: perh. मिश्र, -कम् (comp. मिश्रकोऽध्यायः,<BR> मिश्रकचिकित्सितम्, Sr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mixture
MIXTURE:<BR>I Mixing:<BR>(1) मिश्रणम्, सम्-;<BR>(2)<BR>संयोगः (= union: q. v.).<BR>II The compound:<BR>(1) मिश्रम्;<BR>(2) सं-मिश्रेण जातः (ता, तं).<BR>III A<BR>medley:<BR>(1) सङ्करः;<BR>(2) सन्निपातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mizzen
MIZZEN: of masts, etc.: सर्वपश्चिमः (मा, मं);<BR>चरमस्थ (f. स्था).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mizzle
MIZZLE: शीकरः: v. Also to drizzle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mnemonics
MNEMONICS: *स्मरणसाधनी, -विद्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moan
MOAN (v.): *क्रन्दति (क्रन्द्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>lament, cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moan
MOAN (subs.):<BR>(1) अन्तर्नादः;<BR>(2) अतिरवः: v.<BR>Lamentation, cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moat
MOAT: परिखा: v. Ditch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mob
MOB (subs.): प्राकृतजनसंमर्दः and sim. comp.s.:<BR>v. Crowd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mob
MOB (v.):<BR>to be m.bed:<BR>प्राकृतजनैः अभिभूयते<BR>(pass. of भू)<BR>or<BR>बाध्यते (pass. of बाध्) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mobile
MOBILE:<BR>I Adj.: चलः (ला, लं): v. Fickle.<BR>II Subs.: v. Mob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mock
MOCK (v. t.): विडस्बयति (डम्ब्, c. 10.),<BR>then why<BR>are you m.ing me with falsehood:<BR>तत् किं माम-<BR>सत्यवचनेन विडम्बयसि, P. i. 5.;<BR>m.s the setting<BR>sun:<BR>विडम्बयत्यस्तनिमग्नसूर्यम्, R. xvi. 11.;<BR>(2)<BR>उपहसति (हस्, c. 1 (= to deride).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mock
MOCK (v.): उपहसति: v. Also to jest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mock
MOCK (adj.): विडम्बना affd. in comp.: v.<BR>False, counterfeit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mock
MOCK, MOCKING (subs.): विडम्बना: v. Derision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mocker
MOCKER: विडम्बनाकारिन्: v. Also derider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mockery
MOCKERY:<BR>(1) उपहासः (= derision);<BR>(2)<BR>विडम्बना,<BR>why you are doing this m. of concilia-<BR>tion:<BR>विडम्बनामिमां भूयः करोष्यनुनयात्मिकाम्,<BR>V<BR>p. i. 9. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mockingly
MOCKINGLY: सोपहासम्: v. Derisively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mocking-bird
MOCKING-BIRD: रूतानुकरणकुशलः पक्षिभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

modality
MODALITY: *रौपिकता, -त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mode
MODE:<BR>I Manner: q. v.<BR>II Fashion: q. v.<BR>III Variety: प्रकारः।<BR>IV In logic: रूपम्<BR>(?).<BR>V In music: रागः (f. रागिणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

model
MODEL (adj.):<BR>m. school:<BR>*आदर्शविद्यालयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

model
MODEL (subs.): आदर्शः: v. Pattern, standard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

model
MODEL (v.): expr. by subs.,<BR>m. house:<BR>*आदर्श-<BR>गृहं कुरू।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

modeller
MODELLER: *आदर्शकारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moderate
MODERATE (adj.):<BR>I Within due measure:<BR>मितः (ता, तं), परि-, one whose expenses are m.:<BR>मितव्ययिन् (f. नी); whose language is m. (for the<BR>sake of)<BR>truth:<BR>सत्याय मितभाषिणाम्, R. i. 7.<BR>II Of a middle rate: expr. with negative,<BR>of m. height:<BR>अनतिदीर्घ (f. र्घा); of m. abilities:<BR>अनतितीक्ष्णबुद्धि (mfn); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moderate
MODERATE (v.):<BR>I To mitigate: लघयति<BR>(nomi.).<BR>II To control, restrain: q. v.:<BR>संयच्छति (यम्, c. 1.).<BR>III To preside over<BR>a meeting: अधितिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moderately
MODERATELY:<BR>I In due measure: मितम्,<BR> परि-।<BR>II In a medium degree: v. Mode-<BR>-rate (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moderation
MODERATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) लघूकरणम्;<BR>(2) प्रशमनम् (= quieting).<BR>II Temperance:<BR>संयमः।<BR>III Equanimity: धैर्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moderator
MODERATOR: i.e. president: *अधिष्ठातृ (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

modern
MODERN:<BR>(1) आधुनिकः (की, कं), S. p. b. i.<BR>43.;<BR>(2) इदानीन्तनः (नी, नं). The m.s:<BR>इदानीन्तनाः, S. ;<BR>(3) इदन्तनः (नी, नं),<BR>by the<BR>m.s wanting in energy:<BR>शक्तिहीनैरिदन्तनैः, Vri.:<BR>(4) अधुनातनः (नी, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

modernism
MODERNISM: आधुनिकरीतिः; नव्यरीतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

modernize
MODERNIZE: *आधुनिकीकरोति or by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

modest
MODEST:<BR>I Having a proper sense of<BR>shame:<BR>(1) शालीनः (ना, नं),<BR>woman are<BR>naturally m.:<BR>निसर्गशालीनः स्त्रीजनः, Mal. iv.:<BR>(2) लज्जावत् (f. ती),<BR>the m. bride:<BR>लज्जावती<BR> वधूः, R. vii. 25.;<BR>(3) लज्जाशीलः (ला, लं);<BR>(4) लज्जालु (mfn.);<BR>(5) ह्रीमत् (f. ती); etc.<BR>II Not presumptuous: विनीतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

modestly
MODESTLY: सविनयम्: v. Also decently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

modesty
MODESTY:<BR>(1) शालीनता,<BR>out of m.:<BR>शालीनतया,<BR>R. vi. 81.;<BR>(2) लज्जा (= shame),<BR>like m. of<BR>women:<BR>लज्जेव योषितः, Si ii. 44.: v. Also<BR>decorum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

modicum
MODICUM: अल्पम्: v. Little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

modification
MODIFICATION: विवर्तनम् (?): v. Alteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

modify
MODIFY: विवर्तयति (c. of वृत्) (?): v. To alter,<BR>change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

modulate
MODULATE: संक्रामयति (c. of क्रम्) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

modulation
MODULATION:<BR>m. of voice:<BR>स्वरसंक्रमः, Mr.<BR>iii. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mohammedan
MOHAMMEDAN: v. Mahometan, mussulman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moiety
MOIETY: अर्द्धम्; अर्द्धभागः: v. Half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moil
MOIL:<BR>I Verb.: v. To soil, toil.<BR>II Subs.:<BR>v. Stain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moist
MOIST:<BR>(1) सरसः (सा, सं);<BR>(2) क्लिन्न (f. न्ना)<BR>(?);<BR>(3) आर्द्र (f. र्द्रा) (= wet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moisten
MOISTEN:<BR>(1) क्लेदयति, सं-, परि-, (c. of क्लिद्)<BR>(?);<BR>(2) आर्द्रीकरोति (= to make wet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moisture
MOISTURE: रसः,<BR>m. of the lip:<BR>अधररसः: v.<BR>Also wetness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

molar
MOLAR: i. e.<BR>m teeth:<BR>चर्वणदन्ताः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

molasses
MOLASSES: गुडः,<BR>old m.:<BR>पुराणगुडः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mold
MOLD: v. Mould.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mole
MOLE:<BR>I A mark on the body: तिलः, -कः।<BR>II An animal: *तल्पः; बिलेशयो जन्तुभेदः।<BR>III A mound: q. v. वप्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

molecule
MOLECULE: परमाणुः: v. Particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

molehill
MOLEHILL:<BR>(1) वल्मीक (mn.), born in a m.:<BR>वल्मीकमवः, A. r.;<BR>(2) वामलूरः। Ph.:<BR>to make<BR>mountains of m.s:<BR>तिले तालं पश्यति (comp.<BR>Bengali तिलके ताल करा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

molest
MOLEST: बाधते (बाध्, c. 1.): v. To harass,<BR>trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

molestation
MOLESTATION:<BR>(1) उत्पीडनम्;<BR>(2) by verb:<BR>v. Annoyance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

molester
MOLESTER:<BR>(1) उत्पीडक (f. डिका);<BR>(2) बाधक<BR>(f. धिका), प्र-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mollify
MOLLIFY: शमयति (c. of शम्): v. To calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mollusk
MOLLUSK: *कम्बुः, -जातीयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

molten
MOLTEN:<BR>I Melted: विलीनः (ना, नं), etc.<BR>II Made of melted metal: धातुमयः (यी, यं)<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moment
MOMENT:<BR>I Importance: q. v.: गुरूत्वम्।<BR>II<BR>Of time:<BR>(1) मुहूर्त (mn.), for about a m.:<BR>मुहूर्तमिव, K. ;<BR>in a m.:<BR>मुहूर्तेन, R. ;<BR>but for a<BR>m.:<BR>मुहूर्तमात्रम्, N. ;<BR>after a m.:<BR>मुहूर्तापगमे, K. ;<BR>(2) क्षणः<BR>in a m.:<BR>क्षणेन, V. ; even for a m.:<BR>क्षणमपि, R. ;<BR>at this very m.:<BR>अस्मिन्नेव क्षणे,<BR>D. ;<BR>in the next m.:<BR>तस्मिन्नेव क्षणान्तरे, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

momentarily
MOMENTARILY:<BR>(1) अनुक्षणम्;<BR>(2) प्रतिक्षणम्;<BR>(3) प्रतिमुहूर्तम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

momentary
MOMENTARY: क्षणिकः (का, कं), m. pleasure:<BR>क्षणिका प्रीतिः, H. : v. Transient, fleeting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

momentous
MOMENTOUS: गुरू (f. र्वी): v. Important.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

momentousness
MOMENTOUSNESS: गुरूत्वम्: v. Importance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

momentum
MOMENTUM: जवः (= speed: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monachism
MONACHISM: संन्यासाश्रमः and sim. comp.s.:<BR>v. Anchorite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monad
MONAD: परमाणुः: v. Atom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monarch
MONARCH:<BR>(1) राजन् (f. राज्ञी): v. King;<BR>(2) ईश्वरः (f. री): v. Lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monarchical
MONARCHICAL:<BR>I Royal: q. v.<BR>II Vested<BR>in a monarch:<BR>m. government:<BR>*राजाधीनं<BR> राज्यम्;<BR>m. form of g.:<BR>*राजतन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monarchy
MONARCHY:<BR>I M.cal government:<BR>(1)<BR>राजशासनम्;<BR>(2) राजतन्त्रम्।<BR>II Kingdom: q. v.:<BR>राज्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monastery
MONASTERY:<BR>(1) विहारः,<BR>make him the chief of<BR>all m.ies:<BR>सर्वविहारेषु कुलपतिरयं क्रियताम्, Mr.;<BR>(2) मठः, आयतनम्, etc. (when the sense is<BR>clear.),<BR>here in the m.:<BR>इहैवायतने, D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monastic
MONASTIC, -AL: expr. by comp., m. life:<BR>*विहारजीवनम्: v. Monastery, monk, ancho-<BR>-rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monday
MONDAY:<BR>(1) सोमवारः;<BR>(2) सोमवासरः and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

money
MONEY:<BR>(1) धनम्,<BR>to make m.:<BR>धनं करोति, H. ;<BR>to acquire much m.:<BR>महद्धनम् उपार्जयति, D. ;<BR>if<BR>we are rich with m. dug in the middle of a<BR>house:<BR>गृहमध्यनिखातेन धनेन धनिनो यदि, P. ;<BR>what<BR>is the use of m. who does not give, does not<BR>enjoy:<BR>धनेन किं यो न ददाति न्मश्नुते, H. ;<BR>(2)<BR>अर्थः,<BR>loss of m.:<BR>अर्थनाशः, H. ;<BR>man is slave of<BR>m.:<BR>अर्थस्य पुरुषो दासः, J. ;<BR>(3) वित्तम्,<BR>buying<BR>his poverty with own m.:<BR>वित्तैर्निजैः क्रीत्वा दारिद्रम्,<BR>D. : v. Coin, wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

money-bag
MONEY-BAG: धनभस्त्रिका (after रत्नभस्त्रिका of<BR>D. ii.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

money-changer
MONEY-CHANGER: *धनपरिवर्तकः; टङ्कव्यापारिन्<BR>(m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moneyed
MONEYED:<BR>I Rich:<BR>(1) धनवत् (f. ती);<BR>(2)<BR>धनिन् (f. नी,);<BR>(3) धनशालिन् (f. नी);<BR>(4)<BR>धनाढ्य (f. ढ्या).<BR>II Composed of money:<BR>“m. capital”:<BR>सारधनम्, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

money-lender
MONEY-LENDER: धनिकः: v. Usurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moneyless
MONEYLESS:<BR>(1) निर्धनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) धनहीनः<BR>(ना, नं) and sim. comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

money-order
MONEY-ORDER: टङ्कशासनम्; धनाज्ञापत्रम्,<BR>to pay a<BR>m.:<BR>शासननिर्दिष्टं धनं ददाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moneywort
MONEYWORT: लताविशेषः; *नुमलारिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mongrel
MONGREL: सङ्कर- in comp.: v. Hybrid, mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monition
MONITION: शासनम्: v. Admonition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monitor
MONITOR:<BR>I Lit.: शासकः।<BR>II In a school:<BR>शासकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monk
MONK: no spe. equiv.:<BR>(1) ब्रह्मचारिन् (m.);<BR>(2) यतिः;<BR>(3) संन्यासिन् (m.). Chief of m.s:<BR>कुलपतिः, Mr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monkery
MONKERY: ब्रह्मचर्या, L.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monkey
MONKEY:<BR>(1) वानरः;<BR>(2) कपिः;<BR>(3) मर्कटः;<BR>(4) प्लवङ्गः, -भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monkish
MONKISH: expr. by comp.: v. Monk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monks-hood
MONK'S-HOOD: i. e. aconite: वत्सनाभः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monody
MONODY: विलापः (when the sense is clear);<BR>विलापगीतम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monogamy
MONOGAMY: एकमार्या-परिणयः<BR>or<BR>-परिग्रहः; and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monogram
MONOGRAM: *आद्यक्षरबन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monograph
MONOGRAPH: प्रबन्धः (= dissertation). M.s.:<BR>एकैकविषयप्रबन्धाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monologue
MONOLOGUE: स्वगतोक्तिः and sim. comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monomania
MONOMANIA: एकविषय उन्मादः (?); एकविषये चित्त-<BR>विक्षेपः: v. Madness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monopolist
MONOPOLIST: *अनन्यसाधारणव्यवसायिन् (f. नी)<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monopolize
MONOPOLIZE:<BR>I To forstall: q. v.<BR>II In<BR>gen.: अनन्यसाधारणं (f. णां) करोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monopoly
MONOPOLY: *अनन्यसाधारणो व्यवसायः<BR>or<BR>व्यापारः,<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monosyllabic
MONOSYLLABIC:<BR>(1) एकाक्षरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2)<BR>एकाक्षरिन् (f. णी);<BR>(3) एकस्वरः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monosyllable
MONOSYLLABLE:<BR>(1) एकाक्षरम्;<BR>(2) एकाक्षरशब्दः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monotheism
MONOTHEISM: अद्वैतवादः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monotheist
MONOTHEIST:<BR>(1) अद्वैतवादिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>एकेश्वरवादिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monotone
MONOTONE: एकस्वरः; अभिन्नस्वरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monotonous
MONOTONOUS: Lit.: एकस्वरः (रा, रं).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>एकतानः (ना, नं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monotonously
MONOTONOUSLY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monotony
MONOTONY: expr. by adj.,<BR>avoid m. of deli-<BR>very:<BR>एकस्वरव्याहारं परिहर।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monsoon
MONSOON: *कालवातः,<BR>during the m.s:<BR>*काल-<BR>वातागमे।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monster
MONSTER:<BR>I Anything monstrous: expr.<BR>by adj..<BR>II A marvel: अद्भुतम्। Ph.:<BR>a man-<BR>m.:<BR>नरराक्षसः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monstrous
MONSTROUS:<BR>I Unnatural and misshapen:<BR>(1) अपरूपः (पा, पं) (?);<BR>(2) विकृताकृति (mfn.),<BR>Vi. v. 29.; and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Dread-<BR>-ful, horrible: घोरदर्शनः (ना, नं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.(?).<BR>III Fig.; revolting to reason:<BR>राक्षस (f. सी)<BR>or<BR>पैशाच (f. ची).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monstrously
MONSTROUSLY: उत्कटम्: v. Dreadfully, ex-<BR>-ceedingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monstrousness
MONSTROUSNESS: अपरूपता, etc.: v. Monstrous,<BR>enormity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

month
MONTH: मासः,<BR>within six m.s:<BR>षण्मासाम्यन्तरे, H. ;<BR>in the auspicious m. of Mārgaśīrṣa (Nov.-Dec.) मार्गशीर्षे शुभे मासि, M. ;<BR>for two m.s:<BR>द्वौ<BR> मासौ, H.<BR>or<BR>मासद्वयम्, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monthly
MONTHLY (adj.):<BR>(1) मासिकः (की, कं);<BR>(2)<BR>by comp.;<BR>(3) by adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monthly
MONTHLY (adj.):<BR>(1) मासे मासे;<BR>(2) प्रतिमासम्;<BR>(3) मासि मासि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monument
MONUMENT: कीर्तिस्तम्मः (= memorial pillar),<BR>R. and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

monumental
MONUMENTAL: expr. by comp.: v. Memo-<BR>-rial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mood
MOOD:<BR>I Frame of mind: भावः।<BR>II In gram:<BR>expr. with प्रकारः। N.B. Note how expr.<BR>in Sanskrit:<BR>here the verb is in the imperative,<BR>subjunctive m.:<BR>अत्रानुज्ञायां लोट्, आशङ्कायां लिङ्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moodiness
MOODINESS: वक्रता: v. Peevishness, anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moody
MOODY: वक्र (f. क्रा): v. Peevish, angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moon
MOON:<BR>(1) चन्द्रः,<BR>enjoy the m.-beams:<BR>सेव्यन्तां<BR> चन्द्रपादाः, V. ; full m.: q. v.;<BR>half m.:<BR>अर्द्धचन्द्रः,<BR>P. ;<BR>approaching m. -rise:<BR>आसन्नचन्द्रोदयः, K. ;<BR>(2) शशी,<BR>m. -light passes with the m.:<BR>शशिना<BR> सह याति कौमुदी, Ku.;<BR>(3) इन्दुः, the new m.:<BR>नवेन्दुः, R. ;<BR>the m. -set:<BR>गतोऽस्तमिन्दुः, B. ;<BR>(4)<BR>चन्द्रमस (m.), fixing my sight on the m. which<BR>has whitened the quarters with its rays:<BR>करै-<BR>र्धवलिताशामुखे चन्द्रमसि निहितदृष्टिः, K. ii.;<BR>(5)<BR>विधुः;<BR>(6) निशाकरः;<BR>(7) शशाङ्कः;<BR>(8) सुधांशुः;<BR>(9) द्विजराजः;<BR>(10) शीतमयूखः।<BR>The day of new<BR>m.:<BR>प्रतिपद्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moonless
MOONLESS:<BR>(1) अचन्द्र (f. न्द्रा);<BR>(2) चन्द्रहीनः<BR>(ना, नं); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moonlight
MOONLIGHT (subs.):<BR>(1) कौमुदी,<BR>the m. -festi-<BR>val:<BR>कौमुदीमहोत्सवः, Mu.;<BR>(2) चन्द्रिका,<BR>in m.<BR>lights are superfluous:<BR>चन्द्रिकायां दीपिकाः पुनरूक्ताः,<BR>V. ;<BR>(3) चन्द्रालोकः and sim. comp.s.,<BR>perceiv-<BR>able by m.:<BR>चन्द्रातपेन विभाव्यमानः (ना, नं), K. ;<BR>(4) ज्योत्स्ना (when the sense is clear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moonlight
MOONLIGHT (adj.):<BR>(1) expr. by comp. or<BR>circumlo.,<BR>in the autumnal m.nights:<BR>शरच्चन्द्रिकासु<BR> क्षपासु, Me.;<BR>(2) ज्योत्स्नावत् (f. ती) (= hav-<BR>-ing m.),<BR>enjoys m. evening:<BR>ज्योत्स्नावतो निर्विशति<BR> प्रदोषान्, R. vi. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moon-plant
MOON-PLANT: सोमलता।<BR>Its juice:<BR>सोमरसः।<BR>Its<BR>drinker:<BR>सोमपः, -पीथिन्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moonshine
MOONSHINE:<BR>I Lit.: चन्द्रप्रमा।<BR>II Fig.: मरी-<BR>चिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moonstruck
MOONSTRUCK:<BR>(1) वायुग्रस्तः (स्ता, स्तं);<BR>(2)<BR>वायुनिघ्न (f. घ्ना): v. Mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moor
MOOR (subs.):<BR>I An open waste: सरसपतित-<BR>भूमिः (?).<BR>II A dark African: *मौरः (f. री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moor
MOOR (v.): बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.),<BR>m. the ark<BR>with the peak of the Himālaya:<BR>हिमवतः शृङ्गे<BR> नावं बध्नीत, Mah. iii. 187. 49.; ark-m.ing peak:<BR>नौबन्धनं शृङ्गम्, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moor-hen
MOOR-HEN: जलकुक्कुटी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moorings
MOORINGS: नौबन्धनानि (n. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moor-land
MOOR-LAND: सरसपतितभूमिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moose
MOOSE, MOOSE-DEER: शम्बरः (rarely with स).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moot-point
MOOT-POINT: सन्दिग्धविषयः and sim. comps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mop
MOP (subs.):<BR>I A brush: मार्जनी।<BR>II A<BR>young girl: बाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mop
MOP (v.): सं-मार्ष्टि<BR>or<BR>मार्जयति (मृज्, c. 2.<BR>and 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mope
MOPE (v.): दुर्मनायते (nomi.): v. To drowse,<BR>dejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moping
MOPING, MOPISH (adj.): निस्तेजस् (mfn.): v.<BR>Dull, gloomy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moral
MORAL (adj.):<BR>I Relating to m.s: नीति-<BR>or<BR>नय- in comp.,<BR>m. bond:<BR>नयबन्धनम् (?);<BR>m.<BR>philosophy:<BR>*नीतिदर्शनम्।<BR>II Virtuous, just:<BR>न्याय्य (f. य्या).<BR>III Probable:<BR>there is m.<BR>certainty of his guilt:<BR>*तस्यापराधितां प्रति नास्ति<BR> कश्चिदप्यान्तरः सन्देहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moral
MORAL (subs.):<BR>I Behaviour: q. v.<BR>II<BR>In pl.: नीतिशास्त्रम्।<BR>III Drift: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>भावः;<BR>(2) अभिप्रायः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moralist
MORALIST: नीतिशास्त्रविद् (mfn.) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moralize
MORALIZE (v. i.): नीतिचिन्तां करोति, नीतिप्रबन्धं<BR> लिखति, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

morally
MORALLY:<BR>I In a moral point of view:<BR>नीतिमार्गानुसारेण।<BR>II Virtuously, honestly:<BR>न्यायतः।<BR>III Probably: expr. as shewn<BR>under Moral (adj (III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

morass
MORASS: सजलभूमिः (?): v. Marsh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

morbid
MORBID: दुष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं); v. Also diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

morbidness
MORBIDNESS:<BR>(1) दुष्टता;<BR>(2) दोषः (= fault,<BR>defect).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

morbific
MORBIFIC, -AL: रोगकरः (री, रं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.: v. Disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mordant
MORDANT:<BR>I Adj.: कटु (mfn.);<BR>II Subs.:<BR>रङ्गसंस्थापकं द्रव्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

more
MORE (Adv.):<BR>I With adj.:<BR>(1) by comp.<BR>degree,<BR>m. beloved:<BR>प्रियतरः (रा, रं), K. ;<BR>m. tall:<BR>द्राघीयस् (f. सी), Ki.;<BR>(2) अधिक in<BR>comp.,<BR>m. beautiful:<BR>अधिकमनोज्ञः (ज्ञा, ज्ञं),<BR>Sa.<BR>II With verbs:<BR>(1) अधिकम्,<BR>puts the<BR>eye more:<BR>अधिकं चक्षुरारोपयति, P. ;<BR>(2) अधिक-<BR>तरम् (in comp.),<BR>shines m. now:<BR>अधिकतरमिदानीं<BR> राजते,<BR>V Ph.: what can be m. distressing:<BR>ततो दुःखतरं नु किम्, G. ;<BR>what can be m. wonder-<BR>ful:<BR>किमतः परमाश्चर्यम्, K. ;<BR>favoured her every<BR>day m. and m.:<BR>अम्यधिकं प्रतिदिवसमस्याः प्रसाद-<BR>मकरोत्, K. :<BR>increases m. and m.:<BR>उत्तरोत्तरं<BR> वर्धते (only of succession), H. ;<BR>as said and<BR>m.:<BR>यथोक्तमभ्यधिकञ्च, D. ;<BR>no m.:<BR>न इतः परम्, D.<BR>or<BR>न अतः परम्<BR>or<BR>अत ऊर्ध्वम्, A.r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

more
MORE (adj.):<BR>(1) अधिकः (का, कं), m. devotion:<BR>अधिका भक्तिः, K. ;<BR>five times m. than it:<BR>ततः<BR> पञ्चगुणाधिकम्, Mah.; m. than twenty times:<BR>अधिकविंशान्वारान्, Ana.;<BR>(2) अधिकतरः (रा, रं)<BR>(in comp.),<BR>their trouble is m.:<BR>क्लेशोऽधिकतर-<BR>स्तेषाम्, G. Ph.:<BR>something m.:<BR>अन्यदपि, Sa.;<BR>anything m.:<BR>अतोऽप्यपरम्, Na.; what m.:<BR>किमन्यत्,<BR>V<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

more
MORE (subs.): अधिकम्,<BR>and the king who gave<BR>m. than the wish of the petitioner:<BR>नृपोऽर्थि-<BR>कामादधिकप्रदश्च, R. ; no m. = enough: q. v.:<BR>अलम् (with ins.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moreover
MOREOVER:<BR>(1) अन्यच्च,<BR>m. spies have been<BR>employed:<BR>अन्यच्च नियूक्ताः प्रणिधयः, Mu.;<BR>(2)<BR>अपरञ्च, m. (he)<BR>is cruel:<BR>अपरञ्च क्रूरः, P. ;<BR>(3) किञ्च,<BR>and m. you are our enemy:<BR>किञ्चान्यत् शत्रुर्भवान-<BR>स्माकम्, H. ;<BR>(4) अपि च, C.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

morganatic
MORGANATIC:<BR>m. marriage:<BR>वामाचारविवाहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moribund
MORIBUND:<BR>(1) मुमूर्षु (mfn.);<BR>(2) आसन्नमृत्यु<BR>(mfn.): v. Death, near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

morn
MORN:<BR>(1) विभातम्;<BR>(2) दिनमुखम्, R. : v.<BR>Morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

morning
MORNING (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: प्रभातम्<BR>or<BR>विभातम्,<BR>tomorrow m.:<BR>श्वः प्रभाते, A.r., good m. to you:<BR>*सुप्रमातं ते: v. Dawn; early in the m.:<BR>प्रत्यूषे<BR>or<BR>प्रत्यूषसि<BR>or<BR>ऊषसि, K.<BR>or<BR>अतिकल्यम्, M. ;<BR>the m. has dawned:<BR>प्रमाता रजनी, Sa.;<BR>this<BR>m.:<BR>अद्य प्रातः, H. ;<BR>from m.:<BR>प्रातरारभ्य, Vi.<BR>II Forenoon: पूर्वाह्णः,<BR>in the m.:<BR>पूर्वाह्णे, M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

morning
MORNING (adj.):<BR>(1) by comp., m. breeze:<BR>विभातवायुः, R. ;<BR>the m. star:<BR>*प्रभाततारा;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रातर्- in comp.,<BR>m. time:<BR>प्रातःकालः; m. meal:<BR>प्रातराशः;<BR>m. duties:<BR>प्रातःकृत्यानि;<BR>(3) प्राभातिकः<BR>(की, कं);<BR>(4) प्रगेतनः (नी, नं);<BR>(5) प्रातःकालीनः<BR>(ना, नं). Ph.:<BR>the m. sun:<BR>बालारूणः, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

morocco
MOROCCO: *मौरचर्मन् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

morose
MOROSE: रूक्ष (f. क्षा) (= rough, harsh: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

morosely
MOROSELY: रूक्षम्: v. Harshly, roughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moroseness
MOROSENESS: रौक्ष्यम्: v. Harshness, severity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

morris
MORRIS: Ph.:<BR>m.-dance:<BR>लास्यविशेषः;<BR>nine<BR>men's m.:<BR>अलावूकर्तनम् (comp. Bengali लाउ<BR> काटाकाटि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

morrow
MORROW: v. Tomorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

morsel
MORSEL:<BR>I Lit.: मुष्टिः: v. Also mouthful.<BR>II Fragment: खण्ड (mn.): v. Also little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mortal
MORTAL (subs.): मर्त्यः: v. Man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mortal
MORTAL (adj.):<BR>I Subject to death:<BR>(1)<BR>मृत्युवशः (शा, शं) and sim. comps.;<BR>(2) by<BR>circumlo.,<BR>every one is m., all are m.:<BR>सर्वेण खलु<BR> मर्तव्यम्, सर्वानाविशते मृत्युः, Mah. s.<BR>II Causing<BR>death:<BR>(1) प्राणहरः (री, रं);<BR>(2) साङ्घातिकः<BR>(की, कं), etc.<BR>III Human: q. v.: मर्त्य- in<BR>comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mortality
MORTALITY:<BR>I Subjection to death: expr.<BR>by adj. or circumlo.<BR>II Death: q. v. मृत्युः।<BR>III Humanity: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mortally
MORTALLY:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by adj.,<BR>m.<BR>wounded:<BR>साङ्घातिकव्रणोपेतः (ता, तं).<BR>II Ex-<BR>-tremely: q. v.: दुर्भरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mortar
MORTAR:<BR>I For pounding: उदूखलम्।<BR>II A<BR>cement: इष्टकक्षोदलेपः and sim. expr. accord-<BR>-ing to its composition.<BR>III A kind of can-<BR>-non: *मुषलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mortgage
MORTGAGE (subs.):<BR>(1) आघिः (gen. term),<BR>m. -deed:<BR>आधिलेख्यम्, Kat.;<BR>a m. becomes lost<BR>if it is not redeemed when the debt is doubled:<BR>आधिः प्रणश्येद्द्विगुणे घने यदि न मोक्ष्यते, Y. ;<BR>m. of<BR>real property:<BR>स्थावर आधिः, N.s.;<BR>(2) बन्धः,<BR> -कः (= 1), the same field given on m. to two<BR>(persons): क्षेत्रमेकं द्वयोर्बन्धे दत्तम्, Vri.;<BR>(3)<BR>आधानम् (= m.ing), Kat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mortgage
MORTGAGE (v. t.):<BR>(1) आ-दधाति (धा, c. 3.),<BR>who first m.s and then sells it:<BR>यः पूर्वतरमाधाय<BR> विक्रीणीते तु तं पुनः, Vas.;<BR>(2) आधीकरोति,<BR>who<BR>m.s the same property to two:<BR>आधिमेकं द्वयोर्यस्तु<BR> कुर्यात्, Kat.;<BR>(3) बन्धे ददाति (दा, c. 3.), Vri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mortgagee
MORTGAGEE:<BR>(1) बन्धग्रहीतृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) आधि-<BR>ग्राहक (f. हिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mortgager
MORTGAGER:<BR>(1) आधातृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) आधि-<BR>कर्तृ (f. र्त्री);<BR>(3) बन्धदातृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mortification
MORTIFICATION:<BR>I Gangrene: perh. नाशः।<BR>II Subjection, opposition: इन्द्रियजयः, -दमः,<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR>III Humiliation:<BR>(1)<BR>अभिमवः; मानमङ्गः and sim. comp.s., अभिमान-<BR>व्यसनम्, Ki.<BR>IV Vexation, disappointment:<BR>q. v.: expr. with दुःखम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mortify
MORTIFY (v. i.): perh. नश्यति (नश्, c. 4.) or<BR>म्रियते (मृ, c. 4).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mortify
MORTIFY (v. t.):<BR>I To destroy: मारयति<BR>(c. of मृ), “of m. ed”<BR>iron:<BR>मारितस्य लौहस्य,<BR>Bha.<BR>II Of passions: जयति (जि, c. 1.)<BR>one who has m.ed his lusts:<BR>जितेन्दियः (या, यं).:<BR>v. Also to control.<BR>III To vex, pain:<BR>q. v.: दुःखाकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mortifying
MORTIFYING (adj.): सन्तापक (f. पिका) (?): v.<BR>Also painful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mortise
MORTISE (subs.): छिद्रम् (used in Bengali रन्ध्रम्)<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mortise
MORTISE (v.):<BR>I<BR>To make a m.:<BR>छिद्रं करोति।<BR>II To join: लगयति (c. of लग्) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mortmain
MORTMAIN: *समवायभुक्तिः; अस्खलितभुक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mosaic
MOSAIC:<BR>I Relating to Moses: *मौषः (षी, षं).<BR>II Variegated: विचित्रः (त्रा, त्रं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mosque
MOSQUE: (महम्मदीय- or -यानां) सिद्धायतनम्: v.<BR>Temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mosquito
MOSQUITO: मशः, -कः, H. ,<BR>m.-curtain:<BR>मशहरी,<BR>Wilson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moss
MOSS: शैवालः (or शैवलः<BR>or<BR>शेवलः), m. -grown:<BR>जातशैवालः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moss-trooper
MOSS-TROOPER: दस्युः: v. Robber, bandit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mossy
MOSSY:<BR>(1) शैवलिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) शैवलवत्<BR>(f. ती), R. xvi. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

most
MOST (adj.):<BR>I In number: प्रायेण सर्वे (f. र्वा,<BR>n. र्वाणि): v. All, many.<BR>II Greatest:<BR>निरतिशयः (या, यं). Ph.:<BR>at the m.<BR>अन्ततः;<BR>to<BR>the m. of one's ability:<BR>यावच्छक्तितः;<BR>for the m.<BR>part:<BR>प्रायेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

most
MOST (adv.):<BR>I As a sign of the super-<BR>-lative: expr. with: -तमः (मा, मं) or with:<BR>अति-,<BR>m. wealthy:<BR>आढ्यतमः (मा, मं).<BR>II In the<BR>greatest degree: expr. by circumlo.,<BR>confides<BR>on him m.:<BR>सर्वापेक्षया तस्मिन्नधिकं विश्वसिति or<BR>तमधिकं श्रद्धधाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mostly
MOSTLY:<BR>(1) प्रायशः;<BR>(2) प्रायेण।: v. Also<BR>principally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mote
MOTE: बिन्दुः: v. Spot, speck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moth
MOTH: घुणः (?),<BR>m.-eaten:<BR>घुणक्षतः (ता, तं),<BR>Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mother
MOTHER:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) माता,<BR>m. -queen:<BR>राजमाता;<BR>m. -tongue:<BR>भातृभाषा; his father m.ed him:<BR>पितैवास्य मातृतामकरोत्, C. i.;<BR>(2) जननी,<BR>I am<BR>your m:<BR>साऽहमस्मि वो जननी, D. v.<BR>II Fig., [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">Page459</a>]<BR>parent, source: q. v.:<BR>(1) प्रसवित्री;<BR>(2) प्रसूः;<BR>(3) प्रसूतिः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

motherhood
MOTHERHOOD:<BR>(1) मातृत्वम्, -ता;<BR>(2) जननीत्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mother-in-law
MOTHER-IN-LAW: श्वश्रूः, all (my)<BR>m.s:<BR>श्वश्रूजनं<BR> सर्वम्, R. xiv. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mother-of-pearl
MOTHER-OF-PEARL: शुक्त्युदरम् (?); *मुक्तामुखम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

motherless
MOTHERLESS:<BR>(1) अमातृकः (का, कं), D. ;<BR>(2)<BR>मातृहीनः (ना, नं): v. Devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

motherly
MOTHERLY:<BR>I Pertaining to a mother:<BR>(1) by gen. or comp.;<BR>(2) मातृकः (का, कं).<BR>II Like a m.:<BR>(1) मातृसन्निमः (भा, भं);<BR>(2)<BR>expr. with मातृवत् (adv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

motion
MOTION (subs.):<BR>I Movement: q. v.: गतिः,<BR>eastward m.:<BR>पूर्वगतिः, Gan.; apparent m.:<BR>स्फुटगतिः, com.; mean (daily) m. of the moon:<BR>चन्द्रस्य (दैनिकी) मध्यमगतिः Su. com.<BR>To be in<BR>m.:<BR>चलति: v. To move.: to set in m.:<BR>चालयति (c. of चल्).<BR>II Impulse: q. v.:<BR>Ph.:<BR>of one's own m.:<BR>स्वेच्छया।<BR>III Feeling:<BR>भावः।<BR>IV Proposal: प्रस्तावः। (?),<BR>to second a<BR>m.:<BR>प्रस्तावनाम् अनुमोदते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

motion
MOTION (v.): इङ्गितं करोति: v. To reckon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

motionless
MOTIONLESS: निश्चलः (ला, लं):: v. Immove-<BR>-able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

motive
MOTIVE (adj.): चालक (f. लिका) (?): v. To<BR>move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

motive
MOTIVE (subs.): rewards are m.s for action:<BR>पारितोषिकलाभेच्छया नराः कर्मणि प्रवर्तन्ते;<BR>money<BR>was the m. for murdering her:<BR>अर्थस्य कारणादेषा<BR> मारिता, Mr.; whose m.s cannot be thought of:<BR>अचिन्त्यहेतुकः (का, कं), Ku. v. 75.: v. Reason,<BR>ground, why.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

motley
MOTLEY (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: चित्रविचित्र (f. त्रा).<BR>II Fig.: -सङ्करः in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mottled
MOTTLED (adj.): कर्बुरः (रा, रं): v. Variega-<BR>-ted, spotted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

motto
MOTTO: *आदर्शवाक्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mould
MOULD: (subs.):<BR>I For casting: perh. सञ्चः<BR>(comp. Bengali सांच); संयानः, Wilson.<BR>II<BR>Form, shape: q. v.: भूर्तिः।<BR>III A concre-<BR>-tion: पिण्ड (mn (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mould
MOULD (v.):<BR>I To shape: q. v.: रूपयति (रूप्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR>II To knead: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moulder
MOULDER (subs.): expr. by verb: v. Also<BR>maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moulder
MOULDER (v.):<BR>(1) विशीर्यते (pass. of शृ): v.<BR>To decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mouldiness
MOULDINESS: Of soil: मृदुमृन्मयता (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mouldy
MOULDY: Of soil: मृदुमृन्मयः (यी, यं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moult
MOULT: पशुपक्षिणां रोमादीनि पातयति (c. of पत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mound
MOUND: वप्र (mn.): v. Also hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mount
MOUNT (subs.): शैलः: v. Mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mount
MOUNT (v.t.):<BR>I Lit.: to get up: आ-रोहति,<BR> अधि-, (रूह्, c. 1.).<BR>II To furnish with<BR>horses: आ-रोहयति, अधि-, (c. of रुह्).<BR>III To<BR>set: निदधाति (धा, c. 3.).<BR>IV To raise:<BR>उच्चैः करोति। Ph.:<BR>to m. guard:<BR>रक्षास्थानमधितिष्ठति<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mount
MOUNT (v. i.):<BR>I To ascend: q.v.<BR>II On<BR>horse-back: अश्वम् आरोहति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mountain
MOUNTAIN:<BR>(1) पर्वतः,<BR>a range of m.s:<BR>कुलपर्वतः,<BR>V. p.;<BR>(2) गिरिः, waters of m.-streams:<BR>गिरिनदीसलिलानि, Sa.;<BR>(3) शैलम्, m.-residence:<BR>शैलवासः, Ki.;<BR>(4) अद्रिः, the summit of a m.:<BR>अद्रेः शृङ्गम्;<BR>(5) नगः,<BR>chief of m.s:<BR>नगाधिराजः,<BR>Ku.;<BR>(6) भूधरः and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(7) अचलः;<BR>(8) शिखरिन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mountain-dew
MOUNTAIN-DEW: i. e. Scotch whisky: *गिरि-<BR>मदिरा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mountaineer
MOUNTAINEER:<BR>(1) (प) पार्वतीयः (या, यं),<BR>Ku.;<BR>(2) पर्वतवासिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mountainous
MOUNTAINOUS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प(पा)र्वतीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) शैलमयः (यी, यं); and sim. comp.s.<BR>II<BR>Huge: पर्वतप्रमाण (f. णा) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mountebank
MOUNTEBANK: पीठमर्दः (?): v. Quack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mounting
MOUNTING (subs.):<BR>I Ascent: q. v.<BR>II On<BR>horse-back: अश्वारोहणम्।<BR>III Equipment,<BR>embellishment: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mourn
MOURN (v.):<BR>(1) शोचति, अनु-, परि-, (शुच्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) विलपति (लप्, c. l.);<BR>(3) परि-देवयते (दिव्,<BR>c. 10 (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mourner
MOURNER: शोचकः, अनु-; better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mournful
MOURNFUL:<BR>I Expressing sorrow: शोकसूचक<BR>(f. चिका) and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Full of<BR>sorrow: शोकाकुलः (ला, लं) and sim. comp.s. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">Page460</a>]<BR>III Causing sorrow: शोककरः (री, रं) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mournfully
MOURNFULLY:<BR>(1) सशोकम्;<BR>(2) better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mournfulness
MOURNFULNESS:<BR>I Sorrow, grief: शोकाकुलता<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Sadness, as of places:<BR>शोच्यता।<BR>III Expression of sorrow: शोक-<BR>सूचकता and sim. terms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mourning
MOURNING (subs.):<BR>I As felt: शोकः: v.<BR>Grief, sorrow.<BR>II As expressed by dress,<BR>etc.:<BR>to be in m.s:<BR>शुचा<BR>or<BR>शोकेन तिष्ठति (?);<BR>dressed in m.<BR>*शोकवासांसि परिधाय, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mouse
MOUSE: भूषि(ष)कः,<BR>its hole:<BR>बिलम्<BR>or<BR>विवरम्, H.;<BR>by the smell of a m.:<BR>मूषिकगन्धेन, Mah.;<BR>m.-<BR>trap<BR>*मूषिकबन्धः<BR>or<BR>मूषिकग्रहयन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mouse-trap
MOUSE-TRAP (v.): *मूपिकबन्धेन बध्नाति (बन्ध्,<BR>c. 9).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mouser
MOUSER: *मूषिकग्रहः<BR>or<BR>-ग्राहकः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moustache
MOUSTACHE: गुम्फः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mouth
MOUTH (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मुखम्,<BR>from the<BR>m. of Vasantaka:<BR>वसन्तकस्य मुखात्, K.s.;<BR>of<BR>unchecked m.:<BR>अयन्त्रितमुखः (खा, खं), D. viii.;<BR>honey in m., (but)<BR>poison in heart:<BR>मुखमधुर्हृ दय-<BR>विषः, Sa. v.;<BR>(2) वक्त्रम्;<BR>(3) आस्यम्;<BR>(4)<BR>आननम्;<BR>(5) वदनम्। N.B. These words also<BR>mean face and when the meaning is<BR>doubtful, रन्घ्र should be added, as वक्त्ररन्ध्रम्,<BR>R. ix. 63.<BR>II Of things:<BR>(1) मुखम्,<BR>pots<BR>with closed m.s.:<BR>अपिनद्धमुखा घटाः, Ve. iii.;<BR>rising from the m.s of caves:<BR>दरीमुखोत्थः, Ku.<BR>i. 8.;<BR>(2) वक्त्रम्,<BR>the m. of a quiver:<BR>निषङ्गवक्त्रम्,<BR>Ki. xvii. 36.;<BR>hundred-m.ed hole:<BR>शतमुखं<BR> बिलम्, Mah.: v. Also orifice.<BR>III Of a<BR>river: मुखम्,<BR>waters at the m. of a river:<BR>नदी-<BR>मुखाम्भः, R. xiii. 10.<BR>IV Fig.: मुखम्,<BR>grammar,<BR>the m. of all learning:<BR>सर्वविद्यानां मुखं व्याकरणम्,<BR>K. s. vi. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mouth
MOUTH (v.):<BR>I To devour: q. v.: ग्रसते (ग्रस्,<BR>c. l.).<BR>II To speak out, rant q. v.: शब्दायते<BR>(nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mouthful
MOUTHFUL:<BR>(1) ग्रासः,<BR>large m.:<BR>महान् ग्रासः,<BR>Mah.;<BR>(2) कवलः (rare),<BR>a few m.s of fresh<BR>Dub:<BR>कतिपयदूर्वाप्रबालकवल-, K. ;<BR>(3) मुष्टिः<BR>(= handful).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mouthpiece
MOUTHPIECE:<BR>I Of a wind instrument:<BR>मुखम्।<BR>II A spokesman: मुखम्,<BR>therefore you<BR>become my m.:<BR>तत्त्वं मे मुखं मव, V. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

move
MOVE (subs.):<BR>I Movement: q.v.: चलनम्।<BR>II In play:<BR>(1) चालनम् (?: comp. Bengali<BR>चाल);<BR>(2) परिणायः, A.<BR>III. An ingenious<BR>course of proceeding: perh. कौशलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

move
MOVE (v. i.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) चलति (चल्,<BR>c. l.),<BR>m.ing dust:<BR>चरद्धराधूलि-, Ku.;<BR>the<BR>girl m.d:<BR>चचाल बाला, Ku. v. 84.; for the minds<BR>of (persons)<BR>seeking victory do not m. from<BR>policy:<BR>चलति नयान्न जिगीषतां हि चेतः, Ki. x. 29.;<BR>(2) गच्छति (= to go) q.v.: v. Also to<BR>remove.<BR>II To make a motion: *प्रस्तावं<BR>or<BR>प्रस्तावनां करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

move
MOVE (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: चालयति, वि-, सं-, अभि-,<BR>(c. of चल्),<BR>shalt not m. that:<BR>तां न विचालयेत्,<BR>Vri. Ph.:<BR>to m. the bowel:<BR>विरेचयति (c. of<BR>रिच्), Sr.<BR>II To affect, as with gold:<BR>चालयति, वि-; gen. expr. with चलति।<BR>III To<BR>excite: q. v.: जनयति (c. of जन्). Ph.:<BR>m.d<BR>to pity:<BR>आर्द्रीकृतहृदयः (या, यं), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moveable
MOVEABLE:<BR>(1) चलः (ला, लं),<BR>love for friends<BR>is surely not m.:<BR>न खलु प्रेम चलं सुहृज्जने, Ku. iv.<BR>28.;<BR>(2) चरः (रा, रं) (lit.),<BR>hence is m. and<BR>im.-m. world:<BR>अतश्चराचरं विश्वम्, Ku. ii. 5.;<BR>(3) जङ्गमः (मा, मं) (lit.), m. and im.-m. being:<BR>जङ्गमः स्थावरश्च भूतग्रामः, U. vii.<BR>M.s., im.-m.s,<BR>gold:<BR>जङ्गमं स्थावरं हेम, Vri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

movement
MOVEMENT:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) गतिः: v. Motion;<BR>(2) चलनम्, the earth moves with his m.:<BR>चलनेऽवनिश्चलति तस्य, Ki. xii. 28.;<BR>(3) चारः, प्र-,<BR>(rare),<BR>by the rapid m. of the ball:<BR>कन्दुकस्य<BR> शीघ्रप्रचारतया, D. vi.;<BR>(4) भ्रमणम् (= going<BR>round),<BR>circular m.:<BR>मण्डलभ्रमणम्, D.<BR>II.<BR>Trans., moving: चालनम्, m. of the limbs:<BR>अङ्गचालनम्।<BR>III Agitation, commotion: q. v.<BR>IV In music: मूर्च्छना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mover
MOVER: i. e. proposer: प्रस्तावकारिन् (f. णी) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

moving
MOVING (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: जङ्गमः (मा, मं),<BR>a m.<BR>capital:<BR>जङ्गमराजधानी, R. xvi. 26.: v. Move-<BR>-able.<BR>II Pathetic: हृदयस्पृश् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

movingly
MOVINGLY: हृदयं स्पृष्ट्वा (?): v. Pathetically.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mow
MOW. (v.): लुनाति (लू, c. 9.): v. To cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mower
MOWER: लावकः: v. Cutter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mowing
MOWING (subs.):<BR>(1) लवनम्<BR>or<BR>लावः;<BR>(2) छेदनम्<BR>(= cutting.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mr
MR. (f. MRS): श्रीमत् (f. ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

much
MUCH (adj.):<BR>(1) बहु (f. ह्वी),<BR>showering too m.<BR>wealth on bards:<BR>वसूनि वर्षन् सुबहूनि वन्दिनाम्,<BR>N. xv. 1.;<BR>with m. effort:<BR>बहुयत्नेन;<BR>(2) भूरि-<BR>(mfn (= abundant: q. v.),<BR>m. fear:<BR>भूरि<BR> भयम्, Ki.;<BR>(3) अति- (= excessive: q. v.),<BR>m.<BR>rain:<BR>अतिवृष्टिः;<BR>(4) महत् (f. ती) (= great:<BR>q. v.),<BR>m. time:<BR>महान् कालः, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

much
MUCH (subs.): बहु (n.),<BR>one who eats m.:<BR>बहुमोक्ता,<BR>At.:<BR>I have m. to ask about it:<BR>बहु प्रष्टव्यमत्र,<BR>Mu.; men do not believe those who talk m.:<BR>बहुभाषिणो न श्रद्दधाति लोकः, K. ;<BR>even this is too<BR>m. from him:<BR>एतदेव तस्मिन् बहुतरम्, Sa. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

much
MUCH (adv.):<BR>(1) बहु, we think m. of ourselves:<BR>आत्मानं बहु मन्यामहे वयम्, Ku. vi. 20.;<BR>(2) अति<BR>(= greatly, exceedingly; q. v.), m. pleased:<BR>अतिप्रीतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

much
MUCH, AS, AS: यावत् (f. ती) तावत् (f. ती),<BR>gave as m. wealth as..:<BR>तावद्वसु ददौ यावत्॥,<BR>R. xvii. 17.; as m. as (lies) in one's power:<BR>यावच्छक्तितः, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

much
MUCH, HOW: कियत् (f. ती),<BR>what thing and<BR>how m.:<BR>किं वस्तु कियद्वा, R. v. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

much
MUCH, SO:<BR>I Abs:<BR>(1) इयत् (f. ती),<BR>and for<BR>cooking so m. rice so m. fuel is sufficient:<BR>इयतश्चौदनस्य पाकायैतावदिन्धनं पर्याप्तम्, D. viii.;<BR>(2) एतावत् (f. ती),<BR>if the motion of the moon is<BR>so m. in one day:<BR>यद्येकेन दिनेनैतावती चन्द्रगतिः,<BR>Gan.<BR>II In correlation with as much:<BR>तावत् (f. ती). N.B. Use the neuter acc. sing.<BR>for adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

much
MUCH, THAT: तावत् (f. ती), Ku. v. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

much less
MUCH LESS, MUCH MORE:<BR>(1) किमुत,<BR>even my<BR>parents do not recognise me, m. less others:<BR>पितरावपिमां न प्रतिसंविदाते किमुतेतरः, D.:<BR>he is master<BR>even of my body, m. more of (my) house, of (my)<BR>fortune, and of (my) dependants:<BR>शरीरस्याप्ययमेव<BR> प्रभुः, किमुत भवनस्य विभवस्य परिजनस्य वा, K. ;<BR>(2) किमु,<BR>m. less kings:<BR>किमु राजकम्, Ki. ii. 43.;<BR>(3) किं पुनर्,<BR>m. more one who is so high:<BR>किं<BR> पुनर्यस्तथोच्चैः, Me.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mucilage
MUCILAGE: no equiv.: रसः may be used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muck
MUCK: मलम्: v. Dirt, dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muck-heap
MUCK-HEAP, MUCK-HILL: मलराशिः and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mucous
MUCOUS: चिक्कणः (णा, णं) (= slimy: ?). M.<BR>membrane: prob. जालानि (n. pl.), “यैर्गवाक्षित-<BR>मिदम् शरीरम्” Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mud
MUD:<BR>(1) पङ्कः,<BR>to remove m.:<BR>पङ्कं हरति, V. p.<BR>v. 10. 14.;<BR>stuck in deep m.:<BR>महापङ्के निमग्नः, H.<BR>(Also poet. of<BR>any turbid liquid,<BR>अपूरि पङ्कैरिव<BR> कुङ्कुमस्य, N.);<BR>(2) कर्दमः,<BR>thick m.:<BR>सान्द्रकर्दमः,<BR>Ki.;<BR>(3) जम्बालः (mn (rare),<BR>this pond is<BR>reduced to m.<BR>जम्बालशेषमेतत् सरः सञ्जातम्, P. N.B.<BR>कर्दमः is never applied by accurate writers<BR>to the mire of ponds etc.: comp. Bengali<BR>कादा and पांँक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mud-built
MUD-BUILT:<BR>(1) मार्त्तिकः (की, कं);<BR>(2) by<BR>comp.: v. Earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muddiness
MUDDINESS:<BR>(1) पङ्किलता;<BR>(2) सपङ्कता (rare);<BR>(3) कालुष्यम् (= foulness): m. of water:<BR>कालुष्यमम्भसः, V. p. v. 10. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muddle
MUDDLE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पङ्किलं (f. लां) करोति;<BR>(2) कलुषयति (nomi (= befoul: q v).<BR>II<BR>Fig., to confuse: आकुलयति।<BR>III To be<BR>m.d = to be intoxicated: v. Drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muddy
MUDDY:<BR>(1) पङ्किलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) सपङ्क (f. ङ्का),<BR>from pond whose water was m.:<BR>सपङ्कतोयात् सरसः,<BR>Ri. i. 18.;<BR>(3) कलुषः (षा, षं) (= turbid,<BR>foul).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mud-wall
MUD-WALL: मृत्कुड्यम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muff
MUFF: हस्तसम्भारः; ऊर्णामयं हस्तत्राणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muffin
MUFFIN: पिष्टकभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muffle
MUFFLE: अवगुण्ठयति (गुण्ठ्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>wrap, cover, conceal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muffler
MUFFLER:<BR>(1) अवगुण्ठनम्, let me remove your m.:<BR>अपनेष्यामि तावत्तेऽवगुण्ठनम्, Sa.;<BR>(2) अंशुकम् (when<BR>the sense is clear), Ki. ix. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muggy
MUGGY:<BR>we have m. weather now:<BR>अधुना सरसा<BR> अपि निर्वाततया तापकरा दिवसाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mulberry
MULBERRY:<BR>I The tree: नूदः<BR>or<BR>तूतः।<BR>II<BR>The fruit: नूदम्<BR>or<BR>तूतम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mulct
MULCT:<BR>I Subs: अर्थदण्डः: v. Fine.<BR>II Verb:<BR>v. To fine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mule
MULE:<BR>(1) अश्वतरः;<BR>(2) खेसरः;<BR>(3) वेसरः;<BR>(4) खरः,<BR>horses, m. s and asses:<BR>तुरङ्गान् खरगर्दभान्,<BR>Mat., f. अश्वतरी, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muleteer
MULETEER: खरवाहकः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mulish
MULISH: प्रतीपः (पा, पं): v. Obstinate,<BR>stubborn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mull
MULL (v.): वासयति (c. of वस्),<BR>m. ed:<BR>वासितः<BR>(ता, तं), D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muller
MULLER:<BR>(1) पेषणी;<BR>(2) शिलापट्टः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mullet
MULLET: रोहितः; रोहितमत्स्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mullion
MULLION: *वातायनादिविभागलम्बः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

multangular
MULTANGULAR:<BR>(1) बहुकोणः (णा, णं);<BR>(2)<BR>अनेकास्रः (स्रा, स्रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

multifarious
MULTIFARIOUS: नानाविधः (धा, धं): v. Various,<BR>manifold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

multiform
MULTIFORM:<BR>(1) बहुरूपः (पा, पं);<BR>(2) नैकरूपः<BR>(पा, पं);<BR>(3) नानारूपः (पा, पं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

multilateral
MULTILATERAL:<BR>(1) बहुभुजः (जा, जं);<BR>(2)<BR>भूरिभुजः (जा, जं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

multinomial
MULTINOMIAL: *बहुपदः (दा, दं). The m. theorem:<BR>बहुपदवृद्धितत्त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

multiple
MULTIPLE:<BR>(1) *आधारः, least common m.:<BR>*साधारणनीचाधारः;<BR>(2) expr. by भाज्य (f. ज्या)<BR>(= divisible).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

multiplicand
MULTIPLICAND: गुण्यः, Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

multiplication
MULTIPLICATION:<BR>(1) गुणनम्, Li.;<BR>(2) घातः,<BR>etc. (of the act only).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

multiplier
MULTIPLIER: गुणकः, Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

multiply
MULTIPLY (v. t.):<BR>I In arith.:<BR>(1) गुणयति,<BR>m. ing (we) get (1/6): गुणिते जातम् १/६, Li.;<BR>(2)<BR>हन्ति, आ-, नि-, (हन्, c. 2.), m. ied by three:<BR>त्रिनिघ्नः, Li.<BR>II To increase: q. v.: वर्धयति<BR>(c. of वृध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

multiply
MULTIPLY (v. i.):<BR>(1) बहुलीभवति;<BR>(2) वर्धते (वृध्,<BR>c. 1.): v. To increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

multitude
MULTITUDE:<BR>I A collection, number:<BR>(1)<BR>समूहः;<BR>(2) सङ्घः;<BR>(3) ओघः;<BR>(4) समवायः: v.<BR>Also many.<BR>II Of men: जनसमवायः and<BR>sim. comp.s.: v. Crowd.<BR>III = populace:<BR>(1) प्रजाः (pl. =people);<BR>(2) प्राकृताः (= com-<BR>-mon men).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

multitudinous
MULTITUDINOUS: बहुलः (ला, लं): v. Many,<BR>to crowd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mumble
MUMBLE: गजगजायते (nomi. ?): v. To mur-<BR>-mur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mummer
MUMMER: छद्मवेशिन् (m.)(?): v. Buffoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mummery
MUMMERY: माया (?): v. Jugglery, trick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mummy
MUMMY: सुगन्धौषधादिभिः परिरक्षितः शवः, Ph.:<BR>to<BR>beat a m.:<BR>मृतस्योपरि खड्गपातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mumfs
MUMFS: लालाशयशोथः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

munch
MUNCH: मुखं संवृत्य चर्वति (चर्व्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>chew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mundane
MUNDANE:<BR>(1) सांसारिकः (की, कं);<BR>(2) लौकिकः<BR>(की, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

municipal
MUNICIPAL: expr. by comp. or gen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

municipality
MUNICIPALITY: *क्षेममण्डलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

munificence
MUNIFICENCE:<BR>(1) वदान्यता;<BR>(2) त्यागशालिता;<BR>(3) मुक्तहस्तता; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

munificent
MUNIFICENT:<BR>(1) वदान्य (f. न्या);<BR>(2) दानशौण्ड<BR>(f. ण्डा);<BR>(3) त्यागशालिन् (f. नी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

munificently
MUNIFICENTLY:<BR>(1) मुक्तहस्तम्;<BR>(2) वदान्यतया (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muniment
MUNIMENT: दुर्गम्: v. Fort, fortification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

munition
MUNITION: v. Fortification.<BR>M. of war:<BR>युद्ध-<BR>सामग्री।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mural
MURAL: expr. by comp.,<BR>m. circle:<BR>*कुड्यवृत्तम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

murder
MURDER (subs.):<BR>(1) वधः (intentional:<BR>q. v.),<BR>to commit wife and friend-m.:<BR>स्त्री-<BR>सुहृद्वधं करोति, Mr. xi. 89.; m. of a Brāhmaṇa:<BR>कामतो (= intentional) ब्राह्मणवधः, Go.;<BR>(2) हत्या<BR>(not necessarily i.),<BR>m. of a father:<BR>पितृहत्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

murder
MURDER (v. t.):<BR>(1) expr. by subs:<BR>(2) हन्ति<BR>(हन्, c. 2.): v. To kill;<BR>(3) मारयति (c.<BR>of मृ) (rare), Mr. viii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

murderer
MURDERER: घातकः,<BR>secret m.:<BR>उपांशुघातकः, Vri.:<BR>v. Killer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

murderous
MURDEROUS:<BR>I Accompanied with murder:<BR>expr. by circumlo: v. Also bloody, cruel.<BR>II Intending murder:<BR>(1) हन्तुकामः (मा,<BR> मं),<BR>of m. intent:<BR>हन्तुकामबुद्धिः, Mr. ix.;<BR>(2)<BR>जिघांसु (mfn.),<BR>the m. beast:<BR>जिघांसुर्मृगः, Ki.<BR>xiv. 14. Ph.:<BR>in m. works:<BR>मारणात्मकेषु शास्त्रेषु,<BR>K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

murderously
MURDEROUSLY:<BR>(1) दारूणम् (= ferociously);<BR>(2) निष्ठुरम् (= cruelly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muriatic
MURIATIC: i. e. hydrochloric: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

murkily
MURKILY: expr. by adj.: v. Also obscurely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

murky
MURKY: तामसः (सी, सं): v. Dark, gloomy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

murmur
MURMUR (subs.):<BR>I A low sound: कलकलः।<BR>II A complaint: उत्क्रोशः (= cry: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

murmur
MURMUR (v.):<BR>I To make a low sound:<BR>कलकलं करोति।<BR>II To grumble: q. v.:<BR>खिटखिटायते (nomi.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

murmuring
MURMURING:<BR>I Lit.: Subs.: v. Murmur.<BR>II Adj.: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

murrain
MURRAIN: पशूनां मारी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muscle
MUSCLE:<BR>I Of the body: पेशी, मांस-, Bha.<BR>II A kind of fish: शम्बूकविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muscular
MUSCULAR:<BR>I Pertaining to muscles: by<BR>comp. or gen.,<BR>m. action:<BR>पेशीनां कर्म, Bha.<BR>II Strong, powerful: q. v.: मांसलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muse
MUSE (subs.):<BR>I Meditation: ध्यानम्।<BR>II<BR>Goddess of learing: विद्यादेवी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muse
MUSE (v.): ध्यायति (ध्यै, c. 1.): v. To medi-<BR>-tate, think.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

museum
MUSEUM: *कौतुकागारम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mushroom
MUSHROOM:<BR>(1) छत्रम्, -त्रा;<BR>(2) छत्रकः;<BR>(3)<BR>छत्राकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

music
MUSIC:<BR>I The art:<BR>(1) सङ्गीतम्,<BR>m. -room:<BR>सङ्गीत-<BR>शाला, Sa.;<BR>(2) गीतम् (= vocal m.),<BR>learnt vocal<BR>and instrumental m.:<BR>गीतं वादित्रञ्च प्रत्यविन्दत्,<BR>Mah.;<BR>(3) वाद्यम्<BR>or<BR>वादित्रम् (= instrumental<BR>m.);<BR>(4) गान्धर्वम्,<BR>to hear m.:<BR>गान्धर्वं श्रोतुम्,<BR>Mr. iii.;<BR>one who knows m.:<BR>गान्धर्वज्ञः, K. s.<BR>xi. 11.<BR>II Melody, harmony:<BR>(1) मूर्च्छना or<BR>मार्जना (= succession of modulated sounds),<BR>Si. i. 10.;<BR>(2) स्वनः (= sound), m. of lyre:<BR>तन्त्रीस्वनः, Mr.;<BR>(3) माधुर्यम् (= sweetness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

musical
MUSICAL:<BR>I Relating to music: expr. by<BR>comp.,<BR>in the special m. works:<BR>गान्धर्ववेदविशेषेषु,<BR>K.<BR>II. Fond of m.: सङ्गीतप्रियः (या, यं) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR>III Melodious, sweet: मधुरः<BR>(रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

musically
MUSICALLY: मधुरम्, Mr.: v. Melodiously,<BR>sweetly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

musician
MUSICIAN:<BR>(1) गान्धर्वज्ञ (f. ज्ञा);<BR>(2) गीतकोविदः<BR>(दा, दं) (vocal), Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

musk
MUSK:<BR>(1) कस्तूरी;<BR>(2) मृगनामिः;<BR>(3) मृगमदः।<BR>M.-bag.:<BR>(1) कस्तूरीमल्लिका;<BR>(2) मृगमदवासा;<BR>(3) अण्डः,-ण्डम् (when the sense is clear), Kuv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

musk-deer
MUSK-DEER: कस्तूरीमृगः (?)<BR>or<BR>कस्तूरिकामृगः, Kuv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

musk-melon
MUSK-MELON: खर्बूजम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

musk-rat
MUSK-RAT: गन्धमूषिकः; गन्धाखुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

musket
MUSKET: बन्दुकः,<BR>m.-ball:<BR>*बन्दुकगुलिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

musketeer
MUSKETEER: *बन्दुकभृत् (mfn.); *बन्दुकधारिन् (f.<BR>णी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

musketry
MUSKETRY: *बन्दुकाः (m. pl.), fire of m.:<BR>बन्दुकाग्निः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muslin
MUSLIN: *मम्मलम् (comp. Bengali मल्मल्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mussulman
MUSSULMAN: *महम्मदधर्सावलम्बिन् (f. नी);<BR>महम्मदीयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

must
MUST (subs.): द्राक्षानिष्पीडितं नवमद्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

must
MUST (v.):<BR>(1) अवश्यम् with future pass. part,<BR>if (you)<BR>m. go:<BR>अवश्यं यदि गन्तव्यम्, P. ; you<BR>m. tell (me)<BR>the reason:<BR>त्वयावश्यं कारणं वक्तव्यम्,<BR>Vet.;<BR>what m. come to pass:<BR>अवश्यभव्यः (व्या,<BR> व्यं), N.;<BR>(2) नियमेन (rare) with same cons.,<BR>I m. kill (him): नियमेन मया निवर्हणीयः, Ki.: v.<BR>Also should.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mustard
MUSTARD: सर्षपः,<BR>m.-oil:<BR>सर्षपतैलम्, Sr.<BR>Black<BR>m.:<BR>कृष्णिका, राजिका (rare), P. White m.:<BR>सिद्धार्थकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muster
MUSTER (subs.): expr. by verb.: v. Also<BR>collection, review.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muster
MUSTER (v. t.): समाहरति (हृ, c. 1.): v. To<BR>collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muster
MUSTER (v. i.):<BR>(1) समागच्छति (गम्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) समैति (इ, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muster-roll
MUSTER-ROLL: *संख्यानपत्रिका and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mustiness
MUSTINESS: कालुष्यम्: v. Foulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

musty
MUSTY: कलुषितः (ता, तं): v. Foul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mutability
MUTABILITY: परिवृत्तिशीलता, etc.: v. Also in-<BR>-constancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mutable
MUTABLE:<BR>(1) परिवृत्तिशीलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2)<BR>विकारवत् (f. ती) (gen. for the worse);<BR>(3)<BR>अनवस्थितः (ता, तं) (= inconstant, fickle: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mute
MUTE (adj.): मूकः (का, कं), with the birds m.:<BR>मूकाण्डजम्, Ku. iii. 42.: v. Dumb, speech-<BR>-less.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mute
MUTE (subs.):<BR>I Of birds: पुरीषम्, R.: v.<BR>Dung.<BR>II A consonant: *मूकः (का, कं). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">Page464</a>]<BR>III An attendant at a funeral: मृत-<BR>परिचारकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mute
MUTE (v.):<BR>I To cast off: उत्सृजति (सृज्, c.<BR>6.).<BR>II To dung: पुरीषमुत्सृजति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mutely
MUTELY:<BR>(1) मुकवत्;<BR>(2) निःशब्दम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mutilate
MUTILATE:<BR>I Lit.: व्यङ्गीकरोति,<BR>why you m.d<BR>your wife:<BR>किमर्थं त्वया भार्या व्यङ्गिता, P. i. 4.<BR>II Fig.: Perh. विकलीकरोति, “m.d poets”:<BR>विकलीकृतकवयः;<BR>the Vyaktiviveka and Ālochana<BR>are here only in a m.d form:<BR>व्यक्तिविवेकालोचन-<BR>ग्रन्थावत्र खण्डितावेव स्तः, Mahesha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mutilation
MUTILATION:<BR>I The act: व्यङ्गीकरणम्।<BR>II<BR>The state: वैकल्यम्।<BR>III Of works: *विकली-<BR>करणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mutineer
MUTINEER: विद्रोहिन् (f. णी) (?); अन्तःप्रकोप-<BR>कारिन् (f. णी) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mutinous
MUTINOUS:<BR>(1) विद्रोहजननः (नी, नं) (?);<BR>(2)<BR>अन्तःप्रकोपकरः (री, रं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mutinously
MUTINOUSLY: expr. by adj. or prest. part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mutiny
MUTINY (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) सैनिकविद्रोहः<BR>(?);<BR>(2) सैन्यप्रकोपः (?).<BR>II Fig.: tumult,<BR>uproar: q. v.: संरम्भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mutiny
MUTINY (v.):<BR>(1) विद्रोहं करोति (?);<BR>(2) अधि-<BR>जायते (जन्, c. 4 (with loc.) (?), D. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mutter
MUTTER (v.): अस्फुटं जल्पति (जल्प्, c. 1.) (of<BR>men) and sim. comp.s.,<BR>the sky looks sound-<BR>ing with m.ing thunder and rolling with wind:<BR>अम्बरं विस्पष्टाशनिनिस्वनेन रसतीवाघूर्णतीवानिलैः, Mr.<BR>v. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mutton
MUTTON:<BR>(1) मेषमांसम्;<BR>(2) मेषामिषम्, Bha.;<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mutual
MUTUAL:<BR>(1) परस्पर- in comp. or gen. (= one<BR>another: q. v.),<BR>m. love:<BR>परस्परस्य प्रीतिः,<BR>Raj.;<BR>(2) साधारण (f. णी) (= common),<BR>m.<BR>good:<BR>साधारणं श्रेयः, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mutually
MUTUALLY:<BR>(1) परस्परम्;<BR>(2) अन्योन्यम्;<BR>(3)<BR>मिथः,<BR>m. contending:<BR>मिथोविरोधिन् (f. नी), Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muzzle
MUZZLE (subs.):<BR>I Mouth: q. v.: मुखम्।<BR>II<BR>A fastening for the m.: मुखबन्धनम्, -नी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

muzzle
MUZZLE (v.): मुखं बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.): v.<BR>To bind, prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

my
MY<BR>(1) मम<BR>or<BR>मे (never at the beginning of a<BR>sentence)<BR>or<BR>मत् in comp., I for my part think<BR>so:<BR>मम तावन्मतमिदम्, Si.;<BR>you are my second<BR>heart:<BR>त्वमसि मे हृदयं द्वितीयम्, U. ; my wife:<BR>मद्गेहिनी, Me.;<BR>(2) मदीयः (या, यं),<BR>my milk:<BR>मदीयं<BR> पयः, R. ;<BR>like my mother:<BR>मदीया जननीव, R. ;<BR>(3) often not expr. when the meaning is<BR>clear,<BR>today is the tenth month from the demise<BR>of my father:<BR>अद्य दशमो मासस्तातस्योपरतस्य, Mu.;<BR>even my parents:<BR>पितरावपि, D. ;<BR>(4) मामकीनः<BR>(ना, नं) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

myriad
MYRIAD: अयुतम्; दशसहस्रम्;<BR>M.s. of:<BR>सहस्रशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

myrmidon
MYRMIDON: क्रूरपरिचरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

myrobalan
MYROBALAN: आमलकम्, -की।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

myrrh
MYRRH:<BR>(1) गन्धरसः;<BR>(2) रसगन्धः;<BR>(3) बोलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

myrtle
MYRTLE: लताविशेषः; *मूर्ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

myself
MYSELF:<BR>I In person: स्वयम्,<BR>I m.:<BR>स्वय-<BR>मेवाहम्, K.<BR>II. = me.: आत्मानम्,<BR>I will show<BR>m.:<BR>आत्मानं दर्शयिष्यामि, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mysterious
MYSTERIOUS:<BR>(1) गहनः (ना, नं) (= impene-<BR>-trable);<BR>(2) निगूढः (ढा, ढं) (= secret, obs-<BR>-cure);<BR>(3) दुर्ज्ञेयः and sim. comp.s. (= un-<BR>-intelligible);<BR>(4) तामसः (सी, सं) etc. (= dark).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mysteriously
MYSTERIOUSLY:<BR>(1) expr. with adj.;<BR>(2)<BR>गूढम्, नि- (= secretly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mystery
MYSTERY: निगूढतत्त्वम्, Ki. and sim. expr.<BR>s, m.ies<BR>of London:<BR>*लण्डनरहस्यानि (n.): v. Mysteri-<BR>-ous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mystic
MYSTIC, -AL:<BR>I Mysterious: q. v.: दुर्ज्ञेयः<BR>(या, यं).<BR>II Belonging to mystics: expr.<BR>by comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mystic
MYSTIC (subs.):<BR>(1) परमहंसः (?), Pa.;<BR>(2)<BR>ब्रह्मभिक्षुः (?), Pa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mystically
MYSTICALLY: expr. with adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mysticism
MYSTICISM:<BR>I Obscurity: निगूढता।<BR>II Doc-<BR>-trine of mystic: योगधर्मः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mystify
MYSTIFY:<BR>(1) गहनीकरीति (?);<BR>(2) निगूढीकरोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

myth
MYTH, -E: (?) इतिहासः पुरातनः, Mah.; पौराणिकी<BR> कथा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mythical
MYTHICAL:<BR>I Lit.: पौराणिकः (की, कं).<BR>II<BR>Imaginary, fanciful: काल्पनिकः (की, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mythologist
MYTHOLOGIST: पुराणज्ञः, Mah.; पुराणविद् (m.);<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

mythology
MYTHOLOGY: पुराणम् (specially of the 18<BR>Purāṇas of Hindus).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nab
NAB (v.): अकस्मात् गृह्वाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.): v. To<BR>catch, surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nabob
NABOB:<BR>I Lit.: *नबाबः।<BR>II Fig., a rich<BR>man: *नबाबः; भोगपतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nacre
NACRE, NAKER: शुक्त्युदरम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nadir
NADIR: हरिजतलम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nag
NAG:<BR>I A horse: q. v.: अश्वकः।<BR>II A para-<BR>-mour: जारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

naiad
NAIAD: जलदेवता; अप्सरस् (f.) (usually in the<BR>pl.) (= heavenly nymph).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nail
NAIL (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) नखः, to keep n.s:<BR>नखानि बिमर्ति, M. vi. 6.;<BR>having n.s:<BR>नखिन्<BR>(f. नी), H. ;<BR>n. -brush:<BR>*नखमार्जनी;<BR>(2)<BR>नखरः, striking with n.s (claws): नखप्रहारः,<BR>Mah. iii. Ph.:<BR>tooth and n.:<BR>आकेशाग्रादानखा-<BR>न्तात्, At.; on the n.: (= immediately) तत्-<BR>क्षणात्।<BR>II Of metal: कीलकः। Ph.:<BR>to hit n.<BR>on the head:<BR>मर्मणि विध्यति (व्यध्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nail
NAIL (v.): कीलयति (कील्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>fasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

naive
NAIVE:<BR>(1) सरलः (ला, लं): v. Śimple, in-<BR>-genuous;<BR>(2) प्रकृतिमधुरः (रा, रं), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

naively
NAIVELY: सहजसरलतया; स्वमावसौजन्येन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

naivete
NAIVETE:<BR>(1) सहजसरलता;<BR>(2) स्वभावसुजनता;<BR>(3) प्रकृतिमधुरता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

naked
NAKED:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) नग्न (f. ग्ना),<BR>what are you<BR>looking, n. woman:<BR>किं निरीक्षसे नग्निके, P. iv.<BR>62.;<BR>(2) अनावृतः (ता, तं) (= not covered,<BR>bare), Mah.;<BR>(3) विवस्त्र (f. स्त्रा) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (= without clothes), Mah.;<BR>(4)<BR>दिगम्बरः (रा, रं) (poet),<BR>made n.:<BR>चक्रे दिगम्बरः,<BR>K. s. xiii. 147.<BR>II Fig.: open, plain: अना-<BR>वृतः (ता, तं).<BR>III Mere, simple: केवलः<BR>(ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nakedly
NAKEDLY:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by adj.<BR>II Fig.,<BR>openly: स्पष्टम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nakedness
NAKEDNESS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) नग्नत्वम्, n. of Śiva:<BR>नग्नत्वं नीलकण्ठस्य, H. i.;<BR>(2) दिगम्बरत्वम्, Ku.;<BR>etc.<BR>II Openness, exposure: अनावृतता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

name
NAME (subs.):<BR>I Of person or thing:<BR>(1)<BR>नामन् (n.), only the n. of Duryodhana remains:<BR>नामैकं धार्तराष्ट्रस्य शेषम्, Vi.;<BR>who bear the mere<BR>n.:<BR>केवलं नामधारकाः, Pa.; with (their)<BR>father's<BR>n.:<BR>पितृनामैकपूर्वकम्, Y. :<BR>kept the n. of the son<BR>Chandrāpiḍa:<BR>सूनोश्चन्द्रापीड इति नाम चकार, K. ;<BR>to call by n.:<BR>नामग्राहमाह्वयति, S. k.;<BR>(2) नाम-<BR>धेयम्, asking the n.s of trees: नामधेयानि पृच्छन्तौ<BR>।शाखिनां, R. ; do (you) know them by n.: अपि<BR> ज्ञायन्ते नामघेयतः, Mu.<BR>(3) अभिधानम्,<BR>who is this<BR>girl and what is her n.:<BR>केयं कन्यका किममिधाना,<BR>K.<BR>II. Reputation, renown: q. v.: नामन्,<BR>whose n. even enemies approve:<BR>नाम यस्याभि-<BR>नन्दन्ति द्विषोऽपि, Ki. xi. 73.;<BR>bad n.:<BR>दुर्नाम;<BR>“men of n.”:<BR>नामशालिनः<BR>or<BR>ख्यातनामानः।<BR>III<BR>Authority: वचनम्, go and in my n. rebuke:<BR>गच्छ मद्वचनात् । उपालमस्व, Sa. vi.<BR>IV In<BR>adjuration:<BR>in the n. of gods:<BR>देवान् साक्षीकृत्य।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

name
NAME (v. t.):<BR>I To call: q. v.: नाम करोति or<BR>कुरूते (with gen.), and then should n. (him):<BR>ततश्च नाम कुर्वीत, V. p.;<BR>therefore n.d him Aja<BR>after God:<BR>अतो ब्रह्मणो नाम्ना तमजं चकार, R. v.<BR>36.<BR>II To mention by n.: नाम करोति, गृह्नाति<BR>(ग्रह्, c. 9.)<BR>or<BR>ब्रवीति (ब्रू, c. 2.), etc.;<BR>still<BR>n.s that wretch:<BR>अद्यापि तस्यैव पापस्य नाम गृह्वाति,<BR>Mr. viii.<BR>III To appoint, fix.: नाम्ना<BR> निर्दिशति (दिश्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

named
NAMED (adj.):<BR>(1) नाम (rarely नाम्ना = by<BR>name);<BR>n. Vimardaka:<BR>विमर्दको नाम, D. ii.;<BR>a town n. Valabhi:<BR>वलमी नाम नगरी, D. vi.;<BR>(2) by comp., of a swan n. Karpūrakeli:<BR>कर्पूरकेलिनाम्नो राजहंसस्य, H.: v. Also to call.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nameless
NAMELESS:<BR>(1) अनामकः (का, कं);<BR>(2) नामहीनः<BR>(ना, नं) and sim. comp.s.: v. Name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

namely
NAMELY:<BR>animals are of two kinds, n., worldly<BR>and free:<BR>जीवा द्विविधाः संसारिणो मुक्ताश्च, D. s. iii.;<BR>some say truths are seven, n., animate and inani-<BR>mate beings, allurement, bond, control, casting off<BR>and emancipation:<BR>केचन सप्त तत्त्वानीति वर्णयन्ति, तदाह<BR> जीवाजीवास्रवबन्धसंवरनिर्जरमोक्षास्तत्त्वानीति, D. s.;<BR>there are two ways of correcting disaffective peo-<BR>ple, n., favour and chastisement:<BR>इह खलु विरक्तानां<BR> प्रकृतीनां द्विविधं प्रतिविधानम्, तद्यथानुग्रहो निग्रहश्चे ति;<BR>it is of two kinds, n., visible and invisible:<BR>तद्<BR> द्विविधं दृष्टादृष्टभेदात्, D. s. xi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

namesake
NAMESAKE:<BR>(1) सनामन् (mfn.);<BR>(2) समनामन्<BR>(mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

naming
NAMING (subs.):<BR>(1) नामकरणम्;<BR>(2) नामग्रहणम्;<BR>etc.: v. Name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nap
NAP (subs.):<BR>I A short sleep: स्वल्पनिद्रा (?):<BR>v. Sleep.<BR>II Down: लोमन् (n.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nap
NAP (v.): स्वल्पं<BR>or<BR>क्षण स्वपिति (स्वप्, c. 2.) (?):<BR>v. To sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nape
NAPE: of the neck:<BR>(1) घाटाः<BR>(2) कृकाटिका;<BR>(3) अवटुः:<BR>To turn by the n.:<BR>अर्द्धचन्द्रं दत्त्वा<BR> निःसारयति, P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

napkin
NAPKIN: *मुखमार्जनी and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

napless
NAPLESS: जीर्ण (f. र्णा) (= decayed, old): v.<BR>Threadbare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

narcissus
NARCISSUS: लार्कसाख्ये पुष्पे, तत्प्रसविन्यां लतायाञ्च।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

narcotic
NARCOTIC, -AL (adj.)):<BR>(1) निद्रादायिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) स्वप्नकरः (री, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

narcotic
NARCOTIC (subs.): उपविषम्, ‘सप्त विषजातयः’,<BR>Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nard
NARD:<BR>(1) नलदम्;<BR>(2) जटामांसी;<BR>(3) जटिला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

narrate
NARRATE: वर्णयति, उप-, (वर्ण्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>relate, describe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

narration
NARRATION:<BR>I Description, relation: वर्णना।<BR>II Story: कथा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

narrative
NARRATIVE (subs.):<BR>(1) कथा (= story);<BR>(2)<BR>वर्णना (= description).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

narrative
NARRATIVE (adj.): expr. by comp. or adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

narrator
NARRATOR: कथकः (= tell-tale); वर्णयितृ (f. त्री)<BR>(= describer).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

narrow
NARROW (adj.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अविस्तृतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) अल्पपरिसरः (रा, रं);<BR>(3) संकीर्ण (f. र्णा) (?).<BR>II Mean: क्षुद्र (f. द्रा).<BR>III Exact: सूक्ष्म<BR>(f. क्ष्मा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

narrow
NARROW (v. t.): सं-क्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.): v.<BR>To contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

narrow
NARROW (v. i.): सं-क्षिप्यते (pass. of क्षिप्), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

narrowly
NARROWLY:<BR>I With difficulty: कथं कथमपि।<BR>II Closely, minutely: सूक्ष्मम्।<BR>III Con-<BR>-tractedly: संक्षेपेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

narrow-minded
NARROW-MINDED:<BR>(1) क्षुद्रमनस् (mfn.);<BR>(2)<BR>अल्पचेतस् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

narrowness
NARROWNESS:<BR>I Contractedness: संकीर्णता (?)<BR>II Meanness: क्षुद्रता।<BR>III Poverty: दैन्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

narwhal
NARWHAL, NARWAL, NARWHALE: *एकशृङ्गिन्<BR>(m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nasal
NASAL: अनुनासिकः (की, कं).<BR>N. dot:<BR>अनुस्वारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nasalize
NASALIZE: नासिकया उच्चारयति (c. of चर्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nascent
NASCENT:<BR>(1) जायमानः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) उत्पद्यमानः<BR>(ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nastily
NASTILY: कुत्सितम्: v. Dirtily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nastiness
NASTINESS: कुत्सितता: v. Dirtiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nasty
NASTY: कुत्सितः (ता, तं): v. Dirty, foul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

natal
NATAL: जन्म- in comp.,<BR>n. day:<BR>जन्मदिनम्, Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nation
NATION: no equiv.: जातिः is used, but very<BR>ambiguous: better expr. with देशीयाः<BR>(= natives)<BR>or<BR>लोकाः (= people), all other n.s:<BR>*अपरापरदेशीयाः; a n. is the unity of a people:<BR>*प्रजानामैक्यं देशीयत्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

national
NATIONAL:<BR>(1) देश- in comp., n. language:<BR>देशभाषा;<BR>(2) देशीयः (या, यं),<BR>n. dress:<BR>देशीयवेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nationality
NATIONALITY: देशामिमानिता and sim. comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nationally
NATIONALLY: expr. by comp. or circumlo.:<BR>v. Also wholly, generally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

native
NATIVE (adj.):<BR>I Natal: जन्म- in comp.,<BR>yet<BR>who forgets his n. land:<BR>तथापि केन वा जन्मभूमिर्न<BR> स्मर्यते, V. p.:<BR>n. language:<BR>मातृभाषा।<BR>II Born<BR>with one:<BR>(1) सहजः (जा, जं),<BR>n. unsteadi-<BR>ness:<BR>सहजचापलम्, Si.;<BR>(2) स्वभावजः (जा, जं),<BR>n. dignity:<BR>स्वमावजं धाम, Ki. ii.<BR>III Not<BR>foreign: देशीयः (या, यं).<BR>IV Not artificial:<BR>अकृत्रिमः (मा, मं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

native
NATIVE (subs.):<BR>(1) देशीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) देश-<BR>वासिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) gen. by deriv.,<BR>n. of<BR>Ayodhyā:<BR>आयोध्यिकः, U. N.B. The names of<BR>countries also indicate their n.s,<BR>n. s of<BR>Persia:<BR>पारसिकाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nativity
NATIVITY:<BR>I Birth: q. v.: जन्मन्- (n.),<BR>sign of<BR>n.:<BR>जन्मराशिः।<BR>II Horoscope: जन्मपत्रिका;<BR>great, short work on n.:<BR>बृहज्जातकम्, लघुजातकम्;<BR>to cast, calculate n.:<BR>जातकं निरूपयति, गणयति;<BR>verse about n.:<BR>जातकश्लोकः, M. on. R. iii. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

natural
NATURAL (adj.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) स्वाभाविकः<BR>(की, कं),<BR>n. fragrance:<BR>स्वाभाविकं सौरम्यम्,<BR>R.;<BR>(2) नैसर्गिकः (की, कं), n. opposition:<BR>नैसर्गिको विरोधः, R. vi. 46.;<BR>(3) सहजः (जा, जं)<BR>(= born with one),<BR>n. affection:<BR>सहजस्नेहः, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">Page467</a>]<BR>Ki.;<BR>(4) प्रकृतिसिद्ध (f. द्धा),<BR>this is n. for great<BR>men:<BR>प्रकृतिसिद्धमिदं हि महात्मनाम्, H.;<BR>(5)<BR>निसर्गजः (जा, जं), etc. (rare),<BR>n. friend:<BR>स्वभावजं<BR> मित्रम्, H.;<BR>n. death:<BR>स्वामाविकमृत्युः;<BR>n. caves<BR>or reservoir:<BR>देवखातम्। Ph.: it is n. for...<BR>better expr. by subs.: v. Nature (V).<BR>II.<BR>Of the nature: प्राकृतिकः (की, कं); प्रकृति- in<BR>comp.<BR>III Resembling the object imi-<BR>-tated: स्वरूप- in comp.: v. True.<BR>IV Ille-<BR>-gitimate:<BR>(1) गूढजः (जा, जं) (born in pri-<BR>-vate), Y.;<BR>(2) *बीजजः (जा, जं) (after<BR>क्षेत्रजः). Miscell.:<BR>n. history:<BR>*प्राणितत्त्वम्;<BR>n.<BR>philosophy:<BR>*पदार्थविज्ञानम्;<BR>n. theology:<BR>*प्राकृतं<BR> ब्रह्मदर्शनम्;<BR>n. order:<BR>*प्रकृतश्रेणिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

natural
NATURAL (subs.): यथाजातः (ता, तं): v. Idiot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

naturalism
NATURALISM:<BR>I Lit.: स्वाभाविकावस्था।<BR>II Theo.:<BR>*प्रकृतिवादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

naturalist
NATURALIST:<BR>I In gen.: प्राणितत्त्वविद् (mfn.);<BR>etc.<BR>II Theo.: *प्रकृतिवादिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

naturalization
NATURALIZATION: v. Naturalize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

naturalize
NATURALIZE:<BR>I To make as if native: देशीयं<BR>(f. यां) करोति (?);<BR>n.d German:<BR>*लब्धजर्मना-<BR>धिकारः; जर्मनीकृतः।<BR>II To adopt: स्वीकरोति।<BR>III To adapt: उपयुक्तं (f. क्तां) करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

naturally
NATURALLY:<BR>I By nature:<BR>(1) by comp.,<BR>for bad men are n. not friend of the good:<BR>प्रकृत्यमित्रा हि सतामसाधवः, Ki.; n. complaisant:<BR>निसर्गदक्षिण (f. णा), Si. xv. 68.;<BR>(2) स्वमावतः;<BR>(3) प्रकृत्या;<BR>(4) निसर्गेण।<BR>II By birth: q. v.:<BR>जन्मना।<BR>III Without addition:<BR>a new cloud<BR>is n. beautiful:<BR>केवलोऽपि सुभगो नवाम्बुदः, R. ii.<BR>80.;<BR>pearls are n. pleasing to the eye:<BR>प्रागेव<BR> मुक्ता नयनाभिरामाः, R. xvi. 69.<BR>IV Sponta-<BR>-neously: स्वतः, good men are n. bent for others:<BR>स्वत एव सतां परार्थता, N. ii. 61. V. As a natural<BR>consequence: perh. स्वत एव: v. Indis-<BR>-putably, necessarily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nature
NATURE:<BR>I The creation, the universe:<BR>q. v.: सृष्टिः।<BR>II The original cause: प्रकृतिः।<BR>III Kind, sort: q. v.: प्रकारः।<BR>IV Subs-<BR>-tance, purport: q. v.: भावः। V. Natural<BR>constitution:<BR>(1) स्वभावः,<BR>for n. is at the head<BR>above all qualities:<BR>अतीत्य हि गुणान् सर्वान् स्वमावो<BR>मूर्ध्नि वर्तते, H.;<BR>(2) प्रकृतिः,<BR>it is the n. of the<BR>great:<BR>प्रकृतिः खलु सा महीयसः, Ki.;<BR>(3) निसर्गः<BR>(mostly as =adv.),<BR>this grove is beautiful<BR>by n.:<BR>निसर्गरमणीयोऽयमारामः, Pra.;<BR>(4) भावः<BR>in comp.,<BR>of impure n.:<BR>अशुद्धभावः (वा, वं)<BR>Mah.;<BR>(5) शीलम् (mostly in comp.),<BR>for it<BR>is the n. of inebriety and insanity:<BR>शीलं हि<BR> मदोन्मादयोः, D. ii.;<BR>bad n.d:<BR>दुःशीलः (ला, लं).<BR>VI Essential n.: स्वरूपम्, n. of the soul:<BR>आत्मस्वरूपम्, S. vii. Ph.:<BR>to attend to, satisfy<BR>a call of n.:<BR>मैत्रं करोति, V. p. iii. 13. 8.; शौचं<BR> करोति, Mah. s. 193. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

natured
NATURED: by comp.,<BR>good n.:<BR>सुशीलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

naught
NAUGHT (subs.): शून्यम्।<BR>To set at n.:<BR>न तृणाय<BR> मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

naught
NAUGHT (adj.): अकिञ्चित्करः (री, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

naughty
NAUGHTY: दुष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं): V. Also vicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nausea
NAUSEA:<BR>I Sea-sickness: उत्क्लेदः, Wilson.;<BR>वमिः।<BR>II Fig.: loathing: जुगुप्सा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nauseate
NAUSEATE (v. t.):<BR>I To sicken: उत्क्लेदं जनयति<BR>(c. of जन्) (?).<BR>II Fig.: जुगुप्सते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nauseous
NAUSEOUS: जुगुप्सितः (ता, तं): v. Loathesome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nauseousness
NAUSEOUSNESS: जुगुप्सितता; better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nautical
NAUTICAL: नाविक- in comp., n. almanac:<BR>*नाविकपञ्जिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

naval
NAVAL:<BR>(1) समुद्र- in comp.,<BR>n. fight:<BR>*समुद्र-<BR>युद्धम्;<BR>(2) सामुद्रिकः (की, कं): v. Also D. vi.,<BR>R. iv. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nave
NAVE:<BR>I Of a wheel:<BR>(1) नाभिः (भी) (f.);<BR>(2) पिण्डिः (ण्डी) (f.).<BR>II Of a church: perh.<BR>नाभिः; मध्यमागः<BR>III Fig.: नाभिः,<BR>you are the<BR>n. of this world:<BR>त्वमस्य जगतो नाभिः, V. p.v.<BR>7. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

navel
NAVEL: नाभिः,<BR>n. -string:<BR>नाभिनालम्, R. v. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

navigable
NAVIGABLE:<BR>(1) नाव्यः (व्या, व्यं)<BR>made n.<BR>rivers fordable:<BR>नाव्या नदीः सुप्रतराश्चकार, R. iv.<BR>31.;<BR>(2) नौतार्य (f. र्या), A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

navigate
NAVIGATE:<BR>I To sail: पोतेन<BR>or<BR>नौकया परिक्रामति<BR>(क्रम्, c. 1 (?).<BR>II To direct, steer: चाल-<BR>यति (c. of चल्) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

navigation
NAVIGATION:<BR>I The art: पोतसञ्चालनकला and<BR>sim. comp.s. (?).<BR>II The act: Ph.:<BR>inland<BR>n.,<BR>नद्यादिषु पोतचालनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

navigator
NAVIGATOR: नौचालनविद् (mfn (?); पोतसञ्चा-<BR>लनपटु (mfn (?); etc.: v. Also sailor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

navy
NAVY: पोतावलिः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nay
NAY: v. No. Ph.:<BR>N. more:<BR>अघिकञ्चः v.<BR>Moreover.<BR>N. rather:<BR>वरम्: v. Rather,<BR>better.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neap
NEAP (adj.):<BR>n. -tide:<BR>असंपूर्णा वेला (?): v.<BR>Tide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

near
NEAR (prep.):<BR>(1) उप- in comp., n. Bhaimī:<BR>उपभैमि, N.;<BR>(2) आरात् (with abl.),<BR>n. the<BR>forest:<BR>आराद्वनात्, S. k.;<BR>(3) निकषा (with<BR>acc.),<BR>n. Lankā:<BR>लङ्कां निकषा, Si.;<BR>(4) समया<BR>(with acc.): v. Near (adj. and adv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

near
NEAR (adj.):<BR>I In time: आसन्न (f. न्ना),<BR>“n.<BR>death”:<BR>आसन्नमृत्यु (mfn.), M. n.: v. Approa-<BR>-ching.<BR>II In place:<BR>(1) निकटस्थ (f. स्था);<BR>(2) समीपवर्तिन् (f. नी),<BR>very n. the fire of heart-<BR>ache:<BR>*समीपतरवर्ति हृदयशोकाग्नेः, K.;<BR>(3) आसन्न<BR>(f. न्ना), प्रति-,<BR>at heart, yet not n.:<BR>हृदयस्थमना-<BR>सन्नम, R.;<BR>(4) सन्निहितः (ता, तं), and here (her)<BR>superior is not n.:<BR>न च सन्निहितोऽत्र गुरुजनः, Sa.;<BR>(5) सन्निकृष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं);<BR>(6) अभ्यर्ण (f. र्णा)<BR>(rare);<BR>(7) उपोढ (f. ढा) (rare).<BR>III Inti-<BR>-mate, dear: q. v.: आसन्न (f. न्ना) (?),<BR>does<BR>not admit me in n. concerns:<BR>न मामासन्नकार्येष्व-<BR>भ्यन्तरीकरोति, D. viii.<BR>IV Of roads: perh.<BR>आसन्न (f. न्ना); सन्निहित (f. ता): v. Straight.<BR>V Of relation: निकटः (टा, टं), n. relation:<BR>निकटबन्धुः।<BR>VI Close-fisted: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

near
NEAR (adv.):<BR>I Not remote:<BR>to be n.:<BR>समीपे<BR> वर्तते, Sa.;<BR>came n. the king:<BR>राजान्तिकमाजगाम,<BR>K.;<BR>coming^1 n.er and n.er:<BR>अन्तिकान्तिकगतः<BR>(ता, तं), Ki. ix. 21.;<BR>keep him n.:<BR>तं पार्श्वे<BR> करोति, K.;<BR>n. situated:<BR>निकटस्थ (f. स्था). N.B.<BR>Note the use of acc. after verbs of motion<BR>and of loc. after other verbs.<BR>II Nearly:<BR>q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

near
NEAR (v.): उपसरति (सृ, c. 1.), K.: v. To<BR>approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nearly
NEARLY (adj.):<BR>I Within a little:<BR>(1) प्रायः<BR>(= almost: q. v.),<BR>n. dead:<BR>मृतप्रायः (या, यं);<BR>(2) किञ्चिदूनम् (= little less),<BR>n. ten thousand<BR>winters:<BR>किञ्चिदूनं शरदामयुतम्, R. x. 1.<BR>II<BR>Closely: expr. with adj.: v. Near (VI)<BR>III Pressingly: भृशम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nearness
NEARNESS:<BR>I Of time: आसन्नता।<BR>II Of place:<BR>(1) आसन्नता;<BR>(2) नैकट्यम्;<BR>(3) सामीप्यम्; etc.<BR>III Kindred: नैकट्यम् (?).<BR>IV Stinginess:<BR>बद्धमुष्टिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

near-sighted
NEAR-SIGHTED: अदूरदर्शिन् (f. नी): v. Short-<BR>-sighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neat
NEAT (adj.):<BR>(1) शोमनः (ना, नं) (= fine:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(2) शुद्ध (f. द्धा) (= clean, pure:<BR>q. v.),<BR>n. brandy:<BR>*शुद्धवारूणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neat
NEAT (subs.): गावः (m. pl.): v. Cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neat-herd
NEAT-HERD:<BR>(1) गोपालः;<BR>(2) गोरक्षकः: v. Cow-<BR>-herd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neatness
NEATNESS:<BR>(1) शोभनता: v. Fineness, elegance;<BR>(2) शुद्धता: v. Cleanness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nebula
NEBULA: *गगनकलङ्कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nebulous
NEBULOUS: मेघाच्छन्न (f. न्ना): v. Cloudy,<BR>misty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

necessarian
NECESSARIAN:<BR>(1) दैष्टिकः;<BR>(2) दैवप्रमाणकः (= fata-<BR>-list).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

necessarianism
NECESSARIANISM: दैष्टिकता;<BR>(2) *अवश्यम्भववादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

necessarily
NECESSARILY:<BR>(1) अवश्यम्: v. Must;<BR>(2)<BR>नियतम्: v. Certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

necessary
NECESSARY (adj.):<BR>I Subs., as must be:<BR>(1)<BR>अवश्यम्भाविन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) अवश्यमव्य (f. व्या),<BR>in (all) n. (matters): अवश्यभव्येषु, N. i. 120.<BR>II Indispensable, requisite:<BR>(1) आवश्यकीयः<BR>(या, यं),<BR>satisfying the n. calls of nature:<BR>शौच-<BR>मावश्यकं कृत्वा, Mah. s. 193. 4.;<BR>(2) प्रयोजनीयः<BR>(या, यं).<BR>III Not free: परवत् (f. ती): v.<BR>Dependent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

necessary
NECESSARY (subs.):<BR>I Anything n.: expr.<BR>by adj.<BR>II A privy: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

necessitarian
NECESSITARIAN: *अवश्यम्भववादिन् (f. नी): v.<BR>Necessarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

necessitate
NECESSITATE:<BR>I To compel: q. v.: expr.<BR>with बलात्।<BR>II To make indispensable:<BR>expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

necessitious
NECESSITIOUS: निःस्व (f. स्वा): v. Indigent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

necessity
NECESSITY:<BR>I Unavoidableness: अवश्यम्भाविता।<BR>II Requisiteness: आवश्यकीयता।<BR>III Indi-<BR>-gence: दैन्यम्।<BR>IV Anything necessary: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">Page469</a>]<BR>प्रयोजनम्।<BR>V Fate, fatality:<BR>(1) दिष्टम्;<BR>(2)<BR>मवितव्यता, V.;<BR>(3) नियतिः, J.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neck
NECK:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) ग्रीवा,<BR>long n.ed:<BR>दीर्घग्रीव<BR>(f. वा), U.;<BR>with the n. turned up:<BR>उद्ग्रीव<BR>(f. वा), Ki. vii. 22.;<BR>(2) गलः,<BR>putting his<BR>feet on our n.s:<BR>कृत्वा पदं नो गले, Mu. iii.; who<BR>will seize him by the n. (and turn him out): य<BR> एनं गलहस्तयति, H. iii.<BR>or<BR>अर्द्धचन्द्रं दत्त्वा निःसारयति,<BR>P. i. 3.;<BR>(3) कणठः (= throat),<BR>like a medal<BR>on his n.:<BR>अस्य कण्ठे निष्कमिव, Ku. ii. 49.;<BR>(4) कन्धरा (rare);<BR>(5) शिरोधरा (poet.).<BR>II Of a<BR>vessel: गलः।<BR>III Of land: भूमागः।<BR>N.<BR>break:<BR>गलग्रहः; N. and crop: v. Completely,<BR>utterly.<BR>On the n. of:<BR>उपकण्ठम् (with gen.):<BR>v. After.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neck-band
NECK-BAND, NECK-CLOTH: *गलावरणम्; ग्रैवेयकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

necklace
NECKLACE:<BR>(1) हारः,<BR>n. of pearls:<BR>मौक्तिकहारः<BR>Ma. vi.;<BR>(2) माला (= wreath), (also मुक्ता-<BR>कलापः, Ku.; मुक्तावली, R.; rarely मुक्तालता,<BR>Si.). Indra tied to me a n. of Mandāra flowers:<BR>मम॥ मन्दारमाला हरिणा पिनद्धा, Sa. vii.;<BR>(2)<BR>कण्ठिका, Ku.;<BR>N. of seven strings:<BR>सप्तनाली (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

necrology
NECROLOGY: v. Obituary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

necromancer
NECROMANCER: प्रेतसिद्धः (द्धा, द्धं): v. Magi-<BR>-cian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

necromancy
NECROMANCY: प्रेतसिद्धिः: v. Magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nectar
NECTAR:<BR>I Of gods:<BR>(1) अमृतम्;<BR>(2) सुधा;<BR>(3) पी(पे)यूषम्।<BR>II Of flowers:<BR>(1) मघु (n.);<BR>(2) मकरन्दः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nectarean
NECTAREAN:<BR>(1) सुधामयः (यी, यं);<BR>(2) अमृतमयः<BR>(यी, यं);<BR>(3) by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nectarine
NECTARINE (subs.): ‘पिच्च’जातीयफलविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

need
NEED (subs.):<BR>I Necessity:<BR>(1) प्रयोजनम्,<BR>“at<BR>thy n.”:<BR>प्रयोजनापेक्षितया; what n. of this pair:<BR>किमनेन । युगलेन प्रयोजनम्, K.;<BR>(2) अर्थः: v.<BR>Object.<BR>II Want: q. v.: अभावः।<BR>III Rea-<BR>-son or occasion:<BR>no n. of quarrelling:<BR>*विवादेन<BR> किम्;<BR>there is no n. of going there:<BR>*तास्ति प्रयोजनं<BR> तत्र गमने।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

need
NEED (v.): expr. by subs.: v. Also to re-<BR>-quire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

needful
NEEDFUL:<BR>I Necessary: q. v.<BR>II Indigent:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neediness
NEEDINESS: दैन्यम्: v. Indigence, poverty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

needle
NEEDLE:<BR>(1) सूचिः<BR>or<BR>सूची, the eye of a n.:<BR>सूचिरन्ध्रम्;<BR>the point of a n.:<BR>सूच्यग्रम्; n. woman:<BR>सूचिका;<BR>to sew with a sharp n.:<BR>तीक्ष्णया सूच्या<BR> सीव्यति, Kāśikā;<BR>(2) सेवनी,<BR>n. -maker:<BR>सेवनी-<BR>कारः (?).<BR>The magnetic n.:<BR>*अयस्कान्तशलाका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

needle-work
NEEDLE-WORK:<BR>(1) सूत्रकर्मन् (n.);<BR>(2) सूचि-<BR>कर्मन् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

needless
NEEDLESS:<BR>(1) निष्प्रयोजनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) निरर्थकः<BR>(का, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

needlessly
NEEDLESSLY: निरर्थकम्: v. Unnecessarily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

needlessness
NEEDLESSNESS:<BR>(1) निरर्थकता;<BR>(2) निष्प्रयोजनता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

needs
NEEDS (adv.): gen. with must: अवश्यमेव।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

needy
NEEDY:<BR>(1) निःस्व (f. स्वा);<BR>(2) दीनः (ना, नं):<BR>v. Poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nefarious
NEFARIOUS: पापिष्ठ- in comp.: v. Wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nefariously
NEFARIOUSLY: expr. with adj. or by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nefariousness
NEFARIOUSNESS: पापिष्ठताः v. Wickedness,<BR>heinousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

negation
NEGATION:<BR>(1) नास्तिवादः (after, D.s.);<BR>(2)<BR>अपह्नवः: v. Denial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

negative
NEGATIVE (adj.):<BR>I Implying negation:<BR>अस्वीकारसूचक (f. चिका).<BR>II Of propositions,<BR>etc.: नास्तिगर्म (f. र्मा) (D. s. has स्यान्नास्तीति).<BR>III Opposed to positive:<BR>n. quantity:<BR>क्षय-<BR>राशिः (after Vij.);<BR>n. sign:<BR>क्षयचिह्वम् (अर्द्ध-<BR>बिन्दुः was the Hindu sign).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

negative
NEGATIVE (subs.):<BR>and it is the nature of the n.<BR>that it denies the existence of its connection:<BR>नव-<BR>श्चैष स्वभावो यत् स्वसम्बन्धिनोऽमावं बोधयति, S. i. 4.;<BR>to reply in the n.:<BR>नेति वदति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

negative
NEGATIVE (v.):<BR>I To disapprove: प्रत्याख्याति<BR>(ख्या, c. 2.), S.<BR>II. To reject: प्रतिक्षिपति<BR>(क्षिप्, c. 6.), D. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nagatively
NAGATIVELY:<BR>I With denial: नेति, नास्तीति,<BR>etc. according to the nature of the ques-<BR>-tion.<BR>II Opp. to positively: स्यानास्तीति<BR> न्यायेन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neglect
NEGLECT (v.): उपेक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.),<BR>you should<BR>not n. advice:<BR>शासनमिदं त्वया नोपेक्षितव्यम्: v.<BR>To disregard, despise, attend and not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neglect
NEGLECT (subs.): उपेक्षा: v. Disregard, in-<BR>-attention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neglectful
NEGLECTFUL:<BR>(1) expr. by verb.;<BR>(2) अन-<BR>वहितः (ता, तं) (= inattentive).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neglectfully
NEGLECTFULLY: उपेक्षयाः v. Also inattentively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

negligence
NEGLIGENCE:<BR>(1) शैथिल्यम्;<BR>(2) उपेक्षा (= neg-<BR>-lect).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

negligent
NEGLIGENT:<BR>(1) expr. by verb. or subs.,<BR>he<BR>is n. of his duties:<BR>कृत्यानि स उपेक्षते<BR>or<BR>नाद्रियते;<BR>(2) अनवहितः (ता, तं): v. Needless, careless.<BR>(3) शिथिलः (ला, लं) (= slack).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

negligently
NEGLIGENTLY:<BR>(1) अनादरेणम्, Ki.;<BR>(2) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

negotiate
NEGOTIATE (v.): व्यवहरति (= to treat); often<BR>not expr. or by circumlo.,<BR>sent ambassadors to<BR>n. for peace:<BR>दूतान् विससर्ज सन्धये।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

negotiation
NEGOTIATION:<BR>(1) संवादः (= conference: q. v.),<BR>(2) व्यवहारः (= transaction, conduct)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

negotiator
NEGOTIATOR: दूतः (= ambassador);<BR>(2) मध्यस्थः<BR>(= middle man);<BR>(3) व्यवहर्तृ (m.) (= trans-<BR>-actor).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

negro
NEGRO: *हाप्सिन् (m.),<BR>Negress:<BR>*हाप्सिनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

negus
NEGUS: पानीयविशेषः; मैरेयम्; (??) *माधवं मधु।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neigh
NEIGH (v.): हेषते<BR>or<BR>ह्रेषते (हेष्,<BR>or<BR>ह्रेष्, c. 1.),<BR>if you n. like a horse:<BR>यद्यश्ववद्धेषसे, P. iv. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neigh
NEIGH, -ING (subs.): हेषा<BR>or<BR>ह्रेषा;<BR>(2) हे(ह्रे)षितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neighbour
NEIGHBOUR (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रतिवेशिन् (f. नी),<BR>the n.s:<BR>प्रतिवेशिवर्गः, Mr. iii.;<BR>n. ing house-<BR>holder:<BR>प्रतिवेशिकगृहपतिः, Mr. vi.;<BR>(2) प्रति-<BR>वासिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) प्रातिवेश्य (f. श्या) (rare),<BR>n.ing fortune-teller:<BR>प्रातिवेश्यः कार्तान्तिकः, D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neighbourhood
NEIGHBOURHOOD: सन्निहितप्रदेशः। Ph.:<BR>“in the<BR>n. of death”:<BR>मृत्युसन्निधौ,<BR>“law of n.”:<BR>प्रतिवेशि-<BR>धर्मः;<BR>in the n. of Mithilā:<BR>मिथिलोपकण्ठे, Vi. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neighbouring
NEIGHBOURING (adj.):<BR>I Of men: v. Neigh-<BR>-bour.<BR>II Of places, etc.: निकटवर्तिन् (f. नी):<BR>v. Near, adjoining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neighbourly
NEIGHBOURLY (adj.): by comp., n. dealing:<BR>प्रतिवेशिव्यवहारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neither
NEITHER (conj.):<BR>(1) न॥न वा,<BR>only nine cate-<BR>gories n. more nor less:<BR>नवैव द्रव्याणि नाधिकानि न<BR> न्यूनानि वा, V. d.;<BR>(2) न च॥न च<BR>n. sex nor<BR>age:<BR>न च लिङ्गं न च वयः, U.;<BR>(3) न॥न,<BR>n.<BR>very high nor very low:<BR>नात्युच्छ्रितं नातिनीचम्,<BR>G.;<BR>(4) न॥न च,<BR>nor father n. brothers:<BR>न<BR> पिता न च भ्रातरः, Kat.;<BR>(5) न च॥नापि, S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neither
NEITHER (pron.):<BR>(1) expr. with: एकः (का,<BR> कं), अपि<BR>or<BR>एकतरः (रा, रं) and न,<BR>“both, one, or<BR>n.”:<BR>उपयमेकं नैकतरं वा;<BR>you can enjoy n.:<BR>न<BR> त्वयेकमपि भोक्तुं शक्यम्;<BR>(2) with उभ (= both)<BR>and न।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neogamic
NEOGAMIC: नवकृतपरिग्रहः: v. To marry, newly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neology
NEOLOGY:<BR>I Lit.: नवशब्दव्यवहारः and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II In theology: नवमतम् and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neophyte
NEOPHYTE: नवशिष्य (f. ष्या): v. Novice,<BR>newly convert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neoplastic
NEOPLASTIC: नवोद्भूतः (ता, तं) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neoplatonism
NEOPLATONISM: *नवप्लाटुनदर्शनम्<BR>or<BR>-मतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neoteric
NEOTERIC: नूतनः (ना, नं): v. New.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nepenthe
NEPENTHE, -s: *दुःखहरमौषधम्; सन्तापशमनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nephew
NEPHEW:<BR>I A brother's son:<BR>(1) भ्रात्रीयः;<BR>(2) भ्रातृव्यः;<BR>(3) भ्रातुष्पुत्रः।<BR>II A sister's son:<BR>(1) भागिनेयः;<BR>(2) स्वस्रीयः;<BR>(3) भगिनीसुतः, P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nephritic
NEPHRITIC, -AL: Ph.:<BR>n. disease:<BR>बुक्कारोगः,<BR>n. patient:<BR>बुक्कारोगिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nepotism
NEPOTISM: *नाभिबन्धः; or by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nereid
NEREID: जलदेवता and sim. comps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nerve
NERVE:<BR>I Organ of sensation: शिराः v.<BR>Also sinew.<BR>II Strength, vigour: q. v.:<BR>घैर्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nervous
NERVOUS:<BR>I Lit.: शिरालः (ला, लं).<BR>II Vi-<BR>-gorous: q. v.<BR>III Easily agitated: सहज-<BR>चकितः (ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nervously
NERVOUSLY:<BR>I Weakly: expr. by adj.<BR>II<BR>Strongly: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nervousness
NERVOUSNESS:<BR>I Vigour, strength, as of<BR>style: ओजस् (n.), K.<BR>II. Weakness of ner-<BR>-ves: सहजचकितता (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nest
NEST:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) नीडः,<BR>to build a n.:<BR>नीडं<BR> निर्मिमीते, H.<BR>or<BR>विरचयति, K.;<BR>(2) कुलायः,<BR>n.-<BR>trees:<BR>कुलायद्रुमाः, U. ii. 9. Ph.:<BR>to find a<BR>mare's n.:<BR>शशविषाणम् अधिगच्छति।<BR>II Retreat,<BR>abode: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nestle
NESTLE: लीयते, नि-, (ली, c. 4), n.ing place.:<BR>निलयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nestling
NESTLING (subs.): (नीडस्थः) पक्षिशावः, -कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nestor
NESTOR: in fig. sense: perh. मुख्यः (chief.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

net
NET (subs.): जालम्,<BR>to spread a n.:<BR>जालं विनस्ता- [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">Page471</a>]<BR>रयति, H.; I may use some n. by means of it:<BR>तद्द्वारेण किञ्चिज्जालमाचरेयम्, D. iii.: v. Snare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

net
NET (v.):<BR>I To make network: जालं करोति।<BR>II To catch with a n.: जालेन बध्नाति, n.ed:<BR>पाशबद्धाः, H.<BR>III. To make clear gain: expr.<BR>by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

net
NET (adj.): शुद्ध (f. द्धा): v. Pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nether
NETHER: अधस्,<BR>n. world:<BR>अधोभुवनम्: v. Lower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nethermost
NETHERMOST:<BR>n. hell:<BR>नितलम् (?), V. p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nettle
NETTLE:<BR>I Subs.: a plant: पीतपर्णी।<BR>II<BR>Verbs: क्षोमयति (c. of क्षुभ्): v. To irri-<BR>-tate, vex.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

network
NETWORK: जालकर्मन् (n.); सूत्रकर्मन् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neuralgia
NEURALGIA: *शिराशूलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neuter
NEUTER:<BR>n. gender:<BR>क्लीवलिङ्गम्;<BR>words expressing<BR>species of fruit are n.:<BR>फलजातिवाची शब्दो नपुंसकं<BR> स्यात्, S. k.; (words)<BR>having these terminations<BR>are n.:<BR>एतदन्तानि क्लीवानि, S. k.; a n. verb:<BR>अकर्मकक्रिया; (the verb) मा in (the sense of)<BR>mea-<BR>suring is n.:<BR>मा माने अकर्मकः, S. k.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neutral
NEUTRAL:<BR>(1) मध्यस्थ (f. स्था),<BR>but others rema-<BR>ined n.:<BR>मध्यस्थास्त्वपरेऽमवन्, Mah. ii. 45. 32.;<BR>(2) मध्यमः (मा, मं) (rare), R. xiii. 7.: v.<BR>Indifferent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neutrality
NEUTRALITY: माध्यस्थ्यम्,<BR>to betake n.:<BR>माध्यस्थ्यमव-<BR>लम्बते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

neutralize
NEUTRALIZE: नाशयति (c. of नश्) (= to des-<BR>-troy.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

never
NEVER:<BR>(1) न कदाचित् -अपि, न कदापि,<BR>or<BR>न कदा-<BR>चन, will n. admit in the presence of Rākṣasa:<BR>न कदाचिदपि राक्षसस्याग्रतः प्रतिपत्स्यते, Mu.;<BR>n.<BR>grieve:<BR>खेदं कदापि मा कृथाः, Bham.;<BR>(2) न जातु,<BR>the girl n. felt easy:<BR>न जातु निर्वृतिं बाला लभते स्म,<BR>Ku.;<BR>(3) Often by sim. न, such a horse n. was<BR>and n. will be: नैवंविधो भूतो भावी वा तुरङ्गमः, K.;<BR>n. to open again: अपुनरून्मीलनाय, C.; n. -fad-<BR>ing: अजरः (रा, रं), H.; n. -failing: अक्षय्य<BR>(f. य्या), D. N. so (= ever so) expr. by<BR>यावत्: v. Much as, as. N. more: इतः परं । न।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nevertheless
NEVERTHELESS:<BR>(1) तथापि: v. Yet;<BR>(2) किन्तु<BR>(= but: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

new
NEW:<BR>(1) नवः (वा, व्रं),<BR>a n. lord:<BR>नवेश्वरः, R.;<BR>a n. descent of man:<BR>नवः पुरूषावतारः, U.; the n.<BR>moon:<BR>नवो निशाकरः, Sa.;<BR>n. crops:<BR>नवशस्यानि,<BR>H.;<BR>(2) नवीनः (ना, नं),<BR>a n. shoot:<BR>नवीनोऽङ्कुरः,<BR>Pri.;<BR>(3) अभिनवः (वा, वं), a n. servant:<BR>अभिनवसेवकः, K.;<BR>a n. work:<BR>अभिनवा कृतिः,<BR>Vi.;<BR>(4) नूतनः (ना, नं),<BR>n. cloud:<BR>नूतनघनः,<BR>Vi.;<BR>(5) नव्यः (व्या, व्यं),<BR>n. offering:<BR>नव्यं<BR> हव्यम्, B.r.;<BR>(6) नूत्नः (त्ना, त्नं) (rare);<BR>(7)<BR>अपूर्वः (र्वा, र्वं) (= unprecedented).<BR>New-year's<BR>day:<BR>नववर्षस्य प्रथमदिवसः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

newcomer
NEWCOMER:<BR>(1) आगन्तुकः, as we are n.s:<BR>आगन्तुकतया, Sa. vi.;<BR>(2) नवागतः and sim.<BR>comp.s.,<BR>the n. Chandrāpiḍa:<BR>अभिनवागतश्चन्द्रा-<BR>पीडः, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

new-fangled
NEW-FANGLED: नवकल्पितः (ता, तं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

new-fashioned
NEW-FASHIONED: नवघटितः (ता, तं) (?); नवः<BR>(वा, वं): v. New.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

newly
NEWLY:<BR>n. -married wife:<BR>नवपाणिग्रहणा वधूः, R.<BR>or<BR>अचिरोढा, Si.;<BR>n. -blown:<BR>नवविनिद्रः (द्रा, द्रं),<BR>Ki.: v. New, recently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

newness
NEWNESS:<BR>(1) नवीनता: v. Novelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

news
NEWS:<BR>(1) वार्त्ता, distressed on hearing the n.:<BR>विदितवार्त्तावार्त्तौ, D. i.;<BR>without (any) n.:<BR>वार्त्तया<BR> विना; K.;<BR>(2) वृत्तान्तः, what n. of your friend:<BR>को वृत्तान्तस्ते सख्याः, Mal. iv.; is there any n.:<BR>अस्ति नवीनः कोऽपि वृत्तान्तः, Pri. i.;<BR>(3) प्रवृत्तिः,<BR>receiving our n. from the son of Wind:<BR>प्रामञ्जने-<BR>रस्मत्प्रवृत्तिमुपलम्य, Vi.;<BR>was the conveyer of bad<BR>n.:<BR>दुष्प्रवृत्तिहराऽभवत्, R. xii. 51. Ph.:<BR>good<BR>n.:<BR>भद्रम्, शुभम्, etc.;<BR>bad n.:<BR>अशुभम्, etc.;<BR>pleasant n.:<BR>प्रियम्, Sa.; this is no n. to me:<BR>नेयं नवा वार्त्ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

newsmonger
NEWSMONGER: वार्त्तायनः, वार्त्ताप्रचारकः।; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

newspaper
NEWSPAPER: संवादपत्रिका,<BR>Weekly n.:<BR>साप्ता-<BR>हिकपत्रिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

news-vender
NEWS-VENDER (-DOR): *संवादपत्रविक्रेतृ (f. त्री);<BR>-विक्रयिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

newt
NEWT: तृणगोधा, -धिका: v. Lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

next
NEXT (adj.):<BR>(1) परः (रा, रं), the n. day:<BR>परेद्युः;<BR>in absence of the first, n and n.:<BR>पूर्वाभावे<BR> परः परः, Y. ii. 135.;<BR>(2) आगामिन् (f. नी)<BR>(= coming: of time),<BR>on the n. 14th (lunar)<BR>night:<BR>आगामिन्यां चतुर्दशीक्षपायाम्, C.;<BR>(3) अनन्तरः [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">Page472</a>]<BR>(रा, रं) (= without any interval: rare),<BR>n. -born:<BR>अनन्तरज (f. जा), R. vii. 32.;<BR>in<BR>the n. continent:<BR>अनन्तरे वर्षे, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

next
NEXT (adj.):<BR>I Of place:<BR>(1) अनन्तरम्;<BR>(2)<BR>by adj.<BR>II Of time, succession, etc.: परम्,<BR> परतः<BR>or<BR>परेण,<BR>n. to a daughter's son:<BR>दौहित्रात्परतः,<BR>Da. Ph.:<BR>what n.:<BR>ततः किम्: v. Then.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nib
NIB (Subs.):<BR>I Of a bird: चञ्चुः।<BR>II Of a<BR>pen: कलमाग्रम् (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nib
NIB (v.): तीक्ष्णीकरोति (= to sharpen) (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nibble
NIBBLE:<BR>I To bite: दशति (दंश्, c. 1.).<BR>II<BR>To carp: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nice
NICE:<BR>I Delicate, dainty:<BR>(1) ललितः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(2) स्वादु (mfn.) (= sweet).<BR>II<BR>Agreeable, delightful: रूचिरः (रा, रं).<BR>III<BR>Delicate, refined: सूक्षम (f. क्ष्मा).<BR>IV<BR>Exact, accurate: विशुद्ध (f. द्धा). V. Fasti-<BR>-dious, scrupulous: सूक्ष्मप्रियः (या, यं) (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nicely
NICELY:<BR>I Exactly, accurately: विशुद्धम्।<BR>II Well: शोमनम्।<BR>III Agreeably. रूचिरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

niceness
NICENESS, NICETY:<BR>I Delicacy:<BR>(1) लालित्यम्;<BR>(2) स्वादुता।<BR>II Agreeableness: रूचिरता।<BR>III<BR>Exactness, accuracy: विशुद्धता।<BR>IV Fine-<BR>-ness, minuteness: सूक्ष्मता: v. Fastidious-<BR>-ness: सूक्ष्मप्रियता।<BR>V Delicate management:<BR>perh. वैदग्ध्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

niche
NICHE: perh. तक्रम् (comp. Bengali ताक्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nick
NICK (subs.):<BR>I Notch: ग्रन्थिः,<BR>n. of propi-<BR>tious reckoning:<BR>संख्यामङ्गलग्रन्थिः, U. iii.<BR>II Of<BR>time: शुमक्षणः; उपयुक्तसमयः; and sim. comps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nick
NICK (v.): v. To hit, defeat, wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nickname
NICKNAME (subs.): अपनामन् (n (?): संज्ञा,<BR>(appellation),<BR>got the n. of hare-eater:<BR>शशाद-<BR>संज्ञामवाप, U. p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nickname
NICKNAME (v.): अपनाम करोति (?).<BR>N. d:<BR>-अप-<BR>नामन् (mfn.); -संज्ञ (f. ज्ञा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

niece
NIECE:<BR>I Brother's daughter:<BR>(1) भ्रातुष्पुत्री;<BR>(2) भ्रातृजा (rare).<BR>II Sister's d.:<BR>(1) भागिनेयी;<BR>(2) स्वस्रीया (rare),<BR>maternal n.:<BR>मातृष्वस्रेयी, M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

niggard
NIGGARD: कृपण (f. णा): v. Miser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

niggardliness
NIGGARDLINESS:<BR>(1) कृपणता (= miserliness);<BR>(2) बद्धमुष्टिता (= close-fistedness);<BR>(3) तनु-<BR>त्यागिता (parsimony).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

niggardly
NIGGARDLY:<BR>(1) कृपण (f. णा);<BR>(2) बद्धमुष्टि<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(3) तनुत्याग (f. गा); For dif.: v.<BR>N.ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nigh
NIGH (adj. and adv.): v. Near (adj. and<BR>adv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

night
NIGHT:<BR>(1) रजनी,<BR>at n.:<BR>रजन्याम्, V.;<BR>in the depth<BR>of n.:<BR>गाढायां रजन्याम्, K.;<BR>n. with the moon<BR>(just) risen but darkness not (quite) dispelled:<BR>उद्गतेन्दुरविमिन्नतमिस्रा रजनी, Ki. ix. 36.;<BR>(2)<BR>रात्रिः,<BR>the n. has passed:<BR>रात्रिर्गता, R.;<BR>day and<BR>n.:<BR>अहोरात्रम्: v. Day.:<BR>for three n.s:<BR>त्रिरात्रम्,<BR>Vas.;<BR>when mid.-n. was oozing away:<BR>गलति<BR> मध्यरात्रे, D. viii.;<BR>I will reside here one n.:<BR>अत्र<BR> वसाम्येकां रात्रिम्, K.s. xviii. 255.:<BR>(3) निशा,<BR>end<BR>of n.:<BR>निशावसानम्, B. xi. 17.;<BR>(4) विभावरी,<BR>in<BR>the fourth watch of n.:<BR>विभावर्याः तुरीये यामे, C.;<BR>(5) शर्वरी,<BR>to pass a n.:<BR>शर्वरीं गमयति, Si. xi.<BR>5.;<BR>(6) क्षपा, in autumnal full-moonlight n.s:<BR>परिणतशरच्चन्द्रिकासु क्षपासु, Me. ii. 49.;<BR>(7) यामिनी;<BR>(8) क्षणदा;<BR>(9) त्रियामा।<BR>At n.:<BR>निशि, नक्तम्,<BR>Gi.;<BR>n. -walker:<BR>निशाचरः, रजनीचरः, etc.;<BR>n. -blindness:<BR>रात्र्यन्धता;<BR>n. -dew:<BR>निशातुषारम्;<BR>n. -waking:<BR>रात्रिजागरणम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nightcap
NIGHTCAP: नैशं शिरस्कम्, and sim. expr.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

night-dress
NIGHT-DRESS: नैशी वेशः(षः), Ri. v. 14. and sim.<BR>expr.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nightfall
NIGHTFALL:<BR>(1) निशागमः;<BR>(2) दिनान्तः;<BR>(3)<BR>रजनीमुखम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

night-gown
NIGHT-GOWN: *नैशमाप्रपदीनम्: v. Night-dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nightingale
NIGHTINGALE: *प्रियगीतः; बुल्बुलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nightly
NIGHTLY (adj.):<BR>(1) नैशः (शी, शं);<BR>(2) शार्वरः<BR>(री, रं);<BR>(3) दोषातनः (नी, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nightly
NIGHTLY (adv.):<BR>I By night:<BR>(1) by loc.:<BR>रात्रौ, etc.;<BR>(2) निशि;<BR>(3) नक्तम्।<BR>II Every<BR>night:<BR>(1) प्रतिरात्रम्:<BR>(2) निशि निशि; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

night-man
NIGHT-MAN: *निशासम्भार्जकः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nightmare
NIGHTMARE:<BR>he had a n.:<BR>भूतस्तं पीडयामास स्वप्ने<BR>(after Bengali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nightpiece
NIGHTPIECE: *रात्रिदृश्यम्; रजनीचित्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nightshade
NIGHTSHADE: कण्टकारी (a prickly n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

night-watch
NIGHT-WATCH:<BR>I Lit.: यामः: v. Watch.<BR>II A guard: q. v.: नगररक्षिन् (m.), Ma.<BR>viii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nihilism
NIHILISM: शून्यमतम्, Sa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nihilist
NIHILIST: शून्यवादिन् (f. नी), San.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nihility
NIHILITY: शून्यत्वम्: v. Nothing, -ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nimble
NIMBLE: लघु (f. घ्वी) (= light and gay).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nimbleness
NIMBLENESS: लाघवम्: v. Lightness, activity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nimbly
NIMBLY: सलाघवम्: v. Lightly, quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nine
NINE: नवन् (mfn.),<BR>n. or ten:<BR>नवदशाः (n. -नि);<BR>n. times:<BR>नववारान्;<BR>in n. ways:<BR>नवधा;<BR>of n.<BR>kinds:<BR>नवविधः (धा, धं);<BR>n. gems of Vikramā-<BR>ditya:<BR>विक्रमस्य नव रत्नानि, Ja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ninefold
NINEFOLD: नवगुणितम्: v. Nine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nineteen
NINETEEN:<BR>(1) नवदशन् (mfn.);<BR>(2) ऊनविंशतिः (f.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nineteenth
NINETEENTH:<BR>(2) नवदशः (शी, शं):<BR>(2) ऊनविंशः<BR>(शी, शं);<BR>(3) ऊनविंशतितमः (मी, मं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ninety
NINETY: नवति (f.);<BR>n. -nine:<BR>नवनवतिः;<BR>n.<BR>times:<BR>नवतिवारान्;<BR>n. -fold:<BR>नवतिगुणितम्;<BR>in<BR>n. ways:<BR>नवतिधा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ninny
NINNY: अल्पबुद्धि (mfn.): v. Fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ninth
NINTH: नवमः (मी, मं).<BR>N.-ly:<BR>नवमम्; नवमतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nip
NIP:<BR>I To pinch: निष्पीडयति (पीड्, c. 10.)<BR>(?).<BR>II To cut off: निकृन्तति (कृत्, c. 6.).<BR>III To destroy: q. v.: नाशयति (c. of<BR>नश्). Ph.:<BR>to n. in the bud:<BR>जातमात्रं हन्ति, नि-,<BR>(हन्, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nippers
NIPPERS:<BR>(1) संदंशः, -कः;<BR>(2) कङ्कमुखः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nipple
NIPPLE:<BR>(1) चूचुकम्<BR>or<BR>चुचुकम्;<BR>(2) स्तनाग्रम्;<BR>(3)<BR>कुचाग्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nit
NIT:<BR>(1) लिक्षा;<BR>(2) निक्षा;<BR>(3) रिक्षा;<BR>(4) दिङ्कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nitre
NITRE:<BR>(1) यवक्षारः;<BR>(2) यवलाशः;<BR>(3) यवशूकः;<BR>(4) यवजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nitrogen
NITROGEN: *निष्प्राणवायुः; यवक्षारजनकः।<BR>Nitric<BR>acid:<BR>*निष्प्राणाम्लः।<BR>Nitrous acid:<BR>*उपनिष्प्राणाम्लः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

no
NO (adv.): न,<BR>no, no, become the ornament of<BR>my lap:<BR>न न मदुत्सङ्गविभूषणं भव, N. ix. 114.;<BR>and to say ‘no, no’ to one like you would be<BR>rebuking:<BR>न नेति च त्वादृशि वाग् विगर्हृणा, N. ix.<BR>25.;<BR>to this we say ‘no’:<BR>अत्रोच्यते ‘न’, S.;<BR>there is no greater fault than this:<BR>नातः परतरो<BR> दोषः, H. N.B. Use ‘yes’ in Sanskrit for ‘no’<BR>after negative interrogation,<BR>‘has not this<BR>come to Chandragupta's ears? No, Sir:<BR>न खलु<BR> वृषलस्य श्रवणमुपगतोऽयं॥आर्य, अय किम्, Mu. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

no
NO (adj.):<BR>(1) न, he is no other than Arjuna:<BR>नैषोऽन्यः सव्यसाचिनः, Mah.;<BR>and there is no cessa-<BR>tion of sorrow but from spiritual knowledge:<BR>न चान्यत्र परमात्मज्ञानाच्छोकविनिवृत्तिरस्ति, S. iii. 8.;<BR>(2) अ (or अन् before vowels),<BR>if forced no<BR>evidence:<BR>बलात्कारितमप्रमाणम्, V.s.;<BR>paying no<BR>attention:<BR>अनादृत्य, Sa.; seeing no other recourse;<BR>अन्यदुपायान्तरमपश्यन्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

no one
NO ONE:<BR>(1) न कोऽपि; (f. काऽपि),<BR>there is n.<BR>without some stain:<BR>नास्त्यकलङ्कः कोऽपि, Va.;<BR>(2) न कश्चित् (f. काचित्),<BR>n. is one's friend:<BR>न<BR> कश्चित् कस्यचिन्मित्रम्, H.;<BR>(3) न कश्चन (f. काचन)<BR>(rare): v. None.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nobility
NOBILITY:<BR>I Of rank or birth: no equiv.:<BR>कौलीन्यम् may occasionally do; महत्त्वम्<BR>(= greatness).<BR>II Noblemen collectively:<BR>*अनुराजवर्गः; नायकसम्प्रदायः।<BR>III Greatness:<BR>eminence: महत्त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noble
NOBLE, NOBLEMAN (subs.): *अनुराजः, नायकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noble
NOBLE (adj.):<BR>I Of birth or rank: कुलीनः<BR>(ना, नं) (?);<BR>of n. blood:<BR>कुलजः, N.; महत्<BR>(f. ती) (= great).<BR>II Great, eminent:<BR>q. v.: महत् (f. ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nobleness
NOBLENESS, NOBLESSE: महत्त्वम्: v. Nobility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nobly
NOBLY:<BR>I With ref. to descent:<BR>n. descen-<BR>ded:<BR>कुलीनः (ना, नं), etc.<BR>II Eminently:<BR>splendidly: अतितेजसा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nobody
NOBODY: v. No one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nocturnal
NOCTURNAL; नैशः (शी, शं): v. Nightly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nod
NOD (subs.): शिरःकम्पः<BR>or<BR>मूर्ध्नः कम्पः, Ku. vii.<BR>46.;<BR>forbidden by a n.:<BR>शिरःकम्पसंज्ञावारिता, D.<BR>vi.; whose entry was permitted with a mere n.<BR>(lit. turning of the eye-brow): भ्रूक्षेपमात्रानुमतप्रवेशाम्,<BR>Ku. iii. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nod
NOD (v.):<BR>I To salute: नमति (नम्, c. 1.),<BR>Ku. vi. 89.<BR>II Of kings: शिरःकम्पेन अनु-<BR>मन्यते (मन्, c. 4 (to assent^1 or permit) or<BR>आह्वयति (ह्वे, c. 1.) (to call).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nodding
NODDING:<BR>I Subs.: प्रणतिः।<BR>II Adj.: नतः<BR>(ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noddy
NODDY: अल्पबुद्धिः: v. Simpleton, fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

node
NODE: पातः।<BR>Ascending n.:<BR>प्रथमः सम्पातः, Go.;<BR>पूर्वार्द्धपातः।<BR>Descending n.:<BR>द्वितीयः सम्पातः, Go.;<BR>परार्द्धपातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nodule
NODULE: perh. पिण्डः।<BR>Nodular:<BR>पिण्डाकारः<BR>(रा, रं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noise
NOISE (subs.):<BR>(1) नादः, नि-, soft and high n.:<BR>स्निग्धतारो नादः, Mah.; with the n. of the lions:<BR>केसरिणां निनादेन, K.;<BR>(2) शब्दः (sound),<BR>with<BR>the n. of the hunter's feet:<BR>मृगयनां चरणशब्देन, K.;<BR>(3) ध्वनिः (= low s.),<BR>the n. of bow-strings and<BR>swords:<BR>शरासनज्यातलवारणध्वनिः, Ki.;<BR>(4) रवः,<BR> विरावः (= cry: q.v.):<BR>(5) ध्वानः (= 3);<BR>(6) रणितम्<BR>or<BR>क्वनितम् (= harsh n.);<BR>(7) निह्रादः<BR>or<BR>संह्रादः (= murmuring, roaring n.);<BR>(8)<BR>कलकलः<BR>or<BR>कोलाहलः (= loud confused n.),<BR>when the n. of the hunting ceased:<BR>प्रशान्ते तस्मिन्<BR> मृगयाकलकले, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noise
NOISE, TO MAKE:<BR>(1) नदति, नि- (नद्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) ध्वनति (ध्वन्, c. 1.);<BR>(3) शब्दायते (nomi.);<BR>(4) रणति (रण्, c. 1.): v. Noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noise
NOISE (v. t.): घोषयति, आ-, वि-, (घुष्, c. 10.),<BR>“n.d abroad”:<BR>विघोषितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noiseless
NOISELESS:<BR>(1) निःशब्द (f. ब्दा);<BR>(2) नीरवः<BR>(वा, वं): v. Silent, mute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noiselessly
NOISELESSLY:<BR>(1) निःशब्दम्;<BR>(2) नीरवम्: v.<BR>Silently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noisily
NOISILY: कोलाहलं<BR>or<BR>कलकलं कृत्वा: v. Noise, noisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noisome
NOISOME: उत्पीडकः (का, कं): v. Fetid, noxi-<BR>-ous, insalubrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noisomeness
NOISOMENESS:<BR>(1) उत्पीडकत्वम्;<BR>(2) उद्वेगकरत्वम्<BR>(= offensiveness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noisy
NOISY:<BR>I Making noise: कृतकलकलः (ला, लं)<BR>and sim. comp.s.,<BR>in the n. crowd:<BR>बद्धकलकले<BR> महाजने, D. iv. To be n.: v. Noise. to make.<BR>II Full of noise:<BR>(1) व्याप्तकलकलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) महाशब्द (f. ब्दा) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nomad
NOMAD, NOMADE: *चारक (f. रिका); नैकत्रवासः<BR>(सा, सं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nomadic
NOMADIC: expr. by gen. or comp., n. tribe:<BR>चारकजातिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nomenclator
NOMENCLATOR: नामदातृ (f. त्री) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nomenclature
NOMENCLATURE: परिमाषा, S.k.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nominal
NOMINAL:<BR>I Lit., by comp.,<BR>n., n. verb:<BR>नाम-<BR>धातुः, S.k.<BR>II Fig., existing in name only:<BR>नाममात्र (f. त्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nominalist
NOMINALIST: व्याप्तिज्ञानविसंवादिन् (f. नी) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nominally
NOMINALLY:<BR>I Lit.: नाम्ना।<BR>II Fig.: नाम-<BR>मात्रम्; नामत एव; and sim. comp.s.: v. Only,<BR>merely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nominate
NOMINATE:<BR>I To name: q. v.:<BR>II To an<BR>office: *निर्वाचयति (c. of वच्),<BR>they can n.,<BR>but cannot appoint:<BR>निर्वाचयितुं न तु नियोक्तुं ते<BR> प्रभवन्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nomination
NOMINATION: निर्वाचनम्: v. Also appointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nominative
NOMINATIVE: कर्ता,<BR>n. case:<BR>कर्तृकारकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nominator
NOMINATOR:<BR>(1) *निर्वाचकः;<BR>(2) निर्वाचयितृ (m.);<BR>(3) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nominee
NOMINEE: निर्वाचितः (ता, तं), he is Rājā's n.:<BR>राज्ञा निर्वाचितः सः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

non
NON: prefix: expr. by अ<BR>or<BR>अन्, before<BR>vowels,<BR>n.-enjoyment:<BR>अमोगः, n.-arrival:<BR>अनागमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nonage
NONAGE: v. Minority, childhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

non-attendance
NON-ATTENDANCE: अनुपस्थितिः: v. Attendance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nonce
NONCE:<BR>“for the n.”:<BR>तत्काले।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

non-conductor
NON-CONDUCTOR: अप्रवाहकः,<BR>n. of electricity:<BR>न<BR> तडित्प्रवाहकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nonchalance
NONCHALANCE: निरुत्साहताः: v. Indifference,<BR>carelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nonconformist
NONCONFORMIST: *मतापलापिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nonconformity
NONCONFORMITY: *मतापलापः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nondescript
NONDESCRIPT: न विवृतपूर्वः (र्वा, र्वं): v. New,<BR>odd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

none
NONE: न कोऽपि (f. कापि,<BR>n.<BR>किमपि)<BR>or<BR>कश्चित्<BR>(f. काचित्,<BR>n.<BR>किञ्चित्)<BR>or<BR>कश्चन (f. काचन, n.<BR>किञ्चन),<BR>n. of his brothers:<BR>न कञ्चन भ्रातृषु, R.<BR>xiv. 43.;<BR>n. else:<BR>नान्यः कोऽपि। N. but: expr.<BR>by एव,<BR>n. but the brave:<BR>साहसिका एव: v.<BR>Only.<BR>N. -so-pretty: a plant:<BR>कान्तिमती।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nonentity
NONENTITY:<BR>(1) असत्, there is nothing out of n.:<BR>नासतो विद्यते भावः, G.;<BR>(2) अभावः, G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nones
NONES: in Roman calendar: *नवमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

non-essential
NON-ESSENTIAL: अनावश्यकः (की, कं) (= need-<BR>-less).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nonexistence
NONEXISTENCE: नास्तित्वम्: v. Existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nonjuror
NONJUROR: नवराज्यविद्वेषिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nonpareil
NONPAREIL:<BR>(1) अप्रतिमः (मा, मं);<BR>(2) अनुपमः<BR>(मा, मं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

non-payment
NON-PAYMENT: expr. by verb., to pay and<BR>not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nonplus
NONPLUS (v.): मोहयति, वि-, (c. of मुह्): v.<BR>To confound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

non-resident
NON-RESIDENT: स्थानान्तरवासिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

non-resistance
NON-RESISTANCE: अप्रतिरोधः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nonsense
NONSENSE:<BR>I Subs.: expr. by adj.,<BR>talking<BR>n.:<BR>असम्बद्धप्रलापिन् (f. नी), Sa. i.<BR>II As ex-<BR>-clam.: धिक् प्रहसनम्, U. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nonsensical
NONSENSICAL:<BR>(1) निरर्थकः (का, कं) (without<BR>sense);<BR>(2) असम्बद्ध (f. द्धा) (= inconsistent,<BR>improper);<BR>(3) मृषार्थकः (का, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nonsuit
NONSUIT (v.):<BR>to be n.ed:<BR>अर्थात् हीयते (pass.<BR>of हा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noodle
NOODLE: अल्पबुद्धि (mfn.): v. Simpleton, block-<BR>-head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nook
NOOK:<BR>(1) कोणः (= corner: q.v.);<BR>(2) विविक्तम्<BR>(= secluded retreat).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noon
NOON:<BR>(1) मध्याह्नः;<BR>(2) मध्यन्दिनम्;<BR>(3) दिन-<BR>यौवनम् (poet.), R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noonday
NOONDAY: माध्याह्निकः (की, कं): v. Midday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noontide
NOONTIDE:<BR>(1) मध्याह्नवेला;<BR>(2) मध्याह्नकालः;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noose
NOOSE (subs.): पाशः, to cut (i. e. remove) n.s.:<BR>पाशान् छिनत्ति, H.: v. Halter, snare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noose
NOOSE (v. t.): पाशे पातयति (c. of पत्): v. To<BR>ensnare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nor
NOR: न॥न च: v. Neither, not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

normal
NORMAL: युक्तः (क्ता, क्तं) (?): v. Regular.<BR>N.<BR>school:<BR>*शिक्षकशिक्षानिवेशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

north
NORTH (subs.):<BR>(1) उत्तरा दिश् (f.); उत्तराशा (f.);<BR>etc.,<BR>on the n.:<BR>उत्तरस्यां दिशि, K.; to the n.:<BR>उत्तरतः, V. m.; to the n. of Kuvera's dwelling:<BR>धनपतिगृहानुत्तरेण, Me. ii. 14.;<BR>(2) उदिची,<BR>fac-<BR>ing the n.:<BR>उदङ्मुख (f. खी), V. m.;<BR>(3) कौवेरी<BR> दिश्, etc.,<BR>from the n.:<BR>कौवेर्याः ककुभः, Vi.;<BR>(4) (poet.) कुवेरगुप्ता-, Ku.; धनदपालिता-, Mah.;<BR>सप्तर्षिताराशबला-, K., दिश्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

north
NORTH (adj.): उत्तरः (रा, रं), the n. Kurus:<BR>उत्तरान् कुरून्, Ki.; what is n. of the ocean:<BR>उत्तरं यत् समुद्रस्य, V. p.;<BR>n. wind:<BR>उत्तरो वायुः,<BR>V. m.; (rarely) उदीचीनः (ना, नं)<BR>or<BR>उदीच्य<BR>(f. च्या)<BR>or<BR>कौवेरः (री, रं), the n. quarter:<BR>कौवेरदिग्भागः, Si.<BR>N. star.:<BR>ध्रुवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

north-east
NORTH-EAST:<BR>I Adj.:<BR>(1) पूर्वोत्तरः (रा, रं),<BR>the n. wind:<BR>पूर्वोत्तरो वायुः, Mah.;<BR>to the n. of<BR>Kailāsa:<BR>प्रागुत्तरेण कैलासात्, Mat.;<BR>(2) उत्तरपूर्वः<BR>(र्वा, र्वं);<BR>(3) प्रागुदीच्य (f. च्या)<BR>or<BR>-चीनः<BR>(ना, नं).<BR>II Subs.:<BR>(1) पूर्वोत्तरा<BR>or<BR>उत्तरपूर्वा<BR>or<BR>ऐशानी दिश् (f.),<BR>towards the n.:<BR>ऐशानीं दिशं<BR> प्रति, V.;<BR>(2) पूर्वोत्तरो दिग्भागः,<BR>to the n. of the<BR>mount Kailāsa:<BR>कैलासशिखरिणः पूर्वोत्तरे दिग्भागे,<BR>R.;<BR>(3) प्रागुदीची।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

north-easterly
NORTH-EASTERLY, NORTH-EASTERN: v. North-<BR>-east (I)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

northerly
NORTHERLY (adv.):<BR>I Northwards: q. v.:<BR>II From the north: उत्तरतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

northerly
NORTHERLY, NORTHERN (adj.): उत्तरः (रा, रं)<BR>v. North.<BR>N. lights:<BR>*उत्तरप्रकाशः: v. Aurora<BR>borealis.<BR>N.-most:<BR>सर्वोत्तरः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

northwards
NORTHWARDS: उत्तराभिमुखम्; उत्तरां दिशं प्रति and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

north-west
NORTH-WEST (subs.): पश्चिमोत्तरा<BR>or<BR>उत्तरपश्चिमा or<BR>वायवी दिक्, आशा, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

north-west
NORTH-WEST, NORTH-WESTERLY, NORTH-WESTERN:<BR>(1) पश्चिमोत्तरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) वायव्य<BR>(f. व्या) (rare) (of the n. wind), V. m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nose
NOSE (subs.):<BR>(1) नासा<BR>or<BR>नासिका,<BR>through the<BR>n.:<BR>नासिकया, N.;<BR>tip of the n.:<BR>नासाग्रम्, J.;<BR>diseases of the n.:<BR>नासारोगाः, Sr.;<BR>running of<BR>the n.:<BR>नासापरिस्रावः, Sr.; n.-string: (for<BR>cattle): नास्यम्;<BR>(2) नासिक्यम् (rare);<BR>(3) घ्राणम्<BR>(poet.), with a long elevated bridge of the n.:<BR>आयतोत्तुङ्गघ्राणवंश (f. शा), K. To lead by the n.:<BR>यथेच्छं वाहयति (?). To thrust one's n. into:<BR>अन्यायचर्चां करोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nose
NOSE (v.):<BR>I To scent: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>affront, abuse: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nosegay
NOSEGAY:<BR>(1) कुसुमस्तवकः;<BR>(2) पुष्पगुच्छः;<BR>(3)<BR>प्रसूनप्रकारः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nosology
NOSOLOGY: रोगविज्ञानम्, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nostril
NOSTRIL:<BR>(1) नासारन्घ्रम्;<BR>(2) नासाकुहरम्;<BR>(3)<BR>नासाविवरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nostrum
NOSTRUM: मिथ्यौषधम्; गुप्तौषधम् (?), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

not
NOT:<BR>(1) न, there the sun does n. shine, the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">Page476</a>]<BR>moon does n. gleam: न तत्र सूर्यस्तपति न विराजति<BR> चन्द्रमाः, Mat.; (it is) lightning n. my darling<BR>Urvaśī.. विद्युत्, प्रिया मम नोर्वशी, V.; there was<BR>n. a (single) prince of high birth who did n. go:<BR>नासीदगन्ता कुलजः कुमारः, N.x. 2.; n. that he<BR>was n. beautiful nor that she did n. know to<BR>see well: नासौ न काम्यो न च वेद सम्यग् द्रष्टुं न सा,<BR>R. vi. 30.; n. so much.. as: न तथा॥ यथा, Ki.<BR>xiii. 32.; n. only with (their) hearts: न केवलं<BR> हृदयेन, N. xi. 2.; n. even death can strike on<BR>me: प्रभुः प्रहर्तुं मयि नान्तकोऽपि, R. ii. 62.;<BR>for .. n. : नहिः : v. For;<BR>(2) मा (prohibitive),<BR>do n. boast of wealth, men or youth:<BR>मा कुरू<BR> धनजनयौवनगर्वम्, J.;<BR>let n. your sense-horses carry<BR>you astray:<BR>मा भूवन्नपथहरास्तवेन्द्रियाश्वाः, Ki. v.<BR>50.;<BR>(3) अ-, (अन्-, before vowels)<BR>or<BR>निर्-,<BR>in comp.,<BR>n. able:<BR>अशक्त (f. क्ता); n. kind:<BR>निर्दयः (या, यं);<BR>there is nothing mine which is<BR>n. yours:<BR>अभवदीयं नैव किञ्चिन्मत्सम्बद्धम्, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

notable
NOTABLE: प्रसिद्ध (f. द्धा): v. Remarkable,<BR>memorable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

notably
NOTABLY: विशेषेण (= specially): v. Also<BR>remarkably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

notary
NOTARY: लेखकप्रमाणकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

notation
NOTATION: अङ्कप्रणाली (?).<BR>Musical n.:<BR>प्रस्तरः,<BR>Wilson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

notch
NOTCH (subs.):<BR>(1) छेदः (= cut);<BR>(2) कुन्दकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

notch
NOTCH (v.): छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7.) (= to cut)<BR>(?).<BR>N.ed extremity of a bow:<BR>अटनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

note
NOTE (subs.):<BR>I A mark: लिङ्गम्।<BR>II A sign:<BR>संज्ञा।<BR>III A memorandum: no equiv.:<BR>सारलेखः।<BR>IV Explanatory:<BR>(1) टीका;<BR>(2)<BR>व्याख्या।<BR>V A short letter: पत्रिका।<BR>VI Musi-<BR>-cal symbol: चिह्नम्,।<BR>VII Musical tone:<BR>स्वरः।<BR>VIII Reputation:<BR>of n.:<BR>विश्रुतः (ता,<BR> तं),: v. Renowned, famous.<BR>IX Heed:<BR>take n. of:<BR>अवेक्षते।<BR>X Of birds: रूतम्।<BR>XI Commercial: पत्रम् (when the sense is<BR>clear).<BR>Promissory n.:<BR>*प्रतिज्ञापत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

note
NOTE (v.):<BR>I To observe, remark: q. v.:<BR>वर्णयति, निर्-, (वर्ण्, c. 10.).<BR>II To record,<BR>write: q. v.: लिखति (लिख्, c. 6.).<BR>III To<BR>charge. stigmatize: अभिशंसति (शंस्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

note-book
NOTE-BOOK: *सारलेखबन्धः; स्मरणपत्रिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noted
NOTED: i. e. celebrated: q. v.: प्रसिद्ध (f. द्धा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noteworthy
NOTEWORTHY: expr. with परिग्रहीतव्य (f. व्या);<BR>अवेक्षणीयः (या, यं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nothing
NOTHING (subs.):<BR>I Non-entity:<BR>(1) अभावः;<BR>(2) असत्,<BR>there is n. out of n.:<BR>नासतो विद्यते<BR> भावः, G.;<BR>(3) शून्यम्, San.<BR>II Not anything:<BR>(1) न किञ्चित्,<BR>for there is n. which he cannot do<BR>from shame:<BR>न हि किञ्चिन्न क्रियते ह्रिया, K.;<BR>beyond which there is n. else:<BR>यस्मात्परं<BR> किञ्चिदन्यन्नास्ति, S. iii. 13.; it ts n. to Rāvaṇa:<BR>दशकन्धरमधिकृत्य न किञ्चिदेतत्, An. vi.;<BR>said n.,<BR>only with the feet..<BR>न किञ्चिदूचे चरणेन केवलं॥,<BR>Ki. viii. 14.;<BR>(2) न किञ्चन (rare), Mah. For<BR>n.: (a) without any cause: अकारणम्; अकारणे;<BR> अकाण्डे; अवस्तुनि (rare), Ra. iv.; (b) in vain:<BR>q. v.: वृथा। N. but: (= only: q.v.): नान्यत्<BR> किञ्चित् (with abl.).<BR>To make n. of:<BR>न किञ्चित्<BR> मन्यते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nothing
NOTHING (adv.): किञ्चिदपि<BR>or<BR>मनागपि॥ न<BR>or<BR>अ-<BR>in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nothingness
NOTHINGNESS:<BR>(1) अभावता;<BR>(2) शून्यत्वम्,<BR>San.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

notice
NOTICE (v.):<BR>I To observe, see: लक्षयति,<BR> आ-, सं, अभि-, समा- (लक्ष्, c. 10.), did not n.:<BR>नालक्षयत्, Ku. iii. 51.<BR>II To remark upon:<BR>विवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.) (= to explain): निर्दिशति<BR>(दिश्, c. 6.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

notice
NOTICE (subs.):<BR>I Heed, observation: (a)<BR>to take n. of: v. Notice (v) (I); (b)<BR>to<BR>attract n.:<BR>मनो हरति<BR>or<BR>आकर्षति (कृष्, c. 1.);<BR>(c) to escape n., expr. with लक्षयति and न;<BR>(d) worthy of n., expr. by circumlo.: v. Note-<BR>-worthy.<BR>II Information, intelligence: q. v.:<BR>विज्ञापनम्,<BR>to give n.:<BR>विज्ञापयति (c. of ज्ञा).<BR>III Allusion, mention: उल्लेखः; निर्देशः।<BR>IV<BR>Notification:<BR>(1) विज्ञापनम् (?);<BR>(2) घोषणा<BR>(= proclamation).<BR>V Attention: आदरः।<BR>VI With a view to punishing: I will take<BR>n. of your conduct: perh. चेष्टितं ते स्मरिष्यामि:<BR>v. Also chastise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noticeable
NOTICEABLE: i. e. remarkable: q. v.: विशेष-<BR>in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

notification
NOTIFICATION:<BR>(1) घोषणा (?);<BR>(2) विज्ञापनम्,<BR> -ना (= notice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

notify
NOTIFY: expr. by subs: v. Also to announce,<BR>proclaim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

notion
NOTION:<BR>I Conception: भावः।<BR>II Idea:<BR>q. v.: बुद्धिः।<BR>III Opinion, belief: q. v.:<BR>विश्वासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

notoriety
NOTORIETY:<BR>(1) प्रसिद्धिः;<BR>(2) दुर्नामन् (n.) (= bad<BR>name).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

notorious
NOTORIOUS:<BR>(1) प्रसिद्ध (f. द्धा) (in good or<BR>bad sense);<BR>(2) प्रकाशः (शा, शं) (= open,<BR>manifest),<BR>to get n.:<BR>प्रकाशीमवति, Mu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

notoriously
NOTORIOUSLY:<BR>(1) by adj. or comp.;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रकाशम् (= publicly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

notoriousness
NOTORIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) प्रसिद्धता;<BR>(2) प्रकाशता: v.<BR>Notoriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

notwithstanding
NOTWITHSTANDING:<BR>I As conj.: तथापि।<BR>II<BR>As prep.: by gen. or loc.,<BR>n. Bala:<BR>पश्यतो<BR> बलस्य;<BR>her cries n.:<BR>रूदत्यास्तस्याः<BR>or<BR>रूदत्यामपि<BR> तस्याम्;<BR>n. my advice:<BR>ममोपदेशमनादृत्य: v. Despite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nought
NOUGHT: v. Naught, nothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noun
NOUN: प्रातिपदिकम्, Pāṇini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nourish
NOURISH (v.):<BR>(1) पोषयति<BR>or<BR>पुष्णाति, परि-, (पुष्,<BR>c. 10. and 9.), he also attentively n.ed (the<BR>child), considering as if his brother had returned:<BR>सोऽपि सोदरमागतमिव मन्यमानो विशेषेण पुपोष, D.;<BR>n.ed (developed)<BR>the lovely parts:<BR>पुपोष लावण्य-<BR>मयान् विशेषान्, Ku. i. 25.;<BR>(2) वर्धयति, वि-, (c.<BR>of वृध्): v. To bring up.:<BR>(3) पालयति,<BR> प्रति- (पाल्, c. 10.): v. To protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nourisher
NOURISHER:<BR>(1) पोषकः, परि-;<BR>(2) पोषयितृ (m.);<BR>(3) पालयितृ (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nourishing
NOURISHING (adj.):<BR>(1) पुष्टिकर (f. री)<BR>or<BR>कृत्<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(2) बृंहण (f. णी),<BR>all meat is phlegm-<BR>removing and n., promoting strength and growth:<BR>मांसं वातहरं सर्वं बृंहणं बलपुष्टिकृत्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nourishment
NOURISHMENT:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) पोषणम्, परि-,<BR>(2) पुष्टिः, परि-।<BR>II Food: q. v.: perh. पोषणम्<BR>(as in the expr. भरणपोषणम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

novel
NOVEL (adj.): अभिनवः (वा, वं): v. New, strange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

novel
NOVEL (subs.): no eqiv.: आख्यायिका would do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

novelist
NOVELIST: nearest equiv.: आख्यायिकाकारः, “कथ-<BR>माख्यायिकाकारा न ते वन्द्याः कवीश्वराः”, C. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

novelty
NOVELTY:<BR>I Newness: q.v.: अपूर्वता।<BR>II<BR>Anything novel:<BR>(1) expr. by adj.;<BR>(2)<BR>अपूर्ववस्तु (n.), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

november
NOVEMBER: उत्तराग्रहायणपूर्वकार्त्तिकसंवादीयुरूपीयवर्षस्यै-<BR>कादशो मासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

novice
NOVICE: expr. with: नवः (वा, वं) (= new) or<BR>अलब्धवैदग्ध्य (f. ग्ध्या) and sim. comp.s. (= un-<BR>-trained, unskilled.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

novitiate
NOVITIATE: अन्तेवासित्वम्, after Vri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

now
NOW:<BR>I At the present time:<BR>(1) इदानीम्,<BR>just n.:<BR>इदानीमेब;<BR>enmity of n.:<BR>इदानीन्तनं वैरम्,<BR>A. r.;<BR>(2) सम्प्रति<BR>or<BR>साम्प्रतम्,<BR>but n. my only<BR>wish is:<BR>साम्प्रतं पुनर्मम मनोरथ एष एव, Ma.;<BR>(3)<BR>अधुना,<BR>where are you going now:<BR>क्वाघुना गम्यते,<BR>Vi.;<BR>(4) अद्य (= today),<BR>even n.:<BR>अद्यापि,<BR>U. i.<BR>II As correl.; now.. now:<BR>(1)<BR>अन्तरा । अन्तरा (= at intervals),<BR>conversing n.<BR>about his father, n. about his mother, n. about<BR>Śukanāsa:<BR>अन्तरा पितृसक्तमन्तरा मातृसम्बद्धमन्तरा<BR> शुकनासमयं कुर्वन्नालापम्, K.;<BR>(2) कदाचित् । कदाचित्<BR>(= at one time . at another time), K.;<BR>(3) क्वचित् । क्वचित् (= 2), n. (in the region)<BR>of<BR>the clouds and n. of birds:<BR>क्वचिद्घनानां पततां क्वचिच्च,<BR>R.<BR>III. As particle of transition:<BR>(1) अथ<BR>(or commonly) अथातः,<BR>n. we will describe<BR>penances:<BR>अथातो प्रायश्चित्तानि व्याख्यास्यामः, At.;<BR>(2) अतः परम्<BR>or<BR>अत ऊर्द्धम् (= after this),<BR>n. I will<BR>tell you:<BR>अतः परं॥ युष्माकं सम्प्रवक्ष्यामि, Pa.;<BR>(3)<BR>इदानीम्,<BR>it n. remains:<BR>इदमिदानीमवशिष्टम्, S. iv. i.;<BR>(4) सम्प्रति, S. iv. = but: q.v.: तु<BR>“n. Barab-<BR>bas was a robber”:<BR>बरब्बास्तु दस्युरासीत्। Ph.:<BR>n. and then:<BR>(1) समये समये (= at times);<BR>(2)<BR>कदाचित्: v. Sometimes;<BR>n. and n.:<BR>तदा तदा,<BR>D. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

now-a-days
NOW-A-DAYS: एषु दिवसेषु, V.<BR>People n.:<BR>इदानी-<BR>न्तनाः (लोकाः), S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noway
NOWAY, NOWAYS, NOWISE: न कथञ्चन; न केनापि<BR> प्रकारेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nowhere
NOWHERE: न and क्वचित्, क्वापि, कृत्रचित्,<BR>or<BR>कुत्रापि,<BR>n. else:<BR>नान्यत्र कुत्रापि, N. iii. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noxious
NOXIOUS:<BR>I Of air, etc.: दुष्ट (f. ष्टा): v.<BR>Injurious.<BR>II Of animals: हिंस्र (f. स्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

noxiousness
NOXIOUSNESS: दुष्टता: v. Injuriousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nozzle
NOZZLE:<BR>I Lit.: नासाग्रम्।<BR>II Of a vessel:<BR>कर्णः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nude
NUDE: नग्न (f. ग्ना): v. Naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nudge
NUDGE (v.): perh. स्पृशति (स्पृश्, c. 6 (= to<BR>touch).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nudity
NUDITY: नग्नत्वम्, -ता: v. Nakedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nugatory
NUGATORY:<BR>(1) निष्फलः (ला, लं): v. Fruit-<BR>-less;<BR>(2) निरर्थकः (का, कं): v. Vain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nugget
NUGGET: पिण्ड (mn.): v. Mass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nuisance
NUISANCE:<BR>I Of men, etc.:<BR>(1) उत्पातः;<BR>(2)<BR>कण्टक (mn.) (= thorn),<BR>clearing n.s:<BR>कण्टकान्<BR> विशोघयन्, D. vii.<BR>II In law: no equiv.:<BR>*सम्पीडनम्,<BR>public n.:<BR>*साधारणसम्पीडनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

null
NULL:<BR>(1) निष्फलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) मोघः (घा, घं);<BR>(3) व्यर्थ (f. र्था);<BR>(4) निरर्थकः (का, कं);<BR>(5)<BR>विकलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nullify
NULLIFY:<BR>(1) निष्फलीकरोति, etc.;<BR>(2) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nullity
NULLITY:<BR>I The state:<BR>(1) निष्फलता;<BR>(2)<BR>निरर्थकता, etc.<BR>II Anything null: expr.<BR>by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

numb
NUMB (adj.):<BR>(1) निस्तेजस् (mfn.);<BR>(2) जडः<BR>(डा, डं);<BR>(3) स्तब्ध (f. ब्धा);<BR>(4) अवसन्नः (न्ना,<BR> न्नं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

numb
NUMB (v.): जडीकरोति: v. Numb, to benumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

number
NUMBER (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) संख्या,<BR>tell the<BR>total n. of the flock:<BR>सकलां यूथस्य संख्यां वद, Li.;<BR>beyond n.:<BR>अतीतसंख्यः (ख्या, ख्यं), Ki.;<BR>accord-<BR>ing to the n. of the sciences:<BR>विद्यापरिसंख्यया, R.;<BR>prime n.:<BR>*मूलसंख्या;<BR>theory of n.s:<BR>*संख्यातत्त्वम्;<BR>(2) राशिः (= quantity)<BR>what n.:<BR>को राशिः।<BR>II A great n.:<BR>(1) expr. by बहु (f. ह्वी)<BR>(= many: q. v.);<BR>(2) सङ्घः (= crowd, multi-<BR>-tude: q. v.),<BR>in n. s:<BR>सङ्घशः।<BR>III Nume-<BR>-rousness:<BR>(1) संख्या,<BR>the strength of an army<BR>does not depend on its n.:<BR>*बलानां बलं न संख्याधीनम्;<BR>(2) बहुत्वम्।<BR>III In gram.: वचनम्,<BR>n. and<BR>person:<BR>पुरूषवचने, S. k.;<BR>the singular n.:<BR>एकवचनम्;<BR>the dual n.:<BR>द्विवचनम्;<BR>the plural n.:<BR>वहुबचनम्।<BR>IV In pl., poetry, metre: q. v.: छन्दस् (n.).<BR>V In. pl.,<BR>the book of n.s:<BR>*संख्याध्यायः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

number
NUMBER (v.):<BR>I To count: q. v.: संख्याति,<BR> परि-, (ख्या, c. 2.), by n.ing one, two, three:<BR>एका द्वे तिस्न इति संख्यानेन, M. n.<BR>II To give<BR>the n. of, perh. संख्याति; संख्यां करोति, Mah.<BR>III To reckon as one of a n.:<BR>(1) संख्याति;<BR>(2) expr. by संख्या,<BR>or to n. above men:<BR>मनुष्य-<BR>संख्यामतिवर्तितुं वा, Ki. iii, 40.<BR>IV To amount<BR>to: expr. by संख्या,<BR>n.ing five thousand:<BR>पञ्च-<BR>सहस्रसंख्य (f. ख्या), -क (f. -का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

numberless
NUMBERLESS: असंख्य (f. ख्या): v. Innumer-<BR>-able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

numbness
NUMBNESS:<BR>(1) जाड्यम्;<BR>(2) स्तब्धता;<BR>(3) स्तम्मः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

numeral
NUMERAL:<BR>(1) संख्या;<BR>(2) अङ्कः (= figure).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

numeration
NUMERATION: perh. संख्यानम्, परि- (after<BR>गुणनम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

numerator
NUMERATOR: अंशः, multiply the n.s with the<BR>denominators of other (fractions): तत्तदंशं परेषां<BR> छेदैर्गुणितं कुर्यात्, A. c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

numerical
NUMERICAL: expr. by comp., n. strength:<BR>*संख्याबलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

numerically
NUMERICALLY:<BR>(1) संख्यया, परि-;<BR>(2) संख्यानेन,<BR> परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

numerous
NUMEROUS: बहुसंख्य (f. ख्या), -कः (का, कं): v.<BR>Also many. Ph.:<BR>“n. verse”:<BR>छन्दोबद्धं पद्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

numerously
NUMEROUSLY:<BR>it was n. attended:<BR>तत्र बहवः समा-<BR>गमन्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

numerousness
NUMEROUSNESS:<BR>(1) बहुत्वम्;<BR>(2) आधिक्यम् (when<BR>there is direct or implied comparison): v.<BR>More.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

numismatics
NUMISMATICS: *मुद्राविज्ञानं and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

numismatist
NUMISMATIST, NUMISMATOLOGIST: *मुद्राविज्ञान-<BR>विशारदः (दा, दं), -विद् (mfn.), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nun
NUN: ब्रह्मचारिणी (?).<BR>Buddhist n.:<BR>सौगतपरि-<BR>व्राजिका, Ma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nuncio
NUNCIO: दूतः: v. Ambassador.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nunnery
NUNNERY: विहारः (?); *ब्रह्मचारिणीविहारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nuptial
NUPTIAL (adj.):<BR>(1) by tat.,<BR>n. hall:<BR>विवाह-<BR>मण्डपः, N.;<BR>(2) वैवाहिक (f. की),<BR>with n.<BR>preparations:<BR>वैवाहिकैः संविधानैः, Ku.;<BR>(3) वैवाह<BR>(f. ही),<BR>in proper n. hour:<BR>युक्ते मुहूर्ते वैवाहे, Ram.;<BR>(4) औद्वाहिक (f. की),<BR>n. gift:<BR>औद्वाहिकम्, M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nuptial
NUPTIAL (subs.): gen. in pl.: उद्वाहः, -कर्मन्<BR>(n.) M: v. Marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nurse
NURSE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: धात्री,<BR>wet-n.:<BR>दोग्ध्री घात्री,<BR>Sr.; by Mālatī's n.'s daughter Lavangikā:<BR>मालतीधात्रेय्या लवङ्गिकया, Ma.<BR>II For sick [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">Page479</a>]<BR>men: परिचारिका।<BR>III Fig.:<BR>(1) पालयितृ (f.<BR>त्री);<BR>(2) सम्भावयितृ (f. त्री), the n. of the wise:<BR>सम्भावयिता बुद्धान्, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nurse
NURSE (v. t.):<BR>I To nourish: q.v.: वर्धयति,<BR> वि- (c. of वृध्),<BR>n. ed the plants:<BR>वृक्षकान् व्यव-<BR>र्धयत्, Ku. v. 14.<BR>II To tend: उप-चरति, परि-<BR>(चर्, c. 1.),<BR>the wounded king was n.d by<BR>you yourself:<BR>राजा शस्त्रपरिक्षतः त्वयोपचरितः स्वयम्,<BR>Ram. ii. 8. 14.<BR>III To suckle: q.v.: दुग्धं<BR> पाययति (c. of पा), Sr.<BR>IV To protect,<BR>cherish: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nursery
NURSERY:<BR>I For children: लालनागारम् (?).<BR>II For plants: *वर्धनस्थानम्।<BR>III Fig.:<BR>(1)<BR>आश्रयः;<BR>(2) कुलभवनम्, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nursery-man
NURSERY-MAN: *वर्धनस्थानपालः, लता-। N.B. पुष्पोप-<BR>जीविन् (m.) may occasionally^1 do.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nursing
NURSING (subs.): Of the sick: उपचारः<BR>or<BR>परि-<BR>चारः: v. To nurse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nursling
NURSLING: स्तनन्धयः: v. Infant, child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nurture
NURTURE (subs.):<BR>I Nourishment: q.v.:<BR>पोषणम्।<BR>II Instruction, education: q.v.:<BR>शिक्षा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nurture
NURTURE (v.):<BR>I To nourish: q.v.: पोषयति<BR>(पुष्, c. 10.).<BR>II To educate, bring up:<BR>q.v.: विनयति (नी, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nut
NUT: no. equiv.: *अस्थिफलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nut-brown
NUT-BROWN: perh. श्यावः (वा, वं): v. Brown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nut-cracker
NUT-CRACKER: *अस्थिफलविदंशकः<BR>or<BR>-भञ्जकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nuthatch
NUTHATCH: पक्षिविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nut-hook
NUT-HOOK: आकर्षणी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nutmeg
NUTMEG:<BR>I The plant: जातिः<BR>or<BR>जाती।<BR>II<BR>The fruit:<BR>(1) जातीफलम्;<BR>(2) जातिकोषम्<BR>(शम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nutriment
NUTRIMENT: पौष्टिकम्: v. Nourishment, food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nutrition
NUTRITION: पुष्टिः: v. Nourishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nutritious
NUTRITIOUS, NUTRITIVE: पुष्टिकरः (री, रं): v.<BR>Nourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nutritiousness
NUTRITIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) पुष्टिकरत्वम्;<BR>(2) पौष्टिकता;<BR>(3) बृंहणत्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nutshell
NUTSHELL perh.: कञ्चु कः<BR>or<BR>बहिरस्थि (n.). Ph.:<BR>to lie in a n.: perh. द्व्यक्षरसाध्य (f. ध्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nutting
NUTTING: *अस्थिफलाहरणम्, etc.: v. To gather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nux vomica plant
NUX VOMICA PLANT: वरम्बरा, Wilson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nylgau
NYLGAU, NYLGHAU: नीलः, “नीलांश्चैव महानीलान्”,<BR>Mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

nymph
NYMPH:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अप्सरस् (f.: gen. in pl.);<BR>(2) विद्याधरी;<BR>(3) सुरसुन्दरी।<BR>Wood-n.:<BR>वनदेवता,<BR>U.;<BR>water-n.:<BR>जलदेवता।<BR>II Fig.: सुन्दरी;<BR> विलासिनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

o
O, OH:<BR>I In addressing:<BR>(1) हे;<BR>(2) भो भोः,<BR>or<BR>भो भो (gen. to men),<BR>o, courtiers:<BR>भो भो<BR> कुलचारिणः, Vi.;<BR>(3) अयि<BR>or<BR>अये (expr. of<BR>tenderness),<BR>o, you unbearing:<BR>अयि असहने, Ra.;<BR>(4) रे<BR>or<BR>अरे (to inferiors or in contempt),<BR>o,<BR>you fool:<BR>अरे मूर्ख, Mr.;<BR>(5) हा (in sorrow),<BR>o, my father, o, my mothers, o, my dear friend<BR>Sugriva:<BR>हा तात, हा मातरः, हा प्रियसख सुग्रीव, U;<BR>(6) by voc.<BR>II Of joy and surprise:<BR>(1)<BR>अहो,<BR>oh, how grand and beautiful is earth:<BR>अहो<BR> उदाररमणीया पृथिवी, Sa.;<BR>(2) अयि<BR>or<BR>अये,<BR>oh, you<BR>also don't know:<BR>अयि त्वमपि न वेत्सि, Mah.<BR>III Of surprise, anger, contempt: आः,<BR>oh, I understand, very well:<BR>आः ज्ञातं, तिष्ठ, Mu.<BR>IV Of grief: हा: v. Alas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oak
OAK: a tree: सिन्दूरः, Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oaken
OAKEN:<BR>(1) सिन्दूर- in comp. (?);<BR>(2) सिन्दूर-<BR>काष्ठमयः (यी, यं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oakum
OAKUM: perh. तलपत्रम् (comp. Bengali<BR>कालापाति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oar
OAR:<BR>(1) दण्डः (when the sense is clear);<BR>(2) क्षेपणिः, -णी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oar
OAR (v.): v. To row. O.ed: by comp.,<BR>four-o.:<BR>चतुर्दण्ड (f. ण्डा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oat
OAT, OATS: धान्यभेदः, *ओटः (use also for the<BR>seed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oaten
OATEN:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) *औटः (टी, टं);<BR>(3) *ओटमयः (यी, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oath
OATH:<BR>(1) शपथः,<BR>to take an o.:<BR>शपथं करोति, D.;<BR>to bind with an o.:<BR>शपथेन नियच्छति, N. s.;<BR>to<BR>administer an o.:<BR>शपथं शापयति, Mit.;<BR>he swore<BR>thousand of o.s:<BR>सहस्रशोऽसौ शपथानशप्यत्, B. iii.<BR>32.;<BR>(2) दिव्यम्। (= special oath; ordeal:<BR>q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oath-breaking
OATH-BREAKING (subs.): शपथमङ्गः: v. Per-<BR>-jury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oat-meal
OAT-MEAL: *ओटचूर्णम्<BR>or<BR>ओटक्षोदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obduracy
OBDURACY: काठिन्यम्: v. Hardness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obdurate
OBDURATE: कठिनः (ना, नं): v. Hard, obsti-<BR>-nate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obdurately
OBDURATELY: कठिनम्: v. Hardly, obstinately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obedience
OBEDIENCE: आज्ञानुवृत्तिः and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(2)<BR>वश्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obedient
OBEDIENT:<BR>(1) आज्ञाकरः (री, रं) and sim.<BR>comp.s., your o. servant is exceedingly obliged:<BR>सोऽयमार्येणाज्ञाकरो जनोऽत्यर्थमनुगृहीतः, D. vi.;<BR>(2)<BR>आज्ञानुवर्तिन् (f. नी) and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(3)<BR>वश्य (f. श्या)<BR>or<BR>वशग (f. गा), etc. (= submissive).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obediently
OBEDIENTLY: आज्ञायां तिष्ठत् (f. न्ती): v. To<BR>obey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obeisance
OBEISANCE:<BR>(1) नमस्कारः;<BR>(2) प्रणामः;<BR>(3)<BR>प्रणतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obelisk
OBELISK: perh. स्तूपः; *सूचिस्तूपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obelize
OBELIZE: *सूचिरेखया चिह्नयति (चिह्न, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obelus
OBELUS: *सूचिरेखा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obese
OBESE: भेदस्विन् (f. नी): v. Fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obesity
OBESITY: मेदस्विता: v. Fatness, corpulence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obey
OBEY:<BR>to o. one or one's order:<BR>आज्ञाम्, निर्देशम्, etc.<BR>पालयति, अनु-, प्रति- (पाल्, c. 10.),<BR>or<BR>करोति<BR>(कृ, c. 8.),<BR>or<BR>अनुवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.),<BR>or<BR>अनुविधत्ते<BR>(धा, c. 3.),<BR>or<BR>वचनं शृणोति (श्रु, c. 5.), or<BR>आज्ञायां etc. तिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.); to o. laws etc.:<BR>अनुवर्तते: v. To follow: v. Also to disobey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obfuscate
OBFUSCATE: विक्लवीकरोति: v. To bewilder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obfuscation
OBFUSCATION:<BR>I Lit.: v. To darken.<BR>II<BR>Bewilderment: q.v.: वैक्लव्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obituary
OBITUARY: *मृत्युनिर्देशः; मरणोल्लेखः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

object
OBJECT (subs.):<BR>I As opposed to subject:<BR>विषयः,<BR>of the o. and the subject:<BR>विषयविषयिणोः,<BR>S.<BR>II. An external thing:<BR>(1) द्रव्यम्,<BR>an o.<BR>does not destroy its cause or effect:<BR>न द्रव्यं कार्यं<BR> कारणञ्च वधति, V. d.;<BR>(2) वस्तु (n.),<BR>for external<BR>o.s:<BR>बाह्यवस्तुषु, Ku. Ph.: an o. of sense:<BR>इन्द्रियार्थः, V. d.;<BR>an o. of hearing:<BR>श्रोत्रग्रहणोऽर्थः,<BR>V. d.<BR>III An o. of emotion or effort:<BR>(1)<BR>पात्रम्,<BR>I was the o. of (their) looks:<BR>अहमभूवं पात्र-<BR>मालोकितानाम्, Ma.; (proper) and improper o.:<BR>पात्रमपात्रं वा, Mal.;<BR>(2) भाजनम्,<BR>o. of love:<BR>प्रणय-<BR>भाजनम्;<BR>(3) स्थानम् and sim. words (= place),<BR>excellencies are o.s of adoration:<BR>गुणाः पूजास्थानम्,<BR>U. iv. 11.;<BR>o. of trust:<BR>विश्वासभूमिः, H.;<BR>(4) with become, by circumlo.,<BR>becomes an<BR>o. of hatred among the people:<BR>द्वेष्यतां याति लोके,<BR>P.: v. To become.<BR>IV Aim, intention:<BR>(1) प्रयोजनम्:<BR>without some o.:<BR>निष्प्रयोजनम्, Mu.;<BR>(2) अर्थः,<BR>this o. is io be accomplished with ano-<BR>ther o.:<BR>अर्थोऽयमर्थान्तरमाव्य एव, Ku.;<BR>and with<BR>this o.:<BR>एतदर्थञ्च, Vi.;<BR>(3) अभिप्रायः (= intention),<BR>but I, understanding his o.:<BR>अहन्तु विदितामिप्राया,<BR>K.<BR>V. In gram.: कर्मन् (n.),<BR>without distin-<BR>guishing o. and subject:<BR>अविशिष्टकर्तृकर्ममावम्,<BR>An.;<BR>taking two o. s:<BR>द्विकर्मकः, S. k.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

object
OBJECT (v.):<BR>I In gen.: expr. by verbs<BR>अभिधत्ते (धा, c. 3.), etc. (= to say)<BR>or<BR>मन्यते<BR>(मन्, c. 4.), etc. (= to think) and adj.s<BR>भ्रान्त (f. न्ता), असङ्गत (f. ता), अप्रामाणिक (f.<BR>की), etc.<BR>II To expose: विवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

objection
OBJECTION:<BR>(1) प्रतिवादः (?);<BR>(2) आपत्तिः<BR>(used in Bengali);<BR>(3) बाधा (= obstruction.<BR>obstacle);<BR>(4) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

objectionable
OBJECTIONABLE: दुष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं), असङ्गतः (ता, तं),<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

objective
OBJECTIVE: v. Object (v.), (II)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

objectively
OBJECTIVELY: expr. by adj. विषयगतः (ता, तं).<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

objector
OBJECTOR: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

objurgate
OBJURGATE: भर्त्सयति (भर्त्स्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>reprove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

objurgation
OBJURGATION: भर्त्सना: v. Reproof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oblate
OBLATE: in geo.: *अवनतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oblation
OBLATION:<BR>(1) बलिः, offer o.s to the (divine)<BR>mothers:<BR>मातृभ्यो बलिमुपहर, Mr. i.;<BR>(2) नैवेद्यम्<BR>(of uncooked rice, sweetmeats etc.);<BR>(3)<BR>हव्यम् (in fire, gen. of ghee);<BR>(4) कव्यम् (to the<BR>manes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obligation
OBLIGATION:<BR>I Binding moral power:<BR>(1)<BR>बन्धः (= bond);<BR>(2) धर्मः (= duty).<BR>II A<BR>contract: q.v.: संविद् (f.).<BR>III Indebted-<BR>-ness: under o. expr. by ऋणिन् (f, नी)<BR>(= indebted),<BR>or<BR>उपकृतः (ता, तं) (= done [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">Page481</a>]<BR>good to)<BR>or<BR>अनुगृहीतः (ता, तं) (= favoured)<BR>or<BR>बद्ध (f. द्धा),<BR>his generosity lay the whole vill-<BR>age under o.:<BR>*ग्रामः समग्रस्तस्य दयालुतया बद्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obligatory
OBLIGATORY: expr. with अवश्यम् (= must:<BR>q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oblige
OBLIGE:<BR>I To bind: बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.).<BR>II To compel: q.v. O. d. = under obli-<BR>-gation: v. Obligation (III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obliging
OBLIGING (adj.): दक्षिण (f. णा): v. Also<BR>kind, good-natured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obligingly
OBLIGINGLY: दाक्षिण्येन: v. Also liberally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obligingness
OBLIGINGNESS: दाक्षिण्यम्: v. Kindness, civility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oblique
OBLIQUE: वक्र (f. क्रा),<BR>o. line:<BR>वक्ररेखा;<BR>o.<BR>insinuation:<BR>वक्रोक्तिः;<BR>o. speech:<BR>*कथकस्य<BR>i. e. teller's (in opposition to वक्तुः = speaker's<BR>i. e. direct) उक्तिः;<BR>o. case:<BR>अप्रधानकारकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obliquely
OBLIQUELY: वक्रम्: v. Askance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obliqueness
OBLIQUENESS: Obliquity.<BR>I Lit.: वक्रता: v.<BR>Crookedness.<BR>II Deviation: नतिः।<BR>III<BR>Fig., iniquity: q.v.: वक्रता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obliterate
OBLITERATE:<BR>(1) लुम्पति, वि-, आ-, अव- (लुप्, c.<BR>6.),<BR>my sight is o.d:<BR>दृष्टिरालुप्यते मे, Me. ii. 44.;<BR>(2) मार्ष्टि, परि-, प्र-, अप- (भृज्, c. 2.): To<BR>erase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obliteration
OBLITERATION:<BR>(1) लोपः, वि-, अव-, आ-;<BR>(2)<BR>मार्जना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oblivion
OBLIVION: विस्मृतिः: v. Forgetfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oblivious
OBLIVIOUS:<BR>I Causing oblivion: स्मृतिमुष्<BR>(mfn.), स्मृतिहरः (री, रं) and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Forgetful: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oblong
OBLONG:<BR>I Adj.: आयतः (ता, तं).<BR>II Subs.:<BR>आयतः, Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obloquy
OBLOQUY: परि(री)वादः: v. Censure, reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obnoxious
OBNOXIOUS:<BR>I Liable, subject: q.v.: -वशः<BR>(शा, शं) in comp.<BR>II Offensive, hateful:<BR>q.v.: गर्हितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obnoxiously
OBNOXIOUSLY: expr. by circumlo. with adj.<BR>or pres. part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obolus
OBOLUS: *ऐलेनः क्षुद्ररूप्यमुद्राविशेषः; औपलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obscene
OBSCENE:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) अश्लीलः (ला, लं)<BR>(= indecent: q.v.);<BR>(2) व्रीडाकरः (री, रं)<BR>and sim. comp.s (lit. = producing shame),<BR>Sah.<BR>(3) वियातः (ता, तं) (= immodest);<BR>(4) न्यङ्गसंयुतः (ता, तं) (in low abuse), Mit.<BR>II Ill-omened: अमङ्गलः (ला, लं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obscenely
OBSCENELY:<BR>(1) अश्लीलम् (acc.);<BR>(2) often by<BR>comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obscenity
OBSCENITY:<BR>I The state:<BR>(1) अश्लीलता;<BR>(2)<BR>व्रीडाकरता।<BR>II Anything obscene: expr.<BR>by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obscuration
OBSCURATION:<BR>(1) आच्छादनम्;<BR>(2) आवरणम्,<BR>for o. of sight:<BR>आवरणाय दृष्टेः, R. v. 18.;<BR>(3)<BR>उपरोधः, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obscure
OBSCURE (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) आच्छादयति: v.<BR>Eclipse;<BR>(2) आवृणोति (घृ, c. 5.),<BR>o. ing eye-<BR>sight:<BR>लोचनमार्गमावृण्वत् (f. ती), K. vii. 42.:<BR>v. To cover. Ph.: with eyes o.d with ichor:<BR>मदान्धकारिताक्ष (f. क्षी), V. p. i. ix. 10.: v. To<BR>darken.<BR>II Fig.: expr. by adj.: v. Obs-<BR>-cure; clear, not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obscure
OBSCURE:<BR>I Covered over, darkened:<BR>(1)<BR>आच्छादितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) आवृतः (ता, तं);<BR>(3)<BR>उपरूद्ध (f. द्धा): v. Also dark.<BR>II Retired,<BR>unknown: अप्रसिद्ध (f. द्धा): v. Also humble,<BR>mean.<BR>III Not easily understood:<BR>(1)<BR>कष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं),<BR>o. meaning:<BR>कष्टोऽर्थः, Kav. vii.<BR>7.;<BR>(2) कष्टार्थ (f. र्था) (of passage, etc.);<BR>(3) क्लिष्ट (f. ष्टा) (= difficult: q.v.).<BR>IV<BR>Hidden: गूढ (f. ढा), नि-, whose truths are o.:<BR>निगूढतत्त्व (f. त्त्वा), Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obscurely
OBSCURELY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obscurity
OBSCURITY:<BR>I Darkness: q.v.<BR>II Hidden-<BR>-ness, privacy: गूढता, -त्वम्, नि-।<BR>III Un-<BR>-intelligibleness: कष्टार्थता।<BR>IV Meanness:<BR>q.v.: नीचता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obsequies
OBSEQUIES:<BR>(1) अन्त्येष्टिः, -क्रिया;<BR>(1) नैष्ठिको<BR> विधिः, R. viii. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obsequious
OBSEQUIOUS: छन्दोनुवर्तिन् (f. नी): v. Also<BR>submissive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obsequiously
OBSEQUIOUSLY: expr. with कृताञ्जलि (mfn.),<BR>अधिदैवतमिव, K., etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obsequity
OBSEQUITY: छन्दोनुवर्तित्त्वम्, -ता: v. Also servi-<BR>-lity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

observable
OBSERVABLE: v. Remarkable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

observance
OBSERVANCE:<BR>I Attention: आदरः।<BR>II Per- [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">Page482</a>]<BR>-formance: पालनम्, प्रति-, अनु-।<BR>III Rite,<BR>usage: q.v.: कर्मन् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

observant
OBSERVANT: gen. with of: expr. by verb.:<BR>v. Also attentive, careful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

observation
OBSERVATION:<BR>I The act: अवेक्षणम्, परि-।<BR>II<BR>A remark: q. v.: अनुशासनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

observatory
OBSERVATORY: दिगवलोकनप्रासादः (Sa. but not<BR>in the exact sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

observe
OBSERVE:<BR>I To notice with care: अवेक्षते,<BR> परि- (ईक्ष्, c. 1.), o. ing that the verb (conveys)<BR>the sense of motion:<BR>अवेक्ष्य धातोर्गमनार्थम्, R. iii.<BR>4.: v. To look, consider.<BR>II To keep,<BR>obey. q.v.: पालयति, प्रति-, अनु-, (पाल्, c.<BR>10.).<BR>III To remark: q.v.: अभि-दधाति or<BR>धत्ते (धा, c. 3.).<BR>IV To humour: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

observer
OBSERVER:<BR>I Spectator: q.v.: अवेक्षकः।<BR>II<BR>Keeper: प्रति-पालयितृ (f. त्री), अनु-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

observing
OBSERVING (adj.): अप्रमत्तदृश् (mfn.) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

observingly
OBSERVINGLY: अप्रमत्तः (त्ता, त्तं): v. Care-<BR>-fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obsidian
OBSIDIAN: उपलविशेषः; *अक्षोदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obsolete
OBSOLETE:<BR>(1) गतव्यवहारः (रा, रं) (?);<BR>(2)<BR>लुप्तप्रयोगः (गा, गं) (of words etc (?) and<BR>sim. comp.s.: v. Also ancient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obsoleteness
OBSOLETENESS:<BR>(1) प्रयोगलोपः (?) and sim.<BR>comp.s.;<BR>(2) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obstacle
OBSTACLE:<BR>(1) अन्तरायः;<BR>(2) व्याघातः;<BR>(3)<BR>प्रतिबन्धः;<BR>(4) बाधा;<BR>(5) प्रत्यूहः;<BR>(6) प्रतिष्टम्भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obstetric
OBSTETRIC: प्रजनन- in comp.: v. Also obs-<BR>-tetrics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obstetrician
OBSTETRICIAN: प्रजननकुशलः (ला, लं), Sr.; प्रसव-<BR>कर्मनिपुण (f. णा), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obstetrics
OBSTETRICS: गर्मिणीव्याकरणम्, Sr.: v. Mid-<BR>-wifery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obstinacy
OBSTINACY:<BR>(1) निर्बन्धः (= pertinacity);<BR>(2)<BR>दार्ढ्यम् (= firmness);<BR>(3) अविनेयता (= indoci-<BR>-lity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obstinate
OBSTINATE:<BR>(1) दृढः (ढा, ढं) (= firm),<BR>really<BR>you are very o.:<BR>सत्यमतिदृढासि, U. iv.;<BR>(2)<BR>अविनेयः (या, यं) (= indocile);<BR>(3) निरवग्रहः<BR>(हा, हं) (= self-willed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obstinately
OBSTINATELY:<BR>(1) निर्बन्घेन;<BR>(2) दृढम् (= firmly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obstreperous
OBSTREPEROUS: expr. with कलकलः<BR>or<BR>कोलाहलः<BR>v. Noisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obstreperously
OBSTREPEROUSLY:<BR>(1) कलकलैः;<BR>(2) कोलाहलैः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obstruct
OBSTRUCT:<BR>(1) रूणद्धि<BR>or<BR>रूंधे, अव- (रूध्, c. 9.)<BR>(= to stop, hinder, block up),<BR>your patience<BR>like coast o. s the Yādava-oceans:<BR>यादवाम्भोनिधीन्<BR> रूधे वेलेव भवतः क्षमा, Si.;<BR>(2) बाधते, प्र-, (बाध्,<BR>c. 1 (= to impede, trouble),<BR>you always<BR>o. us:<BR>सदैवास्मान् प्रबाधसे, Mah. iii. 372. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obstruction
OBSTRUCTION: बाधा: v. Obstacle, hindrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obstructive
OBSTRUCTIVE:<BR>(1) बाधक (f. धिका);<BR>(2)<BR>बाधाकरः (री, रं);<BR>(3) संरोधिन् (f. नी), अव-,<BR> प्रति-;<BR>(4) प्रतिबन्धक (f. न्धिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obtain
OBTAIN (v.t.): समासादयति (c. of सद्): v. To<BR>get, gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obtain
OBTAIN (v. i.): expr. with प्रबलः (ला, लं) or<BR>प्रचलितः (ता, तं) (= current).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obtestation
OBTESTATION: अभ्यर्थना: v. Entreaty, suppli-<BR>-cation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obtrude
OBTRUDE: हठेन<BR>or<BR>हठात् प्रविशति (विश्, c. 6 (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obtrusive
OBTRUSIVE: expr. by circumlo.: धृष्ट (f. ष्टा)<BR>(= bold).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obtrusively
OBTRUSIVELY:<BR>(1) साबाधम् (?);<BR>(2) हठेन<BR>(= forcibly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obtuse
OBTUSE:<BR>I In geo.:<BR>o. angle:<BR>*विषमकोणः;<BR> अधिककोणः। K. d.<BR>II Dull, stupid: q.v.:<BR>जडः (डा, डं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obtusely
OBTUSELY: दुर्बुद्धितया: v. Stupidly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obtuseness
OBTUSENESS: जाड्यम्: v. Dullness, stupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obverse
OBVERSE (subs.): of a coin: मुखम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obviate
OBVIATE: दूरीकरोति: v. To prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obvious
OBVIOUS: स्पष्ट (f. ष्टा): v. Manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

obviously
OBVIOUSLY: स्पष्टम्: v. Evidently, plainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

occasion
OCCASION (v.): जनयति: v. To cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

occasion
OCCASION (subs.):<BR>I Opportunity: q.v.:<BR>अवसरः।<BR>II Incidental cause expr. with<BR>निमित्तम्।<BR>III Need: प्रयोजनम्।<BR>IV Incident,<BR>occurrence: घटना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

occasional
OCCASIONAL: expr. by adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

occasionally
OCCASIONALLY:<BR>(1) अन्तरान्तरा;<BR>(2) समये समये<BR>(= at times).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

occidental
OCCIDENTAL: प्रतीच्य (f. च्या): v. Western.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

occipetal
OCCIPETAL:<BR>o. bone:<BR>*शिरःपृष्ठास्थि (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

occult
OCCULT: गूढः (ढा, ढं), नि-,: v. Secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

occupancy
OCCUPANCY: भोगः: v. Possession (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

occupant
OCCUPANT:<BR>(1) भोगकारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) भोक्तृ<BR>(f. क्त्री), परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

occupation
OCCUPATION:<BR>I The act: अधिष्ठानम्।<BR>II<BR>Possession: q.v.: भोगः।<BR>III Employment,<BR>calling: वृत्तिः: v. Livelihood.<BR>IV Busi-<BR>-ness: q.v.: व्यापारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

occupier
OCCUPIER: अधिष्ठातृ (f. त्री) (?): v. Also<BR>occupant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

occupy
OCCUPY:<BR>I To hold, cover: अधितिष्ठति (स्था,<BR>c. 1 (?).<BR>II To possess: q.v.: भुंक्ते (भुज्,<BR>c. 7.).<BR>III To employ: नि-योजयति<BR>or<BR>युंक्ते<BR>(युज्, c. 10. and 7.),<BR>to o. oneself:<BR>व्याप्रियते<BR>(पृ, c. 6.) or with व्यापृतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

occur
OCCUR:<BR>I To be found here and there:<BR>expr. with: अस्ति, वर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.).<BR>II To<BR>come into the mind: मनसि उदेति (इ, c.<BR>2.),<BR>doubts, o. ring to her:<BR>मनसि विकल्पानुद्यतः,<BR>N. xiii. 54.<BR>III To happen: q.v.: वर्तते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

occurrence
OCCURRENCE:<BR>I Occasional presentation:<BR>by verb:<BR>of rare o.:<BR>कदाचित् सम्भवति।<BR>II<BR>Event: q.v.: घटना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ocean
OCEAN (subs.):<BR>(1) समुद्रः;<BR>(2) सागरः;<BR>(3)<BR>अर्णवः;<BR>(4) अम्भोनिधिः, पयोधिः and sim.<BR>comp.;<BR>(5) रत्नाकरः;<BR>(6) वारां राशिः and sim.<BR>comp.s. (poet.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ocean
OCEAN, OCEANIC (adj.):<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2)<BR>सामुद्र (f. द्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ochre
OCHRE:<BR>(1) रक्तोपलम्, Wilson;<BR>(2) सुवर्णगैरिकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

octagon
OCTAGON:<BR>(1) अष्टकोणः;<BR>(2) अष्टभुजः;<BR>(3)<BR>अष्टास्रः, Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

octagonal
OCTAGONAL: अष्टभुजः (जा, जं): v. Octangu-<BR>-lar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

octahadron
OCTAHADRON: *अष्टाग्रः (comp. द्वादशाग्रः, A. b.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

octangular
OCTANGULAR:<BR>(1) अष्टकोणः (णा, णं);<BR>(2) अष्टास्रः<BR>(स्रा, स्रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

octave
OCTAVE: अष्टमी, Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

octavo
OCTAVO: *अष्टक- in comp.: अष्टमङ्गि (mfn.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

octennial
OCTENNIAL: अष्टवार्षिकः (की, कं) (in both<BR>senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

octennially
OCTENNIALLY: अष्टमेऽष्टमे वर्षे and sim. comp.s.:<BR>v. Every.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

october
OCTOBER: उत्तराश्विनपूर्वकार्त्तिकसंवादीयुरूपीयवर्षस्य दशमो<BR> मासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

octogenarian
OCTOGENARIAN:<BR>(1) अशीतिर्यस्य वर्षाणि, A. p.;<BR>(2) अशीतिवर्षवयस्कः (का, कं) and sim. comp.s.<BR>अशीतिवर्ष (f. र्षा), P.;<BR>(3) अशीतिकः (का, कं),<BR>Ka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

octosyllabic
OCTOSYLLABIC: अष्टाक्षर (f. रा); अष्टस्वरः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

octroi
OCTROI: शुल्कम् (= custom).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ocular
OCULAR:<BR>(1) प्रत्यक्ष - in comp.;<BR>(2) चाक्षुषः<BR>(षी, षं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ocularly
OCULARLY:<BR>(1) by ins: चक्षुषा, etc.: v. Eye;<BR>(2) प्रत्यक्षतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oculist
OCULIST: नेत्ररोगचिकित्सकः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

odd
ODD:<BR>I Not even: विषमः (मा, मं).<BR>II<BR>Remaining over and above round num-<BR>-bers: कतिपयः (या, यं).<BR>III Strange, pecu-<BR>-liar, queer: अपरूपः (पा, पं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oddity
ODDITY: anything odd: expr. by adj.:<BR>अपरूपः (पा, पं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oddly
ODDLY:<BR>o. shaped:<BR>अपरूपः (पा, पं): v. Odd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oddness
ODDNESS:<BR>I Of numbers: वैषम्यम् (?).<BR>II<BR>Singularity, strangeness: अपरूपता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

odds
ODDS:<BR>I Excess: आधिक्यम्।<BR>II Inequality:<BR>वैषम्यम्।<BR>III Advantage, superiority: q.v.:<BR>Ph.: (a) at o. i. e. in dispute: expr.<BR>with वैषम्यम्<BR>or<BR>अनैक्यम्; (b) o. and ends:<BR>यत्तद्वस्तु (n.), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ode
ODE:<BR>(1) गीतम् (= song);<BR>(2) कविता (= poetry).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

odious
ODIOUS:<BR>(1) गर्हितः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) कुत्सितः (ता,<BR> तं);<BR>(3) घृणितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

odiously
ODIOUSLY:<BR>(1) गर्हितम्;<BR>(2) घृणितम्;<BR>(3) कुत्सितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

odiousness
ODIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) गर्हितता;<BR>(2) कुत्सितता;<BR>(3)<BR>गर्ह्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

odium
ODIUM:<BR>I Hatred: घृणा।<BR>II Fault: दोषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

odontology
ODONTOLOGY: दन्तव्याकरणं शारीरम् (comp. धमनी-<BR>व्याकरणं शारीरम्, Sr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

odoriferous
ODORIFEROUS:<BR>(1) गन्धवत् (f. ती): v. Frag-<BR>-rant;<BR>(2) गन्धवहः (हा, हं) (= bearing scent,<BR>as o. gales).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

odoriferousness
ODORIFEROUSNESS: गन्धवत्ता: v. Fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

odorous
ODOROUS: सुरभि (mfn.): v. Fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

odour
ODOUR: गन्धः: v. Smell. Ph.:<BR>to be in bad<BR>o.:<BR>अवग्रहगतः (ता, तं): v. Disfavoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

of
OF:<BR>I Denoting relation: expr. by gen.<BR>or tat. comp., daughter of the king of Kāsi:<BR>काशिराजपुत्री, V.;<BR>speed of a chariot:<BR>रथस्य वेगः,<BR>Sa.;<BR>conquest of Tripura:<BR>त्रिपुरविजयः, Me.<BR>N. B. (a) do not use gen. when one subs. is<BR>in apposition with another:<BR>all of us:<BR>सर्वे<BR> वयम्, K.;<BR>entered the city of Oudh:<BR>पुरमविशद-<BR>योध्याम्, R.;<BR>the island of Ceylon:<BR>सिंहलद्वीपः,<BR>Kar.;<BR>in the m. of Fālguna or Chaitra:<BR>फाल्गुने<BR> चैत्रे वा मासि, K. b.; (b) expr. by an adj. or<BR>bah. when it introduces an attributive<BR>clause,<BR>a man of wealth:<BR>धनी;<BR>of great<BR>strength:<BR>महाबलः (ला, लं); of many kinds:<BR>नानाविधः (धा, धं); (c) expr. by a deriv.<BR>when it indicates a man's abode:<BR>a man<BR>of Oudh:<BR>आयोध्यिकः, U.; nobody of this place:<BR>न कश्चिदिहत्यः, D.: v. Inhabitant; (d) part.<BR>in उक (except कामुक) take an acc.,<BR>killer of<BR>demons:<BR>दैत्यान् घातुकः, S. k.<BR>II About, con-<BR>-cerning: q.v.: expr. by gen.,<BR>what would<BR>one say of the other:<BR>किं भणत्वेक एकस्य, Sa.;<BR>do<BR>you remember of your master:<BR>कच्चिद्भर्तुः स्मरसि,<BR>Me.<BR>III Made of: q.v.:<BR>(1) by tat.<BR>comp.,<BR>a house of crystal:<BR>यत्र स्फटिकहर्म्यम्,<BR>Ki.;<BR>(2) -मयः (यी, यं),<BR>a vessel of clay:<BR>मृन्मयं<BR> पात्रम्, R.;<BR>(3) by deriv.,<BR>surely my heart is<BR>of iron:<BR>नूनं हृदयं ममायसम्, Ram.<BR>IV In<BR>partitive sense:<BR>(1) by gen.,<BR>by one of<BR>which:<BR>येषामेकतमेन, P.;<BR>(2) by loc.,<BR>of the<BR>kingdoms you have seen:<BR>भवद्द्य्ष्टेषु राष्ट्रेषु, D.;<BR>(3) gen. expr. by comp. when of follows a<BR>superlative,<BR>best of men:<BR>पुरुषोत्तमः (मा, मं),<BR>A.r.;<BR>greatest of all:<BR>सर्वमहत् (f. ती), S. k.<BR>Ph.: one of the wives (= one wife): एका<BR> भार्या, J.;<BR>many of these:<BR>बहूनीमानि, Mah.<BR>V. To denote cause: expr. by ins., of sorrow:<BR>शोकेन, A. r.: v. From.<BR>VI To denote<BR>descent: expr. by deriv. or by comp.,<BR>of<BR>the lunar race:<BR>सोमवंशीयः (या, यं), Mah.;<BR>prince of high blood:<BR>कुलजः कुमारः, N. Ph.:<BR>of late:<BR>अधुना;<BR>of old:<BR>पुरा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

off
OFF:<BR>I Interj.: अपेहि: v. Away, begone.<BR>II Adj.: दूरवर्तिन् (f. नी) and sim. comp.s.<BR>III Adv.: दूरे<BR>or<BR>दूरतः: v. Far.<BR>IV With<BR>verbs or adverbs: v. The several verbs,<BR>etc. V. Prep.: expr. by circumlo.,<BR>to be o.<BR>the bed:<BR>शय्यां मुञ्चति। Ph.: (a) o. and on:<BR>सक्तासक्तम् (??); (b)<BR>o. -hand:<BR>विना समाधानेन<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

offal
OFFAL: उच्छिष्टम्: v. Refuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

offence
OFFENCE (subs.):<BR>I Crime., fault: q.v.:<BR>fault: अपराधः,<BR>punishing according to the nature<BR>of the o.:<BR>यथापराधदण्ड (f. ण्डा), R. i. 6.;<BR>shall not forgive any one for a second o.:<BR>द्वितीयमपराधं न कस्यचित् क्षमेत, V. s.;<BR>it is not<BR>master's o.:<BR>नास्ति प्रभवतोऽपराधः, V. ii.<BR>II<BR>Displeasure, resentment: q.v.: विरागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

offend
OFFEND: To sin, transgress: q.v.:<BR>(1)<BR>अपराध्यति (राध्, c. 4.), I have o. ed in this<BR>(matter): अहमेवात्रापराद्धा, V. ii.;<BR>(2) अपराधं<BR> करोति, M. n.<BR>II To pain: q. v.: पीडयति<BR>(पीड्, c. 10.).<BR>III To displease, affront:<BR>(1) अपराध्यति, you have o. ed Fāmadagnya:<BR>अपराद्धं त्वया जामदग्नस्य, Vi. iv.;<BR>(2) expr. with:<BR>विरक्त (f. क्ता) (= displeased)<BR>or<BR>कुपितः (ता,<BR> तं) (= enraged), and (my) master is o. ed:<BR>सेव्यो जनश्च कुपितः, V. ii.<BR>IV Cause to<BR>stumble: स्खलयति (c. of स्खल्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

offender
OFFENDER: अपराधिन् (f. नी): v. Also guilty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

offensive
OFFENSIVE:<BR>I Displeasing, disagreeable:<BR>दुष्ट (f. ष्टा),<BR>o. words:<BR>दुष्टवाक्यम्; o. smell:<BR>दुष्टगन्धः।<BR>II Injurious: पीडाकरः (री, रं) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR>III Assailant: आक्रामक- in<BR>comp. (?). Ph.:<BR>league o. and defensive:<BR>सङ्गतः<BR>or<BR>काञ्चनः सन्धिः, Ka. ix. 8.;<BR>to act on the<BR>o.:<BR>परामियोगं करोति (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

offensively
OFFENSIVELY:<BR>(1) सापराधम्;<BR>(2) सदोषम्;<BR>(3)<BR>दुष्टम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

offensiveness
OFFENSIVENESS:<BR>(1) दुष्टता;<BR>(2) पीडकता (= in-<BR>-juriousness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

offer
OFFER (v. t.):<BR>I To present as a sacrifice:<BR>(1) उपहारं करोति<BR>or<BR>ददाति,<BR>if you o. your own<BR>son to the goddess:<BR>यदि त्वमात्मनः पुत्रं भगवत्या<BR> उपहारीकरोषि, H. iii.;<BR>(2) उपढौकते (ढौक्,<BR>c. 1 (not religiously),<BR>o. ed this body to<BR>Garuḍa:<BR>गरूडाय स्वेदहमुपढौकितवान्, Vet. xiii.; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">Page485</a>]<BR>(3) उपनयति (नी, c. 1.);<BR>o. ed his body to the<BR>lion:<BR>हरये स्वदेहमुपानयत्, R. ii. 59.<BR>II To the<BR>mind: उदेति (इ, c. 2.): v. To occur,<BR>arise.<BR>III To propose: q.v.: उपन्यस्यति<BR>(अस्, c. 4 (?).<BR>IV To bid: दित्सति (desi.<BR>दा).<BR>V To make use of: करोति, o. violence:<BR>बलात्कारं करोति;<BR>o. prayers:<BR>स्तवं करोति। Ph.:<BR>to o. hand (in friendship): बाहुं प्रसारयति, Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

offer
OFFER (v.i.):<BR>I To arise, arrive: q.v.:<BR>उपनमति (नम्, c. 1.).<BR>II To volunteer,<BR>promise: q.v.<BR>III To attempt: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

offer
OFFER (subs.): प्रस्तावः (?), to reject an o.:<BR>प्रस्तावं प्रत्याख्याति (?). Ph.: to make an o. of:<BR>दित्सति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

offering
OFFERING (subs.): उपहारः,<BR>take this o.:<BR>गृह्यता-<BR>मुपहारः, H. iii.: v. Oblation, sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

offertory
OFFERTORY: उपहारस्तोत्रम् (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

office
OFFICE:<BR>I Duty, work: q.v.: कर्मन् (n.).<BR>II<BR>An employment: q.v.<BR>(1) कर्मन् (n.);<BR>(2) अधिकारः,<BR>discharged from an o.:<BR>आक्षिप्ता-<BR>धिकारः (रा, रं), Mu.;<BR>(3) पदम् (= position);<BR>(4) कार्यम्।<BR>III Place where business is<BR>transacted: no equiv.: कर्मशरणम्, कुर्मकुलम्,<BR>and sim. comp.s. may be used.<BR>IV For-<BR>-mulary: पद्धतिः। V. Of a house: बहिःशाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

officer
OFFICER:<BR>(1) कर्मचारिन् (m (used in Bengali);<BR>(2) अधिकृतः (= employee),<BR>civil o.:<BR>*पौराधि-<BR>कृतः;<BR>(3) नायकः (= leader).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

official
OFFICIAL (subs.): राजपुरूषः: v. Also officer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

official
OFFICIAL (adj.): by comp.,<BR>o. life:<BR>*अधिकृत-<BR>जीवितम्;<BR>o. dress:<BR>अधिकृतवेषः;<BR>o. duties:<BR>अधि-<BR>कृतकर्माणि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

officialness
OFFICIALNESS: in bad sense: अधिकृतरागः and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

officially
OFFICIALLY: *अधिकृतनियमानुसारेण and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

officiate
OFFICIATE: कर्म करोति,<BR>o. ing magistrate:<BR>*कर्मकर-<BR>दण्डनायकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

officious
OFFICIOUS:<BR>I Meddlesome: अनधिकारचर्चाशीलः<BR>(ला, लं) and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Kind: दक्षिण<BR>(f. णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

officiously
OFFICIOUSLY: अनधिकारचर्चां कृत्वा and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

officiousness
OFFICIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) अनधिकारचर्चा;<BR>(2) प्रागल्भ्यम्<BR>(= boldness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

offing
OFFING: perh. अपारसमुद्रः। Ph.:<BR>in the o.:<BR>विदूरे<BR> गभीरे जले (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

offscouring
OFFSCOURING: उच्छिष्टम्: v. Refuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

offset
OFFSET:<BR>I Lit.: प्ररोहः: v. Shoot.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>v. Set off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

offspring
OFFSPRING:<BR>(1) सन्तानः,<BR>desirous of o.:<BR>सन्तान-<BR>कामः (मा, मं), R.;<BR>(2) सन्ततिः,<BR>for o. of pure<BR>lineage:<BR>सन्ततिः शुद्धवंश्या हि, R. i. 69.;<BR>(3) प्रजा<BR>(f.),<BR>quieting the people like his own o.:<BR>प्रजाः<BR> प्रजाः स्वा इव सान्त्वयित्वा, Sa. v. 3.;<BR>(4) प्रसूतिः,<BR>destitute of o.:<BR>प्रसूतिविकलः (ला, लं), Sa. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oft
OFT, OFTEN:<BR>(1) बहुशः;<BR>(2) अनेकशः;<BR>(3) असकृत्;<BR>(4) अमीक्ष्णम्: v. Frequently. Ph.:<BR>(1) how o.:<BR>कतिशः;<BR>(2)<BR>as o. as..so o.:<BR>यावतो वारान्॥<BR> तावतो वारान्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ogle
OGLE:<BR>I Subs: साचिविलोकितम्: v. Glance.<BR>II Verb: साचि<BR>or<BR>तिर्यक् विलोकयति: v. To<BR>glance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ogre
OGRE: राक्षसः (f. सी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oh
OH: आः: v. O.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oil
OIL (subs.). तैलम्,<BR>sesamum o.:<BR>तिलतैलम्, Bha.:<BR>cooked in o.:<BR>तैलपक्व (f. क्वा), Bha.; o. -seeds:<BR>तिलादिवस्तूनि, Bha.,<BR>or<BR>-द्रव्याणि, or perh. तैल-<BR>बीजानि (comp. खसबीजानां तैलम्, Bha.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oil
OIL (v.): तैलेन अनक्ति (अञ्ज्, c. 7.), लेपयति<BR>(c. of लिप्), etc.: v. To besmear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oilcake
OILCAKE:<BR>(1) तैलकिट्टम्;<BR>(2) पिण्याकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oilcloth
OILCLOTH: *तैलरञ्जितवस्त्रम्, -आस्तरणम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oil-colour
OIL-COLOUR: *तैलरञ्जितरङ्गः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oil-man
OIL-MAN:<BR>(1) तैलिकः;<BR>(2) तैलिन् (m.);<BR>(3)<BR>तैलकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oil-mill
OIL-MILL, OIL-PRESS: तैलचक्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oil-painting
OIL-PAINTING: *तैलरञ्जितरङ्गेन चित्रितम् and sim.<BR>expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oily
OILY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) तैलमयः<BR>(यी, यं) (= consisting of oil)<BR>II Resembl-<BR>-ing oil: मसृण (f. णा).<BR>II Supple, com-<BR>-pliant: छन्दोऽनुवर्तिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ointment
OINTMENT: अञ्जनम्, अभि-: v. Unguent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

old
OLD:<BR>I Aged:<BR>(1) वृद्धः (द्धा, द्धं),<BR>an o. man's<BR>saying:<BR>वृद्धस्यवचनम्, H.;<BR>the o. woman:<BR>सा वृद्धा, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">Page486</a>]<BR>D.;<BR>I am now o.:<BR>इदानीमहं वृद्धः, H.;<BR>an o.<BR>ox:<BR>वृद्धोऽक्षः, Ku.;<BR>(2) स्थविरः (रा, रं);<BR>like<BR>an o. man:<BR>स्थविर इव, Mah.; the king is o.:<BR>स्थविरः स राजा, D.;<BR>an o. maid-servant:<BR>स्थविर-<BR>दासी, Ana.;<BR>(3) प्रवयस् (mfn.): v. Age.;<BR>(4) जरत् (f. ती) (= decayed),<BR>o. and infirm<BR>figure:<BR>जरती तनुः, Ki. xi. 7.<BR>II To expr.<BR>age: by comp. with -वर्ष (f. र्षा), -वत्सर<BR>(f. रा), etc.,<BR>thirteen years o.:<BR>त्रयोदशवर्ष<BR>(f. र्षा), D. viii.: v. Age, of Ph.:<BR>and how<BR>o. is (he):<BR>कियद्वा वयः, K.<BR>III. Not new:<BR>(1)<BR>पुराणः (णा, णं),<BR>our o. dear friend:<BR>पुराणप्रिय-<BR>सुहृदस्माकम्, Ana.;<BR>o. wine:<BR>पुराणमद्यम्, Bha.;<BR>(2) जीर्णः (र्णा, र्णं) (= o. and rotten),<BR>o. tem-<BR>ple:<BR>जीर्णदेवायतनम्, Au.;<BR>(3) चिरन्तनः (नी, नं)<BR>(of long standing),<BR>o. butter:<BR>चिरन्तनं नवनीतम्,<BR>Bha.:<BR>o. friend:<BR>चिरमित्रम्, H.; o. servant:<BR>चिरसेवकः, H.<BR>IV. Ancient: q.v.: पुराणः (णा, णं):<BR>o. sages:<BR>मुनयः पुराणाः, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

old
OLD, OF:<BR>(1) पुरा;<BR>(2) पूर्वकाले: v. Formerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

old age
OLD AGE:<BR>(1) वार्द्धक्यम्;<BR>(2) स्थविरम्;<BR>(3) वार्धकम्,<BR>R. i. 8.;<BR>(4) परिणामः (= advanced age), R.<BR>viii. II.;<BR>(5) जरा (= infirm old age), D. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

olden
OLDEN:<BR>(1) पुराण (f. णा),<BR>of o. custom:<BR>पुराणस्या-<BR>चारस्य, Vi. iii. 38.;<BR>(2) पुरातनः (नी, नं),<BR>o. necklace:<BR>पुरातनी माला, Ku.: v. Ancient,<BR>Ph.:<BR>o. times:<BR>पुराकालः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

old-fashioned
OLD-FASHIONED:<BR>(1) प्राचीनः (ना, नं): v.<BR>Ancient;<BR>(2) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oldness
OLDNESS:<BR>I Antiquity:<BR>(1) पुराणत्वम्, -ता;<BR>(2)<BR>पुरातनत्वम्, -ता।<BR>II Old age:<BR>(1) वृद्धत्वम्;<BR>(2)<BR>स्थविरता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oleaginous
OLEAGINOUS:<BR>(1) तैल- in comp.;<BR>(2) स्निग्ध<BR>(f. ग्धा) (= unctuous).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oleander
OLEANDER: a plant: करवीरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

olfactory
OLFACTORY: गन्धवाहिन् (f. नी) (?) (comp.<BR>वायुवहा शिरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

olibanum
OLIBANUM:<BR>(1) कुन्दुः;<BR>(2) कुन्दुरः (रूः), -कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oligarch
OLIGARCH: *मुख्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oligarchic
OLIGARCHIC, -AL: expr. with subs. or by<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oligarchy
OLIGARCHY: *मुख्यतन्रम्; मुख्यानां शासनम्, Ph.:<BR>o. of bishops:<BR>*कतिपयधर्मनायकशासनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

olio
OLIO: सङ्करः: v. Also medley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

olive
OLIVE:<BR>I The tree: जितः, -वृक्षः (?).<BR>II The<BR>fruit: जितम्, -फलम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

olympian
OLYMPIAN, OLYMPIC: *औलुम्प (f. म्पी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

omelet
OMELET: *अण्डसारः; अण्डसाध्यखाद्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

omen
OMEN (subs.):<BR>(1) निमित्तम्, good and bad o. s:<BR>शुभाशुभानि निमित्तानि, V. m.;<BR>(2) शकुनम्, -नः<BR>(properly from birds), सर्वशकुनसंग्रहः, V. m.<BR>86. 4.;<BR>(3) by adj. (when the meaning is<BR>clear),<BR>good o.:<BR>शुभम्, इष्टम्, शस्तम्, etc.: v. Also<BR>portent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

omen
OMEN (v.): कथयति: v. To betoken. Well-<BR>o. ed, ill-o. ed: v. Auspicious, inauspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ominous
OMINOUS: अनिष्टशंसिन् (f. नी) and sim. comp.s.:<BR>v. Inauspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ominously
OMINOUSLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

omission
OMISSION: वर्जनम् (?);<BR>(2) अतिक्रमः (?);<BR>(3)<BR>उत्क्षेपः (?): v. To omit, neglect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

omit
OMIT:<BR>(1) परित्यजति (त्यज्, c. 1 (= to leave<BR>out);<BR>(2) अतिक्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1 (= to pass<BR>by);<BR>(3) उत्क्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6 (= to throw<BR>out).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

omnibus
OMNIBUS: गोष्ठीयानम्, Mr. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

omnipotence
OMNIPOTENCE:<BR>(1) सर्वशक्तित्वम्;<BR>(2) सर्वशक्ति-<BR>मत्त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

omnipotent
OMNIPOTENT:<BR>(1) सर्वशक्ति (mfn.);<BR>(2) सर्व-<BR>शक्तिमत् (f. ती);<BR>(3) सर्वशक्तिसमन्वितः (ता, तं);<BR>(4) सर्वसमर्थः (र्था, र्थं);<BR>(5) समग्रशक्ति (mfn.);<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

omnipresence
OMNIPRESENCE:<BR>(1) सर्वगतत्वम्, S.;<BR>(2) सर्वत्र<BR> विद्यमानता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

omnipresent
OMNIPRESENT:<BR>(1) सर्वत्र विद्यमानः (ना, नं);<BR>(2)<BR>सर्वगतः (ता, तं);<BR>(3) सर्वव्यापिन् (f. नी) (= all-<BR>-pervading).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

omniscience
OMNISCIENCE:<BR>(1) सर्वज्ञता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2) सर्ववेदित्वम्<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

omniscient
OMNISCIENT:<BR>(1) सर्वज्ञः (ज्ञा, ज्ञं);<BR>(2) सर्वविद्<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(3) सर्ववेदिन् (f. नी); and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

omnivagant
OMNIVAGANT:<BR>(1) सर्वगः (गा, गं); सर्वत्रगः (गा, गं);<BR>(3) सर्वतोगामिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

omnivorous
OMNIVOROUS: सर्वभक्षः (क्षा, क्षं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

on
ON (prep.):<BR>I In contact with:<BR>(1) by loc.,<BR>lying on a grass bed:<BR>संविष्टः कुशशयने, R.;<BR>putting on his head:<BR>शिरस्यारोप्य; Vi.;<BR>to fall<BR>on the ground:<BR>भूमौ पतति, Mr.;<BR>(2) उपरि<BR>(= over: q.v.): (with gen.),<BR>to throw on<BR>Vairodhaka:<BR>वैरोधकस्योपरि निपातनाय, Mu. N. B.<BR>The ins. must be used after verbs of motion:<BR>to go on horse:<BR>अश्वेन गच्छति, S.;<BR>carrying on<BR>his shoulders:<BR>स्कन्धेनोदूह्य, D.; take me to (our)<BR>house on a fresh cloud:<BR>नय मां नवेन वसतिं पयोमुचा,<BR>V.<BR>II. = at, near:<BR>(1) by loc.,<BR>a cow-station<BR>on the Ganges:<BR>गङ्गायां घोषः, Kav.; on the north:<BR>उत्तरस्यां दिशि, Ku.;<BR>(2) by affix तस्,<BR>on the<BR>right:<BR>दक्षिणतः;<BR>on the left:<BR>वामतः; on the rear:<BR>पृष्ठतः;<BR>on both sides:<BR>उभयतः।<BR>III At the time<BR>of: by loc.,<BR>on the first of Āṣāḍha:<BR>आषाढस्य<BR> प्रथमदिवसे, Me.;<BR>on the following day:<BR>परस्मिन्नहनि<BR>(or commonly, परेद्युः).<BR>IV = after: q.v.:<BR>by loc. abs.,<BR>on her departure:<BR>गतायां तस्याम्, K.<BR>V. Denoting logical basis of connexion:<BR>expr. by ins.,<BR>on one condition:<BR>एकेनाभिसन्धिना,<BR>Sa.;<BR>on oath:<BR>शपथेन (?).<BR>VI Concerning:<BR>q.v.: expr. by comp., a treatise on spheres:<BR>गोलप्रबन्धः, Go.<BR>VII To denote various rela-<BR>-tions: v. The several verbs after which<BR>it is used. Miscell.:<BR>on high:<BR>उच्चैः;<BR>on a<BR>sudden:<BR>सपदि; on the wing: v. To fly;<BR>on<BR>the alert:<BR>सावधानः (ना, नं);<BR>on hand:<BR>हस्तगतः<BR>(ता, तं); the gods were on (the side of) Arjuna:<BR>देवा अर्जुनतोऽभवन्, S. k.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

on
ON (adv.):<BR>I After verbs: gen. not expr.<BR>II Attached to the body: अङ्गे। Ph.:<BR>and<BR>so on:<BR>इत्यादि (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

once
ONCE:<BR>I One time:<BR>(1) सकृत्,<BR>even o.:<BR>सकृदपि,<BR>K.;<BR>(2) एकवारम्, o. and again:<BR>(1) असकृत्;<BR>(2) वारं वारम्;<BR>(3) मुहुः।<BR>II At one time: कदा-<BR>चित्।<BR>III Formerly: q.v.: पुरा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

once
ONCE, AT:<BR>I. At the same time:<BR>(1) युगपत्;<BR>(2) समकालम्;<BR>(3) एकावसरम्;<BR>(4) समम्, Ki.<BR>Ph.:<BR>at o. perspicuous and deep:<BR>प्रसन्नगम्भीरः<BR>(रा, रं), Ki.;<BR>at o. terrific and pleasant:<BR>भीम-<BR>कान्तः (न्ता, न्तं), B.<BR>II. Immediately: q.v.:<BR>(1) सद्यः;<BR>(2) तत्क्षणात्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

on dit
ON DIT:<BR>(1) किल (enclitic); (2).. इति श्रूयते;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

one
ONE:<BR>I In gen. sense:<BR>(1) एकः (का, कं),<BR>not o. of you:<BR>भवत्सु नैकम्, N. xiv. 44.;<BR>in o.<BR>hollow:<BR>एकस्मिन् कोटरे, K.; one-horse carriage:<BR>एकाश्वयानम् and sim. comp.s. (?);<BR>(2) एकैकः<BR>(का, कं) (distributive),<BR>takes one Dinār every<BR>day:<BR>प्रतिदिनमेकैकं दीनारं गृह्णाति, P.;<BR>gave o.<BR>code to each:<BR>एकैकां संहितामैककस्मै ददौ, B. p.<BR>One<BR>of two:<BR>एकतरः (रा, रं),<BR>one of many:<BR>एक-<BR>तमः (मा, मत्),<BR>even by o. of which:<BR>येषामेकतमे-<BR>नापि, P. v. 3.<BR>One by one:<BR>एकैकशः, A. r.<BR>O.<BR>day:<BR>एकदा, K.<BR>At o. time:<BR>एकस्मिन् समये, L.<BR>II In contrast to other or another: एकः (का,<BR> कं), the o. brought the kings under subjection,<BR>the other<BR>.<BR>एको नृपतीन् वशमनयत् । अपर ।, R. viii.<BR>19.; one is grinding paints, another stringing<BR>flowers: एका वर्णकं पिनष्टि । अपरा सुमनसो गुम्फति,<BR>Mr.; their clans are fourteen; one is derived from<BR>the mind of Brahmā, another from the Vedas, ano-<BR>ther from the fire: तासां चतुर्दश कुलानि । एकं कमल-<BR>योनेर्मनसः समुत्पन्नम्, अन्यद्वेद्वेभ्यः संभूतम्, अन्यदग्ने रुद्भूतम्,<BR>K.; what will o. say of the other: किं भणति<BR> एक एकस्य, Sa.; on the o. hand . on the other:<BR>एकत्र । एकत्र (better अन्यत्र or अपरत्र), K.; on<BR>the o. hand<BR>. on the other:<BR>एकतः । अन्यतः, Vi.<BR>Ph.: at one time<BR>. at another time:<BR>कदाचित् ।<BR> कदाचित्, R.<BR>III. Denoting identity: expr.<BR>by तद्,<BR>but not the o.:<BR>न पुनः सः, Mr.;<BR>I am the<BR>o.:<BR>सोऽहमस्मि, D.: v. Same. Ph.:<BR>all the<BR>ethical systems are at one that innocence is a car-<BR>dinal virtue:<BR>धर्मशास्त्राणामहिंसा परमो धर्म इत्यत्रैकमत्यम्,<BR>H.;<BR>the great-minded are one in mind, in word,<BR>in action:<BR>मनस्येकं वचस्येकं कर्मण्येकं महात्मनाम्, H.<BR>i. 100.<BR>IV In connexion with rel. pro.:<BR>expr. by तद्,<BR>I do not see o. whom she has not<BR>embraced:<BR>न हि तं पश्यामि योऽनया नोपगूढः, K.<BR>V. Equiv. to some o., any o.: कश्चित्: v. Any,<BR>some.<BR>VI In an indefinite sense (= men)<BR>जनः<BR>or<BR>लोकः,<BR>one would say:<BR>जनो<BR>or<BR>लोको वदि-<BR>ष्यति। Ph.: (a)<BR>little ones:<BR>शिशवः: v. Child;<BR>(b)<BR>one-eyed:<BR>एकाक्ष (f. क्षी) or gen. काण<BR>(f. णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

one another
ONE ANOTHER, ONE .THE OTHER:<BR>(1) अन्योन्यः<BR> (न्या, न्यत्),<BR>why do you eat o. a.'s flesh:<BR>कस्माद्यू-<BR>यमन्योन्यं मांसं भक्षयथ, Kar.;<BR>placing o. a.'s<BR>attributes on o. a.:<BR>अन्योन्यस्मिन्नन्योन्यधर्मानध्यस्य,<BR>S.;<BR>(2) इतरेतरः, (रा, रत्)<BR>feeding o. a.:<BR>इतरेतरं<BR> भोजयतः, S. k.;<BR>without distinguishing one from<BR>the other:<BR>इतरेतराविवेकेन, S.;<BR>(3) परस्परः, (रा, रं)<BR>all spoke to o. a.:<BR>ऊचुः सर्वे परस्परम्, A. r.;<BR>one with the other:<BR>परस्परेण, R. vii. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oneness
ONENESS: एकता, S. p. b.: v. Unity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

onerous
ONEROUS:<BR>(1) गुरू (f. र्वी) (= heavy);<BR>(2)<BR>दुर्भरः (रा, रं) (= oppressive).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

onesided
ONESIDED: असमः (मा, मं) (= inequal): v.<BR>Partial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

onesidedness
ONESIDEDNESS: असमता (= inequality): v.<BR>Partiality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

onion
ONION:<BR>(1) पलाण्डुः;<BR>(2) सुकन्दः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

only
ONLY (adj.):<BR>(1) एक एव (एकैव, एकमेव),<BR>I was<BR>the o. daughter born of them:<BR>तयोरहमेकैवात्मजा<BR> समुत्पन्ना, K.;<BR>(2) एक- in comp., (my)<BR>old<BR>infirm mother who has an o. son in me:<BR>मदेकपुत्रा<BR> जननी जरातुरा, N.;<BR>(3) by adv.: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

only
ONLY (adv.):<BR>(1) केवलम्, (best equiv.),<BR>killing<BR>me is not o. killing an animal:<BR>न केवलं प्राणिवधो<BR> वधो मम, N.; (but) o. (he)<BR>does not bear trans-<BR>gression:<BR>केवलं न सहते विलङ्घनम्, Ki.;<BR>(2) by<BR>मात्र in comp.,<BR>black o. in colour:<BR>वर्णमात्रेण कृष्णः,<BR>Me.;<BR>(3) with एव giving emphasis,<BR>there is<BR>o. one means:<BR>एक एवोपायोऽस्ति, K. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

onomatopoeia
ONOMATOPŒIA: अव्यक्तानुकरणम्, S. k.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

onset
ONSET: अवस्कन्दः: v. Attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

onslaught
ONSLAUGHT: अभिघातः: v. Also invective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ontology
ONTOLOGY: *सत्त्वविज्ञानम्; सत्त्वविचारः; and sim.<BR>comps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

onward
ONWARD (adj.):<BR>(1) अग्रेसरः (री, रं);<BR>(2)<BR>वर्धिष्णु (mfn.) (= increasing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

onward
ONWARD,-s (adv.):<BR>(1) अग्रे;<BR>(2) अग्रतः;<BR>(3)<BR>पुरतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

onyx
ONYX: गोमेदभेदः; पीतरत्नम् (?), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ooze
OOZE (v. i.):<BR>(1) स्रवति, परि-, (स्रु, c. 1.).<BR>and<BR>the secret will o. out:<BR>रहस्यञ्च स्रवति, D. ii.;<BR>(2) क्षरति (क्षर्, c. 1.);<BR>(3) रीयते (री, c. 4.)<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ooze
OOZE (subs.): क्षरितम्: v. Also flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oozy
OOZY (adj.): सरसः (सा, सं): v. Moist, wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opacity
OPACITY: कलुषता<BR>or<BR>कालुष्यम्: v. Transparency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opal
OPAL: perh. पुलकः<BR>or<BR>विमलकः, V. m. 80. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opaque
OPAQUE: कलुषः (षा, षं), V. m. 82. 4.: v.<BR>Transparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ope
OPE (v.): v. Open (V.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

open
OPEN (v. t.):<BR>I To unclose:<BR>(1) वि-वृणोति,<BR> अपा-, (वृ, c. 5.),<BR>o. the back door:<BR>अपावृणु<BR> पक्षद्वारकम्, Mr.;<BR>to o. the mouth:<BR>आस्यं<BR> विवृणोति, V.p.;<BR>(2) उद्घाटयति (c. of घट्),<BR>(from some fastening, etc.), o. the door:<BR>उद्घाटय द्वारम्, Mr.;<BR>(3) उन्मोचयति (मुच्, c. 10.)<BR>(= to free, as from a cover)<BR>o. ed and read<BR>it:<BR>तदुन्मुच्य पपाठ, K.;<BR>(4) उन्मीलयति (c. of<BR>मील्) (of the eyes);<BR>(5) व्यादत्ते, -ददाति (दा,<BR>c. 2 (to open wide, as the mouth);<BR>(6)<BR>प्रसारयति (c. of सृ) (= to stretch, put forth,<BR>as the hands).<BR>II To disclose, reveal:<BR>q.v.: विवृणोति।<BR>III To explain, expound:<BR>q.v.: विवृणोति।<BR>IV Of roads, etc.:<BR>(1)<BR>करोति: v. To make;<BR>(2) शोधयति (c. of<BR>शुध्) (= to clear), कुर्वन्तः शोधयन्तश्च पन्थानं गहने<BR> वने, Ram. V. To begin: q.v.: प्रस्तौति (स्तु,<BR>c. 2.).<BR>VI To lance: विध्यति (व्यध्, c. 4.),<BR>Sr.<BR>VII Of the bowels: रेचयति (रिच्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

open
OPEN (v. i.):<BR>I To unclose:<BR>(1) विवृतः (ता,<BR> तं) भवति;<BR>(2) by pass.<BR>II To appear:<BR>q.v.: आविर्भवति।<BR>III Of flowers, etc.:<BR>उन्मीलति (मील्, c. 1.).<BR>IV To begin:<BR>q.v.: आरभते (रम्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

open up
OPEN UP:<BR>(1) विवृणोति:<BR>(2) प्रकटीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

open
OPEN (adj.):<BR>I Unclosed:<BR>(1) विवृतः, अनावृतः<BR>or<BR>अपावृतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2) उद्घाटितः (ता, तं);<BR>(3) उन्मीलितः (ता, तं);<BR>(4) व्यात्त (f. त्ता);<BR>(5)<BR>उन्मुक्त (f. क्ता);<BR>(6) प्रसारितः (ता, तं),<BR>with o.<BR>arms:<BR>प्रसारितभुजाभ्याम्<BR>or<BR>-भुजैः (for many): for<BR>dif.: v. To open.<BR>II Frank, artless: q.v.:<BR>विवृतः (ता, तं),<BR>to lay o.:<BR>विवृणोति, Ki. xiv. 12.<BR>III Public, exposed: प्रकाशः (शा, शं), what !<BR>I have come out into o. (field): कथं, प्रकाशं निर्ग-<BR>तोऽस्मि, Sa. iii.;<BR>made woods o.:<BR>विपिनानि प्रका- [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">Page489</a>]<BR>-शानि चकार, R. iv. 31.: v. Also clear.<BR>IV<BR>Fig., accessible:<BR>the post is o. to all:<BR>सर्वेषु<BR> मुक्तं पदम्<BR>or<BR>सर्वैरासाद्यं कर्म.: v. Not settled: न<BR> निर्णीतः (ता, तं), etc.: v. To decide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

open-eyed
OPEN-EYED: विवृताक्ष (f. क्षी) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

open-handed
OPEN-HANDED:<BR>(1) मुक्तहस्तः (स्ता, स्तं);<BR>(2)<BR>मुक्तकरः (रा, रं), K. s. 120. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

open-hearted
OPEN-HEARTED: विवृतहृदयः (या, यं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.: v. Also frank, sincere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opening
OPENING (adj.): Ph.:<BR>o. medicine:<BR>रेचकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opening
OPENING (subs.):<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) उद्घाटनम्;<BR>(2) उन्मीलनम्; etc.: v. To open.<BR>II An<BR>aperture: q.v.: छिद्रम्।<BR>III Beginning:<BR>q.v.: आरम्भः, सम्-,<BR>o. of a book:<BR>ग्रन्थारम्भः,<BR>Kav.<BR>IV Appearance: q.v.: आविर्मावः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

openly
OPENLY:<BR>(1) प्रकाशम्;<BR>(2) प्रकटम्;<BR>(3) स्फुटम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

openness
OPENNESS:<BR>(1) विवृतिः;<BR>(2) प्रकाशता; etc.: v.<BR>Open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opera
OPERA: सङ्गीतविशेषः; *कार्मणम्: v. Also music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

operate
OPERATE:<BR>I To act, influence:<BR>II In sur-<BR>-gery:<BR>(1) शस्त्रम् अवचारयति (c. of चर्), Sr.;<BR>(2) कर्म करोति (when the sense is clear),<BR>मूढगर्मोदरार्शोऽश्मरीभगन्दरमुखरोगेष्वभुक्तवतः कर्म कुर्वीत,<BR>Sr.<BR>III In medicine: expr. with गुणः:<BR>Efficacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

operation
OPERATION:<BR>I Action, exertion: व्यापारः।<BR>II Military or naval: कर्मन् (n.).<BR>III<BR>Mathematical: कर्मन् (n.).<BR>IV Surgical:<BR>(1) कर्मन् (n.) or precisely: शस्त्रकर्म;<BR>(2) शस्त्रा-<BR>वचारः। V. Effect: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

operative
OPERATIVE (adj.): कर्मनिपुण (f. णा): v. Also<BR>efficacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

operative
OPERATIVE (subs.): कर्मकरः: v. Labourer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

operator
OPERATOR: in surgery:<BR>a skilful o.:<BR>शस्त्रावचार-<BR>कुशलः (ला, लं) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

operose
OPEROSE: श्रमसाध्य (f. ध्या) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ophthalmia
OPHTHALMIA, OPHTHALMY:<BR>(1) अर्बुद (mn.);<BR>(2) अभिमन्थः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opiate
OPIATE: निद्राजनकमौषधम् and sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opine
OPINE: मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.): v. To think.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opiniated
OPINIATED, OPINIATIVE: v. Opinionated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opinion
OPINION:<BR>I In gen.: मतम्,<BR>in my o. the Vaiśe-<BR>ṣika doctrine is good:<BR>वैशेषिकं चारू मतं मतं मे,<BR>N. xxii. 36.<BR>II Estimation: expr. with मतः<BR>(ता, तं), अभि-, win good o. of your husband:<BR>भतर्बहुमता भव, Sa. iv.<BR>III Honour, fame:<BR>q.v.: मानः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opinionate
OPINIONATE, -D: स्वमतबद्ध (f. द्धा) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opium
OPIUM:<BR>(1) अहिफेनम्:<BR>(2) आफूकम्, “आफूकं<BR> शोषणं ग्राहि”, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opossum
OPOSSUM: *औपसमः; शावककोषभृज्जन्तुविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opponent
OPPONENT: प्रतिद्वन्द्विन् (mfn.): v. Also adver-<BR>-sary, enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opportune
OPPORTUNE:<BR>I Timely:<BR>(1) समयोचितः (ता,<BR> तं);<BR>(2) प्राप्तकालः (ला, लं); and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Fig., becoming: q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opportunely
OPPORTUNELY:<BR>(1) यथावसरम्;<BR>(2) यथासमयम्;<BR>(3) काले: v. Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opportuneness
OPPORTUNENESS:<BR>(1) औचित्यम् (= fitness);<BR>(2)<BR>प्राप्तकालता (of time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opportunity
OPPORTUNITY: अवसरः, kings are to be approa-<BR>ched (when) o. ies. (occur): अवसरोपसर्पणीया राजानः,<BR>Sa. v.;<BR>to give an o.:<BR>अवसरप्रदानाय, Sr.;<BR>this<BR>is the o. to show myself:<BR>अवसरोऽयमात्मानं दर्शयितुम्,<BR>Sa.: looking up for an o. for (discharging)<BR>an<BR>arrow:<BR>बाणावसरं प्रतीक्ष्य, Ku. iii. 64.: v.<BR>Also time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oppose
OPPOSE (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) संमुखयति;<BR>(2) संमुखी-<BR>करोति।<BR>II In gen.:<BR>(1) निरूणद्धि (रूध्, c. 7.)<BR>(= to check),<BR>to o. his progress:<BR>तत्प्रसरं<BR> निरोद्धुम्, Vi. iv. 6.;<BR>(2) प्रतिकूलयति (nomi.)<BR>(= to act adversely), and it (passion)<BR>cannot<BR>be o.d by any one:<BR>न चायं केनापि प्रतिकूलयितुं<BR> शक्यते, K.;<BR>(3) प्रतिक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.) (= to<BR>refute: as of opinion), D. s.; प्रतियोधयति<BR>(c. of युध्) (in fighting), D.;<BR>(4) निवारयति<BR>(वृ, c. 10 (= to prevent).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oppose
OPPOSE (v. i.): in controversies: प्रत्यवतिष्ठते<BR>(स्था, c. 1.),<BR>others o. to this:<BR>अत्रापरे प्रत्यव-<BR>तिष्ठन्ते, S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opposed
OPPOSED:<BR>(1) विरूद्ध (f. द्धा) (o. to practices,<BR>moral, etc.), M. viii. 46.; Ki. xiv. 25.;<BR>(2) प्रतिकूलः (ला, लं) (= adverse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opposite
OPPOSITE (adj.):<BR>I Facing:<BR>(1) संमुख (f.<BR>खा);<BR>(2) संमुखीनः (ना, नं).<BR>II Adverse, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">Page490</a>]<BR>contrary: q.v.:<BR>(1) विरूद्ध (f. द्धा),<BR>of o.<BR>natures like darkness and light:<BR>तमःप्रकाशवद्विरूद्ध-<BR>स्वभावयोः, S.;<BR>(2) विरोधिन् (f. नी), of o. views:<BR>विरोधिवचस् (mfn.), Si. ii. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opposite
OPPOSITE (subs.):<BR>I An enemy: q. v.: विरो-<BR>धिन् (f. नी).<BR>II A contrary: q.v.: विपरीतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opposition
OPPOSITION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) विरोधः, -नम्, etc.;<BR>(2) better by verb: v. To oppose.<BR>II<BR>Obstacle: q.v.: बाधा। Ph.: without o.:<BR>अविरोधेन।<BR>III Contrariety, repugnance:<BR>q.v.: विरोधः। Ph.:<BR>in o. to:<BR>विरूद्धम्: v. Aga-<BR>-inst.<BR>IV Adverse party: विरूद्धपक्षः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oppress
OPPRESS:<BR>(1) पीडयति, प्र-, उत्-, नि-, सं-, उप-<BR>(पीड्, c. 10.),<BR>unjustly o. es men:<BR>अन्यायतः पीडयति<BR> मानवान्, Ram. i. 14. 17.;<BR>was o. ed with the<BR>enjoined price of (this) daughter:<BR>पीडितो दुहितृ-<BR>शुल्कसंस्थया, R. xi. 38.;<BR>(2) बाधते<BR>or<BR>बाधयति, प्र-,<BR> परि-, (बाध्, c.<BR>I and c. 10.),<BR>he o. es the three<BR>worlds:<BR>स बाधयति लोकांस्त्रीन्, Ram.;<BR>(3) उपप्लवते<BR>(प्ल, c. 1 (rare), Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oppression
OPPRESSION:<BR>I The act or that which op-<BR>-presses:<BR>(1) पीडनम्, उत्-, प्र-, o. of people:<BR>प्रजापीडनम्;<BR>(2) उपद्रवः;<BR>(3) उपप्लवः (rare).<BR>II Misery: q.v.: पीडा।<BR>III A sense of<BR>weight: भारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oppressive
OPPRESSIVE:<BR>I Tyrannical:<BR>(1) पीडक (f.<BR>डिका), उत्-, प्र-;<BR>(2) बाधक (f. धिका);<BR>(3)<BR>दारूण (f. णा) (= fierce).<BR>II Heavy, over-<BR>-powering: दुर्भरः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oppressively
OPPRESSIVELY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oppressiveness
OPPRESSIVENESS:<BR>(1) पीडकता etc. (?);<BR>(2)<BR>better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oppressor
OPPRESSOR:<BR>(1) प्रजापीडकः;<BR>(2) लोकबाधकः;<BR>etc.: v. To oppress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opprobrious
OPPROBRIOUS: कुत्सितः (ता, तं): v. Also dis-<BR>-graceful, blameable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opprobriously
OPPROBRIOUSLY: कृत्सितम्: v. Also disgrace-<BR>-fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opprobrium
OPPROBRIUM: कृत्सा: v. Reproach, blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oppugn
OPPUGN (v.): v. To oppose, resist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

optative
OPTATIVE:<BR>o. mood:<BR>आशंसावाचिनी क्रिया (after<BR>S. k.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

optician
OPTICIAN: *आलोकयन्त्रिकः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

optic
OPTIC, -AL: by comp.,<BR>o. angle:<BR>*द्य्क्कोणः;<BR>o.<BR>nerve:<BR>आलोकवाहिनी शिरा (after शब्दवाहिनी, Sr.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

optics
OPTICS: तेजोविज्ञानम्; प्रकाशविज्ञानम्; आलोकविज्ञानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

option
OPTION: अभिरुचिः (?),<BR>is there any o. in the<BR>matter:<BR>किमत्र कस्यचित् स्वरुचिः, Vi. iv.: v.<BR>Choice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

optional
OPTIONAL, -LY: by expr. with subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opulence
OPULENCE:<BR>(1) सम्-ऋद्धिः;<BR>(2) ऐश्वर्यम्;<BR>(3)<BR>विभवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

opulent
OPULENT:<BR>(1) समृद्धिशालिन् (f. नी): v. Rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

or
OR:<BR>I In gen.: वा, whether child or pupil:<BR>शिशुर्वा शिष्या वा, U. iv. 11.;<BR>whether God is<BR>spoken of in this passage or not:<BR>किं ब्रह्मास्मिन्<BR> वाक्येऽभिधीयते न वेति, S. ii. 15.;<BR>from fear of<BR>the king or of thieves:<BR>राजभयाच्चौरमयाद्वा, Mr.<BR>iii.;<BR>or else:<BR>किं वा, Vi. vi. 21. (when=other-<BR>-wise: नोचेत्, H.).<BR>II In interrogation<BR>direct or implied:<BR>is it a dream, an illusion,<BR>or delusion of my mind:<BR>स्वप्नो नु माया नु मतिभ्रमो<BR> नु, Sa.; is my strength gone or am I another:<BR>ध्वस्तं नु मे वीर्यमुताहमन्यः, Ki.;<BR>or is (she) going<BR>to live with hinds:<BR>आहो निवत्स्यति समं हरिणाङ्ग-<BR>नाभिः, Sa.;<BR>shall I kill him, or is he dream-<BR>ing:<BR>किं व्यापादयाम्युतोत्स्वप्नायते, Mr. iii.;<BR>I do<BR>not know whether this is becoming of (your)<BR>bark or (your) matted hair, whether it befits<BR>(your) penances or it is a part of (your) religi-<BR>ous observances:<BR>न जाने किमिदं वल्कलानां सदृशमु-<BR>ताहो जटानां समुचितं, किं तपसोऽनुरूपमाहोस्विद्धर्मकर्मा-<BR>पदेशाङ्गमिदम्, K. (N. B. नु is interro. and not<BR>used in such cases).<BR>III Beginning a<BR>sentence: अथवा, or to injure tender things:<BR>अथवा मृदु वस्तु हिंसितुम्, R. viii. 45.<BR>IV In defi-<BR>-nitions or explanations: by च or not expr.,<BR>is called a fratricide or a brother-killer:<BR>भ्रातृहा<BR> भ्रातृघाती चाभिधीयते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oracle
ORACLE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) दैववाणी;<BR>(2) दैवी वाक्;<BR>(3) आकाशभवा सरस्वती (from heaven); and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR>II A prophet: q. v.: भविष्य-<BR>द्वक्ता (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oracular
ORACULAR:<BR>(1) expr. with subs.,<BR>his words<BR>are o.:<BR>*दैववाणीसन्निमस्तस्य ब्याहारः;<BR>(2) प्रामाणिकः<BR>(की, कं) (= authoritative).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oracularly
ORACULARLY: expr. with subs. or by<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oral
ORAL:<BR>(1) वाचिकः (की, कं) (= verbal), I now<BR>wish to know his o. (communication): वाचिक-<BR>मिदानीं श्रोतुमिच्छामि, Mu. v.;<BR>(2) मौखिकः<BR>(की, कं) (lit. but ambiguous).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orally
ORALLY: वाचा (= in words) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orange
ORANGE:<BR>I The fruit:<BR>(1) नागरङ्गम्;<BR>(2) मधु-<BR>जम्बीरम् (use m. for the tree).<BR>II The colour:<BR>रक्तपीतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orangery
ORANGERY: नागरङ्गवाटिका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orang-outang
ORANG-OUTANG: वनमानुषः (?), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oration
ORATION: वक्तृता (used in Bengali); प्रौढव्याहारः<BR>(?); सरस्वतीनिस्यन्दः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orator
ORATOR:<BR>(1) वाक्यकोविदः (?);<BR>(2) वक्तृ (m.)<BR>(= speaker).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oratorical
ORATORICAL: by comp., or talents: वक्तृता-<BR>शक्तिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oratorio
ORATORIO: *गीतसन्दर्भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oratory
ORATORY:<BR>I The art:<BR>(1) वाग्मिता (?);<BR>(2)<BR>वाक्पाटवम् (?).<BR>II A place of prayer:<BR>*भजनालयम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orb
ORB (subs.): मण्डलम्: v. Circle, disk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orb
ORB (v.):<BR>I Lit.: मण्डलीकरोति।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>मण्डयति (= to adorn: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orbed
ORBED (adj.): मण्डलिन् (f. नी): v. Circular,<BR>round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orbit
ORBIT: कक्षा,<BR>o. of a planet:<BR>ग्रहकक्षा, Su. xii. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orchard
ORCHARD: फलवाटिका (?),<BR>mango-o.:<BR>आम्रवाटिका,<BR> -वनम् and so on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orchestra
ORCHESTRA:<BR>I Part of a theatre: वादित्रभूमिः<BR>(??).<BR>II The body of musical performers:<BR>वादित्रवादकाः (m. pl (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orchid
ORCHID: *कोषलता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ordain
ORDAIN:<BR>(1) नियोजयति (युज् c. 10.): v. To<BR>employ;<BR>(2) आदिशति (दिश्, c. 6.): v. To<BR>order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ordeal
ORDEAL:<BR>I Lit.: here the o. s for clearing (one-<BR>self)<BR>are by balance, by fire, by water, by poison,<BR>by drinking divine water:<BR>तुलाग्नवापो विषं कोषो<BR> दिव्यानीह विशुद्धये, Y. ii. 97.; to accept an o.:<BR>दिव्यं करोति, V. s.<BR>II Fig., severe trial:<BR>expr. with व्यसनम्<BR>or<BR>विपद् (= calamity: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

order
ORDER (subs.):<BR>I Disposition, arrangement:<BR>q. v.: (I) क्रमः (of succession),<BR>without devia-<BR>ting from o.:<BR>अनुज्फितक्रमः, Ku.; in regular o.:<BR>यथाक्रमम्;<BR>(2) परिपाटी, M. n. Ph.: o. of battle:<BR>व्यूहः;<BR>without o.:<BR>उच्छृङ्गलम्।<BR>II Regularity:<BR>q. v.: परिपाटी। Ph.: in o. (as of the organs:) प्रकृतिस्थ<BR>(f. स्था).<BR>III Established usage:<BR>(1) स्थितिः,<BR>observer of o.:<BR>स्भितेरभेत्ता, R. iii. 27.<BR>or<BR>अभिन्न-<BR>स्थितिः, Sa. v. 11.;<BR>(2) मर्यादा, M. n.<BR>IV A<BR>command, direction:<BR>(1) आज्ञा,<BR>sending me<BR>o. s:<BR>प्रेषयन्मह्यमाज्ञाम्, Mu. ii.:<BR>received his o. with<BR>pleasure:<BR>तदाज्ञां मुदितोऽग्रहीत्, R. xii. 7.;<BR>to<BR>give an o.:<BR>आज्ञां ददाति, Ku.;<BR>(2) आदेशः or<BR>निदेशः,<BR>getting their master's o.:<BR>भर्तुरादेशं समवाप्य,<BR>Ki. vi. 46.; I wish to know (his)<BR>o.:<BR>निदेशं<BR> ज्ञातुमिच्छामि, Mah.;<BR>(3) नियोगः, (we) have<BR>carried out (our)<BR>preceptor's o.:<BR>अनुष्ठितो गुरूनियोगः,<BR>Sa.;<BR>(4) शासनम्,<BR>to stand by an o.:<BR>शासने तिष्ठति,<BR>R. xi. 65.<BR>V For paying money: शासनम्,<BR> निदेशः, etc. may be used.<BR>VI Rank, class:<BR>श्रेणिः (णी). Ph.:<BR>the lower o. s:<BR>प्राकृताः or<BR>पृथग्जनाः (m. pl.).<BR>VII Of religious com-<BR>-munities: सम्प्रदायः।<BR>VIII For constructing<BR>houses: विधानम् (?).<BR>IX In pl.,<BR>to take (holy)<BR>o. s.:<BR>*आचार्यक्षेत्रं प्रविशति<BR>or<BR>आचार्यत्वं परिगृह्नाति।<BR>Ph.: (a) in o. to read, etc. (i. e. for the pur-<BR>-pose of): अध्ययनार्थम्<BR>or<BR>अध्ययनाय: v. For;<BR>(b)<BR>o. of the day:<BR>दैनिकक्रमः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

order
ORDER (v.):<BR>I To arrange, dispose: q. v.:<BR>परिकल्पयति (कॢप्, c. 10.).<BR>II To command,<BR>direct:<BR>(2) आ-दिशति, नि-, समा-, (दिश्, c. 6.),<BR>I have been o. ed by the Princess of Benares:<BR>आदिष्टोऽस्मि काशिराजपुत्र्या, V. iii.;<BR>(2) आज्ञापयति,<BR> सम्-, (c. of ज्ञा),<BR>as your Majesty o. s.:<BR>यदाज्ञा-<BR>पयति देवः, Mah.;<BR>o. the forces to eradicate (his)<BR>resolution:<BR>संकल्पसमुन्मूलनाय दण्डचक्रमाज्ञापय, Mah.<BR>i.;<BR>(3) शास्ति (शास्, c. 2 (ambiguous).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orderly
ORDERLY (subs.): *आज्ञावाहकः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orderly
ORDERLY (adj.):<BR>I Well-arranged, well-<BR>-regulated: -परिपाटी in comp.: v. Also to<BR>arrange, methodical.<BR>II Well-conducted:<BR>शिष्ट (f. ष्टा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ordinal
ORDINAL: Ph.:<BR>o. number:<BR>पूरणी सङ्ख्या, Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ordinance
ORDINANCE:<BR>I An injunction:<BR>(1) नियोगः;<BR>(2) शासनम् (= edict).<BR>II Religious: विधिः:<BR>v. Ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ordinarily
ORDINARILY:<BR>I Commonly: प्रायेण: v.<BR>Usually, generally.<BR>II In an ordinary<BR>degree: expr. by circumlo.,<BR>“more than o.<BR>severe”:<BR>*यथा प्रायशो भवति तस्मादधिकतीव्र (f. व्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ordinary
ORDINARY:<BR>I Customary, regular: प्रचलः<BR>(ला, लं)<BR>or<BR>प्रचलितः (ता, तं).<BR>II Common,<BR>inferior: q. v.: सामान्य (f. न्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ordination
ORDINATION: नियोगः, वि-: v. To appoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ordnance
ORDNANCE: *कामानानि (n. pl.): v. Artillery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ordure
ORDURE (subs.):<BR>(1) विष्ठा;<BR>(2) पुरीषम्;<BR>(3)<BR>शकृत्;<BR>(4) गूथम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ore
ORE:<BR>I A metal: धातुः।<BR>II In mining:<BR>आकरः (?). Ph.:<BR>common pyritic iron o.:<BR>स्वर्ण-<BR>माक्षिकम्, Wilson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oread
OREAD: गिरिदेवता and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

organ
ORGAN:<BR>I A medium:<BR>(1) इन्द्रियम् (of men),<BR>the o. of taste:<BR>रसनेन्द्रियम्, D.;<BR>(2) करणम्,<BR>there<BR>are three internal and ten external o. s:<BR>अन्तः-<BR>करणत्रयं दश बाह्यकरणानि, S. p. b. Ph.:<BR>the<BR>male o.:<BR>लिङ्गम्;<BR>the female o.:<BR>योनिः।<BR>II<BR>Fig.: द्वारम्।<BR>III A musical instrument:<BR>*आर्गणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

organic
ORGANIC: by comp.,<BR>o. pleasure:<BR>इन्द्रियसुखम्।<BR>Ph.:<BR>o. substance:<BR>*व्यूढपदार्थः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

organically
ORGANICALLY:<BR>(1) व्यूढ- in comp. (?);<BR>(2)<BR>by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

organism
ORGANISM:<BR>I Lit.: *करणसन्निवेशः।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>यन्नम् (= machine: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

organist
ORGANIST: *आर्गणवादकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

organisation
ORGANISATION:<BR>I The act: परिकल्पना (?).<BR>II =organism: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

organize
ORGANIZE: परिकल्पयति (कॢप्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>arrange, devise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orgies
ORGIES: प्रमोदः (= amusement),<BR>o. of imps in<BR>the first part of night:<BR>प्रादोषिकः प्रमोदः पिशाचाङ्ग-<BR>नानाम्, Ma. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orient
ORIENT:<BR>I Rising: उद्यत् (f. ती): v. To<BR>rise.<BR>II Eastern: q. v.: प्राच्य (f. च्या).<BR>III Bright, shining: उज्ज्वलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oriental
ORIENTAL:<BR>(1) प्राच्य (f. च्या);<BR>(2) पौरस्त्य (f.<BR>स्त्या);<BR>(3) पूर्वदेश्य (f. श्या) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orifice
ORIFICE:<BR>(1) मुखम्;<BR>(2) छिद्रम् (= hole, when<BR>there are several o. s.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

origin
ORIGIN: मूलम्, the o. of all vices like harmfulness:<BR>मूलं दोषस्य हिंसादेः, Ki. xi. 20.;<BR>of good o.:<BR>भौल<BR>(f. ली), R.; wealth always has its o. in piety:<BR>धर्ममूलः सदैवार्थः, Mah. s. 123. 4.: v. Also<BR>beginning, source.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

original
ORIGINAL (adj.):<BR>I Primitive: q. v.: आदिमः<BR>(मा, मं).<BR>II Primary: मूल- in comp., o.<BR>side (of a High Court): *मूलविमागः।<BR>II Not<BR>translated or borrowed: expr. with: मूलम्।<BR>IV Having new ideas, etc.: perh. अनन्य-<BR>साधारण (f. णी): v. Also originality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

original
ORIGINAL (subs.): Origin: q. v.<BR>II An o.<BR>work: मूलम्,<BR>this is just like the o.:<BR>यथा<BR> मूलं तथैवैतत्, K. s. 1. 10.<BR>III First copy:<BR>मूलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

originality
ORIGINALITY: ? अपूर्वकल्पनाशक्तिः। (in invent-<BR>-ing); ? अपूर्वरचनाशक्तिः (in writing), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

originally
ORIGINALLY:<BR>I At first: आदौ।<BR>II From the<BR>origin: मूलात्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

originate
ORIGINATE: expr. by subs.: v. Also to<BR>create, begin, spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

origination
ORIGINATION: expr. with प्रभवः: v. Origin,<BR>beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

originator
ORIGINATOR:<BR>(1) मूलम् (= origin: q. v.);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रभवः (= source: q. v.);<BR>(3) स्रष्टृ (m.) (= crea-<BR>-tor: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oriole
ORIOLE: पक्षिविशेषः: v. Thrush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orion
ORION: a constellation:<BR>(1) मृगशिरस् (m.);<BR>(2) मृगशीर्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orison
ORISON: v. Prayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ornament
ORNAMENT (subs.):<BR>(1) अलङ्कारः,<BR>an o. for<BR>horses:<BR>अश्वालङ्कारः, K.; who (Urvaśī)<BR>is the o.<BR>of heaven:<BR>यालङ्कारः स्वर्गस्य, V. i.;<BR>now speaks<BR>of o. s. of language:<BR>सम्प्रति शब्दालङ्कारानाह, Kav.<BR>ix.;<BR>(2) भूषणम्, वि-, adorned with various o s:<BR>नानाविभूषणविभूषितः (ता, तं), J.;<BR>there is here a city<BR>named Ujjayinī-the o. of earth:<BR>अस्तीहोज्जयिनी<BR> नाम नगरी भूषणं भुवः, K. s. xi. 31.;<BR>(3) आमरणम्<BR>(lit.),<BR>she also taking off all other o. s:<BR>अवमुच्य<BR> तथान्यानि सर्वाण्याभरणानि सा, Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ornament
ORNAMENT: (v.): अलङ्करोति (कृ, c. 8.): v. To<BR>adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ornamental
ORNAMENTAL:<BR>(1) expr. with भूषणम्, वि-,<BR>(2)<BR>शोभावहः (हा, हं) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ornamentally
ORNAMENTALLY:<BR>(1) अलङ्कर्तुम्;<BR>(2) मण्डनार्थम्;<BR>(3) शोभाविवृद्धये; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ornamentation
ORNAMENTATION:<BR>(1) अलङ्क्रिया;<BR>(2) भूषा;<BR>(3)<BR>मण्डनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ornate
ORNATE:<BR>(1) कान्तिमत् (f. ती);<BR>(2) विचित्र<BR>(f. त्रा) (= picturesque).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ornateness
ORNATENESS: of language:<BR>(1) कान्तिः, Kav.;<BR>(2) कान्तिमत्ता;<BR>(3) वैचित्र्यम् (picturesqueness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ornithological
ORNITHOLOGICAL: पक्षिशास्त्रविषयकः (का, कं), etc.<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ornithologist
ORNITHOLOGIST: पक्षिशास्त्रविद् and sim. comp.s.<BR>(after गजशास्त्रविद्, M. n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ornithology
ORNITHOLOGY: पक्षिशास्त्रम्; पक्षिविज्ञानम्; etc. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orphan
ORPHAN:<BR>(1) अनाथः (था, थं) (= masterless),<BR>o. asylum:<BR>*अनाथाश्रमः;<BR>(2) पितृमातृविवर्जितः<BR>(ता, तं), Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orphanage
ORPHANAGE, ORPHANHOOD:<BR>(1) अनाथता;<BR>(2)<BR>पितृमातृविहीनता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orpiment
ORPIMENT:<BR>(1) हरितालम् (= yellow o.);<BR>(2) रक्त-<BR>धातुः (= red o.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orrery
ORRERY: *ग्रहगोलम्, -यन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orthodox
ORTHODOX: स्वधर्मपरायण (f. णा) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (in good sense): v. Also bigotted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orthodoxy
ORTHODOXY: स्वधर्मपरायणता (of men); सत्यता<BR>(of faith etc.): v. Also bigotry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orthographical
ORTHOGRAPHICAL: *वर्णगतः (ता, तं); by<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

orthography
ORTHOGRAPHY: वर्णविज्ञानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ortolan
ORTOLAN: a bird: *औद्यानकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oscillate
OSCILLATE: दोलायते (nomi (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oscillation
OSCILLATION: दोलायितम् (?): परिस्पन्दः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

osier
OSIER: no equiv.: *औषरः (use n. for twig.),<BR>o. cage:<BR>औषरपिञ्जरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

osprey
OSPREY:<BR>(1) कुररः (f. री), R. xiv. 68.;<BR>(2)<BR>उत्क्रोशः (f. शी -वधूः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

osseous
OSSEOUS: अस्थिमयः (यी, यं) and sim. comp.s., S. p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ossification
OSSIFICATION: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ossify
OSSIFY: अस्थित्वम् एति (इ, c. 2.), व्रजति (व्रज्, c. 1.),<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ostensible
OSTENSIBLE: expr. by adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ostensibly
OSTENSIBLY:<BR>(1) प्रकाशम्;<BR>(2) प्रकाशतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ostensive
OSTENSIVE, OSTENSIVELY: v. Ostensible,<BR>ostensibly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ostentation
OSTENTATION:<BR>(1) प्रदर्शनम् (= display);<BR>(2)<BR>आडम्बरः (= pomp).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ostentatious
OSTENTATIOUS: आडम्बरप्रियः (या, यं) (?): v. Also<BR>boastful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ostentatiously
OSTENTATIOUSLY:<BR>(1) साडम्बरम् (?);<BR>(2) दम्भपूर्वम्<BR>(?); v. Boastfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

osteology
OSTEOLOGY: perh. अस्थिव्याकरणं शारीरम् (comp.<BR>Sr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ostium
OSTIUM: rare: नदीमुखम्, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ostler
OSTLER: अश्वपालः, -कः।: v. Groom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ostracise
OSTRACISE: प्रव्राजयति (c. of व्रज्): v. To<BR>banish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ostracism
OSTRACISM: प्रव्राजनम्: v. Banishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ostrich
OSTRICH: *महाद्विजः; खगोष्ट्रः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

other
OTHER:<BR>(1) अन्यः (न्या, -न्यत्),<BR>these and many<BR>others:<BR>एते चान्ये च बहवः, D. b.; by any o.<BR>(individual): त्वदन्येन, R. iii. 63.; at o. times:<BR>अन्यदा, R. xi. 78.;<BR>in o. places:<BR>अन्यत्र, R.<BR>xiii. 56.;<BR>no. o.:<BR>नान्यदितः किञ्चित्, D. vii.;<BR>(2) अपरः (रा, रं), the o. went to Vidarbha:<BR>ययावपरो विदर्भान्, R. v. 60.; but o. s blamed:<BR>अपरे तु निनिन्दुः, D. iv.;<BR>the o. end:<BR>अपरान्तः,<BR>R. iv. 58.;<BR>(3) इतरः (रा, रत्) (= all o.: rare),<BR>of the o. s:<BR>इतरेषाम्, S.; not fit for any o. (man):<BR>इतरस्मै न योग्या, D. v. Ph.: (a)<BR>o.'s:<BR>पर- in<BR>comp.: v. Another.; (b) belonging to o. s.:<BR>(1) अन्यदीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) परकीयः (या, यं);<BR>(c)<BR>the o. day:<BR>तस्मिन् दिवसे (comp. Beng.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

otherwise
OTHERWISE:<BR>I Differently: अन्यथा,<BR>what<BR>should not be done o.:<BR>नान्यथा यद्धि कर्तव्यम्, Mah.<BR>iii. 1. 34.;<BR>if I speak o.:<BR>अन्यथा चेद् ब्रवीम्यहम्,<BR>V. p. iv. 13. 60.<BR>II In other respects:<BR>perh. अन्यथा; अन्यान्य-<BR>or<BR>अपरापरविषयेषु (?).<BR>III = or else:<BR>(1) न (नो) चेत्,<BR>o. I would<BR>kill you:<BR>नो चेद्धन्तव्योऽसि मया, H.;<BR>(2) विपरीते<BR>(= on the contrary), Mah. iii. 10. 36.;<BR>(3) अन्यथा, Da.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

otter
OTTER:<BR>(1) उद्रः (best equiv.);<BR>(2) जलविडालः<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ottoman
OTTOMAN:<BR>I A Turk: तुरूष्कः। Ph.:<BR>the O.<BR>empire:<BR>तुरूष्कसाम्राज्यम्।<BR>II A couch: *तुरूष्क-<BR>शयनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ought
OUGHT:<BR>(1) अर्हति (often = please),<BR>impatience<BR>o. not to lead you away from political success:<BR>न भवन्तमक्षमा नयसिद्धेरपनेतुमर्हति, Ki. ii. 42.;<BR>(2)<BR>by -तव्य, -अनीय and -य part. s, I o. to do that:<BR>मया तत् कर्तव्यम्: v. Should.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ounce
OUNCE:<BR>I A weight = टङ्कद्वयम् (in Troy<BR>weight); = पणार्द्धम् (of gold, silver, etc.).<BR>II An animal: द्वीपिन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

our
OUR, OURS:<BR>(1) अस्मदीयः (या, यं);<BR>(2) by<BR>gen.: v. Also our. N. B. After not expr.:<BR>v. My.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ourselves
OURSELVES: v. Self, myself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ousel
OUSEL: a bird: *अञ्जनः; नीलपक्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oust
OUST: निःसारयति (c. of सृ): v. To drive out,<BR>expel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

out
OUT (adj.):<BR>I Not within: बहिस्: v. The<BR>several verbs with which it is used.<BR>II<BR>Not at home: बहिर्गतः (ता, तं).<BR>III Pub-<BR>-lished: q. v.: बहिर्गतः (ता, तं).<BR>IV Dis-<BR>-closed: विवृतः (ता, तं).:<BR>V Extinguished,<BR>gone: गतः (ता, तं).<BR>VI Not in office:<BR>expr. with नास्ति।<BR>VII Completely: q. v.<BR>VIII Perceptively: उच्चैः।<BR>IX In error:<BR>expr. with भ्रमति, वि- (भ्रम्, c. 1.).<BR>X Un-<BR>-covered: अनावृतः (ता, तं).<BR>XI Away, off:<BR>q.v.:<BR>“o. with the dog”:<BR>दूरीकुरू कुक्कु रम्।<BR>XII<BR>Openly: स्फुटम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

out of
OUT OF:<BR>I Of place: q. v.: by abl.:<BR>to<BR>expel o. of a country:<BR>देशान्निःसारयति, B. p.: v.<BR>From.<BR>II Denoting motive: by abl.,<BR>o. of<BR>fear:<BR>भयात्।: v. From.<BR>III = beyond: expr.<BR>with अतीतः (ता, तं)<BR>or<BR>अति- in comp. (rare),<BR>o. of one's power:<BR>शत्तयतीतः (ता, तं). Ph.:<BR>gone<BR>o. of sight:<BR>चक्षुर्विषयमतिक्रान्तः।<BR>IV In various<BR>senses:<BR>o. of tune:<BR>विस्वरः (रा, रं); o. of use:<BR>गतव्यवहारः (रा, रं);<BR>o. of life:<BR>विगतजीवितः<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>o. of hope:<BR>गताशः (शा, शं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outbid
OUTBID: *अतिवदति: v. To bid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outbreak
OUTBREAK:<BR>I Bursting forth: उद्भेदः।<BR>II A<BR>disturbance: संक्षोभः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outcast
OUTCAST:<BR>I An exile: निष्कासितः (ता, तं).<BR>II<BR>= excommunicated: अपपात्रितः (ता, तं).<BR>III = vagabond: खण्डितवृत्त (f. त्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outcry
OUTCRY: उत्क्रोशः,<BR>to raise an o.:<BR>उत्क्रोशति (क्रुश्,<BR>c. 1.), Mit.: v. Cry, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outdo
OUTDO: अतिक्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.): v. To excel,<BR>surpass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outdoor
OUTDOOR: Ph.:<BR>o. exercise:<BR>प्रकाशव्यायामः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outer
OUTER:<BR>(1) बाह्य (f. ह्या),<BR>o. area:<BR>बाह्यमण्डपः;<BR>(2) बहिस् in comp.,<BR>o. door:<BR>बहिर्द्वारम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outfit
OUTFIT: सज्जा: v. Equipment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outflank
OUTFLANK: पार्श्वम् अतिक्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.).; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outgeneral
OUTGENERAL: अतिक्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.) (= to<BR>surpass: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outgo
OUTGO: अत्येति (इ, c. 2): v. (To go) beyond,<BR>surpass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outgrow
OUTGROW: expr. with अतीत्य वर्धते (वृध्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To grow, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outhouse
OUTHOUSE: बहिःशाला: v. Also shed, hut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outlandish
OUTLANDISH: विजातीयः (या, यं): v. Also un-<BR>-couth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outlast
OUTLAST: expr. with अधिकम्: v. To last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outlaw
OUTLAW (subs.): *उद्घोषितपातकिन् (f. नी) (?);<BR>रूद्धाग्न्युदकः (का, कं) (?) (comp. अग्न्युदकदायिनः,<BR>Mit.); अपपात्रितः (ता, तं) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outlaw
OUTLAW (v.): v. To proscribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outlawry
OUTLAWRY: अग्न्युदकरोधः: v. Proscription.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outlay
OUTLAY: द्रव्यसंग्रहादिव्ययः: v. Expenditure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outlet
OUTLET:<BR>(1) निर्गमः;<BR>(2) मुखम् (= mouth);<BR>(3)<BR>द्वारम् (= door).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outline
OUTLINE: पाण्डुलेख्यम् (?): v. Sketch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outlive
OUTLIVE: v. To live, survive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outlook
OUTLOOK:<BR>I The act: अवेक्षणम्।<BR>II View,<BR>prospect: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outnumber
OUTNUMBER: expr. with संख्या and अधिकः<BR>(का, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outpost
OUTPOST: गुल्मस्थानम्, Mu. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outpour
OUTPOUR:<BR>(1) वर्षति (वृष्, c. 1 (= to shower);<BR>(2) निषिञ्चति (सिच्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outrage
OUTRAGE (subs.): उपद्रवः: v. Also insult,<BR>offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outrage
OUTRAGE (v.):<BR>(1) अभिद्रुह्यति (द्रुह्, c. 4.) (?);<BR>(2) प्रमथति (मथ्, c. 1.) (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outrageous
OUTRAGEOUS:<BR>(1) दारूण (f. णा): v. fierce;<BR>(2) निर्लज्ज (f. ज्जा): v. Shameless. Ph.:<BR>o. conduct.:<BR>अत्याचारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outrageously
OUTRAGEOUSLY:<BR>(1) दारूणम् (= fiercely);<BR>(2)<BR>निर्हीकम् (= shamelessly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outrageousness
OUTRAGEOUSNESS:<BR>(1) दारूणता;<BR>(2) घोरता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outrider
OUTRIDER: परिचरसादिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outright
OUTRIGHT:<BR>I Instantly, at once: q. v.<BR>भटिति।<BR>II Completely, entirely: q. v.:<BR>अशेषेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outrun
OUTRUN: अतिधावति (धाव्, c. 1.): v. Also to<BR>exceed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outset
OUTSET: प्रारम्भः: v. Beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outshine
OUTSHINE: expr. with दीप्तिः etc. (= lustre) and<BR>अधिकम् (= more). Ph.:<BR>“o. beam”:<BR>रोचिष्णुपादाः,<BR>etc.: v. Brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outside
OUTSIDE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) बहिर्भागः;<BR>(2)<BR>often with बहिस्, are beautiful only on the o.:<BR>बहिरेव मनोहराः, H.; करस्य करमो बहिः, A.<BR>II<BR>The utmost: ph.:<BR>at the o.:<BR>अन्ततः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outside
OUTSIDE (adj.): बाह्य (f. ह्या): v. External.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outside
OUTSIDE (adv.): बहिस्,<BR>o. a village:<BR>बहिर्ग्रामात्,<BR>S. k.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outskirt
OUTSKIRT:<BR>in the o. s of the city:<BR>पुर उपशल्ये,<BR>R. xvi. 37.: v. Suburb, border.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outspoken
OUTSPOKEN: स्फुटभाषिन् (f. णी): v. Frank,<BR>candid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outspread
OUTSPREAD (adj.): प्रसारितः (ता, तं): v. To<BR>spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outstanding
OUTSTANDING (adj.): अशोधितः (ता, तं) (= not<BR>cleared, paid).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outstretched
OUTSTRETCHED: प्रसारितः (ता, तं): v. Also to<BR>stretch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outstrip
OUTSTRIP: अत्येति (इ, c. 2 (= to go beyond),<BR>etc.,<BR>o. ping the wind:<BR>अनिलातिगः (गा, गं),<BR>Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outvie
OUTVIE: अत्येति (इ, c. 2.): v. To surpass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outvote
OUTVOTE: expr. with vote and परा-भवति<BR>(भू, c. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outward
OUTWARD: बाह्य (f. ह्या): v. External.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outward
OUTWARD, OUTWARDS (adv.): बहिस or by<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outwardly
OUTWARDLY: बहिस्: v. Externally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outweigh
OUTWEIGH: सारतोऽतिरिच्यते: v. Also to exceed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outwit
OUTWIT: विप्रलभते (लभ्, c. 1 (= To deceive:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

outwork
OUTWORK: बाह्यपरिक्रिया<BR>or<BR>-कर्मन् (n (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oval
OVAL (adj.):<BR>(1) अण्डाकारः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) डिम्बा-<BR>कृति (mfn.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oval
OVAL (subs.): *उपवृत्तम्; उपमण्डलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ovation
OVATION: no equiv.: सभाजनम् may be used:<BR>v. Also feast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oven
OVEN: चुल्लिः (ल्ली), “दत्तचुल्लीपूजा”, D. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

over
OVER (adv.):<BR>I From side to side: expr.<BR>with वेधः।<BR>II On the opposite side: अपारे<BR>or<BR>परपारे।<BR>III With verbs: v. The several<BR>verbs.<BR>IV Beyond a limit: expr. with<BR>शिष्ट (f. ष्टा): v. To remain. Ph.: (a)<BR>o.<BR>again:<BR>पुनरपि; (b)<BR>o. and o.:<BR>पुनः पुनः: v. Re-<BR>-peatedly.; (c)<BR>o. against:<BR>अभितः (with acc.);<BR>(d) o. and above: expr. with अपरञ्च।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

over
OVER (prep.):<BR>I In gen.: उपरि (with gen.),<BR>I found myself fallen o. a heap of dry leaves:<BR>शुष्कपर्णराशेरूपरि निपतितमात्मानमपश्यम्, K.;<BR>being<BR>o. all joy:<BR>सर्वानन्दानामुपरि वर्तमाना, K.;<BR>God is<BR>o. the entire world:<BR>उपर्युपरि लोकं हरिः, S. k.: v.<BR>Also on, above, and the several verbs with<BR>which it is used.<BR>II More than: अधिक- in<BR>comp.,<BR>o. a thousand:<BR>अधिकसहस्र (f. स्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

over-
OVER- (prep.): often = excessive: अति- in<BR>comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

over
OVER, BE: उपरमति (रम्, c. 1.): v. To cease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overabound
OVERABOUND: expr. with अतिप्रचुरः (रा, रं),<BR>बहुलः (ला, लं), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overawe
OVERAWE: भीषयते (c. of भी): v. To frighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overbalance
OVERBALANCE: सारतोऽतिरिच्यते,<BR>Saviour will o.<BR>the whole world:<BR>सारतो जगतः कृत्स्नादतिरिक्तो<BR> जनार्दनः, Mah. v. 68. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overbearing
OVERBEARING (adj.): अवलिप्त (f. प्ता): v.<BR>Insolent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overbearingly
OVERBEARINGLY: सावलेपम्: v. Insolently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overblown
OVERBLOWN (adj.): fig.: प्रध्मातः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overboard
OVERBOARD: expr. by abl. नावः etc. and जले<BR>(= in water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overburden
OVERBURDEN: v. To overload.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overcast
OVERCAST (v.):<BR>I To cloud, darken: q. v.:<BR>II To rate too high: अधिकं मन्यते (मन्,<BR>c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overcautious
OVERCAUTIOUS: अत्यवहितः (ता, तं), etc.: v.<BR>Cautious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overcharge
OVERCHARGE:<BR>I To fill: q. v.: परिपूरयति<BR>(पूर्, c. 10.).<BR>II To charge too much:<BR>अधिकं याचते (याच्, c. 1 (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overclouded
OVERCLOUDED: मेघोपरूद्ध (f. द्धा) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overcoat
OVERCOAT: *उपरिकोटम्; बृहत्कोटम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overcome
OVERCOME:<BR>I To surmount: q. v.: अतिक्राम्यति<BR>(क्रम्, c. 4.).<BR>II To distress, exhaust: अभि-<BR>भवति (भू, c. 1.).<BR>III To conquer: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overcoming
OVERCOMING (adj.): विजयिन् (f. नी), o. prowess:<BR>विजयि वीर्यम्, Vi. i. 8.: v. Victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overdone
OVERDONE: in cooking: अतिसिद्ध (f. द्धा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overdraw
OVERDRAW: अधिकं निष्कर्षति (कृष्, c. 1 (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overdrink
OVERDRINK: अधिकम् पिबति; अतिपानं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overdrive
OVERDRIVE: भृशं वाहयति (c. of वह्), etc.: v.<BR>To drive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overdue
OVERDUE: अतीतशोधनकालः (ला, लं) (??) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overeat
OVEREAT: बहु अश्नाति (अश्, c. 9.), etc.: v. To<BR>eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overestimate
OVERESTIMATE: अधिकं गणयति, परि- (गण्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overfatigue
OVERFATIGUE (subs.): अतिश्रमः: v. Fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overfeed
OVERFEED: बहु भोजयति (c. of भुज्): v. To<BR>feed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overflow
OVERFLOW (subs.): उत्सेकः: v. Inundation,<BR>deluge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overflow
OVERFLOW (v.):<BR>I Lit.: expr. with flow and<BR>उपरिः v. Also to inundate.<BR>II Fig.: expr.<BR>with प्रचुरः (रा, रं): v. Abundant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overflowing
OVERFLOWING: (adj.): v. Abundant, exces-<BR>-sive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overgrow
OVERGROW:<BR>I To cover: q. v.:<BR>o. n with<BR>moss:<BR>शैवलवत् (f. ती), R. xvi. 46.<BR>II To<BR>grow beyond: अतिवर्धते (वृध्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overhang
OVERHANG (v. t.): उपरि बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.):<BR>v. To hang.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overhang
OVERHANG (v. i.): Often expr. with sim. उपरि:<BR>v. Also to hang.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overhanging
OVERHANGING (adj.): as clouds: उपरि प्रलम्ब-<BR>मानः (ना, नं) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overhasty
OVERHASTY: अतिक्षिप्रकारिन् (f. णी): v. Hasty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overhaul
OVERHAUL: Fig.: विविच्य परीक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overhead
OVERHEAD:<BR>(1) उपरि;<BR>(2) ऊर्द्धम् (= above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overhear
OVERHEAR: अलक्षितं शृणोति (श्रु, c. 5.) and<BR>sim. comp.s., “लताव्यवहितः शृणोमि विश्वस्तकथिता-<BR>न्यासाम्”, Sa. iii.: v. To hear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overheat
OVERHEAT: अतितापयति (तप्, c. 10.), etc.: v.<BR>To heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overjoy
OVERJOY (subs.): अतिहर्षः and sim. comp.s.:<BR>v. Joy, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overland
OVERLAND: Ph.:<BR>went o.:<BR>प्रतस्थे स्थलवर्त्मना, R.<BR>iv. 60.;<BR>o. route:<BR>स्थलवर्त्मन् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overlay
OVERLAY:<BR>I To cover, set: q. v.: आवृणोति<BR>(वृ, c. 5.),<BR>o. id with specks of gold:<BR>हेमबिन्दु-<BR>भिरावृतः (ता, तं), Mah. iv. 42. 16.<BR>II To<BR>o. another by laying upon: expr. with<BR>उपरि and a verb, she o. id the child and it died:<BR>*उपरिशयनेन शिशुर्ममार।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overleap
OVERLEAP (v.): लङ्घयति, वि-, उत्-, प्र-, (लङ्घ्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overload
OVERLOAD:<BR>I Lit.: अतिभारं न्यस्यति (अस्, c.<BR>4.) (with loc.).<BR>II Fig.: as the stomach:<BR>अतिपूरयति (पूर्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overlong
OVERLONG: अतिदीर्घ (f. र्घा), etc.: v. Long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overlook
OVERLOOK:<BR>I To command a view of:<BR>expr. by circumlo.: v. To look, see.<BR>II To<BR>inspect, look into: q. v.<BR>III To pass by<BR>refraining from noticing: न पश्यति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overmatch
OVERMATCH: अधिकः (का, कं): v. Also great.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overmuch
OVERMUCH: अत्यधिकम्: v. Much, extremely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overnight
OVERNIGHT (adv.):<BR>(1) पूर्वरात्रौ;<BR>(2) गतनिशायाम्;<BR>and sim. comps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overpass
OVERPASS: v. To pass over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overpeopled
OVERPEOPLED: अतिजनाकीर्ण (f. र्णा) and sim.<BR>comp.s.: v. Populous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overplus
OVERPLUS: उद्व्टत्तम्: v. Surplus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overpower
OVERPOWER:<BR>(1) मृद्राति (मृद्, c. 9.) (= to<BR>crush);<BR>(2) अभिभवति (भू, c. 1 (= to over-<BR>-come): v. To overwhelm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overrate
OVERRATE: अधिकं मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.): v. To<BR>value.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overreach
OVERREACH: अभिसं-दधाति<BR>or<BR>-धत्ते (धा, c. 3.):<BR>v. To deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overreaching
OVERREACHING (subs.): अभिसन्धानम्: v.<BR>Deception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

override
OVERRIDE: Fig.: अधिगच्छति (गम्, c. 1.),<BR>one<BR>who o. s virtue:<BR>धर्मातिगः, Mah. v. 92. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overripe
OVERRIPE: अतिपक्व (f. क्वा): v. Ripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overrule
OVERRULE: अधः क्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6 (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overruling
OVERRULING: (adj.): प्रभविष्णु (mfn): v.<BR>Also omnipotent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overrun
OVERRUN: उपप्लवते (प्लु, c. 1.), the o. world:<BR>उपप्लुतं विश्वम्, Si. i. 38.: v. Also to harass,<BR>oppress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oversee
OVERSEE: v. To inspect, overlook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overseer
OVERSEER: परिदर्शकः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overshadow
OVERSHADOW: छादयति (छद्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overshoot
OVERSHOOT: लक्ष्यम् अतिक्रामति<BR>or<BR>-क्राम्यति (क्रम्,<BR>c. 1. and 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overshot
OVERSHOT:<BR>I Drunk: क्षीवः (वा, वं).<BR>II<BR>Of wheels: *छिद्रवत् (f. ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oversight
OVERSIGHT:<BR>I Care: q. v.<BR>II Mistake:<BR>q. v.: अनवेक्षा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oversleep
OVERSLEEP: दीर्घं स्वपिति (स्वप्, c. 2.): v. To<BR>sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overspread
OVERSPREAD: समावृणोति (वृ, c. 5.): v. To<BR>cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overstate
OVERSTATE: v. To exaggerate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overstep
OVERSTEP: अतिक्राम्यति (क्रम्, c. 4.): v. To<BR>exceed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overstock
OVERSTOCK: पूरयति (= to fill) will gen. do.:<BR>v. Also stock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overstrain
OVERSTRAIN: क्लिश्नाति (क्लिश्, c. 9 (= to pain:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overt
OVERT: प्रकाशः (शा, शं): v. Open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overtake
OVERTAKE:<BR>I To come up with:<BR>I could o.<BR>even Garuḍa:<BR>पूर्वप्रस्थितं वैनतेयमप्यासादयेयम्, V. i.:<BR>v. To reach, catch.<BR>II To fall upon:<BR>पतति, नि-, (पत्, c. 1 (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overtask
OVERTASK: अतिभारं न्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.), etc.<BR>(with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overtax
OVERTAX:<BR>I Lit.: अधिककरं न्यस्यति, etc. (with<BR>loc.).<BR>II Fig.: v. To overtask.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overthrow
OVERTHROW (v.):<BR>I To upset: q. v.<BR>II<BR>To ruin, demolish: q. v.:<BR>(1) पोथयति,<BR> अव-, (पुथ्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) मृद्राति, अव-, (मृद्,<BR>c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overthrow
OVERTHROW (subs.): ध्वंसः, वि-, प्र-: v. Des-<BR>-truction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overtly
OVERTLY: प्रकाशम्: v. Openly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overtop
OVERTOP: अतिक्राम्यति (क्रम्, c. 4.): v. To<BR>exceed, surpass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overture
OVERTURE:<BR>I Proposal: उपन्यासः (?); प्रस्तावना<BR>(?).<BR>II A musical introduction: प्रस्तावना<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overturn
OVERTURN:<BR>I Lit.: विपर्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.),<BR>now the living world is o. ed:<BR>विपर्यस्तः सम्प्रति<BR> जीवलोकः, U. i.<BR>II To overthrow, ruin:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overvalue
OVERVALUE: अधिकम् (f. कां) मन्यते (मन्, c.<BR>4.): v. To esteem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overweening
OVERWEENING: उद्धतः (ता, तं): v. Haughty,<BR>arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overweeningly
OVERWEENINGLY:<BR>(1) साभिमानम्;<BR>(2) उद्धतम्<BR>(= Haughtily).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overweigh
OVERWEIGH: v. To overbalance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overwhelm
OVERWHELM: सादयति, अव-, (c. of सद्),<BR>o. ed<BR>with grief and sorrow:<BR>दुःखशोकसन्न (f. न्ना),<BR>Ram. ii. 59. 32.: v. Also to crush,<BR>immerge. Ph.:<BR>o. ing testimony:<BR>अतिप्रबलं or<BR>-प्रचुरं साक्ष्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overwork
OVERWORK (v.): अधिकं कर्म कारयति (c. of कृ)<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overwork
OVERWORK (subs.): अधिककर्मन् (n.) (?): v.<BR>Work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overwrought
OVERWROUGHT: perh. कार्मिक- in comp.:<BR>Also wrought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

overzealous
OVERZEALOUS:<BR>(1) अत्युत्सुकः (का, कं);<BR>(2)<BR>अत्युत्साहिन् (f. नी): v. Also zealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oviparous
OVIPAROUS: अण्डजः (जा, जं), “मूकाण्डजम्”, Ku.<BR>iii. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

owe
OWE (v. t.): Lit.: धारयति (धृ, c. 10 (with dat.<BR>of the creditor),<BR>he o. s (me) ten sovereigns:<BR>अयं<BR> दशसुवर्णकं धारयति, Mr. ii.;<BR>God o. s liberation<BR>to the pious:<BR>भक्ताय धारयति मोक्षं हरिः, S. k.<BR>II To be obliged for: expr. by circumlo, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">Page498</a>]<BR>I o. my darling to you:<BR>त्वयैवेयं प्रिया मे दत्ता,<BR>D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

owing
OWING:<BR>I Due: expr. by देयः (या, यं) or<BR>प्राप्य (f. प्या).<BR>II (On) account of: q. v.:<BR>fall of (rain)<BR>water is o. to its heaviness:<BR>अपां<BR> गुरूत्वात्पतनम्, V. d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

owl
OWL:<BR>(1) पेचकः;<BR>(2) उ(ऊ)लूकः;<BR>(3) कौशिकः<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

owlet
OWLET: i. e. a little owl: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

own
OWN (adj.):<BR>(1) स्वः (स्वा, स्वं),<BR>by giving my o.<BR>life:<BR>स्वदेहार्पणेन, R.; towards his o. daughter:<BR>स्वदुहितरि, D.;<BR>your o. land:<BR>स्वभूमिः, K.;<BR>(2) स्वकीयः<BR>or<BR>स्वीयः (या, यं) (= one's o.),<BR>if<BR>you want your o. life:<BR>यदि स्वकीयजीवनमिच्छसि,<BR>Vet.;<BR>(3) निजः (जा, जं), to his o. preceptor:<BR>निजाय गुरवे, Ana.;<BR>(4) स्वकः (का, कं),<BR>went<BR>to their o. houses:<BR>स्वकं स्वकं निवेशनं प्रत्युद्गताः,<BR>Kar.;<BR>(5) आत्मीयः (या, यं) (= one's o.),<BR>make it your o.:<BR>अयमात्मीयः क्रियताम्, K. N. B.<BR>Note that possessive pronouns are not expr.<BR>in Sanskrit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

own
OWN (v.):<BR>I To acknowledge: q. v.:<BR>स्वीकरोति।<BR>II To possess: q. v.: expr. by<BR>subs.: v. Owner, belonging to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

owner
OWNER: स्वामिन् (f. नी),<BR>first o.:<BR>पूर्वस्वामी, Vri.;<BR>sale by one who is not the o.:<BR>अस्वामिविक्रयः,<BR>Kat.;<BR>o. of cattle:<BR>गोस्वामी, M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ownership
OWNERSHIP:<BR>(1) स्वत्वम्, creating, destroying o.:<BR>स्वत्वजनक (f. निका), स्वत्वनाशक (f. शिका),<BR>Srikrishna;<BR>partial o.:<BR>एकदेशगतस्वत्वम्, Mit.;<BR>(2) by स्वामिन्,<BR>to acquire o.:<BR>स्वामी भवति, Mi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ox
OX:<BR>(1) गो (m.);<BR>(2) वृषः, -भः;<BR>(3) उक्षन्<BR>(m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ox-hide
OX-HIDE:<BR>(1) गव्यम्, Mah.;<BR>(2) उक्षचर्मन् (n.)<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oxidize
OXIDIZE: जारयति (c. of जॄ), Wilson: v. Also<BR>rush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oxlip
OXLIP: *उक्षकन्दः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ox-stall
OX-STALL: उक्षशाला (?): v. Cow-pen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oxygen
OXYGEN: *प्राणवायुः; सारवायुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oxytone
OXYTONE: in gram: अन्तोदात्त (f. त्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oyez
OYEZ: शृणुत शृणुत (= hear), Mr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oyster
OYSTER: शुक्तिः, -का,<BR>o. -shell:<BR>शुक्तिपुटम्, -पेशी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pabulum
PABULUM: भोजनम्: v. Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pace
PACE (subs.):<BR>I A step: q. v.: पदम्, -न्यासः।<BR>II Gait:<BR>(1) गतिः,<BR>p. of a horse:<BR>अश्वस्य गतिः,<BR>M. n.;<BR>at a quick p.:<BR>द्रुतगत्या;<BR>(2) धारा (of<BR>horses), “पूर्णवेगा तथा चान्या पञ्च धाराः प्रकीर्तिताः”,<BR>M. n. Ph.:<BR>to keep or hold p. with:<BR>सह चलति<BR>(चल्, c. 1.) (used in Bengali).<BR>III A<BR>measure: perh. पदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pace
PACE (v. i.): क्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.), p. up and down:<BR>परिक्रामति: v. To move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pace
PACE (v. t.):<BR>I To pass over: अतिक्रामति।<BR>II<BR>To measure: q. v.: मिमीते (मा, c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pacha
PACHA: v. Pasha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pacific
PACIFIC: शान्तः (न्ता, न्तं), प्र-,<BR>the eastern ocean<BR>is p.:<BR>प्रशान्तः पूर्वसागरः, Ram.: v. Quiet, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pacifically
PACIFICALLY: expr. by circumlo., p. inclined:<BR>शमप्रवण (f. णा): v. Peace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pacification
PACIFICATION: शमनम्, प्र-: v. Also reconcilia-<BR>-tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pacificator
PACIFICATOR, PACIFIER: expr. by circumlo.:<BR>v. Peace, to make.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pacificatory
PACIFICATORY: शान्तिकरः (री, रं); शान्तिदः (दा,<BR> दं); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pacify
PACIFY: शमयति, प्र- (c. of शम्): v. To appease,<BR>reconcile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pack
PACK (subs.):<BR>I A bundle: पोट्टली (?).<BR>II<BR>Of hounds etc.: गणः।<BR>III Of cards:<BR>पटलम् (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pack
PACK (v.): पटलीकरोति (??).<BR>P. off:<BR>अपसारयति<BR>(c. of सृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

package
PACKAGE: no equiv.: पोट्टली<BR>or<BR>पटलम् may be<BR>used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

packet
PACKET:<BR>(1) पोट(ट्ट)लिका (?);<BR>(2) कूर्चः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pack-cloth
PACK-CLOTH: *संवरणवासस् (n.), etc.: v. Cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pack-horse
PACK-HORSE:<BR>(1) स्थूरिन् (m.);<BR>(2) स्थौरिन् (m.);<BR>(3) पृष्ठोऽश्वः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pack-saddle
PACK-SADDLE:<BR>(1) पल्यानम् (comp. Beng.<BR>पालान्);<BR>(2) पर्याणम्<BR>or<BR>पर्ययणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pack-thread
PACK-THREAD: दामन् (n.); v. Cord, string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pad
PAD (subs.):<BR>I A package: कूर्चः।<BR>II A<BR>bolster: उपधानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pad
PAD (v.): तूलादिना पूरयति (पूर्, c. 10.)<BR>or<BR>भरति<BR>(भृ, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

padding
PADDING:<BR>I The act: पूरणम्; भरणम्।<BR>II The<BR>things: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paddle
PADDLE (subs.): क्षेपणिः: v. Oar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paddle
PADDLE (v.):<BR>I Intrans.:<BR>(1) आ-हन्ति (हन्,<BR>c. 2.), Ki. viii. 43.;<BR>(2) ताडयति (तड्, c. 10.),<BR>(poet.), R. xvi. 66.<BR>II Trans: चालयति, सं-,<BR>(c. of चल्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paddle-box
PADDLE-BOX: *चक्रकोष्ठः (the exact sense from<BR>context).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paddle-wheel
PADDLE-WHEEL: *वारिसञ्चालनचक्रम्; पोतचक्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paddock
PADDOCK: वृतिः: v. Enclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

padlock
PADLOCK: *महातालकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paddy
PADDY: धान्यम्।<BR>Winter p.:<BR>शालिधान्यम्;<BR>autum-<BR>nal p.:<BR>आशुधान्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paen
PÆN, PEAN: जयगीतम् and sim. comp.s.: v.<BR>Song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pagan
PAGAN: मिथ्यादेवभक्तः (क्ता, क्तं) (?): v. Heathen,<BR>-ish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paganism
PAGANISM: मिथ्यादेवभक्तिः (?): v. Heathenism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

page
PAGE (subs.):<BR>I Of a book: पृष्ठा।<BR>II A<BR>boy attendant:<BR>(1) चेटः, -कः;<BR>(2) किंकरः:<BR>v. Servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

page
PAGE (v.): पृष्ठाः अङ्कयति<BR>or<BR>पृष्ठाङ्कनं करोति (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pageant
PAGEANT:<BR>I A grand show: समारोहः; any-<BR>-thing showy: perh. दृश्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pageantry
PAGEANTRY: आडम्बरः: v. Show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pagoda
PAGODA: सिद्धायतनम्: v. Temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pail
PAIL: भाण्डः: v. Also bucket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pain
PAIN (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) वेदना,<BR>for this<BR>exercise I have got p. in the head:<BR>व्यायामेन<BR> ममानेन जाता शिरसि वेदना, Mah. iii. 297. 3.;<BR>(my mother) died of p.s of labour: प्रसववेदनया<BR> लोकान्तरमगमत्, K.:<BR>(2) पीडा,<BR>giving p.:<BR>पीडाकरः<BR>(री, रं), V.s.;<BR>(3) व्यथा;<BR>(4) दुःखम्,<BR>who<BR>causes p. without drawing blood:<BR>शोणितेन विना<BR> दुःखमुत्पादयिता, V.s.;<BR>(5) रूज् (f (rare),<BR>who<BR>does not understand my mental p.:<BR>रूजं मम न वेद<BR> यो मानसीम्, V. ii. 11. In pl. labour, effort:<BR>q. v.: परिश्रमः।<BR>III Punishment: expr. by<BR>circumlo.,<BR>“under p. of death”:<BR>नो चेद्धन्तव्योऽसि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pain
PAIN (v.):<BR>(1) पीडयति (पीड्, c. 10.), I am<BR>p. ed:<BR>पीडितोऽस्मि, R. xi. 38.;<BR>(2) व्यथयति<BR>(c. of व्यथ्),<BR>and this proclamation p.s. my<BR>mind:<BR>एषा च व्यथयति घोषणा मनो मे, Mr. x. 22.;<BR>(3) दुःखाकरोति,<BR>this p.s me:<BR>अदो दुःखाकरोति माम्,<BR>Si. ii. 11. To be p.ed:<BR>(1) व्यथते (व्यथ्, c.<BR>1.), Ki. i. 2.;<BR>(2) पीड्यते (pass. of पीड्), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

painful
PAINFUL:<BR>I As an abscess:<BR>(1) रूजावत् (f.<BR>ती), Ni.;<BR>(2) सरूजः (जा, जं), Ni. Very p.:<BR>(1) महारूजः (जा, जं), Ni.;<BR>(2) अत्यर्थवेदनः (ना,<BR> नं), Ni.; etc.<BR>II Causing pain:<BR>(1) कष्टः<BR>(ष्टा, ष्टं),<BR>her awaking was more p. than her<BR>loss of sense:<BR>मोहादभूत् कष्टतरः प्रबोधः, R. xvi.<BR>56.;<BR>(2) दुःखदः (दा, दं), M.n. and sim.<BR>comp.s.;<BR>(3) व्यथक (f. थिका) (rare), Ki.<BR>ii. 4.<BR>III Laborious: श्रमसाध्य (f. ध्या) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

painfully
PAINFULLY:<BR>I With pain:<BR>(1) व्यथितः (ता,<BR> तं); सव्यथः (था, थं).<BR>II Laboriously: श्रमेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

painfulness
PAINFULNESS: सरूजता, etc.: v. Painful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

painless
PAINLESS: अरूजः (जा, जं), Ni. and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

painstaking
PAINSTAKING: expr. by verb: परिश्रमं करोति:<BR>v. Laborious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paint
PAINT (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) चित्रयति (चित्र्, c.<BR>10.);<BR>(2) आ-लिखति (लिख्, c. 6.), बालचूत-<BR>वृक्षस्य पार्श्वे आलिखिता, Sa. vi.<BR>II To colour:<BR>आलिखति,<BR>p. ing idols:<BR>प्रतिमाः आलिखन्ति, Mah.<BR>vi. 3. 9.<BR>III Fig.: वर्णयति: v. To describe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paint
PAINT (subs.):<BR>(1) वर्णकम्,<BR>from vividness of<BR>p.:<BR>वर्णकोच्छ्वासात्, Sa. vi. 18.;<BR>(2) रङ्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paint-brush
PAINT-BRUSH:<BR>(1) वर्तिका, skill in the use of p.:<BR>वर्तिकालेखानिपुणता, Sa.;<BR>(2) वर्णतूली, -लिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

painter
PAINTER:<BR>I Artistic:<BR>(1) चित्रकर (f. री);<BR>(2) चित्रलिख् (mfn (rare).<BR>II Fig.: expr.<BR>by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

painting
PAINTING (subs.):<BR>I The art:<BR>(1) चित्रकर्मन्<BR>(n.) and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Anything paint-<BR>-ed:<BR>(1) चित्रम्,<BR>even in the p.:<BR>चित्रेऽपि, Sa.<BR>vi. 14.;<BR>(2) आलेख्यम्, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pair
PAIR (subs.):<BR>I Of things:<BR>(1) युगम्, -लम्;<BR>(2) युग्मम्;<BR>(3) -द्वयम् in comp. (= two): v.<BR>Both.<BR>II Of the sexes: द्वन्द्वम्,<BR>to couple a<BR>p.:<BR>द्वन्द्वं योजयति, R. vii. 14.: v. Couple.<BR>Ph.:<BR>A p. of sand-pipers:<BR>टिट्टिभदम्पती, P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pair
PAIR (v. t.): योजयति (युज्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>join, match.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pair
PAIR (v. i.):<BR>I To couple:<BR>(1) सम्भवति (भू,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>p. ed with her:<BR>सम्बभूव तया सार्धम्, Mah.<BR>i. 104. 6.;<BR>(2) मैथुनम् आचरति (चर्, c. 1.)<BR>(with loc. of the female), Mah.<BR>II To<BR>suit, fit: q. v.: युज्यते (pass of युज्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pairing
PAIRING (subs.):<BR>(1) व्यवायः;<BR>(2) मैथुनम्;<BR>(3)<BR>सङ्गमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palage
PALAGE:<BR>(1) सौध (mn.);<BR>(2) हर्म्यम्;<BR>(3) राज-<BR>कुलम् (royal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paladin
PALADIN: भटः: v. Champion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palanquin
PALANQUIN:<BR>(1) नरयानम्, Mah.;<BR>(2) मनुष्य-<BR>वाह्यं चतुरस्रयानम्, R. vi. 10.;<BR>(3) शिविका<BR>(= litter), V. p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palatable
PALATABLE:<BR>(1) स्वादु (mfn.): v. Sweet;<BR>(2) आस्वाद्य (f. द्या),<BR>containing p. water:<BR>आस्वाद्य-<BR>तोयः (या, यं), H.: v. Also nice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palatal
PALATAL: i. e.<BR>a p. letter:<BR>तालव्यम्, -वर्णम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palate
PALATE:<BR>I Lit.: तालु (n.). Ph.: soft p.:<BR>उपजिह्वा: v. Uvulla.<BR>II Fig., taste: q. v.:<BR>अभिरूचिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palatial
PALATIAL: Ph.<BR>P. building:<BR>महाप्रासादः: v.<BR>Palace, big.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palatine
PALATINE: Ph.:<BR>Count p.:<BR>*उपराजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palaver
PALAVER:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) चाटूक्तिः (?);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रियवादः (?).<BR>II Verb.: expr. by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pale
PALE (adj.):<BR>I Dusky white:<BR>(1) पाण्डु<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(2) पाण्डुरः (रा, रं);<BR>(3) हरिणः (णी,<BR> णं), “विवर्णो हरिणः कृशः”, Mah. 137.<BR>II Not<BR>ruddy, wan: विवर्ण (f. र्णा),<BR>p. with lustre<BR>gone:<BR>विवर्णा विगतश्रीका, Mah. i. 8. 18.;<BR>those<BR>kings grew p.:<BR>प्रपेदे विवर्णभावं स स भूमिपालः, R.<BR>vi. 67.<BR>III Dim, not bright: मन्दप्रभः (भा,<BR> भं) and sim. comp.s.,<BR>then when the p.<BR>moon:<BR>निधौ कलानामथ मन्दकान्तौ, B. xi. 1.<BR>IV Light (of colours): prob. पाण्डुर- in<BR>comp.: v. Also slight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pale
PALE (subs.):<BR>I A stake: शलाका।<BR>II Limit,<BR>fence: q. v.: सीभा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pale
PALE (v.):<BR>I To enclose: q. v.: परिवृणोति (वृ,<BR>c. 5.).<BR>II To check, stop: q. v.: अवरूणद्धि<BR>(रूध्, c. 7.).<BR>III To turn p.: विवर्णीभवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pale-eyed
PALE-EYED: पाण्डुनयनः (ना, नं) and sim. comp.s.<BR>(comp. विपाण्डुभिर्म्लानतया पयोधरैः, Ki. iv. 24.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paleness
PALENESS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पाण्डुता, वि-;<BR>(2)<BR>पाण्डुरता।<BR>II Loss of colour: विवर्णता<BR>or<BR>वैवर्ण्यम्।<BR>III Dimness: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paleography
PALEOGRAPHY: पुराणवर्णलक्षणम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palette
PALETTE: v. Pallet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palfrey
PALFREY: घोटकभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palindrome
PALINDROME: प्रतिलोमानुलोमपादः (whose every<BR>foot is a p.), Si. xix. 40.: प्रतिलोमानुलोमार्द्धम्<BR>(whose half is a p.), Ki. xv. 20.: प्रतिलोमानु-<BR>लोमेन श्लोकद्वयम् (whose two verses form a p.),<BR>Ki. xv. 22-3., Si. xix. 33-4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paling
PALING: वृतिः: v. Enclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palinode
PALINODE: अपलापः: v. Recantation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palisade
PALISADE: prob. गुञ्जः (comp. गोंँज् in Bengali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palisading
PALISADING (subs.): गुञ्जवृतिः (?) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palish
PALISH:<BR>(1) आपाण्डु (mfn.);<BR>(2) आपाण्डुरः (रा,<BR> रं), etc.: v. Pale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pall
PALL (subs.): वासस् (n.)<BR>or<BR>महार्हवासस् (n.) and<BR>sim. comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pall
PALL (v. i.):<BR>(1) नीरसीभवति;<BR>(2) विरसीभवति;<BR>(3) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palladium
PALLADIUM: fig.: शरणम्: v. Defence, safety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pallet
PALLET:<BR>I A small bed: खट्विका।<BR>II Pain-<BR>-ter's board: रङ्गफलकम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palliate
PALLIATE:<BR>(1) लघयति (nomi.);<BR>(2) लघूकरोति:<BR>v. Also to cover (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palliation
PALLIATION:<BR>(1) by verb;<BR>(2) उपशमः (= abate-<BR>-ment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palliative
PALLIATIVE:<BR>(1) by verb;<BR>(2) उपशमनः (नी,<BR> नं = mitigating: rare);<BR>(3) शान्तिप्रद (f. दा<BR>= 2) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pallid
PALLID: पाण्डु (mfn.): v. Pale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pallor
PALLOR: पाण्डुता: v. Paleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palm
PALM (subs.):<BR>I Of the hand: करतल (mn.)<BR>and sim. comp.s. Ph.: joining the p.s.: (in<BR>respect) कृताञ्जलि (mfn.), -पुटः (टा, टं) or<BR>बद्धाञ्जलि (mfn.), etc.<BR>II A measure: हस्तार्द्धम्।<BR>III A tree: तालः (the palmyra p.: for<BR>other species, use तालजातीयः). Its sap: ताली।<BR>Made of its wood: ताल- in comp. s<BR>or<BR>ताल [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">Page501</a>]<BR>(f. ली).<BR>IV Its fruit: तालम्, like the fall of<BR>the p.-fruit on the crow: (i. e. sudden and<BR>unexpected) काकतालीयः (या, यं), S. k. V. Fig.,<BR>a p.-leaf as a token of victory: जयपताका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palm
PALM (v.): To p. off: i. e. to impose,<BR>defraud: q. v.: संक्रामयति (c. of क्रम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palmary
PALMARY:<BR>I Measuring a palm: षडङ्गुलः<BR>(ला, लं).<BR>II Palmy: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palmate
PALMATE, -D: करतलाकारः (रा, रं) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palmer
PALMER: सदातीर्थनिषेविन् (f. णी) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palmer-worm
PALMER-WORM: लोमशकीटः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palmister
PALMISTER: सामुद्रकज्ञ (f. ज्ञा); करतलविद्याविद्<BR>(mfn.) (?); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palmistry
PALMISTRY: सामुद्रकम्; perh. करतलविद्या (comp.<BR>अङ्कविद्या, V. m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palm-oil
PALM-OIL: *तालतैलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palmy
PALMY: समृद्ध (f. द्धा): v. To flourish, pros-<BR>-perous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palmyra
PALMYRA: तालः,<BR>ashes of p. flowers with<BR>molasses destroy spleen:<BR>तालपुष्पभवः क्षारः सगुडः<BR> प्लीहनाशनः, Chakradatta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palpable
PALPABLE: स्पष्ट (f. ष्टा): v. Plain, clear.<BR>Ph.:<BR>p. darkness:<BR>सूचीभेद्यतमस् (n.);<BR>p. arith-<BR>metic:<BR>*स्पर्शाङ्कः, -शास्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palpably
PALPABLY:<BR>(1) स्पष्टम्;<BR>(2) स्फुटम्: v. Also<BR>clearly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palpitate
PALPITATE: वेपते,<BR>my heart is p. ing:<BR>वेपते मे<BR> हृदयम्: v. To throb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palpitation
PALPITATION:<BR>(1) स्पन्दः, -नम् (natural);<BR>(2)<BR>कम्पः (from fear etc.),<BR>p. of the heart:<BR>हृत्कम्पः;<BR>(2) घेपथुः (rare = 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palsical
PALSICAL, PALSIED: v. Paralysis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palsy
PALSY: स्तम्भः: v. Paralysis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

palter
PALTER: विकुरुते (कृ, c. 8.): v. To shuffle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paltriness
PALTRINESS:<BR>(1) क्षुद्रता;<BR>(2) तुच्छता;<BR>(3) लघुता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paltry
PALTRY:<BR>(1) क्षुद्र (f. द्रा);<BR>(2) तुच्छ (f. च्छा):<BR>v. Trifling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pampas
PAMPAS: विशालक्षेत्राणि (n. pl.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pamper
PAMPER: प्याययति (c. of प्याय्): v. Also<BR>satiate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pamphlet
PAMPHLET: क्षुद्रपुस्तकम् (?): v. Book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pamphleteer
PAMPHLETEER: सन्दर्भलेखकः and sim. comp.s.<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pan
PAN:<BR>I The god: गोपदेवता।<BR>II The prepa-<BR>-ration: ताम्बूलम्,<BR>gave another p. to Maha-<BR>śvetā:<BR>अपरं ताम्बूलं महाश्वे तायै प्रायच्छत्, K.<BR>III. A<BR>vessel: भाजनम्,<BR>frying p.:<BR>भ्राष्ट्रम्।<BR>IV The<BR>skull: कपालम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

panacea
PANACEA: सर्वरोगहर (f. रा) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pancake
PANCAKE: पिष्टकविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pandect
PANDECT: *रोमकसंहिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pandemonium
PANDEMONIUM: रक्षःसभभ्, S. k.; नरकः (= hell).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pander
PANDER (subs.): विटः: v. Procurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pander
PANDER (v.):<BR>I Lit.: सम्भोगाय प्रवर्तते (वृत्, c.<BR>1.); better by circumlo. “सज्जयन्ति हि ते<BR> नारीः”, M. viii. 362.<BR>II Fig.: पूरयति (पूर्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pandering
PANDERING (subs.): संघटनजीविका (comp. सम्भोग-<BR>जीविका, Mit.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pandit
PANDIT, PUNDIT: I. Lit.: पण्डितः।<BR>II A<BR>tutor: शिक्षकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pane
PANE: of glass: *काचफलकम्; चतुरस्रकाचम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

panegyric
PANEGYRIC:<BR>(1) संस्तवः;<BR>(2) स्तुतिवादः: v. Also<BR>praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

panegyrist
PANEGYRIST:<BR>(1) स्तोतृ (f. त्री), सं-;<BR>(2) स्तव-<BR>वक्तृ (f. क्त्री) and sim. comps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

panel
PANEL (subs.):<BR>I Of a door: कपा(वा)ट (mn.).<BR>II Of jurors: सभ्यलेख्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pang
PANG:<BR>(1) वेदना (= pain.), p. s of childbirth:<BR>प्रसववेदना, K.;<BR>(2) यातना;<BR>(3) यन्त्रणा;<BR>(4)<BR>कारणा (rare),<BR>to taste the p. s of hell:<BR>कारणानां<BR> नारकीणां रसज्ञानाय, D. vii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

panic
PANIC (subs.):<BR>I Sudden fright: सन्त्रासः: v.<BR>Terror, fear. Ph.: to be seized with p.:<BR>त्रस्यति, Ki. xv. 1.<BR>II A grass:<BR>(1) दूर्वा (= pani-<BR>-cum dactylon);<BR>(2) अणुः (= p. miliaceum).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

panic-struck
PANIC-STRUCK:<BR>(1) भयविप्लुत (f. ता), Ki. xiii.<BR>24. and sim. comp. s;<BR>(2) पिशाचोपहत (f. ता)<BR>इव, D. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pannel
PANNEL:<BR>I Rustic saddle: पर्याणम्।<BR>II Of a<BR>hawk: जठरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pannier
PANNIER: करण्डः, -कः: v. Basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

panoply
PANOPLY:<BR>(1) सर्वाङ्गवर्मन् (n. ?);<BR>(2) तनुत्रम्<BR>(= armour: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

panorama
PANORAMA: *विश्वदृश्यम्; better by circumlo.:<BR>v. View.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

panslavism
PANSLAVISM: *सर्वश्रावकसंयोगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pansy
PANSY: a plant and its flowers: *प्राणशी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pant
PANT:<BR>I To palpitate: वेपते (वेप्, c. 1.).<BR>II To breathe hard: विनिःश्वसिति (श्वस्, c.<BR>2.).<BR>III To long for: q. v.: स्पृहयति (स्पृह्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pantaloon
PANTALOON:<BR>I A buffoon: भण्डः।<BR>II A<BR>dress: *पान्थलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pantheism
PANTHEISM: *वैश्वदेवम्; विश्वदेवमतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pantheist
PANTHEIST: *विश्वदेविन् (f. नी); विश्वदेवमतः (ता,<BR> तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pantheistic
PANTHEISTIC, -AL: expr. by comp. or subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pantheon
PANTHEON: विश्वदेवकुलम् may be used in every<BR>sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

panther
PANTHER: perh. पुण्डरीकः (= leopard: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

panting
PANTING: (adj.):<BR>(1) विनिःश्वसत् (न्ती);<BR>(2)<BR>वेपमान (f. ना = quaking).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pantomime
PANTOMIME:<BR>I An actor: *मूकाभिनेतृ (f.<BR>त्री).<BR>II A representation: *मूकाभिनयः;<BR> लास्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pantomime
PANTOMIME, PANTOMIMIC (adj.): expr. by<BR>comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pantry
PANTRY: भाण्डारम् (?); खाद्यभाण्डारम् (?). N. B.<BR>In Hindu houses महानसम् (= cooking house)<BR>is also the p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pap
PAP:<BR>I A nipple: q. v.: स्तनः।<BR>II Soft<BR>food for boys: सिद्धचूर्णम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

papa
PAPA: तातः: v. Also father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

papacy
PAPACY: *पातृपदम्; पातृत्वम्: v. Pope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

papal
PAPAL: *पौप (पी, पं), पात्र्य (f. त्र्या), and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

papaw
PAPAW: अमृता (both the tree and its fruit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paper
PAPER (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: पत्रम् may be used,<BR>note-p.:<BR>लेखयपत्रम्।<BR>II Any document:<BR>पत्रम्: v. Writing.<BR>III A newspaper:<BR>*पत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paper
PAPER (v.): *पत्रैः आवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.) and<BR>sim. comp.s.: To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paper-hanger
PAPER-HANGER: *पत्रच्छादकः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paper-maker
PAPER-MAKER: *पत्रकारः; पत्रकृत्; etc.: v.<BR>Maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paper-money
PAPER-MONEY: *धनपत्रम्; टङ्कपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

papist
PAPIST: *पोपध्वजः (जा, जं); पातृध्वजः (जा, जं),<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

papistic
PAPISTIC, -AL: expr. by comp.: v. Also<BR>Popish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

papyrus
PAPYRUS: *पत्रजन्मन् (m.); पत्रवेणुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

par
PAR: समता,<BR>on p., at p.:<BR>समः (मा, मं): v.<BR>Equal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parable
PARABLE:<BR>(1) कथा (= story);<BR>(2) उपमा<BR>(= simile).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parabola
PARABOLA: *समान्तरक्षेत्रम्; अनुवृत्तम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parabolical
PARABOLICAL: expr. by comp. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parade
PARADE (subs.):<BR>I Ostentation, pomp:<BR>आडम्बरः।<BR>II Procession: यात्रा।<BR>III Mili-<BR>-tary: खुरली (?).<BR>IV P. -ground: खलूरिका<BR>(?), H. c.; व्यायामभूमिः, Ka. xvi. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parade
PARADE (v.): खुरलीं करोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parade
PARADE (v. t.):<BR>I Troops etc.: खुरलीं कारयति<BR>(c. of कृ) (?).<BR>II To display: सं-दर्शयति<BR>(c. of दृश्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paradism
PARADISM: रूपाणि (n. pl.)<BR>or<BR>रूपादर्शः, p. of verbs:<BR>धातुरूपादर्शः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paradise
PARADISE:<BR>I The garden: नन्दनम्।<BR>II<BR>Heaven: q. v.:<BR>(1) स्वर्गः;<BR>(2) वैकुण्ठम् (of<BR>Viṣṇu).<BR>Bird of p.:<BR>*नन्दनः; नन्दनखगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paradisiacal
PARADISIACAL: expr. by comp. or deriv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paradox
PARADOX: विरूद्धमतम् and sim. comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paradoxical
PARADOXICAL: विरूद्ध<BR>or<BR>लोकविरूद्ध (f. द्धा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paragon
PARAGON: i. e. model: आदर्शः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paragraph
PARAGRAPH: no. equiv.: परिच्छेदः may be<BR>used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paraleipsis
PARALEIPSIS: in rhetoric: आक्षेपः, Kav.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parallax
PARALLAX: in astro: लम्बनम्, p. in latitude:<BR>नतिः, Su. com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parallel
PARALLEL (adj.): In geo.: समान्तरः (रा, रं),<BR>K. d.<BR>II Fig.: similar: q. v.: सदृशः (शी,<BR> शं),<BR>p. passages:<BR>सदृशवाक्यानि (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parallel
PARALLEL (v.): exps. by adj.: v. Also to<BR>compare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parallel
PARALLEL (subs.):<BR>I A p. line: समान्तररेखा।<BR>P. of latitude:<BR>अक्षवृत्तम्।<BR>II Resemblance,<BR>likeness: q. v.: सादृश्यम्।<BR>III Equal, match:<BR>q. v.: समः (मा, मं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parallelism
PARALLELISM:<BR>I Of lines etc.: समान्तरता।<BR>II Resemblance: q. v.: सादृश्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parallelogram
PARALLELOGRAM: समानान्तरचतुर्भुजः, K. d.,<BR>*समान्तरक्षेत्रम् (after Li.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parallelepiped
PARALLELEPIPED: समान्तरखातः (after Li.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paralysis
PARALYSIS:<BR>(1) स्तम्भः,<BR>p. of the thigh:<BR>ऊरूस्तम्भः;<BR>(2) पक्षाघातः (= hemiplegia);<BR>(3) एकाङ्गवातः,<BR>Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paralytic
PARALYTIC: पक्षाधातिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp.s.: v. Above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paralyze
PARALYZE:<BR>I Lit.: स्तम्भं जनयति (c. of जन्):<BR>v. Above.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) स्तभ्नाति (स्तम्भ्,<BR>c. 9.);<BR>(2) जडीकरोति, Sa. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paramount
PARAMOUNT:<BR>(1) सर्वश्रेष्ठ (f. ष्ठा);<BR>(2) प्रधानतम<BR>(f. मा);<BR>(3) by circumlo. Ph.: p. power:<BR>अधीश्वरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paramour
PARAMOUR:<BR>I Male:<BR>(1) जारः;<BR>(2) उपपतिः।<BR>II Female: उपपत्नी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parapet
PARAPET: वक्षोदघ्नः प्राकारः; or gen. sim. प्राकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paraphernalia
PARAPHERNALIA:<BR>I Wife's: अध्यावहनिकम् (?),<BR>Mit.<BR>II In gen.: सामग्री।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paraphrase
PARAPHRASE (subs.): अनुवादः,<BR>this is p. of the<BR>preceding:<BR>पूर्वस्यायमनुवादः, K. b. on M. viii.<BR>350.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paraphrase
PARAPHRASE (v.): अनुवदति (वद्, c. 1., not<BR>translate as used in Bengali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parasite
PARASITE:<BR>I A diner-out: परान्नभोजिन् (f. नी)<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR>II A sycophant, flat-<BR>-terer: चाटुकारः।<BR>III An animal: *परप्राणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parasitic
PARASITIC, -AL: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parasol
PARASOL: छत्रिका: v. Umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parboil
PARBOIL: ईषत् साधयति (c. of सिध्), p. ed:<BR>ईषत्सिद्ध (f. द्धा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parcel
PARCEL (subs.):<BR>I A small bundle: पोटली-<BR>(लिका).<BR>II A portion: q. v. Ph.:<BR>“part and<BR>p. of it”:<BR>भुक्त (f. क्ता).<BR>III Of men: संघः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parcel out
PARCEL OUT (v.):<BR>(1) विभजति (भज्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) वण्टयति (वण्ट्, c. 10.): v. To divide (I),<BR>distribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parch
PARCH (v.):<BR>(1) दहति (दह्, c. 1. = to burn:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(2) तपति (तप्, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>तापयति (c. of<BR>तप् = to heat: q. v.). P. ed i. e. dry: q. v.:<BR>शुष्क (f. ष्का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parchment
PARCHMENT: *चर्मपत्रम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pardon
PARDON (subs.): क्षमा, touched the feet of the<BR>ascetic saying “I beg your p.”: (lit. forgive<BR>me): चरणौ तपोनिधेः क्षम्यतामिति वदन् समस्पृशत्, R.<BR>xi. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pardon
PARDON (v.): क्षमते (क्षम्, c. 1. = to forgive:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pardonable
PARDONABLE:<BR>(1) क्षन्तव्य (f. व्या);<BR>(2) मर्षणीय<BR>(f. या);<BR>(3) क्षमार्ह (f. र्हा); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pardonably
PARDONABLY: expr. by adj. or by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pardoning
PARDONING (adj.): क्षमाशील (f. ला) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pare
PARE (v.):<BR>I To clip, cut: q. v.: कल्पति<BR>(कॢप्, c. 1.).<BR>II To diminish: q. v.:<BR>तनूकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paregoric
PAREGORIC:<BR>(1) प्रशमनः (नी, नं);<BR>(2) शान्तिप्रद<BR>(f. दा) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parent
PARENT: 1. Father or mother: q. v.:<BR>with-<BR>out p. s.:<BR>पितृमातृवर्जितः (ता, तं), Mah. iv. 11.<BR>9.;<BR>p. s.:<BR>मातापितरौ, Mah.<BR>The P. s of the<BR>world:<BR>जगतः पितरौ, R.; (I) carried (them)<BR>to<BR>my p.s:<BR>मम पित्रोः सन्निधिमनैषम्, D. ii. Fig.:<BR>प्रसूतिः,<BR>p. of the Vedas:<BR>श्रुतीनां प्रसूतिः, Ki. iii.<BR>4.: v. Source.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parentage
PARENTAGE:<BR>(1) अन्वयः;<BR>(2) अन्ववायः;<BR>(3)<BR>अभिजनः,<BR>of good p.:<BR>अभिजनवत् (f. ती), Sa.<BR>iv.;<BR>(4) जन्मन् (n (= birth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parental
PARENTAL:<BR>(1) पितृमातृ- in comp.;<BR>(2) पैतृकः<BR>(की, कं), Da. 54. Ph.:<BR>p. affection:<BR>वात्सल्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parentally
PARENTALLY:<BR>(1) पितृमातृवत्;<BR>(2) मातापितराविव।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parenthesis
PARENTHESIS:<BR>I A sentence: निक्षिप्तवाक्यम् (?).<BR>II A sign: इति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parenthetical
PARENTHETICAL:<BR>(1) निक्षिप्त (f. प्ता) (?);<BR>(2)<BR>by adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parenthetically
PARENTHETICALLY:<BR>(1) निक्षिप्य (?);<BR>(2) निक्षेप-<BR>पूर्वकम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parhelion
PARHELION: मिथ्यासूर्यः and sim. comp. s (?):<BR>v. Sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pariah
PARIAH:<BR>p. s or p. dogs:<BR>ग्रामकुक्कुराः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paring
PARING (subs.):<BR>(1) कॢप्तम्;<BR>(2) छिन्नम्;<BR>(3) by<BR>adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parish
PARISH: no exact equiv. ग्रामः<BR>or<BR>आवसथः may<BR>be used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parishioner
PARISHIONER: ग्रामवासिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parity
PARITY:<BR>(1) साम्यम्;<BR>(2) सादृश्यम् (analogy);<BR>(3) better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

park
PARK:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) उपवनम्;<BR>(2) वनम्<BR>or<BR>काननम्<BR>(prop. =wood), N.;<BR>(3) आक्रीड (mn.), D.<BR>II Of objects: निकरः: v. Collection. Ph.:<BR>p. phaeton:<BR>*आक्रीडयानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

park-keeper
PARK-KEEPER:<BR>(1) उपवनरक्षितृ (m (?);<BR>(2)<BR>वनपालः, N. i. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parlance
PARLANCE: Ph.:<BR>in common p.:<BR>लौकिकभाषया (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parley
PARLEY:<BR>I Subs.: संवादः: v. Conference,<BR>conversation.<BR>II Verb: संवदति (वद्, c. 1.):<BR>v. Confer, converse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parliament
PARLIAMENT: *महासभा,<BR>members of p.:<BR>*महा-<BR>सभाधिष्ठिताः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parliamentary
PARLIAMENTARY: expr. by comp. or by gen.,<BR>p. procedure:<BR>महासभाव्यवहारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parlour
PARLOUR: *संलापकम्; संलापकोष्ठः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parochial
PAROCHIAL:<BR>(1) ग्राम्य (f. म्या ?);<BR>(2) आवसथ्य<BR>(f. थ्या ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parody
PARODY:<BR>I Subs. no equiv. *उपवादः।<BR>II<BR>Verb: *उपवदति (वद्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parol
PAROL,-E:<BR>I In law: उक्तिः,<BR>p. evidence:<BR>साक्षि-<BR>साक्ष्यम्।<BR>II Promise: q. v.: प्रतिज्ञा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paronomasia
PARONOMASIA: श्लेषः,<BR>paronomastically:<BR>श्लिष्टम्, N.<BR>xiv. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paroxysm
PAROXYSM:<BR>I Lit.: वेगः, when the p. is over:<BR>गतवेगेषु दोषेष, Bha.<BR>II Fig.: आवेशः,<BR>in a p.<BR>of rage:<BR>क्रोधावेशात्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parricidal
PARRICIDAL: by comp.,<BR>p. crime:<BR>पितृवधपातकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parricide
PARRICIDE:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) पितृहत्या;<BR>(2)<BR>पितृवधः।<BR>II The doer:<BR>(1) पितृहन् (mfn.);<BR>(2) पितृधातिन् (f. नी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parrot
PARROT:<BR>(1) शुकः;<BR>(2) कीरः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parry
PARRY: निवारयति (वृ, c. 10.): v. To prevent,<BR>avoid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parse
PARSE: *अन्वयविवृतिंकरोति। Parsing: *अन्वयविवृतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parsee
PARSEE: पारसीकः, R. (use पारसिकः for Persian).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parseeism
PARSEEISM: पारसीकधर्मः (?) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parsimonious
PARSIMONIOUS:<BR>(1) अल्पव्ययिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>कृपण (f. णा) (= miserly);<BR>(3) बद्धहस्त (f. स्ता)<BR>(= close-fisted).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parsimoniously
PARSIMONIOUSLY:<BR>(1) बद्धहस्तम्;<BR>(2) कार्पण्येन;<BR>(3) with कुण्ठितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parsimony
PARSIMONY:<BR>(1) अल्पव्ययः;<BR>(2) कार्पण्यम्;<BR>(3)<BR>बद्धहस्तता: v. Adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parsley
PARSLEY: a plant: *पार्श्वलः; शैलिन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parsnip
PARSNIP: a plant: *पौष्टिलकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parson
PARSON: याजकः (?); पुरोहितः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parsonage
PARSONAGE: याजककुलम् (?); पुरोहितावासः (?) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

part
PART (subs.):<BR>I Portion:<BR>(1) भागः,<BR>in the<BR>first p. of the day:<BR>दिवसस्याद्यभागे, Dak.;<BR>(2)<BR>अंशः,<BR>eighth p.:<BR>अष्टमांश, Viv.;<BR>(3) कला (of<BR>a whole),<BR>even the 100th p.:<BR>शततमीमपि कलाम्,<BR>D. ii.;<BR>(4) लवः (rare),<BR>fifth p.:<BR>पञ्चलवः, Li.<BR>Ph.:<BR>to divide into four, five p. s:<BR>चतुर्धा पञ्चधा<BR> करोति, S. k.<BR>II Of a book: अंशः, V. p.;<BR>भागः।<BR>III Region: q. v.: प्रदेशः,<BR>in this p. of<BR>the country:<BR>अस्मिन् प्रदेशे, K.<BR>IV. In gram.: p.<BR>of speech: no equiv.: शब्दभेदः may be<BR>used.<BR>V. Side, party: q. v.<BR>VI share:<BR>q. v.: अंशः।<BR>VII Allotted duty: कर्मन् (n.),<BR>will not do his p.:<BR>कर्म न करिष्यति, Si. xiv. 16.<BR>Ph.: it is the p. of: v. Should.<BR>VIII Con-<BR>-cern, interest: सङ्गः।<BR>IX Character: भूमिका,<BR>while acting the p. of Lakṣmī:<BR>लक्ष्मीभूमिकायां<BR> वर्तमाना, V. iii.;<BR>you have got up the first p. of<BR>Kāmandakī:<BR>कामन्दक्याः प्रथमभूमिकां भाव एवाधीते,<BR>Ma. i.<BR>X. In pl., p. s = qualities: शक्तिः।<BR>XI<BR>A member, an element: q. v.: अङ्गम्। Ph.:<BR>(a)<BR>for my p.:<BR>अहं तावत्; (b) for the most p.:<BR>प्रायशः; (c)<BR>in good p.:<BR>सानुरागम्<BR>or<BR>प्रीतमनसा;<BR>(d)<BR>in ill p.:<BR>विरक्त (f. क्ता); (e) in p.:<BR>अंशतः; (f)<BR>p. and parcel:<BR>प्रधानाङ्गम्; (g) on<BR>the p. of: v. For; (h)<BR>from all p. s:<BR>चतु-<BR>र्दिग्भ्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

part
PART (v. t.):<BR>I To divide, distribute: q. v.:<BR>विभजति (भज्, c. 1.).<BR>II To separate: q. v.:<BR>वियोजयति (c. of युज्).<BR>III Of the hair:<BR>सीमन्तयति (nomi.),<BR>whose thick mire had been<BR>p. ed by wheels:<BR>रथाङ्गसीमन्तितसान्द्रकर्दमान्, Ki.<BR>iv. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

part
PART (v. i.):<BR>I To p. with = leave: q. v.:<BR>त्यजति, परि-, (त्यज्, c. 1.).<BR>II To be separated: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">Page505</a>]<BR>q. v.: वियुज्यते (pass. of युज्).<BR>III To split:<BR>q. v.: विभज्यते (pass. of भज्).<BR>IV To bid<BR>farewell: expr. by circumlo., let me p.:<BR>अनुजानीहि मां गन्तुम्; they p. ed with bad grace:<BR>विनामन्त्रणेन स्वं स्वं गृहं प्रातिष्ठन्त।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

partake
PARTAKE (v.):<BR>I To have a share: expr.<BR>by adv.: अंशिन् (f. नी), भागिन् (f. नी), etc.<BR>II Of food etc.: भुंक्ते (भुज्, c. 7 (= enjoy<BR>with acc) भुंक्ष्व भोगान् मया सार्धम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

partaker
PARTAKER:<BR>(1) अंशिन् (f. नी = sharer: q. v.);<BR>(2) -भाज् (mfn.), in comp., p. of your distress:<BR>तव दुःखभाक्;<BR>(3) by comp.,<BR>your boon com-<BR>panions are equal p. s of your pleasures and<BR>pains:<BR>समदुःखसुखः सखीजनः, R. viii. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parterre
PARTERRE: पुष्पवाटिका and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parthenon
PARTHENON: *कृमारीकुलम्; सरस्वतीमन्दिरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

partial
PARTIAL:<BR>I Not total:<BR>(1) आंशिक (f. की),<BR>p. eclipse:<BR>आंशिकग्रासः, Su. comp.;<BR>(2) क्वचित्<BR> क्वचित् (= in some places, as of p. rain).<BR>II<BR>Biased: पक्षपातिन् (f. नी),<BR>even gods are p.<BR>to the Pāṇḍavas:<BR>पक्षपातिनो देवाऽपि पाण्डवानाम्,<BR>Va.: v. Also unfair, unjust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

partiality
PARTIALITY:<BR>I Undue bias: पक्षपातः<BR>or<BR>-पातिता:<BR>v. Also unfairness.<BR>II Special fondness:<BR>आग्रहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

partially
PARTIALLY:<BR>I Partly, somewhat: q. v.:<BR>(1) अंशतः;<BR>(2) असमग्र- and sim. expr. s in<BR>comp.<BR>II With undue bias:<BR>(1) सपक्षपातम्;<BR>(2) by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

participant
PARTICIPANT: -भाज् (mfn.) in comp.: v.<BR>Partake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

participate
PARTICIPATE: expr. by अंशिन् (f. नी): v.<BR>Partake, -r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

participation
PARTICIPATION:<BR>(1) भोगः (= enjoyment);<BR>(2) better by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

participator
PARTICIPATOR: -भाज् (mfn.) in comp.: v.<BR>Partaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

participial
PARTICIPIAL: expr. by comp. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

participle
PARTICIPLE:<BR>(1) सत् (present p.);<BR>(2) निष्ठा<BR>(past p.); etc.: v. Grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

particle
PARTICLE:<BR>I A minute portion:<BR>(1) कणः;<BR>(2)<BR>कणिका;<BR>(3) अणुः।<BR>II In gram.:<BR>(1) निपातः;<BR>(2) अव्यय (mn. = indeclinable p.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parti-coloured
PARTI-COLOURED:<BR>(1) चित्रविचित्र (f. त्रा);<BR>(2)<BR>नानारङ्ग (f. ङ्गा) and sim. comp.s. (= of many<BR>colours);<BR>(3) कल्माषित (f. ता = variegated).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

particular
PARTICULAR (adj.):<BR>I Not common, singu-<BR>-lar, special:<BR>(1) विशेष- in comp.; p. news:<BR>विशेषवार्त्ता;<BR>p. grant:<BR>विशेषदानम्, He.;<BR>(2) विशिष्ट<BR>(f. ष्टा);<BR>p. mark:<BR>विशिष्टलिङ्गम्।<BR>II Specifiable,<BR>definite: -विशेषः in comp., at p. times:<BR>कालविशेषे;<BR>to p. individuals:<BR>व्यक्तिविशेषेषु, M. n.<BR>on Ku. v. 31.<BR>III Minute: q. v.: सूक्ष्म (f.<BR>क्ष्मा).<BR>IV Hard to suit, punctilious: expr.<BR>by circumlo.,<BR>very p. in dress:<BR>*वेशभूषायां<BR> महादरः। V. Single, individual: not expr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

particular
PARTICULAR (subs.):<BR>in p.:<BR>विशेषतः;<BR>p. s of a<BR>story:<BR>घटनावली (better expr. with विस्तरशः =<BR>in detail);<BR>“for his p.”:<BR>विशिष्टतया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

particularity
PARTICULARITY:<BR>I Lit.: विशिष्टता।<BR>II Detail:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

particularize
PARTICULARIZE: सविशेषं कथयति (कथ्, c. 10.) or<BR>वर्णयति (वर्ण्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

particularly
PARTICULARLY:<BR>I In detail:<BR>(1) विस्तरेण;<BR>(2) विस्तरशः।<BR>II Especially:<BR>(1) विशेषेण;<BR>(2) विशिष्य, N. i. 131.;<BR>(3) विशेषतः, He.: v.<BR>Also chiefly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parting
PARTING (subs.): वियोगः: v. Separation,<BR>departure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

partisan
PARTISAN:<BR>I Of a party: q. v.:<BR>(1) पक्षीयः<BR>(या, यं);<BR>(2) पक्षस्थ (f. स्था).<BR>II A staff:<BR>q. v.: ऋष्टिः, Nil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

partisanship
PARTISANSHIP: पक्षपातिता<BR>or<BR>पक्षपातः, “पक्षपातकृत-<BR>स्नेहः,” Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

partition
PARTITION (subs.):<BR>I In law: विभागः,<BR>deed<BR>of p.:<BR>विभागपत्रम्, Vri.<BR>or<BR>भागलेख्यम्, Da.<BR>II<BR>Division, separation: q. v.: परिच्छेदः।<BR>III<BR>That which separates: व्यवच्छेदिका भूः, Mit.<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR>IV A compartment:<BR>कोष्ठः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

partition
PARTITION (v.): विभजति (भज्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

partitive
PARTITIVE: अंशद्योतक (f. तिका) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

partly
PARTLY:<BR>(1) अंशतः;<BR>(2) with adj. अंशिकः (की,<BR> कं): v. Little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

partner
PARTNER:<BR>I In business:<BR>(1) सम्भूयकारिन् (f.<BR>णी),<BR>by all the p.s:<BR>सम्भूयकारिभिः सर्वैः, Mit.;<BR>(2) सहकारिन् (f. णी), Viv.;<BR>(3) समवायिन् (f.<BR>नी), Vri.<BR>II In matrimony: v. Consort.<BR>III A partaker, sharer: q. v.: समदुःखसुखः<BR> सखीजनः, R. viii. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

partnership
PARTNERSHIP: In business:<BR>(1) सम्भूयसमुत्थानम्,<BR>M.;<BR>(2) सहक्रिया, Vri. N. B. In arith. मिश्रक-<BR>व्यवहारः includes p., Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

partridge
PARTRIDGE:<BR>(1) तित्तिरः (रिः) (= francolin<BR>p.);<BR>(2) चकोरः (= Greek p.);<BR>(3) कृकणः<BR>(= sylvan p.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parturition
PARTURITION: प्रजननम्: v. Also delivery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

party
PARTY:<BR>I A faction: an assembly: पक्षः,<BR>the p. of the bridegroom:<BR>वरपक्षः, R. vi. 86.;<BR>because he is of Prahāravarmā's p.:<BR>प्रहारवर्मणः<BR> पक्ष इति, D. iii.; by the Bhojas of Akrūras p.:<BR>अक्रूरपक्षीयैर्भोजैः, V. p. iv. 13. 52.<BR>II In law:<BR>पक्षः,<BR>opposite p.:<BR>प्रतिपक्षः, Mit.; the first p.:<BR>पूर्वपक्षः, Y. ii. 17.<BR>III Social: expr. with<BR>भोजनम्<BR>or<BR>भोजयति: v. To feed.<BR>IV Mili-<BR>-tary: दलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

party-coloured
PARTY-COLOURED: v. Parti-coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

party-spirit
PARTY-SPIRIT: perh. पक्षपातिता<BR>or<BR>पक्षानुरागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

party-wall
PARTY-WALL: सीमाभित्तिः (?); सीमाकुड्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

parvenu
PARVENU: expr. with नवः (वा, वं): v. New,<BR>upstart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pasha
PASHA:<BR>(1) राजन् (= king); भोगपतिः ( gover-<BR>-nor).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pasquinade
PASQUINADE: कौलीनगीतम् (??) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pass
PASS (v. t.):<BR>I To go beyond:<BR>(1) अतिक्रामति<BR>or<BR>क्राम्यति (क्रम्, c. 1. and 4.);<BR>(2) अत्येति (इ,<BR>c 2.);<BR>(3) लङ्घते, उत्-, वि-, (लङ्घ्, c. 1.),<BR>p.<BR>ing Lahore the Turks reached their encamp-<BR>ment:<BR>उल्लङ्घ्य लोहरं प्रापुस्तुरस्काः स्वनिवेशनम्, Raj.;<BR>(4) तरति, उत्- (तॄ, c. 1.) (= to cross),<BR>p. ing the<BR>next road:<BR>तत्परं वर्त्म तीर्णः, Me. i. 19.<BR>II To<BR>surpass: q. v.<BR>III To spend time:<BR>(1)<BR>गमयति (c. of गम्),<BR>even Śiva p. ed those days<BR>with difficulty:<BR>पशुपतिरपि तान्यहानि कृच्छ्रादगमयत्,<BR>Ku. vi. 95.;<BR>(2) यापयति (c. of या), Me. ii.<BR>28.;<BR>(3) नयति (नी, c. 1.),<BR>the night was<BR>p. ed as a moment:<BR>नीता रात्रिः क्षण इव॥, Me.;<BR>(4) वाहयति, अति-, (c. of वह्), p. ing one night:<BR>रात्रिमेकामतिवाह्य, B. r.;<BR>(5) वसति, वि-, (वस्,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>p. ed that night:<BR>ऊषुस्तां रजनीम्, Mah.;<BR>(6) क्षपयति (c. of क्षी),<BR>p. ed the night as if<BR>in a moment:<BR>क्षणादिव क्षणदां क्षपितवती, K.<BR>IV. To send on: q. v.: प्रापयति (c. of आप्).<BR>V To utter: q. v.: उदीरयति (ईर्, c. 10.).<BR>VI To care: q. v.<BR>VII To put in circu-<BR>-lation:<BR>(1) चालयति, सं-, (c. of चल्);<BR>(2)<BR>चारयति सं-, (c. of चर्).<BR>VIII To carry on,<BR>ratify, as accounts, laws: *संसाधयति (c. of<BR>सिध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pass
PASS (v. i.):<BR>I Of time:<BR>(1) गच्छति (गम्, c.<BR>1.);<BR>(2) याति (या, c. 2.): v. Also p.<BR>away.<BR>II To go, move: q. v.: चलति (चल्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>III To become changed: expr.<BR>by भवति (= to become).<BR>IV To be cur-<BR>-rent:<BR>(1) चलति, प्र-;<BR>(2) by adj.: प्रचलः<BR>(ला, लं)<BR>or<BR>प्रचलितः (f. ता).<BR>V To occur,<BR>happen: q. v.<BR>VI To surpass: q. v.<BR>VII<BR>To be enacted: *सिध्यति (सिध्, c. 4.) or<BR>सिद्धीभवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pass away
PASS AWAY:<BR>(1) विगच्छति,<BR>whose life had then<BR>p. ed a.:<BR>तत्क्षणविगतजीवित (f. ता), K.;<BR>(2) वियाति<BR>(rare),<BR>and the night p. ed a.:<BR>विभावरी च<BR> व्ययासीत्, D. v.;<BR>(3) व्यत्येति (इ, c. 2.),<BR>thrice<BR>seven days p. ed a.:<BR>त्रिगुणानि सप्तदिनानि व्यतीयुः,<BR>R. ii. 25.: v. Also to elapse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pass by
PASS BY:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by अतिक्रामति<BR>or<BR>अत्येति<BR>and words signifying near,<BR>although you p.<BR>by (me), you do not cast a look:<BR>समीपेऽप्यति-<BR>क्रामन्तीतो दृष्टिं न ददासि, Mal. i.<BR>II Of time:<BR>अत्योति (इ, c. 2.): v. Pass away.<BR>III To<BR>pass over, omit: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pass for
PASS FOR:<BR>(1) by nomi.,<BR>even a castor-oil plant<BR>p. es for a tree:<BR>एरण्डोऽपि द्रुमायते, H.;<BR>(2) by<BR>circumlo.,<BR>he p. es for a learned man:<BR>तं पण्डितं<BR> मन्यन्ते।: v. To think.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pass off
PASS OFF:<BR>I To go away: q. v.: अपैति (इ,<BR>c. 2.).<BR>II To palm, impose: भावयति (c.<BR>of भू), D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pass on
PASS ON: प्रयाति (या, c. 2.): v. To proceed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pass over
PASS OVER:<BR>I To cross over: अतिक्रम्य गच्छति [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">Page507</a>]<BR>(गम्, c. 1.), etc.,<BR>II To go over (III): q. v.<BR>III To omit, neglect: आ-क्षिपति, उत्-,<BR>(क्षिप्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pass round
PASS ROUND: अपरान् etc. (= other) प्रापयति<BR>(c. of आप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pass through
PASS THROUGH: भित्त्वा निष्क्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1. = to<BR>come out).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pass
PASS, BRING TO:<BR>(1) घटयति (c. of घट्);<BR>(2) आव-<BR>हति (वह्, c. 1. = to bring).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pass
PASS (subs.):<BR>I A narrow and difficult<BR>way:<BR>(1) कान्तारः;<BR>(2) रन्घ्रम् (mountain p.).<BR>II Passport: q. v.<BR>III Condition: दशा।<BR>IV A thrust or push: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passable
PASSABLE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>the road is not p.:<BR>अगम्योऽयं<BR> पन्थाः;<BR>the stream is p. by boats:<BR>नौतार्येयं सरित्:<BR>v. To pass.<BR>II Current: q. v.: प्रचलः (ला,<BR> लं),<BR>III Mediocre, middling: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passably
PASSABLY: expr. by adj.,<BR>not even p. acquainted<BR>with medicine:<BR>*सामान्यमपि वैद्यकज्ञानं न वर्तते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passage
PASSAGE: The act:<BR>(1) गमनम् (= going);<BR>(2) तरणम् (= crossing);<BR>(3) अतिक्रमः (= 2):<BR>v. To pass. Ph.:<BR>p. to and fro:<BR>यातायातम्;<BR>to effect a p.:<BR>यात्रां करोति: v. To march.<BR>II In vessels:<BR>p. money:<BR>तारिकम्<BR>or<BR>तरपण्यम्;<BR>to take p. in so and so:<BR>अमुकपोतेन यात्रां स्थिरीकरोति<BR>(?).<BR>III Way, road: q. v.: मार्गः।<BR>IV Of<BR>a book:<BR>(1) वचनम्;<BR>(2) स्थलम् (= place).<BR>V. Event: घटना।<BR>VI Reception, currency:<BR>प्रचारः। Ph.:<BR>birds of p,:<BR>*अनवस्थितस्थितयः<BR> पक्षिणः;<BR>p. at arms:<BR>*समर्दो बाहूबाहवि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passenger
PASSENGER:<BR>(1) यात्रिक (f. की);<BR>(2) यात्रिन्<BR>(f. णी);<BR>(3) यायिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passer-by
PASSER-BY:<BR>(1) पथिकः,<BR>by female p.s-by:<BR>पथिक-<BR>वधूमिः, Ma. n. iii. 17.;<BR>(2) पान्थः;<BR>(3) यायिन्<BR>(= passer).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passing
PASSING (adj.): अतिशय- in comp.: v. Exces-<BR>-sive, great.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passing
PASSING (adv.): अतिशय- in comp., p. beautiful:<BR>अतिशयसुन्दर (f. री);<BR>p. shrewdly:<BR>अतिशय-<BR>वैदग्ध्येन: v. Exceedingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passing-bell
PASSING-BELL: मरणघण्टा and sim. comp.s. (?):<BR>v. Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passion
PASSION:<BR>I As opposed to action<BR>I क्रिया (?).<BR>II Endurance, sufferance: q. v.: Ph.:<BR>p. week:<BR>*यातनासप्ताहम् and sim. comp.s.<BR>III Sensual desire:<BR>(1) अभिलाषः,<BR>had p. for<BR>his own daughter:<BR>स्वसुतायामभिलाषमकरोत्, K.;<BR>(2)<BR>कामः,<BR>p. considers (all) itself:<BR>कामः स्वतां पश्यति,<BR>Sa. iii. 2.;<BR>p. never subsides by enjoyment of<BR>pleasures:<BR>न जातु कामः कामानामुपभोगेन शाम्यति,<BR>H.<BR>IV. Rage: q. v.: संरम्भः, roused her p.:<BR>तां संरम्भं निनाय, R.<BR>V. Great fondness for:<BR>व्यसनम्,<BR>p. for living at Kailāsa:<BR>कैलासनिवास-<BR>व्यसनम्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passionate
PASSIONATE:<BR>I Fervent, earnest:<BR>(1) साग्रह<BR>(f. हा);<BR>(2) आत्यन्तिक (f. की) (= exces-<BR>-sive);<BR>(3) गाढ, प्र-, (f. ढा = deep).<BR>II Easily<BR>excited:<BR>(1) क्रीधन (f. ना);<BR>(2) चण्डप्रकृति<BR>(mfn.) and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Lustful:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passionately
PASSIONATELY:<BR>I Fervently:<BR>(3) गाढम्, प्र-,<BR>(= deeply);<BR>(2) एकान्तम् (= exceedingly);<BR>(3) परमम् (= 2).<BR>II With anger;<BR>(1) सरोषम्;<BR>(2) सकोपम्: v. Angrily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passionateness
PASSIONATENESS:<BR>I Insensibility:<BR>(1) क्रोध-<BR>शीलता;<BR>(2) चण्डप्रकृतिः and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Lust: कामिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passionless
PASSIONLESS:<BR>(1) विरक्त (f. क्ता: rare);<BR>(2) राग-<BR>हीन (f. ना);<BR>(3) वीतस्पृह (f. हा), Ki. iii. 12;<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passive
PASSIVE:<BR>I In gram:<BR>p. voice:<BR>कर्मवाच्यम्;<BR>in<BR>the p. voice:<BR>कर्मणि;<BR>on p. verbs:<BR>कर्मतिङ्प्रक्रिया,<BR>S. k.;<BR>in the reflective p. voice:<BR>कर्मकर्तरि, S. k.<BR>II Not active: expr. by सहते (सह्, c. 1.<BR>= to bear)<BR>or<BR>क्रियते (pass. of कृ); p. agent:<BR>कर्माधारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passively
PASSIVELY: In gram. कर्मणि (loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passiveness
PASSIVENESS, PASSIVITY:<BR>(1) सहिष्णुता (= pati-<BR>-ence);<BR>(2) निश्चेष्टता (= inactivity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passover
PASSOVER: A Jewish feast: *अभिक्रमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

passport
PASSPORT:<BR>Without a p.:<BR>अमुद्रालाञ्छितः, Mu. v.;<BR>I will take a. p. from Bhāgurāyaṇa:<BR>अहमपि<BR> भागुरायणाद् मुद्रां प्रतीच्छामि, Mu. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

password
PASSWORD: गमनादेशः and sim. comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

past
PAST (adj.):<BR>(1) गत (f. ता),<BR>p. year:<BR>गतवर्षम्;<BR>(2) अतीत (f. ता). Ph.:<BR>p. tense:<BR>भूतकालः, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">Page508</a>]<BR>in remote p.:<BR>भूतेऽनद्यतने, S. k.; m p. times:<BR>पुरा: v. Formerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

past
PAST (subs.):<BR>(1) भूतम्,<BR>the lord of the p., the<BR>future, and the present:<BR>भूतमव्यभवदीशः, Ki. xii.<BR>19.; (2). अतीतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

past
PAST (= prep.):<BR>p. the time:<BR>अतीतकालः, R. v.<BR>14.: v. After;<BR>p. the house:<BR>गृहमतिक्रम्य: v.<BR>Beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paste
PASTE (subs.):<BR>(1) विलेपी, Bha.;<BR>(2) उदपेषः<BR>(?: उदपेषम् of Pāṇini vi. 3. 58. is an adv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paste
PASTE (v.):<BR>(1) लिम्पति, वि-, (लिप्, c. 6.);<BR>(2) सर्जयति, सं-, (c. of सृज्). P. ed with wax:<BR>मधूच्छिष्टस्थित (f. ता), Mah. iii. 308. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paste-board
PASTE-BOARD: *संसृष्टपत्रम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pastern
PASTERN: of a horse: गुल्फः (= ankle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pastime
PASTIME:<BR>(1) विनोदः (= amusement);<BR>(2) क्रीडा<BR>(= play, sport: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pastor
PASTOR:<BR>I Shepherd: q. v.:<BR>II Religious:<BR>आचार्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pastoral
PASTORAL:<BR>I Adj.:<BR>p. life:<BR>अविपालत्वम्;<BR>p.<BR>poem:<BR>*गोपकाव्यम्;<BR>p. duties:<BR>धर्मकार्याणि;<BR>p.<BR>office:<BR>आचार्यकर्मन् (n.) and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Subs.: *गोपकाव्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pastry
PASTRY:<BR>(1) पिष्टकाः (m. pl.);<BR>(2) आपूपिकम्;<BR>(3) मिष्टान्नम् (= sweetmeats)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pastry-cook
PASTRY-COOK:<BR>(1) आपूपिकः;<BR>(2) पिष्टककारः and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pasturage
PASTURAGE:<BR>I Grazing ground: प्रचारभूमिः,<BR>V. p. com. and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Grazing<BR>for cattle: perh. चारः (comp. Beng. चारा);<BR>यवस (mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pasture
PASTURE (subs.):<BR>(1) यवस (mn.);<BR>(2) शाद्वलम्,<BR>with abundant water and p.:<BR>पर्याप्तजलशाद्वलम्,<BR>Ka. xiv. 30.: v. Pasturage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pasture
PASTURE (v.): चरति (चर्, c. 1.).: v. To<BR>graze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pasty
PASTY (subs.): no equiv.: *मांसापूपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pat
PAT:<BR>I Adj.: सङ्गत (f. ता): v. Also fit.<BR>II Verb: हस्तेन स्पृशति (स्पृश्, c. 6.),<BR>Indra<BR>p. ted his body:<BR>हस्तेन पस्पर्श तदङ्गमिन्द्रः, Ku.<BR>iii. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patch
PATCH (v.):<BR>(1) संग्रथ्नाति (ग्रन्थ्, c. 1.),<BR>eagerly<BR>engaged in p. ing old nets:<BR>जीर्णवागुरासंग्रथनव्यग्रैः,<BR>K.;<BR>(2) perh. संविदधाति<BR>or<BR>-धत्ते (धा, c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patch
PATCH (subs.):<BR>I Of cloth: ग्रथितखण्डम् (?);<BR>perh. युक्तम् (comp. Beng. योडा).<BR>II In<BR>gen.: खण्ड (mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patchwork
PATCHWORK: संग्रथनम्: v. To patch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pate
PATE: मुण्डम्: v. Head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paten
PATEN, PATIN: पात्रम्: v. Plate, vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patent
PATENT (adj.):<BR>I Plain, clear: q. v.: स्पष्ट<BR>(f. ष्टा).<BR>II Specially licensed: *मुद्रितः<BR>(ता, तं), Ph.:<BR>letters p.:<BR>*सार्वलौकिकपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patent
PATENT (subs.): *मुद्रा; असामान्याधिकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patentee
PATENTEE: *मुद्राधारिन् (f. णी); असामान्याधि-<BR>कारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paternal
PATERNAL:<BR>I Pertaining to or derived from<BR>a father:<BR>(1) पितृ- in comp.;<BR>(2) पैतृकः (की,<BR> कं),<BR>p. debt:<BR>पैतृकमृणम्, Da.;<BR>(3) पित्र्य (f. त्र्या),<BR>p. share:<BR>पित्र्योऽशः, R. xi. 64.<BR>II Like<BR>a father: v. Fatherly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paternally
PATERNALLY:<BR>(1) पितृवत्;<BR>(2) पितेव।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paternity
PATERNITY:<BR>I Lit.: पितृत्वम्।<BR>II Fig.: expr.<BR>with प्रसूतिः: v. Origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

path
PATH: पन्थाः (पथिन्),<BR>I did not mark the p. in<BR>this thick wood:<BR>न मया महावने पन्था निरूपितः,<BR>K.;<BR>wrong p.:<BR>अपथः, R. ix. 74.: v. Way;<BR>footpath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pathetic
PATHETIC:<BR>(1) करूण (f. णा);<BR>(2) कारूणिकः (की,<BR> कं) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pathetically
PATHETICALLY:<BR>(1) करूणम्, Ki.;<BR>(2) करूणार्थ-<BR>ग्रथितम् (poet.), R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pathless
PATHLESS: निष्पथः (था, थं) and sim. comp.s.:<BR>v. Also inaccessible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pathology
PATHOLOGY:<BR>(1) निदानम्;<BR>(2) रोगाणां विज्ञानम्, Ni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pathos
PATHOS: करणो रसः, U. iii. 46.; करूणा-<BR>or<BR>कारूण्य-<BR>रसः, N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pathway
PATHWAY: संसरणम्: v. Path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patience
PATIENCE:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) क्षमा;<BR>(2) तितिक्षा;<BR>(3) सहिष्णुता।<BR>II Perseverance: अभियोगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patient
PATIENT (adj.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) क्षमिन् (f.<BR>णी);<BR>(2) तितिक्षु (mfn.);<BR>(3) सहिष्णु (mfn.);<BR>(4) क्षमायुक्त (f. क्ता) and sim. comp.s.<BR>II<BR>Not hasty: धीरः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patient
PATIENT (subs.): रोगिन् (f. णी), in-p.:<BR>अन्तःस्थरोगिन्;<BR>out-p.:<BR>*बहिःस्थरोगिन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patiently
PATIENTLY: धैर्येण: v. Also calmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patois
PATOIS:<BR>(1) ग्राम्यभाषा (comp., Kav. vii. 3.);<BR>(2) म्लेच्छितम् (in contempt), Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patriarch
PATRIARCH:<BR>(1) कृलपतिः, Sa.;<BR>(2) प्रजापतिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patriarchal
PATRIARCHAL: expr. by comp. or gen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patrician
PATRICIAN:<BR>(1) कुलीनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) अभिजात<BR>(f. ता): v. Noble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patrimony
PATRIMONY: पैतृकमृक्थम् and sim. comp. s:<BR>v. Inheritance, property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patriot
PATRIOT:<BR>(1) स्वदेशानुरागिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) मातृ-<BR>भूम्यभिमानिन् (f. नी); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patriotic
PATRIOTIC: expr. by circumlo., p. zeal:<BR>स्वदेशहिताग्रहः;<BR>p. sentiments:<BR>*स्वदेशनिष्ठानि<BR> मतानि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patriotically
PATRIOTICALLY:<BR>(1) स्वदेशानुरागात्;<BR>(2) स्वदेश-<BR>हितेच्छया; and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patriotism
PATRIOTISM:<BR>(1) स्वदेशानुरागिता;<BR>(2) जन्मभूमि-<BR>हितैषिता; and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patrol
PATROL (subs.):<BR>I The act: रात्रिचर्या (?);<BR>निशापरिक्रमः (?).<BR>II The men:<BR>(1) रक्षिणः<BR>(m. pl.);<BR>(2) आरक्षकवर्गः; and sim. comp.s.<BR>Ph.:<BR>town p.:<BR>नागरिकबलम्, D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patrol
PATROL (v.): रात्रौ परिक्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.) or<BR>परिपश्यति (दृश्, c. 1 (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patron
PATRON, PATRONESS: I. In law: स्वामिन् (f.<BR>नी).<BR>II Protector, supporter:<BR>(1) आश्रयः<BR>(= refuge),<BR>p. of wits:<BR>आश्रयो रसिकानाम्, K.;<BR>(2) सम्भावयितृ (f. त्री), p. of the learned:<BR>सम्भावयिता बुद्धान्, D. viii.;<BR>(3) अनुपालयितृ (f.<BR>त्री); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patronage
PATRONAGE:<BR>(1) साहाय्यम् (= aid);<BR>(2) आनु-<BR>कूल्यम् (= favour);<BR>(3) सम्भावना (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patronize
PATRONIZE:<BR>(1) संवर्धयति (c. of वृध् = to<BR>advance);<BR>(2) अनुकूलयति (nomi = favour);<BR>(3) संभावयति (c. of भू = to honour).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patronless
PATRONLESS:<BR>(1) निराश्रय (f. या);<BR>(2) असहाय<BR>(f. या); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patronymic
PATRONYMIC:<BR>I In gram.: p. affixes:<BR>अपत्ये<BR>or<BR>अपत्यार्थे प्रत्ययाः, S.k.<BR>II Surname:<BR>पैतृकनामन् (n.); गोत्रनामन् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patten
PATTEN (subs.): काष्ठपादुका and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patter
PATTER (v.): Intrans.: पटपटायते (nomi.).<BR>II<BR>Trans.: सिञ्चति (सिच्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

patter
PATTER (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: पटपटाशब्दः।<BR>II A<BR>discourse: जल्पितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pattern
PATTERN:<BR>I Lit.: आदर्शः।<BR>II Style of cloth<BR>etc.: perh. धरणम्।<BR>III A full specimen,<BR>as of dress: प्रतिकृतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paucity
PAUCITY:<BR>(1) स्वल्पता;<BR>(2) by adj.: v.<BR>Few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paunch
PAUNCH (subs.): पिचिण्डः: v. Belly.<BR>Having<BR>a p.:<BR>पिचिण्डिल (f. ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paunch
PAUNCH (v.):<BR>(1) निस्तुन्दीकरोति (?);<BR>(2) निरन्त्री-<BR>करोति; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pauper
PAUPER:<BR>(1) अकिञ्चनः (ना, नं): v. Poor;<BR>(2) भिक्षुः, -कः (f. की = beggar);<BR>(3) अनाथ<BR>(f. था = without protector).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pauperism
PAUPERISM:<BR>(1) दारिद्र्यम् ( poverty):<BR>(2)<BR>भिक्षावृत्तिः (= begging);<BR>(3) अनाथता (= with-<BR>-out protection).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pause
PAUSE (subs.):<BR>(1) विरामः (in every sense),<BR>low at p. s:<BR>विरामे मृदुम्, Mr. iii. 5.;<BR>(2) यतिः<BR>(in poetry): v. Also cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pause
PAUSE (v.): विरमति (रम्, c. 1.): v. To cease,<BR>stop,<BR>p. upon:<BR>संचिन्तयति (चिन्त्, c. 10.):<BR>v. To consider, think about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pave
PAVE (v.) प्रस्तरैः (stones)<BR>or<BR>इष्टकाभिः (bricks)<BR>खचयति (खच्, c. 10.),<BR>p. d:<BR>उपलखचित (f. ता),<BR>etc.;<BR>p. d resting places:<BR>इष्टकाखचितविश्रामाः, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pavement
PAVEMENT: इष्टकाखचितभूमिः and sim. comp.s.;<BR>कुट्टिमम्, R. xi. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paver
PAVER, PAVIOR: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pavilion
PAVILION: मण्डप (mn.), “प्रतीहारीमण्डलाधिष्ठित-<BR>पुरोभागं श्रीमण्डपं ददर्श”, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paw
PAW (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पादः;<BR>(2) नखानि<BR>(= nails) may be often used.<BR>II Hand:<BR>q. v. हस्तः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

paw
PAW (v.):<BR>I Intrans: (खुरेण) भूमिम् अभिहन्ति<BR>(हन्, c. 2.).<BR>II Trans: पादेन etc., परामृशति<BR>(मृश्, c. 6.): v. Also to handle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pawn
PAWN (subs.):<BR>I Pledge, mortgage: q. v.:<BR>आधिः।<BR>II Pan (II): q. v.<BR>III In chess:<BR>शारः (रिः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pawn
PAWN (v.):<BR>(1) आदधाति (धा, c. 3.);<BR>(2)<BR>आधीकरोति;<BR>(3) बन्धे ददाति (दा, c. 3.) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pawnbroker
PAWNBROKER: आधिग्रहीतृ (f. त्री) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pay
PAY (v. t.):<BR>I To discharge a debt: q. v.:<BR>ददाति<BR>or<BR>दत्ते (दा, c. 3.),<BR>to p. interest:<BR>वृद्धिं<BR> ददाति, Kat.;<BR>to p. a debt:<BR>ऋणं ददाति, M.<BR>II. To give p.: वेतनं ददाति (दा, c. 3.: with<BR>dat.), Viv.<BR>III In gen.: भूल्यं ददाति,<BR>if a<BR>master discharges a servant before time, he shall<BR>p. him fully:<BR>स्वामी चेद् भृतकमपूर्णे काले जह्यात् तस्य<BR> सकलमेव मूल्यं दद्यात्। Viv.; after being paid:<BR>मूल्यमादाय, Mat.<BR>IV To revenge: शोधयति,<BR> परिशोधयति (c. of शुध्).<BR>V To perform:<BR>करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pay back
PAY BACK: प्रतिददाति (दा, c. 3.): v. To pay,<BR>return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pay for
PAY FOR: Ph.:<BR>I have paid f. it:<BR>अस्य भूल्यं<BR> मया दत्तम्;<BR>you will p. your life f. it:<BR>*एतन्निमित्तं<BR> जीवनं हारयसि<BR>or<BR>जीवनदानेनास्य निष्कृतिं गमिष्यसि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pay off
PAY OFF: v. To pay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pay
PAY (subs.):<BR>(1) वेतनम्,<BR>after taking p.:<BR>गृहीत-<BR>वेतनः, Vri.;<BR>the p. settled:<BR>कृतवेतनम्, Viv.;<BR>(2) भृतिः (prop. maintenance),<BR>he is entitled<BR>to half the p.:<BR>भृतेरर्धं लभेत सः, Vriddha Manu;<BR>(3) मूल्यम् (prop. price),<BR>shall p. his whole<BR>p.:<BR>सर्वमेव मूल्यं दद्यात्, Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

payable
PAYABLE:<BR>(1) देय (f. या), प्र-,<BR>is p. to the<BR>master:<BR>तत्स्वामिने देयम्, Mit.;<BR>is p. although<BR>the (whole) journey may not be over:<BR>अगतस्यापि<BR> देयं स्यात्, Viv.;<BR>(2) परिशोध्य (f. ध्या: of<BR>debts).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

payee
PAYEE (subs.): ग्रहीतृ (f. त्री), परि-, (= re-<BR>-ceiver).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

payer
PAYER:<BR>(1) दातृ (f. त्री), प्र-;<BR>(2) often by<BR>verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

payment
PAYMENT:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) दानम्;<BR>(2)<BR>परिशोधः, -नम्; (of debts).<BR>II Requital:<BR>q. v.: परिशोधः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pay-office
PAY-OFFICE: *ऋणशोधकुलम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pea
PEA:<BR>(1) कलायः, He. (now gen. applied to<BR>Phaseolus radiatus);<BR>(2) सतिनः, -कः;<BR>(3)<BR>सतिलः (ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peace
PEACE (interj.^1): शान्तम्: v. Silence, silent.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peace
PEACE (subs.):<BR>(1) शमः, it is very difficult to<BR>make p. with such persons:<BR>तादृशेन शमः परमदुष्करः,<BR>Mah. v. 74. 5.; let there be p. among you:<BR>शमोऽस्तु भवताम्, Vi. v. 55.;<BR>(2) शान्तिः,<BR>as<BR>there may be p. among the Kurus:<BR>यथा यथैव<BR> शान्तिः स्यात् कुरूणाम्, Mah.; breach of p.:<BR>शान्तिभङ्गः;<BR>hold p.:<BR>शान्तो भव: v. Silence;<BR>(3) सन्धिः ( league: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peaceable
PEACEABLE:<BR>I Disposed to peace: शान्तप्रकृति<BR>(mfn.) and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Calm, quiet:<BR>q. v.: शान्त (f. न्ता), प्र-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peaceably
PEACEABLY: expr. by circumlo.: v. Also<BR>quietly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peaceful
PEACEFUL:<BR>(1) प्र-शान्त (f. न्ता = quiet, still);<BR>(2) निरूपद्रव (f. वा = without any distur-<BR>-bance, as a p. country);<BR>(3) निर्वृत (f.<BR>ता = content, as a p. life);<BR>(4) मधुर (f. रा<BR>= sweet, as p. words).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peacefully
PEACEFULLY:<BR>(1) प्रशान्तम्;<BR>(2) निरूपद्रवम्, etc.:<BR>for dif.: v. Above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peacefulness
PEACEFULNESS:<BR>(1) प्रशान्तता;<BR>(2) निरूपद्रवता;<BR>(3) निर्वृतिः: v. Above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peace-offering
PEACE-OFFERING: नैवेद्यम् (बलिः gen. applied<BR>to animal-o,).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peach
PEACH: no equiv.: *रामठः (n. for the fruit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peacock
PEACOCK:<BR>(1) मयूरः;<BR>(2) नीलकण्ठः;<BR>(3) शिख-<BR>ण्डिन् (m.);<BR>(4) शिखिन् (m.). P.'s tail:<BR>(1)<BR>बर्हम्;<BR>(2) शिखण्डः (rare);<BR>(3) कलापः। Eye in<BR>p.'s tail:<BR>(1) चन्द्रकः;<BR>(2) मेचकः। P.'s cry:<BR>केका।<BR>A tuft of p.'s feathers:<BR>बर्हमारः, Ki. xvi. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peahen
PEAHEN:<BR>(1) मयूरी;<BR>(2) शिखण्डिनी;<BR>(3) कलापिनी<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peak
PEAK:<BR>I Of a mountain:<BR>(1) शिखरम्;<BR>(2)<BR>शृङ्गम्;<BR>(3) कूट (mn (rare), having three p. s:<BR>त्रिकूटः: v. Also summit.<BR>II Of anything:<BR>अग्रम्: v. Tip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peaked
PEAKED: तीक्ष्णाग्र (f. ग्रा) (of things); शिखरिन्<BR>(f णी) etc. (of mountains).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peal
PEAL (subs.):<BR>(1) ध्वनिः;<BR>(2) निनादः: v. Sound,<BR>noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peal
PEAL (v.): ध्वनति (ध्वन्, c. 1.): v. To sound,<BR>ring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pear
PEAR: a fruit: no equiv.: *पीरम्, -फलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pearl
PEARL: मुक्ता, -फलम्,<BR>sources of p. s:<BR>मौक्तिकयोनयः, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">Page511</a>]<BR>Bha.;<BR>large p. s:<BR>मुक्ता बृहत्प्रमाणाः, V. m. 81. 21.<BR>P. necklace:<BR>मुक्तावली, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pearl-fishery
PEARL-FISHERY: perh. शुक्तिबन्धः, -नम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pearl-oyster
PEARL-OYSTER:<BR>(1) शुक्तिः;<BR>(2) मौक्तिकशुक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pearly
PEARLY:<BR>I Lit.: मुक्तामयः (यी, यं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Fig.: pure, transparent: q. v.:<BR>मुक्तावदातः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peasant
PEASANT:<BR>(1) कृषकः;<BR>(2) कृषीवलः;<BR>(3) कृषि-<BR>जीविन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peasantry
PEASANTRY:<BR>I Peasants: कर्षकाः, etc.<BR>II<BR>Their works: कृषिकर्मन् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peascod
PEASCOD, PEA-SHELL: कलायकञ्चुकम् and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pebble
PEBBLE:<BR>I Round stone: उपलः।<BR>II Crys-<BR>-tal:<BR>p. spectacles:<BR>*स्फाटिकमुपनेत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pebbled
PEBBLED, PEBBLY:<BR>(1) प्रचुरोपल (f. ला);<BR>(2)<BR>उपलभूयिष्ठ (f. ष्ठा), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peccable
PECCABLE: i. e. liable to sin.: expr. by cir-<BR>-cumlo.: v. Sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peccadillo
PECCADILLO: स्खलितम्: v. Also fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peccant
PECCANT:<BR>I Sinning, criminal: q. v.: पापिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR>II Morbid, corrupt, as the hu-<BR>-mours: दुष्ट (f. ष्टा), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peccavi
PECCAVI: अपराद्धोऽस्मि; मया कृतोऽपराधः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peck
PECK (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: मानविशेषः।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>शतानि (n. pl.) in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peck
PECK (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) चञ्च्वा<BR>or<BR>चञ्चुपुटेन लिखति,<BR> वि-, अभि-, (लिख्, c. 6.: over the surface),<BR>N. ii. 2.;<BR>or<BR>दशति (दंश्, c. 1. = to bite),<BR>N. i. 125.;<BR>(3) तुण्डेन खण्डयति (खण्ड्, c.<BR>10. = to tear), V. t.<BR>II To pick up by<BR>the beak: चञ्चुपुटेन etc. गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.),<BR>etc.<BR>III To strike, pierce: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pecker
PECKER: प्रतुदः, “प्रतुद्य मक्षयन्त्येते तुण्डेन प्रतुदास्ततः”,<BR>Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pectoral
PECTORAL:<BR>I Adj.: by comp., p. region:<BR>वक्षोदेशः: v. Breast.<BR>II Subs: कासघ्नम् (re-<BR>-moving cough).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peculation
PECULATION: मोषः (= stealth, theft: q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peculiar
PECULIAR: विशेष- in comp.: v. Particular,<BR>singular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peculiarity
PECULIARITY: विशेषचिह्नम् (= mark), -धर्मः (qua-<BR>-lity), -मावः (= nature), etc.: v. Those words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peculiarly
PECULIARLY: expr. by विशेष- in comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pecuniary
PECUNIARY: अर्थ- in comp.,<BR>p. mulct:<BR>अर्थदण्डः:<BR>v. Money.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pedagogue
PEDAGOGUE:<BR>I Lit.: शिशुशिक्षकः and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II A pedant: q. v.: पण्डितम्मन्य<BR>(f. न्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pedal
PEDAL (adj.):<BR>(1) पादिक (f. की);<BR>(2) by<BR>comp.: v. Foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pedant
PEDANT:<BR>(1) पण्डितम्मन्य (f. न्या);<BR>(2) पण्डित-<BR>मानिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) विद्याभिमानिन् (f. नी);<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pedantic
PEDANTIC, -AL: पाण्डित्याभिमानव्यञ्जक (f. ञ्जिका)<BR>and sim. comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pedantically
PEDANTICALLY: expr. by adj. or comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pedantry
PEDANTRY:<BR>(1) पाण्डित्याभिमानः;<BR>(2) विद्यावलेपः,<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peddler
PEDDLER, PEDLAR: perh. पादकारः (comp.<BR>vern. paiker).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peddlery
PEDDLERY:<BR>I The wares: तुच्छभाण्डानि (n.<BR>pl. ?); क्षुद्रपण्यानि (n. pl. ?).<BR>II The busi-<BR>-ness: पादकार्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pedestal
PEDESTAL: स्तम्भादेः पादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pedestrian
PEDESTRIAN:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) पादचारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) पदग (f. गा);<BR>(3) पदाति (mfn.); etc.<BR>II Adj.: by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pedicle
PEDICLE, PEDICEL:<BR>(1) वृन्तम्;<BR>(2) प्रसवबन्धनम्<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pedigree
PEDIGREE:<BR>(1) वंशावलिः (ली);<BR>(2) वंशानुचरितम्<BR>(account of).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peduncle
PEDUNCLE: काण्ड (mn. = stalk).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peel
PEEL (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) त्वचयति (nomi.);<BR>(2) त्वचम्, etc. अपनयति (नी, c. 1.), etc.: v.<BR>To remove.<BR>II Fig.: विलुण्ठति (लुण्ठ्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peel
PEEL (v. i.):<BR>it p. s easily:<BR>अनायासेनास्य त्वग् विश्लेषी-<BR>भवति<BR>or<BR>स्खलति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peel
PEEL (subs.): त्वच् (f.): v. Skin, rind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peel
PEEL (v.):<BR>I Lit.: जालरन्ध्रेण etc. पश्यति (दृश्,<BR>c. 1.): v. To see.<BR>II Fig.: निर्गच्छति (गम्,<BR>c. 1.): v. To come out.<BR>III To cry,<BR>chirp: चुंकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peep
PEEP (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: रन्ध्रेण वीक्षणम्।<BR>II<BR>Fig.: प्रारम्भः (= commencement).<BR>III Cry:<BR>चुंकृतम्, N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peep-hole
PEEP-HOLE, PEEPING-HOLE: जालरन्ध्रम्, and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peer
PEER (v.):<BR>I To appear: q. v.: आविर्भवति।<BR>II To peep: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peer
PEER (subs.):<BR>I An equal, match: q. v.<BR>II A comrade: वयस्य (f. स्या).<BR>III A<BR>nobleman: q. v.: *राजन्यः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peerage
PEERAGE: राजन्यकम् (both of the rank and<BR>the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peerless
PEERLESS: अप्रतिम (f. मा): v. Incomparable,<BR>unmatched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peevish
PEEVISH:<BR>(1) कोपन (f. ना = irascible);<BR>(2)<BR>कलहप्रिय (f. या = quarrelsome):<BR>(3) प्रतीप<BR>(f. पा = cross).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peevishly
PEEVISHLY:<BR>(1) चण्डम् (= angrily);<BR>(2) कार्कश्येन<BR>(= roughly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peevishness
PEEVISHNESS:<BR>(1) कोपनता;<BR>(2) प्रतीपता;<BR>(3)<BR>कार्कश्यम्: v. Above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peg
PEG (subs.):<BR>I A pin:<BR>(1) कीलः, -कः;<BR>(2)<BR>नागदन्तकः (ivory).<BR>II Of brandy: *ब्राण्डि-<BR>जलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peg
PEG (v.): कीलयति (nomi.): v. Also to fasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pekoe
PEKOE: वासितचाविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pelf
PELF: perh. अन्यायोपार्जितं धनम्; अन्यायार्जितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pellet
PELLET: गुटिका: v. Ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pell-mell
PELL-MELL (adv.): perh. हूलस्यूलम् (com.<BR>Beng. and sim. comp.s. in Vāmana: v.<BR>Also confusion (in-).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pellucid
PELLUCID: स्वच्छ (f. च्छा): v. Clear, trans-<BR>-parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pelt
PELT (v. t.):<BR>(1) हन्ति, अभि- (= to strike),<BR>was<BR>p. ed to death:<BR>लोष्टघातं हतम्, Mu. ii.;<BR>p. ed<BR>with shower:<BR>धाराभिहत (f. ता);<BR>(2) क्षिपति<BR> क्षिप्, c. 6.): To throw: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pelt
PELT (v. i.):<BR>with p. ing rain:<BR>चण्डामिर्धाराभिः,<BR>Mu. v. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pelvis
PELVIS: क(कृ)न्दरविभागः (?), D. vi.;<BR>(2) वस्तिदेशः,<BR>Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pen
PEN (v):<BR>I To write: q. v.: लिखति (लिख्,<BR>c. 6.).<BR>II To confine: q. v.: नि-रूणद्धि, अव-,<BR>(रूध्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pen
PEN (subs.):<BR>I For writing:<BR>(1) लेखनी,<BR>if<BR>my p. does not cease to write for a moment:<BR>यदि<BR>मे लेखनी क्षणं लिखतो नावतिष्ठेत, Mah.;<BR>(2) कलमः<BR>(reed-p.).<BR>II For cattle:<BR>cow-p.:<BR>गोशाला,<BR> गोकुलम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penal
PENAL:<BR>I In gen.: by comp., p. servitude:<BR>*दण्डदास्यम्;<BR>p. settlement:<BR>*दण्डितसन्निवेशः।<BR>II Incurring punishment: दण्डार्ह (f. र्हा)<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penalty
PENALTY: दण्डः: v. Punishment, fine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penance
PENANCE:<BR>I Voluntary:<BR>(1) तपस् (n.),<BR>to<BR>perform p.s:<BR>तपस्तप्तुम्<BR>or<BR>चरितुम्;<BR>(2) तपस्या।<BR>II Imposed: प्रायश्चित्तम्,<BR>to do p.:<BR>प्रायश्वित्तं<BR> करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pencil
PENCIL (subs.):<BR>(1) तूलिका (painter's);<BR>(2)<BR>वर्तिका (= 1);<BR>(3) कूर्चिका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pencil
PENCIL (v.): तूलिकया etc. लिखति (लिख्, c. 6.):<BR>v. To draw, write, mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pendant
PENDANT:<BR>I For the ear: कर्णेन्दुः: v. Ear-<BR>-ring.<BR>II In gen. perh. प्रालम्बः, R. vi. 14.<BR>III A flag.: केतुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pendant
PENDANT:<BR>(1) लोल (f. ला = tossing);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रलम्ब (f. म्बा = hanging).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pending
PENDING:<BR>I Adj.:<BR>the case is p.:<BR>अनिर्णीतोऽयं<BR> व्यवहारः।<BR>II Prep.<BR>p. the trial:<BR>यावन्न निर्णीयते<BR> व्यवहारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pendulous
PENDULOUS:<BR>(1) लोल (f. ला = tossing);<BR>(2)<BR>दोलायमान (f. ना = swinging);<BR>(3) प्रलम्ब (f. म्बा =<BR>hanging).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pendulum
PENDULUM: *लोलदण्डः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penetrability
PENETRABILITY:<BR>(1) प्रवेश्यता;<BR>(2) भेद्यता;<BR>(3)<BR>ग्रहणीयता: for dif.: v. Below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penetrable
PENETRABLE:<BR>(1) प्रवेश्य (f. श्या);<BR>(2) भेद्य (f.<BR>द्या);<BR>(3) ग्रहणीय (f. या): etc.: v. To<BR>penetrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penetrate
PENETRATE:<BR>(1) प्रविशति (= to enter: q. v.),<BR>instructions easily p. a clear heart:<BR>अपगतमले<BR> मनसि विशन्ति सुखमुपदेशगुणाः, K.;<BR>to p. into the<BR>poem of Bhāravi:<BR>कर्तुं प्रवेशमिह भारविकाव्यबन्धे,<BR>M. n. 7.;<BR>(2) भिनत्ति, निर्-, (भिद्, c. 7. = to<BR>pierce: q. v.);<BR>(3) गृह्वाति (ग्रह्, c. 9. = to<BR>comprehend: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penetrating
PENETRATING (adj.): Fig.: of a p. mind:<BR>सूक्ष्मबुद्धि (mfn.): v. Shrewd, acute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penetration
PENETRATION:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्रवेशः (= entry); [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">Page513</a>]<BR>(2) भेदः (= piercing);<BR>(3) ग्रहणम् (= com-<BR>-prehension).<BR>II Fig.: सूक्ष्मबुद्धिः: v. Also<BR>sagacity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peninsula
PENINSULA: उपद्वीपः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peninsular
PENINSULAR: Expr. by comp. or circumlo.,<BR>p. war:<BR>*उपद्वीपेन संग्रामः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penitence
PENITENCE: अनुतापः: v. Repentance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penitent
PENITENT: जातानुताप (f. पा) and sim. comp.s.<BR>v. Repentant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penitential
PENITENTIAL: अनुतापज (f. जा) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penitentiary
PENITENTIARY: *दण्डितागारम्; कारागारम् (= jail).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penitently
PENITENTLY:<BR>(1) सानुतापम्;<BR>(2) by adj. अनुतप्त<BR>(f. प्ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penknife
PENKNIFE: *कलमकर्तनी; लेखनीछुरिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penman
PENMAN:<BR>(1) लेखकः: v. Writer;<BR>(2) लिपिकरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penmanship
PENMANSHIP: लिपिः,<BR>knowing p.:<BR>लिपिज्ञः;<BR>good<BR>p.:<BR>सुलिपिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pennant
PENNANT, PENNON: केतुः: v. Banner, flag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penniless
PENNILESS: अकिञ्चनः (ना, नं): v. Destitute,<BR>poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penny
PENNY: ताम्रमुद्राविशेषः।<BR>P. weight:<BR>मानविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pensile
PENSILE: लम्ब (f. म्बा), प्र-: v. Hanging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pension
PENSION:<BR>I Subs.: *अपसरवृत्तिः।<BR>II Verb:<BR>*अपसरवृत्तिं ददाति (दा, c. 3.), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pensioner
PENSIONER: *अपसरवृत्तिभोगिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pensive
PENSIVE: चिन्तापरायण (f. णा) and sim. comp. s:<BR>v. Thoughtful, meditative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pensively
PENSIVELY: expr. by adj. or pres. part.:<BR>v. To think.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pensiveness
PENSIVENESS:<BR>(1) चिन्तावेशः;<BR>(2) ध्यानपरता and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pent-up
PENT-UP: सं-रुद्ध (f. द्धा), अव-, नि-: v. To con-<BR>-fine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pentagon
PENTAGON:<BR>(1) पञ्चभुजः;<BR>(2) पञ्चास्रं क्षेत्रम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pentagonal
PENTAGONAL:<BR>(1) पञ्चभुज; (f. जा);<BR>(2)<BR>पञ्चकोण (f. णा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pentameter
PENTAMETER: पञ्चपदी (वृत्तिः) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pentastich
PENTASTICH: पञ्चश्लोकी, “पञ्चश्लोकीभागवतम्।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penthouse
PENTHOUSE: बहिर्गृहम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penult
PENULT, PENULTIMA:<BR>(1) उपधा;<BR>(2) उपान्त्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penultimate
PENULTIMATE:<BR>I Adj.: उपान्त्य (f. न्त्या).<BR>II<BR>Subs.: उपान्त्यम्, J. Ph.:<BR>p. letter:<BR>उपधा, S. k.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penumbra
PENUMBRA:<BR>(1) खण्डच्छाया (?);<BR>(2) व्यस्तच्छाया<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penurious
PENURIOUS: कृपण (f. णा): v. Miserly, illi-<BR>-beral, mean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penuriousness
PENURIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) कार्पण्यम्;<BR>(2) बद्धमुष्टिता<BR>(= close-fistedness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

penury
PENURY: दारिद्र्यम्: v. Indigence, poverty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peon
PEON: पदातिः, -कः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

people
PEOPLE (subs.):<BR>I A community:<BR>(1) प्रकृतयः<BR>(f. pl.),<BR>for the good of the p.:<BR>प्रकृतिहिताय, Sa.<BR>vii. 6.;<BR>(2) प्रजाः (f. pl.),<BR>to your p.:<BR>तव<BR> प्रजासु, Sa.;<BR>that my p.:<BR>यन्मदीयाः प्रजाः, R. i.<BR>63.<BR>II Persons generally:<BR>(1) लोकः (often<BR>in pl.),<BR>is not known among p.:<BR>लोकेऽप्रसिद्ध (f.<BR>द्धा), Kav. vii.;<BR>all the fādava p.:<BR>अखिल एव<BR> यदुलोकः, V. p. iv. 13. 19.;<BR>(2) जनः (= person:<BR>q. v.),<BR>all the p.:<BR>सर्वे जनाः, P.: v. Also<BR>inhabitant. Ph.: common p.:<BR>(1) प्राकृताः<BR>(m. pl.);<BR>(2) पृथग्जनाः (m. pl.);<BR>(3) इतरो जनः,<BR>Mah.<BR>III Servants, retainers, etc.: लोकाः<BR>(m. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

people
PEOPLE (v.): expr. with subs. P. d: v.<BR>Populated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pepper
PEPPER:<BR>I The black p.:<BR>(1) मरि(री)चम्,<BR>p. box:<BR>मरीचमाण्डम् (?);<BR>(2) कोलम्, -कम्, A.<BR>II The long p.: पिप्पली(लिः)।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peppermint
PEPPERMINT: *पिप्पलमन्थः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pepperwort
PEPPERWORT: तृणविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peppery
PEPPERY:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by comp.<BR>II चण्ड<BR>(f. ण्डा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peradventure
PERADVENTURE: expr. with कदाचित् and<BR>विधिलिङ्: v. Perhaps. Ph.: without p.:<BR>असंशयम्: v. Undoubtedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perambulate
PERAMBULATE: परिभ्राम्यति (भ्रम्, c. 4.): v.<BR>To traverse, travel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perceivable
PERCEIVABLE: v. Perceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perceive
PERCEIVE (v.):<BR>I To cognize:<BR>(1) उपलभते<BR>(लभ्, c. 1.),<BR>to p. by the senses:<BR>इन्द्रियैरुपलभते,<BR>S. c.;<BR>(2) गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.) (= to receive),<BR>p. d before by the senses of hearing and touch:<BR>दर्शनस्पर्शनाभ्यां पूर्वगृहीतम्, S. c.;<BR>(3) निभालयति<BR>(भाल्, c. 10 (rare), S. c.<BR>II To discern, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">Page514</a>]<BR>understand:<BR>(1) उपलभते, no distinction was<BR>p. d even of great (things): विवेकः कस्यचिन्न<BR> महतोऽप्युपलेभे, Ki. ix. 12.;<BR>(2) बुध्यते (बुध्,<BR>c. 4.), gradually p. d that he was Nārada:<BR>क्रमादमुं नारद इत्यबोधिसः, Si. i. 3.: v. To under-<BR>-stand, know:<BR>(2) लक्षयति, सं-, परि-, (लक्ष्,<BR>c. 10 (= to notice: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

percentage
PERCENTAGE: expr. by शतिकः (की, कं) or by<BR>शतम्: v. Cent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perceptible
PERCEPTIBLE:<BR>(1) उपलभ्य (f. भ्या),<BR>from its<BR>being p. to the tongue:<BR>जिह्वयोपलभ्यमानत्वात्,<BR>S. c.;<BR>(2) ग्राह्य (f. ह्या)<BR>or<BR>ग्रहणीयः (या, यं);<BR>(3) संवेद्य (f. द्या) etc. (= knowable).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perceptibly
PERCEPTIBLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perception
PERCEPTION: उपलब्धिः,<BR>and from the non-p. of<BR>others:<BR>इतरेषाञ्चानुपलब्धेः, S.: v. Also know-<BR>-ledge, understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perceptive
PERCEPTIVE: perh. ग्राहक (f. हिका)<BR>or<BR>ग्राहिन्<BR>(f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perch
PERCH (subs.):<BR>I For birds:<BR>(1) वासयष्टिः,<BR>Me. ii. 18.;<BR>(2) यष्टिः, R. xvi. 14.<BR>II For<BR>measuring land: expr. by नल्वः (= 400<BR>cubits).<BR>III A fish: मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perch
PERCH (v.): अध्यास्ते (आस्, c 2.: with acc.):<BR>v. Sit, roost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perchance
PERCHANCE: दैवात्: v. Perhaps, accidentally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

percolate
PERCOLATE: परि-स्रवति (स्रु, c. 1.): v. To<BR>flow, ooze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

percolation
PERCOLATION: लवशः परिस्रवः: v. Flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

percussion
PERCUSSION:<BR>(1) समाधातः;<BR>(2) संघट्टः: v.<BR>Collision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perdition
PERDITION: उच्छेदः: v. Also ruin, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peregrinate
PEREGRINATE: परिभ्रमति<BR>or<BR>भ्राम्यति (भ्रम्, c. 1.<BR>and 4.): v. To travel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peregrination
PEREGRINATION: परिभ्रमणम्: v. Travel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peremptorily
PEREMPTORILY:<BR>(1) अटलम्;<BR>(2) स्पष्टम्;<BR>(3)<BR>सुनिश्चितम्: v. Below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peremptory
PEREMPTORY:<BR>(1) अटल (f. ला = unchange-<BR>-able);<BR>(2) स्पष्ट (f. ष्टा = clear);<BR>(3) सुनिश्चित<BR>(f. ता = decisive).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perennial
PERENNIAL: नित्य (f. त्या): v. Perpetual.<BR>Ph.:<BR>having p. water:<BR>सदानीरा (a name of<BR>the Karatoyā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perennially
PERENNIALLY:<BR>(1) नित्यम्: v. Perpetually,<BR>continually;<BR>(2) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perfect
PERFECT (v.): संपूरयति (पूर्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>finish, complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perfect
PERFECT (adj.):<BR>(1) सम्पूर्ण (f. र्णा): v. Full,<BR>complete;<BR>(2) समग्र (f. ग्रा): v. Entire;<BR>(3) उत्कृष्ट (f. ष्टा): v. Excellent. Ph.:<BR>no<BR>one is p.:<BR>नास्त्यदोषः कोऽपि; p. tense expr. by<BR>निष्पन्नक्रिया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perfection
PERFECTION, PERFECTNESS: I. Completeness:<BR>q. v.: सम्पूर्णता।<BR>II Great skill: q. v.: परं<BR> कौशलम्।<BR>III Excellence: q. v.: उत्कर्वः।<BR>IV<BR>An endowment: गुणः। V. Acme.: q. v.:<BR>परा कोटिः। Ph.:<BR>to p.:<BR>परमेण कौशलेन: v. Also<BR>perfectly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perfectly
PERFECTLY:<BR>(1) सम्पूर्णम्: v. Completely;<BR>(2)<BR>समग्रम् v. Entirely;<BR>(3) by adj. or comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perfidious
PERFIDIOUS:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) असत्यसन्ध (f. न्धा);<BR>(2) विश्वासधातिन् (f. नी): v. Treacherous;<BR>(3) शठ (f. ठा): v. Wicked.<BR>II Of acts:<BR>अनार्य (f. र्या): v. Dishonest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perfidiously
PERFIDIOUSLY: विश्वासमुन्मथ्यः v. Treacherously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perfidiousness
PERFIDIOUSNESS, PERFIDY: विश्वासघातः: v.<BR>Treachery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perforate
PERFORATE: विध्यति (व्यध्, c. 4.): v. To<BR>bore, pierce. P. d;<BR>(1) छिद्रित (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>छिद्रपूर्ण (f. र्णा = full of holes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perforation
PERFORATION:<BR>I Boring: q. v.: वेधः।<BR>II A<BR>hole: q. v.: छिद्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perforce
PERFORCE: बलात्: v. Forcibly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perform
PERFORM:<BR>I To do: q. v.: करोति।<BR>II To<BR>accomplish: q. v.: साधयति (c. of सिघ्).<BR>III To fulfil: q. v.: पूरयति (पूर्, c. 10.).<BR>IV To keep: q. v.: रक्षति (रक्ष्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

performance
PERFORMANCE:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) साधनम्;<BR>(2) सम्पादनम्;<BR>(3) निष्पत्तिः।<BR>II Deed, act:<BR>q. v.: कर्मन् (n.).<BR>III An exhibition: अभिनयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

performer
PERFORMER: अभिनेतृ (f. त्री): v. Actor. In<BR>lit. sense: कर्तृ (f. त्री = doer)<BR>or<BR>साधक (f.<BR>धिका = achiever).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perfume
PERFUME (v.):<BR>(1) वासयति, अनु-, अधि-, (वास्, c.<BR>10.),<BR>p. d, with scent:<BR>आमोदवासित-, Ki. ix.<BR>77.;<BR>(2) सुरभीकरोति, p. ing the lotus filaments: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">Page515</a>]<BR>सुरभितमकरन्दम्, Si. xi. 19.;<BR>(3) सुगन्धयति<BR>(nomi.) Ri. v. 5.;<BR>(4) आमोदयति (c. of मुद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perfume
PERFUME (subs.):<BR>I Scent, fragrance: q. v.:<BR>परिमलः।<BR>II Anything scented.<BR>(1) गन्धद्रव्यम्,<BR>Bha. and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(2) गन्धः,<BR>who live<BR>by selling p. s:<BR>गन्धोपजीविनः, Ram. ii. 90. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perfumer
PERFUMER:<BR>(1) गान्धिकः;<BR>(2) गन्धवणिज् (m.);<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perfumery
PERFUMERY: गन्धाः (m. pl.): v. Perfume (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perfunctorily
PERFUNCTORILY: अनवहितम्: v. Negligently,<BR>inattentively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perfunctory
PERFUNCTORY:<BR>(1) अनवहित (f. ता): v. Care-<BR>-less, negligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perhaps
PERHAPS:<BR>(1) प्रायेण (= probably);<BR>(2) by<BR>विधिलिङ् (= may, gram. §353);<BR>(3) दैवात्<BR>(= by chance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perigee
PERIGEE, PERIGEUM: *उपगवम्; चन्द्रस्य क्रान्ति-<BR>मण्डलस्य पृथिव्या नेदिष्ठपदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peril
PERIL (subs.): भयम्: v. Danger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peril
PERIL (v.): संशये क्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.): v. En-<BR>-danger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perilous
PERILOUS: भयावह (f. हा): v. Dangerous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perilously
PERILOUSLY: expr. by circumlo.: v. Danger-<BR>-ously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

period
PERIOD:<BR>I Time: q. v.: समयः। Ph.:<BR>for a<BR>p. of three months:<BR>मासत्रयम्।<BR>II End: q. v.:<BR>अन्तः।<BR>III A full stop: दण्डः (the corres-<BR>-ponding line).<BR>IV A sentence: वाक्योच्चयः,<BR>Sah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

periodic
PERIODIC,-AL (adj.):<BR>(1) सामयिक (f. की);<BR>(2) नित्य (f. त्या = regular); वार्षिक (f. की =<BR>annual)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

periodical
PERIODICAL (Subs.): *सामयिकपत्रिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

periodically
PERIODICALLY:<BR>(1) समये समये;<BR>(2) नित्यम्<BR>(= regularly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

periodicity
PERIODICITY:<BR>(1) नित्यता (= regularity);<BR>(2)<BR>by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peripatetic
PERIPATETIC: पादचारिन् (f. णी: may be used<BR>lit. and fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

periphery
PERIPHERY:<BR>(1) परिधिः;<BR>(2) परिवेशः(षः);<BR>(3)<BR>प्रधिः (of a wheel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

periphrastic
PERIPHRASTIC: अधिकपदः (दा, दं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perish
PERISH:<BR>(1) नश्यति, वि-, प्र- (नश्, c. 4.);<BR>(2)<BR>नाशम् एति (इ, c. 2.), गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.),<BR>etc.: v. Destroyed, be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perishable
PERISHABLE:<BR>(1) नश्वर (f. री), वि-;<BR>(2) भङ्गुर<BR>(f. रा: prop. breaking).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perishableness
PERISHABLENESS:<BR>(1) नश्वरता, वि-;<BR>(2) भङ्गुरता,<BR>the sudden p. of all pleasures:<BR>अकाण्डभङ्गुरता सर्व-<BR>सुखानाम्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peristaltic
PERISTALTIC: *सर्पसन्निभ (f. भा) and sim.<BR>comp s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peristyle
PERISTYLE: *परितःस्तम्भम् (comp. सर्वतोभद्रम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

periwig
PERIWIG: *परिकेशम्: v. Also wig.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

periwinkle
PERIWINKLE: शम्बूकविशेषः, लताविशेषश्च।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perjure
PERJURE: A p. d witness i. e. who p. s himself:<BR>साक्ष्येऽनृतं वदन् साक्षी, साक्षी साक्ष्यं मृषा ब्रुवन्, etc.<BR>Mit.: v. Falsely, to say. Ph.: p. d oath:<BR>मिथ्याशपथः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perjurer
PERJURER:<BR>(1) कूटसाक्षिन् (f. णी), Mit.;<BR>(2) by<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perjury
PERJURY:<BR>(1) कूटसाक्ष्यम्;<BR>(2) मिथ्यासाक्ष्यम्;<BR>(3)<BR>by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

permanence
PERMANENCE, PERMANENCY:<BR>(1) स्थायिता;<BR>(2)<BR>स्थास्नुता (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

permanent
PERMANENT: स्थायिन् (f. नी): v. Lasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

permanently
PERMANENTLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

permeable
PERMEABLE: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

permeate
PERMEATE:<BR>(1) अन्तर्गच्छति (गम् c. 1. to go<BR>through);<BR>(2) व्याप्नोति (आप्, c. 5. = to<BR>pervade): v. Also to penetrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

permissible
PERMISSIBLE:<BR>(1) ग्राह्य (f. ह्या = acceptable);<BR>(2) युक्त (= proper).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

permission
PERMISSION:<BR>(1) आदेशः;<BR>(2) अनुज्ञा: v. Order<BR>(IV).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

permissive
PERMISSIVE:<BR>(1) आदेशिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) अनुज्ञा-<BR>दायिन् (f. नी), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

permit
PERMIT:<BR>(1) आदिशति (दिश्, c. 6.).;<BR>(2) अनु-<BR>जानाति (ज्ञा, c. 9.): v. To order (II), direct<BR>(II)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

permutation
PERMUTATION: In algebra: अङ्कपाशः, Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pernicious
PERNICIOUS: विनाशिन् (f. नी): v. Injurious,<BR>destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perniciously
PERNICIOUSLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peroration
PERORATION: उपसंहारः (= conclusion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perpendicular
PERPENDICULAR (subs.):<BR>(1) लभ्बः, those lines [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">Page516</a>]<BR>are p. to each other:<BR>ते रेखे मिथो लम्बरूपे भवतः,<BR>K. d.;<BR>(2) अवलम्बः, -कः, Li. 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perpendicular
PERPENDICULAR (adj.):<BR>I In geo.: v.<BR>Above.<BR>II = straight: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perpendicularly
PERPENDICULARLY:<BR>(1) लम्बरूपेण;<BR>(2) लम्बवत्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perpetrate
PERPETRATE: करोतिः v. To do, commit (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perpetration
PERPETRATION: expr. by verb,<BR>in the p. of<BR>murder:<BR>वधं कुर्वन्;<BR>his p. of incest:<BR>अगम्यागमनं<BR> तस्य; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perpetrator
PERPETRATOR: -कारिन् (f. णी)<BR>or<BR>-कृत् (mfn.)<BR>in comp.: v. Doer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perpetual
PERPETUAL:<BR>(1) नित्य (f. त्या),<BR>and considering<BR>that nothing was p.:<BR>भावयित्वा चानित्यतां सर्व-<BR>भावानाम्, K.;<BR>(2) शाश्वत (f. ती): v. Eternal;<BR>(3) सतत (f. ता): v. Continuous, inces-<BR>-sant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perpetually
PERPETUALLY:<BR>(1) नित्यम्;<BR>(2) सततम्: v.<BR>Continually, incessantly;<BR>(3) सदा (= always:<BR>q. v.),<BR>p. moving:<BR>सदागतिः (air).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perpetuate
PERPETUATE: अक्षयं (f. यां)<BR>or<BR>सदातनं (f. नां)<BR>करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perpetuity
PERPETUITY:<BR>(1) नित्यता;<BR>(2) नित्यस्थायिता;<BR>(3) अविच्छिन्नता (= continuity);<BR>(4) चिर-<BR>स्थायिता; etc. Ph.:<BR>to p.:<BR>शाश्वतीः समाः, Mah.<BR>iii. 286. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perplex
PERPLEX: आकुलयति (nomi.): v. To embar-<BR>-rass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perplexed
PERPLEXED:<BR>I Intricate: q. v.: विषम (f. मा).<BR>II Embarrassed: (I) व्याकुलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2)<BR>सम्भ्रान्त (f. न्ता);<BR>(3) उद्विग्न (f. ग्ना = alarmed):<BR>Ph.:<BR>p. what to do:<BR>किंकर्तव्यताभूढः, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perplexing
PERPLEXING (adj.):<BR>(1) विषम (f. मा = intri-<BR>-cate);<BR>(2) सन्दिग्ध (f. ग्धा = doubtful);<BR>(3)<BR>व्यामोहक (f. हिका: rare);<BR>(4) भ्रान्तिजनन (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perplexity
PERPLEXITY:<BR>I The state:<BR>(1) चित्तसंभ्रमः,<BR> चित्तव्यामोहः, and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(2) by adj.<BR>II Doubt: q. v.: संशयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perquisite
PERQUISITE: पुरस्कारः: v. Present, reward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perry
PERRY: *पीरासवम् and sim. comps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

persecute
PERSECUTE. बाधते, प्र-, परि-, (बाध्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To harass, trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

persecution
PERSECUTION:<BR>(1) बाधः, -नम्, प्र-, परि-;<BR>(2)<BR>अभिद्रोहः;<BR>(3) उपद्रवः;<BR>(4) उपप्लवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

persecutor
PERSECUTOR:<BR>(1) बाधक (f. धिका), प्र-;<BR>(2)<BR>उपद्रवकारिन् (f. णी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perseverance
PERSEVERANCE:<BR>(1) अभियोगः;<BR>(2) अभिनिवेशः;<BR>(3) अध्यवसायः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

persevere
PERSEVERE:<BR>(1) मनोऽभियुंक्ते (युज्, c. 7.) or<BR>अभिनिवेशयति (c. of विश्),<BR>(2) by subs. or<BR>adj.: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

persevering
PERSEVERING (adj.):<BR>(1) अभियोगभाज् (mfn.)<BR>K. iii. 40.;<BR>(2) अभिनिवेशवत् (f. ती), M. n.;<BR>(3) अभियुक्त (f. क्ता),<BR>fate cannot be changed<BR>even by perseverance:<BR>न हि शक्यं दैवमन्यथाकर्तुमभि-<BR>युक्तेनापि, K.;<BR>(4) अभिनिविष्ट (f. ष्टा);<BR>(5) अध्य-<BR>वसायिन् (f. नी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perseveringly
PERSEVERINGLY:<BR>(1) अभियोगेन;<BR>(2) by adj.:<BR>अभियुक्त (f. क्ता), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

persian
PERSIAN (subs.):<BR>I Inhabitant: पारसीकः, R.<BR>iv. 60.<BR>II The language: पारसीवाच्, Raj.;<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

persiflage
PERSIFLAGE: परिहासः (= joke: ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

persist
PERSIST: expr. by subs.,<BR>if you p. about it:<BR>तेषु<BR> चेद् ग्राहस्ते, Vi. v. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

persistence
PERSISTENCE, PERSISTENCY:<BR>(1) निर्बन्धः;<BR>(2)<BR>आ-ग्रहः;<BR>(3) ग्राहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

persistent
PERSISTENT:<BR>(1) निर्बन्धपर (f. रा) and sim.<BR>comp.s.;<BR>(2) by adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

persistently
PERSISTENTLY: निर्बन्धेन;<BR>(2) सनिर्बन्धम्;<BR>(3)<BR>साग्रहम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

person
PERSON:<BR>I A human being:<BR>(1) पुरुषः (not<BR>of woman),<BR>like an ordinary p.:<BR>पुरुषः प्राकृतो<BR> यथा, Mah. iv. 46. 13.;<BR>(2) जनः, this p. (i. e.<BR>I Pārvatī): जनोऽयम्, K. v. 64.: v. People,<BR>man. Ph.:<BR>in p.:<BR>स्वयम्: v. Self.; to one's p.<BR>(= face): समक्षे।<BR>II Body: q. v.: शरीरम्,<BR>beauty of p.:<BR>शरीरशोभा, N.<BR>III. Form, chara-<BR>-cter: q. v.: रूपम्, in the p. of Brihannalā:<BR>वृहन्नलारूपमुपेत्य, Mah. iv. 67. 15.<BR>IV In<BR>gram.: पुरूषः,<BR>the first p.:<BR>उत्तमपुरुषः;<BR>the second<BR>p.:<BR>मध्यमपुरुषः;<BR>the third p.:<BR>प्रथमपुरुषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

personage
PERSONAGE:<BR>I Character: q. v.: रूपम्।<BR>II<BR>Person: q. v.: पुरुषः,<BR>great p.:<BR>महापुरुषः, U.<BR>vi. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

personal
PERSONAL:<BR>I Individual: व्यक्तिगत (f. ता).<BR>II Bodily: q. v.: शरीर- in comp., p. charms: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">Page517</a>]<BR>शरीरशोभा, N.<BR>III. Belonging to persons:<BR>expr. by comp. or gen.<BR>IV Done in<BR>person: स्वयंकृत (f. ता).<BR>V. Own: q. v.:<BR>for p. attendance:<BR>आत्मदर्शनार्थम्।<BR>VI Concern-<BR>-ing individual character:<BR>I donot like your<BR>p. observations:<BR>अमुकं लक्षीकृत्य यदुक्तं तन्मे न रोचते।<BR>Ph.:<BR>p. pronouns^1:<BR>पुरुषवाचकानि सर्वनामानि (n.<BR>pl.);<BR>p. property:<BR>अस्थावरसम्पत्तिः।<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

personality
PERSONALITY:<BR>I Individuality:<BR>(1) पुरुषता<BR>(?);<BR>(2) पृथगात्मता।<BR>II Personal reflections:<BR>(1) by circumlo.: v. Personal (IV);<BR>(2)<BR>आक्षेपः (= abuse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

personally
PERSONALLY:<BR>I In person: स्वयम्, p. delivered:<BR>स्वयंदत्त (f. त्ता);<BR>p. came to him:<BR>स्वयं तमभीयाय,<BR>Ki. ii. 54.<BR>II Individually: gen. not expr.:<BR>बिशेषतः (= particularly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

personalty
PERSONALTY:<BR>(1) अस्थावरसम्पत्तिः;<BR>(2) अस्थावरम्;<BR>(3) जङ्गमं द्रव्यम् (rare), Vri.; and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

personate
PERSONATE: रूपं गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9. with gen.),<BR>p. ing a sage:<BR>मुनिरूपः, Ki. xi. 2.;<BR>p. ing a<BR>Kirāta:<BR>किरातरूपधारिन्, M. n.;<BR>p. ing me:<BR>मम<BR> रूपं समास्थाय, Ram. i. 49. 26.; p. ing the sage:<BR>मुनिवेशधरः, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

personated
PERSONATED: i. e. feigned, false: q. v.: कपट-<BR>in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

personation
PERSONATION: रूपग्रहणम्<BR>or<BR>-धारणम्; better by<BR>verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

personification
PERSONIFICATION:<BR>I In Rhe.: समासोक्तिः, Kav.<BR>x. ii. 56.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>p. of justice:<BR>साक्षाद्धर्मः;<BR>p. of death:<BR>कृतान्त इव।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

personify
PERSONIFY: चेतनत्वं<BR>or<BR>चेतनधर्मम् आरोपयति (c. of<BR>रुह्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perspective
PERSPECTIVE: यथादृश्यचित्रालेखः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perspicacious
PERSPICACIOUS: तीक्ष्णदृष्टि (mfn.): v. Also keen,<BR>sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perspicaciously
PERSPICACIOUSLY:<BR>(1) तीक्ष्णदृष्ट्या;<BR>(2) तीक्ष्ण-<BR>बुद्ध्या; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perspicacity
PERSPICACITY:<BR>(1) तीक्ष्णदृष्टिः;<BR>(2) तीक्ष्णबुद्धिः<BR>(fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perspicuity
PERSPICUITY:<BR>(1) प्रसादः, Kav. viii. 6.;<BR>(2)<BR>वैशद्यम्, N. xiv. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perspicuous
PERSPICUOUS:<BR>(1) प्रसन्न (f. न्ना),<BR>language at<BR>once p. and deep:<BR>प्रसन्नगम्भीरपदा सरस्वती, Ki.<BR>xiv. 3.;<BR>(2) विशदः (दा, दं);<BR>(3) निर्मलः<BR>(ला, लं) (= clear: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perspicuously
PERSPICUOUSLY:<BR>(1) सप्रसादम्;<BR>(2) विशदम्;<BR>(3)<BR>निर्मलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perspiration
PERSPIRATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) स्वेदः, -नम्,<BR> प्र-;<BR>(2) स्वेदस्रावः and sim. comp.s.<BR>II<BR>Sweat:<BR>(1) स्वेदः, although drenched with p.:<BR>स्वेदसलिलस्नातापि, K.;<BR>(2) घर्मः;<BR>(3) घर्माम्बु;<BR>(4) स्वेदजलम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perspire
PERSPIRE: स्विद्यति, प्र-, (स्विद्, c. 4.), p. ing:<BR>स्विद्यत् (f. न्ती);<BR>p. ing violently:<BR>भृशस्विद्<BR>(mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

persuade
PERSUADE:<BR>I To induce:<BR>(1) अनुनीय प्रवर्तयति<BR>(c. of वृत्: ?);<BR>(2) sometimes by causal.<BR>II To convince: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

persuasion
PERSUASION:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अभ्यर्थना (= begg-<BR>-ing);<BR>(2) अनुनयः (= inducement);<BR>(3)<BR>प्रवर्तना (?).<BR>II Faith: q. v.: विश्वासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

persuasive
PERSUASIVE:<BR>(1) हृदयग्राहिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) by<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

persuasively
PERSUASIVELY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

persuasiveness
PERSUASIVENESS: हृदयग्राहिताः v. Persuasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pert
PERT: धृष्ट (f. ष्टा): v. Bold, impudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pertain
PERTAIN:<BR>nothing p. s to me which does not p. to<BR>you:<BR>अभवदीयं हि नैव किञ्चिन्मत्सम्बद्धम्, D. i.: v.<BR>Belonging, relate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pertinacious
PERTINACIOUS:<BR>(1) expr. by subs.,<BR>if you are<BR>p.:<BR>ग्राहस्ते, Vi.;<BR>(2) निर्बद्ध (f. द्धा) (rare): v.<BR>Obstinate, persistent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pertinaciously
PERTINACIOUSLY:<BR>(1) सनिर्बन्धम्;<BR>(2) निर्बन्ध-<BR>in comp.;<BR>(3) ग्रहेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pertinaciousness
PERTINACIOUSNESS, PERTINACITY:<BR>(1) निर्बन्धः;<BR>(2) ग्राहः<BR>or<BR>ग्रहः, Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pertinency
PERTINENCY:<BR>(1) प्रासङ्गिकता;<BR>(2) योग्यता: v.<BR>Fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pertinent
PERTINENT:<BR>(1) प्रासङ्गिक (f. की);<BR>(2) योग्य<BR>(f. ग्या): v. Fit;<BR>(3) उपपन्न (f. न्ना): v.<BR>Apposite.<BR>To be p.:<BR>उपपद्यते (पद्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pertinently
PERTINENTLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pertly
PERTLY:<BR>(1) धार्ष्ट्येन;<BR>(2) अविनयेन: v. Also<BR>impudently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pertness
PERTNESS:<BR>(1) धार्ष्ट्यम्;<BR>(2) अविनयः: v. Also<BR>impudence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perturb
PERTURB: क्षोमयति c. of क्षुभ्): v. To dis-<BR>-turb, disquiet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perturbation
PERTURBATION:<BR>p. of mind:<BR>चित्तसम्भ्रमः<BR>or<BR>मनः-<BR>क्षोभः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perusal
PERUSAL: पाठः, प्र-: v. Reading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

peruse
PERUSE: पठति, प्र-, (पठ्, c. 1.): v. To read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pervade
PERVADE:<BR>(1) व्याप्नोति, अभि-, (आप्, c. 5.), all.<BR>p. ing (God): सर्वव्यापिन् (f. नी), S.; (my)<BR>limbs which p. the remotest corners:<BR>व्याप्त-<BR>दिगन्तानि मेऽङ्गानि, Ku. vi. 59.;<BR>(2) अश्नुते, वि-,<BR>(अश्, c. 5.),<BR>as if p. ing the world with his<BR>dignity:<BR>अश्नु वानमिव विश्वमोजसा, Ki. xii. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perverse
PERVERSE:<BR>(1) प्रतीप (f. पा);<BR>(2) कुटिल (f.<BR>ला = crooked: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perversely
PERVERSELY:<BR>(1) प्रतीपतया;<BR>(2) वामतया;<BR>(3)<BR>कौटिल्येन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perverseness
PERVERSENESS, PERVERSITY:<BR>(1) प्रतीपता;<BR>(2)<BR>वामता;<BR>(3) कौटिल्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

perversion
PERVERSION:<BR>(1) पातः<BR>or<BR>पतनम् (= fall);<BR>(2)<BR>पाषण्डपथावतारः (in religion);<BR>(3) विपर्ययः (as<BR>of taste); etc.: v. Also to pervert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pervert
PERVERT (v.):<BR>(1) दूषयति (c. of दुष्): v. To<BR>corrupt;<BR>(2) कलुषयति (nomi. = to befoul),<BR>p.<BR>ed senses:<BR>कलुषितानीन्द्रियाणि, K.;<BR>the intellect<BR>becomes p. ed:<BR>कालुष्यमुपयाति बुद्धिः, K.;<BR>(3)<BR>with subs,<BR>your intellect being p. ed:<BR>एत्य मति-<BR>विपर्ययम्, Ki. ii. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pervious
PERVIOUS: प्रवेश्य (f. श्या): v. Passable, pene-<BR>-trable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pest
PEST:<BR>I Pestilence: मारी।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>p. of<BR>the world:<BR>त्रैलोक्यकण्टकः;<BR>p. of society:<BR>लोक-<BR>दूषकः;<BR>great p.:<BR>खलशल्यम्, Ku. xvii. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pester
PESTER: बाधते (बाध्, c. 1.): v. To harass,<BR>annoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pesthouse
PESTHOUSE: *मारीशरणम्; मरकशाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pestiferous
PESTIFEROUS: मारीजनन (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp.s.: v. Pestilential.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pestilence
PESTILENCE:<BR>(1) मारिः (री),<BR>great p.:<BR>महामारी;<BR>(2) मरकः,<BR>all calamities such as p. and famine<BR>ceased on his arrival there:<BR>तत्रागत एव मरकदुर्भिक्षा-<BR>द्युपद्रवः शशाम, V. p. iv. 13. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pestilential
PESTILENTIAL:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मरकावह (f. हा);<BR>(2) मारिजनन (f. नी); and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Noxious:<BR>(1) अनिष्टकर (f. री);<BR>(2) विना-<BR>शक (f. शिका destructive).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pestle
PESTLE: मुस(ष)ल (mn.),<BR>with a p. of catechu<BR>wood:<BR>खादिरेण मुसलेन, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pet
PET (subs.):<BR>I A favourite: q. v.: वल्लभः।<BR>II A fit of peevishness: विरक्तिः, ‘in a p.’:<BR>विरक्त (f. क्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pet
PET (v.): लालयति (लल, c. 10.): v. To fond-<BR>-le.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

petal
PETAL: दलम्, with hundred p. s (the lotus): शत-<BR>दलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

petition
PETITION (subs.):<BR>I In gen.: प्रार्थना।<BR>II<BR>Written: प्रार्थना, -पत्रम्; निवेदन-<BR>or<BR>आवेदनपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

petition
PETITION (v.):<BR>(1) प्रार्थयते (अर्थ्, c. 10.): v.<BR>To ask (II);<BR>(2) आवेदनपत्रेण याचते (याच्, c.<BR>1.) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

petitioner
PETITIONER: अर्थिन् (f. नी), प्र-, अभि- (in every<BR>sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

petrifaction
PETRIFACTION: expr. by verb: v. To petrify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

petrify
PETRIFY:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) पाषाणीकरोति;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रस्तरीकरोति;<BR>(3) अश्मीकरोति: v. Stone. To<BR>be p. ed (lit. and fig.):<BR>(1) पाषाणीभवति;<BR>(2)<BR>अश्मीभवति; etc.<BR>II To stupefy: जडीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

petroleum
PETROLEUM: शिलातैलम्, Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

petticoat
PETTICOAT: शाटी (?),<BR>p. government:<BR>स्त्री-<BR>शासनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pettifogger
PETTIFOGGER, PETTIFOGGING (adj.): क्षुद्रवृत्ति<BR>(mfn.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pettiness
PETTINESS: क्षुद्रता: v. Smallness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pettish
PETTISH: कर्कश (f. शा): v. Peevish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pettishness
PETTISHNESS: कार्कश्यम्: v. Peevishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

petty
PETTY: क्षुद्र (f. द्रा),<BR>p. princes:<BR>क्षुद्रराजानः: v.<BR>Small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

petulance
PETULANCE:<BR>I Forwardness: धार्ष्ट्यम्।<BR>II<BR>Peevishness: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

petulant
PETULANT:<BR>I Forward, wanton: धृष्ट (f. ष्टा).<BR>II Peevish: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pew
PEW: मञ्चः, -कः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pewit
PEWIT: a bird: कोयष्टिः, “कोयष्टिकष्टीकते”, Mal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pewter
PEWTER: मिश्रधातुभेदः; *राङ्गसीसम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

phalanx
PHALANX:<BR>I Lit.: भोगव्यूहः।<BR>II In gen.:<BR>व्यूहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

phantasm
PHANTASM: v. Phantom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

phantastic
PHANTASTIC: v. Fantastic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

phantasy
PHANTASY: v. Fancy, imagination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

phantom
PHANTOM:<BR>I Ghost, shade: q. v.: भूत (mn.).<BR>II Fancied vision:<BR>is this a p. or my delus-<BR>ion:<BR>माया स्विदेषा मतिविभ्रमो वा, Ki. xvi. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pharisaic
PHARISAIC, -AL: expr. by comp. or gen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pharisaism
PHARISAISM:<BR>I Lit.: *पारसवं मतम्।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>बाह्यिकी धार्मिकता (?); वक्रमतम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pharisee
PHARISEE:<BR>I Lit.: *पारसवः<BR>II Fig.: दाम्भिकः:<BR>v. Hypocrite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pharmacopeia
PHARMACOPEIA: भैषज्यतत्त्वम्; भैषज्यमुक्तावली;<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pharmacy
PHARMACY: Perh. भैषज्यम्; औषधकरणम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pharmos
PHARMOS: *आलोकशरणम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

phase
PHASE:<BR>p. s of the moon:<BR>चन्द्रस्य हासवृद्धी (?);<BR>p. s of an eclipse:<BR>ग्रहणस्य प्रग्रहस्थितिमोक्षाः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pheasant
PHEASANT: जीवञ्जीवः (?); वीजनः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

phenomenon
PHENOMENON:<BR>(1) gen. by विषयः (subject)<BR>or<BR>वस्तु (n. =thing);<BR>(2) उत्पातः (extraordi-<BR>-nary p., portent).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

phial
PHIAL: काचकूपिका (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

philanthropic
PHILANTHROPIC:<BR>(1) लोकहितैषिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2)<BR>सदय (f. या = kind: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

philanthropically
PHILANTHROPICALLY:<BR>(1) लोकहितेच्छया;<BR>(2)<BR>सदयम् (= kindly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

philanthropist
