PICTORIALLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

picture
PICTURE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) चित्रम्,<BR>I think<BR>much of this representation in the picture:<BR>चित्रार्पितामहमिमां बहु मन्यमानः, Sa. vi. 17.;<BR>(2)<BR>आलेख्यम्,<BR>living only in p.:<BR>आलेख्यशेष (f. षा),<BR>R. xiv. 15.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) चित्रम्;<BR>(2) by<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

picture
PICTURE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: चित्रयति।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) मनसि करोति;<BR>(2) पर्यालोचयति (लोच्, c.<BR>10.): v. To consider, think.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

picture-frame
PICTURE-FRAME: चित्रधारणी (?); चित्राधारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

picture-gallery
PICTURE-GALLERY: चित्रावली (= pictures);<BR>चित्रशाला and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

picturesque
PICTURESQUE: विचित्र (f. त्रा), in p. language:<BR>विचित्रपदम्, Ram. Ph.:<BR>p. arrangement of<BR>words:<BR>चित्रम्, Kav. ix. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

picturesqueness
PICTURESQUENESS: वैचित्र्यम्<BR>or<BR>विचित्रता,<BR>p. of<BR>language:<BR>उक्तिवैचित्र्यम्, Kav.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piddle
PIDDLE: मूत्रयति (मूत्र्, c. 10.): v. Water, to<BR>make.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piddling
PIDDLING (adj.): क्षुद्र (f. द्रा): v. Little, trivial<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pie
PIE:<BR>I A bird: किकिः (?).<BR>II An article of<BR>food: no equiv.<BR>III In printing: *मुद्राक्षर-<BR>सङ्करः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piebald
PIEBALD: तित्तिरिकल्माष (f. षा),<BR>very good p.<BR>horses:<BR>तित्तिरिकल्माषान् हयोत्तमान्, Mah. ii. 28. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piece
PIECE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) खण्ड n. n.),<BR>a dirty<BR>rag torn to hundred p.s:<BR>शतखण्डमलिनकन्था, J. ;<BR>to p. s:<BR>खण्डखण्डम्<BR>or<BR>खण्डशः;<BR>(2) शकलम्,<BR>p. s. of<BR>rock-salt:<BR>सैन्धवशिलाशकलानि, R. v. 73.;<BR>(3)<BR>not expr. in fig. ps.,<BR>this is a p. of<BR>excellent advice:<BR>प्रकृष्टोऽयमुपदेशः;<BR>a p. of<BR>music:<BR>सङ्गीतमेकम् (?).<BR>II A gun: अस्त्रम्।<BR>III A coin: not expr.<BR>IV An indivi-<BR>-dual:<BR>(1) लोकः;<BR>(2) often not expr.,<BR>“a<BR>p. of a logician”:<BR>तार्किकः। Ph.: (a) of a p.:<BR>एकरूप (f. पा); (b)<BR>of a p. with:<BR>सदृश (f.<BR>शा): v. Like; (c)<BR>p. of eight:<BR>मुद्राविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piece
PIECE (v.): संदधाति (धा, c. 3.): v. To patch,<BR>unite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piecemeal
PIECEMEAL (adj.): खण्डशः,<BR>to tear p.:<BR>शकलयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piecework
PIECEWORK: perh. स्थिरकर्मन् (n.: comp. vern.<BR>ठिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pied
PIED (adj.):<BR>(1) तित्तिरिकल्माष (f. षा);<BR>(2)<BR>चित्रविचित्र (f. त्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pier
PIER:<BR>I Of a bridge, etc.: स्तम्भः (= pillar).<BR>II A mole: वप्रम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pier-glass
PIER-GLASS: गवाक्षदर्पणः (?) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pierage
PIERAGE: *वप्रशुल्कम्- and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pierce
PIERCE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) विध्यति, सं-, प्रति-, परि-,<BR>(व्यध्, c. 4.),<BR>p. d with arrows:<BR>ईषुभिर्विद्धः, R.<BR>ix. 60.;<BR>(2) भिनत्ति, निर्- (भिद्, c. 7. = to<BR>force a way into),<BR>grief p. d his heart:<BR>विभेद<BR> हृदयं तस्य शोकशङ्कुः, R. viii. 93.<BR>II To touch,<BR>move: चालयति, वि-, (c. of चल्).<BR>III To<BR>dive into, understand: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piercing
PIERCING (adj.):<BR>I Of men: कुशाग्रवुद्धि (mfn.):<BR>v. Acute.<BR>II Of sounds: perh. कर्णवेधिन्<BR>(f. नी): v. Shrill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piercingly
PIERCINGLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo: v.<BR>Also keenly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pierian
PIERIAN:<BR>P. spring:<BR>सरस्वतीकुण्डम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piety
PIETY:<BR>(1) धर्मिष्ठता;<BR>(2) धर्मपरायणता;<BR>(3) धार्मिकता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pig
PIG:<BR>I Prop. शूकरशावः। -कः।<BR>II Gen.: शूकरः,<BR> ग्राम्य-: v. Hog.<BR>III Of metal: perh. पिण्डः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pigeon
PIGEON:<BR>(1) पारावतः;<BR>(2) कपोतः;<BR>(3) हारीतः<BR>(= wood -p.). Ph.:<BR>p. English:<BR>*भ्रष्टेंरेजी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pigeon-hole
PIGEON-HOLE:<BR>I Lit.: कपोतविवरम्, and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR>II In paper: छिद्रम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pigeonry
PIGEONRY:<BR>(1) कपोतपालिका;<BR>(2) विटङ्कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piggery
PIGGERY:<BR>(1) शूकरगृहम्;<BR>(2) शूकरशाला;<BR>(3)<BR>शूकरकुलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pigheaded
PIGHEADED: prob. शूकरशिरस् (mfn.): v.<BR>Also obstinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pigment
PIGMENT: वर्णकः: v. Paint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pigmy
PIGMY: वामनः: v. Dwarf.<BR>The p. s:<BR>वालखिल्याः<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pigsty
PIGSTY: शूकरवृत्तिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pigtail
PIGTAIL:<BR>dressing the hair in p.:<BR>*शूकरपुच्छवत्<BR> केशानि विरचय्य।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pike
PIKE:<BR>I A weapon: perh. पट्टिशः: v. Lance,<BR>spear.<BR>II A fish: जलसूचिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pikeman
PIKEMAN: पट्टिशधारिन् (f. णी) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pilaster
PILASTER: *भुत्तिस्तम्भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pilchard
PILCHARD: मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pile
PILE (subs.):<BR>I A heap: q. v.: राशिः।<BR>II<BR>Funeral: चिता (rarely चित्या and चितिः),<BR>make a p., I will follow my lord:<BR>विरचय<BR> चितामनुसरामि जीवितेश्वरम्, K.;<BR>make a p. for<BR>me:<BR>कुरु मे चिताम्, Ku. iv. 35.<BR>III Edifice:<BR>q. v.: हर्भ्यम्।<BR>IV A timber: स्थूणा। V. Hair:<BR>बालः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pile
PILE (v.): समा-चिनोति (चि, c. 5.): v. To<BR>heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pile-driver
PILE-DRIVER: *स्थूणाचोदनयन्त्रम् and sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piles
PILES: अर्शस् (n.),<BR>internal p.:<BR>अदृश्यान्यर्शांसि, Sr.;<BR>ointments for p.:<BR>अर्शसामालेपाः;<BR>suffering from<BR>p.:<BR>अर्शोभिरुपद्रुतः (ता, तं), Sr.<BR>or<BR>अर्शसः (सा,<BR> सं), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pilfer
PILFER: मुष्णाति (मुष्, c. 9.): v. To steal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pilferer
PILFERER: मोषकः: v. Thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pilfering
PILFERING (subs.): मोषः: v. Theft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pilgrim
PILGRIM:<BR>(1) तीर्थयात्रिकः;<BR>(2) तीर्थानुसारिन् (m.),<BR>V. s.;<BR>(3) यात्रिकः (when sense clear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pilgrimage
PILGRIMAGE:<BR>(1) तीर्थयात्रा,<BR>desirous of p.:<BR>तीर्थ-<BR>यात्राभिलाषी, D.;<BR>(2) तीर्थाभिगमनम्, Mah.; and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR>Place of p.:<BR>तीर्थम्।<BR>P. to the<BR>Ganges:<BR>गङ्गायात्रा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pill
PILL: वटिका। Ph.: it was a bitter p. to swallow:<BR>*असह्यमीदृशं श्रोतुं परुषं कर्णकर्कशम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pillage
PILLAGE (subs.): विलुण्ठनम्: v. Plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pillage
PILLAGE (v.): विलुण्ठति (लुण्ठ्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pillager
PILLAGER: वि-लुण्ठकः: v. Plunderer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pillar
PILLAR: स्तम्भः,<BR>it is not supported by p. s:<BR>स्तम्भैर्न<BR> च धृता सा तु, Mah. ii. 11. 14. Ph.:<BR>p. of<BR>state:<BR>राज्यरक्षकः, राजस्तम्भाधारः (com. v. iii.<BR>17.) and sim. comp.s.<BR>P. ed:<BR>स्तम्भोपेत<BR>(f. ता) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pillion
PILLION: पर्याणम् (?), -च्छदः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pillory
PILLORY: *स्तम्भबन्धः; हडिः, William.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pillow
PILLOW (subs.): उपाधानम्,<BR>a couch with many<BR>p. s:<BR>बहूपाधाना कुथा, K.;<BR>(2) उपबर्हः;<BR>(3)<BR>बालिशम्;<BR>(4) गण्डुः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pillow
PILLOW (v.): उपदधाति (धा, c. 3.): v. To put,<BR>prop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pilot
PILOT (subs.): *जलमानविद् (mfn.) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pilot
PILOT (v.): मार्गं दर्शयति (c. of दृश् with gen.):<BR>v. Way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pilotage
PILOTAGE: *जलमानविदां मूल्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pimp
PIMP (subs.):<BR>(1) विटः;<BR>(2) सुरततालः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pimp
PIMP (v.): स्त्रीः<BR>or<BR>नारीः संयोजयति (c. of युज्), or<BR>सज्जयति (c. of सज्ज्),<BR>or<BR>संश्लेषयति (c. of श्लिष्),<BR>or<BR>संगमयति (c. of गम्), M. viii. 362.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pimple
PIMPLE: स्फोटः, -कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pimpled
PIMPLED, PIMPLY:<BR>(1) स्फोटिन् (f. नो);<BR>(2)<BR>स्फोटकिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pin
PIN (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: perh. सूचिः।<BR>II A peg:<BR>कीलः, -कः।<BR>III Fig.: तृणम्: v. Straw, care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pin
PIN (v.):<BR>I Lit.: सूच्या बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.).<BR>II To confine: q. v.: संरुणद्धि (रुध्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pincers
PINCERS:<BR>(1) संदशः;<BR>(2) कङ्कमुखम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pinch
PINCH (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: expr. by verb: v.<BR>Pinch (I)<BR>II Pressure, oppression: q. v.:<BR>सम्पीडनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pinch
PINCH (v.):<BR>I With the fingers: चर्म कृन्तति<BR>(कृत्, c. 7.: ?).<BR>II To squeeze or press<BR>hard.:<BR>(1) सं-पीडयति (पीड्, c. 10.);<BR>(2)<BR>सं-बाधते (बाध्, c. 1.). Ph.:<BR>p. ed with cold<BR>and hunger:<BR>शीतार्तश्च क्षुधार्तश्च, P. 3. 7.:<BR>p. ing<BR>poverty:<BR>दुःसहदारिद्र्यम्। and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pincushion
PINCUSHION: सूच्याधार and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pine
PINE (subs.): देवदारुः (a kind of p. Use n. for<BR>wood).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pine
PINE (v.):<BR>I To p. away: अङ्गेषु परिहीयते (pass.<BR>of हा), Sa. iii.: v. Also to languish.<BR>II<BR>To p. for:<BR>(1) ताम्यति (तम्, c. 4. = to be<BR>distressed);<BR>(2) अवसीदति (सद्, c. 1. = to<BR>droop).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pineapple
PINEAPPLE: भूपनसः<BR>or<BR>नानारसः (??) (Use n. for<BR>the fruit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pinion
PINION (subs.): पक्षः: v. Wing, feather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pinion
PINION (v.): बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.): v. To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pink
PINK (subs.):<BR>I A plant: लताविशेषः।<BR>II Its<BR>flower: *पिङ्कम्।<BR>III A colour: पाटलवर्णः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pink
PINK (adj.): पाटलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pink
PINK (v.): विध्यति (व्यध्, c. 4.): v. To pierce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pin-money
PIN-MONEY: बाह्यव्ययार्थं धनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pinnace
PINNACE: a boat: *पीनासम् (comp. vern.<BR>पिनिस).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pinnacle
PINNACLE:<BR>I A turret: q. v.: अट्टः।<BR>II<BR>Summit: q. v.: शिखरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pint
PINT: मानविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pioneer
PIONEER:<BR>I Lit.: स्थाणुच्छेदकः।<BR>II Fig.: मार्ग-<BR>दर्शकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pious
PIOUS:<BR>(1) धार्मिक (f. की);<BR>(2) धर्मनिष्ठ (f.<BR>ष्ठा);<BR>(3) धर्मपरायण (f. णा);<BR>(4) धर्मप्रवण (f.<BR>णा); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piously
PIOUSLY:<BR>(1) धार्मिकतया etc.;<BR>(2) better by<BR>adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pip
PIP (v.): चूंकरोति, “कमाहूय चिराय चूंकृतैः”, N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pip
PIP (subs.):<BR>I Of fruits: बीजम्।<BR>II In<BR>fowls: रोगविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pipe
PIPE (subs.):<BR>I Musical:<BR>(1) वंशः, -शी;<BR>(2) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">Page523</a>]<BR>वेणुः;<BR>(3) मुरली।<BR>II A tube: नाली (?).<BR>III<BR>For smoking: धूपनाली (?).<BR>IV A cask:<BR>कुण्डम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pipe
PIPE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: वेणुं वादयति (c. of वद्).<BR>II<BR>To cry: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piper
PIPER:<BR>(1) वांशिकः;<BR>(2) वेणुवादकः;<BR>(3) वंशीधरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pipkin
PIPKIN: स्थाली (gen. term): v. Boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piquancy
PIQUANCY:<BR>(1) तीक्ष्णता (= pungency);<BR>(2)<BR>सरसता (in fig. sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piquant
PIQUANT:<BR>I Lit.: तीक्ष्ण (f. क्ष्णा): v. Pun-<BR>-gent.<BR>II Fig.: सरस (f. सा = flavoured,<BR>witty).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piquantly
PIQUANTLY:<BR>(1) तीक्ष्णम्;<BR>(2) सरसम्: for dif.:<BR>v. Above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pique
PIQUE (subs.):<BR>(1) विरक्तिः (dislike);<BR>(2)<BR>often by कलिः (= quarrel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pique
PIQUE (v.): expr. by विरक्त (f. क्ता)<BR>or<BR>रुष्ट<BR>(f. ष्टा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piracy
PIRACY:<BR>I Lit.: समुद्रदस्युता and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Fig.: चौर्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pirate
PIRATE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: समुद्रदस्युः and sim.<BR>comp.s: v. Robber.<BR>II A vessel: दस्युपोतः<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pirate
PIRATE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: समुद्रे दस्युतां करोति।<BR>II<BR>Fig.: चोरयति (चुर्, c. 10.),<BR>p. d poem:<BR>चोरितं<BR> काव्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piratical
PIRATICAL: expr. by comp.,<BR>p. vessel:<BR>दस्यु-<BR>पोतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piscatory
PISCATORY: मत्स्य-<BR>or<BR>मीन- in comp.: v. Fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pish
PISH (interj.): perh. अरे<BR>or<BR>अरे रे।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pismire
PISMIRE: पिपीलिकाः v. Ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piss
PISS:<BR>I Subs: मूत्रम्।<BR>II Verb.: मूत्रयति, अव-,<BR>(मूत्र्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pistil
PISTIL: गर्भकेशरः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pistol
PISTOL: no equiv.: *हस्तासम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pistole
PISTOLE: हिस्पानीयसुवर्णमुद्राविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piston
PISTON: *सम्पीडनी; सम्पीडननाली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pit
PIT (subs.):<BR>I A hole:<BR>(1) गर्तः;<BR>(2) अवटः,<BR>putting the body in a p.:<BR>कबन्धमवटे कृत्वा (rare),<BR>Ram.;<BR>(3) गह्वरम्। (prop. a cave),<BR>thus men<BR>are thrown in p. s of impropriety:<BR>एवं पुंमासोऽयुक्त-<BR>गह्वरे पात्यन्ते, Vi. v.<BR>II Arm-p.: q. v.: कक्षः।<BR>III, The grave: q. v.<BR>IV of the<BR>stomach: मणिपूरम्। V. Of a theatre: perh.<BR>अङ्गणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pit
PIT (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>his face is p. ted by small-<BR>pox:<BR>*आननं तस्य विस्फोटकेन चिह्नितम्।<BR>II To<BR>set to fight: योद्धुमुत्साहयति (c. of सह्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitapat
PITAPAT:<BR>to go p.:<BR>धुरधुरायते (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitch
PITCH (v. t.):<BR>I To fling, cast: q. v.: क्षिपति<BR>(क्षिप्, c. 6.).<BR>II Of tents: रचयति, वि-,<BR>(रच्, c. 10.); सज्जयति (c. of सज्ज्), M. n.;<BR>प्रतिविदधाति (धा, c. 3.), R. xiii. 79.<BR>III Of<BR>times: सं-स्थापयति (c. of स्था).<BR>IV Of prices:<BR>स्थिरीकरोति।<BR>V To smear with p.: तिन्दुना<BR> लिम्पति (लिप, c. 6.) etc. Ph.: p. ed battle:<BR>तुमुलं युद्धम्, Mah. viii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitch
PITCH (v. i.):<BR>I To alight, fall: q. v.: पतति<BR>(पत्, c. 1.).<BR>II To p. upon, select: वृणोति<BR>(वृ, c. 5.).<BR>III Of ships: याति (या, c. 2.),<BR>क्षणमूर्द्ध मधः क्षणम्, K. s. 25. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitch
PITCH (subs.):<BR>I The resin: तिन्दु, -कम्।<BR>II<BR>Degree of elevation:<BR>highest, lowest p.:<BR>परा<BR> कोटिः, K.<BR>III In music:<BR>at the highest p. of<BR>the voice:<BR>अत्युच्चैःस्वरेण।<BR>IV Declivity, slope:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitcher
PITCHER:<BR>(1) कमण्डलु (mn.);<BR>(2) आरुः;<BR>(3) घटी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitchfork
PITCHFORK: v. Fork.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitchy
PITCHY:<BR>I Lit.: तिन्दुलिप्त (f. प्ता) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>p. darkness:<BR>सूचिभेद्यं तमः<BR>or<BR>अन्धतमसम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piteous
PITEOUS: करुण (f. णा): v. Pitiable, pitiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piteously
PITEOUSLY: करुणम्: v. Pitiably, pitifully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

piteousness
PITEOUSNESS: दीनता (= wretchedness); or by<BR>adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitfall
PITFALL:<BR>(1) छन्नगर्तः and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(2)<BR>गह्वरम्: v. Pit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pith
PITH:<BR>I Lit.: मज्जन् (n.)<BR>or<BR>मज्जा (f.).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>सारः, Ki. xi. 39.: v. Essence, spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pithiness
PITHINESS:<BR>I Lit.: मज्जाबहुलता।<BR>II Fig.: सार-<BR>वत्ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pithless
PITHLESS:<BR>(1) असारः<BR>or<BR>निःसारः (रा, रं);<BR>(2)<BR>फल्गु (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pithy
PITHY:<BR>I Lit.: मज्जाबहुलः (ला, लं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) सारवत् (f. ती);<BR>(2)<BR>सारगर्भ (f. र्भा);<BR>(3) ससारः (रा, रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitiable
PITIABLE:<BR>(1) करुण (f. णा), (I) have reached<BR>this p. condition: प्रपन्ना करुणामवस्थाम्, R. xvi. 10.;<BR>(2) दीनः (ना, नं) ( miserable: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitiably
PITIABLY:<BR>(1) करुणम्;<BR>(2) दीनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitiful
PITIFUL:<BR>I Merciful, kind: q. v.:<BR>(1) करुणा-<BR>मय (f. यी);<BR>(2) कारुणिक (f. की).<BR>II Piti-<BR>-able: करुण (f. णा),<BR>in p. words:<BR>करुणार्थग्रथितम्,<BR>R. viii. 70.<BR>III Paltry, mean: q. v.: क्षुद्र<BR>(f. द्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitifully
PITIFULLY:<BR>I Mercifully, kindly: q. v.:<BR>सकरुणम्।<BR>II Piteously: करुणम्, (they) spoke p.:<BR>करुणममिहितम्, Ki. x. 58.<BR>III Meanly:<BR>p.<BR>dressed:<BR>दीनवेश (f. शा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitifulness
PITIFULNESS:<BR>(1) कारुण्यम्;<BR>(2) दीनता (= wret-<BR>-chedness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitiless
PITILESS: निष्करुण (f. णा): v. Merciless, un-<BR>-kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitilessly
PITILESSLY: निष्करुणम्: v. Unmercifully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitman
PITMAN: आवटिक (f. की ??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pittance
PITTANCE: no equiv.: perh. कल्यवर्तः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pity
PITY (subs.): करणा<BR>or<BR>कारुण्यम्: v. Mercy, kind-<BR>-ness. Ph.:<BR>it is a great p.:<BR>इदमतीव दुःखाकरम्:<BR>v. Distressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pity
PITY (v.):<BR>(1) करुणां करोति (with loc.);<BR>(2)<BR>दयते (दय्, c. 1.: with acc. or gen.),<BR>why<BR>don't you p. me:<BR>ममापि किं नो दयसे, N. ix. 98.;<BR>(8) अनुकम्पते (कम्प्, c. 1. = to shew kindness<BR>for) “गिरानुकम्पस्व”, N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pitying
PITYING (adj.): सकरुण (f. णा): v. Pitiful,<BR>compassionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pityingly
PITYINGLY: सकरुणम्: v. Compassionately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pivot
PIVOT: योगकीलः (?); विवर्तनकीलः, Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

placability
PLACABILITY:<BR>(1) क्षमाशीलता;<BR>(2) तितिक्षुता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

placable
PLACABLE:<BR>(1) क्षमाशील (f. ला);<BR>(2) बहुक्षम<BR>(f. मा), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

placard
PLACARD (subs): घोषणापत्रम्, and sim. comp.s.<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

placard
PLACARD (v.):<BR>I Lit.: घोषणापत्रं निदधाति (धा,<BR>c. 3.): v. To put.<BR>II To notify: घोषयति,<BR> परि-, (घुष्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

placate
PLACATE: शमयति (c. of शम्): v. To appease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

place
PLACE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) स्थानम् (best<BR>equiv.),<BR>should not leave one's p.:<BR>स्वस्थानं न<BR>परित्यजेत्, H.;<BR>(2) भूमिः<BR>or<BR>भूः, make p. s on (the<BR>roof)<BR>of the palace:<BR>क्रियन्तां प्रासादस्योपरि भूमयः,<BR>Mu. iii;<BR>(3) स्थलम्, Ph.: in this p., in that p.:<BR>अत्र, तत्रः v. Here, there, etc.;<BR>nor falsehood<BR>has any p. in you:<BR>नानृतं त्वयि तिष्ठति, Mah.<BR>II<BR>Room: q. v.: स्थानम्।<BR>III Rank:<BR>(1) स्थानम्:<BR>(2) भूमिः,<BR>want my p.:<BR>मदीयां भूमिं कामयन्ते, Mu.<BR>IV With the idea of substitution:<BR>(1) स्थानम्;<BR>some read Lāsikā in the p. of Vilāsikā:<BR>केचिद्वि-<BR>लासिकास्थाने लासिकेति पठन्ति, Sah.;<BR>(2) भूमिः,<BR>here I am in the p. of your comrades:<BR>अयं जनः ते<BR> सखीभूमौ वर्तते, Sah. iii. V. Denoting succes-<BR>-sion: by adv.,<BR>in the first p.:<BR>प्रथमम्;<BR>in the<BR>next p.:<BR>अपरम् (= again). Ph.: to take p.:<BR>v. To happen; out of p. expr. by अस्थानम्,<BR>Ki. xi. 68.<BR>or<BR>असाम्प्रतम्, Si. ii. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

place
PLACE (v.): स्थापयति (c. of स्था): v. To put.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

placid
PLACID: शान्त (f. न्ता): v. Quiet, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

placidly
PLACIDLY: expr. by adj. or comp.: v. Also<BR>quietly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

placidness
PLACIDNESS, PLACIDITY: प्र-शान्तता: v. Calm-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plagiarism
PLAGIARISM: expr. by चौर्यम् (= theft), as<BR>काव्यचौर्यम् (poetical), उक्तिचौर्यम् (of language),<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plagiarist
PLAGIARIST: काव्यचौरः, उक्तिचौरः, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plagiarize
PLAGIARIZE: चोरयति (चुर्, c. 10. = to steal:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plague
PLAGUE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मारिः(री);<BR>(2)<BR>मरकः, V. p. iv. 13. 53. Ph.:<BR>cattle-p.:<BR>पशूनां<BR> मरणरोगः, Ka. xiii. 64.<BR>II Any great cala-<BR>-mity:<BR>(1) उत्पातः;<BR>(2) उपद्रवः।<BR>III A pest:<BR>(1) शल्यम्;<BR>(2) कण्टकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plague
PLAGUE (v.):<BR>I To vex: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>infest with p.: expr. by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plaice
PLAICE, PLAISE: मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plain
PLAIN (subs.):<BR>(1) समभूमिः;<BR>(2) समस्थलम्, -ली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plain
PLAIN (adj.):<BR>I Smooth, level: q. v.: सम<BR>(f. मा).<BR>II Clear, evident: q. v.: स्पष्ट (f.<BR>ष्टा),<BR>in p.:<BR>स्पष्टम्।<BR>III Open, public: q. v.:<BR>प्रकाश (f. शा).<BR>IV Frank, sincere: q. v.:<BR>स्फुटमाषिन् (f. णी = p. spoken).<BR>V Homely,<BR>simple:<BR>(1) सहज (f. जा = natural, as of p. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">Page525</a>]<BR>tune);<BR>(2) सामान्य (f. न्या = common, as of<BR>p. dress);<BR>(3) असंस्कृत (f. ता = unadorned,<BR>poor: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plain-dealing
PLAIN-DEALING:<BR>I Adj.: ऋजु (mfn.): v.<BR>Sincere.<BR>II Subs.: आर्जवम्: v. Sincerity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plainly
PLAINLY:<BR>I Clearly, perspicuously: q. v.:<BR>स्पष्टम्।<BR>II Unreservedly, sincerely:<BR>(1)<BR>निर्व्याजम्;<BR>(2) निष्कपटम्।<BR>III In other senses:<BR>expr. by adj. or comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plainness
PLAINNESS:<BR>I Clearness, perspicuity: q. v.:<BR>स्पष्टता।<BR>II Outspokenness: स्फुटाभषिता।<BR>III<BR>Evenness: समता।<BR>IV Openness: प्रकाशता:<BR>v. Simplicity: expr. by adj., p. of dress:<BR>सामान्यवेषः: v. Plain (V.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plaint
PLAINT: प्रतिज्ञा,<BR>the p. is the most important part<BR>of a law-suit:<BR>सारस्तु व्यवहाराणां प्रतिज्ञा समुदाहृता,<BR>N. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plaintiff
PLAINTIFF:<BR>(1) वादिन् (f. नी), Si. xx. 18.;<BR>(2) अर्थिन् (f. नी), कार्य-, Mr. ix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plaintive
PLAINTIVE:<BR>I Complaining:<BR>(1) परिदेविन्<BR>(f. नी);<BR>(2) by comp.<BR>II Sad, sorrow-<BR>-ful: q. v.: शोकावह (f. हा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plaintively
PLAINTIVELY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plaintiveness
PLAINTIVENESS: शोकावहता: v. Sadness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plait
PLAIT (subs.):<BR>I A fold: भङ्गिः।<BR>II A braid:<BR>कवरी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plait
PLAIT (v.): v. To fold, braid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plan
PLAN (subs.):<BR>I Project, design:<BR>(1) उपायः,<BR>devise some p.:<BR>उपायः क्रियताम्, H. ii.;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रयोगः ( employment of means),<BR>ask for the<BR>success of the p.:<BR>प्रयोगसिद्धिं पृच्छ, Mal. i.;<BR>(3)<BR>मन्त्रणा (= plot).<BR>II A sketch: चित्रलिपिः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plan
PLAN (v.):<BR>I To devise: उपायं करोति,<BR>p. ned<BR>his death:<BR>तस्य वधोपायं चकार<BR>or<BR>वधं मन्त्रयामास।<BR>II To design: चित्रलिपिं करोति (??,: with<BR>gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plane
PLANE (adj.): सम (f. मा), p. trigonometry:<BR>*समत्रिकोणमितिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plane
PLANE (subs.):<BR>I In geo.: *समक्षेत्रम्; धरातलम्,<BR>where two p. s meet:<BR>धरातलयोः सम्पातः, K.<BR>d.<BR>II The tool: तक्षणी, Williams.<BR>III<BR>tree: वृक्षविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plane
PLANE (v.): समीकरोति (कृ, c. 8.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

planet
PLANET: ग्रहः,<BR>superior, inferior p.:<BR>अधःस्थः,<BR> ऊर्द्धस्थो ग्रहः (after Su.).<BR>Minor p.:<BR>उपग्रहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

planetary
PLANETARY: expr. by tat. comp., p. orbit:<BR>ग्रहकक्षा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plank
PLANK (subs.):<BR>(1) फलक (mn.);<BR>(2) काष्ठफलक<BR>(mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plank
PLANK (v.) फलकैः आवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.): v. To<BR>cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plant
PLANT (subs.):<BR>(1) लता;<BR>(2) ओषधिः (annual<BR>p.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plant
PLANT (v.):<BR>I Lit.: रोपयति, आ-, अभि-, (c. of<BR>रुह्), trees are to be p. ed on (the banks of) tanks:<BR>तडागे वृक्षा रोप्याः, He.; p. ing of the Peepul:<BR>पिप्पलारोपणम्, He.:<BR>in trees p. ed by my friend<BR>herself:<BR>द्रुमेषु सख्या कृतजन्मसु स्वयम्, Ku. v. 60.<BR>II To set up, put: q. v.: स्थापयति (c. of<BR>स्था).<BR>III To found, settle: q. v.: स्थापयति।<BR>IV To fit out with plants: वृक्षान् रोपयति<BR>(with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plantain
PLANTAIN:<BR>(1) कदली (both the tree and its<BR>fruit);<BR>(2) रम्भा, with thighs like (the body of)<BR>the p.:) रम्मोरूः, R. vi. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plantation
PLANTATION:<BR>I The act: रोपः, -णम्, आ-।<BR>II<BR>The place:<BR>(1) क्षेत्रम् (= field), sugarcane p.:<BR>इक्षुक्षेत्रम्;<BR>(2) वृक्षवाटिका (= garden: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

planter
PLANTER:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) रोपक (f. पिका), आ-;<BR>(2) रोपयितृ (f. त्री), आ-, “वृक्षारोपयितुः”, He.<BR>II Owner of a plantation: tea-p.s:<BR>*चाक्षेत्रिकाः<BR>or<BR>-क्षेत्रस्वामिनः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plash
PLASH (subs.):<BR>(1) आघातः<BR>or<BR>अभिघातः (= strik-<BR>-ing);<BR>(2) संघट्टः (= collision), “वारिसंघट्टजो<BR> रवः,” Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plash
PLASH (v.):<BR>p. ing of water:<BR>जलास्फालनम्, R.<BR>xvi. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plaster
PLASTER (subs.):<BR>I For covering walls:<BR>चूर्णवालुलेपः (??).<BR>II For wounds: उपनाहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plaster
PLASTER (v.): लेपं<BR>or<BR>उपनाहं ददाति (दा, c. 3.:<BR>with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plasterer
PLASTERER: लेपक (f. पिका), वि-, प्र- (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plastic
PLASTIC:<BR>I Lit.: रूपद (f. दा) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR>II Produced by moulding:<BR>perh. गठित (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plat
PLAT (subs.): Of ground: v. Plot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plate
PLATE (subs.):<BR>I A vessel:<BR>(1) पात्रम्;<BR>(2)<BR>भाजनम्,<BR>p. for eating:<BR>भोजनभाजनम्, N.<BR>II. En-<BR>-graved p.:<BR>(1) फलकम्,<BR>copper-p.:<BR>ताम्रफलकम्;<BR>(2) पत्रम्,<BR>p. s of grant:<BR>नियमपत्राणि, M. n. on<BR>Si. xiv. 36.<BR>III Wrought gold and silver.<BR>(1) कोशः (ambiguous);<BR>(2) कृते हेमरूप्ये, A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plate
PLATE (v.): रजतपत्रेण आवृणोति (वृ, c. 5. = to<BR>cover: q. v. ?),<BR>p. d:<BR>रजतपत्रावृत (f. ता): v.<BR>Overlay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

platform
PLATFORM: expr. by मञ्चः<BR>or<BR>मण्डपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

platinum
PLATINUM: no equiv.: महारजतम् may by used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

platonic
PLATONIC: *प्राक्तनीयः (या, यं); प्लाटुनीयः (या,<BR> यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

platonism
PLATONISM: *प्राक्तनमतम्; प्लाटुनमतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

platonist
PLATONIST: *प्राक्तनमतावलम्बिन् (f. नी); प्लाटुनमत-<BR>वादिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

platoon
PLATOON: गुल्मः: v. Company.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

platter
PLATTER: भोजनपात्रम्<BR>or<BR>-भाजनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plaudit
PLAUDIT: प्रशंसावाच् (f.): v. Acclamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plausibility
PLAUSIBILITY: न्याय्यामासता and sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plausible
PLAUSIBLE: expr. by circumlo.,<BR>and what you<BR>have asked appears p.:<BR>यथेतरन्न्याय्यमिवावभासते,<BR>Ki. xiv. 7.: v. Also probable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plausibly
PLAUSIBLY: expr. by circumlo.: v. Plausible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

play
PLAY (subs.):<BR>I In gen. sense:<BR>(1) क्रीडा,<BR>this is mere p.:<BR>क्रीडामात्रमेतत्, Ra. ii.;<BR>in all<BR>boy's p. s:<BR>बालक्रीडासु सर्वासु, Mah. i. 126. 15.;<BR>real p.:<BR>प्रकृतक्रीडनम्, D. vi.; p. ing in water:<BR>जलक्रीडा, Mah.; at p.: v. To play;<BR>(2)<BR>खेला<BR>or<BR>खेलनम् (rare): v. Also gambling.<BR>II<BR>A drama: नाटकम्।<BR>III Dramatic show:<BR>अभिनयः<BR>IV Motion, movement: q. v.:<BR>चारः,<BR>p. of the feet:<BR>पादचारः, D. vi.<BR>V Ac-<BR>-tion; use: q. v.:<BR>foul p.:<BR>दुश्चे ष्टितम्;<BR>fair<BR>p.:<BR>न्याय्याचारः, (?).<BR>VI Scope: प्रसरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

play
PLAY (v. i.):<BR>I To frolic, sport:<BR>(1)<BR>क्रीडति (क्रीड्, c. 1.), I will just p.:<BR>क्रीडिष्यामि तावत्, V. iii.; we will p. here:<BR>इहैव क्रीडामः, Ra. i.;<BR>(2) खेलति (खेल्,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>of the p. ing boys:<BR>खेलतां वटूनाम्,<BR>U. iv.;<BR>I wish to play with snakes before<BR>Rākṣasa:<BR>इच्छामि राक्षसस्य पुरतः सर्पैः खेलितुम्,<BR>Mu. ii.<BR>II Fig., to trifle: क्रीडति, p. ing<BR>with Anūra for a long time:<BR>अनूरेण चिरं कालं<BR> क्रीडित्वा, V. p. v. 20. 61.<BR>III To gamble:<BR>(1) क्रीडति,<BR>to p. dice.<BR>द्यूतं क्रीडति, Mr. ii.;<BR>(2)<BR>खेलति,<BR>to p. for love:<BR>विना पणेन<BR>or<BR>आमोदार्थं<BR> खेलति (?).<BR>IV On a musical instrument:<BR>वादयति (c. of वद्),<BR>to play on a lute:<BR>वीणां<BR> वादयति, H.<BR>V. On the stage: अभिनयति (नी,<BR>c. 1.): v. To act. Ph.:<BR>to p. a king:<BR>राजायते;<BR>to p. a trick:<BR>क्रीडति;<BR>to p. off:<BR>प्रयुंक्ते (युज्, c.<BR>7.): v. To use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

play-bill
PLAY-BILL: *अभिनयपत्रम्; अभिनयसूची।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

player
PLAYER:<BR>I On the stage: अभिनेतृ (f. त्री):<BR>v. Actor.<BR>II A gambler: q. v.: कितवः,<BR>opposite p.:<BR>प्रतिकितवः, D. ii.<BR>III On an<BR>instrument: वादकः,<BR>p. s. played drums:<BR>वादका<BR> वादयामासुर्भेरीः, Mah. v. 156. 27.: v. To<BR>play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

play-fellow
PLAY-FELLOW, PLAY-MATE:<BR>(1) सहक्रीडकः (?);<BR>(2) सहखेलिन् (m (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

playful
PLAYFUL:<BR>I Given to play: क्रीडासक्त (f. क्ता)<BR>and sim. comp. s,<BR>boys are p.:<BR>बालास्तावत् क्रीडा-<BR>सक्ताः, J.<BR>II. Of acts, etc. क्रीडा- in comp.:<BR>v. Also sportive, merry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

playfully
PLAYFULLY:<BR>I Of acts, etc.:<BR>(1) क्रीड्या;<BR>(2)<BR>क्रीडापूर्वम्;<BR>(3) परिहासेन (= in jest).<BR>II Of<BR>men: by adj., V. p. v. 6. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

playground
PLAYGROUND: रङ्गः, -भूमिः, V. p 20. 31., Mah.<BR>i. 132. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

playhouse
PLAYHOUSE: रङ्गः, -शाला: v. Theatre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plaything
PLAYTHING:<BR>(1) क्रीडनकम्, saw (the gem)<BR>Syam-<BR>antaka made a boy's p.:<BR>कुमारक्रीडनकीकृतं स्यमन्तकं<BR> ददर्श, V. p. iv. 13. 23.;<BR>God plays with beings<BR>like boys with p.s:<BR>क्रीडते भगवान् भूतैर्बालः<BR> क्रीडनकैरिव, Mah. iii. 30, 37.;<BR>(2) खेलनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

playwright
PLAYWRIGHT: आख्यायिकाकारः (?), C. 2.; नाटक-<BR>कारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plea
PLEA:<BR>I In law: कारणोत्तरम्, Mit.<BR>II Ex-<BR>-cuse, pretext: व्यपदेशः।<BR>III Lawsuit: q. v.<BR>IV Prayer: प्रार्थना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plead
PLEAD:<BR>I To enter a plea: उत्त ददाति (दा,<BR>c. 3.).<BR>To p. not guilty:<BR>अदोषोऽस्मीति वदति<BR>(वद्, c. 1.),<BR>to p. justification, etc.:<BR>प्रत्यवस्कन्दनं<BR> करोति (lit. to attack in return), Mit.; to [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">Page527</a>]<BR>allow a person to p.:<BR>उत्तरं दापयति (c. of दा),<BR>Mit.<BR>II To defend, argue:<BR>he p. ed your<BR>case very ably:<BR>*स युक्तियुक्तं तवार्थं निपुणं प्रतिपाद-<BR>यामास।<BR>III To make an excuse: expr. by<BR>subs.,<BR>p. ing headache:<BR>शिरःशूलव्यपदेशेन।<BR>IV<BR>To entreat: q. v.: याचते (याच्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pleader
PLEADER: No equiv.: *अभिभाषकः: v. Ad-<BR>-vocate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pleading
PLEADING (subs.): उत्तरवादः, etc.; better by<BR>verb: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pleasant
PLEASANT:<BR>I Agreeable, delightful: q. v.:<BR>मनोज्ञ (f. ज्ञा).<BR>II Affable: q. v.: मिष्टभाषिन्<BR>(f. णी).<BR>III Pleasing: q. v.: सुखावह (f. हा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pleasantly
PLEASANTLY: सुखेन (= with pleasure); gen.<BR>by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pleasantness
PLEASANTNESS:<BR>I Agreeableness:<BR>(1) मनोज्ञता;<BR>(2) हृद्यता;<BR>(3) अभिरामता;<BR>(4) रम्यता;<BR>(5)<BR>रमणीयता;<BR>(6) रुचिरता;<BR>(7) काम्यता;<BR>(8) कमनीयता।<BR>II Sweetness: q. v.: मधुरता।<BR>III Pleasur-<BR>-ableness: सुखावहता and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pleasantry
PLEASANTRY:<BR>(1) सुखम् (= pleasure);<BR>(2)<BR>परिहासः (= joke);<BR>(3) नर्मभाषितम् (= sprightly<BR>saying), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

please
PLEASE (v. t.):<BR>I To delight: q. v.: सुखयति,<BR>the same rays of the moon p. the body:<BR>पादास्त<BR> एव शशिनः सुखयन्ति गात्रम्, V. iii.<BR>II To<BR>satisfy: q. v.: प्रीणाति or प्रीणयति (प्री, c. 9.<BR>and 10.) when Śiva will be p. d (with you):<BR>प्रीते पिनाकिनि, Ki. xi. 81. Ph.: to be p. d.<BR>to<BR>.: not expr., His Majesty Chandragupta<BR>is p. d to command:<BR>देवश्चन्द्रगुप्तः समाज्ञापयति, Mu.<BR>iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

please
PLEASE (v. i.):<BR>(1) by passive imperative or<BR>occasionally by sim. imper,<BR>p. sit here:<BR>इत<BR> आस्यताम्, U. i.;<BR>p. take this seat:<BR>इदमासनम्,<BR> उपविशत्वार्यः, Mu. ii.;<BR>(2) by अर्हति (अर्ह, c. 1.),<BR>अनुगृह्णाति (ग्रह, c. 9.),<BR>or<BR>प्रसीदति (सद्, c. 1.),<BR>p. put on these ornaments:<BR>इमान्याभरणानि<BR> धारयितुमर्हत्यार्यः, Mu. ii.;<BR>p. promise:<BR>प्रसीद<BR> सन्धेहि, Ki. i. 42. Ph.:<BR>as you p.:<BR>यदभिरोचते<BR> भवते,<BR>V ii. (note also यदाज्ञापयति देवः,<BR>Mal. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pleasing
PLEASING (adj.):<BR>I Gratifying:<BR>(1) by verb,<BR>it is not as p. that you are without your friend:<BR>न तथा नन्दयसि मां सख्या विरहिता तया, V. ii. 13.;<BR>(2) सुखावह (f. हा);<BR>(3) सुखकर (f. री); etc.<BR>II Charming, delightful: q. v.: रम्य (f. म्या),<BR>it is easy to be p. in this world:<BR>सुलभा रम्यता<BR> लोके, Ki. xi. 11.;<BR>of p. deportment:<BR>रम्यहावाः,<BR>Ki. xi. 1. Ph.:<BR>p. to the ear:<BR>सुखश्रव (f. वा):<BR>श्रुतिमधुर (f. रा) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pleasurable
PLEASURABLE: सुखावह (f. हा): v. Pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pleasure
PLEASURE:<BR>I Opposed to pain:<BR>(1) सुखम्,<BR>I do not seek p.:<BR>न सुखं प्रार्थये, Ki. xi. 66.;<BR>the<BR>p. s of affluence:<BR>ऐश्वर्यसुखानि, K.;<BR>the p. of<BR>reciprocity:<BR>व्यतिकरसुखम्, Sa. iii. 27.;<BR>(2) सन्तोषः<BR>(= gratification);<BR>(3) आनन्दः (= delight).<BR>II Will, command: q. v.: इच्छा, at his p.:<BR>स्वेच्छया, Vi.<BR>III A favour: q. v.: अनुग्रहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pleasure-ground
PLEASURE-GROUND:<BR>(1) केलिकाननम्;<BR>(2) विलास-<BR>वनम्: v. Park.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plebeian
PLEBEIAN:<BR>(1) प्राकृतः,<BR>the p. order:<BR>प्राकृताः;<BR>(2)<BR>पृथग्जनः। Ph.:<BR>p. philosophers:<BR>ग्राम्यदार्शनिकाः:<BR>v. Vulgar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pledge
PLEDGE (subs.):<BR>I Pawn, mortgage: q. v.:<BR>आधिः।<BR>II Any security: perh. बन्धः,<BR>the<BR>mutual affection of husband and wife is a p.<BR>against separation:<BR>जायापत्योः परस्परप्रणयस्तयो-<BR>रविच्छेदबन्धः;<BR>to take p.:<BR>प्रतिज्ञां करोति।<BR>III A<BR>surety: q. v.: प्रतिभूः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pledge
PLEDGE (v.):<BR>I To mortgage: q. v.: आधी-<BR>करोति।<BR>II To engage:<BR>(1) बध्नाति, आ-, (बन्ध्,<BR>c. 9. ?);<BR>(2) प्रतिशृणोति (श्रु, c. 5. = to<BR>promise: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pledgee
PLEDGEE:<BR>(1) बन्धग्रहीतृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) आधिग्राहक<BR>(f. हिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pleiades
PLEIADES: the constellation:<BR>(1) कृत्तिका;<BR>(2)<BR>बहुला (pl.: rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plenary
PLENARY: सम्पूर्ण (f. र्णा): v. Full, complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plenipotentiary
PLENIPOTENTIARY: महादूतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plenitude
PLENITUDE: पूर्णता: v. Fullness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plenteous
PLENTEOUS, PLENTIFUL: प्रचुर (f. रा), p. pepper.:<BR>प्रचुरमरिच- B. r.: v. Abundant. To be p.:<BR>v. To abound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plentifully
PLENTIFULLY:<BR>(1) प्रचुरम्;<BR>(2) भूयिष्ठम्;<BR>(3) भूरि;<BR>(4)प्रभूतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plentifulness
PLENTIFULNESS:<BR>(1) प्राचुर्यम्;<BR>(2) बाहुल्यम्;<BR>(3)<BR>प्रभूतता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plenty
PLENTY: expr. by adj., he has p. of money:<BR>तस्य प्रभूतं धनम्: v. Abundant, plentiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pleonasm
PLEONASM: अधिकपदता, -त्वम्; अधिकपददोषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pleonastic
PLEONASTIC: अधिकपद (f. दा), Kav.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plethora
PLETHORA:<BR>I Lit.: रक्तपित्तम्, C. s.<BR>II Abun-<BR>-dance: प्राचुर्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pleurisy
PLEURISY:<BR>(1) उरोग्रहः, Wilson;<BR>(2) वक्षोग्रहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pleuritic
PLEURITIC: उरोग्रहवत् (f. ती), and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pliability
PLIABILITY: आवर्जनीयता: v. Flexibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pliable
PLIABLE, PLIANT: आवर्जनीय (f. या: lit. and<BR>fig.): v. Flexible, soft, docile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plight
PLIGHT (v.): ददाति (दा, c. 3. = to give: q. v.)<BR>v. Also to pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plight
PLIGHT (subs.):<BR>I State, condition: q. v.:<BR>दशा।<BR>II Pledge: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plinth
PLINTH: स्तम्ममूलम् (of a column); भित्तिमूलम्<BR>(of a wall).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plod
PLOD (v.): सततं श्राम्यति (श्रम्, c. 4.)<BR>or<BR>आत्मानम्<BR> आयासयति (c. of यस् ?), a p. ding student:<BR>सततपठनश्रमी<BR>or<BR>सततश्रमाध्यायी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plot
PLOT (subs.):<BR>I Of ground: भूमिभागः (?);<BR>क्षेत्रम् (= field) “ग्रामो ग्रामस्य सामन्तः क्षेत्रं क्षेत्रस्य<BR> कीर्तितम्,” Kat.<BR>II Conspiracy, intrigue:<BR>उपजापः<BR>II Of a drama: कथा (story); इति-<BR>वृत्तम्, Tārānātha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plot
PLOT (v.): उपजपति (जप्, c. 1.): v. To intrigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plotter
PLOTTER: v. Conspirator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plough
PLOUGH (subs.):<BR>(1) हलम्;<BR>(2) लाङ्गलम्;<BR>(3)<BR>सीरः<BR>or<BR>शीरः (rare). The pole or shaft of a p.:<BR>ईषा<BR>or<BR>ईशा; लाङ्गलदण्डः,<BR>the handle of a p. or p.-<BR>tail:<BR>ईषादण्डः;<BR>p. -head:<BR>लाङ्गलमुखम्; p. -share:<BR>(1) फलम्;<BR>(2) कूटकम्;<BR>(3) निरीषम्। P. -man:<BR>(1) हलिन् (m.);<BR>(2) हालिकः;<BR>(3) लाङ्गलिन्<BR>(m.); etc.<BR>P. -boy:<BR>बालहलिन् (m.?) etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plough
PLOUGH (v.):<BR>(1) कर्षति, वि-, प्र-, (कृष्, c. 1.),<BR>it was p. ed by the great Kuru:<BR>प्रकृष्टमेतत् कुरुणा<BR> महात्मना, Mah. ix. 53. 2.;<BR>the village headman<BR>p. s the village with five p. s:<BR>पञ्चभिर्हलैः कर्षति<BR> ग्रामं ग्रामणीः, M. n. on Ku. i. 2.;<BR>(2) वाहयति,<BR> सं-, (c. of वह्),<BR>shall p. low lands where water<BR>lodges:<BR>निम्नां हि वाहयेद् भूमिं यत्र विश्रमते जलम्, Pa.<BR>P. in:<BR>वापयति (c. of वप्),<BR>shall p. in yams<BR>near water:<BR>वापयेत् कन्दानि च जलान्तिके, Pa.<BR>P.<BR>up or out:<BR>हलेन<BR>or<BR>लाङ्गलेन उत्कर्षति<BR>or<BR>उत्पाटयति<BR>(पट्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plover
PLOVER: पक्षिविशेषः, perh. दयालः (comp. Beng.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pluck
PLUCK (v.):<BR>I To gather: q. v.: लुनाति (लू,<BR>c. 5.),<BR>p. ed with her own hand:<BR>स्वहस्तलूनः,<BR>Ku. iii. 61.<BR>II To strip off feathers:<BR>लुनाति, like birds whose feathers have been p. ed:<BR>लूनपक्षाविवाण्डजौ, Mah. v. 116. 20. P. off:<BR>लुनाति,<BR>P. out:<BR>उत्पाटयति (पट्, c. 10.)<BR>or<BR>सम्-<BR>उद्धरति (हृ, c. 1.). P. up (a) eradicate:<BR>उन्मूलयति, (b) = to gather up: समाहरति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pluck
PLUCK (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: हृद्यकृदन्त्राणि (n. pl.).<BR>II Courage, spirit: q. v.: सत्त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plug
PLUG (subs.): रोधनी, अव-, सं- (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plug
PLUG (v.): संरुणद्धि (रुध्, c. 7.): v. To stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plum
PLUM: कर्कन्धूः (strictly the jujube: both the<BR>tree and the fruit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plumage
PLUMAGE:<BR>(1) पक्षाः (m. pl.),<BR>seeing my golden<BR>p.:<BR>समीक्ष्य पक्षान् मम हेमजन्मनः, N. i. 130.;<BR>(2) पर्णाः (m. pl.),<BR>having beautiful p.:<BR>सुपर्ण<BR>(f. णा), Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plumber
PLUMBER: सीसकारः (?) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plumb-line
PLUMB-LINE: सीसकसूत्रम् (?); लम्बसीसकम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plume
PLUME:<BR>I Subs.: पक्षः: v. Feather.<BR>II<BR>Verb: श्लाघते (श्लाघ्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plummet
PLUMMET: सीसकसूत्रम् (?); लम्बसीसकम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plump
PLUMP: पीवर (f. रा): v. Fat, sleek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plumper
PLUMPER: *पूरकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plumpness
PLUMPNESS: पीवरता: v. Fatness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plumy
PLUMY:<BR>(1) पक्षावृत (f. ता);<BR>(2) सपक्ष (f. क्षा);<BR>(3) पक्षिन् (f. णी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plunder
PLUNDER (v.):<BR>(1) लुण्ठति, वि-, अव-, (लुण्ठ्, c. 1.),<BR>Ram. i. 4. 87.;<BR>(2) मुष्णाति (मुष्, c. 9.: prop.<BR>to steal),<BR>p. jewels, carry off nymphs:<BR>मुषाण<BR> रत्नानि हरामराङ्गनाः, Si. i. 51.;<BR>(3) अपहरति<BR>(हृ, c. 1. = to carry off).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plunder
PLUNDER (subs.):<BR>(1) विलुण्ठितम्;<BR>(2) लोप्त्रम्<BR>(= stolen goods: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plunderer
PLUNDERER:<BR>(1) वि- लुण्ठकः (?);<BR>(2) better by<BR>verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plunge
PLUNGE (v. i.):<BR>(1) मज्जति, नि-, अव-, (मस्ज्,<BR>c. 6.),<BR>of the p. ing women:<BR>निमज्जतीनाम्, Ki.<BR>viii. 53.,<BR>half-p. d:<BR>मग्नामग्न (f. ग्ना), D. i.;<BR>(2) अवगाहते, वि-, (गाह्, c. 1. = to dive in),<BR>to<BR>p. in the water:<BR>पयोऽवगाढुम्, Ki. viii. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plunge
PLUNGE (v. t.):<BR>(1) मज्जयति, नि-, अव-, (c. of<BR>मस्ज्);<BR>(2) gen. by मज्जयति etc.,<BR>my mind is<BR>p. d in impenetrable darkness:<BR>अन्धे तमसि मज्जति<BR> मे मनः, Vi. v. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plunge
PLUNGE (subs.):<BR>(1) मज्जनम्; नि-;<BR>(2) अवगाहनम्;<BR>(3) विगाहः, -नम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pluperfect
PLUPERFECT: no equiv.: अतीतभूतकालः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plural
PLURAL: बहुवचनम्, this (word) is generally p.:<BR>अयं प्रायेण बहुवचनान्तः, S. k.; (the words) दार,<BR> लाज,<BR>and<BR>असु are (used in)<BR>the p.:<BR>दारलाजासूनां<BR> बहुत्वम्, S. k.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pluralist
PLURALIST: बहुवृत्तिभोगिन् (f. नी: ??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plurality
PLURALITY:<BR>(1) अनेकता;<BR>(2) gen. by adj.<BR>अनेक: v. Many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plush
PLUSH: वस्त्रविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ply
PLY: To<BR>ply a boat:<BR>नावं वाहयति, Mah. i. 60.<BR>67.: v. To urge, employ, practise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pneumatic
PNEUMATIC: by comp.,<BR>p. engine:<BR>*द्रवयन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pneumatics
PNEUMATICS: *द्रवविज्ञानम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pneumonia
PNEUMONIA: a disease: फुष्फुसदाहः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poach
POACH:<BR>I To plunder: मुष्णाति (मुष्, c. 9.).<BR>II To cook eggs: no eqiv.: अर्धभ्राष्टं (f. ष्टां)<BR>करोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poacher
POACHER: जाङ्गलचौरः and sim. comp.s. (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pock
POCK:<BR>(1) रक्तवटी;<BR>(2) रक्तवरटी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pocket
POCKET (subs.) no equiv.: *चोलकोषः; जेबम्<BR>(vern.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pocket
POCKET (v.):<BR>I Lit.: *चोलकोषे निदधाति (धा,<BR>c. 3.).<BR>II Fig.: आत्मसात्करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pocket-book
POCKET-BOOK: कोषपत्रिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pocket-handkerchief
POCKET-HANDKERCHIEF: *कोषरौमालम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pod
POD:<BR>(1) शमी, p. ded grains (pulses): शमी-<BR>धान्यम्;<BR>(2) शिम्बा;<BR>(3) शिम्बि (f. म्बी,).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poem
POEM:<BR>(1) काव्यम्,<BR>composer of p. s:<BR>कर्ता काव्यानाम्,<BR>D.;<BR>a short p.:<BR>खण्डकाव्यम्, Sah.;<BR>(2) काव्य-<BR>प्रबन्धः,<BR>by writing p. s:<BR>काव्यप्रबन्धरचनेन, K.;<BR>(3) चम्पूः (a p. interspersed with prose),<BR>to<BR>string it:<BR>चम्पूं गुम्फति, Ch.: v. Poetry, verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poesy
POESY:<BR>I The art: कवित्वम्, -ता,<BR>p. is difficult<BR>of attainment:<BR>कवित्वं दुर्लभम्, A p.<BR>II Poetry:<BR>q. v.: कविता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poet
POET:<BR>(1) कविः,<BR>of that old p.:<BR>पुराणस्य कवेस्तस्य,<BR>Ku.;<BR>a great p.:<BR>महाकविः, Bho.;<BR>(2) सूरिः<BR>(rare),<BR>by the former p. s:<BR>पूर्वसूरिभिः, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poetaster
POETASTER: perh. कविबन्धुः; मण्डलकविः, (?),<BR>Dh. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poetess
POETESS:<BR>(1) कविः (f.);<BR>(2) काव्यरचयित्री and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poetic
POETIC, -AL: by comp.,<BR>p. -composition:<BR>काव्य-<BR>प्रबन्धः, K.;<BR>p. license:<BR>कविप्रौढिः, M. n. on Si.<BR>xv. 44.;<BR>p. genius:<BR>कवित्वम्,<BR>J. or<BR>कवित्वशक्तिः,<BR>N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poetically
POETICALLY: काव्यरचनानुसारेण; कविवत्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poetics
POETICS:<BR>(1) काव्यशास्त्रम्;<BR>(2) कवितातत्त्वम्,<BR>versed<BR>in p.:<BR>कवितातत्त्वविद्, Bho.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poetry
POETRY:<BR>(1) काव्यम्, p. is language of sentiment:<BR>वाक्यं रसात्मकं काव्यम्, Sah.;<BR>those who know to<BR>write and weigh p.:<BR>काव्यं कर्तुं विचारयितुञ्च ये<BR> जानन्ति, Kav.;<BR>(2) कविता, sweetness of p.:<BR>कवितामाधुर्यम्, Bho.;<BR>(3) पद्यम् (= verse), what<BR>is in this paper, p.: किं पत्रिकायामिदम् ?, पद्यम् ॥,<BR>Bho.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poignancy
POIGNANCY:<BR>(1) तीव्रता;<BR>(2) उग्रता;<BR>(3) तीक्ष्णता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poignant
POIGNANT:<BR>(1) तीव्र (f. व्रा);<BR>(2) उग्र (f. ग्रा);<BR>(3) तीक्ष्ण (f. क्ष्णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poignantly
POIGNANTLY:<BR>(1) तीव्रम्;<BR>(2) उग्रम्;<BR>(3) तीक्ष्णम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

point
POINT (subs.):<BR>I End: अग्रम्,<BR>with the p. of a<BR>needle:<BR>सूच्या अग्रेण, Mah. v. 127. 15.<BR>II In<BR>geo.: बिन्दुः, K. d.<BR>III A mark: चिह्नम्,<BR>vowel<BR>p.:<BR>*स्वररेखा।<BR>IV Exact place: स्थलम्: v.<BR>Place. V. A particular: विषयः<BR>or<BR>पदम्,<BR>p. s<BR>of dispute:<BR>विवादविषयः<BR>or<BR>विवादपदम्।<BR>VI Pass:<BR>to such a p.:<BR>एतावत् पर्यन्तम्।<BR>VII Eve, verge:<BR>on the p. of death:<BR>मरणोन्मुख (f. खा)<BR>or<BR>मुमूर्षु<BR>(mfn.);<BR>on the p. of rising:<BR>उदितप्राय (f. या);<BR>on the p. of doing:<BR>कर्तुमुद्यत (f. ता);<BR>was on<BR>the p. of cutting off her head:<BR>शिरश्चिकर्तिषयाचेष्टत,<BR>D. vii.<BR>VIII Degree: पदम्। Highest p.:<BR>अग्रभूमिः, Ki. xvii. 55. IX. Note, tune: स्वरः।<BR>X Peculiarity: q. v.<BR>XI A cape: q. v.<BR>XII A lively turn of thought: perh. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">Page530</a>]<BR>लक्ष्यम्। Ph.:<BR>p. s of the compass:<BR>*दिग्भागबिन्दवः<BR>or<BR>-मुखानि (n. pl.);<BR>to gain a p.:<BR>स्वार्थं साधयति;<BR>from your p. of view:<BR>यथा त्वया दृष्टम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

point
POINT (v.):<BR>I To sharpen: q. v.: तीक्ष्णीकरोति।<BR>II To aim: लक्षीकरोति।<BR>III To p. out:<BR>q. v.:<BR>IV To punctuate: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

point out
POINT OUT: दर्शयति, प्र-, (c. of दृश),<BR>p. ed out<BR>the man to the king:<BR>तं राज्ञेऽदर्शयन्नरम्, Raj.<BR>vi. 37.: v. To shew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

point-blank
POINT-BLANK:<BR>I Adj.: स्पष्ट (f. ष्टा).<BR>II Adv.<BR>(1) स्पष्टम्;<BR>(2) भिन्नार्थम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pointed
POINTED (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: तीक्ष्णाग्र (f. ग्रा) and<BR>sim. comp.s.: v. Sharp.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1)<BR>मर्माविध् (mfn.);<BR>(2) अरुन्तुद (f. दा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pointedly
POINTEDLY:<BR>(1) स्पष्टम्;<BR>(2) भिन्नार्थम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pointer
POINTER:<BR>I Anything that points: प्रदेशिनी<BR>(prop. the forefinger).<BR>II A dog: आखेटिक-<BR>कुक्क रभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pointing
POINTING (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: प्रदर्शनम्।<BR>II<BR>Punctuation: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pointless
POINTLESS:<BR>I Lit.: निस्तेजस् (mfn.).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) निस्तेजस् (mfn.);<BR>(2) नीरस (f. सा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poise
POISE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: समीकरोति।<BR>II To weigh:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poison
POISON (subs.):<BR>(1) विषम्,<BR>minor p.:<BR>उपविषम्,<BR>Bha.,<BR>p. is medicine for p.:<BR>विषस्य विषमौषधम्, J.;<BR>checked the p. in a moment:<BR>विषं क्षणादस्तम्मयम्,<BR>D. iv.;<BR>gave p. to Bhima:<BR>भीमाय विषं ददौ,<BR>Mah.;<BR>digested that p.:<BR>जरयामास तद्विषम्, V. p.;<BR>(2) गरम्, -लम् (rare),<BR>it is p.:<BR>गरमेतत्, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poison
POISON (v.):<BR>I To infect with p.: विषेण दूषयति<BR>(c. of दुष्)<BR>or<BR>मिश्रयति (मिश्र, c. 10.)<BR>or<BR>देग्धि<BR>or<BR>दिग्धे, उप-, (दिह्, c. 2.)<BR>or<BR>अनक्ति, अभि-,<BR>(अञ्ज्, c. 7.),<BR>p. ed water:<BR>विषदूषितं पयः;<BR>p. ed<BR>food:<BR>विषदिग्धमन्नम्;<BR>by p. ing:<BR>विषोपदेहात्, Ka.<BR>vii. 20-2., 16.;<BR>p. ed medicine:<BR>विषचूर्णमिश्र-<BR>मौषधम्, Mu. ii.<BR>II To give p.: विषं ददाति<BR>(दा, c. 3: with dat.), Mah.<BR>III To kill<BR>by p.: विषेण हन्ति (हन्, c. 2.), etc.<BR>I will p.<BR>myself:<BR>विषेणात्मानमुत्स्रक्ष्यामि, K.<BR>IV Fig.:<BR>नाशयति, (c. of नश्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poisoner
POISONER:<BR>(1) विषदायिन् (f. नी = giver);<BR>(2)<BR>विषघातिन् (f. नी = killer).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poisonous
POISONOUS:<BR>(1) विष- in comp.,<BR>p. tree:<BR>विष-<BR>वृक्षः, Ku. ii. 55;<BR>(2) सविष (f. षा), “अहयः<BR> सविषाः”, K. s.;<BR>(3) विषमय (f. यी = full of poison,<BR>very p.).<BR>Not p.:<BR>निर्विष (f. षा), K. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poisonousness
POISONOUSNESS: सविषता: v. Poisonous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poke
POKE (subs.): अभिघातः। Ph.: to buy a pig in a<BR>p.: perh. गृहे हस्तिनं क्रीणाति; गुणागुणमज्ञात्वा<BR> क्रीणाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poke
POKE (v.): v. To thrust, grope.<BR>To p. the<BR>fire:<BR>अग्निमुत्तेजयति, (तिज्, c. 10.: ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poker
POKER: *उत्तेजनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polar
POLAR:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>p. longitude of stars:<BR>नक्षत्राणां<BR> ध्रुवाः<BR>or<BR>ध्रुवकाः, Su. viii. 1.;<BR>the southern and<BR>northern p. stars:<BR>दक्षिणोत्तरे ध्रुवतारे, Su. xii. 43.<BR>II Northern: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polarity
POLARITY: ध्रुवाभिचारिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pole
POLE:<BR>I A long staff: यष्टिः, golden p.:<BR>काञ्चनी यष्टिः, Me.<BR>II Of a carriage:<BR>(1)<BR>धुर्, -रा (f.);<BR>(2) युगन्धरः।<BR>III A measure:<BR>दण्डः।<BR>IV In ast.: ध्रुवः, -कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pole-axe
POLE-AXE:<BR>(1) परशुः;<BR>(2) परश्वधः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pole-cat
POLE-CAT: गन्धमार्जारः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polemic
POLEMIC, -AL: वादानुवादिन् (f. नी); वादप्रतिवादिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polemics
POLEMICS: धर्मविषयको वादानुवादः<BR>or<BR>वादप्रतिवादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

police
POLICE: i. e. officer:<BR>oh, how neglectful the<BR>town p. have been:<BR>अहो! नगररक्षिणां प्रमादः, Mr.<BR>ix.;<BR>by the order of the chief of the p.:<BR>आरक्षिक-<BR>नायकस्य शासनात्, D. ii.;<BR>p. magistrate:<BR>दण्ड-<BR>नायकः, H.;<BR>p. administration report:<BR>दण्डनिर्वाह-<BR>वृत्तान्तः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

policeman
POLICEMAN:<BR>(1) रक्षिन् (m.);<BR>(2) रक्ष (क्षि) कः, आ-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

policy
POLICY:<BR>I State: नीतिः, mere p. is cowardice:<BR>कातर्य केवला नीतिः, R. xvii. 47.;<BR>how excellent<BR>is Chāṇakya's p.:<BR>अहो विचित्रता चाणक्यनीतेः, Mu.<BR>v.<BR>II Plan, object: आशयः।<BR>III Prudence,<BR>cunning: q. v.: चातुरी।<BR>IV Of insurance:<BR>*रक्षापत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polish
POLISH (v.):<BR>I Lit.: तेजयति (तिज्, c. 10.:<BR>?); चिक्कणीकरोति (?).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) विनयते<BR>(नी, c. 1.: ?);<BR>(2) संस्करोति (?): v. Also<BR>to refine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polish
POLISH (subs.):<BR>I Glossiness:<BR>(1) कान्तिः [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">Page531</a>]<BR>(?);<BR>(2) चिक्कणता (?).<BR>II Finish: परिष्कारः<BR>(?).<BR>III Refinement:<BR>(1) संस्कारः;<BR>(2) विनयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polished
POLISHED (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: चिक्कण (f. णा ?).<BR>II Fig.: संस्कृत (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polisher
POLISHER: expr. by verb: v. To polish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polite
POLITE:<BR>(1) विनीत (f. ता);<BR>(2) शिष्ट (f. ष्टा);<BR>(3) सौजन्यवत् (f. ती). Ph.: p. literature:<BR>साहित्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

politely
POLITELY:<BR>(1) सविनयम्;<BR>(2) सौजन्येन;<BR>(3)<BR>शिष्टतया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

politeness
POLITENESS:<BR>(1) विनीतता;<BR>(2) शिष्टता;<BR>(3)<BR>सौजन्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

politic
POLITIC: चतुर (f. रा): v. Also prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

political
POLITICAL:<BR>p. science:<BR>नीतिशास्त्रम्; p. economy:<BR>अर्थविज्ञानम्;<BR>p. affairs:<BR>राजकार्याणि;<BR>to lead a p.<BR>life:<BR>*राजकार्येषु जीवनमतिवाहयति; p. institutions:<BR>राज्यतन्त्राणि (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

politically
POLITICALLY: राजतन्त्रविचारणायाम्, and sim.<BR>comp.s. (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

politician
POLITICIAN:<BR>(1) नीतिविद् (mfn.);<BR>(2) नीति-<BR>विशारद (f. दा);<BR>(3) नीतिकुशल (f. ला); and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

politics
POLITICS: नीतिः, -शास्त्रम्, Ka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polity
POLITY: राज्यतन्त्रम्: v. Government.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poll
POLL (subs.):<BR>I Head: q. v.<BR>P. -tax:<BR>पुरुष-<BR>संख्यया शुल्कम्।<BR>II A register of persons:<BR>नामावलिः (?).<BR>III Vote, voting: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poll
POLL (v.):<BR>I To clip, cut: q. v.: लुनाति (लू,<BR>c. 9.).<BR>II To register names: नाम लिखति<BR>(लिख्, c. 6.).<BR>III To elicit votes: *नाम-<BR>ग्राहं मतामतं निश्चिनीति (चि, c. 5.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pollard
POLLARD: छिन्नाग्रो वृक्षः and sim. comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pollen
POLLEN:<BR>(1) परागः (best equiv.);<BR>(2) रजस्<BR>(n.);<BR>(3) रेणुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polling-officer
POLLING-OFFICER: expr. by circumlo.: v. To<BR>poll (III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pollute
POLLUTE (v. t.):<BR>(1) दूषयति, सं-, वि-, प्र-, (c. of<BR>दुष्),<BR>some animal p. d the offering:<BR>हविः<BR> कश्चिन्मृगोऽदूदुषत्, Say.;<BR>you are p. d, you are<BR>disgraced by the wretched Rāma:<BR>दूषिताः स्थ<BR> परिभूताः स्थ रामहतकेन, U.;<BR>who p. s an unwilling<BR>virgin:<BR>योऽकामां दूषयेत् कन्याम्, M.;<BR>(2) कलङ्कयति<BR>(= to stain);<BR>(3) मलिनयति (= to befoul).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pollution
POLLUTION: दूषणम्, सं-,: v. Also impurity.<BR>Ph.:<BR>nocturnal p.:<BR>स्वप्ने रेतःसेकः<BR>or<BR>-पातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poltroon
POLTROON: कापुरुषः: v. Coward, -ly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poltroonery
POLTROONERY: कापुरुषता: v. Cowardice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polyandry
POLYANDRY: बहुभर्तृकता, and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polygamy
POLYGAMY: बहुविवाहः, बहुपत्नीकता, and sim.<BR>comp.s. (of a man).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polyglot
POLYGLOT:<BR>I Adj.: बहुभाषालिखित (f. ता) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR>II Subs.: बहुभाषाविद् (mfn.:<BR>of men); बहुभाषालिखितो ग्रन्थः (of works).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polygon
POLYGON (subs), -AL (adj.): बहुभुज (f. जा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polypode
POLYPODE: सहस्रपादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polypus
POLYPUS: *बहुपदः<BR>or<BR>बहुपादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polysyllabic
POLYSYLLABIC:<BR>I बह्वक्षर (f. रा).<BR>II Subs.:<BR>बह्वक्षरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polytheism
POLYTHEISM: *बह्वीश्वरवादः; अनेकेशवादः; बहुदेव-<BR>विश्वासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

polytheist
POLYTHEIST: *बह्वीश्वरवादिन् (f. नी); बहुदेव-<BR>विश्वासिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pomade
POMADE, POMATUM: केशालेपः (?): v. Unguent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pomegranate
POMEGRANATE: दाडिम(म्ब) (mf. = tree; n.<BR>= fruit).<BR>The pulp of its seed:<BR>बीजम्;<BR>the<BR>kernel:<BR>अस्थि (n.), N. xxii. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pommel
POMMEL (subs.):<BR>I Of a saddle: वङ्का, Si.<BR>xii. 6.<BR>II A knob: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pommel
POMMEL (v. t.): ताडयति (तड्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>beat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pomp
POMP: आडम्बरम्,<BR>with great p.:<BR>महदाडम्बरेण (?);<BR>श्रीः (= magnificence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pompous
POMPOUS:<BR>(1) by circumlo;<BR>(2) रोचिष्णु (mfn.<BR>= splendid);<BR>(3) शोभन (f. ना = beautiful);<BR>(4) उत्सिक्त (f. क्ता = inflated: of style).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pompously
POMPOUSLY:<BR>(1) साडम्बरम् (?);<BR>(2) आडम्बर-<BR>पुरःसरम् (?);<BR>(3) शोभनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pompousness
POMPOUSNESS, POMPOSITY:<BR>(1) सश्रीकता (?);<BR>(2) ऐश्वर्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pond
POND:<BR>(1) तडागः;<BR>(2) जलाशयः;<BR>(3) कासारः<BR>(rare): v. Tank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ponder
PONDER (v.): ध्यायति, अनु-, (ध्यै, c. 1.),<BR>seeing<BR>Arjuna p. ing:<BR>ध्यायन्तमर्जुनं दृष्ट्वा, Mah. iii. 27.<BR>27.: v. To think, consider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ponderous
PONDEROUS:<BR>I Very heavy: अतिगुरु (f. र्वी),<BR>etc.<BR>II Of style: क्लिष्ट (f. ष्टा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poniard
PONIARD: छुरिका: v. Dagger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pontiff
PONTIFF: *धर्मेशः; प्रधानधर्माचार्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pontific
PONTIFIC, -AL: expr. by comp. or gen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pontificals
PONTIFICALS: *धर्मेशवेषः, -परिच्छदः।, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pontificate
PONTIFICATE: *धर्मेशता, -त्वम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pontoon
PONTOON: *प्लवः,<BR>p. bridge:<BR>*प्लवसेतुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pony
PONY: क्षुद्रघोटकः: v. Horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pool
POOL:<BR>I Of water: पल्वलम्: v. Pond.<BR>II<BR>In play: ग्लहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poop
POOP: (*नावः) पृष्ठशिरस् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poor
POOR:<BR>I Indigent:<BR>(1) दरिद्र (f. द्रा);<BR>(2)<BR>निर्धन (f. ना = without money) and sim.<BR>comp.s., a p. man wishes for hundred (pieces):<BR>निःस्वो वष्टि शतम्, J.;<BR>p. life:<BR>धनहीनजीवितम्, J.;<BR>(3) अकिञ्चन (f. ना = without anything).<BR>II<BR>Wretched, to be pitied:<BR>(1) दीन (f. ना),<BR>very poor state:<BR>दशा सुदीना, Ku. xiii. 36.;<BR>(2) वराक (f. की) (rare), for (my) p. Sitā:<BR>सीतां वराकीं प्रति, Vi. v. 22.<BR>III Inferior,<BR>bad: q. v.<BR>IV Of soil:<BR>(1) निर्गुण (f. णा);<BR>(2) असार (f. रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poorhouse
POORHOUSE: दरिद्रशाला and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poor-laws
POOR-LAWS: *दरिद्रविषया विधयः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poorly
POORLY (adv.):<BR>I Like a poor man: दरिद्रवत्।<BR>II Wretchedly,<BR>p. dressed:<BR>दीनवेश (f. शा):<BR>v. Also meanly.<BR>III Very little: अत्यल्पम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poorly
POORLY (adj.): असुस्थ (f. स्था): v. Unwell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poorness
POORNESS: दारिद्र्यम्: v. Poverty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poor-spirited
POOR-SPIRITED:<BR>(1) क्षुद्रमनस् (mfn.);<BR>(2) अल्प-<BR>सत्त्व (f. त्त्वा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pop
POP (subs.):<BR>(1) perh. फुत्कारः;<BR>(2) पट्शब्दः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pop
POP (v.):<BR>I To make a p.: expr. by subs.<BR>II Start forth: निर्गमयति (c. of गम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pope
POPE: रोमकधर्मेश्वरः; *पीपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

popedom
POPEDOM: *पोपत्वम्: v. Papacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

popery
POPERY: *पोपधर्मः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

popinjay
POPINJAY:<BR>I A parrot: शुकः।<BR>II A cox-<BR>-comb: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

popish
POPISH: *पोपीयः (या, यं); expr. by gen. or<BR>comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poplar
POPLAR: *पैपलः; वृक्षविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poppy
POPPY: खसतिलः,<BR>p. -seeds:<BR>खसबीजानि<BR>or<BR>खसतिलाः,<BR>Bha.;<BR>p. -juice:<BR>खसफलक्षीरम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

populace
POPULACE: प्रजाः (f. pl.): v. People, multi-<BR>-tude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

popular
POPULAR:<BR>I Pertaining to or prevailing<BR>among the people:<BR>(1) by comp.,<BR>hearing<BR>p. rumours:<BR>लोकवादश्रवणात्, R. xiv. 61.;<BR>(2)<BR>लौकिक (f. की),<BR>p. instruction:<BR>लौकिकी शिक्षा:<BR>v. People.<BR>II In general favour:<BR>(1)<BR>लोकप्रिय (f. या);<BR>(2) जनप्रिय (f. या); and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR>III Vulgar, common: q. v.:<BR>साधारण (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

popularity
POPULARITY:<BR>(1) लोकप्रियता; and sim. comp. s;<BR>(2) sometimes by जनानुरागः and sim. comp.s.<BR>= people's love).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

popularly
POPULARLY:<BR>I Commonly: लोके (= among<BR>the people).<BR>II To please: लोकरञ्जनार्थम्<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

populate
POPULATE:<BR>(1) सजनीकरोति (?);<BR>(2) जनैः पूरयति<BR>(पूर्, c. 10.: ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

populous
POPULOUS:<BR>(1) जनाकीर्ण (f. र्णा);<BR>(2) जनपूर्ण<BR>(f. र्णा);<BR>(3) बहुलोक (f. का);<BR>(4) जनसंकुल<BR>(f. ला); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

populousness
POPULOUSNESS:<BR>(1) जनाकीर्णता;<BR>(2) बहुलोकता;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

porcelain
PORCELAIN: no equiv.: चीनकौलालकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

porch
PORCH: अलिन्दः (?), “अग्निशरणालिन्दः”, Sa. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

porcine
PORCINE:<BR>(1) वाराहः (ही, हं);<BR>(2) शौकरः (री,<BR> रं), Ki. xii. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

porcupine
PORCUPINE:<BR>(1) शल्यः, -कः;<BR>(2) श्वाविध् (m.).<BR>Its quill or spine:<BR>शल<BR>or<BR>शलल (mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pore
PORE (subs.):<BR>I Of the skin:<BR>(1) रो(लो)मकूपः;<BR>(2) लो(रो)मरन्ध्रम्।<BR>II In gen.: रन्ध्रम्,<BR>through<BR>p. s:<BR>रन्ध्रैः, Vi. v. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pore
PORE (v.): साग्रहम् अधीते (ई, c. 2.): v. To<BR>study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pork
PORK:<BR>(1) शूकरमांसम्;<BR>(2) वराहामिषम्; etc.;<BR>who eat p. with garlic:<BR>ये वाराहं मांसं गृञ्जनेन<BR> खादन्ति, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

porker
PORKER: शूकरः: v. Hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

porous
POROUS:<BR>(1) रन्ध्रविशिष्ट (f. ष्टा);<BR>(2) रन्ध्रबहुल<BR>(f. ला) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

porousness
POROUSNESS, POROSITY:<BR>(1) रन्ध्रविशिष्टता;<BR>(2)<BR>रन्ध्रबहुलता; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

porphyry
PORPHYRY: शिलाविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

porpoise
PORPOISE:<BR>(1) शिशुकः;<BR>(2) शिशुमारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

porridge
PORRIDGE: perh. यूषम्: v. Soup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

porringer
PORRINGER: यूषपात्रम् (?): v. Plate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

port
PORT:<BR>I Harbour: *क्रोडः।<BR>II Bearing, ges-<BR>-ture: चेष्टा।<BR>III A wine: *पूर्तम्; मदिराविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portable
PORTABLE:<BR>(1) बहनीय (f. या),<BR>p. things:<BR>वह-<BR>नीयं द्रव्यम्, Mit.;<BR>(2) लवु (f. घ्वी = light).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portal
PORTAL: द्वारम्: v. Gate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portcullis
PORTCULLIS: *द्वाररोधनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

porte
PORTE: तुरुष्काणां महाराजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portent
PORTENT: उत्पातः,<BR>“dire p. s” appeared (forebod-<BR>ing) Rāvaṇa's ruin:<BR>रावणस्य विनाशायोत्पाता दारुणाः<BR> समुत्पतेतुः, Ram. vi. 90. 18.: v. Also omen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portentous
PORTENTOUS: औत्पातिक (f. की);<BR>(2) उत्पात-<BR>शंसिन् (f. नी) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portentously
PORTENTOUSLY: उत्पातं शंसत् (f. न्ती) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

porter
PORTER:<BR>I Gate-keeper: q. v.: द्वारपालः।<BR>II<BR>Carrier: भारवाहः। and sim. comp.s.<BR>III<BR>A wine: सुराविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

porterage
PORTERAGE: भारवाहमूल्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portfolio
PORTFOLIO:<BR>I Lit.: *पत्रपुस्तम्।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>अधिकारः: v. Office (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portico
PORTICO: निष्काशः; “हर्म्यादिभित्तिषु निर्गतमस्पृष्टभूमिक-<BR>मुपवेशनस्थानम्”, Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portion
PORTION (subs.):<BR>I Part: q. v.: अंशः।<BR>II<BR>Of a wife: यौतुकम्: v. Dower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portion
PORTION (v.):<BR>I To divide, distribute:<BR>q. v.: वण्टयति (वण्ट्, c. 10.).<BR>II To endow:<BR>सौदायिकं ददाति (दा, c. 3.: with dat).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portliness
PORTLINESS: स्थूलकायत्वम्: v. Fatness, corpu-<BR>-lence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portly
PORTLY: स्थूलकाय (f. या): v. Fat, corpulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portmanteau
PORTMANTEAU: चर्मपेटिका (??) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portrait
PORTRAIT: आलेख्यम्, the p. of a young lady:<BR>आलेख्यगता युवतिः, D. vi.: v. Painting.<BR>P.<BR>statue:<BR>प्रतिमा (= image).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portrait-painting
PORTRAIT-PAINTING: प्रतिकृतिरचना, R. xviii.<BR>53.: v. To paint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portraiture
PORTRAITURE:<BR>I Portrait: q. v.: जीवचित्रम्,<BR>Si. iii. 46.<BR>II Portrait-painting: expr.<BR>by circumlo.<BR>III Fig.: अनुकृतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portray
PORTRAY:<BR>I To draw, paint: q. v.:<BR>आलिखति (लिख्, c. 6.).<BR>II To depict,<BR>describe: q. v.: वर्णयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

portress
PORTRESS, PORTERESS:<BR>(1) दौवारिकी;<BR>(2) प्रतिहारी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pose
POSE:<BR>I Subs.: v. Posture.<BR>II Verb:<BR>स्तन्नाति (स्तम्भ्, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

position
POSITION:<BR>I Site, situation: q. v.: संस्थितिः।<BR>II State, condition: q. v.: अवस्था।<BR>III<BR>Posture: q. v.: स्थितिः।<BR>IV Proposition:<BR>q. v.: प्रतिज्ञा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

positive
POSITIVE:<BR>I Explicit, clear: q. v.: स्पष्ट (f.<BR>ष्टा).<BR>II Real, actual: q. v.: यथार्थ (f. र्था).<BR>III Confident: expr. by दृढं<BR>or<BR>निश्चितं मन्यते<BR>(मन्, c. 4.).<BR>IV Of laws: perh. विहित (f.<BR>ता): v. Opposed to negative: नियत (f. ता).<BR>VI In Alg., Gram: not expr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

positively
POSITIVELY:<BR>I Explicitly, clearly: q. v.:<BR>स्पष्टम्।<BR>II Certainly, indubitably: q. v.:<BR>निश्चितम्।<BR>III Absolutely: नियतम्।<BR>IV<BR>Really: यथार्थतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

positiveness
POSITIVENESS:<BR>I Actualness: यथार्थता।<BR>II<BR>Certainty, confidence: q. v.: निश्चयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

possess
POSSESS:<BR>I o have: q. v.:<BR>p. ing much<BR>wealth:<BR>बहुधन (f. ना): v. Having, endowed<BR>with.<BR>II To control the will of: आविशति<BR>(विश्, c. 6.),<BR>p. ed by a devil:<BR>भूताविष्ट (f.<BR>ष्टा), K.<BR>III. To occupy the mind: अधि-<BR>करोति (कृ, c. 8.).<BR>IV To inform: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

possession
POSSESSION:<BR>I In law: भोगः, सम्भोगः, परिभोगः,<BR>(rarely) भुक्तिः (= enjoyment),<BR>p. with title of<BR>long standing, without interruption, without<BR>dispute:<BR>सागमो दीर्घकालो निरन्तरो निराक्रोशो भोगः,<BR>Mi. on Y. ii. 28.; p. is a proof of ownership:<BR>भोगस्य स्वत्वे प्रामाण्यम्, Mi.; अधिकारः (?).<BR>To take p. of:<BR>(1) अधिकरोति (?);<BR>(2) गृह्णाति,<BR> परि- (ग्रह्, c. 9.),<BR>another crocodile has taken<BR>p. of your house:<BR>त्वदीयं गृहमपरेण मकरेण गृहीतम्,<BR>P. iv. 9.<BR>II That which is possessed:<BR>(1) भुक्तिः;<BR>(2) by circumlo.<BR>III By evil<BR>spirits: आवेशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

possessive
POSSESSIVE: Ph.:<BR>p. case:<BR>सम्बन्धः; p. ly:<BR>सम्बन्धद्योतनाय (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

possessor
POSSESSOR: expr. by comp. or verb: v. To<BR>possess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

possibility
POSSIBILITY:<BR>(1) शक्यता;<BR>(2) साध्यता: for dif.:<BR>v. Impossible: v. Also possible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

possible
POSSIBLE:<BR>(1) शक्य (f. क्या),<BR>should distinguish<BR>the p. from the im-p.:<BR>शक्याशक्यपरिच्छेदं कुर्यात्,<BR>Ka. xi. 33.;<BR>(2) साध्य (f. ध्या): v. Im-p.<BR>To be p.:<BR>सम्भवति (भू, c. 1. may be,<BR>may happen).<BR>As far as p.:<BR>यावच्छक्तितः<BR>(with all might). Every p. means:<BR>सर्वोपायाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

possibly
POSSIBLY:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by शक्यते (pass. of<BR>शक्),<BR>what can p. be known:<BR>यत् ज्ञातुं शक्यते।<BR>II Perhaps, probably: q. v.:<BR>(1) सम्भवतः;<BR>(2) सम्भावयामि etc. (= I think).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

post
POST (subs.):<BR>I Of timber etc.:<BR>(1) स्तम्भः<BR>(= pillar);<BR>(2) यष्टिः (= pile).<BR>P. for tying<BR>elephant:<BR>आलानम्।<BR>II Military: गुल्मस्थानम्,<BR>Mu. v.<BR>III Place: q. v.: स्थानम्: v. Also<BR>office.<BR>IV The letter-p. *पत्रवाहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

post
POST (v.):<BR>I To affix: आसंजयति (c. of संज्).<BR>II To place: स्थापयति (c. of स्था): v. To<BR>put.<BR>III To put in the mail: *पत्रवाहे ददाति<BR>(दा, c. 3.).<BR>IV Of accounts: पत्रिकायां<BR> समावेशयति (c. of विश्: ?).<BR>V To travel<BR>with p. horses: *राष्ट्रयानेन गच्छति।<BR>VI To p.<BR>over, travel with speed: जवेन<BR>or<BR>क्षिप्रं गच्छति<BR>(गम्, c. 1.), Ram.<BR>VII To p. up, acqu-<BR>-aint: अवबोधयति (c. of बुध्.: p. off put<BR>off): q. v.: आक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

postage
POSTAGE: *पत्रवाहकशुल्कम् or sim. वाहशुल्कम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

postboy
POSTBOY: जङ्घाकरिकः (foot-), D. ii., *अश्वकरिकः<BR>(horse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

post-chaise
POST-CHAISE: *राष्ट्रयानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

post-date
POST-DATE: परं कालं लिखति (लिख्, c. 6.) or<BR>निवेशयति (c. of विश्) (with loc.: ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

posterior
POSTERIOR (adj.):<BR>(1) gen. with पश्चात्;<BR>(2)<BR>पश्चात्कालीन (f. ना: of p. time);<BR>(3) rarely<BR>अवाच्य (f. च्या)<BR>or<BR>अर्वाचीन (f. ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

posteriors
POSTERIORS (subs.):<BR>(1) पश्चाद्भागः;<BR>(2) पश्चाद्देशः;<BR>(3) नितम्बः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

posterity
POSTERITY:<BR>(1) perh. परे (m. pl.: Vi. has<BR>पूर्वे for ancestors);<BR>(2) सन्तति: v. Off-<BR>-spring;<BR>(3) पुत्रपौत्रादिकम् (= children etc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

postern
POSTERN:<BR>(1) पक्षद्वारम्;<BR>(2) क्षुद्रद्वारम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

post-haste
POST-HASTE:<BR>(1) जवेन;<BR>(2) क्षिप्रम्;<BR>(3) जवनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

posthumous
POSTHUMOUS:<BR>I Lit.: पित्रन्तरजात (f. ता) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR>II Of works: लेत्रकमृत्योः परं<BR> प्रकाशित (f. ता) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

postillion
POSTILLION: v. Postboy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

postman
POSTMAN:<BR>(1) पत्रवाहः, -कः;<BR>(2) लेखहारकः। In<BR>modern sense, better use: *पत्रवाहपुरुषः and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

postmaster
POSTMASTER: *पत्रवाहनायकः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

post-office
POST-OFFICE: *पत्रवाहशरणम्; पत्रवाहकुलम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

postpone
POSTPONE: आक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c 6.), वि-: v. To<BR>put off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

postponement
POSTPONEMENT:<BR>(1) व्याक्षेपः;<BR>(2) विलम्बः<BR>(= delay).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

postcript
POSTCRIPT: *अनुलेखः; निम्नलेखः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

postulate
POSTULATE:<BR>I To assume: परिगृह्णाति (ग्रह्,<BR>c. 9.).<BR>II To solicit: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

posture
POSTURE:<BR>(1) संस्थानम्, संस्थितिः<BR>or<BR>संस्थितम्, “एकं<BR> पादमथैकस्मिन् विन्यस्योरौ तु संस्थितम् । इतरस्मिन्<BR> तथैवोरुं वीरासनमुदाहृतम् ॥,” M. n.;<BR>(2) बन्धः (of<BR>some p. s.) Ku. iii. 45.;<BR>(3) sometimes not<BR>expr.:<BR>in a sitting p.:<BR>आसीन (f. ना): v.<BR>Also gesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

posy
POSY: i. e. nosegay: q. v.: कुसुमस्तवकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pot
POT (subs.):<BR>(1) घटः;<BR>(2) कलशः (सः, -सी<BR>larger);<BR>(3) कृम्भः, -म्भी (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pot
POT (v.): घटे सञ्चिनोति (चि, c. 5.), Ve. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

potable
POTABLE: पेय (f. या): v. Drinkable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

potash
POTASH:<BR>(1) यवक्षारः;<BR>(2) सर्जिः, -का।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

potato
POTATO: *गोलालुः,<BR>sweet p.:<BR>रक्तालुः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pot-bellied
POT-BELLIED:<BR>(1) लम्बोदर (f. रा);<BR>(2) तुन्दिल<BR>(f. ला);<BR>(3) पिचिण्डिल (f. ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pot-boy
POT-BOY: भाण्डवाहः, -कः (?); भाण्डहरः, -हारकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pot-companion
POT-COMPANION: पानगोष्ठीसुहद् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

potency
POTENCY: शक्तिः,: v. Efficacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

potent
POTENT: वीर्यवत् (f. ती): v. Also efficacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

potentate
POTENTATE: अधिपतिः: v. King, sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

potential
POTENTIAL:<BR>p. mood:<BR>विधिलिङ्: v. Grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pot-herb
POT-HERB:<BR>(1) शाक (mn.);<BR>(2) शि(सि)ग्रुः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pot-house
POT-HOUSE:<BR>(1) शुण्डा, -लयः;<BR>(2) शुण्डापानम्;<BR>(3) शौण्डिकापणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

potion
POTION: gen. expr. by औषधम्<BR>or<BR>अगदः (=<BR>medicine), H. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

potsherd
POTSHERD: घटशकलम् and sim. comp.s.: v. Pot,<BR>piece.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pottage
POTTAGE: यू(जू)ष (mn.), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

potter
POTTER:<BR>(1) कुम्भकारः;<BR>(2) कुलालः, P.'s wheel:<BR>चक्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pottery
POTTERY:<BR>I The place: कुलालगृहम् and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Earthen-ware: q. v.: कौलालकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pouch
POUCH:<BR>I Lit.: भस्त्रा।<BR>II The belly: लम्बोदरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poulterer
POULTERER: गृहशकुनिविक्रेतृ (f. त्री) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poultry
POULTRY: गृहपालिताः खाद्यपक्षिणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poultice
POULTICE:<BR>I Subs: उपनाहः।<BR>II Verb: उप-<BR>नाहं ददाति (दा, c. 3.: with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pounce
POUNCE:<BR>I Subs.: मसीशोषणचूर्णम्।<BR>II Verb:<BR>p. on or upon:<BR>अवपत्य गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.);<BR>p. ing<BR>of a hawk:<BR>श्येनावपातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pound
POUND (subs.):<BR>I The weight: *अर्धसेरः।<BR>II<BR>Gold-coin: सुबर्णः, -मुद्रा (?).<BR>III For cattle:<BR>अवरोधः, -शाला (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pound
POUND (v.):<BR>I To pulverize:<BR>(1) चूर्णयति, सं-,<BR> परि-, (चूर्ण्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) चूर्णीकरोति: v. Also<BR>to grind, crush.<BR>II To impound: रुणद्धि,<BR> अव-, (रुध्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poundage
POUNDAGE: expr. शतकं देयम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pounder
POUNDER:<BR>I A pestle: मुस(ष)लम्।<BR>II Of<BR>persons, etc.: by comp.,<BR>ten p.:<BR>दशसुवर्णकः<BR>(after शती of J.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pour
POUR (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पातयति, नि-, (c. of<BR>पत् = to fall), water was p. ed on his head:<BR>तस्यापतन्मूर्ध्नि जलानि, R. xiv. 8.;<BR>(2) ददाति (दा,<BR>c. 3 with loc. = to give, put: q. v.);<BR>(3)<BR>सिञ्चति, नि-, (सिच्, c. 6. = to water, sprinkle).<BR>II To p. forth;<BR>(1) मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.):<BR>v. To discharge;<BR>(2) वर्षति (वृष्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To shower.<BR>III To p. out, i. e. emit,<BR>send forth: q. v.: विसृजति (सृज्, c. 6.).<BR>IV To utter: q. v.: उद्गिरति (गॄ, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pour
POUR (v. i.):<BR>I To flow: q. v.: स्रवति (स्रु, c.<BR>1.).<BR>II Of the rain:<BR>it is p. ing:<BR>धारा जवेन<BR> पतन्ति, Mr. v.<BR>III To come in: समापतति<BR>(पत्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pout
POUT:<BR>I Subs.: क्रोधावेशः।<BR>II Verb: ओष्ठौ<BR> प्रसारयति (c. of सृ)<BR>or<BR>दर्शयति (c. of दृश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

poverty
POVERTY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) दारिद्र्यम्<BR>or<BR>दरिद्रता,<BR>p.<BR>stricken:<BR>दारिद्र्योपहत (f. ता);<BR>p. is unending<BR>misery:<BR>दारिद्र्पमनन्तकं दुःखम्, Mr. i.;<BR>everybody<BR>seems to be in p.:<BR>सर्व एव दरिद्रति, H. ii. 2;<BR>(2)<BR>निर्धनता, etc.: v. Poor;<BR>(3) दैन्यम् (= wret-<BR>-chedness).<BR>II Meagreness, want: q. v.:<BR>हीनता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

powder
POWDER (v.):<BR>I To reduce to p.:<BR>(1) चूर्णी-<BR>करोति;<BR>(2) चूर्णयति (चूर्ण्, c. 10.);<BR>(3) लवशः<BR> करोति।<BR>II To sprinkle with p., as the hair:<BR>चूर्ण ददाति (दा, c. 3.: with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

powder
POWDER (subs.):<BR>(1) चूर्णम्,<BR>clouds reduced to<BR>p.:<BR>चूर्णीभवन्तो घनाः,<BR>V i. 4.;<BR>(2) पिष्टम्, it was<BR>(like)<BR>grinding p.:<BR>तदेष पिपेष पिष्टम्, N. xiii.<BR>19.;<BR>(3) क्षोदः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

powdery
POWDERY:<BR>I Dusty: q. v.: पांशुल (f. ला).<BR>II Powder-like:<BR>(1) चूर्णाम (f. भा);<BR>(2) क्षोदद्युत् (mfn.: rare); and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

power
POWER:<BR>I Strength:<BR>(1) शक्तिः,<BR>my p. is fail-<BR>ing in a fight with an inferior:<BR>शक्तिर्ममावस्यति<BR> हीनयुद्धे, Ki. xvi. 17.;<BR>(2) प्रभावः (as disclosed<BR>in effect), excelling the gods and demons in p.:<BR>अतिशयितसुरासुरप्रभाव (f. वा), U. v. 4.;<BR>(3) वीर्यम्<BR>(= strength),<BR>triumphant p.:<BR>विजयि वीर्यम्, Vi.<BR>i. 8.;<BR>(4) बलम्: v. Force;<BR>(5) सामर्थ्यम्<BR>(rare), Vi.<BR>II Ability:<BR>(1) शक्तिः,<BR>p. of pro-<BR>creation:<BR>प्रजननशक्तिः;<BR>(2) सामर्थ्यम्;<BR>(3) क्षमता।<BR>III Influence:<BR>(1) प्रभुत्वम्, -ता,<BR>as they had<BR>no p. they could not extricate him from the mis-<BR>fortune:<BR>न शेकतुस्तमप्रभुत्वादुत्तारयितुमापदः, D. i.;<BR>p. is founded on money:<BR>प्रभुत्वं धनमूलं हि, H.;<BR>(2) प्रभावः,<BR>through my p.:<BR>मत्प्रभावात्, Mah.<BR>To have p. over:<BR>प्रभवति (भू, c. 1.: with loc.),<BR>K. To be in one's p.: expr. by adj.: v.<BR>Able, to defend.<BR>As far as lies in one's<BR>power:<BR>यावच्छक्तितः, K.<BR>IV In Alg.: घातः।<BR>V. Forces: बलम्।<BR>VI A spirit: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

powerful
POWERFUL:<BR>I Strong: q. v.: बलवत् (f. ती).<BR>II Having great power:<BR>(1) प्रबल (f. ला);<BR>(2) विक्रान्त (f. न्ता);<BR>(3) पराक्रान्त (f. न्ता);<BR>(4) वीर्यवत् (f. ती);<BR>(5) ऊर्जस्वल (f. ला); etc.<BR>III Effacacious:<BR>(1) वीर्यवत्, as in very p. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">Page536</a>]<BR>medicine:<BR>अतिवीर्यवतीव भेषजे, Ki. ii. 4.;<BR>(2)<BR>सामर्थ्यवत् (f. ती: rare), M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

powerfully
POWERFULLY:<BR>(1) बलवत्;<BR>(2) प्रबलम् (?);<BR>(3)<BR>सबलम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

powerless
POWERLESS:<BR>(1) निर्बल (f. ला);<BR>(2) बलहीन (f.<BR>ना):<BR>(3) असमर्थ (f. र्था);<BR>(4) निष्प्रभाव (f.<BR>वा); etc.: v. Also vain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pox
POX:<BR>small p.:<BR>शीतला<BR>or<BR>विस्फोटकः; cow-p.:<BR>गोवसन्तः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

practicability
PRACTICABILITY: साध्यता: v. Also possibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

practicable
PRACTICABLE: साध्य (f. ध्या): v. Also poss-<BR>-ible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

practical
PRACTICAL:<BR>I Not theoretical:<BR>(1) व्यवहारिक<BR>(f. की);<BR>(2) better by circumlo.,<BR>without<BR>sufficient p. knowledge:<BR>कर्मस्वपरिनिष्ठितः, Sr. i. 3.<BR>: v. Use.<BR>II Of men:<BR>(1) व्यवहारकुशल (f. ला),<BR>D. vi.;<BR>(2) by circumlo.<BR>III Relating to life<BR>and practice:<BR>p. rules:<BR>व्यवहारनियमावलिः (?);<BR>p. life:<BR>लौकिकजीवनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

practically
PRACTICALLY:<BR>I Lit.: expr. with व्यवहारः।:<BR>v. Use.<BR>II Not nominally:<BR>(1) कार्यतः;<BR>(2) कर्मतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

practice
PRACTICE (subs.):<BR>I Customary actions:<BR>(1) अभ्यासः,<BR>from great p.:<BR>अत्याभ्यासात्, Mah.<BR>i. 130. 22. com.;<BR>(2) खुरली (military: rare),<BR>who has had p. in the use of arms:<BR>अस्त्रप्रयोग-<BR>खुरली, Vi. ii. 34.;<BR>(3) शिक्षा (= learning),<BR>gifted with use and p.:<BR>प्रयोगशिक्षागुणभूषणेषु, Ki.<BR>xvi. 6.;<BR>(4) अनुग्रहणम् (?), Mah. i. 130.<BR>24.<BR>(5) योग्या (medical or military),<BR>to<BR>train up in p.:<BR>योग्यां कारयति, Sr. i. 9.<BR>II<BR>Custom: q. v.: आचारः।<BR>III Habitually<BR>doing:<BR>(1) क्रियाप्रबन्धः, R. vi. 23.;<BR>(2)<BR>अनुष्ठानसातत्यम्, M. n.; and sim. comp.s.<BR>IV<BR>Use, action: q. v.: व्यवहारः। Ph.:<BR>consumma-<BR>tion of bad p. s:<BR>दुष्कर्मणां परिपाकः, Vi.<BR>V Exer-<BR>-cise of any profession: expr. by circumlo.,<BR>the doctor has great p.:<BR>*बहुभिराहूयते वैद्यः।<BR>VI<BR>Stratagem: कौशलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

practise
PRACTISE (v.):<BR>I To perform frequently:<BR>(1) अभ्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.),<BR>as if p. ing peculiar<BR>restrained breathing:<BR>अपूर्वप्राणायाममिवाभ्यस्यन्तम्,<BR>K.;<BR>(2) अभ्यासं करोति (with gen.);<BR>(3) शिक्षते<BR>(= to learn: q. v.);<BR>(4) परिचयं करोति, should<BR>p. (the use of)<BR>instruments:<BR>यन्त्राणां परिचयः<BR> कार्यः, Sr. 48. P. ed:<BR>(1) by subs.:<BR>v. Practice;<BR>(2) अभिज्ञ (f. ज्ञा): v. Con-<BR>-versant.<BR>II To do habitually: q. v.: नित्यं<BR> करोति and sim. comp.s.<BR>III To carry on:<BR>what calling do you p.sir?:<BR>कां वृत्तिमुपजीवत्यार्यः,<BR>Mr. ii.;<BR>I will p. here:<BR>*अत्र व्यवहारमनुजीवामि।<BR>IV To try artifices: कौशलं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

practitioner
PRACTITIONER:<BR>medical p.:<BR>वैद्यः: v. Physi-<BR>-cian;<BR>legal p.:<BR>*व्यवहाराजीवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

praetor
PRÆTOR: a Roman officer: *अग्रगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

praetorian
PRÆTORIAN: expr. by comp. or gen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pragmatic
PRAGMATIC: Ph.:<BR>p. sanction:<BR>सार्वलौकिकशासनम्<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pragmatical
PRAGMATICAL, -LY: v. Officious, -ly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prairie
PRAIRIE: निर्वृक्षक्षेत्रम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

praise
PRAISE (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रशंसा,<BR>some sang hymns con-<BR>taining p. s.:<BR>केचित प्रशंसामालीढानि सामानि जगुः, C.;<BR>(2) स्तुतिः<BR>or<BR>स्तवः, -सं-;<BR>p. s. of Rāma:<BR>रामाभिष्टवः,<BR>Rām.: v. Eulogy;<BR>(3) नुतिः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

praise
PRAISE (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रशंसति, अभि-, (शंस्, c. 1.),<BR>cheerfully p. ing the boy from all sides:<BR>अभितः<BR> प्रशस्य मुदा कुमाएरम्, Ku. xiii. 20.;<BR>(2) स्तौति or<BR>स्तवीति, सं-, अभि-, परि-, (स्तु, c. 2.:) gen. of<BR>superiors);<BR>(3) नौति, प्र-, अभि-, (नु, c. 2.),<BR>p. d. the couple:<BR>तन्मियुनं नुनाव, Ku. vii. 90.;<BR>(4) कीर्तयति: v. To celebrate;<BR>(5) गायति:<BR>v. To sing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

praiser
PRAISER:<BR>(1) प्रशंसक (f. सिका);<BR>(2) better<BR>by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

praiseworthily
PRAISEWORTHILY: expr. by adj., comp. or<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

praiseworthy
PRAISEWORTHY:<BR>(1) प्रशस्य (f. स्या);<BR>(2) प्रशस्त<BR>(f. स्ता);<BR>(3) प्रशंसनीय (f. या);<BR>(4) प्रशंसार्ह<BR>(f. र्हा and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prance
PRANCE (v.): प्लवते (प्लु, c. 1.: ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prank
PRANK (subs.): क्रीडा: v. Play, frolic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prank
PRANK (v.): विभूषयति (भूष्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prate
PRATE: जल्पति (जल्प्, c. 1.): v. To babble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prater
PRATER:<BR>(1) जल्पाक (f. की;)<BR>(2) वाचाल (f.<BR>ला);<BR>(3) वाचाट (f. टा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pratingly
PRATINGLY: expr. by adj. or present part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prattle
PRATTLE:<BR>I Verbs.: जल्पति: v. To babble.<BR>II Subs.: जल्पितम्: v. Babble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prattler
PRATTLER: जल्पाक (f. की): v. Babble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pravity
PRAVITY: expr. by adj.,:<BR>p. of nature:<BR>नष्ट-<BR>स्वभावः: v. Corrupt, depraved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prawn
PRAWN: इञ्चाकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pray
PRAY:<BR>I To a deity: स्तवीति<BR>or<BR>स्तौति (स्तु, c.<BR>2.),<BR>p. ed the goddess in mind:<BR>अस्तुवन् मनसा<BR> देवीम्, Mah. iv. 6. 1.: the king with his bro-<BR>thers, desirous of a view, again began to p. with<BR>various formulas of p. er, invoking the goddess:<BR>स्तोतुं प्रचक्रमे भूयो विविधैः स्तोत्रसम्भवैः । आमन्त्र्य<BR> दर्शनाकाङ्क्षी राजा देवीं सहानुजः॥<BR>II To entreat,<BR>supplicate: q. v.: याचते (याच्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prayer
PRAYER:<BR>I To a deity:<BR>(1) स्तवः;<BR>(2) स्तोत्रम्:<BR>v. To pray;<BR>(3) स्तुतिः (rare),<BR>this p. was<BR>addressed by the son of Indra:<BR>स्तुतिरिति जगदे<BR> हरेः सूनुना, Ki. xviii. 21.<BR>II Entreaty, supp-<BR>-lication: q. v.: याच्ञा। Ph.: one who grants<BR>p. s (of deities): वरद (f. दा) Mah. iv. 6. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prayer-book
PRAYER-BOOK: स्तोत्रसंहिता and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prayerful
PRAYERFUL: expr. by circumlo: v. Devo-<BR>-tional, pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prayerless
PRAYERLESS:<BR>(1) विना स्तवेन;<BR>(2) स्तुतिमकृत्वा;<BR>etc.: v. Without.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preach
PREACH:<BR>(1) (धर्मं) प्रवक्ति (वच्, c. 2.: ?);<BR>(2) उद्घोषयति (घुष्, c. 10. = to proclaim:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(3) उदीरयति (ईर्, c. 10. = to utter:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preacher
PREACHER:<BR>(1) धर्मप्रवक्तृ (f. त्री: ?);<BR>(2) धर्म-<BR>शासक (f. सिका ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preaching
PREACHING:<BR>I Subs.: धर्मशासनम् and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Adj.: v. Preacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preamble
PREAMBLE: प्रस्तावना: v. Also preface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prebend
PREBEND (subs.): वृत्तिः (= gen. term).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prebendary
PREBENDARY: धर्मोपासकः (?).<BR>P. -ship:<BR>धर्मोपास-<BR>कता (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precarious
PRECARIOUS:<BR>(1) अनिश्चित (f. ता): v. Un-<BR>-certain;<BR>(2) संदिग्ध (f. ग्धा): v. Doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precariously
PRECARIOUSLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precaution
PRECAUTION: he took no p. to avoid the calamity:<BR>तामापदं परिहर्तुं स कमप्युपायं पूर्वं नावललम्बे।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precautionary
PRECAUTIONARY: expr. by circumlo: v.<BR>Above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precede
PRECEDE: expr. by words meaning before,<BR>p.-ing, first, Kālidāsa p. d Bhavabhūti:<BR>*भवभूतेः पूर्वं बभूव कालिदासः;<BR>he p. s me:<BR>*ममाग्रगः<BR> सः;<BR>flowers p. fruits:<BR>उदेति पूर्वं कुसुमं ततः फलम्,<BR>Sa. vii. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precedence
PRECEDENCE:<BR>I Lit.: expr. as above: पूर्व-<BR>वर्तिता,<BR>p. of cause as regards effect:<BR>कार्यं प्रति<BR> कारणस्य पूर्ववर्तिता, Par.<BR>II Superior rank:<BR>(1) प्राधान्यम्;<BR>(2) अग्रस्थानम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precedent
PRECEDENT: in law: perh. व्यवस्था।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preceding
PRECEDING (adj.):<BR>(1) अतिक्रान्त (f. न्ता),<BR>in<BR>the p. section:<BR>अतिक्रान्ते पादे, S. iii. 2.;<BR>the<BR>merits of the preceding kings:<BR>अतिक्रान्तपार्थिव-<BR>गुणान्, Mu. i.;<BR>(2) अग्रग (f. गा);<BR>(3) पूर्ववर्तिन्<BR>(f. नी); and sim. comp.s.: v. Also<BR>former, past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precentor
PRECENTOR:<BR>(1) गायकाग्रणी;<BR>(2) मुख्यगायकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precept
PRECEPT: नियोगः: v. Order, instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preceptive
PRECEPTIVE:<BR>I Containing precepts: नियोग-<BR>गर्भ (f. र्भा).<BR>II Of the nature of p. s: expr.<BR>by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preceptor
PRECEPTOR: गुरुः: v. Teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preceptress
PRECEPTRESS:<BR>(1) उपाध्याया, उपाध्यायी;<BR>(2)<BR>अध्यापिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precession
PRECESSION: of the equinoxes:<BR>(1) अयनचलनम्,<BR>Go. vi. 18.;<BR>(2) क्रान्तिपातगतिः, com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precinct
PRECINCT: सीमन् (m.)<BR>or<BR>सीमा: v. Boundary,<BR>limit.<BR>Within the p. s of:<BR>सीमान्तवर्तिन् (f. नी), J.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precious
PRECIOUS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) महार्ह (f. र्हा), p. bed:<BR>महार्हशय्या, Ki.;<BR>(2) बहुमूल्य (f. ल्या);<BR>(3) महार्घ<BR>(f. र्घा).<BR>P. stone:<BR>उपलरत्नम्, V. m. 80. 2.;<BR>महार्होपलम्: v. Gem.<BR>II Fig.: अमूल्य (f. ल्या)<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preciousness
PRECIOUSNESS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) महार्हता;<BR>(2)<BR>बहुमूल्यता।<BR>II Fig.: अमूल्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precipice
PRECIPICE:<BR>(1) प्रपातः;<BR>(2) अतटः;<BR>(3) भृगुः, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precipitancy
PRECIPITANCY, PRECIPITATION: क्षिप्रकारिता: v.<BR>Hastiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precipitate
PRECIPITATE (v.):<BR>I To throw headlong:<BR>अधः क्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.): v. Also to fall.<BR>II Hasten: त्वरयति (c. of त्वर्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precipitate
PRECIPITATE (adj.):<BR>I Rash, hasty: q. v.:<BR>क्षिप्रकारिन् (f. णी).<BR>II Headlong: q. v.:<BR>अवाङ्मुख (f. खी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precipitately
PRECIPITATELY:<BR>I Hastily: अविमृश्य<BR>or<BR>असमीक्ष्य।<BR>II Headlong: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precipitous
PRECIPITOUS:<BR>I Steep: अवसर्पिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) पातुक (f. का).<BR>II Precipitate: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precipitousness
PRECIPITOUSNESS:<BR>I Lit.: पातुकता; better<BR>by adj.<BR>II Rashness: q. v.: क्षिप्रकारिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precise
PRECISE:<BR>I Exact:<BR>(1) शुद्ध (f. द्धा = correct);<BR>(2) यथार्थ (f. र्था = actual);<BR>(3) सुनिश्चित<BR>(f. ता = well-ascertained);<BR>(4) स्थिर (f. रा<BR>= fixed).<BR>II Punctilious: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precisely
PRECISELY:<BR>(1) यथार्थतः (= actually);<BR>(2)<BR>नियतम् (= certainly: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preciseness
PRECISENESS, PRECISION:<BR>I Exactness:<BR>(1)<BR>विशुद्धता (= accuracy);<BR>(2) यथार्थता (= actua-<BR>-lity);<BR>(3) स्थिरता (= fixedness).<BR>II Puncti-<BR>-liousness: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preclude
PRECLUDE: प्रतिषेधति (सिध्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precocious
PRECOCIOUS:<BR>(1) अकालपरिणत (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>अकालप्रौढ (f. ढा: fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precocity
PRECOCITY:<BR>(1) अकालपरिणतिः;<BR>(2) अकालप्रौढता<BR>(fig.);<BR>(3) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preconceived
PRECONCEIVED:<BR>(1) पूर्वकल्पित (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>पूर्वसम्भावित (f. ता); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preconception
PRECONCEPTION:<BR>(1) पूर्वकल्पना;<BR>(2) पूर्वभावना;<BR>(3) पूर्वबुद्धिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preconcerted
PRECONCERTED:<BR>(1) पूर्वनिर्द्धारित (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>पूर्वमन्त्रित (f. ता) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precursor
PRECURSOR: पूर्वचिह्नम्: v. Also harbinger,<BR>forerunner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

precursory
PRECURSORY:<BR>p. symptoms:<BR>पूर्वलक्षणम्: v. To<BR>forebode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

predatory
PREDATORY:<BR>(1) दस्युवृत्तिः (mfn.: of men);<BR>(2) लुब्धक (f. का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

predecessor
PREDECESSOR:<BR>(1) expr. by अतिक्रान्त (f. न्ता)<BR>(राजा etc.): v. Preceding;<BR>(2) पूर्वस्थ (f.<BR>स्था) with a subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

predestinarian
PREDESTINARIAN:<BR>(1) दैष्टिकः;<BR>(2) दैवप्रमाणकः,<BR>M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

predestination
PREDESTINATION:<BR>I The act.: expr. by<BR>circumlo.<BR>II The theory:<BR>(1) दैष्टिकता;<BR>(2) often by दैवम् (= fate): q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

predestinate
PREDESTINATE, PREDESTINE: expr. by cir-<BR>-cumlo.,<BR>how could you so cruelly p. my sepa-<BR>ration from my beloved:<BR>कथं वियोक्ष्यसे वल्लभयेति<BR> निर्गता लिपिर्ललाटन्तपनिष्ठुराक्षरा, N. i. 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

predetermine
PREDETERMINE: पूर्वं निश्चिनोति (चि, c. 5.): v.<BR>To determine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

predicable
PREDICABLE: expr. by circumlo.: v. To<BR>predicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

predicament
PREDICAMENT:<BR>I Logical: पदार्थः, Par.<BR>II<BR>Condition: q. v.: दशा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

predicate
PREDICATE:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) विधेयम्, Kav.;<BR>(2)<BR>विशेषणम्, M. n. on si. i. 48.<BR>II Verb: perh.<BR>अनुवदति (वद्, c. 1.: अनुवाद्य = subject, Kav.);<BR>उद्दिश्य वदति (वद्, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>वक्ति (वच्, c. 2.),<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

predict
PREDICT:<BR>I To foretell: I. p. ed his death:<BR>तस्य मरणं मया पूर्वमेव कथितम्: v. To tell, before.<BR>II To forbode: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prediction
PREDICTION: उक्तिः (= saying: exact sense<BR>from context).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

predilection
PREDILECTION: पक्षपातः: v. Liking, partiality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

predispose
PREDISPOSE: प्रवर्तयति (c. of वृत्): v. To<BR>induce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

predisposition
PREDISPOSITION: भावः: v. Inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

predominance
PREDOMINANCE:<BR>(1) प्रबलता;<BR>(2) प्रभुत्वम्<BR>(= dominion);<BR>(3) आधिक्यम् (in number).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

predominant
PREDOMINANT<BR>(1) प्रबल (f. ला);<BR>(2) प्रभविष्णु<BR>(mfn.: in power).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

predominate
PREDOMINATE: expr. by adj.,<BR>with a p. ing<BR>force:<BR>प्रभूतबलेन: v. Also to excel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pre-eminence
PRE-EMINENCE:<BR>(1) सर्वश्रेष्ठ<BR>(2) सर्वोत्कृष्टता;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pre-eminent
PRE-EMINENT:<BR>(1) सर्वश्रेष्ठ (f. ष्ठा);<BR>(2) सर्वोत्कृष्ट<BR>(f. ष्टा);<BR>(3) सर्वप्रधान (f. ना);<BR>(4) अग्रगण्य<BR>(f. ण्या): v. Excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pre-eminently
PRE-EMINENTLY:<BR>(1) सर्वापेक्षया;<BR>(2) सर्वाधिकम्;<BR>(3) परमम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pre-engagement
PRE-ENGAGEMENT:<BR>(1) पूर्वप्रतिश्रुतम्, -तिः (or<BR>श्रवः ?); (2)पूर्वसमयः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pre-exist
PRE-EXIST: पूर्वम् अस्ति: v. To exist, before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pre-existence
PRE-EXISTENCE:<BR>(1) पूर्वभूतिः (?);<BR>(2) पूर्वसत्त्वम्;<BR>(3) better by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preface
PREFACE (subs.): मुखबन्धः। N. B. विज्ञापनम् and<BR>उपक्रमणिका used by modern writers. S. p. b.<BR>has भूमिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preface
PREFACE (v.): expr. by subs,<BR>he has p. d it<BR>with an essay on poetry:<BR>*मुखबन्धे काव्यविषयकः<BR> प्रबन्धो निवेशितः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prefatory
PREFATORY: expr. by subs.: v. Preface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prefect
PREFECT: नायकः (?),<BR>p. of the city guard:<BR>नगर-<BR>रक्षिनायकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prefecture
PREFECTURE: नायकता, -त्वम् (?: the office);<BR>नायकाधिकारः (?: the jurisdiction).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prefer
PREFER:<BR>I To offer, address: to p. a charge:<BR>अभियोगं करोति<BR>or<BR>निवेदयति (= to inform).<BR>II<BR>To advance, raise: q. v.: उन्नमयति (c. of<BR>नम्),<BR>p. your friends:<BR>उन्नमय स्वबन्धुवर्गम्, Ki.<BR>III<BR>To regard more: बहु (much)<BR>or<BR>अधिकम्<BR>(more) मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.): v. Also to excel.<BR>IV To like more: अधिकं रोचते (रुच्, c. 1.:<BR>with dat. of the person): v. Also better.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prederable
PREDERABLE: expr. with वरम्,<BR>a forest is p. to<BR>a life of poverty among friends:<BR>वरं वनं॥॥॥न<BR> बन्धुमध्ये धनहीनजीवितम्, H.: v. Better (II), to<BR>prefer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preference
PREFERENCE: often expr. by रुचिः, अभि-<BR>(= liking): v. Also to prefer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preference to
PREFERENCE TO, IN: विहाय, अपहाय, etc. (with<BR>acc.),<BR>in p. to heaps of jewels:<BR>रत्नराशीनपि-<BR>विहाय, Sa. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preferment
PREFERMENT: पदोन्नतिः: v. Promotion, ad-<BR>-vancement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prefigure
PREFIGURE: प्रदर्शयति (c. of दृश्): v. To<BR>announce, shew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prefigurement
PREFIGUREMENT: प्रदर्शनम् (?): v. Announce-<BR>-ment, indication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prefix
PREFIX (v.): expr. by circumlo., whom (they)<BR>say Kashipu with Hiranya p. ed:<BR>यं॥। हिरण्यपूर्वं<BR> कशिपुं प्रचक्षते, Si. i. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prefix
PREFIX (subs.): उपसर्गः, “धातुलीनमुपसर्ग इवार्थम्”,<BR>Si. x. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pregnancy
PREGNANCY:<BR>(1) expr. by गर्भः;<BR>(2) सगर्भता।<BR>Signs of p.:<BR>दोहदलक्षणम्, R. iii. 1. In a state<BR>of p. = pregnant: q. v.<BR>In the first three months<BR>of p. of a woman:<BR>गर्भिणीप्रथमद्वितीयतृतीयमासे, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pregnant
PREGNANT:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) गर्भिणी;<BR>(2) गर्भवती;<BR>(3) अन्तर्घत्नी;<BR>(4) आपन्नसत्त्वा,<BR>she became p. by<BR>me:<BR>सा मयासीदापन्नसत्त्वा, D. iv. To become p.:<BR>गर्भं दधाति (धा, c. 3.)<BR>or<BR>धारयति (धृ, c. 10.),<BR>R. x. 58.<BR>or<BR>गर्भो भवति (with gen. of the<BR>woman), Ku. i. 14.<BR>II Fig.: अर्थवत् (f. ती).<BR>Ph.:<BR>p. signification:<BR>निगूढार्थः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prehensile
PREHENSILE: ग्राहिन् (f. णी): v. To catch,<BR>seize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pre-intimation
PRE-INTIMATION:<BR>(1) प्राङ्निर्देशः;<BR>(2) by cir-<BR>-cumlo.: v. To inform, tell, before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prejudge
PREJUDGE: पूर्वं निश्चिनोति (चि, c. 5.): v. To<BR>judge, before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prejudgement
PREJUDGEMENT: विचारात् प्राङ्निर्णयः and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prejudice
PREJUDICE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पूर्वसंस्कारः;<BR>(2) विद्वेषः (= dislike).<BR>II Injury, mischief:<BR>q. v.: क्षतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prejudice
PREJUDICE (v.):<BR>I To prepossess:<BR>all men<BR>are p. d more or less:<BR>*सर्वे न्यूनाधिकं पूर्वसंस्कारवशाः;<BR>he p. d him against me:<BR>*स तं मयि बद्धविद्वेषं चकार।<BR>II Injure: q. v.: बाधते (बाध्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prejudicial
PREJUDICIAL: क्षतिकर (f. री): v. Injurious,<BR>to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prejudicially
PREJUDICIALLY: expr. by verb or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prelacy
PRELACY: *प्रधानाचार्यत्वम्; -पदम् (the office);<BR>अधिकारः (the jurisdiction).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prelate
PRELATE: *प्रधानाचार्यः; आचार्यमुख्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prelatical
PRELATICAL: v. Episcopal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prelection
PRELECTION: प्रबन्धः (?): v. Lecture, dis-<BR>-course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prelibation
PRELIBATION: v. Foretaste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preliminary
PRELIMINARY:<BR>p. Investigation:<BR>प्रथममनुसन्धानम्;<BR>(?);<BR>p. observation:<BR>मौखिकमनुशासनम्;<BR>p.s of<BR>peace:<BR>प्रशमस्य पूर्वकार्याणि (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prelude
PRELUDE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्रस्तावना;<BR>(2)<BR>पूर्वरङ्गः (musical), Si. ii. 8.<BR>II Fig., fore-<BR>-runner, harbinger: पूर्वलक्षणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prelude
PRELUDE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: expr. by subs.<BR>II<BR>To precede: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prelusive
PRELUSIVE, PRELUSORY:<BR>“p. drops”:<BR>प्रथमोदबिन्दवः<BR>v. First, prelude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

premature
PREMATURE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अकालपक्व (f. क्वा); [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">Page540</a>]<BR>(2) अकालपरिणत (f. ता); etc.: v. Ripe.<BR>II<BR>Untimely:<BR>(1) अकाल-<BR>or<BR>असमय- in comp.,<BR>p. birth:<BR>अकालजात (f. ता);<BR>(2) आकालिक<BR>(f. की);<BR>(3) असामयिक (f. की), p. agitation:<BR>असामयिकः क्षोभः, Ki. ii. 40.<BR>III Arrived at<BR>without due evidence: perh. अपक्व (f. क्वा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prematurely
PREMATURELY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

premeditate
PREMEDITATE: पूर्वं संकल्पयति (c. of कॢप): v.<BR>To meditate, contrive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

premeditation
PREMEDITATION: संकल्पः, पूर्व-: v. Also contri-<BR>-vance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

premier
PREMIER:<BR>(1) मुख्यमन्त्री, P.;<BR>(2) प्रधानसचिवः, H.;<BR>(3) मन्त्रीशः, Say.; and sim. comp.s.: v.<BR>Minister, chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

premise
PREMISE (v.):<BR>(1) उपन्यस्यति। (अस्, c. 4.);<BR>(2)<BR>उल्लिखति (लिख्, c. 6.): v. To state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

premises
PREMISES (subs.):<BR>I In logic: v. Premiss.<BR>II Buildings and land: गृहाः (m. pl.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

premiss
PREMISS:<BR>major p.:<BR>उदाहरणम्, *मूलावयवः,<BR>minor<BR>p.:<BR>उपनयः, *अन्तरवयवः, “उत्पत्तिधर्मकं स्थाल्यादि-<BR>द्रव्यमनित्यमित्युदाहरणं, तथा चोत्पत्तिधर्मकः शब्द इत्युपनयः,<BR> तस्मादत्पतिधर्मकत्वादनित्यः शब्द इति निगमनम्,” N. d.<BR>i. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

premium
PREMIUM:<BR>I Reward: q. v.:<BR>II Commer-<BR>-cial: अतिरिक्तदानम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

premonition
PREMONITION: v. Warning, notice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

premonitory
PREMONITORY: अग्रिमः (मा, मं) (= early): v.<BR>Also to warn. P. symptom (of a disease):<BR>पूर्वरूपम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pre-occupation
PRE-OCCUPATION: पूर्वभोगः<BR>or<BR>-भुक्तिः: v. Posses-<BR>-sion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pre-occupy
PRE-OCCUPY:<BR>I Lit.: पूर्वम् अधिकरोति (कृ,<BR>c. 8.).<BR>II To pre-engage: I am p. ied:<BR>*व्यापृतोऽस्मि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preparation
PREPARATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) उपकल्पः, -नम्;<BR>(2) परिकल्पः, -नम्;<BR>(3) प्र-कल्पनम्<BR>or<BR>कल्पितम्;<BR>(4) सज्जीकरणम्। (= getting ready);<BR>(5) साधनम्<BR>(= of food).<BR>II Anything prepared: expr.<BR>by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preparative
PREPARATIVE: expr. by verb: v. Also<BR>preliminary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prepare
PREPARE (v. t.):<BR>(1) कल्पयति, उप-, प्र-, परि-, (कॢप,<BR>c. 10.),<BR>there everything necessary for coronation<BR>was p. d;<BR>अभिषेचनिकं द्रव्यं सर्वं तत्रोपकल्पितम्, Rām,<BR>ii. 12. 13.;<BR>(2) सज्जीकरोति: v. Ready, to<BR>make;<BR>(3) साधयति (c. of सिध्: of food).<BR>food p. d with five roots:<BR>पञ्चमूलेन सिद्धान्नानि,<BR>Bha.;<BR>(4) करोति, Ram. ii. 12. 2.;<BR>(5)<BR>योजयति, प्र-, सं-, (युज्, c. 10.: to mix, as of<BR>some medicines), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prepare
PREPARE (v. i.):<BR>(1) सज्जीभवति;<BR>(2) sometimes<BR>by trans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prepay
PREPAY: पूर्वं मूल्यं ददाति (दा, c. 3.): v. To pay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prepense
PREPENSE: malice p.: perh. व्यवसितद्रोहः: v.<BR>Deliberate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preponderance
PREPONDERANCE: आधिक्यम्: v. Superiority,<BR>excess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preponderate
PREPONDERATE: अतिरिच्यते (pass. of रिच्), H.<BR>iv. 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preposition
PREPOSITION: कर्मप्रवचनीयः (of some p. s, Pāṇini<BR>i. 4. 83.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prepossess
PREPOSSESS:<BR>(1) प्रह्वीकरोति, my heart p. ed by<BR>(your)<BR>good qualities:<BR>प्रह्वीकृतं मे हृदयं गुणौधैः,<BR>Ki. iii. 12.;<BR>(2) आवर्जयति (वृज्, c. 10.): v.<BR>Also to prejudice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prespossessing
PRESPOSSESSING (adj.): हृदयहारिन् (f. णी): v.<BR>Charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prepossession
PREPOSSESSION:<BR>(1) पक्षपातः (in good sense);<BR>(2) पूर्वसंस्कारः: (= prejudice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preposterous
PREPOSTEROUS: अयुक्त (f. क्ता): v. Also in-<BR>-consistent, unreasonable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preposterously
PREPOSTEROUSLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prepuce
PREPUCE:<BR>(1) लिङ्गाग्रत्वच् (f.);<BR>(2) चर्मन् (n.)<BR>(when the sense is clear), Bha. and sim.<BR>expr. (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prerequisite
PREREQUISITE:<BR>we will say what is p. for an<BR>enquiry about God:<BR>ब्रह्मजिज्ञासायामपि यत्पूर्ववृत्तं<BR> नियमेनापेक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.) तद्वक्तव्यम्, S. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prerogative
PREROGATIVE:<BR>(1) अनन्याधिकारः (?);<BR>(2)<BR>असामान्याधिकारः (?); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presage
PRESAGE (subs.): v. Presentiment, omen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presage
PRESAGE (v.): पूर्वं<BR>or<BR>पुरः शंसति (शंस्, c. 1.),<BR>Si. xv. 96.: v. Also to forebode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presbyterian
PRESBYTERIAN: no equiv. प्रष्ठ (f. ष्ठा) may be<BR>used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prescience
PRESCIENCE:<BR>(1) पूर्वज्ञानम् (?);<BR>(2) भविष्यविज्ञानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prescient
PRESCIENT:<BR>(1) पूर्वदर्शिन्। (f. णी: fig.);<BR>(2)<BR>by verb: v. Foresee, foreknow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prescribe
PRESCRIBE:<BR>I To dictate, direct: q. v.:<BR>निर्दिशति (दिश्, c. 6.).<BR>II Medically: औषधं<BR>(= medicine)<BR>or<BR>अन्नं (= food) निर्दिशति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prescription
PRESCRIPTION:<BR>I Legal: बहुकालभोगः: v.<BR>Possession.<BR>II Medical: औषधनिर्देशः and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prescriptive
PRESCRIPTIVE (adj.): expr. with बहुकालभोगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presence
PRESENCE:<BR>(1) उपस्थितिः;<BR>(2) सन्निधानम् or<BR>सन्निधिः;<BR>(3) by adj.<BR>In the p. of:<BR>समक्षम्: v.<BR>Before.<BR>From the p. of:<BR>पुरस्तात्<BR>or<BR>सम्मुखतः।<BR>To<BR>the p. of:<BR>सम्मुखम्: v. Also near. Ph.:<BR>p. of<BR>mind:<BR>मनःस्थैर्यम् (?)<BR>or<BR>शान्तचित्तता (?) and sim.<BR>expr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

present
PRESENT (subs.):<BR>(1) उपदा,<BR>p. s came to the lord<BR>of Kośala:<BR>उपदा विविशुः कोशलेश्वरम्, R. iv. 70.;<BR>(2) उपायनम्,<BR>fit for p.s to him:<BR>तस्योपायनयोग्यानि,<BR>Ku. ii. 37.;<BR>(3) उपहारः, if you make a p. of<BR>your son to the goddess, (i. e. sacrifice him):<BR>यदि त्वमात्मनः पुत्रं भगवत्या उपहारीकरोषि, H. iii.;<BR>(4) प्राभूतम्, and bringing new p. s day by day:<BR>अहरहश्च नवनवानि प्राभृतान्युपहरन्ती, D. ii.;<BR>(5)<BR>प्रीतिदायः (of love),<BR>accepting the p.:<BR>तं प्रीतिदायं<BR> प्रतिगृह्य, Ram.;<BR>(6) योपढौकनम् (rare), Ph.:<BR>at p.:<BR>वर्तमाने, Vi. v.: v. Now;<BR>in p.:<BR>सपदि:<BR>v. Instantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

present
PRESENT (v.):<BR>I To give freely:<BR>(1) उपहरति<BR>(हृ, c. 1.). what the infallible (Kṛṣṇa) p. ed:<BR>यदुपाहरदच्युतः, Mah. iv. 72. 39.;<BR>(2) उपढौकते<BR>(ढौक्, c. 1.): v. To offer;<BR>(3) उपहारं etc.<BR>ददाति (दा, c. 3.): v. Subs.<BR>II To high<BR>officers: दर्शनं कारयति (c. of कृ: with gen.).<BR>III To p. oneself: उपतिष्ठते (स्था, c. 1. = to<BR>attend on).<BR>IV To exhibit, shew: q. v.:<BR>प्रदर्शयति (c. of दृश्);<BR>to p. arms:<BR>अस्त्राणि परि-<BR>दर्शयति (?).<BR>V To give, deliver: q. v.: ददाति।<BR>Ph.:<BR>p. a false appearance of:<BR>विडम्बयति, R.<BR>xvi. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

present
PRESENT (adj.):<BR>I Now existing:<BR>(1) वर्तमानः<BR>(ना, नं), who is the seventh and p. Manu:<BR>सप्तमो वर्तमानो यो मनुः। B. p.; लट् denotes p.:<BR>वर्तमाने लट, Pāṇiṇi, iii. 2. 123.;<BR>(2) भवत्<BR>(f. न्ती rare), Ki. xii. 19.;<BR>(3) आधुनिक<BR>(f. की: of now).<BR>II In view:<BR>(1) by वर्तते<BR>(वृत्, c. 1. = to be),<BR>you are not p.:<BR>दूरे वर्तसे;<BR>my friend appears to be present before me:<BR>जाने<BR> प्रियसखी मेऽग्रतो वर्तत इति, Sa. vi.;<BR>(2) उपस्थित<BR>(f. ता),<BR>as she is p.:<BR>यदियमुपस्थिता, R. i. 87.;<BR>(3) सन्निहित (f. ता = near: q. v.);<BR>(4)<BR>सम्मुखस्थ (f. स्था = before the face of);<BR>(5)<BR>प्रत्यक्ष (f. क्षा = before the eyes of).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presentation
PRESENTATION:<BR>I The act: v. To present.<BR>II Nomination: निर्वाचनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presentiment
PRESENTIMENT: expr. by circumlo,<BR>I have a p.<BR>of something bad:<BR>चेतो मेऽशुभं कथयति, see Ki.<BR>xiii. 6., xi. 8.: v. To forebode, mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presently
PRESENTLY: अधुना: v. Instantly, soon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presentment
PRESENTMENT:<BR>(1) दानम् (= giving);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रदर्शनम् (= exhibition).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preservation
PRESERVATION: रक्षणम्<BR>or<BR>रक्षा, सं-, परि-, अभि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preservative
PRESERVATIVE:<BR>(1) रक्षा;<BR>(2) sometimes<BR>त्राणम्<BR>or<BR>-त्रम् in comp., बद्धगोधाङ्गुलित्राणौ, Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preserve
PRESERVE (v.): रक्षति, सं-, अभि-, (रक्ष्, c. 1.),<BR>to p. crops:<BR>शस्यं रक्षति, Ka. v. 81.: v. Also<BR>to save, keep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preserve
PRESERVE (subs.): i. e. p. ed fruits etc.: no<BR>equiv.: expr. with रक्षित (f. ता), सं- (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preserver
PRESERVER:<BR>(1) रक्षक (f. क्षिका), सं-, परि-;<BR>(2) रक्षितृ (f. त्री), सं-, परि-;<BR>(3) रक्षिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preside
PRESIDE: अधितिष्ठति, सम्-, (स्था, c. 1.),<BR>he p. s<BR>over the world:<BR>सोऽधितिष्ठति लोकम्, Ki.;<BR>(2) by<BR>subs.: v. President.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presidency
PRESIDENCY:<BR>I Superintendence:<BR>during<BR>my p. of the council:<BR>सभामधितिष्ठति मयि<BR>or<BR>मम<BR> सभाधिनायकत्वे (?).<BR>II Province.: q. v.:<BR>the<BR>Bengal p.:<BR>वङ्गदेशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

president
PRESIDENT:<BR>(1) अधिष्ठातृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) अधि-<BR>नायक (f. यिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presidential
PRESIDENTIAL: expr. by comp., p. chair:<BR>अधिनायकपदम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

press
PRESS (v. t.):<BR>I To squeeze: पीडयति, सं-, नि-,<BR> अभि-, आ-, (पीड्, c. 10.), without being p. ed:<BR>न खलु पीडितः, Vid. i.;<BR>drunk after being fully<BR>p. ed:<BR>निष्पीडितपीत (f. ता), B. xii. 18.<BR>II<BR>To embrace:<BR>(1) निष्पीडयति;<BR>(2) निष्पिनष्टि [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">Page542</a>]<BR>(पिष्, c. 7.), Ki. xvii. 13.<BR>III To urge,<BR>constrain: q. v.: अनुरुणद्धि (रुध्, c. 7.),<BR>being<BR>p. ed about improper things:<BR>अयुक्तमनुरुध्यमानः,<BR>Vi. v.<BR>IV To impress (IV): q. v.: धरति<BR>(धृ, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

press
PRESS (v. i.):<BR>I To crowd, throng: q. v.<BR>II<BR>To urge: अनुरुणद्धि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

press
PRESS (subs.):<BR>I P. ing: पीडनम्, सं-, नि-।<BR>II<BR>Printing-p.: *मुद्रायन्त्रम्।<BR>III Printed publi-<BR>-cations:<BR>the English p. is free:<BR>अयन्त्रितानीं-<BR>लण्डीयमुद्रितानि।<BR>IV Urgency: p. of business:<BR>कार्योपरोधः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

press-gang
PRESS-GANG: नाविकधारकाः (m. pl.) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pressing
PRESSING (subs.): expr. with निर्बन्धेन (adv.)<BR>or by verb.: v. To press (III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pressingly
PRESSINGLY:<BR>(1) निर्बन्धेन;<BR>(2) साग्रहम्;<BR>(3)<BR>निर्बद्धम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pressman
PRESSMAN: *मुद्रायान्त्रिकः: v. Also printer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pressure
PRESSURE:<BR>I Pressing: पीडनम्, सं-, नि-, निष्-,<BR> अभि-।<BR>II Fig., of trying circumstances: expr.<BR>by भारः (= burden: q. v.).<BR>III Of busi-<BR>-ness etc.: उपरोधः। Ph.: atmospheric p.:<BR>वायवो भरः<BR>or<BR>भारः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prestige
PRESTIGE: perh. प्रतिष्ठा<BR>or<BR>गौरवम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presume
PRESUME:<BR>I To suppose: q. v.: सम्भावयति<BR>(c. of भू),<BR>if you p. guilt:<BR>यदि सम्भाव्यते पापम्,<BR>Mr. ix. 36.<BR>II To venture too far: expr.<BR>by adj. or subs.: v. Presumptuous, pre-<BR>-sumption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presumption
PRESUMPTION:<BR>I Conjecture, guess: q. v.: तर्कः<BR>II Presumptuousness:<BR>(1) साहसम् (= bold-<BR>-ness: q. v.);<BR>(2) प्रगल्भता (= audacity: q. v.);<BR>(3) अवलेपः (= arrogance: q. v.).<BR>III In law:<BR>perh. सम्भावना, अनुमानम् (= inference).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presumptive
PRESUMPTIVE: Perh. सम्भावित (f. ता); आनु-<BR>मानिक (f. की).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presumptively
PRESUMPTIVELY: expr. by circumlo.,<BR>p. he is<BR>guilty:<BR>सम्भाव्यते स पापी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presumptuous
PRESUMPTUOUS:<BR>(1) साहसिक (f. की): v. Bold;<BR>(2) प्रगल्भ (f. ल्भा): v. Audacious;<BR>(3)<BR>अवलिप्त (f. प्ता): v. Arrogant. P. -ness: v.<BR>Presumption (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presumptuously
PRESUMPTUOUSLY:<BR>(1) साधसेन;<BR>(2) सावलेपम्;<BR>(3) प्रगल्भम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

presuppose
PRESUPPOSE: सिद्धं (f. द्धां) मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.):<BR>v. To suppose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pretence
PRETENCE:<BR>(1) व्यपदेशः: v. Pretext;<BR>(2)<BR>छलम्: v. Deceit (II);<BR>(3) उपधिः,<BR>with some<BR>p.:<BR>सोपधिः, Ki. i. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pretend
PRETEND:<BR>I To feign:<BR>(1) अपदिशति, वि-,<BR>(दिश्, c. 6.), p. ing a touch of headache:<BR>शिरःशूलस्पर्शमपदिशन्, P. ii.;<BR>(2) भावयति (c. of<BR>भू: rare), p. ing fainting from a rush of poison:<BR>भावितविषवेगविक्रियः, D. ii.;<BR>(3) by subs.<BR>II<BR>To p. to, claim: perh. अभिमन्यते (मन्, c.<BR>4.). P. ed i. e. feigned: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pretender
PRETENDER:<BR>I Impostor: q. v.<BR>II To the<BR>throne: राजाभिमानिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pretension
PRETENSION:<BR>I Claim, demand: q. v.: अभि-<BR>मानः (?).<BR>II Pretext: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pretermission
PRETERMISSION:<BR>I Omission: q. v.<BR>II In<BR>rhe: perh. व्याजस्तुतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preternatural
PRETERNATURAL: अप्राकृत (f. ता): v. Super-<BR>-natural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preternaturally
PRETERNATURALLY: expr. by adj. or<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pretext
PRETEXT:<BR>(1) अपदेशः, वि-,<BR>so that under that p.<BR>I will abduct and give her to you:<BR>तत्तेनैवापदेशेन<BR> हृत्वा तुभ्यं ददामि ताम्, K. s. x. 184.;<BR>under what<BR>p.:<BR>केनापदेशेन, Sa. ii.;<BR>(2) व्याजः,<BR>under a p. of<BR>returning the ring:<BR>अङ्गुलीयार्पणव्याजात्, K. s. x.<BR>102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prettily
PRETTILY:<BR>(1) चारु;<BR>(2) सुन्दरम्;<BR>(3) मञ्जु;<BR>(4) मञ्जुलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prettiness
PRETTINESS:<BR>(1) चारुता;<BR>(2) लावण्यम्;<BR>(3)<BR>सौन्दर्यम्: v. Beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prutty
PRUTTY (adj.):<BR>(1) लावण्यमय (f. यी),<BR>only p.<BR>feathers do not leave you:<BR>केवलं लावण्यमयी छाया<BR> त्वां न मुञ्चति, Sa. iii.<BR>(2) कमनीय (f. या) or rarely<BR>कान्त (f. न्ता),<BR>very p. wife:<BR>सुकान्तकान्ता, Ku.<BR>ix. 2.;<BR>(3) चारु (f. र्वो);<BR>(4) सु- in comp.,<BR>having p. eyes:<BR>सुलोचन (f. ना), R.: v.<BR>Beautiful, charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pretty
PRETTY (adv.): perh. अनल्प- in comp. (not a<BR>little)<BR>or<BR>प्रायेण (= nearly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prevail
PREVAIL: To prove the stronger:<BR>(1) अभि-<BR>भवति (भू, c. 1.: with acc.),<BR>that insanities p.<BR>over men like you:<BR>यद्भवादृशाः प्रमादैरभिभूयन्ते, K.;<BR>(2) अतिरिच्यते: v. To excel.<BR>II To be cur-<BR>-rent: expr. by adj.: प्रबल (f. ला,), प्रचल (f. ला),<BR>or<BR>प्रभूत (f. ता): v. Prevalent.<BR>III With<BR>on, upon, or with, to persuade, induce:<BR>q. v.: अनुनीय प्रवर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prevailing
PREVAILING (adj.), PREVAILINGLY: v. Preva-<BR>-lent, prevalently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prevalence
PREVALENCE:<BR>(1) प्रबलता; प्रचलता;<BR>(3)<BR>आधिक्यम्: v. Below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prevalent
PREVALENT:<BR>(1) प्रबल (f. ला = predominant);<BR>(2) प्रचल (f. ला current);<BR>(3) बहुल (f. ला=<BR>abundant);<BR>(4) साधारण (f. णी = common):<BR>v. Those words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prevalently
PREVALENTLY:<BR>(1) बलवत् (= forcibly);<BR>(2)<BR>बहुलम् (= abundantly);<BR>(3) साधारण्येन (= com-<BR>-monly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prevaricate
PREVARICATE:<BR>(1) अप-लपति (लप्, c. 1.);<BR>(2)<BR>निर्ह्नोतुमिच्छन् (f. न्ती) मिथ्योत्तरं ददाति, see Mu.<BR>i. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prevarication
PREVARICATION:<BR>(1) अपलापः;<BR>(2) निह्नवः;<BR>(3) better by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prevaricator
PREVARICATOR:<BR>(1) अपलापिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>निह्नववादिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prevent
PREVENT:<BR>(1) नि-वारयति, प्रति-, विनि-, (वृ, c.<BR>10.), p. ing the entrance of all attendants:<BR>निवारिताशेषपरिजनप्रवेश (f. शा), K.;<BR>(2) अव-<BR>रुणद्धि (रुध्, c. 7.);<BR>(3) नि-षेधति (सिध्, c.<BR>1.): v. To prohibit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prevention
PREVENTION:<BR>(1) निवारणम्;<BR>(2) अवरोधः;<BR>(3)<BR>निषेधः, प्रतिषेधः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

preventive
PREVENTIVE:<BR>(1) by verb;<BR>(2) -हर (f. रा)<BR>in comp.,<BR>p. of disease:<BR>रोगहर (f. रा);<BR>(3)<BR>घ्न (f. घ्नी = killing, destroying) in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

previous
PREVIOUS: पूर्व (f. र्वा): v. Former, preced-<BR>-ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

previously
PREVIOUSLY: पूर्वम्: v. Formerly. P. to: v.<BR>Before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prevision
PREVISION: expr. by पूर्वं पश्यति (दृश् c. 1. = to<BR>see): v. Foresight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prey
PREY (subs.): आमिषम्,<BR>became the p. of the<BR>enemies:<BR>द्विषामामिषतां ययौ, R. xii. 11. (Beast)<BR>of p.:) आमिषाशिन् (m.)<BR>or<BR>मांसादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prey
PREY (v.):<BR>I Lit.: आमिषं गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.)<BR>भक्षयति (भक्ष्, c. 10. = to eat: q. v.).<BR>II Fig.,<BR>to pillage, rob: q. v.<BR>III Fig., to vex,<BR>waste: प्र-बाधते (बाध्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

price
PRICE (subs.):<BR>(1) भूल्यम्,<BR>at what p.:<BR>कियता<BR> मूल्येन, P.; we have been cruelly fixed by you as<BR>the p. of these (ornaments): कल्पिता भूल्यमेतेषां<BR> क्रूरेण भवता वयम्, Mu. v. 17.;<BR>(2) अर्घः (rare),<BR>at a very low p.:<BR>लघीयसार्घेन, D. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

price
PRICE (v.):<BR>(1) मूल्यं स्थिरीकरोति<BR>or<BR>कल्पयति (c. of<BR>कॢप्).<BR>(2) to have price, or be p. d: अर्घति<BR>(अर्घ, c. 1; rare),<BR>gems have no p.:<BR>नार्घन्ति<BR> रत्नानि, P. i. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

price-current
PRICE-CURRENT: पण्यमूल्यनिर्धण्टः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

priceless
PRICELESS:<BR>(1) अमूल्य (f. ल्या);<BR>(2) अनर्घ (f.<BR>र्घा);<BR>(3) अनर्घ्य (f. र्घ्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prick
PRICK (v.):<BR>I To puncture: q. v.: विध्यति<BR>(व्यध्, c. 4.).<BR>II To goad: q. v.: तुदति<BR>(तुद्, c. 5.).<BR>III Fig., to sting:<BR>(1) विध्यति;<BR>(2) तुदति, Rām. ii. 11. 24. Ph.:<BR>with p. ed<BR>up ears:<BR>स्तब्धकर्ण (f. र्णा), H. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prick
PRICK (subs.):<BR>I Puncture: वेधः, -नम्।<BR>II<BR>A goad: q. v.: प्रतोदः।<BR>III Stinging pain:<BR>(1) दंशः;<BR>(2) यातना।<BR>IV A mark: लक्ष्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prickle
PRICKLE:<BR>(1) शूक (mn.);<BR>(2) कण्टक (mn. =<BR>thorn).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prickly
PRICKLY:<BR>(1) शूकिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) शूकवत् (f.<BR>ती);<BR>(3) कण्टकिन् (f. नी = thorny).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pride
PRIDE (subs.):<BR>I In good sense:<BR>(1) मानः,<BR> अभि-;<BR>(2) मानिता।<BR>II In bad sense:<BR>(1)<BR>अहङ्कारः;<BR>(2) दर्पः;<BR>(3) गर्वः (best equiv.),<BR>whose p. used to look down on the world as<BR>straw:<BR>तृणमिव परिभूतो यस्य गर्वेण लोकः, Ve. v.<BR>III Ornament: q. v.: अलङ्कारः<BR>the p. of the<BR>heaven:<BR>अलङ्कारः स्वर्गस्य (सा नः प्रियसखी॥॥॥),<BR>V. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pride
PRIDE (v.): expr. by subs. or adj.,<BR>you p. your-<BR>self without conquering me:<BR>मामजित्वैव दर्पः, Ve.<BR>v.;<BR>Gauri, who p. s herself in her beauty:<BR>रूप-<BR>गर्विता श्रीगौरी, V. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

priest
PRIEST:<BR>I Family:<BR>(1) पुरोहितः;<BR>(2) पुरोधस [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">Page544</a>]<BR>(m.).<BR>II Sacrificial:<BR>(1) ऋत्विज् (m.);<BR>(2)<BR>याजकः।<BR>III Vedic: श्रोत्रियः।<BR>IV In gen.:<BR>आचार्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

priestcraft
PRIESTCRAFT: पुरोहितानां चातुर्यम् and sim.<BR>expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

priestess
PRIEST ESS:<BR>(1) आचार्या;<BR>(2) होत्री;<BR>(3)<BR>याजिका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

priesthood
PRIESTHOOD:<BR>I The office: पौरोहित्यम्।<BR>II<BR>Priests collectively: by pl., पुरोहिताः, etc.;<BR>ब्राह्मण्यम् (= Brahmins, the Indian p.): v.<BR>Priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prestly
PRESTLY: expr. by comp. or gen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

priest-ridden
PRIEST-RIDDEN:<BR>(1) पुरोहितवश (f. शा ?);<BR>(2)<BR>पुरोहितायत्त (f. त्ता ?);<BR>(3) better by circumlo.<BR>v. Lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prig
PRIG:<BR>(1) दाम्भिक (f. की ?);<BR>(2) दर्पोद्धत (f.<BR>ता ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

priggish
PRIGGISH:<BR>(1) दाम्भिक (f. की ?);<BR>(2) दर्पोद्धत<BR>(f. ता ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prim
PRIM:<BR>(1) विनीत (f. ता);<BR>(2) by subs.: v.<BR>Primness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

primacy
PRIMACY: *प्रधानतमाचार्यत्वम्; प्रधानतमाचार्यपदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

primarily
PRIMARILY:<BR>(1) आदौ;<BR>(2) प्रथमम्: v. First.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

primary
PRIMARY:<BR>I First: q. v.: आदिम (f. मा).<BR>II<BR>Chief, principal: q. v.: मुख्य (f. ख्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

primate
PRIMATE: *प्रधानतमाचार्यः, सर्वप्रधानाचार्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prime
PRIME (subs.):<BR>I Dawn: q. v.: दिनमुखम्।<BR>II<BR>Of life: प्रौढता<BR>or<BR>प्रौढिः,<BR>in the p. of life:<BR>प्रौढ<BR>(f. ढा), J.<BR>III Beginning: q. v.: आदिः।<BR>IV Best portion:<BR>(1) उत्कृष्टभागः;<BR>(2) better<BR>by adj. Ph.:<BR>“p. of the moon”:<BR>नवेन्दुकला,<BR>Sa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prime
PRIME (adj.):<BR>I Primitive: q. v.: आदिम (f.<BR>मा).<BR>II First: q. v.: प्रथम (f. मा). Ph.:<BR>p. minister:<BR>महामन्त्री, Vid. iv.: v. Premier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

primer
PRIMER: प्रथमपुस्तकम् (?); बालपाठ्यम् (?); शिशु-<BR>शिक्षा (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

primeval
PRIMEVAL:<BR>(1) आदिम (f. मा);<BR>(2) प्राक्तन (f.<BR>नी = old, ancient: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

primitive
PRIMITIVE:<BR>(1) आदिम (f. मा); p. state:<BR>आदिमावस्था;<BR>(2) प्राक्तन (f. नी = old, ancient:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(3) प्रथम (f. मा = first: q. v.);<BR>(4)<BR>मूल- in comp. (= original: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

primness
PRIMNESS:<BR>(1) अत्यादरः (= formality);<BR>(2)<BR>विनीतता (= civility).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

primogeniture
PRIMOGENITURE:<BR>I Lit.: ज्येष्ठत्वम्।<BR>II In law:<BR>by circumlo,<BR>the law of p. obtains among the<BR>Iksvākus:<BR>इक्ष्वाकूणां हि सर्वेषां राजा भवति पूर्वजः,<BR>Ram. ii. 119. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

primordial
PRIMORDIAL: आदिम (f. मा): v. Primitive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

primrose
PRIMROSE: लताविशेषः; *भूसेवती।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prince
PRINCE:<BR>I A king: q. v.: अधिपतिः।<BR>II A<BR>king's son:<BR>(1) कुमारः;<BR>(2) राजपुत्रः and sim.<BR>comp.s. P. of Wales: (इंलण्डीय) युवराजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

princely
PRINCELY:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by ph. or comp.,<BR>p. birth:<BR>राजवंशप्रसूतिः;<BR>p. virtues:<BR>राजधर्माः।<BR>II Prince-like: राजसदृशः (शी, शं): v.<BR>Like.<BR>III Becoming a p.: राजयोग्यः (ग्या,<BR> ग्यं); राजोचितः (ता, तं), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

princess
PRINCESS:<BR>I A queen: q. v.<BR>II A king's<BR>daughter:<BR>(1) राजकुमारी;<BR>(2) राजपुत्री and<BR>sim. comp.s. P. of Wales: (इंलण्डीय) युवराज-<BR>पत्नी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

principal
PRINCIPAL (adj.):<BR>(1) मुख्य (f. ख्या);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रधान (f. ना): v. Chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

principal
PRINCIPAL (subs.):<BR>I Chief, master: q. v.:<BR>अध्यक्षः।<BR>II Capital: मूलम्, -धनम्:<BR>p. and<BR>interest:<BR>मूलकलान्तरे, Li. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

principality
PRINCIPALITY: राष्ट्रम्: v. Country, territory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

principally
PRINCIPALLY:<BR>(1) प्रधानतः;<BR>(2) प्राधान्येन;<BR>(3)<BR>विशेषतः। (= specially).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

principle
PRINCIPLE:<BR>I A fundamental truth: perh.<BR>तत्त्वम्<BR>or<BR>मूलतत्त्वम्।<BR>II A faculty: वृत्तिः। Ph.:<BR>a man of p.:<BR>सुवृत्त (f. त्ता); a man of no p.:<BR>खण्डितवृत्त (f. त्ता).<BR>III An element: मूलम्।<BR>IV Source, origin: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

print
PRINT (v. t.):<BR>I To impress: q. v.<BR>II With<BR>types: *मुद्रयति (nomi.),<BR>p. ed books:<BR>मुद्रित-<BR>पुस्तकानि।<BR>III To mark by pressure: perh.<BR>अङ्कयति (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

print
PRINT (subs.):<BR>I A mark: q. v.: चिह्नम्।<BR>II<BR>Type: *मुद्राक्षराणि (n. pl.), this is bad p.:<BR>*न शोभनान्येतानि मुद्राक्षराणि। Ph.: this is in p.:<BR>*मुद्रयन्त्येतत्;<BR>it is out of p.:<BR>*मुद्रितमदो निःशेषितम्;<BR>they like to see their names in p.:<BR>*स्वनामानि<BR> मुद्रितानि द्रष्टुमिच्छन्ति।<BR>III A picture: q. v.: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">Page545</a>]<BR>अङ्कः।<BR>IV A journal: q. v. V. A p. ed<BR>fabric: अङ्कितं वस्त्रम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

printer
PRINTER: *मुद्रयितृ (f. त्री),<BR>p.' s ink:<BR>मुद्रामसी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

printing
PRINTING (subs.): expr. by verb: v. Also<BR>print (subs (II).<BR>P.-press:<BR>मुद्रायन्त्रम्;<BR>p.<BR>office:<BR>मुद्राशाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prior
PRIOR (adj.):<BR>(1) प्रधान (f. ना = chief);<BR>(2)<BR>पौर्विक (f. की = anterior);<BR>(3) गरीयस् (f. सी<BR>= heavier).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prior
PRIOR (subs.): विहारपालः।<BR>P. ess:<BR>विहारपालिनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

priority
PRIORITY:<BR>(1) प्रधानता;<BR>(2) पौर्विकता;<BR>(3)<BR>गरिष्ठता: for dif.: v. Prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

priory
PRIORY: विहारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prise
PRISE: v. Prize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prism
PRISM: *क्रकचायतम्,<BR>achromatic p.:<BR>*अवर्णं<BR> क्रकचायतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prismatic
PRISMATIC, -AL:<BR>of p. form:<BR>*क्रकचायताकारः<BR>(रा, रं);<BR>p. colours:<BR>*क्रकचायतविश्लेषिता वर्णाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prison
PRISON:<BR>(1) कारागारम् and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(2)<BR>बन्धनागारम्;<BR>(3) कारा, Vi.;<BR>(4) चारः, -कः, D.,<BR>Has escaped from the p.:<BR>बन्धनं भित्त्वापक्रामति,<BR>Mr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prisoner
PRISONER:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) बन्दि (f. न्दी);<BR>(2)<BR>कारारुद्धः<BR>or<BR>-बद्धः (-द्धा, द्धं).<BR>II Of war: बन्दि<BR>(f. न्दी): v. Captive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pristine
PRISTINE (adj.):<BR>(1) आदिमः (मा, मं);<BR>(2)<BR>प्राक्तनः (नी, नं): v. Former, old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prithee
PRITHEE: प्रार्थये त्वाम्: v. Pray, thee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

privacy
PRIVACY:<BR>I The state:<BR>(1) विविक्तता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2) रहस् (n.).<BR>II A private place:<BR>(1)<BR>विविक्तम्, Ki. ix. 71.;<BR>(2) रहस् (n.) M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

private
PRIVATE (adj.):<BR>I Belonging to an indivi-<BR>-dual:<BR>(1) स्व (f. स्वा): v. Own;<BR>(2) not<BR>expr.,<BR>woman's p. property:<BR>स्त्रीधनम्, Da.<BR>II<BR>Secluded:<BR>(1) विविक्त (f. क्ता);<BR>(2) विजन<BR>(f. ना);<BR>(3) निर्जन (f. ना);<BR>(4) रहस् in<BR>comp.,<BR>in p.:<BR>रहसि: v. P. ly.<BR>III Secret:<BR>q. v.: गूढ (f. ढा).<BR>IV Not public: p. life:<BR>ग्राम्यवृत्तिः (?);<BR>p. education:<BR>गृहे शिक्षा (?);<BR>p. secretary:<BR>रहःसचिवः (?);<BR>p. person:<BR>साधारण-<BR>लोकः (?);<BR>p. act:<BR>असाधारणो विधिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

private
PRIVATE (subs.): साधारणसैनिकः and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

privateer
PRIVATEER:<BR>I Subs.: साधारणलोकानां बाधनपोतः<BR>(?).<BR>II Verb: expr. by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

privately
PRIVATELY:<BR>(1) रहः, R. xiii. 35.;<BR>(2) रहसि,<BR>D. vi.;<BR>(3) विविक्तम्;<BR>(4) विविक्ते;<BR>(5) एकान्ते;<BR>(6) विजने;<BR>(7) उपह्वरे (rare), D. ii.;<BR>(8) गूढम्<BR>(= secretly: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

privateness
PRIVATENESS:<BR>(1) विविक्तता: v. Privacy;<BR>(2)<BR>गूढता: v. Secrecy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

privation
PRIVATION:<BR>I Deprivation, absence: q. v.:<BR>अभावः।<BR>II Destitution, need: q. v.: कष्टम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

privative
PRIVATIVE: in gram.:<BR>(1) नञ्र्थकः;<BR>(2) अभाव-<BR>सूचकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

privet
PRIVET: लताविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

privilege
PRIVILEGE (subs): perh. अधिकारः; क्षमता<BR>(power); विशेषाधिकारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

privileged
PRIVILEGED (adj.):<BR>(1) by subs.;<BR>(2)<BR>विशेषाधिकारभाज् (mfn.) and sim. comp.s. (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

privily
PRIVILY: गूढम्: v. Secretly, privately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

privity
PRIVITY: i. e. connivance: योगः: v. Also<BR>knowledge. Ph.:<BR>in p.:<BR>गूढम्: v. Secretly;<BR>p. ies.:<BR>गुप्ताङ्गम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

privy
PRIVY (subs.):<BR>(1) शौचस्थानम्;<BR>(2) वर्चःस्थानम्,<BR>Mit.<BR>In the public p. at Benares:<BR>वाराणस्या-<BR>मुच्चारप्रस्रावस्थाने, Kar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

privy
PRIVY (adj.):<BR>I Private, secret: q. v.<BR>II<BR>P. to:<BR>(1) अभिज्ञः (ज्ञा, ज्ञं) (= acquainted<BR>with: q. v.);<BR>(2) सहायः (= accomplice).<BR>Ph.:<BR>p. council:<BR>राजसभा (?); p. councillor:<BR>राजसभाधिष्ठितः (?), राजसभासचिवः (?), etc.; p. seal<BR>(the seal): राजमुद्रा (?), (the minister): राजमुद्रा-<BR>मन्त्रिन् (m.), etc.;<BR>p. purse:<BR>राजधनम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prize
PRIZE (subs.):<BR>I Of honour:<BR>(1) पारितोषिकम्<BR>(= reward);<BR>(2) better by circumlo.,<BR>if a p.<BR>is offered and won:<BR>यदि भवान् भद्रकमुपन्यस्यति तदा<BR> भवते मयैतावद्देयमिति पणितं तत्रोपन्यासं निस्तीर्य लभते;<BR>so a p. won in a literary contest:<BR>तथा शास्त्रविज्ञान-<BR>विवादे निर्जित्य पल्लब्धम्, Da. 93.<BR>II Booty:<BR>expr. with: युद्धे प्राप्त (f. प्ता), N.<BR>s. or<BR>-गृहीत<BR>(f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prize
PRIZE (v.):<BR>I To estimate highly: बहु मन्यते<BR>(मन्, c. 4.).<BR>II To care: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prize-fighter
PRIZE-FIGHTER: मल्लयोद्धृ (f. द्ध्री: ?); मल्लयोधिन्<BR>(f. नी: ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prize-money
PRIZE-MONEY: perh. जयधनम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

probability
PROBABILITY:<BR>(1) सम्भाव्यता,<BR>or<BR>सम्भावनीयता<BR>(= likelihood);<BR>(2) सम्भावना (= presump-<BR>-tion): v. Below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

probable
PROBABLE:<BR>(1) by adv.: v. Probably;<BR>(2)<BR>by सम्भवति (= may be);<BR>(3) सम्भाव्य (f. व्या)<BR>or<BR>सम्भावनीय (f. या) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

probably
PROBABLY:<BR>I Very likely: प्रायेण<BR>or<BR>प्रायः, or<BR>p. he is fallen from the mouth of a hawk:<BR>प्रायेण<BR> श्येनमुखपरिभ्रष्टेन वानेन भवितव्यम्, K.;<BR>Śakuntalā<BR>is passing this time p. on the banks of the<BR>Mālini:<BR>इमां वेलां प्रायेण मालिनीतीरेषु शकुन्तला<BR> गमयति, Sa. iii.<BR>II With probability: expr.<BR>by verb,<BR>p. he will die:<BR>मरिष्यतीति सम्भावयामि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

probation
PROBATION: on p.: perh. परिदर्शनार्थम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

probationary
PROBATIONARY, PROBATIONAL: no equiv.:<BR>पारिदर्शनिक (f. की ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

probationer
PROBATIONER: perh. अन्तेवासिन् (f. नी = appren-<BR>-tice, pupil).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

probe
PROBE (subs.): एषणी, Wilson; शलाका, Williams,<BR>p. ing with a p.:<BR>एषण्या गतिमन्विष्य, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

probe
PROBE (v.): परीक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>examine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

probity
PROBITY: अमायता: v. Honesty, sincerity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

problem
PROBLEM:<BR>I In gen.: उपपाद्यम्, K. d.<BR>II<BR>Question, subject: q. v.: विषयाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

problematical
PROBLEMATICAL: सन्दिग्ध (f. ग्धा): v. Doubt-<BR>-ful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proboscis
PROBOSCIS:<BR>I Lit.: पोत्रम् (?).<BR>II The nose:<BR>प्रोथः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

procedure
PROCEDURE: prob. व्यवहारः,<BR>criminal p.:<BR>*दोष-<BR>व्यवहारः (-कार्यविधिः) used in Bengali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proceed
PROCEED:<BR>I To move, go: q. v.: चलति<BR>(चल्, c. 1.).<BR>II To go on, continue:<BR>प्रवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.): v. To reign.<BR>III In<BR>law; prob.: व्यवहारं करोति,<BR>who has p. ed<BR>against me:<BR>केन सह मम व्यवहारः, Mr. ix.;<BR>निवेदयति (= to inform: q. v.).<BR>IV To<BR>arise:<BR>(1) जायते, सं-, अभि-, उप-, (जन्, c. 4.),<BR>desire p.s from association:<BR>संगात् संजायते कामः,<BR>G. ii. 62.;<BR>(2) प्र- भवति, उप-, सं-, (भू, c. 1.);<BR>लोभात् क्रोधः प्रभवति, H. i. 23.;<BR>(3) उत्तिष्ठते, सम्-,<BR>(स्था, c. 1.),<BR>p. ing from the eye:<BR>नयनसमुत्थ<BR>(f. त्था) R. ii. 75.;<BR>(4) उत्पद्यते, सम्-, (पद्,<BR>c. 4.),<BR>light p. s from air:<BR>ज्योतिरुत्पद्यते वायोः,<BR>M. i. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proceeding from
PROCEEDING FROM: v. To proceed (IV),<BR>arising from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proceeding
PROCEEDING (subs.):<BR>I Action, transaction:<BR>q. v.: कार्यम्।<BR>II Procedure: perh. कार्यावली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proceeds
PROCEEDS: expr. by लब्ध (f. ब्धा), p. of sale:<BR>विक्रयेण लब्धम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

process
PROCESS:<BR>I Going on: in p. of time:<BR>कालक्रमेण, Ku.<BR>II Plan, means: q. v.:<BR>उपायः।<BR>III Legal: perh. आह्वानपत्रम्।<BR>IV<BR>In ana.: expr. with निर्गत (f. ता)<BR>or<BR>उत्थित<BR>(f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

procession
PROCESSION: यात्रा,<BR>bridal p.:<BR>वरयात्रा, N. xvi.<BR>4.;<BR>followers of a p.:<BR>आनुयात्रिको जनः, Ma. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proglaim
PROGLAIM:<BR>(1) घोषयति, वि-, उत्-, आ-, (घुष्, c.<BR>10.), and let (them)<BR>p. your victory:<BR>घोषयन्तु च<BR> ते जयम्, Mah. iv. 67. 20.; p. ing his guilt:<BR>तस्य दोषमुद्घोष्य, D. iv.;<BR>(2) ख्यापयति, प्र-, आ-,<BR>(c. of ख्या), p. (his)<BR>advent:<BR>प्रख्यापयन्त्या-<BR>गमम्, Vi. v. 1.: v. Also to announce,<BR>celebrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proclaimer
PROCLAIMER:<BR>(1) घोषक (f. षिका);<BR>(2) उद्घोषक<BR>(f. षिका);<BR>(3) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proclamation
PROCLAMATION:<BR>(1) घोषणम्, -णा,<BR>proclaim the<BR>p.:<BR>घोषयत घोषणम्,<BR>place for p.:<BR>घोषणास्थानम्,<BR>Mr. x.;<BR>(2) उद्घोषणम्;<BR>(3) विघोषणम्;<BR>(4)<BR>प्र-ख्यापनम्; etc. N. B. 2 to 4 only of the<BR>act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proclivity
PROCLIVITY: प्रवणता: v. Propensity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proconsul
PROCONSUL: भोगपतिः: v. Governor, viceroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

procrastinate
PROCRASTINATE:<BR>I Trans: v. To delay,^1<BR>postpone.<BR>II Intrans: विलम्बते: v. To<BR>delay.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

procrastiantion
PROCRASTIANTION: दीर्घसूत्रता: v. Delay, dial-<BR>-toriness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

procreate
PROCREATE (v. t.): जनयति (c. of जन्): v. To<BR>beget.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proctreation
PROCTREATION:<BR>(1) जननम्, प्र-;<BR>(2) उत्पादनम्;<BR>(3) expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

procreative
PROCREATIVE: expr. by comp., p. power:<BR>जननशक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proctor
PROCTOR:<BR>I In law: *मोक्तारः; उपदेष्टृ (m.).<BR>II In colleges: तत्त्वावधारकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

procumbent
PROCUMBENT: v. Prone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

procurable
PROCURABLE:<BR>(1) लभ्य (f. भ्या);<BR>(2) by verb:<BR>v. To procure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

procurator
PROCURATOR:<BR>I Roman: भोगपतिः।<BR>II In<BR>gen.: perh. निर्वाहकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

procure
PROCURE:<BR>I To get: q. v.: लभते (लभ्, c.<BR>1.).<BR>II To bring: q. v.: आनयति (नी, c.<BR>1.).<BR>III To effect: q. v.: साधयति (c. of<BR>सिध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

procurement
PROCUREMENT:<BR>(1) लाभः (= getting);<BR>(2)<BR>आनयनम् (= bringing);<BR>(3) साधनम् (= effect-<BR>-ing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

procurer
PROCURER:<BR>(1) विटः;<BR>(2) सु-रततालः: v. Also<BR>to pander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

procuress
PROCURESS:<BR>(1) कुट्ट(ट्टि)नी;<BR>(2) दूती;<BR>(3)<BR>शम्भली;<BR>(4) चुन्दी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prodigal
PRODIGAL:<BR>(1) अतिव्ययिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) बहु-<BR>व्ययिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) अमितव्ययिन् (f. नी);<BR>(4) त्यागशालिन् (f. नी);<BR>(5) दानशौण्ड (f.<BR>ण्डा: in giving); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prodigality
PRODIGALITY:<BR>(1) अतिव्ययः;<BR>(2) बहुव्ययः;<BR>(3)<BR>त्यागशालिता, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prodigally
PRODIGALLY:<BR>(1) मुक्तहस्तम् (= with open<BR>hand);<BR>(2) महता व्ययेन and sim. comp.s.<BR>(= with great expense), Mu. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prodigious
PRODIGIOUS:<BR>(1) अद्भुत (f. ता = wonderful);<BR>(2) अतिप्रमाण (f. णा = big).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prodigiously
PRODIGIOUSLY: अत्यन्तम्: v. Exceedingly,<BR>extremely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prodigy
PRODIGY:<BR>I A monster: expr. with अद्भुत<BR>(f. ता = wonderful: q. v.).<BR>II A portent:<BR>उत्पातः। Ph.:<BR>“a p. of learning”:<BR>असाधारण-<BR>पण्डितः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

produce
PRODUCE (v. t.):<BR>I To exhibit, bring for-<BR>-ward: दर्शयति, प्र-, अभि- (c. of दृश्), a surety<BR>for p. ing (a man): दर्शनप्रतिभूः, M.<BR>II To<BR>cause: q. v.<BR>(1) जनयति (c. of जन्),<BR>to p.<BR>heat or cold:<BR>शीतोष्णजननार्थाय, Sr.;<BR>(2)<BR>उत्पादयति (c. of पद्); v. Also to proceed<BR>(IV).<BR>III To bring forth, bear: q. v.<BR>(1)<BR>जनयति;<BR>(2) उत्पादयति;<BR>(3) better by pass.:<BR>v. Produced, be.<BR>IV To yield: q. v.:<BR>ददाति (दा, c. 3.), प्र-।<BR>V To elongate:<BR>वर्धयति (c. of वृध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

produced
PRODUCED, BE:<BR>(1) उत्पद्यते (पद्, c. 4.),<BR>so<BR>much can be p. here:<BR>एतावदत्रोत्पत्तुं योग्यम्, Mit.;<BR>(2) जायते, सं-, प्र-, अभि-, उप-, (जन्, c. 4.),<BR>p.<BR>in water:<BR>जलज (f. जा);<BR>(3) भवति,<BR>a field<BR>where barley is p.:<BR>यवभवं क्षेत्रम्, A.;<BR>(4)<BR>sometimes by deriv.,<BR>p. in autumn:<BR>हैमन<BR>(f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

produce
PRODUCE (subs.):<BR>(1) फलम् (= fruit),<BR>then he<BR>is to take its p. himself:<BR>तदा तस्य फलं स्वयमेव<BR> गृह्नीयात्, Mit.;<BR>(2) उत्पन्नम्<BR>or<BR>उत्पन्नं द्रव्यम्, Mi.;<BR>(3) शदः (= field p (rare), Vy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

product
PRODUCT (subs.):<BR>I Produce: q. v.: फलम्।<BR>II Work: q. v.: कर्मन् (n.).<BR>III In arith.:<BR>(1) गुणनफलम्, Vij.;<BR>(2) बधः<BR>or<BR>घातः, their p.:<BR>अनयोर्घातः, Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

production
PRODUCTION:<BR>I Producing:<BR>(1) उत्पादनम्;<BR>(2) प्र-जननम्।<BR>II Exhibition: q. v.: दर्शनम्, प्र-,<BR>III Produce: q. v.: उत्पन्नम्।<BR>IV Work:<BR>q. v.: कर्मन्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

productive
PRODUCTIVE:<BR>I Of soil: शस्यप्रद (f. दा):<BR>v. Fertile, rich.<BR>II In gen.:<BR>(1) फलप्रद<BR>(f. दा);<BR>(2) फलद (f. दा);<BR>(3) फलदायिन् (f.<BR>नी). Ph.: p. of i. e. producing, causing,<BR>expr. by verb: v. To produce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

productiveness
PRODUCTIVENESS: gen. expr. by adj.: फल-<BR>दायिता (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proem
PROEM: मुखबन्धः: v. Preface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profanation
PROFANATION:<BR>(1) दूषणम्: v. Pollution;<BR>(2)<BR>अपवित्रीकरणम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profane
PROFANE (v.):<BR>(1) दूषयति (c. of दुष्): To<BR>pollute;<BR>(2) अपवित्रीकरणम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profane
PROFANE (adj.):<BR>I Not holy:<BR>(1) अपवित्र<BR>(f. त्रा);<BR>(2) अपुण्य (f. ण्या).<BR>II Impious:<BR>q. v.: अधार्मिक (f. की).<BR>III Secular: q. v.:<BR>लौकिक (f. की).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profanely
PROFANELY:<BR>(1) धर्ममुन्मथ्य, -अतिक्रम्य, etc.;<BR>(2)<BR>by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profanity
PROFANITY: धर्भनिन्दा: v. Also profanation,<BR>impiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profess
PROFESS:<BR>I to assert: q. v.: ब्रवीति<BR>or<BR>ब्रूते (ब्रू, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">Page548</a>]<BR>c. 2.).<BR>II To pretend: q. v. P. ed:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रतिज्ञात (f. ता = declared);<BR>(2) प्रकाश (f. शा<BR>= open).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

professedly
PROFESSEDLY:<BR>(1) प्रकाशम् (= openly);<BR>(2)<BR>perh. विवृत्य।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profession
PROFESSION:<BR>I Declaration, avowal: q. v.:<BR>उक्तिः।<BR>II Claim, pretension: q. v.<BR>III<BR>Vocation, livelihood: q. v.: वृत्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

professional
PROFESSIONAL: expr. by comp., p. pride:<BR>विज्ञानाभिमानः (?);<BR>p. men:<BR>विज्ञानविदः (?);<BR>p. advice (of medical men): वैद्यकोपदेशः (?): v.<BR>Knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

professor
PROFESSOR: no proper equiv.: अध्यापकः: v.<BR>Teacher, master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

professorship
PROFESSORSHIP: अध्यापकपदम् and sim. comp.s.<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proffer
PROFFER: उपन्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.): v. To<BR>offer, propose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proficiency
PROFICIENCY:<BR>(1) प्रावीण्यम्;<BR>(2) कौशलम्,<BR>attained<BR>high p. in the special arts.:<BR>कलाविशेषेषु परं<BR> कौशलमवाप्, K.;<BR>(3) नैपुण्यम्, p. in the Purāṇas:<BR>पुराणगणनैपुण्यम्, D.;<BR>(4) वैचक्षण्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proficient
PROFICIENT:<BR>(1) प्रवीण (f. णा), p. in painting:<BR>चित्रकर्मणि प्रवीणः, K.;<BR>(2) कुशलः (ला, लं),<BR>p. in<BR>mythology and history:<BR>पुराणेतिहासकुशलः, D.;<BR>(3) निपुण (f. णा),<BR>p. in conversation:<BR>आलाप-<BR>निपुणः, K.;<BR>(4) विचक्षण (f. णा),<BR>p. in meta-<BR>physics.:<BR>आन्वीक्षिकीविचक्षणः, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profile
PROFILE: no equiv.: पार्श्वदृश्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profit
PROFIT (subs.): लाभः, p. s of your business:<BR>संव्यवहाराणां लाभा वः, Mu. i.; p. and loss:<BR>लाभालाभौ, Y. ii. 262.;<BR>to have p.:<BR>लाभं गृह्णाति,<BR>Vri.: v. Also benefit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profit
PROFIT (v.):<BR>(1) expr. by subs.,<BR>for p. ing<BR>one's self:<BR>लामार्थम्, Y.;<BR>(2) हितम् आवहति<BR>(वह्, c. 1.);<BR>(3) उपकरोति (कृ, c. 8.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profit
PROFIT (v. i.):<BR>I To gain: expr. with लाभः<BR>or<BR>उपकारः।<BR>II To take advantage of: expr.<BR>with लभते (लभ्, c. 1.),<BR>p. ing by the oppor-<BR>tunity:<BR>अवसरंलब्ध्वा।<BR>III To bring good:<BR>शुभम् आवहति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profitable
PROFITABLE:<BR>I Gainful, lucrative:<BR>(1)<BR>लाभावह (f. हा);<BR>(2) लाभजनन (f. नी);<BR>(3)<BR>लाभकर (f. री).<BR>II Useful, advantageous:<BR>(1) हितकर (f. री);<BR>(2) उपयोगिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profitably
PROFITABLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.: v.<BR>Usefully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profitless
PROFITLESS:<BR>(1) निष्फल (f. ला = useless);<BR>(2)<BR>निर्लाभ (f. भा: rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profligacy
PROFLIGACY:<BR>(1) पापाभिनिवेशः;<BR>(2) नष्टाचारता;<BR>(3) खण्डितवृत्तता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profligate
PROFLIGATE:<BR>(1) पापनिरत (f. रता);<BR>(2) नष्टाचार<BR>(f. रा);<BR>(3) खण्डितवृत्त (f. त्ता); and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profligately
PROFLIGATELY: expr. by circumlo.,<BR>to spend<BR>life p.:<BR>*पापकार्येषु जीवनमतिवाहयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profound
PROFOUND:<BR>I Deep: q. v.:<BR>(1) अतिगमीर (f.<BR>रा);<BR>(2) अगाध (f. धा).<BR>II Fig.: प्रगाढ (f.<BR>दा),<BR>p. reverence:<BR>प्रगाढभक्तिः।<BR>III Abstruse,<BR>occult: गहन (f. ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profoundly
PROFOUNDLY: प्रगाढम्: v. Deeply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profoundness
PROFOUNDNESS, PROFUNDITY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1)<BR>अगाधता;<BR>(2) अतिगर्भीरता।<BR>II Fig.: प्रगाढता।<BR>III Abstruseness:<BR>(1) गहनता;<BR>(2) निगूढता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profuse
PROFUSE:<BR>I Prodigal: q. v.: मुक्तहस्त (f. स्ता).<BR>II Copious, abundant: q. v.: प्रचुर<BR>(f. रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profusely
PROFUSELY:<BR>I Prodigally: q. v.: मुक्तहस्तम्।<BR>II Abundantly: q. v.: प्रचुरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

profusion
PROFUSION:<BR>I Prodigality: q. v.: मुक्तहस्तता।<BR>II Copiousness, abundance: q. v.: प्राचुर्यभ्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

progenitor
PROGENITOR: पितृ (m.), Ki. iii. 65.: v.<BR>Ancestor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

progeny
PROGENY: सन्ततिः: v. Offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prognostic
PROGNOSTIC: शकुनम् (= omen: q.v.): v. Also<BR>to forebode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prognosticate
PROGNOSTICATE: सूचयति (सूच्, c. 10.): v.<BR>Forebode, bespeak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prognostication
PROGNOSTICATION: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prognosticator
PROGNOSTICATOR: शुमाशुभलक्षणविद् (mfn.): v.<BR>Also prophet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

programme
PROGRAMME: सूचिपत्रम् (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

progress
PROGRESS (v.):<BR>I Lit.: चलति (चल्, c. 1.).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) उन्नतिं गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.), etc.;<BR>(2) उत्कृष्यते (pass. of कृष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

progress
PROGRESS (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: यात्रा: v. March [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">Page549</a>]<BR>(II.). Increase, growth: q. v.: वृद्धिः।<BR>III<BR>Advance, improvement: q. v.: उन्नतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

progression
PROGRESSION:<BR>a. p.:<BR>श्रेढीव्यवहारः; first term:<BR>मुखम्, वदनम्, आदिः;<BR>common difference:<BR>चयः;<BR>number of terms.:<BR>गुच्छः;<BR>sum:<BR>श्रेढीफलम्:;<BR>com-<BR>mon ratio:<BR>चयो गुणः;<BR>geometrical mean:<BR>उत्तरो<BR> गुणः, Li.<BR>Terms are in harmonic p. whose reci-<BR>procals are in arithmetic p.:<BR>येषांश्छेदाश्चयान्तरास्ते<BR> विषमचयान्तराः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

progressive
PROGRESSIVE:<BR>I Advancing: अग्रेसर (f. री).<BR>II Gradual: क्रमिक (f. का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prohibit
PROHIBIT: नि-षेधति, प्रति-, (सिध्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>forbid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prohibition
PROHIBITION:<BR>(1) निषेधः;<BR>(2) प्रतिषेधः;<BR>(3)<BR>निवारणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prohibitory
PROHIBITORY:<BR>(1) निषेधिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) निषेधक<BR>(f. धिका);<BR>(3) प्रतिषेधिन् (f. नी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

project
PROJECT (subs.): कल्पना: v. Scheme, plan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

project
PROJECT (v.):<BR>I To throw out: q. v.:<BR>प्रक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.).<BR>II To devise, plan:<BR>q. v.: कल्पयति (c. of कॢप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

project
PROJECT (v. i.):<BR>(1) लम्बते, प्र-, (लम्ब्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) बहिर्वर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.: ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

projecitile
PROJECITILE: क्षेपणीय (f. या = missile: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

projecting
PROJECTING (adj.):<BR>(1) प्र-लम्ब (f. म्बा),<BR>having<BR>a p. belly:<BR>लम्बोदर (f. रा); with a p. nose:<BR>प्रलम्बधोण (f. णा);<BR>(2) उदग्र (f. ग्रा: ?).<BR>Wilson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

projection
PROJECTION:<BR>I The act: प्रलम्बता।<BR>II Any-<BR>-thing projected: expr. with प्रलम्ब (f. म्बा).<BR>III In Math.: छेदकम्, Su. vi. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

projector
PROJECTOR: expr. by verb.: To project,<BR>scheme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proletaire
PROLETAIRE:<BR>(1) प्राकृतः, -जनः;<BR>(2) पृथग्जनः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prolific
PROLIFIC:<BR>I Of females: बहुप्रज (f. जा).<BR>II<BR>Fertile, productive: q. v.: बहुफल (f. ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prolix
PROLIX:<BR>(1) सुविस्तर (f. रा), Si. ii. 24.;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रपञ्च (f. ञ्चा), Mu.;<BR>(3) प्रपञ्चित (f. ता);<BR>(4)<BR>विस्तीर्ण (f. र्णा);<BR>(5) सुदीर्घ (f. र्घा = very long.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prolixity
PROLIXITY:<BR>(1) प्रपञ्चः, -ता;<BR>(2) विस्तीर्णता;<BR>(3)<BR>सुदीर्घता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prolixly
PROLIXLY:<BR>(1) सुविस्तरम्;<BR>(2) प्रपञ्चम्;<BR>(3)<BR>सुदीर्घम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prologue
PROLOGUE:<BR>(1) प्रस्तावना;<BR>(2) पूर्वरङ्गः;<BR>(3) नान्दी<BR>(benedictory p.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prolong
PROLONG:<BR>(1) वितनोति (तन्, c. 8.);<BR>(2) विस्तार-<BR>यति (स्तॄ, c. 10.);<BR>(3) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prolongation
PROLONGATION:<BR>(1) sometimes with प्रपञ्चः,<BR>p.<BR>of discussion:<BR>वादप्रपञ्चः;<BR>(2) by verb or<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prolusion
PROLUSION:<BR>I A prelude: q. v.<BR>II A trial:<BR>परीक्षा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

promenade
PROMENADE (subs.):<BR>I A walk:<BR>(1) विहारः<BR>or<BR>विहरणम् (= amusing);<BR>(2) विचरणम्।<BR>II A<BR>place: no equiv.: विहारप्रदेशः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

promenade
PROMENADE (v.):<BR>(1) विहरति (हृ, c. 1, = to<BR>amuse), R. vi. 57.;<BR>(2) विचरति (चर्, c. 1.),<BR>p. d with my friends:<BR>सह सखीजनेन व्यचरम्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prominence
PROMINENCE, PROMINENCY:<BR>(1) उन्नतता;<BR>(2)<BR>उन्नतिः, सम्-,<BR>the p. of my mind is like the p. s of<BR>your summit:<BR>मनसः शिखराणाञ्च सदृशी ते समुन्नतिः,<BR>Ku. vi. 66.: v. Also eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prominent
PROMINENT:<BR>(1) समुन्नत (f. ता);<BR>(2) उदग्र (f.<BR>ग्रा): v. High, eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prominently
PROMINENTLY:<BR>(1) प्राधान्येन;<BR>(2) विशेषेण (=<BR>specially);<BR>(3) स्पष्टम् (= clearly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

promiscuous
PROMISCUOUS:<BR>(1) प्रकीर्ण (f. र्णा);<BR>(2) संकीर्ण<BR>(f. र्णा);<BR>(3) मिश्रित (f. ता = mixed);<BR>(4)<BR>अविविक्त (f. क्ता = indiscriminate).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

promisciously
PROMISCIOUSLY:<BR>(1) निर्विशेषेण (= without any<BR>distinction);<BR>(2) अविविक्तम् (= indiscrimi-<BR>-nately);<BR>(3) सङ्कीर्णम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

promise
PROMISE (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्रतिजानीते (ज्ञा, c.<BR>9.),<BR>p. ing very well to Droṇa:<BR>तथेति च प्रतिज्ञाय<BR> द्रोणाय, Mah. i. 137. 14.;<BR>(2) प्रति-शृणोति (श्रु,<BR>c. 5.), Rāma p. d them to remedy the danger:<BR>प्रतिशुश्राव काकुत्स्थस्तेभ्यो विघ्नप्रतिक्रियाम्, R. xv. 4.<BR>II To furnish hopes: the crops p. well:<BR>फ्र्लाशंसीनि शस्यानि;<BR>he is a p. ing youth:<BR>वर्धिष्णुरयं<BR> युवा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

promise
PROMISE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्रतिज्ञा, -तम्,<BR>afraid<BR>of breach of p.:<BR>प्रतिज्ञा-भङ्गभीरुः, Ve. iii.;<BR>to ful-<BR>fil a p.:<BR>प्रतिज्ञां पूरयति, Ve. iv.;<BR>(2) प्रतिश्रवः or<BR>प्रतिश्रुतिः (rare);<BR>(3) अङ्गीकारः (= avowal).<BR>II<BR>Expectation, prospect: expr. with आशा,<BR>a<BR>man of the highest p.:<BR>अत्याशाजननोऽयं लोकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

promissory note
PROMISSORY NOTE: *प्रतिश्रवपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

promontory
PROMONTORY:<BR>(1) भूनासिका, Williams;<BR>(2)<BR>टिल्लः, -कः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

promote
PROMOTE:<BR>I To exalt, elevate:<BR>(1) वर्धयति<BR>(c. of वृध्);<BR>(2) उन्नतिं नयति (नी, c. 1.),<BR>Mr. x. 51.<BR>II To further, aid: q. v.<BR>III<BR>To excite: प्रवर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

promoter
PROMOTER:<BR>(1) प्रवर्तयितृ (f. त्री = setter on);<BR>(2) प्रोत्साहयितृ (f. त्री = encourager).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

promotion
PROMOTION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) वर्धनम्;<BR>(2)<BR>उन्नतिः (= exaltation):<BR>II Honour, advance-<BR>-ment: perh. उन्नतिः, पदवृद्धिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prompt
PROMPT (adj.):<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) सत्वर (f. रा<BR>= quick, ready);<BR>(2) with adv. क्षिप्रम् (=<BR>quickly), अविलम्बेन (= without delay), etc.<BR>II Of acts expr. by adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prompt
PROMPT (v.):<BR>I To incite:<BR>(1) उत्साहयति,<BR> प्र-, (c. of सह्);<BR>(2) प्र-णो(चो)दयति (नुद् or<BR>चुद्, c. 10.);<BR>(3) प्रवर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR>II<BR>To Assist by suggesting: perh.: अवबोधयति<BR>(c. of बुध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prompter
PROMPTER:<BR>(1) प्रोत्साहक (f. हिका);<BR>(2) अव-<BR>बोधक (f. धिका): v. To prompt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

promptitude
PROMPTITUDE, PROMPTNESS:<BR>(1) त्वरा, Ku.<BR>iii. 63.;<BR>(2) औत्सुक्यम् (= zeal), M. n.;<BR>(3)<BR>अविलम्बः (= want of delay);<BR>(4) क्षिप्रता (=<BR>quickness.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

promptly
PROMPTLY:<BR>(1) सत्वरम्;<BR>(2) त्वरितम्;<BR>(3) अवि-<BR>लम्बेन;<BR>(4) क्षिप्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

promulgate
PROMULGATE: घोषयति, उत्-, (घुष्, c. 10.): v.<BR>To proclaim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

promulgation
PROMULGATION: उद्घोषणम्: v. Proclamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

promulgator
PROMULGATOR: उद्घोषक (f. षिका): v. Pro-<BR>-claimer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prone
PRONE:<BR>I Inclined, disposed: प्रवण (f. णा).<BR>II Bent, not erect:<BR>(1) नत (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रणत (f. ता);<BR>(3) नम्र (f. म्रा).<BR>III With<BR>the face downward:<BR>(1) अधोमुख (f. खी);<BR>(2) अवाङ्भु ख (f. खी): and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proneness
PRONENESS:<BR>(1) प्रवणता;<BR>(2) नम्रता: for dif.: v.<BR>Above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prong
PRONG:<BR>(1) शूल (mn. ?);<BR>(2) शिखा (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pronominal
PRONOMINAL: expr. by comp.: v. Pronoun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pronoun
PRONOUN: सर्वनामन् (n.);<BR>personal, possessive,<BR>relative, interrogative p.:<BR>पुरुषवाचकं, स्वत्वद्योतकं<BR> सम्बन्धज्ञापकं, प्रश्नार्थकं सर्वनाम (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pronounce
PRONOUNCE:<BR>I To speak distinctly: उच्चारयति<BR>(c. of चर्),<BR>how clearly he p. s letters:<BR>अस्य<BR> स्पष्टता वर्णोच्चारणे, K.<BR>II To utter, deliver:<BR>(1) उदीरयति (ईर्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) perh. उच्चारयति,<BR>p. ing these words:<BR>उच्चार्य वाचमिति, Ki. xi. 81.<BR>III To declare, affirm: q. v.: ब्रवीति<BR>or<BR>ब्रूते<BR>(ब्रू, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pronunciation
PRONUNCIATION: उच्चारः, -णम्, p. of words:<BR>शब्दोच्चारणम्, Say.;<BR>knowing p.:<BR>उच्चारणज्ञः, Si.<BR>iv. 18.<BR>Science of Vedic p.:<BR>शिक्षा, Say.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proof
PROOF (subs.):<BR>I In gen.: प्रमाणम्,<BR>a thing is<BR>proved by marks and p. s.:<BR>लक्षणप्रभाणाभ्यां वस्तु-<BR>सिद्धिः, Say.; it cannot enter the precincts of p.:<BR>तदपि न प्रमाणकोटिं प्रवेष्टुमिष्टे, D. s.<BR>II Trial,<BR>test: q. v.: परीक्षा।<BR>III P. sheet: *परीक्षापत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proof
PROOF (adj.):<BR>water-p.:<BR>जलाभेद्य (f. द्या);<BR>p.<BR>against argument:<BR>युक्तिभिरहार्य (f. र्या); (their)<BR>minds are p. against temptation:<BR>चलति नयान्न हि<BR> चेतः, Ki. x. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prop
PROP (subs.):<BR>(1) आश्रयः (lit. and fig.);<BR>(2)<BR>शरणम् (fig.);<BR>(3) उपघ्नम् (rare), R. xiv. 1.;<BR>(4) आलम्बः, -नम् (lit.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prop
PROP (v.): सं- धारयति (धृ, c. 10.): v. To<BR>support, sustain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propagate
PROPAGATE (v. t.):<BR>I To reproduce:<BR>(1)<BR>संजनयति (जन्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) संवर्धयति (c. of<BR>वृध्, = to increase).<BR>II To spread: q. v.:<BR>विस्तारयति (स्तॄ, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propagate
PROPAGATE (v. i.): शावकान् सूते, प्र-, (सू, c. 2.)<BR>or<BR>जनयति, प्र-, (जन्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propagation
PROPAGATION:<BR>I Lit.: संजननम्।<BR>II Exten-<BR>-sion, dissemination: प्रचारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propel
PROPEL: प्र-णुदति (नुद्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propeller
PROPELLER: प्रचोदकयन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propense
PROPENSE: प्रवण (f. णा): v. Prone, inclined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propensity
PROPENSITY:<BR>(1) प्रवणता (= inclination);<BR>(2)<BR>शीलम् (= disposition);<BR>(3) व्यसनम् (= passion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proper
PROPER:<BR>I Right, becoming:<BR>(1) युक्तः<BR>(क्ता, क्तं), उप-;<BR>was it p. for you......<BR>युक्तं नाम<BR> मवताम्॥॥॥ Ve. iii.;<BR>(2) उचित (f. ता), सम्-, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">Page551</a>]<BR>it is p. for us to attend to the stranger:<BR>उचितं<BR> नोऽतिथिपर्युपासनम्, Sa. i. Ph.:<BR>I will do what is<BR>p.:<BR>यथार्हमाचरिष्यामि, K.; should do what is p.:<BR>कुर्याद्यथोचितम्, H.<BR>II Own: q. v.: स्व (f. स्वा).<BR>III Peculiar: q. v.: विशेष- in comp. Ph.:<BR>p. noun: perh. विशेषनामन् (n.); संज्ञा, Pāṇini,<BR>Vi. 3. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

properly
PROPERLY:<BR>I Suitably, fitly:<BR>(1) युक्तम्, उप्-;<BR>(2) उचितम्, सम्-;<BR>(3) better by adj.<BR>II<BR>Strictly:<BR>(1) तत्त्वतः;<BR>(2) वथार्थतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

property
PROPERTY:<BR>I Quality: q. v.:<BR>(1) धर्मः;<BR>(2)<BR>गुणः।<BR>II What is possessed:<BR>(1) सम्पत्तिः;<BR>(2) द्रव्यम् (= thing),<BR>immoveable and moveable<BR>p.:<BR>स्थावरं जङ्गमं द्रव्यम्, Vri.;<BR>(3) धनम्<BR>(= money),<BR>woman's p.:<BR>स्त्रीधनम्, Mi.;<BR>(4)<BR>अर्थः (= 3.),<BR>of paternal p.:<BR>पित्र्यस्यार्थस्य, Da.;<BR>(5) वित्तम्।: v. Money;<BR>(6) स्वम् (rare),<BR>divided p.:<BR>विभक्तं स्वम्, Da.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prophecy
PROPHECY: perh. भविष्यद्वादः and sim. comp.s.;<BR>better by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prophesy
PROPHESY:<BR>(1) कथयति (कथ्, c. 10. = to say)<BR>or<BR>वि- आदिशति (दिश्, c. 6. = to direct) (when<BR>the sense is clear);<BR>(2) अनागतं (f. तां)<BR>or<BR>मविष्यन्तं (न्तीं, त्) वदति (वद्, c. 1.),<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prophet
PROPHET, PROPHETERS:<BR>(1) सिद्ध (f. द्धा),<BR>say-<BR>ing of a p.:<BR>सिद्धादेशः Ram. i.;<BR>(2) साधु<BR>(f. ध्वी), it was told by a p. in my presence:<BR>शिवादेशकेन साधुना मत्समक्षं व्यादिष्टा, Mal. i.;<BR>(3)<BR>भविष्यद्वक्तृ (f. क्त्री: (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prophetic
PROPHETIC, -AL: expr. by verb or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prophetically
PROPHETICALLY:<BR>(1) perh. सिद्धवत्<BR>or<BR>साधुवत्;<BR>(2) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propinquity
PROPINQUITY: सन्निकर्षः: v. Nearness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propitiate
PROPITIATE:<BR>(1) प्रसादयति (c. of सद्),<BR>p. d<BR>Durvāsas:<BR>दुर्वाससं प्रसादयमास, V. p. i. 9., 18.;<BR>(2) अनुरञ्जयति (c. of रञ्ज् = conciliate).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propitiation
PROPITIATION:<BR>I The act.:<BR>(1) प्रसादनम्, ना,<BR>attended to the p. of gods:<BR>प्रसादनामाद्रियतामराणाम्,<BR>N. xiv. 1.;<BR>(2) अनुरञ्जनम् (= conciliation).<BR>II The means: बलिः (= offering).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propitiator
PROPITIATOR:<BR>(1) प्रसादक (f. दिका);<BR>(2)<BR>अनुरञ्जक (f. ञ्जिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propitiatory
PROPITIATORY (adj.):<BR>(1) प्रसादन (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>अनुरञ्जक (f. ञ्जिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propitious
PROPITIOUS:<BR>I Favourable, kind: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रसन्न (f. न्ना);<BR>(2) सदय (f. या).<BR>II Auspi-<BR>-cious:<BR>(1) शुभ (f. भा);<BR>(2) कल्याण (f. णी);<BR>(3) मङ्गल (f. ला);<BR>(4) मङ्गल्य (f. ल्या);<BR>(5)<BR>कल्याणकर (f. री);<BR>(6) क्षेमंकर (f. रा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propitiously
PROPITIOUSLY:<BR>I Kindly: q. v.: प्रसन्नमनसा।<BR>II Auspiciously: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propitiousness
PROPITIOUSNESS:<BR>I Kindness: q. v.: प्रसादः।<BR>II Auspiciousness: expr. by adj.,<BR>p. of<BR>season:<BR>शुभतुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proportion
PROPORTION:<BR>I Symmetrical arrangement:<BR>perh. अङ्गसौष्ठवम्। Ph.: her body is in perfect p.:<BR>तस्याश्चतुरस्रशोमि (अन्यूनातिरिक्तम्, M. n.) वपुः, Ku.<BR>i. 32.;<BR>the building is out of p.:<BR>*विषमपरिमाणं<BR> हर्म्यम्।<BR>II Share, lot: q. v.: अंशः।<BR>III Rela-<BR>-tion, adaptation: q. v.: सम्बन्धः। Ph.:<BR>in p.<BR>to his strength:<BR>तस्य वीर्यानुसारेण: v. Accord-<BR>-ing.<BR>IV In math.: *सम्बन्धसाम्यम्;<BR>the four<BR>quantities are in p.:<BR>ते चत्वारो राशयः समाननिष्पत्ति-<BR>युता भवन्ति, K. d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proportion
PROPORTION (v.): perh. समीकरोति: v. Also<BR>to adjust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proportional
PROPORTIONAL:<BR>I Lit.: समप्रमाण (f. णा ?).<BR>II In math.: v. Proportion (IV.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proportionally
PROPORTIONALLY, PROPORTIONATELY:<BR>(1)<BR>यथाप्रमाणम्;<BR>(2) sometimes प्रतिप्रतीकम् (= in<BR>every limb.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proposal
PROPOSAL:<BR>(1) उपन्यासः;<BR>(2) प्रस्तावः;<BR>(3) कल्पः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propose
PROPOSE:<BR>(1) उपन्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4. = to put<BR>forward);<BR>(2) प्रस्तौति (स्तु, c. 2.)<BR>or<BR>प्रस्तावं<BR> करोति (as a beginning);<BR>(3) कल्पयति (कॢप्,<BR>c. 10. = to devise, intend: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proposer
PROPOSER: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proposition
PROPOSITION:<BR>I Proposal: q. v.<BR>II In logic<BR>etc.: प्रतिज्ञा।<BR>III In gram.: वाक्यम्।<BR>IV In<BR>Poetry: कथामुखम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propound
PROPOUND:<BR>(1) उपन्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.);<BR>(2)<BR>उपक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.), p. another doctrine:<BR>पक्षान्तरमुपक्षिपन्ति, D. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proprietary
PROPRIETARY: expr. by comp., p. right:<BR>स्वाम्यधिकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proprietor
PROPRIETOR: स्वामिन् (m.): v. Owner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proprietorship
PROPRIETORSHIP: स्वाम्यम्, स्वामित्वम्,<BR>or<BR>स्वामिभावः,<BR>Da.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proprietress
PROPRIETRESS:<BR>(1) स्वामिनी;<BR>(2) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propriety
PROPRIETY:<BR>(1) सङ्गतता: v. Fitness;<BR>(2)<BR>औचित्यम्,<BR>with p.:<BR>समुचितम्: v. Also civility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

propulsion
PROPULSION:<BR>(1) प्रणोदः, -नम्;<BR>(2) प्रचोदः, -नम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prorogation
PROROGATION: व्याक्षेपः: v. Postponement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prorogue
PROROGUE: व्याक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.): v. To<BR>postpone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prosaic
PROSAIC:<BR>I Lit.: गद्य- in comp.<BR>II Dull,<BR>dry: q. v.: नीरस (f. सा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proscribe
PROSCRIBE:<BR>I Lit.: perh. अपपात्रयति (nomi.)<BR>or<BR>अपपात्रीकरोति।<BR>II To reject, interdict:<BR>q. v.: निरस्यति (अस्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proscription
PROSCRIPTION:<BR>I Lit.: अपपात्रीकरणम्।<BR>II Re-<BR>-jection: निरसनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prose
PROSE (subs.): गद्यम्,<BR>p. writer:<BR>गद्यलेखकः; p.<BR>smelling poetry (i. e. intermixed with poetical<BR>feet): वृत्तगन्धि गद्यम्, Sah. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prose
PROSE (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: गद्य- in comp.<BR>II Dull,<BR>plain: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prose
PROSE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: गद्येन लिखति: v. To<BR>write.<BR>II To talk or relate in a prosy<BR>manner: perh. गद्यायते (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prosecute
PROSECUTE:<BR>I In law:<BR>(1) अभियोजयति (युज्,<BR>c. 10. = to accuse: q. v.);<BR>(2) निवेदयति (c.<BR>of विद् = to inform: q. v.).<BR>II To pursue,<BR>continue: अनुसरति (सृ, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prosecution
PROSECUTION:<BR>I In law: अभियोगः: v. Accu-<BR>-sation, information.<BR>II Pursuit:<BR>(1) अनु-<BR>सरणम्;<BR>(2) अनुष्ठानम् (= perpetration).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prosecutor
PROSECUTOR: अभियोक्तृ (m.): अर्थिन् (m.)<BR>(= petitioner).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prosecutrix
PROSECUTRIX: अभियोक्त्री, अभियोगकारिणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proselyte
PROSELYTE:<BR>(1) मिन्नधर्मग (f. गा: ?);<BR>(2)<BR>धर्मान्तरग्राहिन् (f. णी): ?): v. Convert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proserlytism
PROSERLYTISM:<BR>(1) भिन्नधर्मग्राहणम् (?); धर्मान्तर-<BR>नयनम् (?), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proselytize
PROSELYTIZE:<BR>(1) भिन्नधर्मं ग्राहयति (c. of ग्रह:<BR>?).<BR>p. to Christianity:<BR>कृष्टधर्मं ग्राहयति;<BR>(2)<BR>धर्मान्तरं नयति (नी c. 1.: ?); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prosodical
PROSODICAL:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) छान्दस (f. सी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prosodian
PROSODIAN:<BR>(1) छन्दोज्ञ (f. ज्ञा);<BR>(2) छन्दःशास्त्र-<BR>विशारद (f. दा) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prosody
PROSODY:<BR>(1) छन्दस् (n.);<BR>(2) छन्दःशास्त्रम्; and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR>Pingala's p.:<BR>पिङ्गलच्छेन्दःसूत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prosopia
PROSOPIA: समासोक्तिः, Kav. x. 11. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prospect
PROSPECT:<BR>I View: q. v.: दृष्टिः,<BR>a grand p. of<BR>the world is on view:<BR>आश्चर्यदर्शनः संलक्ष्यते<BR> मनुष्यलोकः, Sa. vii.<BR>II Field of view:<BR>(1)<BR>चक्षुर्विषयः;<BR>(2) with दृष्टिगोचर (f. रा).<BR>III<BR>Anticipation: आयतिः, of unpolluted p. s:<BR>अदूषितायति (mfn.), Ki. ii. 35.<BR>IV Expec-<BR>-tation; आशा<BR>or<BR>प्रत्याशा (= hope).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prospective
PROSPECTIVE:<BR>I Relating to future: expr.<BR>with आयतिः<BR>or<BR>उत्तरकालः,<BR>highly conducive to p.<BR>good:<BR>उपकारकमायतेर्भृशम्, Ki. ii. 43.<BR>II Cir-<BR>-cumspect: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prospectively
PROSPECTIVELY: expr. by circumlo.: v. Pros-<BR>-pective (I), future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prosper
PROSPER:<BR>I To favour: q. v.: अनुकूलयति।<BR>II<BR>To thrive, make gain: expr. by adj.: v.<BR>Prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prosperity
PROSPERITY:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) ऋद्धिः, सम्-,<BR>for-<BR>tune is p.:<BR>ऋद्धिः श्रीः, V. p. i. 8. 25.;<BR>(2)<BR>सम्पद् (f. = good fortune), with little p.:<BR>स्वल्पया सम्पदा, Si. ii. 32.;<BR>(3) ऐश्वर्यम् (lordly),<BR>mad with p.:<BR>ऐश्वर्यमत्त (f. त्ता), V. p. i. 9. 12.<BR>II Advancement:<BR>(1) उदयः;<BR>(2) उन्नतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prosperous
PROSPEROUS:<BR>I Successful:<BR>(1) समृद्ध (f. द्धा);<BR>(2) श्रीमत् (f. ती);<BR>(3) ऐश्वर्यशालिन् (f. नी = rich).<BR>II Favourable: q. v.: अनुकूल (f. ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prosperously
PROSPEROUSLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prostitute
PROSTITUTE (subs.):<BR>(1) वेश्या (also used as a<BR>term of reproach to other woman);<BR>(2)<BR>पण्यस्त्री and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(3) वेशवधूः, Mr.;<BR>(4) साधारणस्त्री, Mr.;<BR>(5) स्वाधीनयौवना, Mr.;<BR>v. Courtesan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prostitution
PROSTITUTION:<BR>I Lit.: वेश्यावृत्तिः।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>perh. नीचवृत्तिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prostrate
PROSTRATE (adj.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) भूमिशय (f. या<BR>= laid on the ground):<BR>(2) साष्टाङ्गप्रणत (f.<BR>ता = in supplication);<BR>(3) पतित (f. ता =<BR>fallen).<BR>II Fig.: broken down: अवसन्न<BR>(f. न्ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prostrate
PROSTRATE (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>will p. himself to<BR>make p. supplication:<BR>दण्डप्रणामं कुर्वन् कायप्रपातं<BR> कुरुते, Vet.;<BR>p. yourself before the goddess:<BR>देव्यै<BR> दण्डप्रणामेन प्रणम्, Vet.: v. To fell, prostrate<BR>(adj. II).<BR>II To demolish, destroy: q. v.:<BR>पातयति (c. of पत्).<BR>III To reduce, break-<BR>-down: अवसादयति (c. of सद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prostration
PROSTRATION:<BR>I In adoration: expr. with<BR>दण्डप्रणामः, साष्टाङ्गप्रणामः,<BR>or<BR>प्रणिपातः।<BR>II Dejec-<BR>-tion: q. v.: अवसादः।<BR>III Ruin: q. v.:<BR>पातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prosy
PROSY: perh. दीर्घसूत्र (f. त्रा): v. Also dull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protean
PROTEAN: fig.:<BR>(1) बहुमाय (f. या);<BR>(2) बहुरूपिन्<BR>(f. णी), and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protect
PROTECT:<BR>(1) रक्षति, सं-, अभि-, परि-, प्रति-, (रक्ष्,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>shall always p. self even at the expense<BR>of wife and wealth:<BR>आत्मानं सततं रक्षेद्दारैरपि धनैरपि,<BR>M. vii. 213;<BR>(2) गोपायति, अभि-, (गुप्, c. 1.),<BR>p. ed her like the world:<BR>उर्वीमिव जुगोप ताम्, R.<BR>ii. 3.: v. Also to save.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protection
PROTECTION:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) रक्षा<BR>or<BR>रक्षणम्, अभि-,<BR> परि-, सं-;<BR>(2) गुप्तिः, p. of the three worlds:<BR>त्रिभुवनगुप्तिः, Ki. x. 15.<BR>II That which<BR>protects:<BR>(1) आश्रयः;<BR>(2) शरणम्,<BR>how can I<BR>seek another for p.:<BR>कथं प्रपत्स्ये शरणार्थमन्यम्, R.<BR>xiv. 64.<BR>III In commerce: स्वदेशपण्यरक्षार्थं<BR> विदेशीयपण्यानामुपर्यधिकशुल्कसंस्थापनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protective
PROTECTIVE: expr. by comp., p. duties:<BR>*रक्षाशुल्कानि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protector
PROTECTOR, PROTECTRESS:<BR>(1) रक्षक (f. क्षिका);<BR>सं-, परि-;<BR>(2) रक्षितृ (f. त्री), सं-, परि-;<BR>(3)<BR>गोप्तृ (f. प्त्री);<BR>(4) गोपायक (f. यिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protectorate
PROTECTORATE: perh. शासनम्, during his p.:<BR>शासति तस्मिन्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protege
PROTEGE (f. ee):<BR>(1) आश्रित (f. ता);<BR>(2) perh.<BR>पालित (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protest
PROTEST (v.)<BR>I To avow, assert: q. v,: प्रति-<BR>जानीते (ज्ञा, c. 9.).<BR>II To p. against: विरुद्धं<BR> वदति (वद्, c. 1.: with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protest
PROTEST (subs.): perh. विरुद्धवादः<BR>or<BR>प्रतिवादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protestant
PROTESTANT: *रोमकमतप्रतिवादिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protestantism
PROTESTANTISM: *रोमकमतप्रतिवादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protocol
PROTOCOL: perh. आदिलेखः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prototype
PROTOTYPE:<BR>I Lit.: आदर्शः।<BR>II Of men.:<BR>perh. गुरुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protract
PROTRACT:<BR>I To prolong: वितनोति (तन्, c.<BR>5.).<BR>II To delay: q. v.: विलम्बयति (c. of<BR>लम्ब्). P. ed.: i. e. long: सुदीर्घ (f. र्घा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protrude
PROTRUDE:<BR>I Trans.:<BR>(1) प्रसारयति (c. of<BR>सृ);<BR>(2) perh. निर्गमयति (c. of गम्).<BR>II<BR>Intrans:<BR>(1) उद्भिद्यते (pass. of भिद्);<BR>(2)<BR>निःसरति (सृ, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protrusion
PROTRUSION:<BR>(1) प्रसारणम् (= stretching);<BR>(2)<BR>उद्भेदः (= coming out).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protuberance
PROTUBERANCE:<BR>I Tumour: स्फोटः।<BR>II<BR>Prominence, projection: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

protuberant
PROTUBERANT:<BR>(1) उन्नत (f. ता = raised);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रलम्ब (f. म्बा = projecting.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proud
PROUD:<BR>I In good sense:<BR>(1) मानिन् (f. नी),<BR>अभि-;<BR>(2) मानवत् (f. ती), अभि-, Ki.<BR>II In<BR>bad sense:<BR>(1) गर्वित (f. ता);<BR>(2) दृप्त (f.<BR>प्ता);<BR>(3) अहङ्कारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(4) सगर्व (f. र्वा);<BR>(5) दर्पवत् (f. ती); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proudly
PROUDLY:<BR>(1) सगर्वम्;<BR>(2) सदर्पम्;<BR>(3) साहङ्कारम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prove
PROVE (v. t.):<BR>I To test: q. v.: परीक्षते (ईक्ष्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II To establish: q. v.:<BR>(1) प्रतिपादयति<BR>(c. of पद्),<BR>in the first chapter, we have p. d<BR>that He is the soul of all us:<BR>प्रथमेऽध्याये स एव<BR> सर्वेषां न आत्मैतत् प्रतिपादितम्, S. ii. 1.;<BR>(2) साधयति<BR>(c. of सिध्), a thing may be p. d without<BR>(regular)<BR>proof:<BR>असतापि प्रमाणेन वस्तु सुध्यति,<BR>S. p. b.;<BR>(3) वि-भावयति (c. l. of भू rare),<BR>and<BR>does not p. what he asserts:<BR>उक्तञ्च न विभावयेत्,<BR>M. viii. 56.: v. Also to shew.<BR>III To<BR>verify: प्रमाणयति (nomi.),<BR>p. ing what Yudhiṣ-<BR>ṭhira said:<BR>प्रमाणयन् वाक्यमजातशत्रोः, Ki. iii. 24.<BR>IV To suffer: q. v.: सहते (सह्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prove
PROVE (v. i.):<BR>(1) often by भवति (= to be-<BR>-come);<BR>(2) by circumlo.,<BR>it has p. d to be<BR>false;<BR>तदवैमि कैतवम्, Ku. iv. 9.: v. Also to<BR>turn out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provender
PROVENDER: for cattle: यवसः: v. Fodder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proverb
PROVERB: जनप्रवादः, लोकवादः, and sim. comp.s.:<BR>the p. that shame is only in the eye:<BR>अक्षिलज्जेति<BR> जनप्रवादः, N. xiv. 30; as the common p. is if<BR>you can get honey in the swallow wort, why [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">Page554</a>]<BR>should you go to the mountains:<BR>तथा च<BR> लौकिकानामाभाणकः” अर्के चेन्मधु विन्देत किमर्थं पर्वतं<BR> व्रजेत्”, T.;<BR>there is the p. the state of the mind<BR>bespeaks of coming pleasure or pain:<BR>अस्ति खलु<BR> लोकप्रवादः ‘आगामि सुखं दुःखं वा हृदयसमवस्था कथयती ति,<BR>Mal. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proverbial
PROVERBIAL: expr. by subs.,<BR>p. saying:<BR>लोक-<BR>प्रवादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proverbially
PROVERBIALLY: expr. by subs. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provide
PROVIDE (v. t.):<BR>I To prepare: q. v.: उप-<BR>कल्पयति (कॢप्, c. 10.)<BR>II To furnish, supply:<BR>q. v.: सं-योजयति (युज्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provide
PROVIDE (v. i.):<BR>I With against or for: expr.<BR>by circumlo:<BR>p. against cold:<BR>शीतनिवारणार्थं<BR> सज्जीभवति;<BR>p. for education:<BR>शिक्षामुपपादयति (c.<BR>of पद्).<BR>II To direct, enjoin: it p. s that:<BR>अनेनैतन्निर्दिष्टम्॥॥॥॥।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provided
PROVIDED (conj.):<BR>(1) expr. with यदि and<BR>विधिलिङ्,<BR>p. he does not come to my house:<BR>यदि<BR> स मद्गृहं नागच्छेत्;<BR>(2) sometimes by words<BR>meaning but: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

providence
PROVIDENCE:<BR>I God: q. v.: विधातृ (m.).<BR>II<BR>His care: perh., पर्यवेक्षणम्; हस्तम् (= hand)<BR>will often do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provident
PROVIDENT: पर्यवेक्षक (f. क्षिका): v. Cautious,<BR>prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

providential
PROVIDENTIAL: expr. by adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

providentially
PROVIDENTIALLY: ईश्वरेच्छया;<BR>(2) विधातृवशात्;<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

providently
PROVIDENTLY:<BR>(1) प्रसमीक्ष्य;<BR>(2) पर्यवेक्ष्य;<BR>(3)<BR>विमृश्य।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provider
PROVIDER: उपकल्पक (f. ल्पिका): v. To provide,<BR>prepare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

providing
PROVIDING (conj.): v. Provided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

province
PROVINCE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) विषयः;<BR>(2) मण्डलम्;<BR>(3) राष्ट्रम् (= kingdom).<BR>II Fig., a division:<BR>(1) विषयः;<BR>(2) अङ्गम् (subordinate).<BR>III<BR>Business, duty: q. v.:<BR>(1) कार्यम्;<BR>(2) नियोगः<BR>(= employment).<BR>IV Duty: q. v.: धर्मः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provincial
PROVINCIAL (adj.):<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) देशीय<BR>(f. या = country).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provincialism
PROVINCIALISM: of language: देशभाषा, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provision
PROVISION:<BR>I Providing: उपकल्पः, -नम्।<BR>II<BR>Provisions: q. v.<BR>III Condition, disputa-<BR>-tion: समयः।<BR>IV Arrangement: विधानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provisonal
PROVISONAL:<BR>(1) सामयिक (f. की);<BR>(2) आपात-<BR>in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provisionally
PROVISIONALLY:<BR>(1) आपात- in comp.;<BR>(2)<BR>आपाततः;<BR>(3) perh. तत्कालम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provisions
PROVISIONS:<BR>(1) सामग्री;<BR>(2) पाथेयम् (for a<BR>journey);<BR>(3) उपस्करः (= any article),<BR>she<BR>carrying p. s and other things:<BR>तयोह्यमान-<BR>पाथेयाद्युपस्कारा, D. vi.;<BR>(4) वीवधः (= supplies<BR>for any army), Si. ii. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proviso
PROVISO: अपवादः (= exception), Ku. ii. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provocation
PROVOCATION:<BR>(1) प्रकोपनम्;<BR>(2) क्रोधोद्दीपनम्;<BR>(3) उत्तेजनम्, ना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provocative
PROVOCATIVE:<BR>(1) उद्दीपक (f. पिका);<BR>(2)<BR>उद्दीपन (f. नी);<BR>(3) उत्तेजक (f. जिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provoke
PROVOKE:<BR>I To irritate, make angry:<BR>(1)<BR>प्र-कोपयति (c. of कुप्);<BR>(2) कोपं<BR>or<BR>क्रोधं जनयति<BR>(जन्, c. 10.)<BR>or<BR>उद्दीपयति (c. of दीप्).<BR>II To<BR>excite: q. v.:<BR>(1) उद्दीपयति;<BR>(2) उत्तेजयति<BR>(c. of तिज्).<BR>III To challenge: आह्वयते<BR>(ह्वे, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provoking
PROVOKING (adj.):<BR>(1) क्रोधोद्दीपक (f. पिका);<BR>(2) प्रकोपन (f. नी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provokingly
PROVOKINGLY: expr. by adj. or pres. part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provost
PROVOST: perh. नायकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prow
PROW:<BR>(1) नावोऽग्रभागः;<BR>(2) पोताग्रम्;<BR>(3) sim.<BR>अग्रम (when clear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prowess
PROWESS: वीर्यम्: v. Valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prowl
PROWL: भ्रमति<BR>or<BR>भ्राम्यति, परि-, (भ्रम्, c. 1.<BR>and 4.),<BR>p. ing about:<BR>इतस्ततः परिभ्रमन्,<BR>P. i. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prowler
PROWLER: expr. by verb.: v. Also plunderer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proximate
PROXIMATE: सन्निकृष्ट (f. ष्टा): v. Near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proximately
PROXIMATELY:<BR>(1) सन्निकर्षेण;<BR>(2) by adj. or<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proximity
PROXIMITY:<BR>(1) सन्निकर्षः;<BR>(2) सन्निधिः<BR>or<BR>-धानम्;<BR>(3) नैकट्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

proxy
PROXY:<BR>I A substitute: प्रतिनिधिः,<BR>I have been<BR>sent as his p.:<BR>स्वप्रतिनिधिः प्रेषितोऽस्मि, B. v. I.;<BR>(2) प्रतिहस्तः, -कः,<BR>and in procreating children,<BR>there are no p. ies:<BR>पुत्रस्योत्पादने चैव न सन्ति<BR> प्रतिहस्तकाः, H. ii. 33.<BR>II His agency: expr. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">Page555</a>]<BR>with above words.<BR>III An authority to<BR>vote: प्रतिहस्तपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prude
PRUDE:<BR>(1) अतिविनीत (f. ता ?);<BR>(2) मौखिक-<BR>शालीन: (f. ना: in bad sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prudence
PRUDENCE: विवेकः, Ki. ii. 30.: v. Also wis-<BR>-dom, circumspection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prudent
PRUDENT:<BR>(1) विवेकिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) विभृश्य-<BR>कारिन् (f. णी): v. Circumspect;<BR>(3) प्राज्ञ<BR>(f. ज्ञा): v. Wise;<BR>(4) मतिमत् (f. ती = 3),<BR>Ki. ii. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prudential
PRUDENTIAL:<BR>I Lit.: विवेक- in comp. Ph.:<BR>from p. considerations:<BR>स्वार्थसमीक्षया।<BR>II<BR>Advisory: उपदेशक (f. शिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prudently
PRUDENTLY:<BR>(1) विविच्य;<BR>(2) प्रसमीक्ष्य;<BR>(3)<BR>विमृश्य।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prudery
PRUDERY:<BR>(1) अतिविनीतता (?);<BR>(2) मौखिक-<BR>शालीनता (in bad sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pruddish
PRUDDISH: v. Prude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prune
PRUNE (subs.): i. e. dried plum: *प्रोतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prune
PRUNE (v.): अग्राणि (= tops)<BR>or<BR>अनावश्यकविटपानि<BR>(= branches) लुनाति, अव-, (लु, c. 9.: with<BR>gen.): v. To cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pruner
PRUNER: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pruning-knife
PRUNING-KNIFE:<BR>(1) छुरिका (gen. term);<BR>(2)<BR>*विटपकर्तरिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prurience
PRURIENCE: कण्डूः, -तिः, -या, -यनम् (lit. and fig.),<BR>Si. i. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prurient
PRURIENT:<BR>I Lit.: कण्डूल (f. ला).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>अभिलाषुक (f. का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pry
PRY:<BR>(1) अनुसन्धत्ते (धा, c. 3. with acc.);<BR>(2)<BR>विचिनोति: v. To search.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prying
PRYING (adj.):<BR>(1) अनुसन्धित्सु (mfn.);<BR>(2)<BR>जिज्ञासु (mfn. = inquisitive).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

psalm
PSALM: स्तोत्रम्; (more correctly) पाश्चात्यवेदस्तोत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

psalmist
PSALMIST: *स्तोत्रकारः<BR>or<BR>-रचयितृ (m.)<BR>or<BR>-लेखकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

psalmody
PSALMODY:<BR>I The art: *स्तोत्रसङ्गीतम्।<BR>II<BR>Psalms: स्तोत्राणि (n. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

psalter
PSALTER: स्तोत्रसंहिता; स्तोत्रसंग्रहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

psaltery
PSALTERY: तन्त्रीविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pseudo
PSEUDO: expr. by मिथ्या: v. False; कृत्रिम-:<BR>Counterfeit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pshaw
PSHAW:<BR>(1) धिक् (= fie);<BR>(2) अपेहि (= away);<BR>(3) आः (= what).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

psychic
PSYCHIC, -AL: expr. by comp., p. knowledge:<BR>मनोविज्ञानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

psychologic
PSYCHOLOGIC, -AL: आन्वीक्षिकीविषयकः (का, कं),<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

psychologist
PSYCHOLOGIST: आन्वीक्षिकीविशारदः (दा, दं);<BR>*मनोदर्शनज्ञः (ज्ञा, ज्ञं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

psychology
PSYCHOLOGY: आन्वीक्षिकी; *मनोदर्शनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ptarmigan
PTARMIGAN: वन्यपक्षिभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puberty
PUBERTY:<BR>(1) वयस् (n. = age),<BR>who has attained<BR>p.:<BR>प्राप्तवयस्क (f. स्का);<BR>(2) यौवनम् (= youth:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

public
PUBLIC (adj.):<BR>I Of the p.: expr. by comp.<BR>or gen.,<BR>for the p. good:<BR>प्रकृतिहिताय, Sa. vii.,<BR>लोकानुग्रहः, R. x. 31.; afraid of p. scandal:<BR>जननिर्वादभयात्, Ki. ii. 10.<BR>II Relating to the<BR>state:<BR>p. affairs:<BR>राजकार्याणि; at the p. expenses:<BR>राजव्ययेन (better राष्ट्रव्ययेन, though uncommon).<BR>III Not private or secret: प्रकाश (f. शा).<BR>keeping in p.:<BR>प्रकाशावस्थापनम्, D. iv.;<BR>p.<BR>woman:<BR>प्रकाशनारी, Mr. iii.<BR>IV Open to<BR>common uses: साधारण- in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

public
PUBLIC (subs.):<BR>(1) लोकाः (m. pl.);<BR>(2) जनाः<BR>(m. pl.);<BR>(3) प्रकृतयः (f. pl. = subjects);<BR>(4)<BR>प्रजाः (= 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

publichouse
PUBLICHOUSE:<BR>(1) शौण्डिकालयः;<BR>(2) शुण्डापानम्;<BR>(3) सुरापणः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

publican
PUBLICAN:<BR>I Tax-collector: q. v.<BR>II An<BR>inn-keeper: शौण्डिकः (f. की: spirit-selling<BR>caste in India).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

publication
PUBLICATION:<BR>I The act: प्रकाशनम्: v. To<BR>publish.<BR>II A book or pamphlet published:<BR>प्रकाशितग्रन्थः and sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

publicist
PUBLICIST: *साधारणविधिज्ञः; साधारणविधिपण्डितः;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

publicity
PUBLICITY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्रकाशता;<BR>(2) by<BR>verb.<BR>to bring into p.:<BR>प्रकाशीकरोति।<BR>II<BR>Renown: q. v.: ख्यातिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

publicly
PUBLICLY:<BR>(1) प्रकाशम्;<BR>(2) लोकसमक्षम् and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

public-spirited
PUBLIC-SPIRITED: perh. मनस्विन् (f. नी); लोका-<BR>नुरागिन् (f. णी) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

publish
PUBLISH:<BR>I To make public: प्रकाशीकरोति:<BR>v. To disclose, reveal.<BR>II Of books: perh. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">Page556</a>]<BR>प्रकाशीकरोति।<BR>III To put into circulation:<BR>प्रचारयति (c. of चर्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

publisher
PUBLISHER:<BR>(1) प्रकाशक (f. शिका);<BR>(2) प्रचारक<BR>(f. रिका): v. To publish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puckered
PUCKERED: संकुचित (f. ता): v. To wrinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pudding
PUDDING: no equiv.: मिष्टान्नम् may be used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puddle
PUDDLE:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) वर्तरूक (rare);<BR>(2)<BR>perh. पङ्किलजलम् and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Verb.:<BR>पङ्कीकरोति: v. Also to pollute, muddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puerile
PUERILE:<BR>(1) बालिश (f. शा);<BR>(2) बालेय (f.<BR>यी);<BR>(3) बालोचित (f. ता) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puerlity
PUERLITY:<BR>(1) बालिशता;<BR>(2) बालेयता (rare);<BR>(3) बालिशबुद्धिः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puerperal
PUERPERAL: सूतिका- in comp., p. diseases:<BR>सूतिकारोगाः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puff
PUFF (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: फुत्कारः।<BR>II Fig.: perh.<BR>ध्यानम्, आ-, अभि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puff
PUFF (v. t.):<BR>I In gen.: धमति; आ-, प्र-, उप-,<BR> अभि-, समा- (ध्मा, c. 1.).: v. To inflate,<BR>swell.<BR>II To drive away: अपनुदति (नुद्,<BR>c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puff
PUFF (v. i.):<BR>I To pant: विनिःश्वसिति (श्वस्,<BR>c. 2.).<BR>II To be inflated: expr. with<BR>आध्मात (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puffery
PUFFERY: perh. आध्मानम्; मिथ्यासंस्तवः (or sim.<BR>स्तुतिः, R. x. 33.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puffy
PUFFY: आध्मात (f. ता): v. Also bombastic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pug
PUG:<BR>I A dog: मर्कटास्यः कुक्कु रः।<BR>II A mon-<BR>-key: q. v.: मर्कटः।<BR>III Of the nose:<BR>p.<BR>nosed:<BR>चिपिट (f. टा), -क (f. का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pugilism
PUGILISM:<BR>(1) मुष्टियुद्धम्;<BR>(2) with adv. मुष्टी-<BR>मुष्टि;<BR>(3) मल्लयुद्धम् (gen. term.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puglist
PUGLIST: मुष्टियोध (f. धी)<BR>or<BR>-योद्धृ (f. द्ध्री) or<BR>योधिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pugilistic
PUGILISTIC: v. Pugilism, pugilist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pugnacious
PUGNACIOUS:<BR>(1) कलहप्रिय (f. या = quarrel-<BR>-some);<BR>(2) युयुत्सु (mfn. = disposed to fight).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pugnacity
PUGNACITY:<BR>(1) कलहप्रियता;<BR>(2) युयुत्सुता: for<BR>dif.: v. above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pussance
PUSSANCE:<BR>(1) पराक्रमः;<BR>(2) विक्रमः: v. Strength,<BR>power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puissant
PUISSANT:<BR>(1) पराक्रान्त (f. न्ता);<BR>(2) विक्रान्त<BR>(f. न्ता): v. Powerful, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pule
PULE:<BR>I Of birds: कूजति (कूज्, c. 1.).<BR>II<BR>To whine: रोदिति (रुद्, c, 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pull
PULL (v. t.): कर्षति, आ-, समा- परि-, (कृष्, c. 1.),<BR>(your)<BR>wife was p. ed by the hair:<BR>कृष्टा केशेषु<BR> भार्या, Ve. v.; p. s out a snake from the basket:<BR>भुजङ्गमाकायाः, V. t.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pull
PULL (v. i.):<BR>(1) कर्षति;<BR>(2) वाहयति (c. of वह्)<BR>or<BR>चोदयति (चुद्, c. 10.), Ram. ii. (in rowing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pull down
PULL DOWN: पातयति (c. of पत्), suddenly p.s.<BR>(him)<BR>down by the hair:<BR>केशेषु गृहीत्वा पातयति,<BR>Mr. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puff off
PUFF OFF:<BR>I Lit.: निष्कर्षयति।<BR>II To take<BR>off: q. v.: अपनयति (नी, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puff up
PUFF UP:<BR>I To eradicate, extirpate: q. v.:<BR>उत्पाटयति (पट्, c. 10.).<BR>II To draw the<BR>reins: स्थापयति (c. of स्था).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pulling
PULLING (subs.): कर्षः, -णम्, आ-, वि-, सं-, by p.:<BR>विकर्षणैः, Ki. iv. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pullet
PULLET:<BR>(1) क्षुद्रकुक्कुटी;<BR>(2) कुक्कुटशावः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pulley
PULLEY: *कर्षचक्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pullulate
PULLULATE: अङ्कुरयति (nomi.): v. Sprout,<BR>germinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pulmonary
PULMONARY, PULMONIC: फुष्फुस- in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pulp
PULP:<BR>(1) मज्जा;<BR>(2) सारः;<BR>(3) बीजम् (of seedy<BR>fruits), N. xxii. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pulpit
PULPIT: nearest equiv. पीठम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pulpous
PULPOUS, PULPY: perh. मज्जाबहुल (f. ला)<BR>or<BR>सार-<BR>भूयिष्ठ (f. ष्ठा)<BR>or<BR>बीजमय (f. यी): for dif.: v. Pulp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pulsate
PULSATE:<BR>(1) चेष्टते (चेष्ट्, c. 1. = to act);<BR>(2)<BR>चलति (चल्, c. 1.): v. Also to throb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pulsation
PULSATION:<BR>(1) नाडीचेष्टा (of the arteries),<BR>Bha.;<BR>(2) गतिः (= motion), very rapid p.:<BR>अतिद्रुता गतिः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pulse
PULSE:<BR>I Of blood-vessels: नाडिः (डी),<BR>exa-<BR>mination of p.:<BR>नाडीपरीक्षा, Bha.; (p.)<BR>is slow<BR>from phlegm:<BR>कफान्मन्दगतिर्ज्ञेया, Bha.<BR>II Osci-<BR>-llation, vibration: q. v.<BR>III Any legumin-<BR>-ous plant:<BR>(1) शमी- (शिम्बी) -धान्यम्;<BR>(2) शमी-<BR>(शिम्बी)-जः;<BR>(3) वैदलः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pulverization
PULVERIZATION:<BR>(1) चूर्णीकरणम्;<BR>(2) रेणूकरणम्;<BR>(3) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pulverize
PULVERIZE (v.): चूर्णीकरोति: v. To pound,<BR>grind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pulverulence
PULVERULENCE: रेणुत्वम्, R. xvi. 30.: v.<BR>Powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pulverulent
PULVERULENT: v. Powdery, dusty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puma
PUMA: शार्दूलविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pumice
PUMICE, -STONE: *बोमकम्, बोमकोपलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pummel
PUMMEL: v. Pommel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pump
PUMP (subs.):<BR>I A machine: बम्बवम्, -यन्त्रम्।<BR>II A shoe: पादुकाविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pump
PUMP (v. t.):<BR>I To raise: q. v.: उत्तोलयति<BR>(तुल्, c. 10.).<BR>II To draw out: निष्कर्षति<BR>(कृष्, c. 1.). To p. out: i. e. to drain,<BR>empty: रिक्तीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pump
PUMP (v. i.): *बम्बबेन जलमुत्तोलयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pumpkin
PUMPKIN: कुष्माण्डः (the plant. Use n. or -फलम्<BR>for the fruit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pun
PUN:<BR>I Subs.: no equiv.: श्लेषपरिहासः (?):<BR>v. Joke.<BR>II Verb.: श्लेषपरिहासं करोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punch
PUNCH (subs.):<BR>I The drink: perh. पञ्चकम्।<BR>II Of a puppet show: perh. पञ्चालः, -कः<BR>(comp. पञ्चालिका = doll).<BR>III A tool: *सं-<BR>वेधनी।<BR>IV A blow, stroke: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punch
PUNCH (v.):<BR>I To p. out.: *संवेधन्या भिनत्ति<BR>(भिद्, c. 7.).<BR>II To strike, poke: q. v.:<BR>प्रहरति (हृ, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punchy
PUNCHY: स्थूलकाय (f. या), खर्व (f. र्वा): v.<BR>Fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puncheon
PUNCHEON:<BR>I A punch: *संवेधनी।<BR>II A<BR>cask: कुण्डम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punctilio
PUNCTILIO: सूक्ष्मनियमः; सूक्ष्मविधिः, and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punctilious
PUNCTILIOUS: no proper equiv.:<BR>(1) सक्ष्म-<BR>नियमनिष्ठ (f. ष्ठा);<BR>(2) विधिव्रतिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3)<BR>आचारध्वज (f. जा); and sim. comp.s. may<BR>be used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punctiliously
PUNCTILIOUSLY: expr. by adj. आचारैकदृष्टिः<BR>(mfn.) etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punctiliousness
PUNCTILIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) नियमैकदृष्टिः (?);<BR>(2)<BR>विधिव्रतम् (?);<BR>(3) आचारनिष्ठा (?), and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punctual
PUNCTUAL:<BR>I Exact, precise: q. v.<BR>II About<BR>time:<BR>(1) perh. कालानुवर्तिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>with यथासमयम्,<BR>you are very p. today:<BR>अद्य यथा-<BR>समयमागतो भवान्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punctuality
PUNCTUALITY, PUNCTUALNESS:<BR>(1) कालानुवर्तिता<BR>(?);<BR>(2) with adv. यथासमयम्<BR>or<BR>यथाकालम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punctually
PUNCTUALLY:<BR>(1) यथासमयम्;<BR>(2) यथाकालम्;<BR>(3) नियमितकाले।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punctuate
PUNCTUATE: विरामचिह्नानि ददाति (दा, c. 3.: with<BR>gen.)<BR>or<BR>निवेशयति (c. of विश्, with gen (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punctuation
PUNCTUATION: *विरामचिह्ननिवेशः, -नम्;<BR>or<BR>-दानम्;<BR>or<BR>-अङ्कनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puncture
PUNCTURE (v.): विध्यति (व्यध्, c. 4.),<BR>p. d<BR>wound:<BR>विद्धम्, Sr.: v. To pierce, prick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puncture
PUNCTURE (subs.):<BR>(1) वेधः;<BR>(2) वेधनम् (of<BR>the act only).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pundit
PUNDIT: पण्डितः: v. Learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pungency
PUNGENCY:<BR>(1) तीव्रता;<BR>(2) तीक्ष्णता;<BR>(3) उग्रता;<BR>(4) प्राखर्यम्;<BR>(5) कटुता: for dif.: v. Below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pungent
PUNGENT:<BR>I Of pains etc.:<BR>(1) तीव्र (f. व्रा);<BR>(2) प्रखर (f. रा);<BR>(3) तीक्ष्ण (f. क्ष्णा);<BR>(4)<BR>उग्र (f. ग्रा).<BR>II To taste etc.<BR>(1) तीक्ष्ण (f.<BR>क्ष्णा),<BR>black mustard is p. and hot:<BR>राजिका<BR> तीक्ष्णोष्णा, Bha.;<BR>of p. smell:<BR>तीक्ष्णगन्ध (f.<BR>न्धा). Bha.;<BR>(2) तीव्र (f. व्रा).<BR>III Of lan-<BR>-guage:<BR>(1) कटु (f. also ट्वी);<BR>(2) मर्मविध्<BR>(mfn. = piercing the vital parts, very p.);<BR>(3) अरुन्तुद (f. दा = 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punish
PUNISH:<BR>(1) दण्डयति (दण्ड्, c. 10.): may take<BR>two acc. If an offence is the object, expr.<BR>with the offender,<BR>a king p. ing those who do<BR>not deserve p. ment:<BR>अदण्ड्यान् दण्डयन् राजा, M.;<BR>a washerman wearing another's clothes is to be<BR>p. ed with (a fine of)<BR>three paṇas:<BR>वसानस्त्रीन्<BR> पणान् दड्ण्यो रजकस्तु परांशुकम्, Y. ii. 241.; in go-<BR>ing to a woman of the same caste, (one)<BR>is to be<BR>p. ed with the highest p. meant:<BR>सवर्णागमने तूत्तम-<BR>साहसं दण्ड्यः, V. s.;<BR>(2) शास्ति (शास्, c. 2.:<BR>rare),<BR>he should be p. d like a thief:<BR>चौरवच्छास्यः,<BR>V. s.;<BR>(3) with दण्डः,<BR>p. ing according to the<BR>nature of the offence;<BR>यथापराधदण्ड (ण्डा), R. i.<BR>6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punishable
PUNISHABLE:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) दण्ड्य (f. ण्ड्या);<BR>(2) दण्डनीय (f. या);<BR>(3) शास्य (f. स्या).<BR>II<BR>Of men and offences: दण्डार्ह (f. र्हा) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punisher
PUNISHER:<BR>(1) दण्डयितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) दण्डप्रणेतृ [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">Page558</a>]<BR>(f. त्री);<BR>(3) शास्तृ (f. स्त्री)<BR>or<BR>शासितृ (f. त्री),<BR>Vi. iii. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punishment
PUNISHMENT:<BR>(1) दण्डः,<BR>wise men consider p. to<BR>be virtue:<BR>दण्डं धर्मं विदुर्बुधाः, M. vii. 18.;<BR>to in-<BR>flict p. on those who deserve it;<BR>दण्डं दण्ड्ये षु<BR> प्रणयति, 20.; or rarely पातयति, B. iv. 32.; to<BR>award p. (fine): दण्डं दापयति, V. s.;<BR>corporeal<BR>p.:<BR>शारीरो दण्डः, Mr. ix.;<BR>ignoble p.:<BR>निकारदण्डः,<BR>Mr. ix.;<BR>(2) दमः (rare: of fines), M. N. B.<BR>Legal writers use उत्तमसाहसम् (= highest p.),<BR>मध्यमसाहसम् (= intermediate p.), प्रथमसाहसम्<BR>(= first or lowest p.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punitive
PUNITIVE: expr. by comp. or circumlo.: v.<BR>Punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punster
PUNSTER: श्ले षपरिहासवादिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

punt
PUNT:<BR>(1) तरालुः;<BR>(2) तरान्धुः: v. Also boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puny
PUNY: क्षुद्र (f. द्रा): v. Small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pup
PUP (subs.): कुक्कु रशावः, -कः: v. Puppy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pup
PUP (v.): expr. with सूते, प्र-, (सू, c. 2.)<BR>जनयति (जन्, c. 10.)<BR>or<BR>उत्पादयति (c. of पद्) and<BR>शावम्, -कम्, etc. (= young).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pupil
PUPIL (subs.):<BR>I Of the eye:<BR>(1) तारका;<BR>(2) कनीनिका।<BR>II A scholar:<BR>(1) शिष्य (f.<BR>ष्या),<BR>should teach Brahmin p. s.:<BR>अध्यापयेद्-<BR>द्विजान् शिष्यान्, Pa.;<BR>your p. Mālavikā:<BR>शिष्या वो<BR> मालविका, Māl.;<BR>(2) छात्र (f. त्री),<BR>hostel for<BR>p. s:<BR>छात्रनिलयः, Va. com.;<BR>(3) अन्तेवासिन् (f.<BR>नी) (rare), Ma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pupilage
PUPILAGE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) शिष्यत्वम्;<BR>(2) शिष्यावस्था;<BR>(3) अन्तेवासित्वम्।<BR>II Boyhood: q. v.: शिशुत्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puppet
PUPPET:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पुत्तली (लिका);<BR>(2)<BR>पञ्चाली (लिका);<BR>(3) पुत्रिका;<BR>(4) शालभञ्जी<BR>(ञ्जिका: rare);<BR>II Fig.: क्रीडनकम् (= play-<BR>-thing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puppet-show
PUPPET-SHOW: *पञ्चालीदर्शनम्; पुत्तलिकाभिनयः;<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puppy
PUPPY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) कुक्कु रशावः, -कः;<BR>(2) कुक्कुर-<BR>शिशुः;<BR>(3) बालकुक्कुरः (f. री);<BR>(4) कुक्कुरडिम्भः।<BR>(f. म्भा);<BR>II Fig.: of men: perh. वानरः<BR>or<BR>मर्कटः (= monkey).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purchasable
PURCHASABLE:<BR>(1) क्रेय (f. या);<BR>(2) क्रेतव्य (f.<BR>व्या);<BR>(3) क्रय्य (f. य्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purchase
PURCHASE (v.): क्रीणाति<BR>or<BR>क्रीणीते (क्री, c. 9.),<BR>if<BR>a purchaser, after p. ing a commodity considers<BR>it to be a bad bargain:<BR>क्रीत्वा मूल्येन यत्पण्यं<BR> दुष्क्रीतं मन्यते क्रयी, N. s.;<BR>do you p. Pandits with<BR>thousands of fools:<BR>क्वचित् सहस्रैर्मूर्खाणामेकं क्रीणासि<BR> पण्डितम्, Mah. ii. 5. 84.: v. Also to buy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purchase
PURCHASE (subs.):<BR>I The act.: क्रयः (rarely<BR>परि-, सं-, उप-).<BR>II The thing bought: expr.<BR>with क्रीत (f. ता).<BR>III Power: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purchase-money
PURCHASE-MONEY:<BR>(1) क्रयमूल्यम्;<BR>(2) मूल्यम्:<BR>v. Price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purchaser
PURCHASER:<BR>(1) क्रेतृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) क्रयिन् (f.<BR>णी);<BR>(3) क्रयिक (f. का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pure
PURE:<BR>I Unmixed, unalloyed: शुद्ध (f. द्धा),<BR>वि-,<BR>with hilts of p. ivory:<BR>शुद्धदन्तत्सरु (mfn.),<BR>Mah. ii. 51. 16.;<BR>p. gold:<BR>शुद्धं सुवर्णम्, Bha.<BR>II Clear, clean: q. v.: शुद्ध (f. द्धा), वि-,<BR>but on the p. surface of a mirror:<BR>शुद्धे तु दर्पणतले,<BR>Sa. vii.<BR>III Spotless, chaste:<BR>(1) शुद्ध (f.<BR>द्धा), वि-,<BR>internally p.:<BR>अन्तःशुद्ध (f. द्धा), Me.;<BR>p. fame:<BR>विशुद्धयशस्, D.;<BR>(2) शुचि (mfn.),<BR>p.<BR>knowledge:<BR>शुचि श्रुतम्, Ki. ii. 32.<BR>IV Of<BR>language: शुद्ध (f. द्धा), वि-, Ki.<BR>V Mere:<BR>q. v.: शुद्ध (f. द्धा), from a p. desire for children:<BR>शुद्धसन्तानकामैः। R. xviii. 53. Ph.:<BR>to become<BR>p.:<BR>शुध्यति (शुध्, c. 4.);<BR>or<BR>पूयते (pass. पू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purely
PURELY: शुद्धम् or gen. शुद्ध- in comp.: v. Chas-<BR>-tely, surely, clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pureness
PURENESS: शुद्धता: v. Purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purgation
PURGATION:<BR>(1) शोधनम् (in every sense),<BR>to<BR>practise p.;<BR>शोधनं शीलयति, Bha.;<BR>(2) रेचनम्<BR>(in medical sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purgative
PURGATIVE:<BR>I Subs.: विरेचनम् (कम्), Bha.<BR>II<BR>Adj.:<BR>(1) शोधन (f. नी);<BR>(2) शोधक (f. धिका);<BR>(3) रेचन (f. नी), वि-,<BR>or<BR>रेचक (f. चिका), वि-<BR>(in medical sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purgatory
PURGATORY: यमलोकः: v. Also hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purge
PURGE (subs.):<BR>I The act.: शोधनम्।<BR>II A<BR>purgative: विरेचनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purge
PURGE:<BR>(1) शोधयति (c. of शुध्, in every sense),<BR>how to p. gold:<BR>स्वर्णस्य शोधनविधिः, Bha.: v.<BR>To purify, clear;<BR>(2) रेचयति, वि-, (c. of<BR>रिच्: in medical sense), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purging
PURGING (subs.): विरेचनम्, ना: v. Diarrhœa,<BR>dysentery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purification
PURIFICATION:<BR>(1) पावनम्, simply for my p.:<BR>मत्पावनायैव, Ku. vi. 61.;<BR>(2) शोधनम्, परि-,<BR> वि-, सं-, M. n.;<BR>(3) शुद्धिः, सं-, वि-, परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purification
PURIFICATION, PURIFICATORY: v. Purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purifier
PURIFIER:<BR>(1) पावक (f. विका: rare);<BR>(2)<BR>शोधक (f. धिका);<BR>(3) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purify
PURIFY: पुनाति, पुनीते<BR>or<BR>पावयति, परि-, वि-, (पू, c.<BR>9. and 10.),<BR>who p. ies sins all around:<BR>परितो<BR> दुरितानि यः पुनीते, Ki. xviii. 37.;<BR>men of holy<BR>fame are world-p. ing:<BR>लोकपावनाः खलु पुण्यश्लोकाः।<BR>M. n. on Ku. vi. 69.;<BR>wishing to p. field<BR>produce:<BR>बलजान् पुपूषता, Si. xiv. 7.;<BR>(2) शोधयति,<BR> वि-, परि-, सं-, (c. of शुध्): v. To clear;<BR>(3)<BR>पवित्रीकरोति<BR>or<BR>पवित्रयति (nomi.: in fig. sense<BR>only),<BR>why it will not p. my language:<BR>कथं न<BR> सा मद्गिरं॥॥पवित्रयिष्यति, N. i. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purifying
PURIFYING (adj.):<BR>(1) पावन (f. नी),<BR>entirely<BR>world-p.:<BR>जगदेकपावनी, Ki. iii. 32.;<BR>(2) पाविन्<BR>(f. नी), O Lord, (it is due)<BR>to p. obeisance to<BR>these;<BR>पाविन्यास्तव भव तन्नमस्क्रियायाः, Ki. xviii.<BR>36.;<BR>(3) शोधन (f. नी), वि-, परि-, सं-,<BR>M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purist
PURIST: perh. विशुद्धिप्रियलेखकः (comp. Ki.<BR>xiv. 5.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puritan
PURITAN: पौरातन (f. नी); पूतंमन्य (f. न्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puritanic
PURITANIC, -AL: expr. by comp. or gen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purity
PURITY:<BR>(1) शुद्धिः,<BR>p. of language:<BR>विशुद्धिमुक्तेः<BR>Ki. xiv. 5.: v. Also clearness;<BR>(2) पवित्रता<BR>(moral);<BR>(3) Often by adj., p. of life:<BR>विशुद्धजीवनम्: v. Pure, sacred;<BR>(4) निष्कलङ्कता।<BR>(= spotlessness): v. Also clear, sinless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purl
PURL (subs.):<BR>I A fringe: रजतच्छुरितपर्यन्तः or<BR>प्रान्तः (??).<BR>II A drink: no equiv.: मधु (n.)<BR>may be used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purl
PURL (v.): “p. ing stream”: perh घर्धररवा सरित्,<BR>Ma. v. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purloin
PURLOIN: मुष्णाति (मुष्, c. 9.): v. To steal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purloiner
PURLOINER: -मुष् (mfn.) in comp.: v. Thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purple
PURPLE (adj.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) नीललोहित (f. ता);<BR>(2) वार्ताकुसवर्ण (f. र्णा).<BR>II Fig., bloody:<BR>शोण (f. णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purple
PURPLE (subs.):<BR>(1) नीललोहितः;<BR>(2) वार्ताकुसवर्ण<BR>(comp. Beguni).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purple
PURPLE (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) नीललोहितीकरोति (?);<BR>(2) by adj.<BR>II Fig.: शोणीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purport
PURPORT (subs.):<BR>(1) अभिप्रायः: v. Inten-<BR>-tion;<BR>(2) भावार्थः।<BR>or<BR>भावः (of meaning),<BR>the<BR>p. is...:<BR>इति भावः, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purport
PURPORT (v.):<BR>(1) expr. by subs.;<BR>(2) सूचयति<BR>(सूच्, c. 10.): v. To indicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purpose
PURPOSE (subs.):<BR>(1) अभिप्रायः: v. Intention;<BR>(2) आशयः: v. Design.<BR>(3) अर्थः: v. Object;<BR>(4) चिकीर्षा<BR>or<BR>चिकीर्षितम् (= aim);<BR>(5) आकूतम्<BR>(rare),<BR>who thus declared his p.:<BR>इतीरिताकूतम्,<BR>Ki. xiv. 26. Ph.: (a) on p.: v. Purposely;<BR>(b)<BR>for what p.:<BR>किमर्थम्: v. Why; (c)<BR>to<BR>no p.:<BR>निरर्थकम्: v. Vain, in; (d)<BR>for this,<BR>that p.:<BR>एतदर्थम्, तदर्थम्: v. For (II, III);<BR>(6)<BR>to the p.: (of arguments, words, etc.) उपपन्नम्<BR>(= appositely)<BR>or<BR>सम्यक् (= well).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purpose
PURPOSE (v.): अभिप्रैति (इ, c. 3.): v. To<BR>intend, resolve, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purposeless
PURPOSELESS:<BR>(1) निरर्थक (f. का);<BR>(2) with<BR>वृथा: v. Vain, in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purposely
PURPOSELY:<BR>(1) कामतः: v. Intentionally;<BR>(2) with subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purse
PURSE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: धनभस्त्रिका (D. ii. has<BR>रत्नभस्त्रिका)<BR>II A treasury: q. v.: कोषः।<BR>III<BR>Prize-money: perh. जयधनम्।<BR>IV Money:<BR>q. v.: धनम्,<BR>having long p.:<BR>प्रभूतधनशालिन्<BR>(f. नी). Ph.:<BR>sword and p.:<BR>दण्डकोषौ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purse
PURSE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: भस्त्रिकायां निदधाति (धा, c. 3.).<BR>II To contract: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purse-proud
PURSE-PROUD: धनगर्वित (f. ता) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purser
PURSER: पोतस्य कोषाधिकृतः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pursuance
PURSUANCE:<BR>(1) अनुसरणम्;<BR>(2) अनुवर्तनम्; or<BR>अनुवृत्तिः। Ph.: in p. of:<BR>(1) अनुसारेण: v.<BR>According to;<BR>(2) by prest. part. अनुसरत्<BR>(f. न्ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pursuant
PURSUANT: अनुसारिन् (f. णी), p. to: v. In<BR>pursuance of, according to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pursue
PURSUE:<BR>I To follow (in various senses):<BR>q. v.: अनुसरति (सृ, c. 1.).<BR>II To chase: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">Page560</a>]<BR>(1) अनुसरति (rare), p. d the running (couple)<BR>to<BR>a great distance:<BR>तत् पलायमानं सुदूरमनुससार, K.;<BR>(2) अनुधावति (धाव्, c. 1.), p. d by Rāvaṇa:<BR>रावणेनानुधावितः, M. n.;<BR>(3) अनुद्रवति (द्रु, c. 1.),<BR>p. d by whom in war:<BR>अनुद्रुतः संयति येन, Si. i. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pursuer
PURSUER:<BR>(1) अनुसारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) अनुधावक<BR>(f. विका): v. Also follower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pursuit
PURSUIT:<BR>I Chasing:<BR>(1) अनुसरणम्;<BR>(2) अनु-<BR>धावनम्;<BR>(3) अनुद्रवः (rare).<BR>II Following:<BR>(1) अनुसरणम्;<BR>(2) अनुधावनम्;<BR>(3) अनुवर्तनम् or<BR>अनुवृतिः।<BR>III Occupation, employment:<BR>q.v.: व्यापारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pursuivant
PURSUIVANT: अनुचरः: v. Also herald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pursy
PURSY:<BR>I Punchy: q. v.<BR>II Short-breathed:<BR>दुःश्वासिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purulence
PURULENCE, PURULENCY:<BR>(1) पूयत्वम्;<BR>(2)<BR>सपूयत्वम्, -ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purulent
PURULENT:<BR>(1) पूयस्राविन् (f. णी = running with<BR>pus.);<BR>(2) सपूय (f. या) and sim. comp.s.<BR>(= with pus.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purvey
PURVEY:<BR>I To provide: q. v.:<BR>II To procure,<BR>get: q. v.<BR>III To procure food: खाद्यद्रव्याणि<BR> आहरति। (हृ, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purveyance
PURVEYANCE:<BR>I Provision: उपकल्पनम्।<BR>II<BR>Of food: आहारसमाहारः and sim. comp.s.<BR>III<BR>Provisions, food: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

purveyor
PURVEYOR: perh. महाभोगिकः; आहाराधिकृतः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pus
PUS: पूय (mn.),<BR>bloody p.:<BR>पूयशोणितम्,<BR>p. that has<BR>not come out:<BR>अविनिःसृतः पूयः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

push
PUSH (v.):<BR>I To butt, thrust: q. v.: शृङ्गेण<BR> आविध्यति (व्यध्, c. 4.).<BR>II To p. aside:<BR>(1) अपसारयति (c. of सृ): v. To drive<BR>away;<BR>(2) आविध्यति,<BR>successfully p. es it from<BR>here:<BR>तदितो निर्बन्ध्यमाविध्यति, Vi. v. 39.<BR>III<BR>To p. forward:<BR>(1) प्रणोदयति (c. of नुद्): v.<BR>To drive, impel;<BR>(2) चालयति, सं-, (c. of<BR>चल्): v. To move.<BR>IV To press: q. v.:<BR>पीडयति (पीड्, c. 10.).<BR>V To burst out: उद्भिनत्ति<BR>(भिद्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

push on
PUSH ON:<BR>I Intrans., to hasten, proceed:<BR>q. v.: त्वरते (त्वर्, c. 1.).<BR>II Trans., to urge,<BR>hasten: q. v.: प्रणोदयति (c. of नुद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

push
PUSH (subs.):<BR>I A thrust: q. v.: आवेधः।<BR>II<BR>Any pressure or force applied: आधातः,<BR> अभिघातः,<BR>or<BR>समाधातः।<BR>III P. ing aside:<BR>अपसारणम्।<BR>IV Vigorous effort: अभियोगः।<BR>V. Extremity, emergency: सङ्कटम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pushing
PUSHING (adj.):<BR>I Enterprising, active:<BR>q. v.: उद्योगिन् (f. नी).<BR>II Bold, forward^1:<BR>q. v.: प्रगल्भ (f. ल्भा).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pusillanimity
PUSILLANIMITY: क्षुद्रमनस्कता: v. Cowardice,<BR>timidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pusillanimous
PUSILLANIMOUS:<BR>I Of men: क्षुद्रमनस् (mfn.):<BR>v. Cowardly, mean.<BR>II Of conduct etc.:<BR>(1) कृपण (f. णा);<BR>(2) जघन्य (f. न्या).: v.<BR>Base, low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pusillanimously
PUSILLANIMOUSLY:<BR>(1) क्षुद्रमनस्कतया;<BR>(2) भीरुवत्;<BR>(3) कार्पण्येन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puss
PUSS, PUSSY: विडालः: v. Cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pustule
PUSTULE:<BR>(1) स्फोटः, -कः;<BR>(2) रक्तजो व्रणः or<BR>sim. व्रणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put
PUT:<BR>I To place:<BR>(1) स्थापयति (= to place),<BR>p. it in the treasure box:<BR>कोषपेटके स्थापयैनम्, V.;<BR>(2) नि- दधाति<BR>or<BR>धत्ते (धा, c. 3 (gen. on<BR>something low), p. ting your feet on (my)<BR>lap:<BR>अङ्के ते चरणौ निधाय, Sa.;<BR>(3) आरोपयति<BR>(c. of रुह्) (on something high),<BR>p. on board<BR>the arc:<BR>तस्यामारोपयेर्नावि, Mah.;<BR>(4) अर्पयति,<BR> सम्-, (c. of ऋ) (= to give),<BR>p. s the noose on<BR>the necks:<BR>कण्ठे पाशमर्पयति, Na.;<BR>(5) ददाति<BR>(दा, c. 3. = 4.), presses and p. s on (her) heart:<BR>निष्पीड्य हृदये ददाति Na. ii.;<BR>(6) करोति (in<BR>some phrases), p. ting (his) feet on our necks:<BR>कृत्वा पदं नो गले, Mu. iii. 26.;<BR>(7) निवेशयति,<BR> सं-, (c. of विश् to lay),<BR>if I p. it in its<BR>proper place:<BR>यददीमहमेव यथास्थानं निवेशयामि, Sa.<BR>iii.;<BR>(8) न्यस्यति, वि-, (अस्, c. 4 = 7.),<BR>shall<BR>p. on the ground:<BR>भूमौ विन्यसेत्, M. iii. 226.<BR>II<BR>To cause to be:<BR>to p. to death:<BR>व्यापादयति<BR>(c. of पद्): v. Death, to p. to;<BR>to p. to<BR>flight:<BR>द्रावयति, वि-, (c. of द्रु),<BR>p. darkness to<BR>f.:<BR>तमोऽदिद्रवत्, Si. vi. 43.;<BR>p. in mind:<BR>मनसि<BR> कारयति, (c. of कृ): v. To remind:<BR>p. in<BR>order:<BR>यथायथं विन्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.): v. To<BR>arrange, properly;<BR>p. in writing:<BR>पत्रे निवेशयति<BR>(c. of विश्): v. To enter;<BR>p. in fear:<BR>भयम् [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=561" target="_blank">Page561</a>]<BR>आवेशयति (with loc.): v. To frighten;<BR>p. in<BR>jeopardy:<BR>संशयं नयति (नी, c. i)<BR>or<BR>संशयस्थं (f. स्थां)<BR>करोति,<BR>III In various senses: p. a question:<BR>प्रश्नं करोति;<BR>p. into Sanskrit:<BR>संस्कृतवाचा करोति;<BR>the argument is well pl.:<BR>सम्यगुदाहृतोपपत्तिः।<BR>III<BR>To incite, urge: q. v.: प्रवर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put away
PUT AWAY:<BR>I Lit.: रक्षति (रक्ष्, c. 1. = to<BR>keep: q. v.).<BR>II To renounce, drive away:<BR>q. v.: निरस्यति (अस्, c. 4.).<BR>III To divorce:<BR>त्यजति, परि-, (त्यज्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put back
PUT BACK:<BR>I To delay: व्याक्षिपति (क्षिप्<BR>c. 6.).<BR>II Torestore to original place:<BR>p. it. b.:<BR>तत्र पुनरपि स्थापय: v. Put (II)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put by
PUT BY:<BR>I To put away: रक्ष्ति।<BR>II To lay<BR>aside: आक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.).<BR>III To<BR>refuse: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put down
PUT DOWN:<BR>I To lay down:<BR>(1) अवतारयति<BR>(c. of तॄ);<BR>(2) भूमौ etc. (= on the ground)<BR>निदधाति etc.: v. Put (I).<BR>II. To degrade:<BR>q. v.: अवनमयति (c. of नम्).<BR>III To suppress,<BR>extinguish: q. v.: पातयति, अव-, (c. of पत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put forth
PUT FORTH:<BR>I To stretch: q. v.: प्रसारयति<BR>(c. of सृ).<BR>II To send out:<BR>(1) आविष्करोति,<BR>Sa. iv. 5.;<BR>(2) निष्ठीवति (ष्ठीव् c. 1. = to spit<BR>out), Sa. iv. 5.<BR>III To exert: q. v.<BR>IV<BR>To utter, propose: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put forward
PUT FORWARD:<BR>I To allege: उदाहरति (हृ,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II To promote, advance: q. v.:<BR>वर्धयति (c. of वृध्).<BR>III To aid: q. v.: अनु-<BR>कुलयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put in
PUT IN:<BR>I To introduce: निवेशयति, सं-, (c. of<BR>विश्).<BR>II To conduct, as ships: नयति<BR>(नी, c. 1.)<BR>III In law: perh. प्रदर्शयति<BR>(c. of दृश्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put off
PUT OFF:<BR>I To postpone: व्याक्षिपति (क्षिप्,<BR>c. 6.).<BR>II To take off, discard: q. v.:<BR>उन्मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.).<BR>III To deceive,<BR>delude: q. v.: प्रतारयति (c. of तॄ).<BR>IV Of<BR>boats: मुञ्चति,<BR>the boat is p. o.:<BR>मुक्ता नौः<BR>D. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put on
PUT ON:<BR>I To wear:<BR>(1) वस्ते (वस्, c. 2.),<BR>for ascetics p. on simply skin and bark:<BR>तपस्विनो<BR> हिवसते केवलाजिनवल्कले, Ki. xi. 15.;<BR>(2) परि-<BR>दधाति or (धा, c. 3.);<BR>(3) धारयति (धृ,<BR>c. 10.);<BR>(4) गृह्णाति, परि-, (ग्रह्, c. 9.);<BR>(5)<BR>आमुञ्चति, (मुच्, c. 6.),<BR>why have you p. on this<BR>armour:<BR>कवचं किमामुक्तमिदं त्वया, Ki. xi. 15.:<BR>v. Also clad in.<BR>II To assume: q. v.:<BR>धारयति।<BR>III To impute to: संक्रामयति (c. of<BR>क्रम् with loc.).<BR>IV To impose: आसञ्जयति<BR>(c. of सञ्ज् with loc.). P. on the crown of i. e.<BR>to conclude, finish: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put out
PUT OUT:<BR>I As the tongue: बहिष्करोति।<BR>II<BR>To stretch: q. v.: प्रसारयति (c. of सृ).<BR>III<BR>To dislocate: q. v.<BR>IV To turn out:<BR>q. v.: बहिष्करोति।<BR>V As the eyes:<BR>(1) उद्धरति,<BR> सम्-, (हृ, c. 1.), D.;<BR>(2) उत्पाटयति (पट्, c.<BR>10.).<BR>VI To extinguish: q. v.:<BR>(1) निर्वापयति<BR>(c. of वा);<BR>(2) शमयति, प्र-, नि-, (c. of शम्),<BR>p. ting o. lights:<BR>निशाम्य दीपान्, Si. iii. 45.:<BR>VII To publish: q. v.: प्रकाशयति।<BR>VIII<BR>To provoke, displease: q. v.: क्षोभयति (c. of<BR>क्षुभ्).<BR>IX At interest: perh.: निदधाति or<BR>ध (धा, c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put over
PUT OVER:<BR>I To place in authority: अधि-<BR>स्थापयति (c. of स्था): v. To command.<BR>II<BR>To send: q. v.: प्रेषयति।<BR>III To postpone:<BR>व्याक्षिपति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put to
PUT TO:<BR>I To add: q. v.<BR>II To expose:<BR>q. v.<BR>P. hand to:<BR>हस्तं क्षिपति।<BR>P. to sea:<BR>नावं<BR>etc. मुक्त्वा समुद्रं गच्छति। P. to trial: v. To<BR>try.<BR>P. to the sword:<BR>शिरः छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7.):<BR>v. To slay, behead.<BR>To p. to it:<BR>पीडयति:<BR>v. To distress. To p. to a stand: v. To<BR>stop. See also put (II)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put together
PUT TOGETHER: संयोजयति (युज्, c. 10.): v.<BR>To unite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put up
PUT UP:<BR>I To lodge: q. v.: वसति (वस्, c.<BR>1.: when intrans.)<BR>or<BR>वासं ददाति (दा, c. 3:<BR>when trans.).<BR>II Gen. with to bear:<BR>q. v.: सहते (सह्, c. 1.).<BR>III To expose,<BR>offer: q. v.: दर्शयति (c. of दृश्).<BR>IV To<BR>bring up, as correspondence: समानयति (नी,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>V To hoard, store: q. v.<BR>VI<BR>With to, to incite: q. v.: प्रणोदयति (नुद्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put upon
PUT UPON: v. To put on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

putatijve
PUTATIJVE: लोकभावित (f. ता) and sim. comp.s.:<BR>v. Reputed, false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

put-off
PUT-OFF (subs.): व्यपदेशः: v. Pretence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

putrefaction
PUTREFACTION:<BR>(1) पूतिः,<BR>that there may not be<BR>p.:<BR>मा भूत् पूतिरिति, B. iii. 23. com.;<BR>(2)<BR>पूतत्वम्, -ता;<BR>(3) दुर्गन्धता, and sim. comp.s.<BR>(= bad smell).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

putrefy
PUTREFY:<BR>I Intrans.: पूतीभवति।<BR>II Trans.:<BR>पूतीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

putrescence
PUTRESCENCE:<BR>I v. Putrescent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

putrescent
PUTRESCENT:<BR>I Becomming putrid: पूतीभवत्<BR>(f. न्ती).<BR>II Pertaining to putrefaction:<BR>by comp.,<BR>p. smell:<BR>पूतिगन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

putrid
PUTRID:<BR>(1) पूत (f. ता);<BR>(2) गलित (f. ता =<BR>decomposed).;<BR>(3) दुर्गन्ध (f. न्धा= bad<BR>smelling).<BR>P. smell:<BR>पूतिगन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

putridity
PUTRIDITY, PUTRIDNESS:<BR>(1) पूतिः;<BR>(2) पूतत्वम्,<BR> -ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

putty
PUTTY: काचबन्धनलेपः, Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puzzle
PUZZLE (subs.):<BR>I An enigma:<BR>(1) कूटम्;<BR>(2) गूढम्;<BR>(3) प्रदेलिका (= riddle).<BR>II Per-<BR>-plexity: q. v.: चित्तसम्भ्रमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puzzle
PUZZLE (v. t.): व्यामोहयति (c. of मुह): v. To<BR>perplex, embarrass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

puzzling
PUZZLING (adj.):<BR>I Of things: व्यामोहक (f.<BR>हिका): v. Perplexing.<BR>II Of men: मूढ<BR>(f. ढा): v. Fool, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pygmy
PYGMY (subs.): वामन (f. नी): v. Dwarf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pygmy
PYGMY, PYGMEAN (adj.): वामन (f. नी): v.<BR>Dwarfish, small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pyramid
PYRAMID: no equiv.: *परामितिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pyramidal
PYRAMIDAL, PYRAMIDICAL: परामितिनिभ (f. भा)<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pyre
PYRE: चिता: v. File.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pyrites
PYRITES: स्वर्णमाक्षिकम्, Wilson. Hepatic p.:<BR>रूप्यमाक्षिक्रम्, W.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pyrotechnic
PYROTECHNIC, -AL: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pyrotechnics or -ny
PYROTECHNICS or -NY: अग्निक्रीडाकला and sim.<BR>comp.s.: v. Fireworks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pyrrhic
PYRRHIC: in prosody: लौ (dual).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

pyrrhonist
PYRRHONIST: नास्तिकः: v. Sceptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

python
PYTHON: अहिविशेषः; अजगरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quack
QUACK (subs.):<BR>I Medical:<BR>(1) कुवैद्यः, Sr.<BR>i. 5. ch.;<BR>(2) मिथ्याचिकित्सकः; and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II A mountebank: perh.:<BR>(1) मिथ्याभिमानिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) दाम्भिकः: v.<BR>Impostor.<BR>III Of ducks: प्रणादः: v. Noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quack
QUACK (v.):<BR>I To act as a q.: expr. by<BR>subs.<BR>II To brag, boast: q. v.: मिथ्याभिमानं<BR> करोति।<BR>III As. a duck: प्रणदति (नद्, c. 1.):<BR>v. Noise, to make; cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quackery
QUACKERY:<BR>(1) दुश्चिकित्सा and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(2) मिथ्याभिमानः: v. Imposture, boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quackish
QUACKISH:<BR>(1) मिथ्याभिमानिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) दाम्भिक<BR>(f. की).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quadragesima
QUADRAGESIMA: चत्वारिंशद्दिनोपवासः and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quadrangle
QUADRANGLE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) चतुरस्रम्;<BR>(2)<BR>चतुर्भुजः।<BR>II Of a house: चत्वरम् (= court).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quadrangular
QUADRANGULAR:<BR>(1) चतुरस्र (f. स्रा);<BR>(2)<BR>चतुष्कोण (f. णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quadrant
QUADRANT:<BR>I A quarter: q. v.: पादः।<BR>II<BR>Of a circle:<BR>(1) वृत्तपादः;<BR>(2) पदम् (rare),<BR>Su. ii. 30.<BR>III An instrument: वृत्तपाद-<BR>यन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quadrate
QUADRATE: v. Square (subs. and verb.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quadratic
QUADRATIC: v. Square.<BR>Q. equation:<BR>वर्ग-<BR>समीकरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quadrature
QUADRATURE: in astro.: (पा)पदसंस्थानम् (after<BR>पद of Su. ii. 30).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quadrennial
QUADRENNIAL:<BR>(1) चतुर्वार्षिक (f. की);<BR>(2)<BR>चातुरब्दिक (f. की); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quadrilateral
QUADRILATERAL:<BR>(1) चतुर्भुज (f. जा);<BR>(2)<BR>चतुरस्र (f. स्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quadrille
QUADRILLE:<BR>I A game at cards: *चात्वारिंशम्।<BR>II A dance: *चतुरस्रनृत्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quadripartite
QUADRIPARTITE: चतुर्भागविभक्त (f. क्ता) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quadrisyllable
QUADRISYLLABLE: चतुरक्षरम्<BR>or<BR>चतुरक्षरः शब्दः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quadrivium
QUADRIVIUM:<BR>I Of roads: चतुष्पथम्।<BR>II Of<BR>arts: चतुर्विद्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quadrumanous
QUADRUMANOUS:<BR>(1) चतुष्पाणि (mfn.);<BR>(2)<BR>चतुर्भुजः (जा, जं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quadruple
QUADRUPLE:<BR>I Adj.: चतुर्गुणः (णा, णं).<BR>II<BR>Verb: चतुर्गुणं (f. णां) करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quadruplicate
QUADRUPLICATE: चतुर्गुणीकरोति; चतुर्गुणं (f. णां)<BR>करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quaff
QUAFF: उत्-चुलुम्पति (चुलुम्प्, c. 1.), Vi. v. 32.:<BR>v. To drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quaffer
QUAFFER: अतिपायिन् (f. नी): v. Drinker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quagga
QUAGGA: *चित्रगर्दभः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quagmire
QUAGMIRE: अनुपभूः, -भूमिः: v. Fen, marsh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quail
QUAIL (subs.):<BR>(1) वर्तकः (perdix olivacea);<BR>(2) लवः (p. chinensis).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quail
QUAIL (v.):<BR>I Intrans: विषीदति (सद्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To give way, tremble.<BR>II Trans: v.<BR>To quell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quaint
QUAINT:<BR>I Odd, unusual: q. v.: अपरूप (f.<BR>पा).<BR>II Cunning, subtle: q. v.: विदग्ध (f.<BR>ग्धा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quaintly
QUAINTLY: expr. by comp. or adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quaintness
QUAINTNESS: अपरूपता: v. Also strangeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quake
QUAKE (v.): कम्पते, प्र-, वि-, उत्-, (कम्प्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To tremble, shudder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quake
QUAKE (subs.): कम्पः, -नम्, प्र-, उत्-; earth-q.:<BR>अवनिप्रकम्पनम्, Ku. xv. 23.: v. Also tremor,<BR>shudder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quaker
QUAKER: of the sect.: *बान्धवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quaking
QUAKING (adj.):<BR>(1) कम्पमान (f. ना), प्र-, उत्-;<BR>(2) वेपमान (f. ना),<BR>Q. -grass:<BR>कम्पना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

qualification
QUALIFICATION:<BR>I The state of being quali-<BR>-fied: expr. by adj.: v. Qualified.<BR>II<BR>Endowment, excellency: q. v.: गुणः<BR>III<BR>Condition, restriction: q. v.: नियमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

qualified
QUALIFIED (adj.):<BR>I Fit: q. v.:<BR>(1) योग्य (f.<BR>ग्या);<BR>(2) समर्थ (f. र्थ): v. Able;<BR>(3) गुणो-<BR>पेत (f. ता) and sim. comp.s. (= endowed<BR>with qualifications), first of all should wish<BR>(try)<BR>to be himself q.:<BR>आत्मानमेवस् प्रथमच्छेगुण-<BR>समन्वितम्, Ka. iv. 3.<BR>II Competent: q. v.:<BR>(1) योग्य (f. ग्या);<BR>(2) not expr.<BR>III Li-<BR>-mited, restricted. expr. with subs. नियमः etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

qualify
QUALIFY:<BR>I To make qualified: योग्यं (f.<BR>ग्यां) etc. करोति,: v. Fit. able, q.ied.<BR>II To<BR>modulate, vary: q. v.<BR>III To restrict.,<BR>restrain: q. v.: नियच्छति (यम्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quality
QUALITY:<BR>I Property:<BR>(1) गुणः, the three q. ies.:<BR>त्रिगुणम्, Ch.; not for specifying (your good)<BR>q.ies.:<BR>न गुणानामियत्तया, R. x. 32.;<BR>attached on<BR>account of good q.ies:<BR>गुणानुरक्त (f. त्ता), Ki. i.<BR>31.;<BR>(2) धर्मः (not of good or bad q. ies.),<BR>in pleasures whose q. is evanescent:<BR>विषयेषु<BR> विनाशधर्मसु, R. viii. 10.;<BR>for the absence of<BR>personal q.ies.:<BR>पुरुषधर्मत्वाभावात् S. p. b. 1. 52.<BR>II Rank, station: q. v.<BR>III People of<BR>rank;<BR>(1) कुलीनाः (m. pl.);<BR>(2) कौलिन्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

qualm
QUALM (subs.):<BR>I Of conscience: मनस्तापः<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Nausea:<BR>(1) वमनेच्छा;<BR>(2) विवमिषा (rare.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

qualmish
QUALMISH:<BR>(1) वमनभाव (f. वा ?);<BR>(2) विवमिषु<BR>(mfn.: ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quandary
QUANDARY: संशयः v. Doubt, difficulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quantitative
QUANTITATIVE: परिमाणसूचक (f. चिका) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quantity
QUANTITY:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) परिमाणम्;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रमाणम्। Ph.:<BR>what q.:<BR>कियत् (f. ती): v.<BR>Much, how.;<BR>a great q. of:<BR>प्रभूत (f. ता):<BR>v. Abundant;<BR>a little q. of:<BR>अल्प (f. ल्पा):<BR>v. Little;<BR>that q. which:<BR>यावत् (f. ती): v.<BR>Much, as-;<BR>in large q.ies:<BR>बहुशः; in small q.<BR>अल्पशः।<BR>II In prosody: not expr., long q.:<BR>दीर्घः;<BR>short q.:<BR>ह्रस्वः।<BR>III In logic: अधिकारः<BR>(??).<BR>IV In Math.:<BR>unknown q.:<BR>अव्यक्त-<BR>राशिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarantine
QUARANTINE: गमनागमन-<BR>or<BR>संसर्ग- प्रतिषेधः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarrel
QUARREL (subs.):<BR>(1) कलहः,<BR>affected q.:<BR>कृत-<BR>ककलहः, Mu. iii.;<BR>in (our) q.:<BR>कलहे, Vi. ii.<BR>34.;<BR>(2) विवादः: v. Dispute.;<BR>(3) कलिः<BR>(rare.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarrel
QUARREL (v.):<BR>(1) कलहं करोति;<BR>(2) कलहायते<BR>(nomi.), C. i.;<BR>(3) विवादं करोति: v. Also to<BR>dispute, abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarreller
QUARRELLER: कलहकारिन् (f. णी): v. Also<BR>quarrelsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarrelsome
QUARRELSOME:<BR>(1) कलहप्रिय (f. या):<BR>the people<BR>of Gauḍa are q.:<BR>कलहप्रियाः गौडाः, Mit.;<BR>(2)<BR>विवादप्रवण (f. णा) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarrelsomeness
QUARRELSOMENESS:<BR>(1) कलहप्रियता;<BR>(2) विवाद-<BR>परता and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarry
QUARRY (subs.):<BR>I For stone:<BR>(1) आकरः:<BR>v. Mine;<BR>(2) पाषाणस्थली and sim. comp.s.<BR>(?).<BR>II Of hawks: perh. मार्गितो जङ्गालः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarry
QUARRY (v.):<BR>I To dig.: q. v.: उत्खनति<BR>(खन्, c. 1.).<BR>II To prey: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarryman
QUARRYMAN: *उपलाकरिन् (f. णी); पाषाणो-<BR>त्खनक (f. निका); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quart
QUART:<BR>I A measure: no exact equiv.:<BR>कुडवः, Williams.<BR>II = Quarter: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quartan
QUARTAN i. e. q. ague:<BR>(1) चतुर्थकः, Ni.;<BR>(2)<BR>चातुर्थको ज्वरः, Ni.; त्र्याहिकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarter
QUARTER (subs.):<BR>I Fourth part:<BR>(1) पादः,<BR>three q.s:<BR>पादत्रयम्, Li.;<BR>with a third, a half and<BR>a q. of a quantity:<BR>राशित्र्यंशसार्धपादैः, Li.;<BR>(2)<BR>गुरीयः<BR>or<BR>तुर्यः (rare),<BR>with a q. of which:<BR>यस्य<BR> तुर्येण, Li. 23.;<BR>(3) चतुर्थांशः;<BR>(4) चतुर्थभागः।<BR>II<BR>Of the heaven:<BR>(1) दिश् (f.: best equiv.),<BR>north-east q. (lit. of Śiva): ऐशानी दिक्, V.<BR>from various q.s.:<BR>नानादिग्देशात्, H.;<BR>in every<BR>q.:<BR>प्रतिदिशम्, Ki. xiv. 64.; intermediate q.:<BR>विदिश् (rare);<BR>(2) आशा (f.), the eastern q. (lit.<BR>of Indra): वासवाशा, Si. xi. 16.;<BR>(3) काष्ठा,<BR>the<BR>northern q.:<BR>उदिची काष्ठा, Ki. iii. 55.;<BR>(4) ककुभ्<BR>(f.),<BR>the q.s.:<BR>ककुभाञ्चक्रवालः, Si. xx. 14.;<BR>(5)<BR>हरित् (f.).<BR>III A region: q. v.: देशः।<BR>IV<BR>In pl., abode, residence:<BR>(1) निवासः,<BR>the<BR>lord's q. s. shone in tents:<BR>प्रमोर्निवासाः पटवेश्मभि-<BR>र्बभुः, Si. xii. 63.;<BR>(2) निवेशः (of an army),<BR>the q.s. of an army:<BR>सेनानिवेशाः, M.n.;<BR>(3)<BR>स्थानम् (= place: q. v.). Ph.: Head-q. s.: perh.<BR>प्रधानस्थलम् and sim. comp.s.<BR>V Indulgence<BR>to an adversary: to give q.: perh. दयां दर्शयति;<BR>and shall give q. to (lit. not strike) those who<BR>do not fight or are eunuchs, or have no weapons,<BR>or are cowards or run away, or ask for q. (lit.<BR>say “we are yours”): नायुध्यमानं हन्याच्च न<BR> क्लीवं न निरायुधम् । न भीतं न परावृत्तं न तवास्बीति<BR> वादिनम् ॥, M. vii. 91-3.<BR>VI Of the year:<BR>(1) त्रिमासम्;<BR>(2) मासत्रयम्।<BR>VII Of the<BR>moon's period: expr. by शुक्ल- and कृष्णस्पक्षः<BR>(light, dark fortnight),<BR>VIII Of an ani-<BR>-mal: no equiv.: पादः may be used. Ph.:<BR>at close q. s.:<BR>मिथः प्रत्यासन्न (f. न्ना), M. n.;<BR>came to close q.s.:<BR>बाहूबाहवि व्यासृजेताम् (lit.<BR>engaged arm to arm), Si. xviii. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarter
QUARTER (v.):<BR>I To divide into four parts:<BR>(1) पादीकरोति;<BR>(2) चतुर्धा विभजति (भज्, c. 1.).<BR>II To divide q. v.: विभजति।<BR>III To<BR>lodge: q. v.: वासयति (c. of वस्: rare; वासं<BR> ददाति (दा, c. 3.).<BR>To be q. ed:<BR>वसति, (वस्, c.<BR>1.).<BR>VI To bear, as arms: बिभर्ति (भृ, c.<BR>3.): v. To bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarter-day
QUARTER-DAY: perh. त्रिमासान्तदिनम्; त्रैमासिक-<BR>दिवसः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarter-deck
QUARTER-DECK: no equiv.: उन्नतपृष्ठाम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarter-master
QUARTER-MASTER: *साधननायकः and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarter-sessions
QUARTER-SESSIONS: त्रैमासिकशासनम्: v. Sess-<BR>-ions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarter-staff
QUARTER-STAFF: यष्टिविशेषः; महायष्टिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarterage
QUARTERAGE: त्रैमासिकवृत्तिः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarterly
QUARTERLY:<BR>I Adj.: त्रैमासिक (f. की).<BR>II<BR>Adv.:<BR>(1) त्रिमासे त्रिमासे;<BR>(2) प्रतित्रिमासम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quartern
QUARTERN: मानविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quarto
QUARTO: *पादिक (f. की); पादभङ्गि (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quartz
QUARTZ: *कार्तजः; कार्तजोपलः, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quash
QUASH (v.):<BR>I To crush, beat down: q. v.:<BR>मृद्गाति (मृद्, c. 9.).<BR>II In law, to annul:<BR>perh. उच्छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quasi
QUASI: expr. with aff. s. कल्प (f. ल्पा), देश्य or<BR>देशीय (f. या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quaternary
QUATERNARY: perh. चातुर (f. री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quaternion
QUATERNION:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) चतुष्टयम्;<BR>(2) चतु-<BR>ष्कम्।<BR>II A syllable: चतुरक्षरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quatrain
QUATRAIN: perh. चतुष्पदम् (f. दी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quaver
QUAVER (v.):<BR>I To tremble: q. v.: वेपते<BR>(वेप्, c. 1.).<BR>II To sing: स्वरभङ्गेन गायति<BR>(गै, c. 1.), Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quaver
QUAVER (subs.):<BR>I Of voice: स्वरभङ्गः (?).<BR>II.<BR>A musical note: चिह्वविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quavering
QUAVERING (adj.):<BR>with q. voice:<BR>गद्गदवाचा or<BR>गलदक्षरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quay
QUAY: घट्टः (?), उत्तरणस्थानम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quean
QUEAN: बन्धकी: v. Also woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

queasy
QUEASY:<BR>I Qualmish: q. v.<BR>II Fig.: क्षोभक<BR>(f. मिका,) सं-, प्र-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

queen
QUEEN:<BR>(1) राज्ञी,<BR>the q. governed the kingdom<BR>according to the prescribed rules:<BR>राज्ञी रज्यं<BR> विधिवदशिषत्, R. xix. 57.;<BR>(2) महिषी (= a q.<BR>consort),<BR>he had three q.s:<BR>तिस्रो महिष्यस्तस्या-<BR>भवन्, Ram.;<BR>(3) राजपत्नी and sim. comp.s.<BR>(= wife of a king);<BR>(4) राजमातृ (f.) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (= queen-mother: often = queen<BR>dowager);<BR>(5) देवी (in addressing), Q. bee:<BR>मधुकरराजः। D. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

queenly
QUEENLY: राज्ञुचितः (ता, तं) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

queer
QUEER:<BR>(1) अपरूप (f. पा);<BR>(2) विलक्षण (f. णा ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

queerness
QUEERNESS:<BR>(1) अपरुपता;<BR>(2) विलक्षणता or<BR>वैलक्षण्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quell
QUELL:<BR>I To quiet, allay: q. v.: शमयति, प्र-,<BR>(c. of शम्).<BR>II To subdue, crush: q. v.:<BR>दमयति (c. of दम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

queller
QUELLER:<BR>(1) शमयितृ (f. त्री = quieter);<BR>(2)<BR>दमयितृ (f. त्री): v. Tamer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quencdh
QUENCDH:<BR>I To put out, extinguish: q. v.:<BR>निर्वापयति (c. of वा).<BR>II Of thirst:<BR>(1)<BR>शमयति, प्र-, (c. of शम् = to allay),<BR>thirst is q.<BR>ed with water:<BR>पिपासुता शान्तिमुपैति वारिणा, N.<BR>(2) निवर्तयति (c. of वृत् = to destroy);<BR>(3)<BR>निरस्यति (अस्, c. 4. = to drive away);<BR>(4)<BR>अपनयति (नी, c. 1.) = to remove).<BR>III To<BR>destroy, crush: q. v.: उत्-छिनत्ति (छिद्, c.<BR>7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quenchable
QUENCHABLE:<BR>(1) निर्वापणीय (f. या);<BR>(2) शम-<BR>नीय (f. या)<BR>or<BR>शाम्य (f. म्या), प्र-;<BR>(3) उच्छेद-<BR>नीय (f. या)<BR>or<BR>उच्छेत्य (f. द्या); etc.: for<BR>dif.: v. Above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quencher
QUENCHER:<BR>(1) निर्वापयितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) शमयितृ<BR>(f. त्री);<BR>(3) उच्छेदक (f. दिका): v. To<BR>quench.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quenchless
QUENCHLESS:<BR>(1) अशाम्य (f. म्या);<BR>(2)<BR>अनिर्वाप्य (f. प्या); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

querist
QUERIST: प्रष्ट्ट (f. ष्ट्री): v. Also interrogator,<BR>questioner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

querulous
QUERULOUS: perh. परिदेविन् (f. नी)<BR>or<BR>परिदेवक<BR>(f. विका): v. Also discontented, dissatis-<BR>-fied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

querulously
QUERULOUSLY:<BR>(1) परिदेवयत् (f. न्ती);<BR>(2)<BR>विरक्त (f. क्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

querulousness
QUERULOUSNESS:<BR>(1) परिदेविता (?);<BR>(2) विरक्तता;<BR>(3) अप्रसन्नता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

query
QUERY (subs.): प्रश्नः: v. Question.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

query
QUERY (v.): पृच्छति (प्रच्छ्, c. 6.): v. To<BR>question.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quest
QUEST:<BR>I Search: q. v.: अन्वेषणम्, -णा। In q.<BR>of: often expr. by prest. part: v. To<BR>search.<BR>II Inquest: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

question
QUESTION (subs.):<BR>I An interrogatory:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रश्नः (best equiv.), unless you explain (my) q.s.:<BR>न चेत् प्रश्नन् व्याकरोषि, Mah. iii. 313. 22.;<BR>to<BR>reply q. s.:<BR>प्रश्नान् वक्ति, 30, ब्रवीति, D. vi., etc.;<BR>(2) पृच्छा, सं-, परि-;<BR>(3) अनुयोग, परि-,<BR>II<BR>Doubt: q. v.: सन्देहः,<BR>without q., out of the q.,<BR>past q.:<BR>असंशयम्: v. Undoubtedly,<BR>III<BR>Debate, dispute: expr. by प्रष्टव्य (f. व्या),<BR>here the q. is:<BR>अत्रेदं प्रष्टव्यम्। (अत्र॥॥ इति सन्दि-<BR>ह्यते = doubted), S. i. 3. 1., To put to q.:<BR>पृच्छतिः: v. To ask.<BR>IV Examination, inves-<BR>-tigation: q. v.: परीक्षा:<BR>V Torture: q. v.<BR>VI Theme of enquiry: विवादविषयः, विवाद-<BR>पदम्, and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

question
QUESTION (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पृच्छति (प्रच्छ्, c.<BR>6.): v. To ask;<BR>(2) जिज्ञासते (desi. of ज्ञा<BR>= enquire: q. v.);<BR>(3) प्ररनं करोति (= ask a<BR>q.).<BR>II To doubt: q. v.: शङ्कते (शङ्क्, c. 1.).<BR>III Not to believe: q. v.: न प्रत्येति (इ, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

questionable
QUESTIONABLE: सन्दिग्ध (f. ग्धा): v. Doubt-<BR>-ful, uncertain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

questioner
QUESTIONER:<BR>(1) प्राशिनकः;<BR>(2) प्रशनकर्तृ (m.);<BR>(3) जिज्ञासकः (= inquirer).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

questionless
QUESTIONLESS: असंशयम्: v. Undoubtedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quibble
QUIBBLE (subs.):<BR>(1) वाक्छलम्;<BR>(2) वक्रोक्तिः;<BR>(3) अपलापः (= denial).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quibble
QUIBBLE (v.): वाक्छलं etc. करोति: v. Subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quibbler
QUIBBLER:<BR>(1) वाक्छलिन् (f. नीः ?);<BR>(2) वक्रोक्ति-<BR>वादिन् (f. नीः ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quibbling
QUIBBLING (adj.): वक्र (f. क्रा = crooked: (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quick
QUICK (adj.):<BR>I Alive: q. v.: सजीव (f. वा).<BR>Ph.:<BR>q. with child:<BR>आपन्नसत्त्वा: v. Pregnant.<BR>II Lively, vivacious: q. v.: प्रफुल्ल (f. ल्ला).<BR>III Sharp: q. v.: तीक्ष्ण (f. क्ष्णा).<BR>IV Agile:<BR>q. v.: चटुल (f. ला). V. Speedy, swift:<BR>(1) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">Page566</a>]<BR>शीघ्र (f. घ्रा),<BR>q. in motion:<BR>शीघ्रग (f. गा);<BR>q.<BR>in action:<BR>शीघ्रकर्मन् (mfn.);<BR>(2) द्रुत (f. ता),<BR>with a q. pace:<BR>द्रुतपदम्, Ki. x. 2.;<BR>(3) क्षिप्र<BR>(f. प्रा);<BR>(4) तूर्ण (f. र्णा);<BR>(5) त्वरित (f. ता<BR>= hasty). Ph.:<BR>to be q.:<BR>त्वरते (त्वर्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To hasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quick
QUICK (v.): Quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quick
QUICK (subs.): मर्मन् (n.), piercing to the q.:<BR>मर्मभेदिन् (f. नी), मर्माविध् (mfn.), मर्मस्पृश् (mfn.)<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quicken
QUICKEN (v. i.):<BR>I To vivify: q. v.: जीवयति<BR>(c. of जीव्).<BR>II To sharpen, incite: q. v.:<BR>उत्तेजयति (तिज्, c. 10.).<BR>III To hasten:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) त्वरयति (c. of त्वर्);<BR>(2) by adj.<BR>: v. quick (V).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quicken
QUICKEN (v. i.):<BR>I To receive life: जीवत्वं<BR> प्राप्नोति (आप्, c. 5.): v. To get.<BR>II To<BR>become lively, agile: q. v., the heart q. s. first:<BR>प्रथममुल्लसति हृदयम्।<BR>III To gain speed, move<BR>quicker: expr. by adv.: v. Quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quickening
QUICKENING (adj.): Of life:<BR>(1) जीवद (f.<BR>दा);<BR>(2) प्राणप्रद (f. दा), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quickening
QUICKENING (subs.): Of the fetus: perh.<BR>गर्भसञ्चारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quicklime
QUICKLIME: perh.: चूर्णम्<BR>or<BR>चूर्णजलम् (comp.<BR>vern.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quickly
QUICKLY:<BR>(1) शीघ्रम्;<BR>(2) क्षिप्रम्;<BR>(3) द्रुतम्;<BR>(4) तूर्णम्;<BR>(5) आशु;<BR>(6) त्वरितम्;<BR>(7) सत्वरम्:<BR>v. Also soon, instantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quickness
QUICKNESS:<BR>I Liveliness, acuteness, sagacity:<BR>q. v.<BR>II Speediness:<BR>(1) शीघ्रता, -त्वम्; or<BR>शैघ्य्रम्;<BR>(2) क्षिप्रता, -त्वम्;<BR>(3) द्रुतता, -त्वम्<BR>(rare);<BR>(4) त्वरा (= haste);<BR>(5) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quicksand
QUICKSAND:<BR>(1) चलबालुका (?);<BR>(2) असंस्थितसि-<BR>कताः (m. pl. ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quick-scented
QUICK-SCENTED:<BR>(1) तीक्ष्णघ्राण (f. णा ?);<BR>(2)<BR>सूक्ष्मगन्धग्राहिन् (f. णी ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quick-sighted
QUICK-SIGHTED: तीक्ष्णदृश् (mfn.): v. Keen-<BR>-sighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quicksilver
QUICKSILVER:<BR>(1) पारदः (rarely -तः);<BR>(2) रसः<BR>(rare), D. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quick-witted
QUICK-WITTED:<BR>(1) सूक्ष्मबुद्धि (mfn.);<BR>(2) तीक्ष्णधी<BR>(n. धि); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quiddity
QUIDDITY:<BR>I Lit.: विशेषः।<BR>II A question:<BR>वैशेषिकपृच्छा (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quiescence
QUIESCENCE: शान्तिः: v. Quiet, rest, repose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quiescent
QUIESCENT: शान्त (f. न्ता): v. Quiet, calm,<BR>still.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quiet
QUIET (adj.): शान्त (f. न्ता), प्र-,<BR>q. like the<BR>mind of sages:<BR>शान्तं चित्तमृषेरिव, Ki. xi. 40.;<BR>with the birds silent and the animals q.:<BR>मूकाण्डजं<BR> शान्तमृगप्रचारम्, Ku. iii. 42.; be q. at once:<BR>सद्यः शान्तो भव, Vi. iii. 34.: v. Calm, gentle,<BR>still. To keep. q. i. e.<BR>not to give out:<BR>न प्रका-<BR>शयति (with acc.)<BR>or<BR>जिह्वां रक्षति (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quiet
QUIET (subs.):<BR>(1) शान्तिः, प्र-;<BR>(2) Often by<BR>adj.: v. Also calmness, rest, silence,<BR>peace. Ph.: in q. v. Quietly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quiet
QUIET (v.): शमयति, प्र-, उप-, सं-, परि-, (c. of<BR>शम्),<BR>you q. disputes:<BR>प्रशमयसि विवादम्, Sa. v.<BR>7.;<BR>with a show of q. ed rage:<BR>प्रशान्तसंरम्भ इव,<BR>Ki. xiv. 2.;<BR>(2) शा(सा)न्त्वयति, परि-, उप-,<BR> अभि-, (शान्त्व्<BR>or<BR>सान्त्व्, c. 10.),<BR>q. ing with<BR>sweet words:<BR>सान्त्वयन् मधुरैर्वाक्यैः, Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quietism
QUIETISM: शान्तिः,<BR>eager for q.:<BR>शान्तिमार्गोत्सुक<BR>(f. का), R. vii. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quietly
QUIETLY:<BR>I Peaceably, calmly: expr. by<BR>adj.<BR>II Silently: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quietness
QUIETNESS: शान्तता, प्र-,: v. Quiet, calmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quietude
QUIETUDE: शान्तिः: v. Quiet, rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quill
QUILL:<BR>I Feather: q. v.: पक्षः।<BR>II For<BR>writing: पक्षकलमः (comp. vern.); लेखनी (in<BR>fig. senses).<BR>III Of a porcupine:<BR>(1) शल<BR>(mn.);<BR>(2) शललम् (ली).<BR>IV Of a lute:<BR>(1)<BR>रणः;<BR>(2) कोणः;<BR>(3) शारिका;<BR>(4) परि(री)वादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quilt
QUILT (subs.): तूला-<BR>or<BR>तूलिका-प्रच्छदः and sim.<BR>comp.s. (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quilt
QUILT (v.): to stitch in wool, silk, cotton<BR>etc.: expr. by those words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quinary
QUINARY:<BR>(1) पञ्चक (f. का);<BR>(2) पञ्चगर्भ (f.<BR>र्भाः ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quince
QUINCE: वृक्षविशेषः; तस्य फलञ्च।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quinquennial
QUINQUENNIAL:<BR>(1) पञ्चवार्षिक (f. की);<BR>(2)<BR>पाञ्चाब्दिक (f. की);<BR>(3) पञ्चसमीन (f. नी ?);<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quinsy
QUINSY: perh. श्लेष्मजा रोहिणी, Bha. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quintessence
QUINTESSENCE: सारः: v. Essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quintuple
QUINTUPLE:<BR>I Adj.: पञ्चगुण (f. णा).<BR>II<BR>Verb.: पञ्चगुणीभवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quip
QUIP: अधिक्षेपः: v. Taunt, sarcasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quire
QUIRE:<BR>I Choir q. v.:<BR>II Of paper:<BR>*चतुर्विंशतिकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quirister
QUIRISTER: v. Chorister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quirk
QUIRK:<BR>I Quibble: वाक्छलम्।<BR>II Quip:<BR>अधिक्षेपः।<BR>III Trick, deceit.: q. v.: छलम्।<BR>IV<BR>Fancy: मनोलौल्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quit
QUIT (v.):<BR>I To leave, abandon:<BR>(1) त्यजति,<BR> परि-, (त्यज्, c. 1.),<BR>to q. life:<BR>प्राणान् त्यजति,<BR>Mu. i. 24.; q. ted the outskirts of Vraja:<BR>तत्याज व्रजभूभागम्: V.p. v. 18. 32.;<BR>(2) जहाति,<BR> वि-, (हा, c. 3.), q. your fighting ardour:<BR>विजहीहि रणोत्साहम्, Ki. xi. 31;<BR>(3) उत्-सृजति,<BR> वि-, (सृज्, c. 1.),<BR>to q. life:<BR>जीवितमुत्सृजति, K.<BR>II. To discharge, repay: q. v.: शोधयति,<BR> परि-, (c. of शुध्).<BR>III To absorb, release:<BR>q. v.: मोचयति (c. of मुच्: with abl. of the<BR>thing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quit
QUIT (adj): मुक्त (f. क्ता), वि-, निर्-, (= released),<BR>q. of debts:<BR>ऋणनिर्मुक्त (f. क्ता): v. Also clear,<BR>free. Ph.:<BR>we are now q. s.:<BR>समाः स्मः साम्प्रतं<BR> वयम्;<BR>to cry q.s.:<BR>समोऽस्मीति वदति (वद्, c. 1: ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quite
QUITE (adv.):<BR>I Completely, entirely: q. v.:<BR>(1) अशेषेण;<BR>(2) निरवशेषम्।<BR>II Very consider-<BR>-ably: q. v.:<BR>(1) अति- in comp. (streng-<BR>-thened form अतीव);<BR>(2) अत्यन्तम्;<BR>(3)<BR>सातिशयम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quit-rent
QUIT-RENT: *शोधकरः; नामकरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quittance
QUITTANCE:<BR>(1) निष्कृतिः;<BR>(2) मुक्तिः;<BR>(3) मोक्षः;<BR>(4) शुद्धिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quiver
QUIVER (subs.):<BR>(1) तूणः;<BR>(2) तूणीरः;<BR>(3)<BR>इषुधिः;<BR>(4) निषङ्गः, at the mouth of the q.:<BR>निषङ्गवक्त्रे, Ki. xvii. 36.;<BR>and two great inexhaus-<BR>tible q. s.:<BR>अक्षय्ये च महेषुधी, Mah. i. 223. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quiver
QUIVER (v.): वेपते (वेप्, c. 1.): v. To quake,<BR>tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quivered
QUIVERED:<BR>(1) तूणीरवत् (f. ती);<BR>(2) निषङ्गिन्<BR>(f. नी):<BR>(3) धृतेषुधि (mfn.), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quivering
QUIVERING (adj.);<BR>(1) वेपमान (f. ना);<BR>(2)<BR>स्फुरित (f. ता), (of gentle motion: as of the<BR>lips), स्फुरितोत्तराधरः, Ku. v. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quivive
QUIVIVE: को भवान् (?).<BR>To be on the q.:<BR>सावधान<BR>(f. ना) वर्तते; अप्रमत्त (f. त्ता) तिष्ठति, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quoit
QUOIT: चक्रम्। Q. s (the game): *चक्रक्रीडा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quondam
QUONDAM: पूर्व (f. र्वा): v. Former.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quorum
QUORUM: perh. निर्दिष्टसंख्या<BR>or<BR>-संख्यकजनाः and<BR>sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quota
QUOTA: अंशः (= share: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quotation
QUOTATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) उद्धारः;<BR>(2)<BR>उपन्यासः;<BR>(3) अवतारणम् (rare).<BR>II What is<BR>q. ed: expr. with part. adj.: उद्धृत (f. ता),<BR>उपन्यस्त (f. स्ता), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quote
QUOTE (v.):<BR>(1) उद्धरति<BR>or<BR>उदाहरति (हृ, c. 1.);<BR>(2) उपन्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.);<BR>(3) अवतारयति<BR>(तॄ, c. 10. = to being down),<BR>Yāska having<BR>q.d Vedic passages:<BR>यास्केन वेदवाक्यानामवतारित-<BR>त्वात्, Say.;<BR>(4) उद्ग्राहयति (c. of ग्रह्),<BR>what is<BR>q.d before you:<BR>यत्तवोद्ग्राह्यते पुरः Si. ii. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quoth
QUOTH: आह; उवाच: v. To say.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quotidian
QUOTIDIAN: दैनन्दिनः (नी, नं): v. Every day.<BR>Q. fever:<BR>अन्येद्युष्को ज्वरः, Ni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

quotient
QUOTIENT:<BR>(1) फलम्,<BR>dividing by their respective<BR>divisors (we get) the same q.:<BR>स्वस्वहारेण हृते फलं<BR> तदेव, Li.;<BR>(2) गुण्यः, dividing we get the q.:<BR>भजनेन लब्धो गुण्यः, Vij.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rabbet
RABBET: सन्धिकाष्ठम् (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rabbi
RABBI: स्वामिन् (m.): v. Master, lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rabbinic
RABBINIC, -AL: इयुदीयपण्डितानां (gen.)<BR>or<BR>-पण्डित-<BR>-in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rabbit
RABBIT: शशकः (prop. hare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rabble
RABBLE:<BR>(1) प्राकृताः (m. pl.);<BR>(2) पृथग्जनाः<BR>(m. pl.);<BR>(3) नीचाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rabid
RABID: उन्मत्त (f. त्ता): v. Mad. R. dog:<BR>अलर्कः;<BR>r. poison:<BR>आलर्कं विषम्, U. i. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rabidly
RABIDLY: उन्मत्तवत्: v. Madly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

race
RACE (subs.):<BR>I Lineage:<BR>(1) अन्वयः,<BR>this king<BR>is born of that r.:<BR>तस्यान्वये भूपतिरेष जातः, R.<BR>vi. 41.;<BR>(2) कुलम्: v. Family;<BR>(3) वंशः: v.<BR>Dynasty.<BR>II Nation, tribe: q. v.: जातिः (?). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">Page568</a>]<BR>III March, progress: q. v.: यात्रा।<BR>IV<BR>A contest in running:<BR>chariot -r.:<BR>रथचर्या<BR>(?), Mah. i. 132. 28.;<BR>horse -r.:<BR>अश्वधावनम्<BR>(?);<BR>to win a r.:<BR>अश्वधावने etc. जयं लभते (लभ्,<BR>c. 1.). V. A root: मूलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

race
RACE (v.):<BR>I Intrans: धावति (धाव्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To run.<BR>II Trans.<BR>(1) धावयति (c. of<BR>धाव्);<BR>(2) गमयति (c. of गम्), Si. v. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

race-course
RACE-COURSE:<BR>(1) रङ्गभूमिः (gen. term);<BR>(2)<BR>perh. वीथिः, Si. v. 60.;<BR>(3) चर्याभूमिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

race-horse
RACE-HORSE: no equiv.:<BR>(1) जवनवाजिन् (m.);<BR>(2) जवाश्वः and sim. comp.s. may be used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

racer
RACER:<BR>I Race-horse: q. v.<BR>II A person:<BR>expr. by circumlo.: v. To race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

raciness
RACINESS: सरसता: v. Racy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rack
RACK (subs.):<BR>I For torture: no equiv.:<BR>*सम्पीडनी<BR>or<BR>सम्पीडनयन्त्रम्। To put to r.: i. e. to<BR>torment: q. v.<BR>II Extreme pain: q. v.:<BR>यातना।<BR>R. and ruin:<BR>उच्छेदः: v. Annihilation;<BR>go to r.:<BR>विनश्यति: v. To perish.<BR>III A<BR>framework:<BR>clothes -r.:<BR>*वस्त्रधारणी etc.<BR>IV<BR>Vapour or thin broken clouds: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rack
RACK (v.):<BR>I To torment, torture: q. v.<BR>II To strain: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

racket
RACKET:<BR>(1) The bat: गुलिकाताडनी<BR>or<BR>-ग्राहिणी,<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Clamour, din: q. v.:<BR>(1) कोलाहलः;<BR>(2) कलकलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

racy
RACY:<BR>(1) सरस (f. सा);<BR>(2) रसवत् (f. ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

radiance
RADIANCE:<BR>(1) प्रभा;<BR>(2) दीप्तिः: v. Brilliancy,<BR>lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

radiant
RADIANT:<BR>(1) समुज्ज्वल (f. ला);<BR>(2) दीप्तिमत्<BR>(f. ती): v. Brilliant, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

radiate
RADIATE:<BR>(1) निर्गच्छति (गम्, c. 1. = to come<BR>out: q. v.);<BR>(2) उदेति (इ, c. 2. = to arise:<BR>q. v.),<BR>light r.d from the head of Śiva:<BR>शम्भुमूर्ध्न<BR> उदियाय तेजः, Ki. xvi. 31.;<BR>(3) स्फुरति (स्फुर्,<BR>c. 1. = to sparkle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

radiation
RADIATION: in physics: perh. स्फुरणम्<BR>or<BR>स्फुरितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

radical
RADICAL:<BR>I Primitive, original: q. v.: मूल-<BR>in comp.,<BR>r. word:<BR>मूलशब्दः<BR>or<BR>धातुः (= verbal<BR>root).<BR>II Fundamental, real: q. v.: प्रकृत<BR>(f. ता).<BR>III In politics:<BR>the r. s:<BR>*मूलपावकाः<BR>(m. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

radically
RADICALLY:<BR>(1) आमूलम्;<BR>(2) समूलम्;<BR>(3) मूलतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

radish
RADISH: मूलकः (use n. for the root).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

radius
RADIUS:<BR>I In Geo.:<BR>(1) व्यासार्धम्, “व्यासार्धार्धं<BR> नयेत् केन्द्रात्”, A. b.;<BR>(2) विष्कम्भार्धम्, A. b.;<BR>(3) त्रिज्या (जीवा) (of the meridian), Su. ii.<BR>60.<BR>II A bone: बाहुनलकम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

raffle
RAFFLE (subs.): गुटिकापातादिना स्वत्वनिरूपणम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

raffle
RAFFLE (v.):<BR>to r. a horse:<BR>गुटिकापातेनाश्वाधिकारं<BR> निरूपयति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

raft
RAFT:<BR>(1) उडुप (mn.), R. i. 2.;<BR>(2) प्लवः;<BR>M. n.;<BR>(3) कोलः, A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rafter
RAFTER: तुला, “बृहत्तुलैर्गृहैः”, Si. iii. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rag
RAG:<BR>I A piece of cloth: वस्त्रखण्डम् and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Worn-out cloth: जीर्णवस्त्रम्;<BR>(2)<BR>चीरम्;<BR>(3) चीवरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ragamuffin
RAGAMUFFIN:<BR>(1) नीचजनः: v. Low;<BR>(2)<BR>धूर्तः: v. Rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rage
RAGE (subs.):<BR>I Violent anger:<BR>(1) रोषः<BR>(rarely रुष्, -षा),<BR>tears of r.:<BR>रुषाश्रु, Si. xv.<BR>4.: v. Anger;<BR>(2) संरम्भः,<BR>Sita's laugh<BR>excited her r.:<BR>संरम्भं मैथिलीहासो निनाय ताम्, R.<BR>xii. 36.;<BR>the excitement of r.:<BR>संरम्भवेगः, Ki.<BR>xvii. 49.<BR>II Vehemence, excitement:<BR>q. v.: प्रकोपः।<BR>III Violent passion:<BR>(1)<BR>व्यसनम्;<BR>(2) लालसा (= longing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rage
RAGE (v.):<BR>I To be angry: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>संरम्भम् आप्नोति (आप्, c. 5.), एति (इ, c. 2.),<BR>etc.<BR>II To be violently agitated: q. v.:<BR>अतितरां क्षुभ्यति (क्षुभ्, c. 4.), “r. ing Sea”:<BR>क्षुब्धार्णवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ragged
RAGGED:<BR>I Rent, torn:<BR>(1) जीर्ण (f. र्णा);<BR>(2) जर्जर (f. रा).<BR>II Rough, uneven:<BR>q. v. बन्धुर (f. रा).<BR>III Clad in rags:<BR>(1) चीरचीवरिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) कर्पटिन्<BR>or<BR>कर्पट-<BR>धारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ragout
RAGOUT: no equiv.: *मांसरसा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rail
RAIL (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: लोहतुला (of big. r. s.: ?)<BR>or<BR>-शलाका (in r. ing).<BR>II Fig., r. road:<BR>q. v.<BR>III A bird: पक्षिविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rail
RAIL (v.):<BR>I Lit.: लोहशलाकाभिः आवृणोति (वृ,<BR>c. 5.): v. To enclose.<BR>II To abuse,<BR>revile: q. v.: अधि-क्षिपति, अव-, (क्षिप्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

railing
RAILING (subs.):<BR>I A fence: q. v.: लोहवृतिः [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">Page569</a>]<BR>(of iron rails) or sim. वृतिः।<BR>III Abuse,<BR>reviling: q. v.: आक्षारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

railing
RAILING (adj.):<BR>(1) अवक्षेपक (f. पिका);<BR>(2)<BR>अधिक्षेपक (f. पिका);<BR>(3) आक्षारिन् (f. णी);<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

railroad
RAILROAD, RAILWAY: *लोहपथः and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

raiment
RAIMENT: वस्त्रम्: v. Clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rain
RAIN (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) वृष्टिः, excessive r.:<BR>अतिवृष्टिः, V.m.;<BR>let the r. cease:<BR>भवतु वृष्टेरुपशमः,<BR>H.;<BR>r. -water:<BR>वृष्टिजलम्, Bha. (also मेघोदकम्,<BR>Mr.);<BR>r. of gold:<BR>हिरण्मयी वृष्टिः, R.;<BR>(2)<BR>वर्षम्,<BR>let r. fall incessantly:<BR>वर्षमविरतं पततु, Mr.;<BR>heavy r. came on:<BR>महद्वर्ष प्रादुरासीत्, Mah.<BR>II<BR>In pl., the rainy season: q. v.: वर्षाः (f. pl.),<BR>one day in the r s:<BR>एकदा वर्षासु, H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rain
RAIN (v. i.):<BR>(1) वर्षति, प्र-, अभि-, (वृष्, c. 1.)<BR>(taking as nom. cloud, sky, or Indra),<BR>Indra<BR>did not r. for twelve years:<BR>न ववर्ष वर्षाणि द्वादश<BR> दशशताक्षः, D.; it (lit. the sky) r. ed heavily:<BR>नभस्तलं गाढं ववर्ष, Ku.; when it (lit. the<BR>cloud)<BR>was r. ing gently:<BR>मन्दं मन्दं प्रवर्षति पर्जन्ये,<BR>P.;<BR>(2) वृष्टिर्भवति, it r. ed heavily in torrents:<BR>धारासारैर्महती वृष्टिर्बभूव, H.<BR>R. off:<BR>निर्वर्षति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rain
RAIN (v. t.): वर्षति, प्र-, अभि-,<BR>to r. blood:<BR>शोणितं<BR> वर्षति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rainbow
RAINBOW: इन्द्रधनुस् (n.) and sim. comp.s.,<BR>r. -bearing clouds:<BR>सुरेन्द्रचापं दधतो वलाहकाः, Ri.<BR>ii. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rainfall
RAINFALL:<BR>(1) वृष्टिपातः, R.;<BR>(2) वर्षपातः, Mr.<BR>v.; and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rain-gage or -gauge
RAIN-GAGE or -GAUGE: *वृष्टिमापः, वर्षमापः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rainy
RAINY: वर्षुकः (का, कं),<BR>when the r. season was<BR>over:<BR>अतीते वर्षुके काले, B. R. season:<BR>(1) वर्षाकालः;<BR>(2) प्रावृष् (f.);<BR>(3) तपात्ययः, जलदागमः, and sim.<BR>comp.s (poet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

raise
RAISE (v.):<BR>I To r. up, lift up.:<BR>(1) उत्थापयति<BR>(c. of स्था),<BR>dust r.d by horses in war:<BR>उत्थापितः<BR> संयति रेणुरश्वैः, R. vii. 39.;<BR>(2) तोलयति<BR>or<BR>तोलति,<BR> उत्- (तुल्, c. 10. and I.: physically),<BR>when the<BR>Kailāsa was r. d:<BR>कैलासे तुलिते, Vi. v. 37.;<BR>(3) उन्नमयति (c. of नम्),<BR>to r. the face:<BR>मुख-<BR>मुन्नमयति Sa. iii. 33.;<BR>(4) उच्छ्रयति (श्रि, c.<BR>1.: rare),<BR>to r. banners:<BR>ध्वजमुच्छ्रयति, Mah.<BR>Ph.:<BR>r. ing frightful dust:<BR>उद्धुन्वाना रजो घोरम्,<BR>Ram.;<BR>dust r.d by chariots:<BR>रथोद्धतं रजः, R.<BR>iv. 85.<BR>II Fig., to exalt:<BR>(1) उत्थापयति (rare);<BR>(2) उन्नमयति,<BR>r.s some:<BR>कांश्चिन्नयत्युन्नतिम्, Mr. x.<BR>51.;<BR>(3) उच्छ्रयति, r. ing (his)<BR>heroism:<BR>वीर्य-<BR>मुच्छ्राययिष्यन् (causal), Vi. i. 8.<BR>III Of the<BR>dead: उत्थापयति, Kacha also r.d the dead<BR>(Śukra): उत्थापयामास मृतं कचोऽपि, Mah. i. 73.<BR>61.<BR>IV Of armies: उत्थापयति, r.d an army:<BR>बलसमुत्थानमकरोत्, D. viii.<BR>V To erect, build:<BR>q. v.: स्थापयति, प्रति-, (c. of स्था).<BR>VI To<BR>produce: q. v.:<BR>(1) perh. उत्थापयति;<BR>(2)<BR>जनयति (c. of जन्).<BR>VII To excite, arouse:<BR>q. v.: उत्थापयति।<BR>VIII Of pieces etc.:<BR>वर्धयति (c. of वृध्): v. To increase.<BR>IX To<BR>r. (a siege): मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.): v. To<BR>quit, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

raisin
RAISIN: शुष्कद्राक्षा, and sim. comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rake
RAKE (subs.):<BR>I A libertine: q. v.: खण्डित-<BR>वृत्त (f. त्ता).<BR>II An instrument: दन्तकर्तरिका,<BR> दन्तच्छुरिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rake
RAKE (v.):<BR>I To gather: q. v.: समाहरति<BR>(हृ, c. 1.).<BR>II To lead a dissolute life:<BR>व्यभिचरति (चर्, c. 1.).<BR>III To r. up i. e.<BR>revive: q. v.: उत्तोलयति (तुल्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rally
RALLY (v. t.):<BR>I To gather again, reunite:<BR>समाहरति (हृ, c. 1.): v. To collect.<BR>II To<BR>banter, ridicule: q. v.: उपहसति (हस्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rally
RALLY (v. i.):<BR>I To assemble, reunite:<BR>q. v.: सं-भवति (भू, c. 1.).<BR>II Fig., to<BR>recover: q. v.: सुस्थो<BR>or<BR>स्वस्थो (f. स्था) भवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ram
RAM (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मेषः;<BR>(2) उरभ्रः;<BR>(3) मेढ्रः;<BR>(4) उरणः;<BR>(5) एडकः;<BR>(6) हुडुः,<BR>r. -fight:<BR>हुडुयुद्धम्, P. i. 4.:<BR>II The sign:<BR>मेषः।<BR>III Battering -r.: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ram
RAM (v.): मृद्राति (मृद्, c. 9.): v. To batter,<BR>butt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ramble
RAMBLE (v/):<BR>I Lit.: पर्यटति (अट्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To wander.<BR>II Fig., r. ing talk, perh.:<BR>अव्यवस्थितसंलापः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ramble
RAMBLE, RAMBLING (subs.): पर्यटनम्: v.<BR>Wandering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rambler
RAMBLER:<BR>(1) पथिकः: v. Wayfarer;<BR>(2) पर्यटक<BR>(f. टिका, rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ramification
RAMIFICATION:<BR>I A small branch:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रशाखा;<BR>(2) प्रतिशाखा।<BR>II Fig., member,<BR>head: अङ्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ramify
RAMIFY (v. i.): शाखाप्रशाखाभिर्विस्तीर्यते, (pass. of<BR>स्तॄ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rammer
RAMMER:<BR>(1) मुद्गरः;<BR>(2) अयोघनः (of iron).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ramp
RAMP:<BR>I Subs.: लम्फः।<BR>II Verb.: लम्फं ददातिः<BR>v. To leap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rampant
RAMPANT:<BR>I Wild, ferocious: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>निरवग्रह (f. हा);<BR>(2) अनियन्त्रित (f. ता); etc.<BR>II Standing on the hind legs: पश्चात्पादयोः<BR> स्थित (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rampart
RAMPART:<BR>(1) प्राकारः;<BR>(2) वप्रः;<BR>(3) वरणः;<BR>(4) शालः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ramrod
RAMROD: चूर्णमर्दनी and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rancid
RANCID:<BR>(1) उग्रगन्ध (f. न्धा);<BR>(2) उग्रगन्धि (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rancorous
RANCOROUS:<BR>(1) विद्वेषिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) अभि-<BR>द्रोहिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rancorously
RANCOROUSLY:<BR>(1) परमद्वेषात्;<BR>(2) अभिद्रोहेण;<BR>(3) द्रोहबुद्ध्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rancour
RANCOUR: विद्वेषः: v. Hatred;<BR>(2) अभिद्रोहः: v.<BR>Malignity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

random
RANDOM:<BR>(1) आकस्मिक (f. की): v. Accidental;<BR>(2) अनियत (f. ता): v. Unsettled. Ph.:<BR>at r.:<BR>(1) अकस्मात् (= accidentally);<BR>(2)<BR>उच्छ्टङ्खलम् (= without any order, as to talk<BR>at r.);<BR>(3) यदा तदा (of time, as to come<BR>at r.);<BR>(4) प्रकीर्णम् (in speaking), Si. ii. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

range
RANGE (subs.):<BR>I A row, line: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>श्रेणिः (णी);<BR>(2) राजिः (जी)<BR>II A class,<BR>order: q. v.: गणः।<BR>III Excursion, wander-<BR>-ing: q. v.: परिभ्रमणम्।<BR>IV Compass, reach:<BR>q. v.: विषयः,<BR>beyond the r. of Lakṣmaṇa's<BR>arrows:<BR>सौमित्रेरपि पत्रिणामविषये, U. iii. 44.:<BR>V<BR>Kichen-r.: *लौहयोगराजिः।<BR>VI Of a ladder:<BR>v. Step.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

range
RANGE (v.):<BR>I To arrange: q. v.: विरचयति<BR>(रच्, c. 10.).<BR>II To wander: q. v.: परि-<BR>भ्रमति (भ्रम्, c. 1.).<BR>III To have r.: expr.<BR>by subs.: v. Range (IV).<BR>IV To rank:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ranger
RANGER:<BR>I One who ranges or rows: expr.<BR>by verb.<BR>II Robber: लुब्धकः। q. v.<BR>III<BR>Of a forest: अरण्यपालः; वनपालः; and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rank
RANK (subs.):<BR>I A row, line: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>श्रेणिः (णी);<BR>(2) राजिः (जी).<BR>II Of soldiers:<BR>perh. पंक्तिः। Ph.:<BR>r. and file:<BR>दण्डः (= army);<BR>to leave the r. s:<BR>व्यूहं परित्यजति।<BR>III Place,<BR>position: q. v.: पदम्।<BR>IV High station:<BR>(1) उच्चपदम्। and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(2) मानः<BR>(= honour);<BR>(3) प्रतिष्ठा (= glory);<BR>(4)<BR>कौलीन्यम् (= nobility).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rank
RANK (v. i.): expr. by वर्तते (वृत्, c. 1. = to be)<BR>or<BR>तिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1. = to stand),<BR>character r. s<BR>at the head of all excellences:<BR>अतीत्य हि गुणान्<BR> सर्वान् स्वभावो मूर्ध्नि वर्तते, H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rank
RANK (v. t.):<BR>I To place in a line: स्थापयति<BR>(c. of स्था).<BR>II To class, reckon: q. v.:<BR>(1) गणयति (गण्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rank
RANK (adj.):<BR>I Exuberant, rich: q. v.: प्रभूत<BR>(f. ता).<BR>II Rancid:<BR>(1) उग्रगन्ध (f. न्धा);<BR>(2) उग्रगन्धि (mfn.).<BR>III Gross, course:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rankle
RANKLE:<BR>(1) भृशायते (nomi.);<BR>(2) by adj.: v.<BR>Violent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rankness
RANKNESS:<BR>I Luxuriant growth: प्रभूतता: v.<BR>Abundance.<BR>II Strong smell: उग्रगन्धः, -ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ransack
RANSACK:<BR>I To plunder, pillage: q. v.<BR>II<BR>To violate, ravish: q. v.<BR>III To search<BR>thoroughly: q. v.: निपुणमनुसन्दधाति (धा, c. 3.).<BR>IV लोडयति, -वि (लुड्, c. 10.), r. ed the forest:<BR>वनं लोडयामास, Mah. i. 66. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ransom
RANSOM (subs.):<BR>(1) उद्धारः (= release);<BR>(2)<BR>by circumlo.,<BR>to pay a heavy r. for one's<BR>liberty:<BR>बहु धनं दत्त्वा मुक्तिं क्रीणाति (comp. H. iv.<BR>121.,) “कोषांशेनार्धकोषेण सर्वकोषेण वा पुनः । शिष्टस्य<BR> प्रतिरक्षार्थं परिक्रय उदाहृतः ॥”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ransom
RANSOM (v.): धनं दत्त्वा मोक्षयति (मोक्ष्, c. 10.).<BR>: v. To release.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rant
RANT:<BR>I Verb: साडम्बरं<BR>or<BR>उच्चैः प्रलपति (लप्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II Subs.: निरर्थकप्रलपितम् and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ranter
RANTER: उच्चैः प्रलापिन् (f. नी) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rap
RAP (subs.): क्षिप्राहतिः and sim. comp.s.: v.<BR>Stroke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rap
RAP (v.):<BR>I To strike with a sharp blow:<BR>क्षिप्रमाहन्ति (हन्, c. 2.).<BR>or<BR>ताडयति (तड्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR>II To snatch away: अपहरति (हृ,<BR>c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rapacious
RAPACIOUS:<BR>(1) लुब्ध (f. ब्धा);<BR>(2) लुब्धक<BR>(f. का);<BR>(3) गृध्नु (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rapaciously
RAPACIOUSLY:<BR>(1) by adj.;<BR>(2) प्रसह्य (= with<BR>violence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rapaciousness
RAPACIOUSNESS, RAPACITY:<BR>(1) लुब्धता;<BR>(2)<BR>गृध्नुता; (= greediness);<BR>(3) आततायिता;<BR>(4)<BR>साहसिकता (= boldness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rape
RAPE: I. Abduction: हरणम्, the r. of Draupadī:<BR>द्रौपदीहरणम्, Mah.<BR>II Violence on chastity:<BR>बलात्कारेण सम्भोगः, M. n. on R. x. 47., or<BR>sim. बलात्कारः, Mit. Ph.: to commit r.:<BR>बलात्कारेण रमते, गच्छति, etc.<BR>or<BR>बलाद् व्रजति, M.;<BR>attempted to r. me:<BR>मां बलात्कारेण रन्तुमुद्युंक्ते, D.<BR>III. A tree: खसः (?),<BR>r. -seed-oil:<BR>खसबीजानां<BR> तैलम् (?), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rapid
RAPID:<BR>(1) शीघ्र (f. घ्रा);<BR>(2) त्वरित (f. ता)<BR>: v. Quick, swift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rapidity
RAPIDITY:<BR>(1) शीघ्रता: v. Quickness, swift-<BR>-ness;<BR>(2) वेगः: v. Velocity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rapidly
RAPIDLY:<BR>(1) शीघ्रम्;<BR>(2) क्षिप्रम्;<BR>(3) by<BR>comp.: v. Quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rapier
RAPIER: निस्त्रिंशः: v. Dagger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rapine
RAPINE: लुण्ठनम्: v. Plunder, pillage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rapt
RAPT (p. adj.):<BR>(1) हर्षोन्मत्त (f. त्ता);<BR>(2)<BR>हृषितवपुस् (mfn.); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rapture
RAPTURE: हर्षोन्मादः: v. Ecstasy, joy, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rapturous
RAPTUROUS: उन्मादिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp.s. Ph.:<BR>r. joy:<BR>परमानन्दः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rapturously
RAPTUROUSLY:<BR>(1) सहर्षोन्मादः;<BR>(2) हर्षोन्मत्त<BR>(f. त्ता);<BR>(3) साह्लादम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rare
RARE:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) विरल (f. ला),<BR>with r.<BR>dew-drops:<BR>विरलतुषारकणः, Ki. x. 28.; अविरल-<BR>लाञ्छनहारिणश्च कालाः, Ki. x. 38.;<BR>their advi-<BR>sers are rare:<BR>विरलास्तेषामुपदेष्टारः, K,<BR>(2) दुर्लभ<BR>(f. भा) and sim. comp.s. (= scarce).<BR>II<BR>Excellent: अपूर्व (f. र्वा),<BR>I saw a rare flower-<BR>stalk:<BR>अदृष्टपूर्वां कुसुममञ्जरीमद्राक्षम्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rarefaction
RAREFACTION:<BR>(1) तनूकरणम् (?);<BR>(2) विरली-<BR>करणम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rarefy
RAREFY:<BR>I Lit.: विरलीकरोति।<BR>II Of air:<BR>तनूकरोति (?). Ph.:<BR>r. ed. air:<BR>सूक्ष्मीभूतो<BR> वायुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rarely
RARELY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rareness
RARENESS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) विरलता;<BR>(2) दुर्लभता।<BR>II Excellence: अपूर्वता।<BR>III Thinness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rarity
RARITY:<BR>I Rareness: q. v.<BR>II A rare thing:<BR>अपूर्ववस्तु (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rascal
RASCAL<BR>(1) दुरात्मन् (mfn.);<BR>(2) दुर्वृत्त (f. त्ता);<BR>(3) धूर्त (f. र्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rascality
RASCALITY: दौरात्म्यम्;<BR>(2) दुर्वृत्तता;<BR>(3) धूर्तता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rascally
RASCALLY: जघन्य (f. न्या): v. Low, base,<BR>rascal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rase
RASE:<BR>I To graze: घर्षति (घृष्, c. 1.).<BR>II<BR>To erase प्रमार्ष्टि (मृज्, c. 2.).<BR>III To level<BR>with the ground: भूमिसात्करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rash
RASH (adj.):<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) अविमृश्यकारिन्<BR>(f. णी);<BR>(2) असमीक्ष्यकारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(3)<BR>अपरिणामदर्शिन् (f. नी); and sim. comp.s.<BR>II<BR>Of acts:<BR>(1) expr. with adv. s. अविमृश्य,<BR> असमीक्ष्य।;<BR>(2) अयथालोचित (f. ता) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rash
RASH (subs.): v. Eruption, pimple, itch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rasher
RASHER: of bacon: खण्डम्: v. Price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rashly
RASHLY:<BR>(1) अविमृश्य;<BR>(2) असमीक्ष्य;<BR>(3)<BR>अनालोच्य;<BR>(4) सहसा, Ki. ii. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rashness
RASHNESS:<BR>(1) अविमृश्यकारिता;<BR>(2) असमीक्ष्य-<BR>कारिता;<BR>(3) असमीक्षा;<BR>(4) अविवेकः;<BR>(5) साहसम्<BR>(= boldness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rasp
RASP:<BR>I Subs.: *संघर्षणी।<BR>II Verb: संघर्षण्या<BR> घर्षति (घृष्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

raspberry
RASPBERRY: फलविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rasure
RASURE:<BR>I Scraping: घर्षणम्।<BR>II Erasure:<BR>प्रमार्जनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rat
RAT (subs.):<BR>(1) मूषि(ष)कः,<BR>the story about the<BR>r. and the cat:<BR>मार्जारमूषिकसंवादः, Mah. xii.;<BR>(2) आखुः, H. i.;<BR>(3) उ(इ)न्दुरुः। Ph.:<BR>I smell<BR>a r.:<BR>किमप्यनिष्टमाशङ्के।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rat
RAT (v.): स्वपक्षं त्यक्ता परान् आश्रयति, सम्-, (श्रि,<BR>c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ratan
RATAN:<BR>I The plant:<BR>(1) वेतसः, r. -like [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">Page572</a>]<BR>conduct (i. e. easy submission): वैतसी वृत्तिः,<BR>R. iv. 35.;<BR>(2) वेत्रः।<BR>II A. r. stick:<BR>वेत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rate
RATE (subs.):<BR>I Price, value: q. v.: मूल्यम्।<BR>Ph.:<BR>market r.:<BR>आपणिकः;<BR>r. s.:<BR>अर्थबलाबलम्,<BR>M.<BR>II. Tax: q. v.: करः।<BR>III Of interest:<BR>expr. by circumlo.: v. Interest.<BR>IV Of<BR>velocity: वेगः। Ph.:<BR>at any r.:<BR>अन्ततः, Da.<BR>com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rate
RATE (v.):<BR>I To fix r. s: अर्घं<BR>or<BR>मूल्यं संस्थापयति<BR>(c. of स्था).<BR>II To estimate, value: q. v.:<BR>मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.).<BR>III To reprove, censure:<BR>q. v.: उपालभते (लभ्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rather
RATHER:<BR>I In gen.: वरम्: v. Better (II).<BR>II Somewhat:<BR>r. less:<BR>ईषदून (f. ना).: v.<BR>Little. (adv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ratification
RATIFICATION:<BR>(1) स्थिरीकरणम्;<BR>(2) सत्यापनम्;<BR>(3) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ratify
RATIFY:<BR>(1) स्थिरीकरोति;<BR>(2) सत्यापयति: v.<BR>To confirm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rating
RATING (subs.): उपालम्भः: v. Reproach,<BR>censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ratio
RATIO: सम्बन्धः (?).<BR>Common r. two:<BR>द्विगुणोत्तरा<BR> वृद्धिः, Li. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ratiocinate
RATIOCINATE (v.): युक्तियुक्तं<BR>or<BR>सहेतुकं<BR>or<BR>उपपत्ति-<BR>मुदाहृत्य विचारयति। (c. of चर्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ratiocination
RATIOCINATION:<BR>(1) युक्तियुक्तो विचारः, and sim.<BR>comp.s.;<BR>(2) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ration
RATION: expr.^1 with आहारः and its syn.: v.<BR>Food.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rational
RATIONAL:<BR>I Possessing reason:<BR>(1) व्युत्पत्तिमत्<BR>(f. ती),<BR>of r. beings:<BR>व्युत्पत्तिमतां पुरुषाणाम्, S. i.<BR>1. p.;<BR>(2) व्युत्पन्नचित्त (f. त्ता), S.;<BR>(3) विवेकिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR>II Relating or agreeable to<BR>reason: विवेकिन् (f. नी),<BR>your r. mind:<BR>विवेकिनी<BR> ते मतिः, Ki. ii. 6.<BR>III In alg.: r. quantity:<BR>रूपम्, Vij.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rationale
RATIONALE: i. e.: reasons: उपपत्तिः (f.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rationalism
RATIONALISM:<BR>(1) हेतुवादः;<BR>(2) न्यायवादः (?);<BR>(3) हैतुकता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rationlist
RATIONLIST:<BR>(1) हेतुवादिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) हैतुक<BR>(f. की), V. p. iii. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rationality
RATIONALITY:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) व्युत्पत्तिमत्ता;<BR>(2) व्युत्पन्नचित्तता;<BR>(3) विवेकिता।<BR>II Of acts:<BR>विवेकिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rationalize
RATIONALIZE: in alg: *रूपीकरोति। after मूली-<BR>करोति of A. c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rationally
RATIONALLY: विवेकद्वारा<BR>or<BR>-द्वारेण: v. Wisely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rattle
RATTLE (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) कूजति (कूज्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) क्वणति (क्वण्, c. 1.).;<BR>(3) संक्रीडति (क्रीड्,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>r. ing pole:<BR>संक्रीडन्ती धूः, Si. xvii. 7.<BR>II To r. away (of men):<BR>(1) प्रलपति (लप्,<BR>c. 1.);<BR>(2) वि-जल्पति (जल्प्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rattle
RATTLE (subs.):<BR>I R. ing noise:<BR>(1) कूजितम्;<BR>(2) क्वणितम्;<BR>(3) संक्रीडितम्;<BR>r. of wheels:<BR>रथाङ्ग-<BR>संक्रीडितम्, Ki. xvi. 8.<BR>II Of men:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रलपितम्;<BR>(2) वि-जल्पितम्।<BR>III An instru-<BR>-ment: *शिञ्जिनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rattlesnake
RATTLESNAKE: अहिविशेषः; *शिञ्जाभोगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rattling
RATTLING:<BR>I Adj.:<BR>(1) कूजत् (f. न्ती);<BR>(2) क्वणत् (f. न्ती).<BR>II Subs.: कूजितम्: v.<BR>Rattle (1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ravage
RAVAGE (v.): उपप्लवते (प्लु, c. 1.): v. To<BR>depredate, plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ravage
RAVAGE (subs.): उपप्लवः: v. Depredation,<BR>devastation, plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ravager
RAVAGER:<BR>(1) उपप्लवकारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) उप-<BR>द्रावक (f. विका);<BR>(3) अवमर्दक (f. र्दिका);<BR>(4)<BR>संबाधक (f. धिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rave
RAVE:<BR>I Lit.: उन्मत्तवत् प्रलपति (लप्, c. 1.)<BR>II<BR>To wander in mind: उन्माद्यति (मद्, c. 4.),<BR>of the r. ing (kings): उन्माद्यताम्, Vi. ii. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ravel
RAVEL:<BR>I To unravel: q. v.: विश्लेषयति (c. of<BR>श्लिष्).<BR>II To entangle, involve: q. v.:<BR>संश्लेषयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ravelin
RAVELIN: *प्रतिशालः; कूटविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

raven
RAVEN:<BR>(1) द्रोणकाकः;<BR>(2) काकोलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

raven
RAVEN, RAVIN (v.): v. To devour; greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ravenous
RAVENOUS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) घस्मर (f. रा),<BR>the r.<BR>destructive Rudra:<BR>घस्मरकालरुद्रः, Vi. iii. 48.;<BR>(2) अद्मर (f. रा): v. Also hungry.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>परम (f. मा): v. Excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ravenously
RAVENOUSLY:<BR>(1) घस्मरवत्;<BR>(2) अद्मरवत्;<BR>(3)<BR>बुभुक्षु (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ravenousness
RAVENOUSNESS:<BR>(1) घस्मरता;<BR>(2) अद्मरता;<BR>(3)<BR>गृध्नुता (fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ravine
RAVINE:<BR>(1) कन्दरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) कन्दरभूः;<BR>(3)<BR>दरीभूः, -मिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ravingly
RAVINGLY:<BR>(1) उन्मत्तवत्;<BR>(2) उन्मादात्;<BR>(3)<BR>उन्मादेन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ravish
RAVISH:<BR>I To rape: बलात्कारेण भुङ्क्ते (भुज्,<BR>c. 7.).<BR>or<BR>रमते (रम्, c. 1.).<BR>II To carry<BR>off: (प्रसह्य) हरति, अप-, (हृ, c. 1.).<BR>III To<BR>enrapture: हरति: v. To charm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ravisher
RAVISHER: expr. by verb: v. Also defiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ravishing
RAVISHING (adj.): मनोहारिन् (f. णी): v.<BR>Charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ravishment
RAVISHMENT:<BR>I Abduction: हरणम्, अप-।<BR>II<BR>Rape: बलात्कारसम्भोगः।<BR>III Rapture, delight:<BR>q. v.: हर्षोन्मादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

raw
RAW:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) आम (f. मा), r. -fish-eaters:<BR>आममीनाशिनः, Ram.;<BR>r. mango:<BR>आममाम्रम्,<BR>Bha.; who cuts a r. (i. e. a r. sore) unwittingly:<BR>यो छिनत्त्याममज्ञानात्, Sr.;<BR>(2) अपक्व (f. क्वा =<BR>unripe: q. v.);<BR>(3) असिद्ध (f. द्धा = uncooked).<BR>II Inexperienced, untried:<BR>(1) (1) अपक्व-<BR>बुद्धि (mfn.);<BR>(2) अदृष्टकर्मन् (mfn.); and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>III Of spirits: विना जलेन (= without<BR>water)<BR>or<BR>असंसृष्ट (f. ष्टा = unmixed).<BR>IV<BR>Chilly and damp: क्लिन्नशिशिर<BR>or<BR>-तुषार (f. राः ?).<BR>V Unwrought, impure, etc.: perh. असंस्कृत<BR>(f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

raw-boned
RAW-BONED (adj.):<BR>(1) त्वगस्थिशेष (f. षा);<BR>(2)<BR>क्षामक्षाम (f. मा), D. v.; and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ray
RAY:<BR>I Of light:<BR>(1) किरणः;<BR>(2) करः;<BR>(3)<BR>रश्मिः;<BR>(4) अंशुः;<BR>(5) पादः, r. s of the moon:<BR>चन्द्रपादाः, V.;<BR>(6) मयूखः, the cold-r. ed (moon):<BR>शीतमयूखः, Ki.;<BR>(7) मरीचिः, having streams of<BR>r.s (sun): मरीचिमालिन्, H.;<BR>(8) दीधितिः, the<BR>hot-r. ed (sun): अशीतदीधितिः;<BR>(9) गभस्तिः;<BR>(10)<BR>उस्रः।<BR>II A fish: *अंशुमत् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

raze
RAZE:<BR>I Subs.: मूलम्।<BR>II Verb: उच्छिनत्ति<BR>(छिद्, c. 7.): v. To erase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

razor
RAZOR:<BR>I For shaving: क्षुरः,<BR>r. case:<BR>क्षुर-<BR>भाण्डम्, H.<BR>II. A fish: मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

re-
RE-:<BR>(1) expr. by पुनर्;<BR>(2) sometimes by प्रति-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reach
REACH (v. i.):<BR>I To extend: q. v.: विस्तीर्यते<BR>(pass. of स्तॄ): v. Also to touch, attain,<BR>penetrate.<BR>II To stretch the hand: हस्तं<BR>प्रसारयति। Ph.: as far as the eye can r.:<BR>यावच्चक्षुषा दर्शनीयम्। (?.): v. Reach (subs.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reach
REACH (v. t.):<BR>I To stretch: q. v.: प्रसारयति<BR>(c. of सृ).<BR>II To hand over: q. v.: प्रापयति<BR>(c. of आप्).<BR>III To come to: q. v.:<BR>आयाति (या, c. 2.).<BR>IV To attain: q. v.:<BR>अधिगच्छति (गम्, c. 1.).<BR>V To arrive at:<BR>q. v.: आसादयति, सम्-, (c. of सद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reach
REACH (subs.):<BR>I In gen.: विषयः,<BR>beyond the<BR>r. of even Lakṣmaṇa's arrows:<BR>सौमित्रेरपि<BR> पत्रिणामविषये, U. iii. 44.;<BR>(2) गोचरः,<BR>beyond the<BR>r. of speech and mind:<BR>अवाङ्मनसगोचर (f. रा),<BR>R. x. 15;<BR>beyond the r. of the senses:<BR>अगोचर<BR>(f. रा), Ki. N.B. Within r., out of r.: often<BR>expr. by ग्राह्य, अ-, (= comprehensible, not-),<BR>गम्य, अ- (= approachable, not-), etc.,<BR>within<BR>r. of tall men:<BR>प्रांशुलभ्य (f. भ्या), R. i. 3.<BR>II<BR>Capacity, influence: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

react
REACT:<BR>I Lit.: पुनः करोति: v. To act.<BR>II<BR>To resist: q. v.<BR>III To exercise a reci-<BR>-procal effect: प्रतिकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reaction
REACTION:<BR>I Counteraction:<BR>(1) प्रतिक्रिया;<BR>(2) प्रतिकारः<BR>or<BR>प्रतिकृतिः (rare).<BR>II Of two<BR>forces: प्रतिघातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

read
READ:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पठति (पठ्, c. 1.),<BR>we r.<BR>in the Kāṭhaka:<BR>काठके पठ्यते, S.; himself opened<BR>and r. it (the letter): स्वयमेव तदुन्मुच्य पपाठ, K.;<BR>some r.<BR>लासिका<BR>for<BR>विलासिका: केचिद्विलासिकास्थाने<BR> लासिकेति पठन्ति, Sah.;<BR>(2) वाचयति, निर्-, (c. of<BR>वच्) (= to r. out),<BR>taken and r.s:<BR>गृहीत्वा<BR> वाचयति, An.<BR>II To study:<BR>(1) पठति,<BR>r.<BR>lessons for children:<BR>पपाठ बालपाठ्यानि, V. p. 1.<BR>17. 10.;<BR>(2) अधीते (इ, c. 2.), (well)<BR>r. in<BR>the four Vedas:<BR>अधीती चतुर्ष्वाम्नायेषु, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

read through
READ THROUGH:<BR>(1) आद्यन्तं<BR>or<BR>सम्पूर्णं<BR>or<BR>अशेषतः<BR> पठति;<BR>(2) पारं गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.). and sim.<BR>comp.s.,<BR>one who has r. t. the Vedas:<BR>श्रुतपारदृश्वन्<BR>(mfn.), R. v. 24.;<BR>(3) तरति (तॄ, c. 1. = to<BR>cross: poet), R. iii. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

read
READ, WELL-: (adj.): v. Learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

readable
READABLE:<BR>(1) पाठ्य (f. ठ्या);<BR>(2) पठनीयः<BR>(या, यं);<BR>(3) पाठयोग्य (f. ग्या). and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reader
READER:<BR>(1) पाठक (f. ठिका),<BR>a r. is a religious<BR>lecturer:<BR>पाठको धर्मभाणकः, T. s.;<BR>(2) पठितिन्<BR>(f. नी: rare),<BR>a careless r.:<BR>हठेन पठिती, N.<BR>xxii. 154.;<BR>(3) वाचक (f. चिका = one who<BR>reads out, such as letter),<BR>public r.:<BR>पुस्तक-<BR>वाचकः, C. iii.;<BR>(4) अध्येतृ (f. त्री = one who<BR>has studied).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

readily
READILY:<BR>I Willingly, cheerfully: q. v.:<BR>सोत्साहम्।<BR>II Quickly, promptly: q. v.:<BR>अचिरेण।<BR>III Easily: q. v.: सुखेन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

readiness
READINESS:<BR>I Willingness, cheerfulness:<BR>(1) सोत्साहता;<BR>(2) उत्सुकता<BR>or<BR>औत्सुक्यम्: v.<BR>Also promptitude, quickness.<BR>II Facility,<BR>dexterity: q. v.: लाघवम्।<BR>III State of<BR>preparation:<BR>(1) सज्जितता;<BR>(2) प्रस्तुतता;<BR>(3)<BR>better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reading
READING:<BR>I Perusal: पठनम्<BR>or<BR>पाठः,<BR>incessant<BR>r. of the Vedas:<BR>अश्रान्तश्रुतिपाठः, N.; r. -room:<BR>पाठशाला।<BR>II Studying: अध्ययनम्,<BR>r. with<BR>Yājnavalkya:<BR>योगीश्वरादध्यनम्, An.;<BR>r., teaching<BR>sacrificing:<BR>अध्ययनमध्यापनं यजनम्, Vas.<BR>III. R.<BR>out as letters: वाचनम्, निर्-।<BR>IV Scholar-<BR>-ship, learning: q. v. V. A. lecture or<BR>recital: पाठः,<BR>morning r.:<BR>प्राभातिकपाठः, C. ii.<BR>VI Section, version: पाठः, an erroneous r.:<BR>भ्रममूलकः पाठः, Va. com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reading-book
READING-BOOK: पाठ्यपुस्तकम्, and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ready
READY:<BR>I Prepared:<BR>(1) सज्ज (f. ज्जा) or<BR>सज्जित (f. ता),<BR>be r.:<BR>सज्जा तावद्भव, Sa. iv.;<BR>when the equipments were being got r.:<BR>सज्जी-<BR>क्रियमाणे साधने, K. ii.;<BR>(2) प्रस्तुत (f. ता);<BR>(3)<BR>कल्पित, परि-, उप-, (f. ता = only of things).<BR>II<BR>Willing, cheerful: q. v.:<BR>(1) उत्सुक (f. का),<BR>परि-;<BR>(2) उत्साहवत् (f. ती).<BR>III On the<BR>point of, about: q. v.:<BR>(1) उद्यत (f. ता);<BR>(2) उन्मुख (f. खा).<BR>IV Quick, prompt:<BR>of<BR>r. wit:<BR>प्रत्युत्पन्नमति (mfn.); of r. apprehension:<BR>तीक्ष्णबुद्धि (mfn.).<BR>V Near, short: q. v. Ph.:<BR>r. money:<BR>टङ्कः and an adv. तत्कालम् (= at the<BR>time)<BR>or<BR>हस्ते (= in hand).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

real
REAL:<BR>I True, genuine: q. v.:<BR>(1) सत्यः<BR>(ता, तं),<BR>a r. elephant:<BR>सत्यगजः, K. s. xii. 16.;<BR>(2) ऋत (f. ता: rare), coupling the r. and the<BR>unreal:<BR>सत्यानृते मिथुनीकृत्य;<BR>(3) प्रकृत (f. ता)<BR>(4) वास्तव (f. वा)<BR>or<BR>वास्तविक (f. की).<BR>II In<BR>law:<BR>(1) स्थावर (f. रा);<BR>(2) जङ्गमेतर (f. रा):<BR>v. Property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

realgar
REALGAR: i. e. red orpiment: रक्तधातुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

realist
REALIST: *याथार्थिक (f. की); व्याप्तिज्ञानवादिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reality
REALITY:<BR>I The condition:<BR>(1) सत्यता;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रकृतता;<BR>(3) वास्तविकता;<BR>(4) व्यलीकता;<BR>(5)<BR>अकृत्रिमता। Ph.:<BR>in r.:<BR>तत्त्वतः, K. xviii. 27.<BR>II Anything real: सत्यम्: v. Real. (1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

realization
REALIZATION:<BR>I Accomplishment: q. v.:<BR>साधनम्।<BR>II Of ideas etc.: अनुभवः<BR>or<BR>अनुभूतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

realize
REALIZE:<BR>I To accomplish: q. v.: साधयति<BR>(c. of साध्).<BR>II To feel vividly: अनुभवति,<BR>as if r. ing the pain:<BR>वेदनामनुभवन्निव, Ki. iii.<BR>69.<BR>III To convert into real property:<BR>expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

really
REALLY:<BR>I In truth:<BR>(1) यथार्थतः;<BR>(2) परमा-<BR>र्थतः;<BR>(3) सत्यम्।<BR>II In reality:<BR>(1) तत्त्वतः;<BR>(2) वस्तुतः (= in fact), S. p. b. 1. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

realm
REALM: राष्ट्रम्: v. Kingdom, province.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ream
REAM: of paper: *रीमम्; पोत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reanimate
REANIMATE:<BR>I To cheer, gladden: q. v.:<BR>प्रत्याश्वासयति (c. of श्वस्).<BR>II To revive:<BR>(1)<BR>पुनर् उज्जीवयति (c. of जीव्);<BR>(2) सञ्जीवयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reap
REAP:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) लुनाति (लू, c. 9.),<BR>r. ing<BR>machine:<BR>लवित्रम्;<BR>(2) छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7.),<BR>time for r. ing crops:<BR>शस्यछेदनकालः, Nil. on<BR>Mah. ii. 5. 64.: Also to gather.<BR>II To<BR>get: q. v.: लभते (लभ्, c. 1.): v. To sow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reaper
REAPER:<BR>I The man:<BR>(1) लावक (f. विका)<BR>or<BR>लाव (f. वा);<BR>flower-r.:<BR>पुष्पलावी, Me. i. 27.;<BR>(2) शस्यच्छेदक (f. दिका: of crops.).<BR>II A<BR>machine: लवित्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reaping-hook
REAPING-HOOK: लवित्रम्: v. Sickle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reappear
REAPPEAR: पुनर् आविर्भवति etc.: v. To appear,<BR>again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rear
REAR (subs.):<BR>I The back: q. v.: पृष्ठम्।<BR>II<BR>Of an army:<BR>(1) पृष्ठम्,<BR>on the r.:<BR>अनुपृष्ठम्,<BR>Ka. xix. 36.;<BR>(2) पार्ष्णिः, with the r. guarded:<BR>शुद्धपार्ष्णिः, R. iv. 26. Ph: or shall put the r.<BR>in disorder and attack the front with the pick [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">Page575</a>]<BR>of the army:<BR>पश्चाद्वा सङ्कुलीकृत्य हन्यात् सारेण पूर्वतः,<BR>Ka. xviii. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rear
REAR (v.):<BR>I To bring up, nourish: q. v.:<BR>वर्धयति (c. of वृध्).<BR>II To raise, lift up:<BR>q. v.: उत्थापयति (c. of स्था).<BR>III To rise on<BR>hind legs: shall strike on the eyes when (a<BR>horse)<BR>r. s.:<BR>हन्यान्नेत्रमार्गे दुरुत्थितम्, M. n. on Si. v.<BR>10.;<BR>r. ing;<BR>पुरुष कम्, Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reason
REASON (subs.):<BR>I The intellect;<BR>(1) विवेकः<BR>(good r.);<BR>(2) बुद्धिः: v. Intellect;<BR>(3) मतिः:<BR>v. Mind;<BR>(4) प्रज्ञा: v. Wisdom;<BR>(5) व्युत्पत्तिः,<BR>of men endowed with r.:<BR>व्युत्पत्तिमतां पुरुषाणाम्, S.<BR>II. Ground, motive, cause:<BR>(1) हेतुः,<BR>speaks<BR>of its r. s in the (following) Sūtras:<BR>अत्र हेतूनाह<BR> सूत्रैः, S. p. b.;<BR>(2) कारणम्: v. Cause;<BR>(3)<BR>निमित्तम् (= ground),<BR>say for what r.:<BR>कथय<BR> कस्मिन्निमित्ते। Ph.: (a)<BR>for what r.:<BR>किन्निमित्तम्:<BR>v. Why; (b)<BR>without r.:<BR>अकारणम्, निरर्थकम्,<BR>(c) by r. of by abl.: v. Account of, on;<BR>(d)<BR>for that, this r.:<BR>तदर्थम्, एतदर्थम्<BR>or<BR>तन्निमित्तम्,<BR> एतन्निमित्तम्; (e) for some r. (lit. with some<BR>object): केनापि कामेन, Ku. i. 57.<BR>III Argu-<BR>-ment:<BR>(1) हेतुः, crushing the opponent's r. s:<BR>परपक्षहेतूनुन्मथ्य, S.;<BR>(2) युक्तिः,<BR>to prove some<BR>doctrine by mere r. s.:<BR>केवलाभिर्यु क्तिभिः कञ्चित्<BR> सिद्धान्तं साधयितुम्, S.;<BR>(3) उपपत्तिः,<BR>r. s have been<BR>forcibly adduced:<BR>उपपत्तिरुदाहृता बलात्, Ki. ii.<BR>28.<BR>IV Justice, propriety: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reason
REASON (v.):<BR>(1) तर्कयति, वि-, (तर्क्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) विचारयति (c. of चर्): v. To argue,<BR>debate. Ph.:<BR>r. ing faculty:<BR>धीशक्तिः: v.<BR>Reason (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reasonable
REASONABLE:<BR>I Rational: q. v.: विवेकिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR>II Just, proper: q. v.: न्याय्य<BR>(f. य्या).<BR>III Moderate: q. v.: परिमित<BR>(f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reasonableness
REASONABLENESS:<BR>I Rationality:<BR>(1)<BR>विवेकिता;<BR>(2) धीशक्तिः: v. Also reason (I).<BR>II Justness, propriety: q. v.: न्याय्यता।<BR>III<BR>Moderation: परिमितता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reasonably
REASONABLY:<BR>I Justly:<BR>(1) न्यायतः;<BR>(2)<BR>युक्तितः;<BR>(3) सोपपत्ति।<BR>II Moderately: (I)<BR>परिमितम्;<BR>(2) better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reasoner
REASONER:<BR>(1) तर्किन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) तार्किक<BR>(f. की);<BR>(3) तर्ककारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reasoning
REASONING (subs.):<BR>(1) तर्कः;<BR>(2) विचारः,<BR> “विचारमूढः”, R. ii. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reassume
REASSUME: पुनः परि-गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.): v. To<BR>assume, take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reassure
REASSURE: पुनर् आश्वासयति (c. of श्वस्): v. To<BR>assure, cheer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rebate
REBATE: लघयति: v. To lessen, diminish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rebel
REBEL (subs.):<BR>(1) राजद्रोहिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2)<BR>राजाभिद्रोहिन् (f. णी);<BR>(3) राजद्विष् (mfn.);<BR>(4)<BR>राजद्रुह् (mfn.);<BR>(5) राज्जापथ्यकारिन् (f. णी), Mu.;<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rebel
REBEL (v.): राज्ञे द्रुह्यति (द्रुह्, c. 4.)<BR>or<BR>राजानमभि-<BR>द्रुह्यति<BR>or<BR>राजद्रोहं करोति<BR>or<BR>राज्ञा विरोधं करोति<BR>and sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rebellion
REBELLION:<BR>(1) राजद्रोहः;<BR>(2) राजाभिद्रोहः;<BR>(3)<BR>राजविरोधः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rebellious
REBELLIOUS: राजविरुद्ध (f. द्धा): v. Rebel (subs.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rebound
REBOUND:<BR>I Verb: प्रतिघाताद् उत्पतति, (पत्, c.<BR>1.),<BR>and made the (ball) r. by striking;<BR>प्रशान्तं<BR> तं प्रहारैरुदपातयत्, D. vi.<BR>II Subs.: expr. by<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rebuff
REBUFF (subs.):<BR>I Repulsion:<BR>(1) प्रत्यादेशः;<BR>(2) अवधीरणा।<BR>II Repercussion:<BR>(1) प्रतिघातः;<BR>(2) प्रतिहतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rebuff
REBUFF (v.):<BR>(1) प्रत्यादिशति (दिश्, c. 6.);<BR>(2)<BR>अवधीरयति (अवधीर्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rebuild
REBUILD: प्रतिवि-दधाति<BR>or<BR>-धत्ते (धा, c. 3.): v.<BR>To build, again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rebuke
REBUKE:<BR>I Verb: भर्त्सयति, -ते (भर्त्स्, c. 10.):<BR>v. To censure, reproach.<BR>II Subs.: भर्त्सना:<BR>v. Censure, reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rebuker
REBUKER: भर्त्सनाकारिन् (f. णी): v. Censurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rebus
REBUS: no equiv.: *चित्रप्रहेलिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rebut
REBUT:<BR>(1) निरस्यति (अस्, c. 4.):<BR>(2) प्रतिक्षि-<BR>पति (क्षिप्, c. 6.), D. s. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recall
RECALL (v.):<BR>I Lit.: प्रत्याह्वयति (ह्वे, c. 1.):<BR>v. To call, back.<BR>II To remember: q. v.:<BR>स्मरति (स्मृ, c. 1.).<BR>III To annul, revoke:<BR>q. v.: निवर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recall
RECALL (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रत्याह्वानम् (= calling<BR>back);<BR>(2) निवर्तनम् (= revocation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recant
RECANT: प्रत्याख्याति (ख्या, c. 2): v. To deny,<BR>retract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recantation
RECANTATION: प्रत्याख्यानम्: v. Contradiction,<BR>retraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recapitulate
RECAPITULATE: संक्षेपतः कथयति, (कथ्, c. 10.):<BR>v. To relate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recapitulation
RECAPITULATION: संक्षेपतः पुनरुक्तिः and sim.<BR>expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recede
RECEDE:<BR>I To move back, retreat: q. v.:<BR>अपसरति (सृ, c. 1.).<BR>II To desist: q. v.:<BR>निवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

receipt
RECEIPT:<BR>I Receiving:<BR>(1) आदानम्;<BR>(2)<BR>परि (प्रति) ग्रहः, -णम्;<BR>(3) by verb.<BR>II Income:<BR>q. v.: आयः।<BR>III Note of acknowledge-<BR>-ment: *प्रतिग्रहणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

receivable
RECEIVABLE:<BR>(1) आदेय (f. या), सम्-;<BR>(2) परि-<BR> (प्रति) ग्रहणीय (f. या);<BR>(3) परि (प्रति) ग्राह्य (f. ह्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

receive
RECEIVE:<BR>(1) समासादयति (c. of सद्): v. To<BR>get gain;<BR>(2) परिगृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.): v. To<BR>accept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

receiver
RECEIVER:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्रति(परि)ग्रहीतृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) प्रति (परि) ग्राहक (f. हिका);<BR>(3) प्रति(परि)ग्राहिन्<BR>(f. णी), r. s (of stolen property): प्रतिग्राहिणः,<BR>Mit.<BR>II A reservoir:<BR>(1) आधारः;<BR>(2)<BR>भाजनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recent
RECENT: अभिनव (f. वा): v. New, fresh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recently
RECENTLY: expr. by adj.: v. Also lately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

receptacle
RECEPTACLE:<BR>(1) आधारः;<BR>(2) निधानम्<BR>or<BR>निधिः<BR>(in fig. senses);<BR>(3) भाजनम् (= vessel);<BR>(4)<BR>आश्रयः (= refuge).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reception
RECEPTION:<BR>I Receiving: परि (प्रति) ग्रहः।<BR>II<BR>Entertainment:<BR>(1) perh. परिग्रहः;<BR>(2) उप-<BR>चारः (courteous r.), C.;<BR>(3) सम्भावना (= hon-<BR>-ouring), Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

receptive
RECEPTIVE:<BR>r. of:<BR>-ग्राहिन् (f. णी): v. To<BR>receive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recess
RECESS:<BR>I Place of retirement:<BR>(1) शरणम्<BR>(rare);<BR>(2) विविक्तम् (= secluded spot);<BR>(3)<BR>विलम् (= hole);<BR>(4) विश्रामस्थानम् and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Holidays: विश्रामकालः and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recipe
RECIPE:<BR>r. s for making food:<BR>अन्नानां साधनप्रकारः,<BR>Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recipient
RECIPIENT: ग्राहक (f. हिका): v. Receiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reciprocal
RECIPROCAL:<BR>I Mutual: q. v.: परस्पर- in<BR>comp.<BR>II Mutually interchangeable:<BR>(1)<BR>परस्परानुवर्तिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) अन्योन्यप्रगुण (f. णा),<BR>Mal. i. 17.; and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reciprocally
RECIPROCALLY:<BR>(1) परस्परम्;<BR>(2) अन्योऽन्यम्;<BR>(3) इतरेतरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reciprocate
RECIPROCATE: expr. by circumlo: v. Reci-<BR>-procally, interchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reciprocity
RECIPROCITY:<BR>(1) व्यतिकरः,<BR>pleasure of r.:<BR>व्यति-<BR>करसुखम्, Sa. iii. 27.;<BR>(2) विनिमयः (= inter-<BR>-change);<BR>(3) by adv.: v. Mutual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recital
RECITAL, RECITATION:<BR>I Reading:<BR>(1) पाठः,<BR> प्र-;<BR>(2) वाचनम्, निर्- (as of letters).<BR>II<BR>Narration, description: q. v.: वर्णना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recite
RECITE:<BR>(1) वाचयति (c. of वच्): v. To read;<BR>(2) कथयति (कथ्, c. 10.): v. To narrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reciter
RECITER:<BR>(1) वाचक (f. चिका = reader);<BR>(2)<BR>कथक (f. थिका = narrator).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reckless
RECKLESS: प्रमत्त (f. त्ता): v. Careless, rash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recklessly
RECKLESSLY:<BR>(1) by adj.;<BR>(2) प्रमादात्: v.<BR>Carelessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recklessness
RECKLESSNESS:<BR>(1) प्रमत्तता;<BR>(2) प्रमादः: v.<BR>Carelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reckon
RECKON:<BR>I To count:<BR>(1) गणयति, परि-, वि-,<BR> प्र-, (गण्, c. 10.),<BR>then all his excellencies might<BR>be r. ed:<BR>गणेयनिःशेषगुणोऽपि स स्यात्, N. iii. 40.;<BR>(2) संख्याति परि-, प्र-, (ख्या, c. 2.),<BR>cannot be r.<BR>ed:<BR>न शक्यं परिसंख्यातुम्, Mah.<BR>II To think,<BR>consider: q. v.:<BR>(1) गणयति, वि-, परि-,<BR>r. your<BR>success is not distant:<BR>अदूरवर्तिनीमात्मनः सिद्धिं<BR> विगणय, R. i. 87.;<BR>(2) मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.).<BR>III<BR>To r. on or upon i. e. to depend on:<BR>(1)<BR>गणयति, वि-, परि-;<BR>(2) सम्भावयति (c. of भू): v.<BR>To believe, rely on.<BR>IV To r. for, i. e. to<BR>be answerable for: expr. with दायिन् (f.<BR>नी: ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reckoner
RECKONER:<BR>(1) गणक (f. णिका);<BR>(2) गणयितृ<BR>(f. त्री);<BR>(3) संख्यातृ (f. त्री). Ph.: ready r.:<BR>*सहजगणकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reckoning
RECKONING (subs.):<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) गणनम्,<BR> -ना, वि-, परि-;<BR>(2) संख्यानम्, परि-, प्र-।<BR>II<BR>Thinking, consideration:<BR>(1) गणना;<BR>(2) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">Page577</a>]<BR>वितर्कः (= guess).<BR>III A statement: perh.<BR>गणना(न)पत्रम्। Ph.: dead r. (at sea): perh.<BR>गतिगणना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reclaim
RECLAIM:<BR>I Lit.: v. To claim, again.<BR>II To<BR>effect reformation:<BR>(1) शोधयति, परि-, (c.<BR>of शुध्);<BR>(2) सत्पथे प्रवर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR>III<BR>Of lands: perh. शोधयति, परि-, वि-;<BR>(2) कृषि-<BR>योग्यं (f. ग्यां) करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reclamation
RECLAMATION:<BR>I Recovery: q. v.<BR>II In<BR>gen.: शोधनम्, वि-, परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recline
RECLINE:<BR>I To lean back:<BR>(1) अव-लम्बते,<BR> आ-, समा-, (लम्ब्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) आश्रयति, उपा-,<BR> समा-, (श्रि, c. 1.),<BR>where other women have not<BR>r.d:<BR>अनुपाश्रितोऽन्यया, U. i. 37.;<BR>(3) expr.<BR>with words meaning pillow: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>lie, rest: q. v.: विश्राम्यति (श्रम्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reclining
RECLINING, RECLINED (adj.):<BR>(1) नम्र (f. म्रा),<BR>अव-, प्र- (= bent, low);<BR>(2) शयान (f. ना =<BR>lying down);<BR>(3) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recluse
RECLUSE:<BR>I Subs.: सन्न्यासिन् (f. नी): v. Hermit.<BR>II Adj.: विविक्त (f. क्ता): v. Solitary, lonely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recognition
RECOGNITION: अभिज्ञानम्, प्रति-;<BR>(2) अभिज्ञा, प्रति-;<BR>(3) संवित्तिः, प्रति- (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recognizable
RECOGNIZABLE:<BR>(1) अभिज्ञेयः (या, यं), प्रति-;<BR>(2) संवेद्य (f. द्या)<BR>or<BR>-दनीय (f. या), प्रति- (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recognizance
RECOGNIZANCE: no equiv.: दर्शनाङ्गीकारः<BR>(comp. प्रातिभाव्याङ्गीकारः, Mit.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recognize
RECOGNIZE:<BR>I To see likeness or identity:<BR>(1) अभिजानाति, प्रति-, सं- (ज्ञा, c. 9.),<BR>I am r. d<BR>by him:<BR>प्रत्यभिज्ञातास्म्येतेन, Ra. iii.; अनभिज्ञेयपूर्वा-<BR>कारं तमहमद्राक्षम्, K.;<BR>(2) संवित्ते, प्रति-, (विद्,<BR>c. 2.),<BR>when even my parents do not r. me:<BR>पित-<BR>रावपि यावन्मां न प्रतिसंविदाते, D. iii.<BR>II To ac-<BR>-knowledge: q. v.: अङ्गीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recoil
RECOIL:<BR>I Verb:<BR>(1) परावर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) व्यपवर्तते, Mah. i. 19.: v. Also to fall<BR>back.<BR>II Subs.:<BR>(1) परावृत्तिः;<BR>(2) परावर्तः,<BR> नम्;<BR>(3) व्यपवृत्तिः<BR>or<BR>-वर्तनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recollect
RECOLLECT:<BR>I To remember: q. v.: स्मरति<BR>(स्मृ, c. 1.).<BR>II To r. one's self, not to<BR>forget one's self: धैर्यं न मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.);<BR>विकृतिं न गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.); and sim. expr. s.<BR>III To recognize: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recollection
RECOLLECTION: स्मृतिः: v. Remembrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recommend
RECOMMEND:<BR>I To commend, praise: q. v.:<BR>प्रशंसति (शंस्, c. 1.).<BR>II To another's<BR>favourable notice: expr. by circumlo.,<BR>I will<BR>r. you to Damayanti in such a way:<BR>तदहं विदधे<BR> तव स्तवं दभयन्त्याः सविधे तथा तथा, N. ii. 47.<BR>III<BR>To advise: q. v.: उपदिशति (दिश्, c. 6.).<BR>IV To commit, entrust: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recommendation
RECOMMENDATION:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) प्रशंसा<BR>(= praise);<BR>(2) गुणवर्णना (= description of<BR>good qualities); and sim. expr. s.<BR>II<BR>Advice: q. v.: उपदेशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recommendatory
RECOMMENDATORY:<BR>(1) गुणख्यापक (f. पिका);<BR>(2) गुणोल्लेखिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) गुणशंसिन् (f. नी);<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recompense
RECOMPENSE (v.):<BR>I For some loss:<BR>(1)<BR>शोधयति, परि-, प्रति-, (c. of शुध्);<BR>(2) क्षतिपूरणं<BR> करोति।<BR>II To pay: q. v.: मूल्यं ददाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recompense
RECOMPENSE (subs.):<BR>(1) निष्कृतिः: v. Com-<BR>-pensation;<BR>(2) मूल्यम् (= price);<BR>(3) पारि-<BR>तोषिकम् (= reward).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reconcilable
RECONCILABLE:<BR>(1) प्रसादनीय (f. या);<BR>(2) सा-<BR>(शा) न्त्वनीय (f. या), परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reconcile
RECONCILE:<BR>I To conciliate:<BR>(1) मिलनं or<BR>संमिलनं कारयति (c. of कृ);<BR>(2) संघटयति (c. of<BR>घट्);<BR>(3) कोपं शमयति (c. of शम् = to appease<BR>anger);<BR>(4) प्रसादयति (c. of सद्).<BR>II To<BR>make consistent:<BR>(1) विसंवादम् अपाकरोति (कृ,<BR>c. 8.);<BR>(2) ऐक्यं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reconciliation
RECONCILIATION, RECONCILEMENT:<BR>I The<BR>act:<BR>(1) by verb;<BR>(2) प्रसादनम् (= conci-<BR>-liation).<BR>II The state:<BR>(1) मिलनम्, -सं-;<BR>(2) संघटनम्, -ना;<BR>(3) ऐक्यम्।<BR>III Of figures<BR>etc.: एकीकरणम्: v. To reconcile (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recondite
RECONDITE:<BR>(1) गूढ (f. ढा), नि-;<BR>(2) गहन (f.<BR>ना = difficult, obscure: q. v.);<BR>(3) रहस्य (f.<BR>स्या): v. Secret;<BR>(4) दुर्बोध (f. धा), दुर्ज्ञेय (f.<BR>या), and sim. expr.s (= not intelligible).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reconnaissance
RECONNAISSANCE:<BR>(1) गवेषणा, -णम्;<BR>(2) परीक्षा<BR>(= examination).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reconnoitre
RECONNOITRE:<BR>(1) गवेषयति (गवेष्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) परीक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1. = to examine). Ph.:<BR>r. ing party:<BR>चाराः (= spies), Ram. vi. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reconsider
RECONSIDER: पर्यालोचयति (लोच्, c. 10.): v.<BR>To consider, again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

record
RECORD (subs.);<BR>(1) लेख्यम्<BR>or<BR>लेखः, आ-,<BR>that he<BR>delivers the r.s of Laṇkā for communicating to<BR>Indra:<BR>येन लङ्कालेख्यकमुद्धृत्य समर्पयति पुरन्दरश्रावणाय,<BR>B. r. ix.;<BR>(2) perh. अक्षः, chief r.-keeper:<BR>महाक्षपटलिकः, B. r. ix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

record
RECORD (v.):<BR>(1) लेख्ये<BR>or<BR>पत्रे निवेशयति (c. of<BR>विश्)<BR>or<BR>आरोपयति, सम्-, (c. of रुह्);<BR>(2) लिखति,<BR> अभि-, (लिख्, c. 6 = to write).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recorder
RECORDER: of London and other towns: प्राड्-<BR>विवाकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recount
RECOUNT: श्रावयति (c. of श्रु): v. To tell,<BR>narrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recourse
RECOURSE (subs.):<BR>(1) आश्रयः;<BR>(2) संश्रयः। Ph.:<BR>to have r. to:<BR>श्रयति, -ते, आ-, समुपा-, समा-, उपा-,<BR> सं-, (श्रि, c. 1.),<BR>having r. to spirit:<BR>तेजः समा-<BR>श्रित्य, Ki. xvii. 3.; will have r. to Rāma:<BR>राघवं संश्रयिष्यति, Ram.;<BR>had r. to (the forest)<BR>Naimisha:<BR>नैमिषं शिश्रिये, R. xix. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recover
RECOVER (v. t.):<BR>I To regain:<BR>(1) लभते (लभ्,<BR>c. 1. = to gain: q. v.),<BR>spoke to her when she<BR>r. ed her consciousness:<BR>लब्धचेतानामवादीत्, K.;<BR>let him r. his eye-sight:<BR>स लब्धचक्षुर्भवेत्, Mah.<BR>iii. 297. 27.;<BR>if you r. your possession:<BR>यदि<BR> लब्धा पुनरात्मनः पदम्, Ki. ii. 17.;<BR>(2) अश्नुते,<BR> सम्-, (अश्, c. 5.: rare), if (one)<BR>r. s his<BR>health:<BR>यद्यरोगितां समश्नुते, Si. xiv. 13.<BR>II To<BR>cure: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recover
RECOVER (v. i.):<BR>(1) सु(स्व)स्थ<BR>or<BR>प्रकृतिस्थ (f. स्था)<BR> भवति, Sr.;<BR>(2) आरोग्यं लभते (लभ्, c. 1.): v.<BR>Health, to gain;<BR>(3) प्रकृतिं भजते (भज्, c.<BR>1.), Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recoverable
RECOVERABLE:<BR>(1) प्रतिलभ्य (f. भ्या);<BR>(2)<BR>पुनर्लभ्य (f. भ्या);<BR>(3) gen. by लभ्य (f. भ्या),<BR>प्राप्य (f. प्या), आसादनीय (f. या), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recovery
RECOVERY:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) पुनर्लाभः;<BR>(2)<BR>पुनःप्राप्तिः;<BR>(3) better by verb.<BR>II From<BR>illness:<BR>(1) रोगसमुत्थानम्;<BR>(2) स्वास्थ्यलाभः;<BR>and sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recreant
RECREANT:<BR>I Cowardly: q. v.: कातर (f. रा).<BR>II Apostate: q. v.: धर्मभ्रष्ट (f. ष्टा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recreate
RECREATE:<BR>I Lit: v. To create, again.<BR>II To refresh, cheer: q. v.: आश्वासयति<BR>(c. of श्वश्).<BR>III To repose, rest: q. v.:<BR>विश्राम्यति (श्रम्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recreation
RECREATION:<BR>(1) विनोदः (= amusement);<BR>(2) विहारः (by walking about);<BR>(3) विश्रामः<BR>(= rest). To take r.: v. To amuse, rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recreative
RECREATIVE:<BR>(1) विनोदक (f. दिका);<BR>(2) सुखकर<BR>(f. री);<BR>(3) मनोरञ्जन (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recriminate
RECRIMINATE:<BR>(1) प्रत्यभियुंक्ते (युज्, c. 7.);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रत्यभिशंसते (शंस्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recrimination
RECRIMINATION:<BR>(1) प्रत्यभियोगः;<BR>(2) प्रत्यभिशंसनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recruit
RECRUIT (subs.): perh. नवसैनिकः and sim.<BR>comp.s.: v. Soldier, new.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recruit
RECRUIT (v.):<BR>I To supply deficiency: पुष्णाति<BR>or<BR>पोषयति, परि-, सं-, (पुष्, c. 9. and causal),<BR>r. ed her pretty parts:<BR>पुपोष लावण्यमयान् विशेषान्,<BR>Ku. i. 25.<BR>II To refresh, reinvigorate:<BR>(1) वर्धयति (c. of वृध् = increase);<BR>(2)<BR>आश्वासयति (c. of श्वस् = to cheer);<BR>(3) प्रबली-<BR>करोति (= strengthen).<BR>III Of soldiers:<BR>उत्थापयति, सम्- (c. of स्था = to raise).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rectangle
RECTANGLE: ऋजुकोणः<BR>or<BR>समकोणः चतुर्भुजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rectangular
RECTANGULAR: ऋजुकोण (f. णा)<BR>or<BR>समकोण (f. णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rectification
RECTIFICATION: शोधनम्, परि-, सं-, वि-: v.<BR>Correction, purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rectify
RECTIFY: शोधयति, परि-, सं-, वि-, (c. of शुध्):<BR>v. To correct, purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rectilinear
RECTILINEAR, RECTILINEAL: सरलरेख (f. खा)<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rectitude
RECTITUDE: शुचिता: v. Uprightness, honesty,<BR>justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rector
RECTOR:<BR>I A clergyman: *ग्रामाचार्यः, ग्रामिकः।<BR>II Of colleges etc.: नायकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rectory
RECTORY: ग्रामिकाधिकारः (province); *ग्रामिका-<BR>वासः (residence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recumbent
RECUMBENT:<BR>(1) शयान (f. ना = lying down);<BR>(2) पार्श्वशय (f. या = on the back);<BR>(3) संविष्ट<BR>(f. ष्टा = sitting down);<BR>(4) नम्र (f. म्रा = bent,<BR>low).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recur
RECUR:<BR>I To come again: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रत्यावर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) पुनर् आगच्छति (गम्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II To the mind: उदेति (इ, c. 2.<BR>= to arise).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recurrence
RECURRENCE:<BR>I Return: q. v.: प्रत्यावृत्तिः।<BR>II To the mind: उदयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recusant
RECUSANT: प्रतीप (f. पा): v. Refractory,<BR>obstinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

red
RED:<BR>I Adj.:<BR>(1) रक्त (f. क्ता);<BR>(2) लोहित<BR>(f. ता<BR>or<BR>नी);<BR>(3) रक्तवर्ण (f. र्णा) and sim<BR>comp.s;<BR>(4) शोण (f. णा = crimson);<BR>(5) अरुण<BR>(f. णा = deep r.).<BR>II Subs.: रक्तः, -वर्णः<BR>and sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

redden
REDDEN:<BR>I Intrans.:<BR>(1) रक्तीभवति;<BR>(2) लोहिता-<BR>यते, -ति, (nomi.).<BR>II Trans.:<BR>(1) रक्तीकरोति;<BR>(2) रक्तयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reddish
REDDISH:<BR>(1) आरक्त (f. क्ता);<BR>(2) आलोहित (f. ता<BR>or<BR>नी);<BR>(3) ईषद्रक्त (f. क्ता) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reddishness
REDDISHNESS:<BR>(1) आरक्तता;<BR>(2) आरक्तिमन् (m.);<BR>(3) ईषद्रक्तता; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

redeem
REDEEM:<BR>I To get back, buying back:<BR>(1)<BR>मोक्षयति, परि-, वि-, सं-, if a mortgage is not r.ed:<BR>यद्याधिर्न मोक्ष्यते, Y. ii. 39.;<BR>(2) मोचयति, वि-,<BR> परि-, सं- (c. of मुच्), the debtor should r. (it):<BR>ऋणी मोचितुमर्हति, Vri.;<BR>(3) धनं दत्त्वा मोक्षयति,<BR>etc., Mit.<BR>II To save: q. v.: मोक्षयति।<BR>III<BR>To atone for: शोधयति, परि-, सं- (c. of शुध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

redeemer
REDEEMER: मोक्षक (f. क्षिका), परि-, वि-, सं-;<BR>v. Saviour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

redemption
REDEMPTION:<BR>I Buying back:<BR>(1) मोक्षः,<BR> -णम्, परि-, वि-, सं-;<BR>(2) by circumlo.: v. To<BR>redeem.<BR>II Liberation, deliverance: q. v.:<BR>मोक्षः, -णम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

red-handed
RED-HANDED: शोणितशोणपाणि (mfn.) and sim.<BR>comp.s.: v. Bloody.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

red-hot
RED-HOT:<BR>(1) अभितप्त (f. प्ता = heated);<BR>(2)<BR>उदर्चिस् (mfn. = luminous);<BR>(3) ज्वलत् (f.<BR>न्ती = burning).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

red-lead
RED-LEAD:<BR>(1) सिन्दूरम्;<BR>(2) रक्तचूर्णम्;<BR>(3)<BR>नागसम्भवम्, A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

redness
REDNESS:<BR>(1) रक्तत्वम्, -ता;<BR>(2) रक्तिमन् (m.);<BR>(3) लौहित्यम्;<BR>(4) लोहितिमन् (m.);<BR>(5) अरुणिमन्<BR>(m. = deep r.): v. Red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

redolent
REDOLENT:<BR>(1) सुरभि (mfn.);<BR>(2) सुगन्धि<BR>(mfn.): v. Fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

redouble
REDOUBLE:<BR>r. d.:<BR>विवृद्ध (f. द्धा): v. To in-<BR>-crease, excite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

redoubt
REDOUBT (subs.): प्राकारविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

redoubtable
REDOUBTABLE: भीम (f. मा): v. Terrible,<BR>valiant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

redound
REDOUND:<BR>I To conduce, bring about: q. v.<BR>II To overflow: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

redress
REDRESS (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रति(ती)कारः;<BR>(2) प्रतिक्रियाः<BR>v. Also reparation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

redress
REDRESS (v.):<BR>(1) प्रतिकरोति;<BR>(2) समा-दधति or<BR>धत्ते (धा, c. 3.): v. Also to repair,<BR>amend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reduce
REDUCE:<BR>I Lit.: प्रत्यादिशति (दिश्, c. 6.):<BR>v. To lead.<BR>II To bring to any state:<BR>(1) नयति (नी, c. 1.), the king by r. ing (them)<BR>to the poverty of misery:<BR>प्रणीय दारिद्र्यदरिद्रतां नृपः,<BR>N. i. 45.;<BR>(2) करोति in comp.,<BR>who has r.d<BR>kings to subjection:<BR>करदीकृतभूपालः, Si. ii. 9.;<BR>(3) by circumlo.,<BR>r. d. cupid to ashes:<BR>भस्मावशेषं<BR> मदनं चकार, Ku. iii. 72.;<BR>(4) -सात्करोति, in<BR>some comp.s.,<BR>r. to ashes:<BR>भस्मसात्करोति;<BR>r. to<BR>dust:<BR>धूलिसात्करोति। To be r. d:<BR>(1) by verbs<BR>of motion: v. To become;<BR>(2) भवति- in<BR>comp.,<BR>r. d to mud:<BR>पङ्कीभवत्, N. i. 8.;<BR>r. d<BR>to ashes:<BR>भस्मीभूत (f. ता), D. s.;<BR>(3) -साद्भवति<BR>in some comp.s.<BR>III To diminish:<BR>(1)<BR>न्यूनीकरोति;<BR>(2) ह्रसयति (nomi.);<BR>(3) लघयति<BR>(nomi. = to lower).<BR>IV To order: v. To<BR>arrange.<BR>V In arith.: कथयति (= to say)<BR>and ins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reducible
REDUCIBLE:<BR>r. to ashes:<BR>भस्मसात्करणीय (f. या):<BR>v. To reduce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reduction
REDUCTION: by verb: v. To reduce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

redundance
REDUNDANCE, REDUNDANCY: आधिक्यम्: v.<BR>Excess, abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

redundant
REDUNDANT:<BR>(1) समधिक (f. का);<BR>(2) अतिरिक्त<BR>(f. क्ता): v. Excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

redundantly
REDUNDANTLY:<BR>(1) समधिकम्;<BR>(2) सातिशयम्;<BR>(3) अतिरिक्तम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reduplicate
REDUPLICATE: ph.: in monosyllabic (roots),<BR>the first (syllable)<BR>is r.d:<BR>एकाचो द्वे प्रथमस्य,<BR>Pāṇini vi. 1. 1.: v. Also to double.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reduplication
REDUPLICATION: अभ्यासः, Pāṇini vi. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

re-echo
RE-ECHO:<BR>I Trans.:<BR>(1) प्रतिध्वनयति (c. of<BR>ध्वन्);<BR>(2) प्रतिनादयति (c. of नद्): v. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">Page580</a>]<BR>echo.<BR>II Intrans.:<BR>(1) प्रतिध्वनति (ध्वन्, c.<BR>1.);<BR>(2) प्रतिनदति (नद्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reed
REED:<BR>(1) नलः (डः),<BR>a r. thicket:<BR>नड्या;<BR>(2)<BR>धमनः (rare).<BR>R. -pen:<BR>कलमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reedy
REEDY:<BR>(1) नड्वलः (ला, लं), R. xviii. 5.;<BR>(2)<BR>नड्वत् (f. ती);<BR>(3) नडप्रायः (या, यं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reef
REEF (subs.): of rocks: शिलोच्चयः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reef
REEF (v.): संहरति (हृ, c. 1.): v. To contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reek
REEK:<BR>I Subs., smoke: q. v.: बाष्पः।<BR>II Verb:<BR>वाष्पम् उद्गिरति (गॄ, c. 6.): v. To emit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reel
REEL (v.): स्खलति (स्खल्, c. 1.),<BR>r. ing at every<BR>step:<BR>पदे पदे प्रस्खलन्, P. i. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reel
REEL (subs):<BR>I For winding thread: आवापनम्।<BR>II A dance: q. v.: perh.: ताण्डवम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refection
REFECTION: पारणा: v. Meal, repast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refectory
REFECTORY: perh. भोजनशाला and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refer
REFER:<BR>I To direct for information:<BR>I r.<BR>you to the sage about it:<BR>मुनिमिदं पृच्छ<BR>or<BR>जिज्ञासस्वः<BR>he r. ed me to the letter:<BR>स मां पत्राय<BR>or<BR>पत्रदर्शने<BR> समदिक्षत्: v. To advise, ask, enquire, see.<BR>II To submit to or judge by any<BR>authority: I r. the matter to the judge:<BR>प्राड्विवाकमतज्ञानाय विषयमिमं निर्दिशामि;<BR>I r. this<BR>to the Panchayat:<BR>पञ्चकविचाराय समर्पयामि: v. To<BR>deliver, convey.<BR>III To ascribe: q. v.:<BR>आरोपयति (c. of रुह्); by circumlo.: v. Cause.<BR>IV To allude: q. v.: लक्षीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

referable
REFERABLE: expr. by circumlo.: v. To<BR>refer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

referee
REFEREE: मध्यस्थः: v. Umpire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reference
REFERENCE:<BR>I The act: expr. by circumlo.:<BR>v. To refer. Ph.:<BR>in or with r. to:<BR>उद्दिश्य,<BR> लक्षीकृत्य, etc.: v. About (III)<BR>II That<BR>which is referred to: perh. उदाहरणम्<BR>(= illustration): उद्देशः, सम्- (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refine
REFINE:<BR>I To purify: q. v.: विशोधयति (c. of<BR>शुध्).<BR>II To polish, make elegant:<BR>(1)<BR>संस्करोति (कृ, c. 8.);<BR>(2) विनयते (नी, c. 1.);<BR>(3) संशोधयति (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refined
REFINED (adj.):<BR>I Purified: संशुद्ध (f. द्धा).<BR>II Polished:<BR>(1) संस्कृत (f. ता);<BR>(2) संस्कार-<BR>वत् (f. ती),<BR>r. intellect:<BR>संस्कारवती बुद्धिः, K. ;<BR>(3) संस्कारपूत (f. ता), Ku. vii. 90.<BR>III Nice:<BR>सूक्ष्म (f. क्ष्मा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refinement
REFINEMENT:<BR>I The act: शोधनम्, वि-, सं-।<BR>II<BR>Polished manners:<BR>(1) संस्कारः;<BR>(2) विनयः;<BR>(3) शिष्टाचारः।<BR>III Subtlety, nicety: सूक्ष्मतर्कः<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refiner
REFINER:<BR>(1) शोधक (f. धिका), सं-, वि-;<BR>(2)<BR>संस्कर्तृ (f. र्त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reflect
REFLECT (v. i.):<BR>I To think over, ponder:<BR>(1) चिन्तयति, परि-, वि-, सं-, (चिन्त्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) ध्यायति, अनु-, अभि-, सं-, (ध्यै, c. 1.): v.<BR>To think, consider.<BR>II To censure: q. v.:<BR>अधिक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reflect
REFLECT (v. t.):<BR>I To throw back: प्रतिक्षिपति<BR>(क्षिप्, c. 6.).<BR>II As images: v. Reflec-<BR>-ted, be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reflected
REFLECTED, TO BE:<BR>(1) प्रतिफलति (फल्, c. 1.),<BR>being r. in the heart:<BR>हृदि प्रतिफलत्, N. iv. 13;<BR>the rays being r. d:<BR>प्रतिफलति करौघे, Si. xi. 58;<BR>(2) प्रतिबिम्बति (nomi.),<BR>are r. like bordering<BR>trees in a lake:<BR>प्रतिबिम्बन्ति सरसीव तटद्रुमाः, S.<BR>p. b.;<BR>as if the summit of the Kailāsa r. in the<BR>nocturnal Yamunā:<BR>यामिनीयमुनायां प्रतिबिम्बितमिव<BR> कैलासशिखरम्,<BR>V iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reflection
REFLECTION:<BR>I The act: expr. by verb.<BR>II The image reflected:<BR>(1) प्रतिबिम्बम्<BR>(mn.),<BR>saw his reflection in the well:<BR>कूपमध्ये<BR> आत्मनः प्रतिबिम्बं ददर्श, P.;<BR>(2) प्रतिफलम् (rare):<BR>v. Image, shadow.<BR>III Consideration,<BR>deliberation: q. v.: चिन्ता।<BR>IV Censure:<BR>q. v.: अधिक्षेपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reflector
REFLECTOR: in physic: आदर्शः (prop. mirror).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reflexive
REFLEXIVE, REFLECTIVE:<BR>I In gram.: r.<BR>verb: expr. by कर्मकर्तृवाच्यम्।<BR>II Thinking:<BR>r. faculty:<BR>धीशक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reflexively
REFLEXIVELY: in gram.: कर्मकर्तरि (loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refluent
REFLUENT:<BR>(1) perh. प्रतिस्यन्दमान (f. ना);<BR>(2)<BR>परावर्तिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reflux
REFLUX:<BR>(1) प्रतिस्यन्दः (?);<BR>(2) परावर्तः<BR>or<BR>-वृत्तिः<BR>(?);<BR>(3) ह्रासः (= decrease: of tide).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reform
REFORM (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: प्रतिसृजति (सृज्, c. 6.):<BR>v. To form, create, again.<BR>II To amend,<BR>correct: q. v.:<BR>(1) वि-शोधयति, सं-, परि-, (c. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">Page581</a>]<BR>of शुध्);<BR>(2) दुर्मतिं नाशयति (c. of नश्), छिनत्ति<BR>(छिद्, c. 7.), etc. (of men: with gen.).<BR>III To improve, remove defects: perh.:<BR>प्र-कर्षति, उत्-, (कृष्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reform
REFORM (v. i.):<BR>(1) आत्मानं विशोधयति;<BR>(2) पूतं<BR> पन्थानं भजते (भज, c. l.), Vi. iii. and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reform
REFORM (subs.): perh. संशोधनम्: v. Also<BR>reformation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reformation
REFORMATION:<BR>I Amendment, improve-<BR>-ment: q. v.:<BR>(1) संशोधनम्;<BR>(2) प्रकर्षः, -णम्।<BR>II Of one's self: expr. by circumlo.:<BR>v. Reform (v. i.).<BR>III Lit., as of an island:<BR>पुनरुत्थानम्: v. Formation, appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reformatory
REFORMATORY (subs.): *शोधनालयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reformer
REFORMER:<BR>(1) संशोधक (f. धिका: ?);<BR>(2)<BR>धर्मप्रवर्तक (f. र्तिका: of religion);<BR>(3) by<BR>circumlo.: v. To reform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refract
REFRACT: of rays: perh. परावर्तयति (c. of<BR>वृत्). To be r. ed: perh. परावर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refraction
REFRACTION: perh. परावर्तः<BR>or<BR>परावृत्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refractory
REFRACTORY:<BR>(1) प्रतीप (f. पा);<BR>(2) अविधेय<BR>(f. या): v. Also obstinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refrain
REFRAIN (v. t.): नियच्छति (यम्, c. l.): v. To<BR>restrain, control.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refrain
REFRAIN (v. i.):<BR>(1) निवर्तते (वृत्, c. l.): v.<BR>To abstain;<BR>(2) विरमति (रम्, c. l.): v.<BR>To desist, cease;<BR>(3) by v. t.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refresh
REFRESH:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) आश्वासयति, सम्- (c.<BR>of श्वस् = to cheer, comfort);<BR>(2) अभिनन्दयति<BR>(c. of नन्द् = to gladden, delight);<BR>(3)<BR>प्रह्लादयति (c. of ह्लाद् =2),<BR>Śiva r. ed them by the<BR>cooling command of not to depart:<BR>शिवः प्रह्लादया-<BR>मास तान् निषेधहिमाम्बुना, Ki. xv. 30.<BR>II To<BR>repair, restore: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refreshing
REFRESHING (adj.):<BR>(1) प्रह्लादन (f. नी): v.<BR>Delightful;<BR>(2) शीतल (f. ला): v. Cool;<BR>(3) मधुर (f. रा): v. Sweet;<BR>(4) श्रमापह (f.<BR>हा = fatigue-removing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refreshment
REFRESHMENT:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) आश्वासनम्;<BR>(2) प्रह्लादनम्: v. To refresh.<BR>II Food:<BR>q. v.: अभ्यवहारः,<BR>to take some r.:<BR>किञ्चिद् अभ्य-<BR>वहरति;<BR>r. -room:<BR>*अभ्यवहारशाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refrigeratory
REFRIGERATORY (subs.): *शीतसाधणम्; उष्ण-<BR>निर्वापणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refuge
REFUGE:<BR>(1) आश्रयः, संश्रयः,<BR>or<BR>समाश्रयः,<BR>the r. of<BR>the wits:<BR>आश्रयो रसिकानाम्, K.;<BR>take r. with<BR>enemies^1:<BR>द्विषतां यान्ति संश्रयम्, Ka. xiv. 13.;<BR>(2)<BR>शरणम्,<BR>people obtaining your r.:<BR>शरणं भवन्तमधिगम्य<BR> जनाः, Ki. xviii. 22.;<BR>r. of fire:<BR>अग्निशरणम्, Sa.<BR>iv.: v. Also shelter, abode.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refugee
REFUGEE:<BR>(1) शरणागत (f. ता);<BR>(2) शरणं प्रपन्न<BR>(f. न्ना); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refulgence
REFULGENCE: औज्ज्वल्यम्: v. Brilliancy,<BR>splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refulgent
REFULGENT: समुज्ज्वल (f. ला): v. Brilliant,<BR>splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refund
REFUND: प्रतिददाति (दा, c. 3.): v. To repay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refusal
REFUSAL:<BR>I Rejection, denial:<BR>(1) प्रत्याख्यानम्;<BR>(2) प्रत्यादेशः;<BR>(3) by circumlo.^1<BR>II Pre-emp-<BR>-tion: पूर्वक्रयाधिकारः।<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refuse
REFUSE (v.):<BR>I Not to grant, decline: न<BR> इच्छति (इष्, c. 6. = wish): v. Also to forbid.<BR>II To reject: q. v.:<BR>(1) प्रत्याख्याति (ख्या,<BR>c. 2.),<BR>if you r. me being asked:<BR>यदि मां याचितः<BR> प्रत्याख्यास्यसि, Mah. i. 74. 16.;<BR>(2) प्रत्याचष्टे<BR>(चक्ष, c. l.),<BR>I r. not for any fault:<BR>अहं<BR> प्रत्याचक्षे न दोषतः, 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refuse
REFUSE (subs.):<BR>(1) उच्छिष्टम्;<BR>(2) शेषः<BR>(3)<BR>अवशिष्टम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refutable
REFUTABLE:<BR>(1) निराकरणीय (f. या);<BR>(2)<BR>निरसनीय (f. या); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refutation
REFUTATION:<BR>(1) खण्डनम्, -ना;<BR>(2) निरासः,<BR>your attempt for its r.:<BR>भवतस्तन्निरासप्रयासः,<BR>Khaṇḍana Khaṇḍa;<BR>(3) प्रतिक्षेपः;<BR>(4)<BR>व्याक्षेपः;<BR>(5) बाधनम्<BR>or<BR>बाधा (= opposition);<BR>(6) प्रत्याख्यानम् (gainsaying).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refute
REFUTE (v.):<BR>(1) निराकरोति,<BR>r. d evidence pro-<BR>duced by a claimant by counter-evidence:<BR>वादिकृतं<BR> प्रमाणमन्यैर्निराकरोत् प्रभाणैः, Si. xx. 18.;<BR>(2) निर्-<BR>अस्यति, उत्-, व्युत्-,<BR>the weapon of the defeated is<BR>to be thus r. d:<BR>अनेन भग्नस्यास्त्रं निरसनीयम्,<BR>Khaṇḍana Khaṇḍa;<BR>(3) प्रति-क्षिपति, वि-,<BR>(क्षिप्, c. 6.),<BR>r. ing this doctrine:<BR>तमिमं पक्षं<BR> प्रतिक्षिपन्तः, D. s. vii.;<BR>(4) खण्डयति, परि-, वि-,<BR>(खण्ड, c. 10. = to break, defeat);<BR>(5) बाधते, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">Page582</a>]<BR>प्र-, (बाध्, c. l. = to oppose),<BR>as it cannot be<BR>r. d by inference etc.:<BR>अनुमानादिभिरबाध्यत्वात्,<BR>M. n. on Ki. xi. 39;<BR>(6) प्रत्याख्याति (ख्या, c.<BR>2.): v. To contradict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

refuter
REFUTER:<BR>(1) निराकर्तृ (f. र्त्री);<BR>(2) निरासकारिन्<BR>(f. णी);<BR>(3) बाधक (f. धिका);<BR>(4) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regain
REGAIN: प्रतिलभते (लभ्, c. l.): v. To gain,<BR>get, again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regal
REGAL: राजकीय (f. या): v. Royal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regale
REGALE: सन्तर्पयति (c. of तृप्): v. To satisfy,<BR>entertain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regalia
REGALIA:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) राजलिङ्गानि (n. pl.);<BR>(2) राजचिह्रानि (n. pl.); etc.<BR>II In gen.:<BR>(1) लिङ्गानि;<BR>(2) चिह्नानि;<BR>(3) लक्षणानि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regard
REGARD (v. t.):<BR>I To look at, face: q. v.<BR>II<BR>To observe, (pay) attention to: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>आद्रियते (दृ, c. 4.), where these three are r. ed:<BR>यत्रैते त्रय आद्रिताः, M. ii. 234.;<BR>(2) प्रति-ईक्षते,<BR> प्रत्यव-, (ईक्ष्, c. l.), does not r. my partisans:<BR>न मत्पक्षान् प्रत्यवेक्षते, D. viii.: v. Also to res-<BR>-pect, care.<BR>III To think, consider: q. v.:<BR>मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.).<BR>IV To have relation<BR>to: उद्दिशति (दिश्, c. 6.),<BR>r. ing the god:<BR>उद्दिश्य<BR> दिक्पतिम्, N. xiii. 14.: v. About (III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regard
REGARD (sub.):<BR>I Esteem, respect, honour:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) आदरः, सम्-;<BR>(2) प्रतीक्षा<BR>or<BR>प्रत्यबेक्षा,<BR>to those to whom you should pay r.:<BR>प्रतीक्ष्येषु, R.<BR>v. 14.<BR>II Consideration, attention, care:<BR>q. v.: अवेक्षा। Ph.:<BR>to have r. for:<BR>अवेक्षते (ईक्ष्,<BR>c. l.): v. To regard (II).<BR>III Relation,<BR>reference: Ph.: with, in r. to:<BR>(1) उद्दिश्य,<BR> सम्-;<BR>(2) अधिकृत्य;<BR>(3) प्रतीक्ष्य, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regardless
REGARDLESS:<BR>r. of:<BR>अनादृत्य, अनवेक्ष्य,<BR>or<BR>अगणयित्वा<BR>: v. Also careless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regardlessly
REGARDLESSLY: expr. by circumlo.: v. Also<BR>carelessly, negligently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regatta
REGATTA: perh. नौकाक्रीडा, -देवनम्, and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regency
REGENCY:<BR>(1) शासनम् (= government);<BR>(2)<BR>perh. शून्यपालत्वम्: v. Regent (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regenerate
REGENERATE: पुनर् जनयति (c. of जन्).<BR>To be<BR>r. d:<BR>पुनर् जायते (जन्, c. 4.).<BR>or<BR>भवति (= to<BR>become); fig. शोधयति (c. of शुध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regeneration
REGENERATION:<BR>(1) पुनर्जन्मन् (n.);<BR>(2) पुनरुत्पत्तिः;<BR>(3) पुनर्भवः;<BR>(4) पुनर्जननम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regent
REGENT:<BR>I Governor: शासकः। Ph.:<BR>r. s of the<BR>quarters:<BR>लोकपालाः, R.<BR>II. In a king's<BR>absence etc.: शून्यपालः,<BR>made you r. here:<BR>त्वां<BR> शून्यपालमिहाकरोत्, Mah. iv. 35. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regicide
REGICIDE:<BR>I The crime:<BR>(1) राज्ञो वधः, B. p.;<BR>(2) by tat. comp.<BR>II The man:<BR>(1) राजहन्<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(2) नृपधातिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) राजघः,<BR>S. k.; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regimen
REGIMEN: अन्नपानविधिः (?), C. s.: v. Diet, living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regiment
REGIMENT: वाहिनी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regimental
REGIMENTAL:<BR>I Adj.: by comp.<BR>II In pl.,<BR>r. dress:<BR>वाहिनीवेषः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

region
REGION:<BR>I Country, tract.: q. v.: देशः, प्र-,<BR>and not in this r.:<BR>न चास्मिन् प्रदेशे, K. Ph.:<BR>the lower r. s:<BR>अधोलोकः<BR>or<BR>-भुवनम्; the upper r. s:<BR>ऊर्द्ध लोकः।<BR>II Of the sky: दिश् (f.): v.<BR>Quarter.<BR>III Of the body: देशः, प्र-,<BR>umbilical r.:<BR>नाभिप्रदेशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

register
REGISTER:<BR>I Subs.: perh. पत्रिका, Raj.;<BR>*अक्षवती।<BR>II To record: *अक्षवत्यां निवेशयति<BR>(c. of विश्)<BR>or<BR>आरोपयति (c. of रुह्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

registrar
REGISTRAR: *पत्रिकाशासकः, अक्षवत्यधिकृतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

registration
REGISTRATION, REGISTRY: *अक्षवत्यां निवेशनम्;<BR> पत्रिकारोपणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regnant
REGNANT:<BR>(1) शासनकारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) शासक<BR>(f. सिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regret
REGRET (subs.): दुःखम्: v. Grief, remorse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regret
REGRET (v.): expr. by दुःखित (f. ता): v.<BR>Also to lament, grieve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regretful
REGRETFUL:<BR>(1) दुःखित (f. ता);<BR>(2) अनुतप्त<BR>(f. प्ता = remorseful).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regular
REGULAR (adj.):<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) नियत (f. ता);<BR>(2) व्यवस्थित (f. ता):<BR>(3) नियमानुवर्तिन् (f. नी)<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Symmetrical,<BR>arranged in proper order:<BR>(1) अनुपूर्व<BR>(f. र्वा);<BR>(2) अनुलोम (f. मा);<BR>(3) आनुलोमिक<BR>(f. की).<BR>III Coming in order:<BR>(1) यथाक्रम-<BR>-in comp.;<BR>(2) नैयमिक (f. की);<BR>(3) नित्य<BR>(f. त्या = constant, daily).<BR>IV Normal,<BR>proper:<BR>(1) युक्त (f. क्ता);<BR>(2) उचित (f. ता),<BR>सम्-;<BR>(3) उपपन्न (f. न्ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regularity
REGULARITY:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) नियमानुवर्तिता<BR>and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(2) व्यवस्थितत्वम्, -ता;<BR>(3) अव्यभिचारिता।<BR>II Method, uniformity:<BR>(1) क्रमः, अनु-;<BR>(2) परिपाटिः (टी);<BR>(3) व्यवस्था।<BR>III Symmetrical arrangement: expr. by<BR>adj.: v. Regular (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regularly
REGULARLY:<BR>I In due order:<BR>(1) यथाक्रमम्;<BR>(2) अनुक्रमम्;<BR>(3) अनुज्भितक्रमम्;<BR>(4) अनुपूर्वशः।<BR>II According to rule:<BR>(1) यथाविधि;<BR>(2)<BR>विधिवत्;<BR>(3) यथाविधानम्;<BR>(4) यथाविहितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regulate
REGULATE:<BR>I To adjust, arrange: q. v.:<BR>(1) संवि-दधाति<BR>or<BR>धत्ते (धा, c. 3.);<BR>(2) परि-<BR>कल्पयति, उप-, (क्ल्टप्, c. 10.).<BR>II To manage,<BR>rule: q. v.:<BR>(1) शास्ति, अनु- (शास्, c. 2.);<BR>(2) नियच्छति (यम्, c. l. = to control).<BR>III<BR>To adjust by rule: perh. व्यवस्थापयति (c. of<BR>स्था).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regulation
REGULATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) संविधानम्;<BR>(2)<BR>परि-,<BR>or<BR>उप- कल्पः, -नम्;<BR>(3) शासनम्, अनु-;<BR>(4)<BR>व्यवस्थापनम्; for dif.: v. To regulate.<BR>II<BR>Rule, law: q. v.: व्यवस्था।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

regulator
REGULATOR:<BR>(1) शासक (f. सिका), अनु-;<BR>(2)<BR>नियन्तृ (f. न्त्री), वि-, (= controller).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rehearsal
REHEARSAL:<BR>I Recital, narration: q. v.:<BR>पाठः।<BR>II Previous practice: perh. प्रयोगः:<BR>v. To rehearse (II)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rehearse
REHEARSE:<BR>I To recite, narrate: q. v.: पठति<BR>(पठ्, c. 1.).<BR>II To practise beforehand:<BR>प्रयुंक्ते (युज्, c. 7.),<BR>Bharata will have it r. d by<BR>the nymphs:<BR>भरतस्तमप्सरोभिः प्रयोजयिष्यति, U. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reign
REIGN (v.):<BR>(1) शास्ति, प्र- (शास्, c. 2.),<BR>Daśaratha r. ed at the head of the sages and r.<BR>ing (princes): दशरथः प्रशशास॥ यमवतामवताञ्च धुरि<BR> स्थितः, R. ix. 1.;<BR>(2) अवति (अव्, c. l.:<BR>rare);<BR>(3) राज्यं, भहीं, etc. शास्ति,<BR>while a<BR>Paurava is r. ing:<BR>पौरवे वसुमतीं शासति, Sa. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reign
REIGN (subs.):<BR>(1) शासनम्;<BR>(2) राज्यशासनम् and<BR>sim. comp.s.;<BR>(3) by verb, during whose r.:<BR>यस्मिन् महीं शासति, R. vi. 75.;<BR>when he was<BR>thus killed after a r. of twelve years:<BR>भुक्तक्षितौ<BR> द्वादशाब्दांस्तस्मिन् व्यापादिते तथा, Raj. iv. 686.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reimburse
REIMBURSE: gen expr. by ददाति (दा, c. 3. =<BR>to pay: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reimbursement
REIMBURSEMENT:<BR>(1) परिशोधः, -नम्;<BR>(2)<BR>निर्यातनम् (= repayment);<BR>(3) क्षतिपूरणम् (of<BR>any loss).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rein
REIN (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अभीषुः (शुः),<BR>hold,<BR>slacken the r. s:<BR>प्रगृह्यन्तां, मुच्यन्ताम् अभीषवः, Sa.;<BR>(2) प्रग्र (ग्रा) हः,<BR>I am holding the r. s:<BR>धृताः, प्रग्रहाः,<BR>Sa.;<BR>(3) रश्मिः from tightening of r. s:<BR>रश्मिसंयमनात्, Sa.;<BR>(4) वल्गा,<BR>adept in the use of<BR>r. s:<BR>वल्गाविभागकुशलः, Si. v. 60.; “उत्क्षिप्ता<BR> शिथिला तथोत्तरवती मन्दा च वैहायसी विक्षिप्तैककरार्द्ध-<BR>कन्धरसमोत्कीर्णा विभक्ता तथा । अत्युत्क्षिप्ततलोद्ध्टते खलु<BR> तथा व्यागूढगोकर्णिके वाहानाङ्कथिताश्चतुर्दशविधा वल्गा-<BR>प्रभेदा अमी ॥”, M. n.<BR>II Fig. expr. by<BR>circumlo.: v. Government, power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rein
REIN (v.): संयच्छति (यम्, c. l.): v. To<BR>control, govern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reindeer
REINDEER: वल्गाहरिणः (in Bengali) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reins
REINS (pl.): बुक्कौ (m. dual): v. Kidney.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reinstate
REINSTATE: प्रतिष्ठापयति (c. of स्था): v. To<BR>restore, place, again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reinstatement
REINSTATEMENT:<BR>(1) प्रतिष्ठापनम्;<BR>(2) by<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reinvigorate
REINVIGORATE: प्रत्याश्वासयति (c. of श्वस्): v.<BR>To refresh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reiterate
REITERATE: समभिहरति (हृ, c.1.): v. To<BR>repeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reiteration
REITERATION: समभिहारः: v. Repetition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reject
REJECT<BR>(1) प्रत्याख्याति (ख्या, c. 2.),<BR>she r. ed<BR>the gods:<BR>तया लोकपालाः प्रत्याख्याताः, Mah;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रत्यादिशति (दिश्, c. 6.), r. ed him without<BR>saying (a word): प्रत्यादिदेशैनममाषमाणा, R. vi.<BR>25.; प्रत्याचष्टे (चक्ष्, c. 2.),<BR>should not r. beds<BR>etc.:<BR>शय्यादीनि न प्रत्याचक्षीत, K. b. on M. iv.<BR>250.;<BR>(4) निर्-अस्यति, अप-, (अस्, c. 4. = to<BR>discard),<BR>the lotus r. ed bees:<BR>पद्मिनी भृङ्गं<BR> निरास, B. ii. 6.: v. To dispel, throw away;<BR>(5) अवधीरयति (= to disregard);<BR>(6) निराकरोति<BR>(कृ, c. 8. = with contumely).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rejection
REJECTION:<BR>(1) प्रत्याख्यानम्;<BR>(2) प्रत्यादेशः;<BR>(3)<BR>निराकृतिः (with contumely);<BR>(4) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rejoice
REJOICE (v. i.):<BR>(1) हृष्यति, प्र-, सम्-, (हृष्, c. 4.);<BR>(2) मोदते, प्र-, (मुद्, c. 2.);<BR>(3) प्रीयते (pass. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">Page584</a>]<BR>of प्री = to be pleased): v. To be delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rejoice
REJOICE (v. t.): हर्षयति, प्र-, सं-, (c. of हृष्): v.<BR>To delight, please.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rejoin
REJOIN:<BR>I To come again: q. v.: पुनर् एति<BR>(इ, c. 2.): v. Also to join.<BR>II To answer,<BR>reply: q. v.: प्रतिवक्ति (वच्, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rejoinder
REJOINDER: प्रतिवादः: v. Reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relapse
RELAPSE (v.):<BR>to r. into fever:<BR>पुनर्ज्वरेणाभिभूयते<BR>(pass. of भू), आक्रम्यते (pass of क्रम्), etc.;<BR>to r. into vice:<BR>पुनरपन्थानं गच्छति<BR>or<BR>उत्पथं याति<BR>etc.: v. Also to fall back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relapse
RELAPSE (subs.):<BR>(1) gen. by circumlo.;<BR>(2)<BR>पुनःपतनं<BR>or<BR>-पातः (= falling again).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relate
RELATE (v. i.):<BR>I To refer: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>उद्दिशति, सम्-, (दिश्, c. 6.);<BR>(2) संबध्यते (pass.<BR>of बन्ध्);<BR>(3) by a deriv. in ईय (f. या),<BR>the story r. ing to the hawk and the dove:<BR>श्येनकपोतीयमुपाख्यानम्, Mah. i. 2. 168.: v.<BR>About (III)<BR>II To stand in relation to:<BR>expr. by सनाभि (mfn. = r. d. by blood) or<BR>सम्बन्धिन् (f. नी = r. d by marriage): v.<BR>Relative (I), Relation (IV).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relate
RELATE (v. t.):<BR>(1) आख्याति, समा-, उपा-, अभि-,<BR>(ख्या, c. 2.),<BR>please r. it to me:<BR>तन्ममाख्या-<BR>तुमर्हसि, Mah. iii. 52. 59.;<BR>(2) वर्णयति, उप-,<BR> सम्-, अनु-, (वर्ण्, c. 10. = to describe: q. v.);<BR>(3) आ-चष्टे, सम्-, (चक्ष्, c. 2.), please r. this<BR>to (me) asking (about it): एतदाचक्ष्व पृच्छतः,<BR>Mah. iii. 99. 40.;<BR>(4) वक्ति, प्र-, (वच्, c. 2.),<BR>I will r. all this:<BR>एतत्सर्वं प्रवक्ष्यामि, Mah. iii.<BR>107. 46.: v. To say.;<BR>(5) कथयति (कथ्,<BR>c. 10.).: v. To tell;<BR>(6) श्रावयति, अनु-, (c. of<BR>श्रु = to cause to hear: with double acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relater
RELATER:<BR>(1) आख्यायक (f. यिका);<BR>(2) कथक<BR>(f. कथिका);<BR>(3) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relation
RELATION:<BR>I Narration:<BR>(1) आख्यानम्, सम्-;<BR>(2) वर्णनम्, -ना, उप-;<BR>(3) शंसनम्;<BR>(4) by verb.<BR>II Narrative: q. v.: आख्यानम्।<BR>III Refer-<BR>-ence: q. v.<BR>IV Connexion: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>सम्बन्धः (= gen.: specially of r. by marriage),<BR>closely related Rākṣasas:<BR>अभिन्नसम्बन्धा राक्षसाः,<BR>Vi. iv.; it is said r. is formed by conversation:<BR>सम्बन्धमाभाषणपूर्वमाहुः, R. ii. 58.;<BR>(2) सपिण्डता<BR>or<BR>सापिण्ड्यम् (of agnates): v. Relative (1);<BR>(3) not expr., what r. do you bear to him:<BR>कोऽस्य भवान्।<BR>V Relative (I): q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relationship
RELATIONSHIP:<BR>(1) सम्बन्धः (gen. term);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रत्यासन्नता (= near r.),<BR>among these, first of all<BR>come one's own kinsmen on account of near r.:<BR>तत्रापि प्रत्यसन्नत्वात् प्रथममात्मबन्धवः, Mit.;<BR>(3)<BR>व्यवहितता (= distant r.);<BR>(4) सनाभिता (by<BR>blood);<BR>(5) बन्धुता (= through females): v.<BR>Relative (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relative
RELATIVE:<BR>I Kinsman:<BR>(1) सपिण्ड (f. ण्डा,<BR>agnates up to the seventh degree), near r. s<BR>inherit the property of a childless (man),<BR>in<BR>their absence distant r. s:<BR>अपुत्रधनाधिकार्यासन्न-<BR>सपिण्डस्तदभावे व्यवहितः। Viv.;<BR>(2) समानोदक<BR>(f. का: 8th to 14th.), Mit.;<BR>(3) सगोत्र<BR>(f. त्रा)<BR>or<BR>गोत्रज (f. जा = of the same gotra);<BR>(4) बन्धुः<BR>or<BR>बान्धवः (through females);<BR>(5)<BR>सनाभि (mfn.: by blood);<BR>(6) ज्ञातिः (= 5);<BR>(7) सकुल्य (f. ल्या = of the same class);<BR>(8)<BR>sometimes not expr., in the absence of any r.:<BR>सर्वामावे, Mit.<BR>II Not absolute:<BR>(1) सापेक्ष<BR>(f. क्षा);<BR>(2) by circumlo. Ph.: r. knowledge:<BR>सापेक्षबुद्धिः, Par. 107.<BR>III In gram.: *सम्बन्ध-<BR>द्योतक (f. तिका) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relatively
RELATIVELY: perh. तदपेक्षया<BR>or<BR>तदपेक्ष्य: v. Also<BR>comparative (1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relax
RELAX:<BR>I Trans.: शिथिलयति (nomi.) or<BR>शिथिलीकरोति: v. To loosen, slacken, lighten.<BR>II Intrans.: शिथिलायते (nomi.)<BR>or<BR>शिथिलीभवति<BR>: v. Also to abate, decrease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relaxation
RELAXATION:<BR>I The act: शिथिलीकरणम्।<BR>II<BR>The state: शैथिल्यम्<BR>or<BR>शिथिलता: v. Also<BR>abatement, decrease.<BR>III Diversion,<BR>amusement: q. v.: विनोदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relay
RELAY (subs.):<BR>I Supply: q. v.<BR>II Of<BR>horses: expr. by circumlo.,<BR>by r. s:<BR>*मार्गस्थापितैः<BR> प्रजविभिर्हयैः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

release
RELEASE (v.): मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6 (= to free:<BR>q. v.)<BR>or<BR>मोचयति (c. of मुच् = to cause to<BR>free),<BR>the captive women being r. d:<BR>वन्दिस्त्रियो<BR> मोचिताः, Vi. vii. 5.; as I may be r. d from it<BR>(the debt): तस्मान्मुच्ये यथा॥, R. i. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

release
RELEASE (subs.):<BR>(1) मुक्तिः, वि-,<BR>obtaining r.<BR>from the king:<BR>ईश्वरान्मुक्तिमधिगम्य, N. ii. 1.;<BR>(2) मोक्षः, -णम्, वि-: v. Liberation, discharge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relent
RELENT:<BR>r. and speak:<BR>जहिहि कठिनतां प्रयच्छ<BR> वाचम्, Ki. x. 51.: v. Cruelty and abandon,<BR>soft and become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relentless
RELENTLESS:<BR>(1) कठिन (f. ना = hard);<BR>(2)<BR>निष्करुण (f. णा): v. Merciless, unkind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relevance
RELEVANCE, RELEVANCY:<BR>(1) प्रासङ्गिकता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2) सम्पर्कः (= connexion: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relevant
RELEVANT:<BR>(1) प्रासङ्गिक (f. की);<BR>(2) प्रस्तुनानु-<BR>षङ्गिन् (f. नीः ?);<BR>(3) संपृक्त (f. क्ता = connec-<BR>-ted).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reliance
RELIANCE: विश्वासः: v. Faith, trust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relic
RELIC:<BR>(1) शिष्ट (f. ष्टा), अव- (= remaining);<BR>(2) शव (mn. = corpse);<BR>(3) शरीरम् (= body:<BR>q. v.),<BR>did not burn his r.s:<BR>न चकार शरीरमग्निसात्,<BR>R. N. B. If a part of the body is referred to,<BR>expr. by it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relict
RELICT: विधवा: v. Widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relief
RELIEF:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) साहाय्यम् (= assis-<BR>-tance);<BR>(2) उद्धारः (= saving, succour);<BR>(3) परिहारः (= avoidance);<BR>(4) प्रतिकारः<BR>(= remedy);<BR>(5) उपशमः (= alleviation).<BR>II<BR>The state:<BR>(1) सुखम् (= ease, pleasure);<BR>(2) शमः (= peace, quiet).<BR>III In sculpture:<BR>*समावेशः,<BR>high r.:<BR>*उन्नतसमावेशः; base or low r.:<BR>*समसमावेशः;<BR>middle r.:<BR>अर्द्धोन्नतसमावेशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relieve
RELIEVE:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) मोक्षयति, परि-,<BR>(मोक्ष, c. 10. = to release, free: q. v.);<BR>(2)<BR>शमयति, प्र-, (c. of शम् = to alleviate, mitigate:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(3) उपकरोति (कृ, c. 8. = to help, do<BR>good to: q. v.).<BR>II To r. guards etc.:<BR>perh. मोक्षयति, परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

religion
RELIGION: धर्मः,<BR>devoid of all r.:<BR>सकलधर्मबहिष्कृत<BR>(f. ता), San. vi.: v. Also piety, theology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

religious
RELIGIOUS:<BR>I Pious: q. v.:<BR>(1) धार्मिक (f. की);<BR>(2) धर्मिष्ठ (f. ष्ठा).<BR>II Relating to religion:<BR>धर्म- in comp.,<BR>r. rite:<BR>धर्मकर्मन् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

religiously
RELIGIOUSLY:<BR>(1) धर्मपरतया;<BR>(2) better by<BR>adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

religiousness
RELIGIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) धार्मिकता;<BR>(2) धर्मिष्ठता;<BR>(3)<BR>धर्मशीलता;<BR>(4) धर्मपरायणता; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relinquish
RELINQUISH: त्यजति, परि-, सम्-, (त्यज्, c. l.)<BR>: v. To leave, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reliquary
RELIQUARY: शिष्टाधारः and sim. comp.s. (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relish
RELISH (subs.):<BR>I Taste, flavour:<BR>(1) रसः;<BR>(2) स्वादः, आ-।<BR>II Likeness, fondness: q. v.:<BR>रुचिः, अभि-।<BR>III Something eaten with food:<BR>अव- (उप-) दंशः,<BR>making two or three r. es:<BR>द्वित्रानुप-<BR>दंशानुपपाद्य, D. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relish
RELISH (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) रसयति (रस्, c. 10.),<BR>r. ing highly r. ing wine:<BR>वारुणीमतिरसां रसयित्वा,<BR>Ki. ix. 54.;<BR>(2) स्वादयति (c. of स्वद्), 55.<BR>II<BR>Fig.: रोचते, अभि-, (रुच्, c. l.: with dat. of<BR>the English nomi.),<BR>the ladies did not r.<BR>garlands:<BR>न स्रजो रुरुचिरे रमणीभ्यः। Ki. ix. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

relish
RELISH (v. i.):<BR>(1) स्वदते (स्वद्, c. l.);<BR>(2)<BR>(with subs.) रसः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reluctance
RELUCTANCE(y):<BR>(1) अनिच्छा;<BR>(2) अनिच्छुता;<BR>(3) वैमनस्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reluctant
RELUCTANT:<BR>(1) अनिच्छु (mfn.), -क (f. का);<BR>(2) विमनस् (mfn.);<BR>(3) विरक्त (f. क्ता = averse);<BR>(4) असन्तुष्ट (f. ष्टा = dissatisfied).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reluctantly
RELUCTANTLY:<BR>(1) अनिच्छया;<BR>(2) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rely on
RELY ON:<BR>(1) विश्वसिति (श्वस्, c. 2.: with<BR>loc.): v. To trust, believe;<BR>(2) समाश्रयति<BR>(श्रि, c. l.: with acc.): v. Recourse<BR>(have).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remain
REMAIN:<BR>(1) तिष्ठति, अवतिष्ठते (स्था, c. l.),<BR>will<BR>go wherever it likes or accustomed to this place<BR>will r. here:<BR>यास्यति यत्रास्मै रोचिष्यते, इहैव वा<BR> समुपजातपरिचयः स्थास्यति, K. ;<BR>the king r. ed there<BR>at night:<BR>राजा तत्रैव रात्रावतिष्ठत्, Bha.;<BR>one Gan-<BR>gadatta alone r. ed:<BR>केवलमेको गङ्गदत्तस्तिष्ठति, P.;<BR>not a point of the earth r. ed pathless:<BR>नास्थादपन्था<BR> धरणेः कणोऽपि, N. x. 2.;<BR>(2) शिष्यते, अव- (pass.<BR>of शिष्) (= to be left as a remainder), (you)<BR>r. only in words:<BR>कथासु शिष्यध्वम्, M. i. 142.;<BR>when the fame (alone) of Vikramāditya r. s:<BR>गतवति कीर्तिशेषं विक्रमादित्ये, Va.;<BR>the wives of the<BR>Vrishnis r. ing after abduction:<BR>कलत्रं वृष्णीनां हृत-<BR>शेषितम्, Mah. xvi. 7. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remainder
REMAINDER: expr. by adj.<BR>if this is deducted<BR>from three, the r. is:<BR>अथैतैर्विवर्जितानां त्रयाणां शेषम्,<BR>Li. 8.; and who (spent) two-ninths of the r. at [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">Page586</a>]<BR>Kāsi:<BR>नवलवयुगलं योऽवशेषाच्च काश्याम्, Li. 25.:<BR>v. Also rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remaining
REMAINING (adj.):<BR>(1) शेषः (षा, षं),<BR>the r.<BR>months:<BR>शेषान्मासान्, Me. ii. 25.;<BR>(2) शिष्टः (ष्टा,<BR> ष्टं), अव-,<BR>with the r. arms:<BR>शिष्टैर्दोर्मिः, Vi. vi.<BR>25.;<BR>(3) शिष्यमाण (f. णा), अव-, (rare), An.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remains
REMAINS: v. Remainder, relic, corpse, body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remand
REMAND:<BR>I To send back: q. v.: पुनः प्रेरयति<BR>(ईर्, c. 10.).<BR>II To adjourn: व्याक्षिपति<BR>(क्षिप्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remark
REMARK (v.): लक्षयति (लक्ष्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>observe, notice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remark
REMARK (subs.):<BR>(1) अनुशासनम् (?);<BR>(2) उक्तिः<BR>(= saying);<BR>(3) टीका (= note).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remarkable
REMARKABLE:<BR>(1) अपूर्व (f. र्वा): v. Singular,<BR>uncommon;<BR>(2) विख्यात (f. ता): v. Illu-<BR>-strious, famous;<BR>(3) अद्भुत (f. ता): v. Won-<BR>-derful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remarkably
REMARKABLY:<BR>(1) विशेषेण (= particularly);<BR>(2) सातिशयम्: v. Exceedingly;<BR>(3) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remediable
REMEDIABLE: प्रति (ती) कार्य (f. र्या): v. Cur-<BR>-able, to remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remelt
REMELT: पुनर्द्रवति (द्रु, c. l.: intrans.)<BR>or<BR>द्रावयति<BR>(c. of द्रु: trans.): v. To melt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remedial
REMEDIAL:<BR>(1) by subs.;<BR>(2) प्रति (ती) कारक<BR>(f. रिका): v. Also healing (adj.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remediless
REMEDILESS: अप्रति (ती) कार्य (f. र्या): v. Irre-<BR>-mediable, incurable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remedy
REMEDY (v.):<BR>(1) प्रतिकरोति (कृ, c. 8.),<BR>to r.<BR>diseases:<BR>प्रतीकाराय रोगाणाम्, Bha.;<BR>(2) शमयति,<BR> उप-, प्र-, (c. of शम् = to quiet),<BR>the rage for<BR>relishing poisonous pleasure cannot be r. d:<BR>अशाम्यो<BR> विषयविषास्वादमोहः, K. : v. Also to cure, cor-<BR>-rect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remedy
REMEDY (subs.):<BR>I Medicine: q. v.: औषधम्,<BR>poison is a r. for poison:<BR>विषस्य विषमौषधम्, J.<BR>II.<BR>Cure, alleviation: q. v.:<BR>(1) प्रति (ती) कारः,<BR>his disease has no r.:<BR>अप्रतिकारविकारोऽयम्, K. ;<BR>(2) प्रतिक्रिया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remember
REMEMBER:<BR>I To recollect: स्मरति, सं-, अनु-,<BR>(स्मृ, c. l.: with acc. or gen.),<BR>I do not r.<BR>having accepted this lady:<BR>न खलु स्वीकरणमत्रभवत्याः<BR> स्मरामि, Sa. v.; r. ing the powers of the son of<BR>Indra:<BR>अनुस्मृताखण्डलसूनुविक्रमः, Ki. i. 24.: v.<BR>Also to think of.<BR>II To keep in mind:<BR>(1) स्मरति,<BR>r. what you say:<BR>स्मरसि खल्वेतदात्मनो<BR> वचनम्, V. i.;<BR>(2) हृदये निदधाति (धा, c. 3.) and<BR>sim. expr. s, N. ii. 47.<BR>III To remind: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remembrance
REMEMBRANCE:<BR>I In gen.: स्मरणम्<BR>or<BR>स्मृतिः,<BR> सं-, अनु-,<BR>the favour of your r.:<BR>अनुग्रहं संस्मरण-<BR>प्रवृत्तम्, Ku. iii. 3.;<BR>dispelled by r.:<BR>स्मृतिभिन्न-,<BR>Sa. vii. 22.<BR>II A memorial:<BR>(1) स्मरणचिह्नम्,<BR>and sim. comp. s;<BR>(2) perh. simply स्मरणम्<BR>or<BR>स्मृतिः;<BR>(3) by adv. स्मरणार्थम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remembrancer
REMEMBRANCER: स्मारक (f. रिका). Ph.:<BR>legal<BR>r.:<BR>*स्मृतिशासकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remind
REMIND: स्मारयति, सं-, अनु-, (c. of स्मृ: with two<BR>acc.),<BR>these wild mountain sceneries r. me the<BR>Deccan mountains:<BR>एता अरण्यगिरिभूमयः स्मारयन्ति<BR>[मां] दक्षिणारण्यभूधरान्, Ma. ix.;<BR>constantly<BR>r. ing the attendants of Śiva of the conflagration<BR>of Tripura:<BR>मुहुरनुस्मरयन्तं॥ त्रिपुरदाहमुमापतिसेविनः,<BR>Ki. v. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reminiscence
REMINISCENCE: स्मरणम्: v. Remembrance,<BR>memory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remiss
REMISS:<BR>(1) अनवहित (f. ता): v. Careless,<BR>negligent;<BR>(2) शिथिल (f. ला = lack).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remission
REMISSION:<BR>I Abatement, cessation: q. v.:<BR>उपशमः।<BR>II Release, discharge: q. v.: मोक्षः।<BR>III Pardon, forgiveness: q. v.: क्षमा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remissly
REMISSLY:<BR>(1) अनवधानेन;<BR>(2) by adj.: v.<BR>Carelessly, negligently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remissness
REMISSNESS:<BR>(1) अनवधानम्;<BR>(2) शैथिल्यम्: v.<BR>Carelessness, negligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remit
REMIT (v. t.):<BR>I To send: q. v.: प्रेरयति (ईर्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR>II To forgive, pardon: q. v.:<BR>निर्वर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR>III To relax, diminish:<BR>q. v.: शिथिलीकरोति।<BR>IV To give up, surren-<BR>-der: q. v.: अर्पयति, सम्-, (c. of ऋ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remit
REMIT (v. i.): शिथिलीभवति: v. To relax, dimi-<BR>-nish, abate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remittance
REMITTANCE:<BR>I The act: प्रेरणम्: v. To<BR>send.<BR>II The thing remitted: expr. by<BR>प्रेरित<BR>or<BR>प्रेषित (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remittant
REMITTANT: विसर्गिन् (f. णी) and sim. comp. s,:<BR>v. Intermittent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remnant
REMNANT: शेष (f. षा): v. Remaining, re-<BR>-mainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remonstrance
REMONSTRANCE:<BR>(1) प्रतिवादः;<BR>(2) विरुद्धवाक्यम्;<BR>and sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remonstrate
REMONSTRATE:<BR>(1) प्रतिवादं करोति;<BR>(2) विरुद्धवाक्यं<BR> वदति (वद्, c. l.); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remorse
REMORSE:<BR>(1) अनुतापः;<BR>(2) अनुशयः;<BR>(3) अनु-<BR>शोकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remorseful
REMORSEFUL:<BR>(1) अनुतप्त (f. प्ता);<BR>(2) अनुतापयुत<BR>(f. ता);<BR>(3) अनुशयिन् (f. नी); and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remorseless
REMORSELESS:<BR>(1) कठिन (f. ना): v. Hard;<BR>(2) निर्दय (f. या): v. Merciless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remote
REMOTE:<BR>(1) दूरस्थ (f. स्था): v. Far;<BR>(2)<BR>अनासन्न (f. न्ना);<BR>(3) विप्रकृष्ट (f. ष्टा), r. cause:<BR>विप्रकृष्टं निदानम्, Bha.;<BR>still the time for awaking<BR>is very r.:<BR>अद्यापि विप्रकृष्टतमः प्रबोधकालः, Vi. vi.<BR>and sim. comp.s.: v. Near, not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remotely
REMOTELY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remoteness
REMOTENESS:<BR>(1) दूरता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2) विप्रकर्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

removable
REMOVABLE:<BR>(1) अपसार्य (f. र्या);<BR>(2) अपनेय<BR>(f. या);<BR>(3) बहिष्कार्य (f. र्या);<BR>(4) निरसनीय<BR>(f. या); etc.: v. Remove, removal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

removal
REMOVAL (subs.):<BR>I Personal:<BR>(1) स्थानान्तर-<BR>गमनम्;<BR>(2) अपसरणम्;<BR>(3) often by गमनम् etc.<BR>(= going).<BR>II Of things etc.:<BR>(1) स्थानान्तर-<BR>नयनम्;<BR>(2) अपसारणम्।<BR>III Driving away:<BR>(1) दूरीकरणम्;<BR>(2) अपनयः, -नम् (= taking away);<BR>(3) निरासः<BR>or<BR>निरसनम् (casting away);<BR>(4)<BR>निराकरणम्<BR>or<BR>-कृतिः (= expulsion);<BR>(5)<BR>निर्वासनम् (= banishment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remove
REMOVE (subs.):<BR>I Removal: q. v.<BR>II A<BR>step.: q. v.: भङ्गिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remove
REMOVE (v. t.):<BR>I To move, change place:<BR>(1) स्थानान्तरं नयति (नी, c. l.);<BR>(2) अपसारयति<BR>(c. of सृ).<BR>II To drive away, banish:<BR>q. v.: दूरीकरोति: v. Also to dismiss (II).<BR>III To take away, destroy: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>अपनयति (नी, c. l.);<BR>(2) हरति, अप- (हृ, c. l.),<BR>to r. thirst;<BR>तृष्णां हरति, Bha.;<BR>(3) नुदति, प्र- (नुद्,<BR>c. l.),<BR>r. s phlegms:<BR>कफनुत् (mfn.);<BR>(4) हन्ति,<BR> अप- (हन्, c. 2. = kill),<BR>r. s phlegms:<BR>कफापह<BR>(f. हा), Bha.;<BR>(5) विनाशयति (c. of नश् =<BR>destroy),<BR>r. s cold:<BR>प्रतिश्यायं विनाशयति, Bha.;<BR>(6) छिनत्ति, उत् (छिद्, c. 7. = cut off), r. d the<BR>doubt: वितर्कं चिच्छेद, M. n. on, Ki. iv. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remove
REMOVE (v. i.):<BR>(1) स्थानान्तरं गच्छति (गम्, c. l.),<BR>याति (या, c. 2.), etc.;<BR>(2) अपसरति (सृ, c.<BR>1.): v. To go away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remunerate
REMUNERATE: मूल्यं ददाति (दा, c. 3.): v. To<BR>recompense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

remuneration
REMUNERATION: मूल्यम्: v. Also reward, pay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

recounter
RECOUNTER: संमर्दः: v. Encounter, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rend
REND: दारयति (rarely दृणाति), वि-, परि-, अव-,<BR>rent the mountain:<BR>ददाराद्रिम्, Mah.;<BR>the<BR>thunderbolt rent that hole:<BR>वज्रं तद्विलमदारत्,<BR>Mah. i. 3. 163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

render
RENDER:<BR>I In gen.: करोति,<BR>to r. clear:<BR>विशदी-<BR>करोति, M. n.;<BR>to r. into Persian:<BR>पारसीकभाषायां<BR> करोति, Raj.: v. To make, do.<BR>II To give<BR>back: प्रतिददाति (दा, c. 3.): v. To give,<BR>return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rendering
RENDERING (subs.): i. e. translation: q. v.:<BR>expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rendezvous
RENDEZVOUS: समागम-<BR>or<BR>सङ्गमस्थानम् and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rending
RENDING (subs.): दारः, -णम्, वि-, अव-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

renegade
RENEGADE:<BR>I Apostate: q. v.<BR>II A term<BR>of abuse: पाषण्डः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

renew
RENEW:<BR>I To make again: पुनः करोति<BR>or<BR>पुनः<BR>and the corresponding verb, r. a fight:<BR>पुनर्युद्धं करोति<BR>or<BR>युध्यते;<BR>r. studies:<BR>पुनरध्यनं करोति<BR>or<BR>अधीते;<BR>r. an application:<BR>पुनः प्रार्थनां करोति or<BR>प्रार्थयते, etc.<BR>II To make new: नवीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

renewable
RENEWABLE, RENEWAL: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

renounce
RENOUNCE:<BR>I Not to own:<BR>(1) प्रत्याख्याति<BR>(ख्या, c. 2.);<BR>(2) न स्वीकरोति, अङ्गीकरोति, etc.<BR>II To forsake, abandon: q. v.: त्यजति,<BR> परि-, सं- (त्यज्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

renovate
RENOVATE: नवीकरोति: v. To renew, refresh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

renovation
RENOVATION:<BR>I The act: नवीकरणम्।<BR>II The<BR>state:<BR>(1) नवीभावः (of things);<BR>(2) प्रत्याश्वासः<BR>(of persons).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

renown
RENOWN:<BR>(1) कीर्तिः,<BR>of world-wide r.:<BR>विश्व-<BR>विख्यातकीर्तिः, D. s.;<BR>(2) ख्याति, प्र-;<BR>(3) यशस<BR>(n.): v. Fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

renowned
RENOWNED:<BR>(1) ख्यात (f. ता), वि-, प्र-;<BR>(2)<BR>विश्रुत (f. ता);<BR>(3) प्रथित (f. ता);<BR>(4) प्रसिद्ध<BR>(f. द्धा);<BR>(5) कीर्तिमत् (f. ती); यशस्विन् (f. नी);<BR>etc. (possessing renown).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rent
RENT (subs.):<BR>I Of lands: करः।<BR>II Cleft,<BR>fissure: q. v.: छिद्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rent
RENT (v.):<BR>I To grant by lease: भाटकेन<BR> ददाति (दा, c. 3.).<BR>II To take by lease:<BR>(1)<BR>भाटकेन गृह्णाति (ग्रह, c. 9.);<BR>(2) भाटयति, Viv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rental
RENTAL, RENT-ROLL: *करपत्रिका and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

renter
RENTER: expr. by verb: v. To rent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

renunciation
RENUNCIATION:<BR>I Not owning:<BR>(1) प्रत्या-<BR>ख्यानम्;<BR>(2) निराकृतिः (= rejection);<BR>II<BR>Abandonment: q. v.: परित्यागः, r. of sītā:<BR>सीतापरित्यागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repair
REPAIR (v. t.):<BR>I To restore:<BR>(1) नवीकरोति,<BR>r. ed the town:<BR>पुरं नवीचकार;<BR>(2) पूरयति, परि-,<BR>(पूर्, c. 10.: by filling up what is in-<BR>-complete);<BR>(3) संस्करोति (कृ, c. 8.: by<BR>embellishing);<BR>(4) प्रतिसंस्करोति (कृ, c. 8.).<BR>II To make amends for: पूरयति, परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repair
REPAIR (v. i.):<BR>(1) गच्छति (गम्, c. l.): v.<BR>To go;<BR>(2) समाश्रयति (श्रि, c. l.): v. To<BR>betake, (have) recourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repair
REPAIR (subs.): संस्कारः<BR>or<BR>प्रति-: v. To repair<BR>(v. t.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repairer
REPAIRER: expr. by verb: v. To repair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reparable
REPARABLE<BR>(1) पूरणीय (f. या), परि-;<BR>(2) प्रति-<BR>समाधेय (f. या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reparation
REPARATION:<BR>(1) पूरणम्, परि-: v. Compen-<BR>-sation, redress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repartee
REPARTEE:<BR>(1) व्यङ्ग्योक्तिः (?);<BR>(2) क्षिप्रोत्तरम्<BR>(= quick reply: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repast
REPAST:<BR>(1) आहारः: v. Meal;<BR>(2) भोजनम्:<BR>v. Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repay
REPAY:<BR>(1) निर्यातयति (यत्, c. 10.: lit. and<BR>fig., in good and bad sense);<BR>(2) प्रतिददाति<BR>(दा, c. 3. = to give back, return).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repayment
REPAYMENT:<BR>(1) निर्यातनम्;<BR>(2) प्रतिदानम् or<BR>प्रत्यर्पणम् (= giving back).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repeal
REPEAL:<BR>I Verb, to annul:<BR>(1) लुम्पति, वि-,<BR> अव- (लुप्, c. 6.: ?);<BR>(2) खण्डयति, परि- (खण्ड,<BR>c. 10.: ?).<BR>II Subs., abrogation:<BR>(1)<BR>लोपः, वि- अव- (?);<BR>(2) खण्डनम्, -ना, परि- (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repeat
REPEAT:<BR>I To utter again:<BR>(1) पुनर् उदीरयति<BR>(ईर्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) भूयो गदति, नि-, (गद्, c.<BR>1.);<BR>(3) द्विः (= twice) व्याहरति (हृ c. l.),<BR>as if r. ed the same thing with an echo:<BR>द्विरिव<BR> प्रतिशब्देन व्याजहार तमेवार्थम्, Ku. vi. 64; etc.:<BR>v. To utter, say, again.<BR>II To do again:<BR>(1) पुनः<BR>or<BR>भूयः करोति or by corresponding<BR>verb;<BR>(2) समभि-<BR>or<BR>समभिव्या-हरति (हृ, c. 1.).<BR>III To recite, read: q. v.: व्याहरति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repeatedly
REPEATEDLY<BR>(1) वारं वारम्;<BR>(2) भूयोभूयः;<BR>(3)<BR>पुनःपुनः;<BR>(4) मुहुः;<BR>(5) मुहुर्मुहुः;<BR>(6) अभीक्ष्णम्;<BR>(7) by frequentative verbs (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repeater
REPEATER:<BR>I Reciter: व्याहर्तृ (f. र्त्री).<BR>II<BR>A watch: *होरावादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repel
REPEL: निरस्यति (अस्, c. 4.): v. To drive<BR>away, dispel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repellent
REPELLENT (adj.):<BR>(1) क्रूर (f. रा = fierce: as of<BR>looks);<BR>(2) प्रमाथिन् (f. नी: as a r. medicine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repent
REPENT:<BR>(1) अनु-तप्यते, अनुसं-, पश्चात्-, (pass. of<BR>तप्),<BR>afterwards r.:<BR>पश्चादनुतप्यन्ते, V. iii. 3.;<BR>(2) by subs., “सञ्जातपश्चात्तापात्रभवती”, V. iii.;<BR>(3) अनुशेते (शी, c. 2.: rare);<BR>(4) अनुशोचति<BR>(शुच्, c. l. = to r. for, lament: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repentance
REPENTANCE:<BR>(1) पश्चात्तापः<BR>or<BR>अनुतापः, “पश्चात्ताप-<BR>सदृशवेषः, Sa. vi.;<BR>(2) अनुशयः, “अनुशयादनुरोदिमि<BR> चोत्सुकः”, Sa. vi. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repentant
REPENTANT:<BR>(1) सानुतापः (पा, पं);<BR>(2) पश्चात्ताप-<BR>युतः (ता, तं);<BR>(3) सञ्जातानुशयः (या, यं);<BR>(4)<BR>अनुतापिन् (f. नी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repentantly
REPENTANTLY:<BR>(1) सानुतापम्;<BR>(2) सानुशयम्;<BR>(3) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repercussion
REPERCUSSION: प्रतिधातः: v. Reverberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repertory
REPERTORY: कोषः: v. Treasury, receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repetition
REPETITION:<BR>I Reiteration:<BR>(1) पुनरुक्तिः;<BR>(2) द्विरुक्तिः;<BR>(3) by verb: v. To repeat (1).<BR>II Of acts;<BR>(1) समभिहारः;<BR>(2) समभिव्याहारः,<BR>S. k.<BR>III Recital, rehearsal: q. v.: व्याहारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repine
REPINE: परितप्यते (pass. of तप्): v. To grieve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repining
REPINING (subs.): परितापः: v. Grief, lamen-<BR>-tation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

replace
REPLACE:<BR>I Lit.: प्रतिष्ठापयति (c. of स्था): v. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">Page589</a>]<BR>To put again.<BR>II To supply the place<BR>of: पूरयति, परि-, सं-, (पूर्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

replant
REPLANT: प्रतिरोपयति (c. of रुह्): v. To plant<BR>again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

replenish
REPLENISH: संपूरयति (पूर्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>complete, finish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

replete
REPLETE: पूर्ण (f. र्णा): v. Full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repletion
REPLETION: पूर्णता: v. Fullness, satiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reply
REPLY (subs.):<BR>(1) उत्तरम्,<BR>should give a true<BR>r.:<BR>यथार्थमुत्तरं दद्यात्, Mit.; r. is of four kinds:<BR>उत्तरं स्याच्चतुर्विधम्, Kat.;<BR>(2) प्रतिवाक्यम् and<BR>sim. comp. s (to questions),<BR>that I return no<BR>r. even to you:<BR>येन भवतोऽपि नास्ति प्रतिवचनम्, V.<BR>ii.;<BR>gave no r.:<BR>प्रतिवाचमदत्त न, Si. xvi. 21;<BR>(3) प्रत्युत्तरम् (prop. to a r.), M. n. Ph.: to<BR>leave no ground for r. (i. e. to shut the<BR>mouth): निरुत्तरीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reply
REPLY (v.): उत्तरं ददाति (दा, c. 3.): v. To<BR>answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

report
REPORT (v. t.):<BR>I To inform, relate: q. v.:<BR>आवेदयति (c. of विद्).<BR>II To make a r.:<BR>to<BR>r. about an abortion:<BR>भ्रूणहत्यावृत्तान्तम् आवेदयति<BR>or<BR>प्रेरयति (ईर्, c. 10 = to send).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

report
REPORT (subs.):<BR>I Information, relation:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) आवेदनम्;<BR>(2) विज्ञप्तिः।<BR>II That<BR>which is reported:<BR>(1) वृत्तान्तः (= news,<BR>facts);<BR>(2) not expr.,<BR>your majesty will be<BR>pleased to read the r.:<BR>तद्देवः पत्रारोपितं प्रत्यक्षीकरोतु,<BR>Sa. vi.<BR>III Rumour: q. v.: वार्त्ता। Ph.:<BR>of good r.:<BR>पुण्ययशस् (mfn.): v. Fame.<BR>IV<BR>Sound, noise: q. v.: ध्वनिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repose
REPOSE (subs.): विश्रामः: v. Rest (1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repose
REPOSE (v. i.):<BR>I To rest: q. v.: विश्राम्यति<BR>(c. 4.).<BR>II To lie: q. v.: तिष्ठति (स्था, c.<BR>1.).<BR>III To rest in confidence: व्यवतिष्ठते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repose
REPOSE (v. t.):<BR>I To lay at rest: विश्रामयति<BR>(c. of श्रम्).<BR>II To entrust: q. v.: निक्षिपति<BR>(क्षिप्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repository
REPOSITORY:<BR>(1) निधिः,<BR>r. of knowledge:<BR>ज्ञान-<BR>निधिः: v. Abode;<BR>(2) कोषः (= treasury: q.v.):<BR>(3) आगारम् (= house);<BR>(4) आश्रयः (= refuge).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reprehend
REPREHEND: उपालभते (लभ्, c. l.): v. To<BR>censure, blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reprehensible
REPREHENSIBLE: उपालभ्य (f. भ्या): v. Blame-<BR>-able, culpable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reprehension
REPREHENSION: उपालम्भः: v. Censure, blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

represent
REPRESENT:<BR>I To portray, delineate: q. v.:<BR>वर्णयति (वर्ण्, c. 10.).<BR>II To describe:<BR>q. v.: वर्णयति।<BR>III To inform: q. v.:<BR>आ-वेदयति, नि-, (c. of विद्).<BR>IV To stand in<BR>the place of: भूमौ तिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.), वर्तते<BR>(वृत्, c. l.), etc.<BR>V To personate: भूमिकायां<BR> तिष्ठति, etc.,<BR>Urvasī r. ing Lakṣmī:<BR>लक्ष्मीभूमिकायां<BR> वर्तमानोर्वशी, V. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

representation
REPRESENTATION:<BR>I Delineation, descrip-<BR>-tion: q. v.: वर्णना।<BR>II Information, respect-<BR>-ful statement:<BR>(1) आवेदनम्;<BR>(2) निवेदनम्।<BR>III Image, likeness:<BR>(1) प्रतिकृतिः;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रतिरूपम्।<BR>IV Theatrical: अभिनयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

representative
REPRESENTATIVE:<BR>I Subs.: प्रतिभूः: v. Subs-<BR>-titute, agent.<BR>II Adj.: expr. by verb<BR>or deriv.,<BR>r. of the people:<BR>प्रजास्थानीय (f. या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repress
REPRESS: नियच्छति (यम्, c. l.): v. To res-<BR>-train, check.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repression
REPRESSION: नियन्त्रणा: v. Restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reprieve
REPRIEVE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: दण्डव्याक्षेपः and<BR>sim. comp.s. (??).<BR>II Respite: विश्रामः।<BR>III<BR>Reproof: भर्त्सना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reprieve
REPRIEVE (v.): expr. with व्याक्षिपति (क्षिप्,<BR>c. 6.) or by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reprimand
REPRIMAND (v.): भर्त्सयति: To reprove, cen-<BR>-sure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reprimand
REPRIMAND (subs.): भर्त्सना: v. Reproof,<BR>censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reprint
REPRINT:<BR>I Verb: पुनमुद्रयति (?).<BR>II Subs.:<BR>expr. with पुनर्मुद्रितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reprisal
REPRISAL: प्रत्यपहारः and sim. expr.s. (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reproach
REPROACH (v.):<BR>(1) गर्हयति, वि-, परि-, (गर्ह्,<BR>c. 10.);<BR>I r. ed the garland:<BR>तामेकावलीमगर्हयम्,<BR>K. ;<BR>(2) उपालभते (लभ्, c. l.), (that you may)<BR>not be reviled by elders, r. ed by your friends:<BR>न धिक् क्रियसे गुरुभिः, नोपालभ्यसे सुहृद्भिः, K. ;<BR>(3)<BR>आक्रोशति (क्रुश्, c. l. = to cry against),<BR>surely<BR>the birds r. ed him with (their) cries:<BR>खगास्तमाचुक्रुशु-<BR>रारवैः खलु, N. i. 128.: v. censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reproach
REPROACH:<BR>I Censure, reviling:<BR>(1) उपा- [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">Page590</a>]<BR>-लभ्मः;<BR>(2) तिरस्कारः;<BR>(3) अधिक्षेपः;<BR>(4) धिक्-<BR>कारः;<BR>(5) गर्हणम्, -णा।<BR>II A disgrace: कलङ्कः:<BR>v. Also scandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reproachful
REPROACHFUL:<BR>I Opprobrious:<BR>(1) by comp.,<BR>r. speech:<BR>आक्षेपवचः, Ki. xiv. 25.; तिरस्कार-<BR>वचनम्, M. n.;<BR>(2) अधिक्षेपक (f. पिका) and<BR>sim. deriv. (rare).<BR>II Shameful, vile: q. v.:<BR>गर्हित (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reproachfully
REPROACHFULLY:<BR>I Opprobriously:<BR>(1) साधि-<BR>क्षेपम्;<BR>(2) सोपालम्भम्;<BR>(3) by verb.<BR>II<BR>Shamefully:<BR>(1) गर्हितम्;<BR>(2) better by<BR>adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reprobate
REPROBATE (adj.):<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) खण्डितवृत्त<BR>(f. त्ता);<BR>(2) दुराचार (f. रा);<BR>(3) असाधु (f.<BR>also ध्वी);<BR>(4) पापात्मन् (mfn.); etc.<BR>II Of<BR>acts etc.:<BR>(1) दुष्ट (f. ष्टा): v. Vicious;<BR>(2)<BR>अशुद्ध (f. द्धा = impure).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reprobate
REPROBATE (v.): निराकरोति (कृ, c. 8.): v.<BR>To condemn, reject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reprobation
REPROBATION: निराकृतिः<BR>or<BR>-क्रिया: v. Condem-<BR>-nation, censure, rejection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reproduce
REPRODUCE:<BR>(1) प्रत्युत्पादयति (c. of पद्);<BR>(2)<BR>पुनर् जनयति (c. of जन्); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reproduction
REPRODUCTION:<BR>(1) प्रत्युत्पत्तिः;<BR>(2) पुनर्मिलनम्;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reproductive
REPRODUCTIVE: v. Generative, productive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reproof
REPROOF:<BR>(1) भर्त्सना;<BR>(2) धिक्कारः: v. Cen-<BR>-sure, reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reprove
REPROVE:<BR>(1) भर्त्सयति, -ते, निर्-, सम्- (भर्त्स्, c.<BR>10.);<BR>(2) उपालभते, सम्-, (लभ्, c. l.): v. To<BR>censure, reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reprover
REPROVER: expr. by verb: v. Censurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reptile
REPTILE:<BR>(1) सर्पजातिः;<BR>(2) सरीसृपः: v. Also<BR>snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

republic
REPUBLIC: *प्रजातन्त्रम्; प्रजाराज्यम् (comp. L. iii.<BR>“तेषां॥।नोच्चमध्यवृद्धज्येष्ठानुपालिता । एकैक एव मन्य-<BR>तेऽहं राजाहं राजेति”).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

republican
REPUBLICAN:<BR>I Belonging to a republic:<BR>expr. by comp.<BR>II = subs., of men: *प्राजातन्त्र<BR>(f. न्त्री); प्रजातन्त्रानुग (f. गा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

republicanism
REPUBLICANISM: प्रजातन्त्रानुरागः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

republication
REPUBLICATION: perh. पुनःप्रकाशः and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repudiate
REPUDIATE: प्रत्याख्याति (ख्या, c. 2.): v. To<BR>reject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repudiation
REPUDIATION: प्रत्याख्यानम्: v. Rejection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repugnance
REPUGNANCE (v.):<BR>(1) विरागः: v. Aversion;<BR>(2) द्वेषः: v. Hatred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repugnant
REPUGNANT:<BR>(1) विरुद्ध (f. द्धा = opposed to,<BR>contrary);<BR>(2) प्रतीप (f. पा = disagreeable,<BR>perverse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repugnantly
REPUGNANTLY:<BR>(1) विरक्त (f. क्ता = with aver-<BR>-sion);<BR>(2) प्रतीपम् (= with opposition, per-<BR>-versely).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repulse
REPULSE:<BR>I Verb: निराकरोति (कृ, c. 8.): v.<BR>To drive away.<BR>II Subs.: निराकृतिः<BR>or<BR>निरा-<BR>क्रिया: v. Rejection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repulsion
REPULSION: निराकरणम्: v. Repulse, rejection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repulsive
REPULSIVE: Fig.:<BR>(1) क्रूर (f. रा = fierce);<BR>(2)<BR>अप्रिय (f. या = unpleasant);<BR>(3) द्विष्ट (f. ष्टा =<BR>hated).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reputable
REPUTABLE: मान्य (f. न्या): v. Respectable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reputably
REPUTABLY:<BR>(1) by circumlo.;<BR>(2) सुष्ठु (=<BR>well).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reputation
REPUTATION, REPUTE (subs.):<BR>I Fame, re-<BR>-nown: q. v.: कीर्तिः।<BR>II Estimation, regard:<BR>of bad r.:<BR>दुष्कीर्तिमत् (f. ती); better by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

repute
REPUTE (v.): मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.): v. To<BR>regard, consider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

request
REQUEST (v.): प्रार्थयते (अर्थ्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>ask (II), beg, entreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

request
REQUEST (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रार्थना<BR>or<BR>अभ्यर्थना, r. s to<BR>stronger (men)<BR>end in evils:<BR>प्रार्थनाधिकबले विपत्फला,<BR>Ki. xiii. 61.;<BR>(2) याच्ञा,<BR>it is better that a r.<BR>to a good man is unsuccessful:<BR>याच्ञा मोघा<BR> वरमधिगुणे, Me. i. 6.;<BR>(3) याचितम्, प्र- (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

require
REQUIRE:<BR>I To ask, demand: q. v.: प्रार्थयते।<BR>II To need, call for: अपेक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. l.),<BR>r. s you as the best cause:<BR>अपेक्षते प्रत्ययमुन्त्तमं त्वाम्,<BR>Ku. iii. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

requirement
REQUIREMENT: expr. by verb,<BR>all her r. s were<BR>supplied:<BR>यदेव वव्रे तदपश्यदाहृतम्, R. iii. 6.: v.<BR>Requisition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

requisite
REQUISITE:<BR>(1) आवश्यकीय (f. या = necessary:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(2) by verb: v. To require (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

requisition
REQUISITION:<BR>(1) अनुयोगः (= demand);<BR>(2) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">Page591</a>]<BR>प्रार्थना (= request). Ph.:<BR>to be in r.:<BR>अपेक्षते:<BR>v. To require.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

requital
REQUITAL:<BR>I Retaliation, punishment:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रति (ती) कारः;<BR>(2) प्रतिक्रिया।<BR>II Reward, com-<BR>-pensation: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

requite
REQUITE:<BR>I To retaliate, punish: q. v.:<BR>प्रतिकरोति।<BR>II To reward, repay: निर्यातयति<BR>(c. of यत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rescind
RESCIND: खण्डयति (खण्ड्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>repeal, cancel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rescript
RESCRIPT: शासनम्: v. Edict, command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rescue
RESCUE (v.): मोचयति<BR>or<BR>मोक्षयति, परि-, वि-, निर्-<BR>(मुच् and मोक्ष्, c. 10.),<BR>was r. d by you:<BR>त्वया<BR> मोचितः, Mr. x.: v. Also to save.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rescue
RESCUE (subs.):<BR>(1) मुक्तिः<BR>or<BR>मोक्षः, परि-, वि-;<BR>(2) उद्धारः, सम्-: v. Also release, deliverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

research
RESEARCH (subs.):<BR>(1) गवेषणम्, -णा;<BR>(2) गवे-<BR>षितम्: v. Also search.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resemblance
RESEMBLANCE:<BR>(1) सादृश्यम्,<BR>r. between them and<BR>Rāma:<BR>रामस्य तयोश्च सादृश्यम्, R. xv. 67.;<BR>so<BR>close r. that it cannot be ascertained:<BR>ईदृशं सौसा-<BR>दृश्यं येन न ज्ञायते, Na. ii.;<BR>(2) सारूप्यम्<BR>or<BR>सरूपता,<BR>your excellences bear our r.:<BR>गुणास्त्वदीया नः सरूपतां<BR> मजन्ते, Ki. iii. 42.;<BR>(3) साधर्म्यम्<BR>or<BR>सधर्मता (in<BR>qualities), (the only) r. in imitating me is (your)<BR>great enmity:<BR>साधर्म्यं मदनुकृतेः प्रधानवैरम्, Mu. iii.<BR>12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resemble
RESEMBLE: expr. by adj. or subs.: v. Like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resembling
RESEMBLING: सदृशः (शा, शं): v. Like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resent
RESENT: कुप्यति (कुप्, c. 4.): v. (To be)<BR>angry, indignant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resentful
RESENTFUL: क्रोधशील (f. ला) and sim. comp. s:<BR>v. Angry, irritable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resentment
RESENTMENT: मन्युः: v. Anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reservation
RESERVATION:<BR>I Keeping back, concealing:<BR>(1) संवृतिः;<BR>(2) संवरणम्।<BR>II Exception, res-<BR>-triction: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reserve
RESERVE (v.):<BR>I To keep, retain: q. v.:<BR>रक्षति (रक्ष्, c. 1.).<BR>II To except: q. v.:<BR>वर्जयति (वृज्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reserve
RESERVE (subs.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) संवृतिः,<BR>r.<BR>only disclose one's affections:<BR>कथयति संवृतिरेव<BR> कामितानि, Ki. x. 44.;<BR>r. d mind:<BR>संवृतिमन्मनः,<BR>Si. xv. 11.;<BR>(2) संवरणम्, it is (his)<BR>r.:<BR>संवरणं<BR> हि तत्, Mal. i. Ph.:<BR>without r.:<BR>विवृतम्;<BR>(3)<BR>संकोचः, M. n. on Si. vi. 74;<BR>(4) आशङ्का<BR>(= apprehension),<BR>without r.:<BR>समुद्ध्टताशङ्कम्, Si.:<BR>v. Also openly.<BR>II Of troops: परि (प्रति) ग्रहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reserved
RESERVED (adj.): In disposition: संवृतिमत् (f.<BR>ती) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reservoir
RESERVOIR:<BR>(1) जलाशयः;<BR>(2) तडागः: v. Tank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reside
RESIDE: वसति (वस्, c. l.): v. To dwell,<BR>remain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

residence
RESIDENCE:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) वासः, नि-;<BR>(2)<BR>स्थितिः (= stay). Ph.:<BR>r. abroad:<BR>प्रवासः।<BR>II<BR>The place.:<BR>(1) वासः, नि-;<BR>(2) वसतिः;<BR>(3)<BR>वासभूमिः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resident
RESIDENT:<BR>(1) by deriv., r. of this, that place:<BR>इहत्य, तत्रत्य (f. त्या);<BR>(2) निवासिन् (f. नी): v.<BR>Inhabitant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

residuary
RESIDUARY: अवशिष्ट (f. ष्टा): v. Remaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

residue
RESIDUE: शेषः: v. Remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resign
RESIGN:<BR>I To give up, surrender: अर्पयति,<BR> सम्-, (c. of ऋ).<BR>II To relinquish, abandon:<BR>q. v.: त्यजति, परि-, (त्यज्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resignation
RESIGNATION:<BR>I Relinquishment, abandon-<BR>-ment: q. v.: त्यागः, परि-।<BR>II Giving up,<BR>yielding: (आत्म-) अर्पणम्, सम्-: v. Also sub-<BR>-mission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resin
RESIN:<BR>(1) अरालः<BR>or<BR>रालः;<BR>(2) धूनकः;<BR>(3) सर्ज-<BR>रसः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resinous
RESINOUS: expr. by comp. or deriv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resist
RESIST:<BR>(1) प्रतिकूलयति (nomi.): v. To oppose;<BR>(2) बाधते, प्र।, (बाध्, c. l.): v. To obstruct;<BR>(3) निवारयति, वि-, (c. of वृ): v. To hinder;<BR>(4) प्रत्यवतिष्ठते (स्था, c. l.): v. To withstand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resistance
RESISTANCE:<BR>(1) प्रतिरोधः (= opposition);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रतिघातः (= striking against, as of forces);<BR>(3) निवारणम् (= hindrance);<BR>(4) प्रत्यवस्थानम्<BR>or<BR>-स्थितिः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resistless
RESISTLESS:<BR>(1) अनिवार्य (f. र्या);<BR>(2) दुर्निवार<BR>(f. रा), Si. xiv. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resistlessly
RESISTLESSLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resolute
RESOLUTE:<BR>(1) स्थिरनिश्चय (f. या), a r. mind:<BR>स्थिरनिश्चयं मनः, Ku. v. 5.;<BR>(2) स्थिरमति (mfn.);<BR>(3) दृढसंकल्प (f. ल्पा); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resolutely
RESOLUTELY:<BR>(1) expr. by adj.;<BR>(2) दृढम्<BR>(= firmly);<BR>(3) साग्रहम् (= obstinately).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resolution
RESOLUTION:<BR>I Dissolution, analysis: विश्लेष-<BR>णम् (?).<BR>II Solution, explanation: q. v.<BR>III Firmness, constancy: q. v.: स्थैर्यम्।<BR>IV Determination, resolve:<BR>(1) निश्चयः,<BR>it<BR>is my firm r.:<BR>एष मे स्थिरो निश्चयः, Mu. i.;<BR>(2)<BR>सर्गः (rare), take up arms if this is your r.:<BR>गृहाण शस्त्रं यदि सर्ग एष ते, R. iii. 51.:<BR>V Deci-<BR>-sion: निर्णयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resolvable
RESOLVABLE: विश्लेषणीयः (या, यं) (?): v. To<BR>resolve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resolve
RESOLVE (subs.): v. Resolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resolve
RESOLVE (v. t.):<BR>I To dissolve, analyze: no<BR>prop. equiv.:<BR>(1) विश्लेषयति (c. of श्लिष् ?);<BR>(2) विद्रावयति (c. of द्रु = to melt: q. v.).<BR>II<BR>To solve, explain: q. v.: व्याकरोति (कृ, c.<BR>8.).<BR>III In music: perh. भिन्नी-<BR>or<BR>भिन्नकी-<BR>करोति, Si. xi. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resolve
RESOLVE (v. i.):<BR>I To determine: q. v.:<BR>निश्चयं करोति।<BR>II To pass a resolution:<BR>perh. व्यवस्यति (सो, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resonant
RESONANT:<BR>(1) मुखरित (f. ता),<BR>the quarters r.<BR>with bees:<BR>अलिमालामुखरितककुभः, Ma. i. 1.;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रतिध्वनित (f. ता);<BR>(3) प्रति-<BR>or<BR>अनु- नादिन् (f.<BR>नी): v. To echo, sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resort
RESORT (v.): सेवते, उप-, परि-, सं-, नि-, (सेव्, c.<BR>1.),<BR>sometimes r. ed to drink:<BR>कदाचित् पानमसेवत,<BR>R. ; the forest r. ed to by barbarians and robbers:<BR>वनं म्लेच्छतस्करसेवितम्: v. To (have) recourse,<BR>frequent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resort
RESORT (subs.):<BR>(1) expr. by verb;<BR>(2) शरणम्<BR>(= refuge).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resound
RESOUND (v. i.):<BR>(1) प्रति-नदति (नद्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To echo;<BR>(2) ध्वनति (ध्वन्। c. 1.): v.<BR>To sound. Ph.: r. ing (adj.): v. Resonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resource
RESOURCE:<BR>I Means, remedy: q. v.: उपायः।<BR>II In pl., fortune, affluence: q. v.: विभवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

respect
RESPECT:<BR>I To honour: q. v.:<BR>(1) संमानयति<BR>(c. of मन्);<BR>(2) गौरवेण पश्यति (दृश्, c. 1. =<BR>look upon with r.),<BR>he was highly r. ed:<BR>गौरवेण<BR> ददृशेतरामसौ, Si. xiv. 42.<BR>II To regard,<BR>relate; q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

respect
RESPECT (subs.):<BR>I Reference: Ph.: with r.<BR>to: v. R. ing.<BR>II Honour, regard:<BR>(1)<BR>सम्मानः (= honour);<BR>(2) आदरः (= attention,<BR>consideration;<BR>(3) गौरवम् (= reverence);<BR>(4) पूजा<BR>or<BR>अर्चना (= adoration).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

respectability
RESPECTABILITY:<BR>(1) माननीयता;<BR>(2) पूजनीयता;<BR>(3) पूजार्हता; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

respectable
RESPECTABLE:<BR>I Honourable:<BR>(1) माननीय (f.<BR>या);<BR>(2) मान्य (f. न्या);<BR>(3) पूजनीय (f. या);<BR>(4) पूज्य (f. ज्या);<BR>(5) अर्चनीय (f. या).<BR>II<BR>Moderate: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

respectably
RESPECTABLY:<BR>r. dressed:<BR>आर्यवेष (f. षा);<BR>r.<BR>connected:<BR>पूज्यसम्बन्ध (f. न्धा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

respectful
RESPECTFUL:<BR>(1) विनीत (f. ता);<BR>(2) सादर (f.<BR>रा);<BR>(3) सगौरव (f. वा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

respectfully
RESPECTFULLY:<BR>(1) सविनयम्;<BR>(2) सगौरवम्, B.<BR>xii. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

respecting
RESPECTING: उद्दिश्य, r. the regent of the quarter:<BR>दिक्पतिमुद्दिश्य, N. xiii. 15.: v. About (III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

respective
RESPECTIVE:<BR>I Each to each: expr. by doub-<BR>-ling words meaning<BR>own, let the employees<BR>also attend to their r. works:<BR>स्वे स्वे कर्मण्यथ<BR> समवधत्ताप्यधिकृताः, Vi. vii. 37.<BR>II Relative:<BR>q. v.<BR>III Careful: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

respectively
RESPECTIVELY:<BR>I As relating to each: expr.<BR>as above.<BR>II According to position:<BR>(1)<BR>पौर्वापर्येण;<BR>(2) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

respiration
RESPIRATION:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) श्वासः;<BR>(2)<BR>श्वासप्रश्वासः।<BR>II Resurrection: उज्जीवनम्, प्रति-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

respire
RESPIRE:<BR>I To breathe: q. v.: श्वसिति (श्वस्,<BR>c. 2.).<BR>II To inhale: q. v.: आचामति (चम्,<BR>c. 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

respiratory
RESPIRATORY: श्वास- in comp. (?) or by cir-<BR>-cumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

respite
RESPITE:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) विलम्बः (= delay:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(2) विरामः (= pause: q. v.).<BR>II<BR>Verb.:<BR>(1) अवकाशं ददाति (दा, c. 3.);<BR>(2)<BR>by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resplendence
RESPLENDENCE: औज्ज्वल्यम्: v. Brilliancy,<BR>brightness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resplendent
RESPLENDENT: समुज्ज्वलः (ला, लं): v. Brilli-<BR>-ant, splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resplendently
RESPLENDENTLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

respond
RESPOND:<BR>I To answer, reply: q. v.: प्रति-<BR>वाचं ददाति (दा, c. 3.).<BR>II To suit.: q. v.<BR>III To pay: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

respondent
RESPONDENT:<BR>I One who answers: प्रतिवक्त्ट<BR>(f. क्त्री).<BR>II In law: प्रतिवादिन् (f.<BR>नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

response
RESPONSE:<BR>I An answer:<BR>(1) प्रत्युक्तिः;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रतिवादः (in disputation):<BR>II Of an oracle:<BR>समादेशः।<BR>III An anthem; सूक्तम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

responsibility
RESPONSIBILITY:<BR>(1) भारः<BR>or<BR>भरः (= burden),<BR>to throw r.:<BR>भरं नस्यति, Ra.;<BR>(2) दायः (used<BR>in Bengali): v. Also obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

responsible
RESPONSIBLE:<BR>I Accountable: दायिन् (f. नी)<BR>(used in Bengali) or by circumlo.<BR>II Subs-<BR>-tantial, able to pay: समर्थः (र्था, र्थं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

responsive
RESPONSIVE:<BR>I Able or ready to respond:<BR>expr. by verb.<BR>II Corresponding: संवादिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

responsively
RESPONSIVELY: expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rest
REST (subs.):<BR>I Repose:<BR>(1) विश्रामः,<BR>and let<BR>this bow get r.:<BR>विश्रामं लभतामिदं च धनुः, Sa. ii.<BR>6.;<BR>(2) विश्रान्तिः (rare),<BR>your majesty also gets<BR>r. in the sixth portion of the day:<BR>षष्ठे काले<BR> त्वमपि लभसे देव विश्रान्तिमह्नः, Vi. ii. 1.;<BR>(3) विश्रमः<BR>(rare). “पश्चात्पुत्रैरुपहितभरः कल्पते विश्रमाय”,<BR>V<BR>iii. 1.<BR>II In music: यतिः।<BR>III Support,<BR>prop.: अवलम्बः, -नम्।<BR>IV Remainder:<BR>(1)<BR>अवशिष्ट (f. ष्टा): v. Remaining, remainder;<BR>(2) अन्ये (= others: in contrasting two).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rest
REST (v. i.):<BR>I To repose:<BR>(1) विश्राम्यति (श्रम्,<BR>c. 4.),<BR>r. one day, return next morning:<BR>एकमहो<BR> विश्रम्य श्वोभूते प्रत्यागमिष्यसि, K. ;<BR>r. ed in the cool<BR>shade of rose-apple tree:<BR>जम्बूवृक्षस्य शीतलच्छायायां<BR> विशश्राम, Va.;<BR>(2) विश्रामं करोति।<BR>II To lean:<BR>(1) अव-लम्बते, समा- (लम्ब्, c. 1.: with acc.);<BR>(2) आ-श्रयति, -ते, उपा-, समा-, सम्, (श्रि, c. 1.),<BR>the arm of Rāma on which no other (woman)<BR>r. ed:<BR>रामबाहुरनुपाश्रिनोऽन्यया, U. i. 37.<BR>III To<BR>stand, lie: q. v.: तिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.).<BR>IV<BR>With on or with = depend on: q. v.:<BR>V To<BR>rely: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rest
REST (v. t.):<BR>I To cause to repose: विश्रामयति<BR>(c. of श्रम्), r. the yoked (horses): धूर्यान्विश्रामय,<BR>R. i. 54.<BR>II To place: q. v.: स्थापयति (c.<BR>of स्था).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resting-place
RESTING-PLACE: विश्रामस्थानम् and sim. comp. s<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restitution
RESTITUTION:<BR>(1) पुनरवाप्तिः and sim. comp.s.<BR>(= getting back);<BR>(2) उद्धारः सम्- (= deli-<BR>-verance, release).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restive
RESTIVE:<BR>(1) दुश्चेष्टित (f. ता: as a r. horse),<BR>M. n. on Si. v. 11.;<BR>(2) दुष्ट (f. ष्टा = vicious:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(3) उन्मार्गप्रस्थित (f. ता = going astray),<BR>M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restiveness
RESTIVENESS:<BR>(1) दुश्चेष्टितता;<BR>(2) दुष्टता;<BR>(3)<BR>better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restless
RESTLESS:<BR>I Unquiet, uneasy:<BR>(1) व्याकुल<BR>(f. ला = agitated);<BR>(2) चञ्चल (f. ला = mov-<BR>-ing about);<BR>(3) विह्वल (f. ला = distressed),<BR>my mind is r.:<BR>मनो मे विह्वलति, Gi.<BR>II Afford-<BR>-ing no rest: expr. by circumlo.,<BR>passed a r.<BR>night:<BR>उत्सन्ननिद्रां क्षपां क्षपितवती, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restlessly
RESTLESSLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restlessness
RESTLESSNESS:<BR>(1) व्याकुलता;<BR>(2) चञ्चलता;<BR>(3)<BR>विह्वलता;<BR>(4) अप्रशान्तिः (= want of quiet): v.<BR>Restless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restoration
RESTORATION:<BR>I In gen.: expr. by verbs<BR>given under restore or cor. subs.<BR>II Re-<BR>-covery: q. v.: समुत्थानम्।<BR>III In English<BR>history: *प्रतिष्ठापनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restorative
RESTORATIVE:<BR>(1) बल्य (f. ल्या), Sr.;<BR>(2)<BR>बलवर्धन (f. नी); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restore
RESTORE:<BR>(1) often expr. by पुनर्लभते (लभ्, c.<BR>1.), अवाप्नोति (आप्, c. 5.), etc. (= to get<BR>back = be r. d),<BR>and Puru was r. d to his former<BR>youth:<BR>यौवनं प्रतिपेदे च पुरुः स्वं पुनरात्मनः, Mah. i.<BR>83. 18.;<BR>let the king be r. d to his sight and<BR>strength:<BR>स लब्धचक्षुर्बलवान् भवेन्न्टपः, Mah. iii.<BR>297. 27.; r. d to life (lit. form): प्रतिपन्नमूर्ति<BR>(mfn.), Ku. vii. 92.;<BR>(2) प्रतिददाति<BR>or<BR>पुनर्<BR> ददाति (दा, c. 3.) and sim. comp.s. (= to<BR>give back);<BR>(3) नवीकरोति (= repair: q. v.),<BR>(4) प्रत्यानयति (नी, c. 1. = to bring back:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(5) उद्धरति (हृ, c. 1. = to save, free:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restorer
RESTORER:<BR>(1) प्रतिपादक (f. दिका);<BR>(2) प्रतिदातृ<BR>(f. त्री); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restrain
RESTRAIN:<BR>(1) निगृह्णाति, वि-, सं-, (ग्रह्, c. 9.),<BR>r. ing anger by patience:<BR>कोपं क्षमया निगृह्णन्, B.<BR>xii. 81.;<BR>(2) यन्त्रयति, नि-, विनि-, सं-, (यन्त्र्, c.<BR>10.),<BR>I have r. ed my tongue so much:<BR>एवं मया<BR> जिह्वा संयन्त्रिता, V. ii.;<BR>(3) यच्छति, नि-, सं-, विनि-<BR>-(यम्, c. l.),<BR>come and r. my horses:<BR>एहि, मे त्वं<BR> हयान् यच्छ, Mah. iv. 38. 48.;<BR>(4) रुणद्धि, नि-,<BR> सं-, अव-, (रुध्, c. 7. = to stop, oppose),<BR>whose<BR>motion cannot be r. ed:<BR>असंरुद्धगति (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restrainer
RESTRAINER:<BR>(1) नियन्तृ (f. न्त्री);<BR>(2) निग्रहीतृ<BR>(f. त्री); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restraint
RESTRAINT:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) यमः, सं-, नि-;<BR>(2)<BR>नि-यन्त्रणम्, -णा, वि-, सं-;<BR>(3) निग्रहः;<BR>(4) रोधः,<BR> सं-, अव-, नि-।<BR>II Restriction: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restrict
RESTRICT: निरुणद्धि (रुध्, c. 7.),<BR>when my ac-<BR>tions are thus r. ed by you on all sides:<BR>आर्येणैवं<BR> सर्वतो निरुद्धचेष्टाप्रसरस्य, Mu. iii.: v. Also to<BR>restrain, limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restriction
RESTRICTION:<BR>(1) निरोधः: v. Restraint;<BR>(2)<BR>सीमा: v. Limit. Ph.:<BR>without r.:<BR>यथेच्छम्,<BR>(= at pleasure).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

restrictive
RESTRICTIVE:<BR>(1) निरोधिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) by<BR>verb or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

result
RESULT (subs.):<BR>(1) परिणामः,<BR>this is the unfor-<BR>tunate r. of my quietude:<BR>एष मे प्रशमस्य कर्कशः<BR> परिणामः, Vi. iii.;<BR>(2) फलम्: v. Consequence,<BR>fruit;<BR>(3) सिद्धान्तः (r. of reasoning).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

result
RESULT (v. i.): उत्पद्यते (पद्, c. 4.),<BR>r. ing from<BR>the murder of Parvataka:<BR>पर्वतकवधोत्पन्न (f. न्ना),<BR>Mu. i.: v. To proceed (III);<BR>(2) परि-<BR>णमते, वि-, (नम्, c. l. = to terminate),<BR>it r. s<BR>from his own misdeeds:<BR>आत्मन एव दुश्चरितमेतद्वि-<BR>परिणमयति, Vi. vii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resume
RESUME (subs.): सारः<BR>or<BR>सारसंग्रहः: v. Also<BR>epitome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resume
RESUME (v.): पुनर्<BR>or<BR>भूय आदत्ते (दा, c. 3.): v.<BR>To take again. Ph.:<BR>to r. an argument or<BR>discourse:<BR>प्रकृतमनुसरति (सृ, c. l. = to follow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resumption
RESUMPTION:<BR>(1) प्रत्याहारः;<BR>(2) पुनरादानम् and<BR>sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resurrection
RESURRECTION:<BR>(1) उज्जीवनम्, प्रति-;<BR>(2) मृतो-<BR>त्थानम् after Ku. vii. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resuscitated
RESUSCITATED:<BR>(1) उत्-जीवयति, सं-, प्रत्युत्- (c.<BR>of जीव्), the animal kingdom was suddenly r.:<BR>उदजीवत् सहसैव जीवलोकः, Si. xx. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

resuscitation
RESUSCITATION:<BR>(1) उज्जीवनम्, प्रति-;<BR>(2) सञ्जी-<BR>वनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retail
RETAIL: अल्पशः<BR>or<BR>पादशः विक्रीणीते (क्री, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retail
RETAIL (subs.): perh. अल्पशः<BR>or<BR>पादशो विक्रयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retailer
RETAILER: i. e. retail-dealer: perh. पादकारः;<BR> पण्यविक्रयिन् (m. ?), Ram. ii. 90. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retain
RETAIN:<BR>I To keep, hold: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>धारयति, सं-, वि- (धृ, c. 10.), boldness and ability<BR>to r. (i. e. remember): प्रागल्भ्यं धारयिष्णुता, Ka.<BR>i. 21.;<BR>(2) न मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6. = not to leave:<BR>q. v.).<BR>II To engage, hire: (मूल्यं दत्त्वा etc.)<BR>रक्षति (रक्ष्, c. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retainer
RETAINER:<BR>I Lit.: अनुगः (= follower);<BR>(2)<BR>अनुजीविन् (m. = dependent);<BR>(3) स्वपक्षः (=<BR>partisan);<BR>(4) भृत्यः (= servant).<BR>II Re-<BR>-taining fee: *रक्षामूल्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retaliate
RETALIATE: प्रतिकरोति,<BR>has come to r.:<BR>प्रतिकर्त-<BR>मुपागतः, Ki. xii. 11.: v. Also revenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retaliation
RETALIATION:<BR>(1) प्रति (ती) कारः<BR>or<BR>-क्रिया;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रत्यपकारः (in bad sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retard
RETARD:<BR>(1) विलम्बयति (c. of लम्ब्): v. To<BR>delay;<BR>(2) रुणद्धि (रुध्, c. 7): v. To hinder,<BR>restrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retch
RETCH: perh. विवमिषति (desi. of वम्), or<BR>छर्दिरागच्छति (गम्, c. l.: gen. of person). R. ing:<BR>विवमिषा (?) or by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retention
RETENTION:<BR>I The act: expr. by verb.<BR>II<BR>The faculty: धारणा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retentive
RETENTIVE:<BR>(1) धारणावत् (f. ती);<BR>(2) धारयिष्णु<BR>(mfn.). R. memory:<BR>(1) मेधा,<BR>and has excel-<BR>lent r. m.:<BR>मेधाविनी च, Mal. i.;<BR>(2) धारयिष्णुता,<BR>Ka. i. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retentiveness
RETENTIVENESS:<BR>(1) धारणाशक्तिः;<BR>(2) धारयिष्णुता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reticence
RETICENCE:<BR>(1) मौनम् (silence);<BR>(2) संवृतिः<BR>(= reserve).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reticent
RETICENT: मौनावलम्बिन् (f. नी = silent);<BR>(2)<BR>संवृत्तिमत् (f. ती = reserved).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reticular
RETICULAR, RETICULATED: जालाकार (f. रा)<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retina
RETINA: perh. दृष्टिः, ऽदृष्टिद्वयं कृष्णगोलौ, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retinue
RETINUE:<BR>(1) परिजनः;<BR>(2) परिवारः;<BR>(3) परि- [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">Page595</a>]<BR>-वर्हः;<BR>(4) परिच्छदः: v. Attendant, follower,<BR>servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retire
RETIRE:<BR>I To go away, retreat: q. v.: अप-<BR>क्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.).<BR>II To withdraw:<BR>r. d<BR>from the world:<BR>शान्तिमार्गोत्सुकोऽभूत्, R. vii. 71.;<BR>you will again r. to this hermitage:<BR>करिष्यसि<BR> पदं पुनराश्रमेऽस्मिन् Sa. iv. 19.;<BR>shall r. to a<BR>wood:<BR>वनं व्रजेत्, Y. iii. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retired
RETIRED (adj.):<BR>I Solitary, secluded: q. v.:<BR>विविक्त (f. क्ता).<BR>II From office: कर्मापसृत<BR>(f. ता), त्यक्तकर्मन् (mfn.) and sim. comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retirement
RETIREMENT:<BR>I In gen.: expr. by verb: v.<BR>To retire.<BR>II Seclusion: विविक्तता।<BR>III<BR>From office: कर्मापसृति; and sim. comp. s (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retiring
RETIRING (adj.):<BR>I Reserved, not forward:<BR>विविक्तप्रिय (f. या) and sim. comp. s;<BR>(2) शान्त<BR>(f. न्ता = quiet).<BR>II Suitable at retire-<BR>-ment;<BR>r. pension:<BR>*कर्मापसृतिवृत्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retort
RETORT (v.):<BR>(1) प्रत्यवस्कन्दते (स्कन्द्, c. l.);<BR>(2) प्रत्युत्तरं ददाति (दा, c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retort
RETORT (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रत्यवस्कन्दः;<BR>(2) प्रत्युत्तरम्<BR>(= rejoinder).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retrace
RETRACE:<BR>to r. one's steps:<BR>प्रत्यावर्तते (वृत्, c.<BR>l.): v. To return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retract
RETRACT:<BR>(1) perh. संहरति (हृ, c. l.);<BR>(2)<BR>खादति (खाद्, c. l. = to eat up?);<BR>(3) प्रत्या-<BR>ख्याति (ख्या, c. 2. = to gainsay).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retraction
RETRACTION, RETRACTATION:<BR>(1) by circumlo;<BR>(2) प्रत्याख्यानम्<BR>or<BR>प्रतिवादः (= gainsaying).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retreat
RETREAT (subs.): The act:<BR>(1) अपयानम् or<BR>अपसरणम् (= going away);<BR>(2) पलायनम् (=<BR>fleeing).<BR>II The place:<BR>(1) शरणम्: v.<BR>Refuge.;<BR>(2) आलयः (= abode^1: q. v.).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retreat
RETREAT (v.):<BR>I To retire, go away:<BR>(1)<BR>अपक्रामति (क्रम्, c. l.);<BR>(2) अपसरति (सृ, c. 1.).<BR>II From an enemy: पलायते: v. To<BR>flee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retrench
RETRENCH:<BR>(1) न्यूनीकरोति: v. To lessen,<BR>diminish;<BR>(2) लघयति (nomi.)<BR>or<BR>लघूकरोति: v.<BR>To lighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retrenchment
RETRENCHMENT: expr. by verb.; व्ययसंक्षेपः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retribution
RETRIBUTION:<BR>I Retaliation: प्रतिफलम्।<BR>II<BR>Reward: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retributive
RETRIBUTIVE: perh. परिशोधक (f. धिका);<BR>better by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retrievable
RETRIEVABLE:<BR>(1) उद्धरणीय (f. या), सम्-;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रतिसमाधेय (f. या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retrieve
RETRIEVE: उद्धरति, सम्- (धृ, c. l.): v. To<BR>recover, restore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retrocession
RETROCESSION:<BR>(1) प्रतीपगमनम् (going back);<BR>(2) प्रतिदानम् (giving b.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retrograde
RETROGRADE:<BR>I Adj.:<BR>(1) प्रतीप (f. पा=<BR>reverse);<BR>(2) वक्र (f. क्रा = crooked: in<BR>Astro.), Su. ii. 14.;<BR>(3) परावृत्त (f. त्ता = back-<BR>-ward).<BR>II Verb: परावर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retrogression
RETROGRESSION:<BR>(1) वक्रगतिः (of planets etc.);<BR>(2) प्रतीपगमनम् etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retrospect
RETROSPECT (subs.): गतस्य पर्यालोचनम्; अतीत-<BR>परिदर्शनम् (?); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retrospective
RETROSPECTIVE: r. view = retrospect: q. v.;<BR>with r. effect:<BR>गतेन कालेन<BR>or<BR>समयेन (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

retrospectively
RETROSPECTIVELY:<BR>(1) गतेन कालेन (?);<BR>(2)<BR>अतीतावधि (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

return
RETURN (v. t.):<BR>(1) ददाति (दा, c. 3. = to give:<BR>when the sense is clear),<BR>to r. a reply:<BR>प्रत्युत्तरं<BR> ददाति;<BR>he should r. or take back the thing within<BR>ten days:<BR>सोऽन्तर्दशाहात्तद्द्रव्यं दद्याच्चै वाददतीत च,<BR>M.;<BR>(2) प्रतिददाति (= to give back),<BR>it is to<BR>be r. ed to the seller:<BR>विक्रेतुः प्रतिदेयं तत्, N. s.;<BR>(3) प्रत्यर्पयति (c. of ऋ = 2.),<BR>as if after r. ing<BR>a pledge:<BR>प्रत्यर्पितन्यास इव, Sa. iv. 21.:<BR>(5)<BR>निर्यातयति, -ते, प्रति-, (c. of यत्), I shall r. (it):<BR>निर्यातयिष्ये, Mr. i.;<BR>(6) by प्रति- (in r.:<BR>q. v.),<BR>by r. ing evil for evil:<BR>प्रत्यपकारेण, Si. ii.<BR>Ph.: time for r. ing (in sales): अनुशयः (परावर्तन-<BR>योग्यः कालः), Kat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

return
RETURN (v. i.):<BR>(1) निवर्तते, प्रति-, वि-, सं-, (वृत्,<BR>c. l.), to (our)<BR>governor Kanva when he r. s<BR>from his stay abroad:<BR>प्रवासप्रतिनिवृत्ताय तातकण्वाय,<BR>Sa. iv.;<BR>the king has r. ed to his town:<BR>राजा<BR> प्रतिनिवृत्तो नगरम्, V. v.;<BR>(2) प्रत्यायाति (या, c.<BR>2.), (= to come back: q. v.),<BR>days gone by<BR>do not r. again:<BR>प्रत्यायान्ति गता पुनर्न दिवसाः, J.;<BR>(3) प्रतिगच्छति (= to go back: q. v.), please<BR>give us (your)<BR>message here and r.:<BR>अत्र नः<BR> सन्दिश्य प्रतिगन्तुमर्हसि, Sa. iv.;<BR>(4) पुनरेति (इ, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">Page596</a>]<BR>c. 2. = to come again: q. v.), cunning youth<BR>(once)<BR>past does not r.:<BR>न पुनरेति गतं चतुरं वयः,<BR>R. ix. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

return
RETURN (subs.):<BR>I Coming back:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रत्यागमः, -नम्;<BR>(2) प्रतियानम् (= going back);<BR>(3) निवृत्तिः, प्रति-, सं-, वि-, (rare), “असन्निवृत्यै<BR> तदतीतमेव”, Sa. vi. 10.;<BR>(4) better by verb,<BR>I am desirous of embracing you on your r.:<BR>प्रत्यागतं त्वां परिरब्धुकामा, Ki. iii. 54.<BR>II Giving<BR>back:<BR>(1) प्रत्यर्पणम्;<BR>(2) प्रतिदानम्;<BR>(3)<BR>निर्यातनम्, प्रति-: v. To return. (v. t.).<BR>III<BR>Produce, profit: q. v.: फलम्: v. An<BR>official declaration: *गणना, mortuary r.:<BR>मृत्युगणनापत्रिका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

return
RETURN, IN: प्रति- in comp.<BR>If I do not do some<BR>good to you in r.:<BR>प्रतिप्रियं चेद्भवतो न कुर्याम्, R. v.<BR>56.;<BR>Ś. has done befitting^1 good to f. in r. for<BR>his life:<BR>प्राणप्रदस्य सुसदृशं प्रत्युपकृतं जीमूतवाहनस्य<BR> शङ्खचूडेन, Na. v.;<BR>action in r.:<BR>प्रतिक्रिया,<BR>Mr. iii.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reunion
REUNION:<BR>I Lit.: पुनःसंयोगः and sim. comp.s.<BR>II An assembly, meeting: q. v.:<BR>(1) सङ्गमः;<BR>(2) समागमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

re-unite
RE-UNITE: v. To reconcile, unite again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reveal
REVEAL:<BR>(1) वि-वृणोति, अपा- (वृ, c. 5.),<BR>to r.<BR>one's heart:<BR>हृदयं विवृणोति, Ki. xiv. 12;<BR>(2)<BR>भिनत्ति, निर्- (भिद्, c. 7. = to break),<BR>secretly<BR>r. state secrets:<BR>मिन्दन्ति मन्त्रं प्रच्छन्नाः, Ka. xi.<BR>65.;<BR>(3) प्रकाशयति (काश्, c. 10. = to give<BR>out: q. v.);<BR>(4) by circumlo.,<BR>through my<BR>favour all these will be r. ed to you:<BR>सर्वं विदित-<BR>भेतत्ते मत्प्रसादाद्भविष्यति, Ram. i. 2. 31.;<BR>as it<BR>was r. ed to him:<BR>द्रष्ट्टत्वात्, Say.;<BR>r. s divine<BR>truths to all beings:<BR>ददाति सवर्वभूतानां परं ज्ञानम्,<BR>Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revealer
REVEALER:<BR>(1) expr. by verb.;<BR>(2) भेदक (f.<BR>दिका), निर्- (= breaker: as of secrets):<BR>(3)<BR>विवरीतृ (f. त्री: rare);<BR>(4) प्रकाशक (f. शिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revel
REVEL (v.): प्रभूतभक्ष्यपेयेन मोदते (मुद्, c. l.: see<BR>Mah. xvi. 3. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revel
REVEL, -LING (subs.): भक्ष्यमहोत्सवः (?); पान-<BR>गोष्ठीमहोत्सवः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revelation
REVELATION:<BR>(1) विवृतिः;<BR>(2) भेदः, निर्-,<BR>-विनिर्;<BR>(3) प्रकाशः, -नम्: for dif.: v. To<BR>reveal. Ph.:<BR>divine r.:<BR>ऐशोन्मेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reveler
REVEL(LL)ER: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revelry
REVELRY: v. Revel (subs.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revenge
REVENGE (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रतिहिंसा;<BR>(2) प्रत्यपकारः;<BR>(3) वैरनिर्यातनम् and sim. comp. s (the act);<BR>(4) प्रति (ती) कारः<BR>or<BR>-क्रिया (= requital),<BR>in order<BR>to take r.:<BR>प्रतिचिकीर्षया, Ki. xi. 74.;<BR>if un-<BR>forgivingness had not supported r.:<BR>यद्यमर्षः<BR> प्रतीकारं भुजालम्बं न लम्भयेत्, Ki. xi. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revenge
REVENGE (v.): by subs. with gen.: v. Also<BR>to avenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revengeful
REVENGEFUL:<BR>(1) प्रतिहिंसापरायण (f. णा) and<BR>sim. comp. s;<BR>(2) चिकीर्षु<BR>or<BR>प्रतिचिकीर्षु (mfn.:<BR>rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revenger
REVENGER: प्रति (ती) कर्तृ (f. त्री = avenger:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revenue
REVENUE:<BR>(1) करः,<BR>annual r.:<BR>आब्दिकः करः, M.<BR>vii. 129.;<BR>(2) बलिः, he took r. from them:<BR>स ताभ्यो बलिमग्रहीत्, R. i. 18.;<BR>(3) भागधेयः<BR>(rare), A.;<BR>(4) राजस्वम् (royal): v. Also<BR>fruit, produce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reverberate
REVERBERATE: प्रतिध्वनति (ध्वन्, c. l.): v.<BR>To resound, echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reverberation
REVERBERATION:<BR>I Of sound: प्रतिध्वनिः: v.<BR>Echo.<BR>II Of light or heat:<BR>(1) प्रतिफलः<BR>(?);<BR>(2) प्रतिक्षेपः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revere
REVERE, REVERENCE (v.):<BR>(1) अर्चयति, अभि-,<BR> सम्- (अर्च्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) पूजयति, सम्-, अभि-<BR>-(पूज्, c. 10.): v. To honour, respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reverence
REVERENCE (subs.): अर्चना<BR>or<BR>अर्चा, अभि-,<BR>r. paid<BR>by me to Kṛṣṇa:<BR>विहितं मयाच्युतार्चनम्, Si. xv.<BR>46.;<BR>or if he commands your highest r.:<BR>यदि<BR> वार्चनीयतम एष भवताम्, 18.;<BR>(2) पूजनम्<BR>or<BR>पूजा,<BR> सं-;<BR>(3) अपचितिः;<BR>(4) प्रतिमानना: v. Also<BR>respect. Ph.: Your or His r. (in address):<BR>भगवत् (f. ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revered
REVERED, REVEREND (adj.):<BR>(1) पूज्य (f. ज्या)<BR>or<BR>पूजनीय (f. या), सं-;<BR>(2) अर्चनीय (f. या) or<BR>अर्च्य (f. र्च्या), अभि-, समभि-;<BR>(3) माननीय (f.<BR>या)<BR>or<BR>मान्य (f. न्या), सं-, प्रति-;<BR>(4) पूजार्ह<BR>(f. र्हा) and sim. comp.s. Ph.: r. sir:<BR>भगवन्: v. Reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reverent
REVERENT, REVERENTIAL:<BR>(1) भक्तिमत् (f. ती);<BR>(2) by circumlo.: v. To revere, respectful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reverently
REVERENTLY, REVERENTIALLY:<BR>(1) भक्त्या;<BR>(2)<BR>भक्तिपुरःसरम्;<BR>(3) भक्तिपूर्वकम्: v. Also respect-<BR>-fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reverie
REVERIE: ध्यानम्: v. Meditation, dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reversal
REVERSAL:<BR>(1) परावर्तः, -नम्;<BR>(2) परावृत्तिः: v.<BR>To reverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reverse
REVERSE (subs.):<BR>I The back side: पृष्ठम्।<BR>II<BR>Misfortune: q. v.: विपद् (f.)<BR>or<BR>विपत्तिः।<BR>III<BR>Contrary, opposite: q. v.: विपर्ययः।<BR>IV<BR>Change: q. v.: परावर्तः। Ph.: r. of cold:<BR>शोतेतर (f. रा);<BR>r. of white:<BR>सितेतर (f. रा);<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reverse
REVERSE (v.):<BR>I To annul, make void:<BR>perh. परावर्तयति (c. of वृत्);<BR>(2) खण्डयति, परि-<BR>-(खण्ड्, c. 10.).<BR>II To change, alter:<BR>q. v.: परिवर्तयति। Ph.:<BR>r. ing you and I:<BR>युष्मद-<BR>स्मदोर्व्यत्ययेन, Mu. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reverse
REVERSE, -D (adj.): विपर्यस्त (f. स्ता): v.<BR>Contrary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reversely
REVERSELY: विपर्ययेण: v. Conversely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reversible
REVERSIBLE: परावर्तनीय (f. या);<BR>(2) परावर्त्य<BR>(f. र्त्या);<BR>(3) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reversion
REVERSION:<BR>I Reversing: परावर्तः, -नम्।<BR>II<BR>Reverting: प्रत्यावर्तः, -नम्: v. Also succession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reversionary
REVERSIONARY:<BR>r. heir:<BR>शेषाधिकारिन् (f. णी)<BR>(?);<BR>r. interest or right:<BR>शेषभोगाधिकारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revert
REVERT:<BR>(1) प्रत्यावर्तते (वृत्, c. l.);<BR>(2) पुनर्<BR> आगच्छति (गम्, c. l.): v. To come, again,<BR>at last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

review
REVIEW (subs.):<BR>I Inspection: परिदर्शनम्।<BR>II<BR>Of books: पर्यालोचना (?); दोषगुणविचारः (?).<BR>III In law: पुनर्दर्शनम्, a r. (should be made)<BR>if objections are raised against witnesses or<BR>assessors by losing parties:<BR>साक्षिसभ्यावसन्नानां<BR> दूषणे दर्शनं पुनः, N. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

review
REVIEW (v.):<BR>I Lit. and in law: पुनर्दर्शनं<BR> करोति।<BR>II To revise, inspect: परिपश्यति<BR>(दृश्, c. 1.).<BR>III As books: पर्यालोचयति<BR>(लुच्, c. 10.): v. To examine, criticize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reviewer
REVIEWER:<BR>(1) पर्यालोचक (f. चिका);<BR>(2) गुण-<BR>दोषविचारक (f. रिका) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revile
REVILE: अधि-क्षिपति, आ-, (क्षिप्, c. 6.): v.<BR>To abuse, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reviler
REVILER: अधि-क्षेपक (f. पिका), आ-: v. Cen-<BR>-surer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reviling
REVILING:<BR>I Subs.: अधि-क्षेपः, आ-: v. Abuse,<BR>censure, reproach.<BR>II Adj.: expr. by<BR>comp.: v. Abusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revisal
REVISAL:<BR>(1) परिदर्शनम् (= review);<BR>(2) परिशोधः<BR>(= correction).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revise
REVISE: perh. परिपश्यति (द्यश्, c. l.)<BR>or<BR>परिदर्शनं<BR> करोति: v. Also to amend, correct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revision
REVISION:<BR>I Revisal: q. v.<BR>II What is<BR>revised: शुद्धिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revival
REVIVAL:<BR>I Lit:<BR>(1) उज्जीवनम्<BR>or<BR>सञ्जीवनम्;<BR>(2)<BR>संज्ञालाभः, चेतनागमः, etc. (= recovery of cons-<BR>-ciousness);<BR>(3) उद्वोधनम्<BR>or<BR>वि- (= awakening).<BR>II Fig., as of studies:<BR>(1) पुनरुत्थानम्;<BR>(2)<BR>समुत्थानम् (= rise);<BR>(3) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revive
REVIVE (v. t.):<BR>I To bring to life: जीवयति,<BR> सं-, प्रति-, उत्- (c. of जीव्), r. ing medicine:<BR>सञ्जीवनौषधिः, U. iii. 11.<BR>II To bring to<BR>consciousness: संज्ञां<BR>or<BR>चेतनां लम्भयति (c. of<BR>लभ्)<BR>or<BR>ग्राहयति (c. of ग्रह्), K.<BR>III. To<BR>awaken, arouse: बोधयति, वि-, उत्- (c. of<BR>वुध्),<BR>the wife of Kāma was r. d by fate:<BR>विधिना<BR> कामवधूर्विबोधिता, Ku. iv. 1.<BR>IV To refresh:<BR>q. v.: आश्वासयति, सम्-, (c. of श्वस्).<BR>V To<BR>renew:<BR>(1) (पुनः) प्रवर्तयति (c. of वृत्),<BR>to r.<BR>Vedic studies:<BR>श्रुतिसम्प्रदायं प्रवर्तयितुम्, M. n. on<BR>Si. xiv. 79.;<BR>(2) स्मरति (स्मृ, c. l. = to bring<BR>to recollection), Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revive
REVIVE (v. i.):<BR>I To come to life: q. v.:<BR>उज्जीवति (जीव्, c. 1.).<BR>II To recover cons-<BR>-ciousness: संज्ञां<BR>or<BR>चेतनां लभते, (लभ्, c. l.),<BR>प्राप्नोति (आप्, c. 5.), etc.: v. To get.<BR>III<BR>To reflourish:<BR>(1) पुनर उत्तिष्ठते, सम्-, (स्था,<BR>c. l.);<BR>(2) by v. t.: v. Revive (V).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revocable
REVOCABLE: खण्डनीय (f. या)<BR>or<BR>खण्ड्य (f. ण्ड्या),<BR>परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revocation
REVOCATION: खण्डना: v. Repeal, reversal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revoke
REVOKE: खण्डयति (खण्ड्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>reverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revolt
REVOLT (subs.): राजद्रोहः: v. Rebellion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revolt
REVOLT (v.):<BR>I To rebel: q. v.: राजद्रोहं<BR> करोति।<BR>II To shock, be offensive:<BR>r. ing to<BR>one's feeling:<BR>वीभत्स (f. त्सा): v. Disgusting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revolution
REVOLUTION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) परिवर्तः, -नम्,<BR>and by their r. s:<BR>तेषां तु परिवर्तेन, Su. i. 27.;<BR>(2)<BR>भ्रमणम् (when the sense is clear), circular r.:<BR>चक्रभ्रमणम्, Go.;<BR>(3) गतिः (= motion).<BR>II<BR>The space measured by r.: भगणः, twelve<BR>(signs)<BR>make a r.:<BR>भगणो द्वादशैव ते, Su. i. 28.;<BR>r. s of the Sun, Mercury and Venus:<BR>सूर्ययज्ञशुक्राणां<BR> भगणाः, Su. i. 29.<BR>III In government: राज्य-<BR>परिवर्तः, -नम्, and sim. comp. s (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revolutionary
REVOLUTIONARY: expr. by comp. or cir-<BR>-cumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revolutionist
REVOLUTIONIST: राज्यपरिवर्तिन् (f. नी): v. To<BR>change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revolutionize
REVOLUTIONIZE: अशेषेण परिवर्तयति (c. of वृत्):<BR>v. To change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revolve
REVOLVE (v. i.):<BR>(1) परि-वर्तते, आ, पर्या-, समा-,<BR>(वृत्, c. l.),<BR>r. ing round and round like a<BR>wheel:<BR>चक्रभ्रममावृत्यावृत्य, Vi. vi. 12.;<BR>(2) भ्रमति<BR>or<BR>भ्राभ्यति, परि-, (भ्रम्, c. l. and 4.),<BR>the stars<BR>r. ing over his head:<BR>भ्रमद्भचक्रं निजमस्तकोपरि, Go.;<BR>(2) घूर्णति, -ते, वि-, परि-, (घूर्ण्, c. l.),<BR>the light<BR>of lamps is r. ing:<BR>घूर्णते दैपमर्चिः, Si. xi. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revolve
REVOLVE (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) घूर्णयति, वि-, परि-,<BR>(c. of घूर्ण्);<BR>(2) भ्रामयति, परि-, (c. of भ्रम्);<BR>(3) परिवर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR>II To recollect,<BR>consider: q. v.: विगणयति (गण्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

revolver
REVOLVER: आग्नेयास्त्रविशेषः; *घूर्णचक्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reward
REWARD (subs.):<BR>(1) पारितोषिकम्,<BR>has favoured<BR>you with this r.:<BR>एतत्पारितोषिकं ते प्रसादीकृतम्,<BR>Sa. v.:<BR>(3) प्रति-फलम् (gen. in bad sense),<BR>will get r. befitting his skill:<BR>दाक्ष्यस्यानुरूपं<BR> फलमधिगमिष्यति, Mu. iii.;<BR>(3) मूल्यम् (= price:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

reward
REWARD (v.):<BR>(1) परितोषयति (c. of तुष्),<BR>r,<BR>and dismiss him:<BR>तत्परितोष्य विसर्जयैनम्, Mu.<BR>ii.;<BR>(2) पारितोषिकं ददाति (दा, c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rewarder
REWARDER:<BR>(1) परितोषयितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) by<BR>verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rhapsodic
RHAPSODIC, -AL: expr. by comp. or cir-<BR>-cumlo.: v. below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rhapsody
RHAPSODY: i. e. slightly unconnected dis-<BR>-course: no equiv: असम्बद्धप्रबन्धः and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rhetoric
RHETORIC: अलङ्कारः, -शास्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rhetorical
RHETORICAL:<BR>(1) comp.,<BR>r. work:<BR>अलङ्कारग्रन्थः<BR>or<BR>-निबन्धः;<BR>(2) आलङ्कारिक (f. की: rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rhetorically
RHETORICALLY: अलङ्कारशास्त्रानुसारेण and sim.<BR>expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rhetorician
RHETORICIAN: अलङ्कारशास्त्रज्ञ (f. ज्ञा) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rheum
RHEUM: of the mucous glands: श्लेष्मन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rheumatic
RHEUMATIC: expr. by words given below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rheumatism
RHEUMATISM: स्नायुगतो वातः (= of the muscles),<BR>Bha.; शिरागतो वातः; सन्धिगतो वातः (of the<BR>joints), Bha.; वातशोणितम् (?), C. s. N. B. वात<BR>is general name for some 80 diseases inclu-<BR>-ding, जृम्भा, शिरोग्रह, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rheumy
RHEUMY:<BR>(1) श्लेष्मलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) श्लेष्मण (f.<BR>णा);<BR>(3) क्लिन्न (f. न्ना) (of eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rhinoceros
RHINOCEROS:<BR>(1) गण्डः, -कः;<BR>(2) खङ्गिन् (m.:<BR>खङ्गः = its horn);<BR>(3) तैतिलः (rare). She-r.:<BR>खङ्गिधेनुः, -का, K. ; etc. (G. § 103).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rhomboid
RHOMBOID: तुल्यसम्मुखभुजश्चतुर्भुजः; *विषमायतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rhombus
RHOMBUS:<BR>(1) तुल्यचतुर्भुजः, Li. 148.;<BR>(2) सम-<BR>चतुर्भुजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rhubarb
RHUBARB: खेसम् (in Mahratti).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rhyme
RHYME (subs.):<BR>I Of verses: मित्राक्षरम्।<BR>II<BR>A verse: श्लोकः।<BR>III Poetry: q. v.: पद्यम्।<BR>Ph.:<BR>without r. or reason:<BR>निष्कारणम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rhyme
RHYME (v.):<BR>I To accord in sound: perh.<BR>मित्रीभवति।<BR>II To make r.: पद्यं करोति: v.<BR>Poetry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rhymer
RHYMER:<BR>(1) कविताकारः;<BR>(2) कुकविः (= bad<BR>poet): v. Versifier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rhythm
RHYTHM:<BR>(1) तालः;<BR>(2) लयः (= musical<BR>time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rhythmical
RHYTHMICAL:<BR>(1) तालबद्ध (f. द्धा);<BR>(2) तालानुगत<BR>(f. ता); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rhythmically
RHYTHMICALLY: expr. by adj or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rib
RIB:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पर्शुः, -का;<BR>(2) पार्श्वकम् or<BR>पार्श्वास्थि (n.);<BR>(3) पञ्जरम् (= r. s collectively).<BR>II Of a boat: पोलिन्दः (?).<BR>III Of cloth:<BR>रेखा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ribald
RIBALD: दुर्विनीत (f. ता): v. Mean, obscene.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ribaldry
RIBALDRY: अश्लीलता: v. Obscenity, indecency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ribbon
RIBBON, RIBAND: Perh. पट्टबन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rice
RICE:<BR>I The plant:<BR>(1) शालिः (= winter r.),<BR>red (= table)<BR>r.:<BR>रक्तशालिः;<BR>white r.:<BR>कलमः;<BR>(2) आशुः (= aus, early r.);<BR>(3) व्रीहिः (= boro,<BR>rice ripening in the rains);<BR>(4) षष्टिका (= a<BR>rice of quick growth);<BR>(5) नीवारः (= a wild<BR>rice).<BR>II Husked r.: तण्डुलः, grains of r.:<BR>तण्डुलकणाः, H.<BR>III. Boiled r.:<BR>(1) अन्नम्;<BR>(2)<BR>ओदनम्;<BR>(3) अन्धस्,<BR>(4) भक्तम्। Ph.:<BR>r. boiled<BR>in milk with sugar:<BR>पायसम्, परमान्नम्;<BR>r. boiled<BR>with dāl, khichri:<BR>कृसरा, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rich
RICH:<BR>I Wealthy:<BR>(1) धनिन् (f. नी),<BR>if we<BR>are r. with wealth undistributed and unenjoyed:<BR>दानोपभोगहीनेन धनेन धनिनो यदि, H. i. 156.;<BR>(2)<BR>धनवत् (f. ती);<BR>(3) धनशालिन् (f. नी);<BR>(4)<BR>महाधन (f. ना), धनाढ्य (f. ढ्या), and sim.<BR>comp.s. (= very r.);<BR>(5) वित्तशालिन् (f. नी);<BR>(6) विभवसम्पन्न (f. न्ना);<BR>(7) by subs.,<BR>he has<BR>friends, who is r.:<BR>यस्यार्थास्तस्य मित्राणि, H. i.<BR>124.<BR>II Costly, splendid; q. v.: महाधन<BR>(f. ना) and sim. comp. s,<BR>r. couch:<BR>महाधनं<BR> शयनम्, Ki. i. 38.<BR>III Abundant: q. v.:<BR>प्रचुर (f. रा).<BR>IV Abounding in:<BR>(1) आढ्य<BR>(f. ढ्या), a fort r. in weapons and machines:<BR>दुर्गमायुधयन्त्राढ्यम्, Ka. iv. 60.;<BR>(2) by words<BR>given under<BR>abundant, the first became r. in<BR>gems:<BR>प्रथमा बहुरत्नसूरभूत्। R. viii. 28.;<BR>(3)<BR>समन्वित (f. ता = endowed with: q. v.),<BR>r. in<BR>ore:<BR>खनिद्रव्यसमन्विता, Ka. iv. 51.: v. Also<BR>having. V. Of soil etc.:<BR>(1) सारवत्<BR>or<BR>गुणवत्<BR>(f. ती), Ka. iv. 50. and ix. 18.;<BR>(2) प्रशस्त<BR>(f. स्ता): v. Excellent.<BR>VI Of colours:<BR>उज्ज्वल (f. ला = bright).<BR>VII Highly sea-<BR>-soned:<BR>(1) घृतप्लुत (f. ता) and sim. comp.s.<BR>(= full of ghee);<BR>(2) सुमधुर (f. रा = very<BR>sweet), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

riches
RICHES:<BR>(1) धनम्, every one is strong with r.:<BR>धनवान् बलवान् सर्वः, H. i. 121.: v. Money,<BR>wealth;<BR>(2) समृद्धिः: v. Opulence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

richly
RICHLY:<BR>I With riches: प्रभूतधनेन and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Sumptuously, splendidly: q. v.:<BR>expr. by adj.<BR>III Plentifully, exceedingly:<BR>q. v.: भूरि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

richness
RICHNESS:<BR>I Lit.: धनाढ्यता and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Costliness: महाधनता and sim. comp.s.<BR>III Abundance: q. v.: प्राचुर्यम्।<BR>IV Of<BR>soil: सार-<BR>or<BR>गुणवत्ता।<BR>V Excellence: q. v.:<BR>प्रशस्तता।<BR>VI Of colours: उज्ज्वलता।<BR>VII Of<BR>dishes: सुमधुरता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rick
RICK: राशिः: v. Heap, stock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rickets
RICKETS: a disease: बालग्रहः (gen.), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rickety
RICKETY:<BR>I Lit.: ग्रहजुष्ट (f. ष्टा).<BR>II Shaky:<BR>शिथिलसन्धि (mfn.) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rid
RID: मुञ्चति<BR>or<BR>मोचयति वि-, (मुच्, c. 6. and 10.)<BR>: v. To free, deliver.<BR>To get r. of:<BR>निःसारयति<BR>(c. of सृ): v. To remove, drive away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

riddance
RIDDANCE: मुक्तिः: v. Deliverance, escape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

riddle
RIDDLE (subs.):<BR>I Enigma:<BR>(1) प्रहेलिका;<BR>(2) प्रवह्णिः, का।<BR>II A sieve: q. v.: शोधनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

riddle
RIDDLE (v.):<BR>I To clean grass: शोधयति, वि-,<BR>(c. of शुध्), D. vi.<BR>II To pierce: q. v.:<BR>विध्यति (व्यध्, c. 4.).<BR>III To speak enig-<BR>-matically: प्रहेलिकां वदति (वद्, c. l.): v. To<BR>say, tell.<BR>IV To un-r.: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ride
RIDE (v.):<BR>(1) आ- रोहति, अधि-, समधि-, समा-,<BR> अध्या-, (रुह्, c. l.),<BR>rose in order to r.:<BR>आरुरुक्षुरुद-<BR>तिष्ठत्, K. ;<BR>r. ing on it:<BR>समारुह्य तम्, K. ;<BR>r. for<BR>the battle on a great marine monster:<BR>युद्धेऽधिरूढः<BR> मकरं महत्तरम्, Ku. xiv. 9.;<BR>(2) अधितिष्ठति (स्था,<BR>c. l. = be seated on),<BR>r. ing in their excellent<BR>vehicles:<BR>स्ववाहनानि प्रवराण्यधिष्ठिताः, Ku. xiv. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ride
RIDE (subs.):<BR>I The act:<BR>to take a r.:<BR>अश्वेन<BR> सञ्चरते (चर्, c. l.)<BR>or<BR>विहरति (हृ, c. l.): v.<BR>Also R. ing.<BR>II A road: perh. वीथिः, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rider
RIDER:<BR>I Horse-r.:<BR>(1) अश्वारोहिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) अश्वारूढ (f. ढा); and sim. comp.s.<BR>II<BR>In gen.: आरोहिन् (f. णी): v. To ride.<BR>III<BR>An addition: perh. सहयोगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ridge
RIDGE: no prop. equiv.:<BR>(1) पृष्ठम् (= back);<BR>(2) कटक (mn. = side of a hill);<BR>(3) श्रेणिः,<BR>(णी = chain).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ridicule
RIDICULE (subs.): उपहासः<BR>or<BR>अवहासः<BR>or<BR>अपहासः,<BR>I shall merit r.:<BR>गमिष्याम्युपहास्यताम्, R. i. 3.<BR>: v. Also contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ridicule
RIDICULE (v.): उप- हसति, अव-, अप-, (हस्, c. 1.),<BR>either I shall be r. d by good men:<BR>अपहस्येऽथवा<BR> सद्भिः, Ki. xi. 68.: v. Also to laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ridiculous
RIDICULOUS: उप-, अप-,<BR>or<BR>अव- हास्य (f. स्या)<BR>: v. Also contemptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ridiculously
RIDICULOUSLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ridiculousness
RIDICULOUSNESS: उप-, अप-<BR>or<BR>अव-हास्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

riding
RIDING: (subs.):<BR>I The act: अश्वारोहणम् and<BR>sim. comp. s.,<BR>skill in r.:<BR>तुरङ्गारोहणपाटवम्, D.;<BR>r. -habit:<BR>तुरङ्गाधिरोहणोचितो वेषः, K. : v. Horse,<BR>to ride.<BR>II Of a country: *मण्डलखण्डः;<BR> प्रमण्डलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rife
RIFE (adj.): प्रचल (f. ला): v. Prevalent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rifle
RIFLE:<BR>I Subs.: आग्नेयास्त्रम्।<BR>II Verb: हरति<BR>(हृ, c. 1.): v. To rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rifleman
RIFLEMAN: आग्नेयास्त्रभृत् (mfn.), -धारिन् (f. णी),<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rift
RIFT: छिद्रम्: v. Crack, cleft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rig
RIG (v.): सज्जते (सज्ज्, c. 1.): v. To equip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rig
RIG, RIGGING (subs.):<BR>(1) सज्जा (= equip-<BR>-ment);<BR>(2) रज्जवः (= ropes: of ship's r.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

right
RIGHT (adj.):<BR>I Not left:<BR>(1) दक्षिण (f. णा),<BR>on the r.:<BR>दक्षिणतः;<BR>wounded on the r.:<BR>दक्षिणेर्मन्<BR>(mfn.), B. iv. 44.;<BR>(2) वामेतर<BR>or<BR>सव्येतर (f. रा:<BR>poet.),<BR>by the r. eye:<BR>सव्येतरेणाक्ष्णा, R. xiv.<BR>49.;<BR>(3) अपसव्य (f. व्या: rare).<BR>II Straight:<BR>q. v.:<BR>r. line:<BR>सरलरेखा;<BR>r. angle:<BR>समकोणः।<BR>III Proper; reasonable: q. v.:<BR>(1) उचित<BR>(f. ता), सम्-;<BR>(2) न्याय्य, (f. य्या).<BR>IV<BR>Real, actual: q. v.: यथार्थ (f. र्था).<BR>V True,<BR>correct: q. v.: सत्य (f. त्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

right
RIGHT (subs.):<BR>I Justice, propriety: q. v.:<BR>धर्मः।<BR>II Just claim, title:<BR>(1) अधिकारः;<BR>(2) स्वत्वम्।<BR>III. R. side: v. Right. (adj. 1.).<BR>IV What is r.: expr. by adj.,<BR>neither I<BR>did r. to him:<BR>एतस्मिन्नुचितं न नाम विहितम्, Vi.<BR>v. 46.;<BR>you are in the r.:<BR>सत्ये त्वं वर्तसे (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

right
RIGHT (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) ऋजूकरोति;<BR>(2) समी-<BR>करोति।<BR>II To do r. to: उचितं विदधाति (धा,<BR>c. 3.), व्यवहरति (हृ, c. 1.), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

right
RIGHT (adv.): v. Rightly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

right-angled
RIGHT-ANGLED:<BR>(1) समकोण (f. णा);<BR>(2) ऋजु-<BR>कोण (f. णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

righteous
RIGHTEOUS:<BR>I Just, proper: q. v.: न्याय्य<BR>(f. य्या).<BR>II Virtuous, holy: q. v.: न्याय-<BR>परायण (f. णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

righteously
RIGHTEOUSLY:<BR>(1) न्यायतः (= justly);<BR>(2) by<BR>adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

righteousness
RIGHTEOUSNESS:<BR>(1) न्याय्यता (of acts);<BR>(2)<BR>न्यायपरायणता (of men): v. Piety, rectitude,<BR>purity, propriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rightful
RIGHTFUL: न्याय्य (f. य्या): v. Lawful, just.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rightfully
RIGHTFULLY: न्यायेन: v. Lawfully, justly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

right-minded
RIGHT-MINDED: शुद्धचेतस् (mfn.) and sim.<BR>comp. s.: v. Honest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rightly
RIGHTLY:<BR>I Properly, fitly: q. v.: उचितम्।<BR>II Truly, correctly: q. v.: यथार्थतः,<BR>r. called<BR>“distresser of foes”:<BR>परन्तपो नाम यथार्थनामा, R.<BR>vi. 21.<BR>III Well: q. v.: सम्यक्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rigid
RIGID: कठोर (f. रा): v. Stern, severe,<BR>hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rigidity
RIGIDITY: कठोरता: v. Stiffness, hardness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rigidly
RIGIDLY: कठोरम्: v. Stiffly, hardly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rigmarole
RIGMAROLE: गूढप्रलपितम्, and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rigor
RIGOR, RIGOUR:<BR>I In gen.: कठोरता: v.<BR>Stiffness, hardness.<BR>II Intensity, severity:<BR>q. v.: उग्रता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rigorous
RIGOROUS: कठोर (f. रा),<BR>r. imprisonment:<BR>कठोर-<BR>निरोधः: v. Stiff, hard, severe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rigorously
RIGOROUSLY: expr. by adj. or comp.: v.<BR>Also hardly, severely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rill
RILL:<BR>(1) कुसरित् (f.), H. ;<BR>(2) क्षुद्रनदी; and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rim
RIM:<BR>(1) प्रान्तः: v. Border, edge;<BR>(2) कर्णः<BR>(of vessels).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rime
RIME: घननीहारः: v. Hoar-frost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rimy
RIMY: अतिहिम (f. मा) and sim. comp. s.: v.<BR>Frosty, frost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rind
RIND:<BR>(1) त्वच् (f.): v. Bark, skin;<BR>(2) कञ्चुकः<BR>(= coat, shell).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ring
RING (subs.):<BR>I A circle: q. v.: मण्डलम्,<BR>dancing in a r.:<BR>मण्डलनृत्यम्।<BR>II For fingers:<BR>अङ्गुली (री) यम्, -कम्,<BR>interchange of r. s:<BR>अङ्गुलीयक-<BR>विनिमयः, D. ii.;<BR>r. -finger:<BR>अनामिका (but<BR>मध्यमा, i. e. the middle finger is the Hindoo<BR>r. -f. Hence मध्यमोपलः, Ki. ix. 2.); bezel of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">Page601</a>]<BR>a r.:<BR>मणिबन्धः।, -नम्, Sa. v.<BR>III A circular<BR>area: मण्डलम्, वीथिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ring
RING (v. t.):<BR>I Of bells: चालयति (c. of चल्)<BR>(= to move). N.B. वादयति (c. of वद्) is of<BR>striking bells.<BR>II To fit with r. s: expr. by<BR>circumlo.<BR>III To encircle: परिवेष्टयति (c. of<BR>वेष्ट्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ring
RING (v. i.):<BR>(1) क्वणति (क्वण्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) रणति<BR>(रण्, c. 1.): v. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ring-dove
RING-DOVE: कपोतविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ringing
RINGING:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) क्वणितम्;<BR>(2) रणितम्।<BR>II Adj.:<BR>(1) क्वणत् (f. न्ती);<BR>(2) रणत्<BR>(f. न्ती), रणद्भिः स्वरैः, Si. i. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ring-leader
RING-LEADER:<BR>(1) नायकः: v. Leader;<BR>(2)<BR>मुखयः: v. Head, chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ringlet
RINGLET: अलकः: v. Curl, hair. (1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ringworm
RINGWORM: दद्रु (द्रूः), -रोगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rinse
RINSE (v.):<BR>I Of the mouth:<BR>(1) आचामति<BR>(चम्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) उपस्पृशति (स्पृश्, c. 6.);<BR>drinking fountain water and r. ing (the mouth<BR>with it): पीत्वा प्रस्रवणजलमुपस्पृश्य च, R.<BR>II<BR>To cleanse, wash: q. v.: प्रक्षालयति (क्षल्, c.<BR>10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rinsing
RINSING (subs.):<BR>(1) आचमनम्, water for r.:<BR>आचमनीयम्;<BR>(2) उपस्पर्शः;<BR>(3) प्रक्षालणम्: for<BR>dif.: v. To rinse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

riot
RIOT (subs.):<BR>I Tumult, uproar: q. v.:<BR>संक्षोभः।<BR>II In law: breach of the peace:<BR>perh.: सम्भूयाभिघातः, -अवमर्दः<BR>or<BR>-अभिद्रोहः।<BR>III<BR>Revelry, excess q. v. Ph.: to run r.:<BR>expr. with निरवग्रह (f. हा), अनियन्त्रित (f. ता),<BR>etc.; that (vicious elephant)<BR>has run r. in the<BR>highway:<BR>स (दुष्टहस्ती) महान्तं संक्षोभं कुर्वन् राज-<BR>मार्गमवतीर्णः, Mr. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

riot
RIOT (v.):<BR>I To be greatly excited:<BR>(1)<BR>संक्षुभ्यति (क्षुभ्, c. 4.);<BR>(2) सरम्भं गच्छति (गम्,<BR>c. 1.), etc.<BR>II To revel: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rioter
RIOTER: in law: सम्भूयाभिघातिन् (f. नी),<BR>अवमर्दकारिन् (f. णी), etc.: v. Also reveller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

riotous
RIOTOUS: expr. by comp.: v. Noisy,<BR>tumultuous^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

riotously
RIOTOUSLY:<BR>(1) संक्षोभं कुर्वत् (f. न्ती);<BR>(2) महा-<BR>शब्देन (= noisily).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rip
RIP (v.): पाटयति, वि- (पट्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>tear, cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ripe
RIPE:<BR>(1) पक्व (f. क्वा), परि-, वि-, सं-,<BR>with the<BR>rice r.:<BR>परिपक्वशालिः, Ki. iv. 1.;<BR>thoroughly r.<BR>tumour:<BR>सम्यक्पक्वः शोथः, Bha.;<BR>(2) परिणत<BR>(f. ता),<BR>r. rose-apple:<BR>परिणतजम्बुफलम्, Ki. x.<BR>22.;<BR>r. poetic genius:<BR>परिणतकवित्वशक्तिः, M.n.;<BR>(3) पक्त्रिम (f. मा), वि-, परि- (rare),<BR>by these r.<BR>words:<BR>वाणीभिराभिः परिपक्त्रिमाभिः, N. xxii. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ripen
RIPEN:<BR>I Intrans.:<BR>(1) पाकम् एति (इ, c. 2.),<BR>गच्छति, अवाप्नोति, etc.,<BR>r. ing:<BR>पाकं व्रजन्ती, Ri.<BR>iv. 11.;<BR>(2) पचति, परि-, (पच्, c. 1.: rare),<BR>tumours r.:<BR>पचन्ति शोथाः, Bha. Ph.:<BR>about<BR>to r.:<BR>पाकोन्मुख (f. खा), Bha.<BR>II Trans.:<BR>(1) पक्वीकरोति;<BR>(2) पाकं लम्भयति (c. of लभ्),<BR>जनयति (c. of जन्), etc.;<BR>(3) पाचयति, वि-,<BR> परि- (c. of पच्: rare), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ripeness
RIPENESS:<BR>(1) पाकः, वि-, परि-,<BR>by the r. of the<BR>fruit:<BR>फलस्य विपाकेन, Ki. iv. 26.;<BR>resulting<BR>from the r. of purity:<BR>पुण्यपरिपाकोपादान (f. ना),<BR>Vi. iv.;<BR>(2) पक्वता, -त्वम्, परि-, वि-;<BR>(3) परिणामः;<BR>(4) परिणतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ripple
RIPPLE:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) बुद्बुदः, U. ii. 46.;<BR>(2)<BR>तरङ्गः (= wave: q. v.).<BR>II Verb: क्षुभ्यति<BR>(क्षुभ्, c. 4.: to be agitated). R. ing (adj.):<BR>उद्बुद्बुद (f. दा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rise
RISE (v.):<BR>I To appear:<BR>(1) उदेति, उदयति<BR>(इ, c. 2. and 1.),<BR>r. ing slowly:<BR>मन्दमन्दमुदितः,<BR>Ki.;<BR>for the moon has r. n:<BR>उदयति हि शशाङ्कः,<BR>Mr. i. 54.;<BR>(2) उद्गच्छति,<BR>as soon as the sun<BR>rose:<BR>यावदेवोदगात्पतङ्गमण्डलम्, D. ii.; clusters of<BR>clouds rose from (his)<BR>hair:<BR>उदगुः॥।जलवाहावलयः<BR> शिरोरुहेभ्यः, Si. xx. 66.;<BR>(3) उत्तिष्ठते, सम्-, (स्था,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>clouds are r. ing:<BR>मेघः समुत्तिष्ठते, Mr.<BR>II To be up: उत्तिष्ठति, rose from the bench:<BR>पीठादुदत्तिष्ठत्, Si. i. 12.;<BR>r. ing and washing our<BR>faces:<BR>उत्थाय च धौतवक्त्रौ, D. ii.;<BR>r. n breaking<BR>up the earth:<BR>भित्त्वोत्थितं भूमिम्, Si. iv. 1.;<BR>the<BR>bathing time having approached, the king dis-<BR>missed the chiefs and rose from the assembly-<BR>hall:<BR>समासन्नस्नानसमयो विसर्जितराजलोकः क्षिति-<BR>पतिरास्थानमण्डपादुत्तस्थौ, K.<BR>III. To break out:<BR>उत्तिष्ठते,<BR>a fire has r. n in the zenana:<BR>उत्थितोऽन्तः- [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">Page602</a>]<BR>पुरेऽग्निः, Ra. iv. 14.; (if)<BR>he would r. to kill<BR>us:<BR>उत्तिष्ठेत वधाय नः, Vi. iv. 6.<BR>IV To<BR>advance: उत्तिष्ठते,<BR>but a r. ing enemy:<BR>उत्तिष्ठ-<BR>मानस्तु परः, Si. ii. 10.;<BR>some r. and fall, some<BR>fall and r.:<BR>कोऽप्युत्थितः पतति, कोऽपि पतितोऽप्यु-<BR>त्तिष्ठते, Mr. x.<BR>V To increase: q. v.: वर्धते<BR>(वृध्, c. 1.) (as of rivers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rise
RISE (subs.):<BR>(1) उत्थानम्, सम्-, newly r. n moon:<BR>नवोत्थान इन्दुः, R. vi. 31.; seeing him r.:<BR>तस्याभ्युत्थानदर्शिन्यः, R. iv. 3.;<BR>(2) उदयः, -नम्,<BR> अभि-, in (your)<BR>r.:<BR>उदये, R. viii. 84.;<BR>by<BR>their r. and setting:<BR>व्यसनोदयाभ्याम्, Sa. iv. 2.;<BR>(3) उद्गमः, -नम्, सम्-, (= appearance, as of<BR>heavenly bodies):<BR>(4) वृद्धिः, वि- : v.<BR>Advancement, increase;<BR>(5) उत्पातः (oppo-<BR>-sed to fall: r. ing up, lit. and fig.), H.<BR>Ph.<BR>To give rise to:<BR>उत्पादयति (c. of पद्):<BR>v. To produce, beget.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

riser
RISER: perh. उत्थानकारिन् (f. णी); better by<BR>verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

risibility
RISIBILITY:<BR>(1) हासकरत्वम्, -ता and sim.<BR>comp. s.;<BR>(2) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

risible
RISIBLE:<BR>(1) हासकर (f. री), Si. xv. 33.;<BR>(2)<BR>हासजनन (f. नी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rising
RISING:<BR>I Adj.: expr. by pres. part.: v.<BR>To rise.<BR>II Subs.: v. Rise. Ph.:<BR>popular<BR>r.:<BR>प्रजासंक्षोभः: v. Tumult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

risk
RISK:<BR>I Subs.: सङ्कटम्: v. Danger, peril.<BR>II Verb.:<BR>(1) संशये, सन्देहे<BR>or<BR>सङ्कटे क्षिपति, नि-,<BR>(क्षिप्, c. 6.), etc.:<BR>(2) संशयस्थं (f. स्थां),<BR>etc. करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rite
RITE (subs.):<BR>(1) क्रिया;<BR>(2) विधिः;<BR>(3) कर्मन्<BR>(n.): v. Ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ritual
RITUAL:<BR>I Adj.: by comp.: v. Ceremo-<BR>-rial.<BR>II Subs.: क्रियापद्धतिः (ती) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ritualist
RITUALIST: क्रियापद्धतिज्ञ (f. ज्ञा) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rival
RIVAL (subs. and adj.):<BR>(1) often by प्रति-<BR>in comp.,<BR>r. combatant:<BR>प्रतिद्वन्द्विन् (f. नी),<BR>R. vii. 37.;<BR>r. lady:<BR>प्रतियुवतिः, Si. viii. 38.;<BR>r. elephant:<BR>प्रतिद्विपः, Ki. xvii. 45.;<BR>(2) समान<BR>(f. ना = equal),<BR>r. s in learning are as a rule<BR>jealous of each other's fame:<BR>प्रायः समानविद्या<BR> परस्परयशःपुरोभागाः, Mal. i. 19.;<BR>(3) प्रतियोगिन्<BR>(f. नी);<BR>(4) सपत्नी (a r. wife),<BR>r. rills:<BR>सपत्नी-<BR>र्निम्नगाः, Si. ii. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rival
RIVAL (v.):<BR>I To emulate: q. v.: स्पर्धते<BR>(स्पर्ध्, c. 1.).<BR>II To excel: q. v.: अतिशेते<BR>(शी, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rivalry
RIVALRY:<BR>(1) स्पर्धा (= emulation);<BR>(2) प्रति-<BR>योगिता (= competition);<BR>(3) विरोधः (= con-<BR>-test, opposition: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rive
RIVE: विदारयति (c. of दॄ): v. To tear, split.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

river
RIVER:<BR>(1) नदी (or नदः, of a few r. s — the Indus<BR>सिन्धुः, the Brahmaputra ब्रह्मपुत्रः<BR>or<BR>लौहित्यः, the<BR>Śon शोणः, etc.),<BR>r. bank:<BR>नदीकूलम्; r. diver:<BR>नदीष्णः, R. xvi. 75.;<BR>r. -irrigated:<BR>नदीमातृक<BR>(f. का), M.n. on Ki. i. 17.;<BR>r. fish:<BR>नादेयो<BR> मत्स्यः;<BR>(2) सरित् (f.);<BR>(3) सिन्धुः (f.: rare);<BR>(4) आपगा, Sr.; निम्नगा, तरड्गिणी, स्रोतस्वती, etc.<BR>(poet.);<BR>(5) धुनी (or निः: rare), A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rivet
RIVET (v.): निबध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.),<BR>with r. ed<BR>attention:<BR>निबद्धलक्ष्येण, K. : v. To fasten,<BR>bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rivet
RIVET (subs.):<BR>(1) कीलः, -कः;<BR>(2) शलाका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rivulet
RIVULET:<BR>(1) क्षुद्रसरित् (f.) and sim. comp. s.;<BR>(2) कुसरित् (f.);<BR>(3) निम्नगा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rix-dollar
RIX-DOLLAR: मुद्राविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

road
ROAD:<BR>(1) मार्गः,<BR>high r.:<BR>राजमार्गः;<BR>of r. -side<BR>trees:<BR>मार्गशाखिनाम्, R. i. 45.; looking for r. s:<BR>मार्गैषिन् (f. णी), R. xvi. 31.;<BR>(2) पथिन् (m.:<BR>पथ- in comp. s),<BR>although the r. is not straight<BR>to you:<BR>वक्रः पन्था यदपि भवतः, Me. i. 28.;<BR>making and clearing r. s in the dense forest:<BR>कुर्वन्तः शोधयन्तश्च पन्थानो गहने वने, Ram. ii. 87. 7.;<BR>bad r. (i. e. vicious course): अपन्थाः, An. i.<BR>4.;<BR>where four r. s meet:<BR>चतुष्पथम्, Mit.;<BR>(3)<BR>अध्वन् (m.),<BR>on the r.:<BR>अध्वनि, R. v. 60.;<BR>the<BR>remainder of the r.:<BR>अध्वशेषम्, Me. i. 39.;<BR>(4) वर्त्मन् (n.), from the beaten r.:, क्षुण्णाद्वर्त्मनः,<BR>R. i. 17.;<BR>(5) रथ्या (= high r.),<BR>r. embellish-<BR>ment:<BR>रथ्यासंस्कारः, R. xv. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roam
ROAM (v.):<BR>(1) भ्रमति<BR>or<BR>भ्राम्यति, परि-, (भ्रम्, c.<BR>1. and 4.),<BR>r. ing over countries:<BR>भ्रान्त्वा देशम्,<BR>J.;<BR>(2) अटति, परि-, (अट्, c. 1.),<BR>one day<BR>r. ing:<BR>एकदा पर्यटन्, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roaming
ROAMING (subs.):<BR>(1) भ्रमणम्, परि-;<BR>(2) अटनम्,<BR> परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roan
ROAN (adj.): शुक्लबिन्दुकर्बुरित (f. ता), कृष्ण (f.<BR>ष्णा) and sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roar
ROAR (v.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) गर्जति, परि-, (गर्ज्,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>r. ing fiercely like r. ing clouds:<BR>गर्ज-<BR>त्पर्जन्यघोरस्तनितम्, Vi. v. 53.;<BR>(2) स्तनति (स्तन्,<BR>c. 1.: rare);<BR>(3) हुंकुरुते (as of a lion),<BR>r. s<BR>after thunder:<BR>अनुहुंकुरुते घनध्वनिम्, Si. xvi.<BR>25.;<BR>(4) by subs., like the r. ing Nerbuddā:<BR>रेवेव महाविरावा, R. xvi. 31.: v. Noise.<BR>II<BR>In distress: क्रोशति, वि-, (क्रुश्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roar
ROAR, -ING (subs.):<BR>(1) गर्जनम्<BR>or<BR>गर्जितम्, परि-;<BR>(2) स्तनितम्;<BR>(3) हुंकारः, -कृतिः(तं): v. Also<BR>cry, noise, scream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roast
ROAST (v.):<BR>(1) शूलाकरोति (on a spit), S. k.;<BR>(2) भृज्जति (भ्रस्ज्, c. 6. = to fry: q. v.: also<BR>fig.),<BR>r. ed Rāvaṇa:<BR>बभ्रज्ज रावणम्, B. xiv. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roast
ROAST (adj.): i. e. r. ed on spit: शूल्य (f. ल्या),<BR>we have to eat food chiefly consisting of r. meat:<BR>शूल्यमांसभूयिष्ठ आहारोऽश्यते, Sa. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rob
ROB (v.):<BR>(1) हरति, अप- (हृ, c. 1.), by r. bing you,<BR>say, what has (he)<BR>not r. bed me of:<BR>हरता त्वां<BR> वद किं न मे हृतम्, R. viii. 67.;<BR>(2) मुष्णाति (मुष्,<BR>c. 9. = to steal: q. v.),<BR>r. bing the ocean of<BR>its beauty:<BR>पयोधिलक्ष्मीमुष् (mfn.), N. i. 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

robber
ROBBER:<BR>(1) दस्युः;<BR>(2) तस्करः;<BR>(3) लुब्धः, -कः:<BR>v. Also thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

robbery
ROBBERY:<BR>I The act: हरणम्, अप-।<BR>II In<BR>law:<BR>(1) प्रसमहरणम्, Mit.;<BR>(2) साहसं चौर्यम्,<BR>N.s.<BR>III Robber's state:<BR>(1) दस्युता;<BR>(2)<BR>तास्कर्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

robe
ROBE:<BR>I Subs: वसनम्: v. Dress, cloth.<BR>II<BR>Verb: वस्ते (वस्, c. 2.): v. To dress,<BR>clothe. R. d: v. Clad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

robin
ROBIN: a bird: पक्षिविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

robust
ROBUST:<BR>(1) दृढाङ्ग (f. ङ्गी);<BR>(2) वज्रसंहनन (f.<BR>ना = very r.): v. Strong, muscular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

robustness
ROBUSTNESS: दृढाङ्गता and sim. expr. s: v.<BR>Also strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rock
ROCK (subs.):<BR>(1) शिलोच्चयः;<BR>(2) शिला: v.<BR>Stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rock
ROCK (v.):<BR>I Intrans.: दोलायते (nomi.): v.<BR>Also to move, shake.<BR>II Trans.: दोलयति<BR>(दुल, c. 10.): v. Also to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rock-salt
ROCK-SALT:<BR>(1) सैन्धवम्, -लवणम्;<BR>(2) शीतशिवम्,<BR>A.;<BR>(3) माणिबमन्थम्, A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rocket
ROCKET: perh. हम्बा<BR>or<BR>हम्बतारा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rocky
ROCKY:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) शिलामय (f. यी)<BR>and sim. deriv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rod
ROD:<BR>(1) दण्डः;<BR>(2) यष्टिः;<BR>(3) वेत्रम् (= cane).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rodomontade
RODOMONTADE:<BR>(1) गर्वितवाक्यम्;<BR>(2) उद्धतवचस्<BR>(n.) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roe
ROE:<BR>I Of fishes:<BR>(1) मत्स्याण्डम् and sim.<BR>comp. s;<BR>(2) मत्स्यगर्भः, r. is highly aphrodisiac:<BR>मत्स्यगर्भो भृशं वृष्यः, Bha.<BR>III Female deer:<BR>मृगी etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roe
ROE, ROEBUCK: a deer: कुरङ्गः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rogation
ROGATION:<BR>I Demand: अनुयोगः (?).<BR>II<BR>Litany: सूक्तम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rogue
ROGUE:<BR>(1) धूर्त (f. र्ता), r. s live by snares:<BR>जालोपजीविनी धूर्ताः, K. s. xxiv. 199.;<BR>(2) वञ्चक<BR>(f. ञ्चिका = cheat),<BR>where is the r. now:<BR>स<BR> वञ्चकः क्वास्ते, H. ;<BR>(3) शठ (f. ठा),<BR>hypocrites<BR>and r. s:<BR>वैडालव्रतिकान् शठान्, V.p. iii. 18. 99.;<BR>(4) खल (f. ला) (=mischievous);<BR>(5) दुर्जनः<BR>(= bad man).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roguery
ROGUERY, ROGUISHNESS:<BR>(1) धूर्तता;<BR>(2) खलता;<BR>(3) शठता<BR>or<BR>शाठ्यम् (cheating);<BR>(4) दौर्जन्यम्<BR>(= wickedness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roguish
ROGUISH: expr. by comp.: v. Rogue,<BR>knavish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roguishly
ROGUISHLY:<BR>(1) धूर्तवत् (= like a rogue);<BR>(2)<BR>शाठ्येन: v. Deceitfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roll
ROLL (v. t.):<BR>I To revolve:<BR>(1) भ्र(भ्रा)मयति,<BR> परि- (c. of भ्रम्),<BR>r. ing all beings:<BR>भ्रामयन् सर्व-<BR>भूतानि, G. xviii. 61.;<BR>(2) घूर्णयति, वि-, परि- (c.<BR>of घूर्ण्),<BR>r. ing the eyes:<BR>दृशौ घूर्णयन्, Si. ii. 16.<BR>II On the ground: लोट(ठ)यति (c. of लुट्<BR>or<BR>लुठ्).<BR>III To r. up, wrap round on<BR>itself:<BR>(1) पिण्डीकरोति;<BR>(2) संपुटीकरोति।<BR>IV<BR>To enwrap, encircle: q. v.: वेष्टयति, परि-<BR>(c. of वेष्ट्).<BR>V To press with a r. er:<BR>(1)<BR>वेल्लति (वेल्ल्, c. 1.: to r. flour etc. for cake);<BR>(2) समीकरोति (= to level).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roll
ROLL (v. i.):<BR>I On the ground:<BR>(1) लुठति or<BR>लुट्यति, प्र-, वि-, (लुठ्, c. 1. and लुट्, c. 4.),<BR>r. ing<BR>on the ground:<BR>लुट्यन् भुवि, B. iii. 32;<BR>(2)<BR>वेल्लति (वेल्ल्, c. i.),<BR>to r. on the ground:<BR>भुवि<BR> वेल्लनाय, Si. v. 53;<BR>(3) परिवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1. =<BR>turn round),<BR>r. ing on the ground:<BR>स्थलीषु<BR> परिवृत्य, Si. v: 55.<BR>II To revolve: q. v.:<BR>भ्रमति (भ्रम्, c. 1.),<BR>the Ganges r. ed over<BR>the god's head for one year:<BR>गङ्गा शिरसि<BR> देवस्य संवत्सरं बभ्राम, Ram. i. 45. 8.<BR>III To r.<BR>on or away = to pass away: q. v.: गच्छति,<BR>“time r.s on”:<BR>कालो गच्छति, J. IV. To r.<BR>over and over: व्यावर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.),<BR>by the<BR>r. ings of the snake-king:<BR>व्यावर्तनैरहिपतेः, Ki. V.<BR>To move: q. v. Ph.:<BR>r. -ed out at the foot of<BR>the Vindhyas:<BR>विन्ध्यपादे विशीर्णाम्, Me. i. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roll
ROLL (subs.):<BR>I R. ing:<BR>(1) लुठनम्<BR>or<BR>लुठितम्;<BR>(2) भ्रान्तिः;<BR>(3) व्यावर्तनम्; for dif.: v. To roll.<BR>II Anything r. ed:<BR>(1) by adj.: पिण्डित (f.<BR>ता), सं-, परि, (= r. ed up);<BR>(2) नाली (= tube:<BR>in comp. s),<BR>r. of cotton:<BR>तूलनाली।<BR>III R. er:<BR>q. v.<BR>IV Of bread: no equiv.: *गोलकः।<BR>V<BR>A document, register, list: q. v.: पत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roller
ROLLER:<BR>I A cylinder:<BR>(1) perh. वर्तनी;<BR>(2)<BR>वेल्लनम्, -नी (for rolling flour), वेलयेद्वेल्लनेनैताः,<BR>Bha.<BR>II A bandage: q. v.: पट्टः।<BR>III A<BR>bird: लोट(ठ)नः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

romance
ROMANCE:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) आख्यायिका (= story);<BR>(2) अद्भुतकथा and sim. comp. s.<BR>II Verb: to<BR>write, tell r. s: expr. by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

romantic
ROMANTIC:<BR>I Strange, fanciful: q. v.: अद्भुत<BR>(f. ता).<BR>II Chivalrous, brave: q. v.<BR>III<BR>Of deeds: perh. रोमहर्षण (f. णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

romp
ROMP, -ING (subs.): विहारः: v. Sport, frolic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

romp
ROMP (v.): विहरति: v. To sport, frolic, frisk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rood
ROOD: expr. by निवर्तनम् (= half r. or 20<BR>rods), Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roof
ROOF (subs.):<BR>(1) छदिः;<BR>(2) पटलम;<BR>(3) by cir-<BR>-cumlo., left the window and went up to the r.:<BR>विमुच्य तं गवाक्षं सौधस्योपरितनं शिखरमारुरोह, K.<BR>Ph.:<BR>bamboo framework of a r.:<BR>गोपानसी, Si.<BR>iii. 49.; वंशपञ्जरः, M.n.;<BR>edge of a r.:<BR>नीध्रम्,<BR> बलीकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roof
ROOF (v.):<BR>(1) छादयति (छद्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) by<BR>subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roofless
ROOFLESS:<BR>I Lit.: निष्पटल (f. ला) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR>II Fig., homeless, unsheltered:<BR>निराश्रय (f. या) and sim. comp. s. living r.:<BR>अनिकेतवासिन् (f. नी), Ku. v. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rook
ROOK: काकविशेषः: v. Crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rookery
ROOKERY: काकाश्रयः or in gen. खगाश्रयः and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

room
ROOM:<BR>I Space: q. v.: अवसरः।<BR>II Place:<BR>q. v.: भूमिः।<BR>III An apartment: कोष्ठः।<BR>Top-r.:<BR>(1) चन्द्रशाला;<BR>(2) शिरोगृहम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roominess
ROOMINESS:<BR>(1) असम्बाधता;<BR>(2) विशालता;<BR>(3)<BR>विस्तीर्णता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roomy
ROOMY:<BR>(1) असम्बाध (f. धा);<BR>(3) विशाल (f.<BR>ला): v. Spacious, large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roost
ROOST:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) वासयष्टिः;<BR>(2) यष्टिनिवासः,<BR>R. xvi. 14.; and sim. comp. s.<BR>II Verb:<BR>शेते (शी, c. 2.),<BR>r. ing on trees:<BR>वृक्षेशयाः, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

root
ROOT (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: भूलम्, r. of a tree:<BR>तरुमूलम्, Sa.;<BR>a hurricane does not pluck up<BR>grass by the r.:<BR>तृणानि नोन्मूलयति प्रभञ्जनः, H. ii.<BR>81. Ph.:<BR>Fibrous r.:<BR>शिफा<BR>or<BR>जटा; bulbous r.:<BR>कन्द (mn.).<BR>II Fig.: मूलम्, the r. of faults:<BR>मूलं दोषस्य, Ki. xi. 20.;<BR>with pure progeny from<BR>the r.:<BR>आमूलशुद्धसन्तति, Sa. vi. 28.;<BR>destroying<BR>by the r.:<BR>समूलघातमघ्नन्तः, Si. ii. 33.;<BR>firmly<BR>taken r.:<BR>स्थिरबद्धमूल (f. ला), B. xi. 5.: v.<BR>Also cause, source.<BR>III In arith.: मूलम्,<BR>cube r.:<BR>घनमूलम्, Li.;<BR>to extract a r.:<BR>मूली-<BR>करोति, A.c.<BR>IV Of words: प्रकृतिः। Ph.:<BR>verbal r.:<BR>धातुः;<BR>secondary r.:<BR>नामधातुः;<BR>names<BR>are derived from r. s:<BR>नाम च धातुजम्, Kāśikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

root
ROOT (v.): मूलं बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.). R. ed:<BR>(1) बद्धमूल (f. ला);<BR>(2) रूढमूल (f. ला), M.n.<BR>on Si. i. 38.<BR>R. up or out:<BR>उन्मूलयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rootlet
ROOTLET: शिफा<BR>or<BR>जटा (= fibrous root).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rope
ROPE:<BR>(1) रज्जुः;<BR>(2) दामन् (nf.): v. Also<BR>band.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rope-dancer
ROPE-DANCER:<BR>(1) कलायनः;<BR>(2) सूत्रायणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rope-walk
ROPE-WALK: perh. रज्जुशाला, रज्जुनिर्माणशाला, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ropiness
ROPINESS: चिक्कणता,: v. Stinginess, adhesive-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ropy
ROPY: fig.: चिक्कण (f. णा): v. Glutinous,<BR>viscous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rosary
ROSARY:<BR>I Lit.: perh. सेवतोग्रामः।<BR>II Devo-<BR>-tional:<BR>(1) अक्षमाला;<BR>(2) अक्षसूत्रम्;<BR>(3) जपमाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rose
ROSE:<BR>(1) सेवती;<BR>(2) शतपत्री;<BR>(3) लाक्षा, Bha.;<BR>oil of r.:<BR>लाक्षातैलम् (?);<BR>r. -water:<BR>सेवतीतैलम्<BR>(?).<BR>China-r.:<BR>जवा(पा). R. -apple (both the<BR>tree and its fruit) जम्बूः।<BR>R. -wood:<BR>दारुविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roseate
ROSEATE: v. Rosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rosemary
ROSEMARY: लताविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rosin
ROSIN: v. Resin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rostrum
ROSTRUM:<BR>I Platform: पीठः।<BR>II Beak:<BR>चञ्चुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rosy
ROSY:<BR>(1) पाटल (f. ला);<BR>(2) राजत् (f. न्ती<BR>= blooming).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rot
ROT (v.):<BR>I Intrans:<BR>(1) पूतीभवति (= put-<BR>-refy);<BR>(2) गलति (गल्, c. 1. = be decom-<BR>-posed).<BR>II Trans.:<BR>(1) पूतीकरोति;<BR>(2)<BR>गालयति (c. of गल्). For fig. sense: v. To<BR>spoil, corrupt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rotation
ROTATION:<BR>I Revolution: q. v.: चक्रभ्रमणम्,<BR>from the r. of the planets round the earth:<BR>ग्रहाणां<BR> भूमेः परितो भ्रमणतः, A.c.<BR>II Succession:<BR>पर्यायवृत्तिः,<BR>in r.:<BR>पर्यायेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rotatory
ROTATORY, ROTARY:<BR>r. motion<BR>चक्रभ्रमणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rote
ROTE:<BR>(1) आवृत्तिः;<BR>(2) अभ्यासः। Ph.: learnt by<BR>r.:<BR>(1) मुखस्थ (f. स्था):<BR>(2) कण्ठस्थ (f. स्था).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rotten
ROTTEN:<BR>I Putrid: पूत (f. ता).<BR>II Defec-<BR>-tive, spoiled: दुष्ट (f. ष्टा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rottenness
ROTTENNESS:<BR>I Putridity: पूतिः।<BR>II Un-<BR>-soundness: दुष्टता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rotunda
ROTUNDA (o): perh. सर्वतोभद्रम्, Mat. 253. ch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rotundity
ROTUNDITY: वर्तुलता: v. Roundness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rouge
ROUGE (v.): मञ्जिष्ठादिना रञ्जयति, अनु- (रञ्ज्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rough
ROUGH:<BR>I To the touch:<BR>(1) बन्धु(न्धु)र (f.<BR>रा);<BR>(2) विषम (f. मा), you will have r. steps:<BR>पदानि खलु ते विषमीभवन्ति, Sa. iv. 14.;<BR>(3) नतोन्नत<BR>(f. ता = up and down).<BR>II Harsh, severe:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) रु(रू)क्ष (f. क्षा),<BR>r. mind:<BR>रूक्षचेतस्<BR>(mfn.), K.<BR>(2) कर्कश (f. शा).<BR>III Coarse,<BR>clumsy: q. v.: स्थूल (f. ला), r. measurement:<BR>स्थूलमानम्, Li.<BR>IV Tempestuous, boisterous:<BR>q. v.: क्षुब्ध (f. ब्धा), सं-, प्र-, वि-, r. sea:<BR>क्षुब्धार्णवः, V.p.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rough-cast
ROUGH-CAST:<BR>I Subs.: स्थुललेपः (?).<BR>II<BR>Verb: स्थूललेपेन लिम्पति, वि-, (लिप्, c. 6.):<BR>v. Also to whitewash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rough-draw
ROUGH-DRAW: perh. स्थूलम्<BR>or<BR>मन्दं लिखति, आ-<BR>(लिख्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roughen
ROUGHEN:<BR>I Trans.:<BR>(1) बन्धुरीकरोति;<BR>(2)<BR>रूक्षीकरोति, etc., the body r. ed with dust:<BR>पांशुरूक्षीकृताङ्ग (f. ङ्गी), Mr. x. 2.: for dif.: v.<BR>Rough.<BR>II Intrans:<BR>(1) बन्धुरीभवति;<BR>(2)<BR>रूक्षीभवति; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rough-hew
ROUGH-HEW: perh. स्थूलं तक्षति (तक्ष्, c. 1.) or<BR>विदधाति (धा, c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roughly
ROUGHLY:<BR>I To the touch: expr. by adj.<BR>II Harshly, severely:<BR>(1) रूक्षम्;<BR>(2) कर्कशम्;<BR>(3) परुषम्।<BR>III Coursely: स्थूलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roughness
ROUGHNESS:<BR>I Unevenness:<BR>(1) बन्धु(न्धू)रता;<BR>(2) वैषम्यम्।<BR>II Harshness, severity:<BR>(1) रौक्ष्यम्<BR>or<BR>रु(रू)क्षता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2) कार्कश्यम् or<BR>कर्कशता, -त्वम्।<BR>III Coarseness: स्थूलता।<BR>IV<BR>Tempestuousness: क्षुब्धता, सं-, वि-, प्र-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rough-shod
ROUGH-SHOD:<BR>(1) बद्धनाल (f. ला: (?);<BR>(2)<BR>सनाल (f. ला: (?); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

round
ROUND (adj.):<BR>I Circular, globular:<BR>(1)<BR>वर्तुल (f. ला);<BR>(2) by गोलः (ला, लं): v.<BR>Globe, globular:<BR>(3) वृत्ताकार (f. रा) and<BR>sim. comp. s,<BR>the r. earth:<BR>वृत्ताकारो भूगोलः, A.c.<BR>II Complete: समग्र (f. ग्रा), in r. numbers:<BR>सभग्रसंख्यया।<BR>III Decided, frank: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

round
ROUND (subs.):<BR>I A circle, globe: q. v.:<BR>मण्डलम्,<BR>to go r. s:<BR>मण्डलशश्चरति, Mah.<BR>II Cir-<BR>-cuit: q. v.: परिभ्रमणम्।<BR>III Revolution:<BR>q. v.: परिभ्रमणम्।<BR>IV Cycle, succession:<BR>q. v.: पर्यायः।<BR>V A r. dance: मण्डलनृत्यम्।<BR>VI Of a ladder: भङ्गिः: v. Step.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

round
ROUND (prop.):<BR>(1) परि- in comp., to go r.:<BR>पर्येति, Su. xii. 16.;<BR>(2) परितः (with acc.):<BR>v. Around.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

round
ROUND (adv.):<BR>(1) परि- in comp., to move r.:<BR>पर्यटति, Su. xii. 19.;<BR>(2) मण्डलशः (= circular-<BR>-ly r. and r.): v. Also around. Ph.:<BR>all<BR>the year r.:<BR>समग्रवर्षम्, and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

round
ROUND (v.):<BR>I To make r.: वर्तुलीकरोति, and<BR>sim. deriv.<BR>II To encircle, surround:<BR>q. v.: परिगच्छति (गम्, c. 1.).<BR>III To finish,<BR>complete: q. v.: समादधाति (धा, c. 3.). Ph.:<BR>well-r. ed:<BR>संस्कृत (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roundabout
ROUNDABOUT (adj.): वक्र (f. क्रा): v. Cir-<BR>-cuitous, crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roundly
ROUNDLY:<BR>I Plainly, openly: q. v.: स्पष्टम्।<BR>II Briskly, vigorously: q. v.: वामम्।<BR>III<BR>Circularly: मण्डलशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roundness
ROUNDNESS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) वर्तुलता;<BR>(2) गोलता;<BR>(3) वृत्ताकारता; etc.<BR>II Neatness, finish:<BR>q. v.: संस्कारः।<BR>III Plainness: स्पष्टता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rouse
ROUSE: बोधयति (c. of बुध्): v. To arouse,<BR>excite, awake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rout
ROUT (subs.):<BR>I Mob, crowd: q. v.: जन-<BR>संमर्दः, and sim. comp. s.<BR>II Defeat: q. v.:<BR>भङ्गः।<BR>III Noise, uproar: q. v.: कोलाहलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rout
ROUT (v.): भनक्ति (भञ्ज्, c. 7.): v. To de-<BR>-feat, beat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

route
ROUTE: पथिन् (m.): v. Road, way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

routine
ROUTINE: क्रमः: v. Course. Ph.: r. work:<BR>नित्यकर्मन् (n.) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rove
ROVE: पर्यटति (अट्, c. 1.): v. To roam, wander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rover
ROVER:<BR>I Wanderer: q. v.<BR>II Robber:<BR>q. v.: लुब्धः, -कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

roving
ROVING (subs.):<BR>(1) पर्यटनम्;<BR>(2) परिभ्रमणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

row
ROW (v.):<BR>(1) वाहयति (c. of वह्);<BR>(2) प्रेरयति,<BR>(ईर्, c. 10.);<BR>(3) चोदयति, सं-, प्र- (चुद्, c.<BR>10.),<BR>r ed by boat-men:<BR>नाविकैश्चोदिता, Ram.<BR>ii. 52. 15. Ph.:<BR>by r. ing:<BR>दाशानां भुजवेगेन,<BR>Mah. i. 148. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

row
ROW (subs.):<BR>I Line:<BR>(1) पंक्तिः;<BR>(2) श्रेणिः(णी);<BR>(3) राजिः।<BR>II Disturbance, quarrel: q. v.:<BR>कलहः, U. vi. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rowel
ROWEL: perh. कण्टक (mn.): v. Also spur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rower
ROWER:<BR>(1) पोतवाहः, -कः;<BR>(2) नाविकः (= sai-<BR>-lor): v. To row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

royal
ROYAL:<BR>(1) by com.,<BR>r. edifice:<BR>राजभवनम्: v.<BR>King, queen;<BR>(2) राजार्ह (f. र्हा); राजयोग्य<BR>(f. ग्या), and sim. comp. s (= worthy of a<BR>king);<BR>(3) राजकीय (f. या) and sim. deriv.<BR>(= belonging to a king).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

royalist
ROYALIST: राज- (or राज्ञी-) अनुगत (f. ता) and.<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

royally
ROYALLY:<BR>(1) राजवत्, Si. xv. 15.;<BR>(2) नृपवत्;<BR>(3) राजार्हम्, नृपयोग्यम्, and sim. comp. s (= be-<BR>-fitting a king).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

royalty
ROYALTY:<BR>(1) राजत्वम्, -ता, and sim. comp. s.,<BR>r. by birth:<BR>गर्भेश्वरत्वम्, K. : v. King;<BR>(2) राज-<BR>महिमा (= majesty) and sim. comp. s.,<BR>r. is<BR>inaccessible:<BR>दुरासदो राजमहिमा, Mal.;<BR>(3) by<BR>comp.,<BR>ensigns of r.:<BR>राजलक्षणानि (n. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rub
RUB (v.):<BR>I In gen.: घर्षति, उत्-, नि-, विनि-,<BR> सं-, (घृष्, c. 1.),<BR>r. bed diadems:<BR>चूडामणिभिरु-<BR>द्घृष्ट (f. ष्टा), R. xvii. 28.;<BR>r. bing his ring<BR>against a bed of red arsenic:<BR>निघृष्याङ्गुलिं मनःशिला-<BR>गिरौ, Ram. ii. 105. 17.<BR>II To besmear:<BR>q. v.: अभ्यनक्ति (अञ्ज्, c. 7.).<BR>III To sham-<BR>-poo: q. v.: संवाहयति (c. of वह्).<BR>IV To r.<BR>down, out, off, away, i. e. to cleanse, erase:<BR>q. v.: प्र-मार्ष्टि<BR>or<BR>मार्जयति (मृज्, c. 2. and c. 10).<BR>V To r. off, i. e. wear away: q. v.: क्षीयते<BR>(pass. of क्षी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rub
RUB (subs.):<BR>I The act;<BR>(1) घर्षः, -णम्, नि-,<BR> विनि-, उत्-, सं-;<BR>(2) संवाहनम्;<BR>(3) अभ्यञ्जनम्;<BR>(4) संमार्जनम्: for dif.: v. To rub.<BR>II Obs-<BR>-truction, difficulty: q. v.: अन्तरायः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rubber
RUBBER:<BR>I Lit.: घर्षक (f. र्षिका), etc.<BR>II<BR>Whetstone: शाणः।<BR>III A towel: मार्जनी।<BR>IV In cards: *संघर्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rubbing
RUBBING (subs.): v. Rub (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rubbish
RUBBISH:<BR>(1) अप(व)स्करः;<BR>(2) उच्छिष्ठम् (= re-<BR>-fuse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rubbishy
RUBBISHY: i. e. worthless: q. v.: असार (f. रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rubicund
RUBICUND:<BR>(1) आरक्त (f. क्ता);<BR>(2) रिष्द्रक्त<BR>(f. क्ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rubric
RUBRIC:<BR>(1) व्यवस्था;<BR>(2) विधिः (= injunction).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruby
RUBY:<BR>I Subs.;<BR>(1) पद्मरागः;<BR>(2) माणिक्यम्;<BR>(3) ताम्राश्मः and sim. comp. s (poet.).<BR>II<BR>Adj.:<BR>(1) माणिक्यद्युति (mfn.) and sim. comp. s<BR>(in colour);<BR>(2) पद्मराग, etc. in comp. (= of<BR>r. ies).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruck
RUCK:<BR>I Fold, wrinkle: भङ्गिः (?).<BR>II =mob:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rudder
RUDDER:<BR>(1) अरित्रम्, with r. s moving constantly [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">Page607</a>]<BR>on both sides like feet:<BR>लोलैररित्रैश्चरणैरिवाभितः,<BR>Si. xii. 71.;<BR>(2) केनिपातः, -कः, A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruddiness
RUDDINESS: रक्तिमन्: v. Redness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruddy
RUDDY: रक्त (f. क्ता): v. Red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rude
RUDE:<BR>I Uncivil, impolite, insolent: q. v.:<BR>(1) अविनीत (f. ता);<BR>(2) अशिष्ट (f. ष्टा).<BR>II<BR>Boorish, unpolished:<BR>(1) ग्राम्य- in comp.;<BR>(2) असंस्कृत (f. ता).<BR>III Rough, clumsy:<BR>q. v.: स्थूल (f. ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rudely
RUDELY: expr. by adj.: v. Also insolently,<BR>roughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rudeness
RUDENESS:<BR>(1) अशिष्टता;<BR>(2) अविनीतता;<BR>(3)<BR>ग्राम्यता;<BR>(4) स्थूलता: for dif.: v. Rude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rudiment
RUDIMENT:<BR>(1) आरम्भः, प्र-,: v. Beginning;<BR>(2) उपक्रमः,<BR>r. s of grammar:<BR>उपक्रमणिका, Vidyā-<BR>-sāgara;<BR>(3) बीजम् (= germ, seed: q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rudimentary
RUDIMENTARY:<BR>(1) आदि- in comp.: v. First;<BR>(2) अपक्व (f. क्वा = immature).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rue
RUE:<BR>I Subs., potherb: ब्राह्मी।<BR>II Verb:<BR>शोचति (शुच्, c. 1.): v. To mourn, repent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rueful
RUEFUL: शोकाकुल (f. ला): v. Mournful,<BR>sorrowful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruff
RUFF:<BR>I A collar: गलबन्धविशेषः।<BR>II A bird:<BR>कपोतजातीयपक्षिविशेषः।<BR>III A fish: मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruffian
RUFFIAN:<BR>(1) आततायिन् (m.);<BR>(2) दस्युः;<BR>(3)<BR>साहसिकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruffianly
RUFFIANLY: r. conduct: v. Savage, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruffle
RUFFLE (v.):<BR>I To fold, wrinkle: q. v.<BR>II<BR>To agitate, discompose, throw into con-<BR>-fusion: q. v.: क्षोभयति, वि-, सं-, प्र-,<BR>r. d:<BR>क्षुब्ध<BR>(f. ब्धा), क्षोभं गत (f. ता), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruffle
RUFFLE (subs.):<BR>I Frill: फुल्लाञ्चलः (?).<BR>II<BR>Agitation, commotion: q. v.: क्षोभः, सं-,<BR> वि-।<BR>III Fold, plait: भङ्गिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rug
RUG:<BR>(1) कम्बलः (= shawl);<BR>(2) आस्तरः, -णम्,<BR>(= carpet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rugged
RUGGED:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) बन्धु(न्धू)र (f. रा);<BR>(2)<BR>नतोन्नत (f. ता);<BR>(3) विषम (f. मा).<BR>II Harsh,<BR>rude: q. v.: कर्कश (f. शा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruggedness
RUGGEDNESS:<BR>(1) बन्धुरता (as of surface);<BR>(2)<BR>कर्कशता: v. Harshness, roughness, rudeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruin
RUIN (subs.):<BR>I Destruction: q. v.:<BR>(1) नाशः,<BR> वि-, प्र-,<BR>not going to r.:<BR>अविनाशिन् (f. नी), M.<BR>n.;<BR>(2) ध्वंसः, वि-, प्र-, my heart would go to r.:<BR>ध्वंसेत मे हृदयम्, Ki. xi. 57.: v. Defeat, over-<BR>-throw. Ph.: in r. s:<BR>(1) जीर्ण (f. र्णा),<BR>a<BR>garden in r. s:<BR>जीर्णोद्यानम्, Mu. ii.;<BR>(2) विशीर्ण<BR>(f. र्णा),<BR>with hundreds of buildings almost in<BR>r. s:<BR>विशीर्णकल्पाट्टशत (f. ता), R. xvi. 11.<BR>II<BR>Defilement: q. v.: नाशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruin
RUIN (v. t.): नाशयति, वि-, प्र-, (c. of नश्): v.<BR>To destroy, annihilate, defile, injure, over-<BR>-throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruined
RUINED, BE: नश्यति, वि-, प्र-, (नश, c. 4.),<BR>you<BR>are r. for ten sovereigns:<BR>विनष्टोऽसि दशस्वर्णस्य<BR> कारणात्, Mr. ii. 10.: v. Destroyed (be).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruinous
RUINOUS:<BR>I Destructive, injurious: q. v.:<BR>विनाशिन् (f. नी).<BR>II Characterized by or<BR>composed by ruin: नाश, etc. in comp.: v.<BR>Ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruinously
RUINOUSLY: expr. by pres. part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rule
RULE (subs.):<BR>I Reign, government: q. v.:<BR>शासनम्।<BR>II Regulation, precept: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>विधिः। Ph.: conversant with the r. s of grammar:<BR>शब्दशासनविद् (mfn.), Si. xiv. 34.;<BR>(2)<BR>सूत्रम् (= aphorism).<BR>III An instrument: v.<BR>Ruler.<BR>IV Standard measure: प्रमाणम्। Ph.:<BR>r. of three (in arith.): त्रैराशिकम्;<BR>inverse r. of<BR>three:<BR>व्यस्तत्रैराशिकम्, Li.;<BR>double r.:<BR>पञ्चराशिकम्,<BR> सप्तराशिकम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rule
RULE (v.):<BR>I To reign, govern: q. v.: शास्ति,<BR> प्र-, (शास्, c. 2.).<BR>II To regulate, check:<BR>q. v.: शास्ति।<BR>III To lay down as in a deci-<BR>-sion: perh. शास्ति; व्यवस्थापयति (c. of स्था).<BR>IV To mark with lines: perh. रेखाभिर्<BR> अङ्कयति (अङ्क्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruler
RULER:<BR>I Governor:<BR>(1) शासक (f. सिका),<BR>प्र-;<BR>(2) पालयितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(3) शासितृ (f. त्री),<BR>the r. of the ill-behaved:<BR>दुर्विनीतानां शासिता, Sa.<BR>i. 26.<BR>II An instrument^1: *रेखालेखनी।<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruling
RULING (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: v. To rule, reign.<BR>II Predominant, chief: q. v.: प्रबल (f. ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rum
RUM: शीधुः,<BR>old r.:<BR>पुराणशीधुः, R. xvi. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rumble
RUMBLE (v.): रसति, वि-, (रस्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rumbling
RUMBLING (subs.): निर्घोषः: v. Roar, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruminate
RUMINATE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) रोमन्थायते:<BR>(2) रोमन्थम्<BR> अभ्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.), करोति, etc.<BR>II To<BR>meditate, think over: q. v.:<BR>(1) अनुध्यायति<BR>(ध्यै, c. 1.);<BR>(2) संचिन्तयति (चिन्त्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruminating
RUMINATING, RUMINANT (adj.): expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rumination
RUMINATION:<BR>I Lit.: रोमन्थः।<BR>II Medita-<BR>-tion: q. v.: अनुध्यानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rummage
RUMMAGE (v.):<BR>I Verb: अस्तव्यस्तं कृत्वा निपुणम्<BR> अन्विष्यति (इष्, c. 4.): v. To search.<BR>II<BR>Subs., r. ing: expr. by verb or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rumour
RUMOUR (subs.):<BR>(1) लोकप्रवादः and sim.<BR>comp. s,<BR>the r. spread on all sides:<BR>प्रतिदिशं<BR> लोकवादः प्रासर्पत्, D. viii.;<BR>(2) किंवदन्ती;<BR>(3)<BR>जनश्रुतिः;<BR>(4) जनरवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rumour
RUMOUR (v.): expr. by subs.,<BR>it is r. ed:<BR>अस्तीयं<BR> जनश्रुतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rump
RUMP (subs.): स्फिच् (f.): v. Also buttock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rumple
RUMPLE:<BR>I Verb: संपुटीकरोति: v. Also wrinkle,<BR>contract.<BR>II Subs., fold, plait: भङ्गिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

run
RUN (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) धावति, प्र-, परि- (धाव्,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>r. ning through the skies:<BR>गीर्वाणवर्त्मणा<BR> धावन्, K. ii.;<BR>(2) द्रवति, वि-, (द्रु, c. 1.),<BR>they<BR>ran out of fear:<BR>दुद्रुवुस्ते भयात्, Mah.<BR>II To<BR>go, pass:<BR>(1) गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>go;<BR>(2) धावति (rare),<BR>for the road which runs<BR>to it:<BR>अध्वने तत्र धाविते, N. xvii. 114.;<BR>(3) वहति (वह्, c. 1.),<BR>which r.s through<BR>Kalinda:<BR>कलिन्दान्तरवाहिनी, Mat.: v. To flow.<BR>III To melt: q. v.: द्रवति। Ph.: r. to seed:<BR>बीजानि भवन्ति (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

run
RUN (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: धावयति, सं- (c. of धाव्),<BR>if I ride and r. you:<BR>यद्यहं तव पृष्ठे समारुह्य धावयामि,<BR>P. iv. 7.<BR>II To cause to go, move: चालयति,<BR> सं-, (c. of चल्).<BR>III To drive: q. v.:<BR>वाहयति (c. of वह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

run about
RUN ABOUT:<BR>(1) परि-<BR>or<BR>समभि- धावति;<BR>(2)<BR>प्र-द्रवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

run after
RUN AFTER:<BR>(1) अनु-धावति,<BR>ran a. deer:<BR>मृगमन्व-<BR>धावत्, Mah.:<BR>(2) अनुद्रवति: v. To pursue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

run against or towards
RUN AGAINST or TOWARDS:<BR>(1) अभि-<BR>or<BR>प्रति-<BR>धावति,<BR>r. ning a. him:<BR>अभिधावन्, Ki. xiii. 2.;<BR>(2) अभि-, उप-, समुप-<BR>or<BR>प्रति-द्रवति,<BR>or ran a. the<BR>river:<BR>नदीं नु प्रत्यदुद्रुवत्, B. vi. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

run away
RUN AWAY:<BR>(1) अपधावति (rare), M. viii. 54.;<BR>(2) द्रवति, वि-, आ-, प्र-,: v. Also to flee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

run down
RUN DOWN:<BR>I Lit.: विद्रवति: v. To r. after.<BR>II To crush, decry.: q. v.: मृद्राति, अव-,<BR>(मृद्, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

run into
RUN INTO:<BR>I Lit.: द्रवति, rivers r. i. the ocean:<BR>नद्यः समुद्रं द्रवन्ति, G. ii. 28.<BR>II = to become:<BR>q. v.:<BR>r. i. debt:<BR>ऋणग्रस्त (f. स्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

run on
RUN ON:<BR>I Lit.: प्रधावति।<BR>II To continue,<BR>go on: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

run out
RUN OUT:<BR>(1) अवसीयते: v. To end;<BR>(2)<BR>क्षीयते (pass. = be exhausted).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

run over
RUN OVER:<BR>I To overflow: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>trample: अवमृद्राति।<BR>III To go over curso-<BR>-rily: द्रुतं निर्वाचयति (c. of वच्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

run up
RUN UP: वर्धते (वृध्, c. 1.): v. To increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

run
RUN (subs.):<BR>I R. ning:<BR>(1) धावनम्, प्र-;<BR>(2)<BR>द्रवः, -णम्, वि- (sp. r. away).<BR>II Flow: q. v.:<BR>प्रवाहः।<BR>III Extent, reach: q. v.<BR>IV Pre-<BR>-valence: प्रचारः। Ph.: in the long r.: perh.<BR>अवशेषे;<BR>the ordinary r. of mankind:<BR>साधारणम्,<BR> -णलोकाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

runagate
RUNAGATE, RUNAWAY:<BR>(1) विद्रुत (f. ता);<BR>(2) अपधावित (f. ता (?): v. Fugitive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rundle
RUNDLE:<BR>(1) विभङ्गः;<BR>(2) भङ्गिः: v. Step.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

runlet
RUNLET:<BR>(1) निम्नगा;<BR>(2) कृसरित् (f.) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

runner
RUNNER:<BR>I Lit.: धावक (f. विका), प्र-।<BR>II<BR>Courier: जङ्काकारिकः।<BR>III A branch: प्ररोहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rupee
RUPEE:<BR>(1) perh. टङ्कः;<BR>(2) रू(रौ)प्यमुद्रा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rupture
RUPTURE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) भेदः;<BR>(2)<BR>स्फोटः, -नम् (= bursting).<BR>II Fig, breach:<BR>भेदः,<BR>r. between friends:<BR>सुहृद्भेदः, H.: v. Quar-<BR>-rel.<BR>III Hernia: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rupture
RUPTURE (v.):<BR>(1) भिनति (भिद्, c. 7.): v.<BR>To break;<BR>(2) स्फोटयति (c. of स्फुट्): v.<BR>To burst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rural
RURAL:<BR>(1) ग्राम्य (f. म्या): v. Village, rus-<BR>-tic;<BR>(2) जानपद (f. दी),<BR>r. priest:<BR>जानपदो<BR> विप्रः, R. xv. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruse
RUSE: छलम्: v. Stratagem, deceit, artifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rush
RUSH (v.): वेगेन धावति (धाव्, c. 1. = to run:<BR>q. v.)<BR>or<BR>गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.: lit. = to go: q. v.) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">Page609</a>]<BR>or<BR>पतति, आ-, नि-, प्र- (पत्, c. 1.: lit. = to fall),<BR>r. ing headlong into the stream of arrows:<BR>वेगेन<BR> प्रतिमुखमेत्य बाणनद्याः, Ki. xvii. 63.;<BR>an arrow r.<BR>ed out of the Pināka:<BR>निपपात (आदधाव, M.n.)<BR>जवादिषुः पिनाकात्, K. xiii. 20.;<BR>Arjuna r. ed forth<BR>to take the arrow:<BR>आपपात पार्थः शरं जिधृक्षुः, 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rush
RUSH (subs.):<BR>I The act: expr. by verb.<BR>II<BR>Impetuosity: महावेगः।<BR>II A grass: तृणविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rushingly
RUSHINGLY:<BR>(1) महावेगेन;<BR>(2) महाजवेन; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rushlight
RUSHLIGHT: तृणालोकः and sim. comp. s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rushy
RUSHY: *रासमय (f. यी) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rusk
RUSK: a biscuit^1: *रुष्कम्।<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

russet
RUSSET:<BR>I Adj.:<BR>(1) कपिश (f. शा);<BR>(2) श्याव<BR>(f. वा).<BR>II Subs.: an apple: फलविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rust
RUST (v.): expr. by subs. or adj.: v. Rust, -y.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rust
RUST (subs.):<BR>I Of iron:<BR>(1) किट्टम्;<BR>(2)<BR>मण्डूरम्;<BR>(3) सिंहानम् (-णम्) (rare).<BR>II In<BR>gen.: मलम्, “मलं पृथिव्या वाहीकाः”, Mah. viii.<BR>45. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rustic
RUSTIC:<BR>(1) ग्राम्य (f. म्या),<BR>you will know that<BR>men are not r. s:<BR>अग्राम्यतां मनुष्याणां ज्ञास्यसि, K. ;<BR>(2) ग्रामिक (f. की);<BR>(3) ग्रामीय (f. या);<BR>(4) ग्रामीण (f. णा),<BR>r. maidens:<BR>ग्रामीणवध्वः,<BR>Si. xii. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rusticate
RUSTICATE (v.):<BR>I Trans.: निर्वासयति (c. of<BR>वस्): v. To banish.<BR>II To dwell in the<BR>country: जनपदे वसति (वस्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rustication
RUSTICATION: निर्वासनम्: v. Banishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rusticity
RUSTICITY:<BR>(1) ग्राम्यता;<BR>(2) ग्राम्यभावः;<BR>(3)<BR>ग्रामिकता (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rustle
RUSTLE:<BR>(1) मर्मरायते (nomi.);<BR>(2) मर्मरशब्दं<BR> करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rustling
RUSTLING:<BR>I Subs.: मर्मरः।<BR>II Adj.:<BR>(1)<BR>मर्मर (f. रा),<BR>r. leaves:<BR>मर्मरपत्र-, Ku. iii. 31;<BR>(2)<BR>मर्मरशब्दवत् (f. ती), M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rusty
RUSTY:<BR>(1) मलिन (f. ना);<BR>(2) मलीमस (f. सा);<BR>(3) कलङ्कित (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rut
RUT:<BR>I Of animals: व्यवायः: v. Copula-<BR>-tion.<BR>II Of wheels: गर्तः (= hole).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruthless
RUTHLESS: निर्दय (f. या): v. Merciless, un-<BR>-kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruthlessly
RUTHLESSLY: निर्दयम्: v. Mercilessly, un-<BR>-kindly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ruttish
RUTTISH:<BR>(1) मदोन्मत्त (f. त्ता);<BR>(2) मदोत्कट<BR>(f. टा); and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ryot
RYOT: कर्षकः: v. Cultivator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sabaoth
SABAOTH: देवसेना sim. comp. s: v. Army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sabbatarian
SABBATARIAN: विश्रामवारसेविन् (f. नी) and<BR>sim. comp. s (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sabbath
SABBATH: विश्रामवारः<BR>or<BR>-वासरः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sabbatic
SABBATIC, -AL: expr. by comp.: v. Sabbath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sable
SABLE (adj.): श्याम (f. मा): v. Dark, black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sable
SABLE (subs.):<BR>I An animal: *श्यामकः।<BR>II<BR>Its fur: *श्यामकम्, -लोमन् (n.).<BR>III A robe:<BR>श्यामवेषः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sabot
SABOT: काष्ठपादुकाविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sabre
SABRE:<BR>I Subs.: निर्स्त्रिंशः: v. Sword, scimi-<BR>-tar.<BR>II Verb: खङ्गेन<BR>or<BR>निस्त्रिंशेन शिरश्छिनत्ति<BR>(छिद्, c. 7.): v. To cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saccharine
SACCHARINE: perh. शार्कर (f. री)<BR>or<BR>शार्करिक<BR>(f. की): v. Sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sacerdotal
SACERDOTAL: expr. by comp.: v. Priest,<BR>-hood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sachel
SACHEL:<BR>(1) भस्त्रा;<BR>(2) क्षुद्रकोषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sack
SACK (v.):<BR>(1) लुण्ठति (लुण्ठ्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>plunder;<BR>(2) उपप्लवते (प्लु, c. 1.).: v. To<BR>depredate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sack
SACK (subs.):<BR>I A canvas bag: गोणी,<BR>buying<BR>s. s:<BR>गोणीः क्रीत्वा, D.<BR>II Plunder, devasta-<BR>-tion: q. v.: घातः।<BR>III A garment: शाणी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sack-cloth
SACK-CLOTH: शाणम् (= canvas);<BR>(2) गोणीपटः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sackbut
SACKBUT: वाद्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sacker
SACKER:<BR>(1) लुण्ठाक (f. की);<BR>(2) घातक (f. तिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sacking
SACKING (subs.):<BR>I Sack: q. v.<BR>II Sack-<BR>-cloth: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sacrament
SACRAMENT: perh. संस्कारः,<BR>s. of baptism<BR>*जल-<BR>संस्कारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sacramental
SACRAMENTAL: expr. by comp., s. rite:<BR>संस्कारविधिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sacred
SACRED:<BR>(1) पुण्य (f. ण्या),<BR>the most s. Brahma-<BR>kshetra:<BR>ब्रह्मक्षेत्रं महापुण्यम्, Mah. iii. 83. 6.;<BR>s. history:<BR>पुण्या संहिता, i.<BR>I 21.: v. Holy;<BR>(2)<BR>पवित्र (f. त्रा),<BR>s. waters:<BR>पयः पवित्रम्, R. v. 59.; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">Page610</a>]<BR>s. throughout the world:<BR>जगत्पवित्र (f. त्रा), Si.<BR>iii. 2.: v. Pure;<BR>(3) मेध्य (f. ध्या: rare),<BR>full of sweet and s. flavours:<BR>स्वादुमेध्यरसोपेत<BR>(f. ता), Mah. i. 93.: v. Also religious,<BR>inviolable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sacredly
SACREDLY:<BR>(1) परमभक्तया;<BR>(2) साग्रहम् (=<BR>scrupulously).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sacredness
SACREDNESS:<BR>(1) पुण्यता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2) पवित्रता, -त्वम्;<BR>(3) मेध्यता, -त्वम्;<BR>(4) better by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sacrifice
SACRIFICE (subs.):<BR>I The ceremony:<BR>(1)<BR>यज्ञः;<BR>(2) क्रतुः;<BR>(3) यागः;<BR>(4) इज्या;<BR>(5)<BR>होमः;<BR>(6) मखः;<BR>(7) सत्रम्;<BR>(8) सवनम्;<BR>(9)<BR>अध्वरः: for dif.: v. Special works. Ph.:<BR>horse-s.:<BR>अश्वमेधः;<BR>human-s.:<BR>नरमेधः; imperial-s.:<BR>राजसूयः;<BR>present at i.-s.:<BR>राजसूयकीः दक्षिणाः, Si.<BR>xiv. 33.<BR>II Offering, oblation: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>उत्सर्गः (= abandonment, giving up: q. v.),<BR>s. of things in the name of gods is s.:<BR>देवतोद्देशेन द्रव्यत्यागो यागः, M.n. on Si. xiv. 20.;<BR>(2) आलम्भः, सम्- (= killing: of animals).<BR>III In gen.:<BR>(1) उत्सर्गः, s. one's self:<BR>आत्मोत्सर्गः: v. Surrender, destruction;<BR>(2)<BR>व्ययः (= expense: q. v.), at the s. of life:<BR>प्राणव्ययेनापि, Mu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sacrifice
SACRIFICE (v.): यजति, -ते (यज्, c. 1.: religious),<BR>let the son of Pāṇdu s.:<BR>यजतां पाण्डवः, Si. ii.<BR>65.; what (men)<BR>s., give here:<BR>यद्यजन्ति ददतीह,<BR>He.;<BR>(2) त्यजति (त्यज्, c. 1. = to abandon,<BR>give up: q. v.),<BR>s. d things to gods:<BR>अत्यजन्<BR>(अयजन्, M.n.) द्रव्यजातमपदिश्य देवताः। Si. xiv.<BR>20.; s. s (his)<BR>life:<BR>त्यजति प्राणान्, Mu. i. 24.;<BR>(3) आलभते, सम्-, (लभ्, c. 1. = to kill),<BR>Brāhmins s.d the horse according to the pres-<BR>cribed rite:<BR>तं तुरङ्गं यथाशास्त्रमाभन्त द्विजातयः,<BR>Mah. xiv. 89. 1.;<BR>(4) श्रपयति, सं- (= 3), 2.<BR>: v. Also to offer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sacrificer
SACRIFICER:<BR>(1) याजक (f. जिका = sacred s.)<BR>: v. Priest;<BR>(2) यजमान (f. ना - lay s.), Si.<BR>xiv. 22.;<BR>(3) यष्टृ (f. ष्ट्री = 1 and 2);<BR>(4) in<BR>gen. expr. by verb: v. To sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sacrificial
SACRIFICIAL:<BR>(1) by comp.,<BR>s. vessel:<BR>यज्ञपात्रम्;<BR>s. ground:<BR>यज्ञसंस्तरः, Mah.;<BR>s. work:<BR>यज्ञकर्मन्<BR>(n.), Si. xiv. 1.;<BR>(2) यज्ञिय (f. या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sacrilege
SACRILEGE:<BR>(1) देवस्वापहारः<BR>or<BR>-हरणम्, and sim.<BR>comp. s.;<BR>(2) दूषणम् (= profanation, pollu-<BR>-ted).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sacrilegious
SACRILEGIOUS: पाषण्ड- in comp.: v. Also<BR>impious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sacrilegiously
SACRILEGIOUSLY:<BR>(1) पाषण्डवत्;<BR>(2) धर्मं निहत्य<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sacristy
SACRISTY: पुण्यशाला, -आगारम्, and sim. comp. s.<BR>(??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sad
SAD:<BR>I Mournful: q. v.:<BR>(1) शोकाकुल (f. ला);<BR>(2) विषण्ण (f. ण्णा dejected);<BR>(3) म्लान (f. ना),<BR>परि- (= drooping, gloomy: as of the<BR>countenance).<BR>II Causing sorrow:<BR>(1)<BR>शोचनीय (f. या), परि-;<BR>(2) शोकावह (f. हा) and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR>III Naughty, wicked: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sadden
SADDEN: विषण्णीकरोति: v. To grieve, deject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saddle
SADDLE (subs.):<BR>(1) पर्याणम्,<BR>mounting the s. d<BR>Rainbow:<BR>आरोपितपर्याणमिन्द्रायुधमारुह्य, K. ;<BR>took<BR>of the s. from Rainbow:<BR>व्यपनीतपर्याणमिन्द्रायुध-<BR>मकरोत्, R.;<BR>(2) पल्य(र्य)यनम्, Ph.:<BR>both in s.<BR>and in harness:<BR>पृष्ठेषु च रथेषु च, Mah. iv. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saddle
SADDLE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: पर्याणम् आरोपयति (c. of<BR>रुह्), ददाति (दा, c. 3.), etc. (with loc.), K.<BR>: v. To put.<BR>II Fig.: expr. with भारः<BR>(= burden) or by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saddle-bag
SADDLE-BAG: perh. पल्ययन-<BR>or<BR>पर्याणगोणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saddle-bow
SADDLE-BOW: पल्ययन-<BR>or<BR>पर्याण-मुखम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saddle-horse
SADDLE-HORSE: perh. वाहाश्वः and sim. comp. s.<BR>Ph.:<BR>good s.:<BR>साधुवाहिन् (m.), A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saddler
SADDLER: पर्याण-<BR>or<BR>पल्ययन-कारः (f. री: (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sadducee
SADDUCEE: a sect: *सिद्धकाम (f. मा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sadly
SADLY:<BR>I Mournfully:<BR>(1) सशोकम्;<BR>(2) by<BR>adj.<BR>II Strongly: बलवत्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sadness
SADNESS:<BR>(1) विषादः;<BR>(2) विषण्णता;<BR>(3) शोका-<BR>कुलता and sim. deriv.: v. Sorrowfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

safe
SAFE (adj.):<BR>(1) सुरक्षित (f. = well-protected),<BR>and naturally s.:<BR>प्रकृत्या च सुरक्षितम्, Mah. iii.<BR>15. 17.;<BR>(2) सुस्थ (f. स्था = uninjured, as of<BR>parts: v. Healthy, well);<BR>(3) अलङ्घ्य (f. ङ्घ्या<BR>= inviolable),<BR>we are made s. against the<BR>enemies of gods:<BR>त्रिदशप्रतिपक्षस्यालङ्घनीये कृते स्वः,<BR>V. ii.;<BR>(4) निराबाध (f. धा), असम्बाध (f. धा),<BR>and sim. comp. s. (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

safe
SAFE (subs.):<BR>(1) लौहपेटिका (= iron chest);<BR>(2)<BR>कोष्ठः (for stores).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

safe-conduct
SAFE-CONDUCT: अभयपत्रम् and sim. comp.s. (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

safeguard
SAFEGUARD:<BR>(1) रक्षा, अभि-, सं-;<BR>(2) गुप्तिः: v.<BR>Protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

safely
SAFELY:<BR>(1) निराबाधम्;<BR>(2) असम्बाधम्;<BR>(3)<BR>अक्षतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

safety
SAFETY:<BR>(1) रक्षा (= protection);<BR>(2) gen.<BR>expr. by adj.: v. Safe. Ph.: to promise s.:<BR>अभयं ददाति; in s.: v. Safely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

safety-valve
SAFETY-VALVE: *रक्षाविधानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

safflower
SAFFLOWER: कुसुम्भम्,<BR>dyed with s.:<BR>कौसुम्भ<BR>(f. म्भी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saffron
SAFFRON: कुङ्कुमम्, “बाह्लीकदेशसञ्जातं कुङ्कुमं पाण्डुरं<BR> मतम्,” Bha.;<BR>dark-red with s.:<BR>कुङ्कुमारुण (f. णा),<BR>Ki. ix. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sagacious
SAGACIOUS:<BR>(1) तीक्ष्णबुद्धि (mfn.);<BR>(2) सूक्ष्मधी<BR>(n. धि);<BR>(3) चतुर (f. रा = cunning);<BR>(4)<BR>कुशाग्र- (or -ग्रीय) -मति (mfn. = very s.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sagaciously
SAGACIOUSLY:<BR>(1) तीक्ष्णबुद्ध्या;<BR>(2) सूक्ष्मधिया, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sagacity
SAGACITY:<BR>(1) तीक्ष्णबुद्धिः;<BR>(2) सूक्ष्मधीः;<BR>(3)<BR>कुशाग्रमतिः, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sage
SAGE:<BR>I Wise: q. v.: प्राज्ञः (f. ज्ञा). Ph.:<BR>holy s.:<BR>(1) ऋषिः;<BR>(2) मुनिः, even s. s err:<BR>“मुनीनाञ्च मतिभ्रमः।”<BR>II The plant: perh. वर्वरी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sagely
SAGELY: प्राज्ञवत्: v. Wisely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sagittarius
SAGITTARIUS: धनुस् (mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sago
SAGO: *सागुः (both of the palm and the<BR>preparation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sail
SAIL (subs.):<BR>I Of a ship:<BR>(1) वातवसनम्<BR>and sim. comp. s.;<BR>(2) perh. पताका, Mah.<BR>i.; Ram. ii. Ph.:<BR>to set s.:<BR>नावं मुञ्चति,<BR>D. vi.<BR>II A ship: q. v.: नौः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sail
SAIL (v.):<BR>I To be impelled by wind: वायुना<BR> चोद्यते (pass. of चुद्) etc., s. ing against wind:<BR>अननुकूलवातनुन्ना, D. vi.: v. To drive.<BR>II To<BR>set on a voyage: पोतेन (= on a boat) or<BR>समुद्रेण (by sea) गच्छति (गम्, c. 1. etc.),<BR>s. to<BR>the island:<BR>प्रवहणेन द्वीपं गच्छ, K. s. 25.<BR>36.;<BR>s. ed on his ship:<BR>तदीयं यानपात्रमधिरुह्य<BR> प्रतस्थेऽम्बुधिवर्त्मना, 40.; s. ing (vessels): समुद्र-<BR>यायिन् (f. नी) and sim. comp.s, M.n.: v.<BR>Ship, sea, go, pass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sailyard
SAILYARD: *वातवसनसंस्तरः and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sailor
SAILOR:<BR>(1) नाविकः, D. vi.;<BR>(2) कर्णधारः (prop.<BR>= helmsman), K. s. 18. 300.;<BR>(3) पोतवाहः,<BR> -कः and sim. comp. s.: v. Ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saint
SAINT:<BR>(1) सिद्धः, -जनः etc.;<BR>(2) ऋषिः (= sage);<BR>(3) भगवत् (m. = as a title). S. Anthony's fire:<BR>उदर्दः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sainted
SAINTED:<BR>I Sacred: q. v.<BR>II Of the dead:<BR>(1) मुक्तिभाज् (mfn.);<BR>(2) दिवं गत (f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saintly
SAINTLY:<BR>(1) पवित्र (f. त्रा): v. Sacred;<BR>(2) विमल (f. ला): v. Pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sake
SAKE: Ph.:<BR>for the s. of:<BR>-अर्थम्<BR>or<BR>-अर्थे in<BR>comp.: v. For (III, II.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salacious
SALACIOUS: कामुक (f. की): v. Lustful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salad
SALAD: *शाकावदंशः; सारदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salamander
SALAMANDER: गोधाविशेषः, *सौरमन्द्रः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sal-ammoniac
SAL-AMMONIAC: नैशदलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salaried
SALARIED (adj.): वेतनभोगिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salary
SALARY:<BR>(1) वेतनम्,<BR>s. as arranged:<BR>यथाकृतं<BR> वेतनम्, N.s.: v. Pay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sale
SALE: विक्रयः,<BR>after s.:<BR>विक्रयानन्तरम्, Bha.;<BR>non-<BR>delivery after s.:<BR>विक्रयासम्प्रदानम्, Viv.: v. To<BR>sell.<BR>Underhand s.:<BR>अवक्रयः, Y. ii. 243.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saleable
SALEABLE:<BR>(1) विक्रेयः (या, यं),<BR>even a sold<BR>article is s...:<BR>विक्रीतमपि विक्रेयम्, Y. ii. 252.;<BR>(2) विक्रेतव्य (f. व्या) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salesman
SALESMAN:<BR>(1) विक्रेतृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) विक्रयकारिन्<BR>(f. णी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salient
SALIENT: प्रधान (f. ना = chief: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saline
SALINE:<BR>s. taste:<BR>लवणरसः: v. Salt. Ph.: s.<BR>soil:<BR>(1) ऊषरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) ऊषः(षा), V. p.<BR>vi. 5. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saliva
SALIVA:<BR>(1) लाला;<BR>(2) सृणिका (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salivary
SALIVARY, SALIVAL: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salivate
SALIVATE: लालां स्रावयति (c. of स्रु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salivation
SALIVATION: लालास्रवः<BR>or<BR>स्रतिः<BR>or<BR>स्यन्दः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sallow
SALLOW:<BR>(1) आपीत (f. ता = yellowish);<BR>(2)<BR>पाण्डु (mfn. = pale).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sallowness
SALLOWNESS:<BR>(1) आपीतता;<BR>(2) पाण्डुता;<BR>(3)<BR>विवर्णता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sally
SALLY (v.): निष्पतति, अभि-, (पत्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To rush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sally
SALLY (subs.):<BR>I Lit:<BR>(1) निष्पतनम्;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रपातः।<BR>II Fig.: flight:<BR>(1) विलासः;<BR>(2)<BR>विलसितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salmon
SALMON: रोहितनिभो मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saloon
SALOON: शाला: v. Hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salt
SALT (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: लवणम्, sea-water is<BR>(impregnated)<BR>with s. and alkalis:<BR>सामुद्रं जलं<BR> सक्षारलवणम्, Bha.;<BR>cooked with s., ginger and<BR>asafœtida:<BR>सिद्धा लवणार्द्रकहिङ्गुभिः, Bha. Ph.:<BR>sea-s.:<BR>सामुद्रं लवणम्<BR>or<BR>वसिरम्;<BR>black-s.:<BR>विडम्;<BR>Sambher-s.:<BR>वसुकम्;<BR>rock-s.:<BR>सैन्धवम्<BR>or<BR>शीतशिवम्,<BR>A.<BR>II. Fig.: लावण्यम् (?).<BR>III In chem.:<BR>expr. by लवणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salt
SALT (adj.): लवण- in comp., sea of s.-water:<BR>लवणोदः;<BR>s. -mine:<BR>लवणखनिः;<BR>s.-works:<BR>लवण-<BR>शाला (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salt
SALT (v.): लवणीकरोति<BR>or<BR>लवणयति (nomi. ??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salt-cellar
SALT-CELLAR:<BR>(1) लावणिकम्, Wilson;<BR>(2)<BR>लवणभाजनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salted
SALTED (adj.):<BR>(1) लावण (f. णी);<BR>(2) लवण-<BR>संसृष्ट (f. ष्टा) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saltish
SALTISH: ईषल्लवण (f. णा) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saltness
SALTNESS:<BR>(1) expr. by लवणम्;<BR>(2) लवणता,<BR> -त्वम्<BR>or<BR>लावण्यम् (rare), “लावण्यमस्ति बहु तत्र किमत्र<BR> चित्रम्”, Amaru.;<BR>(3) लवणः(-रसः) (of the<BR>taste).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saltpetre
SALTPETRE:<BR>(1) यवक्षारः;<BR>(2) तीक्ष्णरसः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salubrious
SALUBRIOUS:<BR>(1) स्वास्थ्यकर (f. री) and sim.<BR>comp. s.;<BR>(2) निरामय (f. या);<BR>(3) अनाविल<BR>(f. ला), M. vii. 69.;<BR>(4) क्षेम्य (f. म्या), M.<BR>vii. 212.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salubriously
SALUBRIOUSLY: expr. by adj. or comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salubriousness
SALUBRIOUSNESS, SALUBRITY:<BR>(1) स्वास्थ्यकरता;<BR>(2) निरामयता;<BR>(3) अनाविलता; and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salutary
SALUTARY: क्षेमङ्कर (f. रा), B. xii. 6. and sim.<BR>deriv.: v. Also salubrious, beneficial.<BR>useful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salutation
SALUTATION: v. Salute (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salute
SALUTE (subs.):<BR>I Salutation:<BR>(1) अभिवादः,<BR> -नम्;<BR>(2) वन्दना;<BR>(3) प्रणामः<BR>or<BR>प्रणतिः (prop.<BR>= bow);<BR>(4) नमस्कारः (= 3);<BR>(4) नमस्या<BR>(rare), N. xiv. I.<BR>II. Kiss.: q. v.: चुम्बनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salute
SALUTE (v.):<BR>(1) वन्दते, अभि- (वन्द्, c. 1.),<BR>I s.<BR>the parents of the world:<BR>जगतः पितरौ वन्दे, R.;<BR>(2) अभिवादयति, -ते (c. of वद् = to greet:<BR>q. v.);<BR>I s. thee:<BR>अभिवादये, Ve. vi.;<BR>(3) नमति,<BR> प्र-, (नम्, c. 1.: prop. to make a bow),<BR>always s. Suyodhana:<BR>प्रणमन्ति सदा सुयोधनम्;<BR>Ki. ii. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saluter
SALUTER: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salvage
SALVAGE:<BR>(1) उद्धृतम्, सम्- (of the property);<BR>(2) उद्धारः (of the compensation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salvation
SALVATION:<BR>(1) त्राणम्, परि-;<BR>(2) तारणम्, सं-;<BR>(3) उद्धारः, सम्-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salve
SALVE: अञ्जनम्: v. Ointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salver
SALVER:<BR>(1) रूप्यपात्रम्;<BR>(2) रजतभाजनम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salvo
SALVO:<BR>I Exception, excuse: q. v.<BR>II A<BR>volley: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

salvolatile
SALVOLATILE: *क्षय्यलवणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

same
SAME:<BR>I Identical: expr. by तद्,<BR>it is like<BR>it, but not the s.:<BR>सदृश एषः, न पुनः सः, Mr. ix.;<BR>it is certainly the s.:<BR>नियतं स एषः, U. iii. 12.;<BR>saying he is the s.:<BR>सोऽयमितीरयित्वा, Ma. i.<BR>25.; the order is to go to the very s. place:<BR>तत्रैव गमनादेशः, Vi. iv. 43.;<BR>what I am, the s.<BR>is the son of Sun to you:<BR>योऽहं सूर्यसुतः स एष<BR> भवताम्, Vi. v. 55.<BR>II One, not different:<BR>(1) स- in certain comp. s. (G. § 109. A.),<BR>of the s. colour:<BR>सवर्ण (f. र्णा), Me.;<BR>at the<BR>s. time:<BR>सममेव, Ki. xiv. 44.;<BR>(2) एकः<BR>(का, कं),<BR>living in the s. place:<BR>एकायतनः<BR>(ना, नं), Mah.;<BR>in the s. place:<BR>एकत्र, C. i.;<BR>getting on the s. chariot:<BR>एकं स्यन्दमास्थितौ, R. i.<BR>36.<BR>III Corresponding: समः (मा, मं) or<BR>समानः (ना, नं): v. Equal, like, Ph.:<BR>in<BR>the s. manner:<BR>तथा, तद्वत्;<BR>s. as:<BR>यथा॥।तथैव।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sameness
SAMENESS:<BR>(1) ऐक्यम् (= identity);<BR>(2) साम्यम्<BR>(= similarity);<BR>(3) by circumlo.: v.<BR>Same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sample
SAMPLE: आदर्शः: v. Also specimen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sampler
SAMPLER: perh. सूचिकर्मप्रतिकृतिः, and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sanative
SANATIVE, SANATORY:<BR>(1) प्रति(ती)कार- in<BR>comp.;<BR>(2) रोगनाशन (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sanctification
SANCTIFICATION:<BR>I The act: expr. by verb.<BR>II The state: पवित्रता: v. Sacredness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sanctifier
SANCTIFIER: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sanctify
SANCTIFY:<BR>(1) पवित्रयति (nomi.);<BR>(2) पुण्यी-<BR>करोति;<BR>(3) पवित्रीकरोति: v. Also to conse-<BR>-crate, purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sanctimonious
SANCTIMONIOUS:<BR>I Sacred: q. v.<BR>II Hypo-<BR>-crite: q. v.: दाम्भिक (f. की).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sanctimony
SANCTIMONY:<BR>I Sacredness: पवित्रता।<BR>II<BR>Assumed: दाम्भिकता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sanction
SANCTION:<BR>I Subs.: शासनम् (?): v. Permis-<BR>-sion, ratification.<BR>II Verb.: शास्ति, अनु-,<BR>(शास्, c. 2.): v. To permit, confirm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sanctity
SANCTITY:<BR>(1) पवित्रता: v. Sacredness;<BR>(2)<BR>निर्मलता: v. Purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sanctuary
SANCTUARY:<BR>I Of a temple:<BR>(1) गर्भागारम्,<BR>Wilson;<BR>(2) गर्भः, Mat.<BR>II A temple:<BR>q. v.: महालयः।<BR>III Refuge: q. v.: शरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sand
SAND (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) बालुः, -का,<BR>fomenta-<BR>tion with s.:<BR>बालुकास्वेदः, Bha.; heated s.:<BR>करम्भबालुका, V. p. vi. 5. 45.;<BR>(2) सिकता (gen.<BR>pl.),<BR>particles of s.:<BR>सिकतांशवः; even in s.:<BR>सिकतास्वपि, J.<BR>II. In pl., a sandy country:<BR>मरुः, -भूमिः, crossing the s. s of Marwar:<BR>मरुधन्वमतिक्रम्य, B.p. i. x. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sand
SAND (v.):<BR>I To cover with s.: सिकताभिर्<BR> आवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.): v. To cover.<BR>II To<BR>ground on s.: q. v.:<BR>to be s. ed:<BR>सैकते पतति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sand-glass
SAND-GLASS: बालुकायन्त्रम्, Su. com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sandstone
SANDSTONE: सिकतोपलः, and sim. comp.s. (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sandal
SANDAL:<BR>I The tree:<BR>(1) चन्दनः;<BR>(2) रक्त-<BR>चन्दनः (= red s.). N.B. (a) use n. for the<BR>wood; (b) used also for the unctuous<BR>preparation.<BR>II A shoe: कोषी(शी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sandarac
SANDARAC(CH):<BR>I A tree: वृक्षविशेषः।<BR>II<BR>Realgar: रक्तधातुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sand-blind
SAND-BLIND: perh. नकुलान्ध (f. न्धा), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sanders
SANDERS:<BR>(1) रक्तचन्दनः (red s.);<BR>(2) पीतद्रुः<BR>(yellow s.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sandy
SANDY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) बालुकामय (f. यी);<BR>(2)<BR>बालुकाकीर्ण (f. र्णा); and sim. comp. s.<BR>II<BR>Sand-coloured: बालुकानिभ (f. भा) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sane
SANE:<BR>I Healthy: q. v.: सुस्थ (f. स्था).<BR>II<BR>In mind, not mad:<BR>(1) प्रकृतिस्थ (f. स्था),<BR>“ममैष पुत्रो वायुग्रस्तश्चिरं चिकित्सितः प्रकृतिस्थ एव<BR> जातः”, D. 11.;<BR>(2) अविचलितबुद्धि (mfn.), C.s.;<BR>(3) अनुपहतमनस् (mfn.); and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sanguinary
SANGUINARY:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) रक्तप्रिय (f. या)<BR>and sim. comp. s.;<BR>(2) जिघांसु (mfn. =<BR>murderous).<BR>II Of acts: रक्तदूषित (f. ता)<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sanguine
SANGUINE:<BR>I Hopeful: q. v.:<BR>(1) आशावत्<BR>(f. ती);<BR>(2) जातास्थ (f. स्था), I being s.:<BR>जातास्थया मया, D. ii.<BR>II Ardent, deep:<BR>q. v.: गाढ (f. ढा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sanies
SANIES: पूयम्: v. Pus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sanity
SANITY:<BR>(1) प्रकृतिस्थता;<BR>(2) सुस्थता (only of<BR>body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sanskrit
SANSKRIT:<BR>(1) संस्कृतम्;<BR>(2) संस्कारपूता भाषा, and<BR>sim. expr. s, praised the bridegroom in s.:<BR>संस्कारपूतेन वरं नुनाव, Ku. vii. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sap
SAP:<BR>I Subs.: रसः।<BR>II Verb: खनति (खन्,<BR>c. 1.): v. To undermine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sapid
SAPID: स्वादु (f. also द्वी): v. Tasteful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sapient
SAPIENT: प्राज्ञ (f. ज्ञा): v. Wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sapless
SAPLESS:<BR>(1) नीरस (f. सा);<BR>(2) विरस (f. सा)<BR>: v. Also dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sapling
SAPLING:<BR>(1) वृक्षकः, Ku. v. 14.;<BR>(2) बालवृक्षः<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saponaceous
SAPONACEOUS:<BR>(1) मेदुर (f. रा);<BR>(2) चिक्कण<BR>(f. णा।).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sapper
SAPPER: खनकः: v. Miner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sapphic
SAPPHIC: *साफव (f. वी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sapphire
SAPPHIRE: इन्द्रनीलः<BR>or<BR>महानीलः, a bed of s. s:<BR>इन्द्रनीलस्थलम्, Si. iii. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sappy
SAPPY:<BR>(1) रसवत् (f. ती);<BR>(2) सरस (f. सा);<BR>(3) रसाढ्य (f. ढ्या) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sarcasm
SARCASM:<BR>(1) अवक्षेपः<BR>or<BR>आक्षेपः (= reproach);<BR>(2) व्यङ्गोक्तिः (?);<BR>(3) कर्कशपरि(री)हासः and<BR>sim. expr. s. (= bitter zest).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sarcastic
SARCASTIC, -AL:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) अरुन्तुद<BR>(f. दा = tainting).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sarcastically
SARCASTICALLY:<BR>(1) सावक्षेपम्;<BR>(2) साक्षेपम्;<BR>(3) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sarcophagus
SARCOPHAGUS: a lime-stone: *मांसादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sardine
SARDINE: मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sardonic
SARDONIC: Ph.:<BR>s. laugh:<BR>विकृतहासः, and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sardonyx
SARDONYX: a gem: गोमेदः, -कः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sarsa
SARSA, -PARILLA: उत्कटम् (?), Wilson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sash
SASH (subs.):<BR>I A belt: perh. परिकरः,<BR>wearing a s.:<BR>बद्धपरिकर (f. रा).<BR>II Of a<BR>window: perh. काचाधारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satan
SATAN: *शातनः, पिशाचः (= devil, demon:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satanic
SATANIC:<BR>(1) पैशाच (f. ची: demoniac);<BR>*शातनीय (f. या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satchel
SATCHEL: v. Sachel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sate
SATE, -D: v. Satiate, -d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satellite
SATELLITE:<BR>I Lit.: उपग्रहः।<BR>II A dependant:<BR>पार्श्वचरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satiate
SATIATE: तर्पयति, सं-, परि-, (c. of तृप्),<BR>s. d<BR>forefathers:<BR>पितॄनतार्प्सीत्, B. i.: v. To satisfy.<BR>Be s. d:<BR>तृप्यति, सं-, परि- (तृप्, c. 4.),<BR>he was<BR>s. d when the rice was entirely finished:<BR>सशेष<BR> अन्धस्यतृप्यत, D. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satiety
SATIETY:<BR>(1) तृप्तिः, परि-, सं-, to receive s.:<BR>तृप्तिमधिगच्छति, Mah.;<BR>(2) सौहित्यम् (rare),<BR>Vi.;<BR>(3) वैतृष्णम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satin
SATIN: चीनम्<BR>or<BR>चीनांशुकम्: v. Silk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satire
SATIRE: साक्षेपगीतम्, and sim. comp. s may be<BR>used: v. Sarcasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satiric
SATIRIC, -AL:<BR>(1) expr. by comp.: v. Sarcasm;<BR>(2) सावक्षेप (f. पा = reproachful);<BR>(3) सावहास<BR>(f. सा = contemptuous).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satirically
SATIRICALLY:<BR>(1) सावक्षेपम् (= reproachfully);<BR>(2) सावहासम् (= contemptuously).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satirise
SATIRIS(Z)E: perh. सावक्षेपं भृद्नाति<BR>or<BR>मर्दयति (मृद्,<BR>c. 9. and c. 10).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satirist
SATIRIST: आक्षेपगीतकृत् (mfn.), -बद्धृ (f. द्ध्री), प्रणेतृ<BR>(f. त्री), etc. (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satisfaction
SATISFACTION:<BR>I Gratification, content-<BR>-ment.<BR>(1) सन्तोषः<BR>or<BR>परितोषः,<BR>the old husband<BR>could not give her s.:<BR>स वृद्धपतिस्तस्याः सन्तोषाय<BR> नाभवत्, H. i.;<BR>(2) तुष्टिः, सं-, परि-,<BR>deriving s.<BR>at night:<BR>तुष्टिमुपेयुषां निशि, N. xvi. 111.;<BR>(3)<BR>तृप्तिः, सं-, परि-,<BR>great men do not get s. even with<BR>the greatest greatness:<BR>तृप्तियोगः परेणापि महिम्ना न<BR> महात्मनाम्, Si. ii. 31.<BR>II As of hunger:<BR>(1) शान्तिः: v. Mitigation;<BR>(2) निराकरणम्: v.<BR>Removal.<BR>III As of debts.: शोधः, -नम्, परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satisfactorily
SATISFACTORILY: expr. by circumlo. or pres.<BR>part.: v. To satisfy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satisfactory
SATISFACTORY:<BR>(1) gen. expr. by subs. or<BR>verb;<BR>(2) उपयुक्त (f. क्ता = proper, fit: as a<BR>s. reply);<BR>(3) तुष्टिद (f. दा), तर्पण (f. णी),<BR>etc. (= satisfying).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satisfy
SATISFY:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) पूरयति (पूर्, c. 10.<BR>= to fill up: of the feelings),<BR>my child, s.<BR>your curiosity:<BR>पूरयतु कुतूहलं वत्सः। U. iv.;<BR>(2)<BR>तर्पयति, सं-, परि-, (c. of तृप to satiate: as<BR>with food),<BR>and with various drinks s. ed the<BR>great Brahmins:<BR>तर्पयामास विप्रेन्द्रान् पेयैश्च बहु-<BR>विस्तरैः, Mah. ii. 4. 4.;<BR>(3) तोषयति, सं-, परि-,<BR>(c. of तुष्, = to please, delight: q. v.),<BR>you<BR>go there and s. him and return quick:<BR>त्वं<BR> तत्र गत्वा तं सन्तोष्य सत्वरमागमिष्यसि, H, ii.;<BR>(4) शोधयति (c. of शुध्, = to clear: as of<BR>debts).<BR>II To free from doubt: q. v.:<BR>प्रतिपादयति (c. of पद् = to establish: with<BR>acc. of thing and dat. of person). To be<BR>s. ed:<BR>(1) तुष्यति, सं-, परि-, प्र-, (तुष्, c. 4.),<BR>B. xii. 83.;<BR>(2) तृप्यति, परि-, सं-, वि-,<BR>still not<BR>being s. ed:<BR>अवितृप्ततया (संशयगतत्वेन, M.n.) तथापि,<BR>Ki. ii. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satrap
SATRAP:<BR>(1) छत्रपः (?);<BR>(2) मण्डलेशः;<BR>(3)<BR>भोगपतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satrapy
SATRAPY:<BR>(1) मण्डलम् (= circle);<BR>(2) प्रदेशः<BR>(= province).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saturate
SATURATE: gen. expr. with प्लुत (f. ता), परि-,<BR> आ-, सं-,: v. To steep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saturday
SATURDAY:<BR>(1) शनिवारः;<BR>(2) शनिवासरः and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saturn
SATURN:<BR>(1) शनिः;<BR>(2) शनैश्चरः;<BR>(3) शौरिः<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saturnalia
SATURNALIA: शनैश्चरमहोत्सवः and sim. comp. s.<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

satyr
SATYR: वनदेवता (?); सत्रः (?, सत्रम् = wood, Ki.<BR>xiii. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sauce
SAUCE: उपदंशः (= relish); सूपः (= broth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saucepan
SAUCEPAN: खोलः, -कः: v. Also pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saucer
SAUCER:<BR>(1) शरावम् (?);<BR>(2) आधारः (stand:<BR>when sense clear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saucily
SAUCILY: धार्ष्ट्यात्<BR>or<BR>धार्ष्ट्येन: v. Impudently,<BR>shamelessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saucy
SAUCY: धृष्ट (f. ष्टा): v. Impudent, shame-<BR>-less.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saunter
SAUNTER: मन्दं मन्दं परिक्रामति<BR>or<BR>-क्राम्यति (क्रम्, c.<BR>1. and 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sausage
SAUSAGE: a kind of food: *शासजम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

savage
SAVAGE:<BR>I Wild: q. v.: वन्य (f. न्या),<BR>like s.<BR>Pulindas:<BR>वन्यैः पुलिन्दैरिवः, R. xvi. 19.<BR>II Un-<BR>-civilized, unpolished:<BR>(1) असभ्य (f. भ्या);<BR>(2) अशिष्ट (f. ष्टा). Ph.:<BR>Kirātas, Śavaras,<BR>and Pulindas are different tribes of s. s:<BR>भेदाः<BR> किरातशवरपुलिन्दा म्लेच्छजातयः, A. : v. Barba-<BR>-rian.<BR>III Ferocious, cruel: q. v.: क्रूर (f.<BR>रा), Si. xv. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

savagely
SAVAGELY:<BR>(1) क्रूरम्;<BR>(2) निष्ठुरम्: v. Fiercely,<BR>cruelly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

savageness
SAVAGENESS:<BR>(1) क्रौर्यम्: v. Ferocity, cruelly;<BR>(2) असभ्यता (= barbarity);<BR>(3) वन्यता<BR>(= wildness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

savant
SAVANT:<BR>(1) पण्डितः;<BR>(2) बुधः, -जनः: v. Wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

save
SAVE (v.):<BR>I In theological sense:<BR>(1)<BR>तारयति, निस्, (c. of तॄ), instantly s. ed Yayāti:<BR>ययातिं तारयामासुरञ्जसा, Mah. v. 122. 16.;<BR>(2)<BR>उद्धरति<BR>or<BR>-धारयति (हृ, c. 1. and its c., accord-<BR>-ing to its sense),<BR>one s. himself:<BR>उद्धरेदात्मना-<BR>त्मानम्, V. c.;<BR>(3) त्राति<BR>or<BR>त्रायते, परि (त्रा, c.<BR>2. or त्रै, c. 1.), s. (me),<BR>Lord:<BR>त्राहि त्राहि<BR> जगन्नाथ।<BR>II To preserve:<BR>(1) त्रायते,<BR>or<BR>त्राति,<BR> परि-, s. (your)<BR>friend:<BR>परित्रायतां सुहृदम्, Sa. vi.;<BR>(2) रक्षति, परि-, सं-, (रक्ष्, c. 1.),<BR>s. him from<BR>Bhima:<BR>रक्षैनं भीमात्, Ve. iii.: v. Also to<BR>protect, deliver.<BR>III To lay by:<BR>(1)<BR>संचिनोति (चि, c. 5.);<BR>(2) रक्षति, सं-।<BR>IV To<BR>spare: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

save
SAVE, SAVING (prop.): विहाय, अपहाय, वर्जयिंत्वा<BR>etc.: v. Except; s. attention to elders:<BR>गुरुजनशुश्रूषां वर्जयित्वा, Na. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saving
SAVING (subs.):<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) त्राणम्, परि-;<BR>(2) रक्षा, सं-;<BR>(3) उद्धारः, सम्-;<BR>(4) तारणम्,<BR> सं-;<BR>(5) सञ्चयः: for dif.: v. To save.<BR>II Any<BR>thing saved:<BR>(1) सञ्चित (f. ता);<BR>(2) रक्षित<BR>(f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

savingly
SAVINGLY: expr. by circumlo.: v. To save,<BR>saving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

savings bank
SAVINGS BANK: सञ्चितकोषः and sim. comp. s.:<BR>v. Bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saviour
SAVIOUR:<BR>(1) त्रातृ (f. त्री), परि-;<BR>(2) त्रायक<BR>(f. यिका), परि-;<BR>(3) उद्धर्तृ (f. र्त्री), सम्-;<BR>(4)<BR>तारक (f. रिका), निस्-;<BR>(4) रक्षितृ (f. त्री),<BR>s.<BR>of snakes:<BR>नागानां रक्षिता, Na. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

savory
SAVORY (subs.): सुगन्धिलताविशेषः; *शावरी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

savor
SAVO(U)R (v. i.):<BR>I To taste: q. v.; स्वदते<BR>(स्वद्, c. 1.).<BR>II To smell: q. v.: expr.<BR>with गन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

savor
SAVO(U)R (subs.):<BR>I Taste: q. v.: रसः।<BR>II<BR>Smell: q. v.: गन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

savory
SAVO(U)RY:<BR>I Tasty:<BR>(1) सरस (f. सा);<BR>(2) स्वादु (f. also द्वी).<BR>II Fragrant: q. v.:<BR>सुगन्धि (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

savoy
SAVOY: *कबिभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saw
SAW (subs.):<BR>I The tool:<BR>(1) करपत्रम्,<BR>cut<BR>off by s. like teeth:<BR>दन्तकरपत्रनिकृत्त-, Vi. v.<BR>29.;<BR>(2) क्रकचम्, “क्रकचव्यवहारः”, Li.<BR>II Pro-<BR>-verb: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saw
SAW (v.): क्रकचेन पाटयति (पट्, c. 10.), Mr. x.<BR>47.<BR>or<BR>दारयति (c. of दॄ), s. ing of timber:<BR>दारुदारणम्, Li. 200.;<BR>wood for s. ing:<BR>क्राकच्यं<BR> काष्टम्, Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sawdust
SAWDUST: क्रकचचूर्णम् (?); क्राकच्यकाष्ठचूर्णम् and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saw-fish
SAW-FISH: क्रकचमुखः; मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sawpit
SAWPIT: क्रकचगतिः and sim. comp.s. (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sawyer
SAWYER:<BR>(1) क्राकचिकः, Ram.;<BR>(2) दारुदारकः<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

say
SAY:<BR>(1) वक्ति (वच्, c. 2.), we s. (= reply),<BR>there is omniscient God:<BR>उच्यते, अस्ति सर्वज्ञं ब्रह्म,<BR>S.; in the first chapter, we have said (= shewn)<BR>that God is the cause of the whole world:<BR>प्रथमे<BR> पादे समस्तस्य जगतः कारणं ब्रह्मेत्युक्तम्, S.;<BR>(2)<BR>ब्रवीति<BR>or<BR>ब्रूते (ब्रू, c. 2.),<BR>you better s. whether<BR>you can call him a man:<BR>पुरुषोक्तिः कथं तस्मिन्<BR> ब्रूहि, Ki. xi. 71.; they s. (= it is said): आहुः,<BR>M. ix. 84.;<BR>(3) वदति (वद्, c. 1.), s. what [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">Page616</a>]<BR>has not been taken away:<BR>वद किं न मे हृतम्, R.<BR>viii. 67.;<BR>I do not say anything to you:<BR>त्वां न<BR> किञ्चिद्वदामि, N. iii. 134.;<BR>(4) गदति, नि-, (गद्,<BR>c. 1.), said again to the fine-toothed (lady):<BR>भूयः सुदतीं जगाद, R. vi. 37.;<BR>(5) भाषते (भाष्,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>again said fearlessly to Indra:<BR>पुनर्बभाषेऽप-<BR>भयः पुरन्दरम्, R. iii. 51.;<BR>(6) भणति (भण्, c.<BR>1.),<BR>the daughter of Bhīma said pleased but at<BR>the same time ashamed;<BR>ह्रीणा च हृष्टा च बभाण<BR> भैमी, N. iii. 67.;<BR>(7) कथयति (कथ्, c. 10.<BR>= to tell),<BR>s. what for:<BR>कथय कस्मिन्निमित्ते, Mu.<BR>i.;<BR>(8) आचष्टे (चक्ष्, c. 1. = 7.),<BR>who s. you<BR>are:<BR>का त्वमाचक्ष, R. xvi. 8.;<BR>(9) शंसति, आ-,<BR>(शंस्, c. 1. = 7.),<BR>swan, say what she told<BR>me:<BR>किं मामाह सा शंस हंस, N. ii. 134.;<BR>(10)<BR>अभिदधाति<BR>or<BR>-धत्ते (धा, c. 3.: prop. = to<BR>address),<BR>s. what I shall do for you:<BR>तवेप्सितं<BR> किं विदधेऽभिधेहि, N. iii. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

say
SAY, -ING (subs.):<BR>(1) उक्तिः;<BR>(2) वचनम्;<BR>(3)<BR>वचस् (n.);<BR>(4) वाक्यभ्;<BR>(5) वाच् (f.);<BR>(6)<BR>वादः, प्र-:<BR>(7) भाषितम्;<BR>(8) गदितम्, नि-;<BR>(9)<BR>भणितम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scab
SCAB:<BR>I A disease: पामन् (n.)<BR>or<BR>पामा,<BR>des-<BR>troying s.:<BR>पामाहरः, Bha.: v. Also itch.<BR>II<BR>A thin coating: किणः।<BR>III A mean fellow:<BR>दुरात्मन् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scabbard
SCABBARD: कोषः: v. Sheath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scabby
SCABBY:<BR>(1) पामन (f. ना);<BR>(2) कच्छुर (f. रा);<BR>(3) सिध्मल (f. ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scabious
SCABIOUS: कण्डुमत् (f. ती = itchy), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scaffold
SCAFFOLD, -ING (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: मञ्चः।<BR>II<BR>For execution: वध्यकाष्ठम् (comp. वध्यपुरुष,<BR> वध्यभूमिः, शीर्षच्छेदनशूलः of Mr. x.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scald
SCALD:<BR>I Verb: no proper equiv.: तप्त-<BR>जलादिना दहति (दह्, c. 1. = to burn: q. v.) or<BR>ग्लपयति (c. of ग्लै)<BR>or<BR>म्लापयति, परि- (c. of<BR>म्ला).<BR>II Subs.: perh. स्फोटः; दाहः<BR>(= burnt), P. v. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scale
SCALE (subs.):<BR>I In pl.- a balance: q. v.:<BR>तुला:<BR>the fulcrum:<BR>धटः, Mit.<BR>II Its dish:<BR>(1) शिक्यम् (= loop),<BR>to put in the s.:<BR>शिक्यम्<BR> आरोपयति, V. s.;<BR>(2) पार्श्वः (= side), Mit.<BR>III In astro.: तुला,<BR>IV Of fishes:<BR>(1)<BR>शल्कम्, -लम्;<BR>(2) वल्कम्, -लम्।<BR>V Of serpents:<BR>मण्डलम् (= circular spot), Sr.<BR>VI Of metal<BR>etc: पत्रम् (= leaf); फलकम् (= plate).<BR>VII<BR>A ladder: q. v.: सोपानम्।<BR>VIII In music:<BR>ग्रामः, Si. i. 10.<BR>IX A basis:<BR>(1) Often by<BR>मूलम् (= root);<BR>(2) परिमाणम्<BR>or<BR>प्रमाणम् (= mea-<BR>-sure). Ph.:<BR>on a small s.:<BR>अल्पपरिमाणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scale
SCALE (v.):<BR>I To climb. q. v.: आरोहति (रुह,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II To cross by s. ing: लङ्घयति, उत्-,<BR> वि-, अभि- (लङ्घ्, c. 10.), D. iii.<BR>III To<BR>take off s.s: व(श)ल्कयति (nomi.); विव(श)ल्की-<BR>करोति; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scalene
SCALENE:<BR>s. triangle:<BR>विषमत्रिभुजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scallop
SCALLOP:<BR>I Verb: कल्पयति, परि- (c. of कॢप्,:<BR>might be used also of s. ed oysters).<BR>II<BR>Subs.: कम्बुभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scalp
SCALP:<BR>I Verb: मुण्डम्, etc. त्वचयति (nomi.):<BR>v. Also to remove.<BR>II Subs.: मस्तकत्वच्<BR>(f.) and sim. comp. s: v. Head, skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scalpel
SCALPEL: छुरिकाविशेषः: v. Knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scaly
SCALY:<BR>(1) शल्कलिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) सशल्क (f.<BR>ल्का);<BR>(3) वल्कावृत (f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scamp
SCAMP:<BR>(1) खण्डितवृत्त (f. त्ता);<BR>(2) दुर्वृत्त (f.<BR>त्ता); and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scamper
SCAMPER: विद्रवति (द्रु, c. 1.): v. To run.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scan
SCAN (v.):<BR>I To examine attentively: q. v.:<BR>सूक्ष्मं निरूपयति (रूप्, c. 10.).<BR>II Of verses:<BR>चरणान् विभजति (भज्, c. 1.: (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scandal
SCANDAL:<BR>I Calumny:<BR>(1) निर्वादः, परि(री)वादः<BR>or<BR>अपवादः,<BR>afraid of popular s.:<BR>जननिर्वादभयात्,<BR>Ki. ii. 10.;<BR>(2) वाच्यम्<BR>or<BR>वचनीयम्,<BR>this s.<BR>will remain:<BR>वचनीयमिदं व्यवस्थितम्, Ku. iv.<BR>21.;<BR>(3) दुर्वर्णः<BR>or<BR>अवर्णः,<BR>I cannot bear this<BR>first s.:<BR>सोढुं न तत्पूर्वमवर्णमीशे, R. xiv. 38.;<BR>(4) निन्दा (= censure: q. v.), s. about wife:<BR>कलत्रनिन्दा, 33.<BR>II Fig., disgraceful: q. v.:<BR>कलङ्कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scandalize
SCANDALIZE: बीभत्सं जनयति (जन्, c. 10.): v.<BR>Also to offend, wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scandalous
SCANDALOUS:<BR>I Disgraceful, infamous:<BR>q. v.: कलङ्ककर (f. री).<BR>II Offensive, oppro-<BR>-brious: q. v.: गर्हित (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scandalously
SCANDALOUSLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scansion
SCANSION: छन्दश्चरणविभागः (?);<BR>वृत्तपादगणना (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scant
SCANT:<BR>I Adj.: v. Scanty.<BR>II Verb: v.<BR>To stint, limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scantily
SCANTILY:<BR>(1) स्वल्पम्: v. Little;<BR>(2) अप्रचुरम्;<BR>(3) अपर्याप्तम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scantiness
SCANTINESS:<BR>I Want of sufficiency:<BR>(1)<BR>स्वल्पता: v. Littleness;<BR>(2) अप्राचुर्यम्;<BR>(3)<BR>अपर्याप्तता।<BR>II Narrowness, smallness: तनुता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scanty
SCANTY: Not sufficient: q. v.:<BR>(1) स्वल्प (f.<BR>ल्पा): v. Little;<BR>(2) अप्रचुर (f. रा) and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR>II Narrow, small: q. v.:<BR>तनु (f. also न्वी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scapegoat
SCAPEGOAT: fig.:<BR>(1) बलिः (= oblation);<BR>(2) दायिन् (f. नी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scapegrace
SCAPEGRACE: निर्मयाद (f. दा): v. Also<BR>prodigal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scapular
SCAPULAR, -Y:<BR>(1) स्कन्ध- in comp.: v. Shoul-<BR>-der;<BR>(2) स्कन्धगत (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scar
SCAR (subs.):<BR>I Of a wound:<BR>(1) क्षतम्,<BR>a<BR>dreadful s.:<BR>विकरालं क्षतम्, P. iv. 4.;<BR>(2) क्षत-<BR>चिह्नम् and sim. comp. s.<BR>II Fig.: कलङ्कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scar
SCAR (v.): Chiefly in<BR>s. red:<BR>क्षताङ्कित (f. ता),<BR>किणाङ्क (f. ङ्का, etc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scarce
SCARCE: विरल (f. ला): v. Rare, uncommon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scarce
SCARCE, -LY:<BR>(1) by adj.,<BR>one s. gets a match-<BR>ing wife:<BR>दुर्लभा सदृशी भर्या, J. ;<BR>(2) कथमपि<BR>(= with difficulty: q. v.);<BR>(3) न (= not:<BR>of time),<BR>s. a day passed:<BR>नैकमपि दिनं गतम्;<BR>(4)<BR>Sometimes by एव,<BR>s. I had arrived:<BR>आगतमात्र<BR> एव।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scarceness
SCARCENESS, SCARCITY:<BR>I In gen.<BR>(1) विरलता;<BR>(2) दुर्लभता;<BR>(3) दुष्प्राप्यता।<BR>II Of provisions:<BR>दुर्भिक्षम् (= famine: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scare
SCARE: त्रासयति (c. of त्रस्): v. To frighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scarecrow
SCARECROW: perh. त्रासनम्, वि-;<BR>(2) by<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scarf
SCARF: no prop. equiv.:<BR>(1) सिचयः;<BR>(2) चेलकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scarification
SCARIFICATION: त्वक्छेदः, -नम् and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scarify
SCARIFY: त्वचं छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7.)<BR>or<BR>उल्लिखति<BR>(लिख्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scarlet
SCARLET:<BR>(1) शोण (f. णा): v. Red.;<BR>(2)<BR>सिन्दूरसवर्ण (f. र्णा);<BR>(3) स्वच्छसिन्दूरभास् (mfn.)<BR>Ri. i. 24. Ph.:<BR>s. fever:<BR>उदर्धः, Wilson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scarp
SCARP: no proper equiv.: उपसर्पः may be used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scate
SCATE: v. Skate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scatheless
SCATHELESS:<BR>(1) अक्षत (f. ता);<BR>(2) अविक्षत<BR>(f. ता);<BR>(3) अपरिक्षत (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scatter
SCATTER:<BR>(1) किरति, प्र-, वि-, सं- (कॄ, c. 6.),<BR>to s. the ladies:<BR>विकरितुं वधूः, Si. vi. 52.;<BR>(2)<BR>विक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.),<BR>s. ing the scent:<BR>गन्धं<BR> विक्षिपन्, Ki. ix. 31.;<BR>(3) वि-धूनोति, निर्-, विनिर्<BR>(धू, c. 5.: as armies), Vi. ii. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scavenger
SCAVENGER:<BR>(1) खलपूः (rare);<BR>(2) सम्मार्जकः<BR>(= sweeper).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scene
SCENE:<BR>I Stage: q. v.: रङ्गः, -भूमिः।<BR>II Part<BR>of a play: अंकांशः, Sa. v.; परिच्छेदः (?).<BR>III<BR>A sight, spectacle: दृश्यम्: v. Also s. ry.<BR>IV Place: q. v.: भूमिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scenery
SCENERY (subs.):<BR>I Natural: expr. by<BR>words meaning land, place:<BR>wild moun-<BR>tain s.:<BR>अरण्यगिरिभूमिः, Vi. v.;<BR>oh, how beauti-<BR>ful is the s. here:<BR>अहो रामणीयकमस्य [मलयपर्वतस्य],<BR>Na. i.<BR>II Artificial: v. Scene.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scent
SCENT (subs.):<BR>I The sense of smell: घ्राणम्<BR>: v. Smell.<BR>II Smell, odour:<BR>(1)<BR>गन्धः,<BR>with the mere s.:<BR>गन्धमात्रेण, Sa. iii.;<BR>sweet s. ed:<BR>सुगन्धिन् (mfn.), Bha.;<BR>therefore<BR>it is not consonant to implicate here even the s.<BR>of action:<BR>तस्मात् क्रियाया गन्धमात्रस्याप्यनुप्रवेश इह<BR> नोप्पद्यते, S.;<BR>(2) सौरभम् (= fragrance: q. v.),<BR>of uncommon s.:<BR>असाधारणसौरभः (भा, भं), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scent
SCENT (v.):<BR>I To smell: q. v.: घ्राति, आ-<BR>(घ्रा, c. 2.).<BR>II To perfume: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>वासयति (वास्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) सुरभीकरोति, s. ed:<BR>सुरभितः, Me. i. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scentless
SCENTLESS:<BR>(1) निर्गन्ध (f. न्धा), Ku.;<BR>(2)<BR>गन्धहीनः (ना, नं); and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sceptic
SCEPTIC:<BR>(1) सन्देहकृत्,<BR>an honest s.:<BR>हेतुभिः<BR> सन्देहकृत्, Śridhara;<BR>(2) सन्देहभृत्,<BR>V iii. 35.<BR>(?);<BR>(3) हैतुकः, V.p. iii. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sceptical
SCEPTICAL: सन्देहभृत् (mfn.) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scepticism
SCEPTICISM:<BR>I Doubt: q. v.: सन्देहः।<BR>II<BR>The doctrine: हैतुकवादः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sceptre
SCEPTRE:<BR>(1) राजदण्डः (= mace);<BR>(2) छत्रम्<BR>(= umbrella: fig.),<BR>loss of s.:<BR>छत्राभङ्गः। Ph.:<BR>to hold the s. = reign: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sceptred
SCEPTRED (adj.): दण्डधार (f. री), Ka. i. 2.;<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

schedule
SCHEDULE:<BR>I A paper: पत्रम्।<BR>II A list:<BR>q. v.: परिसंख्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scheme
SCHEME (subs.):<BR>I A plan: q. v. कल्पना।<BR>II<BR>In bad sense: मन्त्रणा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scheme
SCHEME (v.): कल्पयति, परि-, सं-, (कॢप्, c. 10.):<BR>v. To plan, devise.<BR>S. ing:<BR>कुचक्रिन् (f. णी):<BR>v. Also artful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

schism
SCHISM: भेदः: v. Breach, separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

schismatic
SCHISMATIC, -AL: भेदकर (f. री) and sim.<BR>deriv. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scholar
SCHOLAR:<BR>I A pupil: q. v. छात्र (f. त्री).<BR>II A learned person: q. v.: पण्डित (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scholarly
SCHOLARLY:<BR>I Learned, accomplished:<BR>q. v.: पण्डित (f. ता).<BR>II Becoming a<BR>scholar:<BR>(1) पण्डितसदृश (f. शी);<BR>(2) पाण्डित्य-<BR>गर्भ (f. र्भा); and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scholarship
SCHOLARSHIP:<BR>I Learning: q. v.: पाण्डित्यम्।<BR>II Stipend: वृत्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scholastic
SCHOLASTIC, -AL:<BR>(1) expr. by comp.:<BR>v. School;<BR>(2) by circumlo.: v. Also<BR>scholarly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scholiast
SCHOLIAST: टीकाकार (f. री): v. Commentator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scholium
SCHOLIUM (pl. -A): टीका: Commentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

school
SCHOOL (subs.):<BR>I For instruction:<BR>(1)<BR>विद्यालयः and sim. comp. s.,<BR>this is the tenth<BR>year of your residence in s.:<BR>अयमत्रात्रभवतो दशमो<BR> वत्सरो विद्यागृहमधिवसतः, K. ; erected a palatial s.:<BR>अमरागाराकारं विद्यामन्दिरमकारयत्, K. ;<BR>(2) मठः<BR>(religious (?), प्रबुद्धाध्ययनकमठेषु मठेषु, Va.<BR>II<BR>System:<BR>(1) शाखा (= branch),<BR>different s. s<BR>of Vedas:<BR>वेदानां शाखाभेदाः, V. p. iii. 4. 4.;<BR>(2)<BR>शाखिन् (m.: of men),<BR>some s. s.:<BR>एके शाखिनः,<BR>S. iii. 2. 2. Ph.:<BR>epitome of the various s. s of<BR>Hindu philosophy:<BR>सर्वदर्शनसंग्रहः।<BR>III Fig.,<BR>refuge, abode: q. v.: शरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

school
SCHOOL (v.): शिक्षयति (c. of शिक्ष्): v. To<BR>teach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

schoolfellow
SCHOOLFELLOW:<BR>(1) सहाध्यायिन् (f. नी) and<BR>sim. comp. s.;<BR>(2) सतीर्थ (f. र्था)<BR>or<BR>र्थ्य (f. र्थ्या)<BR>(rare), Ma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

schooling
SCHOOLING (subs.): Ph.:<BR>s. fee:<BR>शिक्षामूल्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

schoolmaster
SCHOOLMASTER:<BR>(1) शिक्षकः;<BR>(2) अध्यापकः: v.<BR>Teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

schoolmistress
SCHOOLMISTRESS:<BR>(1) शिक्षयित्री;<BR>(2) अध्यापिका;<BR>(3) उपाध्याया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

school-room
SCHOOL-ROOM: पाठशाला: v. School.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

schooner
SCHOONER: नौभेदः; मद्गुः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sciatic
SCIATIC (adj.):<BR>s. nerve:<BR>वस्तिमार्गशिरा (?);<BR>s.<BR>pains:<BR>वस्तिशूलकोपः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sciatica
SCIATICA: prob. वस्तिशूलः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

science
SCIENCE:<BR>I Knowledge: q. v.: ज्ञानम्।<BR>II<BR>A branch of knowledge:<BR>(1) विद्या, in the<BR>s. s of words (grammar), argument (logic), and<BR>truths (philosophy): शब्दहेतुसमयविद्यासु, D. ii.;<BR>learnt all s. s:<BR>सर्वा विद्या जग्राह, K. ;<BR>(2) शास्त्रम्<BR>(as contained in books),<BR>the s. of astronomy<BR>consists of three branches:<BR>ज्योतिःशास्त्रं स्कन्धत्रया-<BR>धिष्ठितम्, V. m. 9.;<BR>(3) विज्ञानशास्त्रम् (? = physi-<BR>-cal s.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scientific
SCIENTIFIC, -AL:<BR>I Used in science: expr.<BR>by comp.,<BR>s. enquiries:<BR>विज्ञानगवेषणा (?).<BR>II<BR>Versed in s.: विज्ञानविद् (mfn.) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scientifically
SCIENTIFICALLY:<BR>(1) विज्ञानशास्त्रानुसारेण (?);<BR>(2)<BR>यथाविज्ञानम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scimitar
SCIMITAR:<BR>(1) खङ्गः: v. Sword;<BR>(2) निस्त्रिंशः;<BR>(3) करपा(बा)लः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scintillate
SCINTILLATE:<BR>I Lit.: स्फुलिङ्गान् मुञ्चति, वि-<BR>(मुच्, c. 6.).<BR>II To sparkle: q. v.: स्फुरति<BR>(स्फुर्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scintillation
SCINTILLATION:<BR>(1) स्फुलिङ्गनिर्गमः and sim.<BR>comp. s;<BR>(2) स्फुरितम् (fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sciolist
SCIOLIST:<BR>(1) पल्लवग्राहिपण्डितः;<BR>(2) पण्डितमानिन्<BR>(f. नी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scion
SCION:<BR>I Lit.: नवपल्लवः: v. Shoot.<BR>II A<BR>descendant: q. v.:<BR>s. s of nobility:<BR>कुलीनाः<BR> कुमाराः, N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scissors
SCISSORS:<BR>(1) खण्डधारा;<BR>(2) कर्तरी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scoff
SCOFF (v.): अवहसति (हस्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>ridicule, mock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scoff
SCOFF, -ING (subs.): अवहासः: v. Ridicule,<BR>derision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scoffer
SCOFFER:<BR>(1) अवहासक (f. सिका);<BR>(2) उपहासक<BR>(f. सिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scold
SCOLD (v.): भर्त्सयति, परि-, सं-, (भर्त्स्, c. 10.):<BR>v. To revile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scold
SCOLD (subs.): दुर्मुख (f. खी): v. Also shrew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scolding
SCOLDING:<BR>I Subs.: भर्त्सना।<BR>II Adj.:<BR>आक्षारक (f. रिका): v. Also abusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sconce
SCONCE:<BR>I Verb: दण्डयति (दण्ड्, c. 10.):<BR>v. To fine.<BR>II Subs.:<BR>(1) दण्डः (= fine:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(2) दीपाधारः (of candles).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scoop
SCOOP (v.):<BR>I To lade out: सिञ्चति (सिच्,<BR>c. 6.: used by boatmen). To dig out:<BR>कुट्टयति (कुट्ट्, c. 10.: its Bengali used for<BR>s. ed out canoes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scoop
SCOOP (subs.):<BR>I A lade: q. v.: दर्वी।<BR>II<BR>For boats: सेचनी।<BR>III A hollow: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scope
SCOPE:<BR>I End, object: q. v.: अभिप्रायः।<BR>II<BR>Limit, compass: q. v.: इयत्ता।<BR>III Room,<BR>field: q. v.: अवसरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scorbutic
SCORBUTIC, -AL: *लवणरक्त-, in comp.; लवणरक्तिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scorch
SCORCH:<BR>(1) दहति, निर्, वि-, परि, (दह्, c. 1. =<BR>to burn), everywhere the ground is s. ed with fire:<BR>दिशि दिशि परिदग्धा भूमयः पावकेन, Ri. i. 24.;<BR>(2)<BR>तपति, निर् (तप्, c. 1. = to heat: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

score
SCORE (subs.):<BR>I Mark of number: चिह्नम्:<BR>v. Mark.<BR>II Total number gained: expr.<BR>by circumlo.,<BR>what is the s.:<BR>कस्य कति<BR>or<BR>किमा-<BR>वाभ्यामासादितम्: v. To get.<BR>III Account,<BR>bill: q. v.<BR>IV Indebtedness: expr. with<BR>देय (f. या).<BR>V Twenty: q. v.: विंशतिः।<BR>VI<BR>Reason, sake: q. v.:<BR>on the same s.:<BR>तदेवार्ये।<BR>VII In music: perh. विन्यासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

score
SCORE (v.):<BR>I To mark, note: q. v.: अङ्कयति<BR>(अङ्क्। c. 10.).<BR>II To draw a line across:<BR>रेखया कृन्तति (कृत्, c. 7.: after Bengali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scorn
SCORN (subs.):<BR>(1) अवझा, -नम्,: v. Contempt;<BR>(2) घृणा: v. Hatred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scorn
SCORN (v.):<BR>(1) अवजानाति (ज्ञा, c. 9.);<BR>(2)<BR>अवमन्यते (मन्, c. 4.): v. To despise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scornful
SCORNFUL:<BR>(1) अवज्ञाव्यञ्जक (f. ञ्जिका);<BR>(2)<BR>घृणासूचक (f. चिका): v. Also haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scornfully
SCORNFULLY:<BR>(1) अवज्ञया;<BR>(2) सावमानम्;<BR>(3)<BR>सावलेपम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scorpion
SCORPION:<BR>I The reptile: वृश्चिकः।<BR>II The<BR>sign: वृश्चिकः।<BR>III An (ancient) engine:<BR>*पाषाणक्षेपकम्, -यन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scot
SCOT: करः: v. Tax. Ph.: s. free (fig.): अक्षत<BR>(f. ता), अविकल (f. ला), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scotch
SCOTCH:<BR>I Verb: भिनत्ति (भिद्, c. 6.).<BR>II<BR>Adj.: *हिष्काटीय (f. या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scoundrel
SCOUNDREL: खण्डितवृत्त (f. त्ता): Rascal, mean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scour
SCOUR (v.):<BR>I To clean: माऋष्टि<BR>or<BR>मार्जयति,<BR> परि-, सं-, (मृज्, c. 2. and 10.).<BR>II To pass<BR>swiftly over: q. v.: द्रुतं परिक्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scourge
SCOURGE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) कशा(षा);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रतिष्कशः(षः).<BR>II Fury, dreadful^1 visitation:<BR>(1) धूमकेतुः;<BR>(2) कालः।<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scourge
SCOURGE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: कशया हन्ति, आ-, (हन्,<BR>c. 2.), ताडयति (तड्, c. 10.), प्रहरति (हृ, c. 1.).<BR>II Fig.: तुदति (तुद्, c. 6.): v. Also to<BR>chastise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scourging
SCOURGING (subs.): कशाघातः etc., deserves s.:<BR>कश्य (f. श्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scout
SCOUT (subs.):<BR>(1) चारः;<BR>(2) चरः: v. Spy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scout
SCOUT (v.):<BR>I As s. s; चरति, सं- (चर्, c. 1.),<BR>let the s.s s. through every hermitage:<BR>प्रतिमुनि-<BR>निलयं ते च चाराश्चरन्तु, Ve. vi. 2.<BR>II To reject,<BR>scorn: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scowl
SCOWL:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) भ्रूभङगः;<BR>(2) भ्रू(भ्रू<BR>or<BR>ब्खृ)<BR>कुटिः(टी).<BR>II Verb:<BR>(2) भ्रूभङ्गं करोति<BR>or<BR>विद-<BR>धाति (धा, c. 3.);<BR>(2) भ्रूकुटिं बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c.<BR>9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scraggy
SCRAGGY:<BR>I Rough: q. v.: रूक्ष (f. क्षा).<BR>II Lean: q. v.: कुश (f. शा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scramble
SCRAMBLE (v.):<BR>I To climb up: हस्ताभ्यां धृत्वा<BR>or<BR>गृहीत्वा आरोहति<BR>or<BR>अधि- (रुह्, c. 1.).<BR>II<BR>For things: संमर्दं करोति (with dat.); लालायते<BR>(nomi.=to shew eagerness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scramble
SCRAMBLE, -ING (subs.):<BR>I Climbing: expr.<BR>by verb.<BR>II For things:<BR>(1) संमर्दः;<BR>(2)<BR>लालायितम् (=longing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scrap
SCRAP: खण्डः: v. Fragment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scrape
SCRAPE (subs.):<BR>I Perplexity, difficulty:<BR>q. v.: कृच्छ्रम्,<BR>got a s.:<BR>कृच्छ्रगत (f. ता).<BR>II<BR>An awkwardly bow: perh. मूर्ध्नः कम्पः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scrape
SCRAPE (v.):<BR>(1) उद्घर्षति (घृष्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>rub.;<BR>(2) उल्लिखति (लिख्, c. 6.): v. To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">Page620</a>]<BR>scratch.<BR>S. together:<BR>समाहरति (हृ, c. 1.): v.<BR>To collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scraper
SCRAPER:<BR>I In gen.: घर्षणी, निर्।<BR>II For<BR>the tongue: उल्ले खनी (?), Williams.<BR>III<BR>For boats: अभ्रिः(भ्री)।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scraping
SCRAPING (subs.):<BR>I The act: घर्षणम्, उद्-।<BR>II That which is taken off by s.:<BR>(1)<BR>उच्छिष्टम्: v. Refuse;<BR>(2) मलम्: v. Dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scratch
SCRATCH (v.):<BR>I Lit.: वि-लिखत्, उत्, प्र-, प्रोत्-<BR>(लिख्, c. 6.),<BR>s. ing the roots of the wings with<BR>the beak:<BR>विलिखंश्चञ्चुपुटेन पक्षती, N. ii. 2.;<BR>s.<BR>ed his golden stool with the feet:<BR>पादेन हैमं<BR> विलिलेख पीठम्, R. vi. 15<BR>II To allay itching:<BR>कण्डूयति, -ते (nomi.),<BR>s. ing the cheeks:<BR>कटं<BR> कण्डूयमान (f. ना), R. ii. 36.<BR>III To tear:<BR>q. v.: विदारयति (दॄ, c. 10.).<BR>IV To s. out:<BR>प्रमार्ष्टि (भृज्, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scratch
SCRATCH (subs.):<BR>(1) लेखा, -खनम्, वि-, उत्-,<BR>s. es with the nail:<BR>नखलेखाः, Ki. ix. 78.;<BR>(2)<BR>घृष्टम् (excoriation), Sr.;<BR>(3) क्षतम् (=wound:<BR>with a qualifying word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scrawl
SCRAWL (v.): अस्पष्टं<BR>or<BR>स्थूलं लिखति (लिख्,<BR>c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scrawl
SCRAWL (subs.):<BR>(1) अस्पष्टलेखः;<BR>(2) स्थूललेखः,<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scream
SCREAM (subs.):<BR>(1) चि(ची)त्कारः;<BR>(2) आर्तनादः<BR>and sim. comp. s (of man);<BR>(3) उत्क्रोशः: v.<BR>Cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scream
SCREAM (v.):<BR>(1) चि(ची)त्कारं करोति;<BR>(2) आर्तरवं<BR> विमुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.): v. To cry, roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

screech
SCREECH: v. Scream, cry, roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

screech-owl
SCREECH-OWL:<BR>(1) कालपेचकः: v. Owl;<BR>(2)<BR>उलूकः, V. m. 88. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

screen
SCREEN (subs.):<BR>I In gen: आवरणम्।<BR>II For<BR>a house:<BR>(1) तिरस्कर(रि)णी, s. made of grass:<BR>तृणगुणिततिरस्करणी, C. s.;<BR>(2) य(ज)वनिका;<BR>(3)<BR>काण्डपटः (for the tents), Si. v. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

screen
SCREEN (v.):<BR>(1) छादयति (छद्, c. 10.): v.<BR>To cover;<BR>(2) रक्षति (रक्ष्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>protect, save.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

screw
SCREW (subs.):<BR>I The machine: *कर्षणी।<BR>II<BR>A miser: कृपण (f. णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

screw
SCREW (v.):<BR>I To fasten: बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c.<BR>9.).<BR>II To press, squeeze: q. v.: निष्पी-<BR>डयति (पीड्, c. 10.).<BR>III To distort: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scribble
SCRIBBLE (v.), SCRIBBLING (subs.): v. Scr-<BR>-awl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scribbler
SCRIBBLER:<BR>(1) कुललेखकः;<BR>(2) Simply लेखकः:<BR>(when sense clear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scribe
SCRIBE:<BR>(1) लेखकः;<BR>(2) लिपिकरः, s.'s fault:<BR>लिपिकरप्रमादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scrip
SCRIP:<BR>I A bag: पुटः(टी)।<BR>II Of writing:<BR>पत्रिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scriptural
SCRIPTURAL: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scripture
SCRIPTURE:<BR>(1) वेदः;<BR>(2) श्रुतिः;<BR>(3) आगमः;<BR>(4) आम्नायः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scrivener
SCRIVENER:<BR>I Usurer: q. v.: कुसीदः<BR>II A<BR>writer: लेखकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scrofula
SCROFULA:<BR>(1) गण्डमाला;<BR>(2) कण्ठमाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scrofulous
SCROFULOUS:<BR>(1) गण्डमालिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) कण्ठ-<BR>मालिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scroll
SCROLL:<BR>(1) पटः(तृः);<BR>(2) लेखयम्, आ-, (of<BR>writing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scrotum
SCROTUM:<BR>(1) कोषः(शः), अण्ड-;<BR>(2) मुष्कः;<BR>(3)<BR>वृषणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scrub
SCRUB: प्र-मार्ष्टि<BR>or<BR>मार्जयति (मृज्, c. 2. and 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scruple
SCRUPLE:<BR>I Subs.: सन्देहः: v. Doubt.<BR>II<BR>Verb: संदिग्धे (दिह्, c. 2.): v. To doubt,<BR>hesitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scrupulous
SCRUPULOUS:<BR>I Of men: सूक्ष्मजिज्ञासु (mfn.):<BR>v. Also upright.<BR>II Exact, nice: q. v.:<BR>सूक्ष्म (f. क्ष्मा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scrupulously
SCRUPULOUSLY:<BR>(1) सूक्ष्मम्: v. Nicely;<BR>(2)<BR>निपुणम्: v. Carefully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scrupulousness
SCRUPULOUSNESS:<BR>(1) सूक्ष्मजिज्ञासा (?);<BR>(2)<BR>आशङ्का (= apprehension: q. v.);<BR>(3) सूक्ष्मता<BR>(= nicety).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scrutinize
SCRUTINIZE: सूक्ष्मं परिपश्यति (दृश्, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>निरू-<BR>पयति (रूप्, c. 10.): v. Also to examine,<BR>search.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scrutiny
SCRUTINY:<BR>(1) सूक्ष्मपरिदर्शनम्;<BR>(2) सूक्ष्मनिरूपणम्;<BR>(3) गवेषणा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scuff
SCUFF: वेगेन उह्यते (pass. of वह्): v. To drive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scuffle
SCUFFLE:<BR>I Subs.: कलिः: v. Struggle,<BR>quarrel.<BR>II Verb: कलिं करोति: v. To<BR>struggle, quarrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scull
SCULL:<BR>I Skull: q. v.: कर्परः An oar: क्षेपणिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scullery
SCULLERY:<BR>(1) पिठरम् (?), Wilson;<BR>(2) भाण्डा-<BR>गारम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scullion
SCULLION: भाण्डमार्जक (f. र्जिका), -क्षालक (f.<BR>लिका), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sculptor
SCULPTOR:<BR>(1) त्व(त)ष्टृ (f. ष्ट्री);<BR>(2) तक्षक (f.<BR>क्षिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sculpture
SCULPTURE:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) तक्षणम्;<BR>(2) त्वक्षणम्।<BR>II Verb:<BR>(1) त (त्व)क्षति (तक्ष्<BR>or<BR>त्वक्ष्, c. 1.).<BR>(2) उल्लिखति (लिख्, c. 6.: rare), Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scum
SCUM (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मण्ड (mn.),<BR>poured<BR>off rice-s.:<BR>अन्नमण्डमगालयत्, D. vi.;<BR>(2) फेनः<BR>(= froth).<BR>II Fig. मलः,<BR>the Vāhikas are the<BR>s. of the world:<BR>मलं पृथिव्या वाहीकाः, Mah. viii.<BR>45. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scum
SCUM (v.): मण्डं गालयति (c. of गल्), स्रावयति (c.<BR>of स्रु), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scurf
SCURF: शुष्कचर्मन् (n.)<BR>or<BR>-त्वच् (f.): v. Also scab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scurfy
SCURFY: शुष्कचर्मावृत (f. ता) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scurrility
SCURRILITY:<BR>(1) अश्लीलता: v. Indecency;<BR>(2)<BR>परुषता: v. Roughness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scurrilous
SCURRILOUS:<BR>(1) अश्लील (f. ला): v. Indecent;<BR>(2) परुष (f. षा): v. Rough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scurrilously
SCURRILOUSLY:<BR>(1) अश्लीलम्;<BR>(2) व्यङ्गसंयुतम्<BR>(= 1);<BR>(3) परुषम् (= roughly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scurvy
SCURVY: दुष्टरक्तजो व्याधिविशेषः; *लवणरक्तम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scutcheon
SCUTCHEON: *कौलीनकोषः; -आवरणम्; and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scuttle
SCUTTLE (subs.):<BR>I A basket: करण्डः।<BR>II A<BR>hole: छिद्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scuttle
SCUTTLE (v.): (नौकातले<BR>or<BR>-पार्श्वे) छिद्राणि करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

scythe
SCYTHE:<BR>(1) खङ्गीकम्;<BR>(2) लवित्रम्;<BR>(3) शस्य-<BR>कर्तरिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sea
SEA (subs.):<BR>(1) समुद्रः,<BR>s.-foam;<BR>समुद्रफेनः, R.<BR>xiii. 11.;<BR>s.-going vessels:<BR>नौभिः समुद्रवाहिनीभिः,<BR>M. n.;<BR>s.-water:<BR>सामुद्रं जलम्, Bha.;<BR>in the<BR>middle of the s.:<BR>मध्येसमुद्रम्, Si. iii. 33.;<BR>in<BR>his heart — the s. of compassion:<BR>दयासमुद्रे तदाशये,<BR>N. i. 134.;<BR>(2) सागरः, throw him into the s.:<BR>प्रक्षिपैनं सागरे, D. vi.;<BR>as the s. is clear when the<BR>tide had set:<BR>निवृत्तवेल प्रसन्न इव सागरः, Ram. v.<BR>37. 6.;<BR>(3) अर्णवः,<BR>sunk in the s. of his misfor-<BR>tunes:<BR>व्यसनार्णवसंमग्नम्, Ram. ii. 21. 2.;<BR>(4)<BR>अब्धिः, and sim. comp. s.,<BR>situated on the<BR>borders of the s.:<BR>जलधेरुपकण्ठप्रतिष्ठितम्; went by s.:<BR>प्रतस्थेऽम्बुधिवर्त्मना, K. s. 25. 35., 40. 70.;<BR>on the<BR>s. coast:<BR>उदधेः कूले, R. xii. 68.;<BR>crossing the<BR>heavy s.:<BR>पयोधिमाविलं विलङ्घ्य, Si. i. 68.;<BR>growing on the s.-coast:<BR>अम्भोधितटाधिवासान्, Si.<BR>iii. 70.;<BR>(5) जलनिधिः, and sim. comp.s,<BR>saw<BR>on the confines of s.-water:<BR>पारेजलं निरनिधेरपश्यत्,<BR>Si. iii. 70.;<BR>(6) अम्बुराशिः,<BR>the coast of the<BR>salt-s:<BR>वेला लवणाम्बुराशेः, R. xiii. 15.;<BR>(7) रत्ना-<BR>करः;<BR>(8) आपगापतिः and sim. comp.s;<BR>(9)<BR>मकरालयः। Ph.: (a)<BR>go to s.:<BR>समुद्रं गच्छति,<BR> याति, etc.; (b)<BR>beyond the s. s:<BR>द्वीपान्तरम or<BR>ऊमिमतः पारम्, Mah. iv. 26. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sea-bear
SEA-BEAR: *समुद्रकोलः; श्वेतवराहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sea-calf
SEA-CALF: an animal: prob. नक्रः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sea-captain
SEA-CAPTAIN: समुद्रपोताध्यक्षः and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sea-coot
SEA-COOT: पक्षिविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sea-ear
SEA-EAR: शङ्गविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sea-elephant
SEA-ELEPHANT: मातङ्गनक्रः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sea-hare
SEA-HARE: a mollusk: विशङ्खः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seahorse
SEAHORSE: नक्रगवः (f. वी). Also = hippopota-<BR>-mus: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sea-kale
SEA-KALE: शाकभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sea-lion
SEA-LION: *नक्रसिंहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sea-monster
SEA-MONSTER: करियादस् (n. (?), Ki. vi. 14.;<BR>*यादःशार्दूलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sea-needle
SEA-NEEDLE, SEA-PIKE: मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seaport
SEAPORT: पोताश्रयः, पोतशरणम्, and sim. comp. s.<BR>(??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sea-rover
SEA-ROVER: समुद्रदस्युः (?): v. Robber, pirate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seasick
SEASICK: *समुद्रछर्दिमत् (f. ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seasickness
SEASICKNESS: *समुद्रछर्दिस् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sea-serpent
SEA-SERPENT: समुद्रनागः; समुद्रभुजङ्गः, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seaworthy
SEAWORTHY:<BR>(1) समुद्रगमनयोग्य (f. ग्या) and<BR>sim. comp.s;<BR>(2) सर्ववातसह (f. हा = standing<BR>all wind), Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seal
SEAL (subs.):<BR>I Of a letter etc.: मुद्रा,<BR>the s.<BR>is marked with the name of Rākṣasa:<BR>राक्षस-<BR>नामाङ्कितेयं मुद्रा;<BR>without breaking the s.:<BR>मुद्रां<BR> परिपालयन्; without taking a s. (ed pass.):<BR>अगृहीतमुद्रः, Mu. v.<BR>II The sea-calf: prob.<BR>नक्रः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seal
SEAL (v.):<BR>I To put a s. to: मुद्रयति (मुद्र्,<BR>c. 10.),<BR>s. it with this s.:<BR>अनया मुद्रया मुद्रयैनम्,<BR>Mu. i.;<BR>this is the s. ed letter:<BR>अयं स मुद्रितो<BR> लेखः।<BR>II To confirm. q. v.<BR>III Shut,<BR>close: q. v.: बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.),<BR>“s. up<BR>lips”:<BR>मुखं बध्नाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sealing-wax
SEALING-WAX: लाक्षा (rare राक्षा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seam
SEAM:<BR>I In gen.: सन्धिः।<BR>II Cicatrix:<BR>शुष्कव्रणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seaman
SEAMAN: नाविक: v. Sailor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seamanship
SEAMANSHIP:<BR>(1) नाविकता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2) पोतवाहनम्,<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seamless
SEAMLESS:<BR>(1) विसन्धि (mfn.);<BR>(2) वीतसन्धि<BR>(mfn.); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sear
SEAR:<BR>I Adj.: संशुष्क (f. ष्का): v. Dry.<BR>II<BR>Verb: निर्दहति (दह्, c. 1.): v. To burn,<BR>scorch, dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

search
SEARCH:<BR>(1) अन्विष्यति (इष्, c. 4.), to s. (his)<BR>sister:<BR>स्वसारमन्वेष्टुम्, C. vii.;<BR>s. ing skilfully<BR>in his own house:<BR>स्वगृहे निपुणमन्विष्यन्, D. ii.;<BR>(2) मार्गयति<BR>or<BR>मृगयति, -ते, वि-, परि-, (मृग्, c. 10.),<BR>and I cannot s. for Sītā elsewhere:<BR>न चान्यत्र मया<BR> शक्या वैदेही परिमार्गितुम्, Ram. v. 15. 61.;<BR>(3)<BR>विचिनोति (चि, c. 5.), (whom)<BR>you are s. ing<BR>from wood to wood:<BR>विचिनोषि वने वने, Vi. v.<BR>24.; sleeping and sick (men)<BR>in forests should<BR>be s. ed:<BR>सुप्तारोगार्ताश्च वने विचेयाः, Ve. vi. 3.;<BR>(4) गवेषयति (rare), Ri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

search into
SEARCH INTO: गवेषयति: v. To examine,<BR>enquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

search out
SEARCH OUT: अन्विष्य etc. उपलभते (लभ्, c. 1. =<BR>to find out: q. v.),<BR>he himself has been s. ed<BR>out:<BR>सोऽप्युलब्धः, Ve. vi.;<BR>we could not s. them<BR>out:<BR>न हि विद्मो गतिं तेषां वासञ्च, Mah. iv. 26. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

search
SEARCH (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अन्वेषणम्, -णा,<BR>there is going on s. for this:<BR>एतस्यैव अन्वेषणा वर्तते,<BR>V. ii.;<BR>(2) मार्गणम्, वि-, परि-,<BR>it was proper to<BR>make its s.:<BR>तस्य विमार्गणं नयः, Ki. xiv. 9.;<BR>(3)<BR>विचयः, -नम् (rare), लङ्काविचयः, Ram.: v.<BR>II<BR>Examination, enquiry: q. v.:<BR>(1) अन्वीक्षणम्;<BR>(2) गवेषणा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

searcher
SEARCHER:<BR>(1) अन्वेष्टृ (f. ष्ट्री),<BR>many s. s have<BR>been sent after her:<BR>अन्वेष्टारस्तां प्रति प्रभूताः प्रहिताः,<BR>C. vii.;<BR>(2) अन्वेषक (f. षिका);<BR>(3) गवेषक<BR>(f. षिका = enquirer).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

searching
SEARCHING (adj.):<BR>(1) निपुण (f. णा): v.<BR>Skilful;<BR>(2) अविहत (f. ता): v. Attentive;<BR>(3) सूक्ष्म (f. क्ष्मा): v. Minute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

season
SEASON (subs.):<BR>I Of the year:<BR>(1) ऋतुः,<BR>the s. s attend him like common gardeners:<BR>उद्यानपालसामान्यमृतवस्तमुपासते, Ku. ii. 36.;<BR>(2)<BR>कालः (= time),<BR>the hot s.:<BR>निदाघकालः, Ri.<BR>II<BR>= time: q. v.: कालः,<BR>for a s.:<BR>कञ्चित् कालम्,<BR>Mu. i.;<BR>in due s.:<BR>काले।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

season
SEASON (v.):<BR>I To flavour:<BR>(1) वासयति, अधि-,<BR>(वास्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) often by योजयति, सं-,<BR>(= to unite), Bha.<BR>II To habituate, accus-<BR>-tom: q. v.: प्रगुणं (f. णां) करोति, R. ix. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seasonable
SEASONABLE:<BR>(1) सामयिक (f. की): v. Timely;<BR>(2) उपयुक्त (f. क्ता): v. Suitable, proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seasonableness
SEASONABLENESS:<BR>(1) सामयिकता;<BR>(2) उपयुक्तता;<BR>(3) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seasonably
SEASONABLY:<BR>(1) यथाकालम्: v. Timely;<BR>(2)<BR>उपयुक्तम्: v. Properly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seasoning
SEASONING (subs.): उपस्करः: v. Also relish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seat
SEAT (subs.):<BR>I For sitting:<BR>(1) आसनम्,<BR>take this s.:<BR>इदमासनमास्यताम्, Mu. i.; आसन-<BR>परिग्रहं करोतु, U. iii.; from the s. of justice:<BR>धर्मासनात्, U. i. 7.;<BR>(2) पीठ (mn.: dimi-<BR>-nutive पीठिका = a bench, stool),<BR>on a golden-<BR>legged s.:<BR>हेमपादाङ्कितायां पीठिकायाम्, K. ;<BR>(3)<BR>पर्यङ्कः (a sort of sofa),<BR>on a golden s. covered<BR>with Ranku's skin:<BR>सौवर्णे पर्यङ्के राङ्कवास्तृते, Ram.<BR>ii. 13. 6.;<BR>(4) आसन्दी (= a bamboo chair),<BR>when Vaiśampāyana was s. ed:<BR>आसन्द्यामुपविष्टे<BR> वैशम्पायने, K. ;<BR>(5) शयनम्<BR>or<BR>शयनीयम् (for lying<BR>down): v. Bed;<BR>(6) विष्टरः (rare), s. ed:<BR>विष्टरभाज् (mfn.), R. v. 3.<BR>II Station,<BR>abode:<BR>(1) स्थानम्, the s. of our ancestors:<BR>स्थानं नः पूर्वजानाम्, B. xxii. 28.;<BR>(2) धामन् (n.),<BR>the s. of fortitude:<BR>धाम धैर्यस्य, K. ;<BR>(3) आयतनम्,<BR>s. of all misconduct:<BR>सर्वाविनयानामायतनम्, K.<BR>v. Abode.<BR>III Regular place of sitting:<BR>perh. स्थानम्।<BR>IV That part on which a<BR>person sits: आसनम्, Si. v. 7.<BR>V In riding:<BR>expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seat
SEAT (v.):<BR>I To s. oneself: आसने उपविशति,<BR> सम्-, (विश्, c. 6.), निषीदति (सद्, c. 1.), etc.<BR>II To s. another: आसने उपवेशयति (c. of<BR>विश्)<BR>or<BR>अभिनिवेशयति, Si. i. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seated
SEATED:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) आसीन (f. ना),<BR>and<BR>when all of them had s.:<BR>सर्वासु चासीनासु तासु,<BR>K. ;<BR>(2) उपविष्ट (f. ष्टा), सम्-;<BR>(3) स्थ (f. स्था)<BR>in comp.,<BR>s. in heart:<BR>हृदयस्थ (f. स्था), R. x. 19.<BR>II Rooted: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secant
SECANT: in math.: *विच्छेदिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secede
SECEDE:<BR>(1) अपसरति (सृ c. 1.): v. To<BR>retire, withdraw;<BR>(2) आश्रयति (श्रि, c. 1. =<BR>to betake to, as to a different league).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seceder
SECEDER:<BR>(1) भिन्नमतग्राहिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2)<BR>मतान्तराश्रित (f. ता); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secession
SECESSION:<BR>(1) अपसरणम्: v. Withdrawal;<BR>(2) मतान्तरग्रहणम् and sim. expr.s. (in<BR>opinion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seclude
SECLUDE:<BR>I To shut up: q. v.: निरुणद्धि (रुध्,<BR>c. 7.).<BR>II To live in seclusion: विविक्तम्<BR> आश्रयति (श्रि, c. 1.); एकान्ते वसति (वस्, c. 1.);<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secluded
SECLUDED (adj.):<BR>(1) विविक्त (f. क्ता),<BR>in a s.<BR>spot:<BR>विविक्तप्रदेशे, P. i. 4.;<BR>(2) विजन (f. ना)<BR>v. Lonely, solitary;<BR>(3) निभृत (f. ता):<BR>v. Quiet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seclusion
SECLUSION:<BR>(1) विविक्तता, -त्वम् (the state);<BR>(2)<BR>विविक्तम्,<BR>heart-satisfying s.:<BR>चित्तनिर्वृतिविधायि<BR> विविक्तम्, Ki. ix. 71.;<BR>(3) रहस् (n. = privacy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

second
SECOND (adj.): द्वितीय (f. या), in the s. (8th<BR>portion): द्वितीयेऽ(ष्टमे भागे), D. viii.; this<BR>title does not belong to a s. (i. e. to any body<BR>else): द्वितीयगामी न हि शब्द एष नः, R. iii. 49.<BR>Ph.: without a s. (i. e. parallel):<BR>(1)<BR>अद्वितीय (f. या);<BR>(2) अतिद्वय (f. या: rare), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

second
SECOND (v.): अनुकूलयति: v. To help, favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

second
SECOND (subs.):<BR>I Of time:<BR>(1) पलम्, वि-;<BR>(2) विकला: v. Moment.<BR>II Promoter,<BR>supporter: q. v.: अनुकूलकारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

second-hand
SECOND-HAND:<BR>I Not new:<BR>(1) अन्यभुक्त<BR>(f. क्ता) and sim. comp. s.<BR>(2) पुराण (f. णा<BR>= old: q. v.).<BR>II Not original: s. witness:<BR>श्रुतसाक्षी, Mit.;<BR>s. knowledge:<BR>अन्यमूलं ज्ञानम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

second-rate
SECOND-RATE:<BR>(1) द्वितीयश्रेणीय (f. या);<BR>(2)<BR>मध्यम (f. मा = middling).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secondary
SECONDARY:<BR>(1) perh. द्वैतीयिक (f. की);<BR>(2)<BR>अप्रधान (f. ना) and sim. comp.s. (= not<BR>chief: q. v.): v. Also second-rate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secondarily
SECONDARILY:<BR>(1) द्वितीयतः (= secondly);<BR>(2)<BR>गौणतः (= figuratively).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seconder
SECONDER:<BR>(1) अनुकूलयितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) पक्ष-<BR>समर्थक (f. र्थिका); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secondly
SECONDLY:<BR>(1) द्वितीयतः;<BR>(2) द्वितीयम्;<BR>(3) तत्र<BR> पुनः (= then again).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

second sight
SECOND SIGHT: दिव्यचक्षुस् (n.) and sim.<BR>comp.s.,<BR>endowed with s.:<BR>दिव्येन चक्षुषा समन्वित<BR>(f. ता), Mah. vi. 2. 10.: v. Sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secrecy
SECRECY:<BR>(1) गूढता, नि-;<BR>(2) गुह्यता;<BR>(3)<BR>गोपनीयता;<BR>(4) गुप्तिः: for dif.: v. Secret,<BR>seclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secret
SECRET: (adj.):<BR>I Concealed, hid:<BR>(1) गुढ<BR>(f. ढा), नि-,<BR>surrounded by s. emissaries:<BR>गुढ-<BR>पुरुषैः परिवृतः, D. viii.;<BR>(2) गुप्त (f. प्ता);<BR>(3)<BR>छन्न (f. न्ना), प्र-।<BR>II What should be<BR>concealed:<BR>(1) गुह्य (f. ह्या),<BR>shall not dis-<BR>close master's s. doings and plans:<BR>गुह्यं कर्म च<BR> मन्त्रं च न भर्तुः सम्प्रकाशयेत्, Ka. v. 31.;<BR>(2) रहस्य<BR>(f. स्या):<BR>(3) गोप्य (f. प्या);<BR>(4) गोपनीय<BR>(f. या): v. Secret (subs.).<BR>III Occult:<BR>(1) गूढ (f. ढा), नि-;<BR>(2) गुह्य (f. ह्या).<BR>IV<BR>Secluded, retired: q. v.: गूढ (f. ढा), नि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secret
SECRET, KEEP:<BR>(1) निह्नुते (ह्नु, c. 2.: with<BR>abl.), keeping (it) very s. for two, three, four<BR>(days): द्वित्रिचतुरमतिनिह्नु त्यापि, D. ii.;<BR>(2)<BR>गोपायति (गुप्, c. 10.), (gen. with dat.), not<BR>to k. (it)<BR>s. from you:<BR>किं ते गोपायित्वा, D. vi.;<BR>(3) नि-गुहति, -ते (गुह्, c. 1.: with dat, or<BR>abl.),<BR>why do you k. this disease s.:<BR>किमेतमात्मन<BR> उपद्रवं निगूहसि, Sa. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secret
SECRET (subs.):<BR>(1) रहस्यम्,<BR>and the s. will<BR>not ooze out:<BR>रहस्यञ्च न स्रवति, D. ii.;<BR>not to<BR>divulge the s.:<BR>रहस्यानिर्भेदाय, D. ii.;<BR>have you<BR>kept the s. entrusted to you:<BR>रक्ष्यते भवता रहस्य-<BR>निक्षेपः, V. ii.; does not communicate (his) s. s:<BR>नरहस्यानि विवृणोति, D. viii.;<BR>(2) गुह्यम्, गोप्यम्,<BR>etc. (n. of adj. s from गुह and गुप्), if it is [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">Page624</a>]<BR>not a s.:<BR>न चेद्गोप्यम्, D. iv.;<BR>the s. being dis-<BR>closed:<BR>विवृतगुह्यः, D. iv. Ph.: (a)<BR>in s.:<BR>रहसि<BR>: v. Privately, secretly; (b) it is no longer<BR>a s. to the townsmen that: प्रकाशतां गतोऽयमर्थो<BR> पौरेषु यथा ॥॥।, Mu. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secretariate
SECRETARIATE: सचिवसभा (?); सचिवशाला (?);<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secretary
SECRETARY: सचिवः (?),<BR>private s.:<BR>रहस्य-<BR>सचिवः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secrete
SECRETE:<BR>I To hide, conceal: q. v.: गोपायति<BR>(गुप्, c. 10.).<BR>II To separate, produce:<BR>मावयति आ-, परि-, सं-, (c. of, स्रु), Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secretion
SECRETION:<BR>I As of sap: स्रावः, -णम्, आ-,<BR> परि-।<BR>II Matter secreted: स्रावः, आ-, परि-,<BR>watery s.:<BR>सलिलप्रकाश आस्रावः, Sr.<BR>III Con-<BR>-cealment: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secretly
SECRETLY:<BR>(1) रहसि: v. Privately;<BR>(2) गूढम्,<BR> नि-,<BR>s. creating:<BR>गुढमुत्पाद्य, D. viii.;<BR>(3) गुप्तम्,<BR>you are to tell me very s.:<BR>त्वया सुगुप्तं ममावेदनीयम्,<BR>P. iv. 11.;<BR>(4) छन्नम्, प्र-, (= unseen),<BR>threw<BR>away s.:<BR>छन्नमेव प्राक्षिपम्, D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secretness
SECRETNESS: गोपनीयता: v. Secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secretory
SECRETORY:<BR>(1) expr. by comp.;<BR>(2) स्राविन्<BR>(f. णी), आ-, परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sect
SECT:<BR>(1) शाखा (= branch);<BR>(2) सम्प्रदायः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sectarian
SECTARIAN:<BR>(1) शाखागत (f. ता);<BR>(2) साम्प्र-<BR>दायिक (f. की: (?): v. Also sectary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sectarianism
SECTARIANISM: स्वसम्प्रदायानुरागः and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sectary
SECTARY:<BR>(1) शाखिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) सम्प्रदायभुक्त<BR>(f. क्ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

section
SECTION:<BR>I Division: q. v.: छेदः, वि-, परि-।<BR>II Of a book:<BR>(1) परिच्छेदः;<BR>(2) पादः,<BR>ist<BR>s. of ist chapter:<BR>प्रथमाध्यायस्य प्रथमपादः, Kāśikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sector
SECTOR: वृत्तखण्डम्, K. d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secular
SECULAR:<BR>I Worldly: q. v.: लौकिक (f. की).<BR>II Timely: q. v.: सामयिक (f. की).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secularity
SECULARITY:<BR>(1) ऐहिकता;<BR>(2) सांसारिकता;<BR>(3)<BR>लौकिकता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secure
SECURE (adj.):<BR>I Careless: q. v.<BR>II Safe:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) वीतभय (f. या);<BR>(2) निर्विशङ्क (f. ङ्का);<BR>(3) स्थिर (f. रा = firm), fancying very s.:<BR>सुस्थिरंमन्यः, Si. ii. 32.<BR>II Certain: q. v.:<BR>निश्चित (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

secure
SECURE (v.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) रक्षति (रक्ष्,<BR>c. 1.): v. Protect;<BR>(2) स्थिरीकरोति (= to<BR>make firm or give).<BR>II To insure: ध्रुवम्<BR>or<BR>निश्चितम् आवहति (वह्, c. 1.).<BR>III To make<BR>fast, seize: बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

securely
SECURELY:<BR>I Fearlessly: q. v.:<BR>(1) निर्भयम्;<BR>(2) वीतविशङ्कम्।<BR>II Safely: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

security
SECURITY:<BR>I Safety: q. v.:<BR>(1) रक्षा;<BR>(2)<BR>स्थैर्यम् (= firmness).<BR>II Freedom from<BR>anxiety:<BR>(1) निर्विशङ्कता;<BR>(2) निरुपद्रवता;<BR>(3)<BR>निर्विध्नता;<BR>(4) निरृतिः।<BR>III Guard, defence:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) गुप्तिः;<BR>(2) रक्षा।<BR>IV Pledge: q. v.:<BR>प्रातिभाव्यम्,<BR>a debt for s.:<BR>ऋणं प्रातिभाव्यागतम्, Kat.<BR>V. A surety: q. v.: प्रतिभूः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sedan
SEDAN: शिविका: v. Litter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sedater
SEDATER:<BR>(1) धीर (f. रा);<BR>(2) शान्त (f. न्ता)<BR>v. Calm, quiet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sedately
SEDATELY:<BR>(1) धीरम्;<BR>(2) शान्तम्: v. Calmly,<BR>quietly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sedateness
SEDATENESS:<BR>(1) धैर्यम्;<BR>(2) शान्तता: v. Calm-<BR>-ness, quietness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sedative
SEDATIVE:<BR>(1) शीतल (f. ला = cooling), Bha.;<BR>(2) शान्तिकर (f. री), -प्रद (f. दा), etc. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sedentariness
SEDENTARINESS:<BR>(1) निरुद्योगता (?);<BR>(2) चलन-<BR>पराङ्मुखता; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sedentary
SEDENTARY:<BR>(1) निरुद्योग (f. गा) and sim. comp. s.<BR>(= not active: q. v.);<BR>(2) चलनपराङ्भुख<BR>(f. खी (?). Ph.:<BR>s. life:<BR>विविक्तजीवनम् (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sedge
SEDGE: नलविशेषः: v. Reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sediment
SEDIMENT:<BR>(1) मलम्;<BR>(2) किट्टम्;<BR>(3) कल्कम्;<BR>(4) खलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sedition
SEDITION:<BR>(1) राजाक्रोशः and sim. comp. s.;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रजासंक्षोभः and sim. comp. s. (= popular<BR>agitation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seditious
SEDITIOUS:<BR>(1) by comp.,<BR>one who uses s.<BR>language:<BR>राजाक्रोशकारिन् (f. णी), Y. ii. 305.;<BR>(2) राज्यभेदक (f. दिका) and sim. comp. s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seditiously
SEDITIOUSLY:<BR>(1) राज्यभेदं प्रकल्पयत् (f. न्ती);<BR>(2) प्रजासंक्षोभं कुर्वत् (f. ती); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seduce
SEDUCE:<BR>(1) दूषयति (c. of दुष): v. To defile,<BR>pollute;<BR>(2) नाशयति (c. of नश् = to ruin),<BR>will allure and s. the girl:<BR>बालां विलोभ्य<BR> नाशयिष्यति, D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seducement
SEDUCEMENT: v. Seduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seducer
SEDUCER:<BR>(1) दूषयितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) दूषक (f. षिका);<BR>(3) नाशयितृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seduction
SEDUCTION:<BR>(1) दूषणम्,<BR>s. of girls:<BR>कन्यादूषणम्,<BR>Mit.;<BR>(2) नाशः, -नम् (= ruining);<BR>(3) शील-<BR>पातनम् and sim. comp. s. (only of chastity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seductive
SEDUCTIVE:<BR>(1) प्रलोभन (f. नी);<BR>(2) प्रलोभक<BR>(f. भिका);<BR>(3) विलोभन (f. नी)<BR>or<BR>-क<BR>(f. भिका);<BR>(4) हारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(5) आकर्षक<BR>(f. र्षिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seductively
SEDUCTIVELY:<BR>(1) प्र-<BR>or<BR>वि- लोभ्य;<BR>(2) प्रलोभनं<BR> कुर्वत् (f. ती); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sedulity
SEDULITY, SEDULOUSNESS: अध्यवसायः: v. Dili-<BR>-gence, industry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sedulous
SEDULOUS: अध्यवसायिन् (f. नी): v. Diligent,<BR>assiduous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sedulously
SEDULOUSLY:<BR>(1) साध्यवसायम्;<BR>(2) साभियोगम्<BR>: v. Diligently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

see
SEE (subs.): perh.<BR>(1) मण्डलम्;<BR>(2) अधिकारः<BR>(= jurisdiction).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

see
SEE (v.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) पश्यति (दृश्, c. 1.),<BR>old men s. what will come:<BR>वृद्धबुद्धिरनागतं पश्यति,<BR>Vi. vi.;<BR>s. ing close by that he was unassailable<BR>even by mind:<BR>पश्यन्नदूरान्मनसाऽप्यधृष्यम्, Ku. iii.<BR>51.; I do not s. any one greater than or (even)<BR>equal to Rāma:<BR>पश्यामि रामादधिकं समं वा नान्यम्,<BR>B. xii. 51.; you will s. the jaws of death:<BR>द्रक्ष्यसि मृत्युमुखम्, D. ii.;<BR>to s. his dear old friend<BR>Vālmīki:<BR>चिरन्तनप्रियसुहृदं प्राचेतसं द्रष्टुम्, U. iv.;<BR>(2) ईक्षते, वि-, प्र-, निर्- सम्, अव-, सम्प्र-, (ईक्ष,<BR>c. 1.), (gen. with the eye. Also = look into,<BR>look to, etc.: q. v.), s. ing that it is the first<BR>(offence): प्रथममिति प्रेक्ष्य, Sa. iv.;<BR>(3) विलोकयति,<BR> अव-: v. To look;<BR>(4) निर्वर्णयति (वर्ण्, c. 10.<BR>= to look at attentively);<BR>(5) निमालयति,<BR> -ते (भल्, c. 10 = 4.: rare), N. xi. 1.<BR>II<BR>Beware: expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seed
SEED (subs.): बीजम्,<BR>for he who sows as. gets<BR>its fruit also:<BR>यो यद्वपति बीजं हि लभते सोऽपि<BR> तत्फलम्, K. s. xvii. 148.; seller of bad s. s:<BR>अबीजविक्रयी, M. ix. 291.;<BR>he who waters with<BR>discretion the seeds of work to be done:<BR>योऽभि-<BR>वर्षति विधिबीजानि विवेकवारिणा, Ki. ii. 31.; whose<BR>s. is the asking of the daughter of the king of<BR>Videha:<BR>बीजं यस्य विदेहतनयायाच्ञा, Vi. vi. 1.;<BR>to bear the s. of the two:<BR>वोढुमुभयोर्बीजम्, Ku.<BR>v. 60.; as if its starry grains have been ejected<BR>by the s.- (pulp)<BR>eating time:<BR>तारामयं बीज-<BR>भुजादसीयं कालेन निष्ठ्यू तमिवास्थियूथम्, N. xxii. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seed-corn
SEED-CORN, SEED-GRAIN: बीजधान्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seed-plot
SEED-PLOT, SEED-PLAT: prob. वीजक्षेत्रम्, बीज-<BR>भूमिः, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seed-time
SEED-TIME: वपनकालः and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seed-vessel
SEED-VESSEL: बीजकोशः (षः), N. com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seedling
SEEDLING:<BR>(1) बीजप्ररोहः;<BR>(2) बीजरुहः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seedsman
SEEDSMAN:<BR>I The dealer:<BR>(1) बीजविक्रयिन्<BR>(m.);<BR>(2) बीजविक्रेतृ (m.); etc.<BR>II The<BR>owner: बीजवत्<BR>or<BR>बीजिन् (m.), M. ix. 49., 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seedy
SEEDY:<BR>(1) बीजपूर्ण (f. र्णा);<BR>(2) बीजमय (f.<BR>यी);<BR>(3) बहुबीज (f. जा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seeing that
SEEING THAT: = since, for, because: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seek
SEEK (v.):<BR>I To look for: अन्विष्यति (इष्,<BR>c. 4.), you who are to be sought in this world:<BR>अन्वेष्टव्यो यदसि भुवने, U. ii. 13.: v. To search.<BR>II To endeavour to gain:<BR>(1) कामयते, अभि-<BR>(कम्, c. 10. = wish: q. v.),<BR>sought ground with<BR>young shoots:<BR>अचकमत सपल्लवां धरित्रीम्, Ki. x.<BR>49.;<BR>(2) कांक्षते, -ति, आ-, अभि- (कांक्ष, c. 1.<BR>= 1), s.ing (your)<BR>place:<BR>पदकांक्षिन् (f. णी),<BR>Ku. iii. 4.;<BR>(3) प्रार्थयते (अर्थ्, c. 10. = ask,<BR>beg: q. v.), I do not s. pleasure or wealth:<BR>न सुखं प्रार्थये नार्थम्, Ki. xi. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seek
SEEK (v. i.):<BR>I To make search: अन्वेषणं<BR> करोति: v. To search.<BR>II To endeavour,<BR>strive: q. v.: घटते (घट्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seeker
SEEKER:<BR>(1) अन्वेषक (f. षिका): v. Searcher;<BR>(2) प्रार्थयितृ (f. त्री): v. Solicitor;<BR>(3)<BR>कामयितृ (f. त्री), अभि-: v. To wish, long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seem
SEEM:<BR>(1) दृश्यते (pass. of दृश् = to look: q. v.);<BR>(2) भाति, आ-, वि-, प्रति-, निर्- (भा, c. 2. = to<BR>appear),<BR>why the great city of Oude s. s. to me<BR>to be bereft of its beauty:<BR>गतश्रीरिव मे भाति<BR> केनायोध्या महापुरी, Ram. ii. 73. 21. Ph.: it<BR>s. s (= I think): मन्ये;<BR>it s. s simply for my puri-<BR>fication:<BR>मन्ये मत्पावनायैव, Ku. vi. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seeming
SEEMING:<BR>I Subs.: दर्शनम्: v. Appearance, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">Page626</a>]<BR>semblance.<BR>II Adj.: expr. by verb: v.<BR>Also apparent (III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seemingly
SEEMINGLY:<BR>(1) प्रकटम्: v. Openly;<BR>(2)<BR>बहिस् (n.): v. Externally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seemliness
SEEMLINESS:<BR>(1) उपयुक्तता: v. Propriety:<BR>(2)<BR>विनीतता: v. Decency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seemly
SEEMLY:<BR>(1) उपयुक्त (f. क्ता): v. Suitable,<BR>proper;<BR>(2) विनीत (f. ता): v. Decent.<BR>To<BR>be s.:<BR>युज्यते, उप-, (pass. of युज्: with loc.),<BR>Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seer
SEER:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) द्रष्टृ (f. ष्ट्री);<BR>(2) दर्शक<BR>(f. र्शिका);<BR>(3) दर्शिन् (f. नी).<BR>II A pro-<BR>-phet: q. v.: सिद्ध (f. द्धा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seethe
SEETHE: क्वथति<BR>or<BR>क्वाथयति (क्वथ्, c. 1. and c.<BR>10.: lit, and fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

segment
SEGMENT:<BR>(1) धनुःक्षेत्रम्<BR>or<BR>चापक्षेत्रम्, K. d. (of a<BR>circle);<BR>(2) खण्डम् (in gen.) N. B. S. s of the<BR>base of a triangle made by the perpendi-<BR>-cular from the opposite angle: आबाधे or<BR>अवबाधे, Li. 137., in an obtuse a. ed t. ऋणाबाधे,<BR>Li. 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

segregate
SEGREGATE:<BR>(1) वियोजयति (युज्, c. 10.);<BR>(2)<BR>विश्लेषयति (c. of श्लिषः): v. To separate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

segregation
SEGREGATION: विश्लेषः: v. Separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seigneurial
SEIGNEURIAL, SEIGNIORIAL: expr. by gen. or<BR>comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seignior
SEIGNIOR:<BR>(1) स्वामिन् (m.);<BR>(2) प्रभुः: v.<BR>Lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seigniorage
SEIGNIORAGE: करविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seizable
SEIZABLE:<BR>(1) ग्राह्य (f. ह्या);<BR>(2) ग्रहणीय (f.<BR>या);<BR>(3) धार्य (f. र्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seize
SEIZE:<BR>I To catch: q. v.: गृह्नाति (ग्रह्, c.<BR>9.),<BR>to s. me:<BR>ग्रहणे मम, Mah. vii. 73. 1.;<BR>s. s by the hair:<BR>केशैर्गृह्नाति, P.<BR>II To take<BR>possession of: गृह्नाति,<BR>your house has been s. d<BR>by another alligator:<BR>त्वदीयं गृहमपरेण मकरेण गृहीतम्,<BR>P. iv. 9.: v. Also to enter.<BR>III To in-<BR>-vade, attack: q. v.: आक्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.):<BR>v. Also to possess.<BR>IV To apprehend:<BR>गृह्नाति, प्र-,<BR>to s. on suspicion:<BR>शङ्कया गृह्णाति, Y.:<BR>v. To arrest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seizer
SEIZER:<BR>(1) ग्राहक (f. हिका), Y.;<BR>(2) ग्रहीतृ<BR>(f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seizure
SEIZURE:<BR>(1) ग्रहणम् (rarely ग्रहः);<BR>(2) धारणम्<BR>(= catching).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seldom
SELDOM:<BR>(1) क्वचित्;<BR>(2) कदाचित्;<BR>(3) कर्हिचित्<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

select
SELECT (v.): वृणीते (c. 9.): v. To choose;<BR>(2) आहरति (हृ, c. 1. = to pick out).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

select
SELECT (adj.):<BR>(1) वृत (f. ता: (?);<BR>(2) विशिष्ट<BR>(f. ष्टा = choice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

selection
SELECTION: no proper equiv.: expr. by<BR>verb.<BR>Easy s.:<BR>सहजसंग्रहः (?); choice s.:<BR>उत्कृष्टसमाहारः (?); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

selenite
SELENITE: चन्द्रकान्तः (?), -उपलः; *चन्द्रप्रभः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

self
SELF:<BR>(1) आत्मन् (m.),<BR>s.-born:<BR>आत्मभूः (n. भु);<BR>s. -destroyer:<BR>आत्मघातिन् (f. नी); s. -interest:<BR>आत्महितम्;<BR>good for s.:<BR>आत्मनीन (f. ना): v.<BR>Also myself, himself, etc.;<BR>(2) स्वयम् (=<BR>I<BR>myself, you yourself, etc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

selfish
SELFISH:<BR>(1) स्वार्थपर (f. रा);<BR>(2) स्वार्थपरायण<BR>(f. णा);<BR>(3) स्वार्थनिष्ठ (f. ष्ठा);<BR>(4) by verb,<BR>every one is s.:<BR>सर्वः स्वार्थ समीहते, Si. ii. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

selfishly
SELFISHLY: expr. by adj. or verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

selfishness
SELFISHNESS:<BR>(1) स्वार्थपरता;<BR>(2) स्वार्थपरायणता;<BR>(3) स्वार्थनिष्ठा; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sell
SELL (v. t.):<BR>(1) विक्रीणीते (क्री, c. 9.),<BR>s. ing it<BR>to others:<BR>विक्रीणानस्तदन्यत्र, N. s.; Oh., (you)<BR>attempted to s. us like meat:<BR>प्रारब्धा मांसवदहो<BR> विक्रेतुमेते वयम्, Mu. v. 21.;<BR>(2) विक्रयं करोति:<BR>I will very mercilessly s. you:<BR>करोम्येष विक्रयं ते<BR> सुनिर्घृणः, D. b. vii. 22-1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sell
SELL (v. i.): (सूल्यं) लभते, if 8 silk clothes s. for<BR>100 (rupees): पट्टसूत्रपटिका अष्टौ लभन्ते शतम्, Li.<BR>55.; (my)<BR>friend, at what price will fourteen<BR>s.:<BR>चतुर्दश सखे मूल्यं लभन्ते कियत्, Li. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seller
SELLER:<BR>(1) विक्रेतृ (f. त्री),<BR>it is to be returned<BR>to the s.:<BR>विक्रेतुः प्रतिदेयं तत्, N. s.; s. of self (a<BR>slave): आत्मविक्रेता, Mit.;<BR>(2) विक्रयिन् (f. णी),<BR>shame on this s. of honour:<BR>धिङ् मानविक्रयिण-<BR>मिमम् K. s. 43. 85.;<BR>(3) विक्रयिक (f. की);<BR>(4) विक्रयकारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

selling
SELLING (subs.): विक्रयः: v. Sale, to sell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

selvage
SELVA(ED)GE:<BR>(1) दशा;<BR>(2) वस्तिः;<BR>(3) तरी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

semblance
SEMBLANCE:<BR>(1) आभा;<BR>(2) आभासः;<BR>(3)<BR>अवभासः: v. Also appearance (IV), likeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

semen
SEMEN:<BR>(1) शुक्रम्;<BR>(2) रेतस् (n.);<BR>(3) बीजम्;<BR>(4) वीर्यम्;<BR>(5) तेजस्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

semicircle
SEMICIRCLE:<BR>(1) अर्धवृत्तम्;<BR>(2) वृत्तार्धम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seminal
SEMINAL: expr. by comp.,<BR>s. discharge:<BR>रेतः-<BR>पातः, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seminary
SEMINARY: विद्यालयः: v. School.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

semitone
SEMITONE: स्वरावरोहः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

semivowel
SEMIVOWEL: अन्तःस्थो वर्णः (in Sanskrit); *अर्ध-<BR>स्वरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sempiternal
SEMPITERNAL: नित्य (f. त्या): v. Eternal,<BR>everlasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

senate
SENATE:<BR>(1) मन्त्रिसभा (?);<BR>(2) महासभा (?);<BR>(3)<BR>व्यवस्थासभा (?: as in France and univer-<BR>-sities).<BR>S. -home:<BR>सभागृहम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

senator
SENATOR:<BR>(1) सचिवः (= counsellor);<BR>(2)<BR>सदस्यः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

senatorial
SENATORIAL: expr. by comp.,<BR>s. robe:<BR>सचिव-<BR>वेषः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

send
SEND (v.):<BR>I To despatch:<BR>(1) प्रेरयति, सं-,<BR>(ईर्, c. 10.), the rays sent forth by the moon:<BR>प्रेरितः शशधरेण करौघः, Ki. ix. 30.;<BR>(2) प्रेषयति,<BR> सं-, (c. of इष्), does not s. (me)<BR>tempting<BR>things:<BR>न विलोभनवस्तूनि प्रेषयति, D. viii.;<BR>(3)<BR>प्रहिणोति (हि, c. 5.),<BR>Indra sent to him the<BR>nymph Hariṇī:<BR>प्रजिघाय हरिरस्मै हरिणीं सुराङ्गनाम्,<BR>R. viii. 79.;<BR>(4) विसृजति (सृज्, c. 6.: rare),<BR>Bhoja sent an envoy to Raghu:<BR>भोजेन दूतो रघवे<BR> विसृष्टः, R. v. 39.<BR>II To hush, discharge:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.);<BR>(2) विसृजति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

send away
SEND AWAY:<BR>(1) विसृजति;<BR>(2) प्रस्थापयति (c.<BR>of स्था), R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

send for
SEND FOR: आह्वयति (ह्ने, c. 1.): v. To call,<BR>summon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

send forth
SEND FORTH:<BR>(1) विसृजति: v. To emit;<BR>(2)<BR>ऊर्ध्वं वितनोति (तन्, c. 7.) etc. (= to send up,<BR>as branches), R. xiii. 10.;<BR>(3) प्रसारयति (c.<BR>of सृ = to spread).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sender
SENDER:<BR>(1) प्रेर(ष)क (f. रिका<BR>or<BR>षिका);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रेर(ष)यितृ (f. त्री); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sending
SENDING (subs.) प्रेरणम्;<BR>(2) प्रेषः, -णम्, सं-;<BR>(3)<BR>प्रेर(ष)णा (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

senile
SENILE:<BR>(1) वार्धक्यजन्य (f. न्या) and sim.<BR>comp.s;<BR>(2) by circumlo.: v. Old age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

senility
SENILITY:<BR>(1) वृद्धावस्था;<BR>(2) वृद्धभावः;<BR>(3)<BR>वर्षीयस्त्वम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

senior
SENIOR:<BR>(1) ज्येष्ठ (f. ष्ठा): v. Elder;<BR>(2)<BR>वरिष्ठ (f. ष्ठा): v. Superior;<BR>(3) गुरुः, -जनः<BR>(= respectable person), you are (my) s.:<BR>गुरवो यूयम्, Vi. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seniority
SENIORITY: ज्येष्ठता, -त्वम्<BR>or<BR>ज्यैष्ठ्यम्, s. in age:<BR>वयोज्यैष्ठ्यम्;<BR>according to s.:<BR>अनुज्यैष्ठ्यम्: v. Also<BR>superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sennight
SENNIGHT:<BR>(1) सप्ताहः: v. Week;<BR>(2) सप्तरात्रम्<BR>and sim. comp.s (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sensation
SENSATION:<BR>I In philo.: nearest word<BR>प्रत्यक्षम्,<BR>s. is of six kinds involving smell, taste,<BR>sight, touch, hearing, and mind:<BR>घ्राणजं रासनं<BR> चाक्षुषं स्पार्शनं श्रौत्रं मानसमिति षड्विधं प्रत्यक्षम्, Par.<BR>II Consciousness: q. v.: चेतना।<BR>III Per-<BR>-ception, knowledge: q. v.: उपलब्धिः।<BR>IV<BR>A great impression: expr. by circumlo.:<BR>it created s. at the time:<BR>*जनमनस्तत्कालमाचकर्षैतत्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sensational
SENSATIONAL:<BR>s. theory:<BR>प्रत्यक्षमतम्; s. novel:<BR>*हृदयक्षोभिकाख्यायिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sensationalist
SENSATIONALIST:<BR>(1) प्रत्यक्षवादिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sense
SENSE:<BR>I Organ: इन्द्रियम्, s. of touch:<BR>स्पर्शेन्द्रियम्;<BR>s. of taste:<BR>रसनेन्द्रियम्; etc. Ph.:<BR>to deprive one of the s. of sight:<BR>चक्षुषी उद्धरति<BR>(with gen.), D.; and sound is the object of<BR>(the s. of)<BR>hearing:<BR>शब्दोऽपि गोचरः श्रुतेः, Par.<BR>53.<BR>II Perception, feeling: उपलब्धिः। Ph.:<BR>to have s. of:<BR>चेतयते, D. viii. or पश्यति (= to<BR>see: q. v.).<BR>III Soundness of the facul-<BR>-ties:<BR>common s.:<BR>विवेकः;<BR>moral s.:<BR>धर्मबुद्धिः<BR>(?);<BR>to recover s. s:<BR>संज्ञां लभते, Ma. ix.;<BR>loss<BR>of s. s:<BR>धीविभ्रमः, Bha;<BR>one who has lost the s.<BR>of honour by decrepitude:<BR>जरावलुप्तमानावमानचितः,<BR>D. i.<BR>IV Meaning:<BR>(1) अर्थ:,<BR>otherwise the<BR>plural “daughters” has no s.:<BR>अन्यथा दुहितर इति<BR> बहुवचनमनर्थकम्, Da. 141.;<BR>do not take the say-<BR>ing in its real sense:<BR>परमार्थेन न गृह्यतां वचः, Sa.<BR>ii. 19.; have you comprehended its literal s.:<BR>अपि गृहीतो भवताक्षरार्थः, Sa. v.; as the word<BR>अपि<BR>is not described in the s. of<BR>एव: अपिशब्दस्यैव-<BR>कारार्थेऽवर्णनात्, Da.;<BR>a vocabulary of words<BR>having various s. s:<BR>नानार्थशब्दकोषः, Medini; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">Page628</a>]<BR>(2) by sim. loc. in lexicons, रत्न<BR>conveys the s.<BR>of ‘superior’ as well as of ‘gem’:<BR>रत्नं श्रेष्ठे<BR> भणावपि, Viśva;<BR>(3) मावः। (= purport).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sensible
SENSIBLE:<BR>I Perceptible:<BR>(1) इन्द्रियग्राह्य (f.<BR>ह्या);<BR>(2) इन्द्रियगोचर (f. रा); and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR>II Capable of perceiving: विषय-<BR>ग्राहिन् (f. णी) and sim. comp.s. To be s. of<BR>= to perceive, feel: q. v.<BR>III Intelligent,<BR>shrewd: q. v.: बुद्धिमत् (f. ती).<BR>IV As of<BR>replies: उपयुक्त (f. क्ता): v. Proper, suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sensibly
SENSIBLY:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by circumlo.: v.<BR>Sensible (I and<BR>II).<BR>II Judiciously,<BR>cleverly: q. v.: विविच्य।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sensitive
SENSITIVE:<BR>I Having sense:<BR>(1) चेतन (f.<BR>नी);<BR>(2) सचेतन (f. ना);<BR>(3) चेतनवत् (f.<BR>ती).<BR>II Easily affected:<BR>(1) चलेन्द्रिय (f.<BR>या: (?), Ki. ii. 39.;<BR>(2) by circumlo.: v.<BR>To affect, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sensitiveness
SENSITIVENESS:<BR>I Lit.: चेतनत्वम्, -ता, सं-।<BR>II<BR>Acute sensibility:<BR>(1) चलेन्द्रियत्वम्, -ता;<BR>(2)<BR>मृदुप्रकृतिः (= soft nature);<BR>(3) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sensitive plant
SENSITIVE PLANT:<BR>(1) लज्जावती;<BR>(2) लज्जालुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sensual
SENSUAL:<BR>I Lit.: by comp.: v. Sense.<BR>II<BR>Carnal: expr. with विषय<BR>or<BR>इन्द्रिय in comp.,<BR>became indifferent to s. pleasures:<BR>विषयेषु निःस्पृहो-<BR>ऽभवत्, R. viii. 10.;<BR>turning the mind from s.<BR>pleasures:<BR>निवर्त्य विषयसुखेभ्यो मनः, K.<BR>III<BR>Voluptuous:<BR>(1) विषयासक्तचेतस् (mfn.) and<BR>sim. comp.s;<BR>(2) इन्द्रियसुखनिरत (f. ता) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sensualist
SENSUALIST: v. Sensual (III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sensuality
SENSUALITY:<BR>(1) विषयासक्तिः;<BR>(2) विषयसुखासक्तिः;<BR>(3) इन्द्रियसुखोपभोगः;<BR>(4) सुरतसेवा (= lewd-<BR>-ness); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sentence
SENTENCE (subs.):<BR>I Decision: q. v.: निर्णयः।<BR>II Condemnation: दण्डाज्ञा and sim.<BR>comp. s. III. Maxim: सूत्रम्।<BR>IV Of words:<BR>वाक्यम्,<BR>complex s.:<BR>महावाक्यम्, Sah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sentence
SENTENCE (v.):<BR>(1) आदिशति (दिश्, c. 6. = to<BR>order: q. v.,<BR>s. d him to death:<BR>तस्य वधमादिशत्;<BR>(2) शास्ति (शास्, c. 2. = to chastise),<BR>will be<BR>s. d to this punishment:<BR>एतेन दण्डेन शास्यते, Mr.<BR>x.: v. Punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sententious
SENTENTIOUS:<BR>(1) लघु (f. घ्वी);<BR>(2) लाघव-<BR>गुणोपेत (f. ता) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sententiously
SENTENTIOUSLY:<BR>(1) लघु;<BR>(2) सलाघवम्;<BR>(3)<BR>by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sentient
SENTIENT:<BR>(1) चेतन- in comp.;<BR>(2) सचेतन (f.<BR>ना);<BR>(3) चेतनावत् (f. ती);<BR>(4) चैतन्यवत् (f.<BR>ती); सचेतस् (mfn.) and sim. comp.s (hav-<BR>-ing heart).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sentiment
SENTIMENT:<BR>I Thought, opinion: q. v.:<BR>मतम्।<BR>II Feeling, passion: रसः, s. of love:<BR>शृङ्गाररसः।<BR>III Sense: q. v.: भावः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sentimental
SENTIMENTAL:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) रसिक (f. का);<BR>(2) सराग (f. गा : (?).<BR>II Of plays etc.:<BR>रसभूयिष्ठ (f. ष्ठा) and sim. comp.s (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sentimentalism
SENTIMENTALISM, SENTIMENTALITY: रसिकता,<BR> -त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sentinel
SENTINEL, SENTRY: रक्षिन् (f. णी): v. Guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

separability
SEPARABILITY:<BR>(1) विभाज्यता;<BR>(2) वियोजनीयता;<BR>(3) विश्लेष्यता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

separable
SEPARABLE:<BR>(1) विमाज्य (f. ज्या = divisible);<BR>(2) वियोजनीय (f. या);<BR>(3) विश्लेष्य (f. ष्या);<BR>(4) वियोगसह (f. हा); etc.: v. To sepa-<BR>-rate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

separate
SEPARATE (adj.):<BR>(1) भिन्न (f. न्ना), वि-,<BR>having<BR>s ways:<BR>भिन्नपथ (f. था), R. viii. 85.;<BR>(2)<BR>पृथक्कृत (f. ता = S. d: rare), M.n.;<BR>(3) विभक्त<BR>(f. क्ता divided, as a joint family);<BR>(4)<BR>वियुक्त (f. क्ता = disunited): v. Different.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

separate
SEPARATE (v. t.):<BR>(1) पृथक्करोति (कृ, c. 8.),<BR>s. d the rice from the husk:<BR>तुषैस्तण्डुलान् पृथक्चकार,<BR>D. vi.;<BR>(2) वि-योजयति<BR>or<BR>-युंक्ते, विप्र-, विसं-,<BR>(युज्, c. 10. and 7. = to disunite),<BR>you will be<BR>s. d from your darling:<BR>वियोक्ष्यसे वल्लभया, N. i.<BR>38.;<BR>(4) विश्लेषयति (c. of श्लिष्, = 2);<BR>(4)<BR>विच्छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7. = to sever);<BR>(5) अन्त-<BR>रयति (nomi. = to keep apart): v. Also to<BR>distinguish, divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

separate
SEPARATE (v. i.):<BR>(1) पृथग्भवति;<BR>(2) विभज्यते (as<BR>a joint family);<BR>(3) विश्लिष्यति (श्लिष्, c. 4.<BR>= be disunited): v. Also above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

separately
SEPARATELY:<BR>(1) पृथक्, Si. ii. 10.;<BR>(2) भिन्नम्,<BR> वि-;<BR>(3) संकीर्णम् (?) M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

separation
SEPARATION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) पृथक्करणम्;<BR>(2) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">Page629</a>]<BR>वियोजनम्;<BR>(3) विश्लेषणम्।<BR>II Disconnection:<BR>(1) वियोगः,<BR>s. from lightning:<BR>विद्युता विप्रयोगः,<BR>Me. ii. 1.;<BR>time of s.:<BR>वियोगकालः, D. iii.;<BR>(2) विश्लेषः, alarmed<BR>at s.:<BR>विश्लेषकातर (f. रा),<BR>Si.;<BR>(3) विरहः,<BR>state of s.:<BR>विरहावस्था,<BR>Me.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

separator
SEPARATOR:<BR>(1) पृथक्कारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) वियो-<BR>जक (f. जिका); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sepoy
SEPOY: सैनिकः: v. Soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

september
SEPTEMBER: उत्तरभाद्रपूर्वाश्विनसंवादी युरोपीयवर्षस्य<BR> नवमो मासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

septenary
SEPTENARY:<BR>I Subs.: सप्तकम्।<BR>II Adj.: by<BR>comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

septennial
SEPTENNIAL:<BR>(1) सप्तवार्षिक (f. की);<BR>(2) सप्तवर्षीण<BR>(f. णा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

septuagenarian
SEPTUAGENARIAN:<BR>(1) सप्ततिक (f. का);<BR>(2)<BR>सप्ततिवर्ष (f. र्षा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sepulchral
SEPULCHRAL:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) समाधीय<BR>(f. या : (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sepulchre
SEPULCHRE:<BR>(1) समाधिः;<BR>(2) प्रेतावासः and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sepulture
SEPULTURE: निधानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sequel
SEQUEL:<BR>I A succeeding part: परिशिष्टम्।<BR>Ph.:<BR>in the s.:<BR>उपरिष्टात्।<BR>II Consequence:<BR>q. v.: परिणामः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sequence
SEQUENCE: v. Sequel, succession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sequester
SEQUESTER: वियोजयति (युज्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>separate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seraglio
SERAGLIO: अवरोधः,<BR>guard of the s.:<BR>अवरोधरक्षिन्<BR>(m.): v. Harem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serene
SERENE:<BR>(1) प्रसन्न (f. न्ना): v. Clear;<BR>(2)<BR>शान्त (f. न्ता): v. Calm. quiet;<BR>(3) विमल<BR>(f. ला): v. Pure, clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serenely
SERENELY:<BR>(1) प्रसन्नम्: v. Clearly;<BR>(2) शान्तम्:<BR>v. Calmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serenity
SERENITY:<BR>(1) प्रसन्नता;<BR>(2) शान्तिः: q. v.:<BR>Clearness, calmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serf
SERF: दासः: v. Slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serfdom
SERFDOM: दास्यम्: v. Slavery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sergeant
SERGEANT: *संरक्षकः, अधिरक्षकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seriatim
SERIATIM:<BR>(1) यथाक्रमम्;<BR>(2) आनुपूर्व्येण;<BR>(3) अनु-<BR>पूर्वशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

series
SERIES:<BR>I Continuous line:<BR>(1) ततिः;<BR>(2)<BR>माला;<BR>(3) राजिः।<BR>II In math:<BR>(1) चयः,<BR>Li.<BR>III Regular succession: क्रमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serious
SERIOUS:<BR>I Grave: q. v.: गम्भीर (f. रा).<BR>II<BR>Weighty, important: q. v.: गुरु (f. also<BR>र्वी).<BR>III In earnest: expr. by न परिहसति<BR>(हस्, c. 1. = not jest)<BR>or<BR>सत्यं ब्रवीति (ब्रू, c. 2.<BR>= to speak truth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seriously
SERIOUSLY:<BR>I Gravely: q. v.: गम्भीरम्।<BR>II<BR>In earnest:<BR>(1) perh. गम्भीरम्;<BR>(2) सत्यम्: v.<BR>Truly;<BR>(3) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seriousness
SERIOUSNESS:<BR>I Gravity: q. v.: गम्भीरता।<BR>II<BR>Importance: q. v.: गुरुता।<BR>III Earnestness:<BR>(1) गम्भीरता;<BR>(2) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sermon
SERMON: वक्तृता (= speech); धर्मविषयिणी वक्तृता (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serous
SEROUS: perh. जलीय (f. या)<BR>or<BR>द्रव- in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serpent
SERPENT:<BR>(1) सर्पः;<BR>(2) भुजङ्गः, -मः<BR>or<BR>भुजगः;<BR>(3) अहिः;<BR>(4) पन्नगः;<BR>(5) उरगः;<BR>(6) नागः;<BR>(7) फणिन् (m.);<BR>(8) आशीविषः;<BR>(9) दर्वीकरः;<BR>(10) दन्दशूकः: v. Snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serpentine
SERPENTINE:<BR>(1) by comp.,<BR>s. course:<BR>भुजङ्ग-<BR>प्रयातम्, P.;<BR>(2) सार्प (f. र्पी: rare) and sim.<BR>deriv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serrate
SERRATE, -D:<BR>(1) करपत्रनिभ (f. भा (?);<BR>(2) क्रक-<BR>चाभ (f. भा: (?); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serried
SERRIED (adj.):<BR>(1) संहत (f. ता);<BR>(2) संश्लिष्ट<BR>(f. ष्टा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serum
SERUM: no equiv.: पयस् (n.)<BR>or<BR>जलम्, may be<BR>used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

servant
SERVANT:<BR>(1) भृत्यः,<BR>engages a s. without fixing<BR>his wages:<BR>वेतनपरिच्छेदमकृत्वैव भृत्यं कारयति,<BR>Mit.; you (are our) master, we (are)<BR>s. s:<BR>वयं<BR> भृत्या भवान् स्वामी, M.p.;<BR>(2) भृतः, -कः (rare),<BR>if a s. does not do his work after receiving pay:<BR>गृहीतवेतनः कर्म न करोति यथा भृतः, Vri.; s. s are of<BR>three kinds — superior, inferior (menial), and<BR>mean (agricultural): भृतकस्त्रिविधो ज्ञेयः उत्तमाधम-<BR>मध्यमः, N. s.;<BR>a s. paid in money:<BR>अर्थभृतः;<BR>in<BR>kind:<BR>भोगभृतः, N. s.;<BR>(3) सेवकः, with her s.:<BR>स्वसेवकेन सह, H. iv.;<BR>(4) दासः: v. Slave;<BR>(5) चेटः (= page);<BR>(6) किङ्करः (= domestic<BR>s.),<BR>by many disguised s. s:<BR>अनेकच्छन्नकिङ्करैः,<BR>D. viii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serve
SERVE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: सेवते, उप-, सं-, (सेव्, c. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">Page630</a>]<BR>1.),<BR>to s. a big lord:<BR>परमेश्वरं सेवते, H. ii. 28.;<BR>in s.ing a master:<BR>स्वामिसेवायाम्, H. ii.;<BR>s. for<BR>salvation:<BR>संसेवन्ते विमुक्त्यै, Ki. xviii. 24.<BR>II<BR>To wait on, attend: q. v.: सेवते, नि-, उप-,<BR> आ-, परि-।<BR>III As in table, to s. out, to s. up:<BR>पर्यवेषयति (c. of विष्),<BR>s. d Brāhmaṇas:<BR>ब्राह्मणान्<BR> पर्यवेषयन्, Ram,<BR>IV To do good to, bene-<BR>-fit: q. v.: उपकरोति (कृ, c. 8.).<BR>V To be<BR>sufficient: q. v.: पर्याप्त (f. प्ता).<BR>VI To<BR>use, manage: q. v.: प्रयुंक्ते (युज्, c. 7.).<BR>VII To treat: q. v.<BR>VIII In law, to<BR>deliver or execute: निर्वाहयति (c. of वह्: (?):<BR>v. To summon, arrest. To s. out (i. e. to<BR>retaliate: q. v.): प्रतिशोधं ददाति (दा, c. 3.:<BR>with gen. of the object).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

service
SERVICE:<BR>I Lit.: सेवा, seeking money by s.:<BR>सेवया धनमिच्छद्भिः, H. ii. 20.; not acquainted<BR>with s. (how to serve): सेवानभिज्ञः, H;<BR>by s.,<BR>by agriculture:<BR>नृपसेवया कृषिकर्मणा, P.;<BR>I have<BR>done fruitless s.:<BR>सेवा कृता निष्फला, J. Ph.:<BR>I am quite at your s.:<BR>यथेच्छं नियुज्यतामयं<BR> जनः।<BR>II Work: कर्मन् (n.,)<BR>pay is the<BR>price for s.:<BR>वेतनं कर्ममूल्यम्, Mit.; military s.:<BR>सैनिककर्मन्ं (n.);<BR>to be in s.:<BR>कर्म करोति;<BR>out of<BR>s.:<BR>निष्कर्मन् (mfn.).<BR>III Help:<BR>(1) उपकारः<BR>(= benefit),<BR>to render s. to friends:<BR>सुहृदामुपकार-<BR>कारणात्, H. ii. 35.;<BR>(2) साहाय्यम् (= assistance).<BR>IV Use: q. v.: उपयोगः।<BR>V Religious: सेवा,<BR>divine s.:<BR>ईश्वरसेवा (after हरिसंकीर्तनम् of the<BR>Vaiṣṇavas).<BR>VI Of vessels:<BR>silver s.:<BR>रजत-<BR>भाजनानि (n. pl.).<BR>VII In law: perh. निर्वाहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serviceable
SERVICEABLE:<BR>I Useful, beneficial: q. v.:<BR>उपयोगिन् (f. नी)<BR>II Fit for duty:<BR>(1) कार्य-<BR>क्षम (f. मा);<BR>(2) कर्मकुशल (f. ला), and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serviceableness
SERVICEABLENESS:<BR>(1) उपयोगिता: v. Useful-<BR>-ness;<BR>(2) कार्यक्षमता: v. Activity, skill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serviceably
SERVICEABLY: उपयुक्तम्: v. Usefully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

servile
SERVILE:<BR>(1) by comp.,<BR>s. state:<BR>दास-<BR>or<BR>दासी-<BR>मावः, Mah.;<BR>(2) by adv. दासवत्: v. Also<BR>abject, mean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

servilely
SERVILELY: दासवत्: v. Also meanly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

servility
SERVILITY, SERVILENESS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) दास्यम्;<BR>(2) दासता, -त्वम् (also दासीता, -त्वम् of females).<BR>II Slavish deference:<BR>(1) expr. with<BR>दासवत्;<BR>(2) चरणावपातः and sim. comp. s.: v.<BR>Also meanness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

serving
SERVING (adj.):<BR>s. -man:<BR>चेटः;<BR>s. -maid:<BR>चेटी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

servitor
SERVITOR:<BR>I Lit.: सेवकः: v. Servant, atten-<BR>-dant.<BR>II At Oxford: परिचारकः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

servitude
SERVITUDE: दास्यम्: v. Servility (I), service<BR>(I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sesame
SESAME, SESAMUM: तिलः (= both the plant<BR>and its seed),<BR>s. oil:<BR>तिलतैलम्, Bha.; fit for<BR>s. (as ground): तिल्य (f. ल्या), A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sesquipedalian
SESQUIPEDALIAN: of words: perh. बाहुदीर्घ<BR>(f. र्घा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

session
SESSION: उपवेशः, -नम्। Ph.: to hold criminal s. s:<BR>*दण्डशासनं करोति;<BR>s. s. judge:<BR>*दण्डाधिकरणिकः;<BR>s. s (the period): *शासनकालः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sesterce
SESTERCE: मुद्राविशेषः; दीनारपादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set
SET (adj.):<BR>I Fixed, intent: q. v.: दृढ (f.<BR>ढा).<BR>II Regular, uniform: q. v.: विन्यस्त<BR>(f. स्ता).<BR>III Prescribed: विहित (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set
SET (subs.):<BR>I S. ing: अस्तमयः -नम्, R. ix. 9.: v.<BR>To set (v. i.).<BR>II A number of things: जातम्।<BR>III Of persons: जातिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set
SET (v. t.):<BR>I To put: q. v.: स्थापयति (c. of<BR>स्था).<BR>II To lay:<BR>(1) निदधाति<BR>or<BR>धत्ते (धा,<BR>c. 3.),<BR>s. s an arrow on his bow:<BR>निजधनुर्यन्त्रे<BR> निधत्ते शरम्, B. r. iv. 25.;<BR>(2) करोति, in special<BR>phrases, s.ting (his)<BR>feet on our necks:<BR>कृत्वा<BR> पदं नो गले, Mu. iii. 26.<BR>III Of stones:<BR>(1)<BR>नि-दधाति<BR>or<BR>-धत्ते, प्रणि-,<BR>if gem is s. on lead:<BR>यदि<BR> मणिस्त्रपुणि प्रणिधीयते, H. ii.; (प्रतिबध्यते, P.);<BR>(2) खचति (खच्, c. 1. = to inlay), C. ;<BR>(3)<BR>सन्निवेशयति (c. of विश्);<BR>(4) योजयति (युज्, c.<BR>10.: lit = join).<BR>IV To plant: q. v.: रोप-<BR>यति (c. of रुह्).<BR>V To direct;<BR>(1) निर्दिशति<BR>(दिश्, c. 6.);<BR>(2) often by causal.<BR>VI<BR>To regulate, adjust: perh. समीकरोति।<BR>VII<BR>Of limbs: समं सन्दधाति<BR>or<BR>-धत्ते, C. s.;<BR>to become<BR>s.:<BR>सन्धानं याति, etc., Bha. Misc.: (a)<BR>to s. a<BR>trap:<BR>पाशं योजयति; (b) to s. in motion:<BR>चालयति: v. To move; (c) to s. sail:<BR>(1)<BR>नावं मुञ्चति, D.;<BR>(2) lit., वातवसनमुत्तोल्य गच्छति; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">Page631</a>]<BR>(d)<BR>to s. teeth on edge:<BR>दन्तहर्षं जनयति; (e)<BR>to<BR>s. right:<BR>समीकरोति (?); (f.) to s. the fire:<BR>अग्निं ददाति (with loc.); (g) to s. free: v. To<BR>free, release; (h)<BR>to s. at nought:<BR>तृणाय मन्यते<BR>(मन्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set
SET (v. i.):<BR>I Of heavenly bodies:<BR>(1) अस्तं<BR> गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.), याति (या, c. 2.), व्रजति<BR>(व्रज्, c. 1.),<BR>when the sun was s. ting:<BR>सूर्येऽस्त-<BR>मुपगच्छति;<BR>when the sun had s.:<BR>अस्तमिते सूर्ये,<BR>Mah. vi.;<BR>(2) अस्तगिरिम् आरोहति (रुह्, c. 1.),<BR>प्राप्नोति (आप्, c. 5.), etc. (with ref. to the<BR>fabulous mount);<BR>the sun is s.ting:<BR>गिरिमस्तं<BR> भानुमान् प्रतिपद्यते;<BR>then when the sun had s.:<BR>अस्तं<BR> गिरिमथारूढे भास्करे, Mah. vi.;<BR>(3) पतति (fall),<BR>मज्जति (= sink), etc, (poet), about to s.:<BR>पतिष्यत्, Si. ix. 6.;<BR>with the half-s. sun:<BR>सामि<BR> मज्जति रवौ, Ki. ix. 5.;<BR>(4) अभिनिम्लोचति (म्लुच्,<BR>c. 1.) (rare). Ph.:<BR>s. ting time:<BR>अस्तगमनवेला<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR>II To undertake: q. v.:<BR>व्यवस्यति (अस्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set about
SET ABOUT: आरभते (रभ्, c. 1.): v. To begin,<BR>undertake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set against
SET AGAINST: प्रत्यवस्थापयति (c. of स्था): v. To<BR>oppose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set apart
SET APART: पृथग् रक्षति (रक्ष्, c. 1.): v. Also<BR>to keep by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set aside
SET ASIDE:<BR>(1) अवक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 1. = to cast<BR>aside);<BR>(2) परावर्तयति (c. of वृत्): v. To<BR>revoke, annul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set before
SET BEFORE:<BR>I To exhibit: परिदर्शयति (c.<BR>of दृश्).<BR>II To serve: q. v.: परिवेषयति (c.<BR>of विष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set down
SET DOWN:<BR>I To enter: q. v.: निवेशयति (c,<BR>of विश्).<BR>II To ordain: q. v.: निर्दिशति<BR> दिश्, c. 6.).<BR>III To rebuke: आक्षिपति (क्षिप्,<BR>c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set forth
SET FORTH: विन्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.): v. To<BR>display, describe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set forward
SET FORWARD:<BR>I To set out: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>promote, advance: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set in
SET IN: आगच्छति, उप-, समुप-, (गम्, c. 1.),<BR>the<BR>hot season had s. in:<BR>वसन्तकालः समुपागतः, Ri. i.<BR>1.: v. To come. Ph.: to s. in motion:<BR>संचालयति (c. of चल्): v. To move; s. in<BR>order: v. To arrange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set off
SET OFF:<BR>I To separate: पृथक्करोति।<BR>II<BR>With<BR>against:<BR>तुलयति (तुल्, c. 10.).<BR>III<BR>To embellish, adorn: q. v.: संस्करोति।<BR>IV<BR>To praise: q. v.: प्रशंसति (शंस्, c. 1.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set on
SET ON:<BR>I To excite, instigate: q. v.: प्रव-<BR>र्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR>II To employ:<BR>s. the<BR>heart on:<BR>मनो बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.)<BR>or<BR>अभि-<BR>निवेशयति (c. of विश्) (with loc.). Ph.: (a)<BR>s. on fire:<BR>ज्वलयति (c. of ज्वल्): v. Fire, set<BR>on; (b)<BR>s. on foot:<BR>प्रवर्तयति (c. of वृत्): v.<BR>Also to begin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set out
SET OUT:<BR>(1) प्रतिष्ठते (स्था, c. 1.), Si. iii. 1.:<BR>v. To depart;<BR>(2) चलति (चल्, c. 1.). Ki.<BR>xiv. 27.;<BR>(3) निर्गच्छति (गम्, c. 1. = to go<BR>out);<BR>(4) अभिवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.: with acc.).<BR>D. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set to
SET TO: बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.): v. To bind,<BR>fasten. Ph.:<BR>s. to music:<BR>स्वरबद्धं (द्धां) करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set up
SET UP:<BR>I To erect, raise: q. v.: उत्थापयति<BR>(c. of स्था).<BR>II To begin: q. v.: perh.<BR>उत्यापयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

set upon
SET UPON: v. To set on, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

settee
SETTEE: शयनम्<BR>or<BR>शयनीयम् (?): v. Couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

setter
SETTER:<BR>I Of jewels:<BR>(1) योजयित् (f. त्री);<BR>(2) निधातृ (f. त्री).<BR>II A dog: आखेटिकः<BR> कुक्कुरभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

setting
SETTING (subs.):<BR>I Sinking: अस्तगमनम् etc.:<BR>v. Set (v. i.).<BR>II Of stones:<BR>(1) योजना;<BR>(2) निधानम्;<BR>(3) सन्निवेशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

settle
SETTLE (subs.): आसनम्: v. Seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

settle
SETTLE (v. t.):<BR>I To fix, establish: q. v.:<BR>स्थापयति, सं-, अव- (c. of स्था).<BR>II To deter-<BR>-mine, decide: q. v.: व्यवस्थापयति।<BR>III Of<BR>lands: वासयति, अधि-, (c. of वस्).<BR>IV As an<BR>annuity: ददाति (दा, c. 3. = to give).<BR>V To<BR>adjust, arrange: q. v.<BR>VI As disputes:<BR>(1) निवर्तयति (c. of वृत्);<BR>(2) expr. with<BR>सन्धिं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

settle
SETTLE (v. i.):<BR>I To fall to the bottom: तले<BR> पतति (पत्, c. 1.).<BR>II To become fixed:<BR>(1) स्थिरीभवति;<BR>(2) व्यवतिष्ठते (स्था, c. 1.: rare). [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">Page632</a>]<BR>III To fix one's habitation:<BR>(1) निवासं<BR> स्थिरीकरोति;<BR>(2) संवसति (वस्, c. 1.: rare).<BR>IV To sink, as a building: सीदति, अव-, वि-,<BR>(सद्, c. 1.).<BR>V To come to an agree-<BR>-ment: सन्धिं करोति, Mit.: to s. out of court:<BR>मिथः प्रशमं याति, Mit.<BR>VI To make a join-<BR>-ture: वृत्तिं<BR>or<BR>सौदायिकं ददाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

settlement
SETTLEMENT:<BR>I Establishment: स्थापनम्, सं-,<BR> अव-।<BR>II Of lands:<BR>(1) वासनम्, अधि- (?);<BR>(2) संस्थापनम् (?)<BR>III A colony: उपनिवेशः (?).<BR>IV A dower, jointure: q. v.: सौदायिकम्।<BR>V Adjustment, arrangement: q. v.: सन्धा-<BR>नम्।<BR>VI Of debts etc.: शोधनम्।<BR>VII Drugs:<BR>मलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

settler
SETTLER:<BR>I Lit.: वासिन् (f. नी), अधि-।<BR>II<BR>Fig.: निर्णेतृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seven
SEVEN: सप्तन्,<BR>in s. parts or ways:<BR>सप्तधा;<BR>s. hun-<BR>dred:<BR>सप्तशतं (ती);<BR>s. collectively:<BR>सप्तकम्;<BR>thrice<BR>s. times:<BR>त्रिःसप्तकृत्वः, Vi.;<BR>three of us and s. of<BR>Pāṇḍavas:<BR>त्रयोऽस्माकं पाण्डवानाञ्च सप्त, Mah. i.<BR>1. 220.;<BR>for s. or eight days:<BR>सप्ताष्टदिवसान्,<BR>Mah. v. 160. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sevenfold
SEVENFOLD: सप्तगुण (f. णा)<BR>or<BR>सप्तगुणितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seventh
SEVENTH:<BR>I Adj.: सप्तमः (मी, मं).<BR>II Subs.:<BR>(1) सप्तमः;<BR>(2) सप्तमांशः;<BR>(3) सप्तांशः: v. Part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seventhly
SEVENTHLY:<BR>(1) सप्तमतः;<BR>(2) सप्तमम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seventeen
SEVENTEEN:<BR>(1) सप्तदशन्,<BR>s. th:<BR>सप्तदश (f. शी);<BR>s. times:<BR>सप्तदशवारान्;<BR>hundred and s.:<BR>सप्तदशाधिक-<BR>शतम्, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seventieth
SEVENTIETH: सप्ततितमः (मी, मं). Hundred-and-s.:<BR>सप्तत्यधिकशततमः (मी, मं), Mah.; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

seventy
SEVENTY: सप्ततिः,<BR>s. -nine:<BR>ऊनाशीतिः<BR>or<BR>एकोनाशीतिः<BR>or<BR>नवसप्ततिः;<BR>s. -first:<BR>एकसप्ततितमः (मी, मं) or<BR>(rarely) एकसप्ततः (ती, तं) (after S. k.);<BR>s.-<BR>fold:<BR>सप्ततिगुण (f. णा);<BR>seven hundred and s.-<BR>five slokas:<BR>श्लोकसप्तशती चापि पञ्चसप्ततिसंयुता,<BR>Mah. i. 2. 304.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sever
SEVER (v.): पृथक्करोति: v. To separate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

several
SEVERAL:<BR>I Distinct: q. v.<BR>II Many,<BR>numerous: q. v.: अनेके (-काः, -कानि: pl.).<BR>III Respective: q. v.: स्व (f. स्वा) doubled,<BR>their s. weapons:<BR>स्वं स्वं प्रहरणं तेषाम्, Mah. i.<BR>27. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

severally
SEVERALLY:<BR>I = each: q. v.<BR>II Separately:<BR>पृथक् पृथक्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

severe
SEVERE:<BR>I Of persons:<BR>(1) खर (f. रा), प्र-,<BR>was neither s. nor very mild:<BR>न खरो न च भूयसा<BR> मृदुः, R. viii. 9.;<BR>(2) तोक्ष्ण (f. क्ष्णा), Ka.;<BR>(3) निष्ठुर (f. रा): v. Cruel;<BR>(4) परुष (f. षा)<BR>: v. Rough, harsh.<BR>II Of things etc.<BR>(1)<BR>तीव्र (f. व्रा),<BR>s. affliction:<BR>तीव्रामिषङ्गः, Ku. iii.<BR>73.;<BR>(2) चण्ड (f. ण्डा), प्र-,<BR>s. heat:<BR>प्रचण्डातपः,<BR>Ri. i. 10.;<BR>(3) उग्र (f. ग्रा),<BR>s. penances:<BR>उग्रं<BR> तपस् Vi. iii. 44.;<BR>(4) खर (f. रा), प्र-: v.<BR>Also fierce, unbearable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

severely
SEVERELY:<BR>(1) निष्ठुरम्;<BR>(2) परुषम्;<BR>(3) चण्डम्,<BR> प्र-;<BR>(4) उग्रम्;<BR>(5) खरम्, प्र-;<BR>(6) तीक्ष्णम्: for<BR>dif.: v. Severe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

severity
SEVERITY:<BR>(1) निष्ठुरता<BR>or<BR>नैष्ठुर्यम् (= cruelty);<BR>(2) परुषता<BR>or<BR>पारुष्यम् (= harshness);<BR>(3) प्रखरता<BR>or<BR>प्राखर्यम् (= sharpness);<BR>(4) उग्रता (= 3);<BR>(5) चण्डता, प्र-;<BR>(6) तीव्रता;<BR>(7) तीक्ष्णता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sew
SEW: सीव्यति, नि-, परि-, वि- (सिव्, c. 4.),<BR>s. ed<BR>the cloth with the eye:<BR>चक्षुषा सह तद्वासः स्यूतवान्,<BR>M. n. on Si. xviii. 29.;<BR>s. ing the garments of<BR>infamy:<BR>सीव्यति दुर्यशःपटौ, N. i. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sewer
SEWER: प्रणाली: v. Drain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sex
SEX.:<BR>of the s. es:<BR>स्त्रीपुंसयोः, D. ii.: v. Male,<BR>female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sexagenarian
SEXAGENARIAN:<BR>(1) षष्टिक (f. का);<BR>(2) षष्टि-<BR>वर्ष (f. र्षा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sextant
SEXTANT: per instrument: कोणभापः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sexton
SEXTON: समाधिखनकः and sim. comp.s. (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sexual
SEXUAL: स्त्रीपुंस- in comp., s. characteristics:<BR>स्त्रीपुंस-<BR>or<BR>पुंस्त्रीलक्षणम्, (see V. s. 78. ch.) Ph.:<BR>s. desire:<BR>कामः: v. Passion; s. intercourse:<BR>संसर्गः: v. Intercourse, copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shabbily
SHABBILY: expr. by adj. or comp., s. dressed:<BR>कदर्यवेष (f. षा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shabbiness
SHABBINESS:<BR>(1) कदर्यता;<BR>(2) जघन्यता;<BR>(3)<BR>कुत्सितता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shabby
SHABBY:<BR>(1) कदर्य (f. र्या): v. Mean;<BR>(2) कुत्सित<BR>(f. ता = despicable);<BR>(3) कृपण (f. णा = miserly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shackle
SHACKLE:<BR>I Subs.: निगडः। v Chain<BR>(1)<BR>II Verb: निगडयति (nomi.), D. i.: v. To<BR>bind, enchain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shad
SHAD: मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shade
SHADE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: छाया,<BR>in the cool s. of a<BR>Jambu tree:<BR>जम्बुवृक्षस्य शीतलच्छायायाम्, Va.;<BR>will<BR>enter the s.:<BR>प्रवेक्ष्यति छायाम्, Ve.;<BR>where heat is<BR>put off by the s. of banners:<BR>ध्वजच्छायनिवारितोष्णम्,<BR>R. vii. 4. (note the form छाय for abun-<BR>-dance).<BR>II A shadow: q. v.: छाया।<BR>III<BR>A spirit: q. v.: छाया, the s. s of the flesh-eaters:<BR>पिशिताशनानां छायाः, Sa.<BR>IV Of a picture:<BR>छाया (?).<BR>V A degree: Ph.:<BR>s. s. of differ-<BR>ence:<BR>सूक्ष्मभेदाः।<BR>VI A screen: q. v.: Ph.:<BR>to cast into s.:<BR>तिरस्करोति,: v. To eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shade
SHADE (v.):<BR>I To shelter from heat: आतपम्,<BR> उष्णं निवारयति, (वृ, c. 10.). R, vii. 4. Ph.:<BR>this place is not s. d:<BR>आतपाक्रान्तोऽयमुद्देशः, Mah.<BR>iv.<BR>II To cover: q. v.: छादयति (छद्, c. 10.).<BR>III In painting: *अप्रकाशीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shadow
SHADOW:<BR>I Lit.: छाया, the s. of the earth:<BR>भूमेश्छाया, R.; to assail even the s. of Janaka:<BR>विदेहराजस्य छायामप्यवस्कन्दितुम्, Vi. iii.<BR>II Fig.,<BR>faint resemblance: गन्धः (= scent: q. v.),<BR>s. of a doubt:<BR>सन्देहस्य गन्धोऽपि, after S., Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shadowy
SHADOWY:<BR>I Shady: q. v.<BR>II Unreal, false:<BR>q. v.: छायारूप (f. पा) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shady
SHADY:<BR>(1) by comp.,<BR>s. tree:<BR>छायावृक्षः, R.<BR>x. 5.;<BR>(2) छायाप्रधानः (ना, नं) and sim.<BR>comp.s, M. n.;<BR>(3) आतपरहितः (ता, तं)<BR>and sim. comp. s. (= without heat: of<BR>places).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shaft
SHAFT:<BR>I Of an arrow: काण्ड (mn.),<BR>carry-<BR>ing s. s on the back:<BR>काण्डपृष्ठ (f. ष्ठा), Vi.: v.<BR>Also arrow.<BR>II Handle: दण्डः।<BR>III Of a<BR>column: दण्डः, “स्तम्भदण्डैः”, D. i.<BR>IV Of a<BR>carriage: perh. दण्डः: v. Pole (II.)<BR>V<BR>Of a mine: perh. कूपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shag
SHAG:<BR>I A kind of cloth: no equiv.:<BR>*परुषकम्।<BR>II A bird: मदगुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shagginess
SHAGGINESS:<BR>I Lit.: लो (रो) मशता।<BR>II Rough-<BR>-ness: रुक्षता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shaggy
SHAGGY:<BR>I Lit.: लो (रो) मश (f. शा).<BR>II<BR>Rough: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shah
SHAH: यवनराजः: Monarch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shake
SHAKE (v. i.):<BR>(1) कम्पते, प्र-, (कम्प्, c. 1.), his<BR>lips s. ing:<BR>कम्पाधरः, Ku. xvii. 16.; along with<BR>the trees the Lord of Prāgjyotiṣa shook (with<BR>fear): सह द्रुमैः प्राग्ज्योतिषेश्वरश्चकम्पे, R. iv. 81.;<BR>(2) वेपते (= to tremble: q. v.);<BR>(3) चलति<BR>(= to move: in fig. senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shake
SHAKE (v. t.):<BR>(1) कम्पयति, प्र-, (c. of कम्प्),<BR>s. ing the earth:<BR>प्रकम्पयन् गाम्, Ki. xiv. 29.;<BR>as it cannot be s. n by others:<BR>अप्रकम्प्यतयान्येषाम्,<BR>Ki. xi. 39.;<BR>(2) धूनोति<BR>or<BR>धूनोयति<BR>or<BR>धुवति or<BR>धुनाति<BR>or<BR>धूनीते, वि-, अव- (धू, c. 5., 10., 6., 9.),<BR>he shook his body not once:<BR>अधूनीत तनं स नैकधा,<BR>N. ii. 2.; Arjuna s.ing (his)<BR>bow:<BR>विधुवति<BR> धनुः॥॥॥पाण्डुसूनौ, Ki. xvi. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shake off
SHAKE OFF: निर्-धूनीते<BR>or<BR>धूनयति, अव-, वि-: v.<BR>To dispel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shake
SHAKE (subs.):<BR>(1) कम्पः, with a. s. of the head:<BR>कम्पेन मूर्ध्नः, Ku. vii. 49.;<BR>(2) धूतिः, वि-, अव-<BR>(rare),<BR>the pillar which was s.ing:<BR>स्तम्भमुपहित-<BR>धूतिम्, Si. xv. 6.;<BR>(3) कम्पनम्, धूननम्, etc.<BR>(= s.ing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shaky
SHAKY: अस्थिरः, (= unsteady: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shall
SHALL:<BR>I As a sign of future tense: by<BR>ऌट्<BR>or<BR>लुट् (not of today) (G. § 340-3).<BR>II<BR>In injunctions: by विधिलिङ्,<BR>s. live in woods,<BR>making a shed of leaves:<BR>वने पर्णकुटीं कृत्वा वसेत्,<BR>V. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shallop
SHALLOP: तरीविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shallow
SHALLOW (adj.):<BR>I Not deep: गाधः (f. धा),<BR>making rivers s.:<BR>सरितः कुर्वती गाधाः, R. iv. 24.<BR>II Fig.: गाध (f. धा),<BR>s. learning:<BR>पल्लवग्राहि<BR> पाण्डित्यम्, H.: v. Also small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shallow
SHALLOW (subs.): गाधस्थलम् (?); सैकतम्<BR>(= sand-bank).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shallowness
SHALLOWNESS:<BR>(1) गाधता;<BR>(2) क्षुद्रता: v.<BR>Smallness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sham
SHAM:<BR>I Subs.: व्यपदेशः: v. Pretence,<BR>deceit.<BR>II Adj.: by comp.: v. Affected,<BR>false.<BR>III Verb: अप-दिशति, वि-, (दिश्, c.<BR>6.): v. To pretend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sham-fight
SHAM-FIGHT: perh. मिथ्यायुद्धम्, क्रीडायुद्धम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shamble
SHAMBLE: शू (सू) ना: v. Also butcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shambling
SHAMBLING (adj.):<BR>(1) वक्र (f. क्रा): v.<BR>Crooked;<BR>(2) विरूप (f. पा): v. Awkward; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">Page634</a>]<BR>(3) विषम (f. मा): v. Uneven;<BR>(4) चञ्चल<BR>(f. ला): v. Unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shame
SHAME (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) लज्जा,<BR>like the<BR>feeling of s. in women:<BR>लज्जेव योषितः, Si. ii.<BR>44.;<BR>casting off s.:<BR>विहाय लज्जाम्, K.;<BR>feeling<BR>s.:<BR>सञ्जातलज्जः, K. : v. Ashamed (feel);<BR>(2)<BR>हीः,<BR>having no s.:<BR>निर्ह्रोकः (का, कं), K. ;<BR>(3)<BR>त्रपा,<BR>out of s., even my speech does not come out<BR>in words:<BR>वागेव मे नाभिधे यविषयमवतरति त्रपया,<BR>K.;<BR>(4) व्रीडः, -डा (rare),<BR>no one feels s. in<BR>extolling you:<BR>व्रीडमेति न तव प्रियं वदन्, Si. xiv.<BR>2.<BR>II Disgrace: q. v.: अपमानः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shame
SHAME (interj.): धिक्,<BR>s. on us who bear their<BR>arms for nothing:<BR>विफलशस्त्रभृतो धिगस्मान्, Ve.<BR>iii. 11. (G. § 166).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shame
SHAME (v.):<BR>I To make ashamed:<BR>(1)<BR>लज्जयति (c. of लज्ज्), Vi. v. 11.;<BR>(2) ह्रेपयति<BR>(c. of ह्री), Ki. xiii. 41.;<BR>(3) व्रीडयति (c. of<BR>व्रीड्), Ki. xiii. 47.;<BR>(4) त्रपयति (c. of त्रप्);<BR>(5) लज्जां etc. जनयति (c. of जन्: with gen.),<BR>II To disgrace: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shameful
SHAMEFUL (adj.):<BR>(1) लज्जाकर (f. री);<BR>(2)<BR>ह्रेपण (f. णी), very s., improper for maidens:<BR>अतिह्रेपणमकुलकुमारीजनोचितम्, K. iii.;<BR>(3) व्रीडा-<BR>जनन (f. नी); etc.: v. Also odious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shamefully
SHAMEFULLY: expr. by adj. or comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shameless
SHAMELESS:<BR>(1) निर्लज्ज (f. ज्जा);<BR>(2) निह्रीक<BR>(f. का);<BR>(3) निस्त्रप<BR>or<BR>निरपत्रप (f. पा);<BR>(4)<BR>लज्जाहीन (f. ना);<BR>(5) वीतवीड (f. डा); and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shamelessly
SHAMELESSLY: लज्जां विहाय, उत्सृज्य, निरस्य, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shamelessness
SHAMELESSNESS:<BR>(1) निर्लज्जता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2)<BR>निस्त्रपता;<BR>(3) लज्जाहीनता; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shampoo
SHAMPOO: संवाहयति (c. of वह्),<BR>shall I s. your<BR>feet:<BR>संवाहयामि चरणौ, Sa. iii. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shampooer
SHAMPOOER: संवाहक (f. हिका),<BR>profession of a<BR>s.:<BR>संवाहकस्य वृत्तिः, Mr. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shamrock
SHAMROCK: त्रिपत्रलताविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shank
SHANK<BR>I Of the leg: जङ्घास्थि (n.). Ph.:<BR>having long s. s:<BR>दीर्घजङ्घ (f. ङ्घा): v. Leg.<BR>II Of other things: बन्धः may be<BR>used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shape
SHAPE:<BR>I Subs.: आकारः: v. Form.<BR>II<BR>Verb: आकारं विदधाति (धा, c. 3: with gen.)<BR>or sim. विदधाति: v. To form, make.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shapeless
SHAPELESS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) निराकार (f. रा);<BR>(2) निराकृति (mfn);<BR>(3) अमूर्त (f. र्ता);<BR>(4)<BR>विरूप (f. पा); etc.<BR>II Deformed: q. v.:<BR>विरूप (f. पा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shapelessness
SHAPELESSNESS:<BR>I Lit.: निराकारता।<BR>II<BR>Deformity: वैरूप्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shapely
SHAPELY: सुरूप (f. पा): v. Beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shard
SHARD: खण्डः (mfn.): v. Piece.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

share
SHARE (subs.):<BR>I In gen.: अंशः,<BR>he gets two<BR>s. s, the rest one each:<BR>तस्य द्वावंशौ शेषाणामेकैकः,<BR>Viv.;<BR>they are entitled to a third s.:<BR>ते तृतीयांश-<BR>भागिनः, Viv.; eunuchs and outcastes have no s.:<BR>अनंशौ क्लीवपतितौ, M. ix. 201.; “समो न्यूनोऽधिको<BR> वांशो येन क्षिप्तस्तथैव सः । व्ययं दद्यात् कर्म कुर्याल्लाभं<BR> गृह्नीत चैव हि”, Vri.;<BR>(2) भागः,<BR>apportionment<BR>of s. s:<BR>भागकल्पना, Viv.;<BR>two s. s are to be<BR>given him, the rest s. equally:<BR>तस्य भागद्वयं शेषास्तु<BR> समभागिनः, Viv. Ph.:<BR>to go s. s:<BR>अंशिन् (f. नी)<BR>भवति: v. Sharer.<BR>II Of a plough: फालः:<BR>v. Ploughshare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

share
SHARE (v. i.): i. e. to have a s.: v. Share<BR>(subs. and v. t.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

share
SHARE (v. t.):<BR>I To divide: q. v.: विभजति<BR>(भज्, c. 1.).<BR>II To have a portion of:<BR>अशं<BR>or<BR>भागं हरति (हृ, c. 1.), लभते (लभ्, c. 1.).<BR>etc. (with gen).<BR>III To enjoy with others:<BR>भुंक्ते (भुज्, c. 7.): v. To enjoy. IV. Fig.:<BR>the boon companions s. your pleasures and pains:<BR>समदुःखसुखः सखीजनः, R. viii. 65.;<BR>as if s. ing<BR>their distress:<BR>समदुःखा इव, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

share
SHARE:<BR>(1) अंशिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) भागिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) अंशहरः (रा, रं) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shareholder
SHAREHOLDER: अशंभागिन् (f. नी); अंशग्राहिन्<BR>(f. णी), and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shark
SHARK:<BR>I A kind of fish:<BR>(1) ग्राहः;<BR>(2)<BR>हाङ्गरः (rare).<BR>II A cheat, rogue.: q. v.:<BR>वकवृत्तिः, v. p. iii. 1899.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sharp
SHARP (adj.):<BR>(1) तीक्ष्ण (f. क्ष्णा), s. weapon:<BR>तीक्ष्णमस्त्रम्; s.-pointed: (= तीक्ष्णाग्र) (f. ग्रा),<BR>P. 44.:<BR>s. needle:<BR>तीक्ष्णा सुची, Kāśikā;<BR>in-<BR>tellect s. but not piercing:<BR>तीक्ष्णा नारुन्तुदा बुद्धिः, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">Page635</a>]<BR>Si. ii. 109.;<BR>s. means:<BR>तीक्ष्णोपायः, P. 3. 16.;<BR>euphorbia is purgative and s.:<BR>सेहुण्डो रेचनस्तीक्ष्णः,<BR>Bha.;<BR>very s. shower:<BR>सुतीक्ष्णधारा, Ri. ii. 4.;<BR>s. punishment:<BR>तीक्ष्णो दण्डः, Ka. ii. 37.;<BR>(2)<BR>नि-शि (शा) त (f. ता) (= s. -ended), s. weapon:<BR>निशाता हेतिः, Ki.;<BR>s. intellect:<BR>निशिता बुद्धिः,<BR>M. n.;<BR>(3) खर (f. रा), (not of smell or<BR>taste),<BR>s. -witted:<BR>प्रखरबुद्धिः (mfn.);<BR>(4) तिग्म<BR>(f. ग्मा: rare), Vi. v. 53.;<BR>(5) उग्र (f. ग्रा<BR>= not of mind etc.: in good sense); s. arrow:<BR>उग्रेषुः, Ki. xiv. 58.;<BR>s. -smelling:<BR>उग्रगन्ध (f.<BR>न्धा), Bha.;<BR>(6) तीव्र (f. व्रा = 5),<BR>very s.-<BR>rayed:<BR>तीव्रतरांशुमालिन् (f. नी), Ri. ii. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sharp
SHARP (subs.): in music: perh. उत्तानः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sharp-edged
SHARP-EDGED:<BR>(1) तीक्ष्णधार (f. रा);<BR>(2)<BR>नि-शि(शा)तधार (f. रा);<BR>(3) प्रखरधार (f. रा);<BR>(4) धाराल (f. ला), Ku. xvi. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sharpen
SHARPEN:<BR>(1) उत्-तेजयति (तिज्, c. 10.: lit.<BR>and fig.),<BR>s. ed the flower-bow with rays:<BR>कुसुम-<BR>चापमतेजयदंशुभिः, R. ix. 39.;<BR>(2) शाणयति (nomi.:<BR>as on a whet),<BR>s. ed on a sharp sword:<BR>निशित-<BR>निस्त्रिंशशाणित (f. ता), C. v.;<BR>(3) श्यति, नि-,<BR>(शो, c. 4.: rare),<BR>or<BR>नि-शातयति (c. of शो),<BR>s. ed weapons:<BR>-न्यश्यन्नस्त्राणि, B. xvii. 4.;<BR>(4)<BR>तीक्ष्णीकरोति;<BR>(5) क्ष्णौति, प्र-, (क्ष्णु, c. 2.: very<BR>rare), B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sharper
SHARPER: धूर्तः: v. Cheat, rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sharply
SHARPLY:<BR>(1) तीक्ष्णम्,<BR>roaring very s.:<BR>सुतीक्ष्णं<BR> ध्वनताम्, Si. ii. 10.;<BR>(2) प्रखरम्;<BR>(3) तिग्मम्;<BR>(4) तीव्रम्;<BR>(5) उग्रम्: v. Sharp (adj.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sharpness
SHARPNESS:<BR>(1) तीक्ष्णता,<BR>s. in the points of Kuśa<BR>not in conduct:<BR>तीक्ष्णता कुशाग्रेषु न स्वभावेषु, K.;<BR>(2) तैक्ष्ण्यम्;<BR>(3) प्रखरता<BR>or<BR>प्राखर्यम्;<BR>(4) तिग्मता<BR>or<BR>तैग्म्यम्;<BR>(5) उग्रता;<BR>(6) तीव्रता: v. Sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sharp-set
SHARP-SET:<BR>I Hungry: q. v.: क्षुधावसन्न (f.<BR>न्ना).<BR>II Eager: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sharp-sighted
SHARP-SIGHTED:<BR>(1) तीक्ष्णदृष्टि (mfn.);<BR>(2)<BR>तीक्ष्णदृश् (mfn.); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sharp-sightedly
SHARP-SIGHTEDLY:<BR>(1) तीक्ष्णदृष्ट्या;<BR>(2) तिग्मदृशा,<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shatter
SHATTER (v. t.):<BR>(1) शृणाति, वि-, अव-, परि (शॄ,<BR>c. 9.), the king of mountains s. ed to pieces:<BR>विशीर्यमाणः शैलेन्द्रः, Ram. ii. 71, 17.;<BR>blas-<BR>phemers are naturally s. ed:<BR>देवनिन्दकः स्वयं<BR> विशीर्यते, H. iv. 42.;<BR>(2) खण्डशः;<BR>or<BR>शतखण्डशः<BR> भनक्ति (भञ्ज्, c. 7. = to break to pieces): v.<BR>To rend, burst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shave
SHAVE (v.):<BR>I With a razor:<BR>(1) मुण्डयति<BR>(मुण्ड्, c. 10.) (of the hair of the entire<BR>head),<BR>s. ing the head:<BR>मुण्डं मुण्डयित्वा, Mr.<BR>v.;<BR>the Śakas half-s. n:<BR>अर्धमुण्डान् शकान्, V. p.<BR>iv. 3. 21.;<BR>(2) क्षुरेण कल्पते (कॢप्, c. 1. = to<BR>clip), etc., तदस्याः पञ्चचूडत्वं क्षुरकॢप्तं शिरः कुरु,<BR>K. s. xii. 163.;<BR>(3) वापयति, आ-, परि-, (वप्,<BR>c. 10.: rare);<BR>(4) क्षुरति (क्षुर्, c. 6.) (very<BR>rare).<BR>II To cut off: q. v.: लुनाति (लू, c.<BR>9.).<BR>III To skim along: आघर्षति (घृष्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shaver
SHAVER:<BR>I Lit.: क्षौरिकः: v. Barber.<BR>II<BR>Fig.: लुब्धक: v. Also cheat.<BR>III Col., a<BR>boy: माणवकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shaving
SHAVING (subs.):<BR>I The act.:<BR>(1) मुण्डनम् or<BR>मौण्ड्यम् (of the entire head), मौण्ड्ये प्राणान्तिको<BR> दण्डः, M. viii. 379.;<BR>(2) क्षौरम्,<BR>for s.:<BR>क्षौर-<BR>करणाय, H. ii.;<BR>(3) वापः, -नम् (rare),<BR>s. of the<BR>head:<BR>शिरोवापनम्, Vas.<BR>II A thin slice:<BR>शकलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shawl
SHAWL: probably कम्बलः, D. viii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

she
SHE:<BR>I Pro.: सा: v. He.<BR>II In comp.:<BR>she-wolf:<BR>वृकी;<BR>she-goat:<BR>अजा, she-rhinoceros:<BR>खड्गिधेनुका, K.; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheaf
SHEAF:<BR>(1) मुष्टिः;<BR>(2) ताडः, “मुष्टिमेये तृणादिके”,<BR>H. c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shear
SHEAR:<BR>I Lit.: लुनाति (लू, c. 9.): v. To<BR>cut.<BR>II To rob, deprive: q. v.: हरति (हृ,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>Shorn of:<BR>वीत- in comp.; s. of master:<BR>वीतनाथ (f. था), R. xvi. 9.: v. Devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shearer
SHEARER: लोमच्छेदक (f. दिका), -छिद् (mfn.),<BR>लाव (f. वी), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shears
SHEARS:<BR>(1) खण्डधारा;<BR>(2) कर्तरी (नी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheath
SHEATH:<BR>I Case:<BR>(1) कोषः (शः),<BR>a s. made of<BR>tiger-skin:<BR>वैयाघ्रकोशः;<BR>in a golden s.:<BR>हेममये कोशे,<BR>Mah. iv. 42. 12. 15.;<BR>(2) पिधानम् (= cover-<BR>-ing).<BR>II In botany: शुङ्गा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheathe
SHEATHE (v.):<BR>I To put in a case: कोषे (शे)<BR>निदधाति (धा, c. 3.), निवेशयति (c. of विश्), [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">Page636</a>]<BR>अर्पयति (c. of ऋ), etc., Mah. iv. 42. 13. Ph.:<BR>to s. the sword (fig.): खङ्गं समापयति, (after<BR>परशुं समापयति, Vi. iii.).<BR>II To be busy, thrust<BR>deeply: निदधाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheathing
SHEATHING (subs.): to cover a ship's bottom:<BR>पिधानम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheave
SHEAVE: perh. चक्रम्<BR>or<BR>-कम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shed
SHED (v.):<BR>(1) पातयति (c. of पत् = to let fall),<BR>shall never s. blood:<BR>नास्रमापातयेज्जातु, M. iii. 229.;<BR>(2) मुञ्चति, वि-, परि- (मुच्, c. 6. = to discharge,<BR>let go),<BR>s. tears:<BR>मुमोचाश्रूणि, Ram. ii. 58.<BR>25.;<BR>(3) सृजति (सृज्, c. 6. = 2.), s. tears:<BR>अम्नाक्षरस्रम्, B. iii. 17.;<BR>(4) त्यजति, परि- (त्यज्,<BR>c. 1. = 1.),<BR>to s. feathers:<BR>पिच्छं परित्यजति, P. iii.<BR>6.;<BR>(5) स्रावयति (c. of स्रु, = let flow), what<BR>(blood)<BR>was s.:<BR>यत् प्रसुस्राव, Mah. iv. 63. 50.;<BR>(6) क्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6. = to cast: q. v.: as<BR>lustre).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shed
SHED (subs.): शाला,<BR>cow-s.:<BR>गोशाला<BR>or<BR>गोष्ठम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shedder
SHEDDER:<BR>(1) पातक (f. तिका);<BR>(2) स्रावक<BR>(f. विका);<BR>(3) मोचक (f. चिका): v. To shed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheen
SHEEN:<BR>I Adj.: उज्ज्वल (f. ला): v. Bright.<BR>II Subs.: v. Brilliancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheep
SHEEP:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मेषः: v. Ram.;<BR>(2) अविः,<BR>goats and s.:<BR>अजाविकम्;<BR>(3) उरभ्रः, a flock:<BR>औरभ्रकम् (rare).<BR>II Fig., a silly fellow: गर्दभः,<BR>(= ass).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheep-cot
SHEEP-COT, SHEEP-FOLD: मेषशाला and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheepish
SHEEPISH: perh. अप्रतिभः (भा, भं): v. Diffi-<BR>-dent, stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheepishly
SHEEPISHLY:<BR>(1) मेषवत्;<BR>(2) भेष (pl. षा) इव;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheepishness
SHEEPISHNESS: अप्रतिभता, -त्वम् (?): v. Stupidi-<BR>-ty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheep-skin
SHEEP-SKIN:<BR>(1) मेषचर्मन् (n.) and sim. comp.s;<BR>(2) औरभ्रम्, etc. (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheer
SHEER:<BR>I Adj.: शुद्ध (f. द्धा): v. Pure,<BR>mere.<BR>II Verb: व्यपवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To turn away, depart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheet
SHEET:<BR>I Of cloth:<BR>(1) उत्तरच्छदः, bed s.:<BR>शय्यो- R. v. 65.;<BR>(2) प्रच्छदः।<BR>II Of paper:<BR>*तानः।<BR>III Of metal: पत्रम्,<BR>s.-silver.:<BR>रजत-<BR>पत्रम्।<BR>IV Of water: जलराशिः, and sim.<BR>comp.s.:<BR>V A rope: रज्जुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheet-anchor
SHEET-ANCHOR: *महालङ्गरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheet-lightning
SHEET-LIGHTNING: स्फुरन्ती विद्युत्,: v. Light-<BR>-ning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheldrake
SHELDRAKE: हंसविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shelf
SHELF: no equiv.: *शैल्पम्। S. = sandbank:<BR>सैकतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shell
SHELL (subs.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) कोषः, long-s.<BR>ed (a mollusk) दीर्घकोषिका, A. ;<BR>egg-s.:<BR>अण्ड-<BR>कोषः;<BR>(2) कञ्चुकः (hard s., as of the cocoa-<BR>-nut);<BR>(3) त्वच् (f. = bark, as of the pome-<BR>-granate), N. xxii. 14. Ph.:<BR>conch-s:<BR>शङ्खः,<BR>s.-dealer:<BR>शङ्खकारः<BR>or<BR>शाङ्खिकः;<BR>bivalve-s.:<BR>कम्बु<BR>(mn.);<BR>oyster-s.:<BR>शुक्तिः; bazar-s. (used as a<BR>coin): कपर्दः, -कम्।<BR>II Bomb: q. v.: *आग्नेय-<BR>गुली।<BR>III Fig.: कञ्चुकः,<BR>clad in false s. of<BR>religion:<BR>कपटधर्मकञ्चुकः, D. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shell
SHELL (v.): कोषम्<BR>or<BR>कञ्चुकम्<BR>or<BR>त्वचम् अपनयति<BR>(नी, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>निर्हरति (हृ, c. 1.), उन्मुञ्चति or<BR>मोचयति (मुच्, c. 6. and 10.), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shellfish
SHELLFISH: शङ्खः (= conch), covered with s. es.:<BR>शङ्खजालसमावृतः, Ram.;<BR>s. es and oysters burst-<BR>ing:<BR>प्रस्फुटच्छङ्खशुक्तिः, Vi. vi. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shelter
SHELTER (subs.):<BR>(1) आश्रयः (= refuge: q. v.),<BR>take s. with Chandragupta:<BR>समाश्रीयतां चन्द्रगुप्तः,<BR>Mu. v.;<BR>take s. in the peaks:<BR>शृङ्गाण्याश्रयन्ते, Ku.<BR>i. 5.;<BR>(2) -त्राणम्<BR>or<BR>-त्रम् in comp. (= protec-<BR>-tion: q. v.),<BR>s. for body:<BR>तनुत्रम्, Ki.;<BR>s. from<BR>heat:<BR>आतपत्रम्, Si.;<BR>(3) अवकाशः (= space),<BR>to give s.:<BR>अवकाशं ददाति, R. iv. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shelter
SHELTER (v.):<BR>I To protect, save: q. v.:<BR>त्रायति (त्रै, c. 1.).<BR>II To give s.: आश्रयं ददाति<BR>(दा, c. 3).<BR>III To take s.:<BR>(1) आश्रयं याति<BR>(या, c. 3.), शरणं गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.), etc.<BR>(with gen.);<BR>(2) आश्रयति, -ते, सम्- (श्रि, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shelve
SHELVE (v.): अवसर्पति (सृप्, c. 1.),<BR>s. ing:<BR>अव-<BR>सर्पिन् (f. णी), Mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shelvy
SHELVY:<BR>(1) सैकतमय (f. यी: (?);<BR>(2) गूढगाध-<BR>स्थल (f. ला: (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shepherd
SHEPHERD:<BR>(1) मेषपालः, -कः and sim. comp. s.,<BR>from cow-herds and s. s:<BR>आगोपालाविपालेभ्यः, Mah.<BR>iii. 232. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shepherdess
SHEPHERDESS:<BR>(1) मेषपाली;<BR>(2) मेषपालिका and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sherbet
SHERBET: शर्करोदकम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sherd
SHERD: v. Shard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sheriff
SHERIFF: an officer: *नियामकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sherry
SHERRY: मद्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shew
SHEW (v.): दर्शयति (c. of दृश्): v. To show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shield
SHIELD (subs):<BR>I For defending:<BR>(1) फलक<BR>(mn.), with a s. glittering in the left hand:<BR>वामकरतलस्फुरत्फलकः, C. iii.;<BR>(2) चर्मन् (n.),<BR>carrying sword and s.:<BR>खङ्गचर्मधरः;<BR>without sword<BR>and s.:<BR>व्यसिचर्म-, Mah. vii. 48. 34. 39.;<BR>(3)<BR>खेटकः (rare),<BR>bearing sword and s.:<BR>खङ्गखेटक-<BR>धारिन् (f. णी), Mah. iv. 6. 4.<BR>II Fig.,<BR>defence, refuge: q. v.: शरणम्।<BR>III In<BR>heraldry: *खेटकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shield
SHIELD (v.): रक्षति (रक्ष्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>protect, save.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shieldless
SHIELDLESS: विफलक (f. का) and sim. comp. s.,<BR>: v. Shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shift
SHIFT (v. i.):<BR>I To change, move: q. v.:<BR>व्यावर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.).<BR>II To resort: आश्रयति<BR>(श्रि, c. 1.: with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shift
SHIFT (v. t.):<BR>I To change: q. v.: परिवर्तयति<BR>(c. of वृत्).<BR>II To move about: व्यावर्तयति<BR>: v. Also to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shift
SHIFT (subs.):<BR>I Expedient, means: q. v.:<BR>उपायः।<BR>II Artifice, trick: q. v.: छलम्।<BR>III<BR>An undergarment: युतकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shifty
SHIFTY: छलप्रिय (f. या), and sim. comp. s.<BR>: v. Deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shilling
SHILLING: रौप्यमुद्राविशेषः; अर्धटङ्का (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shin
SHIN: perh. अग्रजङ्घा: v. Leg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shine
SHINE (v.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) प्रकाशते, वि-, (काश्,<BR>c. 1.), s. ing above (other)<BR>animals:<BR>प्रकाशमानं<BR> परिभूय देहिनः, Ki. xiv. 41.;<BR>(2) भाति-, आ-,<BR> वि-, प्र-, सं-, (भा, c. 2.),<BR>as the sun s. s in a<BR>clear morning in early autumn:<BR>अभायत यथार्केण<BR> सुप्रातेन शरन्मुखे, B. viii. 2.;<BR>(3) द्योतते, वि-, प्र-,<BR> अभि, (द्युत् c. 1. = to glitter),<BR>shone like the<BR>ocean in fire:<BR>विदिद्युते शिखाभिराश्लिष्ट इवाम्भसां निधिः,<BR>Si. i. 20.;<BR>(4) दीप्यते, वि-, उत्-, (दीप्, c. 4. =<BR>to gleam),<BR>s. s in heaven as if shaming the<BR>sun:<BR>दीप्यते नाकपृष्ठस्था भर्त्स्य यन्तीव भास्करम्, Mah.<BR>ii. 11. 16.;<BR>(5) भासते, वि-, अव-, उत्-, (भास्,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>Arundhatī shone much:<BR>बभासे बह्वरुन्धती,<BR>Ku. vi. 11.;<BR>(6) रोचते, वि-, (रुच्, c. 1.:<BR>rare), (studded)<BR>with s.ing gems:<BR>रोचिष्णु-<BR>रत्नावलिभिर्विरेजे, Ki. xviii. 18.;<BR>(7) विकसति<BR>(कस्, c. 1.), the rays shone on all sides:<BR>व्यकसदंशुचयः ककुन्मुखेषु, Si. xx. 38.;<BR>(8) राजति,<BR> -ते, वि-, सं-, अभि-, (राज्, c. 1.),<BR>the son of<BR>Raghu alone shone with dignity:<BR>रराज धाम्ना<BR> रधुसूनुरेव, R. vi. 6.;<BR>(9) स्फुरति, वि-, अभि-, (स्फुर्,<BR>c. 6. = to glitter);<BR>(10) भ्राजते, वि-, (भ्राज्,<BR>c. 1.).;<BR>(11) काश(स)ते, वि-, (काश्<BR>or<BR>कास्,<BR>c. 1.);<BR>(12) चकास्ति (चकास्, c. 2.).<BR>II To<BR>be eminent:<BR>(1) राजति, -ते, वि-, सं-;<BR>(2)<BR>विकसति;<BR>(3) काश (स)ते, वि-;<BR>(4) चकास्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shine
SHINE (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रभा;<BR>(2) प्रकाशः;<BR>(3) द्युतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shingle
SHINGLE:<BR>I Gravel: q. v.: शर्करा।<BR>II A<BR>plank: फलकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shiny
SHINY:<BR>(1) सप्रकाश (f. शा) and sim. comp. s.;<BR>(2) उज्ज्वल (f. ला): v. Bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ship
SHIP (subs.):<BR>(1) पोतः,<BR>struck by a succession of<BR>billows, the s. sank in the waters of the sea:<BR>कल्लोलमालाभिहतः पोतः समुद्राम्भस्यमज्जत्, D.;<BR>(2)<BR>यानम्, -पात्रम् (= vessel),<BR>s. -wreck;<BR>यानभङ्गः, Ra.<BR>i.;<BR>embarking on the s.:<BR>यानपात्रं समारुह्य, K. s.<BR>18. 293.;<BR>(3) प्र-वहनम् (= यानम्),<BR>and the s.<BR>went up and down every moment:<BR>ययौ च तत्<BR> प्रवहणं क्षणमूर्ध्वमधः क्षणम्, K. s. 25. 44.;<BR>the s.<BR>wrecked^1:<BR>तद्वहनं समभज्यत, 45.;<BR>(4) वहित्रम् (= 3:<BR>rare), early in the morning, a s. was to be seen:<BR>प्रत्यूषस्यदृश्यत किमपि वहित्रम्, D. vi.;<BR>(5) तरी<BR>(= boat), Si. iii. 76.; समुद्रवाहिनी नौः, -का,<BR>M. n. and sim. comp.s (best equiv.).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ship
SHIP (v. t.):<BR>I To embark: q. v.: पोते<BR> आरोपयति (c. of रुह्): v. To put.<BR>II To fix:<BR>स्थापयति (c. of स्था). Ph.: (a)<BR>s. off:<BR>पोतेन<BR> विवासयति (= banish)<BR>or<BR>प्रस्थापयति (= send<BR>away); (b) s. a sea, prob. तरङ्गैर् अभिभूयते or<BR>तरङ्गान् खादति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ship-master
SHIP-MASTER: पोताध्यक्षः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ship-owner
SHIP-OWNER: प्रवहणस्वामिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shipping
SHIPPING (subs.): पोतावलिः, and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shipwreck
SHIPWRECK (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: यानभङ्गः, पोतभङ्गः,<BR>P. and sim. comp. s.: v. Wreck.<BR>II Ruin,<BR>destruction: q. v.: विध्वंसः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shipwreck
SHIPWRECK (v.):<BR>I Lit.: पोतं भनक्ति (भञ्ज्, c.<BR>9.) etc.<BR>II Of persons:<BR>s. ed:<BR>यानभङ्गनिमग्न<BR>(f. ग्ना = sunk), Ra. i.<BR>or<BR>-पतित (f. ता = fallen),<BR>K. s. or भग्नपोतः (ता, तं) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shipwright
SHIPWRIGHT: prob. पोतकारः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shire
SHIRE: प्रदेशः: v. County.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shirk
SHIRK: परिहरति (हृ, c. 1.): v. To avoid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shirt
SHIRT:<BR>(1) चोलः (ली);<BR>(2) युतकम् (= under<BR>-s.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shiver
SHIVER (v. i.):<BR>I To shake, tremble: q. v.:<BR>वेपते (वेप्, c. 1.).<BR>II To shatter: चूर्णीभवति;<BR> शकलीभवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shiver
SHIVER (v. t.):<BR>(1) चूर्णीकरोति;<BR>(2) विशकलयति<BR>(nomi.): v. Also to shatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shiver
SHIVER (subs.):<BR>I Fragment, bit.: q. v.:<BR>शकल (mn.),<BR>“cracked in hundred s. s”:<BR>शतखण्डी-<BR>भूत (f. ता).<BR>II Tremor:<BR>(1) कम्पः;<BR>(2)<BR>वेपथुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shoal
SHOAL:<BR>I Crowd: q. v.: संधः।<BR>II A sha-<BR>-llow: गाधस्थलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shock
SHOCK (subs.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) अभिघातः (=<BR>blow, collision: lit. and fig.);<BR>(2) अभिषङ्गः<BR>(fig.),<BR>arising from the severe s.:<BR>तीव्राभिषङ्ग-<BR>प्रभव (f. वा), Ku. iii. 73.;<BR>then shot with the<BR>quick s.:<BR>ततोऽभिषङ्गानिलविप्रविद्धा, R. xiv. 54.<BR>III A pile:<BR>(1) राशिः;<BR>(2) चितिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shock
SHOCK (v.):<BR>I To strike: q. v.:<BR>(1) अभिहन्ति<BR>(हन्, c. 2.);<BR>(2) विप्रविध्यति (व्यध्, c. 4. = to<BR>pierce: fig.).<BR>II To heap: q. v.: ताडै<BR> राशीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shocking
SHOCKING (adj.):<BR>(1) बीभत्स (f. त्सा);<BR>(2)<BR>उद्वेगकर (f. री): v. Disgusting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shockingly
SHOCKINGLY:<BR>(1) बीभत्सं जनयत् (f. न्ती);<BR>(2)<BR>उद्वेगं कुर्वत् (f. ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shoe
SHOE (subs.):<BR>(1) पादुका (rarely पादुः),<BR>a pair<BR>of Kusa s. s:<BR>कुशपादुके, Ram. ii. 123. 16.; the<BR>illustrious (Rāma) (first)<BR>putting on and then<BR>taking off the s. s:<BR>सोऽधिरोप्य महातेजाः पादुके व्यप-<BR>रोप्य च, 21.;<BR>(2) उपानह् (f.), a pair of golden<BR>s. s:<BR>तपनीयोपानद्युगलम्, Vi. iv.:<BR>(3) पादत्रम्,<BR>and sim. comp.s (very rare);<BR>(4) नालम् (for<BR>animals (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shoe
SHOE (v.):<BR>I To furnish with s. s: नालं बध्नाति<BR>(बन्ध्, c. 9.) (?).<BR>II To beat with s. s:<BR>पादुकया हन्ति (हन्, c. 2.): v. To beat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shoe-black
SHOE-BLACK: पादुकामार्जकः, and sim. comp.s<BR>(??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shoe-maker
SHOE-MAKER:<BR>(1) चर्मकारः, and well-known s. s:<BR>प्रख्याताश्चर्मकाराः, Ram. ii. 90. 23.;<BR>(2) पादुका-<BR>कारः;<BR>(3) पादूकृत्, A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shoe-strings
SHOE-STRINGS: perh. पादुकाबन्धनी and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shoot
SHOOT (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रबाल (mn.);<BR>(2) किस(श)-<BR>लय (mn.);<BR>(3) पल्लव (mn.), a bed of young s. s:<BR>नवपल्लवसंस्तरः, Ku.;<BR>(4) प्ररोहः (= bud).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shoot
SHOOT (v. t.):<BR>I To discharge: q. v.: मुञ्चति<BR>(मुच्, c. 6.): v. Also to send, throw.<BR>II<BR>To wound or kill by s.ing: आग्नेयास्त्रेण (with<BR>fire-arm)<BR>or<BR>शरेण (with arrow) हन्ति, नि-,<BR> अभि-, (हन्, c. 2.): v. To kill, wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shoot
SHOOT (v. i.):<BR>I To discharge a missile:<BR>आग्नेयास्त्रं<BR>or<BR>शरं etc. मुञ्चति, etc.<BR>II As pain:<BR>विध्यते, प्र-, विप्र- (pass. of व्यध् = to pierce).<BR>S.<BR>ing pain:<BR>शूल (mn.).<BR>III To germinate:<BR>(1) by subs., does not seem about to s. forth:<BR>न च प्ररोहाभिमुखोऽपि दृश्यते, Ku. v. 60.;<BR>(2)<BR>अङ्कुरयति (nomi.): v. Also to come out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shop
SHOP (subs.):<BR>I For selling things:<BR>(1)<BR>पण्यशाला and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(2) विपणिः;<BR>(3)<BR>आपणः,<BR>containing rich s. s:<BR>ऋद्धापण (f. णा), R.<BR>xiv. 30.<BR>II In gen.: शाला,<BR>work, s.:<BR>कर्मशाला;<BR>barber's s.:<BR>नापितशाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shop
SHOP (v.): पणायति, -ते: v. Also to buy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shop-keeper
SHOP-KEEPER:<BR>(1) आपणिकः;<BR>(2) विपणिन् (m.);<BR>(3) पण्याजीवः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shop-lifter
SHOP-LIFTER: perh. पण्यतोलः, पण्यमुष्: v.<BR>Thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shore
SHORE (subs):<BR>I Coast:<BR>(1) कूलम्,<BR>on the s. of<BR>the Yamunā:<BR>उपकूलं कालिन्द्याः, R. xv. 28.;<BR>(2)<BR>तीरम्;<BR>(3) तटम्;<BR>(4) वेला (= sea-s.);<BR>(5) रोधस<BR>(n.: rare), R. viii. 33.<BR>II A prop:<BR>(1)<BR>उपघ्रः;<BR>(2) अवष्टम्भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shore
SHORE (v.): usually with<BR>up:<BR>अवष्टभ्नाति<BR>(स्तम्भ्, c. 9.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

short
SHORT:<BR>I In size:<BR>(1) हस्व (f. स्वा):<BR>very s.<BR>and having a s. face:<BR>खर्वटास्योऽतिह्रस्वकः, V.<BR>p. 1. 13. 34;<BR>s. tree:<BR>ह्नस्वो वृक्षः;<BR>s. hovel:<BR>ह्नस्वा<BR> कुटी, Kāśikā:;<BR>(2) खर्व (f. र्वा),<BR>having a s.<BR>stature:<BR>खर्वाकृति (mfn.);<BR>like a s. man:<BR>खर्व<BR> इव, Mu.;<BR>(3) वामन (f. नी): v. Dwarfish.<BR>II Of time etc.: q. v.: अल्प (f. ल्पा), सु-,:<BR>v. Little. Ph.:<BR>in a s. time:<BR>अचिरेण: v. Soon;<BR>for a s. time:<BR>कञ्चित् कालम्, कियत्कालम्, etc.;<BR>and the nights are very s.:<BR>अत्यर्थमेव क्षणदा<BR> च तन्वी (कृशा, M. n.), R. xvi. 45.;<BR>to<BR>become s.:<BR>तनुतां याति, R. ix. 38.<BR>III<BR>Brief: q. v.: संक्षिप्त (f. प्ता). Ph.:<BR>in s.:<BR>किं<BR> बहुना, समासेन।<BR>IV Insufficient: q. v.: न्यून<BR>(f. ना). Ph.:<BR>to fall s. off:<BR>हीयते, परि- (Pass.<BR>of हा with inst.: v. To want).<BR>V = less<BR>than:<BR>nothing s. of his death^1:<BR>विना तस्य मरणेन;:<BR>v. Without, except.<BR>VI In gram.:<BR>(1)<BR>ह्नस्व (f. स्वा: of vowels);<BR>(2) लघु (f. also घ्वी:<BR>of quantities). Ph.: (a)<BR>s. cut:<BR>सरलः पन्थाः;<BR>(b)<BR>to cut s.;<BR>आक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.), K.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shortcoming
SHORTCOMING: दोषः: v. Fault, failing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shorthand
SHORTHAND: i. e. s. writing: *संक्षिप्तलिपिः।<BR>S.<BR>writer:<BR>*संक्षिप्तलिपिकरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

short-lived
SHORT-LIVED: क्षणविध्वंसिन् (f. नी): v. Fickle,<BR>transient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

short-sighted
SHORT-SIGHTED:<BR>(1) अदूरदर्शिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>perh. ह्नस्वदृष्टि (mfn.), see Bha.; and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

short-sightedness
SHORT-SIGHTEDNESS:<BR>(1) अदूरदर्शिता;<BR>(2) ह्रस्व-<BR>दृष्टिः -ता (?); and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

short-winded
SHORT-WINDED: क्षीणश्वास (f. सा); and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shorten
SHORTEN (v. t.)<BR>I In size:<BR>(1) ह्नसयति (c. of<BR>ह्नस्);<BR>(2) ह्रस्वीकरोति;<BR>(3) खर्वीकरोति;<BR>(4)<BR>वामनीकरोति।<BR>II To abridge, contract: q. v.<BR>संक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.),<BR>how the long nights<BR>will be s. ed into moments:<BR>संक्षिप्यते क्षण इव कथं<BR> दीर्घयामा त्रियामा, Me. ii. 47.<BR>III To diminish,<BR>decrease: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shorten
SHORTEN (v. i.):<BR>I In size: ह्नस्वीभवति, etc.<BR>II As nights:<BR>(1) तनुतां याति, गच्छति, etc.;<BR>(2) क्षीयते (pass. of क्षि), M. n.: v. To<BR>diminish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shortly
SHORTLY:<BR>I Soon, quickly: q. v.: अचिरेण।<BR>II Briefly:<BR>(1) संक्षेपतः;<BR>(2) संक्षेपेण;<BR>(3)<BR>समासतः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shortness
SHORTNESS:<BR>(1) ह्नस्वता;<BR>(2) खर्वता;<BR>(3) स्वल्पता;<BR>(4) न्यूनता;<BR>(5) संक्षिप्तता;<BR>(6) तनुता;<BR>(7)<BR>कृशता: for dif.: v. Short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shot
SHOT (subs.):<BR>I Shooting: मोचनम्: v. Dis-<BR>-charge.<BR>II For killing birds, etc. गुलिका<BR>(?). Ph.:<BR>to fire s. s:<BR>*आग्नेयास्त्रं मुञ्चति।<BR>III<BR>Any missile: q. v.<BR>IV Its reach: q. v.:<BR>विषयः।<BR>V A marksman: good, bad s.:<BR>लक्ष्यभेदे कृतहस्त (f. स्ता), अकृतहस्त (f. स्ता).<BR>VI<BR>Share: q. v.: अंशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

should
SHOULD:<BR>I Denoting obligation: by the<BR>कृत्य (G. § 366-9.): (you) s. look at (her)<BR>as<BR>a pupil:<BR>शिष्येव द्रष्टव्या, K.<BR>II. In the condi-<BR>-tional: by विधिलिङ् (§ 347: s. have will be<BR>expressed by ऌङ्, § 345),<BR>even if I s. give up<BR>what I have stolen all my life:<BR>यद्यपि दद्यामाजन्मनो<BR> मुषितं धनम्, D. ii.<BR>III As a softened form of<BR>expression: by लट्<BR>in the Atmanepada, if<BR>possible, I s. think:<BR>मन्ये, Sa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shoulder
SHOULDER (subs.):<BR>(1) स्कन्धः,<BR>bull -s. ed:<BR>वृष-<BR>स्कन्ध (f. न्धा), R. i. 12.;<BR>putting sacrificial<BR>vessels on their s. s:<BR>स्कन्धारोपितयज्ञपात्रनिचयाः,<BR>Vi. iv. 58.;<BR>(2) अंसः (rare),<BR>a quiver on the<BR>s. s;<BR>तूणीरोऽंसे, Vi. ii. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shoulder
SHOULDER (v.):<BR>I To put on the s.: स्कन्धे<BR> करोति: v. To put.<BR>II To push with the<BR>s. s: स्कन्धेन मृद्राति, अव- (मृद्, c. 9.) etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shoulder-bone
SHOULDER-BONE: अंसकपालम्, Bha. and sim<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shoulder-knot
SHOULDER-KNOT: स्कन्धाभरणम्, and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shoulder-joint
SHOULDER-JOINT:<BR>(1) स्कन्धसन्धिः;<BR>(2) चिरु<BR>(n.), Wilson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shout
SHOUT (subs.):<BR>(1) जयध्वनिः, जयरवः, and sim.<BR>comp.s (of joy): v. Noise;<BR>(2) कलकलः:<BR>v. Uproar;<BR>(3) चीत्कारः: v. Scream, roar;<BR>(4) सिंहनादः (of triumph),<BR>raised a s.:<BR>ननाद<BR> सिंहनादम्, Mah. vii. 180. 2.;<BR>(5) क्ष्वेडितम्, -नादः [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">Page640</a>]<BR>(= 4), Ki. xiv. 29.;<BR>(6) महाशब्द;, and sim.<BR>comp.s (= great noise),<BR>high s. s suddenly<BR>rose:<BR>सुमहास्वनः सहसैवोत्थितः, Mah. i. 133. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shout
SHOUT (v.):<BR>(1) expr. by subs. and मुञ्चति<BR>(मुच्, c. 6. = to emit: q. v.)<BR>or<BR>करोति (= to<BR>make);<BR>(2) उत्क्रोशति (क्रुश्, c. 1.),<BR>the<BR>Brāhmins s. ed:<BR>उदक्रोशन् विप्रमुख्याः, Mah. i. 186.<BR>2.: v. To cry, roar;<BR>(2) उच्चैर् नदति (नद्,<BR>c. 1.): v. (To make) noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shove
SHOVE:<BR>I Verb: अपसारयति (c. of सृ): v<BR>To push.<BR>II Subs.: आवेधः: v. Thrust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shovel
SHOVEL (subs.) खन्ता, Nil. on Mah. iv. 8. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shovel
SHOVEL (v.): अव-क्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.): v. To<BR>throw, heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

show
SHOW (v.):<BR>(1) दर्शयति, प्र-, नि-, अभि-, परि-, सं-,<BR> उप- (c. of दृश्),<BR>s. ed him to Indumatī:<BR>निदर्शया-<BR>मास (तम्) इन्दुमत्यै, R. vi. 31.;<BR>s. ing affection<BR>by the mere shedding of useless tears:<BR>निष्फलेन<BR> अश्रुपातमात्रेण स्नेहमुपदर्शयन्, K.; O, merciless fate,<BR>s. mercy (on me): अयि दैव निर्घृण दर्शय दयाम्, K. ;<BR>s. ing (his)<BR>teeth:<BR>दन्तानि दर्शयन्, V. p. v. 28.<BR>16.; the Veda also s. s the unity of science:<BR>दर्शयति वेदोऽपि विद्यैकत्वम्, Si. iii. 3. 4.;<BR>he<BR>always s. s as if his dependents were beloved<BR>friends:<BR>सखीनिव प्रीतियुजोऽनुजीविनः स सन्ततं दर्शयते,<BR>Ki. i. 10.;<BR>(2) उपदिशति (दिश्, c. 6. = to<BR>advise, inform: q. v.),<BR>who will s. the way<BR>to the Golden town:<BR>यः सुवर्णपुरगामिनं पन्थान-<BR>मुपदेक्ष्यति, K. ;<BR>(3) कथयति (= to speak: q. v.),<BR>it shews the excellences of the king that.....:<BR>अनेन कथिता राज्ञो गुणा यत्॥॥, R. x. 53.;<BR>(4)<BR>दर्शनं ददाति (दा, c. 3. = s. one's self),<BR>ashamed<BR>of wantonness, shame itself did not s. to the<BR>prince:<BR>कुमारस्य न ददाति तरलतालज्जिता लज्जैव<BR> दर्शनम्, K. ii.;<BR>(5) प्रतिपादयति (= to estab-<BR>-lish: q. v.). Comp. (a)<BR>s. forth:<BR>दर्शयति:<BR>v. To reveal, manifest; (b)<BR>s. off:<BR>प्रदर्शयति,<BR> सं-; (c)<BR>s. up:<BR>अभि-दर्शयति: v. To expose,<BR>disclose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

show
SHOW (subs.):<BR>I Look: q. v.:<BR>(1) दर्शनम्;<BR>(2) by verb.<BR>II Appearance, semblance:<BR>(1) आभासः;<BR>(2) by verb: भाति, प्रति- (भा,<BR>c. 2.)<BR>or<BR>भासते, अव-, (भास्, c. 1.).<BR>III A<BR>spectacle:<BR>(1) दृश्यम्;<BR>(2) रङ्गः (for amuse-<BR>-ment);<BR>(3) यात्रा (= procession, theatrical s.).<BR>IV Pretence: q. v.: व्यपदेशः।<BR>V Display,<BR>pomp: आडम्बरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shower
SHOWER (subs.):<BR>I Of rain: वृष्टिः,<BR>heavy s.<BR>of hail:<BR>तुमुलकरकावृष्टिः, Me. i. 55.: v. Rain.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) वृष्टिः<BR>or<BR>वर्षः, sent a s. of stones:<BR>अश्मनां वृष्टिं ससर्ज, Ki. xvii. 60.; s. of arrows:<BR>इषुवर्षः, Si. xx. 18.;<BR>(2) धारा (= flow, as of<BR>tears):<BR>(3) जालम् (= thicket, as of arrows).<BR>III One who shows: दर्शकः, प्र-, etc., Mr.<BR>iv. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shower
SHOWER (v.): वर्षति, प्र-, अभि- (वृष्, c. 1.),<BR>s. s.<BR>on them who always flatter:<BR>तत्र वर्षन्ति योऽहर्निशं<BR> स्तैति, K. ; s.ing much wealth on the bards:<BR>वसूनि वर्षन् सुबहूनि वन्दिनाम्, N. xv. 1. (the loc.<BR>is the proper cons.): v. Also to rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shower-bath
SHOWER-BATH:<BR>I The place: धारागृहम् or<BR>यन्त्र- (?), R. xvi. 49.<BR>II The act: धारास्नानम्<BR>and sim. comp. s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

showery
SHOWERY: वर्षुक (f. का); v. Rainy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

showman
SHOWMAN:<BR>(1) दर्शयितृ (f. त्री), प्र-;<BR>(2) by<BR>verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

showy
SHOWY: दृष्टिहारिन् (f. णी): v. Also gaudy,<BR>ostentatious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shred
SHRED:<BR>I Subs.: खण्ड (mn.): v. Piece.<BR>II<BR>Verb:<BR>(1) खण्डीकरोति;<BR>(2) खण्डयति (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrew
SHREW (subs.):<BR>I Of persons: वामशीला स्त्री<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR>II S. -mouse:<BR>(1)<BR>छुछुन्दरी;<BR>(2) गन्धमूष (f. षी);<BR>(4) चिचक्षण (f.<BR>णा): v. Artful, cunning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrewdly
SHREWDLY:<BR>(1) चतुरम्;<BR>(2) विदग्धम्;<BR>(3)<BR>चातुर्येण, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrewdness
SHREWDNESS:<BR>(1) चातुर्यम्;<BR>(2) चतुरता;<BR>(3) चातुरी;<BR>(4) वैदग्ध्यम्;<BR>(5) विदग्धता: v. Also skill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrewish
SHREWISH: कर्कश (f. शा): v. Harsh, peevish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shriek
SHRIEK:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) क्रन्दितम्: v. Cry;<BR>(2) चीत्कारः: v. Scream.<BR>II Verb:<BR>(1)<BR>आ-क्रन्दति (क्रन्द्, c. 1.): v. To cry;<BR>(2)<BR>चीत्करोति: v. To scream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrift
SHRIFT: प्रतिपत्तिः: v. Confession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrike
SHRIKE: a bird:<BR>(1) कलिङ्गः;<BR>(2) पिङ्गः;<BR>(3)<BR>घूम्या (म्रा)टः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrill
SHRILL:<BR>(1) कर्कश (f. शा): v. Harsh;<BR>(2)<BR>तीव्र (f. व्रा): v. Sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrillness
SHRILLNESS:<BR>(1) कर्कशता: v. Harshness;<BR>(2)<BR>तीव्रता: v. Sharpness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrilly
SHRILLY:<BR>(1) कर्कशम्: v. Harshly;<BR>(2) तीव्रम्<BR>: v. Sharply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrimp
SHRIMP: इञ्छाकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrine
SHRINE: देवालयः: v. Temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrink
SHRINK (v. i.): संकुचति (कुच्, c. 6.),<BR>the lotus<BR>s. s:<BR>संकुचति पद्मम्, V. d. 7.: v. To contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrink
SHRINK (v. t.): संकोचति (कुच्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrink
SHRINK, -ING (subs.): संकोचः: v. Contrac-<BR>-tion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrinkingly
SHRINKINGLY:<BR>(1) संकुच्य;<BR>(2) ससंकोचम्: v.<BR>Also timidly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrivel
SHRIVEL:<BR>(1) संकुचति (intrans.)<BR>or<BR>संकोचति<BR>(trans.);<BR>(2) by adj.: वलिपरीत (f. ता), and<BR>sim. comp. s.: v. Wrinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shroud
SHROUD (v.): अवगुण्ठयति (गुण्ठ्, c. 10.): v.<BR>To cover, veil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shroud
SHROUD (subs.):<BR>I Cover: q. v.: आच्छादनम्,<BR>s. ed the dead body of Bāli:<BR>वाससाच्छादयामास<BR> वालिनं नष्टजीवितम्, Ram. iv. 24. 23.<BR>II रज्ज्वः<BR>(f. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrub
SHRUB:<BR>I A tree: गुल्मः।<BR>II A drink: आसव-<BR>भेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrubbery
SHRUBBERY: perh. गुल्मवाटिका after वृक्षवाटिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrubby
SHRUBBY:<BR>(1) गुल्मावृत (f. ता);<BR>(2) गुल्माकीर्ण<BR>(f. र्णा); and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shrug
SHRUG:<BR>I Verb:<BR>(1) धूनोति (धू, c. 5. = to<BR>shake);<BR>(2) संकोचति (कुच्, c. 1.: (?).<BR>II<BR>Subs.:<BR>(1) स्कन्धधूननम् (= shaking);<BR>(2)<BR>स्कन्धसंकोचः (= contraction).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shuck
SHUCK: कञ्चुकः: v. Shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shudder
SHUDDER:<BR>I Verb: वेपते, प्र-, (वेप्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To tremble, quake.<BR>II Subs.: वेपथुः: v.<BR>Tremor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shudderingly
SHUDDERINGLY: expr. by adj.: सञ्जातवेपथु,<BR> सवेपथु (mfn.), and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shuffle
SHUFFLE (v. t.):<BR>I Of cards: perh. भञ्जयति<BR>(c. of भञ्ज्: comp. भांँजा).<BR>II To confuse,<BR>mix up: q. v.: सङ्कुलीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shuffle
SHUFFLE (v. i.):<BR>I Of cards: *तासं भञ्जयति।<BR>II To dissemble: q. v.: निह्नुते (ह्नु, c. 2.).<BR>II To play tricks: छलयति (nomi with<BR>acc.),<BR>s. ing:<BR>छलप्रिय (f. या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shuffle
SHUFFLE, -ING (subs.):<BR>I Of cards: *तास-<BR>मञ्जनम्।<BR>II Confusion.: q. v.: संकुलीकरणम्।<BR>III Evasion, trick: q. v.: छलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shuffler
SHUFFLER:<BR>(1) निह्नोतृ (f. त्री): v. Dissemb-<BR>-ler;<BR>(2) वञ्चक (f. ञ्चिका): v. Cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shun
SHUN:<BR>(1) परिहरति (हृ, c. 1.): v. To avoid;<BR>(2) वर्जयति, परि-, सं-, (वृज्, c. 10.),<BR>shall s.<BR>joking with women:<BR>स्त्रीभिः परिहासं वर्जयेत्, Sr.<BR>: v. To leave;<BR>(3) न उपसर्पति (सृप्, c. 1.).<BR>etc. (= not to approach), “विनीतं पातकिनमिव<BR> नोपसर्पति,” K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shut
SHUT:<BR>(1) अपिदधाति<BR>or<BR>-धत्ते (धा, c. 3.), (by<BR>covering)<BR>who can s. the doors of fate:<BR>को नाम<BR> द्वाराणि दैवस्य पिधातुमीष्टे, U. vii. 4.;<BR>s. -ting the<BR>ears:<BR>कर्णौ पिधाय, Mu. i.;<BR>(2) आ-वृणोति, सं-, समा-,<BR> परा- (वृ, c. 5. = पिदधाति),<BR>here is a house with<BR>the back door not s.:<BR>एतदपरावृतपक्षद्वारकं गेहम्, Mr.<BR>ii.;<BR>to s. the mouth:<BR>मुखं संवृणोति, K.;<BR>(3)<BR>ददाति<BR>or<BR>दत्ते (दा, c. 3.: only of doors by<BR>putting bolts etc.),<BR>s. the gates quick:<BR>दत्त<BR> द्वाराणि तूर्णम्, Vi. vi. 16.;<BR>(4) मीलति<BR>or<BR>मीलयति,<BR> नि- (मील्, c. 1. and its c.: of the eyes),<BR>the<BR>lion of kings s. his eyes never to open again:<BR>अपुनरुन्मीलनाय निमिमील लोचने राजकुलसिंहः, C. v.;<BR>(5) सं-वनते (वन्, c. 1.: rare), Ki. xviii. 2.<BR>Ph.:<BR>to s. one's eyes to anything:<BR>न पश्यति,<BR>K.;<BR>with the eyes s.:<BR>मुकुलितनेत्र (f. त्रा), Si.<BR>xi. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shut in
SHUT IN:<BR>I To confine: q. v.: निरुणद्धि (रुध,<BR>c. 7.).<BR>II To cover the view of: समावृणोति<BR>(वृ, c. 5.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shut out
SHUT OUT: निवारयति (वृ, c. 10.): v. To<BR>prevent, enclose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shut out
SHUT OUT:<BR>I In gen.: नि-रुणद्धि, सं-, अव-,<BR>thus s. in a cage:<BR>तथा पञ्जरे संरुद्धः, K. ii.: v.<BR>To confine, block up, close.<BR>II To<BR>terminate: निवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.).<BR>III To<BR>cause to be silent: prob.: मुखं बघ्नाति (बन्ध्,<BR>c. 9.: with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shutter
SHUTTER: in pl., of windows etc.: *आवरणम्<BR>or<BR>आवृतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shuttle
SHUTTLE:<BR>(1) त्र (त) सरः;<BR>(2) सूत्रवेष्टः, -नम्;<BR>(3)<BR>मल्लिकः;<BR>(4) वेमन्, Mah. i. 13. 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shuttle-cock
SHUTTLE-COCK: *पत्रगोलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shy
SHY:<BR>I Adj.:<BR>(1) लज्जालु (mfn.): v. Bash-<BR>-ful;<BR>(2) शालीन (f. ना): v. Modest;<BR>(3)<BR>कातर (f. रा): v. Timid.<BR>II Verb:<BR>(1)<BR>बिभेति (भी, c. 3.), if (a horse)<BR>s. ies strike it on<BR>the neck:<BR>ग्रीवायां भीतमाहन्यात्, M. n. on Si. v. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shyness
SHYNESS:<BR>(1) लज्जालुता;<BR>(2) शालीनता;<BR>(3)<BR>कातर्यम्: v. Shy (adj.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sib
SIB: सनाभि (mfn.): v. Relative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sibilant
SIBILANT:<BR>I Of letters: उष्मः, -वर्णः।<BR>II<BR>Hissing: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sibyl
SIBYL:<BR>(1) सिद्धा;<BR>(2) सिद्धस्त्री;<BR>(3) योगिनी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sick
SICK:<BR>I Inclined to vomit:<BR>(1) विवमिषु<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(2) छर्द्यात (f. र्ता); and sim. comp. s.<BR>To be s.:<BR>वमति (वम्, c. 1.): v. To vomit;<BR>to make (one)<BR>s.:<BR>वामयति (c. of वम्), Sr.<BR>II<BR>To be disgusted at: expr. with विरक्त<BR>(f. क्ता), वितृष्ण (f. ष्णा), वीतस्पृह (f. हा); and<BR>sim. comp. s.,<BR>being s. of the world:<BR>उदीर्णवैराग्य<BR>(f. ग्या), D. ii.<BR>III Diseased, ill: q. v.:<BR>(1) पीडित (f. ता);<BR>(2) व्याधित (f. ता);<BR>(3)<BR>रुजार्त (f. र्ता);<BR>(4) रोगिन् (f. णी); and sim.<BR>deriv. s.<BR>IV Of mind:<BR>(1) पीडित (f. ता);<BR>(2) व्यथित (f. ता);<BR>(3) उपतप्त (f. प्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sick-bed
SICK-BED: रोगिशय्या and sim. comp. s. Ph.: on<BR>or from s.: better expr. by शय्यागत (f. ता)<BR>with a qualifying word: v. Sick (II.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sicken
SICKEN:<BR>I To disgust: विरक्तिं<BR>or<BR>वैतृष्णं जनयति<BR>(c. of जन्).<BR>II To fall sick: रोगेण or<BR>व्याधिना अभिभूयते (pass. of भू), क्लिश्यते (pass.<BR>of क्लिश्), etc.: v. Also sick.<BR>III To<BR>languish: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sickle
SICKLE:<BR>(1) दात्रम्;<BR>(2) लवित्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sickliness
SICKLINESS:<BR>(1) रुग्नता;<BR>(2) रोगाकुलता, etc.: v.<BR>Sickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sickly
SICKLY:<BR>I Unwell, weak: q. v.: रुग्न (f. ग्ना).<BR>II Of places etc.<BR>(1) रोगाकुल (f. ला), K. b.;<BR>(2) गदोपसृष्ट (f. ष्टा), and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sickness
SICKNESS:<BR>I Nausea:<BR>(1) विवमिषा (the<BR>feeling);<BR>(2) वमनम् (= vomiting);<BR>(3) छर्दिः<BR>(= 2.)<BR>II Illness:<BR>(1) पीडितता;<BR>(2) असुस्थता;<BR>(3) रोगिता: v. Also disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

side
SIDE (subs.):<BR>I Of the body:<BR>(1) पाश्व<BR>(mn.),<BR>to sleep on the left s.:<BR>वामपार्श्वे संविशति,<BR>Sr.;<BR>pain in the s. s:<BR>पार्श्व शूलम्, Bha.;<BR>sleeping<BR>on the s. s:<BR>पार्श्वशयः (यी, यं), S. k.;<BR>(2) पक्षः<BR>(rare), R. v. 72.<BR>II Of anything: पार्श्व<BR>(mn.), in front, on the rear, and on the s. s.:<BR>अग्रे पृष्ठे च पार्श्वयोः, A. r. vi. 1. 30.; rises from<BR>(this)<BR>s. of the Meru:<BR>मेरोः पार्श्वात् प्रभवति, Mat.<BR>120. 67.;<BR>keep them at the s.:<BR>तं पार्श्वे कुर्वन्ति,<BR>K. ; one who remains at the s. (attendant):<BR>पार्श्ववर्तिन् (f. नी); R. ii. 46.; s. by s.<BR>(= abreast): पार्श्वापार्श्वि (adv.); two s. s of<BR>an equation: द्वौ पक्षौ, Vij.<BR>III Party.: पक्षः,<BR>the kings on the s. of Śiśupāla:<BR>शिशुपालपक्षपृथिवी-<BR>भृतां गणः, Si. xv. 47.;<BR>opposite s.:<BR>प्रतिपक्षः,<BR>D. s. Ph.: the gods were on the s. of Arjuna:<BR>देवा अर्जुनतोऽभवन्, S. k.; पाण्डवतोऽभवन्, Mah.<BR>viii. 87. 51.<BR>IV Of consanguinity: पक्षः,<BR>on the father's, mother's s.:<BR>पितृपक्षे, मातृपक्षे, Mah.<BR>v. 140. 10.: v. Of an argument: पक्षः,<BR>the<BR>first s.:<BR>पूर्वपक्षः, S.<BR>VI Of rivers: पारः,<BR>take me<BR>on the raft to the other s. of the Jamunā:<BR>प्रापयस्व परं पारं कालिन्द्या उडुपेन माम्।<BR>VII<BR>Quarter: q. v.:<BR>(1) दिश् (f.);<BR>(2) gen.<BR>expr. with तस्, on both s. s of the road:<BR>उमयतः पथि, Mah. v. 83. 60.;<BR>on one s...on<BR>the other s.:<BR>एकतः॥।अन्यतः, R. vi. 86.;<BR>on<BR>all s. s:<BR>सर्वतः, R.;<BR>on the left s.:<BR>वामतः, D.<BR>VIII In geo.: भुजः (rarely बाहु<BR>or<BR>दोस्),<BR>four-s. d:<BR>चतुर्भुजः (जा, जं), Li.;<BR>s. s of a right-<BR>angled triangle containing the r. a:<BR>भुजकोटी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

side
SIDE (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: by comp., s. -wind:<BR>पक्षवातः, Mah.: v. Side (subs.).<BR>II In-<BR>-direct: वक्र (f. क्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

side
SIDE (v.): पक्षे भवति (भू, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>पक्षं गृह्णाति<BR>(ग्रह्, c. 9.) (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sideboard
SIDEBOARD: no equiv.; *फलकसज्जा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sidelong
SIDELONG:<BR>I Adj.: वक्र (f. क्रा): v. Oblique.<BR>II Adv.:<BR>(1) पार्श्वतः (= on the side);<BR>(2)<BR>अनुपार्श्वम् (= laterally).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sidereal
SIDEREAL: तारा- -in comp.,<BR>s. year:<BR>*तारावर्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sideways
SIDEWAYS, SIDEWISE:<BR>(1) तिर्यक;<BR>(2) तिरश्ची-<BR>नम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sidle
SIDLE: तिर्यग् गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.), वि-सर्पति (सृप्,<BR>c. 1.), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

siege
SIEGE: रोधः, अव-, नि-,<BR>to raise a s.:<BR>रोधं मुञ्चति or<BR>sim. व्यपायाति (या, c. 2. = to go away), Mah.<BR>iii. 19-26. Ph.:<BR>to lay a s. to:<BR>रुणद्धि (रुध्, c.<BR>7.), Mah. iii. 15. 3.: v. To besiege.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

siesta
SIESTA: दिवास्वप्नः and sim. comp. s: v. Sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sieve
SIEVE:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) चालनी;<BR>(2) तितौ<BR>(rarely n.).<BR>II Verb.: v. To sift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sift
SIFT (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) शोधयति, वि-, परि- (c.<BR>of शुध् = to clean),<BR>whose chaff and awn had<BR>been s. ed by the winnowing basket:<BR>शूपशोधित-<BR>कर्णांकशारुकादीन्, D. vi.;<BR>(2) पृथक् करोति (= to<BR>separate), s. ed the rice from the husk:<BR>तुषैस्तण्डुलान् पृथक् चकार, D. vi.<BR>II To examine<BR>minutely:<BR>(1) सूक्ष्मं निरूपयति (रूप्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) निपुणं परीक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sigh
SIGH:<BR>I Subs.: दीर्घनिश्वासः।<BR>II Verb:<BR>(1)<BR>दीर्घं निश्वसिति (श्वस्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) दीर्घनिश्वासं<BR> मुञ्चति, नि-, (मुच्, c. 6.),<BR>or<BR>त्यजति, परि-, (त्यज्,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>or<BR>सृजति, नि-, (सृज्, c. 6.): v. Also<BR>to lament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sight
SIGHT (subs.):<BR>I The act.:<BR>(1) दृष्टिः;<BR>(2)<BR>दर्शनम्;<BR>(3) वि-लोकनम्, अव-, आ-;<BR>(4) ईक्षणम्, प्र-,<BR> अव-।<BR>II View: दृष्टिपथः, -मार्गः, -विषयः, -गोचरः,<BR>and sim. comp.s,<BR>falling within s.:<BR>आलोक-<BR>पथावतारिन् (f. णी), Vi. ii. 45.<BR>III Appea-<BR>-rance, spectacle: q. v.: दर्शनम्,<BR>as by their<BR>gay s.:<BR>दर्शनेन लघुना यथा तयोः, R. xi. 12.<BR>IV<BR>Eye: q. v.:<BR>(1) दृष्टिः, diseases affecting s.:<BR>दृष्टिगतरोगाः, Sr.;<BR>(2)<BR>sense of s.:<BR>दर्शनेन्द्रियम्;<BR>(3) दृश् (f.: rare), N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sight
SIGHT (v.):<BR>(1) विलोकयति: v. To see.;<BR>(2)<BR>by subs, and comp.: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sightly
SIGHTLY:<BR>(1) सुदर्शन (f. ना);<BR>(2) सुदृश्य (f.<BR>श्या);<BR>(3) दर्शनीय (f. या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sign
SIGN (subs.):<BR>I Mark, indication:<BR>(1) चिह्नम्<BR>(best equiv.),<BR>by these s. s, her recognition of<BR>Nala:<BR>चिह्नैरमीभिर्नलसंविदस्याः, N. xiv. 22.;<BR>with<BR>edicts under his s. manual:<BR>स्वहस्तकृतचिह्नशासनः,<BR>Si. xiv. 36.;<BR>(2) लक्षणम्;<BR>by these s. s, you will<BR>find out:<BR>एभिर्लक्षणैर्लक्षयेथाः, Me. ii. 19.;<BR>(3)<BR>लिङ्गम्, (are)<BR>the general s. s of the disease insa-<BR>nity:<BR>सामान्यमुन्मादगदस्य लिङ्गम्, Bha.;<BR>(4) अभि-<BR>ज्ञानम् (for knowing, recognizing), M. n.<BR>II A portent, presage: q. v.:<BR>(1) चिह्नम्;<BR>(2) लक्षणम्।<BR>III In math. etc.: चिह्नम्।<BR>IV<BR>Signal:<BR>(1) संज्ञा,<BR>Chitralekhā makes a s. to<BR>Vidūṣaka:<BR>चित्रलेखा विदूषकं संज्ञां लम्भयति, V. iii.;<BR>(2) इङ्गितम्;<BR>one who understands s. s:<BR>इङ्गितज्ञ<BR>(f. ज्ञा), K. V. In ast.: राशिः, the s. of Leo:<BR>सिंहराशिः,<BR>when the sun was in the s. Aries:<BR>मेषं<BR> गते पूषणि, C. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sign
SIGN (v.):<BR>I To beckon: संज्ञां ददाति (दा, c.<BR>3.), etc.<BR>II To put one's signature to:<BR>नाम लिखति, अभि- (लिख्, c. 6.)<BR>or<BR>निवेशयति (c.<BR>of विश् = to enter) (with loc.), Y. ii. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

signpost
SIGNPOST: *संज्ञादण्डः; मार्गयष्टिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

signal
SIGNAL:<BR>I Subs.: संज्ञा: v. Sign (IV.)<BR>II<BR>Verb: संज्ञां ददाति (दा, c. 3.), लम्भयति (c. of<BR>लभ्), etc.<BR>III Adj.: असाधारण (f. णी): v.<BR>Uncommon, remarkable, great.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

signalize
SIGNALIZE: कीर्तयति (कीर्त्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>celebrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

signally
SIGNALLY: बलवत्: v. greatly, exceedingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

signature
SIGNATURE: expr. by verb,<BR>a debtor should put<BR>a s. with his own hand:<BR>ऋणी नाम स्वहस्तेन निवे-<BR>शयेत्, V. ii. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

signet
SIGNET: मुद्रा: v. Seal.<BR>S. ring:<BR>मुद्राविशिष्टमङ्गुरी-<BR> (ली)यम्, -कम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

significance
SIGNIFICANCE:<BR>I Meaning: q. v.: भावः।<BR>II<BR>Importance, force: q. v.: गौरवम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

significant
SIGNIFICANT:<BR>I Lit.: भावसूचक (f. चिका),<BR>व्यञ्जक (f. ञ्जिका), and sim. comp. s.<BR>II Im-<BR>-portant, great: q. v.: गुरु (f. also र्वी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

significantly
SIGNIFICANTLY:<BR>(1) साकूतम्;<BR>(2) ईरिताकूतम्,<BR>Ki., and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

signification
SIGNIFICATION: अर्थः: v. Sense IV).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

signify
SIGNIFY:<BR>I To mean: q. v.: expr. with अर्थः,<BR>it s. ies nothing:<BR>निरर्थकमेतत्।<BR>II To betoken,<BR>indicate: q. v.: सूचयति (सूच्, c. 10.).<BR>III<BR>To declare, inform: q. v.: कथयति (कथ्, c.<BR>10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

signior
SIGNIOR: आर्यः: v. Sir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silence
SILENCE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मौनम्,<BR>better to<BR>keep s.:<BR>वरं मौनं कार्यम्, H.;<BR>determining to<BR>break his s.:<BR>तन्मौनभङ्गं चिकीर्षुः, Vet.;<BR>one who<BR>leaves off s.:<BR>मुक्तमौनः, K. s. 77. 42.;<BR>one whose<BR>vow is to keep s.:<BR>मौनव्रती, M. n.<BR>or<BR>वाचंयमः, R.<BR>xiii. 44.;<BR>(2) निःशब्दता and sim. comp. s<BR>(= stillness);<BR>(3) शान्तिः, प्र- (= calmness).<BR>Ph.:<BR>in the s. of midnight:<BR>सुप्तजनस्तिमिते निशीथे,<BR>C. iii.<BR>II Secrecy: q. v.<BR>III Oblivion: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silence
SILENCE (exclam.):<BR>(1) तूष्णीम्भव;<BR>(2) मौनं<BR> कुरु, -ष्व;<BR>(3) शान्तम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silence
SILENCE (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मौनं लम्भयति (c. of<BR>(लभ्;<BR>(2) मूकीकरोति, etc.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1)<BR>निरुत्तरीकरोति (= to shut up);<BR>(2) प्र-शमयति;<BR>(c. of शम् = to quiet);<BR>(3) निवारयति (वृ, c.<BR>10. = to prevent).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silent
SILENT:<BR>(1) मौनिन् (f. नी),<BR>with s. steps:<BR>चरणेन<BR> मौनिना, N. i. 124.; in some points you are s.:<BR>कियत्सु मौनं (तव), N. ix. 15.;<BR>(2) expr. with<BR>तूष्णीम् (rarely तूष्णीकः, -का, -कम्),<BR>why are you<BR>s.:<BR>किं भवान् तूष्णीमास्ते, V. ii.;<BR>seeing the bard<BR>become s.:<BR>तूष्णीम्भूतं सूतपुत्रं निशम्य, Mah. iii.<BR>134. 21.;<BR>(3) मूक (f. का: poet),<BR>with the<BR>birds s.:<BR>मूकाण्डजम्, Ku. iii. 42.;<BR>when the lute<BR>became s.:<BR>मूकीभूतवीणा, K.;<BR>(4) निःशब्द (f.<BR>ब्दा), नीरव (f. वा), and sim. comp. s. (= with-<BR>-out any sound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silent
SILENT, BECOME:<BR>(1) मौनं भजते (भज्, c. 1.)<BR>etc.;<BR>(2) उपशाम्यति (शम्, c. 4.);<BR>(3) विरमति<BR>(रम्, c. 1.): v. To cease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silently
SILENTLY:<BR>(1) मौनेन (rare), K. s.;<BR>(2) तूष्णीम्;<BR>(3) जोषम्, Si. xvi. 16.;<BR>(4) निःशब्दम्: v.<BR>Also secretly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silk
SILK:<BR>(1) क्षौमम्;<BR>(2) कौशेयम्;<BR>(3) पट्टः, -जम्,<BR>Mah. ii. 52. 26.;<BR>(4) चीनम् (China-s.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silk
SILK, -EN (adj.): कौशेय (f. यी),<BR>of s. and<BR>woollen clothes:<BR>कौशेयाविकयोः, M. v. 120.;<BR>(2) कीटज (f. जा);<BR>(3) क्षौम (f. मा), s. cloth:<BR>दुकूलम्,<BR>very fine pure s. cloth:<BR>निःश्वासहार्ये शुचिनी<BR> दुकूले, K.: v. Also s. (subs.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silk-cotton tree
SILK-COTTON TREE: शाल्मलिः, -ली, -वृक्षः। Its<BR>gum: पिच्छा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silk-worm
SILK-WORM:<BR>(1) कोश (ष) कारः;<BR>(2) perh. पट्टकीट्ः;<BR>(3) पुण्डरीकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silky
SILKY:<BR>I Silken: q. v.:<BR>II Like silk:<BR>क्षौमाभ (f. भा), and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sill
SILL:<BR>I In gen: मूलम्।<BR>II Of a door: देहली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silliness
SILLINESS: सूर्खता: v. Foolishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silly
SILLY: मूर्ख (f. र्खा): v. Foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silt up
SILT UP: perh. अवरुणद्धि (रुध्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silvan
SILVAN: by comp.,<BR>s. scene:<BR>वनभूमिः; s. diety:<BR>वनदेवता, U.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silver
SILVER (subs.):<BR>(1) रूप्यम्;<BR>(2) रजतम्;<BR>(3)<BR>दुर्वर्णम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silver
SILVER (adj.):<BR>(1) by comp.,<BR>s. coin:<BR>रूप्यमुद्रा;<BR>(2) रूप्यमय: (यी, यं); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silver
SILVER (v.): रूप्येण छादयति (छद्, c. 10. = to<BR>cover: q. v. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silver-leaf
SILVER-LEAF:<BR>(1) रू (रौ) प्यपत्रम्;<BR>(2) रजतपत्र,<BR> “एवं रजतपत्राणां विशुद्धिः सम्प्रजायते”, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silver-mine
SILVER-MINE:<BR>(1) रजतखनिः;<BR>(2) रूप्यमयी भूमिः,<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silversmith
SILVERSMITH:<BR>(1) रूप्यकारः (?);<BR>(2) स्वर्णकारः<BR>(= goldsmith, who is also s. in India).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

silvery
SILVERY:<BR>(1) मुक्तागौर (f. री = pearl-white), Si.<BR>iv. 44.;<BR>(2) सुधासवर्ण (f. र्णा = nectar-coloured),<BR>Si. iv. 28.; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

similar
SIMILAR: सदृशः (शी, शं): v. Like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

similarity
SIMILARITY: सादृश्यम्: v. Resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

similarly
SIMILARLY:<BR>(1) तद्वत्;<BR>(2) तथैव;<BR>(3) एवम्<BR>(= so).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

simile
SIMILE: उपमा,<BR>s. s of Kālidāsa:<BR>“उपमा कालिदासस्य”।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

similitude
SIMILITUDE:<BR>(1) औपम्यम्: v. Simile, resem-<BR>-blance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

simmer
SIMMER: v. To boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

simper
SIMPER: विकृतं स्मयते (स्मि, c. 1.): v. To<BR>laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

simple
SIMPLE (adj.):<BR>(1) सरल (f. ला), very s. bolts:<BR>सरलतराण्यर्गलानि, Vi. vi. 16.;<BR>your very s. good<BR>nature:<BR>अतितरला तवेयं मधुरा सुजनता, K. ; offend-<BR>ing the s. (girl): सरलामपराध्य, J.; s. (commen-<BR>tary): सरला, S. k.;<BR>(2) ऋजु (f. also ज्वी),<BR>with s. arrows:<BR>ऋजुभिर्बाणैः, Si. xx. 77.;<BR>with<BR>a s. bow:<BR>ऋजुप्रणामक्रियया, R. vi. 25.; s. nature:<BR>ऋजून् स्वभावान्, B. ii. 15.; with the s. eye: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">Page645</a>]<BR>ऋजुनैव चक्षुषा, Ku. v. 32.: v. Also frank,<BR>guileless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

simple
SIMPLE (subs.): ओषधिः (धी);<BR>s. s:<BR>ओषधयः, Si.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

simpleton
SIMPLETON: मूढ (f. ढा): v. Fool, -lish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

simplicity
SIMPLICITY:<BR>(1) सरलता;<BR>(2) ऋजुता;<BR>(3)<BR>आर्जवम्: v. Also plainness, frankness, guile-<BR>-lessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

simplification
SIMPLIFICATION:<BR>(1) सरलीकरणम्;<BR>(2) ऋजूकरणम्;<BR>(3) विशदीकरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

simplify
SIMPLIFY: perh.<BR>(1) सरलीकरोति;<BR>(2) ऋजूकरोति;<BR>(3) विशदीकरोति (= to clear: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

simply
SIMPLY:<BR>I Merely, only: q. v.: केवलम्: v.<BR>Also mere.<BR>II In other senses: perh. by<BR>adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

simulate
SIMULATE: व्यपदिशति (दिश्, c. 6.): v. To<BR>pretend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

simulation
SIMULATION: व्यपदेशः: v. Pretence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

simultaneous
SIMULTANEOUS:<BR>(1) समकालीन (f. ना);<BR>(2)<BR>एककालीन (f. ना);<BR>(3) by adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

simultaneously
SIMULTANEOUSLY:<BR>(1) युगपत्;<BR>(2) समम्, R. iv.<BR>4.;<BR>(3) समकालम् and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sin
SIN (subs.):<BR>(1) पापम्,<BR>becomes purified of all<BR>s. s:<BR>सर्वपापेभ्यः पूतो भवति, V. s.;<BR>(2) पातकम्,<BR>attacked by the (passions), (men)<BR>s. about deadly<BR>s. s, great s. s, minor s. s, and venial s. s:<BR>तेनाय-<BR>माक्रान्तोऽतिपातकमहापातकानुपातकोपपातकेषु प्रवर्तते,<BR>V. s.;<BR>(3) पाप्मन् (m.), is absolved of all s. s:<BR>तरति सर्वं पाप्मानम्, Ga.;<BR>(4) एनस् (n.),<BR>he who<BR>commits a s. at night by action, in mind,<BR>or by words:<BR>कर्मणा मनसा वाचा यदेनः कुरुते<BR> निशि, At.;<BR>(5) अघम्, s. -absolving (formula):<BR>अघमर्षणम्, Vi.;<BR>(6) वृजिनम्;<BR>(7) अंहस् (अंधस्)<BR>(n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sin
SIN (v.): पापं करोति, etc.: v. Sin (subs.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

since
SINCE (prep.):<BR>(1) प्रभृति (with abl.), s. seeing<BR>(you): दर्शनात् प्रभृति, K.;<BR>s. then:<BR>तदा प्रभृति,<BR>Ku. v. 55.;<BR>ever s. he came to sight:<BR>यतः<BR> प्रभृति स मम दर्शनपथं गतः, ततः प्रभृति, Sa. iii.;<BR>(2) आ (with abl. or in comp. = from),<BR>s.<BR>her birth:<BR>आ जन्मनः, Sa. v. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

since
SINCE (adv.):<BR>I = s. then: तदा प्रभृति।<BR>II<BR>= ago:<BR>fifteen years s.:<BR>इतः पूर्वं पञ्चदशवर्षे;<BR>long s. expr. with: चिरम्: v. Long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

since
SINCE (conj.):<BR>(1) यस्मात्, यतः<BR>or<BR>यत् (= as),<BR>Ki. xi. 14.;<BR>(2) कुतः<BR>or<BR>कस्मात् (with abl.<BR>clause): v. Because;<BR>(3) हि: v. For.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sincere
SINCERE:<BR>(1) अकृत्रिम (f. भा = unaffected: q. v.);<BR>(2) यथार्थ (f. र्था = true, real: q. v.);<BR>(3)<BR>सरल (f. = simple, frank: q. v.);<BR>(4) विशुद्ध<BR>(f. द्धा = pure: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sincerely
SINCERELY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.: v.<BR>Also guilelessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sincerity
SINCERITY:<BR>(1) अकृत्रिमता (= unaffectedness);<BR>(2) विशुद्धता (= purity);<BR>(3) सरलता (= simpli-<BR>-city);<BR>(4) निव्यार्जता (= guilelessness);<BR>(5)<BR>यथार्थता (= genuineness, reality).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sine
SINE: ज्यापिण्डः, -कः (?). Ph.: versed s.:<BR>उत्क्रमज्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sinecure
SINECURE: to hold a s. appointment, perh.<BR>नामकर्मण्यधिकृत (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sinew
SINEW:<BR>I Lit.: स्नायुः।<BR>II In pl., fig.: बलम्:<BR>v. Strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sinewy
SINEWY:<BR>I Lit.: स्नायुमयः (यी, यं).<BR>II Vigor-<BR>-ous, firm: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sinful
SINFUL:<BR>I Of persons:<BR>(1) पापिन् (f. नी),<BR>very s.:<BR>पापीयस् (f. सी);<BR>(2) पातकिन् (f.<BR>नी);<BR>(3) पापात्मन् (mfn.);<BR>(4) पापकर्मन् (mfn.);<BR>(5) पापकृत् (mfn.); etc.<BR>II Of acts; पाप-<BR>in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sinfully
SINFULLY: expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sinfulness
SINFULNESS: पापपरायणता and sim. comp. s. (of<BR>men): v. Also wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sing
SING:<BR>(1) गायति (गै, c. 1.),<BR>I s. and dance and<BR>play:<BR>गायामि नृत्याम्यथ वादयामि, Mah. iv. 11.<BR>8.; s. s (a song)<BR>expressing different states in<BR>its four feet:<BR>चतुष्पदवस्तुकं गायति, Mal. i.;<BR>sang to whom the entire Veda:<BR>यस्मै ब्रह्मपारायणं<BR> जगौ, Vi. i. 14.;<BR>where with choristers s. ing<BR>out the fame of the Lord of wealth:<BR>उद्गायद्भि-<BR>र्धनपतियशः किन्नरैर्यत्र सार्ध्वम्, Me. ii. 10.;<BR>the<BR>female bee sang:<BR>मधुकराङ्गनयोज्जगे, Si. vi. 20.;<BR>(2) of birds: कूजति (कूज्, c. 1.),<BR>what the<BR>male cuckoo sang sweetly:<BR>पुंस्कोकिलो यन्मधुरं<BR> चुकूज, Ku. ii. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

singe
SINGE: उपदहति, परि- (दह्, c. 1.),<BR>and my skin<BR>is s. d:<BR>त्वक् चैव परिदह्यते, G. i. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

singer
SINGER:<BR>(1) गायन (f. नी);<BR>(2) गायक (f. यिका);<BR>(3) by verb or comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

singing
SINGING (subs.):<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) गीतिः, -तम्,<BR>adapted to s.:<BR>गीतिक्षम (f. मा), Sa. vii. 5.;<BR>time for s.:<BR>गीतसमयः, Mr. iii. 5.;<BR>(2) गानम्;<BR>(3) गेयम्,<BR>who taught you s.:<BR>गेये को नु विनेता वाम्,<BR>R. xv. 69.<BR>II Of birds:<BR>(1) कूजितम् or<BR>कूजनम्;<BR>(2) रुतम् (= sound), Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

singing
SINGING (adj.):<BR>I Of men: गायत् (f. न्ती),<BR>J.<BR>II Of birds: मधुरस्वरः (रा, रं = sweet<BR>toned), and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

singing-master
SINGING-MASTER: perh. गीतशिक्षकः<BR>or<BR>गीताचार्यः<BR>(स शिक्षयामास च गीतवादितम्, Mah. iv. 11.<BR>12.): v. Also musician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

single
SINGLE (adj.):<BR>(1) एक (f. का): v. Alone.<BR>Ph.:<BR>not a s. man:<BR>न कोऽपि; s. combat:<BR>नियुद्धम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

single
SINGLE (v.): gen. with<BR>out:<BR>निर्द्दिशति: v. To<BR>point out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

single-handed
SINGLE-HANDED: एक (f. का),<BR>Śiva s. took the<BR>cities of the enemy:<BR>एकोऽहरद्रिपुपुराणि हरः, Dh.;<BR>v. Alone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

single-stick
SINGLE-STICK:<BR>(1) यष्टिः;<BR>(2) दण्डः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

singly
SINGLY:<BR>I Alone: q. v.: एक (f. का).<BR>II<BR>One by one:<BR>(1) एकैकम्;<BR>(2) एकैकशः;<BR>(3)<BR>प्रत्येकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

singsong
SINGSONG: गाथिका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

singular
SINGULAR:<BR>I Single: एक (f. का), s. number:<BR>एकवचनम्, Sa.<BR>II Remarkable, unpara-<BR>-lleled: q. v.:<BR>(1) अपूर्व (f. र्वा);<BR>(2) अपरूप<BR>(f. पा = odd: spe. in bad sense): v. Also<BR>strange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

singularity
SINGULARITY:<BR>(1) अपूर्वता (uncommonness);<BR>(2) अपरूपता (= oddness);<BR>(3) विशिष्टता<BR>(= particularity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

singularly
SINGULARLY:<BR>(1) अपूर्वम्;<BR>(2) अपरूपम्;<BR>(3)<BR>विशिष्टम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sinister
SINISTER:<BR>I Inauspicious: q. v.: अमङ्गल (f.<BR>ला).<BR>II Crooked, wrong, vicious: q. v.:<BR>दुष्ट (f. ष्टा).<BR>III Left: q. v.: वाम (f. मा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sink
SINK (subs.): भ्रमः, Si. iii. 33.: v. Drain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sink
SINK (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.: मज्जति, नि-, परि-, (मस्ज्,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>the vessel sank in the sea-waters:<BR>पोतः<BR>समुद्राम्भस्यमज्जत्, D.;<BR>sunk in deep mire:<BR>महापङ्के<BR> निमग्नः, H. i.;<BR>of the half s. ing sun:<BR>सामि<BR> मज्जति रवौ, Ki. ix. 5.;<BR>sunk in the calamity<BR>from water which cannot be easily got over:<BR>मग्नस्य तोयापदि दुस्तरायाम्, Si. xiv. 86.<BR>II To<BR>penetrate deep: निविशते (विश्, c. 6.).<BR>III<BR>To decrease, fall: ह्रासमुपैति (इ, c. 2.), अधि-<BR>गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.), etc.<BR>IV To go to<BR>destruction: सीदति, अव-, (सद्, c. 1.), M.<BR>: v. Also to decline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sink
SINK (v. t.):<BR>I To submerge, plunge: q. v.:<BR>मज्जयति, नि-, परि- (c. of मस्ज्),<BR>or s. him in<BR>water:<BR>अप्सु चैनं निमज्जयेत्, M. viii. 114.<BR>II To<BR>dig: q. v.: खनति (खन्, c. 1.).<BR>III To<BR>degrade, ruin: q. v.: अवसादयति (c. of सद्).<BR>Ph.:<BR>s. ing fund:<BR>*शोधनसारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sinless
SINLESS:<BR>(1) अपापः (पा, पं);<BR>(2) अनघः (घा, घं);<BR>(3) निरेनस् (mfn.);<BR>(4) वीतकल्मषः (षा, षं) and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sinner
SINNER:<BR>(1) पापिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) पातकिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) पापकर्मन् (mfn.);<BR>(4) पापात्मन् (mfn.);<BR>(5)<BR>पापकृत् (mfn.); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sinuosity
SINUOSITY:<BR>(1) वक्रता;<BR>(2) वक्रिमन् (m.);<BR>(3)<BR>कुटिलता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sinuous
SINUOUS:<BR>(1) वक्र (f. क्रा);<BR>(2) कुटिलः (ला, लं);<BR>(3) अरालः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sip
SIP (v.):<BR>(1) उपस्पृशति (स्पृश, c. 6.);<BR>(2)<BR>आचामति (चम्, c. 1.),<BR>s. s the drops of sweat on<BR>your face:<BR>आचामति स्वेदलवान् मुखे ते, R. xiii. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sip
SIP (subs.):<BR>(1) आचमनम्;<BR>(2) उपस्पर्शः। To take<BR>a s.: v. To sip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

siphon
SIPHON: a tube: *क्षेपणी, उत्-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sir
SIR: आर्यः,<BR>whence have you come, s.:<BR>कुत आर्यः,<BR>Mr. ii.;<BR>remove s. s:<BR>अपसरत आर्याः, Mr. x.<BR>Ph.:<BR>“my good s.”:<BR>भद्रमुख।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sire
SIRE:<BR>I Of kings: देवः।<BR>II Of holy men:<BR>भगवत् (m.).<BR>III Of father: तातः, Vi.<BR>IV Author, creator: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

siren
SIREN: मोह (हि) नी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sirloin
SIRLOIN:<BR>s. of beef:<BR>गोकटिः (after Bha.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sirname
SIRNAME: v. Surname.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sirocco
SIROCCO: A WIND: *सौरवातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sirrah
SIRRAH (interj.): रे, रेरे, अरे,<BR>or<BR>अरेरे।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sister
SISTER:<BR>(1) भगिनी (any sort of s.);<BR>(2) स्वसृ<BR>(f. =.: rare), R.;<BR>(3) सहोदरी, सोदर्या<BR>or<BR>सगर्भा<BR>(= by the same mother).<BR>Elder s.:<BR>अग्रजा,<BR>Younger s.:<BR>अवरजा, S.'s son:<BR>(1) भागिनेयः;<BR>(2) स्वस्रेयः (rare). S.'s daughter:<BR>(1) भागिनेयी;<BR>(2) स्वस्रेयी<BR>or<BR>स्वस्रि (स्री)या (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sister-in-law
SISTER-IN-LAW:<BR>(1) ननान्दृ (f.) (= husband's<BR>sister); श्याली (= wife's s.);<BR>(3) प्रजावती or<BR>भ्रातृजाया (= brother's wife);<BR>(4) यातृ (f.)<BR>(= husband's brother's w.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sisterhood
SISTERHOOD:<BR>I Lit.: भगिनीत्वम् (?).<BR>II A<BR>society: भगिनीवर्गः, भगिनीसमाजः, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sisterly
SISTERLY:<BR>(1) भगिनीसन्निभः (भा, भं) and sim.<BR>comp. s.;<BR>(2) by adv. भगिनीवत्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sit
SIT (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) आस्ते (आस्, c. 2.).<BR>s. ting on the altar:<BR>वेदिकायामासीन (f. ना), Ku.<BR>iii. 44.;<BR>s. by:<BR>उपास्ते<BR>or<BR>अन्वास्ते, R. i. 56.;<BR>s. on or in:<BR>अध्यास्ते, R. vi. 10.;<BR>(2) निषीदति<BR>(सद्, c. 1.),<BR>s. when she s. s.:<BR>निषण्णायां<BR> निषीदास्याम्, R. i. 89.: v. To sit down. Ph.:<BR>to s. idly:<BR>निष्कर्मन् (mfn.) तिष्ठते or sim. शेते<BR>(शी, c. 2.: fig.), मयाप्यस्मिन् वस्तुनि न शयानेन<BR> स्थीयते, Mr. i.<BR>II As a court: perh. आस्ते,<BR>Mit.<BR>III To incubate: q. v.: perh.<BR>आस्ते, उपविशति (विश्, c. 6.).<BR>IV To fit.:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sit
SIT (v. t.): अध्यास्ते: v. Sit (1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sit down
SIT DOWN:<BR>I To take one's seat: q. v.: उप-<BR>विशति (विश्, c. 6.),<BR>s. for a moment:<BR>मुहूर्तमुप-<BR>विशतु, Sa. i.<BR>II In mil.: expr. with तिष्ठति<BR>(स्था, c. 1.): v. Also to besiege.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sit up
SIT UP:<BR>I Lit. तिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.), R. i. 89.<BR>II To watch: जागर्ति (जागृ, c. 2.),<BR>by s.<BR>ting up late at night:<BR>रात्रिजागरणात्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

site
SITE (subs.):<BR>I Situation, position:<BR>(1)<BR>सन्निवेशः,<BR>s. of the zenana:<BR>अन्तःपुरसन्निवेशः, D.<BR>iii.;<BR>(2) संस्थानम्<BR>or<BR>संस्थितिः।<BR>II Place: भूमिः<BR>etc.,<BR>with s. s of dwelling houses:<BR>वसतिवेश्म-<BR>महीभिः, Ki. ix. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sitting
SITTING (subs.):<BR>I The act: expr. by verb.<BR>II Seat: आसनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

situate
SITUATE, -D:<BR>(1) निविष्ट (f. ष्टा), सं-,<BR>s. on the<BR>banks of the Sarayū:<BR>निविष्टः सरयूतीरे, Ram.;<BR>(2) अवस्थित (f. ता);<BR>(3) संस्थित (f. ता);<BR>(4) -स्थ (f. स्था) in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

situation
SITUATION:<BR>I Location:<BR>(1) निवेशः, -नम्,<BR> सं-;<BR>(2) संस्थानम्<BR>or<BR>अवस्थानम् (स्थितिः).<BR>II<BR>Post, employment: q. v.: पदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

six
SIX: षष्,<BR>s. -faced:<BR>षण्मुख (f. खी); s. oxen:<BR>षङ्गवम्;<BR>with the remaining s. lotuses:<BR>षडिभिः<BR> शेषपद्मैः, Li.; and s. were seen in the thread:<BR>दृष्टं षट्कञ्च सूत्रे, Li. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sixteen
SIXTEEN: षोडशन्,<BR>S. -th.:<BR>षोडशः (शी, शं), s. -fold:<BR>षोडशगुणितः (ता, तं), Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sixth
SIXTH:<BR>(1) षष्ठ, (f. ष्ठी),<BR>with a third, one-fifth,<BR>and a s.:<BR>त्र्यंशपञ्चांशषष्ठैः, Li. 23.:<BR>he was s. in<BR>descent from the moon:<BR>सोमाद्बभूव षष्ठोऽयम्,<BR>Mah. v. 139. 3.;<BR>(2) षाष्ठ (f. ष्ठी) (rare).<BR>S. -ly:<BR>षष्ठतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sixtieth
SIXTIETH: षष्टितमः (मी, मं), “षष्टितमोऽध्यायः,”<BR>Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sixty
SIXTY: षष्टिः,<BR>of s. -two and half:<BR>सार्धद्विषष्टेः,<BR>Li.;<BR>s. -first:<BR>एकषष्टितमः (मी, मं)<BR>or, rarely<BR>एक-<BR>षष्ट (f. ष्टी), S. k.;<BR>s.-nine:<BR>ऊनसप्ततिः, एकोन-<BR>सप्ततिः, or rarely नवषष्टिः, एकान्नसप्ततिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

size
SIZE (subs.): मानम्, प्र-, परि-, what is its s.:<BR>यत्प्रमाणमिदम्, V. p. ii. 2. 3.:<BR>of great s.:<BR>अति-<BR>प्रमाण (f. णा), K.;<BR>befitting their s.:<BR>स्वप्रमाणा-<BR>नुरूप (f. पा), Sa. i.: v. Also shape, extent,<BR>measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sized
SIZED: big-s.: बृहत्प्रमाण (f. णा): v. Size.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skate
SKATE (subs.):<BR>I A fish: शंकुः, शङ्कुचिः,<BR>or<BR>शङ्कोचः।<BR>II An ice-shoe: no equiv.: *नीहारपादुका,<BR> -नाली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skate
SKATE (v.): *नीहारपादुकया विसर्पति (सृप्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skein
SKE(A)IN: पञ्जिः (ञ्जी), पिञ्जिः (ञ्जी), प (पि) ञ्जिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skeleton
SKELETON:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) कङ्कालः,<BR>mules reduced<BR>to s.:<BR>कङ्कालशेषाः खराः, U. iii. 42.;<BR>(2) अस्थिपञ्जरः,<BR>A.<BR>II Fig., outline: गठनम् (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sketch
SKETCH (v.): आलिखति (लिख्, c. 6.): v. To<BR>draw, portray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sketch
SKETCH (subs.): per पाण्डुलेखः, -लेख्यम्; चित्रारम्भः।<BR>(in drawing: (?), R. ii. 31.: v. Also plan,<BR>description.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skewer
SKEWER:<BR>I Subs.: शलाका।<BR>II Verb.: शलाकया<BR> बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.).: v. To fasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skiff
SKIFF: तरणी: v. Boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skilful
SKILFUL, SKILLED:<BR>(1) कुशलः (ला, लं),<BR>I am<BR>s. in breaking and treating horses:<BR>कुशलोऽस्म्यश्व-<BR>शिक्षायां तथैवाश्वचिकित्सिते, Mah. iv. 2. 4.;<BR>(2)<BR>निपुण (f. णा),<BR>s. in conversing about mythological<BR>and historical anecdotes:<BR>पुराणेतिहासकथालापनिपुणः,<BR>K.;<BR>(3) विचक्षण (f. णा),<BR>must be a s. master<BR>of horses:<BR>घ्रुवं हयज्ञो भविता विचक्षणः, Mah. iv.<BR>3.;<BR>(4) प्रवीण (f. णा),<BR>s. in painting, bold in<BR>gambling:<BR>चित्रकर्मणि प्रवीणः, द्यूतव्यापारे प्रगल्भः, K.;<BR>(5) पटु (f. also ट्वी);<BR>(6) विशारदः (दा, दं);<BR>(7) चतुरः (रा, रं) (= shrewd);<BR>(8) दक्ष (f. क्षा<BR>= dexterous);<BR>(9) प्रौढ (f. धा), प्रगल्भ (f. ल्भा),<BR>विदग्ध (f. ग्धा), पेशल (f. ला) (poet. = well<BR>up);<BR>(10) अधीतिन् (f. नी)<BR>or<BR>पठितिन् (f. नी)<BR>(= well-read);<BR>(11) भद्र (f. द्रा = good);<BR>(12) अभिज्ञ (f. ज्ञा = knowing); etc. N. B.<BR>(1)<BR>to<BR>(11) are cons. with loc., or rarely with<BR>dat., or inf. and<BR>(12) with gen. They are<BR>all used in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skilfully
SKILFULLY:<BR>(1) कुशलम्;<BR>(2) निपुणम्;<BR>(3) चतुरम्;<BR>(4) सपाटवम्;<BR>(5) कौशलेन, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skilfulness
SKILFULNESS, SKILL:<BR>(1) कौशलम्, greatest s.:<BR>परं कौशलम्, K.;<BR>(2) नैपुण्यम्,<BR>s. in stirring<BR>anecdotes:<BR>चित्रकथानैपुण्यम्, D.;<BR>(3) पाटवम्,<BR>s. in<BR>riding elephants, horses, and other animals:<BR>मातङ्गतुरङ्गादिवाहनारोहणपाटवम्, D.;<BR>(4) प्रावीण्यम्,<BR>not so much with their s.:<BR>न तथोभयोः प्रावीण्येन,<BR>R. xv. 6.;<BR>(5) वैचक्षण्यम्;<BR>(6) निपुणता;<BR>(7)<BR>चातुर्यम् (= cunning);<BR>(8) दाक्ष्यम् (= dexterity);<BR>(9) अभिज्ञता (= knowledge); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skim
SKIM (v.):<BR>I To remove the scum: फेनं<BR> गालयति (c. of गल्)<BR>or<BR>स्रावयति, वि- (c. of स्रु),<BR>or<BR>निर्हरति (हृ, c. 1.) (with gen.);<BR>II To<BR>pass over gently: perh. परिसर्पति (सृप्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skimmer
SKIMMER:<BR>(1) भ्कर्ज्भ्करम्, -री, Bha.;<BR>(2) खजा<BR>(a. ladle), Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skim-milk
SKIM-MILK: घोलम्, “घोलं तु मथितं तक्रम्”, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skin
SKIN (subs.):<BR>(1) चर्मन् (n.) (= animal;)<BR>cover-<BR>ing with a tiger -s.:<BR>व्याघ्रचर्मणा प्रच्छाद्य, H. iii.;<BR>splitting of the s. (a disease): चर्मदलम्, Bha.;<BR>(2) त्वच् (f.) (general), and of a serpent when<BR>the s. is cast off:<BR>फणावतश्च त्वचि विच्युतायाम्, Ki.<BR>xvii. 45.; clad in the pure s. of Ruru, he...:<BR>त्वचं स मेध्यां परिधाय रौरवीम्, R. iii. 31.;<BR>reduce to<BR>mere s. and bones:<BR>त्वगस्थिमात्रशेषः (षा, षं);<BR>(3) अजिनम् (= hide), s. of an elephant:<BR>गजाजिनम्, Ku. v. 67.;<BR>(4) दृतिः (= leather:<BR>rare);<BR>(5) poet. by deriv.,<BR>in a sheath of<BR>goat -s.:<BR>पाञ्चनखे कोषे, Mah. 42. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skin
SKIN (v.):<BR>I To remove the s.: चर्म<BR>or<BR>त्वचम्<BR> अपोहति (उह्, c. 1.) etc. (with gen.). S. ned:<BR>वि-<BR>or<BR>अप-लोमत्वच् (mfn.), D. viii.<BR>II Of<BR>wounds etc.:<BR>a wound s. s over:<BR>व्रणस्योपरि चर्म<BR> जायते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skin-deep
SKIN-DEEP: चर्मगतः (ता, तं): v. Superficial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skin-fling
SKIN-FLING: बद्धमुष्टि (mfn.): v. Miser,<BR>miserly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skinny
SKINNY: चर्मभूतः (ता, तं) (?): v. Lean,<BR>withered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skip
SKIP (v.): प्लवते (प्लु, c. 1.): v. To leap, frisk,<BR>omit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skip
SKIP, -PING (subs.): प्लुतम्: v. Leap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skirmish
SKIRMISH:<BR>I Subs.: डिम्बः, -आहवः।<BR>II Verb:<BR>expr. by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skirt
SKIRT (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रान्तः: v. Border;<BR>(2)<BR>दशा (of a garment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skirt
SKIRT (v.): expr. by subs.: v. To adjoin;<BR>border.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skittish
SKITTISH:<BR>(1) चपल (f. ला): v. Wanton;<BR>(2)<BR>कातर (f. रा): v. Timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skittishness
SKITTISHNESS:<BR>(1) चपलता: v. Wantonness;<BR>(2) कातर्यम्: v. Timidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skittles
SKITTLES: a play: *नवगुटिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skulk
SKULK (v. i.): निभृतं तिष्ठति, (स्था, c. 1.): v.<BR>To lurk, hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skull
SKULL:<BR>(1) कर्परः;<BR>(2) कपाल (mn.),<BR>the old<BR>necklace of Brahmā's s.s:<BR>पुरातनीं ब्रह्मकपालमालाम्,<BR>Ku. xii. 17.;<BR>a s. for begging:<BR>भिक्षाकपालम्,<BR>K.;<BR>(3) शिरोऽस्थि (= as capitis);<BR>(4) करोटिः<BR>(= 3), Vi. v. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skull-cap
SKULL-CAP:<BR>(1) शिरस्कम्;<BR>(2) शिरस्त्रम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skunk
SKUNK: an animal: *गन्धवीरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sky
SKY:<BR>(1) नभस् (n.),<BR>s. -blue:<BR>नभस्तलश्यामः (मा,<BR> मं), R. xviii. 6.; quickly descending from the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">Page649</a>]<BR>s. ies:<BR>नभोविभागात्तरसावतीर्य, N. iii. 1.;<BR>thunder<BR>fell from a cloudless s.:<BR>पपात वज्रं नभसो निरम्बुदात्,<BR>Ku. xv. 20;<BR>(2) व्योमन् (n.), s. -touching:<BR>व्योमस्पृश् (mfn.), Si. iv. 31.;<BR>(3) आकाशः,<BR>picturesque scene drawn in the s. ies without any<BR>foundation:<BR>आकाशे रचितमभित्ति चित्रकर्म, Si. iv.<BR>53.;<BR>(4) गगनम्,<BR>residents of the s.:<BR>गगनसदः,<BR>Si. iv. 53.;<BR>(5) अन्तरि(री)क्षम्,<BR>then a voice<BR>from the s. loudly proclaimed:<BR>अथान्तरिक्षे वागुच्चैः<BR> प्राह, V. p. v. 28. 21.;<BR>(6) अम्बरम्,<BR>s.<BR>lighting:<BR>अम्बरविकाशिन् (f. नी), Si. v. 3.;<BR>(7)<BR>खम्,<BR>ambling in the s.:<BR>खे खेलगाभी, Ku. vii.<BR>49.;<BR>(8) द्यौः (= heaven: q. v.), s.-bird:<BR>द्युपक्षी, Ku. xv. 14.;<BR>(9) विहायस् (n.);<BR>(10)<BR>वियत्;<BR>(11) गीर्वाणवर्त्म, K., Ki. v. 17. and<BR>sim. comp. s. (poet.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skyey
SKYEY: आकाशनिभः (भा, भं = like the sky);<BR>(2)<BR>दिव्य (f. व्या = heavenly.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skylark
SKYLARK: भरद्वाजः: v. Lark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skylight
SKYLIGHT: *आकाशप्रकाशः: v. Window.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slab
SLAB: शिला (= stone: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slack
SLACK (adj.): शिथिल (f. ला),<BR>with the bow-<BR>trings s.:<BR>शिथिलज्याबन्ध (f. न्धा), Sa. ii. 6.;<BR>(2)<BR>श्लथ (f. था), वि-, परि-,<BR>with the ties s.:<BR>श्लथबन्ध<BR>(f. न्धा)., V. t.: v. Also loose, slow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slack
SLACK, -EN (v.):<BR>I Trans:<BR>(1) शिथिलयति,<BR>I<BR>shall not s. the opportunity of serving:<BR>नाहं<BR> सेवावसरं शिथिलयिष्ये, Sa. iii.;<BR>(2) श्लथयति<BR>(nomi.);<BR>(3) शिथिलीकरोति,<BR>s. ed his hopes<BR>about the life of his father:<BR>पितरि जीविताशां<BR> शिथिलीकरोति, K.;<BR>(4) श्लथीकरोति।<BR>II Intrans.:<BR>(1) शिथिलायते;<BR>(2) शिथिलीभवति,<BR>tie the s. ed<BR>dress:<BR>शिथिलीभूतमाकलय दुकूलम्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slackly
SLACKLY:<BR>(1) शिथिलम्, Sa. ii. 9.;<BR>(2) श्लथम्,<BR>R. v. 69.;<BR>(3) शैथिल्येन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slackness
SLACKNESS:<BR>(1) शिथिलता, -त्वम्<BR>or<BR>शैथिल्यम्,<BR>from<BR>s. of memory:<BR>स्मृतिशैथिल्यात्, Sa. vii.;<BR>(2)<BR>श्लथता, वि-, परि- (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slag
SLAG: मलम्: v. Dross.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slain
SLAIN (adj.): हत (f. ता), नि- etc.: v. To<BR>kill, slay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slake
SLAKE (v.):<BR>I To quench, extinguish: q. v.:<BR>प्रशमयति (c. of शम्).<BR>II घोलयति, refine sugar<BR>s. ed in cold water:<BR>जलेन शीतलेनैव घोलिता शुभ्र-<BR>शर्करा, Bha.<BR>III To go out, be extin-<BR>-guished: q. v.: प्रशाम्यति (शम्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slam
SLAM: v. Bung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slander
SLANDER (subs.): अपवादः: v. Scandal, cal-<BR>-umny, accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slander
SLANDER (v.): अपवदति (वद्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>defame, calumniate, accuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slanderer
SLANDERER:<BR>(1) असूयक (f. यिका): v. Detr-<BR>-acter;<BR>(2) अपवादक (f. दिका),: v. Accuser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slanderous
SLANDEROUS:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) परिवादिन्<BR>(f. दिनी);<BR>(3) परिवादगर्भ (f. र्भा);<BR>(4) व्यपवादकर<BR>(f. री);<BR>(5) सापवाद (f. दा);<BR>(6) आक्षारिन्<BR>(f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slanderously
SLANDEROUSLY:<BR>(1) सापवादम्;<BR>(2) सासूयम्;<BR>(3) परिवादगर्भम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slang
SLANG:<BR>(1) प्रलापः (देशभाषारूपं लुप्तवर्णमधिकवर्णं<BR> क्वचिद्विकृतवर्णञ्च पदजातम्), Mah. i. 143. 19.;<BR>s. of<BR>the boatmen:<BR>नाविकप्रलापः (?);<BR>(2) अपभाषा (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slant
SLANT, -ING (adj.): अवसर्पिन् (f. णी): v. Also<BR>oblique.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slantingly
SLANTINGLY: तिर्यक्: v. Obliquely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slap
SLAP (subs.):<BR>(1) चपे (र्प) टः;<BR>(2) चपेटिका;<BR>(3)<BR>चपेटप्रहारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slap
SLAP (v.):<BR>(1) चपेटेन हन्ति (हन्, c. 2.), प्रहरति<BR>(हृ, c. 2.), आयतं छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 1.), etc.<BR>: v. To strike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slash
SLASH (v.):<BR>I Lit.: आयतं छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7.)<BR>or<BR>निकृन्तति (कृत्, c. 7.).<BR>II Fig.: chiefly<BR>in s. ing: अरुन्तुद (f. दा), when the mind is s. ed:<BR>गाढं क्षते मनसि, Ni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slash
SLASH (subs.):<BR>(1) आयतच्छेदः;<BR>(2) महाच्छेदः;<BR>(3) अतिच्छिन्नम्, Ni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slate
SLATE: *शिलाटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slate
SLATE: (Adj.) *शैलाटः, -कः: v. Also tiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slattern
SLATTERN: v. Slut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slaughter
SLAUGHTER: (subs.):<BR>(1) विशसनम्, vast s.:<BR>घोरं विशसनम्;<BR>(2) कदनम्,<BR>the s. er of innocent<BR>Kshatriyas:<BR>निरपराधराजकुलकदन, Vi. iii.;<BR>(3)<BR>घातः (= killing: q. v.),<BR>s. of the army by the<BR>enemy:<BR>परैः सैन्यघातः, Mah. vi. 108. 28.;<BR>(4)<BR>घातनम्, Ku. xv. 8.;<BR>(5) वैशसम्,<BR>half-s.:<BR>अर्ध-<BR>वैशसम्, Ku. iv. 31.: v. Destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slaughter
SLAUGHTER (v.): विशसति (शस्, c. 1.),<BR>a calf<BR>has been s. ed:<BR>वत्सतरी विशसिता, U. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slaughterhouse
SLAUGHTERHOUSE: सू(शू)ना;<BR>its owner:<BR>सौनिकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slave
SLAVE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: दासः (f. सी), (s.s)<BR>home-bred, bought, got and hereditary:<BR>गृहजात-<BR>क्रीतलब्धपारम्परीणाः, Viv.;<BR>who wishes to make his<BR>s. a free man:<BR>यः स्वं दासमदासं कर्तुमिच्छेत्, N. s.;<BR>it is s.'s property, the master is not entitled to it:<BR>तद्दासधनं स्वामी नार्हति, Viv.;<BR>even a free woman<BR>married by a s. becomes a s.:<BR>दासेनोढा त्वदासी या<BR> सापि दासीत्वमाप्नु यात्, Kat.;<BR>a born s.:<BR>गर्भदासः<BR>(f. सी), Mr.; eating female and male s. s:<BR>दासीदासजनं भक्षयित्वा, D. vi.;<BR>I am your atten-<BR>dant s. with a thousand s. girls:<BR>अहं दासीसहस्रेण<BR> दासी ते परिचारिका, Mah. i. 77. 22.<BR>II Fig.<BR>(1) दासः;<BR>(2) expr. by वश,<BR>a s. of the<BR>passions:<BR>इन्द्रियपरवशः (शा, शं): v. Give way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slave
SLAVE (v.):<BR>I Trans: दासीकरोति, K.<BR>II<BR>Intrans.:<BR>(1) दासायते। (nomi.);<BR>(2) दास्यं or<BR>दासकर्म करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slaver
SLAVER (subs.):<BR>I A slave-merchant: दास-<BR>वणिज् (m.) (?).<BR>II A slave-ship: दासवहनपोतः,<BR>etc. (?).<BR>III Saliva: q. v.: लाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slaver
SLAVER (v.): लालायते (nomi.); by phrases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slavery
SLAVERY:<BR>(1) दास्यम्;<BR>(2) दासत्वम्, -ता;<BR>(3)<BR>दासभावः, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slave-traffic
SLAVE-TRAFFIC, SLAVE-TRADE: दासविक्रयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slavish
SLAVISH:<BR>(1) दास- in comp.: v. Servile;<BR>(2) by adv. दासवत्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slavishly
SLAVISHLY: दासवत् (lit. and fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slavishness
SLAVISHNESS: expr. by circumlo.: v. Ser-<BR>-vility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slay
SLAY (v.):<BR>(1) मारयति (c. of मृ): v. To kill;<BR>(2) शातयति (c. of शत्), “तदानीकमशातयत्”,<BR>Mah. vii. 157. 27.:<BR>(3) विशसति (शस्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To slaughter;<BR>(4) सूदयति, वि-, विनि- (सूद्,<BR>c. 10.),<BR>s. ing many animals:<BR>सूदयन् विविधान्<BR> मृगान्, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slayer
SLAYER:<BR>(1) विशसितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) by subs.<BR>in comp.,<BR>s. of Madhu:<BR>मधुसूदनः; s. of Bala:<BR>बलनिसूदनः, R. ix. 3.: v. Also killer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sledge
SLEDGE: No equiv.: *श्लक्ष्णयानम्, श्लाक्ष्णम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sledge-hammer
SLEDGE-HAMMER:<BR>(1) मुद्गरः;<BR>(2) महाघनः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleek
SLEEK: श्लक्ष्ण (f. क्ष्णा): v. Smooth, glossy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleep
SLEEP (subs.):<BR>(1) निद्रा,<BR>overtaken by s.:<BR>निद्रया<BR> गृहीतः, Va;<BR>I was overpowered with s.:<BR>निद्रया<BR> परामृष्ये, D.;<BR>to go to s.:<BR>निद्रां याति<BR>or<BR>गच्छति,<BR>K.;<BR>to break s.:<BR>निद्रां भनक्ति<BR>or<BR>भिनत्ति, Ma.<BR>n.;<BR>does not s. comes to us today:<BR>आवयोर्निद्राद्य<BR> किमु नोपसद्यते, N.; was sent to long s. (i. e.<BR>death); दीर्घनिद्रां प्रवेशितः, R. xii. 18.;<BR>without having s.:<BR>अनुपजातनिद्र (f. द्रा), K.;<BR>very sound s.:<BR>अतिपक्वनिद्रा, D.;<BR>dead s.:<BR>घोर-<BR>निद्रा, K.;<BR>aroused from s.:<BR>विनिद्र (f. द्रा), B.;<BR>(2) rarely स्वप्नः, स्वापः,<BR>or<BR>सुप्तिः,<BR>in s.:<BR>स्वप्ने, D.;<BR>fond of s.:<BR>प्रियस्वप्न (f. प्ना), K. xii. 81.;<BR>(3)<BR>शयनम्,<BR>went to s.:<BR>शयनमगमत्, Ram. ii. 92. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleep
SLEEP (v.):<BR>(1) स्वपिति, प्र-, अव-, सम्-, (स्वप्, c. 2.)<BR>(lit. and fig.),<BR>I will go and s. in the gate-<BR>house:<BR>द्वारशालायां गत्वा स्वप्स्यामि, Mr.;<BR>s. ing at<BR>proper time:<BR>यथाकालं स्वपन्, R.;<BR>(2) निद्राति<BR>(द्रा, c. 2.),<BR>slept pressing each other:<BR>पीडनां<BR> विदधतौ निदद्रतुः, N.;<BR>(3) निद्रायते, (nomi.),<BR>Mah.;<BR>(4) शेते (शी, c. 2.) (prop.=to lie<BR>down) (lit. and fig.),<BR>s.ing calmly:<BR>विश्रब्धं<BR> शयानम्, Mah.; I will not be s. ing over it:<BR>मयास्मिन्वस्तुनि शयानेन न स्थीयते, Mu.;<BR>s. ing with<BR>the face down:<BR>अवमूर्द्धशयः, S. k.;<BR>(5) संविशति<BR>(विश्, c. 6.) (=शेते),<BR>shall s. on the left<BR>side:<BR>वामपार्श्वेन संविशेत्, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleep-producing
SLEEP-PRODUCING:<BR>(1) स्वापन् (f. नी), प्र-, R.<BR>vii. 61.;<BR>(2) निद्राजनन (f. नी)<BR>or<BR>-जनक (f.<BR>निका), M. n.;<BR>(3) निद्राकर (f. री); and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleeper
SLEEPER:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) expr. by verb;<BR>(2)<BR>निद्रालु (mfn.);<BR>(3) शयालु (mfn.).<BR>II A<BR>beam: *संवेशतुला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleepily
SLEEPILY:<BR>(1) सनिद्रम्, Si. xi. 18.;<BR>(2) expr.<BR>by adj. निद्रावशः (शा, शं), निद्राभिभूतः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleepiness
SLEEPINESS: नैद्रतन्द्रा: v. Sleep, sleepy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleeping
SLEEPING (subs.): शयनम्;<BR>(2) rarely स्वापः,<BR> सुप्तिः,<BR>or<BR>स्वप्नः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleeping-draught
SLEEPING-DRAUGHT: निद्राजनकमौषधम् (see Bha.<BR>on “निद्रानाशः”).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleeping-house
SLEEPING-HOUSE:<BR>(1) शयनगृहम्;<BR>(2) स्वप्ननिकेतनम्<BR>and sim. comp.s (rare), B. xi. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleeping-partner
SLEEPING-PARTNER: भोगसहकारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleepless
SLEEPLESS:<BR>(1) नष्टनिद्र (f. द्रा), and sim.<BR>comp.s,<BR>passed the night s. ly:<BR>उत्सन्ननिद्रा क्षपां<BR> क्षपितवती, K.;<BR>(2) निर्निद्र (f. द्रा; rare). N.B.<BR>विनिद्र and उन्निन्द्र are commonly applied to<BR>awaking after sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleeplessness
SLEEPLESSNESS:<BR>(1) निद्रानाशः (as a disease),<BR>Bha.;<BR>(2) निर्निद्रता;<BR>(3) निद्राभावः and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleepy
SLEEPY:<BR>I Inclined to sleep:<BR>(1) निद्रावशः<BR>(शा, शं);<BR>(2) निद्राभिभूतः (ता, तं);<BR>(3) निद्रा-<BR>परतन्त्र (f. न्त्रा), M. n.;<BR>(4) निद्राविधेयः (या, यं),<BR>R. vii. 62.; and sim. comp.s. Ph.: to feel<BR>s.: (= wish to sleep):<BR>(1) सुषुप्सति;<BR>(2)<BR>शिशयिषते, Si. xi. 22.;<BR>(3) निदिद्रासति, Si. xi.<BR>4.<BR>II Causing sleep: निद्राप्रद (f. दा), Bha.:<BR>v. Sleep-producing.<BR>III Belonging to<BR>sleep: नैद्र (f. द्री), “नश्यन्नैद्रतन्द्रः” Si. xi. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleet
SLEET: Perh. तुषारवर्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleeve
SLEEVE:<BR>(1) पिप्पलः (?), Wilson;<BR>(2) आस्तरणम् (?;<BR>comp. Astin). Ph.: to laugh in one's s.:<BR>अन्तर् हसति (हस्, c. 1.): v. To laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleigh
SLEIGH: no equiv.: *श्लक्षणयानम्; श्लाक्ष्णम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sleight
SLEIGHT: s. of hand: perh. हस्तलाघवम्: v.<BR>Also jugglery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slender
SLENDER:<BR>(1) तनु (f. also नवी), प्र, a. s. girl:<BR>तन्वी, R. vi. 25.;<BR>a s. plant:<BR>तन्वी लता, R.<BR>xiii. 32.;<BR>having s. command of language:<BR>तनु-<BR>वाग्विभव (f. वा), R. i. 9.;<BR>to make s.:<BR>तनू-<BR>करोति, R. vi. 80.;<BR>(2) कृश (f. शा), परि-,<BR>having a s. belly:<BR>कृशोदर (f. री), Ku. v. 42.;<BR>having s. limbs:<BR>कृशाङ्ग (f. ङ्गी), N. iii. 11.;<BR>by s. results:<BR>कृशेन फलेन, Sa. vi. 11.: v. Also<BR>small, feeble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slenderly
SLENDERLY:<BR>(1) तनु, प्र-;<BR>(2) कृशम्, परि-;<BR>(3) by<BR>adj.: v. Also little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slenderness
SLENDERNESS:<BR>(1) तनुता, -त्वम्, Ku. iv. 13.;<BR>(2) कृशता, -त्वम्, परि-;<BR>(3) कार्श्यम्, परि-;<BR>(4)<BR>तानवम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slice
SLICE: Subs.:<BR>I खण्ड (mn.): v. Bit, piece.<BR>II<BR>Verb: खण्डीकरोति: v. To cut up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slide
SLIDE (v.):<BR>I To glide, move: q. v.: विस-<BR>र्पति (सृप, c. 1.).<BR>II To slip: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slide
SLIDE, -ING (subs.):<BR>I The act: विसर्प, -णम्।<BR>II The place: अवसर्पः<BR>or<BR>विसर्पः।<BR>III In<BR>machinery: *विसर्पः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slight
SLIGHT (adj.):<BR>(1) तनु (f. also न्वी): v. Slen-<BR>-der;<BR>(2) अल्प (f. ल्पा): v. Little. Ph.:<BR>not the s. est:<BR>न मनागपि: v. Least;<BR>in a s.<BR>degree:<BR>ईषत्: v. Little (adv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slight
SLIGHT (v.): उपेक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>disregard, neglect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slight
SLIGHT (subs.): उपेक्षा: v. Disregard, neg-<BR>-lect, contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slighter
SLIGHTER: उपेक्षक (f. क्षिका): v. Also des-<BR>-piser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slightingly
SLIGHTINGLY:<BR>(1) सावज्ञम्;<BR>(2) अनादृत्य: v.<BR>Contemptuously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slightly
SLIGHTLY: ईषत्: v. Little, somewhat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slightness
SLIGHTNESS:<BR>(1) तनुता: v. Slenderness;<BR>(2)<BR>अल्पता: v. Smallness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slily
SLILY:<BR>(1) छलेन;<BR>(2) चतुरम् (= cunningly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slim
SLIM: तनु (f. also न्वी): v. Slender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slime
SLIME: शयानकर्दमः and sim. comp.s.: v. Mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sliminess
SLIMINESS:<BR>(1) शयानता;<BR>(2) चिक्कणता: v. Slimy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slimy
SLIMY:<BR>(1) शयान (f. ना);<BR>(2) चिक्कण (f. णा =<BR>glossy);<BR>(3) पङ्किल (f. ला = muddy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sling
SLING (subs.):<BR>I For throwing:<BR>(1) गोफणा<BR>(?), Wilson;<BR>(2) दोला (?: used in Bengalee).<BR>II For bandage: *श्लथालम्बः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sling
SLING (v.):<BR>I To throw: q. v.: क्षिपति (क्षिप्,<BR>c. 6.).<BR>II To hang: q. v.: उद्बध्नाति (बन्ध,<BR>c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slink
SLINK: व्यपयाति (या, c. 2.): v. To creep<BR>away, flee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slip
SLIP (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.: स्खलति (स्खल्, c. 1.),<BR>her<BR>feet s. ping at every step:<BR>पदे पदे प्रस्खलन्ती, K.<BR>II<BR>Fig.: स्खलति, प्र-,<BR>letting words s.:<BR>वचनानि<BR> स्खलयन्, Ku. iv. 12.: v. Also to fall.<BR>To let<BR>s.:<BR>क्षिपति, अव-, (क्षिप्, c. 6. = to throw:<BR>q. v.),<BR>opportunities s:<BR>क्षिप्तकाल (f. ला), Sa.<BR>iii. 27.<BR>III To s. off: स्रंसते (स्रंस, c. 1.),<BR>the Gānḍīva s. s off from my hand:<BR>गाण्डीवं स्रं सते<BR> हस्तात्, G. i. 30.<BR>IV To s. away: व्यपयाति<BR>(या, c. 2.): v. To escape, flee.<BR>V To s.<BR>in: अलक्षितम् आ-विशति, समा- (विश्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slip
SLIP (v. t.):<BR>I To let s.: q. v.: क्षिपति (क्षिप्,<BR>c. 6.).<BR>II To convey secretly: अलक्षितं<BR> ददाति (दा, c. 3.): v. To put.<BR>III To let<BR>loose: q. v.: मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slip
SLIP (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) स्वलनम्:<BR>(2) स्खलि-<BR>तम्।<BR>II Fig., mistake, fault: q. v.: स्खलनम्<BR>or<BR>स्खलितम्,<BR>how shall I cover this s.:<BR>केनेदं<BR> स्खलितं प्रच्छादयामि, K.;<BR>when there is s. of<BR>tongue:<BR>गोत्रेषु स्खलितो यदा भवति, Sa. vi. 4.<BR>III A twig: q. v.: विटपः।<BR>IV Of paper<BR>etc.: खण्ड (mn.: (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slipper
SLIPPER: पादुका: v. Shoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slipperiness
SLIPPERINESS: पिच्छिलता: v. Slippery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slippery
SLIPPERY:<BR>I Lit.: पिच्छिल (f. ला), in the<BR>battle-field s. with mud. (formed by) blood:<BR>रणाङ्गने शोणितपङ्कपिच्छिले, Ku. xvi. 50.<BR>II Un-<BR>-stable, uncertain: q. v.: अस्थिरः।<BR>III Of<BR>men: चपलः (ला, लं), Sa. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slipshod
SLIPSHOD: fig.: perh. शिथिल (f. ला=<BR>slack).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slit
SLIT: Subs.: दीर्घच्छेदः।<BR>II Verb: दारयति (दॄ,<BR>c. 10.): v. To send.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slogan
SLOGAN: क्ष्वेडितम्: v. Shout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sloop
SLOOP: पोतविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slop
SLOP (subs.):<BR>I Water carelessly thrown:<BR>expr. by circumlo.<BR>II In pl., common<BR>clothes: स्थूलपटः।<BR>III Dirty water: q. v.:<BR>अमेध्यं जलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slope
SLOPE (subs.):<BR>(1) अवसर्पिणी भूः, -मिः (= decli-<BR>-vity);<BR>(2) प्रवणः (णा, णं), Wilson;<BR>(3) perh.<BR>अवसर्पः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slope
SLOPE (v.):<BR>I Trans.:<BR>(1) प्रवणीकरोति;<BR>(2)<BR>आवर्जयति (वृज्, c. 10.).<BR>II Intrans.:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रवणीभवति;<BR>(2) अवसर्पति (सृप्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sloping
SLOPING (adj.):<BR>(1) प्रवण (f. णा);<BR>(2) अवसर्पिन्<BR>(f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sloppy
SLOPPY (adj.): पङ्किल (f. ला): v. Muddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sloth
SLOTH:<BR>I Idleness: q. v.: तन्द्रा, sleep, s.:<BR>निद्रा, तन्द्रा, H. i. 33.<BR>II The animal: no<BR>equiv.: *तन्द्रावहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slothful
SLOTHFUL:<BR>(1) तन्द्रित (f. ता), without being s.:<BR>अतन्द्रिता सा, Ku. v. 14.;<BR>(2) तन्द्रालु (mfn.);<BR>(3) अलसि (f. सा = idle: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slothfully
SLOTHFULLY:<BR>(1) by adj.;<BR>(2) तन्द्रया;<BR>(3)<BR>आलस्येन (=idly),<BR>or<BR>अलसम् (Si. viii. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slothfulness
SLOTHFULNESS:<BR>(1) तन्द्रालुता;<BR>(2) तन्द्रा (= sloth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slouching
SLOUCHING (adj.): प्रलम्ब (f. म्बा, = hanging<BR>down:?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slough
SLOUGH (subs.):<BR>I Of a snake;<BR>(1) निर्मोकः,<BR>to cast off s.:<BR>निर्मोकं विमुञ्चति, R. xvi. 17.;<BR>(2)<BR>कञ्चुकः, a venomous snake with the s. shorn off:<BR>विगलत्कञ्चुकः पन्नगेन्द्रः, Vi. vi. 53.<BR>II Of a<BR>wound: perh. कञ्चुकः<BR>or<BR>कोषः (comp. verna-<BR>-cular).<BR>III A deep miry place: महापङ्कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slough
SLOUGH (v.): स्खलति (स्खल्, c. 1.),<BR>in the<BR>third week, it dries and s. s off:<BR>ततस्तृतीये सप्ताहे<BR> शुष्यति स्खलति स्वयम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slovenliness
SLOVENLINESS: perh. अव्यवस्था: v. Careless-<BR>-ness, negligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slovenly
SLOVENLY: perh. अव्यवस्थितः (ता, तं): v.<BR>Careless, negligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slow
SLOW:<BR>(1) मन्द (f. न्दा),<BR>s. motion:<BR>मन्दगतिः,<BR>P. h.;<BR>s. digestion:<BR>मन्दाग्निः, Sr.;<BR>having s.<BR>poison:<BR>मन्दविषः, J.;<BR>being s. I did not see that<BR>my companions would perceive it:<BR>सखीजनोऽप्युप-<BR>लक्षयतीति मन्दया न लक्षितम्, H.; to help s. minds:<BR>मन्दात्मानुजिघृक्षया, K.;<BR>are not s.:<BR>न मन्दायन्ते,<BR>Me. i. 41.;<BR>(2) मन्थर (f. रा), the s. maid:<BR>मन्थरा, Ram.;<BR>s. to recognize:<BR>प्रत्यभिज्ञानमन्थर<BR>(f. रा), Sa. iv.;<BR>(3) बिलम्बित (f. ता = de-<BR>-layed),<BR>quick and s.:<BR>द्रुतबिलम्बित-, P. h.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slowly
SLOWLY:<BR>(1) मन्दम्<BR>or<BR>मन्दं मन्दम्, Me. i. 9.;<BR>(2) मन्थरम्, Ki. iv. 17.;<BR>(3) by comp.;<BR>s. pressed:<BR>मन्दाक्रान्त (f. न्ता). Ph. शनैः<BR>or<BR>शनैः<BR> शनैः, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slowness
SLOWNESS:<BR>(1) मन्दता;<BR>(2) मान्द्यम्;<BR>(3) मन्थरता<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slow-worm
SLOW-WORM: *मन्थरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slug
SLUG: v. Snail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sluggard
SLUGGARD, SLUGGISH:<BR>(1) *तन्द्रालु (mfn.): v.<BR>Slothful;<BR>(2) मन्द (f. न्दा): v. Slow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sluggishly
SLUGGISHLY:<BR>(1) by adj.;<BR>(2) मन्दम्: v. Slowly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sluggishness
SLUGGISHNESS:<BR>(1) तन्द्रालुता;<BR>(2) मान्द्यम् (slow-<BR>-ness);<BR>(3) जाड्यम् (= stupor).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sluice
SLUICE:<BR>I Flood-gate: *रोधद्वारम्।<BR>II Stream:<BR>q. v.: प्रवाहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slumber
SLUMBER:<BR>I Subs.: स्वापः: v. Sleep.<BR>II<BR>Verb: स्वपिति (स्वप्, c. 2.): v. To sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slur
SLUR:<BR>I Subs.: कलङ्कः: v. Stain, disgrace.<BR>II Verb.: कलङ्कयति (nomi.): v. To soil,<BR>pollute, disgrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slut
SLUT:<BR>(1) अविनीता;<BR>(2) बन्धकी;<BR>(3) दुःशीला;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sluttish
SLUTTISH: अविनीत (f. ता): v. Untidy,<BR>careless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sly
SLY:<BR>(1) धूर्त (f. र्ता): v. Rogue;<BR>(2) चतुर<BR>(f. रा): v. Cunning;<BR>(3) दाम्भिक (f. की)<BR>: v. Hypocrite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

slyness
SLYNESS:<BR>(1) धूर्तता;<BR>(2) चतुरता;<BR>(3) दाम्भिकता<BR>: v. Sly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smack
SMACK (v. i.):<BR>it s. s of meat:<BR>आमिषगन्धि (mfn.)<BR>Sa.: v. To smell, taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smack
SMACK (v. t.):<BR>I To make a sharp noise:<BR>आस्फोटयति (स्फुट्, c. 10.).<BR>or<BR>आस्फोटनं करोति।<BR>II To slap: q. v.<BR>III To kiss noisily:<BR>perh. रभसेन चुम्बति (चुम्ब्, c. 1.), Ki. ix. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smack
SMACK (subs.):<BR>I Loud kiss: perh. रसभ-<BR>चुम्बितम्।<BR>II Savour:<BR>(1) स्वादः (= taste:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(2) गन्धः (= smell: q. v.).<BR>III Crack-<BR>-ing: आस्फोटनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

small
SMALL (adj.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) क्षुद्र (f. द्रा:<BR>not of quantity),<BR>s. craft:<BR>क्षुद्रनौः;<BR>s. whirl-<BR>wind:<BR>क्षुद्रनिर्घातः, K.;<BR>s. enemy:<BR>क्षुद्रारातिः, Ve.<BR>iii.;<BR>(2) अल्प (f. ल्पा = little: q. v.),<BR>and my<BR>intellect of s. range:<BR>क्व चाल्पविषया मतिः, R. i. 2.;<BR>at a very s. price:<BR>अल्पीयसा मूल्येन, D. iii. Ph.:<BR>in a s. degree:<BR>ईषत्,: v. Little (adv.), some-<BR>-what.<BR>II Of the voice: v. Weak, low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

small
SMALL (subs.): perh. क्षुद्रभागः, s. s: perh. क्षुद्र-<BR>वासस् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smallage
SMALLAGE: शाकभेदः; *भूगर्भा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smallness
SMALLNESS:<BR>(1) क्षुद्रता, -त्वम्,<BR>from the s. of<BR>woman's nature:<BR>क्षुद्रतया स्त्रीस्वभावस्य, K.;<BR>(2)<BR>अल्पता, -त्वम्,: v. Littleness;<BR>(3) नीचता<BR>(= lowness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

small-pox
SMALL-POX:<BR>(1) वसन्तः, -रोगः;<BR>(2) शीतला (prob.<BR>=goddess of s.),<BR>attacked with s.:<BR>देव्या<BR> शीतलयाक्रान्ताः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

small-talk
SMALL-TALK: संकथा: v. Chat, conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smart
SMART (adj.):<BR>I Sharp: q. v.: तीक्ष्ण (f. क्ष्णा),<BR>II Cunning, skilful: q. v.: चतुर (f. रा).<BR>III Witty:<BR>(1) रसिक (f. का);<BR>(2) सरस<BR>(f. सा).<BR>IV Elegant, lively: q. v.: प्रफुल्ल<BR>(f. ल्ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smart
SMART (subs.):<BR>(1) तीव्रवेदना and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(2) शूलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smart
SMART (v.): expr. by circumlo.:<BR>my heart is<BR>s. ing from disgrace:<BR>न्यक्कारो हृदि वज्रकील इव मे<BR> तीव्रं परिस्पन्दते, Vi. v. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smartly
SMARTLY:<BR>(1) तीक्ष्णम्: v. Sharply;<BR>(2) तूर्णम्<BR>: v. Quickly;<BR>(3) शोभनम्।: v. Beautifully;<BR>(4) सरसम् (=wittily).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smart-money
SMART-MONEY: no equiv.: *शूलशोधः<BR>or<BR>शूलधनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smartness
SMARTNESS:<BR>(1) तीक्ष्णता: v. Sharpness;<BR>(2)<BR>लाघवम्: v. Quickness, dexterity;<BR>(3)<BR>वैदग्धम्: v. Skilfulness;<BR>(4) रसिकता (= witti-<BR>-ness);<BR>(5) शोभा: v. Beauty;<BR>(6) वेगः: v.<BR>Impetuosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smash
SMASH (v.):<BR>(1) मथ्नाति (मन्थ्, c. 9.),<BR>shall I<BR>not s. the hundred Kauravas:<BR>मथ्नामि न कौरवशतम्,<BR>Ve. i. 15.;<BR>of s. ing misfortunes:<BR>प्रमाथिनीनां<BR> विपदाम्, Ki. iii. 14.;<BR>(2) मृद्नाति, अव-, परि-, सं-,<BR> अभि-, (मृद्, c. 9.),<BR>s. ed their armies:<BR>बलान्यभृद्रात्,<BR>R. xviii. 5.;<BR>(3) दलयति<BR>or<BR>दालयति, वि-,<BR> परि-, (दल्, c. 10.),<BR>s. ed his head:<BR>मूर्द्धानमदालयत्,<BR>B.;<BR>(4) पोथयति, अव-, (पुथ्, c. 10.), Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smash
SMASH (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रमाथः;<BR>(2) विमर्दः, -नम्;<BR>(3) दलनम्, परिदलनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smatterer
SMATTERER:<BR>(1) वार्त्तामात्रावबोधिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>पल्लवग्राहिन् (f. णी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smattering
SMATTERING (subs.): s. of knowledge:<BR>(1) वार्त्ता-<BR>मात्रावबोधः, D. ii., and sim. comp.s;<BR>(2) पल्लव-<BR>ग्राहिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smear
SMEAR: लिम्पति, वि-, (लिप्, c. 6.): v. To<BR>besmear, annoint.: s. over, i. e. to set out:<BR>लुम्पति, वि- (लुप्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smell
SMELL (subs.):<BR>I The sense: घ्राणम्,<BR>perceiv-<BR>able by s.:<BR>घ्राणग्राह्य (f. ह्या), Par.<BR>II The<BR>act: घ्राणम्, आ-, उपा-,<BR>the sense of s.:<BR>घ्राणेन्द्रियम्,<BR>K.;<BR>the faculty of s.:<BR>घ्राणशक्तिः।<BR>III Scent,<BR>odour: q. v. गन्धः,<BR>having the s. of fish:<BR>मत्स्य-<BR>गन्ध (f. न्धा), Mah.;<BR>s. of wine:<BR>मद्यस्य or [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">Page654</a>]<BR>मद्यभवो गन्धः, Bha.;<BR>cannot bear even the s. of<BR>others:<BR>नान्यस्य गन्धमपि सहन्ते, Si. v. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smell
SMELL (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: घ्राति, आ-, उपा-, अभि-,<BR> अव- (घ्रा, c. 2.),<BR>I smelt the diffusing scent of a<BR>flower:<BR>विसर्पन्तं कुसुमगन्धमभ्यजिघ्रम्, K.<BR>II Fig.<BR>गन्धं प्राप्नोति (आप्, c. 5.). (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smell
SMELL (v. i.): expr. with गन्धः, it s. s of flesh:<BR>इदमामिषगन्धं वाति, Sa. v.;<BR>s. ing like fat:<BR>वसागन्ध<BR>(f. न्धा), Ve. iii.;<BR>strong-s.ing:<BR>उग्रगन्ध<BR>(f. न्धा), Bha.<BR>or<BR>उद्गन्धि (mfn.: G. A. 25.);<BR>honey-s.ing:<BR>मधुगन्धिन् (f. नी), Bha.;<BR>s. ing<BR>elephant:<BR>गन्धद्विपः, R. vi. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smelling
SMELLING (subs.): v. Smell. Ph.: s. -bottle:<BR>*गन्धकूपी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smelt
SMELT (subs.): मत्स्यविशेषः; *गन्धमीनः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smelt
SMELT (v.): विद्रावयति (c. of द्रु) (?): v. To<BR>melt, fuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smelter
SMELTER: लौहद्रावकः (?): v. Melter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smile
SMILE (subs.):<BR>(1) स्मितम्, with a s. (i. e. s. ing):<BR>सस्मितम्, D. v.;<BR>(2) विहसितम्, (rare);<BR>(3)<BR>ईषद्धास्यम्, मन्दहासः, and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smile
SMILE (v.):<BR>(1) स्मयते (स्मि, c. 1.),<BR>and I s. d a<BR>little:<BR>अहञ्च किञ्चिदस्मैषि, D. v.;<BR>s. d looking at<BR>me and went away:<BR>मामभिवीक्ष्य स्मित्वा प्रातिष्ठत,<BR>D. ii.;<BR>(2) विहसति (हस्, c. 1.),<BR>said s. ing<BR>gently:<BR>मन्दं मन्दं विहस्याब्रवीत्, K.: v. Also to<BR>laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smile on
SMILE ON: i. e. to favour: q. v.: अनुगृह्नाति<BR>(ग्रह्, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smiling
SMILING (adj.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) स्मेरः (रा, रं),<BR>Ku. v. 70.;<BR>(2) सस्मितः (ता, तं);<BR>(3) स्मयमानः<BR>(ना, नं),<BR>I replied s.:<BR>मया स्मयमानेनामिहितम्,<BR>D. ii.;<BR>(4) स्मितः (ता, तं),<BR>with a s. counten-<BR>ance:<BR>स्मितमुख (f. खी), D. ii.<BR>II Joyous:<BR>प्रफुल्ल (f. ल्ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smilingly
SMILINGLY:<BR>(1) सस्मितम्;<BR>(2) विहस्यः v. To<BR>smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smirch
SMIRCH: मलिनयति (nomi.): v. To soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smirk
SMIRK:<BR>I Subs.: विकृतं स्मितम्।<BR>II Verb.:<BR>expr. by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smite
SMITE (v.):<BR>I To strike, kill: q. v.: हन्ति<BR>(हन्, c. 2.).<BR>II Of love: expr. by मदनबाणहतः<BR>(ता, तं) and sim. comp.s.<BR>s. ten by love, I set<BR>out for Srāvastī:<BR>अहं पञ्चबाणवश्यः श्रावस्तीमभ्यवर्तिषि।<BR>D. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smith
SMITH:<BR>(1) शिल्पिन् (m.);<BR>(2) -कारः, in comp.,<BR>iron-s.:<BR>अयस्कारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smithy
SMITHY, SMITHERY:<BR>(1) शिल्पशाला;<BR>(2) कर्मशाला,<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smock
SMOCK, -FROCK: स्थूलशाटी, -टिका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smoke
SMOKE (v. t.):<BR>I As tobacco:<BR>(1) पिबति, (पा,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>s. ing a cigar:<BR>परिपीतधूमवर्तिः, K.;<BR>(2) सेवते, (सेव्, c. 1.: habitually), Bha.<BR>II<BR>To purify by s.: धूमे(पे)न शोधयति (c. of शुध्):<BR>v. To purify.<BR>III To dry by s.: धूमे(पे)न<BR> शोषयति (c. of शुष्): v. To dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smoke
SMOKE (v. i.): धूमा(पा)यते (nomi.),<BR>making the<BR>quarters s.:<BR>धूमाययन् दिशः, Mah. iii. 38. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smoke
SMOKE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: धूमः(पः), dark like s.:<BR>धूमधूम्र (f. म्रा), R. xv. 16.;<BR>forming clouds of<BR>s.:<BR>धृतधूममण्डलः, Ki. xvi., 59.;<BR>where there is<BR>s., there is fire:<BR>यतो धूमस्ततो वह्निः।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>‘ending in s.’: perh. शून्यगर्भ (f. र्भा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smokeless
SMOKELESS:<BR>(1) निर्धूम (f. मा);<BR>(2) विधूम (f.<BR>मा),<BR>of s. lustre:<BR>विधूमरोचिः, M. n. on Si. i.<BR>2.;<BR>(3) धूमहीन (f. ना); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smoker
SMOKER:<BR>(1) धूमप (f. पा)<BR>or<BR>पायिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) धूमसेविन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smoky
SMOKY:<BR>I Smoking:<BR>(1) धूमा(पा)यमान (f.<BR>ना);<BR>(2) सधूम (f. मा).<BR>II Full of smoke:<BR>(1) सधूम (f. मा);<BR>(2) धूमावरुद्ध (f. द्धा);<BR>(3)<BR>धूमबहुल (f. ला); and sim. comp.s.<BR>III<BR>Like s.:<BR>(1) धूमाभ (f. भा), and sim. comp.s;<BR>(2) धूम्र (f. म्रा).<BR>IV Smelling or tasting<BR>like s.:<BR>(1) धूमगन्ध (f. न्धा: of smell);<BR>(2)<BR>धूमस्वाद (f. दा);<BR>(3) by adv.: धूमवत्: v.<BR>To savour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smooth
SMOOTH (adj.):<BR>(1) सम (f. मा = equal, equable,<BR>level: q. v.),<BR>although the ground is s.:<BR>भित्तौ<BR> समायामपि, Sa. vi. 16.;<BR>naturally s., glossy, and<BR>black:<BR>निसर्गसमस्निधनीलः, D. vi.;<BR>(2) श्लक्ष्ण (f.<BR>क्ष्णा = glossy),<BR>quieting by s. words:<BR>शान्त्वयन्<BR> श्लक्ष्णया वाचा, Mah. iii. 37. 56.: v. Mild, soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smooth
SMOOTH (v.):<BR>(1) समीकरोति: v. To level;<BR>(S) श्लक्ष्णीकरोति (in other senses);<BR>(3) श्लक्ष्णयति<BR>(nomi.=2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smoothly
SMOOTHLY:<BR>(1) समम्;<BR>(2) श्लक्ष्णम् (= softly);<BR>(3) सुखेन (easily).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smoothness
SMOOTHNESS:<BR>(1) समता;<BR>(2) श्लक्ष्णता (= glossi-<BR>-ness, softness);<BR>(3) शान्तता (= quiet);<BR>(4)<BR>स्वच्छता (= clearness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smother
SMOTHER (v.):<BR>I To suffocate: q. v.<BR>II To<BR>suppress: q. v.: प्रतिस्तभ्नाति (स्तम्भ्, c. 9.).<BR>III To smash: q. v.: मृद्राति (मृद्, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smoulder
SMOULDER:<BR>(1) अन्तर् ज्वलति, (ज्वल्, c. 1.) or<BR>स्फुरति (स्फुर्, c. 1.),<BR>s. ing rage:<BR>अन्तःस्फुरत्-<BR>कोपानलः, Vi. v. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smuggle
SMUGGLE: expr. by circumlo., by s. ing goods:<BR>प्रतिषिद्धानि भाण्डानि निर्हरतः, M. viii. 399.: v.<BR>To import, export.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smuggler
SMUGGLER: expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smut
SMUT (subs.):<BR>I Obscene language: अश्लीलम्।<BR>II मलम्।<BR>III Lamp-black: मसी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smut
SMUT, SMUTCH (v.): मलिनयति (nomi.): v. To<BR>soil, blacken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

smutty
SMUTTY:<BR>(1) अश्लील (f. ला): v. Obscene;<BR>(2)<BR>मलिन (f. ना): v. Dirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snack
SNACK:<BR>I Equal share: q. v.: समांशः: v.<BR>Half.<BR>II Hasty repast: लध्वाहारः, and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snaffle
SNAFFLE:<BR>I Subs.: खलीनम्: v. Bit.<BR>II<BR>Verb.: perh. खलीनयति (nomi.); खलीनं ददाति<BR>(दा, c. 3.: with loc.), P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snail
SNAIL:<BR>I Lit.; शम्बूकः।<BR>II Fig.: मन्थर (f. रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snake
SNAKE:<BR>(1) सर्पः,<BR>s. -sacrifice:<BR>सर्पयज्ञः, Mah.;<BR>I<BR>have been bitten by a s.:<BR>सर्पेणास्मि दष्टः, Mal.<BR>iv.;<BR>(2) अहिः (= poisonous s.),<BR>all venomous<BR>s. s. are poisonous:<BR>अहयः सविषाः सर्वे, K. s. xiii.<BR>84.;<BR>s. -catcher:<BR>आहितुण्डिकः, Mu. ii.;<BR>(3)<BR>भुजङ्गः, भुजगः<BR>or<BR>भुजङ्गमः,<BR>draws out a s. from the<BR>basket:<BR>भुजङ्गमाकर्षति पेटिकायाः, V. t.;<BR>(4) नागः;<BR>(5) पन्नगः;<BR>(6) उरगः;<BR>(7) व्यलः (rare),<BR>s.-<BR>catcher:<BR>व्यालग्राही, Mu. ii. Ph.:<BR>extricated<BR>himself from the coils of s.:<BR>मोचयामास स्वदेहं<BR> भोगबन्धनात्, V. p. v. 7. 42.;<BR>bending the middle<BR>fold of the expanded hood:<BR>आनम्य मध्यमं फणम्,<BR>V. p. v. 7. 43.; sending forth poison with (their)<BR>fangs without interruption:<BR>विषमाशीभिरनारतं<BR> वमन्तः, Si. xx. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snake-root
SNAKE-ROOT: *सर्पौषधिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snake-worshipper
SNAKE-WORSHIPPER: नागोपासकः (शेषोपासक: in<BR>San. 48, शेष = chief of s. s.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snaky
SNAKY:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) by सर्पवत् etc.<BR>(= like a snake). Ph.:<BR>a s. person:<BR>भुजङ्गः (f.<BR>ङ्गी), V. t.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snap
SNAP (v. t.):<BR>I To strike:<BR>(1) स्फोटयति (स्फुट,<BR>c. 10.), shall not s. (the fingers): नास्फोटयेत्,<BR>M. iv. 64.;<BR>(2) स्फालयति, आ- (स्फल्, c. 10.: as<BR>the bow),<BR>s. ping of the bow-string:<BR>ज्यास्फालनम्,<BR>Sa. ii. 4.<BR>II To break up: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>स्फोटयति (c. of स्फुट्);<BR>(2) त्रोटयति (c. of<BR>त्रुट्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snap
SNAP (v. i.):<BR>I To break suddenly: त्रुट्यति<BR>(त्रुट्, c. 4.).<BR>II To make a sharp sound:<BR>क्वणति (क्वण्, c. 1.).<BR>II To bark: q. v.:<BR>भषति (भष, c. 1.)<BR>IV To aim: लक्ष्यीकरोति।<BR>V To bite: q. v.: दशति (दन्श्, c. 1: with<BR>acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snap
SNAP, -PING (subs.):<BR>I As of fingers:<BR>(1)<BR>आस्फोटनम्;<BR>(2) मोटनम्।<BR>II As of bows:<BR>आस्फालनम्<BR>or<BR>आस्फालितम्।<BR>III Barking: भषितम्।<BR>IV Bite: q. v.: दंशः।<BR>V Sudden break-<BR>-ing:<BR>(1) त्रोटनम्;<BR>(2) स्फोटनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snap-dragon
SNAP-DRAGON: the game: द्राक्षास्फोटनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snappish
SNAPPISH:<BR>I Lit.: दंशनशील (f. ला), and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR>II Peevish: q. v.: कर्कश (f. शा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snare
SNARE (v.): पाशे पातयति (c. of पत्): v. To<BR>ensnare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snare
SNARE (subs.):<BR>(1) पाशः,<BR>to lay s. s:<BR>पाशान्<BR> योजयति;<BR>caught in s. s:<BR>पाशैर्बद्धः, H. i.;<BR>(2)<BR>वागुरा, having fallen into the s. s of bad men:<BR>दुर्जनवागुरासु पतितः, P. i. 3.;<BR>(3) जालम् (= net),<BR>rogues live by s. s:<BR>जालोपजीविनोधूर्ताः, K. s. xxiv.<BR>199.;<BR>(4) उन्माथः (a trap).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snarl
SNARL (v.):<BR>(1) भषति (भष्, c. 1. = bark:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(2) घर्घरं गर्जति, (गर्ज्, c. 1. = roll:<BR>q. v.): v. Also to murmur, complain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snarler
SNARLER:<BR>(1) भषक (f. षिका);<BR>(2) कर्कश (f.<BR>शा harsh, peevish: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snatch
SNATCH (v.):<BR>(1) आच्छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7.),<BR>s. es<BR>away in our presence:<BR>मिषतामाच्छिनत्ति नः, Ku.<BR>ii. 46.;<BR>(2) आक्षिप्य गृह्नाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.), [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">Page656</a>]<BR>M. n.;<BR>(3) हरति, अप-, (हृ, c. 1. = to rob.);<BR>(4) मुष्णाति (मुष्, c. 9. = to filch);<BR>(5) उन्मूलयति<BR>(=to uproot).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snatch
SNATCH (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: expr. by verb.<BR>II<BR>Fig.:<BR>by s. es:<BR>खण्डशः, s. s of moonlight:<BR>कादाचित्कचन्द्रिका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snatching
SNATCHING (adj.): Covetous: q. v.: गृघ्नु<BR>(mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sneak
SNEAK: छन्नम् अपसर्पति (सृप्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>withdraw, privately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sneaking
SNEAKING (adj.): fig.: कुत्सितवृत्ति (mfn.): v.<BR>Mean, low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sneakingly
SNEAKINGLY:<BR>(1) कृपणवत्;<BR>(2) दासवत् (= servile).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sneer
SNEER (v.): अवहसति (हस्, c. 1.: with acc.):<BR>v. To deride, ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sneer
SNEER, SNEERING (subs.): अवहासः: v. Deri-<BR>-sion, ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sneeringly
SNEERINGLY:<BR>(1) सावहासम्;<BR>(2) अवहस्य: v.<BR>Derisively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sneeze
SNEEZE (v.): क्षौति (क्षु, c. 2.);<BR>(2) by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sneeze
SNEEZE, SNEEZING (subs.):<BR>(1) क्षुतम्,<BR>s. -pro-<BR>ducer:<BR>क्षुताभिजननः, A.;<BR>(2) क्षवः, -थुः, Sr.;<BR>(3) क्षुत् (f.);<BR>(4) छिक्का;<BR>(5) हञ्जिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sniff
SNIFF: v. To inhale, snuff, smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snip
SNIP (v.):<BR>I Lit.: अग्रं<BR>or<BR>अग्रभागं छिनत्ति (छिद्,<BR>c. 7.): v. To cut, tap.<BR>II To pilfer:<BR>q. v.: मुष्णाति (मुष्, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snipe
SNIPE: the bird: वटेरः, वटेरकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snivel
SNIVEL (subs.):<BR>(1) नासामलम्;<BR>(2) सिंहानम्(णम्);<BR>सिंघाणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snivel
SNIVEL (v.):<BR>I To run at the nose: expr.<BR>by मलं स्रवति (स्रु, c. 1.: with abl. of nose),<BR>s. ing:<BR>नासास्रवः, Sr.<BR>II Whine: क्रन्दति (क्रन्द्,<BR>c. 1.): v. To cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snob
SNOB, -BISH: perh.: सभ्यम्मन्य (f. न्या), भद्रमानिन<BR>(f. नी), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snooze
SNOOZE: v. Nap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snore
SNORE (v.):<BR>I घर्घरायते (nomi.).<BR>II Subs.:<BR>snoring:<BR>घर्घरः, -शब्दः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snort
SNORT:<BR>I Verb.: फु(फू)त्कारं मुञ्चति (मूच्, c.<BR>6.): अनवरतपरिस्फुरत्प्रोथपुटोन्मुक्तफुत्कारेणातिजवापीत-<BR>मनिलमिव नासिकाविवरेणोद्वमन्तम्, K.<BR>II Subs.:<BR>फु(फू)त्कारः<BR>or<BR>फु(फू)त्कृतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snout
SNOUT: पोत्रम्, Ki. xiii. 3. Hence a boar is<BR>पोत्रिन्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snow
SNOW (subs.):<BR>(1) हिमम्, the abode of s.:<BR>हिमालयः;<BR>s.-bound:<BR>हिमसंरुद्ध (f. द्धा), Mat.;<BR>s.-capped summit:<BR>हिमच्छत्रमहाशृङ्गम्, Mat.;<BR>the<BR>whole surface covered with s.:<BR>हिमानुलिप्तसर्वाङ्ग<BR>(f. ङ्गी), Mat.;<BR>fall of s.:<BR>हिमपातः, Mat.;<BR>heap of s.:<BR>हिमानी, Ki. iv. 38.; हिमपुञ्जः, Mat.;<BR>s.-white:<BR>हिमगौर (f. री); Ki. v. 17.;<BR>(2)<BR>तुषारः,<BR>flow of s.:<BR>तुषारस्रुतिः, Ku. i. 6.;<BR>shower-<BR>ing s.:<BR>तुषारवर्षी, R. xiv. 84.; s.-water:<BR>तुषारजलम्, Ki. ix. 5.;<BR>(3) तुहिनम्,<BR>s.-like:<BR>तुहिन-<BR>सदृश (f. शी), Mat.;<BR>(4) प्रालेयम्, s.-cold:<BR>प्रालेयशीत (f. ता), Si. iv. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snow
SNOW (v.):<BR>it s. s:<BR>हिमं etc. पतति (पत्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snowy
SNOWY:<BR>(1) by comp.,<BR>s. mountain:<BR>हिमाद्रिः;<BR>s.-famed:<BR>तुहिनयशस् (mfn.), Mat. 114. 19.;<BR>(2) हैम (f. मी);<BR>(3) महाहिम (f. मा = very s.);<BR>(4) हिमवत् (f. ती = having snow); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snub
SNUB: perh. पराभवति (भू, c. 1.): v. Also to<BR>chide, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snub-nose
SNUB-NOSE:<BR>(1) चिपिटनासा;<BR>(2) नतनासिका।<BR>S. d:<BR>(1) नतनासिक (f. का);<BR>(2) अवटीट (f. टा);<BR>(3) अवनाट (f. टा);<BR>(4) अवभट (f. टा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snuff
SNUFF (subs.):<BR>I Powdered tobacco^1: नस्यम्,<BR>to take s.:<BR>नस्यं गृह्नाति, Bha.<BR>II Burnt<BR>candle-wick: perh. छत्रम्; दग्धवर्तिः।<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snuff
SNUFF (v.):<BR>I To inhale, smell: q. v.<BR>II<BR>to take out s.: छत्रम् अपनयति (नी, c. 1.).<BR>S. out: v. To extinguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snuff-box
SNUFF-BOX:<BR>(1) नस्यधानी;<BR>(2) नस्याधारः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snuffers
SNUFFERS: no prop. equiv.: कर्तरिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snuffle
SNUFFLE (v.): perh. धुरघुरायते (nomi.), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snug
SNUG:<BR>I Compact: q. v.: संहत (f. ता).<BR>II<BR>Secret, retired: q. v.: गूढ (f. ढा).<BR>III<BR>Comfortable, convenient: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snuggle
SNUGGLE: संघृष्य शेते (शी, c. 2.): v. To lie<BR>down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

snugly
SNUGLY:<BR>I Comfortably: सुखेन।<BR>II Closely:<BR>संघृष्य।<BR>III Secretly: गूढम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

so
SO (interj.): तिष्ठ<BR>or<BR>तिष्ठ तिष्ठ (from स्था).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

so
SO (adv. conj.):<BR>I In gen:<BR>(1) तथा, as<BR>Viṣṇu alone is known as the best of men, so the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">Page657</a>]<BR>sages know me (alone)<BR>to be the performer of<BR>hundred sacrifices:<BR>हरिर्यथैकः पुरुषोत्तमः स्मृतः, तथा<BR> विदुर्मां मुनयः शतक्रतुम्, R. iii. 49.;<BR>not so much<BR>before...as:<BR>तथा न पूर्वं॥।यथा, Ki. viii. 41.;<BR>so<BR>scorched by the rays of the sun:<BR>तथातितप्तं<BR> सवितुर्गभस्तिभिः, Ku. v. 21.;<BR>you should act so<BR>that you are not laughed at by men:<BR>तथा प्रयतेथा<BR> यथा नोपहस्यसे जनैः, K.; let him be entirely so:<BR>तथाविधस्तावदशेषमस्तु सः, Ku. v. 82.; be it so:<BR>तथास्तु, Pra. iii.;<BR>(2) एवम्,<BR>as sparks from<BR>burning fire are scattered in every direction, so:<BR>॥।यथाग्नेर्ज्वलतः सर्वा दिशो विस्फुलिङ्गा विप्रतिष्ठेरन्,<BR>S. 10.;<BR>and so of Viṣṇu:<BR>एवं हरेश्च, Li. 241.;<BR>my child, it is so or a (mere)<BR>joke:<BR>अयीदमेवं<BR> परिहासो (वा), Ku. v. 62.;<BR>don't say so:<BR>मा<BR> मैवम्, Mu. i.;<BR>it is so, but...:<BR>एवभेतत्, किन्तु॥।,<BR>Vi. 6.; when the chief of divine sages said so<BR>(i. e. as described above): एवमुक्तवति देवऋषीन्द्रे,<BR>N. v. 37.;<BR>(3) तद्वत् (= in like manner: gen<BR>with यद्वत्), S. iii. 3. 9.<BR>II Of degree:<BR>expr. by words meaning such:<BR>she is so<BR>pretty:<BR>ईदृशं रूपलावण्यम्;<BR>so excellent:<BR>ईदृग्गुणोपेतः<BR>(ता, तं), Ki. xi. 41.;<BR>so insufferable:<BR>ईदृशं<BR> सुदुःसहम्, Ki. i. 43.; of so great-minded men:<BR>तादृशानां महात्मनाम्, K. N.B. so great, so little,<BR>is gen. expr. by sim.<BR>such, his erudition is so<BR>great:<BR>ईदृशं तस्य पाण्डित्यम्; be so good as to... is<BR>expr. by अनुगृह्नाति (= to favour)<BR>or<BR>भद्रतया<BR>(= out of goodness); ever so: v. However.<BR>III = So that: expr. by तथा॥।यथा,<BR>“were let<BR>loose, s. truth be in the field”:<BR>तथा मुच्येरन्<BR> यथा भुवि सत्यमाविर्भवति: v. Also provided<BR>that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

so and so
SO AND SO: अमुकः (की, कं),<BR>of such and such a<BR>king, son of s.:<BR>अमुकपुत्रस्यामुकस्य महीपतेः, Vy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

so-called
SO-CALLED: नामन्, in comp.: v. Name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

so far
SO FAR:<BR>I With<BR>as:<BR>यावत् (f. ती),<BR>so far as<BR>lies in my power:<BR>यावच्छक्तितः, Ka.<BR>II Abs.:<BR>एतावत्<BR>or<BR>इयत् (f. ती), so far and no further:<BR>एतावन्नाधिकम्।<BR>III With from expr. with<BR>आस्ताम् (=let, alone)<BR>or<BR>दूरतः,<BR>far from<BR>seeing:<BR>दूरे तद्दर्शनम्, K. s. 25. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

so forth
SO FORTH: v. So on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

so long
SO LONG:<BR>I Abs.: एतावत्कालम्, and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II With as or in cor. with as long<BR>as: expr. by यावत्॥।तावत्, so l. as I live, I wish<BR>॥।यावत् प्राणिमि तावत्॥।इच्छामि, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

so many
SO MANY:<BR>I Abs.:<BR>(1) इयत् (f. ती):<BR>(2)<BR>एतावत् (f. ती).<BR>II With as many:<BR>(1) तावत्<BR>(f. ती);<BR>(2) तति (in pl. with यति: rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

so much
SO MUCH:<BR>I Adj.: v. Much, so<BR>II Adv.:<BR>(1) ईदृक्;<BR>(2) एतादृक्;<BR>(3) तादृक्<BR>or<BR>तथा (in cor.<BR>with<BR>as:<BR>तादृक् with यादृक् and तथा with यथा),<BR>Arjuna did not regret so m. at the bad omen as for<BR>their emptiness:<BR>तेनानिमित्तेन तथा न पार्थस्तयोर्यथा<BR> रिक्ततयानुतेपे, Ki. xvii. 40.;<BR>(4) by adj.,<BR>those<BR>who ask do not feel so m. shame as those who<BR>give:<BR>न तादृशी भवति याचमानानां यादृशी ददतां लज्जा,<BR>K. Ph.: so m. the better, the worse for him:<BR>perh. एतत्तावच्छोमनम्, अशोभनमेव।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

so on
SO ON, SO FORTH: expr. by -आदि in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

so soon
SO SOON:<BR>I Abs.: v. So (II).<BR>II = As soon:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

so so
SO SO:<BR>I = Well, well: वाढम्।<BR>II Moderate-<BR>-ly, passably: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

so then
SO THEN: अतः: v. Then, therefore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soak
SOAK:<BR>(1) मज्जयति, नि- (c. of मस्ज् = sink):<BR>मज्जयित्वा सितापके, Bha.;<BR>(2) स्थापयति (c. of<BR>स्था= to put), माषाणां दालयस्तोये स्थापितास्त्यक्त-<BR>कञ्चुकाः, Bha. S. through: v. To drench, wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soap
SOAP:<BR>I Subs.: *सावनम्।<BR>II Verb. सावनेन<BR> मार्ष्टि<BR>or<BR>मार्जयति, परि-, सं-, प्र-, (मृज्, c. 2. and<BR>10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soapy
SOAPY:<BR>I Soft: q. v.: स्निग्ध (f. ग्धा).<BR>II<BR>Sneaking: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soar
SOAR (v.): उत्-पतति (पत्, c. 1.): v. To fly<BR>up, rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sob
SOB (v.): फू(फु)त्करोति,<BR>I spoke s. bing:<BR>फुत्कृत्य<BR> तमवदम्, K. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sob
SOB,-BING (subs.):<BR>(1) फुत्कारः;<BR>(2) फूत्कृतम्;<BR>(3) गद्गदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sobbingly
SOBBINGLY:<BR>(1) फू(फु)त्कृत्य;<BR>(2) गद्गदगिरा and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sober
SOBER:<BR>I Not addicted to drinking: न पान-<BR>प्रसक्त (f. क्ता) and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Not<BR>drunk: न मत्त (f. त्ता), क्षीव (f. वा)<BR>III [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">Page658</a>]<BR>Calm, quiet q. v.: शान्त (f. न्ता).<BR>IV<BR>Grave, sedate: q. v.: धीर, गम्भीर (f. रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soberly
SOBERLY:<BR>I Calmly, coolly: expr. by adj.:<BR>शान्त (f. न्ता).<BR>II Discreetly, gravely:<BR>विविच्य।<BR>III Moderately: भितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soberness
SOBERNESS, SOBRIETY:<BR>I Temperance: q. v.:<BR>संयमः।<BR>II Calmness, gravity: q. v.: धैर्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sobriquet
SOBRIQUET: उपनामन् (n.): v. Also nickname.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sociability
SOCIABILITY, SOCIABLENESS:<BR>(1) सङ्गप्रियता (of<BR>men in general);<BR>(2) मधुरालापिता (= affa-<BR>-bility);<BR>(3) संसर्गार्हता (= fitness to be associa-<BR>-ted).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sociable
SOCIABLE:<BR>(1) सङ्गप्रिय (f. या) and sim. comp.s.<BR>(= fond of society);<BR>(2) मधुरालापिन् (f. नी =<BR>affable: q. v.);<BR>(3) संसर्गार्ह (f. र्हा), and<BR>sim. comp.s. (= fit to be associated).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

social
SOCIAL:<BR>I Pertaining to society:<BR>(1) by<BR>comp.;<BR>(2) सामाजिक (f. की).<BR>II Sociable:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

socialist
SOCIALIST: *समसंसर्गवादिन् (f. नी), and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

society
SOCIETY:<BR>I Association: q. v.: सङ्गः,<BR>fondness<BR>for s. of good men:<BR>सत्संगप्रियता, Vi. ii. 22.<BR>II<BR>Social union:<BR>(1) समाजः;<BR>(2) समवायः,<BR>III<BR>For particular purpose:<BR>(1) समाजः,<BR>s. of<BR>sages:<BR>ऋषीणां समाजः, P. i.;<BR>(2) समितिः,<BR>addressed the s.:<BR>समितिं बभाषे, Bh. xii. 13.;<BR>(3)<BR>सदस् (n.),<BR>eloquence in s.:<BR>सदसि वाक्पटुता, H.;<BR>(4) सभा;<BR>(5) समज्या;<BR>(6) परिषद्<BR>or<BR>संसद् (f);<BR>(7) समित्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sock
SOCK: *पादावरणम्, and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

socket
SOCKET: आधारः (=receptacle: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sod
SOD: शाद्वलम्,<BR>covered with s.<BR>शाद्वल (f. ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soda
SODA: *क्षारकः,<BR>s. -water:<BR>क्षारोदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sodality
SODALITY: बन्धुता: v. Fellowship, fraternity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sodomite
SODOMITE:<BR>(1) पुंसि मैथुनकारिन् (m.);<BR>(2) पुरुष-<BR>मेहिन् (m.): etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sodomy
SODOMY:<BR>(1) पुंसि मैथुनम्, M. xi. 68.,<BR>or<BR>-गमनम्,<BR>V. s.;<BR>(2) पुरुषमेहः। Y. ii. 298.;<BR>(3) गुदमैथुनम्,<BR>K. b.; and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sofa
SOFA: पर्यङ्कः (a sort of s.): v. Seat(1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soft
SOFT:<BR>(1) मृदु (f. also द्वी = mild, gentle: q. v.),<BR>s. like the accasia:<BR>शिरीषमृद्वी, Br. vi. 34.;<BR>s. by<BR>nature but still strong:<BR>मृदु प्रकृत्या च ससारमेव च,<BR>Ku. v. 19.;<BR>(2) कोमल (f. ला),<BR>soft-feathered<BR>bed:<BR>हंसतूलगर्भकोमलशय्या, D. ii.; s. style:<BR>कोमला रीतिः, Kav. ix.;<BR>(3) मृदुल (f. ला = 1),<BR>s. flower:<BR>मृदुलं पुष्पम्, M. n.;<BR>(4) पेलव (f. वा:<BR>rare), Ku. v. 4.;<BR>(5) स्निग्ध (= smooth,<BR>glossy: as of s. words);<BR>(6) श्लक्ष्ण (f. क्ष्णा)<BR>: v. Smooth;<BR>(7) मधुर (f. रा): v. Sweet;<BR>(8) मसृण (f. णा = 5),<BR>s. steps:<BR>मसृणचरणपातः,<BR>Ma. n. iii. 18.;<BR>s. mouthed:<BR>मसृणवाणी,<BR>Gi. x. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soft
SOFT (adv.): v. Softly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soften
SOFTEN:<BR>(1) आर्द्रीकरोति (= melt: q. v.),<BR>his<BR>heart being softened:<BR>आर्द्रीकृतहृदयः, K.;<BR>(2)<BR>expr. by adj. or nomi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

softly
SOFTLY:<BR>(1) मृदु;<BR>(2) कोमलम्;<BR>(3) मृदुलम्;<BR>(4)<BR>पेलवम्;<BR>(5) स्निग्धम्;<BR>(6) श्लक्ष्णम्;<BR>(7) मधुरम्;<BR>(8) मसृणम्: v. Soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

softness
SOFTNESS:<BR>(1) मृदुलता<BR>or<BR>मार्दवम्, s. of Brāhmins:<BR>बाह्मण्यमार्दवम्, P.;<BR>(2) कोमलता;<BR>(3) मृदुलता;<BR>(4) पेलवता;<BR>(5) स्निग्धता;<BR>(6) श्लक्ष्णता<BR>or<BR>मधुरता;<BR>(7) माधुर्यम्;<BR>(8) मसृणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soho
SOHO (interj.): हंहो: v. O.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soil
SOIL (subs.):<BR>I Ground: भूमिः<BR>or<BR>भूः, good s.:<BR>उत्कृष्टभूमिः, K. ii. p.;<BR>rich s.:<BR>सारवती भूः, गुणवती<BR> भूमिः, Ka. ix. 18., iv. 50.;<BR>gravelly, stony,<BR>snaky s. is no s.:<BR>सशर्क्ररा सपाषाणा सव्याला चेति<BR> भूरभूः, Ka. iv. 53.;<BR>s. whose irrigation does not<BR>depend on heaven:<BR>अदेवमातृका भूः, Ka, iv. 52.;<BR>native s.:<BR>जन्मभूमिः: v. Land, earth.<BR>II<BR>Dirt, stain, dung: q. v.: मलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soil
SOIL (v.):<BR>I To stain, pollute: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>मलिनयति (nomi.), dust does not s. (it): न रजांसि<BR> मलिनयन्ति;<BR>(2) कलुषयति।<BR>II To manure:<BR>सारं ददाति (दा, c. 3.: with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sojourn
SOJOURN: अवतिष्ठते (स्था, c. 1.: v. To reside,<BR>stay).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sojourn
SOJOURN, -ING (subs.):<BR>(1) आस्थानम्;<BR>(2) अव-<BR>स्थितिः: v. Stay, residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sojourner
SOJOURNER:<BR>(1) अवस्थायिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) आगन्तुक<BR>(f. का = new comer).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solace
SOLACE:<BR>I Subs.: सा(शा)न्त्वनम्, -ना: v. Con-<BR>-solation, comfort.<BR>II Verb: शा(सा)न्त्वयति, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">Page659</a>]<BR>उप-, परि- [शा(सा)न्त्व्, c. 10.: v. To con-<BR>-sole].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soland
SOLAND or SOLAN-GOOSE: हंसविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solar
SOLAR:<BR>(1) by comp.,<BR>s. dynasty:<BR>सूर्यवंशः;<BR>s. day:<BR>सूर्याहः, Gan.;<BR>s. rays:<BR>अर्ककिरणाः, Vi.;<BR>(2) सौर (f. री);<BR>(3) सावन (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solder
SOLDER:<BR>I Verb: संदधाति (धा, c. 3.).<BR>II<BR>Subs.: सन्धिः: v. Also cement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soldier
SOLDIER:<BR>(1) सैन्यः (rare),<BR>march of s. s:<BR>सैन्य-<BR>निर्याणम्, Mah.;<BR>(2) सैनिकः,<BR>with the cheers of<BR>the s. s:<BR>सैनिकहर्षनिःस्वनैः, R. iii. 61.;<BR>(3) योधः<BR>(= fighting man), surrounded by various s. s:<BR>वृतो बहुविधैर्योधैः, Mah.;<BR>(4) मटः (= warrior);<BR>(5) चमूचरः and sim. comp.s (of a regiment:<BR>rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soldier-like
SOLDIER-LIKE, SOLDIERLY:<BR>I Like a soldier:<BR>expr. with सैनिकवत्<BR>or<BR>सैनिक इव।<BR>II Brave,<BR>martial: q. v.:<BR>s. conduct:<BR>भटता<BR>or<BR>भाट्यम्,<BR>Vi. vi. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soldiery
SOLDIERY:<BR>(1) सेना,<BR>encampment of s.:<BR>सेना-<BR>निवेशः, R.;<BR>(2) सैन्यम्,<BR>armed s.:<BR>युक्तं सैन्यम्,<BR>Mah. iv. 19. 32.;<BR>(3) बलम्: v. Force, army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sole
SOLE (adj.);<BR>(1) एक (f. का): v. Only;<BR>(2)<BR>एकमात्र (f. त्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sole
SOLE (subs.):<BR>I Of the foot: चरणतलम् and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR>II Of shoe: पादुकातलम् (?).<BR>III A fish: मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solecism
SOLECISM:<BR>(1) संस्कारच्युतिः, and sim. comp.s;<BR>(2) by adj.: च्युतसंस्कार (f. रा)<BR>or<BR>च्युतसंस्कृति<BR>(mfn.), Kav.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solecist
SOLECIST: च्युतसंस्कारपदप्रयोक्तृ (f. क्त्री), and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solely
SOLELY:<BR>(1) by adj. एक एव (f. एकैव, n. एकमेव);<BR>(2) एकमात्रम्: v. Also alone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solemn
SOLEMN:<BR>(1) पुण्य (f. ण्या=holy, sacred: q. v.);<BR>(2) गम्भीर (f. रा = grave, serious: q. v.).<BR>Ph.:<BR>on s. occasions^1:<BR>यात्रोत्सवादिषु, D. ii.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solemnity
SOLEMNITY:<BR>I Ceremony, rite: q. v.: क्रिया।<BR>II Gravity: q. v.: गाम्मीर्यम्।<BR>III Sacred-<BR>-ness: q. v.: पवित्रता।<BR>IV Pomp: डम्बरः, आ-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solemnize
SOLEMNIZE:<BR>I To perform, celebrate: q. v.:<BR>(1) अनुतिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.);<BR>(2) सम्पादयति (c.<BR>of पद्).<BR>II To dignify: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solemenly
SOLEMENLY:<BR>I As ordained, formally:<BR>(1)<BR>यथाविधि;<BR>(2) यथाशास्त्रम्;<BR>(3) विधिवत्।<BR>II<BR>Gravely, seriously: q. v.: धीरम्।<BR>III With<BR>pomp: सावम्बरम्, s. accepted (her)<BR>hand:<BR>जग्राह-<BR>विधिवत्पाणी, Mah. i. 70. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solicit
SOLICIT:<BR>(1) याचते (याच्, c. 1.): v. To beg:<BR>(2) नाथति, -ते, (नाथ्, c. 1.: rare),<BR>who does<BR>not s. the lord:<BR>नाथन्ति के नाम न लोकनाथम्, N. iii.<BR>25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solicitation
SOLICITATION:<BR>(1) याच्ञा;<BR>(2) प्रार्थना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solicitor
SOLICITOR:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) याचक (f. चिका);<BR>(2) अर्थिन् (f. नी) प्र-, अमि,<BR>although he expressed<BR>that he was a s.:<BR>अर्थित्वे प्रकटीकृतेऽपि, Vi. ii. 9.;<BR>(3) अभ्यर्थिन् (f. नी);<BR>(4) प्रार्थयितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(5) अभ्यर्थयितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(6) याचितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(7) वनीयक (f. यिका: rare).<BR>III In law:<BR>*समर्थयितृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solicitor-general
SOLICITOR-GENERAL: *व्यवहारसचिवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solicitous
SOLICITOUS: व्यग्र (f. ग्रा): v. Anxious,<BR>eager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solicitously
SOLICITOUSLY: व्यग्रम्: v. Anxiously, eagerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solicitude
SOLICITUDE: व्यग्रता: v. Anxiety, eagerness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solid
SOLID (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: स्थूल (f. ला),<BR>s. geome-<BR>try:<BR>*स्थूलज्यामितिः।<BR>II Substantial, valid:<BR>q. v.: सारवत् (f. ती).<BR>III Compact: q. v.:<BR>संहत (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solid
SOLID (subs.):<BR>(1) perh. स्थूलम्;<BR>(2) स्थूलपदार्थः<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solidly
SOLIDLY:<BR>(1) दृढम्: v. Firmly;<BR>(2) गमीरम्:<BR>v. Deeply;<BR>(3) सम्यक्: v. Thoroughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soliloquy
SOLILOQUY (subs.), SOLILOQUIZE (v.): expr.<BR>with स्वगतम्<BR>or<BR>आत्मगतम् (= to one's self),<BR>“अश्राव्यं खलु यद्वस्तु तदिह स्वगतं मतम्”, Sah. vi.:<BR>v. To say, saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solitarily
SOLITARILY:<BR>(1) by adj.: एकाकिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) विविक्तम् (= in seclusion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solitariness
SOLITARINESS:<BR>(1) विविक्तता: v. Seclusion;<BR>(3) एकाकिता (= state of being alone);<BR>(3)<BR>रहस् (= secrecy: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solitary
SOLITARY:<BR>I Single, one: q. v.: एक (f. का).<BR>II Retired, lonely: q. v.:<BR>(1) विविक्त (f.<BR>क्ता);<BR>(2) निर्जन (f. ना=unpopulated).<BR>III<BR>Living alone:<BR>(1) एकाकिन् (f. नी), although [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">Page660</a>]<BR>they were s.:<BR>एकाकिनोऽपि, Si. ii. 4.;<BR>why do<BR>you lead a s. life in this lonely forest:<BR>किमेकाकिनी<BR> वनमिदमधिवससि, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solitude
SOLITUDE:<BR>I Lonely place:<BR>(1) विविक्तम्;<BR>(2) निर्जनं<BR>or<BR>विविक्तं स्थानम् and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Loneliness:<BR>(1) विविक्तता;<BR>(2) निर्जनता,<BR>etc.<BR>III Lonely life:<BR>(1) एकाकिता;<BR>(2) by<BR>circumlo.,<BR>you have adopted s.:<BR>अङ्गीकृतमरण्या-<BR>वस्थानम्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solo
SOLO: द्विपदी, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solstice
SOLSTICE:<BR>(1) अयनान्तः, Su. xii. 51.;<BR>(2) अयन-<BR>सन्धिः, com.;<BR>(3) अयनम् (अयने दक्षिणोत्तरायणसन्धौ,<BR>com. Su. iii. 11.).<BR>The summer s.:<BR>कर्कटसंक्रान्तिः;<BR>the winter s.:<BR>मकरसंक्रान्तिः, Su. xiv. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solstitial
SOLSTITIAL: expr. by comp. s. point: v. Sol-<BR>-stice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solubility
SOLUBILITY:<BR>(1) द्राव्यता;<BR>(2) विलयनीयता;<BR>(3)<BR>गालनीयता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soluble
SOLUBLE:<BR>(1) द्राव्य (f. व्या), वि-, सं-;<BR>(2) विल-<BR>यनीय (f. या);<BR>(3) गालनीय (f. या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solution
SOLUTION:<BR>I Dissolution: द्रावणम्;<BR>(2) विल-<BR>यनम्;<BR>(3) गालनम्।<BR>II<BR>(1) क्वाथः (= decoction),<BR>s. of Vāsaka:<BR>वासकः क्वाथः, Śāraṅgadhara;<BR>(2) रसः, “गृहीत्वा तं रसं पूतं गव्येन पयसा सह,” C. s.<BR>III Explanation, exposition: q. v.: साधनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solve
SOLVE:<BR>(1) साधयति (c. of सिध्),<BR>what is to be<BR>s. d:<BR>साध्यम्, K. d.;<BR>(2) व्याकरोति: v. To<BR>expound;<BR>(3) उत्तरं वदति (वद्, c. 1. = to<BR>reply). Ph.:<BR>to s. doubt:<BR>संशयं छिनत्ति (छिद्,<BR>c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solvency
SOLVENCY:<BR>(1) वित्तवत्ता;<BR>(2) समृद्धता: v.<BR>Riches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

solvent
SOLVENT:<BR>(1) Able to pay claims:<BR>(1) वित्त-<BR>वत् (f. ती = rich),<BR>if a surety is s.:<BR>प्रतिभूर्यदि<BR> वित्तवान्, Mit.;<BR>(2) समृद्ध (f. द्धा = affluent).<BR>II Capable of dissolving: द्रावण (f. णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sombre
SOMBRE: मलिन (f. ना): v. Dark, gloomy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

some
SOME:<BR>(1) कोऽपि (कापि, किमपि = certain),<BR>s.<BR>body informs s. one from s. place:<BR>कुतोऽपि कोऽपि<BR> कमपि पुरषविशेषमवगमयति, Mu. v.;<BR>thinking s.<BR>thing or other:<BR>किमपि किमपि मन्त्रयन्, V. ii.;<BR>(2)<BR>कश्चित् (काचित्, किञ्चित् = 1. also = few, short),<BR>wait s. time:<BR>कालः कश्चित् प्रतीक्ष्यताम्, K. ii. 34.;<BR>s. recited eulogistic hymns of the Rig Veda:<BR>केचिदृचः स्तुतिचतुराः समुदाहरन्, C. i.;<BR>(3) कश्चन<BR>(काचन, किञ्चन = 2.: rare);<BR>(4) एके (pl.: in<BR>opposition to others, G. § 307. d.),<BR>of s.<BR>systems:<BR>एकेषां शाखिनाम्, S.;<BR>(5) कतिचित् (pl.<BR>= few),<BR>it will take s. days:<BR>तत्र कतिचिद्दिनानि<BR> गमिष्यन्ति, P. iii. 11.;<BR>(6) कतिपयः (या, यं),<BR>after s. days:<BR>गतेषु कतिपयदिनेषु, D.;<BR>(7) कियत्<BR>(f. ती: rare),<BR>in s. points silent:<BR>कियत्सु<BR> मौनम्, N. ix. 15.;<BR>(8) कियानपि, etc., M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

somehow
SOMEHOW:<BR>(1) कथमपि,<BR>s. or other it has fallen<BR>from this tree:<BR>कथमपि तरुशिखरादस्मात्परिच्युतः,<BR>K.;<BR>(2) केनापि<BR>or<BR>केनचित् प्रकारेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

somersault
SOMERSAULT, SOMERSET: perh.: मत्स्योद्वर्तनम् or<BR>ऊर्द्ध पादलङ्घनम्, D. viii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sometime
SOMETIME:<BR>I Formerly: q. v.: पूर्वम्।<BR>II At<BR>one time:<BR>(1) एकदा;<BR>(2) कदाचित्, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sometimes
SOMETIMES:<BR>(1) कदाचित् (rarely कदाचन),<BR>s. at<BR>Ujyayinī. s. at Hemakūṭa:<BR>कदाचिदुज्जयिन्यां<BR> कदाचिद्धेमकूटे, K.;<BR>do the faults of Chandragupta<BR>s. remind his subjects of......:<BR>अपि कदाचिच्चन्द्र-<BR>गुप्तदोषाः स्मारयन्ति॥॥॥प्रकृतीः, Mu. i.;<BR>(2) क्वचित्,<BR>s. poison acts as nectar:<BR>विषमप्यमृतं क्वचिद्भवेत्,<BR>R. viii. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

somewhat
SOMEWHAT (subs.): expr. with किञ्चित्: v.<BR>Somewhat (adv.), little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

somewhat
SOMEWHAT (adv.):<BR>(1) किञ्चित्, s. ashamed:<BR>किञ्चिदुपजातलज्जः, K.: v. Little;<BR>(2) by doubl-<BR>-ing adj.s,<BR>s. afraid:<BR>भीतभीतः (ता, तं), Ki.<BR>xiv. 65.;<BR>s. alarmed:<BR>चकितचकितम्, Me. i.<BR>14.;<BR>s. transparent:<BR>अच्छाच्छ (f. च्छा), K.;<BR>(3) rarely by affixes, -जातीय (f. या), -कल्प<BR>(f. ल्पा), -देश्य (f. श्या), -देशीय (f. या) to<BR>adj. s,<BR>s. clever:<BR>पटुजातीयः (या, यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

somewhere
SOMEWHERE:<BR>I In or to some place:<BR>(1)<BR>क्वापि,<BR>s. else:<BR>अन्यत्र क्वापि, Ra.;<BR>(2) कुत्रापि;<BR>(3) क्वचित्, -अपि;<BR>(4) कुत्रचित्, -अपि।<BR>II From<BR>s.: कुतश्चित्<BR>or<BR>कुतोऽपि;<BR>from s. else:<BR>अन्यतः<BR> कुतश्चित्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

somnambulism
SOMNAMBULISM: (?)<BR>(1) निद्राचारः;<BR>(2) स्वप्नचारः,<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

somnambulist
SOMNAMBULIST:<BR>(1) निद्राचारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2)<BR>निद्राचर (f. री) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

somnolence
SOMNOLENCE, SOMNOLENCY: निद्रालुता: v.<BR>Drowsiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

somnolent
SOMNOLENT: निद्रालु (mfn.): v. Sleepy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

son
SON:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पुत्रः,<BR>which those who have<BR>s. s get:<BR>पुत्रिणो यां व्रजन्ति वै, Mah. i. 12. 24.;<BR>by my eldest s. Yadu:<BR>ममज्येष्ठेन यदुना, Mah. i. 83.<BR>24.;<BR>(2) सुतः;<BR>(3) सूनुः;<BR>(4) तनयः;<BR>(5) नन्दनः;<BR>(6) आत्मजः and sim. comp.s.: ‘भास्करस्यात्म-<BR>सम्भवः,” Mah.;<BR>(7) सन्ततिः (=offspring),<BR>we have one s.:<BR>अस्माकं सन्ततिस्त्वेकः, Mah. i.<BR>12. 18.;<BR>(8) प्रजा (=7),<BR>child, your s. s will<BR>not inherit the kingdom:<BR>तस्मादराज्यमाक् तात प्रजा<BR> तव भविष्यति, Mah. i. 82. 9.;<BR>(9) by deriv.,<BR>s. of<BR>Daśaratha:<BR>दाशरथिः;<BR>s. s of Kuru:<BR>कौरवाः। Ph.:<BR>s. of men:<BR>मनुष्यजन्मन् (m.), Si. i. 35.<BR>II A<BR>native: q. v.: expr. by deriv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

son-in-law
SON-IN-LAW: जामातृ (m.), “जामातुराश्रमम्”,<BR>U. i. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

song
SONG:<BR>(1) गीतम्,<BR>at the end of the song:<BR>गीतान्ते,<BR>Mal. ii.;<BR>fond of s. s:<BR>प्रियगीत (f. ता), K.;<BR>s. s of Govinda:<BR>गीतगोविन्दम्, Gi.;<BR>intent to hear<BR>their s. s:<BR>तद्गीतश्रवणैकाग्रा, K. xv. 66.;<BR>by the<BR>auspicious s. s of bees:<BR>भृङ्गावलीमङ्गलगीतनादैः, P. h.;<BR>(2) गीतिः,<BR>by auspicious eulogistic s. s:<BR>स्तुतिगीति-<BR>मङ्गलैः, Ki. i. 38.; गीत्या देवं विरूपाक्षमुपवीणयन्ति,<BR>K.;<BR>(3) गानम्,<BR>dry s.:<BR>शुष्कं गानम्, Sah. vi.;<BR>consisting of s.;<BR>गानात्मक (f. त्मिका), Say.;<BR>(4) रुतम् (= cry: q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

songster
SONGSTER, SONGSTRESS:<BR>(1) गायक (f. यिका);<BR>(2) गायन (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sonless
SONLESS: अपुत्र (f. त्रा) and sim. comp. s: v.<BR>Childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sonnet
SONNET:<BR>(1) गीतिका;<BR>(2) गाथा: v. Song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sonorous
SONOROUS:<BR>I Lit.; विराविन् (f. णी);<BR>(2)<BR>शब्दन (f. ना).<BR>II Melodious, sweet: q. v.:<BR>मधुर (f. रा).<BR>III Clear: q. v.: स्पष्ट<BR>(f. ष्टा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sonorously
SONOROUSLY:<BR>(1) मधुरम्: v. Sweetly;<BR>(2)<BR>स्पष्टम्: v. Clearly;<BR>(3) उच्चैः: v. Loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sonship
SONSHIP:<BR>(1) पुत्रत्वम्;<BR>(2) पुत्रावस्था (the state);<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soon
SOON:<BR>I Without delay, early: अचिरेण or<BR>अचिरात्, they will be s. separated from us:<BR>पृथगस्मादचिरेण भाविता तैः, Si. ii. 116.;<BR>it will very<BR>s. bear fruit also:<BR>अयमचिरादेव फलोन्मुखोऽपि मविता,<BR>Vi. vi.<BR>II Quickly, speedily:<BR>(1) आशु,<BR>as s.<BR>the king ordered:<BR>यावदादिशति पार्थिवः॥॥॥तावदाशु,<BR>R. xi. 3.;<BR>(2) शीघ्रम्;<BR>(3) क्षिप्रम्;<BR>(4) तूर्णम्;<BR>s. covered the ground:<BR>तूर्णं प्यधुर्वसुमतीम्, Si. v. 4.;<BR>(5) द्रुतम्, B.;<BR>(6) त्वरितम्<BR>or<BR>सत्वरम् (=hastily).<BR>Ph.: (a) as s. as: q. v.: (b) as s. (= will-<BR>-ingly, readily) कामम्: v. Rather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sooner
SOONER:<BR>I Rather: q. v.: वरम्।<BR>II Earlier:<BR>ph.:<BR>s. or latter:<BR>अद्य श्वो वा।<BR>III More<BR>easily: expr. by circumlo.,<BR>it is s. said than<BR>done:<BR>वक्तुमिदं सुकरं न तु कर्तुम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soot
SOOT:<BR>(1) कज्जलम् (?);<BR>(2) किट्टम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sooth
SOOTH:<BR>in s.:<BR>सत्यम्: v. Truly, indeed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soothe
SOOTHE:<BR>(1) प्रसादयति (c. of सद्: v. To<BR>console);<BR>(2) शमयति (c. of शम्: v. To<BR>alleviate, mitigate): v. Also to satisfy,<BR>caress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soothing
SOOTHING (adj.):<BR>I Of medicines: शमन (f.<BR>नी), प्र-,<BR>s. the pangs of spleen:<BR>प्लीहार्तिशमनी,<BR>Bha.;<BR>(2) शान्तिकर (f. री);<BR>(3) शान्तिप्रद (f.<BR>दा).<BR>II Sweet: मधुर (f. रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soothingly
SOOTHINGLY:<BR>(1) मधुरम्: v. Sweetly;<BR>(2)<BR>by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soothsayer
SOOTHSAYER: दैवज्ञः: v. Fortune-teller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soothsaying
SOOTHSAYING: क्षुभाशुभकथनम्: v. Also prophecy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sooty
SOOTY:<BR>I Lit. कज्जवलमय (f. यीः (?).<BR>II Like<BR>soot: धूमशयाम (f. मा) and sim. comp.s., C. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sop
SOP:<BR>I Lit.: perh. पिण्डः।<BR>II Fig.: आमिषम्:<BR>v. Food, meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sophism
SOPHISM, SOPHISTRY:<BR>(1) हेत्वाभासः;<BR>(2) युत्तया-<BR>भासः,<BR>thus many rely on arguments of s. s:<BR>एवं<BR> बहवो युक्तिवाक्यतदाभाससमाश्रयाः, S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sophist
SOPHIST: हेत्वाभासवादिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sophistic
SOPHISTIC, SOPHISTICAL: by comp.s; s. argu-<BR>ment: v. Sophism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sophisticated
SOPHISTICATED: v. Adulterated, false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soporiferous
SOPORIFEROUS, SOPORIFIC:<BR>(1) स्वापन (f. नी);<BR>(2) निद्राजनन (f. नी) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sorcerer
SORCERER, SORCERESS:<BR>(1) ऐन्द्रजालिक (f. की):<BR>v. Magician;<BR>(2) मायाकर (f. री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sorcery
SORCERY:<BR>(1) ऐन्द्रजालम्: v. Magic;<BR>(2)<BR>माया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sordid
SORDID:<BR>(1) कृपण (f. णा): v. Mean, niggard-<BR>-ly;<BR>(2) कुत्सित (f. ता): v. Filthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sordidness
SORDIDNESS:<BR>(1) कार्पण्यम्: v. Meanness;<BR>कुत्सितता: v. Filthiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sore
SORE (subs.):<BR>(1) क्षतम्,<BR>when the mind is deeply<BR>s. d:<BR>गाढं क्षते मनसि, Sr.: v. Injury, abscess,<BR>hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sore
SORE (adj.):<BR>(1) सरुज (f. जा =giving pain);<BR>(2) कष्ट (f. ष्टा= distressing);<BR>(3) उग्र (f. ग्रा<BR>=violent: q. v.): v. Painful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sore
SORE, SORELY: भृशम्: v. Violently, exceed-<BR>-ingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soreness
SORENESS:<BR>I Painfulness: q. v.: सरुजता।<BR>II<BR>Intensity, violence: q. v.: तीव्रता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sorites
SORITES: निगमनम् (?), N. d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sorrel
SORREL:<BR>(1) चुक्रा (the Indian s.);<BR>(2) चुक्रः,<BR>Wilson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sorrow
SORROW (subs.):<BR>(1) शोकः,<BR>he who is affected<BR>by s. is called a coward:<BR>यं शोकः समभिमवति तं<BR> कापुरुषमाचक्षते, C. vi.;<BR>(2) शुच्,<BR>should not give<BR>way to s.:<BR>शुचो वशं गन्तुं नार्हसि, K. viii. 90.;<BR>(3)<BR>सन्तापः (distress),<BR>although knowing the cause<BR>of your s.:<BR>तव विद्वानपि तापकारणम्, K. viii. 76.;<BR>(4) मन्युः (ambiguous),<BR>the speed of s. was<BR>slackened:<BR>शिथिलीभूतो मन्युवेगः, C. vii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sorrow
SORROW (v.): शोचति (शुच्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>grieve, lament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sorrowful
SORROWFUL:<BR>I Full of sorrow:<BR>(1) शोकार्त<BR>(f. र्ता);<BR>(2) सशोक (f. का);<BR>(3) शोकान्वित<BR>(f. ता);<BR>(4) शोकोपहत (f. ता);<BR>(4) शोकोपसृष्ट<BR>(f. ष्टा), and sim. comp.s: v. Also sad.<BR>II Wretched, lamentable: q. v.: शोच्य<BR>(f. च्या)<BR>or<BR>शोचनीय (f. या), परि-, अनु-, सं-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sorrowfully
SORROWFULLY:<BR>(1) सशोकम्;<BR>(2) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sorry
SORRY:<BR>I Grieved, sad:<BR>(1) दुःखित (f. ता),<BR>one who is s. sheds tears:<BR>दुःखितस्याश्रुपातः, Ve.<BR>iii.;<BR>it makes me s.:<BR>अदो दुःखाकरोति माम्, Si.<BR>ii. 12.;<BR>(2) सन्तप्त, अनु- (f. प्ता). To be s.:<BR>v. To repent. To make s.: v. To grieve.<BR>II Poor, wretched;<BR>(1) क्षुद्र (f. द्रा);<BR>(2)<BR>कु- in comp.: v. Bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sort
SORT:<BR>I Subs.: प्रकारः: v. Kind, manner.<BR>Ph.: out of s. s: fig.: असुस्थ (f. स्था): v.<BR>Unwell.<BR>II Trans.: विन्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.):<BR>v. To arrange.<BR>III Intrans.: युज्यते (pass.<BR>of युज्): v. To suit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sorter
SORTER: विन्यस्तृ (f. स्त्री): v. Arranger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sortie
SORTIE: perh.: अवस्कन्दः,<BR>to make a s.:<BR>अव-<BR>स्कन्दति (स्कन्द्, c. 1.), Mal. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sot
SOT, SOTTISH:<BR>I Drunkard; q. v.: पानमूढ<BR>(f. ढा).<BR>II Foolish: q. v.: मूढ (f. ढा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sottishly
SOTTISHLY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sottishness
SOTTISHNESS:<BR>I Drunkenness: पानप्रसक्तिः।<BR>II<BR>Foolishness: मूढता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soul
SOUL:<BR>I The spiritual part:<BR>(1) आत्मन् (m.),<BR>with (their)<BR>whole s.:<BR>सर्वात्मनैव, N. xi. 2.;<BR>you are my s., heart, my life:<BR>त्वमात्मा मे मनः<BR> प्राणाः, B. v.;<BR>individual s.:<BR>प्रत्यगात्मा;<BR>animat-<BR>ing s.:<BR>जीवात्मा;<BR>rational s.:<BR>चिदात्मा; pure<BR>(universal)<BR>s.:<BR>परमात्मा;<BR>(2) जीवः (animating<BR>s.);<BR>s. the chief minister of life:<BR>जीवो मुखयप्राण-<BR>सचिवः, S.<BR>II Heart, mind: q. v.: हृदयम्।<BR>III A person: q. v.: not expr.,<BR>not a single<BR>s. returned:<BR>नैकोऽपि निववृते;<BR>good s.s:<BR>भद्रमुखाः;<BR>poor s.:<BR>मन्दमतिः; etc.<BR>IV Fig., leader,<BR>inspirer:<BR>(1) जीवनम् (=life: q. v.);<BR>(2)<BR>बलम् (= force: q. v.).<BR>V Essence, chief<BR>part: q. v.: सारः।<BR>VI After death:<BR>(1)<BR>जीवः;<BR>(2) प्रेतः (= dead, departed s.);<BR>(3)<BR>Sometimes not expr., “यागाद्यनुष्ठायिनामेवोत्तरेण<BR> पथा गमनम्”, S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sound
SOUND (subs.):<BR>I Noise: q. v.:<BR>(1) शब्दः,<BR>the attribute of s. is applied to object emitting<BR>s. s:<BR>शब्दिषु शब्दधर्मश्चर्यते, M.n. on Si. v. 58.;<BR>(2) ध्वनिः,<BR>by the s. of drums:<BR>पटहध्वनिभिः, R.<BR>ix. 71.;<BR>(3) नादः, heart and ear rending s. s:<BR>हृदयश्रोत्रभिन्नादः, Si.;<BR>(4) स्वनः, निः-, emitted s.:<BR>स्वनमतुनत, Si. vi. 67.;<BR>(5) ह्नादः, निर्-,<BR>s. of<BR>kettle-drums:<BR>दुन्दुभीनां ह्नादः, Ki. viii. 16.<BR>II<BR>Note: q. v. स्वरः।<BR>III Narrow-sea: *सन्धि-<BR>सागरः।<BR>IV A fish: सिन्धुः।<BR>V A probe:<BR>perh. एषणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sound
SOUND (v. i.):<BR>(1) ध्वनति, प्र- (ध्वन्, c. 1.),<BR>s. ed<BR>making the quarters re-s.:<BR>दध्वान ध्वनयन्नाशाः, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">Page663</a>]<BR>Mah.;<BR>drums s. ed being beaten:<BR>पणवा दध्वनुर्हताः,<BR>Bh. xiv. 3.;<BR>(2) नदति, नि-, प्र-, अभि-, वि-, (नद्,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>musical instruments s. ing:<BR>नदत्सु तूर्येषु,<BR>R. vii. 38.;<BR>(3) शब्दं करोति, etc.,<BR>s. ing like<BR>clouds:<BR>अम्बुदनादिन् (f. नी), Ki.: v. Also<BR>Roar, tinkle, murmur, cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sound
SOUND (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: expr. by causal:<BR>s. ing the bow:<BR>चापं प्रध्वनट्य, Ki. xvii. 10.<BR>II<BR>To test, examine: q. v.: परीक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.).<BR>III To celebrate, promulgate: q. v.:<BR>घोषयति (c. of घुष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sound
SOUND (adj.):<BR>I In good condition: सुस्थ<BR>(f. स्था).<BR>II Good, pure: q. v.: सारवत् (f.<BR>ती).<BR>III Severe: q. v.: गुरु (f. also<BR>र्वी).<BR>IV Deep, profound: q. v.: गभीर<BR>(f. रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soundly
SOUNDLY:<BR>(1) सम्यक्: v. Thoroughly;<BR>(2)<BR>गाढम्: v. Chiefly, profoundly;<BR>(3) भृशम्:<BR>v. Severely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soundness
SOUNDNESS:<BR>I Healthiness: q. v.: सुस्थता।<BR>II Goodness, purity: q. v.: सारवत्ता।<BR>III<BR>Profundity: q. v.: गभीरता।<BR>IV Rectitude,<BR>orthodoxy: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

soup
SOUP: जूषः, Bha.: v. Broth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sour
SOUR (adj.):<BR>I Acid:<BR>unripe mango is s. but<BR>tasty:<BR>आम्रमाममम्लं स्वादु, Bha.;<BR>somewhat s.<BR>and sweet:<BR>ईषदम्लञ्च मधुरम्, Bha.<BR>III Fig.,<BR>harsh, bitter: q. v.: कर्कश (f. शा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sour
SOUR (v.):<BR>I Lit.: अम्लीकरोति।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>रुक्षीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

source
SOURCE:<BR>(1) प्रभवः (from which anything<BR>proceeds) and by verb: प्रभवति, taking s. in<BR>the (mount)<BR>Mahendra:<BR>महेन्द्रप्रमवाः, V. p. ii.<BR>3. 13.:<BR>the s. of treasure and force:<BR>प्रभवः खलु<BR> कोषदण्डयोः, Ki. ii.;<BR>its foot is the s. of the<BR>lake called Hill-water:<BR>तस्य पादात्प्रभवति शैलोदं<BR> नाम तत्सरः, Mat.;<BR>(2) योनिः (=origin),<BR>the s.<BR>of all, you are self-born:<BR>सर्वयोनिस्त्वमात्मभूः, R.<BR>x. 20.;<BR>(3) मूलम् (=root);<BR>(4) कारणम्<BR>(= cause);<BR>(5) प्रसूतिः (= parent);<BR>(6) आदिः<BR>(= beginning);<BR>(7) मुखम् (=mouth: of<BR>persons in supplying information).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sourish
SOURISH: ईषदम्ल (f. म्ला): v. Sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sourness
SOURNESS:<BR>I Lit.: अम्लता।<BR>II Harshness:<BR>q. v.: रूक्षता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

souse
SOUSE:<BR>I Plunge: q. v.: मज्जयति (c. of<BR>मस्ज्).<BR>II To steep: q. v.<BR>III To pounce<BR>upon: अवपतति (पत्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

south
SOUTH (subs.):<BR>(1) दक्षिणा दिक्, दक्षिणाशा, and<BR>sim. comp.,<BR>these forests face the s.:<BR>एतान्यरण्यानि<BR> दक्षिणां दिशममिवर्तन्ते, Vi. v.;<BR>to the s. of the<BR>garden:<BR>दक्षिणेन वृक्षवाटिकाम्, Sa. i.;<BR>to or on<BR>the s.:<BR>दक्षिणतः, Mah.;<BR>(2) अवाची (rare);<BR>(3) poet. याम्या, V. m.; त्रिशङ्कुतिलका दिक्, K,<BR>अगस्त्याचरिताशा, R. iv. 44. and sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

south
SOUTH, SOUTHERN (adj.): दक्षिण (f. णा),<BR>s.<BR>wind:<BR>दक्षिणो वायुः, V. m. 27. 3., (gen.<BR>मलयानिलः, मलयवातः, etc. from the Malaya);<BR>s. ocean:<BR>दक्षिणः समुद्रः, Ram. v. 1. 2.; s.<BR>country (the Deccan): दक्षिणापथः, Mah. ii.<BR>31. 17.; s. people armed with swords:<BR>दाक्षिणात्यासिपाणयः, Mah. xii. 101. 5.;<BR>(2) अवाच्य<BR>(f. च्या)<BR>or<BR>अवाच् (f. ची: rare), s. alley:<BR>अवाचीं वीथिम्, D. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

southerly
SOUTHERLY: v. South, southern, southwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

south-east
SOUTH-EAST:<BR>(1) दक्षिणपूर्वा<BR>or<BR>पूर्वदक्षिणा दिक् and<BR>sim. comp.s;<BR>(2) आग्नेयी दिक्<BR>or<BR>आग्ने यो दिग्मागः<BR>and sim. comp.s;<BR>(3) प्रागवाची।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

south-east
SOUTH-EAST, SOUTH-EASTERLY, SOUTH-EASTERN<BR>(adj.):<BR>(1) दक्षिणपूर्व (f. र्वा) etc.;<BR>(2) आग्ने य<BR>(f. यी: poet.),<BR>s. wind:<BR>आग्ने यो वायुः, V. m.<BR>27. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

southward
SOUTHWARD, -s: expr. by adj.: दक्षिणाभिमुख<BR>(f. खी), Mah. ii. 31. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

south-west
SOUTH-WEST, SOUTH-WESTERN (adj.):<BR>(1) दक्षिण-<BR>पश्चिमः (मा, मं),<BR>s. wind:<BR>वातो दक्षिणपश्चिमः,<BR>Mah.;<BR>(2) नैरृ तः (ती, तं),<BR>s. wind:<BR>नैरृ तो<BR> वायुः, V. m. 27. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

southernwood
SOUTHERNWOOD: a plant: दमनः, -कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

souvenir
SOUVENIR (subs.):<BR>(1) प्रीतिदायः (of love),<BR>Ram.;<BR>(2) स्मृतिदायः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sovereign
SOVEREIGN: a coin: स्वर्णमुद्रा, सुवर्णः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sovereign
SOVEREIGN (subs.):<BR>(1) अधिराज (f. ज्ञी),<BR>s. of<BR>animals:<BR>मृगाधिराजः, R. ii. 41.; ईश्वर (f. री),<BR>परम-, महा-,<BR>s. of Vidiśā:<BR>विदिशेश्वरः, Mal.: v.<BR>Also king, lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sovereign
SOVEREIGN (adj.):<BR>(1) परम (f. मा): v.<BR>Supreme;<BR>(2) मुख्य (f. ख्या): v. Chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sovereignty
SOVEREIGNTY: प्रभुत्वम् (= authority, power:<BR>q. v.),<BR>s. of the world:<BR>जगतः प्रभुत्वम्, R. ii. 47.;<BR>(2) राज्यम् (=kingdom),<BR>exercise the s. of the<BR>whole earth:<BR>सकलभुवनराज्यं कारय, Bh. ii. 56.;<BR>to obtain the fortune of s.:<BR>साम्नाज्यश्रियमधिगच्छति,<BR>Si. xiv. 88.;<BR>(3) ईश्वरत्वम् (rare), s. from birth:<BR>गर्मेश्वरत्वम्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sow
SOW (subs.):<BR>(1) शूकरी;<BR>(2) वराही;<BR>(3) कोली<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sow-bread
SOW-BREAD: a plant: शूकर-<BR>or<BR>वराहमोदा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sow
SOW (v.): वपति, प्र-, परि-, (वप्, c. 1.),<BR>who s.<BR>seed in other's land:<BR>ये परक्षेत्रे बीजं वपन्ति, K. ii.;<BR>as one s. s, so one reaps:<BR>यो यद्वपति बीजं हि सोऽपि<BR> तल्लभते फलम्, K. s. xvi. 148. Ph.:<BR>to s. dissen-<BR>sions:<BR>भेदं जनयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sower
SOWER:<BR>(1) वप्तृ (f. प्त्री),<BR>the s. does not get the<BR>produce:<BR>न वप्ता लभते फलम्, M. ix. 54.;<BR>(2)<BR>वापिन् (f. नी),<BR>s. s in other's fields:<BR>परक्षेत्रप्रवापिणः,<BR>M. ix. 49.;<BR>(3) वापक (f. पिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sowing
SOWING (subs.):<BR>(1) वपनम्, K. b.;<BR>(2) उप्तिः;<BR>(3) वापः, Viv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

space
SPACE:<BR>(1) आकाशम्,<BR>s. is distinguished by egress<BR>and ingress:<BR>निष्क्रामणं प्रवेशनमित्याकाशस्य लिङ्गम्, V.<BR>ii. 1. 20.: v. Sky;<BR>(2) दिश् (f=relative s.):<BR>v. Quarter.<BR>II Interval: q. v.: अन्तरम्।<BR>III Room:<BR>(1) अवकाशः,<BR>to give s.:<BR>अवकाशं<BR> ददाति, R.;<BR>(2) स्थानम्: v. Place.<BR>IV Of<BR>time: not expr.,<BR>what s. of time:<BR>कियत्कालम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spacious
SPACIOUS:<BR>(1) विस्तीर्ण (f. र्णा): v. Extensive;<BR>(2) विशाल (f. ला): v. Large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spaciousness
SPACIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) विस्तीर्णता;<BR>(2) विशालता;<BR>(3)<BR>विपुलता;<BR>(4) पृथुता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spade
SPADE:<BR>(1) खनित्रम्;<BR>(2) अवदारणम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

span
SPAN (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) किष्कुः (also=<BR>cubit);<BR>(2) वितस्तिः;<BR>(3) अर्धहस्तः।<BR>II Fig.,<BR>short space:<BR>‘the brief s. of life’:<BR>तरलं जीवनम्,<BR>J. and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

span
SPAN (v.): मिमीते, प्र-, परि-, (मा, c. 3.): v.<BR>To measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spangle
SPANGLE:<BR>I Subs.: रजतपत्रम्।<BR>II Verb: v.<BR>To adorn, studded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spaniel
SPANIEL: आखेटिककुक्कुरविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spanish
SPANISH: हिस्पानीय (f. या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spank
SPANK: v. Slap, to slap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spar
SPAR (subs.):<BR>I Crystallized earth: *स्फटिक-<BR>मृत्तिका; उपधातुः (?).<BR>II A long beam:<BR>(1)<BR>दीर्धकाष्ठम्;<BR>(2) यष्टिः (= pole).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spar
SPAR (v.):<BR>I Lit.: v. To box.<BR>II To<BR>quarrel: q. v.: विवदते (वद्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spare
SPARE (v.):<BR>I Not to throw away:<BR>(1) न<BR> क्षिपति, वि-, विनि-, प्र- (क्षिप्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) संचि-<BR>नोति (चि, c. 5.): v. To save;<BR>(3) रक्षति,<BR> सं-, (रक्ष्, c. 1. = to keep),<BR>shall s. money for<BR>calamities:<BR>आपदर्थे धनं रक्षेत्, H.<BR>II To grant,<BR>give: q. v.: ददाति (दा, c. 3.). Ph.:<BR>s.<BR>him:<BR>मुच्यताम्, Mr. x.: v. To release.<BR>III<BR>To give up: जहाति, वि-, (हा, c. 3.: v.<BR>To abandon).<BR>IV To omit, forbear:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spare
SPARE (adj.):<BR>I Superfluous:<BR>(1) उद्वृत्त (f.<BR>त्ता); अव्यापृत (f. ता = unemployed).<BR>II<BR>Scanty, little: q. v.: अल्प (f. ल्पा).<BR>III<BR>Lean, slender: q. v.: कृश (f. शा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spareness
SPARENESS: कृशता: v. Leanness, slenderness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sparingly
SPARINGLY:<BR>(1) मितम्: v. Moderately;<BR>(2)<BR>अल्पम्: Little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sparingness
SPARINGNESS: मितव्ययिता, -त्वम्, परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spark
SPARK:<BR>I Of fire:<BR>(1) स्फुलिङ्गः, वि-,<BR>whose s. s<BR>were scattered on all sides:<BR>विष्वक्विस्तृतस्फुलिङ्गः,<BR>Ki. xvi. 51.;<BR>(2) कणः (= particle), s. -red:<BR>कणारुण-, Si. v. 55.<BR>II A small particle: कणः<BR>(= drop).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sparkle
SPARKLE: स्फुरति, वि- (स्फुर्, c. 1.: v. To<BR>glitter).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sparring
SPARRING (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मौष्टा, S. k.;<BR>(2) मुष्टियुद्धम्।<BR>II Debate, controversy: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sparrow
SPARROW:<BR>(1) चटकः,<BR>hen s.:<BR>चटका; s. couple:<BR>चटकौ;<BR>a young s.:<BR>चटककः;<BR>(2) कलविङ्कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sparse
SPARSE: विरलः (ला, लं): v. Thin, scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sparseness
SPARSENESS: विरलता: v. Thinness. fewness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spasm
SPASM:<BR>I In general: संकोचः (= contrac-<BR>-tion).<BR>II The disease; शिरासंकोचः, Bha.;<BR>शूलम् (= cholic), हृच्छूलं पार्श्व योश्चापि, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spasmodic
SPASMODIC: expr. by comp. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spatter
SPATTER: अवसिञ्चति (सिच्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>bespatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spatter dashes
SPATTER DASHES: *पङ्कावरणम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spatula
SPATULA: लेपनी, प्र-। वि- (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spavin
SPAVIN: perh. सन्धिशोथः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spawn
SPAWN:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) मीनाण्डम् and sim.<BR>comp.s (of fish);<BR>(2) भेकाण्डम् (of frogs).<BR>II<BR>Verb: अण्डानि मुञ्चति, (मुच्, c. 6.), मोक्षयति<BR>(मोक्ष्, c. 10.), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spay
SPAY:<BR>I Verb: v. To castrate.<BR>II Subs.:<BR>त्रिहायणो हरिणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speak
SPEAK:<BR>(1) वक्ति, प्र-, (वच्, c. 2.),<BR>I spoke to<BR>the sun of this immutable doctrine:<BR>इमं विवस्वते<BR> योगं प्रोक्तवानहमव्ययम्, G. iv. 1.: v. To say;<BR>(2) ब्रवीति<BR>or<BR>ब्रूते (ब्रू, c. 2.),<BR>for good men s. of<BR>their usefulness by results and not by words:<BR>ब्रवते हि फलेन साधवो न तु कण्ठेन निजोपयोगिताम्, N.<BR>ii. 48.;<BR>Manu spoke to Ikṣvāku:<BR>मनुरिक्षा-<BR>कवेऽब्रवीत्, G. iv. 1.;<BR>(3) कथयति (कथ्, c. 10.)<BR>=to tell), this s. s of the king's excellences that:<BR>अनेन कथिता राज्ञो गुणा यत्॥।, R. x. 53.;<BR>which<BR>he was s. ing thus:<BR>इति कथयति तत्र, Ki. iii. 37.;<BR>(4) वदति (वद्, c. 1. = s. to),<BR>given way to rage,<BR>he spoke as follows in very bitter and plain lan-<BR>guage:<BR>वाचमवददिति रोषवशादतिमात्रनिष्ठुरस्फुटतराक्ष-<BR>रामसौ, Si. xv. 13.;<BR>(5) गदति, नि- (गद्, c. 1.<BR>=4.), the lion spoke to him in human tongue:<BR>तं मनुष्यवाचा निजगाद सिंहः, R. ii. 33.;<BR>the general<BR>spoke to them:<BR>सेनान्या ते जगदिरे, Ki. xv. 7.;<BR>(6) भाषते (भाष्, c. 1. = to say, utter),<BR>as if<BR>spoke the same thing again:<BR>तमेवार्थमभाषतेव, R.<BR>ii. 51.;<BR>(7) वाचम्<BR>or<BR>गिरम्<BR>or<BR>गाम् उदीरयति,<BR> उदगिरति, विसृजति, etc. (=make a speech).<BR>Ph.: (a)<BR>s. out plainly:<BR>भिन्नार्थमभिधीयताम्, Sa.<BR>vi.; (b) formerly they also could s. like men:<BR>एतेषामपि पुरा पुरुषाणामिव वागासीत्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speak ill of
SPEAK ILL OF:<BR>(1) अपभाषते, who s. s ill of great<BR>(men): यो महतोऽपभाषते, Ku. v. 83.;<BR>(2) अप-<BR>वदति, -ते, “धनकामो न्यायमपवदते”, Vāmana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speak well of
SPEAK WELL OF: प्रशंसति (शंस्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speak with
SPEAK WITH, SPEAK TOGETHER:<BR>(1) संवदति,<BR>the foe of Bala spoke with Nārada:<BR>नारदं बलरिपुः<BR> समवादीत्, N. v. 12.;<BR>(2) संभाषते, M. n.;<BR>(3)<BR>संकथयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speaker
SPEAKER:<BR>(1) वक्तृ (f. क्त्री),<BR>indifferent to<BR>particular s. s:<BR>वक्तृविशेषनिःस्पृहाः, Ki. ii. 5.;<BR>(2)<BR>वाग्मिन् (f. नी =orator).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speaking
SPEAKING (subs.):<BR>(1) भाषितम्: v. To speak;<BR>(2) वाच् (f.): v. Speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spear
SPEAR:<BR>I Subs.: शूल (mn.): v. Also lance.<BR>II Verb: शूलेन विध्यति: v. To pierce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spearman
SPEARMAN:<BR>(1) शूलिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) शूलधर (f.<BR>रा);<BR>(3) शूलधारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

special
SPECIAL:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) जातीय<BR>(f. या) and sim. deriv. s.<BR>II Opposed to<BR>common:<BR>(1) विशेष in comp.,<BR>by s. injunc-<BR>tions:<BR>विशेषशास्त्रै:, M. n. on Ku. v. 27.;<BR>(2)<BR>वैशेषिक (f. की: rare),<BR>s. attribute:<BR>वैशेषिको<BR> गुणः, Par.;<BR>(3) विशिष्ट (f. ष्टा),<BR>s. jury:<BR>विशिष्ट-<BR>सभ्याः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

specialty
SPECIALTY, SPECIALITY:<BR>(1) विशेषधर्मः and sim.<BR>comp.s; वैशेषिकता, वैशेषिकत्वम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

specially
SPECIALLY:<BR>I Lit.: जात्यनुसारेण and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Particularly:<BR>(1) विशेषेण;<BR>(2)<BR>विशेषतः;<BR>(3) विशिष्टम्;<BR>(4) विशिष्य,<BR>s. to those<BR>who say the praises of Bhaimī:<BR>विशिष्य भैमीं<BR> गुणकीर्तनकृताम्, N. xv. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

specie
SPECIE: मुद्रा: v. Coin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

species
SPECIES:<BR>(1) जातिः,<BR>of the same s.:<BR>सजातीय or<BR>एकजातीय (f. या), Sr.; whatever is best in a s. is<BR>called (its)<BR>gem:<BR>जातौ जातौ यदुत्कृष्टं तद्रत्नं कथ्यते<BR> बधैः, M. n.<BR>II प्रकारः: v. Kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

specific
SPECIFIC: विशेष- in comp.,<BR>s. (remedy):<BR>विशेष-<BR>मौषधम्<BR>or<BR>महौषधम् (when sense clear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

specifically
SPECIFICALLY:<BR>(1) सविशेषम्;<BR>(2) मिन्नार्थम् (= ex-<BR>-plicitly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

specify
SPECIFY:<BR>(1) उदाहरति (हृ, c. 1.);<BR>(2) सविशेषम्<BR> उल्लिखति (लिख, c. 6.): v. To mention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

specimen
SPECIMEN:<BR>(1) निदर्शनम्;<BR>(2) आदर्शः (=model).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

specious
SPECIOUS: v. Plausible, showy; s. ly: v.<BR>Plausibly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speciousness
SPECIOUSNESS: सत्याभासः: v. Plausibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speck
SPECK: बिन्दुः: v. Spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speckle
SPECKLE: बिन्दुभिश्चित्रयति: v. To spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spectacle
SPECTACLE:<BR>I Show:<BR>(1) दृश्यम्;<BR>(2) कौतुकम् [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">Page666</a>]<BR>(= curiosity).<BR>II In pl., for the eye:<BR>उपनेत्रम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spectator
SPECTATOR:<BR>(1) प्रेक्षक (f. क्षिका),<BR>uttered by<BR>s.s:<BR>प्रेक्षकेरिताः, Mah. i. 133. 13.;<BR>(2) प्रेक्षक-<BR>जनः<BR>or<BR>-लोकः;<BR>(3) द्रष्ट्ट (f. ष्ट्री);<BR>(4) दर्शक<BR>(f. शिका), परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spectral
SPECTRAL: by comp.: v. Also ghastly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spectre
SPECTRE:<BR>(1) भूत (mn.): v. Ghost;<BR>(2) छाया:<BR>v. Shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spectrum
SPECTRUM:<BR>solar s.:<BR>*सौरदर्शनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speculate
SPECULATE:<BR>I To consider, meditate: q. v.:<BR>विचारयति (c. of चर्).<BR>II To guess: q. v.:<BR>विकल्पयति (c. of कॢप्).<BR>III In commerce.<BR>perh. कपालं सेवते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speculation
SPECULATION:<BR>I Meditation, consideration:<BR>q. v.: विचारः।<BR>II In commerce: *कपालसेवा।<BR>III Guess: q. v.: विकल्पः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speculative
SPECULATIVE: विचारसेविन् (f. नी). Ph.:<BR>s.<BR>philosophy:<BR>दर्शनशास्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speculator
SPECULATOR:<BR>I Philosophical: मीमांसक (f.<BR>सिका).<BR>II Commercial: *कपालसेवक (f.<BR>विका)<BR>or<BR>-सेविन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speech
SPEECH:<BR>I The faculty:<BR>(1) वाच् (f.);<BR>(2) वाक्शक्तिः।<BR>II Language: q. v.: वाच्।<BR>III Utterance, address:<BR>(1) वाच् (f.) or<BR>वचस् (n.);<BR>(2) गिर् (f.);<BR>(3) वाणी;<BR>(4)<BR>सरस्वती;<BR>(5) भारती: v. Also saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speechless
SPEECHLESS: मूकः (का, कं): v. Silent, dumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speed
SPEED:<BR>(1) वेगः,<BR>motion at full s.:<BR>पूर्णवेगा गतिः,<BR>M. n.;<BR>(2) जवः,<BR>by the s. of the current:<BR>स्रोतो-<BR>जवेन, Mah.;<BR>(3) रंहस् (n.),<BR>s. of wind:<BR>मारुतस्य<BR> रंहः, R. ii. 34.;<BR>(4) त्वरा: v. Haste;<BR>(5)<BR>शीघ्रता: v. Quickness. Ph.:<BR>may you have<BR>god s. on your way:<BR>तव वर्त्मनि वर्ततां शिवम्, N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speed
SPEED (v.): शिवं<BR>or<BR>क्षेमं<BR>or<BR>मङ्गलं करोति (with<BR>gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speedily
SPEEDILY:<BR>(1) आशु;<BR>(2) तूर्णम्: v. Quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

speedy
SPEEDY:<BR>(1) by adv.,<BR>and may your meeting<BR>be s.:<BR>पुनरस्तु त्वरितं समागमः, N. ii. 62.;<BR>(2)<BR>शीघ्र (f. घ्रा = quick);<BR>(3) जवन (f. ना = swift).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spell
SPELL (subs.):<BR>I Sub.:<BR>(1) मन्त्रः;<BR>(2) तन्त्रम्।<BR>II Verb: वर्णयति (वर्ण्, c. 10.: comp.<BR>Bengali Bānana).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spelling
SPELLING (subs.): v. To spell. Ph.:<BR>vocabulary<BR>of words having two s. s. (forms):<BR>द्विरूपकोषः;<BR>s.-book:<BR>*वर्णशिक्षा (comp. वर्णपरिचय of<BR>Vidyāsāgara).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spelt
SPELT: a kind of corn: नीवारः (??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spend
SPEND:<BR>I To expend:<BR>(1) व्ययति, -ते (व्यय्,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>s. ing at pleasure:<BR>व्ययमानः स्ववाञ्छया,<BR>H. ii. 95.;<BR>(2) उत्-सृजति, वि-, समुत् (सृज्, c. 6.),<BR>s. ing money:<BR>धनोत्सर्गं करोति, Ram.;<BR>(3) त्यजति,<BR> परि-, सं-, (त्यज्, c. 1.), receives much, s. s little:<BR>तनुत्यागो बहुग्रहः, H. ii. 91.<BR>II To pass: q. v.:<BR>क्षपयति (c. of क्षप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spendthrift
SPENDTHRIFT:<BR>(1) अतिव्यय (f. या), H.;<BR>(2)<BR>अतिव्ययिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) त्यागशालिन् (f. नी);<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spew
SPEW: वमति (वम्, c. 1.): v. To vomit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sphere
SPHERE:<BR>I A globe: गोलः,<BR>celestial s.:<BR>खगोलः,<BR>Go.;<BR>lunar s.:<BR>चन्द्राधिष्ठानगोलः, Su. com.<BR>II<BR>Province, department: expr. by कर्म<BR>(=work)<BR>or<BR>क्षेत्रम् (= field).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spherical
SPHERICAL:<BR>(1) गोलाकारः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) by गोलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spherics
SPHERICS:<BR>(1) गोलः,<BR>an astronomer not knowing<BR>s.:<BR>गोलानभिज्ञो गणकः, Go. 3.;<BR>(2) गोलग्रन्थः or<BR>गोलप्रबन्धः (= a work on s.), Go. (गोलाध्याय<BR>is the part on S. in S. s).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spheroid
SPHEROID: *उपगोलः (अण्डम् = egg may prop.<BR>be used for prolate s. s).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sphinx
SPHINX: *नरसिंही।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spice
SPICE (subs.): गन्धद्रव्यम्,<BR>s. s:<BR>कर्पूरादिवर्गः, Bha.;<BR>the<BR>three s. s:<BR>त्रिसुगन्धि<BR>or<BR>त्रिजातकम्, Bha;<BR>the four<BR>s. s:<BR>चतुर्जातकम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spice
SPICE (v.): वासयति, अधि- (वास्। c. 10.),<BR>well<BR>s. d with cloves and camphor:<BR>लवङ्गेन्दुसुवासित<BR>(f. ता), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spicy
SPICY:<BR>(1) सुगन्धि (mfn. = fragrant);<BR>(2) वासित<BR>(f. ता = spiced).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spider
SPIDER:<BR>(1) ऊर्णनाभः;<BR>(2) मर्कटः;<BR>(3) लूता,<BR>s's<BR>web:<BR>लूताजालम्;<BR>(4) तन्तुनाभः,<BR>the s. also spins<BR>its web itself:<BR>तन्तुनाभश्च स्वत एव तन्तून् सृजति,<BR>S. ii. 1. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spike
SPIKE (subs.):<BR>I Of flowers:<BR>(1) मञ्जरी;<BR>(2)<BR>वल्लरी।<BR>II Of grain:<BR>(1) कणिशम्;<BR>(2) शीर्षम्<BR>(=head).<BR>III A large nail: महाकीलः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spike
SPIKE (v.): कीलयति (nomi. ??).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spikenard
SPIKENARD:<BR>(1) जटामांसी;<BR>(2) मिशिः(शी);<BR>(3)<BR>नलदा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spiky
SPIKY:<BR>(1) तीक्ष्णाग्र (f. ग्रा = sharp-pointed);<BR>(2) कीलचित (f. ता = furnished with spikes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spill
SPILL:<BR>I Subs.: शलाका।<BR>II Trans.: perh.<BR>क्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6. = throw)<BR>or<BR>पातयति (c. of<BR>पत् = fall).<BR>III Intrans.: पतति (पत्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spin
SPIN (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: कृन्तति (कृत्, c. 7.),<BR>spindle is the instrument for s. ning:<BR>तर्कुः कर्तन-<BR>साधने, H. c. iii. 575.<BR>II To revolve: q. v.:<BR>परि- वर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR>III Intrans.: घूर्णते<BR>(घूर्ण्, c. 1.): v. To revolve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spinach
SPINACH: शाकप्रभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spinal
SPINAL: Ph.:<BR>s. column:<BR>पृष्ठवंशः: v. Spin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spindle
SPINDLE:<BR>(1) तर्कुः;<BR>(2) तर्कुटी;<BR>(3) मेरुयन्त्रम्<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spindle-shanks
SPINDLE-SHANKS: क्षामजङ्घ (f. ङ्घा) and sim.<BR>comp. s.: पृश्नि (ष्णि mfn.), A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spine
SPINE:<BR>I Of the body:<BR>(1) पृष्ठवंशः;<BR>(2) कशेरु<BR>(mn.).<BR>II A thorn: कण्टकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spinner
SPINNER:<BR>(1) कर्तक (f. र्तिका);<BR>(2) तन्तुवाय<BR>(f. यी = weaver).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spinning-wheel
SPINNING-WHEEL: perh. कर्तनचक्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spinster
SPINSTER:<BR>I Lit.: सूत्रकर्तिका।<BR>II An un-<BR>-married woman: अनुढा and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spiracle
SPIRACLE: रन्ध्रम्: v. Pore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spiral
SPIRAL: आवर्तिन् (f. नी : (?), वि-, s. wheel:<BR>आवर्तिचक्रम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spire
SPIRE:<BR>I A coil: आवर्तः, -नम्, वि-।<BR>II Of a<BR>church:<BR>(1) शिखरम्;<BR>(2) शृङ्गम्;<BR>(3) शेखरः<BR>(m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spirit
SPIRIT:<BR>I Breath, life: q. v.: प्राणः।<BR>II<BR>Animating principle: प्राणः,<BR>s. alone is death-<BR>less:<BR>प्राण एवैको मृत्युनाऽनाप्तः, S.: v. Soul. Ph.:<BR>the supreme s.:<BR>ब्रह्मन् (n.)<BR>or<BR>परं ब्रह्म, Vi.<BR>III<BR>Mind: q. v.: मनस् (n.),<BR>loftiness of s.:<BR>मनसः<BR> समुन्नतिः, Ku. vi. 66. Ph.: high s. s (=joy):<BR>प्रहर्षः;<BR>good s. s:<BR>प्रफुल्लता।<BR>IV Energy, vigour:<BR>(1) सत्त्वम्,<BR>loses s.:<BR>सत्त्वात् परिभ्रश्यते, H. 133.;<BR>evincing high s.:<BR>कृतसत्त्ववेगः, Ki. xvii. 15.;<BR>(2) तेजस् (mfn.),<BR>lacking s.:<BR>निस्तेजस्, Mu.<BR>i. 13.; again with the s. hightened from a<BR>determination (to fight): भूयः समाधानविवृद्धतेजाः,<BR>Ki. xvii. 7.<BR>V Of style: ओजस् (n.), Kav.<BR>viii. 4.<BR>VI Temper, disposition: q. v.:<BR>प्रकृतिः।<BR>VII Prevailing disposition (as “s. of<BR>the age”): रीतिः।<BR>VIII Real meaning:<BR>भावः<BR>or<BR>भावार्थः: v. Intention.<BR>IX A person:<BR>व्यक्तिः।<BR>X A ghost:<BR>(1) भूतः। Ph.: evil s.:<BR>प्रेतः, Wilson.<BR>XI Disembodied s.:<BR>(1)<BR>(= dead);<BR>(2) not expr. (as corporeality<BR>is always supposed),<BR>and the s. of the king<BR>Daśaratha:<BR>स च राजा दशरथः, Ram. vi. 102. 4.<BR>XII A spirituous liquor: सुरा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spirited
SPIRITED:<BR>I Of persons:<BR>(1) तेजस्विन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) सत्त्ववत् (f. ती): and sim. comp.s.<BR>II<BR>Of style: ओजस्विन् (f. नी), Ki. vi. 38.<BR>III<BR>In comp.: expr. by comp.: v. Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spiritedly
SPIRITEDLY:<BR>(1) प्रसभम्, Ki. ii. 28.;<BR>(2)<BR>सोत्साहम् (=zealously).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spiritless
SPIRITLESS:<BR>(1) निस्तेजस् (mfn.);<BR>(2) निःसत्त्व<BR>(f. त्त्वा), H.;<BR>(3) तेजोविहीनः (ना, नं), Ki.<BR>xvii. 16. and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spiritlessly
SPIRITLESSLY:<BR>(1) निःसत्त्वम् (rare);<BR>(2) निरुत्साहम्,<BR>(without zeal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spiritlessness
SPIRITLESSNESS:<BR>(1) निरुत्साहिता;<BR>(2) तेजोहीनता;<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spiritual
SPIRITUAL:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) expr. by comp.:<BR>(2) अध्यात्म- in comp.,<BR>s. knowledge:<BR>अध्यात्म-<BR>ज्ञानम्;<BR>(3) आध्यात्मिक (f. की).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1)<BR>पारत्रिक<BR>or<BR>पारलौकिक (f. की = of next world);<BR>(2) मानसिक (f. की = mental);<BR>(3) अमूर्त<BR>(f. र्ता = incorporeal);<BR>(4) सात्त्विक (f. की)<BR>: v. Pure, divine;<BR>(5) धार्मिक (f. की): v.<BR>Religious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spiritualism
SPIRITUALISM:<BR>I Lit.: ब्रह्मवादः।<BR>II Modern:<BR>*भूतवादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spiritualist
SPIRITUALIST:<BR>I Lit.: ब्रह्मवादिन् (f. नी).<BR>II<BR>Modern: भूतवादिन् (f. नी) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spirituality
SPIRITUALITY:<BR>(1) आध्यात्मिकता;<BR>(2) सात्त्विकता,<BR>etc.: v. Spiritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spiritually
SPIRITUALLY:<BR>(1) ब्रह्मधिया, B.;<BR>(2) विशुद्धदृष्ट्या,<BR>and sim. expr.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spirituous
SPIRITUOUS: Ph.:<BR>s. liquor:<BR>सुरासवः, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spit
SPIT (v.):<BR>I To eject saliva: ष्ठीवति, नि- (ष्ठिव्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">Page668</a>]<BR>c. 1.),<BR>s. ting on any one:<BR>अवनिष्ठीवत् (f. ती),<BR>M. viii. 282.;<BR>s. out:<BR>निष्ठीवति, N. xxii. 16.<BR>II<BR>To run a s. through: शूलाकरोति, D. viii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spit
SPIT (subs.):<BR>I What is s. ted: निष्ठ्यू तम्, M.<BR>iv. 132.<BR>II For roasting: शूल (mn.).<BR>III<BR>Of land.: खनित्रमेया भूमिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spite
SPITE (subs.):<BR>I Harted: q. v.: विद्वेषः।<BR>II<BR>In s. of: v. Notwithstanding (II), despite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spite
SPITE (v.): द्वेष्टि (द्विष्, c. 2.: v. To hate,<BR>malign).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spiteful
SPITEFUL:<BR>(1) by adv.;<BR>(2) सासूय (f. या);<BR>(3) विद्वेषिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spitefully
SPITEFULLY:<BR>(1) सासूयम्;<BR>(2) साभ्यसूयम्;<BR>(3)<BR>द्वेषात्;<BR>(4) विद्विष्टम्;<BR>(5) द्रोहबुद्ध्या (= to injure).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spitefulness
SPITEFULNESS: विद्वेषः: v. Harted, malignity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spitting
SPITTING (subs.):<BR>(1) निष्ठीवः, -नम्;<BR>(2) निष्ठेवः,<BR> -नम्;<BR>(3) निष्ठ्यू तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spittle
SPITTLE:<BR>(1) लाला (= saliva);<BR>(2) निष्ठ्यू तम्,<BR>(what is spitted out).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spittoon
SPITTOON:<BR>(1) प्रतिग्राहः;<BR>(2) पतद्ग्रहः, A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

splash
SPLASH:<BR>I Verb: आस्फालयति,<BR>which is s. ed by<BR>women:<BR>आस्फालितं यत् प्रमदाकराग्रैः, R. xvi. 13.<BR>II Subs.: expr. by adj.: आस्फालित (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spleen
SPLEEN:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्लीहन् (m.),<BR>enlargement<BR>of s.:<BR>प्लीहविवृद्धिः,<BR>the disease called s.:<BR>प्लीहसंज्ञो<BR> गदः, Bha.;<BR>(2) गुल्मः (rare).<BR>II Rage,<BR>mortification: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

splendid
SPLENDID:<BR>(1) मासुर (f. रा): v. Brilliant.;<BR>s. sword:<BR>भासुरोऽसिः, N. xvi. 18.;<BR>(2) श्रेष्ठ<BR>(f. ष्ठा): v. Excellent;<BR>(3) वृन्दिष्ठ (f. ष्ठा)<BR>: v. Chief;<BR>(4) प्रशस्त (f. स्ता): v. Praise-<BR>-worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

splendidly
SPLENDIDLY:<BR>(1) by comp.; s. dressed:<BR>उज्ज्वलवेशधारिन् (f. णी), Mr. ix.;<BR>(2) प्रशस्तम्<BR>: v. Excellently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

splendour
SPLENDOUR:<BR>(1) औज्ज्वल्यम्: v. Brilliancy;<BR>(2) शोभा; : v. beauty;<BR>(3) तेजस् (= lustre),<BR>in s. to sun:<BR>तेजसा सवित्रा, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

splenetic
SPLENETIC:<BR>I Lit.: प्लीहरोगिन् (f. णी) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR>II Peevish: q. v.: कर्कश<BR>(f. शा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

splice
SPLICE: संयोजयति (युज्, c. 10.): v. To unite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

splint
SPLINT: in medicine: perh.: आलम्बः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

splinter
SPLINTER:<BR>I Subs.: काष्ठखण्डम् and sim.<BR>comp.s (?).<BR>II Verb: विदारयति (c. of दॄ):<BR>v. To shiver, rend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

split
SPLIT:<BR>I Intrans.:<BR>(1) स्फुटति, प्र-, वि-, परि-<BR>(स्फुट्, c. 1.),<BR>heart is s. ting:<BR>स्फुटति हृदयम्,<BR>Mr. iii.;<BR>(2) दीर्यते, वि-, (pass. of दॄ),<BR>sound of s. ting rock:<BR>विदीर्यमाणाश्मनिनादः, Ki.<BR>II Trans.,: स्फोटयति (c. of स्फुट्);<BR>(2)<BR>विदारयति (c. of दॄ).<BR>III Subs.:<BR>(1) expr.<BR>by verb;<BR>(2) छिद्रम् (=hole)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

splutter
SPLUTTER: मकमकायते (nomi).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spoil
SPOIL (v.)<BR>I To destroy, defile: q. v.: दूषयति<BR>(c. of दुष्).<BR>II To plunder: लुण्ठति, परि-,<BR>(लुण्ठ्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spoil
SPOIL (v. i.):<BR>(1) नश्यति, वि- (नश्, c. 4.);<BR>(2)<BR>नष्टीभवति;<BR>(3) नाशमेति, -उपैति, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spoil
SPOIL (subs.):<BR>(1) युद्धलब्धधनम्, and sim.<BR>comp.s.;<BR>(2) लुण्ठितम्, परि- (= plundered).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spoiler
SPOILER:<BR>I Destroyer, defiler:<BR>(1) नाशयितृ<BR>(f. त्री);<BR>(2) द्वषक (f. षिका); etc.<BR>II<BR>Plunderer: लुण्ठाक (f. की).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spoke
SPOKE:<BR>(1) अरम्<BR>or<BR>आरा,<BR>a row of s. s:<BR>आरावली,<BR>V. iv.;<BR>(2) सक्थि,<BR>a cart with long s. s:<BR>दीर्घ-<BR>सविथ शकटम्, S. k.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spokesman
SPOKESMAN:<BR>(1) मुखम्,<BR>therefore you become my<BR>s.:<BR>तत्त्वं मे मुखं भव, V. i.;<BR>(2) वक्तृ (m. =<BR>speaker: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spoliation
SPOLIATION:<BR>(1) लुण्ठनम्, परि- (= plunder);<BR>(2) हरणम्, अप- (= carrying off).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spondaic
SPONDAIC:<BR>s. foot:<BR>गो (m. dual).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spondee
SPONDEE: गो (m. dual).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sponge
SPONGE:<BR>I Subs.: *स्पञ्जम्।<BR>II Verb: *स्पञ्जेन<BR> मार्ष्टि<BR>or<BR>मार्जयति, परि-, सं- (मृज्, c. 2. and 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sponge cake
SPONGE CAKE: पिष्टकविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sponginess
SPONGINESS: *स्पञ्जाभता and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spongy
SPONGY: *स्पञ्जाभ (f. भा) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sponsor
SPONSOR:<BR>(1) *प्रतिष्ठातृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) धर्मप्रतिभूः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sponsorship
SPONSORSHIP:<BR>(1) *प्रतिष्ठातृत्वम्;<BR>(2) धर्मप्रातिभाव्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spontaneity
SPONTANEITY: expr. with adv.:<BR>s. of move-<BR>ment:<BR>स्वेच्छया गमनशीलत्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spontaneous
SPONTANEOUS: expr. by स्वेच्छातः<BR>or<BR>स्वेच्छया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spontaneously
SPONTANEOUSLY:<BR>(1) स्वेच्छया;<BR>(2) स्वेच्छातः;<BR>(3) स्वेच्छानुसारेण, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spoon
SPOON:<BR>(1) चमस (mn.);<BR>(2) दर्वी(र्विः)।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spoonful
SPOONFUL: expr. by spoon,<BR>giving two s. s of<BR>rice:<BR>ओदनस्य दर्वीद्वयं दत्त्वा, D. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sporadic
SPORADIC: perh. असंलग्न (f. ग्ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sport
SPORT (v.): खेलति (खेल्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sport
SPORT (subs.):<BR>I Play, amusement^1: क्रीडा।<BR>II Hunting: q. v.: मृगया।<BR>III Ridicule,<BR>derision: q. v.: उपहासः।<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sporting
SPORTING: Ph.:<BR>s. magazine:<BR>आखेटिकपत्रिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sportive
SPORTIVE:<BR>(1) खेल (f. ला: rare);<BR>(2) खेलत्<BR>(f. न्ती),<BR>s. cupid:<BR>खेलदनङ्गः, Gi. i. 29.;<BR>(3)<BR>क्रीडत् (f. न्ती),<BR>s. cuckoo:<BR>क्रीडत्कोकिलः, Gi. i.<BR>38.: v. Also playful, merry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sportively
SPORTIVELY:<BR>(1) खेलम्,<BR>marching s.:<BR>खेलगामिन्<BR>(f. नी), Ku. vii. 49.;<BR>(2) सखेलम्: v. Also<BR>playfully, merrily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sportsman
SPORTSMAN: मृगयासेविन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spot
SPOT (subs.):<BR>I Place: q. v.: स्थानम्।<BR>II<BR>Speck:<BR>(1) बिन्दुः,<BR>variegated with hundreds of<BR>silver s. s:<BR>रौप्यबिन्दुशतचित्रः, Ra. iii. 98. 12.;<BR>golden s. s:<BR>बिन्दवो जातरूपस्य, Mah. iv. 42. 1.:<BR>v. Also mark.<BR>III Stain: q. v.: कलङ्कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spot
SPOT (v.):<BR>I Lit.: बिन्दुभिश्चित्रयति (चित्र्, c.<BR>10.): v. Also to mark. Ph.: s. ted leopard:<BR>चित्रव्याध्रः<BR>or<BR>चित्रकः;<BR>s. ted deer:<BR>चित्रो (विचित्र-<BR>बिन्दुमिर्युक्तः) मृगः, Ar.<BR>II To stain: q. v.:<BR>कलङ्कयति (nomi).<BR>III To soil: q. v.: कलुषयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spotless
SPOTLESS:<BR>I Lit.: v. Spot.<BR>II Stainless:<BR>q. v.: निष्कलङ्क (f. ङ्का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spotlessly
SPOTLESSLY: निष्कलङ्कम्: v. Stainlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spousal
SPOUSAL: विवाहः: v. Marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spouse
SPOUSE:<BR>(1) पाणिग्रहीतृ (m. = husband);<BR>(2)<BR>पाणिगृहीती (=wife);<BR>(3) वरः (= bridegroom).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spout
SPOUT (subs.): perh. नाली: v. Pipe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spout
SPOUT (v.):<BR>I Lit.: उदस्यति (अस्, c. 4.):<BR>v. To throw up.<BR>II Fig.: उद्गिरति (गॄ, c.<BR>6.): v. Also to declaim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sprain
SPRAIN:<BR>I Verb: perh. आक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c.<BR>6.), Sr.<BR>II Subs.: perh. आक्षेपः, -णम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spray
SPRAY:<BR>I Water-drop:<BR>(1) शीकरः;<BR>(2)<BR>तुषारः (rare).<BR>II Small branch: q. v.: विटपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spread
SPREAD (v. i.):<BR>(1) प्रसर्पति, वि- (सृप्, c. 1.),<BR>and the<BR>rumour s. on all sides:<BR>प्रतिदिशञ्च लोकवादः प्रासर्पत्,<BR>D.;<BR>(2) प्रसरति वि- (सृ, c. 1.).<BR>the burning of the<BR>body is s. ing:<BR>प्रसरति देहदाहः, Ma.;<BR>(3) विस्तीर्यते,<BR>(pass. of स्तॄ);<BR>(4) वितन्यते (pass. of<BR>तन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spread
SPREAD (v. t.):<BR>(1) तनोति, वि-, प्र-, (तन्, c. 8.),<BR>s. s his white fame by his excellent qualities:<BR>तनोति शुभ्रं गुणसम्पदा यशः, Ki. i. 8.;<BR>(2)<BR>विस्तारयति<BR>or<BR>स्तॄणाति, आ-, वि-, (c. of स्तृ 10 and<BR>स्तॄ, c. 9.),<BR>he s. the net:<BR>तेन जालं विस्तीर्णम्, H.;<BR>(3) प्रसारयति, वि-, (c. of सृ);<BR>(4) प्रसर्पयति<BR>(c. of सृप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sprig
SPRIG: विटपः: v. Twig.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sprightliness
SPRIGHTLINESS: प्रफुल्लता: v. Liveliness, brisk-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sprightly
SPRIGHTLY: प्रफुल्ल (f. ल्ला): v. Lively, brisk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spring
SPRING (subs.):<BR>I The season;<BR>(1) वसन्तः,<BR>s. -time:<BR>वसन्तकालः, Ki.;<BR>s. -festival:<BR>वसन्तोत्सवः,<BR>Pri.;<BR>oh, how beautiful is s.:<BR>अहो रमणीयता<BR> वसन्तस्य, V. t.;<BR>(2) सुरभिः (rare),<BR>beginning of<BR>s.:<BR>सुरभिमुखम्, Ki. x. 30.;<BR>(3) मघुः (rare),<BR>the s. will assist you unasked:<BR>मधुरनुक्तोऽपि सहाय<BR> एव, Ku. iii. 21. Ph.:<BR>s. of life:<BR>अयातयामं<BR> वयः, D. viii.<BR>II Of water: उत्सः: v. Foun-<BR>-tain.<BR>III Any source: q. v.: प्रभवः।<BR>IV<BR>A leap: q. v.: उत्प्लवः।<BR>V An elastic body:<BR>no equiv.: *प्लवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spring
SPRING (v. i.):<BR>I Proceed, rise: q. v.: जायते<BR>(जन्, c. 4.).<BR>II To leap: q. v.: प्लवते, उत्-,<BR> आ-, (प्ल, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spring
SPRING (v. t.):<BR>I To raise:<BR>(1) उत्पातयति (c.<BR>of पत्);<BR>(2) उत्थापयति (c. of स्था), D. vi.<BR>II To produce: q. v.: जनयति (c. of जन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

springe
SPRINGE: पाशः: v. Snare, trap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

springy
SPRINGY: उत्प्लवशील (f. ला: (?), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sprinkle
SPRINKLE (v. t.);<BR>(1) सिञ्चति, अभि-, परि-, नि-, प्र-,<BR> अव-, सं- (सिच्, c. 6.),<BR>s. s water on Mādhavī-<BR>plant:<BR>माधवीलतां सिञ्चति, S. i.;<BR>(2) उक्षति प्र-,<BR> अभि- (उक्ष्, c. 1.), R. xi. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sprinkle
SPRINKLE (v. i.): वर्षति (वृष्, c. 1.), मन्दं मन्दं वर्षति<BR> मेघः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sprinkling
SPRINKLING (subs.): Ph.: s. of = a few: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">Page670</a>]<BR>q. v.: विरल (f. ला), with a s. of dew-drops:<BR>विरलतुषारकणः, Ki. x. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sprout
SPROUT:<BR>I Subs.: पल्लवः: v. Shoot. Ph.:<BR>Brussels s. s:<BR>*कपिभेदः।<BR>II verb: उद्भिनत्ति<BR>(भिद्, c. 7.): v. To shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spruce
SPRUCE:<BR>I adj. विनीत (f. ता): Gentle.<BR>II<BR>Subs.: चर्मविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sprucely
SPRUCELY: विनीतम्: v. Gently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spruceness
SPRUCENESS: विनीतता: v. Elegance, neatness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spud
SPUD: कक्षकर्तरी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spume
SPUME: हिण्डीरः: v. Foam, slime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spur
SPUR (subs.):<BR>I For horses: perh., कण्टकः।<BR>II Incitement: q. v.: उत्साहः।<BR>III Pro-<BR>-jection: perh. नासा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spur
SPUR (v.): (कण्टकेन) उत्साहयति, प्रोत्- (c. of सह्):<BR>v. To incite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spurious
SPURIOUS: कृत्रिम (f. मा): v. Counterfeit,<BR>false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spuriousness
SPURIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) कृत्रिमता;<BR>(2) by adj.: v.<BR>Counterfeit, false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spurn
SPURN: प्रत्याख्याति (ख्या, c. 2.): v. To reject,<BR>scorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spurt
SPURT:<BR>I Subs.: sudden effort: हठोद्यमः and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR>II Trans.: वेगेन उदस्यति or<BR>उत्क्षिपति (अस्, c. 4. or क्षिप्, c. 6.).<BR>II<BR>Intrans.: वेगेन निष्पतति (पत्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sputter
SPUTTER:<BR>s. ed speck:<BR>अम्बूकृतम्, U. ii. 21.: v.<BR>Also to spit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spy
SPY (subs.): चारः<BR>or<BR>चरः,<BR>a s.-eyed king:<BR>चार-<BR>चक्षुर्महीपतिः, Ka. xii. 28.;<BR>spies should go out<BR>everywhere collecting the opinions of the people:<BR>चराश्चरेयुः परितः पिबन्तो जगतां मतम्, Ka xii. 26.;<BR>(2) अपसर्पः (rare);<BR>(3) स्पशः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

spy
SPY (v.):<BR>(1) आहरति (हृ, c. 1 = to collect),<BR>should s. out unperceived what goes on in the<BR>harem:<BR>अन्तःपुरगतां वार्त्तामाहरेयुरलक्षिताः, Ka. xii.<BR>43.;<BR>(2) विजानाति (ज्ञा, c. 9=to know,<BR>ascertain): v. Also look into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squabble
SQUABBLE (subs.): कलहः: v. Quarrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squabble
SQUABBLE (v.): कलहायते (nomi): To quarrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squad
SQUAD: दल (mn.): v. Party, company.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squadron
SQUADRON:<BR>I Of army:<BR>(1) गुल्मद्वयम्;<BR>(2)<BR>गणः ((2/3) of s.).<BR>II Of ships^1: पोतावली।<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squalid
SQUALID:<BR>(1) कुत्सित (f. ता): v. Foul;<BR>(2)<BR>मलिन (f. ना): v. Dirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squalidity
SQUALIDITY, SQUALOR: मालिन्यम्: v. Dirti-<BR>-ness, filth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squall
SQUALL (subs.):<BR>I Scream: q. v.: चीत्कारः।<BR>II Of wind: चण्डवातः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squall
SQUALL (v.): क्रोशति (क्रुश्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squally
SQUALLY: चण्डवात (f. ता) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squander
SQUANDER: व्ययति, -ते (व्यय्, c. 1.),<BR>you have s.<BR>ed your treasury:<BR>कोषांस्त्वमव्ययीः, B. xv. 17.:<BR>v. Also to spend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squarderer
SQUARDERER:<BR>(1) व्ययिन्, अप-, (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>व्ययकारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

square
SQUARE (adj.): वर्ग- in comp.,<BR>s. cubit:<BR>वर्गहस्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

square
SQUARE (subs.):<BR>I In arith.:<BR>(1) वर्गः,<BR>s. of<BR>a. s.:<BR>वर्गवर्गः, Li.;<BR>s. root:<BR>वर्गमूलम्, Li.<BR>or<BR>पदम्;<BR>the root of the sum of their s. s:<BR>तत्कृत्योर्योगपदम्,<BR>Li. 108.;<BR>to take the s. root:<BR>पदीकरोति, A. b.;<BR>(2) कृतिः,<BR>its s.:<BR>अस्य कृतिः, Li. 30.<BR>II In<BR>Geo.:<BR>(1) वर्गः, a s. is an equal quadrilateral:<BR>वर्गः समचतुरस्रः, A. b.;<BR>(2) तुल्यश्रुतिस्तुल्यचतुर्भुजः,<BR>and sim. comp.s., Li. 148.<BR>III In towns:<BR>no equiv.: चतुरस्रम् may be used: v. Also<BR>court.<BR>IV Of armies: वर्गव्यूहः (?): comp.<BR>पद्मव्यूहः etc., Mah. vii. 87. 24.<BR>V An intru-<BR>-ment: *समयन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squre
SQURE (v. t.):<BR>I In arith.: वर्गयति or वर्गीकरोति,<BR>what (number) multiplied by three...s.d: कस्त्रिघ्नः<BR>॥वर्गितः, A. b.<BR>II To settle, adjust: q. v.:<BR>शोधयति (c. of शुध्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

square
SQUARE (v. i.):<BR>I To agree: q. v.: संवदति<BR>(वद्, c. 1.).<BR>II To take a boxing attitude:<BR>मुष्टिं बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.: with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squash
SQUASH:<BR>I Verb.: मृद्राति (मृद्, c. 9.): v.<BR>To smash.<BR>II Subs.: संमर्दः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squat
SQUAT (v.):<BR>s. ing:<BR>उत्कटुकासनम्;<BR>(2) अवसविथ-<BR>कासनम्, Wilson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squeak
SQUEAK, SQUEAL:<BR>I Subs.: कर्कशरावः & sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Verb: वाशते<BR>or<BR>वाश्यते (वाश्, c. 1.<BR>and 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squeamish
SQUEAMISH:<BR>I Lit.: विवमिषु (mfn.).<BR>II<BR>Fastidious: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squeamishness
SQUEAMISHNESS:<BR>I Lit.: विवमिषा।<BR>II Fasti-<BR>-diousness: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squeeze
SQUEEZE: निष्पीडयति (पीड्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>press.<BR>S. out:<BR>गालयति (c. of गल्);<BR>s. d out of<BR>cloth:<BR>वस्त्रगालितः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squeeze
SQUEEZE, -ING (subs.):<BR>(1) पीडनम्, सं-; निस्-,<BR> नि-;<BR>(2) निष्पेषः (fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squib
SQUIB:<BR>I Small firework: स्पोटकम् (comp.<BR>फट्का).<BR>II A lampoon: परि(री)वादप्रबन्धः,<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squint
SQUINT (subs. and verb): expr. by s. -eyed^1:<BR>q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squint-eyed
SQUINT-EYED:<BR>(1) टेर (f. रा), -क (f. का);<BR>(2) केकर (f. रा);<BR>(3) वलिर (f. रा);<BR>(4)<BR>केदर (f. रा);<BR>(5) टगर (f. रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squire
SQUIRE: महाजनः: v. Gentleman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squirrel
SQUIRREL:<BR>(1) काष्ठविडालः;<BR>(2) काष्ठमार्जारः, and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

squirt
SQUIRT:<BR>I Subs.: धारायन्त्रम्, R.<BR>II Verb:<BR>उदस्यति (अस्, c. 4.): v. To throw out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stab
STAB (v.):<BR>(1) विध्यति (व्यध्, c. 4.): v. To<BR>pierce;<BR>(2) भिनत्ति (भिद्, c. 7.),<BR>to s. in the<BR>secret:<BR>परोक्षे मर्मभेदं करोति: v. To wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stab
STAB (subs.):<BR>(1) विद्धम्;<BR>(2) भिन्नम्, Sr.;<BR>(3)<BR>क्षतम् (=injury).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stability
STABILITY: स्थैर्यम्: v. Firmness, steadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stable
STABLE (adj.): स्थिरः (रा, रं): v. Firm con-<BR>-stant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stable
STABLE (subs.):<BR>I For horses:<BR>(1) मन्दुरा,<BR>s.<BR>keeper:<BR>मन्दुरापालः, K.;<BR>(2) अश्वशाला and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II For elephants (the place where<BR>they are tied up or confined): वारी, R. v.<BR>45.<BR>III For cattle: गोशाला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stable
STABLE (v.): रक्षति (रक्ष्, c. 1.): v. To keep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stabling
STABLING (subs.):<BR>I The act: रक्षणम्।<BR>II<BR>Stable: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stack
STACK (subs.): राशिः: v. Heap, pile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stack
STACK (v.): राशीकरोति: v. To heap, pile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

staff
STAFF:<BR>I Stick: q. v.: दण्डः,<BR>flag-s.:<BR>केतुदण्डः,<BR>D.<BR>II Support: q. v.: आलम्बः, -नम्।<BR>III<BR>Of officers: perh. वर्गः। Ph.:<BR>he belongs to my<BR>s.;<BR>मदधीनस्थः कर्मचारी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stag
STAG:<BR>(1) मृगः;<BR>(2) हरिणः;<BR>(3) कुरङ्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stage
STAGE:<BR>I For acting, etc.: रङ्गः, -भूमिः, -शाला,<BR>then the whole s. was sprightly:<BR>ततः सर्वस्य<BR> रङ्गस्य समुत्पिञ्जलकोऽभवत्, Mah. i. 133. 10. Ph.:<BR>behind the s.:<BR>नेपथ्ये;<BR>speaking off the s.:<BR>आकाश-<BR>वचनम्, Sah. vi.<BR>II Scaffolding: मञ्चः,<BR>in the<BR>s. es.:<BR>मञ्चेषु, R. vi. 1.<BR>III On a journey,<BR>perh.<BR>(1) वसतिः,<BR>passing three s. s:<BR>तिस्रो<BR> वसतीरुषित्वा, R. vii. 33.;<BR>(2) निवासस्थानम्, and<BR>sim. comp.s;<BR>(3) प्रयाणकम् (=march: q. v.).<BR>IV Condition, state: q. v.: दशा,<BR>on the<BR>various s. s of life:<BR>दशान्तरेषु, S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stage-coach
STAGE-COACH: अध्वगयानम् and sim. comp. s (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stage-player
STAGE-PLAYER: रङ्गोपजीविन् (f. नी): v. Player.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stagger
STAGGER: Intrans.:<BR>(1) स्खलति (स्खल्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To reel;<BR>(2) घूर्ण्यते, (घूर्ण्, c. 4.): v.<BR>To roll.<BR>II Trans.: expr. by causal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

staggers
STAGGERS: a disease of animals: घूर्णिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stagnant
STAGNANT:<BR>I Lit.: स्थिर (f. रा): v. Also<BR>motionless.<BR>II Inert, dull: q. v.: जड (f. डा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stagnate
STAGNATE:<BR>I Lit.: स्थिरीभवति।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>शिथिलीमवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stagnation
STAGNATION:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) स्थैर्यम्, स्थिरता, स्थिर-<BR>त्वम्;<BR>(2) निश्चलता।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) मान्द्यम्;<BR>(2) श्लथता;<BR>(3) शिथिलता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

staid
STAID: स्थिर (f. रा): v. Grave, sober.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stain
STAIN (v.):<BR>I In general:<BR>(1) कलङ्कयति, V. t.:<BR>(2) दूषयति (c. of दुष् = pollute),<BR>but I will not<BR>thus s. my great vow of holding arms:<BR>न त्वेवं<BR> दूषयिष्यामि शस्त्रग्रहमहाव्रतम्, Vi. ii. 8.;<BR>(3) मलिनयति<BR>(nomi.), fortune is s. ed by bowing to others:<BR>परिणत्या मलिनीकृताः श्रियः, Ki. xiv. 48.;<BR>(4)<BR>आविलयति (nomi.=3.),<BR>why are you striving to<BR>s. your family:<BR>व्यपदेशमाविलयितुं किमीहसे, Sa. v.<BR>21.;<BR>(5) कलुषयति (nomi.),<BR>fortune s. s even<BR>what is clear:<BR>लक्षमीः स्वच्छमपि कलुषीकरोति, K.<BR>II To dye: q. v.: रञ्जयति (रञ्ज्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stain
STAIN (subs.):<BR>(1) कलङ्कः,<BR>the s. of the wheel-<BR>wright caste:<BR>रथकारकुलकलङ्कस्य, Vi. iii.;<BR>with-<BR>out any s.<BR>निष्कलङ्क (f. ङ्का), Ma. i. 23.;<BR>(3)<BR>अङ्कः (=mark: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stainless
STAINLESS:<BR>(1) निष्कलङ्क<BR>or<BR>अकलङ्क (f. ङ्का),<BR>thus<BR>there is nobody s.:<BR>इत्थं नास्त्यकलङ्कः कोऽपि, Va.;<BR>(2) निर्मलः (ला, लं): v. Pure, chaste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stainlessly
STAINLESSLY:<BR>(1) निष्कलङ्कम्;<BR>(2) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stair
STAIR:<BR>I A flight of steps:<BR>(1) सोपानम्;<BR>(2) निःश्रेणिः(णी) (rare), R. xv. 1.;<BR>(3) अधि-<BR>रोह(हि)णी, M. n.<BR>II A single step:<BR>(1) पर्वन्<BR>(n.), R. xvi. 46.; भङ्गिः(ङ्गी), Me. i. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

staircase
STAIRCASE: सोपानपथः, सोपानपद्धतिः, etc.: v.<BR>Stair (1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stake
STAKE (subs.):<BR>I A wage: q. v.: ग्लहः।<BR>II<BR>Of word:<BR>(1) कीलः;<BR>(2) शङ्कुः।<BR>II For pri-<BR>-soners: शूल (mn.). Ph.: to be in s.:<BR>(1)<BR>संशयस्थ (f. स्था);<BR>(2) संशयमापन्न (f. न्ना) and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stake
STAKE (v.):<BR>I To wager: q. v.: पणते (पण्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II To pierce with a s.: कीलयति<BR>(nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stale
STALE (adj.):<BR>(1) यातयाम (f. मा);<BR>(2) पुराण<BR>(f. णा = old);<BR>(3) दुष्ट (f. ष्टा = spoiled),<BR>s. d<BR>water:<BR>दुष्टं जलम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stale
STALE (v.):<BR>(1) मेहति (मिह्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) मूत्रयति<BR>(मुत्र्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stalk
STALK (subs.):<BR>(1) काण्ड (mn.);<BR>(2) स्तम्बः;<BR>(3) वृन्तम् (= foot-s. of a flower);<BR>(4) मञ्जरी<BR>(of corn).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stalk
STALK (v.):<BR>I To walk proudly: साटोपं परि-<BR>क्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.) and sim. expr.s.<BR>II To<BR>follow stealthily: निःशब्दमनुसरति (सृ, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stalk-horse
STALK-HORSE: Fig.: v. Pretence, pretext.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stall
STALL (subs.):<BR>I A shop: q. v.: पण्यवीथिः,<BR> -का।<BR>II For cattle: शाला। Ph.: s. for cattle:<BR>गोष्ठम्।<BR>III A seat: आसनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stall
STALL (v.): बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.): v. Subs.<BR>and put.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stallion
STALLION: perh. बीजाश्वः and sim. comp.s:<BR>v. Horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stamen
STAMEN:<BR>I Of flower: केसरः।<BR>II Fig.,<BR>specially in pl. stamina.:<BR>(1) सारः;<BR>(2)<BR>सत्त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stammer
STAMMER:<BR>I Verb: perh. तोतलायते (nomi.)<BR>II Subs.: perh. तोतलायितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stammerer
STAMMERER: perh. तोतलः (ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stamp
STAMP (subs.):<BR>I For using: no equiv.:<BR>*ष्टम्पः।<BR>II For making impression: मूद्रा।<BR>III<BR>Of foot:<BR>(1) पदाघातः;<BR>(2) पादप्रहारः।<BR>IV<BR>Mark: q. v.: चिह्नम्। V. Miscell: of high s.:<BR>महाभाव (f. वा);<BR>ordinary s.:<BR>सामान्यप्रकृति (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stamp
STAMP (v.):<BR>I To mark: चिह्नयति (चिह्न्, c.<BR>10.).<BR>II With the foot: पादेन अभिहन्ति<BR>(हन्, c. 2.=to strike: q. v.)<BR>or<BR>मृद्राति, अव-<BR>(मृद्, c. 9. = smash: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stanch
STANCH (adj.): दृढ (f. ढा): v. Firm, constant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stanch
STANCH (v.): v. To stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stanchion
STANCHION: अवस्तम्भः: v. Prop, support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stand
STAND (subs.):<BR>I Stopping, s. still:<BR>to bring<BR>to a s.:<BR>स्तम्भयति<BR>or<BR>स्तभ्नाति: v. To stop;<BR>to<BR>come to s.:<BR>स्तब्धीभवति,<BR>to be at s.:<BR>स्तब्ध (f.<BR>ब्धा), नि-, निस्-। Ph.: to make a s. against:<BR>प्रतीपयति (nomi.): v. To oppose.<BR>II Plat-<BR>-form: q. v.: मञ्चः।<BR>III For other things:<BR>s. for lamps:<BR>दीपाधारः;<BR>ink.s.:<BR>मसीभाजनम्,<BR> -पात्रम्;<BR>salt-s.:<BR>लवणपात्रम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stand
STAND (v. i.):<BR>I Opposed to sit: तिष्ठति (स्था,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>stood determined to fight:<BR>तस्थौ<BR> सिसंग्रामिषुः, B. iii. 47.;<BR>why do you experience<BR>the pain of long s. ing:<BR>किमिति चिरस्थितिक्लेशोऽनु-<BR>भूयते, D. v.<BR>II Not to move: तिष्ठति,<BR>s. ing<BR>when she stood, going when she moved:<BR>स्थितः<BR> स्थितामुच्चलितः प्रयाताम्, R. ii. 6.;<BR>s. s. wretched<BR>goblin:<BR>तिष्ठ तिष्ठ कौणपापसद, Sa. vi.<BR>III To<BR>remain: q. v.: तिष्ठति,<BR>I stood resolved not to<BR>leave the ground on which I slept without ascer-<BR>taining the facts of the case:<BR>नाहमिदं तत्त्वतोऽनव-<BR>बुध्य मोक्ष्यामि भूमिशय्यामिति निश्चितमतिरतिष्ठम्, D.<BR>v.<BR>IV To be situated: तिष्ठति, अव-<BR>or<BR>सं-तिष्ठते,<BR>so s. s the Fig Continent, surrounding the Salt<BR>Ocean:<BR>संवेष्ट्य क्षारमुदधिं प्लक्षद्वीपस्तथा स्थितः, V. p.<BR>ii. 4. 1. V. To adhere: तिष्ठते, आ-,<BR>who s. s<BR>with Karṇa and others:<BR>कर्णादिषु तिष्ठते यः, Ki.<BR>iii. 14.<BR>VI To be, become: q. v.: भवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stand
STAND (v. t.):<BR>I To endure: q. v.: सहते<BR>(सह्, c. 1.).<BR>II To withstand: q. v.<BR>III<BR>To abide by: q. v.: तिष्ठति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stand against
STAND AGAINST: प्रत्यवतिष्ठते, others s. a. this:<BR>अत्रापरे प्रत्यवतिष्ठन्ते, S. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stand by
STAND BY:<BR>I Lit.: उपतिष्ठति।<BR>II To abide<BR>by: तिष्ठति, अवतिष्ठते,<BR>who did not s. by their<BR>superiors' commands:<BR>न शासनेऽवास्थित यो गुरूणाम्, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">Page673</a>]<BR>B. iii. 14.<BR>III To assist: q. v.: prob.<BR>उपतिष्ठति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stand for
STAND FOR:<BR>I In place of: -स्थाने<BR>or<BR>-भूमौ तिष्ठति,<BR> वर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.), etc.<BR>II For the sake of:<BR>अर्थं<BR>or<BR>अर्थे तिष्ठति, वर्तते, etc. Ph.: s. for good<BR>(i. e. lie for ever, die): संतिष्ठते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

standin
STAND(ONE)IN: v. To cost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stand on
STAND ON: fig.: तिष्ठते, आ- (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stand out
STAND OUT:<BR>I To project: q. v.:<BR>II To s.<BR>out against: प्रत्यव-तिष्ठते, prob. प्रतिसं-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stand over
STAND OVER: fig.: अधितिष्ठति (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stand to
STAND TO:<BR>I To abide by: तिष्ठति (with<BR>loc.).<BR>II To be consistent with: संवदति<BR>(वद्, c. 1.); better by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stand under
STAND UNDER: v. To endure, support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stand up
STAND UP:<BR>I Lit.: उत्तिष्ठति।<BR>II Fig.: उत्तिष्ठते:<BR>v. To rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stand with
STAND WITH: i. e. be consistent with: expr.<BR>by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

standard
STANDARD:<BR>I Ensign:<BR>(1) ध्वज (mfn.),<BR>des-<BR>cription of s. s:<BR>ध्वजवर्ण नम्, Mah. vii. 10. 50.;<BR>(2) केतुः<BR>or<BR>केतनम्;<BR>(3) पताका (= flag);<BR>(4)<BR>वैजयन्ती (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

standard-bearer
STANDARD-BEARER:<BR>(1) पताकिन् (m.);<BR>(2)<BR>ध्वजिन् (m.);<BR>(3) वैजयन्तिकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

standing
STANDING (subs.):<BR>I Not sitting or walking:<BR>स्थितिः, R. i. 89.<BR>II Continuance: स्थितिः।<BR>Ph.:<BR>of long s.:<BR>बहोः कालात् (= for a long<BR>time) and sim. expr. s.<BR>III Position, rank:<BR>q. v.: स्थानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stand still
STAND STILL (subs.): v. Stand (I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stanza
STANZA: श्लोकः: v. Verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

staple
STAPLE (subs.):<BR>I Of iron: लोहपुटः (?).<BR>II<BR>Market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

staple
STAPLE (adj.): मुख्य (f. ख्या): v. Chief.<BR>II<BR>Market: q. v.: हट्टः।<BR>III S. product:<BR>प्रधानपण्यम्, and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

star
STAR (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) तारा<BR>or<BR>तारका (not<BR>तारिका), interspersed with s. s and darkness:<BR>तारातमोदन्तुर (f. रा), N. xxii. 17.;<BR>her breast<BR>s. red with eye-drops:<BR>अश्रुबिन्दुतारकितपयोधरा, D.<BR>ii.;<BR>(2) नक्षत्रम् (sp. of the signs),<BR>the s.<BR>under which one is born:<BR>जन्मनक्षत्रम्;<BR>shooting<BR>s.:<BR>नक्षत्रपतनम्, Sr.;<BR>(3) ज्योतिस् (n. = lumi-<BR>-nary), I salute the chief of s. s (moon): ज्योतिषां<BR> पतिमहं महयामि, Pra.;<BR>shooting s. s:<BR>पतमानानि<BR>(पतन्ति) ज्योतींषि, Mah.;<BR>(4) ऋक्ष (rare),<BR>surrounded all around by s. s:<BR>परिवारितः परित<BR> ऋक्षगणैः, Si. ix. 31.;<BR>(5) उडु (mfn.);<BR>(6)<BR>भम्।<BR>II Fig.: of persons: expr. by सूर्यः<BR>(= sun), चन्द्रः (=moon), and their syn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

starboard
STARBOARD: (नावो) दक्षिणपार्श्वः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

starch
STARCH: Subs.: मण्डः (?).<BR>II Verb: perh.<BR>मण्डयति (nomi: comp. माड देओया): v. Also<BR>stiffen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stare
STARE:<BR>I Verb: स्थिरदृष्ट्या निरीक्ष्यते (ईक्ष्, c.<BR>1.): v. To gaze:<BR>II Subs.: स्थिरदृष्टिः:<BR>v. Gaze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

starfish
STARFISH: a marine animal: *समुद्रतारा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stark
STARK (adj.):<BR>I Stiff, rugged: q. v.:<BR>II<BR>Complete, full: q. v.: समग्र (f. ग्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stark
STARK (adj.): सम्पूर्णम्: v. Fully, completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

starlight
STARLIGHT (adv.):<BR>(1) तारावदात (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>ताराप्रकाश (f. शा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

star-like
STAR-LIKE (adj.):<BR>(1) तारानिम (f. भा);<BR>(2)<BR>तारावभास (f. सा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

starling
STARLING: पक्षिविशेषः, *तारका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

starry
STARRY:<BR>I Consisting of, or abounding in<BR>stars:<BR>(1) तारामय (f. यी),<BR>s. refuse:<BR>तारामय-<BR>मस्थियूथम्, N. xxii. 14.;<BR>(2) तारासङ्कुल (f. ला<BR>= covered with stars), R. vi. 22.; and sim.<BR>comp.s;<BR>(3) तारकित (f. ता), D. ii.<BR>II<BR>Starlike: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

start
START (v. i.):<BR>I To set out: q. v.: प्रतिष्ठते<BR>(स्था, c. 1.).<BR>II To move suddenly: चकति,<BR> -ते (चक्, c. 1.),<BR>s. ing:<BR>चकितम्, Sah.<BR>III<BR>कुतोऽपि दयितस्यग्रे चकितं भयसम्भ्रमः, Sah. iii.;<BR>s. ing (= adv.) चकितम्<BR>or<BR>सचकितम्।<BR>IV To<BR>shrink: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

start
START (v. t.):<BR>I To set on foot: प्रवर्तयति (c.<BR>of वृत्),<BR>to s. the teaching of Vedas:<BR>श्रुतिसम्प्रदायं<BR> प्रवर्तयितुम्, M. n. on Si. xiv. 79.<BR>II To alarm,<BR>frighten: q. v.: त्रासयति, सं-, (c. of त्रस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

start after
START AFTER: अनुसरति (सृ, c. 1.): v. To<BR>pursue, run after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

start up
START UP: सहसा उत्तिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1. = rise: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">Page674</a>]<BR>q. v.),<BR>would s.:<BR>सहसा व्यबुध्यत, Ku. v. 57.:<BR>v. To awake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

start
START (subs.):<BR>I Sudden motion: चकितम्।<BR>II Beginning: q. v.: प्रवर्तनम्, -ना।<BR>III A<BR>setting out: प्रस्थानम्। Ph.:<BR>to get or have the<BR>s. of:<BR>पूर्वं प्रवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.: with abl.); by<BR>s. s, perh. प्लुतैः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

starter
STARTER: of a race: perh. धावयितृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

startle i
STARTLE I. Intrans.: चकति, -ते (चक्, c. 1.).<BR>II To alarm, frighten: q. v.: उद्वेजयति (c.<BR>of विज्);<BR>s. ing:<BR>उद्वेगकर (f. री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

starvation
STARVATION: expr. by verb: v. Also fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

starve
STARVE (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.: शीतेन<BR>or<BR>क्षुधया सीदति<BR> अव-, (सद्, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>म्रीयते (मृ, c. 4. = die).<BR>II Fig.: सीदति, अव-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strave
STRAVE (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.: (शीतेन or) क्षुधया<BR> सादयति, अव- (c. of सद्)<BR>or<BR>मारयति (c. of मृ<BR>= kill).<BR>II Fig.: सादयति, अव-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

starveling
STARVELING: क्षुत्क्षामकण्ठ (f. ण्ठा): v. Hungry,<BR>lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

state
STATE (subs.):<BR>I Condition: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>अवस्था;<BR>(2) दशा।<BR>II Government, sover-<BR>-eignty: q. v.: राज्यम्, Ph.: s. affairs:<BR>राजकार्याणि;<BR>s. servant:<BR>राजसेवक (f. विका); etc.<BR>III Grandeur, splendour: q. v.: ऐश्वर्यम।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

state
STATE (v.): कथयति (कथ्, c. 10.): v. To say,<BR>tell, narrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stateliness
STATELINESS: औदार्यम्: v. Grandeur, majesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stately
STATELY: उदार (f. रा): v. Grand, majestic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

statement
STATEMENT: उक्तिः: v. Saying, narration,<BR>representation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

statesman
STATESMAN:<BR>(1) नीतिज्ञ (f. ज्ञा);<BR>(2) नयविद्<BR>(mfn.), and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

statesmanship
STATESMANSHIP:<BR>(1) नयज्ञता;<BR>(2) नीतिकौशलम्,<BR>etc.: v. Also policy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

statics
STATICS: स्थैर्यविज्ञानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

station
STATION (subs.):<BR>I As civil, military or<BR>railway: निवेशः।<BR>II Position, rank: q. v.:<BR>पदम्,<BR>high s.:<BR>उन्नतं पदम्, Ku.<BR>III Situation,<BR>position: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

station
STATION (v.): स्थापयति, अव-, (c. of स्था): v. To<BR>put. Ph.:<BR>s. ed at Burdwan:<BR>वर्धमाननिवेश (f. शा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stationary
STATIONARY: स्थिर (f. रा): v. Fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stationer
STATIONER: पत्रकलमादिविक्रेतृ (f. त्री: (?) and<BR>sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stationery
STATIONERY: पत्रकलमादि (?), and sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

statistical
STATISTICAL: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

statistics
STATISTICS: *संख्यानम्,<BR>s. of crime:<BR>अपराधसंख्यानम्<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

statuary
STATUARY:<BR>I The maker: प्रतिमाकार (f. री)<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR>II The art: प्रतिमानिर्माणम्,<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

statue
STATUE:<BR>(1) प्रतिमा,<BR>stand for s.:<BR>प्रतिमापिण्डिका,<BR>A. p.;<BR>(2) मुर्तिः,<BR>s. keeper:<BR>मूर्तिपः, Mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stature
STATURE: प्रमाणम्: v. Size.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

statute
STATUTE: व्यवस्था: v. Law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

statutory
STATUTORY:<BR>s. provision:<BR>व्यवस्थाविधिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stave
STAVE:<BR>I Of wood: काष्ठखण्डम्।<BR>II Of songs:<BR>भागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stave
STAVE (v.):<BR>I To burst: स्फोटयति (c. of<BR>स्फुट्).<BR>II With off: v. Put off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stay
STAY (v.):<BR>(1) वसति (वस्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>live;<BR>(2) तिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.): v. To remain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stay
STAY (v. t.): स्तभ्नाति (स्तम्भ्, c. 9.): v. To<BR>stop, obstruct, delay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stay
STAY (subs.):<BR>I Sojourn:<BR>(1) अवस्थितिः<BR>(-स्थानम्);<BR>(2) निवासः (rare), Si. xii. 63.<BR>II<BR>A prop: स्तम्भः, उप-।<BR>III Stop, hindrance:<BR>(1) स्तम्भः;<BR>(2) प्रतिष्टम्भः।<BR>IV In pl., bodies:<BR>q. v.: अङ्गिका।<BR>V A rope: रज्जुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stead
STEAD, IN: v. Instead of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steadfast
STEADFAST: स्थिरः (रा, रं): v. Firm, cons-<BR>-tant, true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steadfastness
STEADFASTNESS: स्थिरता: v. Firmness, constancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steadfastly
STEADFASTLY:<BR>(1) दृढम्: v. Firmly;<BR>(2)<BR>सन्ततम्: v. Constantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steadily
STEADILY:<BR>(1) स्थिरम्;<BR>(2) दृढम्;<BR>(3) धीरम्:<BR>v. Steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steadiness
STEADINESS:<BR>(1) स्थैर्यम्;<BR>(2) दार्ढ्यम्;<BR>(3) धैर्यम्:<BR>v. Steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steady
STEADY:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) स्थिर (f. रा = cons-<BR>-tant, fixed),<BR>s. minded:<BR>स्थिरधीः, R. viii. 22.;<BR>one whose actions are steady:<BR>स्थिरकर्मन् (mfn.);<BR>(2) दृढ (f. ढा = firm: q. v.).<BR>II Of men:<BR>धीर (f. रा). Ph.:<BR>to lead a s. life:<BR>न व्यभिचरति,<BR>(चर्, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>सन्मार्गे तिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steak
STEAK: मांसफाली, N. xvi. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steal
STEAL (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) चोरयति (चुर्, c. 10.),<BR>we stole so as to reduce him to earthen<BR>pots:<BR>मृद्भाण्डावशेषमचोरयाव, D. ii.; for s. ing:<BR>चौर्यार्थम्, Viv.;<BR>(2) स्तेनयति (स्तेन्, c. 10.: rare),<BR>for those who s. large animals:<BR>महापशून् स्तेनयतः,<BR>N. s.;<BR>(3) मुष्णाति, परि- (मुष्, c. 9.),<BR>s. ing the<BR>valuable leather from Udāraka:<BR>अजिनरत्नमुदारका-<BR>न्मुषित्वा, D. ii.;<BR>(4) हरति, अप- (हृ, c. 1. = to<BR>take away),<BR>to s. paddy:<BR>धान्यं हरति, M. viii.<BR>320.<BR>II Fig., to s. away: अलक्षितं गच्छति,<BR>(=to go)<BR>or<BR>अपसरति (=go away).<BR>III Fig.,<BR>to s. over or upon=to slip in: अलक्षितं<BR> समाक्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.).<BR>IV To gain or win<BR>unperceived; अपहरति, (your)<BR>heart which is<BR>going to be stolen away by her:<BR>अपह्नियमाणमनया<BR> हृदयम्, K.: v. To rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stealer
STEALER:<BR>(1) स्तेयकृत्,<BR>s. of gold:<BR>सुवर्णस्तेयकृत्,<BR>K. b.;<BR>(2) -मुष्, in comp., s. from travellers:<BR>पांथमुष्, Viv.;<BR>(3) हर्तृ, अप- (f. र्त्री), man-s.:<BR>नरहर्ता, Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stealing
STEALING (subs.): स्तेयम्: v. Theft, robbery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stealth
STEALTH:<BR>I Stealing:<BR>(1) स्तेयम्<BR>or<BR>स्तैन्यम्;<BR>(2) चौरी (or रिका: rare);<BR>(3) मोषः।<BR>II<BR>Fig.:<BR>(1) चौरिका,<BR>marriage by s.:<BR>चौरिका-<BR>विवाहः, Ma. i.;<BR>(2) मोषः,<BR>carrying off Kanaka-<BR>vatī by s.:<BR>कनकवतीं मोषेणापहृत्य, D. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stealthily
STEALTHILY:<BR>(1) चौरिकया;<BR>(2) मोषेण;<BR>(3)<BR>निभृतम् (= quietly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stealthy
STEALTHY:<BR>(1) निभृतः (ता, तं = quiet);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रच्छन्न (f. न्ना hidden);<BR>(3) मौनिन् (f. नी =<BR>silent): v. Also secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steam
STEAM (subs.): बाष्पः,<BR>s. boat:<BR>*बाष्पीयतरी,<BR>s. -engine:<BR>*बाष्पीययन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steam
STEAM (v. i.): बाष्पायते।<BR>S. out or off:<BR>*वाष्पयोगेन<BR> चलति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steam
STEAM (v. t.): *बाष्पितं करीति।<BR>S. out:<BR>*बाष्प-<BR>योगेन चालयति (c. of चल्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steamer
STEAMER: *बाष्पीयपोतः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steed
STEED: वाजिन् (m.): v. Horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steel
STEEL (subs.):<BR>I Prepared iron:<BR>(1)<BR>चित्रायसम्;<BR>(2) शस्त्रम्: v. Iron.<BR>II Weapon:<BR>q. v.: शस्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steel
STEEL (v.):<BR>(1) कठिनीकरोति (= to harden);<BR>(2) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steelyard
STEELYARD: तुलादण्डः: v. Balance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steep
STEEP (adj.):<BR>(1) उत्सर्पिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) दुरारोह<BR>(f. हा = difficult to climb).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steep
STEEP (v.): निःक्षिप्य स्थापयति (c. of स्था): v.<BR>Also to soak, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steeple
STEEPLE:<BR>(1) शिखरम्;<BR>(2) शृङ्गम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steeplechase
STEEPLECHASE: अश्वचर्या: v. Race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steepness
STEEPNESS:<BR>(1) उत्सर्पिता;<BR>(2) दुरारोहता: v. Steep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steer
STEER (v.): चालयति, (c. of चल्): v. To<BR>guide, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steer
STEER (subs.): वत्सतरः, K. iii. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steerage
STEERAGE:<BR>I The act: चालनम्: v. Also<BR>guidance.<BR>II Hinder part of a vessel:<BR>पश्चाद्भागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steerer
STEERER, STEERSMAN:<BR>(1) कर्णधार (f. री);<BR>(2)<BR>कर्णिन् (f. नी: rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stem
STEM (subs.):<BR>I S. of a tree:<BR>(1) काण्ड<BR>(mn.);<BR>(2) स्तम्भः।<BR>II Of a vessel: v.<BR>row.<BR>III Stock: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stem
STEM (v.): प्रतिकूलयति (nomi.): v. To resist,<BR>oppose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stench
STENCH: v. Stink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stenography
STENOGRAPHY: v. Short-hand. Stenographist<BR>: v. S. writer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

step
STEP (subs.):<BR>I A pace:<BR>(1) पदम्,<BR>I cannot<BR>move a single s.:<BR>पदात्पदमपि गन्तुं न शक्नोमि, Ra.<BR>ii.;<BR>at every s.:<BR>पदे पदे, N.;<BR>(2) क्रमः, वि-<BR>(rare),<BR>the s. which covered the spheres of the<BR>sun and the moon:<BR>लङ्घितार्कशशिमण्डलक्रमः, Si. xiv.<BR>75.;<BR>(3) पादन्यासः, पदविक्षेपः, and sim. comp.s<BR>(=throwing of feet).<BR>II Gradation,<BR>degree: क्रमः,<BR>s. by s.:<BR>क्रमशः, A.<BR>III Of a<BR>ladder: भङ्गः(ङ्गिः), वि-: v. Stair.<BR>IV Mea-<BR>-sure, plan: q. v.: उपायः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

step
STEP (v.):<BR>I To throw, set: q. v.: न्यस्यति,<BR> वि- (अस्, c. 4.).<BR>II To move the foot:<BR>पदविक्षेपं करोति and sim. expr.s.<BR>III To<BR>walk: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

step-brother
STEP-BROTHER: अन्यपितृजो भ्राता (by a different<BR>father): अन्योदर्यो भ्राता (by a different<BR>mother): v. Half-brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

step-child
STEP-CHILD: अन्यपितृजः (f. जा)<BR>or<BR>अन्योदर्यः (f.<BR>र्या) पुत्रः (= son)<BR>or<BR>कन्या (= daughter).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

step-father
STEP-FATHER: मातुः पतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

step-mother
STEP-MOTHER: विमातृ (f.) (simply मातृ when<BR>clear, R. xiv. 22.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

steppe
STEPPE: मालं क्षेत्रम्, Me. i. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stereotype
STEREOTYPE: *स्थिराक्षरफलकम्। S. d: fig.: समय-<BR>गत (f. ता), Sah. vii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sterile
STERILE, STERILITY: v. Barren, barrenness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sterling
STERLING:<BR>I Subs.: इंलण्डीयमुद्रा।<BR>II Adj.:<BR>यथार्थ (f. र्था): v. Genuine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stern
STERN (subs.): पश्चाद्भागः: v. Also back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stern
STERN (adj.): परुष (f. षा): v. Harsh, rough,<BR>severe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sternly
STERNLY: परुषम्: v. Harshly, severely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sternness
STERNNESS: पारुष्यम्: v. Harshness, severity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stethoscope
STETHOSCOPE: *हृदयवीक्षणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stew
STEW (subs.):<BR>I S. ed meat: मांसक्वाथः (?).<BR>II<BR>Brothel: q. v.: वेश्यालयः।<BR>III Agitation,<BR>confusion: q. v.: संक्षोभः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stew
STEW (v.): no prop. equiv.: क्वथति (क्वथ्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stewaed
STEWAED, -ESS (v.): परिचारक (f. रिका: v. Also<BR>manager, servant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stewardship
STEWARDSHIP: परिचारकत्वम्, -त्ता (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stick
STICK (subs.):<BR>I A staff:<BR>(1) यष्टिः,<BR>blind-<BR>man's s.:<BR>अन्धस्य यष्टिः, Mah.;<BR>(2) दण्डः,;<BR>(3)<BR>वेत्रम् (= cane);<BR>(4) आषाढः (=Palasa s.), Ku.<BR>v. 30.<BR>II As of sealing wax: perh. यष्टिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stick
STICK (v.):<BR>I To thrust, set: निवेशयति, सम्-<BR>(c. of विश्).<BR>II To adhere: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>लगति, सम्- (लग्, c. 1.), it has stuck fast:<BR>दृढं खलु लग्ना, V. i.;<BR>(2) निविशते (विश्, c. 1.<BR>= enter: q. v.).<BR>III To stop: स्तभ्नाति (स्तम्भ्,<BR>c. 9.). Comp. (a) s. by: v. Stand by;<BR>(b) s. out: v. To project; (c) s. up:<BR>बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.): v. To fasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stickles
STICKLES: पक्षसमर्थक (f. र्थिका): v. Also umpire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sticky
STICKY: संश्लेषक (f. षिका): v. Also glossy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stiff
STIFF:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) संहत (f. ता = compact);<BR>(2) कठिन (f. ना = hard).<BR>II Fig.: कर्कश (f.<BR>शा): v. Harsh, rough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stiffen
STIFFEN:<BR>(1) कठिनीकरोति (=harden);<BR>(2)<BR>रुक्षीकरोति (=roughen).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stiffly
STIFFLY:<BR>(1) कठिनम्: v. Hardly;<BR>(2) रूक्षम्:<BR>v. Roughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stiffness
STIFFNESS:<BR>(1) काठिन्यम्: v. Hardness;<BR>(2)<BR>रौक्षम्: v. Roughness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stifle
STIFLE:<BR>I Lit.: श्वासरोधं करोति<BR>or<BR>श्वासं रुणद्धि,<BR>(रुध्, c. 7.) (with gen.).<BR>II Fig.: स्तभ्नाति<BR>or<BR>स्तम्मयति, सं- (स्तम्भ्, c. 9. and 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stigma
STIGMA: कलङ्कः: v. Stain, disgrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stigmatize
STIGMATIZE:<BR>(1) निन्दति (निन्द्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To censure;<BR>(2) परिवदति (वद्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To defame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stile
STILE:<BR>I Style: q. v.<BR>II Of steps: सोपान-<BR>पद्धतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stiletto
STILETTO: perh. छुरिका: v. Also knife, dagger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

still
STILL (subs.): अधोयन्त्रम्, Wilson; मध्यनिष्कर्ष-<BR>भाण्डम् (भाटि in Bengali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

still
STILL (adj.):<BR>I Without any noise:<BR>(1)<BR>निःशब्द (f. ब्दा);<BR>(2) नीरवः (वा, वं); and<BR>sim. comp.s.: v. Silent.<BR>II Without any<BR>motion:<BR>(1) निश्चलः (ला, लं);<BR>(2) निष्कम्प<BR>(f. म्पा), and sim. comp.s.<BR>III Quiet,<BR>calm: q. v.: शान्त (f. न्ता), प्र-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

still
STILL (v.): शमयति, प्र- (c. of शम्): v. Calm,<BR>still (adj.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

still
STILL (adv.):<BR>I As yet: अद्यापि।<BR>II Yet,<BR>nevertheless: q. v.: तथापि।<BR>III With com-<BR>-paratives: expr. with यावत्॥।तावत्। Ph.:<BR>s.<BR>and anon:<BR>यदा तदा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

still-born
STILL-BORN: मृतजातः (ता, तं), D. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stillness
STILLNESS:<BR>(1) निःशब्दता;<BR>(2) नीरवता;<BR>(3)<BR>निश्चलता;<BR>(4) निष्कम्पता;<BR>(5) शान्तिः, प्र-; etc.:<BR>for dif.: v. Still (adj.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stilly
STILLY:<BR>I Adj.: v. Still.<BR>II Adv.:<BR>(1)<BR>निःशब्दम्: v. Silently:<BR>(2) निष्कम्पम् (=with-<BR>-out agitation);<BR>(3) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stilt
STILT: perh. पादयष्टिः,<BR>to go on s.:<BR>पादयष्टिभ्यां<BR> चरति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stilted
STILTED (adj.): of style: prob. *विकट (f.<BR>टा), Kav.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stimulant
STIMULANT: दीपन (f. नी),<BR>coriander is relishing<BR>and s.:<BR>दीपनं रोचकं धान्यम्, Bha.;<BR>s. to diges-<BR>tion:<BR>अग्निप्रदीपन (f. नी), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stimulate
STIMULATE:<BR>(1) उत्तेजयति (तिज्, c. 10.): v. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">Page677</a>]<BR>To excite;<BR>(2) वर्धयति (c. of वृध्): v. To<BR>increase;<BR>(3) दीपयति (c. of दीप् = warm up).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stimulus
STIMULUS: दीपनम्: Ph.: to give a s.: v. To<BR>stimulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sting
STING (v.):<BR>I Lit.: दशति, वि- (दंश्, c. 1.),<BR>stung by bees, men ran away:<BR>क्षुद्राभिर्विदशयमानेन<BR> जनेन दुद्रुवे, Si. xii. 54.<BR>II Fig.: दहति (दह्,<BR>c. 1. = burn: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sting
STING (subs.):<BR>I The act or wound: दंशः।<BR>II The instrument: चंचुः, (= bill) is used<BR>by M. n. on Si. xii. 44.<BR>III Fig.: दंशः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stingily
STINGILY: expr. by adj.: v. Also meanly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stinginess
STINGINESS: बद्धमुष्टिता: v. Miserliness, mean-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stinging
STINGING (adj.):<BR>(1) दंशक (f. शिका);<BR>(2) कटु<BR>(mfn.: = bitter).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stingy
STINGY: बद्धमुष्टि (mfn.): v. Miser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stink
STINK:<BR>I Subs.: पूति, -गन्धः।<BR>II Verb:<BR>पूतीमवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stinking
STINKING: (adj.):<BR>(1) पूतिगन्धि (mfn.);<BR>(2)<BR>पूति- in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stint
STINT (v.): नियच्छति (यम्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>restrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stint
STINT (subs.): परिमाणम्: v. Quantity, limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stipend
STIPEND: वृत्तिः: v. Also pay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stipendiary
STIPENDIARY:<BR>(1) वेतनभोगिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>वेतनभुज् (mfn.) etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stipulate
STIPULATE: समयं करोति: v. To agree, promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stipulation
STIPULATION: समयः: v. Agreement, condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stir
STIR (v.):<BR>I Trans.:<BR>(1) विलोडयति, आ-, (c.<BR>of लुड्),<BR>s. ring of the ocean:<BR>उदधिविलोडनम्,<BR>Ki. xiv. 83.;<BR>(2) क्षोभयति (c. of क्षुभ् = agi-<BR>-tate, excite: q. v.:).<BR>II Intrans.: क्षुम्यति<BR>(क्षुभ्, c. 4.): v. Agitated, to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stitch
STITCH (v.): आसञ्जयति (c. of सञ्ज् = adhere):<BR>v. Also to sew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stitch
STITCH (subs.):<BR>I Of needle: गुणः।<BR>II A<BR>pain: शूलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stock
STOCK (subs.):<BR>I Capital: q. v.: मूलम्, -धनम्।<BR>Ph.:<BR>s. of cattle:<BR>गोधनम्, Mah.; live s.:<BR>perh. जीवसम्पत्तिः।<BR>II Lineage, origin: q. v.:<BR>मूलम्,<BR>of noble s.:<BR>मौल (f. ली), K.<BR>III Store,<BR>accumulation: q. v.: संचयः q. v.<BR>IV Stem:<BR>q. v.: प्रकाण्डः।<BR>V Block-head: q. v.: स्थूलबुद्धि<BR>(mfn.).<BR>VI Pillar: q. v.: स्तम्भः।<BR>VII<BR>Handle: q. v.: दण्डः।<BR>VIII In pl. for<BR>vessels: *अवष्टम्भः।<BR>IX For the feet: निगडः<BR>(fetters: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stock
STOCK (v.): सम्भरति (भृ, c. 1.): v. To store,<BR>provide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stock
STOCK (adj.): expr. by comp., s. argument:<BR>मूलयुक्तिः: also chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stockbroker
STOCKBROKER: *मूलदल्लालः, मूलविनियामकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stock-dove
STOCK-DOVE: कपोतः: v. Dove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stock-still
STOCK-STILL: स्थाणुरिवाचल (f. ला)<BR>or<BR>स्थिर (f.<BR>रा), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stockade
STOCKADE: यष्टिवृतिः: v. Fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stocking
STOCKING: *पादावरणम्; चरणच्छदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stoic
STOIC:<BR>(1) जिनः (ना, नं) (?);<BR>(2) निःस्पृह (f.<BR>हा = indifferent);<BR>(3) जितेन्द्रिय (f. या = con-<BR>-tinent).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stoic
STOIC, -AL: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stoicism
STOICISM:<BR>(1) जैनम् (?);<BR>(2) निःस्पृहता;<BR>(3)<BR>निःसङ्गता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stoker
STOKER: आङ्गारिक (f. की) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stole
STOLE (subs.): a dress: perh. आप्रपदीनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stolen
STOLEN (adj.): चोरितः (ता, तं) etc.: v. To<BR>steal: S. goods:<BR>(1) लोप्त्रम्, Vri.;<BR>(2) चोरितम्,<BR> -कम्,<BR>if you do not return to the citizens their s.<BR>goods:<BR>न चेन्नागरिकेभ्यश्चोरितकानि प्रत्यर्पयिष्यसि, D.<BR>ii:<BR>(3) मुषितम्, -कम्,<BR>burying the s. goods some-<BR>where:<BR>क्वचिन्मुषितकं निधाय, D. ii.;<BR>(4) चोरित-<BR>द्रव्यम् and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(5) होढम् (rare),<BR>with or without s. property:<BR>सहोढमसहोढंवा, Kat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stolid
STOLID, STOLIDITY: v. Stupid, stupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stomach
STOMACH (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पक्वाशयः, Sr.;<BR>(2) जठरम्: v. Belly.<BR>II Fig., relish: q. v.:<BR>I have no s. for it:<BR>इदं मह्यं न रोचते।<BR>III<BR>Arrogance, haughtiness: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stomach
STOMACH (v.):<BR>I To bear: q. v.: सहते।<BR>II<BR>To dislike: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stomacher
STOMACHER: an ornament:<BR>(1) उरःसूत्रम् (?);<BR>(2) वक्षोभूषणम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stomachic
STOMACHIC (adj. and subs.): of medicines:<BR>अग्निवर्धनः<BR>or<BR>अग्निदीपनः (नी, नं) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stone
STONE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अश्मन् (m.),<BR>even<BR>a s. attains divinity:<BR>अश्मापि याति देवत्वम्, H.;<BR>red s.: (=ruby) ताम्राश्मन्, Si. iii. 7.;<BR>(2)<BR>उपलः, variety of (precious)<BR>s. s:<BR>वैचित्र्यमुपलानाम्,<BR>V. m. 80. 3.;<BR>(3) शिला (not applied to<BR>precious s. s: but applied also to s. for<BR>grinding),<BR>sitting on another s.:<BR>द्वितीयशिला-<BR>तलोपविष्टः, K.; like a (grinding) s. of gold:<BR>कनकशिलानिभः, Ki. xvii. 63.;<BR>(4) पाषाणः<BR>(=3.);<BR>(5) प्रस्तरः (=3);<BR>(6) ग्रावन् (m. = 3);<BR>(7) दृषद् (f.: rare).<BR>II In the bladder:<BR>अश्मन् (m.),<BR>s. -breaking:<BR>अश्मभिद् (mfn.), Sr.;<BR>अश्मरी (the disease).<BR>III Of fruits: अस्थि<BR>(n.= bone).<BR>IV Testicle: q. v.: फलम्,<BR>be<BR>without s. s:<BR>त्वं विफलो भव, Ram. i. 49. 27.<BR>V A weight: *सप्तसेरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stone
STONE (adj.):<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) औपलः<BR>(ली, लं),<BR>as with a s. raft:<BR>यथा प्लवेनौपलेन, M.<BR>iv. 194.<BR>(3) पाषाणमयः (यी, यं), K. b.; and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stone
STONE (v.):<BR>s. to death:<BR>उपलघातं हन्ति (हन्, c.<BR>2. after लोष्टघातं हन्ति, Mu.): v. To kill,<BR>beat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stone-cutter
STONE-CUTTER:<BR>(1) औपलिक (f. की);<BR>(2)<BR>आश्मिक (f. की), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stone-fruit
STONE-FRUIT: अस्थिमत्फलम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stone-hearted
STONE-HEARTED: पाषाणहृदय (f. या);<BR>(2) अश्म-<BR>हृदय (f. या), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stone-pit
STONE-PIT, STONE-QUARRY: प्रस्तरखनिः, and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stones-throw
STONE'S-THROW: पाषाणक्षेपः, and sim. comp.s.<BR>(comp. इषुविक्षेपः, V. p. iii. 118.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stoniness
STONINESS:<BR>(1) पाषाणबाहुल्यम्;<BR>(2) पाषाणसादृशयम्<BR>etc.: v. Stony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stony
STONY:<BR>I Abounding in stone:<BR>(1) पाषाण-<BR>बहुल (f. ला);<BR>(2) उपलसङ्कुल (f. ला), and<BR>sim. comp.s.:<BR>II Made of s.:<BR>(1) शिलामय<BR>(f. यी);<BR>(2) प्रस्तरमय (f. यी);<BR>(3) आश्मन<BR>(f. नी);<BR>(4) औपल (f. ली), etc.<BR>III Like<BR>s.:<BR>(1) by comp.,<BR>s. -heart:<BR>पाषाणहृदयम्;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रस्तरनिम (f. भा), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stool
STOOL:<BR>I A seat: q. v.: पीठः (ठी, ठं).<BR>II<BR>Evacuation: मलोत्सर्गः, and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stoop
STOOP (v. i.):<BR>I To bend the body: गात्रं<BR> नमयति (नम्, c. 10.)<BR>or<BR>आवर्जयति (वृज्, c. 10.).<BR>II Not intentionally: expr. by भग्नपृष्ठक (f.<BR>का = s. ing), K.<BR>III To condescend:<BR>(1)<BR>प्रवणीभवति;<BR>(2) प्रह्वीभवति,<BR>s. ing:<BR>वैतसी वृत्तिः, R.<BR>iv. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stoop
STOOP (subs.):<BR>I Lit.; नतिः।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>प्रणतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stooping
STOOPING (adj.): fig.:<BR>(1) नम्र (f. म्रा);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रणतिप्रवण (f. णा), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stop
STOP (v. t.):<BR>I To close, shut up: q. v.:<BR>वारयति (वृ, c. 10.): v. Also to cover, fill<BR>up;<BR>shall s. all holes:<BR>सर्वं छिद्रं वारयेत्, M. ix.<BR>II To obstruct, prevent: q. v.:<BR>(1) स्तम्भयति,<BR> सं-, अव- (c. of स्तम्भ्),<BR>s. ped by Hoonkāra:<BR>हुङ्कारेण<BR> स्तम्भित (f. ता);<BR>(2) रुणद्धि, सं-, वि-, प्रति-, अव-<BR>(रुध्, c. 7.), I will s. the passage of the sun:<BR>रुणध्मि सवितुर्मार्गम्, B. vi. 35.;<BR>(3) प्रतिबध्नाति<BR>(बन्ध्, c. 9.),<BR>s. s good:<BR>श्रेयः प्रतिबध्नाति,<BR>R. i. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stop
STOP (v. i.):<BR>(1) तिष्ठति, अवतिष्ठते (स्था, c. 1.),<BR>s.<BR>ping for a moment:<BR>मुहूर्तं स्थित्वा, Me. i. 19.;<BR>did not go nor s.:<BR>न ययौ न तस्थौ, Ku. v. 85.;<BR>if my pen does not s. for a moment:<BR>यदि मे<BR> लेखनी क्षणं नावतिष्ठेत, Mah. 78.;<BR>(2) शाम्यति, प्र-<BR>(शम्, c. 4.=to be quiet), when it (the ball)<BR>s. ped, made it fly up, and on the reverse made it<BR>s.:<BR>प्रशान्तं तमुदपातयद् विपर्ययेण च प्राशमयत्, D. vi.:<BR>v. To cease;<BR>(3) विश्राम्यति (श्रम्, c. 3.=rest:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stop
STOP (subs.):<BR>I Obstruction, hindrance:<BR>q. v.: स्तम्भः, प्रति-। Ph.:<BR>to put a s. to:<BR>प्रतिष्ट-<BR>म्भयति (c. of स्तम्भ्): v. To stop.<BR>II Pause,<BR>cessation^1: q. v.:<BR>(1) स्थितिः;<BR>(2) अवस्थितिः;<BR>(3) प्रशान्तिः;<BR>(4) विश्रान्तिः।<BR>III In punctua-<BR>-tion: विरामः, बिन्दुः (?).<BR>IV In music; नाहः<BR>(?)<BR>V Of an organ: दण्डः (?).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stop-cock
STOP-COCK: perh. प्रतिष्टम्भः<BR>or<BR>अवष्टम्भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stoppage
STOPPAGE:<BR>I Stay, rest: q. v.: स्थितिः, अव-।<BR>II Obstruction, hindrance: q. v.: स्तम्भः,<BR> प्रति-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stopper
STOPPER, STOPPLE:<BR>(1) रोधः (?);<BR>(2) प्रतिष्टम्भः<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

storage
STORAGE:<BR>(1) सञ्चयः;<BR>(2) सम्मारः;<BR>(3) समाहारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

store
STORE (v.):<BR>(1) संभरति (भृ, c. 1.),<BR>s. ing money<BR>for spending:<BR>त्यागाय संभृतार्थानाम्, R. i. 7.;<BR>(2)<BR>संचिनोति (चि, c. 5.),<BR>how much blood have<BR>you s. d up:<BR>अथ कियत्प्रभूतं त्वया सञ्चितं रुधिरम्,<BR>Ve. iii.; (हृ, c. 1.): v. To collect;<BR>(4)<BR>परिपूरयति (पूर्, c. 10.: v. To fill up).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

store
STORE:<BR>(1) सम्भारः,<BR>sacrificial s. s:<BR>यज्ञसंभारविस्तरः,<BR>Ram. xi. 17.;<BR>(2) सञ्चयः, or s. of excellencies:<BR>सञ्चयो वा गुणानाम्, Vi. ii. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

storehouse
STOREHOUSE:<BR>(1) कोषः: v. Treasury;<BR>(2)<BR>भाण्डारम्, (of things);<BR>(3) आगारम् (=house)<BR>as भाण्डागारम्, Mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

store-keeper
STORE-KEEPER:<BR>(1) भाण्डारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2)<BR>भाण्डाराध्यक्ष (f. क्षा) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

storey
STOREY:<BR>(1) भूमिः, N.;<BR>(2) तलम्, Seven-s. ed:<BR>सप्ततल (f. ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stork
STORK: सारसः: v. Crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

storm
STORM:<BR>I Of wind:<BR>(1) वात्या;<BR>(2) चण्डवातः,<BR>heavy rain came on accompanied with violent s.:<BR>चण्डवातं महद्वर्षं प्रादुरासीत्, Mah. iii. 143. 7.;<BR>(3) प्रभञ्जनः; भ्कञ्भ्का, -वातः, (=hurricane).<BR>II<BR>S. ing:<BR>(1) आस्कन्दः, -नम्<BR>or<BR>-न्दितम्;<BR>(2) ग्रहणम्<BR>(=taking).<BR>III Commotion, rage: q. v.:<BR>संरम्भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

storm
STORM (v. t.):<BR>(1) आस्कन्दति (स्कन्द्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To attack;<BR>(2) गृह्नाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.): v. To<BR>take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

storm
STORM (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.: expr. by subs.<BR>II<BR>Fig.: v. To rage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stormy
STORMY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्रचण्डवात (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>वात्याकुल (f. ला);<BR>(3) वातल (f. ला = windy);<BR>(4) by subs.<BR>II Violent, furious: q. v.:<BR>संरब्ध (f. ब्धा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

story
STORY:<BR>I A tale:<BR>(1) कथा,<BR>second s.:<BR>कथा २,<BR>P.;<BR>(2) इतिहासः, this old s. runs about it:<BR>अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम्, Mah. xii. 175. 2.<BR>II History: q. v.:<BR>(1) इतिहासः;<BR>(2) वृत्तान्तः,<BR>(what has happened to one), K.<BR>III A<BR>lie: q. v.: अलीकः (का, कं).<BR>IV Of a house:<BR>भूमिः: v. Storey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

story-teller
STORY-TELLER:<BR>I Narrator: कथकः, K. s. 10.<BR>2.<BR>II Liar; q. v.: मिथ्यावादिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stout
STOUT:<BR>I Lit.: स्थूलकायः (या, यं): v. Fat,<BR>corpulent.<BR>II Fig., brave, resolute: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stout-hearted
STOUT-HEARTED: बृहन्मनस्, (mfn.), Ki. xviii.<BR>3.: v. Brave, resolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stoutly
STOUTLY:<BR>(1) स्फीतम्;<BR>(2) प्रगल्भम् (= boldly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stove
STOVE: चुल्ली: v. Fire-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stow
STOW: v. To store, put.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

straddle
STRADDLE (v.): जङ्घे पृथक् कृत्वा तिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.<BR>=remain)<BR>or<BR>उपविशति (विश्, c. 6. = sit) (with<BR>loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

straggle
STRAGGLE: व्यभिचरति (चर्, c. 1.): v. Also<BR>to wander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

straggler
STRAGGLER: व्यभिचारिन् (f. णी): v. Also<BR>vagabond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

straight
STRAIGHT (adv.):<BR>(1) सरल (f. ला), s. line:<BR>सरला रेखा, K. d.;<BR>(2) ऋजु (f. ज्वी),<BR>making<BR>the nose s.:<BR>नासामृज्वीं कृत्वा, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

straight
STRAIGHT (adv.):<BR>I Instantly: q. v.: सपदि।<BR>II Directly: perh. परावरम्, comp. वरावर।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

straighten
STRAIGHTEN:<BR>(1) ऋजूकरोति;<BR>(2) सरलीकरोति;<BR>(3) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

straightforward
STRAIGHTFORWARD: सरलप्रकृति (mfn.): v. Also<BR>frank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

staightforwardly
STAIGHTFORWARDLY:<BR>(1) सरलम्;<BR>(2) स्फुटम्।<BR>: v. Openly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

straightforwardness
STRAIGHTFORWARDNESS:<BR>(1) आर्जवम्;<BR>(2)<BR>सरलता: v. Frankness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

straightway
STRAIGHTWAY: सपदि: v. Instantly, imme-<BR>-diately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strain
STRAIN (v. t.):<BR>I In gen.: आयासयति (c. of<BR>यस्): v. Also to stretch;<BR>why have I s. ed<BR>myself for nothing:<BR>किमिति निरर्थकमात्मा मयाया-<BR>सितः, K.<BR>II To filter:<BR>(1) गालयति, (c. of<BR>गल्),<BR>s. ed through cloth:<BR>वस्त्रगालित (f. ता),<BR>Bha.;<BR>(2) स्रावयति (c. of स्रु),<BR>to s. through<BR>cloth:<BR>स्रावयेत् पटात्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strain
STRAIN (v. i.):<BR>I In gen.: आयस्यति (यस्, c.<BR>4.): v. To exert, labour.<BR>II To filter:<BR>गलति, (गल्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strain
STRAIN (subs.):<BR>I The act.:<BR>(1) आयासः;<BR>(2) आयासितम्, (rare).<BR>II Style: q. v.: रीतिः।<BR>III Of music: रागः।<BR>IV Theme: q. v.:<BR>विषयः।<BR>V Tendency: q. v.: प्रवणता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strained
STRAINED (adj.): Fig.: क्लिष्ट (f. ष्टा), नेयार्थमथ<BR> भवेत् क्लिष्टम्, Kav.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strainer
STRAINER: गालनी (after चालनी) for cleansing<BR>rice, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strait
STRAIT (adj.): संकीर्ण (f. र्णा): v. Narrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strait
STRAIT (subs.):<BR>I Distress: q. v.: कृच्छ्रम्।<BR>II<BR>Of sea:<BR>(1) प्रणाली (?);<BR>(2) सागरसङ्करः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strait-laced
STRAIT-LACED: Fig.: v. Rigid, strict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strait-waist-coat
STRAIT-WAIST-COAT: वस्त्रबद्धः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

straiten
STRAITEN: बाधते (बाध्, c. 1.): v. To torment.<BR>Ph.:<BR>s. d circumstances:<BR>कृच्छ्रम्: v. Distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

straitly
STRAITLY: संकीर्णम्: v. Closely, narrowly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strand
STRAND:<BR>I Subs.: तीरम्: v. Shore.<BR>II<BR>Verb.: v. To ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strange
STRANGE (adj.):<BR>I Foreign: q. v.: विदेशीय<BR>(f. या).<BR>II Another's: q. v.: परकीय (f.<BR>या).<BR>III New: q. v.:<BR>(1) अपूर्व (f. र्वा);<BR>(2) चित्र (f. त्रा): v. Wonderful.<BR>IV<BR>Odd.: q. v.: अपरूप (f. पा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strange
STRANGE (exclam.): चित्रम्, s. it was not satiated<BR>चित्रमापदपतृष्णतां न सा, N. xviii. 124.; s., very<BR>s., some divine (being)<BR>is rising from it:<BR>चित्रं<BR> चित्रमुदेति कोऽप्ययमितो दिव्यः, Vi. v. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strangely
STRANGELY: चित्रम्: v. Also wonderfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strangeness
STRANGENESS:<BR>(1) विचित्रता;<BR>(2) वैचित्र्यम्: v.<BR>Also wonderfulness, unusuality, novelty,<BR>oddness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stranger
STRANGER:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) आगन्तुक (f. का): v.<BR>New-comer;<BR>(2) वैदेशिक (f. की): v. For-<BR>-eigner.<BR>II Not acquainted with: अपरिचित<BR>(f. ता): v. Acquaintance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strangle
STRANGLE, STRANGULATE: कण्ठं मर्दयित्वा or<BR>निपीड्य मारयति (c. of मृ): v. Also suffocate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strangulation
STRANGULATION: expr. by verb: v. Also<BR>suffocation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strap
STRAP:<BR>I Subs.: चर्मपट्टः and sim. comp. s.<BR>II Verb: चर्मपट्टेन न आहन्ति (हन्, c. 2.): v.<BR>To strike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strapping
STRAPPING (adj.): अतिप्रमाण (f. णा): v. Also<BR>tall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strangury
STRANGURY: a disease: मूत्रकृच्छ्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strategem
STRATEGEM: छलम्: v. Deceit, pretext, arti-<BR>-fice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strategic
STRATEGIC: expr. by comp. or circumlo.: v.<BR>Also skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strategically
STRATEGICALLY: कौशलेन: v. Skilfully, art-<BR>-fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strategy
STRATEGY: युद्धकौशलम्: v. Skill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stratified
STRATIFIED: perh. स्तरीभूत (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stratum
STRATUM: स्तरः: v. Layer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

straw
STRAW (subs.):<BR>I Of corn:<BR>(1) पलः;<BR>(2)<BR>पलालः;<BR>(3) नालः।<BR>II Fig.: तृणम्,<BR>not to care a<BR>s. for:<BR>न तृणाय मन्यते: v. To care. Ph.:<BR>a (man)<BR>of s.:<BR>अकिञ्चन (f. ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strawberry
STRAWBERRY:<BR>a plant and its fruit:<BR>*कोषजम्बुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stray
STRAY (adj.):<BR>(1) उन्मुक्त (f. क्ता);<BR>(2) आगन्तुक<BR>(f. का = strange), Mit.;<BR>(3) यूथभ्रष्ट (f. ष्टा), and<BR>sim. comp.s (= separated from a flock).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stray
STRAY (v.): इतस्ततश्चरति (चर, c. 1.): v. Also<BR>to wander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

streak
STREAK:<BR>I Subs.: रेखा: v. Stripe.<BR>II Verb.:<BR>expr. by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

streaky
STREAKY: रेखाभिश्चित्रितः (f. ता); कल्माषित<BR>(f. ता): v. Striped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stream
STREAM (subs.):<BR>I Of water:<BR>(1) स्रोतस् (n.),<BR>tasting waters of s. s:<BR>पयः स्रोतसामुपयुज्य, Me. i.<BR>13.;<BR>(2) सरित् (f.),<BR>making s. s shallow:<BR>सरितः<BR> कुर्वती गाधाः, R. iv. 24.: v. Also river.<BR>II<BR>Current: q. v.: स्रोतस्।<BR>III Flow: q. v.:<BR>धारा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stream
STREAM (v.): वर्षति, अभि- (वृष्, c. 1.=to<BR>shower): v. Also to pour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

streamer
STREAMER:<BR>I A flag: q. v.: वैजयन्ती।<BR>II A<BR>stream of light: *आलोकप्रवाहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

streamlet
STREAMLET:<BR>(1) कुसरित् (f.), H.;<BR>(2) क्षुद्र-<BR>सरित् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

street
STREET:<BR>(1) राजपथ: and sim. comp.s.<BR>(=royal s.),<BR>the high s. is frequented by<BR>jackals:<BR>स वाह्यते राजपथः शिवाभिः, R. xvi. 12.;<BR>(2) महापथः and sim. comp.s. (= big road),<BR>its s. s were strewed with coral flowers:<BR>सन्तान-<BR>काकीर्णमहापथं तत्, Ku. vii. 3.;<BR>(3) रथ्या<BR>(= carriage road),<BR>in every s.:<BR>प्रतिरथ्यम्, Si.<BR>31. iii.: v. Road, way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strength
STRENGTH:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) बलम्,<BR>for possessing<BR>s.:<BR>बलशालितया, Ki.; to know from me the s. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">Page681</a>]<BR>and weakness of the three objects:<BR>इतस्त्रिवर्गबल-<BR>लाघवज्ञानम्, D. ii.;<BR>these are the eight-fold s.<BR>(of a state):<BR>तदष्टाङ्गबलं स्मृतम्, Mah. xii. 121.<BR>44.;<BR>(2) वीर्यम्, (=manliness),<BR>equal to<BR>Viṣṇu in s.:<BR>विष्णुना सदृशो वीर्ये, Ram. 21.;<BR>(3) शक्तिः (power),<BR>or if he has s, away<BR>with begging:<BR>अयास्ति शक्तिः कृतमेव याच्ञया, Ki.<BR>xiv. 20.;<BR>(4) सामर्थ्यम् (=3), to take up s.:<BR>सामर्थ्यमवलम्बते, M.n.;<BR>(5) प्राणता (physical),<BR>wonderful s.:<BR>विस्मयजननी प्राणता, K.;<BR>(6) ओजस्<BR>(of style), Kav.<BR>II Force measured: expr.<BR>by कियत् (=how many, एतावत्) (= so many),<BR>etc.: q. v. Ph.:<BR>on the s. of:<BR>ऊ(उ)री-<BR>or<BR>उररी-<BR>कृत्य (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strengthen
STRENGTHEN:<BR>I Trans.:<BR>(1) प्रबलयति (nomi.),<BR>s. s spirit:<BR>सत्वं प्रबलयति, Vi. ii. 15.;<BR>(2) प्रबली-<BR>करोति;<BR>(3) by adj.: v. Strong: v. Also<BR>confirmed.<BR>II Intrans.: प्रबलीभवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strengthening
STRENGTHENING (adj.):<BR>(1) बल्य (f. ल्या);<BR>(2)<BR>बलवर्द्धन (f. नी);<BR>(3) बलप्रद (f. दा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strenuous
STRENUOUS:<BR>(1) सोत्साह (f. हा): v. Zealous;<BR>साग्रह (f. हा): v. Persistent;<BR>(3) प्रगल्भ<BR>(f. ल्भा): v. Bold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strenuously
STRENUOUSLY:<BR>(1) सोत्साहम्;<BR>(2) साग्रहम्;<BR>(3)<BR>प्रगल्भम्: v. adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strenousness
STRENOUSNESS:<BR>(1) उत्साहः: v. Zeal;<BR>(2)<BR>आग्रहः: v. Persistency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stress
STRESS:<BR>I Pressure: भारः।<BR>II Emphasis:<BR>गुरुत्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stretch
STRETCH (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) प्रसारयति (c. of,<BR>सृ),<BR>s. ing the arms:<BR>प्रसार्य हस्तौ, Mah.;<BR>to s.<BR>thread:<BR>सूत्रं प्रसारयति, Mat.;<BR>(2) लम्बयति (c. of<BR>लम्ब् = elongate),<BR>who will stretch (his) hand<BR>to take it:<BR>को लम्बयेदाहरणाय हस्तम्: v. Spread.<BR>II Fig.: perh. प्रसारयति।<BR>III विस्तारयति<BR>(c. of स्तॄ),<BR>s. ing the body:<BR>अङ्गं विस्तार्य, Vi.<BR>v. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stretch
STRETCH (v. i.): प्रसरति: (सृ, c. 1.): v. To<BR>spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stretch
STRETCH (subs.):<BR>I The act: प्रसारणम्।<BR>II<BR>Extent: q. v.: प्रसरः।<BR>III Effort: q. v.: यत्नः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stretcher
STRETCHER:<BR>I Litter: शिविका।<BR>II In boats<BR>etc.: पिण्डिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strew
STREW: किरति, वि-, प्र-, अव-, आ- (कॄ, c. 6.)<BR>: v. To scatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strict
STRICT: perh. अशिथिल (f. ला) in every sense<BR>: v. Also severe, firm, nice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strictly
STRICTLY: अशिथिलम्। (?): v. Also severely,<BR>firmly, nicely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strictness
STRICTNESS: अशैथिल्यम् (?): v. Severity, firm-<BR>-ness, nicety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stricture
STRICTURE:<BR>I Censure: q. v.: भर्त्सना।<BR>II<BR>In medicine:<BR>urethral s.:<BR>मूत्रग्रन्थिः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stride
STRIDE:<BR>I Subs.: विक्रमः: v. Step.<BR>II Verb:<BR>क्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.).: v. Also to advance,<BR>cross.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strife
STRIFE: कलिः: v. Quarrel, dispute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strike
STRIKE (v. t.):<BR>I To hit.:<BR>(1) हन्ति, अभि-, उप-,<BR> आ-, परा-, समा-, वि-, (हन्, c. 2.),<BR>s. ing him on<BR>the breast with the knee:<BR>एनं वक्षस्याहत्य जानुना,<BR>V. p. v. 20. 65.;<BR>s. back:<BR>प्रतिहन्ति, Ki. xviii.<BR>1.;<BR>s. ing the ball:<BR>कन्दुकं समाहत्य, D. vi. (not<BR>of musical instruments);<BR>(2) प्रहरति, सं-<BR>(हृ, c. 1.),<BR>struck him on the breast with a<BR>knife:<BR>छुरिकयोरसि प्राहार्षम्, D. ii.;<BR>(3) ताडयति,<BR> अभि-, (तड्, c. 10.), “श्रोतुर्वितन्त्रीरिव ताड्यमानाः”<BR>Ku. i. 45.<BR>II Of clocks etc.: it s. s one:<BR>*एको वाद्यते।<BR>III To stamp, coin (money):<BR>टङ्कयति (टङ्क्, c. 10.).<BR>IV Of plants:<BR>s. ing<BR>root deep:<BR>स्थिरबद्धमूलः (ला, लं).<BR>V To lower,<BR>let down, as of sail: पातयति, अव-, (c. of पत्).<BR>VI To affect, impress strongly:<BR>(1)<BR>उपहन्ति;<BR>(2) अभि-प्लावयति, सं- वि- (c. of प्ल),<BR>struck with fear:<BR>भयविप्लुतम्, Ki. xiii. 24.<BR>VII To afflict:<BR>to s. blind:<BR>अन्धीकरोति;<BR>to<BR>be struck dumb:<BR>मूकीभवति, etc.<BR>VIII To<BR>produce: q. v.: जनयति (जन्, c. 10.). Ph.:<BR>to s. sail i. e. to stop: q. v.; to s. account i. e.<BR>to balance: q. v.;<BR>to s. ground:<BR>भूमौ लगति;<BR>it s. s me:<BR>इदं मे प्रतिभाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strike
STRIKE: (v. i.):<BR>I Lit.: v. (v. t. l.); s. against:<BR>प्रतिहन्ति।<BR>II To be stranded: भूमौ etc. लगति<BR>(लग्, c. 1.).<BR>III To quit work: perh.<BR>संहताः कर्म परित्यजन्ति।<BR>IV To lower flag: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strike down
STRIKE DOWN (v.): पातयति, अव- (c. of पत्)<BR>: v. To fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strike for
STRIKE FOR: प्रतिष्ठते (स्था, c. 1.): v. To set<BR>out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strike in
STRIKE IN:<BR>I To come in: समुपगच्छति (गम्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II To interrupt: q. v.: v. Also to<BR>strike (III).<BR>III With with: v. To side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strike off
STRIKE OFF:<BR>I To erase, deduct: q. v.:<BR>शोधयति (c. of शुध्).<BR>II To print: q. v.<BR>III<BR>Cut off: q. v.: विघटयति (c. of घट्), Vi.<BR>iii. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strike out
STRIKE OUT:<BR>I As fire: निघृष्य<BR>or<BR>घट्टयित्वा<BR> जनयति (c. of जन्).<BR>II To erase, obliterate:<BR>q. v.: लुम्पति (लुप्, c. 6.).<BR>III To contrive,<BR>invent: q. v.: कल्पयति (c. of कॢप्).<BR>IV To<BR>wander: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strike through
STRIKE THROUGH: भिनत्ति (भिद्, c. 7.).: v.<BR>To pierce, penetrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strike up
STRIKE UP:<BR>I To strike: q. v.<BR>II To begin:<BR>q. v.: प्रस्तौति (स्तु, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strike
STRIKE (subs.):<BR>I Bushel: q. v.<BR>II Combina-<BR>-tion: सम्भूय कर्मपरित्यागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

striker
STRIKER:<BR>(1) ताडयितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) आस्फालयितृ<BR>(f. त्री) (=harper).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

striking
STRIKING (adj.):<BR>I विचित्र (f. त्रा): v. Wonder-<BR>-ful;<BR>s. shade:<BR>भूयिष्टा छाया, U. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strikingly
STRIKINGLY: चित्रम्: v. Wonderfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

string
STRING (v.):<BR>I Gen.:<BR>(1) ग्रथ्नाति (ग्रन्थ्, c. 9.),<BR>strung the garland of speech:<BR>वचःस्रजं जग्रन्थ, N.<BR>xiv. 13.;<BR>s. together:<BR>संग्रथ्नाति, K.;<BR>(2) गुम्फति<BR>(गुम्फ्, c. 1.),<BR>another s. ing flowers:<BR>अपरा<BR> सुमनसो गुम्फति, M. i.<BR>II To furnish with s. s:<BR>(1) perh. तन्त्रयति (nomi.);<BR>(2) तन्त्रीभिः or<BR>गुणैराकलयति<BR>or<BR>बध्नाति (कल्, c. 10<BR>or<BR>बन्ध्, c. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

string
STRING (subs.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) गुणः, bow-s.:<BR>धनुर्गुणः, H.;<BR>constantly harping the s. s of the<BR>lyre:<BR>अजस्नमास्फालितवल्लकीगुणः, Si. i. 9.;<BR>like<BR>clouds in autumn with s. s of lightning:<BR>घनं<BR> घनान्ते तडितां गुणैरिव, Si. i. 7.;<BR>(2) तन्त्रः (-न्त्री),<BR>(a lute)<BR>with seven s.s:<BR>सप्ततन्त्री;<BR>like a bad s. ed<BR>(lute):<BR>वितन्त्रीरिव, Ku. i. 45.;<BR>(3) तन्तुः<BR>(=thread: q. v. ),<BR>with s.s of creepers:<BR>वल्ली-<BR>तन्तुभिः, Si. i. 45.;<BR>(4) रज्जुः (=rope: q. v. ).<BR>II Human: शिरा, शिराभिरिव परिगतो व्रततिभिः,<BR>K.<BR>III A series, succession: q. v.: ततिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stringency
STRINGENCY: कठोरता: v. Severity, strictness,<BR>hardness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stringent
STRINGENT: कठोर (f. रा): v. Severe, hard,<BR>strict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stringently
STRINGENTLY:<BR>(1) कठोरम्: v. Hardly;<BR>(2)<BR>दृढम्: v. Firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stringy
STRINGY:<BR>I Lit.: तन्तुमय (f. यी).<BR>II Sticky:<BR>श्यान (f. ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strip
STRIP (v.t.):<BR>(1) by comp. with वि-, निर्-, or<BR>अप-,<BR>to s. the clothes off:<BR>विवस्त्रयति;<BR>to s. the<BR>bark off:<BR>विवल्कयति; to s. the leaves off:<BR>निष्पत्रयति, Mah.;<BR>a s. ped sword:<BR>विकोषोऽसिः,<BR>Ki. xvii. 45.;<BR>s. ped of the bow:<BR>विकार्मुक (f. का),<BR>Ki. xvii. 53.;<BR>s. ped off, of skin:<BR>अपत्वच्<BR>(mfn.), D. vii.;<BR>s. ped of water:<BR>अपपयस् (mfn.),<BR>Ki. v. 12.;<BR>(2) हरति (हृ, c. 1. = to deprive of:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strip
STRIP (v.i.): विवस्त्रीभवति: v. To undress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strip
STRIP (subs.): खण्ड (mn.): v. Piece.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stripe
STRIPE (subs.):<BR>I =Line: रे(ले)खा,<BR>variegated<BR>with black, yellow, green and pink s. s.:<BR>असित-<BR>पीतहरितपाटलाभिर्लेखाभिः कल्माषित (f. ता), K.;<BR>s.s of striking the bow-string:<BR>ज्याघातरेखे, R.<BR>vi. 55.<BR>II Stroke: कशाघातः and sim.<BR>comp.s.;<BR>deserving s.:<BR>कशार्ह (f. र्हा)<BR>or<BR>कश्य<BR>(f. श्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stripe
STRIPE (v.):<BR>I With lines: ले(रे)खाभिः कल्माषयति<BR>(nomi.).<BR>II To lash:<BR>(1) कशाघातं करोति;<BR>(2) कशया ताडयति (तड्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stripling
STRIPLING: शिशुः: v. Child, youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strive
STRIVE:<BR>I To endeavour, attempt: q. v.:<BR>यतते, प्र- (यत्, c. 1.), some s. s after success:<BR>कश्चिद् यतति सिद्धये, G. vii. 3.<BR>II With against:<BR>प्रतिकूलयति (nomi.): v. To oppose (II).<BR>III<BR>To vie: q. v.: स्पर्द्धते (स्पर्द्ध्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

striving
STRIVING:<BR>I Subs.: यत्नः: v. Attempt, end-<BR>-eavour.<BR>II Adj.: यत्नवत् (f. ती) and sim.<BR>comp.s: v. Active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stroke
STROKE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.;<BR>(1) आघातः;<BR>(2)<BR>अभिघातः;<BR>(3) आहतिः (rare), s. of arm:<BR>भुजाहतिः, Ki. xviii. 3.;<BR>(4) क्षेपः (=throw:<BR>as of oars);<BR>(5) पातः (= fall: as of thunder).<BR>II A line: रेखा: q. v. Ph.; with a s. of the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">Page683</a>]<BR>pen:<BR>*एकेनैव कलमेन।<BR>III Sudden attack:<BR>q. v.: आवेशः।<BR>IV Masterly effort: प्रयत्नः।<BR>Ph.:<BR>s. of policy:<BR>नीतिकौशलम्;<BR>upon the s. of<BR>ten:<BR>दशघटिका वाद्यते (?); to keep s. (in rowing)<BR>यथातथं क्षिपति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stroke
STROKE (v.):<BR>(1) परामृशति (मृश्, c. 6.),<BR>s. ing<BR>his body:<BR>तदीयमङ्गं परामृशन्, R. iii. 68.;<BR>(2)<BR>स्पृशति (स्पृश्, c. 6. = to touch).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stroll
STROLL (v.): परिक्रामति<BR>or<BR>क्राम्यति (क्रम्, c. 1.<BR>and 4.),<BR>tell the soldiers not to s. about<BR>on the skirts of the hermitage:<BR>उच्यन्तां<BR> सैनिका न कैश्चिदाश्रमाम्यर्णभूमयः परिक्राम्यन्तामिति,<BR>Vi. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stroll
STROLL (subs.): परिक्रमः, -णम्: v. Also ramble,<BR>wandering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stroller
STROLLER: परिव्राजक (f. जिका): v. Also<BR>rambler, wanderer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strong
STRONG:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) बलवत् (f. ती),<BR>being<BR>s.:<BR>बलवानपि, Ki. ii. 37.;<BR>men are s. with<BR>money:<BR>धनेन बलवान् लोकः, H.;<BR>s. thirst:<BR>बलवती<BR> पिपासा, K.;<BR>by s. er fate:<BR>बलीयसा विधिना, Ki.<BR>xiv. 63.;<BR>(2) प्रबल (f. ला),<BR>to destroy the s.<BR>enemy:<BR>प्रणाशनाय प्रबलस्य विद्विषः, R. iii. 60.;<BR>s. pain:<BR>प्रबला वेदना, K.;<BR>(3) ऊर्जित (f. ता),<BR>s. bow:<BR>ऊर्जितं धनुः, R. xi. 64.; s. lustre:<BR>ऊर्जितं तेजः, Ve. i.; (language)<BR>s. like the ruffled<BR>sea:<BR>क्षुभितोदन्वदूर्जितम्, Ki. ii. 40.;<BR>(4) ऊर्जस्वल<BR>(f. ला),<BR>those s. horses and elephants:<BR>ऊर्जस्वलं<BR> हस्तितुरङ्गमेतत्, B. iii. 55.;<BR>(5) वीर्यवत् (f. ती):<BR>v. Valiant, powerful;<BR>(6) बलशालिन् (f. नी)<BR>and sim. comp s. (physically). Ph.:<BR>a<BR>naturally s. fortress:<BR>प्रकृत्या सुरक्षितं दुर्गम्, Mah.<BR>iii. 15. 17.<BR>II Able, competent: q. v.: क्षम<BR>(f. मा),<BR>s. for his work:<BR>आत्मकर्मक्षम (f. मा),<BR>R. i. 13.<BR>III Firm, resolute: दृढ (f. ढा).<BR>IV Sharp (as of smell): q. v.: उग्र (f.<BR>ग्रा).<BR>V Deep (as of colour): q. v.: गाढ<BR>(f. ढा).<BR>VI Undecayed: q. v.: अक्षीण (f.<BR>णा).<BR>VII =numbering: q. v.:1000 s.:<BR>सहस्रसंख्यक (f. का). S. er- superior: q. v.<BR>To<BR>make s.:<BR>बलं ददाति (दा, c. 3.=give or वर्द्धयति,<BR>c. of वृध् =increase).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strong-bodied
STRONG-BODIED, STRONG-BUILT:<BR>(1) मांसल (f.<BR>ला);<BR>(2) दृढाङ्ग (f. ङ्गी);<BR>(3) वज्रसंहनन (f.<BR>ना); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stronghold
STRONGHOLD: कोटः: v. Fort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strongly
STRONGLY:<BR>(1) बलवत्: v. Forcibly;<BR>(2)<BR>दृढम्: v. Firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strong-minded
STRONG-MINDED:<BR>(1) ऊर्जितमनस् (mfn.);<BR>(2)<BR>बृहन्मनस् (mfn.); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strong-smelling
STRONG-SMELLING:<BR>(1) उग्रगन्धि (mfn.);<BR>(2)<BR>तीक्ष्णगन्ध (f. न्धा); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strop
STROP: perh. चर्मठ (mn.: comp. चाम्ठी): v.<BR>Also strap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

structure
STRUCTURE:<BR>I Organization: संस्थानम्।<BR>II<BR>Building: q. v.: भवनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

structural
STRUCTURAL: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

struggle
STRUGGLE:<BR>I To exert: q. v.: यत्नं करोति।<BR>II To contend:<BR>(1) अन्योन्यं ताडयति (=to<BR>strike one another);<BR>(2) युध्यते (युध्, c. 4.<BR>=to fight).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

struggle
STRUGGLE (subs.):<BR>I Contest:<BR>(1) युद्धम्<BR>(= fighting);<BR>(2) विवादः (= quarrel).<BR>II<BR>Great effort:<BR>(1) प्रयासः;<BR>(2) better by<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strumpet
STRUMPET:<BR>(1) बन्धकी;<BR>(2) पुंश्चली: v. Pros-<BR>-titute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

strut
STRUT:<BR>I Verb: साटोपं चलति (चल्, c. 1.),<BR>s.<BR>up and down:<BR>साटोपं परिक्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.).<BR>II Subs: साटोपगतिः and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stubble
STUBBLE: नालः, -ली: v. Straw, stump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stubborn
STUBBORN:<BR>(1) दुर्दान्त (f. न्ता);<BR>(2) प्रतीप (f.<BR>पा): v. Refractory, obstinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stubbornly
STUBBORNLY:<BR>(1) निर्वन्धेन (=obstinately);<BR>(2) निरवग्रहम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stubbornness
STUBBORNNESS:<BR>(1) दुर्दान्तता;<BR>(2) निरवग्रहता:<BR>v. Obstinacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stucco
STUCCO: सुधा, -लेपः: v. Plaster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stud
STUD (subs.):<BR>(1) a button: गण्डः;<BR>(2)<BR>horses: q. v.: अश्वाः, अश्वीयम्, etc.;<BR>(3) their<BR>place: अश्वशाला and sim. comp. s., s. bred:<BR>perh. आजानेयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stud
STUD (v.):<BR>s. ded with stars:<BR>तारकित (f. ता);<BR>s. ded with jewels:<BR>रत्नखचित (f. ता): v. To set.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

student
STUDENT:<BR>(1) अव्येतृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) छात्र (f.<BR>त्री: v. Pupil);<BR>(3) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

studied
STUDIED (adj.):<BR>I Premeditated: q. v.:<BR>सुनिश्चित (f. ता).<BR>II Learned: q. v.: अधीतिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

studio
STUDIO: कर्मशाला and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

studious
STUDIOUS:<BR>I Given to study:<BR>(1) अध्ययनशील<BR>(f. ला);<BR>(2) अध्ययनपरायण (f. णा); etc.<BR>II<BR>Eager, diligent: q. v.: उत्सुक (f. का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

studiously
STUDIOUSLY:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by circumlo.<BR>II<BR>Zealously: q. v.: साग्रहम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

study
STUDY (v.):<BR>I To learn, read: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>अधीते (इ, c. 2.),<BR>he s. ed this with me:<BR>एतन्मत्तः<BR> सोऽधिजगे, M. i. 59.;<BR>one who has s. ied all<BR>Śāstras:<BR>अधीतसर्वशास्र (f. स्रा), K.;<BR>one who<BR>has s. ied the four Vedas:<BR>अधीती चतुर्ष्वाम्नायेषु,<BR>D. v.;<BR>(2) अधिगच्छति (गम्, c. 1. = acquire:<BR>q. v. ).<BR>II To practise, learn by rote: q. v.:<BR>अभ्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.), do you s. archery:<BR>कच्चिदभ्यस्यते धनुर्वेदस्य सूत्रम्, Mah. ii. 5. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

study
STUDY (subs.):<BR>(1) अध्ययः, -नम्,<BR>s. of the<BR>Vedas:<BR>वेदाध्ययनम्, H.;<BR>(2) आगमः (rare), R.<BR>i. 15.;<BR>(3) शिक्षा (=learning);<BR>(4) अभ्यासः<BR>(close s.), वेदाभ्यासजडः, V. i. 9.<BR>II Room for<BR>s.:<BR>अध्ययनशाला and sim. comp.s.<BR>III Medi-<BR>-tation, consideration: q. v.: चर्चा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stuff
STUFF (subs.):<BR>I Thing, material: q. v.: वस्तु<BR>(n.).<BR>II Cloth: q. v.: पटः।<BR>III Household<BR>goods: गृहसामग्री।<BR>IV Nonsense, trash: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stuff
STUFF (v.):<BR>I To fill up: q. v.: पूरयति (पूर्,<BR>c. 10.),<BR>s. ing the belly:<BR>उदरपूरम्।<BR>II To<BR>crowd: p.v.<BR>III To fill the belly: उदरं<BR> पूरयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stuffing
STUFFING (subs.): i. e. seasoning: उपस्करः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stultify
STULTIFY:<BR>(1) मिथ्याकरोति: v. To falsify;<BR>(2)<BR>मोघीकरोति: v. To frustrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stumble
STUMBLE:<BR>I Intrans.: स्खलति, प्र-, (स्खल्, c.<BR>1.),<BR>strike (a horse) on the loins if it s. s:<BR>जघने<BR> स्खलितं हन्यात्, M. n. on Si. v. 10.<BR>II Trans:<BR>स्खलयति, प्र- (c. of स्खल्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stumble
STUMBLE (subs.):<BR>(1) स्खलनम्;<BR>(2) स्खलितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stumbling-block
STUMBLING-BLOCK:<BR>it is a s. to many:<BR>अत्र बहवः<BR> स्खलन्ति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stump
STUMP: कन्द (mn.),<BR>was formerly reduced like a<BR>tree to a s.:<BR>तरुरिव विहितः कुल्यकन्दः पुराभूत्, Vi.<BR>ii. 16. N. B. स्थाणुः = a tree with branches cut<BR>off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stun
STUN (v.): to be s.ned:<BR>(1) मुह्यति (मुह्, c. 4.),<BR>others were s. ned:<BR>मुमुहुः, Ku.;<BR>(2) मूर्च्छति<BR>(मूर्च्छ्, c. 1.),<BR>he was s. ned by it:<BR>तेनामूर्च्छीदसौ<BR> क्षतः, B. xv. 55.;<BR>(3) by subs.,<BR>the people<BR>were s. ned by the noise:<BR>निःस्वनेन मूर्च्छेवामवज्जनस्य,<BR>K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stunt
STUNT: वृद्धिं रुणद्धि (रुध्, c. 7.)<BR>or<BR>स्तम्भयति (c.<BR>of स्तम्भ्): v. To check.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stupefaction
STUPEFACTION: v. Stupor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stupefy
STUPEFY:<BR>(1) जडयति (nomi.), s. ies the mind:<BR>अन्तर्जडयति, Ma. i. 31.; make even masters of<BR>speech dumb (i. e. s. them): वागीशाश्नपि मूकान् कूर्वते<BR>(जडयन्तीत्यर्थः), M n. on Si. ii. 25.;<BR>(2)<BR>जडीकरोति,<BR>s. ied by the sight of Shiva:<BR>जडीकृत-<BR>स्त्रयम्बकवीक्षणेन, R. ii. 42.;<BR>(3) निष्पन्दीकरोति,<BR>M.n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stupendous
STUPENDOUS:<BR>(1) विशाल (f. ला): v. Large;<BR>(2) विस्मयकर (f. री): v. Wonderful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stupendousness
STUPENDOUSNESS:<BR>(1) विशालता: v. Largeness;<BR>(2) विस्मयकरत्वम्: v. Wonderfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stupid
STUPID:<BR>I Of persons etc.:<BR>(1) मूढ (f. ढा):<BR>v. Foolish;<BR>(2) मन्द (f. न्दा): v. Slow;<BR>(3) जड (f. डा),<BR>very s.:<BR>अतिजडः, Si. xv. 21.<BR>II Bad: q. v. Ph.:<BR>s. mistake:<BR>गरीयन् भ्रमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stupidity
STUPIDITY:<BR>(1) मूर्खता: v. Foolishness;<BR>(2)<BR>जाड्यम्,<BR>who completely removes s.:<BR>निःशेष-<BR>जाड्यापहा;<BR>to overcome s.:<BR>जडतां जयति, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stupidly
STUPIDLY:<BR>(1) जाड्येन<BR>or<BR>जाड्यात्;<BR>(2) मौढ्येन;<BR>(3) मूर्खतया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stupor
STUPOR:<BR>(1) जाड्यम्;<BR>(2) जडता;<BR>(3) जडत्वम्;<BR>(4) जडिमन् (m.):<BR>to cause s.:<BR>जाड्यं जनयति;<BR>internal s.:<BR>अन्तर्जडिमा, Gi. vi. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sturdiness
STURDINESS:<BR>(1) ऊर्जस्वलत्वम्: v. Strength;<BR>(2) कठोरता: v. Hardness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sturdy
STURDY:<BR>I Stout, hard: q. v.<BR>II Violent:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sturgeon
STURGEON: मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stutter
STUTTER: v. Stammer. S. er: v. Stammerer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sty
STY:<BR>I For pigs: शूकरशाला।<BR>II A tumour:<BR>अञ्जनम् -नी- (निका), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

style
STYLE (subs.):<BR>I Method, kind: रीतिः, the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">Page685</a>]<BR>Gauḍa s.:<BR>गौडी रीतिः, Kav.<BR>II A pencil:<BR>लेखनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

style
STYLE (v.): वदति (वद्, c. 1.): v. To call,<BR>name. S. d: expr. by comps.: v. Name,<BR>term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

stylish
STYLISH: शोभन (f. ना): v. Elegant, fashion-<BR>-able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

styptic
STYPTIC: रक्तरोधिन् (f. नी), and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

styx
STYX: a river: वैतरणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suavity
SUAVITY:<BR>(1) मनोज्ञता: v. Pleasantness;<BR>(2)<BR>माधुर्यम्: v. SWEETNESS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subaltern
SUBALTERN (subs.): अनुचरः (?): v. Atten-<BR>-dant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subdivide
SUBDIVIDE: प्रविभजति (भज्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subdivision
SUBDIVISION:<BR>(1) प्रविभागः, R. xvi. 2.: v.<BR>Division, branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subdue
SUBDUE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) वशीकरोति: v. To sub-<BR>-jugate;<BR>(2) विजयते (जि, c. 1.): v. To<BR>conquer.<BR>II To control, restrain: q. v.:<BR>नियच्छति (यम्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subjacent
SUBJACENT: अधःस्थ (f. स्था), and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subject
SUBJECT (subs.):<BR>I As opposed to sovereign:<BR>(1) प्रजा, quieting s. s like (his) own children:<BR>प्रजाः प्रजाः स्वा इव सान्त्वयित्वा, Sa. v.;<BR>(2) प्रकृतिः<BR>(rare)<BR>everyone among his s. s:<BR>सर्वः प्रकृतिषु, R.<BR>viii. 3.<BR>II Philo.: विषयिन् (m.),<BR>of s. and<BR>object:<BR>विषयविषयिणोः, S.<BR>III A matter of<BR>theme: q. v.: विषयः।<BR>IV In gram:<BR>(1) कर्तृ<BR>(m. when nomi.):<BR>(2) उद्देश्य (f. शया as distin-<BR>-guished from विधेय = predicate).<BR>V Hero<BR>of a piece: नायकः (f. यिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subject
SUBJECT (adj.):<BR>(1) वशवर्तिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp. s, he conquered kings and made them s.:<BR>स विजित्य महीपालांश्चकार वशवर्तिनः। Mah. i. 71.<BR>129.;<BR>(2) वश (f. शा),<BR>made the country s.:<BR>देशं वशं<BR> चक्रे, Mah. ii. 30. 4.; everybody is s. to death:<BR>सर्वः कालवशं याति, Mah. xii. 152. 43. (सर्वेण खलु<BR> मर्तव्यम्, 12.: v. Must): v. Also dependant,<BR>depend, possess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subject
SUBJECT (v.):<BR>I To subjugate: q. v.: वशी-<BR>करोति।<BR>II To expose, make liable: expr.<BR>by circumlo., cowardice s. s people in danger:<BR>विपदोऽभिभवन्त्यविक्रमम्, Ki. ii. 14.;<BR>foolish men<BR>s. themselves to passion:<BR>मूढो मदनेनायास्यते, K.;<BR>God, without any effort, s. s men to ridicule:<BR>अयत्नेनैव खलूपहासास्पदतामीश्वरो नयति, K.: v.<BR>Also to attack, possess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subjection
SUBJECTION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) by verb;<BR>(2)<BR>वशीकरणम् (= subjugation).<BR>II The state:<BR>(1) वशयता, my s. and your holding me under s:<BR>वशित्वं वो वशयता च मम, Vi. v.;<BR>(2) वशम् (with<BR>a verb),<BR>bringing Karṇa under s.:<BR>कर्णं वशे कृत्वा,<BR>Mah. ii. 30. 20.; when a son is under s.:<BR>अस्ति पुत्रो वशे यस्य, J.;<BR>then they will come under<BR>my s.:<BR>वशमेष्यन्ति मे तदा, H. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subjective
SUBJECTIVE, -LY: expr. by circumlo.: v.<BR>Subject, self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subjectivity
SUBJECTIVITY: विषयिनिष्ठता; better by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subjoin
SUBJOIN: निम्ने लिखति (लिख्, c. 6.): v. Also<BR>to add.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subjugate
SUBJUGATE:<BR>(1) वशीकरोति,<BR>what quarters have<BR>not been s. d:<BR>का दिशो न वशीकृताः, K.;<BR>(2) वशी-<BR>करोति;<BR>(3) वशं नयति (नी, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subjugation
SUBJUGATION:<BR>(1) वशीकरणम्;<BR>(2) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subjunctive
SUBJUNCTIVE: आशंसावाचक (f. चिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sublimate
SUBLIMATE: of mercury: रसकर्पूरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sublime
SUBLIME: तुङ्ग (f. ङ्गा), Si. ii. 39.: v. High, lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sublimely
SUBLIMELY:<BR>(1) तुङ्गभ्<BR>or<BR>उत्-;<BR>(2) expr. by<BR>comp. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sublimity
SUBLIMITY: तुङ्गता(त्वम्), K. ii. 60.: v. Lofti-<BR>-ness, elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sublunary
SUBLUNARY: ऐहिक (f. की).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

submarine
SUBMARINE: सामुद्रिक (f. की): v. Marine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

submerge
SUBMERGE: प्लावयति (c. of प्लु): v. To plunge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

submersion
SUBMERSION: प्लावनम्: Also immersion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

submission
SUBMISSION:<BR>I Subjection, obedience: q. v.:<BR>(1) प्रणतिः (= bowing);<BR>(2) अनुवृत्तिः (= fol-<BR>-lowing).<BR>II Resignation, yielding: expr.<BR>by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

submissive
SUBMISSIVE:<BR>(1) प्रणतिप्रवण (f. णा), Ki. ii. 44.;<BR>(2) वशय (f. शया),<BR>and a wife not s.:<BR>स्त्री चावशा,<BR>H. ii. 182.: v. Subject;<BR>(3) वचनकर (f.<BR>री): v. Obedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

submissively
SUBMISSIVELY:<BR>(1) प्रणिपत्य (= bowing);<BR>(2)<BR>by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

submit
SUBMIT:<BR>I To yield: q. v.:<BR>(1) वशं गच्छति;<BR>(2) प्रणमति (नम्, c. 1.=to bow),<BR>do not always<BR>s. to Duryodhana:<BR>न प्रणमन्ति सदा सुयोधनम्, Ki.<BR>ii. 44.: v. Also to obey.<BR>II To refer:<BR>q. v.: उपच्छन्दयति (छन्द्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subordinate
SUBORDINATE (adj., subs.):<BR>(1) अधीन (f. ना =<BR>dependant: q. v.);<BR>(2) अधस्तन (f. नी =<BR>lower);<BR>(3) अप्रघान (f. ना = not chief).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subordinate
SUBORDINATE (v.):<BR>(1) वशं नयति (नी, c. 1. =<BR>subject);<BR>(2) संयच्छति (यम्, c. 1. = restrain,<BR>with ins.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subordination
SUBORDINATION:<BR>I Subjection: q. v.: वश्यता।<BR>II Inferiority: q. v.: अप्रधानता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suborn
SUBORN:<BR>to s. witness:<BR>कौटसाक्ष्यं करोति<BR>or<BR>दापयति<BR>(c. of दा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subpoena
SUBPŒNA:<BR>I Subs.: आह्नानपत्रम्।<BR>II Verb:<BR>आह्नयति (ह्ने, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subscribe
SUBSCRIBE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: निम्ने नाम लिखति<BR>(लिख्, c. 6.)<BR>or<BR>निवेशयति (c. of विश्).<BR>II<BR>Promise to pay or take: दातुं ग्रहीतुं वा प्रतिजनीते<BR>(ज्ञा, c. 9.).<BR>III To assent: स्वीकरोति (with<BR>acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subscriber
SUBSCRIBER:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by the verb.:<BR>II As of paper: ग्राहक (f. हिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subscription
SUBSCRIPTION:<BR>I Act: expr. by verb.:<BR>v. Also signature.<BR>II Sum subscribed:<BR>perh. छन्दः (com. चांँदा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subsequent
SUBSEQUENT:<BR>(1) पश्चात् in comp.;<BR>(2) पश्चिम<BR>(f. मा: rare);<BR>(3) by adverb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subsequently
SUBSEQUENTLY:<BR>(1) पश्चात्: v. Afterwards;<BR>(2) इत ऊर्द्धम्;<BR>(3) उपरिष्टात्: v. Hereafter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subserve
SUBSERVE: अनुकूलयति: v. To promote, assist,<BR>serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subservience
SUBSERVIENCE (y): निघ्नता: v. Dependence,<BR>subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subservient
SUBSERVIENT: निव्न (f. घ्ना): v. Dependent,<BR>useful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subside
SUBSIDE:<BR>I To settle: q. v.<BR>II To cease:<BR>q. v.: शाम्यति, प्र- (शम्, c. 4.),<BR>when the wind<BR>s. d:<BR>वाते शमतां गते, Mah. iii. 143. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subsidence
SUBSIDENCE (Y.): expr. by verb: v. To<BR>subside, settle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subsidiary
SUBSIDIARY:<BR>(1) सहकारिन् (f. णी): v. Auxi-<BR>liary, assistant;<BR>(2) अनुकूल (f. ला): v.<BR>Favourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subsidy
SUBSIDY:<BR>(1) साहाय्यम्: v. Assistance;<BR>(2)<BR>करः: v. Tribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subsist
SUBSIST:<BR>I To exist: q. v.<BR>II To live, be<BR>maintained: q. v.: जीवति, उप- (जीव्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subsistence
SUBSISTENCE:<BR>I Existence: q. v.: अवस्थितिः।<BR>II Livelihood, maintenance: q. v.: जीवनम्,<BR>to give s.:<BR>जीवनं ददाति; Da. 129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

substance
SUBSTANCE:<BR>I Essence: q. v.: सारः।<BR>II<BR>Thing: q. v.: वस्तु (n.).<BR>III In phil.:<BR>(1)<BR>द्रव्यम्;<BR>(2) पदार्थः, Par.;<BR>(3) धर्मिन् (m.: rare),<BR>S.<BR>IV Form, matter: q. v.: मूर्तिः।<BR>V<BR>Property, goods: q. v.: सम्पत्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

substantial
SUBSTANTIAL:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) चास्तव (f. वी);<BR>वास्तविक (f. की:) v. Real, material, corpo-<BR>-real.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) सारवत् (f. ती);<BR>(2) ससार<BR>(f. रा): v. Valid, rich, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

substantiality
SUBSTANTIALITY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) वास्तवम्, S. p.<BR>b. ii. 5.;<BR>(2) वास्तवत्वम्;<BR>(3) वास्तविकत्वम्।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) सारवत्ता;<BR>(2) ससारतां।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

substantially
SUBSTANTIALLY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) वास्तवम्;<BR>(2)<BR>वस्तुतः।<BR>II Fig.: v. Richly, thoroughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

substantiate
SUBSTANTIATE: प्रमाणयति (nomi.): v. To esta-<BR>-blish, verify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

substantive
SUBSTANTIVE:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) सत्वम्, H. c.;<BR>(2)<BR>विशेष्यम्, A.<BR>II Solid, firm: q. v.:<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

substitute
SUBSTITUTE (subs.):<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) प्रतिनिधिः<BR>v. Agent; प्रतिहस्त, -कः,<BR>there can be no s. s<BR>in procreating children:<BR>पुत्रस्योत्पादने न सन्ति<BR> प्रतिहस्तकाः, H. ii. 33.<BR>II In gen.:<BR>(1) expr.<BR>by verb or circumlo.;<BR>(2) स्थानीय (f. या =<BR>occupying the place of), देवं पितृमातृस्थानीयमाग-<BR>तोऽस्मि, D. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

substitute
SUBSTITUTE (v.):<BR>(1) परिवर्तयति (c. of वृत्): v.<BR>To change, exchange;<BR>(2) स्थाने निवेशयति<BR>(c. of विश् =to put: q. v.),<BR>s. d Sugriva for<BR>him:<BR>तत्पदे सुग्रीवं संन्यवेशयत्, R. xii. 58.;<BR>Ādeśa is one word s. d for another:<BR>आदेशो नाम<BR> शब्दान्तरस्य स्थाने विधीयमानं शब्दान्तरम्, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

substitution
SUBSTITUTION:<BR>(1) परिवर्तनम् (= changing);<BR>(2) by verb, like the s. of changes for roots:<BR>धातोः स्थान इवादेशम्, R. xii. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subterfuge
SUBTERFUGE: छलम्: v. Artifice, pretext.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subterranean
SUBTERRANEAN:<BR>(1) भौम (f. मी);<BR>(2) भूमि-<BR>in comp.,<BR>s. house:<BR>भूमिगृहम्, D. iv.;<BR>(3)<BR>अन्तर्भौम (f. मी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subtle
SUBTLE:<BR>I Fine, deep: q. v.: सूक्ष्म (f.<BR>क्ष्मा).<BR>II Cunning, artful: q. v.: चतुर<BR>(f. रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subtlety
SUBTLETY:<BR>I Fineness, deepness: q. v.:<BR>सूक्षमता।<BR>II Artfulness: q. v.: चतुरता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subtly
SUBTLY:<BR>I Finely, deeply: q. v.: सूक्ष्मम्।<BR>II<BR>Artfully: q. v.: चतुरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subtract
SUBTRACT:<BR>(1) वियोजयति (युज्, c. 10.),<BR>by s.<BR>ing:<BR>वियोजिते, Li.;<BR>(2) व्यवकलयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subtraction
SUBTRACTION:<BR>(1) व्यवकलितम्, addition and s.:<BR>सङ्कलितव्यवकलिते, Li.;<BR>(2) व्यवकलनम्, Vij.;<BR>(3)<BR>वियोगः<BR>or<BR>वियोजनम्, Li.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suburb
SUBURB:<BR>(1) परिसरः,<BR>in the s. s of the city:<BR>पुरी-<BR>परिसरेषु, B. r. vi. 3. 4.;<BR>(2) उपशल्यम्, in s. s:<BR>उपशल्ये, R. xvi. 37; नगरोपकण्ठे, R. v. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suburban
SUBURBAN: शाखानगर- in comps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subversion
SUBVERSION:<BR>(1) उन्मूलनम्;<BR>(2) विध्वंसः: v.<BR>Destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subversive
SUBVERSIVE: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

subvert
SUBVERT:<BR>(1) उन्मूलयति: v. Irradicate;<BR>(2)<BR>ध्वंसयति (c. of ध्वंस्): v. To destroy;<BR>(3)<BR>खण्डयति (खण्ड्, c. 10.).: v. To break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

succeed
SUCCEED (v. i.):<BR>(1) सियति, सं- (सिध्, c. 4.),<BR>if one does not s. after striving there is no fault:<BR>यत्ने कृते यदि न सिध्यति कोऽत्र दोषः, H. i. 31.<BR>well-<BR>planned actions s.:<BR>सिव्यन्ति कार्याणि सुमन्त्रितानि,<BR>B. xii. 14.;<BR>(2) निष्पद्यते (पद्, c. 4. = to be<BR>accomplished: q. v.),<BR>I have not s. ed in the<BR>princely work I started:<BR>राजधर्मः प्रवर्तितो ननिष्पन्नः,<BR>K.;<BR>(3) साधयति (c. of सिध् = to accomplish:<BR>of men: with acc.), go and s. in your wish:<BR>अपि साधय साधयेप्सितम्, N. ii. 62.; you can go<BR>everywhere and succeed (in everything): त्वं<BR> सर्वतोगामि च साधकञ्च, Ku. iii. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

succeed
SUCCEED (v. t.): s. ing his father (to the<BR>sovereignty)<BR>of northern Koshala:<BR>पितुरनन्तरमुत्तर-<BR>कोशलान् समधिगम्य, R. ix. 1.;<BR>the child born of<BR>me s. you:<BR>मयि जायेत यः पुत्रः स भवेत्त्वदनन्तरः, Mah.<BR>i. 70. 75.;<BR>shower s. ing thunder:<BR>गर्जितानन्तरा<BR> वृष्टिः, Ku. ii. 53.: v. After, to get, to come,<BR>to follow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

succeeding
SUCCEEDING (adj.):<BR>(1) पर (f. रा = next: q. v.);<BR>(2) आगामिन् (f. नी = coming).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

success
SUCCESS:<BR>(1) सिद्धिः, सं-,<BR>s. comes to those who<BR>persevere:<BR>अभियोगभाजामङ्कमुपैति सिद्धिः, Ki. iii.<BR>40.;<BR>(2) कृतार्थता<BR>or<BR>चरितार्थता (= satisfaction<BR>after accomplishment of an object),<BR>surely<BR>the general had greater s.:<BR>कृतार्थता नन्वधिका<BR> चमूपतेः, Ki. xiv. 17.;<BR>(3) साफल्यम् (= fruitful-<BR>-ness),<BR>showing s.:<BR>साफल्यं कृत्वा, Ki. xvi. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

successful
SUCCESSFUL:<BR>I Of persons:<BR>(1) सिद्धार्थ (f. र्था),<BR>for those who patiently tried do not return<BR>without being s.:<BR>असिद्धार्था निवर्तन्ते न हि धीराः<BR> कृतोद्यमाः, K. s. xxvi. 114.;<BR>(2) कृतिन् (f. नी),<BR>you cannot consider yourself s. without conquer-<BR>ing Raghu:<BR>न खल्वनिर्जित्य रघुं कृती भवान्, R. iii.<BR>51.;<BR>(3) कृतकृत्य (f. त्या = 2).<BR>II Of things:<BR>(1) सिद्ध (f. द्धा),<BR>our attempt has been s.:<BR>सिद्धं<BR> नः समीहितम्, H.;<BR>(2) सिद्धिमत् (f. ती), N.;<BR>(3) सिद्धिशक्तिक (f. का), Com.;<BR>(4) सफल<BR>(f. ला = fruitful: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

successfully
SUCCESSFULLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

succession
SUCCESSION:<BR>I The act: expr. by verb: v.<BR>To succeed (v. t.)<BR>II Sequence: q. v.:<BR>आनन्तर्यम्।<BR>III Right to succeed:<BR>(1) उत्तराधिकारः<BR>or<BR>-रिता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2) by verb.<BR>IV Series, order: q. v.: परम्परा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

successive
SUCCESSIVE:<BR>(1) क्रमबद्ध (f. द्धा);<BR>(2) क्रमिक or<BR>आनु- (f. की).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

successively
SUCCESSIVELY:<BR>(1) क्रमेण, क्रमतः<BR>or<BR>क्रमशः;<BR>(2)<BR>अनुक्रमम्,<BR>or<BR>-शः;<BR>(3) अनेकशः (= repeatedly:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

successor
SUCCESSOR:<BR>(1) अनन्तर (f. रा);<BR>(2) उत्तराधि-<BR>कारिन् (f. णी = heir);<BR>(3) प्रत्यनन्तर (f. रा),<BR>M. viii. 185.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

succinct
SUCCINCT:<BR>(1) संक्षिप्त (f. प्ता): v. Concise;<BR>(2) विशद (f. दा): v. Clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

succinctly
SUCCINCTLY:<BR>(1) संक्षिप्तम्,: v. Concisely;<BR>(2)<BR>विशदम्: v. Clearly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

succory
SUCCORY: a plant: कासनी (Williams).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

succour
SUCCOUR:<BR>I Subs.: साहाय्यम्: v. Help.<BR>II<BR>Verb: expr. by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

succulence
SUCCULENCE: सरसता: v. Al o juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

succulent
SUCCULENT: सरस (f. सा): v. Also juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

succumb
SUCCUMB: न अत्येति (इ, c. 2.),<BR>s. ed under the<BR>disease:<BR>गदं नात्यगात्, R. xix. 53.: v. To pass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

such
SUCH:<BR>(1) तादृशः (शी, शं)<BR>or<BR>तादृश् (mfn.).<BR>(=of that kind),<BR>s. Kurus:<BR>तादृशाः कुरवः,<BR>Mah. iv. 68. 37.; there was s. a sage:<BR>आसीत्तादृशो मुनिः, D. ii.;<BR>(2) ईदृशः (शी, शं) or<BR>ईदृश् (mfn.). (= of this kind),<BR>in s. fire of<BR>litigation:<BR>ईदृशे व्यवहाराग्नौ, Mr. ix. 39.;<BR>a<BR>speaker who is not of s. a mind:<BR>यो वक्ता नेदृगाशयः,<BR>Ki. xi. 41.;<BR>(3) एतादृशः (शी, शं)<BR>or<BR>एतादृश्<BR>(mfn.=2.);<BR>(4) एवंविध, (धा, धं =2.),<BR>s.<BR>personages:<BR>एवंविधा मूर्तयः, K.;<BR>(5) तथाविधः<BR>(धा, धं = 1.),<BR>s. love and s. a husband:<BR>तथाविधं<BR> प्रेम पतिश्च तादृशः, Ku. v. 2.;<BR>s. and s.:<BR>अमुकः<BR>(का, कं);<BR>in s. and s. a time, in s. and s. a<BR>place:<BR>अमुकस्मिन् काले अमुकस्मिन् देशे, He.<BR>S. as<BR>myself:<BR>मादृशः (शी, शं), मादृश् (mfn.),<BR>or<BR>मद्विधः<BR>(धा, धं), N. iii. 71.<BR>S. as yourself:<BR>त्वादृशः<BR>(शी, शं), त्वादृश् (mfn.), भवादृशः (शी, शं) etc.,<BR>Ki. i. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suck
SUCK (v.):<BR>I As children: स्तनम्<BR>or<BR>स्तन्यं पिबति<BR>(पा, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>धयति (धे, c. 1.).<BR>thirst for s.-<BR>ing:<BR>स्तन्यपाने पिपासा, J.<BR>II In gen.:<BR>(1) चूषति<BR>or<BR>चोषति (चुष्, c. 1.),<BR>and with various<BR>(dishes) for s. ing:<BR>चोष्यैश्च विविधैः, Man. ii. 4. 3.;<BR>(2) पिबति, (= drink),<BR>which s. s by the root<BR>(tree):<BR>पादपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sucker
SUCKER:<BR>(1) चोषक (f. षिका);<BR>(2) चूषयितृ<BR>(f. त्री);<BR>(3) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suck
SUCK, SUCKING (subs.):<BR>for s.:<BR>चूषणार्थम्, Sr.<BR>vii.: v. Suction. To give s.: v. Suckle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suckle
SUCKLE: स्तनम्<BR>or<BR>स्तन्यं ददाति<BR>or<BR>पाययति (दा,<BR>c. 3. or c. of पा), Sr.;<BR>s. d. by jar-water:<BR>घट-<BR>स्तनप्रस्रवणैर्व्यवर्द्धयत्, Ku. v. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suckling
SUCKLING:<BR>I The act: स्तन्यदानम्।<BR>II A<BR>child:<BR>(1) स्तन्यप (f. पा), Sr.;<BR>(2) स्तनन्धय<BR>(f. यी);<BR>(3) स्तनपायिन् (f. नी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suction
SUCTION:<BR>(1) चोषः;<BR>(2) चृ(चो)षणम्;<BR>(3) पानम्,<BR>s. of breast:<BR>स्तनपानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sudden
SUDDEN:<BR>(1) आकस्मिक (f. की), s. noise:<BR>आकस्मिकः स्वनः, N. iii. 1.;<BR>(2) by adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suddenly
SUDDENLY:<BR>(1) अकस्मात्;<BR>(2) सहसा,<BR>Rama s.<BR>became filled with tears:<BR>बभूव रामः सहसा सबाष्पः,<BR>R. xiv. 84.;<BR>(3) द्राक् (=instantly: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suddenness
SUDDENNESS: आकस्मिकत्वम्, -ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sudorific
SUDORIFIC:<BR>(1) स्वेदन (f. नी), प्र-;<BR>(2) स्वेदजनन<BR>(f. नी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suds
SUDS: *सावनजलम्। and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sue
SUE:<BR>I To entreat: q. v.: छन्दयति (छन्द्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR>II To prosecute, inform: q. v.:<BR>अभियुंक्ते<BR>or<BR>-योजयति (युज, c. 7. and 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suet
SUET:<BR>(1) वसा;<BR>(2) मेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suffer
SUFFER (v. t.):<BR>I To feel: q. v.: अनुभवति।<BR>II<BR>To bear: q. v.: सहते (सह्, c. 1.).<BR>III<BR>Undergo: q. v.: याति, (या, c. 2.).<BR>IV To<BR>allow, permit: q. v.: अनुजानाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suffer
SUFFER (v. i.):<BR>(1) क्लिश्यते (क्लिश्, c. 4.);<BR>(2)<BR>सीदति (सद्, c. 1.), Ki. xiii. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sufferable
SUFFERABLE:<BR>(1) सह्य (f. ह्या);<BR>(2) सहनीय<BR>(f. या);<BR>(3) सोढव्य (f. व्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sufferance
SUFFERANCE, SUFFERING:<BR>I Endurance:<BR>q. v.: सहनम्।<BR>II Pain, distress: q. v.: क्लेशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suffered
SUFFERED:<BR>(1) क्लिष्ट (f. ष्टा), s. from disease:<BR>रोगक्लिष्टः;<BR>(2) दुःखमागिन् (f. नी = miserable).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suffice
SUFFICE: expr. by adj.: v. Sufficient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sufficiency
SUFFICIENCY:<BR>(1) पर्याप्तिः;<BR>(2) पर्याप्तता, -त्वम्: v.<BR>Sufficient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sufficient
SUFFICIENT:<BR>(1) पर्याप्त (f. प्ता),<BR>s. for mainten-<BR>ance of servants:<BR>पर्याप्तं भृत्यवृत्तये, M. xi. 7.: v.<BR>Enough;<BR>(2) यथेष्ट (f. ष्टा)<BR>or<BR>यथेच्छ (f. च्छा)<BR>(= as much as desired);<BR>(3) प्रचुर (f. रा =<BR>abundant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sufficiently
SUFFICIENTLY:<BR>(1) पर्याप्तम्;<BR>(2) प्रचुरम् (= abun-<BR>-dantly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suffocate
SUFFOCATE:<BR>(1) श्वासं रुणद्धि, अव- (रुध्, c. 7.:<BR>with gen.);<BR>(2) श्वासरोधं करोति (with gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suffocation
SUFFOCATION:<BR>(1) श्वासरोधः;<BR>(2) श्वासावरोधः, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suffragan
SUFFRAGAN: धर्मनायकः: v. Bishop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suffrage
SUFFRAGE: सम्मतिः (?): v. Vote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suffuse
SUFFUSE: परिप्लवते, उप- (प्लु, c. 1.),<BR>s. d with<BR>tears:<BR>अश्रूपरिप्लत (f. ता); s. d with blushes:<BR>ह्नीपरिगत (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suffusion
SUFFUSION: परिप्लबः<BR>or<BR>-प्लुतिः: v. Also to<BR>pervade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sugar
SUGAR (subs.):<BR>(1) शर्करा, a doll made of s.:<BR>शार्करी पुत्रिका, N. xvi. 163.;<BR>(2) सिता, s. ed:<BR>ससित (f. ता), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sugar
SUGAR (v.):<BR>I Lit.: expr. by subs.<BR>II To<BR>flatter: q. v.:<BR>“s. ed word”:<BR>मधुमयं वाक्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sugar-candy
SUGAR-CANDY:<BR>(1) सिताखण्डः;<BR>(2) खण्डमोदकः;<BR>(3) माक्षिकशर्करा (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sugar-cane
SUGAR-CANE: इक्षुः<BR>“plant s.”:<BR>बाल इक्षुः;<BR>ripe s.<BR>juice:<BR>पक्वेक्षुरसः;<BR>scorched s.:<BR>पौण्ड्रः, -कः;<BR>red s.:<BR>कोषकारः;<BR>bamboo s.:<BR>वंशकः; juicy s.:<BR>कान्तारः, -कः; etc., Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suggest
SUGGEST:<BR>(1) सूचयति (सूच्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>indicate, intimate;<BR>(2) लक्षयति (लक्ष्, c.<BR>10.): v. To show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suggestion
SUGGESTION:<BR>(1) सूचना (=indication);<BR>(2)<BR>इङ्गितम् (=hint);<BR>(3) प्रोत्साहः (=instigation);<BR>(4) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suggestive
SUGGESTIVE:<BR>(1) सूचक (f. चिका =indicative);<BR>(2) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suicidal
SUICIDAL:<BR>(1) expr. by comp.;<BR>(2) आत्मघातिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suicide
SUICIDE:<BR>I The act: आत्महत्या and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>To commit s.:<BR>प्राणान् उत्सृजति (सृज,<BR>c. 6.=to quit life) and sim. expr. s.,<BR>I will<BR>commit. s. by hanging:<BR>रज्ज्वात्मानमुत्स्रक्ष्यामि, K.,<BR>उद्वध्यात्मानं व्यापादयिष्यामि, Na. ii.<BR>II The<BR>person:<BR>(1) आत्मघातिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) आत्महन्<BR>(mfn.); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suit
SUIT (v. t.): युनक्ति<BR>or<BR>युंक्ते, उप- (युज्, c. 7.),<BR>do<BR>not s. a poor husband:<BR>न गतश्रीकं मर्तारमुपयुञ्जीत,<BR>Mah. iii. 286. 18.; what is s. ed to any one:<BR>यद् येन युज्यते, H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suit
SUIT (v. i.):<BR>I To fit, become: q. v.: युज्यते,<BR> उप- (pass. of युज्).<BR>II To agree: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suit
SUIT (subs.):<BR>I Law-suit: q. v.: कार्यम्।<BR>II<BR>Solicitation: q. v.: प्रणयः, Ki. xiii. 60.<BR>III<BR>III Of clothes:<BR>(1) युगलम्;<BR>(2) मुग्मम्।<BR>IV<BR>Set: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suitable
SUITABLE: उपयुक्त (f. क्ता): v. Proper, fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suitableness
SUITABLENESS: उपयुक्तता: v. Propriety, fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suitably
SUITABLY:<BR>I Appropriately:<BR>(1) यथोचितम्;<BR>(2) यथायोग्यम्;<BR>(3) समुचितम्।<BR>II Accordingly:<BR>q. v.: अनुसारेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suite
SUITE:<BR>I Retinue: q. v.: परिच्छदः।<BR>II Of<BR>rooms, etc.: perh. समष्टिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suitor
SUITOR:<BR>I Solicitor: q. v.: प्रार्थयितृ (f. त्री).<BR>II A plaintiff: q. v.: अर्थिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sulkily
SULKILY, SULLENLY: रुक्षम् (=roughly, harsh-<BR>-ly: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sulkiness
SULKINESS, SULLENNESS: रौक्षम् (=harshness,<BR>roughness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sulky
SULKY, SULLEN: रु(रू)क्ष (f. क्षा = harsh, rough:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sully
SULLY: कलङ्कयति (nomi.): v. To pollute,<BR>stain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sulphate
SULPHATE:<BR>(1)<BR>of copper:<BR>तुत्थम्;<BR>(2)<BR>red s.<BR>of iron:<BR>काशी(सी)शम्;<BR>(3) green s. of iron.:<BR>धातुशेखरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sulphur
SULPHUR:<BR>(1) गन्धकः, “चतुर्धा गन्धकः प्रोक्तो रक्तः<BR> पीतः सितोऽसितः”, Bha.;<BR>(2) गन्धाश्मन् (m.) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sulphurated
SULPHURA(E)TED: गन्धकसंपृक्त (f. क्ता) and sim.<BR>comp. s (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sulphuret
SULPHURET:<BR>(1) of iron: ताप्य (mn.):<BR>(2) of<BR>mercury: कज्जली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sulphureous
SULPHUREOUS: गन्धकगर्भ (f. र्भा), गन्धकसंपृक्त (f.<BR>क्ता), and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sulphuric acid
SULPHURIC ACID: *गन्धकाम्लः; तुत्थाम्लः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sultan
SULTAN, -NA: अधिराजः (f. ज्ञी): v. Emperor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sultriness
SULTRINESS:<BR>(1) प्रवृद्धतापः;<BR>(2) अत्युष्णता;<BR>(3)<BR>तापवृद्धिः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sultry
SULTRY: प्रवृद्धताप (f. पा), days were very s.:<BR>प्रवृद्धतापो दिवसोऽतिमात्रम्, R. xvi. 45.: v. Hot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sum
SUM (subs.):<BR>I Aggregate:<BR>(1) योगः (= addi-<BR>-tion),<BR>whose s. is hundred and one:<BR>ययोर्योगं<BR> शतं सैकम्, Li. 27.;<BR>(2) मानम्, प्रमाणम् (=total<BR>number),<BR>tell me the s. of his things:<BR>तस्य द्रव्य-<BR>प्रमाणं वद्, Li. 25.;<BR>(3) ऐक्यम् (=total).<BR>II<BR>Quantity: राशिः, what s. becomes 68......:<BR>स्यात् को राशिर्द्व्यूनसप्ततिः, Li. 21.<BR>III Of<BR>money: no expr.,<BR>why do you spend a large s.<BR>of money:<BR>किं महानर्थोत्सर्गः क्रियते, Mu. iii.<BR>IV<BR>S. and substance:<BR>(1) मर्मन्, (n.);<BR>(2) सारः।<BR>V. Acme: q. v.:<BR>(1) परा कोटिः;<BR>(2) फलितम्,<BR>M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sum
SUM (v.): संकलयति (कल्, c. 10.): v. To add, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">Page690</a>]<BR>compute.<BR>S. up:<BR>संक्षेपतो विवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.),<BR>S. c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

summarily
SUMMARILY:<BR>I Briefly: q. v.: संक्षेपेण।<BR>II<BR>Hastily, quickly: q. v.: क्षिप्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

summary
SUMMARY:<BR>I Adj.:<BR>(1) संक्षिप्त (f. प्ता = brief);<BR>(2) क्षिप्र (f. प्रा = hasty).<BR>II Subs.: संक्षेपः:<BR>v. Epitome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

summer
SUMMER (subs.):<BR>(1) ग्रीष्मः, -समयः, a s. flower:<BR>ग्रैष्मः पुष्पविशेषः, M. n.;<BR>(2) निदाघः, -कालः;<BR>(3)<BR>उष्णः, -आगमः;<BR>(4) तपः;<BR>(5) घर्मः, R. xvi. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

summer
SUMMER (v.): ग्रीष्मकालं गमयति, अतिवाहयति, etc.:<BR>v. To pass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

summer-house
SUMMER-HOUSE: with waterworks: धारागृहम्,<BR>R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

summerset
SUMMERSET: v. Somersault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

summit
SUMMIT:<BR>(1) शि(शे)खरम्;<BR>(2) शृङ्गम्;<BR>(3) चूडा:<BR>v. Peak, tip, top. Ph.: highest s.: (fig.)<BR>परा कोटिः: v. Acme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

summon
SUMMON: आह्वयति (ह्ने, c. 1.): v. To call.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

summoner
SUMMONER:<BR>(1) आह्वातृ (f. त्री ?);<BR>(2) आह्वायक<BR>(f. यिका ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

summons
SUMMONS:<BR>(1) आह्नानम्, -पत्रम् (?), to serve a s.:<BR>आहानं ददाति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

summum bonum
SUMMUM BONUM:<BR>(1) निःश्रेयसम्;<BR>(2) परमार्थः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sumpter
SUMPTER, -HORSE: स्थू(स्थौ)रिन् (m.): v. Pack-<BR>-horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sumptuary
SUMPTUARY: व्ययनियामक (f. मिका) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sumptuous
SUMPTUOUS: महार्घ (f. र्घा): v. Costly, rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sumptuously
SUMPTUOUSLY:<BR>I Costly: expr. by comp.,<BR>s. dressed:<BR>महार्घवेष (f. षा).<BR>II Splendidly:<BR>s. fed:<BR>मोजनविशेषैस्तर्पित (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sumptuousness
SUMPTUOUSNESS:<BR>I Costliness; महार्घता।<BR>II<BR>Richness, excellence: q. v.: विशिष्टता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sun
SUN (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) सूर्यः;<BR>(2) दिवाकरः;<BR>(3) दिनकरः;<BR>(4) आदित्यः;<BR>(5) मास्करः;<BR>(6)<BR>भानुः;<BR>(7) सवितृ (m.);<BR>(8) अरुणः (also= sun's<BR>charioteer);<BR>(9) अर्कः;<BR>(10) रविः;<BR>(11)<BR>मिहिरः;<BR>(12) विवस्वत् (m.);<BR>(13) विभावसुः;<BR>(14) मार्तण्डः;<BR>(15) हरिदश्वः;<BR>(16) सप्तसप्तिः;<BR>(17) विकर्तनः;<BR>(18) घर्मदीधितिः।<BR>The rising, the<BR>setting s.:<BR>उद्यन्तं, अस्तं यान्तम् आदित्यम्, M. iv.<BR>37.;<BR>the morning s.:<BR>बालारुणः, Ku.;<BR>there is<BR>nothing new under the s.:<BR>*नास्ति किमप्यपूर्वं<BR> महीतले;<BR>a worshipper of the s.:<BR>सौरः (री, रं),<BR>San.<BR>II Sunshine: q. v. Ph.:<BR>to expose to<BR>the s. (as things):<BR>आतपे ददाति, Si.<BR>or<BR>धारयति,<BR>Bha.;<BR>to bask in the morning s.:<BR>बालातपं सेवते,<BR>V. t.;<BR>dried in the s.:<BR>आतपे शोषितः (ता, तं),<BR>Bha.;<BR>to go in the s.:<BR>आतपे गच्छति, Sa. iii.;<BR>going about in the s.:<BR>आतपलङ्घनम्, Sa. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sun
SUN (v. t.): आतपे<BR>or<BR>सूर्यातपे ददाति (दा, c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sunbeam
SUNBEAM:<BR>(1) सूर्यरशिमः;<BR>(2) सूर्यांशुः;<BR>(3) सूर्य-<BR>किरणः; etc.: v. Ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sunburnt
SUNBURNT: सूर्यतापितः (ता, तं), and sim.<BR>comp.s. IV.: Also swarthy, dark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sunday
SUNDAY:<BR>(1) रविवारः;<BR>(2) रविवासरः;<BR>(3) भट्टारक-<BR>वारः;<BR>(4) भानुवारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sundial
SUNDIAL: perh. घटीयन्त्रम्, Go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sunflower
SUNFLOWER: सूर्यमुखी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sunrise
SUNRISE:<BR>(1) सूर्योदयः etc,<BR>about s.:<BR>आदित्यस्योदयं<BR> प्रति, Mah. iv. 11.;<BR>(2) अरुणोदयः;<BR>(3) often<BR>by verb.,<BR>before s.:<BR>अनुदिते भास्करे; after s.:<BR>समुत्थिते रवौ, K.;<BR>at s.:<BR>प्रत्युन्मिषत्यरुणार्चिषि, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sunset
SUNSET: सूर्यास्तमयः, -नम् and sim. comp.s;<BR>at<BR>s.:<BR>अस्तं गच्छति सूर्ये<BR>or<BR>अस्ताचलचूडावलम्बिनि<BR> भास्करे;<BR>after s.:<BR>अस्तं गते सूर्ये।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sunder
SUNDER: विश्लेषयति (c. of श्लिष्): v. To sepa-<BR>-rate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sundry
SUNDRY: कतिपयः (या, यं = few: q. v.): v.<BR>Also diverse, several.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sunny
SUNNY:<BR>I Of sun.: सौर (f. री).<BR>II Not<BR>shady: आतपाक्रान्त (f. न्ता) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sup
SUP (v.):<BR>I To sip: q. v.<BR>II To take a<BR>night-meal: q. v.: रजनी भोजनं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

super
SUPER: expr. by अति-<BR>or<BR>अतिशय- in comp.,<BR>s.-<BR>abundance:<BR>अतिबाहुल्यम्।<BR>S. annuation:<BR>अति-<BR>वयस्कता; etc.: v. Also below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superb
SUPERB: अतिशोभन (f. ना): v. Magnificent,<BR>splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supercilious
SUPERCILIOUS: अवलिप्त (f. प्ता): v. Haughty,<BR>arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superciliously
SUPERCILIOUSLY: सावलेपम्: v. Haughtily,<BR>arrogantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superciliousness
SUPERCILIOUSNESS: अवलेपः: v. Haughtiness,<BR>arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superficial
SUPERFICIAL:<BR>I Lit.: पृष्ठ- in comp., s. area:<BR>पृष्ठफलम्, Li.<BR>II Fig.: स्थूल (f. ला). Ph.:<BR>s. scholar: v. Smatterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superficially
SUPERFICIALLY:<BR>(1) स्थूलम् (=not minute);<BR>(2) स्वल्पम् (=little).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superficies
SUPERFICIES:<BR>(1) तलम्, K. d.;<BR>(2) पृष्ठम् (= back),<BR>s. of sphere:<BR>गोलपृष्ठम्, K. d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superfine
SUPERFINE:<BR>I Of texture: अतिसूक्ष्म (f. क्ष्मा).<BR>II Excellent: q. v.: अत्युत्कृष्ट (f. ष्टा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superfluity
SUPERFLUITY:<BR>(1) आधिक्यम्;<BR>(2) अतिरेकः;<BR>(3)<BR>अतिरिक्तता, -त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superfluous
SUPERFLUOUS:<BR>(1) अधिक (f. का),<BR>here the<BR>word<BR>आकृति<BR>is s.:<BR>अत्राकृतिपदमधिकम्, Sah.<BR>vii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superfluously
SUPERFLUOUSLY:<BR>(1) अधिकम्;<BR>(2) अतिरिक्तम्;<BR>(3) बाहुल्येन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superhuman
SUPERHUMAN:<BR>(1) अतिमानुष (f. षी);<BR>(2)<BR>अमानुष (f. षी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superincumbent
SUPERINCUMBENT:<BR>(1) अधिशयान (f. ना);<BR>(2)<BR>by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superinduce
SUPERINDUCE: आवहति (वह्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>induce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superintend
SUPERINTEND: पर्यवेक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.) (?): v.<BR>Also to manage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superintendence
SUPERINTENDENCE: पर्यवेक्षणम् (?): v. Also<BR>management.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superintendent
SUPERINTENDENT: पर्यवेक्षक (f. क्षिका) (?): v.<BR>Manager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superior
SUPERIOR:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) ज्यायस् (f. सी),<BR>and the enemy is s. (to you) in the strength of his<BR>arms and forces:<BR>ज्यायांश्च वीर्यास्रबलैर्विपक्षः, Ki.<BR>iii. 17.;<BR>(2) अधिक (f. का =greater),<BR>the s.<BR>animals did not torment the lower ones:<BR>ऊनं न<BR> सत्वेष्वधिको बबाधे, R. ii. 14.: v. Also excellent,<BR>to excel.<BR>II A senior:<BR>(1) गुरुः;<BR>(2) ज्येष्ठ<BR>(f. ष्ठा: rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superiority
SUPERIORITY:<BR>(1) ज्येष्ठता;<BR>(2) ज्यैष्ठ्यम्,<BR>s. in<BR>knowledge:<BR>विद्याजैष्ठ्यम्;<BR>(3) आधिक्यम् (= state<BR>of being greater):<BR>(4) श्रेष्ठता: v. Excellence;<BR>(5) वरिष्ठता (=3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superlative
SUPERLATIVE:<BR>I Excellent, unparalleled:<BR>q. v.: सर्वोत्कृष्ट (f. ष्टा).<BR>II In gram: अति-<BR>शयद्योतक (f. तिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supernatural
SUPERNATURAL: अलौकिक (f. की): v. Also<BR>superhuman, wonderful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supernaturally
SUPERNATURALLY: expr. by comp. or<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supernumerary
SUPERNUMERARY: अतिरिक्त (f. क्ता), s. officer:<BR>अतिरिक्तकर्मचारी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superscribe
SUPERSCRIBE: in letters: बाह्यनाम ददाति (दा,<BR>c. 3.), Mu. i. or लिखति, अभि- (लिख्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superscription
SUPERSCRIPTION: बाह्यनामन् (n.), mu. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supersede
SUPERSEDE:<BR>I In office: s. d me in this post:<BR>मामुल्लङ्घ्य पदमिदमधिजगाम।<BR>II To set aside:<BR>व्यावर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supersession
SUPERSESSION:<BR>I In office:<BR>(1) by verb;<BR>(2) अतिक्रमः (= passing over).<BR>II Setting<BR>aside: व्यावृत्तिः<BR>or<BR>व्यावर्तनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superstition
SUPERSTITION: मूढविश्वासः (?) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superstitious
SUPERSTITIOUS:<BR>I Of men: मूढविश्वासिन् (f.<BR>नी) and sim. comp. s.<BR>II Of rite, etc.:<BR>मूढविश्वासनिष्ठ (f. ष्ठा) and sim. comp. s. Ph.:<BR>s. belief:<BR>मूढविश्वासः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superstitiously
SUPERSTITIOUSLY:<BR>(1) मूढविश्वासेन;<BR>(2) by<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superstitiousness
SUPERSTITIOUSNESS: मूढविश्वासनिष्ठा (?): v.<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

superstructure
SUPERSTRUCTURE: भवनम्: v. Edifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supervene
SUPERVENE: समापतति (पत्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>happen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supervise
SUPERVISE, SUPERVISION: v. To superintend,<BR>superintendence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supine
SUPINE (adj.):<BR>I Lying on the back: उत्तान-<BR>शयः (यी, यं: in sleeping); अवपृष्ठ- in comp.<BR>II Fig. indolent: q. v.: तुन्दपरिमृजः (जा, जं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supine
SUPINE (subs.): तुमर्थकः क्रियाविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supinely
SUPINELY: expr. by adj.: v. Indolently,<BR>indifferently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supineness
SUPINENESS:<BR>(1) निरीहता (=indifference);<BR>(2)<BR>आलस्यम् (=indolence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supper
SUPPER:<BR>(1) रजनीभोजनम्;<BR>(2) रात्र्याहारः and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supplant
SUPPLANT:<BR>(1) स्थानमधितिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.=<BR>occupy the place: with gen.);<BR>(2) निष्का-<BR>शयति (c. of काश् = drive out, dispel: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supple
SUPPLE: सुकुमार (f. रा): v. Soft, pliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supplement
SUPPLEMENT: परिशिष्टम्, s. to the Kātantra:<BR>कातन्त्रपरिशिष्टम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supplemental
SUPPLEMENTAL: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suppleness
SUPPLENESS: सौकृमार्यम्: v. Softness, pliancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suppliant
SUPPLIANT:<BR>I Solicitor: q. v.: अर्थिन् (f.<BR>नी).<BR>II Submissive: q. v.: प्रणत (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suppliantly
SUPPLIANTLY:<BR>(1) कृताञ्जलि (mfn.);<BR>(2) सानु-<BR>नयम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supplicate
SUPPLICATE: v. To entreat, beg, seek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supplication
SUPPLICATION: अनुनयः: v. Entreaty, solici-<BR>-tation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supplicatory
SUPPLICATORY: सानुनय (f. या): v. Humble,<BR>submissive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supply
SUPPLY (subs.):<BR>I In gen.: सम्भारः: v. Store,<BR>to supply.<BR>II In pl.:<BR>to vote s. ies:<BR>साधनान्यु-<BR>पकल्पयति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supply
SUPPLY (v.):<BR>I To fill up: q. v.: पूरयति,<BR> परि- (पूर्, c. 10.).<BR>II To provide:<BR>(1)<BR>आहरति (हृ, c. 1.= bring),<BR>whatever asked she<BR>found s. ed:<BR>यदेव वव्रे तदपश्यदाहृतम्, R. iii. 6.;<BR>(2) संयोजयति (युज्, c. 10.=unite): v. Also<BR>To store, prepare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

support
SUPPORT (subs.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) आलम्बः, -नम्,<BR>s. to (men) in distress:<BR>विपत्तिमग्नाय करावलम्बनम्,<BR>P. h.;<BR>(2) अवलम्बः, -नम्,<BR>manliness is the highest<BR>s. for self:<BR>मतमालम्बनमात्मपौरुषम्, Ki. ii. 13.;<BR>(3) आश्रयः: v. Refuge;<BR>(4) उपघ्नः (rare),<BR>s.<BR>ing tree:<BR>उपघ्नतरुः, R. xiv. 1.;<BR>(5) अवष्टम्भः,<BR>s.<BR>from knowledge:<BR>ज्ञानावष्टम्भः, K.<BR>II Nourish-<BR>-ment, maintenance: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

support
SUPPORT (v.):<BR>I To bear up: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>अवष्टभ्नाति (स्तम्भ्, c. 9.),<BR>s. ing. me:<BR>मामवष्टभ्य,<BR>Vi. v. 5.;<BR>(2) आलम्बम्<BR>or<BR>अवलम्बनं ददाति (दा,<BR>c. 3.): v. Subs.<BR>II To nourish, main-<BR>-tain: q. v.:<BR>(1) भरति (भृ, c. 1.),<BR>who must<BR>be s. ed:<BR>अवश्यभरणीय (f. या), K. b. on M. xi.<BR>9.;<BR>(2) ग्रासाच्छादनं ददाति (दा, c. 3.=give<BR>board and lodging).<BR>III To countenance,<BR>aid: समर्थयति (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supportable
SUPPORTABLE:<BR>(1) अवष्टभ्य (f. म्या);<BR>(2) भर्तव्य<BR>(f. व्या);<BR>(3) समर्थनीय (f. या): for dif.:<BR>v. To support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supporter
SUPPORTER:<BR>I Lit.: v. Support (I).<BR>II<BR>Maintainer: q. v.: भरणदातृ (f. त्री).<BR>III<BR>Defender: समर्थयितृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supposable
SUPPOSABLE:<BR>(1) सम्भाव्य (f. व्या);<BR>(2) सम्भाव-<BR>नीय (f. या); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suppose
SUPPOSE:<BR>I To assume to be true: expr.<BR>by विधिलिङ्<BR>or<BR>लोट्,<BR>s. he is entirely so:<BR>तथाविध-<BR>स्तावदशेषमस्तु सः, Ku. v. 82.<BR>II To imagine:<BR>(1) तर्कयति (तर्क्, c. 10.);<BR>(2) सम्भावयति (c.<BR>of भू);<BR>(3) मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.=think): v.<BR>Also to suspect, guess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supposition
SUPPOSITION:<BR>(1) ऊहः;<BR>(2) तर्कः, वि-: v. Also<BR>inference. On the s.: expr. with कक्षीकरोति<BR>or<BR>क्रोडीकरोति (= admit: with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supposititious
SUPPOSITITIOUS: कूट- in comp.: v. Also false,<BR>not genuine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suppress
SUPPRESS:<BR>I To extinguish, destroy: q. v.:<BR>दमयति (c. of दम्).<BR>II To restrain, check:<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) नि-यच्छति, सं-, विनि-, (यम्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) निगृह्नाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.).<BR>III To conceal:<BR>q. v.: गोपायति (गुप्, c. 1.),<BR>Indra s. ed (his)<BR>rising satisfaction:<BR>निजुगोप हर्षमुदितं मघवा, Ki.<BR>vi. 38. Ph.:<BR>with s. ed tears:<BR>स्तम्भिताश्रुः, M. n.<BR>on R. xiv. 53. (अन्तर्गतबाष्पकण्ठः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suppression
SUPPRESSION:<BR>I Putting down: दमनम्: v.<BR>Irradication, destruction.<BR>II Restraint:<BR>q. v.: निग्रहः।<BR>II Concealment: q. v.: गोपनम्<BR>IV Stoppage: स्तम्मः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suppurate
SUPPURATE:<BR>(1) पाकं गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.), पक्वतां<BR> व्रजति (व्रज्, c. 1.): etc., Bha.;<BR>(2) पचति<BR>(पच्, c. 1.), Bha.<BR>S. ing or s. ive thing:<BR>पाच-<BR>नीयानि द्रव्याणि, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suppuration
SUPPURATION:<BR>(1) पाकः, परि-;<BR>(2) पक्वता, परि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supremacy
SUPREMACY:<BR>(1) प्रभविष्णुता;<BR>(2) प्रभुत्वम्;<BR>(3)<BR>आधिपत्यम्: v. Sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supreme
SUPREME:<BR>I Extreme: q. v.: परम (f. मा).<BR>Ph.:<BR>S. Being:<BR>परमब्रह्म।<BR>II Chief: q. v.:<BR>मुख्य (f. ख्या). Ph.: to be s. i. e. to have<BR>mastery over:<BR>(1) प्रभविष्णु (mfn.);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रभवति (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

supremely
SUPREMELY:<BR>(1) परमम्;<BR>(2) परम्;<BR>(3) निरति-<BR>शयम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surcharge
SURCHARGE: v. To overload.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surd
SURD: करणी, adding a quadratic s. with a s. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">Page693</a>]<BR>index 8 we get a s. with indes 18:<BR>क २+क ८<BR> योगे जातं क १८, Vij. N. B. This ref. to the<BR>same rational quantity under the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sure
SURE:<BR>I Of things: निश्चित (f. ता): v. Cer-<BR>-tain, undoubted.<BR>II Of men:<BR>feeling s. of<BR>victory:<BR>जयं ध्रुवं मन्यमान (f. ना): v. To think,<BR>certain (II).<BR>III Secure: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surely
SURELY: नूनम्: v. Certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surety
SURETY: प्रतिभूः,<BR>to take s.:<BR>प्रतिभूं गृह्नाति, Mit.;<BR>four kinds of s. ies:<BR>चतुःप्रकारः प्रतिभूः, Vri.;<BR>to<BR>stand s.:<BR>प्रतिभूस्तिष्ठति, Kat.; to give time to s.:<BR>प्रतिभुवे कालं ददाति, Vri.;<BR>(2) लग्नकः, to make s.:<BR>लग्नकं कारयति, Kat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suretyship
SURETYSHIP:<BR>(1) प्रातिभाव्यम्;<BR>(2) प्रतिभूत्वम्, -ता;<BR>(3) लग्नकत्वम्, -ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surf
SURF:<BR>(1) लहरिः(री);<BR>(2) कल्लोलः;<BR>(3) उल्लोलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surface
SURFACE:<BR>(1) तलम्,<BR>s. of earth:<BR>भूतलम्;<BR>(2)<BR>पृष्ठम्। Ph.:<BR>on the s. of water:<BR>जलोपरि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surfeit
SURFEIT:<BR>I Verb:<BR>(1) अतिमोजनं करोति;<BR>(2)<BR>अतिपूरयति (पूर्, c. 10, as to s. the belly).<BR>II<BR>Subs.:<BR>(1) अतिभोजनम् (lit.);<BR>(2) अतिपूर्तिः,<BR> -पूरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surge
SURGE (v.): उल्लोलति (लुल्, c. 1.), s. ing wave:<BR>उल्लोलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surge
SURGE (subs.): कलोलः: v. Billow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surgeon
SURGEON: शस्त्रवैद्यः or sim. वैद्यः, when sense<BR>clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surgery
SURGERY: शल्यम्, -शास्त्रम्, -ज्ञानम्, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surgical
SURGICAL: by comp.,<BR>s. operation:<BR>शस्त्रकर्म, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surliness
SURLINESS:<BR>(1) कार्कश्यम्;<BR>(2) कर्कशता: v. Harsh-<BR>-ness, roughness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surly
SURLY: कर्कश (f. शा): v. Harsh, rough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surmise
SURMISE (subs.): वितर्कः: v. Supposition,<BR>conjecture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surmise
SURMISE (v.): शङ्कते (शङ्क्, c. 1.): v. To appre-<BR>-hend, guess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surmount
SURMOUNT:<BR>(1) अतिक्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.);<BR>(2)<BR>अत्येति (इ, c. 2.);<BR>(3) तरति (तॄ, c. 1.),<BR>may<BR>everybody s. the difficulties:<BR>सर्वस्तरतु दुर्गाणि, V. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surmountable
SURMOUNTABLE:<BR>(1) अतिक्रमणीय (f. या);<BR>(2)<BR>अतिक्रम्य (f. म्या); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surname
SURNAME: कुलनामन् (n.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surpass
SURPASS:<BR>(1) अतिक्रामति<BR>or<BR>-क्राम्यति (क्रम्, c. 1.<BR>and 4.),<BR>I see she is about s. ing Irābatī:<BR>अति-<BR>क्रामन्तीमिवेरावतीं प्रेक्षे, Mu. i.;<BR>(2) अत्येति (इ,<BR>c. 2.), Ki.: v. To excel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surpassing
SURPASSING:<BR>I Exceeding: expr. by comp.<BR>with अति-,<BR>s. the sun:<BR>अत्यादित्य (f. त्या), Me.<BR>i. 44.<BR>II Excellent: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surplice
SURPLICE:<BR>(1) उपरिच्छदः (?);<BR>(2) धौतावारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surplus
SURPLUS: उद्वृत्तम्,<BR>s. amount:<BR>उद्वृत्तं धनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surprise
SURPRISE (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) चमत्करोति,<BR>they<BR>were all s. ed with it:<BR>तेन चमत्कृताः सर्वे, Bha.;<BR>(2) विस्मापयति (c. of स्मि): v. To astonish.<BR>II To attack suddenly: अतर्कितं परति, (पत्,<BR>c. 1.: with loc.), Pri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surprise
SURPRISE (subs.):<BR>I Wonder: q. v.: विस्मयः<BR>II A sudden attack: अवस्कन्दः।<BR>III An<BR>unexpected event:<BR>fate brings on s. s:<BR>विधिरेव<BR> तानि घटयति यानि पुमान्नैव चिन्तयति, Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surprising
SURPRISING (adj.): विस्मयकर (f. री) and sim.<BR>comp.s.: v. Wonderful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surprisingly
SURPRISINGLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.:<BR>v. Also extremely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surrender
SURRENDER (v.):<BR>I To deliver, present:<BR>q. v.: उपानयति (नी, c. 1.).<BR>II To submit,<BR>take refuge: q. v.:<BR>(1) शरणं गच्छति, याति,<BR>etc.;<BR>(2) भजते, -ति (भज्, c. 1.),<BR>s. yourself<BR>to Lakṣmaṇa:<BR>सौमित्रेश्चरणं मज, Vi. vi. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surrender
SURRENDER (subs.):<BR>(1) समर्पणम् (= delivery);<BR>(2) उपानयनम् (= presenting);<BR>(3) प्रणतिः<BR>(= submission).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surreptitious
SURREPTITIOUS: मोषेण कृत (f. ता = done) or<BR>निवेशित (f. ता = entered), etc.: v. Stealth,<BR>fraudulent, forged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surreptitiously
SURREPTITIOUSLY: मोषेण: v. Stealthily, frau-<BR>-dulently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surround
SURROUND:<BR>(1) परिवृणोति<BR>or<BR>वारयति (वृ, c. 5.<BR>and 10.),<BR>your (men) s. ed him:<BR>तं तावकाः<BR> पर्यवारयन्, Mah. vii. 49. 16.;<BR>(2) वेष्टते<BR>or<BR>वेष्टयति,<BR> परि-, सं- (वेष्ट, c. 1. and 10.),<BR>s. ed by the<BR>serpent's coils:<BR>सर्पभोगेन वेष्टित (f. ता), V. p.<BR>v. 7. 22.;<BR>s. ed by the ocean:<BR>सागरेणाभिसंवृत<BR>(f. ता), Ram. v. 9. 14.: v. Also to en-<BR>-circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surrounding
SURROUNDING (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: expr. by verb. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">Page694</a>]<BR>परितस्तिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.): v. Also neighbour-<BR>-ing, near, bordering.<BR>II Of circumstances<BR>etc.: without knowing the s. s (s. circumstances):<BR>पौर्वापर्यमपरिज्ञाय।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surtout
SURTOUT: *अध्यावारः: v. Overcoat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

survey
SURVEY (v.):<BR>I To view, contemplate:<BR>q. v.: पश्यति (दृश्, c. 1.),<BR>to s. the far-reaching<BR>quarters:<BR>दिगन्तदिदृक्षया, Ki. i.; v. To see.<BR>II To measure: मापयति, परी- (c. of मा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

survey
SURVEY, -ING (subs.):<BR>I View, contempla-<BR>-tion: q. v.: अव-लोकः, -नम्।<BR>II Measurement:<BR>क्षेत्रमापः, -नम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

surveyor
SURVEYOR:<BR>I Lit.: दर्शक, परि- (f. र्शिका).<BR>II<BR>क्षेत्रमाप (f. पी), -क (f. पिका) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

survive
SURVIVE (v.):<BR>(1) जीवति (जीव्, c. 1.:) when<BR>sense clear),<BR>who else would like to s.:<BR>का<BR> मदन्या जिजीविषेत्, Mah. iv. 20. 11.;<BR>he alone<BR>might s.:<BR>एकः स जीव्यात्, Vi. iv. 10.;<BR>(2) by<BR>circumlo., Rati s.d Madana for a moment:<BR>मदनेन विनाकृता रतिः क्षणमात्रं जीविता, Ku. iv.<BR>21.: v. After, to live, remain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

survivor
SURVIVOR:<BR>(1) expr. by verb;<BR>(2) शेष (f. षा<BR>=remaining), the s.s submitted to him:<BR>शेषास्तं शरणं ययुः, R. iv. 64.;<BR>alas ! I heard that<BR>there were ten s.s:<BR>कष्टं युद्धे दश शेषाः श्रुता मे,<BR>Mah. i. 1. 220.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

susceptibility
SUSCEPTIBILITY:<BR>(1) योग्यता (= fitness);<BR>(2)<BR>ग्राह्यता (= admissibility): v. Also sensi-<BR>-bility, emotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

susceptible
SUSCEPTIBLE:<BR>(1) योग्य (f. ग्या = fit: q. v.);<BR>(2) ग्राह्य (f. ह्या = admissible).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suspect
SUSPECT:<BR>(1) शङ्कते, आ-, परि-, अभि-, वि-, सं-, प्र-,<BR>(शङ्क्, c. 1.), from whom you s. disregard:<BR>विशङ्कसे यतोऽवधीरणम्, Sa. iii. 16.;<BR>I did not s.<BR>that I had not seen him before:<BR>अदृष्टपूर्वोऽयमिति<BR> यथा न शङ्कितम्, K.; s. ing him that he was Nala:<BR>शङ्कमाना नलं तं वै, Mah. iii. 75. 10.;<BR>s. ing some-<BR>thing bad:<BR>अशोभनमाशङ्कमानः, K.;<BR>(2) by subs.:<BR>affection s.s evil:<BR>स्नेहः पापाशङ्की, S. iv.: v.<BR>Also apprehend, to guess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suspend
SUSPEND:<BR>I To hang up: q. v.: उद्बध्नाति<BR>(बन्ध्, c. 9.): v. Also to swing.<BR>II To<BR>defer: q. v.: निवर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR>III No<BR>equiv.: विष्टम्भयति (c. of स्तम्भ्) may be<BR>used: v. To dismiss (II).<BR>IV To make<BR>one depend: निघ्नं (f. घ्नां) करोति: v. To<BR>depend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suspense
SUSPENSE:<BR>(1) अनिश्चयः (=uncertainty);<BR>(2)<BR>सन्देहः (= doubt);<BR>(3) better by circumlo.:<BR>v. To waver, not know.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suspension
SUSPENSION:<BR>I Hanging up, swinging: by<BR>verb.<BR>II Interruption, cessation: q. v.:<BR>निवृत्तिः। Ph.:<BR>s. bridge:<BR>*उत्प्लवसेतुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suspicion
SUSPICION: शङ्का, आ-, परि-;<BR>others are to be<BR>arrested on s.:<BR>अन्येऽपि शङ्कया ग्राह्याः, Y.;<BR>without<BR>any s.:<BR>निःशङ्क (f. ङ्का), Bh.;<BR>disregarding all<BR>s. s:<BR>अगणितसर्वशङ्क (f. ङ्का), K.; various s.s:<BR>शङ्काततिः, N. xiii. 25.; I will remove your s.:<BR>तवाशङ्कामपनेष्यामि, Sa. v.; your s. is proper:<BR>साम्प्रतं ते आशङ्का, Sa. v.: v. Also doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suspicious
SUSPICIOUS:<BR>(1) शङ्कित, परि-, आ-, (f. ता),<BR>always s.:<BR>नित्यशङ्कितः, H. i. 24.;<BR>(2) शङ्किन्<BR>(f. नी), आ-, परि-; s. of my being another's wife:<BR>परपरिग्रहशङ्की, Sa. v.;<BR>(3) by verb or subs.,<BR>feeling s.:<BR>उपजातशङ्क (f. ङ्का), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suspiciously
SUSPICIOUSLY:<BR>(1) साशङ्कम्;<BR>(2) by pres. part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suspiciousness
SUSPICIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) शङ्कितता;<BR>(2) शङ्कितत्वम्,<BR> वि-, परि-: v. Suspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sustain
SUSTAIN: विभर्ति, प्र- (भृ, c. 3.) or rarely भरति<BR>(भृ, c. 1.),<BR>s. ed the burden of the world:<BR>धुरं<BR> धरित्र्या बिभराम्बभूव, R. xviii. 45.: v. To bear;<BR>you s. the appearance of the discontented:<BR>बिभर्षि<BR> चाकारमनिर्वृतानाम्, R. xiv. 7.: v. To keep up,<BR>hold;<BR>s. poor men:<BR>दरिद्रान् भर, H.: v. To<BR>maintain, support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sustenance
SUSTENANCE:<BR>(1) वर्तनम्,<BR>s. money:<BR>वर्तनधनम्,<BR>Da. 129.;<BR>(2) जीवनम् (rarely), to give s.:<BR>जीवनं ददाति, Da.: v. Support, maintenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sutler
SUTLER: पण्योपजीविन् (f. नी), Ra. and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

suture
SUTURE:<BR>I The act.:<BR>(1) सीवनम्;<BR>(2) स्यूतिः।<BR>II Seam: सन्धिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swab
SWAB:<BR>I Verb: मार्ष्टि (मृज्, c. 2.).<BR>II A<BR>brush: मार्जनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swaddle
SWADDLE: क्षौमपरिवृतं (f. तां) करोति, Bha.:<BR>v. To surround.<BR>S. ing cloth:<BR>क्षौमम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swagger
SWAGGER: (v.): v. To brag, strut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swain
SWAIN: ग्रामिकः: v. Rustic, lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swallow
SWALLOW (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) ग्रसते (ग्रस्,<BR>c. 1.), as if s. ing up the spirit (of other):<BR>ग्रसमानमिवौजांसि, Ki. xi. 73.;<BR>before he is s. ed<BR>up by the human king:<BR>यावन्नसंग्रस्यतेऽसौ पुरुषाधिपेन,<BR>B. xii. 4.;<BR>(2) गिल(र)ति (गॄ, c. 6.),<BR>that s.s<BR>whales:<BR>तिमिङ्गिलः।<BR>II Fig., to put up with,<BR>bear: q. v. perh. जरयति (c. of ज: compare<BR>Bengali idiom).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swallow
SWALLOW (subs.):<BR>I A bird: पक्षिविशेषः।<BR>II<BR>The gullet: गलः।<BR>III The act:<BR>(1) ग्रासः;<BR>(2) गिलनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swallow-wort
SWALLOW-WORT: a tree:<BR>(1) अर्कः, -पर्णः;<BR>(2)<BR>क्षीररसः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swamp
SWAMP:<BR>I Subs.: कच्छभूः: v. Marsh.<BR>II<BR>Verb: v. To plunge, overwhelm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swampy
SWAMPY:<BR>(1) अनूप (f. पा);<BR>(2) कच्छ (f. च्छा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swan
SWAN:<BR>(1) राजहंसः (?);<BR>(2) मरालः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sward
SWARD: perh. शाद्वलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swarm
SWARM (subs.):<BR>(1) संघः;<BR>(2) वृन्दम्: v.<BR>Multitude, throng, assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swarm
SWARM (v.):<BR>I To collect: q. v.: संपतति (पत्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II To crowd: q. v.: s. s with bees:<BR>शरघाव्याप्त (f. प्ता), -संकुल (f. ला), आकीर्ण (f. र्णा),<BR>जुष्ट (f. ष्टा), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swarthy
SWARTHY: श्याम (f. मा): v. Dark, black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swath
SWATH, -E (subs.): पट्टः: v. Bandage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swathe
SWATHE (v.): पट्टेन वेष्टयति (वेष्ट्, c. 10.),<BR>आवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swaz
SWAZ (subs.):<BR>I Rule, government: q. v.:<BR>शासनम्।<BR>II Power, control: q. v.: वशम्,<BR>under the s. of anger:<BR>क्रोधवश (f. शा).<BR>III<BR>Swing, sweep: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swaz
SWAZ (v.):<BR>I To rule, govern: q. v.: शास्ति<BR>(शास्, c. 2.).<BR>II To sweep, swing: q. v.:<BR>प्रेंखति (रिंख्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swear
SWEAR (v. t.):<BR>I To make: to s. an oath:<BR>शपथं शपति<BR>or<BR>शप्यति-ते (शप्, c. 1. and 4.), B.<BR>iii. 36.<BR>II To administer in oath to:<BR>शापयति (c. of शप्), shall s. Brahmins on truth:<BR>सत्येन शापयेद्विप्रम्, M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swear
SWEAR (v. i.): शपति<BR>or<BR>शप्यति,<BR>who have sworn<BR>together:<BR>संशप्तकाः, Mah. vii.: v. Also to<BR>curse;<BR>(2) शपथं करोति (=take an oath),<BR>swore before her friends:<BR>सखीनां पुरतः सशपथ-<BR>मभिहितवती, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swearer
SWEARER:<BR>(1) शप्तृ (f. प्त्री);<BR>(2) शापयितृ (f.<BR>त्री = of others);<BR>(3) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sweat
SWEAT (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) स्वेदः, s.-drops:<BR>स्वेदलवाः, R. xiii. 20.;<BR>(2) घर्मः;<BR>(3) स्वेदजलम्,<BR>and sim. comp.s, Si. i. 58.<BR>II Toil,<BR>labour: q. v.: परिश्रमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sweat
SWEAT (v. i.):<BR>I To perspire: स्विद्यति, प्र-<BR>(स्विद्, c. 4.),<BR>s. ing in fingers:<BR>स्विन्नाङ्गुलि<BR>(mfn.), Ku.<BR>II Labour: q. v.: परिश्राम्यति<BR>(श्रम्, c. 4.).<BR>III To rite oneself: ताम्यति<BR>(तम्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sweat
SWEAT (v. t.): To cause to s.: स्वेदयति, प्र- (c.<BR>of स्विद्), Bha.<BR>II To emit: q. v.: मुञ्जति<BR>(मुच्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sweep
SWEEP (subs.):<BR>I Compass, circuit: q. v.:<BR>(1) प्रसरः;<BR>(2) परिसरः, ph.:<BR>in one s. of the<BR>sword:<BR>एकेनैव कृपाणप्रहारेण, K.<BR>II Seer: q. v.<BR>III For drawing water: यष्टियन्त्रम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sweep
SWEEP (v.):<BR>I To cleanse: मार्ष्टि, मार्जयति, or<BR>मार्जति, सं-, परि- (मृज्, c. 2., 10. and 1.).<BR>II<BR>To s. away or off: वाहयति, अप- (c. of वह्),<BR>which has swept away Vaśiṣṭha:<BR>वशिष्ठापवाहः,<BR>Mah. ix. 14. 40.<BR>III To move rapidly<BR>over: जवेन अतिक्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>pass, move.<BR>IV To beat, strike: q. v.:<BR>ताड्यति (तड्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sweeper
SWEEPER:<BR>(1) सम्मार्जकः, etc.,<BR>the king's house-<BR>s.:<BR>नृपतेर्गृहसम्मार्जनकर्ता, P. i. 3.;<BR>(2) खलपूः<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sweepings
SWEEPINGS:<BR>(1) अवकरः;<BR>(2) सङ्करः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sweet
SWEET:<BR>(1) मधुर (f. रा),<BR>s. glances:<BR>मधुरा:<BR> कटाक्षाः, Ma. i. 26.;<BR>in the s. moon-like face<BR>of Rādhā:<BR>मधुरे राधामुखेन्दौ, Gi. iii. 16.;<BR>is light,<BR>s. and removes thirst:<BR>तृष्णाघ्नं मधुरं लघु, Bha.;<BR>by s. looks:<BR>मधुरैर्निरीक्षितैः, Ki. ii. 55.;<BR>what<BR>does not adorn s. figures:<BR>किमिव हि मधुराणां मण्डनं<BR> नाकृतीनाम्, S. i. 19.;<BR>(3) मिष्ट (f. ष्टा),<BR>eating<BR>s. things:<BR>मिष्टभोजिन् (f. नी), N. xvi. 111.;<BR>(3) मधुमय (f. यी: =honied), by s. words; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">Page696</a>]<BR>मधुमयीभिर्वाग्भिः, D.: v. Also tasteful, plea-<BR>-sant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sweeten
SWEETEN:<BR>I Trans.:<BR>(1) मधुरयति;<BR>(2) मधुरी-<BR>करोति।<BR>II Intrans.: मधुरीभवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sweetheart
SWEETHEART:<BR>(1) वल्लभ (f. भा), Si. vi. 26.;<BR>(2) प्रणयिन् (f. नी), Si. vi. 13.;<BR>(3) प्रिय (f. या),<BR>Si. vi. 15.;<BR>(4) दयित (f. ता), Si. iii. 27.;<BR>(5) कान्त (f. न्ता), Ki. ix. 6.;<BR>(6) रमण<BR>(f. णी), Si. vi. 71.;<BR>(7) कमन (f. नी:<BR>rare), Si vi. 74.;<BR>(8) इष्ट (f. ष्टा), Si. vi. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sweetly
SWEETLY: मधुरम्;<BR>(2) मिष्टम्;<BR>(3) by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sweetmeat
SWEETMEAT: मिष्टान्नम्,<BR>s. s and cakes:<BR>मिष्टान्नानि<BR> तथापूपान्, Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sweetness
SWEETNESS:<BR>(1) मधुरता<BR>or<BR>माधुर्यम्, s. of voice:<BR>स्वरे मधुरता, K.;<BR>(2) माधुरी;<BR>(3) मिष्टता: v.<BR>Also tastefulness, pleasantness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swell
SWELL (v. i.):<BR>(1) श्वयति, प्र-, उत्-, (श्वि, c. 1.),<BR>with highly swollen fierce red eyes:<BR>शेश्वीयमनारुण-<BR>रौद्रनेत्रः, B. iii. 30.;<BR>(2) स्फायते (स्फाय्, c. 1.),<BR>their martial dexterity s. ed:<BR>पस्फाये शस्त्रलाघवम्;<BR>B. xiv. 109.;<BR>(3) स्फीतीभवति: v. Also to<BR>increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swell
SWELL (v. t.):<BR>(1) स्फावयति, परि-, आ- (c. of<BR>स्फाय्),<BR>s. ing his pride:<BR>स्फावयन् स्वं प्रभावम्, B.<BR>xii. 76.;<BR>(2) श्वाययति (c. of श्वि: rare);<BR>(3)<BR>धमति, आ-। प्र- (ध्मा, c. 1.= puff up),<BR>as if<BR>swollen with sins:<BR>पापेनेवाध्मातमूर्तयः, K.: v.<BR>Also to increase, fill up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swell
SWELL (subs.):<BR>I S. ing: q. v.<BR>II Of waves:<BR>तरङ्गमाला, and sim. comp.s: v. Wave,<BR>billow.<BR>III As showy person: perh. स्फीत<BR>(f. ता) -जनः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swelling
SWELLING:<BR>I Lit.: स्फीतिः: v. Also increase,<BR>inflation.<BR>II Of the body:<BR>(1) श्वयथुः,<BR>to<BR>produce a s.:<BR>श्वयथुं जनयति, Si.; very deep s.:<BR>प्रगाढः श्वयथुः, Sr.;<BR>(2) शोथः<BR>or<BR>शोफः, ripe s.:<BR>पक्वः शोफः, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swellish
SWELLISH: स्फीत (f. ता),<BR>in a s. dress:<BR>स्फीत-<BR>परिवर्ह (f. र्हा), D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swerve
SWERVE: चलति (चल्, c. 1.), Ki. x. 29.: v.<BR>To move, deviate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swift
SWIFT (adj.):<BR>(1) वेगवत् (f. ती),<BR>very s.:<BR>वेगवत्तरः,<BR>K. xiii. 50.;<BR>(2) महावेग (f. गा), K.;<BR>(3)<BR>जवन (f. ना),<BR>swift horse:<BR>जवनवाजि-, R. ix.;<BR>(4) प्रजविन् (f. नी),<BR>s. camel-drivers:<BR>प्रजविन<BR> उष्ट्रपालाः, C. 51.;<BR>(5) शीघ्रग (f. गा) and sim.<BR>comp. s: v. Quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swift
SWIFT (subs.): a bird: *प्रजवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swiftly
SWIFTLY:<BR>(1) तूर्णम्: v. Quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swiftness
SWIFTNESS:<BR>(1) वेगः: v. Speed;<BR>(2) शीघ्रता:<BR>v. Quickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swill
SWILL: i. e. to take a s. of: अतिपानं करोति:<BR>v. To drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swim
SWIM (v.):<BR>I To float: q. v.: तरति (तॄ, c.<BR>1.),<BR>stones will s. in water not leaves:<BR>शिला<BR> तरिष्यत्युदके न पर्णम्, B. xii. 77.<BR>II With hands<BR>etc.: तरति, सं-,<BR>some swam across the waters<BR>with their hands:<BR>पयः केचिदतारिषुर्भुजैः, Si. xii.<BR>76.;<BR>s. ming in the waters:<BR>जले सन्तरन्, Vet.<BR>vii. Ph.:<BR>s. ming against the surfs:<BR>बाहुम्यां<BR> लहरीशिछन्दन्, Raj.<BR>III To be drenched:<BR>the<BR>earth s. s in blood:<BR>शोणितप्लाविता मही।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swim
SWIM, SWIMMING (subs.): सं-तरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swimmer
SWIMMER: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swimmingly
SWIMMINGLY: v. Successfully, smoothly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swindle
SWINDLE: वञ्चयति (वञ्च्, c. 10.): v. To cheat,<BR>deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swindler
SWINDLER: वञ्चक (f. ञ्चिका): v. Cheat,<BR>rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swindling
SWINDLING (subs.):<BR>(1) वञ्चना, प्र-;<BR>(2) शाठ्यभ्:<BR>v. Roguery<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swine
SWINE: शूकरः: v. Boar, hog, sow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swing
SWING (subs.):<BR>I For s. ing: दोला, R. ix. 46.<BR>II S. ing:<BR>(1) दोलनम्;<BR>(2) प्रेङ्खनम्, हिन्दोलः<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swing
SWING:<BR>I Intrans.:<BR>(1) दोलायते (nomi.);<BR>(2) प्रेङ्खति (ईङ्ख्, c. 1.), with s. ing leaves:<BR>प्रेङ्खत्पत्र (f. त्रा), K.<BR>II Trans.:<BR>(1) प्रेङ्खयति<BR>(c. of ईङ्ख्),<BR>s. ing them:<BR>ताः प्रेङ्खयन्, R. xix.<BR>44.;<BR>(2) आन्दोलयति (nomi.);<BR>(3) हिन्दोलयति<BR>(nomi.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swinish
SWINISH: शूकरसन्निभ and sim. comp. s (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

switch
SWITCH: पिञ्जा: v. Rod, twig.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swivel
SWIVEL: संबन्धनी (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swoon
SWOON (subs.):<BR>(1) मूर्च्छा;<BR>(2) मोहः, प्र-, Ku.<BR>iii. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swoon
SWOON (v.):<BR>(1) मूर्च्छति (मूर्च्छ्, c. 1.);<BR>(2)<BR>मुह्यति (मुह्, c. 4.);<BR>(3) मोहं गच्छति; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

swoop
SWOOP:<BR>I Subs.: अवपातः।<BR>II Verb.:<BR>आकस्मिकावपातेन गृह्णाति (ग्रह्, c. 9. = sieze: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sword
SWORD:<BR>(1) असिः,<BR>s. s whose sharpness has been<BR>increased by case-hardening:<BR>असयः पानवर्द्धित-<BR>तैक्ष्ण्याः, K.; fortune dwells on the edges of s. s:<BR>लक्ष्मीरसिधारासु निवसति, K.; without s. or shield:<BR>व्यसिचर्मन् (mfn.), Mah. vii. 48. 39.;<BR>(2) खङ्गः,<BR>whose is this s. with golden hilt in a sheath of<BR>cow-skin:<BR>कस्य हेमत्सरुः खङ्गो गव्ये कोशे समर्पितः,<BR>Mah. iv. 42. 13.;<BR>(3) निस्त्रिंशः,<BR>he striving with<BR>a s. in his hand:<BR>हस्तेन निस्त्रिंशभृता स दीप्तः, Ki.<BR>xvii. 56.;<BR>(4) कृपाणः,<BR>having a great s.:<BR>महा-<BR>कृपाणं कलयत् (f. न्ती), Ku. xv. 43.; use (your)<BR>s. on this Śudra-sage:<BR>विसृज शूद्रमुनौ कृपाणम्, M.<BR>ii. 10;<BR>(5) करपाल (बाल<BR>or<BR>वार);<BR>(6) तरवारः(लः)<BR>or<BR>तरवारिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sycamore
SYCAMORE: वृक्षविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sycophancy
SYCOPHANCY: चाटुकारिता, -त्वम्: v. Flattery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sycophant
SYCOPHANT:<BR>(1) चाटुकार (f. री);<BR>(2) चाटुकारिन्<BR>(f. णी): v. Flatterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

syllabic
SYLLABIC: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

syllable
SYLLABLE: अक्षरम्, vocabulary of words of one s.:<BR>एकाक्षरकोशः;<BR>descriptions of metres with feet of<BR>eleven s. s:<BR>एकादशाक्षरपादवृत्तभेदः, P. h.;<BR>words of<BR>three s. s with penultimate D.:<BR>दत्रिः, Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

syllogism
SYLLOGISM: न्यायः,<BR>s. is not required for what is<BR>ascertained:<BR>न निर्णीतार्थे न्यायः प्रवर्तते, N. d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

syllogistic
SYLLOGISTIC:<BR>(1) न्याय- in comp.;<BR>(2) न्याय-<BR>सङ्गत (f. ता) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

symbol
SYMBOL:<BR>(1) चिह्नम्: v. Sign, mark;<BR>(2) प्रति-<BR>रूपम् (=representative).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

symbolical
SYMBOLICAL:<BR>(1) by subs.: he is (merely)<BR>s.<BR>of piety:<BR>स धर्मप्रतिरूपकः, M. xi. 9.;<BR>(2) लाक्षणिक<BR>(f. की = significant, indicative: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

symmetrical
SYMMETRICAL:<BR>(1) सुष्ठु (mfn. (?);<BR>(2) सम (f.<BR>मा= even).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

symmetrically
SYMMETRICALLY:<BR>(1) सुष्ठु;<BR>(2) by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

symmetry
SYMMETRY:<BR>(1) सौष्ठवम् (?);<BR>(2) साम्यम् (= even-<BR>-ness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sympathetic
SYMPATHETIC, -AL:<BR>(1) समानुभूति (mfn.);<BR>(2)<BR>सदय (f. या = kind);<BR>(3) स्निग्ध (f. ग्धा=loving).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sympathetically
SYMPATHETICALLY:<BR>(1) सहानुभूत्या;<BR>(2) सदयम्<BR>(=kindly);<BR>(3) स्निग्धम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sympathize
SYMPATHIZE:<BR>I To feel: q. v.: अनुभवति (भू,<BR>c. 1.: with acc.).<BR>II To have considera-<BR>-tion for: आद्रियते (दृ, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sympathy
SYMPATHY:<BR>I The feeling:<BR>(1) सहानुभूतिः (?);<BR>(2) प्रेमन् (n. = love),<BR>subdivided by s.:<BR>प्रेम्णा<BR> समानीय विभज्यमानः Ki. iii. 33.<BR>II Kindness,<BR>compassion: q. v.: दया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

symphony
SYMPHONY: एकतानता: v. Harmony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

symptom
SYMPTOM:<BR>(1) लक्षणम्;<BR>(2) चिह्नम्;<BR>(3) लिङ्गम्,<BR>are the general s.s of insanity:<BR>सामान्यमुन्मादग-<BR>दस्य लिङ्गम्, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

synagogue
SYNAGOGUE:<BR>(1) समाजः: v. Assembly;<BR>(2)<BR>सभागृहम्: v. Hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

synchronism
SYNCHRONISM:<BR>(1) यौगपद्यम्;<BR>(2) समकालीनताः;<BR>(3) एककालिकता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

synchronous
SYNCHRONOUS:<BR>(1) समकालीन (f. ना);<BR>(2)<BR>एककालिक (f. की); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

syncope
SYNCOPE (subs.):<BR>I Swoon, fainting: q. v.:<BR>मूर्च्छा।<BR>II In gram: मध्याक्षरलोपः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

syndic
SYNDIC: प्रविवेचकः,<BR>s. ate:<BR>*समा<BR>or<BR>समितिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

synecdoche
SYNECDOCHE: लक्षणा, Kav.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

synod
SYNOD: धर्मसमवायः and sim. comp.: v. Assem-<BR>-bly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

synodical
SYNODICAL: expr. by comp.; ph.: s. month:<BR>चान्द्रमासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

synonym
SYNONYM: i. e. synonymous^1 word: q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

synonymous
SYNONYMOUS: एकार्थवाचिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp. s,<BR>of s. terms:<BR>एकार्थवाचिनां पर्यायशब्दानाम्,<BR>Say.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

synopsis
