tailor-bird
TAILOR-BIRD:<BR>(1) चञ्चुसूचिः;<BR>(2) टुण्टुकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tailoring
TAILORING:<BR>(1) सूचिकर्मन् (n.);<BR>(2) सूच्यासेवनम्,<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taint
TAINT (v.): दूषयति (c. of दुष्): v. To stain,<BR>pollute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taint
TAINT (subs.):<BR>I Corruption: q. v.: दूषणम्<BR>II Stain: q. v.: कलङ्कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

take
TAKE (v. t.):<BR>I In general:<BR>(1) गृह्नाति (ग्रह,<BR>c. 9.),<BR>t. ing and looking:<BR>गृहीत्वा निरीक्ष्य, Mu.<BR>i.;<BR>t. up arms:<BR>गृहाण शस्त्रम्, R. iii. 51.;<BR>t. n but<BR>afterwards released:<BR>गृहीतप्रतिमुक्त (f. क्ता), R.<BR>iv. 43.;<BR>he took the way of running pigs:<BR>जग्राह<BR> स द्रुतवराहकुलस्य मार्गम्, R. ix. 59.; did she t. (it)<BR>from the hinds:<BR>तया गृहीतं नु मृगाङ्गनाभ्यः, Ku. i.<BR>46.;<BR>when he t. s your hand solemnly:<BR>अनेन<BR> पाणौ विधिवद् गृहीते, R. vi. 63.;<BR>intending to t.<BR>the arrow:<BR>शरं जिगृक्षुः, Ki. xiii. 32.;<BR>without t.<BR>ing beetles:<BR>अगृहीतताम्बूल (f. ला), C. v.;<BR>took<BR>a few mouthfuls:<BR>कतिचित् कवलान्यगृह्णात्, C. v.;<BR>rustics t. (it)<BR>otherwise:<BR>अन्यथा गृह्णन्ति ग्राम्याः,<BR>C. vii.;<BR>do not t. advice:<BR>न गृह्णन्त्युपदेशम्, K.;<BR>to t. all forms:<BR>विश्वरूपत्वं ग्रहीतुम्, K.;<BR>to t.<BR>venerable men by service:<BR>ग्रहीतुमार्यान् परिचर्यया,<BR>Si. i. 17.; so long as Rākṣasa is not t.n:<BR>अगृहीते राक्षसे, Mu. i.;<BR>when they t.ing your<BR>signs:<BR>तेषु गृहीतसंज्ञेषु, Mu. i.;<BR>are t.n as if by<BR>evils stars:<BR>ग्रहैरिव गृह्यन्ते, K.; t. the pride of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">Page699</a>]<BR>killing a woman:<BR>गृहाण वधूवधपौरुषम्, N. iv.<BR>53.; His Majesty who has t.n his name well:<BR>तस्य सुगृहीतनाम्नो देवस्य, C. vii.;<BR>(2) आदत्ते, सम्-,<BR>(दा, c. 3.: physically),<BR>t.ing the girl by the<BR>hand:<BR>कन्यामाददानः करेण, Ku.;<BR>for t. ing is for<BR>spending:<BR>आदानं हि विसर्गाय, R.: v. Also to<BR>catch, hold, view, understand.<BR>II Special.<BR>Ph.:<BR>to t. food:<BR>आहारं करोति;<BR>t. rest:<BR>विश्रामं<BR> करोति;<BR>t. aim at:<BR>लक्ष्यीकरोति;<BR>t. root:<BR>मूलं बध्नाति;<BR>t. compassion:<BR>दयां करोति;<BR>t. fire:<BR>अग्निमुपैति;<BR>t.<BR>courage:<BR>समाश्वसिति;<BR>t. leave of:<BR>आमन्त्रयति;<BR>t. oath:<BR>शपथं करोति;<BR>t. pains:<BR>परिश्रमं करोति; t.<BR>place: v. To happen;<BR>t. part:<BR>हस्तं ददाति;<BR>t. care of:<BR>रक्षति;<BR>t. effect:<BR>सफलीभवति;<BR>t.<BR>wine etc.:<BR>मद्यं etc. सेवते, नि- (सेव्, c. 1.),<BR>Ni.;<BR>time for t.ing medicines:<BR>भैषज्यसेवनकालः,<BR>Bha.;<BR>it is time to t. bath and food:<BR>समयः<BR> खलु स्नानभोजने सेवितुम्। V. v. 11.<BR>III To<BR>conduct, convey: q. v.: नयति (नी, c. 1.),<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

take
TAKE (v. i.):<BR>I To have effect: to t. well:<BR>हितं करोति।<BR>II To resort: q. v.: श्रयति (श्रि,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>III To please: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

take away
TAKE AWAY:<BR>I To take, carry: q. v.: आदत्ते।<BR>II To remove: q. v.:<BR>(1) अपनयति, वि-,<BR>the<BR>darkness of rage should be taken away:<BR>रोषमयं<BR> तिमिरमपनेयम्, Ki. ii. 36.;<BR>(2) हरति, अप-,<BR>I will<BR>t. this fortune by gambling:<BR>द्यूतेन श्रियं हरिष्यामि,<BR>Mah. ii. 56. 1.;<BR>(3) अपवहति (वह्, c. 1.),<BR>t.ing away the bladder:<BR>क्लोमपोह्य, D. viii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

take down
TAKE DOWN:<BR>I Lit.: अधो नयति etc.<BR>II To<BR>write down: लिखति (लिख्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

take for
TAKE FOR: v. To take, regard, view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

take in
TAKE IN, INTO:<BR>I To take, as water: गृह्णाति।<BR>II To cheat: q. v.: विप्रलभते (लभ्, c. 1.).<BR>III To contract: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

take off
TAKE OFF:<BR>I To remove: q. v.:<BR>(1) अपनयति,<BR>t.ing off their helmets:<BR>अपनीतशिरस्त्राणाः, R. iv.<BR>64.;<BR>(2) उन्मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.: only of shoes,<BR>etc.), t. ing them (the shoes)<BR>off:<BR>तद्य्न्मुच्य,<BR>Vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

take on
TAKE ON:<BR>I To assume: गृह्णाति।<BR>II To<BR>lament: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

take out
TAKE OUT:<BR>I Lit.: बहिष्करोति,<BR>t. ing out his son<BR>from the granary:<BR>तत्पुत्रं कुशूलाद्वहिष्कृत्य, H. ii.<BR>II To remove: q. v.: अपनयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

take round
TAKE ROUND: परिणयति, Ku. vii. 80.: v. Take,<BR>round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

take to
TAKE TO: सेवते, (सेव्, c. 1.),<BR>everyday took to<BR>hunting:<BR>सदा सिषेवे मृगयाम्, K. s. xi. 3.: v.<BR>Betake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

take to oneself
TAKE TO ONESELF: v. Take upon oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

take up
TAKE UP:<BR>I In gen.: गृह्णाति, परि-।<BR>II To<BR>begin: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

take upon oneself
TAKE UPON ONESELF: स्वयं व्यवस्यति (सो, c. 4.).<BR>: v. To undertake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taker
TAKER:<BR>(1) ग्रहीतृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) नेतृ (f. त्री);<BR>etc.: v. To take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taking
TAKING (adj.): मोहन (f. नी): v. Charming,<BR>attractive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talc
TALC:<BR>(1) अभ्रम्, -कम्,<BR>calx of t.:<BR>अभ्र्तकभस्मन् (n.);<BR>(2) अम्बरम्;<BR>(3) गिरिजम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tale
TALE:<BR>I Story: q. v.:<BR>(1) कथा,<BR>narrate some<BR>t. to me:<BR>कथामाखयाहि मे कांचित्, K. s. x. 3.;<BR>(2) आख्यानम्, उप- (=narrative);<BR>(3)<BR>आख्यायिका (=romance).<BR>II Enumeration:<BR>गणना, परि-, Me. i. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talent
TALENT:<BR>I Natural ability: शक्तिः: v.<BR>Genius.<BR>II Intellectual ability: धीशक्तिः<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR>III A coin or<BR>weight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talented
TALENTED: धीशक्तिसम्पन्न (f. न्ना) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talisman
TALISMAN:<BR>I Amulet: q. v.: कवचः।<BR>II<BR>Magic: माया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talk
TALK (subs.):<BR>(1) आलापः,<BR>it is the t. of the<BR>remotest corners:<BR>दिगन्तरेष्वयमालापो वर्तते, K.:<BR>v. Conversation;<BR>(2) उक्तिः: v. Saying,<BR>rumour;<BR>(3) जल्पः, -नम्<BR>or<BR>जल्पितम् (=idle t.);<BR>(4) कथा, सम्- (= chat), and having other t.:<BR>अन्याभिश्च कथामिः, K.;<BR>I will hear their private<BR>t.:<BR>शृणोमि विश्वस्तकथितान्यासाम्, Sa. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talk
TALK (v.):<BR>(1) आलपति, सं- (लप्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To converse;<BR>(2) भाषते, सं- (भाष्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To speak, say.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talkative
TALKATIVE:<BR>(1) जल्पाक (f. की), with t. women:<BR>जल्पाकीभिः सह स्त्रीभिः। B. vii. 19.;<BR>(2) जल्पनशील [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">Page700</a>]<BR>(f. ला), and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(3) बहुभाषिन्<BR>(f. णी) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talkativeness
TALKATIVENESS:<BR>(1) बहुभाषिता, etc.;<BR>(2) by<BR>adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tall
TALL:<BR>(1) उच्च (f. च्चा,=high),<BR>she has protrud-<BR>ing eyes, is very t.:<BR>कठोरनेत्रा सात्युच्चा, M. p.<BR>69. 30.;<BR>from a t. tree:<BR>उच्चतरोः, Si. vii. 38.;<BR>(2) दीर्घ (f. र्घा=long), and (she)<BR>who is very<BR>t.:<BR>अतीव या च दीर्घा, V. m. 70. 20.;<BR>(3) प्रांशु<BR>(mfn.: rare), which can be reached by a t.<BR>(man): प्रंशुलभ्य (f. भ्या), R. i. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tallness
TALLNESS:<BR>(1) उच्चता;<BR>(2) दीर्घता (only of<BR>person);<BR>(3) प्रांशुता (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tallow
TALLOW: मेषादीनां वसा: v. Fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tallow-candle
TALLOW-CANDLE: वसावर्तिः (?) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tally
TALLY (v.): संवदति (वद्, c. 1.): v. To agree,<BR>fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tally
TALLY (subs.):<BR>I Match: q. v.: अनुरूप (f. पा).<BR>II *व्यवहारदण्डः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talmud
TALMUD: इहुदीयसंहिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talon
TALON: नखरः: v. Claw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tamarind
TAMARIND:<BR>I The tree:<BR>(1) चिञ्चा, -वृक्षः, D.;<BR>(2) तिन्तिडी(ली);<BR>(3) अम्लि(म्ली)का।<BR>II The<BR>fruit:<BR>(1) चिञ्चा, -फलम्;<BR>(2) तिन्तिडी, -कम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tamarind-fish
TAMARIND-FISH: [चिञ्चारसरञ्जितः] इल्लसः, Bha.<BR>(ईल्लीशः<BR>or<BR>ईलीशः, Wilson).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tamarisk
TAMARISK:<BR>(1) भ्कावुः(वूः), -कः;<BR>(2) पिचुलः<BR>(ambiguous).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tambour
TAMBOUR, -INE: डिण्डिमः: v. Drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tame
TAME (adj.):<BR>I Of animals:<BR>(1) गृह्य (f. ह्या<BR>= domestic: q. v. );<BR>(2) ग्राम्य (f. म्या =<BR>village: q. v. );<BR>(3) विनीत (f. ता).<BR>II<BR>Spiritless: निस्तेजस् (mfn.), and sim. comp.s.<BR>: v. Also dull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tame
TAME (v.):<BR>(1) दमयति (c. of दम्), t.ing all:<BR>सर्वदमन (f. नी), Sa. vii.;<BR>(2) विनयति (नी,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>as if to t. the wild beasts:<BR>वन्यान्<BR> विनेष्यन्निव दुष्टसत्त्वान्, R. ii. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tamely
TAMELY: कापुरुषवत्: v. Meanly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tameness
TAMENESS:<BR>I Lit.: विनीतता: v. Tame.<BR>II<BR>Fig.: निस्तेजस्कता: v. Also dullness, mean-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tamer
TAMER:<BR>(1) दमयितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) विनेतृ (f. त्री),<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tamper with
TAMPER WITH (v.):<BR>I To meddle: q. v.:<BR>II To corrupt: q. v.:<BR>(1) दूषयति (c. of<BR>दुष्);<BR>(2) वशीकरोति (=get over).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tan
TAN:<BR>I As leather: शोधयति (c. of शुध्).<BR>II<BR>To make brown: श्यामीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tandem
TANDEM:<BR>to drive t.:<BR>अग्रपश्चादश्वौ चालयति etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tangent
TANGENT: *स्पर्शरेखा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tangible
TANGIBLE:<BR>I Lit.: स्पर्शनीय (f. या): v. To<BR>touch.<BR>II Perceptible, palpable: q. v.:<BR>प्रकट (f. टा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tangle
TANGLE: v. Entangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tank
TANK:<BR>I Of water:<BR>(1) तडागम्;<BR>(2) दीर्घिका<BR>(long t.);<BR>(3) वापी (= square t.);<BR>(4)<BR>जलाशयः (in gen.).<BR>II A vessel: कृण्डम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tankard
TANKARD: चषक (mn.= cup).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tanner
TANNER: चर्मशोधक (f. धिका) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tantalize
TANTALIZE: perh. आशां वर्द्धयति (c. of वृध् =<BR>raise hope).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tantamount
TANTAMOUNT: expr. with फलित (f. ता): v.<BR>Equivalent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tanyard
TANYARD: चर्मशोधनचत्वरम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tap
TAP (v.):<BR>I To base a hole; छिद्रयति (छिद्र,<BR>c. 10.).<BR>II To hit lightly: लघु आहन्ति<BR>(हन्, c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tap
TAP:<BR>(1) लघुघातः;<BR>(2) मृदुचपेटः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tape
TAPE: no equiv.: *तेपः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taper
TAPER (Sus): दीपिका (?): v. Light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taper
TAPER, -ING (adj.):<BR>(1) वृत्तानुपूर्व (f. र्वा);<BR>(2)<BR>गोपुच्छाकार (f. रा), M.n.; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tapestry
TAPESTRY: चित्रयवनिका (?): v. Screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tapeworm
TAPEWORM: कृमिः,<BR>removes t.s:<BR>कृमिनुत् (mfn.),<BR>Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tapir
TAPIR: a pig-like animal: *तापीडः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tar
TAR:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) सर्जरसः;<BR>(2) सरलद्रवः;<BR>(3) रालः, अ-।<BR>II Smear with t.: v. To<BR>besmear;<BR>t. red:<BR>अराललिप्त (f. प्ता), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tarantula
TARANTULA: a spider: *तारन्तकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tardily
TARDILY: चिरेण: v. Slowly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tardiness
TARDINESS: v. Slowness, lateness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tardy
TARDY:<BR>(1) चिरक्रियः (या, यं: of men); [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">Page701</a>]<BR>(2) with चिर- in comp.<BR>or<BR>चिरेण<BR>or<BR>विलम्बित<BR>(= delayed): v. Slow, late.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tare
TARE:<BR>I A weed: कक्षभेदः।<BR>II In commerce:<BR>क्षयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

target
TARGET:<BR>I A shield: क्षुद्रचर्मन् (n.).<BR>II Aim:<BR>लक्ष्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

targeteer
TARGETEER: चर्मधरः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tariff
TARIFF: (पण्य) शुल्कपत्रिका and sim. comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tarnish
TARNISH (v. t.): दूषयति (c. of दुष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tarnish
TARNISH (v. i.): मलिनीभवति: v. Also dull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tarry
TARRY: विलम्ब्ते (लम्ब्, c. 1.): v. To stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tart
TART:<BR>I Adj.: अम्ल (f. म्ला): v. Sour.<BR>II<BR>Subs.: *अम्लीयम्,<BR>t. fruit:<BR>अब्लीयं फलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tartar
TARTAR:<BR>(1) दन्तशर्करा;<BR>(2) पुष्पिका;<BR>(3) दन्त-<BR>मलम्;<BR>(4) पिप्पिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

task
TASK (subs.):<BR>(1) कर्मन्: v. Work;<BR>(2) भारः:<BR>Burden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

task
TASK (v.):<BR>I Lit.: कर्म न्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.).<BR>II To take to t.: अनुशास्ति (शास्, c. 2.): v.<BR>Also to task.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tassel
TASSEL: perh. पिच्छः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taste
TASTE:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) स्वादः, -नम्, आ-;<BR>(2)<BR>रसः, -नम्। Ph.: to have a t. of: v. To<BR>taste.<BR>II Flavour, relish:<BR>(1) स्वादः, आ-;<BR>(2) रसः,<BR>so t. of tongue:<BR>तथा रसो रसज्ञायाः, Par.<BR>III The sense: रसनम्,<BR>of t. of sight:<BR>रासनं,<BR> चाक्षुषम्, Par.<BR>IV Critical judgment, liking:<BR>रुचिः,<BR>men have different t. s:<BR>भिन्नरुचिर्लोकः, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taste
TASTE (v. t.):<BR>(1) स्वादयति, आ- (c. of स्वद्),<BR>to<BR>t. blood:<BR>शोणितमास्वादयति, Mu. i. 8.;<BR>(2)<BR>रसयति (रस्, c. 10.),<BR>to t. wine:<BR>वारुणीं रसयति,<BR>Ki. ix. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taste
TASTE (v.i.): स्वदते (स्वद्, c. 1.), N. iii. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taste of
TASTE OF (v.t.):<BR>I To taste: q. v.: रसयति।<BR>II To smack of:<BR>(1) स्वदते with an adj. or<BR>adv.,<BR>t. s of garlic:<BR>सलशुनः (ना, नं) स्वदते;<BR>(2)<BR>by comp. with स्वाद (= flavour).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tasteful
TASTEFUL:<BR>I Savoury:<BR>(1) स्वादु (f. also द्वी),<BR>sand-water is cool and t.:<BR>चिकिरं शीतलं स्वादु,<BR>Bha.;<BR>(2) रुच्य (f. च्या = relishing);<BR>(3)<BR>रुचिकर (f. री = 2.);<BR>(4) रोचन (f. नी = 2.).<BR>II<BR>Showing good taste:<BR>(1) हृद्य;<BR>(2) हृदय-<BR>ग्राहिन् (f. णी) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tastefully
TASTEFULLY: expr. by adj.: v. Also neatly,<BR>skilfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tastefulness
TASTEFULNESS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) स्वादुता;<BR>(2) रुच्यता;<BR>(3) रुचिकरत्वम्;<BR>(4) रोचनत्वम्।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1)<BR>हृद्यता;<BR>(2) हृदयग्राहिता, and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tasteless
TASTELESS:<BR>(1) नीरस (f. सा);<BR>(2) विरस (f.<BR>सा);<BR>(3) अरस (f. सा);<BR>(4) रसहीन (f. ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taster
TASTER: Lit. and fig.:<BR>(1) रसयितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) स्वादयितृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tastily
TASTILY, TASTINESS, TASTY: v. Tastefully,<BR>tastefulness, tasteful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tatter
TATTER: चीरचीवरम्: v. Rag.<BR>T.ed:<BR>जीर्ण<BR>(f. र्णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tattle
TATTLE, TATTLER: v. Babble, babbler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tattoo
TATTOO:<BR>I Subs.: पटहप्रणादः and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Verb.: संरञ्जयति (रन्ज्, c. 10.)<BR>(?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taunt
TAUNT:<BR>I Verb: अधिक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.):<BR>v. To censure, abuse.<BR>II Subs.: आक्षेपः:<BR>v. Censure, abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tauntingly
TAUNTINGLY:<BR>(1) साक्षेपम्;<BR>(2) साधिक्षेपम्;<BR>(3)<BR>सोपालम्भम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tautological
TAUTOLOGICAL or TAUTOLOGOUS: t. (expres-<BR>sion): पुनरुक्त (f. क्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tautology
TAUTOLOGY:<BR>(1) पुनरुक्तिः;<BR>(2) पुनरुक्तम्, -त्वम् (ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tavern
TAVERN: पथिकाश्रमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tawdry
TAWDRY: बहिरुज्ज्वल (f. ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tawny
TAWNY:<BR>(1) पिङ्ग (f. ङ्गा);<BR>(2) पिङ्गलः (ला, लं);<BR>(3) पिशङ्ग (f. ङ्गी);<BR>(4) कपिलः (ला, लं);<BR>(5)<BR>कडारः (रा, रं);<BR>(6) कद्रु (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tax
TAX:<BR>(1) करः, M. viii. 307.: v. Revenue;<BR>(2) शुल्कः: v. Custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tax
TAX (v.):<BR>I Lit.: करं न्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.)<BR>or<BR>निदधाति (धा, c. 3.) (with loc.).<BR>II Fig.,<BR>as to t. one's energies: आयासयति (nomi.).<BR>III To censure: q. v.: अनुशास्ति (शास्,<BR>c. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taxable
TAXABLE:<BR>(1) करयोग्य (f. ग्या);<BR>(2) करार्ह (f.<BR>र्हा), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taxation
TAXATION:<BR>indirect and direct t.:<BR>*व्यवहिता-<BR>व्यवहितकरनिधानम्<BR>or<BR>-स्थापनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tea
TEA: चहा,<BR>to take t.:<BR>चहां पिबति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teach
TEACH: अध्यापयति (c. of इ: with double [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">Page702</a>]<BR>acc.),<BR>taught you the Vedantas:<BR>वेदान्तानध्यजीगपत्,<BR>An. iii. 13.; अव्यापितस्योशनसापि नीतिम्, Ku.<BR>iii. 6.: v. To instruct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teachable
TEACHABLE:<BR>(1) अध्यापनीय (f. या);<BR>(2) शिक्षार्ह<BR>(f. र्हा), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teacher
TEACHER:<BR>(1) अव्यापक (f. पिका);<BR>(2) शिक्षक<BR>(f. क्षिका);<BR>(3) शिक्षयितृ (f. त्री). Religious<BR>t.:<BR>(1) उपाव्याय (f. यी);<BR>(2) आचार्य (f. र्यानी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teaching
TEACHING (subs.):<BR>(1) अव्यापनम् (the act);<BR>(2)<BR>शिक्षा (= instruction: q. v. ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teak
TEAK:<BR>I The tree: अर्णः।<BR>II The wood:<BR>अर्णम्, -काष्ठम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teal
TEAL: a bird: श्मरालिः (तिः also -री<BR>or<BR>ली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

team
TEAM: expr. by pl. or with युग्य (f. ग्या =<BR>yoked),<BR>t. of oxen:<BR>गावः;<BR>t. of horses:<BR>युग्याः<BR>(when sense clear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teamster
TEAMSTER: expr. by वाहक etc. (= driver:<BR>q. v. ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tear
TEAR (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अश्रु (स्रु, n.),<BR>shedding of t. s.:<BR>अश्रुपातः, Ve.;<BR>her breast<BR>starred with t.-drops:<BR>अश्रुबिन्दुतारकितपयोधरा, D.<BR>ii.;<BR>veiled with continuous flow of t.s;<BR>अश्रुस्रोतो-<BR>ऽवगुण्ठितः (ता, तं) D. i.; with cool t.s (i. e. of<BR>joy): शिशिरेणाश्रुणा, D. v.;<BR>(2) बाष्पः, -जलम्,<BR>etc.,<BR>the throat almost choked with t.s:<BR>बाष्प-<BR>कुण्ठकण्ठः, D. v.;<BR>drew t. s in the shape of sap<BR>from boughs;<BR>अकरोत्॥॥॥स्रुतशाखारसबाष्पदूषितान्,<BR>R. viii. 70.;<BR>(3) अस्रम्(श्रम्), blinded by t.s:<BR>अस्रान्धतया, R. xiv. 2.;<BR>(4) नयनजलम्, and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Rent, fissure: छिद्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tear
TEAR (v.):<BR>I To rend, shatter: q. v.:<BR>विदारयति (दॄ, c. 10.).<BR>II As letters: छिनत्ति<BR>(छिद्, c. 7. = to cut),<BR>torn garment:<BR>छिन्नं<BR> वस्रम्; t.s away (or off) in our presence:<BR>मिषतामाच्छिनत्ति नः, Ku. ii. 46.<BR>III To pluck,<BR>pull: q. v.<BR>IV Move violently: धावति,<BR> परि- (धाव्, c. 1.). Ph.:<BR>t. open:<BR>छित्वा<BR> उन्मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.): v. To open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tearful
TEARFUL:<BR>(1) साश्रु (mfn.);<BR>(2) पर्यश्रु (mfn.);<BR>(3) अश्रुसङ्कुल (f. ला);<BR>(4) सबाष्प (f. ष्पा), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tearfully
TEARFULLY: expr. by adj. or comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tearless
TEARLESS:<BR>(1) निरश्रु (mfn.) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tease
TEASE: क्षोभयति (c. of क्षुभ्): v. To vex.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teat
TEAT: वृन्तम्: v. Also nipple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

technical
TECHNICAL:<BR>I Lit.: परिभाषिक (f. की).<BR>II<BR>As of objection: कूट- in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

technicality
TECHNICALITY:<BR>I Lit.: पारिभाषिकत्वम् (-ता).<BR>A t. term: पारिभाषिकशब्दः।<BR>III As of objec-<BR>-tion: कूटता<BR>or<BR>त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

technically
TECHNICALLY:<BR>(1) परिभाषानुसारेण;<BR>(2) better<BR>by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

technology
TECHNOLOGY:<BR>I Of arts: शिल्पविज्ञानम्।<BR>II<BR>Of terms: परिभाषा,<BR>general t.:<BR>सामान्यपरिभाषा।<BR>Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tedious
TEDIOUS:<BR>I Tiresome, wearisome: q. v.:<BR>क्लान्तिकर (f. री) and sim. comp.s,<BR>if it is not<BR>very t.:<BR>तद् यदि नातिखेदकरम्, K.<BR>II Slow:<BR>q. v.: मन्थर (f. रा).<BR>III As a writer:<BR>दीर्घसूत्र (f. त्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tediously
TEDIOUSLY:<BR>I So as to tire:<BR>(1) expr. by<BR>circumlo.;<BR>(2) अतिदीर्घम् (= very long).<BR>II<BR>Slowly: मन्थरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teadiousness
TEADIOUSNESS:<BR>I Wearisomeness:<BR>(1) खेद-<BR>जननत्वम्, -ता;<BR>(2) by circumlo.<BR>II Slowness:<BR>मन्थरता।<BR>III As of writings: दीर्घसूत्रता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teem
TEEM (v.): expr. with, प्रचुरः (रा, रं): v. To<BR>abound, abundant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teeth
TEETH (v.): expr. by दन्त and a verb उद्गच्छति<BR>(गम्, c. 1.), जायते (जन्, c. 4.), etc., T.ing<BR>i.e. dentition: दन्तोद्गमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tegument
TEGUMENT: वेष्टनम्, आ-, Bha.: v. Covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

telegram
TELEGRAM: *ताडिती वार्त्ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

telegraph
TELEGRAPH:<BR>I Subs.: *तडिद्वार्त्तावहः।<BR>II<BR>Verb.: *ताडितेन सन्दिशति (दिश्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teleology
TELEOLOGY: मीमांसा (?); हेतुविद्या (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

telescope
TELESCOPE: *दूरवीक्षणम्, -यन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tell
TELL (v.t.):<BR>(1) कथयति (कथ्, c. 10.),<BR>learnt<BR>without being told:<BR>अकथितशिक्षित (f. ता),<BR>K.;<BR>when I tell the history of (his) former<BR>life:<BR>जन्मान्तरवृत्तन्तं मयि कथयति, K.;<BR>that (my)<BR>internal wish is told by the eyes:<BR>यच्चक्षुषैव<BR> हृदयाभिलाष कथ्यते, K.;<BR>whom should I tell:<BR>कस्य<BR> कथयामि, K.;<BR>(2) आवेदयति (c. of विद् = inform,<BR>narrate),<BR>I will t. (you) everything from the<BR>beginning:<BR>आदितः प्रभृति सर्वं निवेदयिष्यामः, K.:<BR>v. To say, relate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tell
TELL (v. i.):<BR>I In good sense: expr. with<BR>गुणः (effect)<BR>or<BR>वलं (strength) दृश्यते।<BR>II In<BR>bad sense with on: दुर्बलीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teller
TELLER:<BR>(1) कथक (f. थिका);<BR>(2) कथयितृ (f.<BR>त्री);<BR>(3) आवेदक (f. दिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tell-tale
TELL-TALE: i.e. informer: सूचकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temerity
TEMERITY: साहसम्: v. Boldness, rashness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temper
TEMPER (v.):<BR>I To mix: q. v.: संमिश्रयति<BR>(मिश्र्, c. 10.).<BR>II To soften, mollify:<BR>स्निग्धी करोति।<BR>III Of steel, etc. मृदूकरोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temper
TEMPER (subs.):<BR>I Character, nature: q. v.:<BR>शीलम्। Ph.:<BR>bad t.ed:<BR>कोपन (f. ना): v.<BR>Irritable,<BR>II Due mixture: सम्भेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temperament
TEMPERAMENT: प्रकृतिः: v. Nature, character.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temperance
TEMPERANCE: perh. संयमः,<BR>t. in eating and<BR>drinking:<BR>पानाशनसंयमः (?);<BR>t. society:<BR>पान-<BR>संयमसभा (?): v. Moderation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temperate
TEMPERATE:<BR>I Moderate: q. v.: मित (f.<BR>ता).<BR>II Cool, calm: q. v.: शान्त (f. न्ता).<BR>III Continent: q. v.: संयत (f. ता), perh.:<BR>t. zone:<BR>*नातिशीतोष्णमण्डलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temperately
TEMPERATELY<BR>(1) मितम्;<BR>(2) शान्तम्;<BR>(3) संयतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temperature
TEMPERATURE: उष्णमानम् (?) धर्मपरिमाणम् (?)<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tempest
TEMPEST, TEMPESTUOUS: v. Storm, stormy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temple
TEMPLE (subs.):<BR>I A sacred building:<BR>(1)<BR>देवालयः and sim. comp.s,<BR>t. of Śiva:<BR>शिवायतनम्<BR>Vet. 20.;<BR>empty t.:<BR>शून्यं देवकुलम्, Mr. ii.; t.<BR>of the mistress of the world (Durgā): भुवनेश्वरी-<BR>देवतालयः, Bh.;<BR>t. of Viṣṇu:<BR>विष्णोर्निकेतनम्,<BR>Kaj.: v. House, edifice;<BR>(2) सिद्धायतनम्,<BR>t. of Śiva:<BR>शूलपाणेः सिद्धायतनम् K.;<BR>(3) मठः,<BR>P.;<BR>(4) विहारः (of Buddhas).<BR>II Of the<BR>head:<BR>(1) शङ्खः;<BR>(2) कुम्भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temporal
TEMPORAL:<BR>I Worldly: q. v.: सांसारिक (f.<BR>की).<BR>II Of the temple of the head: by<BR>comp.,<BR>t. region:<BR>कुम्भदेशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temporarily
TEMPORARILY:<BR>(1) स्वल्पकालम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temporary
TEMPORARY:<BR>(1) अचिरस्थायिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>स्वल्पकालिक (f. की); etc.: v. Also transient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temporize
TEMPORIZE:<BR>I To be a time-server: छन्दो-<BR>ऽनुरुणद्धि (रुध्, c. 7.)<BR>or<BR>अनुवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.).<BR>II To delay: q. v.: विलम्बते (लम्ब्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temporizer
TEMPORIZER:<BR>(1) छन्दोऽनुरोधिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>समयानुवर्तिन् (f. नी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tempt
TEMPT:<BR>I To allure, entice: q. v.: प्रलोभयति<BR>(c. of लुभ्).<BR>II To attempt, try: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temptation
TEMPTATION:<BR>(1) प्रलोभनम्;<BR>(2) विलोभनम्,<BR>who<BR>is not allured by other t. s:<BR>अहृतस्य विलोभनान्तरैः,<BR>R. viii. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tempter
TEMPTER:<BR>(1) प्रलोभक (f. भिका);<BR>(2) विलोभक<BR>(f. भिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ten
TEN: दशन् (mfn.),<BR>t.-armed:<BR>दशभुजः (जा, जं);<BR>twice t.:<BR>द्विदशाः;<BR>in t. ways:<BR>दशघा; t. times:<BR>दशकृत्वः, दशवारान्;<BR>in the t. quarters:<BR>दशसु दिक्षु<BR>R. viii. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tenable
TENABLE:<BR>(1) रक्षणीय (f. या);<BR>(2) by verb.:<BR>v. To keep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tenacious
TENACIOUS:<BR>I Pertinacious: q. v.: ग्राहिन्<BR>(f. णी).<BR>II Retentive: q. v.: धारणावत् (f.<BR>ती).<BR>III Glutinous: q. v.: श्यान (f. ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tenaciously
TENACIOUSLY: साग्रहम्: v. Persistently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tenacity
TENACITY:<BR>I Pertinacity: ग्राहः।<BR>II Reten-<BR>-tiveness: q. v.: धारणाशक्तिः।<BR>III Glutinous-<BR>-ness: श्यानता, -त्वम्, आ-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tenancy
TENANCY: भूम्यधिवासित्वम्<BR>or<BR>गृहाधिवासित्वम् (?),<BR>a right of t.:<BR>भूम्यधिवासाधिकारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tenant
TENANT (subs.): भूम्यधिवासिन् (f. नी) (?),<BR>t. of<BR>house:<BR>गृहाधिवासिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tenant
TENANT (v.):<BR>(1) अधिवसति (वस्, c. 1.=inha-<BR>-bit: q. v. ;<BR>(2) भाटयति (=hire: q. v. ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tenantry
TENANTRY: अधिवासिवर्गः and sim. comp.s (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tench
TENCH: मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tend
TEND:<BR>I To take care of:<BR>(1) चारयति (c.<BR>of चर्,: only of cattle, etc.),<BR>t. ing cattle at<BR>distance:<BR>चारयन्तो दूरे गाः, V. p. v. 9. 3.;<BR>(2)<BR>पालयति (पाल्, c. 10.: gen.),<BR>t.ing cattle:<BR>गाः<BR> पालयन्तौ v. p. v. 8. 1.<BR>II To conduce;<BR>(1) कल्पते, परि- (कॢप्, c. 1.),<BR>and tend to their<BR>protection:<BR>कल्पसे रक्षणाय, Sa. v. 8.;<BR>(2) उपपद्यते<BR>(पद्, c. 4.),<BR>t.s to my state:<BR>मद्भावायोपपद्यते,<BR>G. xiii. 18.<BR>III Direct, aim: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tendency
TENDENCY:<BR>(1) प्रवणता<BR>or<BR>प्रावण्यम्;<BR>(2) स्वभावः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tender
TENDER (adj.):<BR>I Soft, delicate: q. v.:<BR>सुकुमारः (रा, रं),<BR>delicate weapon:<BR>सुकुमारमस्त्रम्,<BR>K.;<BR>in this t. age:<BR>अस्मिन् सुकुमारवयसि। [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">Page704</a>]<BR>II Compassionate, kind: q. v.: t. sentiment:<BR>करुणो रसः, U.;<BR>the hearts of good men are always<BR>t.:<BR>करुणार्द्राणि सतां खलु भवन्ति सदा चेतांसि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tender
TENDER (v.): उपनयति (नी, c. 1.): v. To<BR>offer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tender
TENDER (subs.): उपन्यासः: v. Offer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tenderly
TENDERLY:<BR>I Softly: q. v.: स्निग्धम्।<BR>II<BR>Kindly: q. v.: करुणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tenderness
TENDERNESS:<BR>I Softness: q. v.: सौकुमार्यम्।<BR>II<BR>Kindness: q. v.: करुणा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tendinous
TENDINOUS: शिराल (f. ला): v. Sinewy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tendon
TENDON:<BR>(1) शिरा;<BR>(2) स्नायुः: v. Sinew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tendril
TENDRIL: तन्तुः (=thread).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tenement
TENEMENT:<BR>I In law: स्थावरम्।<BR>II A house:<BR>भवनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tenet
TENET: मतम्: v. Opinion, doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tenfold
TENFOLD: expr. by adj. दशगुण (f. णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tennis
TENNIS: क्रीडाविशेषः,<BR>t. ball:<BR>*विक्षेपकन्दुकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tenor
TENOR:<BR>I Lit.: भावः: v. Purport.<BR>II In<BR>music: मध्यमस्वरः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tense
TENSE (subs.): कालः (=time): v. Grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tense
TENSE (adj.): आतत (f. ता): v. Stretch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tension
TENSION:<BR>I Lit.: आततिः (?).<BR>II Severity,<BR>rigour: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tent
TENT (subs.):<BR>I Of canvas:<BR>(1) पटवेश्मन् (n.)<BR>and sim. comp.s,<BR>in the way the lord's stays<BR>were in t.s:<BR>पथि प्रभोर्निवासाः पटवेशमभिर्बभुः Si. xii.<BR>63.:<BR>(2) दूष्यम्, Si. xii. 65.<BR>II Roll of lint:<BR>perh. पट्टः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tentive
TENTIVE, -LY: expr. by circumlo.: v. To try.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tented
TENTED: expr. by comp.: v. Tent, to have,<BR>to cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tenth
TENTH:<BR>I Adj.: दशमः (मी, मं),<BR>t. (in descent)<BR>from Prajāpati:<BR>दशमः प्रजापतेः। Mah. i. 70. 1.;<BR>Hundred and t.:<BR>दशाधिकशततमः (मी, मं).<BR>II<BR>Subs.:<BR>(1) दशमः,<BR>a t. was collected by (her)<BR>lover:<BR>दशमकः संगृहीतः प्रियेण, Li. 24.;<BR>(2) दशमांशः;<BR>(3) दशांशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tenuity
TENUITY: तानवम्: v. Thinness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tepid
TEPID:<BR>(1) कवोष्ण, कदुष्ण,<BR>or<BR>कोष्ण (f. ष्णा);<BR>(2) ईषदुष्ण (f. ष्णा);<BR>(3) कुतपः (पा, पं: rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tepidness
TEPIDNESS:<BR>(1) कवोष्णता;<BR>(2) ईषदुष्णता; etc.: v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tergiversation
TERGIVERSATION: Evasion, prevarication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

term
TERM (subs.): Limit, end: q. v.: अवधिः।<BR>II A period of time:<BR>(1) कालावधिः;<BR>(2)<BR>not expr.;<BR>(3) अवधिः (absol.),<BR>or if you wait<BR>for a term:<BR>अथ चेदवधिः प्रतीक्ष्यते, Ki. ii. 16.<BR>III<BR>A word: q. v.:<BR>here the word paśu:<BR>अत्र पशुपदम्,<BR>Kav. viii.<BR>IV In plu. = agreement: q. v.:<BR>समयः,<BR>as t.s (have support) in justice:<BR>न्यायमवधय<BR> इव, Ki. xii. 17.<BR>V State of intercourse:<BR>भावः,<BR>good t.s:<BR>सद्भावः: v. Friendship;<BR>bad<BR>t s:<BR>असद्भावः। v. Enmity.<BR>VI In arith.:<BR>पदम्,<BR>seven t.s:<BR>सप्तपदम्, Li. 93.; first t.:<BR>वदनम्, आदिः Li. 100; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

term
TERM (v.): अभिधत्ते (धा, c. 3.): v. To call,<BR>name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

termagant
TERMAGANT: दुर्दान्तकलहप्रिय (f. या) and sim.<BR>comp.s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

terminal
TERMINAL:<BR>(1) अन्त्य (f. न्त्या): v. Last;<BR>(2)<BR>सीमा in comp.: v. Boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

terminate
TERMINATE:<BR>I Intrans.: expr. by subs.,<BR>t.ing syllable:<BR>अन्त्यवर्णः: v. To end.<BR>II<BR>Trans.: समापयति (c. of आप्): v. To finish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

termination
TERMINATION:<BR>(1) अन्तम्: v. End.;<BR>(2) अव-<BR>सानम्: v. Conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

terminology
TERMINOLOGY: परिभाषा, Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tern
TERN: जलकुक्कु टविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ternary
TERNARY:<BR>T. number:<BR>त्रिकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

terrace
TERRACE:<BR>I Balcony: अलिन्दः।<BR>II Roof:<BR>छदिः (m.).<BR>III Raised ground: perh. वप्र<BR>(mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

terraqueous
TERRAQUEOUS:<BR>(1) जलस्थलमयः (यी, यं);<BR>(2)<BR>जलस्थलात्मक (f. त्मिका); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

terrene
TERRENE, TERRESTRIAL:<BR>I Pertaining to<BR>earth:<BR>(1) by comp.,<BR>t. globe:<BR>भूगोलः;<BR>(2)<BR>पार्थिवः, (वी, वं);<BR>(3) भौमः (मी, मं).<BR>II Rela-<BR>-ting to this life:<BR>(1) ऐहिकः (की, कं);<BR>(2)<BR>सांसारिकः (की, कं);<BR>(3) लौकिकः (की, कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

terrible
TERRIBLE:<BR>(1) घोरः (रा, रं);<BR>(2) दारुण (f. णा),<BR>नि-: v. Frightful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

terribly
TERRIBLY:<BR>(1) बलवत्;<BR>(2) गाढम् (= deeply);<BR>(3) भृशम् (= exceedingly^1).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

terrier
TERRIER: कुक्कु रभेदः; *भौमिकश्वन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

terrific
TERRIFIC:<BR>(1) भीषण (f. णा);<BR>(2) भीमः (मा,<BR> मं): v. Also terrible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

terrify
TERRIFY: भीषयते (c. of भी): v. To frighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

territorial
TERRITORIAL: expr. by comp., t. boundaries:<BR>देशसीमा, R. xvi. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

territory
TERRITORY:<BR>(1) राष्ट्रम्: v. Kingdom;<BR>(2)<BR>देशः, प्र-: Country, province.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

terror
TERROR:<BR>I Great fear: q. v.: त्रासः, सं-, परि-।<BR>II Object of dread: त्रासकर (f. री) and<BR>sim. comp.s,<BR>a t. even to the sages:<BR>त्रासजनन-<BR>मपि तत्वविदाम्, Ki. xii. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

terse
TERSE:<BR>(1) लवु (f. also ध्वी), Si. ii. 23.;<BR>(2)<BR>लाघवान्वितः (ता, तं), Ki. xi. 38.;<BR>(3) संक्षिप्त<BR>(f. प्ता = brief, concise: q. v. ), Si. ii. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tersely
TERSELY: expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

terseness
TERSENESS: लाघवम्: v. Terse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tertian
TERTIAN: तृतीयकः, -ज्वरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tesselated
TESSELATED: विचित्र (f. त्रा: (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

test
TEST:<BR>I Verb.: परीक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To examine.<BR>II Subs.: परीक्षा: v. Exa-<BR>-mination.<BR>III Means of trial:<BR>(1) प्रमाणम्,<BR>you are the only t.:<BR>यूयमेव प्रमाणम्, Sa. v. 25.;<BR>(2) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

testament
TESTAMENT:<BR>I A will: *इच्छापत्रम।<BR>II Of<BR>the Bible: संहिता,<BR>old:<BR>प्राचीनसंहिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

testamentary
TESTAMENTARY: *इच्छापत्रविहित (f. ता) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

testator
TESTATOR, TESTATRIX: *इच्छापत्रकारिन् (f. णी)<BR>and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

testicle
TESTICLE: अण्डम्, -कोषः(शः);<BR>(2) मुष्कः;<BR>(3) वृषणः,<BR>t. s:<BR>वृषणौ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

testify
TESTIFY:<BR>I As a witness: साक्ष्यं ददाति (दा,<BR>c. 3.).<BR>II In gen.: ब्रवीति<BR>or<BR>ब्रूते (ब्रू, c. 2.).<BR>if one t.ies falsely:<BR>अथ चेदनृतं ब्रूयात्, Mit.: v.<BR>To tell, speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

testimonial
TESTIMONIAL: *प्रशंसापत्रम्, and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

testimony
TESTIMONY: साक्ष्यम्,<BR>a witness giving false t.:<BR>साक्षी<BR> साक्ष्यं मृषा ब्रुवन्, Mit.: v. Also evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tetanus
TETANUS: धनुष्टङ्कारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tether
TETHER:<BR>I Verb: बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.).<BR>II<BR>Subs.: बन्धनरज्जुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tetrad
TETRAD:<BR>(1) चतुष्टयम्;<BR>(2) चतुष्कम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tetrarch
TETRARCH: मण्डलेशः (?): v. Chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tetter
TETTER: दद्रुविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

text
TEXT:<BR>I Original writing: मूलम्,<BR>I shall not<BR>write any thing outside the t.:<BR>नामूलं लिख्यते किञ्चित्,<BR>M. n.<BR>II Of scripture:<BR>(1) वचनम्;<BR>(2)<BR>ॠच् (f. of the Rigveda).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

textile
TEXTILE:<BR>(1) तान्तव (f. वी);<BR>(2) तन्तुनिर्मित (f.<BR>ता), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

textual
TEXTUAL:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) मूलापेक्ष (f.<BR>क्षा) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

texture
TEXTURE:<BR>I Lit.: तान्तवम्।<BR>II Quality of<BR>threads: गुणः।<BR>III Arrangement: विन्यासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

than
THAN:<BR>(1) by abl.,<BR>the people of Mathurā are<BR>richer t. the people of Pātnā:<BR>माथुराः पाटलीपुत्रभ्य<BR> आढ्यतराः, S. k.;<BR>swifter t. the mind:<BR>मनसोऽप्या-<BR>शुतरम्, Ki. xiii. 22.;<BR>and the king who gave<BR>more t. was asked for:<BR>नृपोऽर्थिकामादधिकप्रदश्च, R.<BR>v. 31.;<BR>dearer to you t. I.:<BR>मत्तः प्रियतरस्तव, K.;<BR>(2) sometimes by comp.,<BR>more t. twenty<BR>times:<BR>अधिकविंशान् वारान्, Au.: v. Also more.<BR>N.B. In old books the ins. is often used for<BR>the<BR>abl.:<BR>कोऽन्वस्ति दुःखिततरो मया दुष्कृतकर्मणा,<BR>Ram. ii. 59. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thank
THANK: धन्यवादं करोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thankful
THANKFUL:<BR>(1) कृतज्ञ (f. ज्ञा);<BR>(2) कृतवेदिन्<BR>(f. नी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thankfully
THANKFULLY:<BR>(1) धन्यवादपुरःसरम्, and sim.<BR>comp.s (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thankfulness
THANKFULNESS:<BR>(1) धन्यवादः<BR>or<BR>धन्यवादिता (?):<BR>v. Gratitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thankless
THANKLESS:<BR>I Of men: अकृतज्ञ (f. ज्ञा): v.<BR>Ungrateful.<BR>II Of work. etc.: यः (या,<BR> यत्) न प्रशस्यते: v. To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thanklessly
THANKLESSLY: expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thanks
THANKS: धन्यवादः (?), thanksgiving: perh.<BR>स्तुतिपाठः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

that
THAT:<BR>I Demonstrative pronoun: तद्,<BR>t.<BR>object:<BR>सोऽर्थः, D. iii.;<BR>in t. season:<BR>तस्मिन्<BR> समये, R. xvi. 53.;<BR>narrated all t.:<BR>तत्सर्वमाचख्यौ,<BR>Mah.: v. Also this. Ph.: (a) t. is to say<BR>॥॥॥: इत्यर्थः, तस्य यूनोऽपि विषयवैराग्यादिगुणसम्पत्त्या<BR> ज्ञानतो वृद्धत्वमासीदित्यर्थः, M.n. (N. B. Use......:<BR>इति यावत्, when a full explanation is not<BR>given, मनीषिणो विदुषो दोषज्ञस्यैति यावत्, M. p.);<BR>(b) t. is not expr., by object t. is by sound<BR>etc. M.n.<BR>II Relative pronoun=who, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=706" target="_blank">Page706</a>]<BR>which: q. v.<BR>III Conjunction, introduc-<BR>-ing clauses or sentences as object of the<BR>preceding verb.:<BR>(1) expr. with इति,<BR>would<BR>think t. they adore him out of fear:<BR>मंस्यति<BR> भयादर्चन्ति मामिति, Mah. v. 88. 3. (note the<BR>use of direct speech);<BR>t. he might allow the<BR>race of Nimi......:<BR>दिश्यतां कुलमिदं निमेरिति, R.<BR>xi. 49.;<BR>we hear t. king has come to the Jana-<BR>sthāna:<BR>श्रूयते राजा जनस्थानमागत इति, U. iii. (N.B.<BR>Sometimes इति is understood as t. in<BR>English: “श्रूयते तौ महात्मानौ नरनारायणावुभौ । तपो<BR> घोरमनिर्देश्यं तप्येते गन्धमादने ॥”, Mah. v. 96.<BR>14.):<BR>(2) by acc. after trans. verbs,<BR>know-<BR>ing t. his end was born:<BR>जानन्नपि जातमन्तमात्मनः,<BR>Si. i. 67.;<BR>informed t. a golden shower had<BR>fallen from heaven:<BR>हिरण्मयीं वृष्टिं शशंसुः पतितां<BR> नमस्तः, R. v. 29.;<BR>(3) with यथा<BR>or<BR>यत्,<BR>Vaśisṭha said t. they would go and live in the<BR>hermitage of Vālmīki:<BR>वशिष्ठस्य वाचः ‘यथा वाल्मीकि-<BR>तपोवनं गत्वा तत्र वत्स्याम इति’, U. ii.;<BR>this is new<BR>rule t. one repents after killing an enemy:<BR>अयं<BR> नूतनो न्यायो यदरातिं हत्वा संतापः क्रीयते, H. ii. Ph.:<BR>granting t. expr. by: अस्तु, स्ताम्, सन्तु।<BR>IV<BR>Introducing reason etc.: (a) so t.: यथा॥।<BR> तथा, do so t. (he) hears from your messenger:<BR>यथा तव सन्देशहराच्छृणोति तथा विधीयताम्, R. iii. 66.;<BR>(b) in order t.: यथा ॥तथा: v. also for (II),<BR>to; (c) in t.= because: q. v. Ph.: oh<BR>that: expr. with कच्चित्: v. To wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thatch
THATCH:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) छदिः;<BR>(2) छादनम्;<BR>(3) पटलम्, A.<BR>II Verb.: (तृणादिना) छादयति,<BR> आ-, (c. of छद्),<BR>t.ed:<BR>तृणाच्छादित (f. ता) and<BR>sim. comp.s or simply तृण- in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thaw
THAW (v.):<BR>I Intrans.: द्रवति (दु, c. 1.):<BR>v. To melt.<BR>II Trans.: द्रवीकरोति।<BR>III<BR>Subs.: हिमस्रुतिः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

the
THE:<BR>I The definite article:<BR>(1) not<BR>expr.,<BR>I salute the parents of the world:<BR>जगतः<BR> पितरौ वन्दे, R. i. 1.;<BR>the kind said:<BR>राजोवाच,<BR>H.;<BR>in the house of Vasudeva:<BR>वसुदेवसद्मनि, Si.<BR>i. 1.;<BR>(2) by demonstrative pronouns,<BR>where shall I get the bird:<BR>क्व प्राप्यते स पतगः, N.<BR>xiii. 40.;<BR>the day is advanced:<BR>कठोरीभूतोऽयं<BR> दिवसः, U. ii.<BR>II Of distinction: by तद् or<BR>rarely अदस्, we are the Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa:<BR>आवां तौ रामलक्ष्मणौ, An v.;<BR>and you are the<BR>Lakṣmaṇa:<BR>त्वं पुनरसौ लक्ष्मणः, Vi. v.<BR>III<BR>With comp. adv.s:<BR>(1) with यथा यथा॥॥॥<BR> तथा तथा,<BR>the closer the sound of the drums came,<BR>the more excited the hostile army (became):<BR>उपागमद्यथा यथा पटहरवः समीपतां तथा तथा हृषित-<BR>वपुर्द्विषाञ्चमूः, Si. xvii. 43.; “रोमकूपनिवहं यथा यथा<BR> नैषधस्य दृगपात्तथा तथा चित्रमापदपतृष्णता न सा”, N.<BR>xviii. 124.;<BR>(2) with यावत् यावत्॥॥॥तावत्<BR> तावत्, M.n. Ph.:<BR>the more so:<BR>विशेषतः<BR>(= specially).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

theatre
THEATRE:<BR>(1) रङ्गः (both lit. and fig.): v.<BR>Stage;<BR>(2) नाट्यशाला and sim. comps. (the<BR>house);<BR>(3) रङ्गगतो जनः and sim. comp.s.<BR>(the people).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

theatrical
THEATRICAL:<BR>(1) expr. by comp., t. tutor:<BR>नाट्याचार्यः;<BR>(2) नाटकीय (f. या = dramatic),<BR>Si. ii. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

theism
THEISM: ईश्वरवादः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

theist
THEIST: ईश्वरवादिन् (f. नी) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

theme
THEME:<BR>(1) विषयः: v. Subject;<BR>(2) वस्तु: v.<BR>Thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

theft
THEFT:<BR>(1) चौर्यम्,<BR>to commit t. at night:<BR>रात्रौ<BR> चौर्यं करोति, M. ix. 276.; implements of t.:<BR>चौर्यसाधनम्, Mit.;<BR>(2) स्तेयम्,<BR>and (taking)<BR>grass for cattle is not t.:<BR>तृणञ्च गोभ्यो ग्रासार्थम्,<BR> अस्तेयम्, M. viii. 339.;<BR>(3) मोषः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

then
THEN:<BR>(1) तदा (of time, rarely of cause),<BR>when...t.:<BR>यदा॥।तदा, Ku. v. 18.;<BR>t. (he)<BR>knew:<BR>तदा विवेद, Ki. iii. 18.;<BR>(2) तदानीम् (of<BR>time),<BR>but t. by the narration of the story of her<BR>life:<BR>तदानीन्तु स्ववृत्तान्तकथनेन, K.;<BR>(3) ततः (of<BR>sequence and cause),<BR>t. when your Highness<BR>came away:<BR>ततः खल्वागते देवे, K.;<BR>what t.:<BR>ततः<BR> किम्, K.;<BR>first of all splendour, t. sound, t.<BR>dust:<BR>प्रतापोऽग्रे ततः शब्दः परागस्तदन्तरम्, R. iv.<BR>30.;<BR>if she does not vanish from my sight, t. I<BR>shall ask her all these:<BR>तद्यदि मे दर्शनपथान्नापयाति<BR> ततः॥।सर्वमेतदेनां पृच्छामि, K.; and t. (as a<BR>question): ततस्ततः, Mr. ii.;<BR>(4) अथ (of<BR>sequence at the head of a sentence), t. at [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">Page707</a>]<BR>the end of the song:<BR>अथ गीतावसाने, K.;<BR>(5)<BR>तर्हि, (of time and cause: rare),<BR>t. the world<BR>is learned:<BR>तर्हि पण्डितः संसारः, U. ii.; what t.:<BR>किं तर्हि, S. i. 2. 1.;<BR>(6) तत् (causal),<BR>t. how<BR>is the gentle Rāma now to be consoled:<BR>तत्<BR> कथमिदानीं रामभद्र आश्वासनीयः, U. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thence
THENCE: ततः and तस्मात् (in every sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thenceforth
THENCEFORTH, THENCEFORWARD:<BR>(1) ततः<BR> प्रभृति;<BR>(2) तदवधि; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

theologian
THEOLOGIAN:<BR>(1) परमार्थविद् (mfn.: (?);<BR>(2)<BR>ईश्वरविज्ञानविशारद (f. दा: (?); and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

theological
THEOLOGICAL: expr. by comp., t. subject:<BR>अध्यात्मविषयः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

theologically
THEOLOGICALLY: तत्वविद्यानुसारेण and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

theology
THEOLOGY:<BR>(1) परमार्थविद्या (?);<BR>(2) ईश्वरविज्ञानम्;<BR>(3) तत्त्वज्ञानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

theorem
THEOREM:<BR>(1) सम्पाद्यम् (?);<BR>(2) प्रमेयोपपाद्यम्,<BR>K.d.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

theoretical
THEORETICAL,-LY: expr. by comp. or<BR>circumlo.: v. Speculative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

theorize
THEORIZE (v.): perh. मतं कल्पयति, प्र-, उप-।<BR>(c. of कॢप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

theory
THEORY:<BR>I Doctrine: q. v.: मतम्।<BR>II As<BR>opposed to practice: विज्ञानम्।<BR>III Exposi-<BR>-tion: q. v.: विवृतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

theraputic
THERAPUTIC (adj.): शान्तिकरः (f. री), etc.: v.<BR>To cure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

theraputics
THERAPUTICS: भैषज्यविज्ञानम् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

there
THERE:<BR>(1) तत्र,<BR>of t.:<BR>तत्रत्य (f. त्या: rare);<BR>(2) अमुत्र (=yonder t.: rare), D. vi. N.B.<BR>Not expr. when used pleonastically,<BR>t. is a<BR>town called Valabhi in Saurāśṭra:<BR>अस्ति<BR> सौराष्ट्रेषु वलभी नाम नगरी, D. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thereabout
THEREABOUT, -S:<BR>I Of place: तत्र क्वचित्।<BR>II<BR>Of number: उप- in comp., ten men or t.:<BR>उपदशपुरुषाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thereafter
THEREAFTER: After that: ततः परम्।<BR>II = and<BR>then:<BR>(1) ततः;<BR>(2) तदनु;<BR>(3) तदनन्तरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thereat
THEREAT:<BR>(1) तत्र;<BR>(2) तस्मिन् (loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thereby
THEREBY:<BR>(1) तेन;<BR>(2) by येन (= by which),<BR>t. I will play with you:<BR>येन दीव्याम्यहं त्वया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

therefore
THEREFORE:<BR>(1) अतः (= for this),<BR>t. it is<BR>mere boldness to say...:<BR>अतः॥।इति वचनं साहस-<BR>मात्रम्, S. 4.;<BR>t. spirit:<BR>अतएव प्राणः, S. 23.;<BR>(2) तस्मात् (= from that),<BR>t.<BR>ब्रह्मणः<BR>is objective<BR>genitive:<BR>तस्माद् ब्रह्मण इति कर्मणि षष्ठी।;<BR>(3) ततः<BR>(=2).: v. Then;<BR>(4) तत् (=2: rare),<BR>t.<BR>here:<BR>तदिह, S. i. 2. 2.;<BR>(5) तेन (=2),<BR>as<BR>regards this women are t. better:<BR>तेनात्र वरमङ्गनाः,<BR>V. m. 74. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

therein
THEREIN: अत्र (=in this: q. v. )<BR>or<BR>तत्र (=in<BR>that: q. v. ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thereinto
THEREINTO: तत्र: v. That, into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thereof
THEREOF:<BR>(1) अस्य (=of this: q. v. )<BR>or<BR>तस्य<BR>(=of that: q. v. );<BR>(2) by comp., arising t.:<BR>ततस्तय (f. स्त्या), Ki. i. 27.;<BR>men t.:<BR>तत्रत्या:<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thereupon
THEREUPON: तत्र: v. Then.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

therewith
THEREWITH: तेन (=with that: q. v. ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thermometer
THERMOMETER: *तापमानम्, -यन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thesis
THESIS:<BR>I Proposition: प्रतिज्ञा।<BR>II Disserta-<BR>-tion: प्रबन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thick
THICK (adj.):<BR>I Dense: q. v.: घन (f. ना),<BR>t. black hair:<BR>घननीलशिरोरुहः, Ri. iv. 16.<BR>II<BR>Muddy, dirty: q. v.: कलुषित (f. ता).<BR>III<BR>Large (as a t. volume): q. v.: बृहत् (f. ती).<BR>IV Of voice: expr. by subs.,<BR>the voice<BR>becomes t.:<BR>स्वरोपघातो भवेत्, Sr. V. Dull:<BR>q. v.:<BR>IV In measurement: expr. with<BR>वेधः (=thickness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thick
THICK (subs.): मध्यम् (=middle): v. Also<BR>dense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thick
THICK, THICKLY (adv.):<BR>I Closely, densely:<BR>q. v.:expr. by comp.,<BR>t. sown:<BR>घनोप्त (f. प्ता);<BR>t. covered:<BR>सान्द्रावृत (f. ता); etc.<BR>II Qui-<BR>-ckly, uninterrupted: q. v.: निरन्तरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thicken
THICKEN:<BR>I Intrans.: घनीभवति, etc.<BR>II<BR>Trans.: घनीकरोति, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thicket
THICKET: गहनम्: v. Wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thick-headed
THICK-HEADED:<BR>(1) स्थूलधी (n. धि);<BR>(2) जड-<BR>बुद्धि (mfn.); and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thickness
THICKNESS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) घनता;<BR>(2) सान्द्रता;<BR>(3) better by adj.<BR>II In measurement:<BR>(1) वेध (= depth), Li.;<BR>(2) विस्तृतिः (= bre-<BR>-adth as of a heap of bricks), Li. 198.;<BR>(3) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">Page708</a>]<BR>पिण्डः (as of wood), Li. 203.<BR>III Of voice:<BR>(1) स्वरोपघातः;<BR>(2) स्वरभङ्गः; and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thick-set
THICK-SET:<BR>(1) संहत (f. ता): v. Compact;<BR>(2) निविड (f. डा): v. Dense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thick-skinned
THICK-SKINNED: Fig.:<BR>(1) कठिन (f. ना = call-<BR>-ous);<BR>(2) सहिष्णु (mfn. = forbearing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thief
THIEF:<BR>(1) चौरः, open t. ves such as merchants:<BR>प्रकाशचौरा वणिगादयः, Viv.;<BR>t. -catcher:<BR>चौरग्राहः,<BR>Kat.;<BR>(2) तस्करः,<BR>for putting down t.s:<BR>तस्कर-<BR>प्रतिषेधार्थम्, M. ix. 266.;<BR>(3) स्तेनः,<BR>who give food<BR>and lodging to t.ves:<BR>भक्तावकाशदातारः स्तेनानाम्,<BR>N. d.;<BR>(4) मोषः, -कः,<BR>seeing a t.:<BR>मोषाभिदर्शने,<BR>M. ix. 274.;<BR>(5) कुम्भिलः, -कः;<BR>(6) मलिम्लुचः;<BR>(7) पाटच्चरः। N.B. 5 to 7 are rare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thieve
THIEVE: स्तेनयति (स्तेन्, c. 10.): v. To steal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thievish
THIEVISH:<BR>I Lit.: by comp.,<BR>II Secret:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thievishness
THIEVISHNESS: चौर्यशीलता and sim. comp.s: v.<BR>Also secrecy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thigh
THIGH:<BR>(1) ऊरुः,<BR>t.s:<BR>ऊरू, Ve.;<BR>(2) सक्थि (n.),<BR>long-t.ed:<BR>दीर्घसवथ (f. वथा:) v. Gram. A. 11.<BR>and 56).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thimble
THIMBLE: perh. अङ्गुलित्रम्<BR>or<BR>-त्राणम् and sim.<BR>comp.s, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thin
THIN (adj.):<BR>(1) सूक्ष्म (f. क्ष्मा),<BR>t. oil:<BR>सूक्ष्मं<BR> तैलम्, Bha.: v. Fine.;<BR>(2) तनु (f. also न्वी),<BR>t. dress:<BR>तन्वंशुकम्, Ri. iv. 3.: v. Slender,<BR>lean, little;<BR>(3) विरल (f. ला: rare),<BR>having<BR>t. arrangement:<BR>विरलभक्ति (mfn.), R. v. 74.:<BR>v. Rare, scarce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thin
THIN (v.):<BR>(1) क्रशयति (nomi.=make slender);<BR>(2) विरलयति (nomi. = make less close).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thine
THINE: त्वदीयः (या, यं): v. Thy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thing
THING:<BR>(1) वस्तु (n.),<BR>sir, what t. is to be given<BR>to your preceptor:<BR>किं वस्तु विद्वन् गुरवे प्रदेयम्, R. v.<BR>18.;......<BR>why I have been confined or why I have<BR>been brought here, about these t.s my curiosity<BR>has not been removed:<BR>किमर्थं वाहं बद्धो बद्ध्वा वा<BR> किमर्थमिहानीत इत्यत्र वस्तुन्यहमनपगतकौतुक एव, K.;<BR>(2) द्रव्यम् (=material),<BR>he who injures, breaks<BR>or crushes t.s:<BR>क्षतं भङ्गावमर्दौ व कुर्याद्रव्येषु यो नरः,<BR>Kat.;<BR>(3) विषयः (=object: q. v. ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

think
THINK:<BR>(1) मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.),<BR>t.ing that title of<BR>lord only remains with you:<BR>मत्वा भवन्तं प्रभुशब्द-<BR>शेषम्, R. v. 22.; if you t. much of what I say:<BR>अस्माकमुक्तं बहुमन्यसे चेत्, B. iii. 53.: v. Consider,<BR>suppose;<BR>(2) चिन्तयति, वि-, सं-, परि-, अनु-<BR>(चिन्त्, c. 10. =reflect)<BR>he simply t.s of fears<BR>to come from you:<BR>स चिन्तयत्येव भियस्त्वदेष्यतीः,<BR>Ki. i. 23.;<BR>while I was thus t.ing:<BR>इत्येवं<BR> चिन्तयन्तम्, K.;<BR>(3) ध्यायति, अनु- (ध्यै, c. 1.=2.)<BR>t. of the child in womb:<BR>प्रजानिषेकमनुध्यायत, R.<BR>xiv. 60.;<BR>(4) स्मरति, अनु- (स्मृ, c. 1.=rem-<BR>-ember),<BR>to t. of heaven:<BR>दिवः स्मर्तुम्, Ki. v.<BR>28.;<BR>(5) अध्येति (इ, c. 2.=5), t. s only of me:<BR>मामेवाध्येति, Ki. xi. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thinker
THINKER:<BR>(1) सूरिः;<BR>(2) मुनिः (= sage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thinly
THINLY:<BR>(1) तनु: v. Slenderly;<BR>(2) विरलम्:<BR>v. Rarely;<BR>(3) by comp., t. populated:<BR>विरलजन<BR>or<BR>अल्पजन (f. ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thinness
THINNESS:<BR>(1) तनुता: v. Slenderness;<BR>(2)<BR>सूक्ष्मता: v. Fineness;<BR>(3) विरलता<BR>or<BR>वैरल्यम्<BR>(= scarcity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thin-skinned
THIN-SKINNED: Fig.: Sensitive: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

third
THIRD (adj.): तृतीयः (या, यं), in the t. place:<BR>तृतीयतः;<BR>for the t. time:<BR>तृतीयवारम्;<BR>there is no t.<BR>course:<BR>अन्या गतिर्नास्ति। Ph.: t. estate i. e. com-<BR>-monalty: प्रकृतयः (f. pl. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

third
THIRD (subs.):<BR>I A t. part:<BR>(1) तृतीयांशः;<BR>(2) तृतीयभागः;<BR>(3) त्रिमागः;<BR>(4) त्र्यंशः, two-t. s:<BR>द्वौ त्र्यंशौ, Li.;<BR>(5) त्रिलवः,<BR>two-t. s:<BR>त्रिलवद्वयम्,<BR>Li.<BR>II In music: गान्धारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thirdly
THIRDLY:<BR>(1) तृतीयतः;<BR>(2) तृतीयम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thirst
THIRST (subs.):<BR>(1) तृष्णा (lit. and fig.),<BR>t. for<BR>wealth:<BR>धनागमतृष्णा, J.;<BR>t., you are still not<BR>satisfied:<BR>तृष्णे नाद्यापि सन्तुष्यसि, J.;<BR>(2) पिपासा<BR>(lit.),<BR>to quench t.:<BR>पिपासां प्रतिकर्तुम्, D. viii.;<BR>to remove t.:<BR>पिपासामपनयति, D.; very great t.:<BR>अतिप्रबलपिपासा, K.;<BR>(3) उदन्या (=2: rare),<BR>quenching of t.:<BR>उदन्याप्रतीकारः, Ve. vi.;<BR>(4)<BR>तृष्<BR>or<BR>तृषा (=1: rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thirst
THIRST (v.i.):<BR>(1) तृष्यति (तृष्, c. 4.: lit. and<BR>fig.), Ki. xi. 74.;<BR>(2) उदन्यति (nomi.: lit.<BR>rare), B. iv. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thirsty
THIRSTY:<BR>(1) तृषितः (ता, तं),<BR>I am t.:<BR>तृषितोऽस्मि<BR>Ve. vi.;<BR>(2) तृषार्त: (र्ता, र्तं);<BR>(3) पिपासितः [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">Page709</a>]<BR>(ता, तं);<BR>(4) सतृष्णः (ष्णा, ष्णां);<BR>(5) पिपासु<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(6) तृष्णातुरः (रा, रं);<BR>(7) तृष्णाकुलः<BR>(ला, लं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thirteen
THIRTEEN: त्रयोदशन् (mfn.).<BR>T.-th:<BR>त्रयोदशः<BR>(शी, शं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thirtieth
THIRTIETH:<BR>(1) त्रिंशः (शा, शं);<BR>(2) त्रिशत्तमः<BR>(मी, मं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thirty
THIRTY: त्रिंशत् (f.),<BR>t.-fold:<BR>त्रिंशद्गुणः (णा, णं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

this
THIS:<BR>(1) by एतद्,<BR>who is t. Rāma:<BR>क एष रामः,<BR>Pra.;<BR>t. speech of Uddhava:<BR>औद्धवीं वाचमेनाम्,<BR>Si. ii. 118.;<BR>for t. I live:<BR>एतदर्थं हि जीवामि,<BR>Mah.;<BR>(2) by इदम्,<BR>through t. row of young<BR>plants:<BR>अनया बालपादपवीथ्या, Sa. iii.;<BR>t. way,<BR>gentlemen:<BR>इत इतो भवन्तः, Sa. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thistle
THISTLE: a plant: अऋगालपुच्छः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thither
THITHER: तत्र।<BR>T. wards:<BR>तं देशं प्रति and sim.<BR>expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thong
THONG:<BR>(1) वरत्रा;<BR>(2) वध्री;<BR>(3) चर्मरज्जुः, and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thorn
THORN:<BR>I A prickle: कण्टक (mn.).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>कण्टक (mn.),<BR>avoids heroes like t.s:<BR>शूरं कण्टक-<BR>भिव परिहरति, K.<BR>III A thorny plant: कण्ट-<BR>किन् (f. नी), -वृक्षः (or लता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thorn-apple
THORN-APPLE:<BR>I The tree: धुस्तु(स्तू)रः।<BR>II<BR>The fruit: धुस्तुरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thorny
THORNY:<BR>(1) कण्टकिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) कण्टकावृत<BR>(f. ता), and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thorough
THOROUGH:<BR>(1) सम्यक् (मीची), t. instruction:<BR>सम्यगविनयनम्, D. ii.;<BR>(2) सम्पूर्ण (f. र्णा = full,<BR>complete: q. v. ), Pr.; t. master:<BR>(1) पारग<BR>(f. गा);<BR>(2) पारदृश्वन् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thoroughbred
THOROUGHBRED:<BR>(1) आजानेय (f. यी);<BR>(2)<BR>महाकुलीन (f. ना); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thoroughfare
THOROUGHFARE: राजमार्गः: v. Street, road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thoroughly
THOROUGHLY:<BR>(1) सम्यक,<BR>after being t. instru-<BR>cted:<BR>सम्यग् विनीय, R. v. 10.;<BR>(2) आद्यन्तम्<BR>(= from beginning to end): v. Also fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thou
THOU:<BR>I Subs.: त्वम् (G. ch. xviii.).<BR>II<BR>Verb: त्वंकरोति,<BR>one should avoid t.ing and<BR>calling seniors by name:<BR>त्वङ्कारं नामधेयञ्च ज्येष्ठानां<BR> परिवर्जयेत्, Mah. xii. 193. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

though
THOUGH: -अपि: v. Although.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thought
THOUGHT:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) चिन्ता,<BR>with hun-<BR>dreds of t.s:<BR>चिन्ताशतैः, K.;<BR>(2) विचारः (=<BR>consideration);<BR>(3) ध्यानम् (=meditation).<BR>II Idea, notion: q. v.: मतम्।<BR>III = mind:<BR>q. v.: बुद्धिः,<BR>evil t.s:<BR>द्रोहबुद्धिः;<BR>she could not<BR>express her t.s:<BR>मनोगतं सा न शशाक शंसितुम्, Ku.<BR>v. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thoughtful
THOUGHTFUL:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) चिन्ताशील (f.<BR>ला);<BR>(2) चिन्तापरायण (f. णा), and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Attentive, careful: q. v.<BR>III<BR>Full of thought:<BR>चिन्ताकुल (f. ला), and sim.<BR>comp.s: v. Waking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thoughtfully
THOUGHTFULLY:<BR>(1) विचिन्त्य;<BR>(2) विचार्य;<BR>(3) विमृष्य।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thoughtfulness
THOUGHTFULNESS:<BR>(1) चिन्ताशीलता;<BR>(2) चिन्ता-<BR>कृलता; etc.: v. Adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thoughtless
THOUGHTLESS:<BR>I Lit.: निश्चिन्त (f. न्ता).<BR>II<BR>Careless: q. v.: प्रमत्त (f. त्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thoughtlessly
THOUGHTLESSLY:<BR>I Lit.: निश्चिन्तम्।<BR>II<BR>Carelessly: q. v.: अविमृष्य।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thousand
THOUSAND:<BR>(1) सहस्रम्,<BR>not less than four t.<BR>verses:<BR>अन्यूनचत्वारि श्लोकसहस्राणि, V. m. 107.<BR>11.;<BR>two t.:<BR>द्वे सहस्रे;<BR>ten t.:<BR>दश सहस्राणि;<BR>t. arms:<BR>दोष्णां सहस्रम्, Mah.;<BR>(2) दशशतम् (ती)<BR>(rare).<BR>T. times:<BR>सहस्रकृत्वः; t.s of times:<BR>सहस्रशः;<BR>in t. ways or parts:<BR>सहस्रधा; ten t.:<BR>अयुतम्;<BR>hundred t.:<BR>लक्षम्; the t.-eyed (Indra):<BR>सहस्राक्षः;<BR>the t.-armed (Arjuna):<BR>सहस्रबाहुः;<BR>the<BR>t.-rayed (sun):<BR>सहस्रांशुः; the t.-headed (sun):<BR>सहस्रशीर्षः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thousandth
THOUSANDTH:<BR>I Adj.: सहस्रतमः (मी, मं).<BR>II<BR>Subs.: सहस्रांशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrall
THRALL: दासः। v. Slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thraldom
THRALDOM or THRALDOM: दास्यम्: v.<BR>Slavery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrash
THRASH:<BR>I Lit.: निस्तुषीकरोति।<BR>II To beat<BR>soundly: परुषं प्रहरति (हृ, c. 1.),<BR>t. ing:<BR>परुष-<BR>प्रहारः and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thread
THREAD (subs.):<BR>(1) सूत्रम्,<BR>golden t.:<BR>सुवर्णसूत्रम्,<BR>Si.;<BR>(2) तन्तुः;<BR>t. of hope:<BR>आशातन्तुः, Ma.<BR>ix. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thread
THREAD (v.):<BR>I To string: q. v.: सूत्रयति।<BR>II To t. one's way: प्रसर्पति (सृप्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threadbare
THREADBARE:<BR>I Lit.: सूत्रदरिद्र (f. द्रा), Mr.<BR>ii. 7.<BR>II Fig.: शून्यगर्भ (f. र्भा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thready
THREADY:<BR>(1) सूत्रमय (f. यी);<BR>(2) तन्तुमय (f.<BR>यी);<BR>(3) तान्तव (f. वी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threat
THREAT:<BR>(1) विभीषिका, by various t. s:<BR>विभीषिकाभिर्बह्वीभिः Mah. ii. 41. 1.;<BR>(2) तर्जनम्<BR>or<BR>तर्जितम्, सं-।<BR>(3) मीषा, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threaten
THREATEN:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) तर्जयति, सं- (तर्ज्, c.<BR>10.),<BR>t. ed much against Dhanamitra:<BR>धनमित्र-<BR>मुल्लङ्घ्य बह्वतर्जयत्, D. ii.;<BR>t. ed them:<BR>तावतर्जयत्,<BR>R. xii. 41.;<BR>(2) भीषयति (c. of भी = frighten:<BR>q. v.).<BR>II Fig.: expr. by circumlo.:<BR>it t. s<BR>rain or t. ing weather:<BR>वृष्ट्याशंसि दिवसम्;<BR>weather<BR>is t. ing:<BR>प्रत्यासीदति भ्कञ्भ्क: v. To bespeak,<BR>impend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threateningly
THREATENINGLY: तर्जयत् (f. न्ती), सं-: v. To<BR>threaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

three
THREE: त्रि,<BR>by the t. states:<BR>तिसृभिरवस्थाभिः, Ku.;<BR>t. times:<BR>त्रिः;<BR>in t. ways:<BR>त्रिधा<BR>or<BR>त्रेधा;<BR>t. or<BR>four:<BR>त्रिचतुराः (n. pl. णि);<BR>interest at t.<BR>percent per mensem:<BR>त्रिकं शतं मासस्य वृद्धिः, M.<BR>viii. 143.;<BR>the t. Vedas:<BR>त्रयी;<BR>the t. objects<BR>of life (virtue, wealth and love):<BR>त्रिवर्गः;<BR>the t.<BR>spices (cinnamon, nutmeg, and cardamoms):<BR>त्रिजातकम्, D.;<BR>a heifer t. years old:<BR>त्रिहायणी;<BR>for t. nights:<BR>त्रिरात्रम्। त्रयम् is often affixed to<BR>express t.:<BR>t. years:<BR>वर्षत्रयम्। T. score: v.<BR>Sixty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

three-cornered
THREE-CORNERED:<BR>(1) त्रिकोणः(णा, णं);<BR>(2)<BR>त्र्यस्रः (स्रा, स्रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

three-eyed
THREE-EYED:<BR>(1) त्रिनयनः (ना, नं);<BR>(2) त्रिनेत्रः<BR>(त्रा, त्रं);<BR>(3) त्रिलोचनः (ना, नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threefold
THREEFOLD: त्रिगुणः (णा, णं): v. Also<BR>three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

three-footed
THREE-FOOTED:<BR>(1) त्रिपदः (दी, दं).<BR>(2) त्रिपादः<BR>(दा, दं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

three-headed
THREE-HEADED:<BR>(1) त्रिमूर्ध (f. र्धी) (the form<BR>त्रिमूर्धन् is also found);<BR>(2) त्रिशिरस् (mfn.);<BR>(3) त्रिशीर्षकः (का, का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

three hundred
THREE HUNDRED: त्रिशतम्,<BR>T. th:<BR>त्रिशतः (ती,<BR> तं)<BR>or<BR>त्रिशततमः (मी, मं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

three-leaved
THREE-LEAVED:<BR>(1) त्रिपत्रः (त्रा, त्रं);<BR>(2)<BR>त्रिपर्णः (र्णा, र्णं), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thresh
THRESH: मृद्राति<BR>or<BR>मर्दयति, सं-, परि-, (मृद्, c. 9.<BR>and 10.). Ph.:<BR>t. ing floor:<BR>खलः (ली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threshold
THRESHOLD:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) देहली;<BR>(2) द्वारपिण्डी;<BR>(3) गृहावग्रहणी;<BR>(4) उडुम्बरः (rare).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>प्रारम्भः: v. Beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrice
THRICE:<BR>(1) त्रिः;<BR>(2) त्रिवारम्। T. seven (i. e.<BR>twentyone)<BR>times:<BR>त्रिःसप्तकृत्वः; t. ploughed:<BR>त्रिगुणाकृतः (ता, तं)<BR>or<BR>त्रिहल्यः (ल्या, ल्यं),<BR>t. as<BR>long as that:<BR>तस्मात्त्रिगुणदीर्घः (र्घा, र्घं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrift
THRIFT:<BR>I Thriftiness: मितव्ययः, -यिताः v.<BR>Frugality.<BR>II Growth, increase: q. v.:<BR>(1) संवृद्धिः;<BR>(2) विवृद्धिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thriftily
THRIFTILY, THRIFTINESS: v. Frugally, fruga-<BR>-lity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrifty
THRIFTY: मितव्ययिन् (f. नी): v. Frugal,<BR>sparing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrill
THRILL:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) वेपथुः (= shivering);<BR>(2) रोमाञ्चः, and sim. comp.s (=horripila-<BR>-tion), a t. came over the bodies of the sages:<BR>मुनीनामङ्गानि रोमाञ्जं बिभराम्बभूवुः, Ki. xv. 53.<BR>II<BR>Verb: expr. by subs.<BR>T. ing:<BR>लो(रो)महर्षण<BR>(f. णा), Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrive
THRIVE: वर्द्धते (वृध्, c. 1.),<BR>t. ing:<BR>वर्धिष्णु, (mfn.),<BR>Si. v. 14.: v. Also prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throat
THROAT:<BR>(1) कण्ठः;<BR>(2) गलः: v. Neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throb
THROB:<BR>I Verb:<BR>(1) फुर्फुरायते (nomi.), Mr.<BR>1.;<BR>(2) दुरदुरायते (nomi.);<BR>(3) वेपते (वेप्, c.<BR>1.): v. To palpitate.<BR>II T. bing:<BR>(1)<BR>फुर्फुरायितम्;<BR>(2) दुरदुरायितम्;<BR>(3) वेपनम्<BR>(= quake).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throe
THROE: यातना: v. Pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throne
THRONE:<BR>I Lit.: सिंहासनम् and sim. comp.s,<BR>seated on t. s:<BR>सिंहासनस्थान्, R. vi. l.;<BR>ascended<BR>the paternal t.:<BR>भेजे पैतृकमासनम्, R. xvii. 28.<BR>II Fig.: छत्रम्,<BR>one who has lost his t.:<BR>छत्रभ्रष्ट<BR>(f. ष्टा), Mah.: v. Kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throng
THRONG:<BR>I Subs.: जनसंमर्दः and sim. comp.s:<BR>v. Crowd, multitude.<BR>II Verb: expr. by<BR>जनाकीर्ण (f. र्णा) and sim. adj.s: v. To<BR>crowd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throttle
THROTTLE (v.): गलं निष्पीड्यति (पीड्, c. 10.<BR>= press)<BR>or<BR>निष्पीड्य मारयति (=t. to death).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

through
THROUGH (prep.):<BR>I On account of: q. v.: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">Page711</a>]<BR>t. fear:<BR>भयात्: v. For.<BR>II By the agency<BR>of:<BR>(1) -मुखेन (= by the mouth of),<BR>I have<BR>asked his Majesty t. Nipuṇikā:<BR>मया निपुणिका-<BR>मुखेन याचितो महाराजः, Mal. iii.;<BR>(2) द्वारेण or<BR>द्वारा (from द्वार and -र् = door),<BR>I shall spread<BR>some snare t. her:<BR>तद्द्वारेण किञ्चिज्जालमारचेयम्, D.<BR>iii.<BR>III Throughout: q. v.<BR>IV With<BR>verbs of motion: by ins.,<BR>t. this row of young<BR>plants:<BR>अनया बालपादपवीथ्या, Sa. iii.;<BR>now<BR>passes t. the region of clouds:<BR>क्वचित्पथा सञ्चरते<BR> घनानाम्, R. xiii. 19.<BR>V From the other side<BR>of: -अन्तरेण,<BR>to listen t. a clink:<BR>छिद्रान्तरेणा-<BR>कर्णयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

through
THROUGH (adv.): expr. by adj. all: q. v.:<BR>to read a book t.:<BR>समग्रं ग्रन्थं पठति; to see t.:<BR>सर्वं पशयति; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throughout
THROUGHOUT (prep.):<BR>t. the town:<BR>सर्वत्र नगरे;<BR>t. the year:<BR>समस्ते वर्षे;<BR>t. one's life:<BR>आजन्मनः<BR>(= from birth);<BR>t. the world:<BR>यावत्संसारमण्डलम्:<BR>v. Also all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teroughout
TEROUGHOUT (adv.):<BR>(1) सर्वत्र (= everywhere),<BR>in this poem the metre t. is<BR>मन्दाक्रान्ता: अत्र काव्ये<BR> सर्वत्र मन्दाक्रान्तावृत्तम्, M. n. on Me.;<BR>(2) आद्यन्तम्<BR>(= from beginning to end);<BR>(3) अशेषतः<BR>(= entirely: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throw
THROW:<BR>(1) क्षिपति, threw a mace at the prince:<BR>राजपुत्राय चिक्षेप दण्डम्, M. p. 127. 18.;<BR>to t.<BR>(him) on the ground:<BR>क्षेप्तुकाममवनौ, Ki.;<BR>who has thrown her eyes on the bed:<BR>शयने<BR> निःक्षिप्ताक्षी, Gi. vii. 1.;<BR>(2) अस्यति (अस्, c.<BR>4.),<BR>threw a dirt on him:<BR>तस्मिन्नास्थदिषीकास्रम्,<BR>R. xii. 23.;<BR>(3) पातयति (c. of पत् = fell),<BR>t. ing of dice:<BR>अक्षपातनम्, Mah. ii. 59. 4.<BR>com.; श्रुतौ पातयति, V. iii. 13.<BR>(4) वपति (वप्,<BR>c. 1.: only of dice),<BR>t. ing dice:<BR>अक्षानुप्त्वा<BR>Mah.: v. Also to cast, discharge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throw about
THROW ABOUT:<BR>(1) विक्षिपति,<BR>as if t. ing about<BR>the light of the sun:<BR>प्रमां रवेर्विक्षिपन्निव, Ki. xvi.<BR>50.: v. To scatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throw around
THROW AROUND: परिक्षिपति: v. To encircle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throw away
THROW AWAY:<BR>I To spend, squander,<BR>waste: q. v.: क्षिपति, प्र-, निः-, वि-।<BR>II To<BR>reject: q. v.:<BR>(1) निरस्यति;<BR>(2) अपास्यति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throw down
THROW DOWN:<BR>(1) पातयति (c. of पत् = fell),<BR>seizes (him) by the hair and t. s (him) d.:<BR>केशेषु<BR> गृहीत्वा पातयति, Mr. vi.;<BR>(2) अधः क्षिपति, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throw in
THROW IN: v. To throw, put, give up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throw off
THROW OFF:<BR>I Lit.: क्षिपति, प्र-, निः-,<BR>t. ing off<BR>the collyrium of (her) eyes:<BR>अक्ष्णोर्निःक्षिपदञ्जनम्,<BR>Gi. xi. 11.: v. Throw.<BR>II To discard,<BR>drive out: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throw out
THROW OUT:<BR>I To reject, dispel: q. v.:<BR>निरस्यति।<BR>II To t. up: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throw together
THROW TOGETHER:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) संक्षिपति;<BR>(2) समस्यति।<BR>II To bring together: v.<BR>Together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throw up
THROW UP:<BR>(1) उत्क्षिपति, t. n up for a moment:<BR>क्षणोत्क्षिप्त, Si. i. 4.;<BR>(2) उदस्यति,<BR>t. ing up for-<BR>titude:<BR>उदस्य धैर्यम्, Ki. viii. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throw
THROW (subs.): क्षेपः, वि-, प्र-, निः- (the<BR>distance of),<BR>an arrow's throw:<BR>इषुविक्षेपः,<BR>Mah.;<BR>t. ing away of a moment:<BR>क्षणक्षेपः, Si.<BR>xii. i.;<BR>t. ing off:<BR>क्षेपणम्, V. p. v. 20. 54.;<BR>t. ing down:<BR>अवपातनम्, B. p. x. 44. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrower
THROWER:<BR>(1) क्षेप्तृ (f. प्त्री);<BR>(2) क्षेपक (f. पिका)<BR>: v. To throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrum
THRUM (subs.):<BR>(1) दशाः (f. pl.);<BR>(2) वर्तयः<BR>(f. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrush
THRUSH, THRUSTLE: पक्षिविशेषः; सारिका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrust
THRUST (v. t.): आविध्यति (व्यध्, c. 4.): v. To<BR>push. Comp.s (a)<BR>t. at:<BR>आविध्यति।: v. To<BR>attack; (b)<BR>t. away:<BR>निरस्यति (अस्, c. 4.)<BR>: v. To dispel; (c)<BR>t. in, into:<BR>निवेशयति, सं-<BR>(c. of विश्): v. To put, enter; (d) t. off:<BR>आविध्यति: v. To push; (e)<BR>t. on:<BR>प्रचोदयति<BR>(चुद्, c. 10.).: v. To impel, encourage;<BR>(f)<BR>t. out:<BR>अपसारयति (c. of सृ).: v. Drive<BR>out; (g)<BR>t. through:<BR>मिनत्ति (भिद्, c. 7.).: v.<BR>To pierce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrust
THRUST (subs.):<BR>I Blow, stroke: q. v.:<BR>आधातः।<BR>II With the fist: मुष्टिः।<BR>III A<BR>wound with a pointed instrument: भिन्नम्,<BR>Ni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thud
THUD: निर्घोषः: v. Loud noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thumb
THUMB (subs.):<BR>(1) अङ्गुष्ठः;<BR>(2) वृद्धाङ्गुलिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thumb
THUMB (v. t.): अङ्गुष्ठेन स्पृशति (स्पृश, c. 6.=to) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">Page712</a>]<BR>touch) etc. (Comp. न्युब्जाङ्गुष्ठेन तन्त्रीताडनम्,<BR>M. n. on Si. i. 9.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thumbscrew
THUMBSCREW: *अङ्गुष्ठमर्दनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thump
THUMP:<BR>I Verb: आहन्ति (हन्, c. 2.).: v.<BR>To strike.<BR>II Subs.: आघातः: v. To blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thunder
THUNDER (subs.):<BR>I The noise: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>मेघनिर्घोषः;<BR>(2) घनध्वनिः;<BR>(3) स्फूर्जथुः, वि।<BR>II<BR>Roar: q. v.: गर्जितम्।<BR>III T. -bolt: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thunder
THUNDER (v.): गर्जति, परि- (गर्ज्, c. 1.).: v.<BR>Roar.<BR>T. out:<BR>सगर्जितम् उद्गिरति (गॄ, c. 6.)<BR>: v. To utter, emit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thunderbolt
THUNDERBOLT:<BR>(1) वज्रम्, about to hurl t.:<BR>वज्रं मुमुक्षन्, R. ii. 42.;<BR>(2) कुलिशम्, t. -holder:<BR>कुलिशभृत् (m.), Ki. x. 16.;<BR>(3) अशनिः,<BR>struck<BR>with t.:<BR>अशनिहत (f. ता), K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thunderer
THUNDERER:<BR>I Lit.: स्तनयित्नुः: v. Roar.<BR>II<BR>Of gods:<BR>(1) वज्रिन् (m.);<BR>(2) वज्रपाणिः, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thunder-struck
THUNDER-STRUCK:<BR>(1) वज्राहतः (ता, तं);<BR>(2)<BR>अशनिताडितः (ता, तं) and sim. comp. s. N. B.<BR>In fig. sense, इव (= as if) is added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thursday
THURSDAY:<BR>(1) गुरुवारः;<BR>(2) बृहस्पतिवारः;<BR>(3)<BR>गुरुवासरः;<BR>(4) लक्ष्मीवासरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thus
THUS:<BR>(1) इत्थम्,<BR>the king first argued t.:<BR>इत्थं नृपः<BR> पूर्वमवालुलुचे, B. i. 23.;<BR>(2) एवम्,<BR>while the<BR>divine sage was talking t.:<BR>एवंवादिनि देवर्षौ, Ku.<BR>vi. 84.;<BR>(3) इति (to connect a quotation),<BR>R. viii. 75. Ph.:<BR>t. much:<BR>एतावत्: v. Much,<BR>so;<BR>t. far:<BR>एतावतीं भूमिम्, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thwack
THWACK: ताडयति (तड्, c. 10.): v. To strike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thwart
THWART (v.): मोघीकरोतिः v. To frustrate,<BR>defeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thyme
THYME: सुगन्धिगुल्मविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tiara
TIARA: मुकुटम्: v. Crown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tibia
TIBIA: जङ्घाया अग्रास्थि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tick
TICK:<BR>I An insect: यूकः।<BR>II Credit: q. v.<BR>III A covering: आस्तरणम्।<BR>IV A noise:<BR>perh. टीकितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tick
TICK (v.): perh. टीकते (टीक्, c. 1.).: v. Also<BR>to beat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ticket
TICKET:<BR>I Subs.: *त्रिकटम्; निदर्शनी: v. Also<BR>mark.<BR>II Verb: *त्रिकटयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tickle
TICKLE:<BR>I Lit.: perh. कुतकुतयति (nomi.),<BR>t. ing<BR>sensation:<BR>कुतकुतम्। (?).<BR>II Fig.: v. To excite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ticklish
TICKLISH: expr. with कुतकुतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tidal
TIDAL: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tide
TIDE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: वेला,<BR>the sea-t. flows on<BR>the day of the full moon:<BR>पूर्णिमादिने समुद्रवेला<BR> चरति, P. i. 12.;<BR>rising t.:<BR>वर्द्धमाना वेला, Raj.;<BR>the t. is coming on:<BR>वेलेयमागच्छति, Na.;<BR>spring-<BR>t.:<BR>पूर्णवेला (?).<BR>II Fig.: current, stream:<BR>q. v.: स्रोतस् (n.).<BR>III Time: q. v.: वेला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tide over
TIDE OVER (v.): तरति (तॄ, c. 1.).: v. To<BR>cross.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tidily
TIDILY, TIDINESS, TIDY: v. Neatly, neatness,<BR>neat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tiding
TIDING: वार्त्ता: v. News.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tie
TIE (v.): sometimes with up and down:<BR>(1)<BR>बघ्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.).: v. To bind, fasten;<BR>(2) योक्त्रयति (nomi.),<BR>t. d him up with the arms<BR>like a beast with a rope:<BR>एनं योक्त्रयामास बाहुभ्यां<BR> पशुं रसनया यथा, Mah. iii. 9. 61.: v. Also<BR>restrain, check, string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tie
TIE (subs.): बन्धः: v. Bond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tier
TIER: पंक्तिः: v. Row, line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tierce
TIERCE: in music: गान्धारः। (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tiger
TIGER: व्याघ्रः। Tigress: व्याघ्री।<BR>T. -skin:<BR>व्याघ्रचर्म,<BR>M. n.;<BR>a sheet of t. -skin:<BR>वैयाघ्रकोशः, Mah. iv.<BR>42. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tight
TIGHT:<BR>(1) अशिथिल (f. ला);<BR>(2) दृढ (f. ढा)<BR>: v. Firm. Ph.: with the very t. bark:<BR>अतिपिनद्धेन वल्कलेन, Sa. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tighten
TIGHTEN:<BR>I To make firm: द्रढयति (nomi.).<BR>II As reins: नियच्छति (यम्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>restrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tightly
TIGHTLY:<BR>(1) अशिथिलम्;<BR>(2) दृढम्: v.<BR>Firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tightness
TIGHTNESS:<BR>(1) अशैथिल्यम्;<BR>(2) दार्ढ्यम्: v.<BR>Firmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tile
TILE (subs.): *खप्परः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tile
TILE (v. t.): *खप्परैः छादयति (c. of छद्).<BR>T. d<BR>house:<BR>*खप्परगृहम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tiler
TILER (subs.): *खप्परिकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

till
TILL (prep.): v. Until.<BR>T. now:<BR>अद्यावधि;<BR>t. death:<BR>आ मृत्योः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

till
TILL (v. t.): कर्षति (कृष्, c. 1.): v. To culti-<BR>-vate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

till
TILL (subs.): i. e. money-box: *टङ्कपेटी; टङ्का-<BR>धारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tillage
TILLAGE:<BR>(1) कृषिः, -कर्मन् (n.);<BR>(2) कर्षणम्।<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tiller
TILLER: कृषक<BR>or<BR>कर्षक (f. षिका): v. Cultiva-<BR>-tor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tilt
TILT (subs.):<BR>I An awing: वितानम्।<BR>II A<BR>combat: v. Tournament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tilt
TILT (v.):<BR>I To incline: आवर्जयति (वृज्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR>II To practise<BR>t.:<BR>प्राशयुद्धमभ्यस्यति<BR>(अस्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

timber
TIMBER: काष्ठम्: v. Wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

timbrel
TIMBREL: डिण्डिमः: v. Drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

time
TIME (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) कालः, from t. to t.:<BR>काले काले, Me.;<BR>by this t.:<BR>इयता कालेन, D. iii.;<BR>in the course of t.:<BR>कालेन, Ve. iii.<BR>or<BR>कालक्रमेण,<BR>Ku.<BR>or<BR>गच्छति काले, K.;<BR>t. should not be thrown<BR>away:<BR>न कालः परिक्षेप्तव्यः, Vi. ii.;<BR>without los-<BR>ing any t.:<BR>विहाय कालहरणम्, Vi. iv.;<BR>I will not<BR>waste my t.:<BR>न कालं हास्यामि, Sa. iii.; for a<BR>long t. (= for some hours): महान्तं कालम्, K.;<BR>after a long t.: (= after many years): बहोः<BR> कालात्, U. ii.;<BR>of the same t.:<BR>समकालीनः<BR>(ना, नं);<BR>(2) समयः (= definite t.), by this t.:<BR>अनेन समयेन, K.;<BR>at the wrong t.:<BR>असमये, Sa. i.;<BR>at the right t.:<BR>समये, R. iii. 13. Ph.:<BR>pleasant<BR>for the t. being:<BR>आपातरम्यः (म्या, म्यं), Ki. xi.<BR>12. (note the position of आपात);<BR>in a short<BR>t.:<BR>अचिरेण; in the mean t. (=meanwhile:<BR>q. v.);<BR>at the t. when:<BR>यदा॥।तदा, Ku.;<BR>at the<BR>same t.:<BR>समम्<BR>or<BR>एकावसरम्;<BR>at another^1 t., at<BR>other t. s:<BR>अन्यदा, R.; at t. s: v. Sometimes;<BR>at that t.: v. Then; at this t.: v. Now;<BR>at<BR>any t.:<BR>यदा, तदा; of the present t., of our t.:<BR>इदानीन्तनः (नी, नं);<BR>of that time:<BR>तदानीन्तनः<BR>(नी, नं);<BR>hard t.s:<BR>आपत्कालः; five t. s, six t. s,<BR>etc.: पञ्चकृत्वः, षट्कृत्वः etc.;<BR>many t. s:<BR>बहुशः।<BR>II Time of the day: वेला,<BR>ascertain what is<BR>the t.:<BR>ज्ञायतां का वेला वर्तत इति, Mu. iv.;<BR>dinner<BR>t.:<BR>मोजनवेला, P. iii.: v. Musical measure:<BR>(1) लयः,<BR>in t. mean, slow and quick:<BR>मध्य-<BR>विलम्बितलये दुतलये च, D. vi.; her steps keeping t.:<BR>पदन्यासो लयमुपगतः;<BR>(2) तालः (= beating t.).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

time
TIME (v.): expr. by circumlo.: v. Time,<BR>regulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

timeliness
TIMELINESS:<BR>(1) सामयिकता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2) better<BR>by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

timely
TIMELY (adj.):<BR>(1) by comp., by t. showers:<BR>समयवर्षितया, R. ix. 3.;<BR>(2) सामयिक (f. की),<BR>un-t. agitation:<BR>असामयिकक्षोभः, Ki. ii. 40.;<BR>(3) यथासमय (f. या) and sim. comp.s.,<BR>t.<BR>risers:<BR>यथाकालप्रबोधिनः, R. i. 6.;<BR>(4) कालिक<BR>(f. कालिकी: rare),<BR>un-t. flow:<BR>आकालिकी<BR> प्रवृत्तिः, Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

timely
TIMELY (adv.):<BR>(1) काले;<BR>(2) यथाकालम्;<BR>(3)<BR>यथासमयम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

timepiece
TIMEPIECE: कालांशमानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

time-server
TIME-SERVER: perh. कालानुवर्तिन् (f. नी), समयानु-<BR>रोधिन् (f. नी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

timid
TIMID:<BR>(1) त्रस्नु (mfn.);<BR>(2) भीरु (f. also रू);<BR>(3) कातर (f. रा): v. Also fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

timidity
TIMIDITY:<BR>(1) साध्वसम्: v. Fear;<BR>(2) कातर्यम्;<BR>(3) भीरुता, -त्वम्;<BR>(4) त्रस्नुता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

timidly
TIMIDLY:<BR>(1) by adj.;<BR>(2) समयम्: v. Fearfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

timorous
TIMOROUS, TIMOROUSLY, TIMOROUSNESS: v.<BR>Fearful, -ly, -ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tin
TIN:<BR>(1) रङ्गम्;<BR>(2) वङ्गम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tincture
TINCTURE:<BR>I Of colour, etc.: आभा।<BR>II An<BR>extract: लेपः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tincture
TINCTURE (v.): expr. with आभा<BR>or<BR>छाया।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tinder
TINDER:<BR>(1) इन्धनम्;<BR>(2) एधस् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tinge
TINGE:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) आभा;<BR>(2) छाया।<BR>II<BR>Verb: रञ्जयति (रञ्ज्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tingle
TINGLE: रणरणायते (nomi.) (?),<BR>t. ing:<BR>रणरणः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tinker
TINKER: कांस्यकार (f. री = brazier).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tinkle
TINKLE:<BR>(1) क्वणति (क्वण्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) शिंक्ते<BR>(शिञ्ज्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tinkling
TINKLING (subs.):<BR>(1) क्वणितम्;<BR>(2) शिञ्जतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tinman
TINMAN:<BR>(1) वङ्गकार (f. री);<BR>(2) रङ्गकार (f. री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tindel
TINDEL: perh. रङ्ग (f. ङ्गी: both lit. and fig.:<BR>comp. रांता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tint
TINT: v. Tinge, colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tiny
TINY: क्षुद्र (f. द्रा): v. Small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tip
TIP (subs.):<BR>(1) अग्रम्,<BR>t. of the nose:<BR>नासाग्रम्,<BR>J.;<BR>(2) शिखरम् (rare), having a whetted t.:<BR>निशितशिखर (f. रा), C. vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tip
TIP (v.):<BR>I Lit.: expr. by subs.,<BR>t.ped with<BR>gold:<BR>सुवर्णाग्र (f. ग्रा): v. To put.<BR>II To<BR>top.: q. v.<BR>III Tip up, incline: आवर्जयति<BR>(वृज्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tippet
TIPPET:<BR>(1) ग्रैवेयम्, -कम् (?);<BR>(2) ग्रीवावारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tipple
TIPPLE: अतिपानं करोति: v. To drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tippler
TIPPLER: अतिपायिन् (f. नी): v. Drunkard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tipsily
TIPSILY: expr. by adj.,<BR>as if t.:<BR>क्षीव इव, Ki.<BR>xvi. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tipsy
TIPSY: क्षीव (f. वा): v. Drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tiptoe
TIPTOE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पादाग्रम्;<BR>(2) प्रपदम्।<BR>II<BR>Fig.:<BR>t. mirth:<BR>आपादमस्तकं हर्षः;<BR>t. of expec-<BR>tation:<BR>आनखान्ता आशा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tirade
TIRADE: अधिक्षेपः: v. Declamation, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tire
TIRE (subs.): Head-dress: उष्णीषम्।<BR>II For<BR>wheels: लोहवलयः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tire
TIRE (v. t.): खेदयति (c. of खिद्): v. To<BR>fatigue.<BR>To be t. d:<BR>परिश्राम्यति (श्रम्, c. 4.);<BR>you are also t.d:<BR>यूयमपि परिश्रान्ताः, Sa. i.: v.<BR>Fatigued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tiresome
TIRESOME:<BR>(1) खेदकरः (री, रं), if it is not very t.:<BR>तद्यदि नातिखेदकरम्, K.;<BR>(2) क्लमजनन (f. नी);<BR>(3) श्रमकर (f. री);<BR>(4) आयासक (f. सिका);<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tiro
TIRO: v. Novice, unskilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tissue
TISSUE:<BR>I Brocade: q. v.<BR>II Of the body:<BR>fibrous t.:<BR>जालम् (?), Sr.<BR>III Succession,<BR>series: प्रबन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

titan
TITAN:<BR>(1) दैत्यः;<BR>(2) दानवः;<BR>(3) असुरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tithe
TITHE:<BR>(1) दशांशः;<BR>(2) दशमांशः;<BR>(3) दशमभागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

titillate
TITILLATE, TITILLATION: v. Tickle, tickling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

title
TITLE:<BR>I Name, appellation: q. v.: नामन्<BR>(n.),<BR>t. page:<BR>*नामपत्रम्।<BR>II Right: q. v.:<BR>(1) अधिकारः;<BR>(2) आगमः, Mi.<BR>III Rank:<BR>q. v.: उपाधिः।<BR>IV Inscription: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

title-deed
TITLE-DEED:<BR>(1) आगमः, -पत्रम्;<BR>(2) पट्टोलिका<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

titter
TITTER: v. Laugh, ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

title
TITLE: लेशः: v. Iota.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tittle-tattle
TITTLE-TATTLE: विजल्पितम्: v. Babble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

titular
TITULAR:<BR>(1) नाममात्र (f. त्रा);<BR>(2) by adv.:<BR>नाम्नैव: v. Name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

to
TO:<BR>I With verbs of motion: by acc.,<BR>I<BR>was taken to the edifice of the princess:<BR>नीतोऽहं<BR> कन्यकानिकेतनम्, D. vii. (G. § 162-3).<BR>II<BR>Expressing indirect object: by dat.,<BR>shew-<BR>ing to the queen:<BR>दर्शयन् पत्न्यै, R. (G. § 180.).<BR>III With inf.: by inf.,<BR>I have come to impart<BR>the knowledge:<BR>विद्यां दातुमुपागतोऽस्भि, Ki. v. 23.<BR>(G. § 279-83).<BR>IV With special verb: q. v.<BR>V. In comparison to: by gen.,<BR>who are<BR>other archers to me:<BR>के मम धन्विनोऽन्ये, Ku. iii.<BR>10. (G. § 211, 209),<BR>VI Of direction:<BR>to<BR>the north-west of Kailāsa:<BR>कैलासात् पश्चिमोदीच्याम्,<BR>Mat.:<BR>to the north of Nishadha:<BR>निषधस्योत्तरेण,<BR>Mah. (G. § 207, 196).<BR>VII=towards: q. v.<BR>VIII=up to: q. v.: आ with abl. or in comp.,<BR>to the coast of the four oceans:<BR>आ पारेभ्यश्चतुर्णा-<BR>मम्भोधीनाम्, Mu. iii. 24.<BR>IX Expressing<BR>number: expr. by comp.,<BR>to the number<BR>of five hundred:<BR>पञ्चशतसंख्यक (f. का).<BR>X<BR>In other senses;<BR>hand to hand:<BR>हस्ताहस्ति;<BR>to one's face:<BR>सम्मुखे;<BR>“to his ruin”:<BR>स्वनाशाय;<BR>“she to his image was made”:<BR>सा तदनुरूपा कृता;<BR>“I have a king here to my flatterer”:<BR>अयं राजा<BR> मम स्तावकभूमौ वर्तते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toad
TOAD: मण्डूकः: v. Frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toadstool
TOADSTOOL: a plant: छत्रविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

today
TODAY: चाटुशील (f. ला): v. Sycophant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toast
TOAST:<BR>I Subs.: भृष्टं रोटिखण्डम्।<BR>II Verb.:<BR>भृज्जति (भ्रस्ज्, c. 6.): v. To fry. Ph.:<BR>to<BR>drink a t.:<BR>*जलपानं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tobacco
TOBACCO: ताम्रकूटः<BR>or<BR>-कुट्टः, -कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tobacconist
TOBACCONIST: ताम्रकुट्टविक्रयिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

today
TODAY: अद्य,<BR>of t.:<BR>अद्यतनः (नी, नं), तल्लिख्यता-<BR>मद्यतनो दिवसः। P.: v. Also now.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

today
TODAY:<BR>(1) ताडिः(डी);<BR>(2) ताली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toe
TOE:<BR>(1) अङ्गुलिः, -ली (when the sense is clear),<BR>R. vi. 15.;<BR>(2) पादाङ्गुलिः, -ली and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR>The great t.:<BR>पादाङ्गुष्ठः or sim. अङ्गुष्ठः,<BR>(when the sense is clear). Ph.:<BR>from top<BR>to t.:<BR>आ केशाग्रादा नखान्तात्, At.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

together
TOGETHER:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) एकत्र,<BR>these families<BR>t. number fourteen:<BR>एतान्येकत्र चतुर्दशकुलानि, K.;<BR>all excellences do not live t.:<BR>न वसन्त्येकत्र सर्वेगुणाः, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">Page715</a>]<BR>Vi. i. 33.;<BR>(2) सह, gen. in comp. (= co-),<BR>coming out t.:<BR>सहैव निर्यती, Ki. xiv. 56.;<BR>living t.:<BR>सहवसतिः, Sa. ii. 3.;<BR>(3) समम्<BR>(rare),<BR>flew t.:<BR>समं समुत्पेतुः, Ki. xiv. 45.<BR>II<BR>With verbs.: सम् in comp.,<BR>mix t.:<BR>संमिश्रयति;<BR>live t.:<BR>संवसति, etc.<BR>III T. with: सह<BR>(rarely साकम्, समम्<BR>or<BR>सार्धम् with ins.): v.<BR>With.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toil
TOIL (subs.):<BR>I Labour:<BR>(1) परिश्रमः,<BR>the t.<BR>of going to a hermitage:<BR>तपोवनगमनपरिश्रमः, Sa.<BR>1.;<BR>(2) क्लेशः,<BR>t. when fruitful is no t.:<BR>सफलः<BR> क्ले शो न क्ले शः, M.n. on Ku. v. 36.;<BR>(3) आयासः:<BR>v. Fatigue.<BR>II A net: q. v.: जालम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toil
TOIL (v.): परिश्रमं<BR>or<BR>क्लेशं करोति: v. To<BR>labour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toilet
TOILET: भूषा, वि-, Ki. ix. 1.: v. Dress, orna-<BR>-ment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toilsome
TOILSOME:<BR>(1) कष्टकर (f. री);<BR>(2) कष्टसाव्य<BR>(f. ध्या);<BR>(3) क्लेशकर (f. री), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

token
TOKEN: चिह्नम्: v. Mark, sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tolerable
TOLERABLE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) सह्य (f. ह्या);<BR>(2)<BR>सहनीय (f. या);<BR>(3) सोढव्य (f. व्या).<BR>II<BR>Moderately good: perh. नातिमन्द (f. न्दा:<BR>comp. Bengali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tolerably
TOLERABLY:<BR>t. good or clever:<BR>नातिमन्द (f. न्दा);<BR>t. cold:<BR>नातिग्रीष्म (f. ष्मा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tolerance
TOLERANCE: v. Toleration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tolerant
TOLERANT: expr. by verb.: v. To tolerate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tolerate
TOLERATE:<BR>(1) सहते (सह्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>bear;<BR>(2) क्षमते (क्षम्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toleration
TOLERATION:<BR>(1) क्षमा;<BR>(2) तितिक्षा: v. For-<BR>-giveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toll
TOLL (v.): धीरं वादयति: v. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toll
TOLL (subs.):<BR>(1) शुल्क (mn.), t.-collector:<BR>शौल्किकः;<BR>(2) करः (=tax).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toll-booth
TOLL-BOOTH:<BR>I Lit.: शुल्कस्थानम् and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II Prison: कारा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tomato
TOMATO: विजातीय-<BR>or<BR>विलातीय-हिण्डरिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tomb
TOMB: समाधिः।<BR>T.-stone:<BR>समाधिफलकम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tomorrow
TOMORROW:<BR>(1) श्वः,<BR>day after t.:<BR>परश्वः:<BR>t.<BR>morning:<BR>श्वः प्रभाते, Ram.;<BR>of t.:<BR>श्वस्तनः (नी,<BR> नं)<BR>or<BR>श्वस्त्य (f. स्त्या);<BR>(2) कल्यम् (also =<BR>yesterday).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tomtom
TOMTOM:<BR>I A drum: q. v.: डिण्डिमः।<BR>II A<BR>cart: यानविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ton
TON: मानविशेषः, expr. with भणः (about 80 lbs.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tone
TONE (subs.):<BR>I Voice: q. v.: स्वरः।<BR>II<BR>Manner:<BR>(1) भावः;<BR>(2) चेष्टा<BR>or<BR>चेष्टितम्, D.<BR>viii.<BR>III In music: स्वरम्,<BR>quarter t.:<BR>श्रुतिः,<BR>Si. xi. 1.<BR>IV Of the body: बलम्: v.<BR>Strength.<BR>V In painting: औज्ज्वल्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tongs
TONGS:<BR>(1) संदशकः;<BR>(2) कङ्कमुखः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tongue
TONGUE:<BR>I Lit.: जिह्वा, I cannot hold my t.:<BR>न शक्नोम्यात्मनो जिह्वां धारयितुम्,<BR>V ii.:<BR>I cannot<BR>keep my t.:<BR>जिह्वां रक्षितुं न शक्नोमि, V. ii.; I have<BR>controlled (my)<BR>t. in such a way:<BR>एवं मया जिह्वा<BR> संयन्त्रिता,<BR>V ii.;<BR>(2) रश(स)ना,<BR>the Vedas were<BR>on the tip of his t.:<BR>तस्य किल छन्दांसि रसनाग्रे,<BR>D. vii.<BR>II Speech, language: q. v.: वाच्,<BR>in human t.:<BR>मनुस्यवाचा, R. ii. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tonic
TONIC (adj. and subs.):<BR>(1) सर्वदोषहरः (री, रं)<BR>(=remover of all disorder of the system),<BR>Sr.;<BR>(2) मेधाग्निबलवर्धनः (नी, नं) (=improving<BR>memory, appetite, and strength), Sr.;<BR>(4) बल्य (f. ल्या = strengthening), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

to-night
TO-NIGHT: अद्य रात्रौ, निशि, नक्तं<BR>or<BR>रजन्याम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tonnage
TONNAGE: expr. with भारः (=weight, bur-<BR>-den: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tonsil
TONSIL: कण्ठस्नोतस (?), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

too
TOO:<BR>I Also: q. v.: अपि,<BR>he t.:<BR>सोऽपि।<BR>II<BR>Very: अति-<BR>or<BR>सु- in comp. t. long (of time):<BR>सुचिरम्, K.; t. long (of direction): सुदीर्घ (f.<BR>र्घा), C.;<BR>t. great a load:<BR>अतिभारः, H.: v.<BR>Also excessively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tool
TOOL:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) उपकरणम्,<BR>t. and apparatus<BR>of artisans:<BR>शिल्पिनां द्रव्योपकरणम्, Mah. ii. 5.<BR>128.; t. s by which he earns his livelihood:<BR>यद् यद् यस्योपकरणं तेन जीवन्ति जीविकाम्, N. s.<BR>II<BR>Fig.:<BR>he is a mere t. in his hands:<BR>स तेन यन्त्र-<BR>वच्चाल्यते।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tooth
TOOTH:<BR>(1) दन्तः,<BR>“skin of t.:<BR>दन्तवेष्टः”, Sr.;<BR>white t. ed:<BR>शुभ्रदन्त (f. न्ती). Ph.: t.-powder:<BR>दन्तशोधनचूर्णम्, Sr.;<BR>t. picker:<BR>दन्तस्य निर्घर्षणकम्,<BR>H.; ii.;<BR>having fine teeth:<BR>सुदत् (f. ती), R.;<BR>(2) दशन (mn.),<BR>marks of teeth:<BR>दशनचिह्नम्, Si.;<BR>(3) रदः (rare),<BR>row of teeth:<BR>रदावली, Ku. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">Page716</a>]<BR>xvii. 43. Ph.: on the teeth of: i. e. in spite<BR>of: expr. with gen. or loc.:<BR>on the teeth of<BR>the Vedas:<BR>वेदेषु जागरूकेषु, D. s.;<BR>in the teeth of<BR>us:<BR>मिषतां नः, Ku. ii. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tooth-brush
TOOTH-BRUSH:<BR>(1) कुर्चकम्<BR>or<BR>दन्तधावनकुर्चकम्,<BR>Sr.;<BR>(2) दन्तपावनम्, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toothless
TOOTHLESS:<BR>(1) दन्तहीन (f. ना);<BR>(2) वीतदन्त<BR>(f. न्ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toothsome
TOOTHSOME: स्वादु (f. also द्वी): v. Palatable,<BR>tasty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

top
TOP (subs.):<BR>I Tip, peak: q. v.: अग्रम्;<BR>(2) शिखरम्,<BR>from the top of a tree:<BR>तरुशिखरात्,<BR>K.<BR>II<BR>A playing t.:<BR>भ्रमरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

top
TOP (adj.):<BR>(1) अग्र- in comp.,<BR>in the t.-most<BR>summit:<BR>अग्रसानुषु, Ki. ix. 7.: v. First;<BR>(2)<BR>मुख्य (f. ख्या): v. Chief;<BR>(3) श्रेष्ठ (f. ष्ठा);<BR>: v. Superior, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

top
TOP (v.):<BR>I Lit.: v. Top (subs.), to cover,<BR>put. Ph.:<BR>t.ed with white clouds:<BR>श्वेतमेघकृतशीर्ष<BR>(f. र्षा।), Mat. 116. 5.<BR>II Overcome, sur-<BR>-pass: q. v.: अतिक्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

topaz
TOPAZ:<BR>(1) पुष्परागः;<BR>(2) पीतसारः;<BR>(3) पीतामन्<BR>(m.) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tope
TOPE:<BR>I Buddhist: स्तूपः।<BR>II Of trees:<BR>(1)<BR>स्तूपः;<BR>(2) फ्काटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

topic
TOPIC: विषयः: v. Subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

top-knot
TOP-KNOT: चूडा: v. Crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

topography
TOPOGRAPHY: संस्थानवर्णनम्, -ना (?) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

topple
TOPPLE: पतति (पत्, c. 1.): v. To fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

topsyturvy
TOPSYTURVY:<BR>(1) अस्तव्यस्त (f. स्ता);<BR>(2)<BR>विपर्यस्त (f. स्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

torch
TORCH:<BR>(1) उल्का,<BR>moved about with t. es in their<BR>hands:<BR>उल्काहस्तौ विचेरतुः, Ram. vi. 53. 7.;<BR>with hundreds of lighted t.es:<BR>उल्काशतैः प्रज्वलितैः,<BR>Mah.;<BR>(2) उल्मुकम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

torment
TORMENT (v.):<BR>(1) खलीकरोति,<BR>this man is t.ed<BR>by the head gambler:<BR>अयं सभिकेन खलीक्रियते,<BR>Mr. ii.;<BR>(2) बाधते: v. To vex, trouble,<BR>pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

torment
TORMENT (subs.):<BR>(1) यातना;<BR>(2) यन्त्रणा;<BR>(3)<BR>कारणा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tormentor
TORMENTOR: expr. by verb or subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tornado
TORNADO: घूर्णवायुः and sim. comp. s.: v.<BR>Storm, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

torpedo
TORPEDO:<BR>I a fish: *वैद्युतकः।<BR>II An<BR>engine: *प्रमाथिनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

torpid
TORPID: जड (f. डा): v. Numb, slow, in-<BR>-active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

torpidity
TORPIDITY, TORPOR: जाड्यम्: v. Numbness,<BR>slowness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

torrent
TORRENT:<BR>I Of rain etc.:<BR>(1) धारा;<BR>(2)<BR>आसारः: v. Rain.<BR>II Stream: q. v.: स्रोतस्<BR>(n.): v. Also flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

torrid
TORRID: उष्ण (f. ष्णा): v. Hot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tortoise
TORTOISE:<BR>(1) कूर्मः;<BR>(2) कच्छपः;<BR>(3) कमठः।<BR>Ph.:<BR>t. -shell:<BR>कमठपृष्ठम्, Ma. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tortuous
TORTUOUS: वक्र (f. क्रा): v. Crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

torture
TORTURE (subs.): यातना;<BR>(2) कारणा (rare),<BR>of the eighteen t.s:<BR>अष्टादशानां कारणानाम्, D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

torture
TORTURE (v.): यातनां<BR>or<BR>कारणां ददाति (दा, c. 3.):<BR>v. Also to pain, torment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

torturer
TORTURER:<BR>(1) यातनादायिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) by<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toss
TOSS (v.):<BR>I Trans.: विक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.):<BR>v. To throw about, scatter, roll.<BR>II In-<BR>-trans.:<BR>(1) विक्षिप्यते (pass. of क्षिप्);<BR>(2)<BR>इतस्ततः स्यन्दते (स्यन्द्, c. 1.): v. Also to roll.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toss
TOSS (subs.):<BR>(1) उत्क्षेपः -णम्, सं-;<BR>(2) क्षेपः:<BR>v. Throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

total
TOTAL (adj.):<BR>(1) सकल (f. ला),<BR>t. number of<BR>lotuses:<BR>सकलकमलसंख्या, Li. 28.;<BR>(2) समग्र (f.<BR>ग्रा): v. All, whole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

total
TOTAL, TOTALITY (subs.):<BR>(1) साकल्यम्;<BR>(2)<BR>समष्टिः;<BR>(3) ऐक्यम्, Li. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

totally
TOTALLY: सम्पूर्णम्: v. Fully, wholly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

totter
TOTTER: ह्वलति, प्र-, वि- (ह्वल्, c. 1.): v. Wa-<BR>-ver, stagger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

touch
TOUCH (v.):<BR>(1) स्पृशति, rarely with परि-<BR>or<BR>सं-<BR>(स्पृश्, c. 6.),<BR>you t. her eyes:<BR>दृष्टिं स्पृशसि,<BR>Sa. i. 24.;<BR>this will not t. me:<BR>न मां स्पृशेदयम्,<BR>Mah.;<BR>(2) by subs., what can be t.ed:<BR>स्पर्शवत् (f. ती), Par. 56.: v. Also affect,<BR>feel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tough
TOUGH (subs.): स्पर्शः, -नम्, or rarely स्पृष्टिः, सं-,<BR> परि-;<BR>pleasure of t.:<BR>स्पर्शसुखम्, Ki.; admit- [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">Page717</a>]<BR>-ting of t.:<BR>स्पर्शक्षम् (f. मा), Sa. i. 29.;<BR>t. ing<BR>my feet:<BR>मत्पादस्पृष्टिकया, Vi. iv.: v. Also<BR>contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

touch at
TOUCH AT, TOUCH ON or UPON: स्पृशति: v. To<BR>touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

touching
TOUCHING:<BR>I Adj.: हृदयस्पृश् (mfn.): v.<BR>Pathetic.<BR>II = about: q. v.: उद्दिश्य।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

touch-me-not
TOUCH-ME-NOT: a plant: लताविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

touchstone
TOUCHSTONE: कषः, नि-, “कषपाषाणनिभे नभस्तले”, N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

touchy
TOUCHY: कोपन (f. ना): v. Irritable, peevish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tough
TOUGH:<BR>(1) कठिन (f. ना=hard);<BR>(2) दृढ (f.<BR>ढा= firm);<BR>(3) गुरु (f. also र्वी=heavy: as<BR>of meat), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toughness
TOUGHNESS:<BR>(1) काठिन्यम्: v. Hardness;<BR>(2)<BR>दृढता<BR>or<BR>दार्ढ्यम्: v. Firmness;<BR>(3) गुरुत्त्वम्:<BR>v. Heaviness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tour
TOUR: परिभ्रमणम्: v. Travel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tourist
TOURIST:<BR>(1) परिभ्रमणकारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) पर्यटक<BR>(f. टिका); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tournament
TOURNAMENT: सादिनां नियुद्धम्<BR>or<BR>क्रीडायुद्धम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tow
TOW:<BR>I Verb: कर्षति (कृष्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>drag.<BR>II Subs.: स्थूलशाणम् and sim. comp. s:<BR>v. Rope. Ph.:<BR>to take in t.:<BR>बद्धा नयति, (नी,<BR>c. 1.: comp. Bengali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toward
TOWARD, TOWARDS:<BR>(1) प्रति in comp.,<BR>t.<BR>Śiva:<BR>ईशं प्रति, Ku. v. 31.; t. the north-east:<BR>ऐशानीं दिशं प्रति, V. i.;<BR>(2) अभि (gen. in comp.),<BR>t. evening:<BR>अभिसायम्, Si. i. 16.; t. Ayodhyā:<BR>अभ्ययोध्यम्, B. ii. 49.: v. Also to (VI).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toward
TOWARD, TOWARDLY: अनुविधायिन् (f. नी): v.<BR>Compliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

towel
TOWEL: गात्रमार्जनी and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tower
TOWER (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: खट्टः (?).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>t. of strength:<BR>बलोपस्तम्भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tower
TOWER (v.): उपरि तिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.): v. To<BR>stand, high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

towline
TOWLINE: i. e. towing rope: गुणः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

town
TOWN: नगरम्(री);<BR>(2) पुरम्(री)।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

townsman
TOWNSMAN, TOWNSWOMAN:<BR>(1) नागरिक (f.<BR>की);<BR>(2) पौर (f. री);<BR>(3) पौरजनः (f. वधूः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

townhall
TOWNHALL: पौरशाला (?) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toy
TOY:<BR>I Subs.: क्रीडनकम्।<BR>II Verb.: v. To<BR>play, sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trace
TRACE (v.):<BR>I To draw: q. v.: आलिखति<BR>(लिख्, c. 6.).<BR>II With<BR>out:<BR>आसादयति (c.<BR>of सद्): v. To find out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trace
TRACE (subs.):<BR>I Mark: q. v.: चिह्नम्।<BR>II<BR>Foot-print: q. v.: पदवी।<BR>III Of a carriage:<BR>प्रग्रहः (ग्राहः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trace
TRACE (subs.):<BR>I Mark: q. v.: चिह्नम्।<BR>II<BR>Way: q. v.: मार्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

track
TRACK (v.):<BR>(1) विमार्गयति (मृग, c. 10.): v.<BR>search;<BR>(2) अनुसरति (सृ, c. 1.): v. To<BR>follow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trackless
TRACKLESS:<BR>I Markless: expr. by circumlo.<BR>II Without any path.: निःसञ्चार (f. रा) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tract
TRACT:<BR>I Place, region: q. v.: भूभागः।<BR>II<BR>Treatise, book: q. v.: प्रबन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tractable
TRACTABLE: विधेय (f. या): v. Docile, sub-<BR>-missive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trade
TRADE (subs.):<BR>(1) वाणिज्यम् (rarely वणिज्या =<BR>commerce);<BR>(2) व्यवहारः (= business);<BR>(3)<BR>व्यापारः (=2);<BR>(4) व्यवसायः (=2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trade
TRADE (v.): वाणिज्यं करोति, K. s. vi. 47.;<BR>one<BR>who t.s in paddy:<BR>धान्यव्यवसायिन् (f. नी);<BR>one<BR>who t. s in book:<BR>पुस्तकविक्रयिन् (f. णी): v. To<BR>sell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trader
TRADER:<BR>(1) वाणिज्यकारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) विक्रयिन्<BR>(f. णी = seller: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tradesman
TRADESMAN: पण्यविक्रयिन् (f. णी): v. Shop-<BR>-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tradition
TRADITION:<BR>handed down by t.:<BR>अनेकवृद्धपरम्परा-<BR>समागत (f. ता), K.: v. Also rumour, his-<BR>-tory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

traditional
TRADITIONAL, TRADITIONALLY: expr. by cir-<BR>-cumlo: v. Above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

traduce
TRADUCE: अभिशंसति (शंस्, c. 1.): v. Calum-<BR>-niate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

traducer
TRADUCER: अभिशंसक (f. सिका): v. Calum-<BR>-niator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

traffic
TRAFFIC: v. Trade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tragedian
TRAGEDIAN: *महानाटककृत् (mfn.); लोकनाटककार<BR>(f. री); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tragedy
TRAGEDY: *महानाटकम्, लोकनाटकम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tragic
TRAGIC, TRAGICAL:<BR>I Of a tragedy: expr. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">Page718</a>]<BR>by comp.<BR>II Fatal, mournful: q. v.: दुरन्त<BR>(f. न्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tragi-comedy
TRAGI-COMEDY: *मिश्रनाटकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trail
TRAIL (subs.):<BR>I Foot-print: q. v.: पदवी।<BR>II Scent left: गन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trail
TRAIL (v.): आकर्षति (कृष्, c. 1.): v. To drag,<BR>draw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

train
TRAIN (subs.):<BR>I A series, succession: परम्परा।<BR>II Retinue: q. v.: परिवर्हः।<BR>III Railway:<BR>*लौहशकटमाला।<BR>IV Of dress: पुच्छः (?). V.<BR>Of army: perh. परिवर्हः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

train
TRAIN (v.):<BR>I Educate, instruct: q. v.: विनयति<BR>(नी, c. 1.).<BR>II To accustom, exercise:<BR>q. v.: परिचयं करोति,<BR>t. ed to arms:<BR>परिचितशस्त्र<BR>(f. स्त्रा): v. Conversant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

training
TRAINING (subs.): शिक्षा: v. Instruction,<BR>education.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trait
TRAIT: लक्षणम्: v. Feature, mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

traitor
TRAITOR, TRAITOROUS:<BR>(1) विश्वासघातक (f.<BR>तिका);<BR>(2) विश्वासहन् (mfn.);<BR>(3) विश्वासघातिन्<BR>(f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trammel
TRAMMEL:<BR>I Subs.: बन्धः: v. Fetter.<BR>II<BR>Verb: बध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.): v. To fetter,<BR>bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trample
TRAMPLE: मृद्राति (मृद्, c. 9.): v. To crush,<BR>overwhelm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trance
TRANCE: perh. प्रमोहः: v. Also ecstasy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tranquil
TRANQUIL: शान्त, प्र- (f. न्ता): v. Calm,<BR>quiet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tranquillity
TRANQUILLITY: शान्तिः, प्र-ः v. Calmness, peace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tranquillize
TRANQUILLIZE: सा(शा)न्त्वयति(सा[शा]न्त्व्, c. 10.):<BR>v. To quiet, pacify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transact
TRANSACT:<BR>(1) करोतिः v. To do;<BR>(2) निष्पा-<BR>दयतिः v. To accomplish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transaction
TRANSACTION:<BR>I The act:<BR>(1) करणम्;<BR>(2)<BR>अनुष्ठानम्: v. Accomplishment, performance.<BR>II Act, affair: कार्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transcend
TRANSCEND: अतिक्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>surpass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transcendent
TRANSCENDENT, -AL:<BR>(1) सर्वातिशायिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) सर्वातिरिक्त (f. क्ता), R. i. 14.; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transcribe
TRANSCRIBE: लिखति (लिख्, c. 6.: when sense<BR>clear): v. To copy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transcriber
TRANSCRIBER: लिपिकरः: v. Copyist, writer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transcript
TRANSCRIPT: perh. प्रतिलिपिः<BR>or<BR>प्रतिलेखः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transfer
TRANSFER (v.): I t. the case in another court:<BR>*विचारकान्तरे समर्पयाम्यर्थम्; t. red to another division:<BR>*विभागान्तरं प्रेषित (f. ता): v. To send,<BR>deliver, give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transfer
TRANSFER (subs.), TRANSFERENCE,<BR>TRANSFERABLE; expr. as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transfiguration
TRANSFIGURATION, TRANSFIGURE: v. Trans-<BR>-formation, transform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transfix
TRANSFIX:<BR>I Lit.: प्रवयति (वे, c. 1.),<BR>t. ed<BR>with dart:<BR>प्रासप्रोत (f. ता), Vi.: v. Also to<BR>pierce.<BR>II Fig.: जडीकरोतिः v. To stupefy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transform
TRANSFORM:<BR>she will be t. ed into a plant:<BR>सा<BR> लताभावे परिणतरूपा भविष्यति, Vi. iv.; as if t. ed:<BR>रूपान्तरेणेव परिणत (f. ता), K.: v. To change,<BR>form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transformation
TRANSFORMATION:<BR>(1) रूपान्तरपरिणतिः;<BR>(2)<BR>परिवर्तः (= change).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transfuse
TRANSFUSE:<BR>I To pour: q. v.<BR>II To pass,<BR>pervade: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transfuse
TRANSFUSE:<BR>(1) संक्रामणम्;<BR>(2) संक्रान्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transgress
TRANSGRESS (v.):<BR>I Trans.: अतिक्रामति, वि-<BR>(क्रम्, c. 1.): v. To break, violate.<BR>II<BR>Intrans.: अपराध्यति (राध्, c. 4.): v. To<BR>offend, sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transgression
TRANSGRESSION:<BR>I The act: अतिक्रमः, वि-: v.<BR>Violation.<BR>II Offence, fault: q. v.: अपराधः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transgressor
TRANSGRESSOR:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by verb or<BR>comp.: v. Violator.<BR>II Offender, sinner:<BR>q. v.: अपराधिन् (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transient
TRANSIENT:<BR>I Fleeting, passing:<BR>(1) अचिर-<BR>स्थायिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) चञ्चलः (ला, लं),<BR>wealth<BR>is t.:<BR>चञ्चलं वसु, Ki. xiii. 53.;<BR>(3) चपलः<BR>(ला, लं = unsteady),<BR>life is very t.:<BR>जीवन-<BR>मतिशयचपलम्, J.;<BR>(4) अनित्य (f. त्या = not<BR>eternal).<BR>II Momentary, hasty: क्षणिक<BR>(f. का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transit
TRANSIT: क्रान्तिः (?),<BR>t. of Venus<BR>*शुक्रक्रान्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transition
TRANSITION: expr. by circumlo.: v. Change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transitive
TRANSITIVE: सकर्मकः, “ननु सर्वेषां सकर्मकतायान्ति”<BR>Kaṇāda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transitively
TRANSITIVELY: expr. by adj. or subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transitoriness
TRANSITORINESS:<BR>(1) क्षणभङ्गुरता;<BR>(2) अचिर-<BR>स्थायिता etc. (= transientness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transitory
TRANSITORY: क्षणभङ्गुरः (रा, रं): v. Transient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

translate
TRANSLATE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) करोति (=render);<BR>(2) भाषान्तरीकरोति (?).<BR>II To transform:<BR>q. v.<BR>III By death: लोकान्तरं नयति (नी,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>t. d:<BR>लोकान्तरगत (f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

translation
TRANSLATION:<BR>I The act: t. into English:<BR>इंलण्डीयभाषायां करणम्।<BR>II What is translated:<BR>*भाषान्तरीकृत (f. ताः (?).<BR>III Removal,<BR>transformation: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

translator
TRANSLATOR: *भाषान्तरीकारक (f. रिका); better<BR>by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

translucent
TRANSLUCENT: स्वच्छ (f. च्छा): v. Clear, lucid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transmigrate
TRANSMIGRATE: v. To emigrate, migrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transmission
TRANSMISSION: expr. by circumlo.: v. Below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transmit
TRANSMIT:<BR>I To send: q. v.: प्रेरयति (ईर्,<BR>c. 10.). To be t. ted: (= to pass): q. v.:<BR>गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.).<BR>II To suffer, to pass<BR>through:<BR>iron t. s electricity:<BR>*लौहेन<BR> विद्युन्निष्पतति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transmutation
TRANSMUTATION: परिणतिः: v. Change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transmute
TRANSMUTE: परिवर्तयति (c. of वृत्): v. To<BR>change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transparency
TRANSPARENCY:<BR>I Lit.: स्वच्छता: v. Clear-<BR>-ness.<BR>II A picture: *स्वच्छालेख्यम्<BR>or<BR>-चित्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transparent
TRANSPARENT: अच्छ (f. च्छा), सु-: v. Clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transpire
TRANSPIRE:<BR>I To become public: q. v.:<BR>प्रकाशीमवति।<BR>II To come out: निःसरति (सृ,<BR>c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transplant
TRANSPLANT: स्थानान्तरे रोपयति (c. of रुह्): v.<BR>To plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transport
TRANSPORT:<BR>I Carry, convey: q. v.: नयति<BR>(नी, c. 1.).<BR>II To banish: द्वीपान्तरं नयति।<BR>III To delight: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transport
TRANSPORT (subs.):<BR>I Conveyance:<BR>(1)<BR>नयनम्;<BR>(2) better by verb.<BR>II A ship:<BR>प्रवहणम्।<BR>III Rapture, ecstacy: q. v.: हर्ष-<BR>निर्भरः।<BR>IV Of passion: क्रोधावेशः and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transportation
TRANSPORTATION:<BR>I Conveyance: वाहनम्।<BR>II Banishment: द्वीपान्तरविवासनम् and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transpose
TRANSPOSE: विनिमयः (मे, c. 1.): v. To<BR>interchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transposition
TRANSPOSITION:<BR>(1) विनिमयः (= interchange);<BR>(2) व्यत्ययः;<BR>(3) व्यत्यासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transverse
TRANSVERSE: व्यत्यस्त (f. स्ता): v. Also inverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

transversely
TRANSVERSELY:<BR>(1) व्यत्यासेन (?);<BR>(2) तिर्यक्<BR>(= obliquely).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trap
TRAP (subs.): कूटम्: v. Snare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trap
TRAP (v.): v. To ensnare, entrap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trap-door
TRAP-DOOR:<BR>(1) कूटाद्वारं (?);<BR>(2) पक्ष्मद्वारम्<BR>(= side-door).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trappings
TRAPPINGS:<BR>(1) सज्जा (= equipment);<BR>(2)<BR>भूषा (= ornament).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trapezium
TRAPEZIUM: अतुल्यलम्बकं क्षेत्रम्, Li. 160.; *विषम-<BR>चतुर्भुजः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trapezoid
TRAPEZOID: समलम्बं क्षेत्रम्, Li. and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trash
TRASH (subs.): expr. by adj.: असार (f. रा),<BR>तुच्छ (f. च्छा)<BR>or<BR>निरर्थक (f. का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

travail
TRAVAIL: v. Labour, toil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

travel
TRAVEL, TRAVELLING:<BR>(1) परिभ्रमणम्;<BR>(2)<BR>पर्यटनम्;<BR>(3) विचरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

travel
TRAVEL:<BR>(1) भ्राम्यति<BR>or<BR>भ्रमति (भ्रम्, c. 4. and<BR>1.),<BR>I have t. led through many countries:<BR>भ्रान्तो<BR> देशमनेकम्, J.;<BR>(2) अटति, परि- (अट्, c. 1.),<BR>t. the holy places:<BR>तीर्थाणि पर्यटस्व, Mah.;<BR>(3)<BR>विचरति (to move about),<BR>he t. ed over this<BR>world:<BR>व्यचरत्स महीमिमां, Mah. iii. 135. 50.;<BR>(4) चंक्रम्यते (from क्रम्: rare), Mah iii. 136.<BR>1.: v. Also to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

traveller
TRAVELLER:<BR>(1) पथिकः (= wayfarer), became<BR>t. s in the forest by the bank of the Bhāgīrathī:.<BR>भागीरथीतटवने पथिकावभूताम्, C. r. ii. 53.;<BR>(2)<BR>पान्थः (= 1);<BR>(3) परिभ्रमणकारिन् (f. णी) and<BR>sim. comp. s (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

traverse
TRAVERSE:<BR>I To cross: q. v.: तरति (तॄ, c.<BR>1.).<BR>II To travel: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

travesty
TRAVESTY: v. Parody.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tray
TRAY:<BR>(1) भाजनम् (?);<BR>(2) आधारः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treacherous
TREACHEROUS:<BR>(1) विश्वासहन्तृ (f. न्त्री),<BR>and t.<BR>men:<BR>विश्वासहन्ता च नरः, M. p. 15. 7.;<BR>(2)<BR>विश्वासघातिन् (f. नी), I am not t. Rākṣasa:<BR>नाहं विश्रम्भघाती राक्षसः, Mu. v.; and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treacherously
TREACHEROUSLY:<BR>(1) निकृत्या (= wickedly),<BR>M.p. 15. 41.;<BR>(2) शाठ्येन (= deceitfully:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treacherousness
TREACHEROUSNESS, TREACHERY:<BR>(1) विश्वास-<BR>भङ्गः;<BR>(2) विश्रम्भघातः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treacle
TREACLE:<BR>(1) गुडः (= molasses);<BR>(2) गुडोच्छिष्टम्<BR>(the refuse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tread
TREAD (v.): क्षुणत्ति (क्षुद्, c. 7.),<BR>momentarily<BR>trodden by the fādava's forces:<BR>क्षुण्णः क्षणं यदुबलैः,<BR>Si. v. 11.; were trodden upon by chariots:<BR>चुक्षुदिरे रथौघैः, Si. iii. 27.;<BR>from the trodden<BR>path:<BR>क्षुण्णाद्वर्त्मनः, R. i. 17.: v. Also to press,<BR>put.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tread
TREAD:<BR>(1) पादन्यासः;<BR>(2) चरणपातः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treason
TREASON:<BR>(1) राजद्रोहः;<BR>(2) राजाभिद्रोहः, and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treasonable
TREASONABLE, TREASONOUS:<BR>(1) by comp. s.;<BR>(2) राजद्रोहिन् (f. णी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treasure
TREASURE (v.): संचिनोति (चि, c. 5.): v. To<BR>store.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treasure
TREASURE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) कोशः(षः),<BR>t. is<BR>the life of those who possess it:<BR>कोषः कोषवतां<BR> प्राणः, H. ii. 92.;<BR>(2) धनम् (= money;<BR>riches).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) रत्नम्;<BR>(2) धनम्;<BR>(3)<BR>भाण्डम्,<BR>t. of a son:<BR>पुत्रभाण्डम्, Vi. B. r.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treasurer
TREASURER:<BR>(1) कोषाध्यक्षः;<BR>(2) कोशाधीशः, Vi.<BR>vi. 1.; and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treasurership
TREASURERSHIP:<BR>(1) कोशाध्यक्षता and sim.<BR>comp. s;<BR>(2) अर्थाधिकारः, H. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treasure-trove
TREASURE-TROVE:<BR>(1) निधिः,<BR>like a poor man<BR>getting t.:<BR>निधिं लब्ध्वेव निर्धनः, S. p.;<BR>(2) निखातं<BR> धनम् and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treasury
TREASURY:<BR>(1) कोशः(षः):<BR>should send the second<BR>half to the t.:<BR>द्वितीयमर्धं कोशे निवेशयेत्, V. s.;<BR>(2) कोशगृहम् and sim. comp. s, R. v. 29.;<BR>(3) माण्डागारम् (= store-house), Y. i. 320.;<BR>(4) भाण्डारम् (= 3),<BR>employees in t.:<BR>भाण्डारिकाः,<BR>M.n. on R. v. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treat
TREAT (v. t.):<BR>I To behave, act: q. v.:<BR>आचरति, सम्- (चर्, c. 1.),<BR>should t. (grown<BR>up) sons like friends:<BR>पुत्रं मित्रवदाचरेत्, J. Ph.:<BR>to t. with respect: v. To respect; to t. with<BR>contumely: v. To despise.<BR>II To describe:<BR>q. v.: वर्णयति (वर्ण्, c. 10.).<BR>III To satiate:<BR>q. v.: तर्पयति, सं- (c. of तृप्).<BR>IV Medically:<BR>(1) चिकित्सति (कित्, c. 1.), Sr.;<BR>(2) उप-चरति,<BR> उपा-, (चर्, c. 1.),<BR>should t. him with febri-<BR>fuges:<BR>तं ज्वरघ्नैः समुपाचरेत्, Sr.;<BR>(3) उपक्रामति<BR>(क्रम्, c. 1.) (rare),<BR>having t. ed me with gesti-<BR>culations, charms, prayers, meditations etc.:<BR>मां<BR> मुद्रातन्त्रमन्त्रध्यानादिभिरुपक्रम्य, D. ii. T. with: i. e.<BR>negotiate: सं-दधाति<BR>or<BR>-धत्ते (धा, c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treat
TREAT (subs.): to give a grand or rich t. to:<BR>भोजनविशेषैः सन्तर्पयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treatise
TREATISE:<BR>(1) प्रबन्धः;<BR>(2) ग्रन्थः (= book).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treatment
TREATMENT:<BR>I Behaviour, conduct:<BR>(1)<BR>आचरणम्;<BR>(2) व्यवहारः;<BR>(3) वृत्तिः।<BR>II Medical<BR>t.;<BR>(1) चिकित्सा;<BR>(2) उपचारः;<BR>(3) उपक्रमः<BR>(rare).<BR>III Description: q. v.: वर्णना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treaty
TREATY:<BR>I Negotiation: सन्धानम्<BR>or<BR>सन्धिः।<BR>II<BR>Agreement, condition: पत्रम्, t. of peace:<BR>सन्धिपत्रम्;<BR>t. of marriage:<BR>विवाहपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treble
TREBLE:<BR>I Lit.: त्रिगुण (f. णा).<BR>II In<BR>music: तार (f. रा).<BR>III Verb: त्रिगुणी-<BR>करोति<BR>or<BR>त्रिगुणयति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trebly
TREBLY:<BR>(1) त्रेधा<BR>or<BR>त्रिधा;<BR>(2) त्रिगुणम् (= three-<BR>-fold).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tree
TREE:<BR>(1) वृक्षः,<BR>t.-planter:<BR>वृक्षरोपयिता, He.;<BR>(2) तरुः,<BR>who wear bark of t. s:<BR>तरुवल्कवासस्<BR>(mfn.), R. viii. 11.;<BR>(2) द्रुमः, full of t. s:<BR>द्रुमवत् (f. ती), R. ix. 26.;<BR>(4) पादपः,<BR>a t.<BR>with thick shade:<BR>घनच्छायः पादपः, He.;<BR>(5)<BR>वनस्पतिः (= large t.),<BR>made of five t. s:<BR>पञ्च-<BR>वनस्पतिरचितः, V. m. 79. 39.;<BR>(6) महीरुहः;<BR>(7) शाखिन् (m.);<BR>(8) दुः;<BR>(9) अनोकहः;<BR>(10) वनराजिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trefoil
TREFOIL:<BR>(1) त्रिपर्णः (?);<BR>(2) त्रिदलः;<BR>(3)<BR>त्रिपत्रः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trellis
TRELLIS: v. Lattice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tremble
TREMBLE:<BR>(1) वेपते, प्र- (वेप्, c. 1.),<BR>t. ing<BR>mother:<BR>वेपमानजननी, R. xi. 65.;<BR>(2) कम्पते,<BR> प्र- (कम्प्, c. 1.),<BR>he made the kings t.:<BR>नृप-<BR>गणमसावकम्पयत्, Si. xv. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trembling
TREMBLING (subs.): कम्पः: v. Tremor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tremendous
TREMENDOUS: घोर (f. रा): v. Immense,<BR>huge, terrible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tremendously
TREMENDOUSLY: घोरम्: v. Also immensely,<BR>exceedingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tremendousness
TREMENDOUSNESS: घोरता: v. Also greatness,<BR>largeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tremor
TREMOR:<BR>(1) वेपथुः,<BR>some were in t.:<BR>केचिद्वेपथु-<BR>मासेदुः, B. iv. 43.;<BR>(2) कम्पः, प्र-,<BR>already t. from<BR>old age:<BR>प्रागेव जरसा कम्पः, Sa. vi. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tremulous
TREMULOUS:<BR>(1) कम्प्र (f. म्प्रा);<BR>(2) वेपमान<BR>(f. ना);<BR>(3) कम्पमान (f. ना);<BR>(4) लोल (f.<BR>ला), व्या- (= shaking: of things).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trench
TRENCH:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) खातम् (= ditch);<BR>(2)<BR>परिखा (round a fort etc.);<BR>(3) नाली, प्रणाली<BR>(channel for irrigation);<BR>(4) आलवालम्<BR>(round a tree).<BR>II Verb: खातं<BR>or<BR>प्रणालीं<BR> करोतिः v. Also to dig.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trencher
TRENCHER:<BR>I A digger: खनकः।<BR>II A vessel:<BR>काष्ठभाजनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trench upon
TRENCH UPON: v. To encroach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trepan
TREPAN:<BR>I Subs.: perh. दन्तशङ्कुः, Sr.<BR>II<BR>Verb: v. To cheat, deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trepidation
TREPIDATION: उद्वेगः: v. Alarm, agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trespass
TRESPASS (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: अतिक्रमः: v. Trans-<BR>-gression, offence.<BR>II In law: अतिक्रम्य प्रवेशः<BR>(?),<BR>house-t. by night:<BR>अतिक्रम्य रजन्यां गृह-<BR>प्रवेशः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trespass
TRESPASS (v.):<BR>I Lit.: अतिक्रामति (क्रम्, c.<BR>1.).<BR>II In law: अतिक्रभ्य प्रविशति (विश्, c.<BR>6.).<BR>III Of time: हरति (हृ, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trespasser
TRESPASSER: expr. by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tress
TRESS: कवरी: v. Curl, hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

triad
TRIAD:<BR>(1) त्रयम् (f. यी);<BR>(2) त्रिकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trial
TRIAL:<BR>I Examination: q. v.: परीक्षा।<BR>II<BR>Judicial: विचारः।<BR>III Affliction, calamity:<BR>कृच्छ्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

triangle
TRIANGLE:<BR>(1) त्रिभुजम्,<BR>right-angled t.:<BR>कोटिमत्<BR>or<BR>ऋजुभुजं त्रिभुजम्, Li. 125. (समकोणत्रिभुजम्),<BR>K. d.;<BR>acute-a. t.:<BR>अन्तर्लम्बं त्रिभुजम्;<BR>obtuse-a.<BR>t.:<BR>बहिर्लम्बं त्रिभुजम्;<BR>base of a t.:<BR>भुः, भूमिः,<BR> क्ष्मा, etc.;<BR>(2) त्र्यस्रम्;<BR>(3) त्रिबाहुकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

triangular
TRIANGULAR:<BR>(1) त्रिकोण (f. णा);<BR>(2) त्र्यस्र<BR>(f. स्रा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tribe
TRIBE: जातिः: v. Caste, race, nation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tribulation
TRIBULATION: कष्टम्: v. Trouble, calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tribunal
TRIBUNAL:<BR>I Seat of a judge: and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR>II Court: q. v.: धर्मसभा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tribune
TRIBUNE: प्रजापालः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tributary
TRIBUTARY: करद (f. दा: perh. also of rivers),<BR>who has made (other) kings t.:<BR>करदीकृतभूपालः,<BR>Si. ii. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tribute
TRIBUTE:<BR>I Lit.: करः,<BR>pay in kind some t. to<BR>Yudhiṣṭhira:<BR>युधिष्ठिराय यक्तिंचित् करपण्यं प्रदीयताम्,<BR>Mah. ii. 28. 15.<BR>II Fig.: उपहारः (= pre-<BR>-sent: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trice
TRICE: निमेषः,<BR>in a t.:<BR>निमेषमात्रेण<BR>or<BR>मात्रात्,<BR>R. iii. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trice
TRICE (subs.):<BR>I Artifice, stratagem: q. v.:<BR>(1) छलम्;<BR>(2) छद्मन्।<BR>II Juggler's: माया,<BR>in all the t. s of Śambara:<BR>शम्बरस्य मायासु।<BR>III<BR>Play: q. v.: खेला<BR>or<BR>खेलितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trick
TRICK (v.): छलयति (छल्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trickery
TRICKERY: छलम्: v. Deceit, deception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trickle
TRICKLE: मन्दं मन्दं स्रवति (स्रु, c. 1.): v. To<BR>ooze, flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trickster
TRICKSTER: वञ्चक (f. ञ्चिका), प्र-: v. Cheat,<BR>deceitful, rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trident
TRIDENT: त्रिशूलम्, T.-handed (Śiva) शूलपाणिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

triennial
TRIENNIAL:<BR>(1) त्रैवार्षिक (f. की);<BR>(2) त्र्यब्दिक<BR>(f. की); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trifle
TRIFLE:<BR>I Subs.: expr. by adj.: v. Trifl-<BR>-ing.<BR>II Verb: खेलति (खेल्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>play.<BR>To t. away:<BR>क्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.): v.<BR>To waste, spend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trifling
TRIFLING (adj.):<BR>(1) तुच्छ (f. च्छा);<BR>(2)<BR>निरर्थक (f. का = useless);<BR>(3) लधु (f. also घ्वी<BR>=light);<BR>(4) क्षुद्र (f. द्रा = small).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trigger
TRIGGER: अवष्टम्भः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trigonometrical
TRIGONOMETRICAL: expr. by comp.,<BR>t.<BR>survey:<BR>त्रिकोणमितिमापः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trigonometry
TRIGONOMETRY: त्रिकोणमितिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trilateral
TRILATERAL: त्रिभुजः (जा, जं) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trill
TRILL: v. Quaver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trillion
TRILLION: दशपरार्द्धम्<BR>or<BR>परःपरार्द्धम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trim
TRIM (v.): कल्पयति (कॢप्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>clip, arrange, dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trim
TRIM (adj.): कॢप्त (f. प्ता): v. Neat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trim
TRIM, TRIMMING (subs.): परिकल्पः: v. Also<BR>dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trinity
TRINITY: त्रयैकत्वम् (?) “एकैव मूर्तिर्बिभिदे त्रिधा सा,<BR>K. vii. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trinket
TRINKET: अलङ्कारः: v. Ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trio
TRIO: त्रयम्<BR>or<BR>त्रयी, Si. ii. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trip
TRIP (subs.):<BR>I An excursion: भ्रमणम्।<BR>II<BR>A tremble: स्खलितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trip
TRIP (v.):<BR>I Intrans.: स्खलति (स्खल्, c. 1.).<BR>II Trans.: स्खलयति (c. of स्खल्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tripartite
TRIPARTITE: त्रिभाग-<BR>or<BR>त्रेधा-विभक्त (f. क्ता) and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tripe
TRIPE:<BR>I Entrails: अन्त्राणि (n. pl.).<BR>II<BR>Stomach: जठरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

triple
TRIPLE: Treble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tripler
TRIPLER:<BR>I Lit.: त्रिकम्।<BR>II Of verses:<BR>विशेषकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tripod
TRIPOD: त्रिपदी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tripos
TRIPOS:<BR>mathematical t.:<BR>गणितपरीक्षा (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trisyllabic
TRISYLLABIC:<BR>(1) त्र्यक्षर (f. रा);<BR>(2) त्रिक (f.<BR>का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trisyllable
TRISYLLABLE:<BR>(1) त्र्यक्षरम्;<BR>(2) त्रिकम्, ‘म’<BR>is the<BR>technical name of a t. whose every syllable is long:<BR>सर्वगुरोस्त्रिकस्य मसंज्ञा परिभाष्यते, P. h.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trite
TRITE:<BR>(1) क्षुण्ण (f. ण्णा),<BR>if one leaves out the<BR>subject of Rāma, because it is t.:<BR>यदि क्षुण्णं पूर्वैरिति<BR> जहति रामस्य चरितम्, A. n. i. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

triumph
TRIUMPH (subs.):<BR>I Victory: q. v.: विजयः।<BR>II Roman: विजयोत्सवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

triumph
TRIUMPH (v.):<BR>I Exalt, celebrate victory:<BR>विजयोत्सवं करोति।<BR>II To gain victory, win:<BR>q. v.: विजयते (जि, c. 1.).<BR>III To thrive,<BR>prosper: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

triumphal
TRIUMPHAL: जय-<BR>or<BR>विजय- in comp., t. arch:<BR>जयतोरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

triumphant
TRIUMPHANT:<BR>(1) जयिन् (f. नी), वि-,<BR>in the t.<BR>seat:<BR>जयिन्यासने, Ki. xviii. 38.;<BR>(2) जैत्र (f.<BR>त्री);<BR>(3) जित्वर (f. री), वि-;<BR>(4) जयशालिन्<BR>(f. नी); and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

triumvirate
TRIUMVIRATE: त्रिजनशासनम् and sim. comp. s (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

triune
TRIUNE: त्रिकैक (f. का) (?) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trivial
TRIVIAL: v. Trifling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

triviality
TRIVIALITY:<BR>(1) तुच्छता;<BR>(2) क्षुद्रता (= small-<BR>-ness);<BR>(3) निरर्थकता (= uselessness): v.<BR>Also trifle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trochee
TROCHEE:<BR>(1) तालः (Wilson);<BR>(2) गलौ (dual);<BR>(3) आदिगुरुद्विकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

troop
TROOP:<BR>I In pl.: सैनिकाः<BR>or<BR>सैन्याः: v. Also<BR>forces, army.<BR>II Company: q. v.: गुल्मः।<BR>III Collection, multitude: q. v.: यूथम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trooper
TROOPER: सादिन् (m.): v. Horseman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trope
TROPE: रूपकम्: v. Metaphor, figure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trophy
TROPHY:<BR>(1) जयस्तम्भः (column);<BR>(2) विजय-<BR>लिङ्गम् (mark); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tropic
TROPIC:<BR>(1) अयनवृत्तम् (?). Ph.:<BR>the space with-<BR>in the t. s.:<BR>क्रान्तिवलयः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tropical
TROPICAL:<BR>I Metaphorical: q. v.<BR>II Belong-<BR>-ing to the t. s: क्रान्तिवलय- in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trot
TROT:<BR>I Subs.: धो(धी)रीतम्, -कम्।<BR>II Verb:<BR>धोरितकेन याति (या, c. 2.) etc.: v. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

troth
TROTH: विश्वासः: v. Faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trotter
TROTTER: धोरितकुशलो हयः and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trouble
TROUBLE (subs.):<BR>(1) कष्टम् (in every sense);<BR>v. Distress, pain, calamity;<BR>(2) क्लेशः<BR>(=toil),<BR>forgot her t. s:<BR>क्लेशं विसस्मार, M. n.<BR>on Ku. v. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trouble
TROUBLE (v.):<BR>(1) क्लिश्नाति, परि-, सं- (क्लिश्, c.<BR>9.), even the keeping up of what is gained t. s:<BR>क्लिश्नाति लब्धपरिपालनवृत्तिरेव, Sa. v. 5.;<BR>(2) बाधते;<BR>(बाध्, c. 1. = harass),<BR>t. good citizens:<BR>बाधन्ते<BR> भद्रिकाः प्रजाः, Mu.;<BR>(2) पीडयति (पीड्, c. 10.):<BR>v. To pain.: Ph.: don't t. yourself:<BR>अलमलमायासेन, S. iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

troublesome
TROUBLESOME:<BR>(1) कष्टकर (f. री);<BR>(2) क्लेशावह<BR>(f. हा), and sim. deriv. Ph.: a t. fellow:<BR>कण्टकः (= thorn).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

troublous
TROUBLOUS:<BR>t. sea:<BR>क्षुब्धार्णवः:<BR>t. misery:<BR>बाधकं<BR> कष्टम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trough
TROUGH: द्रोणिः(णी)।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trousers
TROUSERS: अधरावारः, and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trout
TROUT: मत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trowel
TROWEL:<BR>(1) कर्णी (?);<BR>(2) कर्णीशः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

truant
TRUANT: कर्मपराङ्मुख (f. खी): v. Idle, lazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

truce
TRUCE:<BR>I Peace: q. v.; सन्धिः।<BR>II Ceassa-<BR>-tion: विरामः,<BR>a t. to your frolics:<BR>विरमतु तव खेला।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

truck
TRUCK:<BR>I A cart: शकटः।<BR>II Barter: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

truckle
TRUCKLE: चाटु करोतिः v. To flatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

truculent
TRUCULENT: क्रूर (f. रा): v. Savage, cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trudge
TRUDGE: मन्थरं चलति (चल्, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>व्रजति (व्रज्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

true
TRUE:<BR>(1) सत्य (f. त्या), whose blessings are t.:<BR>(i. e. not falsified) सत्याशिस् (mfn.), Ki.;<BR>one<BR>not t. to his words:<BR>असत्यसन्ध (f. न्धा), H.;<BR>(2) तथ्य (f. थ्या), one whose sayings are t.:<BR>तथ्यगिर् (mfn.), R.;<BR>(3) यथार्थ (f. र्था = actual<BR>real: q. v.);<BR>(4) वास्तविक (f. की = 3): v.<BR>Also genuine, false. Ph.:<BR>it is t.:<BR>सत्यम्;<BR>it<BR>is very t.:<BR>युक्तम्, उपपन्नम् (proper).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

truism
TRUISM: सत्यम्: v. Truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

truly
TRULY:<BR>(1) सत्यम्;<BR>(2) तथ्यम्;<BR>(3) वस्तुतः (=<BR>in fact);<BR>(4) यथार्थतः (= really).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trump
TRUMP:<BR>I Subs.: रङ्गः (?).<BR>II Verb: तर्पयति<BR>(c. of तृप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trump up
TRUMP UP: v. To invent, fabricate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trumpery
TRUMPERY: expr. by adj. असार (f. रा): v.<BR>Trifling<BR>or<BR>कृत्रिम (f. मा = counterfeit, false).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trumpet
TRUMPET:<BR>I Subs.: तूरी।<BR>II Verb: v. To<BR>proclaim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trumpet-flower
TRUMPET-FLOWER: पाटला (लिः, also लम् for the<BR>flower only, Sa. i. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trumpeter
TRUMPETER:<BR>I Lit.: तूरीवादः, -कः।<BR>II Pro-<BR>-claimer: उद्घोषयितृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

truncheon
TRUNCHEON:<BR>(1) दण्डः;<BR>(2) यष्टिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trundle
TRUNDLE: v. To roll.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trunk
TRUNK:<BR>I Of an elephant:<BR>(1) शुण्डः, -ण्डा,<BR> -दण्डः,<BR>a small t.:<BR>शुण्डारः, Vi. i. 53.;<BR>(2) हस्तः,<BR>R. v. 45.;<BR>(3) करः, by the t. s of elephants:<BR>नागकरैः, M. n.<BR>II Of the body:<BR>(1) कबन्धः<BR>(= headless t.),<BR>saw their own t. s dancing on<BR>the ground:<BR>भुवि नृत्यन्तौ स्वकबन्धावपश्यताम्, Ku.<BR>xvi. 49.;<BR>(2) गात्रम् (= body).<BR>III Of a tree:<BR>(1) स्कन्धः;<BR>(2) काण्ड (mn.), प्र-;<BR>(3) स्थाणुः (of<BR>a lopped tree). Ph.:<BR>grand t. road:<BR>सुमहा-<BR>मार्गः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

truss
TRUSS:<BR>I Bandage: पट्टः।<BR>II Bandle; कूर्च्चः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trust
TRUST (subs.):<BR>I Confidence:<BR>(1) विश्वासः,<BR>never repose your t. on women and courts:<BR>विश्वासो<BR> नैव कर्तव्यः स्त्रीषु राजकुलेषु च, H.;<BR>(2) विश्रम्भः,<BR>out<BR>of t.:<BR>विश्रम्भतः, Mu. v. 7.;<BR>(3) प्रत्ययः, give<BR>him things on my t.:<BR>मत्प्रत्ययेनास्य द्रव्यं देहि, Mit.<BR>II Any thing t. ed:<BR>(1) निःक्षेपः;<BR>(2) न्यासः,<BR>Ph.:<BR>t.-property:<BR>विश्वासधनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trust
TRUST (v.):<BR>I To believe, confide: q. v.:<BR>विश्वसिति (श्वस्, c. 1.).<BR>II To entrust: q. v.:<BR>न्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trustee
TRUSTEE: विश्वासधनरक्षितृ (f. त्री) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trustworthy
TRUSTWORTHY, TRUSTY:<BR>(1) विश्वासार्ह (f. र्हा);<BR>(2) विश्वासयोग्य (f. ग्या), and sim. comp. s.:<BR>v. Also confidential.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

truth
TRUTH:<BR>I What is true:<BR>(1) सत्यम्;<BR>(2)<BR>तथ्यम्;<BR>(3) ऋतम्;<BR>(4) अवितथम् and sim.<BR>comp. s,<BR>t. although sweet:<BR>प्रियमप्यमिथ्या।<BR>II<BR>Trueness:<BR>(1) सत्यता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2) तथ्यता, -त्वम्;<BR>(3) याथार्थ्यम्<BR>or<BR>यथार्थता;<BR>(4) तत्त्वम्। Ph.: in t.:<BR>सत्यम्: v. Truly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

truthful
TRUTHFUL:<BR>I True: सत्य (f. त्या).<BR>II Of<BR>men: सत्यवादिन् (f. नी) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

truthfully
TRUTHFULLY: सत्यम्: v. Truly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

truthfulness
TRUTHFULNESS:<BR>(1) सत्यता (of words etc.);<BR>(2) सत्यवादिता (of men).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

try
TRY:<BR>I To examine: परीक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.),<BR>I have tried you forming (this) illusion:<BR>मायां<BR> मयोद्भाव्य परीक्षितोऽसि, R. ii. 62.<BR>II Judicially:<BR>(1) विचारयति (c. of चर्);<BR>(2) पश्यति (दृश्,<BR>c. 1. = to see), shall not t. (cases) on these days:<BR>तिथिष्वासु न पश्येत्, Mit.<BR>III To attempt,<BR>endeavour: q. v.: यतते,<BR>I will t. to save his<BR>life:<BR>प्राणरक्षणे तावदस्य यत्नमाचरामि, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trying
TRYING (adj.):<BR>(1) कष्टकर (f. री);<BR>(2) by<BR>subs. कृच्छ्रम्: v. Difficulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tub
TUB: द्रोणिः (र्णा),<BR>golden t.:<BR>कणकमयद्रोणी, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tube
TUBE:<BR>(1) नालः (ली, लं);<BR>(2) नालिका (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tuber
TUBER: कन्द (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tubercle
TUBERCLE: सूक्ष्मव्रण and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tuberous
TUBEROUS:<BR>(1) ग्रन्थिल (f. ला);<BR>(2) ग्रन्थिमत्<BR>(f. ती); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tubular
TUBULAR: नालाकार (f. रा) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tuck
TUCK;<BR>I Subs.: गुञ्जः (?).<BR>II गुञ्जयति (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tuesday
TUESDAY:<BR>(1) मङ्गलवारः;<BR>(2) कुजवारः;<BR>(3)<BR>अङ्गारकवारः, M. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tuft
TUFT:<BR>I Of hair:<BR>(1) चूडा;<BR>(2) शिखा। [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">Page724</a>]<BR>T. ed:<BR>(1) चूडाल (f. ला);<BR>(2) शिखिन् (f. नी),<BR>etc.<BR>II Of mangoes: पल्लवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tug
TUG:<BR>I Verb: कर्षति (कृष्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>pull.<BR>II A boat: पोतविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tuition
TUITION: शिक्षा: v. Instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tumble
TUMBLE (v. and subs.): v. Stumble, fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tumbler
TUMBLER:<BR>I A glass vessel: काचपात्रम्।<BR>II<BR>A pigeon: लोटनः।<BR>III A mountebank:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tumid
TUMID: स्फीत (f. ता): v. Inflated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tumour
TUMOUR: स्फोटः, -कः: v. Also swelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tumult
TUMULT:<BR>I Confusion: q. v.:<BR>(1) तुमुलम्;<BR>(2) सङ्कुलम्।<BR>II Uproar: कोलाहलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tumultuous
TUMULTUOUS:<BR>(1) तुमुल (f. ला);<BR>(2) सङ्कुल<BR>(f. ला);<BR>(3) क्षुब्ध (f. ब्धा = agitated);<BR>(4)<BR>विहस्त (f. स्ता = bewildered), R. v. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tumultuously
TUMULTUOUSLY:<BR>(1) तुमुलम्;<BR>(2) सङ्कुलम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tun
TUN: कृण्डम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tune
TUNE (subs.):<BR>I An air: रागः। Ph.: out of t.:<BR>विस्वर (f. रा); in t. (adv.): श्लिष्टस्वरम्।<BR>II<BR>Harmony, peace: q. v.: ऐक्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tune
TUNE: perh. सारयति (c. of सृ): comp.<BR>Bengali, Mr. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tuneful
TUNEFUL: सुस्वर (f. रा): v. Melodious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tuner
TUNER: perh. सारक (f. रिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tunic
TUNIC: चोलः, ली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tunnel
TUNNEL:<BR>(1) कुल्या;<BR>(2) सुरु(र)ङ्गा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turban
TURBAN:<BR>(1) उष्णीषम्;<BR>(2) शिरोवेष्टनम्;<BR>(3)<BR>शिरश्छदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turbid
TURBID:<BR>(1) कलुष (f. षा): v. Dirty;<BR>(2)<BR>पङ्किल (f. ला): v. Muddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turbot
TURBOT: *महाचन्द्रः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turbulence
TURBULENCE: संक्षोभः: v. Confusion, agita-<BR>-tion, disorder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turbulent
TURBULENT:<BR>I Tumultuous, agitated: संक्षुब्ध<BR>(f. ब्धा).<BR>II Not quiet: दुर्दान्त (f. न्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turf
TURF:<BR>I Subs.: शाद्वलम् (?).<BR>II Verb: शाद्वलेन<BR> चिनोति, (चि, c. 5.). (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turgid
TURGID: स्फीत (f. ता): v. Inflated, bom-<BR>-bastic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turgidity
TURGIDITY:<BR>(1) स्फीतता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turmeric
TURMERIC:<BR>(1) हरिद्रा;<BR>(2) काञ्चनी (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turmoil
TURMOIL: संक्षोमः: v. Agitation, disquiet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turn
TURN (subs.):<BR>I Revolution: q. v.: आवर्तः,<BR> -नम्<BR>or<BR>आवृत्तिः।<BR>II Bend, curve: वङ्कः।<BR>III<BR>Change, vicissitude: q. v.: परिवृत्तिः।<BR>IV<BR>Alternation: पर्यायः,<BR>by t. s, in t.:<BR>पर्यायेण or<BR>पर्याय- in comp., Ki. xvii. 18.<BR>V Successive<BR>course: वारः,<BR>one day a hare's t. came:<BR>अथ<BR> कदाचिच्छशकस्य वारः समायातः, H.<BR>VI Of mind:<BR>गतिः: v. Also inclination.<BR>VII Of ex-<BR>-pression: भङ्गिः(ङ्गी): v. Also form.<BR>VIII<BR>Of requital:<BR>good t.:<BR>उपकारः;<BR>ill t.:<BR>अपकारः।<BR>IX A short walk: परिक्रमः।<BR>X Course: q. v.:<BR>गतिः।<BR>XI Occasion, opportunity: अवसरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turn
TURN (v. t.):<BR>I To revolve, roll: q. v.: घूर्णयति<BR>(c. of घूर्ण्).<BR>II To change: q. v.: परि-<BR>वर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR>III To reverse: q. v.:<BR>विपर्यासयति (c. of अस).<BR>IV To adopt,<BR>divert, utilize: q. v.: to t. into good account:<BR>सफलीकरोतिः;<BR>to t. into ashes:<BR>भस्मीकरोति;<BR>to. t.<BR>into some use:<BR>उपयोजयति;<BR>to t. one's eyes:<BR>नेत्रं<BR> पातयति;<BR>to t. one's attention:<BR>अवधानं ददाति;<BR>to<BR>t. the back:<BR>पृष्ठं दर्शयति: v. To shape, form:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turn
TURN (v. i.):<BR>I To revolve, roll: q. v.:<BR>घूर्णते (घूर्ण, c. 1.).<BR>II To change: q. v.:<BR>(1) परिवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.); by भवति,<BR>to t. into<BR>red:<BR>रक्तीभवति।<BR>III To t. out: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turn about
TURN ABOUT: from side to side: पार्श्व परिवर्तनं<BR>or<BR>विवर्तनं करोति; by t. ing about in the bed:<BR>शय्योपान्तविवर्तनैः, Ta. vi. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turn against
TURN AGAINST:<BR>I प्रतीपयति (nomi.).<BR>II<BR>Intrans.: प्रतिकूलीभवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turn away
TURN AWAY:<BR>I To remove: q. v.: अपनयति<BR>(नी, c. 1.).<BR>II Drive out, dispel: q. v.:<BR>दूरीकरोति।<BR>III Intrans.: परांमुखीभवति, विमुखी-<BR>भवति; etc.,<BR>(although) she generally t. s away<BR>from me:<BR>कामं न तिष्ठति मदाननसम्मुखीयम्। Sa. i.<BR>32;<BR>when I look she t. s away:<BR>अभिमुखे मयि<BR> संहृतमीक्षितम्, Sa. ii. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turn back
TURN BACK:<BR>I Trans.: परावर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR>II Intrans.: परावर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turn down
TURN DOWN, TURN IN: v. To fold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turn off
TURN OFF:<BR>I Divert: विवर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR>II To dismiss, discharge: q. v.: दूरीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turn out
TURN OUT (v. i.):<BR>I To happen: q. v.:<BR>सम्पतति (पत्, c. 1.).<BR>II To become: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turn out
TURN OUT (v. t.):<BR>(1) बहिष्करोति (कृ, c. 8.),<BR>ordered to t. him out:<BR>तं बहिष्कर्तुमादिदेश, M. c.;<BR>(2) निःसारयति (c. of सृ): v. To drive out,<BR>expel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turn over
TURN OVER:<BR>I To upset, overturn: q. v.<BR>II Of pages: उत्क्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.),<BR>t. ing<BR>over the next leaf:<BR>अनन्तरं पत्रमुत्क्षिप्य, C. iii.<BR>III To transfer: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turn round
TURN ROUND: परि- वर्तते, परा-, वि- (वृत्, c. 1.),<BR>t. ing round and seeing the king:<BR>परिवृत्य राजनमव-<BR>लोक्य, Ve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turn to
TURN TO: i. e. to refer to: पश्यति (दृश्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turn towards
TURN TOWARDS: अभिमुखीमवति, सम्मुखीमवति, (with<BR>gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turn up
TURN UP:<BR>I To appear: आविर्भवति।<BR>II To<BR>occur: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turncoat
TURNCOAT: स्वपक्षत्यागिन् and sim. comp. s.: v.<BR>Also renegade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turner
TURNER: perh.<BR>(1) कौन्दिक (f. की);<BR>(2)<BR>कुन्दाजीवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turnip
TURNIP: no equiv.: शालगोमः (comp. Bengali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turpentine
TURPENTINE: prob. देवदारुस्नेहः, Sr.; श्रीवासः<BR>(Wilson).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turpitude
TURPITUDE: दुष्टताः v. Baseness, wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turret
TURRET:<BR>(1) तल्पः;<BR>(2) शिरोगृहम्;<BR>(3) प्रासाद-<BR>शृङ्गम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turtle
TURTLE:<BR>(1) कूर्मः;<BR>(2) कच्छपः;<BR>(3) कमठः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

turtle-dove
TURTLE-DOVE: कपोतविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tusk
TUSK:<BR>(1) दन्तः,<BR>t. ed:<BR>दन्तिन्<BR>or<BR>दन्ताबलः;<BR>(2)<BR>दंष्ट्रा (of lions etc).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tutelage
TUTELAGE: v. Minority, guardianship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tutelary
TUTELARY: t. deity.:<BR>(1) इष्टदेवता, अधिदेवता, U.<BR>or rarely: मनीषिता देवता, Ku. v. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tutenag
TUTENAG:<BR>(1) तुत्यम्, -कम्;<BR>(2) तुत्याञ्जनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tutor
TUTOR:<BR>I Subs.: गुरुः: v. Teacher.<BR>II<BR>Verb: शिक्षापयति (c. of शिक्ष्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tutorship
TUTORSHIP: expr. by tutor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twain
TWAIN: Ph.:<BR>in t.:<BR>द्विधा<BR>or<BR>द्वेधा: v. Two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twang
TWANG:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) टङ्कारः;<BR>(2) टङ्कृतम्: v.<BR>Noise, clang.<BR>II Verb: टङ्करोतिः v. To<BR>sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tweezers
TWEEZERS:<BR>(1) सन्दंशः (?);<BR>(2) कङ्कमुखम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twelfth
TWELFTH:<BR>I Adj.: द्वादशः (शी, शं).<BR>II Subs.:<BR>द्वादशांशः<BR>or<BR>द्वादशभागः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twelve
TWELVE: द्वादशन् (mfn.),<BR>t. hundred:<BR>द्वादशशतम्;<BR>t. thousand:<BR>द्वादशसहस्रम्;<BR>t. times:<BR>द्वादशकृत्वः;<BR>lasting t. years:<BR>द्वादशवार्षिकः (की, कं), U. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twelvemonth
TWELVEMONTH:<BR>for a t.:<BR>द्वादशभासान्, Vas.<BR>: v. Year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twentieth
TWENTIETH:<BR>(1) विंशः (शी, शं);<BR>(2) विंशतितमः<BR>(मी, मं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twenty
TWENTY: विंशतिः,<BR>with t. arrows:<BR>विंशत्या शरैः;<BR>three hundred and t.:<BR>शतत्रयं विंशतिश्च, Li. or<BR>gen.: विंशत्यधिकत्रिशतम्, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twice
TWICE:<BR>(1) द्विः;<BR>(2) द्विवारम्,<BR>T. born:<BR>द्विजः<BR>(जा, जं);<BR>t. ploughed:<BR>द्विगुणाकृतः (ता, तं);<BR>t. as<BR>valiant as he:<BR>तस्माद्विगुणपराक्रान्तः (न्ता, न्तं);<BR>t. a day:<BR>द्विरह्रः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twig
TWIG:<BR>(1) विटपः (= branch), “कोमलविटपानु-<BR>कारिणौ बाहू,” Sa. i. 21.;<BR>(2) प्रशाखा (= b. of<BR>a b.);<BR>(3) पल्लवः (= sprout).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twilight
TWILIGHT:<BR>(1) सन्ध्या (sp. of evening), Ki. ix.<BR>9.;<BR>morning t.:<BR>पूर्वसंध्या, Si. xi. 40.<BR>or<BR>प्रातः-<BR>सन्ध्या, M. n.;<BR>(2) उषस् (n. = dawn);<BR>(3)<BR>दिनमुखम् and sim. comp. s (= 2);<BR>(4) दिनान्तः<BR>and sim. comp. s. (= evening).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twin
TWIN:<BR>(1) यमः (मा, मं),<BR>these t. s:<BR>एतौ यमौ,<BR>Ki. i. 36.;<BR>(2) यमजः (जा, जं),<BR>we are t.<BR>brothers:<BR>भ्रातरावावां यमजौ, U.;<BR>(3) यमलः (ला, लं),<BR>The t. s (constellation): मिथुनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twine
TWINE (subs.): सूत्रम्: v. Thread, rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twine
TWINE (v.): v. To entwine, encircle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twinge
TWINGE:<BR>I Subs.: शूलम्: v. Pain.<BR>II<BR>Verb: expr. by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twinkle
TWINKLE (v.):<BR>I Of the eye: निमिषति (मिष्,<BR>c. 6.): v. To close, open; without t. ing:<BR>निर्निमेषम्।<BR>II To sparkle: स्फुरति (स्फुर्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twinkle
TWINKLE, TWINKLING (subs.):<BR>I Of the eye:<BR>निमेषः,<BR>in the t. of an eye:<BR>निमेषमात्रात्<BR>or<BR>-मात्रेण।<BR>II Sparkling: स्फुरितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twirl
TWIRL: v. Turn, roll, revolve, revolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twist
TWIST: मोटयति<BR>or<BR>मोट्टयति<BR>or<BR>मोडयति (मुट्, मुट्ट्,<BR> मुड्, c. 10.: Also = kill by t. ing the neck),<BR>Mr. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twist
TWIST, TWISTING (subs.): मोटनम्, मोडनम् or<BR>मुट्टनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twit
TWIT: उपालमते (लभ्, c. 1.): v. To reproach,<BR>revile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twitch
TWITCH: आकर्षति (कृष्, c. 1.): v. To pull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twitter
TWITTER: प्रजल्पति (जल्प्, c. 1.): v. To chatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

two
TWO: द्वि,<BR>t. -year old:<BR>द्विवर्ष (f. र्षा):<BR>in t.<BR>ways or parts:<BR>द्विधा<BR>or<BR>द्वेधा; of t. months:<BR>द्विमास्य (f. स्या); two-hundred and fifth:<BR>पञ्चाधिकद्विशततमः (मी, मं), Mah.;<BR>t. or three<BR>days:<BR>द्वित्राण्यहानि, R. v. 25.: v. Also both.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

two-fold
TWO-FOLD:<BR>(1) द्विगुण (f. णा);<BR>(2) द्विगुणितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

type
TYPE:<BR>I Model: आदर्शः।<BR>II Mark, stamp:<BR>q. v.: चिह्नम्।<BR>III Printing letters: मुद्राक्षरम्।<BR>IV Kind, species: q. v.: प्रकारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

typical
TYPICAL, -LY: expr. by comp. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

typify
TYPIFY: आदर्शयतिः v. To represent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

typographer
TYPOGRAPHER:<BR>(1) मुद्रयितृ, (f. त्री);<BR>(2)<BR>मुद्राङ्कयितृ (f. त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

typographical
TYPOGRAPHICAL: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

typography
TYPOGRAPHY:<BR>(1) मुद्राङ्कनम्;<BR>(2) मुद्राङ्कितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tyrannical
TYRANNICAL: expr. by comp.: v. Tyrant,<BR>tyranny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tyrannically
TYRANNICALLY:<BR>(1) निष्ठुरम् (= cruelly);<BR>(2)<BR>मर्दयत् (f. न्ती = crushing: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tyrannicide
TYRANNICIDE:<BR>I The act.: प्रजापीडकहत्या and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR>II The killer: प्रजापीडकघातिन्<BR>(f. नी) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tyrannize over
TYRANNIZE OVER:<BR>(1) निष्ठुरं शास्ति (शास्, c.<BR>2. = rule rigorously);<BR>(2) पीडयति (पीड्, c.<BR>10. = oppress: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tyranny
TYRANNY:<BR>(1) निष्ठुरशासनम् (= cruel govern-<BR>-ment);<BR>(2) प्रजापीडनम्, जनमर्दनम्, लोकमर्दनम्,<BR>and sim. comp. s (= oppression of people).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tyrant
TYRANT:<BR>I A monarch: अधीश्वरः।<BR>II<BR>Oppressor: q. v.:<BR>(1) प्रजापीडक (f. डिका);<BR>(2) लोकोपप्लावक (f. विका), and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tyro
TYRO: v. Novice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ubiquitous
UBIQUITOUS:<BR>(1) सर्वव्यापिन् (f. नी) (= all-<BR>-pervading);<BR>(2) सर्वगतः (ता, तं), Ku. v. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ubiquity
UBIQUITY: सर्वगतत्वम्: v. Omnipresence etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

udder
UDDER:<BR>(1) ऊ(उ)धस् (n.), with large u. s:<BR>पीनोध्न (f. ध्नी);<BR>(2) आपीनम्;<BR>(3) स्तनः (gen.<BR>human).<BR>“U. less lambs”:<BR>स्तन्यहीना मेषशावाः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ugliness
UGLINESS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) वैरूप्यम्,<BR>with super-<BR>fluous u.:<BR>वैरूप्यपौनरुक्तयेन, R. xii. 40.;<BR>(2)<BR>कुरूपता;<BR>(3) कदाकारता;<BR>(4) अनभिरूपता;<BR>(5)<BR>विकृतता।<BR>II Badness: कुत्सितता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ugly
UGLY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) कदाकार (f. रा);<BR>(2)<BR>कुरूप (f. पा);<BR>(3) विरूप (f. पा): v.<BR>Deformed.<BR>II Bad: q. v.: कुत्सित (f. ता);<BR>u. wound:<BR>कुत्सितं व्रणम्, (comp. Bengali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ulcer
ULCER:<BR>(1) पूयव्रणम्;<BR>(2) विद्रधिः (= abscess);<BR>(3) नाडीव्रणम् (a deep u.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ulcerate
ULCERATE, ULCERATION: expr. with ulcer,<BR>-ated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ulcerated
ULCERATED, ULCEROUS:<BR>(1) पूयव्रणिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) पूयव्रणोपहत (f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ulterior
ULTERIOR: उत्तर (f. रा = succeeding): v.<BR>Also remote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ultimate
ULTIMATE: चरम (f. मा): v. Last, final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ultimately
ULTIMATELY: अन्ततः: v. Lastly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ultimatum
ULTIMATUM: चरमाभिसन्धिः, and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ultra
ULTRA:<BR>I = excessive: अति- in comp.,<BR>u.-<BR>democrat:<BR>अतिप्रजातन्त्रिन् (f. णी).<BR>II Beyond:<BR>पार- in comp.,<BR>u. marine:<BR>समुद्रपारीण (f. णा);<BR>u. montane:<BR>पर्वतपारीण (f. णा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

umbel
UMBEL, UMBELLA: *प्रततसवकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

umbilical
UMBILICAL:<BR>(1) नाभि- in comp., u. cord:<BR>नाभिनालम्, R. v. 7.;<BR>(2) नाभ्य (f. भ्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

umbrage
UMBRAGE:<BR>I Lit.: छाया।<BR>II Resentment:<BR>q. v.: असन्तोषः। Ph.:<BR>to take u.:<BR>कुप्यति (कुप्,<BR>c. 4.);<BR>to give u.:<BR>विरञ्जयति (रञ्ज्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

umbrella
UMBRELLA:<BR>(1) छत्रम् (state)<BR>or<BR>छत्रा (common),<BR>an u. of peacock's tail:<BR>मयूरपिच्छमयी छत्रिका, K.<BR>ii.;<BR>(2) आतपत्रम्;<BR>(3) घर्मवारणम्, Ku. xiv. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

umpire
UMPIRE:<BR>(1) मव्यस्थ (f. स्था);<BR>(2) मध्यम (f. मा),<BR>R. xiii. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

un
UN:<BR>(1) अ- (अन्- before vowels) in comp.;<BR>(2) निर्- in comp.;<BR>(3) वि- in comp. (rare):<BR>v. Also devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unabashed
UNABASHED:<BR>(1) निह्रीकः (का, कं);<BR>(2) निर्ल्लज्ज<BR>(f. ज्जा): v. Also shameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unabated
UNABATED: अक्षीण (f. णा): v. Undiminished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unable
UNABLE:<BR>(1) अशक्त (f. क्ता);<BR>(2) असमर्थ (f.<BR>र्था);<BR>(3) अक्षमः (मा, मं);<BR>(4) अनीश (f. शा):<BR>v. Able, can.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unaccented
UNACCENTED: अनुदात्त (f. त्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unacceptable
UNACCEPTABLE:<BR>(1) अग्राह्य (f. ह्या);<BR>(2) अपरि-<BR>ग्राह्य (f. ह्या);<BR>(3) अप्रतिग्राह्य, (f. ह्या);<BR>(4)<BR>अग्रहणीय (f. या); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unaccompanied
UNACCOMPANIED:<BR>(1) असहाय (f. या);<BR>(2)<BR>अद्वितीय (f. या): v. Alone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unaccomplished
UNACCOMPLISHED:<BR>(1) अनिष्पन्न (f. न्ना);<BR>(2)<BR>असमाहित (f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unaccountable
UNACCOUNTABLE:<BR>I Inexplicable: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Irresponsible: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unaccustomed
UNACCUSTOMED:<BR>(1) अपरिचित (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>अनभिज्ञ (f. ज्ञा = unacquainted);<BR>(3) अननुभूत<BR>(f. ता = unfelt),<BR>u. to ornaments:<BR>अननुभुतभुषण<BR>(f. णा), Sa. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unacknowledged
UNACKNOWLEDGED:<BR>(1) अप्रतिपन्न (f. न्ना);<BR>(2)<BR>अनम्युपेत (f. ता), etc.: v. To acknow-<BR>-ledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unacquainted
UNACQUAINTED:<BR>(1) अनभिज्ञ (f. ज्ञा): v.<BR>Acquainted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unactionable
UNACTIONABLE:<BR>(1) अव्यवहार्य (f. र्या);<BR>(2)<BR>व्यवहारायोग्य (f. ग्या), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unadorned
UNADORNED: अनलङ्कृत (f. ता): v. Adorn,<BR>ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unadulterated
UNADULTERATED:<BR>(1) असंमिश्र (f. श्रा);<BR>(2)<BR>विशुद्ध (f. द्धा = pure).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unadvised
UNADVISED: expr. by part. s असमीक्ष्य<BR>or<BR>अविविच्य।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unaffected
UNAFFECTED:<BR>I Unmoved: निर्दय (f. या):<BR>v. Hard, unkind.<BR>II Unfeigned, sincere:<BR>q. v.: अकृत्रिम (f. मा).<BR>III Not influenced:<BR>(1) अनभिभूत (f. ता);<BR>(2) अस्पृष्ट (f. ष्टा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unaffectedly
UNAFFECTEDLY:<BR>(1) अमायया;<BR>(2) अवैलक्ष्येण:<BR>v. Sincerely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unaided
UNAIDED:<BR>(1) असहाय (f. या);<BR>(2) निःसहाय<BR>(f. या);<BR>(3) साहाय्यहीन (f. ना); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unalienable
UNALIENABLE:<BR>(1) अविश्लेष्य (f. ष्या);<BR>(2)<BR>निर्विघटनीय (f. या);<BR>(3) अहार्य (f. र्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unalloyed
UNALLOYED:<BR>(1) असंमिश्र (f. श्रा = unmixed);<BR>(2) शुद्ध (f. द्धा), वि- (= pure: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unalterable
UNALTERABLE:<BR>(1) अविकार्य (f. र्या = immov-<BR>able);<BR>(2) अहार्य (f. र्या = immovable): v.<BR>Constant, fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unambiguous
UNAMBIGUOUS: असन्दिग्ध (f. ग्धा): v. Un-<BR>-doubted, clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unamiable
UNAMIABLE: अप्रिय (f. या): v. Amiable,<BR>pleasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unanimity
UNANIMITY:<BR>(1) ऐकमत्यम्;<BR>(2) एकचित्तता;<BR>(3)<BR>ऐक्यम् (= unity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unanimous
UNANIMOUS:<BR>(1) एकमत (f. ता);<BR>(2) एकचित्त<BR>(f. त्ता);<BR>(3) by subs.,<BR>about this the Śāstras<BR>are u.:<BR>शास्त्राणामत्रैकमत्यम्। H. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unanimously
UNANIMOUSLY:<BR>(1) एकचित्तीभूय;<BR>(2) ऐकमत्येन;<BR>(3) by circumlo.,<BR>u. cried out:<BR>एकवाक्यं विवव्रुः<BR>R. vi. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unanswerable
UNANSWERABLE:<BR>I Irrefutable: निरुत्तर (f. रा).<BR>II Not responsible: अदायिन् (f. नी), (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unappalled
UNAPPALLED: अपभयः (या, यं): v. Undaunt-<BR>-ed, fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unappeased
UNAPPEASED: अप्रसन्न (f. न्ना): v. To appease,<BR>satisfy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unapproachable
UNAPPROACHABLE:<BR>I Lit.: अगम्य (f. म्या):<BR>v. Inaccessible.<BR>II Fig.: दुरुपगम्य (f. म्या):<BR>v. Also unrivalled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unapt
UNAPT:<BR>(1) अयोग्य (f. ग्या): v. Unsuitable;<BR>अकुशल (f. ला): v. Unskilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unaptly
UNAPTLY:<BR>(1) अकुशलम्;<BR>(2) अदक्षम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unarmed
UNARMED: अशस्त्र (f. स्त्रा);<BR>(2) निरायुध (f. धा);<BR>(3) विशस्त्र (f. स्त्रा), and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unasked
UNASKED:<BR>(1) अपृष्ट (f. ष्टा);<BR>(2) अयाचित (f.<BR>ता): v. To ask.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unaspirated
UNASPIRATED: अल्पप्राण (f. णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unaspiring
UNASPIRING (adj.):<BR>(1) निराकाङ्क्ष (f. ङ्क्षा);<BR>(2)<BR>निःस्पृह (f. हा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unassailable
UNASSAILABLE:<BR>(1) अधृष्य (f. ष्या), Ku. iii.<BR>51.;<BR>(2) दुष्प्रधर्ष (f. र्षा), R. ii. 27. and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unassisted
UNASSISTED: v. Unaided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unassuming
UNASSUMING: नम्र (f. म्रा): v. Humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unassumingly
UNASSUMINGLY:<BR>(1) by adj.;<BR>(2) नम्रीभूय;<BR>(3) विनीतवत्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unassured
UNASSURED:<BR>I Adj.: अनिश्चित (f. ता): v.<BR>Uncertain.<BR>II Adv.:<BR>(1) अनिश्चित्य;<BR>(2)<BR>अविज्ञाय।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unattainable
UNATTAINABLE:<BR>(1) दुष्प्राप्य (f. प्या);<BR>(2)<BR>अलम्य (f. भ्या);<BR>(3) दुरासद (f. दा); etc.:<BR>v. To attain, get.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unattended
UNATTENDED:<BR>(1) असहाय (f. या);<BR>(2) असहायिन्<BR>(f. नी): v. Also alone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unattested
UNATTESTED:<BR>(1) by circumlo.: v. To attest;<BR>(2) अप्रमाणित (f. ता = unauthenticated).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unauthenticated
UNAUTHENTICATED:<BR>(1) अप्रमाणित (f. ता);<BR>(2) अप्रामाणिक (f. की); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unauthorized
UNAUTHORIZED:<BR>(1) अनियुक्त (f. क्ता);<BR>(2)<BR>निरनुमत (f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unavailable
UNAVAILABLE: v. Unattainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unavailing
UNAVAILING (adj.): निष्फल (f. ला): v.<BR>Ineffectual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unavoidable
UNAVOIDABLE:<BR>(1) अनतिक्रमणीय (f. या);<BR>(2)<BR>अपरिहार्य (f. र्या); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unawares
UNAWARES:<BR>(1) अतर्कितम्;<BR>(2) अलक्षितम्: v.<BR>Also suddenly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbaked
UNBAKED:<BR>(1) अपक्व (f. क्वा);<BR>(2) आम (f.<BR>मा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbar
UNBAR:<BR>(1) निरर्गलयति (nomi.): v. Bar, to<BR>remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbearable
UNBEARABLE: असह्य (f. ह्या): v. Intolerable,<BR>insufferable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbecoming
UNBECOMING:<BR>(1) अविनीत (f. ता = indecor-<BR>-ous);<BR>(2) अनुचित (f. ता = improper).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbelief
UNBELIEF: अविश्वासः: v. Disbelief, infidelity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbeliever
UNBELIEVER, UNBELIEVING: v. Disbelieving,<BR>infidel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbend
UNBEND:<BR>I Lit.: सरलीकरोति।<BR>II To relax:<BR>शिथिलयति (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbending
UNBENDING (adj.): दुरानम्य (f. म्या): v. Also<BR>hard, cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbiassed
UNBIASSED: अनावर्जित (f. ता): v. Impartial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbidden
UNBIDDEN:<BR>(1) अचोदित (f. ता);<BR>(2) अनाज्ञप्त<BR>(f. प्ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbind
UNBIND: मोचयति (मुच्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>loosen, free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unblamable
UNBLAMABLE, UNBLAMED: अनिन्द्य (f. न्द्या):<BR>v. Blameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbleached
UNBLEACHED:<BR>u. cloth:<BR>निष्प्रवाणिः<BR>or<BR>निष्प्रवाणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unblemished
UNBLEMISHED: निष्कलङ्क (f. ङ्का);<BR>(2) निर्मल (f.<BR>ला);<BR>(3) निर्दोष (f. षा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unblest
UNBLEST: विश्लिष्टभागधेय (f. या): v. Unfor-<BR>-tunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unblushing
UNBLUSHING (adj.): निर्लज्ज (f. ज्जा): v. Sha-<BR>-meless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbolt
UNBOLT: निरर्गलयति (nomi.): v. Bolt, re-<BR>-move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unborn
UNBORN: अजात (f. ता): v. Born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbosom
UNBOSOM:<BR>to u. one's self:<BR>हृदयं विवृणोति (वृ, c.<BR>5.): v. Disclose, reveal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbounded
UNBOUNDED:<BR>(1) असीम (f. मा);<BR>(2) निरवधि<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(3) अनन्त (f. न्ता = endless).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbridled
UNBRIDLED:<BR>(1) अनियन्त्रित (f. ता);<BR>(2) उद्दाम<BR>(f. मा): Unrestrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbroken
UNBROKEN:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अभग्न (f. ग्ना);<BR>(2)<BR>अभिन्न (f. न्ना);<BR>(3) अखण्डित (f. ता).<BR>II Not<BR>trained:<BR>(1) अशिक्षित (f. ता);<BR>(2) अविनीत<BR>(f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbruised
UNBRUISED:<BR>(1) अक्षत (f. ता);<BR>(2) अपरिक्षत<BR>(f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unburden
UNBURDEN: भारमपनयति (नी, c. 1.): v. To<BR>remove<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unburnt
UNBURNT:<BR>I Lit.: अदग्ध (f. ग्धा), etc.<BR>II<BR>Unbaked: अपक्व (f. क्वा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unbutton
UNBUTTON: *निर्बुदामयति (nomi.), अपबुदामीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncalled for
UNCALLED FOR (adj.):<BR>(1) अनाहूत (f. ता (?);<BR>(2) निरर्थक (f. र्थिका = needless).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unceasing
UNCEASING: अविरत (f. ता): v. Incessant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unceasingly
UNCEASINGLY: अश्रान्तम्ः v. Incessantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncensured
UNCENSURED: अनिन्दित (f. ता): v. To censure,<BR>blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unceremonious
UNCEREMONIOUS:<BR>(1) मन्दादर (f. रा);<BR>(2)<BR>अनादत (f. रा);<BR>(3) by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncertain
UNCERTAIN:<BR>(1) अनिश्चित (f. ता);<BR>(2) सन्दिग्ध<BR>(f. ग्धा = doubtful).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncertainty
UNCERTAINTY:<BR>I The state:<BR>(1) अनिश्चयः;<BR>(2) संशयः (= doubt).<BR>II Anything uncer-<BR>-tain:<BR>(1) अध्रुवम्;<BR>(2) अनिश्चितम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unchain
UNCHAIN: अपनिगडयति (nomi.): v. Chain,<BR>remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unchangeable
UNCHANGEABLE:<BR>(1) अपरिवर्तनीय (f. या);<BR>(2)<BR>अपरिवर्त्य (f. र्त्या): v. Immutable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unchangeably
UNCHANGEABLY:<BR>(1) स्थिरम् (= firmly);<BR>(2)<BR>निश्चितम् (= certainly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncharitable
UNCHARITABLE: अनुदार (f. रा): v. Harsh,<BR>censorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncharitably
UNCHARITABLY: अनुदारम्: v. Harshly, un-<BR>-mercifully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unchaste
UNCHASTE:<BR>(1) असत् (f. ती in morals);<BR>(2)<BR>अशुचि (mfn. = impure).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unchecked
UNCHECKED:<BR>(1) अनियन्त्रित (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>निरवग्रह (f. हा);<BR>(3) निरर्गल (f. ला); etc.<BR>N. B. Use n. for adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncircumcised
UNCIRCUMCISED: अच्छिन्नत्वच् (mfn.) (?) and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncivil
UNCIVIL:<BR>(1) असभ्य (f. भ्या);<BR>(2) अशिष्ट<BR>(f. ष्टा);<BR>(3) अविनीत (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncivilized
UNCIVILIZED:<BR>(1) असभ्य (f. भ्या);<BR>(2) वर्वर<BR>(f. रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncle
UNCLE:<BR>I Paternal:<BR>(1) पितृव्यः;<BR>(2) ज्येष्ठ-<BR>तातः (father's elder brother);<BR>(3) कनिष्ठतातः<BR>(f.'s younger b.), Vi.;<BR>(4) खु(क्षु)ल्लतातः। (= 3).<BR>II Maternal: मातुलः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unclean
UNCLEAN:<BR>(1) अशुद्ध (f. द्धा);<BR>(2) अशुचि<BR>(mfn.): v. Clean, dirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncleanness
UNCLEANNESS:<BR>(1) अशुचित्वम्, -ता;<BR>(2) अशुद्धता<BR> -त्वम्: v. Also dirtiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unclose
UNCLOSE: विवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.): v. To<BR>open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unclothe
UNCLOTHE: बिवस्त्रयति (nomi.),<BR>u. d:<BR>विवस्त्र<BR>(f. स्त्रा): v. Naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unclouded
UNCLOUDED:<BR>(1) निरभ्र (f. भ्रा);<BR>(2) व्यभ्र<BR>(f. भ्रा);<BR>(3) अपमेघ (f. घा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncloven
UNCLOVEN:<BR>u.-hoofed:<BR>एकशफ (f. फा)<BR>or<BR>एकखुर<BR>(f. रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncomely
UNCOMELY:<BR>(1) विरूप (f. पा): v. Ugly;<BR>(2)<BR>अनभिमत (f. ता): v. Unpleasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncomfortable
UNCOMFORTABLE: perh. असुख (f. खा): v.<BR>Comfortable, pleasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncomfortably
UNCOMFORTABLY: असुखेन<BR>or<BR>असुखम्<BR>or<BR>अपसुखम्<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncommon
UNCOMMON:<BR>(1) असामान्य (f. न्या);<BR>(2)<BR>असाधारण (f. णी);<BR>(3) अपूर्व (f. र्वा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncommonly
UNCOMMONLY:<BR>(1) by circumlo.;<BR>(2) अत्यन्तम्<BR>(= exceedingly: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncompounded
UNCOMPOUNDED:<BR>(1) अमिश्र (f. श्रा = unmixed);<BR>(2) अयुक्त (f. क्ता = not joined).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unconcern
UNCONCERN: expr. with चिन्ता (= care) or<BR>आदरः (= attention)<BR>or<BR>अवेक्षा (= inspection).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unconcerned
UNCONCERNED:<BR>(1) वीतादर (f. रा);<BR>(2)<BR>अनादर (f. रा): v. Indifferent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unconditional
UNCONDITIONAL:<BR>(1) अनिबद्ध (f. द्धा);<BR>(2)<BR>अनियमित (f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unconformable
UNCONFORMABLE: विसंवादिन् (f. नी): v. Con-<BR>-formable, agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncongenial
UNCONGENIAL:<BR>(1) प्रतिकूल (f. ला = unfavour-<BR>-able).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unconnected
UNCONNECTED:<BR>(1) असंबद्ध (f. द्धा);<BR>(2)<BR>असम्बन्ध (f. न्धा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unconquerable
UNCONQUERABLE:<BR>(1) अजेय (f. या);<BR>(2) अजय्य<BR>(f. य्या);<BR>(3) अविजेय (f. या); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unconquerd
UNCONQUERD:<BR>(1) अजित (f. ता);<BR>(2) अविजित<BR>(f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unconscionable
UNCONSCIONABLE: v. Unreasonable, enor-<BR>-mous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unconscious
UNCONSCIOUS:<BR>I Insensible:<BR>(1) अचेतन (f.<BR>ना);<BR>(2) विसंज्ञ (f. ज्ञा);<BR>(3) विगतचेतन (f.<BR>ना).<BR>II Not sensible, aware: expr. by<BR>verb: न चेतयति (c. of चित्)<BR>or<BR>जानाति (ज्ञा,<BR>c. 9. = know: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unconsciously
UNCONSCIOUSLY:<BR>(1) अजानत् (f. ती = not know-<BR>-ing);<BR>(2) अज्ञानतः (= unknowingly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unconsciousness
UNCONSCIOUSNESS:<BR>I Insensibility: अचैतन्यम्।<BR>II Not knowing: expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unconsecrated
UNCONSECRATED:<BR>(1) अप्रतिष्ठित (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>अप्रणीत (f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncontaminated
UNCONTAMINATED:<BR>(1) अद्वषित (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>अस्पृष्ट (f. ष्टा = untouched).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncontested
UNCONTESTED: निर्विवाद (f. दा): v. Undis-<BR>-puted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncontrollable
UNCONTROLLABLE:<BR>(1) अतिग्रहणीय (f. या);<BR>(2) असंयम्य (f. म्या);<BR>(3) अनियन्त्रणीय<BR>(f. या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncontrolled
UNCONTROLLED:<BR>(1) अनियन्त्रित (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>असंयत (f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncouple
UNCOUPLE:<BR>(1) विघटयति (घट्, c. 10.);<BR>(2)<BR>वियोजयति (युज्, c. 10. = disjoin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncourteous
UNCOURTEOUS:<BR>(1) अदक्षिण (f. णा);<BR>(2) अविनीत<BR>(f. ता);<BR>(3) असभ्य (f. म्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncouth
UNCOUTH: विरूप (f. पा): v. Odd, strange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncover
UNCOVER: अपावृणोति (वृ, c. 5.): v. Divest,<BR>strip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncovered
UNCOVERED:<BR>(1) अनावृत (f. ता); (?) अनाच्छादित<BR>(f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncreated
UNCREATED: असृष्ट (f. ष्टा): v. To create.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unction
UNCTION:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अञ्जनम्, अभि-;<BR>(2)<BR>आलेपः, -नम्;<BR>(3) विलेपः, -नम्।<BR>II Fig. as in<BR>address: स्निग्धता<BR>or<BR>स्नैग्ध्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unctuous
UNCTUOUS:<BR>(1) स्निग्ध (f. ग्धा);<BR>(2) चिङ्कण (f.<BR>णा);<BR>(3) मसृण (f. णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncultivated
UNCULTIVATED:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) खिल (f. ला =<BR>waste);<BR>(2) अप्रतिहत (f. ता).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) असंस्कृत (f. ता);<BR>(2) अविनीत (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uncurbed
UNCURBED: निरवग्रह (f. हा): v. Unchecked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undaunted
UNDAUNTED: निर्भीक (f. का): v. Fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undauntedly
UNDAUNTEDLY: expr. by adj.: v. Fearlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undecayed
UNDECAYED:<BR>(1) अक्षीण (f. णा);<BR>(2) अशीर्ण<BR>(f. र्णा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undecaying
UNDECAYING:<BR>(1) अक्षय (f. या);<BR>(2) अक्षय्य<BR>(f. य्या): v. Imperishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undeceive
UNDECEIVE: भ्रमं निरस्यतिः v. Mistake, to<BR>remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undecided
UNDECIDED: अनिश्चित (f. ता): v. To decide,<BR>doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undecked
UNDECKED:<BR>(1) अमण्डित (f. ता);<BR>(2) अभूषित<BR>(f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undefended
UNDEFENDED: of cases: अविप्रतिपन्न (f. न्ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undefiled
UNDEFILED:<BR>(1) अदूषित (f. ता);<BR>(2) अक्षत<BR>(f. ता): v. Also pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undefinable
UNDEFINABLE: अनिर्वचनीय (f. या): v. To<BR>define.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undeniable
UNDENIABLE: प्रत्याख्येय (f. या): v. To deny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undeniably
UNDENIABLY:<BR>(1) निर्विवादम् (= indisputedly);<BR>(2) निःसन्देहम् (= undoubtedly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

under
UNDER (adj.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अधर (f. रा);<BR>(2)<BR>अधस्- in comp.;<BR>u. current:<BR>अधःप्रवाहः;<BR>u. -<BR>garment:<BR>अधोंशुकम्।<BR>II Subordinate: q. v.:<BR>u. teacher:<BR>अनुशिक्षकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

under
UNDER (prep.):<BR>I Below, beneath: q. v.:<BR>तले (with gen.). Ph.:<BR>u. one's hand:<BR>हस्ततल-<BR>गत (f. ता), Mu. iii.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>u. this pre-<BR>text:<BR>अनेन व्यपदेशेन: v. With;<BR>groaning u.<BR>pain:<BR>पीडार्त (f. र्ता), V. p. v. l. 26.; u.<BR>misfortunes:<BR>विपदिः v. in:<BR>u. act nine:<BR>नवम-<BR>विध्यनुसारेण।<BR>III = less than: ऊन- in comp.,<BR>and boys u. sixteen:<BR>बालो वाय्यूनषोडशः, Ap.;<BR>for those who are u. eleven years of age:<BR>न्यूनैकादशवर्षस्य, Ap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

underage
UNDERAGE (adj.): अप्राप्तवयस्क (f. स्का) and<BR>sim. comp. s.: v. Minor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

underdone
UNDERDONE: असम्यकसिद्ध (f. द्धा): v. To do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undergo
UNDERGO:<BR>(1) अनुमवति: v. To suffer;<BR>(2)<BR>अधिगच्छतिः v. To get, become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

underground
UNDERGROUND (adj.): अन्तर्मौम (f. मी). Ph.:<BR>u. building:<BR>भूमिगृहम्, D. iv.;<BR>u. passage:<BR>सुरङ्गम्,<BR> -ङ्गा, D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

underhand
UNDERHAND:<BR>(1) परोक्षे (= in the back);<BR>(2)<BR>गूढम् (= secretly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

underlie
UNDERLIE: लीयते (ली, c. 4.),<BR>meaning u. ing<BR>and not clear:<BR>अर्था लीना अनिर्मलाः, Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

underline
UNDERLINE: अधो रेखयति (nomi.)<BR>or<BR>रेखया अङ्कयति<BR>(अङ्क्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

underling
UNDERLING: अनुजीविन् (f. नी): v. Depen-<BR>-dant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undermine
UNDERMINE:<BR>I Lit.: सुरङ्गां करोति।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>गूढं नाशयति (c. of नश्): v. To destroy,<BR>infuse, secretly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undermost
UNDERMOST: अधस्तम (f. मा);<BR>(2) नीचैस्तम (f.<BR>मा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

underneath
UNDERNEATH: अधस्: v. Below, beneath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

underrate
UNDERRATE:<BR>I lit.: v. To undervalue.<BR>II<BR>Fig.: लघु मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.): v. To con-<BR>-sider, estimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undersong
UNDERSONG: v. Chorus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

understand
UNDERSTAND:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) बुध्यते (बुध्,<BR>c. 4.),<BR>did (he) u. it to be a golden lotus:<BR>अबुद्ध<BR> तं काञ्चनमम्बुजन्म किम्, N. i. 122.; then made<BR>him u. (i. e. informed): अथैनं प्रत्यबोधयत्, R. i.<BR>74.;<BR>u. (i. e. learn) this from me:<BR>मत्सकाशान्नि-<BR>बोधत, M. i. 119.;<BR>(2) अवगच्छति (गम्, c. 1.),<BR>foolish men u. the loss of friend as thorns put in<BR>the heart:<BR>अवगच्छति मूढचेतनः प्रियनाशं हृदि शल्य-<BR>मर्पितम्, R. viii. 38.;<BR>(3) अवैति (इ, c. 2.):<BR>v. To know;<BR>(4) गृह्नाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.): v.<BR>To comprehend;<BR>(5) उपलभते (लभ्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To perceive.<BR>II To imply; here the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">Page731</a>]<BR>nominative is understood:<BR>अत्र कर्तोह्यः;<BR>open or<BR>understood:<BR>प्रकाशः सूचितो वा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

understanding
UNDERSTANDING (subs.):<BR>I Intellect: q. v.:<BR>बुद्धिः।<BR>II Feeling, harmony: good u.:<BR>सद्भावः;<BR>to come to an u.:<BR>ऐक्यमुपगच्छति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undertake
UNDERTAKE:<BR>I To begin: q. v.: आरभते (रभ्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR>II To attempt: q. v.: व्यवसयति (सी,<BR>c. 4.).<BR>III Accept: q. v.: अङ्गीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undertaker
UNDERTAKER:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) अनुष्ठातृ (f. त्री =<BR>performer);<BR>(2) आरब्धृ- (f. ब्ध्री = beginner).<BR>II Of funerals: प्रेतकर्मनिर्हारक (f. रिका) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undertaking
UNDERTAKING:<BR>(1) कर्मन् (n.): v. Work;<BR>(2)<BR>व्यवसायः: v. Attempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undervalue
UNDERVALUE:<BR>I Lit.: न्यूनमूल्यं कल्पयति (c.<BR>of कॢप्).<BR>II Fig.; लधु मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.):<BR>v. Also despise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undeserved
UNDESERVED, -LY: expr. by circumlo.: v.<BR>To deserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undeserving
UNDESERVING (adj.): अनर्ह (f. र्हा): v. Un-<BR>-worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undesignedly
UNDESIGNEDLY:<BR>(1) असंकल्य्य;<BR>(2) अज्ञानतः<BR>(= unknowingly);<BR>(3) अकामतः (= uninten-<BR>-tionally).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undesigning
UNDESIGNING: निष्कपट (f. टा): v. Artless,<BR>sincere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undesirable
UNDESIRABLE:<BR>(1) अनाकांक्ष्य (f. क्ष्या);<BR>(2)<BR>न वाञ्छनीय (f. या); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undeviating
UNDEVIATING (adj.):<BR>(1) अव्यभिचारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) अविचलित (f. ता): v. Steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undigested
UNDIGESTED:<BR>I Lit.: अजीर्ण (f. र्णा).<BR>II<BR>Fig.: perh.: अविन्यस्त (f. स्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undiminished
UNDIMINISHED:<BR>(1) अक्षीण (f. णा);<BR>(2) अनपचित<BR>(f. ता);<BR>(3) अजातह्रास (f. सा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undisciplined
UNDISCIPLINED:<BR>(1) अशासित (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>अविनीत (f. ता = untrained).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undisguised
UNDISGUISED:<BR>(1) निश्छद्मन् (mfn.);<BR>(2) निर्व्याज<BR>(f. जा);<BR>(3) अमाय (f. या), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undisputed
UNDISPUTED:<BR>(1) निर्विवाद (f. दा);<BR>(2)<BR>अविप्रतिपन्न (f. न्ना); अविवदित (f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undisturbed
UNDISTURBED:<BR>(1) अक्षुब्ध (f. ब्धा);<BR>(2) निरा-<BR>कुल (f. ला);<BR>(3) निरुद्वेग (f. गा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undivided
UNDIVIDED:<BR>(1) अखण्डित (f. ता);<BR>(2) अविभक्त<BR>(f. क्ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undo
UNDO:<BR>I To unite: उन्मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.).<BR>II Ruin, destroy: q. v.: हन्ति, उप- (हन्,<BR>c. 2.).<BR>III To reverse, annul: q. v.:<BR>परावर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undone
UNDONE:<BR>I Lit.: अकृत (f. ता).<BR>II Ruined,<BR>done for:<BR>(1) हत (f. ता), alas! I am u.:<BR>हा हतोऽस्मि, K.<BR>III Reversed: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>परिवर्तित (f. ता);<BR>(2) खण्डित (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undoubted
UNDOUBTED:<BR>(1) असन्दिग्ध (ग्धा, ग्धं);<BR>(2)<BR>निःसन्देहः (हा, हं);<BR>(3) निःसंशयः (या, यं);<BR>(4)<BR>असंशयः (या, यं);<BR>(5) अविमृष्य (ष्याः ष्यं): v.<BR>Certain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undoubtedly
UNDOUBTEDLY: असंशयम्;<BR>(2) निःसंशयम्;<BR>(3)<BR>निःसन्देहम्;<BR>(4) असन्दिग्धम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undraw
UNDRAW: अपसारयति (c. of सृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undress
UNDRESS (v.): वस्त्रं<BR>or<BR>वासः अपनयति (नी, c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>अवतारयति (c. of तॄ)<BR>or<BR>उन्मुञ्चति (मुच्, c.<BR>6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undress
UNDRESS (subs.): perh. लघुवासस् (n.) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undressed
UNDRESSED: of food:<BR>(1) असंस्कृत (f. ता);<BR>(2) अनुपस्कृत (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undue
UNDUE: अनुचित (f. ता): v. Improper, un-<BR>-worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undulate
UNDULATE:<BR>(1) तरङ्गायते (nomi. = wavy);<BR>(2)<BR>expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undulating
UNDULATING, UNDULATORY:<BR>(1) भङ्गुर (f. रा<BR>= curling);<BR>(2) उन्नतावनत (f. ता = high and<BR>low); ऊर्मिमत् (f. ती = wavy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undulation
UNDULATION:<BR>(1) भङ्गुरता;<BR>(2) उच्चनीचता;<BR>(3)<BR>ऊर्मिमत्ता<BR>or<BR>त्त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unduly
UNDULY:<BR>(1) अनुचितम्: v. Improperly;<BR>(2)<BR>अतिरिक्तम्: v. Exceedingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undutiful
UNDUTIFUL: अमक्त (f. क्ता): v. Dutiful,<BR>disobedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

undying
UNDYING: अमरः (रा, रं): v. Deathless, un-<BR>-fading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unearth
UNEARTH: उत्खनति (खन्, c. 1.): v. To dig<BR>up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unearthly
UNEARTHLY:<BR>(1) अपार्थिव (f. वी), R. vii. 34.:<BR>v. Earthly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uneasiness
UNEASINESS:<BR>(1) असुखम्;<BR>(2) अनिर्वृतिः;<BR>(3)<BR>कष्टम्: v. Distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uneasy
UNEASY:<BR>(1) अनिर्वृत (f. ता);<BR>(2) असुखिन् (f.<BR>नी);<BR>(3) उत्कण्ठित (f. ता = anxious).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uneducated
UNEDUCATED: अशिक्षित (f. ता): v. Ignorant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unembarrassed
UNEMBARRASSED:<BR>(1) अनाकुलित (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>अबाधित (f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unemployed
UNEMPLOYED: अव्यापृत (f. ता);<BR>(2) निर्व्यापार<BR>(f. रा);<BR>(3) निष्कर्मन् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unencumbered
UNENCUMBERED: perh. अबन्ध (f. न्धा)<BR>or<BR>अग्रस्त<BR>(f. स्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unenterprising
UNENTERPRISING:<BR>(1) निरुद्यम (f. मा);<BR>(2)<BR>निरुद्योग (f. गा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unenviable
UNENVIABLE:<BR>(1) निस्पृहणीय (f. या);<BR>(2)<BR>अनाकांक्ष्य (f. क्ष्या); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unequal
UNEQUAL:<BR>(1) असम (f. मा);<BR>(2) असमान (f.<BR>ना);<BR>(3) विषम (f. मा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unequalled
UNEQUALLED: अप्रतिम (f. मा): v. Incompar-<BR>-able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unequally
UNEQUALLY:<BR>(1) असमम्;<BR>(2) विषमम्;<BR>(3)<BR>वैषम्येण;<BR>(4) असमानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unequivocal
UNEQUIVOCAL: असन्दिग्ध (f. ग्धा): v. Clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unerring
UNERRING:<BR>I Lit.: अभ्रान्त (f. न्ता).<BR>II<BR>Fig.:<BR>(1) अमोघ (f. घा);<BR>(2) अव्यर्थ (f. र्था).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uneven
UNEVEN: v. Unequal, undulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unevenly
UNEVENLY, UNEVENNESS: v. Unequally, in-<BR>-equality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unexampled
UNEXAMPLED:<BR>(1) अनिदर्शन (f. ना) (?);<BR>(2)<BR>अपूर्व (f. र्वा = unprecedented).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unexceptionable
UNEXCEPTIONABLE:<BR>(1) अनवद्य (f. द्या);<BR>(2)<BR>निरवद्य (f. द्या); अवाच्य (f. च्या); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unexpected
UNEXPECTED:<BR>(1) अचिन्तित (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>अतर्कित (f. ता);<BR>(3) असम्भावित (f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unexpectedly
UNEXPECTEDLY:<BR>(1) अतर्कितम्;<BR>(2) अचिन्तितम्;<BR>(3) असम्भावितम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfading
UNFADING (adj.):<BR>(1) अम्लान (f. ना);<BR>(2)<BR>अपरिम्लान (f. ना); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfailing
UNFAILING:<BR>(1) अव्यर्थ (f. र्था = not vain, effec-<BR>-tual);<BR>(2) अक्षय (f. या = inexhaustible).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfair
UNFAIR: अनृजु (mfn.): v. Dishonest, impro-<BR>-per, deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfairly
UNFAIRLY:<BR>(1) अनार्जवेन;<BR>(2) अन्यायेन;<BR>(3)<BR>अधर्मतः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfairness
UNFAIRNESS: अनार्जवम्: v. Dishonesty, in-<BR>-sincerity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfaithful
UNFAITHFUL, -LY, -NESS: v. Faithless, -ly,<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfashionable
UNFASHIONABLE:<BR>(1) असम्मत (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>अप्रचलित (f. ता = not current).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfasten
UNFASTEN: उन्मुञ्चति (मुच्, c. 6.): v. Tie, to<BR>remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfathomable
UNFATHOMABLE, UNFATHOMED:<BR>(1) अगाध (f.<BR>धा);<BR>(2) अतलस्पर्श (f. र्शा): v. Deep, pro-<BR>-found.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfavourable
UNFAVOURABLE:<BR>(1) प्रतिकूल (f. ला);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रति (= against) in comp.: v. Favourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfavourably
UNFAVOURABLY: expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfeeling
UNFEELING: अहृदय (f. या): v. Unkind,<BR>merciless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfeigned
UNFEIGNED: अकृत्रिम (f. मा);<BR>(2) निर्व्याज (f.<BR>जा);<BR>(3) अकृतक (f. का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfeignedly
UNFEIGNEDLY:<BR>(1) अकृत्रिमम्;<BR>(2) निर्व्याजम्;<BR>(3) by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfetter
UNFETTER: विनिगडयति (nomi.): v. Fetter,<BR>to remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfinished
UNFINISHED:<BR>(1) असमाप्त (f. प्ता);<BR>(2) अनवसित<BR>(f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfit
UNFIT (adj.):<BR>(1) अयोग्य (f. ग्या);<BR>(2) अनर्ह<BR>(f. र्हा);<BR>(3) अनुपयुक्त (f. क्ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfit
UNFIT (v.): expr. by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfitness
UNFITNESS:<BR>(1) अयोग्यता;<BR>(2) अनर्हता;<BR>(3)<BR>अनुपयुक्तता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfix
UNFIX:<BR>I Lit.: v. To release.<BR>II To dis-<BR>-solve: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfold
UNFOLD:<BR>(1) विवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.): v. To<BR>open;<BR>(2) विस्तारयति (c. of स्तृ): v. To<BR>expand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unforeseen
UNFORESEEN: अचिन्तित (f. ता = unexpected:<BR>q. v.): v. Also foresee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unforgiving
UNFORGIVING:<BR>(1) अमर्षण (f. णा);<BR>(2) अक्षमिन्<BR>(f. णी);<BR>(3) अक्षान्ति (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unformed
UNFORMED:<BR>I Not formed:<BR>(1) अकृत (f.<BR>ता);<BR>(2) अविहित (f. ता);<BR>(3) अनिर्मित (f.<BR>ता).<BR>II Dissolved: नष्टरूप (f. पा) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfortunate
UNFORTUNATE:<BR>(1) दुर्भाग्य (f. ग्या);<BR>(2) हत-<BR>भाग्य (f. ग्या);<BR>(3) मन्दभाग्य (f. ग्या);<BR>(4)<BR>अभाग (f. गा);<BR>(5) विश्लिष्टभागधेय (f. या); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfortunately
UNFORTUNATELY:<BR>(1) दुर्भाग्यतया;<BR>(2) दुरदृष्टात्;<BR>(3) दुर्दैववशात्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unfounded
UNFOUNDED:<BR>(1) अभूलक (f. का);<BR>(2) निर्मल<BR>(f. ला): v. False.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

