untie
UNTIE:<BR>(1) मोचयति<BR>or<BR>मोक्षयति (मुच्<BR>or<BR>मुक्ष्, c.<BR>10.=release),<BR>shall u. him:<BR>एनं मोक्षयेत्, Sr.;<BR>(2) शिथिलयति<BR>or<BR>श्लथयति (nomi. = loosen),<BR>the<BR>tight knots being u. d by preceptors:<BR>गुरुश्लथीकृतदृढ-<BR>ग्रन्थिः, N. xxii. 154.;<BR>(3) विग्रथ्नाति (ग्रन्थ्, c.<BR>9.: rare), Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

until
UNTIL: यावत्, u. the day and whole night passed:<BR>यावदपासरद्वासरः शर्वरी च सर्वा, D. vi.: v. Till.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

untimely
UNTIMELY:<BR>I Adj.:<BR>(1) असामयिक (f. की);<BR>(2) आकालिक (f. की);<BR>(3) by comp.,<BR>u.<BR>death of men:<BR>अकालमरणं नृणाम्, M. p. vii. 2.<BR>II Adv.:<BR>(1) अकाले;<BR>(2) असमये; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

untired
UNTIRED:<BR>(1) अक्लान्त (f. न्ता);<BR>(2) अखिन्न (f.<BR>न्ना); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unto
UNTO: v. To.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

untold
UNTOLD:<BR>I Not told: अनुक्त (f. क्ता), etc.:<BR>v. To tell, related.<BR>II Not counted:<BR>असंख्यात (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

untouched
UNTOUCHED:<BR>I Adj.:<BR>(1) अस्पृष्ट (f. ष्टा);<BR>(2) असम्पृक्त (f. क्ता).<BR>II Adv.: असंस्पृश्य, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

untoward
UNTOWARD: विषम (f. मा): v. Perverse, stub-<BR>-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

untrained
UNTRAINED:<BR>(1) अशिक्षित (f. ता);<BR>(2) अविनीत<BR>(f. ता);<BR>(3) अनागमित (f. ता: rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

untried
UNTRIED:<BR>I Not tested: अपरीक्षित (f. ता).<BR>II Judicially: अनिर्णीत (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

untrodden
UNTRODDEN: अक्षुण्ण (f. ण्णा): v. To tread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

untrue
UNTRUE: असत्य (f. त्या): v. False.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

untruly
UNTRULY: मिध्या: v. Falsely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

untruth
UNTRUTH:<BR>(1) असत्यम्;<BR>(2) अनृतम्: v. False-<BR>-hood, lie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

untwine
UNTWINE, UNTWIST: अपावृणोति (वृ, c. 5.): v.<BR>To open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unusual
UNUSUAL:<BR>(1) असाधारण (f. णी): v. Uncom-<BR>-mon;<BR>(2) अपूर्व (f. र्वा),<BR>oh! your such sloth is<BR>u.:<BR>अपूर्वमालस्यमहो तवेदृशम्, N. ix. 90.: v.<BR>Strange, wonderful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unusually
UNUSUALLY: expr. by comp. or circumlo.:<BR>v. Also exceedingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unutterable
UNUTTERABLE:<BR>(1) अनिर्वचनीय (f. या);<BR>(2)<BR>अनाख्येय (f. या);<BR>(3) अकयनीय (f. या); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unvarnished
UNVARNISHED: Fig.: अकृत्रिम (f. मा): v.<BR>Unaffected, plain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unveil
UNVEIL: अपावृणोति (वृ, c. 5.): v. To open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unwarrantable
UNWARRANTABLE: अन्याय्य (f. य्या): v. Un-<BR>-just, improper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unwary
UNWARY: प्रमत्त (f. त्ता): v. Careless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unwavering
UNWAVERING: अविचलित (f. ता): v. Firm,<BR>constant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unwearied
UNWEARIED:<BR>(1) अक्लान्त (f. न्ता);<BR>(2) अखिन्न<BR>(f. न्ना); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unwelcome
UNWELCOME:<BR>(1) अनमिमत (f. ता);<BR>(2) अप्रिय<BR>(f. या = unpleasant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unwell
UNWELL: असुस्थ<BR>or<BR>अस्वस्थ (f. स्था), became u.:<BR>अस्वस्थोऽभूत्, K. s. viii. 23.;<BR>looks very u.:<BR>बल-<BR>वदस्वस्थशरीरा दृश्यते, Sa. iii.: v. Also ill, sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unwholesome
UNWHOLESOME:<BR>(1) अनपथ्य (f. थ्या);<BR>(2)<BR>अहित (f. ता): v. Wholesome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unwiedly
UNWIEDLY:<BR>I Unmanagable: q. v.<BR>II Big,<BR>heavy: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unwind
UNWIND: विग्रथ्नाति (ग्रन्थ, c. 9. = unite): v.<BR>To open, free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unwise
UNWISE: अज्ञ (f. ज्ञा): v. Ignorant, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unwisely
UNWISELY: मूढतया: v. Foolishly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unwittingly
UNWITTINGLY:<BR>(1) अज्ञानतः;<BR>(2) अज्ञानात्;<BR>(3)<BR>अबोधपूर्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unworthily
UNWORTHILY:<BR>(1) अनर्हम्;<BR>(2) अयोग्यम्;<BR>(3)<BR>by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unworthiness
UNWORTHINESS:<BR>(1) अनर्हता;<BR>(2) अयोग्यता;<BR>(3) निव्नता = absence of excellences: of men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unworthy
UNWORTHY:<BR>(1) अनर्ह (f. र्हा);<BR>(2) अयोग्य<BR>(f. ग्या),<BR>I am u. of this:<BR>अयोग्या वयमेतस्य, Mu.<BR>vii.;<BR>(3) by circumlo.: v. To become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unwrap
UNWRAP: अपावृणोति (वृ, c. 5.): v. To open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unwritten
UNWRITTEN:<BR>(1) अलिखित (f. ता);<BR>(2) मौखिक<BR>(f. की = verbal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unwrought
UNWROUGHT:<BR>(1) अकृत (f. ता);<BR>(2) असंस्कृत<BR>(f. ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unyielding
UNYIELDING:<BR>(1) अनावर्जनीय (f. या): v. To<BR>yield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unyoke
UNYOKE:<BR>I Lit.: मोचयति<BR>or<BR>मोक्षयति (मुच् or<BR>मुक्ष, c. 10.).<BR>II To separate: q. v.:<BR>वियोजयति (युज्, c. 10.), u. d, i. e. unrestrained:<BR>उच्छृङ्खल (f. ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

up
UP (adv.):<BR>(1) उत्- in comp.,<BR>going up and<BR>down:<BR>उत्सर्पणापसर्पणम्, B. p. x. 44. 4.;<BR>with<BR>arms up:<BR>उद्वाहु (mfn.), R. i. 3.;<BR>(2) ऊर्ध्वम्,<BR>up, sidewise and down:<BR>ऊर्ध्वं तिरश्चीनमधश्च, Ki.<BR>xvi. 50.;<BR>(3) उपरि, if they look up and up:<BR>उपर्युपरि पश्यन्तः, H. ii. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

up
UP (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: उन्नतम्।<BR>II Fig.: उन्नतिः<BR>: v. Down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

up
UP (prep.): v. Against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

up to
UP TO:<BR>(1) by comp. with आ,<BR>lord of the<BR>earth up to the ocean:<BR>आसमुद्रक्षितीशाः;<BR>working<BR>up to fructification:<BR>आफलोदयकर्मन् (mfn.), R. i.<BR>5.;<BR>(3) पर्यन्तः in comp.,<BR>from brother up to<BR>husband:<BR>भ्रात्रादिभर्तृपर्यन्त (f. न्ता), D. 72.;<BR>(3) यावत् (with acc.: rare), up to marriage:<BR>परिणयनं यावत्, D. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

upbraid
UPBRAID: भर्त्सयति (भर्त्स्, c. 10.): v. To<BR>reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uphill
UPHILL:<BR>I Lit.: उत्सर्पिन् (f. णी).<BR>II Difficult:<BR>विषम (f. मा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uphold
UPHOLD: समर्थयति (अर्थ्, c. 10.: v. To support,<BR>defend).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

upholsterer
UPHOLSTERER: *उपस्कराजोवः and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

upland
UPLAND: उच्चभूमिः and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

upon
UPON: उपरि (with gen.): v. On.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

upper
UPPER:<BR>(1) उपरितन (f. नी);<BR>(2) ऊर्ध्वतन<BR>(f. नी);<BR>(3) ऊर्ध्व (f. र्ध्वा);<BR>(4) ऊर्ध्वस्थ (f. स्था);<BR>(5) उपरिस्थ (f. स्था);<BR>(6) उत्तर (f. रा), u. half:<BR>उत्तरार्धम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

upperhand
UPPERHAND: Ph.:<BR>to get the u.:<BR>अभिभवति (भू,<BR>c. 1.): v. Also ascendency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uppermost
UPPERMOST: सर्वोपरिस्थ (f. स्था): v. Upper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

upright
UPRIGHT:<BR>I Erect: q. v.: उन्नत (f. ता).<BR>II<BR>Honest, just: q. v.: शुचि (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uprightly
UPRIGHTLY:<BR>I Erectly: दण्डायमान (f. ना).<BR>II Honestly: शुचि।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uprightness
UPRIGHTNESS:<BR>I Erection: q. v.<BR>II Honesty,<BR>justness: q. v.: शुचित्वम्, -ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uproar
UPROAR:<BR>(1) कोलाहलः;<BR>(2) कलकलः;<BR>(3) हल-<BR>हलायितम्: v. Also tumult, quarrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uproot
UPROOT:<BR>(1) उन्मूलयति, सं- (nomi.),<BR>u. ing big<BR>trees:<BR>उन्मूलयन् महावृक्षान्, Mah.; to u. the enemy:<BR>उन्मूलयिष्यन् विपक्षम्, Ki.;<BR>(2) मूलोच्छेदं करोति,<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

upset
UPSET: परावर्तयति (c. of वृत्): v. Overturn,<BR>overthrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

upshot
UPSHOT: परिणामः: v. End, conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

upside
UPSIDE: अघरांशः and sim. comp. s. Ph.: to turn<BR>u. down (fig.): अस्तव्यस्तं (f. स्तां) करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

upstart
UPSTART:<BR>(1) नवोत्थान (f. ना);<BR>(2) नवर्द्धि<BR>(mfn.); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

upward
UPWARD,-S:<BR>I Of direction:<BR>(1) ऊर्ध्वभ्;<BR>(2)<BR>उपरि;<BR>(3) उच्चैः (= high).<BR>II Of number:<BR>अधि-<BR>or<BR>अधिक- in comp.,<BR>u. of twenty:<BR>अधिकविंश<BR>(f. शा), An.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urban
URBAN:<BR>(1) पौर (f. री);<BR>(2) नागर (f. री);<BR>(3) नागरिक (f. की).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urbanity
URBANITY: दाक्षिण्यम्: v. Politeness. refine-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urchin
URCHIN:<BR>(1) वटुः;<BR>(2) माणवकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urethra
URETHRA:<BR>(1) मूत्रमार्गः and sim. comp. s.;<BR>(2)<BR>मूत्रस्रोतःपथः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urge
URGE:<BR>(1) प्रोत्साहयति (c. of सह्): v. To<BR>incite;<BR>(2) प्रचोदयति (चुद्, c. 10.),<BR>u. d the<BR>charioteer to go quick:<BR>चोदयामास शीघ्रं याहीति<BR> सारथिम्, Ram. ii. 39. 42.;<BR>(3) अनुरुणद्धि (रुध्,<BR>c. 7.): v. To press.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urgency
URGENCY:<BR>I Importunity:<BR>(1) अनुरोधः;<BR>(2)<BR>ग्रहः<BR>or<BR>ग्राहः;<BR>(3) निर्बन्धः।<BR>II Pressure:<BR>(1)<BR>उपरोधः;<BR>(2) भारः (= burden).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urgent
URGENT:<BR>(1) गुरु (f. also र्वी = important);<BR>(2) उपरोधक (f. धिका = pressing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urgently
URGENTLY:<BR>(1) निर्बन्धेन (= pressingly);<BR>(2)<BR>बलवत् (= forcibly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urinal
URINAL: *मूत्रग्रहः (-ग्राहः) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urinary
URINARY:<BR>I Adj.: by comp.<BR>II Subs.:<BR>मूत्रशाला and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urine
URINE:<BR>(1) मूत्रम्,<BR>to void u.:<BR>मूत्रम् उत्सृजति or<BR>विसृजति, मूत्रोच्चारं करोति, etc.;<BR>(2) प्रस्रावः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urn
URN:<BR>(1) कुम्भः;<BR>(2) कलसः (सी, सम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

usage
USAGE: व्यवहारः: v. Use, practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

use
USE (subs.):<BR>I Employment, application:<BR>(1) प्रयोगः,<BR>u. of words:<BR>पदप्रयोगः, N. xxii. 84.;<BR>popular u. is of more force than grammar:<BR>व्याकरणाल्लोके प्रयोग एव बलीयान्, Com.;<BR>(2)<BR>व्यवहारः,<BR>making u. of signs on account of deaf-<BR>ness:<BR>वधिरतया संज्ञाव्यवहारिन् (f. णी), K.<BR>II<BR>Utility:<BR>(1) उपयोगः, does not know my u.:<BR>ममोपयोगं न जानाति, H. ii.;<BR>(2) प्रयोजनम्<BR>(=need), of no u., i. e. simply to fill the foot:<BR>निरर्थकं, पादपूरणमात्रप्रयोजनम्, Kav. vii.;<BR>(3)<BR>अर्थः: v. Object, purpose. Ph.: to be of u.,<BR>i. e. useful: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

use
USE (v. t.):<BR>I To put to purpose:<BR>(1) उपयुंक्ते,<BR> योजयति। (युज्, c. 7. and 10.),<BR>onions u. d with<BR>herbs:<BR>शाके पलाण्डुरुपयोजितः, Bha.; I wish to u.<BR>all that (in satisfying) great Brahmins:<BR>अहमिच्छामि तत्सर्वभुपयोक्तुं द्विजाग्रेभ्यः, Mah. ii. 33.<BR>19.<BR>II To employ:<BR>(1) प्रयुंक्ते<BR>or<BR>प्रयोजयति<BR>(युज्, c. 7. and 10.), no one u. s the word<BR>Daivata,<BR>in the masculine:<BR>दैवतशब्दः पुंसि न<BR> केनचित् प्रयुज्यते, Kav. vii.;<BR>in u. ing once:<BR>सकृ-<BR>त्प्रयोगे, Mit.: v. Also to practise.<BR>III To<BR>treat: q. v.: व्यवहरति (हृ, c. 1.).<BR>IV To<BR>spend: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

use
USE (v. i.):<BR>I Of habitual past.: expr. by<BR>पुरा and लट्:<BR>you who u. d to be aroused:<BR>पुरा<BR> विबोध्यसे, Ki. i. 38.<BR>II = accustomed,<BR>acquainted with: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

useful
USEFUL:<BR>(1) उपयोगिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) हित (f. ता<BR>= beneficial, wholesome: q. v.);<BR>(3) by<BR>subs.: v. Use (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

usefully
USEFULLY:<BR>(1) सोपयोगम्;<BR>(2) सफलम् (= fruit-<BR>-fully);<BR>(3) न वृथा, etc. (= not in vain);<BR>(4)<BR>by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

usefulness
USEFULNESS: उपयोगिता, N. ii. 48.: v. Fitness,<BR>benefit, use (II).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

useless
USELESS:<BR>(1) निरर्थक (f. का);<BR>(2) निष्प्रयोजन<BR>(f. ना);<BR>(3) निरुपयोग (f. गा);<BR>(4) अनुप-<BR>योगिन् (f. नी);<BR>(5) वृथा in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uselessly
USELESSLY:<BR>(1) निरर्थकम्;<BR>(2) निष्प्रयोजनम्;<BR>(3)<BR>वृथा (= in vain).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uselessness
USELESSNESS:<BR>(1) अनुपयोगः, -गिता;<BR>(2) निष्प्रयो-<BR>जनता;<BR>(3) निरर्थकता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

user
USER: in law: व्यवहारः: v. Use, practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

usher
USHER:<BR>I Of a court: शोधनकः, Mr. ix.<BR>II<BR>A teacher: अनुशिक्षकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

usher in
USHER IN:<BR>I To admit: q. v.: प्रवेशयति<BR>(c. of विश्).<BR>II To bring on: आवहति (वह्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

usual
USUAL:<BR>(1) साधारण (f. णी): v. Common;<BR>(2) प्रायिक (f. की = found as rule);<BR>(3) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">Page741</a>]<BR>व्यवहारिक (f. की = customary);<BR>(4) लौकिक<BR>(f. की = popular);<BR>(5) प्रसिद्ध (f. द्धा = well-<BR>-known).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

usually
USUALLY:<BR>(1) साधारण्येन (= commonly);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रायेण (= as a rule: generally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

usufruct
USUFRUCT: फलाधिकारः<BR>or<BR>फलभोगाधिकारः, u. uary:<BR>फलाधिकारिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

usurer
USURER:<BR>(1) कृ(कौ)सीदिकः;<BR>(2) वार्धुषिकः;<BR>(3)<BR>वृद्ध्याजीवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

usurious
USURIOUS:<BR>(1) कौसीद (f. दी)<BR>or<BR>कौसीदिक<BR>(f. की);<BR>(2) विपुल (f. ला = enormous: as<BR>u. rate).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

usurp
USURP: बलाद् गृह्नाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.)<BR>or<BR>आत्म-<BR>सात्करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

usurpation
USURPATION: बलाद्ग्रहणम्<BR>or<BR>आत्मसात्करणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

usurper
USURPER: बलाद्ग्राहिन् (f. णी)<BR>or<BR>आत्मसात्कारिन्<BR>(f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

usury
USURY:<BR>(1) कुशीदम्, -पथः<BR>poverty from u.:<BR>कुसी-<BR>दाद्दारिद्र्यम्, P.;<BR>(2) वार्धुष्यम्;<BR>(3) कौसीद्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

utensil
UTENSIL:<BR>(1) भाण्डम्;<BR>(2) उपकरणम्;<BR>(3) उपस्करः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uterine
UTERINE:<BR>u. brother:<BR>अन्यपितृजो भ्राता, K. b.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uterus
UTERUS:<BR>(1) गर्भशय्या;<BR>(2) गर्भकोशः;<BR>(3) गर्भाशयः;<BR>(4) जरायुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

utilitarian
UTILITARIAN: उपयोगवादिन् (f. नी), u. doctrine:<BR>उपयोगवादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

utility
UTILITY: उपयोगः: v. Use, usefulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

utmost
UTMOST: परम (f. मा): v. Extreme. Ph.:<BR>to<BR>the u. of one's power:<BR>यावच्छक्तितः;<BR>to try one's<BR>u.:<BR>यावच्छक्यं यतते;<BR>the u. limit:<BR>परा कोटिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

utopian
UTOPIAN: perh. काल्पनिक (f. की)<BR>or<BR>मनःसृष्ट<BR>(f. ष्टा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

utter
UTTER (adj.): सम्पूर्ण (f. र्णा): v. Complete,<BR>entire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

utter
UTTER (v.):<BR>(1) उद्-ईरयति, (ईर्, c. 10.);<BR>(2)<BR>व्या-हरति, उदा-, (हृ, c. 1.);<BR>(3) उच्चारयति<BR>(c. of चर्): v. To pronounce, speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

utterance
UTTERANCE:<BR>(1) उच्चारः, -णम् (= pronuncia-<BR>-tion),<BR>easy of u.:<BR>सुखोच्चार्य (f. र्या);<BR>(2)<BR>व्याहारः, व्याहरणम्<BR>or<BR>व्याहृतिः;<BR>(3) उदीरितम्, सम्-;<BR>(4) उद्गारः<BR>or<BR>उद्गिरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

utterly
UTTERLY: अशेषेणः v. Wholly, completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uttermost
UTTERMOST: v. Utmost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uvula
UVULA:<BR>(1) उपजिह्वा;<BR>(2) अलिजिह्वा;<BR>(3) शुण्डिका।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uxorious
UXORIOUS:<BR>(1) स्त्रीवश्य (f. श्या), P. ix. 7.;<BR>(2) स्त्रीविधेयः (या, यं);<BR>(3) स्त्रीवश (f. शा);<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vacancy
VACANCY:<BR>I The state:<BR>(1) शून्यता;<BR>(2)<BR>रिक्तता।<BR>II Vacant post, etc.:<BR>(1) शून्यम्;<BR>(2) रिक्तम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vacant
VACANT: शून्य (f. न्या), placing me in v.<BR>(throne): शून्ये संप्रणिधाय माम्, Mah. iv. 38. 17.;<BR>scarcely went towards her house with a v. mind:<BR>शून्या जगाम भवनाभिमुखी कथञ्चित्, Ku. iii. 75.;<BR>having v. looks:<BR>शून्याकृति (mfn.), Ki. xvii.<BR>39.: v. Also empty, free, unoccupied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vacate
VACATE: उत्सृजति (सृज्, c. 6.): v. To relin-<BR>-quish, leave, empty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vacation
VACATION:<BR>(1) अवकाशः (?);<BR>(2) विरामः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vaccinate
VACCINATE: गोबीजं निवेशयति (c. of विश्) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vaccination
VACCINATION: गोबीजनिवेशनम् (?) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vaccine
VACCINE:<BR>I Cow's: गव्य (f. व्या).<BR>II Of<BR>vaccination: by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vacillate
VACILLATE: दोलायते (nomi.): v. To waver,<BR>swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vacillating
VACILLATING (adj.): of men: अस्थिर (f. रा):<BR>v. Fickle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vacillation
VACILLATION: अस्थिरता: v. Fickleness, in-<BR>-constancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vacuity
VACUITY, VACUUM:<BR>(1) शून्यम्;<BR>(2) खम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vagabond
VAGABOND:<BR>(1) अविज्ञातनिवास (f. सा), Mit.<BR>and sim. comp. s; गूढचारिन् (f. णी), M. n.<BR>ix. 260.;<BR>he leads a v. life:<BR>स गूढं चरति वासो<BR> न ज्ञातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vagary
VAGARY:<BR>(1) भ्रमिः (?);<BR>(2) भ्रान्तम्, वि- (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vagrancy
VAGRANCY: *गूढचारिविषयको विधिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vagrant
VAGRANT: v. Vagabond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vague
VAGUE:<BR>(1) अनिश्चित (f. ता): v. Uncertain;<BR>(2) सन्दिग्ध (f. ग्धा): v. Doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vaguely
VAGUELY:<BR>(1) अनिश्चितम्: v. Uncertainly;<BR>(2) सन्दिग्धम् = doubtfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vagueness
VAGUENESS:<BR>(1) अनिश्चयः (=uncertainty);<BR>(2)<BR>सन्दिग्धता (= doubtfulness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vain
VAIN:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) निष्फल (f. ला = fruit-<BR>-less: q. v.),<BR>one whose efforts are v.:<BR>निष्फल-<BR>प्रयत्न (f. त्ना), M. n. on Ki. ix. 46.;<BR>(2)<BR>निरर्थक (f. र्थिका = useless: q. v.),<BR>advice is<BR>now v.:<BR>इदानीं निरर्थकाः खलु उपदेशाः, K.;<BR>(3)<BR>व्यर्थ (f. र्था = 2.);<BR>(4) मोघ (f. घा),<BR>made her<BR>hand v.:<BR>तत्पाणिं मोघं वितेने, N. iii. 5.;<BR>(5) वृथा-<BR>in comp.:<BR>v. jest:<BR>वृथापरीहासः, N. ix. 25.;<BR>(your)<BR>toils are v.:<BR>वृथाश्रमः, Ki. v. 45.<BR>II<BR>Proud: वृथाभिमानिन् (f. नी), and sim. comp. s.<BR>III Showy, ostentatious: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vain
VAIN, IN-, VAINLY: वृथा,<BR>do not talk in v.:<BR>न<BR> वृथा वाक्यं समुच्चार्यताम्, J.;<BR>(2) व्यर्थम्,<BR>and why<BR>are you tiring yourself in v.:<BR>व्यर्थ परिश्राम्यसि वा<BR> किमर्थम्, N. iii. 13.;<BR>(3) मुधा, why in vain:<BR>किमर्थ मुधा, Ve. iii. 4.;<BR>(4) निरर्थकम् (= 2);<BR>(5) निष्फलम् (= fruitlessly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vainglorious
VAINGLORIOUS: वृथाभिमानिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp. s: v. Boastful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vale
VALE: उपत्यका: v. Valley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

valediction
VALEDICTION: आमन्त्रणम्: v. Farewell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

valedictory
VALEDICTORY: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

valerian
VALERIAN: a plant: जननी (Wilson).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

valet
VALET:<BR>(1) पार्श्वचरः;<BR>(2) पार्श्विकः;<BR>(3) चेटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

valetudinarian
VALETUDINARIAN:<BR>(1) रोगिन् (f. णी = sickly);<BR>(2) दुर्बल (f. ला = weak).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

valiant
VALIANT:<BR>(1) विक्रान्तः (f. न्ता);<BR>(2) पराक्रान्त<BR>(f. न्ता);<BR>(3) पराक्रमशालिन् (f. नी); etc.:<BR>v. Also brave, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

valiantly
VALIANTLY:<BR>(1) साहसपूर्वकम्;<BR>(2) सविक्रमम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

valid
VALID:<BR>(1) प्रबल (f. ला);<BR>(2) बलवत् (f. ती):<BR>v. Strong, sound, good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

validity
VALIDITY:<BR>(1) प्रबलता;<BR>(2) प्राबल्यम्;<BR>(3)<BR>बलवत्त्वम्, -त्ताः v. Strength, soundness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

valley
VALLEY:<BR>(1) उपत्यका;<BR>(2) द्रोणी (Wilson).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

valour
VALOUR:<BR>(1) विक्रमः;<BR>(2) पराक्रमः;<BR>(3) विक्रान्तिः:<BR>v. Also boldness, prowess, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

valorous
VALOROUS: विक्रान्त (f. न्ता): v. Valiant,<BR>brave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

valuable
VALUABLE:<BR>I Adj.: बहुमूल्य (f. ल्या) and<BR>sim. comp. s: v. Costly, rich.<BR>II Subs.:<BR>(1) बहुमूल्यद्रव्यम् and sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

valuation
VALUATION: मूल्यनिरुपणम् and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

value
VALUE (subs.):<BR>I Price (lit. and fig.):<BR>q. v.:<BR>(1) मूल्यम्;<BR>(2) अर्घः,<BR>as it is above all<BR>value:<BR>अनर्घत्वात्, H.<BR>II Precise import: शक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

value
VALUE (v.):<BR>I Lit.: मूल्यं<BR>or<BR>अर्घं निरूपयति (रूप्,<BR>c. 10.)<BR>or<BR>स्थापयति, सं- (c. of स्था).<BR>II<BR>Estimate: q. v.:<BR>(1) मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.),<BR>to<BR>v. much:<BR>बहु मन्यते, An.;<BR>(2) आकलयति (कल्,<BR>c. 10.): v. To consider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

valuer
VALUER:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) मूल्यनिरूपक (f. पिका);<BR>(2) अर्घसंस्थापक (f. पिका).<BR>II Fig.: expr. ed<BR>by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

valve
VALVE:<BR>I Of a door: कपा(वा)ट (mfn.).<BR>II<BR>Of a machine: perh. पिधानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vampire
VAMPIRE:<BR>I A ghost:<BR>(1) भूतः;<BR>(2) प्रेतः।<BR>II An extortioner:<BR>(1) निष्कर्षक (f. र्षिका);<BR>(2) चूषक (f. षिका).<BR>III A bat: मङ्गारी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

van
VAN:<BR>I Front: q. v.: मुखम्।<BR>II Car: q. v.:<BR>यानम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vandalism
VANDALISM: बार्बरिकत्वम्, -ता: v. Also cruelty,<BR>ferocity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vane
VANE: वायुदर्शनी and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vanguard
VANGUARD:<BR>(1) अग्रानीकम्;<BR>(2) नासीरचराः,<BR>(m. p.);<BR>(3) सेनामुखम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vanish
VANISH:<BR>(1) नश्यति, वि- (नश्, c. 4.): v. To<BR>disappear;<BR>(2) पलायते (अय्, c. 1. = fly),<BR>so<BR>long this account will not v.:<BR>तावदिदमाख्यानं न<BR> पलायिष्यते, H. iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vanity
VANITY:<BR>(1) वृथाभिमानः;<BR>(2) मिथ्याभिमानिता;<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vanquish
VANQUISH: पराजयते (जि, c. 1.): v. To defeat,<BR>conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vanquisher
VANQUISHER: जेतृ (f. त्री): v. Victor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vantage
VANTAGE, VANTAGE GROUND: अग्रभूमिः: v.<BR>Also superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vapid
VAPID:<BR>(1) विरस (f. सा);<BR>(2) नीरस (f. सा);<BR>(3) रसहीन (f. ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vaporous
VAPOROUS, VAPOURY:<BR>I Lit.: बाष्पमय (f. यी).<BR>II Fig.: असार (f. रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vapour
VAPOUR:<BR>I Subs.: बाष्पः।<BR>II Verb: विकत्थते<BR>(त्थ्, c. 1.): v. To break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

variable
VARIABLE:<BR>(1) अस्थिर (f. रा): v. Inconstant;<BR>(2) चञ्चल (f. ला): v. Fickle;<BR>(3) परिवर्तन-<BR>शील (f. ला = changeable).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

variableness
VARIABLENESS:<BR>(1) अस्थैर्यम्: v. Inconstancy;<BR>(2) चञ्चलताः v. Fickleness;<BR>(3) परिवर्तन-<BR>शीलत्वम् (= changeableness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

variance
VARIANCE: भेदः: v. Difference, dissension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

variation
VARIATION: परिवृत्तिः: v. Change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

varied
VARIED: विविधविषयक (f. का): v. Various.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

variegate
VARIEGATE:<BR>(1) चित्रयति (nomi.);<BR>(2) चित्री-<BR>करोति;<BR>(3) कर्वुरीकरोति;<BR>(4) शबलीकरोति, V. d:<BR>(1) चित्र (f. त्रा);<BR>(2) चित्रविचित्र (f. त्रा);<BR>(3) कवुर (f. रा)<BR>or<BR>कर्वुरित (f. ता),<BR>v. d like the<BR>dove:<BR>कपोतकर्वुर (f. रा), Ku. iv. 27.;<BR>(4)<BR>किर्मीर (f. रा)<BR>or<BR>किर्मीरित (f. ता),<BR>v. d with<BR>planets:<BR>ग्राहौघकिर्मीरित (f. ता), N. xxii. 18.:<BR>(5) शबल (f. ला),<BR>the v. d sky:<BR>शबलं विहायः, Vi.<BR>vii. 26.;<BR>(6) कम्बर (f. राः rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

variety
VARIETY:<BR>I Diversity:<BR>(1) वैचित्र्यम्;<BR>(2)<BR>विचित्रता। Ph.: v. of = various: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Difference, kind: भेदः, प्र-,<BR>paṭi is a v. of<BR>cloth:<BR>पटिः पटभेदे, Medini. Ph.:<BR>men have v.<BR>of tastes:<BR>भिन्नरुचिर्लोकः, R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

various
VARIOUS:<BR>(1) विविध (f. धा),<BR>and with v. wild<BR>rice:<BR>विविधैश्चैव नीवारैः, Mat.;<BR>I was the v.<BR>object of their glances:<BR>विविधमहमभूवं पात्र-<BR>मालोकितानाम्, Mal. i. 24.;<BR>(2) नानाविध (f.<BR>धा)<BR>or<BR>नाना (=many),<BR>of v. colours:<BR>नाना-<BR>रागविराग (f. गा), Mah. ii. 68. 48.; of v. hues:<BR>नानावर्ण (f. र्णा), Mat.;<BR>(3) बहुविध (f. धा)<BR>and sim. comp. s, with v. means of cheating:<BR>नैकविधविप्रलम्भोपायैः, D. i.; v. weapons:<BR>पृथग्विधानि शस्त्राणि, Ki. xvi. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

variously
VARIOUSLY:<BR>(1) बहुधा, R. x. 26.;<BR>(2) नैकधा or<BR>अनेकधा;<BR>(3) विविधम्;<BR>(4) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

varnish
VARNISH:<BR>I Subs.: कृक्कुभः -कः, (Wilson).<BR>II<BR>Verb: कुक्कुभयति (nomi.) (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vary
VARY (v. i.):<BR>(1) भिद्यते (pass. of भिद्);<BR>(2)<BR>with भिन्न (f. न्ना) वि-: v. To differ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vary
VARY (v. t.):<BR>I To alter, change: q. v.:<BR>परिवर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR>II To diversify:<BR>नानाविधं(धां)करोतिः v. Various.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vase
VASE:<BR>(1) कुम्भः;<BR>(2) कलशः। (सः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vassal
VASSAL: प्रजाः v. Subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vast
VAST: विपुल (f. ला): v. Large, enormous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vastly
VASTLY: विपुलम्: v. Largely, immensely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vastness
VASTNESS: विपुलता, -त्वम्: v. Largeness, im-<BR>-mensity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vat
VAT: बृहद्भाण्डविशेषः, कुण्डम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vaticinate
VATICINATE: v. To prophesy, predict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vault
VAULT (subs.):<BR>I Arched roof: खोडकशीर्षम्,<BR>(Wilson). Ph.:<BR>v. of heaven:<BR>नभोमण्डलम्, and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR>II Cellar: गुप्तिः (?).<BR>III<BR>Leap: q. v.: लम्फः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vault
VAULT (v.):<BR>I To form a vault: expr. by<BR>subs.: v. To form, vault.<BR>II To leap:<BR>लम्फं ददाति (दा, c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vaunt
VAUNT: विकत्थते (कत्थ्, c. 1.): To boast.<BR>V. ing:<BR>विकत्थना।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vaunter
VAUNTER: विकत्थिन् (f. नी): v. Boaster,<BR>boastful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

veal
VEAL:<BR>(1) गोवत्समांसम्;<BR>(2) वत्सामिषम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

veer
VEER:<BR>I Intrans.: परावर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.).<BR>II<BR>Trans.: परावर्तयति (c. of वृत्): v. To turn,<BR>change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vegetable
VEGETABLE (subs.): for table: शाक (mn.),<BR>we shall now speak of v. s:<BR>शाकान्यत ऊर्ध्वं वक्ष्यामः,<BR>Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vegetable
VEGETABLE (adj.):<BR>(1) उद्भिद् (mfn.);<BR>(2)<BR>उद्भिज्ज (f. ज्जा);<BR>(3) औद्भिद (f. दी),<BR>the v.<BR>kingdom is fourfold:<BR>औद्भिदन्तु चतुर्विधम्, C. s.<BR>(Sr. uses उद्भिज्ज in a different sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vegetate
VEGETATE:<BR>I To grow, come out: q. v.:<BR>उद्भिद्यते (pass. भिद्).<BR>II Fig.: perh. शाक-<BR>वृत्तिमुपजीवति, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vegetation
VEGETATION:<BR>I Germination: उद्भेदः।<BR>II<BR>Plants: उद्भिद् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vehemence
VEHEMENCE: चण्डता, प्र-, उत्-,: v. Sharpness,<BR>speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vehement
VEHEMENT: चण्ड (f. ण्डा), प्र-, उत्-: v. wind:<BR>चण्डमरुत्, Ki. xvii. 44.: v. Sharp, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vehemently
VEHEMENTLY:<BR>(1) चण्डम्, प्र-, उत्-;<BR>(2) by<BR>comp.: v. Also sharply, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vehicle
VEHICLE:<BR>I Carriage: q. v.: यानम्।<BR>II<BR>Medium: द्वारम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

veil
VEIL (v.): अवगुण्ठयति (गुण्ठ्, c. 10.), with the<BR>body covered and (head)<BR>v. ed:<BR>संवीतङ्गोपगुण्ठित,<BR>M. iv. 49.: v. To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

veil
VEIL (subs.): अवगुण्ठनम्, let me remove your v.: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">Page744</a>]<BR>अपनेष्यामि तावत्तेऽवगुण्ठनम्, Sa. v.: v. Also cover,<BR>screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vein
VEIN:<BR>I Animal:<BR>(1) शिरा (gen. term);<BR>(2)<BR>धमनी (= artery);<BR>(3) नाडी।<BR>II Of leaves:<BR>शिरा, K.<BR>III Of stones: रेखा<BR>or<BR>लेखा,<BR>full of<BR>v. s:<BR>रेखाकीर्ण (f. र्णा), V. m. 82. 4.<BR>IV Fig.:<BR>stream, train: q. v.: स्रोतस् (n.). V. Tem-<BR>-per: q. v.: स्वगतिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

veined
VEINED, VEINY:<BR>(1) शिराल (f. ला) (?);<BR>(2)<BR>by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

velocity
VELOCITY:<BR>(1) जवः;<BR>(2) वेगः: v. Speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

venal
VENAL:<BR>v. beauty:<BR>पण्यस्त्री;<BR>v. prostitute; v.<BR>services:<BR>भृतकसेवा; v. servant of Minerva:<BR>ज्ञानपण्यो वणिक्, Mal.: v. Also corrupt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

venality
VENALITY:<BR>(1) धनभेद्यता;<BR>(2) by circumlo.:<BR>v. Also corruption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vend
VEND: विक्रिणीते: v. To sell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vender
VENDER: विक्रयकारिन् (f. णी): v. Seller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vendible
VENDIBLE: विक्रेय (f. या): v. Saleable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

venerable
VENERABLE:<BR>(1) पूज्यतम (f. मा): v. Reve-<BR>-rent, respectable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

venerate
VENERATE: समभ्यर्चयति (अर्च्, c. 1.): v. Re-<BR>-vere, respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

veneration
VENERATION: अर्चाः v. Reverence, respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

venereal
VENEREAL:<BR>v. disease:<BR>योनिरोगः, Sr.; v. (i. e.<BR>aphrodisiac)<BR>treatment:<BR>वाजीकरो विधिः, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

venesection
VENESECTION:<BR>(1) शिराव्यधः, Sr.;<BR>(3) शिरावेधः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vengeance
VENGEANCE: प्रतिहिंसाः v. Revenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

venial
VENIAL:<BR>(1) लघु (f. also ध्वी = light);<BR>(2) मर्ष-<BR>णीय (f. या = forgivable).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

venison
VENISON:<BR>(1) मृगमांसम्;<BR>(2) हारिणं मांसम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

venom
VENOM: विषम्: v. Poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

venomous
VENOMOUS: सविष (f. षा): v. Poisonous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vent
VENT (v.): विसृजति (सृज्, c. 6.): v. Emit,<BR>throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vent
VENT (subs.):<BR>I In gen.: छिद्रम्: v. Aper-<BR>-ture, hole.<BR>II Sale: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ventilate
VENTILATE:<BR>I To fan.: q. v.: वीजयति (वीज्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR>II To cause air to pass:<BR>the house<BR>is well v. d:<BR>वायुप्रसारबहुलं गृहम्।<BR>III To circu-<BR>-late: प्रचारयति (c. of चर्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ventilation
VENTILATION:<BR>I Lit.: वायुप्रसारः and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR>II Fig.: प्रचारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ventilator
VENTILATOR:<BR>I A machine: वायुप्रसारिणी (?).<BR>II Publisher: प्रचारक (f. रिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ventricle
VENTRICLE: कोषः (शः);<BR>fourth v.:<BR>चतुर्थकोशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ventriloquism
VENTRILOQUISM:<BR>(1) गारुडवाणी;<BR>(2) उदरवादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ventriloquist
VENTRILOQUIST: गारुडवादिन् (f. नी) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

venture
VENTURE (subs.):<BR>I Bold undertaking:<BR>साहसम्।<BR>II Risk: सङ्कटम्। Ph.: at a venture:<BR>सहसा: v. Suddenly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

venture
VENTURE:<BR>I To risk: q. v.<BR>II To attempt:<BR>q. v. Ph.:<BR>nothing v. nothing gain:<BR>उद्यमेन हि<BR> सिध्यन्ति कार्याणि न मनोरथैः, H. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

venturesome
VENTURESOME, VENTUROUS: साहसिक (f. की):<BR>v. Bold, dangerous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

venue
VENUE: स्थानम्: v. Place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

veracious
VERACIOUS:<BR>(1) सत्यवादिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) सत्यवाच्<BR>(mfn.);<BR>(3) सत्यगिर् (mfn.);<BR>(4) सत्यशील (f.<BR>ला), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

veracity
VERACITY:<BR>(1) सत्यवादित्वम्-, ता;<BR>(2) सत्यभाषणम्;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verandah
VERANDAH:<BR>(1) वरण्डः;<BR>(2) निष्काशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verb
VERB:<BR>(1) धातुः (verbal root), intransitive v.:<BR>अकर्मको धातुः, Kaṇada;<BR>although the v. ‘to do’ is<BR>transitive:<BR>यद्यपि कृधातोः सकर्मत्वमस्त्येव;<BR>(2) क्रिया<BR>(conjugated).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verbal
VERBAL:<BR>I Oral:<BR>(1) वाचिक (f. की),<BR>now I<BR>wish to hear the v. message:<BR>वाचिकमिदानीं श्रोतु-<BR>मिच्छामि, Mu. v.;<BR>(2) वाचनिक (f. की).<BR>II<BR>Of words:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) शाब्दिक (f.<BR>की);<BR>(3) शाब्द (f. ब्दी).<BR>III Literal: q. v.:<BR>पदानुपदिक (f. की ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verbally
VERBALLY:<BR>I Orally: वाचा, and sim. expr. s.<BR>II Lit.: पदानुपदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verbatim
VERBATIM:<BR>(1) पदानुपदम्;<BR>(2) यथाव्याहृतम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verbena
VERBENA: सुगन्धितृणविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verbiage
VERBIAGE, VERBOSITY:<BR>(1) वाग्विस्तारः;<BR>(2)<BR>वाक्प्रपञ्चः;<BR>(3) भूयसी वाक्, Si. ii. 23.; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verbose
VERBOSE:<BR>(1) वाग्बहुल (f. ला);<BR>(2) विस्तीर्ण<BR>(f. र्णा = frolics).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verdant
VERDANT:<BR>(1) हरित (f. ता): v. Green;<BR>(2)<BR>शाद्वल (f. ला): v. Grassy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verdict
VERDICT: निर्णयः: Decision, opinion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verdigris
VERDIGRIS: ताम्रकिट्टम्, ताम्रमलम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verdure
VERDURE:<BR>(1) शादः;<BR>(2) शाद्वलताः v. of = ver-<BR>-dant: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verge
VERGE (subs.):<BR>I Border, edge: प्रान्तः।<BR>II<BR>Rod: दण्डः। Ph.:<BR>on the v. of ruin:<BR>पतनो-<BR>न्मुख (f. खी): v. About.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verge
VERGE (v.):<BR>I To incline, slope: q. v.: लम्बते<BR>(लम्ब्, c. 1.).<BR>II Fig.: v. ing on middle age:<BR>मध्यमोपान्ते वयसि वर्तमानयोः, Va.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verger
VERGER:<BR>(1) दण्डिन् (m.);<BR>(2) दण्डधरः;<BR>(3)<BR>वेत्रिन् (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verification
VERIFICATION:<BR>(1) by verb;<BR>(2) समर्थनम्, ना<BR>: v. Also examination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verify
VERIFY:<BR>(1) प्रमाणयति (nomi.);<BR>(2) समर्थयति<BR>(nomi.),<BR>I would v. this proverb...:<BR>इति लोकवादं<BR> समर्थयेयम्, D. vi.: v. Also to prove, estab-<BR>-lish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verily
VERILY:<BR>(1) सत्यम्: v. Indeed, truly;<BR>(2)<BR>नूनम्: v. Certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verisimilar
VERISIMILAR, VERISIMILITUDE: v. Probable,<BR>probability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

veritable
VERITABLE, VERITY: v. True, truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vermilion
VERMILION:<BR>I Lit.: सिन्दूरम्।<BR>II Fig.: शोण<BR>(f. णा): v. Red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vermilion
VERMILION (v.): सिन्दूरेण रञ्जयति, अभि-, अनु- (रञ्ज्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vermin
VERMIN: कृमिः<BR>or<BR>कृमयः (m. pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vernacular
VERNACULAR:<BR>I Adj.: जन्म- in comp.: v.<BR>Native, country.<BR>II Subs.:<BR>(1) मातृभाषा;<BR>(2) भाषा (when sense is clear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vernal
VERNAL:<BR>(1) वसन्त- in comp.;<BR>(2) वासन्त<BR>(f. न्ती);<BR>(3) वासन्तिक (f. की); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

versatile
VERSATILE:<BR>I Unsteady: q. v.: चञ्चल (f. ला).<BR>II Readily applied to various subjects:<BR>of v. genius:<BR>सर्वदक्ष (f. क्षा): v. Skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

verse
VERSE:<BR>I Poetry: q. v.: कबिता।<BR>II Stanza:<BR>श्लोकः। Ph.: a poem of seven hundred v. s:<BR>सप्तशती।<BR>III Metrical line:<BR>(1) चरणम्;<BR>(2)<BR>पादः;<BR>(3) पदम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

versed
VERSED:<BR>(1) अभिज्ञ (f. ज्ञा): v. Knowing;<BR>(2) विशारद (f. दा): v. Proficient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

versicle
VERSICLE: क्षुद्रकविता, and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

versification
VERSIFICATION: छन्दोबन्धः; श्लोकरचना; and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

versifier
VERSIFIER:<BR>(1) कवयितृ (f. त्री);<BR>(2) पद्यरचयितृ<BR>(f. त्री) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

versify
VERSIFY:<BR>(1) कवयति (nomi.), Bho.;<BR>(2) पद्यं<BR> करोति, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

version
VERSION: authorized<BR>v.:<BR>*परिनिष्ठितव्यावृतिः: v.<BR>Translation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vertebra
VERTEBRA: पृष्ठवंशास्थि (n.);<BR>(2) मांससन्धिः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vertebraty
VERTEBRATY,-E:<BR>(1) कशेरुमत् (f. ती);<BR>(2)<BR>पृष्ठवंशयुत (f. ता) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vertex
VERTEX: शीर्षम्: v. Top, summit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vertical
VERTICAL:<BR>I Upper: q. v.: ऊर्ध्वतन (f. नी).<BR>II Perpendicular: q. v. Ph.: v. circle:<BR>दृग्वृत्तम्;<BR>v. parallax:<BR>दृग्लम्बनम्;<BR>prime v.:<BR>सम-<BR>मण्डलम्, Su.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vertically
VERTICALLY:<BR>(1) अधोमुखम्;<BR>(2) अवाङ्मुखम्: v.<BR>Also perpendicularly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vertigo
VERTIGO: भ्रमरम्: v. Dizziness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

very
VERY (adj.):<BR>I Real, actual: q. v.: expr. by<BR>adv. सत्यम् etc.<BR>II Same: q. v.,<BR>he is the v.<BR>man:<BR>अयं सः।<BR>III Emphatic: expr. with एव,<BR>it is the v. same forest:<BR>एतत्तदेव हि वनम्, U. ii.<BR>22.;<BR>these are the v. same mountains:<BR>एते त एव<BR> गिरयः, U. ii. 23.;<BR>this very day:<BR>अद्यैव, Ve.<BR>iv. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

very
VERY (adv.):<BR>(1) अति- in comp., v. scarce:<BR>अतिदुर्लभ (f. भा);<BR>(2) सु- in comp. (= good),<BR>v. many (= good many): सुबहु (mfn.); v. far,<BR>(= good distance): सुदूरम्; v. hot (= well<BR>heated): सुतप्त (f. प्ता);<BR>(3) by comp. or<BR>super.,<BR>v. heavy rain:<BR>बंहीयसी वृष्टिः, Si. iii.<BR>6.;<BR>v. quick:<BR>क्षेपीयस्, Vi. v. 15.; v. swift:<BR>द्रुततर (f. रा), Si. xi. 8.;<BR>v. big:<BR>विपुलतर (f. रा),<BR>Si. xi. 5.: v. Also exceeding, extremely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vesicle
VESICLE: perh. कोषकः; क्षुद्रकोषः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vesicular
VESICULAR:<BR>I Lit.: कोषकमय (f. यी).<BR>II<BR>Hollow: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vesper
VESPER:<BR>I Evening: q. v.: सन्ध्या।<BR>II<BR>Evening star: सायन्तनी तारा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vessel
VESSEL:<BR>I A receptacle:<BR>(1) पात्रम्;<BR>(2)<BR>भाजनम्।<BR>II A ship: q. v.: यानपात्रम्।<BR>III Of<BR>the body: नाडिः (डी): v. Vein, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vest
VEST (subs.):<BR>I Gen.: वस्त्रम्: v. Garment.<BR>II Spe.: चोलः -ली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vest
VEST (v.):<BR>I To clothe: q. v.<BR>II To invest:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vestal
VESTAL:<BR>I Lit.: prob. वास्तव (f. वीः वास्तु<BR>= Gr. estia, L. vesta).<BR>II Pure, chaste:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vested
VESTED (adj.): as rights: व्यवस्थित (f. ता):<BR>v. Fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vestibule
VESTIBULE: देहलिः (ली): v. Also porch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vestige
VESTIGE: चिह्नम्: v. Mark, trace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vestment
VESTMENT, VESTURE: वासस् (n.): v. Dress,<BR>clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vestry
VESTRY: भाजनशाला (?) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vetch
VETCH: a plant:<BR>(1) द्विदलम्;<BR>(2) द्विपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

veteran
VETERAN:<BR>v. soldiers or v. s:<BR>योधाः परिदृष्टयुद्धाः;<BR>v. skill:<BR>पक्वकौशलम्;<BR>v. politician:<BR>अभ्यस्तनीति-<BR>शास्त्र (f. स्त्रा), B. xii. 14. com.: v. Experi-<BR>-enced, old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

veterinary
VETERINARY: v. surgeon:<BR>(1) पशुचिकित्सकः;<BR>(2) शालिहोत्रशो वैद्यः, (a class of), P. v. 10.;<BR>v. art:<BR>पशुचिकित्सा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

veto
VETO:<BR>I Prohibition: प्रतिषेधः।<BR>II To prohi-<BR>-bit: प्रतिषेधति (सिध्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vex
VEX:<BR>(1) बाधते (बाध, c. 1.): v. To harass;<BR>(2) कोपयति (c. of कुप्): v. To enrage;<BR>(3)<BR>पीडयति (पीड्, c. 10.): v. To pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vexation
VEXATION: कष्टम्: v. Distress;<BR>(2) दुःखम्: v.<BR>Pain;<BR>(3) क्लेशः: v. Trouble;<BR>(4) बाधा,<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vexatious
VEXATIOUS:<BR>(1) बाधक (f. धिका);<BR>(2) कष्टद<BR>(f. दा);<BR>(3) क्लेशकर (f. री); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vexatiously
VEXATIOUSLY: expr. by pres. part. or<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

viand
VIAND: अन्नम्: v. Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

viaticum
VIATICUM:<BR>(1) पाथेयम्;<BR>(2) सम्बलम् (= provi-<BR>-sions).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vibrate
VIBRATE:<BR>I Intrans.: दोलायते (nomi.): v.<BR>To swing, move.<BR>II Trans.: भ्रामयति (c.<BR>of भ्रम्): v. To roll, swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vibration
VIBRATION:<BR>(1) आन्दोलनम्;<BR>(2) दोलायितम्;<BR>(3)<BR>स्फुरितम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vicar
VICAR:<BR>I Substitute: प्रतिनिधिः।<BR>II An<BR>officer: *अन्वाचार्यः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vicarage
VICARAGE:<BR>I Residence: *अन्वाचार्यवासः, etc.<BR>II The benefice: *अन्वाचार्याधिकारः: or sim.<BR>अधिकारः (when sense is clear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vicarious
VICARIOUS: expr. by comp. or gen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vice
VICE:<BR>I Wickedness:<BR>(1) अधर्मः;<BR>(2) पापम्:<BR>v. Sin.<BR>II Fault: दोषः: v. Also demerit,<BR>passion.<BR>III An instrument: संदंशः।<BR>IV<BR>= in the place of: स्थले<BR>or<BR>स्थाने with gen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vice-chancellor
VICE-CHANCELLOR: *उपप्राड्विवाकः; *अनुघर्मशासकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vicegerent
VICEGERENT: प्रतिनिधिः: v. Deputy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

viceroy
VICEROY:<BR>(1) मोगपतिः, (= governor);<BR>(2)<BR>राजप्रतिनिधिः (?); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

viceroyal
VICEROYAL: expr. by comp.<BR>V. ty:<BR>भोग-<BR>पतिशासनम् (= government).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vicinage
VICINAGE: सन्निधानम्: v. Neighbourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vicious
VICIOUS:<BR>I Defective, imperfect: q. v.<BR>II<BR>Wicked, corrupt.: q. v.: दुष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं), Mit.<BR>III Unruly:<BR>(1) दुष्टः (ष्टा, ष्टं): v. elephant:<BR>दुष्टहस्ती, Mr. ii.;<BR>(2) व्यालः (ला, लं), Ki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

viciously
VICIOUSLY:<BR>(1) दुष्टतयाः<BR>(2) दुष्टम्;<BR>(3) by<BR>circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

viciousness
VICIOUSNESS:<BR>(1) दुष्टता,-त्वम्;<BR>(2) व्यालत्वम्, -ता<BR>(of animals^1);<BR>(3) दुर्वृत्तता,-त्वम् (= wicked-<BR>-ness).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vicissitude
VICISSITUDE:<BR>(1) परिवृत्तिः (= change);<BR>(2)<BR>विपर्ययः (=reverse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

victim
VICTIM:<BR>I Lit.: बलिः: v. Sacrifice, offer-<BR>-ing.<BR>II Fig.: expr. by verb: v. To<BR>destroy, cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

victimize
VICTIMIZE: उपहारीकरोतिः v. To offer, sacri-<BR>-fice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

victor
VICTOR, VICTRESS:<BR>(1) जेतृ (f. त्री), वि- (gen.<BR>with gen., acc. with acc.), v. of armies:<BR>विजेतारं सेनाः, Vi. iv. 18.;<BR>(2) जयिन् (f. नी),<BR>the v. s over titans:<BR>असुरविजयिनः, Vi. ii.;<BR>(3)<BR>जिष्णु (mfn.: rare), Si. xii. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

victorious
VICTORIOUS:<BR>(1) वि-जयिन् (f. नी), v. prowess:<BR>विजयि वीर्यम्, Vi. i. 8.;<BR>(2) जैत्र (f. त्री),<BR>v.<BR>hymns:<BR>जैत्रानुबाकान्, Vi. iii. 23.;<BR>(3) जित्वर<BR>(f. री: rare): v. Also to conquer, van.<BR>-quish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

victoriously
VICTORIOUSLY: expr. by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

victory
VICTORY: जयः, वि-;<BR>to gain a v.:<BR>विजयं प्राप्नोति,<BR>Ki. xviii. 43.;<BR>eager for v.:<BR>जयैषिन् (f. णी), [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">Page747</a>]<BR>R. iii. 57. Ph.:<BR>v. to your majesty:<BR>विजयस्व<BR> राजन्, Sa. v.; जय जय जय महाराज, N. xix. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

victual
VICTUAL:<BR>I In pl.: खाद्यसामग्री: v. Also<BR>food.<BR>II Verb: v. To supply, give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

victualler
VICTUALLER: खाद्यद्रव्यविक्रेतृ (f. त्री). and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

victualling-house
VICTUALLING-HOUSE: खाद्यशाला, and sim.<BR>comp. s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vie with
VIE WITH: स्पर्धते (स्पर्ध्, c. 1.): v. To emulate,<BR>rival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

view
VIEW (subs.):<BR>I Sight: q. v.: दृष्टिः।<BR>II<BR>Prospect, appearance: q. v.: दृष्टिः।<BR>III<BR>Opinion, judgment: q. v.: मतम्।<BR>IV<BR>Design, intention: q. v.: आशयः। Ph.:<BR>with<BR>what v.:<BR>किमुद्दिश्य;<BR>with this v.:<BR>एतदर्थम्।<BR>V<BR>Notion, mind: q. v.: धीः, of liberal v. s:<BR>उदारधीः (n. धि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

view
VIEW (v.): समीक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.): v. To see,<BR>look, descry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

viewless
VIEWLESS:<BR>(1) अदृष्ट (f. ष्टा = unseen);<BR>(2)<BR>अदृश्य (f. श्या = invisible); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vigil
VIGIL:<BR>(1) जागरणम्;<BR>(2) जागर्या;<BR>(3) जागर्तिः<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vigilance
VIGILANCE:<BR>I Vigil: q. v.<BR>II Carefulness:<BR>q. v.: अवहितत्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vigilant
VIGILANT:<BR>I Lit.: जागरूक (f. का).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>(1) जागरूक (f. का);<BR>(2) अवहित (f. ता): v.<BR>Careful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vigilantly
VIGILANTLY:<BR>(1) सावधानम्;<BR>(2) अप्रमादेन;<BR>(3)<BR>by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vigorous
VIGOROUS:<BR>(1) तेजस्विन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) ओजस्विन्<BR>(f. नी);<BR>(3) ऊर्जस्वल (f. ला): v. Strong,<BR>powerful, vehement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vigorously
VIGOROUSLY:<BR>(1) चण्डम्: v. Vehemently,<BR>sharply;<BR>(2) बलवत्; v. Strongly:<BR>(3)<BR>तरसा (= speedily).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vigorousness
VIGOROUSNESS:<BR>(1) तेजस्विता;<BR>(2) ओजस्विता;<BR>(3) ऊर्जस्वलत्वम्;<BR>(4) वीर्यवत्ता, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vigour
VIGOUR:<BR>(1) वीर्यम्: v. Strength;<BR>(2) तेजस्<BR>(n.): v. Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

viking
VIKING: v. Pirate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vile
VILE: जघन्य (f. न्या): v. Low, base,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vilely
VILELY: जघन्यम्: v. Lowly, basely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vileness
VILENESS: जघन्यता, -त्वम्: v. Lowness, base-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vilification
VILIFICATION: कुत्सनम्: v. Deformation,<BR>calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vilifier
VILIFIER: कुत्सयितृ (f. त्री): v. Defamer,<BR>detractor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vilify
VILIFY: कुत्सयति (कुत्स्, c. 10.): v. To defame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

villa
VILLA: ग्राम्यं गृहम्, and sim. comp. s (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

village
VILLAGE (subs.):<BR>(1) ग्रामः, head of a v.:<BR>ग्रामाध्यक्षः, V. s.; ग्रामणीः, M. n.; head of ten v. s:<BR>दशाध्यक्ष्यः, V. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

village
VILLAGE (adj.):<BR>(1) ग्राम- in comp., v. priest:<BR>ग्रामयाजकः;<BR>(2) ग्राम्य (f. म्या);<BR>(3) ग्रामीण<BR>(f. णा),<BR>v. women:<BR>ग्रामीणवध्वः, Si. xiii. 37.;<BR>(4) ग्रामीयः (या, यं);<BR>(5) ग्रामिकः (f. की).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

villager
VILLAGER:<BR>(1) ग्रामिन् (m.);<BR>(2) ग्रामिकः;<BR>(3)<BR>ग्रामवासिन् (m.) and sim. comp. s;<BR>(4) by<BR>adj.,<BR>saw v. s drinking spirit:<BR>ग्राम्यानपश्यत् कपिशं<BR> पिपासतः, Si. xii. 38.; invited by the v. s:<BR>ग्रामीणैर्निमन्त्रिताः, P. v. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

villain
VILLAIN: दुर्वृत्त (f. त्ता): v. Rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

villainous
VILLAINOUS: दुर्वृत्त (f. त्ता): v. Roguish,<BR>wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

villainy
VILLAINY, VILLAINOUSNESS: दुर्वृत्तता: v.<BR>Roguery, wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

villein
VILLEIN:<BR>(1) दासः (= slave);<BR>(2) प्रजाः<BR>(= subject).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vindicate
VINDICATE:<BR>(1) प्रतिपादयति (c. of पद् = estab-<BR>-lish: q. v.);<BR>(2) प्रमाणीकरोति (= to prove);<BR>(3) रक्षति (रक्ष्, c. 1. = defend);<BR>(4) समर्थयति<BR>(अर्थ्, c. 10. = support).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vindication
VINDICATION:<BR>(1) प्रतिपादनम्;<BR>(2) प्रमाणीकरणम्;<BR>(3) परिरक्षणम्;<BR>(4) समर्थनम्, for dif.: v. To<BR>vindicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vindicator
VINDICATOR, -Y:<BR>(1) प्रतिपादक (f. दिका);<BR>(2)<BR>परिरक्षक (f. क्षिका);<BR>(3) समर्थयितृ (f. त्री); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vindictive
VINDICTIVE: प्रतिकारपरायण (f. णा): v. Revenge-<BR>-ful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vindictively
VINDICTIVELY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vindictiveness
VINDICTIVENESS:<BR>(1) प्रतिकारपरायणता;<BR>(2) प्रति-<BR>जिघांसता; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vine
VINE (subs.): द्राक्षा, -लता,<BR>mountain v.:<BR>पर्वतजा<BR> द्राक्षा, Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vinery
VINERY: द्राक्षागृहम्, and sim. comp. s ?.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vinegar
VINEGAR<BR>(1) शुक्तम्,<BR>v. is digestive:<BR>शुक्तं पाचनम्,<BR>Bha.;<BR>(2) चुक्रम्;<BR>(3) शौक्तिकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vineyard
VINEYARD:<BR>(1) द्राक्षावाटिका;<BR>(2) द्राक्षाक्षेत्रम्,<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vinous
VINOUS:<BR>I Of vine: by comp. s.: v. spirit:<BR>द्राक्षारिष्टम्, Bha.<BR>II Wine: by comp.: v.<BR>wine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vintage
VINTAGE:<BR>I Produce: द्राक्षा।<BR>II Season:<BR>द्राक्षाहरणकालः and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vintner
VINTNER:<BR>(1) मद्यविक्रेतृ (f. त्री) and sim.<BR>comp. s.;<BR>(2) शौण्डिक (f. की = caste).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

violate
VIOLATE:<BR>I To transgress, break: q. v.:<BR>लङ्घयति, उत्- (लङ्घ्, c. 10.).<BR>II To ravish,<BR>defile: q. v.: धर्षयति, (धृष्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

violation
VIOLATION:<BR>I Transgression: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>लङ्घनम्, उत्-;<BR>(2) व्यतिक्रमः;<BR>(3) भङ्गः (= breach).<BR>II Defilement, rape: q. v.: धर्षणा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

violator
VIOLATOR:<BR>I Transgressor: उल्लङ्घक (f. घिका).<BR>II Defiler: q. v.: धर्षक (f. र्षिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

violence
VIOLENCE:<BR>I Force, strength: q. v.: बलम्।<BR>II Vehemence, speed: q. v.: तरस् (n.).<BR>III<BR>V to chastity: बलात्कारः।<BR>IV Any outrage:<BR>(1) साहसम्,<BR>highest v.:<BR>उत्तमं साहसम्, N. s.;<BR>one<BR>who abets v.:<BR>यः साहसं कारयति, Y.;<BR>(2)<BR>सहोबलम् (rare), Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

violent
VIOLENT:<BR>I Vehement: प्रचण्ड (f. ण्डा);<BR>(2)<BR>उग्र (f. ग्रा): v. Sharp.;<BR>(3) गाढ (f. ढा):<BR>v. Deep;<BR>(4) गुरु (f. also र्वी): v. Heavy;<BR>(5) प्रबल (f. ला): v. Strong, powerful.<BR>II<BR>Outrageous: साहसिक (f. की). Ph.: v. end:<BR>दारुणः परिणामः;<BR>v. death:<BR>अपघातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

violently
VIOLENTLY: चण्डम्: v. Vehemently;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रचण्डम्;<BR>(3) प्रसभम्;<BR>(4) उग्रम्: v. Sharply;<BR>(5) अतीव; v. Exceedingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

violet
VIOLET (subs.):<BR>I The flower: पुष्पविशेषः।<BR>II<BR>A colour: नीललोहित (f. ता?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

violin
VIOLIN:<BR>(1) सा(शा)रङ्गी;<BR>(2) पिनाकी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

viper
VIPER: दण्डशुकः (lit. and fig.; (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

virago
VIRAGO:<BR>I A female warrior: स्त्रीयोधी।<BR>II<BR>A vixen: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

virgin
VIRGIN (subs.):<BR>(1) कुमारी;<BR>(2) कन्या (= girl).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

virgin
VIRGIN (adj.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2)<BR>कौमार (f. री: rare).<BR>II Fig.: शुद्ध (f. द्धा),<BR>वि-: v. Chaste, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

virginity
VIRGINITY:<BR>(1) कौमारम्, he who deprived my v.:<BR>यः कौमारहरः, Kav.;<BR>(2) कुमारीत्वम्;<BR>(3) कन्या-<BR>त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

virgo
VIRGO: the sign: कन्या, -राशिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

virile
VIRILE:<BR>(1) पुरुष- in comp.;<BR>(2) पौरुष (f. षी);<BR>(3) पौरुषेय (f. यी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

virility
VIRILITY: पुंस्त्वम्;<BR>(2) पुरुषत्वम्;<BR>(3) पुंशक्तिः;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

virtual
VIRTUAL:<BR>(1) वास्तव (f. वी);<BR>(2) वास्तविक (f.<BR>की);<BR>(3) by adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

virtually
VIRTUALLY:<BR>(1) वस्तुतः;<BR>(2) यथार्थतः (= really,<BR>truly: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

virtue
VIRTUE:<BR>I In gen:<BR>(1) धर्मः, v. and vice:<BR>धर्माधर्मौ, Par. 161.; riches alone (will be)<BR>the<BR>show of all v. s:<BR>धनमेवाशेषधर्महेतुः, V. p. iv. 24.<BR>22.;<BR>(2) पुण्यम् (as opposed to sin.).<BR>II<BR>Excellence, merit: q. v.: गुणः।<BR>III Strength,<BR>power: q. v.: शक्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

virtuous
VIRTUOUS:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) धार्मिक (f. की);<BR>(2) कर्मशील (f. ला);<BR>(3) साधु (f. also ध्वी =<BR>good);<BR>(4) पुण्यात्मन् (mfn.); etc. Ph.:<BR>a<BR>v. woman:<BR>सती: v. Chaste.<BR>II Of acts<BR>etc.:<BR>(1) धर्म्य (f. र्म्या);<BR>(2) पुण्य (f. ण्या);<BR>(3) साधु (f. also ध्वी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

virtuously
VIRTUOUSLY:<BR>(1) धर्मतः;<BR>(2) धर्मेण;<BR>(3) धर्मानु-<BR>सारेण; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

virulence
VIRULENCE:<BR>(1) कटुता: v. Bitterness;<BR>(2)<BR>उग्रता: v. Sharpness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

virulent
VIRULENT:<BR>(1) उग्र (f. ग्रा): v. Sharp;<BR>(2)<BR>कटु (mfn. = bitter).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

virulently
VIRULENTLY:<BR>(1) उग्रम्: v. Sharply;<BR>(2)<BR>चण्डम्: v. Violently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

virus
VIRUS: विषम् (= poison: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

visage
VISAGE:<BR>(1) आस्यम्: v. Face;<BR>(2) आकारः:<BR>v. Countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

viscera
VISCERA: अन्त्राणि (n. pl.), to remove the v.:<BR>निरन्त्रयति (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

viscid
VISCID, VISCOUS:<BR>(1) श्यान (f. ना);<BR>(2) सान्द्र<BR>(f. न्द्रा);<BR>(3) शीन (f. ना: rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

viscidity
VISCIDITY:<BR>(1) श्यानता;<BR>(2) सान्द्रता;<BR>(3) शीनता<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

visibility
VISIBILITY:<BR>(1) दृश्यता;<BR>(2) दृष्टिगम्यता;<BR>(3)<BR>दृग्गोचरता; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

visible
VISIBLE:<BR>(1) दृश्य (f. श्या);<BR>(2) दृग्गोचर (f.<BR>रा);<BR>(3) दृष्टिगम्य (f. म्या); etc.: v. To see,<BR>sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

visibly
VISIBLY:<BR>I Lit.: प्रत्यक्षम्, प्रत्यक्षतः।<BR>II Appa-<BR>-rently: q. v.: प्रकाशम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vision
VISION:<BR>I Sight: q. v.: दृष्टिः।<BR>II An appa-<BR>-rition: छाया: v. Shade, spectre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

visionary
VISIONARY (adj.):<BR>(1) काल्पनिक (f. की);<BR>(2)<BR>अवास्तव (f. वा = unreal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

visit
VISIT (subs.):<BR>(1) साक्षात्कारः;<BR>(2) दर्शनम्, सं-<BR>(= seeing);<BR>(3) अभ्यागमः (= coming).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

visit
VISIT (v.):<BR>(1) पश्यति (दृश्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>see.;<BR>(2) अभ्येति (इ, c. 2.): v. To come;<BR>(3) साक्षात्करोति,<BR>you should be v. ed:<BR>त्वमेव<BR> साक्षात्करणीयः, Si. i. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

visitant
VISITANT, VISITOR: अभ्यागत (f. ता): v. Guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

visitation
VISITATION:<BR>I Visit: q. v.<BR>II Inspection:<BR>परीक्षणम्।<BR>III Of nature etc. (in bad sense):<BR>दुर्विपाकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vista
VISTA: वीथी: v. Avenue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

visual
VISUAL:<BR>(1) दृष्टि- in comp.;<BR>(2) दृष्टिगत (f.<BR>ता);<BR>(3) चाक्षुष (f. षी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vital
VITAL:<BR>I Lit.: by comp.,<BR>v. air:<BR>प्राणवायुः<BR>: v. Life, spirit. Ph.:<BR>v. part:<BR>मर्मन् (n.).<BR>II Essential, necessary: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vitality
VITALITY:<BR>(1) जीवनम् (= life: q. v.);<BR>(2)<BR>सजीवत्वम् (as of plants);<BR>(3) स्पन्दितम् (of<BR>limbs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vitally
VITALLY:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by circumlo.<BR>II<BR>Essentially, particularly: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vitals
VITALS:<BR>I Lit.: मर्माणि (n. pl.).<BR>II Fig.:<BR>आलम्बः: v. Support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vitiate
VITIATE: दूषयति (c. of दुष्): v. To corrupt,<BR>pollute, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vitiation
VITIATION: दूषणम्: v. Corruption, pollution,<BR>destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vitreous
VITREOUS:<BR>(1) काचज (f. जा etc. = produced<BR>from glass);<BR>(2) काचमय (f. यी = consisting of<BR>glass.);<BR>(3) काचाम (f. भा etc. = resembling<BR>glass).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vitrify
VITRIFY: काचीकरोति (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vitriol
VITRIOL:<BR>I Blue:<BR>(1) तुत्थम्, -कम्;<BR>(2) वितुन्न-<BR>कम् (rare).<BR>II Green:<BR>(1) कासी(शी)सम्;<BR>(2)<BR>पुष्पकम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vituperate
VITUPERATE: आक्षिपति (क्षिप्, c. 6.): v. To<BR>censure, revile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vituperation
VITUPERATION: आक्षेपः: v. Censure, reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vivacious
VIVACIOUS: प्रफुल्ल (f. ल्ला): v. Lively, active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vivaciously
VIVACIOUSLY:<BR>(1) प्रफुल्लभ्: v. Cheerfully;<BR>(2)<BR>तेजसा (= vigorously).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vivaciousness
VIVACIOUSNESS, VIVACITY:<BR>(1) प्रफुल्लता (= cheer-<BR>-fulness);<BR>(2) तेजस्विता (= vigorousness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

viva-voce
VIVA-VOCE:<BR>v. examination:<BR>मौखिकपरीक्षा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vivid
VIVID:<BR>(1) विचित्र (f. त्रा = picturesque);<BR>(2)<BR>विशद (f. दा = clear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vividly
VIVIDLY: विचित्रम्;<BR>(2) विशदम्;<BR>(3) by circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vivify
VIVIFY: जीवयति (c. of जीव्);<BR>(2) सजीवीकरोति;<BR>(3) जीवनं ददाति (दा, c. 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

viviparous
VIVIPAROUS:<BR>(1) जरायुजः (जा, जं), Sr.;<BR>(2)<BR>जीवजः (जा, जं), Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vixen
VIXEN:<BR>I A quarrelsome woman: कलहप्रिया<BR>and sim. comp. s<BR>II A she-fox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vixenish
VIXENISH:<BR>(1) खिङ्खिरी;<BR>(2) खिखिवधूः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vocable
VOCABLE:<BR>(1) शब्दः (= word);<BR>(2) वचनम् (=<BR>term).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vocabulary
VOCABULARY:<BR>(1) अभिधानम्;<BR>(2) कोषः;<BR>(3)<BR>शब्दार्णवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vocal
VOCAL:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) वाग्विशिष्ट (f. ष्टा) and<BR>sim. comp. s (= endowed with voice);<BR>(2)<BR>वाचिक (f. की = oral: q. v.).<BR>II Sonorous:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vocation
VOCATION:<BR>(1) वृत्तिः;<BR>(2) व्यवसायः;<BR>(3) कर्मन्<BR>(n.): v. Business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vocative
VOCATIVE:<BR>(1) सम्बोधनम्;<BR>(2) सम्बुद्धिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vociferate
VOCIFERATE: उत्क्रोशति (क्रुश्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>shout, cry out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vociferation
VOCIFERATION: उत्क्रोशः: v. Noise, shout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vociferous
VOCIFEROUS: महाशब्द (f. ब्दा) and sim. comp. s.:<BR>v. Noisy, tumultuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vociferously
VOCIFEROUSLY: महाशब्देन: v. Noisily, tum-<BR>-ultuously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vogue
VOGUE: व्यवहारः,<BR>words in v.:<BR>व्यवहृताः शब्दाः;<BR>it<BR>is not in v. here:<BR>नात्रेदृशो व्यवहारः;<BR>(2) रीतिः (=<BR>fashion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

voice
VOICE:<BR>I In gen.: स्वरः,<BR>the Brahmin's v.<BR>has been changed with fear:<BR>भीतिभिन्नस्वरो ब्राह्मणः;<BR>it seems to be the distressed v. of Mādhavya,<BR>अये माधव्यस्येवार्तस्वरः, Sa. vi.<BR>II Opinion:<BR>मतम्,<BR>with one v.:<BR>ऐक्यमत्येन;<BR>he has no v. in the<BR>matter:<BR>न तद्धस्तगतमिदम्।<BR>III In gram.:<BR>वाच्यम्,<BR>active v.:<BR>कर्तृवाच्यम्; Passive v.:<BR>कर्मवाच्यम्;<BR>reflective v.:<BR>कर्मकर्तृवाच्यम्; neuter v.:<BR>भाववाच्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

void
VOID (adj.):<BR>I Empty, vacant: q. v.: शून्य<BR>(f. न्या).<BR>II Devoid: q. v.: v. of anything:<BR>अकिञ्चन (f. ना).<BR>III Null, invalid:<BR>(1)<BR>निरर्थक (f. का);<BR>(2) अकिञ्चित्कर (f. रा), असिद्ध<BR>(f. द्धा). Ph.:<BR>such a document is v.:<BR>तदप्रमाणं<BR> लिखितम्, N. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

void
VOID (subs.):<BR>(1) शून्यम्:<BR>(2) रिक्तम्;<BR>(3) शून्यं<BR> स्थानम्; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

void
VOID (v.):<BR>I To empty: q. v.: शून्यीकरोति।<BR>II To nullify: निष्फलीकरोति।<BR>III To emit,<BR>discharge: q. v.: उत्सृजति (सृज्, c. 6.). Ph.:<BR>to v. excrements:<BR>(1) गुवति (गु, c. 6.);<BR>(2)<BR>हदति (हद्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

voidable
VOIDABLE: perh. निरसनीय (f. या), विवर्जनीय (f.<BR>या), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

volatile
VOLATILE:<BR>I Passing into air: वायुपरिणाम-<BR>शील (f. ला) and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Fickle:<BR>q. v.: चञ्चल (f. ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

volatility
VOLATILITY:<BR>I Lit.: वायुपरिणामशीलता।<BR>II<BR>Fickleness: चञ्चलता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

volcanic
VOLCANIC: expr. by comp. s. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

volcano
VOLCANO: आग्नेयगिरिः (?), ज्वालामुखः (?); and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

volition
VOLITION: संकल्पः: v. Will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

volley
VOLLEY: वर्षः,<BR>v. of stones:<BR>अश्मवर्षः: v. Shower,<BR>discharge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

volubility
VOLUBILITY:<BR>I Lit.: चञ्चलता।<BR>II Fluency:<BR>q. v.: वाचालता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

voluble
VOLUBLE:<BR>I Lit.: चञ्चल (f. ला).<BR>II Fluent:<BR>q. v.: वाचाल (f. ला), Me. ii. 33. Ph.:<BR>having<BR>v. tongue:<BR>चपलजिह्व (f. ह्वा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

volume
VOLUME: Of books: खण्ड (mn.): v. Also<BR>book.<BR>II Of solids: अन्तर्गतं घनफलम्, Li. 176.<BR>III Collection,<BR>v. of smoke:<BR>धूमावलिः (ली),<BR>Ku.; धूमसंहतिः, Ki.;<BR>v. of dust:<BR>धूलिपटलम्;<BR>v. of water:<BR>अम्बुराशिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

voluminous
VOLUMINOUS: विस्तीर्ण (f. र्णा): v. Large,<BR>extensive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

voluntarily
VOLUNTARILY:<BR>(1) कामतः;<BR>(2) इच्छापूर्वकम्;<BR>(3) संकल्पपुरःसरम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

voluntary
VOLUNTARY: expr. by adv.: v. Also inten-<BR>-tion, spontaneous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

volunteer
VOLUNTEER (subs.): स्वेच्छासैनिकः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

volunteer
VOLUNTEER (v.): अयाचितमर्पयति (c. of ऋ) or<BR>उपानयति (नी, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

voluptuary
VOLUPTUARY:<BR>(1) विषयासक्त (f. क्ता);<BR>(2) विषय-<BR>सङ्गिन् (f. नी);<BR>(3) भोगनिरत (f. ता), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

voluptuous
VOLUPTUOUS:<BR>I Sensual, licentious:<BR>इन्द्रियसुखनिरत (f. ता) and sim. comp. s.<BR>II<BR>Luxurious, charming: q. v.: मनोहारिन्<BR>(f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

voluptuously
VOLUPTUOUSLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

voluptuousness
VOLUPTUOUSNESS:<BR>I Sensuality: इन्द्रियसुखनि-<BR>रतिः, -आसङ्गः, and sim. comp.s.<BR>II Luxuri-<BR>-ousness, pleasantness: मनोहारिता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

volute
VOLUTE: perh. आवर्तः, -नम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vomit
VOMIT (v.):<BR>(1) वमति (वम्, c. 1.), v. ed blood:<BR>रक्तं ववमुः, B.;<BR>(2) छर्दयति (छर्द्, c. 10.: rare),<BR>blood drunk and then v.ed:<BR>पीतच्छर्दितरक्त-, Vi. i.<BR>35. V. up:<BR>(1) उद्वमति; उद्गिरति (गॄ, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vomit
VOMIT: (subs.):<BR>I Matter vomited:<BR>(1)<BR>वान्तम्;<BR>(2) छर्दितम् (rare).<BR>II An emetic:<BR>वमनम्,<BR>to give a v.:<BR>वमनं ददाति or sim. वामयति<BR>(c. of वम्), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vomiting
VOMITING (subs.): वमनम्;<BR>(2) वान्तिः;<BR>(3)<BR>छर्दनम्<BR>or<BR>छर्दितम् (rare);<BR>(4) वमथुः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vomitive
VOMITIVE:<BR>(1) वमनम् (f. नी),<BR>give a v.:<BR>वमनं<BR> पाययति, Sr.;<BR>(2) वान्तिकर (f. री);<BR>(3) वान्तिद<BR>(f. दा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

voracious
VORACIOUS: घस्मर (f. रा),<BR>the women of Madra<BR>are v.:<BR>घस्मरा मद्रिका इति, Mah.: v. Greedy,<BR>gluttonous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

voraciousness
VORACIOUSNESS, VORACITY:<BR>(1) घस्मरता;<BR>(2)<BR>औदरिकता: v. Also greediness, gluttony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vortex
VORTEX:<BR>(1) आवर्तः;<BR>(2) आवर्तनी;<BR>(3) भ्रमिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

votary
VOTARY:<BR>(1) भक्त (f. क्ता);<BR>(2) by comp.,<BR>v. ies of Śiva:<BR>शैवाः: v. Also worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vote
VOTE: (subs.): no equiv.: सम्मतिः (= appro-<BR>-val) may be used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vote
VOTE (v.):<BR>I To give v.: सम्मतिं ददाति (दा,<BR>c. 3.: (?).<BR>II To elect: q. v.: वृणोति (वृ,<BR>c. 5.).<BR>III To provide, supply: q. v.:<BR>उपकल्पयति (कॢप्, c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

voter
VOTER: सम्मतिदायिन् (f. नी) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

votive
VOTIVE: भक्तिपूर्वमुपाहृत (f. ता = offered)<BR>or<BR>समाहित<BR>(f. ता = put).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vouch
VOUCH:<BR>I To call upon to witness: साक्षी-<BR>करोति।<BR>II To attest, confirm: q. v.: द्रढयति<BR>(nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

voucher
VOUCHER: Lit.<BR>I expr. by verb.<BR>II A docu-<BR>-ment: प्रमाणपत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vouchsafe
VOUCHSAFE:<BR>I To permit: q. v.: अनुजानाति<BR>(ज्ञा, c. 9.).<BR>II To deign, condescend:<BR>q. v.: प्रसीदति (सद्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vow
VOW (subs.):<BR>(1) व्रतः, -तम् (= religious),<BR>breach<BR>of v.:<BR>व्रतभङ्गः, K.;<BR>(2) संकल्पः (= resolution);<BR>(3) प्रतिज्ञा (= promise).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vow
VOW (v.): प्रतिज्ञां करोति, Arjuna v. ed his death:<BR>गाण्डीविना तस्य वधः प्रतिज्ञातः, Ve. ii.: v. To<BR>promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vowel
VOWEL:<BR>(1) स्वरः,<BR>short v.:<BR>ह्नस्वस्वरः;<BR>(2) अच्<BR>(t. t),<BR>ending in a v.:<BR>अजन्त (f. न्ता), S. k.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

voyage
VOYAGE (subs.):<BR>(1) समुद्रयानम् (by sea);<BR>(2)<BR>जलयात्रा (by water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

voyage
VOYAGE (v.): expr. by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vulgar
VULGAR:<BR>(1) ग्राम्य (f. म्या = rustic),<BR>you will<BR>know that men are not v.:<BR>अग्राम्यतां मनुष्याणां<BR> ज्ञास्यसि, K.;<BR>although the words......are<BR>v.:<BR>अत्र॥॥॥शब्दा ग्राम्या अपि, Kav. vii.;<BR>(2)<BR>असभ्य (f. भ्या = not civilized);<BR>(3) जघन्य (f.<BR>न्या = low, mean).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vulgarism
VULGARISM:<BR>I Of manners: ग्राम्या रीतिः,<BR>Kav. ix. 13. Of words: ग्राम्यः शब्दः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vulgarity
VULGARITY:<BR>(1) ग्राम्यत्वम्;<BR>(2) असभ्यता;<BR>(3)<BR>जघन्यता: v. Vulgar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vulgarly
VULGARLY:<BR>I Commonly: q. v.: साधारणतः।<BR>II Meanly, lowly: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vulgarize
VULGARIZE:<BR>(1) ग्राम्यीकरोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vulnerable
VULNERABLE:<BR>(1) भेद्य (f. द्या);<BR>(2) धृष्य (f.<BR>ष्या = assailable^1). Ph.: v. point or part:<BR>छिद्रम्<BR>or<BR>रन्ध्रम्; well guarding all v. points:<BR>सुनिश्छिद्रम्, Ka. xviii. 25.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vulpine
VULPINE:<BR>I Lit.: by comp.: v. Fox,<BR>jackal.<BR>II Artful, crafty: धूर्त (f. र्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vulture
VULTURE:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) गृध्रः;<BR>(2) शकुनः<BR>(comp., शगुन in B.).<BR>II Fig.: perh. गृध्रः<BR>(from गृध्: comp. एभिर्मन्त्रिवकैर्यूष्मत्तश्चौर्यार्जितं धनम्,<BR>D. viii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vulturine
VULTURINE:<BR>(1) comp.;<BR>(2) गाध्र (f. घ्री:<BR>rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wad
WAD:<BR>I Subs.: लोष्टम् (?).<BR>II Verb: लोष्टयति<BR>(nomi: (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waddle
WADDLE:<BR>(1) खेलति (खेल्, c. 1. = play);<BR>(2)<BR>चरति (चर्, c. 1. = move).<BR>W.ing:<BR>हंसगति<BR>(mfn.) and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wade
WADE: कष्टेन गच्छति (गम्, c. 1. = to go: q. v.)<BR>or<BR>तरति (तॄ, c. 1. = cross: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wafer
WAFER: no equiv.: वैभारम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waft
WAFT:<BR>I To drive: q. v.: वाहयति (c. of वह्).<BR>II To float: q. v.: प्लवते (प्लु, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wag
WAG (v. t.):<BR>(1) चालयति (c. of चल् = move),<BR>w. ging of tail:<BR>लाङ्गूलचालनम्, H. ii. 42.;<BR>(2)<BR>विधूनयति (धू, c. 10. = shake),<BR>by w.ging their<BR>tails:<BR>लाङ्गूलविधूननैः, M. n. on Ku. i. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wag
WAG (v. i.):<BR>(1) चलति (चल्, c. 1. = move);<BR>(2) धुवति (धू, c. 6. = shake).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wager
WAGER:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) पणः, counter w.:<BR>प्रतिपणः, Mah. ii. 60. 7.;<BR>(2) ग्लहः,<BR>description<BR>of different kinds of w. s:<BR>ग्लहप्रभेदवर्णनम्, D. ii.<BR>II Verb.:<BR>(1) पणते (पण्, c. 1.),<BR>one who<BR>has no property cannot w. another's property:<BR>अस्वो ह्यशक्तः पणितुं परस्वम्, Mah. ii. 67. 47.;<BR>(2) ग्लहते (ग्लह्, c. 1.), Mah. ii. 61. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wages
WAGES:<BR>I Lit.: वेतनम्: v. Salary.<BR>II Fig.:<BR>मूल्यम्: v. Price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waggery
WAGGERY: v. Roguery, criticism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waggish
WAGGISH: v. Mischievous, frolicsome, witty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wagon
WAGON: प्रवहणम्: v. Cart, carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wagtail
WAGTAIL: a bird:<BR>(1) खञ्जनः;<BR>(2) खञ्जखेलः;<BR>(3) खञ्जरीटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waif
WAIF: अभिज्ञातस्वामिकं<BR>or<BR>अस्वामिकं द्रव्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wail
WAIL: शोचति (शुच्, c. 1.): v. To lament,<BR>bewail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wailing
WAILING (subs.): परिदेवनम्: v. Lamentation,<BR>cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wain
WAIN: गोवहनम्: v. Cart, carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wainscot
WAINSCOT: no equiv.: फलकिनी may be<BR>used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waist
WAIST: मध्य (mn.),<BR>having slender w.:<BR>कृशमध्य<BR>or<BR>तनुमध्य (f. ध्या), M. n. on Ku. i. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waistcoat
WAISTCOAT: no equiv.: उरश्चोलः may be used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wait
WAIT (v.):<BR>(1) प्रति- ईक्षते, अप- (ईक्ष्, c. 1.),<BR>w. for a short time:<BR>कालः कश्चित् प्रतीक्ष्यताम्, Ku.<BR>ii. 54.;<BR>(2) प्रति-पालयति परि-, अनु-, (पाल्, c.<BR>10.),<BR>where will you w. for me:<BR>क्व पुनर्मां भवत्यः<BR> प्रतिपालयिष्यन्ति, V. i.;<BR>(3) तिष्ठति (स्था, c. 1.<BR>= to stay: q. v.);<BR>(4) सहते (सह्, c. 1.<BR>= bear up),<BR>w. for two months:<BR>सहस्व मासद्वयम्,<BR>D. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wait on or upon
WAIT ON or UPON:<BR>I To attend:<BR>(1) उप-<BR>तिष्ठते (स्था, c. 1.),<BR>I will w. on the king:<BR>उप-<BR>स्थास्यामि राजानम्, Mah. iv. 2. 1.;<BR>(2) उप-आस्ते,<BR> अनु- (आस्, c. 2.), w. ed on by Arundhatī:<BR>अन्वासितमरुन्धत्या, R. i. 56.;<BR>(3) उपचरति (चर्,<BR>c. 1.);<BR>(4) सेवते, उप-, (सेव्, c. 1.).<BR>II To<BR>await: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waiter
WAITER:<BR>I An attendant: परिवेषक (f. षिका).<BR>II A tray: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waive
WAIVE: त्यजति, परि-, (त्यज्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>relinquish, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waiver
WAIVER: in law: आक्षेपः: v. Abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wake
WAKE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: जागरणम्।<BR>II Track:<BR>पदवी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wake
WAKE (v.):<BR>I Trans.: प्रबोधयति (c. of बुध्):<BR>v. To awake, arouse.<BR>II Intrans.: बुध्यते,<BR> प्र-, वि- (बुध्, c. 4.): v. To awake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wakeful
WAKEFUL:<BR>(1) जागरूक (f. का);<BR>(2) जागरणशील<BR>(f. ला); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wakefulness
WAKEFULNESS:<BR>(1) जागरणम्;<BR>(2) जागर्या;<BR>(3)<BR>जागरूकत्वम्, -ता; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

walk
WALK (v.): पादाभ्यां चरति (चर्, c. 1.), गच्छति<BR>(गम्। c. 1.)<BR>or<BR>क्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>go, to move.<BR>W. to and fro:<BR>परिक्रामति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

walk
WALK, WALKING (subs.): पादचारः: and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>W. about:<BR>परिक्रमः, -णम्,<BR>W. for<BR>amusement:<BR>विहारः<BR>or<BR>विहरणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

walker
WALKER: पादचारिन् (f. णी) and sim. comp. s:<BR>v. Above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wall
WALL:<BR>I Of a house:<BR>(1) भित्तिः;<BR>(2) कृड्यम्।<BR>II An inclosing w.:<BR>(1) प्राकारः;<BR>(2) वरणः;<BR>(3) सालः। Ph.: (a) to drive to the w.:<BR>अवसादयति (c. of सद्); (b) to go to the w.:<BR>अवसीदति (सद्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wall
WALL (v.): प्राकारेण आवृणोति (वृ, c. 5.): v.<BR>To surround.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wallet
WALLET:<BR>(1) गोणी (= sack);<BR>(2) भस्त्रा (= bag).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wallow
WALLOW:<BR>(1) लुठति (लुठ्, c. 1. = roll);<BR>(2)<BR>क्रीडति (क्रीड्, c. 1. = sport).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

walnut
WALNUT:<BR>I The tree: अक्षोटः (also आखोटः).<BR>II The fruit: अक्षोटम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

walrus
WALRUS: नक्रः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waltz
WALTZ (subs.):<BR>I A dance: प्रतिलोमानु-<BR>लोमत्वम्; *आवर्तनम्।<BR>II A music: *आवर्तन-<BR>सङ्गीतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waltz
WALTZ (v.): expr. by subs. and करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wan
WAN: विवर्ण (f. र्णा): v. Pale, languid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wand
WAND:<BR>(1) दण्डः;<BR>(2) यष्टिः;<BR>(3) वेत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wander
WANDER:<BR>(1) भ्रमति<BR>or<BR>भ्राम्यति, परि- (भ्रम्, c. 1.<BR>and 4.),<BR>w. ed about the world:<BR>परिबभ्राम<BR> मेदिनीम्, V. p.;<BR>(2) अटति (अट्, c. 1.),<BR>w.ing<BR>through forest again and again:<BR>अटाट्यमानोऽ-<BR>रण्यानीम्, B. iv. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wanderer
WANDERER:<BR>(1) भ्रमणकारिन् (f. णी), परि-;<BR>(2)<BR>परिभ्रामक (f. मिका) etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wane
WANE (subs.):<BR>(1) ह्रासः;<BR>(2) क्षयः: v.<BR>Decrease, decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wane
WANE (v.):<BR>(1) हसमुपैति (इ, c. 2.);<BR>(2) क्षयं<BR> गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waning
WANING (adj.):<BR>(1) by comp., w. fortnight:<BR>क्षयपक्षः, Ki. ii. 27.;<BR>(2) क्षयिन् (f. णी);<BR>(3)<BR>ह्रासगामिन् (f. नी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wanness
WANNESS: विवर्णताः Paleness, languor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

want
WANT (subs.):<BR>I Destitution, absence:<BR>(1)<BR>अभावः,<BR>w. of money:<BR>धनाभावः;<BR>(2) राहित्यभ्;<BR>(3)<BR>रहितता, त्वम्;<BR>(4) हीनता, त्वम्। N. B.<BR>(2) to<BR>(4)<BR>chiefly in comp.<BR>II Indigence, poverty: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">Page753</a>]<BR>q. v.: दारिद्र्यम्।<BR>III Anything wanted:<BR>अभावः,<BR>to supply w. s:<BR>अभावं पूरयति।<BR>IV Need:<BR>प्रयोजनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

want
WANT (v.):<BR>I To be without: हीयते, परि-<BR>(pass. of हा),<BR>nothing is w.ing in you:<BR>आर्यस्य<BR> किमपि न परिहास्यते, Sa. i.; w.ing in riches:<BR>धनहीन (f. ना): v. Devoid of.<BR>II To require,<BR>need:<BR>(1) अपेक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.),<BR>that it would<BR>w. other visible illustrations:<BR>येनान्यत्र दृष्ट निदर्शन-<BR>मपेक्षेत, S. i. 4.;<BR>(2) आकाङ्क्षति (काङ्क्ष्, c. 1.),<BR>here it w. s<BR>अपेक्षितुम्: अत्र उपेक्षितुमित्याकांङ्क्षति,<BR>Kav. vii.<BR>III To long for, wish: q. v.:<BR>वृणोति<BR>or<BR>वृणुते (वृ, c. 5.),<BR>whatever she w. ed<BR>she found brought to her:<BR>यदेव वव्रे तदपश्यदाहृतम्,<BR>R. iii. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wanton
WANTON (adj.):<BR>I Sportive: विलासिन् (f. नी<BR>specially of men).<BR>II Unrestrained: अनिय-<BR>न्त्रित (f. ता).<BR>III Luxuriant: प्रचुर (f. रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wanton
WANTON (v.): विलसति (लस्, c. 1.),<BR>w. ed with<BR>her:<BR>तया सह विललास, H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wantonly
WANTONLY:<BR>I In gen.: सविलासम्।<BR>II With-<BR>-out restraint: अनियन्त्रितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wantonness
WANTONNESS:<BR>(1) विलासः;<BR>(2) विलासिता: v.<BR>Also sportiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

war
WAR (subs.):<BR>(1) संग्रामः;<BR>(2) समरः;<BR>(3) रणम्;<BR>(4) सम्प्रहारः;<BR>(5) संयुगः;<BR>(6) आजिः;<BR>(7) सम्परायः;<BR>(8) विग्रहः: v. Also battle. Ph.: w. cry.:<BR>(1) सिंहनादः;<BR>(2) क्ष्वेडा<BR>or<BR>क्ष्वेडितम्, -नादः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

war
WAR (v.):<BR>(1) विगृह्वाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.: lit. and<BR>fig.);<BR>(2) संग्रामयति, -ते (rare);<BR>(3) संग्रामं<BR> करोति, etc.: v. Also to fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warble
WARBLE: कूजति (कूज्, c. 1.): v. To sing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warbler
WARBLER: expr. by verb: v. Also singer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ward
WARD (subs.):<BR>I Custody, protection:<BR>q. v.: रक्षा।<BR>II Opposed to guardian: perh.<BR>रक्षितो बालः।<BR>III Of a town etc.: विभागः।<BR>IV In fencing: अपसारणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ward
WARD (v.): निवारयति (वृ, c. 10.): v. To<BR>prevent, dispel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warden
WARDEN: रक्षक (f. क्षिका): v. Keeper, guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warder
WARDER:<BR>(1) रक्षक (f. क्षिका = guard);<BR>(2)<BR>दौवारिक (f. की = gatekeeper: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wardrobe
WARDROBE:<BR>I A closet; वस्त्राधानम्, and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR>II Clothes: q. v.: वासांसि (n.<BR>pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ware
WARE, WARES: पण्यम्: v. Commodity,<BR>goods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warehouse
WAREHOUSE: *पण्याधानम्, द्रव्यनिधानम् and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warfare
WARFARE: युद्धम्: v. War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warily
WARILY, WARINESS: v. Cautiously, cauti-<BR>-ousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warlike
WARLIKE:<BR>I Disposed to war:<BR>(1) रणप्रिय<BR>(f. या), युद्धदुर्मद (f. दा) and sim. comp.s.;<BR>(2) युयुत्सु (mfn. = desirous of w.).<BR>II Mili-<BR>-tary: q. v.: सांग्रामिक (f. की).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warm
WARM (adj.):<BR>I Hot: q. v.: तप्त (f. प्ता).<BR>II<BR>Fig.: चण्ड (f. ण्डा): v. Vehement, sharp.<BR>III Rich: q. v. Ph.:<BR>to be or feel w.:<BR>घर्म-<BR>मनुभवति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warm
WARM (v. t.): तापयति, -ते, प्र-, सं-, (c. of तप्),<BR>w.<BR>yourself:<BR>स्वगात्राणि प्रतापयस्व, P. iii. 19.: v. To<BR>heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warm
WARM (v. i.): fig.:<BR>(1) दीप्यते (दीप्, c. 4.);<BR>(2) by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warm-hearted
WARM-HEARTED:<BR>(1) सरलहृदय (f. या);<BR>(2)<BR>सहृदय (f. या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warmly
WARMLY:<BR>I Lit.: उष्णम्।<BR>II Vehemently:<BR>चण्डम्।<BR>III Cordially: साग्रहम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warmth
WARMTH:<BR>I Heat: q. v.: उत्तापः।<BR>II Vehe-<BR>-mence: q. v.: चण्डता।<BR>II Zeal, enthusiasm:<BR>q. v.: उत्साहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warn
WARN:<BR>(1) सतर्कयति (nomi.: (?);<BR>(2) उपदिशति<BR>(दिश्, c. 6. = advice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warning
WARNING:<BR>(1) सतर्कः (?);<BR>(2) उपदेशः (= advice:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warp
WARP (subs.): तानः, V. d. i.<BR>I 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warp
WARP (v.):<BR>I Trans.: आवर्तयति (c. of वृत्):<BR>v. To turn, bend, deprave.<BR>II Intrans.:<BR>आवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warrant
WARRANT (subs.):<BR>I Authority: क्षमता।<BR>II<BR>The writ: क्षमतापत्रम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warrant
WARRANT (v.):<BR>I To authorize: क्षमतां ददाति।<BR>II To justify: समर्थयति (अर्थ, c. 1.).<BR>III<BR>To assure: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warranty
WARRANTY: perh. प्रत्ययपत्रम् and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warren
WARREN:<BR>(1) शशकभूमिः etc. (for rabbits: (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warrior
WARRIOR:<BR>(1) भटः;<BR>(2) योधः;<BR>(3) योद्धृ (m.):<BR>v. Also hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wart
WART: किणः (= scar, corn).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wary
WARY: अप्रमत (f. त्ता): v. Cautious, careful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wash
WASH (v.):<BR>(1) धावते<BR>or<BR>धावयति (धाव्, c. 1.<BR>and 10.), w. (his)<BR>feet:<BR>पादौ धावस्व, Mr. iii.;<BR>(2) क्षालयति, प्र- (क्षाल्, c. 10.), w. ing in water:<BR>जलक्षालनम्, K.;<BR>to w. out infamy:<BR>अयशः प्रक्षालयति,<BR>Mah.;<BR>(3) नेनेक्ति<BR>or<BR>नेजयति, निर्- (निज्, c.<BR>3. and 10.: rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wash
WASH (subs.):<BR>I W.ing.:<BR>(1) धावनम्;<BR>(2)<BR>क्षालणम्, प्र-;<BR>(3) नेजनम् निर्-।<BR>II A lotion:<BR>लेपः, वि-, आ-।<BR>III Marsh, fen: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

washhand basin
WASHHAND BASIN: हस्तधावनभाजनम्, and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

washhand stand
WASHHAND STAND: धावनभाजनाधारः, and sim.<BR>comp. s. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

washerman
WASHERMAN:<BR>(1) रजकः;<BR>(2) नेजकः, निर्-, Y.<BR>ii. 141.;<BR>(3) वस्त्रधावकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

washerwoman
WASHERWOMAN:<BR>(1) रजकी;<BR>(2) रजकवधूः; etc.;<BR>v. Above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wasp
WASP:<BR>(1) वरटा;<BR>(2) गन्धोली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waspish
WASPISH: Irritable, passionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waste
WASTE (v. t.):<BR>I To wear, impair:<BR>(1)<BR>क्षिणोति, परि-, अव-, प्र-, सं- (क्षि, c. 5.),<BR>without<BR>w. ing the body:<BR>तनुमक्षिण्वन्, M. ii. 100.;<BR>he<BR>is to be w. d.:<BR>परिक्षीयत एवासौ, H. ii. 95.;<BR>(2)<BR>अवचिनोति (चि, c. 5.), if (it)<BR>is afterwards w.<BR>d.:<BR>अर्वाक् चेदपचीयते, Mit.<BR>II To ruin, des-<BR>-troy: q. v.: क्षिणोति,<BR>it does not w. the reputa-<BR>tion of warriors:<BR>न तद्यशः शस्त्रभृतां क्षिणोति, R.<BR>ii. 40.<BR>III To squander: q. v.: क्षपयति (c.<BR>of क्षि),<BR>when the night was w. d:<BR>अथ क्षीणायां<BR> क्षपायाम्, K.: v. To pass, spend, throw away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waste
WASTE (v. i.):<BR>(1) क्षीयते (pass. of क्षि);<BR>(2)<BR>अपचीयते, (pass. of चि);<BR>(3) क्षयं याति (या, c.<BR>2.); etc.,<BR>it gradually w.s:<BR>स्तोकं स्तोकं क्षयं<BR> याति, Mr. x. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waste
WASTE (subs.):<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) क्षयः,<BR>in the<BR>case of immoveables shall be made to pay the w.:<BR>स्थावरस्य क्षयं दाप्यः, N. s.;<BR>(2) अपचयः,<BR>increase<BR>and w.:<BR>उपचयापचयौ, Mit.;<BR>(3) अपव्ययः<BR>(= squandering);<BR>(4) क्षेपः (= throwing<BR>away).<BR>II W. land:<BR>(1) खिलम्,<BR>cultivation<BR>of w.:<BR>खिलकर्षणम्, Viv.;<BR>(2) खिलभूमिः and<BR>sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waste
WASTE (adj.): Of lands: (land)<BR>that lies w.<BR>for one year is half-w.:<BR>एकवर्षपतितमर्धखिलम्,<BR>Viv.: v. Waste (subs.: II.).<BR>II Desolate,<BR>empty, desert: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wasteful
WASTEFUL:<BR>(1) अपव्ययिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2) वृथाव्य-<BR>यिन् (f. नी); etc.: v. Prodigal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waste-pipe
WASTE-PIPE:<BR>(1) परि(री)वाहः;<BR>(2) उच्छिष्टजल-<BR>नाली।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

watch
WATCH (subs.):<BR>I Keeping awake: जागरणम्।<BR>II Protection: q. v.: रक्षा।<BR>III Guard:<BR>q. v.: रक्षिन् (m.).<BR>IV Of time:<BR>(1) प्रहरः;<BR>(2) यामः।<BR>V A time-piece: कालमापः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

watch
WATCH (v.):<BR>I To observe: अवधत्ते (धा, c.<BR>3.).<BR>II To tend, wait on: q. v.: उपास्ते<BR>(आस्, c. 2.).<BR>III To guard, protect:<BR>रक्षति (रक्ष्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

watch
WATCH (v. i.):<BR>I To be awake: जागर्ति (जागृ,<BR>c. 2.: lit. and fig.).<BR>II To wait: q. v.:<BR>प्रतीक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.).<BR>To w. over:<BR>पर्यवेक्षते<BR>(ईक्ष्, c. 1.): v. To look into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

watchful
WATCHFUL:<BR>I Of men: v. Wakeful.<BR>II<BR>Of nights etc.: जागर-<BR>or<BR>प्रजागर- in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

watchfully
WATCHFULLY:<BR>(1) सजागरम्: v. Also care-<BR>-fully, cautiously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

watch-house
WATCH-HOUSE, WATCH-BOX:<BR>(1) उद्घाटः (?);<BR>(2) पिठरम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

watch-maker
WATCH-MAKER: कालमापकार (f. री) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

watchman
WATCHMAN:<BR>(1) रक्षिन् (f. णी), आ-;<BR>(2) रक्षक<BR>(f. क्षिका);<BR>(3) प्रहरिन् (f. णी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

watchword
WATCHWORD: perh. प्रत्ययवाच् (f.): v. Also<BR>signal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

water
WATER (subs.): Lit.:<BR>(1) जलम्,<BR>cool w.-drink-<BR>ing:<BR>शीतलजलपानम्;<BR>rain-w.:<BR>वृष्टिजलम्; sea-w.:<BR>सामुद्रं जलम्;<BR>how to purify bad w.:<BR>दुष्टजलस्य<BR> निर्दोषीकरणोपायः, Bha.;<BR>(2) वारि (n.);<BR>(3) अम्बु<BR>(n.);<BR>(4) सलिलम्;<BR>(5) आपः (f. pl.);<BR>(6) उदकम्;<BR>(7) अम्भस् (n.);<BR>(8) पयस् (n.);<BR>(9) तोयम्;<BR>(10) नीरम्;<BR>(11) पानीयम्। Ph.: by land and [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">Page755</a>]<BR>w.:<BR>स्थलेन च जलेन च; it will not hold w.:<BR>तदपि प्रमाणकोटिं प्रवेष्टुमिष्टे, D. s. l.; first w.:<BR>अनर्घेयो मणिः (?), V. m. 82. 5.<BR>II Urine:<BR>q. v.: प्रस्रावः,<BR>to make w.:<BR>प्रस्रावं<BR>or<BR>मूत्रं करोति,<BR>An.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

water
WATER (v. t.):<BR>I To wet with w.: (जलेन,<BR> सलिलेन, etc.) सिञ्चति, अभि-, प्र-, (सिच्, c. 6.),<BR>is<BR>w. ing the Mādhavi plant:<BR>माधवीलतां सिञ्चति, Sa.<BR>i.;<BR>richly w. ed with tears:<BR>आप्यायिता नेत्रजलप्रसेकैः,<BR>B. xi. 5.;<BR>these trees have been w. ed:<BR>उदकं<BR> लम्भिता एते वृक्षाः, Sa. i.<BR>II To give w.: जलम्<BR>etc. पाययति (c. of पा); he w. ed the horses:<BR>हयान् पाययामास वारि सः, Mah. vii. 100. 15.;<BR>place for w. ing horse:<BR>अश्वानामुदपानम्, Mah. vii.<BR>99. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

water
WATER (v. i.):<BR>I Of the eyes: वारि मुञ्चति (मुच्,<BR>c. 6.).<BR>II Of the mouth: लालायते (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

water-carrier
WATER-CARRIER:<BR>(1) जलवाहकः;<BR>(2) उदवाहः,<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

water-clock
WATER-CLOCK: कपालयन्त्रम्, Su. xiii. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

water-closet
WATER-CLOSET: *शौचकोष्ठः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

water-cress
WATER-CRESS: शाकभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

watered
WATERED:<BR>well w.:<BR>जलभूयिष्ठ (f. ष्ठा) and<BR>sim. comp. s;<BR>w. by rivers:<BR>नदीमातृक (f. का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waterfall
WATERFALL:<BR>(1) प्रपातः;<BR>(2) जलप्रपातः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

water-fowl
WATER-FOWL, WATER-HEN: जलकुक्कुटः (f. टी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

watering-place
WATERING-PLACE:<BR>I Lit.: प्रपा।<BR>II A sana-<BR>-torium: जलसेवनम् (नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

water-lily
WATER-LILY: कमलम्: v. Lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waterman
WATERMAN:<BR>I Boat-man: नाविकः।<BR>II<BR>Water-carrier: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

water-melon
WATER-MELON:<BR>I The fruit:<BR>(1) गोडुम्बम्;<BR>(2) सेटु (n.); तरम्बुजम्।<BR>II The plant:<BR>(1)<BR>गोडुम्बः;<BR>(2) सेटुः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

water-mill
WATER-MILL: जलप्राणं चक्रम्, जलचलचक्रम्। etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

water-pot
WATER-POT:<BR>(1) घटः;<BR>(2) कमण्डलुः;<BR>(3) कलसः<BR>(large w.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waterproof
WATERPROOF: जलाभेद्य (f. द्या) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

water-snake
WATER-SNAKE:<BR>(1) जलव्यालः;<BR>(2) जलसर्पः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waterspout
WATERSPOUT:<BR>(1) उदवज्रः (?);<BR>(2) जलस्तम्भः<BR>(?, Akshoy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waterwheel
WATERWHEEL: घटीयन्त्रम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waterworks
WATERWORKS: perh. जलकर्मन् (n.)<BR>or<BR>जलीय-<BR>कर्मन् and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

watery
WATERY:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) जलमय (f. यी)<BR>and sim. comp. s. (= consisting of, abound-<BR>-ing in, water);<BR>(3) जलीय (f. या) etc. (= of<BR>w.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wattle
WATTLE:<BR>I Hurdle: काष्ठबन्धः।<BR>II Of cocks:<BR>फुल्लम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wave
WAVE (subs.):<BR>(1) तरङ्गः,<BR>large w. s.:<BR>वृहतस्तर-<BR>ङ्गान्, R.;<BR>(2) ऊर्मिः,<BR>w. crowned:<BR>ऊर्मिमालिन्<BR>(f. नी);<BR>(3) भङ्गिः: v. Also billow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wave
WAVE (v. t.):<BR>(1) धूनयति (धू, c. 10. = shake:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(2) चालयति (c. of चल् = move: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wave
WAVE (v. i.):<BR>(1) धूयते (pass. of धु।): v.<BR>Shake;<BR>(2) चलति (चल्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waver
WAVER: दोलायते (nomi.), with w. ing mind:<BR>दोलायमानचेतसा;<BR>w. ing:<BR>अकृतनिश्चय (f. या = un-<BR>-settled, unsteady: q. v.): v. Also to reel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wavy
WAVY:<BR>(1) तरङ्गित (f. ता),<BR>w. bank:<BR>तरङ्गितं<BR> सैकतम्, Ki. iv. 6.; making the banners w.:<BR>तरङ्गितालम्बितकेतुसन्ततिः, Ki. xiv. 28.;<BR>(2) ऊर्मि-<BR>मत् (f. ती);<BR>(3) ऊर्मिमालिन् (f. नी);<BR>(4)<BR>भङ्गिमत् (f. ती), M. n.; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wax
WAX (subs.):<BR>I Of bees:<BR>(1) सिक्थम्;<BR>(2)<BR>मधूच्छिष्टम्।<BR>II For sealing: लाक्षा।<BR>III Of<BR>the ear:<BR>(1) तोक्नम्;<BR>(2) कर्णमलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wax
WAX (v.):<BR>I Intrans.: वर्धते (वृध्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To increase.<BR>II Trans.: लिम्पति (लिप्,<BR>c. 6.): v. To besmear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waxen
WAXEN, WAXY:<BR>(1) सिक्थमयः (यी, यं = made<BR>of wax);<BR>(2) सिक्थाक्त (f. क्ता = coated with<BR>wax.);<BR>(3) सिक्थाम (f. भा = like w.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

way
WAY:<BR>I Road:<BR>(1) मार्गः,<BR>to give w.:<BR>मार्गं<BR> ददाति, Mr. x.;<BR>to lead the w.:<BR>मार्गमादिशति,<BR>Sa. v.;<BR>(2) पन्थाः,<BR>tell me the w. which leads to<BR>the hermitage of Agastya:<BR>अगस्त्याश्रमस्य पन्थानं ब्रूहि,<BR>U. ii.;<BR>tread in improper w. s.:<BR>अपथे पदमर्पयन्ति,<BR>R. ix. 74.;<BR>(3) अध्वन् (m.), going a little w.:<BR>गत्वा कञ्चिदध्वानम्, K.; accidentally in the w.:<BR>अध्वनि दैवयोगात्, R. v. 60.;<BR>(4) वर्त्मन् (n.),<BR>one<BR>who has lost his w.:<BR>प्रनष्टवर्त्मन् (mfn.), K.;<BR>women go the w. of their husbands:<BR>प्रमदाः पति- [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">Page756</a>]<BR>वर्त्मगाः, Ku. iv. 33. Ph.:<BR>I have come such a<BR>long w.:<BR>एतावतीं भूमिभायातः, K.;<BR>this w. your<BR>majesty:<BR>इतो इतो देवी, V. ii.; did you not see<BR>(meet)<BR>the Queen on the w.:<BR>न खल्वन्तरे त्वया<BR> दृष्टा देवी, Sa. vi.;<BR>make w.:<BR>अन्तरमन्तरम्, Mr.<BR>x.;<BR>which w. is the wretch gone:<BR>कतमेन दिग्वि-<BR>भागेन गतः स जाल्मः ? V. i.;<BR>right of w.:<BR>गमनाधि-<BR>कारः।<BR>II Device: q. v.: उपायः।<BR>III Manner,<BR>method: q. v.: प्रकारः। Miscell.:<BR>in two,<BR>three, many w. s:<BR>द्विधा, त्रिधा, बहुधा;<BR>by w. of<BR>illustration:<BR>निदर्शनरूपेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wayfarer
WAYFARER:<BR>(1) पथिकः;<BR>(2) अध्वनीनः;<BR>(3)<BR>अध्वन्यः;<BR>(4) अध्वगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waylay
WAYLAY: पथि अवस्कन्दते (स्कन्द्, c. 1. = attack:<BR>q. v.). or निभृतं प्रतीक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1. = wait:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wayside
WAYSIDE: expr. by comp.,<BR>w. trees:<BR>मार्गशाखिनः<BR>R. i. 45.: v. Border.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wayward
WAYWARD: प्रतीप (f. पा): v. Perverse, wil-<BR>-ful, forward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wayworn
WAYWORN:<BR>(1) अध्वश्रान्त (f. न्ता);<BR>(2) अध्वना<BR> परिक्लान्त (f. न्ता), Ki. xi. 2.; and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

we
WE: वयम्। Ph.:<BR>here are we:<BR>इमे स्मः, Sa.<BR>iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weak
WEAK:<BR>(1) दुर्बल (f. ला),<BR>the strong would have<BR>roasted the w.:<BR>अपक्ष्यन् दुर्बलान् बलवत्तराः, M. vii.<BR>20.;<BR>w. digestion:<BR>दुर्बलोऽग्निः, Bha.;<BR>(2) अबल<BR>(f. ला),<BR>eating their own w. brothers:<BR>अबलस्व-<BR>कुलाशिनः, N. ii. 10.;<BR>(3) बलहीन (f. ना), S.;<BR>(4)<BR>क्षीणबल (f. ला), Bha.; and sim. comp. s: v.<BR>Also feeble, slender, decay. Ph.: w. point:<BR>दोषः (fault: q. v.), छिद्रम् (= hole: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weaken
WEAKEN:<BR>(1) दुर्बलीकरोति;<BR>(2) बलक्षयं करोति<BR>(with gen.);<BR>(3) बलं हरति (हृ, c. 1. = remove:<BR>q. v.)<BR>or<BR>क्षिणोति (क्षि, c. 5. = waste: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weakly
WEAKLY:<BR>I Adj.: क्षीणबल (f. ला): v. Weak.<BR>II Adv.:<BR>(1) दुर्बलम्;<BR>(2) by adj. or cir-<BR>-cumlo.: v. Also in vain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weakness
WEAKNESS:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) दुर्बलता, -त्वम् or<BR>दौर्बल्यम्,<BR>w. of a king:<BR>दौर्बल्यं राज्ञः, M. viii.<BR>171.;<BR>w. of the senses:<BR>इन्द्रियाणां दौर्बल्यम्,<BR>Bha.;<BR>(2) अबल (rare),<BR>strength and w. of the<BR>enemy:<BR>अमित्रबलाबलम्, M. n. on Si. ii. 36.;<BR>(3) बलहीनता and sim. deriv. s.<BR>II Foible,<BR>fault: q. v.: व्यसनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weal
WEAL:<BR>I Welfare, happiness: q. v.: क्षेमम्।<BR>Ph.:<BR>for the public w.:<BR>प्रकृतिहिताय, Sa. vii.<BR>II Mark of a blow: क्षतचिह्नम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wealth
WEALTH:<BR>I Riches:<BR>(1) धनम् (= pro. money),<BR>what is the use of w. (to one)<BR>who does not give,<BR>does not eat:<BR>धनेन किं यो न ददाति नाश्नुते, H.;<BR>(2) वसु (n. = 1), not only the w. of the monarch:<BR>वसु तस्य विमोर्न केवलम्, R.;<BR>(3) विभवः;<BR>(4)<BR>वैभवम्;<BR>(5) ऐश्वर्यम्;<BR>(6) सम्पत्तिः (= property);<BR>(7) वित्तम् (= 1).<BR>II Prosperity: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wealthy
WEALTHY: महाधन (f. ना): v. Rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wean
WEAN:<BR>I Lit.: स्तन्यं त्याजयति, परि- (c. of<BR>त्यज्)<BR>or<BR>हापयति, परि- (c. of हा)<BR>or<BR>विसर्जयति<BR>(c. of सृज्).<BR>II Fig.: वियोजयति (युज्, c. 10)<BR>or<BR>विधटयति (घट्, c. 10.): v. To separate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weapon
WEAPON:<BR>(1) शस्त्रम्,<BR>when victory was not inter-<BR>cepted by w. s.:<BR>शस्त्रैरव्यधीयमानविजयः, Vi. v. 51.;<BR>(2) अस्त्रम् (properly a missile), various w.:<BR>विविधमस्त्रम्, Ki. xviii. 46.;<BR>(3) आयुधम्;<BR>(4)<BR>प्रहरणम्;<BR>(5) हेतिः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wear
WEAR (subs.):<BR>I Waste: q. v.: क्षयः, परि-,<BR> अव-।<BR>II Dress: q. v.: वासस् (n.).<BR>III Dam:<BR>बन्धः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wear
WEAR (v. t.):<BR>I To put on: q. v.: धरति or<BR>धारयति (धृ, c. 1. and 10),<BR>ornaments worn by<BR>women during the life-time of their husbands:<BR>पत्यौ जीवति यः स्त्रीभिरलङ्कारो धृतो भवेत्, Mit.;<BR>clothes etc., worn by a father.:<BR>पितृधृतं वस्त्रादिकम्,<BR>Mit. Ph.:<BR>w. ing apparel:<BR>परिधानवासस्, (n.)<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR>II To impair: क्षिणोति<BR>(क्षि, c. 5.): v. Waste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wear
WEAR (v. t.): क्षीयते (pass. of क्षि): v. To<BR>waste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wear off
WEAR OFF:<BR>(1) नश्यति (नश्, c. 4.): v. Des-<BR>-troy;<BR>(2) अपगच्छति (गम्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>go away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wear out
WEAR OUT:<BR>I By use:<BR>(1) जीर्णीकरोति;<BR>(2)<BR>जर्जरीकरोति।<BR>II Intrans.: जीर्यति, परि- (जॄ, c.<BR>4.);<BR>(2) जीर्णीभवति;<BR>(3) जर्जरीभवति।<BR>III To<BR>fatigue, tire: q. v.: सादयति, अव- (c. of सद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wearied
WEARIED:<BR>(1) क्लान्त (f. न्ता);<BR>(2) परिश्रान्त (f.<BR>न्ता): v. Fatigued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weariness
WEARINESS:<BR>(1) क्लमः;<BR>(2) क्लान्तिः: Fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wearisome
WEARISOME:<BR>(1) श्रमजनन (f. नी);<BR>(2) आयास-<BR>कर (f. री);<BR>(3) स्वेदजनक (f. निका); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weary
WEARY (adj.):<BR>I Fatigued: q. v.: क्लान्त (f.<BR>न्ता).<BR>II Wearisome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weary
WEARY (v.): आयासयति (c. of यस्): v. To<BR>fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weasand
WEASAND: v. Windpipe, throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weasel
WEASEL:<BR>(1) नकुलः;<BR>(2) बभ्रुः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weather
WEATHER (v.):<BR>I To air: q. v.:<BR>II To<BR>sail to the windward of: प्रतिवातमतिक्रामति<BR>(क्रम्, c. 1.): v. To cross.<BR>III Fig.: तरति<BR>(त, c. 1.): v. To cross, bear, sustain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weather
WEATHER (subs.):<BR>(1) by circumlo.;<BR>(2)<BR>कालः (= time: q. v.);<BR>(3) दिनम्। Ph.:<BR>bad<BR>w.:<BR>दुर्दिनम्, वार्दलम्;<BR>good w.:<BR>सुदिनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weather-beaten
WEATHER-BEATEN:<BR>(1) वाताहत (f. ता: by<BR>wind);<BR>(2) भञ्भाहत (f. ता: by hurricane);<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weathercock
WEATHERCOCK: वायुप्रदर्शिनी and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weather-glass
WEATHER-GLASS: वायुयन्त्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weather-wise
WEATHER-WISE: वातादिलक्षणविद (mfn.) and<BR>sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weave
WEAVE: व्यति, प्र- (वे, c. 1.),<BR>w. ing cloth:<BR>पटं<BR> वयन्तौ, Mah. i. 3. 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weaver
WEAVER:<BR>(1) तन्तु(न्त्र)वायः(पः);<BR>(2) कुवि(पि)न्दः;<BR>(3) पट्टकारः, -कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

web
WEB:<BR>I gen.: जालम्।<BR>II Of the eye: पटलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

web-footed
WEB-FOOTED: जालपादः (f. दा); a w. animal:<BR>कश्चिज्जालपादः, D. i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wed
WED: परिणयति (नी, c. 1.): v. To marry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wedded
WEDDED: Fig.: आसक्त (f. क्ता): v. Atta-<BR>-ched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wedding
WEDDING: विवाहः: v. Marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wedlock
WEDLOCK: विवाहः: v. Marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wednesday
WEDNESDAY:<BR>(1) बुधवारः;<BR>(2) बुधवासरः;<BR>(3)<BR>सौम्यवारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weed
WEED (subs.):<BR>I A noxious plant:<BR>(1) कक्षः,<BR>to take up w. s:<BR>कक्षमुद्धरति, M. vii. 110.;<BR>(2)<BR>तृणादिकम्, R. t.;<BR>(3) perh. अगच्छः। (comp.<BR>Bengalee आगाछा).<BR>II Widow's dress:<BR>perh. क्लिष्टनिबसनम्, D. v.; चीरम्<BR>or<BR>चीवरम् (prop.<BR>rag).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weed
WEED (v.): उद्धरति (धृ, c. 1.);<BR>(2) निर्दाति or<BR>-द्यति (दा, c. 2. or दो, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weeder
WEEDER:<BR>(1) निर्दातृ (f. त्री), M. vii. 110.;<BR>(2) कक्षोद्धर्तृ (f. र्त्री) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

week
WEEK: सप्ताहम्,<BR>every w.:<BR>सप्तहात् सप्ताहात्, Sr;<BR>w.<BR>day:<BR>वारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weekly
WEEKLY:<BR>I Adj.: साप्ताहिक (f. की).<BR>II Adv.:<BR>सप्ताहे सप्ताहे।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ween
WEEN: मन्यते (मन्, c. 4.): v. To think.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weep
WEEP:<BR>(1) रोदिति, प्र-, अभि- (रुद्, c. 2.), how<BR>will you get (her)<BR>w. ing:<BR>रुदता कुत एव लभ्यते, R.<BR>viii. 85.; embracing (me)<BR>w.ing:<BR>सरुदितं परिष्वज्य,<BR>D. iii.;<BR>(2) विलपति (लप्, c. 1. = bewail);<BR>(3) अश्रूणि पातयति (= shed tears): v. Also<BR>to cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weeping
WEEPING (subs.):<BR>(1) रोदनम्;<BR>(2) रुदितम्;<BR>(3)<BR>क्रन्दनम्;<BR>(4) क्रन्दितम्;<BR>(5) विलापः (= lamen-<BR>-tation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weeping-willow
WEEPING-WILLOW: वृक्षविशेषः; नम्रशाखः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weevil
WEEVIL: कीटविशेषः, *जालकीटः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weigh
WEIGH (v. t.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) तोलयति<BR>or<BR>तूलयति<BR>(तुल्<BR>or<BR>तूल्, c. 10.), if increases when w. ed:<BR>तुलितो यदि वर्धते, N. s.;<BR>(2) तुलायां करोति<BR>or<BR>धारयति<BR>(prop. in a balance),<BR>if truth is w. ed with<BR>thousand horse-sacrifices:<BR>अश्वमेधसहस्राणि सत्यञ्च<BR> तुलया धृतम्, H. iv. 131.<BR>II As anchor:<BR>तोलयति, उत्-: v. To lift, raise.<BR>III To<BR>ponder, consider: q. v.: विमृशति (मृश्, c. 6.)<BR>Comp., w. down: v. To overcome, oppress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weigh
WEIGH (v. i.): expr. by subs. or adj.,<BR>The<BR>dove w. ed greater:<BR>गुरुतर एव कपोत आसीत्, Mah.<BR>iii. 197. 21.;<BR>what does it w.:<BR>किंभारभिदम्।<BR>Comp.<BR>w. upon:<BR>पीडयति (पीड्, c. 10.): v.<BR>To press, pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weighing
WEIGHING (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: तोलनम्।<BR>II Fig.:<BR>विगणनम्, -ना: v. Consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weight
WEIGHT:<BR>I For measuring: मानम्, उत्-,<BR>true<BR>and false w. s:<BR>पूर्णापूर्णे माने, P.; names of w. s:<BR>मानपरिभाषा।<BR>II Heaviness, burden: q. v.:<BR>भारः,<BR>w. of iron:<BR>लोहभारः, P.<BR>III Impor-<BR>-tance: q. v.: गुरुत्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weighty
WEIGHTY: गुरु (f. also र्वी): v. Heavy, im-<BR>-portant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weir
WEIR:<BR>(1) बन्धः (?);<BR>(2) योगः (?), Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

welcome
WELCOME (adj.):<BR>I Lit.: स्वागत (f. ता).<BR>II<BR>Propitious, good: q. v.: शुभ (f. भा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

welcome
WELCOME (v.):<BR>(1) सभाजयति (सभाज्, c. 10.):<BR>v. To greet;<BR>(2) अभिनन्दति (नन्द्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To cheer, salute;<BR>(3) सत्करोति; पूजयति<BR>(पूज्, c. 10.): v. To honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

welcome
WELCOME (interj.): स्वगतम् (with dat.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

welcome
WELCOME (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: स्वागतम्,<BR>w. to you<BR>sir:<BR>स्वागतमार्याय, Mr. i.;<BR>bade him w.:<BR>तस्मै<BR> स्वागतं व्याजहार, Me. i. 4.<BR>II Fig.: सभाजनम्:<BR>v. Greeting, salute, honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weld
WELD: संयोजयति (युज्, c. 10.): v. To unite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

welfare
WELFARE:<BR>(1) क्षेमम्,<BR>tending to w.:<BR>क्षेमङ्कर (f.<BR>री), B.;<BR>(2) हितम् (= good: q. v.);<BR>(3)<BR>मङ्गलम्;<BR>(4) कल्याणम्;<BR>(5) कुशलम्;<BR>(6) श्रेयस् (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

welkin
WELKIN: नभस् (n.): v. Sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

well
WELL (subs.):<BR>(1) कूपः,<BR>blind w.:<BR>अन्धकूपः,<BR>Va.;<BR>w.-maker:<BR>कूपकृत्, He.;<BR>(2) अन्धुः (rare)<BR>Of a ship: गुप्तिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

well
WELL (adj.):<BR>(1) कुशलिन् (f. नी),<BR>is your pre-<BR>ceptor w.:<BR>कुशली गुरुस्ते, R. v. 4.;<BR>is Chāru-<BR>datta w.:<BR>अपि कुशलं सार्थवाहपुत्रस्य, Mr. ix.;<BR>(2) सुस्थशरीर (f. रा: in body): v. Healthy;<BR>(3) सुस्थ<BR>or<BR>स्वस्थ (f. स्था),<BR>in a few days you<BR>will hear your father is w. and recovered to his<BR>health:<BR>कतिपयैरेव दिवसैः पुनः स्वां प्रकृतिमापन्नं स्वस्थं<BR> श्रोष्यसि पितरम्, C. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

well
WELL (adv.):<BR>(1) सु- in comp.,<BR>w.-born:<BR>सुजात<BR>(f. ता);<BR>w.-bred:<BR>सुशिक्षित (f. ता); w.-done:<BR>सुकृत (f. ता);<BR>w.-favoured:<BR>सुदर्शन (f. ना);<BR>w.-formed:<BR>सुरूप (f. प);<BR>w.-known:<BR>सुप्रसिद्ध<BR>(f. द्धा);<BR>w.-read:<BR>स्वधीत (f. ता); etc.;<BR>(2)<BR>सुष्ठु;<BR>(3) साधु (= w.-to-do);<BR>(4) सम्यक्।<BR>W.<BR>off:<BR>आढ्य (f. ढ्या): v. Rich, prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

well
WELL (interj.):<BR>(1) वाढम् (=very well);<BR>(2)<BR>no expr. when concessive, w., what next:<BR>ततस्ततः;<BR>w., be it so:<BR>भवतु; w., I am going:<BR>मया तावद्गम्यते। Ph.: w.-done: i. e. admirable,<BR>साधु साधु;<BR>w.-affected, well-disposed:<BR>हितबुद्धि<BR>(mfn.) and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

well-being
WELL-BEING: कुशलम्: v. Welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

well-informed
WELL-INFORMED:<BR>(1) बहुज्ञ (f. ज्ञा);<BR>(2) विशेषविद्<BR>(mfn.); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

well-meaning
WELL-MEANING:<BR>(1) सदाशय (f. या);<BR>(2)<BR>सदभिप्राय (f. या); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

well-nigh
WELL-NIGH: प्रायेण: v. Nearly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

well-versed
WELL-VERSED:<BR>(1) सम्यग्विनीत (f. ता);<BR>(2)<BR>स्वधीतिन् (f. नी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

well-wisher
WELL-WISHER:<BR>(1) हितैषिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) हित-<BR>काम (f. मा);<BR>(3) शुभाकाङ्क्षिन् (f. णी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

welter
WELTER (v.): लुठति (लुठ्, c. 6.): v. To roll.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wen
WEN: अर्वुदम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wench
WENCH:<BR>(1) बन्धकी;<BR>(2) पुंश्चली;<BR>(3) दुर्वृत्ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wench
WENCH (v.): अभिसरति (सृ, c. 1.): v. Also<BR>to fornicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wend
WEND: to w. one's way: गच्छति (गम्, c. 1.<BR>= go, pass: q. v.)<BR>or<BR>आगच्छति (= come:<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

west
WEST:<BR>(1) पश्चिमा दिक् and sim. expr.s: v.<BR>Quarter;<BR>(2) प्रतीची;<BR>(3) वारुणी दिक् and sim.<BR>expr.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

west
WEST, WESTERLY, WESTERN:<BR>(1) पश्चिम (f.<BR>मा),<BR>in the w. sky:<BR>पश्चिमे नभसि, Ki. ix. 5.;<BR>(2) पाश्चात्य (f. त्या),<BR>with the w. erns whose<BR>strength lay in horse:<BR>पाश्चात्यैरश्वसाधनैः, R. iv.<BR>62.;<BR>(3) प्रतीच्य (f. च्या) or rarely प्रतीचीन<BR>(f. ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

westward
WESTWARD, -S: प्रतीचीमभितो दिशम्, Mah.; and<BR>sim. exprs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wet
WET (adj.):<BR>(1) आर्द्र (f. र्द्रा),<BR>the hair being<BR>wet with rain:<BR>जलार्द्रालका, Mr. v. 34.;<BR>by the<BR>w. track:<BR>आर्द्रपदपंक्तिभिः, R. ix. 59.;<BR>(2) क्लिन्न<BR>(f. न्ना),<BR>w. clothes:<BR>क्लिन्ने वाससी, Mr. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wet
WET (subs.):<BR>I Wetness: आर्द्रता।<BR>II Rainy<BR>weather: दुर्दिनम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wet
WET (v.):<BR>(1) आर्द्रीकरोति;<BR>(2) क्लेदयति, सं-, प्र-,<BR>(c. of क्लिद्),<BR>and water does not w. him:<BR>न<BR> चैनं क्लेदयन्त्यापः, G. ii. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wet-nurse
WET-NURSE: स्तन्यदात्री धात्री, Viv.; and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wether
WETHER: छिन्नवृषणो मेषः, and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wettish
WETTISH:<BR>(1) ईषदार्द्र (f. र्द्रा);<BR>(2) आक्लिन्न (f.<BR>न्ना), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whale
WHALE: तिमिः, R. xiii. 10. N. B. तिमिङ्गिलः = w.<BR>eater, a fabulous sea-monster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whaler
WHALER: *तिमिपोतः, तिमिग्रहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wharf
WHARF:<BR>(1) घट्टः (?);<BR>(2) उमः (?);<BR>(3) गुल्मः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

what
WHAT (interj.):<BR>(1) किम्, w. disgrace of Droṇa:<BR>किं किं भारद्वाजस्य परिभवः, Ve.;<BR>(2) कथम्,<BR>w.<BR>vying with me:<BR>कथं मया सह स्पर्धते, Mu.;<BR>(3)<BR>आः,<BR>w. is this also to be asked:<BR>आः इदमपि<BR> किं प्रष्टव्यः, Pra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

what
WHAT (interro.): किम्,<BR>w. kind, sort:<BR>कीदृशः<BR>(शी, शं);<BR>w. is his mother by caste:<BR>किमीया<BR> जात्यास्य माता, D. viii.;<BR>w. then:<BR>ततः किम्,<BR>K.; w. is (he)<BR>doing now:<BR>किंव्यापारः सम्प्रति,<BR>Sa. vii.;<BR>w. is this trial for Rāvaṇa:<BR>दश-<BR>कन्धरस्य कैषा परीक्षा, B. r.;<BR>w. is his object in<BR>sending such a message:<BR>एवं सन्दिशतस्तस्य कोऽभि-<BR>प्रायः, K. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

what
WHAT (rel.): that which: q. v.: यद्॥॥॥तद्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whatever
WHATEVER, WHATSOEVER:<BR>(1) यद् यद्, w. sin:<BR>यद्यत्पापम्, Mah. i. 4.: v. Also soever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheal
WHEAL:<BR>I Mine: q. v.: खनिः।<BR>II Scar:<BR>किणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheat
WHEAT: गोधूमः (both the plant and grain).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheaten
WHEATEN:<BR>(1) गोधूम- in comp., w. powder:<BR>गोधूमचूर्णम्;<BR>(2) गोधूममय (f. यी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheedle
WHEEDLE: चाटुभिर्विप्रलभते (लभ्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>coax, flatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheedler
WHEEDLER, WHEEDLING: v. Flatterer, flat-<BR>-tery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheel
WHEEL (subs.):<BR>(1) चक्रम्, two-w.ed carriage:<BR>द्विचक्रं यानम्;<BR>potter's w.:<BR>कुलालचक्रम्;<BR>(2) रथाङ्गम्<BR>(poet.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheel
WHEEL (v.):<BR>I Trans.: आवर्तयति (c. of वृत्).<BR>II Intrans.: आवर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>roll, revolve, turn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheelbarrow
WHEELBARROW: हस्तङ्गमं चक्रम् (?) and sim.<BR>expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheelwright
WHEELWRIGHT: चक्रकार (f. री: (?);<BR>(2) रथ-<BR>कार (f. री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheeze
WHEEZE: सशब्दम्<BR>or<BR>घोषेण श्वसिति (श्वस्, c. 2.),<BR>Sr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whelk
WHELK: शङ्खविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whelp
WHELP: शावः-कः,<BR>lion's w.:<BR>सिंहशावः; v. Young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

when
WHEN:<BR>I Rel.:<BR>(1) यदा, w. (she)<BR>saw no<BR>other source for acquiring him:<BR>यदा तस्याधिगमेऽन्यं<BR> विधिं नापश्यत्, Ku.;<BR>w. I heard that Arjuna had<BR>won Draupadī:<BR>यदाश्रौषं द्रौपदीं निर्जितामर्जुनेन,<BR>Mah.;<BR>(2) by loc. absol. (when denoting<BR>sequence),<BR>w. Chandrāpīḍa said this:<BR>इत्यभिहित-<BR>वति चन्द्रापीडे, K.; w. the night had declined:<BR>अवसन्नायां रात्रौ, H.;<BR>(3) यर्हि (rare).<BR>II<BR>Interro.:<BR>(1) कदा,<BR>w. did Paraśurāma conquer<BR>the heaven and the hell:<BR>कदा नु खलु परशुरामो<BR> रसातलत्रिदिवयोर्जेता, B. r.; I donot know w.:<BR>न वेद्मि कदा॥।, Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whence
WHENCE:<BR>I Rel.:<BR>(1) यतः,<BR>w. you apprehend<BR>disregard:<BR>विशङ्कसे भीरु यतोऽवधीरणाम्, Sa. iii.<BR>16.;<BR>(2) यस्मात्।<BR>II Interro.: कुतः,<BR>whence<BR>have you come:<BR>कुतो भवान्, Mr. ii.;<BR>(2) कस्मात्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whenever
WHENEVER, WHENSOEVER:<BR>(1) यदा यदा;<BR>(2)<BR>यदा कदाचित्;<BR>(3) यर्हि (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

where
WHERE:<BR>I Interro.:<BR>(1) कुत्र,<BR>w. did you get<BR>this:<BR>कुत्र त्वयैतत्समासादितम्, Sa.;<BR>(2) क्व,<BR>w. is<BR>that destroyer of the ten-headed:<BR>कासौ<BR> दशास्यान्तकः, Bho.<BR>II Relative: यत्र,<BR>w. Rāma<BR>passed sometime:<BR>यत्र रामः कञ्चित् कालमुवास, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whereas
WHEREAS:<BR>(1) यतः;<BR>(2) यस्मात्: v. Since.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whereby
WHEREBY:<BR>I Relative: येन।<BR>II Interro.:<BR>केन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wherefore
WHEREFORE:<BR>I Rel.: यदर्थम्।<BR>II Interro.:<BR>किमर्थम्: v. Why.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wherein
WHEREIN:<BR>I Rel.: यत्र।<BR>II Interro.: कुत्र।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whereof
WHEREOF:<BR>I Rel.: यस्य।<BR>II Interro.: कस्य।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whereto
WHERETO:<BR>I Rel.: यत्र।<BR>II Interro.: कुत्र।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whereupon
WHEREUPON: यदन्तरम् (= after which); तदा<BR>(= then).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wherever
WHEREVER:<BR>(1) यत्र यत्र;<BR>(2) यतो यतः;<BR>(3)<BR>यत्र कुत्रचित् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wherry
WHERRY: क्षुद्रनौकाविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whet
WHET (v.): शाण्यति (nomi.),<BR>with an edge<BR>cleared by w.ting:<BR>शाणेन धौतधारया। N. xvi. 20.:<BR>v. To sharpen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whet
WHET (subs.):<BR>I W. stone: शाणः (णी).<BR>II<BR>Fig.: v. Stimulus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whether
WHETHER (pron.): कतरः (रा, त्): v. Which<BR>(inter.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whether
WHETHER (conj.):<BR>they w. tigers or lions:<BR>ते<BR> व्याघ्रो वा सिंहो वा, S. iii. 2. 9.;<BR>it is doubtful<BR>w. the word<BR>प्राण<BR>here refers to only air, or<BR>soul, or the supreme spirit:<BR>तत्र संशयः किमिह<BR> प्राणशब्देन वायुमात्रममिधीयते, उत जीवः, अथवा परं<BR> ब्रह्मे ति, S. 28.;<BR>w. it is the supreme spirit or<BR>something else:<BR>तत् किं परं ब्रह्म स्यादाहोस्विदर्थान्तरम्,<BR>S. iii. 1.: v. Or.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whetstone
WHETSTONE:<BR>(1) शाणः (also -अश्मन् etc.: v.<BR>Stone), (my)<BR>axe which has been whetted on<BR>the w. of enemies' heads:<BR>रिपुशिरःशाणशातः कुठारः,<BR>Vi. iii. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whey
WHEY:<BR>(1) मस्तु (n.);<BR>(2) दधिमण्ड (mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

which
WHICH (rel.): यत्: v. Who, what.<BR>W. of<BR>two:<BR>यतरः (रा, त्);<BR>w. of many:<BR>यतमः (मा,<BR> -त्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

which
WHICH (inter.): किम्: v. Who, what;<BR>w. of<BR>two:<BR>कतरः (रा, -त्);<BR>w. of many:<BR>कतमः (मा,<BR> -त्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whichever
WHICHEVER: यो यः (या या, यद् यत्): v. Who-<BR>-ever, whatever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whiff
WHIFF:<BR>I Subs.: फुत्कारः<BR>or<BR>फुत्कृतम्।<BR>II Verb:<BR>फुत्करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whig
WHIG: no equiv.: *विगः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

while
WHILE (subs.):<BR>for a little w.:<BR>कियत्क्षणम् or<BR>किञ्चित्कालम्।<BR>After a long w.:<BR>चिरेण: v.<BR>Time, moment. Ph.:<BR>not worth w.:<BR>निष्फल<BR>(f. ला): v. Vain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

while
WHILE, WHILST<BR>(1) यदा: v. When; यावत् (as<BR>a conj.: with तावत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

while
WHILE, -AWAY: गमयति (c. of गम्): v. To<BR>pass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whim
WHIM: कामचारः: v. Caprice, freak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whimper
WHIMPER: चूंकरोति: v. To cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whimsical
WHIMSICAL:<BR>(1) कामचारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) चञ्चल<BR>(f. ला): v. Capricious, fickle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whine
WHINE:<BR>I Verb: v. To complain, murmur.<BR>II Subs.: v. Complaint, murmur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whinny
WHINNY:<BR>(1) खिटखिटायितम् (=murmur);<BR>(2)<BR>क्रन्दितम् (= cry).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whip
WHIP (subs.):<BR>(1) कशा(षा) (also = w. ping), Si.<BR>v. 10.;<BR>(2) प्रतिष्कषः (शः: rare): v. Also<BR>scourge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whip
WHIP (v.): कशया हन्ति (हन्, c. 2.)<BR>or<BR>ताडयति<BR>(c. of तड्);<BR>(2) कशाघातं करोति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whirl
WHIRL:<BR>I Trans.: घूर्णयति (c. of घूर्ण्).<BR>II<BR>Intrans.: घूर्णते (घूर्ण्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>revolve.<BR>III Subs.: घूर्णिः: v. Revolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whirlpool
WHIRLPOOL:<BR>(1) जलावर्तः;<BR>(2) भ्रमिः (मः);<BR>(3)<BR>भ्रमरः, -कः;<BR>(4) जलगुल्मः;<BR>(5) अवघूर्णः;<BR>(6) आवर्तनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whirlwind
WHIRLWIND:<BR>(1) चक्रवातः;<BR>(2) वातावर्तः;<BR>(3)<BR>वायुगुल्मः; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whisk
WHISK:<BR>I Subs.: कूर्च्छम्।<BR>II Verb: आलोडयति<BR>(c. of लुड्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whisker
WHISKER:<BR>(1) गुम्फः (?);<BR>(2) गुम्फलोमन् (n. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whisper
WHISPER: (subs.):<BR>(1) expr. by verb.;<BR>(2) जनरवः (=rumour).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whisper
WHISPER: (v.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) कर्णमूले वदति<BR>(वद्, c. 1.), V. p.;<BR>(2) कर्णाकर्णि कथयति (कथ्,<BR>c. 10.),<BR>all the Yādavas w. ed among them-<BR>selves that Prasena was not murdered by any-<BR>body else:<BR>नान्येन प्रसेनो हन्यत इत्यखिल एव यदुलोकः<BR> कर्णाकर्ण्यकथयत्, V.p.;<BR>(3) कर्णे जपति (जप्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whist
WHIST:<BR>I Subs.: तासक्रीडाविशेषः।<BR>II Silent,<BR>silence: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whistle
WHISTLE: शीशयति (nomi.: (?); शीशं ददाति<BR>(दा, c. 3: (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whistle
WHISTLE (subs.):<BR>I W. ing: शीशः, -शब्दः (?):<BR>v. Also cry, noise.<BR>II An instrument:<BR>वंशः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whit
WHIT: लेशः: v. Iota, Ph.:<BR>not a w.:<BR>न<BR> मनागपि;<BR>every w.:<BR>सर्वथा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

white
WHITE (adj.):<BR>(1) शुक्ल (f. क्ला);<BR>(2) श्वेत (f.<BR>ता);<BR>(3) धवल (f. ला);<BR>(4) सित (f. ता);<BR>(5) गौर (f. री);<BR>(6) शुभ्र (f. भ्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

white
WHITE (subs.):<BR>I The colour:<BR>(1) शुक्लः,<BR> -वर्णः;<BR>(2) श्वेतः, -वर्णः, etc.<BR>II Of the eye:<BR>श्वेतभागः, Bha. and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whitebait
WHITEBAIT: क्षुद्रमत्स्यविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whiten
WHITEN:<BR>I Trans.:<BR>(1) धवलयति (nomi.);<BR>(2) धवलीकरोति;<BR>(3) शुक्लीकरोति; etc. Intrans.:<BR>(1) धवलायते (nomi.);<BR>(2) धवलीभवति;<BR>(3)<BR>श्वेतीभवति; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whiteness
WHITENESS:<BR>(1) शुक्लता, त्वम्; धवलता, -त्वम्, etc.;<BR>(2) शौक्ल्यम् etc.;<BR>(3) श्वेतिमन्, धवलिमन्, सितिमन्<BR>(m.); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whitewash
WHITEWASH:<BR>I Subs.: सुधालेपः।<BR>II Verb.:<BR>सुधया लिम्पति, आ-, वि- (लिप्, c. 6.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whither
WHITHER:<BR>I Interro.:<BR>(1) क्व;<BR>(2) कुत्र।<BR>II<BR>Rel.: यत्र।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whitish
WHITISH:<BR>(1) ईषच्छुक्ल (f. क्ला);<BR>(2) आश्वेत (f.<BR>ता); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whitlow
WHITLOW:<BR>(1) चिप्पम्;<BR>(2) नखंपचः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whitsuntide
WHITSUNTIDE, WHITSUNDAY: *श्वेतार्कवासरः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whiz
WHIZ: शणशणायते (nomi. : (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

who
WHO:<BR>I Interro.: किम्,<BR>w. is here:<BR>कः कोऽत्र<BR> मोः, U.;<BR>w. does not know Agastya:<BR>कः<BR> पुनरगस्त्यं न जानाति, B. r.;<BR>w. is this girl:<BR>केयं<BR> कन्यका, K.<BR>II Rel.:<BR>(1) यद्,<BR>I w. with two<BR>arms:<BR>योऽहं दाभ्यां भुजाभ्याम्, Vi. vi. ii.;<BR>whom<BR>the wise call resplendent lustre:<BR>प्रेद्धं धाम यदा-<BR>मनन्ति सुधियः, Vi. iv. 30. (G. § 145);<BR>(2) by<BR>bah. comp. (G. § 298).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whoever
WHOEVER: v. Whosoever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whole
WHOLE (adj.):<BR>(1) सकलः (ला, लं),<BR>the w.<BR>mountain:<BR>सकलः शैलः, Ki. xiii. 16.;<BR>(2)<BR>समग्र (f. ग्रा),<BR>the w. kingdom:<BR>समग्रं राज्यम्,<BR>K.;<BR>(3) कृत्स्न (f. त्स्ना);<BR>(4) अखण्ड (f. ण्डा):<BR>v. Also entire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whole
WHOLE (subs.):<BR>(1) साकल्यम्;<BR>(2) कार्त्स्न्यम्;<BR>etc. Ph.: w. of = whole (adj.): q. v.:<BR>w.<BR>of the Rāmāyaṇa:<BR>समग्रं रामायणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wholesale
WHOLESALE:<BR>w.-dealer:<BR>स्तूपविक्रयिन् (f. णी:<BR>?);<BR>w.-purchase:<BR>स्तूपक्रयः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wholesome
WHOLESOME:<BR>(1) पथ्य (f. थ्या),<BR>is generally<BR>very w. for all animals:<BR>सर्वप्राणिनां सामान्यतः<BR> पथ्यतमः, Sr.;<BR>(2) हित (f. ता = good),<BR>abso-<BR>lutely w.:<BR>एकान्तहित (f. ता), Sr.;<BR>(3) क्षेम्य<BR>(f. म्या= salutary: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wholly
WHOLLY:<BR>(1) साकल्येन;<BR>(2) कार्त्स्न्येन;<BR>(3)<BR>समग्रम्;<BR>(4) सम्पूर्णम्;<BR>(5) अशेषेण;<BR>(6) निरवशेषम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whoop
WHOOP: war w.:<BR>(1) सिंहनादः;<BR>(2) क्ष्वेडा,<BR> -डितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whore
WHORE: वेश्या: v. Prostitute, harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whoredom
WHOREDOM:<BR>(1) वेश्यावृत्तिः and sim. comp. s.<BR>(of women);<BR>(2) वेश्याप्रसक्तिः and sim.<BR>comp. s. (of men),<BR>to commit w.:<BR>वेश्यां भुंक्ते<BR> भजते, सेवते, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whoremonger
WHOREMONGER:<BR>(1) वेश्यागामिन् (m.);<BR>(2)<BR>भुजङ्गः;<BR>(3) विटः;<BR>(4) गम्यः (rare), “हृतशिष्टानां<BR> गम्यधनानां चित्रैरुपायैरपहरणम्,” D. ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whoreson
WHORESON: वेश्यापुत्रः and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whosoever
WHOSOEVER:<BR>(1) यो यः (या या, यद्यत्), at whom-<BR>soever lady the beloved (Kṛṣṇa)<BR>looked:<BR>यां यां<BR> प्रियः प्रैक्षत, Si. iii. 16.;<BR>(2) यः कश्चित्<BR>or<BR>कश्चन<BR>(या काचित्<BR>or<BR>-चन, यत्किञ्चित्<BR>or<BR>-चन) (= any<BR>one w. G. 301).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

why
WHY (adv.):<BR>(1) किम् (not absol.),<BR>w. are you<BR>thus tiring yourself for nothing:<BR>व्यर्थ परिश्राम्यसि<BR> वा किमित्थम्, N. iii. 13;<BR>(2) कुतः<BR>or<BR>कस्मात्, w.<BR>because the word soul (is used): कस्मात् आत्म-<BR>शब्दात्, S.;<BR>(3) किमर्थम् (= for what object);<BR>(4) किन्निमित्तम्;<BR>(5) किंकारणम्, केन हेतुना,<BR> कस्माद्धेतोः, etc. (= for what reason).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

why
WHY (interj.):<BR>w. what have I done:<BR>किं नाम<BR> मया कृतम्;<BR>w. yes I say so:<BR>वाढं ब्रवीम्येवम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wick
WICK:<BR>(1) दशा;<BR>(2) वर्तिः, -का;<BR>(3) पिञ्जलम्;<BR>(4) तैलिनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wicked
WICKED:<BR>I Of men:<BR>(1) दुष्ट (f. ष्टा);<BR>(2)<BR>दुर्वृत्त (f. त्ता);<BR>(3) दुरात्मन् (mfn.);<BR>(3) पाप-<BR>कर्मन् (mfn.);<BR>(5) पामर (f. रा);<BR>(6) खल (f.<BR>ला);<BR>(7) पापमति (mfn.) and sim. comp. s.<BR>II Of acts:<BR>(1) दुष्ट (f. ष्टा);<BR>(2) पाप- in<BR>comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wickedly
WICKEDLY:<BR>(1) दुष्टतया;<BR>(2) दुर्वृत्ततया;<BR>(3)<BR>दुराचारतया; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wickedness
WICKEDNESS:<BR>(1) दुष्टता;<BR>(2) दुर्वृत्तता;<BR>(3)<BR>दुराचारता, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wicker
WICKER:<BR>(1) वैदल (f. ली);<BR>(2) वैणव (f. वी),<BR>w.-work:<BR>वैदलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wide
WIDE:<BR>(1) विस्तीर्ण (f. र्णा);<BR>(2) विशाल (f.<BR>ला);<BR>(3) विपुल (f. ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wide
WIDE, WIDELY:<BR>(1) विस्तीर्णम्;<BR>(2) विशालम्;<BR>(3) विपुलम्। Ph.:<BR>w. awake:<BR>सुप्रबुद्ध (f. द्धा);<BR>w. open:<BR>सुविवृत (f. ता);<BR>w. -spread:<BR>बहुविस्तीर्ण<BR>(f. र्णा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

widen
WIDEN:<BR>(1) विशालीकरोति;<BR>(2) पृथूकरोति;<BR>(3)<BR>by adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wideness
WIDENESS:<BR>(1) विस्तीर्णता;<BR>(2) विशालता;<BR>(3) पृथुता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

widow
WIDOW:<BR>(1) विधवा;<BR>(2) गतभर्तृका;<BR>(3) रण्डा<BR>(specially as a term of abuse).<BR>A w. before<BR>puberty:<BR>बालविधवा; a<BR>childless w.:<BR>अवीरा, A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

widow
WIDOW (v.): विधवां करोति। W. ed:<BR>(1) अनाथः<BR>(था, थं);<BR>(2) गतभर्तृक (f. का) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR>Un-w.ed lady:<BR>अविधवा, Me. ii. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

widower
WIDOWER:<BR>(1) मृतभार्यः, P. iv. 9.;<BR>(2) मृतपत्नीकः,<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

widowhood
WIDOWHOOD: वैधव्यम्,<BR>burning with w.:<BR>वैधव्यता-<BR>पितः (ता, तं), Ki. xi. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

width
WIDTH:<BR>(1) विस्तारः;<BR>(2) व्यासः;<BR>(3) परिणाहः:<BR>v. Breadth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wield
WIELD:<BR>(1) विभर्ति (भृ, c. 3. = hold);<BR>(2)<BR>प्रणयति (नी, c. 1. = manage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wife
WIFE:<BR>(1) भार्या;<BR>(2) जाया;<BR>(3) पत्नी;<BR>(4) दाराः<BR>(only in m. pl.);<BR>(5) स्त्री;<BR>(6) वधूः;<BR>(7)<BR>कलत्रम्;<BR>(8) सहधर्मिणी (not used absol.);<BR>(9)<BR>परिग्रहः (rare),<BR>although I have many wives:<BR>परि-<BR>ग्रहबहुत्वेऽपि, Sa.<BR>A rival w.:<BR>सपत्नी।<BR>Taking a<BR>w.:<BR>दारपरिग्रहः।<BR>To supersede a w.:<BR>अधिविन्दति<BR>(विद्, c. 6.), R.<BR>W. of a teacher:<BR>उपाध्यायी;<BR>w. of a spiritual guide:<BR>आचार्यानी; w. of Indra:<BR>इन्द्राणी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wig
WIG: *कैशिकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wight
WIGHT: माणवकः: v. Person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wild
WILD:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) by comp., by w. plants:<BR>वनलताभिः, Sa.;<BR>w. mountain scenery:<BR>अरण्य-<BR>गिरिभूमिः, Vi.;<BR>(2) वन्य (f. न्या),<BR>w. instru-<BR>ment of sustenance:<BR>वन्यं स्थितिसाधनम्, R. v. 9.;<BR>(3) आरण्य (f. ण्या), -क (f. का), w. animal:<BR>आरण्यो मृगः, M. v. 9.;<BR>(4) वनजात (f. ता) and<BR>sim. comp.s;<BR>w. animal:<BR>वनजं सत्त्वम्, Ki.<BR>xiii. 8;<BR>marshy and w.:<BR>अनूपोत्थं वनोत्थं च, Mat.<BR>117. 45.<BR>II Fig.: v. Savage, rude.<BR>III<BR>Violent, unrestrained: q. v.: दुर्दान्त (f. न्ता).<BR>IV Bewildered, mad: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wild
WILD, WILDERNESS (subs.):<BR>I Forest, wood:<BR>q. v.: वनम्।<BR>II Desert: q. v.: मरुः,<BR> -भूमिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wildly
WILDLY:<BR>(1) उन्मत्तवत् (=madly);<BR>(2) व्याकुलम्<BR>(= bewildered);<BR>(3) चण्डम् (= violently).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wildness
WILDNESS:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) वन्यता;<BR>(2) better<BR>by adj.<BR>II Irregularity: q. v.: उच्छृङ्खलता,<BR> त्वम्।<BR>III Savageness, ferocity: q. v.:<BR>IV<BR>Alienation: विभ्रमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wile
WILE: छलम्: v. Trick, pretext, deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wilful
WILFUL:<BR>I In good sense:<BR>(1) by adv.;<BR>(2) कामतः कृत (f. ता); etc.<BR>II Perverse,<BR>headstrong:<BR>(1) स्वैरिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) स्वेच्छा-<BR>चारिन् (f. णी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wilfully
WILFULLY:<BR>(1) कामतः;<BR>(2) कामात्;<BR>(3) इच्छा-<BR>पूर्वकम् etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wilfulness
WILFULNESS:<BR>I Voluntariness: expr. by<BR>adv.<BR>II Obstinacy:<BR>(1) कामचारः, कामचारिता;<BR>(2) स्वेच्छाचारिता; etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wilily
WILILY:<BR>(1) छलेन;<BR>(2) मायया;<BR>(3) छद्मना;<BR>(4)<BR>सकपटम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

will
WILL (v.):<BR>I To resolve, determine: q. v.:<BR>(1) संकल्पयति (कॢप, c. 10.);<BR>(2) संकल्पं करोति।<BR>II To direct, order: q. v.: निर्दिशति (दिश,<BR>c. 6.).<BR>III To devise by will: *इच्छापत्रेण<BR> ददाति (दा, c. 3.).<BR>IV Denoting future:<BR>expr. by ऌट्<BR>or<BR>लुट् (Vide Grammar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

will
WILL (subs.):<BR>I Volition: संकल्पः।<BR>II De-<BR>-sire, wish: q. v.: कामः, against one's will:<BR>अकामतः, M.<BR>III Testament: *इच्छापत्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

willing
WILLING:<BR>I Desirous, consenting:<BR>(1) इच्छु,<BR>(mfn.), -क (f. का);<BR>(2) सकाम (f. मा),<BR>a w.<BR>woman:<BR>सकामा स्त्री।<BR>II Chosen, desired:<BR>इष्ट (f. ष्टा), अभि-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

willingly
WILLINGLY:<BR>(1) साग्रहम् (= zealously);<BR>(2)<BR>सानुरागम् (= ardently).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

willow
WILLOW: वृक्षविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wily
WILY:<BR>(1) बहुच्छल (f. ला);<BR>(2) कपटप्रिय (f. या);<BR>(3) चतुर (f. रा = artful).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

win
WIN:<BR>I In a contest: जयति, विजयते (जि,<BR>c. 1.),<BR>I have won:<BR>जितम्, Mah. ii. 61. 27.;<BR>I won (the case)<BR>first:<BR>जित एव मयायं प्राक्, Mit.<BR>II To gain, get: q. v.: लभते (लभ्, (c. 1.),<BR>what is won in a controversy:<BR>यद्वादाल्लब्धं, विवादे<BR> यन्निस्तीर्य लब्धम्, Da. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wince
WINCE: v. To shrink, start.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

winch
WINCH: perh. दण्डः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wind
WIND (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) वायुः,<BR>with favour-<BR>able w.:<BR>अनुकूलेन वायुना, Mah. i. 148. 20.;<BR>(2) वातः,<BR>head w.:<BR>प्रतिवातः, D. vi.;<BR>(3) पवनः,<BR>gentle w.:<BR>मृदुपवनः, V. iv.;<BR>(4) अनिलः,<BR>w.<BR>footed:<BR>अनिलरंहस्, (mfn.), Mah.;<BR>(5) समीरः,<BR> -णः;<BR>(6) मरुत्;<BR>(7) मारुतः।<BR>II Of stomach: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">Page763</a>]<BR>वायुः।<BR>III Flatulence: q. v.<BR>IV Breath:<BR>श्वासः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wind
WIND (v. i.):<BR>I To bend: वक्रं<BR>or<BR>कुटिलं गच्छति<BR>(गम्, c. 1.) or सर्पति (सृप्, c. 1.), w. ing: v.<BR>Crooked.<BR>II To turn: q. v.: आवर्तते (वृत्,<BR>c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wind
WIND (v. t.):<BR>I To turn, twine: आवर्तयति (c.<BR>of वृत्).<BR>II To blow: q. v.: पूरयति (पूर्,<BR>c. 10.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wind up
WIND UP:<BR>I Lit.: सम्पुटीकरोति।<BR>II To con-<BR>-clude: उपसंहरति, (हृ, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

windfall
WINDFALL:<BR>I Lit.: *वायुपातः।<BR>II Fig.: आक-<BR>स्मिकसमागमः and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

winding
WINDING (subs.): वक्रम्: v. Bend, crooked-<BR>-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

winding-sheet
WINDING-SHEET: आच्छादनम्: v. Shroud,<BR>cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

windlass
WINDLASS: *उत्तोलनयन्त्रम्, उत्तोलनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

windmill
WINDMILL: *वायुचलं चक्रम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

window
WINDOW:<BR>(1) वातायनम्, taking to the w. s:<BR>वातायनसंश्रित (f. ता), R. vi. 24.;<BR>(2) गवाक्षः,<BR>the w. s filled with the faces:<BR>व्याप्तान्तरा मुखैस्तासां<BR> गवाक्षाः R. vii. 11.;<BR>(3) जालः (ली, लम्)<BR>another looking through the w.:<BR>जालान्तरप्रेषितदृष्टि-<BR>रन्या, R. vii. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

windward
WINDWARD (adj.): वाताभिमुख (f. खी) and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

windy
WINDY:<BR>(1) वातल (f. ली);<BR>(2) वातमय (f. यी)<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wine
WINE:<BR>(1) मद्यम्,<BR>to drink w.:<BR>मद्यं पिबति;<BR>to take<BR>w.:<BR>मद्यं सेवते, Ni.;<BR>new w.:<BR>नवं मद्यम्, Sr.;<BR>w.<BR>pot:<BR>मद्यमाण्डम्, P.; destroying the smell of w.:<BR>भद्यगन्धनाशनम्, Bha.;<BR>(2) मदिरा, w. -tasting:<BR>मदिरास्वादः, Si.;<BR>(3) मधु (poet.), sweet w.:<BR>स्वादु मधु, Si.;<BR>(4) सुरा (= spirit), to make w.:<BR>सुरां करोति, Mah.;<BR>(5) आसवः (= liquor),<BR>taking of w.:<BR>आसवसेवनम्, D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wine-bibber
WINE-BIBBER:<BR>(1) मद्यपः;<BR>(2) मद्यपायिन् (m.);<BR>(3) सुरापः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wine-seller
WINE-SELLER: शौण्डिकः (f. की, the Śuri caste).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wing
WING (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) पक्षः,<BR>protected me<BR>with his own w. s:<BR>स्वपक्षाभ्यां मामरक्षत्, Vi. v.<BR>5.; stretched the w. s and flew up to heaven:<BR>वितत्य पक्षौ नभ उत्पपात, Mah. i. 25. 17.;<BR>root<BR>of a w.:<BR>पक्षतिः, N. ii. 2.;<BR>(2) पतत्रम्;<BR>(3)<BR>गरुत् (m.: rare). Ph.:<BR>on the w.:<BR>डीयते: v.<BR>To fly.<BR>II Fig., as of an army: पक्षः,<BR>who<BR>formed side-w.s and w. s:<BR>के ते प्रपक्षौ पक्षौ वा,<BR>Mah. viii. 46. 6. Ph.: under the w. s of:<BR>expr. by: आश्रितः (ता, तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

winged
WINGED:<BR>(1) पक्षिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) पक्षवत् (f.<BR>ती);<BR>(3) पतत्रिन् (f. णी);<BR>(4) पक्षयुक्त (f. क्ता);<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wink
WINK (subs.): Of the eye: निमेषः।<BR>II Hint:<BR>(1) नेत्रसंकेतः;<BR>(2) अक्षिसंज्ञा, and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wink
WINK (v.):<BR>I Of the eye:<BR>(1) निमिषति (मिष्,<BR>c. 6.);<BR>(2) निमीलति (मील्, c. 1. = close).<BR>II To make a sign: नेत्रेण सङ्केतं ददाति (दा<BR>c. 3.)<BR>or<BR>संज्ञां करोति। W. at, i. e. connive:<BR>उपेक्षते (ईक्ष्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

winner
WINNER:<BR>(1) जयिन् (f. नी), Mit.: v. Victor;<BR>(2) लब्धृ (f. ब्ध्री = gainer);<BR>(3) by verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

winning
WINNING:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) by verb: v. To<BR>win;<BR>(2) लाभः (= profit);<BR>(3) अर्जितम् (=<BR>earning).<BR>II Adj.: हृदयहारिन् (f. णी): v.<BR>Charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

winnow
WINNOW:<BR>I Lit.: शोधयति, वि- (c. of शुध्):<BR>v. To cleanse, purify. Ph.: w. ing fan:<BR>सू(शू)र्प (mn.).<BR>II Fig.: to sift, examine:<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

winnower
WINNOWER:<BR>(1) शोधक (f. धिका);<BR>(2) पावक,<BR> -निः (f. विका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

winnowing-fan
WINNOWING-FAN: शू(सू)र्प (mn.), D. vi.;<BR>(2)<BR>प्रस्फोटनम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

winter
WINTER (subs.):<BR>I The season:<BR>(1) हेमन्तः<BR>(Nov.-Jan.);<BR>(2) शिशिरः (Jan.-March);<BR>(3)<BR>हिमागमः, Si.;<BR>(4) तुषारकालः, Ki.; and sim.<BR>comp.s.<BR>II = year: शरद् (f. = autumn),<BR>ten<BR>thousand w. s passed:<BR>शरदामयुतं ययौ, R. x. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

winter
WINTER (v.): हेमन्तं गमयति (c. of गम्), नयति (नी,<BR>c. 1.), etc.: v. To pass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wintery
WINTERY, WINTRY:<BR>I Lit.: expr. by comp.<BR>II Cold: q. v.: शीत (f. ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wire
WIRE:<BR>I Subs.:<BR>(1) तन्त्रम्(न्त्री);<BR>(2) तारः।<BR>II<BR>Verb: ताडिततन्त्रेण प्रेषयति (c. of इष्): v. To<BR>send.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wisdom
WISDOM:<BR>(1) प्रज्ञा;<BR>(2) ज्ञानम् (= knowledge:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(3) बुद्धिः (= intellect: q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wise
WISE:<BR>I Having wisdom:<BR>(1) प्राज्ञ (f. ज्ञा);<BR>(2) विज्ञ (f. ज्ञा);<BR>(3) प्रज्ञावत् (f. ती);<BR>(4)<BR>धीमत् (f. ती): v. Intelligent;<BR>(5) ज्ञानिन्<BR>(f. नी): v. Learned;<BR>(6) विवेकिन् (f. नी):<BR>v. Prudent.<BR>II Of acts etc.: w. saying:<BR>बुधभाषितम्;<BR>w. action:<BR>ज्ञानमूला क्रिया; w. intellect:<BR>विवेकिनी मतिः;<BR>w. deportment:<BR>विवेकव्यवहारः;<BR>etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wise
WISE (subs.): v. Manner, way. Ph.:<BR>in no<BR>w.:<BR>न कथञ्चन;<BR>in any wise:<BR>केनापि प्रकारेण।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wiseacre
WISEACRE:<BR>(1) पण्डिताभिमानिन् (f. नी);<BR>(2)<BR>पण्डितम्मन्य (f. न्या); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wisely
WISELY:<BR>(1) प्रज्ञया;<BR>(2) ज्ञानेन;<BR>(3) सविवेकम्<BR>(= prudently);<BR>(4) प्रसमीक्ष्य (= considerate-<BR>-ly);<BR>(5) सम्यक् (= well).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wish
WISH (v.): इच्छति (इष्, c. 6.),<BR>I w. to know<BR>from the beginning:<BR>आदितः श्रोतुमिच्छामि, Mu.<BR>ii.;<BR>(2) अभिलषति (लष्, c. 1.), w.ing valour:<BR>विक्रममभिलषत् (f. न्ती), Ki. xvii. 64.;<BR>(3)<BR>कामयते, अभि- (कम्, c. 1.),<BR>I do not w. such<BR>decrepitude:<BR>तां जरां न कामये, Mah.;<BR>(4) वाञ्छति<BR>(वाञ्छ्, c. 1.);<BR>(5) काङ्क्षति (काङ्क्ष्, c. 1.);<BR>(6) by desi.: v. Also to long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wish
WISH (subs.):<BR>(1) इच्छा;<BR>(2) कामना;<BR>(3) मनोरथः;<BR>(4) इष्टम्;<BR>(5) ईप्सितम्;<BR>(6) वाच्छितम्: v.<BR>Desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wisp
WISP: a small bundle: कूर्च (mn.), -क (mn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wistful
WISTFUL, WISTFULLLY: v. Eager, eagerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wit
WIT:<BR>I Intellect: q. v.: धीः।<BR>II Humour:<BR>(1) प्रज्ञा (?);<BR>(2) सरसता (?).<BR>III A witty<BR>man: वाक्चतुर (f. रा) and sim. comp.s (?).<BR>Ph.:<BR>to w.;<BR>तद्यथा: v. Namely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

witch
WITCH:<BR>(1) डाकिनी;<BR>(2) मायाविनी;<BR>(3) मायिनी;<BR>(4) कुहकिनी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

witchcraft
WITCHCRAFT: माया: v. Sorcery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

with
WITH:<BR>I Denoting instrument, means: by<BR>ins.,<BR>to play w. dice:<BR>अक्षैर्दीव्यति, Ve. i. 13.;<BR>not only w. (their)<BR>hearts:<BR>न केवलं हृदयेन, N.<BR>xi. 2.;<BR>he was looked w. greater respect:<BR>गौरवेण<BR> ददृशेतरामसौ, Si. xiv. 43.<BR>II Along w.: by<BR>ins. gen. with सह (or rarely) साकं, सार्धम्,<BR>समम्,<BR>to live w. Brahmans:<BR>ब्राह्मणैर्वसति, Mah.<BR>i. 84. 2.; did not burn himself w. the queen:<BR>न चकार शरीरमग्निसात् सह देव्या, R. viii. 72.;<BR>w.<BR>Uddhava and Balavbhadra:<BR>सार्धमुद्धवसीरिभ्याम्,<BR>Si. ii. 2.;<BR>w. your fame, your body is getting<BR>thin:<BR>परैति कार्श्यं यशसा समं वपुः, Ki. i. 39.<BR>III Denoting manner:<BR>(1) by adv. with<BR>स,<BR>w. pleasure:<BR>सहर्षम्;<BR>w. alarm:<BR>सोद्वेगम्;<BR>(2) by adj.,<BR>w. great pleasure:<BR>मुदा परमया<BR> युतः;<BR>w. stick in hand:<BR>दण्डहस्तः; etc.;<BR>the<BR>goddess w. ten arms:<BR>दशभुजा।<BR>IV On the<BR>side of:<BR>the divine sages were w. the sons of<BR>Pāṇḍu:<BR>देवर्षीणां गणाः पाण्डवतोऽभवन्, Mah. viii.<BR>87. 51.<BR>V In the opinion of: expr. w.<BR>मतम्,<BR>“w. the ancients”:<BR>प्राचां मते।<BR>VI With<BR>verbs denoting resentment etc.: by dat.<BR>(G.). Ph.: one w. another:<BR>(1) परस्परम्;<BR>(2)<BR>अन्योऽन्यम्। N. B. w. with verbs is also expr.<BR>by सम्- in comp.,<BR>to live w.:<BR>संवसति।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

withal
WITHAL:<BR>(1) सममेव (= at the same time);<BR>(2) तथा च (=likewise).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

withdraw
WITHDRAW:<BR>(1) अपनयति (नी, c. 1.): v. To<BR>remove, take away;<BR>(2) संहरति, उप-, प्रति-<BR>(हृ, c. 1. = draw back), w. ing and throwing:<BR>संहारविक्षेपौ, R. v. 45.;<BR>(3) अपकर्षति<BR>or<BR>अपा-<BR>(कृष्, c. 1.): v. To draw away, draw off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

withdraw
WITHDRAW (v. i.):<BR>(1) अपक्रामति (क्रम्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) अपसरति (सृ, c. 1.): v. To retire, flee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wither
WITHER:<BR>I Intrans.: म्लायति (म्लै, c. 1.):<BR>v. To fade, waste.<BR>II Trans.: म्लापयति,<BR> परि- (c. of म्लै).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

withers
WITHERS: स्कन्धः, -देशः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

withhold
WITHHOLD:<BR>(1) संहरति (हृ, c. 1. draw back),<BR>w. your anger:<BR>क्रोधं संहर, Ku. iii. 72.;<BR>(2)<BR>निगृह्नाति (ग्रह्, c. 9.): v. To restrain, check;<BR>(3) प्रतिबध्नाति (बन्ध्, c. 9.): v. To obstruct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

within
WITHIN (adj. or adv.): अन्तर्: v. Inner,<BR>inward, in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

within
WITHIN (prep.):<BR>I Inside: w. the house:<BR>अन्तर्गृहम्, गृहाभ्यन्तरे<BR>or<BR>गृहमध्ये: v. Also in.<BR>II Of time:<BR>w. ten days:<BR>अन्तर्दशाहात्, M.<BR>viii. 222;<BR>w. a week:<BR>सप्ताहमध्ये, K. b. or<BR>सप्ताहाभ्यन्तरे, Mit.<BR>or<BR>सप्ताहात्, M. viii. 108.: [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">Page765</a>]<BR>v. Also in.<BR>III In the limits of:<BR>w.<BR>sight:<BR>दृष्टिगोचर (f. रा): w. one's power:<BR>हस्तवर्तिन् (f. नी);<BR>w. arrow-shot:<BR>बाणविषय<BR>(f. या); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

without
WITHOUT (prep.):<BR>I Before nouns:<BR>(1) विना<BR>(with ins. or acc., rarely with abl.),<BR>I can-<BR>not remain a moment w. you:<BR>न शक्नोमि मवता<BR> विना क्षणमष्यवस्थातुम्, K.;<BR>(2) by negatives,<BR>w.<BR>eyes He sees, w. ears He hears:<BR>पश्यत्यचक्षुः स<BR> शृणोत्यकर्णः, S.: v. Devoid of;<BR>(3) अन्तरेण<BR>(with acc.: rarely),<BR>there is no pleasure w.<BR>God:<BR>अन्तरेण हरिं न सुखम्, S. k.;<BR>(4) ऋते (with acc.<BR>and abl.),<BR>w. a general:<BR>ऋते सेनाप्रणेतारम्, Mah.<BR>v. 150-2.<BR>(5) by part.s, वर्जयित्वा (= leav-<BR>-ing off) etc.; “न भूरिदानं विरहय्य सत्क्रियाम्”,<BR>Ki. i. 12.; “न हीन्द्रियाण्यनुपादाय प्रत्यक्षादिव्यवहारः<BR> सम्भवति”, S.<BR>II Before part.s: अ (अन्,<BR>before vowels), w. reducing dust to mud:<BR>अनीत्वा पङ्कतां धूलिम्, Si. ii. 34.; w. being seen:<BR>अलक्षितः (ता, तं), etc.<BR>III Outside of:<BR>q. v.: बहिः (with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

without
WITHOUT (adv.): बहिस्,<BR>lying w.:<BR>बहिःस्थ (f.<BR>स्था): v. Externally, outside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

withstand
WITHSTAND: प्रतिकूलयति (nomi.): v. To resist,<BR>oppose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

witness
WITNESS (subs.):<BR>I<BR>The person w. ing:<BR>साक्षिन्<BR>(m.),<BR>one w. is no w.:<BR>एकश्चासाक्षी, V. s.; and<BR>among women, women (will be)<BR>w. es:<BR>स्त्रियः<BR> स्त्रीषु च साक्षिणः, N. s.; in the absence of w. es:<BR>साक्ष्यभावे, M.; to cite, swear, examine w. es:<BR>साक्षिणः दिशति, शापयति, परीक्षते, M.;<BR>w. es for<BR>the prosecution, for the defence:<BR>साक्षिणः पूर्ववादिनः,<BR> उत्तरवादिनः, Y.;<BR>ear-w.:<BR>श्रुतसाक्षी, Mit.;<BR>to<BR>produce w. es:<BR>साक्षिण उपन्यस्यति, Mit.; “जागर-<BR>दुःखसाक्षिणी निशा च शय्या च”, N. i. 49.<BR>II<BR>Testimony: साक्ष्यम्,<BR>to bear w.:<BR>साक्ष्यं ददाति,<BR>Y.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

witness
WITNESS (v. i.): साक्ष्यं ददाति (दा, c. 3.), Y. or<BR>वदति (वद्, c. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

witness
WITNESS (v. t.):<BR>I To see or know: q. v.:<BR>(1) प्रत्यक्षीकरोति, I will w. the king's doing:<BR>राजर्षेर्वृत्तान्तं प्रत्यक्षीकरिष्यामि, Sa. vi.;<BR>(2) expr.<BR>by subs.<BR>II To testify: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

witticism
WITTICISM:<BR>(1) प्राज्ञभाषितम्;<BR>(2) सरसोक्तिः;<BR>(3)<BR>नर्मवाक्यम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wittily
WITTILY:<BR>(1) सरसम् (= humorously);<BR>(2)<BR>बुद्धिविलासेन (?);<BR>(3) भङ्ग्या (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

witty
WITTY:<BR>(1) प्राज्ञ (f. ज्ञा = wise);<BR>(2) रसिक (f.<BR>का = humorous): v. Also wit (III).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wizard
WIZARD: मायाकारः: v. Magician, sorcerer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woad
WOAD: लताविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woe
WOE:<BR>I Subs.: दुःखम्: v. Distress, sorrow.<BR>II Interj.:<BR>(1) हा (= alas);<BR>(2) धिक्<BR>(= shame).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woeful
WOEFUL, WOEFULLY: v. Sorrowful, sorrow-<BR>-fully, calamitous, miserable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wolf
WOLF:<BR>(1) वृकः,<BR>she-w.:<BR>वृकी;<BR>(2) कोकः;<BR>(3)<BR>ईहामृगः (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wolfs bane
WOLF'S BANE: वत्सनाभजातीयो वृक्षभेदः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woman
WOMAN:<BR>(1) स्त्री, for as w. should not leave<BR>(their)<BR>husbands:<BR>अत्याज्यो हि यथा भर्ता स्त्रीणाम्,<BR>M. p. 71. 11.; w.'s (separate)<BR>property:<BR>स्त्रीधनम्,<BR>Da. 53.;<BR>(2) नारी,<BR>six vices of w.:<BR>नारीणां<BR> दूषणानि षट्, H. 114.;<BR>(3) अङ्गना,<BR>what fault w.<BR>really have:<BR>दोषोऽस्ति सत्यं कतरोऽङ्गनानाम्, V. m.<BR>74. 6.;<BR>(4) प्रमदा,<BR>that w. follow the way of<BR>their husbands:<BR>प्रमदा पतिवर्त्मगा इति, Ku. iv.<BR>33.;<BR>(5) अबला;<BR>(6) योषित्;<BR>(7) वधूः (sp.<BR>married w.);<BR>(8) कामिनी;<BR>(9) नितम्बिनी;<BR>(10) विलासिनी;<BR>(11) सीमन्तिनी;<BR>(12) वरारोहा;<BR>(13) मत्तकाशिनी;<BR>(14) by adj., young w.:<BR>युवती;<BR>old w.:<BR>वृद्धा; w. with beautiful brows:<BR>सुभ्रूः। N. B. 8. to 13 are for beautiful w.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

womanish
WOMANISH: स्त्रौण (f. णी): v. Effeminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

womanishly
WOMANISHLY: स्त्रीवत् (= like a woman), Ve. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

womanly
WOMANLY:<BR>(1) by comp.;<BR>(2) स्त्रैण (f. णी):<BR>v. Feminine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

womb
WOMB: गर्भः: v. Also uterus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wonder
WONDER (subs.):<BR>I Astonishment:<BR>(1)<BR>विस्मयः,<BR>with eyes blooming with, w.:<BR>विस्मय-<BR>विकसिताक्षी, D. i.;<BR>(2) चमत्कारः, चमत्कारिता;<BR>(3) आश्चर्यम्, -त्वम्;<BR>(4) चित्रीया (rare).<BR>II<BR>Anything w. ful:<BR>(1) अद्भुतम्, great w. to us:<BR>महदद्भुतं नः, Vi. iv. 50;<BR>(2) आश्चर्यम्,<BR>it is a great<BR>w.:<BR>इदमेव महदाश्चर्यम्, K.;<BR>(3) चित्रम् (= strange:<BR>q. v.),<BR>it is no w.:<BR>नैतच्चित्रम्, Sa. ii. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wonder
WONDER (v.):<BR>(1) विस्मयते (स्मि, c. 1.),<BR>neither<BR>w. ed nor felt dejected:<BR>न विसिस्मिये न विषसाद,<BR>Ki. xi. 5.;<BR>(2) gen. by subs. or adj.;<BR>w. ing at the speech:<BR>तां श्रुत्वा सञ्जातविस्मयः, K.;<BR>w. ing:<BR>सविस्मयः, R. xvi. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wonderful
WONDERFUL, WONDROUS:<BR>(1) आश्चर्य (f. र्या);<BR>(2) अद्भुत (f. ता);<BR>(3) विस्मयकर (f. री);<BR>(4) विस्मयजनन (f. नी);<BR>(5) विस्मापक (f. पिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wonderfully
WONDERFULLY: expr. by adj. or circumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wont
WONT:<BR>I Subs.: रीतिः: v. Habit, custom.<BR>II Adj. परिचित (f. ता): v. Accustomed,<BR>practised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woo
WOO: याचते (याच, c. 1.), Vi. i. 59.: v. To<BR>beg, solicit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wood
WOOD:<BR>I Of trees:<BR>(1) काष्ठम्, to cut w.:<BR>काष्ठं पाटयति, Mah. iii. 297. 2.;<BR>made of w. of<BR>trees:<BR>तरूणां काष्ठैर्घटित (f. ता), V. m. 79. 39.;<BR>w. -cutter:<BR>काष्ठिकः, K. s. vi. 43.;<BR>(2) दारु (n.),<BR>the enemy of Mura h s transformed himself into<BR>w.:<BR>दारुभूतो मुरारिः, Ha. ii.;<BR>(3) by comp.,<BR>with a pestle of catechu w.:<BR>खादिरेण मुसलेन, D.<BR>vi.<BR>II Forest: q. v.: वनम्, went to w.:<BR>प्रस्थितो वनम्, Mah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woodcock
WOODCOCK: वनकुक्कुटः,<BR>or<BR>काष्ठकुक्कुटः, Mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wooded
WOODED: v. Woody.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wooden
WOODEN:<BR>(1) काष्ठमय (f. यी);<BR>(2) दारुमय (f.<BR>यी);<BR>(3) दारव (f. वी);<BR>(4) by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woodland
WOODLAND:<BR>(1) वृक्षभूमिः;<BR>(2) वृक्षावृतभूमिः etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woodman
WOODMAN:<BR>I Forester: q. v.: आटविक (f.<BR>की).<BR>II Wood-cutter: काष्ठिक (f. की).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wood-nymph
WOOD-NYMPH: वनदेवी and sim. comp.s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woodpecker
WOODPECKER:<BR>(1) काष्ठकुट्टः;<BR>(2) दार्वाधाटः (तः);<BR>शतपत्रकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wood-pigeon
WOOD-PIGEON: वनकपोतः and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wood-sorrel
WOOD-SORREL:<BR>(1) चुक्रिभा;<BR>(2) चाङ्गेरी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woody
WOODY:<BR>I Wooden: q. v.<BR>II Wooded:<BR>(1) वृक्षावृत (f. ता);<BR>(2) वृक्षाकीर्ण (f. र्णा);<BR>(3) तरुभूयिष्ठ (f. ष्ठा); and sim. comp.s.<BR>III<BR>Wild: q. v.: वन्य (f. न्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wooer
WOOER:<BR>(1) विवाहार्थिन् (f. णी);<BR>(2) विवाहकाम<BR>(f. मा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woof
WOOF: प्रतितन्त्रः, यथा एकेनैव तन्तुना तानप्रतितन्त्रौ<BR> भवतः, V. d. ii. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wool
WOOL:<BR>(1) लो(रो)मन् (n.);<BR>(2) ऊर्णा (properly<BR>of sheep);<BR>(3) by comp.;<BR>made of sheep's<BR>w., rat's w. and dog's w.:<BR>और्णान् वैलान् वार्षदंशान्,<BR>Mah. ii. 51. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woolen
WOOL(L)EN:<BR>(1) ऊर्णामय (f. यी),<BR>w. marriage-<BR>string:<BR>ऊर्णामयं कौतुकहस्तसूत्रम्, Ku. vii. 25.;<BR>(2)<BR>और्ण (f. र्णी),<BR>w. and silken fabrics:<BR>ओर्णञ्च<BR> राङ्कवञ्चैव पट्टजं कीटजं तथा, Mah. ii. 51. 26.;<BR>(3)<BR>लो(रो)मनिर्मित (f. ता), M. n.;<BR>(4) लो(रो)मज<BR>(f. जा), Nil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woolly
WOOLLY:<BR>I Lit.: लो(रो)मश (f. शा).<BR>II W.<BR>-like: ऊर्णाभ (f. भा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

word
WORD (subs.):<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) शब्दः, low w.:<BR>अपशब्दः;<BR>(2) नामन् (n. = name),<BR>of primitive,<BR>derivative and compound w. s:<BR>रुढयौगिकमिश्राणां<BR> नाम्नाम्, H. c.;<BR>(3) पदम् (= formed word),<BR>here the w.<BR>पशु: अत्र पशुपदम्, Kav. viii.<BR>II In<BR>plu.: saying: q. v.: वचस् (n.)<BR>or<BR>वाच् (f.),<BR>by the haughty w. s:<BR>वचोभिरुद्धतैः, Ki. xiv. 1.;<BR>one whose w. s can be trusted:<BR>आप्तवाच् (mfn.);<BR>Sa. v. 27. Ph.:<BR>a man of few w. s:<BR>मितभाषिन्<BR>(f. णी), R. i. 7.<BR>III Promise: q. v.:<BR>(1)<BR>वाक्यम्;<BR>(2) वचनम्।<BR>IV Tidings, news:<BR>q. v.: सन्देशः। Ph.:<BR>in a word:<BR>किं बहुना; in<BR>a few words:<BR>(1) समासतः;<BR>(2) समासेन।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

word
WORD (v.):<BR>simply w. ed:<BR>विशदशब्दविन्यस्त (f.<BR>स्ता);<BR>well-w.:<BR>सम्यग्ग्रथित (f. ता): v. To<BR>express, declare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wordy
WORDY:<BR>(1) बहुशब्द (f. ब्दा), -क (f. का);<BR>(2)<BR>विस्तीर्णवाच् (mfn.); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

work
WORK (subs.):<BR>(1) कर्मन् (n.: in every sense),<BR>to leave w.:<BR>कर्म त्यजति, Y.;<BR>who commencing<BR>a w.:<BR>कर्मारम्भं तु यः कृत्वा, Mit.; driver's w.:<BR>यन्तृकर्म, Si. xvii. 35.;<BR>(2) क्रिया,<BR>this w. of<BR>Kālidāsa:<BR>क्रियामिमां कालिदासस्य, V. i. 2.;<BR>obstruction to religious w. s:<BR>धर्मक्रियाविघ्नः, Sa. v.<BR>15.;<BR>(3) कार्यम्,<BR>in this important w.:<BR>कार्ये<BR> गुरुणि, Ku. iii. 13.;<BR>(4) कृतिः (rare),<BR>in a w.<BR>of Kālidāsa:<BR>कालिदासस्य कृतौ, Mal. i.: v.<BR>Also occupation, labour, deed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

work
WORK (v. i.):<BR>I To labour: q. v.: कर्म or<BR>कार्य करोति,<BR>you do not w.:<BR>न कर्म करोषि, D. vi.;<BR>will w. like w.-men:<BR>कर्म कर्मकरवत् करिष्यति, Si. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">Page767</a>]<BR>II To operate: q. v.:<BR>(1) फलं ददाति (दा,<BR>c. 3.);<BR>(2) expr. with गुणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

work
WORK (v. t.):<BR>I To manufacture, make:<BR>q. v.: करोति।<BR>II To make w.: कर्म कारयतिः<BR>v. Also to toil.<BR>III To move (as a ma-<BR>-chine): q. v.: चालयति (c. of चल्).<BR>IV To<BR>embroider: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

work out
WORK OUT:<BR>I To accomplish: q. v.: निष्पा-<BR>दयति (c. of पद्).<BR>II To invent: परिकल्पयति<BR>(c. of कॢप्).<BR>III To efface: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

work up
WORK UP:<BR>I To raise: q. v.<BR>II To employ,<BR>use: प्रयुंक्ते (युज्, c. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

workhouse
WORKHOUSE: *कर्मागारम्, अनाथाश्रमः (= asylum).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

working
WORKING (subs.):<BR>(1) कार्यप्रणाली (?);<BR>(2) परि-<BR>णामः (= result, fruit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

workman
WORKMAN, WORKWOMAN:<BR>(1) कर्मकरः (f. री);<BR>(2) कर्मकारः (f. री);<BR>(3) कर्मकारिन् (f. णी);<BR>(4) शिल्पकारः (f. री = artisan).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

workmanlike
WORKMANLIKE:<BR>(1) कर्मठ (f. ठा);<BR>(2) दक्ष (f.<BR>क्षा = skilful: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

workmanship
WORKMANSHIP:<BR>I Skill: कर्मकौशलम् and sim.<BR>comp.s<BR>II = work:<BR>(1) कर्मन् (n.);<BR>(2)<BR>निर्माणम् (= manufacture).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

workshop
WORKSHOP:<BR>(1) कर्मशाला (?);<BR>(2) शिल्पशाला;<BR>(3) आवेशनम्, प्र-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

world
WORLD: Lit.:<BR>(1) विश्वम् (= universe),<BR>of w.<BR>wide reputation:<BR>विश्वविख्यातकीर्तिः, D. s.;<BR>con-<BR>ducive to the good of the w.:<BR>विश्वजनीनः (ना, नं)<BR>Si. i. 41.;<BR>supporter of the w.:<BR>विश्वम्भरः, Si. i. 38.;<BR>(2) जगत् (= the whole w., also particular w.-<BR>s), the w. is now an empty withered wilderness:<BR>शून्यमधुना जीर्णारण्यं जगत्, U. i.;<BR>the whole w.<BR>from God to worm:<BR>आब्रह्म कीटान्तमिदं समस्तं जगत्,<BR>V. m. 74. 20.;<BR>(3) लोकः (any w.),<BR>the w. of<BR>gods:<BR>अमरलोकः, Ve. vii.; has left the w. (i. e.<BR>died): परलोकमितो गतः, Ve. iii. 15.;<BR>(4) भुवनम्<BR>(= 3),<BR>the three w. s robbed of their jewel:<BR>परि-<BR>मुषितरत्न त्रिभुवनम्, Ma. v. 29.;<BR>(5) संसारः (=<BR>living w.),<BR>throughout the w.:<BR>यावत्संसारमण्डलम्,<BR>Si.;<BR>(6) भूः (= earth: q. v.). Ph.:<BR>in this<BR>w.:<BR>इह: v. Here;<BR>of this w.:<BR>ऐहिकः (की,<BR> कम्);<BR>of the next w.<BR>पारत्रिक (f. की) or<BR>आमुष्मिक (f. की), D. ii.<BR>II People: q. v.:<BR>लोकः।<BR>III Mundane w.: संसारः,<BR>snares of the<BR>w.:<BR>संसारमाया (also sim. मायाजालम्, मोहपाशः,<BR>etc.).<BR>To renounce the w.:<BR>संन्यस्यति (अस्, c.<BR>4.);<BR>aversion to w.:<BR>वैराग्यम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worldly
WORLDLY:<BR>I Lit.:<BR>(1) ऐहिकः (की, कं);<BR>(2) सांसारिक (f. की);<BR>(3) ऐहलौकिकः (की,<BR> कं);<BR>(4) by comp.<BR>II Devoted to world:<BR>(1) विषयासक्त (f. क्ता),<BR>w.-minded:<BR>विषयासक्तचेतस्,<BR>(mfn.) and sim. comp.s;<BR>(2) संसारनिष्ठ (f.<BR>ष्ठा) and sim. comp. s (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worm
WORM:<BR>I The animal:<BR>(1) कीटः, w.-eaten:<BR>कीटैर्विद्ध (f. द्धा), V. m. 79. 87.;<BR>(2) कृ(क्रि)भिः,<BR>of w. s, insects, and butterflies:<BR>कृमिकीटपतङ्गानाम्,<BR>M. xii. 56.<BR>II Of the stomach: कृ(क्रि)मिः,<BR>destroying w. s:<BR>कृमिघ्न (f. घ्ना), Bha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wormy
WORMY:<BR>(1) कृमिल (f. ला);<BR>(2) कृमिन् (f. णी);<BR>(3) कृमिमय (f. यी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worry
WORRY:<BR>(1) बाधते, प्र-, सं-, वि-, (बाध्, c. 1.);<BR>(2) क्लिश्नाति (क्लिश्, c. 9.): v. To trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worse
WORSE:<BR>I In gen.:<BR>(1) अधिकदुष्ट (f. ष्टा =<BR>more faulty);<BR>(2) निकृष्टतर (f. रा = more low);<BR>(3) पापीयस् (f. सी = more wicked; etc.)<BR>II<BR>In health: अधिकरुग्ण (f. ग्णा) etc.: v.<BR>III<BR>sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worse
WORSE (adv.):<BR>(1) निकृष्टतरम्;<BR>(2) पापीयस् (n.);<BR>etc.: v. Above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worship
WORSHIP (subs.):<BR>(1) उपासनम्, -ना;<BR>(2) पूजा,<BR> -जनम्;<BR>(3) अर्चना, -नम्, अभि-। Ph.: Your w. (in<BR>address): देवः<BR>or<BR>धर्मावतारः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worship
WORSHIP (v.):<BR>(1) उपास्ते, (आस्, c. 2.),<BR>who<BR>w. s other gods:<BR>योऽन्यां देवतामुपास्ते, San. iv.;<BR>(2) पूजयति (पूज्, c. 10.),<BR>I will describe how<BR>to w. Śiva:<BR>शिवपूजां प्रवक्ष्यामि, A. p.: v. Also<BR>to honour, serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worshipful
WORSHIPFUL:<BR>(1) अर्चनीय (f. या), अभि, समभि-;<BR>(2) पूज्य (f. ज्या)<BR>or<BR>पूजनीय (f. या);<BR>(3) उपास्य<BR>(f. स्या)<BR>or<BR>उपासनीय (f. या); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worshipper
WORSHIPPER:<BR>(1) उपासक (f. सिका);<BR>(2) पूजक<BR>(f. जिका);<BR>idol-w.:<BR>प्रतिमापूजकः;<BR>(3) by<BR>comp.,<BR>w. of Energy:<BR>शाक्तः; w. of Viṣṇu:<BR>वैष्णवः;<BR>(4) भक्त (f. क्ता = attached to);<BR>w. of<BR>Gaṇeśa:<BR>गणेशभक्तः;<BR>w. of Yama:<BR>यमपरायणः,<BR>San. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worst
WORST:<BR>I Adj.:<BR>I<BR>(1) दुष्टतम (f. मा = very<BR>faulty);<BR>(2) पापिष्ठ (f. ष्ठा = very wicked);<BR>(3) कष्टतम (f. मा = very distressing);<BR>(4)<BR>अतिनिकृष्ट (f. ष्टा = very bad); etc.<BR>II Adv.:<BR>expr. by adj. or comp.<BR>III Subs.: कष्टतमा<BR> दशा and sim. expr. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worst
WORST (v.): पराभवति (भू, c. 1.): v. To de-<BR>-feat, overthrow^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worsted
WORSTED (subs.):<BR>(1) और्णसूत्रम् (?);<BR>(2) ऊर्णातन्तुः<BR>(?); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wort
WORT: लताविशेषे नवसुरायाञ्च।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worth
WORTH (subs.):<BR>I Value, price: q. v.: अर्धः।<BR>II Excellence, virtue: q. v.: गुणः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worth
WORTH (adj.): expr. by comp., what is it w.:<BR>किंमूल्यमिदम्;<BR>w. much:<BR>बहुमूल्य (f. ल्या);<BR>w.<BR>little:<BR>अल्पार्घ (f. र्घा);<BR>w. while:<BR>साम्प्रतम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worthy
WORTHY: Adj.: योग्य (f. ग्या): v. Deserv-<BR>-ing, fit.<BR>To be w. of:<BR>अर्हति (अर्ह्, c. 1.):<BR>v. To deserve,-ing of.<BR>II Subs.: मान्यजनः<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worthily
WORTHILY:<BR>(1) योग्यतया;<BR>(2) by adj. or cir-<BR>-cumlo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worthiness
WORTHINESS:<BR>(1) योग्यता, -त्वम्;<BR>(2) उपयुक्तता,<BR> -त्वम्;<BR>(3) अर्हता, -त्वम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worthless
WORTHLESS:<BR>(1) निर्गुण (f. णा), गुणहीन (f. ना),<BR>and sim. comp. s (= without any virtue);<BR>(2) असार (f. रा), अकिञ्चित्कर (f. री), etc.<BR>(= good-for-nothing);<BR>(3) अ- (=not) in<BR>comp.,<BR>w. object:<BR>अपात्रम्, Mu.; w. thing:<BR>अद्रव्यम्, Ku.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

worthlessness
WORTHLESSNESS:<BR>(1) निर्गुणता, -त्वम्; असारता, -त्वम्;<BR>etc.: v. Above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wound
WOUND (subs.):<BR>(1) व्रण (mn.),<BR>w. s are of vari-<BR>ous shapes:<BR>नानाकृतयो व्रणाः, Ni.;<BR>(2) क्षतम्:<BR>v. Hurt;<BR>(3) ईर्मम् (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wound
WOUND (v.):<BR>(1) विध्यति (व्यध्, c. 4. = to<BR>pierce: q. v.);<BR>(2) हन्ति (हन्, c. 2. = to<BR>strike),<BR>w. ed with horns:<BR>विषाणैर्हतः, Ni.;<BR>(3)<BR>क्षिणोति (क्षि, c. 5.: rare),<BR>w. ed her deeply in<BR>the heart:<BR>इमां हृदि व्यायतपातमक्षिणोत्, Ku. v.<BR>54.;<BR>(4) तुदति (तुद्, c. 6.): v. To hurt.<BR>W. ed:<BR>(1) क्षत (f. ता), परि-, वि-;<BR>(2) व्रणित<BR>(f. ता);<BR>(3) कृतव्रण (f. णा) and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR>Severly w. ed:<BR>क्षतविक्षत (f. ता).<BR>Mortally w.:<BR>भिन्नमर्मन् (mfn.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wove
WOVE, WOVEN: v. To weave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrangle
WRANGLE: कलहायते (nomi.): v. To quarrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrangling
WRANGLING (subs.); कलहः: v. Quarrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrap
WRAP: अवगुण्ठयति (गुण्ठ्, c. 1.): v. To cover,<BR>envelop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrapper
WRAPPER:<BR>(1) प्रावारः;<BR>(2) प्रावरणम्;<BR>(3) बृहतिका<BR>(rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrath
WRATH: रोषः: v. Anger, rage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrathful
WRATHFUL: रोषण (f. णा): v. Angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrathfully
WRATHFULLY:<BR>(1) सरोषम्, etc.;<BR>(2) by adj.:<BR>संरब्ध (f. ब्धा), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wreak
WREAK: साधयति (c. of सिध्): v. To execute,<BR>satisfy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wreath
WREATH:<BR>(1) माला;<BR>(2) माल्यम् (flowery);<BR>(3)<BR>स्रज् (f. = 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wreathe
WREATHE:<BR>I To string: q. v.: ग्रथ्नाति (ग्रन्थ्,<BR>c. 9.).<BR>II To encircle with a w.:<BR>w. d his<BR>neck:<BR>कण्ठे गुणं निवेशयामास<BR>or<BR>आसञ्जयामास, R.<BR>vi. 83.;<BR>w. d:<BR>स्रजान्वित (f. ता), N. xv. 1.:<BR>v. To put, adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wreck
WRECK (subs.):<BR>I Ship-w.: q. v.: पोतभङ्गः<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR>II The thing w. d:<BR>(1)<BR>भग्नपोतः;<BR>(2) नष्टनौका, etc.<BR>III Ruin, des-<BR>-truction: q. v.: उच्छेदः, सम-।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wreck
WRECK (v.):<BR>I Trans.:<BR>(1) भनक्ति (भञ्ज्, c.<BR>7. = to break: q. v.);<BR>(2) नाशयति (c. of<BR>नश् = destroy: q. v.).<BR>II Intrans.: भज्यते<BR>(pass. of भञ्ज्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wren
WREN: पक्षिविशेषः; स्वर्णचूडः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrench
WRENCH:<BR>I Verb.: बलादाकर्षति (कृष्, c. 1.<BR>= to pull: q. v.)<BR>or<BR>आच्छिनत्ति (छिद्, c. 7.<BR>= to carry off).<BR>II Subs.: बलादाकर्षणम् or<BR>आच्छेदः (त्तिः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrest
WREST:<BR>I To wrench: बलादाच्छिनत्ति।<BR>II To<BR>distort, writhe: q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrestle
WRESTLE:<BR>(1) मल्लयुद्धं करोति;<BR>(2) बाहुयुद्धं करोति;<BR>(3) बाहूबाहवि युध्यते (युध्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrestler
WRESTLER:<BR>(1) भल्लः;<BR>(2) मल्लः;<BR>(3) बाहुयोधः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrestling
WRESTLING (subs.):<BR>(1) मल्लयुद्धम्;<BR>(2) बाहुयुद्धम्;<BR>(3) मल्लक्रीडा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wretch
WRETCH:<BR>I In bad sense: दुरात्मन् (mfn.): [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">Page769</a>]<BR>v. Wicked.<BR>II A miserable person:<BR>(1)<BR>वराक (f. की);<BR>(2) मन्दभाग्य (f. ग्या): v.<BR>Unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wretched
WRETCHED:<BR>I Miserable, pitiable: q. v.:<BR>(1) दीन (f. ना);<BR>(2) वराक (f. की: only of<BR>persons: v. Poor).<BR>II Contemptible,<BR>low: q. v.: जघन्य (f. न्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wretchedly
WRETCHEDLY: expr. by adj. or comp.,<BR>w.<BR>dressed:<BR>दीनवेष<BR>or<BR>जघन्यवेष (f. षा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wretchedness
WRETCHEDNESS:<BR>(1) दीनता: v. Misery;<BR>(2)<BR>जघन्यता: v. Lowness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wriggle
WRIGGLE: इतस्ततश्चलति (चल्, c. 1. = to move:<BR>when intrans.)<BR>or<BR>चालयति (c. of चल्: when<BR>trans.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wring
WRING:<BR>I Lit.: आकुञ्चति (कुञ्च्, c. 1.): v.<BR>Also to twist.<BR>II Fig., with out, off, etc.:<BR>निष्पीड्य बहिष्करोतिः v. Also to squeeze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrinkle
WRINKLE:<BR>I Subs.: बलिः (ली),<BR>the body filled<BR>with w. s.:<BR>बलीसङ्गतगात्र (f. त्री), Mah. i. 82.<BR>6.;<BR>three w. s:<BR>बलित्रयम्, Ku. i. 32.<BR>II Verb:<BR>expr. by subs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrinkled
WRINKLED:<BR>(1) बलितः (ता, तं),<BR>eyes with<BR>w. edges:<BR>बलितापाङ्गलोचनः, Ki. xi. 4.;<BR>(2)<BR>बलिमत् (f. ती);<BR>(3) बलिभः (भा, भं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrist
WRIST: मणिबन्धः, -नम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

writ
WRIT:<BR>(1) शासनम्;<BR>(2) लेखः (= writing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

write
WRITE: लिखति (लिख्, c. 6.),<BR>to w. with one's<BR>own hand:<BR>स्वहस्तेन लिखति, Y. ii. 89.;<BR>I saw this<BR>couplet written on it:<BR>तस्यामिमाममिलिखितामार्या-<BR>मपश्यम्, K.;<BR>he has written this back:<BR>इदमनेन<BR> प्रतिलिखितम्, Mal. i.;<BR>getting a letter written by<BR>Śakaṭadāsa in these words:<BR>एभिरक्षरैर्लेखं शकट-<BR>दासेन लेखयित्वा, Mu. i.;<BR>what is not written on<BR>our minds:<BR>अस्माकं चेतसि किं नाम न लिखितमस्ति,<BR>Ana. vii.: v. Also to compose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

writer
WRITER:<BR>I Lit.: लेखकः,<BR>be the w. of this<BR>Bhārata:<BR>लेखको भारतस्यास्य भव, Mah. 77.<BR>II<BR>Author: q. v.: प्रणेतृ (f. त्री).<BR>III A scribe:<BR>(1) लिपिकरः;<BR>(2) लेखकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

writhe
WRITHE:<BR>I To shrink: q. v.: संकुचति (कुच्,<BR>c. 6.).<BR>II To distort: आकुञ्चयति (c. of<BR>कुञ्च्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

writing
WRITING (subs.):<BR>I The art of w.:<BR>(1)<BR>लिपिः,<BR>ignorant of w.:<BR>अलिपिज्ञः, N. s.;<BR>(2)<BR>लेखः (खा);<BR>(3) ले (लि) खतम्।<BR>II Anything<BR>written:<BR>(1) लेखः, looking at the w.:<BR>लेखमवलोकयन्, Mu. v.;<BR>(2) लेख्यम् (= docu-<BR>-ment);<BR>(3) लिखितम्।<BR>III Hand-w:<BR>(1)<BR>लेखः (खा);<BR>(2) लिखितम्, Mu. v.<BR>IV<BR>Composition:<BR>(1) लेखः (f. खा); लि(ले)खनम्;<BR>(3) लिखितम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrong
WRONG (adj.):<BR>I Unjust: q. v.; अन्याय्य<BR>(f. य्या).<BR>II Improper: q. v.: अयुक्त (f.<BR>क्ता).<BR>III Erroneous: q. v.: भ्रान्त (f. न्ता).<BR>IV False: q. v.: मिथ्या।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrong
WRONG (subs.):<BR>I Injury: q. v.: अपकारः।<BR>II Injustice: q. v.: अन्यायः।<BR>III Error:<BR>q. v.: भ्रमः।<BR>IV Fault: q. v.: दोषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrong
WRONG (v.):<BR>I To injure: q. v.: अपकरोति।<BR>II To find fault unjustly: मिथ्यादोषं विक्षिपति<BR>(क्षिप्, c. 6.), न्यस्यति (अस्, c. 4.), etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrong-doer
WRONG-DOER<BR>(1) अपराधिन् (f. नी = offender);<BR>(2) अपकारक (f. रिका = injurer);<BR>(3) उत्पीडक<BR>(f. डिका = tormentor).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrongful
WRONGFUL<BR>(1) अन्याय (f. या): v. Unjust;<BR>(2) दुष्ट (f. ष्टा): v. Wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrongfully
WRONGFULLY:<BR>(1) अन्यायतः: v. Unjustly;<BR>(2) दुष्टमावेनः v. Wickedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrongly
WRONGLY:<BR>(1) भिथ्या: v. Falsely;<BR>(2) अयुक्तम्:<BR>v. Improperly;<BR>(3) अन्यायतः: v. Unjustly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wroth
WROTH: कुपित (f. ता): v. Enraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrought
WROUGHT:<BR>(1) कृत (f. ता);<BR>(2) संस्कृत or<BR>उपस्कृत (f. ता).<BR>W. iron:<BR>कुशी।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wry
WRY:<BR>(1) वक्र (f. क्रा = crooked: q. v.),<BR>w-<BR>necked:<BR>वक्रग्रीव (f. वा);<BR>(2) विकृत (f. ता<BR>= deformed: q. v.),<BR>w.-faced:<BR>विकृतानन (f. ना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

xenodochy
XENODOCHY: अतिथिसेवा and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yacht
YACHT: केलिपोतः: v. Boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yak
YAK: चमर (f. री), a fan made of y.'s tail (an<BR>ensign of royalty): चामरम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yam
YAM: आलु (रु) कम्, Bha. Note the following<BR>species:<BR>(1) रक्तालुकम्;<BR>(2) काष्ठालुकम्;<BR>(3)<BR>शृङ्गालुकम्;<BR>(4) पिण्डालुकम्;<BR>(5) हस्त्यालुकम्;<BR>(6)<BR>सप्तालुकम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yankee
YANKEE: of United States: *अयङ्कः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yard
YARD:<BR>I A court: अङ्गनम्, प्राङ्गणम्;<BR>(2) चत्वरम्;<BR>(3) अजिरम् (rare), Ki. i. 16.<BR>II A<BR>measure: गजः, Li.<BR>III of a sail.: कूप-<BR>काष्ठम् (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yarn
YARN:<BR>I Lit.: सूत्रम् (general name).<BR>II<BR>Fig.: दीर्घकथा।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yawl
YAWL: नौविशेषः; *पोतकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yawn
YAWN (v.): जृम्भते, वि-, प्र-, (जृम्भ्, c. 1.): v.<BR>To gape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yawn
YAWN (subs.):<BR>(1) जृम्भा;<BR>(2) जृम्भणम्;<BR>(3)<BR>जृम्भितम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ye
YE: यूयम् (pl.); युवाम् (dual).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yea
YEA:<BR>I In assent: वाढम्: v. Yes.<BR>II More-<BR>-over, also: q. v.: तथा।<BR>Y. more:<BR>अधिकञ्च।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

year
YEAR:<BR>(1) वर्षम्,<BR>in three y. s.:<BR>वर्षत्रयेण, K.;<BR>for<BR>twelve y. s:<BR>द्वादशवर्षाणि, D. vi.;<BR>became ten y. s<BR>old:<BR>बभूव दशवार्षिकः, D. b. vii. 15. 44.;<BR>lasting<BR>twelve y. s:<BR>द्वादशवार्षिकः (की, कं), U. ii.;<BR>(2)<BR>वत्सरः, सं-, Li. 50.;<BR>(3) अब्दः,<BR>in the 8th. y. from<BR>conception:<BR>गर्भाष्टमेऽब्दे, M. ii. 36.;<BR>(4) हायनः, (a<BR>cow)<BR>four, three y. s old:<BR>चतुष्त्रिहायणी, H. c. i.<BR>4. 338.;<BR>(5) समा (mostly in pl.), 14 y. s:<BR>चतुर्दश समाः, Vi. iv. 41.; for 100<BR>y. s:<BR>सहस्र-<BR>समम्, B. p. 4.;<BR>(6) शरद्, (= autumn): v.<BR>Winter. Ph.:<BR>last y.:<BR>परुत्, A.; of last y.:<BR>परुत्र (f. त्री) (rare);<BR>this y.:<BR>ऐषमस्, A.;<BR>y.<BR>before last:<BR>परारि (inde.), A.:<BR>of y. before<BR>last:<BR>परारित्र (f. त्री) (rare).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yearly
YEARLY:<BR>I Adj.:<BR>(1) वार्षिक (f. की);<BR>(2)<BR>वात्सरिक (f. की);<BR>(3) आब्दिक (f. की);<BR>(4)<BR>प्रतिवार्षिक (f. की); etc. Half-y.:<BR>(1) षाण्मासिक<BR>(f. की);<BR>(2) अर्धवार्षिक (f. की); etc.<BR>II<BR>Adv.:<BR>(1) वर्षे वर्षे;<BR>(2) प्रतिवर्षम्;<BR>(3) अनु-<BR>वत्सरम्, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yearn
YEARN:<BR>(1) स्पृहयति (स्पृह्, c. 10. = long for:<BR>q. v.);<BR>(2) स्निह्यति (स्निह्, c. 4. = to have<BR>affection for);<BR>(3) उत्सुकायते (nomi. = to be<BR>eager).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yearning
YEARNING (subs.):<BR>(1) स्पृहा (= longing);<BR>(2)<BR>वात्सल्यम् (= affection);<BR>(3) औत्सुक्यम् (= eager-<BR>-ness).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yeast
YEAST:<BR>(1) सुरामण्डः;<BR>(2) किण्व (mn.);<BR>(3)<BR>अभिषवः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yeal
YEAL:<BR>I Subs.: चीत्कारः: v. Scream, cry.<BR>II Verb: उत्क्रोशत्रि (क्रुश्, c. 1.): v. To<BR>scream, shout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yellow
YELLOW:<BR>(1) पीत (f. ता);<BR>(2) पीतवर्ण (f.<BR>र्णा);<BR>(3) पीतल (f. ला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yeallow-bird
YEALLOW-BIRD, YELLOW-HAMMER: हरिद्राङ्गः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yellowish
YELLOWISH:<BR>(1) आपीत (f. ता);<BR>(2) हरिद्राभ<BR>(f. भा); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yeep
YEEP: भषति (भष्, c. 1.): v. To bark, cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yeoman
YEOMAN:<BR>(1) गृहस्थः (?);<BR>(2) गृहपतिः (?);<BR>(3)<BR>क्षेत्रपालः (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yes
YES:<BR>(1) अथ किम्,<BR>do the Rishis bear message<BR>from Kaṇva, y.:<BR>किं कण्वसन्देशहारिणस्तपस्विनः ?<BR> अथ किम्, Sa. v.;<BR>y. by your favour my mercantile<BR>business is not failing:<BR>अथ किम्, आर्यस्य प्रसादेन<BR> नाखण्डिता मे वणिज्या, Mu. i.;<BR>(2) वाढम् (= very<BR>well, indeed);<BR>(3) एवम् (= so, with एव =<BR>just so);<BR>(4) by repetition of verb,<BR>y., I<BR>have heard of him:<BR>अस्ति, श्रूयते, Sa. i.;<BR>y., you<BR>have guessed all right:<BR>सम्यगुपलक्षितं भवत्या, Sa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yesterday
YESTERDAY:<BR>(1) ह्यस्,<BR>of y.:<BR>ह्यस्तन (f. नी);<BR>(2) पूर्वेद्यूः (= on the previous day);<BR>(3) कल्यम्<BR>(= day gone by as well as day coming).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yesternight
YESTERNIGHT:<BR>(1) गतरात्रिः;<BR>(2) कल्यरात्रिः;<BR>and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yet
YET:<BR>I Nevertheless:<BR>(1) तथापि,<BR>yet I am<BR>desirous of hearing:<BR>तथापि शुश्रूषुरहम्, Si. i. 29.;<BR>(2) not expr.,<BR>although it is infested with<BR>fierce animals, y. it is frequented by sages:<BR>क्रूर-<BR>सत्त्वापि मुनिजनसेविता, K.;<BR>(3) परन्तु (= but:<BR>q. v.).<BR>II Of time:<BR>(1) अद्यापि,<BR>I y. think of<BR>her:<BR>अद्यापि तां चिन्तयामि, J.;<BR>(2) अधुनापि,<BR>where<BR>y. in the rainy season:<BR>अधुनापि यत्र जलधरसमये,<BR>K.;<BR>(3) इदानीमपि।<BR>III Further, over and<BR>above,<BR>y. blacker:<BR>अधिकतरकृष्ण (f. ष्णा);<BR>y.<BR>another reason:<BR>अपरमपि कारणम्: y. a little longer:<BR>एतदधिकं कियत्क्षणम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yew
YEW: शाखोटजातीयवृक्षविशेषः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yield
YIELD:<BR>I To produce: q. v.<BR>(1) सूते (सू,<BR>c. 2.),<BR>y. ed gems in mines, crops in fields and<BR>elephants in forests:<BR>खनिभिः सुषुवे रत्नं क्षेत्रं शस्यैर्वनै-<BR>र्गजान्, R. xvii. 66.;<BR>(2) ददाति, प्र- (दा, c. 3.<BR>give),<BR>y. ing every crop:<BR>सर्वशस्यप्रद (f. दा).<BR>II<BR>To give up, relinquish.<BR>II To concede,<BR>allow, permit: q. v.: अनुमन्यते (मन्, c. 4.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yield
YIELD (v. i.):<BR>I To give way: q. v.: वशं गच्छति<BR>(गम्, c. 1.), एति (इ, c. 2.); etc.<BR>II To<BR>comply with: अनुमन्यते (मन्, c. 4.: with<BR>acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yield
YIELD (subs.): उत्पन्नम्: v. Produce, fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yoke
YOKE (subs.):<BR>I Lit.: युगः,<BR>fit for y.:<BR>युग्य (f.<BR>ग्या), K. v. 49.<BR>II A pair: q. v.: युगम्।<BR>III Fig.: योक्त्रम्: v. Bond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yoke
YOKE (v.):<BR>(1) योजयति (युज्, c. 10.);<BR>(2)<BR>योक्त्रयति (nomi.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yoke-fellow
YOKE-FELLOW: सहचर (f. री): v. Compa-<BR>-nion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yon
YON, YONDER: expr. by अदस्,<BR>the y. waters of<BR>Pampā:<BR>अमूनि पम्पासलिलानि, R. xiii. 30. Y.<BR>(i. e. further on): अमुत्र, K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yore
YORE:<BR>of y.:<BR>पुरा: v. Formerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

you
YOU: त्वद्,<BR>therefore you:<BR>स त्वम्, R. ii. 45.;<BR>y.<BR>yourself:<BR>त्वमेव, Ku. v. 67. y. alone know<BR>यूयमेव जानीथ, Sa. v. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

young
YOUNG (adj.):<BR>(1) युवन् (f. ती),<BR>having a y.<BR>wife:<BR>युवजानिः, B. v. 13.;<BR>y. camel:<BR>दासेरयुवा,<BR>Si.;<BR>y. sugarcane:<BR>युवेक्षुः, Bha.;<BR>(2) तरुण (f.<BR>णी),<BR>y. wife:<BR>तरुणी भार्या, H.;<BR>(3) बाल (f. ला<BR>= very y. child);<BR>y. plant:<BR>बालपादपः, Sa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

young
YOUNG (subs.):<BR>(1) शावः, -कः;<BR>(2) अर्भः, -कः;<BR>(3) पोतः, -कः;<BR>(4) डिम्बः, -कः: v. Also<BR>child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

younger
YOUNGER:<BR>(1) यवीयस् (f. सी),<BR>y. sister:<BR>यवीयसी<BR> स्वसा, R. xvi. 85.;<BR>(2) कनीयस् (f. सी), D.<BR>Ph.: y. brother, sister:<BR>(1) अनुज (f. जा);<BR>(2) अवरज (f. जा);<BR>(3) अन्तरज (f. जा);<BR>(4)<BR>जघन्यज (f. जा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

youngest
YOUNGEST:<BR>(1) कनिष्ठ f. ष्ठा;<BR>(2) यविष्ठ f. ष्ठा;<BR>(3) जघन्य f. न्या (rare),<BR>although y., senior in<BR>virtues:<BR>जघन्योऽपि गुणज्येष्ठः, Sca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

your
YOUR:<BR>(1) त्वदीय (f. या);<BR>(2) तावक (f. की);<BR>(3) तावकीन (f. ना);<BR>(4) युष्मदीय (f. या);<BR>(5) यौष्माक (f. की);<BR>(6) यौष्माकीन (f. नी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

youth
YOUTH:<BR>I The age:<BR>(1) यौवनम्,<BR>seeking plea-<BR>sures in y.:<BR>यौवने विषयैषिणाम्, R. i. 8.;<BR>a girl<BR>in the prime of y.:<BR>नवयौवना, R. ix. 7.;<BR>(2)<BR>तारुण्यम्,<BR>exchange of y.:<BR>तारुण्यविनिमयः, C. r.;<BR>(3) नवं वयस् (n.), Ku. v. 41.;<BR>(4) प्रथमं वयः,<BR>K.<BR>II The state:<BR>(1) यौवनम्, -दशा, H.;<BR>(2)<BR>तारुण्यम्, -अवस्था।<BR>III A young man:<BR>(1) युवन्<BR>(m.),<BR>ascetic y.:<BR>तपोधनयुवा, K.;<BR>(2) तरुणः,<BR>y. s<BR>are fond of young women:<BR>तरुणस्तावत्तरुणीरक्तः, J.;<BR>(3) युवजनः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

youthful
YOUTHFUL:<BR>(1) यौवनवत् (f. ती);<BR>(2) तरुणवयस्क<BR>(f. स्का); etc.: v. Also young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

youthfulness
YOUTHFULNESS: तरुणवयस्कता and sim. comp. s:<BR>v. Youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zany
ZANY: भण्डः: v. Buffoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zeal
ZEAL:<BR>(1) उत्साहः;<BR>(2) औत्सुक्यम्;<BR>(3) उत्सुकता,<BR> -त्वम्;<BR>(4) सोत्साहता, -त्वम्;<BR>(5) आग्रहः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zealot
ZEALOT, ZEALOUS:<BR>(1) उत्साहवत् (f. ती);<BR>(2)<BR>सोत्साह (f. हा);<BR>(3) उत्सुक (f. का);<BR>(4) आग्र-<BR>हिन् (f. णी); etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zealously
ZEALOUSLY:<BR>(1) सोत्साहम्, who carried orders z.:<BR>सोत्साहं धृतशासनैः, Vi. vii. 10.;<BR>(2) औत्सुक्येन;<BR>(3) उत्सुकम्;<BR>(4) साग्रहम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zebra
ZEBRA: an animal: *चित्रगर्दभः; चित्ररासमः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zebu
ZEBU:<BR>(1) ककुद्मत् (m.);<BR>(2) वृषमः = ox : q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zedoary
ZEDOARY: a plant:<BR>(1) सटिः (टी);<BR>(2) कर्च्-<BR>(र्बू) रकः;<BR>(3) द्राविडकः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zenith
ZENITH:<BR>(1) खमध्यम्;<BR>(2) शिरोबिन्दुः, z. distance:<BR>नतम्, Su. iii. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zephyr
ZEPHYR:<BR>I Lit.: पश्चिमानिलः and sim. comp. s.<BR>II Poet. मलयानिलः, मलयवातः and sim. comp. s.<BR>(lit.: of Malaya).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zero
ZERO:<BR>(1) शून्यम्;<BR>(2) बिन्दुः;<BR>(3) खम्, Vij.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zest
ZEST:<BR>I Lit.: रोचकम्।<BR>II Relish, taste:<BR>q. v.: आस्वादः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zigzag
ZIGZAG:<BR>(1) अङ्कवङ्क (f. ङ्काः: (?);<BR>(2) वक्र (f. क्रा<BR>= crooked: q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zinc
ZINC: a metal: दस्ता।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zodiac
ZODIAC:<BR>(1) ज्योतिश्चक्रम्;<BR>(2) भचक्रम्;<BR>(3) राशि-<BR>चक्रम्,<BR>sign of the z.:<BR>राशिः।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zone
ZONE:<BR>I A girdle: q. v.: मेखला।<BR>II Of<BR>the earth: *मण्डलम् (?),<BR>torrid, frigid z.:<BR>*घर्म-<BR>मण्डलम्, शीतमण्डलम्।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zoography
ZOOGRAPHY: *प्राणिविवरणम् and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zoological
ZOOLOGICAL: expr. by comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zoologist
ZOOLOGIST: *जीवविज्ञानविशारद (f. दा); प्राणितत्त्व-<BR>विद् (mfn.); and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zoology
ZOOLOGY: *जीवविज्ञानम्; प्राणितत्त्वम्; and sim.<BR>comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zootomy
ZOOTOMY: *जीवव्यवच्छेदः and sim. comp. s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

